high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT1","text":"Der Axiomensatz reicht zur Rekonstruktion der zentralen Bewegung von Mehrwertproduktion über organischen Wechsel zur Reservearmee und zum Pauperismus aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT2","text":"Der empirische Beleggang bleibt unterbestimmt, weil die Source Unit während der Untersuchung ländlicher Wohnverhältnisse abbricht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0284","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0340","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern zwischen absolutem Kapitalwachstum, relativem Rückgang des variablen Kapitalteils und absoluter Arbeiterzahl unterschieden wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Vermittlung liegt in der Bestimmung der Arbeitsnachfrage durch das variable Kapital statt durch das Gesamtkapital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT5","text":"Die Bezeichnung als absolutes allgemeines Gesetz steht unter Spannung zur zugleich eingeräumten Modifikation durch nicht ausgeführte Umstände.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT6","text":"Die Möglichkeit steigender Löhne und besserer Konsumtion bleibt nur unvollständig mit der späteren Behauptung vermittelt, die Lage des Arbeiters verschlechtere sich unabhängig von seiner Zahlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0134","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT7","text":"Die Kausalrolle der organischen Zusammensetzung hängt von einer nur annähernden Spiegelung technischer Veränderungen in Wertverhältnissen ab; die modifizierenden Faktoren werden vertagt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT8","text":"Die Reservearmee erklärt die Möglichkeit zyklischer Expansion, leitet aber die konkrete Periodizität des industriellen Zyklus nicht vollständig her.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT9","text":"Die englischen Daten belegen die Koexistenz von Reichtumswachstum und Degradation; ihre kausale Verbindung hängt zusätzlich von der vorangehenden Mechanik und von komprimierter Fallauswahl ab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0180","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0190","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT10","text":"Die tatsächliche Argumentbewegung bleibt rekonstruierbar, wenn die günstige Ausgangsannahme, ihre Aufhebung, die endogene Reservebildung und der empirische Belastungstest in dieser Reihenfolge erhalten bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211315282781Z_f2781e8c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c) The general law of capitalist accumulation. · reading part 1/2","source_sha256":"3f5ad065bf5ce7ee45baef80559f63ae880c995004b5221f830d620221b6ea5e","sha256":"58ed0444bc839fe3b0040576f31c7824f2290ca3342ee0e8be70f13b8da0cd4a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:13:15.284328+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS1","text":"What must be explained is why growing social wealth simultaneously produces dependence, surplus labour, and pauperism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS2","text":"Capitalist accumulation reproduces the capital relation, alters the organic composition of capital, and thereby produces a relative surplus population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds conditionally, reconstructively, diagnostically, and polemically against the naturalization of population phenomena produced by capitalism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS4","text":"The analysis begins with the most favourable assumption of an unchanged technical composition and shows that even rising wages do not abolish the domination of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5","text":"The removal of this assumption shifts the explanation from absolute population growth to productivity, organic composition, concentration, and the release of workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS6","text":"The produced surplus population becomes the industrial reserve army and thus the precondition for further accumulation, cyclical expansion, and wage discipline.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS7","text":"The English case serves as an empirical stress test of the chain wealth growth → displacement of labour → pauperism → material degradation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0272","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0181","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0190","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A1","text":"The production of surplus value is the absolute law of the capitalist mode of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A2","text":"Labour-power is purchased as a means of capital valorization and as a source of unpaid labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A3","text":"The wage relation presupposes the continued resalability of labour-power and the delivery of unpaid labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A4","text":"Accumulation is the continued reconversion of surplus value into capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5","text":"Expanded reproduction reproduces the capital relation on an expanded scale and multiplies the proletariat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A6","text":"Given an unchanged technical composition, demand for labour-power grows proportionally to capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7","text":"The dynamic of accumulation limits the price of labour to a level that does not seriously endanger the expanded reproduction of the capital relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","text":"Rising social productivity enlarges the mass of means of production set in motion by a given labour-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9","text":"The organic composition of capital is the approximate value reflection of its technical composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","text":"Demand for labour is determined by the variable part of capital and not by total capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A11","text":"Capital accumulation and the specifically capitalist development of productive power mutually accelerate one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A12","text":"Accumulation concentrates means of production and command over labour within growing individual capitals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","text":"The attraction of already formed capitals redistributes existing capital and is accelerated by competition and credit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14","text":"Growth, attraction, and technological revolution reduce the variable part of capital relative to the constant part of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A15","text":"Capital can increase its supply of labour through extensive or intensive exploitation and through the replacement of labour-powers more rapidly than its demand for workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0090","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","text":"The superfluity of labour-power is determined relative to the average valorization requirements of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","text":"A disposable industrial reserve army is the precondition of sudden expansion and of the form of movement of modern industry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18","text":"The competitive pressure of the reserve army disciplines the active army of workers and limits its demands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0108","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX1","text":"Accumulation is not identical with the complete consumption of the capitalized surplus product by additional productive workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX2","text":"Not every poor person is a proletarian, but rather the wage worker who produces capital and is released when no longer valorisable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX3","text":"A rising wage abolishes neither exploitation nor dependence nor the compulsion to resell labour-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX4","text":"Labour-power is not acquired for the satisfaction of the buyer's personal needs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX5","text":"Accumulation is not a merely quantitative enlargement of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX6","text":"The value composition is not an exact measure of the technical composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX7","text":"Concentration conditioned by accumulation is not identical with the attraction and fusion of already existing capitals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX8","text":"Growth of total capital is not identical with proportional growth in demand for labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX9","text":"Labour shortages and labour surpluses do not arise primarily from autonomous movements of the absolute worker population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX10","text":"The expansion and contraction of credit are not the fundamental cause of the industrial cycle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX11","text":"Machinery does not release capital for workers, but workers for additional capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX12","text":"Pauperism is neither a mere result of idleness nor an external disturbance of accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0126","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0188","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX13","text":"An abstract law of population valid for all historical modes of production does not exist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D1","text":"Under an unchanged technical composition, accumulation can increase demand for labour and wages while at the same time extending the relation of dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D2","text":"If a wage increase diminishes the incentive to valorize, accumulation weakens, abolishes the labour shortage, and restores a wage level compatible with capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D3","text":"Accumulation produces the material basis of greater production, this increases productivity and surplus-value production, and the additional surplus value in turn accelerates accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A11","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A12","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D4","text":"The increase in value of the constant part of capital understates the technical shift, because rising productivity relatively cheapens the means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D5","text":"The variable part of capital can grow absolutely and nevertheless fall relative to total capital and to the scale of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D6","text":"New capital attracts proportionately ever fewer workers, while technologically renewed old capital repels workers already employed.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D7","text":"The quantity of available labour becomes partially decoupled from the number of available workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D8","text":"Accumulation produces a worker population surplus to the average requirements of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A15","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D9","text":"The industrial reserve army is simultaneously absorbed, released, and reproduced by the industrial cycle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A11","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D10","text":"Absolute movements of capital appear as relative movements of the worker population and make capital-produced superfluity appear as a demographic cause.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D11","text":"The general movement of wages is regulated by the changing relation between the active army of workers and the reserve army.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0099","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12","text":"The relative surplus population sediments into floating, latent, and stagnant forms, as well as into pauperism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D13","text":"Pauperism forms the hospital of invalids of the active army of workers, the dead weight of the reserve army, and necessary incidental costs of capitalist production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0126","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D14","text":"With growing wealth, capital, productive power, and worker population, the relative surplus population, consolidated misery, and official pauperism grow.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0128","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D15","text":"Earlier economists grasp the functional necessity of a poor working class, but naturalize or moralize it instead of deriving it from the mechanism of accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0141","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:D16","text":"The English evidence functions as a negative test of demographic dogma, because slowed population growth coexists with accelerated wealth growth, concentration, displacement of labour, undernourishment, housing distress, and pauperism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0147","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0149","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0153","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0272","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0181","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0190","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1","text":"With the reserve army, capital itself produces the labour-market condition of its expansion independent of natural population growth.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A15","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD2","text":"Under capitalist property relations, an increase in productivity is transformed not primarily into free time, but simultaneously into overwork of the employed and enforced idleness of those released.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A15","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0093","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD3","text":"Capital acts on both sides of the labour market by producing demand for labour and, at the same time, shaping the supply of labour through release and overwork.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A15","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0111","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4","text":"The effects of accumulation become conditions of its repetition, such that expansion, release, reserve formation, and renewed expansion form a recursive cycle structure.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A11","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD5","text":"Capitalist accumulation privatizes the wealth produced and shifts the costs of pauperism, illness, and inadequate reproduction onto the working class, the small middle class, and public poor relief.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0174","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0187","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD6","text":"The organized association of employed and unemployed persons intervenes directly in the disciplinary mechanism of the reserve army.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD7","text":"Where the spontaneous production of a reserve army fails, capital tends to supplement the labour-market mechanism through coercion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0113","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX1","text":"Demand for labour and supply of labour are not magnitudes independent of one another and of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0110","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX2","text":"The worker population is not an external, purely natural cause of the movements of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0100","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX3","text":"Within the capitalist form, the development of productive power has no socially neutral effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0131","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX4","text":"The juridical freedom of the wage worker does not mean material independence from capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX5","text":"Growth in social wealth does not necessarily improve the conditions of reproduction of the producers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0164","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX6","text":"Full employment does not constitute a stable normal state of developed capitalist production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX7","text":"Property and legal relations are not neutral shells of a production process proceeding independently of them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX8","text":"Cyclical unemployment is not a mere malfunction that can be permanently eliminated without altering the mode of accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX9","text":"Individual thrift, mobility, or wage increases do not dissolve the reproduced class relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0107","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX1","text":"Structurally absent is a production order in which objective wealth is subordinated to the developmental needs of workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX2","text":"Blocked is a permanent abolition of the industrial reserve army under an unchanged cyclical mode of expansion of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX3","text":"Excluded is a non-antagonistic capitalist accumulation in which the same process increases wealth without reproducing dependence and surplus population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0135","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX4","text":"Unavailable is the immediate translation of labour-saving into a general reduction of working time and secured free development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0097","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS1","text":"Surplus-value production → capitalization of surplus value → expanded reproduction of the capital relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS2","text":"Unchanged technical composition → proportional demand for labour → possible wage increase → valorization limit → accumulative counter-correction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS3","text":"Accumulation → greater scale of production → increase in productive power → additional surplus-value production → accelerated accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS4","text":"Increase in productive power → growing technical composition → rising organic composition → relative decrease of variable capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS5","text":"Concentration of accumulation and attraction of formed capitals → revolutionization of new and old capital → declining relative demand for labour → release of workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS6","text":"Release of workers plus intensified squeezing of labour → relative surplus population → reserve army → wage pressure and flexible expansion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0108","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS7","text":"Reserve formation → cyclical absorption and repulsion → consolidated surplus population → pauperism → antagonistic accumulation of wealth and misery.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0125","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0128","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0135","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AF1","text":"Most favourable assumption of accumulation → rising demand for labour → rising wage → continuing exploitation → capital-immanent wage limit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AF2","text":"Removal of the constant composition → increase in productivity → organic change → relative decrease of variable capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AF3","text":"Concentration and attraction of capital → reduced attraction of workers plus repulsion of workers → relative surplus population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:AF4","text":"Surplus population → industrial reserve army → cyclical expansion and wage discipline → pauperism → general law of accumulation → English counter-test.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0108","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0128","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME1","text":"Accumulation is remapped from mere increase of wealth to the expanded reproduction of a class relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME2","text":"Wage movements are reclassified from demographic reflexes into dependent variables of the movement of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME3","text":"Overpopulation is redefined from an absolute surplus of people into relative superfluity in relation to capitalist requirements of valorization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME4","text":"Technical progress is transformed from general relief into a form-dependent mechanism of simultaneous increase in productive power and release of workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME5","text":"Concentration splits into the growth of individual capitals through accumulation and the attraction of already formed capitals through competition and credit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME6","text":"The labour market no longer appears as a neutral encounter of independent magnitudes, but as a field shaped on both sides by accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0110","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0111","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME7","text":"Unemployment is reclassified from a temporary deviation into a condition of existence of cyclical capitalist expansion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME8","text":"Undernourishment, housing distress, and pauperism become legible as material forms of reproduction of accumulation rather than as external social defects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0181","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0190","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME9","text":"The naturalizations of political economy become visible as an ideological inversion of effects produced by capital into population-conditioned causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT1","text":"Surface — Wages, employment, unemployment, food, housing, illness, and pauperism constitute the visible level of phenomena.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0174","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0181","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0190","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT2","text":"Structural — Surplus-value production, organic composition, concentration, capital attraction, and reserve-army formation produce the phenomena.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The explanation is shifted from natural population, individual guilt, and neutral market equilibration to capital-immanent reproduction and class power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0100","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0111","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Capital appears as a recursively self-reproducing social relation whose cyclical time transforms effects into conditions of their repetition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT1","text":"The set of axioms suffices to reconstruct the central movement from surplus-value production through organic change to the reserve army and pauperism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0126","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT2","text":"The empirical course of proof remains underdetermined because the Source Unit breaks off during the examination of rural housing conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0284","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0340","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent insofar as a distinction is made between absolute capital growth, the relative decline of the variable part of capital, and the absolute number of workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT4","text":"The strongest mediation lies in the determination of demand for labour by variable capital rather than by total capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT5","text":"The designation as an absolute general law stands in tension with the simultaneously admitted modification by circumstances not elaborated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT6","text":"The possibility of rising wages and better consumption remains only incompletely mediated with the later assertion that the worker's condition worsens independently of his payment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0134","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT7","text":"The causal role of the organic composition depends on only an approximate reflection of technical changes in value relations; the modifying factors are deferred.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0064","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT8","text":"The reserve army explains the possibility of cyclical expansion, but does not fully derive the concrete periodicity of the industrial cycle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT9","text":"The English data demonstrate the coexistence of wealth growth and degradation; their causal connection additionally depends on the preceding mechanics and on compressed case selection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0180","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0190","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT10","text":"The actual movement of the argument remains reconstructible if the favourable initial assumption, its removal, endogenous reserve formation, and the empirical stress test are retained in this order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CDAG:P0146","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]}],"revision":"CH_V4GB_CDAG@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_V4GB_CDAG:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 20","title":"c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 1/2","context":"Chapter 20"}},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2","layer":"CH","title":"c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 2/2","order":21,"parents":["RAW_V4GB_CD_2"],"revision":"CH_V4GB_CD_2@R001","sha256":"b482e33b70518d981fa2b18022a94f3ceec29741890c6bcf44ab4ef256ed3311","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS1","text":"Zu erklären ist, wie Entvölkerung, lokale Wohnungsnot, Arbeitsüberschuss, zeitweiliger Arbeitsmangel und steigende Renten gleichzeitig entstehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS2","text":"Relative Übervölkerung wird als Verhältnis der Arbeitsbevölkerung zur kapitalistisch bestimmten Arbeitsnachfrage neu bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS3","text":"Das Argument verfährt diagnostisch, rekonstruktiv und polemisch gegen die Erklärung des Elends aus absoluter Bevölkerungsgröße.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS4","text":"Konzentration, agrarische Umstrukturierung und Wohnraumentzug erzeugen zugleich räumliche Entleerung, lokale Verdichtung und Lohndruck.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS5","text":"Das Gangsystem vermittelt den Widerspruch zwischen minimalem Dauerpersonal und kurzfristigem Mehrbedarf durch billige, mobile Frauen- und Kinderarbeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS6","text":"Irlands Massenauswanderung fungiert als Gegenexperiment: Absolute Entvölkerung beseitigt weder relative Übervölkerung noch Elend, während Renten und konzentriertes Kapital wachsen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7","text":"Die Bewegung führt vom englischen Agrarwiderspruch über seine institutionelle Vermittlung zur irischen Widerlegung des demographischen Gleichgewichtsmodells und zur politischen Rückkehr der Verdrängten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","text":"Relative Übervölkerung ist ein Verhältnis zwischen verfügbarer Arbeitskraft und kapitalistisch bestimmter Arbeitsnachfrage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","text":"Die Konzentration von Boden und Produktionsmitteln trennt Produzenten von ihren Beschäftigungs- und Subsistenzmitteln.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","text":"Kapitalistische Agrarumstrukturierung senkt den dauerhaften Arbeitskräftebedarf relativ zu Fläche und Produktionsvermögen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","text":"Die Verfügung über Cottages reguliert die räumliche Verfügbarkeit, Abhängigkeit und Widerstandsfähigkeit der Landarbeiter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","text":"Agrarische Arbeitsnachfrage ist zeitlich ungleich und verlangt bei geringem Dauerbedarf periodische Zusatzarbeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6","text":"Frauen- und Kinderarbeit deckt temporäre Arbeitsspitzen, ohne eine entsprechende Erhöhung des männlichen Arbeitslohns zu erzwingen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A7","text":"Die Ausweitung von Frauen- und Kinderarbeit verdrängt männliche Arbeit und reproduziert Lohndruck.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","text":"Das Gangsystem verwandelt räumlich verstreute Familienarbeitskraft durch Vermittlung und Stücklohn in eine mobile Arbeitsreserve.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9","text":"Das Gangsystem besteht als kostensenkendes Flexibilitätsinstrument großer Pächter und Grundeigentümer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10","text":"Die agrarische Revolution kann relative Übervölkerung schneller erzeugen, als Emigration die absolute Bevölkerung vermindert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11","text":"Produktionsmittel werden erst durch die Einverleibung fremder Arbeit zu Kapital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12","text":"Die Masse des Mehrprodukts kann bei sinkendem Gesamtprodukt wachsen, wenn sein Anteil am Gesamtprodukt steigt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A13","text":"Steigende Marktpreise können den Geldwert des Mehrprodukts schneller erhöhen als dessen physische Masse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","text":"Emigration ist ein rekursiver Transferprozess und keine einmalige Vernichtung der verdrängten Bevölkerung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A15","text":"Absolute Entvölkerung kontrahiert den Binnenmarkt und proletarisiert Teile der kleinen Mittelklasse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16","text":"Irland fungiert innerhalb des betrachteten Systems als agrarisches Zuliefer- und Rekrutierungsgebiet Englands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX1","text":"Cottages erzeugen oder attrahieren die arme Bevölkerung nicht naturgesetzlich; fehlender Wohnraum vertreibt sie aus noch ungünstigeren Orten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX2","text":"Menschenleere Distrikte sind nicht frei von relativer Übervölkerung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX3","text":"Temporärer Arbeitsmangel führt nicht notwendig zu höheren Arbeitslöhnen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX4","text":"Das Gangsystem besteht nicht um des Gangmeisters willen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX5","text":"Das Gangsystem ist keine neutrale Antwort auf einen vorausgesetzten natürlichen Mangel an männlicher Arbeit; es produziert männliche Beschäftigungslosigkeit mit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX6","text":"Arbeiterelend ist nicht aus absoluter Übervölkerung ableitbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX7","text":"Absolute Entvölkerung stellt kein demographisch-ökonomisches Gleichgewicht her.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX8","text":"Produktionsmittel und Produkte sind nicht aufgrund ihrer physischen Gestalt Kapital oder Ware.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX9","text":"Steigende Grundrente bedeutet weder Wohlergehen des Bodens noch Wohlergehen der Bevölkerung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX10","text":"Die Wirkungen einer mittelalterlichen Pest liefern kein übertragbares Modell für kapitalistische Bevölkerungs- und Produktionsverhältnisse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX11","text":"Die von den Berichten erfasste Beteiligung der Arbeiterfamilien am Gangsystem gilt nicht als freie Zustimmung oder als Beweis autonomer moralischer Verderbtheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D1","text":"Flächenhafte Menschenentleerung und lokale Überfüllung der verbleibenden Dörfer sind komplementäre Wirkungen desselben Konzentrationsprozesses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D2","text":"Pauperisierung legitimiert Eviktion, Eviktion verschärft Wohnungsnot und Abhängigkeit, und diese Abhängigkeit befestigt den Mindestlohn.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D3","text":"Dieselbe Agrarbevölkerung ist für den durchschnittlichen Arbeitsbedarf zu zahlreich und für periodische Spitzen zu knapp.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D4","text":"Temporäre Arbeitsknappheit steigert unter verfügbarer Familienarbeit die Ausbeutungsintensität statt den Lohn.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D5","text":"Die Deckung des Zusatzbedarfs durch Frauen und Kinder erzeugt erneut männliche Überzähligkeit und erweitert damit die Reserve, auf die sie zurückgreift.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D6","text":"Das Gangsystem löst für das Agrarkapital den Widerspruch zwischen geringem permanentem Personal und jederzeit verfügbarer Zusatzarbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D7","text":"Irlands Bevölkerungsabnahme vermindert die relative Übervölkerung nicht, weil Konzentration, Weidewirtschaft und Verdrängung kleiner Pächter gleichzeitig fortschreiten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D8","text":"Ein sinkendes Gesamtprodukt kann mit steigenden und stärker konzentrierten Renten und Profiten koexistieren, wenn Mehrproduktanteil und Marktpreise wachsen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D9","text":"Die physische Masse landwirtschaftlicher Produktionsmittel kann abnehmen, während die Kapitalmasse wächst, sofern zuvor selbständig genutzte Mittel in Verwertungsmittel fremder Arbeit überführt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D10","text":"Rücküberweisungen der Ausgewanderten finanzieren weitere Auswanderung und machen den Bevölkerungsexodus selbstverstärkend.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D11","text":"Die durch Entvölkerung erzeugte Binnenmarktlücke trifft Kleinhändler, Handwerker und kleine Gewerbetreibende und liefert dem Proletariat neue Rekruten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12","text":"Die agrarisch verdrängte Bevölkerung verschwindet nicht aus dem System, sondern akkumuliert sich in Amerika als Träger einer gegen England gerichteten politischen Kraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1","text":"Relative Übervölkerung ist ein endogenes Regulationsprodukt der Akkumulation: Das Kapital erzeugt durch die Veränderung seiner Arbeitsnachfrage die Reserve, deren Vorhandensein es voraussetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2","text":"Die agrarische Arbeitsreserve wird durch das Zusammenwirken von Wohnraumentzug, saisonaler Nachfrage, Familienarbeit und mobiler Gangvermittlung räumlich und zeitlich produziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD3","text":"Entvölkerung kann eine Form kapitalistischer Akkumulation sein, wenn sie Konzentration, Kapitalisierung vormals selbständiger Produktionsmittel und Vergrößerung des Mehrproduktanteils vermittelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD4","text":"Der Fortbestand oder Zuwachs gesellschaftlichen Reichtums ist systematisch von der Reproduktion der arbeitenden Bevölkerung entkoppelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD5","text":"Die englisch-irische Arbeitsteilung externalisiert die menschlichen Kosten agrarischer Akkumulation nach Irland, während England Produkte und Rekruten erhält.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6","text":"Die territoriale Entfernung der Überzähligen löst den sozialen Widerspruch nicht, sondern überführt ihn in eine transatlantische politische Gegnerschaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD7","text":"Die durch das Arbeitsregime erzeugte Verwahrlosung kann ideologisch als Eigenschaft der Arbeiter zurückgedeutet und von ihren strukturellen Bedingungen abgelöst werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX1","text":"Der Arbeitsmarkt ist kein selbstkorrigierender Mechanismus, der Knappheit notwendig in steigende Löhne übersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX2","text":"Bevölkerung ist keine dem Kapital äußerliche biologische Größe, aus deren absolutem Umfang Beschäftigung und Elend folgen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX3","text":"Die nationale Bevölkerung ist keine homogene Einheit; Entvölkerung, Klassenkonzentration und relative Überzähligkeit können gleichzeitig zunehmen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX4","text":"Produktivitäts-, Renten- und Profitsteigerung sind keine Stellvertretergrößen für die Reproduktion der Produzenten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX5","text":"Eigentumsform und Verfügung über Produktionsmittel sind keine neutralen Zusätze zu deren physischer Existenz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX6","text":"Räumliche Entfernung beendet weder das Kapitalverhältnis noch dessen soziale und politische Folgen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX7","text":"Die Arbeitskräftefrage des Kapitals ist nicht mit dem gesellschaftlichen Bedarf an Arbeit oder Lebensmitteln identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX8","text":"Moralische Degradation besitzt innerhalb des Systems keine von Wohnungsnot, Arbeitszwang und Organisationsform unabhängige Kausalität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX1","text":"Ein stabiles demographisches Gleichgewicht ist innerhalb der Akkumulationsbewegung nicht verfügbar, weil jede Anpassung die Bedingungen neuer relativer Übervölkerung erzeugt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX2","text":"Das Rentenkriterium enthält keine positive Bestimmung einer hinreichenden Bevölkerung; jede verbleibende Bevölkerung kann erneut als überschüssig klassifiziert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX3","text":"Der arbeitenden Bevölkerung bleibt ein gesicherter Ort der Wohnung, Subsistenz und unabhängigen Reproduktion strukturell versperrt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX4","text":"Ein gemeinsames nationales Wohlergehen von Bodenbesitz, Kapital und Bevölkerung ist nicht voraussetzbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX5","text":"Für die Verdrängten existiert kein endgültiges territoriales Außen; die exportierte Bevölkerung kehrt als politisches Verhältnis zurück.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS1","text":"Akkumulation → Konzentration von Boden und Produktionsmitteln → Trennung der Produzenten von Subsistenzmitteln → relative Übervölkerung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS2","text":"Cottage-Abbau → räumliche Vertreibung → Verdichtung in offenen Ortschaften → Wohnungsnot → Abhängigkeit → Lohnfixierung am Minimum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS3","text":"Geringer Dauerbedarf + periodischer Spitzenbedarf → Rekrutierung von Frauen und Kindern → ausbleibende Lohnsteigerung → Verdrängung männlicher Arbeit → erneuerte Reserve.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS4","text":"Entfernte Arbeiterdörfer → Gangmeistervermittlung → Stücklohn und mobile Bande → maximale Arbeitsausgabe bei minimaler Bindung des Pächters → Reproduktion des Gangsystems.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS5","text":"Massenemigration + fortgesetzte Agrarrevolution → absolute Entvölkerung + unveränderte relative Übervölkerung → Widerlegung des absoluten Übervölkerungsmodells.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS6","text":"Pachtkonzentration + Verwandlung von Acker in Weide → sinkendes Gesamtprodukt + steigender Mehrproduktanteil + steigende Preise → wachsende Renten und Pachtprofite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS7","text":"Enteignung selbständiger Produzenten → Umwandlung ihrer Produktionsmittel in Verwertungsmittel fremder Arbeit → steigende Kapitalmasse relativ zur schrumpfenden Bevölkerung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS8","text":"Emigration → Rücküberweisungen → weitere Emigration → Binnenmarktkontraktion → Proletarisierung → Diasporabildung → politische Rückwirkung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF1","text":"Wohnungsstreit in Badsey → Zurückweisung der natürlichen Bevölkerungsattraktion → allgemeiner Zusammenhang von Eviktion und relativer Übervölkerung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF2","text":"Flächenhafte Entvölkerung → lokale Überfüllung → Pauperismus und Wohnungsnot → Befestigung des Mindestlohns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF3","text":"Gleichzeitiger Arbeitsüberschuss und saisonaler Arbeitsmangel → Frauen- und Kinderarbeit → Gangsystem → erneute männliche Überzähligkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF4","text":"Organisation und Wirkungen der Gangs → Bestimmung ihrer Klassenfunktion → billige flexible Arbeitsreserve für Großpächter und Grundeigentümer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF5","text":"Irische Bevölkerungs- und Produktionsdaten → steigende Renten trotz Entvölkerung → Widerlegung des malthusianischen Gleichgewichtsmodells.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF6","text":"Fortgesetzte Konzentration → Forderung weiterer Entvölkerung → Verwandlung Irlands in Weide- und Rekrutierungsgebiet → Fenianische Rückkehr des verdrängten Widerspruchs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME1","text":"Das Bevölkerungsproblem wird von einer absoluten Menschenzahl auf ein Verhältnis zwischen Arbeitskraft und Kapitalbedarf umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME2","text":"Untervölkerung, Arbeitsmangel und Übervölkerung werden als räumlich und zeitlich differenzierte Koexistenz statt als Gegensätze lesbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME3","text":"Wohnraum wird vom privaten Lebensumstand zum Instrument der Arbeitsmarktregulierung und Lohndisziplin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME4","text":"Frauen- und Kinderarbeit wird von bloßer Zusatzarbeit zu einem Mechanismus der Erzeugung männlicher Überzähligkeit umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME5","text":"Das Gangsystem wird von lokaler Verwahrlosung zu einer Institution kapitalistischer Arbeitskräftebeschaffung umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME6","text":"Entvölkerung erscheint nicht länger als Gegenteil, sondern als mögliche Vollzugsform der Akkumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME7","text":"Kapital wird von der physischen Masse der Produktionsmittel abgelöst und als gesellschaftliche Verwertungsform bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME8","text":"Irland wird nicht als geschlossene Nationalökonomie, sondern als funktional untergeordnetes Agrar- und Rekrutierungsgebiet Englands kartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME9","text":"Emigration wird von einem demographischen Sicherheitsventil zu einem rekursiven Export- und Konfliktverlagerungsprozess umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME10","text":"Agrarische Verbesserung und menschliche Degradation werden als komplementäre Produkte desselben Produktionsregimes sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Unmittelbare Gegenstände sind Cottage-Zerstörung, ländliche Überfüllung, Gangarbeit, irische Entvölkerung sowie die gegenläufige Bewegung von Produktion, Renten und Profiten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT2","text":"Structural — Der tragende Mechanismus verbindet Bodenkonzentration, wechselnde Arbeitsnachfrage, Wohnraumkontrolle, Familienarbeit, Kapitalisierung und Marktpreisbewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Empirische Widersprüche werden gegen die orthodoxe Erklärung aus absoluter Übervölkerung gewendet und als Wirkungen der Akkumulation rekonstruiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Kapital und Übervölkerung sind relationale Formen; durchschnittlicher und temporärer Arbeitsbedarf, absolute Abnahme und relative Zunahme sowie gegenwärtige Verdrängung und spätere politische Rückkehr operieren auf verschiedenen Zeitskalen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen zur Rekonstruktion der englischen Mechanismusanalyse, des Gangkreislaufs und des irischen Gegenexperiments aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT2","text":"Die quantitative Kalibrierung bleibt unterbestimmt, weil mehrere Tabellen im vorliegenden Quelltext ohne vollständige Datenkörper erscheinen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern relative Übervölkerung relational und Arbeitsmangel zeitlich beziehungsweise lokal bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT4","text":"Die größte Erklärungskraft liegt in der Auflösung der Gleichzeitigkeit von Arbeitsüberschuss und Arbeitsmangel sowie von Entvölkerung und Rentenwachstum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT5","text":"Der Übergang von beobachteten Korrelationen zu einer einheitlichen Kausalbewegung der Akkumulation komprimiert alternative Gewichtungen der beteiligten Mechanismen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT6","text":"Die Behauptung wachsender Kapitalmasse bei sinkender Masse von Produktionsmitteln hängt strikt von der Bestimmung des Kapitals als gesellschaftlichem Verwertungsverhältnis ab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT7","text":"Die moralisch aufgeladene Darstellung des Gangsystems überschreitet stellenweise dessen Funktionsanalyse, während die Berichte über strukturellen Zwang die Verantwortungszuschreibung wieder begrenzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT8","text":"Irlands Funktion als englisches Agrargebiet stützt die Akkumulationsdiagnose, macht den Fall aber nicht ohne Vermittlung mit einer selbständigen entwickelten kapitalistischen Ökonomie identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT9","text":"Die fenianische Schlusswendung ist eine strategische Konsequenz der Konfliktverlagerung, keine vollständig ausgearbeitete ökonomische Ableitung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT10","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn Wohnraummechanismus, Gangvermittlung, irische Entvölkerung, Kapitaldefinition und politische Rückwirkung gemeinsam erhalten bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211344105925Z_3fb2f43f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c) The general law of capitalist accumulation. · reading part 2/2","source_sha256":"b482e33b70518d981fa2b18022a94f3ceec29741890c6bcf44ab4ef256ed3311","sha256":"be675700246e88b7ec1acf90309a9b767370450367e6dc3d1b57dc069086ad7e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:13:44.107583+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS1","text":"What is to be explained is how depopulation, local housing scarcity, labour surplus, temporary labour shortage, and rising rents arise simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS2","text":"Relative overpopulation is redefined as the relation of the working population to capitalistically determined labour demand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds diagnostically, reconstructively, and polemically against the explanation of misery from absolute population size.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS4","text":"Concentration, agrarian restructuring, and the withdrawal of housing simultaneously produce spatial emptying, local densification, and wage pressure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS5","text":"The gang system mediates the contradiction between minimal permanent personnel and short-term additional demand through cheap, mobile women’s and children’s labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS6","text":"Ireland’s mass emigration functions as a counterexperiment: absolute depopulation eliminates neither relative overpopulation nor misery, while rents and concentrated capital grow.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7","text":"The movement leads from the English agrarian contradiction through its institutional mediation to the Irish refutation of the demographic equilibrium model and to the political return of the displaced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","text":"Relative overpopulation is a relation between available labour-power and capitalistically determined labour demand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","text":"The concentration of land and means of production separates producers from their means of employment and subsistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","text":"Capitalist agrarian restructuring reduces permanent labour-power requirements relative to land area and productive capacity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","text":"Control over cottages regulates the spatial availability, dependence, and capacity for resistance of agricultural labourers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","text":"Agrarian labour demand is temporally uneven and requires periodic additional labour amid low permanent demand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6","text":"Women’s and children’s labour covers temporary peaks in labour demand without compelling a corresponding rise in male wages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A7","text":"The expansion of women’s and children’s labour displaces male labour and reproduces wage pressure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","text":"The gang system transforms spatially dispersed family labour-power, through mediation and piece wages, into a mobile labour reserve.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9","text":"The gang system exists as a cost-reducing instrument of flexibility for large tenant farmers and landowners.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10","text":"The agrarian revolution can produce relative overpopulation more quickly than emigration reduces the absolute population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11","text":"Means of production become capital only through the incorporation of others’ labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12","text":"The mass of surplus product can grow while total product declines, if its share of total product rises.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A13","text":"Rising market prices can increase the monetary value of surplus product more rapidly than its physical mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","text":"Emigration is a recursive process of transfer and not a one-time annihilation of the displaced population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A15","text":"Absolute depopulation contracts the domestic market and proletarianizes parts of the petty middle class.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16","text":"Within the system under consideration, Ireland functions as England’s agrarian supply and recruitment territory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX1","text":"Cottages do not generate or attract the poor population by natural law; the absence of housing drives it out of places still more unfavourable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX2","text":"Sparsely populated districts are not free of relative overpopulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX3","text":"Temporary labour shortage does not necessarily lead to higher wages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX4","text":"The gang system does not exist for the sake of the gang-master.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX5","text":"The gang system is not a neutral response to a presupposed natural shortage of male labour; it also produces male unemployment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX6","text":"Workers’ misery cannot be derived from absolute overpopulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX7","text":"Absolute depopulation does not establish demographic-economic equilibrium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX8","text":"Means of production and products are not capital or commodity by virtue of their physical form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX9","text":"Rising ground-rent signifies neither the well-being of the soil nor the well-being of the population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX10","text":"The effects of a medieval plague provide no transferable model for capitalist population and production relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX11","text":"The participation of working families in the gang system recorded in the reports is not taken as free consent or as proof of autonomous moral depravity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D1","text":"Area-wide emptying of people and local overcrowding of the remaining villages are complementary effects of the same process of concentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D2","text":"Pauperization legitimates eviction, eviction intensifies housing scarcity and dependence, and this dependence consolidates the minimum wage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D3","text":"The same agrarian population is too numerous for average labour requirements and too scarce for periodic peaks.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D4","text":"Under available family labour, temporary labour scarcity increases the intensity of exploitation rather than wages.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D5","text":"Meeting additional demand through women and children produces male supernumerariness anew and thereby expands the reserve upon which it draws.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D6","text":"For agrarian capital, the gang system resolves the contradiction between low permanent personnel and additional labour available at any time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D7","text":"Ireland’s population decline does not reduce relative overpopulation because concentration, pasture farming, and the displacement of small tenant farmers advance simultaneously.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D8","text":"A declining total product can coexist with rising and more concentrated rents and profits if the surplus-product share and market prices grow.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D9","text":"The physical mass of agricultural means of production can decline while the mass of capital grows, provided means previously used independently are converted into means of valorizing others’ labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D10","text":"Remittances from emigrants finance further emigration and make the population exodus self-reinforcing.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D11","text":"The domestic-market gap produced by depopulation strikes small traders, artisans, and small business owners and supplies the proletariat with new recruits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12","text":"The agrarianly displaced population does not disappear from the system but accumulates in America as the bearer of a political force directed against England.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1","text":"Relative overpopulation is an endogenous regulatory product of accumulation: capital produces, by altering its labour demand, the reserve whose existence it presupposes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2","text":"The agrarian labour reserve is produced spatially and temporally by the interaction of withdrawal of housing, seasonal demand, family labour, and mobile gang mediation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD3","text":"Depopulation can be a form of capitalist accumulation if it mediates concentration, the capitalization of formerly independent means of production, and an enlargement of the surplus-product share.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD4","text":"The persistence or growth of social wealth is systematically decoupled from the reproduction of the working population.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD5","text":"The English-Irish division of labour externalizes the human costs of agrarian accumulation to Ireland, while England receives products and recruits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6","text":"The territorial removal of the supernumerary does not resolve the social contradiction but transforms it into transatlantic political antagonism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD7","text":"The neglect produced by the labour regime can ideologically be reinterpreted as a characteristic of the workers and detached from its structural conditions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0028","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX1","text":"The labour market is not a self-correcting mechanism that necessarily translates scarcity into rising wages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX2","text":"Population is not a biological magnitude external to capital, from whose absolute extent employment and misery follow.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX3","text":"The national population is not a homogeneous unit; depopulation, class concentration, and relative supernumerariness can increase simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX4","text":"Increases in productivity, rent, and profit are not proxy measures for the reproduction of producers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX5","text":"The form of property and control over means of production are not neutral additions to their physical existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX6","text":"Spatial removal ends neither the capital relation nor its social and political consequences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX7","text":"Capital’s question of labour-power is not identical with society’s need for labour or foodstuffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX8","text":"Within the system, moral degradation has no causality independent of housing scarcity, labour compulsion, and organizational form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX1","text":"A stable demographic equilibrium is unavailable within the movement of accumulation, because every adjustment produces the conditions of new relative overpopulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX2","text":"The criterion of rent contains no positive determination of a sufficient population; every remaining population can again be classified as superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX3","text":"A secured place of dwelling, subsistence, and independent reproduction remains structurally barred to the working population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX4","text":"A common national well-being of landed property, capital, and population cannot be presupposed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX5","text":"For the displaced, no final territorial outside exists; the exported population returns as a political relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS1","text":"Accumulation → concentration of land and means of production → separation of producers from means of subsistence → relative overpopulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS2","text":"Dismantling of cottages → spatial displacement → densification in open localities → housing scarcity → dependence → wage fixation at the minimum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS3","text":"Low permanent demand + periodic peak demand → recruitment of women and children → absent wage increase → displacement of male labour → renewed reserve.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS4","text":"Distant workers’ villages → gang-master mediation → piece wages and mobile gangs → maximum labour output with minimal commitment by the tenant farmer → reproduction of the gang system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS5","text":"Mass emigration + continued agrarian revolution → absolute depopulation + unchanged relative overpopulation → refutation of the absolute-overpopulation model.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS6","text":"Concentration of tenancies + transformation of arable land into pasture → declining total product + rising surplus-product share + rising prices → growing rents and tenant profits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS7","text":"Expropriation of independent producers → conversion of their means of production into means of valorizing others’ labour → rising mass of capital relative to the shrinking population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS8","text":"Emigration → remittances → further emigration → domestic-market contraction → proletarianization → formation of a diaspora → political repercussion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF1","text":"Housing dispute in Badsey → rejection of natural population attraction → general connection between eviction and relative overpopulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF2","text":"Area-wide depopulation → local overcrowding → pauperism and housing scarcity → consolidation of the minimum wage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF3","text":"Simultaneous labour surplus and seasonal labour shortage → women’s and children’s labour → gang system → renewed male supernumerariness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF4","text":"Organization and effects of the gangs → determination of their class function → cheap flexible labour reserve for large tenant farmers and landowners.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF5","text":"Irish population and production data → rising rents despite depopulation → refutation of the Malthusian equilibrium model.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:AF6","text":"Continued concentration → demand for further depopulation → transformation of Ireland into pasture and recruitment territory → Fenian return of the displaced contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME1","text":"The population problem is remapped from an absolute number of people onto a relation between labour-power and capital’s requirements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME2","text":"Underpopulation, labour shortage, and overpopulation become legible as spatially and temporally differentiated coexistence rather than opposites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME3","text":"Housing is transformed from a private circumstance of life into an instrument of labour-market regulation and wage discipline.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME4","text":"Women’s and children’s labour is reclassified from mere supplementary labour into a mechanism for producing male supernumerariness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME5","text":"The gang system is remapped from local neglect into an institution of capitalist labour-power procurement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME6","text":"Depopulation no longer appears as the opposite but as a possible mode of realization of accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME7","text":"Capital is detached from the physical mass of means of production and determined as a social form of valorization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME8","text":"Ireland is mapped not as a closed national economy but as a functionally subordinate agrarian and recruitment territory of England.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME9","text":"Emigration is reclassified from a demographic safety valve into a recursive process of export and displacement of conflict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME10","text":"Agrarian improvement and human degradation become visible as complementary products of the same regime of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Immediate objects are the destruction of cottages, rural overcrowding, gang labour, Irish depopulation, and the opposed movement of production, rents, and profits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT2","text":"Structural — The supporting mechanism connects land concentration, changing labour demand, housing control, family labour, capitalization, and market-price movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Empirical contradictions are turned against the orthodox explanation from absolute overpopulation and reconstructed as effects of accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Capital and overpopulation are relational forms; average and temporary labour requirements, absolute decrease and relative increase, as well as present displacement and later political return operate on different timescales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the English analysis of mechanisms, the gang cycle, and the Irish counterexperiment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT2","text":"Quantitative calibration remains underdetermined because several tables in the present source text appear without complete data bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent provided that relative overpopulation is understood relationally and labour shortage temporally or locally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT4","text":"The greatest explanatory force lies in resolving the simultaneity of labour surplus and labour shortage, as well as depopulation and rent growth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT5","text":"The transition from observed correlations to a unified causal movement of accumulation compresses alternative weightings of the mechanisms involved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT6","text":"The claim of a growing mass of capital amid a declining mass of means of production depends strictly on the determination of capital as a social valorization relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT7","text":"The morally charged presentation of the gang system at points exceeds its functional analysis, while the reports of structural compulsion in turn limit the attribution of responsibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT8","text":"Ireland’s function as an English agrarian territory supports the diagnosis of accumulation, but does not render the case identical, without mediation, to an independent developed capitalist economy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT9","text":"The Fenian concluding turn is a strategic consequence of the displacement of conflict, not a fully elaborated economic derivation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if the housing mechanism, gang mediation, Irish depopulation, definition of capital, and political repercussion are retained together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_V4GB_CD_2:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]}],"revision":"CH_V4GB_CD_2@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_V4GB_CD_2:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 21","title":"c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 2/2","context":"Chapter 21"}},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG","layer":"CH","title":"2) Die s. g. Ursprüngliche Accumulation.","order":22,"parents":["RAW_V4GB_2DSG"],"revision":"CH_V4GB_2DSG@R001","sha256":"35da32d3916f6ff2bb19141799a157697396349c88e716ae57ee8cfacd441e51","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS1","text":"Die wechselseitige Voraussetzung von Akkumulation, Mehrwert, kapitalistischer Produktion und vorhandenen Kapitalmassen erzwingt eine Erklärung der historischen Genesis des Kapitalverhältnisses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2","text":"Die politische Ökonomie verdeckt diese Genesis durch eine moralische Ursprungserzählung von Fleiß, Sparsamkeit und selbstverschuldeter Armut.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS3","text":"Die sogenannte ursprüngliche Akkumulation wird als historischer Scheidungsprozess von Produzenten und Produktionsmitteln neu bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4","text":"Die englische Entwicklung dient als klassische Rekonstruktion der gewaltsamen Erzeugung von Grundeigentum, Kapital, Lohnarbeit und innerem Markt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS5","text":"Das Argument ist genealogisch in der Herleitung, diagnostisch in der Analyse des Kapitalverhältnisses, polemisch gegen dessen Ursprungsmythos und dialektisch in seiner Endbewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS6","text":"Die Bewegung führt von der Expropriation über staatliche Disziplinierung und globale Kapitalbildung zur selbsttätigen Reproduktion kapitalistischer Abhängigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS7","text":"Die erste Expropriation erzeugt kapitalistisches Privateigentum; dessen Konzentration und Vergesellschaftung erzeugen die Bedingungen einer zweiten, gegen die Expropriateure gerichteten Expropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","text":"Kapitalistische Akkumulation setzt Mehrwert, kapitalistische Produktion und bereits vorhandene größere Kapitalmassen voraus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","text":"Geld, Waren, Produktionsmittel und Lebensmittel sind nicht an sich Kapital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","text":"Kapital entsteht nur durch die Polarität zwischen Eigentümern der Verwertungsmittel und Verkäufern der Arbeitskraft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","text":"Der Lohnarbeiter ist doppelt frei: rechtlich unveräußerlich und materiell von den Verwirklichungsbedingungen seiner Arbeit getrennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","text":"Die sogenannte ursprüngliche Akkumulation ist der historische Scheidungsprozess von Produzent und Produktionsmittel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","text":"Die Auflösung feudaler Abhängigkeit beseitigt persönliche Knechtschaft, kann aber zugleich deren kapitalistischen Formwechsel vollziehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","text":"Die Expropriation der Arbeiter von Grund und Boden bildet die Grundlage des gesamten Scheidungsprozesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","text":"Die entscheidenden Gründungsoperationen des Kapitalverhältnisses beruhen auf Eroberung, Enteignung, Terror, Rechtsumbau und organisierter Staatsgewalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","text":"Die etablierte kapitalistische Produktion reproduziert die ursprüngliche Scheidung auf wachsender Stufenleiter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","text":"Die Expropriation erzeugt zunächst mehr eigentumslose Menschen, als die entstehende Manufaktur absorbieren kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","text":"Terroristische Gesetzgebung verwandelt die expropriierte und kriminalisierte Bevölkerung in disziplinierte Lohnarbeiter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","text":"Unmittelbare Staatsgewalt normalisiert das entstehende Lohnverhältnis; im entwickelten Kapitalismus wird sie im gewöhnlichen Betrieb durch den stummen Zwang der ökonomischen Verhältnisse ersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","text":"Die Agrarrevolution konzentriert Boden und Produktion, erzeugt den Kapitalpächter und bereichert ihn durch dieselbe Bewegung, die das Landvolk verarmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","text":"Die Expropriation setzt Arbeitskräfte, Lebensmittel und Rohstoffe als Kapitalelemente frei und erzeugt durch Zerstörung ländlicher Selbstversorgung den inneren Markt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15","text":"Die Auflösung feudaler und zünftiger Schranken sowie Kolonialsystem, Staatsschuld, Steuern, Protektion und Handelskrieg beschleunigen die Bildung industriellen Kapitals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","text":"Kapitalistisches Privateigentum ist die Negation des auf eigener Arbeit und eigenen Produktionsmitteln beruhenden individuellen Privateigentums.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","text":"Die Konzentration der Kapitalien vergesellschaftet Arbeit und Produktionsmittel, reduziert die Zahl der Kapitalmagnaten und vereinigt zugleich die wachsende Arbeiterklasse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","text":"Die Unvereinbarkeit vergesellschafteter Produktion mit kapitalistischem Monopol erzeugt die Expropriation der Expropriateure und Gemeineigentum auf Grundlage freier Kooperation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX1","text":"Ursprüngliche Akkumulation ist nicht das Ergebnis bloßen Fleißes, Sparens oder moralisch ungleicher Lebensführung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX2","text":"Kapital ist kein natürlicher Sachcharakter von Geld, Waren oder Produktionsmitteln.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX3","text":"Der freie Arbeiter ist weder Sklave noch unabhängiger Eigentümer seiner Arbeitsbedingungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX4","text":"Recht und Arbeit sind nicht die ausschließlichen historischen Bereicherungsmittel.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX5","text":"Die Aufhebung feudaler Bindungen ist nicht mit der Herstellung materieller Unabhängigkeit identisch.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX6","text":"Pauperisierung folgt nicht notwendig aus der Abschaffung der Leibeigenschaft, sondern aus der Trennung der Produzenten von Grund und Produktionsmitteln.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX7","text":"Vagabundage und Pauperismus sind nicht primär freiwillige Abweichungen, sondern Folgen gewaltsamer Expropriation und unzureichender Absorption.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX8","text":"Nationalreichtum ist nicht mit dem Wohlstand der Volksmasse identisch.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX9","text":"Der innere Markt entsteht nicht allein durch spontane Ausweitung des Tauschs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX10","text":"Die Genesis des industriellen Kapitalisten ist nicht hinreichend aus der allmählichen Bereicherung kleiner Meister und Handwerker erklärbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX11","text":"Die entwickelte Herrschaft des Kapitals beruht im gewöhnlichen Betrieb nicht hauptsächlich auf offener physischer Gewalt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX12","text":"Die Negation kapitalistischen Privateigentums ist keine Rückkehr zum zersplitterten Kleinbetrieb.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D1","text":"Die historische Genesis des Kapitals ist die Erzeugung eines Klassenverhältnisses, nicht die bloße Anhäufung eines Sachbestands.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D2","text":"Rechtliche Emanzipation und materielle Proletarisierung können zwei Seiten desselben Übergangs sein.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D3","text":"Die Scheidung verwandelt gleichzeitig Produktionsmittel in Kapital und unmittelbare Produzenten in Verkäufer von Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D4","text":"Staatsgewalt ist ein konstitutives Produktionsmittel der kapitalistischen Genesis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D5","text":"Der Übergang von offenem Terror zu ökonomischem Zwang bezeichnet den Übergang von der Herstellung zur routinemäßigen Reproduktion des Kapitalverhältnisses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D6","text":"Agrarische Produktivitätssteigerung, Konzentration des Bodens und Verarmung der Produzenten werden als Wirkungen desselben Umwandlungsprozesses erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D7","text":"Der innere Markt wird durch die Vernichtung nichtmarktlicher Selbstversorgung und ländlicher Nebenproduktion hergestellt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D8","text":"Die agrarische Expropriation erzeugt neben dem Proletariat einen verwertenden Pächterpol.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D9","text":"Globale Plünderung und staatlich organisierte Transfers überbrücken die zeitliche und quantitative Grenze der graduellen Kapitalbildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D10","text":"Das Recht schützt angeeignete Eigentumstitel und kriminalisiert zugleich die Widerstands- und Koalitionsformen der expropriierten Arbeiter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D11","text":"Ursprüngliche Expropriation und spätere Kapitalkonzentration sind verschiedene historische Formen derselben Trennung und Aneignungsbewegung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D12","text":"Die als Objekt von Enteignung und Disziplinierung erzeugte Arbeiterklasse wird durch kapitalistische Vergesellschaftung zum möglichen Subjekt der Gegenexpropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13","text":"Gesellschaftliches Eigentum übernimmt die kooperative Produktivkraft des Kapitalismus, ohne dessen private Aneignungsform zu bewahren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","text":"Die ursprüngliche Akkumulation ist zeitlich Vorgeschichte, aber ihre Scheidung wird zur permanenten Reproduktionsbedingung des entwickelten Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD2","text":"Die formale Gleichheit des Arbeitsvertrags setzt eine historisch ungleiche Verteilung der Bedingungen voraus, unter denen dieser Vertrag geschlossen wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD3","text":"Politischer Zwang und ökonomischer Zwang bilden keine getrennten Erklärungen, sondern aufeinanderfolgende Betriebsweisen derselben Klassenherrschaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD4","text":"Kapitalreichtum und Volksarmut sind nicht bloß gleichzeitig, sondern werden durch die Konzentration derselben Produktionsbedingungen gemeinsam erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD5","text":"Außereuropäische Plünderung und unverhüllte Sklaverei werden in Europa als Kapital, Kredit, Manufaktur und verhüllte Lohnabhängigkeit internalisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD6","text":"Die erfolgreiche Entwicklung des Kapitals erzeugt durch Konzentration, Kooperation und Organisation die gesellschaftliche Form, die seiner privaten Aneignung widerspricht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX1","text":"Kapital und Lohnarbeit besitzen keine transhistorische Natürlichkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX2","text":"Eine vorpolitische, von Staatsgewalt unabhängige kapitalistische Ökonomie ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX3","text":"Eigentumsrecht und Arbeitsrecht fungieren nicht als neutrale Formen zwischen bereits gleichgestellten Parteien.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX4","text":"Freiheit ist nicht auf rechtliche Selbstverfügung reduzierbar, solange die Verfügung über die Arbeitsbedingungen ausgeschlossen bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX5","text":"Die europäische Kapitalbildung ist nicht von kolonialer Enteignung, Sklaverei und globalem Gewalttransfer isolierbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX6","text":"Dauerhafte Vereinbarkeit gesellschaftlicher Produktion mit monopolistischer Privatan­eignung ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX1","text":"Das System verweigert dem Kapital einen unschuldigen, aus seinen eigenen Rechtsformen ableitbaren Ursprung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX2","text":"Eine materielle Freiheit der Lohnarbeit ohne vorgängige Verfügung über Produktionsbedingungen bleibt innerhalb des Kapitalverhältnisses versperrt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX3","text":"Eine stationäre Endform des Kapitalismus ist ausgeschlossen, weil seine Reproduktion Konzentration, Vergesellschaftung und Gegenorganisation steigert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX4","text":"Die Rückkehr zur vorkapitalistischen Zersplitterung ist als Lösung versperrt; verfügbar bleibt nur eine Aufhebung, welche die erzeugte gesellschaftliche Kooperation erhält.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS1","text":"Akkumulation → Mehrwert → kapitalistische Produktion → vorausgesetzte Kapitalmassen → historische Anfangsfrage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS2","text":"Geld, Ware und Produktionsmittel ≠ Kapital; Kapital entsteht erst durch die Gegenüberstellung von Verwertungsmitteln und eigentumsloser Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS3","text":"Scheidung von Produzent und Produktionsmittel → Produktionsmittel werden Kapital → Produzent wird Lohnarbeiter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS4","text":"Auflösung feudaler Bindungen + Landexpropriation + Enclosure + Kirchengut- und Staatslandraub + Clearing → agrarische Eigentumskonzentration und vogelfreies Proletariat.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS5","text":"Expropriierte Bevölkerung > anfängliche Absorptionskapazität → Vagabundage und Pauperismus → Kriminalisierung → terroristische Lohndisziplin.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS6","text":"Staatliche Lohn- und Koalitionsregulation → normalisierte Abhängigkeit → relative Überbevölkerung und ökonomischer Zwang → selbsttätige Reproduktion des Lohnverhältnisses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS7","text":"Agrarische Konzentration → Kapitalpächter + freigesetzte Lebensmittel und Rohstoffe + zerstörte Selbstversorgung → industrieller innerer Markt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS8","text":"Entschränkung von Wucher- und Kaufmannskapital + koloniale Plünderung + Staatsschuld + Steuern + Protektion + Handelskrieg → beschleunigte Genesis industriellen Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS9","text":"Kapitalistische Konzentration → Vergesellschaftung der Arbeit → Monopolisierung der Aneignung + Organisation der Arbeiterklasse → Unvereinbarkeit von Produktionsform und Eigentumshülle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS10","text":"Erste Negation des Arbeitseigentums durch Kapital → immanente Negation des Kapitaleigentums → Expropriation weniger Expropriateure → Gemeineigentum kooperierender freier Arbeiter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AF1","text":"Zirkuläre Voraussetzung der Akkumulation → Demontage des Sparmythos → relationale Bestimmung des Kapitals → historische Bestimmung der ursprünglichen Akkumulation als Scheidung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AF2","text":"Landexpropriation → doppelt freie Arbeiter → überschüssiges Proletariat → staatliche Lohndisziplin → Kapitalpächter und innerer Markt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AF3","text":"Globale und staatliche Kapitalbildung → selbstreproduzierendes Kapitalverhältnis → Konzentration und Vergesellschaftung → kapitalistische Eigentumsschranke → Expropriation der Expropriateure.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME1","text":"Akkumulation wird von einer quantitativen Anhäufung zu einer qualitativen Herstellung gesellschaftlicher Klassenpole umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","text":"Der freie Arbeiter wird von einem unabhängigen Vertragssubjekt zu einem doppelt freien, durch Eigentumslosigkeit bestimmten Subjekt umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME3","text":"Feudale Emanzipation wird zugleich als Aufhebung persönlicher Unfreiheit und als Übergang zu unpersönlicher Abhängigkeit lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME4","text":"Privateigentum zerfällt in Arbeitseigentum und kapitalistisches Eigentum; die abstrakte Einheit des Eigentumsbegriffs wird aufgehoben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME5","text":"Gewalt, Gesetz und Staat wechseln von äußeren Störungen des Marktes zu konstitutiven Bedingungen seiner kapitalistischen Form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME6","text":"Der Markt erscheint nicht als vorausgesetzter Raum, sondern als Produkt der Zerstörung unmittelbarer Subsistenz- und Produktionszusammenhänge.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME7","text":"Nationalreichtum und Volksarmut wechseln von Gegensätzen zu komplementären Resultaten kapitalistischer Konzentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME8","text":"Koloniale Gewalt, Sklaverei, Staatsschuld und europäische Lohnarbeit werden in einer gemeinsamen Akkumulationsarchitektur verknüpft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME9","text":"Expropriation erhält zwei entgegengesetzte historische Vektoren: Enteignung der Volksmasse durch wenige und Enteignung weniger Kapitalmonopolisten durch die organisierte Volksmasse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der unmittelbare Gegenstand sind die historischen Verfahren der Landenteignung, Lohndisziplinierung, Kapitalistenbildung und kolonialen Akkumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die historischen Verfahren erzeugen und reproduzieren die Polarität von Kapitalbesitz und eigentumsloser Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Die Genealogie entzieht dem kapitalistischen Eigentum seine moralische Ursprungserzählung und verlagert die Eigentumsfrage auf Expropriation, Klassenmacht und Gegenexpropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Kapital gilt als historisches Verhältnis mit den Phasen gewaltsamer Genesis, selbsttätiger Reproduktion und immanent erzeugter Negation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Bewegung von der Ursprungsfrage über Scheidung, Disziplin und Kapitalbildung bis zur zweiten Expropriation zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die rein ökonomischen Agentien der Agrarrevolution, die mittelalterlichen Übergangsformen und die länderspezifischen Abweichungen vom englischen Verlauf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern Kapital konsequent als reproduziertes gesellschaftliches Verhältnis und nicht als vorgängiger Sachbestand behandelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Verknüpfung liegt in der Ableitung beider Kapitalpole, des inneren Marktes und der Lohndisziplin aus demselben Scheidungsprozess.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT5","text":"Die zeitliche Unterscheidung zwischen unmittelbarer Staatsgewalt und späterem ökonomischem Zwang vermittelt beide Mechanismen, bestimmt aber den Umschlagspunkt nicht exakt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT6","text":"Eine Bruchlinie besteht zwischen der historischen Vielfalt und Kontingenz der Expropriationsmethoden und der abschließenden Darstellung der zweiten Negation als naturprozessuale Notwendigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT7","text":"Das auf eigener Arbeit beruhende Kleineigentum fungiert zugleich als Bedingung freier Individualität und als produktiv begrenzte Form, deren notwendige Vernichtung behauptet wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT8","text":"Die historische Genealogie belegt die erste Expropriation ausführlicher als die terminale Expropriation; deren Notwendigkeit hängt stärker an der komprimierten Theorie von Konzentration, Vergesellschaftung und organisierter Gegenmacht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT9","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung, wenn der historische Katalog als Funktionsfolge von Scheidung, Kapitalisierung, Disziplinierung, Reproduktion und Negation erhalten bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T210746096207Z_39288f97","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"2) So-Called Primitive Accumulation.","source_sha256":"35da32d3916f6ff2bb19141799a157697396349c88e716ae57ee8cfacd441e51","sha256":"5a806baf60ed1cf30db9cafef48f521a4bc8bea28467fbf10166ae1a7386f4ea","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:07:46.097837+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS1","text":"The reciprocal presupposition of accumulation, surplus value, capitalist production, and existing masses of capital compels an explanation of the historical genesis of the capital relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2","text":"Political economy conceals this genesis through a moral origin narrative of diligence, thrift, and self-incurred poverty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS3","text":"So-called primitive accumulation is redefined as the historical process of separation of producers from the means of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4","text":"English development serves as a classical reconstruction of the violent production of landed property, capital, wage labour, and the internal market.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS5","text":"The argument is genealogical in its derivation, diagnostic in its analysis of the capital relation, polemical against its myth of origin, and dialectical in its final movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS6","text":"The movement leads from expropriation, through state disciplining and global capital formation, to the automatic reproduction of capitalist dependency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS7","text":"The first expropriation produces capitalist private property; its concentration and socialization produce the conditions of a second expropriation directed against the expropriators.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","text":"Capitalist accumulation presupposes surplus value, capitalist production, and already existing larger masses of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","text":"Money, commodities, means of production, and means of subsistence are not capital in themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","text":"Capital arises only through the polarity between owners of the means of valorization and sellers of labour-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","text":"The wage labourer is doubly free: legally inalienable and materially separated from the conditions for realizing his labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","text":"So-called primitive accumulation is the historical process of separation of producer and means of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","text":"The dissolution of feudal dependency abolishes personal servitude, but can at the same time effect its capitalist change of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","text":"The expropriation of workers from land forms the basis of the entire process of separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","text":"The decisive founding operations of the capital relation rest on conquest, dispossession, terror, legal transformation, and organized state power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","text":"Established capitalist production reproduces the original separation on an expanding scale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","text":"Expropriation initially produces more propertyless people than the emerging manufactory can absorb.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","text":"Terroristic legislation transforms the expropriated and criminalized population into disciplined wage labourers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","text":"Direct state power normalizes the emerging wage relation; in developed capitalism it is replaced in ordinary operation by the mute compulsion of economic relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","text":"The agricultural revolution concentrates land and production, produces the capitalist tenant farmer, and enriches him through the same movement that impoverishes the rural population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","text":"Expropriation sets labour-power, means of subsistence, and raw materials free as elements of capital and produces the internal market through the destruction of rural self-sufficiency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15","text":"The dissolution of feudal and guild barriers, together with the colonial system, state debt, taxes, protection, and commercial war, accelerates the formation of industrial capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","text":"Capitalist private property is the negation of individual private property based on one's own labour and one's own means of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","text":"The concentration of capitals socializes labour and means of production, reduces the number of capital magnates, and at the same time unites the growing working class.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","text":"The incompatibility of socialized production with capitalist monopoly produces the expropriation of the expropriators and common property on the basis of free cooperation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX1","text":"Primitive accumulation is not the result of mere diligence, saving, or morally unequal conduct of life.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX2","text":"Capital is not a natural material character of money, commodities, or means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX3","text":"The free worker is neither a slave nor the independent owner of his conditions of labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX4","text":"Law and labour are not the exclusive historical means of enrichment.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX5","text":"The abolition of feudal ties is not identical with the production of material independence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX6","text":"Pauperization does not necessarily follow from the abolition of serfdom, but from the separation of producers from land and means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX7","text":"Vagrancy and pauperism are not primarily voluntary deviations, but consequences of violent expropriation and insufficient absorption.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX8","text":"National wealth is not identical with the prosperity of the mass of the people.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX9","text":"The internal market does not arise solely through the spontaneous expansion of exchange.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX10","text":"The genesis of the industrial capitalist cannot be sufficiently explained by the gradual enrichment of small masters and artisans.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX11","text":"The developed domination of capital does not rest in ordinary operation principally on open physical violence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX12","text":"The negation of capitalist private property is not a return to fragmented small-scale enterprise.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D1","text":"The historical genesis of capital is the production of a class relation, not the mere accumulation of a stock of things.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D2","text":"Legal emancipation and material proletarianization can be two sides of the same transition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D3","text":"The separation simultaneously transforms means of production into capital and immediate producers into sellers of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D4","text":"State power is a constitutive means of production of capitalist genesis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D5","text":"The transition from open terror to economic compulsion marks the transition from the production to the routine reproduction of the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D6","text":"Agricultural productivity increases, concentration of land, and impoverishment of producers are produced as effects of the same process of transformation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D7","text":"The internal market is produced through the destruction of non-market self-sufficiency and rural subsidiary production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D8","text":"Agrarian expropriation produces, alongside the proletariat, a valorizing pole of tenant farmers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D9","text":"Global plunder and state-organized transfers bridge the temporal and quantitative limit of gradual capital formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D10","text":"Law protects appropriated titles to property and simultaneously criminalizes the forms of resistance and coalition of expropriated workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D11","text":"Original expropriation and later capital concentration are different historical forms of the same movement of separation and appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D12","text":"The working class, produced as an object of dispossession and disciplining, becomes through capitalist socialization the possible subject of counter-expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13","text":"Social property takes over the cooperative productive power of capitalism without preserving its form of private appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","text":"Primitive accumulation is temporally prehistory, but its separation becomes a permanent condition of reproduction of developed capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD2","text":"The formal equality of the labour contract presupposes a historically unequal distribution of the conditions under which this contract is concluded.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD3","text":"Political compulsion and economic compulsion do not constitute separate explanations, but successive modes of operation of the same class domination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD4","text":"Capital wealth and popular poverty are not merely simultaneous, but are jointly produced through the concentration of the same conditions of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD5","text":"Non-European plunder and undisguised slavery are internalized in Europe as capital, credit, manufacture, and disguised wage dependency.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD6","text":"The successful development of capital produces, through concentration, cooperation, and organization, the social form that contradicts its private appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX1","text":"Capital and wage labour possess no transhistorical naturalness.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX2","text":"A pre-political capitalist economy independent of state power is excluded.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX3","text":"Property law and labour law do not function as neutral forms between parties already placed on an equal footing.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX4","text":"Freedom cannot be reduced to legal self-disposal so long as disposal over the conditions of labour remains excluded.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX5","text":"European capital formation cannot be isolated from colonial dispossession, slavery, and global transfers of violence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX6","text":"The lasting compatibility of social production with monopolistic private appropriation is excluded.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX1","text":"The system denies capital an innocent origin derivable from its own legal forms.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX2","text":"A material freedom of wage labour without prior disposal over conditions of production remains barred within the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX3","text":"A stationary final form of capitalism is excluded, because its reproduction increases concentration, socialization, and counter-organization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX4","text":"Return to pre-capitalist fragmentation is barred as a solution; only a supersession remains available that preserves the social cooperation produced.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS1","text":"Accumulation → surplus value → capitalist production → presupposed masses of capital → historical question of beginnings.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS2","text":"Money, commodity, and means of production ≠ capital; capital arises only through the confrontation of means of valorization and propertyless labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS3","text":"Separation of producer and means of production → means of production become capital → producer becomes wage labourer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS4","text":"Dissolution of feudal ties + land expropriation + Enclosure + plunder of Church property and state lands + Clearing → agrarian concentration of property and outlawed proletariat.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS5","text":"Expropriated population > initial absorption capacity → vagrancy and pauperism → criminalization → terroristic wage discipline.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS6","text":"State regulation of wages and coalitions → normalized dependency → relative surplus population and economic compulsion → automatic reproduction of the wage relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS7","text":"Agrarian concentration → capitalist tenant farmer + released means of subsistence and raw materials + destroyed self-sufficiency → industrial internal market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS8","text":"Removal of restrictions on usurer's and merchant's capital + colonial plunder + state debt + taxes + protection + commercial war → accelerated genesis of industrial capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS9","text":"Capitalist concentration → socialization of labour → monopolization of appropriation + organization of the working class → incompatibility of form of production and property shell.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:FGS10","text":"First negation of property based on labour by capital → immanent negation of capital property → expropriation of few expropriators → common property of cooperating free workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AF1","text":"Circular presupposition of accumulation → dismantling of the myth of saving → relational determination of capital → historical determination of primitive accumulation as separation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AF2","text":"Land expropriation → doubly free workers → surplus proletariat → state wage discipline → capitalist tenant farmers and internal market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:AF3","text":"Global and state capital formation → self-reproducing capital relation → concentration and socialization → capitalist property barrier → expropriation of the expropriators.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME1","text":"Accumulation is remapped from a quantitative amassing into a qualitative production of social class poles.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","text":"The free worker is reclassified from an independent contractual subject into a doubly free subject determined by propertylessness.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME3","text":"Feudal emancipation becomes readable simultaneously as the abolition of personal unfreedom and as transition to impersonal dependency.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME4","text":"Private property divides into property based on labour and capitalist property; the abstract unity of the concept of property is aufgehoben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME5","text":"Violence, law, and state shift from external disturbances of the market to constitutive conditions of its capitalist form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME6","text":"The market appears not as a presupposed space, but as the product of the destruction of immediate contexts of subsistence and production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME7","text":"National wealth and popular poverty shift from opposites to complementary results of capitalist concentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME8","text":"Colonial violence, slavery, state debt, and European wage labour are linked within a common architecture of accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME9","text":"Expropriation receives two opposed historical vectors: dispossession of the mass of the people by the few and dispossession of few capital monopolists by the organized mass of the people.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT1","text":"Surface — The immediate object is the historical procedures of land dispossession, wage disciplining, capitalist formation, and colonial accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A13","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT2","text":"Structural — The historical procedures produce and reproduce the polarity of capital ownership and propertyless labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A3","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The genealogy deprives capitalist property of its moral origin narrative and shifts the property question to expropriation, class power, and counter-expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A5","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Capital is understood as a historical relation with the phases of violent genesis, automatic reproduction, and immanently produced negation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the movement from the question of origins through separation, discipline, and capital formation to the second expropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT2","text":"What remains underdetermined are the purely economic agencies of the agricultural revolution, the medieval transitional forms, and country-specific deviations from the English course.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent insofar as capital is consistently treated as a reproduced social relation and not as a pre-existing stock of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT4","text":"The strongest linkage lies in deriving both poles of capital, the internal market, and wage discipline from the same process of separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT5","text":"The temporal distinction between direct state power and later economic compulsion mediates both mechanisms, but does not determine the point of transition exactly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT6","text":"A line of rupture exists between the historical diversity and contingency of the methods of expropriation and the concluding presentation of the second negation as a necessity analogous to a natural process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT7","text":"Small property based on one's own labour functions simultaneously as a condition of free individuality and as a productively limited form whose necessary destruction is asserted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT8","text":"The historical genealogy substantiates the first expropriation more extensively than the terminal expropriation; the necessity of the latter depends more strongly on the compressed theory of concentration, socialization, and organized counter-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement if the historical catalogue is retained as a functional sequence of separation, capitalization, disciplining, reproduction, and negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CH_V4GB_2DSG@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_V4GB_2DSG:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 22","title":"2) Die s. g. Ursprüngliche Accumulation.","context":"Chapter 22"}},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK","layer":"CH","title":"3) Die moderne Kolonisationstheorie.","order":23,"parents":["RAW_V4GB_3DMK"],"revision":"CH_V4GB_3DMK@R001","sha256":"7ea094fadb87555c07cd1286ca3d3cd035dccd758e7b054525cb0298fe78c87a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS1","text":"Die politische Ökonomie verdeckt den Gegensatz zwischen auf eigener Arbeit beruhendem Privateigentum und kapitalistischem Privateigentum durch deren begriffliche Gleichsetzung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2","text":"Die Argumentation ist diagnostisch und rekonstruktiv, weil sie die freie Kolonie als praktischen Prüfbereich für die im Mutterland verdeckten Voraussetzungen des Kapitals verwendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS3","text":"Die freie Kolonie legt offen, dass Geld, Produktionsmittel und Boden ohne eine beständige Klasse lohnabhängiger Arbeiter kein Kapitalverhältnis erzeugen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4","text":"Der freie Zugang zu Boden ermöglicht den Austritt aus der Lohnarbeit und unterbricht damit die Reproduktion von Arbeitsmarkt, kombinierter Arbeit und kapitalistischer Akkumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS5","text":"Wakefields systematische Kolonisation soll diese Unterbrechung durch staatlich erzeugte Bodenschranken und regulierten Arbeiterimport in künstliche Lohnabhängigkeit übersetzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS6","text":"Die Kolonie enthüllt damit, dass kapitalistische Produktion und Akkumulation die Expropriation des selbstarbeitenden Produzenten voraussetzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS7","text":"Die Schlussbewegung überführt die Analyse von der Herstellung mehrwerttragender Waren zur notwendigen Realisation ihres Werts im Zirkulationsprozess des Kapitals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","text":"Auf eigener Arbeit beruhendes Privateigentum und kapitalistisches Privateigentum sind entgegengesetzte Aneignungsweisen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","text":"Kapital ist kein Gegenstand, sondern ein durch Gegenstände vermitteltes gesellschaftliches Verhältnis zwischen Personen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","text":"Kapital setzt die Existenz von Arbeitern voraus, die zum Verkauf ihrer Arbeitskraft gezwungen sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","text":"Die Expropriation der Produzenten von ihren Arbeitsbedingungen und vom Boden begründet kapitalistische Produktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","text":"In der freien Kolonie bleibt Boden allgemein zugänglich und kann von Ansiedlern in eigenes Produktionsmittel verwandelt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","text":"Der Zugang zu eigenem Boden erlaubt dem Lohnarbeiter, die Lohnarbeit zu verlassen und unabhängiger Produzent zu werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","text":"Kapitalistische Akkumulation reproduziert die Lohnarbeiterklasse und eine relative Übervölkerung, um soziale Abhängigkeit und Arbeitszufuhr zu sichern.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8","text":"Die politische Ökonomie stellt die soziale Abhängigkeit des Lohnarbeiters als freies Vertragsverhältnis gleicher Warenbesitzer dar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9","text":"Wakefields systematische Kolonisation verwendet künstlich verteuerten Boden und Arbeiterimport, um eine beständige Lohnarbeiterklasse herzustellen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10","text":"Das unmittelbare Produkt kapitalistischer Produktion ist eine mehrwerttragende Ware, deren Wert erst durch Verkauf realisiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX1","text":"Kapitalistisches Privateigentum ist nicht die Fortsetzung des auf eigener Arbeit beruhenden Privateigentums.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX2","text":"Geld, Maschinen, Lebensmittel und Produktionsmittel sind nicht schon als Dinge Kapital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX3","text":"Produktionsmittel im Eigentum ihrer unmittelbaren Produzenten sind nicht kapitalistische Produktionsmittel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX4","text":"Der Lohnvertrag ist nicht materiell ein Verhältnis gleicher Unabhängigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX5","text":"Bevölkerungswachstum erzeugt nicht notwendig eine verlässliche Zufuhr von Lohnarbeitern.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX6","text":"Naturwüchsige Kolonisation ist nicht mit systematischer kapitalistischer Kolonisation identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX7","text":"Der ausreichende Bodenpreis ist nicht durch Nachfrage und Zufuhr bestimmter Marktpreis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX8","text":"Nationalreichtum ist nicht mit dem Wohlstand der arbeitenden Bevölkerung identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX9","text":"Kapitalistische Kooperation ist nicht eine technisch neutrale Form gemeinsamer Arbeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX10","text":"Die Trennung von Kapital- und Arbeitseigentümern ist nicht Ergebnis freiwilliger Selbstexpropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D1","text":"Die freie Kolonie macht den Gegensatz zwischen selbstarbeitendem und kapitalistischem Privateigentum praktisch sichtbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D2","text":"Mitgebrachte Geldmittel und Produktionsmittel bleiben funktionslos als Kapital, wenn keine dauerhaft verfügbare Lohnarbeit existiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D3","text":"Solange Arbeiter ihre eigenen Produktionsmittel besitzen oder erwerben können, fehlt die für kapitalistische Akkumulation notwendige Klasse der Lohnarbeiter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D4","text":"Die fehlende Trennung des Produzenten vom Boden verhindert zugleich die dauerhafte Scheidung von Agrikultur und Industrie sowie die Ausbildung eines inneren Kapitalmarkts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D5","text":"Die Möglichkeit des Übergangs in unabhängige Produktion macht Lohnarbeit unsicher, verteuert sie und hemmt langfristige kapitalistische Unternehmungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D6","text":"Der künstliche Bodenpreis verzögert die Selbständigkeit des Arbeiters und verwandelt seinen ausgeschlossenen Bodenzugang in einen Fonds zur Einfuhr neuer Lohnarbeiter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7","text":"Die Herstellung eines kapitalistischen Arbeitsmarkts verlangt die politische Suspendierung gerade jener Marktgesetzlichkeit, die später als naturgesetzlich ausgegeben wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8","text":"Die Kolonie enthüllt die im Mutterland verdeckte Wahrheit, weil die dort historisch hergestellte Lohnabhängigkeit im Kolonialraum noch nicht selbstverständlich funktioniert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D9","text":"Die Herstellung des Lohnverhältnisses erklärt die Produktion einer mehrwerttragenden Ware, nicht aber deren Wertrealisierung; diese verlangt den Zirkulationsprozess des Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD1","text":"Kapital erscheint als soziale Form, deren Abwesenheit durch den bloßen Überfluss an Geld, Boden und Produktionsmitteln nicht aufgehoben wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD2","text":"Der kapitalistische Arbeitsmarkt ist kein vorausgesetzter neutraler Ort des Tauschs, sondern ein Ergebnis von Expropriation, Reproduktion und Bevölkerungsregulierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD3","text":"Die rechtliche Freiheit des Arbeiters ist mit seiner materiell hergestellten Abhängigkeit vereinbar und dient deren ideologischer Verdeckung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4","text":"Arbeiterunabhängigkeit und kapitalistische Akkumulation stehen in der freien Kolonie in einem inversen Verhältnis: Was den Produzenten stärkt, entzieht dem Kapital seine Arbeitsbasis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5","text":"Die ursprüngliche Akkumulation erscheint zugleich als historische Voraussetzung und als fortlaufend reproduzierbare Technik zur Sicherung von Lohnabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD6","text":"Der kapitalistische Begriff des Nationalreichtums misst gesellschaftlichen Erfolg an der Verfügbarkeit ausbeutbarer Arbeit, nicht an der Unabhängigkeit oder Versorgung der Produzenten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX1","text":"Kapitalistische Kategorien sind nicht zeitlose Eigenschaften von Dingen, sondern historisch bestimmte gesellschaftliche Verhältnisse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2","text":"Die rechtliche Freiheit des Arbeiters ist nicht hinreichend für seine materielle Unabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX3","text":"Eine allgemeine Zugänglichkeit des Bodens erzeugt nicht spontan eine kapitalistische Gesellschaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX4","text":"Das Gesetz von Nachfrage und Zufuhr begründet nicht autonom die Lohnabhängigkeit, die es als Marktgesetz regulieren soll.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX5","text":"Produktivkraft, Arbeitsteilung und Kooperation erzeugen Kapital nicht ohne die vorherige Trennung der Produzenten von ihren Arbeitsbedingungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX1","text":"Eine Gesellschaft mit dauerhaft allgemein zugänglichem Boden und zugleich dauerhaft verfügbarer Lohnarbeiterklasse ist innerhalb der kapitalistischen Logik nicht stabilisierbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2","text":"Eine nichtzwangsförmige Entstehung kapitalistischen Privateigentums bleibt ausgeschlossen, weil kapitalistische Akkumulation Expropriation voraussetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX3","text":"Eine kapitalistische Kolonisation, die den Produzenten volle Verfügung über Boden und Arbeitsbedingungen belässt, ist als kapitalistische Kolonisation unmöglich.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4","text":"Die Versöhnung von kapitalistisch definiertem Nationalreichtum und allgemeiner Produzentenunabhängigkeit bleibt systemisch versperrt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS1","text":"Selbstarbeitseigentum ≠ kapitalistisches Eigentum → politische Ökonomie erzeugt durch Gleichsetzung ideologische Inversion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS2","text":"Freie Kolonie + öffentlicher Boden → praktisches Auftreten beider Eigentumsformen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS3","text":"Produktionsmittel ohne gezwungene Lohnarbeit → kein Kapitalverhältnis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS4","text":"Bodenzugang → Austritt aus Lohnarbeit → unsichere Arbeitszufuhr → Hemmung von Kooperation und Akkumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS5","text":"Kapitalakkumulation → Reproduktion der Lohnarbeit + relative Übervölkerung → soziale Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS6","text":"Künstlicher Bodenpreis + Importfonds → verzögerte Selbständigkeit + Erneuerung der Lohnarbeiterklasse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS7","text":"Expropriation → Lohnverhältnis → mehrwerttragende Ware → Verkauf → Zirkulationsprozess des Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF1","text":"Die Gleichsetzung zweier gegensätzlicher Eigentumsformen **→** die freie Kolonie wird zum Gegenbild der kapitalistischen Normalität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF2","text":"Der freie Bodenzugang **→** die Möglichkeit unabhängiger Produzenten **→** der Zerfall einer stabilen Lohnarbeiterklasse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF3","text":"Der Zerfall der Lohnarbeiterklasse **→** Arbeitsknappheit und unsichere Kooperation **→** Hemmung der Akkumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF4","text":"Die Hemmung der Akkumulation **→** Wakefields Programm eines künstlichen Bodenpreises und staatlich finanzierten Arbeiterimports.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF5","text":"Die künstliche Herstellung der Lohnabhängigkeit **→** Enthüllung der Expropriation als Voraussetzung kapitalistischen Eigentums.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF6","text":"Die Expropriation als Produktionsvoraussetzung **→** die mehrwerttragende Ware **→** die Notwendigkeit ihrer Realisation in der Kapitalzirkulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME1","text":"Privateigentum wird in selbstarbeitendes Eigentum und auf Expropriation beruhendes kapitalistisches Eigentum gespalten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME2","text":"Geld, Maschinen und Produktionsmittel werden von stofflichen Gegenständen zu Trägern eines nur unter bestimmten Klassenverhältnissen wirksamen sozialen Verhältnisses umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3","text":"Boden erscheint nicht primär als Naturressource, sondern als Regulierungspunkt des Übergangs zwischen unabhängiger Produktion und Lohnabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4","text":"Der Arbeitsmarkt erscheint nicht als spontane Begegnung von Angebot und Nachfrage, sondern als institutionell erzeugte und reproduzierte Klassenstruktur.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME5","text":"Die Kolonie wird von einem Randfall des Mutterlands zu einem Erkenntnisinstrument für dessen verdeckte Entstehungsbedingungen umgeordnet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME6","text":"Der freie Vertrag wird vom Ursprung der sozialen Ordnung zu ihrer ideologischen Oberfläche herabgestuft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der Text untersucht Wakefields Theorie der systematischen Kolonisation und ihre Behandlung des Arbeitsmangels in freien Kolonien.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT2","text":"Structural — Der Text rekonstruiert die Trennung von Produzenten und Produktionsmitteln als Bedingung der Lohnarbeit, Akkumulation und kapitalistischen Kooperation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Der Text benutzt die Kolonie als Gegenexperiment, das die im Mutterland naturalisierte Abhängigkeit als politisch und historisch hergestellte Ordnung ausweist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Kapital wird als historisches Verhältnis bestimmt, dessen Fortbestand eine fortlaufende Reproduktion von Lohnabhängigkeit und Arbeitskräfteüberschuss verlangt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Kernbewegung von der Eigentumsunterscheidung über die koloniale Gegenprobe bis zur Expropriationsschlussfolgerung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT2","text":"Die innere Kohärenz liegt in der Kette Kapitalverhältnis, Expropriation, Lohnarbeiterklasse, Arbeitsmarktreproduktion und staatlicher Kolonialtechnik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist am stärksten dort, wo frei zugänglicher Boden als konkrete Negation der dauerhaften Lohnabhängigkeit fungiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT4","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, warum Wakefields Programm historisch scheitert und durch welche unterschiedlichen Mechanismen regionale Arbeiterübervölkerung entsteht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT5","text":"Die zentrale Bruchlinie besteht zwischen der Behauptung naturgesetzlicher Marktregulierung und der Notwendigkeit staatlich organisierter Zwangsmittel zur Herstellung des Arbeitsmarkts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT6","text":"Die satirische Figur der freiwilligen Selbstexpropriation komprimiert eine historische Widerlegung, ersetzt aber keine eigenständige historische Herleitung ihrer konkreten Formen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung von ideologischer Gleichsetzung über koloniale Enthüllung und politische Gegenmaßnahme bis zum Übergang von Produktion zu Zirkulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T210842588115Z_c6cacbe6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"3) The modern theory of colonisation.","source_sha256":"7ea094fadb87555c07cd1286ca3d3cd035dccd758e7b054525cb0298fe78c87a","sha256":"8ec868a380f6100efea4a6edb2d9654726e28d9302c66195304e7fcd5a8177b3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:08:42.590075+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS1","text":"Political economy conceals the opposition between private property based on one's own labour and capitalist private property by conceptually equating them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2","text":"The argument is diagnostic and reconstructive because it uses the free colony as a practical testing ground for the conditions of capital concealed in the mother country.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS3","text":"The free colony reveals that money, means of production, and land do not generate a capital relation without a permanent class of wage-dependent workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4","text":"Free access to land enables departure from wage labour and thereby interrupts the reproduction of the labour market, combined labour, and capitalist accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS5","text":"Wakefield's systematic colonisation is intended to translate this interruption into artificial wage dependence through state-produced barriers to land and regulated worker importation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS6","text":"The colony thus reveals that capitalist production and accumulation presuppose the expropriation of the self-working producer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS7","text":"The concluding movement transfers the analysis from the production of surplus-value-bearing commodities to the necessary realisation of their value in the circulation process of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","text":"Private property based on one's own labour and capitalist private property are opposed modes of appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","text":"Capital is not an object, but a social relation between persons mediated by objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","text":"Capital presupposes the existence of workers compelled to sell their labour-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","text":"The expropriation of producers from their conditions of labour and from the land grounds capitalist production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","text":"In the free colony, land remains generally accessible and can be transformed by settlers into their own means of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","text":"Access to one's own land permits the wage worker to leave wage labour and become an independent producer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","text":"Capitalist accumulation reproduces the wage-worker class and a relative surplus population in order to secure social dependence and the supply of labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8","text":"Political economy presents the social dependence of the wage worker as a free contractual relation between equal owners of commodities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9","text":"Wakefield's systematic colonisation employs artificially high-priced land and worker importation in order to produce a permanent wage-worker class.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10","text":"The immediate product of capitalist production is a surplus-value-bearing commodity whose value is realised only through sale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX1","text":"Capitalist private property is not the continuation of private property based on one's own labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX2","text":"Money, machines, foodstuffs, and means of production are not already capital as things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX3","text":"Means of production owned by their immediate producers are not capitalist means of production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX4","text":"The wage contract is not materially a relation of equal independence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX5","text":"Population growth does not necessarily generate a reliable supply of wage workers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX6","text":"Natural colonisation is not identical with systematic capitalist colonisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX7","text":"The sufficient price of land is not a market price determined by demand and supply.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX8","text":"National wealth is not identical with the prosperity of the working population.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX9","text":"Capitalist cooperation is not a technically neutral form of collective labour.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX10","text":"The separation of capital owners and labour owners is not the result of voluntary self-expropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D1","text":"The free colony makes the opposition between self-working and capitalist private property practically visible.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D2","text":"Imported monetary resources and means of production remain functionless as capital if no permanently available wage labour exists.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D3","text":"So long as workers possess or can acquire their own means of production, the wage-worker class necessary for capitalist accumulation is absent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D4","text":"The absent separation of the producer from the land simultaneously prevents the enduring separation of agriculture and industry as well as the formation of an internal capital market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D5","text":"The possibility of transition to independent production makes wage labour insecure, raises its cost, and impedes long-term capitalist enterprises.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D6","text":"The artificial land price delays the worker's independence and transforms his excluded access to land into a fund for importing new wage workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7","text":"The creation of a capitalist labour market requires the political suspension of precisely that market regularity which is later presented as natural law.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8","text":"The colony reveals the truth concealed in the mother country because the wage dependence historically produced there does not yet function as a matter of course in the colonial sphere.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:D9","text":"The production of the wage relation explains the production of a surplus-value-bearing commodity, but not the realisation of its value; this requires the circulation process of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD1","text":"Capital appears as a social form whose absence is not overcome by the mere abundance of money, land, and means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD2","text":"The capitalist labour market is not a presupposed neutral site of exchange, but a result of expropriation, reproduction, and population regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD3","text":"The worker's legal freedom is compatible with his materially produced dependence and serves its ideological concealment.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4","text":"Worker independence and capitalist accumulation stand in an inverse relation in the free colony: what strengthens the producer withdraws from capital its labour base.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5","text":"Primitive accumulation appears at once as a historical precondition and as a continuously reproducible technique for securing wage dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD6","text":"The capitalist concept of national wealth measures social success by the availability of exploitable labour, not by the independence or provision of producers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX1","text":"Capitalist categories are not timeless properties of things, but historically determined social relations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2","text":"The worker's legal freedom is not sufficient for his material independence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX3","text":"General accessibility of land does not spontaneously generate a capitalist society.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX4","text":"The law of demand and supply does not autonomously ground the wage dependence that it is supposed to regulate as a market law.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX5","text":"Productive power, division of labour, and cooperation do not produce capital without the prior separation of producers from their conditions of labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX1","text":"A society with permanently generally accessible land and, at the same time, a permanently available wage-worker class cannot be stabilised within capitalist logic.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2","text":"A non-coercive emergence of capitalist private property remains excluded because capitalist accumulation presupposes expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX3","text":"A capitalist colonisation that leaves producers full control over land and conditions of labour is impossible as capitalist colonisation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4","text":"The reconciliation of capitalistically defined national wealth and general producer independence remains systemically blocked.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS1","text":"Self-working property ≠ capitalist property → political economy produces ideological inversion through equation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS2","text":"Free colony + public land → practical appearance of both forms of property.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS3","text":"Means of production without compelled wage labour → no capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS4","text":"Access to land → departure from wage labour → insecure labour supply → impediment to cooperation and accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS5","text":"Capital accumulation → reproduction of wage labour + relative surplus population → social dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS6","text":"Artificial land price + import fund → delayed independence + renewal of the wage-worker class.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:FGS7","text":"Expropriation → wage relation → surplus-value-bearing commodity → sale → circulation process of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF1","text":"The equation of two opposed forms of property **→** the free colony becomes the counter-image of capitalist normality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF2","text":"Free access to land **→** the possibility of independent producers **→** the disintegration of a stable wage-worker class.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF3","text":"The disintegration of the wage-worker class **→** labour scarcity and insecure cooperation **→** impediment to accumulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF4","text":"The impediment to accumulation **→** Wakefield's programme of an artificial land price and state-financed worker importation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF5","text":"The artificial production of wage dependence **→** revelation of expropriation as the precondition of capitalist property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:AF6","text":"Expropriation as a precondition of production **→** the surplus-value-bearing commodity **→** the necessity of its realisation in the circulation of capital.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME1","text":"Private property is split into self-working property and capitalist property based on expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME2","text":"Money, machines, and means of production are reclassified from material objects into bearers of a social relation effective only under specific class relations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3","text":"Land appears not primarily as a natural resource, but as a point of regulation for the transition between independent production and wage dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4","text":"The labour market appears not as a spontaneous encounter of supply and demand, but as an institutionally produced and reproduced class structure.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME5","text":"The colony is reordered from a marginal case of the mother country into an instrument of knowledge for its concealed conditions of emergence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME6","text":"The free contract is demoted from the origin of social order to its ideological surface.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text examines Wakefield's theory of systematic colonisation and its treatment of labour scarcity in free colonies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT2","text":"Structural — The text reconstructs the separation of producers and means of production as the condition of wage labour, accumulation, and capitalist cooperation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text uses the colony as a counter-experiment that identifies the dependence naturalised in the mother country as a politically and historically produced order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Capital is determined as a historical relation whose continuance requires an ongoing reproduction of wage dependence and surplus labour-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the core movement from the distinction of property through the colonial counter-test to the conclusion of expropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT2","text":"The inner coherence lies in the chain of capital relation, expropriation, wage-worker class, labour-market reproduction, and state colonial technique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT3","text":"The structure is strongest where freely accessible land functions as the concrete negation of permanent wage dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT4","text":"It remains underdetermined why Wakefield's programme historically fails and through which different mechanisms regional worker overpopulation arises.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT5","text":"The central fault line consists between the assertion of market regulation as natural law and the necessity of state-organised means of coercion for creating the labour market.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT6","text":"The satirical figure of voluntary self-expropriation compresses a historical refutation, but does not replace an independent historical derivation of its concrete forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement from ideological equation through colonial revelation and political countermeasure to the transition from production to circulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CH_V4GB_3DMK@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_V4GB_3DMK:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 23","title":"3) Die moderne Kolonisationstheorie.","context":"Chapter 23"}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 01–03","order":1,"parents":["CH_V4GB_1DW0","CH_V4GB_2DAD","CH_V4GB_3DGO"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_01@R001","sha256":"78f00f3c0c37f6a7ccfb747aa75dda89463c99605ee4fc4b1755ba3a9db217db","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-01","text":"Das System erklärt, wie sich die elementare Warenform über Austausch und allgemeines Äquivalent zu einem differenzierten Gefüge notwendiger Geldfunktionen entwickelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-02","text":"Seine Kernthese lautet, dass voneinander unabhängige Privatarbeiten nur durch sachliche Wertformen gesellschaftlich vermittelt werden und deshalb die Verdopplung ihrer Produkte in Ware und Geld erzwingen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-03","text":"Das Argument wird zu einer genetischen Formrekonstruktion, die ökonomische Erscheinungen aus ihren gesellschaftlichen Voraussetzungen ableitet und zugleich ihre Verkehrungen diagnostiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-04","text":"Die gerichtete Bewegung führt vom inneren Warenwiderspruch über seine polare Externalisierung in Ware und Geld bis zur funktionellen Ausdifferenzierung des verselbständigten Werts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-05","text":"Diese Bewegung ist kumulativ, rekursiv und mutationsgetrieben: Jede Form löst einen vorausgehenden Widerspruch operativ, bewahrt ihn jedoch in einer umfassenderen Bewegungsform.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-06","text":"Die Schließung bleibt expansiv und unvollständig, weil Weltgeld und Krisenmöglichkeit die Warenvermittlung nicht versöhnen, sondern ihre sachliche Abhängigkeit auf globaler Ebene materialisieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Warenproduktion setzt selbständige Privatarbeiten voraus, deren gesellschaftliche Geltung nicht vorgängig feststeht, sondern erst durch den Austausch ihrer Produkte vermittelt wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Wert besitzt seine gesellschaftliche Substanz in abstrakter menschlicher Arbeit und sein immanentes quantitatives Maß in gesellschaftlich notwendiger Arbeitszeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Der Widerspruch von Gebrauchswert und Wert wird nicht aufgehoben, sondern aus der Ware in die Polarität von Ware und Geld und anschließend in deren zeitlich trennbare Bewegungen verlagert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A19","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Dieselbe Arbeit erzeugt als konkrete Tätigkeit Gebrauchswerte und gilt als abstrakte Arbeit wertbildend, wodurch stofflicher Reichtum und Wertgröße auseinanderfallen können.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A8","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Weil Wert sich nicht im eigenen Warenkörper darstellen kann, benötigt er eine fremde Naturalform, die durch gesellschaftliche Ausschließung zur allgemeinen Äquivalentform wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A12","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Gesellschaftliche Allgemeinheit entsteht im Wertsystem nicht durch symmetrische Teilhabe, sondern durch polare Verteilung und Konzentration allgemeiner Austauschbarkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A16","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Der Austausch entwickelt sich von der Darstellung bereits vorausgesetzten Werts zu einem nachträglichen Validierungsmechanismus, der entscheidet, ob private Arbeit gesellschaftlich zählt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:D16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Geld ist die dingliche Gestalt gesellschaftlich erzeugter allgemeiner Äquivalenz und mutiert funktionsabhängig zwischen ideeller, symbolischer und materiell selbständiger Wertgestalt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Je erfolgreicher gesellschaftliche Vermittlung in einer sachlichen Form kristallisiert, desto stärker verschwindet ihre Genesis und erscheint ihr Resultat als selbständige Eigenschaft des Dings.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A17","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Die reale Trennbarkeit komplementärer Austauschmomente erzeugt einen unkontrollierten gesellschaftlichen Zusammenhang und die formale Möglichkeit seiner krisenhaften Wiedervereinigung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Recht, Vertrag, staatliche Denomination und Zeichengeltung formen die ökonomische Vermittlung, können deren Wertverhältnisse aber weder souverän erzeugen noch suspendieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Auf dem Weltmarkt fallen lokale Geldformen ab, sodass allgemeine gesellschaftliche Geltung als materielles Zahlungsmittel, Kaufmittel und übertragbare Reichtumsgestalt zurückkehrt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-01","text":"Wert bewahrt seine Identität als vergegenständlichte abstrakte Arbeit, während seine Darstellungsfunktion von der relationalen Wertform über den Preis zur realisierten Geldgestalt wandert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-02","text":"Private Arbeit mutiert von der strukturellen Voraussetzung des Werts zum Gegenstand eines nachträglichen Markturteils über gesellschaftliche Nützlichkeit, Notwendigkeit und proportionale Verteilung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A11","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-03","text":"Gebrauchswert erscheint zunächst als stoffliche Nützlichkeit, wird im Austausch positionsabhängig und fungiert schließlich als Bedingung der gesellschaftlichen Bewährung privater Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-04","text":"Der Warenwiderspruch eskaliert von einer inneren Einheit über die äußere Polarität von Ware und Geld zur möglichen gewaltsamen Wiederherstellung auseinandergetretener Zirkulationsmomente.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A19","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-05","text":"Das allgemeine Äquivalent wandert von einer strukturell bestimmten Stelle über die gesellschaftliche Ausschließung einer Ware zur funktionell differenzierten Geldgestalt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD5","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-06","text":"Geld kehrt mit umgekehrter Valenz wieder: Es ist ideelles Maß ohne aktuelle Anwesenheit, zirkulierendes Zeichen mit begrenzter Materialität und in Zahlung sowie Weltverkehr erneut hartes Geld.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-07","text":"Fetischismus intensiviert sich vom sachlichen Schein der Warenwerte über die Naturalisierung der Geldware bis zur kausalen Verkehrung, in der Geld scheinbar die von Waren erzeugte Bewegung hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A17","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-08","text":"Der Warenbesitzer wird zunächst rechtlich anerkannt, dann zur Personifikation des ökonomischen Verhältnisses reduziert und schließlich in funktionsabhängige Rollen wie Käufer, Verkäufer, Schuldner und Gläubiger zerlegt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-01","text":"Die Reduktion komplizierter Arbeit und die genaue Produktivitätswirkung bleiben lokale Bestimmungen der Wertgröße; auf der aktuellen Ebene sichern sie lediglich die quantitative Konsistenz des Wertmaßes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A7","CH_V4GB_1DW0:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-02","text":"Die einzelnen Entwicklungsstufen der Wertform verbleiben als lokaler Ableitungsapparat, während die Unfähigkeit des Werts zur Selbstdarstellung und die exklusive Äquivalentstelle global fortbestehen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS6","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-03","text":"Wechselseitige Eigentümeranerkennung und die historische Entstehung des Austauschs an Gemeinwesengrenzen bleiben lokale Voraussetzungen; sie ersetzen nicht die globale Formnotwendigkeit des Geldes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:AS2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-04","text":"Teilbarkeit, Gleichartigkeit und andere Stoffeigenschaften eines Geldmaterials bleiben trägerbezogene Bedingungen und werden nicht zur Ursache seines gesellschaftlichen Geldcharakters hochgestuft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A14","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-05","text":"Zirkulationsformeln, Münzverschleiß und lokale Zeichengeltung bleiben funktionsspezifische Mechanismen; nach oben skaliert allein die notwendige Differenzierung gegensätzlicher Daseinsweisen des Geldes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A13","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-06","text":"Auf die aktuelle Ebene skaliert die Struktur, dass unabhängige Arbeit ihre gesellschaftliche Geltung ausschließlich nachträglich durch sachliche Vermittlung erhält.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-07","text":"Ebenfalls global wird die Folge, dass jede operative Lösung des Warenwiderspruchs dessen Gegensätze stabilisiert, verselbständigt und bis zur Krisenmöglichkeit erweitert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-01","text":"Das System schließt aus, Wert aus Nützlichkeit, physischer Beschaffenheit oder einer intrinsischen Eigenschaft des isolierten Warenkörpers abzuleiten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX2","CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-02","text":"Austausch und Geld erzeugen weder Wert noch Kommensurabilität, sondern stellen eine durch abstrakte Arbeit bereits gesetzte gesellschaftliche Gleichheit dar und realisieren sie.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX9","CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-03","text":"Vertrag und gemeinsamer Wille dürfen nicht als souveräne Quellen des ökonomischen Inhalts gelten, den ihre Rechtsform lediglich ausdrückt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:NX1","CH_V4GB_2DAD:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-04","text":"Allgemeine Austauschbarkeit kann weder allen Waren gleichzeitig zukommen noch aus der Selbstsetzung jeder Ware als allgemeines Äquivalent hervorgehen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX13","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-05","text":"Geld wird weder als bloßes Zeichen oder Konvention noch als Produkt einer staatlichen Fähigkeit zur freien Wert- und Reichtumsschöpfung zugelassen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:NX6","CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-06","text":"Die Identität von Verkauf und Kauf garantiert kein zeitliches Gleichgewicht, und die einfache Zirkulation begründet nur die Krisenmöglichkeit, nicht die wirkliche Krise.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-01","text":"Damit das System Bestand hat, darf private Arbeit weder unmittelbar gesellschaftlich sein noch durch bewusste vorgängige Koordination dem Markturteil entzogen werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-02","text":"Wert darf keine eigene selbstgenügsame Erscheinungsform besitzen, und allgemeine unmittelbare Austauschbarkeit darf nicht symmetrisch auf alle Waren verteilt sein.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX2","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-03","text":"Rechtssubjekt, Vertragswille und Staat dürfen nicht als autonome soziale Substanzen auftreten, weil sie sonst die Ableitung ökonomischer Formen aus sachlich vermittelter Privatarbeit unterbrechen würden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-04","text":"Wert, Wertgröße, Preis, Geldzeichen und realisierte Zahlung dürfen nicht in einer unmittelbar identischen Größe zusammenfallen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-05","text":"Nationale Geldformen dürfen kein geschlossenes, selbstgenügsames System bilden, weil allgemeine Wertgeltung auf dem Weltmarkt ihre lokale Symbolik abstreift.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-01","text":"Die grundlegende Abwesenheit ist eine unmittelbare gesellschaftliche Beziehung der Produzenten, in der ihre Arbeiten ohne Warenwert, Marktprüfung und Geld gesellschaftlich gelten könnten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-02","text":"Die Gesamtbewegung ist um die fehlende Garantie organisiert, dass gesellschaftliches Bedürfnis, Privatarbeit, Verkauf, Preis und Zahlung miteinander übereinstimmen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-03","text":"Eine Welt gleichmäßig verteilter unmittelbarer Austauschbarkeit ist ontologisch unstatthaft, weil allgemeine Äquivalenz nur als asymmetrische Ausschließungsstruktur existiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX3","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-04","text":"Eine innere Versöhnung von Gebrauchswert und Wert bleibt ausgeschlossen; Geld verleiht ihrem Gegensatz nur eine bewegliche, funktionell belastbare äußere Form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-05","text":"Keine Geldgestalt kann ideellen Anspruch, symbolische Geltung und materielle Einlösbarkeit endgültig vereinigen oder die qualitative Schrankenlosigkeit allgemeinen Reichtums in einer endlichen Summe abschließen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-01","text":"Weil die isolierte Ware ihren inneren Gegensatz weder darstellen noch lösen kann, erzeugt sie zunächst das Geld als äußeren Wertpol und danach die Zirkulation als Bewegungsform dieses fortbestehenden Gegensatzes; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-03","CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-02","text":"Allgemeine gesellschaftliche Geltung wird durch Ausschließung produziert: Die gemeinsame Gleichheit aller Waren benötigt einen asymmetrischen Pol, in dem sie sich unmittelbar darstellt; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","CL_V4GB_01:GA-06","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD3","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-03","text":"Die Objektivität des Werts ist zugleich real und prekär, weil ihre Arbeitsgrundlage gesellschaftlich vorausgesetzt wird, ihre konkrete Geltung aber vom nachträglichen Erfolg der Veräußerung abhängt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-04","text":"Die äußere Beweglichkeit des Warenwiderspruchs erzeugt asynchrone Akte; deren Trennbarkeit verwandelt eine logische Polarität in eine reale Krisenmöglichkeit; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-03","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-05","text":"Die Symbolisierung des Geldes bleibt durch die von ihm repräsentierten Wert- und Zirkulationsverhältnisse begrenzt und schlägt bei Zahlung, Krise und Weltverkehr in materielle Geldgeltung zurück; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-06","text":"Fetischismus ist kein äußerer Irrtum, sondern der rekursive Effekt erfolgreicher Formbildung: Vermittlung wird operativ wirksam, indem sie ihre eigene Genesis im Resultat auslöscht; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-07","text":"Rechtliche und staatliche Geldmacht bleibt real, aber abgeleitet: Sie normiert die Erscheinungs- und Geltungsweise ökonomischer Verhältnisse, ohne deren Wertsubstanz oder globale Grenzen frei setzen zu können; Trace Type — Negative.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-01","text":"Gesellschaftliche Objektivität ist weder natürlich noch konventionell: Sie besteht als historisch erzeugte relationale Gegenständlichkeit, die den Handelnden praktisch entgegentritt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD1","CH_V4GB_1DW0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird vom autonomen Urheber zum Träger positionsabhängiger Funktionen innerhalb eines Systems allseitiger sachlicher Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-03","text":"Die maßgebliche Zeitform ist nachträglich und asynchron: Gesellschaftliche Geltung wird rückwirkend validiert, während zeitliche Trennungen komplementäre Akte verselbständigen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CH_V4GB_1DW0:D16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-04","text":"Die erscheinende Kausalität verkehrt die wirkliche: Die Bewegung der Waren erzeugt den Geldumlauf, tritt den Handelnden aber als selbständige Bewegung und Macht des Geldes gegenüber.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS6","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-05","text":"Strategien bloßer Bewusstseinskorrektur, moralischer Geldkritik oder souveräner Währungssetzung verfehlen die materielle Vermittlung, aus der Geldmacht hervorgeht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnis muss Geldfunktionen genetisch unterscheiden, weil ihre Reduktion auf eine einzige Erscheinungsweise regelmäßig die Richtung ökonomischer Kausalität verfälscht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-01","text":"Privatarbeit erzeugt Waren, Waren erzwingen Austausch, Austausch validiert Privatarbeit nachträglich und reproduziert damit die Ausgangsbedingung unabhängiger Produktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A11","CH_V4GB_3DGO:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-02","text":"Warenwiderspruch → äußere Verdopplung → Stabilisierung durch Geld → Trennung der Bewegungsmomente → Krisenmöglichkeit bildet den zentralen Eskalationspfad.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-03","text":"Der Attraktor allgemeiner gesellschaftlicher Geltung konzentriert verstreute Warenrelationen auf eine ausgeschlossene Ware und entfaltet diese anschließend als einheitliches Geldsystem.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-04","text":"Vermittlung → sachliche Kristallisation → Auslöschung der Genesis → scheinbare Eigenbewegung des Geldes bildet die rekursive Fetischschleife.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-05","text":"Die Trennung von Verkauf und Kauf eskaliert über Schuld- und Zahlungsketten: Normale Verrechnung reduziert den Geldbedarf, während Störung die Abhängigkeit von unmittelbar verfügbarem Geld steigert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-06","text":"Idealisierung → Symbolisierung → Kreditierung → materielle Einlösung → Weltgeld bildet eine Spirale, in der jede Entmaterialisierung die Möglichkeit verschärfter Rematerialisierung erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B01","text":"Unabhängige Privatarbeiten → private Produkte → Austauschzwang → nachträgliche gesellschaftliche Geltung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A10","CH_V4GB_1DW0:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B02","text":"Arbeitsprodukt = Gebrauchswert ∧ Wert → konkrete Arbeit / abstrakte Arbeit → stofflicher Reichtum ≠ Wertreichtum.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A3","CH_V4GB_1DW0:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B03","text":"Fehlende Eigenerscheinung des Werts → fremde Naturalform → relative Wertform ↔ Äquivalentform → polare Wertdarstellung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A12","CH_V4GB_1DW0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B04","text":"Konkurrenz partikularer Äquivalentansprüche → gesellschaftliche Ausschließung einer Ware → allgemeines Äquivalent → Geld als dingliche Form kollektiver Vermittlung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B05","text":"Warenwert → ideeller Preis → Verkauf → nachträgliche Validierung privater Arbeit → Kauf → verschlungene Warenmetamorphosen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B06","text":"Räumlich-zeitliche Trennung von Verkauf und Kauf → verselbständigte Zirkulationsmomente → sachliche Gesamtbewegung → Krisenmöglichkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B07","text":"Wertmaß → Zirkulationszeichen → Schatz → Zahlungsmittel → Weltgeld; funktionelle Mutation + verschwundene Vermittlung → gesteigerte Verselbständigung und Fetischisierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AFM-B01","text":"Warenerscheinung → Gebrauchswert-Wert-Spaltung → Abstraktion auf gesellschaftliche Arbeit → polare Wertform → exklusives allgemeines Äquivalent → Geld → Preis → Warenmetamorphose → funktionelle Gelddifferenzierung → Weltgeld.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AFM-B02","text":"Unmittelbare Einheit → widersprüchliche Externalisierung → operative Vermittlung → Auslöschung der Vermittlung → sachliche Verselbständigung → allseitige Abhängigkeit → Krisenmöglichkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:FGS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-01","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen intrinsischem Wert und willkürlicher Konvention wird durch das Feld gesellschaftlich-relationaler Objektivität ersetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD1","CH_V4GB_1DW0:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-02","text":"Allgemeinheit wird von gleichmäßiger Teilhabe auf asymmetrische Ausschließung und konzentrierte Darstellungsfähigkeit umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD3","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-03","text":"Der Markt wird vom neutralen Tauschort zum nachträglichen Validierungsmechanismus privater Arbeit und gesellschaftlicher Proportionen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-04","text":"Persönliche Unabhängigkeit und ökonomische Abhängigkeit werden nicht länger als Gegensätze behandelt: Erstere ist die personale Form eines allseitigen sachlichen Zwangszusammenhangs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-05","text":"Geld wird nicht in äußere Arten zerlegt, sondern als einheitliche Wertform mit funktionsspezifisch gegensätzlichen Daseinsweisen kartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-06","text":"Krise wird weder als äußerer Unfall noch als bereits erklärte Notwendigkeit klassifiziert, sondern als endogene Möglichkeit real getrennter, innerlich zusammengehöriger Akte.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-07","text":"Staatliche Geldordnung und nationale Zirkulation werden als begrenzte Ebenen innerhalb eines Wertzusammenhangs neu eingeordnet, der seine materielle Allgemeinheit erst auf dem Weltmarkt behauptet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene entfaltet sich das System von Gebrauchswert, Wertsubstanz und Wertform zu den besonderen Funktionen von Wertmaß, Rechengeld, Zirkulationsmittel, Schatz, Zahlungsmittel und Weltgeld.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene organisiert die nachträgliche Vermittlung unabhängiger Privatarbeiten eine naturwüchsige gesellschaftliche Arbeitsteilung durch Warenwert und Geld.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene ersetzt die Formgenese Erklärungen aus Nutzen, Recht, Konvention, Geldmenge oder Staatsmacht durch die Ableitung ihrer begrenzten Wirksamkeit aus Wertform und Warenbewegung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-temporalen Ebene werden gesellschaftliche Abstraktionen praktisch real, während nachträgliche Geltung und zeitliche Trennung selbständige Prozesse, Abhängigkeit und Krisenmöglichkeit erzeugen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollzieht die Darstellung selbst die behauptete Umkehrung: Sie rekonstruiert die verschwundene Vermittlung und kehrt die von der Erscheinung nahegelegte Kausalrichtung um.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-01","text":"Die logische Notwendigkeit einer exklusiven Geldform erklärt nicht vollständig, wie eine bestimmte Ware praktisch ausgewählt und ihre Äquivalentgeltung dauerhaft gesichert wird; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-02","text":"Abstrakte Arbeit bleibt zwischen allgemein menschlicher Arbeitsverausgabung und spezifisch gesellschaftlicher Geltungsform voneinander unabhängiger Privatarbeiten gespannt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:MRT4","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-03","text":"Der Wert soll durch gesellschaftlich notwendige Arbeitszeit bestimmt sein, wird aber erst durch einen Markt validiert, dessen Urteil die konkrete gesellschaftliche Geltung der verausgabten Arbeit nachträglich verändert; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A6","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-04","text":"Die Ableitung hält am eigenwertigen Geldmaterial fest, obwohl Zeichen, Kredit und Verrechnung reale Geldfunktionen übernehmen; die Grenze zwischen funktioneller Vertretung und notwendiger materieller Einlösung bleibt beweglich; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A15","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-05","text":"Die Trennung der Zirkulationsakte erklärt die formale Möglichkeit der Krise, aber nicht die Bedingungen ihres notwendigen Umschlags in eine wirkliche Krise; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-06","text":"Die aus wechselseitiger Anerkennung entwickelte Austauschform integriert die Möglichkeit gewaltsamer Aneignung nicht in ihre eigene Genesis; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-01","text":"Gebrauchswert mutiert von einer stofflichen Bestimmung zur positionsabhängigen Bedingung gesellschaftlicher Nützlichkeitsbewährung; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-02","text":"Die Äquivalentform mutiert von einer relationalen Polfunktion zur gesellschaftlich monopolisierten Geldgestalt und erscheint danach als selbständige Eigenschaft ihres Trägers; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A13","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-03","text":"Der Warenwiderspruch mutiert von statischer Einheit zu äußerer Bewegung und schließlich zur Möglichkeit einer gewaltsamen Wiedervereinigung getrennter Momente; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A19","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-04","text":"Geld mutiert vom ideellen Preisausdruck über lokal geltende Zeichen zur materiell verlangten Zahlungs- und Weltgeldgestalt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als dezentrale Validierungsmaschine, in der gesellschaftliche Beziehungen in Dingen kristallisieren und deren verschlungene Bewegungen einen unkontrollierten Zusammenhang bilden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:ALT4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist kein souveräner Mittelpunkt, sondern ein beweglicher Träger ökonomischer Funktionen innerhalb allseitiger sachlicher Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-03","text":"Die Zeit ist rückwirkend und asynchron: Vergangene Privatarbeit erhält erst nachträglich gesellschaftliche Geltung, während getrennte Akte zukünftige Verpflichtungen und Krisenrisiken erzeugen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:D16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-04","text":"Wirksame Intervention kann weder bei moralischer Kritik noch bei monetärer Benennung stehenbleiben, sondern müsste die materielle Produktionsvermittlung verändern, welche die sachliche Macht des Geldes reproduziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD8","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B01","text":"Die extrahierten Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von der Warenform über Austausch und Geldentstehung bis zur funktionellen Ausdifferenzierung des Geldes und ihrer Krisenimplikation zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B02","text":"Die Architektur ist am stärksten geschlossen, wo Warenzwiespalt, Doppelcharakter der Arbeit, gesellschaftliche Wertrealisierung und Umkehrung der erscheinenden Geldkausalität ineinandergreifen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:MRT2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B03","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die praktische Durchsetzung einer bestimmten Geldware und die Bedingungen, unter denen die formale Krisenmöglichkeit notwendig in eine wirkliche Krise umschlägt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B04","text":"Die Kohärenz ist rekursiv statt rein linear: Die logische Notwendigkeit der Geldform wird durch wiederkehrende Funktionsmutationen, kausale Umkehrungen und materielle Rückkehrbewegungen bewahrt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B05","text":"Axiomatischer Reduktion widersteht der praktische Vollzug, durch den Gesellschaft eine Geldware ausschließt, Privatarbeit tatsächlich validiert und eine Krisenmöglichkeit aktualisiert; diese Übergänge sind strukturell markiert, aber nicht vollständig erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211625597724Z_e5ff31f3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 01–03","source_sha256":"78f00f3c0c37f6a7ccfb747aa75dda89463c99605ee4fc4b1755ba3a9db217db","sha256":"011ec57e0079d550b29c88fbc41784e0927bcf775a880acfb45b033aa5d9f7c0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:16:25.599364+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-01","text":"The system explains how the elementary commodity form develops through exchange and the general equivalent into a differentiated configuration of necessary money functions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-02","text":"Its core thesis is that mutually independent private labours are socially mediated only through objective forms of value and therefore compel the duplication of their products into commodity and money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-03","text":"The argument becomes a genetic reconstruction of forms, which derives economic phenomena from their social preconditions while also diagnosing their inversions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-04","text":"The directed movement proceeds from the inner contradiction of the commodity through its polar externalization in commodity and money to the functional differentiation of autonomized value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-05","text":"This movement is cumulative, recursive, and mutation-driven: each form operationally resolves a preceding contradiction, yet preserves it in a more comprehensive form of movement.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AS-06","text":"The closure remains expansive and incomplete because world money and the possibility of crisis do not reconcile commodity mediation, but materialize its objective dependence at the global level.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Commodity production presupposes autonomous private labours whose social validity is not established in advance, but is mediated only through the exchange of their products.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Value possesses its social substance in abstract human labour and its immanent quantitative measure in socially necessary labour-time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The contradiction between use-value and value is not abolished, but displaced from the commodity into the polarity of commodity and money and subsequently into their temporally separable movements.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A19","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The same labour produces use-values as concrete activity and counts as value-creating as abstract labour, whereby material wealth and magnitude of value can diverge.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A8","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Because value cannot represent itself in its own commodity body, it requires an alien natural form, which through social exclusion becomes the general equivalent form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A12","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Social universality arises in the value system not through symmetrical participation, but through polar distribution and concentration of universal exchangeability.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A16","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Exchange develops from the representation of already presupposed value into a retrospective validation mechanism that decides whether private labour counts socially.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:D16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Money is the objective form of socially produced general equivalence and mutates, depending on function, between ideal, symbolic, and materially autonomous forms of value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] The more successfully social mediation crystallizes in an objective form, the more its genesis disappears and its result appears as an autonomous property of the thing.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A17","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The real separability of complementary moments of exchange produces an uncontrolled social interconnection and the formal possibility of its crisis-ridden reunification.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Law, contract, state denomination, and the validity of signs shape economic mediation, but can neither sovereignly produce nor suspend its value relations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] On the world market, local forms of money fall away, so that universal social validity returns as material means of payment, means of purchase, and transferable form of wealth.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-01","text":"Value preserves its identity as objectified abstract labour, while its function of representation migrates from the relational value form through price to the realized money form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-02","text":"Private labour mutates from the structural precondition of value into the object of a retrospective market judgment concerning social usefulness, necessity, and proportional distribution.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A11","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-03","text":"Use-value initially appears as material usefulness, becomes position-dependent in exchange, and ultimately functions as a condition of the social proving of private labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-04","text":"The commodity contradiction escalates from an inner unity through the external polarity of commodity and money to the possible violent restoration of diverged moments of circulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A19","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-05","text":"The general equivalent moves from a structurally determined position through the social exclusion of a commodity to the functionally differentiated money form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD5","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-06","text":"Money returns with reversed valence: it is an ideal measure without present existence, a circulating sign with limited materiality, and in payment and world commerce again hard money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-07","text":"Fetishism intensifies from the objective appearance of commodity values through the naturalization of the money commodity to the causal inversion in which money seemingly brings forth the movement generated by commodities.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A17","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RMD-08","text":"The commodity owner is first legally recognized, then reduced to the personification of the economic relation, and finally decomposed into function-dependent roles such as buyer, seller, debtor, and creditor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-01","text":"The reduction of complex labour and the precise effect of productivity remain local determinations of magnitude of value; at the current level, they merely secure the quantitative consistency of the measure of value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A7","CH_V4GB_1DW0:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-02","text":"The individual developmental stages of the value form remain a local apparatus of derivation, while the incapacity of value for self-representation and the exclusive equivalent position persist globally.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS6","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-03","text":"Mutual recognition of owners and the historical emergence of exchange at the boundaries of communities remain local preconditions; they do not replace the global formal necessity of money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:AS2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-04","text":"Divisibility, homogeneity, and other material properties of a money material remain carrier-specific conditions and are not elevated into the cause of its social money character.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A14","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-05","text":"Formulas of circulation, coin wear, and local validity of signs remain function-specific mechanisms; what alone scales upward is the necessary differentiation of opposed modes of existence of money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A13","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-06","text":"What scales to the current level is the structure whereby independent labour receives its social validity exclusively retrospectively through objective mediation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:CGD-07","text":"Also global is the consequence that every operational solution to the commodity contradiction stabilizes, autonomizes, and extends its oppositions to the possibility of crisis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes deriving value from usefulness, physical constitution, or an intrinsic property of the isolated commodity body.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX2","CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-02","text":"Exchange and money produce neither value nor commensurability, but represent and realize a social equality already posited by abstract labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX9","CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-03","text":"Contract and common will must not count as sovereign sources of the economic content that their legal form merely expresses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:NX1","CH_V4GB_2DAD:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-04","text":"Universal exchangeability can neither accrue to all commodities simultaneously nor emerge from the self-positing of every commodity as general equivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:NX13","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-05","text":"Money is admitted neither as a mere sign or convention nor as the product of a state's capacity freely to create value and wealth.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:NX6","CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:GNX-06","text":"The identity of sale and purchase guarantees no temporal equilibrium, and simple circulation grounds only the possibility of crisis, not the actual crisis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-01","text":"For the system to subsist, private labour must neither be immediately social nor be withdrawn from market judgment through conscious prior coordination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-02","text":"Value must possess no self-sufficient form of appearance of its own, and general immediate exchangeability must not be distributed symmetrically across all commodities.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX2","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-03","text":"The legal subject, contractual will, and state must not appear as autonomous social substances, because otherwise they would interrupt the derivation of economic forms from objectively mediated private labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-04","text":"Value, magnitude of value, price, money sign, and realized payment must not coincide in a directly identical magnitude.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:DBN-05","text":"National forms of money must not constitute a closed, self-sufficient system, because universal validity of value sheds their local symbolism on the world market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-01","text":"The fundamental absence is an immediate social relation among producers in which their labours could count socially without commodity value, market testing, and money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-02","text":"The overall movement is organized around the absent guarantee that social need, private labour, sale, price, and payment correspond with one another.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-03","text":"A world of evenly distributed immediate exchangeability is ontologically inadmissible, because general equivalence exists only as an asymmetrical structure of exclusion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX3","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-04","text":"An inner reconciliation of use-value and value remains excluded; money merely confers upon their opposition a mobile, functionally viable external form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SNX5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSA-05","text":"No form of money can definitively unite ideal claim, symbolic validity, and material redeemability, or conclude the qualitative boundlessness of general wealth in a finite sum.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-01","text":"Because the isolated commodity can neither represent nor resolve its inner opposition, it first generates money as an external pole of value and then circulation as the form of movement of this persisting opposition; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-03","CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-02","text":"Universal social validity is produced through exclusion: the common equality of all commodities requires an asymmetrical pole in which it represents itself immediately; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","CL_V4GB_01:GA-06","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD3","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-03","text":"The objectivity of value is at once real and precarious, because its labour basis is socially presupposed, while its concrete validity depends on the retrospective success of alienation; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-04","text":"The external mobility of the commodity contradiction generates asynchronous acts; their separability transforms a logical polarity into a real possibility of crisis; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-03","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-05","text":"The symbolization of money remains limited by the value and circulation relations it represents and reverts, in payment, crisis, and world commerce, to material monetary validity; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-06","text":"Fetishism is not an external error, but the recursive effect of successful form formation: mediation becomes operationally effective by erasing its own genesis in the result; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:XD-07","text":"Legal and state monetary power remains real, but derivative: it regulates the mode of appearance and validity of economic relations without being able freely to posit their value substance or global limits; Trace Type — Negative.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-01","text":"Social objectivity is neither natural nor conventional: it exists as historically produced relational objectivity that confronts agents in practice.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-02","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD1","CH_V4GB_1DW0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes transformed from an autonomous author into the bearer of position-dependent functions within a system of universal objective dependence.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-03","text":"The decisive temporal form is retrospective and asynchronous: social validity is validated retroactively, while temporal separations autonomize complementary acts.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CH_V4GB_1DW0:D16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-04","text":"Appearing causality inverts the real: the movement of commodities generates monetary circulation, yet confronts agents as the autonomous movement and power of money.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS6","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-05","text":"Strategies of mere correction of consciousness, moral critique of money, or sovereign currency positing miss the material mediation from which monetary power arises.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CL_V4GB_01:GA-11","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:BSD-06","text":"Cognition must genetically distinguish money functions, because their reduction to a single mode of appearance regularly falsifies the direction of economic causality.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_01:GA-10","CL_V4GB_01:GA-12","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-01","text":"Private labour produces commodities, commodities compel exchange, exchange retrospectively validates private labour, and thereby reproduces the initial condition of independent production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A11","CH_V4GB_3DGO:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-02","text":"Commodity contradiction → external duplication → stabilization through money → separation of moments of movement → possibility of crisis constitutes the central path of escalation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-03","text":"The attractor of universal social validity concentrates dispersed commodity relations upon an excluded commodity and subsequently unfolds it as a unified monetary system.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-04","text":"Mediation → objective crystallization → erasure of genesis → apparent self-movement of money constitutes the recursive fetish loop.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-05","text":"The separation of sale and purchase escalates through chains of debt and payment: normal clearing reduces the need for money, whereas disruption increases dependence on immediately available money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:RLE-06","text":"Idealization → symbolization → credit extension → material redemption → world money forms a spiral in which every dematerialization generates the possibility of intensified rematerialization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B01","text":"Independent private labours → private products → compulsion to exchange → retrospective social validity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A10","CH_V4GB_1DW0:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B02","text":"Product of labour = use-value ∧ value → concrete labour / abstract labour → material wealth ≠ value wealth.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A3","CH_V4GB_1DW0:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B03","text":"Lack of value's own appearance → alien natural form → relative value form ↔ equivalent form → polar representation of value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A12","CH_V4GB_1DW0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B04","text":"Competition of particular claims to equivalence → social exclusion of one commodity → general equivalent → money as the objective form of collective mediation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B05","text":"Commodity value → ideal price → sale → retrospective validation of private labour → purchase → intertwined commodity metamorphoses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B06","text":"Spatial-temporal separation of sale and purchase → autonomized moments of circulation → objective overall movement → possibility of crisis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A10","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FGS-B07","text":"Measure of value → token of circulation → hoard → means of payment → world money; functional mutation + vanished mediation → intensified autonomization and fetishization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AFM-B01","text":"Commodity appearance → use-value–value division → abstraction to social labour → polar value form → exclusive general equivalent → money → price → commodity metamorphosis → functional differentiation of money → world money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:AFM-B02","text":"Immediate unity → contradictory externalization → operational mediation → erasure of mediation → objective autonomization → universal dependence → possibility of crisis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:FGS7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-01","text":"The opposition between intrinsic value and arbitrary convention is replaced by the field of social-relational objectivity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD1","CH_V4GB_1DW0:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-02","text":"Universality is remapped from uniform participation to asymmetrical exclusion and concentrated capacity for representation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD3","CH_V4GB_2DAD:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-03","text":"The market is transformed from a neutral site of exchange into a retrospective validation mechanism for private labour and social proportions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-04","text":"Personal independence and economic dependence are no longer treated as opposites: the former is the personal form of a universal nexus of objective compulsion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-05","text":"Money is not divided into external kinds, but mapped as a unified value form with function-specifically opposed modes of existence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-06","text":"Crisis is classified neither as an external accident nor as an already explained necessity, but as the endogenous possibility of really separated, inwardly connected acts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MME-07","text":"State monetary order and national circulation are reclassified as limited levels within a value nexus that asserts its material universality only on the world market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the system unfolds from use-value, value substance, and value form to the particular functions of measure of value, money of account, means of circulation, hoard, means of payment, and world money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT1","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, the retrospective mediation of independent private labours organizes a spontaneous social division of labour through commodity value and money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the genesis of forms replaces explanations from utility, law, convention, quantity of money, or state power with the derivation of their limited efficacy from value form and commodity movement.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, social abstractions become practically real, while retrospective validity and temporal separation generate autonomous processes, dependence, and the possibility of crisis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:ALT4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the exposition itself carries out the asserted inversion: it reconstructs vanished mediation and reverses the causal direction suggested by appearance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:AS3","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-01","text":"The logical necessity of an exclusive money form does not fully explain how a particular commodity is practically selected and how its validity as equivalent is durably secured; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-02","text":"Abstract labour remains strained between universally human expenditure of labour and the specifically social form of validity of mutually independent private labours; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:MRT4","CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-03","text":"Value is supposed to be determined by socially necessary labour-time, but is validated only by a market whose judgment retrospectively alters the concrete social validity of the labour expended; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A6","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-04","text":"The derivation adheres to money material possessing value in itself, although signs, credit, and clearing assume real money functions; the boundary between functional representation and necessary material redemption remains mobile; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A15","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-05","text":"The separation of acts of circulation explains the formal possibility of crisis, but not the conditions of its necessary transition into an actual crisis; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:NX8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:FL-06","text":"The form of exchange developed from mutual recognition does not integrate the possibility of violent appropriation into its own genesis; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-01","text":"Use-value mutates from a material determination into a position-dependent condition of proving social usefulness; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-02","text":"The equivalent form mutates from a relational polar function into a socially monopolized money form and subsequently appears as an autonomous property of its bearer; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A13","CH_V4GB_2DAD:A9","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-03","text":"The commodity contradiction mutates from static unity into external movement and ultimately into the possibility of a violent reunification of separated moments; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:A19","CH_V4GB_3DGO:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MP-04","text":"Money mutates from ideal price expression through locally valid signs into a materially required form of payment and world money; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A14","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a decentralized validation machine in which social relations crystallize in things and whose intertwined movements form an uncontrolled interconnection.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:ALT4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not a sovereign center, but a mobile bearer of economic functions within universal objective dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:A4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-03","text":"Time is retroactive and asynchronous: past private labour acquires social validity only retrospectively, while separated acts generate future obligations and crisis risks.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:D16","CH_V4GB_3DGO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:HSI-04","text":"Effective intervention can stop neither at moral critique nor at monetary designation, but would have to transform the material mediation of production that reproduces the objective power of money.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:SD8","CH_V4GB_2DAD:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from commodity form through exchange and the emergence of money to the functional differentiation of money and its implication of crisis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B02","text":"The architecture is most strongly closed where commodity duality, the dual character of labour, social realization of value, and inversion of the apparent causality of money interlock.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1DW0:MRT2","CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B03","text":"The practical establishment of a particular money commodity and the conditions under which the formal possibility of crisis necessarily turns into an actual crisis remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B04","text":"The coherence is recursive rather than purely linear: the logical necessity of the money form is preserved through recurrent functional mutations, causal inversions, and material return movements.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT8","CH_V4GB_3DGO:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B05","text":"Axiomatic reduction is resisted by the practical process through which society excludes a money commodity, actually validates private labour, and actualizes a possibility of crisis; these transitions are structurally marked, but not fully generated.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DAD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DGO:D4","CH_V4GB_3DGO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_01:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 01–03","context":"1) Die Waare. · 2) Der Austauschprozess der Waaren. · 3) Das Geld oder die Waarencirculation."}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 04–06","order":2,"parents":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV","CH_V4GB_1AUV","CH_V4GB_2CKU"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_02@R001","sha256":"0a7860a9b8a08108a7a4265ea169507aa2d60bad2d3c6a9ce02022dedc169c7e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B01","text":"Das System erklärt, wie der Austausch rechtlich und wertmäßig äquivalenter Waren einen Wertüberschuss hervorbringen kann, ohne seine eigenen Austauschgesetze zu verletzen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B02","text":"Kapital wird von einer vorhandenen Geld- oder Sachmenge in eine rekursive Wertbewegung umbestimmt, deren Resultat keinen Abschluss, sondern einen erneuten Ausgangspunkt bildet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B03","text":"Die Zirkulation vermittelt die Verwertung, kann sie aber nicht erzeugen; ihre immanente Unzulänglichkeit erzwingt den Übergang zum produktiven Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A11","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B04","text":"Der gesellschaftsformübergreifende Arbeitsprozess wird kapitalistisch eingefasst, indem Kontrolle, Produkteigentum und Verwertungszweck seine technische Allgemeinform überlagern.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B05","text":"Die Differenz zwischen dem Wert der Arbeitskraft und dem Wert ihres Gebrauchs wird als zeitliche Überschreitung des bloßen Ersatzes ihrer Reproduktionskosten realisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B06","text":"Die Produktenwertanalyse zerlegt den scheinbar einheitlichen Produktionsbeitrag in die Übertragung vorhandenen Werts und die Erzeugung neuen Werts durch die Doppelseitigkeit lebendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B07","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv und kumulativ: Ergebnisse vergangener Arbeit werden zu Bedingungen neuer Arbeit, während jedes Verwertungsresultat den nächsten Kreislauf eröffnet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D3","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B08","text":"Die vorläufige Schließung erfolgt durch die funktionale Spaltung des Vorschusses in konstantes und variables Kapital, wobei nur der variable Teil sein Äquivalent reproduziert und einen Überschuss erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:A14","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Kapital ist die rekursive Identität eines Werts, der Geld-, Waren- und Produktionsform durchläuft, seine Größe verändert und aus dem Resultat erneut beginnt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Zirkulation ist notwendige Vermittlung, aber keine hinreichende Quelle des Mehrwerts; dessen Entstehung verlangt einen produktiven Prozess außerhalb der reinen Austauschakte.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Arbeitskraft trägt eine asymmetrische Doppelbestimmung: Ihr Wert wird vor ihrem Gebrauch festgelegt, während ihr Gebrauch einen größeren Wert erzeugen kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Die Warenform der Arbeitskraft setzt rechtliche Verfügungsfähigkeit und materielle Trennung von selbständigen Produktionsbedingungen zugleich voraus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Kapitalistische Produktion ist die Einheit von Arbeitsprozess und Verwertungsprozess unter der institutionellen Verbindung von Eigentum, Kontrolle und zeitlich verlängerter Wertbildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Derselbe unteilbare Arbeitsakt wirkt konkret als Gebrauchswertproduktion und abstrakt als gesellschaftlich quantifizierte Neuwertbildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Der Produktenwert besteht aus übertragenem vorhandenem Wert und durch lebendige Arbeit neu erzeugtem Wert; diese Bestandteile besitzen verschiedene Ursachen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Mehrwert entsteht durch die Fortsetzung lebendiger Arbeit über die zur Reproduktion des Arbeitskraftwerts notwendige Arbeitszeit hinaus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:A18","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Gesellschaftlich notwendige Arbeitszeit fungiert zugleich als Wertmaß, Produktionsnorm und gegenwartsbezogene Instanz der Neubewertung vorhandener Werte.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Konstantes und variables Kapital bezeichnen relationale Wertfunktionen, nicht natürliche Eigenschaften ihrer Stoffe, absolute Größen oder technischen Proportionen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Lebendige Arbeit ist der verborgene Attraktor der Kapitalbewegung, weil sie vorhandenen Kapitalwert erhält und zugleich den Neuwert erzeugt, aus dem Mehrwert hervorgeht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Der produzierte Mehrwert schließt die Bewegung nicht ab, sondern ermöglicht die Rückkehr des vergrößerten Geldwerts und dessen erneuten Vorschuss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-01","text":"Geld mutiert von einer Zirkulationsform unter anderen zur Erscheinungsform eines prozessierenden Werts; seine Identität liegt nun in der rekursiven Bewegung statt in der ruhenden Geldgestalt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-02","text":"Arbeitskraft wandert von der Marktware über ihren Gebrauch als lebendige Arbeit zur Wertfunktion des variablen Kapitals; dabei bleibt ihr Träger identisch, ihre systemische Funktion jedoch nicht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-03","text":"Gebrauchswert kehrt nicht als bloß stofflicher Gegenpol des Werts wieder, sondern wird erst zur Quelle der besonderen Wertschöpfungskraft der Arbeitskraft und dann zum Medium der Übertragung alten Werts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-04","text":"Zirkulation wird vom sichtbaren Gesamtmodell des Kapitals zum notwendigen, aber kausal untergeordneten Vermittlungsmoment der Produktion verschoben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-05","text":"Freiheit, Gleichheit und Eigentum behalten innerhalb des Vertrags Geltung, mutieren aber auf Produktionsebene zu Voraussetzungen asymmetrischer Verfügung über den Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A18","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-06","text":"Der Arbeitsprozess bleibt als technische Allgemeinform bestehen, wird jedoch durch Eigentum, Kontrolle und Verwertungsdauer in eine historisch bestimmte gesellschaftliche Funktion versetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-07","text":"Zeit eskaliert von der endlosen Wiederholung der Zirkulation über den Schwellenpunkt zwischen notwendiger Arbeit und Mehrarbeit zur gegenwärtigen Neubewertung vergangener Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-08","text":"Produktionsmittel werden von objektiven Faktoren des Arbeitsprozesses in konstantes Kapital umcodiert; ihre stoffliche Rolle bleibt, ihre werttheoretische Funktion wird präzisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D12","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-01","text":"Der Vergleich von W–G–W und G–W–G′ bleibt ein lokales Beweisverfahren; auf Clusterebene skaliert allein die daraus gewonnene Bestimmung des Kapitals als rekursive Wertidentität.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-02","text":"Die Klassifikation von Arbeitsgegenstand, Arbeitsmittel und Produkt bleibt eine lokale Funktionsanalyse; global tragend wird sie erst durch die Doppelseitigkeit des Arbeitsakts und seiner Wertwirkungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:A5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-03","text":"Verschleiß, Abfall und stoffliche Aufnahme sind lokale Grenzfälle der Wertübertragung; auf Clusterebene stützen sie die allgemeine Trennung von übertragenem Wert und Neuwert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-04","text":"Die historische Erzeugung des freien Arbeitskraftverkäufers skaliert als unverzichtbare Systemvoraussetzung, bleibt aber genealogisch außerhalb der entwickelten Produktionsanalyse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A15","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-05","text":"Die Rechtskategorien der Zirkulation werden nicht aufgehoben, sondern auf der aktuellen Ebene als Oberflächenform eines Produktionsverhältnisses mit asymmetrischem Kommando umcodiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A18","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-06","text":"Die Unterscheidung von konstantem und variablem Kapital überschreitet ihre lokale Definitionsfunktion, weil sie die gesamte vorausgehende Bewegung von Kauf, Produktion, Werterhaltung und Mehrwertbildung terminal integriert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-01","text":"Weder Äquivalententausch noch bloße Zirkulation können gesellschaftlichen Mehrwert erzeugen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-02","text":"Produktionsmittel sind keine autonome Quelle neuen Werts und können sich nicht kraft ihrer Gegenständlichkeit selbst verwerten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:NX3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-03","text":"Weder stofflicher Wareninhalt noch technische Gestalt des Arbeitsprozesses bestimmen aus sich die gesellschaftliche Kapitalform.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-04","text":"Mehrwert kann weder aus der Addition vorhandener Werte noch aus deren bloßem Wiedererscheinen im Produkt hervorgehen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-05","text":"Stoffliche Teilnahme am Produkt, produktive Nützlichkeit und wertmäßige Zurechnung dürfen nicht als deckungsgleiche Ordnungen behandelt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-06","text":"Der freie Arbeitskraftverkäufer ist weder Naturgegebenheit noch durch Warenzirkulation als solche bereits gesetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX14","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-01","text":"Falsch sein muss jedes Gesamtmodell, das die Rechtsgleichheit des Austauschs als vollständige Bestimmung des Kapitalverhältnisses behandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX16","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-02","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine autonome Selbstverwertung des Werts, die lebendige Arbeit nur als äußerliche Hilfe eines bereits selbsttätigen Kapitals behandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-03","text":"Technische Wirksamkeit, Nützlichkeit und Produktivitätssteigerung dürfen nicht als selbständige Quellen von Tauschwert oder Neuwert fungieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-04","text":"Historische Anschaffungskosten können keine unveränderliche Wertidentität garantieren, weil gegenwärtige Produktionsbedingungen vorhandene Werte neu bestimmen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-05","text":"Tatsächlich verausgabte Arbeit darf nicht unabhängig von Zweckmäßigkeit, Normalität und gesellschaftlicher Notwendigkeit als wertbildend gelten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-01","text":"Die nicht verfügbare Möglichkeit selbständiger Produktion strukturiert das System: Könnte der Arbeiter über seine Produktionsbedingungen verfügen, müsste Arbeitskraft nicht als Ware auftreten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SNX2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-02","text":"Ein erreichbarer Endzustand der Verwertung ist ausgeschlossen; jedes Resultat bleibt unvollständig, solange es nicht erneut als Vorschuss fungiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SNX1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-03","text":"Eine Mehrwertquelle außerhalb fortgesetzter lebendiger Arbeit sowie ein selbständiger dritter Existenzort des Werts werden ontologisch nicht zugelassen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-04","text":"Die Herrschaftsform bleibt am fertigen Gebrauchswert abwesend; sie wird nur durch die Rekonstruktion von Eigentum, Zeit, Kontrolle und Prozessstellung sichtbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SNX4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-05","text":"Die vollständige Veräußerung der Person bleibt ausgeschlossen, weil das Kapitalverhältnis den rechtlich verfügungsfähigen Besitzer für wiederholte, zeitlich begrenzte Verkäufe seiner Arbeitskraft erhalten muss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SNX4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-01","text":"Die formale Äquivalenz des Arbeitskraftkaufs erzeugt keine materielle Symmetrie, weil Wertzahlung und wertschöpfender Gebrauch verschiedenen Bestimmungen und Zeitabschnitten angehören. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-03","CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-02","text":"Arbeitskraft wird erst durch eine dreistufige Funktionsmutation vollständig bestimmt: als gekaufte Ware, als lebendige Arbeit und als sich reproduzierender sowie überschießender variabler Kapitalteil. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-03","CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-10","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-03","text":"Zirkulation und Produktion bilden eine asymmetrische Schließung: Der Kauf ermöglicht die Wertschöpfung außerhalb der Zirkulation, deren Resultat erst durch die Rückkehr in Geldform als Kapitalbewegung vollendet wird. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-12","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-04","text":"Die Verbindung materieller Produktionsmittellosigkeit mit kapitalistischer Kontrolle verwandelt den rechtmäßigen Kauf eines zeitlich begrenzten Gebrauchs in die Aneignung des durch Mehrarbeit erzeugten Wertüberschusses. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:GA-05","CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-05","text":"Die Darstellung des Kapitals als automatisches Subjekt ist nur operativ haltbar, wenn seine scheinbare Selbstbewegung als Einverleibung und doppelte Nutzung lebendiger Arbeit rekonstruiert wird. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-01","CL_V4GB_02:GA-11","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT8","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-06","text":"Gesellschaftlich notwendige Arbeitszeit verbindet Reproduktion, Produktionsdisziplin und Revaluation: Sie bestimmt den Arbeitskraftwert, normiert den Vollzug und kann vorhandene Warenwerte rückwirkend verändern. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-09","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A16","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-07","text":"Produktivitätssteigerung kann Stoffdurchsatz und übertragene Wertmasse erhöhen, ohne die Neuwertmenge einer gegebenen Arbeitsdauer zu erhöhen; technische Expansion und Verwertung sind daher nicht identisch. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-07","CH_V4GB_1AUV:D8","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-08","text":"Rechtliche Selbstverfügung und materieller Verkaufszwang erzeugen keine auflösbare Inkonsistenz, sondern die Bedingung, unter der der freie Vertrag in asymmetrisches Produktionskommando übergehen kann. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:GA-05","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-01","text":"Kapital erhält den ontologischen Status eines verteilten Verhältnisses: Seine Identität liegt weder im Geld noch in Produktionsmitteln, sondern in der reproduzierten Kopplung von Zirkulation, Eigentum und lebendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-02","text":"Die erzeugte Zeitordnung ist dreifach: rekursive Zirkulationszeit, schwellenförmig geteilte Arbeitszeit und gegenwartsbezogene Revaluationszeit vergangener Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-03","text":"Das Arbeitssubjekt wird zugleich zum freien Warenbesitzer, zum Objekt asymmetrischer Prozesskontrolle und zur alleinigen Quelle des Neuwerts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-04","text":"Der Kapitalist ist nicht schöpferische Ursache des Mehrwerts, sondern bewusster Träger einer objektivierten Verwertungsfunktion, deren Wirksamkeit von fremder lebendiger Arbeit abhängt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX11","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-05","text":"Kapitalistische Kausalität ist überlagert statt linear: Derselbe Arbeitsakt verändert Stoff, überträgt alten Wert und erzeugt Neuwert, ohne dass diese Wirkungen kausal identisch werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-06","text":"Gleichheit und Ausbeutung bilden keinen einfachen logischen Gegensatz, sondern gehören verschiedenen Ebenen desselben Prozesses an: dem äquivalenten Vertrag und dem kontrollierten Gebrauch der gekauften Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A18","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-01","text":"Die primäre Schleife lautet: Wertvorschuss → Produktion eines Überschusses → vergrößerter Rückfluss → erneuter Vorschuss; ihr Resultat reproduziert den Ausgangszwang auf höherer Größenstufe.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-02","text":"Die zentrale Eskalation verläuft von der dreifachen Ausschließung zirkulatorischer Mehrwertquellen über die besondere Ware Arbeitskraft zur Mehrwertproduktion außerhalb der Zirkulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:FGS5","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-03","text":"Produktion bildet eine zweite Schleife: Produkte vergangener Arbeit werden Produktionsmittel, deren Wert durch lebendige Arbeit erhalten wird und in neuen Produkten erneut erscheint.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A7","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-04","text":"Der Wertersatzpunkt fungiert als Phasenübergang: Dieselbe Arbeit bleibt technisch kontinuierlich, wechselt aber jenseits der notwendigen Arbeitszeit von Reproduktion zu Verwertung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D9","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A18","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-05","text":"Gesellschaftliche Normalität erzeugt eine Normierungsschleife, in der Wertmaß, Kontrolle zweckmäßiger Verausgabung und nachträgliche Zurechnung einander stabilisieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A13","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-06","text":"Lebendige Arbeit ist der dominante Attraktor: Jede scheinbar autonome Kapitalfunktion konvergiert auf ihre Fähigkeit, vergangenen Wert zu erhalten, den Arbeitskraftwert zu ersetzen und Mehrwert zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-07","text":"Gegenwärtige Wertbedingungen bilden eine destabilisierende Rückkopplung, weil sie vorhandene Werte revidieren und damit die Größen des zirkulierenden Kapitalwerts ohne Änderung seiner früheren Produktionsgeschichte verschieben können.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B01","text":"Warenzirkulation → Geldform → Vergleich der Kreisläufe → Unterscheidung von Geld als Geld und Geld als Kapital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B02","text":"Ausschluss von Äquivalententausch, Nichtäquivalententausch und isolierter Produktion als hinreichenden Mehrwertquellen → widersprüchliche Suchbedingung innerhalb und außerhalb der Zirkulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS5","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B03","text":"Kauf einer Ware zu ihrem Wert + rechtliche Verfügbarkeit + materielle Produktionsmittellosigkeit → Arbeitskraft als besondere Ware.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D8","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B04","text":"Arbeitskraftkauf → Übergang in die Produktion → kapitalistische Kontrolle → produktiver Gebrauch → Wertüberschuss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B05","text":"Arbeitsprozess + Wertbildungsprozess → Doppelseitigkeit desselben Arbeitsakts → Gebrauchswertproduktion, Wertübertragung und Neuwertbildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B06","text":"Produktenwert → übertragener Produktionsmittelwert + neu geschaffener Wert → Arbeitskraftäquivalent + Mehrwert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B07","text":"Vorschuss → konstantes und variables Kapital → Mehrwertproduktion → vergrößerter Rückfluss → erneuter Vorschuss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:FGS7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B01","text":"Geldform → rekursive Wertbewegung → Scheitern zirkulatorischer Mehrwerterklärungen → Arbeitskraft → verborgene Produktion → zeitlicher Wertersatzpunkt → Mehrarbeit → konstantes und variables Kapital → erneuerte Kapitalbewegung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS8","CH_V4GB_2CKU:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B02","text":"Historische Trennung → doppelt freie Arbeitskraft → äquivalenter Vertrag → kapitalistische Kontrolle → nicht zusätzlich vergütete Arbeitsdauer → reproduziertes Kapitalverhältnis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A15","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B03","text":"Negative Ausschließung → analytische Zerlegung → kontrollierte Variation der Wertwirkungen → funktionale Reklassifikation der Kapitalbestandteile.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-01","text":"Geld und Kapital werden von verschiedenen Stoffen zu verschiedenen Bewegungsweisen desselben prozessierenden Werts umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ME1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-02","text":"Marktgleichheit und Produktionskommando werden als kompatible Ebenen statt als einander ausschließende Gesamtbeschreibungen lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ME5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-03","text":"Der kapitalistische Charakter der Produktion wird aus der Technik entfernt und in die Verbindung von Eigentum, Kontrolle und Verwertungszeit verlagert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-04","text":"Die Unterscheidung objektiver und subjektiver Produktionsfaktoren wird durch die wertfunktionale Unterscheidung von konstantem und variablem Kapital überformt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D12","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-05","text":"Produktivkraft, Gebrauchswertmasse und Wertschöpfung werden entkoppelt; technische Steigerung ist nicht länger als autonome Wertvermehrung interpretierbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-06","text":"Der Produktenwert wird als zeitliche Schichtung von gegenwärtig bewertetem vergangenem Arbeitswert und neu vergegenständlichter lebendiger Arbeit lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-07","text":"Ausbeutung wird von Preisbetrug und Unterbezahlung gelöst und als Resultat des rechtmäßigen Kaufs einer zeitlich überschießend nutzbaren Arbeitskraft rekonstruiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberfläche erscheinen Kreislaufformen, Produktionsfaktoren, Arbeitsvertrag, Produktenwert sowie konstantes und variables Kapital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B02","text":"Strukturell überlagern sich Äquivalententausch, Eigentumsordnung, Produktionskontrolle, Arbeitsprozess und Verwertungsprozess, obwohl ihre Faktoren stofflich identisch bleiben können.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategisch wird die Erklärung von Marktillusionen und moralischen Zuschreibungen auf Prozessstellung, Zeitteilung und spezifische Wertfunktion verlagert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B04","text":"Ontologisch und temporal erscheint Kapital als prozessierende Wertidentität, deren Reproduktion von Schwellenzeit, Trägerwechsel und gegenwartsbezogener Revaluation abhängt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B05","text":"Methodologisch vollzieht die Darstellung ihre These durch immanente Widerspruchsbildung, rekonstruktive Zerlegung und kontrollierte Variation scheinbar gekoppelter Wertwirkungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-01","text":"Die Darstellung des Werts als automatisches Subjekt kollidiert mit dem Nachweis seiner vollständigen doppelten Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT8","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT9","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-02","text":"Rechtliche Freiheit und materielle Verkaufsnotwendigkeit bleiben konstitutiv gespannt, weil dieselbe Selbstverfügung den Übergang in asymmetrisches Produktionskommando ermöglicht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-03","text":"Die Ableitung des Produkteigentums komprimiert den Übergang vom zeitlich begrenzten Kauf des Arbeitskraftgebrauchs zur vollständigen Aneignung seines Produkts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT8","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-04","text":"Die Bindung der Wertübertragung an produktiven Wertverlust steht unter Spannung zur externen Revaluation noch brauchbarer Produktionsmittel.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-05","text":"Wert muss an einen Gebrauchswertträger gebunden sein und zugleich gegenüber jedem bestimmten Träger gleichgültig bleiben; diese doppelte Bestimmung wird nicht vollständig ontologisch aufgelöst.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-06","text":"Gesellschaftliche Notwendigkeit, normale Vernutzung und durchschnittliche Lebensdauer tragen die Zurechnung, ohne dass ihre konkrete gesellschaftliche Feststellung innerhalb des Clusters abgeleitet wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-01","text":"Gebrauchswert mutiert vom ausgeschlossenen stofflichen Erklärungsgrund zur entscheidenden Differenz der Arbeitskraft und zum Medium der Wertübertragung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-02","text":"Geld mutiert zu Kapital, sobald seine Form nicht mehr als ruhende Größe, sondern als rekursive Identität einer sich vergrößernden Wertbewegung bestimmt wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-03","text":"Arbeitskraft mutiert von einer verkauften Fähigkeit über lebendige Arbeit zum variablen Kapitalteil, der sein Äquivalent reproduziert und Mehrwert erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-04","text":"Zeit mutiert von endloser Zirkulationswiederholung zur inneren Produktionsschwelle und anschließend zur Instanz gegenwärtiger Neubewertung vergangener Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als überlagerte Doppelmaschine: Ein stofflicher Arbeitsprozess verwandelt Gebrauchswerte, während ein Wertprozess dieselben Faktoren funktional neu codiert und in die Kapitalzirkulation zurückführt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt spaltet sich in den Kapitalisten als bewussten Funktionsträger und den Arbeiter als rechtlich freien Verkäufer, kontrollierten Prozessfaktor und Quelle des Neuwerts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A7","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist zugleich kreisförmig, schwellenförmig und revisionär: Sie wiederholt den Vorschuss, teilt den Arbeitstag und bewertet vergangene Arbeit aus der Gegenwart neu.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-04","text":"Strategische Intervention bleibt an den Grenzen des Arbeitskraftgebrauchs, der Kontrolle des Vollzugs und der gesellschaftlichen Normierung von Arbeitszeit möglich, nicht an der bloßen Gültigkeit des Äquivalententauschs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B01","text":"Die extrahierte Architektur reicht aus, um den Übergang von der Zirkulationsform über die Arbeitskraft und den Produktionsprozess bis zur funktionalen Kapitaldifferenz zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B02","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bleibt kohärent, sofern Gebrauchswert und Wert, konkrete und abstrakte Arbeit sowie Arbeitsprozess und Verwertungsprozess als verbundene, aber nicht identische Bestimmungen erhalten bleiben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B03","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die historische Erzeugung der Eigentumsordnung, die Grenzen des verfügbaren Arbeitstags und die gesellschaftliche Feststellung normaler Wertzurechnungsbedingungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B04","text":"Die stärkste Architektur verbindet die negative Ausschließung zirkulatorischer Mehrwertquellen mit dem zeitlichen Nachweis der Mehrarbeit und der kontrollierten Entkopplung von Neuwert und Wertübertragung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B05","text":"Einer statischen Axiomatisierung widersteht die notwendige Darstellungsbewegung selbst: Die Arbeitskraft muss aus dem Scheitern der Zirkulationserklärungen hervorgehen, der Arbeitsprozess kapitalistisch umcodiert und die Wertfunktion an ihren Grenzfällen geprüft werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211702855282Z_b724ee46","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 04–06","source_sha256":"0a7860a9b8a08108a7a4265ea169507aa2d60bad2d3c6a9ce02022dedc169c7e","sha256":"cc471aeefdac0be3cb083d619df8cd5fe1cd8c26b12ac73bf5f67726c83a5a26","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:17:02.856750+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B01","text":"The system explains how the exchange of legally and value-equivalent commodities can produce a value surplus without violating its own laws of exchange.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B02","text":"Capital is redefined from an existing sum of money or material goods into a recursive movement of value whose result forms not a conclusion but a renewed point of departure.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B03","text":"Circulation mediates valorization but cannot generate it; its immanent insufficiency compels the transition to the productive use of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A11","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B04","text":"The labour process that extends across social forms is capitalistically framed insofar as control, ownership of the product, and the purpose of valorization overlay its general technical form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B05","text":"The difference between the value of labour-power and the value of its use is realized as a temporal excess over the mere replacement of its reproduction costs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B06","text":"Analysis of product value decomposes the apparently unitary contribution to production into the transfer of existing value and the creation of new value through the dual character of living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B07","text":"The movement is recursive and cumulative: results of past labour become conditions of new labour, while every result of valorization opens the next circuit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D3","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AS-B08","text":"The provisional closure occurs through the functional division of the advance into constant and variable capital, whereby only the variable part reproduces its equivalent and generates a surplus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:A14","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Capital is the recursive identity of a value that passes through money, commodity, and production forms, alters its magnitude, and begins anew from the result.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Circulation is necessary mediation, but not a sufficient source of surplus value; its emergence requires a productive process outside the pure act of exchange.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Labour-power bears an asymmetric dual determination: its value is established before its use, while its use can generate a greater value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The commodity form of labour-power presupposes both legal capacity of disposal and material separation from independent conditions of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Capitalist production is the unity of the labour process and the valorization process under the institutional connection of ownership, control, and temporally extended value formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The same indivisible act of labour operates concretely as use-value production and abstractly as socially quantified formation of new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Product value consists of transferred existing value and value newly created by living labour; these components have different causes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Surplus value arises through the continuation of living labour beyond the labour time necessary for reproducing the value of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:A18","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Socially necessary labour time functions simultaneously as measure of value, norm of production, and present-oriented instance of the revaluation of existing values.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Constant and variable capital designate relational value-functions, not natural properties of their materials, absolute magnitudes, or technical proportions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Living labour is the hidden attractor of the movement of capital because it preserves existing capital value and simultaneously generates the new value from which surplus value arises.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The produced surplus value does not conclude the movement, but enables the return of the expanded money-value and its renewed advance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-01","text":"Money mutates from a form of circulation among others into the form of appearance of a value in process; its identity now lies in recursive movement rather than in the static money-form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-02","text":"Labour-power moves from a market commodity through its use as living labour to the value-function of variable capital; its bearer remains identical, but its systemic function does not.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-03","text":"Use-value returns not as a merely material counterpart to value, but first becomes the source of labour-power's distinctive value-creating force and then the medium of the transfer of old value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-04","text":"Circulation is displaced from the visible overall model of capital into a necessary but causally subordinate moment of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-05","text":"Freedom, equality, and property retain validity within the contract, but mutate at the level of production into conditions of asymmetric disposal over the use of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A18","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-06","text":"The labour process persists as a general technical form, but is placed into a historically determinate social function through ownership, control, and duration of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-07","text":"Time escalates from the endless repetition of circulation through the threshold point between necessary labour and surplus labour to the present revaluation of past labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RMD-08","text":"Means of production are recoded from objective factors of the labour process into constant capital; their material role remains, while their value-theoretical function is specified.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D12","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-01","text":"The comparison of W–G–W and G–W–G′ remains a local procedure of proof; at cluster level, only the determination of capital thereby gained as recursive value-identity scales.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-02","text":"The classification of object of labour, instrument of labour, and product remains a local functional analysis; it becomes globally load-bearing only through the dual character of the labour act and its effects on value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:A5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-03","text":"Wear, waste, and material absorption are local limiting cases of value transfer; at cluster level, they support the general separation of transferred value and new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-04","text":"The historical production of the free seller of labour-power scales as an indispensable systemic presupposition, but remains genealogically outside the developed analysis of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A15","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-05","text":"The legal categories of circulation are not abolished, but recoded at the current level as the surface form of a relation of production with asymmetric command.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A18","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:CGD-06","text":"The distinction between constant and variable capital exceeds its local definitional function because it terminally integrates the entire preceding movement of purchase, production, preservation of value, and formation of surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-01","text":"Neither exchange of equivalents nor mere circulation can generate social surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-02","text":"Means of production are not an autonomous source of new value and cannot valorize themselves by virtue of their objecthood.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:NX3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-03","text":"Neither the material content of commodities nor the technical form of the labour process determines the social form of capital from itself.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-04","text":"Surplus value can arise neither from the addition of existing values nor from their mere reappearance in the product.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-05","text":"Material participation in the product, productive usefulness, and value attribution must not be treated as congruent orders.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:GNX-06","text":"The free seller of labour-power is neither a natural given nor already posited by commodity circulation as such.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX14","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-01","text":"Any overall model that treats the legal equality of exchange as the complete determination of the capital relation must be false.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX16","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-02","text":"Excluded is an autonomous self-valorization of value that treats living labour merely as external assistance to capital already active on its own.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-03","text":"Technical efficacy, usefulness, and increases in productivity must not function as independent sources of exchange-value or new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-04","text":"Historical acquisition costs cannot guarantee an unchanging value-identity, because present conditions of production redetermine existing values.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:DBN-05","text":"Actually expended labour must not count as value-creating independently of expediency, normality, and social necessity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-01","text":"The unavailable possibility of independent production itself structures the system: if the worker could dispose over his conditions of production, labour-power would not have to appear as a commodity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SNX2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-02","text":"An attainable final state of valorization is excluded; every result remains incomplete so long as it does not function anew as an advance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SNX1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-03","text":"A source of surplus value outside continued living labour, as well as an independent third locus of existence of value, is not ontologically admitted.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-04","text":"The form of domination remains absent from the finished use-value; it becomes visible only through the reconstruction of ownership, time, control, and process-position.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SNX4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSA-05","text":"The complete alienation of the person remains excluded because the capital relation must preserve the legally capable possessor for repeated, temporally limited sales of his labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SNX4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-01","text":"The formal equivalence of the purchase of labour-power produces no material symmetry because value payment and value-creating use belong to different determinations and temporal intervals. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-03","CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-02","text":"Labour-power is fully determined only through a three-stage functional mutation: as a purchased commodity, as living labour, and as a reproducing and surplus-producing variable part of capital. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-03","CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-10","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-03","text":"Circulation and production form an asymmetric closure: purchase enables value creation outside circulation, whose result is completed as a movement of capital only through its return to money form. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-12","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-04","text":"The connection of material deprivation of means of production with capitalist control transforms the lawful purchase of a temporally limited use into the appropriation of the value surplus produced by surplus labour. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:GA-05","CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-05","text":"The representation of capital as an automatic subject is operationally tenable only if its apparent self-movement is reconstructed as the incorporation and dual use of living labour. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-01","CL_V4GB_02:GA-11","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT8","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-06","text":"Socially necessary labour time connects reproduction, production discipline, and revaluation: it determines the value of labour-power, norms its execution, and can retroactively alter existing commodity values. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-09","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A16","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-07","text":"An increase in productivity can increase material throughput and the mass of transferred value without increasing the quantity of new value in a given duration of labour; technical expansion and valorization are therefore not identical. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-07","CH_V4GB_1AUV:D8","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:XD-08","text":"Legal self-disposal and material compulsion to sell produce not a resolvable inconsistency, but the condition under which the free contract can pass into asymmetric command over production. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:GA-05","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-01","text":"Capital receives the ontological status of a distributed relation: its identity lies neither in money nor in means of production, but in the reproduced coupling of circulation, ownership, and living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-02","text":"The produced temporal order is threefold: recursive circulation time, threshold-like divided labour time, and present-oriented revaluation time of past labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-03","text":"The subject of labour becomes simultaneously the free owner of a commodity, the object of asymmetric process-control, and the sole source of new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-04","text":"The capitalist is not the creative cause of surplus value, but the conscious bearer of an objectified valorization-function whose efficacy depends on the living labour of others.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX11","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-05","text":"Capitalist causality is layered rather than linear: the same act of labour transforms material, transfers old value, and creates new value, without these effects becoming causally identical.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:BSD-06","text":"Equality and exploitation form no simple logical opposition, but belong to different levels of the same process: the equivalent contract and the controlled use of purchased labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A18","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-01","text":"The primary loop is: advance of value → production of a surplus → expanded return flow → renewed advance; its result reproduces the compulsion of departure at a higher scale of magnitude.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-02","text":"The central escalation proceeds from the threefold exclusion of circulatory sources of surplus value through the special commodity labour-power to the production of surplus value outside circulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:FGS5","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-03","text":"Production forms a second loop: products of past labour become means of production, whose value is preserved by living labour and reappears anew in new products.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A7","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-04","text":"The point of value replacement functions as a phase transition: the same labour remains technically continuous, but beyond necessary labour time shifts from reproduction to valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D9","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A18","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-05","text":"Social normality generates a normalization loop in which the measure of value, control of expedient expenditure, and subsequent attribution stabilize one another.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A13","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-06","text":"Living labour is the dominant attractor: every apparently autonomous capital function converges on its capacity to preserve past value, replace the value of labour-power, and generate surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:RLE-07","text":"Present value conditions form a destabilizing feedback because they revise existing values and can thereby shift the magnitudes of circulating capital value without altering its earlier production history.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B01","text":"Commodity circulation → money form → comparison of the circuits → distinction between money as money and money as capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B02","text":"Exclusion of exchange of equivalents, exchange of non-equivalents, and isolated production as sufficient sources of surplus value → contradictory condition of search within and outside circulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS5","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B03","text":"Purchase of a commodity at its value + legal availability + material deprivation of means of production → labour-power as a special commodity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D8","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B04","text":"Purchase of labour-power → transition into production → capitalist control → productive use → value surplus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B05","text":"Labour process + value-formation process → dual character of the same act of labour → use-value production, value transfer, and formation of new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B06","text":"Product value → transferred value of means of production + newly created value → labour-power equivalent + surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FGS-B07","text":"Advance → constant and variable capital → production of surplus value → expanded return flow → renewed advance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:FGS7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:FGS8","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B01","text":"Money form → recursive movement of value → failure of circulatory explanations of surplus value → labour-power → hidden production → temporal point of value replacement → surplus labour → constant and variable capital → renewed movement of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS8","CH_V4GB_2CKU:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B02","text":"Historical separation → doubly free labour-power → equivalent contract → capitalist control → additionally uncompensated duration of labour → reproduced capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A15","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B03","text":"Negative exclusion → analytical decomposition → controlled variation of effects on value → functional reclassification of the components of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-01","text":"Money and capital are remapped from different materials into different modes of movement of the same value in process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ME1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-02","text":"Market equality and command over production become legible as compatible levels rather than mutually exclusive overall descriptions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ME5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-03","text":"The capitalist character of production is removed from technology and relocated into the connection of ownership, control, and valorization time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-04","text":"The distinction between objective and subjective factors of production is overlaid by the value-functional distinction between constant and variable capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:D12","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-05","text":"Productive force, mass of use-values, and value creation are decoupled; technical increase is no longer interpretable as autonomous augmentation of value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-06","text":"Product value becomes legible as a temporal stratification of presently evaluated past labour-value and newly objectified living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MME-07","text":"Exploitation is detached from price fraud and underpayment and reconstructed as the result of the lawful purchase of labour-power usable for a temporally excessive duration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B01","text":"On the surface appear forms of circulation, factors of production, the labour contract, product value, and constant and variable capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B02","text":"Structurally, exchange of equivalents, property order, control over production, labour process, and valorization process overlap, although their factors may remain materially identical.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT2","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, explanation is displaced from market illusions and moral attributions to process-position, division of time, and specific value-function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B04","text":"Ontologically and temporally, capital appears as a value-identity in process, whose reproduction depends on threshold time, change of bearer, and present-oriented revaluation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B05","text":"Methodologically, the exposition enacts its thesis through immanent formation of contradiction, reconstructive decomposition, and controlled variation of apparently coupled effects on value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:AS3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:AS2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-01","text":"The representation of value as an automatic subject collides with the demonstration of its complete double dependence on living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT8","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT9","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-02","text":"Legal freedom and material necessity to sell remain constitutively tense because the same self-disposal enables the transition into asymmetric command over production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-03","text":"The derivation of ownership of the product compresses the transition from the temporally limited purchase of the use of labour-power to the complete appropriation of its product.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT8","CH_V4GB_1AUV:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-04","text":"The binding of value transfer to productive loss of value stands in tension with the external revaluation of still usable means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-05","text":"Value must be bound to a bearer of use-value and at the same time remain indifferent to every determinate bearer; this dual determination is not fully resolved ontologically.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:FL-06","text":"Social necessity, normal wear, and average lifespan support attribution without their concrete social determination being derived within the cluster.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT7","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-01","text":"Use-value mutates from the excluded material ground of explanation into the decisive difference of labour-power and the medium of value transfer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX1","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:DNX2","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-02","text":"Money mutates into capital as soon as its form is determined no longer as a static magnitude but as the recursive identity of an expanding movement of value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:NX2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-03","text":"Labour-power mutates from a sold capacity through living labour into the variable part of capital that reproduces its equivalent and generates surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A12","CH_V4GB_1AUV:A1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MP-04","text":"Time mutates from endless repetition of circulation into the internal threshold of production and subsequently into the instance of the present revaluation of past labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a layered double machine: a material labour process transforms use-values, while a value process functionally recodes the same factors and returns them to the circulation of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:D6","CH_V4GB_2CKU:ALT2","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject divides into the capitalist as conscious bearer of a function and the worker as legally free seller, controlled process-factor, and source of new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A7","CH_V4GB_ZKDV:D10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is simultaneously circular, threshold-like, and revisionary: it repeats the advance, divides the working day, and revalues past labour from the present.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:A6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:ALT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:HSI-04","text":"Strategic intervention remains possible at the boundaries of the use of labour-power, control of its execution, and the social normalization of labour time, not at the mere validity of exchange of equivalents.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1AUV:A10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:SD3","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted architecture suffices to reconstruct the transition from the form of circulation through labour-power and the production process to the functional distinction within capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT1","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT1","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction remains coherent provided that use-value and value, concrete and abstract labour, as well as labour process and valorization process are retained as connected but non-identical determinations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT4","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT4","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B03","text":"What remain underdetermined are the historical production of the property order, the limits of the available working day, and the social determination of normal conditions of value attribution.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT6","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT3","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B04","text":"The strongest architecture connects the negative exclusion of circulatory sources of surplus value with the temporal demonstration of surplus labour and the controlled decoupling of new value and value transfer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT5","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT5","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B05","text":"The necessary movement of exposition itself resists a static axiomatization: labour-power must emerge from the failure of explanations based on circulation, the labour process must be capitalistically recoded, and the value-function tested in its limiting cases.","refs":["CH_V4GB_ZKDV:MRT10","CH_V4GB_1AUV:MRT10","CH_V4GB_2CKU:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_02:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 04–06","context":"Zweites Kapitel. Die Verwandlung von Geld in Kapital. · 1) Arbeitsprozess und Verwerthungsprozess. · 2) Constantes Kapital und variables Kapital."}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 07–09","order":3,"parents":["CH_V4GB_3DRD","CH_V4GB_4DAR","CH_V4GB_4D_2"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_03@R001","sha256":"71e352ed8dd2481d0c7ad23ce85f79e3ea196b088bb1998df37e1273c62ffabb","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-01","text":"Der sichtbare Wertüberschuss muss zunächst auf seine Quelle und sein proportionales Maß zurückgeführt werden, bevor seine zeitliche und gesellschaftliche Erzeugungsweise bestimmbar wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-02","text":"Die funktionelle Trennung von konstantem und variablem Kapital isoliert lebendige Arbeit als Quelle des Mehrwerts und übersetzt Verwertung in das Verhältnis von Mehrarbeit zu notwendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-03","text":"Das exakte Verhältnis der beiden Teile des Arbeitstags bestimmt deren Proportion, lässt aber die Gesamtdauer offen und verwandelt quantitative Messbarkeit in eine unentschiedene Grenzfrage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-04","text":"Der Zweck der Mehrwertproduktion, die Nutzung vorgeschossener Produktionsmittel und der Konkurrenzzwang treiben die offene Mehrarbeitszeit über individuelle Erhaltungsinteressen hinaus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-05","text":"Weil der vereinzelte Arbeitskraftverkäufer diese Expansion nicht begrenzen kann, mutiert die formale Zeitrelation zum Klassenkampf um eine vollstreckbare gesellschaftliche Schranke.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-06","text":"Die Bewegung verläuft analytisch, antinomisch und rekursiv von der Mehrwertrate über zerstörerische Zeitaneignung zur gesetzlichen Trennung von Verkaufszeit und Eigenzeit; ihre Schließung bleibt wegen fortgesetzter Umgehung vorläufig.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Konstantes Kapital überträgt vorhandenen Wert, während ausschließlich der durch Arbeitskraft vermittelte Prozess neuen Wert erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A3","CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Notwendige Arbeit reproduziert den Wert der Arbeitskraft; Arbeit jenseits dieser Reproduktionszeit erzeugt Mehrwert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A7","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Das Verhältnis von Mehrwert zu variablem Kapital ist zugleich monetäres Verwertungsmaß, zeitliches Verhältnis und Bestimmung des Exploitationsgrades.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Der Arbeitstag besteht aus notwendiger Arbeit und Mehrarbeit, ohne dass diese Zerlegung seine absolute Dauer festlegt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A15","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Die Bestimmtheit der notwendigen Arbeitszeit erzeugt keine bestimmte Gesamtlänge, weil die Mehrarbeitszeit innerhalb elastischer physischer und sozialer Schranken variabel bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Mehrwertproduktion ist der systemische Zweck, der Kapital zur größtmöglichen Aneignung lebendiger Arbeitszeit drängt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A17","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Der Warentausch legitimiert entgegengesetzte Ansprüche auf die Gebrauchsdauer der Arbeitskraft, enthält aber kein Maß, das zwischen ihnen entscheidet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Konkurrenz verwandelt den Verwertungszweck in äußeren Zwang und macht den vereinzelten Arbeiter wie den einzelnen Kapitalisten unfähig, eine stabile Grenze freiwillig herzustellen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Der Normalarbeitstag entsteht nur als kollektiv erzwungene, vollstreckbare und institutionell kontrollierte Schranke kapitalistischer Zeitaneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A17","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Arbeitskraft ist keine gewöhnlich konsumierbare Ware, weil ihre gegenwärtige Nutzung ihre künftige Reproduktion, Lebensdauer und erneute Verkäuflichkeit verändert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Lohnform und Vertragsgleichheit verschleiern gemeinsam, dass die formal freie Veräußerung der Arbeitskraft eine erzwungene Verfügung über unbezahlte Lebenszeit vermittelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A12","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Die gesetzliche Grenze trennt kapitalistisch angeeignete Verkaufszeit von Eigenzeit und erzeugt dadurch eine materielle Voraussetzung weiterer Emanzipation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-01","text":"Die Identität von Mehrwertrate und Zeitverhältnis bleibt stabil, während ihre Funktion von der rechnerischen Bestimmung des Exploitationsgrades zur Kartierung eines gesellschaftlichen Zeitkonflikts übergeht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A13","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-02","text":"Konstantes Kapital bleibt als Wertquelle ausgeschlossen, kehrt aber als operativer Druck zur Verlängerung und Verstetigung des Produktionsprozesses wieder.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A11","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-03","text":"Der Arbeitstag mutiert von einer rechnerischen Summe über eine quantitativ offene Variable zu einer gesetzlich umkämpften Grenze zwischen Verkaufszeit und Eigenzeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A15","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-04","text":"Variables Kapital wird zunächst durch sein prozessuales Resultat bestimmt; seine Warenform verschiebt sich anschließend zur endlichen und reproduktionsabhängigen Lebenskraft seines Trägers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-05","text":"Das Recht wechselt seine Funktion von der Besiegelung entgegengesetzter Austauschansprüche zur kollektiv erzwungenen Begrenzung der durch den Vertrag eröffneten Aneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-06","text":"Freiheit kehrt ihre Valenz um: Individuelle Vertragsfreiheit erscheint als Form fortgesetzter Abhängigkeit, während zwingende kollektive Begrenzung erst materielle Zeitfreiheit ermöglicht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-07","text":"Gesetzgebung wandert von der formalen Norm über Durchsetzungsversagen und Umgehung zu einer rekursiv präzisierten gesellschaftlichen Kontrolltechnik.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-08","text":"Die formationsübergreifende Mehrarbeitsstruktur wird in eine globale politische Architektur absorbiert, in der Lohnarbeit, Sklaverei und nationale Rechtsformen verschiedene Bedingungen derselben Arbeitszeitfrage bilden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A16","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-01","text":"Auf der unteren Ebene verbleiben die buchhalterische Behandlung nicht verzehrten Fixkapitals und die aliquote Produktzerlegung; auf Clusterebene tragen sie nur die allgemeinere Trennung von Wertübertragung und Wertneubildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX1","CH_V4GB_3DRD:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-02","text":"Die Widerlegung der letzten Arbeitsstunde und die bedingte Gleichsetzung von Preisen und Werten bleiben lokale Sicherungen der Rechnung, ohne die politische Architektur des Normalarbeitstags zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX9","CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-03","text":"Nationale Gesetzesformen skalieren nicht als einheitliches Modell nach oben; nur ihre Funktion als kontingente Realisierungen einer allgemeinen gesellschaftlichen Schranke bleibt erhalten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-04","text":"Die lokale Bestimmung der Mehrwertquelle skaliert nach oben, weil sie die quantitative Offenheit jenes Arbeitstags erzeugt, der zum Gegenstand von Rechtsantinomie und Klassenkampf wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-05","text":"Der individuelle Verkäuferanspruch wird auf Clusterebene durch die Bildung eines kollektiven Handlungssubjekts abgelöst, da Vereinzelung keine wirksame Grenzsetzung erlaubt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-06","text":"Die monetäre Mehrwertrate wird nach oben nicht verworfen, sondern als codierte gesellschaftliche Zeitrelation in eine politische Theorie der Verfügung über Leben integriert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-01","text":"Die homogene Wertproduktivität des Gesamtkapitals wird ausgeschlossen; technische Produktionsbedingungen und wertbildende Kausalität dürfen nicht gleichgesetzt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:DNX1","CH_V4GB_3DRD:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-02","text":"Die Mehrwertrate darf weder am Gesamtkapital gemessen noch als Bestimmung der absoluten Länge des Arbeitstags gelesen werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-03","text":"Weder Warentausch noch physische oder soziale Naturgrenzen liefern aus sich heraus einen bestimmten Normalarbeitstag.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-04","text":"Moralische Eigenschaften, langfristiges Eigeninteresse und freiwillige Selbstbegrenzung einzelner Kapitalisten gelten nicht als verlässliche Quellen einer menschlichen Zeitgrenze.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-05","text":"Rechtliche Gleichheit und freier Vertrag werden als hinreichende Garantien realer Verfügung über die Verkaufsdauer der Arbeitskraft zurückgewiesen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-06","text":"Gesetzliche Form ohne Vollstreckung, Kontrolle und Schutz gegen Umgehung zählt nicht als wirksame Begrenzung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-07","text":"Eine Arbeiteremanzipation, die Arbeitszeitbegrenzung oder die Überwindung rassifizierter Unfreiheit ausspart, wird ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-01","text":"Das System kann kein Produktionsmodell zulassen, in dem alle Kapitalbestandteile unterschiedslos Wert erzeugen, weil dann Quelle, Maß und Zeitgestalt des Mehrwerts unbestimmbar würden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-02","text":"Ein harmonisches Marktmodell muss falsch sein, weil Äquivalenz des Tauschs weder eine nichtdestruktive Konsumtion der Arbeitskraft noch eine Grenze ihrer Gebrauchsdauer garantiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-03","text":"Eine natürliche oder moralische Selbstregulation der Arbeitszeit ist unzulässig, weil gerade das Fehlen eines immanenten Maßes die Klassenentscheidung notwendig macht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04","text":"Die Trennung von ökonomischer und politischer Sphäre kann nicht bestehen, da die ökonomische Zeitaneignung erst durch organisierte Gegenmacht und staatliche Vollstreckung begrenzt wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:SNX4","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-05","text":"Eine national isolierte Freiheit der Lohnarbeit wird disqualifiziert, solange versklavte oder rassifizierte Arbeit die allgemeine Klassenbildung und Arbeitszeitforderung strukturell spaltet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A9","CH_V4GB_4D_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-01","text":"Im System fehlt ein vorpolitisch verfügbares Normalmaß der Arbeitszeit; gerade diese Abwesenheit organisiert den Übergang von Wertanalyse zu Klassenkampf.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-02","text":"Eine dem Arbeiter unverfügbar eigene Zeit existiert unter unbeschränkter Verwertung nicht als positive Größe, sondern muss durch Begrenzung der Verkaufszeit erst erzeugt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-03","text":"Der vereinzelte Warenbesitzer kann innerhalb des freien Vertrags seine eigene Nichtverwertung nicht sichern; ein autonomes vorpolitisches Arbeitersubjekt bleibt daher strukturell abwesend.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-04","text":"Eine endgültige Versöhnung von maximaler Verwertung, normaler Reproduktion und dauerhafter Freiheit ist nicht verfügbar; die Grenze bleibt eine institutionalisierte, erneuerbare Konfliktform.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-01","text":"Die kausale Isolierung lebendiger Arbeit erzeugt zugleich ein neues Problem: Sobald Mehrwert als Mehrarbeitszeit bestimmt ist, wird die offene Dauer dieser Zeit zum zentralen Konfliktfeld.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-01","CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","CL_V4GB_03:GA-03","CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-02","text":"Konstantes Kapital erzeugt keinen Neuwert, kann aber über den Druck zu kontinuierlicher Nutzung die Dauer und Intensität der mehrwertbildenden Arbeit steigern.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-01","CL_V4GB_03:GA-06","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A11","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-03","text":"Ein exakter Exploitationsgrad bestimmt weder die absolute Belastungsdauer noch die biologische Schädigung, weil dieselbe proportionale Rate mit verschieden langen Arbeitstagen vereinbar ist.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-03","CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CH_V4GB_3DRD:D6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-04","text":"Der äquivalente Tageskauf der Arbeitskraft kann mit einer Unterreproduktion ihres Gesamtwerts koexistieren, sobald ihre tägliche Nutzung Lebensdauer und künftige Verkäuflichkeit beschleunigt vermindert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-07","CL_V4GB_03:GA-10","CH_V4GB_3DRD:DNX3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-05","text":"Die Lohnform verbirgt die Trennung notwendiger und unbezahlter Arbeit, während die Vertragsform die erzwungene Wiederholung dieses Verhältnisses als freiwilligen Austausch erscheinen lässt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","CL_V4GB_03:GA-11","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A12","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-06","text":"Konkurrenz vermittelt den allgemeinen Verwertungszweck als Zwang für Einzelkapitale, während Vereinzelung die Gegenwehr der Arbeiter neutralisiert; erst kollektive Gesetzgebung kann beide dezentralen Zwänge begrenzen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-06","CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-07","text":"Der Normalarbeitstag übersetzt die offene algebraische Mehrarbeitsvariable in eine gesellschaftlich vollstreckbare Höchstgrenze und erzeugt dadurch einen positiven Bereich nicht verkaufter Zeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_03:GA-12","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-08","text":"Die Universalisierung der Arbeitszeitforderung setzt die Aufhebung von Arbeitsordnungen voraus, die die Arbeiterschaft durch rechtlich verschiedene Grade von Unfreiheit spalten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_03:GA-12","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS4","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-09","text":"Weil Natur, Austausch und Privatmoral keine bestimmte Grenze liefern, kann Normalität nur als politisch erzwungene und gegen Umgehung fortlaufend revidierte Institution existieren.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-07","CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-01","text":"Kapital erweist sich nicht als autonom wertschöpfendes Ding, sondern als gesellschaftliche Relation, die endliche lebendige Arbeitsfähigkeit in die Erscheinungsform einer Selbstbewegung des Werts zwingt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-02","text":"Kapitalistische Zeit ist zugleich messbar, elastisch und antagonistisch: Sie wird rechnerisch geteilt, durch Verwertung expandiert und durch politische Grenzsetzung neu segmentiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-03","text":"Erkenntnis der Ausbeutung verlangt die Trennung von Quelle, proportionaler Rate, absoluter Dauer und institutioneller Durchsetzung; keine dieser Größen kann die anderen ersetzen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:D6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-04","text":"Formale Austauschgleichheit erzeugt keine soziale Harmonie, sondern eine Antinomie, deren materielle Entscheidung die Rechtsform selbst in ein Feld des Klassenkampfs verwandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-05","text":"Das Arbeitersubjekt entsteht politisch nicht vor dem Konflikt, sondern durch den Übergang von vereinzeltem Warenbesitz zu kollektiver Organisation und international verallgemeinerbarer Forderung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-06","text":"Geschichte erscheint als sedimentierter Grenzkampf: Gesetze fixieren vorläufige Kräfteverhältnisse, werden umgangen, präzisiert und über nationale sowie sektorale Grenzen hinaus erweitert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-01","text":"Wertzerlegung führt zur Zeitzerlegung; die Zeitzerlegung legt die Unbestimmtheit der Gesamtdauer frei; diese Unbestimmtheit erzeugt Konflikt, dessen gesetzliche Lösung zur quantitativen Begrenzung der Mehrarbeit zurückkehrt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-02","text":"Mehrwertzweck führt zu Zeitexpansion, Zeitexpansion zu Verschleiß, Verschleiß bei verfügbarem Ersatz zu weiterer Externalisierung der Reproduktionskosten und damit zu erneuter Expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A14","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-03","text":"Vertragsfreiheit schlägt im Produktionsprozess in Zeitunterwerfung um; kollektiver Zwang gegen den Vertrag schlägt wiederum in eine höhere materielle Freiheit der Eigenzeit um.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-04","text":"Überarbeit erzeugt Schädigung und Widerstand, Widerstand erzeugt Gesetz, Gesetz erzeugt Umgehung, und Umgehung erzeugt präzisere Kontrolle sowie sektorale Verallgemeinerung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:FGS5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-05","text":"Das analytisch ausgeschlossene konstante Kapital kehrt auf höherer Ebene als Intensivierungsmechanismus zurück: Es bildet keinen Mehrwert, treibt aber die möglichst lückenlose Nutzung lebendiger Arbeit an.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-06","text":"Der dominante Attraktor ist die bewegliche Grenze zwischen notwendiger und überschüssiger, verkaufter und eigener, kapitalistisch angeeigneter und politisch zurückgewonnener Zeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A15","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B01","text":"Kapitalvorschuss C=c+v → Übertragung von c und Aktivierung lebendiger Arbeit durch v → Wertprodukt v+m.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A1","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B02","text":"Wertprodukt v+m → notwendige Arbeit reproduziert v → Mehrarbeit erzeugt m → m/v entspricht Mehrarbeit/notwendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A7","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A8","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B03","text":"m/v bestimmt die relative Teilung → T=N+S bleibt absolut offen → die Exploitationsrate erzeugt keine Normaldauer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:D6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B04","text":"Fehlendes Austauschmaß → Käuferrecht auf maximale Nutzung versus Verkäuferrecht auf Reproduktion → Rechtsantinomie → Entscheidung durch Kräfteverhältnis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B05","text":"Mehrwertzweck + Konkurrenz + Nutzungsdruck vorgeschossener Produktionsmittel → Verlängerung, Intensivierung und Verstetigung der Arbeitszeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B06","text":"Zeitexpansion → beschleunigte Abnutzung → Widerstand und Klassenorganisation → gesetzliche Grenzsetzung → Umgehung → präzisierte Vollstreckung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B07","text":"Vollstreckbare Schranke → Trennung von Verkaufszeit und Eigenzeit → materielle Voraussetzung sozialer und politischer Handlungsfähigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AFM-B01","text":"Sichtbarer Wertüberschuss → funktionelle Kapitalzerlegung → Isolierung lebendiger Arbeit → Mehrwertrate → zeitliche Teilung des Arbeitstags → quantitative Offenheit seiner Gesamtdauer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AFM-B02","text":"Quantitative Offenheit → unvereinbare Austauschansprüche → Rechtsantinomie → Verwertungseskalation → Verschleiß der Arbeitskraft → kollektiver Widerstand.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AFM-B03","text":"Niederlage des vereinzelten Arbeiters → Klassenbildung → erzwungene Gesetzgebung → rekursive Nachregulierung → Normalarbeitstag → Eigenzeit → offene Emanzipationsperspektive.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AF1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AF5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AF6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-01","text":"Kapital wird zugleich als funktionell gespaltene Wertstruktur und als gesellschaftlicher Zwangsmechanismus neu kartiert; Wertquelle und Durchsetzungsmechanismus fallen nicht zusammen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:ME1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-02","text":"Ausbeutung wird in drei nicht austauschbare Dimensionen gegliedert: Quelle des Mehrwerts, proportionale Rate und absolute Dauer der Zeitaneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS3","CH_V4GB_3DRD:D5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-03","text":"Der Arbeitstag wird von einer natürlichen Betriebseinheit zu einem Grenzobjekt zwischen Reproduktion, Mehrwertproduktion und politisch gesicherter Eigenzeit umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-04","text":"Der Warentausch verliert den Status eines harmonischen Koordinationsmodells und wird zur formalen Matrix unvereinbarer Zeitansprüche.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-05","text":"Überarbeit wird von persönlicher Grausamkeit zu einem verteilten Effekt aus Mehrwertzweck, Konkurrenz, Fixkapitalnutzung und ersetzbarem Arbeitskräfteangebot umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-06","text":"Gesetzgebung erscheint weder als systemfremder Eingriff noch als neutrale Ableitung, sondern als endogen erzeugtes und umkämpftes Organisationsmedium gesellschaftlicher Reproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-07","text":"Lohnarbeit und Sklaverei werden nicht als getrennte Ordnungen gelesen, sondern als unterschiedlich vermittelte Formen, deren Koexistenz die Universalisierung der Arbeiterfreiheit blockiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene werden Mehrwertrate, Länge des Arbeitstags und gesetzlicher Normalarbeitstag als drei aufeinander bezogene, aber nicht identische Bestimmungsgegenstände behandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A12","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene organisieren Wertübertragung, lebendige Arbeit, Konkurrenz, Arbeitskräfteersatz und staatliche Vollstreckung gemeinsam die Aneignung von Mehrarbeitszeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene wird individuelle Vertragsbehauptung durch kollektive Klassenorganisation und die Forderung nach kontrollierbaren, verallgemeinerbaren Zeitnormen ersetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-temporalen Ebene steht endliche, reproduktionsbedürftige Lebenskraft einer abstrakten Verwertungszeit gegenüber, die Regeneration und Lebensdauer als Kosten behandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollzieht die Argumentation selbst den Übergang von analytischer Zerlegung über Antinomie und historische Eskalation zu einer nur rekursiv stabilisierbaren institutionellen Grenze.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-01","text":"Die analytische Ausschaltung des konstanten Kapitals aus der Wertquelle steht in produktiver Spannung zu seiner späteren Wirksamkeit als Druckmittel für verlängerte und kontinuierliche Arbeitszeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-02","text":"Die Voraussetzung, Arbeitskraft werde zu ihrem Wert gekauft, destabilisiert sich, sobald ihre Konsumtionsdauer den Umfang ihrer reproduzierbaren Lebensleistung verändert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-03","text":"Die formale Symmetrie gleicher Rechte verdeckt eine materielle Asymmetrie von Eigentum, Existenzmitteln und Fähigkeit zur Vertragsverweigerung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-04","text":"Der Staat erscheint zugleich als von herrschenden Eigentumsinteressen geprägt und als notwendiges Vollstreckungsmedium ihrer Begrenzung; die institutionelle Vermittlung dieses Umschlags bleibt unterbestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-05","text":"Die universelle Norm des Normalarbeitstags bleibt von national unterschiedlichen Rechtsformen, Kräfteverhältnissen und Umgehungsweisen abhängig.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-06","text":"Die Erzeugung von Eigenzeit begründet die Möglichkeit weiterer Emanzipation, garantiert aber nicht deren Übergang in dauerhafte politische Macht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-01","text":"Der Begriff des variablen Kapitals mutiert von einem scheinbar festen Geldvorschuss zur prozessualen Fähigkeit, durch lebendige Arbeit einen Überschuss zu erzeugen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:D4","CH_V4GB_3DRD:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-02","text":"Die Mehrwertrate mutiert vom rechnerischen Verhältnis zum Konfliktkoeffizienten, dessen Nenner und Zähler gesellschaftlich getrennte Teile der Lebenszeit darstellen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-03","text":"Arbeitskraft mutiert von einer formal gewöhnlichen Ware zu einer Ware, deren Gebrauch den Träger und die künftige Verfügbarkeit der Ware selbst verändert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-04","text":"Recht mutiert von der Bestätigung des freien Austauschs zur materiellen Gegengewalt gegen die Resultate dieses Austauschs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-05","text":"Freiheit mutiert von individueller Verfügung im Zirkulationsakt zur kollektiv erzwungenen Begrenzung der im Produktionsprozess verfügbaren Zeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als Akkumulationsmaschine, die über funktionelle Wertspaltung, Konkurrenz und Recht endliche lebendige Zeit in Mehrwert überführt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt erscheint zunächst als reproduktionsabhängiger Träger verkäuflicher Arbeitskraft und wird erst durch kollektiven Grenzkampf zu einem handlungsfähigen Klassensubjekt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-03","text":"Zeit erscheint als teilbares, expandierbares und politisch segmentierbares Medium, in dem notwendige Arbeit, Mehrarbeit, Verkaufszeit und Eigenzeit um dieselbe Lebensdauer konkurrieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-04","text":"Mögliche Gegenmacht besteht nicht in Flucht aus der Zeitrechnung, sondern in ihrer kollektiven Umkehrung: Messung wird Grenzforderung, Grenzforderung wird Gesetz und Gesetz erzeugt einen Bereich eigener Zeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:D2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B01","text":"Die Architektur ist rekonstruierbar, wenn Wertquellentrennung, Mehrwertrate, offene Gesamtdauer, Rechtsantinomie, Konkurrenzzwang und gesetzlicher Normalarbeitstag gemeinsam erhalten bleiben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B02","text":"Ihre stärkste Kohärenz liegt im Übergang von der analytischen Isolierung lebendiger Arbeit zur politischen Begrenzung der Zeit, während der Mehrwert produziert wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B03","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die vorgängige Arbeitswerttheorie, die Preis-Wert-Vermittlung, die konkrete Zahl des Normalarbeitstags und die institutionelle Transformation von Klassenmacht in dauerhaftes Staatsrecht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B04","text":"Das System ist auf Clusterebene kohärent, sofern Wertanalyse, Konkurrenz, Klassenkampf und Gesetz als verschiedene Vermittlungen derselben gesellschaftlichen Zeitrelation behandelt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B05","text":"Die Rekonstruktion hängt wesentlich an der Sequenz vom Maß zur Unbestimmtheit und von dort zur Gewaltentscheidung; ohne diesen Übergang zerfiele sie in getrennte Wertrechnung und Sozialgeschichte.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT9","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B06","text":"Axiomatischer Reduktion widersteht die konkrete Grenzzahl: Sie kann weder aus Wertform noch aus Natur deduziert werden und bleibt ein historisch kontingentes Resultat institutionalisierter Kräfteverhältnisse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A17","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211742288213Z_54202f3f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 07–09","source_sha256":"71e352ed8dd2481d0c7ad23ce85f79e3ea196b088bb1998df37e1273c62ffabb","sha256":"60b758060a0f007635eacdb100231ef0ba17c78e1a0e4e43161f0b0bcc036015","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:17:42.290106+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-01","text":"The visible surplus of value must first be traced back to its source and its proportional measure before its temporal and social mode of production can be determined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-02","text":"The functional separation of constant and variable capital isolates living labour as the source of surplus value and translates valorization into the ratio of surplus labour to necessary labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-03","text":"The exact ratio of the two parts of the working day determines their proportion, but leaves the total duration open and transforms quantitative measurability into an undecided question of limits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-04","text":"The purpose of surplus-value production, the use of advanced means of production, and the coercion of competition drive open-ended surplus labour time beyond individual interests in preservation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-05","text":"Because the isolated seller of labour-power cannot limit this expansion, the formal time relation mutates into class struggle over an enforceable social limit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AS-06","text":"The movement proceeds analytically, antinomically, and recursively from the rate of surplus value through destructive appropriation of time to the legal separation of selling time and own time; its closure remains provisional owing to continuing evasion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Constant capital transfers existing value, whereas only the process mediated by labour-power produces new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A3","CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Necessary labour reproduces the value of labour-power; labour beyond this reproduction time produces surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A7","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The ratio of surplus value to variable capital is at once a monetary measure of valorization, a temporal ratio, and a determination of the degree of exploitation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The working day consists of necessary labour and surplus labour, without this division determining its absolute duration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A15","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The determinacy of necessary labour time produces no determinate total length, because surplus labour time remains variable within elastic physical and social limits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Surplus-value production is the systemic purpose that impels capital toward the greatest possible appropriation of living labour time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A17","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Commodity exchange legitimates opposing claims to the duration of use of labour-power, but contains no measure that decides between them.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Competition transforms the purpose of valorization into external coercion and renders both the isolated worker and the individual capitalist incapable of voluntarily establishing a stable limit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] The normal working day arises only as a collectively enforced, enforceable, and institutionally controlled limit on capitalist appropriation of time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A17","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Labour-power is not an ordinarily consumable commodity, because its present use alters its future reproduction, lifespan, and renewed saleability.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Wage form and contractual equality jointly conceal that the formally free alienation of labour-power mediates a coerced disposal over unpaid lifetime.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A12","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] The legal limit separates capitalistically appropriated selling time from own time and thereby produces a material precondition for further emancipation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-01","text":"The identity of the rate of surplus value and the time ratio remains stable, while its function shifts from the computational determination of the degree of exploitation to the mapping of a social conflict over time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A13","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-02","text":"Constant capital remains excluded as a source of value, but returns as operational pressure for the prolongation and continuous maintenance of the production process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A11","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-03","text":"The working day mutates from a computational sum through a quantitatively open variable into a legally contested boundary between selling time and own time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A15","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-04","text":"Variable capital is initially determined through its processual result; its commodity form subsequently shifts toward the finite and reproduction-dependent life-force of its bearer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-05","text":"Law changes its function from sealing opposing claims of exchange to the collectively enforced limitation of the appropriation opened by the contract.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-06","text":"Freedom reverses its valence: individual contractual freedom appears as a form of continuing dependency, while compulsory collective limitation first makes material freedom of time possible.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-07","text":"Legislation moves from the formal norm through enforcement failure and evasion to a recursively refined social technique of control.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RMD-08","text":"The trans-formation surplus-labour structure is absorbed into a global political architecture in which wage labour, slavery, and national legal forms constitute different conditions of the same question of working time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A16","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-01","text":"At the lower level remain the accounting treatment of unconsumed fixed capital and the aliquot division of the product; at the cluster level, they support only the more general separation of value transfer and new-value formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX1","CH_V4GB_3DRD:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-02","text":"The refutation of the last hour and the conditional equation of prices and values remain local safeguards of the calculation, without generating the political architecture of the normal working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX9","CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-03","text":"National legal forms do not scale upward as a uniform model; only their function as contingent realizations of a general social limit is retained.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-04","text":"The local determination of the source of surplus value scales upward because it generates the quantitative openness of that working day which becomes the object of legal antinomy and class struggle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-05","text":"At the cluster level, the individual seller's claim is superseded by the formation of a collective subject of action, since isolation permits no effective setting of limits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:CGD-06","text":"The monetary rate of surplus value is not discarded upward, but integrated as a coded social time relation into a political theory of disposal over life.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-01","text":"The homogeneous value-productivity of total capital is excluded; technical conditions of production and value-forming causality must not be equated.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:DNX1","CH_V4GB_3DRD:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-02","text":"The rate of surplus value must be measured neither against total capital nor read as a determination of the absolute length of the working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-03","text":"Neither commodity exchange nor physical or social natural limits provide, of themselves, a determinate normal working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-04","text":"Moral qualities, long-term self-interest, and voluntary self-limitation of individual capitalists do not count as reliable sources of a human limit to time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-05","text":"Legal equality and free contract are rejected as sufficient guarantees of real disposal over the duration for which labour-power is sold.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-06","text":"Legal form without enforcement, control, and protection against evasion does not count as an effective limitation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:GNX-07","text":"A workers' emancipation that omits the limitation of working time or the overcoming of racialized unfreedom is excluded.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-01","text":"The system cannot admit a model of production in which all components of capital produce value indiscriminately, because the source, measure, and temporal form of surplus value would then become indeterminate.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-02","text":"A harmonious market model must be false, because equivalence of exchange guarantees neither a non-destructive consumption of labour-power nor a limit to its duration of use.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-03","text":"A natural or moral self-regulation of working time is inadmissible, because precisely the absence of an immanent measure makes class decision necessary.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04","text":"The separation of the economic and political spheres cannot stand, since economic appropriation of time is limited only through organized counter-power and state enforcement.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:SNX4","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:DBN-05","text":"A nationally isolated freedom of wage labour is disqualified so long as enslaved or racialized labour structurally divides general class formation and the demand for working time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A9","CH_V4GB_4D_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-01","text":"The system lacks a pre-politically available normal measure of working time; this very absence organizes the transition from value analysis to class struggle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-02","text":"A time inherently unavailable to the worker does not exist under unrestricted valorization as a positive magnitude, but must first be produced through limitation of selling time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-03","text":"Within the free contract, the isolated commodity owner cannot secure his own non-valorization; an autonomous pre-political worker-subject therefore remains structurally absent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSA-04","text":"A final reconciliation of maximum valorization, normal reproduction, and enduring freedom is unavailable; the limit remains an institutionalized, renewable form of conflict.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-01","text":"The causal isolation of living labour simultaneously produces a new problem: once surplus value is determined as surplus labour time, the open duration of this time becomes the central field of conflict.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-01","CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","CL_V4GB_03:GA-03","CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-02","text":"Constant capital produces no new value, but can increase the duration and intensity of surplus-value-forming labour through the pressure toward continuous utilization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-01","CL_V4GB_03:GA-06","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A11","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-03","text":"An exact degree of exploitation determines neither the absolute duration of strain nor biological injury, because the same proportional rate is compatible with working days of different lengths.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-03","CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CH_V4GB_3DRD:D6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-04","text":"The equivalent daily purchase of labour-power can coexist with an under-reproduction of its total value as soon as its daily use accelerates the diminution of lifespan and future saleability.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-07","CL_V4GB_03:GA-10","CH_V4GB_3DRD:DNX3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-05","text":"The wage form conceals the separation of necessary and unpaid labour, while the contractual form makes the coerced repetition of this relation appear as voluntary exchange.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","CL_V4GB_03:GA-11","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A12","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-06","text":"Competition mediates the general purpose of valorization as coercion upon individual capitals, while isolation neutralizes workers' resistance; only collective legislation can limit both decentralized coercions.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-06","CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-07","text":"The normal working day translates the open algebraic surplus-labour variable into a socially enforceable maximum limit and thereby produces a positive sphere of unsold time.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_03:GA-12","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-08","text":"The universalization of the demand for working time presupposes the abolition of labour orders that divide the working class through legally different degrees of unfreedom.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_03:GA-12","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS4","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:XD-09","text":"Because nature, exchange, and private morality provide no determinate limit, normality can exist only as a politically enforced institution continually revised against evasion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-07","CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-01","text":"Capital proves to be not an autonomously value-creating thing, but a social relation that compels finite living labour-capacity into the appearance-form of a self-motion of value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-02","text":"Capitalist time is simultaneously measurable, elastic, and antagonistic: it is computationally divided, expanded through valorization, and newly segmented through political setting of limits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-03","text":"Knowledge of exploitation requires the separation of source, proportional rate, absolute duration, and institutional enforcement; none of these magnitudes can replace the others.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:D6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-04","text":"Formal equality of exchange produces not social harmony but an antinomy whose material decision transforms legal form itself into a field of class struggle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-05","text":"The worker-subject arises politically not before conflict, but through the transition from isolated commodity ownership to collective organization and an internationally generalizable demand.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:BSD-06","text":"History appears as sedimented struggle over limits: laws fix provisional relations of force, are evaded, refined, and extended beyond national as well as sectoral boundaries.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-01","text":"Value division leads to time division; time division reveals the indeterminacy of total duration; this indeterminacy produces conflict, whose legal resolution returns to the quantitative limitation of surplus labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-02","text":"The purpose of surplus value leads to time expansion, time expansion to wear, wear in the presence of available replacement to further externalization of reproduction costs and thus to renewed expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A14","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-03","text":"Contractual freedom turns into subjection to time in the production process; collective coercion against the contract in turn becomes a higher material freedom of own time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-04","text":"Overwork produces injury and resistance, resistance produces law, law produces evasion, and evasion produces more precise control as well as sectoral generalization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:FGS5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-05","text":"Constant capital, analytically excluded, returns at a higher level as a mechanism of intensification: it forms no surplus value, but drives the most seamless possible utilization of living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:NX2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:RLE-06","text":"The dominant attractor is the mobile boundary between necessary and surplus, sold and own, capitalistically appropriated and politically recovered time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A15","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B01","text":"Capital advance C=c+v → transfer of c and activation of living labour by v → value product v+m.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A1","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B02","text":"Value product v+m → necessary labour reproduces v → surplus labour produces m → m/v corresponds to surplus labour/necessary labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A7","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A8","CH_V4GB_3DRD:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B03","text":"m/v determines the relative division → T=N+S remains absolutely open → the rate of exploitation produces no normal duration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:D6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B04","text":"Absent measure of exchange → buyer's right to maximum use versus seller's right to reproduction → legal antinomy → decision through relation of forces.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B05","text":"Purpose of surplus value + competition + pressure to utilize advanced means of production → prolongation, intensification, and continuous maintenance of working time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B06","text":"Time expansion → accelerated wear → resistance and class organization → legal setting of limits → evasion → refined enforcement.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FGS-B07","text":"Enforceable limit → separation of selling time and own time → material precondition of social and political capacity for action.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AFM-B01","text":"Visible surplus of value → functional division of capital → isolation of living labour → rate of surplus value → temporal division of the working day → quantitative openness of its total duration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AFM-B02","text":"Quantitative openness → incompatible claims of exchange → legal antinomy → escalation of valorization → wear of labour-power → collective resistance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:AFM-B03","text":"Defeat of the isolated worker → class formation → enforced legislation → recursive re-regulation → normal working day → own time → open perspective of emancipation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:AF1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AF5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AF6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-01","text":"Capital is remapped simultaneously as a functionally divided value structure and as a social mechanism of coercion; source of value and mechanism of enforcement do not coincide.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:ME1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-02","text":"Exploitation is divided into three non-interchangeable dimensions: source of surplus value, proportional rate, and absolute duration of the appropriation of time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:AS3","CH_V4GB_3DRD:D5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-03","text":"The working day is reclassified from a natural unit of operation into a boundary object between reproduction, surplus-value production, and politically secured own time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-04","text":"Commodity exchange loses the status of a harmonious model of coordination and becomes the formal matrix of incompatible claims to time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-05","text":"Overwork is remapped from personal cruelty into a distributed effect of the purpose of surplus value, competition, fixed-capital utilization, and the available supply of replaceable labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-06","text":"Legislation appears neither as an intervention external to the system nor as a neutral derivation, but as an endogenously produced and contested organizational medium of social reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MME-07","text":"Wage labour and slavery are read not as separate orders but as differently mediated forms whose coexistence blocks the universalization of workers' freedom.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ME3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the rate of surplus value, the length of the working day, and the legal normal working day are treated as three interrelated but non-identical objects of determination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A12","CH_V4GB_4DAR:NX2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, value transfer, living labour, competition, replacement of labour-power, and state enforcement jointly organize the appropriation of surplus labour time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B03","text":"At the meta-strategic level, individual contractual assertion is replaced by collective class organization and the demand for controllable, generalizable norms of time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, finite life-force requiring reproduction confronts an abstract time of valorization that treats regeneration and lifespan as costs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the argument itself enacts the transition from analytical division through antinomy and historical escalation to an institutional limit stabilizable only recursively.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS3","CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-01","text":"The analytical exclusion of constant capital from the source of value stands in productive tension with its later efficacy as a means of pressure for prolonged and continuous working time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-02","text":"The premise that labour-power is purchased at its value destabilizes itself once the duration of its consumption alters the extent of its reproducible life performance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-03","text":"The formal symmetry of equal rights conceals a material asymmetry of property, means of subsistence, and capacity to refuse the contract.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-04","text":"The state appears both as shaped by ruling property interests and as the necessary medium of enforcement for their limitation; the institutional mediation of this reversal remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-05","text":"The universal norm of the normal working day remains dependent on nationally differing legal forms, relations of force, and modes of evasion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:FL-06","text":"The production of own time grounds the possibility of further emancipation, but does not guarantee its transition into enduring political power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-01","text":"The concept of variable capital mutates from an apparently fixed monetary advance into the processual capacity to produce a surplus through living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:D4","CH_V4GB_3DRD:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-02","text":"The rate of surplus value mutates from a computational ratio into a coefficient of conflict, whose denominator and numerator represent socially separated parts of lifetime.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:SD3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-03","text":"Labour-power mutates from a formally ordinary commodity into a commodity whose use alters the bearer and the future availability of the commodity itself.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A7","CH_V4GB_4DAR:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-04","text":"Law mutates from the confirmation of free exchange into material counter-force against the results of this exchange.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A8","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MP-05","text":"Freedom mutates from individual disposal in the act of circulation into the collectively enforced limitation of time available in the production process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a machine of accumulation that, through functional division of value, competition, and law, converts finite living time into surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:A1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A6","CH_V4GB_4D_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-02","text":"The subject initially appears as a reproduction-dependent bearer of saleable labour-power and becomes a capable class subject only through collective struggle over limits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:A3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-03","text":"Time appears as a divisible, expandable, and politically segmentable medium in which necessary labour, surplus labour, selling time, and own time compete over the same lifespan.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:A2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:HSI-04","text":"Possible counter-power consists not in flight from the calculation of time, but in its collective reversal: measurement becomes a demand for limits, the demand for limits becomes law, and law produces a sphere of one's own time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4D_2:D2","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS5","CH_V4GB_4D_2:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B01","text":"The architecture is reconstructible if separation of the value source, rate of surplus value, open total duration, legal antinomy, coercion of competition, and legal normal working day are jointly retained.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT1","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT1","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B02","text":"Its strongest coherence lies in the transition from the analytical isolation of living labour to the political limitation of time while surplus value is produced.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT4","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B03","text":"The prior labour theory of value, the mediation of price and value, the concrete number of the normal working day, and the institutional transformation of class power into enduring state law remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DRD:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B04","text":"The system is coherent at the cluster level insofar as value analysis, competition, class struggle, and law are treated as different mediations of the same social time relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT3","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction depends essentially on the sequence from measure to indeterminacy and thence to the decision by force; without this transition, it would disintegrate into separate value calculation and social history.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:AS6","CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT9","CH_V4GB_4D_2:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B06","text":"The concrete number of the limit resists axiomatic reduction: it can be deduced neither from value form nor from nature and remains a historically contingent result of institutionalized relations of force.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4DAR:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4DAR:A17","CH_V4GB_4D_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_03:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 07–09","context":"3) Die Rate des Mehrwerths. · 4) Der Arbeitstag. · reading part 1/2 · 4) Der Arbeitstag. · reading part 2/2"}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 10–12","order":4,"parents":["CH_V4GB_5RUM","CH_V4GB_1BDR","CH_V4GB_2COO"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_04@R001","sha256":"9e8c65bf5b788581d11f935746cd0f002495d425d4b6e0a75d829282e56bf158","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B01","text":"Das zentrale Problem besteht darin, wie Kapital trotz endlicher Arbeitszeit die Mehrwerthsproduktion durch Arbeiterzahl, innere Umverteilung des Arbeitstags und gesellschaftliche Kombination der Arbeitskräfte erweitert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B02","text":"Die globale These bestimmt lebendige Arbeit als einzige Quelle neuen Werths, während Produktivität und Kooperation die Formen verändern, in denen diese Quelle zeitlich geteilt, quantitativ skaliert und gesellschaftlich angeeignet wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A8","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B03","text":"Das Argument verbindet eine extensive Achse der Arbeiterzahl, eine intensive Achse der Mehrwerthsrate und eine organisatorische Achse der kombinierten Arbeitskraft zu einer einheitlichen Architektur der Mehrwerthssteigerung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B04","text":"Die Bewegung verläuft von linearer Werthaggregation zu qualitativer Produktivitätssteigerung, ohne die Differenz zwischen additiver Werthbildung und emergentem Gebrauchswerthnutzen aufzuheben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_2COO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B05","text":"Sobald die äußere Ausdehnung des Arbeitstags an Grenzen stößt, mutiert die Verwerthungsstrategie zur Veränderung der Produktionsweise, zur Verkürzung notwendiger Arbeit und zur organisatorischen Verdichtung des Gesamtarbeitstags.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B06","text":"Die technisch erforderliche Verbindung vieler Arbeiten wird kapitalistisch als äußere Leitung, Kontrolle und Kommando organisiert, wodurch gesellschaftliche Arbeitskraft als Produktivkraft des Kapitals erscheint.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS6","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B07","text":"Konkurrenz macht den individuellen Produktivitätsvorsprung zu einer selbstaufhebenden Übergangsform: Sie erzeugt Extra-Mehrwert, erzwingt Verallgemeinerung und setzt den Produktivitätszwang auf neuer gesellschaftlicher Grundlage fort.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B08","text":"Die Schließung ist rekursiv statt terminal: Reale Subsumtion erweitert das Kapitalkommando über gesellschaftliche Arbeit, hebt aber weder dessen Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit noch die daraus entstehende Spannung auf.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A18","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Lebendige Arbeit allein bildet neuen Werth und Mehrwerth; constantes Kapital überträgt vorhandenen Werth, ohne selbst Quelle der Werthneubildung zu sein.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A7","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Die Mehrwerthsmasse wird durch den Umfang des in Arbeitskraft umgesetzten variablen Kapitals und durch die Mehrwerthsrate bestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS2","CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Mehrwerth kann extensiv durch zusätzliche Arbeitskräfte oder intensiv durch einen größeren Mehrarbeitsanteil gesteigert werden; die Grenze extensiver und absoluter Ausdehnung erzwingt den Übergang zu innerer Zeitumverteilung und organisatorischer Produktivität.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Quantitative Arbeiterkonzentration vergrößert die Werthmasse linear, erzeugt auf der Gebrauchswerthseite jedoch eine kombinierte Produktivkraft, die nicht auf die Summe individueller Kräfte reduzierbar ist.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Produktivkraftsteigerung senkt Warenwerte über die Verringerung gesellschaftlich notwendiger Arbeitszeit, vermindert den Werth der Arbeitskraft aber nur, soweit sie notwendige Lebensmittel oder deren Produktionsmittel verbilligt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Der Arbeitstag ist nicht nur eine äußerlich verlängerbare Größe, sondern ein intern verteilbares Zeitfeld, in dem notwendige Arbeit und Mehrarbeit gegensinnig variieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Die größtmögliche Selbstverwerthung richtet technische Veränderung, Warenproduktion, Zeitökonomie und Arbeitsorganisation auf die Produktion realisierbaren Mehrwerths aus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A13","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Kapital kauft individuelle Arbeitskräfte, eignet sich aber zusätzlich die erst im Produktionsprozess entstehende kombinierte Arbeitskraft ohne besonderes Äquivalent an.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A15","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Der allgemeine Koordinationsbedarf gesellschaftlicher Arbeit wird unter kapitalistischen Eigentums- und Ausbeutungsverhältnissen in eine antagonistische Kommandofunktion umgeformt, ohne mit dieser historisch besonderen Form identisch zu sein.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Äquivalententausch beim Kauf der Arbeitskraft schließt die Aneignung unbezahlter Arbeit nicht aus, weil diese erst durch den Gebrauch der gekauften Arbeitskraft im Produktionsprozess entsteht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Der individuelle Extra-Mehrwert verschwindet mit der Konkurrenzverallgemeinerung seiner Produktionsmethode, während deren gesellschaftliche Produktivitätswirkung fortbestehen kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Kapital bleibt von lebendiger Arbeit abhängig und versucht zugleich, den zu ihrer Reproduktion notwendigen Zeitanteil, ihre Zahl je Produkt und ihre selbständige Verfügung über den Arbeitsprozess zu vermindern.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Ein hinreichendes Kapitalminimum bildet die Schwelle, an der dauernde Beschäftigung vieler Arbeitskräfte, gesellschaftliche Durchschnittsbildung und kapitalistische Leitungsfunktion stabil zusammenfallen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Kooperation eröffnet die reale Subsumtion als organisatorische Veränderung des Arbeitsprozesses und bleibt die Basisschicht späterer technischer und arbeitsteiliger Formen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_2COO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-01","text":"Arbeitszeit behält ihre Funktion als Werthmaß, erweitert ihren Geltungsbereich aber vom individuellen Arbeitstag über den gesellschaftlichen Gesammtarbeitstag bis zur synchronisierten Zeit des Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A9","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-02","text":"Die Arbeiterzahl mutiert von einem skalaren Faktor der Mehrwerthsmasse zur materiellen Grundlage eines funktional gegliederten kollektiven Arbeitskörpers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-03","text":"Produktivität verschiebt sich von technischer Warenverbilligung zur Macht über gesellschaftlich notwendige Zeit und schließlich zur kapitalistischen Umverteilung des Arbeitstags zugunsten der Mehrarbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-04","text":"Kooperation behält ihre allgemeine Funktion als Verbindung vieler Arbeiten, kehrt aber unter kapitalistischen Bedingungen als äußeres Kommando über die Kooperierenden wieder.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:NX9","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-05","text":"Kapital mutiert von einer vorgeschossenen Werthsumme zum Organisations- und Kommandozentrum, das gegenständliche Produktionsbedingungen als scheinbar selbständiges Subjekt der Arbeitsaneignung auftreten lässt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS8","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-06","text":"Der Extra-Mehrwert verschwindet als dauerhafte individuelle Differenz, nachdem er die Konkurrenzverallgemeinerung produktiverer Verfahren und damit eine gesellschaftliche Niveauverschiebung ausgelöst hat.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-07","text":"Constantes Kapital bleibt von der Werthneubildung ausgeschlossen, gewinnt aber als konzentrierte materielle Bedingung gemeinsamer Produktion, verbilligter Produkte und externalisierten Kommandos eine erweiterte operative Funktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-08","text":"Die Produktion absoluten Mehrwerths wird nicht widerlegt, sondern als begrenzte Basisschicht in eine Architektur absorbiert, die durch Kooperation und relative Mehrwerthsproduktion den Arbeitsprozess selbst transformiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A13","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-01","text":"Die Formel der Mehrwerthsmasse bleibt eine lokale quantitative Bestimmung; auf Clusterebene wird sie zum Ausgangspunkt einer dreifachen Skalierung durch Arbeiterzahl, Mehrarbeitsanteil und kombinierte Produktivkraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-02","text":"Die natürliche Grenze des einzelnen Arbeitstags bleibt lokal; global wirksam wird sie als Katalysator des Übergangs von äußerer Verlängerung zu innerer Zeitverschiebung und produktiver Reorganisation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-03","text":"Die sektorale Bedingung, dass nur die Verbilligung notwendiger Lebensmittel den Werth der Arbeitskraft senkt, bleibt spezifisch; sie skaliert zur Vermittlung zwischen gesellschaftlicher Produktivität und allgemeiner Mehrwerthsrate.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-04","text":"Einzelne Kooperationsformen wie Synchronisation, räumliche Konzentration und gemeinsamer Produktionsmittelkonsum bleiben lokale Mechanismen; auf Clusterebene tragen sie die Emergenz einer nichtadditiven gesellschaftlichen Produktivkraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D3","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-05","text":"Die genaue Größe des Kapitalminimums bleibt historisch unterbestimmt; nach oben skaliert allein seine Funktion als Schwelle zwischen Selbstarbeit, Beschäftigung vieler Arbeitskräfte und verselbständigtem Kapitalkommando.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:MRT6","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-06","text":"Die Unterscheidung zwischen Extra-Mehrwert und relativem Mehrwerth bleibt eine lokale Wirkungstrennung; auf Clusterebene erzeugt sie den rekursiven Übergang von individueller Abweichung zu gesellschaftlichem Produktivitätszwang.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:NX4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-07","text":"Erst auf Clusterebene werden extensive Mehrwerthsmasse, relative Zeitumverteilung und kooperative Emergenz als komplementäre Momente einer fortschreitenden realen Subsumtion sichtbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-01","text":"Die Größe oder technische Ausstattung des Gesammtkapitals kann nicht als unmittelbare Quelle neuen Werths gelten; entscheidend bleibt seine Verfügung über lebendige Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX2","CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-02","text":"Weder Arbeiterzahl noch Exploitationsgrad können die Mehrwerthsmasse unbegrenzt ersetzen, weil Arbeitszeit, Bevölkerung und Reproduktionsbedingungen absolute oder gesellschaftliche Grenzen setzen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX3","CH_V4GB_5RUM:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-03","text":"Produktivitätssteigerung ist nicht mit freier Zeit für die Arbeiter identisch; unter Mehrwerthsorientierung kann sie den Mehrarbeitsanteil bei unverändertem oder verlängertem Arbeitstag erhöhen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:NX7","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-04","text":"Gesellschaftliche Produktivität lässt sich nicht atomistisch aus isolierten persönlichen Fähigkeiten erklären, da die Kombination selbst eine zusätzliche Produktivkraft erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:DNX1","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-05","text":"Die Notwendigkeit von Koordination begründet weder kapitalistisches Eigentum noch die despotische Form der Leitung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD3","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-06","text":"Marktgleichheit und voller Werthkauf der Arbeitskraft widerlegen die Ausbeutung nicht, weil sie die produktive Verwendung und kollektive Kombination der Arbeitskräfte nicht erfassen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:DNX3","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-01","text":"Falsch sein muss ein Modell sich selbst verwerthender todter Arbeit, das Mehrwerth unabhängig von endlicher lebendiger Arbeit und ihrer gesellschaftlichen Organisation erzeugen könnte.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-02","text":"Falsch sein muss eine wert- und herrschaftsneutrale Technik, deren Eingriff in Produktivität von Reproduktionskosten, Zeitteilung und kapitalistischer Aneignung getrennt bliebe.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:DNX1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-03","text":"Falsch sein muss ein ausschließlich marktliches Modell selbständiger Arbeitskraftverkäufer, weil der Produktionsprozess sie in einen fremd geleiteten Gesamtarbeiter und ein kollektives Abhängigkeitsverhältnis verwandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2COO:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-04","text":"Falsch sein muss die transhistorische Einheit von Eigentum, industrieller Leitung und gesellschaftlicher Koordination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:DNX4","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-05","text":"Falsch sein muss die Gleichsetzung von Gebrauchswerthproduktivität und Werthschöpfung, da kooperative Arbeit mehr Nutzeffekt hervorbringen kann, ohne den pro Arbeitsstunde gebildeten Werth zu steigern.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:NX4","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste strukturelle Abwesenheit ist der Gesamtarbeiter als Eigentümer, Leiter und Nutznießer seiner eigenen gesellschaftlichen Produktivkraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar bleibt die Rückgabe eingesparter notwendiger Arbeitszeit an die Arbeiter als selbstbestimmte freie Zeit; die Zeitersparnis wird systematisch als Mehrarbeit rekonfiguriert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-03","text":"Umkreist, aber nicht positiv integriert wird eine unmittelbare Arbeiterassoziation, deren gesellschaftliche Einheit aus den Beziehungen der Arbeiter selbst statt aus der Einheit des Kapitals hervorgeht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX3","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-04","text":"Ontologisch unstatthaft ist ein Kapital, das seine Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit vollständig beseitigt und dennoch als sich verwertender Werth fortbesteht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-01","text":"Die absolute Grenze des Arbeitstags verwandelt Produktivitätssteigerung und kooperative Reorganisation aus bloßen Optionen in systematische Wege zur weiteren Mehrwerthssteigerung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","CL_V4GB_04:GA-06","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A6","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-02","text":"Arbeiterkonzentration besitzt einen doppelten Ertrag: Sie vergrößert die Mehrwerthsmasse proportional und erzeugt zugleich eine nichtproportionale Produktivkraft des Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-02","CL_V4GB_04:GA-04","CL_V4GB_04:GA-13","CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-03","text":"Soweit kooperative Produktionsmittelökonomie notwendige Lebensmittel verbilligt, kann eine organisatorische Produktivkraft über den sinkenden Werth der Arbeitskraft in relativen Mehrwerth übersetzt werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-05","CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_2COO:D2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-04","text":"Die Konkurrenz verwandelt den temporären Vorteil einzelner Kapitale in einen allgemeinen Zwang zur fortgesetzten Veränderung von Technik und Arbeitsorganisation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-07","CL_V4GB_04:GA-11","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-05","text":"Weil nur individuelle Arbeitskräfte gekauft werden, liegt die gesellschaftliche Kombinationskraft außerhalb der expliziten Äquivalentform und kann als kostenlose Eigenkraft des Kapitals erscheinen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2COO:A15","CH_V4GB_2COO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-06","text":"Das Kapitalminimum ist nicht nur eine quantitative Vorschussschwelle, sondern der Umschlagspunkt, an dem Mehrwerthsmasse, Gesamtarbeiter und verselbständigtes Kommando einander reproduzieren.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-02","CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:GA-13","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-07","text":"Der Versuch, notwendige Arbeit und Arbeiterzahl je Produkt zu vermindern, steigert die Verwerthungsmacht des Kapitals und verschärft zugleich dessen unaufhebbare Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-01","CL_V4GB_04:GA-05","CL_V4GB_04:GA-12","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-08","text":"Die Trennbarkeit technischer Koordination von kapitalistischem Kommando macht eine selbstbestimmte gesellschaftliche Arbeitsorganisation begrifflich möglich, obwohl sie in der positiven Architektur ausgeschlossen bleibt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-01","text":"Kapital erscheint auf Clusterebene nicht primär als Ding oder Geldsumme, sondern als Einrichtung zur Erfassung, Kombination und Umverteilung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:ME1","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-02","text":"Kapitalistische Kausalität ist mehrskalig: Demographie begrenzt die Arbeitsmasse, Technik verändert gesellschaftlich notwendige Zeit, Kooperation erzeugt Produktivkraft und Konkurrenz verallgemeinert lokale Veränderungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:D5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-03","text":"Das Subjekt der Produktion spaltet sich: Der einzelne Arbeiter bleibt Verkäufer seiner Arbeitskraft, wird im Produktionsprozess Organ des Gesamtarbeiters, während Kapital als scheinbares Subjekt der gemeinsamen Produktivkraft auftritt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-04","text":"Kapitalistische Zeit ist zugleich extensiv, distributiv und synchron: Sie verlängert Arbeit, verschiebt die Grenze innerhalb des Arbeitstags und verdichtet viele individuelle Zeiten zu einem kombinierten gesellschaftlichen Arbeitstag.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-05","text":"Die politische Herrschaft des Kapitals entsteht nicht außerhalb der Produktion, sondern aus der Einheit von Eigentum an Produktionsbedingungen, Mehrwerthszweck, Koordination und Kontrolle des Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A14","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnistheoretisch verlangt die Architektur eine strikte Trennung von Werthbildung und Gebrauchswerthproduktivität, individuellem und gesellschaftlichem Werth sowie technischer Leitung und kapitalistischer Herrschaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:ME4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A9","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-07","text":"Historisch erscheint reale Subsumtion als Spirale: Organisatorische Kooperation schafft die Basisschicht, technische Innovation verändert die Produktionsweise und Konkurrenz erzwingt deren erneute gesellschaftliche Verallgemeinerung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-01","text":"Die Mehrwerthsschleife verläuft von gesteigerter Mehrwerthsmasse über mehr variables Kapital oder höhere Mehrwerthsrate zu erneuter Verfügung über größere Arbeitsmassen und intensiverer Zeitaneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A5","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-02","text":"Die Grenzschleife führt von endlicher Arbeitstagsverlängerung zur Senkung notwendiger Arbeitszeit, von dort zur Umwälzung der Produktionsweise und schließlich zur erneuten Steigerung des Mehrarbeitsanteils.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-03","text":"Die Innovationsschleife lautet: individueller Produktivitätsvorsprung, Extra-Mehrwert, Konkurrenzdruck, Verallgemeinerung, Aufhebung des Sondervorteils und erneuter Innovationszwang.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-04","text":"Die Konzentrationsschleife verbindet größeres Kapital, mehr gleichzeitig beschäftigte Arbeiter, stärkere Kooperation, höhere Produktivkraft und eine erneuerte materielle Überlegenheit konzentrierten Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS5","CH_V4GB_2COO:A9","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-05","text":"Die Kommandoschleife verbindet wachsende Kooperation mit Koordinationsbedarf, antagonistischem Widerstand, verstärkter Aufsicht und weiterer Verselbständigung der Leitungsfunktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:D7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-06","text":"Die Verdinglichungsschleife führt von einer durch Arbeiter erzeugten Kombinationskraft über ihre Aneignung durch das Kapital zu ihrer Erscheinung als Kapitalproduktivität, welche die Notwendigkeit des Kapitalkommandos scheinbar bestätigt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-07","text":"Der zentrale Attraktor ist die maximale Aneignung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit: Arbeiterzahl, Produktivität, Reproduktionskosten und Kooperation werden fortgesetzt um diesen Zweck reorganisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A13","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-08","text":"Die reale Subsumtion verläuft spiralförmig, weil jede organisatorische oder technische Produktivitätssteigerung eine neue Norm setzt, deren Verallgemeinerung erneute Transformationen verlangt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B01","text":"Gegebener Werth der Arbeitskraft bestimmt notwendige Arbeitszeit; die Differenz zwischen notwendiger Arbeitszeit und Gesammtarbeitstag bestimmt die individuelle Mehrarbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B02","text":"Arbeiterzahl mal Werth der einzelnen Arbeitskraft ergibt variables Kapital; variables Kapital mal Mehrwerthsrate ergibt die Mehrwerthsmasse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A3","CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B03","text":"Endliche Arbeitstagslänge und begrenzte Arbeiterbevölkerung beschränken extensive Mehrwerthsausdehnung und erzwingen eine Verschiebung zur Veränderung des notwendigen Zeitanteils.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A10","CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B04","text":"Hinreichende Kapitalkonzentration führt zur gleichzeitigen Beschäftigung vieler Arbeiter; planmäßige Verbindung verwandelt die numerische Summe in einen Gesamtarbeiter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A1","CH_V4GB_2COO:A2","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B05","text":"Gemeinsamer Produktionsmittelkonsum, Synchronisation und funktionale Ergänzung erhöhen den Nutzeffekt des Gesamtarbeitstags, ohne die additive Werthlogik aufzuheben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS4","CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_2COO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B06","text":"Produktivitätssteigerung senkt gesellschaftlich notwendige Arbeitszeit je Ware; betrifft sie notwendige Lebensmittel, sinken Arbeitskraftwerth und notwendige Arbeit, während Mehrarbeit innerhalb desselben Arbeitstags steigt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B07","text":"Vereinzelte Produktivitätssteigerung erzeugt Extra-Mehrwert; Konkurrenz verallgemeinert das Verfahren, beseitigt den Sondervorteil und macht die neue Produktivität zur gesellschaftlichen Norm.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B08","text":"Individueller Arbeitskraftkauf plus unbezahlte Kombinationskraft plus externalisierte Leitung erzeugt Kapital als Kommando über einen gesellschaftlichen Arbeitskörper und reproduziert reale Subsumtion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A15","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AFM-B01","text":"Endliche lebendige Arbeit → quantitative Mehrwerthsbestimmung → Grenze extensiver Ausdehnung → innere Verschiebung von notwendiger Arbeit zu Mehrarbeit → Produktivitätssteigerung → Konkurrenzverallgemeinerung → Konzentration vieler Arbeitskräfte → Entstehung des Gesamtarbeiters → Aneignung seiner Kombinationskraft → Kapitalkommando → reale Subsumtion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AFM-B02","text":"Kapitalkommando → gesteigerte gesellschaftliche Produktivität → veränderte Reproduktionskosten und Zeitteilung → höhere Mehrwerthsrate oder Mehrwerthsmasse → erneuerte Konzentration → vertiefte organisatorische und technische Subsumtion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-01","text":"Die Mehrwerthsproduktion wird als dreiachsiges Feld aus Arbeitskräfteumfang, Mehrarbeitsanteil und gesellschaftlicher Kombinationskraft neu kartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-02","text":"Die Opposition von quantitativer und qualitativer Veränderung zerfällt: Arbeiterkonzentration ist zugleich lineare Skalierung der Werthmasse und qualitativer Umschlag des realen Arbeitsprozesses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-03","text":"Produktivität wird von einer technischen Eigenschaft in eine Vermittlung zwischen gesellschaftlich notwendiger Zeit, Arbeitskraftwerth, Mehrarbeitsanteil und Konkurrenzzwang umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-04","text":"Der freie Arbeitsvertrag und der despotische Produktionsprozess werden nicht als widersprüchliche Alternativen, sondern als aufeinanderfolgende Formen derselben kapitalistischen Aneignungsrelation lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2COO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-05","text":"Industrielle Leitung wird in sachliche Koordination und historisch spezifische Eigentums-, Ausbeutungs- und Kontrollfunktionen zerlegt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:ME6","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-06","text":"Das Einzelkapital und das gesellschaftliche Kapital werden als verschiedene, rekursiv vermittelte Ebenen sichtbar: Lokale Abweichung erzeugt Sondergewinn, gesellschaftliche Verallgemeinerung setzt eine neue Norm.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-07","text":"Produktionsmittel werden zugleich als Nichtquelle neuen Werths, als materielle Bedingung kooperativer Produktivität und als verselbständigte Träger kapitalistischen Kommandos lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX1","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene werden Mehrwerthsmasse, relativer Mehrwerth und Kooperation als drei Bestimmungen der quantitativen, zeitlichen und organisatorischen Erweiterung unbezahlter Arbeit verbunden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene vermitteln variables Kapital, Reproduktion der Arbeitskraft, gesellschaftlich notwendige Arbeitszeit und Kapitalkonzentration zwischen individueller Arbeit und gesellschaftlicher Verwerthung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT2","CH_V4GB_5RUM:ME1","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene ersetzt die Analyse isolierter Ausbeutungsakte durch eine Karte verschiebbarer Skalierungsachsen, selbstaufhebender Innovationsvorsprünge und angeeigneter Kooperationskräfte.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:ME2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-zeitlichen Ebene erscheint Realität als asymmetrische Verbindung todter Produktionsbedingungen mit endlicher lebendiger Arbeit, deren individuelle Zeiten zu gesellschaftlicher Zeit verdichtet und kapitalistisch geteilt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollzieht die Architektur ihren Gegenstand, indem sie quantitative Formeln schrittweise in gesellschaftliche Relationen, rekursive Konkurrenzschleifen und Verkehrungen von Arbeit und Produktionsmitteln überführt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS8","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-01","text":"Das Kapital benötigt lebendige Arbeit als einzige Quelle neuen Werths, strebt aber zugleich danach, notwendige Arbeitszeit und Arbeiterzahl je Produkt fortgesetzt zu vermindern.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A8","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-02","text":"Gesellschaftliche Großarbeit verlangt Koordination, doch die Architektur begründet nicht vollständig, weshalb diese Koordination unter Lohnarbeitsbedingungen dauerhaft außerhalb der Arbeiter liegen muss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-03","text":"Die Ableitung relativen Mehrwerths setzt voraus, dass sinkende Reproduktionskosten tatsächlich den Werth der Arbeitskraft senken; der soziale Übertragungsmechanismus bleibt unterbestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-04","text":"Additive Werthbildung und qualitative Kooperationsproduktivität bleiben nur kohärent, wenn gesteigerter Nutzeffekt, potenzierte individuelle Arbeit und gesellschaftliche Durchschnittsarbeit nicht ineinander überführt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT6","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-01","text":"Der erste Mutationspunkt liegt im Umschlag der Arbeiterzahl von einer bloßen Multiplikationsgröße der Mehrwerthsmasse in die Morphologie eines Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-02","text":"Der zweite Mutationspunkt liegt im Übergang von individuellem Produktivitätsvorsprung und Extra-Mehrwert zu gesellschaftlich verallgemeinerter Produktivität und relativem Mehrwerth.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-03","text":"Der dritte Mutationspunkt verwandelt constantes Kapital von einem bloßen Werthüberträger in eine konzentrierte Organisations- und Kommandobedingung, ohne es deshalb zur Quelle neuen Werths zu machen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-04","text":"Der vierte Mutationspunkt führt von der formellen Unterwerfung vorgegebener Arbeitsbedingungen über organisatorische Kooperation zur technischen Umwälzung der Produktionsweise.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A13","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als gekoppelte Verwerthungsmaschine, in der gegenständliche Arbeitsbedingungen lebendige Arbeitskräfte sammeln, synchronisieren und auf die Produktion zusätzlichen Werths ausrichten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A14","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird vom selbständigen Verkäufer seiner Arbeitskraft zum abhängigen Organ eines gesellschaftlichen Arbeitskörpers, dessen Einheit ihm als fremde Kapitalmacht gegenübertritt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist endlich, teilbar und synchronisierbar: Kapital kann sie nicht erschaffen, sondern nur verlängern, umverteilen, verdichten und fremd aneignen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME1","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04","text":"Der verbleibende Kampf betrifft die Verfügung über Produktionsmittel, gesellschaftliche Kombination und frei werdende Zeit; mögliche Flucht liegt in der Selbstorganisation des Gesamtarbeiters, bleibt aber systematisch außerhalb der positiven Form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B01","text":"Die Architektur ist hinreichend rekonstruierbar, wenn die Mehrwerthsformel, die innere Teilung des Arbeitstags, die emergente Produktivkraft der Kooperation und deren kapitalistische Aneignung gemeinsam erhalten bleiben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B02","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die historische Bestimmung des Arbeitskraftwerths, die genaue Schwelle des Kapitalminimums, die quantitative Größe einzelner Kooperationseffekte und die Übertragung verbilligter Reproduktion in gesunkenen Arbeitskraftwerth.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:MRT2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B03","text":"Das System ist kohärent, sofern Werthbildung und Gebrauchswerthproduktivität, individueller Extra-Mehrwert und allgemeiner relativer Mehrwerth sowie Koordination und kapitalistisches Kommando strikt unterschieden werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT8","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B04","text":"Die stärkste Struktur liegt in der Verbindung von endlicher lebendiger Arbeit, begrenzter extensiver Skalierung, innerer Zeitumverteilung und nichtadditiver gesellschaftlicher Produktivität.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B05","text":"Die tatsächliche Bewegung bleibt nur erhalten, wenn die Rekonstruktion rekursiv von Grenzen zu Mutationen, von lokalen Produktivitätsvorsprüngen zu gesellschaftlichen Normen und von Konzentration zu Kommando fortschreitet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT8","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B06","text":"Axiomatischer Reduktion widersteht die antagonistische Doppelgestalt der Kooperation: Sie ist zugleich reale gesellschaftliche Produktivkraft und ihre entfremdete Existenz als Kapitalmacht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211824861917Z_32570fe1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 10–12","source_sha256":"9e8c65bf5b788581d11f935746cd0f002495d425d4b6e0a75d829282e56bf158","sha256":"0eb3e5ae8a46d7c75c1f13b4d06d429b9257672f2e4e48d5ec4a2f1798bc0e64","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:18:24.863383+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B01","text":"The central problem consists in how capital, despite finite working time, expands surplus-value production through the number of workers, the internal redistribution of the working day, and the social combination of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B02","text":"The global thesis determines living labour as the sole source of new value, while productivity and cooperation alter the forms in which this source is temporally divided, quantitatively scaled, and socially appropriated.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A8","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B03","text":"The argument connects an extensive axis of worker numbers, an intensive axis of the rate of surplus-value, and an organisational axis of combined labour-power into a unified architecture of surplus-value augmentation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B04","text":"The movement proceeds from linear value aggregation to qualitative productivity increase, without abolishing the difference between additive value formation and emergent use-value benefit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_2COO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B05","text":"Once the external extension of the working day encounters limits, the valorisation strategy mutates into alteration of the mode of production, the shortening of necessary labour, and the organisational condensation of the total working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B06","text":"The technically required connection of many labours is organised capitalistically as external management, control, and command, whereby social labour-power appears as a productive force of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS6","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B07","text":"Competition makes the individual productivity advantage a self-abolishing transitional form: it generates extra surplus-value, compels generalisation, and continues the productivity compulsion on a new social basis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AS-B08","text":"The closure is recursive rather than terminal: real subsumption extends capital's command over social labour, but abolishes neither its dependence on living labour nor the tension arising therefrom.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A18","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Living labour alone forms new value and surplus-value; constant capital transfers existing value without itself being a source of new value formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A7","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The mass of surplus-value is determined by the magnitude of variable capital converted into labour-power and by the rate of surplus-value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS2","CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Surplus-value can be increased extensively through additional labour-powers or intensively through a greater surplus-labour share; the limit of extensive and absolute expansion compels the transition to internal redistribution of time and organisational productivity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Quantitative worker concentration enlarges the mass of value linearly, yet on the use-value side generates a combined productive force that cannot be reduced to the sum of individual forces.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Productivity increase lowers commodity values by reducing socially necessary labour-time, but reduces the value of labour-power only insofar as it cheapens necessary means of subsistence or their means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The working day is not merely an externally extendable magnitude, but an internally distributable field of time in which necessary labour and surplus-labour vary inversely.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] The greatest possible self-valorisation directs technical change, commodity production, time economy, and labour organisation toward the production of realisable surplus-value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A13","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Capital purchases individual labour-powers, but additionally appropriates, without a special equivalent, the combined labour-power that first arises in the production process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A15","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] The general need for coordination of social labour is reshaped under capitalist relations of property and exploitation into an antagonistic command function, without being identical with this historically particular form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Exchange of equivalents in the purchase of labour-power does not exclude the appropriation of unpaid labour, because this arises only through the use of the purchased labour-power in the production process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Individual extra surplus-value disappears with the competitive generalisation of its production method, while its social productivity effect may persist.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Capital remains dependent on living labour and simultaneously attempts to reduce the share of time necessary for its reproduction, its number per product, and its autonomous disposal over the labour process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] A sufficient capital minimum forms the threshold at which the permanent employment of many labour-powers, social averaging, and the capitalist managerial function stably coincide.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Cooperation opens real subsumption as an organisational transformation of the labour process and remains the basic layer of later technical and division-of-labour forms.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_2COO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-01","text":"Labour-time retains its function as the measure of value, but expands its scope from the individual working day through the social total working day to the synchronised time of the collective worker.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A9","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-02","text":"The number of workers mutates from a scalar factor of the mass of surplus-value into the material basis of a functionally articulated collective labour-body.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-03","text":"Productivity shifts from technical cheapening of commodities to power over socially necessary time and finally to the capitalist redistribution of the working day in favour of surplus-labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-04","text":"Cooperation retains its general function as the connection of many labours, but returns under capitalist conditions as external command over those cooperating.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:NX9","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-05","text":"Capital mutates from an advanced sum of value into the organisational and command centre that causes objective conditions of production to appear as the seemingly autonomous subject of labour appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS8","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-06","text":"Extra surplus-value disappears as a permanent individual difference after it has triggered the competitive generalisation of more productive methods and hence a shift in the social level.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-07","text":"Constant capital remains excluded from new value formation, but acquires an expanded operational function as the concentrated material condition of common production, cheapened products, and externalised command.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RMD-08","text":"The production of absolute surplus-value is not refuted, but absorbed as a limited basic layer into an architecture that transforms the labour process itself through cooperation and relative surplus-value production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A13","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-01","text":"The formula of the mass of surplus-value remains a local quantitative determination; at cluster level it becomes the point of departure for a threefold scaling through worker numbers, surplus-labour share, and combined productive force.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-02","text":"The natural limit of the individual working day remains local; it becomes globally effective as a catalyst for the transition from external extension to internal temporal displacement and productive reorganisation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-03","text":"The sectoral condition that only the cheapening of necessary means of subsistence lowers the value of labour-power remains specific; it scales into the mediation between social productivity and the general rate of surplus-value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-04","text":"Individual forms of cooperation such as synchronisation, spatial concentration, and common consumption of means of production remain local mechanisms; at cluster level they sustain the emergence of a non-additive social productive force.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D3","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-05","text":"The exact magnitude of the capital minimum remains historically underdetermined; only its function as a threshold between self-labour, the employment of many labour-powers, and autonomised capital command scales upward.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:MRT6","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-06","text":"The distinction between extra surplus-value and relative surplus-value remains a local distinction of effects; at cluster level it generates the recursive transition from individual deviation to social productivity compulsion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:NX4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:CGD-07","text":"Only at cluster level do extensive mass of surplus-value, relative redistribution of time, and cooperative emergence become visible as complementary moments of advancing real subsumption.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-01","text":"The magnitude or technical equipment of total capital cannot count as the immediate source of new value; decisive remains its disposal over living labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX2","CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-02","text":"Neither the number of workers nor the degree of exploitation can replace the mass of surplus-value without limit, because labour-time, population, and conditions of reproduction impose absolute or social limits.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX3","CH_V4GB_5RUM:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-03","text":"Productivity increase is not identical with free time for workers; under a surplus-value orientation it can increase the surplus-labour share with an unchanged or extended working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:NX7","CH_V4GB_1BDR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-04","text":"Social productivity cannot be explained atomistically from isolated personal capacities, since combination itself generates an additional productive force.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:DNX1","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-05","text":"The necessity of coordination establishes neither capitalist property nor the despotic form of management.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD3","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:GNX-06","text":"Market equality and the full-value purchase of labour-power do not refute exploitation, because they do not grasp the productive use and collective combination of labour-powers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:DNX3","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-01","text":"False must be a model of self-valorising dead labour that could generate surplus-value independently of finite living labour and its social organisation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-02","text":"False must be a value- and domination-neutral technology whose intervention in productivity remained separated from reproduction costs, the division of time, and capitalist appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:DNX1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-03","text":"False must be an exclusively market-based model of autonomous sellers of labour-power, because the production process transforms them into an externally directed collective worker and a collective relation of dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2COO:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-04","text":"False must be the transhistorical unity of property, industrial management, and social coordination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:DNX4","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:DBN-05","text":"False must be the equation of use-value productivity and value creation, since cooperative labour can produce more useful effect without increasing the value formed per labour-hour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:NX4","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-01","text":"The deepest structural absence is the collective worker as owner, manager, and beneficiary of its own social productive force.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable remains the return of saved necessary labour-time to workers as self-determined free time; the saving of time is systematically reconfigured as surplus-labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-03","text":"Circled around, but not positively integrated, is an immediate association of workers whose social unity proceeds from the relations of the workers themselves rather than from the unity of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX3","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSA-04","text":"Ontologically inadmissible is a capital that completely abolishes its dependence on living labour and nevertheless persists as self-valorising value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-01","text":"The absolute limit of the working day transforms productivity increase and cooperative reorganisation from mere options into systematic paths to further surplus-value augmentation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","CL_V4GB_04:GA-06","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A6","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-02","text":"Worker concentration possesses a double yield: it enlarges the mass of surplus-value proportionally and simultaneously generates a non-proportional productive force of the collective worker.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-02","CL_V4GB_04:GA-04","CL_V4GB_04:GA-13","CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-03","text":"Insofar as cooperative economy in means of production cheapens necessary means of subsistence, an organisational productive force can be translated into relative surplus-value through the falling value of labour-power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-05","CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_2COO:D2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-04","text":"Competition transforms the temporary advantage of individual capitals into a general compulsion for the continuous alteration of technology and labour organisation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-07","CL_V4GB_04:GA-11","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-05","text":"Because only individual labour-powers are purchased, the social force of combination lies outside the explicit equivalent form and can appear as a free inherent force of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2COO:A15","CH_V4GB_2COO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-06","text":"The capital minimum is not merely a quantitative threshold of advance, but the turning point at which the mass of surplus-value, the collective worker, and autonomised command reproduce one another.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-02","CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:GA-13","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-07","text":"The attempt to reduce necessary labour and the number of workers per product increases capital's power of valorisation and simultaneously sharpens its irremovable dependence on living labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-01","CL_V4GB_04:GA-05","CL_V4GB_04:GA-12","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:XD-08","text":"The separability of technical coordination from capitalist command makes a self-determined social organisation of labour conceptually possible, although it remains excluded in the positive architecture.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-01","text":"At cluster level, capital appears not primarily as a thing or sum of money, but as an apparatus for the capture, combination, and redistribution of social labour-time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:ME1","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-02","text":"Capitalist causality is multiscalar: demography limits the mass of labour, technology alters socially necessary time, cooperation generates productive force, and competition generalises local changes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:D5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-03","text":"The subject of production divides: the individual worker remains seller of labour-power, becomes in the production process an organ of the collective worker, while capital appears as the seeming subject of the common productive force.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-04","text":"Capitalist time is at once extensive, distributive, and synchronous: it extends labour, shifts the boundary within the working day, and condenses many individual times into a combined social working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-05","text":"The political domination of capital arises not outside production, but from the unity of ownership of conditions of production, the purpose of surplus-value, coordination, and control of the collective worker.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A14","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-06","text":"Epistemologically, the architecture requires a strict separation of value formation and use-value productivity, individual and social value, and technical management and capitalist domination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:ME4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A9","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:BSD-07","text":"Historically, real subsumption appears as a spiral: organisational cooperation creates the basic layer, technical innovation alters the mode of production, and competition compels its renewed social generalisation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-01","text":"The surplus-value loop proceeds from an increased mass of surplus-value, through more variable capital or a higher rate of surplus-value, to renewed disposal over larger masses of labour and more intensive appropriation of time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A5","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-02","text":"The limit loop leads from finite extension of the working day to the reduction of necessary labour-time, thence to the revolutionisation of the mode of production, and finally to the renewed increase of the surplus-labour share.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-03","text":"The innovation loop is: individual productivity advantage, extra surplus-value, competitive pressure, generalisation, abolition of the special advantage, and renewed innovation compulsion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-04","text":"The concentration loop connects larger capital, more simultaneously employed workers, stronger cooperation, higher productive force, and a renewed material superiority of concentrated capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS5","CH_V4GB_2COO:A9","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-05","text":"The command loop connects growing cooperation with the need for coordination, antagonistic resistance, intensified supervision, and further autonomisation of the managerial function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:D7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-06","text":"The reification loop leads from a force of combination generated by workers, through its appropriation by capital, to its appearance as capital productivity, which seemingly confirms the necessity of capital command.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-07","text":"The central attractor is the maximum appropriation of social labour-time: worker numbers, productivity, reproduction costs, and cooperation are continuously reorganised around this purpose.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A13","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:RLE-08","text":"Real subsumption proceeds spirally because every organisational or technical productivity increase sets a new norm whose generalisation demands renewed transformations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B01","text":"Given value of labour-power determines necessary labour-time; the difference between necessary labour-time and the total working day determines individual surplus-labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B02","text":"Number of workers times the value of individual labour-power yields variable capital; variable capital times the rate of surplus-value yields the mass of surplus-value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A3","CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B03","text":"Finite length of the working day and limited worker population restrict extensive surplus-value expansion and compel a shift toward altering the necessary share of time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A10","CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B04","text":"Sufficient capital concentration leads to the simultaneous employment of many workers; planned connection transforms the numerical sum into a collective worker.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A1","CH_V4GB_2COO:A2","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B05","text":"Common consumption of means of production, synchronisation, and functional complementarity increase the useful effect of the total working day without abolishing additive value logic.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:AS4","CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_2COO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B06","text":"Productivity increase lowers socially necessary labour-time per commodity; where it concerns necessary means of subsistence, the value of labour-power and necessary labour fall, while surplus-labour rises within the same working day.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A7","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B07","text":"Isolated productivity increase generates extra surplus-value; competition generalises the method, eliminates the special advantage, and makes the new productivity the social norm.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FGS-B08","text":"Individual purchase of labour-power plus unpaid force of combination plus externalised management generates capital as command over a social labour-body and reproduces real subsumption.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A15","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AFM-B01","text":"Finite living labour → quantitative determination of surplus-value → limit of extensive expansion → internal shift from necessary labour to surplus-labour → productivity increase → competitive generalisation → concentration of many labour-powers → emergence of the collective worker → appropriation of its force of combination → capital command → real subsumption.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:AFM-B02","text":"Capital command → increased social productivity → altered reproduction costs and division of time → higher rate or mass of surplus-value → renewed concentration → deepened organisational and technical subsumption.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-01","text":"Surplus-value production is remapped as a three-axis field of labour-power magnitude, surplus-labour share, and social force of combination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-02","text":"The opposition of quantitative and qualitative change disintegrates: worker concentration is simultaneously linear scaling of the mass of value and a qualitative transformation of the real labour process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-03","text":"Productivity is reclassified from a technical property into a mediation between socially necessary time, value of labour-power, surplus-labour share, and competitive compulsion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-04","text":"The free labour contract and the despotic production process become legible not as contradictory alternatives, but as successive forms of the same capitalist relation of appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2COO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-05","text":"Industrial management is divided into objective coordination and historically specific functions of property, exploitation, and control.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:ME6","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-06","text":"Individual capital and social capital become visible as different, recursively mediated levels: local deviation generates special profit, social generalisation establishes a new norm.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MME-07","text":"Means of production become legible simultaneously as non-sources of new value, as the material condition of cooperative productivity, and as autonomised bearers of capitalist command.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:NX1","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, mass of surplus-value, relative surplus-value, and cooperation are connected as three determinations of the quantitative, temporal, and organisational expansion of unpaid labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, variable capital, reproduction of labour-power, socially necessary labour-time, and capital concentration mediate between individual labour and social valorisation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:ALT2","CH_V4GB_5RUM:ME1","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the analysis of isolated acts of exploitation is replaced by a map of shiftable scaling axes, self-abolishing innovation advantages, and appropriated forces of cooperation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:ME2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2","CH_V4GB_2COO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, reality appears as the asymmetric connection of dead conditions of production with finite living labour, whose individual times are condensed into social time and divided capitalistically.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS6","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the architecture enacts its object by progressively transforming quantitative formulas into social relations, recursive loops of competition, and inversions of labour and means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:FGS8","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-01","text":"Capital requires living labour as the sole source of new value, but simultaneously strives continuously to reduce necessary labour-time and the number of workers per product.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A8","CH_V4GB_5RUM:SD2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-02","text":"Large-scale social labour requires coordination, yet the architecture does not fully establish why this coordination must permanently lie outside the workers under conditions of wage labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A10","CH_V4GB_2COO:A11","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-03","text":"The derivation of relative surplus-value presupposes that falling reproduction costs actually lower the value of labour-power; the social transmission mechanism remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:FL-04","text":"Additive value formation and qualitative cooperative productivity remain coherent only if increased useful effect, potentiated individual labour, and social average labour are not collapsed into one another.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT6","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point lies in the transformation of the number of workers from a mere multiplicative magnitude of the mass of surplus-value into the morphology of a collective worker.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:A3","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point lies in the transition from individual productivity advantage and extra surplus-value to socially generalised productivity and relative surplus-value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point transforms constant capital from a mere transmitter of value into a concentrated condition of organisation and command, without thereby making it a source of new value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A7","CH_V4GB_2COO:D5","CH_V4GB_2COO:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MP-04","text":"The fourth mutation point leads from the formal subjection of pre-given labour conditions, through organisational cooperation, to the technical revolutionisation of the mode of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A13","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD5","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a coupled machine of valorisation in which objective labour conditions collect, synchronise, and orient living labour-powers toward the production of additional value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:A14","CH_V4GB_2COO:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-02","text":"The subject changes from the autonomous seller of its labour-power into the dependent organ of a social labour-body, whose unity confronts it as an alien power of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD4","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is finite, divisible, and synchronisable: capital cannot create it, but can only extend, redistribute, condense, and alienly appropriate it.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:ME1","CH_V4GB_2COO:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04","text":"The remaining struggle concerns disposal over means of production, social combination, and time becoming free; possible escape lies in the self-organisation of the collective worker, but remains systematically outside the positive form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:SNX2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:SNX1","CH_V4GB_2COO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B01","text":"The architecture is sufficiently reconstructible if the formula of surplus-value, the internal division of the working day, the emergent productive force of cooperation, and its capitalist appropriation are jointly retained.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:D1","CH_V4GB_1BDR:A2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B02","text":"Underdetermined remain the historical determination of the value of labour-power, the exact threshold of the capital minimum, the quantitative magnitude of individual cooperation effects, and the transmission of cheapened reproduction into a lowered value of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:MRT2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT2","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B03","text":"The system is coherent provided value formation and use-value productivity, individual extra surplus-value and general relative surplus-value, as well as coordination and capitalist command, are strictly distinguished.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT3","CH_V4GB_1BDR:MRT8","CH_V4GB_2COO:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B04","text":"The strongest structure lies in the connection of finite living labour, limited extensive scaling, internal redistribution of time, and non-additive social productivity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_5RUM:AS4","CH_V4GB_1BDR:AS2","CH_V4GB_2COO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B05","text":"The actual movement is retained only if reconstruction advances recursively from limits to mutations, from local productivity advantages to social norms, and from concentration to command.","refs":["CH_V4GB_1BDR:SD2","CH_V4GB_2COO:MRT8","CH_V4GB_5RUM:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B06","text":"Axiomatic reduction resists the antagonistic dual form of cooperation: it is at once real social productive force and its alienated existence as a power of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2COO:SD1","CH_V4GB_2COO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_04@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_04:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 10–12","context":"5) Rate und Masse des Mehrwerths. · 1) Begriff des relativen Mehrwerths. · 2) Cooperation."}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 13–15","order":5,"parents":["CH_V4GB_3TDA","CH_V4GB_4MUG","CH_V4GB_4M_2"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_05@R001","sha256":"c6ce6c1ced5645f4f41f298f389e2623dad8482f510e592b7ca2bd91fd6b22de","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-01","text":"Das zentrale Problem ist die endogene Umwandlung der handwerklich fundierten Manufaktur in ein maschinelles Produktionssystem, dessen technische Arbeitsersparnis unter kapitalistischen Bedingungen Verwertung, Beherrschung und umfassende Reorganisation der Produktionsformen erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-02","text":"Die globale These lautet, dass gesellschaftlich erzeugte Produktivkraft nur durch kapitalistische Verfügung wirksam wird und deshalb den Produzenten als fremde Macht gegenübertritt, während ihre Kosten auf Arbeitskraft, Familie, Gesellschaft und Natur verlagert werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-03","text":"Die gerichtete Bewegung führt vom menschlich gegliederten Gesamtarbeiter über den objektiven Maschinenorganismus zur gesellschaftlichen und ökologischen Totalisierung des Fabrikprinzips.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-04","text":"Das Argument wird auf Clusterebene zu einer genealogischen, kausalen und widerspruchslogischen Rekonstruktion, in der jede Produktionsform die Bedingungen ihrer eigenen Überschreitung hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-05","text":"Die Manufaktur erzeugt spezialisierte Werkzeuge und Skalierungszwänge, die ihre handwerkliche Grundlage sprengen; die maschinelle Produktion beseitigt diese Schranke, reproduziert sich technisch selbst und ordnet ältere Produktionsformen als abhängige Abteilungen unter.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A8","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-06","text":"Die Bewegung ist kumulativ, mutationsgetrieben und rekursiv: zeitliche Folge wird synchronisiert, technische Selbstreproduktion beschleunigt die Umwälzung, und marktvermittelte Expansion kehrt zyklisch als Krise und erneuter Rationalisierungszwang zurück.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-07","text":"Die Schließung bleibt negativ: Regulation kann einzelne Zerstörungen begrenzen, aber keine endgültige Stabilität herstellen; der Prozess endet bei der Untergrabung seiner menschlichen und natürlichen Voraussetzungen sowie bei der unbestimmten Notwendigkeit bewusster gesellschaftlicher Verfügung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Kapitalistische Produktivkraftentwicklung ist auf die Verkürzung notwendiger Arbeit zugunsten der Mehrarbeit gerichtet und wird durch Mehrwertproduktion, Warenverwohlfeilerung und Konkurrenz selektiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Gesellschaftliche Kooperation, Wissen und Naturkräfte erscheinen den Produzenten als Produktivkräfte des Kapitals, weil Eigentum und Kommando ihre gemeinsame Wirksamkeit aneignen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A17","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Das produktive Organ mutiert vom spezialisierten menschlichen Glied des Gesamtarbeiters zum objektiven Maschinenorganismus, der dem Arbeiter als autonomes Subjekt gegenübertritt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Arbeitsteilung wandelt sich von der empirischen Zerlegung handwerklicher Tätigkeiten zur wissenschaftlich-technischen Analyse des Produktionsprozesses, ohne die kapitalistische Fixierung des Arbeiters auf Teilfunktionen automatisch aufzuheben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:NX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Die Steigerung gesellschaftlicher Produktivkraft wird durch Entselbständigung und Entwertung individueller Produktionsfähigkeit erzeugt, obwohl sie zugleich die materielle Möglichkeit vielseitiger Individualität hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Gesellschaftliche Arbeitsersparnis und kapitalistische Rentabilität bilden verschiedene Selektionsmaße; daher kann das Kapital produktivere Technik zurückweisen, wenn bezahlte Arbeitskraft billiger bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Maschinerie verwandelt variables in konstantes Kapital und erzeugt relative Arbeitsverdrängung, die mit absoluter Beschäftigungszunahme während quantitativer Akkumulationsphasen vereinbar bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A18","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Werkstattdespotie erweitert sich zur Fabrikdisziplin und schließlich zu einem internationalen Produktionsnetz, während ihre äußere Vermittlung anarchisch, konkurrenzförmig und zyklisch bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D14","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Marktlich gesetzter Zeitdruck wird zunächst zum technischen Gesetz gekoppelter Teilprozesse und danach zum Verwertungsdruck auf Nutzungsdauer, Geschwindigkeit und Arbeitsdichte des maschinellen Systems.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A14","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Gesetzliche Begrenzung beendet den Verwertungszwang nicht, sondern verlagert ihn in technische Intensivierung, Maschinisierung, Konzentration und erneute Regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Jede entwickelte Produktionsform erzeugt durch ihre eigenen Produktivitäts- und Skalierungszwänge die technische Grundlage ihrer Überschreitung und beschleunigt damit die fortlaufende Entwertung bestehender Produktionsmittel und Fähigkeiten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Kapitalistische Produktivkraftentwicklung kulminiert in der gleichzeitigen Untergrabung von Arbeitskraft und Boden, also ihrer beiden materiellen Reproduktionsbedingungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","text":"[Attractor] Die verdrängte Gegenform besteht in kollektiver Verfügung über den vergesellschafteten Produktionsorganismus, wechselnden Funktionen, polytechnischer Bildung und bewusster Regulation des gesellschaftlichen Stoffwechsels.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-01","text":"Handwerksgeschick bleibt zunächst technologische Grundlage, mutiert dann zur Schranke von Kontrolle und Skalierung und verschwindet als regulierendes Prinzip, sobald Maschinen durch Maschinen produziert werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A5","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-02","text":"Das Werkzeug kehrt funktional verändert wieder: Zuerst verlängert es den spezialisierten Teilarbeiter, dann wird seine operative Funktion vom menschlichen Organismus gelöst und in den Mechanismus übertragen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-03","text":"Der Gesamtarbeiter mutiert vom gegliederten Kollektiv menschlicher Organe zum objektiven Produktionsorganismus; seine Vergesellschaftung bleibt bestehen, während seine Einheit vom Kapital in die Apparatur verlagert wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A9","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-04","text":"Arbeitsteilung wechselt ihre Funktion von der subjektiven Spezialisierung der Arbeiter zur objektiven Prozessanalyse und erscheint zuletzt als Konflikt zwischen technologischer Funktionsbeweglichkeit und kapitalistischer Fixierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-05","text":"Zeit mutiert vom Nacheinander handwerklicher Operationen über synchrone Kopplung zur intensiven Verdichtung maschineller Arbeitszeit und zur zyklischen Zeit des Weltmarkts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-06","text":"Die Einheit von innerer Planung und äußerer Anarchie persistiert, erweitert aber ihren Geltungsbereich von der einzelnen Werkstatt über Fabrikorganisation und Arbeitsmarkt bis zur internationalen Arbeitsteilung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD3","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-07","text":"Regulation kehrt ihre zunächst begrenzende Valenz teilweise um: Die Schranke extensiver Ausbeutung katalysiert intensive Ausbeutung und technisch konzentrierte Kapitalherrschaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-08","text":"Der ganze Arbeiter verschwindet zunächst als reale Produktionsfigur und kehrt als versperrte Möglichkeit vielseitiger Individualität auf höherer Ebene wieder.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-01","text":"Die Kombination verschiedener Handwerke und die Zerlegung eines gleichartigen Handwerks bleiben lokale Entstehungsvarianten; auf Clusterebene zählt ihre Konvergenz in der Figur des unselbständigen Teilarbeiters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A3","CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-02","text":"Die Unterscheidung heterogener und organischer Manufaktur bleibt eine lokale Produkttypologie; nach oben skaliert nur die Umwandlung zeitlicher Folge in synchronisierte und proportionierte Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A9","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-03","text":"Die dreiteilige Anatomie entwickelter Maschinerie bleibt eine technische Bestimmung der unteren Ebene; clustertragend ist die Übertragung der operierenden Funktion vom Arbeiter auf den Mechanismus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-04","text":"Die partielle Wertübertragung der Maschine bleibt ein lokaler Wertmechanismus; sie skaliert zur globalen Unterscheidung zwischen technischer Produktivität, gesellschaftlicher Arbeitsersparnis und kapitalistischer Einsatzgrenze.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-05","text":"Frauen- und Kinderarbeit sind nicht bloß besondere Fabrikfälle; auf Clusterebene zeigen sie die Einziehung der Familie und vermeintlichen Privatsphäre in die Verwertungsarchitektur.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-06","text":"Einzelne neue Produktionszweige und Beschäftigungszahlen bleiben lokale Erscheinungen; nach oben skaliert das Verhältnis von relativer Arbeitsabnahme, bedingter Wiederanziehung und zyklischer Beschäftigungsunsicherheit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:NX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-07","text":"Die kapitalistische Agrikultur erscheint lokal als abschließender Gegenstandsbereich, wird auf Clusterebene jedoch zur terminalen Generalisierung eines Systems, das seine Reproduktionskosten auf Arbeitskraft und Natur externalisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:A17","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-01","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein neutraler Begriff von Arbeitsteilung oder Technik, der Eigentum, Kommando und Verwertungsform von ihren Wirkungen abtrennt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-02","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist der selbständige Einzelproduzent oder Kleinbetrieb als dauerhaftes Gegenmodell zur kapitalistischen Organisation gesellschaftlicher Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-03","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Gleichrichtung von Produktivitätssteigerung, individueller Fähigkeitsentwicklung und Verbesserung der Produzentenlage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX3","CH_V4GB_4MUG:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-04","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein automatischer Kompensationsmechanismus, der verdrängte Arbeiter notwendig und gleichzeitig in neu erzeugte Beschäftigung überführt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX15","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-05","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Annahme, Vertragsgleichheit, Konkurrenz und individuelles Eigeninteresse erzeugten hinreichende humane Grenzen der Verwertung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:DNX5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-06","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine endgültige regulatorische Schließung, weil jede Begrenzung zugleich Intensivierung, technische Anpassung oder Konzentration hervorbringen kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-07","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine automatische Befreiung von Arbeitsteilung durch technologische Aufhebung handwerklicher Spezialisierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-01","text":"Damit das System Bestand hat, muss die Vorstellung falsch sein, Kapital sei nur ein äußerliches Eigentumsverhältnis; es muss den gesellschaftlichen Arbeitskörper technisch organisieren und als eigene Apparateigenschaft verkörpern.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-02","text":"Falsch sein muss die Naturalisierung dauerhafter Berufsspezialisierung, weil permanente technologische Beweglichkeit die fixierte Arbeitsfunktion historisch erzeugt und fortlaufend entwertet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-03","text":"Falsch sein muss die Annahme, persönliche Produktionsmittel, räumliche Zerstreuung oder Kleineigentum bildeten einen stabilen Außenraum des Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:NX11","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-04","text":"Falsch sein muss die Behandlung von Familienzerstörung, Arbeitskraftverschleiß und Naturverwüstung als zufällige Nebenfolgen; sie bilden systematische Kostenverlagerungen einer einheitlichen Verwertungsarchitektur.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-05","text":"Disqualifiziert werden sowohl technischer Determinismus als auch reine Äußerlichkeit der gesellschaftlichen Form: Wirkungen lassen sich nicht aus Technik allein ableiten, doch die konkrete Technik entsteht selbst unter Verwertungszwang.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:DNX7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste Abwesenheit ist ein kollektiver Produzent, der die objektiv vergesellschaftete Produktivkraft selbst besitzt, leitet und disponiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-02","text":"Die technisch mögliche freie Zeit bleibt als gesellschaftliche Wirklichkeit unzugänglich, weil Arbeitsersparnis in zusätzliche Verfügungszeit des Kapitals umschlägt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-03","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Versöhnung permanenter technologischer Revolution mit dauerhaft gesicherter Arbeit und voller menschlicher Entwicklung; Vielseitigkeit existiert nur als erzeugte, aber versperrte Möglichkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-04","text":"Die positive Gegenform bewusster Regulation von Produktion, Arbeitswechsel, Bildung, Familie und Naturstoffwechsel bleibt institutionell unbestimmt und wirkt deshalb nur als negativer Attraktor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-01","text":"Der Widerspruch der Manufaktur erzeugt die Maschinerie endogen: Die handwerkliche Grundlage liefert spezialisierte Werkzeuge, wird aber zur Schranke und erzwingt die Übertragung der operierenden Funktion auf den Mechanismus. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","CL_V4GB_05:GA-11","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-02","text":"Die Vergesellschaftung der Arbeit steigert sich zur ontologischen Inversion: Der Gesamtarbeiter verliert mit der Verlagerung seiner Einheit in den Maschinenorganismus die Möglichkeit, als autonomes kollektives Subjekt aufzutreten. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-02","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-03","text":"Die Marktzeit wird in der Manufaktur zum technischen Kopplungsgesetz und in der großen Industrie zum Druck auf Maschinennutzung, Geschwindigkeit und Arbeitsdichte. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-09","CH_V4GB_3TDA:D5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A14","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-04","text":"Die Verbilligung und Vereinfachung von Arbeitskraft erweitert sich durch Familienarbeit, technische Verdrängung und zyklische Unsicherheit zur Reproduktion einer disponiblen Arbeiterbevölkerung. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A16","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-05","text":"Die Verbindung innerbetrieblicher Planung mit gesellschaftlicher Anarchie totalisiert sich als globales Fabriknetz, dessen internationale Arbeitsteilung durch industrielle Zyklen destabilisiert wird. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-08","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-06","text":"Arbeitsgesetzgebung ist zugleich Gegenmacht und Modernisierungszwang: Sie begrenzt extensive Ausbeutung, treibt intensive Ausbeutung an und beschleunigt den Untergang kleiner Produzenten. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-07","text":"Die objektive Beweglichkeit technischer Funktionen verschärft den Widerspruch zur kapitalistischen Fixierung des Arbeiters und erzeugt daraus die Notwendigkeit polytechnischer Bildung und vielseitiger Entwicklung. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-04","CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-08","text":"Die Einheit von Fortschritt und Exploitation erweitert sich von der Verarmung individueller Produktionsfähigkeit zur gleichzeitigen Erschöpfung von Arbeitskraft und Boden. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD8","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-01","text":"Das produktive Subjekt ist weder der Einzelarbeiter noch das autonome Kollektiv, sondern eine vom Kapital organisierte Einheit, die vom menschlichen Gesamtarbeiter in den Maschinenorganismus wandert und den Produzenten zum austauschbaren Funktionsträger macht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-02","text":"Realität spaltet sich in gesellschaftlich mögliche Produktivität und kapitalistisch aktualisierte Rentabilität; technische Überlegenheit garantiert deshalb weder Einsatz noch gesellschaftliche Rationalität.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-03","text":"Die dominante Zeitform verbindet Synchronisierung, kontinuierliche Beschleunigung, intensive Verdichtung und industrielle Zyklen, während die technisch mögliche freie Zeit gesellschaftlich blockiert bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-04","text":"Kausalität wird rekursiv: Technische Schranken, gesetzliche Grenzen und soziale Widerstände unterbrechen die Verwertung nicht, sondern werden in neue Organisations- und Innovationszwänge übersetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-05","text":"Politik erscheint weder als äußerer Korrekturmechanismus noch als endgültige Lösung, sondern als immanentes Feld, auf dem Schutz, Verallgemeinerung der Regulation und technisch konzentrierte Herrschaft ineinandergreifen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D15","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-06","text":"Räumliche Expansion universalisiert die innere Asymmetrie des Fabriksystems als internationale Arbeitsteilung und verbindet industrielle Akkumulation mit Rohstoffabhängigkeit, Bodenerschöpfung und gestörtem Stoffwechsel.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-07","text":"Geschichte erhält die Form selbstuntergrabender Entwicklung: Die Produktionsweise erzeugt ihre Transformationsbedingungen nicht außerhalb, sondern durch die Zuspitzung der Widersprüche ihrer eigenen Produktivkraftentwicklung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-01","text":"Spezialisierung erhöht Produktivität und Materialdurchsatz, steigert den Kapitalbedarf, ermöglicht weitere Arbeitsteilung und erzeugt schließlich den Skalierungsdruck zur maschinellen Überschreitung der Manufaktur.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD1","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-02","text":"Teure Maschinerie erzeugt Nutzungs- und Entwertungsdruck, dieser verlängert den Arbeitstag, gesetzliche Begrenzung erzwingt Intensivierung, und technische Verbesserung setzt den Kreislauf auf höherer Apparatebasis fort.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-03","text":"Technische Verdrängung reproduziert disponible Arbeitskraft; niedrige Löhne können anschließend weitere Maschinisierung verzögern und erzeugen dadurch räumlich und sektoral ungleiche Technisierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D8","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-04","text":"Maschinelle Selbstproduktion beschleunigt Innovation und moralische Entwertung; qualitative technische Veränderung ersetzt Arbeit und verschärft damit den Konkurrenzdruck zu weiterer Innovation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-05","text":"Partielle Regulation verschiebt Ausbeutung in unregulierte Bereiche, erzeugt Verallgemeinerungsdruck und führt über größere Kapitalauslagen zum Untergang kleiner Produzenten und zu weiterer Konzentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:D9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D10","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-06","text":"Elastische Fabrikexpansion erschließt Weltmärkte, zerstört fremde Produktionsformen, erzeugt Überfüllung und Krise und setzt dadurch einen neuen Kostensenkungs- und Expansionszyklus in Gang.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-07","text":"Der verborgene Attraktor ist bewusste kollektive Verfügung: Je vollständiger die Arbeit technisch vergesellschaftet und funktional beweglich wird, desto schärfer tritt das Fehlen gesellschaftlicher Selbstleitung hervor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B01","text":"Gereifte gesellschaftliche Arbeitsteilung + Verkauf vieler Arbeitskräfte an ein Kapital → konzentrierte Kooperation als Ausgangsbedingung des kapitalistischen Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A13","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B02","text":"Zerlegung des Arbeitsprozesses + lebenslange Bindung an eine Teilfunktion + Werkzeugdifferenzierung → spezialisierter Teilarbeiter als menschliches Elementarorgan.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A6","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B03","text":"Komplementäre Teilorgane + kapitalistisches Kommando → gesellschaftlicher Gesamtarbeiter → Erscheinung gemeinsamer Produktivkraft als Kapitalmacht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A17","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B04","text":"Handwerkliche Grundlage + steigender Kontroll- und Skalierungsbedarf → technologische Schranke → Übertragung des operierenden Werkzeugs auf den Mechanismus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B05","text":"Objektive Prozessanalyse + zentral gekoppelte Teilmaschinen → kontinuierlicher Automat → Maschinenproduktion durch Maschinen → selbstrevolutionierende technische Basis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B06","text":"Differenz zwischen Maschinenwert und ersetztem Arbeitskraftwert + steigender konstanter Kapitalanteil → kapitalistische Einsatzselektion + relative Arbeitsverdrängung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B07","text":"Intensivierung + relative Verdrängung + sekundäre Arbeitsnachfrage + Weltmarktabhängigkeit → kein Beschäftigungsgleichgewicht, sondern zyklische Repulsion und Attraktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B08","text":"Soziale Verwüstung → gesetzliche Begrenzung → technische Rekonfiguration → größere Kapitalauslage → Konzentration und erweiterte Herrschaft des Fabrikregimes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B09","text":"Globale Externalisierung auf Arbeitskraft und Natur → Zuspitzung innerer Widersprüche → negative Notwendigkeit bewusster gesellschaftlicher Regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A18","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:AFM-B01","text":"Handwerkliche Kooperation → spezialisierter Teilarbeiter → kapitalistisch beherrschter Gesamtarbeiter → technologische Schranke → Werkzeugübertragung auf den Mechanismus → Automat → maschinelle Selbstproduktion → Unterordnung älterer Produktionsformen → Widerspruch zwischen technischer Beweglichkeit und fixierter Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AF1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AF1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:AFM-B02","text":"Marktlicher Zeitdruck → technische Prozessdisziplin → Verlängerung des Arbeitstags → gesetzliche Begrenzung → Intensivierung → Maschinisierung → Konzentration → erneuter Regulationsbedarf.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:AFM-B03","text":"Industrielle Revolution → Ausdehnung auf verbundene Produktionszweige → Weltmarktexpansion → internationale Arbeitsteilung → Rohstoffabhängigkeit → gestörter Naturstoffwechsel → Notwendigkeit bewusster Synthese.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-01","text":"Der Produzent wird vom selbständigen Warenhersteller zum Organ des Gesamtarbeiters, dann zum Anhängsel des Automaten und schließlich zum austauschbaren Knoten eines erweiterten Fabriknetzes umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-02","text":"Arbeitsteilung zerfällt nicht mehr nur in gesellschaftliche und werkstattinterne Formen, sondern wird als historische Mutation von subjektiver Spezialisierung zu objektiver Prozessanalyse und kapitalistischer Funktionsfixierung kartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME2","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-03","text":"Produktivität verliert den Status neutraler Effizienz und wird in drei inkommensurable Maße aufgespalten: technische Leistungsfähigkeit, gesellschaftliche Arbeitsersparnis und kapitalistische Rentabilität.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-04","text":"Die Beschäftigungsfrage wird von absoluten Arbeiterzahlen auf das Verhältnis zwischen Beschäftigung, Gesamtkapital, technischer Zusammensetzung und Akkumulationsphase umgestellt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-05","text":"Die Fabrik wird von einem lokalen Gebäude zu einem transnationalen Netz aus Maschinenbetrieben, abhängigen Manufakturen, Hausarbeit, Rohstoffgebieten und Absatzmärkten erweitert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-06","text":"Arbeitsgesetzgebung wird zugleich als Schutzform, technischer Innovationszwang und Konzentrationsmechanismus neu kartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-07","text":"Familie und Natur verlassen den Status äußerer oder privater Voraussetzungen und werden als innere Reproduktionsfelder kapitalistischer Produktivkraftentwicklung lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-08","text":"Fortschritt wird als widersprüchliche Einheit gesellschaftlicher Produktivkraftentwicklung, individueller Entmächtigung und Erzeugung eigener Transformationsbedingungen reklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene erscheinen Entstehungsformen der Manufaktur, Maschinenanatomie, Beschäftigungszahlen, Arbeitszeiten, Fabrikformen, Hausarbeit, Gesetzgebung und Agrikultur.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene verbinden sich Kapitalbesitz, proportionierte Kooperation, Wertübertragung, Kapitalzusammensetzung, Familienarbeit, Konkurrenz, Weltmarkt und industrielle Zyklen zu einem einheitlichen Verwertungsmechanismus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene wird der Konflikt von isolierter Technikabwehr und lokaler Missstandskorrektur auf Eigentum, gesellschaftliche Anwendung, allgemeine Regulation, politische Macht und Aufhebung fixierter Arbeitsteilung verschoben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologischen und zeitlichen Ebene erscheint Realität als permanente technologische Umwälzung, in der zeitliche Folge räumlich synchronisiert, vergegenständlichte Arbeit subjektiviert und Geschichte zyklisch sowie transformationsförmig wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologischen und performativen Ebene vollzieht die Argumentform ihre These, indem sie genealogische Entstehung, technische Rekonstruktion und widerspruchslogische Eskalation selbst als fortlaufende Mutation organisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-01","text":"Die Trennung zwischen Maschine und kapitalistischer Anwendung bleibt instabil, weil die Maschine nicht der eigentliche Gegner sein soll, ihre konkrete Gestalt aber bereits unter dem Verwertungszwang entwickelt wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX14","CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-02","text":"Die Kausalanteile allgemeiner Kooperation, spezifischer manufakturmäßiger Arbeitsteilung und Maschinerie an der Produktivitätssteigerung bleiben nicht vollständig separiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D13","CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-03","text":"Fabrikgesetzgebung bleibt strukturell doppeldeutig, weil sie Ausbeutung real begrenzt und zugleich Intensivierung, Konzentration und technisch verdichtete Kapitalherrschaft beschleunigt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-04","text":"Die positive Alternative bleibt unterbestimmt: Kollektive Verfügung, vielseitige Individualität und Arbeitermacht werden als notwendig gesetzt, aber institutionell und politisch nicht vollständig vermittelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-05","text":"Das quantitative Verhältnis von unmittelbarer Verdrängung, sekundärer Beschäftigung und langfristiger Wiederanziehung bleibt offen und begrenzt die empirische Geschlossenheit der Systembehauptung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-01","text":"Das Handwerksgeschick mutiert von der technologischen Grundlage der Manufaktur zur Schranke ihrer Kontrolle und Skalierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A5","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-02","text":"Die spezifische Maschinerie mutiert vom menschlich gegliederten Gesamtarbeiter zum objektiven Maschinenorganismus, der die produktive Subjektposition besetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:NX2","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-03","text":"Arbeitsteilung mutiert von subjektiver Anpassung der Operationen an spezialisierte Arbeiter zur objektiven Prozesszerlegung, während die soziale Fixierung des Arbeiters fortbesteht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-04","text":"Technologische Funktionsbeweglichkeit mutiert von einer Quelle permanenter Entwertung zum materiellen Ausgangspunkt polytechnischer Bildung und vielseitiger Individualität.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-05","text":"Gesetzliche Begrenzung mutiert von einer äußeren Schranke der Arbeitszeit zum internen Innovations-, Maschinisierungs- und Konzentrationsmechanismus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-01","text":"Realität erscheint als selbstrevolutionierender Produktionsorganismus, der Fabriken, abhängige Produktionsformen, Weltmarkt und Naturstoffwechsel in ein ungleiches Maschinennetz integriert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird zunächst zum einseitigen Organ, dann zum beherrschten Anhängsel des objektiven Systems und bleibt zugleich Träger einer technisch erzeugten, gesellschaftlich blockierten Vielseitigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist synchronisiert, kontinuierlich, intensiv formbar und zyklisch; sie erzeugt Beschleunigung und Unsicherheit, ohne die gewonnene Zeit den Produzenten verfügbar zu machen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-04","text":"Möglicher Kampf richtet sich nicht gegen Technik als solche, sondern um ihre gesellschaftliche Anwendung, kollektive Verfügung, Funktionsbeweglichkeit und bewusste Regulation des Stoffwechsels.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B01","text":"Die Clusterarchitektur ist aus sechs Elementen rekonstruierbar: kapitalistischer Mehrwertzweck, Mutation des Produktionsorgans, Aneignung gesellschaftlicher Produktivkraft, relative Arbeitsverdrängung, rekursive Regulation und terminale Untergrabung der Reproduktionsbedingungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT1","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B02","text":"Das System ist kohärent, sofern Kapitalverwertung als gemeinsames Vermittlungsprinzip von Eigentum, Kommando, Technik, Beschäftigung, Regulation und Naturverhältnis festgehalten wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT3","CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B03","text":"Am stärksten ist die Architektur beim endogenen Übergang von der handwerklichen Schranke zur Maschinerie und bei der Unterscheidung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitsersparnis von kapitalistischer Rentabilität und Beschäftigungswirkung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B04","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben das quantitative Nettoverhältnis der Beschäftigungsbewegungen und die positive institutionelle Form kollektiver Verfügung, vielseitiger Arbeit und geregelten Naturstoffwechsels.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B05","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn die Spannung zwischen Technik und Anwendung, die regulatorische Rückkopplung und die Eskalation zur allgemeinen Widerspruchsform nicht in eine lineare Fortschrittserzählung aufgelöst werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B06","text":"Axiomatischer Reduktion widersteht die empirische Reichweite der Totalisierung: Branchenfälle, historische Varianten und quantitative Grenzen bleiben partiell offen, während exemplarische Verdichtung die systemische Verallgemeinerung trägt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT8","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211906278555Z_e573dc9f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 13–15","source_sha256":"c6ce6c1ced5645f4f41f298f389e2623dad8482f510e592b7ca2bd91fd6b22de","sha256":"38a1d8c3af40f6f3935b6df68c2ac52f3578c4492784f1e2a2992f3792ede81c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:19:06.279833+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-01","text":"The central problem is the endogenous transformation of manufacture grounded in craftsmanship into a mechanized production system whose technical saving of labor, under capitalist conditions, produces valorization, domination, and comprehensive reorganization of the forms of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-02","text":"The global thesis is that socially produced productive power becomes effective only through capitalist disposal and therefore confronts the producers as an alien power, while its costs are shifted onto labor-power, family, society, and nature.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-03","text":"The directed movement leads from the humanly articulated collective worker through the objective machinery organism to the social and ecological totalization of the factory principle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-04","text":"At the cluster level, the argument becomes a genealogical, causal, and contradiction-logical reconstruction in which each form of production brings forth the conditions of its own transcendence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-05","text":"Manufacture produces specialized tools and pressures toward scale that burst its artisanal foundation; mechanized production removes this barrier, technically reproduces itself, and subordinates older forms of production as dependent departments.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A8","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-06","text":"The movement is cumulative, mutation-driven, and recursive: temporal succession is synchronized, technical self-reproduction accelerates upheaval, and market-mediated expansion returns cyclically as crisis and renewed pressure toward rationalization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ASP-07","text":"The closure remains negative: regulation can limit individual destructions but cannot establish final stability; the process ends in the undermining of its human and natural prerequisites as well as in the indeterminate necessity of conscious social disposal.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Capitalist development of productive power is directed toward shortening necessary labor in favor of surplus labor and is selected through surplus-value production, cheapening of commodities, and competition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Social cooperation, knowledge, and forces of nature appear to the producers as productive powers of capital because property and command appropriate their common efficacy.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A17","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The productive organ mutates from the specialized human member of the collective worker into the objective machinery organism that confronts the worker as an autonomous subject.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Division of labor changes from the empirical subdivision of artisanal activities to the scientific-technical analysis of the production process, without automatically abolishing the capitalist fixation of the worker upon partial functions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:NX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The increase of social productive power is produced through the loss of autonomy and devaluation of individual productive capacity, although it simultaneously brings forth the material possibility of versatile individuality.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Social labor-saving and capitalist profitability constitute different measures of selection; capital can therefore reject more productive technology if paid labor-power remains cheaper.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Machinery transforms variable into constant capital and produces relative displacement of labor, which remains compatible with an absolute increase in employment during phases of quantitative accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A18","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Workshop despotism expands into factory discipline and finally into an international production network, while its external mediation remains anarchic, shaped by competition, and cyclical.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D14","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Market-imposed time pressure first becomes the technical law of coupled partial processes and then the pressure of valorization upon the service life, speed, and labor density of the machinery system.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A14","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Legal limitation does not end the compulsion of valorization, but shifts it into technical intensification, mechanization, concentration, and renewed regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Through its own pressures of productivity and scale, every developed form of production produces the technical foundation of its transcendence and thereby accelerates the ongoing devaluation of existing means of production and capacities.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Capitalist development of productive power culminates in the simultaneous undermining of labor-power and soil, that is, of its two material conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","text":"[Attractor] The displaced counter-form consists in collective disposal over the socialized production organism, changing functions, polytechnical education, and conscious regulation of social metabolism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-01","text":"Artisanal skill initially remains the technological foundation, then mutates into a barrier to control and scale, and disappears as a regulating principle once machines are produced by machines.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A5","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-02","text":"The tool returns in functionally altered form: first it extends the specialized partial worker, then its operative function is detached from the human organism and transferred to the mechanism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-03","text":"The collective worker mutates from the articulated collective of human organs into the objective production organism; its socialization persists, while its unity is shifted by capital into the apparatus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A9","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-04","text":"Division of labor changes its function from the subjective specialization of workers to objective process analysis and ultimately appears as a conflict between technological functional mobility and capitalist fixation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-05","text":"Time mutates from the succession of artisanal operations through synchronous coupling to the intensive condensation of machine labor-time and to the cyclical time of the world market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-06","text":"The unity of internal planning and external anarchy persists, but expands its scope from the individual workshop through factory organization and the labor market to the international division of labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD3","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-07","text":"Regulation partially reverses its initially limiting valence: the barrier to extensive exploitation catalyzes intensive exploitation and technically concentrated capitalist domination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RMD-08","text":"The whole worker first disappears as a real figure of production and returns, at a higher level, as the blocked possibility of versatile individuality.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-01","text":"The combination of different crafts and the subdivision of a homogeneous craft remain local variants of emergence; at the cluster level, what counts is their convergence in the figure of the dependent partial worker.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A3","CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-02","text":"The distinction between heterogeneous and organic manufacture remains a local typology of products; what scales upward is only the transformation of temporal succession into synchronized and proportioned dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A9","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-03","text":"The tripartite anatomy of developed machinery remains a technical determination of the lower level; what bears the cluster is the transfer of the operative function from the worker to the mechanism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-04","text":"The partial transfer of value by the machine remains a local mechanism of value; it scales to the global distinction between technical productivity, social labor-saving, and the capitalist limit of deployment.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-05","text":"Women's and children's labor are not merely particular factory cases; at the cluster level, they show the incorporation of the family and supposed private sphere into the architecture of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-06","text":"Individual new branches of production and employment figures remain local appearances; what scales upward is the relation of relative decline of labor, conditional re-attraction, and cyclical employment insecurity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:NX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:CGD-07","text":"Capitalist agriculture appears locally as a final object-domain, but at the cluster level becomes the terminal generalization of a system that externalizes its reproduction costs onto labor-power and nature.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:A17","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-01","text":"Excluded is a neutral concept of division of labor or technology that separates property, command, and the form of valorization from their effects.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-02","text":"Excluded is the independent individual producer or small enterprise as an enduring counter-model to the capitalist organization of social labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-03","text":"Excluded is the alignment of productivity increase, development of individual capacities, and improvement of the producers' condition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX3","CH_V4GB_4MUG:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-04","text":"Excluded is an automatic compensatory mechanism that necessarily and simultaneously transfers displaced workers into newly created employment.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX15","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-05","text":"Excluded is the assumption that contractual equality, competition, and individual self-interest produce sufficient humane limits to valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:DNX5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-06","text":"Excluded is a final regulatory closure, because every limitation can simultaneously bring forth intensification, technical adaptation, or concentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:GNX-07","text":"Excluded is an automatic liberation from division of labor through the technological abolition of artisanal specialization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-01","text":"For the system to persist, the notion that capital is merely an external property relation must be false; it must technically organize the social labor-body and embody it as a property of its own apparatus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:DNX6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-02","text":"The naturalization of permanent occupational specialization must be false, because permanent technological mobility historically produces and continually devalues the fixed labor function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-03","text":"The assumption that personal means of production, spatial dispersion, or small property constitute a stable outside of capital must be false.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:NX11","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-04","text":"The treatment of family destruction, wear of labor-power, and devastation of nature as accidental side effects must be false; they constitute systematic cost-shifting within a unified architecture of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:DBN-05","text":"Both technological determinism and the pure externality of social form are disqualified: effects cannot be derived from technology alone, yet concrete technology itself arises under the compulsion of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:DNX7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is a collective producer that itself owns, directs, and disposes over objectively socialized productive power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-02","text":"Technically possible free time remains inaccessible as social reality because labor-saving turns into additional time at the disposal of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-03","text":"Unavailable is a reconciliation of permanent technological revolution with durably secured labor and full human development; versatility exists only as a produced but blocked possibility.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSA-04","text":"The positive counter-form of conscious regulation of production, changing labor, education, family, and natural metabolism remains institutionally indeterminate and therefore operates only as a negative attractor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-01","text":"The contradiction of manufacture endogenously produces machinery: the artisanal foundation supplies specialized tools, but becomes a barrier and compels the transfer of the operative function to the mechanism. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","CL_V4GB_05:GA-11","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-02","text":"The socialization of labor intensifies into an ontological inversion: with the displacement of its unity into the machinery organism, the collective worker loses the possibility of appearing as an autonomous collective subject. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-02","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-03","text":"Market time becomes the technical law of coupling in manufacture and, in large-scale industry, becomes pressure upon machine utilization, speed, and labor density. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-09","CH_V4GB_3TDA:D5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A14","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-04","text":"The cheapening and simplification of labor-power expands, through family labor, technical displacement, and cyclical insecurity, into the reproduction of an available working population. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A16","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-05","text":"The connection of intra-enterprise planning with social anarchy totalizes itself as a global factory network whose international division of labor is destabilized by industrial cycles. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-08","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-06","text":"Labor legislation is at once counter-power and a pressure toward modernization: it limits extensive exploitation, drives intensive exploitation, and accelerates the downfall of small producers. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-07","text":"The objective mobility of technical functions sharpens the contradiction with the capitalist fixation of the worker and thereby produces the necessity of polytechnical education and versatile development. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-04","CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:XD-08","text":"The unity of progress and exploitation expands from the impoverishment of individual productive capacity to the simultaneous exhaustion of labor-power and soil. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD8","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-01","text":"The productive subject is neither the individual worker nor the autonomous collective, but a unity organized by capital that migrates from the human collective worker into the machinery organism and makes the producer an interchangeable bearer of functions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-02","text":"Reality splits into socially possible productivity and capitalistically actualized profitability; technical superiority therefore guarantees neither deployment nor social rationality.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-03","text":"The dominant form of time combines synchronization, continuous acceleration, intensive condensation, and industrial cycles, while technically possible free time remains socially blocked.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes recursive: technical barriers, legal limits, and social resistances do not interrupt valorization, but are translated into new organizational and innovation pressures.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-05","text":"Politics appears neither as an external corrective mechanism nor as a final solution, but as an immanent field in which protection, generalization of regulation, and technically concentrated domination interlock.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D15","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-06","text":"Spatial expansion universalizes the inner asymmetry of the factory system as an international division of labor and connects industrial accumulation with dependence on raw materials, soil exhaustion, and disturbed metabolism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:BSD-07","text":"History assumes the form of self-undermining development: the mode of production generates its conditions of transformation not externally, but through the sharpening of the contradictions of its own development of productive power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-01","text":"Specialization increases productivity and material throughput, raises the capital requirement, enables further division of labor, and finally generates the pressure of scale toward the mechanized transcendence of manufacture.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD1","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-02","text":"Expensive machinery produces pressure for utilization and against devaluation; this extends the working day, legal limitation compels intensification, and technical improvement continues the cycle on a higher apparatus basis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-03","text":"Technical displacement reproduces available labor-power; low wages can subsequently delay further mechanization and thereby produce spatially and sectorally uneven technologization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:D8","CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-04","text":"Machine self-production accelerates innovation and moral depreciation; qualitative technical change replaces labor and thereby intensifies competitive pressure toward further innovation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-05","text":"Partial regulation shifts exploitation into unregulated areas, produces pressure toward generalization, and leads, through larger capital outlays, to the downfall of small producers and further concentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:D9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D10","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-06","text":"Elastic factory expansion opens world markets, destroys foreign forms of production, produces overfilling and crisis, and thereby initiates a new cycle of cost reduction and expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:RLE-07","text":"The hidden attractor is conscious collective disposal: the more completely labor becomes technically socialized and functionally mobile, the more sharply the absence of social self-direction emerges.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SNX2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B01","text":"Mature social division of labor + sale of many labor-powers to one capital → concentrated cooperation as the initial condition of the capitalist collective worker.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A13","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B02","text":"Subdivision of the labor process + lifelong attachment to a partial function + differentiation of tools → specialized partial worker as human elementary organ.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A6","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B03","text":"Complementary partial organs + capitalist command → social collective worker → appearance of common productive power as capital power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A17","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B04","text":"Artisanal foundation + rising need for control and scale → technological barrier → transfer of the operative tool to the mechanism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B05","text":"Objective process analysis + centrally coupled partial machines → continuous automaton → machine production by machines → self-revolutionizing technical basis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B06","text":"Difference between machine value and replaced labor-power value + rising share of constant capital → capitalist selection of deployment + relative displacement of labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B07","text":"Intensification + relative displacement + secondary labor demand + dependence on the world market → no employment equilibrium, but cyclical repulsion and attraction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B08","text":"Social devastation → legal limitation → technical reconfiguration → larger capital outlay → concentration and expanded domination of the factory regime.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FGS-B09","text":"Global externalization onto labor-power and nature → sharpening of internal contradictions → negative necessity of conscious social regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A18","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:AFM-B01","text":"Artisanal cooperation → specialized partial worker → capitalistically dominated collective worker → technological barrier → transfer of the tool to the mechanism → automaton → machine self-production → subordination of older forms of production → contradiction between technical mobility and fixed labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AF1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AF1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:AFM-B02","text":"Market time pressure → technical process discipline → extension of the working day → legal limitation → intensification → mechanization → concentration → renewed need for regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:D12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:AFM-B03","text":"Industrial revolution → expansion into connected branches of production → world-market expansion → international division of labor → dependence on raw materials → disturbed natural metabolism → necessity of conscious synthesis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-01","text":"The producer is reclassified from an independent commodity producer to an organ of the collective worker, then to an appendage of the automaton, and finally to an interchangeable node of an expanded factory network.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-02","text":"Division of labor is no longer divided merely into social and workshop-internal forms, but is mapped as a historical mutation from subjective specialization to objective process analysis and capitalist fixation of functions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME2","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-03","text":"Productivity loses the status of neutral efficiency and is split into three incommensurable measures: technical performance, social labor-saving, and capitalist profitability.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME5","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-04","text":"The question of employment is shifted from absolute numbers of workers to the relation among employment, total capital, technical composition, and phase of accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-05","text":"The factory is expanded from a local building into a transnational network of machine-operated enterprises, dependent manufactures, domestic labor, raw-material regions, and sales markets.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-06","text":"Labor legislation is remapped simultaneously as a form of protection, a technical pressure toward innovation, and a mechanism of concentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-07","text":"Family and nature leave the status of external or private prerequisites and become legible as internal fields of reproduction of capitalist development of productive power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MME-08","text":"Progress is reclassified as the contradictory unity of social development of productive power, individual disempowerment, and the production of its own conditions of transformation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level appear forms of the emergence of manufacture, machine anatomy, employment figures, working hours, factory forms, domestic labor, legislation, and agriculture.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT1","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, capital ownership, proportioned cooperation, value transfer, capital composition, family labor, competition, the world market, and industrial cycles combine into a unified mechanism of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the conflict is shifted from isolated resistance to technology and local correction of abuses to property, social application, general regulation, political power, and the abolition of fixed division of labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality appears as permanent technological upheaval, in which temporal succession is spatially synchronized, objectified labor is subjectivized, and history becomes cyclical as well as transformative.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4MUG:ALT4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the form of argument enacts its thesis by itself organizing genealogical emergence, technical reconstruction, and contradiction-logical escalation as ongoing mutation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:AS7","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-01","text":"The separation between machine and capitalist application remains unstable because the machine is not supposed to be the actual adversary, yet its concrete form is already developed under the compulsion of valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX14","CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-02","text":"The causal shares of general cooperation, specific manufacturing division of labor, and machinery in the increase of productivity remain not fully separated.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:D13","CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-03","text":"Factory legislation remains structurally ambiguous because it genuinely limits exploitation while simultaneously accelerating intensification, concentration, and technically condensed capitalist domination.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-04","text":"The positive alternative remains underdetermined: collective disposal, versatile individuality, and workers' power are posited as necessary, but are not fully institutionally and politically mediated.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:FL-05","text":"The quantitative relation between immediate displacement, secondary employment, and long-term re-attraction remains open and limits the empirical closure of the system claim.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-01","text":"Artisanal skill mutates from the technological foundation of manufacture into the barrier to its control and scale.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A5","CH_V4GB_3TDA:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-02","text":"Specific machinery mutates from the humanly articulated collective worker into the objective machinery organism that occupies the productive subject-position.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:NX2","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-03","text":"Division of labor mutates from the subjective adaptation of operations to specialized workers into objective subdivision of the process, while the social fixation of the worker persists.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX7","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-04","text":"Technological functional mobility mutates from a source of permanent devaluation into the material point of departure for polytechnical education and versatile individuality.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:AS6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MP-05","text":"Legal limitation mutates from an external barrier to working time into an internal mechanism of innovation, mechanization, and concentration.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:NX12","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a self-revolutionizing production organism that integrates factories, dependent forms of production, the world market, and natural metabolism into an unequal machinery network.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:A9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:ME2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-02","text":"The subject first becomes a one-sided organ, then the dominated appendage of the objective system, and simultaneously remains the bearer of a technically produced, socially blocked versatility.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A6","CH_V4GB_4MUG:AS6","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is synchronized, continuous, intensively malleable, and cyclical; it produces acceleration and insecurity without making the time gained available to the producers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:A10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:A16","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:HSI-04","text":"Possible struggle is directed not against technology as such, but around its social application, collective disposal, functional mobility, and conscious regulation of metabolism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:ME9","CH_V4GB_4M_2:SNX3","CH_V4GB_4M_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B01","text":"The cluster architecture is reconstructible from six elements: capitalist purpose of surplus value, mutation of the production organ, appropriation of social productive power, relative displacement of labor, recursive regulation, and terminal undermining of the conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT1","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT1","CH_V4GB_3TDA:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B02","text":"The system is coherent insofar as capital valorization is retained as the common mediating principle of property, command, technology, employment, regulation, and relation to nature.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT3","CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B03","text":"The architecture is strongest in the endogenous transition from the artisanal barrier to machinery and in the distinction of social labor-saving from capitalist profitability and employment effect.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT10","CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT4","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B04","text":"What remains underdetermined is the quantitative net relation of employment movements and the positive institutional form of collective disposal, versatile labor, and regulated natural metabolism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if the tension between technology and application, the regulatory feedback, and the escalation toward the general form of contradiction are not dissolved into a linear narrative of progress.","refs":["CH_V4GB_4MUG:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT5","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B06","text":"The empirical scope of totalization resists axiomatic reduction: sectoral cases, historical variants, and quantitative limits remain partially open, while exemplary condensation sustains systemic generalization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3TDA:MRT2","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT8","CH_V4GB_4M_2:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_05@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_05:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 13–15","context":"3) Theilung der Arbeit und Manufaktur. · 4) Maschinerie und grosse Industrie. · reading part 1/2 · 4) Maschinerie und grosse Industrie. · reading part 2/2"}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 16–18","order":6,"parents":["CH_V4GB_FNKW","CH_V4GB_SKDA","CH_V4GB_EINR"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_06@R001","sha256":"77d2dfc1705cf74daac2b15f81d9d289a2d13e8269aaac5776965821bd8214be","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-01","text":"Der isolierte Produktions- oder Austauschakt kann nicht erklären, wie Kapital seine Verwertungsbedingungen über mehrere Perioden hinweg reproduziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-02","text":"Die tragende Bewegung verbindet die Erzeugung unbezahlter Mehrarbeit mit ihrer Realisierung und mit der erneuten Hervorbringung der Trennung, die ihre Aneignung ermöglicht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_EINR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-03","text":"Produktion, Zirkulation und Reproduktion bilden eine asymmetrische Einheit: Die Produktion erzeugt den Mehrwert, die Zirkulation realisiert ihn, und die Reproduktion erneuert seine sozialen Voraussetzungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A12","CH_V4GB_EINR:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-04","text":"Lohn-, Einkommens- und Vertragsformen zerlegen das Kapitalverhältnis in scheinbar selbstständige Transaktionen, obwohl sie dieselbe Aneignungs- und Reproduktionsbewegung vermitteln.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-05","text":"Die gerichtete Bewegung führt von der funktionalen Bestimmung produktiver Arbeit über Subsumtion und Mehrwertproduktion zur Realisierung und schließlich zur rekursiven Reproduktion der Klassenpole.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:AS3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-06","text":"Der Maßstab wechselt von Länge, Intensität und Produktivität des einzelnen Arbeitstags zur kumulierten Zeit gesellschaftlicher Klassenreproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:AS5","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-07","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv und kumulativ: Wiederholung auf gleicher Produktionsskala bewahrt Größen, verändert aber Wertprovenienz und soziale Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-08","text":"Die Schließung besteht in der Reproduktion von Kapitalist und Lohnarbeiter als komplementären Polen; konkrete Zirkulationsformen und die historische Genesis ihrer ursprünglichen Trennung bleiben aufgeschoben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:D12","CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Mehrwert beruht auf angeeigneter unbezahlter Arbeit; weder seine Realisierung noch seine spätere Aufspaltung verändert diese Substanz.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Die Lohnform verwandelt den Wert der Arbeitskraft in den Schein bezahlter Arbeit und vertieft sich in der Reproduktion zur Verdeckung eines von der Arbeiterklasse selbst erzeugten Lohnfonds.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A17","CH_V4GB_EINR:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Akkumulation verlangt die Realisierung des in der Ware enthaltenen Mehrwerts und seine Rückverwandlung in Kapital, ohne dass die Zirkulation dadurch zur Quelle des Mehrwerts wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Die Verteilung des Mehrwerts auf selbstständige Eigentums- und Einkommensformen verändert seine Erscheinung, nicht seine gemeinsame Produktionsgrundlage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A8","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Die Trennung der Arbeitskraft von ihren objektiven Bedingungen ist zugleich Voraussetzung und fortlaufend erzeugtes Resultat des kapitalistischen Prozesses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A12","CH_V4GB_EINR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Zeitliche Kontinuität löst die Selbstständigkeit des einzelnen Austauschakts und die dauerhafte Wertidentität des ursprünglichen Kapitalvorschusses auf.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A5","CH_V4GB_EINR:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Reelle Subsumtion verlagert die Herrschaft des Kapitals von äußerem Kommando in Technik und Organisation und erweitert sich auf der Reproduktionsebene zur funktionalen Einbeziehung der Arbeiterexistenz.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Rechtliche Äquivalenz, Vertragsfreiheit und ökonomische Ausbeutung sind vereinbar, weil formale Selbstständigkeit die materielle Trennung nicht aufhebt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD2","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Der kapitalistische Prozess erzeugt nicht nur Waren und Mehrwert, sondern reproduziert Kapitalist, Lohnarbeiter und ihr Verhältnis als seine gesellschaftliche Gesamtausgabe.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8","CH_V4GB_EINR:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Die genetische Erklärung verlangt kontrollierte Abstraktion und anschließenden Maßstabswechsel von Erscheinungsformen zu Produktionsquelle, Vermittlung und Klassenreproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-01","text":"Unbezahlte Arbeit bewahrt stabile Identität: Sie erscheint nacheinander als Substanz des Mehrwerts, gemeinsame Grundlage seiner Teilformen und materieller Kern des reproduzierten Kapitals.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-02","text":"Produktive Arbeit mutiert von einer gesellschaftlichen Verwertungsfunktion innerhalb des Gesamtarbeiters zur Quelle des Werts, dessen fortlaufender Ersatz das Kapitalverhältnis reproduziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D1","CH_V4GB_EINR:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-03","text":"Subsumtion erweitert ihren Geltungsbereich: Technische Reorganisation des Arbeitsprozesses wird zur rekursiven Organisation der sozialen Bedingungen, unter denen Arbeitskraft erneut verkauft werden muss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-04","text":"Die Lohninversion vertieft sich von der scheinbaren Bezahlung der gesamten Arbeit zur Vorstellung, der Kapitalist schieße einen unabhängig von den Arbeitern bestehenden Arbeitsfonds vor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_EINR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-05","text":"Zirkulation wird zunächst aus der Grundanalyse verdrängt, kehrt aber als notwendige Realisierungsvermittlung und als Klassenbewegung des Lohnrückflusses zurück.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A12","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-06","text":"Akkumulation mutiert an der Grenze zur einfachen Reproduktion: Rückverwandlung erweitert Kapital, während vollständige Mehrwertkonsumtion die Skala konstant hält, aber dennoch Wertprovenienz und Klassenverhältnis transformiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-07","text":"Freiheit erfährt eine Valenzumkehr: Äquivalenter Einzelvertrag und Arbeitgeberwechsel widerlegen Abhängigkeit nicht, sondern werden zu ihren wiederkehrenden Vermittlungsformen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD2","CH_V4GB_EINR:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-01","text":"Die quantitative Matrix aus Arbeitsdauer, Intensität und Produktivität bleibt ein lokales Instrument zur Bestimmung von Wertbewegungen; auf Clusterebene wird sie dem Reproduktionsmechanismus der Mehrarbeit untergeordnet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-02","text":"Zeitlohn, Stücklohn und Weltmarktvergleich bleiben besondere Kontroll- und Vergleichsformen; nach oben skaliert allein ihre gemeinsame Funktion, Extraktion zu messen, zu individualisieren und zu verdecken.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ME8","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-03","text":"Profit, Zins, Handelsgewinn und Grundrente bleiben auf dieser Ebene aufgeschobene Verteilungsformen und tragen nur insofern global, als ihre gemeinsame Herkunft erhalten bleibt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:NX6","CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-04","text":"Zur Clusterarchitektur skaliert die Verbindung von unbezahlter Arbeit, Realisierung und Rückverwandlung beziehungsweise Reproduktion, weil erst sie den vollständigen Kreislauf des Kapitalverhältnisses bestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT5","CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-05","text":"Der erste Aneigner und der ursprüngliche Kapitalvorschuss verlieren ihre globale Erklärungsfunktion; sie werden in Klassenverteilung und kumulierte Reproduktionszeit absorbiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A5","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-06","text":"Die individuelle Konsumtion der Arbeiter steigt von einem lokalen Reproduktionsmoment zur vermittelnden Struktur auf, durch die Arbeitskraft und Kapitalverhältnis gleichzeitig erneuert werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:D9","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-01","text":"Natürliche Fruchtbarkeit oder technische Produktivität darf nicht als selbsttätige Ursache von Mehrwert gelten; sie eröffnet nur disponible Zeit, deren Aneignung gesellschaftlich organisiert wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-02","text":"Der Arbeiter verkauft weder bereits geleistete Arbeit noch erhält er im Lohn deren vollständigen Wert; Gegenstand des Tauschs ist die Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:NX6","CH_V4GB_FNKW:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-03","text":"Zirkulation kann Mehrwert realisieren und verteilen, aber nicht seine ursprüngliche Quelle bilden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-04","text":"Selbstständige Revenue- und Eigentumsformen dürfen nicht als voneinander unabhängige Quellen des Mehrwerts behandelt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-05","text":"Formale Marktfreiheit darf weder materielle Selbstverfügung noch die Abwesenheit ökonomischer Abhängigkeit verbürgen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-06","text":"Einfache Reproduktion darf nicht als folgenlose Wiederholung oder historische Stillstellung gelesen werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:NX2","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-01","text":"Das System kann Erscheinungsformen wie Lohn, Geldvorschuss, Einzelvertrag und Einkommensanteil nicht als letzte Erklärungsebene zulassen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:DNX7","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-02","text":"Gegenwärtiges Kapitaleigentum darf nicht dauerhaft aus einem ursprünglichen Erwerbsakt legitimiert werden, weil reproduktiver Wertersatz dessen Identität auflöst.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-03","text":"Kapitalistische Reproduktion ist ohne die fortdauernde Trennung von Arbeitskraft und Arbeitsbedingungen undenkbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-04","text":"Die private Konsumtionssphäre kann keine vollständig autonome Außenseite des Kapitals bilden, sofern sie die erneute Verkaufsfähigkeit der Arbeitskraft erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-05","text":"Weder unmittelbare Produktion noch Zirkulation kann für sich allein das Gesamtsystem erklären; ihre Trennung ist methodisch notwendig, ihre endgültige Verselbstständigung jedoch unzulässig.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-01","text":"Eine automatische Verwandlung von Produktivitätsgewinn in allgemeine freie Zeit oder gesellschaftliche Emanzipation bleibt ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SNX3","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-02","text":"Der reproduzierte Prozess enthält keinen immanenten Mechanismus, der die Trennung von Produzenten und Produktionsbedingungen aus eigenem Vollzug aufhebt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-03","text":"Eine vollständig transparente Erscheinungsform, in der unbezahlte Arbeit, gemeinsame Mehrwertquelle und Klassenrekursion unmittelbar sichtbar würden, ist strukturell nicht verfügbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SNX1","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-04","text":"Die Deckung von rechtlicher Personfreiheit und materieller Selbstverfügung bildet die zentrale nicht verfügbare Möglichkeit, um welche die Architektur organisiert ist.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-01","text":"Weil die Lohnform die gesamte Arbeit als bezahlt erscheinen lässt, während die Arbeiterklasse den Fonds ihrer eigenen Entlohnung vorher erzeugt, ist der Lohn zugleich Äquivalenzform und Rückfluss bereits angeeigneten Werts; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_06:GA-02","CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_EINR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-02","text":"Die notwendige Realisierung des Mehrwerts begründet eine Einheit von Produktion und Zirkulation, deren Asymmetrie darin liegt, dass allein die Produktion den zu realisierenden unbezahlten Wert erzeugt; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_06:GA-03","CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:D1","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-03","text":"Reelle Subsumtion und Klassenreproduktion bilden zwei Reichweiten derselben Herrschaftsbewegung: Die erste reorganisiert den Arbeitsprozess, die zweite erneuert dessen verfügbare Träger; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-04","text":"Kapitalistische Reproduktion ist nicht mit quantitativer Akkumulation identisch: Selbst bei vollständiger Konsumtion des Mehrwerts und gleichbleibender Skala verändern sich Wertprovenienz und soziale Voraussetzungen; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-06","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-05","text":"Die Aufspaltung des Mehrwerts pluralisiert seine Eigentümer, während die Reproduktion Kapitalist und Lohnarbeiter erneut als einheitliche Klassenpole hervorbringt; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-04","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-06","text":"Äquivalenter Tausch und wiederholter freier Vertrag stabilisieren die Ausbeutungsrelation, weil sie deren einzelne Vollzüge legitimieren und zugleich deren Klassenkontinuität verdecken; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-02","CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD2","CH_V4GB_EINR:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-07","text":"Produktivitätsgewinne und Arbeiterkonsumtion erhalten erst durch das fortbestehende Trennungsverhältnis ihre kapitalistische Funktion: Die einen erweitern aneigenbare Zeit, die andere erneuert verkäufliche Arbeitskraft; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD3","CH_V4GB_EINR:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-01","text":"Kapital erhält auf dieser Ebene den ontologischen Status eines selbstreproduzierenden gesellschaftlichen Verhältnisses, das lebendige Arbeit in eine fremde objektive Macht verwandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD8","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-02","text":"Kapitalistische Zeit ist zugleich zyklisch und kumulativ: Jeder Zyklus erneuert die Produktionsskala, während die Folge der Zyklen Herkunft, Abhängigkeit und Klassenposition transformiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-03","text":"Kausalität wird rekursiv: Die Trennung erzwingt den Verkauf der Arbeitskraft, dessen Resultat die Bedingungen erzeugt, unter denen derselbe Verkauf erneut notwendig wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:D7","CH_V4GB_EINR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-04","text":"Das Subjekt spaltet sich in den rechtlich freien Träger der Arbeitskraft und das funktional reproduzierte Mittel des Kapitals; der Kapitalist erscheint entsprechend als Repräsentant einer Verwertungs- und Verteilungsfunktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME7","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-05","text":"Erkenntnis verlangt eine doppelte Operation: Vermittlungen werden zunächst abstrahiert, um die genetische Grundform freizulegen, und anschließend durch Klassen- und Zeitmaßstab wieder eingeführt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-06","text":"Eine nichtkapitalistische Zeitordnung müsste die Verteilung notwendiger Arbeit und die Verfügung über ihre Produktivitätsgewinne verändern; der rekonstruierte Mechanismus erzeugt diesen Übergang jedoch nicht selbst.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD7","CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-01","text":"Die zentrale Klassenrekursion lautet: Trennung von Arbeitskraft und Arbeitsbedingungen, Verkauf der Arbeitskraft, Erzeugung eines fremden Produkts, Konsumtion des Lohns und erneute Verkaufsnotwendigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A12","CH_V4GB_EINR:A13","CH_V4GB_EINR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-02","text":"Die Extraktionseskalation verläuft von steigender Produktivität über erweiterte Mehrarbeitszeit zu technischer Kontrolle, Leistungsmetrik und Konkurrenz, die den erhöhten Extraktionsgrad normalisieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD3","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-03","text":"Der realisierte Mehrwert besitzt eine Verzweigung: Seine Rückverwandlung erweitert Kapital, seine vollständige Konsumtion erhält die Skala; beide Pfade setzen jedoch die Erneuerung des Kapitalverhältnisses voraus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-04","text":"Die Verdeckung eskaliert von der Lohnform über selbstständige Revenueformen zum freien Einzelvertrag; jede zusätzliche Vermittlung erhöht die Entfernung zwischen Erscheinung und gemeinsamer Quelle.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-05","text":"Der begriffliche Attraktor ist das Kapitalverhältnis selbst: verstreute Analysen von Arbeitstag, Lohn, Realisierung, Konsumtion und Eigentum konvergieren auf seine rekursive Selbsterhaltung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B01","text":"Ausgangsbedingung: Arbeitskraft ist von Produktionsmitteln und Produkt getrennt und muss daher als Ware auftreten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B02","text":"Produktionsoperation: Kauf der Arbeitskraft, formelle oder reelle Subsumtion und Überschreitung notwendiger Arbeitszeit erzeugen unbezahlten Mehrwert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A5","CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B03","text":"Formoperation: Lohn und verselbstständigte Einkommensformen übersetzen die gemeinsame Mehrwertquelle in scheinbar selbstständige Preise und Ansprüche.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A17","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B04","text":"Vermittlungsoperation: Verkauf realisiert den Mehrwert; Rückverwandlung führt zur Akkumulation, vollständige Konsumtion zur einfachen Reproduktion auf gleichbleibender Skala.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B05","text":"Rekursionsoperation: Arbeiterkonsumtion reproduziert Arbeitskraft bei fortbestehender Trennung, während der Produktionszyklus Kapital und Klassenpole erneuert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A14","CH_V4GB_EINR:A15","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B06","text":"Erkenntnisoperation: Abstraktion isoliert die genetische Grundform; zeitliche und gesellschaftliche Reintegration rekonstruiert ihre verdeckten Vermittlungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AFM-B01","text":"Funktionale Bestimmung produktiver Arbeit → Subsumtion des Arbeitsprozesses → unbezahlte Mehrarbeit → Lohninversion → Realisierung des Mehrwerts → Verzweigung in Akkumulation oder einfache Reproduktion → erneuerte Trennung → reproduziertes Kapitalverhältnis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:AS7","CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AFM-B02","text":"Erscheinungsform → kontrollierte Abstraktion → genetische Produktionsquelle → Wiedereinführung der Zirkulationsvermittlung → zeitliche Aggregation → Klassenrekursion → systemische Schließung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-01","text":"Produktivität wird von einer neutralen Quelle gesellschaftlichen Wohlstands zu einer technisch eröffneten Zeitreserve umkartiert, deren Verwendung durch das Kapitalverhältnis bestimmt wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ME3","CH_V4GB_FNKW:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-02","text":"Der Gegensatz von Produktion und Zirkulation zerfällt: Beide sind notwendig, aber nicht symmetrisch, weil die eine Mehrwert erzeugt und die andere ihn realisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-03","text":"Lohn und Kapitaleigentum werden von selbstständigen Ansprüchen auf fremden Wert zu zeitlich vermittelten Formen eines von der Arbeiterklasse erzeugten Reproduktionszusammenhangs umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME2","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-04","text":"Der Gegensatz von Wiederholung und Veränderung bricht zusammen: Gleichbleibende Produktionsgröße kann mit kumulativer Transformation der Wertprovenienz einhergehen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME4","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-05","text":"Der Outputbegriff erweitert sich von Waren und Mehrwert auf reproduzierte Arbeitskraft, Kapital, Klassenpositionen und das Verhältnis zwischen ihnen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME9","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B01","text":"Auf dem Surface level erscheinen Lohnhöhe, Arbeitsdauer, Stückzahl, Warenverkauf, Geldrückfluss und gleichbleibende Produktionsskala als getrennte Vorgänge.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT1","CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B02","text":"Auf dem Structural level verbinden unbezahlte Arbeit, Subsumtion, Realisierung, fortbestehende Trennung und Arbeitskraftreproduktion diese Vorgänge zu einem Klassenmechanismus.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT2","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B03","text":"Auf dem Metastrategic level ersetzt der Wechsel von Einzelakt zu Klassenkontinuität die Erklärung durch Marktformen durch eine Rekonstruktion ihrer Produktions- und Reproduktionsbedingungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B04","text":"Auf dem Ontological / Temporal level sind soziale Identitäten keine statischen Träger, sondern rekursiv erzeugte Positionen innerhalb einer Zeit, die notwendige, unbezahlte und reproduktive Arbeit verschränkt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT4","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B05","text":"Auf dem Methodological / Performative level vollzieht die Darstellung ihre These, indem sie abstrahiert, ausgeschlossene Vermittlungen zurückführt und durch Maßstabswechsel scheinbar selbstständige Formen in einen Prozess auflöst.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-01","text":"Akkumulation setzt Zirkulation voraus, während ihre reine Analyse Zirkulation ausklammert; die Kohärenz hängt daher am vorläufigen Charakter dieser Abstraktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-02","text":"Die Gleichsetzung des produzierenden Kapitalisten mit dem gesamten Mehrwerteigentümer kollidiert mit seiner Bestimmung als bloß erstem Aneigner, bleibt aber als methodische Kompression produktiv.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-03","text":"Die Arbeiterkonsumtion schwankt zwischen notwendiger Reproduktion der Arbeitskraft und umfassender funktionaler Vereinnahmung einer Lebenssphäre, die das Kapital nicht vollständig kontrolliert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-04","text":"Juristische Nicht-Eigentümerschaft und funktionale Bindung dürfen weder identifiziert noch getrennt werden; ihre Spannung trägt die Bestimmung des freien und zugleich abhängigen Lohnarbeiters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MP-01","text":"Der Begriff produktiver Arbeit mutiert durch gleichzeitige stoffliche Erweiterung auf den Gesamtarbeiter und gesellschaftliche Verengung auf Kapitalverwertung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MP-02","text":"Variables Kapital mutiert vom scheinbaren Vorschuss des Kapitalisten zum zirkulierenden Rückfluss eines von der Arbeiterklasse selbst erzeugten Produktteils.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A8","CH_V4GB_EINR:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MP-03","text":"Kapital mutiert vom vorgeschossenen Wertding zur rekursiven sozialen Macht, deren Produkt als handelndes Subjekt und deren Produzent als reproduziertes Mittel erscheint.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als rekursive Konversionsmaschine, die lebendige Arbeitszeit in fremde objektive Macht und diese Macht in erneuerte Bedingungen ihrer eigenen Verwertung verwandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt erscheint als rechtlich freier, austauschbarer Träger von Arbeitskraft, dessen Selbsterhaltung zugleich seine funktionale Verfügbarkeit reproduziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist zugleich geteilter Arbeitstag und kumulative Reproduktionszeit: unbezahlte Stunden erzeugen Mehrwert, wiederholte Perioden verwandeln Voraussetzungen in Resultate.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-04","text":"Als mögliche Gegenbewegung bleibt nur eine Neuordnung notwendiger Arbeit und verfügbarer Zeit sichtbar; der rekonstruierte Mechanismus selbst stellt keinen internen Fluchtweg bereit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD7","CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B01","text":"Die extrahierten Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von Mehrwertproduktion über Realisierung und Lohnverdeckung bis zur Reproduktion des Kapitalverhältnisses auf Clusterebene zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT1","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B02","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die konkreten Zirkulations- und Reproduktionsbedingungen sowie die historische Genesis der ursprünglichen Trennung und des ersten Kapitalvorschusses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B03","text":"Die Architektur ist kohärent, sofern Produktionsquelle und Realisierungsvermittlung sowie konstante Produktionsgröße und veränderte Wertprovenienz strikt unterschieden werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT4","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B04","text":"Ihre höchste Beweiskraft liegt im kombinierten Wechsel vom Lohn zur unbezahlten Arbeit, vom Einzelakt zur Klassenbewegung und von der Einzelperiode zur kumulierten Zeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT4","CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B05","text":"Der Reduktion widerstehen die nur teilweise mechanisierten Konkurrenzübergänge, die ambivalente Einbeziehung der Arbeiterkonsumtion und das Fehlen eines immanent erzeugten Übergangs aus der reproduzierten Trennung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:MRT7","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT6","CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T211941146089Z_2b1fd350","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 16–18","source_sha256":"77d2dfc1705cf74daac2b15f81d9d289a2d13e8269aaac5776965821bd8214be","sha256":"53fb6976d6129394f9f0e03239d5bee65830d8e7fc877d6432ce1e386ce1007d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:19:41.147078+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-01","text":"The isolated act of production or exchange cannot explain how capital reproduces its conditions of valorization across multiple periods.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-02","text":"The underlying movement connects the production of unpaid surplus labour with its realization and with the renewed production of the separation that enables its appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_EINR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-03","text":"Production, circulation, and reproduction form an asymmetrical unity: production generates surplus value, circulation realizes it, and reproduction renews its social preconditions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A12","CH_V4GB_EINR:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-04","text":"Wage, income, and contract forms disaggregate the capital relation into seemingly independent transactions, although they mediate the same movement of appropriation and reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-05","text":"The directed movement proceeds from the functional determination of productive labour through subsumption and surplus-value production to realization and finally to the recursive reproduction of the class poles.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:AS3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-06","text":"The scale shifts from the length, intensity, and productivity of the individual working day to the cumulative time of social class reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:AS5","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-07","text":"The movement is recursive and cumulative: repetition on the same scale of production preserves magnitudes but changes value provenance and social dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AS-08","text":"Closure consists in the reproduction of capitalist and wage labourer as complementary poles; concrete forms of circulation and the historical genesis of their original separation remain deferred.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:D12","CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Surplus value rests on appropriated unpaid labour; neither its realization nor its subsequent division alters this substance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] The wage form transforms the value of labour-power into the appearance of paid labour and, in reproduction, deepens into the concealment of a wage fund produced by the working class itself.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A17","CH_V4GB_EINR:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Accumulation requires the realization of the surplus value contained in the commodity and its reconversion into capital, without circulation thereby becoming the source of surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The distribution of surplus value among independent forms of property and income changes its appearance, not its common basis of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A8","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] The separation of labour-power from its objective conditions is at once the presupposition and the continuously produced result of the capitalist process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A12","CH_V4GB_EINR:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Temporal continuity dissolves the independence of the individual act of exchange and the enduring value identity of the original capital advance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A5","CH_V4GB_EINR:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Real subsumption shifts capital's domination from external command into technology and organization and, at the level of reproduction, extends into the functional incorporation of the worker's existence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Legal equivalence, contractual freedom, and economic exploitation are compatible because formal independence does not abolish material separation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD2","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] The capitalist process produces not only commodities and surplus value, but also reproduces capitalist, wage labourer, and their relation as its overall social output.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8","CH_V4GB_EINR:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Genetic explanation requires controlled abstraction and a subsequent shift of scale from forms of appearance to the source of production, mediation, and class reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-01","text":"Unpaid labour preserves a stable identity: it appears successively as the substance of surplus value, the common basis of its partial forms, and the material core of reproduced capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-02","text":"Productive labour mutates from a social valorization function within the collective worker into the source of value, whose continuous replacement reproduces the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D1","CH_V4GB_EINR:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-03","text":"Subsumption expands its scope: the technical reorganization of the labour process becomes the recursive organization of the social conditions under which labour-power must be sold anew.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-04","text":"Wage inversion deepens from the apparent payment of all labour to the notion that the capitalist advances a labour fund existing independently of the workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_EINR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-05","text":"Circulation is initially displaced from the basic analysis, but returns as necessary mediation of realization and as the class movement of wage reflux.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A12","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-06","text":"Accumulation mutates at the boundary of simple reproduction: reconversion expands capital, whereas complete consumption of surplus value keeps the scale constant, yet nevertheless transforms value provenance and the class relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RMD-07","text":"Freedom undergoes a reversal of valence: equivalent individual contract and change of employer do not refute dependence, but become its recurrent forms of mediation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD2","CH_V4GB_EINR:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-01","text":"The quantitative matrix of duration of labour, intensity, and productivity remains a local instrument for determining movements of value; at cluster level it is subordinated to the reproductive mechanism of surplus labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-02","text":"Time wages, piece wages, and world-market comparison remain particular forms of control and comparison; what alone scales upward is their common function of measuring, individualizing, and concealing extraction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ME8","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-03","text":"Profit, interest, commercial profit, and ground rent remain at this level deferred forms of distribution and bear globally only insofar as their common origin is preserved.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:NX6","CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-04","text":"What scales to the cluster architecture is the connection of unpaid labour, realization, and reconversion or reproduction, because only this determines the complete circuit of the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT5","CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-05","text":"The first appropriator and the original capital advance lose their global explanatory function; they are absorbed into class distribution and cumulative reproductive time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A5","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:CGD-06","text":"The individual consumption of workers rises from a local moment of reproduction to a mediating structure through which labour-power and the capital relation are renewed simultaneously.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:D9","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-01","text":"Natural fertility or technical productivity must not be regarded as a self-acting cause of surplus value; it only opens up disposable time, whose appropriation is socially organized.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-02","text":"The worker sells neither labour already performed nor receives its full value in wages; the object of exchange is labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:NX6","CH_V4GB_FNKW:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-03","text":"Circulation can realize and distribute surplus value, but cannot constitute its original source.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-04","text":"Independent forms of revenue and property must not be treated as mutually independent sources of surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-05","text":"Formal market freedom must guarantee neither material self-disposal nor the absence of economic dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:GNX-06","text":"Simple reproduction must not be read as consequence-free repetition or historical stasis.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:NX2","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-01","text":"The system cannot admit forms of appearance such as wage, monetary advance, individual contract, and income share as the final level of explanation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:DNX7","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-02","text":"Present capital ownership must not be permanently legitimated by an original act of acquisition, because reproductive value replacement dissolves its identity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-03","text":"Capitalist reproduction is unthinkable without the continuing separation of labour-power and the conditions of labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-04","text":"The sphere of private consumption cannot form a fully autonomous exterior of capital insofar as it produces the renewed saleability of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:DBN-05","text":"Neither immediate production nor circulation can by itself explain the overall system; their separation is methodologically necessary, but their definitive autonomization is impermissible.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-01","text":"An automatic transformation of productivity gains into general free time or social emancipation remains excluded.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SNX3","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-02","text":"The reproduced process contains no immanent mechanism that abolishes, through its own operation, the separation between producers and conditions of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-03","text":"A fully transparent form of appearance in which unpaid labour, the common source of surplus value, and class recursion would become immediately visible is structurally unavailable.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SNX1","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSA-04","text":"The coincidence of legal personal freedom and material self-disposal constitutes the central unavailable possibility around which the architecture is organized.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-01","text":"Because the wage form makes all labour appear paid, while the working class produces in advance the fund of its own remuneration, the wage is at once a form of equivalence and a reflux of already appropriated value; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_06:GA-02","CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_EINR:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-02","text":"The necessary realization of surplus value grounds a unity of production and circulation whose asymmetry lies in the fact that production alone generates the unpaid value to be realized; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_06:GA-03","CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:D1","CH_V4GB_SKDA:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-03","text":"Real subsumption and class reproduction form two ranges of the same movement of domination: the first reorganizes the labour process, the second renews its available bearers; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-04","text":"Capitalist reproduction is not identical with quantitative accumulation: even with complete consumption of surplus value and an unchanged scale, value provenance and social preconditions change; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-06","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-05","text":"The division of surplus value pluralizes its owners, while reproduction produces capitalist and wage labourer anew as unified class poles; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-04","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-06","text":"Equivalent exchange and repeated free contract stabilize the relation of exploitation because they legitimate its individual enactments while simultaneously concealing its class continuity; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-02","CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD2","CH_V4GB_EINR:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:XD-07","text":"Productivity gains and workers' consumption acquire their capitalist function only through the persisting relation of separation: the former expand appropriable time, the latter renews saleable labour-power; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD3","CH_V4GB_EINR:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-01","text":"At this level, capital acquires the ontological status of a self-reproducing social relation that transforms living labour into an alien objective power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD8","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-02","text":"Capitalist time is at once cyclical and cumulative: each cycle renews the scale of production, while the sequence of cycles transforms origin, dependence, and class position.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-03","text":"Causality becomes recursive: separation compels the sale of labour-power, whose result produces the conditions under which the same sale becomes necessary anew.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:D7","CH_V4GB_EINR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-04","text":"The subject divides into the legally free bearer of labour-power and the functionally reproduced means of capital; correspondingly, the capitalist appears as the representative of a valorization and distribution function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME7","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-05","text":"Knowledge requires a double operation: mediations are initially abstracted in order to expose the genetic basic form, and subsequently reintroduced through the scale of class and time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:BSD-06","text":"A non-capitalist temporal order would have to alter the distribution of necessary labour and the disposal of its productivity gains; the reconstructed mechanism does not, however, itself produce this transition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD7","CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-01","text":"The central class recursion is: separation of labour-power and conditions of labour, sale of labour-power, production of an alien product, consumption of wages, and renewed necessity of sale.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A12","CH_V4GB_EINR:A13","CH_V4GB_EINR:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-02","text":"The escalation of extraction proceeds from increasing productivity through expanded surplus-labour time to technical control, performance metrics, and competition, which normalize the increased degree of extraction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD3","CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-03","text":"Realized surplus value possesses a bifurcation: its reconversion expands capital, its complete consumption maintains the scale; both paths, however, presuppose the renewal of the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-04","text":"Concealment escalates from the wage form through independent revenue forms to the free individual contract; every additional mediation increases the distance between appearance and common source.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D14","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7","CH_V4GB_EINR:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is the capital relation itself: scattered analyses of the working day, wage, realization, consumption, and property converge on its recursive self-preservation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B01","text":"Initial condition: labour-power is separated from means of production and product and must therefore appear as a commodity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B02","text":"Production operation: purchase of labour-power, formal or real subsumption, and the exceeding of necessary labour-time produce unpaid surplus value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A5","CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B03","text":"Form operation: wage and autonomized forms of income translate the common source of surplus value into seemingly independent prices and claims.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A17","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B04","text":"Mediation operation: sale realizes surplus value; reconversion leads to accumulation, complete consumption to simple reproduction at an unchanged scale.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:A3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:A4","CH_V4GB_EINR:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B05","text":"Recursion operation: workers' consumption reproduces labour-power under persisting separation, while the production cycle renews capital and the class poles.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A14","CH_V4GB_EINR:A15","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B06","text":"Knowledge operation: abstraction isolates the genetic basic form; temporal and social reintegration reconstructs its concealed mediations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AFM-B01","text":"Functional determination of productive labour → subsumption of the labour process → unpaid surplus labour → wage inversion → realization of surplus value → bifurcation into accumulation or simple reproduction → renewed separation → reproduced capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:AS7","CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:AFM-B02","text":"Form of appearance → controlled abstraction → genetic source of production → reintroduction of the mediation of circulation → temporal aggregation → class recursion → systemic closure.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-01","text":"Productivity is remapped from a neutral source of social wealth into a technically opened reserve of time, whose use is determined by the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ME3","CH_V4GB_FNKW:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-02","text":"The opposition between production and circulation disintegrates: both are necessary, but not symmetrical, because one produces surplus value and the other realizes it.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS3","CH_V4GB_SKDA:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-03","text":"Wage and capital ownership are reclassified from independent claims upon alien value into temporally mediated forms of a reproductive nexus produced by the working class.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME2","CH_V4GB_EINR:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-04","text":"The opposition between repetition and change collapses: an unchanged magnitude of production can coincide with cumulative transformation of value provenance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME4","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MME-05","text":"The concept of output expands from commodities and surplus value to reproduced labour-power, capital, class positions, and the relation between them.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME9","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B01","text":"At the Surface level, wage level, duration of labour, piece quantity, commodity sale, monetary reflux, and an unchanged scale of production appear as separate processes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT1","CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B02","text":"At the Structural level, unpaid labour, subsumption, realization, persisting separation, and reproduction of labour-power connect these processes into a class mechanism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:ALT2","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B03","text":"At the Metastrategic level, the shift from individual act to class continuity replaces explanation through market forms with a reconstruction of their conditions of production and reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B04","text":"At the Ontological / Temporal level, social identities are not static bearers but recursively produced positions within a time that interweaves necessary, unpaid, and reproductive labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:ALT4","CH_V4GB_EINR:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B05","text":"At the Methodological / Performative level, the presentation enacts its thesis by abstracting, restoring excluded mediations, and dissolving seemingly independent forms into a process through changes of scale.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:AS6","CH_V4GB_EINR:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-01","text":"Accumulation presupposes circulation, while its pure analysis excludes circulation; coherence therefore depends on the provisional character of this abstraction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-02","text":"The equation of the producing capitalist with the total owner of surplus value conflicts with his determination as merely the first appropriator, but remains productive as a methodological compression.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-03","text":"Workers' consumption oscillates between the necessary reproduction of labour-power and the comprehensive functional incorporation of a sphere of life that capital does not fully control.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:FL-04","text":"Juridical non-ownership and functional binding must neither be identified nor separated; their tension sustains the determination of the free and yet dependent wage labourer.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MP-01","text":"The concept of productive labour mutates through simultaneous material expansion to the collective worker and social narrowing to capital valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MP-02","text":"Variable capital mutates from the capitalist's apparent advance into the circulating reflux of a portion of the product produced by the working class itself.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:A8","CH_V4GB_EINR:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MP-03","text":"Capital mutates from an advanced value-thing into a recursive social power, whose product appears as an acting subject and whose producer as a reproduced means.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a recursive conversion machine that transforms living labour-time into alien objective power and this power into renewed conditions of its own valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-02","text":"The subject appears as a legally free, exchangeable bearer of labour-power, whose self-preservation simultaneously reproduces its functional availability.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is at once a divided working day and cumulative reproductive time: unpaid hours produce surplus value, repeated periods transform presuppositions into results.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:A3","CH_V4GB_EINR:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:HSI-04","text":"As a possible counter-movement, only a reordering of necessary labour and available time remains visible; the reconstructed mechanism itself provides no internal escape route.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:SD7","CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct, at cluster level, the movement from surplus-value production through realization and wage concealment to the reproduction of the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT1","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B02","text":"The concrete conditions of circulation and reproduction, as well as the historical genesis of the original separation and the first capital advance, remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT3","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B03","text":"The architecture is coherent provided that the source of production and the mediation of realization, as well as constant magnitude of production and changed value provenance, are strictly distinguished.","refs":["CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT4","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B04","text":"Its highest evidentiary force lies in the combined shift from wage to unpaid labour, from individual act to class movement, and from individual period to cumulative time.","refs":["CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT4","CH_V4GB_SKDA:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B05","text":"What resists reduction are the only partially mechanized transitions of competition, the ambivalent incorporation of workers' consumption, and the absence of an immanently produced transition out of reproduced separation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_FNKW:MRT7","CH_V4GB_EINR:MRT6","CH_V4GB_EINR:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_06@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_06:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 16–18","context":"Fünftes Kapitel. Weitere Untersuchungen über die Produktion des absoluten und relativen Mehrwerths. · Sechstes Kapitel. Der Accumulationsprozess des Kapitals. · a) Einfache Reproduktion."}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 19–21","order":7,"parents":["CH_V4GB_BVVM","CH_V4GB_CDAG","CH_V4GB_CD_2"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_07@R001","sha256":"9839f888549ce64428ae062bfe9dcbde994ad2c559c6e96e99aad30f2684a8f7","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-01","text":"Das System erklärt, wie aus Mehrwert erzeugtes Kapital die Voraussetzungen seiner erneuten Verwertung hervorbringt und dabei wachsendes gesellschaftliches Vermögen mit Abhängigkeit, Arbeitsüberschuss und Pauperismus verbindet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-02","text":"Akkumulation wird von der bloßen Kapitalisierung eines Überschusses zur erweiterten Reproduktion eines Klassenverhältnisses umbestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-03","text":"Die Rekursion des Surpluskapitals endogenisiert zunächst die Finanzierung weiterer Aneignung und anschließend die Arbeitsmarktbedingungen, unter denen diese Aneignung fortgesetzt werden kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04","text":"Der Übergang von quantitativer Kapitalvergrößerung zu veränderter organischer Zusammensetzung verwandelt zusätzliche Produktivkraft in relative Arbeiterfreisetzung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-05","text":"Die relative Surpluspopulation ist weder äußerer Überschuss noch bloße Folge natürlicher Bevölkerungsbewegung, sondern eine vom Kapital erzeugte Voraussetzung flexibler Expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-06","text":"Wohnraumkontrolle, saisonale Nachfrage, Familienarbeit, Gangvermittlung und Emigration konkretisieren die Reservebildung als räumlich und zeitlich organisierte Produktion von Verfügbarkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-07","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv, kumulativ, zyklisch und mutationsgetrieben, weil jedes Anpassungsresultat zur Bedingung einer neuen Akkumulations- und Freisetzungsrunde wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-08","text":"Die Schließung bleibt historisch offen: Die kapitalistische Form erzeugt materielle Möglichkeiten ihrer Überschreitung, ohne einen Übergangsmechanismus zu liefern, während räumlich exportierte Widersprüche politisch zurückkehren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Akkumulation ist die fortgesetzte Rückverwandlung von Mehrwert in Kapital und damit die rekursive Kapitalisierung unbezahlter Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Erweiterte Reproduktion verlangt geeignete stoffliche Produktionsmittel, verfügbare Arbeitskraft und die erneute Reproduktion des Kapitalverhältnisses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Der Äquivalententausch behält im Einzelakt formelle Geltung, mutiert aber durch seine reproduktive Wiederholung zur Rechtsform systematischer Aneignung ohne Äquivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A8","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Produktivkraftsteigerung erweitert die von gegebener Arbeitskraft bewegte Produktionsmittelmasse und vermindert dadurch den variablen Kapitalteil relativ zum Gesamtkapital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Akkumulation, Konzentration und Attraktion steigern das Kommando über Arbeit, während neues Kapital relativ weniger Arbeiter anzieht und umgewälztes Kapital beschäftigte Arbeiter freisetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A12","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Relative Übervölkerung ist eine relationale Größe gegenüber den Verwertungsbedürfnissen des Kapitals und wird als Reserve für dessen Expansion endogen erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Die industrielle Reservearmee ermöglicht plötzliche Expansion und diszipliniert zugleich die aktive Arbeiterarmee.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Die Verfügung über Wohnraum, Mobilität und Familienarbeitskraft institutionalisiert die räumliche, zeitliche und soziale Verfügbarkeit der Reserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Konkurrenz begrenzt den individuellen Willen des Kapitalisten und erzwingt sowohl fortgesetzte Akkumulation als auch ein mit der Verwertung vereinbares Lohnniveau.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Gesellschaftliches Reichtumswachstum und die Reproduktion der Produzenten sind systematisch entkoppelt, sodass Kapitalvermehrung mit konsolidierter Not koexistieren kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Kapital ist keine physische Sache, sondern die gesellschaftliche Form, in der Produktionsmittel durch Einverleibung fremder Arbeit zu Verwertungsmitteln werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Die kapitalistische Form ist historisch transitorisch, weil sie Produktivkräfte und materielle Bedingungen entwickelt, deren nichtantagonistische Verwendung sie selbst blockiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A17","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Räumliche Entfernung vernichtet den erzeugten Widerspruch nicht, sondern überführt ihn in rekursive Migration, Diasporabildung und politische Rückwirkung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-01","text":"Akkumulation bewahrt ihre Identität als Kapitalisierung von Mehrwert, erweitert ihren Geltungsbereich jedoch von der individuellen Kapitalmetamorphose zur gesellschaftlichen Reproduktion von Klassenmacht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-02","text":"Das Surpluskapital mutiert vom zusätzlichen Vorschuss zur rekursiven Maschine, die ihre Finanzierung, ihre Arbeitskräftebasis und ihre Expansionsbedingungen selbst erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-03","text":"Der Äquivalententausch erfährt keine einfache Aufhebung, sondern eine Maßstabsumkehr: Seine lokale Gültigkeit vermittelt die globale Reproduktion von Aneignung ohne Äquivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A7","CH_V4GB_BVVM:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-04","text":"Produktivkraft wechselt ihre Valenz von einer elastischen Expansionspotenz des Kapitals zu einem Mechanismus gleichzeitiger Mehrwertsteigerung, Arbeiterfreisetzung und Reservebildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-05","text":"Bevölkerung wird von einer absoluten biologischen Größe zu einem relationalen Index der Differenz zwischen verfügbarer Arbeitskraft und kapitalistisch bestimmter Nachfrage verschoben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-06","text":"Das Proletariat bleibt als abhängige Klasse persistent, differenziert sich aber funktional in aktive Arbeiterarmee, Reserve, Pauperismus, mobile Familienarbeit und Diaspora.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-07","text":"Kapital mutiert vom scheinbar fixen Bestand zur elastischen gesellschaftlichen Funktionsgröße und schließlich zum territorial verteilten Kommando über Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-08","text":"Emigration kehrt ihre anfängliche Valenz als demographische Entlastung um und erscheint als selbstverstärkender Transfer, Binnenmarktkontraktion und politische Konfliktverlagerung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-09","text":"Die Teilung des Mehrwerts in Revenue und Akkumulationsfonds bleibt als lokale Entscheidungsmatrix bestehen, wird auf Clusterebene aber in den übergeordneten Konkurrenz-, Kompositions- und Reservebildungsprozess absorbiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A10","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-01","text":"Die Aufteilung des kapitalisierten Mehrwerts in konstantes und variables Kapital sowie in Revenue und Akkumulationsfonds bleibt eine notwendige Mechanik der unteren Ebene, bildet aber noch nicht das allgemeine Akkumulationsgesetz.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-02","text":"Schatzbildung, Abstinenz und persönliche Konsumtion sind lokal widerlegte Fehlmodelle; auf Clusterebene werden sie durch die umfassendere Zurückweisung individualistischer Akkumulationserklärungen ersetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX1","CH_V4GB_BVVM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-03","text":"Die einzelnen Formen der Surpluspopulation, englische Wohnungsfälle, Gangarbeit und irische Daten bleiben empirisch und institutionell lokal, während ihre gemeinsame Funktion als Produktion flexibler Arbeitsverfügbarkeit nach oben skaliert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-04","text":"Die Eigentumsdialektik skaliert, weil sie den Übergang von der Kapitalisierung unbezahlter Arbeit zur endogenen Produktion abhängiger und überschüssiger Arbeitskraft begründet.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-05","text":"Die organische Zusammensetzung wird erst auf der aktuellen Ebene zum Scharnier zwischen Akkumulation und Reservearmeebildung; isoliert bleibt sie lediglich eine Relation von Wert- und Technikstruktur.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9","CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-06","text":"Wohnraumkontrolle und Gangvermittlung skalieren nicht als selbständige Allgemeingesetze, sondern als konkrete räumliche und zeitliche Implementationen der endogenen Reserveproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-07","text":"Die politische Rückkehr der Emigrierten überschreitet die ökonomische Mechanik der unteren Ebene und erzeugt eine terminale, aber nicht vollständig vermittelte Schließung des Clusters.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-01","text":"Akkumulation ist weder Schatzbildung noch moralisch verdiente Frucht persönlicher Entsagung, sondern gesellschaftliche Reproduktion durch kapitalisierten Mehrwert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX1","CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-02","text":"Formell gleicher Tausch erklärt nicht den gesellschaftlichen Inhalt des reproduzierten Eigentums- und Klassenverhältnisses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX7","CH_V4GB_BVVM:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-03","text":"Bevölkerungsgröße ist keine autonome Ursache von Beschäftigung, Lohn oder Elend; Überzähligkeit wird relativ zu kapitalistischen Verwertungsbedürfnissen bestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-04","text":"Produktivkraftentwicklung ist sozial nicht neutral und übersetzt Arbeitsersparnis nicht notwendig in kürzere Arbeitszeit oder gesicherte Entwicklung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-05","text":"Der Arbeitsmarkt ist kein Zusammentreffen unabhängiger Größen und kein selbstkorrigierender Mechanismus, der Knappheit notwendig in höhere Löhne verwandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-06","text":"Produktionsmittel, vergangene Arbeit und technischer Fortschritt sind nicht an sich Kapital, sondern werden erst innerhalb eines bestimmten Aneignungsverhältnisses zu dessen Potenzen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-07","text":"Emigration, Entvölkerung und räumliche Entfernung beseitigen weder relative Übervölkerung noch das Kapitalverhältnis und seine politischen Folgen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-01","text":"Damit die Architektur Bestand hat, muss falsch sein, dass steigende Löhne die Abhängigkeit des Lohnarbeiters und den Zwang zum Wiederverkauf der Arbeitskraft aufheben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-02","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Kapitalismus, dessen entwickelter Normalzustand stabile Vollbeschäftigung ohne Reservearmee wäre.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX6","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-03","text":"Unzulässig ist die Gleichsetzung kapitalistischer Wertsteigerung mit der Befriedigung gesellschaftlicher Bedürfnisse oder der gesicherten Reproduktion der Produzenten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04","text":"Die Architektur schließt ein endgültiges territoriales Außen aus, in dem verdrängte Bevölkerung und exportierte Widersprüche folgenlos verschwinden könnten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-05","text":"Eigentum, Recht und nationale Einheit dürfen nicht als neutrale Hüllen behandelt werden, weil sie die Trennung von Produzenten, Produktionsbedingungen und Reproduktionsorten organisieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste strukturierende Abwesenheit ist die unmittelbare Aneignung von Produkt und Produktionsbedingungen durch die Produzenten selbst.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine Ordnung, in der Arbeitsersparnis unmittelbar in allgemeine freie Zeit und gegenständlicher Reichtum in Mittel menschlicher Entwicklung übergeht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-03","text":"Das System umkreist einen gesicherten Ort unabhängiger Reproduktion, den es den Arbeitenden strukturell verweigert und durch Wohnraumentzug, Mobilisierung und Enteignung ersetzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-04","text":"Ontologisch unstatthaft ist eine nichtantagonistische kapitalistische Akkumulation, die Reichtum vermehrt, ohne Trennung, Reservebildung und Elend zu reproduzieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-01","text":"Jeder neue kapitalisierte Mehrwert vergrößert nicht bloß das Kapital, sondern tritt in eine veränderte Zusammensetzung ein, die seine proportionale Arbeitsnachfrage vermindern kann.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-04","CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-02","text":"Die Rekursion unbezahlter Arbeit erzeugt sowohl den Fonds weiterer Akkumulation als auch die relative Surpluspopulation, deren Verfügbarkeit die Fortsetzung dieser Akkumulation absichert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-06","CL_V4GB_07:GA-07","CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-03","text":"Juristische Freiheit und Äquivalententausch bleiben mit systemischer Unfreiheit vereinbar, weil Reservekonkurrenz die Bedingungen des wiederholten Verkaufs der Arbeitskraft strukturiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","CL_V4GB_07:GA-07","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A7","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-04","text":"Sobald Wissenschaft, Natur und lebendige Arbeit als Potenzen des Kapitals erscheinen, kann Produktivitätssteigerung zugleich als Selbstverwertung des Kapitals und als Überzähligkeit von Arbeitern auftreten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-04","CL_V4GB_07:GA-11","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-05","text":"Der abstrakte Konkurrenzzwang materialisiert sich durch Konzentration, Wohnraumkontrolle und mobile Arbeitsvermittlung in lokalen Institutionen, welche Widerstandsfähigkeit senken und Verfügbarkeit erhöhen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-05","CL_V4GB_07:GA-08","CL_V4GB_07:GA-09","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A16","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-06","text":"Die Entkopplung von Kapitalvermehrung und Produzentenreproduktion ermöglicht, private Renten und Profite zu steigern, während die Kosten von Krankheit, Pauperismus und unzureichender Reproduktion sozial verlagert werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-07","text":"Weil erweiterte Reproduktion nicht ausschließlich kapitalistisch ist, gehören Reservearmee und Pauperismus nicht zur Erweiterung als solcher, sondern zu deren antagonistischer gesellschaftlicher Form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-02","CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX8","CH_V4GB_BVVM:D13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-08","text":"Territorialer Bevölkerungsexport ist keine Schließung, sondern eine zeitversetzte Transformation des ökonomischen Widerspruchs in transnationale politische Gegnerschaft.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-13","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-01","text":"Kapital erhält den Status eines rekursiven gesellschaftlichen Verhältnisses, das Finanzierung, Arbeitsangebot, Disziplin und räumliche Verfügbarkeit als eigene Reproduktionsbedingungen erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-02","text":"Die Zeit der Akkumulation ist gleichzeitig rekursiv, zyklisch, saisonal, generationell und transnational: Vergangene Arbeit kommandiert gegenwärtige Arbeit, Reserven wechseln zwischen Absorption und Freisetzung, und Emigration kehrt politisch zurück.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ALT4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-03","text":"Das Subjekt zerfällt in Systemfunktionen: Der Kapitalist personifiziert den Akkumulationszwang, während die Arbeiterklasse in beschäftigte, überarbeitete, freigesetzte, mobile und ausgewanderte Segmente gegliedert wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-04","text":"Kausalität wird endogen und rückgekoppelt: Wirkungen der Akkumulation werden zu Voraussetzungen ihrer Wiederholung, statt als äußerliche demographische oder moralische Ursachen zu fungieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-05","text":"Politische Handlungsfähigkeit entsteht dort, wo die organisatorische Verbindung von Beschäftigten, Arbeitslosen und Verdrängten die segmentierende Funktion der Reserve unterbricht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnis verlangt systematischen Maßstabswechsel: Einzeltausch, Kapitalzusammensetzung, Arbeitsmarkt, Wohnraum, Nation und Migration müssen als verschiedene Ebenen derselben Reproduktionsarchitektur gelesen werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-07","text":"Historische Transitorität folgt aus der Trennbarkeit erweiterter Reproduktion von ihrer kapitalistischen Form, garantiert aber weder automatische Aufhebung noch einen ausgearbeiteten politischen Übergang.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-01","text":"Mehrwert → Kapitalisierung → Surpluskapital → neuer Mehrwert bildet die elementare Rekursionsschleife, in der unbezahlte vergangene Arbeit zusätzliche lebendige Arbeit kommandiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-02","text":"Akkumulation → größere Produktionsleiter → Produktivkraftsteigerung → zusätzliche Mehrwertproduktion → beschleunigte Akkumulation bildet die expansive Verstärkungsschleife.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-03","text":"Produktivkraftsteigerung → steigende organische Zusammensetzung → relative Verringerung der Arbeitsnachfrage → Reservebildung → flexible Expansion bildet die zentrale Mutationsschleife.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-04","text":"Arbeitskräftemangel → Lohnsteigerung → sinkender Verwertungsanreiz → verlangsamte Akkumulation → erneute Arbeitskräfteverfügbarkeit bildet einen kapitalimmanenten Korrekturpfad.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-05","text":"Konzentration → Wohnraumentzug → Abhängigkeit → Mindestlohn → mobile Zusatzarbeit → erneuerte Reserve bildet die räumlich-institutionelle Eskalationsschleife.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-06","text":"Emigration → Rücküberweisungen → weitere Emigration → Binnenmarktkontraktion → Proletarisierung → Diasporabildung bildet eine territoriale Schleife, deren ökonomische Verdrängung politisch zurückwirkt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D11","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-07","text":"Der begriffliche Attraktor ist die Selbstproduktion der Verwertungsbedingungen: Finanzierung, Produktivkraft, Reserve, Lohndisziplin und Mobilität konvergieren auf eine Architektur, in der das Kapital seine Voraussetzungen als eigene Wirkungen setzt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B01","text":"Mehrwert → Teilung in Revenue und Akkumulationsfonds → Rückverwandlung in konstantes und variables Kapital → erweiterte Reproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A10","CH_V4GB_BVVM:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B02","text":"Kapitalisierter Mehrwert + stofflich geeignetes Mehrprodukt + zusätzliche Arbeitskraft → neues Surpluskapital → vergrößerte Verfügung über unbezahlte Arbeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A3","CH_V4GB_BVVM:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B03","text":"Formell gültiger Äquivalententausch × reproduktive Wiederholung → Trennung von Arbeit und Eigentum → Aneignung ohne Äquivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B04","text":"Akkumulation + Produktivkraftsteigerung → steigende organische Zusammensetzung → relativer Rückgang des variablen Kapitals → Arbeiterfreisetzung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B05","text":"Konzentration + Kapitalattraktion + technologische Umwälzung → verstärktes Kommando über Arbeit + verringerte proportionale Arbeitsnachfrage → relative Surpluspopulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B06","text":"Wohnraumentzug + saisonale Nachfrageschwankung + Frauen- und Kinderarbeit + Gangvermittlung → mobile, billige und disziplinierte Agrarreserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B07","text":"Absolute Entvölkerung + fortgesetzte Konzentration → persistente relative Übervölkerung → Binnenmarktkontraktion → Diasporabildung → politische Rückkehr des verdrängten Widerspruchs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A15","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:AFM-B01","text":"Mehrwertkapitalisierung → erweiterte Reproduktion → Umschlag von Tausch und Eigentum → konkurrenzerzwungene Expansion → Produktivkraftsteigerung → organischer Strukturwandel → Arbeiterfreisetzung → Reservearmeebildung → Lohndisziplin und Pauperismus → räumlich-institutionelle Reserveproduktion → Entvölkerung ohne Aufhebung relativer Übervölkerung → transnationale politische Rückkehr.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS6","CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-01","text":"Akkumulation wird von Sparen und Reichtumsvermehrung zur rekursiven Reproduktion eines Klassenverhältnisses mit endogener Reservebildung umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-02","text":"Äquivalententausch und Ausbeutung erscheinen nicht länger als logische Gegensätze, sondern als Vorgänge verschiedener Ebenen derselben Reproduktionsform.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-03","text":"Reichtum und Wohlergehen werden entkoppelt; Renten-, Profit- und Kapitalwachstum verlieren ihren Status als Indikatoren gelingender gesellschaftlicher Reproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-04","text":"Überbevölkerung wird von absoluter Menschenzahl zu relativer Überzähligkeit gegenüber kapitalistisch bestimmter Arbeitsnachfrage umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-05","text":"Der Arbeitsmarkt wird als vom Kapital auf Angebots- und Nachfrageseite produziertes Machtfeld statt als neutraler Austauschraum sichtbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-06","text":"Untervölkerung, Arbeitsmangel und Übervölkerung werden als räumlich und zeitlich differenzierte Koexistenz statt als einander ausschließende Zustände lesbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-07","text":"Wohnraum, Familienstruktur und Mobilität werden von privaten oder demographischen Umständen zu Instrumenten der Arbeitsmarktregulierung und Reserveproduktion reklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-08","text":"Emigration wird vom Sicherheitsventil zum rekursiven Export sozialer Kosten und zur zeitversetzten politischen Rückkehr des Konflikts umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene erscheinen Lohn, Beschäftigung, Arbeitslosigkeit, Wohnungsnot, Gangarbeit, Entvölkerung, Renten und Pauperismus als heterogene Phänomene.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene werden diese Phänomene durch Mehrwertkapitalisierung, organische Zusammensetzung, Konzentration, Reservearmeebildung und Kontrolle der Reproduktionsbedingungen verbunden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene ersetzt die Analyse moralische, demographische und individualistische Erklärungen durch eine Rekonstruktion kapitalimmanenter Reproduktion und Klassenmacht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-temporalen Ebene erscheint Realität als relationales Gefüge verschiedener Zeitskalen, in dem vergangene Arbeit gegenwärtige Arbeit kommandiert und erzeugte Wirkungen zukünftige Bedingungen bilden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ALT4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollzieht die Argumentation ihre These durch wiederholte Maßstabswechsel, Negationen naturalisierter Erklärungen und empirische Widerspruchsanordnungen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-01","text":"Die formelle Geltung des Äquivalententauschs und die substantielle Aneignung ohne Äquivalent bleiben spannungsvoll, sind aber als Differenz von Einzeltransaktion und gesellschaftlicher Reproduktion produktiv.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-02","text":"Die Teilung des Mehrwerts erscheint zugleich als Willensakt des Kapitalisten und als durch Konkurrenz begrenzte Systemfunktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-03","text":"Die Möglichkeit steigender Löhne bleibt nur unvollständig mit der allgemeinen Verschlechterungsdiagnose vermittelt, weil relative Abhängigkeit, Konsumtion und materielle Lage nicht durchgehend getrennt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT6","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-04","text":"Die Kausalrolle der organischen Zusammensetzung bleibt instabil, weil ihre Wertseite technische Veränderungen nur annähernd abbildet und modifizierende Faktoren vertagt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9","CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-05","text":"Der Anspruch eines absoluten allgemeinen Gesetzes steht unter Spannung zur räumlichen, historischen und institutionellen Modifikation seiner konkreten Erscheinungsformen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-06","text":"Die empirischen Fälle zeigen robuste Koexistenzmuster, doch der Übergang zu einer einheitlichen Akkumulationskausalität komprimiert alternative Gewichtungen der beteiligten Mechanismen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-07","text":"Die historische Transitorität bleibt unterbestimmt, weil materielle Bedingungen einer höheren Form benannt werden, ohne deren politische und institutionelle Vermittlung abzuleiten.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A17","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-01","text":"Akkumulation mutiert am Übergang von bloßer Kapitalvergrößerung zur qualitativen Veränderung der Kapitalzusammensetzung und Arbeitsnachfrage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-02","text":"Überbevölkerung mutiert von einer absoluten demographischen Kategorie zu einer relationalen Funktion kapitalistischer Verwertungsbedürfnisse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX13","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-03","text":"Die abstrakte Reservearmee mutiert durch Wohnraumkontrolle, Familienarbeit und Gangvermittlung zu einer räumlich, geschlechtlich und zeitlich organisierten Arbeitsreserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-04","text":"Emigration mutiert von vermeintlicher Entlastung zur rekursiven Reproduktion von Entvölkerung, Proletarisierung, Diaspora und politischer Gegnerschaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als rekursive Verwertungsmaschine, die lebendige Arbeit, vergangene Arbeit, Natur, Wissenschaft und soziale Entwurzelung in Bedingungen ihrer eigenen Expansion verwandelt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D10","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt erscheint nicht als souveränes Zentrum, sondern als verteilte Funktion: personifizierendes Kapital auf der einen und segmentierte, mobile oder überzählige Arbeitskraft auf der anderen Seite.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist eine verschachtelte Rekursion aus Akkumulationsfolge, industriellem Zyklus, saisonalem Bedarf, generationeller Reproduktion und verzögerter politischer Rückkehr.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-04","text":"Möglich bleibt ein Kampf, der die vom Kapital erzeugten Trennungen zwischen Beschäftigten, Reserve und Verdrängten praktisch unterbricht und die Produktionsbedingungen ihrer kapitalistischen Form entzieht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B01","text":"Die globalen Axiome reichen aus, um die Bewegung von Mehrwertkapitalisierung über organischen Wandel und Reservebildung bis zur räumlichen und politischen Rückkehr der Verdrängung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B02","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die proportionale Verteilung des gesellschaftlichen Mehrprodukts, die konkrete Periodizität des industriellen Zyklus und die quantitative Kalibrierung der empirischen Mechanismen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B03","text":"Das System ist kohärent, sofern Einzeltransaktion und gesellschaftliche Reproduktion, absolutes Kapitalwachstum und relativer Variablenrückgang sowie lokale Knappheit und relationale Übervölkerung auseinandergehalten werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B04","text":"Die stärkste Architektur liegt in der Endogenisierung: Das Kapital erzeugt aus seinen Wirkungen die Fonds, Reserven, Disziplinierungsformen und räumlichen Bedingungen seiner Wiederholung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B05","text":"Die Rekonstruktion hängt von der Sequenzierung des Maßstabswechsels ab: Kapitalisierung muss vor Kompositionswandel, Reservebildung vor ihrer räumlichen Konkretisierung und Emigration vor politischer Rückwirkung stehen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B06","text":"Empirische Tabellen, lokale Berichte und moralisch aufgeladene Darstellungen widerstehen teilweise axiomatischer Reduktion, weil Belegdichte, Funktionsanalyse und Verantwortungszuschreibung nicht vollständig zusammenfallen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B07","text":"Ein unverzichtbares Element bleibt unreduziert: Die Architektur begründet die historische Begrenztheit der kapitalistischen Form, erzeugt aber keinen hinreichenden Mechanismus ihres Übergangs in eine höhere Gesellschaftsform.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SNX4","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T212022585464Z_a4cfa96d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 19–21","source_sha256":"9839f888549ce64428ae062bfe9dcbde994ad2c559c6e96e99aad30f2684a8f7","sha256":"450f1d5156dab2d685db724010c58de9ae30e161714fe9ec5bdbf1b37a873752","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:20:22.587189+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-01","text":"The system explains how capital generated from surplus-value brings forth the conditions of its renewed valorization, thereby linking growing social wealth with dependency, surplus labor, and pauperism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-02","text":"Accumulation is redefined from the mere capitalization of a surplus into the expanded reproduction of a class relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-03","text":"The recursion of surplus capital first endogenizes the financing of further appropriation and subsequently the labor-market conditions under which this appropriation can be continued.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04","text":"The transition from quantitative enlargement of capital to an altered organic composition transforms additional productive power into the relative release of workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-05","text":"The relative surplus population is neither an external surplus nor the mere consequence of natural population movement, but a precondition of flexible expansion produced by capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-06","text":"Control of housing, seasonal demand, family labor, gang mediation, and emigration concretize reserve formation as the spatially and temporally organized production of availability.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-07","text":"The movement is recursive, cumulative, cyclical, and mutation-driven, because every result of adaptation becomes the condition of a new round of accumulation and release.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ASP-08","text":"The closure remains historically open: the capitalist form produces the material possibilities of its transcendence without supplying a mechanism of transition, while spatially exported contradictions return politically.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Accumulation is the continued reconversion of surplus-value into capital and thus the recursive capitalization of unpaid labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Expanded reproduction requires suitable material means of production, available labor-power, and the renewed reproduction of the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Exchange of equivalents retains formal validity in the individual act, but mutates through its reproductive repetition into the legal form of systematic appropriation without equivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A8","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] An increase in productive power expands the mass of means of production set in motion by a given labor-power and thereby diminishes the variable part of capital relative to total capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A8","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Accumulation, concentration, and attraction increase command over labor, while new capital attracts relatively fewer workers and transformed capital releases employed workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A12","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Relative overpopulation is a relational magnitude relative to the valorization needs of capital and is endogenously produced as a reserve for its expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] The industrial reserve army enables sudden expansion and simultaneously disciplines the active army of workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A17","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] The disposal of housing, mobility, and family labor-power institutionalizes the spatial, temporal, and social availability of the reserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Competition limits the individual will of the capitalist and compels both continued accumulation and a wage level compatible with valorization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A16","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The growth of social wealth and the reproduction of the producers are systematically decoupled, so that capital augmentation can coexist with consolidated distress.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Capital is not a physical thing, but the social form in which means of production become means of valorization through the incorporation of others' labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The capitalist form is historically transitory because it develops productive forces and material conditions whose non-antagonistic use it itself blocks.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A17","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Spatial distance does not annihilate the contradiction produced, but transforms it into recursive migration, diaspora formation, and political feedback.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-01","text":"Accumulation preserves its identity as the capitalization of surplus-value, yet expands its scope from the individual metamorphosis of capital to the social reproduction of class power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-02","text":"Surplus capital mutates from an additional advance into a recursive machine that itself produces its financing, its labor-power base, and its conditions of expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-03","text":"Exchange of equivalents undergoes no simple abolition, but a reversal of scale: its local validity mediates the global reproduction of appropriation without equivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A7","CH_V4GB_BVVM:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-04","text":"Productive power changes its valence from an elastic potential for the expansion of capital into a mechanism of simultaneous increase in surplus-value, release of workers, and reserve formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-05","text":"Population is displaced from an absolute biological magnitude to a relational index of the difference between available labor-power and capitalistically determined demand.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-06","text":"The proletariat persists as a dependent class, but differentiates functionally into an active army of workers, reserve, pauperism, mobile family labor, and diaspora.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-07","text":"Capital mutates from an apparently fixed stock into an elastic social functional magnitude and finally into territorially distributed command over labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-08","text":"Emigration reverses its initial valence as demographic relief and appears as a self-reinforcing transfer, domestic-market contraction, and displacement of political conflict.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RMD-09","text":"The division of surplus-value into revenue and accumulation fund persists as a local decision matrix, but at the cluster level is absorbed into the higher-order process of competition, composition, and reserve formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A10","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-01","text":"The division of capitalized surplus-value into constant and variable capital, as well as into revenue and accumulation fund, remains a necessary mechanism of the lower level, but does not yet constitute the general law of accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-02","text":"Hoard formation, abstinence, and personal consumption are locally refuted false models; at the cluster level they are replaced by the more comprehensive rejection of individualistic explanations of accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX1","CH_V4GB_BVVM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-03","text":"The individual forms of the surplus population, English housing cases, gang labor, and Irish data remain empirically and institutionally local, while their shared function as the production of flexible labor availability scales upward.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-04","text":"The dialectic of property scales because it grounds the transition from the capitalization of unpaid labor to the endogenous production of dependent and surplus labor-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-05","text":"Organic composition becomes the hinge between accumulation and the formation of the reserve army only at the current level; in isolation it remains merely a relation of value and technical structure.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9","CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-06","text":"Control of housing and gang mediation do not scale as independent general laws, but as concrete spatial and temporal implementations of endogenous reserve production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:CGD-07","text":"The political return of emigrants exceeds the economic mechanism of the lower level and produces a terminal, yet not fully mediated, closure of the cluster.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-01","text":"Accumulation is neither hoard formation nor the morally deserved fruit of personal renunciation, but social reproduction through capitalized surplus-value.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX1","CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-02","text":"Formally equal exchange does not explain the social content of the reproduced property and class relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX7","CH_V4GB_BVVM:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-03","text":"Population size is not an autonomous cause of employment, wages, or misery; supernumerariness is determined relative to capitalist valorization needs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-04","text":"The development of productive power is not socially neutral and does not necessarily translate labor-saving into shorter working time or secured development.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-05","text":"The labor market is neither a meeting of independent magnitudes nor a self-correcting mechanism that necessarily transforms scarcity into higher wages.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-06","text":"Means of production, past labor, and technical progress are not capital in themselves, but become its powers only within a determinate relation of appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:GNX-07","text":"Emigration, depopulation, and spatial distance eliminate neither relative overpopulation nor the capital relation and its political consequences.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, it must be false that rising wages abolish the wage-worker's dependence and the compulsion to resell labor-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-02","text":"Excluded is a capitalism whose developed normal state would be stable full employment without a reserve army.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX6","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-03","text":"Impermissible is the equation of capitalist value augmentation with the satisfaction of social needs or the secured reproduction of the producers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04","text":"The architecture excludes a final territorial outside in which displaced population and exported contradictions could disappear without consequence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:DBN-05","text":"Property, law, and national unity must not be treated as neutral shells, because they organize the separation of producers, conditions of production, and sites of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:DNX7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-01","text":"The deepest structuring absence is the direct appropriation of product and conditions of production by the producers themselves.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SNX1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is an order in which labor-saving directly becomes general free time and objective wealth becomes a means of human development.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-03","text":"The system circles around a secured site of independent reproduction, which it structurally denies to workers and replaces through withdrawal of housing, mobilization, and expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSA-04","text":"Ontologically inadmissible is a non-antagonistic capitalist accumulation that augments wealth without reproducing separation, reserve formation, and misery.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-01","text":"Every newly capitalized surplus-value not only enlarges capital, but enters into an altered composition that may diminish its proportional demand for labor.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-04","CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-02","text":"The recursion of unpaid labor produces both the fund of further accumulation and the relative surplus population whose availability secures the continuation of this accumulation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-06","CL_V4GB_07:GA-07","CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-03","text":"Juridical freedom and exchange of equivalents remain compatible with systemic unfreedom because reserve competition structures the conditions of the repeated sale of labor-power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","CL_V4GB_07:GA-07","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A7","CH_V4GB_CDAG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-04","text":"As soon as science, nature, and living labor appear as powers of capital, an increase in productivity can simultaneously appear as the self-valorization of capital and as the supernumerariness of workers.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-04","CL_V4GB_07:GA-11","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-05","text":"The abstract compulsion of competition materializes through concentration, control of housing, and mobile labor mediation in local institutions that lower resilience and increase availability.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-05","CL_V4GB_07:GA-08","CL_V4GB_07:GA-09","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A16","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-06","text":"The decoupling of capital augmentation and the reproduction of producers makes it possible to increase private rents and profits while socially displacing the costs of illness, pauperism, and inadequate reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-10","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-07","text":"Because expanded reproduction is not exclusively capitalist, the reserve army and pauperism belong not to expansion as such, but to its antagonistic social form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-02","CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","CH_V4GB_BVVM:NX8","CH_V4GB_BVVM:D13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:XD-08","text":"Territorial population export is not a closure, but a temporally displaced transformation of economic contradiction into transnational political antagonism.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-13","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-01","text":"Capital acquires the status of a recursive social relation that produces financing, labor supply, discipline, and spatial availability as its own conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-02","text":"The time of accumulation is simultaneously recursive, cyclical, seasonal, generational, and transnational: past labor commands present labor, reserves alternate between absorption and release, and emigration returns politically.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ALT4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-03","text":"The subject disintegrates into system functions: the capitalist personifies the compulsion to accumulate, while the working class is divided into employed, overworked, released, mobile, and emigrated segments.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes endogenous and feedback-driven: effects of accumulation become preconditions of its repetition, instead of functioning as external demographic or moral causes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-05","text":"Political agency arises where the organizational connection of the employed, unemployed, and displaced interrupts the segmenting function of the reserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD6","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-06","text":"Knowledge requires systematic shifts of scale: individual exchange, capital composition, labor market, housing, nation, and migration must be read as different levels of the same architecture of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:BSD-07","text":"Historical transitoriness follows from the separability of expanded reproduction from its capitalist form, but guarantees neither automatic abolition nor an elaborated political transition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-01","text":"Surplus-value → capitalization → surplus capital → new surplus-value forms the elementary recursion loop in which unpaid past labor commands additional living labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-02","text":"Accumulation → larger scale of production → increase in productive power → additional production of surplus-value → accelerated accumulation forms the expansive reinforcement loop.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-03","text":"Increase in productive power → rising organic composition → relative reduction in labor demand → reserve formation → flexible expansion forms the central mutation loop.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-04","text":"Labor shortage → wage increase → declining incentive to valorization → slowed accumulation → renewed availability of labor-power forms a correction path immanent to capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-05","text":"Concentration → withdrawal of housing → dependency → minimum wage → mobile supplementary labor → renewed reserve forms the spatial-institutional escalation loop.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-06","text":"Emigration → remittances → further emigration → domestic-market contraction → proletarianization → diaspora formation forms a territorial loop whose economic displacement feeds back politically.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D11","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:RLE-07","text":"The conceptual attractor is the self-production of the conditions of valorization: financing, productive power, reserve, wage discipline, and mobility converge upon an architecture in which capital posits its preconditions as its own effects.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B01","text":"Surplus-value → division into revenue and accumulation fund → reconversion into constant and variable capital → expanded reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A10","CH_V4GB_BVVM:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B02","text":"Capitalized surplus-value + materially suitable surplus product + additional labor-power → new surplus capital → enlarged command over unpaid labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A3","CH_V4GB_BVVM:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B03","text":"Formally valid exchange of equivalents × reproductive repetition → separation of labor and property → appropriation without equivalent.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B04","text":"Accumulation + increase in productive power → rising organic composition → relative decline of variable capital → release of workers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B05","text":"Concentration + capital attraction + technological transformation → intensified command over labor + reduced proportional demand for labor → relative surplus population.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A13","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B06","text":"Withdrawal of housing + seasonal fluctuation of demand + labor by women and children + gang mediation → mobile, cheap, and disciplined agricultural reserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B07","text":"Absolute depopulation + continued concentration → persistent relative overpopulation → domestic-market contraction → diaspora formation → political return of the displaced contradiction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D7","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A15","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:AFM-B01","text":"Capitalization of surplus-value → expanded reproduction → reversal of exchange and property → competition-enforced expansion → increase in productive power → organic structural transformation → release of workers → formation of reserve army → wage discipline and pauperism → spatial-institutional reserve production → depopulation without abolition of relative overpopulation → transnational political return.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS6","CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-01","text":"Accumulation is remapped from saving and wealth augmentation into the recursive reproduction of a class relation with endogenous reserve formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-02","text":"Exchange of equivalents and exploitation no longer appear as logical opposites, but as processes at different levels of the same form of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-03","text":"Wealth and well-being are decoupled; growth in rents, profits, and capital loses its status as an indicator of successful social reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:NX9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-04","text":"Overpopulation is reclassified from an absolute number of persons into relative supernumerariness vis-à-vis capitalistically determined demand for labor.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-05","text":"The labor market becomes visible as a field of power produced by capital on both the supply and demand sides, rather than as a neutral space of exchange.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD3","CH_V4GB_CDAG:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-06","text":"Underpopulation, labor scarcity, and overpopulation become legible as spatially and temporally differentiated coexistence rather than mutually exclusive states.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:D3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-07","text":"Housing, family structure, and mobility are reclassified from private or demographic circumstances into instruments of labor-market regulation and reserve production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MME-08","text":"Emigration is remapped from a safety valve into the recursive export of social costs and the temporally displaced political return of conflict.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:ME9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, wages, employment, unemployment, housing shortage, gang labor, depopulation, rents, and pauperism appear as heterogeneous phenomena.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, these phenomena are connected through the capitalization of surplus-value, organic composition, concentration, formation of the reserve army, and control of the conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, analysis replaces moral, demographic, and individualistic explanations with a reconstruction of reproduction immanent to capital and class power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:ALT3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, reality appears as a relational configuration of different time scales, in which past labor commands present labor and produced effects form future conditions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:ALT4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the argument enacts its thesis through repeated shifts of scale, negations of naturalized explanations, and empirical arrangements of contradiction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:AS5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-01","text":"The formal validity of exchange of equivalents and substantial appropriation without equivalent remain tension-filled, but are productive as a difference between individual transaction and social reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD2","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-02","text":"The division of surplus-value appears simultaneously as an act of will by the capitalist and as a system function limited by competition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-03","text":"The possibility of rising wages remains only incompletely mediated with the diagnosis of general deterioration, because relative dependency, consumption, and material situation are not consistently distinguished.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT6","CH_V4GB_CDAG:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-04","text":"The causal role of organic composition remains unstable because its value side only approximately represents technical changes and modifying factors are deferred.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:A9","CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-05","text":"The claim of an absolute general law stands in tension with the spatial, historical, and institutional modification of its concrete forms of appearance.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-06","text":"The empirical cases show robust patterns of coexistence, yet the transition to a unified causality of accumulation compresses alternative weightings of the mechanisms involved.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:FL-07","text":"Historical transitoriness remains underdetermined because the material conditions of a higher form are named without deriving their political and institutional mediation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:A17","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-01","text":"Accumulation mutates at the transition from the mere enlargement of capital to the qualitative alteration of capital composition and labor demand.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX5","CH_V4GB_CDAG:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-02","text":"Overpopulation mutates from an absolute demographic category into a relational function of capitalist valorization needs.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:NX13","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-03","text":"The abstract reserve army mutates through control of housing, family labor, and gang mediation into a spatially, gendered, and temporally organized labor reserve.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A4","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MP-04","text":"Emigration mutates from purported relief into the recursive reproduction of depopulation, proletarianization, diaspora, and political antagonism.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:A14","CH_V4GB_CD_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a recursive machine of valorization that transforms living labor, past labor, nature, science, and social uprooting into conditions of its own expansion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:D10","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-02","text":"The subject appears not as a sovereign center, but as a distributed function: personifying capital on one side and segmented, mobile, or supernumerary labor-power on the other.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is an interlaced recursion of the sequence of accumulation, industrial cycle, seasonal requirement, generational reproduction, and delayed political return.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:D9","CH_V4GB_CD_2:A5","CH_V4GB_CD_2:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:HSI-04","text":"A struggle remains possible that practically interrupts the separations produced by capital between the employed, the reserve, and the displaced, and withdraws the conditions of production from their capitalist form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:SD6","CH_V4GB_BVVM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B01","text":"The global axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the capitalization of surplus-value through organic transformation and reserve formation to the spatial and political return of displacement.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B02","text":"Underdetermined remain the proportional distribution of the social surplus product, the concrete periodicity of the industrial cycle, and the quantitative calibration of the empirical mechanisms.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT2","CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT8","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B03","text":"The system is coherent provided that individual transaction and social reproduction, absolute capital growth and relative decline of the variable component, as well as local scarcity and relational overpopulation, are kept distinct.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT4","CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT3","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B04","text":"The strongest architecture lies in endogenization: capital produces from its effects the funds, reserves, forms of discipline, and spatial conditions of its repetition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SD1","CH_V4GB_CD_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction depends on the sequencing of the shift of scale: capitalization must precede compositional transformation, reserve formation its spatial concretization, and emigration political feedback.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CDAG:MRT10","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B06","text":"Empirical tables, local reports, and morally charged representations partially resist axiomatic reduction, because evidentiary density, functional analysis, and attribution of responsibility do not fully coincide.","refs":["CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT2","CH_V4GB_CD_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B07","text":"One indispensable element remains unreduced: the architecture grounds the historical limitation of the capitalist form, but produces no sufficient mechanism for its transition into a higher social form.","refs":["CH_V4GB_BVVM:SNX4","CH_V4GB_BVVM:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_07@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_07:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 19–21","context":"b) Verwandlung von Mehrwerth in Kapital. · c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 1/2 · c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 2/2"}},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 22–23","order":8,"parents":["CH_V4GB_2DSG","CH_V4GB_3DMK"],"revision":"CL_V4GB_08@R001","sha256":"52bfaed15b900afbe77ccdce542382fe665e13d5e79d4c0252c49c8b0608a46e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-01","text":"Die zirkulären Voraussetzungen kapitalistischer Akkumulation erzwingen eine historische Erklärung des Kapitalverhältnisses, deren Geltung durch seine Funktionsstörung bei fehlender Lohnarbeiterklasse geprüft wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-02","text":"Kapital entsteht und besteht nur, sofern Produzenten von ihren Arbeitsbedingungen getrennt und dadurch als eigentumslose Arbeitskraft verfügbar gehalten werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-03","text":"Die Argumentation verbindet diachrone Genealogie mit synchronem Gegenexperiment: Die englische Gewaltgeschichte rekonstruiert die Herstellung, während die freie Kolonie durch deren Ausfall die notwendige Bedingung offenlegt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-04","text":"Die Bewegung führt von offener Enteignung und staatlicher Disziplinierung über die Selbstreproduktion ökonomischer Abhängigkeit zur kolonialen Wiederherstellung derselben Trennung durch künstliche Bodenschranken.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-05","text":"Die Architektur ist rekursiv: Expropriation erzeugt Lohnarbeit, Akkumulation reproduziert deren Voraussetzungen, freier Bodenzugang unterbricht die Schleife und provoziert ihre politische Neuinstallation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-06","text":"Die Schließung verzweigt sich in die immanente Negation kapitalistischen Eigentums und in den Übergang von der Produktion des Mehrwerts zu seiner Realisation in der Kapitalzirkulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Kapital ist keine Eigenschaft von Dingen, sondern ein gesellschaftliches Verhältnis, das Geld und Produktionsmittel erst unter bestimmten Klassenbedingungen funktionalisiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] Die Trennung der Produzenten von Boden und Produktionsmitteln ist die generative Bedingung kapitalistischer Produktion, Akkumulation und Reproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Auf eigener Arbeit beruhendes Eigentum und kapitalistisches Privateigentum sind entgegengesetzte Aneignungsweisen, nicht Entwicklungsstufen einer einheitlichen Eigentumsform.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Rechtliche Freiheit wird zur Form materieller Abhängigkeit, sofern der Arbeiter nicht über seine Arbeitsbedingungen verfügt; erst reale Austrittsmöglichkeiten geben Freiheit eine gegensätzliche Funktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Bodenzugang ist die zentrale Schaltvariable des Kapitalverhältnisses: Enteignung erzeugt Lohnabhängigkeit, allgemeiner Zugang ermöglicht ihren Abbruch.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Der Arbeitsmarkt ist kein vorausgesetzter Tauschraum, sondern das institutionell erzeugte Resultat von Expropriation, Disziplinierung und fortgesetzter Bevölkerungsregulierung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Staatsgewalt bleibt konstitutiv, wechselt jedoch von unmittelbarem Terror zu ökonomischem Zwang, künstlicher Bodenknappheit und regulierter Arbeitskräftezufuhr.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Akkumulation reproduziert nicht nur Kapital, sondern auch die Trennung, die verfügbare Lohnarbeiterklasse und den Arbeitskräfteüberschuss, auf denen sie beruht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Ursprüngliche Akkumulation bezeichnet zugleich historische Genesis und reaktivierbare Technik zur Wiederherstellung gefährdeter Lohnabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Die freie Kolonie fungiert als Gegenexperiment, das durch das Ausbleiben kapitalistischer Normalität die im Mutterland sedimentierten Voraussetzungen sichtbar macht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Produzentenunabhängigkeit und kapitalistische Akkumulation stehen in einem inversen Verhältnis, weil Selbstversorgung und eigener Bodenzugang Arbeitsmarkt und inneren Markt zugleich unterbrechen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Die Negation kapitalistischen Eigentums kann nicht als Wiederherstellung isolierten Kleineigentums erfolgen, sondern muss den Produzentenzugang zu Arbeitsbedingungen mit der erreichten gesellschaftlichen Kooperation verbinden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-01","text":"Kapital bewahrt seine Identität als gesellschaftliches Verhältnis; seine dinglichen Träger wechseln, ohne selbst die Kapitalfunktion garantieren zu können.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-02","text":"Expropriation mutiert vom datierbaren historischen Scheidungsereignis zur fortlaufend einsetzbaren Technik der Klassenreproduktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-03","text":"Boden verschiebt sich vom Gegenstand ursprünglicher Enteignung zum strategischen Regulierungspunkt zwischen unabhängiger Produktion und Lohnabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-04","text":"Staatsgewalt behält ihre marktstiftende Funktion, mutiert aber von offenem Terror und Rechtsumbau zur künstlichen Preisbildung und gesteuerten Arbeiterzufuhr.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-05","text":"Freiheit kehrt ihre Valenz um: Die Aufhebung persönlicher Knechtschaft kann materielle Proletarisierung erzeugen, während realer Bodenzugang den Austritt aus dem Lohnverhältnis ermöglicht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-06","text":"Akkumulation erweitert ihre Funktion von Kapitalvermehrung zur rekursiven Reproduktion der Scheidung und der relativen Überbevölkerung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-07","text":"Das auf eigener Arbeit beruhende Eigentum bleibt als Negation kapitalistischen Eigentums bestehen, wird terminal jedoch in eine kooperative Eigentumsform höherer Ordnung absorbiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-01","text":"Die englischen Enclosures, Landräubereien und Disziplinargesetze bleiben lokale historische Implementierungen; auf Clusterebene skaliert ihre gemeinsame Funktion als Herstellung der Produzententrennung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-02","text":"Wakefields künstlicher Bodenpreis und Arbeiterimport bleiben lokale Kolonialinstrumente; nach oben skaliert die politische Erzeugung von Knappheit als allgemeiner Mechanismus kapitalistischer Arbeitsmarktbildung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-03","text":"Die Kolonie ist auf unterer Ebene ein besonderer Schauplatz, auf Clusterebene jedoch ein Erkenntnisverfahren zur Entnaturalisierung der Verhältnisse des Mutterlands.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-04","text":"Der Übergang von der mehrwerttragenden Ware zur Wertrealisation bleibt eine nachgelagerte Buchbrücke und organisiert nicht die zentrale Clusterarchitektur der Expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-05","text":"Die Gegenexpropriation skaliert als terminaler Horizont, wird durch die koloniale Gegenprobe aber nicht positiv bewiesen; diese demonstriert nur die Unvereinbarkeit allgemeiner Produzentenunabhängigkeit mit stabiler Akkumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-01","text":"Kapitalistisches Eigentum kann weder aus moralischer Sparsamkeit noch aus einer nichtzwangsförmigen Akkumulation selbstarbeitender Produzenten erklärt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-02","text":"Geld, Maschinen und Produktionsmittel sind weder von Natur aus noch aufgrund ihres bloßen Vorhandenseins Kapital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-03","text":"Rechtliche Emanzipation und Vertragsfreiheit sind nicht mit materieller Unabhängigkeit oder Verfügung über Arbeitsbedingungen identisch.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-04","text":"Arbeitsmarkt und innerer Markt entstehen nicht spontan aus Tausch, Bevölkerungswachstum oder Angebot und Nachfrage.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-05","text":"Eine von Staatsgewalt unabhängige Ökonomie kann die Lohnabhängigkeit, die ihre Marktgesetze voraussetzen, nicht selbst begründen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-06","text":"Kapitalistisches Privateigentum ist weder Fortsetzung des Arbeitseigentums noch durch Rückkehr zum zersplitterten Kleinbetrieb aufhebbar.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-01","text":"Damit das System Bestand hat, müssen transhistorische Kapitalbegriffe ausgeschlossen und ökonomische Kategorien als historisch bestimmte Sozialverhältnisse behandelt werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-02","text":"Eine neutrale Rechts- und Marktordnung zwischen bereits unabhängigen Parteien ist unzulässig, weil gerade diese Unabhängigkeit durch die vorausgesetzte Eigentumsverteilung negiert wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-03","text":"Allgemeiner Zugang zu Boden und dauerhaft verfügbare Lohnarbeit dürfen nicht stabil koexistieren; ihre Vereinbarkeit würde den zentralen Reproduktionsmechanismus aufheben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-04","text":"Nationalreichtum darf nicht als automatischer Ausdruck des Wohlstands der Produzenten gelten, weil Kapitalreichtum gerade durch deren Abhängigkeit wachsen kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-05","text":"Ein stationärer Kapitalismus ohne erneuerte Trennung ist ausgeschlossen, weil Akkumulation ihre soziale Voraussetzung fortlaufend reproduzieren muss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste ausgeschlossene Möglichkeit ist ein unschuldiger kapitalistischer Ursprung, der sich aus den späteren Rechtsformen des Systems ableiten ließe.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-02","text":"Eine kapitalistische Ordnung, die vollständige Verfügung der Produzenten über Boden und Arbeitsbedingungen bewahrt, ist ontologisch unstatthaft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-03","text":"Die dauerhafte Versöhnung gesellschaftlicher Produktion, monopolistischer Aneignung und allgemeiner Produzentenunabhängigkeit bleibt systemisch versperrt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-04","text":"Ebenso versperrt ist eine Aufhebung durch bloße Wiederherstellung isolierter Selbstarbeit; die nicht verfügbare Lösung muss Unabhängigkeit und gesellschaftliche Kooperation zugleich realisieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-01","text":"Genealogische Rekonstruktion und koloniales Gegenexperiment bilden gemeinsam einen doppelten Nachweis: Die erste zeigt die gewaltsame Herstellung, das zweite die Funktionsunfähigkeit des Kapitals bei Ausfall derselben Bedingung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-01","CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-02","text":"Wo der Austritt aus der Lohnarbeit materiell möglich bleibt, muss ursprüngliche Akkumulation als wiederholbare Schließung dieser Austrittsmöglichkeit zurückkehren.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-08","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09","CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-03","text":"Marktgesetzlichkeit setzt eine politische Vorproduktion ihrer Teilnehmer voraus; sie kann erst autonom erscheinen, nachdem Gewalt die Eigentumslosigkeit und Arbeitszufuhr hergestellt hat.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-06","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-04","text":"Die doppelte Freiheit besitzt eine reversible Klassenfunktion: Ohne Arbeitsbedingungen zwingt sie zum Verkauf der Arbeitskraft, mit zugänglichem Boden ermöglicht sie den Übergang zur unabhängigen Produktion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-04","CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-05","text":"Expropriation schaltet Arbeitsmarkt, inneren Markt und Kapitalfunktion gemeinsam ein; das Ausbleiben der Trennung unterbricht daher nicht nur Lohnarbeit, sondern den gesamten Reproduktionszusammenhang.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-06","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-06","text":"Der stumme Zwang des Mutterlands ist sedimentierte Gewalt; sobald die historisch erzeugte Abhängigkeit im Kolonialraum fehlt, muss ihre politische Konstruktion wieder sichtbar werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CL_V4GB_08:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-07","text":"Gegenexpropriation kann nicht im bloßen Zugang einzelner Produzenten zu Parzellen enden, weil dieser zwar Lohnabhängigkeit negiert, aber die gesellschaftlich entwickelte Kooperation noch nicht positiv organisiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-11","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-01","text":"Ontologisch ist Kapital eine relationale Positionsordnung, in der dieselben Dinge gemäß der Eigentums- und Klassenverteilung Kapital oder bloße Produktionsmittel sind.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-02","text":"Die kapitalistische Zeit ist geschichtet: Ein historischer Gewaltakt wird zur reproduzierten Gegenwart und kehrt bei Störung als reaktivierte Gründungstechnik zurück.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-03","text":"Epistemisch enthüllt die Peripherie den verborgenen Bau des Zentrums, weil das dortige Scheitern einer naturalisierten Kategorie ihre historischen Voraussetzungen isoliert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-04","text":"Politische und ökonomische Herrschaft sind keine getrennten Ursachen, sondern unterschiedliche Betriebszustände derselben Klassenordnung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-05","text":"Das Subjekt ist keine stabile anthropologische Einheit, sondern eine durch Eigentumszugang umschaltbare Position zwischen Lohnarbeiter, unabhängigem Produzenten und möglichem Träger kollektiver Gegenaneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-06","text":"Strategische Handlungsmacht liegt nicht primär im Vertragsakt, sondern in der Kontrolle über Arbeitsbedingungen, Austrittsmöglichkeiten und die gesellschaftliche Form kooperativer Produktion.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-01","text":"Scheidung erzeugt Produktionsmittel als Kapital und Produzenten als Lohnarbeiter; Akkumulation reproduziert anschließend beide Pole und intensiviert ihre Trennung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-02","text":"Bodenzugang erzeugt Austritt aus der Lohnarbeit, dieser erzeugt Arbeitsknappheit und Akkumulationshemmung, worauf künstliche Bodenpreise und Arbeiterimport die Schleife erneut schließen sollen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-03","text":"Offener Terror normalisiert das Lohnverhältnis, ökonomischer Zwang verdeckt seine Gewaltgeschichte, und koloniale Funktionsstörungen erzwingen die Rückkehr zu sichtbarer politischer Intervention.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-04","text":"Ideologische Gleichsetzung naturalisiert Eigentum und Vertrag; die naturalisierte Oberfläche verbirgt die Trennung, deren Verbergung wiederum die Kategorien als voraussetzungslos erscheinen lässt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-05","text":"Konzentration expropriiert Kapitalisten, steigert zugleich Kooperation und Arbeiterorganisation und verschärft dadurch den Widerspruch zwischen gesellschaftlicher Produktion und privater Aneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-06","text":"Der begriffliche Attraktor ist die Scheidung selbst, die nacheinander als Ursprung, Reproduktionsbedingung, kolonialer Ausfall und politisch programmierbare Technik erscheint.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-07","text":"Mit der mehrwerttragenden Ware erreicht die Expropriationsarchitektur ihre Produktionsgrenze und öffnet eine neue Schleife, in der Wert erst durch Verkauf realisiert werden muss.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B01","text":"Geld plus Produktionsmittel ergeben ohne gesellschaftliche Polarität kein Kapital; Kapitalfunktion entsteht erst durch die Verfügbarkeit eigentumsloser Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B02","text":"Enteignung von Boden und Arbeitsbedingungen erzeugt die Polarität von Verwertungsmittelbesitz und gezwungenem Arbeitskraftverkauf.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B03","text":"Produzententrennung → Lohnarbeiterklasse plus freigesetzte Produktionsmittel plus zerstörte Selbstversorgung → Arbeitsmarkt und innerer Markt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B04","text":"Akkumulation → Reproduktion der Scheidung plus relative Überbevölkerung → verstetigte Arbeitszufuhr und selbsttätige Abhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B05","text":"Allgemeiner Bodenzugang → unabhängige Produktion → Austritt aus Lohnarbeit → Arbeitsknappheit → Hemmung kombinierter Arbeit und Akkumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B06","text":"Künstlicher Bodenpreis plus Arbeiterimport → verzögerte Selbständigkeit plus erneuerte Lohnarbeiterklasse → koloniale Wiederinstallation des Kapitalverhältnisses.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B07","text":"Erfolgreiche politische Installation → normalisiertes Vertragsverhältnis → stummer ökonomischer Zwang → Verdeckung der historischen Gewalt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B08","text":"Konzentration plus Vergesellschaftung → Unvereinbarkeit privater Aneignung mit kooperativer Produktion → mögliche Gegenexpropriation; mehrwerttragende Ware → Verkauf → Kapitalzirkulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B01","text":"Zirkuläre Akkumulationsvoraussetzung → moralischer Ursprungsmythos → relationale Kapitalbestimmung → historische Scheidung von Produzent und Produktionsmittel.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B02","text":"Gewaltsame Expropriation → Lohndisziplin → Freisetzung von Arbeitskräften und Produktionsmitteln → innerer Markt → selbsttätige Reproduktion der Scheidung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B03","text":"Koloniales Gegenexperiment → freier Bodenzugang → Austritt aus Lohnarbeit → Akkumulationshemmung → künstliche Bodenschranke und Arbeiterimport → Bestätigung der Expropriationsbedingung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B04","text":"Kapitalistische Konzentration → Vergesellschaftung und Gegenorganisation → Eigentumswiderspruch → Gegenexpropriation; abgeschlossene Mehrwertproduktion → Realisationsproblem → Kapitalzirkulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-01","text":"Ursprüngliche Akkumulation wird von einem vergangenen Gründungsakt zu einem permanent reaktivierbaren Reproduktionsprotokoll umkartiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-02","text":"Die Kolonie wechselt vom geographischen Randfall zum epistemischen Prüfstand der verdeckten Mutterlandsverhältnisse.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-03","text":"Boden wird von einer Naturressource zum klassenstrukturellen Umschalter zwischen Selbstproduktion und Lohnabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-04","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen Staat und Markt bricht zusammen, weil Staatsgewalt die Bedingungen erzeugt, unter denen Marktzwang autonom erscheinen kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-05","text":"Freiheit zerfällt in rechtliche Selbstverfügung und materielle Verfügung über Arbeitsbedingungen; nur die zweite eröffnet wirklichen Austritt aus Lohnabhängigkeit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-06","text":"Privateigentum wird in selbstarbeitendes, kapitalistisches und mögliches kooperatives Eigentum differenziert; dadurch verliert der abstrakte Eigentumsbegriff seine analytische Einheit.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-07","text":"Nationalreichtum und Produzentenwohlstand werden als potenziell inverse Größen lesbar, weil der kapitalistische Reichtumsmaßstab verfügbare Abhängigkeit prämiert.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene erscheinen Landenteignung, Lohndisziplinierung, koloniale Akkumulation und Wakefields systematische Kolonisation als benannte Verfahren und Gegenstände.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene erzeugen diese Verfahren die Polarität von Kapitalbesitz und eigentumsloser Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene verbindet das System Genealogie und Gegenexperiment, um Eigentum, Markt und Vertrag als Resultate von Klassenmacht neu zu lesen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-temporalen Ebene ist Realität ein historisch erzeugtes Verhältnis, dessen Vergangenheit als reproduzierte Gegenwart und wiederholbare Intervention fortbesteht.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollziehen genealogische Rekonstruktion, koloniale Umkehrung und satirische Zuspitzung die Demontage der naturalisierten Kategorien.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-01","text":"Die historische Vielfalt und Kontingenz der Expropriationsverfahren steht unter Spannung zur terminalen Darstellung der kapitalistischen Negation als notwendigem Prozess.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-02","text":"Selbstarbeitseigentum erscheint kolonial als materielle Unabhängigkeit, terminal jedoch als produktiv begrenzte Form, die nicht unverändert wiederhergestellt werden kann.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-03","text":"Der Anspruch naturgesetzlicher Marktregulierung kollidiert mit der notwendigen politischen Suspendierung derselben Marktgesetze bei der Herstellung des Arbeitsmarkts.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-04","text":"Die erste Expropriation ist historisch breit rekonstruiert, während die Gegenexpropriation als stark komprimierte Folgerung aus Konzentration, Vergesellschaftung und Organisation erscheint.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-05","text":"Die Architektur abstrahiert von länderspezifischen Übergängen und lässt sowohl die Abweichungen vom englischen Verlauf als auch das historische Scheitern einzelner Kolonialtechniken unterbestimmt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-01","text":"Expropriation wechselt vom historischen Ursprung zur reproduzierten und politisch reaktivierbaren Betriebsbedingung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-02","text":"Gewalt mutiert von offenem Terror zu ökonomischem Zwang und kehrt bei kolonialer Instabilität als künstliche Preis- und Bevölkerungssteuerung zurück.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-03","text":"Freiheit mutiert von rechtlicher Loslösung ohne Produktionsmittel zur materiellen Fähigkeit, Lohnarbeit durch eigenen Bodenzugang zu verlassen.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-04","text":"Die Kolonie mutiert vom Objekt kapitalistischer Expansion zum diagnostischen Instrument für die verborgene Architektur des Mutterlands.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als Trennungsmaschine, die Dinge, Personen und Zugangsrechte zu Klassenpolen ordnet und dadurch Kapitalfunktion erzeugt.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist eine umschaltbare Position: Eigentumslosigkeit macht es zum Arbeitskraftverkäufer, Bodenzugang zum unabhängigen Produzenten und Vergesellschaftung zum möglichen Träger kollektiver Aneignung.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-03","text":"Die vorausgesetzte Zeit ist rekursiv statt linear: Der Ursprung wird reproduziert, bei Störungen wiederholt und durch seine eigenen Akkumulationsfolgen in eine mögliche Negation getrieben.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-04","text":"Kampf richtet sich auf die Kontrolle der Arbeitsbedingungen und Austrittsmöglichkeiten; Flucht durch individuellen Bodenzugang bleibt möglich, strategische Schließung verlangt jedoch kooperatives Gemeineigentum.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B01","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Clusterbewegung von der Scheidung über Arbeitsmarktbildung und Selbstreproduktion bis zur kolonialen Gegenprobe und möglichen Gegenexpropriation zu rekonstruieren.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B02","text":"Das System ist kohärent, sofern Kapital durchgehend als reproduziertes gesellschaftliches Verhältnis und Expropriation als dessen generative Bedingung behandelt wird.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B03","text":"Die stärkste Architektur liegt im doppelten Nachweis durch positive Genesis und negative Gegenprobe: Derselbe Bodenzugang, dessen Entzug Kapitalpole erzeugt, löst bei seiner Verfügbarkeit die Lohnarbeiterklasse auf.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B04","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die ökonomischen Agentien einzelner Übergänge, die länderspezifischen Abweichungen und die konkreten Ursachen des historischen Scheiterns von Wakefields Programm.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B05","text":"Die terminale Gegenexpropriation widersteht vollständiger axiomatischer Reduktion, weil ihre Notwendigkeit stärker theoretisch komprimiert ist als die historische Herleitung der ersten Expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B06","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung, sofern historische Sequenz, rekursive Reproduktion, koloniale Umkehrung und terminale Verzweigung nicht zu einer linearen Ursprungserzählung eingeebnet werden.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T212058624685Z_a32ad2d1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 22–23","source_sha256":"52bfaed15b900afbe77ccdce542382fe665e13d5e79d4c0252c49c8b0608a46e","sha256":"fd348e512d186729f76b1a212fd9453eac0daf1c94c085b8e5b2e0fc552cd81e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:20:58.626046+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-01","text":"The circular presuppositions of capitalist accumulation compel a historical explanation of the capital relation, whose validity is tested by its malfunction in the absence of a wage-labouring class.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-02","text":"Capital arises and persists only insofar as producers are separated from their conditions of labour and thereby kept available as propertyless labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-03","text":"The argument combines diachronic genealogy with a synchronic counterexperiment: English history of violence reconstructs the production, while the free colony reveals the necessary condition through its absence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from open expropriation and state disciplining, through the self-reproduction of economic dependence, to the colonial restoration of the same separation through artificial barriers to land.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-05","text":"The architecture is recursive: expropriation produces wage labour, accumulation reproduces its presuppositions, free access to land interrupts the loop and provokes its political reinstallation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AS-06","text":"The closure branches into the immanent negation of capitalist property and into the transition from the production of surplus-value to its realization in the circulation of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Capital is not a property of things, but a social relation that renders money and means of production functional only under specific class conditions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] The separation of producers from land and means of production is the generative condition of capitalist production, accumulation, and reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Property based on one's own labour and capitalist private property are opposed modes of appropriation, not developmental stages of a unified form of property.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Legal freedom becomes a form of material dependence insofar as the worker does not dispose of his conditions of labour; only real possibilities of exit give freedom an opposite function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Access to land is the central switching variable of the capital relation: expropriation produces wage dependence, general access makes its interruption possible.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The labour market is not a presupposed space of exchange, but the institutionally produced result of expropriation, disciplining, and continued population regulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A11","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] State power remains constitutive, but shifts from direct terror to economic compulsion, artificial land scarcity, and regulated labour supply.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Accumulation reproduces not only capital, but also the separation, the available wage-labouring class, and the surplus labour force on which it rests.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Primitive accumulation denotes both historical genesis and a reactivatable technique for restoring endangered wage dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The free colony functions as a counterexperiment that, through the absence of capitalist normality, renders visible the presuppositions sedimented in the mother country.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Producer independence and capitalist accumulation stand in an inverse relation, because self-sufficiency and one's own access to land interrupt both the labour market and the internal market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The negation of capitalist property cannot occur as a restoration of isolated small property, but must combine producers' access to conditions of labour with achieved social cooperation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-01","text":"Capital preserves its identity as a social relation; its material bearers change without themselves being able to guarantee the capital function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-02","text":"Expropriation mutates from a datable historical event of separation into a continuously deployable technique of class reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-03","text":"Land shifts from the object of original expropriation to the strategic point of regulation between independent production and wage dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-04","text":"State power retains its market-constituting function, but mutates from open terror and legal transformation to artificial price formation and controlled worker supply.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-05","text":"Freedom reverses its valence: the abolition of personal servitude can produce material proletarianization, whereas real access to land enables exit from the wage relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-06","text":"Accumulation extends its function from capital augmentation to the recursive reproduction of separation and relative overpopulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RMD-07","text":"Property based on one's own labour persists as the negation of capitalist property, but is terminally absorbed into a cooperative form of property of a higher order.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A16","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-01","text":"English enclosures, land robberies, and disciplinary laws remain local historical implementations; at the cluster level, their common function scales as the production of producer separation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-02","text":"Wakefield's artificial land price and worker import remain local colonial instruments; what scales upward is the political production of scarcity as a general mechanism of capitalist labour-market formation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-03","text":"At the lower level, the colony is a particular site; at the cluster level, however, it is a procedure of knowledge for denaturalizing the relations of the mother country.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-04","text":"The transition from the surplus-value-bearing commodity to value realization remains a downstream book bridge and does not organize the central cluster architecture of expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:CGD-05","text":"Counter-expropriation scales as a terminal horizon, but is not positively proved by the colonial countertest; the latter demonstrates only the incompatibility of general producer independence with stable accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-01","text":"Capitalist property can be explained neither by moral thrift nor by a non-coercive accumulation of self-labouring producers.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-02","text":"Money, machines, and means of production are capital neither by nature nor by their mere existence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-03","text":"Legal emancipation and freedom of contract are not identical with material independence or disposal over conditions of labour.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-04","text":"The labour market and the internal market do not arise spontaneously from exchange, population growth, or supply and demand.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-05","text":"An economy independent of state power cannot itself establish the wage dependence presupposed by its market laws.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:GNX-06","text":"Capitalist private property is neither a continuation of labour-property nor abolishable through a return to fragmented small-scale enterprise.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-01","text":"For the system to endure, transhistorical concepts of capital must be excluded and economic categories treated as historically determined social relations.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-02","text":"A neutral legal and market order between already independent parties is inadmissible, because precisely this independence is negated by the presupposed distribution of property.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-03","text":"General access to land and permanently available wage labour must not coexist stably; their compatibility would abolish the central mechanism of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-04","text":"National wealth must not be regarded as an automatic expression of the prosperity of producers, because capital wealth can grow precisely through their dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:NX8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:DBN-05","text":"A stationary capitalism without renewed separation is excluded, because accumulation must continually reproduce its social presupposition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-01","text":"The deepest excluded possibility is an innocent capitalist origin that could be derived from the system's later legal forms.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-02","text":"A capitalist order that preserves producers' complete disposal over land and conditions of labour is ontologically impermissible.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-03","text":"The lasting reconciliation of social production, monopolistic appropriation, and general producer independence remains systemically blocked.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:DNX6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSA-04","text":"Likewise blocked is an abolition through the mere restoration of isolated self-labour; the unavailable solution must realize independence and social cooperation simultaneously.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SNX4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-01","text":"Genealogical reconstruction and the colonial counterexperiment jointly form a double proof: the first shows the violent production, the second the incapacity of capital to function when the same condition is absent.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-01","CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-02","text":"Where exit from wage labour remains materially possible, primitive accumulation must return as the repeatable closure of this possibility of exit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-08","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09","CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-03","text":"Market lawfulness presupposes a political pre-production of its participants; it can appear autonomous only after violence has produced propertylessness and labour supply.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-06","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-04","text":"Double freedom has a reversible class function: without conditions of labour, it compels the sale of labour-power; with accessible land, it enables the transition to independent production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-04","CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-05","text":"Expropriation activates the labour market, the internal market, and the capital function jointly; the absence of separation therefore interrupts not only wage labour but the entire nexus of reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-06","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-06","text":"The mute compulsion of the mother country is sedimented violence; as soon as historically produced dependence is absent in colonial space, its political construction must become visible again.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CL_V4GB_08:GA-10","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:XD-07","text":"Counter-expropriation cannot end in the mere access of individual producers to parcels, because this indeed negates wage dependence but does not yet positively organize socially developed cooperation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-11","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-01","text":"Ontologically, capital is a relational positional order in which the same things are capital or mere means of production according to the distribution of property and classes.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-02","text":"Capitalist time is layered: a historical act of violence becomes a reproduced present and, when disrupted, returns as a reactivated founding technique.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-03","text":"Epistemically, the periphery reveals the hidden structure of the centre, because the failure there of a naturalized category isolates its historical presuppositions.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-04","text":"Political and economic domination are not separate causes, but different operating states of the same class order.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-05","text":"The subject is not a stable anthropological unity, but a position switchable through access to property between wage labourer, independent producer, and possible bearer of collective counter-appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:BSD-06","text":"Strategic agency lies not primarily in the contractual act, but in control over conditions of labour, possibilities of exit, and the social form of cooperative production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-01","text":"Separation produces means of production as capital and producers as wage labourers; accumulation subsequently reproduces both poles and intensifies their separation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-02","text":"Access to land produces exit from wage labour; this produces labour scarcity and impeded accumulation, whereupon artificial land prices and worker import are meant to close the loop again.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-03","text":"Open terror normalizes the wage relation, economic compulsion conceals its history of violence, and colonial malfunctions compel the return to visible political intervention.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-04","text":"Ideological equation naturalizes property and contract; the naturalized surface conceals the separation, whose concealment in turn makes the categories appear presuppositionless.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-05","text":"Concentration expropriates capitalists, while simultaneously increasing cooperation and worker organization, thereby sharpening the contradiction between social production and private appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-06","text":"The conceptual attractor is separation itself, which appears successively as origin, condition of reproduction, colonial absence, and politically programmable technique.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:RLE-07","text":"With the surplus-value-bearing commodity, the architecture of expropriation reaches its limit of production and opens a new loop in which value must first be realized through sale.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B01","text":"Money plus means of production do not yield capital without social polarity; the capital function arises only through the availability of propertyless labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B02","text":"Expropriation of land and conditions of labour produces the polarity of possession of means of valorization and compelled sale of labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B03","text":"Producer separation → wage-labouring class plus released means of production plus destroyed self-sufficiency → labour market and internal market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B04","text":"Accumulation → reproduction of separation plus relative overpopulation → continuous labour supply and self-acting dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B05","text":"General access to land → independent production → exit from wage labour → labour scarcity → impediment to combined labour and accumulation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B06","text":"Artificial land price plus worker import → delayed independence plus renewed wage-labouring class → colonial reinstallation of the capital relation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B07","text":"Successful political installation → normalized contractual relation → mute economic compulsion → concealment of historical violence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A12","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B08","text":"Concentration plus socialization → incompatibility of private appropriation with cooperative production → possible counter-expropriation; surplus-value-bearing commodity → sale → circulation of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B01","text":"Circular presupposition of accumulation → moral myth of origin → relational determination of capital → historical separation of producer and means of production.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS1","CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B02","text":"Violent expropriation → wage disciplining → release of labour forces and means of production → internal market → self-acting reproduction of separation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A14","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B03","text":"Colonial counterexperiment → free access to land → exit from wage labour → impeded accumulation → artificial barrier to land and worker import → confirmation of the condition of expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B04","text":"Capitalist concentration → socialization and counter-organization → contradiction of property → counter-expropriation; completed production of surplus-value → problem of realization → circulation of capital.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A17","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-01","text":"Primitive accumulation is remapped from a past founding act into a permanently reactivatable protocol of reproduction.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-02","text":"The colony shifts from a geographical marginal case to an epistemic testing ground of the concealed relations of the mother country.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-03","text":"Land is transformed from a natural resource into a class-structural switch between self-production and wage dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-04","text":"The opposition between state and market collapses because state power produces the conditions under which market compulsion can appear autonomous.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-05","text":"Freedom splits into legal self-disposal and material disposal over conditions of labour; only the latter opens real exit from wage dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-06","text":"Private property is differentiated into self-labouring, capitalist, and possible cooperative property; thereby the abstract concept of property loses its analytical unity.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MME-07","text":"National wealth and producer well-being become legible as potentially inverse magnitudes, because the capitalist measure of wealth rewards available dependence.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, land expropriation, wage disciplining, colonial accumulation, and Wakefield's systematic colonization appear as named procedures and objects.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, these procedures produce the polarity of capital possession and propertyless labour-power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the system combines genealogy and counterexperiment in order to reread property, market, and contract as results of class power.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, reality is a historically produced relation whose past persists as reproduced present and repeatable intervention.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ALT4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, genealogical reconstruction, colonial inversion, and satirical intensification enact the dismantling of naturalized categories.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:AS5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-01","text":"The historical diversity and contingency of procedures of expropriation stands in tension with the terminal presentation of capitalist negation as a necessary process.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT6","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-02","text":"Property based on self-labour appears colonially as material independence, but terminally as a productively limited form that cannot be restored unchanged.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-03","text":"The claim of natural-law market regulation collides with the necessary political suspension of those same market laws in the production of the labour market.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:D7","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-04","text":"The first expropriation is reconstructed broadly in historical terms, whereas counter-expropriation appears as a highly compressed consequence of concentration, socialization, and organization.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT8","CH_V4GB_2DSG:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:FL-05","text":"The architecture abstracts from country-specific transitions and leaves underdetermined both deviations from the English course and the historical failure of individual colonial techniques.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-01","text":"Expropriation shifts from historical origin to a reproduced and politically reactivatable operating condition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-02","text":"Violence mutates from open terror to economic compulsion and returns, under colonial instability, as artificial price and population control.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D5","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-03","text":"Freedom mutates from legal detachment without means of production into the material capacity to leave wage labour through one's own access to land.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:A4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MP-04","text":"The colony mutates from an object of capitalist expansion into a diagnostic instrument for the hidden architecture of the mother country.","refs":["CH_V4GB_3DMK:AS2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a machine of separation that orders things, persons, and rights of access into class poles and thereby produces the capital function.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a switchable position: propertylessness makes it a seller of labour-power, access to land an independent producer, and socialization a possible bearer of collective appropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:ME2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-03","text":"The presupposed time is recursive rather than linear: the origin is reproduced, repeated in the event of disruptions, and driven by its own consequences of accumulation into a possible negation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:SD1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:HSI-04","text":"Struggle concerns control over conditions of labour and possibilities of exit; escape through individual access to land remains possible, but strategic closure requires cooperative common property.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:D13","CH_V4GB_3DMK:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the cluster movement from separation through labour-market formation and self-reproduction to the colonial countertest and possible counter-expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT1","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B02","text":"The system is coherent insofar as capital is consistently treated as a reproduced social relation and expropriation as its generative condition.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT3","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B03","text":"The strongest architecture lies in the double proof through positive genesis and negative countertest: the same access to land whose withdrawal produces the poles of capital dissolves the wage-labouring class when it is available.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT4","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B04","text":"The economic agencies of individual transitions, country-specific deviations, and the concrete causes of the historical failure of Wakefield's programme remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT2","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B05","text":"Terminal counter-expropriation resists complete axiomatic reduction, because its necessity is more strongly theoretically compressed than the historical derivation of the first expropriation.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT8","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement insofar as historical sequence, recursive reproduction, colonial inversion, and terminal branching are not flattened into a linear narrative of origin.","refs":["CH_V4GB_2DSG:MRT9","CH_V4GB_3DMK:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"CL_V4GB_08@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_V4GB_08:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"Chapters 22–23","context":"2) Die s. g. Ursprüngliche Accumulation. · 3) Die moderne Kolonisationstheorie."}},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01","layer":"MC","title":"V4Gb L1 01","order":1,"parents":["CL_V4GB_01","CL_V4GB_02","CL_V4GB_03","CL_V4GB_04"],"revision":"MC_V4GB_L1_01@R001","sha256":"b23447d822d28dfbcc6d281086f000fb12b1fc6a144e1182ae68368f5092707c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-01","text":"Das System löst das Problem, wie nachträglich vergesellschaftete Privatarbeit unter rechtlich äquivalentem Austausch in eine asymmetrische Bewegung übergeht, die lebendige Arbeit erfasst und einen Wertüberschuss produziert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:AS-02","CL_V4GB_02:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-02","text":"Kapital wird auf dieser Ebene als rekursive Organisation gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit bestimmt, deren Wertbewegung nur durch lebendige Arbeit expandiert, ihre Quelle aber als Eigenbewegung des Werts erscheinen lässt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-03","text":"Die Waren- und Geldform erzeugt die sachliche Objektivität, in der gesellschaftliche Allgemeinheit durch Ausschließung konzentriert und ihre soziale Genesis im verselbständigten Resultat ausgelöscht wird.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-04","text":"Weil die Zirkulation Verwertung nur vermittelt, erzwingt ihre kausale Unzulänglichkeit den Übergang zur Arbeitskraft, deren vorab bestimmter Wert von ihrem wertschöpfenden Gebrauch abweicht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:AS-B03","CL_V4GB_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-05","text":"Im Produktionsprozess bewahrt lebendige Arbeit vorhandenen Wert, erzeugt Neuwert und setzt die Wertbildung über die Reproduktion der Arbeitskraft hinaus als Mehrarbeit fort.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:AS-B06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-06","text":"Da die Teilung in notwendige Arbeit und Mehrarbeit keine bestimmte Gesamtdauer erzeugt, wird die quantitative Offenheit des Arbeitstags erst durch kollektiv erzwungene und vollstreckbare Grenzen geschlossen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-07","text":"Sobald die extensive Zeitaneignung auf Grenzen stößt, mutiert Verwertung zur Verkürzung notwendiger Arbeit, zur Kombination vieler Arbeitskräfte und zur Aneignung ihrer emergenten gesellschaftlichen Produktivkraft.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B05","CL_V4GB_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-08","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv, kumulativ und mutationsgetrieben: Jede operative Grenze wird in eine neue Verwertungsstrategie übersetzt, deren Verallgemeinerung weitere Transformationen erzwingt, ohne die Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit aufzuheben.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:AS-05","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Unabhängige Privatarbeit erhält gesellschaftliche Geltung nicht unmittelbar, sondern erst durch sachliche Wertformen und nachträgliche Validierung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Gesellschaftliche Allgemeinheit wird asymmetrisch in einer ausgeschlossenen Äquivalentform konzentriert und erscheint nach erfolgreicher Formbildung als Eigenschaft eines Dings.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-06","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Kapital ist keine ruhende Geld- oder Sachmenge, sondern eine rekursive Wertidentität, die ihre Formen wechselt, sich vergrößert und ihr Resultat erneut vorschießt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:AS-B02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Zirkulation ist notwendige Bedingung der Verwertung, kann Mehrwert aber nur vermitteln; dessen Erzeugung beruht auf der Differenz zwischen Wert und Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Lebendige Arbeit ist die einzige Quelle neuen Werts, während derselbe Arbeitsakt zugleich Gebrauchswerte hervorbringt und vorhandenen Wert überträgt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_04:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Mehrwert entsteht durch die Fortsetzung lebendiger Arbeit über die zur Reproduktion der Arbeitskraft notwendige Zeit hinaus, nicht durch eine Verletzung des Äquivalententauschs.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Rechtliche Selbstverfügung und materielle Trennung von Produktionsbedingungen erzeugen gemeinsam die Form, in der freier Austausch in asymmetrisches Produktionskommando übergeht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Die Bestimmtheit notwendiger Arbeit erzeugt kein immanentes Maß der Gesamtdauer; der Warentausch legitimiert entgegengesetzte Zeitansprüche, ohne zwischen ihnen entscheiden zu können.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","CL_V4GB_03:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Konkurrenz vermittelt die größtmögliche Selbstverwertung als äußeren Zwang, der Einzelkapitale auf fortgesetzte Expansion und Reorganisation der Arbeitszeit festlegt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Eine gesellschaftlich wirksame Arbeitszeitgrenze existiert nur als kollektiv erzwungene, institutionell kontrollierte Schranke, die einen Bereich nicht verkaufter Eigenzeit erzeugt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Grenzen extensiver Mehrwertproduktion erzwingen die Verschiebung zur Verkürzung gesellschaftlich notwendiger Arbeit und zur inneren Umverteilung des Arbeitstags.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","CL_V4GB_04:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Die Konzentration vieler Arbeitskräfte erzeugt neben additiver Wertbildung eine nichtadditive gesellschaftliche Produktivkraft, die ohne besonderes Äquivalent vom Kapital angeeignet wird.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-04","CL_V4GB_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-13","text":"[Attractor] Kapital versucht, notwendige Arbeitszeit, Arbeitskräfte je Produkt und selbständige Prozessverfügung zu vermindern, bleibt aber für jede Wertvermehrung von lebendiger Arbeit abhängig.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-12","CL_V4GB_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Kooperation eröffnet die reale Subsumtion, indem sie gesellschaftliche Arbeitskraft organisatorisch verändert und deren Einheit als fremdes Kapitalkommando verselbständigt, ohne die Abhängigkeit des Kapitals aufzulösen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CL_V4GB_04:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-01","text":"Wert bewahrt seine Identität als vergegenständlichte abstrakte Arbeit, mutiert aber von einer relational dargestellten Eigenschaft zum rekursiv prozessierenden Zweck der Kapitalbewegung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:RMD-01","CL_V4GB_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-02","text":"Geld wandert von der ideellen, symbolischen und materiellen Wertgestalt zur Erscheinungsform eines Werts, dessen Identität nur noch in seinem vergrößerten Formwechsel besteht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-03","text":"Arbeitskraft mutiert von der gekauften Marktware über lebendige Arbeit und variables Kapital zum Organ eines funktional gegliederten Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-02","CL_V4GB_04:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-04","text":"Gebrauchswert wird vom ausgeschlossenen Wertgrund zur entscheidenden Differenz der Arbeitskraft und zum stofflichen Medium von Werterhaltung, Neuwertbildung und Verwertung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-05","text":"Zeit erweitert sich vom Wertmaß über Reproduktionsschwelle und umkämpfte Arbeitstagsgrenze bis zur synchronisierten Zeit eines gesellschaftlichen Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_03:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_04:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-06","text":"Freiheit kehrt ihre Valenz um: Formale Vertragsfreiheit ermöglicht asymmetrische Verfügung, während zwingende kollektive Begrenzung erst materielle Eigenzeit hervorbringt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-05","CL_V4GB_03:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-07","text":"Konstantes Kapital bleibt als Quelle neuen Werts ausgeschlossen, kehrt jedoch als materielle Konzentrations-, Nutzungs-, Organisations- und Kommandobedingung der Mehrwertproduktion wieder.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GNX-02","CL_V4GB_04:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-08","text":"Kooperation bleibt sachlich die Verbindung vieler Arbeiten, wird aber unter kapitalistischen Eigentumsbedingungen in fremdes Kommando und scheinbare Kapitalproduktivität umgekehrt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RMD-04","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-01","text":"Die einzelnen Entwicklungsstufen der Wertform verbleiben als lokaler Ableitungsapparat; auf die aktuelle Ebene skaliert die Notwendigkeit sachlicher und nachträglicher Vergesellschaftung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:CGD-02","CL_V4GB_01:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-02","text":"Die besonderen Geldfunktionen bleiben lokale Daseinsweisen; höherstufig tragend wird erst ihr Übergang in die rekursive Identität eines formwechselnden Kapitalwerts.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:CGD-05","CL_V4GB_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-03","text":"Buchhalterische Wertzerlegung und Mehrwertformeln bleiben lokale Messapparate; auf der aktuellen Ebene werden sie zu Elementen einer Skalierung durch Arbeitszeit, Arbeitskräftezahl und Kombinationskraft.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:CGD-01","CL_V4GB_04:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-04","text":"Technische Einzelbestimmungen des Arbeitsprozesses verbleiben unten; nach oben skaliert die Trennung zwischen stofflicher Produktivität, Wertwirkung und nichtadditiver gesellschaftlicher Kooperation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:CGD-02","CL_V4GB_04:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-05","text":"Die historische Erzeugung des produktionsmittellosen Arbeitskraftverkäufers bleibt vorausgesetzt und genealogisch unterbestimmt, obwohl sie für die gesamte Kapitalarchitektur unverzichtbar ist.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:CGD-04","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-06","text":"Nationale Gesetzesformen skalieren nicht als einheitliches Modell; global bleibt ihre Funktion als umkämpfte, vollstreckbare und gegen Umgehung revidierbare Reproduktionsgrenze erhalten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:CGD-03","CL_V4GB_03:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-07","text":"Individueller Extra-Mehrwert bleibt eine vorübergehende Abweichung; höherstufig wirksam ist die Konkurrenzschleife, die Sondervorteile verallgemeinert und in neue gesellschaftliche Normen überführt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:CGD-06","CL_V4GB_04:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-01","text":"Wert darf weder aus Nützlichkeit und Stofflichkeit noch aus isolierter Dingnatur abgeleitet werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-02","text":"Äquivalententausch und bloße Zirkulation können keinen gesellschaftlichen Mehrwert erzeugen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-03","text":"Produktionsmittel, Technik und totes Kapital können vorhandenen Wert übertragen, aber keine autonome Quelle neuen Werts bilden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GNX-02","CL_V4GB_04:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-04","text":"Rechtliche Gleichheit darf nicht als vollständige Bestimmung des Kapitalverhältnisses oder als Garantie realer Verfügung über die eigene Arbeitszeit gelten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:DBN-01","CL_V4GB_03:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-05","text":"Weder Naturgrenzen noch Markt, Privatmoral oder Konkurrenz erzeugen aus sich einen bestimmten und reproduktionsgerechten Normalarbeitstag.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-06","text":"Produktivitätssteigerung ist weder mit freier Zeit identisch noch rechtfertigt der allgemeine Koordinationsbedarf kapitalistisches Eigentum und despotische Leitung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GNX-03","CL_V4GB_04:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-01","text":"Damit die Architektur Bestand hat, darf Privatarbeit nicht unmittelbar gesellschaftlich sein; eine direkte Beziehung der Produzenten würde Warenwert, Marktvalidierung und Geldvermittlung entbehrlich machen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:DBN-01","CL_V4GB_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-02","text":"Kapital darf weder als statischer Besitz noch als autonomes Subjekt behandelt werden, weil seine Identität nur in der reproduzierten Kopplung von Zirkulation, Eigentum und lebendiger Arbeit besteht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:DBN-01","CL_V4GB_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-03","text":"Ein harmonisches Marktmodell und eine stabile Trennung ökonomischer von politischer Herrschaft müssen falsch sein, weil Austauschgleichheit die zerstörerische Nutzung der Arbeitskraft weder verhindert noch begrenzt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-02","CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-04","text":"Technik, industrielle Leitung und gesellschaftliche Koordination dürfen nicht als wert-, herrschafts- oder eigentumsneutrale Einheit auftreten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:DBN-02","CL_V4GB_04:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-05","text":"Ein atomistisches Modell selbständiger Arbeitskraftverkäufer ist ausgeschlossen, weil Kombination eine zusätzliche gesellschaftliche Produktivkraft erzeugt und die Produzenten in einen fremd geleiteten Gesamtarbeiter verwandelt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:DBN-03","CL_V4GB_04:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste Abwesenheit ist eine unmittelbare Assoziation der Produzenten, in der gesellschaftliche Arbeit ohne sachliche Wertvermittlung organisiert wird.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_04:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-02","text":"Eigenzeit ist nicht vorpolitisch verfügbar; sie muss durch Begrenzung der Verkaufszeit erzeugt werden, während eingesparte notwendige Arbeit sonst erneut als Mehrarbeit erscheint.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:BSA-02","CL_V4GB_04:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-03","text":"Strukturell abwesend bleibt der Gesamtarbeiter als Eigentümer, Leiter und Nutznießer der von ihm erzeugten Kombinationskraft, die stattdessen als kostenlose Eigenkraft des Kapitals erscheint.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_04:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-04","text":"Ontologisch unzulässig ist ein Kapital, das lebendige Arbeit vollständig beseitigt und dennoch als sich verwertender Wert fortbesteht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:BSA-04","CL_V4GB_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-01","text":"Die Geldform stellt die gesellschaftliche Objektivität bereit, in der Wert seine Träger wechseln und als rekursive Kapitalidentität durch Zirkulation und Produktion fortbestehen kann; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-02","text":"Die scheinbare Selbstbewegung des Kapitals ist die gesteigerte Form des Geldfetischs: Die Auslöschung gesellschaftlicher Genesis wird nun durch die Einverleibung lebendiger Arbeit reproduziert; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CL_V4GB_02:XD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-03","text":"Nachträgliche Marktvalidierung und gesellschaftlich notwendige Arbeitszeit verbinden Zirkulation mit Produktionsdisziplin, indem sie private Verausgabung zugleich anerkennen, normieren und revidieren; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CL_V4GB_02:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-04","text":"Die allgemeine Rechtsform des Warenbesitzers wird beim Arbeitskraftkauf zur Bedingung einer asymmetrischen Verfügung, weil Selbstverfügung mit materieller Produktionsmittellosigkeit gekoppelt ist; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:XD-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-05","text":"Sobald lebendige Arbeit als Mehrwertquelle isoliert ist, verwandelt die offene Dauer der Mehrarbeit eine werttheoretische Differenz in einen gesellschaftlichen Konflikt um Lebenszeit; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-06","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-06","text":"Die politische Begrenzung absoluter Mehrarbeit beseitigt den Verwertungszwang nicht, sondern verschiebt ihn auf Produktivität, relative Mehrwertproduktion und kooperative Reorganisation; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:XD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-07","text":"Die Warenförmigkeit individueller Arbeitskräfte lässt die im Produktionsprozess erzeugte Kombinationskraft außerhalb des expliziten Äquivalents entstehen und deshalb als natürliche Produktivität des Kapitals erscheinen; Trace Type — Negative.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:XD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-08","text":"Konkurrenz transformiert individuelle Produktivitätsabweichung in gesellschaftliche Norm, hebt den Sondervorteil auf und erneuert dadurch den Zwang zu technischer und organisatorischer Veränderung; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B07","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-03","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-01","text":"Gesellschaftliche Objektivität ist weder Natur noch Konvention, sondern eine relationale Prozesswirklichkeit, die sich als Wert, Geld und Kapital gegen ihre Produzenten verselbständigt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-01","CL_V4GB_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird seriell dezentriert: Es erscheint als Warenbesitzer, Funktionsträger, kontrollierter Arbeitskraftträger, Organ des Gesamtarbeiters und mögliches kollektives Gegensubjekt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-03","text":"Kapitalistische Zeit ist zugleich nachträglich, rekursiv, schwellenförmig, antagonistisch und synchronisierend: Sie validiert vergangene Arbeit, teilt den Arbeitstag und verdichtet individuelle Zeiten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_02:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-04","text":"Kausalität wird mehrschichtig: Demographie begrenzt Arbeitsmassen, Eigentum ermöglicht Kommando, lebendige Arbeit erzeugt Neuwert, Technik verändert notwendige Zeit und Konkurrenz verallgemeinert lokale Veränderungen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:BSD-05","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-05","text":"Politik ist kein äußerer Zusatz zur Ökonomie, weil ökonomische Zeitaneignung rechtliche Form, organisierte Gegenmacht und staatliche Vollstreckung benötigt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_03:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnis verlangt die genetische Trennung von Wertbildung, Gebrauchswertproduktivität, Geldfunktion, Zeitmaß, technischer Koordination und kapitalistischer Herrschaft.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-06","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-07","text":"Strategische Intervention richtet sich auf Produktionsvermittlung, Verfügung über gesellschaftliche Kombination und Rückgewinnung frei werdender Zeit, nicht auf moralische Geldkritik oder isolierte Vertragskorrektur.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-01","text":"Privatarbeit erzeugt Waren, Austausch validiert Privatarbeit, Wert kehrt als Kapitalvorschuss zurück, und der vergrößerte Rückfluss erneuert die Bedingungen unabhängiger Produktion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:RLE-01","CL_V4GB_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-02","text":"Gesellschaftliche Vermittlung kristallisiert sachlich, löscht ihre Genesis aus, erscheint als Kapitalproduktivität und bestätigt dadurch scheinbar die Notwendigkeit des Kapitalkommandos.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:XD-06","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-03","text":"Wertvorschuss → Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft → Mehrwert → vergrößerter Rückfluss → erneuter Vorschuss bildet die zentrale Verwertungsschleife.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-04","text":"Wertzerlegung → Zeitzerlegung → offene Gesamtdauer → Rechtsantinomie → Klassenkampf → institutionelle Grenze bildet den Eskalationspfad absoluter Mehrwertproduktion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RLE-01","CL_V4GB_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-05","text":"Überarbeit erzeugt Widerstand, Widerstand erzeugt Gesetz, Gesetz erzeugt Umgehung, und Umgehung erzwingt präzisere Kontrolle sowie erneute Verallgemeinerung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RLE-04","CL_V4GB_03:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-06","text":"Endliche Arbeitstagsausdehnung → Verkürzung notwendiger Arbeit → Produktivitätsinnovation → Extra-Mehrwert → Konkurrenzverallgemeinerung → erneuter Innovationszwang bildet die relative Mehrwertschleife.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RLE-02","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-07","text":"Kapitalkonzentration erzeugt Kooperation, Kooperation erhöht Produktivität und Koordinationsbedarf, antagonistische Leitung verstärkt Aufsicht, und verselbständigtes Kommando begünstigt weitere Konzentration.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RLE-04","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-08","text":"Der dominante Attraktor ist die maximale Aneignung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit unter gleichzeitiger Verminderung der für ihre Reproduktion erforderlichen Zeit; seine unaufhebbare Grenze bleibt die Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RLE-07","CL_V4GB_04:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B01","text":"Unabhängige Privatarbeit → privates Arbeitsprodukt → Austauschzwang → abstrakte Gleichsetzung → Wertobjektivität → allgemeines Äquivalent.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B02","text":"Allgemeines Äquivalent → Geldfunktionen → Formwechsel des Werts → rekursive Wertidentität → Geld als Kapital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B03","text":"Unzulänglichkeit der Zirkulation + rechtliche Selbstverfügung + materielle Produktionsmittellosigkeit → Arbeitskraft als besondere Ware.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B04","text":"Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft → konkreter Arbeitsprozess + abstrakte Wertbildung → Übertragung alten Werts + Erzeugung neuen Werts.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B05","text":"Neuwert → Reproduktion des Arbeitskraftwerts + Fortsetzung der Arbeit → Mehrarbeit → Mehrwert → erneuter Kapitalvorschuss.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CL_V4GB_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B06","text":"Bestimmte notwendige Arbeit + unbestimmte Mehrarbeitsdauer → entgegengesetzte Rechtsansprüche → Kräfteentscheidung → vollstreckbare Arbeitstagsgrenze.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B07","text":"Grenze absoluter Mehrarbeit → Verkürzung notwendiger Arbeit → Produktivitätssteigerung → Senkung des Arbeitskraftwerts → relative Mehrarbeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","CL_V4GB_04:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B08","text":"Kapitalkonzentration → gleichzeitige Beschäftigung vieler Arbeitskräfte → Gesamtarbeiter → emergente Kombinationskraft → Aneignung ohne besonderes Äquivalent → Kapitalkommando → reale Subsumtion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AFM-B01","text":"Privatarbeit → Warenwert → Geld → Kapitalbewegung → Arbeitskraft → Produktionsprozess → Mehrarbeit → Mehrwert → erneuter Vorschuss → erweiterte Erfassung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:AS-04","CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AFM-B02","text":"Äquivalenter Vertrag → asymmetrischer Gebrauch → offene Mehrarbeitsdauer → Rechtsantinomie → Klassenbildung → vollstreckbare Begrenzung → Eigenzeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:XD-08","CL_V4GB_03:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AFM-B03","text":"Grenze extensiver Verwertung → relative Mehrwertstrategie → Produktivitätsvorsprung → Konkurrenzverallgemeinerung → Kooperation → fremdes Kommando → reale Subsumtion → erneute Transformation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B05","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-01","text":"Der Gegensatz von intrinsischer Dingqualität und willkürlicher Konvention wird durch gesellschaftlich-relationale Objektivität ersetzt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-02","text":"Kapital wird von einer Geld- oder Sachmenge zu einer rekursiven Einrichtung der Erfassung, Kombination und Umverteilung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit umkartiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-03","text":"Marktgleichheit und Produktionskommando erscheinen nicht länger als unvereinbare Beschreibungen, sondern als aufeinanderfolgende Ebenen derselben Aneignungsrelation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MME-02","CL_V4GB_04:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-04","text":"Ausbeutung wird in Quelle, proportionale Rate, absolute Dauer und organisatorische Aneignung gesellschaftlicher Produktivkraft zerlegt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:MME-02","CL_V4GB_04:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-05","text":"Gebrauchswertproduktivität, Wertbildung und freie Zeit werden entkoppelt; technische oder kooperative Steigerung kann Mehrwert erhöhen, ohne den Wert je Arbeitsstunde zu vermehren.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:DBN-05","CL_V4GB_04:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-06","text":"Die Trennung ökonomischer und politischer Sphäre bricht zusammen, weil Arbeitszeitaneignung rechtlich eröffnet, kollektiv bekämpft und institutionell begrenzt wird.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_03:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-07","text":"Individuelle Vertragsfreiheit wird als abhängige Oberflächenform reklassifiziert, während kollektive Begrenzung und mögliche Selbstorganisation die materielle Dimension von Freiheit bilden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RMD-06","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B01","text":"Auf der Oberflächenebene verbindet das System Ware, Geld, Arbeitskraft, Mehrwertrate, Arbeitstag, relativen Mehrwert und Kooperation als aufeinander bezogene Erscheinungsformen der Verwertung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B01","CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B02","text":"Auf der strukturellen Ebene koppeln sachliche Vermittlung, Eigentum, Produktionskontrolle, Zeitteilung, Konkurrenz und Kooperation unabhängige Arbeit an die rekursive Reproduktion von Kapital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B02","CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B03","text":"Auf der metastrategischen Ebene verschiebt sich Intervention von Geldkritik und individuellem Vertrag auf Prozessstellung, Arbeitszeitgrenzen, Produktionsbedingungen und Verfügung über gesellschaftliche Kombination.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B03","CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B04","text":"Auf der ontologisch-temporalen Ebene steht endliche, reproduktionsbedürftige Lebenskraft einem abstrakten Wertprozess gegenüber, der Zeit validiert, teilt, synchronisiert und fremd aneignet.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B05","text":"Auf der methodologisch-performativen Ebene vollzieht die Darstellung die behauptete Bewegung, indem sie Erscheinungsformen genetisch zurückführt, quantitative Formeln in gesellschaftliche Relationen überführt und operative Lösungen als neue Widerspruchsstufen rekonstruiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B05","CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-01","text":"Abstrakte Arbeit bleibt zwischen allgemein menschlicher Verausgabung und spezifischer gesellschaftlicher Geltungsform gespannt, während ihre Wertbestimmung erst nachträglich praktisch validiert wird; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:FL-02","CL_V4GB_01:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-02","text":"Die Darstellung des Kapitals als automatisches Subjekt kollidiert mit seiner vollständigen Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit; die Verselbständigung ist real wirksam, aber nicht selbstgenügsam; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:FL-01","CL_V4GB_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-03","text":"Die Voraussetzung des wertgerechten Arbeitskraftkaufs destabilisiert sich, sobald gegenwärtige Nutzung die Lebensdauer und künftige Reproduzierbarkeit der Ware selbst vermindert; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:XD-04","CL_V4GB_03:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-04","text":"Der Staat erscheint zugleich als Medium bestehender Eigentumsordnung und als notwendige Vollstreckungsinstanz ihrer Begrenzung; der institutionelle Umschlag bleibt unterbestimmt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-05","text":"Die Bindung übertragener Werte an produktiven Verschleiß steht unter Spannung zur gegenwärtigen Revaluation noch brauchbarer Produktionsmittel; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-06","text":"Die Ableitung relativen Mehrwerts setzt voraus, dass verbilligte Reproduktionsmittel den Arbeitskraftwert tatsächlich senken; der soziale Übertragungsmechanismus bleibt unvollständig bestimmt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-07","text":"Additive Wertbildung und nichtadditive Kooperationsproduktivität bleiben nur vereinbar, wenn Gebrauchswertnutzen, potenzierte individuelle Leistung und gesellschaftliche Durchschnittsarbeit strikt getrennt werden; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-01","text":"Geld mutiert zur Kapitalform, sobald seine Identität nicht mehr in einer ruhenden Gestalt, sondern in rekursiv vergrößertem Formwechsel liegt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-02","text":"Gebrauchswert mutiert vom ausgeschlossenen Grund des Werts zur besonderen Wertschöpfungskapazität der Arbeitskraft und zum Medium der Wertübertragung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-03","text":"Arbeitskraft mutiert von einer verkauften Fähigkeit über lebendige Arbeit zum variablen Kapital und schließlich zu einer Ware, deren Gebrauch ihren Träger verändert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MP-03","CL_V4GB_03:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-04","text":"Zeit mutiert von Zirkulationswiederholung und Wertmaß zur Produktionsschwelle, umkämpften Grenze und synchronisierten Zeit des Gesamtarbeiters.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MP-04","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-05","text":"Recht und Freiheit mutieren von der Besiegelung individuellen Austauschs zur kollektiv erzwungenen Gegengewalt gegen dessen zeitliche Resultate.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RMD-05","CL_V4GB_03:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-06","text":"Konstantes Kapital mutiert vom bloßen Wertüberträger zur konzentrierten Organisations- und Kommandobedingung, ohne dadurch selbst Quelle neuen Werts zu werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:FL-01","CL_V4GB_04:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-01","text":"Die Realität erscheint als gekoppelte Validierungs- und Verwertungsmaschine, in der gesellschaftliche Beziehungen in Dingen kristallisieren und gegenständliche Bedingungen lebendige Arbeitskräfte sammeln.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-01","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist zunächst Träger einer ökonomischen Funktion und wird im Produktionsprozess zum abhängigen Organ eines gesellschaftlichen Arbeitskörpers, dessen Einheit ihm als fremde Macht gegenübertritt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-02","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-03","text":"Zeit ist rückwirkend, endlich, teilbar und synchronisierbar: Kapital kann sie nicht erzeugen, sondern nur validieren, verlängern, umverteilen, verdichten und aneignen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-03","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-04","text":"Kampf besteht in der Umkehrung der Zeitmessung zur Grenzforderung und in der möglichen Rückgewinnung gesellschaftlicher Kombination durch den selbstorganisierten Gesamtarbeiter.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B01","text":"Die Architektur ist auf dieser Ebene hinreichend rekonstruierbar, wenn Wertform, rekursive Kapitalbewegung, besondere Ware Arbeitskraft, Mehrarbeitszeit, politische Grenzsetzung und angeeignete Kooperationskraft gemeinsam erhalten bleiben.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B02","text":"Ihre stärkste Struktur liegt in der Verbindung von sachlicher Wertobjektivität, kausaler Isolierung lebendiger Arbeit, zeitlicher Exploitation und organisatorischer Aneignung gesellschaftlicher Produktivität.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B04","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B03","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die praktische Durchsetzung bestimmter Geld- und Eigentumsordnungen, die institutionelle Transformation von Klassenmacht, die konkrete Arbeitszeitgrenze und die Übertragung von Produktivitätsgewinnen in gesunkenen Arbeitskraftwert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B04","text":"Die Kohärenz hängt davon ab, Gebrauchswert und Wert, Arbeitsprozess und Verwertungsprozess, Wertbildung und Produktivität sowie Koordination und Kommando zugleich zu verbinden und strikt zu unterscheiden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B05","text":"Die tatsächliche Bewegung wird nur bewahrt, wenn die Rekonstruktion vom Scheitern zirkulatorischer Erklärungen über Zeitkonflikt und Grenzsetzung zu Produktivitätsmutation, Konkurrenzverallgemeinerung und realer Subsumtion fortschreitet.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B06","text":"Axiomatischer Reduktion widerstehen die praktischen Umschläge, durch die Gesellschaft eine Geldform stabilisiert, Arbeitskraft tatsächlich validiert, historische Grenzen institutionell fixiert und Kooperation zugleich als Produktivkraft und fremde Kapitalmacht realisiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B06","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T212147913557Z_5e849220","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"V4Gb L1 01","source_sha256":"b23447d822d28dfbcc6d281086f000fb12b1fc6a144e1182ae68368f5092707c","sha256":"2153fe2a9f9c3eef7e849e619caed4b5bdf7abd58e23e92ee23a37ccae12e6d7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:21:47.914580+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-01","text":"The system resolves the problem of how subsequently socialized private labour, under legally equivalent exchange, passes into an asymmetrical movement that seizes living labour and produces a surplus of value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:AS-02","CL_V4GB_02:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-02","text":"At this level, capital is determined as the recursive organization of social labour-time, whose movement of value expands only through living labour, but makes its source appear as the self-movement of value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-03","text":"The commodity and money form produces the objective reality in which social universality is concentrated through exclusion and its social genesis is erased in the autonomized result.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-05","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-04","text":"Because circulation only mediates valorization, its causal insufficiency compels the transition to labour-power, whose pre-determined value diverges from its value-creating use.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:AS-B03","CL_V4GB_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-05","text":"In the production process, living labour preserves existing value, creates new value, and continues value formation beyond the reproduction of labour-power as surplus labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:AS-B06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-06","text":"Since the division into necessary labour and surplus labour produces no determinate total duration, the quantitative openness of the working day is closed only by collectively enforced and enforceable limits.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-07","text":"As soon as extensive appropriation of time encounters limits, valorization mutates into the shortening of necessary labour, the combination of many labour-powers, and the appropriation of their emergent social productive force.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B05","CL_V4GB_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-08","text":"The movement is recursive, cumulative, and mutation-driven: every operational limit is translated into a new strategy of valorization, whose generalization compels further transformations without abolishing dependence on living labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:AS-05","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Independent private labour receives social validity not directly, but only through objective forms of value and subsequent validation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Social universality is asymmetrically concentrated in an excluded equivalent form and, after successful form-formation, appears as a property of a thing.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-06","CL_V4GB_01:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Capital is not a static quantity of money or things, but a recursive identity of value that changes its forms, enlarges itself, and advances its result anew.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:AS-B02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Circulation is a necessary condition of valorization, but can only mediate surplus-value; its production rests on the difference between the value and use of labour-power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Living labour is the sole source of new value, while the same act of labour simultaneously produces use-values and transfers existing value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_04:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Surplus-value arises through the continuation of living labour beyond the time necessary for the reproduction of labour-power, not through a violation of equivalent exchange.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Legal self-disposal and material separation from conditions of production jointly produce the form in which free exchange passes into asymmetrical command over production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] The determinacy of necessary labour produces no immanent measure of total duration; commodity exchange legitimates opposing claims to time without being able to decide between them.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-04","CL_V4GB_03:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Competition mediates the greatest possible self-valorization as an external compulsion that commits individual capitals to continued expansion and reorganization of labour-time.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] A socially effective limit to labour-time exists only as a collectively enforced, institutionally controlled barrier that produces a sphere of un-sold time of one's own.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Limits to extensive surplus-value production compel the shift toward shortening socially necessary labour and toward the internal redistribution of the working day.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","CL_V4GB_04:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] The concentration of many labour-powers produces, alongside additive value formation, a non-additive social productive force that is appropriated by capital without a special equivalent.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-04","CL_V4GB_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-13","text":"[Attractor] Capital seeks to reduce necessary labour-time, labour-powers per product, and independent disposition over the process, but remains dependent on living labour for every increase of value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-12","CL_V4GB_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Cooperation opens real subsumption by organizationally transforming social labour-power and autonomizing its unity as alien capital-command, without dissolving capital's dependence.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-14","CL_V4GB_04:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-01","text":"Value preserves its identity as objectified abstract labour, but mutates from a relationally represented property into the recursively processing purpose of the movement of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:RMD-01","CL_V4GB_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-02","text":"Money moves from the ideal, symbolic, and material form of value to the form of appearance of a value whose identity consists only in its enlarged change of form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-03","text":"Labour-power mutates from the purchased market commodity through living labour and variable capital into the organ of a functionally articulated collective worker.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-02","CL_V4GB_04:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-04","text":"Use-value becomes, from the excluded ground of value, the decisive difference of labour-power and the material medium of value preservation, new-value formation, and valorization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-05","text":"Time expands from the measure of value through the threshold of reproduction and the contested limit of the working day to the synchronized time of a social collective worker.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_03:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_04:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-06","text":"Freedom reverses its valence: formal contractual freedom enables asymmetrical disposal, while compulsory collective limitation first brings forth material time of one's own.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-05","CL_V4GB_03:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-07","text":"Constant capital remains excluded as a source of new value, but returns as the material condition of concentration, use, organization, and command in surplus-value production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GNX-02","CL_V4GB_04:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-08","text":"Cooperation remains objectively the connection of many labours, but under capitalist conditions of property is reversed into alien command and apparent capital productivity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RMD-04","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-01","text":"The individual stages of development of the value-form remain a local apparatus of derivation; what scales to the current level is the necessity of objective and subsequent socialization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:CGD-02","CL_V4GB_01:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-02","text":"The particular functions of money remain local modes of existence; what becomes structurally decisive at the higher level is their transition into the recursive identity of a capital-value changing forms.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:CGD-05","CL_V4GB_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-03","text":"Accounting decomposition of value and surplus-value formulas remain local measuring apparatuses; at the current level, they become elements of a scaling through labour-time, number of labour-powers, and combinatory force.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:CGD-01","CL_V4GB_04:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-04","text":"Technical determinations of the individual labour process remain below; what scales upward is the separation between material productivity, effects on value, and non-additive social cooperation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:CGD-02","CL_V4GB_04:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-05","text":"The historical production of the labour-power seller deprived of means of production remains presupposed and genealogically underdetermined, although it is indispensable to the entire architecture of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:CGD-04","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-06","text":"National legal forms do not scale as a uniform model; globally, their function remains as a contested, enforceable, and revisable limit of reproduction against evasion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:CGD-03","CL_V4GB_03:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-07","text":"Individual extra surplus-value remains a temporary deviation; effective at the higher level is the loop of competition that generalizes special advantages and transfers them into new social norms.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:CGD-06","CL_V4GB_04:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-01","text":"Value must be derived neither from utility and materiality nor from an isolated nature of things.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-02","text":"Equivalent exchange and mere circulation cannot generate any social surplus-value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-03","text":"Means of production, technology, and dead capital can transfer existing value, but cannot constitute an autonomous source of new value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GNX-02","CL_V4GB_04:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-04","text":"Legal equality must not count as a complete determination of the capital relation or as a guarantee of real disposal over one's own labour-time.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:DBN-01","CL_V4GB_03:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-05","text":"Neither natural limits nor the market, private morality, or competition produce from themselves a determinate normal working day adequate to reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-06","text":"An increase in productivity is neither identical with free time, nor does the general need for coordination justify capitalist property and despotic direction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GNX-03","CL_V4GB_04:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to endure, private labour must not be immediately social; a direct relation among producers would render commodity value, market validation, and monetary mediation superfluous.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:DBN-01","CL_V4GB_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-02","text":"Capital must be treated neither as static possession nor as an autonomous subject, because its identity consists only in the reproduced coupling of circulation, property, and living labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:DBN-01","CL_V4GB_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-03","text":"A harmonious market model and a stable separation of economic from political domination must be false, because equality in exchange neither prevents nor limits the destructive use of labour-power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-02","CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-04","text":"Technology, industrial direction, and social coordination must not appear as a unity neutral with respect to value, domination, or property.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:DBN-02","CL_V4GB_04:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-05","text":"An atomistic model of independent sellers of labour-power is excluded because combination produces an additional social productive force and transforms producers into a collectively working body directed by another.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:DBN-03","CL_V4GB_04:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is an immediate association of producers in which social labour is organized without objective value mediation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_04:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-02","text":"Time of one's own is not available pre-politically; it must be produced through the limitation of sale-time, while saved necessary labour otherwise reappears as surplus labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:BSA-02","CL_V4GB_04:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-03","text":"Structurally absent remains the collective worker as owner, director, and beneficiary of the combinatory force it produces, which instead appears as capital's gratuitous power of its own.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_04:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-04","text":"Ontologically inadmissible is a capital that completely abolishes living labour and yet persists as self-valorizing value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:BSA-04","CL_V4GB_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-01","text":"The money form provides the social objectivity in which value can change its bearers and persist as a recursive capital identity through circulation and production; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-02","text":"The apparent self-movement of capital is the intensified form of money fetishism: the erasure of social genesis is now reproduced through the incorporation of living labour; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CL_V4GB_02:XD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-03","text":"Subsequent market validation and socially necessary labour-time connect circulation with production discipline by simultaneously recognizing, standardizing, and revising private expenditure; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-07","CL_V4GB_02:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-04","text":"The general legal form of the commodity owner becomes, in the purchase of labour-power, the condition of asymmetrical disposal, because self-disposal is coupled with material lack of means of production; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-04","CL_V4GB_02:XD-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-05","text":"Once living labour is isolated as the source of surplus-value, the open duration of surplus labour transforms a difference in value theory into a social conflict over lifetime; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-02","CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-06","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-06","text":"The political limitation of absolute surplus labour does not abolish the compulsion to valorize, but shifts it onto productivity, relative surplus-value production, and cooperative reorganization; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:XD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-07","text":"The commodity character of individual labour-powers allows the combinatory force produced in the production process to arise outside the explicit equivalent and therefore to appear as the natural productivity of capital; Trace Type — Negative.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:XD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-08","text":"Competition transforms individual deviations in productivity into a social norm, abolishes the special advantage, and thereby renews the compulsion to technical and organizational change; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B07","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-03","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-01","text":"Social objectivity is neither nature nor convention, but a relational process-reality that autonomizes itself as value, money, and capital against its producers.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-01","CL_V4GB_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-02","text":"The subject is serially decentered: it appears as commodity owner, functionary, controlled bearer of labour-power, organ of the collective worker, and possible collective counter-subject.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-03","text":"Capitalist time is simultaneously subsequent, recursive, threshold-like, antagonistic, and synchronizing: it validates past labour, divides the working day, and condenses individual times.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_02:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes multilayered: demography limits masses of labour, property enables command, living labour creates new value, technology alters necessary time, and competition generalizes local changes.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:BSD-05","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-05","text":"Politics is not an external addition to economics, because economic appropriation of time requires legal form, organized counter-power, and state enforcement.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_03:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-06","text":"Cognition requires the genetic separation of value formation, use-value productivity, money function, measure of time, technical coordination, and capitalist domination.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-06","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-07","text":"Strategic intervention is directed toward mediation of production, disposal over social combination, and recovery of time becoming free, not toward moral critique of money or isolated correction of contracts.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-01","text":"Private labour produces commodities, exchange validates private labour, value returns as an advance of capital, and the enlarged reflux renews the conditions of independent production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:RLE-01","CL_V4GB_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-02","text":"Social mediation crystallizes objectively, erases its genesis, appears as capital productivity, and thereby seemingly confirms the necessity of capital-command.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:XD-06","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-03","text":"Advance of value → use of labour-power → surplus-value → enlarged reflux → renewed advance forms the central valorization loop.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-04","text":"Value decomposition → time decomposition → open total duration → legal antinomy → class struggle → institutional limit forms the escalation path of absolute surplus-value production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RLE-01","CL_V4GB_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-05","text":"Overwork produces resistance, resistance produces law, law produces evasion, and evasion compels more precise control as well as renewed generalization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RLE-04","CL_V4GB_03:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-06","text":"Finite extension of the working day → shortening of necessary labour → productivity innovation → extra surplus-value → competitive generalization → renewed compulsion to innovate forms the relative surplus-value loop.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RLE-02","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-07","text":"Concentration of capital produces cooperation, cooperation increases productivity and the need for coordination, antagonistic direction intensifies supervision, and autonomized command favours further concentration.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RLE-04","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-08","text":"The dominant attractor is the maximal appropriation of social labour-time together with the reduction of the time required for its reproduction; its unabolishable limit remains dependence on living labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:RLE-07","CL_V4GB_04:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B01","text":"Independent private labour → private product of labour → compulsion to exchange → abstract equation → value-objectivity → general equivalent.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-01","CL_V4GB_01:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B02","text":"General equivalent → money functions → change of form of value → recursive identity of value → money as capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:GA-08","CL_V4GB_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B03","text":"Insufficiency of circulation + legal self-disposal + material lack of means of production → labour-power as a special commodity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-02","CL_V4GB_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B04","text":"Use of labour-power → concrete labour process + abstract value formation → transfer of old value + production of new value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B05","text":"New value → reproduction of the value of labour-power + continuation of labour → surplus labour → surplus-value → renewed advance of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:GA-08","CL_V4GB_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B06","text":"Determinate necessary labour + indeterminate duration of surplus labour → opposing legal claims → decision by force → enforceable limit of the working day.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:GA-05","CL_V4GB_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B07","text":"Limit of absolute surplus labour → shortening of necessary labour → increase in productivity → reduction of the value of labour-power → relative surplus labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-03","CL_V4GB_04:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FGS-B08","text":"Concentration of capital → simultaneous employment of many labour-powers → collective worker → emergent combinatory force → appropriation without a special equivalent → capital-command → real subsumption.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:GA-08","CL_V4GB_04:GA-09","CL_V4GB_04:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AFM-B01","text":"Private labour → commodity value → money → movement of capital → labour-power → production process → surplus labour → surplus-value → renewed advance → extended seizure of social labour-time.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:AS-04","CL_V4GB_02:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AFM-B02","text":"Equivalent contract → asymmetrical use → open duration of surplus labour → legal antinomy → class formation → enforceable limitation → time of one's own.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:XD-08","CL_V4GB_03:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:AFM-B03","text":"Limit of extensive valorization → strategy of relative surplus-value → productivity advantage → competitive generalization → cooperation → alien command → real subsumption → renewed transformation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:AS-B05","CL_V4GB_04:RLE-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-01","text":"The opposition between intrinsic quality of things and arbitrary convention is replaced by socially relational objectivity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-02","text":"Capital is remapped from a quantity of money or things into a recursive apparatus for the seizure, combination, and redistribution of social labour-time.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-03","text":"Market equality and command over production no longer appear as incompatible descriptions, but as successive levels of the same relation of appropriation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MME-02","CL_V4GB_04:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-04","text":"Exploitation is decomposed into source, proportional rate, absolute duration, and organizational appropriation of social productive force.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:MME-02","CL_V4GB_04:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-05","text":"Use-value productivity, value formation, and free time are decoupled; a technical or cooperative increase can raise surplus-value without increasing value per hour of labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:DBN-05","CL_V4GB_04:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-06","text":"The separation of economic and political spheres collapses because the appropriation of labour-time is legally enabled, collectively contested, and institutionally limited.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_03:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-07","text":"Individual contractual freedom is reclassified as a dependent surface form, while collective limitation and possible self-organization constitute the material dimension of freedom.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RMD-06","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the system connects commodity, money, labour-power, the rate of surplus-value, the working day, relative surplus-value, and cooperation as interrelated forms of appearance of valorization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B01","CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, objective mediation, property, control of production, division of time, competition, and cooperation couple independent labour to the recursive reproduction of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B02","CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B03","text":"At the meta-strategic level, intervention shifts from critique of money and the individual contract to position in the process, limits on labour-time, conditions of production, and disposal over social combination.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:ALT-B03","CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, finite life-force in need of reproduction confronts an abstract value-process that validates, divides, synchronizes, and alienly appropriates time.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the presentation enacts the asserted movement by genetically tracing back forms of appearance, translating quantitative formulas into social relations, and reconstructing operational solutions as new stages of contradiction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:ALT-B05","CL_V4GB_04:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-01","text":"Abstract labour remains tense between generally human expenditure and a specific social form of validity, while its determination of value is practically validated only subsequently; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:FL-02","CL_V4GB_01:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-02","text":"The presentation of capital as an automatic subject collides with its complete dependence on living labour; autonomization is really effective, but not self-sufficient; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:FL-01","CL_V4GB_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-03","text":"The presupposition of the purchase of labour-power at its value destabilizes itself as soon as present use reduces the lifetime and future reproducibility of the commodity itself; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:XD-04","CL_V4GB_03:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-04","text":"The state appears both as the medium of the existing property order and as the necessary enforcement instance of its limitation; the institutional reversal remains underdetermined; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-05","text":"The binding of transferred values to productive wear stands in tension with the present revaluation of still usable means of production; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-06","text":"The derivation of relative surplus-value presupposes that cheaper means of reproduction actually lower the value of labour-power; the social transmission mechanism remains incompletely determined; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-07","text":"Additive value formation and non-additive cooperative productivity remain compatible only if use-value benefit, potentiated individual performance, and social average labour are strictly distinguished; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["CL_V4GB_04:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-01","text":"Money mutates into the capital form as soon as its identity no longer lies in a static shape, but in recursively enlarged change of form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-02","text":"Use-value mutates from the excluded ground of value into the special value-creating capacity of labour-power and the medium of value transfer.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-03","text":"Labour-power mutates from a sold capacity through living labour into variable capital and finally into a commodity whose use transforms its bearer.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MP-03","CL_V4GB_03:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-04","text":"Time mutates from repetition of circulation and measure of value into the threshold of production, contested limit, and synchronized time of the collective worker.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MP-04","CL_V4GB_04:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-05","text":"Law and freedom mutate from the sealing of individual exchange into collectively enforced counter-force against its temporal results.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:RMD-05","CL_V4GB_03:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-06","text":"Constant capital mutates from a mere transmitter of value into the concentrated condition of organization and command, without thereby becoming itself a source of new value.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:FL-01","CL_V4GB_04:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a coupled machine of validation and valorization, in which social relations crystallize in things and objective conditions gather living labour-powers.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-01","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-02","text":"The subject is initially the bearer of an economic function and becomes, in the production process, the dependent organ of a social body of labour, whose unity confronts it as an alien power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-02","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-03","text":"Time is retroactive, finite, divisible, and synchronizable: capital cannot produce it, but can only validate, extend, redistribute, condense, and appropriate it.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:HSI-03","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-04","text":"Struggle consists in reversing the measurement of time into a demand for limits and in the possible recovery of social combination by the self-organized collective worker.","refs":["CL_V4GB_03:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_04:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B01","text":"At this level, the architecture is sufficiently reconstructible if value-form, recursive movement of capital, labour-power as special commodity, surplus labour-time, political imposition of limits, and appropriated cooperative force are jointly preserved.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B02","text":"Its strongest structure lies in the connection of objective value-objectivity, causal isolation of living labour, temporal exploitation, and organizational appropriation of social productivity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B04","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B03","text":"What remains underdetermined are the practical enforcement of determinate monetary and property orders, the institutional transformation of class power, the concrete limit of labour-time, and the transmission of productivity gains into a reduced value of labour-power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on connecting and strictly distinguishing at once use-value and value, labour process and valorization process, value formation and productivity, as well as coordination and command.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B05","text":"The actual movement is preserved only if reconstruction proceeds from the failure of circulatory explanations through conflict over time and the imposition of limits to productivity mutation, competitive generalization, and real subsumption.","refs":["CL_V4GB_02:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B06","text":"What resists axiomatic reduction are the practical reversals through which society stabilizes a money form, actually validates labour-power, institutionally fixes historical limits, and realizes cooperation simultaneously as productive force and alien power of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_01:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_03:MRT-B06","CL_V4GB_04:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"MC_V4GB_L1_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_V4GB_L1_01:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"V4Gb L1 01","context":"Chapters 01–12 · 1) Die Waare. · 2) Der Austauschprozess der Waaren. · 3) Das Geld oder die Waarencirculation. · Zweites Kapitel. Die Verwandlung von Geld in Kapital. · 1) Arbeitsprozess und Verwerthungsprozess. · 2) Constantes Kapital und variables Kapital. · 3) Die Rate des Mehrwerths. · 4) Der Arbeitstag. · reading part 1/2 · 4) Der Arbeitstag. · reading part 2/2 · 5) Rate und Masse des Mehrwerths. · 1) Begriff des relativen Mehrwerths. · 2) Cooperation."}},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02","layer":"MC","title":"V4Gb L1 02","order":2,"parents":["CL_V4GB_05","CL_V4GB_06","CL_V4GB_07","CL_V4GB_08"],"revision":"MC_V4GB_L1_02@R001","sha256":"181290d5944b8c43471dd7341ba48c552eef67b03dd2b09a6ff1b1928eff696a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-01","text":"Das zentrale Problem besteht darin, die technischen, ökonomischen, rechtlichen und historischen Teilprozesse als Reproduktion eines Kapitalverhältnisses zu erklären, das seine Voraussetzungen über einzelne Produktions- und Austauschakte hinaus selbst erneuert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:AS-01","CL_V4GB_08:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-02","text":"Die globale These lautet, dass die Trennung der Produzenten von ihren Arbeitsbedingungen Kapitalfunktion ermöglicht, unbezahlte Arbeit aneigenbar macht und durch Produktion, Zirkulation, Reproduktion und Akkumulation erneut hervorgebracht wird.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-03","text":"Die technische Reorganisation des Produktionsorgans und die quantitative Vergrößerung des Kapitals sind verschiedene Phasen derselben Bewegung, in der gesellschaftliche Produktivkraft objektiviert, Arbeitskraft relativ verdrängt und Herrschaft materiell verankert wird.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:ASP-03","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-04","text":"Das Argument wird zu einer genetisch-funktionalen Rekonstruktion, die historische Genealogie, kontrollierte Abstraktion, technische Analyse, Klassenreproduktion und negatives Gegenexperiment kombiniert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AS-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-05","text":"Die gerichtete Bewegung verläuft von gewaltsamer Produzententrennung über technische Subsumtion und Mehrwertproduktion zur Realisierung, reproduktiven Schließung, veränderten Kapitalzusammensetzung und endogenen Reservebildung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AS-04","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","CL_V4GB_06:AS-03","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06","text":"Diese Bewegung ist rekursiv, kumulativ und mutationsgetrieben: Ihre Resultate werden zu Voraussetzungen neuer Verwertungszyklen, während Wiederholung Größen bewahren und zugleich Wertprovenienz, Klassenposition und technische Struktur verändern kann.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:ASP-06","CL_V4GB_06:AS-07","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","text":"Widerstand, Regulation, Arbeitsknappheit und räumliche Flucht bilden keine stabilen Außengrenzen, sondern werden durch Intensivierung, technische Rekonfiguration, Reserveproduktion oder erneute politische Schließung in den Prozess zurückgeführt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CL_V4GB_08:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08","text":"Die Schließung bleibt negativ: Die kapitalistische Form erzeugt gesellschaftliche Kooperation und materielle Möglichkeiten ihrer Überschreitung, liefert aber keinen hinreichenden Übergangsmechanismus zu kollektiver Verfügung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Kapital ist kein Ding oder bloßer Wertvorschuss, sondern ein gesellschaftliches Verhältnis, das Produktionsmittel, Geld und Arbeitskraft durch Eigentumstrennung und Kommando funktionalisiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] Die Trennung der Arbeitskraft von ihren objektiven Bedingungen ist historische Voraussetzung, gegenwärtige Betriebsbedingung und fortlaufend reproduziertes Resultat des Gesamtprozesses.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Unbezahlte Arbeit bildet die Substanz des Mehrwerts, den Fonds weiterer Akkumulation und den materiellen Kern der reproduzierten Kapitalmacht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Gesellschaftliche Kooperation und Wissen mutieren vom menschlich gegliederten Gesamtarbeiter zum objektiven Maschinenorganismus und erscheinen dadurch als autonome Produktivkräfte des Kapitals.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-02","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Produktion, Zirkulation und Reproduktion bilden eine asymmetrische Einheit: Produktion erzeugt Mehrwert, Zirkulation realisiert ihn, und Reproduktion erneuert die Bedingungen seiner weiteren Erzeugung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:AS-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Rechtliche Freiheit und Äquivalententausch behalten lokale Geltung, mutieren durch wiederholte Reproduktion jedoch zur Vermittlungsform materieller Abhängigkeit und systematischer Aneignung ohne Äquivalent.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Akkumulation kapitalisiert Mehrwert, verändert mit wachsender Produktivkraft die organische Zusammensetzung und vermindert dadurch die proportionale Nachfrage nach Arbeitskraft.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Technische Arbeitsersparnis und kapitalistische Verwertung folgen verschiedenen Selektionsmaßen; Produktivitätssteigerung kann daher zugleich gesellschaftliche Potenz, Arbeitsverdrängung und Reservebildung erzeugen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-06","CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","CL_V4GB_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Klassenherrschaft wechselt zwischen offener Gewalt, technischer Disziplin, ökonomischem Zwang und politischer Reinstallation, ohne dass Staat und Markt getrennte Ordnungen bilden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CL_V4GB_08:XD-06","CL_V4GB_05:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Der gesellschaftliche Output des Prozesses umfasst nicht nur Waren und Mehrwert, sondern reproduzierte Klassenpositionen, verfügbare Arbeitskraft, Reservepopulation und kontrollierte Reproduktionsbedingungen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-09","CL_V4GB_07:GA-08","CL_V4GB_08:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Familie, Konsumtion, Boden, Naturstoffwechsel und territoriale Mobilität sind keine äußeren Milieus, sondern innere Reproduktionsfelder, auf die Verwertung ihre Kosten verlagert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:CGD-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","CL_V4GB_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Grenzen der Verwertung werden nicht notwendig akzeptiert, sondern in Intensivierung, technische Innovation, Konzentration, Mobilisierung oder politische Wiederherstellung ihrer Voraussetzungen übersetzt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:AS-05","CL_V4GB_07:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Die kapitalistische Form entwickelt gesellschaftliche Kooperation und Produktivkräfte, blockiert aber deren nichtantagonistische Verwendung und untergräbt zugleich ihre menschlichen und natürlichen Reproduktionsbedingungen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-14","text":"[Attractor] Kollektive Verfügung über vergesellschaftete Produktionsbedingungen bildet den negativen Gegenpol des Systems, muss aber Produzentenunabhängigkeit mit entwickelter Kooperation verbinden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CL_V4GB_08:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-01","text":"Die Produzententrennung bewahrt ihre Funktion, verschiebt sich aber vom historischen Scheidungsereignis zur reproduzierten Voraussetzung, technischen Betriebsbedingung und reaktivierbaren politischen Schließung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RMD-02","CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-02","text":"Kapital mutiert vom vorgeschossenen Wertding zur objektivierten Produktionsmacht, rekursiven Sozialrelation und territorial verteilten Kommandostruktur.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MP-03","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-03","text":"Der Gesamtarbeiter bleibt als Vergesellschaftungsform erhalten, doch seine Einheit wandert vom menschlichen Kollektiv in die Apparatur und von dort in ein erweitertes Netz reproduktiver und territorialer Abhängigkeiten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_05:MME-05","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-04","text":"Zeit mutiert vom geteilten Arbeitstag über technische Synchronisierung zur kumulativen Reproduktions-, Akkumulations-, Zyklus- und Rückkehrzeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RMD-05","CL_V4GB_06:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_07:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-05","text":"Freiheit kehrt ihre Valenz um: Vertrags- und Arbeitgeberfreiheit vermitteln Abhängigkeit, während materieller Zugang zu Arbeitsbedingungen einen wirklichen Austritt aus Lohnabhängigkeit ermöglicht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_08:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06","text":"Staatsgewalt behält ihre konstitutive Funktion, mutiert jedoch vom offenen Terror über Rechtsumbau zum stummen Zwang und kehrt bei Funktionsstörungen als Preis-, Boden- und Bevölkerungssteuerung zurück.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RMD-04","CL_V4GB_08:MP-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-07","text":"Räumliche Entfernung mutiert vom vermeintlichen Außenraum zur Infrastruktur der Arbeitsreserve und zur zeitversetzten politischen Rückkehr exportierter Widersprüche.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:RMD-08","CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-08","text":"Auf eigener Arbeit beruhendes Eigentum verschwindet nicht einfach, sondern wird zunächst als Austrittsmöglichkeit bewahrt und terminal in die höhere Forderung kooperativer Aneignung absorbiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-01","text":"Maschinenanatomie, Werkzeugübertragung und konkrete Fabrikformen bleiben lokale technische Bestimmungen; nach oben skaliert die Verlagerung gesellschaftlicher Einheit und Kontrolle in einen objektivierten Produktionsorganismus.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:CGD-03","CL_V4GB_05:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-02","text":"Zeitlohn, Stücklohn und einzelne Einkommensformen bleiben lokale Erscheinungsweisen; metaclustertragend ist ihre gemeinsame Funktion, unbezahlte Arbeit zu individualisieren und ihre Herkunft zu verdecken.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-03","text":"Besondere Reserveformen, Wohnungsfälle und Gangvermittlung bleiben institutionelle Implementierungen; nach oben skaliert die endogene Produktion flexibler, billiger und disziplinierter Arbeitsverfügbarkeit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-04","text":"Enclosures, Landraub, Disziplinargesetze und künstliche Bodenpreise bleiben historische Verfahren der unteren Ebene; global trägt ihre gemeinsame Funktion als politische Herstellung und Wiederherstellung der Produzententrennung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:CGD-01","CL_V4GB_08:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-05","text":"Technische Subsumtion und Klassenreproduktion skalieren gemeinsam, weil die eine den Arbeitsprozess reorganisiert und die andere dessen verfügbare Träger erneuert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:XD-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-06","text":"Einfache und erweiterte Reproduktion sind keine getrennten Systemlogiken: Beide reproduzieren das Trennungsverhältnis, während erweiterte Reproduktion zusätzlich Zusammensetzung, Reserve und territoriale Reichweite transformiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:XD-04","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-07","text":"Die koloniale Gegenprobe skaliert über ihren Schauplatz hinaus, weil sie die in der Normalform verdeckte Abhängigkeit des gesamten Kapitalprozesses von Eigentumslosigkeit und blockierten Austrittsmöglichkeiten isoliert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:CGD-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-01","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein neutraler Technik- oder Produktivitätsbegriff, der Eigentum, Verwertungsselektion, Arbeitsverdrängung und soziale Kosten voneinander trennt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GNX-01","CL_V4GB_07:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-02","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein dinglicher Kapitalbegriff, nach dem Geld, Maschinen oder Produktionsmittel unabhängig von Klassenpolarität Kapitalfunktion besitzen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GNX-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-03","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die spontane Entstehung von Arbeitsmarkt, innerem Markt und Lohnabhängigkeit aus Tausch, Angebot, Nachfrage oder Bevölkerungsbewegung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GNX-04","CL_V4GB_08:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-04","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Gleichsetzung rechtlicher Freiheit mit materieller Selbstverfügung oder eines formal äquivalenten Vertrags mit Abwesenheit von Ausbeutung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GNX-05","CL_V4GB_08:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-05","text":"Ausgeschlossen sind automatische Kompensation und ein stabiler kapitalistischer Vollbeschäftigungszustand, weil technische Verdrängung und Reserveproduktion funktionale Bedingungen der Expansion bilden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GNX-04","CL_V4GB_07:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-06","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine vom Staat unabhängige Marktordnung, da politische Gewalt Eigentumslosigkeit und Arbeitszufuhr hervorbringt, bevor ökonomischer Zwang autonom erscheinen kann.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GNX-05","CL_V4GB_08:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-07","text":"Ausgeschlossen sind endgültige regulatorische oder territoriale Schließungen, weil Begrenzungen in technische Anpassung und räumlich exportierte Widersprüche in erneute Rückwirkung übergehen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GNX-06","CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-01","text":"Unzulässig ist die dauerhafte Koexistenz allgemeinen Zugangs zu Arbeitsbedingungen mit einer stabil verfügbaren Lohnarbeiterklasse; ihre Möglichkeit würde die generative Trennung außer Kraft setzen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:DBN-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-02","text":"Falsch sein muss die Vorstellung, Reproduktion sei bloße Wiederholung, weil selbst konstante Produktionsgröße Wertprovenienz, Abhängigkeit und Klassenkontinuität transformiert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GNX-06","CL_V4GB_06:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-03","text":"Die private Konsumtion, Familie und Natur dürfen keine autonome Außenseite bilden, weil sie Arbeitskraft und materielle Reproduktionsbedingungen erneuern und zugleich Kosten aufnehmen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_05:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-04","text":"Unzulässig ist die Identität von Kapitalwachstum und gelingender gesellschaftlicher Reproduktion, da Reichtumszuwachs mit Reservebildung, Pauperismus und zerstörten Reproduktionsbedingungen koexistieren kann.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:DBN-03","CL_V4GB_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-05","text":"Unzulässig ist die Annahme, die Gründungsgewalt verschwinde vollständig in der Normalität des Markts; bei gefährdeten Voraussetzungen muss sie als sichtbare Intervention reaktivierbar bleiben.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:XD-06","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste strukturierende Abwesenheit ist ein kollektiver Produzent, der den vergesellschafteten Produktionsorganismus selbst besitzt, disponiert und reguliert.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_05:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist die unmittelbare Verwandlung technischer Arbeitsersparnis in allgemeine freie Zeit und vielseitige menschliche Entwicklung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSA-02","CL_V4GB_07:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-03","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt ein unschuldiger Ursprung, der Eigentum und Kapital aus Sparsamkeit, Vertrag oder den späteren Rechtsformen des Systems ableitet.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_08:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-04","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein folgenloses territoriales Außen, in das Reserve, Kosten und Konflikte dauerhaft abgeschoben werden könnten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05","text":"Ebenso nicht verfügbar ist ein automatischer Übergang aus der kapitalistischen Vergesellschaftung in kollektive Verfügung; die materielle Möglichkeit bleibt vom politischen und institutionellen Übergangsmechanismus getrennt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:BSD-07","CL_V4GB_05:FL-04","CL_V4GB_08:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-01","text":"Die objektive Gestalt des Maschinenorganismus ist sedimentierte Klassenordnung: Historische Produzententrennung schafft die Verfügbarkeit, die technische Subsumtion anschließend als apparative Notwendigkeit organisiert. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","CL_V4GB_08:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02","text":"Relative Arbeitsverdrängung ist zugleich technischer Effekt und reproduktive Voraussetzung: Maschinerie setzt Arbeitskraft frei, während Akkumulation diese Freisetzung als Reserve für flexible Expansion funktionalisiert. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","CL_V4GB_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-03","text":"Einfache und erweiterte Reproduktion unterscheiden den Grad, nicht das Grundprinzip der Klassenrekursion: Gleichbleibende Skala erneuert die Trennung, während Akkumulation ihre technische, demographische und räumliche Organisation intensiviert. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","CL_V4GB_06:XD-04","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04","text":"Die lokale Gültigkeit des Äquivalententauschs stabilisiert die globale Aneignung ohne Äquivalent, weil der freie Einzelvertrag die reproduzierte Eigentumslosigkeit voraussetzt und zugleich verdeckt. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","CL_V4GB_08:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05","text":"Arbeitsgesetzgebung und Staatsgewalt sind keine bloß äußeren Korrekturen des Kapitals; sie wechseln zwischen Schutz, Modernisierungszwang und Wiederherstellung der Verwertungsbedingungen. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-06","text":"Die Reproduktion der Arbeitskraft und die Verlagerung ihrer Kosten bilden eine Einheit: Konsumtion erhält die Verkaufsfähigkeit, während Familie, Gesellschaft und Natur die nicht vergüteten Verschleißfolgen aufnehmen. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","CL_V4GB_06:FL-03","CL_V4GB_05:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_05:ASP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-07","text":"Weltmarkt und Migration beseitigen innere Widersprüche nicht, sondern verteilen Rohstoffabhängigkeit, Reservebildung und Reproduktionskosten räumlich und führen sie ökonomisch oder politisch zurück. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:BSD-06","CL_V4GB_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-08","text":"Eine tragfähige Gegenform muss individuellen Zugang zu Arbeitsbedingungen mit der erreichten gesellschaftlichen Kooperation verbinden; isoliertes Kleineigentum negiert Lohnabhängigkeit, organisiert aber noch nicht die vergesellschaftete Produktion. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-14","CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CL_V4GB_08:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-01","text":"Kapital erhält den ontologischen Status eines selbstreproduzierenden Relationssystems, das lebendige Arbeit in objektive Macht und diese Macht in erneuerte Bedingungen ihres Kommandos verwandelt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:BSD-01","CL_V4GB_06:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird zu einer verteilten Systemposition: Kapitalisten personifizieren Verwertungszwang, während Produzenten als Teilarbeiter, Maschinenanhängsel, Arbeitskraftverkäufer, Reserve oder mögliche kollektive Aneigner auftreten.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSD-01","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-03","text":"Kapitalistische Zeit ist geschichtet: Arbeitstagszeit, technische Synchronisierung, Reproduktionsperiode, Akkumulationszyklus, historische Gewalt und politische Rückkehr wirken gleichzeitig.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_08:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_07:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-04","text":"Kausalität wird rekursiv, weil technische, soziale und politische Wirkungen der Verwertung zu Voraussetzungen ihrer nächsten Runde werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSD-04","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-05","text":"Politische Handlungsmacht verschiebt sich vom isolierten Vertrag auf die Kontrolle über Arbeitsbedingungen, Austrittsmöglichkeiten, Reservebildung und die Verbindung segmentierter Produzentengruppen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:BSD-06","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-06","text":"Erkenntnis verlangt den Wechsel zwischen Abstraktion, technischer Rekonstruktion, Klassenmaßstab, Genealogie und peripherem Gegenexperiment; keine einzelne Perspektive kann den Gesamtmechanismus isoliert erklären.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:BSD-05","CL_V4GB_08:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-07","text":"Geschichte erscheint als selbstuntergrabende, aber nicht teleologische Entwicklung: Das System erzeugt materielle Transformationsbedingungen, ohne deren politische Aktivierung zu garantieren.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSD-07","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-01","text":"Produzententrennung → Verkauf der Arbeitskraft → fremdes Produkt → Lohnkonsumtion → erneute Verkaufsnotwendigkeit bildet die elementare Klassenrekursion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:RLE-01","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-02","text":"Teure Maschinerie → Nutzungsdruck → verlängerte oder verdichtete Arbeitszeit → gesetzliche Begrenzung → Intensivierung → technische Verbesserung bildet eine regulatorisch beschleunigte Apparateschleife.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RLE-02","CL_V4GB_05:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-03","text":"Akkumulation → Produktivkraftsteigerung → veränderte organische Zusammensetzung → relative Arbeiterfreisetzung → Reservebildung → flexible Expansion bildet die zentrale Mutationsschleife.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04","CL_V4GB_07:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-04","text":"Räumliche Verdrängung → Emigration → Transfers und Binnenmarktkontraktion → weitere Proletarisierung → Diaspora → politische Rückkehr bildet die territoriale Rückkopplung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:RMD-08","CL_V4GB_07:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-05","text":"Offene Gewalt → normalisiertes Lohnverhältnis → verdeckter ökonomischer Zwang → Funktionsstörung → erneute politische Intervention bildet die rekursive Gründungsschleife.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RLE-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-06","text":"Lohnform → verselbstständigte Revenueformen → freier Einzelvertrag → zunehmende Entfernung von unbezahlter Arbeit bildet die Eskalation der Verdeckung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:RLE-04","CL_V4GB_06:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-07","text":"Der gemeinsame Attraktor ist bewusste kollektive Verfügung: Je vollständiger Produktion und Reproduktion vergesellschaftet werden, desto deutlicher erscheint ihre private Beherrschung als blockierende Form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RLE-07","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B01","text":"Enteignung von Boden und Arbeitsbedingungen → eigentumslose Arbeitskraft plus konzentrierte Produktionsmittel → Kapital-Lohnarbeit-Polarität.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B02","CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B02","text":"Kauf der Arbeitskraft plus Subsumtion plus Überschreitung notwendiger Arbeitszeit → unbezahlter Mehrwert → Erscheinung gesellschaftlicher Produktivkraft als Kapitalmacht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B02","CL_V4GB_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B03","text":"Lohn- und Revenueformen plus Warenverkauf → Verdeckung der gemeinsamen Mehrwertquelle plus Realisierung des erzeugten Werts.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B04","text":"Arbeiterkonsumtion plus fortbestehende Trennung plus erneuter Produktionszyklus → reproduzierte Arbeitskraft, Kapitalistenklasse und Lohnarbeiterklasse.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B05","text":"Kapitalisierter Mehrwert plus Produktivkraftsteigerung → steigende organische Zusammensetzung → relativer Rückgang des variablen Kapitals → Reservepopulation und Lohndisziplin.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B04","CL_V4GB_07:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B06","text":"Soziale oder politische Grenze → Intensivierung, technische Rekonfiguration, Mobilisierung oder erneute Enteignung → Wiederherstellung der Verwertungsbedingungen auf höherer Organisationsstufe.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B07","text":"Konzentration plus Vergesellschaftung plus Untergrabung der Reproduktionsbedingungen → verschärfte Unvereinbarkeit privater Aneignung mit kooperativer Produktion → negativer Attraktor kollektiver Gegenaneignung ohne garantierten Übergang.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B08","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:AFM-B01","text":"Historische Produzententrennung → Arbeitsmarktbildung → formelle und reelle Subsumtion → objektiver Maschinenorganismus → Mehrwertproduktion → Lohnverdeckung und Realisierung → Klassenreproduktion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B01","CL_V4GB_06:AS-05","CL_V4GB_05:ASP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:AFM-B02","text":"Klassenreproduktion → Mehrwertkapitalisierung → Produktivkraftsteigerung → organischer Strukturwandel → Arbeiterfreisetzung → Reservebildung → Lohndisziplin, Pauperismus und räumliche Mobilisierung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:ASP-03","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:AFM-B03","text":"Widerstand oder Austritt → Verwertungshemmung → technische, regulatorische oder politische Wiederschließung → erweiterte gesellschaftliche Kooperation → verschärfter Eigentumswiderspruch → unbestimmte Gegenexpropriation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AS-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-01","text":"Produktivität wird in technische Leistungsfähigkeit, gesellschaftliche Arbeitsersparnis und kapitalistische Rentabilität zerlegt; dadurch verliert Effizienz ihren neutralen Status.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MME-03","CL_V4GB_05:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-02","text":"Produktion und Zirkulation werden als notwendige, aber asymmetrische Momente rekonstruiert, während Reproduktion ihre soziale Kontinuität erklärt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MME-02","CL_V4GB_06:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-03","text":"Der Outputbegriff erweitert sich von Waren und Mehrwert auf Arbeitskraft, Klassenpositionen, Reservepopulation, Eigentumstrennung und Naturbedingungen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MME-05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-04","text":"Der Arbeitsmarkt wird vom neutralen Austauschraum zum politisch und technisch produzierten Machtfeld umkartiert, dessen Angebot und Nachfrage durch Kapitalakkumulation selbst geformt werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:MME-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-05","text":"Der Gegensatz von Staat und Markt bricht zusammen, weil politische Gewalt die Bedingungen erzeugt und repariert, unter denen ökonomischer Zwang selbsttätig erscheint.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-06","text":"Zentrum und Peripherie werden epistemisch umgeordnet: Der koloniale Ausfall einer naturalisierten Kategorie enthüllt die sedimentierten Voraussetzungen ihrer metropolitanen Normalität.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MME-02","CL_V4GB_08:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-07","text":"Eigentum zerfällt in Selbstarbeitseigentum, kapitalistisches Privateigentum und mögliche kooperative Aneignung; der abstrakte Eigentumsbegriff verliert dadurch seine analytische Einheit.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MME-06","CL_V4GB_08:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B01","text":"Auf dem Surface level erscheinen Maschinen, Arbeitszeit, Lohn, Warenverkauf, Beschäftigung, Arbeitslosigkeit, Wohnraum, Landenteignung und Migration als heterogene Vorgänge.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B01","CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B01","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B02","text":"Auf dem Structural level verbinden Produzententrennung, Subsumtion, unbezahlte Arbeit, Realisierung, Kapitalzusammensetzung und Reservebildung diese Vorgänge zu einer Reproduktionsarchitektur.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B02","CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B02","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B03","text":"Auf dem Metastrategic level verlagert sich Interpretation vom Einzelvertrag, technischen Objekt oder lokalen Missstand auf Eigentumszugang, Klassenkontinuität, gesellschaftliche Anwendung und kollektive Verfügung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B03","CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B03","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B04","text":"Auf dem Ontological / Temporal level besteht Realität aus rekursiv erzeugten Relationen und verschachtelten Zeiten, in denen vergangene Arbeit gegenwärtige Arbeit kommandiert und Ursprung als reproduzierte Gegenwart fortbesteht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B04","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B05","text":"Auf dem Methodological / Performative level vollzieht die Darstellung ihre These durch Abstraktion, Wiedereinführung ausgeschlossener Vermittlungen, Maßstabswechsel, Genealogie, Gegenexperiment und widerspruchslogische Eskalation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B05","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B05","CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-01","text":"Die Trennung von Maschine und kapitalistischer Anwendung bleibt instabil, weil Technik nicht als autonomer Gegner gelten soll, ihre konkrete Gestalt aber bereits unter Verwertungszwang entsteht.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:FL-01","CL_V4GB_05:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-02","text":"Die funktionale Einbeziehung der Arbeiterexistenz bleibt unvollständig, weil Konsumtion zugleich notwendige Reproduktion des Kapitals und eine nicht vollständig kontrollierte Lebenssphäre ist.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FL-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-03","text":"Der Anspruch eines allgemeinen Akkumulationsgesetzes steht unter Spannung zur historischen, räumlichen und institutionellen Vielfalt seiner Erscheinungs- und Durchsetzungsformen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:FL-05","CL_V4GB_08:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-04","text":"Die lokale Geltung des Äquivalententauschs und die gesellschaftliche Aneignung ohne Äquivalent bleiben nur durch einen Maßstabswechsel vereinbar; wird dieser Übergang verwischt, droht begriffliche Inkohärenz.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:FL-01","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-05","text":"Die terminale Gegenexpropriation ist schwächer vermittelt als Genesis und Reproduktion des Kapitalverhältnisses; materielle Möglichkeit, politische Organisation und institutionelle Form bleiben auseinander.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:FL-04","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B07","CL_V4GB_05:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-01","text":"Expropriation mutiert vom historischen Ursprung zur reproduzierten und politisch reaktivierbaren Betriebsbedingung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MP-01","CL_V4GB_08:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-02","text":"Kapital mutiert vom vorgeschossenen Wert und dinglichen Bestand zur rekursiven sozialen Macht, die ihre Träger und Voraussetzungen erzeugt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MP-03","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-03","text":"Produktivkraft mutiert von gesellschaftlicher Expansionspotenz zur Einheit von Mehrwertsteigerung, Arbeiterfreisetzung und Reservebildung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:RMD-04","CL_V4GB_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-04","text":"Freiheit mutiert von rechtlicher Loslösung und wiederholtem Vertrag zur materiellen Fähigkeit, Lohnarbeit durch Verfügung über Arbeitsbedingungen zu verlassen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MP-03","CL_V4GB_06:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-05","text":"Begrenzung mutiert von äußerer Schranke zum internen Innovationsmechanismus, während Gewalt vom offenen Terror zum ökonomischen Zwang und bei Instabilität zurück zur sichtbaren Intervention wechselt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MP-05","CL_V4GB_08:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-01","text":"Realität erscheint als rekursive Trennungs- und Konversionsmaschine, die Personen, Dinge und Zugangsrechte polarisiert, lebendige Arbeit objektiviert und ihre Wirkungen in neue Verwertungsbedingungen verwandelt.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:HSI-01","CL_V4GB_06:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist kein souveränes Zentrum, sondern eine umschaltbare und segmentierte Position zwischen Kapitalfunktion, Lohnarbeit, Reserve, unabhängiger Produktion und möglicher kollektiver Aneignung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:HSI-02","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03","text":"Zeit ist synchronisiert, kumulativ und rekursiv: Sie verdichtet den Arbeitstag, schichtet Reproduktionsperioden und lässt historische Gewalt als gegenwärtige Struktur oder wiederholbare Intervention fortbestehen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:HSI-03","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-04","text":"Möglicher Kampf richtet sich auf Verfügung über Arbeitsbedingungen, technische Anwendung, Austrittsmöglichkeiten und die Verbindung der vom Kapital segmentierten Produzenten; individuelle Flucht bleibt gegenüber kooperativer Gegenaneignung unzureichend.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_07:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B01","text":"Die Architektur ist aus sechs Elementen rekonstruierbar: Produzententrennung, unbezahlte Arbeit, objektivierte Produktivkraft, asymmetrische Einheit von Produktion und Zirkulation, Klassenreproduktion sowie Akkumulation mit Reservebildung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B02","text":"Das System bleibt kohärent, sofern Kapital als gesellschaftliches Verhältnis, Trennung als Voraussetzung und Resultat sowie Reproduktion als maßstabsabhängige Transformation statt als bloße Wiederholung behandelt werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B03","text":"Die stärkste Architektur liegt in der Endogenisierung: Technische Organisation, Fonds, Arbeitsangebot, Reserve, Disziplin und politische Wiederschließung werden aus Wirkungen des Kapitalprozesses zu Bedingungen seiner Wiederholung.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B04","CL_V4GB_06:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B04","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben quantitative Beschäftigungsbewegungen, sektorale und nationale Varianten sowie die relative Gewichtung technischer, institutioneller und demographischer Mechanismen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B04","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B05","text":"Ebenfalls unterbestimmt bleibt die positive Form kollektiver Verfügung: Die Rekonstruktion begründet ihre materielle Möglichkeit und negative Notwendigkeit, aber weder ihre politische Sequenz noch ihre Institutionen.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:FL-04","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B07","CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B06","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn Genesis, technische Mutation, reproduktive Wiederkehr, Akkumulationseskalation, koloniale Gegenprobe und terminale Offenheit nicht zu einer linearen Fortschritts- oder Ursprungserzählung eingeebnet werden.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T212239935490Z_af39259c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"V4Gb L1 02","source_sha256":"181290d5944b8c43471dd7341ba48c552eef67b03dd2b09a6ff1b1928eff696a","sha256":"3cfc9cdc0fef59b96edc2a4ccc46dce605afeca475e51efded59f86b563a72ed","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:22:39.937435+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-01","text":"The central problem consists in explaining the technical, economic, legal, and historical subprocesses as the reproduction of a capital relation that itself renews its preconditions beyond individual acts of production and exchange.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:AS-01","CL_V4GB_08:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis is that the separation of producers from their conditions of labour enables the function of capital, makes unpaid labour appropriable, and is reproduced anew through production, circulation, reproduction, and accumulation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-03","text":"The technical reorganization of the organ of production and the quantitative enlargement of capital are different phases of the same movement, in which social productive power is objectified, labour-power is relatively displaced, and domination is materially anchored.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:ASP-03","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-04","text":"The argument becomes a genetic-functional reconstruction that combines historical genealogy, controlled abstraction, technical analysis, class reproduction, and negative counter-experiment.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AS-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-05","text":"The directed movement proceeds from violent separation of producers through technical subsumption and surplus-value production to realization, reproductive closure, altered composition of capital, and endogenous reserve formation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AS-04","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03","CL_V4GB_06:AS-03","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06","text":"This movement is recursive, cumulative, and mutation-driven: its results become preconditions of new cycles of valorization, while repetition can preserve magnitudes and at the same time alter value provenance, class position, and technical structure.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:ASP-06","CL_V4GB_06:AS-07","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","text":"Resistance, regulation, labour scarcity, and spatial flight form no stable external boundaries, but are returned to the process through intensification, technical reconfiguration, reserve production, or renewed political closure.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CL_V4GB_08:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08","text":"The closure remains negative: the capitalist form produces social cooperation and the material possibilities of its transcendence, but supplies no sufficient transition mechanism to collective disposal.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Capital is not a thing or mere advance of value, but a social relation that functionalizes means of production, money, and labour-power through separation of ownership and command.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] The separation of labour-power from its objective conditions is a historical precondition, a present condition of operation, and a continuously reproduced result of the overall process.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Unpaid labour forms the substance of surplus value, the fund of further accumulation, and the material core of reproduced capital power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Social cooperation and knowledge mutate from the humanly articulated collective worker into an objective machine organism and thereby appear as autonomous productive forces of capital.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-02","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Production, circulation, and reproduction form an asymmetric unity: production generates surplus value, circulation realizes it, and reproduction renews the conditions of its further generation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:AS-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Legal freedom and exchange of equivalents retain local validity, but through repeated reproduction mutate into the mediating form of material dependence and systematic appropriation without equivalent.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Accumulation capitalizes surplus value, alters the organic composition with growing productive power, and thereby reduces proportional demand for labour-power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-01","CL_V4GB_07:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Technical labour-saving and capitalist valorization follow different criteria of selection; increases in productivity can therefore simultaneously produce social potential, displacement of labour, and reserve formation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-06","CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","CL_V4GB_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Class domination alternates between open violence, technical discipline, economic compulsion, and political reinstallation, without state and market constituting separate orders.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GA-07","CL_V4GB_08:XD-06","CL_V4GB_05:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The social output of the process comprises not only commodities and surplus value, but reproduced class positions, available labour-power, reserve population, and controlled conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GA-09","CL_V4GB_07:GA-08","CL_V4GB_08:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Family, consumption, land, metabolism with nature, and territorial mobility are not external milieus, but internal fields of reproduction onto which valorization shifts its costs.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:CGD-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","CL_V4GB_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Limits to valorization are not necessarily accepted, but translated into intensification, technical innovation, concentration, mobilization, or political restoration of their preconditions.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:AS-05","CL_V4GB_07:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] The capitalist form develops social cooperation and productive forces, but blocks their non-antagonistic use and at the same time undermines their human and natural conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-14","text":"[Attractor] Collective disposal over socialized conditions of production forms the negative counterpole of the system, but must connect producer independence with developed cooperation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CL_V4GB_08:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-01","text":"The separation of producers preserves its function, but shifts from a historical event of separation to a reproduced precondition, a technical condition of operation, and a politically reactivatable closure.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RMD-02","CL_V4GB_06:GA-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-02","text":"Capital mutates from the advanced value-thing into objectified productive power, recursive social relation, and territorially distributed structure of command.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MP-03","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_05:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-03","text":"The collective worker remains as a form of socialization, yet its unity migrates from the human collective into the apparatus and from there into an expanded network of reproductive and territorial dependencies.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RMD-03","CL_V4GB_05:MME-05","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-04","text":"Time mutates from the divided working day through technical synchronization into cumulative time of reproduction, accumulation, cycle, and return.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RMD-05","CL_V4GB_06:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_07:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-05","text":"Freedom reverses its valence: contractual freedom and employers' freedom mediate dependence, whereas material access to conditions of labour enables a real exit from wage dependence.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_08:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06","text":"State power retains its constitutive function, but mutates from open terror through legal restructuring into mute compulsion and returns, in cases of dysfunction, as regulation of prices, land, and population.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RMD-04","CL_V4GB_08:MP-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-07","text":"Spatial distance mutates from a presumed external space into the infrastructure of the labour reserve and into the time-delayed political return of exported contradictions.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:RMD-08","CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-08","text":"Property based on one's own labour does not simply disappear, but is initially preserved as a possibility of exit and terminally absorbed into the higher demand for cooperative appropriation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RMD-07","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-01","text":"Machine anatomy, tool transmission, and concrete factory forms remain local technical determinations; scaled upward is the displacement of social unity and control into an objectified organism of production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:CGD-03","CL_V4GB_05:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-02","text":"Time wages, piece wages, and individual forms of income remain local modes of appearance; what bears the metacluster is their common function of individualizing unpaid labour and concealing its origin.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-03","text":"Particular reserve forms, housing cases, and gang mediation remain institutional implementations; scaled upward is the endogenous production of flexible, cheap, and disciplined labour availability.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-04","text":"Enclosures, land robbery, disciplinary laws, and artificial land prices remain historical procedures of the lower level; globally, their common function as the political production and restoration of the separation of producers is load-bearing.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:CGD-01","CL_V4GB_08:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-05","text":"Technical subsumption and class reproduction scale jointly, because the former reorganizes the labour process and the latter renews its available bearers.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:XD-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-06","text":"Simple and expanded reproduction are not separate system logics: both reproduce the relation of separation, while expanded reproduction additionally transforms composition, reserve, and territorial scope.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:XD-04","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-07","text":"The colonial counter-test scales beyond its scene, because it isolates the dependence of the entire capital process on propertylessness and blocked possibilities of exit, concealed in the normal form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:CGD-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-01","text":"Excluded is a neutral concept of technology or productivity that separates property, valorization selection, displacement of labour, and social costs from one another.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GNX-01","CL_V4GB_07:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-02","text":"Excluded is a reified concept of capital according to which money, machines, or means of production possess the function of capital independently of class polarity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GNX-02","CL_V4GB_08:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-03","text":"Excluded is the spontaneous emergence of the labour market, internal market, and wage dependence from exchange, supply, demand, or population movement.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GNX-04","CL_V4GB_08:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-04","text":"Excluded is the equation of legal freedom with material self-disposal, or of a formally equivalent contract with the absence of exploitation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GNX-05","CL_V4GB_08:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-05","text":"Excluded are automatic compensation and a stable capitalist state of full employment, because technical displacement and reserve production constitute functional conditions of expansion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GNX-04","CL_V4GB_07:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-06","text":"Excluded is a market order independent of the state, since political violence produces propertylessness and the supply of labour before economic compulsion can appear autonomous.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:GNX-05","CL_V4GB_08:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-07","text":"Excluded are definitive regulatory or territorial closures, because limitations pass into technical adaptation and spatially exported contradictions into renewed feedback.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GNX-06","CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-01","text":"Impermissible is the permanent coexistence of general access to conditions of labour with a stably available wage-worker class; its possibility would nullify the generative separation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:DBN-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-02","text":"The notion that reproduction is mere repetition must be false, because even a constant scale of production transforms value provenance, dependence, and class continuity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:GNX-06","CL_V4GB_06:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-03","text":"Private consumption, family, and nature must not form an autonomous outside, because they renew labour-power and material conditions of reproduction while at the same time absorbing costs.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_05:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-04","text":"Impermissible is the identity of capital growth and successful social reproduction, since an increase in wealth can coexist with reserve formation, pauperism, and destroyed conditions of reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:DBN-03","CL_V4GB_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-05","text":"Impermissible is the assumption that founding violence disappears entirely into the normality of the market; when preconditions are endangered, it must remain reactivatable as visible intervention.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:XD-06","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-01","text":"The deepest structuring absence is a collective producer that itself owns, disposes over, and regulates the socialized organism of production.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_05:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is the immediate transformation of technical labour-saving into general free time and multifaceted human development.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSA-02","CL_V4GB_07:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-03","text":"Excluded remains an innocent origin that derives property and capital from thrift, contract, or the later legal forms of the system.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:BSA-01","CL_V4GB_08:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-04","text":"Unavailable is a consequence-free territorial outside into which reserve, costs, and conflicts could be permanently displaced.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05","text":"Likewise unavailable is an automatic transition from capitalist socialization to collective disposal; the material possibility remains separate from the political and institutional mechanism of transition.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:BSD-07","CL_V4GB_05:FL-04","CL_V4GB_08:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-01","text":"The objective form of the machine organism is sedimented class order: historical separation of producers creates availability, which technical subsumption subsequently organizes as an apparatus-based necessity. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","CL_V4GB_08:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02","text":"Relative displacement of labour is at once a technical effect and a reproductive precondition: machinery releases labour-power, while accumulation functionalizes this release as a reserve for flexible expansion. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","CL_V4GB_05:GA-07","CL_V4GB_07:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-03","text":"Simple and expanded reproduction distinguish degree, not the basic principle of class recursion: constant scale renews separation, while accumulation intensifies its technical, demographic, and spatial organization. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","CL_V4GB_06:XD-04","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04","text":"The local validity of exchange of equivalents stabilizes global appropriation without equivalent, because the free individual contract presupposes and at the same time conceals reproduced propertylessness. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06","CL_V4GB_07:GA-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-08","CL_V4GB_08:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05","text":"Labour legislation and state power are not merely external corrections to capital; they alternate between protection, compulsion to modernization, and restoration of the conditions of valorization. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-06","text":"The reproduction of labour-power and the displacement of its costs form a unity: consumption preserves capacity for sale, while family, society, and nature absorb the uncompensated consequences of wear. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","CL_V4GB_06:FL-03","CL_V4GB_05:DBN-04","CL_V4GB_05:ASP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-07","text":"World market and migration do not eliminate internal contradictions, but distribute raw-material dependence, reserve formation, and reproduction costs spatially and return them economically or politically. ; Trace Type — Composite","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12","CL_V4GB_05:BSD-06","CL_V4GB_07:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-08","text":"A viable counter-form must connect individual access to conditions of labour with the attained social cooperation; isolated small property negates wage dependence, but does not yet organize socialized production. ; Trace Type — Tension","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-14","CL_V4GB_05:GA-13","CL_V4GB_08:GA-12","CL_V4GB_08:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-01","text":"Capital acquires the ontological status of a self-reproducing system of relations that transforms living labour into objective power and this power into renewed conditions of its command.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:BSD-01","CL_V4GB_06:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes a distributed system position: capitalists personify the compulsion to valorize, while producers appear as partial workers, appendages of machinery, sellers of labour-power, reserve, or possible collective appropriators.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSD-01","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-03","text":"Capitalist time is layered: working-day time, technical synchronization, period of reproduction, cycle of accumulation, historical violence, and political return operate simultaneously.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_08:BSD-02","CL_V4GB_07:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes recursive because technical, social, and political effects of valorization become preconditions of its next round.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSD-04","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-05","text":"Political agency shifts from the isolated contract to control over conditions of labour, possibilities of exit, reserve formation, and the connection of segmented producer groups.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:BSD-06","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-06","text":"Knowledge requires movement between abstraction, technical reconstruction, class scale, genealogy, and peripheral counter-experiment; no single perspective can explain the overall mechanism in isolation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:BSD-05","CL_V4GB_08:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-07","text":"History appears as a self-undermining but non-teleological development: the system produces material conditions of transformation without guaranteeing their political activation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:BSD-07","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-01","text":"Separation of producers → sale of labour-power → alien product → wage consumption → renewed necessity of sale forms the elementary class recursion.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:RLE-01","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-02","text":"Expensive machinery → pressure for utilization → extended or intensified working time → legal limitation → intensification → technical improvement forms a regulatorily accelerated apparatus loop.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RLE-02","CL_V4GB_05:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-03","text":"Accumulation → increase in productive power → altered organic composition → relative release of workers → reserve formation → flexible expansion forms the central mutation loop.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04","CL_V4GB_07:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-04","text":"Spatial displacement → emigration → transfers and contraction of the internal market → further proletarianization → diaspora → political return forms territorial feedback.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:RMD-08","CL_V4GB_07:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-05","text":"Open violence → normalized wage relation → concealed economic compulsion → dysfunction → renewed political intervention forms the recursive founding loop.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:RLE-03","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-06","text":"Wage form → autonomized revenue forms → free individual contract → increasing distance from unpaid labour forms the escalation of concealment.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:RLE-04","CL_V4GB_06:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-07","text":"The common attractor is conscious collective disposal: the more completely production and reproduction are socialized, the more clearly their private domination appears as a blocking form.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:RLE-07","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B01","text":"Expropriation of land and conditions of labour → propertyless labour-power plus concentrated means of production → capital–wage-labour polarity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B02","CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B02","text":"Purchase of labour-power plus subsumption plus exceeding necessary labour-time → unpaid surplus value → appearance of social productive power as capital power.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B02","CL_V4GB_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B03","text":"Wage and revenue forms plus sale of commodities → concealment of the common source of surplus value plus realization of the value produced.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B04","text":"Workers' consumption plus continuing separation plus renewed production cycle → reproduced labour-power, capitalist class, and wage-worker class.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FGS-B05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B05","text":"Capitalized surplus value plus increase in productive power → rising organic composition → relative decline of variable capital → reserve population and wage discipline.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:FGS-B04","CL_V4GB_07:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B06","text":"Social or political limit → intensification, technical reconfiguration, mobilization, or renewed expropriation → restoration of the conditions of valorization at a higher level of organization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FGS-B07","text":"Concentration plus socialization plus undermining of conditions of reproduction → intensified incompatibility of private appropriation with cooperative production → negative attractor of collective counter-appropriation without guaranteed transition.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:FGS-B08","CL_V4GB_05:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:AFM-B01","text":"Historical separation of producers → formation of the labour market → formal and real subsumption → objective machine organism → surplus-value production → wage concealment and realization → class reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AFM-B01","CL_V4GB_06:AS-05","CL_V4GB_05:ASP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:AFM-B02","text":"Class reproduction → capitalization of surplus value → increase in productive power → organic structural change → release of workers → reserve formation → wage discipline, pauperism, and spatial mobilization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:ASP-03","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-04","CL_V4GB_07:ASP-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:AFM-B03","text":"Resistance or exit → obstruction of valorization → technical, regulatory, or political reclosure → expanded social cooperation → intensified property contradiction → indeterminate counter-expropriation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:AS-05","CL_V4GB_05:GA-10","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-01","text":"Productivity is divided into technical performance capacity, social labour-saving, and capitalist profitability; efficiency thereby loses its neutral status.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MME-03","CL_V4GB_05:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-02","text":"Production and circulation are reconstructed as necessary but asymmetric moments, while reproduction explains their social continuity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MME-02","CL_V4GB_06:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-03","text":"The concept of output expands from commodities and surplus value to labour-power, class positions, reserve population, separation of ownership, and conditions of nature.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MME-05","CL_V4GB_06:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-04","text":"The labour market is remapped from a neutral space of exchange into a politically and technically produced field of power, whose supply and demand are themselves shaped by capital accumulation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:MME-05","CL_V4GB_08:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-05","text":"The opposition between state and market collapses, because political violence produces and repairs the conditions under which economic compulsion appears automatic.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-06","text":"Centre and periphery are epistemically reordered: the colonial failure of a naturalized category reveals the sedimented preconditions of its metropolitan normality.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MME-02","CL_V4GB_08:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-07","text":"Property disintegrates into property based on one's own labour, capitalist private property, and possible cooperative appropriation; the abstract concept of property thereby loses its analytical unity.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MME-06","CL_V4GB_08:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B01","text":"At the Surface level, machines, working time, wages, sale of commodities, employment, unemployment, housing, land expropriation, and migration appear as heterogeneous processes.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B01","CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B01","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B02","text":"At the Structural level, separation of producers, subsumption, unpaid labour, realization, composition of capital, and reserve formation connect these processes into an architecture of reproduction.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B02","CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B02","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B03","text":"At the Metastrategic level, interpretation shifts from the individual contract, technical object, or local grievance to access to property, class continuity, social application, and collective disposal.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B03","CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B03","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B04","text":"At the Ontological / Temporal level, reality consists of recursively produced relations and nested times, in which past labour commands present labour and origin persists as reproduced present.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:ALT-B04","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B05","text":"At the Methodological / Performative level, the presentation enacts its thesis through abstraction, reintroduction of excluded mediations, changes of scale, genealogy, counter-experiment, and contradiction-logical escalation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:ALT-B05","CL_V4GB_08:ALT-B05","CL_V4GB_05:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-01","text":"The separation of machine and capitalist application remains unstable, because technology is not to count as an autonomous adversary, yet its concrete form already emerges under the compulsion to valorize.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:FL-01","CL_V4GB_05:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-02","text":"The functional inclusion of workers' existence remains incomplete, because consumption is at once a necessary reproduction of capital and a sphere of life not fully controlled.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:FL-03","CL_V4GB_06:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-03","text":"The claim of a general law of accumulation stands in tension with the historical, spatial, and institutional diversity of its forms of appearance and enforcement.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:FL-05","CL_V4GB_08:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-04","text":"The local validity of exchange of equivalents and social appropriation without equivalent remain compatible only through a change of scale; if this transition is blurred, conceptual incoherence threatens.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:FL-01","CL_V4GB_07:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-05","text":"Terminal counter-expropriation is mediated more weakly than the genesis and reproduction of the capital relation; material possibility, political organization, and institutional form remain separate.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:FL-04","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B07","CL_V4GB_05:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-01","text":"Expropriation mutates from historical origin into a reproduced and politically reactivatable condition of operation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MP-01","CL_V4GB_08:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-02","text":"Capital mutates from advanced value and reified stock into recursive social power that produces its bearers and preconditions.","refs":["CL_V4GB_06:MP-03","CL_V4GB_07:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-03","text":"Productive power mutates from social potential for expansion into the unity of increasing surplus value, release of workers, and reserve formation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:RMD-04","CL_V4GB_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-04","text":"Freedom mutates from legal detachment and repeated contract into the material capacity to leave wage labour through disposal over conditions of labour.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MP-03","CL_V4GB_06:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-05","text":"Limitation mutates from an external barrier into an internal mechanism of innovation, while violence shifts from open terror to economic compulsion and, in instability, back to visible intervention.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MP-05","CL_V4GB_08:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a recursive machine of separation and conversion that polarizes persons, things, and rights of access, objectifies living labour, and transforms its effects into new conditions of valorization.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:HSI-01","CL_V4GB_06:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not a sovereign centre, but a switchable and segmented position between capital function, wage labour, reserve, independent production, and possible collective appropriation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:HSI-02","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03","text":"Time is synchronized, cumulative, and recursive: it intensifies the working day, layers periods of reproduction, and allows historical violence to persist as present structure or repeatable intervention.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:HSI-03","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-04","text":"Possible struggle is directed toward disposal over conditions of labour, technical application, possibilities of exit, and the connection of producers segmented by capital; individual flight remains inadequate in relation to cooperative counter-appropriation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_07:HSI-04","CL_V4GB_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B01","text":"The architecture is reconstructible from six elements: separation of producers, unpaid labour, objectified productive power, asymmetric unity of production and circulation, class reproduction, and accumulation with reserve formation.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B01","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B02","text":"The system remains coherent provided that capital is treated as a social relation, separation as precondition and result, and reproduction as scale-dependent transformation rather than mere repetition.","refs":["CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_06:MRT-B03","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B03","text":"The strongest architecture lies in endogenization: technical organization, funds, labour supply, reserve, discipline, and political reclosure become, from effects of the capital process, conditions of its repetition.","refs":["CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B04","CL_V4GB_06:BSD-03","CL_V4GB_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B04","text":"Quantitative movements in employment, sectoral and national variants, and the relative weighting of technical, institutional, and demographic mechanisms remain underdetermined.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B04","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B02","CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B05","text":"The positive form of collective disposal likewise remains underdetermined: the reconstruction grounds its material possibility and negative necessity, but neither its political sequence nor its institutions.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:FL-04","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B07","CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B06","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if genesis, technical mutation, reproductive recurrence, escalation of accumulation, colonial counter-test, and terminal openness are not flattened into a linear narrative of progress or origin.","refs":["CL_V4GB_05:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_07:MRT-B05","CL_V4GB_08:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"MC_V4GB_L1_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_V4GB_L1_02:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · Capital Volume 1","title":"V4Gb L1 02","context":"Chapters 13–23 · 3) Theilung der Arbeit und Manufaktur. · 4) Maschinerie und grosse Industrie. · reading part 1/2 · 4) Maschinerie und grosse Industrie. · reading part 2/2 · Fünftes Kapitel. Weitere Untersuchungen über die Produktion des absoluten und relativen Mehrwerths. · Sechstes Kapitel. Der Accumulationsprozess des Kapitals. · a) Einfache Reproduktion. · b) Verwandlung von Mehrwerth in Kapital. · c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 1/2 · c) Das allgemeine Gesetz der kapitalistischen Accu- mulation. · reading part 2/2 · 2) Die s. g. Ursprüngliche Accumulation. · 3) Die moderne Kolonisationstheorie."}},{"id":"WB_V4GB","layer":"WB","title":"Capital Volume 1","order":1,"parents":["MC_V4GB_L1_01","MC_V4GB_L1_02"],"revision":"WB_V4GB@R002","sha256":"e8136f0291369e6f5bf5cc9cc32bf5d4186e2b0ac91b4c65fac4d1ae2a6cc46e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-01","text":"Das System erklärt, wie nachträglich vergesellschaftete Privatarbeit in ein Kapitalverhältnis übergeht, das seine historischen, technischen, rechtlichen und reproduktiven Voraussetzungen selbst erneuert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-02","text":"Kapital wird als rekursive Organisation gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit bestimmt, deren gegenwärtige Betriebsfähigkeit auf der fortdauernden Trennung der Produzenten von ihren Arbeitsbedingungen beruht.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-03","text":"Rechtliche Selbstverfügung und Äquivalententausch bilden keinen Gegenpol zur Herrschaft, sondern die Vermittlungsform, durch die materielle Produktionsmittellosigkeit in asymmetrisches Produktionskommando übersetzt wird.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-04","text":"Die Expansion des Werts beruht auf lebendiger Arbeit, deren unbezahlter Anteil Mehrwert erzeugt und als akkumulierter Fonds die Macht über ihre künftige Verausgabung verstärkt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-05","text":"Jede Grenze extensiver Aneignung wird in Produktivitätssteigerung, technische Reorganisation, Konzentration, Reservebildung oder politische Wiederherstellung der Verwertungsbedingungen übersetzt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-06","text":"Der Gesamtprozess produziert deshalb nicht nur Waren und Mehrwert, sondern auch gesellschaftliche Produktivkraft, Klassenpositionen, verfügbare Arbeitskraft und belastete Reproduktionsfelder.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-07","text":"Die Bewegung ist rekursiv und spiralförmig, weil Resultate der Verwertung zu Voraussetzungen ihres nächsten Zyklus werden und jeder vergrößerte Rückfluss die Bedingungen erneuter Unterordnung erweitert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06","MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-08","text":"Die Schließung bleibt negativ: Die Vergesellschaftung der Produktion erzeugt die materielle Möglichkeit kollektiver Verfügung, aber keinen automatischen politischen oder institutionellen Übergang zu ihr.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Privatarbeit erhält gesellschaftliche Geltung erst durch sachliche Wertformen und nachträgliche Validierung; diese Vermittlung bleibt die elementare Formbedingung des Gesamtprozesses.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Kapital ist weder Ding noch ruhender Wertbestand, sondern eine rekursive Wertidentität und gesellschaftliche Relation, die ihre Formen, Träger und Voraussetzungen funktionalisiert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-03","text":"[Attractor] Die Trennung der Arbeitskraft von ihren objektiven Bedingungen ist zugleich historische Genesis, gegenwärtige Betriebsbedingung und reproduziertes Resultat der Kapitalbewegung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Lebendige Arbeit ist die einzige Quelle neuen Werts; ihr unbezahlter Anteil bildet Mehrwert, Akkumulationsfonds und erneuerte Kapitalmacht.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Produktion, Zirkulation und Reproduktion bilden eine asymmetrische Einheit: Produktion erzeugt Mehrwert, Zirkulation realisiert ihn und Reproduktion erneuert seine sozialen Bedingungen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Formale Freiheit mutiert unter materieller Trennung zur Vermittlungsform von Abhängigkeit, sodass lokaler Äquivalententausch die globale Aneignungsrelation nicht aufhebt, sondern operationalisiert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Die Aneignung von Arbeitszeit verschiebt sich von der Ausdehnung des Arbeitstags zur Verkürzung notwendiger Arbeit und zur technischen Reorganisation, ohne die Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit zu beseitigen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Kooperation und gesellschaftliches Wissen erscheinen zunächst als nichtadditive Kraft des Gesamtarbeiters, werden dann im Maschinenorganismus objektiviert und als Eigenproduktivität des Kapitals verselbständigt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Konkurrenz und Akkumulation vermitteln Expansion als äußeren Zwang, verändern die organische Zusammensetzung und erzeugen fortgesetzt relative Arbeitsverdrängung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Der Output des Kapitalprozesses umfasst neben Waren und Mehrwert reproduzierte Klassenpositionen, Arbeitsverfügbarkeit sowie belastete familiäre, natürliche und territoriale Reproduktionsfelder.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Klassenherrschaft wechselt zwischen offener Gewalt, rechtlicher Form, technischer Disziplin, stummem ökonomischem Zwang und sichtbarer politischer Intervention.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Grenzen bleiben dem System nicht äußerlich, sondern werden in Innovation, Intensivierung, räumliche Verlagerung oder politische Wiederschließung übersetzt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Kapital kann seine menschlichen und natürlichen Reproduktionsbedingungen untergraben und lebendige Arbeit relativ verdrängen, darf sie als Wertquelle jedoch nicht vollständig beseitigen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-14","text":"[Attractor] Kollektive Verfügung über vergesellschaftete Produktionsbedingungen bildet den negativen Gegenpol privater Aneignung, bleibt aber von ihrem politischen Übergangsmechanismus getrennt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-14","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-01","text":"Wert bewahrt seine Bestimmung als gesellschaftliche Objektivität abstrakter Arbeit, mutiert jedoch von einer relational dargestellten Eigenschaft zur rekursiven und territorial ausgreifenden Kapitalrelation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-02","text":"Geld wandert von der ausgeschlossenen Äquivalentform zur Erscheinungsform eines prozessierenden Werts und wird schließlich in die reproduktive Identität des Kapitalverhältnisses absorbiert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-03","text":"Arbeitskraft mutiert von der gekauften Ware zum Organ des Gesamtarbeiters und weiter zur segmentierten Position als Teilarbeiter, Maschinenanhängsel oder Reserve.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-04","text":"Kooperation bleibt gesellschaftliche Kombinationskraft, verlagert ihre Einheit aber vom menschlichen Kollektiv in fremdes Kommando und den objektivierten Maschinenorganismus.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-05","text":"Zeit erweitert sich vom Wertmaß und umkämpften Arbeitstag zur technischen Synchronisierung sowie zu Reproduktionsperiode, Akkumulationszyklus und historischer Rückkehr.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-06","text":"Freiheit kehrt ihre Valenz um: Vertragsfreiheit ermöglicht asymmetrische Verfügung, während materielle Freiheit den Zugang zu Arbeitsbedingungen und die Fähigkeit zum Austritt voraussetzt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-07","text":"Staatsgewalt mutiert vom offenen Terror über Rechtsumbau zum stummen Zwang und kehrt bei gefährdeter Reproduktion als sichtbare Intervention wieder.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-08","text":"Begrenzung mutiert von einer äußeren Schranke zum internen Innovationsmechanismus, durch den die Blockade einer Verwertungsweise die Ausbildung ihrer Nachfolgeform beschleunigt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-09","text":"Räumliche Entfernung verliert die Funktion eines stabilen Außenraums und wird zur zeitversetzten Rückkehr exportierter Arbeitskräfte, Kosten und Konflikte.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-01","text":"Die einzelnen Wertformentwicklungen und Geldfunktionen bleiben lokale Ableitungsapparate; auf Gesamtbuchebene trägt ihre gemeinsame Leistung, gesellschaftliche Vermittlung zu objektivieren und rekursive Kapitalidentität zu ermöglichen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-02","text":"Mehrwertformeln und buchhalterische Zerlegungen bleiben lokale Messapparate; höherstufig werden sie in eine Architektur geschichteter Arbeits-, Reproduktions- und Akkumulationszeiten integriert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-03","text":"Maschinenanatomie und konkrete Fabrikformen verbleiben auf der technischen Unterebene; nach oben skaliert die Verlagerung gesellschaftlicher Einheit und Kontrolle in einen objektivierten Produktionsorganismus.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-04","text":"Lohnformen, Reserveformen und institutionelle Vermittler bleiben besondere Implementierungen; gesamtbuchtragend ist ihre Funktion, unbezahlte Arbeit zu verdecken und flexible Arbeitsverfügbarkeit zu erzeugen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-05","text":"Enteignungsakte, Disziplinargesetze und Bodenpolitiken bleiben historische Verfahren; auf Gesamtbuchebene werden sie als politische Herstellung und Wiederherstellung der Produzententrennung lesbar.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-06","text":"Die koloniale Gegenprobe bleibt ein besonderer Schauplatz, skaliert aber als Beweis, dass die normalisierte Kapitalrelation blockierte Austrittsmöglichkeiten und Eigentumslosigkeit voraussetzt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-01","text":"Wert und Kapital dürfen weder aus Nützlichkeit und Dingnatur noch aus dem Besitz von Geld oder Produktionsmitteln abgeleitet werden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-02","text":"Bloße Zirkulation kann keinen gesellschaftlichen Mehrwert erzeugen, und Produktionsmittel können trotz ihrer technischen Wirksamkeit keine autonome Quelle neuen Werts bilden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-03","text":"Rechtliche Gleichheit darf weder mit materieller Selbstverfügung noch mit einer Garantie realer Kontrolle über die eigene Arbeits- und Lebenszeit gleichgesetzt werden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-04","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein neutraler Technik- oder Produktivitätsbegriff, der technische Leistung von Eigentum, Arbeitsverdrängung, Verwertungsselektion und freier Zeit trennt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-05","text":"Arbeitsmarkt und Lohnabhängigkeit dürfen nicht als spontane Resultate von Tausch oder Bevölkerungsbewegung erscheinen, weil politische Gewalt Eigentumslosigkeit und Arbeitszufuhr konstituiert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-06","text":"Ausgeschlossen sind automatische Beschäftigungskompensation und endgültige regulatorische oder territoriale Schließungen, weil Arbeitsverdrängung und räumliche Rückkopplung funktionale Momente der Expansion bilden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-07","text":"Kapitalwachstum darf nicht mit gelingender gesellschaftlicher Reproduktion identifiziert werden, da Expansion mit Reservebildung, Pauperisierung und zerstörten Reproduktionsbedingungen vereinbar bleibt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-01","text":"Damit die Wertarchitektur Bestand hat, darf Privatarbeit nicht unmittelbar gesellschaftlich sein; eine unmittelbare Assoziation der Produzenten würde ihre sachliche Validierungsform entbehrlich machen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-02","text":"Allgemeiner und gesicherter Zugang zu Arbeitsbedingungen ist mit einer dauerhaft verfügbaren Lohnarbeiterklasse unvereinbar, weil er die reproduzierte Verkaufsnotwendigkeit aufheben würde.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-03","text":"Reproduktion darf keine bloße Wiederholung sein und Gründungsgewalt nicht vollständig verschwinden; andernfalls wären Klassenkontinuität und politische Wiederschließung unerklärbar.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-04","text":"Familie, Konsumtion und Natur dürfen keine autonome Außenseite bilden, und Kapitalwachstum darf nicht als zureichendes Maß ihrer Reproduktion gelten.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-05","text":"Kapital darf weder als statischer Besitz noch als selbstgenügsames Subjekt gelten, weil seine Fortdauer die wiederholte Kopplung an lebendige Arbeit voraussetzt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-06","text":"Ein automatischer Übergang aus kapitalistischer Vergesellschaftung ist unzulässig; materielle Möglichkeit ersetzt weder politische Sequenz noch institutionelle Konstruktion.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-01","text":"Die tiefste strukturierende Abwesenheit ist der Gesamtarbeiter als kollektiver Eigentümer, Leiter und Regulator des von ihm hervorgebrachten Produktionsorganismus.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-02","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist die unmittelbare Verwandlung technischer Arbeitsersparnis in allgemeine freie Zeit; Eigenzeit entsteht erst durch gesellschaftliche Begrenzung der Verkaufszeit.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-03","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleiben sowohl ein unschuldiger Eigentumsursprung als auch ein folgenloses territoriales Außen, in das die Kosten der Verwertung dauerhaft ausgelagert werden könnten.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-04","text":"Das System umkreist eine kollektive Gegenform, kann aber den Abstand zwischen ihrer materiellen Möglichkeit und ihrer politischen Hervorbringung nicht schließen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-01","text":"Die sachliche Objektivität des Werts und die Produzententrennung erzeugen gemeinsam eine Relation, die in Dingen erscheint, obwohl ihre Wirksamkeit aus gesellschaftlicher Abhängigkeit hervorgeht; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-01","WB_V4GB:GA-02","WB_V4GB:GA-03","MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-02","text":"Die Differenz zwischen Wert und Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft verwandelt den lokal äquivalenten Einzelvertrag über reproduzierte Eigentumslosigkeit in eine zyklische Aneignung ohne gesellschaftliches Äquivalent; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-03","WB_V4GB:GA-04","WB_V4GB:GA-05","WB_V4GB:GA-06","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-03","text":"Die kooperative Produktivkraft wandert in den Maschinenorganismus und kehrt den gesellschaftlichen Zusammenhang der Produzenten in eine objektive Kommandogewalt über sie um; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-08","WB_V4GB:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-04","text":"Die politische Begrenzung extensiver Mehrarbeit kann als Modernisierungszwang wirken, weil sie Verwertung auf Intensivierung, Produktivität und technische Rekonfiguration verschiebt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-07","WB_V4GB:GA-11","WB_V4GB:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-05","text":"Unter privater Verfügung wird gesellschaftliche Arbeitsersparnis nicht notwendig zu freier Zeit, sondern kann über veränderte Kapitalzusammensetzung als Arbeitsverdrängung und flexible Reserve zurückkehren; Trace Type — Negative.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-07","WB_V4GB:GA-09","WB_V4GB:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-06","text":"Konkurrenz verallgemeinert lokale Produktivitätsvorteile, hebt sie als Sondervorteile auf und erneuert über sinkende proportionale Arbeitsnachfrage den Innovations- und Disziplinierungszwang; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-09","WB_V4GB:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-07","text":"Staatsgewalt ist zugleich Vollstreckungsinstanz einer Begrenzung und Medium der Wiederherstellung von Verwertungsbedingungen; ihre widersprüchliche Funktion gehört daher zur Reproduktion des Verhältnisses selbst; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-11","WB_V4GB:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-08","text":"Die Reproduktion der Arbeitskraft verteilt nicht vergütete Verschleißfolgen auf Familie, Gesellschaft, Natur und Territorien, ohne diese Kosten dauerhaft aus dem Gesamtprozess entfernen zu können; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-10","WB_V4GB:GA-12","WB_V4GB:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-09","text":"Je weiter Produktion und Reproduktion vergesellschaftet werden, desto stärker wirkt kollektive Verfügung als systemischer Attraktor; aus dieser Zuspitzung folgt jedoch kein hinreichender Übergangsmechanismus; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-13","WB_V4GB:GA-14","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-01","text":"Realität erhält den Status einer relationalen Prozesswirklichkeit, in der lebendige Arbeit objektive Macht erzeugt und diese Macht die Bedingungen weiterer Unterordnung reproduziert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-02","text":"Das Subjekt wird zu einer verteilten und umschaltbaren Systemposition zwischen Warenbesitz, Lohnarbeit, Maschinenfunktion, Reserve und möglicher kollektiver Aneignung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-03","text":"Kapitalistische Zeit ist nachträglich, antagonistisch und geschichtet: Marktvalidierung, Arbeitstag, Synchronisierung, Reproduktionsperiode, Akkumulationszyklus und historische Gewalt wirken gleichzeitig.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-04","text":"Kausalität wird mehrschichtig und rekursiv, weil demographische, technische, eigentumsförmige und politische Wirkungen zu Voraussetzungen der nächsten Verwertungsrunde werden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-05","text":"Politik ist kein äußerer Zusatz zur Ökonomie, sondern der Kampf um Arbeitsbedingungen, Zeitgrenzen, Austrittsmöglichkeiten, Reservebildung und gesellschaftliche Kombination.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-06","text":"Geschichte erscheint als gegenwärtige Reproduktion vergangener Gewalt und als nichtteleologische Erzeugung materieller Transformationsbedingungen, deren politische Aktivierung offenbleibt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-07","text":"Erkenntnis muss genetische Formanalyse, technische Rekonstruktion, Klassenreproduktion, Genealogie und territoriales Gegenexperiment verbinden, weil keine Einzelperspektive den Gesamtmechanismus trägt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-01","text":"Privatarbeit erzeugt Waren, Austausch validiert sie, der Wert kehrt als Kapitalvorschuss zurück, und der vergrößerte Rückfluss macht das Resultat zur Voraussetzung erneuter Produktion.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-02","text":"Produzententrennung erzwingt Arbeitskraftverkauf, Lohnkonsumtion reproduziert die Verkaufsfähigkeit, und die Wiederholung reproduziert zugleich das Trennungsverhältnis.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-03","text":"Gesellschaftliche Vermittlung löscht ihre Genesis aus, erscheint als Eigenschaft des Maschinenorganismus und bestätigt dadurch scheinbar die Notwendigkeit des Kapitalkommandos.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-04","text":"Überarbeit und Umgehung erzeugen Widerstand und Kontrolle; die verschärfte Kontrolle erzeugt wiederum Intensivierung, Innovation und neue Umgehungsformen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-05","text":"Produktivitätsvorsprung wird zur gesellschaftlichen Norm, hebt den Einzelvorteil auf und kehrt als Arbeitsverdrängung, Reservebildung und erneuter Innovationszwang zurück.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-06","text":"Offene Gewalt normalisiert das Lohnverhältnis, verschwindet im stummen Zwang und wird bei gefährdeten Voraussetzungen als politische Intervention reaktiviert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-07","text":"Räumliche Auslagerung erzeugt kein Außen, sondern eine territoriale Rückkopplung, in der exportierte Arbeitskräfte, Kosten und Konflikte ökonomisch oder politisch zurückkehren.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-08","text":"Der dominante Attraktor ist die maximale Aneignung gesellschaftlicher Arbeitszeit; ihr negativer Gegenattraktor ist bewusste kollektive Verfügung über die vergesellschafteten Bedingungen dieser Arbeit.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B01","text":"Produzententrennung + unabhängige Privatarbeit → Austauschzwang → abstrakte Gleichsetzung → sachliche Wertobjektivität → nachträgliche gesellschaftliche Geltung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B02","text":"Wertform + Geldvermittlung + rechtliche Selbstverfügung + materielle Produktionsmittellosigkeit → Arbeitskraft als käufliche Ware → asymmetrische Verfügung im Produktionsprozess.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B03","text":"Gebrauch der Arbeitskraft → Werterhaltung + Neuwertbildung + Überschreitung notwendiger Arbeit → Mehrarbeit → Mehrwert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B04","text":"Mehrwertproduktion + Realisierung + erneuter Vorschuss → Reproduktion des Kapitalverhältnisses → Resultate als Voraussetzungen des folgenden Zyklus.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B05","text":"Konzentration + Kooperation + gesellschaftliches Wissen → nichtadditive Produktivkraft → objektivierter Maschinenorganismus → verselbständigtes Kapitalkommando.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B06","text":"Kapitalisierter Mehrwert + Produktivkraftsteigerung → steigende organische Zusammensetzung → relative Arbeitsverdrängung → Reservebildung → Lohndisziplin und flexible Expansion.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B07","text":"Soziale, rechtliche oder räumliche Grenze → Intensivierung, technische Rekonfiguration oder politische Wiederschließung → Wiederherstellung der Verwertungsbedingungen auf höherer Organisationsstufe.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B08","text":"Vergesellschaftung + private Aneignung + Untergrabung der Reproduktionsbedingungen → negativer Attraktor kollektiver Verfügung, jedoch ohne automatische Übergangssequenz.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:AFM-B01","text":"Privatarbeit → Wertform → Geld → Kapitalvorschuss → Arbeitskraftkauf → Produktionsprozess → Mehrarbeit → Mehrwert → erneuter Vorschuss.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AFM-B02","text":"Teilung in notwendige Arbeit und Mehrarbeit ohne immanentes Maß der Gesamtdauer → entgegengesetzte Zeitansprüche, die weder Markt noch Natur oder Privatmoral entscheiden → kollektiv erzwungene und institutionell vollstreckbare Begrenzung → relative Mehrwertproduktion → Kooperation und Maschinerie → Akkumulation → veränderte Zusammensetzung → Reservebildung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AFM-B03","text":"Gewaltsame Produzententrennung → normalisiertes Lohnverhältnis → technische und reproduktive Wiederschließung → erweiterte Vergesellschaftung → verschärfter Eigentumswiderspruch → materielle Möglichkeit, aber politisch und institutionell unbestimmte kollektive Gegenaneignung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-01","text":"Kapital wird von Geld- oder Sachbesitz zu einer rekursiven Einrichtung der Erfassung, Objektivierung und Reproduktion gesellschaftlicher Arbeitsmacht umkartiert.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-02","text":"Marktgleichheit und Produktionskommando werden als aufeinanderfolgende Ebenen derselben Aneignungsrelation lesbar, nicht als einander ausschließende Beschreibungen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-03","text":"Der Outputbegriff erweitert sich von Waren und Mehrwert auf Klassenpositionen, Reservepopulation, Eigentumstrennung und Naturbedingungen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-04","text":"Produktivität zerfällt in technische Leistungsfähigkeit, Gebrauchswertwirkung, Wertbildung, gesellschaftliche Arbeitsersparnis und kapitalistische Rentabilität; ihre scheinbare Neutralität bricht zusammen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-05","text":"Der Gegensatz von Staat und Markt kollabiert, weil rechtlich eröffnete Arbeitszeitaneignung politisch begrenzt und ihre gefährdeten Bedingungen staatlich repariert werden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-06","text":"Zentrum und Peripherie werden als rückgekoppelte Räume rekonstruiert: Der koloniale Ausfall naturalisierter Kategorien enthüllt Voraussetzungen, die im Zentrum sedimentiert erscheinen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-07","text":"Eigentum und Freiheit zerfallen in kapitalistisches Privateigentum, Selbstarbeitseigentum und kooperative Aneignung; materielle Freiheit bemisst sich am Zugang zu gesellschaftlichen Arbeitsbedingungen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-07","MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B01","text":"Auf dem Surface level erscheinen Ware, Geld, Arbeitskraft, Mehrwert, Maschine, Lohn, Beschäftigung und Migration als heterogene Gegenstände des Kapitalprozesses.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B02","text":"Auf dem Structural level verbinden Wertvermittlung, Eigentum, Produzententrennung, Subsumtion, unbezahlte Arbeit, Zeitteilung und Reservebildung diese Gegenstände zu einer Reproduktionsarchitektur.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B03","text":"Auf dem Metastrategic level verlagert sich Intervention vom Einzelvertrag und technischen Objekt auf Eigentumszugang, Klassenkontinuität, Arbeitszeitgrenzen und kollektive Verfügung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B04","text":"Auf dem Ontological / Temporal level kommandiert vergangene Arbeit gegenwärtige, während endliche Lebenskraft einer rekursiven Ordnung nachträglicher Validierung und kumulativer Akkumulation untersteht.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B05","text":"Auf dem Methodological / Performative level vollzieht die Darstellung ihre These durch genetische Rückführung, Wiedereinführung ausgeschlossener Vermittlungen, Maßstabswechsel und die Rekonstruktion jeder Lösung als neue Widerspruchsstufe.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-01","text":"Abstrakte Arbeit oszilliert zwischen allgemein menschlicher Verausgabung und spezifischer gesellschaftlicher Geltungsform; ihre Einheit bleibt von nachträglicher Validierung abhängig; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-02","text":"Die Darstellung des Kapitals als automatisches Subjekt kollidiert mit seiner Abhängigkeit von lebendiger Arbeit und seinem gleichzeitigen Zwang, deren proportionalen Einsatz zu vermindern; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-03","text":"Die Trennung zwischen Maschine und kapitalistischer Anwendung bleibt instabil, weil Technik nicht autonom kapitalistisch sein soll, ihre konkrete Gestalt aber bereits unter Verwertungsselektion entsteht; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-04","text":"Lokaler Äquivalententausch und globale Aneignung ohne Äquivalent bleiben nur durch einen Maßstabswechsel vereinbar; seine Verwischung bedroht die begriffliche Kohärenz; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-05","text":"Der Staat erscheint zugleich als Garant der Eigentumsordnung, Vollstrecker ihrer Begrenzung und Agent ihrer technischen Modernisierung; der institutionelle Umschlag bleibt unterbestimmt; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-06","text":"Die kollektive Gegenaneignung ist schwächer vermittelt als Genesis und Reproduktion des Kapitalverhältnisses, weil materielle Möglichkeit, politische Organisation und Institution auseinanderfallen; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-01","text":"Kapital mutiert von einem formwechselnden Wertvorschuss zur rekursiven sozialen Macht, die ihre eigenen Träger und Voraussetzungen erzeugt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-02","text":"Arbeitskraft mutiert von der verkauften Fähigkeit über lebendige Arbeit und Gesamtarbeiterfunktion zur segmentierten Position zwischen Maschinenanhängsel, Verkäufer und Reserve.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-03","text":"Zeit mutiert vom Wertmaß zur umkämpften Grenze, synchronisierten Produktionszeit und rekursiven Schichtung historischer, reproduktiver und akkumulativer Dauer.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-04","text":"Freiheit mutiert von rechtlicher Vertragsfähigkeit zur kollektiv erzwungenen Gegengewalt und schließlich zur materiellen Fähigkeit, Lohnarbeit durch Verfügung über Arbeitsbedingungen zu verlassen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-05","text":"Produktivkraft mutiert von kooperativer Organisationskraft zur konzentrierten Kommandobedingung und weiter zur Einheit von Mehrwertsteigerung, Arbeitsverdrängung und Reservebildung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-06","text":"Begrenzung mutiert von äußerer Schranke zum Innovationsmechanismus, während Gewalt vom offenen Eingriff zum stummen Zwang und bei Instabilität zurück zur Intervention wechselt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-01","text":"Realität erscheint als Validierungs-, Trennungs- und Konversionsmaschine, die gesellschaftliche Beziehungen in Dingen kristallisiert und Zugangsrechte in wiederholbare Verwertungsbedingungen übersetzt.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-02","text":"Das Subjekt ist kein souveränes Zentrum, sondern ein abhängiges Organ und eine umschaltbare Position zwischen Kapitalfunktion, Lohnarbeit, Reserve und möglicher kollektiver Aneignung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-03","text":"Zeit ist rückwirkend, endlich, teilbar, synchronisiert und kumulativ; Kapital erzeugt sie nicht, sondern validiert, verdichtet, schichtet und eignet sie an.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-04","text":"Kampf besteht in der Rückgewinnung gesellschaftlicher Kombination sowie in der Verfügung über Arbeitsbedingungen, technische Anwendung, Austrittsmöglichkeiten und Reproduktionszeit.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B01","text":"Die Gesamtarchitektur ist rekonstruierbar, wenn Wertform, rekursive Kapitalbewegung, Produzententrennung, Arbeitskraft, unbezahlte Arbeit, objektivierte Produktivkraft, Klassenreproduktion und Reservebildung gemeinsam erhalten bleiben.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B02","text":"Ihre stärkste Struktur liegt in der Endogenisierung: Wertobjektivität, Arbeitszeitaneignung, technische Organisation, Arbeitsangebot und politische Wiederschließung werden aus Wirkungen des Prozesses zu Bedingungen seiner Wiederholung.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B03","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die institutionelle Transformation von Klassenmacht, quantitative Beschäftigungsbewegungen sowie die relative Gewichtung technischer, demographischer und politischer Mechanismen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B04","text":"Die positive Form kollektiver Verfügung bleibt unzureichend bestimmt, weil weder ihre politische Sequenz noch ihre dauerhafte institutionelle Organisation aus der negativen Architektur folgen.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B05","text":"Die Kohärenz hängt davon ab, Wert und Gebrauchswert, Produktivität und Wertbildung, Koordination und Kommando sowie lokale Austauschgleichheit und reproduktive Klassenmacht zugleich zu verbinden und zu unterscheiden.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B06","text":"Der axiomatischen Reduktion widerstehen die praktischen Umschläge, in denen Kooperation zugleich als Produktivkraft und fremde Macht realisiert wird und terminale Offenheit in politische Form übergehen müsste.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T212324927065Z_0f76612e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Capital Volume 1","source_sha256":"e8136f0291369e6f5bf5cc9cc32bf5d4186e2b0ac91b4c65fac4d1ae2a6cc46e","sha256":"923efa394318e814f986d6daecb22914c436d1ea2131eac9ef06100c5293528b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T21:23:24.928457+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-01","text":"The system explains how retrospectively socialized private labour passes into a capital relation that itself renews its historical, technical, legal, and reproductive presuppositions.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-02","text":"Capital is determined as a recursive organization of social labour-time, whose present operability rests on the continuing separation of producers from their conditions of labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-03","text":"Legal self-disposal and exchange of equivalents form not an opposite to domination, but the mediating form through which material lack of means of production is translated into asymmetric command over production.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-04","text":"The expansion of value rests on living labour, whose unpaid portion produces surplus-value and, as an accumulated fund, reinforces power over its future expenditure.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-05","text":"Every limit to extensive appropriation is translated into increases in productivity, technical reorganization, concentration, reserve formation, or political restoration of the conditions of valorization.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-06","text":"The overall process therefore produces not only commodities and surplus-value, but also social productive power, class positions, available labour-power, and burdened fields of reproduction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-07","text":"The movement is recursive and spiral-shaped because results of valorization become presuppositions of its next cycle, and each enlarged reflux expands the conditions of renewed subordination.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06","MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AS-08","text":"The closure remains negative: the socialization of production creates the material possibility of collective disposal, but no automatic political or institutional transition to it.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Private labour acquires social validity only through objective forms of value and retrospective validation; this mediation remains the elementary formal condition of the overall process.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Capital is neither a thing nor a static stock of value, but a recursive identity of value and social relation that functionalizes its forms, bearers, and presuppositions.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-03","text":"[Attractor] The separation of labour-power from its objective conditions is at once historical genesis, present operating condition, and reproduced result of the movement of capital.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Living labour is the sole source of new value; its unpaid portion forms surplus-value, the fund of accumulation, and renewed capital power.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Production, circulation, and reproduction form an asymmetric unity: production generates surplus-value, circulation realizes it, and reproduction renews its social conditions.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Formal freedom mutates, under material separation, into the mediating form of dependence, so that local exchange of equivalents does not abolish but operationalizes the global relation of appropriation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] The appropriation of labour-time shifts from extending the working day to shortening necessary labour and technical reorganization, without abolishing dependence on living labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Cooperation and social knowledge initially appear as the non-additive force of the collective worker, are then objectified in the machine organism, and autonomized as capital's own productivity.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Competition and accumulation mediate expansion as external compulsion, alter the organic composition, and continuously produce relative displacement of labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The output of the capital process includes, alongside commodities and surplus-value, reproduced class positions, labour availability, and burdened familial, natural, and territorial fields of reproduction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Class domination shifts between open violence, legal form, technical discipline, mute economic coercion, and visible political intervention.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-09","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Limits do not remain external to the system, but are translated into innovation, intensification, spatial displacement, or political reclosure.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Capital can undermine its human and natural conditions of reproduction and relatively displace living labour, but it may not completely abolish it as the source of value.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GA-14","text":"[Attractor] Collective disposal over socialized conditions of production forms the negative opposite of private appropriation, but remains separate from its political mechanism of transition.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-14","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-01","text":"Value preserves its determination as the social objectivity of abstract labour, but mutates from a relationally represented property into a recursive and territorially expansive capital relation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-02","text":"Money migrates from the excluded equivalent form to the form of appearance of a value in process and is ultimately absorbed into the reproductive identity of the capital relation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-03","text":"Labour-power mutates from the purchased commodity into the organ of the collective worker and further into the segmented position of partial worker, machine appendage, or reserve.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-04","text":"Cooperation remains a social power of combination, but shifts its unity from the human collective into alien command and the objectified machine organism.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-05","text":"Time expands from the measure of value and contested working day to technical synchronization as well as to the period of reproduction, cycle of accumulation, and historical return.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-06","text":"Freedom reverses its valence: contractual freedom enables asymmetric disposal, whereas material freedom presupposes access to conditions of labour and the capacity to exit.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RMD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-07","text":"State power mutates from open terror through legal restructuring into mute coercion and returns as visible intervention when reproduction is endangered.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-08","text":"Limitation mutates from an external barrier into an internal mechanism of innovation, through which the blockage of one mode of valorization accelerates the formation of its successor form.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RMD-09","text":"Spatial distance loses the function of a stable outside and becomes the time-shifted return of exported labour-powers, costs, and conflicts.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-01","text":"The individual developments of the value-form and functions of money remain local apparatuses of derivation; at the level of the whole book, their common achievement is to objectify social mediation and enable recursive capital identity.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-02","text":"Surplus-value formulas and accounting decompositions remain local measuring apparatuses; at a higher level, they are integrated into an architecture of layered times of labour, reproduction, and accumulation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:CGD-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-03","text":"Machine anatomy and concrete factory forms remain at the technical sublevel; scaling upward is the displacement of social unity and control into an objectified organism of production.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-04","text":"Wage forms, reserve forms, and institutional mediators remain particular implementations; bearing the whole book is their function of concealing unpaid labour and producing flexible labour availability.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-05","text":"Acts of expropriation, disciplinary laws, and land policies remain historical procedures; at the level of the whole book, they become legible as the political production and restoration of producer separation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:CGD-06","text":"The colonial counter-test remains a particular site, but scales as proof that the normalized capital relation presupposes blocked possibilities of exit and propertylessness.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-01","text":"Value and capital must be derived neither from utility and the nature of things nor from the possession of money or means of production.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-02","text":"Mere circulation cannot generate any social surplus-value, and means of production, despite their technical efficacy, cannot form an autonomous source of new value.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-03","text":"Legal equality must be equated neither with material self-disposal nor with a guarantee of real control over one's own labour-time and life-time.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-04","text":"Excluded is a neutral concept of technology or productivity that separates technical performance from property, labour displacement, selection by valorization, and free time.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-05","text":"The labour market and wage dependence must not appear as spontaneous results of exchange or population movement, because political violence constitutes propertylessness and the supply of labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-06","text":"Excluded are automatic employment compensation and definitive regulatory or territorial closures, because labour displacement and spatial feedback form functional moments of expansion.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:GNX-07","text":"Capital growth must not be identified with successful social reproduction, since expansion remains compatible with reserve formation, pauperization, and destroyed conditions of reproduction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture of value to persist, private labour must not be immediately social; an immediate association of producers would render its objective form of validation superfluous.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-02","text":"General and secure access to conditions of labour is incompatible with a permanently available class of wage-workers, because it would abolish the reproduced necessity of sale.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-03","text":"Reproduction must not be mere repetition, and founding violence must not disappear completely; otherwise class continuity and political reclosure would be inexplicable.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-04","text":"Family, consumption, and nature must not form an autonomous outside, and capital growth must not count as a sufficient measure of their reproduction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-05","text":"Capital must count neither as static possession nor as a self-sufficient subject, because its continuation presupposes repeated coupling with living labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:DBN-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:DBN-06","text":"An automatic transition from capitalist socialization is impermissible; material possibility replaces neither political sequence nor institutional construction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-01","text":"The deepest structuring absence is the collective worker as collective owner, director, and regulator of the organism of production brought forth by it.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is the immediate transformation of technical labour-saving into general free time; time of one's own arises only through the social limitation of time spent selling labour-power.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-02","MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-03","text":"Excluded remain both an innocent origin of property and a consequence-free territorial outside to which the costs of valorization could be permanently externalized.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSA-04","text":"The system circles around a collective counter-form, but cannot close the gap between its material possibility and its political production.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-01","text":"The objective objectivity of value and producer separation jointly generate a relation that appears in things, although its efficacy arises from social dependence; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-01","WB_V4GB:GA-02","WB_V4GB:GA-03","MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-02","text":"The difference between the value and use of labour-power transforms the locally equivalent individual contract, by way of reproduced propertylessness, into a cyclical appropriation without social equivalent; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-03","WB_V4GB:GA-04","WB_V4GB:GA-05","WB_V4GB:GA-06","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-03","text":"Cooperative productive power migrates into the machine organism and reverses the social interconnection of producers into an objective power of command over them; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-08","WB_V4GB:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-04","text":"The political limitation of extensive surplus-labour can act as a compulsion toward modernization because it shifts valorization toward intensification, productivity, and technical reconfiguration; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-07","WB_V4GB:GA-11","WB_V4GB:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-05","text":"Under private disposal, social labour-saving does not necessarily become free time, but can return, through an altered composition of capital, as labour displacement and flexible reserve; Trace Type — Negative.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-07","WB_V4GB:GA-09","WB_V4GB:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-11","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-06","text":"Competition generalizes local advantages in productivity, abolishes them as special advantages, and renews, through declining proportional demand for labour, the compulsion toward innovation and discipline; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-09","WB_V4GB:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-07","text":"State power is at once the enforcing instance of a limitation and the medium of restoring conditions of valorization; its contradictory function therefore belongs to the reproduction of the relation itself; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-11","WB_V4GB:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-08","text":"The reproduction of labour-power distributes uncompensated consequences of wear across family, society, nature, and territories, without being able permanently to remove these costs from the overall process; Trace Type — Composite.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-10","WB_V4GB:GA-12","WB_V4GB:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:XD-09","text":"The further production and reproduction are socialized, the more strongly collective disposal operates as a systemic attractor; yet no sufficient mechanism of transition follows from this intensification; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["WB_V4GB:GA-13","WB_V4GB:GA-14","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}]},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-01","text":"Reality acquires the status of a relational process-reality in which living labour produces objective power and this power reproduces the conditions of further subordination.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes a distributed and switchable system position between commodity possession, wage labour, machine function, reserve, and possible collective appropriation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-03","text":"Capitalist time is retrospective, antagonistic, and layered: market validation, the working day, synchronization, the period of reproduction, the cycle of accumulation, and historical violence operate simultaneously.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes multilayered and recursive because demographic, technical, proprietary, and political effects become presuppositions of the next round of valorization.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-05","text":"Politics is not an external addition to economics, but the struggle over conditions of labour, time limits, possibilities of exit, reserve formation, and social combination.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-06","text":"History appears as the present reproduction of past violence and as the non-teleological production of material conditions of transformation, whose political activation remains open.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:BSD-07","text":"Knowledge must combine genetic analysis of forms, technical reconstruction, class reproduction, genealogy, and territorial counter-experiment, because no individual perspective bears the overall mechanism.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:BSD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-01","text":"Private labour produces commodities, exchange validates them, value returns as an advance of capital, and the enlarged reflux makes the result the presupposition of renewed production.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-02","text":"Producer separation compels the sale of labour-power, wage consumption reproduces the capacity for sale, and repetition simultaneously reproduces the relation of separation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:CGD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-03","text":"Social mediation erases its genesis, appears as a property of the machine organism, and thereby seemingly confirms the necessity of capital command.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-04","text":"Overwork and evasion generate resistance and control; intensified control in turn generates intensification, innovation, and new forms of evasion.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-05","text":"An advantage in productivity becomes the social norm, abolishes the individual advantage, and returns as labour displacement, reserve formation, and renewed compulsion toward innovation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:XD-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-06","text":"Open violence normalizes the wage relation, disappears into mute coercion, and is reactivated as political intervention when its presuppositions are endangered.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-07","text":"Spatial externalization produces no outside, but rather territorial feedback in which exported labour-powers, costs, and conflicts return economically or politically.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:RLE-08","text":"The dominant attractor is the maximum appropriation of social labour-time; its negative counter-attractor is conscious collective disposal over the socialized conditions of this labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:RLE-08","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B01","text":"Producer separation + independent private labour → compulsion to exchange → abstract equation → objective value-objectivity → retrospective social validity.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B02","text":"Value-form + monetary mediation + legal self-disposal + material lack of means of production → labour-power as purchasable commodity → asymmetric disposal in the production process.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B03","text":"Use of labour-power → preservation of value + formation of new value + exceeding necessary labour → surplus-labour → surplus-value.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B04","text":"Surplus-value production + realization + renewed advance → reproduction of the capital relation → results as presuppositions of the subsequent cycle.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B05","text":"Concentration + cooperation + social knowledge → non-additive productive power → objectified machine organism → autonomized capital command.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:GA-12","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B06","text":"Capitalized surplus-value + increase in productive power → rising organic composition → relative labour displacement → reserve formation → wage discipline and flexible expansion.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B07","text":"Social, legal, or spatial limit → intensification, technical reconfiguration, or political reclosure → restoration of the conditions of valorization at a higher organizational level.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FGS-B08","text":"Socialization + private appropriation + undermining of conditions of reproduction → negative attractor of collective disposal, yet without an automatic sequence of transition.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-13","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:AFM-B01","text":"Private labour → value-form → money → capital advance → purchase of labour-power → production process → surplus-labour → surplus-value → renewed advance.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-04","MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AFM-B02","text":"Division into necessary labour and surplus-labour without an immanent measure of total duration → opposing claims to time, decided by neither market nor nature or private morality → collectively enforced and institutionally enforceable limitation → relative surplus-value production → cooperation and machinery → accumulation → altered composition → reserve formation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:AS-07","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:AFM-B03","text":"Violent producer separation → normalized wage relation → technical and reproductive reclosure → extended socialization → intensified property contradiction → material possibility, but politically and institutionally indeterminate collective counter-appropriation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-01","text":"Capital is remapped from possession of money or things into a recursive apparatus for the capture, objectification, and reproduction of social labour-power.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-02","text":"Market equality and command over production become legible as successive levels of the same relation of appropriation, not as mutually exclusive descriptions.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-03","text":"The concept of output expands from commodities and surplus-value to class positions, the reserve population, property separation, and conditions of nature.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-04","text":"Productivity decomposes into technical capacity, use-value effect, value formation, social labour-saving, and capitalist profitability; its apparent neutrality collapses.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-01","MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-05","text":"The opposition between state and market collapses because legally enabled appropriation of labour-time is politically limited and its endangered conditions are repaired by the state.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-05","MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-06","text":"Centre and periphery are reconstructed as feedback-linked spaces: the colonial breakdown of naturalized categories reveals presuppositions that appear sedimented at the centre.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MME-07","text":"Property and freedom split into capitalist private property, property based on one's own labour, and cooperative appropriation; material freedom is measured by access to social conditions of labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MME-07","MC_V4GB_L1_01:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B01","text":"At the Surface level, commodity, money, labour-power, surplus-value, machine, wage, employment, and migration appear as heterogeneous objects of the capital process.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B02","text":"At the Structural level, value mediation, property, producer separation, subsumption, unpaid labour, division of time, and reserve formation connect these objects into an architecture of reproduction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B03","text":"At the Metastrategic level, intervention shifts from the individual contract and technical object to access to property, class continuity, limits on labour-time, and collective disposal.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B04","text":"At the Ontological / Temporal level, past labour commands present labour, while finite vital force is subject to a recursive order of retrospective validation and cumulative accumulation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:ALT-B05","text":"At the Methodological / Performative level, the exposition enacts its thesis through genetic regression, reintroduction of excluded mediations, shifts of scale, and reconstruction of every solution as a new stage of contradiction.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:ALT-B05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-01","text":"Abstract labour oscillates between generally human expenditure and a specific form of social validity; its unity remains dependent on retrospective validation; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-02","text":"The presentation of capital as an automatic subject collides with its dependence on living labour and its simultaneous compulsion to reduce the proportional employment of that labour; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-03","text":"The separation between machine and capitalist application remains unstable because technology is not supposed to be autonomously capitalist, yet its concrete form already arises under selection by valorization; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-04","text":"Local exchange of equivalents and global appropriation without equivalent remain compatible only through a shift of scale; its blurring threatens conceptual coherence; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-05","text":"The state appears simultaneously as guarantor of the property order, enforcer of its limitation, and agent of its technical modernization; the institutional reversal remains underdetermined; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:FL-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:FL-06","text":"Collective counter-appropriation is mediated more weakly than the genesis and reproduction of the capital relation, because material possibility, political organization, and institution fall apart; Trace Type — Tension.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-01","text":"Capital mutates from a form-changing advance of value into a recursive social power that produces its own bearers and presuppositions.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-02","text":"Labour-power mutates from the sold capacity, through living labour and collective-worker function, into the segmented position between machine appendage, seller, and reserve.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-03","text":"Time mutates from the measure of value into a contested limit, synchronized production time, and recursive layering of historical, reproductive, and accumulative duration.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-04","text":"Freedom mutates from legal contractual capacity into collectively enforced counter-force and ultimately into the material capacity to leave wage labour through disposal over conditions of labour.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-05","text":"Productive power mutates from cooperative organizational power into a concentrated condition of command and further into the unity of increased surplus-value, labour displacement, and reserve formation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MP-06","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MP-06","text":"Limitation mutates from an external barrier into a mechanism of innovation, while violence shifts from open intervention to mute coercion and, under instability, back to intervention.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MP-05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a machine of validation, separation, and conversion that crystallizes social relations in things and translates rights of access into repeatable conditions of valorization.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not a sovereign centre, but a dependent organ and a switchable position between capital function, wage labour, reserve, and possible collective appropriation.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-03","text":"Time is retroactive, finite, divisible, synchronized, and cumulative; capital does not produce it, but validates, condenses, layers, and appropriates it.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:HSI-04","text":"Struggle consists in regaining social combination as well as in disposal over conditions of labour, technical application, possibilities of exit, and reproduction time.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:HSI-04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B01","text":"The overall architecture is reconstructible if value-form, recursive movement of capital, producer separation, labour-power, unpaid labour, objectified productive power, class reproduction, and reserve formation are jointly retained.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B01","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B02","text":"Its strongest structure lies in endogenization: value-objectivity, appropriation of labour-time, technical organization, labour supply, and political reclosure are transformed from effects of the process into conditions of its repetition.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B02","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B03","text":"What remain underdetermined are the institutional transformation of class power, quantitative movements of employment, and the relative weighting of technical, demographic, and political mechanisms.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B03","MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B04","text":"The positive form of collective disposal remains insufficiently determined because neither its political sequence nor its enduring institutional organization follows from the negative architecture.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_02:MRT-B05","MC_V4GB_L1_02:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B05","text":"Coherence depends on connecting and distinguishing simultaneously value and use-value, productivity and value formation, coordination and command, as well as local equality of exchange and reproductive class power.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B04","MC_V4GB_L1_02:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_V4GB:MRT-B06","text":"What resists axiomatic reduction are the practical reversals in which cooperation is realized simultaneously as productive power and alien power, and in which terminal openness would have to pass into political form.","refs":["MC_V4GB_L1_01:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}]}],"revision":"WB_V4GB@R002","source_variant_id":"canonical:WB_V4GB:WB_V4GB@R002","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"WB","kicker":"Whole book","title":"Capital Volume 1","context":""}}],"seal":"SEAL_V4GB_196DF0AF7C84E9BC7F9B","version_work_id":"WORK_STORE_HISTORICAL_MARX_CAPITAL_I_1867","version_label":"Added 16 Oct 2026 · Run 16 Oct 2026 · gpt-5.6-terra / gpt-5.6-sol","version_revision":"e4596e253f3fe2670838a2ed44f8be68e127e72e687d632ce4da7b72bed5a000"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG6729","slug":"beta-f03cac44c6d2d3c9","title":"Science of Logic","author":"Georg Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel","edition":"Project Gutenberg transcription","year":"1813","original_year":1813,"publication_year":null,"description":"","cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-f03cac44c6d2d3c9-d925a75208887813.png","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/6729","source_notices":{"provider":"Project Gutenberg editions","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/6729","licence":"https://www.gutenberg.org/policy/license.html","statement":"Freely available from Project Gutenberg; edition and local rights review required"},"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","sources":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA","title":"Preface to the First Edition.","order":1,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_VZEA","text":"Die völlige Umänderung, welche die philosophische Denkweise seit etwa fünf und zwanzig Jahren unter uns erlitten, der höhere Standpunkt, den das Selbstbewußtseyn des Geistes in dieser Zeitperiode über sich erreicht hat, hat bisher noch wenig Einfluß auf die Gestalt der Logik gehabt.\n\nDasjenige, was vor diesem Zeitraum Metaphysik hieß, ist, so zu sagen, mit Stumpf und Stiel ausgerottet worden, und aus der Reihe der Wissenschaften verschwunden. Wo lassen oder wo dürfen sich Laute der vormaligen Ontologie, der rationellen Psychologie, der Kosmologie oder selbst gar der vormaligen natürlichen Theologie noch vernehmen lassen? Untersuchungen, zum Beispiel über die Immaterialität der Seele, über die mechanische und die Endursachen, wo sollten sie noch ein Interesse finden? Auch die sonstige Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes werden nur historisch, oder zum Behufe der Erbauung und Gemüthserhebung angeführt. Es ist dieß ein Faktum, daß das Interesse Theils am Inhalte, Theils an der Form der vormaligen Metaphysik, Theils an beiden zugleich verloren ist. So merkwürdig es ist, wenn einem Volke, z.B. die Wissenschaft seines Staatsrechts, wenn ihm seine Gesinnungen, seine sittlichen Gewohnheiten und Tugenden unbrauchbar geworden sind, so merkwürdig ist es wenigstens, wenn ein Volk seine Metaphysik verliert, wenn der mit seinem reinen Wesen sich beschäftigende Geist kein wirkliches Daseyn mehr in demselben hat.\n\nDie exoterische Lehre der kantischen Philosophie,—daß der Verstand die Erfahrung nicht überfliegen dürfe, sonst werde das Erkenntnisvermögen theoretische Vernunft, welche für sich nichts als Hirngespinnste gebähre, hat es von der wissenschaftlichen Seite gerechtfertigt, dem spekulativen Denken zu entsagen. Dieser popularen Lehre kam das Geschrei der modernen Pädagogik, die Noth der Zeiten, die den Blick auf das unmittelbare Bedürfniß richtet, entgegen, daß, wie für die Erkenntniß die Erfahrung das Erste, so für die Geschicklichkeit im öffentlichen und Privatleben, theoretische Einsicht sogar schädlich, und Übung und praktische Bildung überhaupt das Wesentliche, allein Förderliche sey.—Indem so die Wissenschaft und der gemeine Menschenverstand sich in die Hände arbeiteten, den Untergang der Metaphysik zu bewirken, so schien das sonderbare Schauspiel herbeigeführt zu werden, ein gebildetes Volk ohne Metaphysik zu sehen;—wie einen sonst mannigfaltig ausgeschmückten Tempel ohne Allerheiligstes.—Die Theologie, welche in frühern Zeiten die Bewahrerin der spekulativen Mysterien und der obzwar abhängigen Metaphysik war, hatte diese Wissenschaft gegen Gefühle, gegen das Praktisch-populare und gelehrte Historische aufgegeben. Welcher Veränderung entsprechend ist, daß anderwärts jene Einsamen, die von ihrem Volke aufgeopfert und aus der Welt ausgeschieden wurden, zu dem Zwecke, daß die Kontemplation des Ewigen und ein ihr allein dienendes Leben vorhanden sey, nicht um eines Nutzens, sondern um des Segens willen,—verschwanden; ein Verschwinden, das in einem andern Zusammenhange, dem Wesen nach als dieselbe Erscheinung, wie das vorhin Erwähnte, betrachtet werden kann.—So daß, nach Vertreibung dieser Finsternisse, der farblosen Beschäftigung des in sich gekehrten Geistes mit sich selbst, das Daseyn in die heitere Welt der Blumen verwandelt zu seyn schien, unter denen es bekanntlich keine schwarze giebt.\n\nGanz so schlimm als der Metaphysik ist es der Logik nicht ergangen. Daß man durch sie denken lerne, was sonst für ihren Nutzen und damit für den Zweck derselben galt,—gleichsam als ob man durch das Studium der Anatomie und Physiologie erst verdauen und sich bewegen lernen sollte—, dieß Vorurtheil hat sich längst verloren, und der Geist des Praktischen dachte ihr wohl kein besseres Schicksal zu, als ihrer Schwester. Dessen ungeachtet, wahrscheinlich um einigen formellen Nutzens willen, wurde ihr noch ein Rang unter den Wissenschaften gelassen, ja sie wurde selbst als Gegenstand des öffentlichen Unterrichts beibehalten. Dieß bessere Loos betrifft jedoch nur das äußere Schicksal; denn ihre Gestalt und Inhalt ist derselbe geblieben, als er sich durch eine lange Tradition fortgeerbt, jedoch in dieser Überlieferung immer mehr verdünnt und abgemagert hatte; der neue Geist, welcher der Wissenschaft nicht weniger als der Wirklichkeit aufgegangen ist, hat sich in ihr noch nicht verspüren lassen. Es ist aber ein für allemal vergebens, wenn die substantielle Form des Geistes sich umgestaltet hat, die Formen früherer Bildung erhalten zu wollen; sie sind welke Blätter, welche von den neuen Knospen, die an ihren Wurzeln schon erzeugt sind, abgestoßen werden.\n\nMit dem Ignoriren der allgemeinen Veränderung fängt es nach gerade an, auch im Wissenschaftlichen auszugehen. Unbemerkter Weise sind selbst den Gegnern die andern Vorstellung geläufig und eigen geworden, und wenn sie gegen deren Quelle und Principien fortdauernd spröde thun und sich widersprechend dagegen benehmen, so haben sie dafür die Konsequenzen sich gefallen lassen, und des Einflusses derselben sich nicht zu erwehren vermocht; zu ihrem immer unbedeutender werdenden negativen Verhalten wissen sie sich auf keine andere Weise eine positive Wichtigkeit und einen Inhalt zu geben, als daß sie in den neuen Vorstellungsweisen mitsprechen.\n\nVon der andern Seite scheint die Zeit der Gährung, mit der eine neue Schöpfung beginnt, vorbei zu seyn. In ihrer ersten Erscheinung pflegt eine solche sich mit fanatischer Feindseligkeit gegen die ausgebreitete Systematisierung des frühen Princips zu verhalten, Theils auch furchtsam zu seyn, sich in der Ausdehnung des Besondern zu verlieren, Theils aber die Arbeit die zur wissenschaftlichen Ausbildung erfordert wird, zu scheuen, und im Bedürfnisse einer solchen zuerst zu einem leeren Formalismus zu greifen. Die Anforderung der Verarbeitung und Ausbildung des Stoffes wird nun um so dringender. Es ist eine Periode in der Bildung einer Zeit, wie in der Bildung des Individuums, wo es vornehmlich um Erwerbung und Behauptung des Princips in seiner unentwickelten Intensität zu thun ist. Aber die höhere Forderung geht darauf, daß es zur Wissenschaft werde.\n\nWas nun auch für die Sache und für die Form der Wissenschaft bereits in sonstiger Rücksicht geschehen seyn mag; die logische Wissenschaft, welche die eigentliche Metaphysik oder reine spekulative Philosophie ausmacht, hat sich bisher noch sehr vernachlässigt gesehen. Was ich unter dieser Wissenschaft und ihrer Standpunkte näher verstehe, habe ich in der Einleitung vorläufig angegeben. Die Nothwendigkeit, mit dieser Wissenschaft wieder einmal von vorne anzufangen, die Natur des Gegenstandes selbst, und der Mangel an Vorarbeiten, welche für die vorgenommene Umbildung hätten benutzt werden können, mögen bei billigen Beurtheilern in Rücksicht kommen, wenn auch eine vieljährige Arbeit diesem Versuche nicht eine größere Vollkommenheit geben konnte.—Der wesentliche Gesichtspunkt ist, daß es überhaupt um einen neuen Begriff wissenschaftlicher Behandlung zu thun ist. Die Philosophie, indem sie Wissenschaft seyn soll, kann, wie ich anderwärts erinnert [1] habe, hierzu ihre Methode nicht von einer untergeordneten Wissenschaft, wie die Mathematik ist, borgen, so wenig als es bei kategorischen Versicherungen innerer Anschauung bewenden lassen, oder sich des Raisonnements aus Gründen der äußern Reflexion bedienen. Sondern es kann nur die Natur des Inhalts seyn, welche sich im wissenschaftlichen Erkennen bewegt, indem zugleich diese eigne Reflexion des Inhalts es ist, welche seine Bestimmung selbst erst setzt und erzeugt.\n\n[1] Phänomenologie des Geistes, Vorrede zur ersten Ausgabe—Die eigentliche Ausführung ist die Erkenntniß der Methode, und hat ihre Stelle in der Logik selbst.\n\nDer Verstand bestimmt und hält die Bestimmungen fest; die Vernunft ist negativ und dialektisch, weil sie die Bestimmungen des Verstands in Nichts auflöst; sie ist positiv, weil sie das Allgemeine erzeugt, und das Besondere darin begreift. Wie der Verstand als etwas Getrenntes von der Vernunft überhaupt, so pflegt auch die dialektische Vernunft als etwas Getrenntes von der positiven Vernunft genommen zu werden. Aber in ihrer Wahrheit ist die Vernunft Geist, der höher als Beides, verständige Vernunft, oder vernünftiger Verstand ist. Er ist das Negative, dasjenige, welches die Qualität sowohl, der dialektischen Vernunft, als des Verstandes ausmacht;—er negirt das Einfache, so setzt er den bestimmten Unterschied des Verstandes, er löst ihn eben so sehr auf, so ist er dialektisch. Er hält sich aber nicht im Nichts dieses Resultates, sondern ist darin ebenso positiv, und hat so das erste Einfache damit hergestellt, aber als Allgemeines, das in sich konkret ist; unter dieses wird nicht ein gegebenes Besonderes subsumirt, sondern in jenem Bestimmen und in der Auflösung desselben hat sich das Besondere schon mit bestimmt. Diese geistige Bewegung, die sich in ihrer Einfachheit ihre Bestimmtheit, und in dieser ihre Gleichheit mit sich selbst giebt, die somit die immanente Entwickelung des Begriffes ist, ist die absolute Methode des Erkennens, und zugleich die immanente Seele des Inhalts selbst. —Auf diesem sich selbst konstruirenden Wege allein, behaupte ich, ist die Philosophie fähig, objektive, demonstrirte Wissenschaft zu seyn.—In dieser Weise habe ich das Bewußtseyn in der Phänomenologie des Geistes darzustellen versucht. Das Bewußtseyn ist der Geist als konkretes und zwar in der Äußerlichkeit befangenes Wissen; aber die Formbewegung dieses Gegenstandes beruht allein, wie die Entwickelung alles natürlichen und geistigen Lebens, auf der Natur der reinen Wesenheiten, die den Inhalt der Logik ausmachen. Das Bewußtseyn, als der erscheinende Geist, welcher sich auf seinem Wege von seiner Unmittelbarkeit und äußerlichen Konkretion befreit, wird zum reinen Wissen, das sich jene reinen Wesenheiten selbst, wie sie an und für sich sind, zum Gegenstand giebt. Sie sind die reinen Gedanken, der sein Wesen denkende Geist. Ihre Selbstbewegung ist ihr geistiges Leben, und ist das, wodurch sich die Wissenschaft konstituirt, und dessen Darstellung sie ist.\n\nEs ist hiermit die Beziehung der Wissenschaft, die ich Phänomenologie des Geistes nenne, zur Logik angegeben.—Was das äußerliche Verhältniß betrifft, so war dem ersten Theil des Systems der Wissenschaft, [2] der die Phänomenologie enthält, ein zweiter Theil zu folgen bestimmt, welcher die Logik und die beiden realen Wissenschaften der Philosophie, die Philosophie der Natur und die Philosophie des Geistes, enthalten sollte, und das System der Wissenschaft beschlossen haben würde. Aber die nothwendige Ausdehnung, welche die Logik für sich erhalten mußte, hat mich veranlaßt, diese besonders ans Licht treten zu lassen; sie macht also in einem erweiterten Plane die erste Folge zur Phänomenologie des Geistes aus. Späterhin werde ich die Verarbeitung der beiden genannten realen Wissenschaften der Philosophie folgen lassen.—Dieser erste Band der Logik aber enthält als erstes Buch die Lehre vom Seyn; das zweite Buch, die Lehre vom Wesen, als zweite Abtheilung des ersten Bandes; der zweite Band aber wird die subjektive Logik, oder die Lehre vom Begriff enthalten.\n\nNürnberg, den 22 März 1812\n\n[2] (Bamberg und Würzburg bei Göbhard 1807). Dieser Titel wird der zweiten Ausgabe, die auf nächsten Ostern erscheinen wird, nicht mehr beigegeben werden.—An die Stelle des im Folgenden erwähnten Vorhabens eines zweiten Theils, der die sämmtlichen andern philosophischen Wissenschaften enthalten sollte, habe ich seitdem die Encyklopädie der philosophischen Wissenschaften, voriges Jahr in der dritten Ausgabe, ans Licht treten lassen (Anmerkung zur zweiten Ausgabe),","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","text":"Die völlige Umänderung, welche die philosophische Denkweise seit etwa fünf und zwanzig Jahren unter uns erlitten, der höhere Standpunkt, den das Selbstbewußtseyn des Geistes in dieser Zeitperiode über sich erreicht hat, hat bisher noch wenig Einfluß auf die Gestalt der Logik gehabt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"1.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","text":"Dasjenige, was vor diesem Zeitraum Metaphysik hieß, ist, so zu sagen, mit Stumpf und Stiel ausgerottet worden, und aus der Reihe der Wissenschaften verschwunden. Wo lassen oder wo dürfen sich Laute der vormaligen Ontologie, der rationellen Psychologie, der Kosmologie oder selbst gar der vormaligen natürlichen Theologie noch vernehmen lassen? Untersuchungen, zum Beispiel über die Immaterialität der Seele, über die mechanische und die Endursachen, wo sollten sie noch ein Interesse finden? Auch die sonstige Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes werden nur historisch, oder zum Behufe der Erbauung und Gemüthserhebung angeführt. Es ist dieß ein Faktum, daß das Interesse Theils am Inhalte, Theils an der Form der vormaligen Metaphysik, Theils an beiden zugleich verloren ist. So merkwürdig es ist, wenn einem Volke, z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"1.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003","text":"die Wissenschaft seines Staatsrechts, wenn ihm seine Gesinnungen, seine sittlichen Gewohnheiten und Tugenden unbrauchbar geworden sind, so merkwürdig ist es wenigstens, wenn ein Volk seine Metaphysik verliert, wenn der mit seinem reinen Wesen sich beschäftigende Geist kein wirkliches Daseyn mehr in demselben hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"1.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0004","text":"Die exoterische Lehre der kantischen Philosophie,—daß der Verstand die Erfahrung nicht überfliegen dürfe, sonst werde das Erkenntnisvermögen theoretische Vernunft, welche für sich nichts als Hirngespinnste gebähre, hat es von der wissenschaftlichen Seite gerechtfertigt, dem spekulativen Denken zu entsagen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"1.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0005","text":"Dieser popularen Lehre kam das Geschrei der modernen Pädagogik, die Noth der Zeiten, die den Blick auf das unmittelbare Bedürfniß richtet, entgegen, daß, wie für die Erkenntniß die Erfahrung das Erste, so für die Geschicklichkeit im öffentlichen und Privatleben, theoretische Einsicht sogar schädlich, und Übung und praktische Bildung überhaupt das Wesentliche, allein Förderliche sey.—Indem so die Wissenschaft und der gemeine Menschenverstand sich in die Hände arbeiteten, den Untergang der Metaphysik zu bewirken, so schien das sonderbare Schauspiel herbeigeführt zu werden, ein gebildetes Volk ohne Metaphysik zu sehen;—wie einen sonst mannigfaltig ausgeschmückten Tempel ohne Allerheiligstes.—Die Theologie, welche in frühern Zeiten die Bewahrerin der spekulativen Mysterien und der obzwar abhängigen Metaphysik war, hatte diese Wissenschaft gegen Gefühle, gegen das Praktisch-populare und","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"1.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0006","text":"gelehrte Historische aufgegeben. Welcher Veränderung entsprechend ist, daß anderwärts jene Einsamen, die von ihrem Volke aufgeopfert und aus der Welt ausgeschieden wurden, zu dem Zwecke, daß die Kontemplation des Ewigen und ein ihr allein dienendes Leben vorhanden sey, nicht um eines Nutzens, sondern um des Segens willen,—verschwanden; ein Verschwinden, das in einem andern Zusammenhange, dem Wesen nach als dieselbe Erscheinung, wie das vorhin Erwähnte, betrachtet werden kann.—So daß, nach Vertreibung dieser Finsternisse, der farblosen Beschäftigung des in sich gekehrten Geistes mit sich selbst, das Daseyn in die heitere Welt der Blumen verwandelt zu seyn schien, unter denen es bekanntlich keine schwarze giebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"1.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","text":"Ganz so schlimm als der Metaphysik ist es der Logik nicht ergangen. Daß man durch sie denken lerne, was sonst für ihren Nutzen und damit für den Zweck derselben galt,—gleichsam als ob man durch das Studium der Anatomie und Physiologie erst verdauen und sich bewegen lernen sollte—, dieß Vorurtheil hat sich längst verloren, und der Geist des Praktischen dachte ihr wohl kein besseres Schicksal zu, als ihrer Schwester. Dessen ungeachtet, wahrscheinlich um einigen formellen Nutzens willen, wurde ihr noch ein Rang unter den Wissenschaften gelassen, ja sie wurde selbst als Gegenstand des öffentlichen Unterrichts beibehalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"1.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","text":"Dieß bessere Loos betrifft jedoch nur das äußere Schicksal; denn ihre Gestalt und Inhalt ist derselbe geblieben, als er sich durch eine lange Tradition fortgeerbt, jedoch in dieser Überlieferung immer mehr verdünnt und abgemagert hatte; der neue Geist, welcher der Wissenschaft nicht weniger als der Wirklichkeit aufgegangen ist, hat sich in ihr noch nicht verspüren lassen. Es ist aber ein für allemal vergebens, wenn die substantielle Form des Geistes sich umgestaltet hat, die Formen früherer Bildung erhalten zu wollen; sie sind welke Blätter, welche von den neuen Knospen, die an ihren Wurzeln schon erzeugt sind, abgestoßen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"1.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0009","text":"Mit dem Ignoriren der allgemeinen Veränderung fängt es nach gerade an, auch im Wissenschaftlichen auszugehen. Unbemerkter Weise sind selbst den Gegnern die andern Vorstellung geläufig und eigen geworden, und wenn sie gegen deren Quelle und Principien fortdauernd spröde thun und sich widersprechend dagegen benehmen, so haben sie dafür die Konsequenzen sich gefallen lassen, und des Einflusses derselben sich nicht zu erwehren vermocht; zu ihrem immer unbedeutender werdenden negativen Verhalten wissen sie sich auf keine andere Weise eine positive Wichtigkeit und einen Inhalt zu geben, als daß sie in den neuen Vorstellungsweisen mitsprechen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"1.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","text":"Von der andern Seite scheint die Zeit der Gährung, mit der eine neue Schöpfung beginnt, vorbei zu seyn. In ihrer ersten Erscheinung pflegt eine solche sich mit fanatischer Feindseligkeit gegen die ausgebreitete Systematisierung des frühen Princips zu verhalten, Theils auch furchtsam zu seyn, sich in der Ausdehnung des Besondern zu verlieren, Theils aber die Arbeit die zur wissenschaftlichen Ausbildung erfordert wird, zu scheuen, und im Bedürfnisse einer solchen zuerst zu einem leeren Formalismus zu greifen. Die Anforderung der Verarbeitung und Ausbildung des Stoffes wird nun um so dringender. Es ist eine Periode in der Bildung einer Zeit, wie in der Bildung des Individuums, wo es vornehmlich um Erwerbung und Behauptung des Princips in seiner unentwickelten Intensität zu thun ist. Aber die höhere Forderung geht darauf, daß es zur Wissenschaft werde.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"1.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","text":"Was nun auch für die Sache und für die Form der Wissenschaft bereits in sonstiger Rücksicht geschehen seyn mag; die logische Wissenschaft, welche die eigentliche Metaphysik oder reine spekulative Philosophie ausmacht, hat sich bisher noch sehr vernachlässigt gesehen. Was ich unter dieser Wissenschaft und ihrer Standpunkte näher verstehe, habe ich in der Einleitung vorläufig angegeben. Die Nothwendigkeit, mit dieser Wissenschaft wieder einmal von vorne anzufangen, die Natur des Gegenstandes selbst, und der Mangel an Vorarbeiten, welche für die vorgenommene Umbildung hätten benutzt werden können, mögen bei billigen Beurtheilern in Rücksicht kommen, wenn auch eine vieljährige Arbeit diesem Versuche nicht eine größere Vollkommenheit geben konnte.—Der wesentliche Gesichtspunkt ist, daß es überhaupt um einen neuen Begriff wissenschaftlicher Behandlung zu thun ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"1.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","text":"Die Philosophie, indem sie Wissenschaft seyn soll, kann, wie ich anderwärts erinnert [1] habe, hierzu ihre Methode nicht von einer untergeordneten Wissenschaft, wie die Mathematik ist, borgen, so wenig als es bei kategorischen Versicherungen innerer Anschauung bewenden lassen, oder sich des Raisonnements aus Gründen der äußern Reflexion bedienen. Sondern es kann nur die Natur des Inhalts seyn, welche sich im wissenschaftlichen Erkennen bewegt, indem zugleich diese eigne Reflexion des Inhalts es ist, welche seine Bestimmung selbst erst setzt und erzeugt.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"1.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0013","text":"[1] Phänomenologie des Geistes, Vorrede zur ersten Ausgabe—Die eigentliche Ausführung ist die Erkenntniß der Methode, und hat ihre Stelle in der Logik selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"1.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","text":"Der Verstand bestimmt und hält die Bestimmungen fest; die Vernunft ist negativ und dialektisch, weil sie die Bestimmungen des Verstands in Nichts auflöst; sie ist positiv, weil sie das Allgemeine erzeugt, und das Besondere darin begreift. Wie der Verstand als etwas Getrenntes von der Vernunft überhaupt, so pflegt auch die dialektische Vernunft als etwas Getrenntes von der positiven Vernunft genommen zu werden. Aber in ihrer Wahrheit ist die Vernunft Geist, der höher als Beides, verständige Vernunft, oder vernünftiger Verstand ist. Er ist das Negative, dasjenige, welches die Qualität sowohl, der dialektischen Vernunft, als des Verstandes ausmacht;—er negirt das Einfache, so setzt er den bestimmten Unterschied des Verstandes, er löst ihn eben so sehr auf, so ist er dialektisch.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"1.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","text":"Er hält sich aber nicht im Nichts dieses Resultates, sondern ist darin ebenso positiv, und hat so das erste Einfache damit hergestellt, aber als Allgemeines, das in sich konkret ist; unter dieses wird nicht ein gegebenes Besonderes subsumirt, sondern in jenem Bestimmen und in der Auflösung desselben hat sich das Besondere schon mit bestimmt. Diese geistige Bewegung, die sich in ihrer Einfachheit ihre Bestimmtheit, und in dieser ihre Gleichheit mit sich selbst giebt, die somit die immanente Entwickelung des Begriffes ist, ist die absolute Methode des Erkennens, und zugleich die immanente Seele des Inhalts selbst. —Auf diesem sich selbst konstruirenden Wege allein, behaupte ich, ist die Philosophie fähig, objektive, demonstrirte Wissenschaft zu seyn.—In dieser Weise habe ich das Bewußtseyn in der Phänomenologie des Geistes darzustellen versucht.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"1.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","text":"Das Bewußtseyn ist der Geist als konkretes und zwar in der Äußerlichkeit befangenes Wissen; aber die Formbewegung dieses Gegenstandes beruht allein, wie die Entwickelung alles natürlichen und geistigen Lebens, auf der Natur der reinen Wesenheiten, die den Inhalt der Logik ausmachen. Das Bewußtseyn, als der erscheinende Geist, welcher sich auf seinem Wege von seiner Unmittelbarkeit und äußerlichen Konkretion befreit, wird zum reinen Wissen, das sich jene reinen Wesenheiten selbst, wie sie an und für sich sind, zum Gegenstand giebt. Sie sind die reinen Gedanken, der sein Wesen denkende Geist. Ihre Selbstbewegung ist ihr geistiges Leben, und ist das, wodurch sich die Wissenschaft konstituirt, und dessen Darstellung sie ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"1.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","text":"Es ist hiermit die Beziehung der Wissenschaft, die ich Phänomenologie des Geistes nenne, zur Logik angegeben.—Was das äußerliche Verhältniß betrifft, so war dem ersten Theil des Systems der Wissenschaft, [2] der die Phänomenologie enthält, ein zweiter Theil zu folgen bestimmt, welcher die Logik und die beiden realen Wissenschaften der Philosophie, die Philosophie der Natur und die Philosophie des Geistes, enthalten sollte, und das System der Wissenschaft beschlossen haben würde. Aber die nothwendige Ausdehnung, welche die Logik für sich erhalten mußte, hat mich veranlaßt, diese besonders ans Licht treten zu lassen; sie macht also in einem erweiterten Plane die erste Folge zur Phänomenologie des Geistes aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"1.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018","text":"Späterhin werde ich die Verarbeitung der beiden genannten realen Wissenschaften der Philosophie folgen lassen.—Dieser erste Band der Logik aber enthält als erstes Buch die Lehre vom Seyn; das zweite Buch, die Lehre vom Wesen, als zweite Abtheilung des ersten Bandes; der zweite Band aber wird die subjektive Logik, oder die Lehre vom Begriff enthalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"1.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0019","text":"Nürnberg, den 22 März 1812","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"1.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0020","text":"[2] (Bamberg und Würzburg bei Göbhard 1807). Dieser Titel wird der zweiten Ausgabe, die auf nächsten Ostern erscheinen wird, nicht mehr beigegeben werden.—An die Stelle des im Folgenden erwähnten Vorhabens eines zweiten Theils, der die sämmtlichen andern philosophischen Wissenschaften enthalten sollte, habe ich seitdem die Encyklopädie der philosophischen Wissenschaften, voriges Jahr in der dritten Ausgabe, ans Licht treten lassen (Anmerkung zur zweiten Ausgabe),","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"1.20"}],"sha256":"ff1b04f8dffc735b4bc2c2ac8297077d3b46644c68dd411426c0a7f6f85682a5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101257618884Z_adfe2884","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Preface to the First Edition.","source_sha256":"ff1b04f8dffc735b4bc2c2ac8297077d3b46644c68dd411426c0a7f6f85682a5","sha256":"319ac2afd75419d63473581f3d91e59a989d2f30b511d49c99ead7b72167b143","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:12:57.618905+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","text":"The complete transformation which the philosophical mode of thinking has undergone among us for approximately twenty-five years, the higher standpoint which the self-consciousness of Spirit has attained over itself in this period, has hitherto had little influence on the shape of logic.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"1.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","text":"That which before this period was called metaphysics has, so to speak, been eradicated root and branch, and has disappeared from the ranks of the sciences. Where do, or where may, sounds of the former ontology, rational psychology, cosmology, or indeed even the former natural theology still make themselves heard? Investigations, for example, concerning the immateriality of the soul, concerning mechanical and final causes—where could they still find an interest? Even the former proofs of the existence of God are adduced only historically, or for the purpose of edification and elevation of the mind. It is a fact that interest has been lost partly in the content, partly in the form of the former metaphysics, partly in both at once. Remarkable as it is when a people, e.g.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"1.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003","text":"the science of its constitutional law, when its dispositions, its moral habits and virtues have become useless to it, it is at least equally remarkable when a people loses its metaphysics, when the Spirit occupied with its pure essence no longer has any actual existence within it.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"1.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0004","text":"The exoteric doctrine of the Kantian philosophy—that the Understanding must not soar beyond experience, lest the faculty of cognition become theoretical Reason, which of itself gives birth to nothing but chimeras—has justified, from the scientific side, renouncing speculative thinking.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"1.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0005","text":"This popular doctrine was met by the outcry of modern pedagogy, by the need of the times, which directs its gaze to immediate need: that, just as experience is primary for cognition, so for skill in public and private life theoretical insight is even harmful, while practice and practical cultivation in general are what is essential and alone conducive.—Thus, as science and common human understanding worked hand in hand to bring about the downfall of metaphysics, the strange spectacle seemed to be produced of seeing a cultivated people without metaphysics;—like an otherwise variously adorned temple without a holy of holies.—Theology, which in earlier times was the guardian of speculative mysteries and of metaphysics, though dependent, had surrendered this science to feelings, to the practical-popular and","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"1.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0006","text":"learned-historical. Corresponding to this change is the fact that elsewhere those solitaries who were sacrificed by their people and removed from the world, to the end that contemplation of the eternal and a life serving it alone might exist, not for the sake of utility but for that of blessing,—disappeared; a disappearance which, in another connection, may in its essence be regarded as the same phenomenon as that mentioned above.—So that, after the expulsion of these obscurities, of the colourless occupation of the Spirit withdrawn into itself with itself, existence appeared to have been transformed into the cheerful world of flowers, among which, as is well known, there is no black one.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"1.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","text":"Logic has not fared quite as badly as metaphysics. That one learns to think through it—which otherwise counted as its usefulness and thus as its purpose—as though one should first learn to digest and to move by studying anatomy and physiology—this prejudice has long since disappeared, and the spirit of practicality doubtless intended no better fate for it than for its sister. Nevertheless, probably for the sake of some formal usefulness, it was still left a rank among the sciences; indeed, it was even retained as an object of public instruction.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"1.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","text":"This better lot, however, concerns only its external fate; for its shape and content have remained the same as they were transmitted through a long tradition, though in this transmission they had become ever more diluted and emaciated; the new Spirit that has arisen no less for science than for actuality has not yet made itself felt in it. Yet it is once and for all futile, when the substantial form of Spirit has transformed itself, to wish to preserve the forms of earlier cultivation; they are withered leaves, cast off by the new buds already produced at their roots.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"1.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0009","text":"The ignoring of the universal transformation is gradually beginning to come to an end in the scientific sphere as well. Unnoticed, the other conception has become familiar and proper even to its opponents; and if they continue to act obstinately against its source and principles and to behave contradictorily toward them, they have had to accept its consequences and have been unable to resist its influence; for their ever more insignificant negative attitude, they know no other way of giving themselves positive importance and a content than by joining in speaking in the new modes of conception.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"1.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","text":"On the other hand, the time of fermentation with which a new creation begins seems to be past. In its first appearance, such a creation is wont to comport itself with fanatical hostility toward the extensive systematization of the earlier principle, partly also to be apprehensive of losing itself in the extension of the particular, but partly to shun the labour required for scientific cultivation, and, in need of such cultivation, initially to resort to an empty formalism. The demand for the working-over and cultivation of the material now becomes all the more urgent. There is a period in the cultivation of an age, as in the cultivation of the individual, in which the chief concern is to acquire and maintain the principle in its undeveloped intensity. But the higher demand is that it should become science.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"1.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","text":"Whatever may already have been accomplished in other respects for the matter and for the form of science, logical science, which constitutes metaphysics proper, or pure speculative philosophy, has hitherto found itself greatly neglected. What I understand more precisely by this science and its standpoint, I have indicated provisionally in the Introduction. The necessity of beginning once more from the beginning with this science, the nature of the object itself, and the lack of preliminary labours which might have been used for the transformation undertaken, may be taken into account by equitable judges, even if a labour of many years could not give this attempt a greater perfection.—The essential point of view is that what is at issue in general is a new concept of scientific treatment.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"1.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","text":"Insofar as philosophy is to be science, it cannot, as I have elsewhere remarked [1], borrow its method for this purpose from a subordinate science such as mathematics, any more than it can rest content with categorical assurances of inner intuition, or avail itself of reasoning from grounds of external reflection. Rather, it can only be the nature of the content which moves itself in scientific cognition, while at the same time it is this proper reflection of the content which first posits and generates its determination itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"1.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0013","text":"[1] Phenomenology of Spirit, Preface to the first edition—The proper exposition is the cognition of the method, and has its place in logic itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"1.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","text":"The Understanding determines and holds determinations fixed; Reason is negative and dialectical, because it dissolves the determinations of the Understanding into nothing; it is positive because it produces the universal and comprehends the particular within it. Just as Understanding is generally taken as something separate from Reason, so dialectical Reason too is wont to be taken as something separate from positive Reason. But in its truth Reason is Spirit, which is higher than both, understanding Reason, or rational Understanding. It is the negative, that which constitutes the quality both of dialectical Reason and of Understanding;—it negates the simple, and thereby posits the determinate difference of Understanding; it dissolves it just as much, and is thus dialectical.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"1.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","text":"But it does not remain in the nothingness of this result; rather, it is therein equally positive, and thus has restored the first simple, but as a universal that is concrete within itself; beneath this a given particular is not subsumed; rather, in that determining and in its dissolution, the particular has already determined itself along with it. This spiritual movement, which in its simplicity gives itself its determinacy, and in this its equality with itself, which is thus the immanent development of the Concept, is the absolute method of cognition, and at the same time the immanent soul of the content itself. —I maintain that philosophy is capable of being objective, demonstrated science only upon this self-constructing path.—In this manner I have attempted to present consciousness in the Phenomenology of Spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"1.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","text":"Consciousness is Spirit as concrete knowledge, indeed knowledge caught up in externality; but the movement of form of this object rests solely, like the development of all natural and spiritual life, upon the nature of the pure essentialities that constitute the content of logic. Consciousness, as appearing Spirit, which on its path frees itself from its immediacy and external concretion, becomes pure knowledge, which gives itself those pure essentialities themselves, as they are in and for themselves, as its object. They are the pure thoughts, Spirit thinking its essence. Their self-movement is their spiritual life, and is that through which science constitutes itself and of which it is the exposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"1.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","text":"Herewith the relation of the science that I call Phenomenology of Spirit to logic has been indicated.—As regards the external relation, a second part was intended to follow the first part of the system of science, [2] which contains the Phenomenology and was to contain logic and the two real sciences of philosophy, the philosophy of nature and the philosophy of Spirit, and would have concluded the system of science. But the necessary extension which logic had to receive for itself has induced me to bring it separately to light; thus, in an expanded plan, it constitutes the first sequel to the Phenomenology of Spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"1.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018","text":"Later I shall cause the treatment of the two named real sciences of philosophy to follow.—This first volume of logic, however, contains as its first book the Doctrine of Being; the second book, the Doctrine of Essence, as the second division of the first volume; but the second volume will contain subjective logic, or the Doctrine of the Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"1.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0019","text":"Nuremberg, 22 March 1812","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"1.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0020","text":"[2] (Bamberg and Würzburg, published by Göbhard, 1807). This title will no longer be appended to the second edition, which will appear next Easter.—In place of the plan mentioned below for a second part, which was to contain all the other philosophical sciences, I have since brought out the Encyclopedia of the Philosophical Sciences, last year in its third edition (note to the second edition),","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"1.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0020"]}],"source_digest":"cbf73ec86a0fed572feaeb8b03a11f3b5b19fd36c419b3382f2221fdfdb48cd9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Vorrede zur ersten Ausgabe."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Vorrede zur ersten Ausgabe.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA","title":"Preface to the Second Edition.","order":2,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_VZZA","text":"An diese neue Bearbeitung der Wissenschaft der Logik, wovon hiermit der erste Band erscheint, bin ich wohl mit dem ganzen Bewußtseyn sowohl der Schwierigkeit des Gegenstandes für sich und dann seiner Darstellung, als der Unvollkommenheit, welche die Bearbeitung desselben in der ersten Ausgabe an sich trägt, gegangen; so sehr ich nach weiterer vieljähriger Beschäftigung mit dieser Wissenschaft bemüht gewesen, dieser Unvollkommenheit abzuhelfen, so fühle ich noch Ursache genug zu haben, die Nachsicht des Lesers in Anspruch zu nehmen. Ein Titel solchen Anspruchs aber zunächst darf wohl auf den Umstand gegründet werden, daß sich für den Inhalt vornehmlich nur äußerliches Material in der früheren Metaphysik und Logik vorgefunden hat. So allgemein und häufig dieselben, die letztere noch bis auf unsere Zeiten fort, getrieben worden, so wenig hat solche Bearbeitung die spekulative Seite betroffen; vielmehr ist im Ganzen dasselbe Material wiederholt, abwechselnd bald bis zu trivialer Oberflächlichkeit verdünnt, bald der alte Ballast umfangsreicher von Neuem hervorgeholt und mitgeschleppt worden, so daß durch solche, häufig ganz nur mechanische Bemühungen dem philosophischen Gehalt kein Gewinn zuwachsen konnte. Das Reich des Gedankens philosophisch, d.i. in seiner eigenen immanenten Thätigkeit, oder was dasselbe ist, in seiner nothwendigen Entwickelung darzustellen, mußte deswegen ein neues Unternehmen seyn, und dabei von vorne angefangen werden; jenes erworbene Material, die bekannten Denkformen, aber ist als eine höchst wichtige Vorlage, ja eine nothwendige Bedingung, dankbar anzuerkennende Voraussetzung anzusehen, wenn dieselbe auch nur hier und da einen dürren Faden, oder die leblosen Knochen eines Skeletts, sogar in Unordnung untereinander geworfen, dargiebt.\n\nDie Denkformen sind zunächst in der Sprache des Menschen herausgesetzt und niedergelegt, es kann in unseren Tagen nicht oft genug daran erinnert werden, daß das, wodurch sich der Mensch vom Thiere unterscheidet, das Denken ist. In Alles, was ihm zu einem Innerlichen, zur Vorstellung überhaupt, wird, was er zu dem Seinigen macht, hat sich die Sprache eingedrängt, und was er zur Sprache macht und in ihr äußert, enthält eingehüllter, vermischter, oder herausgearbeitet, eine Kategorie; so sehr natürlich ist ihm das Logische, oder vielmehr dasselbige ist seine eigenthümliche Natur selbst. Stellt man aber die Natur überhaupt, als das Physikalische, dem Geistigen gegenüber, so müßte man sagen, daß das Logische vielmehr das Übernatürliche ist, welches sich in alles Naturverhalten des Menschen, in sein Empfinden, Anschauen, Begehren, Bedürfniß, Trieb eindrängt und es dadurch überhaupt zu einem Menschlichen, wenn auch nur formell, zu Vorstelllungen und Zwecken, macht. Es ist der Vortheil einer Sprache, wenn sie einen Reichthum an logischen Ausdrücken, nämlich eigenthümlichen und abgesonderten, für die Denkbestimmungen selbst besitzt; von den Präpositionen, Artikeln, gehören schon viele solchen Verhältnissen an, die auf dem Denken beruhen; die chinesische Sprache soll es in ihrer Ausbildung gar nicht oder nur dürftig bis dahin gebracht haben; aber diese Partikeln treten ganz dienend, nur etwas weniges abgelöster, als die Augmente, Flexionszeichen und dergl. auf. Viel wichtiger ist es, daß in einer Sprache die Denkbestimmungen zu Substantiven und Verben herausgestellt und so zur gegenständlichen Form gestempelt sind; die deutsche Sprache hat darin viele Vorzüge vor den anderen modernen Sprachen; sogar sind manche ihrer Wörter von der weiteren Eigenheit, verschiedene Bedeutungen nicht nur, sondern entgegengesetzte zu haben, so daß darin selbst ein spekulativer Geist der Sprache nicht zu verkennen ist; es kann dem Denken eine Freude gewähren, auf solche Wörter zu stoßen, und die Vereinigung Entgegengesetzter, welches Resultat der Spekulation für den Verstand aber widersinnig ist, auf naive Weise schon lexikalisch als Ein Wort von den entgegengesetzten Bedeutungen vorzufinden. Die Philosophie bedarf daher überhaupt keiner besonderen Terminologie; es sind wohl aus fremden Sprachen einige Wörter aufzunehmen, welche jedoch durch den Gebrauch bereits das Bürgerrecht in ihr erhalten haben, ein affektirter Purismus würde da, wo es am entschiedensten auf die Sache ankommt, am wenigsten am Platze seyn.—Das Fortschreiten der Bildung überhaupt und insbesondere der Wissenschaften, selbst der empirischen und sinnlichen; indem sie im Allgemeinen sich in den gewöhnlichsten Kategorien (z.B. eines Ganzen und der Theile, eines Dinges und seiner Eigenschaften und dergleichen) bewegen, fördert nach und nach auch höhere Denkverhältnisse zu Tage, oder hebt sie wenigstens zu größerer Allgemeinheit und damit zu näherer Aufmerksamkeit hervor. Wenn z.B. in der Physik die Denkbestimmung der Kraft vorherrschend geworden ist, so spielt in neuerer Zeit die Kategorie der Polarität, die übrigens zu sehr… tort e… travers in Alles selbst in das Licht eingedrängt wird, die bedeutendste Rolle,—die Bestimmung von einem Unterschiede, in welchem die Unterschiedenen untrennbar verbunden sind;—daß auf solche Weise von der Form der Abstraktion, der Identität, durch welche eine Bestimmtheit z.B. als Kraft eine Selbstständigkeit erhält, fortgegangen, und die Form des Bestimmens, des Unterschiedes, welcher zugleich als ein Untrennbares in der Identität bleibt, herausgehoben und eine geläufige Vorstellung geworden, ist von unendlicher Wichtigkeit. Die Naturbetrachtung bringt durch die Realität, in welcher ihre Gegenstände sich festhalten, dieses Zwingende mit sich, die Kategorien, die in ihr nicht länger ignorirt werden können, wenn auch mit der größten Inkonsequenz gegen andere, die auch geltend gelassen werden, zu fixiren, und es nicht zu gestatten, daß, wie im Geistigen leichter geschieht, zu Abstraktionen von dem Gegensatze und zur Allgemeinheit übergegangen wird.\n\nAber indem so die logischen Gegenstände, wie deren Ausdrücke, etwa in der Bildung Allbekanntes sind, so ist, wie ich anderwärts gesagt, was bekannt ist, darum nicht erkannt, und es kann selbst die Ungeduld erregen, sich noch mit Bekanntem beschäftigen zu sollen, und was ist bekannter, als eben die Denkbestimmungen, von denen wir allenthalben Gebrauch machen, die uns in jedem Satze, den wir sprechen, zum Munde herausgehen. Über den Gang des Erkennens von diesem Bekannten aus, über das Verhältniß des wissenschaftlichen Denkens zu diesem natürlichen Denken, die allgemeinen Momente anzugeben soll dieses Vorwort bestimmt seyn, so viel, zusammengenommen mit dem, was die frühere Einleitung enthält, wird hinreichend seyn, um eine allgemeine Vorstellung, wie man eine solche von einer Wissenschaft zum voraus, vor derselben, welche die Sache selbst ist, zu erhalten fordert, von dem Sinne des logischen Erkennens zu geben.\n\nZunächst ist es als ein unendlicher Fortschritt anzusehen, daß die Formen des Denkens von dem Stoffe, in welchen sie im selbstbewußten Anschauen, Vorstellen, wie in unserem Begehren und Wollen, oder vielmehr auch in dem vorstellenden Begehren und Wollen (—und es ist kein menschliches Begehren oder Wollen ohne Vorstellen—) versenkt sind, befreit, diese Allgemeinheiten für sich herausgehoben, und wie Plato, dann aber Aristoteles vornehmlich gethan, zum Gegenstande der Betrachtung für sich gemacht worden; dieß giebt den Anfang des Erkennens derselben. \"Erst nachdem beinahe alles Nothwendige\", sagt Aristoteles, \"und was zur Bequemlichkeit und zum Verkehr des Lebens gehört, vorhanden war, hat man angefangen, sich um philosophische Erkenntniß zu bemühen.\" \"In Ägypten,\" hatte er vorher bemerkt, \"sind die mathematischen Wissenschaften früh ausgebildet worden, weil daselbst der Priesterstand früh in die Lage versetzt worden, Muße zu haben.\"—In der That setzt das Bedürfniß sich mit den reinen Gedanken zu beschäftigen einen weiten Gang voraus, den der Menschengeist durchgemacht haben muß, es ist, kann man sagen, es ist das Bedürfniß des schon befriedigten Bedürfnisses der Nothwendigkeit der Bedürfnißlosigkeit, zu dem er gekommen seyn muß, der Abstraktion von dem Stoffe des Anschauens, Einbildens u.s.f. der konkreten Interessen des Begehrens, der Triebe, des Willens, in welchem Stoffe die Denkbestimmungen eingehüllt stecken. In den stillen Räumen des zu sich selbst gekommenen und nur in sich seyenden Denkens schweigen die Interessen, welche das Leben der Völker und der Individuen bewegen. \"Nach so vielen Seiten,\" sagt Aristoteles in demselben Zusammenhange, \"ist die Natur des Menschen abhängig, aber diese Wissenschaft, die nicht zu einem Gebrauche gesucht wird, ist allein die an und für sich freie und sie scheint darum nicht ein menschlicher Besitz zu seyn. \"—Die Philosophie überhaupt hat es noch mit konkreten Gegenständen, Gott, Natur, Geist, in ihren Gedanken zu thun, aber die Logik beschäftigt sich ganz nur mit diesen für sich in ihrer vollständigen Abstraktion. Diese Logik pflegt darum dem Studium der Jugend zunächst anheim zu fallen, als welche noch nicht in die Interessen des konkreten Lebens eingetreten ist, in der Muße in Rücksicht derselben lebt, und nur erst für ihren subjektiven Zweck mit der Erwerbung der Mittel und der Möglichkeiten, in den Objekten jener Interessen thätig zu werden, sich und mit diesen selbst noch theoretisch sich zu beschäftigen hat. Unter diese Mittel wird im Widerspiele von der angeführten Vorstellung des Aristoteles, die logische Wissenschaft gerechnet, die Bemühung mit derselben ist eine vorläufige Arbeit, ihr Ort die Schule, auf welche erst der Ernst des Lebens und die Thätigkeit für die wahrhaften Zwecke folgen soll. Im Leben geht es zum Gebrauch der Kategorien, sie werden von der Ehre, für sich betrachtet zu werden, dazu herabgesetzt, in dem geistigen Betrieb lebendigen Inhalts in dem Erschaffen und Auswechseln der darauf bezüglichen Vorstellungen, zu dienen,—Theils als Abbreviaturen durch ihre Allgemeinheit;—denn welche unendliche Menge von Einzelnheiten des äußerlichen Daseyns und der Thätigkeit faßt die Vorstellung. Schlacht, Krieg, Volk, oder Meer, Thier u.s.f. in sich zusammen;—wie ist in der Vorstellung: Gott oder Liebe u.s.f. in die Einfachheit solchen Vorstellens eine unendliche Menge von Vorstellungen, Thätigkeit, Zuständen u.s.f. epitomirt!—Theils zur näheren Bestimmung und Findung der gegenständlichen Verhältnisse, wobei aber Gehalt und Zweck, die Richtigkeit und Wahrheit des sich einmischenden Denkens ganz von dem Vorhandenen selbst abhängig gemacht ist und den Denkbestimmungen für sich keine Inhaltbestimmende Wirksamkeit zugeschrieben wird. Solcher Gebrauch der Kategorien, der vorhin die natürliche Logik genannt worden ist, ist bewußtlos, und wenn ihnen in wissenschaftlicher Reflexion das Verhältniß, als Mittel zu dienen, im Geiste angewiesen wird, so wird das Denken überhaupt zu etwas den anderen geistigen Bestimmungen Untergeordnetem gemacht. Von unseren Empfindungen, Trieben, Interessen sagen wir nicht wohl, daß sie uns dienen, sondern sie gelten als selbstständige Kräfte und Mächte, so daß wir dieß selbst sind, so zu empfinden, dieß zu begehren und zu wollen, in dieß unser Interesse zu legen. Aber wieder kann es vielmehr unser Bewußtseyn werden, daß wir im Dienste unserer Gefühle, Triebe, Leidenschaften, Interessen, ohnehin von Gewohnheiten stehen, als daß wir sie im Besitz haben, noch weniger, daß sie bei unser innigen Einheit mit ihnen uns als Mittel dienen. Dergleichen Bestimmungen des Gemüths und Geistes zeigen sich uns bald als Besondere im Gegensatze gegen die Allgemeinheit, als die wir uns bewußt werden, in der wir unsere Freiheit haben, und halten dafür, in diesen Besonderheiten vielmehr befangen zu seyn, von ihnen beherrscht zu werden. Sonach können wir dann viel weniger dafür halten, daß die Denkformen, die sich durch alle unserer Vorstellungen, diese seyen bloß theoretisch, oder enthalten einen Stoff, der der Empfindung, dem Triebe, dem Willen angehört, hindurch ziehen, uns dienen, daß wir sie, und sie nicht vielmehr uns im Besitz haben; was ist uns übrig gegen sie, wie sollen wir, ich mich als das Allgemeinere über sie hinausstellen, sie die selbst das Allgemeine als solches sind. Wenn wir uns in eine Empfindung, Zweck, Interesse legen, und uns darin beschränkt, unfrei fühlen, so ist der Ort, in den wir daraus heraus und in die Freiheit zurück zu ziehen vermögen, dieser Ort der Gewißheit seiner selbst, der reinen Abstraktion, des Denkens. Oder ebenso, wenn wir von den Dingen sprechen wollen, so nennen wir die Natur oder das Wesen derselben ihren Begriff, und dieser ist nur für das Denken; von den Begriffen der Dinge aber werden wir noch viel weniger sagen, daß wir sie beherrschen oder daß die Denkbestimmungen, von denen sie der Komplex sind, uns dienen, im Gegentheil muß sich unser Denken nach ihnen beschränken und unsere Willkür oder Freiheit soll sie nicht nach sich zurichten wollen. Insofern also das subjektive Denken unser eigenstes, innerlichstes Thun ist, und der objektive Begriff der Dinge die Sache selbst ausmacht, so können wir aus jenem Thun nicht heraus seyn, nicht über demselben stehen, und ebenso wenig können wir über die Natur der Dinge hinaus. Von der letzteren Bestimmung jedoch können wir absehen; sie fällt mit der ersteren insofern zusammen, da sie eine Beziehung unserer Gedanken auf die Sache, aber nur etwas Leeres ergäbe, weil die Sache damit als Regel für unsere Begriffe aufgestellt werden würde, aber eben die Sache für uns nichts Anderes als unsere Begriffe von ihr seyn kann. Wenn die kritische Philosophie das Verhältniß dieser drei Terminorum so versteht, daß wir die Gedanken zwischen uns und zwischen die Sachen als Mitte stellen in dem Sinne, daß diese Mitte uns von den Sachen vielmehr abschließt, statt uns mit denselben zusammenzuschließen, so ist dieser Ansicht die einfache Bemerkung entgegenzusetzen, daß eben diese Sachen, die jenseits unserer und jenseits der sich auf sie beziehenden Gedanken auf dem anderen Extreme stehen sollen, selbst Gedankendinge, und als ganz unbestimmte, nur Ein Gedankending, (—das sogenannte Ding-an-sich) der leeren Abstraktion selbst sind.\n\nDoch dieß mag für den Gesichtspunkt genügen, aus welchem das Verhältniß verschwindet, nach welchem die Denkbestimmungen nur als zum Gebrauch und als Mittel genommen werden; wichtiger ist das weiter damit Zusammenhängende, nach welchem sie als äußere Formen gefaßt zu werden pflegen.—Die uns alle Vorstellungen, Zwecke, Interessen und Handlungen durchwirkende Thätigkeit des Denkens ist, wie gesagt, bewußtlos geschäftig (die natürliche Logik); was unser Bewußtseyn vor sich hat, ist der Inhalt, die Gegenstände der Vorstellungen, das, womit das Interesse erfüllt ist; die Denkbestimmungen gelten nach diesem Verhältniß als Formen, die nur an dem Gehalt, nicht der Gehalt selbst seyen. Wenn es aber an dem ist, was vorhin angegeben worden, und was sonst im Allgemeinen zugestanden wird, daß die Natur, das eigenthümliche Wesen, das wahrhaft Bleibende und Substantielle bei der Mannigfaltigkeit und Zufälligkeit des Erscheinens und der Zufälligkeit des Erscheinens und der vorübergehenden Äußerung, der Begriff der Sache, das in ihr selbst Allgemeine ist, wie jedes menschliche Individuum zwar ein unendlich eigenthümliches, das Prius aller seiner Eigenthümlichkeit darin Mensch zu seyn in sich hat, wie jedes einzelne Thier, das Prius, Thier zu seyn: so wäre nicht zu sagen, was, wenn diese Grundlage aus dem mit noch so vielfachen sonstigen Prädikaten Ausgerüsteten weggenommen würde, ob sie gleich wie die anderen ein Prädikat genannt werden kann, was so ein Individuum noch seyn sollte. Die unerläßliche Grundlage, der Begriff, das Allgemeine, das der Gedanke, insofern man nur von der Vorstellung bei dem Worte: Gedanke, abstrahiren kann, selbst ist, kann nicht nur als eine gleichgültige Form, die an einem Inhalte sey, angesehen werden. Aber diese Gedanken aller natürlichen und geistigen Dinge, selbst der substantielle Inhalt, sind noch ein socher, der vielfache Bestimmtheiten enthält und noch den Unterschied einer Seele und eines Leibes, des Begriffs und einer relativen Realität an ihm hat; die tiefere Grundlage ist die Seele für sich, der reine Begriff, der das Innerste der Gegenstände, ihr einfacher Lebenspuls, wie selbst des subjektiven Denkens derselben ist. Diese logische Natur, die den Geist beseelt, in ihm treibt und wirkt, zum Bewußtseyn zu bringen, dieß ist die Aufgabe. Das instinktartige Thun unterscheidet sich von dem intelligenten und freien Thun dadurch überhaupt, daß dieses mit Bewußtseyn geschieht, indem der Inhalt des Treibenden heraus aus der unmittelbaren Einheit mit dem Subjekte zur Gegenständlichkeit vor dieses gebracht ist, beginnt die Freiheit des Geistes, der in dem instinktweisen Wirken des Denkens befangen in den Banden seiner Kategorien in einen unendlich mannigfachen Stoff zersplittert ist. In diesem Netze schürzen sich hin und wieder festere Knoten, welche die Anhalts- und Richtungspunkte seines Lebens und Bewußtseyns sind, sie verdanken ihre Festigkeit und Macht eben dem, daß sie vor das Bewußtseyn gebracht an und für sich seyenden Begriffe seiner Wesenheit sind. Der wichtigste Punkt für die Natur des Geistes ist das Verhältniß nicht nur dessen, was er an sich ist, zu dem was er wirklich ist, sondern dessen, als was er sich weiß; dieses Sichwissen ist darum, weil er wesentlich Bewußtseyn, Grundbestimmung seiner Wirklichkeit. Diese Kategorien, die nur instinktmäßig als Triebe wirksam sind, und zunächst vereinzelt, damit veränderlich und sich verwirrend in das Bewußtseyn des Geistes gebracht, und ihm so eine vereinzelte und unsichere Wirklichkeit gewähren, zu reinigen und ihn damit in ihnen zur Freiheit und Wahrheit zu erheben, dieß ist also das höhere logische Geschäft.\n\nWas wir als Anfang der Wissenschaft, dessen hoher Werth für sich und zugleich als Bedingung der wahrhaften Erkenntniß vorhin anerkannt worden ist, angaben, die Begriffe und die Momente des Begriffs überhaupt, die Denkbestimmungen zunächst als Formen, die von dem Stoffe verschieden und nur an ihm seyen, zu behandeln, dieß giebt sich sogleich an sich selbst als ein zur Wahrheit, die als Gegenstand und Zweck der Logik angegeben wird, unangemessenes Verhalten kund. Denn so als bloße Formen, als verschieden von dem Inhalte, werden sie in einer Bestimmung stehend angenommen, die sie zu endlichen stempelt und die Wahrheit, die in sich unendlich ist, zu fassen unfähig macht. Mag das Wahre sonst, in welcher Rücksicht es sey, wieder mit Beschränkung und Endlichkeit vergesellschaftet seyn, dieß ist die Seite seiner Negation, seiner Unwahrheit und Unwirklichkeit, eben seines Endes, nicht der Affirmation, welche es als Wahres ist. Gegen die Kahlheit der bloß formellen Kategorien hat der Instinkt der gesunden Vernunft sich endlich so erstarkt gefühlt, daß er ihre Kenntniß mit Verachtung dem Gebiete einer Schullogik und Schulmetaphysik überläßt, zugleich mit der Mißachtung des Werthes, den schon das Bewußtseyn dieser Fäden für sich hat, und mit der Bewußtlosigkeit, in dem instinktartigen Thun natürlicher Logik, noch mehr in dem reflektirten Verwerfen der Kenntniß und Erkenntniß der Denkbestimmungen selbst, im Dienste des ungereinigten und damit unfreien Denkens gefangen zu seyn. Die einfache Grundbestimmung oder gemeinschaftliche Formbestimmung der Sammlung solcher Formen ist die Identität, die als Gesetz, als A=A, als Satz des Widerspruchs in der Logik dieser Sammlung behauptet wird. Die gesunde Vernunft hat ihre Ehrerbietung vor der Schule, die im Besitze solcher Gesetze der Wahrheit und in der sie noch immer so fortgeführt werden, so sehr verloren, daß sie dieselbe darob verlacht, und einen Menschen, der nach solchen Gesetzen wahrhaft zu sprechen weiß: die Pflanze ist eine—Pflanze, die Wissenschaft ist—die Wissenschaft, und sofort ins Unendliche, für unerträglich hält. Über die Formeln auch, welche die Regeln des Schließens, das in der That ein Hauptgebrauch des Verstandes ist, hat sich—so ungerecht es ist zu verkennen, daß sie ihr Feld in der Erkenntniß haben, worin sie gelten müssen und zugleich, daß sie wesentliches Material für das Denken der Vernunft sind,—das ebenso gerechte Bewußtsein festgesetzt, daß sie gleichgültige Mittel wenigstens ebenso sehr des Irrthums und der Sophisterei sind, und wie man auch sonst die Wahrheit bestimmen mag, für die höhere, z.B. die religiöse Wahrheit unbrauchbar sind; daß sie überhaupt nur eine Richtigkeit der Erkenntnisse, nicht die Wahrheit betreffen.\n\nDie Unvollständigkeit dieser Weise, das Denken zu betrachten, welche die Wahrheit auf der Seite läßt, ist allein dadurch zu ergänzen, daß nicht bloß das, was zu äußeren Form gerechnet zu werden pflegt, sondern der Inhalt mit in die denkende Betrachtung gezogen wird. Es zeigt sich von selbst bald, daß was in der nächsten gewöhnlichsten Reflexion als Inhalt von der Form geschieden wird, in der That nicht formlos, nicht bestimmungslos in sich, seyn soll; so wäre er nur das Leere, etwa die Abstraktion des Dings-an-sich,—daß er vielmehr Form in ihm selbst, ja durch sie allein Beseelung und Gehalt hat und daß sie selbst es ist, die nur in den Schein eines Inhalts, so wie damit auch in den Schein eines an diesem Scheine Äußerlichen, umschlägt. Mit dieser Einführung des Inhalts in die logische Betrachtung, sind es nicht die Dinge, sondern die Sache, der Begriff der Dinge, welcher Gegenstand wird.\n\nHierbei kann man aber auch daran erinnert werden, daß es eine Menge Begriffe, eine Menge Sachen giebt. Wodurch aber diese Menge beschränkt wird, ist Theils vorhin gesagt worden, daß der Begriff als Gedanke überhaupt, als Allgemeines, die unermeßliche Abbreviatur gegen die Einzelnheit der Dinge, wie sie ihre Menge dem unbestimmten Anschauen und Vorstellen vorschweben, ist; Theils aber ist ein Begriff sogleich erstens der Begriff an ihm selbst, und dieser ist nur Einer, und ist die substantielle Grundlage; vor's Andere aber ist er wohl ein bestimmter Begriff, welche Bestimmtheit an ihm das ist, was als Inhalt erscheint, die Bestimmtheit des Begriffs aber ist eine Formbestimmung dieser substantiellen Einheit, ein Moment der Form als Totalität, des Begriffes selbst, der die Grundlage der bestimmten Begriffe ist. Dieser wird nicht sinnlich angeschaut oder vorgestellt; er ist nur Gegenstand, Produkt und Inhalt des Denkens, und die an und für sich seyende Sache, der Logos, die Vernunft dessen, was ist, die Wahrheit dessen, was den Namen der Dinge führt; am wenigsten ist es der Logos, was außerhalb der logischen Wissenschaft gelassen werden soll. Es muß darum nicht ein Belieben seyn, ihn in die Wissenschaft herein zu ziehen oder ihn draußen zu lassen. Wenn die Denkbestimmungen, welche nur äußerliche Formen sind, wahrhaft an ihnen selbst betrachtet werden, kann nur ihre Endlichkeit und die Unwahrheit ihres Für-sich-seyn-sollens und als ihre Wahrheit, der Begriff, hervorgehen. Daher wird die logische Wissenschaft, indem sie die Denkbestimmungen, die überhaupt unsern Geist instinktartig und bewußtlos durchziehen, und selbst indem sie in die Sprache hereintreten, ungegenständlich, unbeachtet bleiben, abhandelt, auch die Rekonstruktion derjenigen seyn, welche durch die Reflexion herausgehoben und von ihr als subjektive, an dem Stoff und Gehalt äußere Formen fixiert sind.\n\nDie Darstellung keines Gegenstandes wäre an und für sich fähig, gar streng ganz immanent plastisch zu seyn, als die der Entwickelung des Denkens in seiner Nothwendigkeit; keiner führte so sehr diese Forderung mit sich; seine Wissenschaft müßte darin auch die Mathematik übertreffen, denn kein Gegenstand hat in ihm selbst diese Freiheit und Unabhängigkeit. Solcher Vortrag erforderte, wie dieß in seiner Art in dem Gange der mathematischen Konsequenz vorhanden ist, daß bei keiner Stufe der Entwickelung eine Denkbestimmung und Reflexion vorkäme, die nicht in dieser Stufe unmittelbar hervorgeht, und aus den vorhergehenden in sie herübergekommen ist. Allein auf solche abstrakte Vollkommenheit der Darstellung muß freilich im Allgemeinen Verzicht gethan werden; schon indem die Wissenschaft mit dem rein Einfachen, hiermit dem Allgemeinsten und Leersten, anfangen muß, ließe der Vortrag nur eben diese selbst ganz einfachen Ausdrücke des Einfachen ohne allen weiteren Zusatz irgend eines Wortes zu;—was der Sache nach Statt finden dürfte, wären negirende Reflexionen, die das abzuhalten und zu entfernen sich bemühten, was sonst die Vorstellung oder ein ungeregeltes Denken einmischen könnte. Solche Einfälle in den einfachen immanenten Gang der Entwickelung sind jedoch für sich zufällig, und die Bemühung, sie abzuwehren, wird somit selbst mit dieser Zufälligkeit behaftet; ohnehin ist es vergeblich allen solchen Einfällen, eben weil sie außer der Sache liegen, begegnen zu wollen, und wenigstens wäre Unvollständigkeit das, was hierbei für die systematische Befriedigung verlangt würde. Aber die eigenthümliche Unruhe und Zerstreuung unseres modernen Bewußtseyns läßt es nicht anders zu, als gleichfalls mehr oder weniger auf nahe liegende Reflexionen und Einfälle Rücksicht zu nehmen, ein plastischer Vortrag erfordert dann auch einen plastischen Sinn des Aufnehmens und Verstehens; aber solche plastische Jünglinge und Männer so ruhig mit der Selbstverläugnung eigener Reflexionen und Einfälle, womit das Selbstdenken sich zu erweisen ungeduldig ist, nur der Sache folgende Zuhörer, wie sie Plato dichtet, würden in einem modernen Dialoge nicht aufgestellt werden können; noch weniger dürfte auf solche Leser gezählt werden. Im Gegentheil haben sich mir zu häufig und zu heftig solche Gegner gezeigt, welche nicht die einfache Reflexion machen mochten, daß ihre Einfälle und Einwürfe Kategorien enthalten, welche Voraussetzungen sind und selbst erst der Kritik bedürfen, ehe sie gebraucht werden. Die Bewußtlosigkeit hierüber geht unglaublich weit; sie macht das Grund-Mißverständniß, das üble d. h. ungebildete Benehmen, bei einer Kategorie, die betrachtet wird, etwas Anderes zu denken und nicht diese Kategorie selbst. Diese Bewußtlosigkeit ist um so weniger zu rechtfertigen, als solches Anderes andere Denkbestimmungen und Begriffe sind, in einem Systeme der Logik aber eben diese anderen Kategorien gleichfalls ihre Stelle müssen gefunden haben, und daselbst für sich der Betrachtung werden unterworfen seyn. Am auffallendsten ist dieß in der überwiegenden Menge von Einwürfen und Angriffen, die auf die ersten Begriffe oder Sätze der Logik, das Seyn und Nichts und das Werden, als welches, selbst eine einfache Bestimmung, wohl unbestritten,—die einfachste Analyse zeigt dieß,—jene beiden Bestimmungen als Momente enthält. Die Gründlichkeit scheint zu erfordern, den Anfang, als den Grund, worauf Alles gebaut sey, vor Allem aus zu untersuchen, ja nicht weiter zu gehen, als bis er sich fest erwiesen hat, im Gegentheil vielmehr, wenn dieß nicht der Fall ist, alles noch Folgende zu verwerfen. Diese Gründlichkeit hat zugleich den Vortheil, die größte Erleichterung für das Denkgeschäft zu gewähren, sie hat die ganze Entwickelung in diesen Keim eingeschlossen vor sich, und hält sich für mit Allem fertig, wenn sie mit diesem fertig ist, der das Leichteste zum Abthun ist, denn er ist das Einfachste, das Einfache selbst; es ist die geringe Arbeit, die erforderlich ist, wodurch sich diese so selbst zufriedene Gründlichkeit wesentlich empfiehlt. Diese Beschränkung auf das Einfache läßt der Willkür des Denkens, das für sich nicht einfach bleiben will, sondern seine Reflexionen darüber anbringt, freien Spielraum. Mit dem guten Rechte, sich zuerst nur mit dem Princip zu beschäftigen, und damit sich auf das Weitere nicht einzulassen, thut diese Gründlichkeit in ihrem Geschäfte selbst das Gegentheil hiervon, vielmehr das Weitere, d.i. andere Kategorien als nur das Princip ist, andere Voraussetzungen und Vorurtheile herbeizubringen. Solche Voraussetzungen, daß die Unendlichkeit verschieden von der Endlichkeit, der Inhalt etwas Anderes als die Form, das Innere ein Anderes als das Äußere, die Vermittelung ebenso nicht die Unmittelbarkeit sey, als ob einer dergleichen nicht wüßte, werden zugleich belehrungsweise vorgebracht und nicht sowohl bewiesen, als erzählt und versichert. In solchem Belehren als Benehmen liegt—man kann es nicht anders nennen,—eine Albernheit; der Sache nach aber Theils das Unberechtigte, dergleichen nur vorauszusetzen und geradezu anzunehmen, Theils aber noch mehr die Unwissenheit, daß es das Bedürfniß und Geschäft des logischen Denkens ist, eben dieß zu untersuchen, ob denn so ein Endliches ohne Unendlichkeit etwas Wahres ist, ebenso solche abstrakte Unendlichkeit, ferner ein formloser Inhalt und eine inhaltlose Form, so ein Inneres für sich, das keine Äußerung hat, eine Äußerlichkeit ohne Innerlichkeit u.s.f.—etwas Wahres, ebenso etwas Wirkliches ist.—Aber diese Bildung und Zucht des Denkens, durch welche ein plastisches Verhalten desselben bewirkt und die Ungeduld der einfallenden Reflexion überwunden würde, wird allein durch das Weitergehen, das Studium und die Produktion der ganzen Entwickelung verschafft.\n\nBei der Erwähnung platonischer Darstellung kann, wer ein selbstständiges Gebäude philosophischer Wissenschaft in modernen Zeiten neu aufzuführen arbeitet, an die Erzählung erinnert werden, daß Plato seine Bücher über den Staat sieben Mal umgearbeitet habe. Die Erinnerung hieran, eine Vergleichung, insofern sie eine solche in sich zu schließen schiene, dürfte nur um so mehr bis zu dem Wunsch treiben, daß für ein Werk, das, als der modernen Welt angehörig, ein tieferes Princip, einen schwereren Gegenstand und ein Material von reicherm Umfang zur Bearbeitung vor sich hat, die freie Muße, es sieben und siebenzig Mal durchzuarbeiten, gewährt gewesen wäre. So aber mußte der Verfasser, indem er es im Angesicht der Größe der Aufgabe betrachtet, sich mit dem begnügen, was es hat werden mögen, unter den Umständen einer äußerlichen Nothwendigkeit, der unabwendbaren Zerstreuung durch die Größe und Vielseitigkeit der Zeitinteressen, sogar unter dem Zweifel, ob der laute Lärm des Tages und die betäubende Geschwätzigkeit der Einbildung, die auf denselben sich zu beschränken eitel ist, noch Raum für die Theilnahme an der leidenschaftslosen Stille der nur denkenden Erkenntniß offen lasse.\n\nBerlin, den 7. November 1831.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001","text":"An diese neue Bearbeitung der Wissenschaft der Logik, wovon hiermit der erste Band erscheint, bin ich wohl mit dem ganzen Bewußtseyn sowohl der Schwierigkeit des Gegenstandes für sich und dann seiner Darstellung, als der Unvollkommenheit, welche die Bearbeitung desselben in der ersten Ausgabe an sich trägt, gegangen; so sehr ich nach weiterer vieljähriger Beschäftigung mit dieser Wissenschaft bemüht gewesen, dieser Unvollkommenheit abzuhelfen, so fühle ich noch Ursache genug zu haben, die Nachsicht des Lesers in Anspruch zu nehmen. Ein Titel solchen Anspruchs aber zunächst darf wohl auf den Umstand gegründet werden, daß sich für den Inhalt vornehmlich nur äußerliches Material in der früheren Metaphysik und Logik vorgefunden hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"2.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","text":"So allgemein und häufig dieselben, die letztere noch bis auf unsere Zeiten fort, getrieben worden, so wenig hat solche Bearbeitung die spekulative Seite betroffen; vielmehr ist im Ganzen dasselbe Material wiederholt, abwechselnd bald bis zu trivialer Oberflächlichkeit verdünnt, bald der alte Ballast umfangsreicher von Neuem hervorgeholt und mitgeschleppt worden, so daß durch solche, häufig ganz nur mechanische Bemühungen dem philosophischen Gehalt kein Gewinn zuwachsen konnte. Das Reich des Gedankens philosophisch, d.i.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"2.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","text":"in seiner eigenen immanenten Thätigkeit, oder was dasselbe ist, in seiner nothwendigen Entwickelung darzustellen, mußte deswegen ein neues Unternehmen seyn, und dabei von vorne angefangen werden; jenes erworbene Material, die bekannten Denkformen, aber ist als eine höchst wichtige Vorlage, ja eine nothwendige Bedingung, dankbar anzuerkennende Voraussetzung anzusehen, wenn dieselbe auch nur hier und da einen dürren Faden, oder die leblosen Knochen eines Skeletts, sogar in Unordnung untereinander geworfen, dargiebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"2.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","text":"Die Denkformen sind zunächst in der Sprache des Menschen herausgesetzt und niedergelegt, es kann in unseren Tagen nicht oft genug daran erinnert werden, daß das, wodurch sich der Mensch vom Thiere unterscheidet, das Denken ist. In Alles, was ihm zu einem Innerlichen, zur Vorstellung überhaupt, wird, was er zu dem Seinigen macht, hat sich die Sprache eingedrängt, und was er zur Sprache macht und in ihr äußert, enthält eingehüllter, vermischter, oder herausgearbeitet, eine Kategorie; so sehr natürlich ist ihm das Logische, oder vielmehr dasselbige ist seine eigenthümliche Natur selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"2.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005","text":"Stellt man aber die Natur überhaupt, als das Physikalische, dem Geistigen gegenüber, so müßte man sagen, daß das Logische vielmehr das Übernatürliche ist, welches sich in alles Naturverhalten des Menschen, in sein Empfinden, Anschauen, Begehren, Bedürfniß, Trieb eindrängt und es dadurch überhaupt zu einem Menschlichen, wenn auch nur formell, zu Vorstelllungen und Zwecken, macht. Es ist der Vortheil einer Sprache, wenn sie einen Reichthum an logischen Ausdrücken, nämlich eigenthümlichen und abgesonderten, für die Denkbestimmungen selbst besitzt; von den Präpositionen, Artikeln, gehören schon viele solchen Verhältnissen an, die auf dem Denken beruhen; die chinesische Sprache soll es in ihrer Ausbildung gar nicht oder nur dürftig bis dahin gebracht haben; aber diese Partikeln treten ganz dienend, nur etwas weniges abgelöster, als die Augmente, Flexionszeichen und dergl. auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"2.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0006","text":"Viel wichtiger ist es, daß in einer Sprache die Denkbestimmungen zu Substantiven und Verben herausgestellt und so zur gegenständlichen Form gestempelt sind; die deutsche Sprache hat darin viele Vorzüge vor den anderen modernen Sprachen; sogar sind manche ihrer Wörter von der weiteren Eigenheit, verschiedene Bedeutungen nicht nur, sondern entgegengesetzte zu haben, so daß darin selbst ein spekulativer Geist der Sprache nicht zu verkennen ist; es kann dem Denken eine Freude gewähren, auf solche Wörter zu stoßen, und die Vereinigung Entgegengesetzter, welches Resultat der Spekulation für den Verstand aber widersinnig ist, auf naive Weise schon lexikalisch als Ein Wort von den entgegengesetzten Bedeutungen vorzufinden.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"2.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0007","text":"Die Philosophie bedarf daher überhaupt keiner besonderen Terminologie; es sind wohl aus fremden Sprachen einige Wörter aufzunehmen, welche jedoch durch den Gebrauch bereits das Bürgerrecht in ihr erhalten haben, ein affektirter Purismus würde da, wo es am entschiedensten auf die Sache ankommt, am wenigsten am Platze seyn.—Das Fortschreiten der Bildung überhaupt und insbesondere der Wissenschaften, selbst der empirischen und sinnlichen; indem sie im Allgemeinen sich in den gewöhnlichsten Kategorien (z.B. eines Ganzen und der Theile, eines Dinges und seiner Eigenschaften und dergleichen) bewegen, fördert nach und nach auch höhere Denkverhältnisse zu Tage, oder hebt sie wenigstens zu größerer Allgemeinheit und damit zu näherer Aufmerksamkeit hervor. Wenn z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"2.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0008","text":"in der Physik die Denkbestimmung der Kraft vorherrschend geworden ist, so spielt in neuerer Zeit die Kategorie der Polarität, die übrigens zu sehr… tort e… travers in Alles selbst in das Licht eingedrängt wird, die bedeutendste Rolle,—die Bestimmung von einem Unterschiede, in welchem die Unterschiedenen untrennbar verbunden sind;—daß auf solche Weise von der Form der Abstraktion, der Identität, durch welche eine Bestimmtheit z.B. als Kraft eine Selbstständigkeit erhält, fortgegangen, und die Form des Bestimmens, des Unterschiedes, welcher zugleich als ein Untrennbares in der Identität bleibt, herausgehoben und eine geläufige Vorstellung geworden, ist von unendlicher Wichtigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"2.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0009","text":"Die Naturbetrachtung bringt durch die Realität, in welcher ihre Gegenstände sich festhalten, dieses Zwingende mit sich, die Kategorien, die in ihr nicht länger ignorirt werden können, wenn auch mit der größten Inkonsequenz gegen andere, die auch geltend gelassen werden, zu fixiren, und es nicht zu gestatten, daß, wie im Geistigen leichter geschieht, zu Abstraktionen von dem Gegensatze und zur Allgemeinheit übergegangen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"2.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","text":"Aber indem so die logischen Gegenstände, wie deren Ausdrücke, etwa in der Bildung Allbekanntes sind, so ist, wie ich anderwärts gesagt, was bekannt ist, darum nicht erkannt, und es kann selbst die Ungeduld erregen, sich noch mit Bekanntem beschäftigen zu sollen, und was ist bekannter, als eben die Denkbestimmungen, von denen wir allenthalben Gebrauch machen, die uns in jedem Satze, den wir sprechen, zum Munde herausgehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"2.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0011","text":"Über den Gang des Erkennens von diesem Bekannten aus, über das Verhältniß des wissenschaftlichen Denkens zu diesem natürlichen Denken, die allgemeinen Momente anzugeben soll dieses Vorwort bestimmt seyn, so viel, zusammengenommen mit dem, was die frühere Einleitung enthält, wird hinreichend seyn, um eine allgemeine Vorstellung, wie man eine solche von einer Wissenschaft zum voraus, vor derselben, welche die Sache selbst ist, zu erhalten fordert, von dem Sinne des logischen Erkennens zu geben.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"2.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","text":"Zunächst ist es als ein unendlicher Fortschritt anzusehen, daß die Formen des Denkens von dem Stoffe, in welchen sie im selbstbewußten Anschauen, Vorstellen, wie in unserem Begehren und Wollen, oder vielmehr auch in dem vorstellenden Begehren und Wollen (—und es ist kein menschliches Begehren oder Wollen ohne Vorstellen—) versenkt sind, befreit, diese Allgemeinheiten für sich herausgehoben, und wie Plato, dann aber Aristoteles vornehmlich gethan, zum Gegenstande der Betrachtung für sich gemacht worden; dieß giebt den Anfang des Erkennens derselben. \"Erst nachdem beinahe alles Nothwendige\", sagt Aristoteles, \"und was zur Bequemlichkeit und zum Verkehr des Lebens gehört, vorhanden war, hat man angefangen, sich um philosophische Erkenntniß zu bemühen.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"2.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","text":"\"In Ägypten,\" hatte er vorher bemerkt, \"sind die mathematischen Wissenschaften früh ausgebildet worden, weil daselbst der Priesterstand früh in die Lage versetzt worden, Muße zu haben.\"—In der That setzt das Bedürfniß sich mit den reinen Gedanken zu beschäftigen einen weiten Gang voraus, den der Menschengeist durchgemacht haben muß, es ist, kann man sagen, es ist das Bedürfniß des schon befriedigten Bedürfnisses der Nothwendigkeit der Bedürfnißlosigkeit, zu dem er gekommen seyn muß, der Abstraktion von dem Stoffe des Anschauens, Einbildens u.s.f. der konkreten Interessen des Begehrens, der Triebe, des Willens, in welchem Stoffe die Denkbestimmungen eingehüllt stecken. In den stillen Räumen des zu sich selbst gekommenen und nur in sich seyenden Denkens schweigen die Interessen, welche das Leben der Völker und der Individuen bewegen.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"2.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","text":"\"Nach so vielen Seiten,\" sagt Aristoteles in demselben Zusammenhange, \"ist die Natur des Menschen abhängig, aber diese Wissenschaft, die nicht zu einem Gebrauche gesucht wird, ist allein die an und für sich freie und sie scheint darum nicht ein menschlicher Besitz zu seyn. \"—Die Philosophie überhaupt hat es noch mit konkreten Gegenständen, Gott, Natur, Geist, in ihren Gedanken zu thun, aber die Logik beschäftigt sich ganz nur mit diesen für sich in ihrer vollständigen Abstraktion. Diese Logik pflegt darum dem Studium der Jugend zunächst anheim zu fallen, als welche noch nicht in die Interessen des konkreten Lebens eingetreten ist, in der Muße in Rücksicht derselben lebt, und nur erst für ihren subjektiven Zweck mit der Erwerbung der Mittel und der Möglichkeiten, in den Objekten jener Interessen thätig zu werden, sich und mit diesen selbst noch theoretisch sich zu beschäftigen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"2.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0015","text":"Unter diese Mittel wird im Widerspiele von der angeführten Vorstellung des Aristoteles, die logische Wissenschaft gerechnet, die Bemühung mit derselben ist eine vorläufige Arbeit, ihr Ort die Schule, auf welche erst der Ernst des Lebens und die Thätigkeit für die wahrhaften Zwecke folgen soll. Im Leben geht es zum Gebrauch der Kategorien, sie werden von der Ehre, für sich betrachtet zu werden, dazu herabgesetzt, in dem geistigen Betrieb lebendigen Inhalts in dem Erschaffen und Auswechseln der darauf bezüglichen Vorstellungen, zu dienen,—Theils als Abbreviaturen durch ihre Allgemeinheit;—denn welche unendliche Menge von Einzelnheiten des äußerlichen Daseyns und der Thätigkeit faßt die Vorstellung. Schlacht, Krieg, Volk, oder Meer, Thier u.s.f. in sich zusammen;—wie ist in der Vorstellung: Gott oder Liebe u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"2.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","text":"in die Einfachheit solchen Vorstellens eine unendliche Menge von Vorstellungen, Thätigkeit, Zuständen u.s.f. epitomirt!—Theils zur näheren Bestimmung und Findung der gegenständlichen Verhältnisse, wobei aber Gehalt und Zweck, die Richtigkeit und Wahrheit des sich einmischenden Denkens ganz von dem Vorhandenen selbst abhängig gemacht ist und den Denkbestimmungen für sich keine Inhaltbestimmende Wirksamkeit zugeschrieben wird. Solcher Gebrauch der Kategorien, der vorhin die natürliche Logik genannt worden ist, ist bewußtlos, und wenn ihnen in wissenschaftlicher Reflexion das Verhältniß, als Mittel zu dienen, im Geiste angewiesen wird, so wird das Denken überhaupt zu etwas den anderen geistigen Bestimmungen Untergeordnetem gemacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"2.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0017","text":"Von unseren Empfindungen, Trieben, Interessen sagen wir nicht wohl, daß sie uns dienen, sondern sie gelten als selbstständige Kräfte und Mächte, so daß wir dieß selbst sind, so zu empfinden, dieß zu begehren und zu wollen, in dieß unser Interesse zu legen. Aber wieder kann es vielmehr unser Bewußtseyn werden, daß wir im Dienste unserer Gefühle, Triebe, Leidenschaften, Interessen, ohnehin von Gewohnheiten stehen, als daß wir sie im Besitz haben, noch weniger, daß sie bei unser innigen Einheit mit ihnen uns als Mittel dienen. Dergleichen Bestimmungen des Gemüths und Geistes zeigen sich uns bald als Besondere im Gegensatze gegen die Allgemeinheit, als die wir uns bewußt werden, in der wir unsere Freiheit haben, und halten dafür, in diesen Besonderheiten vielmehr befangen zu seyn, von ihnen beherrscht zu werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"2.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","text":"Sonach können wir dann viel weniger dafür halten, daß die Denkformen, die sich durch alle unserer Vorstellungen, diese seyen bloß theoretisch, oder enthalten einen Stoff, der der Empfindung, dem Triebe, dem Willen angehört, hindurch ziehen, uns dienen, daß wir sie, und sie nicht vielmehr uns im Besitz haben; was ist uns übrig gegen sie, wie sollen wir, ich mich als das Allgemeinere über sie hinausstellen, sie die selbst das Allgemeine als solches sind. Wenn wir uns in eine Empfindung, Zweck, Interesse legen, und uns darin beschränkt, unfrei fühlen, so ist der Ort, in den wir daraus heraus und in die Freiheit zurück zu ziehen vermögen, dieser Ort der Gewißheit seiner selbst, der reinen Abstraktion, des Denkens.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"2.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","text":"Oder ebenso, wenn wir von den Dingen sprechen wollen, so nennen wir die Natur oder das Wesen derselben ihren Begriff, und dieser ist nur für das Denken; von den Begriffen der Dinge aber werden wir noch viel weniger sagen, daß wir sie beherrschen oder daß die Denkbestimmungen, von denen sie der Komplex sind, uns dienen, im Gegentheil muß sich unser Denken nach ihnen beschränken und unsere Willkür oder Freiheit soll sie nicht nach sich zurichten wollen. Insofern also das subjektive Denken unser eigenstes, innerlichstes Thun ist, und der objektive Begriff der Dinge die Sache selbst ausmacht, so können wir aus jenem Thun nicht heraus seyn, nicht über demselben stehen, und ebenso wenig können wir über die Natur der Dinge hinaus.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"2.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","text":"Von der letzteren Bestimmung jedoch können wir absehen; sie fällt mit der ersteren insofern zusammen, da sie eine Beziehung unserer Gedanken auf die Sache, aber nur etwas Leeres ergäbe, weil die Sache damit als Regel für unsere Begriffe aufgestellt werden würde, aber eben die Sache für uns nichts Anderes als unsere Begriffe von ihr seyn kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"2.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","text":"Wenn die kritische Philosophie das Verhältniß dieser drei Terminorum so versteht, daß wir die Gedanken zwischen uns und zwischen die Sachen als Mitte stellen in dem Sinne, daß diese Mitte uns von den Sachen vielmehr abschließt, statt uns mit denselben zusammenzuschließen, so ist dieser Ansicht die einfache Bemerkung entgegenzusetzen, daß eben diese Sachen, die jenseits unserer und jenseits der sich auf sie beziehenden Gedanken auf dem anderen Extreme stehen sollen, selbst Gedankendinge, und als ganz unbestimmte, nur Ein Gedankending, (—das sogenannte Ding-an-sich) der leeren Abstraktion selbst sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"2.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","text":"Doch dieß mag für den Gesichtspunkt genügen, aus welchem das Verhältniß verschwindet, nach welchem die Denkbestimmungen nur als zum Gebrauch und als Mittel genommen werden; wichtiger ist das weiter damit Zusammenhängende, nach welchem sie als äußere Formen gefaßt zu werden pflegen.—Die uns alle Vorstellungen, Zwecke, Interessen und Handlungen durchwirkende Thätigkeit des Denkens ist, wie gesagt, bewußtlos geschäftig (die natürliche Logik); was unser Bewußtseyn vor sich hat, ist der Inhalt, die Gegenstände der Vorstellungen, das, womit das Interesse erfüllt ist; die Denkbestimmungen gelten nach diesem Verhältniß als Formen, die nur an dem Gehalt, nicht der Gehalt selbst seyen.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"2.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0023","text":"Wenn es aber an dem ist, was vorhin angegeben worden, und was sonst im Allgemeinen zugestanden wird, daß die Natur, das eigenthümliche Wesen, das wahrhaft Bleibende und Substantielle bei der Mannigfaltigkeit und Zufälligkeit des Erscheinens und der Zufälligkeit des Erscheinens und der vorübergehenden Äußerung, der Begriff der Sache, das in ihr selbst Allgemeine ist, wie jedes menschliche Individuum zwar ein unendlich eigenthümliches, das Prius aller seiner Eigenthümlichkeit darin Mensch zu seyn in sich hat, wie jedes einzelne Thier, das Prius, Thier zu seyn: so wäre nicht zu sagen, was, wenn diese Grundlage aus dem mit noch so vielfachen sonstigen Prädikaten Ausgerüsteten weggenommen würde, ob sie gleich wie die anderen ein Prädikat genannt werden kann, was so ein Individuum noch seyn sollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"2.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","text":"Die unerläßliche Grundlage, der Begriff, das Allgemeine, das der Gedanke, insofern man nur von der Vorstellung bei dem Worte: Gedanke, abstrahiren kann, selbst ist, kann nicht nur als eine gleichgültige Form, die an einem Inhalte sey, angesehen werden. Aber diese Gedanken aller natürlichen und geistigen Dinge, selbst der substantielle Inhalt, sind noch ein socher, der vielfache Bestimmtheiten enthält und noch den Unterschied einer Seele und eines Leibes, des Begriffs und einer relativen Realität an ihm hat; die tiefere Grundlage ist die Seele für sich, der reine Begriff, der das Innerste der Gegenstände, ihr einfacher Lebenspuls, wie selbst des subjektiven Denkens derselben ist. Diese logische Natur, die den Geist beseelt, in ihm treibt und wirkt, zum Bewußtseyn zu bringen, dieß ist die Aufgabe.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"2.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0025","text":"Das instinktartige Thun unterscheidet sich von dem intelligenten und freien Thun dadurch überhaupt, daß dieses mit Bewußtseyn geschieht, indem der Inhalt des Treibenden heraus aus der unmittelbaren Einheit mit dem Subjekte zur Gegenständlichkeit vor dieses gebracht ist, beginnt die Freiheit des Geistes, der in dem instinktweisen Wirken des Denkens befangen in den Banden seiner Kategorien in einen unendlich mannigfachen Stoff zersplittert ist. In diesem Netze schürzen sich hin und wieder festere Knoten, welche die Anhalts- und Richtungspunkte seines Lebens und Bewußtseyns sind, sie verdanken ihre Festigkeit und Macht eben dem, daß sie vor das Bewußtseyn gebracht an und für sich seyenden Begriffe seiner Wesenheit sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"2.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","text":"Der wichtigste Punkt für die Natur des Geistes ist das Verhältniß nicht nur dessen, was er an sich ist, zu dem was er wirklich ist, sondern dessen, als was er sich weiß; dieses Sichwissen ist darum, weil er wesentlich Bewußtseyn, Grundbestimmung seiner Wirklichkeit. Diese Kategorien, die nur instinktmäßig als Triebe wirksam sind, und zunächst vereinzelt, damit veränderlich und sich verwirrend in das Bewußtseyn des Geistes gebracht, und ihm so eine vereinzelte und unsichere Wirklichkeit gewähren, zu reinigen und ihn damit in ihnen zur Freiheit und Wahrheit zu erheben, dieß ist also das höhere logische Geschäft.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"2.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","text":"Was wir als Anfang der Wissenschaft, dessen hoher Werth für sich und zugleich als Bedingung der wahrhaften Erkenntniß vorhin anerkannt worden ist, angaben, die Begriffe und die Momente des Begriffs überhaupt, die Denkbestimmungen zunächst als Formen, die von dem Stoffe verschieden und nur an ihm seyen, zu behandeln, dieß giebt sich sogleich an sich selbst als ein zur Wahrheit, die als Gegenstand und Zweck der Logik angegeben wird, unangemessenes Verhalten kund. Denn so als bloße Formen, als verschieden von dem Inhalte, werden sie in einer Bestimmung stehend angenommen, die sie zu endlichen stempelt und die Wahrheit, die in sich unendlich ist, zu fassen unfähig macht.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"2.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0028","text":"Mag das Wahre sonst, in welcher Rücksicht es sey, wieder mit Beschränkung und Endlichkeit vergesellschaftet seyn, dieß ist die Seite seiner Negation, seiner Unwahrheit und Unwirklichkeit, eben seines Endes, nicht der Affirmation, welche es als Wahres ist. Gegen die Kahlheit der bloß formellen Kategorien hat der Instinkt der gesunden Vernunft sich endlich so erstarkt gefühlt, daß er ihre Kenntniß mit Verachtung dem Gebiete einer Schullogik und Schulmetaphysik überläßt, zugleich mit der Mißachtung des Werthes, den schon das Bewußtseyn dieser Fäden für sich hat, und mit der Bewußtlosigkeit, in dem instinktartigen Thun natürlicher Logik, noch mehr in dem reflektirten Verwerfen der Kenntniß und Erkenntniß der Denkbestimmungen selbst, im Dienste des ungereinigten und damit unfreien Denkens gefangen zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"2.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0029","text":"Die einfache Grundbestimmung oder gemeinschaftliche Formbestimmung der Sammlung solcher Formen ist die Identität, die als Gesetz, als A=A, als Satz des Widerspruchs in der Logik dieser Sammlung behauptet wird. Die gesunde Vernunft hat ihre Ehrerbietung vor der Schule, die im Besitze solcher Gesetze der Wahrheit und in der sie noch immer so fortgeführt werden, so sehr verloren, daß sie dieselbe darob verlacht, und einen Menschen, der nach solchen Gesetzen wahrhaft zu sprechen weiß: die Pflanze ist eine—Pflanze, die Wissenschaft ist—die Wissenschaft, und sofort ins Unendliche, für unerträglich hält.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"2.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","text":"Über die Formeln auch, welche die Regeln des Schließens, das in der That ein Hauptgebrauch des Verstandes ist, hat sich—so ungerecht es ist zu verkennen, daß sie ihr Feld in der Erkenntniß haben, worin sie gelten müssen und zugleich, daß sie wesentliches Material für das Denken der Vernunft sind,—das ebenso gerechte Bewußtsein festgesetzt, daß sie gleichgültige Mittel wenigstens ebenso sehr des Irrthums und der Sophisterei sind, und wie man auch sonst die Wahrheit bestimmen mag, für die höhere, z.B. die religiöse Wahrheit unbrauchbar sind; daß sie überhaupt nur eine Richtigkeit der Erkenntnisse, nicht die Wahrheit betreffen.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"2.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","text":"Die Unvollständigkeit dieser Weise, das Denken zu betrachten, welche die Wahrheit auf der Seite läßt, ist allein dadurch zu ergänzen, daß nicht bloß das, was zu äußeren Form gerechnet zu werden pflegt, sondern der Inhalt mit in die denkende Betrachtung gezogen wird. Es zeigt sich von selbst bald, daß was in der nächsten gewöhnlichsten Reflexion als Inhalt von der Form geschieden wird, in der That nicht formlos, nicht bestimmungslos in sich, seyn soll; so wäre er nur das Leere, etwa die Abstraktion des Dings-an-sich,—daß er vielmehr Form in ihm selbst, ja durch sie allein Beseelung und Gehalt hat und daß sie selbst es ist, die nur in den Schein eines Inhalts, so wie damit auch in den Schein eines an diesem Scheine Äußerlichen, umschlägt.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"2.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0032","text":"Mit dieser Einführung des Inhalts in die logische Betrachtung, sind es nicht die Dinge, sondern die Sache, der Begriff der Dinge, welcher Gegenstand wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"2.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","text":"Hierbei kann man aber auch daran erinnert werden, daß es eine Menge Begriffe, eine Menge Sachen giebt. Wodurch aber diese Menge beschränkt wird, ist Theils vorhin gesagt worden, daß der Begriff als Gedanke überhaupt, als Allgemeines, die unermeßliche Abbreviatur gegen die Einzelnheit der Dinge, wie sie ihre Menge dem unbestimmten Anschauen und Vorstellen vorschweben, ist; Theils aber ist ein Begriff sogleich erstens der Begriff an ihm selbst, und dieser ist nur Einer, und ist die substantielle Grundlage; vor's Andere aber ist er wohl ein bestimmter Begriff, welche Bestimmtheit an ihm das ist, was als Inhalt erscheint, die Bestimmtheit des Begriffs aber ist eine Formbestimmung dieser substantiellen Einheit, ein Moment der Form als Totalität, des Begriffes selbst, der die Grundlage der bestimmten Begriffe ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"2.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","text":"Dieser wird nicht sinnlich angeschaut oder vorgestellt; er ist nur Gegenstand, Produkt und Inhalt des Denkens, und die an und für sich seyende Sache, der Logos, die Vernunft dessen, was ist, die Wahrheit dessen, was den Namen der Dinge führt; am wenigsten ist es der Logos, was außerhalb der logischen Wissenschaft gelassen werden soll. Es muß darum nicht ein Belieben seyn, ihn in die Wissenschaft herein zu ziehen oder ihn draußen zu lassen. Wenn die Denkbestimmungen, welche nur äußerliche Formen sind, wahrhaft an ihnen selbst betrachtet werden, kann nur ihre Endlichkeit und die Unwahrheit ihres Für-sich-seyn-sollens und als ihre Wahrheit, der Begriff, hervorgehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"2.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","text":"Daher wird die logische Wissenschaft, indem sie die Denkbestimmungen, die überhaupt unsern Geist instinktartig und bewußtlos durchziehen, und selbst indem sie in die Sprache hereintreten, ungegenständlich, unbeachtet bleiben, abhandelt, auch die Rekonstruktion derjenigen seyn, welche durch die Reflexion herausgehoben und von ihr als subjektive, an dem Stoff und Gehalt äußere Formen fixiert sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"2.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","text":"Die Darstellung keines Gegenstandes wäre an und für sich fähig, gar streng ganz immanent plastisch zu seyn, als die der Entwickelung des Denkens in seiner Nothwendigkeit; keiner führte so sehr diese Forderung mit sich; seine Wissenschaft müßte darin auch die Mathematik übertreffen, denn kein Gegenstand hat in ihm selbst diese Freiheit und Unabhängigkeit. Solcher Vortrag erforderte, wie dieß in seiner Art in dem Gange der mathematischen Konsequenz vorhanden ist, daß bei keiner Stufe der Entwickelung eine Denkbestimmung und Reflexion vorkäme, die nicht in dieser Stufe unmittelbar hervorgeht, und aus den vorhergehenden in sie herübergekommen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"2.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037","text":"Allein auf solche abstrakte Vollkommenheit der Darstellung muß freilich im Allgemeinen Verzicht gethan werden; schon indem die Wissenschaft mit dem rein Einfachen, hiermit dem Allgemeinsten und Leersten, anfangen muß, ließe der Vortrag nur eben diese selbst ganz einfachen Ausdrücke des Einfachen ohne allen weiteren Zusatz irgend eines Wortes zu;—was der Sache nach Statt finden dürfte, wären negirende Reflexionen, die das abzuhalten und zu entfernen sich bemühten, was sonst die Vorstellung oder ein ungeregeltes Denken einmischen könnte.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"2.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","text":"Solche Einfälle in den einfachen immanenten Gang der Entwickelung sind jedoch für sich zufällig, und die Bemühung, sie abzuwehren, wird somit selbst mit dieser Zufälligkeit behaftet; ohnehin ist es vergeblich allen solchen Einfällen, eben weil sie außer der Sache liegen, begegnen zu wollen, und wenigstens wäre Unvollständigkeit das, was hierbei für die systematische Befriedigung verlangt würde.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"2.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","text":"Aber die eigenthümliche Unruhe und Zerstreuung unseres modernen Bewußtseyns läßt es nicht anders zu, als gleichfalls mehr oder weniger auf nahe liegende Reflexionen und Einfälle Rücksicht zu nehmen, ein plastischer Vortrag erfordert dann auch einen plastischen Sinn des Aufnehmens und Verstehens; aber solche plastische Jünglinge und Männer so ruhig mit der Selbstverläugnung eigener Reflexionen und Einfälle, womit das Selbstdenken sich zu erweisen ungeduldig ist, nur der Sache folgende Zuhörer, wie sie Plato dichtet, würden in einem modernen Dialoge nicht aufgestellt werden können; noch weniger dürfte auf solche Leser gezählt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"2.39"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","text":"Im Gegentheil haben sich mir zu häufig und zu heftig solche Gegner gezeigt, welche nicht die einfache Reflexion machen mochten, daß ihre Einfälle und Einwürfe Kategorien enthalten, welche Voraussetzungen sind und selbst erst der Kritik bedürfen, ehe sie gebraucht werden. Die Bewußtlosigkeit hierüber geht unglaublich weit; sie macht das Grund-Mißverständniß, das üble d. h. ungebildete Benehmen, bei einer Kategorie, die betrachtet wird, etwas Anderes zu denken und nicht diese Kategorie selbst. Diese Bewußtlosigkeit ist um so weniger zu rechtfertigen, als solches Anderes andere Denkbestimmungen und Begriffe sind, in einem Systeme der Logik aber eben diese anderen Kategorien gleichfalls ihre Stelle müssen gefunden haben, und daselbst für sich der Betrachtung werden unterworfen seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"2.40"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","text":"Am auffallendsten ist dieß in der überwiegenden Menge von Einwürfen und Angriffen, die auf die ersten Begriffe oder Sätze der Logik, das Seyn und Nichts und das Werden, als welches, selbst eine einfache Bestimmung, wohl unbestritten,—die einfachste Analyse zeigt dieß,—jene beiden Bestimmungen als Momente enthält. Die Gründlichkeit scheint zu erfordern, den Anfang, als den Grund, worauf Alles gebaut sey, vor Allem aus zu untersuchen, ja nicht weiter zu gehen, als bis er sich fest erwiesen hat, im Gegentheil vielmehr, wenn dieß nicht der Fall ist, alles noch Folgende zu verwerfen.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"2.41"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0042","text":"Diese Gründlichkeit hat zugleich den Vortheil, die größte Erleichterung für das Denkgeschäft zu gewähren, sie hat die ganze Entwickelung in diesen Keim eingeschlossen vor sich, und hält sich für mit Allem fertig, wenn sie mit diesem fertig ist, der das Leichteste zum Abthun ist, denn er ist das Einfachste, das Einfache selbst; es ist die geringe Arbeit, die erforderlich ist, wodurch sich diese so selbst zufriedene Gründlichkeit wesentlich empfiehlt. Diese Beschränkung auf das Einfache läßt der Willkür des Denkens, das für sich nicht einfach bleiben will, sondern seine Reflexionen darüber anbringt, freien Spielraum. Mit dem guten Rechte, sich zuerst nur mit dem Princip zu beschäftigen, und damit sich auf das Weitere nicht einzulassen, thut diese Gründlichkeit in ihrem Geschäfte selbst das Gegentheil hiervon, vielmehr das Weitere, d.i.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"2.42"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043","text":"andere Kategorien als nur das Princip ist, andere Voraussetzungen und Vorurtheile herbeizubringen. Solche Voraussetzungen, daß die Unendlichkeit verschieden von der Endlichkeit, der Inhalt etwas Anderes als die Form, das Innere ein Anderes als das Äußere, die Vermittelung ebenso nicht die Unmittelbarkeit sey, als ob einer dergleichen nicht wüßte, werden zugleich belehrungsweise vorgebracht und nicht sowohl bewiesen, als erzählt und versichert.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"2.43"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","text":"In solchem Belehren als Benehmen liegt—man kann es nicht anders nennen,—eine Albernheit; der Sache nach aber Theils das Unberechtigte, dergleichen nur vorauszusetzen und geradezu anzunehmen, Theils aber noch mehr die Unwissenheit, daß es das Bedürfniß und Geschäft des logischen Denkens ist, eben dieß zu untersuchen, ob denn so ein Endliches ohne Unendlichkeit etwas Wahres ist, ebenso solche abstrakte Unendlichkeit, ferner ein formloser Inhalt und eine inhaltlose Form, so ein Inneres für sich, das keine Äußerung hat, eine Äußerlichkeit ohne Innerlichkeit u.s.f.—etwas Wahres, ebenso etwas Wirkliches ist.—Aber diese Bildung und Zucht des Denkens, durch welche ein plastisches Verhalten desselben bewirkt und die Ungeduld der einfallenden Reflexion überwunden würde, wird allein durch das Weitergehen, das Studium und die Produktion der ganzen Entwickelung verschafft.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"2.44"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0045","text":"Bei der Erwähnung platonischer Darstellung kann, wer ein selbstständiges Gebäude philosophischer Wissenschaft in modernen Zeiten neu aufzuführen arbeitet, an die Erzählung erinnert werden, daß Plato seine Bücher über den Staat sieben Mal umgearbeitet habe. Die Erinnerung hieran, eine Vergleichung, insofern sie eine solche in sich zu schließen schiene, dürfte nur um so mehr bis zu dem Wunsch treiben, daß für ein Werk, das, als der modernen Welt angehörig, ein tieferes Princip, einen schwereren Gegenstand und ein Material von reicherm Umfang zur Bearbeitung vor sich hat, die freie Muße, es sieben und siebenzig Mal durchzuarbeiten, gewährt gewesen wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"2.45"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0046","text":"So aber mußte der Verfasser, indem er es im Angesicht der Größe der Aufgabe betrachtet, sich mit dem begnügen, was es hat werden mögen, unter den Umständen einer äußerlichen Nothwendigkeit, der unabwendbaren Zerstreuung durch die Größe und Vielseitigkeit der Zeitinteressen, sogar unter dem Zweifel, ob der laute Lärm des Tages und die betäubende Geschwätzigkeit der Einbildung, die auf denselben sich zu beschränken eitel ist, noch Raum für die Theilnahme an der leidenschaftslosen Stille der nur denkenden Erkenntniß offen lasse.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"2.46"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0047","text":"Berlin, den 7. November 1831.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"2.47"}],"sha256":"735c8914b1b9617e429e419de2fba025b802b1383c31b57340e34976e55cb01d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101402612025Z_4a3ab1a1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Preface to the Second Edition.","source_sha256":"735c8914b1b9617e429e419de2fba025b802b1383c31b57340e34976e55cb01d","sha256":"09399562ecc9363ddee9806611f1f5d7bf7ce4a6e4da15cdc5ab459924870d07","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:14:02.612048+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001","text":"I have certainly undertaken this new treatment of the Science of Logic, of which the first volume is hereby appearing, with full consciousness both of the difficulty of the subject in itself and then of its presentation, and of the imperfection which its treatment in the first edition bears within itself; however much I have endeavoured, after further years of occupation with this science, to remedy this imperfection, I still feel that I have sufficient cause to claim the reader’s indulgence. A title to such a claim, however, may in the first place well be founded on the circumstance that, for the content, only external material was chiefly to be found in the earlier metaphysics and logic.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"2.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","text":"However generally and frequently these, the latter even down to our times, have been cultivated, such treatment has little affected the speculative side; rather, on the whole, the same material has been repeated, alternately diluted to trivial superficiality, alternately the old ballast has been brought forth anew more extensively and dragged along, so that by such, often wholly mechanical, endeavours no gain could accrue to philosophical content. To present the realm of thought philosophically, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"2.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","text":"in its own immanent activity, or, what is the same thing, in its necessary development, had therefore to be a new undertaking, and had to begin from the beginning; but that acquired material, the familiar forms of thought, is to be regarded as a most important given, indeed as a necessary condition, a presupposition to be gratefully acknowledged, even if it affords only here and there a dry thread, or the lifeless bones of a skeleton, even thrown together among one another in disorder.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"2.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","text":"The forms of thought are first set forth and deposited in human language; in our days one cannot be reminded often enough that that whereby the human being distinguishes himself from the animal is thought. Language has intruded itself into everything that becomes an inward element for him, representation in general, everything that he makes his own; and whatever he makes into language and expresses in it contains, enveloped, mixed, or worked out, a category; so natural is the logical to him, or rather it is his own peculiar nature itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"2.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005","text":"But if nature in general, as the physical, is set in opposition to the spiritual, then one would have to say that the logical is rather the supernatural, which intrudes into every natural comportment of the human being, into his feeling, intuiting, desiring, need, drive, and thereby makes it generally into something human, even if only formally, into representations and ends. It is the advantage of a language if it possesses a wealth of logical expressions, namely expressions proper to and separate for the determinations of thought themselves; among prepositions and articles, many already belong to such relations, which rest on thought; the Chinese language is said in its development not to have attained this at all, or only scantily; but these particles appear entirely subserviently, only somewhat more detached than augmentations, inflectional signs, and the like.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"2.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0006","text":"Much more important is it that, in a language, the determinations of thought are set forth as nouns and verbs and thus stamped into objective form; the German language has in this many advantages over the other modern languages; indeed, some of its words have the further peculiarity of having not merely different meanings, but opposed ones, so that a speculative spirit of language itself cannot be overlooked in this; it can give thought pleasure to encounter such words, and to find the union of opposites—which is the result of speculation, but is absurd for the understanding—already, in a naïve manner, lexically as one word with the opposed meanings.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"2.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0007","text":"Philosophy therefore requires no special terminology at all; certainly some words are to be adopted from foreign languages, though through usage they have already received citizenship in it; an affected purism would be least in place where what is at issue most decidedly is the matter itself.—The progress of culture generally, and of the sciences in particular, even the empirical and sensuous sciences, since in general they move in the most ordinary categories (e.g. of a whole and the parts, of a thing and its properties, and the like), gradually also brings higher relations of thought to light, or at least raises them to greater universality and thereby to closer attention. When, e.g.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"2.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0008","text":"in physics the determination of thought of force has become predominant, in more recent times the category of polarity—which, moreover, is too much… à tort et à travers forced into everything, even into light—plays the most significant role,—the determination of a difference in which the different are inseparably connected;—that in this manner there has been advanced from the form of abstraction, of identity, through which a determinacy, e.g. as force, receives an independence, and the form of determining, of difference, which at the same time remains as an inseparable element in identity, has been brought out and has become a familiar representation, is of infinite importance.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"2.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0009","text":"Through the reality in which its objects hold fast, the consideration of nature brings with it this compulsion to fix the categories, which can no longer be ignored in it, even with the greatest inconsistency towards others which are likewise allowed to be valid, and not to permit that, as happens more readily in the spiritual sphere, one should advance to abstractions from opposition and to universality.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"2.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","text":"But while logical objects, like their expressions, are thus something altogether familiar in culture, yet, as I have said elsewhere, what is familiar is not therefore cognized, and it can even provoke impatience to have still to occupy oneself with what is familiar; and what is more familiar than precisely the determinations of thought, of which we make use everywhere, which come from our mouths in every sentence that we speak.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"2.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0011","text":"This preface is intended to indicate the general moments concerning the course of cognition from this familiar starting-point, concerning the relation of scientific thought to this natural thought; so much, taken together with what the earlier Introduction contains, will be sufficient to give a general representation—as one demands to receive such a representation of a science in advance, before that science which is the matter itself—of the sense of logical cognition.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"2.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","text":"First of all, it is to be regarded as an infinite advance that the forms of thought have been freed from the material in which they are submerged in self-conscious intuiting and representing, as in our desiring and willing—or rather also in representational desiring and willing (—and there is no human desiring or willing without representing—)—that these universals have been brought out for themselves and, as Plato and then above all Aristotle did, made into objects of consideration for themselves. This gives the beginning of cognition of them. “Only after almost everything necessary,” says Aristotle, “and what belongs to the convenience and intercourse of life, was present, did people begin to endeavour after philosophical cognition.”","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"2.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","text":"“In Egypt,” he had remarked previously, “the mathematical sciences were developed early, because there the priestly estate was early placed in the situation of having leisure.”—Indeed, the need to occupy oneself with pure thoughts presupposes a long course which the human spirit must have gone through; it is, one may say, it is the need of the already satisfied need, of the necessity of freedom from need, to which it must have come, the abstraction from the material of intuiting, imagining, etc., from the concrete interests of desire, drives, and will, in which material the determinations of thought lie enveloped. In the quiet spaces of thought that has come to itself and is only in itself, the interests which move the life of peoples and individuals fall silent.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"2.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","text":"“In so many respects,” says Aristotle in the same context, “human nature is dependent, but this science, which is not sought for some use, alone is free in and for itself, and thus it seems not to be a human possession.”—Philosophy in general still has to do, in its thoughts, with concrete objects—God, nature, spirit—but logic concerns itself wholly only with these for themselves in their complete abstraction. Therefore this logic is wont to fall initially to the study of youth, which has not yet entered into the interests of concrete life, lives in leisure with respect to them, and initially has only to occupy itself, for its subjective end, with acquiring the means and possibilities of becoming active in the objects of those interests, and to occupy itself with these themselves still theoretically.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"2.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0015","text":"Among these means, contrary to Aristotle’s cited representation, logical science is counted; the labour upon it is a preliminary work, its place is the school, which is only to be followed by the seriousness of life and activity for true ends. In life the categories come to be used; they are lowered from the honour of being considered for themselves to serve, in the spiritual occupation with living content, in the creation and exchange of the representations relating thereto,—partly as abbreviations through their universality;—for what an infinite multitude of particulars of external existence and activity is comprehended by the representation: battle, war, people, or sea, animal, etc.;—how, in the representation: God or love, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"2.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","text":"an infinite multitude of representations, activities, states, etc. is epitomized into the simplicity of such representing!—Partly, [the categories serve] for the more precise determination and finding of objective relations; yet in this case the content and end, the correctness and truth of the thought that intervenes, are made wholly dependent on what is present itself, and no content-determining efficacy is ascribed to the determinations of thought for themselves. Such use of the categories, which was previously called natural logic, is unconscious; and when, in scientific reflection, the relation of serving as means is assigned to them in the spirit, thought in general is made into something subordinate to the other spiritual determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"2.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0017","text":"Of our feelings, drives, interests, we do not properly say that they serve us; rather, they count as independent forces and powers, such that we ourselves are this: to feel thus, to desire and will thus, to place our interest in this. But it can rather become our consciousness that we stand in the service of our feelings, drives, passions, interests, and indeed of habits, than that we possess them; still less that, in our intimate unity with them, they serve us as means. Such determinations of disposition and spirit soon show themselves to us as particulars in opposition to the universality of which we become conscious, in which we have our freedom, and we hold that in these particularities we are rather confined, ruled by them.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"2.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","text":"Accordingly, we can then much less hold that the forms of thought, which run through all our representations, whether these are merely theoretical or contain a material belonging to feeling, drive, will, serve us; that we possess them, rather than they us; what remains to us in opposition to them, how are we, how am I, to set myself as the more universal above them, they who are themselves the universal as such? When we place ourselves in a feeling, end, interest, and find ourselves therein restricted, unfree, then the place into which we are able to withdraw from these and back into freedom is this place of the certainty of oneself, of pure abstraction, of thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"2.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","text":"Or likewise, when we wish to speak of things, we call their nature or essence their concept, and this is only for thought; but of the concepts of things we shall still less say that we rule them, or that the determinations of thought, of which they are the complex, serve us; on the contrary, our thought must restrict itself according to them, and our arbitrariness or freedom ought not to wish to fashion them after itself. Insofar, therefore, as subjective thought is our most proper, most inward activity, and the objective concept of things constitutes the matter itself, we cannot be outside that activity, cannot stand above it, and just as little can we go beyond the nature of things.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"2.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","text":"Yet we can disregard the latter determination; it coincides with the former insofar as it would yield a relation of our thoughts to the thing, but only something empty, since the thing would thereby be posited as the rule for our concepts, whereas the thing itself can be nothing other for us than our concepts of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"2.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","text":"If critical philosophy understands the relation of these three termini in such a way that we place thoughts between ourselves and things as a middle, in the sense that this middle rather shuts us off from things instead of joining us with them, then the simple observation must be set against this view that precisely these things, which are supposed to stand at the other extreme beyond us and beyond the thoughts relating to them, are themselves thought-things, and, as wholly indeterminate, only One thought-thing,—the so-called thing-in-itself—are the empty abstraction itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"2.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","text":"Yet this may suffice for the point of view from which the relation disappears according to which determinations of thought are taken merely for use and as means; more important is what is further connected with this, according to which they are customarily conceived as external forms.—The activity of thinking that pervades all our representations, purposes, interests, and actions is, as stated, unconsciously active (natural logic); what consciousness has before it is the content, the objects of representations, that with which interest is filled; according to this relation, determinations of thought count as forms that are only on the content, and are not themselves the content.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"2.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0023","text":"But if it is as was indicated above, and as is otherwise generally conceded, that nature, the peculiar essence, the truly enduring and substantial amid the multiplicity and contingency of appearance and the contingency of appearance and transitory expression, is the concept of the thing, the universal in it itself—just as every human individual, though infinitely peculiar, has within itself the prius of all its peculiarity in being human, just as every individual animal has the prius of being animal—then it could not be said what such an individual would still be if this foundation were removed from that which is equipped with ever so many other predicates, although it too can be called, like the others, a predicate.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"2.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","text":"The indispensable foundation, the concept, the universal, which is thought itself, insofar as one can abstract merely from representation in the word “thought,” cannot be regarded merely as an indifferent form that is on a content. But these thoughts of all natural and spiritual things, even the substantial content, are still such as contain manifold determinacies and still have in themselves the distinction of a soul and a body, of the concept and a relative reality; the deeper foundation is the soul for itself, the pure concept, which is the innermost of objects, their simple pulse of life, as it is also of the subjective thinking of them. To bring to consciousness this logical nature which animates spirit, impels and works within it, this is the task.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"2.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0025","text":"Instinct-like action differs from intelligent and free action generally in that the latter occurs with consciousness: when the content of what impels is brought forth from its immediate unity with the subject into objectivity before it, there begins the freedom of spirit, which, caught in the instinctive working of thought, is fragmented in the bonds of its categories into an infinitely manifold material. In this net, firmer knots are tied here and there, which are the points of support and direction of its life and consciousness; they owe their firmness and power precisely to the fact that, brought before consciousness, they are concepts of its essence that are in and for themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"2.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","text":"The most important point for the nature of spirit is the relation not only of what it is in itself to what it actually is, but of that as which it knows itself; this self-knowing is, because spirit is essentially consciousness, the fundamental determination of its actuality. To purify these categories, which are effective only instinctively as drives and initially, in isolation, thus variably and confusingly, are brought into the consciousness of spirit and thereby afford it an isolated and uncertain actuality, and thereby to raise it in them to freedom and truth—this, then, is the higher logical task.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"2.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","text":"What we indicated as the beginning of science, whose high value in itself and at the same time as the condition of genuine cognition was acknowledged above—to treat the concepts and the moments of the concept in general, the determinations of thought initially as forms that are distinct from material and only on it—immediately reveals itself in itself as a comportment inappropriate to truth, which is indicated as the object and purpose of logic. For, as mere forms, as distinct from content, they are assumed to stand in a determination that stamps them as finite and makes them incapable of grasping truth, which is infinite in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"2.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0028","text":"Whatever else may be associated with limitation and finitude in the true, in whatever respect it may be, this is the side of its negation, its untruth and unreality, precisely its end, not the affirmation that it is as true. Against the barrenness of merely formal categories, the instinct of sound reason has finally felt itself so strengthened that it leaves knowledge of them, with contempt, to the domain of school logic and school metaphysics—together with disregard for the value which even consciousness of these threads has for itself, and with unconsciousness of still being captive, in the instinct-like activity of natural logic, and even more in the reflective rejection of knowledge and cognition of the determinations of thought themselves, in the service of unpurified and hence unfree thinking.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"2.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0029","text":"The simple fundamental determination, or common formal determination, of the collection of such forms is identity, which is asserted in the logic of this collection as law, as A=A, as the principle of contradiction. Sound reason has so greatly lost its reverence for the school, which possesses such laws of truth and in which they are still constantly taught, that it laughs at it on this account, and considers intolerable a person who knows how to speak truly according to such laws: the plant is a—plant, science is—science, and so forth to infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"2.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","text":"Concerning the formulae, too, that constitute the rules of inference—which is in fact a chief use of the understanding—the equally justified consciousness has established itself, however unjust it is to fail to recognize that they have their field in cognition, in which they must be valid, and at the same time that they are essential material for the thinking of reason: that they are indifferent means, at least equally, of error and sophistry, and, however truth may otherwise be determined, are unusable for higher truth, e.g. religious truth; that in general they concern only a correctness of cognitions, not truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"2.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","text":"The incompleteness of this way of considering thought, which leaves truth aside, can be supplemented only by drawing into thinking consideration not merely what is customarily reckoned as external form, but also content. It soon shows itself of its own accord that what is separated from form as content in the nearest and most ordinary reflection ought in fact not to be formless, not indeterminate in itself; for then it would be only the empty, perhaps the abstraction of the thing-in-itself,—but rather that it has form within itself, indeed has animation and content only through this form, and that form itself is what passes over only into the semblance of a content, and thereby also into the semblance of something external to this semblance.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"2.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0032","text":"With this introduction of content into logical consideration, it is not things but the matter, the concept of things, that becomes the object.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"2.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","text":"Here one may also be reminded that there is a multitude of concepts, a multitude of matters. But what limits this multitude has in part been said above: that the concept, as thought in general, as universal, is the immeasurable abbreviation in contrast to the individuality of things as their multitude hovers before indeterminate intuition and representation; but in part, a concept is immediately, first, the concept in itself, and this is only One and is the substantial foundation; while, secondly, it is indeed a determinate concept, and this determinacy in it is what appears as content; but the determinacy of the concept is a formal determination of this substantial unity, a moment of form as totality, of the concept itself, which is the foundation of determinate concepts.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"2.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","text":"This is not sensuously intuited or represented; it is only object, product, and content of thought, and the matter that is in and for itself, the Logos, the reason of what is, the truth of what bears the name of things; least of all is the Logos something that should be left outside logical science. Therefore it must not be optional to draw it into science or to leave it outside. If determinations of thought, which are only external forms, are truly considered in themselves, only their finitude and the untruth of their supposed being-for-self can emerge, and, as their truth, the concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"2.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","text":"Hence logical science, in treating the determinations of thought that generally pervade our spirit instinctively and unconsciously, and which, even when they enter into language, remain unobjectified and unnoticed, will also be the reconstruction of those which reflection has raised out and fixed as subjective forms external to material and content.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"2.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","text":"The presentation of no object would be capable, in and for itself, of being altogether strictly and wholly immanently plastic as much as that of the development of thought in its necessity; no object carries this demand with it so greatly; its science would in this respect have to surpass even mathematics, for no object possesses in itself this freedom and independence. Such an exposition would require, as is present in its fashion in the course of mathematical consequence, that at no stage of development should a determination of thought or reflection occur which does not arise immediately at this stage and has passed over into it from the preceding stages.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"2.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037","text":"Yet such abstract perfection of presentation must indeed generally be renounced; already because science must begin with the purely simple, and thus with the most universal and emptiest, the exposition would permit only these wholly simple expressions of the simple itself, without any further addition of any word;—what might take place in accordance with the matter would be negating reflections, which endeavoured to ward off and remove what representation or an unregulated thinking might otherwise intermingle.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"2.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","text":"Such incursions into the simple immanent course of development are, however, accidental in themselves, and the endeavour to repel them is thus itself afflicted with this contingency; besides, it is futile to wish to meet all such incursions, precisely because they lie outside the matter, and at the very least incompleteness would be what would here be required for systematic satisfaction.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"2.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","text":"But the peculiar unrest and distraction of our modern consciousness permits no other course than likewise to take more or less account of reflections and notions that lie close at hand; a plastic exposition then also requires a plastic sense of reception and understanding; but such plastic youths and men, listeners quietly following only the matter, with the self-renunciation of their own reflections and notions by which independent thinking is impatient to prove itself, as Plato depicts them, could not be presented in a modern dialogue; still less could one count on such readers.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"2.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","text":"On the contrary, opponents have shown themselves to me too frequently and too vehemently who would not make the simple reflection that their notions and objections contain categories which are presuppositions and themselves first require criticism before they are used. The unconsciousness about this goes incredibly far; it produces the fundamental misunderstanding, the bad, i.e. uncultivated, conduct of thinking something other than the category itself when a category is under consideration. This unconsciousness is all the less justifiable since such an other consists of other determinations of thought and concepts; but in a system of logic these other categories too must likewise have found their place, and there be subjected to consideration for themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"2.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","text":"This is most striking in the preponderant multitude of objections and attacks directed against the first concepts or propositions of logic, being and nothing and becoming, which, itself a simple determination, undoubtedly—as the simplest analysis shows—contains those two determinations as moments. Thoroughness seems to require that the beginning, as the ground upon which everything is built, be investigated before all else, indeed that one go no further until it has proved itself firm; on the contrary, if this is not the case, that everything following be rejected.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"2.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0042","text":"This thoroughness at the same time has the advantage of affording the greatest relief for the work of thinking; it has before it the whole development enclosed in this germ, and considers itself finished with everything when it is finished with this, which is the easiest to dispose of, for it is the simplest, simplicity itself; it is the slight labour required that essentially recommends this thoroughness, so self-satisfied as it is. This restriction to the simple leaves free play to the arbitrariness of thinking, which does not wish to remain simple for itself, but introduces its reflections upon it. With the good right of occupying itself at first only with the principle, and thus not entering upon what follows, this thoroughness, in its own procedure, does the opposite of this, namely, what follows, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"2.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043","text":"to bring in categories other than merely the principle, other presuppositions and prejudices. Such presuppositions—that infinity is different from finitude, content something other than form, the inner something other than the outer, mediation likewise not immediacy—as though one did not know such things, are at the same time advanced by way of instruction and not so much proved as narrated and asserted.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"2.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","text":"In such instruction as conduct there lies—one cannot call it otherwise—an absurdity; but as to the matter, partly the unwarrantedness of merely presupposing and directly assuming such things, and still more the ignorance that it is the need and business of logical thinking to investigate precisely this: whether such a finite without infinity is something true, likewise such abstract infinity; further, a formless content and a contentless form; such an inner for itself that has no expression, an externality without inwardness, etc.—whether these are something true, likewise something actual.—But this cultivation and discipline of thinking, through which a plastic comportment of it would be brought about and the impatience of intrusive reflection overcome, is imparted only through proceeding further, through study and the production of the whole development.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"2.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0045","text":"At the mention of Platonic presentation, one who is working to erect anew, in modern times, an independent edifice of philosophical science may be reminded of the account that Plato reworked his books on the state seven times. The recollection of this, a comparison, insofar as it might seem to contain one, could only all the more lead to the wish that, for a work which, as belonging to the modern world, has before it for treatment a deeper principle, a more difficult subject, and material of richer scope, the free leisure to work through it seventy-seven times might have been granted.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"2.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0046","text":"But thus the author, when he considered it in the face of the magnitude of the task, had to content himself with what it may have become, under the circumstances of an external necessity, of the unavoidable distraction caused by the magnitude and multiplicity of the interests of the age, indeed under the doubt whether the loud din of the day and the deafening chatter of vain imagination, which prides itself on confining itself to it, might still leave open room for participation in the passionless stillness of merely thinking cognition.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"2.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0047","text":"Berlin, 7 November 1831.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"2.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0047"]}],"source_digest":"7e4661a8605561e3be54d0c7557df07698ee43e9cede744877cc8bbbf720aadf","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Vorrede zur zweiten Auflage."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Vorrede zur zweiten Auflage.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL","title":"General Concept of Logic","order":3,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ABDL","text":"## Einleitung\n\n## Allgemeiner Begriff der Logik\n\nEs fühlt sich bei keiner Wissenschaft stärker das Bedürfniß, ohne vorangehende Reflexionen, von der Sache selbst anzufangen, als bei der logischen Wissenschaft. In jeder andern ist der Gegenstand, den sie behandelt, und die wissenschaftliche Methode von einander unterschieden; so wie auch der Inhalt nicht einen absoluten Anfang macht, sondern von andern Begriffen abhängt, und um sich herum mit anderem Stoffe zusammenhängt. Diesen Wissenschaften wird es daher zugegeben, von ihrem Boden und dessen Zusammenhang, so wie von der Methode nur lemmatischer Weise zu sprechen, die als bekannt und angenommen vorausgesetzten Formen von Definitionen und dergleichen ohne weiteres anzuwenden, und sich der gewöhnlichen Art des Raisonnements zur Festsetzung ihrer allgemeinen Begriffe und Grundbestimmungen zu bedienen.\n\nDie Logik dagegen kann keine dieser Formen der Reflexion oder Regeln und Gesetze des Denkens voraussetzen, denn sie machen einen Theil ihres Inhalts selbst aus und haben erst innerhalb ihrer begründet zu werden. Nicht nur aber die Angabe der wissenschaftlichen Methode, sondern auch der Begriff selbst der Wissenschaft überhaupt gehört zu ihrem Inhalte, und zwar macht er ihr letztes Resultat aus; was sie ist, kann sie daher nicht voraussagen, sondern ihre ganze Abhandlung bringt dieß Wissen von ihr selbst erst als ihr Letztes und als ihre Vollendung hervor. Gleichfalls ihr Gegenstand, das Denken oder bestimmter das begreifende Denken, wird wesentlich innerhalb ihrer abgehandelt; der Begriff desselben erzeugt sich in ihrem Verlaufe, und kann somit nicht vorausgeschickt werden. Was daher in dieser Einleitung vorausgeschickt wird, hat nicht den Zweck, den Begriff der Logik etwa zu begründen, oder den Inhalt und die Methode derselben zum voraus wissenschaftlich zu rechtfertigen, sondern, durch einige Erläuterungen und Reflexionen, in raisonnirendem und historischem Sinne, den Gesichtspunkt, aus welchem diese Wissenschaft zu betrachten ist, der Vorstellung näher zu bringen.\n\nWenn die Logik als die Wissenschaft des Denkens im Allgemeinen angenommen wird, so wird dabei verstanden, daß dieß Denken die bloße Form einer Erkenntniß ausmache, daß die Logik von allem Inhalte abstrahire, und das sogenannte zweite Bestandstück, das zu einer Erkenntniß gehöre, die Materie, anderswoher gegeben werden müsse, daß somit die Logik als von welcher diese Materie ganz und gar unabhängig sey, nur die formalen Bedingungen wahrhafter Erkenntniß angeben, nicht aber reale Wahrheit selbst enthalten, noch auch nur der Weg zu realer Wahrheit seyn könne, weil gerade das Wesentliche der Wahrheit, der Inhalt, außer ihr liege.\n\nVors Erste aber ist es schon ungeschickt zu sagen, daß die Logik von allem Inhalte abstrahire, daß sie nur die Regeln des Denkens lehre, ohne auf das Gedachte sich einzulassen und auf dessen Beschaffenheit Rücksicht nehmen zu können. Denn da das Denken und die Regeln des Denkens ihr Gegenstand seyn sollen, so hat sie ja unmittelbar daran ihren eigenthümlichen Inhalt; sie hat daran auch jenes zweite Bestandstück der Erkenntniß, eine Materie, um deren Beschaffenheit sie sich bekümmert.\n\nAllein zweitens sind überhaupt die Vorstellungen, auf denen der Begriff der Logik bisher beruhte, Theils bereits untergegangen, Theils ist es Zeit, daß sie vollends verschwinden, daß der Standpunkt dieser Wissenschaft höher gefaßt werde, und daß sie eine völlig veränderte Gestalt gewinne.\n\nDer bisherige Begriff der Logik beruht auf der im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn ein für allemal vorausgesetzten Trennung des Inhalts der Erkenntniß und der Form derselben, oder der Wahrheit und der Gewißheit. Es wird erstens vorausgesetzt, daß der Stoff des Erkennens, als eine fertige Welt außerhalb des Denkens, an und für sich vorhanden, daß das Denken für sich leer sey, als eine Form äußerlich zu jener Materie hinzutrete, sich damit erfülle, erst daran einen Inhalt gewinne und dadurch ein reales Erkennen werde.\n\nAlsdann stehen diese beiden Bestandtheile,—(denn sie sollen das Verhältniß von Bestandtheilen haben, und das Erkennen wird aus ihnen mechanischer oder höchstens chemischer Weise zusammengesetzt—) in dieser Rangordnung gegen einander, daß das Objekt ein für sich Vollendetes, Fertiges sey, das des Denkens zu seiner Wirklichkeit vollkommen entbehren könne, da hingegen das Denken etwas Mangelhaftes sey, das sich erst an einem Stoffe zu vervollständigen, und zwar als eine weiche unbestimmte Form sich seiner Materie angemessen zu machen habe. Wahrheit ist die Übereinstimmung des Denkens mit dem Gegenstande, und es soll, um diese Übereinstimmung hervorzubringen, —denn sie ist nicht an und für sich vorhanden,—das Denken nach dem Gegenstande sich fügen und bequemen.\n\nDrittens, indem die Verschiedenheit der Materie und der Form, des Gegenstandes und des Denkens nicht in jener neblichten Unbestimmtheit gelassen, sondern bestimmter genommen wird, so ist jede eine von der andern geschiedene Sphäre. Das Denken kommt daher in seinem Empfangen und Formiren des Stoffs nicht über sich hinaus, sein Empfangen und sich nach ihm Bequemen bleibt eine Modifikation seiner selbst, es wird dadurch nicht zu seinem Andern; und das selbstbewußte Bestimmen gehört ohnedieß nur ihm an; es kommt also auch in seiner Beziehung auf den Gegenstand nicht aus sich heraus zu dem Gegenstande, dieser bleibt als ein Ding an sich, schlechthin ein Jenseits des Denkens.\n\nDiese Ansichten über das Verhältnis des Subjektes und Objekts zu einander drücken die Bestimmungen aus, welche die Natur unsers gewöhnlichen, des erscheinenden Bewußtseins ausmachen; aber diese Vorurtheile, in die Vernunft übergetragen, als ob in ihr dasselbe Verhältniß Gott finde, als ob dieses Verhältniß an und für sich Wahrheit habe, so sind sie die Irrthümer, deren durch alle Theile des geistigen und natürlichen Universums durchgeführte Widerlegung die Philosophie ist, oder die vielmehr, weil sie den Eingang in die Philosophie versperren, vor derselben abzulegen sind.\n\nDie ältere Metaphysik hatte in dieser Rücksicht einen höhern Begriff von dem Denken als in der neuern Zeit gäng und gäb geworden ist. Jene legte nämlich zu Grunde, daß das, was durchs Denken von und an den Dingen erkannt werde, das allein an ihnen wahrhaft Wahre sey; somit nicht sie in ihrer Unmittelbarkeit, sondern sie erst in die Form des Denkens erhoben, als Gedachte. Diese Metaphysik hielt somit dafür, daß das Denken und die Bestimmungen des Denkens nicht ein den Gegenständen Fremdes, sondern vielmehr deren Wesen sey, oder daß die Dinge und das Denken derselben, (—wie auch unsere Sprache eine Verwandtschaft derselben ausdrückt,—) an und für sich übereinstimmen, daß das Denken in seinen immanenten Bestimmungen, und die wahrhafte Natur der Dinge, ein und derselbe Inhalt sey.\n\nAber der reflektirende Verstand bemächtigte sich der Philosophie. Es ist genau zu wissen, was dieser Ausdruck sagen will, der sonst vielfach als Schlagwort gebraucht wird; es ist überhaupt darunter der abstrahirende und damit trennende Verstand zu verstehen, der in seinen Trennungen beharrt. Gegen die Vernunft gekehrt beträgt er sich als gemeiner Menschenverstand und macht seine Ansicht geltend, daß die Wahrheit auf sinnlicher Realität beruhe, daß die Gedanken nur Gedanken seyen, in dem Sinne, daß erst die sinnliche Wahrnehmung ihnen Gehalt und Realität gebe, daß die Vernunft, insofern sie an und für sich bleibe, nur Hinrgespinnste erzeuge. In diesem Verzichtthun der Vernunft auf sich selbst, geht der Begriff der Wahrheit verloren, sie ist darauf eingeschränkt, nur subjektive Wahrheit, nur die Erscheinung zu erkennen, nur etwas, dem die Natur der Sache selbst nicht entspreche; das Wissen ist zur Meinung zurückgefallen.\n\nDiese Wendung jedoch, welche das Erkennen nimmt, und die als Verlust und Rückschritt erscheint, hat das Tiefere zum Grunde, worauf überhaupt die Erhebung der Vernunft in den höhern Geist der neuern Philosophie beruht. Der Grund jener allgemein gewordenen Vorstellung ist nämlich in der Einsicht von dem nothwendigen Widerstreite der Bestimmungen des Verstandes mit sich selbst, zu suchen.—Die schon namhaft gemacht Reflexion ist dieß, über das konkrete Unmittelbare hinaus zu gehen, und dasselbe zu bestimmen und zu trennen. Aber sie muß ebenso sehr über diese ihre trennenden Bestimmungen hinausgehen, und sie zunächst beziehen. Auf dem Standpunkte dieses Beziehens tritt der Widerstreit derselben hervor. Dieses Beziehen der Reflexion gehört an sich der Vernunft an; die Erhebung über jene Bestimmungen, die zur Einsicht des Widerstreits derselben gelangt, ist der große negative Schritt zum wahrhaften Begriffe der Vernunft. Aber die nicht durchgeführte Einsicht fällt in den Mißverstand, als ob die Vernunft es sey, welche in Widerspruch mit sich gerathe; sie erkennt nicht, daß der Widerspruch eben das Erheben der Vernunft über die Beschränkungen des Verstandes und das Auflösen derselben ist. Statt von hier aus den letzten Schritt in die Höhe zu thun, ist die Erkenntniß von dem Unbefriedigenden der Verstandesbestimmungen zu der sinnlichen Existenz zurückgeflohen, an derselben das Feste und Einige zu haben vermeinend.\n\nIndem aber auf der andern Seite diese Erkenntniß sich als die Erkenntniß von Erscheinendem weiß, wird das Unbefriedigende derselben eingestanden, aber zugleich vorausgesetzt, als ob zwar nicht die Dinge an sich, aber doch innerhalb der Sphäre der Erscheinung richtig erkannt würde; als ob dabei gleichsam nur die Art der Gegenstände verschieden wäre, und die eine Art, nämlich die Dinge an sich zwar nicht, aber doch die andere Art, nämlich die Erscheinungen, in die Erkenntniß fielen. Wie wenn einem Manne richtige Einsicht beigemessen würde, mit dem Zusatz, daß er jedoch nichts Wahres, sondern nur Unwahres einzusehen fähig sey. So ungereimt das Letztere wäre, so ungereimt ist eine wahre Erkenntniß, die den Gegenstand nicht erkennte, wie er an sich ist.\n\nDie Kritik der Formen des Verstandes hat das angeführte Resultat gehabt, daß diese Formen keine Anwendung auf die Dinge an sich haben. —Dieß kann keinen andern Sinn haben, als daß diese Formen an ihnen selbst etwas Unwahres sind. Allein indem sie für die subjektive Vernunft und für die Erfahrung als geltend gelassen werden, so hat die Kritik keine Änderung an ihnen selbst bewirkt, sondern läßt sie für das Subjekt in derselben Gestalt, wie sie sonst für das Objekt galten. Wenn sie aber ungenügend für das Ding an sich sind, so müßte der Verstand, dem sie angehören sollen, noch weniger dieselben sich gefallen lassen und damit vorlieb nehmen wollen. Wenn sie nicht Bestimmungen des Dings an sich seyn können, so können sie noch weniger Bestimmungen des Verstandes seyn, dem wenigstens die Würde eines Dings an sich zugestanden werden sollte. Die Bestimmungen des Endlichen und Unendlichen sind in demselben Widerstreit, es sey, daß sie auf Zeit und Raum, auf die Welt angewendet werden, oder daß sie Bestimmungen innerhalb des Geistes seyen; so gut als schwarz und weiß ein Grau geben, ob sie an einer Wand, oder aber noch auf der Pallete mit einander vereinigt werden; wenn unsere Weltvorstellung sich auflöst, indem die Bestimmungen des Unendlichen und Endlichen auf sie übergetragen werden, so ist noch mehr der Geist selbst, welcher sie beide in sich enthält, ein in sich selbst Widersprechendes, ein sich Auflösendes.—Es ist nicht die Beschaffenheit des Stoffes oder Gegenstandes, worauf sie angewendet würde, oder in dem sie sich befänden, was einen Unterschied ausmachen kann; denn der Gegenstand hat nur durch und nach jenen Bestimmungen den Widerspruch an ihm.\n\nJene Kritik hat also die Formen des objektiven Denkens nur vom Ding entfernt, aber sie im Subjekt gelassen, wie sie vorgefunden. Sie hat dabei nämlich diese Formen nicht an und für sich selbst, nach ihrem eigenthümlichen Inhalt, betrachtet, sondern sie lemmatisch aus der subjektiven Logik geradezu aufgenommen; so daß von einer Ableitung ihrer an ihnen selbst, oder auch einer Ableitung derselben als subjektiv-logischer Formen, noch weniger aber von der dialektischen Betrachtung derselben die Rede war.\n\nDer konsequenter durchgeführte transcendentale Idealismus hat die Richtigkeit des von der kritischen Philosophie noch übrig gelassenen Gespensts des Dings-an-sich, dieses abstrakten von allem Inhalt abgeschiedenen Schattens erkannt, und den Zweck gehabt, ihn vollends zu zerstören. Auch machte diese Philosophie den Anfang, die Vernunft aus sich selbst ihre Bestimmungen darstellen zu lassen. Aber die subjektive Haltung dieses Versuchs ließ ihn nicht zur Vollendung kommen. Fernerhin ist diese Haltung und mit ihr auch jener Anfang und die Ausbildung der reinen Wissenschaft aufgegeben worden.\n\nGanz ohne Rücksicht auf metaphysische Bedeutung aber wird dasjenige betrachtet, was gemeinhin unter Logik verstanden wird. Diese Wissenschaft, in dem Zustande, worin sie sich noch befindet, hat freilich keinen Inhalt der Art, wie er als Realität und als eine wahrhafte Sache in dem gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn gilt, Aber sie ist nicht aus diesem Grunde eine formelle, inhaltsvoller Wahrheit entbehrende Wissenschaft. In jenem Stoffe, der in ihr vermißt, welchem Mangel das Unbefriedigende derselben zugeschrieben zu werden pflegt, ist ohnehin das Gebiet der Wahrheit nicht zu suchen. Sondern das Gehaltlose der logischen Formen liegt vielmehr allein in der Art, sie zu betrachten und zu behandeln. Indem sie als feste Bestimmungen aus einander fallen und nicht in organischer Einheit zusammengehalten werden, sind sie todte Formen, und haben den Geist in ihnen nicht wohnen, der ihre lebendige konkrete Einheit ist. Damit aber entbehren sie des gediegenen Inhalts,—einer Materie, welche Gehalt an sich selbst wäre. Der Inhalt, der an den logischen Formen vermißt wird, ist nichts anderes, als eine feste Grundlage und Konkretion dieser abstrakten Bestimmungen,; und ein solches substantielles Wesen pflegt für sie außen gesucht zu werden. Aber die logische Vernunft selbst ist das Substantielle oder Reelle, das alle abstrakten Bestimmungen in sich zusammenhält, und ihre gediegene, absolut-konkrete Einheit ist. Nach dem also, was eine Materie genannt zu werden pflegt, brauchte nicht weit gesucht zu werden; es ist nicht Schuld des Gegenstandes der Logik, wenn sie gehaltlos seyn soll, sondern allein der Art, wie derselbe gefaßt wird.\n\nDiese Reflexion führt näher auf die Angabe des Standpunkts, nach welchem die Logik zu betrachten ist, inwiefern er sich von der bisherigen Behandlungsweise dieser Wissenschaft unterscheidet, und der allein wahrhafte Standpunkt ist, auf den sie in Zukunft für immer zu stellen ist.\n\nIn der Phänomenologie des Geistes habe ich das Bewußtseyn in seiner Fortbewegung von dem ersten unmittelbaren Gegensatz seiner und des Gegenstandes bis zum absoluten Wissen dargestellt. Dieser Weg geht durch alle Formen des Verhältnisses des Bewußtseyns zum Objekte durch, und hat den Begriff der Wissenschaft zu seinem Resultate. Dieser Begriff bedarf also (abgesehen davon, daß er innerhalb der Logik selbst hervorgeht) hier keiner Rechtfertigung, weil er sie daselbst erhalten hat; und er ist keiner andern Rechtfertigung fähig, als nur dieser Hervorbringung desselben durch das Bewußtseyn, dem sich seine eignen Gestalten alle in denselben als in die Wahrheit auflösen. —Eine raisonnirende Begründung der Erläuterung des Begriffs der Wissenschaft kann zum höchsten dieß leisten, daß er vor die Vorstellung gebracht und eine historische Kenntniß davon bewirkt werde; aber eine Definition der Wissenschaft oder näher der Logik hat ihren Beweis allein in jener Nothwendigkeit ihres Hervorgangs. Eine Definition, mit der irgend eine Wissenschaft den absoluten Anfang macht, kann nichts anders enthalten, als den bestimmten, regelrechten Ausdruck von demjenigen, was man sich zugegebner- und bekanntermaßen unter dem Gegenstande und Zweck der Wissenschaft vorstellt. Daß man sich gerade dieß darunter vorstelle, ist eine historische Versicherung in Ansehung deren man sich allein auf dieses und jenes Anerkannte berufen, oder eigentlich nur bittweise beibringen kann, daß man dieß und jenes als anerkannt gelten lassen möge. Es hört gar nicht auf, daß der Eine daher, der Andere dorther einen Fall und Instanz beibringt, nach der auch noch etwas mehr und anderes bei diesem und jenem Ausdrucke zu verstehen, in dessen Definition also noch eine nähere oder allgemeinere Bestimmung aufzunehmen und darnach auch die Wissenschaft einzurichten sey.—Es kommt dabei ferner auf Raisonnement an, was alles und bis zu welcher Grenze und Umfang es hereingezogen oder ausgeschlossen werden müsse; dem Raisonnement selbst aber steht das mannigfaltigste und verschiedenartigste Dafürhalten offen, worüber am Ende allein die Willkür eine feste Bestimmung abschließen kann. Bei diesem Verfahren, die Wissenschaft mir ihrer Definition anzufangen, wird von dem Bedürfniß nicht die Rede, daß die Nothwendigkeit ihres Gegenstandes und damit ihrer selbst aufgezeigt würde.\n\nDer Begriff der reinen Wissenschaft und seiner Deduktion wird in gegenwärtiger Abhandlung also insofern vorausgesetzt, als die Phänomenologie des Geistes nichts anderes als die Deduktion desselben ist. Das absolute Wissen ist die Wahrheit aller Weisen des Bewußtseins, weil, wie jener Gang desselben es hervorbrachte, nur in dem absoluten Wissen, die Trennung des Gegenstandes von der Gewißheit seiner selbst vollkommen sich aufgelöst hat, und die Wahrheit, dieser Gewißheit, so wie diese Gewißheit, der Wahrheit gleich geworden ist.\n\nDie reine Wissenschaft setzt somit die Befreiung von dem Gegensatze des Bewußtseyns voraus. Sie enthält den Gedanken, insofern er eben so sehr die Sache an sich selbst ist, oder die Sache an sich selbst, insofern sie ebenso sehr der reine Gedanke ist. Als Wissenschaft ist die Wahrheit das reine sich entwicklende Selbstbewußtseyn, und hat die Gestalt des Selbst, daß das an und für sich seyende gewußter Begriff, der Begriff als solcher aber das an und für sich seyende ist. Dieses objektive Denken ist denn der Inhalt der reinen Wissenschaft. Sie ist daher so wenig formell, sie entbehrt so wenig der Materie zu einer wirklichen und wahren Erkenntniß, daß ihr Inhalt vielmehr allein das absolute Wahre, oder wenn man sich noch des Worts Materie bedienen wollte, die wahrhafte Materie ist,—eine Materie aber, der die Form nicht ein Äußerliches ist, da diese Materie vielmehr der reine Gedanke, somit die absolute Form selbst ist. Die Logik ist sonach als das System der reinen Vernunft, als das Reich des reinen Gedankens zu fassen. Dieses Reich ist die Wahrheit, wie sie ohne Hülle an und für sich selbst ist. Man kann sich deswegen ausdrücken, daß dieser Inhalt die Darstellung Gottes ist, wie er in seinem ewigen Wesen vor der Erschaffung der Natur und des endlichen Geistes ist.\n\nAnaxagoras wird als derjenige gepriesen, der zuerst den Gedanken ausgesprochen habe, daß der Nus, der Gedanke, das Princip der Welt, daß das Wesen der Welt als der Gedanke bestimmt ist. Er hat damit den Grund zu einer Intellektualansicht des Universums gelegt, deren reine Gestalt die Logik seyn muß. Es ist in ihr nicht um ein Denken über etwas, das für sich außer dem Denken zu Grunde läge, zu thun, um Formen, welche bloße Merkmale der Wahrheit abgeben sollten; sondern die nothwendigen Formen und eigenen Bestimmungen des Denkens sind der Inhalt und die höchste Wahrheit selbst.\n\nUm dieß in der Vorstellung wenigstens aufzunehmen, ist die Meinung auf die Seite zu legen, als ob die Wahrheit etwas Handgreifliches seyn müsse. Solche Handgreiflichkeit wird zum Beispiel selbst noch in die platonischen Ideen, die in dem Denken Gottes sind, hineingetragen, als ob sie gleichsam existirende Dinge, aber in einer andern Welt oder Region seyen, außerhalb welcher die Welt der Wirklichkeit sich befinde und eine von jenen Ideen verschiedene, erst durch diese Verschiedenheit reale Substantialität habe. Die platonische Idee ist nichts anderes, als das Allgemeine oder bestimmter der Begriff des Gegenstandes; nur in seinem Begriffe hat Etwas Wirklichkeit; insofern es von seinem Begriffe verschieden ist, hört es auf wirklich zu seyn, und ist ein Nichtiges; die Seite der Handgreiflichkeit und des sinnlichen Außersichseyns gehört dieser nichtigen Seite an.—Von der andern Seite aber kann man sich auf die eigenen Vorstellungen der gewöhnlichen Logik berufen; es wird nämlich angenommen, daß z.B. Definitionen nicht Bestimmungen enthalten, die nur ins erkennende Subjekt fallen, sondern die Bestimmungen des Gegenstandes, welche seine wesentlichste eigenste Natur ausmachen. Oder wenn von gegebenen Bestimmungen auf andere geschlossen wird, wird angenommen, daß das Erschlossene nicht ein dem Gegenstande Äußerliches und Fremdes sey, sondern daß es ihm vielmehr selbst zukomme, daß diesem Denken das Seyn entspreche.—Es liegt überhaupt bei dem Gebrauche der Formen des Begriffs, Urtheils, Schlusses, Definition, Division u.s.f. zu Grunde, daß sie nicht bloß Formen des selbstbewußten Denken sind, sondern auch des gegenständlichen Verstandes. Denken ist ein Ausdruck, der die in ihm enthaltene Bestimmung vorzugsweise dem Bewußtseyn beilegt. Aber insofern gesagt wird, daß Verstand, daß Vernunft in der gegenständlichen Welt ist, daß der Geist und die Natur allgemeine Gesetze habe, nach welchen ihr Leben und ihre Veränderung sich machen, so wird zugegeben, daß die Denkbestimmungen eben so sehr objektiven Werth und Existenz haben.\n\nDie kritische Philosophie machte zwar bereits die Metaphysik zur Logik, aber sie, wie der spätere Idealismus, gab, wie vorhin erinnert worden, aus Angst vor dem Objekt den logischen Bestimmungen eine wesentlich subjektive Bedeutung; dadurch bleiben sie zugleich mit dem Objekte, das sie flohen, behaftet, und ein Ding-an-sich, ein unendlicher Anstoß, blieb als ein Jenseits an ihnen übrig. Aber die Befreiung von dem Gegensatze des Bewußtseyns, welche die Wissenschaft muß voraussetzen können, erhebt die Denkbestimmungen über diesen ängstlichen, unvollendeten Standpunkt, und fordert die Betrachtung derselben, wie sie an und für sich, ohne eine solche Beschränkung und Rücksicht, das Logische, das Rein-vernünftige sind.\n\nKant preist sonst die Logik, nämlich das Aggregat von Bestimmungen und Sätzen, das im gewöhnlichen Sinne Logik heißt, darüber glücklich, daß ihr vor andern Wissenschaften eine so frühe Vollendung zu Theil geworden sey; seit Aristoteles habe sie keinen Rückschritt gethan, aber auch keinen Schritt vorwärts, das Letztere deswegen, weil sie allem Ansehen nach geschlossen und vollendet zu seyn scheine.—Wenn die Logik seit Aristoteles keine Veränderung erlitten hat,—wie denn in der That die Veränderungen, wenn man die neuern Kompendien der Logik betrachtet, häufig mehr nur in Weglassungen bestehen,—so ist daraus eher zu folgern, daß sie um so mehr einer totalen Umarbeitung bedürfe; denn ein zweitausendjähriges Fortarbeiten des Geistes muß ihm ein höheres Bewußtseyn über sein Denken und über seine reine Wesenheit in sich selbst, verschafft haben. Die Vergleichung der Gestalten, zu denen sich der Geist der praktischen und der religiösen Welt und der Geist der Wissenschaft in jeder Art reellen und ideellen Bewußtseyns emporgehoben hat, mit der Gestalt, in der sich die Logik, sein Bewußtseyn über sein reines Wesen, befindet, zeigt einen zu großen Unterschied, als daß es nicht der oberflächlichsten Betrachtung sogleich auffallen sollte, daß dieß letztere Bewußtseyn den erstern Erhebungen durchaus unangemessen und ihrer unwürdig ist.\n\nIn der That ist das Bedürfniß einer Umgestaltung der Logik längst gefühlt worden. In der Form und im Inhalt, wie sie sich in den Lehrbüchern zeigt, ist sie, man darf sagen, in Verachtung gekommen. Sie wird noch mitgeschleppt mehr im Gefühle, daß eine Logik überhaupt nicht zu entbehren sey, und aus einer noch fortdauernden Gewohnheit an die Tradition von ihrer Wichtigkeit, als aus Überzeugung, daß jener gewöhnliche Inhalt und die Beschäftigung mit jenen leeren Formen Werth und Nutzen habe.\n\nDie Erweiterungen, die ihr durch psychologisches, pädagogisches und selbst physiologisches Material eine Zeitlang gegeben wurden, sind nachher für Verunstaltungen ziemlich allgemein anerkannt worden. An und für sich muß ein großer Theil dieser psychologischen, pädagogischen, physiologischen Beobachtungen, Gesetze und Regeln, sie mochten in der Logik, oder wo es sey, stehen, als sehr schaal und trivial erscheinen. Vollends solche Regeln, als zum Beispiel, daß man dasjenige durchdenken und prüfen solle, was man in Büchern lese oder mündlich höre; daß man, wenn man nicht gut sehe, seinen Augen durch Brillen zu Hülfe zu kommen habe,—Regeln, die von den Lehrbüchern in der sogenannten angewandten Logik, und zwar ernsthaft in Paragraphen abgetheilt gegeben wurden, auf daß man zur Wahrheit gelange,—müssen jedermann als überflüßig vorkommen,—nur höchstens dem Schriftsteller oder Lehrer nicht, der in Verlegenheit ist, den sonst zu kurzen und todten Inhalt der Logik durch irgend etwas auszudehnen.\n\nWas solchen Inhalt betrifft, so ist schon oben der Grund angegeben worden, warum er so geistlos ist. Die Bestimmungen desselben gelten in ihrer Festigkeit unverrückt, und werden nur in äußerliche Beziehung miteinander gebracht. Dadurch daß bei den Urtheilen und Schlüssen die Operationen vornehmlich auf das Quantitative der Bestimmungen zurückgeführt und gegründet werden, beruht Alles auf einem äußerlichen Unterschiede, auf bloßer Vergleichung, wird ein völlig analytisches Verfahren und begriffloses Kalkuliren. Das Ableiten der sogenannten Regeln und Gesetze, des Schließens vornehmlich, ist nicht viel besser, als ein Befingern von Stäbchen von ungleicher Länge, um sie nach ihrer Größe zu sortiren und zu verbinden,—als die spielende Beschäftigung der Kinder, von mannigfaltig zerschnittenen Gemälden die passenden Stücke zusammen zu suchen.—Man hat daher nicht mit Unrecht dieses Denken dem Rechnen und das Rechnen wieder diesem Denken gleichgesetzt. In der Arithmetik werden die Zahlen als das Begrifflose genommen, das außer seiner Gleichheit oder Ungleichheit, das heißt, außer seinem ganz äußerlichen Verhältnisse keine Bedeutung hat, das weder an ihm selbst, noch dessen Beziehung ein Gedanke ist.\n\nWenn auf mechanische Weise ausgerechnet wird, daß dreiviertel mit zweidrittel multipliziert, ein Halbes ausmacht, so enthält diese Operation ungefähr so viel und so wenig Gedanken, als die Berechnung, ob in einer Figur diese oder jene Art des Schlusses Statt haben könne.\n\nDamit daß dieß todte Gebein der Logik durch den Geist zu Gehalt und Inhalt belebt werde, muß ihre Methode diejenige seyn, wodurch sie allein fähig ist, reine Wissenschaft zu seyn. In dem Zustande, in dem sie sich befindet, ist kaum eine Ahnung von wissenschaftlicher Methode zu erkennen. Sie hat ungefähr die Form einer Erfahrungswissenschaft. Erfahrungswissenschaften haben für das, was sie seyn sollen, ihre eigenthümliche Methode, des Definirens und des Klassificirens ihres Stoffes, so gut es geht, gefunden. Auch die reine Mathematik hat ihre Methode, die für ihre abstrakten Gegenstände und für die quantitative Bestimmung, in der sie allein betrachtet, passend ist. Ich habe über diese Methode und überhaupt das Untergeordnete der Wissenschaftlichkeit, die in der Mathematik Statt finden kann, in der Vorrede zur Phänomenologie des Geistes, das Wesentliche gesagt; aber sie wird auch innerhalb der Logik selbst näher betrachtet werden. Spinoza, Wolf und Andere haben sie verführen lassen, sie auch auf die Philosophie anzuwenden, und den äußerlichen Gang der begrifflosen Quantität zum Gange des Begriffes zu machen, was an und für sich widersprechend ist. Bisher hatte die Philosophie ihre Methode noch nicht gefunden; sie betrachtete mit Neid das systematische Gebäude der Mathematik und borgte sie, wie gesagt, von ihr, oder behalf sich mit der Methode von Wissenschaften, die nur Vermischungen von gegebenem Stoffe, Erfahrungssätzen und Gedanken sind,—oder half sich auch mit dem rohen Wegwerfen aller Methode. Die Exposition dessen aber, was allein die wahrhafte Methode der philosophischen Wissenschaft seyn kann, fällt in die Abhandlung der Logik selbst; denn die Methode ist das Bewußtseyn über die Form der inneren Selbstbewegung ihres Inhalts. Ich habe in der Phänomenologie des Geistes ein Beispiel von dieser Methode, an einem konkreteren Gegenstande, an dem Bewußtseyn ein Beispiel von dieser Methode, an einem konkreteren Gegenstande, an dem Bewußtseyn, aufgestellt. [3] Es sind hier Gestalten des Bewußtseyns, deren jede in ihrer Realisirung sich zugleich selbst auflöst, ihre eigene Negation zu ihrem Resultate hat,—und damit in eine höhere Gestalt übergegangen ist. Das Einzige, um den wissenschaftlichen Fortgang zu gewinnen, und um dessen ganz einfache Einsicht sich wesentlich zu bemühen ist,—ist die Erkenntniß des logischen Satzes, daß das Negative ebenso sehr positiv ist, oder daß das sich Widersprechende sich nicht in Null, in das abstrakte Nichts auflöst, sondern wesentlich nur in die Negation seines besonderen Inhalts, oder daß eine solche Negation nicht alle Negation, sondern die Negation der bestimmten Sache, die sich auflöst, somit bestimmte Negation ist; daß also im Resultate wesentlich das enthalten ist, woraus es resultirt;—was eigentlich eine Tautologie ist, denn sonst wäre es ein Unmittelbares, nicht ein Resultat. Indem das Resultirende, die Negation, bestimmte Negation ist, hat sie einen Inhalt. Sie ist ein neuer Begriff, aber der höhere, reichere Begriff als der vorhergehende; denn sie ist um dessen Negation oder Entgegengesetztes reicher geworden; enthält ihn also, aber auch mehr als ihn, und ist die Einheit seiner und seines Entgegengesetzten.—In diesem Wege hat sich das System der Begriffe überhaupt zu bilden,— und in unaufhaltsamen, reinem, von Außen nichts hereinnehmendem Gange, sich zu vollenden.\n\n[3] Später an den anderen konkreten Gegenständen und resp. Theilen der Philosophie.\n\nWie würde ich meinen können, daß nicht die Methode, die ich in diesem Systeme der Logik befolgt,—oder vielmehr die dieß System an ihm selbst befolgt,—noch vieler Vervollkommnung, vieler Durchbildung im Einzelnen fähig sey, aber ich weiß zugleich, daß sie die einzige wahrhafte ist. Dieß erhellt für sich schon daraus, daß sie von ihrem Gegenstande und Inhalte nichts Unterschiedenes ist;—denn es ist der Inhalt in sich, die Dialektik, die er an ihm selbst hat, welche ihn fortbewegt. Es ist klar, daß keine Darstellungen für wissenschaftlich gelten können, welche nicht den Gang dieser Methode gehen und ihrem einfachen Rhythmus gemäß sind, denn es ist der Gang der Sache selbst.\n\nIn Gemäßheit dieser Methode erinnere ich, daß die Eintheilungen und Überschriften der Bücher, Abschnitte und Kapitel, die in dem Werke angegeben sind, so wie etwa die damit verbundenen Erklärungen, zum Behuf einer vorläufigen Übersicht gemacht, und daß sie eigentlich nur von historischem Werthe sind. Sie gehören nicht zum Inhalte und Körper der Wissenschaft, sondern sind Zusammenstellungen der äußeren Reflexion, welche das Ganze der Ausführung schon durchlaufen hat, daher die Folge seiner Momente voraus weiß und angiebt, ehe sie noch durch die Sache selbst sich herbeiführen.\n\nIn den anderen Wissenschaften sind solche Vorausbestimmungen und Eintheilungen gleichfalls für sich nichts anderes, als solche äußere Angaben; aber auch innerhalb der Wissenschaft werden sie nicht über diesen Charakter erhoben. Selbst in der Logik zum Beispiel, heißt es etwa, \"die Logik hat zwei Hauptstücke, die Elementarlehre und die Methodik\", alsdann unter der Elementarlehre findet sich ohne weiteres etwa die Überschrift: Gesetze des Denkens;—alsdann erstes Kapitel: von den Begriffen. Erster Abschnitt: von der Klarheit der Begriffe u. s.f.—Diese ohne irgend eine Deduktion und Rechtfertigung gemachten Bestimmungen und Eintheilungen machen das systematische Gerüste und den ganze Zusammenhang solcher Wissenschaften aus. Eine solche Logik sieht es für ihren Beruf an, davon zu sprechen, daß die Begriffe und Wahrheiten aus Principien müssen abgeleitet seyn; aber bei dem, was sie Methode nennt, wird auch nicht von weitem an ein Ableiten gedacht. Die Ordnung besteht etwa in der Zusammenstellung von Gleichartigem, in der Vorausschickung des Einfacheren vor dem Zusammengesetzten und anderen äußerlichen Rücksichten. Aber in Rücksicht eines inneren, nothwendigen Zusammenhangs bleibt es bei dem Register der Abtheilungsbestimmungen, und der Übergang macht sich nur damit, daß es jetzt heißt: Zweites Kapitel;—oder: wir kommen nunmehr zu den Urtheilen, u. dergl.\n\nAuch die Überschriften und Eintheilungen, die in diesem Systeme vorkommen, sollen für sich keine andere Bedeutung haben, als die der Inhaltsanzeige. Außerdem aber muß die Nothwendigkeit des Zusammenhangs und die immanente Entstehung der Unterschiede sich in der Abhandlung der Sache selbst vorfinden, denn sie fällt in die eigene Fortbestimmung des Begriffes.\n\nDas, wodurch sich der Begriff selbst weiter leitet, ist das vorhin angegebene Negative, das er in sich selbst hat; dieß macht das wahrhaft Dialektische aus. Die Dialektik, die als ein abgesonderter Theil der Logik betrachtet und in Ansehung ihres Zwecks und Standpunktes, man kann sagen, gänzlich verkannt worden, erhält dadurch eine ganz andere Stellung.—Auch die platonische Dialektik hat selbst im Parmenides, und anderswo ohnehin noch direkter, Theils nur die Absicht, beschränkte Behauptungen durch sich selbst aufzulösen und zu widerlegen, Theils aber überhaupt das Nichts zum Resultate. Gewöhnlich sieht man die Dialektik für ein äußerliches und negatives Thun an, das nicht der Sache selbst angehöre, in bloßer Eitelkeit als einer subjektiven Sucht, sich das Feste und Wahre in Schwanken zu setzen und aufzulösen, seinen Grund habe oder wenigstens zu Nichts führe, als zur Eitelkeit des dialektisch behandelten Gegenstandes.\n\nKant hat die Dialektik höher gestellt, und diese Seite gehört unter die größten seiner Verdienste,—indem er ihr den Schein von Willkür nahm, den sie nach der gewöhnlichen Vorstellung hat, und sie als ein nothwendiges Thun der Vernunft darstellte. Indem sie nur für die Kunst, Blendwerke vorzumachen und Illusionen hervorzubringen, galt, wurde schlechthin vorausgesetzt, daß sie ein falsches Spiel spiele, und ihre ganze Kraft allein darauf beruhe, daß sie den Betrug verstecke; daß ihre Resultate nur erschlichen und ein subjektiver Schein seyen. Kant's dialektische Darstellungen in den Antinomien der reinen Vernunft verdienen zwar, wenn sie näher betrachtet werden, wie dieß im Verfolge dieses Werkes weitläufiger geschehen wird, freilich kein großes Lob; aber die allgemeine Idee, die er zu Grunde gelegt und geltend gemacht hat, ist die Objektivität des Scheins und Nothwendigkeit des Widerspruchs, der zur Natur der Denkbestimmungen gehört: zunächst zwar in der Art, insofern diese Bestimmungen von der Vernunft auf die Dinge an sich angewendet werden; aber eben, was sie in der Vernunft und in Rücksicht auf das sind, was an sich ist, ist ihre Natur. Es ist dieß Resultat in seiner positiven Seiten aufgefaßt, nichts anderes, als die innere Negativität derselben, als ihre sich selbstbewegende Seele, das Princip aller natürlichen und geistigen Lebendigkeit überhaupt. Aber so wie nur bei der abstrakt-negativen Seite des Dialektischen stehen geblieben wird, so ist das Resultat nur das Bekannte, daß die Vernunft unfähig sey, das Unendliche zu erkennen;—ein sonderbares Resultat, indem das Unendliche das Vernünftige ist, zu sagen, die Vernunft sey nicht fähig, das Vernünftige zu erkennen.\n\nIn diesem Dialektischen, wie es hier genommen wird, und damit in dem Fassen des Entgegengesetzten in seiner Einheit, oder des Positiven im Negativen besteht das Spekulative. Es ist die wichtigste, aber für die noch ungeübte, unfreie Denkkraft schwerste Seite. Ist solche noch darin begriffen, sich vom sinnlich-konkreten Vorstellen und vom Raisonniren loszureißen, so hat sie sich zuerst im abstrakten Denken zu üben. Begriffe in ihrer Bestimmtheit festzuhalten und aus ihnen erkennen zu lernen. Eine Darstellung der Logik zu diesem Behuf hätte sich in ihrer Methode an das obenbesagte Eintheilen und in Ansehung des näheren Inhalts an die Bestimmungen, die sich für die einzelnen Begriffe ergeben, zu halten, ohne sich auf das Dialektische einzulassen. Sie würde der äußeren Gestalt nach dem gewöhnlichen Vortrag dieser Wissenschaft ähnlich werden, sich übrigens dem Inhalte nach auch davon unterscheiden, und immer noch dazu dienen, das abstrakte, ob zwar nicht das spekulative Denken zu üben, welchen Zweck die durch psychologische und anthropologische Zuthaten populair gewordene Logik nicht einmal erfüllen kann. Sie würde dem Geiste das Bild eines methodisch geordneten Ganzen geben, obgleich die Seele des Gebäudes, die Methode, die im Dialektischen lebt, nicht selbst darin erschiene.\n\nIn Rücksicht auf die Bildung und das Verhältniß des Individuums zur Logik, merke ich schließlich noch an, daß diese Wissenschaft wie die Grammatik, in zwei verschiedenen Ansichten oder Werthen erscheint. Sie ist etwas Anderes für den, der zu ihr und den Wissenschaften überhaupt erst hinzutritt, und etwas Anderes für den, der von ihnen zu ihr zurückkommt. Wer die Grammatik anfängt kennen zu lernen, findet in ihren Formen und Gesetzen trockene Abstraktionen, zufällig Regeln, überhaupt eine isolirte Menge von Bestimmungen, die nur den Werth und die Bedeutung dessen zeigen, was in ihrem unmittelbaren Sinne liegt; das Erkennen erkennt in ihnen zunächst nichts als sie. Wer dagegen einer Sprache mächtig ist und zugleich andere Sprachen in Vergleichung mit ihr kennt, dem erst kann sich der Geist und die Bildung eines Volks in der Grammatik seiner Sprache zu fühlen geben; dieselben Regeln und Formen haben nunmehr einen erfüllten, lebendigen Werth. Er kann durch die Grammatik hindurch den Ausdruck des Geistes überhaupt, die Logik, erkennen. So wer zur Wissenschaft hinzutritt, findet in der Logik zunächst ein isolirtes System von Abstraktionen, das auf sich selbst beschränkt, nicht über die anderen Kenntnisse und Wissenschaften übergreift. Vielmehr, gehalten gegen den Reichthum der Weltvorstellungen, gegen den real erscheinenden Inhalt der anderen Wissenschaften, und verglichen mit dem Versprechen der absoluten Wissenschaft, das Wesen dieses Reichthums, die innere Natur des Geistes und der Welt, die Wahrheit zu enthüllen, hat diese Wissenschaft in ihrer abstrakten Gestalt, in der farblosen, kalten Einfachheit ihrer reinen Bestimmungen vielmehr das Ansehen, Alles eher zu leisten als dieß Versprechen, und gehaltlos jenem Reichthum gegenüber zu stehen, Die erste Bekanntschaft mit der Logik schränkt ihre Bedeutung auf sie selbst ein; ihr Inhalt gilt nur für eine isolirte Beschäftigung mit den Denkbestimmungen, neben der die anderen wissenschaftlichen Beschäftigungen ein eigener Stoff und Gehalt für sich sind, auf welche das Logische etwa einen formellen Einfluß hat, und zwar einen solchen, der sich mehr von selbst macht, und für den die wissenschaftliche Gestalt und deren Studium allerdings auch zur Noth entbehrt werden kann. Die anderen Wissenschaften haben die regelrechte Methode, eine Folge von Definitionen, Axiomen, Theoremen und deren Beweisen u.s.f. zu seyn, im Ganzen abgeworfen; die sogenannte natürliche Logik macht sich für sich in ihnen geltend und hilft sich ohne besondere, auf das Denken selbst gerichtete Erkenntnis fort. Vollends aber hält sich der Stoff und Inhalt dieser Wissenschaften für sich selbst vom Logischen völlig unabhängig, und ist auch für Sinn, Gefühl, Vorstellung und praktisches Interesse jeder Art ansprechender.\n\nSo muß denn allerdings die Logik zuerst gelernt werden, als etwas, das man wohl versteht und einsieht, aber woran Umfang, Tiefe und weitere Bedeutung anfangs vermißt wird. Erst aus der tiefern Kenntniß der anderen Wissenschaften erhebt sich für den subjektiven Geist das Logische als ein nicht nur abstrakt Allgemeines, sondern als das den Reichthum des Besonderen in sich fassende Allgemeine; —wie derselbe Sittenspruch in dem Munde des Jünglings, der ihn ganz richtig versteht, nicht die Bedeutung und den Umfang besitzt, welchen er im Geiste eines lebenserfahrenen Mannes hat, dem sich damit die ganze Kraft des darin enthaltenen Gehaltes ausdrückt, so erhält das Logische erst dadurch die Schätzung seines Werths, wenn es zum Resultate der Erfahrung der Wissenschaften geworden ist; es stellt sich daraus als die allgemeine Wahrheit, nicht als eine besondere Kenntniß neben anderem Stoffe und Realitäten, sondern als das Wesen alles dieses sonstigen Inhalts dem Geiste dar.\n\nOb nun das Logische zwar im Anfange des Studiums nicht in dieser bewußten Kraft für den Geist vorhanden ist, so empfängt er durch dasselbe darum nicht weniger die Kraft in sich, die ihn in alle Wahrheit leitet. Das System der Logik ist das Reich der Schatten, die Welt der einfachen Wesenheiten, von aller sinnlichen Konkretion befreit. Das Studium dieser Wissenschaft, der Aufenthalt und die Arbeit in diesem Schattenreich ist die absolute Bildung und Zucht des Bewußtseyns. Es treibt darin ein von sinnlichen Anschauungen und Zwecken, von Gefühlen, von der bloß gemeinten Vorstellungswelt fernes Geschäft. Von seiner negativen Seite betrachtet, besteht dieß Geschäft in dem Fernhalten der Zufälligkeit des raisonnirenden Denkens und der Willkür, diese oder die entgegengesetzten Gründe sich einfallen oder gelten zu lassen.\n\nVornehmlich aber gewinnt der Gedanke dadurch Selbstständigkeit und Unabhängigkeit. Er wird in dem Abstrakten und in dem Fortgehen durch Begriffe ohne sinnliche Substrate einheimisch, wird zur unbewußten Macht, die sonstige Mannigfaltigkeit der Kenntniß und Wissenschaften in die vernünftige Form aufzunehmen, sie in ihrem Wesentlichen zu erfassen und festzuhalten, das Äußerliche abzustreifen und auf diese Weise aus ihnen das Logische auszuziehen,—oder was dasselbe ist, die vorher durch das Studium erworbene abstrakte Grundlage des Logischen mit dem Gehalte aller Wahrheit zu erfüllen, und ihm den Werth eines Allgemeinen zu geben, das nicht mehr als ein Besonderes neben anderem Besonderen steht, sondern über alles dieses übergreift und dessen Wesen, das Absolut-wahre, ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0001","text":"## Einleitung","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"3.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0002","text":"## Allgemeiner Begriff der Logik","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"3.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0003","text":"Es fühlt sich bei keiner Wissenschaft stärker das Bedürfniß, ohne vorangehende Reflexionen, von der Sache selbst anzufangen, als bei der logischen Wissenschaft. In jeder andern ist der Gegenstand, den sie behandelt, und die wissenschaftliche Methode von einander unterschieden; so wie auch der Inhalt nicht einen absoluten Anfang macht, sondern von andern Begriffen abhängt, und um sich herum mit anderem Stoffe zusammenhängt. Diesen Wissenschaften wird es daher zugegeben, von ihrem Boden und dessen Zusammenhang, so wie von der Methode nur lemmatischer Weise zu sprechen, die als bekannt und angenommen vorausgesetzten Formen von Definitionen und dergleichen ohne weiteres anzuwenden, und sich der gewöhnlichen Art des Raisonnements zur Festsetzung ihrer allgemeinen Begriffe und Grundbestimmungen zu bedienen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"3.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","text":"Die Logik dagegen kann keine dieser Formen der Reflexion oder Regeln und Gesetze des Denkens voraussetzen, denn sie machen einen Theil ihres Inhalts selbst aus und haben erst innerhalb ihrer begründet zu werden. Nicht nur aber die Angabe der wissenschaftlichen Methode, sondern auch der Begriff selbst der Wissenschaft überhaupt gehört zu ihrem Inhalte, und zwar macht er ihr letztes Resultat aus; was sie ist, kann sie daher nicht voraussagen, sondern ihre ganze Abhandlung bringt dieß Wissen von ihr selbst erst als ihr Letztes und als ihre Vollendung hervor. Gleichfalls ihr Gegenstand, das Denken oder bestimmter das begreifende Denken, wird wesentlich innerhalb ihrer abgehandelt; der Begriff desselben erzeugt sich in ihrem Verlaufe, und kann somit nicht vorausgeschickt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"3.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","text":"Was daher in dieser Einleitung vorausgeschickt wird, hat nicht den Zweck, den Begriff der Logik etwa zu begründen, oder den Inhalt und die Methode derselben zum voraus wissenschaftlich zu rechtfertigen, sondern, durch einige Erläuterungen und Reflexionen, in raisonnirendem und historischem Sinne, den Gesichtspunkt, aus welchem diese Wissenschaft zu betrachten ist, der Vorstellung näher zu bringen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"3.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","text":"Wenn die Logik als die Wissenschaft des Denkens im Allgemeinen angenommen wird, so wird dabei verstanden, daß dieß Denken die bloße Form einer Erkenntniß ausmache, daß die Logik von allem Inhalte abstrahire, und das sogenannte zweite Bestandstück, das zu einer Erkenntniß gehöre, die Materie, anderswoher gegeben werden müsse, daß somit die Logik als von welcher diese Materie ganz und gar unabhängig sey, nur die formalen Bedingungen wahrhafter Erkenntniß angeben, nicht aber reale Wahrheit selbst enthalten, noch auch nur der Weg zu realer Wahrheit seyn könne, weil gerade das Wesentliche der Wahrheit, der Inhalt, außer ihr liege.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"3.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","text":"Vors Erste aber ist es schon ungeschickt zu sagen, daß die Logik von allem Inhalte abstrahire, daß sie nur die Regeln des Denkens lehre, ohne auf das Gedachte sich einzulassen und auf dessen Beschaffenheit Rücksicht nehmen zu können. Denn da das Denken und die Regeln des Denkens ihr Gegenstand seyn sollen, so hat sie ja unmittelbar daran ihren eigenthümlichen Inhalt; sie hat daran auch jenes zweite Bestandstück der Erkenntniß, eine Materie, um deren Beschaffenheit sie sich bekümmert.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"3.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0008","text":"Allein zweitens sind überhaupt die Vorstellungen, auf denen der Begriff der Logik bisher beruhte, Theils bereits untergegangen, Theils ist es Zeit, daß sie vollends verschwinden, daß der Standpunkt dieser Wissenschaft höher gefaßt werde, und daß sie eine völlig veränderte Gestalt gewinne.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"3.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","text":"Der bisherige Begriff der Logik beruht auf der im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn ein für allemal vorausgesetzten Trennung des Inhalts der Erkenntniß und der Form derselben, oder der Wahrheit und der Gewißheit. Es wird erstens vorausgesetzt, daß der Stoff des Erkennens, als eine fertige Welt außerhalb des Denkens, an und für sich vorhanden, daß das Denken für sich leer sey, als eine Form äußerlich zu jener Materie hinzutrete, sich damit erfülle, erst daran einen Inhalt gewinne und dadurch ein reales Erkennen werde.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"3.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010","text":"Alsdann stehen diese beiden Bestandtheile,—(denn sie sollen das Verhältniß von Bestandtheilen haben, und das Erkennen wird aus ihnen mechanischer oder höchstens chemischer Weise zusammengesetzt—) in dieser Rangordnung gegen einander, daß das Objekt ein für sich Vollendetes, Fertiges sey, das des Denkens zu seiner Wirklichkeit vollkommen entbehren könne, da hingegen das Denken etwas Mangelhaftes sey, das sich erst an einem Stoffe zu vervollständigen, und zwar als eine weiche unbestimmte Form sich seiner Materie angemessen zu machen habe. Wahrheit ist die Übereinstimmung des Denkens mit dem Gegenstande, und es soll, um diese Übereinstimmung hervorzubringen, —denn sie ist nicht an und für sich vorhanden,—das Denken nach dem Gegenstande sich fügen und bequemen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"3.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","text":"Drittens, indem die Verschiedenheit der Materie und der Form, des Gegenstandes und des Denkens nicht in jener neblichten Unbestimmtheit gelassen, sondern bestimmter genommen wird, so ist jede eine von der andern geschiedene Sphäre. Das Denken kommt daher in seinem Empfangen und Formiren des Stoffs nicht über sich hinaus, sein Empfangen und sich nach ihm Bequemen bleibt eine Modifikation seiner selbst, es wird dadurch nicht zu seinem Andern; und das selbstbewußte Bestimmen gehört ohnedieß nur ihm an; es kommt also auch in seiner Beziehung auf den Gegenstand nicht aus sich heraus zu dem Gegenstande, dieser bleibt als ein Ding an sich, schlechthin ein Jenseits des Denkens.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"3.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","text":"Diese Ansichten über das Verhältnis des Subjektes und Objekts zu einander drücken die Bestimmungen aus, welche die Natur unsers gewöhnlichen, des erscheinenden Bewußtseins ausmachen; aber diese Vorurtheile, in die Vernunft übergetragen, als ob in ihr dasselbe Verhältniß Gott finde, als ob dieses Verhältniß an und für sich Wahrheit habe, so sind sie die Irrthümer, deren durch alle Theile des geistigen und natürlichen Universums durchgeführte Widerlegung die Philosophie ist, oder die vielmehr, weil sie den Eingang in die Philosophie versperren, vor derselben abzulegen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"3.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013","text":"Die ältere Metaphysik hatte in dieser Rücksicht einen höhern Begriff von dem Denken als in der neuern Zeit gäng und gäb geworden ist. Jene legte nämlich zu Grunde, daß das, was durchs Denken von und an den Dingen erkannt werde, das allein an ihnen wahrhaft Wahre sey; somit nicht sie in ihrer Unmittelbarkeit, sondern sie erst in die Form des Denkens erhoben, als Gedachte. Diese Metaphysik hielt somit dafür, daß das Denken und die Bestimmungen des Denkens nicht ein den Gegenständen Fremdes, sondern vielmehr deren Wesen sey, oder daß die Dinge und das Denken derselben, (—wie auch unsere Sprache eine Verwandtschaft derselben ausdrückt,—) an und für sich übereinstimmen, daß das Denken in seinen immanenten Bestimmungen, und die wahrhafte Natur der Dinge, ein und derselbe Inhalt sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"3.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0014","text":"Aber der reflektirende Verstand bemächtigte sich der Philosophie. Es ist genau zu wissen, was dieser Ausdruck sagen will, der sonst vielfach als Schlagwort gebraucht wird; es ist überhaupt darunter der abstrahirende und damit trennende Verstand zu verstehen, der in seinen Trennungen beharrt. Gegen die Vernunft gekehrt beträgt er sich als gemeiner Menschenverstand und macht seine Ansicht geltend, daß die Wahrheit auf sinnlicher Realität beruhe, daß die Gedanken nur Gedanken seyen, in dem Sinne, daß erst die sinnliche Wahrnehmung ihnen Gehalt und Realität gebe, daß die Vernunft, insofern sie an und für sich bleibe, nur Hinrgespinnste erzeuge.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"3.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015","text":"In diesem Verzichtthun der Vernunft auf sich selbst, geht der Begriff der Wahrheit verloren, sie ist darauf eingeschränkt, nur subjektive Wahrheit, nur die Erscheinung zu erkennen, nur etwas, dem die Natur der Sache selbst nicht entspreche; das Wissen ist zur Meinung zurückgefallen.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"3.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","text":"Diese Wendung jedoch, welche das Erkennen nimmt, und die als Verlust und Rückschritt erscheint, hat das Tiefere zum Grunde, worauf überhaupt die Erhebung der Vernunft in den höhern Geist der neuern Philosophie beruht. Der Grund jener allgemein gewordenen Vorstellung ist nämlich in der Einsicht von dem nothwendigen Widerstreite der Bestimmungen des Verstandes mit sich selbst, zu suchen.—Die schon namhaft gemacht Reflexion ist dieß, über das konkrete Unmittelbare hinaus zu gehen, und dasselbe zu bestimmen und zu trennen. Aber sie muß ebenso sehr über diese ihre trennenden Bestimmungen hinausgehen, und sie zunächst beziehen. Auf dem Standpunkte dieses Beziehens tritt der Widerstreit derselben hervor.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"3.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","text":"Dieses Beziehen der Reflexion gehört an sich der Vernunft an; die Erhebung über jene Bestimmungen, die zur Einsicht des Widerstreits derselben gelangt, ist der große negative Schritt zum wahrhaften Begriffe der Vernunft. Aber die nicht durchgeführte Einsicht fällt in den Mißverstand, als ob die Vernunft es sey, welche in Widerspruch mit sich gerathe; sie erkennt nicht, daß der Widerspruch eben das Erheben der Vernunft über die Beschränkungen des Verstandes und das Auflösen derselben ist. Statt von hier aus den letzten Schritt in die Höhe zu thun, ist die Erkenntniß von dem Unbefriedigenden der Verstandesbestimmungen zu der sinnlichen Existenz zurückgeflohen, an derselben das Feste und Einige zu haben vermeinend.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"3.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0018","text":"Indem aber auf der andern Seite diese Erkenntniß sich als die Erkenntniß von Erscheinendem weiß, wird das Unbefriedigende derselben eingestanden, aber zugleich vorausgesetzt, als ob zwar nicht die Dinge an sich, aber doch innerhalb der Sphäre der Erscheinung richtig erkannt würde; als ob dabei gleichsam nur die Art der Gegenstände verschieden wäre, und die eine Art, nämlich die Dinge an sich zwar nicht, aber doch die andere Art, nämlich die Erscheinungen, in die Erkenntniß fielen. Wie wenn einem Manne richtige Einsicht beigemessen würde, mit dem Zusatz, daß er jedoch nichts Wahres, sondern nur Unwahres einzusehen fähig sey. So ungereimt das Letztere wäre, so ungereimt ist eine wahre Erkenntniß, die den Gegenstand nicht erkennte, wie er an sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"3.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019","text":"Die Kritik der Formen des Verstandes hat das angeführte Resultat gehabt, daß diese Formen keine Anwendung auf die Dinge an sich haben. —Dieß kann keinen andern Sinn haben, als daß diese Formen an ihnen selbst etwas Unwahres sind. Allein indem sie für die subjektive Vernunft und für die Erfahrung als geltend gelassen werden, so hat die Kritik keine Änderung an ihnen selbst bewirkt, sondern läßt sie für das Subjekt in derselben Gestalt, wie sie sonst für das Objekt galten. Wenn sie aber ungenügend für das Ding an sich sind, so müßte der Verstand, dem sie angehören sollen, noch weniger dieselben sich gefallen lassen und damit vorlieb nehmen wollen. Wenn sie nicht Bestimmungen des Dings an sich seyn können, so können sie noch weniger Bestimmungen des Verstandes seyn, dem wenigstens die Würde eines Dings an sich zugestanden werden sollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"3.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020","text":"Die Bestimmungen des Endlichen und Unendlichen sind in demselben Widerstreit, es sey, daß sie auf Zeit und Raum, auf die Welt angewendet werden, oder daß sie Bestimmungen innerhalb des Geistes seyen; so gut als schwarz und weiß ein Grau geben, ob sie an einer Wand, oder aber noch auf der Pallete mit einander vereinigt werden; wenn unsere Weltvorstellung sich auflöst, indem die Bestimmungen des Unendlichen und Endlichen auf sie übergetragen werden, so ist noch mehr der Geist selbst, welcher sie beide in sich enthält, ein in sich selbst Widersprechendes, ein sich Auflösendes.—Es ist nicht die Beschaffenheit des Stoffes oder Gegenstandes, worauf sie angewendet würde, oder in dem sie sich befänden, was einen Unterschied ausmachen kann; denn der Gegenstand hat nur durch und nach jenen Bestimmungen den Widerspruch an ihm.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"3.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0021","text":"Jene Kritik hat also die Formen des objektiven Denkens nur vom Ding entfernt, aber sie im Subjekt gelassen, wie sie vorgefunden. Sie hat dabei nämlich diese Formen nicht an und für sich selbst, nach ihrem eigenthümlichen Inhalt, betrachtet, sondern sie lemmatisch aus der subjektiven Logik geradezu aufgenommen; so daß von einer Ableitung ihrer an ihnen selbst, oder auch einer Ableitung derselben als subjektiv-logischer Formen, noch weniger aber von der dialektischen Betrachtung derselben die Rede war.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"3.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0022","text":"Der konsequenter durchgeführte transcendentale Idealismus hat die Richtigkeit des von der kritischen Philosophie noch übrig gelassenen Gespensts des Dings-an-sich, dieses abstrakten von allem Inhalt abgeschiedenen Schattens erkannt, und den Zweck gehabt, ihn vollends zu zerstören. Auch machte diese Philosophie den Anfang, die Vernunft aus sich selbst ihre Bestimmungen darstellen zu lassen. Aber die subjektive Haltung dieses Versuchs ließ ihn nicht zur Vollendung kommen. Fernerhin ist diese Haltung und mit ihr auch jener Anfang und die Ausbildung der reinen Wissenschaft aufgegeben worden.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"3.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0023","text":"Ganz ohne Rücksicht auf metaphysische Bedeutung aber wird dasjenige betrachtet, was gemeinhin unter Logik verstanden wird. Diese Wissenschaft, in dem Zustande, worin sie sich noch befindet, hat freilich keinen Inhalt der Art, wie er als Realität und als eine wahrhafte Sache in dem gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn gilt, Aber sie ist nicht aus diesem Grunde eine formelle, inhaltsvoller Wahrheit entbehrende Wissenschaft. In jenem Stoffe, der in ihr vermißt, welchem Mangel das Unbefriedigende derselben zugeschrieben zu werden pflegt, ist ohnehin das Gebiet der Wahrheit nicht zu suchen. Sondern das Gehaltlose der logischen Formen liegt vielmehr allein in der Art, sie zu betrachten und zu behandeln.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"3.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","text":"Indem sie als feste Bestimmungen aus einander fallen und nicht in organischer Einheit zusammengehalten werden, sind sie todte Formen, und haben den Geist in ihnen nicht wohnen, der ihre lebendige konkrete Einheit ist. Damit aber entbehren sie des gediegenen Inhalts,—einer Materie, welche Gehalt an sich selbst wäre. Der Inhalt, der an den logischen Formen vermißt wird, ist nichts anderes, als eine feste Grundlage und Konkretion dieser abstrakten Bestimmungen,; und ein solches substantielles Wesen pflegt für sie außen gesucht zu werden. Aber die logische Vernunft selbst ist das Substantielle oder Reelle, das alle abstrakten Bestimmungen in sich zusammenhält, und ihre gediegene, absolut-konkrete Einheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"3.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0025","text":"Nach dem also, was eine Materie genannt zu werden pflegt, brauchte nicht weit gesucht zu werden; es ist nicht Schuld des Gegenstandes der Logik, wenn sie gehaltlos seyn soll, sondern allein der Art, wie derselbe gefaßt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"3.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0026","text":"Diese Reflexion führt näher auf die Angabe des Standpunkts, nach welchem die Logik zu betrachten ist, inwiefern er sich von der bisherigen Behandlungsweise dieser Wissenschaft unterscheidet, und der allein wahrhafte Standpunkt ist, auf den sie in Zukunft für immer zu stellen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"3.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0027","text":"In der Phänomenologie des Geistes habe ich das Bewußtseyn in seiner Fortbewegung von dem ersten unmittelbaren Gegensatz seiner und des Gegenstandes bis zum absoluten Wissen dargestellt. Dieser Weg geht durch alle Formen des Verhältnisses des Bewußtseyns zum Objekte durch, und hat den Begriff der Wissenschaft zu seinem Resultate. Dieser Begriff bedarf also (abgesehen davon, daß er innerhalb der Logik selbst hervorgeht) hier keiner Rechtfertigung, weil er sie daselbst erhalten hat; und er ist keiner andern Rechtfertigung fähig, als nur dieser Hervorbringung desselben durch das Bewußtseyn, dem sich seine eignen Gestalten alle in denselben als in die Wahrheit auflösen.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"3.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","text":"—Eine raisonnirende Begründung der Erläuterung des Begriffs der Wissenschaft kann zum höchsten dieß leisten, daß er vor die Vorstellung gebracht und eine historische Kenntniß davon bewirkt werde; aber eine Definition der Wissenschaft oder näher der Logik hat ihren Beweis allein in jener Nothwendigkeit ihres Hervorgangs. Eine Definition, mit der irgend eine Wissenschaft den absoluten Anfang macht, kann nichts anders enthalten, als den bestimmten, regelrechten Ausdruck von demjenigen, was man sich zugegebner- und bekanntermaßen unter dem Gegenstande und Zweck der Wissenschaft vorstellt. Daß man sich gerade dieß darunter vorstelle, ist eine historische Versicherung in Ansehung deren man sich allein auf dieses und jenes Anerkannte berufen, oder eigentlich nur bittweise beibringen kann, daß man dieß und jenes als anerkannt gelten lassen möge.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"3.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029","text":"Es hört gar nicht auf, daß der Eine daher, der Andere dorther einen Fall und Instanz beibringt, nach der auch noch etwas mehr und anderes bei diesem und jenem Ausdrucke zu verstehen, in dessen Definition also noch eine nähere oder allgemeinere Bestimmung aufzunehmen und darnach auch die Wissenschaft einzurichten sey.—Es kommt dabei ferner auf Raisonnement an, was alles und bis zu welcher Grenze und Umfang es hereingezogen oder ausgeschlossen werden müsse; dem Raisonnement selbst aber steht das mannigfaltigste und verschiedenartigste Dafürhalten offen, worüber am Ende allein die Willkür eine feste Bestimmung abschließen kann. Bei diesem Verfahren, die Wissenschaft mir ihrer Definition anzufangen, wird von dem Bedürfniß nicht die Rede, daß die Nothwendigkeit ihres Gegenstandes und damit ihrer selbst aufgezeigt würde.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"3.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","text":"Der Begriff der reinen Wissenschaft und seiner Deduktion wird in gegenwärtiger Abhandlung also insofern vorausgesetzt, als die Phänomenologie des Geistes nichts anderes als die Deduktion desselben ist. Das absolute Wissen ist die Wahrheit aller Weisen des Bewußtseins, weil, wie jener Gang desselben es hervorbrachte, nur in dem absoluten Wissen, die Trennung des Gegenstandes von der Gewißheit seiner selbst vollkommen sich aufgelöst hat, und die Wahrheit, dieser Gewißheit, so wie diese Gewißheit, der Wahrheit gleich geworden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"3.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","text":"Die reine Wissenschaft setzt somit die Befreiung von dem Gegensatze des Bewußtseyns voraus. Sie enthält den Gedanken, insofern er eben so sehr die Sache an sich selbst ist, oder die Sache an sich selbst, insofern sie ebenso sehr der reine Gedanke ist. Als Wissenschaft ist die Wahrheit das reine sich entwicklende Selbstbewußtseyn, und hat die Gestalt des Selbst, daß das an und für sich seyende gewußter Begriff, der Begriff als solcher aber das an und für sich seyende ist. Dieses objektive Denken ist denn der Inhalt der reinen Wissenschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"3.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","text":"Sie ist daher so wenig formell, sie entbehrt so wenig der Materie zu einer wirklichen und wahren Erkenntniß, daß ihr Inhalt vielmehr allein das absolute Wahre, oder wenn man sich noch des Worts Materie bedienen wollte, die wahrhafte Materie ist,—eine Materie aber, der die Form nicht ein Äußerliches ist, da diese Materie vielmehr der reine Gedanke, somit die absolute Form selbst ist. Die Logik ist sonach als das System der reinen Vernunft, als das Reich des reinen Gedankens zu fassen. Dieses Reich ist die Wahrheit, wie sie ohne Hülle an und für sich selbst ist. Man kann sich deswegen ausdrücken, daß dieser Inhalt die Darstellung Gottes ist, wie er in seinem ewigen Wesen vor der Erschaffung der Natur und des endlichen Geistes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"3.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033","text":"Anaxagoras wird als derjenige gepriesen, der zuerst den Gedanken ausgesprochen habe, daß der Nus, der Gedanke, das Princip der Welt, daß das Wesen der Welt als der Gedanke bestimmt ist. Er hat damit den Grund zu einer Intellektualansicht des Universums gelegt, deren reine Gestalt die Logik seyn muß. Es ist in ihr nicht um ein Denken über etwas, das für sich außer dem Denken zu Grunde läge, zu thun, um Formen, welche bloße Merkmale der Wahrheit abgeben sollten; sondern die nothwendigen Formen und eigenen Bestimmungen des Denkens sind der Inhalt und die höchste Wahrheit selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"3.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0034","text":"Um dieß in der Vorstellung wenigstens aufzunehmen, ist die Meinung auf die Seite zu legen, als ob die Wahrheit etwas Handgreifliches seyn müsse. Solche Handgreiflichkeit wird zum Beispiel selbst noch in die platonischen Ideen, die in dem Denken Gottes sind, hineingetragen, als ob sie gleichsam existirende Dinge, aber in einer andern Welt oder Region seyen, außerhalb welcher die Welt der Wirklichkeit sich befinde und eine von jenen Ideen verschiedene, erst durch diese Verschiedenheit reale Substantialität habe.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"3.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0035","text":"Die platonische Idee ist nichts anderes, als das Allgemeine oder bestimmter der Begriff des Gegenstandes; nur in seinem Begriffe hat Etwas Wirklichkeit; insofern es von seinem Begriffe verschieden ist, hört es auf wirklich zu seyn, und ist ein Nichtiges; die Seite der Handgreiflichkeit und des sinnlichen Außersichseyns gehört dieser nichtigen Seite an.—Von der andern Seite aber kann man sich auf die eigenen Vorstellungen der gewöhnlichen Logik berufen; es wird nämlich angenommen, daß z.B. Definitionen nicht Bestimmungen enthalten, die nur ins erkennende Subjekt fallen, sondern die Bestimmungen des Gegenstandes, welche seine wesentlichste eigenste Natur ausmachen.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"3.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0036","text":"Oder wenn von gegebenen Bestimmungen auf andere geschlossen wird, wird angenommen, daß das Erschlossene nicht ein dem Gegenstande Äußerliches und Fremdes sey, sondern daß es ihm vielmehr selbst zukomme, daß diesem Denken das Seyn entspreche.—Es liegt überhaupt bei dem Gebrauche der Formen des Begriffs, Urtheils, Schlusses, Definition, Division u.s.f. zu Grunde, daß sie nicht bloß Formen des selbstbewußten Denken sind, sondern auch des gegenständlichen Verstandes. Denken ist ein Ausdruck, der die in ihm enthaltene Bestimmung vorzugsweise dem Bewußtseyn beilegt. Aber insofern gesagt wird, daß Verstand, daß Vernunft in der gegenständlichen Welt ist, daß der Geist und die Natur allgemeine Gesetze habe, nach welchen ihr Leben und ihre Veränderung sich machen, so wird zugegeben, daß die Denkbestimmungen eben so sehr objektiven Werth und Existenz haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"3.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0037","text":"Die kritische Philosophie machte zwar bereits die Metaphysik zur Logik, aber sie, wie der spätere Idealismus, gab, wie vorhin erinnert worden, aus Angst vor dem Objekt den logischen Bestimmungen eine wesentlich subjektive Bedeutung; dadurch bleiben sie zugleich mit dem Objekte, das sie flohen, behaftet, und ein Ding-an-sich, ein unendlicher Anstoß, blieb als ein Jenseits an ihnen übrig. Aber die Befreiung von dem Gegensatze des Bewußtseyns, welche die Wissenschaft muß voraussetzen können, erhebt die Denkbestimmungen über diesen ängstlichen, unvollendeten Standpunkt, und fordert die Betrachtung derselben, wie sie an und für sich, ohne eine solche Beschränkung und Rücksicht, das Logische, das Rein-vernünftige sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"3.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0038","text":"Kant preist sonst die Logik, nämlich das Aggregat von Bestimmungen und Sätzen, das im gewöhnlichen Sinne Logik heißt, darüber glücklich, daß ihr vor andern Wissenschaften eine so frühe Vollendung zu Theil geworden sey; seit Aristoteles habe sie keinen Rückschritt gethan, aber auch keinen Schritt vorwärts, das Letztere deswegen, weil sie allem Ansehen nach geschlossen und vollendet zu seyn scheine.—Wenn die Logik seit Aristoteles keine Veränderung erlitten hat,—wie denn in der That die Veränderungen, wenn man die neuern Kompendien der Logik betrachtet, häufig mehr nur in Weglassungen bestehen,—so ist daraus eher zu folgern, daß sie um so mehr einer totalen Umarbeitung bedürfe; denn ein zweitausendjähriges Fortarbeiten des Geistes muß ihm ein höheres Bewußtseyn über sein Denken und über seine reine Wesenheit in sich selbst, verschafft haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"3.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0039","text":"Die Vergleichung der Gestalten, zu denen sich der Geist der praktischen und der religiösen Welt und der Geist der Wissenschaft in jeder Art reellen und ideellen Bewußtseyns emporgehoben hat, mit der Gestalt, in der sich die Logik, sein Bewußtseyn über sein reines Wesen, befindet, zeigt einen zu großen Unterschied, als daß es nicht der oberflächlichsten Betrachtung sogleich auffallen sollte, daß dieß letztere Bewußtseyn den erstern Erhebungen durchaus unangemessen und ihrer unwürdig ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"3.39"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0040","text":"In der That ist das Bedürfniß einer Umgestaltung der Logik längst gefühlt worden. In der Form und im Inhalt, wie sie sich in den Lehrbüchern zeigt, ist sie, man darf sagen, in Verachtung gekommen. Sie wird noch mitgeschleppt mehr im Gefühle, daß eine Logik überhaupt nicht zu entbehren sey, und aus einer noch fortdauernden Gewohnheit an die Tradition von ihrer Wichtigkeit, als aus Überzeugung, daß jener gewöhnliche Inhalt und die Beschäftigung mit jenen leeren Formen Werth und Nutzen habe.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"3.40"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0041","text":"Die Erweiterungen, die ihr durch psychologisches, pädagogisches und selbst physiologisches Material eine Zeitlang gegeben wurden, sind nachher für Verunstaltungen ziemlich allgemein anerkannt worden. An und für sich muß ein großer Theil dieser psychologischen, pädagogischen, physiologischen Beobachtungen, Gesetze und Regeln, sie mochten in der Logik, oder wo es sey, stehen, als sehr schaal und trivial erscheinen.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"3.41"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0042","text":"Vollends solche Regeln, als zum Beispiel, daß man dasjenige durchdenken und prüfen solle, was man in Büchern lese oder mündlich höre; daß man, wenn man nicht gut sehe, seinen Augen durch Brillen zu Hülfe zu kommen habe,—Regeln, die von den Lehrbüchern in der sogenannten angewandten Logik, und zwar ernsthaft in Paragraphen abgetheilt gegeben wurden, auf daß man zur Wahrheit gelange,—müssen jedermann als überflüßig vorkommen,—nur höchstens dem Schriftsteller oder Lehrer nicht, der in Verlegenheit ist, den sonst zu kurzen und todten Inhalt der Logik durch irgend etwas auszudehnen.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"3.42"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0043","text":"Was solchen Inhalt betrifft, so ist schon oben der Grund angegeben worden, warum er so geistlos ist. Die Bestimmungen desselben gelten in ihrer Festigkeit unverrückt, und werden nur in äußerliche Beziehung miteinander gebracht. Dadurch daß bei den Urtheilen und Schlüssen die Operationen vornehmlich auf das Quantitative der Bestimmungen zurückgeführt und gegründet werden, beruht Alles auf einem äußerlichen Unterschiede, auf bloßer Vergleichung, wird ein völlig analytisches Verfahren und begriffloses Kalkuliren.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"3.43"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0044","text":"Das Ableiten der sogenannten Regeln und Gesetze, des Schließens vornehmlich, ist nicht viel besser, als ein Befingern von Stäbchen von ungleicher Länge, um sie nach ihrer Größe zu sortiren und zu verbinden,—als die spielende Beschäftigung der Kinder, von mannigfaltig zerschnittenen Gemälden die passenden Stücke zusammen zu suchen.—Man hat daher nicht mit Unrecht dieses Denken dem Rechnen und das Rechnen wieder diesem Denken gleichgesetzt. In der Arithmetik werden die Zahlen als das Begrifflose genommen, das außer seiner Gleichheit oder Ungleichheit, das heißt, außer seinem ganz äußerlichen Verhältnisse keine Bedeutung hat, das weder an ihm selbst, noch dessen Beziehung ein Gedanke ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"3.44"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0045","text":"Wenn auf mechanische Weise ausgerechnet wird, daß dreiviertel mit zweidrittel multipliziert, ein Halbes ausmacht, so enthält diese Operation ungefähr so viel und so wenig Gedanken, als die Berechnung, ob in einer Figur diese oder jene Art des Schlusses Statt haben könne.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"3.45"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0046","text":"Damit daß dieß todte Gebein der Logik durch den Geist zu Gehalt und Inhalt belebt werde, muß ihre Methode diejenige seyn, wodurch sie allein fähig ist, reine Wissenschaft zu seyn. In dem Zustande, in dem sie sich befindet, ist kaum eine Ahnung von wissenschaftlicher Methode zu erkennen. Sie hat ungefähr die Form einer Erfahrungswissenschaft. Erfahrungswissenschaften haben für das, was sie seyn sollen, ihre eigenthümliche Methode, des Definirens und des Klassificirens ihres Stoffes, so gut es geht, gefunden. Auch die reine Mathematik hat ihre Methode, die für ihre abstrakten Gegenstände und für die quantitative Bestimmung, in der sie allein betrachtet, passend ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"3.46"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","text":"Ich habe über diese Methode und überhaupt das Untergeordnete der Wissenschaftlichkeit, die in der Mathematik Statt finden kann, in der Vorrede zur Phänomenologie des Geistes, das Wesentliche gesagt; aber sie wird auch innerhalb der Logik selbst näher betrachtet werden. Spinoza, Wolf und Andere haben sie verführen lassen, sie auch auf die Philosophie anzuwenden, und den äußerlichen Gang der begrifflosen Quantität zum Gange des Begriffes zu machen, was an und für sich widersprechend ist. Bisher hatte die Philosophie ihre Methode noch nicht gefunden; sie betrachtete mit Neid das systematische Gebäude der Mathematik und borgte sie, wie gesagt, von ihr, oder behalf sich mit der Methode von Wissenschaften, die nur Vermischungen von gegebenem Stoffe, Erfahrungssätzen und Gedanken sind,—oder half sich auch mit dem rohen Wegwerfen aller Methode.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"3.47"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","text":"Die Exposition dessen aber, was allein die wahrhafte Methode der philosophischen Wissenschaft seyn kann, fällt in die Abhandlung der Logik selbst; denn die Methode ist das Bewußtseyn über die Form der inneren Selbstbewegung ihres Inhalts. Ich habe in der Phänomenologie des Geistes ein Beispiel von dieser Methode, an einem konkreteren Gegenstande, an dem Bewußtseyn ein Beispiel von dieser Methode, an einem konkreteren Gegenstande, an dem Bewußtseyn, aufgestellt. [3] Es sind hier Gestalten des Bewußtseyns, deren jede in ihrer Realisirung sich zugleich selbst auflöst, ihre eigene Negation zu ihrem Resultate hat,—und damit in eine höhere Gestalt übergegangen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"3.48"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","text":"Das Einzige, um den wissenschaftlichen Fortgang zu gewinnen, und um dessen ganz einfache Einsicht sich wesentlich zu bemühen ist,—ist die Erkenntniß des logischen Satzes, daß das Negative ebenso sehr positiv ist, oder daß das sich Widersprechende sich nicht in Null, in das abstrakte Nichts auflöst, sondern wesentlich nur in die Negation seines besonderen Inhalts, oder daß eine solche Negation nicht alle Negation, sondern die Negation der bestimmten Sache, die sich auflöst, somit bestimmte Negation ist; daß also im Resultate wesentlich das enthalten ist, woraus es resultirt;—was eigentlich eine Tautologie ist, denn sonst wäre es ein Unmittelbares, nicht ein Resultat. Indem das Resultirende, die Negation, bestimmte Negation ist, hat sie einen Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"3.49"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","text":"Sie ist ein neuer Begriff, aber der höhere, reichere Begriff als der vorhergehende; denn sie ist um dessen Negation oder Entgegengesetztes reicher geworden; enthält ihn also, aber auch mehr als ihn, und ist die Einheit seiner und seines Entgegengesetzten.—In diesem Wege hat sich das System der Begriffe überhaupt zu bilden,— und in unaufhaltsamen, reinem, von Außen nichts hereinnehmendem Gange, sich zu vollenden.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"3.50"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0051","text":"[3] Später an den anderen konkreten Gegenständen und resp. Theilen der Philosophie.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"3.51"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","text":"Wie würde ich meinen können, daß nicht die Methode, die ich in diesem Systeme der Logik befolgt,—oder vielmehr die dieß System an ihm selbst befolgt,—noch vieler Vervollkommnung, vieler Durchbildung im Einzelnen fähig sey, aber ich weiß zugleich, daß sie die einzige wahrhafte ist. Dieß erhellt für sich schon daraus, daß sie von ihrem Gegenstande und Inhalte nichts Unterschiedenes ist;—denn es ist der Inhalt in sich, die Dialektik, die er an ihm selbst hat, welche ihn fortbewegt. Es ist klar, daß keine Darstellungen für wissenschaftlich gelten können, welche nicht den Gang dieser Methode gehen und ihrem einfachen Rhythmus gemäß sind, denn es ist der Gang der Sache selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"3.52"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","text":"In Gemäßheit dieser Methode erinnere ich, daß die Eintheilungen und Überschriften der Bücher, Abschnitte und Kapitel, die in dem Werke angegeben sind, so wie etwa die damit verbundenen Erklärungen, zum Behuf einer vorläufigen Übersicht gemacht, und daß sie eigentlich nur von historischem Werthe sind. Sie gehören nicht zum Inhalte und Körper der Wissenschaft, sondern sind Zusammenstellungen der äußeren Reflexion, welche das Ganze der Ausführung schon durchlaufen hat, daher die Folge seiner Momente voraus weiß und angiebt, ehe sie noch durch die Sache selbst sich herbeiführen.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"3.53"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0054","text":"In den anderen Wissenschaften sind solche Vorausbestimmungen und Eintheilungen gleichfalls für sich nichts anderes, als solche äußere Angaben; aber auch innerhalb der Wissenschaft werden sie nicht über diesen Charakter erhoben. Selbst in der Logik zum Beispiel, heißt es etwa, \"die Logik hat zwei Hauptstücke, die Elementarlehre und die Methodik\", alsdann unter der Elementarlehre findet sich ohne weiteres etwa die Überschrift: Gesetze des Denkens;—alsdann erstes Kapitel: von den Begriffen. Erster Abschnitt: von der Klarheit der Begriffe u. s.f.—Diese ohne irgend eine Deduktion und Rechtfertigung gemachten Bestimmungen und Eintheilungen machen das systematische Gerüste und den ganze Zusammenhang solcher Wissenschaften aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"3.54"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0055","text":"Eine solche Logik sieht es für ihren Beruf an, davon zu sprechen, daß die Begriffe und Wahrheiten aus Principien müssen abgeleitet seyn; aber bei dem, was sie Methode nennt, wird auch nicht von weitem an ein Ableiten gedacht. Die Ordnung besteht etwa in der Zusammenstellung von Gleichartigem, in der Vorausschickung des Einfacheren vor dem Zusammengesetzten und anderen äußerlichen Rücksichten. Aber in Rücksicht eines inneren, nothwendigen Zusammenhangs bleibt es bei dem Register der Abtheilungsbestimmungen, und der Übergang macht sich nur damit, daß es jetzt heißt: Zweites Kapitel;—oder: wir kommen nunmehr zu den Urtheilen, u. dergl.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"3.55"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","text":"Auch die Überschriften und Eintheilungen, die in diesem Systeme vorkommen, sollen für sich keine andere Bedeutung haben, als die der Inhaltsanzeige. Außerdem aber muß die Nothwendigkeit des Zusammenhangs und die immanente Entstehung der Unterschiede sich in der Abhandlung der Sache selbst vorfinden, denn sie fällt in die eigene Fortbestimmung des Begriffes.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"3.56"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0057","text":"Das, wodurch sich der Begriff selbst weiter leitet, ist das vorhin angegebene Negative, das er in sich selbst hat; dieß macht das wahrhaft Dialektische aus. Die Dialektik, die als ein abgesonderter Theil der Logik betrachtet und in Ansehung ihres Zwecks und Standpunktes, man kann sagen, gänzlich verkannt worden, erhält dadurch eine ganz andere Stellung.—Auch die platonische Dialektik hat selbst im Parmenides, und anderswo ohnehin noch direkter, Theils nur die Absicht, beschränkte Behauptungen durch sich selbst aufzulösen und zu widerlegen, Theils aber überhaupt das Nichts zum Resultate.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"3.57"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0058","text":"Gewöhnlich sieht man die Dialektik für ein äußerliches und negatives Thun an, das nicht der Sache selbst angehöre, in bloßer Eitelkeit als einer subjektiven Sucht, sich das Feste und Wahre in Schwanken zu setzen und aufzulösen, seinen Grund habe oder wenigstens zu Nichts führe, als zur Eitelkeit des dialektisch behandelten Gegenstandes.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"3.58"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0059","text":"Kant hat die Dialektik höher gestellt, und diese Seite gehört unter die größten seiner Verdienste,—indem er ihr den Schein von Willkür nahm, den sie nach der gewöhnlichen Vorstellung hat, und sie als ein nothwendiges Thun der Vernunft darstellte. Indem sie nur für die Kunst, Blendwerke vorzumachen und Illusionen hervorzubringen, galt, wurde schlechthin vorausgesetzt, daß sie ein falsches Spiel spiele, und ihre ganze Kraft allein darauf beruhe, daß sie den Betrug verstecke; daß ihre Resultate nur erschlichen und ein subjektiver Schein seyen.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"3.59"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0060","text":"Kant's dialektische Darstellungen in den Antinomien der reinen Vernunft verdienen zwar, wenn sie näher betrachtet werden, wie dieß im Verfolge dieses Werkes weitläufiger geschehen wird, freilich kein großes Lob; aber die allgemeine Idee, die er zu Grunde gelegt und geltend gemacht hat, ist die Objektivität des Scheins und Nothwendigkeit des Widerspruchs, der zur Natur der Denkbestimmungen gehört: zunächst zwar in der Art, insofern diese Bestimmungen von der Vernunft auf die Dinge an sich angewendet werden; aber eben, was sie in der Vernunft und in Rücksicht auf das sind, was an sich ist, ist ihre Natur. Es ist dieß Resultat in seiner positiven Seiten aufgefaßt, nichts anderes, als die innere Negativität derselben, als ihre sich selbstbewegende Seele, das Princip aller natürlichen und geistigen Lebendigkeit überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"3.60"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0061","text":"Aber so wie nur bei der abstrakt-negativen Seite des Dialektischen stehen geblieben wird, so ist das Resultat nur das Bekannte, daß die Vernunft unfähig sey, das Unendliche zu erkennen;—ein sonderbares Resultat, indem das Unendliche das Vernünftige ist, zu sagen, die Vernunft sey nicht fähig, das Vernünftige zu erkennen.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"3.61"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","text":"In diesem Dialektischen, wie es hier genommen wird, und damit in dem Fassen des Entgegengesetzten in seiner Einheit, oder des Positiven im Negativen besteht das Spekulative. Es ist die wichtigste, aber für die noch ungeübte, unfreie Denkkraft schwerste Seite. Ist solche noch darin begriffen, sich vom sinnlich-konkreten Vorstellen und vom Raisonniren loszureißen, so hat sie sich zuerst im abstrakten Denken zu üben. Begriffe in ihrer Bestimmtheit festzuhalten und aus ihnen erkennen zu lernen. Eine Darstellung der Logik zu diesem Behuf hätte sich in ihrer Methode an das obenbesagte Eintheilen und in Ansehung des näheren Inhalts an die Bestimmungen, die sich für die einzelnen Begriffe ergeben, zu halten, ohne sich auf das Dialektische einzulassen.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"3.62"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0063","text":"Sie würde der äußeren Gestalt nach dem gewöhnlichen Vortrag dieser Wissenschaft ähnlich werden, sich übrigens dem Inhalte nach auch davon unterscheiden, und immer noch dazu dienen, das abstrakte, ob zwar nicht das spekulative Denken zu üben, welchen Zweck die durch psychologische und anthropologische Zuthaten populair gewordene Logik nicht einmal erfüllen kann. Sie würde dem Geiste das Bild eines methodisch geordneten Ganzen geben, obgleich die Seele des Gebäudes, die Methode, die im Dialektischen lebt, nicht selbst darin erschiene.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"3.63"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0064","text":"In Rücksicht auf die Bildung und das Verhältniß des Individuums zur Logik, merke ich schließlich noch an, daß diese Wissenschaft wie die Grammatik, in zwei verschiedenen Ansichten oder Werthen erscheint. Sie ist etwas Anderes für den, der zu ihr und den Wissenschaften überhaupt erst hinzutritt, und etwas Anderes für den, der von ihnen zu ihr zurückkommt. Wer die Grammatik anfängt kennen zu lernen, findet in ihren Formen und Gesetzen trockene Abstraktionen, zufällig Regeln, überhaupt eine isolirte Menge von Bestimmungen, die nur den Werth und die Bedeutung dessen zeigen, was in ihrem unmittelbaren Sinne liegt; das Erkennen erkennt in ihnen zunächst nichts als sie.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"3.64"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","text":"Wer dagegen einer Sprache mächtig ist und zugleich andere Sprachen in Vergleichung mit ihr kennt, dem erst kann sich der Geist und die Bildung eines Volks in der Grammatik seiner Sprache zu fühlen geben; dieselben Regeln und Formen haben nunmehr einen erfüllten, lebendigen Werth. Er kann durch die Grammatik hindurch den Ausdruck des Geistes überhaupt, die Logik, erkennen. So wer zur Wissenschaft hinzutritt, findet in der Logik zunächst ein isolirtes System von Abstraktionen, das auf sich selbst beschränkt, nicht über die anderen Kenntnisse und Wissenschaften übergreift.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"3.65"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0066","text":"Vielmehr, gehalten gegen den Reichthum der Weltvorstellungen, gegen den real erscheinenden Inhalt der anderen Wissenschaften, und verglichen mit dem Versprechen der absoluten Wissenschaft, das Wesen dieses Reichthums, die innere Natur des Geistes und der Welt, die Wahrheit zu enthüllen, hat diese Wissenschaft in ihrer abstrakten Gestalt, in der farblosen, kalten Einfachheit ihrer reinen Bestimmungen vielmehr das Ansehen, Alles eher zu leisten als dieß Versprechen, und gehaltlos jenem Reichthum gegenüber zu stehen, Die erste Bekanntschaft mit der Logik schränkt ihre Bedeutung auf sie selbst ein; ihr Inhalt gilt nur für eine isolirte Beschäftigung mit den Denkbestimmungen, neben der die anderen wissenschaftlichen Beschäftigungen ein eigener Stoff und Gehalt für sich sind, auf welche das Logische etwa einen formellen Einfluß hat, und zwar einen solchen, der sich mehr von selbst macht, und","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"3.66"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0067","text":"für den die wissenschaftliche Gestalt und deren Studium allerdings auch zur Noth entbehrt werden kann. Die anderen Wissenschaften haben die regelrechte Methode, eine Folge von Definitionen, Axiomen, Theoremen und deren Beweisen u.s.f. zu seyn, im Ganzen abgeworfen; die sogenannte natürliche Logik macht sich für sich in ihnen geltend und hilft sich ohne besondere, auf das Denken selbst gerichtete Erkenntnis fort. Vollends aber hält sich der Stoff und Inhalt dieser Wissenschaften für sich selbst vom Logischen völlig unabhängig, und ist auch für Sinn, Gefühl, Vorstellung und praktisches Interesse jeder Art ansprechender.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"3.67"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","text":"So muß denn allerdings die Logik zuerst gelernt werden, als etwas, das man wohl versteht und einsieht, aber woran Umfang, Tiefe und weitere Bedeutung anfangs vermißt wird. Erst aus der tiefern Kenntniß der anderen Wissenschaften erhebt sich für den subjektiven Geist das Logische als ein nicht nur abstrakt Allgemeines, sondern als das den Reichthum des Besonderen in sich fassende Allgemeine; —wie derselbe Sittenspruch in dem Munde des Jünglings, der ihn ganz richtig versteht, nicht die Bedeutung und den Umfang besitzt, welchen er im Geiste eines lebenserfahrenen Mannes hat, dem sich damit die ganze Kraft des darin enthaltenen Gehaltes ausdrückt, so erhält das Logische erst dadurch die Schätzung seines Werths, wenn es zum Resultate der Erfahrung der Wissenschaften geworden ist; es stellt sich daraus als die allgemeine Wahrheit, nicht als eine besondere Kenntniß neben anderem Stoffe und","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"3.68"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0069","text":"Realitäten, sondern als das Wesen alles dieses sonstigen Inhalts dem Geiste dar.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"3.69"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0070","text":"Ob nun das Logische zwar im Anfange des Studiums nicht in dieser bewußten Kraft für den Geist vorhanden ist, so empfängt er durch dasselbe darum nicht weniger die Kraft in sich, die ihn in alle Wahrheit leitet. Das System der Logik ist das Reich der Schatten, die Welt der einfachen Wesenheiten, von aller sinnlichen Konkretion befreit. Das Studium dieser Wissenschaft, der Aufenthalt und die Arbeit in diesem Schattenreich ist die absolute Bildung und Zucht des Bewußtseyns. Es treibt darin ein von sinnlichen Anschauungen und Zwecken, von Gefühlen, von der bloß gemeinten Vorstellungswelt fernes Geschäft. Von seiner negativen Seite betrachtet, besteht dieß Geschäft in dem Fernhalten der Zufälligkeit des raisonnirenden Denkens und der Willkür, diese oder die entgegengesetzten Gründe sich einfallen oder gelten zu lassen.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"3.70"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","text":"Vornehmlich aber gewinnt der Gedanke dadurch Selbstständigkeit und Unabhängigkeit. Er wird in dem Abstrakten und in dem Fortgehen durch Begriffe ohne sinnliche Substrate einheimisch, wird zur unbewußten Macht, die sonstige Mannigfaltigkeit der Kenntniß und Wissenschaften in die vernünftige Form aufzunehmen, sie in ihrem Wesentlichen zu erfassen und festzuhalten, das Äußerliche abzustreifen und auf diese Weise aus ihnen das Logische auszuziehen,—oder was dasselbe ist, die vorher durch das Studium erworbene abstrakte Grundlage des Logischen mit dem Gehalte aller Wahrheit zu erfüllen, und ihm den Werth eines Allgemeinen zu geben, das nicht mehr als ein Besonderes neben anderem Besonderen steht, sondern über alles dieses übergreift und dessen Wesen, das Absolut-wahre, ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"3.71"}],"sha256":"579dd1a3f3c3fc727cd9dc7ea73a5d528389814b20519e464801d07a3a70a590","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101527233763Z_54204ef8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"General Concept of Logic","source_sha256":"579dd1a3f3c3fc727cd9dc7ea73a5d528389814b20519e464801d07a3a70a590","sha256":"837e853b1c32efa1f70fb97e334ef44fc786060d16b27c96ba953f41e9eaaf06","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:15:27.233776+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0001","text":"## Introduction","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"3.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0002","text":"## General Concept of Logic","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"3.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0003","text":"In no science is the need felt more strongly to begin with the matter itself, without preceding reflections, than in the logical science. In every other science, the object which it treats and the scientific method are distinguished from one another; likewise, its content does not make an absolute beginning, but depends upon other concepts and is connected all around with other material. These sciences are therefore permitted to speak only lemmatically of their ground and its connection, as well as of the method; to apply without further ado the forms of definitions and the like which are presupposed as known and accepted; and to avail themselves of the ordinary manner of reasoning for the establishment of their universal concepts and fundamental determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"3.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","text":"Logic, on the other hand, cannot presuppose any of these forms of reflection, or rules and laws of thinking, for they themselves constitute a part of its content and must first be grounded within it. Yet not only the exposition of the scientific method, but also the concept of science in general itself belongs to its content, and indeed constitutes its final result; what it is, it therefore cannot announce in advance, but its entire exposition first produces this knowledge of itself as its final point and as its completion. Likewise, its object, thinking, or more specifically conceptual thinking, is essentially treated within it; the concept of this object produces itself in its course, and thus cannot be sent ahead.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"3.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","text":"What is therefore set forth in advance in this Introduction does not have the purpose of grounding, as it were, the concept of logic, or of scientifically justifying in advance its content and method, but rather, by means of some elucidations and reflections, in a reasoning and historical sense, of bringing closer to representation the standpoint from which this science is to be regarded.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"3.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","text":"If logic is assumed to be the science of thinking in general, it is thereby understood that this thinking constitutes the mere form of a cognition; that logic abstracts from all content; and that the so-called second constituent belonging to a cognition, matter, must be given from elsewhere; that logic, therefore, upon which this matter is wholly and entirely independent, can indicate only the formal conditions of true cognition, but can contain neither real truth itself nor even be the path to real truth, because precisely the essential element of truth, the content, lies outside it.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"3.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","text":"First of all, however, it is already inept to say that logic abstracts from all content, that it teaches only the rules of thinking, without entering into what is thought and being able to take account of its constitution. For since thinking and the rules of thinking are supposed to be its object, it has in them its peculiar content directly; in them it also has that second constituent of cognition, a matter whose constitution concerns it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"3.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0008","text":"But secondly, the representations upon which the concept of logic has hitherto rested have in part already perished; and it is time that they should disappear altogether, that the standpoint of this science should be conceived more highly, and that it should assume an entirely altered shape.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"3.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","text":"The concept of logic hitherto prevailing rests upon the separation, once and for all presupposed in ordinary consciousness, of the content of cognition from its form, or of truth from certainty. First, it is presupposed that the material of knowing, as a finished world outside thinking, is present in and for itself; that thinking is empty for itself, enters as a form external to that matter, fills itself with it, first thereby gains a content, and through this becomes real cognition.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"3.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010","text":"Then these two constituents,—(for they are supposed to have the relation of constituents, and cognition is composed out of them in a mechanical or at most chemical manner—)—stand in this rank-order toward one another: the object is something complete and finished in itself, which can entirely dispense with thinking for its actuality, whereas thinking is something deficient, which must first complete itself upon a material and, as a soft indeterminate form, make itself appropriate to its matter. Truth is the correspondence of thinking with the object, and, in order to bring about this correspondence,—for it is not present in and for itself,—thinking is supposed to conform and accommodate itself to the object.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"3.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","text":"Thirdly, when the difference of matter and form, of object and thinking, is not left in that nebulous indeterminacy but is taken more determinately, each is a sphere separated from the other. In its receiving and forming of the material, thinking therefore does not go beyond itself; its receiving it and accommodating itself to it remains a modification of itself; it does not thereby become its other; and self-conscious determining belongs, in any case, only to it. Thus even in its relation to the object it does not go out of itself to the object; the latter remains, as a thing in itself, absolutely a beyond of thinking.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"3.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","text":"These views of the relation of subject and object to one another express the determinations that constitute the nature of our ordinary, appearing consciousness; but when these prejudices are carried over into reason, as though the same relation obtained in it, as though this relation had truth in and for itself, then they are the errors whose refutation, carried through all parts of the spiritual and natural universe, is philosophy—or which, rather, because they bar the entrance into philosophy, must be cast off before it.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"3.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013","text":"In this respect, the older metaphysics had a higher concept of thinking than has become current and customary in more recent times. For it laid down as its basis that what is cognized through thinking of and in things is the only truly true element in them; thus, not things in their immediacy, but only things elevated into the form of thinking, as thought. This metaphysics thus held that thinking and the determinations of thinking are not something alien to objects, but rather their essence; or that things and the thinking of them,—(as our language too expresses an affinity between them,)—correspond in and for themselves, that thinking in its immanent determinations and the true nature of things are one and the same content.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"3.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0014","text":"But the reflecting understanding took possession of philosophy. One must know exactly what this expression is intended to say, which otherwise is often used as a catchword; in general, it is to be understood as the abstracting and thereby separating understanding, which persists in its separations. Turned against reason, it conducts itself as common human understanding and asserts its view that truth rests upon sensuous reality; that thoughts are merely thoughts, in the sense that only sensuous perception gives them content and reality; that reason, insofar as it remains in and for itself, produces only figments of the brain.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"3.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015","text":"In this renunciation by reason of itself, the concept of truth is lost; it is restricted to cognizing only subjective truth, only appearance, only something to which the nature of the matter itself does not correspond; knowledge has fallen back into opinion.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"3.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","text":"Yet this turn that cognition takes, and which appears as loss and regression, has as its ground the deeper basis upon which in general the elevation of reason into the higher spirit of modern philosophy rests. The ground of that representation which has become universal is, namely, to be sought in the insight into the necessary conflict of the determinations of the understanding with themselves.—The reflection already mentioned is this: to go beyond the concrete immediate, and to determine and separate it. But it must just as much go beyond these its separating determinations, and initially relate them. At the standpoint of this relating, their conflict emerges.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"3.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","text":"This relating of reflection belongs in itself to reason; the elevation above those determinations that arrives at insight into their conflict is the great negative step toward the true concept of reason. But the insight not carried through falls into the misunderstanding that it is reason which falls into contradiction with itself; it does not recognize that contradiction is precisely the elevation of reason above the limitations of the understanding and the dissolution of these limitations. Instead of taking the final step upward from here, cognition of the unsatisfactory character of the determinations of the understanding has fled back to sensuous existence, supposing that it possesses therein what is firm and unitary.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"3.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0018","text":"But since, on the other hand, this cognition knows itself as cognition of what appears, its unsatisfactory character is admitted; but at the same time it is presupposed that, while things in themselves are indeed not correctly cognized, yet correct cognition takes place within the sphere of appearance; as though, so to speak, only the kind of objects were different, and one kind, namely things in themselves, did not fall within cognition, but the other kind, namely appearances, did. This is as if a man were credited with correct insight, with the addition that he is nevertheless capable of perceiving nothing true, but only what is untrue. As absurd as the latter would be, so absurd is a true cognition that did not cognize the object as it is in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"3.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019","text":"The critique of the forms of the understanding has had the cited result that these forms have no application to things in themselves. —This can have no other meaning than that these forms are in themselves something untrue. But since they are allowed to stand as valid for subjective reason and for experience, the critique has effected no alteration in them themselves, but leaves them for the subject in the same shape in which they formerly held for the object. But if they are inadequate for the thing in itself, then the understanding, to which they are supposed to belong, ought even less to allow them to please it and to be content with them. If they cannot be determinations of the thing in itself, then they can still less be determinations of the understanding, to which at least the dignity of a thing in itself ought to be accorded.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"3.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020","text":"The determinations of finite and infinite are in the same conflict, whether they are applied to time and space, to the world, or whether they are determinations within spirit; just as black and white yield a gray, whether they are united on a wall or still on the palette; if our representation of the world dissolves when the determinations of infinite and finite are transferred to it, then spirit itself, which contains both within itself, is still more something contradictory within itself, something dissolving itself.—It is not the constitution of the material or object to which they are applied, or in which they are found, that can make a difference; for the object has contradiction in it only through and in accordance with those determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"3.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0021","text":"That critique has thus only removed the forms of objective thinking from the thing, but has left them in the subject as it found them. For it did not consider these forms in and for themselves, according to their peculiar content, but took them over lemmatically and directly from subjective logic; so that there was no question of a derivation of them in themselves, or even of a derivation of them as subjectively logical forms, still less of a dialectical consideration of them.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"3.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0022","text":"The transcendental idealism carried out more consistently recognized the incorrectness of the specter of the thing-in-itself still left over by critical philosophy, this abstract shadow separated from all content, and had the aim of destroying it completely. This philosophy also made a beginning in allowing reason to present its determinations from itself. But the subjective posture of this attempt did not allow it to attain completion. Subsequently, this posture, and with it also that beginning and the elaboration of pure science, has been abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"3.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0023","text":"But what is commonly understood by logic is considered wholly without regard to metaphysical significance. This science, in the state in which it still finds itself, certainly has no content of the kind that counts in ordinary consciousness as reality and as a true thing. But it is not for this reason a formal science devoid of substantial truth. Moreover, the domain of truth is not to be sought in that material which is missed in it, and to the lack of which its unsatisfactory character is usually attributed. Rather, the lack of content of the logical forms lies solely in the manner of considering and treating them.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"3.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","text":"Inasmuch as they fall apart from one another as fixed determinations and are not held together in organic unity, they are dead forms, and do not have dwelling in them the spirit which is their living concrete unity. But thereby they lack solid content,—a matter which would be content in itself. The content which is missed in the logical forms is nothing other than a fixed foundation and concretion of these abstract determinations; and such a substantial essence is customarily sought for them outside. But logical reason itself is the substantial or the real, which holds all abstract determinations together within itself, and is their solid, absolutely concrete unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"3.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0025","text":"Thus, what is customarily called a matter need not be sought far afield; it is not the fault of the object of logic if it is supposed to be without content, but solely of the manner in which it is apprehended.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"3.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0026","text":"This reflection leads more closely to an indication of the standpoint from which logic is to be considered, insofar as it differs from the previous manner of treating this science, and is the sole true standpoint upon which it is henceforth to be placed for all time.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"3.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0027","text":"In the Phenomenology of Spirit I have presented consciousness in its progression from the first immediate opposition between itself and the object up to absolute knowing. This path traverses all forms of the relation of consciousness to the object, and has the Concept of science as its result. This Concept therefore requires here no justification (apart from the fact that it itself arises within logic), since it has received it there; and it is capable of no justification other than this production of it through consciousness, for which all its own shapes dissolve into that Concept as into the truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"3.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","text":"—A ratiocinative grounding of the elucidation of the Concept of science can at most accomplish this: that it be brought before representation and that a historical acquaintance with it be brought about; but a definition of science, or more specifically of logic, has its proof solely in that necessity of its emergence. A definition with which any science makes its absolute beginning can contain nothing other than the determinate, regular expression of what one admittedly and knowingly represents to oneself under the object and purpose of the science. That one represents precisely this under it is a historical assurance, with respect to which one can appeal only to this or that which is acknowledged, or, properly speaking, can merely submit by way of request that this or that may be allowed to count as acknowledged.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"3.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029","text":"There is no end to one person adducing a case and an instance from this source, another from that, according to which still something more and something else is to be understood by this or that expression, into whose definition, therefore, a more specific or more general determination is also to be admitted, and according to which the science is likewise to be arranged.—Moreover, it then depends upon ratiocination what is to be drawn in or excluded, and to what limit and extent; but to ratiocination itself the most manifold and various opinions stand open, concerning which in the end only arbitrariness can settle upon a fixed determination. In this procedure of beginning science with its definition, there is no mention of the need to show the necessity of its object and therewith of science itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"3.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","text":"The Concept of pure science and its deduction are thus presupposed in the present treatise insofar as the Phenomenology of Spirit is nothing other than its deduction. Absolute knowing is the truth of all modes of consciousness, because, as that progression of consciousness brought it forth, only in absolute knowing has the separation of the object from the certainty of itself completely dissolved, and truth become equal to this certainty, just as this certainty has become equal to truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"3.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","text":"Pure science thus presupposes liberation from the opposition of consciousness. It contains thought, insofar as thought is equally the thing in itself, or the thing in itself, insofar as it is equally pure thought. As science, truth is pure self-developing self-consciousness, and has the shape of the self, such that that which is in and for itself is known Concept, while the Concept as such is that which is in and for itself. This objective thinking is then the content of pure science.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"3.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","text":"It is therefore so far from being formal, so far from lacking the matter for an actual and true cognition, that its content is rather alone the absolute true, or, if one still wished to make use of the word matter, the genuine matter,—but a matter for which form is not something external, since this matter is rather pure thought, hence absolute form itself. Logic is consequently to be conceived as the system of pure reason, as the realm of pure thought. This realm is truth as it is in and for itself without veil. One may therefore express oneself by saying that this content is the exposition of God as he is in his eternal essence before the creation of nature and of finite spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"3.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033","text":"Anaxagoras is praised as the one who first pronounced the thought that the Nous, thought, is the principle of the world, that the essence of the world is determined as thought. Thereby he laid the foundation for an intellectual view of the universe, whose pure shape must be logic. In it the concern is not with a thinking about something which would lie at the basis for itself outside thinking, nor with forms which were merely to furnish marks of truth; rather, the necessary forms and proper determinations of thinking are the content and the highest truth itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"3.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0034","text":"In order at least to receive this into representation, the opinion must be set aside that truth must be something tangible. Such tangibility is, for example, still carried into the Platonic Ideas which are in the thinking of God, as though they were, as it were, existing things, but in another world or region, outside which the world of actuality would be situated and possess a real substantiality different from those Ideas only through this difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"3.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0035","text":"The Platonic Idea is nothing other than the universal, or, more determinately, the Concept of the object; only in its Concept does something have actuality; insofar as it is different from its Concept, it ceases to be actual and is a nullity; the side of tangibility and sensuous being-outside-itself belongs to this null side.—But, on the other side, one may appeal to the proper representations of ordinary logic; for it is assumed, namely, that, for example, definitions do not contain determinations which fall merely into the cognizing subject, but rather the determinations of the object, which constitute its most essential, proper nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"3.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0036","text":"Or, when one infers from given determinations to others, it is assumed that what is inferred is not something external and alien to the object, but rather belongs to it itself, that being corresponds to this thinking.—In general, the use of the forms of Concept, judgment, syllogism, definition, division, and so forth, rests upon the assumption that they are not merely forms of self-conscious thinking, but also of objective understanding. Thinking is an expression which preferentially ascribes the determination contained in it to consciousness. But insofar as it is said that understanding, that reason, is in the objective world, that spirit and nature have universal laws according to which their life and change proceed, it is conceded that the determinations of thought have just as much objective value and existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"3.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0037","text":"Critical philosophy had indeed already made metaphysics into logic; but it, like the later idealism, as was recalled above, out of fear of the object gave the logical determinations an essentially subjective significance; thereby they remain at the same time burdened with the object from which they fled, and a thing-in-itself, an infinite obstacle, remained as a beyond adhering to them. But liberation from the opposition of consciousness, which science must be able to presuppose, raises the determinations of thought above this anxious, incomplete standpoint, and demands their consideration as they are in and for themselves, without such limitation and reference: the logical, the purely rational.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"3.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0038","text":"Kant otherwise praises logic, namely the aggregate of determinations and propositions which in the ordinary sense is called logic, as fortunate above other sciences in having attained such an early completion; since Aristotle it has taken no backward step, but also no step forward, the latter because to all appearances it seems closed and complete.—If logic has undergone no alteration since Aristotle,—as indeed the alterations, if one considers the more recent compendia of logic, often consist more merely in omissions,—it is rather to be inferred from this that it requires a total reworking all the more; for a two-thousand-year continued labour of spirit must have procured for it a higher consciousness of its thinking and of its pure essence in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"3.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0039","text":"The comparison of the shapes to which the spirit of the practical and religious world, and the spirit of science in every kind of real and ideal consciousness, have raised themselves, with the shape in which logic, its consciousness of its pure essence, finds itself, shows too great a difference for it not immediately to strike even the most superficial consideration that this latter consciousness is wholly inappropriate to, and unworthy of, the former elevations.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"3.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0040","text":"In fact, the need for a transformation of logic has long been felt. In the form and content in which it appears in textbooks, it has, one may say, fallen into contempt. It is still dragged along more from the feeling that logic in general cannot be dispensed with, and from a still continuing habit of the tradition of its importance, than from conviction that that ordinary content and occupation with those empty forms have value and utility.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"3.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0041","text":"The expansions which were for a time given to it through psychological, pedagogical, and even physiological material have subsequently been fairly generally acknowledged to be disfigurements. In and for themselves, a great part of these psychological, pedagogical, physiological observations, laws, and rules, whether they stand in logic or wherever else, must appear very vapid and trivial.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"3.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0042","text":"Especially such rules as, for example, that one should think through and examine what one reads in books or hears orally; that, if one does not see well, one should assist one's eyes with spectacles,—rules which were given by the textbooks in so-called applied logic, and indeed seriously divided into paragraphs, in order that one might arrive at truth,—must appear superfluous to everyone,—at most not to the writer or teacher who is embarrassed to expand by something or other the otherwise too brief and dead content of logic.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"3.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0043","text":"As regards such content, the reason why it is so spiritless has already been given above. Its determinations count as fixed and immutable, and are brought into merely external relation with one another. Because in judgments and syllogisms the operations are chiefly reduced to and grounded upon the quantitative aspect of the determinations, everything rests upon an external difference, upon mere comparison; it becomes a wholly analytic procedure and a calculation devoid of Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"3.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0044","text":"The derivation of the so-called rules and laws, especially of inference, is not much better than fingering little rods of unequal length in order to sort and connect them according to their size,—than the playful occupation of children seeking out from pictures cut up in various ways the pieces which fit together.—Thus this thinking has not without justification been equated with calculation, and calculation in turn with this thinking. In arithmetic numbers are taken as that which is devoid of Concept and which, apart from their equality or inequality, that is, apart from their wholly external relation, have no significance, neither in themselves nor in their relation a thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"3.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0045","text":"When it is mechanically calculated that three quarters multiplied by two thirds makes one half, this operation contains approximately as much and as little thought as the calculation whether this or that kind of syllogism may take place in a figure.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"3.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0046","text":"In order that this dead bonework of logic may be animated by spirit into substance and content, its method must be that by which alone it is capable of being pure science. In the condition in which it finds itself, scarcely an intimation of scientific method is recognizable. It has approximately the form of an empirical science. Empirical sciences have, for what they are supposed to be, found their peculiar method of defining and classifying their material, as best they can. Pure mathematics too has its method, which is appropriate to its abstract objects and to the quantitative determination in which alone it considers them.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"3.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","text":"I have stated what is essential concerning this method and, in general, concerning the subordinate role that scientificity can have in mathematics, in the Preface to the Phenomenology of Spirit; but it will also be considered more closely within logic itself. Spinoza, Wolff, and others allowed themselves to be seduced into applying it to philosophy as well, and into making the external course of conceptless quantity into the course of the Concept, which is contradictory in and for itself. Until now philosophy had not yet found its method; it looked with envy upon the systematic edifice of mathematics and, as stated, borrowed it from it, or made do with the method of sciences which are only mixtures of given material, propositions of experience, and thoughts,—or else made do with the crude rejection of all method.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"3.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","text":"But the exposition of what alone can be the true method of philosophical science falls within the treatment of logic itself; for the method is consciousness of the form of the inner self-movement of its content. In the Phenomenology of Spirit I have presented an example of this method, in a more concrete object, in consciousness, an example of this method, in a more concrete object, in consciousness. [3] Here there are shapes of consciousness, each of which, in its realization, at the same time dissolves itself, has its own negation as its result,—and thereby has passed over into a higher shape.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"3.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","text":"The sole thing necessary in order to attain scientific progress, and the quite simple insight into which it is essential to strive,—is the cognition of the logical proposition that the negative is equally positive, or that what contradicts itself does not dissolve into zero, into abstract nothing, but essentially only into the negation of its particular content, or that such a negation is not all negation, but the negation of the determinate thing that dissolves itself, hence determinate negation; that, therefore, the result essentially contains that from which it results;—which is properly a tautology, for otherwise it would be an immediate, not a result. Since that which results, the negation, is determinate negation, it has a content.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"3.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","text":"It is a new Concept, but the higher, richer Concept than the preceding one; for it has become richer by its negation or opposite; thus it contains it, but also more than it, and is the unity of it and its opposite.—In this way the system of Concepts in general is to form itself,—and to complete itself in an irresistible, pure course, taking nothing into itself from without.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"3.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0051","text":"[3] Later, in the other concrete objects and respective parts of philosophy.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"3.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","text":"How could I suppose that the method which I have followed in this system of logic,—or rather which this system follows in itself,—were not capable of much perfection, of much elaboration in particulars; but I know at the same time that it is the only true one. This is already evident in itself from the fact that it is not distinct from its object and content;—for it is the content within itself, the dialectic which it has in itself, that moves it forward. It is clear that no presentations can count as scientific which do not follow the course of this method and are not in accordance with its simple rhythm, for it is the course of the matter itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"3.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","text":"In accordance with this method, I recall that the divisions and headings of the books, sections, and chapters given in the work, as well as any explanations connected with them, have been made for the purpose of a preliminary overview, and that they properly have only historical value. They do not belong to the content and body of science, but are compilations of external reflection, which has already run through the whole of the exposition and therefore knows and indicates in advance the sequence of its moments, before they have yet been brought forth through the matter itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"3.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0054","text":"In the other sciences, such prior determinations and divisions likewise are in themselves nothing other than such external indications; but even within science they are not elevated above this character. Even in logic, for example, it is said that “logic has two principal parts, the doctrine of elements and methodology”; then, under the doctrine of elements, one finds without further ado such a heading as: Laws of Thought;—then first chapter: On Concepts. First section: On the Clarity of Concepts, etc.—These determinations and divisions, made without any deduction and justification whatever, constitute the systematic framework and the entire connection of such sciences.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"3.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0055","text":"Such a logic regards it as its vocation to speak of the fact that concepts and truths must be derived from principles; but in what it calls method, there is not even remotely any thought of deriving. The order consists perhaps in the grouping together of homogeneous things, in placing the simpler before the more composite, and other external considerations. But with regard to an inner, necessary connection, it remains at the register of divisional determinations, and the transition is made merely by the statement that there is now: Second Chapter;—or: we now come to judgments, and the like.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"3.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","text":"The headings and divisions occurring in this system, too, are not intended in themselves to have any other significance than that of a table of contents. Apart from this, however, the necessity of the connection and the immanent genesis of the differences must be found in the treatment of the matter itself, for it falls within the Concept's own further determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"3.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0057","text":"That through which the Concept itself leads itself further is the negative previously indicated, which it has within itself; this constitutes the truly dialectical. Dialectic, which is regarded as a separate part of logic and, with respect to its end and standpoint, may be said to have been wholly misconceived, thereby receives an entirely different position.—Even Platonic dialectic itself in the Parmenides, and elsewhere still more directly in any case, partly has only the aim of dissolving and refuting limited assertions through themselves, and partly has nothingness in general as its result.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"3.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0058","text":"Dialectic is commonly regarded as an external and negative activity that does not belong to the matter itself, as having its ground in mere vanity, as a subjective urge to set what is firm and true wavering and to dissolve it, or at least as leading to nothing but the vanity of the object treated dialectically.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"3.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0059","text":"Kant placed dialectic higher, and this aspect belongs among his greatest merits,—in that he removed from it the appearance of arbitrariness which it has in the ordinary conception, and presented it as a necessary activity of reason. Since it counted merely as the art of producing illusions and bringing forth deceptions, it was simply presupposed that it played a false game, and that its entire power rested solely upon its concealing the deception; that its results were only surreptitiously obtained and were a subjective appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"3.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0060","text":"Kant's dialectical presentations in the antinomies of pure reason admittedly deserve, when they are considered more closely, as will be done more extensively in the course of this work, certainly no great praise; but the universal idea that he laid at their foundation and made valid is the objectivity of appearance and the necessity of contradiction, which belongs to the nature of determinations of thought: initially, indeed, in the sense that these determinations are applied by reason to things in themselves; but precisely what they are in reason and in relation to what is in itself is their nature. This result, taken in its positive aspect, is nothing other than their inner negativity, as their self-moving soul, the principle of all natural and spiritual vitality in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"3.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0061","text":"But as soon as one remains at the abstract-negative side of the dialectical, the result is only the familiar one, that reason is incapable of cognizing the infinite;—a strange result, since the infinite is the rational, namely to say that reason is not capable of cognizing the rational.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"3.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","text":"The speculative consists in this dialectical, as it is taken here, and thus in grasping the opposite in its unity, or the positive in the negative. It is the most important aspect, but for the still unpractised, unfree power of thought the most difficult. If it is still occupied with tearing itself away from sensuous-concrete representation and from reasoning, it must first practise itself in abstract thinking, in holding Concepts fast in their determinacy and learning to cognize from them. A presentation of logic for this purpose would have to adhere in its method to the above-mentioned dividing, and with respect to its more specific content to the determinations that result for the individual Concepts, without entering upon the dialectical.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"3.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0063","text":"In external form it would become similar to the customary presentation of this science, while otherwise differing from it in content as well, and would still serve to exercise abstract, though not speculative, thinking, a purpose which the logic made popular through psychological and anthropological additions cannot even fulfil. It would give the spirit the image of a methodically ordered whole, although the soul of the edifice, the method that lives in the dialectical, would not itself appear therein.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"3.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0064","text":"With regard to education and the relation of the individual to logic, I note in conclusion that this science, like grammar, appears in two different respects or values. It is one thing for one who is only first approaching it and the sciences in general, and another for one who returns to it from them. Whoever begins to become acquainted with grammar finds in its forms and laws dry abstractions, arbitrary rules, in general an isolated multitude of determinations that display only the value and significance of what lies in their immediate sense; cognition initially cognizes in them nothing but themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"3.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","text":"Whoever, by contrast, has mastery of a language and at the same time knows other languages in comparison with it, only for such a person can the spirit and culture of a people make itself felt in the grammar of its language; the same rules and forms now have a fulfilled, living value. Through grammar he can cognize the expression of spirit in general, logic. Thus one who approaches science finds in logic at first an isolated system of abstractions, confined to itself, not extending over the other cognitions and sciences.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"3.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0066","text":"Rather, set against the wealth of representations of the world, against the content of the other sciences that appears real, and compared with the promise of absolute science to disclose the essence of this wealth, the inner nature of spirit and world, truth, this science in its abstract form, in the colourless, cold simplicity of its pure determinations, has rather the appearance of fulfilling anything sooner than this promise, and of standing devoid of content in relation to that wealth. The first acquaintance with logic restricts its significance to itself; its content counts only as an isolated occupation with determinations of thought, alongside which the other scientific occupations are a material and content of their own for themselves, upon which the logical perhaps has a formal influence, indeed such an influence as comes about more of itself, and","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"3.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0067","text":"for which the scientific form and its study can indeed, if necessary, also be dispensed with. The other sciences have altogether cast off the regular method of being a sequence of definitions, axioms, theorems and their proofs, etc.; the so-called natural logic asserts itself in them on its own and proceeds without special cognition directed toward thinking itself. But the material and content of these sciences holds itself as wholly independent of the logical, and is also more appealing to sense, feeling, representation, and practical interest of every kind.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"3.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","text":"Thus logic must indeed first be learned as something that one understands and comprehends well, but in which extent, depth, and further significance are initially missed. Only from the deeper cognition of the other sciences does the logical rise for subjective spirit as not merely an abstract universal, but as the universal that comprehends within itself the wealth of the particular;—just as the same moral maxim in the mouth of a youth, who understands it quite correctly, does not possess the significance and extent which it has in the spirit of a man experienced in life, to whom the whole force of the content contained in it is thereby expressed, so the logical first receives an estimation of its value when it has become the result of the experience of the sciences; from this it presents itself to spirit as universal truth, not as a particular cognition alongside other material and","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"3.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0069","text":"realities, but as the essence of all this other content.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"3.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0070","text":"Even if, then, the logical is not present for the mind at the beginning of study in this conscious power, it nonetheless thereby receives into itself the power that guides it into all truth. The system of logic is the realm of shadows, the world of simple essentialities, freed from all sensuous concretion. The study of this science, the sojourn and work in this realm of shadows, is the absolute cultivation and discipline of consciousness. In it, consciousness pursues a business remote from sensuous intuitions and ends, from feelings, from the merely intended world of representations. Considered from its negative side, this business consists in keeping at a distance the contingency of ratiocinative thinking and the arbitrariness of allowing these or the opposite grounds to occur to oneself or to count as valid.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"3.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","text":"Above all, however, thought thereby gains self-subsistence and independence. It becomes at home in the abstract and in progression through concepts without sensuous substrates; it becomes the unconscious power to receive the otherwise manifold contents of knowledge and sciences into rational form, to grasp and hold them fast in their essentiality, to strip off the external, and thus to extract the logical from them—or, what is the same thing, to fill the abstract foundation of the logical, previously acquired through study, with the content of all truth, and to give it the value of a universal that no longer stands as a particular alongside other particulars, but extends over all this and is its essence, the absolutely true.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"3.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071"]}],"source_digest":"3ee927f078f1d383ae21d4e427385d2c04a7be781fea26aae799a1d870310a7d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Allgemeiner Begriff der Logik"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Allgemeiner Begriff der Logik","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL","title":"General Division of Logic","order":4,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AEDL","text":"In dem, was über den Begriff dieser Wissenschaft und wohin seine Rechtfertigung falle, gesagt worden ist, liegt, daß die allgemeine Eintheilung hier nur vorläufig seyn, gleichsam nur insofern angegeben werden kann, als der Verfasser die Wissenschaft bereits kennt, daher historisch hier zum Voraus anzuführen im Stande ist, zu welchen Hauptunterschieden sich der Begriff in seiner Entwickelung bestimmen wird.\n\nDoch kann versucht werden, das was zum Eintheilen erforderlich ist, zum Voraus im Allgemeinen verständlich zu machen, obgleich auch dabei ein Verfahren der Methode in Anspruch genommen werden muß, das seine volle Verständigung und Rechtfertigung erst innerhalb der Wissenschaft erhält.—Zuvörderst also ist zu erinnern, daß hier vorausgesetzt wird, die Eintheilung müsse mit dem Begriffe zusammenhängen, oder vielmehr in ihm selbst liegen. Der Begriff ist nicht unbestimmt, sondern bestimmt an ihm selbst; die Eintheilung aber drückt entwickelt diese seine Bestimmtheit aus; sie ist das Urtheil desselben, nicht ein Urtheil über irgend einen äußerlich genommenen Gegenstand, sondern das Urtheilen, d.i. Bestimmen des Begriffs an ihm selbst. Die Rechtwinklichkeit, Spitzwinklichkeit u.s. f., wie die Gleichseitigkeit u.s.f., nach welchen Bestimmungen die Dreiecke eingetheilt werden, liegt nicht in der Bestimmtheit des Dreiecks selbst, d.h. nicht in dem, was der Begriff des Dreiecks genannt zu werden pflegt, ebenso wenig als in dem, was für den Begriff des Thieres überhaupt, oder des Säugethiers, Vogels u.s.w. die Bestimmungen liegen, nach welchen jenes in Säugethiere, Vögel u.s. w. und diese Klassen in weitere Gattungen eingetheilt werden. Solche Bestimmungen werden anderswoher, aus der empirischen Anschauung aufgenommen; sie treten zu jenem sogenannten Begriffe von Außen hinzu. In der philosophischen Behandlung des Eintheilens muß der Begriff selbst sich als ihren Ursprung enthaltend zeigen.\n\nDer Begriff der Logik aber selbst ist in der Einleitung als das Resultat einer jenseits liegenden Wissenschaft, damit hier gleichfalls als eine Voraussetzung angegeben worden. Die Logik bestimmte sich danach als die Wissenschaft des reinen Denkens, die zu ihrem Princip das reine Wissen habe, die nicht abstrakte, sondern dadurch konkrete lebendige Einheit, daß in ihr der Gegensatz des Bewußtseyns von einem subjektiv—für sich Seyenden und einem zweiten solchen Seyenden, einem Objektiven, als überwunden, und das Seyn als reiner Begriff an sich selbst, und der reine Begriff als das wahrhafte Seyn gewußt wird. Dieß sind sonach die beiden Momente, welche im Logischen enthalten sind. Aber sie werden nun als untrennbar seyend gewußt, nicht wie im Bewußtseyn jedes auch als für sich seyend; dadurch, allein, daß sie zugleich als unterschiedene (jedoch nicht für sich seyende) gewußt werden, ist ihre Einheit nicht abstrakt, todt, unbewegend, sondern konkret.\n\nDiese Einheit macht das logische Princip zugleich als Element aus, so daß die Entwickelung jenes Unterschiedes, der sogleich in ihm ist, nur innerhalb dieses Elementes vor sich geht. Denn indem die Eintheilung, wie gesagt worden, das Urtheil des Begriffs, das Setzen der ihm schon immanenten Bestimmung und damit seines Unterschiedes ist, so darf dieß Setzen nicht als ein Wiederauflösen jener konkreten Einheit in ihre Bestimmungen, wie sie als für sich seyend gelten sollen, gefaßt werden, was hier ein leeres Zurückgehen auf den vorigen Standpunkt, den Gegensatz des Bewußtseyns wäre; dieser ist vielmehr verschwunden; jene Einheit bleibt das Element, und aus ihr tritt jenes Unterscheiden der Eintheilung und überhaupt der Entwickelung nicht mehr heraus. Damit sind die früher (auf dem Wege zur Wahrheit) für sich seyenden Bestimmungen, wie ein Subjektives und Objektives, oder auch Denken und Seyn oder Begriff und Realität, wie sie in irgend einer Rücksicht bestimmt worden seyn mögen, nun in ihrer Wahrheit, d.i. in ihrer Einheit, zu Formen herabgesetzt. In ihrem Unterschiede blieben sie daher selbst an sich der ganze Begriff und dieser wird in der Eintheilung nur unter seinen eigenen Bestimmungen gesetzt.\n\nSo ist es der ganze Begriff, der das eine Mal als seyender Begriff, das andere Mal als Begriff zu betrachten ist; dort ist er nur Begriff an sich, der Realität oder des Seyns, hier ist er Begriff als solcher, für sich seyender Begriff, (wie er es um konkrete Formen zu nennen, im denkenden Menschen, aber auch schon, freilich nicht als bewußter noch weniger als gewußter Begriff, im empfindenden Thier, und in der organischen Individualität überhaupt ist; Begriff an sich ist er aber nur in der unorganischen Natur).—Die Logik wäre hiernach zunächst in die Logik des Begriffs als Seyns, und des Begriffs als Begriffs, —oder indem wir uns der sonst gewöhnlichen, obgleich der unbestimmtesten und darum der vieldeutigsten Ausdrücke bedienen,—in die objektive und subjektive Logik einzutheilen.\n\nNach dem zu Grunde liegenden Elemente aber der Einheit des Begriffs in sich selbst und damit der Untrennbarkeit seiner Bestimmungen, müssen diese ferner auch, insofern sie unterschieden, der Begriff in ihrem Unterschiede gesetzt wird, wenigstens in Beziehung aufeinander stehen. Es ergiebt sich daraus eine Sphäre der Vermittelung, der Begriff als System der Reflexionsbestimmungen, d.i. des zum Insichseyn des Begriffs übergehenden Seyns, der auf diese Weise noch nicht als solcher für sich gesetzt ist, sondern mit dem unmittelbaren Seyn als einem ihm auch Äußeren zugleich behaftet ist. Dieß ist die Lehre von dem Wesen, die zwischen der Lehre vom Seyn und der vom Begriff inmitten steht.—Sie ist in der allgemeinen Eintheilung dieses logischen Werks noch unter die objektive Logik gestellt worden, insofern, ob das Wesen zwar bereits das Innere, dem Begriffe der Charakter des Subjekts ausdrücklich vorzubehalten ist.\n\nKant [4] hat in neueren Zeiten dem, was gewöhnlich Logik genannt worden, noch eine, nämlich eine transcendentale Logik gegenüber gestellt. Das, was hier objektive Logik genannt worden, würde zum Theil dem entsprechen, was bei ihm die transcendentale Logik ist. Er unterscheidet sie von dem, was er allgemeine Logik nennt, so, daß sie à) die Begriffe betrachte, die sich a priori auf Gegenstände beziehen, somit nicht von allem Inhalte der objektiven Erkenntniß abstrahire, oder daß sie die Regeln des reinen Denkens eines Gegenstandes enthalte, und ß) zugleich auf den Ursprung unserer Erkenntniß gehe, insofern sie nicht den Gegenständen zugeschrieben werden könne.—Diese zweite Seite ist es, auf die das philosophische Interesse Kants ausschließend gerichtet ist. Sein Hauptgedanke ist, die Kategorien dem Selbstbewußtseyn, als dem subjektiven Ich, zu vindiciren. Vermöge dieser Bestimmung bleibt die Ansicht innerhalb des Bewußtseyns und seines Gegensatzes stehen, und hat außer dem Empirischen des Gefühls und der Anschauung noch Etwas, das nicht durch das denkende Selbstbewußtseyn gesetzt und bestimmt ist, ein Ding-an-sich, ein dem Denken fremdes und äußerliches, übrig bleiben; obgleich leicht einzusehen ist, daß ein solches Abstraktum, wie Ding-an-sich, selbst nur ein Produkt des, und zwar nur abstrahirenden, Denkens ist.—Wenn andere Kantianer sich über das Bestimmen des Gegenstandes durch Ich so ausgedrückt haben, daß das Objektiviren des Ich, als ein ursprüngliches und nothwendiges Thun des Bewußtseyns anzusehen sey, so daß in diesem ursprünglichen Thun noch nicht die Vorstellung des Ich selbst ist,—als welche erst ein Bewußtseyn jenes Bewußtseyns, oder selbst ein Objektiviren jenes Bewußtseyn sey,—so ist dieses von dem Gegensatze des Bewußtseyns befreite objektivirende Thun näher dasjenige, was für Denken als solches überhaupt genommen werden kann. [5] Dieses Thun sollte aber nicht mehr Bewußtseyn genannt werden; Bewußtseyn schließt den Gegensatz des Ich und seines Gegenstandes in sich, der in jenem ursprünglichen Thun nicht vorhanden ist. Die Benennung Bewußtseyn wirft noch mehr den Schein von Subjektivität auf dasselbe, als der Ausdruck Denken, der aber hier überhaupt im absoluten Sinne als unendliches mit der Endlichkeit des Bewußtseyns nicht behaftetes, Denken, kurz Denken als solches, zu nehmen ist.\n\n[4] Ich erinnere, daß ich auf die kantische Philosophie in diesem Werke darum häufig Rücksicht nehme, (was manchen überflüssig scheinen könnte) weil sie,—ihre nähere Bestimmtheit so wie die besonderen Theile der Ausführung mögen sonst und auch in diesem Werke betrachtet werden, wie sie wollen,—die Grundlage und den Ausgangspunkt der neueren deutschen Philosophie ausmacht, und dieß ihr Verdienst durch das, was an ihr ausgesetzt werden möge, ihr ungeschmälert bleibt. Auch darum ist auf sie in der objektiven Logik häufig Rücksicht zu nehmen, weil sie sich auf wichtige bestimmtere Seiten des Logischen näher einläßt, spätere Darstellungen von Philosophie hingegen dasselbe wenig beachtet, zum Theil oft nur eine rohe,—aber nicht ungerächte,—Verachtung dagegen bewiesen haben. Das bei uns am weitesten verbreitete Philosophiren tritt nicht aus den kantischen Resultaten, daß die Vernunft keinen wahren Gehalt erkennen könne, und in Ansehung der absoluten Wahrheit auf das Glauben zu verweisen sey, heraus. Was aber bei Kant Resultat ist, damit wird in diesem Philosophiren unmittelbar angefangen, damit die vorhergehende Ausführung, aus welche jenes Resultat herkömmt, und welche philosophisches Erkennen ist, vorweggeschnitten. Die kantische Philosophie dient so als ein Polster für die Trägheit des Denkens, die sich damit beruhigt, daß bereits Alles bewiesen und abgethan sey. Für Erkenntniß und einen bestimmten Inhalt des Denkens, der in solcher unfruchtbaren und trockenen Beruhigung sich nicht findet, ist sich daher an jene vorangegangene Ausführung zu wenden.\n\n[5] Wenn der Ausdruck objektivirendes Thun des Ich an andere Produktionen des Geistes, z.B. die der Phantasie erinnern kann, so ist zu bemerken, daß von einem Bestimmen eines Gegenstandes die Rede ist, insofern dessen Inhalts-Momente nicht dem Gefühl und der Anschauung angehören. Solcher Gegenstand ist ein Gedanke, und ihn bestimmen heißt Theils ihn erst produciren, Theils insofern er ein Vorausgesetztes ist, weitere Gedanken über ihn haben, ihn denkend weiter entwickeln.\n\nIndem nun das Interesse der kantischen Philosophie auf das sogenannte Transcendentale der Denkbestimmungen gerichtet war, ist die Abhandlung derselben selbst leer ausgegangen; was sie an ihnen selbst sind, ohne die abstrakte, allen gleiche Relation auf Ich, ihre Bestimmtheit gegen und ihr Verhältniß zu einander ist nicht zu einem Gegenstande der Betrachtung gemacht worden; die Erkenntniß ihrer Natur hat sich daher durch diese Philosophie nicht im geringsten gefördert gefunden. Das einzige Interessante, was hierauf Beziehung hat, kommt in der Kritik der Ideen vor. Für den wirklichen Fortschritt der Philosophie aber war es nothwendig, daß das Interesse des Denkens auf die Betrachtung der formellen Seite, des Ich, des Bewußtseyns als solchen, d.i. der abstrakten Beziehung eines subjektiven Wissens auf ein Objekt, gezogen, daß die Erkenntniß der unendlichen Form, d.i. des Begriffs, auf diese Weise eingeleitet wurde. Um jedoch diese Erkenntniß zu erreichen, mußte jene endliche Bestimmtheit, in der die Form als Ich, Bewußtseyn ist, noch abgestreift werden. Die Form so in ihre Reinheit herausgedacht, enthält es dann in sich selbst, sich zu bestimmen, d.i. sich Inhalt zu geben, und zwar denselben in seiner Nothwendigkeit,—als System der Denkbestimmungen.\n\nDie objektive Logik tritt damit vielmehr an die Stelle der vormaligen Metaphysik, als welche das wissenschaftliche Gebäude über die Welt war, das nur durch Gedanken aufgeführt seyn sollte.—Wenn wir auf die letzte Gestalt der Ausbildung dieser Wissenschaft Rücksicht nehmen, so ist erstens unmittelbar die Ontologie, an deren Stelle die objektive Logik tritt,—der Theil jener Metaphysik, der die Natur des Ens überhaupt erforschen sollte;—das Ens begreift sowohl Seyn als Wesen in sich, für welchen Unterschied unsere Sprache glücklicherweise den verschiedenen Ausdruck gerettet hat.—Alsdann aber begreift die objektive Logik auch die übrige Metaphysik insofern in sich, als diese mit den reinen Denkformen die besondern, zunächst aus der Vorstellung genommenen Substrate, die Seele, die Welt, Gott, zu fassen suchte, und die Bestimmungen des Denkens das Wesentliche der Betrachtungsweise ausmachten. Aber die Logik betrachtet diese Formen frei von jenen Substraten, den Subjekten der Vorstellung, und ihre Natur und Werth an und für sich selbst. Jene Metaphysik unterließ dieß und zog sich daher den gerechten Vorwurf zu, sie ohne Kritik gebraucht zu haben, ohne die vorgängige Untersuchung, ob und wie sie fähig seyen, Bestimmungen des Dings-an-sich, nach kantischem Ausdruck,—oder vielmehr des Vernünftigen zu seyen.—Die objektive Logik ist daher die wahrhafte Kritik derselben,—eine Kritik, die sie nicht nach der abstrakten Form der Apriorität gegen das Aposteriorische, sondern sie selbst in ihrem besondern Inhalte betrachtet.\n\nDie subjektive Logik ist die Logik des Begriffs,—des Wesens, das seine Beziehung auf ein Seyn oder seinen Schein aufgehoben hat, und in seiner Bestimmung nicht äußerlich mehr, sondern das freie selbstständig, sich in sich bestimmende Subjektive, oder vielmehr das Subjekt selbst ist.—Indem das Subjektive das Mißverständniß von Zufälligem und Willkürlichem, so wie überhaupt von Bestimmungen, die in die Form des Bewußtseyns gehören, mit sich führt, so ist hier auf den Unterschied von Subjektivem und Objektivem, der sich späterhin innerhalb der Logik selbst näher entwickeln wird, kein besonderes Gewicht zu legen.\n\nDie Logik zerfällt also zwar überhaupt in objektive und subjektive Logik, bestimmter aber hat sie die drei Theile:\n\nI. Die Logik des Seyns,\n\nII. die Logik des Wesens und\n\nIII. die Logik des Begriffs.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","text":"In dem, was über den Begriff dieser Wissenschaft und wohin seine Rechtfertigung falle, gesagt worden ist, liegt, daß die allgemeine Eintheilung hier nur vorläufig seyn, gleichsam nur insofern angegeben werden kann, als der Verfasser die Wissenschaft bereits kennt, daher historisch hier zum Voraus anzuführen im Stande ist, zu welchen Hauptunterschieden sich der Begriff in seiner Entwickelung bestimmen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"4.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","text":"Doch kann versucht werden, das was zum Eintheilen erforderlich ist, zum Voraus im Allgemeinen verständlich zu machen, obgleich auch dabei ein Verfahren der Methode in Anspruch genommen werden muß, das seine volle Verständigung und Rechtfertigung erst innerhalb der Wissenschaft erhält.—Zuvörderst also ist zu erinnern, daß hier vorausgesetzt wird, die Eintheilung müsse mit dem Begriffe zusammenhängen, oder vielmehr in ihm selbst liegen. Der Begriff ist nicht unbestimmt, sondern bestimmt an ihm selbst; die Eintheilung aber drückt entwickelt diese seine Bestimmtheit aus; sie ist das Urtheil desselben, nicht ein Urtheil über irgend einen äußerlich genommenen Gegenstand, sondern das Urtheilen, d.i. Bestimmen des Begriffs an ihm selbst. Die Rechtwinklichkeit, Spitzwinklichkeit u.s.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"4.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","text":"f., wie die Gleichseitigkeit u.s.f., nach welchen Bestimmungen die Dreiecke eingetheilt werden, liegt nicht in der Bestimmtheit des Dreiecks selbst, d.h. nicht in dem, was der Begriff des Dreiecks genannt zu werden pflegt, ebenso wenig als in dem, was für den Begriff des Thieres überhaupt, oder des Säugethiers, Vogels u.s.w. die Bestimmungen liegen, nach welchen jenes in Säugethiere, Vögel u.s. w. und diese Klassen in weitere Gattungen eingetheilt werden. Solche Bestimmungen werden anderswoher, aus der empirischen Anschauung aufgenommen; sie treten zu jenem sogenannten Begriffe von Außen hinzu. In der philosophischen Behandlung des Eintheilens muß der Begriff selbst sich als ihren Ursprung enthaltend zeigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"4.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","text":"Der Begriff der Logik aber selbst ist in der Einleitung als das Resultat einer jenseits liegenden Wissenschaft, damit hier gleichfalls als eine Voraussetzung angegeben worden. Die Logik bestimmte sich danach als die Wissenschaft des reinen Denkens, die zu ihrem Princip das reine Wissen habe, die nicht abstrakte, sondern dadurch konkrete lebendige Einheit, daß in ihr der Gegensatz des Bewußtseyns von einem subjektiv—für sich Seyenden und einem zweiten solchen Seyenden, einem Objektiven, als überwunden, und das Seyn als reiner Begriff an sich selbst, und der reine Begriff als das wahrhafte Seyn gewußt wird. Dieß sind sonach die beiden Momente, welche im Logischen enthalten sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"4.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","text":"Aber sie werden nun als untrennbar seyend gewußt, nicht wie im Bewußtseyn jedes auch als für sich seyend; dadurch, allein, daß sie zugleich als unterschiedene (jedoch nicht für sich seyende) gewußt werden, ist ihre Einheit nicht abstrakt, todt, unbewegend, sondern konkret.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"4.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","text":"Diese Einheit macht das logische Princip zugleich als Element aus, so daß die Entwickelung jenes Unterschiedes, der sogleich in ihm ist, nur innerhalb dieses Elementes vor sich geht. Denn indem die Eintheilung, wie gesagt worden, das Urtheil des Begriffs, das Setzen der ihm schon immanenten Bestimmung und damit seines Unterschiedes ist, so darf dieß Setzen nicht als ein Wiederauflösen jener konkreten Einheit in ihre Bestimmungen, wie sie als für sich seyend gelten sollen, gefaßt werden, was hier ein leeres Zurückgehen auf den vorigen Standpunkt, den Gegensatz des Bewußtseyns wäre; dieser ist vielmehr verschwunden; jene Einheit bleibt das Element, und aus ihr tritt jenes Unterscheiden der Eintheilung und überhaupt der Entwickelung nicht mehr heraus.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"4.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","text":"Damit sind die früher (auf dem Wege zur Wahrheit) für sich seyenden Bestimmungen, wie ein Subjektives und Objektives, oder auch Denken und Seyn oder Begriff und Realität, wie sie in irgend einer Rücksicht bestimmt worden seyn mögen, nun in ihrer Wahrheit, d.i. in ihrer Einheit, zu Formen herabgesetzt. In ihrem Unterschiede blieben sie daher selbst an sich der ganze Begriff und dieser wird in der Eintheilung nur unter seinen eigenen Bestimmungen gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"4.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","text":"So ist es der ganze Begriff, der das eine Mal als seyender Begriff, das andere Mal als Begriff zu betrachten ist; dort ist er nur Begriff an sich, der Realität oder des Seyns, hier ist er Begriff als solcher, für sich seyender Begriff, (wie er es um konkrete Formen zu nennen, im denkenden Menschen, aber auch schon, freilich nicht als bewußter noch weniger als gewußter Begriff, im empfindenden Thier, und in der organischen Individualität überhaupt ist; Begriff an sich ist er aber nur in der unorganischen Natur).—Die Logik wäre hiernach zunächst in die Logik des Begriffs als Seyns, und des Begriffs als Begriffs, —oder indem wir uns der sonst gewöhnlichen, obgleich der unbestimmtesten und darum der vieldeutigsten Ausdrücke bedienen,—in die objektive und subjektive Logik einzutheilen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"4.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","text":"Nach dem zu Grunde liegenden Elemente aber der Einheit des Begriffs in sich selbst und damit der Untrennbarkeit seiner Bestimmungen, müssen diese ferner auch, insofern sie unterschieden, der Begriff in ihrem Unterschiede gesetzt wird, wenigstens in Beziehung aufeinander stehen. Es ergiebt sich daraus eine Sphäre der Vermittelung, der Begriff als System der Reflexionsbestimmungen, d.i. des zum Insichseyn des Begriffs übergehenden Seyns, der auf diese Weise noch nicht als solcher für sich gesetzt ist, sondern mit dem unmittelbaren Seyn als einem ihm auch Äußeren zugleich behaftet ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"4.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","text":"Dieß ist die Lehre von dem Wesen, die zwischen der Lehre vom Seyn und der vom Begriff inmitten steht.—Sie ist in der allgemeinen Eintheilung dieses logischen Werks noch unter die objektive Logik gestellt worden, insofern, ob das Wesen zwar bereits das Innere, dem Begriffe der Charakter des Subjekts ausdrücklich vorzubehalten ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"4.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","text":"Kant [4] hat in neueren Zeiten dem, was gewöhnlich Logik genannt worden, noch eine, nämlich eine transcendentale Logik gegenüber gestellt. Das, was hier objektive Logik genannt worden, würde zum Theil dem entsprechen, was bei ihm die transcendentale Logik ist. Er unterscheidet sie von dem, was er allgemeine Logik nennt, so, daß sie à) die Begriffe betrachte, die sich a priori auf Gegenstände beziehen, somit nicht von allem Inhalte der objektiven Erkenntniß abstrahire, oder daß sie die Regeln des reinen Denkens eines Gegenstandes enthalte, und ß) zugleich auf den Ursprung unserer Erkenntniß gehe, insofern sie nicht den Gegenständen zugeschrieben werden könne.—Diese zweite Seite ist es, auf die das philosophische Interesse Kants ausschließend gerichtet ist. Sein Hauptgedanke ist, die Kategorien dem Selbstbewußtseyn, als dem subjektiven Ich, zu vindiciren.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"4.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","text":"Vermöge dieser Bestimmung bleibt die Ansicht innerhalb des Bewußtseyns und seines Gegensatzes stehen, und hat außer dem Empirischen des Gefühls und der Anschauung noch Etwas, das nicht durch das denkende Selbstbewußtseyn gesetzt und bestimmt ist, ein Ding-an-sich, ein dem Denken fremdes und äußerliches, übrig bleiben; obgleich leicht einzusehen ist, daß ein solches Abstraktum, wie Ding-an-sich, selbst nur ein Produkt des, und zwar nur abstrahirenden, Denkens ist.—Wenn andere Kantianer sich über das Bestimmen des Gegenstandes durch Ich so ausgedrückt haben, daß das Objektiviren des Ich, als ein ursprüngliches und nothwendiges Thun des Bewußtseyns anzusehen sey, so daß in diesem ursprünglichen Thun noch nicht die Vorstellung des Ich selbst ist,—als welche erst ein Bewußtseyn jenes Bewußtseyns, oder selbst ein Objektiviren jenes Bewußtseyn sey,—so ist dieses von dem Gegensatze des","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"4.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0013","text":"Bewußtseyns befreite objektivirende Thun näher dasjenige, was für Denken als solches überhaupt genommen werden kann. [5] Dieses Thun sollte aber nicht mehr Bewußtseyn genannt werden; Bewußtseyn schließt den Gegensatz des Ich und seines Gegenstandes in sich, der in jenem ursprünglichen Thun nicht vorhanden ist. Die Benennung Bewußtseyn wirft noch mehr den Schein von Subjektivität auf dasselbe, als der Ausdruck Denken, der aber hier überhaupt im absoluten Sinne als unendliches mit der Endlichkeit des Bewußtseyns nicht behaftetes, Denken, kurz Denken als solches, zu nehmen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"4.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0014","text":"[4] Ich erinnere, daß ich auf die kantische Philosophie in diesem Werke darum häufig Rücksicht nehme, (was manchen überflüssig scheinen könnte) weil sie,—ihre nähere Bestimmtheit so wie die besonderen Theile der Ausführung mögen sonst und auch in diesem Werke betrachtet werden, wie sie wollen,—die Grundlage und den Ausgangspunkt der neueren deutschen Philosophie ausmacht, und dieß ihr Verdienst durch das, was an ihr ausgesetzt werden möge, ihr ungeschmälert bleibt. Auch darum ist auf sie in der objektiven Logik häufig Rücksicht zu nehmen, weil sie sich auf wichtige bestimmtere Seiten des Logischen näher einläßt, spätere Darstellungen von Philosophie hingegen dasselbe wenig beachtet, zum Theil oft nur eine rohe,—aber nicht ungerächte,—Verachtung dagegen bewiesen haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"4.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0015","text":"Das bei uns am weitesten verbreitete Philosophiren tritt nicht aus den kantischen Resultaten, daß die Vernunft keinen wahren Gehalt erkennen könne, und in Ansehung der absoluten Wahrheit auf das Glauben zu verweisen sey, heraus. Was aber bei Kant Resultat ist, damit wird in diesem Philosophiren unmittelbar angefangen, damit die vorhergehende Ausführung, aus welche jenes Resultat herkömmt, und welche philosophisches Erkennen ist, vorweggeschnitten. Die kantische Philosophie dient so als ein Polster für die Trägheit des Denkens, die sich damit beruhigt, daß bereits Alles bewiesen und abgethan sey. Für Erkenntniß und einen bestimmten Inhalt des Denkens, der in solcher unfruchtbaren und trockenen Beruhigung sich nicht findet, ist sich daher an jene vorangegangene Ausführung zu wenden.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"4.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0016","text":"[5] Wenn der Ausdruck objektivirendes Thun des Ich an andere Produktionen des Geistes, z.B. die der Phantasie erinnern kann, so ist zu bemerken, daß von einem Bestimmen eines Gegenstandes die Rede ist, insofern dessen Inhalts-Momente nicht dem Gefühl und der Anschauung angehören. Solcher Gegenstand ist ein Gedanke, und ihn bestimmen heißt Theils ihn erst produciren, Theils insofern er ein Vorausgesetztes ist, weitere Gedanken über ihn haben, ihn denkend weiter entwickeln.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"4.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","text":"Indem nun das Interesse der kantischen Philosophie auf das sogenannte Transcendentale der Denkbestimmungen gerichtet war, ist die Abhandlung derselben selbst leer ausgegangen; was sie an ihnen selbst sind, ohne die abstrakte, allen gleiche Relation auf Ich, ihre Bestimmtheit gegen und ihr Verhältniß zu einander ist nicht zu einem Gegenstande der Betrachtung gemacht worden; die Erkenntniß ihrer Natur hat sich daher durch diese Philosophie nicht im geringsten gefördert gefunden. Das einzige Interessante, was hierauf Beziehung hat, kommt in der Kritik der Ideen vor. Für den wirklichen Fortschritt der Philosophie aber war es nothwendig, daß das Interesse des Denkens auf die Betrachtung der formellen Seite, des Ich, des Bewußtseyns als solchen, d.i. der abstrakten Beziehung eines subjektiven Wissens auf ein Objekt, gezogen, daß die Erkenntniß der unendlichen Form, d.i.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"4.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","text":"des Begriffs, auf diese Weise eingeleitet wurde. Um jedoch diese Erkenntniß zu erreichen, mußte jene endliche Bestimmtheit, in der die Form als Ich, Bewußtseyn ist, noch abgestreift werden. Die Form so in ihre Reinheit herausgedacht, enthält es dann in sich selbst, sich zu bestimmen, d.i. sich Inhalt zu geben, und zwar denselben in seiner Nothwendigkeit,—als System der Denkbestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"4.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","text":"Die objektive Logik tritt damit vielmehr an die Stelle der vormaligen Metaphysik, als welche das wissenschaftliche Gebäude über die Welt war, das nur durch Gedanken aufgeführt seyn sollte.—Wenn wir auf die letzte Gestalt der Ausbildung dieser Wissenschaft Rücksicht nehmen, so ist erstens unmittelbar die Ontologie, an deren Stelle die objektive Logik tritt,—der Theil jener Metaphysik, der die Natur des Ens überhaupt erforschen sollte;—das Ens begreift sowohl Seyn als Wesen in sich, für welchen Unterschied unsere Sprache glücklicherweise den verschiedenen Ausdruck gerettet hat.—Alsdann aber begreift die objektive Logik auch die übrige Metaphysik insofern in sich, als diese mit den reinen Denkformen die besondern, zunächst aus der Vorstellung genommenen Substrate, die Seele, die Welt, Gott, zu fassen suchte, und die Bestimmungen des Denkens das Wesentliche der Betrachtungsweise ausmachten.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"4.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","text":"Aber die Logik betrachtet diese Formen frei von jenen Substraten, den Subjekten der Vorstellung, und ihre Natur und Werth an und für sich selbst. Jene Metaphysik unterließ dieß und zog sich daher den gerechten Vorwurf zu, sie ohne Kritik gebraucht zu haben, ohne die vorgängige Untersuchung, ob und wie sie fähig seyen, Bestimmungen des Dings-an-sich, nach kantischem Ausdruck,—oder vielmehr des Vernünftigen zu seyen.—Die objektive Logik ist daher die wahrhafte Kritik derselben,—eine Kritik, die sie nicht nach der abstrakten Form der Apriorität gegen das Aposteriorische, sondern sie selbst in ihrem besondern Inhalte betrachtet.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"4.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","text":"Die subjektive Logik ist die Logik des Begriffs,—des Wesens, das seine Beziehung auf ein Seyn oder seinen Schein aufgehoben hat, und in seiner Bestimmung nicht äußerlich mehr, sondern das freie selbstständig, sich in sich bestimmende Subjektive, oder vielmehr das Subjekt selbst ist.—Indem das Subjektive das Mißverständniß von Zufälligem und Willkürlichem, so wie überhaupt von Bestimmungen, die in die Form des Bewußtseyns gehören, mit sich führt, so ist hier auf den Unterschied von Subjektivem und Objektivem, der sich späterhin innerhalb der Logik selbst näher entwickeln wird, kein besonderes Gewicht zu legen.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"4.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","text":"Die Logik zerfällt also zwar überhaupt in objektive und subjektive Logik, bestimmter aber hat sie die drei Theile:","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"4.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","text":"I. Die Logik des Seyns,","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"4.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","text":"II. die Logik des Wesens und","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"4.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","text":"III. die Logik des Begriffs.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"4.25"}],"sha256":"3f679529b3d55c48078ab4339f7a599f0a1396fa2271bf44310d37d25c214d2a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101558156650Z_092fc1ed","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"General Division of Logic","source_sha256":"3f679529b3d55c48078ab4339f7a599f0a1396fa2271bf44310d37d25c214d2a","sha256":"3c6895d015435baff4f0823abb3a74e2b02abb5d30e899198887cbf6be0909d4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:15:58.156679+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","text":"In what has been said concerning the concept of this science and where its justification falls, it is implied that the general division here can only be provisional, can, as it were, be indicated only insofar as the author already knows the science, and is therefore in a position here to state in advance historically into which principal distinctions the concept will determine itself in its development.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"4.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","text":"Yet an attempt may be made to render intelligible in advance, in general, what is required for dividing, although even in doing so a procedure of the method must be invoked which receives its full elucidation and justification only within the science.—First, then, it is to be recalled that it is here presupposed that the division must be connected with the concept, or rather must lie in it itself. The concept is not indeterminate, but determinate in itself; division, however, articulates this its determinacy in developed form; it is its judgment, not a judgment concerning some externally taken object, but the judging, i.e. determining, of the concept in itself. Right-angledness, acuteness, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"4.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","text":"etc., just as equilateralness, etc., according to which determinations triangles are divided, does not lie in the determinacy of the triangle itself, i.e. not in what is usually called the concept of the triangle, any more than the determinations lie in what constitutes the concept of animal in general, or of mammal, bird, etc., according to which the former is divided into mammals, birds, etc., and these classes into further genera. Such determinations are taken from elsewhere, from empirical intuition; they are added from outside to that so-called concept. In the philosophical treatment of dividing, the concept itself must show itself to contain their origin.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"4.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","text":"But the concept of logic itself has been indicated in the Introduction as the result of a science lying beyond it, and thus here likewise as a presupposition. Accordingly, logic determined itself as the science of pure thinking, which has pure knowing as its principle; not abstract, but a concrete, living unity by virtue of the fact that in it the opposition of consciousness between a subjective—being-for-itself and a second such being, an objective one, is known as overcome, and being as pure concept in itself, and pure concept as true being. These, therefore, are the two moments contained in the logical.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"4.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","text":"But they are now known as inseparable, not as in consciousness each also as being for itself; solely by being known at the same time as distinct (yet not as being for themselves), is their unity not abstract, dead, immobile, but concrete.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"4.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","text":"This unity at the same time constitutes the logical principle as element, so that the development of that distinction which is immediately in it proceeds only within this element. For since division, as has been said, is the judgment of the concept, the positing of the determination already immanent in it and hence of its distinction, this positing must not be conceived as a dissolution back of that concrete unity into its determinations, as though these were to count as being for themselves; that would here be an empty return to the previous standpoint, the opposition of consciousness. This has rather vanished; that unity remains the element, and that distinguishing of division and of development generally no longer emerges from it.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"4.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","text":"Thereby the determinations which formerly (on the path to truth) were beings for themselves, such as a subjective and an objective, or likewise thinking and being, or concept and reality, however they may have been determined in any respect, are now reduced in their truth, i.e. in their unity, to forms. Thus in their distinction they themselves remain in themselves the whole concept, and in division this is posited only under its own determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"4.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","text":"Thus it is the whole concept which is to be considered at one time as being concept, at another as concept; there it is only concept in itself, that of reality or of being; here it is concept as such, concept being for itself (as, to name concrete forms, it is in the thinking human being, but also already, though of course not as conscious and still less as known concept, in the sentient animal, and in organic individuality generally; but it is concept in itself only in inorganic nature).—Accordingly, logic would first be divisible into the logic of concept as being and of concept as concept—or, if we avail ourselves of the otherwise customary, though most indeterminate and therefore most ambiguous, expressions—into objective and subjective logic.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"4.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","text":"But according to the underlying element of the unity of the concept within itself, and hence the inseparability of its determinations, these must further, insofar as they are distinct, insofar as the concept is posited in their distinction, stand at least in relation to one another. From this there results a sphere of mediation, the concept as a system of determinations of reflection, i.e. of being passing over into the being-within-itself of the concept, which in this way is not yet posited as such for itself, but is at the same time still encumbered with immediate being as with something also external to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"4.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","text":"This is the doctrine of essence, which stands midway between the doctrine of being and that of the concept.—In the general division of this logical work it has still been placed under objective logic, insofar as, although essence is already the inward, the character of subject is expressly to be reserved for the concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"4.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","text":"In more recent times Kant [4] has set over against what has commonly been called logic yet another, namely transcendental logic. What has here been called objective logic would in part correspond to what for him is transcendental logic. He distinguishes it from what he calls general logic in that it α) considers concepts which relate a priori to objects, and thus does not abstract from all content of objective cognition, or that it contains the rules of the pure thinking of an object; and β) at the same time goes to the origin of our cognition, insofar as this cannot be ascribed to objects.—It is this second aspect to which Kant’s philosophical interest is exclusively directed. His principal thought is to vindicate the categories for self-consciousness, as the subjective I.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"4.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","text":"By virtue of this determination, the view remains within consciousness and its opposition, and besides the empirical element of feeling and intuition it has something remaining which is not posited and determined by thinking self-consciousness: a thing-in-itself, something alien and external to thinking; although it is easy to see that such an abstractum as thing-in-itself is itself only a product of thinking, and indeed only of abstracting thinking.—If other Kantians have expressed themselves concerning the determination of the object by the I in such a way that the objectifying of the I is to be regarded as an original and necessary activity of consciousness, so that in this original activity the representation of the I itself is not yet present—as this first is a consciousness of that consciousness, or itself an objectifying of that consciousness—then this objectifying activity, freed from the opposition of","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"4.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0013","text":"consciousness, is more nearly that which can be taken for thinking as such in general. [5] But this activity should no longer be called consciousness; consciousness includes within itself the opposition of the I and its object, which is not present in that original activity. The designation consciousness casts even more the appearance of subjectivity upon it than the expression thinking, which, however, is here to be taken generally in the absolute sense as infinite thinking, not encumbered with the finitude of consciousness; in short, thinking as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"4.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0014","text":"[4] I recall that I frequently take account of the Kantian philosophy in this work for the reason that it,—however its more precise determinacy and the particular parts of its execution may otherwise, and also in this work, be regarded,—constitutes the foundation and the point of departure of modern German philosophy, and this its merit remains undiminished by what may be criticized in it. It must also frequently be taken account of in objective logic because it enters more closely into important more determinate aspects of the logical, whereas later presentations of philosophy have paid little heed to it, and in part have often displayed toward it only a crude,—but not unavenged,—contempt.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"4.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0015","text":"The philosophizing most widely disseminated among us does not emerge from the Kantian results that reason can cognize no true content, and that with respect to absolute truth one must refer to faith. But what in Kant is a result is immediately begun with in this philosophizing; thereby the preceding exposition, from which that result derives, and which is philosophical cognition, is cut off in advance. Kantian philosophy thus serves as a cushion for the indolence of thinking, which reassures itself that everything has already been proved and disposed of. For cognition and for a determinate content of thought, which is not to be found in such barren and dry reassurance, one must therefore turn to that preceding exposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"4.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0016","text":"[5] If the expression objectifying activity of the I can recall other productions of spirit, e.g. those of imagination, it should be noted that there is talk of a determining of an object insofar as its moments of content do not belong to feeling and intuition. Such an object is a thought, and to determine it means partly first to produce it, partly, insofar as it is something presupposed, to have further thoughts concerning it, to develop it further in thinking.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"4.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","text":"Now, since the interest of Kantian philosophy was directed toward the so-called transcendental aspect of the determinations of thought, the treatment of these itself came away empty-handed; what they are in themselves, apart from the abstract relation to the I, the same for all, their determinacy over against and their relation to one another, was not made an object of consideration; cognition of their nature has therefore not been advanced in the least by this philosophy. The only thing of interest that relates to this occurs in the Critique of Ideas. But for the actual progress of philosophy it was necessary that the interest of thinking be drawn to the consideration of the formal aspect, of the I, of consciousness as such, i.e. of the abstract relation of a subjective knowing to an object; that cognition of the infinite form, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"4.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","text":"of the concept, be thus introduced. Yet in order to attain this cognition, that finite determinacy in which form is I, consciousness, had still to be stripped off. When form is thus thought out into its purity, it then contains within itself the capacity to determine itself, i.e. to give itself content, and indeed this content in its necessity—as a system of determinations of thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"4.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","text":"Objective logic thereby takes the place rather of the former metaphysics, which was the scientific edifice concerning the world, meant to be erected solely by means of thoughts.—If we take account of the last form of development of this science, then first of all there is ontology, in whose place objective logic steps—the part of that metaphysics which was meant to investigate the nature of ens in general; ens comprehends within itself both being and essence, for which distinction our language has fortunately preserved the distinct expression.—But then objective logic also comprehends the rest of metaphysics insofar as the latter sought to grasp, with the pure forms of thought, the particular substrates taken initially from representation—the soul, the world, God—and the determinations of thought constituted the essential element of its mode of consideration.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"4.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","text":"But logic considers these forms free of those substrates, the subjects of representation, and considers their nature and value in and for themselves. That metaphysics omitted this, and hence incurred the justified reproach that it had used them without criticism, without the prior investigation whether and how they were capable of being determinations of the thing-in-itself, in Kantian expression—or rather, of the rational.—Objective logic is therefore their true critique: a critique which considers them not according to the abstract form of apriority as against the a posteriori, but considers them themselves in their particular content.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"4.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","text":"Subjective logic is the logic of the concept,—of the essence which has sublated its relation to a being or to its semblance, and in its determinacy is no longer external, but is the free, self-subsistent subjective determining itself within itself, or rather is the subject itself.—Since the subjective carries with it the misunderstanding of the contingent and arbitrary, as well as generally of determinations belonging to the form of consciousness, no special weight is to be laid here on the distinction between subjective and objective, which will later develop more precisely within logic itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"4.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","text":"Thus logic does indeed generally divide into objective and subjective logic, but more determinately it has the three parts:","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"4.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","text":"I. The logic of being,","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"4.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","text":"II. the logic of essence and","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"4.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","text":"III. the Logic of the Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"4.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025"]}],"source_digest":"5034eebf18b8fd7be6c449a43e557987d8625a7bb42028545623def663e3482c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung der Logik"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung der Logik","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA","title":"With What Must the Science Begin?","order":5,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_WMDA","text":"## Erstes Buch Die Lehre vom Seyn.\n\n## Womit muß der Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht werden?\n\nIn neuern Zeiten erst ist das Bewußtseyn entstanden, daß es eine Schwierigkeit sey, einen Anfang in der Philosophie zu finden, und der Grund dieser Schwierigkeit so wie die Möglichkeit, sie zu lösen, ist vielfältig besprochen worden. Der Anfang der Philosophie muß entweder ein Vermitteltes oder Unmittelbares seyn, und es ist leicht zu zeigen, daß es weder das Eine noch das Andere seyn könne; somit findet die eine oder die andere Weise des Anfangens ihre Widerlegung.\n\nDas Princip einer Philosophie drückt wohl auch einen Anfang aus, aber nicht sowohl einen subjektiven als objektiven, den Anfang aller Dinge. Das Princip ist ein irgendwie bestimmter Inhalt,—das Wasser, das Eine, Nus, Idee,—Substanz, Monade u.s.f., oder wenn es sich auf die Natur des Erkennens bezieht und damit mehr nur ein Kriterium als eine objektive Bestimmung seyn soll Denken, Anschauen, Empfinden, Ich, die Subjektivität selbst, so ist es hier gleichfalls die Inhaltsbestimmung, auf welche das Interesse geht. Das Anfangen als solches dagegen bleibt als ein Subjektives in dem Sinne einer zufälligen Art und Weise, den Vortrag einzuleiten, unbeachtet und gleichgültig, somit auch das Bedürfniß der Frage, womit anzufangen sey, unbedeutend gegen das Bedürfniß des Princips, als in welchem allein das Interesse der Sache zu liegen scheint, das Interesse, was das Wahre, was der absolute Grund von Allem sey.\n\nAber die moderne Verlegenheit um den Anfang geht aus einem weiteren Bedürfnisse hervor, welches diejenigen noch nicht kennen, denen es dogmatisch um das Erweisen des Princips zu thun ist, oder skeptisch um das Finden eines subjektiven Kriteriums gegen dogmatisches Philosophiren und welches diejenigen ganz verleugnen, die wie aus der Pistole, aus ihrer innern Offenbarung, aus Glauben, intellektueller Anschauung u.s.w. anfangen, und der Methode und Logik überhoben seyn wollten. Wenn das früher abstrakte Denken zunächst nur für das Princip als Inhalt sich interessirt, aber im Fortgange der Bildung auf die andere Seite, auf das Benehmen des Erkennens zu achten getrieben ist, so wird auch das subjektive Thun als wesentliches Moment der objektiven Wahrheit erfaßt, und das Bedürfniß führt sich herbei, daß die Methode mit dem Inhalt, die Form mit dem Princip vereint sey. So soll das Princip auch Anfang und das, was das Prius für das Denken ist, auch das Erste im Gange des Denkens seyn.\n\nEs ist hier nur zu betrachten, wie der logische Anfang erscheint; die beiden Seiten, nach denen er genommen werden kann, sind schon genannt, entweder als Resultat auf vermittelte, oder als eigentlicher Anfang auf unmittelbare Weise. Die in der Bildung der Zeit so wichtig erscheinende Frage, ob das Wissen der Wahrheit ein unmittelbares, schlechthin anfangendes Wissen, ein Glauben, oder aber ein vermitteltes Wissen sey, ist an diesem Orte nicht zu erörtern. Insofern solche Betrachtung vorläufig angestellt werden kann, ist dieß anderwärts (in m. Encykl. der philos. Wissenschaf. 3te Ausg. im Vorbegr. §. 61. ff.) geschehen. Hier mag daraus nur dieß angeführt werden, daß es Nichts giebt, nichts im Himmel oder in der Natur oder im Geiste oder wo es sey, was nicht ebenso die Unmittelbarkeit enthält, als die Vermittelung, so daß sich diese beiden Bestimmungen als ungetrennt und untrennbar und jener Gegensatz sich als ein Richtiges zeigt. Was aber die wissenschaftliche Erörterung betrifft, so ist es jeder logische Satz, in welchem die Bestimmungen der Unmittelbarkeit und der Vermittelung und also die Erörterung ihres Gegensatzes und ihrer Wahrheit vorkommt. Insofern dieser Gegensatz in Beziehung auf Denken, Wissen, Erkennen, die konkretere Gestalt von unmittelbarem oder vermitteltem Wissen erhält, wird die Natur des Erkennens überhaupt, sowohl innerhalb der Wissenschaft der Logik betrachtet, als dasselbe in seiner weitern konkreten Form, in die Wissenschaft vom Geiste, und in die Phänomenologie desselben fällt. Vor der Wissenschaft aber schon über das Erkennen ins Reine kommen wollen, heißt verlangen, daß es außerhalb derselben erörtert werden sollte; außerhalb der Wissenschaft läßt sich dieß wenigstens nicht auf wissenschaftliche Weise, um die es hier allein zu thun ist, bewerkstelligen.\n\nLogisch ist der Anfang, indem er im Element des frei für sich seyenden Denkens, im reinen Wissen gemacht werden soll. Vermittelt ist es hiermit dadurch, daß das reine Wissen die letzte, absolute Wahrheit des Bewußtseyns ist. Es ist in der Einleitung bemerkt, daß die Phänomenologie des Geistes die Wissenschaft des Bewußtseyns, die Darstellung davon ist, daß das Bewußtseyn den Begriff der Wissenschaft, d.i. das reine Wissen, zum Resultate hat. Die Logik hat insofern die Wissenschaft des erscheinenden Geistes zu ihrer Voraussetzung, welche die Nothwendigkeit und damit den Beweis der Wahrheit des Standpunkts, der das reine Wissen ist, wie dessen Vermittelung überhaupt, enthält und aufzeigt. In dieser Wissenschaft des erscheinenden Geistes wird von dem empirischen, sinnlichen Bewußtseyn ausgegangen; und dieses ist das eigentliche unmittelbare Wissen; daselbst wird erörtert, was an diesem unmittelbaren Wissen ist. Anderes Bewußtseyn, wie der Glaube an göttliche Wahrheiten, innere Erfahrung, Wissen durch innere Offenbarung u.s.f. zeigt sich bei geringer Überlegung sehr uneigentlich als unmittelbares Wissen aufgeführt zu werden. In jener Abhandlung ist das unmittelbare Bewußtseyn auch das in der Wissenschaft Erste und Unmittelbare, somit die Voraussetzung; in der Logik aber ist dasjenige die Voraussetzung, was aus jener Betrachtung sich als das Resultat erwiesen hatte,—die Idee als reines Wissen. Die Logik, ist die reine Wissenschaft, d.i. das reine Wissen in dem ganzen Umfange seiner Entwickelung. Diese Idee aber hat sich in jenem Resultate dahin bestimmt, die zur Wahrheit gewordenen Gewißheit zu seyn, die Gewißheit, die nach der einen Seite dem Gegenstande nicht mehr gegenüber ist, sondern ihn innerlich gemacht hat, ihn als sich selbst weiß,—und die auf der andern Seite das Wissen von sich als von einem, das dem Gegenständlichen gegenüber und nur dessen Vernichtung sey, aufgegeben, dieser Subjektivität entäußert und Einheit mit seiner Entäußerung ist.\n\nDaß nun von dieser Bestimmung des reinen Wissens aus der Anfang seiner Wissenschaft immanent bleibe, ist nichts zu thun, als das zu betrachten oder vielmehr mit Beiseitsetzung aller Reflexionen, aller Meinungen, die man sonst hat, nur aufzunehmen was vorhanden ist.\n\nDas reine Wissen als in diese Einheit zusammengegangen, hat alle Beziehung auf ein Anderes und auf Vermittelung aufgehoben; es ist das Unterschiedslose; dieses Unterschiedslose hört somit selbst auf, Wissen zu seyn; es ist nur einfache Unmittelbarkeit vorhanden.\n\nDie einfache Unmittelbarkeit ist selbst ein Reflexionsausdruck, und bezieht sich auf den Unterschied von dem Vermittelten. In ihrem wahren Ausdrucke ist daher diese einfache Unmittelbarkeit das reine Seyn. Wie das reine Wissen nichts heißen soll, als das Wissen als solches, ganz abstrakt, so soll auch reines Seyn nichts heißen, als das Seyn überhaupt; Seyn, sonst nichts, ohne alle weitere Bestimmung und Erfüllung.\n\nHier ist das Seyn das Anfangende, als durch Vermittelung und zwar durch sie, welche zugleich Aufheben ihrer selbst ist, entstanden, dargestellt; mit der Voraussetzung des reinen Wissens als Resultats des endlichen Wissens, des Bewußtseyns. Soll aber keine Voraussetzung gemacht, der Anfang selbst unmittelbar genommen werden, so bestimmt er sich nur dadurch, daß es der Anfang der Logik des Denkens für sich, seyn soll. Nur der Entschluß, den man auch für eine Willkür ansehen kann, nämlich daß man das Denken als solches betrachten wolle, ist vorhanden. So muß der Anfang absoluter oder was hier gleichbedeutend ist, abstrakter Anfang seyn; er darf so nichts voraussetzen, muß durch nichts vermittelt seyn, noch einen Grund haben; er soll vielmehr selbst Grund der ganzen Wissenschaft seyn. Er muß daher schlechthin ein Unmittelbares seyn, oder vielmehr nur das Unmittelbare selbst. Wie er nicht gegen Anderes eine Bestimmung haben kann, so kann er auch keine in sich, keinen Inhalt enthalten, denn dergleichen wäre Unterscheidung und Beziehung von Verschiedenem aufeinander, somit eine Vermittelung. Der Anfang ist also das reine Seyn.\n\nNach dieser einfachen Darlegung dessen, was zunächst nur zu diesem selbst Allereinfachsten, dem logischen Anfang, gehört, können noch folgende weitere Reflexionen beigebracht werden; doch können sie nicht sowohl zur Erläuterung und Bestätigung jener Darlegung, die für sich fertig ist, dienen sollen, als sie vielmehr nur durch Vorstellungen und Reflexionen veranlaßt werden, die uns zum Voraus in den Weg kommen können, jedoch, wie alle andere vorangehende Vorurtheile, in der Wissenschaft selbst ihr Erledigung finden müssen, und daher eigentlich zur Geduld hierauf zu verweisen wären.\n\nDie Einsicht, daß das Absolut-Wahre ein Resultat seyn müsse, und umgekehrt, daß ein Resultat ein erstes Wahres voraussetzt, das aber, weil es Erstes ist, objektiv betrachtet, nicht nothwendig, und nach der subjektiven Seite, nicht erkannt ist,—hat in neuern Zeiten den Gedanken hervorgebracht, daß die Philosophie nur mit einem hypothetischen und problematischen Wahren anfangen, und das Philosophiren daher zuerst nur ein Suchen seyn könne, eine Ansicht, welche Reinhold in den spätern Zeiten seines Philosphirens vielfach urgiert hat, und der man die Gerechtigkeit widerfahren lassen muß, daß ihr ein wahrhaftes Interesse zu Grunde liegt, welches die spekulative Natur des philosophischen Anfangs betrifft. Die Auseinandersetzung dieser Ansicht ist zugleich eine Veranlassung, ein vorläufiges Verständniß über den Sinn des logischen Fortschreitens überhaupt, einzuleiten; denn jene Ansicht schließt die Rücksicht auf das Fortgehen sogleich in sich. Und zwar stellt sie es so vor, daß das Vorwärtsschreiten in der Philosophie vielmehr ein Rückwärtsgehen und Begründen sey, durch welches erst sich ergebe, daß das, womit angefangen wurde, nicht bloß ein willkürlich Angenommenes, sondern in der That Theils das Wahre, Theils das erste Wahre sey.\n\nMan muß zugeben, daß es eine wesentliche Betrachtung ist,—die sich innerhalb der Logik selbst näher ergeben wird,—daß das Vorwärtsgehen ein Rückgang in den Grund, zu dem Ursprünglichen und Wahrhaften ist, von dem das, womit der Anfang gemacht wurde, abhängt, und in der That hervorgebracht wird.—So wird das Bewußtseyn auf seinem Wege von der Unmittelbarkeit aus, mit der es anfängt, zum absoluten Wissen, als seiner innersten Wahrheit, zurückgeführt. Dieß Letzte, der Grund, ist denn auch dasjenige, aus welchem das Erste hervorgeht, das zuerst als Unmittelbares auftrat.—So wird noch mehr der absolute Geist, der als die konkrete und letzte höchste Wahrheit alles Seyns sich ergiebt, erkannt, als am Ende der Entwickelung sich mit Freiheit entäußernd und sich zur Gestalt eines unmittelbaren Seyns entlassend,—zur Schöpfung einer Welt sich entschließend, welche alles das enthält, was in die Entwickelung, die jenem Resultate vorangegangen, fiel, und das durch diese umgekehrte Stellung, mit seinem Anfang in ein von dem Resultate als dem Principe Abhängiges verwandelt wird. Das Wesentliche für die Wissenschaft, ist nicht so sehr, daß ein rein Unmittelbares der Anfang sey, sondern daß das Ganze derselben ein Kreislauf in sich selbst ist, worin das Erste auch das Letzte, und das Letzte auch das Erste wird.\n\nDaher ergiebt sich auf der andern Seite als ebenso nothwendig, dasjenige, in welches die Bewegung als in seinen Grund zurückgeht, als Resultat zu betrachten. Nach dieser Rücksicht ist das Erste ebenso sehr der Grund, und das Letzte ein Abgeleitetes; indem von dem Ersten ausgegangen und durch richtige Folgerung auf das Letzte, als auf den Grund, gekommen wird, ist dieser Resultat. Der Fortgang ferner von dem, was den Anfang macht, ist nur als eine weitere Bestimmung desselben zu betrachten, so daß das Anfangende allem Folgenden zu Grunde liegen bleibt, und nichts daraus verschwindet. Das Fortgehen besteht nicht darin, daß nur ein Anderes abgeleitet, oder daß in ein wahrhaft Anderes übergegangen würde;—und insofern dieß Übergehen vorkommt, so hebt es sich ebenso sehr wieder auf. So ist der Anfang der Philosophie, die in allen folgenden Entwickelungen gegenwärtige und sich erhaltende Grundlage, das seinen weiteren Bestimmungen durchaus immanent Bleibende.\n\nDurch diesen Fortgang denn verliert der Anfang das, was er in dieser Bestimmtheit, ein Unmittelbares und Abstraktes überhaupt zu seyn, einseitiges hat; er wird ein Vermitteltes, und die Linie der wissenschaftlichen Fortbewegung macht sich damit zu einem Kreise. —Zugleich ergiebt sich, daß das, was den Anfang macht, indem es darin das noch Unentwickelte, Inhaltlose ist, im Anfange noch nicht wahrhaft erkannt wird, und daß erst die Wissenschaft, und zwar in ihrer ganzen Entwickelung, seine vollendete, inhaltsvolle und erst wahrhaft begründete Erkenntniß ist.\n\nDarum aber, weil das Resultat erst als der absolute Grund hervortritt, ist das Fortschreiten dieses Erkennens nicht etwas Provisorisches, noch ein problematisches und hypothetisches, sondern es muß durch die Natur der Sache und des Inhaltes selbst bestimmt seyn. Weder ist jener Anfang etwas Willkürliches und nur einstweilen Angenommenes, noch ein als willkürlich Erscheinendes und bittweise Vorausgesetztes, von dem sich aber doch in der Folge zeige, daß man Recht daran gethan habe, es zum Anfange zu machen; nicht wie bei den Konstruktionen, die man zum Behuf des Beweises eines geometrischen Satzes zu machen angewiesen wird, es der Fall ist, daß von ihnen es sich erst hinterher an den Beweisen ergiebt, daß man wohlgethan habe, gerade diese Linien zu ziehen, und dann in den Beweisen selbst, mit der Vergleichung dieser Linien oder Winkel anzufangen; für sich an diesem Linienziehen oder Vergleichen begreift es sich nicht. So ist vorhin der Grund, warum in der reinen Wissenschaft vom reinen Seyn angefangen wird, unmittelbar an ihr selbst angegeben worden. Dieß reine Seyn ist die Einheit, in die das reine Wissen zurückgeht, oder wenn dieses selbst noch als Form von seiner Einheit unterschieden gehalten werden soll, so ist es auch der Inhalt desselben. Dieß ist die Seite, nach welcher dieß reine Seyn, dieß Absolut-Unmittelbare, ebenso absolut Vermitteltes ist. Aber es muß ebenso wesentlich nur in der Einseitigkeit, das Rein-Unmittelbare zu seyn, genommen werden, eben weil es hier als der Anfang ist. Insofern es nicht diese reinen Unbestimmtheit, insofern es bestimmt wäre, würde es als Vermitteltes, schon weiter Geführtes, genommen; ein Bestimmtes enthält ein Anderes zu einem Ersten. Es liegt also in der Natur des Anfangs selbst, daß er das Seyn sey, und sonst nichts. Es bedarf daher keiner sonstigen Vorbereitungen, um in die Philosophie hineinzukommen, noch anderweitiger Reflexionen und Anknüpfungspunkte.\n\nDaß der Anfang, Anfang der Philosophie ist, daraus kann eigentlich auch keine nähere Bestimmung oder ein positiver Inhalt für denselben genommen werden. Denn die Philosophie ist hier im Anfange, wo die Sache selbst noch nicht vorhanden ist, ein leeres Wort oder irgend eine angenommene ungerechtfertigte Vorstellung. Das reine Wissen giebt nur diese negative Bestimmung, daß er der abstrakte Anfang seyn soll. Insofern das reine Seyn als Inhalt des reinen Wissens genommen wird, so hat dieses von seinem Inhalte zurückzutreten, ihn für sich selbst gewähren zu lassen und nicht weiter zu bestimmen.—Oder indem das reine Seyn als die Einheit zu betrachten ist, in die das Wissen, auf seiner höchsten Spitze der Einigung mit dem Objekte, zusammengefallen, so ist das Wissen in diese Einheit verschwunden, und hat keinen Unterschied von ihr und somit keine Bestimmung für sich übrig gelassen.—Auch sonst ist nicht Etwas, oder irgend ein Inhalt vorhanden, der gebracht werden könnte, um damit den bestimmteren Anfang zu machen.\n\nAber auch die bisher als Anfang angenommmene Bestimmung des Seyns könnte weggelassen werden, so daß nur gefordert würde, daß ein reiner Anfang gemacht werde. Dann ist nichts vorhanden, als der Anfang selbst, und es wäre zu sehen, was er ist.—Diese Stellung könnte zugleich als ein Vorschlag zur Güte an diejenigen gemacht werden, welche Theils damit, daß mit dem Seyn angefangen werde, aus welchen Reflexionen es sey, sich nicht beruhigen und noch weniger mit dem Erfolge, den das Seyn hat, in das Nichts überzugehn,—Theils überhaupt nicht anders wissen, als daß in einer Wissenschaft mit der Voraussetzung einer Vorstellung angefangen werde,—einer Vorstellung, welche hierauf analysirt werde, so daß nun das Ergebniß solcher Analyse den ersten bestimmten Begriff in der Wissenschaft abgebe. Indem wir auch dieß Verfahren beobachteten, so hätten wir keinen besondern Gegenstand, weil der Anfang als des Denkens, ganz abstrakt, ganz allgemein, ganz Form ohne allen Inhalt seyn soll; wir hätten somit gar nichts, als die Vorstellung von einem bloßen Anfang als solchem. Es ist also nur zu sehen, was wir in dieser Vorstellung haben.\n\nEs ist noch Nichts, und es soll Etwas werden. Der Anfang ist nicht das reine Nichts, sondern ein Nichts, von dem Etwas ausgehen soll; das Seyn ist also auch schon im Anfang enthalten. Der Anfang enthält also Beides, Seyn und Nichts; ist die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts; —oder ist Nichtseyn, das zugleich Seyn, und Seyn, das zugleich Nichtseyn ist.\n\nFerner Seyn und Nichts sind im Anfang als unterschieden vorhanden; denn er weißt auf etwas Anderes hin;—er ist ein Nichtseyn, das auf das Seyn als auf ein Anderes bezogen ist; das Anfangende ist noch nicht; es geht erst dem Seyn zu. Der Anfang enthält also das Seyn als ein solches, das sich von dem Nichtseyn entfernt oder es aufhebt, als ein ihm Entgegengesetztes.\n\nFerner aber ist das, was anfängt, schon, eben so sehr aber ist es auch noch nicht. Die Entgegengesetzten, Seyn und Nichtseyn sind also in ihm in unmittelbarer Vereinigung; oder er ist ihre ununterschiedene Einheit.\n\nDie Analyse des Anfangs gäbe somit den Begriff der Einheit des Seyns und des Nichtseyns,—oder in reflektirterer Form, der Einheit des Unterschieden—und des Nichtunterschiedenseyns,—oder der Identität der Identität und Nichtidentität. Dieser Begriff könnte als die erste, reinste d.i. abstrakteste, Definition des Absoluten angesehen werden;—wie er dieß in der That seyn würde, wenn es überhaupt um die Form von Definitionen und um den Namen des Absoluten zu thun wäre. In diesem Sinne würden, wie jener abstrakte Begriff die erste, so alle weitern Bestimmungen und Entwickelungen nur bestimmtere und reichere Definitionen dieses Absoluten seyn. Aber die, welche mit dem Seyn als Anfang darum nicht zufrieden sind, weil es in Nichts übergeht, und daraus die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts entsteht, mögen zusehen, ob sie mit diesem Anfange, der mit der Vorstellung des Anfangs anfängt, und mit deren Analyse, die wohl richtig seyn wird, aber gleichfalls auf die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts führt, zufriedener seyn mögen, als damit, daß das Seyn zum Anfange gemacht wird.\n\nEs ist aber noch einen weitere Betrachtung über dieses Verfahren zu machen. Jene Analyse setzt die Vorstellung des Anfangs als bekannt voraus; es ist so nach dem Beispiele anderer Wissenschaften verfahren worden. Diese setzen ihren Gegenstand voraus, und nehmen bittweise an, daß jedermann dieselbe Vorstellung von ihm habe, und darin ungefähr dieselben Bestimmungen finden möge, die sie durch Analyse, Vergleichung und sonstiges Raisonnement von ihm da und dorther beibringen und angeben. Das aber, was den absoluten Anfang macht, muß gleichfalls ein sonst Bekanntes seyn; wenn es nun ein Konkretes, somit in sich mannigfaltig Bestimmtes ist, so ist diese Beziehung, die es in sich ist, als etwas Bekanntes vorausgesetzt; sie ist damit als etwas Unmittelbares angegeben, was sie aber nicht ist; denn sie ist nur Beziehung als von Unterschiedenen, enthält somit die Vermittelung in sich. Ferner tritt am Konkreten die Zufälligkeit und Willkür der Analyse und des verschiedenen Bestimmtes ein. Welche Bestimmungen herausgebracht werden, hängt von dem ab, was jeder in seiner unmittelbaren zufälligen Vorstellung vorfindet. Die in einem Konkreten, einer synthetischen Einheit, enthaltene Beziehung ist eine nothwendige nur, insofern sie nicht vorgefunden, sondern durch die eigenen Bewegung der Momente, in diese Einheit zurück zu gehen, hervorgebracht ist;—eine Bewegung, die das Gegentheil des analytischen Verfahrens ist, eines der Sache selbst äußerlichen, in das Subjekt fallenden Thuns.\n\nHierin ist auch das Nähere enthalten, daß das, womit der Anfang zu machen ist, nicht ein Konkretes, nicht ein solches seyn kann, das eine Beziehung innerhalb seiner selbst enthält. Denn ein solches setzt ein Vermitteln und Herübergehen von einem Ersten zu einem Anderen innerhalb seiner, voraus, wovon das einfachgewordene Konkrete das Resultat wäre. Aber der Anfang soll nicht selbst schon ein Erstes und ein Anders seyn; ein solches das ein Erstes und ein Anderes in sich ist, enthält bereits ein Fortgegangenseyn. Was den Anfang macht, der Anfang selbst, ist daher als ein Nichtanalysirbares, in seiner einfachen unerfüllten Unmittelbarkeit, also als Seyn, als das ganz Leere zu nehmen.\n\nWenn man etwa, gegen die Betrachtung des abstrakten Anfangs ungeduldig, sagen wollte, es solle nicht mit dem Anfange angefangen werden, sondern geradezu mit der Sache, so ist diese Sache nichts als jenes leere Seyn; denn was die Sache sey, dieß ist es, was sich eben erst im Verlaufe der Wissenschaft ergeben soll, was nicht vor ihr als bekannt vorausgesetzt werden kann.\n\nWelche Form sonst genommen werde, um einen andern Anfang zu haben, als das leere Seyn, so leidet er an den angeführten Mängeln. Diejenigen, welche mit diesem Anfange unzufrieden bleiben, mögen sich zu der Aufgabe auffordern, es anders anzufangen, um dabei diese Mängel zu vermeiden.\n\nEin origineller Anfang der Philosophie aber kann nicht ganz unerwähnt gelassen werden, der sich in neuerer Zeit berühmt gemacht hat, der Anfang mit dem Ich. Er kam Theils aus der Reflexion, daß aus dem ersten Wahren alles Folgende abgeleitet werden müsse, Theils aus dem Bedürfnisse, daß das erste Wahre ein Bekanntes und noch mehr ein unmittelbar Gewisses sey. Dieser Anfang ist im Allgemeinen nicht eine solche Vorstellung, die zufällig ist, und in einem Subjekte so, in einem andern anders, beschaffen seyn kann. Denn Ich, dieß unmittelbare Selbstbewußtseyn, erscheint zunächst selbst Theils als ein Unmittelbares, Theils als ein in einem viel höhern Sinne Bekanntes, als eine sonstige Vorstellung; etwas sonst Bekanntes gehört zwar dem Ich an, aber ist noch ein von ihm unterschiedener, damit sogleich zufälliger Inhalt; Ich hingegen ist die einfache Gewißheit seiner selbst. Aber Ich überhaupt ist auch zugleich ein Konkretes, oder Ich ist vielmehr das Konkreteste,—das Bewußtseyn seiner, als unendlich mannigfaltiger Welt. Daß Ich Anfang und Grund der Philosophie sey, dazu wird die Absonderung dieses Konkreten erfordert,—der absolute Akt, wodurch Ich von sich selbst gereinigt wird, und als abstraktes Ich in sein Bewußtseyn tritt. Allein dieß reine Ich ist nun nicht ein unmittelbares, noch das bekannte, das gewöhnliche Ich unsers Bewußtseyns, woran unmittelbar und für jede die Wissenschaft angeknüpft werden sollte. Jener Akt wäre eigentlich nichts Anderes, als die Erhebung auf den Standpunkt des reinen Wissens, auf welchem der Unterschied des Subjektiven und Objektiven verschwunden ist. Aber wie diese Erhebung so unmittelbar gefordert ist, ist sie ein subjektives Postulat; um als wahrhafte Forderung sich zu erweisen, müßte die Fortbewegung des konkreten Ichs vom unmittelbaren Bewußtseyn zum reinen Wissen an ihm selbst, durch seine eigene Nothwendigkeit, aufgezeigt und dargestellt worden seyn. Ohne diese objektive Bewegung erscheint das reine Wissen, auch als die intellektuelle Anschauung bestimmt, als ein willkürlicher Standpunkt, oder selbst als einer der empirischen Zustände des Bewußtseyns, in Rücksicht dessen es darauf ankommt, ob ihn der Eine in sich vorfinde oder hervorbringen könne, ein Anderer aber nicht. Insofern aber dieß reine Ich das wesentliche reine Wissen seyn muß, und das reine Wissen aber nur durch den absoluten Akt der Selbsterhebung im individuellen Bewußtseyn gesetzt wird, und nicht unmittelbar in ihm vorhanden ist, geht gerade der Vortheil verloren, der aus diesem Anfange der Philosophie entspringen soll, daß er nämlich etwas schlechthin Bekanntes sey, was jeder unmittelbar in sich finde, und daran die weitere Reflexion anknüpfen könne; jenes reine Ich ist vielmehr in seiner abstrakten Wesenheit, etwas dem gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn Unbekanntes, etwas, das es nicht darin vorfindet. Damit tritt vielmehr der Nachtheil der Täuschung ein, daß von etwas Bekanntem, dem Ich des empirischen Selbstbewußtseyns die Rede seyn solle, indem in der That von etwas diesem Bewußtseyn Fernem die Rede ist. Die Bestimmung des reinen Wissens als Ich, führt die fortdauernde Rückerinnerung an das subjektive Ich mit sich, dessen Schranken vergessen werden sollen, und erhält die Vorstellung gegenwärtig, als ob die Sätze und Verhältnisse, die sich in der weitern Entwickelung vom Ich ergeben, im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn, da es ja das sey, von dem sie behauptet werden, vorkommen und darin vorgefunden werden können. Diese Verwechslung bringt statt unmittelbarer Klarheit vielmehr nur eine um so grellere Verwirrung und gänzliche Desorientirung hervor; nach Außen hat sie vollends die gröbsten Mißverständnisse veranlaßt.\n\nWas ferner die subjektive Bestimmtheit des Ich überhaupt betrifft, so benimmt wohl das reine Wissen dem Ich seine beschränkte Bedeutung, an einem Objekte seinen unüberwindlichen Gegensatz zu haben. Aus diesem Grunde wäre es aber wenigstens überflüssig, noch diese subjektive Haltung und die Bestimmung des reinen Wesens als Ich, beizubehalten. Allein diese Bestimmung führt nicht nur jene störende Zweideutigkeit mit sich, sondern sie bleibt auch, näher betrachtet, ein subjektives Ich. Die wirkliche Entwickelung der Wissenschaft, die vom Ich ausgeht, zeigt es, daß das Objekt darin die perennirende Bestimmung eines Anderen für das Ich hat und behält, daß also das Ich, von dem ausgegangen wird, nicht das reine Wissen, das den Gegensatz des Bewußtseyns in Wahrheit überwunden hat, sondern noch in der Erscheinung befangen ist.\n\nEs ist hierbei noch die wesentliche Bemerkung in machen, daß wenn an sich wohl Ich als das reinen Wissen oder als intellektuelle Anschauung bestimmt und als Anfang behauptet werden könnte, daß es in der Wissenschaft nicht um das zu thun ist, was an sich oder innerlich vorhanden sey, sondern um das Daseyn des Innerlichen im Denken, und um die Bestimmtheit, die ein solches in diesem Daseyn hat. Was aber von der intellektuellen Anschauung—oder wenn ihr Gegenstand das Ewige, das Göttliche, das Absolute genannt wird,—was vom Ewigen oder Absoluten im Anfange der Wissenschaft da ist, dieß kann nichts Anderes seyn, als erste, unmittelbare, einfache Bestimmung. Welcher reichere Name ihm gegeben werde, als das bloße Seyn ausdrückt, so kann nur in Betracht kommen, wie solches Absolute in das denkende Wissen und in das Aussprechen dieses Wissens eintritt. Die intellektuelle Anschauung ist wohl die gewaltsame Zurückweisung des Vermittelns und der beweisenden, äußerlichen Reflexion. Was sie aber mehr ausspricht, als einfache Unmittelbarkeit, ist ein Konkretes, ein in sich verschiedene Bestimmungen Enthaltendes. Das Aussprechen und die Darstellung eines solchen jedoch ist, wie schon bemerkt, eine vermittelnde Bewegung, die von einer der Bestimmungen anfängt, und zu der anderen fortgeht, wenn diese auch zur ersten zurückgeht;—es ist eine Bewegung, die zugleich nicht willkürlich oder assertorisch seyn darf. Von was daher in solcher Darstellung angefangen wird, ist nicht das Konkrete selbst, sondern nur das einfache Unmittelbare, von dem die Bewegung ausgeht. Außerdem fehlt, wenn ein Konkretes zum Anfange gemacht wird, der Beweis, dessen die Verbindung der im Konkreten enthaltenen Bestimmungen bedarf.\n\nWenn also im Ausdrucke des Absoluten oder Ewigen oder Gottes (und das unbestrittenste Recht hätte Gott, daß mit ihm der Anfang gemacht werde), wenn in deren Anschauung oder Gedanken mehr liegt, als im reinen Seyn, so soll das, was darin liegt, ins Wissen als denkendes, nicht vorstellendes erst hervortreten; das was darin liegt, es sey so reich, als es wolle, so ist die Bestimmung, die ins Wissen zuerst hervortritt, ein Einfaches; denn nur im Einfachen ist nicht mehr als der reine Anfang; nur das Unmittelbare ist einfach, denn nur im Unmittelbaren ist noch nicht ein Fortgegangenseyn von Einem zu einem Anderen. Was somit über das Seyn ausgesprochen oder enthalten seyn soll, in den reicheren Formen des Vorstellens von Absolutem oder Gott, dieß ist im Anfange nur leeres Wort, und nur Seyn; dieß Einfache, das sonst keine weitere Bedeutung hat, dieß Leere ist also schlechthin der Anfang der Philosophie.\n\nDiese Einsicht ist selbst so einfach, daß dieser Anfang als solcher, keiner Vorbereitung noch weiteren Einleitung bedarf; und diese Vorläufigkeit von Raisonnement über ihn konnte nicht die Absicht haben, ihn herbeizuführen, als vielmehr alle Vorläufigkeit zu entfernen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0001","text":"## Erstes Buch Die Lehre vom Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"5.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0002","text":"## Womit muß der Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht werden?","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"5.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","text":"In neuern Zeiten erst ist das Bewußtseyn entstanden, daß es eine Schwierigkeit sey, einen Anfang in der Philosophie zu finden, und der Grund dieser Schwierigkeit so wie die Möglichkeit, sie zu lösen, ist vielfältig besprochen worden. Der Anfang der Philosophie muß entweder ein Vermitteltes oder Unmittelbares seyn, und es ist leicht zu zeigen, daß es weder das Eine noch das Andere seyn könne; somit findet die eine oder die andere Weise des Anfangens ihre Widerlegung.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"5.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004","text":"Das Princip einer Philosophie drückt wohl auch einen Anfang aus, aber nicht sowohl einen subjektiven als objektiven, den Anfang aller Dinge. Das Princip ist ein irgendwie bestimmter Inhalt,—das Wasser, das Eine, Nus, Idee,—Substanz, Monade u.s.f., oder wenn es sich auf die Natur des Erkennens bezieht und damit mehr nur ein Kriterium als eine objektive Bestimmung seyn soll Denken, Anschauen, Empfinden, Ich, die Subjektivität selbst, so ist es hier gleichfalls die Inhaltsbestimmung, auf welche das Interesse geht.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"5.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005","text":"Das Anfangen als solches dagegen bleibt als ein Subjektives in dem Sinne einer zufälligen Art und Weise, den Vortrag einzuleiten, unbeachtet und gleichgültig, somit auch das Bedürfniß der Frage, womit anzufangen sey, unbedeutend gegen das Bedürfniß des Princips, als in welchem allein das Interesse der Sache zu liegen scheint, das Interesse, was das Wahre, was der absolute Grund von Allem sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"5.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","text":"Aber die moderne Verlegenheit um den Anfang geht aus einem weiteren Bedürfnisse hervor, welches diejenigen noch nicht kennen, denen es dogmatisch um das Erweisen des Princips zu thun ist, oder skeptisch um das Finden eines subjektiven Kriteriums gegen dogmatisches Philosophiren und welches diejenigen ganz verleugnen, die wie aus der Pistole, aus ihrer innern Offenbarung, aus Glauben, intellektueller Anschauung u.s.w. anfangen, und der Methode und Logik überhoben seyn wollten. Wenn das früher abstrakte Denken zunächst nur für das Princip als Inhalt sich interessirt, aber im Fortgange der Bildung auf die andere Seite, auf das Benehmen des Erkennens zu achten getrieben ist, so wird auch das subjektive Thun als wesentliches Moment der objektiven Wahrheit erfaßt, und das Bedürfniß führt sich herbei, daß die Methode mit dem Inhalt, die Form mit dem Princip vereint sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"5.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","text":"So soll das Princip auch Anfang und das, was das Prius für das Denken ist, auch das Erste im Gange des Denkens seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"5.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0008","text":"Es ist hier nur zu betrachten, wie der logische Anfang erscheint; die beiden Seiten, nach denen er genommen werden kann, sind schon genannt, entweder als Resultat auf vermittelte, oder als eigentlicher Anfang auf unmittelbare Weise. Die in der Bildung der Zeit so wichtig erscheinende Frage, ob das Wissen der Wahrheit ein unmittelbares, schlechthin anfangendes Wissen, ein Glauben, oder aber ein vermitteltes Wissen sey, ist an diesem Orte nicht zu erörtern. Insofern solche Betrachtung vorläufig angestellt werden kann, ist dieß anderwärts (in m. Encykl. der philos. Wissenschaf. 3te Ausg. im Vorbegr. §. 61. ff.) geschehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"5.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","text":"Hier mag daraus nur dieß angeführt werden, daß es Nichts giebt, nichts im Himmel oder in der Natur oder im Geiste oder wo es sey, was nicht ebenso die Unmittelbarkeit enthält, als die Vermittelung, so daß sich diese beiden Bestimmungen als ungetrennt und untrennbar und jener Gegensatz sich als ein Richtiges zeigt. Was aber die wissenschaftliche Erörterung betrifft, so ist es jeder logische Satz, in welchem die Bestimmungen der Unmittelbarkeit und der Vermittelung und also die Erörterung ihres Gegensatzes und ihrer Wahrheit vorkommt. Insofern dieser Gegensatz in Beziehung auf Denken, Wissen, Erkennen, die konkretere Gestalt von unmittelbarem oder vermitteltem Wissen erhält, wird die Natur des Erkennens überhaupt, sowohl innerhalb der Wissenschaft der Logik betrachtet, als dasselbe in seiner weitern konkreten Form, in die Wissenschaft vom Geiste, und in die Phänomenologie desselben fällt.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"5.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","text":"Vor der Wissenschaft aber schon über das Erkennen ins Reine kommen wollen, heißt verlangen, daß es außerhalb derselben erörtert werden sollte; außerhalb der Wissenschaft läßt sich dieß wenigstens nicht auf wissenschaftliche Weise, um die es hier allein zu thun ist, bewerkstelligen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"5.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","text":"Logisch ist der Anfang, indem er im Element des frei für sich seyenden Denkens, im reinen Wissen gemacht werden soll. Vermittelt ist es hiermit dadurch, daß das reine Wissen die letzte, absolute Wahrheit des Bewußtseyns ist. Es ist in der Einleitung bemerkt, daß die Phänomenologie des Geistes die Wissenschaft des Bewußtseyns, die Darstellung davon ist, daß das Bewußtseyn den Begriff der Wissenschaft, d.i. das reine Wissen, zum Resultate hat. Die Logik hat insofern die Wissenschaft des erscheinenden Geistes zu ihrer Voraussetzung, welche die Nothwendigkeit und damit den Beweis der Wahrheit des Standpunkts, der das reine Wissen ist, wie dessen Vermittelung überhaupt, enthält und aufzeigt.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"5.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0012","text":"In dieser Wissenschaft des erscheinenden Geistes wird von dem empirischen, sinnlichen Bewußtseyn ausgegangen; und dieses ist das eigentliche unmittelbare Wissen; daselbst wird erörtert, was an diesem unmittelbaren Wissen ist. Anderes Bewußtseyn, wie der Glaube an göttliche Wahrheiten, innere Erfahrung, Wissen durch innere Offenbarung u.s.f. zeigt sich bei geringer Überlegung sehr uneigentlich als unmittelbares Wissen aufgeführt zu werden. In jener Abhandlung ist das unmittelbare Bewußtseyn auch das in der Wissenschaft Erste und Unmittelbare, somit die Voraussetzung; in der Logik aber ist dasjenige die Voraussetzung, was aus jener Betrachtung sich als das Resultat erwiesen hatte,—die Idee als reines Wissen. Die Logik, ist die reine Wissenschaft, d.i. das reine Wissen in dem ganzen Umfange seiner Entwickelung.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"5.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","text":"Diese Idee aber hat sich in jenem Resultate dahin bestimmt, die zur Wahrheit gewordenen Gewißheit zu seyn, die Gewißheit, die nach der einen Seite dem Gegenstande nicht mehr gegenüber ist, sondern ihn innerlich gemacht hat, ihn als sich selbst weiß,—und die auf der andern Seite das Wissen von sich als von einem, das dem Gegenständlichen gegenüber und nur dessen Vernichtung sey, aufgegeben, dieser Subjektivität entäußert und Einheit mit seiner Entäußerung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"5.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0014","text":"Daß nun von dieser Bestimmung des reinen Wissens aus der Anfang seiner Wissenschaft immanent bleibe, ist nichts zu thun, als das zu betrachten oder vielmehr mit Beiseitsetzung aller Reflexionen, aller Meinungen, die man sonst hat, nur aufzunehmen was vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"5.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","text":"Das reine Wissen als in diese Einheit zusammengegangen, hat alle Beziehung auf ein Anderes und auf Vermittelung aufgehoben; es ist das Unterschiedslose; dieses Unterschiedslose hört somit selbst auf, Wissen zu seyn; es ist nur einfache Unmittelbarkeit vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"5.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","text":"Die einfache Unmittelbarkeit ist selbst ein Reflexionsausdruck, und bezieht sich auf den Unterschied von dem Vermittelten. In ihrem wahren Ausdrucke ist daher diese einfache Unmittelbarkeit das reine Seyn. Wie das reine Wissen nichts heißen soll, als das Wissen als solches, ganz abstrakt, so soll auch reines Seyn nichts heißen, als das Seyn überhaupt; Seyn, sonst nichts, ohne alle weitere Bestimmung und Erfüllung.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"5.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","text":"Hier ist das Seyn das Anfangende, als durch Vermittelung und zwar durch sie, welche zugleich Aufheben ihrer selbst ist, entstanden, dargestellt; mit der Voraussetzung des reinen Wissens als Resultats des endlichen Wissens, des Bewußtseyns. Soll aber keine Voraussetzung gemacht, der Anfang selbst unmittelbar genommen werden, so bestimmt er sich nur dadurch, daß es der Anfang der Logik des Denkens für sich, seyn soll. Nur der Entschluß, den man auch für eine Willkür ansehen kann, nämlich daß man das Denken als solches betrachten wolle, ist vorhanden. So muß der Anfang absoluter oder was hier gleichbedeutend ist, abstrakter Anfang seyn; er darf so nichts voraussetzen, muß durch nichts vermittelt seyn, noch einen Grund haben; er soll vielmehr selbst Grund der ganzen Wissenschaft seyn. Er muß daher schlechthin ein Unmittelbares seyn, oder vielmehr nur das Unmittelbare selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"5.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","text":"Wie er nicht gegen Anderes eine Bestimmung haben kann, so kann er auch keine in sich, keinen Inhalt enthalten, denn dergleichen wäre Unterscheidung und Beziehung von Verschiedenem aufeinander, somit eine Vermittelung. Der Anfang ist also das reine Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"5.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0019","text":"Nach dieser einfachen Darlegung dessen, was zunächst nur zu diesem selbst Allereinfachsten, dem logischen Anfang, gehört, können noch folgende weitere Reflexionen beigebracht werden; doch können sie nicht sowohl zur Erläuterung und Bestätigung jener Darlegung, die für sich fertig ist, dienen sollen, als sie vielmehr nur durch Vorstellungen und Reflexionen veranlaßt werden, die uns zum Voraus in den Weg kommen können, jedoch, wie alle andere vorangehende Vorurtheile, in der Wissenschaft selbst ihr Erledigung finden müssen, und daher eigentlich zur Geduld hierauf zu verweisen wären.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"5.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0020","text":"Die Einsicht, daß das Absolut-Wahre ein Resultat seyn müsse, und umgekehrt, daß ein Resultat ein erstes Wahres voraussetzt, das aber, weil es Erstes ist, objektiv betrachtet, nicht nothwendig, und nach der subjektiven Seite, nicht erkannt ist,—hat in neuern Zeiten den Gedanken hervorgebracht, daß die Philosophie nur mit einem hypothetischen und problematischen Wahren anfangen, und das Philosophiren daher zuerst nur ein Suchen seyn könne, eine Ansicht, welche Reinhold in den spätern Zeiten seines Philosphirens vielfach urgiert hat, und der man die Gerechtigkeit widerfahren lassen muß, daß ihr ein wahrhaftes Interesse zu Grunde liegt, welches die spekulative Natur des philosophischen Anfangs betrifft.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"5.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","text":"Die Auseinandersetzung dieser Ansicht ist zugleich eine Veranlassung, ein vorläufiges Verständniß über den Sinn des logischen Fortschreitens überhaupt, einzuleiten; denn jene Ansicht schließt die Rücksicht auf das Fortgehen sogleich in sich. Und zwar stellt sie es so vor, daß das Vorwärtsschreiten in der Philosophie vielmehr ein Rückwärtsgehen und Begründen sey, durch welches erst sich ergebe, daß das, womit angefangen wurde, nicht bloß ein willkürlich Angenommenes, sondern in der That Theils das Wahre, Theils das erste Wahre sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"5.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","text":"Man muß zugeben, daß es eine wesentliche Betrachtung ist,—die sich innerhalb der Logik selbst näher ergeben wird,—daß das Vorwärtsgehen ein Rückgang in den Grund, zu dem Ursprünglichen und Wahrhaften ist, von dem das, womit der Anfang gemacht wurde, abhängt, und in der That hervorgebracht wird.—So wird das Bewußtseyn auf seinem Wege von der Unmittelbarkeit aus, mit der es anfängt, zum absoluten Wissen, als seiner innersten Wahrheit, zurückgeführt.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"5.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","text":"Dieß Letzte, der Grund, ist denn auch dasjenige, aus welchem das Erste hervorgeht, das zuerst als Unmittelbares auftrat.—So wird noch mehr der absolute Geist, der als die konkrete und letzte höchste Wahrheit alles Seyns sich ergiebt, erkannt, als am Ende der Entwickelung sich mit Freiheit entäußernd und sich zur Gestalt eines unmittelbaren Seyns entlassend,—zur Schöpfung einer Welt sich entschließend, welche alles das enthält, was in die Entwickelung, die jenem Resultate vorangegangen, fiel, und das durch diese umgekehrte Stellung, mit seinem Anfang in ein von dem Resultate als dem Principe Abhängiges verwandelt wird. Das Wesentliche für die Wissenschaft, ist nicht so sehr, daß ein rein Unmittelbares der Anfang sey, sondern daß das Ganze derselben ein Kreislauf in sich selbst ist, worin das Erste auch das Letzte, und das Letzte auch das Erste wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"5.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","text":"Daher ergiebt sich auf der andern Seite als ebenso nothwendig, dasjenige, in welches die Bewegung als in seinen Grund zurückgeht, als Resultat zu betrachten. Nach dieser Rücksicht ist das Erste ebenso sehr der Grund, und das Letzte ein Abgeleitetes; indem von dem Ersten ausgegangen und durch richtige Folgerung auf das Letzte, als auf den Grund, gekommen wird, ist dieser Resultat. Der Fortgang ferner von dem, was den Anfang macht, ist nur als eine weitere Bestimmung desselben zu betrachten, so daß das Anfangende allem Folgenden zu Grunde liegen bleibt, und nichts daraus verschwindet. Das Fortgehen besteht nicht darin, daß nur ein Anderes abgeleitet, oder daß in ein wahrhaft Anderes übergegangen würde;—und insofern dieß Übergehen vorkommt, so hebt es sich ebenso sehr wieder auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"5.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","text":"So ist der Anfang der Philosophie, die in allen folgenden Entwickelungen gegenwärtige und sich erhaltende Grundlage, das seinen weiteren Bestimmungen durchaus immanent Bleibende.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"5.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","text":"Durch diesen Fortgang denn verliert der Anfang das, was er in dieser Bestimmtheit, ein Unmittelbares und Abstraktes überhaupt zu seyn, einseitiges hat; er wird ein Vermitteltes, und die Linie der wissenschaftlichen Fortbewegung macht sich damit zu einem Kreise. —Zugleich ergiebt sich, daß das, was den Anfang macht, indem es darin das noch Unentwickelte, Inhaltlose ist, im Anfange noch nicht wahrhaft erkannt wird, und daß erst die Wissenschaft, und zwar in ihrer ganzen Entwickelung, seine vollendete, inhaltsvolle und erst wahrhaft begründete Erkenntniß ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"5.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","text":"Darum aber, weil das Resultat erst als der absolute Grund hervortritt, ist das Fortschreiten dieses Erkennens nicht etwas Provisorisches, noch ein problematisches und hypothetisches, sondern es muß durch die Natur der Sache und des Inhaltes selbst bestimmt seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"5.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028","text":"Weder ist jener Anfang etwas Willkürliches und nur einstweilen Angenommenes, noch ein als willkürlich Erscheinendes und bittweise Vorausgesetztes, von dem sich aber doch in der Folge zeige, daß man Recht daran gethan habe, es zum Anfange zu machen; nicht wie bei den Konstruktionen, die man zum Behuf des Beweises eines geometrischen Satzes zu machen angewiesen wird, es der Fall ist, daß von ihnen es sich erst hinterher an den Beweisen ergiebt, daß man wohlgethan habe, gerade diese Linien zu ziehen, und dann in den Beweisen selbst, mit der Vergleichung dieser Linien oder Winkel anzufangen; für sich an diesem Linienziehen oder Vergleichen begreift es sich nicht. So ist vorhin der Grund, warum in der reinen Wissenschaft vom reinen Seyn angefangen wird, unmittelbar an ihr selbst angegeben worden.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"5.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","text":"Dieß reine Seyn ist die Einheit, in die das reine Wissen zurückgeht, oder wenn dieses selbst noch als Form von seiner Einheit unterschieden gehalten werden soll, so ist es auch der Inhalt desselben. Dieß ist die Seite, nach welcher dieß reine Seyn, dieß Absolut-Unmittelbare, ebenso absolut Vermitteltes ist. Aber es muß ebenso wesentlich nur in der Einseitigkeit, das Rein-Unmittelbare zu seyn, genommen werden, eben weil es hier als der Anfang ist. Insofern es nicht diese reinen Unbestimmtheit, insofern es bestimmt wäre, würde es als Vermitteltes, schon weiter Geführtes, genommen; ein Bestimmtes enthält ein Anderes zu einem Ersten. Es liegt also in der Natur des Anfangs selbst, daß er das Seyn sey, und sonst nichts. Es bedarf daher keiner sonstigen Vorbereitungen, um in die Philosophie hineinzukommen, noch anderweitiger Reflexionen und Anknüpfungspunkte.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"5.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0030","text":"Daß der Anfang, Anfang der Philosophie ist, daraus kann eigentlich auch keine nähere Bestimmung oder ein positiver Inhalt für denselben genommen werden. Denn die Philosophie ist hier im Anfange, wo die Sache selbst noch nicht vorhanden ist, ein leeres Wort oder irgend eine angenommene ungerechtfertigte Vorstellung. Das reine Wissen giebt nur diese negative Bestimmung, daß er der abstrakte Anfang seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"5.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0031","text":"Insofern das reine Seyn als Inhalt des reinen Wissens genommen wird, so hat dieses von seinem Inhalte zurückzutreten, ihn für sich selbst gewähren zu lassen und nicht weiter zu bestimmen.—Oder indem das reine Seyn als die Einheit zu betrachten ist, in die das Wissen, auf seiner höchsten Spitze der Einigung mit dem Objekte, zusammengefallen, so ist das Wissen in diese Einheit verschwunden, und hat keinen Unterschied von ihr und somit keine Bestimmung für sich übrig gelassen.—Auch sonst ist nicht Etwas, oder irgend ein Inhalt vorhanden, der gebracht werden könnte, um damit den bestimmteren Anfang zu machen.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"5.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0032","text":"Aber auch die bisher als Anfang angenommmene Bestimmung des Seyns könnte weggelassen werden, so daß nur gefordert würde, daß ein reiner Anfang gemacht werde. Dann ist nichts vorhanden, als der Anfang selbst, und es wäre zu sehen, was er ist.—Diese Stellung könnte zugleich als ein Vorschlag zur Güte an diejenigen gemacht werden, welche Theils damit, daß mit dem Seyn angefangen werde, aus welchen Reflexionen es sey, sich nicht beruhigen und noch weniger mit dem Erfolge, den das Seyn hat, in das Nichts überzugehn,—Theils überhaupt nicht anders wissen, als daß in einer Wissenschaft mit der Voraussetzung einer Vorstellung angefangen werde,—einer Vorstellung, welche hierauf analysirt werde, so daß nun das Ergebniß solcher Analyse den ersten bestimmten Begriff in der Wissenschaft abgebe.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"5.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0033","text":"Indem wir auch dieß Verfahren beobachteten, so hätten wir keinen besondern Gegenstand, weil der Anfang als des Denkens, ganz abstrakt, ganz allgemein, ganz Form ohne allen Inhalt seyn soll; wir hätten somit gar nichts, als die Vorstellung von einem bloßen Anfang als solchem. Es ist also nur zu sehen, was wir in dieser Vorstellung haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"5.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0034","text":"Es ist noch Nichts, und es soll Etwas werden. Der Anfang ist nicht das reine Nichts, sondern ein Nichts, von dem Etwas ausgehen soll; das Seyn ist also auch schon im Anfang enthalten. Der Anfang enthält also Beides, Seyn und Nichts; ist die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts; —oder ist Nichtseyn, das zugleich Seyn, und Seyn, das zugleich Nichtseyn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"5.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0035","text":"Ferner Seyn und Nichts sind im Anfang als unterschieden vorhanden; denn er weißt auf etwas Anderes hin;—er ist ein Nichtseyn, das auf das Seyn als auf ein Anderes bezogen ist; das Anfangende ist noch nicht; es geht erst dem Seyn zu. Der Anfang enthält also das Seyn als ein solches, das sich von dem Nichtseyn entfernt oder es aufhebt, als ein ihm Entgegengesetztes.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"5.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0036","text":"Ferner aber ist das, was anfängt, schon, eben so sehr aber ist es auch noch nicht. Die Entgegengesetzten, Seyn und Nichtseyn sind also in ihm in unmittelbarer Vereinigung; oder er ist ihre ununterschiedene Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"5.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0037","text":"Die Analyse des Anfangs gäbe somit den Begriff der Einheit des Seyns und des Nichtseyns,—oder in reflektirterer Form, der Einheit des Unterschieden—und des Nichtunterschiedenseyns,—oder der Identität der Identität und Nichtidentität. Dieser Begriff könnte als die erste, reinste d.i. abstrakteste, Definition des Absoluten angesehen werden;—wie er dieß in der That seyn würde, wenn es überhaupt um die Form von Definitionen und um den Namen des Absoluten zu thun wäre. In diesem Sinne würden, wie jener abstrakte Begriff die erste, so alle weitern Bestimmungen und Entwickelungen nur bestimmtere und reichere Definitionen dieses Absoluten seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"5.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0038","text":"Aber die, welche mit dem Seyn als Anfang darum nicht zufrieden sind, weil es in Nichts übergeht, und daraus die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts entsteht, mögen zusehen, ob sie mit diesem Anfange, der mit der Vorstellung des Anfangs anfängt, und mit deren Analyse, die wohl richtig seyn wird, aber gleichfalls auf die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts führt, zufriedener seyn mögen, als damit, daß das Seyn zum Anfange gemacht wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"5.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","text":"Es ist aber noch einen weitere Betrachtung über dieses Verfahren zu machen. Jene Analyse setzt die Vorstellung des Anfangs als bekannt voraus; es ist so nach dem Beispiele anderer Wissenschaften verfahren worden. Diese setzen ihren Gegenstand voraus, und nehmen bittweise an, daß jedermann dieselbe Vorstellung von ihm habe, und darin ungefähr dieselben Bestimmungen finden möge, die sie durch Analyse, Vergleichung und sonstiges Raisonnement von ihm da und dorther beibringen und angeben. Das aber, was den absoluten Anfang macht, muß gleichfalls ein sonst Bekanntes seyn; wenn es nun ein Konkretes, somit in sich mannigfaltig Bestimmtes ist, so ist diese Beziehung, die es in sich ist, als etwas Bekanntes vorausgesetzt; sie ist damit als etwas Unmittelbares angegeben, was sie aber nicht ist; denn sie ist nur Beziehung als von Unterschiedenen, enthält somit die Vermittelung in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"5.39"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","text":"Ferner tritt am Konkreten die Zufälligkeit und Willkür der Analyse und des verschiedenen Bestimmtes ein. Welche Bestimmungen herausgebracht werden, hängt von dem ab, was jeder in seiner unmittelbaren zufälligen Vorstellung vorfindet. Die in einem Konkreten, einer synthetischen Einheit, enthaltene Beziehung ist eine nothwendige nur, insofern sie nicht vorgefunden, sondern durch die eigenen Bewegung der Momente, in diese Einheit zurück zu gehen, hervorgebracht ist;—eine Bewegung, die das Gegentheil des analytischen Verfahrens ist, eines der Sache selbst äußerlichen, in das Subjekt fallenden Thuns.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"5.40"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","text":"Hierin ist auch das Nähere enthalten, daß das, womit der Anfang zu machen ist, nicht ein Konkretes, nicht ein solches seyn kann, das eine Beziehung innerhalb seiner selbst enthält. Denn ein solches setzt ein Vermitteln und Herübergehen von einem Ersten zu einem Anderen innerhalb seiner, voraus, wovon das einfachgewordene Konkrete das Resultat wäre. Aber der Anfang soll nicht selbst schon ein Erstes und ein Anders seyn; ein solches das ein Erstes und ein Anderes in sich ist, enthält bereits ein Fortgegangenseyn. Was den Anfang macht, der Anfang selbst, ist daher als ein Nichtanalysirbares, in seiner einfachen unerfüllten Unmittelbarkeit, also als Seyn, als das ganz Leere zu nehmen.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"5.41"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0042","text":"Wenn man etwa, gegen die Betrachtung des abstrakten Anfangs ungeduldig, sagen wollte, es solle nicht mit dem Anfange angefangen werden, sondern geradezu mit der Sache, so ist diese Sache nichts als jenes leere Seyn; denn was die Sache sey, dieß ist es, was sich eben erst im Verlaufe der Wissenschaft ergeben soll, was nicht vor ihr als bekannt vorausgesetzt werden kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"5.42"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","text":"Welche Form sonst genommen werde, um einen andern Anfang zu haben, als das leere Seyn, so leidet er an den angeführten Mängeln. Diejenigen, welche mit diesem Anfange unzufrieden bleiben, mögen sich zu der Aufgabe auffordern, es anders anzufangen, um dabei diese Mängel zu vermeiden.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"5.43"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0044","text":"Ein origineller Anfang der Philosophie aber kann nicht ganz unerwähnt gelassen werden, der sich in neuerer Zeit berühmt gemacht hat, der Anfang mit dem Ich. Er kam Theils aus der Reflexion, daß aus dem ersten Wahren alles Folgende abgeleitet werden müsse, Theils aus dem Bedürfnisse, daß das erste Wahre ein Bekanntes und noch mehr ein unmittelbar Gewisses sey. Dieser Anfang ist im Allgemeinen nicht eine solche Vorstellung, die zufällig ist, und in einem Subjekte so, in einem andern anders, beschaffen seyn kann. Denn Ich, dieß unmittelbare Selbstbewußtseyn, erscheint zunächst selbst Theils als ein Unmittelbares, Theils als ein in einem viel höhern Sinne Bekanntes, als eine sonstige Vorstellung; etwas sonst Bekanntes gehört zwar dem Ich an, aber ist noch ein von ihm unterschiedener, damit sogleich zufälliger Inhalt; Ich hingegen ist die einfache Gewißheit seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"5.44"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","text":"Aber Ich überhaupt ist auch zugleich ein Konkretes, oder Ich ist vielmehr das Konkreteste,—das Bewußtseyn seiner, als unendlich mannigfaltiger Welt. Daß Ich Anfang und Grund der Philosophie sey, dazu wird die Absonderung dieses Konkreten erfordert,—der absolute Akt, wodurch Ich von sich selbst gereinigt wird, und als abstraktes Ich in sein Bewußtseyn tritt. Allein dieß reine Ich ist nun nicht ein unmittelbares, noch das bekannte, das gewöhnliche Ich unsers Bewußtseyns, woran unmittelbar und für jede die Wissenschaft angeknüpft werden sollte. Jener Akt wäre eigentlich nichts Anderes, als die Erhebung auf den Standpunkt des reinen Wissens, auf welchem der Unterschied des Subjektiven und Objektiven verschwunden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"5.45"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0046","text":"Aber wie diese Erhebung so unmittelbar gefordert ist, ist sie ein subjektives Postulat; um als wahrhafte Forderung sich zu erweisen, müßte die Fortbewegung des konkreten Ichs vom unmittelbaren Bewußtseyn zum reinen Wissen an ihm selbst, durch seine eigene Nothwendigkeit, aufgezeigt und dargestellt worden seyn. Ohne diese objektive Bewegung erscheint das reine Wissen, auch als die intellektuelle Anschauung bestimmt, als ein willkürlicher Standpunkt, oder selbst als einer der empirischen Zustände des Bewußtseyns, in Rücksicht dessen es darauf ankommt, ob ihn der Eine in sich vorfinde oder hervorbringen könne, ein Anderer aber nicht.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"5.46"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0047","text":"Insofern aber dieß reine Ich das wesentliche reine Wissen seyn muß, und das reine Wissen aber nur durch den absoluten Akt der Selbsterhebung im individuellen Bewußtseyn gesetzt wird, und nicht unmittelbar in ihm vorhanden ist, geht gerade der Vortheil verloren, der aus diesem Anfange der Philosophie entspringen soll, daß er nämlich etwas schlechthin Bekanntes sey, was jeder unmittelbar in sich finde, und daran die weitere Reflexion anknüpfen könne; jenes reine Ich ist vielmehr in seiner abstrakten Wesenheit, etwas dem gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn Unbekanntes, etwas, das es nicht darin vorfindet. Damit tritt vielmehr der Nachtheil der Täuschung ein, daß von etwas Bekanntem, dem Ich des empirischen Selbstbewußtseyns die Rede seyn solle, indem in der That von etwas diesem Bewußtseyn Fernem die Rede ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"5.47"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0048","text":"Die Bestimmung des reinen Wissens als Ich, führt die fortdauernde Rückerinnerung an das subjektive Ich mit sich, dessen Schranken vergessen werden sollen, und erhält die Vorstellung gegenwärtig, als ob die Sätze und Verhältnisse, die sich in der weitern Entwickelung vom Ich ergeben, im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn, da es ja das sey, von dem sie behauptet werden, vorkommen und darin vorgefunden werden können. Diese Verwechslung bringt statt unmittelbarer Klarheit vielmehr nur eine um so grellere Verwirrung und gänzliche Desorientirung hervor; nach Außen hat sie vollends die gröbsten Mißverständnisse veranlaßt.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"5.48"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0049","text":"Was ferner die subjektive Bestimmtheit des Ich überhaupt betrifft, so benimmt wohl das reine Wissen dem Ich seine beschränkte Bedeutung, an einem Objekte seinen unüberwindlichen Gegensatz zu haben. Aus diesem Grunde wäre es aber wenigstens überflüssig, noch diese subjektive Haltung und die Bestimmung des reinen Wesens als Ich, beizubehalten. Allein diese Bestimmung führt nicht nur jene störende Zweideutigkeit mit sich, sondern sie bleibt auch, näher betrachtet, ein subjektives Ich. Die wirkliche Entwickelung der Wissenschaft, die vom Ich ausgeht, zeigt es, daß das Objekt darin die perennirende Bestimmung eines Anderen für das Ich hat und behält, daß also das Ich, von dem ausgegangen wird, nicht das reine Wissen, das den Gegensatz des Bewußtseyns in Wahrheit überwunden hat, sondern noch in der Erscheinung befangen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"5.49"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0050","text":"Es ist hierbei noch die wesentliche Bemerkung in machen, daß wenn an sich wohl Ich als das reinen Wissen oder als intellektuelle Anschauung bestimmt und als Anfang behauptet werden könnte, daß es in der Wissenschaft nicht um das zu thun ist, was an sich oder innerlich vorhanden sey, sondern um das Daseyn des Innerlichen im Denken, und um die Bestimmtheit, die ein solches in diesem Daseyn hat. Was aber von der intellektuellen Anschauung—oder wenn ihr Gegenstand das Ewige, das Göttliche, das Absolute genannt wird,—was vom Ewigen oder Absoluten im Anfange der Wissenschaft da ist, dieß kann nichts Anderes seyn, als erste, unmittelbare, einfache Bestimmung. Welcher reichere Name ihm gegeben werde, als das bloße Seyn ausdrückt, so kann nur in Betracht kommen, wie solches Absolute in das denkende Wissen und in das Aussprechen dieses Wissens eintritt.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"5.50"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","text":"Die intellektuelle Anschauung ist wohl die gewaltsame Zurückweisung des Vermittelns und der beweisenden, äußerlichen Reflexion. Was sie aber mehr ausspricht, als einfache Unmittelbarkeit, ist ein Konkretes, ein in sich verschiedene Bestimmungen Enthaltendes. Das Aussprechen und die Darstellung eines solchen jedoch ist, wie schon bemerkt, eine vermittelnde Bewegung, die von einer der Bestimmungen anfängt, und zu der anderen fortgeht, wenn diese auch zur ersten zurückgeht;—es ist eine Bewegung, die zugleich nicht willkürlich oder assertorisch seyn darf. Von was daher in solcher Darstellung angefangen wird, ist nicht das Konkrete selbst, sondern nur das einfache Unmittelbare, von dem die Bewegung ausgeht. Außerdem fehlt, wenn ein Konkretes zum Anfange gemacht wird, der Beweis, dessen die Verbindung der im Konkreten enthaltenen Bestimmungen bedarf.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"5.51"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","text":"Wenn also im Ausdrucke des Absoluten oder Ewigen oder Gottes (und das unbestrittenste Recht hätte Gott, daß mit ihm der Anfang gemacht werde), wenn in deren Anschauung oder Gedanken mehr liegt, als im reinen Seyn, so soll das, was darin liegt, ins Wissen als denkendes, nicht vorstellendes erst hervortreten; das was darin liegt, es sey so reich, als es wolle, so ist die Bestimmung, die ins Wissen zuerst hervortritt, ein Einfaches; denn nur im Einfachen ist nicht mehr als der reine Anfang; nur das Unmittelbare ist einfach, denn nur im Unmittelbaren ist noch nicht ein Fortgegangenseyn von Einem zu einem Anderen.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"5.52"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","text":"Was somit über das Seyn ausgesprochen oder enthalten seyn soll, in den reicheren Formen des Vorstellens von Absolutem oder Gott, dieß ist im Anfange nur leeres Wort, und nur Seyn; dieß Einfache, das sonst keine weitere Bedeutung hat, dieß Leere ist also schlechthin der Anfang der Philosophie.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"5.53"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0054","text":"Diese Einsicht ist selbst so einfach, daß dieser Anfang als solcher, keiner Vorbereitung noch weiteren Einleitung bedarf; und diese Vorläufigkeit von Raisonnement über ihn konnte nicht die Absicht haben, ihn herbeizuführen, als vielmehr alle Vorläufigkeit zu entfernen.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"5.54"}],"sha256":"7a3a97d52bb529a06747c3e9a02f2e964c7cc66df1e3d69c10e62f27ddd42ed4","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101701272214Z_f02e2e6a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"With What Must the Science Begin?","source_sha256":"7a3a97d52bb529a06747c3e9a02f2e964c7cc66df1e3d69c10e62f27ddd42ed4","sha256":"5ab57dc40d07fc53545c7790d336077abb76de5e0614a1f313f82653734a18c1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:17:01.272253+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0001","text":"## First Book. The Doctrine of Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"5.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0002","text":"## With what must the beginning of science be made?","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"5.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","text":"Only in modern times has the consciousness arisen that it is a difficulty to find a beginning in philosophy, and the ground of this difficulty, as well as the possibility of resolving it, has been discussed in various ways. The beginning of philosophy must be either something mediated or immediate, and it is easy to show that it can be neither the one nor the other; thus one or the other mode of beginning finds its refutation.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"5.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004","text":"The principle of a philosophy indeed also expresses a beginning, but not so much a subjective as an objective one, the beginning of all things. The principle is some determinate content,—water, the One, Nous, Idea,—substance, monad, etc.; or, if it relates to the nature of cognition and is therefore meant to be more merely a criterion than an objective determination, thinking, intuition, sensation, I, subjectivity itself, then here too it is the determination of content in which the interest lies.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"5.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005","text":"Beginning as such, on the other hand, remains disregarded and indifferent as something subjective, in the sense of a contingent manner of introducing the exposition; thus also the need of the question with what one ought to begin remains insignificant in comparison with the need for the principle, in which alone the interest of the matter seems to lie, the interest in what truth is, what the absolute ground of everything is.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"5.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","text":"But the modern embarrassment concerning the beginning proceeds from a further need, which those who are dogmatically concerned with proving the principle, or skeptically with finding a subjective criterion against dogmatic philosophizing, do not yet know, and which those altogether disavow who, as if from a pistol, begin from their inner revelation, from faith, intellectual intuition, etc., and would wish to be exempt from method and logic. If formerly abstract thinking was at first interested only in the principle as content, but in the progress of culture has been driven to attend to the other side, to the conduct of cognition, then subjective activity too is apprehended as an essential moment of objective truth, and the need arises that method be united with content, form with principle.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"5.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","text":"Thus the principle too is to be beginning, and that which is the prius for thinking is also to be the first in the course of thinking.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"5.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0008","text":"Here there is only to be considered how the logical beginning appears; the two sides according to which it can be taken have already been named: either, as result, in a mediated manner, or, as an actual beginning, in an immediate manner. The question which appears so important in the culture of the age, whether knowledge of truth is immediate knowledge, absolutely commencing knowledge, a faith, or whether it is mediated knowledge, is not to be discussed here. In so far as such a consideration can be made provisionally, this has been done elsewhere (in my Encyclopaedia of the Philosophical Sciences, 3rd ed., in the Preliminary Concept, § 61 ff.).","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"5.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","text":"Here let only this be adduced from it: that there is nothing, nothing in heaven or in nature or in spirit or wherever it may be, which does not contain immediacy just as much as mediation, so that these two determinations show themselves to be inseparate and inseparable, and that opposition to be something correct. But as regards scientific discussion, every logical proposition is one in which the determinations of immediacy and mediation, and thus the discussion of their opposition and their truth, occur. In so far as this opposition, in relation to thinking, knowing, cognition, receives the more concrete shape of immediate or mediated knowledge, the nature of cognition in general is considered both within the science of logic, and falls, in its further concrete form, into the science of spirit and its phenomenology.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"5.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","text":"But to wish already before science to get clear about cognition means to demand that it should be discussed outside science; outside science this cannot at least be accomplished in a scientific manner, which alone is what is at issue here.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"5.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","text":"The beginning is logical, inasmuch as it is to be made in the element of thinking that freely is for itself, in pure knowing. It is thereby mediated here, in that pure knowing is the final, absolute truth of consciousness. It has been remarked in the Introduction that the Phenomenology of Spirit is the science of consciousness, the presentation of the fact that consciousness has the concept of science, i.e. pure knowing, as its result. Logic thus has as its presupposition the science of appearing spirit, which contains and demonstrates the necessity, and thereby the proof of the truth, of the standpoint that is pure knowing, as well as its mediation in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"5.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0012","text":"In this science of appearing spirit, the point of departure is empirical, sensuous consciousness; and this is knowledge properly immediate; there it is discussed what is in this immediate knowledge. Other consciousness, such as faith in divine truths, inner experience, knowing through inner revelation, etc., upon slight reflection shows itself very improperly to be adduced as immediate knowledge. In that treatise immediate consciousness is also what is first and immediate in science, thus the presupposition; but in logic, what proved itself in that consideration to be the result is the presupposition,—the Idea as pure knowing. Logic is the pure science, i.e. pure knowing in the entire extent of its development.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"5.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","text":"But in that result this Idea has determined itself to be certainty become truth, certainty which, on the one side, no longer stands over against the object, but has made it inward, knows it as itself,—and which, on the other side, has given up knowledge of itself as of something standing over against objectivity and being only its annihilation, has divested itself of this subjectivity, and is unity with its divestment.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"5.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0014","text":"Now, for the beginning of its science to remain immanent from this determination of pure knowing, nothing is required but to consider—or rather, setting aside all reflections, all opinions one otherwise has—to take up only what is present.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"5.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","text":"Pure knowing, as having passed over into this unity, has suspended every relation to an other and to mediation; it is the undifferentiated; this undifferentiated thus itself ceases to be knowing; only simple immediacy is present.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"5.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","text":"Simple immediacy is itself an expression of reflection and relates to the distinction from the mediated. In its true expression, therefore, this simple immediacy is pure being. Just as pure knowing is to mean nothing but knowing as such, quite abstractly, so pure being is to mean nothing but being in general; being, otherwise nothing, without any further determination and fulfilment.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"5.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","text":"Here being is presented as what begins, as having arisen through mediation, and indeed through that mediation which is at the same time the suspension of itself; presented with the presupposition of pure knowing as the result of finite knowing, of consciousness. But if no presupposition is to be made, if the beginning itself is to be taken immediately, it determines itself only by being meant to be the beginning of logic, of thinking for itself. There is present only the resolve—which may also be regarded as an arbitrariness—namely, that one wishes to consider thinking as such. Thus the beginning must be absolute, or, what is equivalent here, abstract beginning; it may thus presuppose nothing, be mediated by nothing, nor have a ground; rather, it is itself to be the ground of the entire science. It must therefore be absolutely an immediate, or rather only immediacy itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"5.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","text":"Just as it cannot have a determination in opposition to an other, so neither can it contain one within itself, any content; for such a thing would be distinction and relation of different things to one another, thus a mediation. The beginning is therefore pure being.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"5.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0019","text":"After this simple exposition of what belongs in the first instance only to this itself most simple thing, the logical beginning, the following further reflections may still be adduced; yet they cannot so much serve to elucidate and confirm that exposition, which is complete in itself, as they are rather occasioned merely by representations and reflections which may come in our way in advance, but which, like all other preceding prejudices, must find their settlement in science itself, and therefore one would properly have to refer to patience in this regard.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"5.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0020","text":"The insight that the absolutely true must be a result, and conversely that a result presupposes a first truth which, however, because it is first, is, objectively considered, not necessary and, on the subjective side, not known,—has in modern times given rise to the thought that philosophy can begin only with a hypothetical and problematic truth, and that philosophizing can therefore at first only be a seeking, a view which Reinhold repeatedly urged in the later period of his philosophizing, and to which justice must be done in acknowledging that a genuine interest lies at its basis, one that concerns the speculative nature of the philosophical beginning.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"5.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","text":"The exposition of this view is at the same time an occasion for introducing a preliminary understanding concerning the sense of logical progression in general; for that view immediately includes the consideration of proceeding. Namely, it represents matters thus: that the advance in philosophy is rather a going backward and grounding, through which it first emerges that that with which the beginning was made is not merely something arbitrarily assumed, but is in fact partly the true and partly the first truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"5.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","text":"One must admit that it is an essential consideration,—which will emerge more closely within logic itself,—that going forward is a return into the ground, to the original and true, upon which that with which the beginning was made depends, and is in fact produced.—Thus consciousness, on its path from the immediacy with which it begins, is led back to absolute knowing as its innermost truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"5.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","text":"This latter, the ground, is then also that from which the first proceeds, which at first appeared as immediate.—Thus, still more, absolute spirit, which emerges as the concrete and final highest truth of all being, is cognized as, at the end of development, freely divesting itself and releasing itself into the shape of an immediate being,—resolving upon the creation of a world which contains all that fell within the development preceding that result, and which, through this reversed position, is transformed, together with its beginning, into something dependent upon the result as principle. What is essential for science is not so much that a purely immediate be the beginning, as that its whole be a circle within itself, in which the first also becomes the last, and the last also the first.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"5.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","text":"Hence, on the other side, it emerges as equally necessary to regard as result that into which the movement returns as into its ground. From this standpoint, the first is equally the ground, and the last something derived; since one proceeds from the first and arrives, by correct inference, at the last, as at the ground, this latter is result. Furthermore, the progression from what makes the beginning is to be regarded only as a further determination of it, so that what begins remains underlying everything that follows and nothing disappears from it. Proceeding does not consist in merely deriving an other, or in passing over into a truly other;—and in so far as this passing over occurs, it likewise suspends itself again.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"5.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","text":"Thus the beginning of philosophy is the foundation that is present and preserves itself throughout all subsequent developments, that which remains thoroughly immanent in its further determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"5.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","text":"Through this progression, then, the beginning loses what is one-sided about it in this determinacy, namely, being an immediate and abstract [thing] in general; it becomes a mediated [thing], and the line of scientific advance thereby makes itself into a circle. —At the same time, it follows that what constitutes the beginning, since it is therein the still undeveloped, contentless [thing], is not yet truly cognized in the beginning, and that only science, indeed science in its entire development, is its complete, contentful, and only truly grounded cognition.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"5.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","text":"But because the result emerges only as the absolute ground, the advance of this cognition is not something provisional, nor something problematic and hypothetical; rather, it must be determined by the nature of the matter and of the content itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"5.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028","text":"That beginning is neither something arbitrary and merely assumed for the time being, nor something appearing arbitrary and presupposed by way of request, of which, however, it subsequently turns out that one did right to make it the beginning; it is not as in the case of constructions which one is instructed to make for the purpose of proving a geometrical proposition, where it only subsequently becomes evident in the proofs that one did well to draw precisely these lines, and then to begin in the proofs themselves with the comparison of these lines or angles; in and for itself, there is no comprehending this drawing of lines or comparing. Thus, above, the ground why pure science begins with pure Being was immediately indicated in it itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"5.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","text":"This pure Being is the unity into which pure knowing returns, or, if the latter itself is still to be held distinct as form from its unity, then it is also its content. This is the side according to which this pure Being, this absolutely immediate [thing], is likewise absolutely mediated. But it must just as essentially be taken only in the one-sidedness of being purely immediate, precisely because it is here the beginning. Insofar as it were not this pure indeterminacy, insofar as it were determinate, it would be taken as mediated, as already carried further; a determinate [thing] contains an other in relation to a first. Thus it lies in the nature of the beginning itself that it be Being, and nothing else. Therefore no further preparations are required in order to enter into philosophy, nor any other reflections and points of connection.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"5.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0030","text":"That the beginning is the beginning of philosophy cannot properly yield any more precise determination or a positive content for it either. For philosophy here at the beginning, where the matter itself is not yet present, is an empty word or some assumed, unjustified representation. Pure knowing gives only this negative determination, that it is to be the abstract beginning.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"5.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0031","text":"Insofar as pure Being is taken as the content of pure knowing, the latter must withdraw from its content, let it be on its own account, and not determine it further.—Or, since pure Being is to be regarded as the unity into which knowing has fallen together at its highest point of unification with the object, knowing has vanished into this unity, and has left over no distinction from it and hence no determination for itself.—Nor is there otherwise anything, or any content, present that could be brought in so as to make a more determinate beginning with it.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"5.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0032","text":"But even the determination of Being hitherto assumed as the beginning could be omitted, so that only the demand would be made that a pure beginning be made. Then nothing is present but the beginning itself, and it would be necessary to see what it is.—This position could at the same time be made as a conciliatory proposal to those who, partly, are not satisfied that one begins with Being, whatever reflections may underlie it, and still less with the result that Being has, namely, to pass over into Nothing,—partly, who generally know no other way than that a science begins with the presupposition of a representation,—a representation which is then analyzed, so that the result of such analysis yields the first determinate concept in the science.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"5.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0033","text":"If we likewise observed this procedure, we would have no particular object, since the beginning, as the beginning of thinking, is supposed to be wholly abstract, wholly universal, wholly form without any content; we would thus have nothing at all but the representation of a mere beginning as such. Thus it is only necessary to see what we have in this representation.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"5.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0034","text":"There is still Nothing, and Something is supposed to become. The beginning is not pure Nothing, but a Nothing from which Something is supposed to proceed; thus Being is also already contained in the beginning. The beginning therefore contains both, Being and Nothing; it is the unity of Being and Nothing;—or it is non-Being, which is at the same time Being, and Being, which is at the same time non-Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"5.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0035","text":"Further, Being and Nothing are present in the beginning as distinct; for it points to something other;—it is a non-Being that is related to Being as to an other; what begins is not yet; it is only proceeding toward Being. The beginning thus contains Being as one that removes itself from non-Being or sublates it, as something opposed to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"5.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0036","text":"But further, what begins already is, yet just as much it is also not yet. The opposites, Being and non-Being, are therefore in it in immediate union; or it is their undistinguished unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"5.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0037","text":"The analysis of the beginning would thus yield the concept of the unity of Being and non-Being,—or, in a more reflective form, of the unity of being-distinguished and being-undistinguished,—or of the identity of identity and non-identity. This concept could be regarded as the first, purest, i.e. most abstract, definition of the Absolute;—as indeed it would be, if the concern were at all with the form of definitions and with the name of the Absolute. In this sense, just as that abstract concept would be the first definition, so all further determinations and developments would be only more determinate and richer definitions of this Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"5.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0038","text":"But those who are not satisfied with Being as a beginning because it passes over into Nothing and from this the unity of Being and Nothing arises, may see whether they are more satisfied with this beginning, which begins with the representation of the beginning and with its analysis, which will indeed be correct but likewise leads to the unity of Being and Nothing, than with making Being the beginning.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"5.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","text":"Yet a further consideration must be made concerning this procedure. That analysis presupposes the representation of the beginning as known; thus it has proceeded after the example of other sciences. These presuppose their object and assume by way of request that everyone has the same representation of it and may find in it approximately the same determinations which they adduce and indicate from here and there by analysis, comparison, and other reasoning. But that which makes the absolute beginning must likewise be something otherwise known; if it is now a concrete [thing], and hence something determined in itself in manifold ways, then this relation which it is in itself is presupposed as something known; it is thereby stated as something immediate, which, however, it is not; for it is relation only as relation of distinct [things], and thus contains mediation within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"5.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","text":"Further, with the concrete [thing] there enters the contingency and arbitrariness of analysis and of the various determining. Which determinations are brought out depends upon what each person finds in his immediate contingent representation. The relation contained in a concrete [thing], a synthetic unity, is necessary only insofar as it is not found, but produced by the movement of the moments themselves to return into this unity;—a movement that is the opposite of analytical procedure, of an activity external to the matter itself and falling within the subject.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"5.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","text":"This also contains the more precise point that that with which the beginning is to be made cannot be a concrete [thing], cannot be one that contains a relation within itself. For such a [thing] presupposes a mediating and a transition from a first to an other within it, of which the concretized concrete [thing] would be the result. But the beginning is not itself to be already a first and an other; such a [thing] as is a first and an other within itself already contains a having-proceeded. What makes the beginning, the beginning itself, is therefore to be taken as something unanalyzable, in its simple unfulfilled immediacy, thus as Being, as the wholly empty [thing].","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"5.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0042","text":"If, perhaps, impatient with the consideration of the abstract beginning, one wished to say that one should not begin with the beginning, but directly with the matter, then this matter is nothing but that empty Being; for what the matter is, this is precisely what is first to emerge in the course of the science, what cannot be presupposed before it as known.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"5.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","text":"Whatever form may otherwise be adopted in order to have another beginning than empty Being, it suffers from the defects indicated. Those who remain dissatisfied with this beginning may set themselves the task of beginning otherwise, while avoiding these defects.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"5.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0044","text":"But an original beginning of philosophy, which has made itself famous in modern times, cannot be left entirely unmentioned: the beginning with the I. It arose partly from the reflection that all that follows must be derived from the first truth, partly from the need that the first truth be something known and, still more, immediately certain. This beginning is in general not such a representation as may be contingent and constituted one way in one subject and another way in another. For I, this immediate self-consciousness, at first itself appears partly as something immediate, partly as something known in a much higher sense than any other representation; something otherwise known does indeed belong to the I, but is still a content distinct from it and thus at once contingent; the I, by contrast, is the simple certainty of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"5.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","text":"But the I in general is at the same time also a concrete [thing], or rather, the I is the most concrete [thing],—the consciousness of itself as an infinitely manifold world. For the I to be the beginning and ground of philosophy, the abstraction of this concrete [thing] is required,—the absolute act whereby the I is purified from itself and enters into its consciousness as abstract I. Yet this pure I is now not something immediate, nor the known, ordinary I of our consciousness, to which science ought immediately to attach itself for everyone. That act would properly be nothing other than the elevation to the standpoint of pure knowing, at which the distinction of subjective and objective has vanished.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"5.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0046","text":"But as immediately as this elevation is demanded, it is a subjective postulate; in order to prove itself a genuine demand, the movement of the concrete I from immediate consciousness to pure knowing would have to have been exhibited and presented in itself, through its own necessity. Without this objective movement, pure knowing, also when determined as intellectual intuition, appears as an arbitrary standpoint, or even as one of the empirical states of consciousness, with respect to which it depends on whether one person finds it in himself or can produce it, while another cannot.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"5.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0047","text":"But insofar as this pure I must be essential pure knowing, while pure knowing is posited in individual consciousness only through the absolute act of self-elevation and is not immediately present in it, precisely the advantage that is supposed to arise from this beginning of philosophy is lost, namely, that it be something absolutely known, which everyone finds immediately within himself and to which further reflection can attach itself; this pure I is rather, in its abstract essence, something unknown to ordinary consciousness, something it does not find therein. There thus arises instead the disadvantage of the illusion that the subject is something known, the I of empirical self-consciousness, whereas in fact the subject is something remote from this consciousness.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"5.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0048","text":"The determination of pure knowing as I carries with it the persistent recollection of the subjective I, whose limits are supposed to be forgotten, and keeps present the representation as though the propositions and relations that emerge from the I in the further development occur in ordinary consciousness, since this is supposed to be that of which they are asserted, and can be found therein. Instead of immediate clarity, this confusion produces only an all the more glaring bewilderment and complete disorientation; externally, moreover, it has occasioned the crudest misunderstandings.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"5.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0049","text":"As regards, furthermore, the subjective determinacy of the I in general, pure knowing indeed deprives the I of its restricted significance of having its insurmountable opposition in an object. For this reason, however, it would at least be superfluous still to retain this subjective attitude and the determination of pure essence as I. Yet this determination not only brings with it that disturbing ambiguity, but, more closely considered, it also remains a subjective I. The actual development of science, which proceeds from the I, shows that the object therein has and retains the perennial determination of an Other for the I; that is, that the I from which one proceeds is not pure knowing, which has in truth overcome the opposition of consciousness, but is still entangled in appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"5.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0050","text":"Here the essential observation must further be made that, even if the I could indeed be determined in itself as pure knowing or as intellectual intuition and asserted as the beginning, in science the issue is not what may be present in itself or inwardly, but the existence of the inward in thinking, and the determinacy which such a thing has in this existence. But whatever is present at the beginning of science of intellectual intuition—or, if its object is called the eternal, the divine, the absolute—whatever is present of the eternal or absolute, this can be nothing other than the first, immediate, simple determination. Whatever richer name may be given to it than that expressed by mere being, only the question can come into consideration how such an absolute enters into thinking knowing and into the utterance of this knowing.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"5.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","text":"Intellectual intuition is indeed the forcible rejection of mediation and of demonstrative, external reflection. But what it expresses beyond simple immediacy is a concrete, containing determinations differentiated within itself. Yet the utterance and presentation of such a concrete is, as already remarked, a mediating movement, which begins from one of the determinations and proceeds to the other, even if this other returns to the first;—it is a movement which at the same time must not be arbitrary or assertoric. That from which one therefore begins in such a presentation is not the concrete itself, but only the simple immediate from which the movement proceeds. Besides, if a concrete is made the beginning, the proof is lacking which the connection of the determinations contained in the concrete requires.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"5.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","text":"Thus, if in the expression of the absolute or eternal or God (and God would have the most indisputable right for the beginning to be made with him), if in their intuition or thought there lies more than in pure being, then what lies therein is first to emerge into knowing as thinking, not as representational; whatever lies therein, however rich it may be, the determination which first emerges into knowing is a simple one; for only in the simple is there no more than the pure beginning; only the immediate is simple, for only in the immediate has there not yet been a proceeding from one to an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"5.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","text":"What is thus supposed to be uttered or contained beyond being in the richer forms of representation of the absolute or God is at the beginning only an empty word, and only being; this simple, which otherwise has no further significance, this empty, is therefore absolutely the beginning of philosophy.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"5.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0054","text":"This insight is itself so simple that this beginning as such requires neither preparation nor further introduction; and this preliminary reasoning about it could have had no intention of bringing it about, but rather of removing all preliminary matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"5.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0054"]}],"source_digest":"90884a8791cfcd3e221de73aab0a2b33ec74b9d17790b87cf2a20cc46c27bb43","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Womit muß der Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht werden?"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Womit muß der Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht werden?","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS","title":"General Division of Being","order":6,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AEDS","text":"Das Seyn ist zuerst gegen Anderes überhaupt bestimmt;\n\nZweitens ist es sich innerhalb seiner selbst bestimmend;\n\nDrittens, indem diese Vorläufigkeit des Eintheilens weggeworfen ist, ist es die abstrakte Unbestimmtheit und Unmittelbarkeit, in der es der Anfang seyn muß.\n\nNach der ersten Bestimmung theilt das Seyn sich gegen das Wesen ab, indem es weiterhin in seiner Entwickelung seine Totalität nur als Eine Sphäre des Begriffs erweist, und ihr als Moment eine andere Sphäre gegenüberstellt.\n\nNach der zweiten ist es die Sphäre, innerhalb welcher die Bestimmungen und die ganze Bewegung seiner Reflexion fällt. Das Seyn wird sich darin in den drei Bestimmungen setzen:\n\nI. als Bestimmtheit; als solche, Qualität;\n\nII. als aufgehobene Bestimmtheit; Größe, Quantität;\n\nIII. als qualitativ bestimmte Quantität; Maaß.\n\nDiese Eintheilung ist hier, wie in der Einleitung von diesen Eintheilungen überhaupt erinnert worden, eine vorläufige Anführung; ihre Bestimmungen haben erst aus der Bewegung des Seyns selbst zu entstehen, sich dadurch zu definiren und zu rechtfertigen. Über die Abweichung dieser Eintheilung von der gewöhnlichen Aufführung der Kategorien, nämlich als Quantität, Qualität, Relation und Modalität, was übrigens bei Kant nur die Titel für seine Kategorien seyn sollen, in der That aber selbst, nur allgemeinere, Kategorien sind,—ist hier nichts zu erinnern, da die ganze Ausführung das überhaupt von der gewöhnlichen Ordnung und Bedeutung der Kategorien Abweichende zeigen wird.\n\nNur dieß kann etwa bemerkt werden, daß sonst die Bestimmung der Quantität von der Qualität aufgeführt wird,—und dieß—wie das Meiste—ohne weiteren Grund. Es ist bereits gezeigt worden, daß der Anfang sich mit dem Seyn als solchem macht, daher mit dem qualitativen Seyn. Aus der Vergleichung der Qualität mit der Quantität erhellt leicht, daß jene die der Natur nach erste ist. Denn die Quantität ist die schon negativ gewordenen Qualität; die Größe ist die Bestimmtheit, die nicht mehr mit dem Seyn Eins, sondern schon von ihm unterschieden, die aufgehobene, gleichgültig gewordenen Qualität ist. Sie schließt die Veränderlichkeit des Seyns ein, ohne daß die Sache selbst, das Seyn, dessen Bestimmung sie ist, durch sie verändert werde; da hingegen die qualitative Bestimmtheit mit ihrem Seyn Eins ist, nicht darüber hinausgeht, noch innerhalb desselben steht, sondern dessen unmittelbare Beschränktheit ist. Die Qualität ist daher, als die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit die erste und mit ihr der Anfang zu machen.\n\nDas Maaß ist eine Relation, aber nicht die Relation überhaupt, sondern bestimmt der Qualität und Quantität zu einander; die Kategorien, die Kant unter der Relation befaßt, werden ganz anderwärts ihre Stelle nehmen. Das Maaß kann auch für eine Modalität, wenn man will, angesehen werden; aber indem bei Kant diese nicht mehr eine Bestimmung des Inhalts ausmachen, sondern nur die Beziehung desselben auf das Denken, auf das Subjektive, angehen soll, so ist dieß eine ganz heterogene, hierher nicht gehörige Beziehung.\n\nDie dritte Bestimmung des Seyns fällt innerhalb des Abschnittes, der Qualität, indem es sich als abstrakte Unmittelbarkeit zu einer einzelnen Bestimmtheit gegen seine anderen innerhalb seiner Sphäre herabsetzt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","text":"Das Seyn ist zuerst gegen Anderes überhaupt bestimmt;","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"6.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","text":"Zweitens ist es sich innerhalb seiner selbst bestimmend;","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"6.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","text":"Drittens, indem diese Vorläufigkeit des Eintheilens weggeworfen ist, ist es die abstrakte Unbestimmtheit und Unmittelbarkeit, in der es der Anfang seyn muß.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"6.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","text":"Nach der ersten Bestimmung theilt das Seyn sich gegen das Wesen ab, indem es weiterhin in seiner Entwickelung seine Totalität nur als Eine Sphäre des Begriffs erweist, und ihr als Moment eine andere Sphäre gegenüberstellt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"6.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","text":"Nach der zweiten ist es die Sphäre, innerhalb welcher die Bestimmungen und die ganze Bewegung seiner Reflexion fällt. Das Seyn wird sich darin in den drei Bestimmungen setzen:","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"6.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","text":"I. als Bestimmtheit; als solche, Qualität;","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"6.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","text":"II. als aufgehobene Bestimmtheit; Größe, Quantität;","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"6.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","text":"III. als qualitativ bestimmte Quantität; Maaß.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"6.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","text":"Diese Eintheilung ist hier, wie in der Einleitung von diesen Eintheilungen überhaupt erinnert worden, eine vorläufige Anführung; ihre Bestimmungen haben erst aus der Bewegung des Seyns selbst zu entstehen, sich dadurch zu definiren und zu rechtfertigen. Über die Abweichung dieser Eintheilung von der gewöhnlichen Aufführung der Kategorien, nämlich als Quantität, Qualität, Relation und Modalität, was übrigens bei Kant nur die Titel für seine Kategorien seyn sollen, in der That aber selbst, nur allgemeinere, Kategorien sind,—ist hier nichts zu erinnern, da die ganze Ausführung das überhaupt von der gewöhnlichen Ordnung und Bedeutung der Kategorien Abweichende zeigen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"6.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","text":"Nur dieß kann etwa bemerkt werden, daß sonst die Bestimmung der Quantität von der Qualität aufgeführt wird,—und dieß—wie das Meiste—ohne weiteren Grund. Es ist bereits gezeigt worden, daß der Anfang sich mit dem Seyn als solchem macht, daher mit dem qualitativen Seyn. Aus der Vergleichung der Qualität mit der Quantität erhellt leicht, daß jene die der Natur nach erste ist. Denn die Quantität ist die schon negativ gewordenen Qualität; die Größe ist die Bestimmtheit, die nicht mehr mit dem Seyn Eins, sondern schon von ihm unterschieden, die aufgehobene, gleichgültig gewordenen Qualität ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"6.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","text":"Sie schließt die Veränderlichkeit des Seyns ein, ohne daß die Sache selbst, das Seyn, dessen Bestimmung sie ist, durch sie verändert werde; da hingegen die qualitative Bestimmtheit mit ihrem Seyn Eins ist, nicht darüber hinausgeht, noch innerhalb desselben steht, sondern dessen unmittelbare Beschränktheit ist. Die Qualität ist daher, als die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit die erste und mit ihr der Anfang zu machen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"6.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","text":"Das Maaß ist eine Relation, aber nicht die Relation überhaupt, sondern bestimmt der Qualität und Quantität zu einander; die Kategorien, die Kant unter der Relation befaßt, werden ganz anderwärts ihre Stelle nehmen. Das Maaß kann auch für eine Modalität, wenn man will, angesehen werden; aber indem bei Kant diese nicht mehr eine Bestimmung des Inhalts ausmachen, sondern nur die Beziehung desselben auf das Denken, auf das Subjektive, angehen soll, so ist dieß eine ganz heterogene, hierher nicht gehörige Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"6.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","text":"Die dritte Bestimmung des Seyns fällt innerhalb des Abschnittes, der Qualität, indem es sich als abstrakte Unmittelbarkeit zu einer einzelnen Bestimmtheit gegen seine anderen innerhalb seiner Sphäre herabsetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"6.13"}],"sha256":"e3cf82be4e627496439a1e1b07e3b76dd3c7bafc3bcb03bfcebf4b0d0889bdc5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101711136199Z_9bc4359d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"General Division of Being","source_sha256":"e3cf82be4e627496439a1e1b07e3b76dd3c7bafc3bcb03bfcebf4b0d0889bdc5","sha256":"86d339e60a07dadb01b2091a2002e187203caf0330aa297a1583bcccac3cdd72","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:17:11.136220+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","text":"Being is at first determined in opposition to Other in general;","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"6.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","text":"Secondly, it is self-determining within itself;","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"6.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","text":"Thirdly, when this preliminary character of dividing has been cast aside, it is the abstract indeterminacy and immediacy in which it must be the beginning.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"6.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","text":"According to the first determination, Being divides itself off from Essence, in that, further on in its development, it proves its totality to be only one sphere of the Concept, and sets another sphere over against it as a moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"6.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","text":"According to the second, it is the sphere within which the determinations and the entire movement of its reflection fall. Being will posit itself therein in the three determinations:","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"6.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","text":"I. as determinacy; as such, quality;","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"6.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","text":"II. as sublated determinacy; magnitude, quantity;","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"6.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","text":"III. as qualitatively determined quantity; measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"6.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","text":"This division is here, as has been noted in the Introduction concerning these divisions in general, a preliminary presentation; its determinations are first to arise from the movement of Being itself, thereby to define and justify themselves. Concerning the divergence of this division from the customary enumeration of the categories, namely as quantity, quality, relation, and modality—which, moreover, in Kant are supposed to be only the titles for his categories, but are in fact themselves, only more general, categories—nothing is to be remarked here, since the entire exposition will show what in general diverges from the customary order and significance of the categories.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"6.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","text":"Only this may perhaps be remarked, that otherwise the determination of quantity is enumerated before quality,—and this—as is the case with most things—without further ground. It has already been shown that the beginning is made with Being as such, hence with qualitative Being. From the comparison of quality with quantity it is readily apparent that the former is first by nature. For quantity is quality that has already become negative; magnitude is determinacy which is no longer one with Being, but is already distinguished from it, is sublated quality that has become indifferent.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"6.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","text":"It includes the alterability of Being, without the thing itself, Being, whose determinacy it is, being altered through it; whereas qualitative determinacy is one with its Being, does not go beyond it, nor stand within it, but is its immediate limitation. Quality is therefore, as immediate determinacy, the first, and the beginning is to be made with it.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"6.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","text":"Measure is a relation, but not relation in general; rather, it is the determinate relation of quality and quantity to one another; the categories which Kant comprehends under relation will take their place quite elsewhere. Measure can also, if one wishes, be regarded as a modality; but since in Kant this is no longer supposed to constitute a determination of content, but to concern only the relation of that content to thinking, to the subjective, this is an entirely heterogeneous relation, not belonging here.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"6.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","text":"The third determination of Being falls within the section on quality, inasmuch as it lowers itself, as abstract immediacy, to a single determinacy over against its others within its sphere.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"6.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"b14ff9fa9377113bbbede7edbe2940ef6aa699bbfd7d9419af98a246299a23ee","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung des Seyns"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung des Seyns","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ","title":"First Section. Determinateness (Quality).","order":7,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_EABQ","text":"Das Seyn ist das unbestimmte Unmittelbare; es ist frei von der Bestimmtheit gegen das Wesen, so wie noch von jeder, die es innerhalb seiner selbst erhalten kann. Dieß reflexionslose Seyn ist das Seyn, wie es unmittelbar nur an ihm selber ist. Weil es unbestimmt ist, ist es qualitätsloses Seyn; aber an sich kommt ihm der Charakter der Unbestimmtheit nur im Gegensatze gegen das Bestimmte oder Qualitative zu. Dem Seyn überhaupt tritt aber das bestimmte Seyn als solches gegenüber, damit aber macht seine Unbestimmtheit selbst seine Qualität aus. Es wird sich daher zeigen, daß das erste Seyn, an sich bestimmtes, und hiermit\n\nZweitens, daß es in das Daseyn übergeht, Daseyn ist, daß aber dieses als endliches Seyn sich aufhebt, und in die unendliche Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst,\n\nDrittens in das Fürsichseyn übergeht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","text":"Das Seyn ist das unbestimmte Unmittelbare; es ist frei von der Bestimmtheit gegen das Wesen, so wie noch von jeder, die es innerhalb seiner selbst erhalten kann. Dieß reflexionslose Seyn ist das Seyn, wie es unmittelbar nur an ihm selber ist. Weil es unbestimmt ist, ist es qualitätsloses Seyn; aber an sich kommt ihm der Charakter der Unbestimmtheit nur im Gegensatze gegen das Bestimmte oder Qualitative zu. Dem Seyn überhaupt tritt aber das bestimmte Seyn als solches gegenüber, damit aber macht seine Unbestimmtheit selbst seine Qualität aus. Es wird sich daher zeigen, daß das erste Seyn, an sich bestimmtes, und hiermit","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"7.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","text":"Zweitens, daß es in das Daseyn übergeht, Daseyn ist, daß aber dieses als endliches Seyn sich aufhebt, und in die unendliche Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst,","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"7.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","text":"Drittens in das Fürsichseyn übergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"7.3"}],"sha256":"ec80590133d4656fa84d72328ad06c197742ff1f6bd31acfa1f19a3e8a38d624","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101714289112Z_55749258","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Section. Determinateness (Quality).","source_sha256":"ec80590133d4656fa84d72328ad06c197742ff1f6bd31acfa1f19a3e8a38d624","sha256":"d9fea3d1bb3584ffaa484df7990decf0212bb750f78f4ff64e72bdd4d8faed8b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:17:14.289140+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","text":"Being is the indeterminate immediate; it is free from determinateness in relation to essence, as likewise still from every [determinateness] that it can receive within itself. This reflectionless being is being as it immediately is only in itself. Because it is indeterminate, it is qualityless being; but in itself the character of indeterminateness belongs to it only in opposition to the determinate or qualitative. But determinate being as such confronts being in general; thereby its indeterminateness itself constitutes its quality. It will therefore show itself that the first being, determinate in itself, and thereby","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"7.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","text":"Secondly, that it passes over into determinate being, is determinate being, but that this, as finite being, sublates itself, and into the infinite relation of being to itself,","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"7.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","text":"Thirdly, passes over into being-for-self.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"7.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"4b6541c396b2415bdb56fccf07fb1f1a74b63403148e0d4bf8f3fb4d39a9783c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Erster Abschnitt. Bestimmtheit (Qualität)."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Erster Abschnitt. Bestimmtheit (Qualität).","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN","title":"A. Being.","order":8,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_SEYN","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Seyn.\n\n## A. Seyn.\n\nSeyn, reines Seyn,—ohne alle weitere Bestimmung. In seiner unbestimmten Unmittelbarkeit ist es nur sich selbst gleich, und auch nicht ungleich gegen Anderes, hat keine Verschiedenheit innerhalb seiner, noch nach Außen. Durch irgend eine Bestimmung oder Inhalt, der in ihm unterschieden, oder wodurch es als unterschieden von einem Anderen gesetzt würde, würde es nicht in seiner Reinheit festgehalten. Es ist die reine Unbestimmtheit und Leere.—Es ist nichts in ihm anzuschauen, wenn von Anschauen hier gesprochen werden kann; oder es ist nur dieß reine, leere Anschauen selbst. Es ist eben so wenig etwas in ihm zu denken, oder es ist ebenso nur dieß leere Denken. Das Seyn, das unbestimmte Unmittelbare ist in der That Nichts, und nicht mehr noch weniger als Nichts.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"8.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","text":"## A. Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"8.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","text":"Seyn, reines Seyn,—ohne alle weitere Bestimmung. In seiner unbestimmten Unmittelbarkeit ist es nur sich selbst gleich, und auch nicht ungleich gegen Anderes, hat keine Verschiedenheit innerhalb seiner, noch nach Außen. Durch irgend eine Bestimmung oder Inhalt, der in ihm unterschieden, oder wodurch es als unterschieden von einem Anderen gesetzt würde, würde es nicht in seiner Reinheit festgehalten. Es ist die reine Unbestimmtheit und Leere.—Es ist nichts in ihm anzuschauen, wenn von Anschauen hier gesprochen werden kann; oder es ist nur dieß reine, leere Anschauen selbst. Es ist eben so wenig etwas in ihm zu denken, oder es ist ebenso nur dieß leere Denken. Das Seyn, das unbestimmte Unmittelbare ist in der That Nichts, und nicht mehr noch weniger als Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"8.3"}],"sha256":"0d9e1d90df6d218594d36aef0f8d08cca739cf8602b453596a93e5ce0a494cb0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101718547269Z_41379ee1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Being.","source_sha256":"0d9e1d90df6d218594d36aef0f8d08cca739cf8602b453596a93e5ce0a494cb0","sha256":"385d3e0cf355aa3028451066ad65a8600dfe580778a07c40692262b9191d0501","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:17:18.547291+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","text":"## First Chapter. Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"8.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","text":"## A. Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"8.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","text":"Being, pure being,—without any further determination. In its indeterminate immediacy it is only equal to itself, and also not unequal in relation to an other; it has no diversity within itself, nor externally. Through any determination or content which would be distinguished in it, or through which it would be posited as distinguished from an other, it would not be retained in its purity. It is pure indeterminateness and emptiness.—There is nothing to intuit in it, if intuition may be spoken of here; or it is only this pure, empty intuition itself. There is just as little anything to think in it, or it is likewise only this empty thinking. Being, the indeterminate immediate, is in fact Nothing, and neither more nor less than Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"8.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"3185d040ed7111c7442d6fa543f5c136151141b4fe75bfe72007f83a62d16bb2","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Seyn."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Seyn.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC","title":"B. Nothing.","order":9,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BNIC","text":"Nichts, das reine Nichts; es ist einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst, vollkommene Leerheit, Bestimmungs- und Inhaltslosigkeit; Ununterschiedenheit in ihm selbst.—Insofern Anschauen oder Denken hier erwähnt werden kann, so gilt es als ein Unterschied, ob etwas oder nichts angeschaut oder gedacht wird. Nichts Anschauen oder Denken hat also eine Bedeutung; beide werden unterschieden, so ist (existirt) Nichts in unserem Anschauen oder Denken; oder vielmehr ist es das leere Anschauen und Denken selbst; und dasselbe leere Anschauen oder Denken, als das reine Seyn.—Nichts ist somit dieselbe Bestimmung oder vielmehr Bestimmungslosigkeit, und damit überhaupt dasselbe, was das reine Seyn ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","text":"Nichts, das reine Nichts; es ist einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst, vollkommene Leerheit, Bestimmungs- und Inhaltslosigkeit; Ununterschiedenheit in ihm selbst.—Insofern Anschauen oder Denken hier erwähnt werden kann, so gilt es als ein Unterschied, ob etwas oder nichts angeschaut oder gedacht wird. Nichts Anschauen oder Denken hat also eine Bedeutung; beide werden unterschieden, so ist (existirt) Nichts in unserem Anschauen oder Denken; oder vielmehr ist es das leere Anschauen und Denken selbst; und dasselbe leere Anschauen oder Denken, als das reine Seyn.—Nichts ist somit dieselbe Bestimmung oder vielmehr Bestimmungslosigkeit, und damit überhaupt dasselbe, was das reine Seyn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"9.1"}],"sha256":"b4dee298884d7a8e97aab1b15b62bc3228c2200789aa77ac5e17780dbee5b4f6","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101722193671Z_e22dd940","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Nothing.","source_sha256":"b4dee298884d7a8e97aab1b15b62bc3228c2200789aa77ac5e17780dbee5b4f6","sha256":"0b6e79f296784d32929821d69dac9b97bc6859024b4af82f1d2e186921797557","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:17:22.193696+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","text":"Nothing, pure nothing; it is simple equality with itself, complete emptiness, absence of determination and content; undifferentiatedness within itself.—In so far as intuiting or thinking can be mentioned here, it counts as a difference whether something or nothing is intuited or thought. To intuit or think nothing therefore has a meaning; the two are distinguished, so Nothing is (exists) in our intuiting or thinking; or rather, it is empty intuiting and thinking itself; and the same empty intuiting or thinking, as pure Being.—Nothing is thus the same determination, or rather absence of determination, and thereby altogether the same as pure Being is.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"9.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001"]}],"source_digest":"c95945153d7dbd6fea4c2a243f28a04120891412b7c824dc6e6765172cb48721","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Nichts."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Nichts.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS","title":"1. Unity of Being and Nothing.","order":10,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_1EDS","text":"## C. Werden.\n\n## 1. Einheit des Seyns und Nichts.\n\nDas reine Seyn und das reine Nichts ist also dasselbe. Was die Wahrheit ist, ist weder das Seyn, noch das Nichts, sondern daß das Seyn in Nichts, und das Nichts in Seyn,—nicht übergeht,—sondern übergegangen ist. Aber eben so sehr ist die Wahrheit nicht ihre Ununterschiedenheit, sondern daß sie nicht dasselbe, daß sie absolut unterschieden, aber ebenso ungetrennt und untrennbar sind, und unmittelbar jedes in seinem Gegentheil verschwindet. Ihre Wahrheit ist also diese Bewegung des unmittelbaren Verschwindens des einen in dem andern; das Werden; eine Bewegung, worin beide unterschieden sind, aber durch einen Unterschied, der sich eben so unmittelbar aufgelöst hat.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","text":"## C. Werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"10.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","text":"## 1. Einheit des Seyns und Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"10.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","text":"Das reine Seyn und das reine Nichts ist also dasselbe. Was die Wahrheit ist, ist weder das Seyn, noch das Nichts, sondern daß das Seyn in Nichts, und das Nichts in Seyn,—nicht übergeht,—sondern übergegangen ist. Aber eben so sehr ist die Wahrheit nicht ihre Ununterschiedenheit, sondern daß sie nicht dasselbe, daß sie absolut unterschieden, aber ebenso ungetrennt und untrennbar sind, und unmittelbar jedes in seinem Gegentheil verschwindet. Ihre Wahrheit ist also diese Bewegung des unmittelbaren Verschwindens des einen in dem andern; das Werden; eine Bewegung, worin beide unterschieden sind, aber durch einen Unterschied, der sich eben so unmittelbar aufgelöst hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"10.3"}],"sha256":"796b897d77cfe544f689d75359ea69b295305e4776f0dce037efc12a4891edf0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101725164736Z_d05f52e1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"1. Unity of Being and Nothing.","source_sha256":"796b897d77cfe544f689d75359ea69b295305e4776f0dce037efc12a4891edf0","sha256":"0741d0c9bbd6e6379a9956ee8eec30e76d373786a2c0a62e313e0633d578364a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:17:25.164761+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","text":"## C. Becoming.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"10.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","text":"## 1. Unity of Being and Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"10.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing are therefore the same. What the truth is, is neither Being nor Nothing, but that Being into Nothing, and Nothing into Being,—does not pass over,—but has passed over. But just as much the truth is not their indistinguishableness, but that they are not the same, that they are absolutely distinct, yet equally unseparated and inseparable, and each immediately vanishes in its opposite. Their truth is therefore this movement of the immediate vanishing of the one in the other; Becoming; a movement in which both are distinct, but through a distinction which has just as immediately dissolved itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"10.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"7c4d8bfc851292c1f8cee77581e5ffc79872dd6a4086012c0ea110d29352d009","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"1. Einheit des Seyns und Nichts."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"1. Einheit des Seyns und Nichts.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1","title":"Remark 1.","order":11,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ANM1","text":"Nichts pflegt dem Etwas entgegengesetzt zu werden; Etwas aber ist schon ein bestimmtes Seyendes, das sich von anderem Etwas unterscheidet; so ist also auch das dem Etwas entgegengesetzte Nichts, das Nichts von irgend Etwas, ein bestimmtes Nichts.\n\nHier aber ist das Nichts in seiner unbestimmten Einfachheit zu nehmen. —Wollte man es für richtiger halten, daß statt des Nichts dem Seyn das Nichtseyn entgegengesetzt würde, so wäre in Rücksicht auf das Resultat nichts dawider zu haben, denn im Nichtseyn ist die Beziehung auf das Seyn enthalten; es ist Beides, Seyn und die Negation desselben, in Einem ausgesprochen, das Nichts, wie es im Werden ist. Aber es ist zunächst nicht um die Form der Entgegensetzung, d. i. zugleich der Beziehung zu thun, sondern um die abstrakte, unmittelbare Negation, das Nichts rein für sich, die beziehungslose Verneinung,—was man, wenn man will, auch durch das bloße: Nicht ausdrücken könnte.\n\nDen einfachen Gedanken des reinen Seyns haben die Eleaten zuerst, vorzüglich Parmenides als das Absolute und als einzige Wahrheit, und in den übergebliebenen Fragmenten von ihm, mit der reinen Begeisterung des Denkens, das zum ersten Male sich in seiner absoluten Abstraktion erfaßt, ausgesprochen: nur das Seyn ist, und das Nichts ist gar nicht.—In orientalischen Systemen, wesentlich im Buddaismus ist bekanntlich das Nichts, das Leere, das absolute Princip.—Der tiefsinnige Heraklit hob gegen jene einfache und einseitige Abstraktion den höheren totalen Begriff des Werdens hervor, und sagte: das Seyn ist so wenig, als das Nichts, oder auch Alles fließt, das heißt, Alles ist Werden.—Die populären, besonders orientalischen Sprüche, daß alles, was ist, den Keim seines Vergehens in seiner Geburt selbst habe, der Tod umgekehrt der Eingang in neues Leben sey, drücken im Grunde dieselbe Einigung des Seyns und Nichts aus. Aber diese Ausdrücke haben ein Substrat, an dem der Übergang geschieht; Seyn und Nichts werden in der Zeit auseinander gehalten, als in ihr abwechselnd vorgestellt, nicht aber in ihrer Abstraktion gedacht, und daher auch nicht so, daß sie an und für sich dasselbe sind.\n\nEx nihilo nihil fit—ist einer der Sätze, denen in der Metaphysik große Bedeutung zugeschrieben wurde. Es ist darin entweder nur die gehaltlose Tautologie zu sehen: Nichts ist Nichts; oder wenn das Werden wirkliche Bedeutung darin haben sollte, so ist vielmehr, indem nur Nichts aus Nichts wird, in der That kein Werden darin vorhanden, denn Nichts bleibt darin Nichts. Das Werden enthält, daß Nichts nicht Nichts bleibe, sondern in sein Anderes, in das Seyn übergehe. —Wenn die spätere vornehmlich christliche Metaphysik den Satz, aus Nichts werde Nichts, verwarf, so behauptete sie einen Übergang von Nichts in Seyn; so synthetisch oder bloß vorstellend sie auch diesen Satz nahm, so ist doch auch in der unvollkommensten Vereinigung ein Punkt enthalten, worin Seyn und Nichts zusammentreffen, und ihre Unterschiedenheit verschwindet.—Seine eigentliche Wichtigkeit hat der Satz: Aus Nichts wird Nichts, Nichts ist eben Nichts, durch seinen Gegensatz gegen das Werden überhaupt und damit auch gegen die Erschaffung der Welt aus Nichts. Diejenigen, welche den Satz: Nichts ist eben Nichts, sogar sich dafür ereifernd, behaupten, sind bewußtlos darüber, daß sie damit dem abstrakten Pantheismus der Eleaten, der Sache nach auch dem spinozistischen, beipflichten. Die philosophische Ansicht, welcher: Seyn ist nur Seyn, Nichts ist nur Nichts, als Princip gilt, verdient den Namen Identitätssystem; diese abstrakte Identität ist das Wesen des Pantheismus.\n\nWenn das Resultat, daß Seyn und Nichts dasselbe ist, für sich auffällt oder paradox scheint, so ist hierauf nicht weiter zu achten; es wäre sich vielmehr über jene Verwunderung zu verwundern, die sich so neu in der Philosophie zeigt und vergißt, daß in dieser Wissenschaft ganz andere Bestimmungen vorkommen, als im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn und im sogenannten gemeinen Menschenverstande, der nicht gerade der gesunde, sondern auch der zu Abstraktionen und zu dem Glauben oder vielmehr Aberglauben an Abstraktionen heraufgebildete Verstand ist. Es wäre nicht schwer, diese Einheit von Seyn und Nichts, in jedem Beispiele, in jedem Wirklichen oder Gedanken aufzuzeigen. Es muß dasselbe, was oben von der Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittelung, (welche letztere eine Beziehung aufeinander, damit Negation enthält), vom Seyn und Nichts gesagt werden, daß es nirgend im Himmel und auf Erden Etwas gebe, was nicht beides Seyn und Nichts in sich enthielte. Freilich da hierbei von einem irgend Etwas und Wirklichem die Rede wird, so sind darin jene Bestimmungen nicht mehr in der vollkommenen Unwahrheit, in der sie als Seyn und Nichts sind, vorhanden, sondern in einer weitern Bestimmung, und werden z.B. als Positives und Negatives aufgefaßt, jenes das gesetzte, reflektirte Seyn, dieses das gesetzte, reflektirte Nichts; aber Positives und Negatives enthalten jenes das Seyn, dieses das Nichts als ihre abstrakte Grundlage.—So in Gott selbst enthält die Qualität, Thätigkeit, Schöpfung, Macht u.s.f. wesentlich die Bestimmung des Negativen,—sie sind ein Hervorbringen eines Anderen. Aber eine empirische Erläuterung von jener Behauptung durch Beispiele wäre hier ganz und gar überflüssig. Da nunmehr diese Einheit von Seyn und Nichts als erste Wahrheit ein für allemal zu Grunde liegt, und das Element von allem Folgenden ausmacht, so sind außer dem Werden selbst, alle ferneren logischen Bestimmungen: Daseyn, Qualität, überhaupt alle Begriffe der Philosophie, Beispiele dieser Einheit.—Aber der sich so nennende gemeine oder gesunde Menschenverstand mag auf den Versuch hingewiesen werden, insofern er die Ungetrenntheit des Seyns und Nichts verwirft, sich ein Beispiel ausfindig zu machen, worin eins vom andern (Etwas von Grenze, Schranke, oder das Unendliche, Gott, wie so eben erwähnt, von Thätigkeit) getrennt zu finden sey. Nur die leeren Gedankendinge, Seyn und Nichts, selbst, sind diese Getrennte, und sie sind es, die der Wahrheit, der Ungetrenntheit beider, die allenthalben vor uns ist, von jenem Verstande vorgezogen werden.\n\nMan kann nicht die Absicht haben wollen, den Verwirrungen, in welche sich das gewöhnliche Bewußtseyn bei einem solchen logischen Satze versetzt, nach allen Seiten hin begegnen zu wollen, denn sie sind unerschöpflich. Es können nur einige erwähnt werden. Ein Grund solcher Verwirrung ist unter andern, daß das Bewußtseyn zu solchem abstrakten logischen Satze Vorstellungen von einem konkreten Etwas mitbringt und vergißt, daß von einem solchen nicht die Rede ist, sondern nur von den reinen Abstraktionen des Seyns und Nichts, und daß diese allein festzuhalten sind.\n\nSeyn und Nichtseyn ist dasselbe; also ist es dasselbe, ob ich bin oder nicht bin, ob dieses Haus ist oder nicht ist, ob diese hundert Thaler in meinem Vermögenszustand sind oder nicht.—Dieser Schluß oder Anwendung jenes Satzes verändert dessen Sinn vollkommen. Der Satz enthält die reinen Abstraktionen des Seyns und Nichts; die Anwendung aber macht ein bestimmtes Seyn und bestimmtes Nichts daraus. Allein vom bestimmten Seyn ist, wie gesagt, hier nicht die Rede. Ein bestimmtes, ein endliches Seyn ist ein solches, das sich auf anderes bezieht; es ist ein Inhalt, der im Verhältnisse der Nothwendigkeit mit anderem Inhalte, mit der ganzen Welt, steht. In Rücksicht des wechselbestimmenden Zusammenhangs des Ganzen konnte die Metaphysik die—im Grunde tautologische—Behauptung machen, daß wenn ein Stäubchen zerstört würde, das ganze Universum zusammenstürzte. In den Instanzen, die gegen den in Rede stehenden Satz gemacht werden, erscheint etwas als nicht gleichgültig, ob es sey oder nicht sey, nicht um des Seyns oder Nichtseyns willen, sondern seines Inhalts willen, der es mit anderem zusammenhängt. Wenn ein bestimmter Inhalt, irgend ein bestimmtes Daseyn vorausgesetzt wird, so ist dieß Daseyn, weil es bestimmtes ist, in mannigfaltiger Beziehung auf anderen Inhalt; es ist für dasselbe nicht gleichgültig, ob ein gewisser anderer Inhalt, mit dem es in Beziehung steht, ist oder nicht ist; denn nur durch solche Beziehung ist es wesentlich das, was es ist. Dasselbe ist der Fall in dem Vorstellen (indem wir das Nichtseyn in dem bestimmteren Sinne des Vorstellens gegen die Wirklichkeit nehmen), in dessen Zusammenhange das Seyn oder die Abwesenheit eines Inhalts, der als bestimmt mit anderem in Beziehung vorgestellt wird, nicht gleichgültig ist.—Diese Betrachtung enthält dasselbe, was ein Hauptmoment in der Kantischen Kritik des ontologischen Beweises vom Daseyn Gottes ausmacht, auf welche jedoch hier nur im Betreff des in ihr vorkommenden Unterschieds von Seyn und Nichts überhaupt und von bestimmtem Seyn oder Nichtseyn Rücksicht genommen wird.—Bekanntlich wurde in jenem sogenannten Beweise der Begriff eines Wesens vorausgesetzt, dem alle Realitäten zukommen, somit auch die Existenz, die gleichfalls als eine der Realitäten angenommen wurde. Die Kantische Kritik hielt sich vornehmlich daran, daß die Existenz oder das Seyn (was hier für gleichbedeutend gilt) keine Eigenschaft oder kein reales Prädikat sey, das heiße, nicht ein Begriff von etwas, was zu dem Begriffe eines Dinges hinzukommen könne. [6] —Kant will damit sagen, daß Seyn keine Inhaltsbestimmung sey.—Also enthalte, fährt er fort, das Mögliche nicht mehr als das Wirkliche; hundert wirkliche Thaler enthalten nicht das Mindeste mehr, als hundert mögliche;—nämlich jene haben keine andere Inhaltsbestimmung als diese. Für diesen als isolirt betrachteten Inhalt ist es in der That gleichgültig, zu seyn oder nicht zu seyn; es liegt in ihm kein Unterschied des Seyns oder Nichtseyns, dieser Unterschied berührt ihn überhaupt gar nicht; die hundert Thaler werden nicht weniger, wenn sie nicht sind, und nicht mehr, wenn sie sind. Ein Unterschied muß erst anderswoher kommen. —\"Hingegen, erinnert Kant, in meinem Vermögenszustande ist mehr bei hundert wirklichen Thalern, als bei dem bloßen Begriff derselben, oder bei ihrer Möglichkeit. Denn der Gegenstand ist bei der Wirklichkeit nicht bloß in meinem Begriff analytisch enthalten, sondern kommt zu meinem Begriffe, (der eine Bestimmung meines Zustandes ist,) synthetisch hinzu, ohne daß durch dieses Seyn außer meinem Begriffe, diese gedachten hundert Thaler selbst im mindesten vermehrt würden.\"\n\n[6] Kants Kritik der r. Vern. 2te Aufl. S. 628ff.\n\nEs werden hier zweierlei Zustände, um bei den Kantischen Ausdrücken, die nicht ohne verworrene Schwerfälligkeit sind, zu bleiben, vorausgesetzt, der eine, welchen Kant den Begriff nennt, darunter die Vorstellung zu verstehen ist, und ein anderer, der Vermögenszustand. Für den einen wie für den andern, das Vermögen wie das Vorstellen, sind hundert Thaler eine Inhaltsbestimmung, oder \"sie kommen zu einem solchen, wie Kant sich ausdrückt, synthetisch hinzu;\" Ich als Besitzer von hundert Thalern, oder als Nichtbesitzer derselben, oder auch ich als mir hundert Thaler vorstellend, oder sie nicht vorstellend, ist allerdings ein verschiedener Inhalt. Allgemeiner gefaßt: Die Abstraktionen von Seyn und Nichts hören beide auf, Abstraktionen zu seyn, indem sie einen bestimmten Inhalt erhalten; Seyn ist dann Realität, das bestimmte Seyn von Thalern, das Nichts Negation, das bestimmte Nichtseyn von denselben. Diese Inhaltsbestimmtheit selbst, die hundert Thaler, auch abstrakt für sich gefaßt, ist in dem einen unverändert dasselbe, was in dem andern. Indem aber ferner das Seyn als Vermögens-Zustand genommen wird, treten die hundert Thaler in Beziehung zu einem Zustand, und für diesen ist solche Bestimmtheit, die sie sind, nicht gleichgültig; ihr Seyn oder Nichtseyn ist nur Veränderung; sie sind in die Sphäre des Daseyns versetzt. Wenn daher gegen die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts urgirt wird, es sey doch nicht gleichgültig, ob dieß und jenes (die Thaler) sey oder nicht sey, so ist es eine Täuschung, daß wir den Unterschied bloß aufs Seyn und Nichtseyn hinausschieben, ob ich die hundert Thaler habe oder nicht habe—eine Täuschung, die wie gezeigt, auf der einseitigen Abstraktion beruht, welche das bestimmte Daseyn, das in solchen Beispielen vorhanden ist, wegläßt und bloß das Seyn und Nichtseyn festhält; wie sie umgekehrt das abstrakte Seyn und Nichts, das aufgefaßt werden soll, in ein bestimmtes Seyn und Nichts, in ein Daseyn, verwandelt. Erst das Daseyn enthält den realen Unterschied von Seyn und Nichts, nämlich ein Etwas und ein Anderes. —Dieser reale Unterschied schwebt der Vorstellung vor, statt des abstrakten Seyns und reinen Nichts, und ihrem nur gemeinten Unterschiede.\n\nWie Kant sich ausdrückt, so kommt \"durch die Existenz etwas in den Kontext der gesammten Erfahrung,\" \"wir bekommen dadurch einen Gegenstand der Wahrnehmung mehr, aber unser Begriff von dem Gegenstande wird dadurch nicht vermehrt.\"\n\nDieß heißt, wie aus dem Erläuterten hervorgeht, so viel, durch die Existenz, wesentlich darum weil Etwas bestimmte Existenz ist, ist es in dem Zusammenhang mit Anderem, und unter anderem auch mit einem Wahrnehmenden.—\"Der Begriff der hundert Thaler, sagt Kant, werde nicht durch das Wahrnehmen vermehrt.\" Der Begriff heißt hier die vorhin bemerkten isolirt vorgestellten hundert Thaler. In dieser isolirten Weise sind sie zwar ein empirischer Inhalt, aber abgeschnitten, ohne Zusammenhang und Bestimmtheit gegen Anderes; die Form der Identität mit sich benimmt ihnen die Beziehung auf anderes und macht sie gleichgültig, ob sie wahrgenommen seyen oder nicht. Aber dieser sogenannte Begriff der hundert Thaler ist ein falscher Begriff, die Form der einfachen Beziehung auf sich gehört solchem begränzten, endlichen Inhalt nicht selbst; es ist eine ihm vom subjektiven Verstande angethane und geliehene Form; hundert Thaler sind nicht ein sich auf sich Beziehendes, sondern ein Veränderliches und Vergängliches.\n\nDas Denken oder Vorstellen, dem nur ein bestimmtes Seyn, das Daseyn, vorschwebt, ist zu dem erwähnten Anfange der Wissenschaft zurück zu weisen, welchen Parmenides gemacht hat, der sein Vorstellen und damit auch das Vorstellen der Folgezeit zu dem reinen Gedanken, dem Seyn als solchen, geläutert und erhoben, und damit das Element der Wissenschaft erschaffen hat.—Was das Erste in der Wissenschaft ist, hat sich müssen geschichtlich als das Erste zeigen. Und das Eleatische Eine oder Seyn haben wir für das Erste des Wissens vom Gedanken anzusehen; das Wasser und dergleichen materielle Principien sollen wohl das Allgemeine seyn, aber sind als Materien nicht reine Gedanken; die Zahlen sind weder der erste einfache noch der bei sich bleibende, sondern der sich selbst ganz äußerliche Gedanke.\n\nDie Zurückweisung vom besonderen endlichen Seyn zum Seyn als solchen in seiner ganz abstrakten Allgemeinheit ist wie als die allererste theoretische so auch sogar praktische Forderung anzusehen. Wenn nämlich ein Aufhebens von den hundert Thalern gemacht wird, daß es in meinem Vermögenszustand einen Unterschied mache, ob ich sie habe oder nicht, noch mehr ob Ich sey oder nicht, ob Anderes sey oder nicht, so kann—ohne zu erwähnen, daß es Vermögenszustände geben wird, für die solcher Besitz von hundert Thalern gleichgültig seyn wird,—daran erinnert werden, daß der Mensch sich zu dieser abstrakten Allgemeinheit in seiner Gesinnung erheben soll, in welcher es ihm in der That gleichgültig sey, ob die hundert Thaler, sie mögen ein quantitatives Verhältniß zu seinem Vermögenszustand haben, welches sie wollen, seyen oder ob sie nicht seyen, ebenso sehr als es ihm gleichgültig sey, ob er sey oder nicht, d. i. im endlichen Leben sey oder nicht (denn ein Zustand, bestimmtes Seyn ist gemeint) u.s.f. —selbst si fractus illabatur orbis, impavidum ferient ruinae, hat ein Römer gesagt, und der Christ soll sich noch mehr in dieser Gleichgültigkeit befinden.\n\nEs ist noch die unmittelbare Verbindung anzumerken, in welcher die Erhebung über die hundert Thaler und die endlichen Dinge überhaupt mit dem ontologischen Beweise und der angeführten kantischen Kritik desselben steht. Diese Kritik hat sich durch ihr populäres Beispiel allgemein plausibel gemacht; wer weiß nicht, daß hundert wirkliche Thaler verschieden sind von hundert bloß möglichen Thalern? daß sie einen Unterschied in meinem Vermögenszustand ausmachen? Weil sich so an den hundert Thalern diese Verschiedenheit hervorthut, so ist der Begriff d. h. die Inhaltsbestimmtheit als leere Möglichkeit, und das Seyn verschieden von einander; also ist auch Gottes Begriff von seinem Seyn verschieden, und so wenig ich aus der Möglichkeit der hundert Thaler ihre Wirklichkeit herausbringen kann, eben so wenig kann ich aus dem Begriffe Gottes seine Existenz \"herausklauben\"; aus diesem Herausklauben aber der Existenz Gottes aus seinem Begriffe soll der ontologische Beweis bestehen. Wenn es nun allerdings seine Richtigkeit hat, daß Begriff vom Seyn verschieden ist, so ist noch mehr Gott verschieden von den hundert Thalern und den anderen endlichen Dingen. Es ist die Definition der endlichen Dinge, daß in ihnen Begriff und Seyn verschieden, Begriff und Realität, Seele und Leib, trennbar, sie damit vergänglich und sterblich sind; die abstrakte Definition Gottes ist dagegen eben dieß, daß sein Begriff und sein Seyn ungetrennt und untrennbar sind. Die wahrhafte Kritik der Kategorien und der Vernunft ist gerade diese, das Erkennen über diesen Unterschied zu verständigen und dasselbe abzuhalten, die Bestimmungen und Verhältnisse des Endlichen auf Gott anzuwenden.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","text":"Nichts pflegt dem Etwas entgegengesetzt zu werden; Etwas aber ist schon ein bestimmtes Seyendes, das sich von anderem Etwas unterscheidet; so ist also auch das dem Etwas entgegengesetzte Nichts, das Nichts von irgend Etwas, ein bestimmtes Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"11.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","text":"Hier aber ist das Nichts in seiner unbestimmten Einfachheit zu nehmen. —Wollte man es für richtiger halten, daß statt des Nichts dem Seyn das Nichtseyn entgegengesetzt würde, so wäre in Rücksicht auf das Resultat nichts dawider zu haben, denn im Nichtseyn ist die Beziehung auf das Seyn enthalten; es ist Beides, Seyn und die Negation desselben, in Einem ausgesprochen, das Nichts, wie es im Werden ist. Aber es ist zunächst nicht um die Form der Entgegensetzung, d. i. zugleich der Beziehung zu thun, sondern um die abstrakte, unmittelbare Negation, das Nichts rein für sich, die beziehungslose Verneinung,—was man, wenn man will, auch durch das bloße: Nicht ausdrücken könnte.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"11.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","text":"Den einfachen Gedanken des reinen Seyns haben die Eleaten zuerst, vorzüglich Parmenides als das Absolute und als einzige Wahrheit, und in den übergebliebenen Fragmenten von ihm, mit der reinen Begeisterung des Denkens, das zum ersten Male sich in seiner absoluten Abstraktion erfaßt, ausgesprochen: nur das Seyn ist, und das Nichts ist gar nicht.—In orientalischen Systemen, wesentlich im Buddaismus ist bekanntlich das Nichts, das Leere, das absolute Princip.—Der tiefsinnige Heraklit hob gegen jene einfache und einseitige Abstraktion den höheren totalen Begriff des Werdens hervor, und sagte: das Seyn ist so wenig, als das Nichts, oder auch Alles fließt, das heißt, Alles ist Werden.—Die populären, besonders orientalischen Sprüche, daß alles, was ist, den Keim seines Vergehens in seiner Geburt selbst habe, der Tod umgekehrt der Eingang in neues Leben sey, drücken im Grunde dieselbe Einigung","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"11.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","text":"des Seyns und Nichts aus. Aber diese Ausdrücke haben ein Substrat, an dem der Übergang geschieht; Seyn und Nichts werden in der Zeit auseinander gehalten, als in ihr abwechselnd vorgestellt, nicht aber in ihrer Abstraktion gedacht, und daher auch nicht so, daß sie an und für sich dasselbe sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"11.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","text":"Ex nihilo nihil fit—ist einer der Sätze, denen in der Metaphysik große Bedeutung zugeschrieben wurde. Es ist darin entweder nur die gehaltlose Tautologie zu sehen: Nichts ist Nichts; oder wenn das Werden wirkliche Bedeutung darin haben sollte, so ist vielmehr, indem nur Nichts aus Nichts wird, in der That kein Werden darin vorhanden, denn Nichts bleibt darin Nichts. Das Werden enthält, daß Nichts nicht Nichts bleibe, sondern in sein Anderes, in das Seyn übergehe.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"11.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","text":"—Wenn die spätere vornehmlich christliche Metaphysik den Satz, aus Nichts werde Nichts, verwarf, so behauptete sie einen Übergang von Nichts in Seyn; so synthetisch oder bloß vorstellend sie auch diesen Satz nahm, so ist doch auch in der unvollkommensten Vereinigung ein Punkt enthalten, worin Seyn und Nichts zusammentreffen, und ihre Unterschiedenheit verschwindet.—Seine eigentliche Wichtigkeit hat der Satz: Aus Nichts wird Nichts, Nichts ist eben Nichts, durch seinen Gegensatz gegen das Werden überhaupt und damit auch gegen die Erschaffung der Welt aus Nichts. Diejenigen, welche den Satz: Nichts ist eben Nichts, sogar sich dafür ereifernd, behaupten, sind bewußtlos darüber, daß sie damit dem abstrakten Pantheismus der Eleaten, der Sache nach auch dem spinozistischen, beipflichten.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"11.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","text":"Die philosophische Ansicht, welcher: Seyn ist nur Seyn, Nichts ist nur Nichts, als Princip gilt, verdient den Namen Identitätssystem; diese abstrakte Identität ist das Wesen des Pantheismus.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"11.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","text":"Wenn das Resultat, daß Seyn und Nichts dasselbe ist, für sich auffällt oder paradox scheint, so ist hierauf nicht weiter zu achten; es wäre sich vielmehr über jene Verwunderung zu verwundern, die sich so neu in der Philosophie zeigt und vergißt, daß in dieser Wissenschaft ganz andere Bestimmungen vorkommen, als im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn und im sogenannten gemeinen Menschenverstande, der nicht gerade der gesunde, sondern auch der zu Abstraktionen und zu dem Glauben oder vielmehr Aberglauben an Abstraktionen heraufgebildete Verstand ist. Es wäre nicht schwer, diese Einheit von Seyn und Nichts, in jedem Beispiele, in jedem Wirklichen oder Gedanken aufzuzeigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"11.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","text":"Es muß dasselbe, was oben von der Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittelung, (welche letztere eine Beziehung aufeinander, damit Negation enthält), vom Seyn und Nichts gesagt werden, daß es nirgend im Himmel und auf Erden Etwas gebe, was nicht beides Seyn und Nichts in sich enthielte. Freilich da hierbei von einem irgend Etwas und Wirklichem die Rede wird, so sind darin jene Bestimmungen nicht mehr in der vollkommenen Unwahrheit, in der sie als Seyn und Nichts sind, vorhanden, sondern in einer weitern Bestimmung, und werden z.B. als Positives und Negatives aufgefaßt, jenes das gesetzte, reflektirte Seyn, dieses das gesetzte, reflektirte Nichts; aber Positives und Negatives enthalten jenes das Seyn, dieses das Nichts als ihre abstrakte Grundlage.—So in Gott selbst enthält die Qualität, Thätigkeit, Schöpfung, Macht u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"11.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","text":"wesentlich die Bestimmung des Negativen,—sie sind ein Hervorbringen eines Anderen. Aber eine empirische Erläuterung von jener Behauptung durch Beispiele wäre hier ganz und gar überflüssig. Da nunmehr diese Einheit von Seyn und Nichts als erste Wahrheit ein für allemal zu Grunde liegt, und das Element von allem Folgenden ausmacht, so sind außer dem Werden selbst, alle ferneren logischen Bestimmungen: Daseyn, Qualität, überhaupt alle Begriffe der Philosophie, Beispiele dieser Einheit.—Aber der sich so nennende gemeine oder gesunde Menschenverstand mag auf den Versuch hingewiesen werden, insofern er die Ungetrenntheit des Seyns und Nichts verwirft, sich ein Beispiel ausfindig zu machen, worin eins vom andern (Etwas von Grenze, Schranke, oder das Unendliche, Gott, wie so eben erwähnt, von Thätigkeit) getrennt zu finden sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"11.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","text":"Nur die leeren Gedankendinge, Seyn und Nichts, selbst, sind diese Getrennte, und sie sind es, die der Wahrheit, der Ungetrenntheit beider, die allenthalben vor uns ist, von jenem Verstande vorgezogen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"11.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","text":"Man kann nicht die Absicht haben wollen, den Verwirrungen, in welche sich das gewöhnliche Bewußtseyn bei einem solchen logischen Satze versetzt, nach allen Seiten hin begegnen zu wollen, denn sie sind unerschöpflich. Es können nur einige erwähnt werden. Ein Grund solcher Verwirrung ist unter andern, daß das Bewußtseyn zu solchem abstrakten logischen Satze Vorstellungen von einem konkreten Etwas mitbringt und vergißt, daß von einem solchen nicht die Rede ist, sondern nur von den reinen Abstraktionen des Seyns und Nichts, und daß diese allein festzuhalten sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"11.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","text":"Seyn und Nichtseyn ist dasselbe; also ist es dasselbe, ob ich bin oder nicht bin, ob dieses Haus ist oder nicht ist, ob diese hundert Thaler in meinem Vermögenszustand sind oder nicht.—Dieser Schluß oder Anwendung jenes Satzes verändert dessen Sinn vollkommen. Der Satz enthält die reinen Abstraktionen des Seyns und Nichts; die Anwendung aber macht ein bestimmtes Seyn und bestimmtes Nichts daraus. Allein vom bestimmten Seyn ist, wie gesagt, hier nicht die Rede. Ein bestimmtes, ein endliches Seyn ist ein solches, das sich auf anderes bezieht; es ist ein Inhalt, der im Verhältnisse der Nothwendigkeit mit anderem Inhalte, mit der ganzen Welt, steht. In Rücksicht des wechselbestimmenden Zusammenhangs des Ganzen konnte die Metaphysik die—im Grunde tautologische—Behauptung machen, daß wenn ein Stäubchen zerstört würde, das ganze Universum zusammenstürzte.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"11.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","text":"In den Instanzen, die gegen den in Rede stehenden Satz gemacht werden, erscheint etwas als nicht gleichgültig, ob es sey oder nicht sey, nicht um des Seyns oder Nichtseyns willen, sondern seines Inhalts willen, der es mit anderem zusammenhängt. Wenn ein bestimmter Inhalt, irgend ein bestimmtes Daseyn vorausgesetzt wird, so ist dieß Daseyn, weil es bestimmtes ist, in mannigfaltiger Beziehung auf anderen Inhalt; es ist für dasselbe nicht gleichgültig, ob ein gewisser anderer Inhalt, mit dem es in Beziehung steht, ist oder nicht ist; denn nur durch solche Beziehung ist es wesentlich das, was es ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"11.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0015","text":"Dasselbe ist der Fall in dem Vorstellen (indem wir das Nichtseyn in dem bestimmteren Sinne des Vorstellens gegen die Wirklichkeit nehmen), in dessen Zusammenhange das Seyn oder die Abwesenheit eines Inhalts, der als bestimmt mit anderem in Beziehung vorgestellt wird, nicht gleichgültig ist.—Diese Betrachtung enthält dasselbe, was ein Hauptmoment in der Kantischen Kritik des ontologischen Beweises vom Daseyn Gottes ausmacht, auf welche jedoch hier nur im Betreff des in ihr vorkommenden Unterschieds von Seyn und Nichts überhaupt und von bestimmtem Seyn oder Nichtseyn Rücksicht genommen wird.—Bekanntlich wurde in jenem sogenannten Beweise der Begriff eines Wesens vorausgesetzt, dem alle Realitäten zukommen, somit auch die Existenz, die gleichfalls als eine der Realitäten angenommen wurde.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"11.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","text":"Die Kantische Kritik hielt sich vornehmlich daran, daß die Existenz oder das Seyn (was hier für gleichbedeutend gilt) keine Eigenschaft oder kein reales Prädikat sey, das heiße, nicht ein Begriff von etwas, was zu dem Begriffe eines Dinges hinzukommen könne. [6] —Kant will damit sagen, daß Seyn keine Inhaltsbestimmung sey.—Also enthalte, fährt er fort, das Mögliche nicht mehr als das Wirkliche; hundert wirkliche Thaler enthalten nicht das Mindeste mehr, als hundert mögliche;—nämlich jene haben keine andere Inhaltsbestimmung als diese. Für diesen als isolirt betrachteten Inhalt ist es in der That gleichgültig, zu seyn oder nicht zu seyn; es liegt in ihm kein Unterschied des Seyns oder Nichtseyns, dieser Unterschied berührt ihn überhaupt gar nicht; die hundert Thaler werden nicht weniger, wenn sie nicht sind, und nicht mehr, wenn sie sind. Ein Unterschied muß erst anderswoher kommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"11.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017","text":"—\"Hingegen, erinnert Kant, in meinem Vermögenszustande ist mehr bei hundert wirklichen Thalern, als bei dem bloßen Begriff derselben, oder bei ihrer Möglichkeit. Denn der Gegenstand ist bei der Wirklichkeit nicht bloß in meinem Begriff analytisch enthalten, sondern kommt zu meinem Begriffe, (der eine Bestimmung meines Zustandes ist,) synthetisch hinzu, ohne daß durch dieses Seyn außer meinem Begriffe, diese gedachten hundert Thaler selbst im mindesten vermehrt würden.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"11.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0018","text":"[6] Kants Kritik der r. Vern. 2te Aufl. S. 628ff.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"11.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019","text":"Es werden hier zweierlei Zustände, um bei den Kantischen Ausdrücken, die nicht ohne verworrene Schwerfälligkeit sind, zu bleiben, vorausgesetzt, der eine, welchen Kant den Begriff nennt, darunter die Vorstellung zu verstehen ist, und ein anderer, der Vermögenszustand. Für den einen wie für den andern, das Vermögen wie das Vorstellen, sind hundert Thaler eine Inhaltsbestimmung, oder \"sie kommen zu einem solchen, wie Kant sich ausdrückt, synthetisch hinzu;\" Ich als Besitzer von hundert Thalern, oder als Nichtbesitzer derselben, oder auch ich als mir hundert Thaler vorstellend, oder sie nicht vorstellend, ist allerdings ein verschiedener Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"11.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","text":"Allgemeiner gefaßt: Die Abstraktionen von Seyn und Nichts hören beide auf, Abstraktionen zu seyn, indem sie einen bestimmten Inhalt erhalten; Seyn ist dann Realität, das bestimmte Seyn von Thalern, das Nichts Negation, das bestimmte Nichtseyn von denselben. Diese Inhaltsbestimmtheit selbst, die hundert Thaler, auch abstrakt für sich gefaßt, ist in dem einen unverändert dasselbe, was in dem andern. Indem aber ferner das Seyn als Vermögens-Zustand genommen wird, treten die hundert Thaler in Beziehung zu einem Zustand, und für diesen ist solche Bestimmtheit, die sie sind, nicht gleichgültig; ihr Seyn oder Nichtseyn ist nur Veränderung; sie sind in die Sphäre des Daseyns versetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"11.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","text":"Wenn daher gegen die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts urgirt wird, es sey doch nicht gleichgültig, ob dieß und jenes (die Thaler) sey oder nicht sey, so ist es eine Täuschung, daß wir den Unterschied bloß aufs Seyn und Nichtseyn hinausschieben, ob ich die hundert Thaler habe oder nicht habe—eine Täuschung, die wie gezeigt, auf der einseitigen Abstraktion beruht, welche das bestimmte Daseyn, das in solchen Beispielen vorhanden ist, wegläßt und bloß das Seyn und Nichtseyn festhält; wie sie umgekehrt das abstrakte Seyn und Nichts, das aufgefaßt werden soll, in ein bestimmtes Seyn und Nichts, in ein Daseyn, verwandelt. Erst das Daseyn enthält den realen Unterschied von Seyn und Nichts, nämlich ein Etwas und ein Anderes. —Dieser reale Unterschied schwebt der Vorstellung vor, statt des abstrakten Seyns und reinen Nichts, und ihrem nur gemeinten Unterschiede.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"11.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","text":"Wie Kant sich ausdrückt, so kommt \"durch die Existenz etwas in den Kontext der gesammten Erfahrung,\" \"wir bekommen dadurch einen Gegenstand der Wahrnehmung mehr, aber unser Begriff von dem Gegenstande wird dadurch nicht vermehrt.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"11.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","text":"Dieß heißt, wie aus dem Erläuterten hervorgeht, so viel, durch die Existenz, wesentlich darum weil Etwas bestimmte Existenz ist, ist es in dem Zusammenhang mit Anderem, und unter anderem auch mit einem Wahrnehmenden.—\"Der Begriff der hundert Thaler, sagt Kant, werde nicht durch das Wahrnehmen vermehrt.\" Der Begriff heißt hier die vorhin bemerkten isolirt vorgestellten hundert Thaler. In dieser isolirten Weise sind sie zwar ein empirischer Inhalt, aber abgeschnitten, ohne Zusammenhang und Bestimmtheit gegen Anderes; die Form der Identität mit sich benimmt ihnen die Beziehung auf anderes und macht sie gleichgültig, ob sie wahrgenommen seyen oder nicht.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"11.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024","text":"Aber dieser sogenannte Begriff der hundert Thaler ist ein falscher Begriff, die Form der einfachen Beziehung auf sich gehört solchem begränzten, endlichen Inhalt nicht selbst; es ist eine ihm vom subjektiven Verstande angethane und geliehene Form; hundert Thaler sind nicht ein sich auf sich Beziehendes, sondern ein Veränderliches und Vergängliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"11.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025","text":"Das Denken oder Vorstellen, dem nur ein bestimmtes Seyn, das Daseyn, vorschwebt, ist zu dem erwähnten Anfange der Wissenschaft zurück zu weisen, welchen Parmenides gemacht hat, der sein Vorstellen und damit auch das Vorstellen der Folgezeit zu dem reinen Gedanken, dem Seyn als solchen, geläutert und erhoben, und damit das Element der Wissenschaft erschaffen hat.—Was das Erste in der Wissenschaft ist, hat sich müssen geschichtlich als das Erste zeigen. Und das Eleatische Eine oder Seyn haben wir für das Erste des Wissens vom Gedanken anzusehen; das Wasser und dergleichen materielle Principien sollen wohl das Allgemeine seyn, aber sind als Materien nicht reine Gedanken; die Zahlen sind weder der erste einfache noch der bei sich bleibende, sondern der sich selbst ganz äußerliche Gedanke.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"11.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0026","text":"Die Zurückweisung vom besonderen endlichen Seyn zum Seyn als solchen in seiner ganz abstrakten Allgemeinheit ist wie als die allererste theoretische so auch sogar praktische Forderung anzusehen. Wenn nämlich ein Aufhebens von den hundert Thalern gemacht wird, daß es in meinem Vermögenszustand einen Unterschied mache, ob ich sie habe oder nicht, noch mehr ob Ich sey oder nicht, ob Anderes sey oder nicht, so kann—ohne zu erwähnen, daß es Vermögenszustände geben wird, für die solcher Besitz von hundert Thalern gleichgültig seyn wird,—daran erinnert werden, daß der Mensch sich zu dieser abstrakten Allgemeinheit in seiner Gesinnung erheben soll, in welcher es ihm in der That gleichgültig sey, ob die hundert Thaler, sie mögen ein quantitatives Verhältniß zu seinem Vermögenszustand haben, welches sie wollen, seyen oder ob sie nicht seyen, ebenso sehr als es ihm gleichgültig sey, ob er sey oder","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"11.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0027","text":"nicht, d. i. im endlichen Leben sey oder nicht (denn ein Zustand, bestimmtes Seyn ist gemeint) u.s.f. —selbst si fractus illabatur orbis, impavidum ferient ruinae, hat ein Römer gesagt, und der Christ soll sich noch mehr in dieser Gleichgültigkeit befinden.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"11.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0028","text":"Es ist noch die unmittelbare Verbindung anzumerken, in welcher die Erhebung über die hundert Thaler und die endlichen Dinge überhaupt mit dem ontologischen Beweise und der angeführten kantischen Kritik desselben steht. Diese Kritik hat sich durch ihr populäres Beispiel allgemein plausibel gemacht; wer weiß nicht, daß hundert wirkliche Thaler verschieden sind von hundert bloß möglichen Thalern? daß sie einen Unterschied in meinem Vermögenszustand ausmachen? Weil sich so an den hundert Thalern diese Verschiedenheit hervorthut, so ist der Begriff d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"11.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","text":"die Inhaltsbestimmtheit als leere Möglichkeit, und das Seyn verschieden von einander; also ist auch Gottes Begriff von seinem Seyn verschieden, und so wenig ich aus der Möglichkeit der hundert Thaler ihre Wirklichkeit herausbringen kann, eben so wenig kann ich aus dem Begriffe Gottes seine Existenz \"herausklauben\"; aus diesem Herausklauben aber der Existenz Gottes aus seinem Begriffe soll der ontologische Beweis bestehen. Wenn es nun allerdings seine Richtigkeit hat, daß Begriff vom Seyn verschieden ist, so ist noch mehr Gott verschieden von den hundert Thalern und den anderen endlichen Dingen. Es ist die Definition der endlichen Dinge, daß in ihnen Begriff und Seyn verschieden, Begriff und Realität, Seele und Leib, trennbar, sie damit vergänglich und sterblich sind; die abstrakte Definition Gottes ist dagegen eben dieß, daß sein Begriff und sein Seyn ungetrennt und untrennbar sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"11.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","text":"Die wahrhafte Kritik der Kategorien und der Vernunft ist gerade diese, das Erkennen über diesen Unterschied zu verständigen und dasselbe abzuhalten, die Bestimmungen und Verhältnisse des Endlichen auf Gott anzuwenden.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"11.30"}],"sha256":"e25c219b074e7a800f9d2e71c06f6c06e79545cd6816383b474d4073021431a1","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101802444213Z_ceecaee4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"e25c219b074e7a800f9d2e71c06f6c06e79545cd6816383b474d4073021431a1","sha256":"09d156ced5f5e5c018b524d17c5097b57250de3380a8b862ad0cd0dbfa28b2c5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:18:02.444240+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","text":"Nothing is customarily opposed to Something; but Something is already a determinate Being, which distinguishes itself from another Something; thus the Nothing opposed to Something, the Nothing of some Something, is likewise a determinate Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"11.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","text":"Here, however, Nothing is to be taken in its indeterminate simplicity. —If one wished to consider it more correct that, instead of Nothing, non-being should be opposed to Being, there would be nothing to object to in this respect as regards the result, for non-being contains the relation to Being; both, Being and its negation, are expressed in one, Nothing as it is in Becoming. But the point initially is not the form of opposition, i.e. at the same time of relation, but rather abstract, immediate negation, Nothing purely for itself, the unrelated negation,—which, if one wishes, could also be expressed by the mere: Not.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"11.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","text":"The Eleatics were the first to pronounce the simple thought of pure Being, pre-eminently Parmenides, as the Absolute and as the sole truth; and in the fragments that remain of him, with the pure enthusiasm of thinking which for the first time grasps itself in its absolute abstraction: only Being is, and Nothing is not at all.—In Oriental systems, essentially in Buddhism, Nothing, the Void, the absolute principle, is well known.—The profound Heraclitus, against that simple and one-sided abstraction, brought forward the higher total concept of Becoming, and said: Being is no more than Nothing, or also, Everything flows, that is, everything is Becoming.—The popular, especially Oriental sayings, that everything which is has the germ of its passing-away in its birth itself, that death, conversely, is the entrance into new life, fundamentally express the same unification","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"11.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","text":"of Being and Nothing. But these expressions have a substrate in which the transition takes place; Being and Nothing are kept apart in time, as alternatingly represented in it, but not thought in their abstraction, and hence not in such a way that they are in and for themselves the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"11.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","text":"Ex nihilo nihil fit—is one of the propositions to which great significance was attributed in metaphysics. In it one is either to see only the contentless tautology: Nothing is Nothing; or, if Becoming was supposed to have real significance in it, then rather, since only Nothing becomes from Nothing, there is in fact no Becoming in it, for Nothing remains Nothing in it. Becoming contains that Nothing does not remain Nothing, but passes over into its Other, into Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"11.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","text":"—When later, predominantly Christian metaphysics rejected the proposition that nothing comes from nothing, it maintained a transition from Nothing into Being; however synthetically or merely representationally it took this proposition, even in the most imperfect unification there is nevertheless contained a point at which Being and Nothing meet, and their difference vanishes.—The proposition: Nothing comes from Nothing, Nothing is simply Nothing, has its proper importance through its opposition to Becoming in general and thereby also to the creation of the world out of Nothing. Those who assert the proposition: Nothing is simply Nothing, even becoming heated in its defense, are unconscious that by so doing they assent to the abstract pantheism of the Eleatics, and in substance also to the Spinozistic.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"11.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","text":"The philosophical view for which: Being is only Being, Nothing is only Nothing, counts as principle, deserves the name system of identity; this abstract identity is the essence of pantheism.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"11.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","text":"If the result that Being and Nothing are the same strikes one as strange or seems paradoxical, no further heed is to be paid to this; one ought rather to be astonished at that astonishment which shows itself as so new in philosophy and forgets that in this science quite other determinations occur than in ordinary consciousness and in so-called common sense, which is not precisely sound sense, but rather understanding educated up to abstractions and to belief, or rather superstition, in abstractions. It would not be difficult to demonstrate this unity of Being and Nothing in every example, in every actuality or thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"11.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","text":"The same thing that was said above of immediacy and mediation, (the latter of which contains a relation to one another, and thereby negation), must be said of Being and Nothing: that nowhere in heaven or on earth is there anything that did not contain both Being and Nothing within itself. To be sure, since there is talk here of some Something and of actuality, those determinations are no longer present therein in the complete untruth in which they are as Being and Nothing, but in a further determination, and are grasped, e.g., as Positive and Negative, the former as posited, reflected Being, the latter as posited, reflected Nothing; but Positive and Negative contain the former, Being, and the latter, Nothing, as their abstract foundation.—Thus in God himself, quality, activity, creation, power, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"11.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","text":"essentially contain the determination of the Negative,—they are a bringing-forth of an Other. But an empirical elucidation of that assertion by examples would here be wholly superfluous. Since this unity of Being and Nothing now lies at the basis once and for all as the first truth, and constitutes the element of everything that follows, all further logical determinations, apart from Becoming itself—determinate being, quality, in general all concepts of philosophy—are examples of this unity.—But so-called common or sound sense may be referred to the attempt, insofar as it rejects the inseparability of Being and Nothing, to discover an example in which one is to be found separated from the other (Something from limit, restriction, or the Infinite, God, as just mentioned, from activity).","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"11.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","text":"Only the empty thought-things, Being and Nothing themselves, are these separated ones, and it is they that are preferred by that understanding to the truth, the inseparability of both, which is everywhere before us.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"11.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","text":"One cannot intend to meet, in every direction, the confusions into which ordinary consciousness places itself in the case of such a logical proposition, for they are inexhaustible. Only a few can be mentioned. One ground of such confusions is, among others, that consciousness brings to such an abstract logical proposition representations of a concrete Something and forgets that there is no talk of such a thing, but only of the pure abstractions of Being and Nothing, and that these alone are to be held fast.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"11.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","text":"Being and non-being are the same; therefore it is the same whether I am or am not, whether this house is or is not, whether these hundred thalers are or are not in my pecuniary condition.—This inference or application of that proposition alters its meaning completely. The proposition contains the pure abstractions of Being and Nothing; but the application makes them into a determinate Being and determinate Nothing. Yet determinate Being, as stated, is not under discussion here. A determinate, a finite Being is one that relates itself to another; it is a content which stands in a relation of necessity with other content, with the whole world. With regard to the reciprocally determining connection of the whole, metaphysics could make the—in essence tautological—assertion that if a speck of dust were destroyed, the whole universe would collapse.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"11.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","text":"In the instances brought against the proposition in question, something appears not to be indifferent whether it is or is not, not for the sake of Being or non-being, but for the sake of its content, which connects it with something else. If a determinate content, any determinate determinate being, is presupposed, then this determinate being, because it is determinate, stands in manifold relation to other content; it is not indifferent to it whether a certain other content with which it stands in relation is or is not; for only through such relation is it essentially what it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"11.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0015","text":"The same is the case in representation (when we take non-being in the more determinate sense of representation as against actuality), in whose connection the Being or absence of a content that is represented as determinate in relation to another is not indifferent.—This consideration contains the same thing as constitutes a main moment in the Kantian critique of the ontological proof of God's existence, to which, however, attention is here paid only with respect to the distinction occurring in it between Being and Nothing in general and determinate Being or non-being.—As is known, in that so-called proof the concept of a being to which all realities belong was presupposed, thus also existence, which was likewise assumed as one of the realities.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"11.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","text":"The Kantian critique held chiefly to the point that existence or Being (which here counts as synonymous) is no property or real predicate, that is to say, not a concept of something that could be added to the concept of a thing. [6] —Kant thereby means that Being is no determination of content.—Thus, he continues, the possible contains no more than the actual; a hundred actual thalers contain not the least more than a hundred possible ones;—namely, the former have no other determination of content than the latter. For this content, considered as isolated, it is in fact indifferent to be or not to be; there lies in it no difference of Being or non-being, this difference does not affect it at all; the hundred thalers do not become fewer if they are not, nor more if they are. A difference must first come from elsewhere.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"11.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017","text":"—“By contrast,” Kant observes, “there is more in my pecuniary condition with a hundred actual thalers than with the mere concept of them, or with their possibility. For in actuality the object is not merely analytically contained in my concept, but is added synthetically to my concept (which is a determination of my condition), without these thought hundred thalers themselves being in the least increased by this Being outside my concept.”","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"11.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0018","text":"[6] Kant’s Critique of Pure Reason, 2nd ed., pp. 628ff.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"11.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019","text":"Here two kinds of condition are presupposed, to remain with the Kantian expressions, which are not without confused cumbersomeness: one, which Kant calls the concept, by which representation is to be understood, and another, the pecuniary condition. For the one as for the other, pecuniary means as well as representing, a hundred thalers are a determination of content, or “they are synthetically added to such a thing,” as Kant expresses himself; I as possessor of a hundred thalers, or as non-possessor of them, or also I as representing a hundred thalers to myself, or not representing them, am indeed a different content.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"11.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","text":"Put more generally: the abstractions of Being and Nothing both cease to be abstractions when they receive a determinate content; Being is then reality, the determinate Being of thalers, Nothing negation, the determinate non-being of the same. This determinacy of content itself, the hundred thalers, even grasped abstractly for itself, is unchangedly the same in the one as in the other. But when, further, Being is taken as pecuniary condition, the hundred thalers enter into relation with a condition, and for this such determinacy as they are is not indifferent; their Being or non-being is only alteration; they are transferred into the sphere of determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"11.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","text":"Thus, when it is urged against the unity of Being and Nothing that it is surely not indifferent whether this or that (the thalers) is or is not, it is a deception that we ascribe the difference merely to Being and non-being, whether I have the hundred thalers or do not have them—a deception which, as shown, rests on the one-sided abstraction that leaves out the determinate being present in such examples and holds fast merely to Being and non-being; just as, conversely, it transforms the abstract Being and Nothing that is to be grasped into a determinate Being and Nothing, into a determinate being. Only determinate being contains the real difference of Being and Nothing, namely a Something and an Other. —This real difference hovers before representation, in place of abstract Being and pure Nothing, and their merely intended difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"11.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","text":"As Kant expresses himself, “through existence something enters into the context of total experience,” “we thereby obtain one more object of perception, but our concept of the object is not thereby increased.”","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"11.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","text":"This means, as follows from what has been explained, as much as this: through existence, essentially because Something is determinate existence, it is in connection with an Other, and among other things also with a perceiver.—“The concept of the hundred thalers,” says Kant, “is not increased by perception.” Here concept means the previously noted hundred thalers represented in isolation. In this isolated manner they are indeed an empirical content, but cut off, without connection and determinacy over against an Other; the form of identity with themselves removes from them relation to another and renders it indifferent whether they are perceived or not.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"11.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024","text":"But this so-called concept of the hundred thalers is a false concept; the form of simple relation to itself does not belong to such limited, finite content itself; it is a form imposed upon and lent to it by subjective understanding; a hundred thalers are not something relating itself to itself, but something alterable and perishable.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"11.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025","text":"Thinking or representing, before which there hovers only a determinate Being, determinate existence, is to be referred back to the aforementioned beginning of science, which Parmenides made, who purified and elevated his representing, and thereby also the representing of subsequent times, to the pure thought, to Being as such, and thereby created the element of science.—What is first in science had necessarily to show itself historically as the first. And the Eleatic One or Being is to be regarded by us as the first of the knowledge of thought; water and similar material principles are indeed supposed to be the universal, but, as matters, they are not pure thoughts; numbers are neither the first simple thought nor the thought that remains with itself, but the thought wholly external to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"11.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0026","text":"The reference back from particular finite Being to Being as such in its wholly abstract universality is to be regarded not only as the very first theoretical but even as a practical demand. For if much fuss is made over the hundred thalers, that it makes a difference in my pecuniary condition whether I have them or not, still more whether I am or am not, whether others are or are not, then—without mentioning that there will be pecuniary conditions for which such possession of a hundred thalers will be indifferent,—it may be recalled that the human being ought to raise himself in his disposition to this abstract universality, in which it is in fact indifferent to him whether the hundred thalers, whatever quantitative relation they may have to his pecuniary condition, are or are not, just as much as it is indifferent to him whether he is or","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"11.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0027","text":"is not, i.e. is or is not in finite life (for a condition, determinate Being, is meant), and so forth.—even if the shattered world should fall upon him, its ruins will strike him unafraid, a Roman has said, and the Christian ought to be still more in this indifference.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"11.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0028","text":"The immediate connection in which the elevation above the hundred thalers and finite things in general stands with the ontological proof and the Kantian critique of it cited above is still to be noted. This critique has made itself generally plausible through its popular example; who does not know that a hundred actual thalers are different from a hundred merely possible thalers? that they make a difference in my pecuniary condition? Because this difference shows itself in the case of the hundred thalers, the concept, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"11.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","text":"the determinacy of content, as empty possibility, and Being are distinct from one another; therefore God’s concept too is distinct from his Being, and just as little as I can extract the actuality of the hundred thalers from their possibility can I “pick out” God’s existence from the concept of God; yet the ontological proof is supposed to consist in this picking out of God’s existence from his concept. Now, although it is indeed correct that the concept is distinct from Being, God is still more distinct from the hundred thalers and the other finite things. It is the definition of finite things that in them concept and Being are distinct, concept and reality, soul and body, separable, and that they are thereby transitory and mortal; the abstract definition of God, on the contrary, is precisely this, that his concept and his Being are undivided and inseparable.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"11.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","text":"The true critique of the categories and of reason is precisely this: to make cognition aware of this difference and to restrain it from applying the determinations and relations of the finite to God.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"11.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030"]}],"source_digest":"7add105ee72da0a1fede3edb154028aad8451d02e0d11a6e96d589b546b82193","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2","title":"Remark 2.","order":12,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ANM2","text":"Es ist weiter ein anderer Grund anzuführen, welcher zu dem Widerwillen gegen den Satz über Seyn und Nichts behülflich ist; dieser Grund ist, daß der Ausdruck des Resultats, das sich aus der Betrachtung des Seyns und des Nichts ergiebt, durch den Satz: Seyn und Nichts ist eins und dasselbe, unvollkommen ist. Der Accent wird vorzugsweise auf das Eins- und dasselbe-seyn gelegt, wie im Urtheile überhaupt, als in welchem das Prädikat erst es aussagt, was das Subjekt ist. Der Sinn scheint daher zu seyn, daß der Unterschied geläugnet werde, der doch zugleich im Satze unmittelbar vorkommt; denn er spricht die beiden Bestimmungen, Seyn und Nichts, aus, und enthält sie als unterschiedene.—Es kann zugleich nicht gemeint seyn, daß von ihnen abstrahirt und nur die Einheit festgehalten werden soll. Dieser Sinn gäbe sich selbst für einseitig, da das, wovon abstrahirt werden soll, gleichwohl im Satze vorhanden ist und genannt wird.—Insofern nun der Satz: Seyn und Nichts ist dasselbe, die Identität dieser Bestimmungen ausspricht, aber in der That ebenso sie beide als unterschieden enthält, widerspricht er sich in sich selbst und löst sich auf. Halten wir dieß näher fest, so ist also hier ein Satz gesetzt, der näher betrachtet, die Bewegung hat, durch sich selbst zu verschwinden. Damit aber, geschieht an ihm selbst das, was seinen eigentlichen Inhalt ausmachen soll, nämlich das Werden.\n\nDer Satz enthält somit das Resultat, er ist dieses an sich selbst. Der Umstand aber, auf den hier aufmerksam zu machen ist, ist der Mangel, daß das Resultat nicht selbst im Satze ausgedrückt ist; es ist eine äußere Reflexion, welche es in ihm erkennt.—Es muß hierüber sogleich im Anfange diese allgemeine Bemerkung gemacht werden, daß der Satz, in Form eines Urtheils, nicht geschickt ist, spekulative Wahrheiten auszudrücken; die Bekanntschaft mit diesem Umstande wäre geeignet, viele Mißverständnisse spekulativer Wahrheiten zu beseitigen. Das Urtheil ist eine identische Beziehung zwischen Subjekt und Prädikat; es wird dabei davon abstrahirt, daß das Subjekt noch mehrere Bestimmtheiten hat als die des Prädikats, so wie davon, daß das Prädikat weiter ist als das Subjekt. Ist nun aber der Inhalt spekulativ, so ist auch das Nichtidentische des Subjekts und Prädikats wesentliches Moment, aber dieß ist im Urtheile nicht ausgedrückt. Das paradoxe und bizarre Licht, in dem Vieles der neueren Philosophie den mit dem spekulativen Denken nicht Vertrauten erscheint, fällt vielfältig in die Form des einfachen Urtheils, wenn sie für den Ausdruck spekulativer Resultate gebraucht wird.\n\nDer Mangel wird, zum Behuf, die spekulative Wahrheit auszudrücken, zunächst so ergänzt, daß der entgegengesetzte Satz hinzugefügt wird, der Satz: Seyn und Nichts ist nicht dasselbe, der oben gleichfalls ausgesprochen ist. Allein so entsteht der weitere Mangel, daß diese Sätze unverbunden sind, somit den Inhalt nur in der Antinomie darstellen, während doch ihr Inhalt sich auf Ein und Dasselbe bezieht, und die Bestimmungen, die in den zwei Sätzen ausgedrückt sind, schlechthin vereinigt seyn sollen,—eine Vereinigung, welche dann nur als eine Unruhe zugleich unverträglicher, als eine Bewegung ausgesprochen werden kann. Das gewöhnlichste Unrecht, welches spekulativem Gehalte angethan wird, ist, ihn einseitig zu machen, d. i. den einen der Sätze nur, in die er aufgelöst werden kann, heraus zu heben. Es kann dann nicht geläugnet werden, daß dieser Satz behauptet wird; so richtig die Angabe ist, so falsch ist sie, denn wenn einmal Ein Satz aus dem Spekulativen genommen ist, so müßte wenigstens ebenso sehr der andere gleichfalls beachtet und angegeben werden.—Es ist hierbei noch das so zu sagen unglückliche Wort: Einheit besonders zu erwähnen; die Einheit bezeichnet noch mehr als die Identität eine subjektive Reflexion; sie wird vornehmlich als die Beziehung genommen, welche aus der Vergleichung, der äußerlichen Reflexion, entspringt. Insofern diese in zwei verschiedenen Gegenständen dasselbe findet, ist eine Einheit so vorhanden, daß dabei die vollkommene Gleichgültigkeit der Gegenstände selbst, die verglichen werden, gegen diese Einheit vorausgesetzt wird, so daß dieß Vergleichen und die Einheit die Gegenstände selbst nichts angeht, und ein ihnen äußerliches Thun und Bestimmen ist. Die Einheit drückt daher die ganz abstrakte Dieselbigkeit aus, und lautet um so härter und auffallender, je mehr die, von denen sie ausgesprochen wird, sich schlechthin unterschieden zeigen. Für Einheit würde daher insofern besser nur Ungetrenntheit und Untrennbarkeit gesagt; aber damit ist das Affirmative der Beziehung des Ganzen nicht ausgedrückt.\n\nSo ist das ganze, wahre Resultat, das sich hier ergeben hat, das Werden, welches nicht bloß die einseitige oder abstrakte Einheit des Seyns und Nichts ist. Sondern es besteht in dieser Bewegung, daß das reine Seyn unmittelbar und einfach ist, daß es darum eben so sehr das reine Nichts ist, daß der Unterschied derselben ist, aber eben so sehr sich aufhebt und nicht ist. Das Resultat behauptet also den Unterschied des Seyns und des Nichts eben so sehr, aber als einen nur gemeinten.\n\nMan meint, das Seyn sey vielmehr das schlechthin Andere, als das Nichts ist, und es ist nichts klarer, als ihr absoluter Unterschied, und es scheint nichts leichter, als ihn angeben zu können. Es ist aber eben so leicht, sich zu überzeugen, daß dieß unmöglich, daß er unsagbar ist. Die, welche auf dem Unterschiede von Seyn und Nichts beharren wollen, mögen sich auffordern, anzugeben, worin er besteht. Hätte Seyn und Nichts irgend eine Bestimmtheit, wodurch sie sich unterschieden, so wären sie, wie erinnert worden, bestimmtes Seyn und bestimmtes Nichts, nicht das reine Seyn und das reine Nichts, wie sie es hier noch sind. Ihr Unterschied ist daher völlig leer, jedes der beiden ist auf gleiche Weise das Unbestimmte; er besteht daher nicht an ihnen selbst, sondern nur in einem Dritten, im Meinen. Aber das Meinen ist eine Form des Subjektiven, das nicht in diese Reihe der Darstellung gehört. Das Dritte aber, worin Seyn und Nichts ihr Bestehen haben, muß auch hier vorkommen; und es ist vorgekommen, es ist das Werden. In ihm sind sie als unterschiedene; Werden ist nur, insofern sie unterschieden sind. Dieß Dritte ist ein Anderes als sie; —sie bestehen nur in einem Anderen, dieß heißt gleichfalls, sie bestehen nicht für sich. Das Werden ist das Bestehen des Seyns so sehr als des Nichtseyns; oder ihr Bestehen ist nur ihr Seyn in Einem; gerade dieß ihr Bestehen ist es, was ihren Unterschied eben so sehr aufhebt.\n\nDie Aufforderung, den Unterschied von Seyn und Nichts anzugeben, schließt auch die in sich, zu sagen, was denn Seyn und was Nichts ist. Die sich dagegen sträuben, das eine wie das andere nur als ein Übergehen in einander zu erkennen, und vom Seyn und vom Nichts dieß oder das behaupten, mögen angeben, von was sie sprechen, d. i. eine Definition vom Seyn und Nichts aufstellen, und aufzeigen, daß sie richtig ist. Ohne dieser ersten Forderung der alten Wissenschaft genügt zu haben, deren logische Regeln sie sonst gelten lassen und anwenden, sind alle jene Behauptungen über das Seyn und Nichts nur Versicherungen, wissenschaftliche Ungültigkeiten. Wenn man sonst gesagt hat, die Existenz, insofern man diese zunächst für gleichbedeutend mit Seyn hält, sey die Ergänzung zur Möglichkeit, so ist damit eine andere Bestimmung, die Möglichkeit, vorausgesetzt, das Seyn nicht in seiner Unmittelbarkeit, sogar als nicht selbstständig, als bedingt ausgesprochen. Für das Seyn, welches vermittelt ist, werden wir den Ausdruck: Existenz, aufbehalten. Aber man stellt sich wohl das Seyn vor—etwa unter dem Bilde des reinen Lichts, als die Klarheit ungetrübten Sehens, das Nichts aber als die reine Nacht, und knüpft ihren Unterschied an diese wohlbekannte sinnliche Verschiedenheit. In der That aber, wenn man auch dieß Sehen sich genauer vorstellt, so kann man leicht gewahr werden, daß man in der absoluten Klarheit so viel und so wenig sieht, als in der absoluten Finsterniß, daß das eine Sehen so gut als das andere, reines Sehen, Sehen von Nichts ist. Reines Licht und reine Finsterniß sind zwei Leeren, welche dasselbe sind. Erst in dem bestimmten Lichte—und das Licht wird durch die Finsterniß bestimmt,—also im getrübten Lichte, ebenso erst in der bestimmten Finsterniß,—und die Finsterniß wird durch das Licht bestimmt,—in der erhellten Finsterniß kann etwas unterschieden werden, weil erst das getrübte Licht und die erhellte Finsterniß den Unterschied an ihnen selbst haben, und damit bestimmtes Seyn, Daseyn, sind.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","text":"Es ist weiter ein anderer Grund anzuführen, welcher zu dem Widerwillen gegen den Satz über Seyn und Nichts behülflich ist; dieser Grund ist, daß der Ausdruck des Resultats, das sich aus der Betrachtung des Seyns und des Nichts ergiebt, durch den Satz: Seyn und Nichts ist eins und dasselbe, unvollkommen ist. Der Accent wird vorzugsweise auf das Eins- und dasselbe-seyn gelegt, wie im Urtheile überhaupt, als in welchem das Prädikat erst es aussagt, was das Subjekt ist. Der Sinn scheint daher zu seyn, daß der Unterschied geläugnet werde, der doch zugleich im Satze unmittelbar vorkommt; denn er spricht die beiden Bestimmungen, Seyn und Nichts, aus, und enthält sie als unterschiedene.—Es kann zugleich nicht gemeint seyn, daß von ihnen abstrahirt und nur die Einheit festgehalten werden soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"12.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","text":"Dieser Sinn gäbe sich selbst für einseitig, da das, wovon abstrahirt werden soll, gleichwohl im Satze vorhanden ist und genannt wird.—Insofern nun der Satz: Seyn und Nichts ist dasselbe, die Identität dieser Bestimmungen ausspricht, aber in der That ebenso sie beide als unterschieden enthält, widerspricht er sich in sich selbst und löst sich auf. Halten wir dieß näher fest, so ist also hier ein Satz gesetzt, der näher betrachtet, die Bewegung hat, durch sich selbst zu verschwinden. Damit aber, geschieht an ihm selbst das, was seinen eigentlichen Inhalt ausmachen soll, nämlich das Werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"12.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","text":"Der Satz enthält somit das Resultat, er ist dieses an sich selbst. Der Umstand aber, auf den hier aufmerksam zu machen ist, ist der Mangel, daß das Resultat nicht selbst im Satze ausgedrückt ist; es ist eine äußere Reflexion, welche es in ihm erkennt.—Es muß hierüber sogleich im Anfange diese allgemeine Bemerkung gemacht werden, daß der Satz, in Form eines Urtheils, nicht geschickt ist, spekulative Wahrheiten auszudrücken; die Bekanntschaft mit diesem Umstande wäre geeignet, viele Mißverständnisse spekulativer Wahrheiten zu beseitigen. Das Urtheil ist eine identische Beziehung zwischen Subjekt und Prädikat; es wird dabei davon abstrahirt, daß das Subjekt noch mehrere Bestimmtheiten hat als die des Prädikats, so wie davon, daß das Prädikat weiter ist als das Subjekt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"12.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","text":"Ist nun aber der Inhalt spekulativ, so ist auch das Nichtidentische des Subjekts und Prädikats wesentliches Moment, aber dieß ist im Urtheile nicht ausgedrückt. Das paradoxe und bizarre Licht, in dem Vieles der neueren Philosophie den mit dem spekulativen Denken nicht Vertrauten erscheint, fällt vielfältig in die Form des einfachen Urtheils, wenn sie für den Ausdruck spekulativer Resultate gebraucht wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"12.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","text":"Der Mangel wird, zum Behuf, die spekulative Wahrheit auszudrücken, zunächst so ergänzt, daß der entgegengesetzte Satz hinzugefügt wird, der Satz: Seyn und Nichts ist nicht dasselbe, der oben gleichfalls ausgesprochen ist. Allein so entsteht der weitere Mangel, daß diese Sätze unverbunden sind, somit den Inhalt nur in der Antinomie darstellen, während doch ihr Inhalt sich auf Ein und Dasselbe bezieht, und die Bestimmungen, die in den zwei Sätzen ausgedrückt sind, schlechthin vereinigt seyn sollen,—eine Vereinigung, welche dann nur als eine Unruhe zugleich unverträglicher, als eine Bewegung ausgesprochen werden kann. Das gewöhnlichste Unrecht, welches spekulativem Gehalte angethan wird, ist, ihn einseitig zu machen, d. i. den einen der Sätze nur, in die er aufgelöst werden kann, heraus zu heben.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"12.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","text":"Es kann dann nicht geläugnet werden, daß dieser Satz behauptet wird; so richtig die Angabe ist, so falsch ist sie, denn wenn einmal Ein Satz aus dem Spekulativen genommen ist, so müßte wenigstens ebenso sehr der andere gleichfalls beachtet und angegeben werden.—Es ist hierbei noch das so zu sagen unglückliche Wort: Einheit besonders zu erwähnen; die Einheit bezeichnet noch mehr als die Identität eine subjektive Reflexion; sie wird vornehmlich als die Beziehung genommen, welche aus der Vergleichung, der äußerlichen Reflexion, entspringt. Insofern diese in zwei verschiedenen Gegenständen dasselbe findet, ist eine Einheit so vorhanden, daß dabei die vollkommene Gleichgültigkeit der Gegenstände selbst, die verglichen werden, gegen diese Einheit vorausgesetzt wird, so daß dieß Vergleichen und die Einheit die Gegenstände selbst nichts angeht, und ein ihnen äußerliches Thun und Bestimmen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"12.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0007","text":"Die Einheit drückt daher die ganz abstrakte Dieselbigkeit aus, und lautet um so härter und auffallender, je mehr die, von denen sie ausgesprochen wird, sich schlechthin unterschieden zeigen. Für Einheit würde daher insofern besser nur Ungetrenntheit und Untrennbarkeit gesagt; aber damit ist das Affirmative der Beziehung des Ganzen nicht ausgedrückt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"12.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","text":"So ist das ganze, wahre Resultat, das sich hier ergeben hat, das Werden, welches nicht bloß die einseitige oder abstrakte Einheit des Seyns und Nichts ist. Sondern es besteht in dieser Bewegung, daß das reine Seyn unmittelbar und einfach ist, daß es darum eben so sehr das reine Nichts ist, daß der Unterschied derselben ist, aber eben so sehr sich aufhebt und nicht ist. Das Resultat behauptet also den Unterschied des Seyns und des Nichts eben so sehr, aber als einen nur gemeinten.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"12.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","text":"Man meint, das Seyn sey vielmehr das schlechthin Andere, als das Nichts ist, und es ist nichts klarer, als ihr absoluter Unterschied, und es scheint nichts leichter, als ihn angeben zu können. Es ist aber eben so leicht, sich zu überzeugen, daß dieß unmöglich, daß er unsagbar ist. Die, welche auf dem Unterschiede von Seyn und Nichts beharren wollen, mögen sich auffordern, anzugeben, worin er besteht. Hätte Seyn und Nichts irgend eine Bestimmtheit, wodurch sie sich unterschieden, so wären sie, wie erinnert worden, bestimmtes Seyn und bestimmtes Nichts, nicht das reine Seyn und das reine Nichts, wie sie es hier noch sind. Ihr Unterschied ist daher völlig leer, jedes der beiden ist auf gleiche Weise das Unbestimmte; er besteht daher nicht an ihnen selbst, sondern nur in einem Dritten, im Meinen. Aber das Meinen ist eine Form des Subjektiven, das nicht in diese Reihe der Darstellung gehört.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"12.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","text":"Das Dritte aber, worin Seyn und Nichts ihr Bestehen haben, muß auch hier vorkommen; und es ist vorgekommen, es ist das Werden. In ihm sind sie als unterschiedene; Werden ist nur, insofern sie unterschieden sind. Dieß Dritte ist ein Anderes als sie; —sie bestehen nur in einem Anderen, dieß heißt gleichfalls, sie bestehen nicht für sich. Das Werden ist das Bestehen des Seyns so sehr als des Nichtseyns; oder ihr Bestehen ist nur ihr Seyn in Einem; gerade dieß ihr Bestehen ist es, was ihren Unterschied eben so sehr aufhebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"12.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011","text":"Die Aufforderung, den Unterschied von Seyn und Nichts anzugeben, schließt auch die in sich, zu sagen, was denn Seyn und was Nichts ist. Die sich dagegen sträuben, das eine wie das andere nur als ein Übergehen in einander zu erkennen, und vom Seyn und vom Nichts dieß oder das behaupten, mögen angeben, von was sie sprechen, d. i. eine Definition vom Seyn und Nichts aufstellen, und aufzeigen, daß sie richtig ist. Ohne dieser ersten Forderung der alten Wissenschaft genügt zu haben, deren logische Regeln sie sonst gelten lassen und anwenden, sind alle jene Behauptungen über das Seyn und Nichts nur Versicherungen, wissenschaftliche Ungültigkeiten.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"12.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","text":"Wenn man sonst gesagt hat, die Existenz, insofern man diese zunächst für gleichbedeutend mit Seyn hält, sey die Ergänzung zur Möglichkeit, so ist damit eine andere Bestimmung, die Möglichkeit, vorausgesetzt, das Seyn nicht in seiner Unmittelbarkeit, sogar als nicht selbstständig, als bedingt ausgesprochen. Für das Seyn, welches vermittelt ist, werden wir den Ausdruck: Existenz, aufbehalten. Aber man stellt sich wohl das Seyn vor—etwa unter dem Bilde des reinen Lichts, als die Klarheit ungetrübten Sehens, das Nichts aber als die reine Nacht, und knüpft ihren Unterschied an diese wohlbekannte sinnliche Verschiedenheit. In der That aber, wenn man auch dieß Sehen sich genauer vorstellt, so kann man leicht gewahr werden, daß man in der absoluten Klarheit so viel und so wenig sieht, als in der absoluten Finsterniß, daß das eine Sehen so gut als das andere, reines Sehen, Sehen von Nichts ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"12.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","text":"Reines Licht und reine Finsterniß sind zwei Leeren, welche dasselbe sind. Erst in dem bestimmten Lichte—und das Licht wird durch die Finsterniß bestimmt,—also im getrübten Lichte, ebenso erst in der bestimmten Finsterniß,—und die Finsterniß wird durch das Licht bestimmt,—in der erhellten Finsterniß kann etwas unterschieden werden, weil erst das getrübte Licht und die erhellte Finsterniß den Unterschied an ihnen selbst haben, und damit bestimmtes Seyn, Daseyn, sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"12.13"}],"sha256":"55590250478b36e902233b9ba9391c3604c58e75a6791702565f9943c697cf82","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101819053148Z_131d34cf","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"55590250478b36e902233b9ba9391c3604c58e75a6791702565f9943c697cf82","sha256":"00154e2837172cf06efc2328af0e3d45e2f2b6937ff278354e317e861fedfbfc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:18:19.053174+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","text":"A further reason must be adduced which assists in the aversion to the proposition concerning Being and Nothing; this reason is that the expression of the result which emerges from the consideration of Being and Nothing, by means of the proposition: Being and Nothing are one and the same, is imperfect. The accent is placed pre-eminently on being-one-and-the-same, as in judgment in general, in which it is the predicate that first states what the subject is. The meaning therefore seems to be that the difference is denied, which nevertheless at the same time occurs immediately in the proposition; for it enunciates the two determinations, Being and Nothing, and contains them as distinct.—Nor can it at the same time be meant that one is to abstract from them and retain only the unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"12.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","text":"This meaning would itself prove to be one-sided, since that from which abstraction is supposed to be made is nevertheless present and named in the proposition.—Now insofar as the proposition: Being and Nothing are the same, expresses the identity of these determinations, but in fact equally contains both of them as distinct, it contradicts itself within itself and dissolves itself. If we hold fast to this more closely, then a proposition is here posited which, considered more closely, has the movement of vanishing through itself. But thereby there occurs in it itself what is supposed to constitute its proper content, namely, becoming.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"12.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","text":"Thus the proposition contains the result; it is this result in itself. But the circumstance to which attention is to be drawn here is the defect that the result is not itself expressed in the proposition; it is an external reflection that recognizes it in the proposition.—At the very beginning, this general observation must be made concerning this: that the proposition, in the form of a judgment, is not suited to express speculative truths; acquaintance with this circumstance would be apt to remove many misunderstandings of speculative truths. Judgment is an identical relation between subject and predicate; abstraction is made in it from the fact that the subject has yet more determinacies than that of the predicate, as likewise from the fact that the predicate is broader than the subject.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"12.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","text":"But if the content is speculative, then the non-identical element of subject and predicate is also an essential moment; yet this is not expressed in judgment. The paradoxical and bizarre light in which much of modern philosophy appears to those unacquainted with speculative thinking falls, in many ways, upon the form of the simple judgment when it is used for the expression of speculative results.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"12.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","text":"For the purpose of expressing speculative truth, the defect is at first supplemented by adding the opposite proposition, the proposition: Being and Nothing are not the same, which was likewise stated above. But then the further defect arises that these propositions are unconnected, and consequently present the content only in antinomy, whereas their content relates to one and the same thing, and the determinations expressed in the two propositions are supposed to be united absolutely,—a union which can then only be expressed as an unrest of simultaneously incompatible elements, as a movement. The most common wrong done to speculative content is to make it one-sided, i.e. to single out only one of the propositions into which it can be resolved.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"12.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","text":"It cannot then be denied that this proposition is asserted; however correct the report is, it is nevertheless false, for once one proposition has been taken from the speculative, at least the other too ought equally to be heeded and stated.—Here the, so to speak, unfortunate word: unity, must also be mentioned in particular; unity denotes, even more than identity, a subjective reflection; it is taken principally as the relation that arises from comparison, from external reflection. Insofar as this finds the same thing in two different objects, a unity is present in such a way that the complete indifference of the objects themselves that are compared toward this unity is presupposed, so that this comparing and the unity do not concern the objects themselves, and are an activity and determination external to them.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"12.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0007","text":"Unity therefore expresses wholly abstract sameness, and sounds all the harsher and more striking the more those of which it is enunciated show themselves to be absolutely distinct. Thus, instead of unity, it would in this respect be better to say only non-separation and inseparability; but thereby the affirmative element of the relation of the whole is not expressed.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"12.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","text":"Thus the whole, true result that has emerged here is becoming, which is not merely the one-sided or abstract unity of Being and Nothing. Rather, it consists in this movement: that pure Being is immediate and simple, that for this reason it is equally pure Nothing, that their difference is, but equally sublates itself and is not. The result therefore asserts the difference of Being and Nothing equally, but as one that is merely meant.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"12.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","text":"One thinks that Being is rather the absolutely other than Nothing is, and nothing is clearer than their absolute difference, and nothing seems easier than to be able to state it. But it is equally easy to convince oneself that this is impossible, that it is unsayable. Those who wish to insist on the difference between Being and Nothing may be called upon to state wherein it consists. If Being and Nothing had any determinacy whereby they were distinct, then, as has been recalled, they would be determinate Being and determinate Nothing, not pure Being and pure Nothing, as they still are here. Their difference is therefore completely empty; each of the two is in the same way the indeterminate; it therefore does not consist in themselves, but only in a third, in meaning. But meaning is a form of the subjective, which does not belong in this series of exposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"12.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","text":"But the third in which Being and Nothing have their subsistence must also occur here; and it has occurred: it is becoming. In it they are as distinct; becoming is only insofar as they are distinct. This third is an Other than they are;—they subsist only in an Other, which likewise means: they do not subsist for themselves. Becoming is the subsistence of Being no less than of non-being; or their subsistence is only their Being in One; it is precisely this their subsistence that equally sublates their difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"12.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011","text":"The demand to state the difference between Being and Nothing also includes the demand to say what Being and what Nothing are. Those who resist recognizing both the one and the other only as a transition into each other, and who assert this or that of Being and of Nothing, may state what they are speaking of, i.e. may set forth a definition of Being and Nothing and demonstrate that it is correct. Without having satisfied this first demand of ancient science, whose logical rules they otherwise allow and apply, all those assertions concerning Being and Nothing are merely assurances, scientific invalidities.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"12.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","text":"When it has otherwise been said that existence, insofar as this is at first held to be synonymous with Being, is the complement to possibility, another determination, possibility, has thereby been presupposed, and Being has been pronounced not in its immediacy, indeed as not self-subsistent, as conditioned. For mediated Being, we shall reserve the expression: existence. But one readily represents Being to oneself—perhaps under the image of pure light, as the clarity of unclouded sight, and Nothing as pure night—and connects their difference with this familiar sensible diversity. Yet in fact, if one represents this seeing more exactly, one can easily perceive that in absolute clarity one sees as much and as little as in absolute darkness, that one seeing is just as much as the other, pure seeing, seeing of Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"12.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","text":"Pure light and pure darkness are two voids, which are the same. Only in determinate light—and light is determined by darkness,—thus in clouded light; likewise only in determinate darkness—and darkness is determined by light,—in illuminated darkness, can something be distinguished, because only clouded light and illuminated darkness have difference in themselves and are thereby determinate Being, being-there.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"12.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"e7369eef4491f718596ed8724f40d97a3376bfeb1afa24538ed7c71085a34971","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3","title":"Remark 3.","order":13,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ANM3","text":"Die Einheit, deren Momente, Seyn und Nichts, als untrennbare sind, ist von ihnen selbst zugleich verschieden, so ein Drittes gegen sie, welches in seiner eigenthümlichsten Form das Werden ist. Übergehen ist dasselbe als Werden, nur daß in jenem die beiden, von deren Einem zum anderen übergegangen wird, mehr als außereinander ruhend und das Übergehen als zwischen ihnen geschehend vorgestellt wird. Wo und Wie nun vom Seyn oder Nichts die Rede wird, muß dieses Dritte vorhanden seyn; denn jene bestehen nicht für sich, sondern sind nur im Werden, in diesem Dritten. Aber dieses Dritte hat vielfache empirische Gestalten, welche von der Abstraktion bei Seite gestellt oder vernachläßigt werden, um jene ihre Produkte, das Seyn und das Nichts, jedes für sich festzuhalten und sie gegen das Übergehen geschützt zu zeigen. Gegen solches einfaches Verhalten der Abstraktion ist ebenso einfach nur an die empirische Existenz zu erinnern, in der jene Abstraktion selbst nur Etwas ist, ein Daseyn hat. Oder es sind sonst Reflexionsformen, durch welche die Trennung der Untrennbaren fixirt werden soll. An solcher Bestimmung ist an und für sich das Gegentheil ihrer selbst vorhanden, und ohne auf die Natur der Sache zurückzugehen und an diese zu appelliren, ist jene Reflexionsbestimmung an ihr selbst dadurch zu konfondiren, daß sie genommen wird, wie sie sich giebt, und ihr Anderes an ihr selbst aufgezeigt wird. Es würde eine vergebliche Mühe seyn, alle Wendungen und Einfälle der Reflexion und ihres Raisonnements gleichsam einfangen zu wollen, um ihr die Auswege und Absprünge, womit sie sich ihren Widerspruch gegen sich selbst verdeckt, zu benehmen und unmöglich zu machen. Darum enthalte ich mich auch, gegen vielfache sich so nennende Einwürfe und Widerlegungen, welche dagegen, daß weder Seyn noch Nichts etwas Wahrhaftes, sondern nur das Werden ihre Wahrheit ist, aufgebracht worden sind, Rücksicht zu nehmen; die Gedanken-Bildung, die dazu gehört, die Nichtigkeit jener Widerlegungen einzusehen oder vielmehr solche Einfälle sich selbst zu vertreiben, wird nur durch die kritische Erkenntniß der Verstandesformen bewirkt; aber die, welche am ergiebigsten an dergleichen Einwürfen sind, fallen sogleich über die ersten Sätze mit ihren Reflexionen her, ohne durch das weitere Studium der Logik sich zum Bewußtseyn über die Natur dieser kruden Reflexionen zu verhelfen oder verholfen zu haben.\n\nEs sollen einige der Erscheinungen betrachtet werden, die sich daran ergeben, wenn das Seyn und das Nichts von einander isolirt, und Eins außer dem Bereiche des Anderen gesetzt wird, so daß hiermit das Übergehen negirt ist.\n\nParmenides hielt das Seyn fest und war am konsequentesten, indem er zugleich vom Nichts sagte, daß es gar nicht ist; nur das Seyn ist. Das Seyn so ganz für sich ist das Unbestimmte, hat also keine Beziehung auf Anderes; es scheint daher, daß von diesem Anfang aus nicht weiter fortgegangen werden könne, nämlich aus ihm selbst, und ein Fortgang nur dadurch geschehen könne, daß von Außen etwas Fremdes daran geknüpft würde. Der Fortgang, daß das Seyn dasselbe ist als das Nichts, erscheint somit als ein zweiter, absoluter Anfang,—ein Übergehen, das für sich ist, und äußerlich zu dem Seyn hinzuträte. Seyn wäre überhaupt nicht der absolute Anfang, wenn es eine Bestimmtheit hätte; alsdann hänge es von einem Andern ab, und wäre nicht unmittelbar, nicht der Anfang. Ist es aber unbestimmt, und damit wahrer Anfang, so hat es auch nichts, wodurch es sich zu einem anderen überleitet, es ist zugleich das Ende. Es kann ebenso wenig etwas aus demselben hervorbrechen, als etwas in dasselbe einbrechen kann; bei Parmenides wie bei Spinoza soll von dem Seyn oder der absoluten Substanz nicht fortgegangen werden zu dem Negativen, Endlichen. Wird nun dennoch fortgegangen, was wie bemerkt, von dem beziehungs—hiermit fortgangslosen Seyn aus nur auf äußerliche Weise geschehen kann, so ist dieser Fortgang ein zweiter, neuer Anfang. So ist Fichte's absolutester, unbedingter Grundsatz: A = A Setzen; der zweite ist Entgegensetzen; dieser soll zum Theil bedingt, zum Theil unbedingt (somit der Widerspruch in sich) seyn. Es ist dieß ein Fortgehen der äußern Reflexion, welches ebensowohl das, womit es als einem Absoluten anfängt, wieder verneint,—das Entgegensetzen ist die Negation der ersten Identität,—als es sein zweites Unbedingtes sogleich ausdrücklich zugleich zu einem Bedingten macht. Wenn aber überhaupt eine Berechtigung wäre, fortzugehen, d. i. den ersten Anfang aufzuheben, so müßte es in diesem ersten selbst liegen, daß ein Anderes sich darauf beziehen könnte; es müßte also ein Bestimmtes seyn. Allein für ein solches giebt sich das Seyn oder auch die absolute Substanz nicht aus; im Gegentheil. Es ist das Unmittelbare, das noch schlechthin Unbestimmte.\n\nDie beredtesten, vielleicht vergessenen Schilderungen über die Unmöglichkeit, von einem Abstrakten zu einem Ferneren und zu einer Vereinigung beider zu kommen, macht Jacobi im Interesse seiner Polemik gegen die kantische Synthesis des Selbstbewußtseyns a priori, in seiner Abh. über das Unternehmen des Kriticismus, die Vernunft zu Verstande zu bringen (Jac. Werke III. Bd.). Er stellt (S. 113) die Aufgabe so, daß in einem Reinen, sey es des Bewußtseyns, des Raums oder der Zeit, das Entstehen oder Hervorbringen einer Synthesis aufgezeigt werde. \"Der Raum sey Eines, die Zeit sey Eines, das Bewußtseyn sey Eines;—sagt nun an, wie sich eines von diesen drei Einen in ihm selbst rein vermannigfaltiget;—jedes ist nur Eines und kein Anderes;—eine Einerleiheit, eine Der- Die- Das- Selbigkeit! ohne Derheit, Dieheit, Dasheit; denn diese schlummern, mit den Der, Die, Das noch im unendlichen = 0 des Unbestimmten, woraus alles und jedes Bestimmte auch erst hervorgehen soll! Was bringt in jene, drei Unendlichkeiten, Endlichkeit; was befruchtet Raum und Zeit a priori mit Zahl und Maß, und verwandelt sie in ein reines Mannigfaltiges; was bringt die reine Spontaneität (Ich) zur Oscillation? Wie kommt sein reiner Vokal zum Mitlauter, oder vielmehr wie setzt sein lautloses ununterbrochenes Blasen, sich selbst unterbrechend, ab, um wenigstens eine Art von Selbstlaut, einen Accent zu gewinnen?\"—Man sieht, Jacobi hat sehr bestimmt das Unwesen der Abstraktion, es sey nun sogenannter absoluter d. i. nur abstrakter Raum, oder ebensolche Zeit, oder ebensolches reines Bewußtseyn, Ich, erkannt; er beharrt darin zu dem Behuf, die Unmöglichkeit eines Fortgangs zu Anderem, der Bedingung einer Synthesis, und zur Synthesis selbst zu behaupten. Die Synthesis, welche das Interesse ausmacht, muß nicht als eine Verknüpfung von äußerlich schon vorhandenen Bestimmungen genommen werden,—Theils ist es selbst um die Erzeugung eines Zweiten zu einem Ersten, eines Bestimmten zum unbestimmten Anfänglichen zu thun; Theils aber um die immanente Synthesis, Synthesis a priori,—an und für sich seyende Einheit des Unterschiedenen. Werden ist diese immanente Synthesis des Seyns und Nichts; aber weil der Synthesis der Sinn von einem äußerlichen Zusammenbringen äußerlich gegeneinander Vorhandener am nächsten liegt, ist mit Recht der Name Synthesis, synthetische Einheit außer Gebrauch gesetzt worden.—Jacobi fragt, wie kommt der reine Vokal des Ich zum Mitlauter, was bringt Bestimmtheit in die Unbestimmtheit—das was? wäre leicht beantwortet, und von Kant ist diese Frage auf seine Weise beantwortet worden; aber die Frage nach dem Wie? heißt: auf welche Art und Weise, nach welchem Verhältniß und dergleichen, und verlangt so die Angabe einer besondern Kategorie; aber von Art und Weise, Verstandes-Kategorien kann hierbei nicht die Rede seyn. Die Frage nach dem wie? gehört selbst zu den übeln Manieren der Reflexion, welche nach der Begreiflichkeit frägt, aber dabei ihre festen Kategorien voraussetzt, und damit zum Voraus gegen die Beantwortung dessen, nach was sie fragt, sich gewaffnet weiß. Den höheren Sinn einer Frage nach der Nothwendigkeit der Synthese hat sie bei Jacobi auch nicht, denn er bleibt, wie gesagt, fest in den Abstraktionen beharren, für die Behauptung der Unmöglichkeit der Synthese. Insbesondere anschaulich beschreibt er (S. 147) die Procedur zur Abstraktion des Raumes zu gelangen. \"Ich muß für so lange rein zu vergessen suchen, daß ich je irgend etwas sah, hörte, rührte und berührte, mich selbst ausdrücklich nicht ausgenommen. Rein, rein, rein vergessen muß ich alle Bewegung, und mir gerade dieß Vergessen, weil es das schwerste ist, am angelegentlichsten seyn lassen. Alles überhaupt muß ich, so wie ich es weggedacht habe, auch ganz und vollkommen weggeschafft seyn lassen, und gar nichts übrig behalten, als die mit Gewalt stehen gebliebene Anschauung allein des unendlichen unveränderlichen Raums. Ich darf mich daher auch nicht selbst als etwas von ihm Unterschiedenes und gleichwohl mit ihm Verbundenes, wieder in ihn hineindenken; ich darf mich nicht von ihm bloß umgeben und durchdringen lassen; sondern ich muß ganz übergehen in ihn, Eins mit ihm werden, mich in ihn verwandeln; ich muß von mir selbst nichts übrig lassen, als diese meine Anschauung selbst, um sie als eine wahrhaft selbstständige, unabhängige, Einig- und Alleinige Vorstellung zu betrachten.\"\n\nBei dieser ganz abstrakten Reinheit der Kontinuität, d. i. Unbestimmtheit und Leerheit des Vorstellens ist es gleichgültig, diese Abstraktion Raum zu nennen, oder reines Anschauen, reines Denken;—es ist alles dasselbe, was der Inder, wenn er äußerlich bewegungslos, und ebenso in Empfindung, Vorstellung, Phantasie, Begierde u.s.f. regungslos jahrelang nur auf die Spitze seiner Nase sieht, nur Om, Om, Om innerlich in sich, oder gar Nichts spricht, —Brahma nennt. Dieses dumpfe, leere Bewußtseyn ist, als Bewußtseyn aufgefaßt,—das Seyn.\n\nIn diesem Leeren, sagt nun Jacobi weiter, widerfahre ihm das Gegentheil von dem, was kantischer Versicherung gemäß, ihm widerfahren sollte; er finde sich nicht als ein Vieles und Mannigfaltiges, vielmehr als Eines ohne alle Vielheit und Mannigfaltigkeit; ja, \"ich bin die Unmöglichkeit selbst, bin die Vernichtung alles Mannigfaltigen und Vielen,—kann aus meinem reinen, schlechterdings einfachen, unveränderlichen Wesen auch nicht das Mindeste wieder herstellen oder in mich hinein gespenstern;—so offenbart sich in dieser Reinheit, alles Außerund Nebeneinanderseyn, alle hierauf beruhende Mannigfaltigkeit und Vielheit, als ein rein Unmögliches.\"\n\nDiese Unmöglichkeit heißt nichts anders als die Tautologie, ich halte an der abstrakten Einheit fest und schließe alle Vielheit und Mannigfaltigkeit aus, halte mich im Unterschiedslosen und Unbestimmten, und sehe weg von allem Unterschiedenen und Bestimmten. Die kantische Synthesis a priori des Selbstbewußtseyns, das ist, die Thätigkeit dieser Einheit, sich zu dirimiren und in dieser Diremtion sich selbst zu erhalten, verdünnt sich Jacobi zu derselben Abstraktion. Jene \"Synthesis an sich\", das \"ursprüngliche Urtheilen,\" macht er einseitig zu \"der Kopula an sich;—ein Ist, Ist, Ist, ohne Anfang und Ende und ohne Was, Wer und Welche; dieses ins Unendliche fortgehende Wiederholen der Wiederholung ist die alleinige Geschäftigkeit, Funktion und Produktion der allerreinsten Synthesis; sie selbst ist das bloße, reine, absolute Wiederholen selbst.\" Oder in der That, da kein Absatz, d. i. keine Negation, Unterscheiden darin ist, so ist sie nicht ein Wiederholen, sondern nur das ununterschiedene einfache Seyn.—Aber ist dieß denn noch Synthesis, wenn Jacobi gerade das wegläßt, wodurch die Einheit synthetische Einheit ist?\n\nZunächst, wenn Jacobi sich so in dem absoluten d. h. abstrakten Raum, Zeit, auch Bewußtseyn festsetzt, ist zu sagen, daß er sich auf diese Weise in etwas empirisch-Falsches versetzt und festhält; es giebt d. h. empirisch vorhanden ist kein Raum und Zeit, die ein unbegrenztes Räumliches und Zeitliches wären, nicht in ihrer Kontinuität von mannigfaltig begrenztem Daseyn und Veränderung erfüllt wären, so daß diese Grenzen und Veränderungen ungetrennt und untrennbar der Räumlichkeit und Zeitlichkeit angehören; ebenso ist das Bewußtseyn mit bestimmtem Empfinden, Vorstellen, Begehren u.s.f. erfüllt; es existirt ungetrennt von irgend einem besonderen Inhalt.—Das empirische Übergehen versteht sich ohnehin von selbst; das Bewußtseyn kann sich wohl den leeren Raum, leere Zeit und das leere Bewußtseyn selbst, oder das reine Seyn, zum Gegenstand und Inhalt machen; aber es bleibt nicht dabei, sondern geht nicht nur, sondern drängt sich aus solcher Leerheit hinaus zu einem besseren, d. i. auf irgend eine Weise konkreteren Inhalt, und so schlecht ein Inhalt sonst sey, so ist er insofern besser und wahrer; eben ein solcher Inhalt ist ein synthetischer überhaupt; synthetisch in allgemeinerem Sinne genommen. So bekommt Parmenides mit dem Scheine und der Meinung, dem Gegentheil des Seyns und der Wahrheit, zu thun; so Spinoza mit den Attributen, den Modis, der Ausdehnung, Bewegung, dem Verstande, Willen u.s.f. Die Synthesis enthält und zeigt die Unwahrheit jener Abstraktionen, in ihr sind sie in Einheit mit ihrem Anderen, also nicht als für sich bestehende, nicht als absolute, sondern schlechthin als relative.\n\nDas Aufzeigen der empirischen Nichtigkeit des leeren Raums u.s.f. aber ist es nicht, um das es zu thun ist. Das Bewußtseyn kann sich abstrahirend allerdings auch mit jenem Unbestimmten erfüllen, und die festgehaltenen Abstraktionen sind die Gedanken von reinem Raum, Zeit, reinen Bewußtseyn, reinem Seyn. Der Gedanke des reinen Raums u.s.f. d. i. der reine Raum u.s.f. an ihm selbst soll als nichtig aufgezeigt werden, d. i. daß er als solcher schon sein Gegentheil, daß an ihm selbst schon sein Gegentheil in ihn eingedrungen, er schon für sich das Herausgegangenseyn aus sich selbst, Bestimmtheit, sey.\n\nDieß ergiebt sich aber unmittelbar an ihnen. Sie sind, was Jacobi reichlich beschreibt, Resultate der Abstraktion, sind ausdrücklich als Unbestimmte bestimmt, was—um zu seiner einfachsten Form zurückzugehen, das Seyn ist. Eben diese Unbestimmtheit ist aber das, was die Bestimmtheit desselben ausmacht; denn die Unbestimmtheit ist der Bestimmtheit entgegengesetzt; sie ist somit als Entgegengesetztes selbst das Bestimmte, oder Negative, und zwar das reine, ganz abstrakt Negative. Diese Unbestimmtheit oder abstrakte Negation, welche so das Seyn an ihm selbst hat, ist es, was die äußere wie die innere Reflexion ausspricht, indem sie es dem Nichts gleich setzt, es für ein leeres Gedankending, für Nichts erklärt.—Oder kann man sich ausdrücken, weil das Seyn das Bestimmungslose ist, ist es nicht die (affirmative) Bestimmtheit, die es ist, nicht Seyn, sondern Nichts.\n\nIn der reinen Reflexion des Anfangs, wie er in dieser Logik mit dem Seyn als solchem gemacht wird, ist der Übergang noch verborgen; weil das Seyn nur als unmittelbar gesetzt ist, bricht das Nichts an ihm nur unmittelbar hervor. Aber alle folgenden Bestimmungen, wie gleich das Daseyn, sind konkreter; es ist an diesem das schon gesetzt, was den Widerspruch jener Abstraktionen und daher ihr Übergehen enthält und hervorbringt. Beim Seyn als jenem Einfachen, Unmittelbaren wird die Erinnerung, daß es Resultat der vollkommenen Abstraktion, also schon von daher abstrakte Negativität, Nichts, ist, hinter der Wissenschaft zurückgelassen, welchem innerhalb ihrer selbst, ausdrücklich vom Wesen aus, jene einseitige Unmittelbarkeit als eine Vermittelte darstellen wird, wo das Seyn als Existenz und das Vermittelnde dieses Seyns, der Grund, gesetzt ist.\n\nMit jener Erinnerung läßt sich der Übergang von Seyn in Nichts als etwas selbst leichtes und triviales so vorstellen oder auch, wie man es nennt, erklären und begreiflich machen, daß Freilich das Seyn, welches zum Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht worden, Nichts sey, denn man könne von Allem abstrahiren, und wenn von Allem abstrahirt worden, so bleibe Nichts übrig. Aber, kann man fortfahren, somit sey der Anfang nicht ein Affirmatives, nicht Seyn, sondern eben Nichts, und Nichts sey dann auch das Ende, wenigstens sosehr als das unmittelbare Seyn und selbst noch vielmehr. Das Kürzeste ist solches Raisonniren gewähren zu lassen und zuzusehen, wie denn die Resultate beschaffen sind, auf welche es pocht. Daß hiernach das Nichts das Resultat jenes Raisonnements wäre, und nun der Anfang mit Nichts (wie in chinesischer Philosophie) gemacht werden sollte, so wäre darum nicht die Hand umzukehren, denn ehe man sie umkehrte, hätte sich ebenso sehr dieß Nichts in Seyn verkehrt, (s. oben: B. Nichts). Aber ferner wenn jene Abstraktion von Allem, welches Alles denn doch Seyendes ist, vorausgesetzt wäre, so ist sie genauer zu nehmen; das Resultat der Abstraktion von allem Seyenden ist zunächst abstraktes Seyn, Seyn überhaupt; wie im kosmologischen Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes aus dem zufälligen Seyn der Welt, über welches sich darin erhoben wird, noch das Seyn mit hinaufgebracht, das Seyn zum unendlichen Seyn bestimmt wird. Es kann aber allerdings auch von diesem reinen Seyn abstrahirt, das Seyn noch zu dem Allem, wovon bereits abstrahirt worden, geschlagen werden; dann bleibt Nichts. Man kann nun, wenn man das Denken des Nichts, d.i. sein Umschlagen in Seyn vergessen will oder nichts davon wüßte, im Style jenes Könnens fortfahren; es kann nämlich (Gottlob!) auch vom Nichts abstrahirt werden (wie denn auch die Schöpfung der Welt eine Abstraktion vom Nichts ist) und dann bleibt nicht Nichts, denn eben von diesem wird abstrahirt, sondern man ist so wieder im Seyn angekommen.—dieß Können giebt ein äußerliches Spiel des Abstrahirens, wobei das Abstrahiren selbst nur das einseitige Thun des Negativen ist. Zunächst liegt in diesem Können selbst, daß ihm das Seyn so gleichgültig ist als das Nichts, und daß so sehr jedes von Beiden verschwindet, ebenso sehr jedes auch entsteht; aber ebenso gleichgültig ist es, ob vom Thun des Nichts, oder dem Nichts ausgegangen wird; das Thun des Nichts, d. i. das bloße Abstrahiren ist nicht mehr noch weniger etwas Wahrhaftes als das bloße Nichts.\n\nDie Dialektik, nach welcher Plato das Eine im Parmenides behandelt, ist gleichfalls mehr für eine Dialektik der äußern Reflexion zu achten. Das Seyn und das Eine sind beides Eleatische Formen, die Dasselbe sind. Aber sie sind auch zu unterscheiden, so nimmt sie Plato in jenem Dialoge. Nachdem er von dem Einen die mancherlei Bestimmungen von Ganzen und Theilen, in sich selbst, in einem anderen seyn u.s.f. von Figur, Zeit u.s.f. entfernt, so ist das Resultat, daß dem Einen das Seyn nicht zukomme, denn anders komme einem Etwas das Seyn nicht zu, als nach einer jener Weisen (p. 141 e. Vol. III. ed. Steph.). Hierauf behandelt Plato den Satz: das Eine ist; und es ist bei ihm nachzusehen, wie von diesem Satze aus der Übergang zu dem Nichtseyn des Einen bewerkstelligt wird; es geschieht durch die Vergleichung der beiden Bestimmungen des vorausgesetzten Satzes: das Eine ist; er enthält das Eine und das Seyn; und das Eine ist enthält mehr, als wenn man nur sagt: das Eine. Darin daß sie verschieden sind, wird das Moment der Negation, das der Satz enthält, aufgezeigt. Es erhellt, daß dieser Weg eine Voraussetzung hat, und eine äußere Reflexion ist.\n\nWie hier das Eine mit dem Seyn in Verbindung gesetzt ist, wird das Seyn, welches abstrakt für sich festgehalten werden soll am einfachsten, ohne sich in das Denken einzulassen, in einer Verbindung aufgezeigt, die das Gegentheil dessen enthält, was behauptet werden soll. Das Seyn, wie es unmittelbar ist, genommen gehört einem Subjekte an, ist ein ausgesprochenes, hat ein empirisches Daseyn überhaupt, und steht damit im Boden der Schranke und des Negativen. In welchen Ausdrücken oder Wendungen der Verstand sich fasse, wenn er sich gegen die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts sträubt, und sich auf das, was unmittelbar vorhanden sey, beruft, wird er eben in dieser Erfahrung selbst nichts als bestimmtes Seyn, Seyn mit einer Schranke oder Negation,—jene Einheit finden, die er verwirft. Die Behauptung des unmittelbaren Seyns reducirt sich so auf eine empirische Existenz, deren Aufzeigen sie nicht verwerfen kann, weil es die Unmittelbarkeit außerhalb des Denkens ist, an die sie sich halten will.\n\nDasselbe ist der Fall mit dem Nichts, nur auf entgegengesetzte Weise, und diese Reflexion ist bekannt und oft genug über dasselbe gemacht worden. Das Nichts zeigt sich in seiner Unmittelbarkeit genommen als seyend; denn seiner Natur nach ist es dasselbe als das Seyn. Das Nichts wird gedacht, vorgestellt, es wird von ihm gesprochen; es ist also; das Nichts hat an dem Denken, Vorstellen, Sprechen, u.s.f. sein Seyn. Dieß Seyn ist aber ferner, auch von ihm unterschieden; es wird daher gesagt, daß das Nichts zwar im Denken, Vorstellen ist, aber daß darum nicht es ist, nicht ihm als solchem das Seyn zukomme, daß nur Denken oder Vorstellen dieses Seyn ist. Bei diesem Unterscheiden ist eben so sehr nicht zu läugnen, daß das Nichts in Beziehung auf ein Seyn steht; aber in der Beziehung, ob sie gleich auch den Unterschied enthält, ist eine Einheit mit dem Seyn vorhanden. Auf weiche Weise das Nichts ausgesprochen oder aufgezeigt werde, zeigt es sich in Verbindung oder wenn man will Berührung mit einem Seyn, ungetrennt von einem Seyn, eben in einem Daseyn.\n\nIndem aber so das Nichts in einem Daseyn aufgezeigt wird, pflegt noch dieser Unterschied desselben vom Seyn vorzuschweben, daß das Daseyn des Nichts durchaus nichts ihm selbst zukommendes sey, daß es nicht das Seyn für sich selbst an ihm habe, es nicht das Seyn als solches sey; das Nichts sey nur Abwesenheit des Seyns, die Finsterniß so nur Abwesenheit des Lichts, die Kälte nur Abwesenheit der Wärme u.s.f. Finsterniß habe nur Bedeutung in Beziehung auf das Auge, in äußerer Vergleichung mit dem Positiven, dem Lichte, ebenso Kälte sey nur Etwas in unserer Empfindung, Licht, Wärme, wie Seyn, hingegen seyen für sich das Objektive, Reale, Wirksame, von schlechthin anderer Qualität und Würde, als jene Negativen, als Nichts. Man kann es häufig als eine sehr wichtige Reflexion und bedeutende Erkenntniß aufgeführt finden, daß Finsterniß nur Abwesenheit des Lichts, Kälte nur Abwesenheit der Wärme sey. Über diese scharfsinnige Reflexion kann in diesem Felde von empirischen Gegenständen empirisch bemerkt werden, daß die Finsterniß sich im Lichte allerdings wirksam zeigt, indem sie dasselbe zur Farbe bestimmt und ihm selbst dadurch erst Sichtbarkeit ertheilt, indem wie früher gesagt, im reinen Lichte ebenso wenig gesehen wird, als in der reinen Finsterniß. Die Sichtbarkeit ist aber Wirksamkeit im Auge, an der jenes Negative ebenso viel Antheil hat, als das für das Reale, Positive geltende Licht; ebenso giebt sich die Kälte dem Wasser, unserer Empfindung u.s. f. genugsam zu erkennen, und wenn wir ihr sogenannte objektive Realität absprechen, so ist damit durchaus nichts gegen sie gewonnen. Aber ferner wäre zu rügen, daß hier gleichfalls, wie oben, von einem Negativen von bestimmtem Inhalte gesprochen wird, nicht beim Nichts selbst stehen geblieben wird, dem das Seyn an leerer Abstraktion nicht nachsteht, noch etwas voraus hat.—Allein Kälte, Finsterniß und dergleichen bestimmte Negationen sind sogleich für sich zu nehmen, und es ist zu sehen, was damit in Rücksicht ihrer allgemeinen Bestimmung, nach der sie hierher gebracht werden, gesetzt ist. Sie sollen nicht das Nichts überhaupt, sondern das Nichts vom Licht, Wärme u.s.f. von etwas Bestimmten, einem Inhalte seyn; so sind sie bestimmte, inhaltige Nichts, wenn man so sagen kann. Aber eine Bestimmtheit ist, wie noch weiter hin vorkommt, selbst eine Negation; so sind sie negative Nichts; aber ein negatives Nichts ist etwas Affirmatives. Das Umschlagen des Nichts durch seine Bestimmtheit (die vorhin als ein Daseyn im Subjekte, oder in sonst was es sey, erschien) in ein Affirmatives, erscheint dem Bewußtseyn, das in der Verstandes-Abstraktion feststeht, als das paradoxeste, so einfach die Einsicht ist, oder auch wegen ihrer Einfachheit selbst erscheint die Einsicht, daß die Negation der Negation Positives ist, als etwas Triviales, auf welches der stolze Verstand daher nicht zu achten brauche, obgleich die Sache ihre Richtigkeit habe,—und sie hat nicht nur diese Richtigkeit, sondern um der Allgemeinheit solcher Bestimmungen willen ihre unendliche Ausdehnung und allgemeine Anwendung, so daß wohl darauf zu achten wäre.\n\nNoch kann über die Bestimmung des Übergangs von Seyn und Nichts in einander bemerkt werden, daß derselbe eben so ohne weitere Reflexionsbestimmung aufzufassen ist. Er ist unmittelbar und ganz abstrakt, um der Abstraktion der übergehenden Momente willen, d. i. indem an diesen Momenten noch nicht die Bestimmtheit des anderen gesetzt ist, vermittelst dessen sie übergingen; das Nichts ist am Seyn noch nicht gesetzt, ob zwar Seyn wesentlich Nichts ist, und umgekehrt. Es ist daher unzulässig, weiters bestimmte Vermittelungen hier anzuwenden, und Seyn und Nichts in irgend einem Verhältnisse zu fassen,—jenes Übergehen ist noch kein Verhältniß. Es ist also unstatthaft zu sagen: Das Nichts ist der Grund vom Seyn; oder Seyn ist der Grund von Nichts;—das Nichts Ursache vom Seyn u.s.f.; oder es kann nur unter der Bedingung in das Nichts übergegangen werden, daß etwas ist, oder in das Seyn nur unter der Bedingung des Nichtseyns. Die Art der Beziehung kann nicht weiter bestimmt seyn, ohne daß zugleich die bezogenen Seiten weiter bestimmt würden. Der Zusammenhang von Grund und Folge u.s.f. hat nicht mehr das bloße Seyn und Nichts zu den Seiten, die er verbindet, sondern ausdrücklich Seyn, das Grund ist, und etwas, das zwar nur ein gesetztes, nicht Selbstständiges sey, das aber nicht das abstrakte Nichts ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","text":"Die Einheit, deren Momente, Seyn und Nichts, als untrennbare sind, ist von ihnen selbst zugleich verschieden, so ein Drittes gegen sie, welches in seiner eigenthümlichsten Form das Werden ist. Übergehen ist dasselbe als Werden, nur daß in jenem die beiden, von deren Einem zum anderen übergegangen wird, mehr als außereinander ruhend und das Übergehen als zwischen ihnen geschehend vorgestellt wird. Wo und Wie nun vom Seyn oder Nichts die Rede wird, muß dieses Dritte vorhanden seyn; denn jene bestehen nicht für sich, sondern sind nur im Werden, in diesem Dritten. Aber dieses Dritte hat vielfache empirische Gestalten, welche von der Abstraktion bei Seite gestellt oder vernachläßigt werden, um jene ihre Produkte, das Seyn und das Nichts, jedes für sich festzuhalten und sie gegen das Übergehen geschützt zu zeigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"13.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","text":"Gegen solches einfaches Verhalten der Abstraktion ist ebenso einfach nur an die empirische Existenz zu erinnern, in der jene Abstraktion selbst nur Etwas ist, ein Daseyn hat. Oder es sind sonst Reflexionsformen, durch welche die Trennung der Untrennbaren fixirt werden soll. An solcher Bestimmung ist an und für sich das Gegentheil ihrer selbst vorhanden, und ohne auf die Natur der Sache zurückzugehen und an diese zu appelliren, ist jene Reflexionsbestimmung an ihr selbst dadurch zu konfondiren, daß sie genommen wird, wie sie sich giebt, und ihr Anderes an ihr selbst aufgezeigt wird. Es würde eine vergebliche Mühe seyn, alle Wendungen und Einfälle der Reflexion und ihres Raisonnements gleichsam einfangen zu wollen, um ihr die Auswege und Absprünge, womit sie sich ihren Widerspruch gegen sich selbst verdeckt, zu benehmen und unmöglich zu machen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"13.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","text":"Darum enthalte ich mich auch, gegen vielfache sich so nennende Einwürfe und Widerlegungen, welche dagegen, daß weder Seyn noch Nichts etwas Wahrhaftes, sondern nur das Werden ihre Wahrheit ist, aufgebracht worden sind, Rücksicht zu nehmen; die Gedanken-Bildung, die dazu gehört, die Nichtigkeit jener Widerlegungen einzusehen oder vielmehr solche Einfälle sich selbst zu vertreiben, wird nur durch die kritische Erkenntniß der Verstandesformen bewirkt; aber die, welche am ergiebigsten an dergleichen Einwürfen sind, fallen sogleich über die ersten Sätze mit ihren Reflexionen her, ohne durch das weitere Studium der Logik sich zum Bewußtseyn über die Natur dieser kruden Reflexionen zu verhelfen oder verholfen zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"13.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004","text":"Es sollen einige der Erscheinungen betrachtet werden, die sich daran ergeben, wenn das Seyn und das Nichts von einander isolirt, und Eins außer dem Bereiche des Anderen gesetzt wird, so daß hiermit das Übergehen negirt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"13.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","text":"Parmenides hielt das Seyn fest und war am konsequentesten, indem er zugleich vom Nichts sagte, daß es gar nicht ist; nur das Seyn ist. Das Seyn so ganz für sich ist das Unbestimmte, hat also keine Beziehung auf Anderes; es scheint daher, daß von diesem Anfang aus nicht weiter fortgegangen werden könne, nämlich aus ihm selbst, und ein Fortgang nur dadurch geschehen könne, daß von Außen etwas Fremdes daran geknüpft würde. Der Fortgang, daß das Seyn dasselbe ist als das Nichts, erscheint somit als ein zweiter, absoluter Anfang,—ein Übergehen, das für sich ist, und äußerlich zu dem Seyn hinzuträte. Seyn wäre überhaupt nicht der absolute Anfang, wenn es eine Bestimmtheit hätte; alsdann hänge es von einem Andern ab, und wäre nicht unmittelbar, nicht der Anfang.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"13.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","text":"Ist es aber unbestimmt, und damit wahrer Anfang, so hat es auch nichts, wodurch es sich zu einem anderen überleitet, es ist zugleich das Ende. Es kann ebenso wenig etwas aus demselben hervorbrechen, als etwas in dasselbe einbrechen kann; bei Parmenides wie bei Spinoza soll von dem Seyn oder der absoluten Substanz nicht fortgegangen werden zu dem Negativen, Endlichen. Wird nun dennoch fortgegangen, was wie bemerkt, von dem beziehungs—hiermit fortgangslosen Seyn aus nur auf äußerliche Weise geschehen kann, so ist dieser Fortgang ein zweiter, neuer Anfang. So ist Fichte's absolutester, unbedingter Grundsatz: A = A Setzen; der zweite ist Entgegensetzen; dieser soll zum Theil bedingt, zum Theil unbedingt (somit der Widerspruch in sich) seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"13.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0007","text":"Es ist dieß ein Fortgehen der äußern Reflexion, welches ebensowohl das, womit es als einem Absoluten anfängt, wieder verneint,—das Entgegensetzen ist die Negation der ersten Identität,—als es sein zweites Unbedingtes sogleich ausdrücklich zugleich zu einem Bedingten macht. Wenn aber überhaupt eine Berechtigung wäre, fortzugehen, d. i. den ersten Anfang aufzuheben, so müßte es in diesem ersten selbst liegen, daß ein Anderes sich darauf beziehen könnte; es müßte also ein Bestimmtes seyn. Allein für ein solches giebt sich das Seyn oder auch die absolute Substanz nicht aus; im Gegentheil. Es ist das Unmittelbare, das noch schlechthin Unbestimmte.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"13.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008","text":"Die beredtesten, vielleicht vergessenen Schilderungen über die Unmöglichkeit, von einem Abstrakten zu einem Ferneren und zu einer Vereinigung beider zu kommen, macht Jacobi im Interesse seiner Polemik gegen die kantische Synthesis des Selbstbewußtseyns a priori, in seiner Abh. über das Unternehmen des Kriticismus, die Vernunft zu Verstande zu bringen (Jac. Werke III. Bd.). Er stellt (S. 113) die Aufgabe so, daß in einem Reinen, sey es des Bewußtseyns, des Raums oder der Zeit, das Entstehen oder Hervorbringen einer Synthesis aufgezeigt werde. \"Der Raum sey Eines, die Zeit sey Eines, das Bewußtseyn sey Eines;—sagt nun an, wie sich eines von diesen drei Einen in ihm selbst rein vermannigfaltiget;—jedes ist nur Eines und kein Anderes;—eine Einerleiheit, eine Der- Die- Das- Selbigkeit!","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"13.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0009","text":"ohne Derheit, Dieheit, Dasheit; denn diese schlummern, mit den Der, Die, Das noch im unendlichen = 0 des Unbestimmten, woraus alles und jedes Bestimmte auch erst hervorgehen soll! Was bringt in jene, drei Unendlichkeiten, Endlichkeit; was befruchtet Raum und Zeit a priori mit Zahl und Maß, und verwandelt sie in ein reines Mannigfaltiges; was bringt die reine Spontaneität (Ich) zur Oscillation? Wie kommt sein reiner Vokal zum Mitlauter, oder vielmehr wie setzt sein lautloses ununterbrochenes Blasen, sich selbst unterbrechend, ab, um wenigstens eine Art von Selbstlaut, einen Accent zu gewinnen?\"—Man sieht, Jacobi hat sehr bestimmt das Unwesen der Abstraktion, es sey nun sogenannter absoluter d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"13.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","text":"nur abstrakter Raum, oder ebensolche Zeit, oder ebensolches reines Bewußtseyn, Ich, erkannt; er beharrt darin zu dem Behuf, die Unmöglichkeit eines Fortgangs zu Anderem, der Bedingung einer Synthesis, und zur Synthesis selbst zu behaupten. Die Synthesis, welche das Interesse ausmacht, muß nicht als eine Verknüpfung von äußerlich schon vorhandenen Bestimmungen genommen werden,—Theils ist es selbst um die Erzeugung eines Zweiten zu einem Ersten, eines Bestimmten zum unbestimmten Anfänglichen zu thun; Theils aber um die immanente Synthesis, Synthesis a priori,—an und für sich seyende Einheit des Unterschiedenen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"13.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","text":"Werden ist diese immanente Synthesis des Seyns und Nichts; aber weil der Synthesis der Sinn von einem äußerlichen Zusammenbringen äußerlich gegeneinander Vorhandener am nächsten liegt, ist mit Recht der Name Synthesis, synthetische Einheit außer Gebrauch gesetzt worden.—Jacobi fragt, wie kommt der reine Vokal des Ich zum Mitlauter, was bringt Bestimmtheit in die Unbestimmtheit—das was? wäre leicht beantwortet, und von Kant ist diese Frage auf seine Weise beantwortet worden; aber die Frage nach dem Wie? heißt: auf welche Art und Weise, nach welchem Verhältniß und dergleichen, und verlangt so die Angabe einer besondern Kategorie; aber von Art und Weise, Verstandes-Kategorien kann hierbei nicht die Rede seyn. Die Frage nach dem wie?","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"13.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","text":"gehört selbst zu den übeln Manieren der Reflexion, welche nach der Begreiflichkeit frägt, aber dabei ihre festen Kategorien voraussetzt, und damit zum Voraus gegen die Beantwortung dessen, nach was sie fragt, sich gewaffnet weiß. Den höheren Sinn einer Frage nach der Nothwendigkeit der Synthese hat sie bei Jacobi auch nicht, denn er bleibt, wie gesagt, fest in den Abstraktionen beharren, für die Behauptung der Unmöglichkeit der Synthese. Insbesondere anschaulich beschreibt er (S. 147) die Procedur zur Abstraktion des Raumes zu gelangen. \"Ich muß für so lange rein zu vergessen suchen, daß ich je irgend etwas sah, hörte, rührte und berührte, mich selbst ausdrücklich nicht ausgenommen. Rein, rein, rein vergessen muß ich alle Bewegung, und mir gerade dieß Vergessen, weil es das schwerste ist, am angelegentlichsten seyn lassen.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"13.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0013","text":"Alles überhaupt muß ich, so wie ich es weggedacht habe, auch ganz und vollkommen weggeschafft seyn lassen, und gar nichts übrig behalten, als die mit Gewalt stehen gebliebene Anschauung allein des unendlichen unveränderlichen Raums. Ich darf mich daher auch nicht selbst als etwas von ihm Unterschiedenes und gleichwohl mit ihm Verbundenes, wieder in ihn hineindenken; ich darf mich nicht von ihm bloß umgeben und durchdringen lassen; sondern ich muß ganz übergehen in ihn, Eins mit ihm werden, mich in ihn verwandeln; ich muß von mir selbst nichts übrig lassen, als diese meine Anschauung selbst, um sie als eine wahrhaft selbstständige, unabhängige, Einig- und Alleinige Vorstellung zu betrachten.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"13.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0014","text":"Bei dieser ganz abstrakten Reinheit der Kontinuität, d. i. Unbestimmtheit und Leerheit des Vorstellens ist es gleichgültig, diese Abstraktion Raum zu nennen, oder reines Anschauen, reines Denken;—es ist alles dasselbe, was der Inder, wenn er äußerlich bewegungslos, und ebenso in Empfindung, Vorstellung, Phantasie, Begierde u.s.f. regungslos jahrelang nur auf die Spitze seiner Nase sieht, nur Om, Om, Om innerlich in sich, oder gar Nichts spricht, —Brahma nennt. Dieses dumpfe, leere Bewußtseyn ist, als Bewußtseyn aufgefaßt,—das Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"13.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0015","text":"In diesem Leeren, sagt nun Jacobi weiter, widerfahre ihm das Gegentheil von dem, was kantischer Versicherung gemäß, ihm widerfahren sollte; er finde sich nicht als ein Vieles und Mannigfaltiges, vielmehr als Eines ohne alle Vielheit und Mannigfaltigkeit; ja, \"ich bin die Unmöglichkeit selbst, bin die Vernichtung alles Mannigfaltigen und Vielen,—kann aus meinem reinen, schlechterdings einfachen, unveränderlichen Wesen auch nicht das Mindeste wieder herstellen oder in mich hinein gespenstern;—so offenbart sich in dieser Reinheit, alles Außerund Nebeneinanderseyn, alle hierauf beruhende Mannigfaltigkeit und Vielheit, als ein rein Unmögliches.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"13.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0016","text":"Diese Unmöglichkeit heißt nichts anders als die Tautologie, ich halte an der abstrakten Einheit fest und schließe alle Vielheit und Mannigfaltigkeit aus, halte mich im Unterschiedslosen und Unbestimmten, und sehe weg von allem Unterschiedenen und Bestimmten. Die kantische Synthesis a priori des Selbstbewußtseyns, das ist, die Thätigkeit dieser Einheit, sich zu dirimiren und in dieser Diremtion sich selbst zu erhalten, verdünnt sich Jacobi zu derselben Abstraktion. Jene \"Synthesis an sich\", das \"ursprüngliche Urtheilen,\" macht er einseitig zu \"der Kopula an sich;—ein Ist, Ist, Ist, ohne Anfang und Ende und ohne Was, Wer und Welche; dieses ins Unendliche fortgehende Wiederholen der Wiederholung ist die alleinige Geschäftigkeit, Funktion und Produktion der allerreinsten Synthesis; sie selbst ist das bloße, reine, absolute Wiederholen selbst.\" Oder in der That, da kein Absatz, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"13.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0017","text":"keine Negation, Unterscheiden darin ist, so ist sie nicht ein Wiederholen, sondern nur das ununterschiedene einfache Seyn.—Aber ist dieß denn noch Synthesis, wenn Jacobi gerade das wegläßt, wodurch die Einheit synthetische Einheit ist?","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"13.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","text":"Zunächst, wenn Jacobi sich so in dem absoluten d. h. abstrakten Raum, Zeit, auch Bewußtseyn festsetzt, ist zu sagen, daß er sich auf diese Weise in etwas empirisch-Falsches versetzt und festhält; es giebt d. h. empirisch vorhanden ist kein Raum und Zeit, die ein unbegrenztes Räumliches und Zeitliches wären, nicht in ihrer Kontinuität von mannigfaltig begrenztem Daseyn und Veränderung erfüllt wären, so daß diese Grenzen und Veränderungen ungetrennt und untrennbar der Räumlichkeit und Zeitlichkeit angehören; ebenso ist das Bewußtseyn mit bestimmtem Empfinden, Vorstellen, Begehren u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"13.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019","text":"erfüllt; es existirt ungetrennt von irgend einem besonderen Inhalt.—Das empirische Übergehen versteht sich ohnehin von selbst; das Bewußtseyn kann sich wohl den leeren Raum, leere Zeit und das leere Bewußtseyn selbst, oder das reine Seyn, zum Gegenstand und Inhalt machen; aber es bleibt nicht dabei, sondern geht nicht nur, sondern drängt sich aus solcher Leerheit hinaus zu einem besseren, d. i. auf irgend eine Weise konkreteren Inhalt, und so schlecht ein Inhalt sonst sey, so ist er insofern besser und wahrer; eben ein solcher Inhalt ist ein synthetischer überhaupt; synthetisch in allgemeinerem Sinne genommen. So bekommt Parmenides mit dem Scheine und der Meinung, dem Gegentheil des Seyns und der Wahrheit, zu thun; so Spinoza mit den Attributen, den Modis, der Ausdehnung, Bewegung, dem Verstande, Willen u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"13.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0020","text":"Die Synthesis enthält und zeigt die Unwahrheit jener Abstraktionen, in ihr sind sie in Einheit mit ihrem Anderen, also nicht als für sich bestehende, nicht als absolute, sondern schlechthin als relative.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"13.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","text":"Das Aufzeigen der empirischen Nichtigkeit des leeren Raums u.s.f. aber ist es nicht, um das es zu thun ist. Das Bewußtseyn kann sich abstrahirend allerdings auch mit jenem Unbestimmten erfüllen, und die festgehaltenen Abstraktionen sind die Gedanken von reinem Raum, Zeit, reinen Bewußtseyn, reinem Seyn. Der Gedanke des reinen Raums u.s.f. d. i. der reine Raum u.s.f. an ihm selbst soll als nichtig aufgezeigt werden, d. i. daß er als solcher schon sein Gegentheil, daß an ihm selbst schon sein Gegentheil in ihn eingedrungen, er schon für sich das Herausgegangenseyn aus sich selbst, Bestimmtheit, sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"13.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","text":"Dieß ergiebt sich aber unmittelbar an ihnen. Sie sind, was Jacobi reichlich beschreibt, Resultate der Abstraktion, sind ausdrücklich als Unbestimmte bestimmt, was—um zu seiner einfachsten Form zurückzugehen, das Seyn ist. Eben diese Unbestimmtheit ist aber das, was die Bestimmtheit desselben ausmacht; denn die Unbestimmtheit ist der Bestimmtheit entgegengesetzt; sie ist somit als Entgegengesetztes selbst das Bestimmte, oder Negative, und zwar das reine, ganz abstrakt Negative. Diese Unbestimmtheit oder abstrakte Negation, welche so das Seyn an ihm selbst hat, ist es, was die äußere wie die innere Reflexion ausspricht, indem sie es dem Nichts gleich setzt, es für ein leeres Gedankending, für Nichts erklärt.—Oder kann man sich ausdrücken, weil das Seyn das Bestimmungslose ist, ist es nicht die (affirmative) Bestimmtheit, die es ist, nicht Seyn, sondern Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"13.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","text":"In der reinen Reflexion des Anfangs, wie er in dieser Logik mit dem Seyn als solchem gemacht wird, ist der Übergang noch verborgen; weil das Seyn nur als unmittelbar gesetzt ist, bricht das Nichts an ihm nur unmittelbar hervor. Aber alle folgenden Bestimmungen, wie gleich das Daseyn, sind konkreter; es ist an diesem das schon gesetzt, was den Widerspruch jener Abstraktionen und daher ihr Übergehen enthält und hervorbringt. Beim Seyn als jenem Einfachen, Unmittelbaren wird die Erinnerung, daß es Resultat der vollkommenen Abstraktion, also schon von daher abstrakte Negativität, Nichts, ist, hinter der Wissenschaft zurückgelassen, welchem innerhalb ihrer selbst, ausdrücklich vom Wesen aus, jene einseitige Unmittelbarkeit als eine Vermittelte darstellen wird, wo das Seyn als Existenz und das Vermittelnde dieses Seyns, der Grund, gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"13.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0024","text":"Mit jener Erinnerung läßt sich der Übergang von Seyn in Nichts als etwas selbst leichtes und triviales so vorstellen oder auch, wie man es nennt, erklären und begreiflich machen, daß Freilich das Seyn, welches zum Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht worden, Nichts sey, denn man könne von Allem abstrahiren, und wenn von Allem abstrahirt worden, so bleibe Nichts übrig. Aber, kann man fortfahren, somit sey der Anfang nicht ein Affirmatives, nicht Seyn, sondern eben Nichts, und Nichts sey dann auch das Ende, wenigstens sosehr als das unmittelbare Seyn und selbst noch vielmehr. Das Kürzeste ist solches Raisonniren gewähren zu lassen und zuzusehen, wie denn die Resultate beschaffen sind, auf welche es pocht.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"13.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0025","text":"Daß hiernach das Nichts das Resultat jenes Raisonnements wäre, und nun der Anfang mit Nichts (wie in chinesischer Philosophie) gemacht werden sollte, so wäre darum nicht die Hand umzukehren, denn ehe man sie umkehrte, hätte sich ebenso sehr dieß Nichts in Seyn verkehrt, (s. oben: B. Nichts). Aber ferner wenn jene Abstraktion von Allem, welches Alles denn doch Seyendes ist, vorausgesetzt wäre, so ist sie genauer zu nehmen; das Resultat der Abstraktion von allem Seyenden ist zunächst abstraktes Seyn, Seyn überhaupt; wie im kosmologischen Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes aus dem zufälligen Seyn der Welt, über welches sich darin erhoben wird, noch das Seyn mit hinaufgebracht, das Seyn zum unendlichen Seyn bestimmt wird. Es kann aber allerdings auch von diesem reinen Seyn abstrahirt, das Seyn noch zu dem Allem, wovon bereits abstrahirt worden, geschlagen werden; dann bleibt Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"13.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0026","text":"Man kann nun, wenn man das Denken des Nichts, d.i. sein Umschlagen in Seyn vergessen will oder nichts davon wüßte, im Style jenes Könnens fortfahren; es kann nämlich (Gottlob!) auch vom Nichts abstrahirt werden (wie denn auch die Schöpfung der Welt eine Abstraktion vom Nichts ist) und dann bleibt nicht Nichts, denn eben von diesem wird abstrahirt, sondern man ist so wieder im Seyn angekommen.—dieß Können giebt ein äußerliches Spiel des Abstrahirens, wobei das Abstrahiren selbst nur das einseitige Thun des Negativen ist. Zunächst liegt in diesem Können selbst, daß ihm das Seyn so gleichgültig ist als das Nichts, und daß so sehr jedes von Beiden verschwindet, ebenso sehr jedes auch entsteht; aber ebenso gleichgültig ist es, ob vom Thun des Nichts, oder dem Nichts ausgegangen wird; das Thun des Nichts, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"13.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0027","text":"das bloße Abstrahiren ist nicht mehr noch weniger etwas Wahrhaftes als das bloße Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"13.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0028","text":"Die Dialektik, nach welcher Plato das Eine im Parmenides behandelt, ist gleichfalls mehr für eine Dialektik der äußern Reflexion zu achten. Das Seyn und das Eine sind beides Eleatische Formen, die Dasselbe sind. Aber sie sind auch zu unterscheiden, so nimmt sie Plato in jenem Dialoge. Nachdem er von dem Einen die mancherlei Bestimmungen von Ganzen und Theilen, in sich selbst, in einem anderen seyn u.s.f. von Figur, Zeit u.s.f. entfernt, so ist das Resultat, daß dem Einen das Seyn nicht zukomme, denn anders komme einem Etwas das Seyn nicht zu, als nach einer jener Weisen (p. 141 e. Vol. III. ed. Steph.).","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"13.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0029","text":"Hierauf behandelt Plato den Satz: das Eine ist; und es ist bei ihm nachzusehen, wie von diesem Satze aus der Übergang zu dem Nichtseyn des Einen bewerkstelligt wird; es geschieht durch die Vergleichung der beiden Bestimmungen des vorausgesetzten Satzes: das Eine ist; er enthält das Eine und das Seyn; und das Eine ist enthält mehr, als wenn man nur sagt: das Eine. Darin daß sie verschieden sind, wird das Moment der Negation, das der Satz enthält, aufgezeigt. Es erhellt, daß dieser Weg eine Voraussetzung hat, und eine äußere Reflexion ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"13.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","text":"Wie hier das Eine mit dem Seyn in Verbindung gesetzt ist, wird das Seyn, welches abstrakt für sich festgehalten werden soll am einfachsten, ohne sich in das Denken einzulassen, in einer Verbindung aufgezeigt, die das Gegentheil dessen enthält, was behauptet werden soll. Das Seyn, wie es unmittelbar ist, genommen gehört einem Subjekte an, ist ein ausgesprochenes, hat ein empirisches Daseyn überhaupt, und steht damit im Boden der Schranke und des Negativen. In welchen Ausdrücken oder Wendungen der Verstand sich fasse, wenn er sich gegen die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts sträubt, und sich auf das, was unmittelbar vorhanden sey, beruft, wird er eben in dieser Erfahrung selbst nichts als bestimmtes Seyn, Seyn mit einer Schranke oder Negation,—jene Einheit finden, die er verwirft.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"13.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031","text":"Die Behauptung des unmittelbaren Seyns reducirt sich so auf eine empirische Existenz, deren Aufzeigen sie nicht verwerfen kann, weil es die Unmittelbarkeit außerhalb des Denkens ist, an die sie sich halten will.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"13.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","text":"Dasselbe ist der Fall mit dem Nichts, nur auf entgegengesetzte Weise, und diese Reflexion ist bekannt und oft genug über dasselbe gemacht worden. Das Nichts zeigt sich in seiner Unmittelbarkeit genommen als seyend; denn seiner Natur nach ist es dasselbe als das Seyn. Das Nichts wird gedacht, vorgestellt, es wird von ihm gesprochen; es ist also; das Nichts hat an dem Denken, Vorstellen, Sprechen, u.s.f. sein Seyn. Dieß Seyn ist aber ferner, auch von ihm unterschieden; es wird daher gesagt, daß das Nichts zwar im Denken, Vorstellen ist, aber daß darum nicht es ist, nicht ihm als solchem das Seyn zukomme, daß nur Denken oder Vorstellen dieses Seyn ist. Bei diesem Unterscheiden ist eben so sehr nicht zu läugnen, daß das Nichts in Beziehung auf ein Seyn steht; aber in der Beziehung, ob sie gleich auch den Unterschied enthält, ist eine Einheit mit dem Seyn vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"13.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0033","text":"Auf weiche Weise das Nichts ausgesprochen oder aufgezeigt werde, zeigt es sich in Verbindung oder wenn man will Berührung mit einem Seyn, ungetrennt von einem Seyn, eben in einem Daseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"13.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0034","text":"Indem aber so das Nichts in einem Daseyn aufgezeigt wird, pflegt noch dieser Unterschied desselben vom Seyn vorzuschweben, daß das Daseyn des Nichts durchaus nichts ihm selbst zukommendes sey, daß es nicht das Seyn für sich selbst an ihm habe, es nicht das Seyn als solches sey; das Nichts sey nur Abwesenheit des Seyns, die Finsterniß so nur Abwesenheit des Lichts, die Kälte nur Abwesenheit der Wärme u.s.f. Finsterniß habe nur Bedeutung in Beziehung auf das Auge, in äußerer Vergleichung mit dem Positiven, dem Lichte, ebenso Kälte sey nur Etwas in unserer Empfindung, Licht, Wärme, wie Seyn, hingegen seyen für sich das Objektive, Reale, Wirksame, von schlechthin anderer Qualität und Würde, als jene Negativen, als Nichts.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"13.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","text":"Man kann es häufig als eine sehr wichtige Reflexion und bedeutende Erkenntniß aufgeführt finden, daß Finsterniß nur Abwesenheit des Lichts, Kälte nur Abwesenheit der Wärme sey. Über diese scharfsinnige Reflexion kann in diesem Felde von empirischen Gegenständen empirisch bemerkt werden, daß die Finsterniß sich im Lichte allerdings wirksam zeigt, indem sie dasselbe zur Farbe bestimmt und ihm selbst dadurch erst Sichtbarkeit ertheilt, indem wie früher gesagt, im reinen Lichte ebenso wenig gesehen wird, als in der reinen Finsterniß. Die Sichtbarkeit ist aber Wirksamkeit im Auge, an der jenes Negative ebenso viel Antheil hat, als das für das Reale, Positive geltende Licht; ebenso giebt sich die Kälte dem Wasser, unserer Empfindung u.s. f. genugsam zu erkennen, und wenn wir ihr sogenannte objektive Realität absprechen, so ist damit durchaus nichts gegen sie gewonnen.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"13.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","text":"Aber ferner wäre zu rügen, daß hier gleichfalls, wie oben, von einem Negativen von bestimmtem Inhalte gesprochen wird, nicht beim Nichts selbst stehen geblieben wird, dem das Seyn an leerer Abstraktion nicht nachsteht, noch etwas voraus hat.—Allein Kälte, Finsterniß und dergleichen bestimmte Negationen sind sogleich für sich zu nehmen, und es ist zu sehen, was damit in Rücksicht ihrer allgemeinen Bestimmung, nach der sie hierher gebracht werden, gesetzt ist. Sie sollen nicht das Nichts überhaupt, sondern das Nichts vom Licht, Wärme u.s.f. von etwas Bestimmten, einem Inhalte seyn; so sind sie bestimmte, inhaltige Nichts, wenn man so sagen kann. Aber eine Bestimmtheit ist, wie noch weiter hin vorkommt, selbst eine Negation; so sind sie negative Nichts; aber ein negatives Nichts ist etwas Affirmatives.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"13.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0037","text":"Das Umschlagen des Nichts durch seine Bestimmtheit (die vorhin als ein Daseyn im Subjekte, oder in sonst was es sey, erschien) in ein Affirmatives, erscheint dem Bewußtseyn, das in der Verstandes-Abstraktion feststeht, als das paradoxeste, so einfach die Einsicht ist, oder auch wegen ihrer Einfachheit selbst erscheint die Einsicht, daß die Negation der Negation Positives ist, als etwas Triviales, auf welches der stolze Verstand daher nicht zu achten brauche, obgleich die Sache ihre Richtigkeit habe,—und sie hat nicht nur diese Richtigkeit, sondern um der Allgemeinheit solcher Bestimmungen willen ihre unendliche Ausdehnung und allgemeine Anwendung, so daß wohl darauf zu achten wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"13.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","text":"Noch kann über die Bestimmung des Übergangs von Seyn und Nichts in einander bemerkt werden, daß derselbe eben so ohne weitere Reflexionsbestimmung aufzufassen ist. Er ist unmittelbar und ganz abstrakt, um der Abstraktion der übergehenden Momente willen, d. i. indem an diesen Momenten noch nicht die Bestimmtheit des anderen gesetzt ist, vermittelst dessen sie übergingen; das Nichts ist am Seyn noch nicht gesetzt, ob zwar Seyn wesentlich Nichts ist, und umgekehrt. Es ist daher unzulässig, weiters bestimmte Vermittelungen hier anzuwenden, und Seyn und Nichts in irgend einem Verhältnisse zu fassen,—jenes Übergehen ist noch kein Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"13.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","text":"Es ist also unstatthaft zu sagen: Das Nichts ist der Grund vom Seyn; oder Seyn ist der Grund von Nichts;—das Nichts Ursache vom Seyn u.s.f.; oder es kann nur unter der Bedingung in das Nichts übergegangen werden, daß etwas ist, oder in das Seyn nur unter der Bedingung des Nichtseyns. Die Art der Beziehung kann nicht weiter bestimmt seyn, ohne daß zugleich die bezogenen Seiten weiter bestimmt würden. Der Zusammenhang von Grund und Folge u.s.f. hat nicht mehr das bloße Seyn und Nichts zu den Seiten, die er verbindet, sondern ausdrücklich Seyn, das Grund ist, und etwas, das zwar nur ein gesetztes, nicht Selbstständiges sey, das aber nicht das abstrakte Nichts ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"13.39"}],"sha256":"0cbf858ae5d7d3a0cfe709e29266132fc089a789e9bb3d866385b4beb5c8a8b9","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101917921822Z_315c825b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 3.","source_sha256":"0cbf858ae5d7d3a0cfe709e29266132fc089a789e9bb3d866385b4beb5c8a8b9","sha256":"f356c44b7b121792cdfb58a70cb5d6ec364f7f23f8f77993c92a1e25e65da8ec","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:17.921850+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","text":"The unity whose moments, Being and Nothing, are inseparable, is at the same time distinct from them themselves, thus a third in relation to them, which in its most proper form is Becoming. Passing-over is the same as Becoming, only that in the former the two, from one of which passage is made to the other, are represented more as resting apart from one another, and the passing-over as occurring between them. Wherever and however Being or Nothing is spoken of, this third must be present; for they do not subsist for themselves, but are only in Becoming, in this third. But this third has manifold empirical shapes, which abstraction sets aside or neglects in order to hold fast those its products, Being and Nothing, each for itself, and to show them protected against passing-over.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"13.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","text":"Against such simple conduct of abstraction, it is equally simple merely to recall empirical existence, in which that abstraction itself is only something, has a determinate being. Or else there are forms of reflection through which the separation of the inseparable is to be fixed. In such a determination, the opposite of itself is present in and for itself; and, without going back to the nature of the matter and appealing to it, that determination of reflection is to be confounded in itself by taking it as it gives itself and showing its other in itself. It would be a futile effort to try, as it were, to catch all the turns and conceits of reflection and its ratiocination, in order to deprive it of, and render impossible, the evasions and leaps by which it conceals its contradiction with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"13.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","text":"For this reason I also refrain from taking account of the many so-called objections and refutations that have been raised against the proposition that neither Being nor Nothing is anything true, but that only Becoming is their truth; the formation of thought required to perceive the nullity of those refutations, or rather to repel such conceits by itself, is brought about only through critical cognition of the forms of understanding; but those who are most prolific in objections of this kind immediately fall upon the first propositions with their reflections, without having helped themselves, or having been helped, through further study of Logic to consciousness of the nature of these crude reflections.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"13.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004","text":"Some of the phenomena which arise when Being and Nothing are isolated from one another and one is set outside the sphere of the other, so that passing-over is thereby negated, are now to be considered.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"13.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","text":"Parmenides held fast to Being and was most consistent in saying at the same time of Nothing that it is not at all; only Being is. Being wholly by itself is the indeterminate, and thus has no relation to an other; it therefore appears that no further progress can be made from this beginning, namely from itself, and that a progression could occur only by some alien thing being attached to it from without. The progression that Being is the same as Nothing thus appears as a second, absolute beginning,—a passing-over which is for itself and would accrue externally to Being. Being would in general not be the absolute beginning if it had a determinacy; it would then depend upon an other and would not be immediate, not the beginning.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"13.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","text":"But if it is indeterminate, and thereby a true beginning, it likewise has nothing by which it passes over into an other; it is at the same time the end. As little can anything break forth from it as anything can break into it; with Parmenides as with Spinoza, there is to be no progression from Being or absolute substance to the negative, the finite. If nevertheless there is a progression, which, as remarked, can occur from relational—and thereby progressionless—Being only in an external manner, then this progression is a second, new beginning. Thus Fichte's most absolute, unconditional fundamental proposition is: the positing A = A; the second is counter-positing; this is to be partly conditioned, partly unconditioned (thus a contradiction within itself).","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"13.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0007","text":"This is a proceeding of external reflection, which just as much negates again that with which it begins as with an Absolute—the counter-positing is the negation of the first identity—as it immediately and expressly at the same time makes its second unconditioned into a conditioned. But if there were any justification at all for proceeding, i.e. for sublating the first beginning, it would have to lie in this first itself that an other could relate to it; it would therefore have to be something determinate. But Being, or likewise absolute substance, does not give itself out as such; on the contrary. It is the immediate, still utterly indeterminate.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"13.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008","text":"The most eloquent, perhaps forgotten, depictions of the impossibility of getting from an abstract to something further and to a union of both are given by Jacobi, in the interest of his polemic against the Kantian synthesis of self-consciousness a priori, in his essay On the Enterprise of Criticism to Bring Reason to Understanding (Jacobi, Works, vol. III). He poses the task (p. 113) thus: that the emergence or production of a synthesis is to be shown in a Pure, whether of consciousness, space, or time. “Space is one, time is one, consciousness is one;—now say how one of these three ones purely multiplies itself within itself;—each is only one and no other;—a sameness, a der-die-das self-sameness!”","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"13.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0009","text":"without der-ness, die-ness, das-ness; for these slumber, together with the der, die, das, still in the infinite = 0 of the indeterminate, from which every and any determinate is first supposed to emerge! What brings finitude into those three infinities; what fructifies space and time a priori with number and measure, and transforms them into a pure manifold; what sets pure spontaneity (I) into oscillation? How does its pure vowel come to the consonant, or rather, how does its soundless uninterrupted blowing, interrupting itself, set itself off in order to gain at least a kind of vowel-sound, an accent?”—One sees that Jacobi has recognized very definitely the absurdity of abstraction, whether it be so-called absolute, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"13.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","text":"merely abstract space, or time of the same sort, or similarly pure consciousness, I; he persists in it for the purpose of asserting the impossibility of a progression to an other, the condition of a synthesis, and to synthesis itself. The synthesis which constitutes the interest must not be taken as a connection of determinations already externally present,—partly, what is at issue is the production of a second for a first, of a determinate for the indeterminate initial; but partly, too, it is the immanent synthesis, synthesis a priori,—the unity of the differentiated, being in and for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"13.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","text":"Becoming is this immanent synthesis of Being and Nothing; but because the sense nearest to synthesis is that of an external bringing-together of things externally present over against one another, the name synthesis, synthetic unity, has rightly fallen out of use.—Jacobi asks, how does the pure vowel of the I come to the consonant, what brings determinacy into indeterminacy—the what? would be easily answered, and Kant has answered this question in his way; but the question concerning the how? means: in what manner and way, according to what relation, and the like, and thus demands the indication of a particular category; but there can be no question here of manner and way, categories of understanding. The question concerning the how?","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"13.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","text":"itself belongs to the bad manners of reflection, which asks after intelligibility while presupposing its fixed categories and thereby knows itself armed in advance against the answer to what it asks. Nor does it have in Jacobi the higher sense of a question concerning the necessity of synthesis; for, as has been said, he remains fixedly persisting in abstractions, in support of the assertion of the impossibility of synthesis. In particular, he vividly describes (p. 147) the procedure for arriving at the abstraction of space. “For a time I must seek purely to forget that I ever saw, heard, touched, and felt anything, expressly not excepting myself. Purely, purely, purely, I must forget all movement, and make precisely this forgetting, because it is the most difficult thing, my most urgent concern.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"13.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0013","text":"Everything whatever, just as I have thought it away, I must also allow to have been wholly and completely removed, and retain absolutely nothing save the forcibly remaining intuition alone of infinite unchangeable space. I must therefore not think myself back into it as something distinguished from it and yet connected with it; I must not let myself be merely surrounded and pervaded by it; rather, I must wholly pass over into it, become one with it, transform myself into it; I must leave nothing of myself remaining except this my intuition itself, in order to regard it as a truly self-subsistent, independent, sole and only representation.”","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"13.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0014","text":"With this wholly abstract purity of continuity, i.e. indeterminacy and emptiness of representation, it is indifferent whether this abstraction be called space, or pure intuition, pure thought;—it is all the same thing as what the Indian, when he, outwardly motionless and likewise motionless in sensation, representation, imagination, desire, etc., for years gazes only at the tip of his nose, speaks only Om, Om, Om inwardly to himself, or even Nothing,—calls Brahma. This dull, empty consciousness, apprehended as consciousness,—is Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"13.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0015","text":"In this emptiness, Jacobi now goes on to say, the opposite happens to him of what, according to the Kantian assurance, ought to happen to him; he finds himself not as a many and manifold, but rather as one without all plurality and manifoldness; indeed, “I am impossibility itself, am the annihilation of all manifold and many,—from my pure, absolutely simple, unchangeable essence I cannot restore or ghost back into myself even the least thing;—thus, in this purity, all being-outside-and-beside-one-another, all manifoldness and plurality based upon it, reveals itself as something purely impossible.”","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"13.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0016","text":"This impossibility means nothing other than tautology: I hold fast to abstract unity and exclude all plurality and manifoldness; I remain in the undifferentiated and indeterminate and look away from everything differentiated and determinate. Jacobi attenuates the Kantian synthesis a priori of self-consciousness, that is, the activity of this unity to dirempt itself and maintain itself in this diremption, into the same abstraction. That “synthesis in itself,” that “original judging,” he makes one-sidedly into “the copula in itself;—an Is, Is, Is, without beginning and end and without What, Who, and Which; this repetition of repetition proceeding into infinity is the sole activity, function, and production of the purest synthesis; it itself is mere, pure, absolute repetition itself.” Or indeed, since there is no interruption, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"13.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0017","text":"no negation or differentiating in it, it is not a repetition, but only undifferentiated simple Being.—But is this still synthesis, when Jacobi precisely leaves out that whereby unity is synthetic unity?","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"13.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","text":"First of all, when Jacobi thus establishes himself in absolute, i.e. abstract, space, time, and also consciousness, it must be said that in this way he places and holds himself fast in something empirically false; there is, i.e. there is empirically present, no space and time which would be an unlimited spatial and temporal, which would not be filled in their continuity with manifold limited determinate being and change, so that these limits and changes belong inseparately and inseparably to spatiality and temporality; likewise consciousness is filled with determinate sensation, representation, desire, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"13.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019","text":"it exists inseparably from some particular content.—Empirical passing-over is in any case self-evident; consciousness can indeed make empty space, empty time, and empty consciousness itself, or pure Being, into its object and content; but it does not remain with this, but not only proceeds, it presses out of such emptiness toward a better, i.e. in some way more concrete content; and however bad a content may otherwise be, it is in this respect better and truer; indeed, such a content is a synthetic one in general; synthetic in a more general sense. Thus Parmenides has to deal with semblance and opinion, the opposite of Being and truth; thus Spinoza with attributes, modes, extension, motion, understanding, will, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"13.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0020","text":"Synthesis contains and displays the untruth of those abstractions; in it they are in unity with their other, thus not as subsisting for themselves, not as absolute, but simply as relative.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"13.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","text":"But the showing of the empirical nullity of empty space, etc., is not what is at issue. Consciousness can indeed, by abstracting, also fill itself with that indeterminate, and the abstractions held fast are the thoughts of pure space, time, pure consciousness, pure Being. The thought of pure space, etc., i.e. pure space, etc. in itself, is to be shown to be null, i.e. that as such it is already its opposite, that its opposite has already entered into it in itself, that it is already for itself the having-gone-forth-from-itself, determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"13.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","text":"But this follows immediately from them. They are, as Jacobi describes amply enough, results of abstraction; they are expressly determined as indeterminate—which, to return to its simplest form, Being is. Yet this very indeterminacy is what constitutes its determinacy; for indeterminacy is opposed to determinacy; it is thus, as an opposed [term], itself the determinate, or negative, namely the pure, wholly abstract negative. This indeterminacy or abstract negation, which Being thus has in itself, is what external as well as internal reflection expresses when it equates it with Nothing, declares it to be an empty thing of thought, to be Nothing.—Or one may express oneself thus: because Being is the indeterminate, it is not the (affirmative) determinacy that it is, not Being, but Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"13.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","text":"In the pure reflection upon the beginning, as it is made in this Logic with Being as such, the transition is still concealed; because Being is posited only as immediate, Nothing breaks forth in it only immediately. But all subsequent determinations, such as at once determinate being, are more concrete; in the latter there is already posited that which contains and brings forth the contradiction of those abstractions and hence their passing over. In the case of Being as that simple, immediate [term], the recollection that it is the result of complete abstraction, hence already for that reason abstract negativity, Nothing, is left behind science, which within itself, expressly from essence onward, will present that one-sided immediacy as a mediated one, where Being is posited as existence and the mediating factor of this Being, the ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"13.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0024","text":"With that recollection, the transition from Being into Nothing can readily be represented as something easy and trivial, or, as it is called, explained and made comprehensible, so that certainly the Being which has been made the beginning of science is Nothing, for one can abstract from everything, and when abstraction has been made from everything, Nothing remains. But, one may continue, thus the beginning is not an affirmative, not Being, but precisely Nothing, and Nothing is then also the end, at least just as much as immediate Being, and indeed still more so. The shortest course is to allow such reasoning free rein and to see what the results are like on which it prides itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"13.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0025","text":"If, accordingly, Nothing were the result of that reasoning, and if the beginning should now be made with Nothing (as in Chinese philosophy), one would not therefore have to turn one's hand around, for before one turned it around, this Nothing would just as much have turned itself into Being (see above: B. Nothing). But further, if that abstraction from everything, which everything is nevertheless what is, were presupposed, it must be taken more precisely; the result of abstraction from all that is is initially abstract Being, Being in general; just as in the cosmological proof of the existence of God, from the contingent Being of the world, above which one rises in it, Being too is carried upward, and Being is determined as infinite Being. But one may indeed also abstract from this pure Being, add Being to all that from which abstraction has already been made; then Nothing remains.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"13.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0026","text":"Now, if one wishes to forget the thinking of Nothing, i.e. its overturning into Being, or knew nothing of it, one can continue in the style of that ability; namely, one can (thank God!) also abstract from Nothing (just as the creation of the world is an abstraction from Nothing), and then not Nothing remains, for it is precisely from this that abstraction is made, but one has thus arrived again at Being.—This ability affords an external play of abstracting, in which abstracting itself is only the one-sided activity of the negative. Initially, this ability itself entails that Being is as indifferent to it as Nothing, and that just as much as each of the two disappears, each also arises; but it is equally indifferent whether one proceeds from the activity of Nothing, or from Nothing; the activity of Nothing, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"13.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0027","text":"mere abstracting, is no more and no less something true than mere Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"13.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0028","text":"The dialectic by which Plato treats the One in the Parmenides is likewise to be regarded more as a dialectic of external reflection. Being and the One are both Eleatic forms, which are the same. But they are also to be distinguished, and Plato takes them as such in that dialogue. After he removes from the One the manifold determinations of wholes and parts, being in itself, in another, etc., of figure, time, etc., the result is that Being does not pertain to the One, for Being does not otherwise pertain to a something than in one of those modes (p. 141 e. Vol. III. ed. Steph.).","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"13.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0029","text":"Thereupon Plato treats the proposition: the One is; and it should be seen in him how, beginning from this proposition, the transition to the non-being of the One is effected; it occurs through the comparison of the two determinations of the presupposed proposition: the One is; it contains the One and Being; and the One is contains more than if one says only: the One. In their being different, the moment of negation which the proposition contains is exhibited. It is evident that this way has a presupposition and is an external reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"13.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","text":"Just as here the One is placed in connection with Being, Being, which is to be held fast abstractly for itself, is displayed most simply, without entering into thinking, in a connection that contains the opposite of what is to be asserted. Being, taken as it is immediate, belongs to a subject, is something uttered, has an empirical determinate being in general, and thereby stands upon the ground of limitation and the negative. In whatever expressions or turns of phrase the understanding may ensconce itself when it resists the unity of Being and Nothing and appeals to what is immediately present, it will find in this experience itself nothing but determinate Being, Being with a limitation or negation,—that unity which it rejects.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"13.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031","text":"The assertion of immediate Being thus reduces itself to an empirical existence, the exhibiting of which it cannot reject, because it is the immediacy outside thinking to which it wishes to adhere.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"13.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","text":"The same is the case with Nothing, only in the opposite manner, and this reflection is well known and has often enough been made concerning it. Nothing, taken in its immediacy, shows itself as being; for by its nature it is the same as Being. Nothing is thought, represented; it is spoken of; thus it is; Nothing has its Being in thinking, representing, speaking, etc. But this Being is further distinguished from it as well; it is therefore said that Nothing is indeed in thinking, representing, but that it is not thereby, that Being does not pertain to it as such, that only thinking or representing is this Being. In this distinguishing, it is equally impossible to deny that Nothing stands in relation to a Being; but in the relation, although it also contains the difference, a unity with Being is present.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"13.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0033","text":"In whatever manner Nothing may be uttered or exhibited, it shows itself in connection, or, if one will, contact with a Being, inseparable from a Being, precisely in a determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"13.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0034","text":"But when Nothing is thus exhibited in a determinate being, there is usually still the notion hovering before one of its difference from Being, namely that the determinate being of Nothing is absolutely nothing that pertains to it itself, that it does not have Being for itself in it, that it is not Being as such; Nothing is only absence of Being, darkness thus only absence of light, cold only absence of warmth, etc. Darkness has significance only in relation to the eye, in external comparison with the positive, light; likewise cold is only something in our sensation, whereas light, warmth, like Being, are in themselves the objective, real, effective, of an altogether different quality and dignity from those negatives, from Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"13.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","text":"One can frequently find it adduced as a very important reflection and significant cognition that darkness is only absence of light, cold only absence of warmth. Against this ingenious reflection, it may be empirically remarked in this field of empirical objects that darkness does indeed show itself effective in light, in that it determines the latter to colour and thereby first imparts visibility to it itself, since, as was said earlier, just as little is seen in pure light as in pure darkness. But visibility is effectiveness in the eye, in which that negative has as much share as the light regarded as the real, positive [one]; likewise cold makes itself sufficiently known to water, to our sensation, etc., and if we deny it so-called objective reality, absolutely nothing has thereby been gained against it.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"13.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","text":"But further, it would be necessary to censure the fact that here likewise, as above, a negative of determinate content is spoken of, and one has not remained with Nothing itself, to which Being does not yield in empty abstraction, nor has anything over it.—Yet cold, darkness, and such determinate negations are at once to be taken for themselves, and it is to be seen what is thereby posited with regard to their universal determination, according to which they are brought here. They are not supposed to be Nothing in general, but the Nothing of light, warmth, etc., of something determinate, of a content; thus they are determinate, contentful Nothings, if one may so speak. But a determinacy is, as will occur further on, itself a negation; thus they are negative Nothings; but a negative Nothing is something affirmative.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"13.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0037","text":"The overturning of Nothing, through its determinacy (which previously appeared as a determinate being in the subject, or in whatever else it may be), into an affirmative, appears to consciousness that stands fast in the abstraction of the understanding as the most paradoxical thing; however simple the insight is—or indeed, on account of its very simplicity, the insight that the negation of negation is positive appears as something trivial, to which proud understanding therefore need pay no attention, although the matter is correct—and it has not merely this correctness, but, on account of the universality of such determinations, infinite extension and universal application, so that it would certainly deserve attention.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"13.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","text":"One may further remark concerning the determination of the transition of Being and Nothing into one another that it is likewise to be apprehended without further determination of reflection. It is immediate and wholly abstract, on account of the abstraction of the transitioning moments, i.e. because in these moments the determinacy of the other is not yet posited, by means of which they would transition; Nothing is not yet posited in Being, although Being is essentially Nothing, and conversely. It is therefore inadmissible to apply further determinate mediations here and to take Being and Nothing in any relation,—that transition is not yet a relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"13.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","text":"It is thus impermissible to say: Nothing is the ground of Being; or Being is the ground of Nothing;—Nothing the cause of Being, etc.; or that one can pass over into Nothing only on the condition that something is, or into Being only on the condition of non-being. The mode of relation cannot be further determined without the related sides at the same time being further determined. The connection of ground and consequence, etc., no longer has mere Being and Nothing as the sides it connects, but expressly Being that is ground, and something that is indeed only a posited, not self-subsistent [thing], but is not abstract Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"13.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039"]}],"source_digest":"38470fecdad826500650c645d4e49f101a0511a2561a18444dad4ad43ca7b0eb","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 3."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 3.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4","title":"Remark 4.","order":14,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ANM4","text":"Es geht aus dem Bisherigen hervor, welche Bewandniß es mit der Dialektik gegen den Anfang der Welt, auch deren Untergang hat, wodurch die Ewigkeit der Materie erwiesen werden sollte, d. i. mit der Dialektik gegen das Werden, Entstehen oder Vergehen überhaupt. —Die Kantische Antinomie über die Endlichkeit oder Unendlichkeit der Welt in Raum und Zeit wird unten bei dem Begriffe der quantitativen Unendlichkeit näher betrachtet werden.—Jene einfache gewöhnliche Dialektik beruht auf dem Festhalten des Gegensatzes von Seyn und Nichts. Es wird auf folgende Art bewiesen, daß kein Anfang der Welt oder von Etwas möglich sey: Es kann nichts anfangen, weder insofern etwas ist, noch insofern es nicht ist; denn insofern es ist, fängt es nicht erst an; insofern es aber nicht ist, fängt es auch nicht an. -Wenn die Welt oder Etwas angefangen haben sollte, so hätte sie im Nichts angefangen, aber im Nichts oder das Nichts ist nicht Anfang; denn Anfang schließt ein Seyn in sich, aber das Nichts enthält kein Seyn. Nichts ist nur Nichts. In einem Grunde, Ursache u.s.w. wenn das Nichts so bestimmt wird, ist eine Affirmation, Seyn enthalten. —Aus demselben Grunde kann auch Etwas nicht aufhören. Denn so müßte das Seyn das Nichts enthalten, Seyn aber ist nur Seyn, nicht das Gegentheil seiner selbst.\n\nEs erhellt, daß hierin gegen das Werden, oder Anfangen und Aufhören, diese Einheit des Seyns und Nichts, nichts vorgebracht wird, als sie assertorisch zu läugnen, und dem Seyn und Nichts, jedem getrennt von dem andern, Wahrheit zuzuschreiben.—Diese Dialektik ist jedoch wenigstens konsequenter als das reflektirende Vorstellen. Ihm gilt es für vollkommene Wahrheit, daß Seyn und Nichts nur getrennt seyen; auf der anderen Seite aber läßt es ein Anfangen und Aufhören als eben so wahrhafte Bestimmungen gelten; in diesen aber nimmt es die Ungetrenntheit des Seyns und Nichts faktisch an.\n\nBei der Voraussetzung der absoluten Geschiedenheit des Seyns vom Nichts, ist—was man so oft hört—der Anfang oder das Werden allerdings etwas Unbegreifliches; denn man macht eine Voraussetzung, welche den Anfang oder das Werden aufhebt, das man doch wieder zugibt, und dieser Widerspruch, den man selbst setzt und dessen Auflösung unmöglich macht, heißt das Unbegreifliche.\n\nDas Angeführte ist auch dieselbe Dialektik, die der Verstand gegen den Begriff braucht, den die höhere Analysis von den unendlich-kleinen Größen giebt. Von diesem Begriffe wird weiter unten ausführlicher gehandelt.—Diese Größen sind als solche, bestimmt worden, die in ihrem Verschwinden sind, nicht vor ihrem Verschwinden, denn als dann sind sie endliche Größen;—nicht nach ihrem Verschwinden, denn alsdann sind sie nichts. Gegen diesen reinen Begriff ist eingewendet und immer wiederholt worden, daß solche Größen entweder Etwas seyen, oder Nichts; daß es keinen Mittelzustand (Zustand ist hier ein unpassender, barbarischer Ausdruck) zwischen Seyn und Nichtseyn gebe.—Es ist hierbei gleichfalls die absolute Trennung des Seyns und Nichts angenommen. Dagegen ist aber gezeigt worden, daß Seyn und Nichts in der That dasselbe sind, oder um in jener Sprache zu sprechen, daß es gar nichts giebt, das nicht ein Mittelzustand zwischen Seyn und Nichts ist. Die Mathematik hat ihre glänzendsten Erfolge der Annahme jener Bestimmung, welcher der Verstand widerspricht, zu danken.\n\nDas angeführte Raisonnement, das die falsche Voraussetzung der absoluten Getrenntheit des Seyns und Nichtseyns macht, und bei derselben stehen bleibt, ist nicht Dialektik, sondern Sophisterei zu nennen. Denn Sophisterei ist ein Raisonnement aus einer grundlosen Voraussetzung, die man ohne Kritik und unbesonnen gelten läßt; Dialektik aber nennen wir die höhere vernünftige Bewegung, in welche solche schlechthin getrennt scheinende, durch sich selbst, durch das, was sie sind, in einander übergehen, die Voraussetzung sich aufhebt. Es ist die dialektische immanente Natur des Seyns und Nichts selbst, daß sie ihre Einheit, das Werden, als ihre Wahrheit zeigen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","text":"Es geht aus dem Bisherigen hervor, welche Bewandniß es mit der Dialektik gegen den Anfang der Welt, auch deren Untergang hat, wodurch die Ewigkeit der Materie erwiesen werden sollte, d. i. mit der Dialektik gegen das Werden, Entstehen oder Vergehen überhaupt. —Die Kantische Antinomie über die Endlichkeit oder Unendlichkeit der Welt in Raum und Zeit wird unten bei dem Begriffe der quantitativen Unendlichkeit näher betrachtet werden.—Jene einfache gewöhnliche Dialektik beruht auf dem Festhalten des Gegensatzes von Seyn und Nichts. Es wird auf folgende Art bewiesen, daß kein Anfang der Welt oder von Etwas möglich sey: Es kann nichts anfangen, weder insofern etwas ist, noch insofern es nicht ist; denn insofern es ist, fängt es nicht erst an; insofern es aber nicht ist, fängt es auch nicht an.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"14.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","text":"-Wenn die Welt oder Etwas angefangen haben sollte, so hätte sie im Nichts angefangen, aber im Nichts oder das Nichts ist nicht Anfang; denn Anfang schließt ein Seyn in sich, aber das Nichts enthält kein Seyn. Nichts ist nur Nichts. In einem Grunde, Ursache u.s.w. wenn das Nichts so bestimmt wird, ist eine Affirmation, Seyn enthalten. —Aus demselben Grunde kann auch Etwas nicht aufhören. Denn so müßte das Seyn das Nichts enthalten, Seyn aber ist nur Seyn, nicht das Gegentheil seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"14.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","text":"Es erhellt, daß hierin gegen das Werden, oder Anfangen und Aufhören, diese Einheit des Seyns und Nichts, nichts vorgebracht wird, als sie assertorisch zu läugnen, und dem Seyn und Nichts, jedem getrennt von dem andern, Wahrheit zuzuschreiben.—Diese Dialektik ist jedoch wenigstens konsequenter als das reflektirende Vorstellen. Ihm gilt es für vollkommene Wahrheit, daß Seyn und Nichts nur getrennt seyen; auf der anderen Seite aber läßt es ein Anfangen und Aufhören als eben so wahrhafte Bestimmungen gelten; in diesen aber nimmt es die Ungetrenntheit des Seyns und Nichts faktisch an.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"14.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","text":"Bei der Voraussetzung der absoluten Geschiedenheit des Seyns vom Nichts, ist—was man so oft hört—der Anfang oder das Werden allerdings etwas Unbegreifliches; denn man macht eine Voraussetzung, welche den Anfang oder das Werden aufhebt, das man doch wieder zugibt, und dieser Widerspruch, den man selbst setzt und dessen Auflösung unmöglich macht, heißt das Unbegreifliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"14.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","text":"Das Angeführte ist auch dieselbe Dialektik, die der Verstand gegen den Begriff braucht, den die höhere Analysis von den unendlich-kleinen Größen giebt. Von diesem Begriffe wird weiter unten ausführlicher gehandelt.—Diese Größen sind als solche, bestimmt worden, die in ihrem Verschwinden sind, nicht vor ihrem Verschwinden, denn als dann sind sie endliche Größen;—nicht nach ihrem Verschwinden, denn alsdann sind sie nichts. Gegen diesen reinen Begriff ist eingewendet und immer wiederholt worden, daß solche Größen entweder Etwas seyen, oder Nichts; daß es keinen Mittelzustand (Zustand ist hier ein unpassender, barbarischer Ausdruck) zwischen Seyn und Nichtseyn gebe.—Es ist hierbei gleichfalls die absolute Trennung des Seyns und Nichts angenommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"14.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","text":"Dagegen ist aber gezeigt worden, daß Seyn und Nichts in der That dasselbe sind, oder um in jener Sprache zu sprechen, daß es gar nichts giebt, das nicht ein Mittelzustand zwischen Seyn und Nichts ist. Die Mathematik hat ihre glänzendsten Erfolge der Annahme jener Bestimmung, welcher der Verstand widerspricht, zu danken.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"14.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","text":"Das angeführte Raisonnement, das die falsche Voraussetzung der absoluten Getrenntheit des Seyns und Nichtseyns macht, und bei derselben stehen bleibt, ist nicht Dialektik, sondern Sophisterei zu nennen. Denn Sophisterei ist ein Raisonnement aus einer grundlosen Voraussetzung, die man ohne Kritik und unbesonnen gelten läßt; Dialektik aber nennen wir die höhere vernünftige Bewegung, in welche solche schlechthin getrennt scheinende, durch sich selbst, durch das, was sie sind, in einander übergehen, die Voraussetzung sich aufhebt. Es ist die dialektische immanente Natur des Seyns und Nichts selbst, daß sie ihre Einheit, das Werden, als ihre Wahrheit zeigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"14.7"}],"sha256":"940eb6fe924baa590d409251eb3942135dd7bccf0294b92560c54a2e63c83c9a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101926822391Z_319b924f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 4.","source_sha256":"940eb6fe924baa590d409251eb3942135dd7bccf0294b92560c54a2e63c83c9a","sha256":"975a338862e2ad01128a8fe4e768aacbe055dda05fc5d6233c56573b6a13dc71","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:26.822404+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","text":"It follows from what has preceded what is the case with the dialectic against the beginning of the world, and also against its end, by which the eternity of matter was supposed to be proved, i.e. with the dialectic against becoming, arising, or passing away in general. —Kant’s antinomy concerning the finitude or infinitude of the world in space and time will be considered more closely below under the concept of quantitative infinity.—That simple ordinary dialectic rests on holding fast to the opposition of being and nothing. It is proved in the following way that no beginning of the world or of anything is possible: nothing can begin, neither insofar as something is, nor insofar as it is not; for insofar as it is, it does not first begin; but insofar as it is not, it likewise does not begin.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"14.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","text":"-If the world or anything were to have begun, it would have begun in nothing, but in nothing, or nothing, there is no beginning; for beginning includes being within itself, but nothing contains no being. Nothing is merely nothing. In a ground, cause, etc., when nothing is thus determined, an affirmation, being, is contained. —For the same reason, something likewise cannot cease. For then being would have to contain nothing; but being is merely being, not its own opposite.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"14.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","text":"It is evident that, against becoming, or beginning and ceasing, nothing is advanced here concerning this unity of being and nothing except assertorily to deny it and to ascribe truth to being and nothing, each separately from the other.—Yet this dialectic is at least more consistent than reflective representation. For it holds it to be perfect truth that being and nothing are only separate; on the other hand, however, it lets beginning and ceasing count as equally true determinations; but in these it factually assumes the inseparability of being and nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"14.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","text":"Given the presupposition of the absolute distinctness of being from nothing, beginning or becoming is indeed—as one so often hears—something incomprehensible; for one makes a presupposition that abolishes beginning or becoming, which one nevertheless again admits, and this contradiction, which one oneself posits and makes its resolution impossible, is called the incomprehensible.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"14.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","text":"What has been adduced is also the same dialectic that the understanding employs against the concept which higher analysis gives of infinitesimal magnitudes. This concept will be discussed more fully below.—Such magnitudes have been determined as such as are in their vanishing, not before their vanishing, for then they are finite magnitudes;—not after their vanishing, for then they are nothing. Against this pure concept it has been objected, and repeatedly objected, that such magnitudes are either something or nothing; that there is no intermediate state (state is here an inappropriate, barbarous expression) between being and non-being.—Here likewise the absolute separation of being and nothing has been assumed.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"14.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","text":"Against this, however, it has been shown that being and nothing are in fact the same, or, to speak in that language, that there is nothing whatever that is not an intermediate state between being and nothing. Mathematics owes its most brilliant successes to the assumption of that determination to which the understanding objects.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"14.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","text":"The reasoning adduced, which makes the false presupposition of the absolute separateness of being and non-being and remains with it, is not to be called dialectic, but sophistry. For sophistry is reasoning from a groundless presupposition, which one allows to count without criticism and unreflectively; but we call dialectic the higher rational movement in which such things as appear absolutely separate pass over into one another through themselves, through what they are, and the presupposition sublates itself. It is the dialectical immanent nature of being and nothing themselves that they show their unity, becoming, as their truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"14.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"9a24e894ad8871d827b8ad2c33de5a4b123e29f941861604914ac956c0e84ba3","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 4."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 4.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW","title":"2. Moments of Becoming.","order":15,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_2MDW","text":"Das Werden, Entstehen und Vergehen, ist die Ungetrenntheit des Seyns und Nichts; nicht die Einheit, welche vom Seyn und Nichts abstrahirt; sondern als Einheit des Seyns und Nichts ist es diese bestimmte Einheit, oder in welcher sowohl Seyn als Nichts ist. Aber indem Seyn und Nichts, jedes ungetrennt von seinem Anderen ist, ist es nicht. Sie sind also in dieser Einheit, aber als verschwindende, nur als Aufgehobene. Sie sinken von ihrer zunächst vorgestellten Selbstständigkeit zu Momenten herab, noch unterschiedenen, aber zugleich aufgehobenen.\n\nNach dieser ihrer Unterschiedenheit sie aufgefaßt, ist jedes in derselben als Einheit mit dem Anderen. Das Werden enthält also Seyn und Nichts als zwei solche Einheiten, deren jede selbst Einheit des Seyns und Nichts ist; die eine das Seyn als unmittelbar und als Beziehung auf das Nichts; die andere das Nichts als unmittelbar und als Beziehung auf das Seyn; die Bestimmungen sind in ungleichem Werthe in diesen Einheiten.\n\nDas Werden ist auf diese Weise in gedoppelter Bestimmung; in der einen ist das Nichts als unmittelbar, d. i. sie ist anfangend vom Nichts, das sich auf das Seyn bezieht, das heißt, in dasselbe übergeht, in der anderen ist das Seyn als unmittelbar d. i. sie ist anfangend vom Seyn, das in das Nichts übergeht,—Entstehen und Vergehen.\n\nBeide sind dasselbe, Werden, und auch als diese so unterschiedenen Richtungen durchdringen und paralysiren sie sich gegenseitig. Die eine ist Vergehen; Seyn geht in Nichts über, aber Nichts ist eben so sehr das Gegentheil seiner selbst, Übergehen in Seyn, Entstehen. Dieß Entstehen ist die andere Richtung; Nichts geht in Seyn über, aber Seyn hebt ebenso sehr sich selbst auf und ist vielmehr das Übergehen in Nichts, ist Vergehen.—Sie heben sich nicht gegenseitig, nicht das eine äußerlich das andere auf; sondern jedes hebt sich an sich selbst auf und ist an ihm selbst das Gegentheil seiner.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","text":"Das Werden, Entstehen und Vergehen, ist die Ungetrenntheit des Seyns und Nichts; nicht die Einheit, welche vom Seyn und Nichts abstrahirt; sondern als Einheit des Seyns und Nichts ist es diese bestimmte Einheit, oder in welcher sowohl Seyn als Nichts ist. Aber indem Seyn und Nichts, jedes ungetrennt von seinem Anderen ist, ist es nicht. Sie sind also in dieser Einheit, aber als verschwindende, nur als Aufgehobene. Sie sinken von ihrer zunächst vorgestellten Selbstständigkeit zu Momenten herab, noch unterschiedenen, aber zugleich aufgehobenen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"15.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","text":"Nach dieser ihrer Unterschiedenheit sie aufgefaßt, ist jedes in derselben als Einheit mit dem Anderen. Das Werden enthält also Seyn und Nichts als zwei solche Einheiten, deren jede selbst Einheit des Seyns und Nichts ist; die eine das Seyn als unmittelbar und als Beziehung auf das Nichts; die andere das Nichts als unmittelbar und als Beziehung auf das Seyn; die Bestimmungen sind in ungleichem Werthe in diesen Einheiten.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"15.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","text":"Das Werden ist auf diese Weise in gedoppelter Bestimmung; in der einen ist das Nichts als unmittelbar, d. i. sie ist anfangend vom Nichts, das sich auf das Seyn bezieht, das heißt, in dasselbe übergeht, in der anderen ist das Seyn als unmittelbar d. i. sie ist anfangend vom Seyn, das in das Nichts übergeht,—Entstehen und Vergehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"15.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","text":"Beide sind dasselbe, Werden, und auch als diese so unterschiedenen Richtungen durchdringen und paralysiren sie sich gegenseitig. Die eine ist Vergehen; Seyn geht in Nichts über, aber Nichts ist eben so sehr das Gegentheil seiner selbst, Übergehen in Seyn, Entstehen. Dieß Entstehen ist die andere Richtung; Nichts geht in Seyn über, aber Seyn hebt ebenso sehr sich selbst auf und ist vielmehr das Übergehen in Nichts, ist Vergehen.—Sie heben sich nicht gegenseitig, nicht das eine äußerlich das andere auf; sondern jedes hebt sich an sich selbst auf und ist an ihm selbst das Gegentheil seiner.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"15.4"}],"sha256":"6090f535e42afa6136844958c0abee1cad1c8c26dfa2d9d806d2b13101c1c0ff","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101931540989Z_ade6921d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"2. Moments of Becoming.","source_sha256":"6090f535e42afa6136844958c0abee1cad1c8c26dfa2d9d806d2b13101c1c0ff","sha256":"e580be805b7360cb191a825dc18c8c61b3b9355f6e7a39b94e1c0b338f68b2d9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:31.541001+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","text":"Becoming, coming-to-be and passing-away, is the inseparability of Being and Nothing; not the unity which abstracts from Being and Nothing; but, as the unity of Being and Nothing, it is this determinate unity, or that in which both Being and Nothing are. But inasmuch as Being and Nothing, each inseparable from its Other, is not, they are therefore in this unity, but as vanishing, only as sublated. They sink from their initially represented independence to moments, still distinguished, but at the same time sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"15.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","text":"Apprehended according to this their distinctness, each is therein as unity with the Other. Becoming thus contains Being and Nothing as two such unities, each of which is itself unity of Being and Nothing; the one Being as immediate and as relation to Nothing; the other Nothing as immediate and as relation to Being; the determinations are of unequal value in these unities.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"15.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","text":"In this way Becoming is in a twofold determination; in the one, Nothing is as immediate, i.e. it begins from Nothing, which relates itself to Being, that is, passes over into it; in the other, Being is as immediate, i.e. it begins from Being, which passes over into Nothing,—coming-to-be and passing-away.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"15.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","text":"Both are the same, Becoming, and even as these directions so distinguished they interpenetrate and paralyse one another. The one is passing-away; Being passes over into Nothing, but Nothing is just as much the opposite of itself, passing-over into Being, coming-to-be. This coming-to-be is the other direction; Nothing passes over into Being, but Being equally sublates itself and is rather the passing-over into Nothing, is passing-away.—They do not sublate one another, not one externally the other; rather, each sublates itself in itself and is in itself the opposite of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"15.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"84ede083711dcee33bf1ed816339538c03d0c47031c21367f34cf42fe8e7533e","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"2. Momente des Werdens."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"2. Momente des Werdens.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW","title":"3. Sublation of Becoming.","order":16,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_3ADW","text":"Das Gleichgewicht, worein sich Entstehen und Vergehen setzen, ist zunächst das Werden selbst. Aber dieses geht eben so in ruhige Einheit zusammen. Seyn und Nichts sind in ihm nur als verschwindende; aber das Werden als solches ist nur durch die Unterschiedenheit derselben. Ihr Verschwinden ist daher das Verschwinden des Werdens, oder Verschwinden des Verschwindens selbst. Das Werden ist eine haltungslose Unruhe, die in ein ruhiges Resultat zusammensinkt.\n\nDieß könnte auch so ausgedrückt werden: Das Werden ist das Verschwinden von Seyn in Nichts, und von Nichts in Seyn, und das Verschwinden von Seyn und Nichts überhaupt; aber es beruht zugleich auf dem Unterschiede derselben. Es widerspricht sich also in sich selbst, weil es solches in sich vereint, das sich entgegengesetzt ist; eine solche Vereinigung aber zerstört sich.\n\nDieß Resultat ist das Verschwundenseyn, aber nicht als Nichts; so wäre es nur ein Rückfall in die eine der schon aufgehobenen Bestimmungen, nicht Resultat des Nichts und des Seyns. Es ist die zur ruhigen Einfachheit gewordene Einheit des Seyns und Nichts. Die ruhige Einfachheit aber ist Seyn, jedoch ebenso, nicht mehr für sich, sondern als Bestimmung des Ganzen.\n\nDas Werden so Übergehen in die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts, welche als seyend ist, oder die Gestalt der einseitigen unmittelbaren Einheit dieser Momente hat, ist das Daseyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0001","text":"Das Gleichgewicht, worein sich Entstehen und Vergehen setzen, ist zunächst das Werden selbst. Aber dieses geht eben so in ruhige Einheit zusammen. Seyn und Nichts sind in ihm nur als verschwindende; aber das Werden als solches ist nur durch die Unterschiedenheit derselben. Ihr Verschwinden ist daher das Verschwinden des Werdens, oder Verschwinden des Verschwindens selbst. Das Werden ist eine haltungslose Unruhe, die in ein ruhiges Resultat zusammensinkt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"16.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0002","text":"Dieß könnte auch so ausgedrückt werden: Das Werden ist das Verschwinden von Seyn in Nichts, und von Nichts in Seyn, und das Verschwinden von Seyn und Nichts überhaupt; aber es beruht zugleich auf dem Unterschiede derselben. Es widerspricht sich also in sich selbst, weil es solches in sich vereint, das sich entgegengesetzt ist; eine solche Vereinigung aber zerstört sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"16.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0003","text":"Dieß Resultat ist das Verschwundenseyn, aber nicht als Nichts; so wäre es nur ein Rückfall in die eine der schon aufgehobenen Bestimmungen, nicht Resultat des Nichts und des Seyns. Es ist die zur ruhigen Einfachheit gewordene Einheit des Seyns und Nichts. Die ruhige Einfachheit aber ist Seyn, jedoch ebenso, nicht mehr für sich, sondern als Bestimmung des Ganzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"16.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0004","text":"Das Werden so Übergehen in die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts, welche als seyend ist, oder die Gestalt der einseitigen unmittelbaren Einheit dieser Momente hat, ist das Daseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"16.4"}],"sha256":"351e5ecd6ac9e38995d27bac185f107facd3f108985e5f7e9de6cb7fcdfd610e","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101935607077Z_91547170","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"3. Sublation of Becoming.","source_sha256":"351e5ecd6ac9e38995d27bac185f107facd3f108985e5f7e9de6cb7fcdfd610e","sha256":"3f55377b6176c7c4b71af011bc55b4adf8666a8d418fe9fcdbe504cd927af37e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:35.607094+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0001","text":"The equilibrium into which coming-to-be and passing-away place themselves is, at first, becoming itself. But it likewise coalesces into a tranquil unity. Being and nothing are in it only as vanishing; but becoming as such is only through their difference. Their vanishing is therefore the vanishing of becoming, or the vanishing of vanishing itself. Becoming is an unstable unrest that sinks down into a tranquil result.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"16.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0002","text":"This could also be expressed thus: Becoming is the vanishing of being into nothing, and of nothing into being, and the vanishing of being and nothing altogether; but it rests at the same time upon their difference. Thus it contradicts itself within itself, because it unites within itself that which is opposed to itself; but such a union destroys itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"16.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0003","text":"This result is vanishedness, but not as nothing; otherwise it would merely be a relapse into one of the determinations already sublated, not the result of nothing and being. It is the unity of being and nothing that has become tranquil simplicity. But tranquil simplicity is being, yet equally, no longer for itself, but as a determination of the whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"16.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0004","text":"This transition of becoming into the unity of being and nothing, which is as being, or has the shape of the one-sided immediate unity of these moments, is determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"16.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3ADW:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"649aa240c269f2d2e1ec6ac7e518819209c9aa869a1fe24276ee17b68d8030c5","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"3. Aufheben des Werdens."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"3. Aufheben des Werdens.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME","title":"Remark.","order":17,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ANME","text":"Aufheben und das Aufgehobene (das Ideelle) ist einer der wichtigsten Begriffe der Philosophie, eine Grundbestimmung, die schlechthin allenthalben wiederkehrt, deren Sinn bestimmt aufzufassen und besonders vom Nichts zu unterscheiden ist.—Was sich aufhebt, wird dadurch nicht zu Nichts. Nichts ist das Unmittelbare; ein Aufgehobenes dagegen ist ein Vermitteltes, es ist das Nichtseyende, aber als Resultat, das von einem Seyn ausgegangen ist; es hat daher die Bestimmtheit aus der es herkommt, noch an sich.\n\nAufheben hat in der Sprache den gedoppelten Sinn, daß es so viel als aufbewahren, erhalten bedeutet, und zugleich so viel als aufhören lassen, ein Ende machen. Das Aufbewahren selbst schließt schon das Negative in sich, daß etwas seiner Unmittelbarkeit und damit einem den äußerlichen Einwirkungen offenen Daseyn entnommen wird, um es zu erhalten.—So ist das Aufgehobene ein zugleich Aufbewahrtes, das nur seine Unmittelbarkeit verloren hat, aber darum nicht vernichtet ist. —Die angegebenen zwei Bestimmungen des Aufhebens können lexikalisch als zwei Bedeutungen dieses Wortes aufgeführt werden. Auffallend müßte es aber dabei seyn, daß eine Sprache dazu gekommen ist, ein und dasselbe Wort für zwei entgegengesetzte Bestimmungen zu gebrauchen. Für das spekulative Denken ist es erfreulich, in der Sprache Wörter zu finden welche eine spekulative Bedeutung an ihnen selbst haben; die deutsche Sprache hat mehrere dergleichen. Der Doppelsinn des lateinischen: tollere (der durch den ciceronianischen Witz tollendum esse Octavium, berühmt geworden) geht nicht so weit, die affirmative Bestimmung geht nur bis zum Emporheben. Etwas ist nur insofern aufgehoben, als es in die Einheit mit seinem Entgegengesetzten getreten ist; in dieser nähern Bestimmung als ein reflektirtes kann es passend Moment genannt werden. Gewicht und Entfernung von einem Punkt heißen beim Hebel, dessen mechanische Momente, um der Dieselbigkeit ihrer Wirkung willen bei aller sonstigen Verschiedenheit eines Reellen, wie das ein Gewicht ist, und eines Ideellen, der bloßen räumlichen Bestimmung, der Linie; s. Encykl. der philos. Wissenschaft 3te Ausg. § 261. Anm.—Noch öfter wird die Bemerkung sich aufdringen, daß die philosophische Kunstsprache für reflektirte Bestimmungen lateinische Ausdrücke gebraucht, entweder weil die Muttersprache keine Ausdrücke dafür hat, oder wenn sie deren hat, wie hier, weil ihr Ausdruck mehr an das Unmittelbare, die fremde Sprache aber mehr an das Reflektirte erinnert.\n\nDer nähere Sinn und Ausdruck, den Seyn und Nichts, indem sie nunmehr Momente sind, erhalten, hat sich bei der Betrachtung des Daseyns, als der Einheit, in der sie aufbewahrt sind, zu ergeben. Seyn ist Seyn, und Nichts ist Nichts nur in ihrer Unterschiedenheit von einander; in ihrer Wahrheit aber, in ihrer Einheit, sind sie als diese Bestimmungen verschwunden, und sind nun etwas anderes. Seyn und Nichts sind dasselbe; darum weil sie dasselbe sind, sind sie nicht mehr Seyn und Nichts, und haben eine verschiedene Bestimmung; im Werden waren sie Entstehen und Vergehen; im Daseyn als einer anders bestimmten Einheit sind sie wieder anders bestimmte Momente. Diese Einheit bleibt nun ihre Grundlage, aus der sie nicht mehr zur abstrakten Bedeutung von Seyn und Nichts heraustreten.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0001","text":"Aufheben und das Aufgehobene (das Ideelle) ist einer der wichtigsten Begriffe der Philosophie, eine Grundbestimmung, die schlechthin allenthalben wiederkehrt, deren Sinn bestimmt aufzufassen und besonders vom Nichts zu unterscheiden ist.—Was sich aufhebt, wird dadurch nicht zu Nichts. Nichts ist das Unmittelbare; ein Aufgehobenes dagegen ist ein Vermitteltes, es ist das Nichtseyende, aber als Resultat, das von einem Seyn ausgegangen ist; es hat daher die Bestimmtheit aus der es herkommt, noch an sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"17.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0002","text":"Aufheben hat in der Sprache den gedoppelten Sinn, daß es so viel als aufbewahren, erhalten bedeutet, und zugleich so viel als aufhören lassen, ein Ende machen. Das Aufbewahren selbst schließt schon das Negative in sich, daß etwas seiner Unmittelbarkeit und damit einem den äußerlichen Einwirkungen offenen Daseyn entnommen wird, um es zu erhalten.—So ist das Aufgehobene ein zugleich Aufbewahrtes, das nur seine Unmittelbarkeit verloren hat, aber darum nicht vernichtet ist. —Die angegebenen zwei Bestimmungen des Aufhebens können lexikalisch als zwei Bedeutungen dieses Wortes aufgeführt werden. Auffallend müßte es aber dabei seyn, daß eine Sprache dazu gekommen ist, ein und dasselbe Wort für zwei entgegengesetzte Bestimmungen zu gebrauchen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"17.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0003","text":"Für das spekulative Denken ist es erfreulich, in der Sprache Wörter zu finden welche eine spekulative Bedeutung an ihnen selbst haben; die deutsche Sprache hat mehrere dergleichen. Der Doppelsinn des lateinischen: tollere (der durch den ciceronianischen Witz tollendum esse Octavium, berühmt geworden) geht nicht so weit, die affirmative Bestimmung geht nur bis zum Emporheben. Etwas ist nur insofern aufgehoben, als es in die Einheit mit seinem Entgegengesetzten getreten ist; in dieser nähern Bestimmung als ein reflektirtes kann es passend Moment genannt werden. Gewicht und Entfernung von einem Punkt heißen beim Hebel, dessen mechanische Momente, um der Dieselbigkeit ihrer Wirkung willen bei aller sonstigen Verschiedenheit eines Reellen, wie das ein Gewicht ist, und eines Ideellen, der bloßen räumlichen Bestimmung, der Linie; s. Encykl. der philos. Wissenschaft 3te Ausg. § 261.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"17.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0004","text":"Anm.—Noch öfter wird die Bemerkung sich aufdringen, daß die philosophische Kunstsprache für reflektirte Bestimmungen lateinische Ausdrücke gebraucht, entweder weil die Muttersprache keine Ausdrücke dafür hat, oder wenn sie deren hat, wie hier, weil ihr Ausdruck mehr an das Unmittelbare, die fremde Sprache aber mehr an das Reflektirte erinnert.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"17.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0005","text":"Der nähere Sinn und Ausdruck, den Seyn und Nichts, indem sie nunmehr Momente sind, erhalten, hat sich bei der Betrachtung des Daseyns, als der Einheit, in der sie aufbewahrt sind, zu ergeben. Seyn ist Seyn, und Nichts ist Nichts nur in ihrer Unterschiedenheit von einander; in ihrer Wahrheit aber, in ihrer Einheit, sind sie als diese Bestimmungen verschwunden, und sind nun etwas anderes. Seyn und Nichts sind dasselbe; darum weil sie dasselbe sind, sind sie nicht mehr Seyn und Nichts, und haben eine verschiedene Bestimmung; im Werden waren sie Entstehen und Vergehen; im Daseyn als einer anders bestimmten Einheit sind sie wieder anders bestimmte Momente. Diese Einheit bleibt nun ihre Grundlage, aus der sie nicht mehr zur abstrakten Bedeutung von Seyn und Nichts heraustreten.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"17.5"}],"sha256":"d194f8cb22d206e82802e974b974d2d32650dbd571cb991664b972d3aec0f348","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101942954727Z_6db2bbbc","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"d194f8cb22d206e82802e974b974d2d32650dbd571cb991664b972d3aec0f348","sha256":"04d479f409d9cc08cd72a37bc13b0efb23ee0777643cdfba90752934912a2a9c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:42.954749+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0001","text":"Sublation and the sublated (the ideal) is one of the most important concepts of philosophy, a fundamental determination that recurs absolutely everywhere, whose meaning is to be grasped determinately and especially distinguished from Nothing.—What sublates itself does not thereby become Nothing. Nothing is the immediate; a sublated [something], on the other hand, is a mediated [something]; it is the non-being, but as a result that has proceeded from a being; it therefore still has within itself the determinacy from which it comes.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"17.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANME:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0002","text":"Sublate has in language the doubled sense that it means as much as to preserve, to maintain, and at the same time as much as to cause to cease, to make an end. Preservation itself already includes the negative within itself, namely, that something is withdrawn from its immediacy and thereby from an existence open to external influences, in order to preserve it.—Thus the sublated is at the same time something preserved, which has only lost its immediacy, but is not thereby annihilated. —The two stated determinations of sublation can lexically be listed as two meanings of this word. But it would have to be striking that a language has come to use one and the same word for two opposed determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"17.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANME:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0003","text":"For speculative thinking, it is gratifying to find in language words that have a speculative significance in themselves; the German language has several such. The double sense of the Latin tollere (which has become famous through the Ciceronian witticism tollendum esse Octavium) does not extend so far; the affirmative determination extends only to lifting up. Something is sublated only insofar as it has entered into unity with its opposite; in this more specific determination as something reflected, it can appropriately be called a moment. Weight and distance from a point are called, in the case of the lever, its mechanical moments, on account of the identity of their effect amid all other difference between a real [something], such as a weight is, and an ideal [something], the merely spatial determination, the line; see Encycl. of the Philosophical Sciences, 3rd ed., § 261.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"17.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANME:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0004","text":"Remark.—Still more frequently the observation will impose itself that philosophical technical language employs Latin expressions for reflected determinations, either because the mother tongue has no expressions for them, or, when it does have them, as here, because its expression recalls the immediate more, whereas the foreign language recalls the reflected more.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"17.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANME:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANME:P0005","text":"The more specific meaning and expression that Being and Nothing, since they are now moments, receive, has emerged in the consideration of Existence, as the unity in which they are preserved. Being is Being, and Nothing is Nothing, only in their distinctness from one another; in their truth, however, in their unity, they have vanished as these determinations and are now something else. Being and Nothing are the same; because they are the same, they are no longer Being and Nothing, and have a different determination; in Becoming they were coming-to-be and ceasing-to-be; in Existence, as a unity determined otherwise, they are again otherwise determined moments. This unity now remains their foundation, from which they no longer emerge into the abstract meaning of Being and Nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"17.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ANME:P0005"]}],"source_digest":"09207a0edc46e35864e484dbfad13abaccaab4878044aca893879a250a1022b9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0","title":"A. Determinate Being as Such.","order":18,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DAS0","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Das Daseyn.\n\nDaseyn ist bestimmtes Seyn; seine Bestimmtheit ist seyende Bestimmtheit, Qualität. Durch seine Qualität ist Etwas gegen ein Anderes, ist veränderlich und endlich, nicht nur gegen ein Anderes, sondern an ihm schlechthin negativ bestimmt. Diese seine Negation dem endlichen Etwas zunächst gegenüber ist das Unendliche; der abstrakte Gegensatz, in welchem diese Bestimmungen erscheinen, löst sich in die gegensatzlose Unendlichkeit, in das Fürsichseyn auf.\n\nDie Abhandlung des Daseyns hat so die drei Abtheilungen:\n\nA. das Daseyn als solches,\n\nB. Etwas und Anderes, die Endlichkeit,\n\nC. die qualitative Unendlichkeit.\n\n## A. Daseyn als solches.\n\nAn dem Daseyn\n\na. als solchem, ist zunächst seine Bestimmtheit\n\nb. als Qualität zu unterscheiden. Diese aber ist sowohl in der einen als in der anderen Bestimmung des Daseyns zu nehmen, als Realität und als Negation. Aber in diesen Bestimmtheiten ist Daseyn eben so sehr in sich reflektirt; und als solches gesetzt ist es\n\nc. Etwas, Daseyendes.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0001","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Das Daseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"18.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0002","text":"Daseyn ist bestimmtes Seyn; seine Bestimmtheit ist seyende Bestimmtheit, Qualität. Durch seine Qualität ist Etwas gegen ein Anderes, ist veränderlich und endlich, nicht nur gegen ein Anderes, sondern an ihm schlechthin negativ bestimmt. Diese seine Negation dem endlichen Etwas zunächst gegenüber ist das Unendliche; der abstrakte Gegensatz, in welchem diese Bestimmungen erscheinen, löst sich in die gegensatzlose Unendlichkeit, in das Fürsichseyn auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"18.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0003","text":"Die Abhandlung des Daseyns hat so die drei Abtheilungen:","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"18.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0004","text":"A. das Daseyn als solches,","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"18.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0005","text":"B. Etwas und Anderes, die Endlichkeit,","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"18.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0006","text":"C. die qualitative Unendlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"18.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0007","text":"## A. Daseyn als solches.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"18.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0008","text":"An dem Daseyn","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"18.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0009","text":"a. als solchem, ist zunächst seine Bestimmtheit","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"18.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0010","text":"b. als Qualität zu unterscheiden. Diese aber ist sowohl in der einen als in der anderen Bestimmung des Daseyns zu nehmen, als Realität und als Negation. Aber in diesen Bestimmtheiten ist Daseyn eben so sehr in sich reflektirt; und als solches gesetzt ist es","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"18.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0011","text":"c. Etwas, Daseyendes.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"18.11"}],"sha256":"5bd08c5e67805b33f2caf5a2f05bfebea72389db5915597a7cbd1c3644584853","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101949202854Z_af3fdea8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Determinate Being as Such.","source_sha256":"5bd08c5e67805b33f2caf5a2f05bfebea72389db5915597a7cbd1c3644584853","sha256":"8752153690d96d6080e44060fa371196f2ffd087fea033cc62208d6cf0ac00fb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:49.202871+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0001","text":"## Second Chapter. Determinate Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"18.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0002","text":"Determinate being is determinate being; its determinateness is being determinateness, quality. Through its quality, Something is in relation to an Other, is mutable and finite, not merely in relation to an Other, but determined in itself as simply negative. This its negation, at first opposed to finite Something, is the Infinite; the abstract opposition in which these determinations appear resolves itself into oppositionless infinity, into being-for-self.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"18.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0003","text":"The treatment of determinate being thus has the three divisions:","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"18.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0004","text":"A. determinate being as such,","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"18.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0005","text":"B. Something and Other, finitude,","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"18.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0006","text":"C. qualitative infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"18.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0007","text":"## A. Determinate Being as Such.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"18.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0008","text":"In determinate being","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"18.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0009","text":"a. as such, its determinateness is at first to be distinguished;","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"18.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0010","text":"b. as quality. But this is to be taken both in the one and in the other determination of determinate being, as reality and as negation. But in these determinatenesses determinate being is just as much reflected into itself; and posited as such, it is","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"18.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0011","text":"c. Something, a determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"18.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAS0:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"c533129af26e73a47b176232e425dd72fe89007a24978b835bee70fd7b9bbbbd","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Daseyn als solches."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Daseyn als solches.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB","title":"a. Determinate Being in General.","order":19,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DASB","text":"Aus dem Werden geht das Daseyn hervor. Das Daseyn ist das einfache Einsseyn des Seyns und Nichts. Es hat um dieser Einfachheit willen, die Form von einem Unmittelbaren. Seine Vermittelung, das Werden, liegt hinter ihm; sie hat sich aufgehoben, und das Daseyn erscheint daher als ein erstes, von dem ausgegangen werde. Es ist zunächst in der einseitigen Bestimmung des Seyns, die andere, die es enthält, das Nichts, wird sich gleichfalls an ihm hervorthun, gegen jene.\n\nEs ist nicht bloßes Seyn, sondern Daseyn; etymologisch genommen Seyn an einem gewissen Orte; aber die Raumvorstellung gehört nicht hierher. Daseyn ist, nach seinem Werden, überhaupt Seyn mit einem Nichtseyn, so daß dieß Nichtseyn in einfache Einheit mit dem Seyn aufgenommen ist. Das Nichtseyn so in das Seyn aufgenommen, daß das konkrete Ganze in der Form des Seyns, der Unmittelbarkeit ist, macht die Bestimmtheit als solche aus.\n\nDas Ganze ist gleichfalls in der Form d. i. Bestimmtheit des Seyns, denn Seyn hat im Werden sich gleichfalls nur ein Moment zu seyn gezeigt,—ein aufgehobenes, negativ bestimmtes; aber so ist es für uns in unserer Reflexion, noch nicht gesetzt an ihm selbst. Aber die Bestimmtheit des Daseyns als solche ist die gesetzte, die auch im Ausdruck Daseyn liegt.—Beides ist immer sehr wohl von einander zu unterscheiden; nur das, was gesetzt ist an einem Begriffe, gehört in die entwickelnde Betrachtung desselben, zu seinem Inhalte. Die noch nicht an ihm selbst gesetzte Bestimmtheit aber gehört unserer Reflexion, sie betreffe nun die Natur des Begriffes selbst, oder sie sey äußere Vergleichung; eine Bestimmtheit der letztern Art bemerklich zu machen kann nur zur Erläuterung oder Vorausandeutung des Ganges dienen, der in der Entwickelung selbst sich darstellen wird. Daß das Ganze, die Einheit des Seyns und des Nichts, in der einseitigen Bestimmtheit des Seyns sey, ist eine äußerliche Reflexion; in der Negation aber, im Etwas und Anderen u.s.f. wird sie dazu kommen, als gesetzte zu seyn.—Es hat hier auf den angegebenen Unterschied aufmerksam gemacht werden sollen; über alles aber, was die Reflexion sich erlauben kann zu bemerken, Rechenschaft zu geben, würde in die Weitläufigkeit führen, das zu anticipiren, was sich an der Sache selbst ergeben muß. Wenn dergleichen Reflexionen dienen können, die Übersicht und damit das Verständniß zu erleichtern, so führen sie wohl auch den Nachtheil herbei, als unberechtigte Behauptungen, Gründe und Grundlagen für das Weitere auszusehen. Man soll sie daher für nichts mehr nehmen, als was sie seyn sollen, und sie von dem unterscheiden, was ein Moment im Fortgange der Sache selbst ist.\n\nDas Daseyn entspricht dem Seyn der vorigen Sphäre; das Seyn jedoch ist das Unbestimmte, es ergeben sich deswegen keine Bestimmungen an demselben. Aber das Daseyn ist bestimmtes Seyn, ein konkretes; es thun sich daher sogleich mehrere Bestimmungen, unterschiedene Verhältnisse seiner Momente an ihm auf.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0001","text":"Aus dem Werden geht das Daseyn hervor. Das Daseyn ist das einfache Einsseyn des Seyns und Nichts. Es hat um dieser Einfachheit willen, die Form von einem Unmittelbaren. Seine Vermittelung, das Werden, liegt hinter ihm; sie hat sich aufgehoben, und das Daseyn erscheint daher als ein erstes, von dem ausgegangen werde. Es ist zunächst in der einseitigen Bestimmung des Seyns, die andere, die es enthält, das Nichts, wird sich gleichfalls an ihm hervorthun, gegen jene.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"19.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0002","text":"Es ist nicht bloßes Seyn, sondern Daseyn; etymologisch genommen Seyn an einem gewissen Orte; aber die Raumvorstellung gehört nicht hierher. Daseyn ist, nach seinem Werden, überhaupt Seyn mit einem Nichtseyn, so daß dieß Nichtseyn in einfache Einheit mit dem Seyn aufgenommen ist. Das Nichtseyn so in das Seyn aufgenommen, daß das konkrete Ganze in der Form des Seyns, der Unmittelbarkeit ist, macht die Bestimmtheit als solche aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"19.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0003","text":"Das Ganze ist gleichfalls in der Form d. i. Bestimmtheit des Seyns, denn Seyn hat im Werden sich gleichfalls nur ein Moment zu seyn gezeigt,—ein aufgehobenes, negativ bestimmtes; aber so ist es für uns in unserer Reflexion, noch nicht gesetzt an ihm selbst. Aber die Bestimmtheit des Daseyns als solche ist die gesetzte, die auch im Ausdruck Daseyn liegt.—Beides ist immer sehr wohl von einander zu unterscheiden; nur das, was gesetzt ist an einem Begriffe, gehört in die entwickelnde Betrachtung desselben, zu seinem Inhalte. Die noch nicht an ihm selbst gesetzte Bestimmtheit aber gehört unserer Reflexion, sie betreffe nun die Natur des Begriffes selbst, oder sie sey äußere Vergleichung; eine Bestimmtheit der letztern Art bemerklich zu machen kann nur zur Erläuterung oder Vorausandeutung des Ganges dienen, der in der Entwickelung selbst sich darstellen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"19.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0004","text":"Daß das Ganze, die Einheit des Seyns und des Nichts, in der einseitigen Bestimmtheit des Seyns sey, ist eine äußerliche Reflexion; in der Negation aber, im Etwas und Anderen u.s.f. wird sie dazu kommen, als gesetzte zu seyn.—Es hat hier auf den angegebenen Unterschied aufmerksam gemacht werden sollen; über alles aber, was die Reflexion sich erlauben kann zu bemerken, Rechenschaft zu geben, würde in die Weitläufigkeit führen, das zu anticipiren, was sich an der Sache selbst ergeben muß. Wenn dergleichen Reflexionen dienen können, die Übersicht und damit das Verständniß zu erleichtern, so führen sie wohl auch den Nachtheil herbei, als unberechtigte Behauptungen, Gründe und Grundlagen für das Weitere auszusehen. Man soll sie daher für nichts mehr nehmen, als was sie seyn sollen, und sie von dem unterscheiden, was ein Moment im Fortgange der Sache selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"19.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0005","text":"Das Daseyn entspricht dem Seyn der vorigen Sphäre; das Seyn jedoch ist das Unbestimmte, es ergeben sich deswegen keine Bestimmungen an demselben. Aber das Daseyn ist bestimmtes Seyn, ein konkretes; es thun sich daher sogleich mehrere Bestimmungen, unterschiedene Verhältnisse seiner Momente an ihm auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"19.5"}],"sha256":"0f00638fc5ab0ebbb8803eed69990d60bdb05cc8f8a9a41efc6e160653b37380","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T101957848002Z_23e1f3f6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Determinate Being in General.","source_sha256":"0f00638fc5ab0ebbb8803eed69990d60bdb05cc8f8a9a41efc6e160653b37380","sha256":"b862bb4b8e6f33ba47fe164cb34a077117954486cafb967e3360b9453a63a4a8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:19:57.848023+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0001","text":"Existence emerges from becoming. Existence is the simple unity of being and nothing. On account of this simplicity, it has the form of an immediate. Its mediation, becoming, lies behind it; it has sublated itself, and existence therefore appears as a first, from which one is to proceed. It is initially in the one-sided determinacy of being; the other which it contains, nothing, will likewise show itself in it, in opposition to the former.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"19.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DASB:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0002","text":"It is not mere being, but existence; etymologically taken, being in a certain place; but the representation of space does not belong here. Existence, according to its becoming, is being in general with a not-being, such that this not-being is taken up into simple unity with being. Not-being thus taken up into being, so that the concrete whole is in the form of being, of immediacy, constitutes determinacy as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"19.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DASB:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0003","text":"The whole is likewise in the form, i.e. determinacy, of being, for being too has shown itself in becoming to be only a moment,—a sublated, negatively determined one; but thus it is for us in our reflection, not yet posited in it itself. But the determinacy of existence as such is the posited determinacy, which also lies in the expression existence.—The two must always be very carefully distinguished from one another; only that which is posited in a concept belongs to its developing consideration, to its content. But determinacy not yet posited in it itself belongs to our reflection, whether it concerns the nature of the concept itself or is external comparison; to make a determinacy of the latter kind noticeable can serve only to elucidate or to indicate in advance the course that will present itself in the development itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"19.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DASB:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0004","text":"That the whole, the unity of being and nothing, is in the one-sided determinacy of being, is an external reflection; but in negation, in something and other, etc., it will come to be posited.—Here attention was to be drawn to the indicated distinction; but to give an account of everything that reflection may permit itself to remark would lead into prolixity, anticipating what must emerge from the matter itself. If reflections of this sort can serve to facilitate the overview and thereby understanding, they also readily bring with them the disadvantage of appearing as unwarranted assertions, reasons, and foundations for what follows. One should therefore take them for nothing more than what they are supposed to be, and distinguish them from what is a moment in the progression of the matter itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"19.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DASB:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DASB:P0005","text":"Existence corresponds to the being of the preceding sphere; being, however, is the indeterminate, and therefore no determinations emerge in it. But existence is determinate being, a concrete; thus several determinations, distinct relations of its moments, immediately disclose themselves in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"19.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DASB:P0005"]}],"source_digest":"e9384860cd45439294a8614b3df7bea813398c369353a0ac238cbeb507c90925","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Daseyn überhaupt."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Daseyn überhaupt.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0","title":"b. Quality.","order":20,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BQT0","text":"Um der Unmittelbarkeit willen, in der im Daseyn, Seyn und Nichts, Eins sind, gehen sie nicht übereinander hinaus; so weit das Daseyn seyend ist, so weit ist es Nichtseyn, ist es bestimmt. Das Seyn ist nicht das Allgemeine, die Bestimmtheit nicht das Besondere. Die Bestimmtheit hat sich noch nicht vom Seyn abgelöst; zwar wird sie sich auch nicht mehr von ihm ablösen; denn das nunmehr zum Grunde liegende Wahre ist die Einheit des Nichtseyns mit dem Seyn; auf ihr als dem Grunde ergeben sich alle fernern Bestimmungen. Aber die Beziehung, in der hier die Bestimmtheit mit dem Seyn steht, ist die unmittelbare Einheit beider, so daß noch keine Unterscheidung derselben gesetzt ist.\n\nDie Bestimmtheit so für sich isolirt, als seyende Bestimmtheit, ist die Qualität;—ein ganz Einfaches, Unmittelbares. Die Bestimmtheit überhaupt ist das Allgemeinere, das ebenso sehr auch das Quantitative, wie weiter Bestimmte seyn kann. Um dieser Einfachheit willen ist von der Qualität als solcher weiter nichts zu sagen.\n\nAber das Daseyn, in welchem ebenso wohl das Nichts als das Seyn enthalten, ist selbst der Maßstab für die Einseitigkeit der Qualität als nur unmittelbarer oder seyender Bestimmtheit. Sie ist ebenso sehr in der Bestimmung des Nichts zu setzen, womit dann die unmittelbare oder die seyende Bestimmtheit als eine unterschiedene, reflektirte gesetzt wird, das Nichts so als das bestimmte einer Bestimmtheit, ist ebenso ein reflektirtes, eine Verneinung. Die Qualität, so daß sie unterschieden als seyende gelte, ist die Realität; sie als mit einer Verneinung behaftet, Negation überhaupt, gleichfalls eine Qualität, aber die für einen Mangel gilt, sich weiterhin als Grenze, Schranke bestimmt.\n\nBeide sind ein Daseyn, aber in der Realität als Qualität mit dem Accente, eine seyende, zu seyn, ist es versteckt, daß sie die Bestimmtheit, also auch die Negation enthält; die Realität gilt daher nur als etwas Positives, aus welchem Verneinung, Beschränktheit, Mangel ausgeschlossen sey. Die Negation als bloßer Mangel genommen, wäre was Nichts ist; aber sie ist ein Daseyn, eine Qualität nur mit einem Nichtseyn bestimmt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0001","text":"Um der Unmittelbarkeit willen, in der im Daseyn, Seyn und Nichts, Eins sind, gehen sie nicht übereinander hinaus; so weit das Daseyn seyend ist, so weit ist es Nichtseyn, ist es bestimmt. Das Seyn ist nicht das Allgemeine, die Bestimmtheit nicht das Besondere. Die Bestimmtheit hat sich noch nicht vom Seyn abgelöst; zwar wird sie sich auch nicht mehr von ihm ablösen; denn das nunmehr zum Grunde liegende Wahre ist die Einheit des Nichtseyns mit dem Seyn; auf ihr als dem Grunde ergeben sich alle fernern Bestimmungen. Aber die Beziehung, in der hier die Bestimmtheit mit dem Seyn steht, ist die unmittelbare Einheit beider, so daß noch keine Unterscheidung derselben gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"20.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0002","text":"Die Bestimmtheit so für sich isolirt, als seyende Bestimmtheit, ist die Qualität;—ein ganz Einfaches, Unmittelbares. Die Bestimmtheit überhaupt ist das Allgemeinere, das ebenso sehr auch das Quantitative, wie weiter Bestimmte seyn kann. Um dieser Einfachheit willen ist von der Qualität als solcher weiter nichts zu sagen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"20.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0003","text":"Aber das Daseyn, in welchem ebenso wohl das Nichts als das Seyn enthalten, ist selbst der Maßstab für die Einseitigkeit der Qualität als nur unmittelbarer oder seyender Bestimmtheit. Sie ist ebenso sehr in der Bestimmung des Nichts zu setzen, womit dann die unmittelbare oder die seyende Bestimmtheit als eine unterschiedene, reflektirte gesetzt wird, das Nichts so als das bestimmte einer Bestimmtheit, ist ebenso ein reflektirtes, eine Verneinung. Die Qualität, so daß sie unterschieden als seyende gelte, ist die Realität; sie als mit einer Verneinung behaftet, Negation überhaupt, gleichfalls eine Qualität, aber die für einen Mangel gilt, sich weiterhin als Grenze, Schranke bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"20.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0004","text":"Beide sind ein Daseyn, aber in der Realität als Qualität mit dem Accente, eine seyende, zu seyn, ist es versteckt, daß sie die Bestimmtheit, also auch die Negation enthält; die Realität gilt daher nur als etwas Positives, aus welchem Verneinung, Beschränktheit, Mangel ausgeschlossen sey. Die Negation als bloßer Mangel genommen, wäre was Nichts ist; aber sie ist ein Daseyn, eine Qualität nur mit einem Nichtseyn bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"20.4"}],"sha256":"d10d35346b31752ebc35e3f37af97d9379414825388afe3bee3fb166f3541cab","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102002993346Z_6a58c851","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Quality.","source_sha256":"d10d35346b31752ebc35e3f37af97d9379414825388afe3bee3fb166f3541cab","sha256":"25924b5de7a6b6074be526d63c9e72bea835d170900010eb8ea60360fb567c1b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:20:02.993362+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0001","text":"For the sake of the immediacy in which, in determinate being, being and nothing are one, they do not go beyond one another; insofar as determinate being is being, it is non-being, it is determinate. Being is not the universal, determinacy not the particular. Determinacy has not yet detached itself from being; indeed, it will no longer detach itself from it either; for the truth now lying at the ground is the unity of non-being with being; upon it as ground all further determinations arise. But the relation in which determinacy here stands with being is the immediate unity of both, so that no distinction between them has yet been posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"20.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0002","text":"Determinacy thus isolated for itself, as being determinacy, is quality;—a wholly simple, immediate [thing]. Determinacy in general is the more universal, which can equally well be the quantitative as further determinate. On account of this simplicity, nothing further can be said about quality as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"20.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0003","text":"But determinate being, in which nothing is contained just as much as being, is itself the standard for the one-sidedness of quality as merely immediate or being determinacy. It is just as much to be posited in the determination of nothing, whereby immediate or being determinacy is then posited as a distinguished, reflected determinacy; nothing, thus as the determinate [nothing] of a determinacy, is likewise a reflected [nothing], a negation. Quality, insofar as it counts as distinguished, as being, is reality; it, as afflicted with a negation, is negation in general, likewise a quality, but one which counts as a lack and further determines itself as limit, bound.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"20.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0004","text":"Both are a determinate being, but in reality, as quality with the emphasis that it is a being, it is concealed that it contains determinacy, hence also negation; reality therefore counts only as something positive, from which negation, limitation, lack are supposed to be excluded. Negation, taken as mere lack, would be that which is nothing; but it is a determinate being, a quality determined only with a non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"20.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BQT0:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"757a354cffb6dcdc7abaa0a869bcf92db6329de49276ed8f5ccef5df8e460e07","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Qualität."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Qualität.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2","title":"Remark.","order":21,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_2","text":"Realität kann ein vieldeutiges Wort zu seyn scheinen, weil es von verschiedenen, ja entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen gebraucht wird. Im philosophischen Sinne wird etwa von bloß empirischer Realität als einem werthlosen Daseyn gesprochen. Wenn aber von Gedanken, Begriffen, Theorien gesagt wird, sie haben keine Realität, so heißt dieß, daß ihnen keine Wirklichkeit zukomme; an sich oder im Begriffe könne die Idee einer platonischen Republik z.B. wohl wahr seyn. Der Idee wird hier ihr Werth nicht abgesprochen, und sie neben der Realität auch belassen. Aber gegen sogenannte bloße Ideen, gegen bloße Begriffe gilt das Reelle als das allein Wahrhafte.—Der Sinn, in welchem das eine Mal dem äußerlichen Daseyn die Entscheidung über die Wahrheit eines Inhalts zugeschrieben wird, ist ebenso einseitig, als wenn die Idee, das Wesen oder auch die innere Empfindung als gleichgültig gegen das äußerliche Daseyn vorgestellt und gar für um so vortrefflicher gehalten wird, je mehr es von der Realität entfernt sey.\n\nBei dem Ausdrucke: Realität ist der sonstige metaphysische Begriff von Gott, der vornehmlich dem sogenannten ontologischen Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes zu Grunde gelegt wurde, zu erwähnen. Gott wurde als der Inbegriff aller Realitäten bestimmt, und von diesem Inbegriffe gesagt, daß er keinen Widerspruch in sich enthalte, daß keine der Realitäten die andere aufhebe; denn eine Realität sey nur als eine Vollkommenheit, als ein Affirmatives zu nehmen, das keine Negation enthalte. Somit seyen die Realitäten sich nicht entgegengesetzt und widersprechen sich nicht.\n\nBei diesem Begriffe der Realität wird angenommen, daß sie dann noch bleibe, wenn alle Negation weggedacht werde; damit wird aber alle Bestimmtheit derselben aufgehoben. Die Realität ist Qualität, Daseyn; damit enthält sie das Moment des Negativen, und ist allein dadurch das Bestimmte, das sie ist. Im sogenannten eminenten Sinne oder als unendliche,—in der gewöhnlichen Bedeutung des Worts,—wie sie genommen werden soll, wird sie ins Bestimmungslose erweitert, und verliert ihre Bedeutung. Die Güte Gottes soll nicht Güte im gewöhnlichen, sondern im eminenten Sinne, nicht verschieden von der Gerechtigkeit, sondern durch sie temperirt seyn, (ein leibnitzischer Vermittelungs-Ausdruck) so wie umgekehrt die Gerechtigkeit durch die Güte; so ist weder Güte mehr Güte, noch Gerechtigkeit mehr Gerechtigkeit. Die Macht solle durch die Weisheit temperirt seyn, aber so ist sie nicht Macht als solche, denn sie wäre jener unterworfen,—die Weisheit solle zur Macht erweitert seyn, aber so verschwindet sie als den Zweck und Maaß bestimmende Weisheit. Der wahre Begriff des Unendlichen und dessen absolute Einheit, der sich später ergeben wird, ist nicht als ein Temperiren, gegenseitiges Beschränken oder Vermischen zu fassen, als welches eine oberflächliche, in unbestimmtem Nebel gehaltene Beziehung ist, mit der sich nur begriffloses Vorstellen begnügen kann.—Die Realität, wie sie in jener Definition Gottes als bestimmte Qualität genommen wird, über ihre Bestimmtheit hinausgeführt, hört auf Realität zu seyn; sie wird zum abstrakten Seyn; Gott als das rein Reale in allem Realen, oder als Inbegriff aller Realitäten, ist dasselbe Bestimmungs- und Gehaltlose, was das leere Absolute, in dem alles Eins ist.\n\nWird dagegen die Realität in ihrer Bestimmtheit genommen, so wird, da sie wesentlich das Moment des Negativen enthält, der Inbegriff aller Realitäten ebenso sehr zu einem Inbegriffe aller Negationen, dem Inbegriffe aller Widersprüche, zunächst etwa zur absoluten Macht, in der alles Bestimmte absorbirt ist, aber da sie selbst nur ist, insofern sie noch ein von ihr nicht Aufgehobenes sich gegenüber hat, so wird sie, indem sie zur ausgeführten, schrankenlosen Macht erweitert gedacht wird, zum abstrakten Nichts. Jenes Reale in allem Realen, das Seyn in allem Daseyn, welches den Begriff Gottes ausdrücken soll, ist nichts anderes, als das abstrakte Seyn, dasselbe was das Nichts ist.\n\nDie Bestimmtheit ist die Negation als affirmativ gesetzt, ist der Satz des Spinoza: Omnis determinatio est negatio, dieser Satz ist von unendlicher Wichtigkeit; nur ist die Negation als solche die formlose Abstraktion; der spekulativen Philosophie muß aber nicht Schuld gegeben werden, daß ihr die Negation oder das Nichts ein Letztes sey; dieß ist es ihr so wenig als die Realität das Wahrhafte.\n\nVon diesem Satze, daß die Bestimmtheit Negation ist, ist die Einheit der Spinozistischen Substanz, oder daß nur Eine Substanz ist,—die nothwendige Konsequenz. Denken und Seyn oder Ausdehnung, die zwei Bestimmungen, die Spinoza nämlich vor sich hat, mußte er in dieser Einheit in eins setzen, denn als bestimmte Realitäten, sind sie Negationen, deren Unendlichkeit ihre Einheit ist; nach Spinozas Definition, wovon weiter unten, ist die Unendlichkeit von Etwas seine Affirmation. Er begriff sie daher als Attribute, d. h. als solche, die nicht ein besonderes Bestehen, ein An-und-für-sich-Seyn haben, sondern nur als aufgehobene, als Momente sind; oder vielmehr sind sie ihm nicht einmal Momente, denn die Substanz ist das in ihr selbst ganz bestimmungslose, und die Attribute sind, wie auch die Modi, Unterscheidungen, die ein äußerer Verstand macht.—Eben so kann die Substantialität der Individuen, nicht gegen jenen Satz bestehen. Das Individuum ist Beziehung auf sich dadurch, daß es allein Anderen Grenzen setzt; aber diese Grenzen sind damit auch Grenzen seiner selbst, Beziehungen auf Anderes, es hat sein Daseyn nicht in ihm selbst. Das Individuum ist wohl mehr als nur das nach allen Seiten beschränkte, aber dieß Mehr gehört in eine andere Sphäre des Begriffs; in der Metaphysik des Seyns ist es ein schlechthin bestimmtes; und daß ein solches, daß das Endliche als solches an und für sich sey, dagegen macht sich die Bestimmtheit wesentlich als Negation geltend, und reißt es in dieselbe negative Bewegung des Verstandes, welche alles in der abstrakten Einheit, der Substanz, verschwinden läßt.\n\nDie Negation steht unmittelbar der Realität gegenüber; weiterhin in der eigentlichen Sphäre der reflektirten Bestimmungen, wird sie dem Positiven entgegengesetzt, welches die auf die Negation reflektirende Realität ist,—die Realität, an der das Negative scheint, das in der Realität als solcher noch versteckt ist.\n\nDie Qualität ist erst in der Rücksicht vornehmlich Eigenschaft, als sie in einer äußerlichen Beziehung sich als immanente Bestimmung zeigt. Unter Eigenschaften z.B. von Kräutern versteht man Bestimmungen, die einem Etwas nicht nur überhaupt eigen sind, sondern insofern es sich dadurch in der Beziehung auf andere auf eine eigenthümliche Weise erhält, die fremden in ihm gesetzten Einwirkungen nicht in sich gewähren läßt, sondern seine eigene Bestimmungen in dem Anderen,—ob es dieß zwar nicht von sich abhält, —geltend macht. Die mehr ruhenden Bestimmtheiten, z.B. Figur, Gestalt, nennt man dagegen nicht wohl Eigenschaften, auch etwa nicht Qualitäten, insofern sie als veränderlich, mit dem Seyn nicht identisch vorgestellt werden.\n\nDie Qualirung oder Inqualirung, ein Ausdruck der Jacob-Böhmischen, einer in die Tiefe aber in eine trübe Tiefe gehenden Philosophie, bedeutet die Bewegung einer Qualität (der sauren, herben, feurigen u. s.f.) in ihr selbst, insofern sie in ihrer negativen Natur (in ihrer Qual) sich aus anderem setzt und befestigt, überhaupt die Unruhe ihrer an ihr selbst ist, nach der sie nur im Kampfe sich hervorbringt und erhält.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0001","text":"Realität kann ein vieldeutiges Wort zu seyn scheinen, weil es von verschiedenen, ja entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen gebraucht wird. Im philosophischen Sinne wird etwa von bloß empirischer Realität als einem werthlosen Daseyn gesprochen. Wenn aber von Gedanken, Begriffen, Theorien gesagt wird, sie haben keine Realität, so heißt dieß, daß ihnen keine Wirklichkeit zukomme; an sich oder im Begriffe könne die Idee einer platonischen Republik z.B. wohl wahr seyn. Der Idee wird hier ihr Werth nicht abgesprochen, und sie neben der Realität auch belassen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"21.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0002","text":"Aber gegen sogenannte bloße Ideen, gegen bloße Begriffe gilt das Reelle als das allein Wahrhafte.—Der Sinn, in welchem das eine Mal dem äußerlichen Daseyn die Entscheidung über die Wahrheit eines Inhalts zugeschrieben wird, ist ebenso einseitig, als wenn die Idee, das Wesen oder auch die innere Empfindung als gleichgültig gegen das äußerliche Daseyn vorgestellt und gar für um so vortrefflicher gehalten wird, je mehr es von der Realität entfernt sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"21.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0003","text":"Bei dem Ausdrucke: Realität ist der sonstige metaphysische Begriff von Gott, der vornehmlich dem sogenannten ontologischen Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes zu Grunde gelegt wurde, zu erwähnen. Gott wurde als der Inbegriff aller Realitäten bestimmt, und von diesem Inbegriffe gesagt, daß er keinen Widerspruch in sich enthalte, daß keine der Realitäten die andere aufhebe; denn eine Realität sey nur als eine Vollkommenheit, als ein Affirmatives zu nehmen, das keine Negation enthalte. Somit seyen die Realitäten sich nicht entgegengesetzt und widersprechen sich nicht.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"21.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0004","text":"Bei diesem Begriffe der Realität wird angenommen, daß sie dann noch bleibe, wenn alle Negation weggedacht werde; damit wird aber alle Bestimmtheit derselben aufgehoben. Die Realität ist Qualität, Daseyn; damit enthält sie das Moment des Negativen, und ist allein dadurch das Bestimmte, das sie ist. Im sogenannten eminenten Sinne oder als unendliche,—in der gewöhnlichen Bedeutung des Worts,—wie sie genommen werden soll, wird sie ins Bestimmungslose erweitert, und verliert ihre Bedeutung. Die Güte Gottes soll nicht Güte im gewöhnlichen, sondern im eminenten Sinne, nicht verschieden von der Gerechtigkeit, sondern durch sie temperirt seyn, (ein leibnitzischer Vermittelungs-Ausdruck) so wie umgekehrt die Gerechtigkeit durch die Güte; so ist weder Güte mehr Güte, noch Gerechtigkeit mehr Gerechtigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"21.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0005","text":"Die Macht solle durch die Weisheit temperirt seyn, aber so ist sie nicht Macht als solche, denn sie wäre jener unterworfen,—die Weisheit solle zur Macht erweitert seyn, aber so verschwindet sie als den Zweck und Maaß bestimmende Weisheit. Der wahre Begriff des Unendlichen und dessen absolute Einheit, der sich später ergeben wird, ist nicht als ein Temperiren, gegenseitiges Beschränken oder Vermischen zu fassen, als welches eine oberflächliche, in unbestimmtem Nebel gehaltene Beziehung ist, mit der sich nur begriffloses Vorstellen begnügen kann.—Die Realität, wie sie in jener Definition Gottes als bestimmte Qualität genommen wird, über ihre Bestimmtheit hinausgeführt, hört auf Realität zu seyn; sie wird zum abstrakten Seyn; Gott als das rein Reale in allem Realen, oder als Inbegriff aller Realitäten, ist dasselbe Bestimmungs- und Gehaltlose, was das leere Absolute, in dem alles Eins ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"21.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0006","text":"Wird dagegen die Realität in ihrer Bestimmtheit genommen, so wird, da sie wesentlich das Moment des Negativen enthält, der Inbegriff aller Realitäten ebenso sehr zu einem Inbegriffe aller Negationen, dem Inbegriffe aller Widersprüche, zunächst etwa zur absoluten Macht, in der alles Bestimmte absorbirt ist, aber da sie selbst nur ist, insofern sie noch ein von ihr nicht Aufgehobenes sich gegenüber hat, so wird sie, indem sie zur ausgeführten, schrankenlosen Macht erweitert gedacht wird, zum abstrakten Nichts. Jenes Reale in allem Realen, das Seyn in allem Daseyn, welches den Begriff Gottes ausdrücken soll, ist nichts anderes, als das abstrakte Seyn, dasselbe was das Nichts ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"21.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0007","text":"Die Bestimmtheit ist die Negation als affirmativ gesetzt, ist der Satz des Spinoza: Omnis determinatio est negatio, dieser Satz ist von unendlicher Wichtigkeit; nur ist die Negation als solche die formlose Abstraktion; der spekulativen Philosophie muß aber nicht Schuld gegeben werden, daß ihr die Negation oder das Nichts ein Letztes sey; dieß ist es ihr so wenig als die Realität das Wahrhafte.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"21.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0008","text":"Von diesem Satze, daß die Bestimmtheit Negation ist, ist die Einheit der Spinozistischen Substanz, oder daß nur Eine Substanz ist,—die nothwendige Konsequenz. Denken und Seyn oder Ausdehnung, die zwei Bestimmungen, die Spinoza nämlich vor sich hat, mußte er in dieser Einheit in eins setzen, denn als bestimmte Realitäten, sind sie Negationen, deren Unendlichkeit ihre Einheit ist; nach Spinozas Definition, wovon weiter unten, ist die Unendlichkeit von Etwas seine Affirmation. Er begriff sie daher als Attribute, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"21.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0009","text":"als solche, die nicht ein besonderes Bestehen, ein An-und-für-sich-Seyn haben, sondern nur als aufgehobene, als Momente sind; oder vielmehr sind sie ihm nicht einmal Momente, denn die Substanz ist das in ihr selbst ganz bestimmungslose, und die Attribute sind, wie auch die Modi, Unterscheidungen, die ein äußerer Verstand macht.—Eben so kann die Substantialität der Individuen, nicht gegen jenen Satz bestehen. Das Individuum ist Beziehung auf sich dadurch, daß es allein Anderen Grenzen setzt; aber diese Grenzen sind damit auch Grenzen seiner selbst, Beziehungen auf Anderes, es hat sein Daseyn nicht in ihm selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"21.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0010","text":"Das Individuum ist wohl mehr als nur das nach allen Seiten beschränkte, aber dieß Mehr gehört in eine andere Sphäre des Begriffs; in der Metaphysik des Seyns ist es ein schlechthin bestimmtes; und daß ein solches, daß das Endliche als solches an und für sich sey, dagegen macht sich die Bestimmtheit wesentlich als Negation geltend, und reißt es in dieselbe negative Bewegung des Verstandes, welche alles in der abstrakten Einheit, der Substanz, verschwinden läßt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"21.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0011","text":"Die Negation steht unmittelbar der Realität gegenüber; weiterhin in der eigentlichen Sphäre der reflektirten Bestimmungen, wird sie dem Positiven entgegengesetzt, welches die auf die Negation reflektirende Realität ist,—die Realität, an der das Negative scheint, das in der Realität als solcher noch versteckt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"21.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0012","text":"Die Qualität ist erst in der Rücksicht vornehmlich Eigenschaft, als sie in einer äußerlichen Beziehung sich als immanente Bestimmung zeigt. Unter Eigenschaften z.B. von Kräutern versteht man Bestimmungen, die einem Etwas nicht nur überhaupt eigen sind, sondern insofern es sich dadurch in der Beziehung auf andere auf eine eigenthümliche Weise erhält, die fremden in ihm gesetzten Einwirkungen nicht in sich gewähren läßt, sondern seine eigene Bestimmungen in dem Anderen,—ob es dieß zwar nicht von sich abhält, —geltend macht. Die mehr ruhenden Bestimmtheiten, z.B. Figur, Gestalt, nennt man dagegen nicht wohl Eigenschaften, auch etwa nicht Qualitäten, insofern sie als veränderlich, mit dem Seyn nicht identisch vorgestellt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"21.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0013","text":"Die Qualirung oder Inqualirung, ein Ausdruck der Jacob-Böhmischen, einer in die Tiefe aber in eine trübe Tiefe gehenden Philosophie, bedeutet die Bewegung einer Qualität (der sauren, herben, feurigen u. s.f.) in ihr selbst, insofern sie in ihrer negativen Natur (in ihrer Qual) sich aus anderem setzt und befestigt, überhaupt die Unruhe ihrer an ihr selbst ist, nach der sie nur im Kampfe sich hervorbringt und erhält.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"21.13"}],"sha256":"db892f10c963a381e24f772100fcb3e53da0bde350505b5381f55417db7ccfb2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102019555744Z_65d75e2c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"db892f10c963a381e24f772100fcb3e53da0bde350505b5381f55417db7ccfb2","sha256":"c08ef0ff3f8e62b2ca4ff6850098854cef4f74e5bc487482d31312a07016ecb2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:20:19.555764+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0001","text":"Reality may seem to be an ambiguous word, because it is used of different, indeed opposite determinations. In the philosophical sense, one speaks, for example, of merely empirical reality as a worthless existence. But when it is said of thoughts, concepts, theories that they have no reality, this means that no actuality belongs to them; in itself or in the concept, the idea of a Platonic republic, for example, may indeed be true. Here its value is not denied to the idea, and it is also left alongside reality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"21.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0002","text":"But in opposition to so-called mere ideas, to mere concepts, the real counts as the sole truth.—The sense in which, on one occasion, external existence is ascribed the decision concerning the truth of a content is just as one-sided as when the idea, essence, or even inner feeling is represented as indifferent to external existence and even held to be all the more excellent the further it is removed from reality.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"21.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0003","text":"With the expression: reality, mention must be made of the otherwise metaphysical concept of God, which was laid at the basis principally of the so-called ontological proof of the existence of God. God was determined as the sum-total of all realities, and it was said of this sum-total that it contains no contradiction within itself, that none of the realities cancels the other; for a reality is to be taken only as a perfection, as an affirmative, which contains no negation. Thus the realities are not opposed to one another and do not contradict one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"21.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0004","text":"In this concept of reality it is assumed that it still remains when all negation is thought away; but thereby all its determinacy is aufgehoben. Reality is quality, existence; thereby it contains the moment of the negative, and only through this is it the determinate that it is. In the so-called eminent sense, or as infinite,—in the ordinary meaning of the word,—as it is supposed to be taken, it is expanded into indeterminacy and loses its meaning. The goodness of God is supposed not to be goodness in the ordinary but in the eminent sense, not distinct from justice but tempered by it (a Leibnizian expression of mediation), just as, conversely, justice is tempered by goodness; thus goodness is no longer goodness, nor justice justice.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"21.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0005","text":"Power is supposed to be tempered by wisdom, but thus it is not power as such, for it would be subject to the latter,—wisdom is supposed to be expanded into power, but thus it disappears as wisdom determining end and measure. The true concept of the infinite and its absolute unity, which will emerge later, is not to be grasped as a tempering, reciprocal limiting, or mixing, which is a superficial relation kept in an indeterminate mist, with which only conceptless representation can content itself.—Reality, as it is taken in that definition of God as determinate quality, carried beyond its determinacy, ceases to be reality; it becomes abstract being; God as the purely real in all that is real, or as the sum-total of all realities, is the same devoid of determinacy and content as the empty Absolute, in which everything is one.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"21.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0006","text":"If, on the other hand, reality is taken in its determinacy, then, since it essentially contains the moment of the negative, the sum-total of all realities becomes just as much a sum-total of all negations, the sum-total of all contradictions, at first, for example, absolute power, in which everything determinate is absorbed; but since it itself is only insofar as it still has something not cancelled by it over against itself, then, as it is thought expanded into consummate, boundless power, it becomes abstract nothing. That real in all that is real, the being in all existence, which is supposed to express the concept of God, is nothing other than abstract being, the same as nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"21.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0007","text":"Determinacy is negation posited as affirmative; this is Spinoza's proposition: Omnis determinatio est negatio; this proposition is of infinite importance; only, negation as such is formless abstraction; but speculative philosophy must not be blamed for taking negation or nothing as an ultimate; it does so just as little as it takes reality to be the truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"21.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0008","text":"From this proposition, that determinacy is negation, the unity of the Spinozistic substance, or that there is only One substance,—is the necessary consequence. Thought and being or extension, the two determinations which Spinoza has before him, he had to posit as one in this unity, for as determinate realities they are negations, whose infinity is their unity; according to Spinoza's definition, of which more below, the infinity of something is its affirmation. He therefore conceived them as attributes, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"21.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0009","text":"as such as do not have a particular subsistence, a being-in-and-for-itself, but are only as sublated, as moments; or rather, for him they are not even moments, for substance is that which is wholly devoid of determinacy within itself, and the attributes, like the modes also, are distinctions made by an external understanding.—Likewise, the substantiality of individuals cannot stand against that proposition. The individual is relation to itself in that it sets limits only to others; but these limits are thereby also limits of itself, relations to others; it does not have its existence in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"21.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0010","text":"The individual is indeed more than merely that which is limited on all sides, but this more belongs to another sphere of the concept; in the metaphysics of being it is an absolutely determinate [thing]; and against the claim that such a thing, that the finite as such, is in and for itself, determinacy essentially asserts itself as negation and tears it into the same negative movement of the understanding which lets everything vanish in the abstract unity, substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"21.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0011","text":"Negation stands immediately opposed to reality; further on, in the proper sphere of reflected determinations, it is opposed to the positive, which is reality reflected upon negation,—reality in which the negative appears, which is still concealed in reality as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"21.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0012","text":"Quality is primarily property only in the respect that, in an external relation, it shows itself as an immanent determination. By properties, for example, of herbs, one understands determinations which are not merely generally proper to a something, but insofar as it thereby maintains itself in relation to others in a peculiar way, does not allow the alien effects posited in it to take place within it, but asserts its own determinations in the other,—although it does not indeed keep this other away from itself. The more quiescent determinacies, e.g. figure, shape, on the other hand, are not properly called properties, nor perhaps qualities either, insofar as they are represented as mutable, as not identical with being.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"21.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0013","text":"Qualitation or inqualitation, an expression of the Jacob-Böhmean philosophy, a philosophy that goes into the depths, but into a turbid depth, signifies the movement of a quality (the sour, harsh, fiery, and so forth) within itself, insofar as, in its negative nature (in its torment), it posits and strengthens itself out of another; in general, the unrest of its being at itself, according to which it brings itself forth and maintains itself only in struggle.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"21.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_2:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"f1d62403ea16a2bdcae33a993fda0b0cf537a74fe33f74ac932dabfc17da282f","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW","title":"c. Something.","order":22,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CETW","text":"An dem Daseyn ist seine Bestimmtheit als Qualität unterschieden worden; an dieser als daseyender ist der Unterschied,—der Realität und der Negation. So sehr nun diese Unterschiede an dem Daseyn vorhanden sind, so sehr sind sie auch nichtig und aufgehoben. Die Realität enthält selbst die Negation, ist Daseyn, nicht unbestimmtes, abstraktes Seyn. Ebenso ist die Negation Daseyn, nicht das abstraktseynsollende Nichts, sondern hier gesetzt wie es an sich ist, als seyend, dem Daseyn angehörig. So ist die Qualität überhaupt nicht vom Daseyn getrennt, welches nur bestimmtes, qualitatives Seyn ist.\n\nDieses Aufheben der Unterscheidung ist mehr als ein bloßes Zurücknehmen und äußeres Wieder-Weglassen derselben oder als ein einfaches Zurückkehren zum einfachen Anfange, dem Daseyn als solchem. Der Unterschied kann nicht weggelassen werden; denn er ist. Das Faktische, was also vorhanden ist, ist das Daseyn überhaupt, Unterschied an ihm, und das Aufheben dieses Unterschiedes; das Daseyn nicht als unterschiedlos, wie Anfangs, sondern als wieder sich selbst gleich, durch Aufheben des Unterschieds, die Einfachheit des Daseyns vermittelt durch dieses Aufheben. Dieß Aufgehobenseyn des Unterschieds ist die eigne Bestimmtheit des Daseyns; so ist es Insichseyn; das Daseyn ist Daseyendes, Etwas.\n\nDas Etwas ist die erste Negation der Negation, als einfache seyende Beziehung auf sich. Daseyn, Leben, Denken u.s.f. bestimmt sich wesentlich zum Daseyenden, Lebendigen, Denkenden (Ich) u.s.f. Diese Bestimmung ist von der höchsten Wichtigkeit, um nicht bei dem Daseyn, Leben, Denken u.s.f. auch nicht bei der Gottheit (statt Gottes), als Allgemeinheiten stehen zu bleiben. Etwas gilt der Vorstellung mit Recht als ein Reelles. Jedoch ist Etwas noch eine sehr oberflächliche Bestimmung; wie Realität und Negation, das Daseyn und dessen Bestimmtheit zwar nicht mehr die leeren: Seyn und Nichts, aber ganz abstrakte Bestimmungen sind. Deswegen sind sie auch die gegenläufigsten Ausdrücke, und die philosophisch nicht gebildete Reflexion gebraucht sie am meisten, gießt ihre Unterscheidungen darein, und meint daran etwas recht gut und fest Bestimmtes zu haben. —Das Negative des Negativen ist als Etwas nur der Anfang des Subjekts;—das Insichseyn nur erst ganz unbestimmt. Es bestimmt sich fernerhin zunächst als Fürsichseyendes und sofort bis es erst im Begriff die konkrete Intensität des Subjekts erhält. Allen diesen Bestimmungen liegt die negative Einheit mit sich zu Grunde. Aber dabei ist die Negation als erste, als Negation überhaupt wohl zu unterscheiden von der zweiten, der Negation der Negation, welche die konkrete, absolute Negativität, wie jene erste dagegen nur die abstrakte Negativität ist.\n\nEtwas ist seyend als die Negation der Negation; denn diese ist das Wiederherstellen der einfachen Beziehung auf sich;—aber ebenso ist damit Etwas, die Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst. Schon in dem Einfachen des Etwas, dann noch bestimmter im Fürsichseyn, Subjekt u.s. f. ist die Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst vorhanden, bereits auch im Werden nur die ganz abstrakte Vermittelung; die Vermittelung mit sich ist im Etwas gesetzt, insofern es als einfaches Identisches bestimmt ist.—Auf das Vorhandenseyn der Vermittelung überhaupt kann gegen das Princip der behaupteten bloßen Unmittelbarkeit des Wissens, von welcher die Vermittelung ausgeschlossen seyn solle, aufmerksam gemacht werden; aber es bedarf weiterhin nicht besonders auf das Moment der Vermittelung aufmerksam zu machen; denn es befindet sich überall und allenthalben, in jedem Begriffe.\n\nDiese Vermittelung mit sich, die Etwas an sich ist, hat nur als Negation der Negation genommen, keine konkrete Bestimmungen zu ihren Seiten; so fällt sie in die einfache Einheit zusammen, welche Seyn ist. Etwas ist, und ist denn auch Daseyendes; es ist an sich ferner auch Werden, das aber nicht mehr nur Seyn und Nichts zu seinen Momenten hat. Das eine derselben, das Seyn, ist nun Daseyn und weiter Daseyendes. Das zweite ist ebenso ein Daseyendes, aber als Negatives des Etwas bestimmt,—ein Anderes. Das Etwas als Werden ist ein Übergehen, dessen Momente selbst Etwas sind, und das darum Veränderung ist;—ein bereits konkret gewordenes Werden.—Das Etwas aber verändert sich zunächst nur in seinem Begriffe; es ist noch nicht so als vermittelnd und vermittelt gesetzt; zunächst nur als sich in seiner Beziehung auf sich einfach erhaltend, und das Negative seiner als ein ebenso qualitatives, nur ein Anderes überhaupt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0001","text":"An dem Daseyn ist seine Bestimmtheit als Qualität unterschieden worden; an dieser als daseyender ist der Unterschied,—der Realität und der Negation. So sehr nun diese Unterschiede an dem Daseyn vorhanden sind, so sehr sind sie auch nichtig und aufgehoben. Die Realität enthält selbst die Negation, ist Daseyn, nicht unbestimmtes, abstraktes Seyn. Ebenso ist die Negation Daseyn, nicht das abstraktseynsollende Nichts, sondern hier gesetzt wie es an sich ist, als seyend, dem Daseyn angehörig. So ist die Qualität überhaupt nicht vom Daseyn getrennt, welches nur bestimmtes, qualitatives Seyn ist.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Dieses Aufheben der Unterscheidung ist mehr als ein bloßes Zurücknehmen und äußeres Wieder-Weglassen derselben oder als ein einfaches Zurückkehren zum einfachen Anfange, dem Daseyn als solchem. Der Unterschied kann nicht weggelassen werden; denn er ist. Das Faktische, was also vorhanden ist, ist das Daseyn überhaupt, Unterschied an ihm, und das Aufheben dieses Unterschiedes; das Daseyn nicht als unterschiedlos, wie Anfangs, sondern als wieder sich selbst gleich, durch Aufheben des Unterschieds, die Einfachheit des Daseyns vermittelt durch dieses Aufheben. Dieß Aufgehobenseyn des Unterschieds ist die eigne Bestimmtheit des Daseyns; so ist es Insichseyn; das Daseyn ist Daseyendes, Etwas.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Das Etwas ist die erste Negation der Negation, als einfache seyende Beziehung auf sich. Daseyn, Leben, Denken u.s.f. bestimmt sich wesentlich zum Daseyenden, Lebendigen, Denkenden (Ich) u.s.f. Diese Bestimmung ist von der höchsten Wichtigkeit, um nicht bei dem Daseyn, Leben, Denken u.s.f. auch nicht bei der Gottheit (statt Gottes), als Allgemeinheiten stehen zu bleiben. Etwas gilt der Vorstellung mit Recht als ein Reelles. Jedoch ist Etwas noch eine sehr oberflächliche Bestimmung; wie Realität und Negation, das Daseyn und dessen Bestimmtheit zwar nicht mehr die leeren: Seyn und Nichts, aber ganz abstrakte Bestimmungen sind. Deswegen sind sie auch die gegenläufigsten Ausdrücke, und die philosophisch nicht gebildete Reflexion gebraucht sie am meisten, gießt ihre Unterscheidungen darein, und meint daran etwas recht gut und fest Bestimmtes zu haben. —Das Negative des Negativen ist als Etwas nur der Anfang des Subjekts;—das Insichseyn nur erst ganz unbestimmt. Es bestimmt sich fernerhin zunächst als Fürsichseyendes und sofort bis es erst im Begriff die konkrete Intensität des Subjekts erhält. Allen diesen Bestimmungen liegt die negative Einheit mit sich zu Grunde. Aber dabei ist die Negation als erste, als Negation überhaupt wohl zu unterscheiden von der zweiten, der Negation der Negation, welche die konkrete, absolute Negativität, wie jene erste dagegen nur die abstrakte Negativität ist.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Etwas ist seyend als die Negation der Negation; denn diese ist das Wiederherstellen der einfachen Beziehung auf sich;—aber ebenso ist damit Etwas, die Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst. Schon in dem Einfachen des Etwas, dann noch bestimmter im Fürsichseyn, Subjekt u.s. f. ist die Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst vorhanden, bereits auch im Werden nur die ganz abstrakte Vermittelung; die Vermittelung mit sich ist im Etwas gesetzt, insofern es als einfaches Identisches bestimmt ist.—Auf das Vorhandenseyn der Vermittelung überhaupt kann gegen das Princip der behaupteten bloßen Unmittelbarkeit des Wissens, von welcher die Vermittelung ausgeschlossen seyn solle, aufmerksam gemacht werden; aber es bedarf weiterhin nicht besonders auf das Moment der Vermittelung aufmerksam zu machen; denn es befindet sich überall und allenthalben, in jedem Begriffe.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Diese Vermittelung mit sich, die Etwas an sich ist, hat nur als Negation der Negation genommen, keine konkrete Bestimmungen zu ihren Seiten; so fällt sie in die einfache Einheit zusammen, welche Seyn ist. Etwas ist, und ist denn auch Daseyendes; es ist an sich ferner auch Werden, das aber nicht mehr nur Seyn und Nichts zu seinen Momenten hat. Das eine derselben, das Seyn, ist nun Daseyn und weiter Daseyendes. Das zweite ist ebenso ein Daseyendes, aber als Negatives des Etwas bestimmt,—ein Anderes. Das Etwas als Werden ist ein Übergehen, dessen Momente selbst Etwas sind, und das darum Veränderung ist;—ein bereits konkret gewordenes Werden.—Das Etwas aber verändert sich zunächst nur in seinem Begriffe; es ist noch nicht so als vermittelnd und vermittelt gesetzt; zunächst nur als sich in seiner Beziehung auf sich einfach erhaltend, und das Negative seiner als ein ebenso qualitatives, nur ein Anderes überhaupt.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"d4522b781d55dbfdbf552c80eff225fb66fc5724589285021317d5f06928e334","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102030600988Z_f368d095","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Something.","source_sha256":"d4522b781d55dbfdbf552c80eff225fb66fc5724589285021317d5f06928e334","sha256":"09ca30f29d5c2a32b7f4e851f888414666077f2d360ac219e9ee6c8101e6188d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:20:30.601012+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0001","text":"In determinate being, its determinacy has been distinguished as quality; in this, as existing, there is the distinction—of reality and negation. Now, as much as these distinctions are present in determinate being, so much are they null and sublated. Reality itself contains negation, is determinate being, not indeterminate, abstract Being. Likewise, negation is determinate being, not the Nothing that ought to be abstract, but posited here as it is in itself, as being, belonging to determinate being. Thus quality in general is not separated from determinate being, which is only determinate, qualitative Being.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0002","text":"This sublation of the distinction is more than a mere withdrawal and external removal of it once again, or than a simple return to the simple beginning, to determinate being as such. The distinction cannot be omitted; for it is. What is factually present, therefore, is determinate being in general, distinction within it, and the sublation of this distinction; determinate being not as distinctionless, as at the beginning, but as once more equal to itself through the sublation of the distinction, the simplicity of determinate being mediated by this sublation. This being-sublated of the distinction is the determinacy proper to determinate being; thus it is being-within-itself; determinate being is a being-there, a something.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102030600988Z_f368d095:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Something is the first negation of negation, as simple being relation to itself. Determinate being, life, thought, etc. essentially determine themselves as being-there, living, thinking (I), etc. This determination is of the highest importance, so as not to remain with determinate being, life, thought, etc., nor with divinity (instead of God), as universalities. Something rightly counts for representation as something real. Yet something is still a very superficial determination; like reality and negation, determinate being and its determinacy, though no longer the empty determinations Being and Nothing, are nevertheless wholly abstract determinations. For this reason they are also the most contrary expressions, and reflection not philosophically cultivated employs them most of all, pours its distinctions into them, and imagines that in them it has something quite good and firmly determinate.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102030600988Z_f368d095:DISPLAY-0004","text":"—The negative of the negative, as something, is only the beginning of the subject;—being-within-itself is at first still wholly indeterminate. It further determines itself next as being-for-itself, and then onwards until only in the Concept does it receive the concrete intensity of the subject. At the basis of all these determinations lies negative unity with itself. But negation as the first, as negation in general, is indeed to be distinguished from the second, the negation of negation, which is concrete, absolute negativity, whereas that first, by contrast, is only abstract negativity.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Something is being as the negation of negation; for this is the restoration of the simple relation to itself;—but equally, thereby something is the mediation of itself with itself. Already in the simple [character] of something, then more determinately in being-for-itself, subject, etc., the mediation of itself with itself is present; already in becoming, too, there is only the wholly abstract mediation; mediation with itself is posited in something insofar as it is determined as simple identity.—Attention may be drawn to the presence of mediation in general against the principle of the asserted mere immediacy of knowing, from which mediation is supposed to be excluded; but henceforth there is no need to draw particular attention to the moment of mediation, for it is found everywhere and in all things, in every Concept.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102030600988Z_f368d095:DISPLAY-0006","text":"This mediation with itself, which something is in itself, taken only as negation of negation, has no concrete determinations as its sides; it thus collapses into the simple unity that is Being. Something is, and is then also a being-there; it is in itself further also becoming, but this no longer has merely Being and Nothing as its moments. One of them, Being, is now determinate being and further being-there. The second is likewise a being-there, but determined as the negative of something,—an other.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102030600988Z_f368d095:DISPLAY-0007","text":"Something as becoming is a transition, the moments of which are themselves somethings, and which is therefore alteration;—a becoming that has already become concrete.—But something initially alters itself only in its Concept; it is not yet posited as mediating and mediated; initially only as preserving itself simply in its relation to itself, and its negative as likewise qualitative, only an other in general.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CETW:DISPLAY-0005"]}],"source_digest":"c297aafbf95d78f845117b5a67958c1b7355fcf6f4b2c91d05a00df7665ffc0e","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Etwas."}],"original_title":"c. Etwas.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0","title":"B. Finitude.","order":23,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDE0","text":"a. Etwas und Anderes; sie sind zunächst gleichgültig gegeneinander; ein Anderes ist auch ein unmittelbar Daseyendes, ein Etwas; die Negation fällt so außer beiden. Etwas ist an sich gegen sein Seyn-für anderes. Aber die Bestimmtheit gehört auch seinem Ansich an, und ist\n\nb. dessen Bestimmung, welche ebenso sehr in Beschaffenheit übergeht, die mit jener identisch das immanente und zugleich negirte Seyn-für-Anders, die Grenze des Etwas ausmacht, welche\n\nc. die immanente Bestimmung des Etwas selbst, und dieses somit das Endliche ist.\n\nIn der ersten Abtheilung, worin das Daseyn überhaupt betrachtet wurde, hatte dieses als zunächst aufgenommen, die Bestimmung des Seyenden. Die Momente seiner Entwicklung, Qualität und Etwas, sind darum ebenso affirmativer Bestimmung. In dieser Abtheilung hingegen entwickelt sich die negative Bestimmung, die im Daseyn liegt, welche dort nur erst Negation überhaupt, erste Negation war, nun aber zu dem Puncte des In-sichseyns des Etwas, zur Negation der Negation bestimmt ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0001","text":"a. Etwas und Anderes; sie sind zunächst gleichgültig gegeneinander; ein Anderes ist auch ein unmittelbar Daseyendes, ein Etwas; die Negation fällt so außer beiden. Etwas ist an sich gegen sein Seyn-für anderes. Aber die Bestimmtheit gehört auch seinem Ansich an, und ist","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"23.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0002","text":"b. dessen Bestimmung, welche ebenso sehr in Beschaffenheit übergeht, die mit jener identisch das immanente und zugleich negirte Seyn-für-Anders, die Grenze des Etwas ausmacht, welche","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"23.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0003","text":"c. die immanente Bestimmung des Etwas selbst, und dieses somit das Endliche ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"23.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0004","text":"In der ersten Abtheilung, worin das Daseyn überhaupt betrachtet wurde, hatte dieses als zunächst aufgenommen, die Bestimmung des Seyenden. Die Momente seiner Entwicklung, Qualität und Etwas, sind darum ebenso affirmativer Bestimmung. In dieser Abtheilung hingegen entwickelt sich die negative Bestimmung, die im Daseyn liegt, welche dort nur erst Negation überhaupt, erste Negation war, nun aber zu dem Puncte des In-sichseyns des Etwas, zur Negation der Negation bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"23.4"}],"sha256":"0f8dbc1582a0605506467ec96e5792b365065a81694cf2d0684b29d31c9ada93","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102034092745Z_b6c81dbf","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Finitude.","source_sha256":"0f8dbc1582a0605506467ec96e5792b365065a81694cf2d0684b29d31c9ada93","sha256":"870771561ff7de791d1fc03edfa5803d6bf0e1def8142668a1c401dea1e7d61f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:20:34.092757+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0001","text":"a. Something and Other; they are at first indifferent to one another; an Other is likewise an immediately existing being, a Something; negation thus falls outside both. Something is in itself over against its Being-for-other. But determinateness also belongs to its In-itself, and is","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"23.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0002","text":"b. its determination, which equally passes over into constitution, which, identical with that [determination], constitutes the immanent and at the same time negated Being-for-Other, the limit of Something, which","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"23.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0003","text":"c. is the immanent determination of Something itself, and thus makes it finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"23.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0004","text":"In the first division, in which Existence in general was considered, this, as immediately taken up, had the determination of Being. The moments of its development, quality and Something, are therefore likewise of affirmative determination. In this division, by contrast, the negative determination that lies in Existence develops itself; there it was only negation in general, first negation, but is now determined as the point of the Being-within-itself of Something, as the negation of negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"23.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDE0:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"b83d8a6fead0a91a3f230ef11a3e181ab67f373be9bc8c038b96e4d0a3ebd2b7","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Die Endlichkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Die Endlichkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA","title":"a. Something and an Other.","order":24,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_EUEA","text":"1. Etwas und Anderes sind beide erstens Daseyende oder Etwas.\n\nZweitens ist ebenso jedes ein Anderes. Es ist gleichgültig, welches zuerst und bloß darum Etwas genannt wird; (im Lateinischen, wenn sie in einem Satze vorkommen, heißen beide aliud, oder einer den andern, alius alium; bei einer Gegenseitigkeit ist der Ausdruck: alter alterum analog.) Wenn wir ein Daseyn A nennen, das andere aber B, so ist zunächst B als das Andere bestimmt. Aber A ist ebenso sehr das Andere des B. Beide sind auf gleiche Weise Andere. Um den Unterschied und das als affirmativ zu nehmende Etwas zu fixiren, dient das Dieses. Aber Dieses spricht eben es aus, daß dieß Unterscheiden und Herausheben des einen Etwas ein subjektives, außerhalb des Etwas selbst fallendes Bezeichnen ist. In dieses äußerliche Monstriren fällt die ganze Bestimmtheit; selbst der Ausdruck: Dieses enthält keinen Unterschied; alle und jede Etwas sind gerade so gut Diese, als sie auch Andere sind. Man meint, durch: Dieses, etwas vollkommen bestimmtes auszudrücken; es wird übersehen, daß die Sprache, als Werk des Verstandes, nur Allgemeines ausspricht, außer in dem Namen eines einzelnen Gegenstandes; der individuelle Name ist aber ein Sinnloses in dem Sinne, daß er nicht ein Allgemeines ausdrückt, und erscheint als ein bloß Gesetztes, Willkürliches aus demselben Grunde, wie denn auch Einzelnamen willkürlich angenommen, gegeben oder ebenso verändert werden können.\n\nEs erscheint somit das Andersseyn als eine dem so bestimmten Daseyn fremde Bestimmung, oder das Andere außer dem einen Daseyn; Theils, daß ein Daseyn erst durch das Vergleichen eines Dritten, Theils, daß es nur um des Anderen willen, das außer ihm ist, als anderes bestimmt werde, aber nicht für sich so sey. Zugleich, wie bemerkt worden, bestimmt sich jedes Daseyn, auch für die Vorstellung, ebenso sehr als ein anderes Daseyn, so daß nicht ein Daseyn bleibt, das nur als ein Daseyn bestimmt, das nicht außerhalb eines Daseyns, also nicht selbst ein Anderes wäre.\n\nBeide sind sowohl als Etwas als auch als Anderes bestimmt, hiermit dasselbe und es ist noch kein Unterschied derselben vorhanden. Diese Dieselbigkeit der Bestimmungen fällt aber ebenso nur in die äußere Reflexion, in die Vergleichung beider; aber wie das Andere zunächst gesetzt ist, so ist dasselbe für sich zwar in Beziehung auf das Etwas, aber auch für sich außerhalb desselben.\n\nDrittens ist daher das Andere zu nehmen, als isolirt, in Beziehung auf sich selbst; abstrakt als das Andere,…… des Plato, der es als eins der Momente der Totalität, dem Einen entgegensetzt, und dem Anderen auf diese Weise eine eigne Natur zuschreibt. So ist das Andere allein als solches gefaßt, nicht das Andere von Etwas, sondern das Andere an ihm selbst, d. i. das Andere seiner selbst.—Solches seiner Bestimmung nach Andere ist die physische Natur; sie ist das Andere des Geistes; diese ihre Bestimmung ist so zunächst eine bloße Relativität, wodurch nicht eine Qualität der Natur selbst, sondern nur eine ihr äußerliche Beziehung ausgedrückt wird. Aber indem der Geist das wahrhafte Etwas, und die Natur daher an ihr selbst nur das ist, was sie gegen den Geist ist, so ist, insofern sie für sich genommen wird, ihre Qualität eben dieß, das Andere an ihr selbst, das Außer-sich-seyende (in den Bestimmungen des Raumes, der Zeit, der Materie) zu seyn.\n\nDas Andere für sich ist das Andere an ihm selbst, hiermit das Andere seiner selbst, so das Andere des Anderen,—also das in sich schlechthin Ungleiche, sich Negirende, das sich Verändernde. Aber ebenso bleibt es identisch mit sich, denn dasjenige, in welches es sich veränderte, ist das Andere, das sonst weiter keine Bestimmung hat; aber das sich Verändernde ist auf keine verschiedene Weise, sondern auf dieselbe, ein Anderes zu seyn, bestimmt, es geht daher in demselben nur mit sich zusammen. So ist es gesetzt als in sich Reflektirtes mit Aufheben des Andersseyns; mit sich identisches Etwas, von dem hiermit das Andersseyn, das zugleich Moment desselben ist, ein Unterschiedenes, ihm nicht als Etwas selbst zukommendes ist.\n\n2. Etwas erhält sich in seinem Nichtdaseyn; es ist wesentlich Eins mit ihm, und wesentlich nicht Eins mit ihm.\n\nEs steht also in Beziehung auf sein Andersseyn; es ist nicht rein sein Andersseyn. Das Andersseyn ist zugleich in ihm enthalten, und zugleich noch davon getrennt; es ist Seyn-für-Anderes.\n\nDaseyn als solches ist Unmittelbares, Beziehungsloses; oder es ist in der Bestimmung des Seyns. Aber Daseyn als das Nichtseyn in sich schließend, ist bestimmtes, in sich verneintes Seyn, und dann zunächst Anderes,—aber weil es sich in seiner Verneinung zugleich auch erhält, nur Seyn-für-Anderes.\n\nEs erhält sich in seinem Nichtdaseyn, und ist Seyn; aber nicht Seyn überhaupt, sondern als Beziehung auf sich gegen seine Beziehung auf Anderes, als Gleichheit mit sich gegen seine Ungleichheit. Ein solches Seyn ist Ansichseyn.\n\nSeyn-für-Anderes und Ansichseyn machen die zwei Momente des Etwas aus. Es sind zwei Paare von Bestimmungen, die hier vorkommen: 1) Etwas und Anderes. 2) Seyn-für-Anderes, und Ansichseyn. Die erstern enthalten die Beziehungslosigkeit ihrer Bestimmtheit; Etwas und Anderes fallen auseinander. Aber ihre Wahrheit ist ihre Beziehung; das Seyn-für-Anderes und das Ansichseyn sind daher jene Bestimmungen als Momente Eines und desselben gesetzt, als Bestimmungen, welche Beziehungen sind und in ihrer Einheit, in der Einheit des Daseyns bleiben. Jedes selbst enthält damit an ihm zugleich auch sein von ihm verschiedenes Moment.\n\nSeyn und Nichts in ihrer Einheit, welche Daseyn ist, sind nicht mehr als Seyn und Nichts;—dieß sind sie nur außer ihrer Einheit; so in ihrer unruhigen Einheit, im Werden, sind sie Entstehen und Vergehen. —Seyn im Etwas ist Ansichseyn. Seyn, die Beziehung auf sich, die Gleichheit mit sich, ist jetzt nicht mehr unmittelbar, sondern Beziehung auf sich nur als Nichtseyn des Andersseyns, (als in sich reflektirtes Daseyn).—Eben so ist Nichtseyn als Moment des Etwas in dieser Einheit des Seyns und Nichtseyns, nicht Nichtdaseyn überhaupt, sondern Anderes, und bestimmter nach der Unterscheidung des Seyns von ihm zugleich, Beziehung auf sein Nichtdaseyn, Seyn-für-Anderes.\n\nSomit ist Ansichseyn erstlich negative Beziehung auf das Nichtdaseyn, es hat das Andersseyn außer ihm und ist demselben entgegen; insofern Etwas an sich ist, ist es dem Anders-seyn und dem Seyn-für-Anderes entnommen. Aber zweitens hat es das Nichtseyn auch selbst an ihm; denn es selbst ist das Nicht-seyn des Seyns-für Anderes.\n\nDas Seyn-für-Anderes aber ist erstlich Negation der einfachen Beziehung des Seyns auf sich, die zunächst Daseyn und Etwas seyn soll; insofern Etwas in einem Anderen oder für ein Anderes ist, entbehrt es des eigenen Seyns. Aber zweitens ist es nicht das Nichtdaseyn als reines Nichts; es ist Nichtdaseyn, das auf das Ansichseyn als auf sein in sich reflektirtes Seyn hinweist, so wie umgekehrt das Ansichseyn auf das Seyn-für-Anderes hinweist.\n\nBeide Momente sind Bestimmungen eines und des selben, nämlich des Etwas. Ansich ist Etwas, insofern es aus dem Seyn-für-Anderes heraus, in sich zurückgekehrt ist. Etwas hat aber auch eine Bestimmung oder Umstand an sich (hier fällt der Accent auf an) oder an ihm, insofern dieser Umstand äußerlich an ihm, ein Seyn-für-Anderes ist.\n\nDieß führt zu einer weitern Bestimmung. Ansichseyn und Seyn-für-Anderes sind zunächst verschieden; aber daß Etwas dasselbe, was es an sich ist, auch an ihm hat, und umgekehrt, was es als Seyn-für-Anderes ist, auch an sich ist,—dieß ist die Identität des Ansichseyns und Seyns-für-Anderes, nach der Bestimmung, daß das Etwas selbst ein und dasselbe beider Momente ist, sie also ungetrennt in ihm sind.—Es ergiebt sich formell diese Identität schon in der Sphäre des Daseyns, aber ausdrücklicher in der Betrachtung des Wesens und dann des Verhältnisses der Innerlichkeit und Äußerlichkeit, und am bestimmtesten in der Betrachtung der Idee, als der Einheit des Begriffs und der Wirklichkeit.—Man meint, mit dem Ansich etwas Hohes zu sagen, wie mit dem Inneren; was aber Etwas nur ansich ist, ist auch nur an ihm; ansich ist eine nur abstrakte, damit selbst äußerliche Bestimmung. Die Ausdrücke: es ist nichts an ihm, oder es ist etwas daran, enthalten, obgleich etwa dunkel, daß das, was an einem ist, auch zu seinem Ansichseyn, seinem inneren wahrhaften Werthe gehöre.\n\nEs kann bemerkt werden, daß sich hier der Sinn des Dings-an-sich ergiebt, das eine sehr einfache Abstraktion ist, aber eine Zeitlang eine sehr wichtige Bestimmung, gleichsam etwas Vornehmes, so wie, der Satz, daß wir nicht wissen, was die Dinge an sich sind, eine vielgeltende Weisheit war.—Die Dinge heißen an-sich, insofern von allem Seyn-für-Anderes abstrahirt wird, das heißt überhaupt, insofern sie ohne alle Bestimmung, als Nichtse gedacht werden. In diesem Sinn kann man freilich nicht wissen, was das Ding-an-sich ist. Denn die Frage: was? verlangt, daß Bestimmungen angegeben werden; indem aber die Dinge, von denen sie anzugeben verlangt würde, zugleich Dinge-an-sich seyn sollen, das heißt eben ohne Bestimmung, so ist in die Frage gedankenloserweise die Unmöglichkeit der Beantwortung gelegt, oder man macht nur eine widersinnige Antwort.—Das Ding-an-sich ist dasselbe, was jenes Absolute, von dem man nichts weiß, als daß Alles eins in ihm ist. Man weiß daher sehr wohl, was an diesen Dingen-an-sich ist; sie sind als solche nichts als Wahrheitslose, leere Abstraktionen. Was aber das Ding-an-sich in Wahrheit ist, was wahrhaft an sich ist, davon ist die Logik die Darstellung, wobei aber unter Ansich etwas Besseres als die Abstraktion verstanden wird, nämlich was etwas in seinem Begriffe ist; dieser aber ist konkret in sich, als Begriff überhaupt begreiflich, und als bestimmt und Zusammenhang seiner Bestimmungen in sich erkennbar.\n\nDas Ansichseyn hat zunächst das Seyn-für-Anderes zu seinem gegenüberstehenden Momente; aber es wird demselben auch das Gesetztseyn gegenübergestellt; in diesem Ausdruck liegt zwar auch das Seyn-für-Anderes, aber er enthält bestimmt die bereits geschehene Zurückbeugung dessen, was nicht an sich ist, in das, was sein Ansichseyn, worin es positiv ist. Das Ansichseyn ist gewöhnlich als eine abstrakte Weise den Begriff auszudrücken zu nehmen; Setzen fällt eigentlich erst in die Sphäre des Wesens, der objektiven Reflexion; der Grund setzt das, was durch ihn begründet wird; die Ursache noch mehr bringt eine Wirkung hervor, ein Daseyn, dessen Selbstständigkeit unmittelbar negirt ist und das den Sinn an ihm hat, in einem anderen seine Sache, sein Seyn zu haben. In der Sphäre des Seyns geht das Daseyn aus dem Werden nur hervor, oder mit dem Etwas ist ein Anderes, mit dem Endlichen das Unendliche gesetzt, aber das Endliche bringt das Unendliche nicht hervor, setzt dasselbe nicht. In der Sphäre des Seyns ist das Sich-bestimmen des Begriffs selbst nur erst an sich, so heißt es ein Übergehen; auch die reflektirenden Bestimmungen des Seyns, wie Etwas und Anderes, oder das Endliche und Unendliche, ob sie gleich wesentlich auf einander hinweisen, oder als Seyn-für-Anderes sind, gelten als qualitative für sich bestehend; das Andere ist, das Endliche gilt ebenso als unmittelbar seyend und für sich feststehend, wie das Unendliche; ihr Sinn erscheint als vollendet auch ohne ihr Anderes. Das Positive und Negative hingegen, Ursache und Wirkung, so sehr sie auch als isolirt seyend genommen werden, haben zugleich keinen Sinn ohne einander; es ist an ihnen selbst ihr Scheinen in einander, das Scheinen seines Anderen in jedem, vorhanden.—In den verschiedenen Kreisen der Bestimmung und besonders im Fortgange der Exposition, oder näher im Fortgange des Begriffs zu seiner Exposition ist es eine Hauptsache, dieß immer wohl zu unterscheiden, was noch an sich und was gesetzt ist, wie die Bestimmungen als im Begriffe und wie sie als gesetzt oder als seyend-für-Anderes sind. Es ist dieß ein Unterschied, der nur der dialektischen Entwickelung angehört, den das metaphysische Philosophiren, worunter auch das kritische gehört, nicht kennt; die Definitionen der Metaphysik, wie ihre Voraussetzungen, Unterscheidungen und Folgerungen, wollen nur Seyendes und zwar Ansichseyendes behaupten und hervorbringen.\n\nDas Seyn-für-Anderes ist in der Einheit des Etwas mit sich, identisch mit seinem Ansich; das Seyn-für-Anderes ist so am Etwas. Diese in sich reflektirte Bestimmtheit ist damit wieder einfache seyende, somit wieder eine Qualität,—die Bestimmung.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0001","text":"1. Etwas und Anderes sind beide erstens Daseyende oder Etwas.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"24.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0002","text":"Zweitens ist ebenso jedes ein Anderes. Es ist gleichgültig, welches zuerst und bloß darum Etwas genannt wird; (im Lateinischen, wenn sie in einem Satze vorkommen, heißen beide aliud, oder einer den andern, alius alium; bei einer Gegenseitigkeit ist der Ausdruck: alter alterum analog.) Wenn wir ein Daseyn A nennen, das andere aber B, so ist zunächst B als das Andere bestimmt. Aber A ist ebenso sehr das Andere des B. Beide sind auf gleiche Weise Andere. Um den Unterschied und das als affirmativ zu nehmende Etwas zu fixiren, dient das Dieses. Aber Dieses spricht eben es aus, daß dieß Unterscheiden und Herausheben des einen Etwas ein subjektives, außerhalb des Etwas selbst fallendes Bezeichnen ist. In dieses äußerliche Monstriren fällt die ganze Bestimmtheit; selbst der Ausdruck: Dieses enthält keinen Unterschied; alle und jede Etwas sind gerade so gut Diese, als sie auch Andere sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"24.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0003","text":"Man meint, durch: Dieses, etwas vollkommen bestimmtes auszudrücken; es wird übersehen, daß die Sprache, als Werk des Verstandes, nur Allgemeines ausspricht, außer in dem Namen eines einzelnen Gegenstandes; der individuelle Name ist aber ein Sinnloses in dem Sinne, daß er nicht ein Allgemeines ausdrückt, und erscheint als ein bloß Gesetztes, Willkürliches aus demselben Grunde, wie denn auch Einzelnamen willkürlich angenommen, gegeben oder ebenso verändert werden können.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"24.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0004","text":"Es erscheint somit das Andersseyn als eine dem so bestimmten Daseyn fremde Bestimmung, oder das Andere außer dem einen Daseyn; Theils, daß ein Daseyn erst durch das Vergleichen eines Dritten, Theils, daß es nur um des Anderen willen, das außer ihm ist, als anderes bestimmt werde, aber nicht für sich so sey. Zugleich, wie bemerkt worden, bestimmt sich jedes Daseyn, auch für die Vorstellung, ebenso sehr als ein anderes Daseyn, so daß nicht ein Daseyn bleibt, das nur als ein Daseyn bestimmt, das nicht außerhalb eines Daseyns, also nicht selbst ein Anderes wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"24.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0005","text":"Beide sind sowohl als Etwas als auch als Anderes bestimmt, hiermit dasselbe und es ist noch kein Unterschied derselben vorhanden. Diese Dieselbigkeit der Bestimmungen fällt aber ebenso nur in die äußere Reflexion, in die Vergleichung beider; aber wie das Andere zunächst gesetzt ist, so ist dasselbe für sich zwar in Beziehung auf das Etwas, aber auch für sich außerhalb desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"24.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0006","text":"Drittens ist daher das Andere zu nehmen, als isolirt, in Beziehung auf sich selbst; abstrakt als das Andere,…… des Plato, der es als eins der Momente der Totalität, dem Einen entgegensetzt, und dem Anderen auf diese Weise eine eigne Natur zuschreibt. So ist das Andere allein als solches gefaßt, nicht das Andere von Etwas, sondern das Andere an ihm selbst, d. i. das Andere seiner selbst.—Solches seiner Bestimmung nach Andere ist die physische Natur; sie ist das Andere des Geistes; diese ihre Bestimmung ist so zunächst eine bloße Relativität, wodurch nicht eine Qualität der Natur selbst, sondern nur eine ihr äußerliche Beziehung ausgedrückt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"24.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0007","text":"Aber indem der Geist das wahrhafte Etwas, und die Natur daher an ihr selbst nur das ist, was sie gegen den Geist ist, so ist, insofern sie für sich genommen wird, ihre Qualität eben dieß, das Andere an ihr selbst, das Außer-sich-seyende (in den Bestimmungen des Raumes, der Zeit, der Materie) zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"24.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0008","text":"Das Andere für sich ist das Andere an ihm selbst, hiermit das Andere seiner selbst, so das Andere des Anderen,—also das in sich schlechthin Ungleiche, sich Negirende, das sich Verändernde. Aber ebenso bleibt es identisch mit sich, denn dasjenige, in welches es sich veränderte, ist das Andere, das sonst weiter keine Bestimmung hat; aber das sich Verändernde ist auf keine verschiedene Weise, sondern auf dieselbe, ein Anderes zu seyn, bestimmt, es geht daher in demselben nur mit sich zusammen. So ist es gesetzt als in sich Reflektirtes mit Aufheben des Andersseyns; mit sich identisches Etwas, von dem hiermit das Andersseyn, das zugleich Moment desselben ist, ein Unterschiedenes, ihm nicht als Etwas selbst zukommendes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"24.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0009","text":"2. Etwas erhält sich in seinem Nichtdaseyn; es ist wesentlich Eins mit ihm, und wesentlich nicht Eins mit ihm.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"24.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0010","text":"Es steht also in Beziehung auf sein Andersseyn; es ist nicht rein sein Andersseyn. Das Andersseyn ist zugleich in ihm enthalten, und zugleich noch davon getrennt; es ist Seyn-für-Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"24.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0011","text":"Daseyn als solches ist Unmittelbares, Beziehungsloses; oder es ist in der Bestimmung des Seyns. Aber Daseyn als das Nichtseyn in sich schließend, ist bestimmtes, in sich verneintes Seyn, und dann zunächst Anderes,—aber weil es sich in seiner Verneinung zugleich auch erhält, nur Seyn-für-Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"24.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0012","text":"Es erhält sich in seinem Nichtdaseyn, und ist Seyn; aber nicht Seyn überhaupt, sondern als Beziehung auf sich gegen seine Beziehung auf Anderes, als Gleichheit mit sich gegen seine Ungleichheit. Ein solches Seyn ist Ansichseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"24.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0013","text":"Seyn-für-Anderes und Ansichseyn machen die zwei Momente des Etwas aus. Es sind zwei Paare von Bestimmungen, die hier vorkommen: 1) Etwas und Anderes. 2) Seyn-für-Anderes, und Ansichseyn. Die erstern enthalten die Beziehungslosigkeit ihrer Bestimmtheit; Etwas und Anderes fallen auseinander. Aber ihre Wahrheit ist ihre Beziehung; das Seyn-für-Anderes und das Ansichseyn sind daher jene Bestimmungen als Momente Eines und desselben gesetzt, als Bestimmungen, welche Beziehungen sind und in ihrer Einheit, in der Einheit des Daseyns bleiben. Jedes selbst enthält damit an ihm zugleich auch sein von ihm verschiedenes Moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"24.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0014","text":"Seyn und Nichts in ihrer Einheit, welche Daseyn ist, sind nicht mehr als Seyn und Nichts;—dieß sind sie nur außer ihrer Einheit; so in ihrer unruhigen Einheit, im Werden, sind sie Entstehen und Vergehen. —Seyn im Etwas ist Ansichseyn. Seyn, die Beziehung auf sich, die Gleichheit mit sich, ist jetzt nicht mehr unmittelbar, sondern Beziehung auf sich nur als Nichtseyn des Andersseyns, (als in sich reflektirtes Daseyn).—Eben so ist Nichtseyn als Moment des Etwas in dieser Einheit des Seyns und Nichtseyns, nicht Nichtdaseyn überhaupt, sondern Anderes, und bestimmter nach der Unterscheidung des Seyns von ihm zugleich, Beziehung auf sein Nichtdaseyn, Seyn-für-Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"24.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0015","text":"Somit ist Ansichseyn erstlich negative Beziehung auf das Nichtdaseyn, es hat das Andersseyn außer ihm und ist demselben entgegen; insofern Etwas an sich ist, ist es dem Anders-seyn und dem Seyn-für-Anderes entnommen. Aber zweitens hat es das Nichtseyn auch selbst an ihm; denn es selbst ist das Nicht-seyn des Seyns-für Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"24.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0016","text":"Das Seyn-für-Anderes aber ist erstlich Negation der einfachen Beziehung des Seyns auf sich, die zunächst Daseyn und Etwas seyn soll; insofern Etwas in einem Anderen oder für ein Anderes ist, entbehrt es des eigenen Seyns. Aber zweitens ist es nicht das Nichtdaseyn als reines Nichts; es ist Nichtdaseyn, das auf das Ansichseyn als auf sein in sich reflektirtes Seyn hinweist, so wie umgekehrt das Ansichseyn auf das Seyn-für-Anderes hinweist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"24.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0017","text":"Beide Momente sind Bestimmungen eines und des selben, nämlich des Etwas. Ansich ist Etwas, insofern es aus dem Seyn-für-Anderes heraus, in sich zurückgekehrt ist. Etwas hat aber auch eine Bestimmung oder Umstand an sich (hier fällt der Accent auf an) oder an ihm, insofern dieser Umstand äußerlich an ihm, ein Seyn-für-Anderes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"24.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0018","text":"Dieß führt zu einer weitern Bestimmung. Ansichseyn und Seyn-für-Anderes sind zunächst verschieden; aber daß Etwas dasselbe, was es an sich ist, auch an ihm hat, und umgekehrt, was es als Seyn-für-Anderes ist, auch an sich ist,—dieß ist die Identität des Ansichseyns und Seyns-für-Anderes, nach der Bestimmung, daß das Etwas selbst ein und dasselbe beider Momente ist, sie also ungetrennt in ihm sind.—Es ergiebt sich formell diese Identität schon in der Sphäre des Daseyns, aber ausdrücklicher in der Betrachtung des Wesens und dann des Verhältnisses der Innerlichkeit und Äußerlichkeit, und am bestimmtesten in der Betrachtung der Idee, als der Einheit des Begriffs und der Wirklichkeit.—Man meint, mit dem Ansich etwas Hohes zu sagen, wie mit dem Inneren; was aber Etwas nur ansich ist, ist auch nur an ihm; ansich ist eine nur abstrakte, damit selbst äußerliche Bestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"24.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0019","text":"Die Ausdrücke: es ist nichts an ihm, oder es ist etwas daran, enthalten, obgleich etwa dunkel, daß das, was an einem ist, auch zu seinem Ansichseyn, seinem inneren wahrhaften Werthe gehöre.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"24.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0020","text":"Es kann bemerkt werden, daß sich hier der Sinn des Dings-an-sich ergiebt, das eine sehr einfache Abstraktion ist, aber eine Zeitlang eine sehr wichtige Bestimmung, gleichsam etwas Vornehmes, so wie, der Satz, daß wir nicht wissen, was die Dinge an sich sind, eine vielgeltende Weisheit war.—Die Dinge heißen an-sich, insofern von allem Seyn-für-Anderes abstrahirt wird, das heißt überhaupt, insofern sie ohne alle Bestimmung, als Nichtse gedacht werden. In diesem Sinn kann man freilich nicht wissen, was das Ding-an-sich ist. Denn die Frage: was?","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"24.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0021","text":"verlangt, daß Bestimmungen angegeben werden; indem aber die Dinge, von denen sie anzugeben verlangt würde, zugleich Dinge-an-sich seyn sollen, das heißt eben ohne Bestimmung, so ist in die Frage gedankenloserweise die Unmöglichkeit der Beantwortung gelegt, oder man macht nur eine widersinnige Antwort.—Das Ding-an-sich ist dasselbe, was jenes Absolute, von dem man nichts weiß, als daß Alles eins in ihm ist. Man weiß daher sehr wohl, was an diesen Dingen-an-sich ist; sie sind als solche nichts als Wahrheitslose, leere Abstraktionen.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"24.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0022","text":"Was aber das Ding-an-sich in Wahrheit ist, was wahrhaft an sich ist, davon ist die Logik die Darstellung, wobei aber unter Ansich etwas Besseres als die Abstraktion verstanden wird, nämlich was etwas in seinem Begriffe ist; dieser aber ist konkret in sich, als Begriff überhaupt begreiflich, und als bestimmt und Zusammenhang seiner Bestimmungen in sich erkennbar.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"24.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0023","text":"Das Ansichseyn hat zunächst das Seyn-für-Anderes zu seinem gegenüberstehenden Momente; aber es wird demselben auch das Gesetztseyn gegenübergestellt; in diesem Ausdruck liegt zwar auch das Seyn-für-Anderes, aber er enthält bestimmt die bereits geschehene Zurückbeugung dessen, was nicht an sich ist, in das, was sein Ansichseyn, worin es positiv ist. Das Ansichseyn ist gewöhnlich als eine abstrakte Weise den Begriff auszudrücken zu nehmen; Setzen fällt eigentlich erst in die Sphäre des Wesens, der objektiven Reflexion; der Grund setzt das, was durch ihn begründet wird; die Ursache noch mehr bringt eine Wirkung hervor, ein Daseyn, dessen Selbstständigkeit unmittelbar negirt ist und das den Sinn an ihm hat, in einem anderen seine Sache, sein Seyn zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"24.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0024","text":"In der Sphäre des Seyns geht das Daseyn aus dem Werden nur hervor, oder mit dem Etwas ist ein Anderes, mit dem Endlichen das Unendliche gesetzt, aber das Endliche bringt das Unendliche nicht hervor, setzt dasselbe nicht. In der Sphäre des Seyns ist das Sich-bestimmen des Begriffs selbst nur erst an sich, so heißt es ein Übergehen; auch die reflektirenden Bestimmungen des Seyns, wie Etwas und Anderes, oder das Endliche und Unendliche, ob sie gleich wesentlich auf einander hinweisen, oder als Seyn-für-Anderes sind, gelten als qualitative für sich bestehend; das Andere ist, das Endliche gilt ebenso als unmittelbar seyend und für sich feststehend, wie das Unendliche; ihr Sinn erscheint als vollendet auch ohne ihr Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"24.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0025","text":"Das Positive und Negative hingegen, Ursache und Wirkung, so sehr sie auch als isolirt seyend genommen werden, haben zugleich keinen Sinn ohne einander; es ist an ihnen selbst ihr Scheinen in einander, das Scheinen seines Anderen in jedem, vorhanden.—In den verschiedenen Kreisen der Bestimmung und besonders im Fortgange der Exposition, oder näher im Fortgange des Begriffs zu seiner Exposition ist es eine Hauptsache, dieß immer wohl zu unterscheiden, was noch an sich und was gesetzt ist, wie die Bestimmungen als im Begriffe und wie sie als gesetzt oder als seyend-für-Anderes sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"24.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0026","text":"Es ist dieß ein Unterschied, der nur der dialektischen Entwickelung angehört, den das metaphysische Philosophiren, worunter auch das kritische gehört, nicht kennt; die Definitionen der Metaphysik, wie ihre Voraussetzungen, Unterscheidungen und Folgerungen, wollen nur Seyendes und zwar Ansichseyendes behaupten und hervorbringen.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"24.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0027","text":"Das Seyn-für-Anderes ist in der Einheit des Etwas mit sich, identisch mit seinem Ansich; das Seyn-für-Anderes ist so am Etwas. Diese in sich reflektirte Bestimmtheit ist damit wieder einfache seyende, somit wieder eine Qualität,—die Bestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"24.27"}],"sha256":"a839a639d3048155fcd83417e0639c8b4bc8cbd572e4c7c4bd6361ae4a67e02a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102102335115Z_0570b78a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Something and an Other.","source_sha256":"a839a639d3048155fcd83417e0639c8b4bc8cbd572e4c7c4bd6361ae4a67e02a","sha256":"5c486620a5aba3b378f7e48f4da569196d36873cd394eec02932da8ecd3ef031","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:21:02.335171+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0001","text":"1. Something and Other are both, first, existents or Something.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"24.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0002","text":"Secondly, each is likewise an Other. It is immaterial which is called Something first and merely for that reason; (in Latin, when they occur in one sentence, both are called aliud, or one the other, alius alium; in a reciprocity the expression is: alter alterum analogously.) If we call one existent A, but the other B, then B is at first determined as the Other. But A is equally the Other of B. Both are Others in the same way. In order to fix the difference and the Something to be taken affirmatively, This serves. But This precisely expresses that this distinguishing and singling out of one Something is a subjective designation falling outside Something itself. Into this external pointing falls the entire determinacy; even the expression: This contains no difference; all and every Something are just as much These as they are also Others.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"24.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0003","text":"One thinks that by means of: This, one expresses something completely determinate; one overlooks that language, as the work of the understanding, expresses only universals, except in the name of an individual object; but the individual name is a meaningless thing in the sense that it does not express a universal, and appears as something merely posited, arbitrary, for the same reason that individual names can also be arbitrarily assumed, given, or equally altered.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"24.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0004","text":"Thus otherness appears as a determination foreign to existent being so determined, or the Other outside the one existent being; partly, that an existent being is first determined as other through the comparison of a third, partly, that it is determined as other only for the sake of the Other that is outside it, but is not so for itself. At the same time, as has been remarked, every existent being determines itself, even for representation, equally as another existent being, so that there does not remain an existent being that is determined merely as an existent being, that would not be outside an existent being, and thus would not itself be an Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"24.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0005","text":"Both are determined both as Something and as Other, hence [they are] the same, and there is as yet no difference between them. But this sameness of determinations likewise falls only into external reflection, into the comparison of the two; yet, as the Other is at first posited, so it is indeed for itself in relation to Something, but also for itself outside it.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"24.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0006","text":"Thirdly, therefore, the Other is to be taken as isolated, in relation to itself; abstractly as the Other,…… of Plato, who opposes it to the One as one of the moments of totality, and in this way ascribes a nature of its own to the Other. Thus the Other is apprehended solely as such, not as the Other of Something, but as the Other in itself, i.e. the Other of itself.—Such an Other according to its determination is physical nature; it is the Other of spirit; this its determination is thus at first a mere relativity, by which not a quality of nature itself, but only a relation external to it, is expressed.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"24.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0007","text":"But since spirit is the true Something, and nature therefore in itself is only what it is over against spirit, then, insofar as it is taken for itself, its quality is precisely this, to be the Other in itself, to be outside itself (in the determinations of space, time, matter).","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"24.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0008","text":"The Other for itself is the Other in itself, hence the Other of itself, thus the Other of the Other,—thus that which is absolutely unequal within itself, self-negating, self-altering. But equally it remains identical with itself, for that into which it altered is the Other, which otherwise has no further determination; but that which alters is determined to be an Other not in a different manner, but in the same manner; it therefore comes together only with itself in the same. Thus it is posited as reflected into itself, with the sublation of otherness; an Something identical with itself, from which otherness, which is at the same time its moment, is something differentiated, not belonging to it as Something itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"24.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0009","text":"2. Something maintains itself in its non-existence; it is essentially one with it, and essentially not one with it.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"24.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0010","text":"It thus stands in relation to its otherness; it is not purely its otherness. Otherness is at once contained in it and still separated from it; it is Being-for-Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"24.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0011","text":"Existent being as such is immediate, relationless; or it is in the determination of Being. But existent being, as enclosing non-being within itself, is determinate Being, Being negated within itself, and then at first Other,—but because it maintains itself at the same time in its negation, only Being-for-Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"24.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0012","text":"It maintains itself in its non-existence and is Being; but not Being in general, rather as relation to itself over against its relation to Other, as equality with itself over against its inequality. Such Being is Being-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"24.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0013","text":"Being-for-Other and Being-in-itself constitute the two moments of Something. There occur here two pairs of determinations: 1) Something and Other. 2) Being-for-Other and Being-in-itself. The former contain the relationlessness of their determinacy; Something and Other fall apart. But their truth is their relation; Being-for-Other and Being-in-itself are therefore posited as those determinations as moments of one and the same [thing], as determinations which are relations and remain in their unity, in the unity of existent being. Thus each itself contains at the same time within it also its moment different from it.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"24.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0014","text":"Being and Nothing in their unity, which is existent being, are no longer Being and Nothing;—they are these only outside their unity; thus, in their restless unity, in becoming, they are coming-to-be and passing-away. —Being in Something is Being-in-itself. Being, the relation to itself, equality with itself, is now no longer immediate, but relation to itself only as non-being of otherness (as existent being reflected into itself).—Likewise, non-being as a moment of Something, in this unity of Being and non-being, is not non-existence in general, but Other, and more determinately, according to the distinction of Being from it, at the same time relation to its non-existence, Being-for-Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"24.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0015","text":"Thus Being-in-itself is, first, negative relation to non-existence; it has otherness outside it and is opposed to it; insofar as Something is in itself, it is withdrawn from otherness and from Being-for-Other. But secondly, it also has non-being itself in it; for it itself is the non-being of Being-for-Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"24.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0016","text":"But Being-for-Other is, first, negation of the simple relation of Being to itself, which at first is supposed to be existent being and Something; insofar as Something is in an Other or for an Other, it lacks its own Being. But secondly, it is not non-existence as pure Nothing; it is non-existence that points to Being-in-itself as to its Being reflected into itself, just as conversely Being-in-itself points to Being-for-Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"24.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0017","text":"Both moments are determinations of one and the same, namely of Something. Something is in itself insofar as it has returned into itself out of Being-for-Other. But Something also has a determination or circumstance at itself (here the accent falls on at) or in it, insofar as this circumstance, external at it, is a Being-for-Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"24.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0018","text":"This leads to a further determination. Being-in-itself and Being-for-Other are at first different; but that Something has in it the same thing that it is in itself, and conversely, what it is as Being-for-Other it also is in itself,—this is the identity of Being-in-itself and Being-for-Other, according to the determination that Something itself is one and the same of both moments, which are thus inseparate in it.—This identity formally emerges already in the sphere of existent being, but more expressly in the consideration of essence and then of the relation of inwardness and externality, and most determinately in the consideration of the Idea, as the unity of the Concept and actuality.—One thinks, with the in-itself, to say something lofty, as with the inner; but what Something is only in itself, it is also only in it; in-itself is only an abstract, and thereby itself external, determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"24.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0019","text":"The expressions: there is nothing in it, or there is something in it, contain, however obscurely perhaps, that what is in a thing also belongs to its Being-in-itself, its inner true worth.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"24.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0020","text":"It may be remarked that here the meaning of the thing-in-itself emerges, which is a very simple abstraction, but was for a time a very important determination, as it were something distinguished, just as the proposition that we do not know what things are in themselves was a wisdom of great currency.—Things are called in-themselves insofar as abstraction is made from all Being-for-Other, that is, in general insofar as they are thought without any determination, as non-beings. In this sense one certainly cannot know what the thing-in-itself is. For the question: what?","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"24.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0021","text":"demands that determinations be stated; but since the things of which they would be demanded to be stated are at the same time supposed to be things-in-themselves, that is, precisely without determination, the impossibility of answering is thoughtlessly placed in the question, or one merely gives an absurd answer.—The thing-in-itself is the same as that Absolute of which one knows nothing except that everything is one in it. One therefore knows very well what is in these things-in-themselves; as such, they are nothing but untrue, empty abstractions.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"24.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0022","text":"But what the thing-in-itself is in truth, what is truly in itself, logic is the presentation of; in this connection, however, by in-itself something better than abstraction is understood, namely what something is in its Concept; but this is concrete within itself, intelligible as Concept in general, and cognizable as determinate and as the connection of its determinations within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"24.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0023","text":"Being-in-itself initially has Being-for-Other as its opposing moment; but positedness is also set against it; this expression indeed likewise contains Being-for-Other, but it specifically contains the already accomplished bending-back of that which is not in itself into that which is its Being-in-itself, in which it is positive. Being-in-itself is ordinarily to be taken as an abstract way of expressing the Concept; positing properly falls only into the sphere of essence, of objective reflection; the ground posits that which is grounded through it; the cause, still more, brings forth an effect, an existent being whose independence is immediately negated and which has the sense in it of having its matter, its Being, in another.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"24.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0024","text":"In the sphere of Being, existent being merely proceeds from becoming, or with Something an Other, with the finite the infinite, is posited, but the finite does not bring forth the infinite, does not posit it. In the sphere of Being, the self-determining of the Concept itself is only in itself at first; thus it is called a transition; the reflective determinations of Being too, such as Something and Other, or the finite and infinite, although they essentially point to one another, or are as Being-for-Other, count as qualitative, subsisting for themselves; the Other is, the finite counts as immediately being and as standing fast for itself, just as the infinite; their sense appears complete even without their Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"24.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0025","text":"The positive and the negative, on the other hand, cause and effect, however much they may be taken as being isolated, at the same time have no sense without one another; in them themselves there is present their appearing in one another, the appearing of its other in each.—In the different spheres of determination, and especially in the course of the exposition, or more precisely in the course of the Concept toward its exposition, it is a principal matter always to distinguish well what is still in itself and what is posited, how the determinations are in the Concept and how they are posited or are being-for-another.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"24.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0026","text":"This is a distinction that belongs only to dialectical development, which metaphysical philosophizing, including critical philosophizing, does not know; the definitions of metaphysics, like its presuppositions, distinctions, and conclusions, seek only to assert and produce being, and indeed being-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"24.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0027","text":"Being-for-another, in the unity of something with itself, is identical with its in-itself; being-for-another is thus in something. This determinacy reflected into itself is thereby again simple being, and thus again a quality,—determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"24.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EUEA:P0027"]}],"source_digest":"17ee573f32f96463ca845114f765f40c9f098115b0cb893faad9960a7ca854f1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Etwas und ein Anderes."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Etwas und ein Anderes.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU","title":"b. Determination, Constitution, and Limit.","order":25,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BBBU","text":"Das Ansich, in welches das Etwas aus seinem Seyn-für-Anderes in sich reflektirt ist, ist nicht mehr abstraktes Ansich, sondern als Negation seines Seyns-für-Anderes durch dieses vermittelt, welches so sein Moment ist. Es ist nicht nur die unmittelbare Identität des Etwas mit sich, sondern die, durch welche das Etwas das, was es an sich ist, auch an ihm ist; das Seyn-für-Anderes ist an ihm, weil das Ansich das Aufheben desselben ist, aus demselben in sich ist; aber ebenso sehr auch schon, weil es abstrakt, also wesentlich mit Negation, mit Seyn-für-Anderes behaftet ist. Es ist hier nicht nur Qualität und Realität, seyende Bestimmtheit, sondern an-sich-seyende Bestimmtheit vorhanden, und die Entwickelung ist, sie als diese in sich reflektirte Bestimmtheit zu setzen.\n\n1. Die Qualität, die das Ansich im einfachen Etwas wesentlich in Einheit mit dessen anderen Momente, dem An-ihm-Seyn, ist, kann seine Bestimmung genannt werden, insofern dieses Wort in genauerer Bedeutung von Bestimmtheit überhaupt unterschieden wird. Die Bestimmung ist die affirmative Bestimmtheit, als das Ansichseyn, dem das Etwas in seinem Daseyn gegen seine Verwicklung mit Anderem, wo von es bestimmt würde, gemäß bleibt, sich in seiner Gleichheit mit sich erhält, sie in seinem Seyn-für-Anderes geltend macht. Es erfüllt seine Bestimmung, insofern die weitere Bestimmtheit, welche zunächst durch sein Verhalten zu Anderem mannigfaltig erwächst, seinem Ansichseyn gemäß, seine Fülle wird. Die Bestimmung enthält dieß, daß was Etwas an sich ist, auch an ihm sey.\n\nDie Bestimmung des Menschen ist die denkende Vernunft: Denken überhaupt ist seine einfache Bestimmtheit, er ist durch dieselbe von dem Thiere unterschieden; er ist Denken an sich, insofern dasselbe auch von seinem Seyn-für-Anderes, seiner eigenen Natürlichkeit und Sinnlichkeit, wodurch er unmittelbar mit Anderem zusammenhängt, unterschieden ist. Aber das Denken ist auch an ihm; der Mensch selbst ist Denken, er ist da als denkend, es ist seine Existenz und Wirklichkeit; und ferner indem es in seinem Daseyn, und sein Daseyn im Denken ist, ist es konkret, ist mit Inhalt und Erfüllung zu nehmen, es ist denkende Vernunft, und so ist es Bestimmung des Menschen. Aber selbst diese Bestimmung ist wieder nur an sich, als ein Sollen, d. i. sie mit der Erfüllung, die ihrem Ansich einverleibt ist, in der Form des Ansich überhaupt, gegen das ihr nicht einverleibte Daseyn, das zugleich noch als äußerlich gegenüberstehende, unmittelbare Sinnlichkeit und Natur ist.\n\n2. Die Erfüllung des Ansichseyns mit Bestimmtheit ist auch unterschieden von der Bestimmtheit, die nur Seyn-für-Anderes ist und außer der Bestimmung bleibt. Denn im Felde des Qualitativen bleibt den Unterschieden in ihrem Aufgehobenseyn auch das unmittelbare, qualitative Seyn gegeneinander. Das, was das Etwas an ihm hat, theilt sich so, und ist nach dieser Seite äußerliches Daseyn des Etwas, das auch sein Daseyn ist, aber nicht seinem Ansichseyn angehört.—Die Bestimmtheit ist so Beschaffenheit.\n\nSo oder anders beschaffen, ist Etwas als in äußerem Einfluß und Verhältnissen begriffen. Diese äußerliche Beziehung, von der die Beschaffenheit abhängt, und das Bestimmtwerden durch ein Anderes, erscheint als etwas Zufälliges. Aber es ist Qualität des Etwas, dieser Äußerlichkeit preisgegeben zu seyn und eine Beschaffenheit zu haben.\n\nInsofern Etwas sich verändert, so fällt die Veränderung in die Beschaffenheit; sie ist am Etwas das, was ein Anderes wird. Es selbst erhält sich in der Veränderung, welche nur diese unstäte Oberfläche seines Andersseyns, nicht seine Bestimmung trifft.\n\nBestimmung und Beschaffenheit sind so von einander unterschieden; Etwas ist seiner Bestimmung nach gleichgültig gegen seine Beschaffenheit. Das aber, was Etwas an ihm hat, ist die sie beide verbindende Mitte dieses Schlusses. Das Am Etwas seyn zeigte sich aber vielmehr in jene beide Extreme zu zerfallen. Die einfache Mitte ist die Bestimmtheit als solche; ihrer Identität gehört sowohl Bestimmung als Beschaffenheit an. Aber die Bestimmung geht für sich selbst in Beschaffenheit und diese in jene über. Dieß liegt im Bisherigen; der Zusammenhang ist näher dieser: Insofern das, was Etwas an sich ist, auch an ihm ist, ist es mit Seyn-für-Anderes behaftet; die Bestimmung ist damit als solche offen dem Verhältniß zu Anderem. Die Bestimmtheit ist zugleich Moment, enthält aber zugleich den qualitativen Unterschied, vom Ansichseyn verschieden, das Negative des Etwas, ein anderes Daseyn zu seyn. Die so das Andere in sich fassende Bestimmtheit mit dem Ansichseyn vereinigt bringt das Andersseyn in das Ansichseyn oder in die Bestimmung hinein, welche dadurch zur Beschaffenheit herabgesetzt ist. Umgekehrt das Seyn-für-Anders als Beschaffenheit isolirt und für sich gesetzt ist es an ihm dasselbe, was das Andere als solches, das Andere an ihm selbst d. i. seiner selbst ist; so ist es aber sich auf sich beziehendes Daseyn, so Ansichseyn mit einer Bestimmtheit, also Bestimmung.—Es hängt hiermit, insofern beide auch außereinander zu halten sind, die Beschaffenheit, die in einem Äußerlichen, einem Anderen überhaupt gegründet erscheint, auch von der Bestimmung ab, und das fremde Bestimmen ist durch die eigene, immanente des Etwas zugleich bestimmt. Aber ferner gehört die Beschaffenheit zu dem, was das Etwas an sich ist; mit seiner Beschaffenheit ändert sich Etwas.\n\nDiese Änderung des Etwas ist nicht mehr die erste Veränderung des Etwas bloß nach seinem Seyn-für-Anderes; jene erste war nur die an sich seyende, dem innern Begriffe angehörige Veränderung; die Veränderung ist nunmehr auch die am Etwas gesetzte.—Das Etwas selbst ist weiter bestimmt, und die Negation als ihm immanent gesetzt, als sein entwickeltes Insichseyn.\n\nZunächst ist das Übergehen der Bestimmung und Beschaffenheit ineinander das Aufheben ihres Unterschiedes, damit ist das Daseyn oder Etwas überhaupt gesetzt; und, indem es aus jenem Unterschiede resultirt, der das qualitative Andersseyn ebenso in sich befaßt, sind Zwei Etwas, aber nicht nur Andere gegen einander überhaupt, so daß diese Negation noch abstrakt wäre und nur in die Vergleichung fiele, sondern sie ist nunmehr den Etwas immanent. Sie sind als daseyend gleichgültig gegeneinander, aber diese ihre Affirmation ist nicht mehr unmittelbare, jedes bezieht sich auf sich selbst vermittelst des Aufhebens des Andersseyns, welches in der Bestimmung in das Ansichseyn reflektirt ist.\n\nEtwas verhält sich so aus sich selbst zum Anderen, weil das Andersseyn als sein eigenes Moment in ihm gesetzt ist, sein Insichseyn befaßt die Negation in sich, vermittelst deren überhaupt es nun sein affirmatives Daseyn hat. Aber von diesem ist das Andere auch qualitativ unterschieden, es ist hiermit außer dem Etwas gesetzt. Die Negation seines Anderen ist nur die Qualität des Etwas, denn als dieses Aufheben seines Anderen ist es Etwas. Damit tritt erst eigentlich das Andere einem Daseyn selbst gegenüber; dem ersten Etwas ist das Andere nur äußerlich gegenüber, oder aber indem sie in der That schlechthin, d. i. ihrem Begriffe nach zusammenhängen, ist ihr Zusammenhang dieser, daß das Daseyn in Andersseyn, Etwas in Anderes übergegangen, Etwas sosehr als das Andere, ein Anderes ist. Insofern nun das Insichseyn das Nichtseyn des Andersseyns, welches in ihm enthalten, aber Zugleich als seyend unterschieden, ist das Etwas selbst, die Negation, das Aufhören eines Anderen an ihm; es ist als sich negativ dagegen verhaltend und sich damit erhaltend gesetzt; —dieß Andere, das Insichseyn des Etwas als Negation der Negation ist sein Ansichseyn, und zugleich ist dieß Aufheben als einfache Negation an ihm, nämlich als seine Negation des ihm äußerlichen anderen Etwas. Es ist Eine Bestimmtheit derselben, welche sowohl mit dem Insichseyn der Etwas identisch, als Negation der Negation, als auch indem diese Negationen als andere Etwas gegeneinander sind, sie aus ihnen selbst zusammenschließt und ebenso von einander, jedes das Andere negirend, abscheidet,—die Grenze.\n\n3. Seyn-für-Anderes ist unbestimmte, affirmative Gemeinschaft von Etwas mit seinem Anderen; in der Grenze hebt sich das Nichtseyn-für-Anderes hervor, die qualitative Negation des Anderen, welches dadurch von dem in sich reflektirten Etwas abgehalten wird. Die Entwickelung dieses Begriffs ist zu sehen, welche sich aber vielmehr als Verwicklung und Widerspruch zeigt. Dieser ist sogleich darin vorhanden, daß die Grenze als in sich reflektirte Negation des Etwas die Momente des Etwas und des Anderen in ihr ideell enthält, und diese als unterschiedene Momente zugleich in der Sphäre des Daseyns als reell, qualitativ unterschieden gesetzt sind.\n\nà. Etwas also ist unmittelbares sich auf sich beziehendes Daseyn und hat eine Grenze zunächst als gegen Anderes; sie ist das Nichtseyn des Anderen, nicht des Etwas selbst; es begrenzt in ihr sein Anderes. —Aber das Andere ist selbst ein Etwas überhaupt; die Grenze also, welche das Etwas gegen das Andere hat, ist auch Grenze des Anderen als Etwas, Grenze desselben, wodurch es das erste Etwas als sein Anderes von sich abhält, oder ist ein Nichtseyn jenes Etwas; so ist sie nicht nur Nichtseyn des Andern, sondern des einen wie des anderen Etwas, somit des Etwas überhaupt.\n\nAber sie ist wesentlich ebenso das Nichtseyn des Anderen, so ist Etwas zugleich durch seine Grenze. Indem Etwas begrenzend ist, wird es zwar dazu herabgesetzt, selbst begrentzt zu seyn; aber seine Grenze ist, als Aufhören des Anderen an ihm, zugleich selbst nur das Seyn des Etwas; dieses ist durch sie das, was es ist, hat in ihr seine Qualität.—Dieß Verhältniß ist die äußere Erscheinung dessen, daß die Grenze einfache Negation oder die erste Negation, das Andere aber zugleich die Negation der Negation, das Insichseyn des Etwas, ist.\n\nEtwas ist also als unmittelbares Daseyn die Grenze gegen anderes Etwas, aber es hat sie an ihm selbst und ist Etwas durch die Vermittelung derselben, die ebenso sehr sein Nichtseyn ist. Sie ist die Vermittelung, wodurch Etwas und Anderes sowohl ist, als nicht ist.\n\nß. Insofern nun Etwas in seiner Grenze ist und nicht ist, und diese Momente ein unmittelbarer, qualitativer Unterschied sind, so fällt das Nichtdaseyn und das Daseyn des Etwas außer einander. Etwas hat sein Daseyn außer (oder wie man es sich auch vorstellt, innerhalb) seiner Grenze; eben so ist auch das Andere, weil es Etwas ist, außerhalb derselben. Sie ist die Mitte zwischen beiden, in der sie aufhören. Sie haben das Daseyn jenseits von einander von ihrer Grenze; die Grenze als das Nichtseyn eines jeden ist das Andere von beiden.\n\n—Nach dieser Verschiedenheit des Etwas von seiner Grenze, erscheint die Linie als Linie nur außerhalb ihrer Grenze, des Punktes; die Fläche als Fläche außerhalb der Linie; der Körper als Körper nur außerhalb seiner begrenzenden Fläche.—Dieß ist die Seite, von welcher die Grenze zunächst in die Vorstellung,—das Außersichseyn des Begriffes,—fällt, als vornehmlich auch in den räumlichen Gegenständen genommen wird.\n\ny. Ferner aber ist das Etwas, wie es außer der Grenze ist, das unbegrenzte Etwas, nur das Daseyn überhaupt. So ist es nicht von seinem Anderen unterschieden; es ist nur Daseyn, hat also mit seinem Anderen dieselbe Bestimmung, jedes ist nur Etwas überhaupt oder jedes ist Anderes; beide sind so Dasselbe. Aber dieß ihr zunächst unmittelbares Daseyn ist nun gesetzt mit der Bestimmtheit als Grenze, in welcher beide sind, was sie sind, unterschieden von einander. Sie ist aber ebenso ihre gemeinschaftliche Unterschiedenheit, die Einheit und Unterschiedenheit derselben, wie das Dasein. Diese doppelte Identität beider, das Daseyn und die Grenze enthält dieß, daß das Etwas sein Daseyn nur in der Grenze hat, und daß, indem die Grenze und das unmittelbare Daseyn beide zugleich das Negative von einander sind, das Etwas, welches nur in seiner Grenze ist, eben so sehr sich von sich selbst trennt und über sich hinaus auf sein Nichtseyn weißt und dieß als sein Seyn ausspricht, und so in dasselbe übergeht. Um dieß auf das vorige Beispiel anzuwenden, so ist die eine Bestimmung, daß Etwas, das was es ist, nur in seiner Grenze ist;—so ist also der Punkt nicht nur so Grenze der Linie, daß diese in ihm nur aufhört und sie als Daseyn außer ihm ist;—die Linie nicht nur so Grenze der Fläche, daß diese in der Linie nur aufhört, ebenso die Fläche als Grenze des Körpers. Sondern im Punkte fängt die Linie auch an; er ist ihr absoluter Anfang, auch insofern sie als nach ihren beiden Seiten unbegrenzt, oder wie man es ausdrückt, als ins Unendliche verlängert vorgestellt wird, macht der Punkt ihr Element aus, wie die Linie das Element der Fläche, die Fläche das des Körpers. Diese Grenzen sind Princip dessen, das sie begrenzen; wie das Eins, z.B. als Hundertstes, Grenze ist, aber auch Element des ganzen Hundert.\n\nDie andere Bestimmung ist die Unruhe des Etwas in seiner Grenze, in der es immanent ist, der Widerspruch zu seyn, der es über sich selbst hinausschickt. So ist der Punkt, diese Dialektik seiner selbst, zur Linie zu werden, die Linie die Dialektik, zur Fläche, die Fläche die zum totalen Raume zu werden. Von Linie, Fläche, und ganzem Raum wird eine zweite Definition so gegeben, daß durch die Bewegung des Punktes die Linie, durch die Bewegung der Linie die Fläche entsteht u.s.f. Diese Bewegung des Punkts, der Linie u.s.f. wird aber als etwas Zufälliges oder nur so Vorgestelltes angesehen. Dieß ist jedoch eigentlich darin zurückgenommen, daß die Bestimmungen, aus denen Linie u.s.f. entstehen sollen, ihre Elemente und Principien seyen, und diese sind nichts anderes als zugleich ihre Grenzen; das Entstehen wird so nicht für zufällig oder nur so vorgestellt, betrachtet. Daß Punkt, Linie, Fläche, für sich, sich widersprechend, Anfänge sind, welche selbst sich von sich abstossen, und der Punkt somit aus sich durch seinen Begriff in die Linie übergeht, sich an sich bewegt und sie entstehen macht, u.s.f.—liegt in dem Begriffe der dem Etwas immanenten Grenze. Die Anwendung jedoch selbst gehört in die Betrachtung des Raums; um sie hier anzudeuten, so ist der Punkt die ganz abstrakte Grenze, aber in einem Daseyn; dieses ist noch ganz unbestimmt genommen, es ist der sogenannte absolute, d. h. abstrakte Raum, das schlechthin kontinuirliche Außereinanderseyn. Damit daß die Grenze s nicht abstrakte Negation, sondern in diesem Daseyn, daß sie räumliche Bestimmtheit ist, ist der Punkt räumlich, der Widerspruch der abstrakten Negation und der Kontinuität und damit das Übergehen und Übergegangenseyn in Linie u.s.f. wie es denn keinen Punkt giebt, wie auch nicht eine Linie und Fläche.\n\nEtwas mit seiner immanenten Grenze gesetzt als der Widerspruch seiner selbst, durch den es über sich hinausgewiesen und getrieben wird, ist das Endliche.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0001","text":"Das Ansich, in welches das Etwas aus seinem Seyn-für-Anderes in sich reflektirt ist, ist nicht mehr abstraktes Ansich, sondern als Negation seines Seyns-für-Anderes durch dieses vermittelt, welches so sein Moment ist. Es ist nicht nur die unmittelbare Identität des Etwas mit sich, sondern die, durch welche das Etwas das, was es an sich ist, auch an ihm ist; das Seyn-für-Anderes ist an ihm, weil das Ansich das Aufheben desselben ist, aus demselben in sich ist; aber ebenso sehr auch schon, weil es abstrakt, also wesentlich mit Negation, mit Seyn-für-Anderes behaftet ist. Es ist hier nicht nur Qualität und Realität, seyende Bestimmtheit, sondern an-sich-seyende Bestimmtheit vorhanden, und die Entwickelung ist, sie als diese in sich reflektirte Bestimmtheit zu setzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"25.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0002","text":"1. Die Qualität, die das Ansich im einfachen Etwas wesentlich in Einheit mit dessen anderen Momente, dem An-ihm-Seyn, ist, kann seine Bestimmung genannt werden, insofern dieses Wort in genauerer Bedeutung von Bestimmtheit überhaupt unterschieden wird. Die Bestimmung ist die affirmative Bestimmtheit, als das Ansichseyn, dem das Etwas in seinem Daseyn gegen seine Verwicklung mit Anderem, wo von es bestimmt würde, gemäß bleibt, sich in seiner Gleichheit mit sich erhält, sie in seinem Seyn-für-Anderes geltend macht. Es erfüllt seine Bestimmung, insofern die weitere Bestimmtheit, welche zunächst durch sein Verhalten zu Anderem mannigfaltig erwächst, seinem Ansichseyn gemäß, seine Fülle wird. Die Bestimmung enthält dieß, daß was Etwas an sich ist, auch an ihm sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"25.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0003","text":"Die Bestimmung des Menschen ist die denkende Vernunft: Denken überhaupt ist seine einfache Bestimmtheit, er ist durch dieselbe von dem Thiere unterschieden; er ist Denken an sich, insofern dasselbe auch von seinem Seyn-für-Anderes, seiner eigenen Natürlichkeit und Sinnlichkeit, wodurch er unmittelbar mit Anderem zusammenhängt, unterschieden ist. Aber das Denken ist auch an ihm; der Mensch selbst ist Denken, er ist da als denkend, es ist seine Existenz und Wirklichkeit; und ferner indem es in seinem Daseyn, und sein Daseyn im Denken ist, ist es konkret, ist mit Inhalt und Erfüllung zu nehmen, es ist denkende Vernunft, und so ist es Bestimmung des Menschen. Aber selbst diese Bestimmung ist wieder nur an sich, als ein Sollen, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"25.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0004","text":"sie mit der Erfüllung, die ihrem Ansich einverleibt ist, in der Form des Ansich überhaupt, gegen das ihr nicht einverleibte Daseyn, das zugleich noch als äußerlich gegenüberstehende, unmittelbare Sinnlichkeit und Natur ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"25.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0005","text":"2. Die Erfüllung des Ansichseyns mit Bestimmtheit ist auch unterschieden von der Bestimmtheit, die nur Seyn-für-Anderes ist und außer der Bestimmung bleibt. Denn im Felde des Qualitativen bleibt den Unterschieden in ihrem Aufgehobenseyn auch das unmittelbare, qualitative Seyn gegeneinander. Das, was das Etwas an ihm hat, theilt sich so, und ist nach dieser Seite äußerliches Daseyn des Etwas, das auch sein Daseyn ist, aber nicht seinem Ansichseyn angehört.—Die Bestimmtheit ist so Beschaffenheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"25.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0006","text":"So oder anders beschaffen, ist Etwas als in äußerem Einfluß und Verhältnissen begriffen. Diese äußerliche Beziehung, von der die Beschaffenheit abhängt, und das Bestimmtwerden durch ein Anderes, erscheint als etwas Zufälliges. Aber es ist Qualität des Etwas, dieser Äußerlichkeit preisgegeben zu seyn und eine Beschaffenheit zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"25.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0007","text":"Insofern Etwas sich verändert, so fällt die Veränderung in die Beschaffenheit; sie ist am Etwas das, was ein Anderes wird. Es selbst erhält sich in der Veränderung, welche nur diese unstäte Oberfläche seines Andersseyns, nicht seine Bestimmung trifft.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"25.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0008","text":"Bestimmung und Beschaffenheit sind so von einander unterschieden; Etwas ist seiner Bestimmung nach gleichgültig gegen seine Beschaffenheit. Das aber, was Etwas an ihm hat, ist die sie beide verbindende Mitte dieses Schlusses. Das Am Etwas seyn zeigte sich aber vielmehr in jene beide Extreme zu zerfallen. Die einfache Mitte ist die Bestimmtheit als solche; ihrer Identität gehört sowohl Bestimmung als Beschaffenheit an. Aber die Bestimmung geht für sich selbst in Beschaffenheit und diese in jene über. Dieß liegt im Bisherigen; der Zusammenhang ist näher dieser: Insofern das, was Etwas an sich ist, auch an ihm ist, ist es mit Seyn-für-Anderes behaftet; die Bestimmung ist damit als solche offen dem Verhältniß zu Anderem. Die Bestimmtheit ist zugleich Moment, enthält aber zugleich den qualitativen Unterschied, vom Ansichseyn verschieden, das Negative des Etwas, ein anderes Daseyn zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"25.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0009","text":"Die so das Andere in sich fassende Bestimmtheit mit dem Ansichseyn vereinigt bringt das Andersseyn in das Ansichseyn oder in die Bestimmung hinein, welche dadurch zur Beschaffenheit herabgesetzt ist. Umgekehrt das Seyn-für-Anders als Beschaffenheit isolirt und für sich gesetzt ist es an ihm dasselbe, was das Andere als solches, das Andere an ihm selbst d. i. seiner selbst ist; so ist es aber sich auf sich beziehendes Daseyn, so Ansichseyn mit einer Bestimmtheit, also Bestimmung.—Es hängt hiermit, insofern beide auch außereinander zu halten sind, die Beschaffenheit, die in einem Äußerlichen, einem Anderen überhaupt gegründet erscheint, auch von der Bestimmung ab, und das fremde Bestimmen ist durch die eigene, immanente des Etwas zugleich bestimmt. Aber ferner gehört die Beschaffenheit zu dem, was das Etwas an sich ist; mit seiner Beschaffenheit ändert sich Etwas.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"25.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0010","text":"Diese Änderung des Etwas ist nicht mehr die erste Veränderung des Etwas bloß nach seinem Seyn-für-Anderes; jene erste war nur die an sich seyende, dem innern Begriffe angehörige Veränderung; die Veränderung ist nunmehr auch die am Etwas gesetzte.—Das Etwas selbst ist weiter bestimmt, und die Negation als ihm immanent gesetzt, als sein entwickeltes Insichseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"25.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0011","text":"Zunächst ist das Übergehen der Bestimmung und Beschaffenheit ineinander das Aufheben ihres Unterschiedes, damit ist das Daseyn oder Etwas überhaupt gesetzt; und, indem es aus jenem Unterschiede resultirt, der das qualitative Andersseyn ebenso in sich befaßt, sind Zwei Etwas, aber nicht nur Andere gegen einander überhaupt, so daß diese Negation noch abstrakt wäre und nur in die Vergleichung fiele, sondern sie ist nunmehr den Etwas immanent. Sie sind als daseyend gleichgültig gegeneinander, aber diese ihre Affirmation ist nicht mehr unmittelbare, jedes bezieht sich auf sich selbst vermittelst des Aufhebens des Andersseyns, welches in der Bestimmung in das Ansichseyn reflektirt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"25.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0012","text":"Etwas verhält sich so aus sich selbst zum Anderen, weil das Andersseyn als sein eigenes Moment in ihm gesetzt ist, sein Insichseyn befaßt die Negation in sich, vermittelst deren überhaupt es nun sein affirmatives Daseyn hat. Aber von diesem ist das Andere auch qualitativ unterschieden, es ist hiermit außer dem Etwas gesetzt. Die Negation seines Anderen ist nur die Qualität des Etwas, denn als dieses Aufheben seines Anderen ist es Etwas. Damit tritt erst eigentlich das Andere einem Daseyn selbst gegenüber; dem ersten Etwas ist das Andere nur äußerlich gegenüber, oder aber indem sie in der That schlechthin, d. i. ihrem Begriffe nach zusammenhängen, ist ihr Zusammenhang dieser, daß das Daseyn in Andersseyn, Etwas in Anderes übergegangen, Etwas sosehr als das Andere, ein Anderes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"25.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0013","text":"Insofern nun das Insichseyn das Nichtseyn des Andersseyns, welches in ihm enthalten, aber Zugleich als seyend unterschieden, ist das Etwas selbst, die Negation, das Aufhören eines Anderen an ihm; es ist als sich negativ dagegen verhaltend und sich damit erhaltend gesetzt; —dieß Andere, das Insichseyn des Etwas als Negation der Negation ist sein Ansichseyn, und zugleich ist dieß Aufheben als einfache Negation an ihm, nämlich als seine Negation des ihm äußerlichen anderen Etwas. Es ist Eine Bestimmtheit derselben, welche sowohl mit dem Insichseyn der Etwas identisch, als Negation der Negation, als auch indem diese Negationen als andere Etwas gegeneinander sind, sie aus ihnen selbst zusammenschließt und ebenso von einander, jedes das Andere negirend, abscheidet,—die Grenze.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"25.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0014","text":"3. Seyn-für-Anderes ist unbestimmte, affirmative Gemeinschaft von Etwas mit seinem Anderen; in der Grenze hebt sich das Nichtseyn-für-Anderes hervor, die qualitative Negation des Anderen, welches dadurch von dem in sich reflektirten Etwas abgehalten wird. Die Entwickelung dieses Begriffs ist zu sehen, welche sich aber vielmehr als Verwicklung und Widerspruch zeigt. Dieser ist sogleich darin vorhanden, daß die Grenze als in sich reflektirte Negation des Etwas die Momente des Etwas und des Anderen in ihr ideell enthält, und diese als unterschiedene Momente zugleich in der Sphäre des Daseyns als reell, qualitativ unterschieden gesetzt sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"25.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0015","text":"à. Etwas also ist unmittelbares sich auf sich beziehendes Daseyn und hat eine Grenze zunächst als gegen Anderes; sie ist das Nichtseyn des Anderen, nicht des Etwas selbst; es begrenzt in ihr sein Anderes. —Aber das Andere ist selbst ein Etwas überhaupt; die Grenze also, welche das Etwas gegen das Andere hat, ist auch Grenze des Anderen als Etwas, Grenze desselben, wodurch es das erste Etwas als sein Anderes von sich abhält, oder ist ein Nichtseyn jenes Etwas; so ist sie nicht nur Nichtseyn des Andern, sondern des einen wie des anderen Etwas, somit des Etwas überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"25.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0016","text":"Aber sie ist wesentlich ebenso das Nichtseyn des Anderen, so ist Etwas zugleich durch seine Grenze. Indem Etwas begrenzend ist, wird es zwar dazu herabgesetzt, selbst begrentzt zu seyn; aber seine Grenze ist, als Aufhören des Anderen an ihm, zugleich selbst nur das Seyn des Etwas; dieses ist durch sie das, was es ist, hat in ihr seine Qualität.—Dieß Verhältniß ist die äußere Erscheinung dessen, daß die Grenze einfache Negation oder die erste Negation, das Andere aber zugleich die Negation der Negation, das Insichseyn des Etwas, ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"25.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0017","text":"Etwas ist also als unmittelbares Daseyn die Grenze gegen anderes Etwas, aber es hat sie an ihm selbst und ist Etwas durch die Vermittelung derselben, die ebenso sehr sein Nichtseyn ist. Sie ist die Vermittelung, wodurch Etwas und Anderes sowohl ist, als nicht ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"25.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0018","text":"ß. Insofern nun Etwas in seiner Grenze ist und nicht ist, und diese Momente ein unmittelbarer, qualitativer Unterschied sind, so fällt das Nichtdaseyn und das Daseyn des Etwas außer einander. Etwas hat sein Daseyn außer (oder wie man es sich auch vorstellt, innerhalb) seiner Grenze; eben so ist auch das Andere, weil es Etwas ist, außerhalb derselben. Sie ist die Mitte zwischen beiden, in der sie aufhören. Sie haben das Daseyn jenseits von einander von ihrer Grenze; die Grenze als das Nichtseyn eines jeden ist das Andere von beiden.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"25.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0019","text":"—Nach dieser Verschiedenheit des Etwas von seiner Grenze, erscheint die Linie als Linie nur außerhalb ihrer Grenze, des Punktes; die Fläche als Fläche außerhalb der Linie; der Körper als Körper nur außerhalb seiner begrenzenden Fläche.—Dieß ist die Seite, von welcher die Grenze zunächst in die Vorstellung,—das Außersichseyn des Begriffes,—fällt, als vornehmlich auch in den räumlichen Gegenständen genommen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"25.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0020","text":"y. Ferner aber ist das Etwas, wie es außer der Grenze ist, das unbegrenzte Etwas, nur das Daseyn überhaupt. So ist es nicht von seinem Anderen unterschieden; es ist nur Daseyn, hat also mit seinem Anderen dieselbe Bestimmung, jedes ist nur Etwas überhaupt oder jedes ist Anderes; beide sind so Dasselbe. Aber dieß ihr zunächst unmittelbares Daseyn ist nun gesetzt mit der Bestimmtheit als Grenze, in welcher beide sind, was sie sind, unterschieden von einander. Sie ist aber ebenso ihre gemeinschaftliche Unterschiedenheit, die Einheit und Unterschiedenheit derselben, wie das Dasein.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"25.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0021","text":"Diese doppelte Identität beider, das Daseyn und die Grenze enthält dieß, daß das Etwas sein Daseyn nur in der Grenze hat, und daß, indem die Grenze und das unmittelbare Daseyn beide zugleich das Negative von einander sind, das Etwas, welches nur in seiner Grenze ist, eben so sehr sich von sich selbst trennt und über sich hinaus auf sein Nichtseyn weißt und dieß als sein Seyn ausspricht, und so in dasselbe übergeht. Um dieß auf das vorige Beispiel anzuwenden, so ist die eine Bestimmung, daß Etwas, das was es ist, nur in seiner Grenze ist;—so ist also der Punkt nicht nur so Grenze der Linie, daß diese in ihm nur aufhört und sie als Daseyn außer ihm ist;—die Linie nicht nur so Grenze der Fläche, daß diese in der Linie nur aufhört, ebenso die Fläche als Grenze des Körpers.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"25.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0022","text":"Sondern im Punkte fängt die Linie auch an; er ist ihr absoluter Anfang, auch insofern sie als nach ihren beiden Seiten unbegrenzt, oder wie man es ausdrückt, als ins Unendliche verlängert vorgestellt wird, macht der Punkt ihr Element aus, wie die Linie das Element der Fläche, die Fläche das des Körpers. Diese Grenzen sind Princip dessen, das sie begrenzen; wie das Eins, z.B. als Hundertstes, Grenze ist, aber auch Element des ganzen Hundert.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"25.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0023","text":"Die andere Bestimmung ist die Unruhe des Etwas in seiner Grenze, in der es immanent ist, der Widerspruch zu seyn, der es über sich selbst hinausschickt. So ist der Punkt, diese Dialektik seiner selbst, zur Linie zu werden, die Linie die Dialektik, zur Fläche, die Fläche die zum totalen Raume zu werden. Von Linie, Fläche, und ganzem Raum wird eine zweite Definition so gegeben, daß durch die Bewegung des Punktes die Linie, durch die Bewegung der Linie die Fläche entsteht u.s.f. Diese Bewegung des Punkts, der Linie u.s.f. wird aber als etwas Zufälliges oder nur so Vorgestelltes angesehen. Dieß ist jedoch eigentlich darin zurückgenommen, daß die Bestimmungen, aus denen Linie u.s.f. entstehen sollen, ihre Elemente und Principien seyen, und diese sind nichts anderes als zugleich ihre Grenzen; das Entstehen wird so nicht für zufällig oder nur so vorgestellt, betrachtet.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"25.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0024","text":"Daß Punkt, Linie, Fläche, für sich, sich widersprechend, Anfänge sind, welche selbst sich von sich abstossen, und der Punkt somit aus sich durch seinen Begriff in die Linie übergeht, sich an sich bewegt und sie entstehen macht, u.s.f.—liegt in dem Begriffe der dem Etwas immanenten Grenze. Die Anwendung jedoch selbst gehört in die Betrachtung des Raums; um sie hier anzudeuten, so ist der Punkt die ganz abstrakte Grenze, aber in einem Daseyn; dieses ist noch ganz unbestimmt genommen, es ist der sogenannte absolute, d. h. abstrakte Raum, das schlechthin kontinuirliche Außereinanderseyn. Damit daß die Grenze s nicht abstrakte Negation, sondern in diesem Daseyn, daß sie räumliche Bestimmtheit ist, ist der Punkt räumlich, der Widerspruch der abstrakten Negation und der Kontinuität und damit das Übergehen und Übergegangenseyn in Linie u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"25.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0025","text":"wie es denn keinen Punkt giebt, wie auch nicht eine Linie und Fläche.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"25.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0026","text":"Etwas mit seiner immanenten Grenze gesetzt als der Widerspruch seiner selbst, durch den es über sich hinausgewiesen und getrieben wird, ist das Endliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"25.26"}],"sha256":"fc45e94ccf74fe42ebfe54e08a5d2f2f85bb2af62b3cb69c65108fabb1cba1a5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102133864278Z_0a7cd310","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Determination, Constitution, and Limit.","source_sha256":"fc45e94ccf74fe42ebfe54e08a5d2f2f85bb2af62b3cb69c65108fabb1cba1a5","sha256":"8951d81767dc152afec3949ff55a564ec87b466505f426e1ee31b916a8ec9113","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:21:33.864291+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0001","text":"The in-itself, into which Something has reflected itself out of its being-for-other, is no longer abstract in-itself, but, as negation of its being-for-other, mediated through the latter, which is thus its moment. It is not merely the immediate identity of Something with itself, but that through which Something is, in it as well, what it is in itself; being-for-other is in it, because the in-itself is the sublation of the same, is in itself out of the same; but equally already because it is abstract, thus essentially affected with negation, with being-for-other. Here there is present not merely quality and reality, existent determinateness, but determinateness-being-in-itself, and the development consists in positing it as this determinateness reflected into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"25.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0002","text":"1. The quality which, in simple Something, is essentially in unity with its other moment, being-in-it, can be called its determination, insofar as this word is distinguished, in a more precise sense, from determinateness in general. Determination is affirmative determinateness, as being-in-itself, to which Something, in its existence, remains adequate in contrast to its involvement with an Other, by which it would be determined; it maintains itself in its equality with itself and makes this count in its being-for-other. It fulfils its determination insofar as the further determinateness, which at first arises variously through its relation to Other, becomes, in accordance with its being-in-itself, its fullness. Determination contains this: that what Something is in itself should also be in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"25.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0003","text":"The determination of the human being is thinking reason: thinking in general is his simple determinateness; through it he is distinguished from the animal; he is thinking in itself, insofar as the latter is also distinguished from his being-for-other, his own naturality and sensuousness, through which he is immediately connected with Other. But thinking is also in him; the human being himself is thinking, he is there as thinking, it is his existence and actuality; and further, since it is in his existence, and his existence is in thinking, it is concrete, is to be taken with content and fulfilment, it is thinking reason, and thus it is the determination of the human being. But even this determination is again only in itself, as an ought, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"25.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0004","text":"it, together with the fulfilment incorporated into its in-itself, is in the form of in-itself in general, in contrast to the existence not incorporated into it, which is at the same time still immediate sensuousness and nature standing over against it as external.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"25.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0005","text":"2. The fulfilment of being-in-itself with determinateness is also distinguished from determinateness which is merely being-for-other and remains outside determination. For in the sphere of the qualitative, immediate, qualitative being also remains over against the distinctions in their sublatedness. What Something has in it thus divides itself, and on this side is the external existence of Something, which is indeed its existence, but does not belong to its being-in-itself.—Determinateness is thus constitution.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"25.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0006","text":"Constituted thus or otherwise, Something is as caught up in external influence and relations. This external relation, on which constitution depends, and determination by an Other, appears as something contingent. But it is a quality of Something to be given over to this externality and to have a constitution.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"25.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0007","text":"Insofar as Something changes, the change falls into constitution; it is in Something that which becomes an Other. It itself maintains itself in the change, which affects only this unstable surface of its otherness, not its determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"25.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0008","text":"Determination and constitution are thus distinguished from one another; Something is, according to its determination, indifferent to its constitution. But what Something has in it is the middle which connects them both in this syllogism. Yet being-in-Something showed itself rather to fall apart into those two extremes. The simple middle is determinateness as such; both determination and constitution belong to its identity. But determination passes by itself into constitution, and this into the former. This lies in what has preceded; the connection is more precisely this: insofar as what Something is in itself is also in it, it is affected with being-for-other; determination is thereby, as such, open to relation to Other. Determinateness is at the same time a moment, but it likewise contains the qualitative difference, distinct from being-in-itself, the negative of Something, to be another existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"25.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0009","text":"Determinateness, thus containing the Other within itself and united with being-in-itself, brings otherness into being-in-itself or into determination, which thereby is reduced to constitution. Conversely, being-for-other, as constitution, isolated and posited for itself, is in it the same as the Other as such, the Other in itself, i.e. of itself; but thus it is existence relating itself to itself, thus being-in-itself with a determinateness, hence determination.—It follows from this, insofar as both are also to be kept apart from one another, that constitution, which appears grounded in an externality, in an Other in general, also depends upon determination, and the alien determining is at the same time determined by the proper, immanent determining of Something. But further, constitution belongs to what Something is in itself; Something changes with its constitution.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"25.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0010","text":"This alteration of Something is no longer the first change of Something merely according to its being-for-other; that first was only the change existing in itself, belonging to the inner concept; the change is now also that posited in Something.—Something itself is further determined, and negation is posited as immanent to it, as its developed being-within-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"25.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0011","text":"At first, the passing over of determination and constitution into one another is the sublation of their difference; thereby existence, or Something in general, is posited; and, since it results from that difference which likewise contains within itself qualitative otherness, there are two Somethings, yet not merely Others over against one another in general, so that this negation would still be abstract and would fall only into comparison, but it is now immanent in the Somethings. As existent, they are indifferent to one another, but this their affirmation is no longer immediate; each relates to itself by means of the sublation of otherness, which in determination is reflected into being-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"25.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0012","text":"Something thus relates from itself to the Other, because otherness, as its own moment, is posited in it; its being-within-itself comprehends within itself the negation through which it has its affirmative existence at all. But the Other is also qualitatively distinct from this; it is thereby posited outside Something. The negation of its Other is merely the quality of Something, for as this sublation of its Other it is Something. Thus the Other first properly confronts an existence itself; to the first Something the Other is only externally opposed, or else, since in fact they are absolutely connected, i.e. according to their concept, their connection is this, that existence has passed over into otherness, Something into Other, Something is, just as much as the Other, an Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"25.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0013","text":"Insofar, then, as being-within-itself is the non-being of otherness, which is contained in it but at the same time distinguished as being, Something itself is the negation, the ceasing of an Other in it; it is posited as relating negatively to the latter and thereby maintaining itself;—this Other, the being-within-itself of Something as negation of negation, is its being-in-itself, and at the same time this sublation is in it as simple negation, namely as its negation of the other Something external to it. It is one determinateness of the same, which is both identical with the being-within-itself of the Somethings, as negation of negation, and also, insofar as these negations are other Somethings over against one another, joins them together from themselves and equally separates them from one another, each negating the Other,—the limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"25.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0014","text":"3. Being-for-other is indeterminate, affirmative community of Something with its Other; in the limit, non-being-for-other stands forth, the qualitative negation of the Other, which thereby is held off from Something reflected into itself. The development of this concept is to be seen, though it shows itself rather as entanglement and contradiction. This is present immediately in the fact that the limit, as negation of Something reflected into itself, contains ideally within itself the moments of Something and of Other, and these, as distinct moments, are at the same time posited in the sphere of existence as real, qualitatively distinct.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"25.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0015","text":"à. Something, then, is immediate existence relating itself to itself and initially has a limit as against Other; it is the non-being of the Other, not of Something itself; in it, it limits its Other. —But the Other is itself a Something in general; the limit, therefore, which Something has against the Other, is also the limit of the Other as Something, its limit whereby it holds off the first Something from itself as its Other, or is a non-being of that Something; thus it is not merely non-being of the Other, but of the one as well as of the other Something, and hence of Something in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"25.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0016","text":"But it is essentially likewise the non-being of the Other; thus Something is at the same time through its limit. Inasmuch as Something is limiting, it is indeed reduced thereby to being itself limited; but its limit, as the ceasing of the Other in it, is at the same time itself only the being of Something; through it, Something is what it is and has its quality in it.—This relation is the external appearance of the fact that the limit is simple negation, or the first negation, while the Other is at the same time the negation of negation, the being-within-itself of Something.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"25.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0017","text":"Something is thus, as immediate existence, the limit against another Something, but it has it in itself and is Something through mediation by it, which is just as much its non-being. It is the mediation through which Something and Other both are and are not.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"25.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0018","text":"ß. Insofar, now, as Something is and is not in its limit, and these moments are an immediate, qualitative difference, the non-existence and the existence of Something fall apart from one another. Something has its existence outside (or, however one may represent it to oneself, within) its limit; likewise the Other, because it is Something, is outside it. It is the middle between the two, in which they cease. They have existence beyond one another, beyond their limit; the limit, as the non-being of each, is the Other of both.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"25.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0019","text":"—According to this difference of Something from its limit, the line appears as line only outside its limit, the point; the surface as surface outside the line; the body as body only outside its limiting surface.—This is the side from which the limit initially falls into representation,—the being-outside-itself of the concept,—as it is also taken pre-eminently in spatial objects.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"25.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0020","text":"y. But further, Something, as it is outside the limit, is the unlimited Something, merely existence in general. Thus it is not distinct from its Other; it is merely existence, thus has the same determination as its Other; each is merely Something in general, or each is Other; thus both are the Same. But their initially immediate existence is now posited with determinateness as limit, in which both are what they are, distinct from one another. But it is equally their common distinctness, their unity and distinction, as existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"25.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0021","text":"This twofold identity of both, existence and limit, contains this: that Something has its existence only in the limit, and that, since the limit and immediate existence are both at the same time the negative of one another, Something, which is only in its limit, equally separates itself from itself and points beyond itself to its non-being and declares this to be its being, and thus passes over into it. To apply this to the preceding example, the one determination is that Something is what it is only in its limit;—thus the point is not merely the limit of the line in such a way that the latter merely ceases in it and is, as existence, outside it;—nor is the line merely the limit of the surface in such a way that the latter merely ceases in the line, and likewise the surface as limit of the body.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"25.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0022","text":"Rather, the line also begins in the point; it is its absolute beginning; even insofar as the line is represented as unlimited on its two sides, or, as one expresses it, as extended to infinity, the point constitutes its element, just as the line constitutes the element of the surface, and the surface that of the body. These limits are the principle of that which they limit; just as the one, e.g. as a hundredth, is limit, but also element of the whole hundred.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"25.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0023","text":"The other determination is the unrest of Something in its limit, in which it is immanent, to be the contradiction that sends it beyond itself. Thus the point is this dialectic of itself, to become a line; the line, the dialectic of becoming a surface; the surface, that of becoming total space. A second definition of line, surface, and whole space is accordingly given thus: that through the movement of the point the line arises, through the movement of the line the surface, and so forth. But this movement of the point, the line, and so forth is regarded as something contingent or merely represented as such. Yet this is properly retracted in the fact that the determinations from which line and so forth are supposed to arise are their elements and principles, and these are nothing other than at the same time their limits; thus the arising is not regarded as contingent or merely represented as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"25.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0024","text":"That point, line, surface, taken by themselves, are self-contradictory beginnings, which themselves repel themselves from themselves, and that the point consequently passes over from itself through its Concept into the line, moves itself within itself and brings it forth, and so forth—lies in the Concept of the limit immanent in something. The application itself, however, belongs to the consideration of space; to indicate it here, the point is the wholly abstract limit, but in an existence; this is still taken quite indeterminately, it is so-called absolute, i.e. abstract, space, the absolutely continuous being-outside-one-another. In that the limit is not abstract negation, but in this existence, in that it is spatial determinacy, the point is spatial, the contradiction of abstract negation and continuity, and hence the transition and having-transition into line, and so forth.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"25.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0025","text":"as indeed there is no point, nor likewise a line and surface.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"25.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0026","text":"Something posited with its immanent limit as the contradiction of itself, through which it is directed and driven beyond itself, is the finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"25.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BBBU:P0026"]}],"source_digest":"9017af120d11382e1a3155158cc10c6064f2eea3df3c0fd28cf4bfd566a02dfa","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Bestimmung, Beschaffenheit und Grenze."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Bestimmung, Beschaffenheit und Grenze.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDE0","title":"c. Finitude.","order":26,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDE0","text":"Das Daseyn ist bestimmt; Etwas hat eine Qualität, und ist in ihr nicht nur bestimmt, sondern begrenzt; seine Qualität ist seine Grenze, mit welcher behaftet, es zunächst affirmatives, ruhiges Daseyn bleibt. Aber diese Negation entwickelt, so daß der Gegensatz seines Daseyns und der Negation als ihm immanenter Grenze selbst das Insichseyn des Etwas, und dieses somit nur Werden an ihm selbst sey, macht seine Endlichkeit aus. Wenn wir von den Dingen sagen, sie sind endlich, so wird darunter verstanden, daß sie nicht nur eine Bestimmtheit haben, die Qualität nicht nur als Realität und ansichseyende Bestimmung, daß sie nicht blos begrenzt sind, sie haben so noch Daseyn außer ihrer Grenze,—sondern daß vielmehr das Nichtseyn ihre Natur, ihr Seyn, ausmacht. Die endlichen Dinge sind, aber ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, daß sie als negativ sich auf sich selbst beziehen, eben in dieser Beziehung auf sich selbst sich über sich, über ihr Seyn, hinauszuschicken. Sie sind, aber die Wahrheit dieses Seyns ist ihr Ende. Das Endliche verändert sich nicht nur, wie Etwas überhaupt, sondern es vergeht, und es ist nicht bloß möglich, daß es vergeht, so daß es seyn könnte, ohne zu vergehen. Sondern das Seyn der endlichen Dinge als solches ist, den Keim des Vergehens als ihr Insichseyn zu haben, die Stunde ihrer Geburt ist die Stunde ihres Todes.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDE0:P0001","text":"Das Daseyn ist bestimmt; Etwas hat eine Qualität, und ist in ihr nicht nur bestimmt, sondern begrenzt; seine Qualität ist seine Grenze, mit welcher behaftet, es zunächst affirmatives, ruhiges Daseyn bleibt. Aber diese Negation entwickelt, so daß der Gegensatz seines Daseyns und der Negation als ihm immanenter Grenze selbst das Insichseyn des Etwas, und dieses somit nur Werden an ihm selbst sey, macht seine Endlichkeit aus. Wenn wir von den Dingen sagen, sie sind endlich, so wird darunter verstanden, daß sie nicht nur eine Bestimmtheit haben, die Qualität nicht nur als Realität und ansichseyende Bestimmung, daß sie nicht blos begrenzt sind, sie haben so noch Daseyn außer ihrer Grenze,—sondern daß vielmehr das Nichtseyn ihre Natur, ihr Seyn, ausmacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"26.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDE0:P0002","text":"Die endlichen Dinge sind, aber ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, daß sie als negativ sich auf sich selbst beziehen, eben in dieser Beziehung auf sich selbst sich über sich, über ihr Seyn, hinauszuschicken. Sie sind, aber die Wahrheit dieses Seyns ist ihr Ende. Das Endliche verändert sich nicht nur, wie Etwas überhaupt, sondern es vergeht, und es ist nicht bloß möglich, daß es vergeht, so daß es seyn könnte, ohne zu vergehen. Sondern das Seyn der endlichen Dinge als solches ist, den Keim des Vergehens als ihr Insichseyn zu haben, die Stunde ihrer Geburt ist die Stunde ihres Todes.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"26.2"}],"sha256":"0f04f97a1643b98b871d8f42b361c7fbef10f302912ffdf2decc2ae030dad5a5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102137610994Z_1d1e1eba","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Finitude.","source_sha256":"0f04f97a1643b98b871d8f42b361c7fbef10f302912ffdf2decc2ae030dad5a5","sha256":"70fc4288fe03ede9cceb455dc36d40fabad8988343b12a387a22619af0351f4b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:21:37.611013+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDE0:P0001","text":"Being-there is determinate; Something has a quality, and is not merely determinate in it, but limited; its quality is its limit, with which encumbered, it initially remains affirmative, tranquil being-there. But this negation develops, so that the opposition of its being-there and of negation as a limit immanent to it itself constitutes the being-within-itself of Something, and thus this is only becoming within itself; this constitutes its finitude. When we say of things that they are finite, this is understood to mean that they do not merely have a determinateness, that quality is not merely reality and determination being-in-itself, that they are not merely limited—they thus still have being-there outside their limit—but rather that non-being constitutes their nature, their being.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"26.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDE0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDE0:P0002","text":"Finite things are, but their relation to themselves is that, as negative, they relate to themselves, precisely in this relation to themselves sending themselves beyond themselves, beyond their being. They are, but the truth of this being is their end. The finite does not merely alter, like Something in general, but it passes away, and it is not merely possible that it passes away, such that it could be without passing away. Rather, the being of finite things as such consists in having the germ of passing-away as their being-within-themselves; the hour of their birth is the hour of their death.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"26.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDE0:P0002"]}],"source_digest":"9efbee44ffd287983579be10485f376d07088367f19e6cbfa11a52ea83b6829e","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die Endlichkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die Endlichkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD","title":"1. The Immediacy of Finitude.","order":27,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_1DUD","text":"Der Gedanke an die Endlichkeit der Dinge führt diese Trauer mit sich, weil sie die auf die Spitze getriebene qualitative Negation ist, in der Einfachheit solcher Bestimmung ihnen nicht mehr ein affirmatives Seyn unterschieden von ihrer Bestimmung zum Untergange gelassen ist. Die Endlichkeit ist um dieser qualitativen Einfachheit der Negation, die zum abstrakten Gegensatze des Nichts und Vergehens gegen das Seyn zurückgegangen ist, die hartnäckigste Kategorie des Verstandes; die Negation überhaupt, Beschaffenheit, Grenze vertragen sich mit ihrem Anderen, dem Daseyn; auch das abstrakte Nichts wird für sich als Abstraktion aufgegeben; aber Endlichkeit ist die als an sich fixirte Negation, und steht daher seinem Affirmativen schroff gegenüber. Das Endliche läßt sich so in Fluß wohl bringen, es ist selbst dieß, zu seinem Ende bestimmt zu seyn, aber nur zu seinem Ende;—es ist vielmehr das Verweigern, sich zu seinem Affirmativen, dem Unendlichen hin affirmativ bringen, mit ihm sich verbinden zu lassen; es ist also untrennbar von seinem Nichts gesetzt, und alle Versöhnung mit seinem Anderen, dem Affirmativen, dadurch abgeschnitten. Die Bestimmung der endlichen Dinge ist nicht eine weitere als ihr Ende. Der Verstand verharrt in dieser Trauer der Endlichkeit, indem er das Nichtseyn zur Bestimmung der Dinge, es zugleich unvergänglich und absolut macht. Ihre Vergänglichkeit könnte nur in ihrem Anderen, dem Affirmativen, vergehen; so trennte sich ihre Endlichkeit von ihnen ab; aber sie ist ihre unveränderliche, d. i. nicht in ihr Anderes d. i. nicht in ihr Affirmatives übergehende Qualität, so ist sie ewig.\n\nDieß ist eine sehr wichtige Betrachtung daß aber das Endliche absolut sey, solchen Standpunkt wird sich freilich irgend eine Philosophie oder Ansicht oder der Verstand nicht aufbürden lassen wollen; vielmehr ist das Gegentheil ausdrücklich in der Behauptung des Endlichen vorhanden; das Endliche ist das Beschränkte, Vergängliche; das Endliche ist nur das Endliche, nicht das Unvergängliche; dieß liegt unmittelbar in seiner Bestimmung und Ausdruck. Aber es kommt darauf an, ob in der Ansicht beim Seyn der Endlichkeit beharrt wird, die Vergänglichkeit bestehen bleibt, oder ob die Vergänglichkeit und das Vergehen vergeht? Daß dieß aber nicht geschieht, ist das Faktum eben in derjenigen Ansicht des Endlichen, welche das Vergehen zum Letzten des Endlichen macht. Es ist die ausdrückliche Behauptung, daß das Endliche mit dem Unendlichen unverträglich und unvereinbar sey, das Endliche dem Unendlichen schlechthin entgegen gesetzt sey. Dem Unendlichen ist Seyn, absolutes Seyn zugeschrieben; ihm gegenüber bleibt so das Endliche festgehalten, als das Negative desselben; unvereinbar mit dem Unendlichen bleibt es absolut auf seiner eigenen Seite; Affirmation erhielte es von Affirmativen, dem Unendlichen und verginge so; aber eine Vereinigung mit demselben ist das, was für das Unmögliche erklärt wird. Soll es nicht beharren dem Unendlichen gegenüber, sondern vergehen, so ist, wie vorhin gesagt, eben sein Vergehen das Letzte, nicht das Affirmative, welches nur das Vergeben des Vergehens seyn würde. Sollte aber das Endliche nicht im Affirmativen vergehen, sondern sein Ende als das Nichts gefaßt werden, so wären wir wieder bei jenem ersten, abstrakten Nichts, das selbst längst vergangen ist.\n\nBei diesem Nichts jedoch, welches nur Nichts seyn soll und dem zugleich eine Existenz, im Denken, Vorstellen oder Sprechen zugegeben wird, kommt derselbe Widerspruch vor, als so eben bei dem Endlichen, angegeben worden, nur daß er dort nur vorkommt, aber in der Endlichkeit ausdrücklich ist. Dort erscheint er als subjektiv, hier wird behauptet, das Endliche stehe perennirend dem Unendlichen entgegen, das an sich Nichtige sey, und es sey als an sich Nichtiges. Dieß ist zum Bewußtseyn zu bringen; und die Entwickelung des Endlichen zeigt, daß es an ihm als dieser Widerspruch in sich zusammenfällt, aber ihn dahin wirklich auflöst, nicht daß es nur vergänglich ist und vergeht, sondern daß das Vergehen, das Nichts, nicht das Letzte ist, sondern vergeht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0001","text":"Der Gedanke an die Endlichkeit der Dinge führt diese Trauer mit sich, weil sie die auf die Spitze getriebene qualitative Negation ist, in der Einfachheit solcher Bestimmung ihnen nicht mehr ein affirmatives Seyn unterschieden von ihrer Bestimmung zum Untergange gelassen ist. Die Endlichkeit ist um dieser qualitativen Einfachheit der Negation, die zum abstrakten Gegensatze des Nichts und Vergehens gegen das Seyn zurückgegangen ist, die hartnäckigste Kategorie des Verstandes; die Negation überhaupt, Beschaffenheit, Grenze vertragen sich mit ihrem Anderen, dem Daseyn; auch das abstrakte Nichts wird für sich als Abstraktion aufgegeben; aber Endlichkeit ist die als an sich fixirte Negation, und steht daher seinem Affirmativen schroff gegenüber.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"27.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0002","text":"Das Endliche läßt sich so in Fluß wohl bringen, es ist selbst dieß, zu seinem Ende bestimmt zu seyn, aber nur zu seinem Ende;—es ist vielmehr das Verweigern, sich zu seinem Affirmativen, dem Unendlichen hin affirmativ bringen, mit ihm sich verbinden zu lassen; es ist also untrennbar von seinem Nichts gesetzt, und alle Versöhnung mit seinem Anderen, dem Affirmativen, dadurch abgeschnitten. Die Bestimmung der endlichen Dinge ist nicht eine weitere als ihr Ende. Der Verstand verharrt in dieser Trauer der Endlichkeit, indem er das Nichtseyn zur Bestimmung der Dinge, es zugleich unvergänglich und absolut macht. Ihre Vergänglichkeit könnte nur in ihrem Anderen, dem Affirmativen, vergehen; so trennte sich ihre Endlichkeit von ihnen ab; aber sie ist ihre unveränderliche, d. i. nicht in ihr Anderes d. i. nicht in ihr Affirmatives übergehende Qualität, so ist sie ewig.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"27.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0003","text":"Dieß ist eine sehr wichtige Betrachtung daß aber das Endliche absolut sey, solchen Standpunkt wird sich freilich irgend eine Philosophie oder Ansicht oder der Verstand nicht aufbürden lassen wollen; vielmehr ist das Gegentheil ausdrücklich in der Behauptung des Endlichen vorhanden; das Endliche ist das Beschränkte, Vergängliche; das Endliche ist nur das Endliche, nicht das Unvergängliche; dieß liegt unmittelbar in seiner Bestimmung und Ausdruck. Aber es kommt darauf an, ob in der Ansicht beim Seyn der Endlichkeit beharrt wird, die Vergänglichkeit bestehen bleibt, oder ob die Vergänglichkeit und das Vergehen vergeht? Daß dieß aber nicht geschieht, ist das Faktum eben in derjenigen Ansicht des Endlichen, welche das Vergehen zum Letzten des Endlichen macht.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"27.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0004","text":"Es ist die ausdrückliche Behauptung, daß das Endliche mit dem Unendlichen unverträglich und unvereinbar sey, das Endliche dem Unendlichen schlechthin entgegen gesetzt sey. Dem Unendlichen ist Seyn, absolutes Seyn zugeschrieben; ihm gegenüber bleibt so das Endliche festgehalten, als das Negative desselben; unvereinbar mit dem Unendlichen bleibt es absolut auf seiner eigenen Seite; Affirmation erhielte es von Affirmativen, dem Unendlichen und verginge so; aber eine Vereinigung mit demselben ist das, was für das Unmögliche erklärt wird. Soll es nicht beharren dem Unendlichen gegenüber, sondern vergehen, so ist, wie vorhin gesagt, eben sein Vergehen das Letzte, nicht das Affirmative, welches nur das Vergeben des Vergehens seyn würde.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"27.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0005","text":"Sollte aber das Endliche nicht im Affirmativen vergehen, sondern sein Ende als das Nichts gefaßt werden, so wären wir wieder bei jenem ersten, abstrakten Nichts, das selbst längst vergangen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"27.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0006","text":"Bei diesem Nichts jedoch, welches nur Nichts seyn soll und dem zugleich eine Existenz, im Denken, Vorstellen oder Sprechen zugegeben wird, kommt derselbe Widerspruch vor, als so eben bei dem Endlichen, angegeben worden, nur daß er dort nur vorkommt, aber in der Endlichkeit ausdrücklich ist. Dort erscheint er als subjektiv, hier wird behauptet, das Endliche stehe perennirend dem Unendlichen entgegen, das an sich Nichtige sey, und es sey als an sich Nichtiges. Dieß ist zum Bewußtseyn zu bringen; und die Entwickelung des Endlichen zeigt, daß es an ihm als dieser Widerspruch in sich zusammenfällt, aber ihn dahin wirklich auflöst, nicht daß es nur vergänglich ist und vergeht, sondern daß das Vergehen, das Nichts, nicht das Letzte ist, sondern vergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"27.6"}],"sha256":"e33040545c1f84df9ef4744fd1f42ecc6c86aeba586f7550617ac328cbfae939","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102213373767Z_c38471ea","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"1. The Immediacy of Finitude.","source_sha256":"e33040545c1f84df9ef4744fd1f42ecc6c86aeba586f7550617ac328cbfae939","sha256":"db7a1f95245e56d665af6ec28b4dce04906900e28a4cfc789cada7b95b436f16","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:22:13.373779+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0001","text":"The thought of the finitude of things carries this grief with it, because it is the qualitative negation driven to its extreme, in the simplicity of whose determination there is no longer left to them an affirmative Being distinguished from their determination to perish. Finitude is, on account of this qualitative simplicity of negation, which has reverted to the abstract opposition of Nothing and passing-away against Being, the most obstinate category of the Understanding; negation in general, constitution, limit, are compatible with their Other, determinate being; even abstract Nothing is relinquished for itself as abstraction; but finitude is negation fixed as in itself, and therefore stands starkly opposed to its affirmative.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"27.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0002","text":"The finite can indeed thus be set in flux; it is itself this, to be determined to its end, but only to its end;—it is rather the refusal to allow itself to be brought affirmatively to its affirmative, the infinite, to allow itself to be united with it; it is thus posited inseparably from its Nothing, and every reconciliation with its Other, the affirmative, is thereby cut off. The determination of finite things is no further than their end. The Understanding persists in this grief of finitude, in that it makes non-being the determination of things, and at the same time makes it imperishable and absolute. Their perishability could perish only in their Other, the affirmative; thus their finitude would separate itself from them; but it is their unchangeable, i.e. non-transitioning into its Other, i.e. into its affirmative, quality; thus it is eternal.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"27.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0003","text":"This is a very important consideration; but that the finite is absolute—such a standpoint, to be sure, no philosophy or view or the Understanding will wish to impose upon itself; rather, the opposite is expressly present in the assertion of the finite; the finite is the limited, the transitory; the finite is only the finite, not the imperishable; this lies immediately in its determination and expression. But the question is whether, in the view, one persists with the Being of finitude, whether transitoriness remains, or whether transitoriness and passing-away pass away? But that this does not happen is the fact precisely in that view of the finite which makes passing-away the ultimate of the finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"27.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0004","text":"It is the explicit assertion that the finite is incompatible and irreconcilable with the infinite, that the finite is absolutely opposed to the infinite. Being, absolute Being, is ascribed to the infinite; over against it the finite is thus held fast as its negative; incompatible with the infinite, it remains absolutely on its own side; it would receive affirmation from the affirmative, the infinite, and would thus perish; but a union with the same is what is declared impossible. If it is not to persist over against the infinite, but to perish, then, as was said above, precisely its passing-away is the ultimate, not the affirmative, which would only be the forgiving of passing-away.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"27.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0005","text":"But if the finite were not to perish in the affirmative, but its end were conceived as Nothing, then we should again be at that first, abstract Nothing, which itself has long since passed away.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"27.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0006","text":"Yet in the case of this Nothing, which is supposed to be only Nothing and which at the same time is granted an existence in thinking, representing, or speaking, there occurs the same contradiction as was just now indicated in the case of the finite; only there it merely occurs, whereas in finitude it is explicit. There it appears as subjective; here it is asserted that the finite stands perennially opposed to the infinite, that it is null in itself, and that it is as null in itself. This is to be brought to consciousness; and the development of the finite shows that it collapses within itself as this contradiction, but actually resolves it in such a way that it is not merely transitory and passes away, but rather that passing-away, Nothing, is not the ultimate, but passes away.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"27.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DUD:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"895210db90ceae3978f04ffd7d0188a740f83d03618434f705858b872d0469fc","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"1. Die Unmittelbarkeit der Endlichkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"1. Die Unmittelbarkeit der Endlichkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU","title":"2. The Limit and the Ought.","order":28,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_2DSU","text":"Dieser Widerspruch ist zwar abstrakt sogleich darin vorhanden, daß das Etwas endlich ist, oder daß das Endliche ist. Aber Etwas oder das Seyn ist nicht mehr abstrakt gesetzt, sondern in sich reflektirt, und entwickelt als Insichseyn, das eine Bestimmung und Beschaffenheit an ihm hat, und noch bestimmter, daß es eine Grenze an ihm hat, welche als das dem Etwas immanente und die Qualität seines Insichseyns ausmachend, die Endlichkeit ist. In diesem Begriffe des endlichen Etwas ist zu sehen, was für Momente enthalten sind.\n\nBestimmung und Beschaffenheit ergaben sich als Seiten für die äußerliche Reflexion; jene enthielt aber schon das Andersseyn als dem Ansich des Etwas angehörig; die Äußerlichkeit des Andersseyns ist einer Seits in der eigenen Innerlichkeit des Etwas, andererseits bleibt sie als Äußerlichkeit unterschieden davon, sie ist noch Äußerlichkeit als solche, aber an dem Etwas. Indem aber ferner das Andersseyn als Grenze, selbst als Negation der Negation, bestimmt ist, so ist das dem Etwas immanente Andersseyn, als die Beziehung der beiden Seiten gesetzt, und die Einheit des Etwas mit sich, dem sowohl die Bestimmung als die Beschaffenheit angehört, seine gegen sich selbst gekehrte Beziehung, die seine immanente Grenze in ihm negirende Beziehung seiner an sich seyenden Bestimmung darauf. Das mit sich identische Insichseyn bezieht sich so auf sich selbst als sein eigenes Nichtseyn, aber als Negation der Negation, als dasselbe negirend, das zugleich Daseyn in ihm behält, denn es ist die Qualität seines Insichseyns. Die eigene Grenze des Etwas, so von ihm als ein Negatives, das zugleich wesentlich ist, gesetzt, ist nicht nur Grenze als solche, sondern Schranke. Aber die Schranke ist nicht allein das als negirt gesetzte; die Negation ist zweischneidig, indem das von ihr als negirt Gesetzte, die Grenze ist; diese nämlich ist überhaupt das Gemeinschaftliche des Etwas und des Anderen, auch Bestimmtheit des Ansichseyns der Bestimmung als solcher. Dieses Ansichseyn hiermit ist als die negative Beziehung auf seine von ihm auch unterschiedene Grenze, auf sich als Schranke, Sollen.\n\nDaß die Grenze, die am Etwas überhaupt ist, Schranke sey, muß es zugleich in sich selbst über sie hinausgehen, sich an ihm selbst auf sie als auf ein Nichtseyendes beziehen. Das Daseyn des Etwas liegt ruhig gleichgültig, gleichsam neben seiner Grenze. Etwas geht aber über seine Grenze nur hinaus, insofern es deren Aufgehobenseyn, das gegen sie negative Ansichseyn ist. Und indem sie in der Bestimmung selbst als Schranke ist, geht Etwas damit über sich selbst hinaus.\n\nDas Sollen enthält also die verdoppelte Bestimmung, einmal sie als an sich seyende Bestimmung gegen die Negation, das andere Mal aber dieselbe als ein Nichtseyn, das als Schranke von ihr unterschieden, aber zugleich selbst ansichseyende Bestimmung ist.\n\nDas Endliche hat sich so als die Beziehung seiner Bestimmung auf seine Grenze bestimmt; jene ist in dieser Beziehung Sollen, diese ist Schranke. Beide sind so Momente des Endlichen, somit beide selbst endlich, sowohl das Sollen, als die Schranke. Aber nur die Schranke ist als das Endliche gesetzt; das Sollen ist nur an sich, somit für uns, beschränkt. Durch seine Beziehung auf die ihm selbst schon immanente Grenze ist es beschränkt, aber diese seine Beschränkung ist in das Ansichseyn eingehüllt, denn nach seinem Daseyn, d. i. nach seiner Bestimmtheit gegen die Schranke ist es als das Ansichseyn gesetzt.\n\nWas seyn soll, ist und ist zugleich nicht. Wenn es wäre, so sollte es nicht bloß seyn. Also das Sollen hat wesentlich eine Schranke. Diese Schranke ist nicht ein Fremdes; das, was nur seyn soll, ist die Bestimmung, die nun gesetzt ist, wie sie in der That ist, nämlich zugleich nur eine Bestimmtheit.\n\nDas An-sich-seyn des Etwas in seiner Bestimmung setzt sich also zum Sollen herab, dadurch daß dasselbe, was sein Ansichseyn ausmacht, in einer und derselben Rücksicht als Nichtseyn ist; und zwar so, daß im Insichseyn, der Negation der Negation, jenes Ansichseyn als die eine Negation (das Negirende) Einheit mit der anderen ist, die zugleich als qualitativ andere, Grenze ist, wodurch jene Einheit als Beziehung auf sie ist. Die Schranke des Endlichen ist nicht ein Äußeres, sondern seine eigene Bestimmung ist auch seine Schranke; und diese ist sowohl sie selbst als auch Sollen; sie ist das Gemeinschaftliche beider, oder vielmehr das, worin beide identisch sind.\n\nAls Sollen geht nun aber ferner das Endliche über seine Schranke hinaus; dieselbe Bestimmtheit, welche seine Negation ist, ist auch aufgehoben, und ist so sein Ansichseyn; seine Grenze ist auch nicht seine Grenze.\n\nAls Sollen ist somit Etwas über seine Schranke erhaben, umgekehrt hat es aber nur als Sollen seine Schranke. Beides ist untrennbar. Etwas hat insofern eine Schranke, als es in seiner Bestimmung die Negation hat, und die Bestimmung ist auch das Aufgehobenseyn der Schranke.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0001","text":"Dieser Widerspruch ist zwar abstrakt sogleich darin vorhanden, daß das Etwas endlich ist, oder daß das Endliche ist. Aber Etwas oder das Seyn ist nicht mehr abstrakt gesetzt, sondern in sich reflektirt, und entwickelt als Insichseyn, das eine Bestimmung und Beschaffenheit an ihm hat, und noch bestimmter, daß es eine Grenze an ihm hat, welche als das dem Etwas immanente und die Qualität seines Insichseyns ausmachend, die Endlichkeit ist. In diesem Begriffe des endlichen Etwas ist zu sehen, was für Momente enthalten sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"28.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0002","text":"Bestimmung und Beschaffenheit ergaben sich als Seiten für die äußerliche Reflexion; jene enthielt aber schon das Andersseyn als dem Ansich des Etwas angehörig; die Äußerlichkeit des Andersseyns ist einer Seits in der eigenen Innerlichkeit des Etwas, andererseits bleibt sie als Äußerlichkeit unterschieden davon, sie ist noch Äußerlichkeit als solche, aber an dem Etwas. Indem aber ferner das Andersseyn als Grenze, selbst als Negation der Negation, bestimmt ist, so ist das dem Etwas immanente Andersseyn, als die Beziehung der beiden Seiten gesetzt, und die Einheit des Etwas mit sich, dem sowohl die Bestimmung als die Beschaffenheit angehört, seine gegen sich selbst gekehrte Beziehung, die seine immanente Grenze in ihm negirende Beziehung seiner an sich seyenden Bestimmung darauf.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"28.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0003","text":"Das mit sich identische Insichseyn bezieht sich so auf sich selbst als sein eigenes Nichtseyn, aber als Negation der Negation, als dasselbe negirend, das zugleich Daseyn in ihm behält, denn es ist die Qualität seines Insichseyns. Die eigene Grenze des Etwas, so von ihm als ein Negatives, das zugleich wesentlich ist, gesetzt, ist nicht nur Grenze als solche, sondern Schranke. Aber die Schranke ist nicht allein das als negirt gesetzte; die Negation ist zweischneidig, indem das von ihr als negirt Gesetzte, die Grenze ist; diese nämlich ist überhaupt das Gemeinschaftliche des Etwas und des Anderen, auch Bestimmtheit des Ansichseyns der Bestimmung als solcher. Dieses Ansichseyn hiermit ist als die negative Beziehung auf seine von ihm auch unterschiedene Grenze, auf sich als Schranke, Sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"28.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0004","text":"Daß die Grenze, die am Etwas überhaupt ist, Schranke sey, muß es zugleich in sich selbst über sie hinausgehen, sich an ihm selbst auf sie als auf ein Nichtseyendes beziehen. Das Daseyn des Etwas liegt ruhig gleichgültig, gleichsam neben seiner Grenze. Etwas geht aber über seine Grenze nur hinaus, insofern es deren Aufgehobenseyn, das gegen sie negative Ansichseyn ist. Und indem sie in der Bestimmung selbst als Schranke ist, geht Etwas damit über sich selbst hinaus.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"28.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0005","text":"Das Sollen enthält also die verdoppelte Bestimmung, einmal sie als an sich seyende Bestimmung gegen die Negation, das andere Mal aber dieselbe als ein Nichtseyn, das als Schranke von ihr unterschieden, aber zugleich selbst ansichseyende Bestimmung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"28.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0006","text":"Das Endliche hat sich so als die Beziehung seiner Bestimmung auf seine Grenze bestimmt; jene ist in dieser Beziehung Sollen, diese ist Schranke. Beide sind so Momente des Endlichen, somit beide selbst endlich, sowohl das Sollen, als die Schranke. Aber nur die Schranke ist als das Endliche gesetzt; das Sollen ist nur an sich, somit für uns, beschränkt. Durch seine Beziehung auf die ihm selbst schon immanente Grenze ist es beschränkt, aber diese seine Beschränkung ist in das Ansichseyn eingehüllt, denn nach seinem Daseyn, d. i. nach seiner Bestimmtheit gegen die Schranke ist es als das Ansichseyn gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"28.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0007","text":"Was seyn soll, ist und ist zugleich nicht. Wenn es wäre, so sollte es nicht bloß seyn. Also das Sollen hat wesentlich eine Schranke. Diese Schranke ist nicht ein Fremdes; das, was nur seyn soll, ist die Bestimmung, die nun gesetzt ist, wie sie in der That ist, nämlich zugleich nur eine Bestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"28.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0008","text":"Das An-sich-seyn des Etwas in seiner Bestimmung setzt sich also zum Sollen herab, dadurch daß dasselbe, was sein Ansichseyn ausmacht, in einer und derselben Rücksicht als Nichtseyn ist; und zwar so, daß im Insichseyn, der Negation der Negation, jenes Ansichseyn als die eine Negation (das Negirende) Einheit mit der anderen ist, die zugleich als qualitativ andere, Grenze ist, wodurch jene Einheit als Beziehung auf sie ist. Die Schranke des Endlichen ist nicht ein Äußeres, sondern seine eigene Bestimmung ist auch seine Schranke; und diese ist sowohl sie selbst als auch Sollen; sie ist das Gemeinschaftliche beider, oder vielmehr das, worin beide identisch sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"28.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0009","text":"Als Sollen geht nun aber ferner das Endliche über seine Schranke hinaus; dieselbe Bestimmtheit, welche seine Negation ist, ist auch aufgehoben, und ist so sein Ansichseyn; seine Grenze ist auch nicht seine Grenze.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"28.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0010","text":"Als Sollen ist somit Etwas über seine Schranke erhaben, umgekehrt hat es aber nur als Sollen seine Schranke. Beides ist untrennbar. Etwas hat insofern eine Schranke, als es in seiner Bestimmung die Negation hat, und die Bestimmung ist auch das Aufgehobenseyn der Schranke.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"28.10"}],"sha256":"8262301ed265c5af20dce7b3e966796565b48d090d45cef022417f05121df57c","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102224811609Z_65a83448","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"2. The Limit and the Ought.","source_sha256":"8262301ed265c5af20dce7b3e966796565b48d090d45cef022417f05121df57c","sha256":"bce81d77a001d1fa644725f2d7f0ec83cc7eead844919a1e40ec4f8482922509","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:22:24.811627+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0001","text":"This contradiction is indeed present at once, abstractly, in the fact that the Something is finite, or that the finite is. But Something, or Being, is no longer posited abstractly, but reflected into itself, and developed as being-within-itself, which has a determination and constitution in it, and, more determinately still, that it has a limit in it, which, as immanent in the Something and constituting the quality of its being-within-itself, is finitude. In this concept of the finite Something, it is to be seen what moments are contained.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"28.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0002","text":"Determination and constitution emerged as sides for external reflection; yet the former already contained otherness as belonging to the in-itself of the Something; the externality of otherness is, on the one hand, in the proper inwardness of the Something; on the other hand, it remains distinguished from it as externality; it is still externality as such, but in the Something. But since, further, otherness is determined as limit, itself as negation of negation, the otherness immanent in the Something is posited as the relation of the two sides, and the unity of the Something with itself, to which both determination and constitution belong, is its relation turned back upon itself, the relation of its determination, which is in itself, to this, a relation negating its immanent limit in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"28.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0003","text":"Being-within-itself, identical with itself, thus relates itself to itself as its own non-being, but as negation of negation, as negating the same, which at the same time retains existence in it, for it is the quality of its being-within-itself. The proper limit of the Something, thus posited by it as a negative which is at the same time essential, is not merely limit as such, but limitation. But limitation is not merely that which is posited as negated; negation is two-edged, since that which is posited by it as negated is the limit; for this is in general the common element of the Something and the Other, also the determinateness of the being-in-itself of determination as such. This being-in-itself is thereby, as the negative relation to its limit, which is also distinct from it, to itself as limitation, ought.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"28.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0004","text":"Since the limit which is in the Something in general is limitation, it must at the same time go beyond it in itself, relate itself in it to it as to a non-being. The existence of the Something lies calmly indifferent, as it were, alongside its limit. But Something goes beyond its limit only insofar as it is its sublatedness, being-in-itself negative toward it. And since it is in determination itself as limitation, Something thereby goes beyond itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"28.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0005","text":"Ought therefore contains the doubled determination: first, it as determination which is in itself over against negation; but second, the same as a non-being, which, as limitation, is distinct from it, yet at the same time is itself determination in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"28.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0006","text":"The finite has thus determined itself as the relation of its determination to its limitation; the former is ought in this relation, the latter is limitation. Both are thus moments of the finite, hence both are themselves finite, both ought and limitation. But only limitation is posited as the finite; ought is only in itself, hence limited for us. Through its relation to the limit already immanent in it itself, it is limited; but this its limitation is enveloped in being-in-itself, for according to its existence, i.e. according to its determinateness over against limitation, it is posited as being-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"28.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0007","text":"What ought to be is and at the same time is not. If it were, it ought not merely to be. Thus ought essentially has a limitation. This limitation is not something alien; that which merely ought to be is the determination which is now posited as it in fact is, namely, at the same time merely a determinateness.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"28.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0008","text":"The being-in-itself of the Something in its determination thus lowers itself to ought, in that the same thing which constitutes its being-in-itself is, in one and the same respect, non-being; and indeed in such a way that in being-within-itself, the negation of negation, that being-in-itself as the one negation (the negating) is unity with the other, which at the same time, as qualitatively other, is limit, whereby that unity is relation to it. The limitation of the finite is not an externality; rather, its own determination is also its limitation; and this is both itself and ought; it is the common element of both, or rather that in which both are identical.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"28.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0009","text":"But as ought, the finite further goes beyond its limitation; the same determinateness which is its negation is also sublated, and is thus its being-in-itself; its limit is also not its limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"28.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0010","text":"As ought, Something is therefore elevated above its limitation; conversely, however, it has its limitation only as ought. Both are inseparable. Something has a limitation insofar as it has negation in its determination, and determination is also the sublatedness of limitation.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"28.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DSU:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"8dcdd04495f67ec29af9f4e64d45dbf65af6c8537d7efe690f65a9afc038d505","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"2. Die Schranke und das Sollen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"2. Die Schranke und das Sollen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3","title":"Remark.","order":29,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_3","text":"Das Sollen hat neuerlich eine große Rolle in der Philosophie, vornehmlich in Beziehung auf Moralität, und metaphysisch überhaupt auch als der letzte und absolute Begriff von der Identität des Ansichseyns oder der Beziehung auf sich selbst und der Bestimmtheit oder der Grenze gespielt.\n\nDu kannst, weil du sollst,—dieser Ausdruck, der viel sagen sollte, liegt im Begriffe des Sollens. Denn das Sollen ist das Hinausseyn über die Schranke; die Grenze ist in demselben aufgehoben, das Ansichseyn des Sollens ist so identische Beziehung auf sich, somit die Abstraktion des Könnens.—Aber umgekehrt ist es eben so richtig: Du kannst nicht, eben weil du sollst. Denn im Sollen liegt ebenso sehr die Schranke als Schranke; jener Formalismus der Möglichkeit hat an ihr eine Realität, ein qualitatives Andersseyn, sich gegenüber, und die Beziehung beider auf einander ist der Widerspruch, somit das Nicht-Können oder vielmehr die Unmöglichkeit.\n\nIm Sollen beginnt das Hinausgehen über die Endlichkeit, die Unendlichkeit. Das Sollen ist dasjenige, was sich in weiterer Entwickelung, nach jener Unmöglichkeit als der Progreß ins Unendliche darstellt.\n\nIn Ansehung der Form der Schranke und des Sollens können zwei Vorurtheile näher gerügt werden. Es pflegt zuerst viel auf die Schranken des Denkens, der Vernunft u.s.f. gehalten zu werden, und es wird behauptet, es könne über die Schranke nicht hinausgegangen werden. In dieser Behauptung liegt die Bewußtlosigkeit, daß darin selbst, daß etwas als Schranke bestimmt ist, darüber bereits hinausgegangen ist. Denn eine Bestimmtheit, Grenze, ist als Schranke nur bestimmt, im Gegensatz gegen sein Anderes überhaupt, also gegen sein Unbeschränktes; das Andere einer Schranke ist eben das Hinaus über dieselbe. Der Stein, das Metall ist nicht über seine Schranke hinaus, darum weil sie für ihn nicht Schranke ist. Wenn jedoch bei solchen allgemeinen Sätzen des verständigen Denkens, daß über die Schranke nicht hinausgegangen werden könne, das Denken sich nicht anwenden will, um zu sehen, was im Begriffe liegt, so kann an die Wirklichkeit verwiesen werden, wo denn solche Sätze sich als das Unwirklichste zeigen. Dadurch eben, daß das Denken etwas Höheres, als die Wirklichkeit seyn, von ihr sich entfernt in höheren Regionen halten soll, dasselbe also selbst als ein Sollen bestimmt ist, geht es einer Seits nicht zum Begriffe fort, und geschieht ihm andererseits, daß es sich ebenso unwahr gegen die Wirklichkeit als gegen den Begriff verhält.—Weil der Stein nicht denkt, nicht einmal empfindet, ist seine Beschränktheit für ihn keine Schranke, d. h. in ihm nicht eine Negation für die Empfindung, Vorstellung, Denken u.s.f. die er nicht hat. Aber auch selbst der Stein ist als Etwas in seine Bestimmung oder sein Ansichseyn und sein Daseyn unterschieden, und insofern geht auch er über seine Schranke hinaus; der Begriff der er an sich ist, enthält die Identität mit seinem Anderen. Ist er eine säurungsfähige Basis, so ist er oxidirbar, neutralisirbar u.s.f. In der Oxidation, Neutralisation u.s.f. hebt sich seine Schranke, nur als Basis da zu seyn, auf; er geht darüber hinaus; sowie die Säure ihre Schranke als Säure zu seyn aufhebt, und es ist in ihr wie in der kaustischen Basis sosehr das Sollen, über ihre Schranke hinauszugehen, vorhanden, daß sie nur mit Gewalt als—wasserlose, d. i. rein nicht neutrale—Säure und kaustische Basis festgehalten werden können.\n\nEnthält aber eine Existenz den Begriff nicht bloß als abstraktes Ansichseyn, sondern als für sich seyende Totalität, als Trieb, als Leben, Empfindung, Vorstellen u.s.f., so vollbringt sie selbst aus ihr dieß, über die Schranke hinaus zu seyn und hinaus zu gehen. Die Pflanze geht über die Schranke, als Keim zu seyn, ebenso über die, als Blüthe, als Frucht, als Blatt zu seyn, hinaus; der Keim wird entfaltete Pflanze, die Blüthe verblüht u.s.f. Das Empfindende in der Schranke des Hungers, Durstes u.s.f. ist der Trieb über diese Schranke hinauszugehen und vollführt dieß Hinausgehen. Es empfindet Schmerz, und das Vorrecht empfindender Natur ist Schmerz zu empfinden; es ist eine Negation in seinem Selbst, und sie ist als eine Schranke in seinem Gefühle bestimmt, eben weil das Empfindende das Gefühl seiner Selbst hat, welches die Totalität ist, das über jene Bestimmtheit hinaus ist. Wäre es nicht darüber hinaus, so empfände es dieselbe nicht als seine Negation und hätte keinen Schmerz.—Die Vernunft aber, das Denken, sollte nicht über die Schranke hinausgehen können,—sie, die das Allgemeine, das für sich über die, d. i. über alle Besonderheit hinaus ist, nur das Hinausgehen über die Schranke ist.—Freilich ist nicht jedes Hinausgehen und Hinausseyn über die Schranke eine wahrhafte Befreiung von derselben, wahrhafte Affirmation; schon das Sollen selbst ist ein solches unvollkommenes Hinausgehen, und die Abstraktion überhaupt. Aber das Hinweisen auf das ganz abstrakte Allgemeine reicht aus gegen die ebenso abstrakte Versicherung, es könne nicht über die Schranke hinausgegangen werden, oder schon das Hinweisen auf das Unendliche überhaupt gegen die Versicherung, daß nicht über das Endliche hinausgegangen werden könne.\n\nEs kann hierbei ein sinnreich scheinender Einfall Leibnitzens erwähnt werden,—wenn ein Magnet Bewußtseyn hätte, so würde derselbe seine Richtung nach Norden für eine Bestimmung seines Willens, ein Gesetz seiner Freyheit ansehen. Vielmehr wenn er Bewußtseyn damit Willen und Freiheit hätte, wäre er denkend, somit würde der Raum für ihn als allgemeiner alle Richtung enthaltender, und damit die eine Richtung nach Norden vielmehr als eine Schranke für seine Freyheit seyn, so sehr als es für den Menschen eine Schranke auf einer Stelle festgehalten zu werden, für die Pflanze aber nicht ist.\n\nDas Sollen andererseits ist das Hinausgehen über die Schranke, aber ein selbst nur endliches Hinausgehen. Es hat daher seine Stelle und sein Gelten im Felde der Endlichkeit, wo es das Ansichseyn gegen das Beschränkte festhält und es als die Regel und das Wesentliche gegen das Nichtige behauptet. Die Pflicht ist ein Sollen gegen den besonderen Willen, gegen die selbstsüchtige Begierde und das willkürliche Interesse gekehrt; dem Willen, insofern er in seiner Beweglichkeit sich vom Wahrhaften isoliren kann, wird dieses als ein Sollen vorgehalten. Diejenigen, welche das Sollen der Moral so hoch halten, und darin, daß das Sollen nicht als Letztes und Wahrhaftes anerkannt wird, meinen, daß die Moralität zerstört werden solle, sowie die Raisonneurs, deren Verstand sich die unaufhörliche Befriedigung giebt, gegen Alles, was da ist, ein Sollen und somit ein Besser-wissen vorbringen zu können, die sich das Sollen darum ebenso wenig wollen rauben lassen, sehen nicht, daß für die Endlichkeit ihrer Kreise das Sollen vollkommen anerkannt wird.—Aber in der Wirklichkeit selbst steht es nicht so traurig um Vernünftigkeit und Gesetz, daß sie nur seyn sollten, dabei bleibt nur das Abstraktum des Ansichseyns,—so wenig als daß das Sollen an ihm selbst perennirend und, was dasselbe ist, die Endlichkeit absolut wäre. Die Kantische und Fichtesche Philosophie giebt als den höchsten Punkt der Auflösung der Widersprüche der Vernunft das Sollen an, was aber vielmehr nur der Standpunkt des Beharrens in der Endlichkeit und damit im Widerspruche, ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0001","text":"Das Sollen hat neuerlich eine große Rolle in der Philosophie, vornehmlich in Beziehung auf Moralität, und metaphysisch überhaupt auch als der letzte und absolute Begriff von der Identität des Ansichseyns oder der Beziehung auf sich selbst und der Bestimmtheit oder der Grenze gespielt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"29.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0002","text":"Du kannst, weil du sollst,—dieser Ausdruck, der viel sagen sollte, liegt im Begriffe des Sollens. Denn das Sollen ist das Hinausseyn über die Schranke; die Grenze ist in demselben aufgehoben, das Ansichseyn des Sollens ist so identische Beziehung auf sich, somit die Abstraktion des Könnens.—Aber umgekehrt ist es eben so richtig: Du kannst nicht, eben weil du sollst. Denn im Sollen liegt ebenso sehr die Schranke als Schranke; jener Formalismus der Möglichkeit hat an ihr eine Realität, ein qualitatives Andersseyn, sich gegenüber, und die Beziehung beider auf einander ist der Widerspruch, somit das Nicht-Können oder vielmehr die Unmöglichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"29.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0003","text":"Im Sollen beginnt das Hinausgehen über die Endlichkeit, die Unendlichkeit. Das Sollen ist dasjenige, was sich in weiterer Entwickelung, nach jener Unmöglichkeit als der Progreß ins Unendliche darstellt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"29.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0004","text":"In Ansehung der Form der Schranke und des Sollens können zwei Vorurtheile näher gerügt werden. Es pflegt zuerst viel auf die Schranken des Denkens, der Vernunft u.s.f. gehalten zu werden, und es wird behauptet, es könne über die Schranke nicht hinausgegangen werden. In dieser Behauptung liegt die Bewußtlosigkeit, daß darin selbst, daß etwas als Schranke bestimmt ist, darüber bereits hinausgegangen ist. Denn eine Bestimmtheit, Grenze, ist als Schranke nur bestimmt, im Gegensatz gegen sein Anderes überhaupt, also gegen sein Unbeschränktes; das Andere einer Schranke ist eben das Hinaus über dieselbe. Der Stein, das Metall ist nicht über seine Schranke hinaus, darum weil sie für ihn nicht Schranke ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"29.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0005","text":"Wenn jedoch bei solchen allgemeinen Sätzen des verständigen Denkens, daß über die Schranke nicht hinausgegangen werden könne, das Denken sich nicht anwenden will, um zu sehen, was im Begriffe liegt, so kann an die Wirklichkeit verwiesen werden, wo denn solche Sätze sich als das Unwirklichste zeigen. Dadurch eben, daß das Denken etwas Höheres, als die Wirklichkeit seyn, von ihr sich entfernt in höheren Regionen halten soll, dasselbe also selbst als ein Sollen bestimmt ist, geht es einer Seits nicht zum Begriffe fort, und geschieht ihm andererseits, daß es sich ebenso unwahr gegen die Wirklichkeit als gegen den Begriff verhält.—Weil der Stein nicht denkt, nicht einmal empfindet, ist seine Beschränktheit für ihn keine Schranke, d. h. in ihm nicht eine Negation für die Empfindung, Vorstellung, Denken u.s.f. die er nicht hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"29.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0006","text":"Aber auch selbst der Stein ist als Etwas in seine Bestimmung oder sein Ansichseyn und sein Daseyn unterschieden, und insofern geht auch er über seine Schranke hinaus; der Begriff der er an sich ist, enthält die Identität mit seinem Anderen. Ist er eine säurungsfähige Basis, so ist er oxidirbar, neutralisirbar u.s.f. In der Oxidation, Neutralisation u.s.f. hebt sich seine Schranke, nur als Basis da zu seyn, auf; er geht darüber hinaus; sowie die Säure ihre Schranke als Säure zu seyn aufhebt, und es ist in ihr wie in der kaustischen Basis sosehr das Sollen, über ihre Schranke hinauszugehen, vorhanden, daß sie nur mit Gewalt als—wasserlose, d. i. rein nicht neutrale—Säure und kaustische Basis festgehalten werden können.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"29.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0007","text":"Enthält aber eine Existenz den Begriff nicht bloß als abstraktes Ansichseyn, sondern als für sich seyende Totalität, als Trieb, als Leben, Empfindung, Vorstellen u.s.f., so vollbringt sie selbst aus ihr dieß, über die Schranke hinaus zu seyn und hinaus zu gehen. Die Pflanze geht über die Schranke, als Keim zu seyn, ebenso über die, als Blüthe, als Frucht, als Blatt zu seyn, hinaus; der Keim wird entfaltete Pflanze, die Blüthe verblüht u.s.f. Das Empfindende in der Schranke des Hungers, Durstes u.s.f. ist der Trieb über diese Schranke hinauszugehen und vollführt dieß Hinausgehen. Es empfindet Schmerz, und das Vorrecht empfindender Natur ist Schmerz zu empfinden; es ist eine Negation in seinem Selbst, und sie ist als eine Schranke in seinem Gefühle bestimmt, eben weil das Empfindende das Gefühl seiner Selbst hat, welches die Totalität ist, das über jene Bestimmtheit hinaus ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"29.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0008","text":"Wäre es nicht darüber hinaus, so empfände es dieselbe nicht als seine Negation und hätte keinen Schmerz.—Die Vernunft aber, das Denken, sollte nicht über die Schranke hinausgehen können,—sie, die das Allgemeine, das für sich über die, d. i. über alle Besonderheit hinaus ist, nur das Hinausgehen über die Schranke ist.—Freilich ist nicht jedes Hinausgehen und Hinausseyn über die Schranke eine wahrhafte Befreiung von derselben, wahrhafte Affirmation; schon das Sollen selbst ist ein solches unvollkommenes Hinausgehen, und die Abstraktion überhaupt. Aber das Hinweisen auf das ganz abstrakte Allgemeine reicht aus gegen die ebenso abstrakte Versicherung, es könne nicht über die Schranke hinausgegangen werden, oder schon das Hinweisen auf das Unendliche überhaupt gegen die Versicherung, daß nicht über das Endliche hinausgegangen werden könne.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"29.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0009","text":"Es kann hierbei ein sinnreich scheinender Einfall Leibnitzens erwähnt werden,—wenn ein Magnet Bewußtseyn hätte, so würde derselbe seine Richtung nach Norden für eine Bestimmung seines Willens, ein Gesetz seiner Freyheit ansehen. Vielmehr wenn er Bewußtseyn damit Willen und Freiheit hätte, wäre er denkend, somit würde der Raum für ihn als allgemeiner alle Richtung enthaltender, und damit die eine Richtung nach Norden vielmehr als eine Schranke für seine Freyheit seyn, so sehr als es für den Menschen eine Schranke auf einer Stelle festgehalten zu werden, für die Pflanze aber nicht ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"29.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0010","text":"Das Sollen andererseits ist das Hinausgehen über die Schranke, aber ein selbst nur endliches Hinausgehen. Es hat daher seine Stelle und sein Gelten im Felde der Endlichkeit, wo es das Ansichseyn gegen das Beschränkte festhält und es als die Regel und das Wesentliche gegen das Nichtige behauptet. Die Pflicht ist ein Sollen gegen den besonderen Willen, gegen die selbstsüchtige Begierde und das willkürliche Interesse gekehrt; dem Willen, insofern er in seiner Beweglichkeit sich vom Wahrhaften isoliren kann, wird dieses als ein Sollen vorgehalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"29.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0011","text":"Diejenigen, welche das Sollen der Moral so hoch halten, und darin, daß das Sollen nicht als Letztes und Wahrhaftes anerkannt wird, meinen, daß die Moralität zerstört werden solle, sowie die Raisonneurs, deren Verstand sich die unaufhörliche Befriedigung giebt, gegen Alles, was da ist, ein Sollen und somit ein Besser-wissen vorbringen zu können, die sich das Sollen darum ebenso wenig wollen rauben lassen, sehen nicht, daß für die Endlichkeit ihrer Kreise das Sollen vollkommen anerkannt wird.—Aber in der Wirklichkeit selbst steht es nicht so traurig um Vernünftigkeit und Gesetz, daß sie nur seyn sollten, dabei bleibt nur das Abstraktum des Ansichseyns,—so wenig als daß das Sollen an ihm selbst perennirend und, was dasselbe ist, die Endlichkeit absolut wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"29.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0012","text":"Die Kantische und Fichtesche Philosophie giebt als den höchsten Punkt der Auflösung der Widersprüche der Vernunft das Sollen an, was aber vielmehr nur der Standpunkt des Beharrens in der Endlichkeit und damit im Widerspruche, ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"29.12"}],"sha256":"844608c5e303c37399505128e13ce973c49cca5b362fd11e6655d639c60b7683","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102239922462Z_7e71a123","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"844608c5e303c37399505128e13ce973c49cca5b362fd11e6655d639c60b7683","sha256":"2e70f6410bdcf42aa0d013d9a415cc3c81b3a5f6cc542a8d73110227cfb333b6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:22:39.922481+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0001","text":"Ought has lately played a great role in philosophy, chiefly in relation to morality, and metaphysically in general also as the ultimate and absolute concept of the identity of being-in-itself, or of relation to self, and determinateness, or limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"29.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0002","text":"You can, because you ought,—this expression, which was meant to say much, lies in the concept of ought. For ought is being beyond the limit; in it the limit is sublated; the being-in-itself of ought is thus identical relation to self, hence the abstraction of can.—But conversely it is equally correct: You cannot, precisely because you ought. For in ought the limit is equally present as limit; that formalism of possibility has in it a reality, a qualitative other-being, confronting it, and the relation of the two to one another is contradiction, hence non-can, or rather impossibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"29.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0003","text":"In ought begins the going beyond finitude, infinity. Ought is that which, in further development, after that impossibility, presents itself as progress into infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"29.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0004","text":"With regard to the form of limit and ought, two prejudices may be more closely censured. First, much is customarily made of the limits of thinking, of reason, etc., and it is asserted that one cannot go beyond the limit. In this assertion lies the unconsciousness that, in the very fact that something is determined as a limit, one has already gone beyond it. For a determinateness, a limit, is determined as a limit only in opposition to its other in general, hence to its unlimited; the other of a limit is precisely what lies beyond it. Stone, metal, does not go beyond its limit because for it the limit is not a limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"29.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0005","text":"But if, in the case of such general propositions of understanding thought, that one cannot go beyond the limit, thinking does not wish to exert itself in order to see what lies in the concept, then one may refer to actuality, whereupon such propositions show themselves to be the most unreal. Precisely by the fact that thinking is supposed to be something higher than actuality, to hold itself apart from it in higher regions, and is therefore itself determined as an ought, it does not, on the one hand, advance to the concept, and, on the other hand, it happens to it that it relates itself as untruly to actuality as to the concept.—Because stone does not think, does not even feel, its restrictedness is for it no limit, i.e. not in it a negation for the feeling, representation, thinking, etc. that it does not possess.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"29.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0006","text":"But even stone itself, as something, is distinguished into its determinateness or its being-in-itself and its existence, and insofar it too goes beyond its limit; the concept that it is in itself contains identity with its other. If it is an acidifiable base, then it is oxidizable, neutralizable, etc. In oxidation, neutralization, etc., its limit of existing only as a base is sublated; it goes beyond it; just as acid sublates its limit of being acid, and in it, as in the caustic base, ought, to go beyond its limit, is present to such an extent that they can be retained only by force as—anhydrous, i.e. purely non-neutral—acid and caustic base.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"29.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0007","text":"But if an existence contains the concept not merely as abstract being-in-itself, but as a totality that is for itself, as drive, as life, sensation, representation, etc., then it itself accomplishes from within itself this being beyond the limit and going beyond it. The plant goes beyond the limit of being a germ, just as it goes beyond that of being blossom, fruit, leaf; the germ becomes the unfolded plant, the blossom fades, etc. That which feels, in the limit of hunger, thirst, etc., is the drive to go beyond this limit and accomplishes this going beyond. It feels pain, and the prerogative of sentient nature is to feel pain; there is a negation in its self, and it is determined as a limit in its feeling, precisely because that which feels has the feeling of its self, which is the totality that is beyond that determinateness.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"29.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0008","text":"Were it not beyond it, it would not feel it as its negation and would have no pain.—But reason, thinking, should not be able to go beyond the limit,—it, which is the universal, which for itself is beyond particularity, i.e. beyond all particularity, is only the going beyond the limit.—Certainly, not every going beyond and being beyond the limit is a genuine liberation from it, a genuine affirmation; ought itself is already such an imperfect going beyond, as is abstraction in general. But pointing to the wholly abstract universal suffices against the equally abstract assurance that one cannot go beyond the limit; or merely pointing to infinity in general suffices against the assurance that one cannot go beyond the finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"29.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0009","text":"Here one may mention a seemingly ingenious notion of Leibniz,—if a magnet had consciousness, it would regard its direction toward the north as a determination of its will, a law of its freedom. Rather, if it had consciousness, and therewith will and freedom, it would be thinking; thus space would be for it, as the universal containing every direction, and thereby the one direction toward the north would rather be a limit upon its freedom, just as being held fast in one place is a limit for the human being, but not for the plant.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"29.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0010","text":"Ought, on the other hand, is going beyond the limit, but itself only a finite going beyond. It therefore has its place and its validity in the field of finitude, where it maintains being-in-itself against what is limited and asserts it as the rule and the essential against the null. Duty is an ought directed against the particular will, against selfish desire and arbitrary interest; to the will, insofar as in its mobility it can isolate itself from the true, this is held up as an ought.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"29.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0011","text":"Those who hold the ought of morality so highly, and who think that morality is to be destroyed by the fact that ought is not recognized as the ultimate and the true, as well as the reasoners whose understanding gives itself the continual satisfaction of being able to advance an ought, and hence a knowing-better, against everything that exists, and who therefore wish just as little to let ought be taken from them, do not see that ought is fully recognized for the finitude of their spheres.—But in actuality itself it is not so sadly situated with rationality and law that they should merely be, in which case only the abstraction of being-in-itself remains,—any more than ought should be perennial in itself and, what is the same thing, finitude should be absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"29.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0012","text":"Kantian and Fichtean philosophy posit ought as the highest point of the resolution of the contradictions of reason, whereas it is rather only the standpoint of persisting in finitude and thereby in contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"29.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_3:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"21999a454bcd91e3499fab51486f2a474e1720155ad9af41e5d5590153e00239","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BDE","title":"3. Transition of the Finite into the Infinite.","order":30,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_3BDE","text":"Das Sollen für sich enthält die Schranke, und die Schranke das Sollen. Ihre Beziehung auf einander ist das Endliche selbst, das sie beide in seinem Insichseyn enthält. Diese Momente seiner Bestimmung sind sich qualitativ entgegengesetzt; die Schranke ist bestimmt als das Negative des Sollens, und das Sollen ebenso als das Negative der Schranke. Das Endliche ist so der Widerspruch seiner in sich; es hebt sich auf, vergeht. Aber dieß sein Resultat, das Negative überhaupt, ist à) seine Bestimmung selbst; denn es ist das Negative des Negativen. So ist das Endliche in dem Vergehen nicht vergangen; es ist zunächst nur ein anderes Endliches geworden, welches aber ebenso das Vergehen als Übergehen in ein anderes Endliches ist, und so fort, etwa ins Unendliche. Aber ß) näher dieß Resultat betrachtet, so hat das Endliche in seinem Vergehen, dieser Negation seiner selbst, sein Ansichseyn erreicht, es ist darin mit sich selbst zusammengegangen. Jedes seiner Momente enthält eben dieß Resultat; das Sollen geht über die Schranke, d. i. über sich selbst hinaus; über es hinaus aber oder sein Anderes ist nur die Schranke selbst. Die Schranke aber weist über sich selbst unmittelbar hinaus zu seinem Anderen, welches das Sollen ist; dieses aber ist dieselbe Entzweiung des Ansichseyns und des Daseyns wie die Schranke, ist dasselbe; über sich hinaus geht sie daher ebenso nur mit sich zusammen. Diese Identität mit sich, die Negation der Negation, ist affirmatives Seyn, so das Andere des Endlichen, als welches die erste Negation zu seiner Bestimmtheit haben soll;—jenes Andere ist das Unendliche.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BDE:P0001","text":"Das Sollen für sich enthält die Schranke, und die Schranke das Sollen. Ihre Beziehung auf einander ist das Endliche selbst, das sie beide in seinem Insichseyn enthält. Diese Momente seiner Bestimmung sind sich qualitativ entgegengesetzt; die Schranke ist bestimmt als das Negative des Sollens, und das Sollen ebenso als das Negative der Schranke. Das Endliche ist so der Widerspruch seiner in sich; es hebt sich auf, vergeht. Aber dieß sein Resultat, das Negative überhaupt, ist à) seine Bestimmung selbst; denn es ist das Negative des Negativen. So ist das Endliche in dem Vergehen nicht vergangen; es ist zunächst nur ein anderes Endliches geworden, welches aber ebenso das Vergehen als Übergehen in ein anderes Endliches ist, und so fort, etwa ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"30.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BDE:P0002","text":"Aber ß) näher dieß Resultat betrachtet, so hat das Endliche in seinem Vergehen, dieser Negation seiner selbst, sein Ansichseyn erreicht, es ist darin mit sich selbst zusammengegangen. Jedes seiner Momente enthält eben dieß Resultat; das Sollen geht über die Schranke, d. i. über sich selbst hinaus; über es hinaus aber oder sein Anderes ist nur die Schranke selbst. Die Schranke aber weist über sich selbst unmittelbar hinaus zu seinem Anderen, welches das Sollen ist; dieses aber ist dieselbe Entzweiung des Ansichseyns und des Daseyns wie die Schranke, ist dasselbe; über sich hinaus geht sie daher ebenso nur mit sich zusammen. Diese Identität mit sich, die Negation der Negation, ist affirmatives Seyn, so das Andere des Endlichen, als welches die erste Negation zu seiner Bestimmtheit haben soll;—jenes Andere ist das Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"30.2"}],"sha256":"39fc3540ad3162beda89b6ae623ce807c9b0ce138c16191d9db358f2c9652d6d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102244609920Z_11909857","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"3. Transition of the Finite into the Infinite.","source_sha256":"39fc3540ad3162beda89b6ae623ce807c9b0ce138c16191d9db358f2c9652d6d","sha256":"8d48cd2d017e10b603db283551f743c4d6721278bc412ffe81b0dcc0a4a2fbdf","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:22:44.609930+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BDE:P0001","text":"Oughtness in itself contains the limit, and the limit [contains] oughtness. Their relation to one another is the finite itself, which contains them both in its being-within-itself. These moments of its determination are qualitatively opposed to one another; the limit is determined as the negative of oughtness, and oughtness likewise as the negative of the limit. The finite is thus the contradiction of itself within itself; it sublates itself, passes away. But this its result, the negative in general, is α) its determination itself; for it is the negative of the negative. Thus the finite has not passed away in passing away; it has at first only become another finite, which, however, is likewise a passing away as transition into another finite, and so on, perhaps to infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"30.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BDE:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BDE:P0002","text":"But β) considered more closely, this result is such that the finite, in its passing away, this negation of itself, has attained its being-in-itself; in it, it has come together with itself. Each of its moments contains precisely this result; oughtness goes beyond the limit, i.e. beyond itself; but beyond it, or its other, is only the limit itself. The limit, however, points immediately beyond itself to its other, which is oughtness; but this is the same diremption of being-in-itself and determinate being as the limit, is the same thing; thus in going beyond itself it likewise only comes together with itself. This identity with itself, the negation of negation, is affirmative being, thus the other of the finite, which is supposed to have the first negation as its determinateness;—that other is the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"30.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BDE:P0002"]}],"source_digest":"36766f70cdbd5a24f31e7f82f6162c8f4a4d0d5777d19bfaebc31f5992fc0b12","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"3. Übergang des Endlichen in das Unendliche."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"3. Übergang des Endlichen in das Unendliche.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0","title":"C. Infinity.","order":31,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDU0","text":"Das Unendliche in seinem einfachen Begriff kann zunächst als eine neue Definition des Absoluten angesehen werden; es ist als die bestimmungslose Beziehung auf sich gesetzt als Seyn und Werden. Die Formen des Daseyns fallen aus in der Reihe der Bestimmungen, die für Definitionen des Absoluten angesehen werden können, da die Formen jener Sphäre für sich unmittelbar nur als Bestimmtheiten, als endliche überhaupt, gesetzt sind. Das Unendliche aber gilt schlechthin für absolut, da es ausdrücklich als Negation des Endlichen bestimmt ist, hiermit auf die Beschränktheit, deren das Seyn und Werden, wenn sie auch an ihnen keine Beschränktheit haben oder zeigen, doch etwa fähig seyn könnten, im Unendlichen ausdrücklich Beziehung genommen und eine solche an ihm negirt ist.\n\nDamit aber selbst ist das Unendliche nicht schon in der That der Beschränktheit und Endlichkeit entnommen; die Hauptsache ist, den wahrhaften Begriff der Unendlichkeit von der schlechten Unendlichkeit, das Unendliche der Vernunft von dem Unendlichen des Verstandes zu unterscheiden; doch Letzteres ist das verendlichte Unendliche, und es wird sich ergeben, daß eben indem das Unendliche vom Endlichen rein und entfernt gehalten werden soll, es nur verendlicht wird.\n\nDas Unendliche ist\n\na. in einfacher Bestimmung das Affirmative als Negation des Endlichen;\n\nb. es ist aber damit in Wechselbestimmung mit dem Endlichen, und ist das abstrakte, einseitige Unendliche;\n\nc. das Sich-aufheben dieses Unendlichen, wie des Endlichen als Ein Proceß,—ist das wahrhafte Unendliche.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0001","text":"Das Unendliche in seinem einfachen Begriff kann zunächst als eine neue Definition des Absoluten angesehen werden; es ist als die bestimmungslose Beziehung auf sich gesetzt als Seyn und Werden. Die Formen des Daseyns fallen aus in der Reihe der Bestimmungen, die für Definitionen des Absoluten angesehen werden können, da die Formen jener Sphäre für sich unmittelbar nur als Bestimmtheiten, als endliche überhaupt, gesetzt sind. Das Unendliche aber gilt schlechthin für absolut, da es ausdrücklich als Negation des Endlichen bestimmt ist, hiermit auf die Beschränktheit, deren das Seyn und Werden, wenn sie auch an ihnen keine Beschränktheit haben oder zeigen, doch etwa fähig seyn könnten, im Unendlichen ausdrücklich Beziehung genommen und eine solche an ihm negirt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"31.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0002","text":"Damit aber selbst ist das Unendliche nicht schon in der That der Beschränktheit und Endlichkeit entnommen; die Hauptsache ist, den wahrhaften Begriff der Unendlichkeit von der schlechten Unendlichkeit, das Unendliche der Vernunft von dem Unendlichen des Verstandes zu unterscheiden; doch Letzteres ist das verendlichte Unendliche, und es wird sich ergeben, daß eben indem das Unendliche vom Endlichen rein und entfernt gehalten werden soll, es nur verendlicht wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"31.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0003","text":"Das Unendliche ist","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"31.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0004","text":"a. in einfacher Bestimmung das Affirmative als Negation des Endlichen;","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"31.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0005","text":"b. es ist aber damit in Wechselbestimmung mit dem Endlichen, und ist das abstrakte, einseitige Unendliche;","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"31.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0006","text":"c. das Sich-aufheben dieses Unendlichen, wie des Endlichen als Ein Proceß,—ist das wahrhafte Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"31.6"}],"sha256":"9fe5164a95156b67bb627a03b0aae567138a00ea4a48a144a25082f7374b9d6a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102248730874Z_52d5f12b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Infinity.","source_sha256":"9fe5164a95156b67bb627a03b0aae567138a00ea4a48a144a25082f7374b9d6a","sha256":"d18d7d9dde85735fcc53b70a3035b532ddda35814f359238a6b3a5887a6bf19d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:22:48.730885+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0001","text":"The infinite, in its simple concept, can at first be regarded as a new definition of the absolute; it is posited as indeterminate relation to itself, as being and becoming. The forms of determinate being drop out in the series of determinations that can be regarded as definitions of the absolute, since the forms of that sphere are, for themselves, immediately posited only as determinacies, as finite in general. But the infinite counts without qualification as absolute, since it is expressly determined as the negation of the finite, and thus relation has expressly been taken, in the infinite, to the limitation of which being and becoming, even if they have or exhibit no limitation in themselves, might nevertheless perhaps be capable, and such limitation has been negated in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"31.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0002","text":"But thereby the infinite has not in fact already been withdrawn from limitation and finitude; the main thing is to distinguish the true concept of infinity from bad infinity, the infinite of reason from the infinite of the understanding; yet the latter is the finitized infinite, and it will emerge that precisely in so far as the infinite is to be kept pure and removed from the finite, it is only finitized.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"31.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0003","text":"The infinite is","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"31.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0004","text":"a. in simple determination, the affirmative as negation of the finite;","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"31.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0005","text":"b. but thereby it is in reciprocal determination with the finite, and is the abstract, one-sided infinite;","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"31.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0006","text":"c. the self-sublation of this infinite, as of the finite, as one process,—is the true infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"31.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDU0:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"cc4f5ca2e88da7879b39889eec30240dedb2b8a968eb97adc8e25cb6e087ccfa","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Die Unendlichkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Die Unendlichkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0","title":"a. The Infinite in General.","order":32,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DUB0","text":"Das Unendliche ist die Negation der Negation, das Affirmative, das Seyn, das sich aus der Beschränktheit wieder hergestellt hat. Das Unendliche ist, und in intensiverem Sinn als das erste unmittelbare Seyn; es ist das wahrhafte Seyn; die Erhebung aus der Schranke. Bei dem Namen des Unendlichen geht dem Gemüth und dem Geiste sein Licht auf, denn er ist darin nicht nur abstrakt bei sich, sondern erhebt sich zu sich selbst, zum Lichte seines Denkens, seiner Allgemeinheit, seiner Freiheit.\n\nZuerst hat sich für den Begriff des Unendlichen ergeben, daß das Daseyn in seinem Ansichseyn sich als Endliches bestimmt, und über die Schranke hinausgeht. Es ist die Natur des Endlichen selbst, über sich hinauszugehen, seine Negation zu negiren und unendlich zu werden. Das Unendliche steht somit nicht als ein für sich Fertiges über dem Endlichen, so daß das Endliche außer oder unter jenem sein Bleiben hätte und behielte. Noch gehen wir nur als eine subjektive Vernunft über das Endliche ins Unendliche hinaus. Wie wenn man sagt, daß das Unendliche der Vernunftbegriff sey, und wir uns durch die Vernunft über das Zeitliche erheben, so läßt man dieß ganz unbeschadet des Endlichen geschehen, welches jene ihm äußerlich bleibende Erhebung nichts angeht. Insofern aber das Endliche selbst in die Unendlichkeit erhoben wird, ist es eben so wenig eine fremde Gewalt, welche ihm dieß anthut, sondern es ist dieß seine Natur, sich auf sich als Schranke, sowohl als Schranke als solche, wie als Sollen, zu beziehen, und über dieselbe hinauszugehen, oder vielmehr als Beziehung auf sich sie negirt zu haben und über sie hinaus zu seyn. Nicht im Aufheben der Endlichkeit überhaupt wird die Unendlichkeit überhaupt, sondern das Endliche ist nur dieß, selbst durch seine Natur dazu zu werden. Die Unendlichkeit ist seine affirmative Bestimmung, das was es wahrhaft an sich ist.\n\nSo ist das Endliche im Unendlichen verschwunden, und was ist, ist nur das Unendliche.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0001","text":"Das Unendliche ist die Negation der Negation, das Affirmative, das Seyn, das sich aus der Beschränktheit wieder hergestellt hat. Das Unendliche ist, und in intensiverem Sinn als das erste unmittelbare Seyn; es ist das wahrhafte Seyn; die Erhebung aus der Schranke. Bei dem Namen des Unendlichen geht dem Gemüth und dem Geiste sein Licht auf, denn er ist darin nicht nur abstrakt bei sich, sondern erhebt sich zu sich selbst, zum Lichte seines Denkens, seiner Allgemeinheit, seiner Freiheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"32.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0002","text":"Zuerst hat sich für den Begriff des Unendlichen ergeben, daß das Daseyn in seinem Ansichseyn sich als Endliches bestimmt, und über die Schranke hinausgeht. Es ist die Natur des Endlichen selbst, über sich hinauszugehen, seine Negation zu negiren und unendlich zu werden. Das Unendliche steht somit nicht als ein für sich Fertiges über dem Endlichen, so daß das Endliche außer oder unter jenem sein Bleiben hätte und behielte. Noch gehen wir nur als eine subjektive Vernunft über das Endliche ins Unendliche hinaus. Wie wenn man sagt, daß das Unendliche der Vernunftbegriff sey, und wir uns durch die Vernunft über das Zeitliche erheben, so läßt man dieß ganz unbeschadet des Endlichen geschehen, welches jene ihm äußerlich bleibende Erhebung nichts angeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"32.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0003","text":"Insofern aber das Endliche selbst in die Unendlichkeit erhoben wird, ist es eben so wenig eine fremde Gewalt, welche ihm dieß anthut, sondern es ist dieß seine Natur, sich auf sich als Schranke, sowohl als Schranke als solche, wie als Sollen, zu beziehen, und über dieselbe hinauszugehen, oder vielmehr als Beziehung auf sich sie negirt zu haben und über sie hinaus zu seyn. Nicht im Aufheben der Endlichkeit überhaupt wird die Unendlichkeit überhaupt, sondern das Endliche ist nur dieß, selbst durch seine Natur dazu zu werden. Die Unendlichkeit ist seine affirmative Bestimmung, das was es wahrhaft an sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"32.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0004","text":"So ist das Endliche im Unendlichen verschwunden, und was ist, ist nur das Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"32.4"}],"sha256":"48f2285c6ca6eba503635bba5593d67c2d1502e9b57bc90e93ead60f18e80fe5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102254753952Z_a14117f7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. The Infinite in General.","source_sha256":"48f2285c6ca6eba503635bba5593d67c2d1502e9b57bc90e93ead60f18e80fe5","sha256":"1d2e6300522072d27ef6f6ecf9458d6b066da317bd847c3994320601336141ee","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:22:54.753978+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0001","text":"The infinite is the negation of negation, the affirmative, being, which has restored itself out of limitation. The infinite is, and in a more intensive sense than the first immediate being; it is true being; the elevation out of the limit. At the name of the infinite, the mind and the spirit are illumined, for in it they are not merely abstractly with themselves, but raise themselves to themselves, to the light of their thinking, their universality, their freedom.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"32.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0002","text":"First, it has emerged for the concept of the infinite that determinate being, in its being-in-itself, determines itself as finite and goes beyond the limit. It is the nature of the finite itself to go beyond itself, to negate its negation and become infinite. The infinite thus does not stand as something complete for itself above the finite, so that the finite would have and retain its abiding outside or beneath the former. Nor do we merely, as a subjective reason, go beyond the finite into the infinite. When, for example, one says that the infinite is the concept of reason, and that through reason we raise ourselves above the temporal, this is allowed to occur wholly without prejudice to the finite, which is not affected by that elevation remaining external to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"32.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0003","text":"But insofar as the finite itself is elevated into infinity, this is just as little a foreign power that does this to it; rather, this is its nature: to relate itself to itself as limit, both as limit as such and as ought, and to go beyond the same, or rather, as relation to itself, to have negated it and to be beyond it. It is not in the sublation of finitude in general that infinity in general comes to be; rather, the finite is only this, to become so itself through its nature. Infinity is its affirmative determination, that which it truly is in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"32.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0004","text":"Thus the finite has vanished in the infinite, and what is, is only the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"32.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DUB0:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"5b65d51b59840b8ee12ede9832f2528108059499ef101f110ee17d3b6d038385","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Das Unendliche überhaupt."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Das Unendliche überhaupt.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE","title":"b. Reciprocal Determination of the Finite and the Infinite.","order":33,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BWDE","text":"Das Unendliche ist; in dieser Unmittelbarkeit ist es zugleich die Negation eines Andern, des Endlichen. So als seyend und zugleich als Nichtseyn eines Andern ist es in die Kategorie des Etwas als eines bestimmten überhaupt, näher weil es das in sich-reflektirte, vermittelst des Aufhebens der Bestimmtheit überhaupt resultirende Daseyn, hiermit als das von seiner Bestimmtheit unterschiedene Daseyn gesetzt ist,—in die Kategorie des Etwas mit einer Grenze, zurückgefallen. Das Endliche steht nach dieser Bestimmtheit dem Unendlichen als reales Daseyn gegenüber; so stehen sie in qualitativer Beziehung als außer einander bleibende; das unmittelbare Seyn des Unendlichen erweckt das Seyn seiner Negation, des Endlichen wieder, das zunächst im Unendlichen verschwunden schien.\n\nAber das Unendliche und Endliche sind nicht nur in diesen Kategorien der Beziehung; die beiden Seiten sind weiter bestimmt, als bloß Andere gegeneinander zu seyn. Die Endliche ist nämlich die als Schranke gesetzte Schranke, es ist das Daseyn mit der Bestimmung gesetzt in sein Ansichseyn überzugehen, unendlich zu werden. Die Unendlichkeit ist das Nichts des Endlichen, dessen Ansichseyn und Sollen, aber dieses zugleich als in sich reflektirt, das ausgeführte Sollen, nur sich auf sich beziehendes ganz affirmatives Seyn. In der Unendlichkeit ist die Befriedigung vorhanden, daß alle Bestimmtheit, Veränderung, alle Schranke und mit ihr das Sollen selbst verschwunden, als aufgehoben, das Nichts des Endlichen gesetzt ist. Als diese Negation des Endlichen ist das Ansichseyn bestimmt, welches so als Negation der Negation in sich affirmativ ist. Diese Affirmation jedoch ist als qualitativ unmittelbare Beziehung auf sich; Seyn; hierdurch ist das Unendliche auf die Kategorie zurückgeführt, daß es das Endliche als ein Anderes sich gegenüber hat; seine negative Natur ist als die seyende, hiermit erste und unmittelbare Negation gesetzt. Das Unendliche ist auf diese Weise mit dem Gegensatze gegen das Endliche behaftet, welches, als Anderes, das bestimmte, reale Daseyn zugleich bleibt, obschon es in seinem Ansichseyn, dem Unendlichen, zugleich als aufgehoben gesetzt ist; dieses ist das Nicht-endliche; —ein Seyn in der Bestimmtheit der Negation. Gegen das Endliche, den Kreis der seyenden Bestimmtheiten, der Realitäten, ist das Unendliche das unbestimmte Leere, das Jenseits des Endlichen, welches sein Ansichseyn nicht an seinem Daseyn, das ein bestimmtes ist, hat.\n\nSo das Unendliche gegen das Endliche in qualitativer Beziehung von Anderen zu einander gesetzt, ist es das Schlecht-Unendliche, das Unendliche des Verstandes zu nennen, dem es für die höchste, für die absolute Wahrheit gilt; ihn zum Bewußtseyn darüber zu bringen, daß, indem er seine Befriedigung in der Versöhnung der Wahrheit erreicht zu haben meint, er in dem unversöhnten, unaufgelösten, absoluten Widerspruche sich befindet, müßten die Widersprüche bewirken, in die er nach allen Seiten verfällt, so wie er sich auf die Anwendung und Explikation dieser seiner Kategorien einläßt.\n\nDieser Widerspruch ist sogleich darin vorhanden, daß dem Unendlichen das Endliche als Daseyn gegenüber bleibt; es sind damit zwei Bestimmtheiten; es giebt zwei Welten, eine unendliche und eine endliche, und in ihrer Beziehung ist das Unendliche nur Grenze des Endlichen, und ist damit nur ein bestimmtes, selbst endliches Unendliches.\n\nDieser Widerspruch entwickelt seinen Inhalt zu ausdrücklicheren Formen.—Das Endliche ist das reale Daseyn, welches so verbleibt, auch indem zu seinem Nichtseyn, dem Unendlichen, übergegangen wird;— dieses hat, wie gezeigt, nur die erste, unmittelbare Negation zu seiner Bestimmtheit gegen das Endliche, so wie dieses gegen jene Negation, als Negirtes nur die Bedeutung eines Anderen hat, und daher noch Etwas ist. Wenn somit der sich aus dieser endlichen Welt erhebende Verstand zu seinem Höchsten, dem Unendlichen, aufsteigt, so bleibt ihm diese endliche Welt als ein Diesseits stehen, so daß das Unendliche nur über dem Endlichen gesetzt, von diesem abgesondert und eben damit das Endliche von dem Unendlichen abgesondert wird;—beide an einen verschiedenen Platz gestellt,—das Endliche als das hiesige Daseyn, das Unendliche aber, zwar das Ansich des Endlichen, doch als ein Jenseits in die trübe, unerreichbare Ferne, außerhalb welcher jenes sich befinde und dableibe.\n\nSo abgesondert sind sie ebenso wesentlich eben durch die sie abscheidende Negation auf einander bezogen. Diese sie, die in sich reflektirten Etwas, beziehende Negation ist die gegenseitige Grenze des einen gegen das Andere; und zwar so, daß jedes derselben, sie nicht bloß gegen das Andere an ihm hat, sondern die Negation ist ihr Ansichseyn, jedes hat die Grenze so an ihm selbst für sich, in seiner Absonderung von dem Anderen. Die Grenze ist aber als die erste Negation, so sind beide begrenzte, endliche an sich selbst. Jedoch ist jedes auch als sich auf sich affirmativ beziehend die Negation seiner Grenze; so stößt es sie als sein Nichtseyn unmittelbar von sich ab, und qualitativ davon getrennt, setzt es sie als ein anderes Seyn außer ihm, das Endliche sein Nichtseyn als dieß Unendliche, dieses ebenso das Endliche. Daß von dem Endlichen zum Unendlichen nothwendig d. h. durch die Bestimmung des Endlichen übergegangen und es als zum Ansichseyn erhoben werde, wird leicht zugegeben, indem das Endliche zwar als bestehendes Daseyn aber zugleich auch als das an sich nichtige also sich nach seiner Bestimmung auflösende bestimmt ist, das Unendliche aber zwar als mit Negation und Grenze behaftet, bestimmt ist, aber zugleich auch als das Ansichseyende, so daß diese Abstraktion der sich auf sich beziehenden Affirmation seine Bestimmung ausmache, nach dieser hiermit das endliche Daseyn nicht in ihr liege. Aber es ist gezeigt worden, daß das Unendliche selbst nur vermittelst der Negation, als Negation der Negation, zum affirmativen Seyn resultirt, und daß diese seine Affirmation als nur einfaches, qualitatives Seyn genommen, die in ihm enthaltene Negation, zur einfachen unmittelbaren Negation, und damit zur Bestimmtheit und Grenze herabsetzt, welches dann ebenso als widersprechend seinem Ansichseyn, aus ihm ausgeschlossen, als nicht das Seinige, vielmehr seinem Ansichseyn entgegengesetzte, das Endliche, gesetzt wird. Indem so jedes, an ihm selbst und aus seiner Bestimmung das Setzen seines Anderen ist, sind sie untrennbar. Aber diese ihre Einheit ist in dem qualitativen Andersseyn derselben verborgen, sie ist die innerliche, die nur zu Grunde liegt.\n\nDadurch ist die Weise der Erscheinung dieser Einheit bestimmt; im Daseyn gesetzt ist sie als ein Umschlagen oder Übergehen des Endlichen zum Unendlichen, und umgekehrt; so daß das Unendliche an dem Endlichen, und das Endliche an dem Unendlichen, das Andere an dem Anderen, nur hervortrete, das heißt, jedes ein eigenes unmittelbares Entstehen an dem Anderen und ihre Beziehung nur eine äußerliche sey.\n\nDer Proceß ihres Übergehens hat folgende, ausführliche Gestalt. Es wird über das Endliche hinausgegangen in das Unendliche. Dieß Hinausgehen erscheint als ein äußerliches Thun. In diesem dem Endlichen jenseitigen Leeren was entsteht? Was ist das Positive darin? Um der Untrennbarkeit des Unendlichen und Endlichen willen, (oder weil dieß auf seiner Seite stehende Unendliche selbst beschränkt ist), entsteht die Grenze; das Unendliche ist verschwunden, sein Anderes, das Endliche, ist eingetreten. Aber dieß Eintreten des Endlichen, erscheint als ein dem Unendlichen äußerliches Geschehen, und die neue Grenze als ein solches, das nicht aus dem Unendlichen selbst entstehe, sondern ebenso vorgefunden werde. Es ist damit der Rückfall in die vorherige, vergebens aufgehobene Bestimmung vorhanden. Diese neue Grenze aber ist selbst nur ein solches, das aufzuheben, oder über das hinaus zu gehen ist. Somit ist wieder das Leere, das Nichts entstanden, in welchem ebenso jene Bestimmtheit, eine neue Grenze, angetroffen wird,—und sofort ins Unendliche.\n\nEs ist die Wechselbestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen vorhanden; das Endliche ist endlich nur in der Beziehung auf das Sollen oder auf das Unendliche, und das Unendliche ist nur unendlich in Beziehung auf das Endliche. Sie sind untrennbar und zugleich schlechthin Andere gegeneinander; jedes hat das Andere seiner an ihm selbst; so ist jedes die Einheit seiner und seines Anderen, und ist in seiner Bestimmtheit Daseyn, das nicht zu seyn, was es selbst und was sein Anderes ist.\n\nDiese sich selbst und seine Negation negirende Wechselbestimmung ist es, welche als der Progreß ins Unendliche auftritt, der in so vielen Gestalten und Anwendungen als ein Letztes gilt, über das nicht mehr hinausgegangen wird, sondern angekommen bei jenem: Und so fort ins Unendliche, pflegt der Gedanke sein Ende erreicht zu haben.—Dieser Progreß tritt allenthalben ein, wo relative Bestimmungen bis zu ihrer Entgegensetzung getrieben sind, so daß sie in untrennbarer Einheit sind, und doch jeder gegen die andere ein selbstständiges Daseyn zugeschrieben wird. Dieser Progreß ist daher der Widerspruch, der nicht aufgelöst ist, sondern immer nur als vorhanden ausgesprochen wird.\n\nEs ist ein abstraktes Hinausgehen vorhanden, das unvollständig bleibt, indem über dieß Hinausgehen nicht selbst hinausgegangen wird. Es ist das Unendliche vorhanden; über dasselbe wird allerdings hinausgegangen, denn es wird eine neue Grenze gesetzt, aber damit eben wird vielmehr nur zum Endlichen zurückgekehrt. Diese schlechte Unendlichkeit ist an sich dasselbe, was das perennirende Sollen, sie ist zwar die Negation des Endlichen, aber sie vermag sich nicht in Wahrheit davon zu befreien; dieß tritt an ihr selbst wieder hervor, als ihr Anderes, weil dieß Unendliche nur ist als in Beziehung auf das ihm andere Endliche. Der Progreß ins Unendliche ist daher nur die sich wiederholende Einerleiheit, eine und dieselbe langweilige Abwechslung dieses Endlichen und Unendlichen.\n\nDie Unendlichkeit des unendlichen Progresses bleibt mit dem Endlichen als solchem behaftet, ist dadurch begrenzt, und selbst endlich. Somit wäre es aber in der That als die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen gesetzt. Aber auf diese Einheit wird nicht reflektirt. Sie ist es jedoch nur, welche im Endlichen das Unendliche, und im Unendlichen das Endliche hervorruft, sie ist so zu sagen die Triebfeder des unendlichen Progresses. Er ist das Äußere jener Einheit, bei welchem die Vorstellung stehen bleibt, bei jener perennirenden Wiederholung eines und desselben Abwechselns, der leeren Unruhe des Weitergehens über die Grenze hinaus zur Unendlichkeit, das in diesem Unendlichen eine neue Grenze findet, auf derselben aber sich so wenig halten kann, als in dem Unendlichen. Dieses Unendliche hat die feste Determination eines Jenseits, das nicht erreicht werden kann, darum weil es nicht erreicht werden soll, weil von der Bestimmtheit des Jenseits, der seyenden Negation nicht abgelassen wird. Er hat nach dieser Bestimmung das Endliche als ein Diesseits sich gegenüber, das sich eben so wenig ins Unendliche erheben kann, darum weil es diese Determination eines Andern, hiermit eines perennirenden, sich in seinem Jenseits wieder und zwar als davon verschieden, erzeugenden Daseyns hat.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0001","text":"Das Unendliche ist; in dieser Unmittelbarkeit ist es zugleich die Negation eines Andern, des Endlichen. So als seyend und zugleich als Nichtseyn eines Andern ist es in die Kategorie des Etwas als eines bestimmten überhaupt, näher weil es das in sich-reflektirte, vermittelst des Aufhebens der Bestimmtheit überhaupt resultirende Daseyn, hiermit als das von seiner Bestimmtheit unterschiedene Daseyn gesetzt ist,—in die Kategorie des Etwas mit einer Grenze, zurückgefallen. Das Endliche steht nach dieser Bestimmtheit dem Unendlichen als reales Daseyn gegenüber; so stehen sie in qualitativer Beziehung als außer einander bleibende; das unmittelbare Seyn des Unendlichen erweckt das Seyn seiner Negation, des Endlichen wieder, das zunächst im Unendlichen verschwunden schien.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"33.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0002","text":"Aber das Unendliche und Endliche sind nicht nur in diesen Kategorien der Beziehung; die beiden Seiten sind weiter bestimmt, als bloß Andere gegeneinander zu seyn. Die Endliche ist nämlich die als Schranke gesetzte Schranke, es ist das Daseyn mit der Bestimmung gesetzt in sein Ansichseyn überzugehen, unendlich zu werden. Die Unendlichkeit ist das Nichts des Endlichen, dessen Ansichseyn und Sollen, aber dieses zugleich als in sich reflektirt, das ausgeführte Sollen, nur sich auf sich beziehendes ganz affirmatives Seyn. In der Unendlichkeit ist die Befriedigung vorhanden, daß alle Bestimmtheit, Veränderung, alle Schranke und mit ihr das Sollen selbst verschwunden, als aufgehoben, das Nichts des Endlichen gesetzt ist. Als diese Negation des Endlichen ist das Ansichseyn bestimmt, welches so als Negation der Negation in sich affirmativ ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"33.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0003","text":"Diese Affirmation jedoch ist als qualitativ unmittelbare Beziehung auf sich; Seyn; hierdurch ist das Unendliche auf die Kategorie zurückgeführt, daß es das Endliche als ein Anderes sich gegenüber hat; seine negative Natur ist als die seyende, hiermit erste und unmittelbare Negation gesetzt. Das Unendliche ist auf diese Weise mit dem Gegensatze gegen das Endliche behaftet, welches, als Anderes, das bestimmte, reale Daseyn zugleich bleibt, obschon es in seinem Ansichseyn, dem Unendlichen, zugleich als aufgehoben gesetzt ist; dieses ist das Nicht-endliche; —ein Seyn in der Bestimmtheit der Negation. Gegen das Endliche, den Kreis der seyenden Bestimmtheiten, der Realitäten, ist das Unendliche das unbestimmte Leere, das Jenseits des Endlichen, welches sein Ansichseyn nicht an seinem Daseyn, das ein bestimmtes ist, hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"33.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0004","text":"So das Unendliche gegen das Endliche in qualitativer Beziehung von Anderen zu einander gesetzt, ist es das Schlecht-Unendliche, das Unendliche des Verstandes zu nennen, dem es für die höchste, für die absolute Wahrheit gilt; ihn zum Bewußtseyn darüber zu bringen, daß, indem er seine Befriedigung in der Versöhnung der Wahrheit erreicht zu haben meint, er in dem unversöhnten, unaufgelösten, absoluten Widerspruche sich befindet, müßten die Widersprüche bewirken, in die er nach allen Seiten verfällt, so wie er sich auf die Anwendung und Explikation dieser seiner Kategorien einläßt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"33.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0005","text":"Dieser Widerspruch ist sogleich darin vorhanden, daß dem Unendlichen das Endliche als Daseyn gegenüber bleibt; es sind damit zwei Bestimmtheiten; es giebt zwei Welten, eine unendliche und eine endliche, und in ihrer Beziehung ist das Unendliche nur Grenze des Endlichen, und ist damit nur ein bestimmtes, selbst endliches Unendliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"33.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0006","text":"Dieser Widerspruch entwickelt seinen Inhalt zu ausdrücklicheren Formen.—Das Endliche ist das reale Daseyn, welches so verbleibt, auch indem zu seinem Nichtseyn, dem Unendlichen, übergegangen wird;— dieses hat, wie gezeigt, nur die erste, unmittelbare Negation zu seiner Bestimmtheit gegen das Endliche, so wie dieses gegen jene Negation, als Negirtes nur die Bedeutung eines Anderen hat, und daher noch Etwas ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"33.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0007","text":"Wenn somit der sich aus dieser endlichen Welt erhebende Verstand zu seinem Höchsten, dem Unendlichen, aufsteigt, so bleibt ihm diese endliche Welt als ein Diesseits stehen, so daß das Unendliche nur über dem Endlichen gesetzt, von diesem abgesondert und eben damit das Endliche von dem Unendlichen abgesondert wird;—beide an einen verschiedenen Platz gestellt,—das Endliche als das hiesige Daseyn, das Unendliche aber, zwar das Ansich des Endlichen, doch als ein Jenseits in die trübe, unerreichbare Ferne, außerhalb welcher jenes sich befinde und dableibe.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"33.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0008","text":"So abgesondert sind sie ebenso wesentlich eben durch die sie abscheidende Negation auf einander bezogen. Diese sie, die in sich reflektirten Etwas, beziehende Negation ist die gegenseitige Grenze des einen gegen das Andere; und zwar so, daß jedes derselben, sie nicht bloß gegen das Andere an ihm hat, sondern die Negation ist ihr Ansichseyn, jedes hat die Grenze so an ihm selbst für sich, in seiner Absonderung von dem Anderen. Die Grenze ist aber als die erste Negation, so sind beide begrenzte, endliche an sich selbst. Jedoch ist jedes auch als sich auf sich affirmativ beziehend die Negation seiner Grenze; so stößt es sie als sein Nichtseyn unmittelbar von sich ab, und qualitativ davon getrennt, setzt es sie als ein anderes Seyn außer ihm, das Endliche sein Nichtseyn als dieß Unendliche, dieses ebenso das Endliche. Daß von dem Endlichen zum Unendlichen nothwendig d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"33.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0009","text":"durch die Bestimmung des Endlichen übergegangen und es als zum Ansichseyn erhoben werde, wird leicht zugegeben, indem das Endliche zwar als bestehendes Daseyn aber zugleich auch als das an sich nichtige also sich nach seiner Bestimmung auflösende bestimmt ist, das Unendliche aber zwar als mit Negation und Grenze behaftet, bestimmt ist, aber zugleich auch als das Ansichseyende, so daß diese Abstraktion der sich auf sich beziehenden Affirmation seine Bestimmung ausmache, nach dieser hiermit das endliche Daseyn nicht in ihr liege.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"33.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0010","text":"Aber es ist gezeigt worden, daß das Unendliche selbst nur vermittelst der Negation, als Negation der Negation, zum affirmativen Seyn resultirt, und daß diese seine Affirmation als nur einfaches, qualitatives Seyn genommen, die in ihm enthaltene Negation, zur einfachen unmittelbaren Negation, und damit zur Bestimmtheit und Grenze herabsetzt, welches dann ebenso als widersprechend seinem Ansichseyn, aus ihm ausgeschlossen, als nicht das Seinige, vielmehr seinem Ansichseyn entgegengesetzte, das Endliche, gesetzt wird. Indem so jedes, an ihm selbst und aus seiner Bestimmung das Setzen seines Anderen ist, sind sie untrennbar. Aber diese ihre Einheit ist in dem qualitativen Andersseyn derselben verborgen, sie ist die innerliche, die nur zu Grunde liegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"33.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0011","text":"Dadurch ist die Weise der Erscheinung dieser Einheit bestimmt; im Daseyn gesetzt ist sie als ein Umschlagen oder Übergehen des Endlichen zum Unendlichen, und umgekehrt; so daß das Unendliche an dem Endlichen, und das Endliche an dem Unendlichen, das Andere an dem Anderen, nur hervortrete, das heißt, jedes ein eigenes unmittelbares Entstehen an dem Anderen und ihre Beziehung nur eine äußerliche sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"33.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0012","text":"Der Proceß ihres Übergehens hat folgende, ausführliche Gestalt. Es wird über das Endliche hinausgegangen in das Unendliche. Dieß Hinausgehen erscheint als ein äußerliches Thun. In diesem dem Endlichen jenseitigen Leeren was entsteht? Was ist das Positive darin? Um der Untrennbarkeit des Unendlichen und Endlichen willen, (oder weil dieß auf seiner Seite stehende Unendliche selbst beschränkt ist), entsteht die Grenze; das Unendliche ist verschwunden, sein Anderes, das Endliche, ist eingetreten. Aber dieß Eintreten des Endlichen, erscheint als ein dem Unendlichen äußerliches Geschehen, und die neue Grenze als ein solches, das nicht aus dem Unendlichen selbst entstehe, sondern ebenso vorgefunden werde. Es ist damit der Rückfall in die vorherige, vergebens aufgehobene Bestimmung vorhanden. Diese neue Grenze aber ist selbst nur ein solches, das aufzuheben, oder über das hinaus zu gehen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"33.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0013","text":"Somit ist wieder das Leere, das Nichts entstanden, in welchem ebenso jene Bestimmtheit, eine neue Grenze, angetroffen wird,—und sofort ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"33.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0014","text":"Es ist die Wechselbestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen vorhanden; das Endliche ist endlich nur in der Beziehung auf das Sollen oder auf das Unendliche, und das Unendliche ist nur unendlich in Beziehung auf das Endliche. Sie sind untrennbar und zugleich schlechthin Andere gegeneinander; jedes hat das Andere seiner an ihm selbst; so ist jedes die Einheit seiner und seines Anderen, und ist in seiner Bestimmtheit Daseyn, das nicht zu seyn, was es selbst und was sein Anderes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"33.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0015","text":"Diese sich selbst und seine Negation negirende Wechselbestimmung ist es, welche als der Progreß ins Unendliche auftritt, der in so vielen Gestalten und Anwendungen als ein Letztes gilt, über das nicht mehr hinausgegangen wird, sondern angekommen bei jenem: Und so fort ins Unendliche, pflegt der Gedanke sein Ende erreicht zu haben.—Dieser Progreß tritt allenthalben ein, wo relative Bestimmungen bis zu ihrer Entgegensetzung getrieben sind, so daß sie in untrennbarer Einheit sind, und doch jeder gegen die andere ein selbstständiges Daseyn zugeschrieben wird. Dieser Progreß ist daher der Widerspruch, der nicht aufgelöst ist, sondern immer nur als vorhanden ausgesprochen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"33.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0016","text":"Es ist ein abstraktes Hinausgehen vorhanden, das unvollständig bleibt, indem über dieß Hinausgehen nicht selbst hinausgegangen wird. Es ist das Unendliche vorhanden; über dasselbe wird allerdings hinausgegangen, denn es wird eine neue Grenze gesetzt, aber damit eben wird vielmehr nur zum Endlichen zurückgekehrt. Diese schlechte Unendlichkeit ist an sich dasselbe, was das perennirende Sollen, sie ist zwar die Negation des Endlichen, aber sie vermag sich nicht in Wahrheit davon zu befreien; dieß tritt an ihr selbst wieder hervor, als ihr Anderes, weil dieß Unendliche nur ist als in Beziehung auf das ihm andere Endliche. Der Progreß ins Unendliche ist daher nur die sich wiederholende Einerleiheit, eine und dieselbe langweilige Abwechslung dieses Endlichen und Unendlichen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"33.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0017","text":"Die Unendlichkeit des unendlichen Progresses bleibt mit dem Endlichen als solchem behaftet, ist dadurch begrenzt, und selbst endlich. Somit wäre es aber in der That als die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen gesetzt. Aber auf diese Einheit wird nicht reflektirt. Sie ist es jedoch nur, welche im Endlichen das Unendliche, und im Unendlichen das Endliche hervorruft, sie ist so zu sagen die Triebfeder des unendlichen Progresses. Er ist das Äußere jener Einheit, bei welchem die Vorstellung stehen bleibt, bei jener perennirenden Wiederholung eines und desselben Abwechselns, der leeren Unruhe des Weitergehens über die Grenze hinaus zur Unendlichkeit, das in diesem Unendlichen eine neue Grenze findet, auf derselben aber sich so wenig halten kann, als in dem Unendlichen.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"33.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0018","text":"Dieses Unendliche hat die feste Determination eines Jenseits, das nicht erreicht werden kann, darum weil es nicht erreicht werden soll, weil von der Bestimmtheit des Jenseits, der seyenden Negation nicht abgelassen wird. Er hat nach dieser Bestimmung das Endliche als ein Diesseits sich gegenüber, das sich eben so wenig ins Unendliche erheben kann, darum weil es diese Determination eines Andern, hiermit eines perennirenden, sich in seinem Jenseits wieder und zwar als davon verschieden, erzeugenden Daseyns hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"33.18"}],"sha256":"ade500c920354009d859c18c216636a39f4f0a2fbd242bb4ef28f307be6a05fc","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102317514803Z_8c25503e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Reciprocal Determination of the Finite and the Infinite.","source_sha256":"ade500c920354009d859c18c216636a39f4f0a2fbd242bb4ef28f307be6a05fc","sha256":"312ed4d617e653fc65cd68ac2e078487000f82dc2c0f95d8ceb3b5ea44afb51d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:23:17.514848+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0001","text":"The infinite is; in this immediacy it is at the same time the negation of an other, of the finite. Thus, as being and at the same time as non-being of an other, it has relapsed into the category of something as a determinate in general, more specifically because it is posited as the existence reflected into itself, resulting through the sublation of determinateness in general, and hence as existence distinguished from its determinateness,—into the category of something with a limit. According to this determinateness, the finite stands opposed to the infinite as real existence; thus they stand in a qualitative relation as remaining external to one another; the immediate being of the infinite reawakens the being of its negation, of the finite, which at first seemed to have disappeared in the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"33.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0002","text":"But the infinite and finite are not merely in these categories of relation; the two sides are further determined than merely to be others in relation to one another. The finite is, namely, the limitation posited as limitation; it is existence posited with the determination to pass over into its being-in-itself, to become infinite. Infinity is the nothing of the finite, its being-in-itself and ought, but this at the same time as reflected into itself, the fulfilled ought, only self-relating wholly affirmative being. In infinity there is present the satisfaction that all determinateness, alteration, every limitation, and with it ought itself, has disappeared, is posited as sublated, as the nothing of the finite. As this negation of the finite, being-in-itself is determined, which is thus affirmative in itself as negation of negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"33.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0003","text":"This affirmation, however, is as qualitatively immediate relation to itself; being; thereby the infinite is led back to the category that it has the finite as an other opposed to it; its negative nature is posited as being, and hence as the first and immediate negation. The infinite is in this way burdened with opposition to the finite, which, as other, at the same time remains determinate, real existence, although in its being-in-itself, the infinite, it is at the same time posited as sublated; this is the non-finite;—a being in the determinateness of negation. Over against the finite, the sphere of determinate beings, of realities, the infinite is the indeterminate void, the beyond of the finite, which does not have its being-in-itself in its existence, which is a determinate one.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"33.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0004","text":"Thus, with the infinite posited over against the finite in the qualitative relation of others to one another, it is the spurious infinite, the infinite of the understanding, which it takes to be the highest, the absolute truth; to bring it to consciousness of the fact that, while it thinks it has attained its satisfaction in the reconciliation of truth, it finds itself in the unreconciled, unresolved, absolute contradiction, would have to be effected by the contradictions into which it falls on every side as soon as it undertakes the application and explication of these its categories.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"33.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0005","text":"This contradiction is immediately present in the fact that the finite remains opposed to the infinite as existence; there are thereby two determinatenesses; there are two worlds, an infinite and a finite one, and in their relation the infinite is only the limit of the finite, and is thereby only a determinate, itself finite infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"33.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0006","text":"This contradiction develops its content into more explicit forms.—The finite is the real existence which thus remains, even when the transition is made to its non-being, the infinite;—this, as has been shown, has only the first, immediate negation as its determinateness over against the finite, just as the latter, over against that negation, as negated, has only the significance of an other, and is therefore still something.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"33.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0007","text":"Thus, when the understanding raising itself from this finite world ascends to its highest, the infinite, this finite world remains standing for it as a here-below, so that the infinite is only posited above the finite, separated from it, and precisely thereby the finite is separated from the infinite;—both are placed in a different location,—the finite as the existence here, the infinite, however, indeed as the in-itself of the finite, yet as a beyond in the dim, unattainable distance, outside of which the former is and remains.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"33.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0008","text":"Thus separated, they are likewise essentially related to one another precisely through the negation that separates them. This negation relating them, the somethings reflected into themselves, is the reciprocal limit of the one against the other; and indeed in such a way that each of them does not merely have it in it against the other, but negation is their being-in-itself; each thus has the limit in itself for itself, in its separation from the other. But the limit is the first negation; thus both are limited, finite in themselves. Yet each, as relating affirmatively to itself, is also the negation of its limit; it thus immediately repels it from itself as its non-being, and, qualitatively separated from it, posits it as another being outside itself, the finite its non-being as this infinite, and this likewise the finite. That the transition from the finite to the infinite necessarily, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"33.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0009","text":"through the determination of the finite, takes place, and that it is elevated to being-in-itself, is readily conceded, since the finite is determined indeed as subsisting existence, but at the same time also as that which is null in itself and thus dissolves itself according to its determination; whereas the infinite is determined indeed as burdened with negation and limit, but at the same time also as that which is in itself, so that this abstraction of self-relating affirmation constitutes its determination, according to which finite existence does not lie in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"33.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0010","text":"But it has been shown that the infinite itself results in affirmative being only by means of negation, as negation of negation, and that this its affirmation, taken as merely simple, qualitative being, reduces the negation contained in it to simple immediate negation, and thereby to determinateness and limit, which is then likewise posited as contradicting its being-in-itself, excluded from it as not its own but rather as opposed to its being-in-itself, as the finite. Since thus each, in itself and out of its determination, is the positing of its other, they are inseparable. But this their unity is concealed in their qualitative otherness; it is the inner unity, which merely underlies.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"33.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0011","text":"Thereby the mode of appearance of this unity is determined; posited in existence, it is a turning-over or transition of the finite into the infinite, and conversely; so that the infinite in the finite, and the finite in the infinite, the other in the other, only comes forth, that is, each has an independent immediate arising in the other, and their relation is only an external one.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"33.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0012","text":"The process of their transition has the following detailed form. One goes beyond the finite into the infinite. This going-beyond appears as an external act. In this void beyond the finite, what arises? What is the positive in it? For the sake of the inseparability of the infinite and the finite, (or because this infinite standing on its side is itself limited), the limit arises; the infinite has disappeared, its other, the finite, has entered. But this entry of the finite appears as an occurrence external to the infinite, and the new limit as one which does not arise out of the infinite itself, but is equally found already there. Thereby there is a relapse into the previous determination, vainly sublated. But this new limit is itself only one which is to be sublated, or beyond which one is to go.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"33.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0013","text":"Thus there has again arisen the void, the nothing, in which likewise that determinateness, a new limit, is encountered,—and so on to infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"33.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0014","text":"The reciprocal determination of finite and infinite is present; the finite is finite only in relation to ought or to the infinite, and the infinite is infinite only in relation to the finite. They are inseparable and at the same time absolutely others in relation to one another; each has its other in itself; thus each is the unity of itself and its other, and is, in its determinateness, existence which is not to be what it itself and what its other is.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"33.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0015","text":"This reciprocal determination which negates itself and its negation is what appears as progress to infinity, which in so many forms and applications counts as an ultimate, beyond which one does not proceed further, but upon arriving at that: And so on to infinity, thought is wont to have reached its end.—This progress occurs everywhere where relative determinations are driven to their opposition, so that they are in inseparable unity, and yet each is ascribed a self-subsistent existence over against the other. This progress is therefore the contradiction which is not resolved, but is always merely pronounced as present.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"33.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0016","text":"There is an abstract going-beyond which remains incomplete, since one does not go beyond this going-beyond itself. The infinite is present; one indeed goes beyond it, for a new limit is posited, but precisely thereby one rather merely returns to the finite. This spurious infinity is in itself the same as the perennial ought; it is indeed the negation of the finite, but it is unable truly to free itself from it; this again comes forth in it itself as its other, because this infinite is only as in relation to the finite other than it. Progress to infinity is therefore only the repeated sameness, one and the same tedious alternation of this finite and infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"33.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0017","text":"The infinity of infinite progress remains burdened with the finite as such, is thereby limited, and itself finite. Thus it would in fact be posited as the unity of finite and infinite. But reflection is not directed to this unity. Yet it alone is what calls forth the infinite in the finite, and the finite in the infinite; it is, so to speak, the mainspring of infinite progress. It is the externality of that unity, at which representation remains fixed, at that perennial repetition of one and the same alternation, the empty unrest of proceeding beyond the limit to infinity, which finds a new limit in this infinity, but can remain at that limit as little as in the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"33.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0018","text":"This infinite has the fixed determination of a beyond which cannot be reached, because it is not to be reached, because one does not relinquish the determinateness of the beyond, of being negation. According to this determination, it has the finite as a here-below opposed to it, which can just as little elevate itself into infinity, because it has this determination of an other, and hence of a perennial existence reproducing itself in its beyond, and indeed as distinct from it.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"33.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BWDE:P0018"]}],"source_digest":"5ce0c65eaa750e7fcf96e101cd276d47750998cc505cc5d16ba8e7c81cada307","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Wechselbestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Wechselbestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU","title":"c. Affirmative Infinity.","order":34,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDAU","text":"In dem aufgezeigten herüber- und hinübergehenden Wechselbestimmen des Endlichen und Unendlichen ist die Wahrheit derselben an sich schon vorhanden, und es bedarf nur des Aufnehmens dessen, was vorhanden ist. Dieß Herüber- und Hinübergehen macht die äußere Realisation des Begriffes aus; es ist in ihr das, aber äußerlich, außer einander fallend, gesetzt, was der Begriff enthält; es bedarf nur der Vergleichung dieser verschiedenen Momente, in welcher die Einheit sich ergiebt, die den Begriff selbst giebt;—die Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen, ist, wie schon oft bemerkt, hier aber vornehmlich in Erinnerung zu bringen ist, der schiefe Ausdruck für die Einheit, wie sie selbst wahrhaft ist; aber auch das Entfernen dieser schiefen Bestimmung muß in jener vor uns liegenden Äußerung des Begriffes vorhanden seyn.\n\nNach ihrer nächsten, nur unmittelbaren Bestimmung genommen, so ist das Unendliche nur als das Hinausgehen über das Endliche; es ist seiner Bestimmung nach die Negation des Endlichen; so ist das Endliche nur als das, worüber hinausgegangen werden muß, die Negation seiner an ihm selbst, welche die Unendlichkeit ist. In jedem liegt hiermit die Bestimmtheit des Andern, die nach der Meinung des unendlichen Progresses von einander ausgeschlossen seyn sollen und nur abwechselnd auf einander folgen; es kann keines gesetzt und gefaßt werden ohne das Andere, das Unendliche nicht ohne das Endliche, dieses nicht ohne das Unendliche. Wenn gesagt wird, was das Unendliche ist, nämlich die Negation des Endlichen, so wird das Endliche selbst mit ausgesprochen; es kann zur Bestimmung des Unendlichen nicht entbehrt werden. Man bedarf nur zu wissen, was man sagt, um die Bestimmung des Endlichen im Unendlichen zu finden. Vom Endlichen seinerseits wird sogleich zugegeben, daß es das Nichtige ist, aber eben seine Nichtigkeit ist die Unendlichkeit, von der es ebenso untrennbar ist.—In diesem Auffassen können sie nach ihrer Beziehung auf ihr Anderes genommen zu seyn scheinen. Werden sie hiermit beziehungslos genommen, so daß sie nur durch das: Und verbunden seyen, so stehen sie als selbstständig, jedes nur an ihm selbst seyend, einander gegenüber. Es ist zu sehen, wie sie in solcher Weise beschaffen sind. Das Unendliche so gestellt ist Eines der beiden; aber als nur Eines der beiden ist es selbst endlich, es ist nicht das Ganze, sondern nur die Eine Seite; es hat an dem gegenüberstehenden seine Grenze; es ist so das endliche Unendliche. Es sind nur zwei Endliche vorhanden. Eben darin, daß es so vom Endlichen abgesondert, damit als Einseitiges gestellt wird, liegt seine Endlichkeit, also seine Einheit mit dem Endlichen.—Das Endliche seinerseits als für sich vom Unendlichen entfernt gestellt, ist diese Beziehung auf sich, in der seine Relativität, Abhängigkeit, seine Vergänglichkeit entfernt ist; es ist dieselbe Selbstständigkeit und Affirmation seiner, welche das Unendliche seyn soll.\n\nBeide Betrachtungsweisen, die zunächst eine verschiedene Bestimmtheit zu ihrem Ausgangspunkte zu haben scheinen, in sofern die erstere nur als Beziehung des Unendlichen und Endlichen auf einander, eines jeden auf sein Anderes, und die zweite sie in ihrer völligen Absonderung von einander halten soll, geben ein und dasselbe Resultat; das Unendliche und Endliche nach der Beziehung beider auf einander, die ihnen äußerlich wäre, aber die ihnen wesentlich, ohne die keines ist, was es ist, enthält so sein Anderes in seiner eigenen Bestimmung, ebenso sehr als jedes für sich genommen, an ihm selbst betrachtet, sein Anderes in ihm als sein eigenes Moment liegen hat.\n\nDieß giebt denn die—verrufene—Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen, —die Einheit, die selbst das Unendliche ist, welches sich selbst und die Endlichkeit in sich begreift,—also das Unendliche in einem anderen Sinne als in dem, wornach das Endliche von ihm abgetrennt und auf die andere Seite gestellt ist. Indem sie nun auch unterschieden werden müssen, ist jedes, wie vorhin gezeigt, selbst an ihm die Einheit beider; so ergeben sich zwei solche Einheiten. Das Gemeinschaftliche, die Einheit beider Bestimmtheiten, setzt als Einheit sie zunächst als negirte, da jedes das seyn soll, was es ist in ihrer Unterschiedenheit; in ihrer Einheit verlieren sie also ihre qualitative Natur;—eine wichtige Reflexion gegen die Vorstellung, die sich nicht davon losmachen will, in der Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen sie nach der Qualität, welche sie als außereinander genommen haben sollen, festzuhalten, und daher in jener Einheit nichts als den Widerspruch, nicht auch die Auflösung desselben durch die Negation der qualitativen Bestimmtheit beider sieht; so wird die zunächst einfache, allgemeine Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen verfälscht.\n\nFerner aber, indem sie nun auch als unterschieden zu nehmen sind, so ist die Einheit des Unendlichen, die jedes dieser Momente selbst ist, in jedem derselben auf verschiedene Weise bestimmt. Das seiner Bestimmung nach Unendliche hat die von ihm unterschiedene Endlichkeit an ihm, jenes ist das Ansich in dieser Einheit, und dieses ist nur Bestimmtheit, Grenze an ihm, allein es ist eine Grenze, welche das schlechthin Andere desselben, sein Gegentheil ist; seine Bestimmung, welche das An-sich-seyn als solches ist, wird durch den Beischlag einer Qualität solcher Art verdorben; es ist so ein verendlichtes Unendliches. Auf gleiche Weise, indem das Endliche als solches nur das Nicht-ansichseyn ist, aber nach jener Einheit gleichfalls sein Gegentheil an ihm hat, wird es über seinen Werth und zwar so zu sagen unendlich erhoben; es wird als das verunendlichte Endliche gesetzt.\n\nAuf gleiche Weise wie vorhin die einfache, so wird vom Verstande auch die gedoppelte Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen verfälscht. Dieß geschieht hier ebenso dadurch, daß in der einen der beiden Einheiten, das Unendliche als nicht negirtes, vielmehr als das An-sich-seyn angenommen wird, an welches also nicht die Bestimmtheit und Schranke gesetzt werden soll; es werde dadurch das An-sich-seyn herabgesetzt und verdorben. Umgekehrt wird das Endliche gleichfalls als das nicht negirte, obgleich an sich Nichtige, festgehalten, so daß es in seiner Verbindung mit dem Unendlichen zu dem, was es nicht sey, erhoben, und dadurch gegen seine nicht verschwundene, vielmehr perennirende Bestimmung verunendlicht werde.\n\nDie Verfälschung, die der Verstand mit dem Endlichen und Unendlichen vornimmt, ihre Beziehung aufeinander als qualitative Verschiedenheit festzuhalten, sie in ihrer Bestimmung als getrennt und zwar absolut getrennt zu behaupten, gründet sich auf das Vergessen dessen, was für ihn selbst der Begriff dieser Momente ist. Nach diesem ist die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen nicht ein äußerliches Zusammenbringen derselben, noch eine ungehörige, ihrer Bestimmung zuwiderlaufende Verbindung, in welcher an sich getrennte und entgegengesetzte, gegeneinander Selbstständige, Seyende, somit unverträgliche verknüpft würden, sondern jedes ist an ihm selbst diese Einheit, und dieß nur als Aufheben seiner selbst worin keines vor dem andern einen Vorzug des Ansichseyns und affirmativen Daseyns hätte. Wie früher gezeigt, ist die Endlichkeit nur als Hinausgehen über sich; es ist also in ihr die Unendlichkeit, das Andere ihrer selbst, enthalten. Eben so ist die Unendlichkeit nur als Hinausgehen über das Endliche; sie enthält also wesentlich ihr Anderes, und ist somit an ihr das Andere ihrer selbst. Das Endliche wird nicht vom Unendlichen als einer außer ihm vorhandenen Macht aufgehoben, sondern es ist seine Unendlichkeit, sich selbst aufzuheben.\n\nDieß Aufheben ist somit nicht die Veränderung oder das Andersseyn überhaupt, nicht das Aufheben von Etwas. Das, worin sich das Endliche aufhebt, ist das Unendliche als das Negiren der Endlichkeit; aber diese ist längst selbst nur das Daseyn als ein Nichtseyn bestimmt. Es ist also nur die Negation, die sich in der Negation aufhebt. So ist ihrer Seits die Unendlichkeit als das Negative der Endlichkeit und damit der Bestimmtheit überhaupt, als das leere Jenseits, bestimmt; sein Sich-aufheben im Endlichen ist ein Zurückkehren aus der leeren Flucht, Negation des Jenseits, das ein Negatives an ihm selbst ist.\n\nWas also vorhanden ist, ist in beiden dieselbe Negation der Negation. Aber diese ist an sich Beziehung auf sich selbst, die Affirmation aber als Rückkehr zu sich selbst, d. i. durch die Vermittelung, welche die Negation der Negation ist. Diese Bestimmungen sind es, die wesentlich ins Auge zu fassen sind; das zweite aber ist, daß sie im unendlichen Progresse auch gesetzt sind, und wie sie in ihm gesetzt sind,—nämlich noch nicht in ihrer letzten Wahrheit.\n\nEs werden darin erstens beide, sowohl das Unendliche als das Endliche negirt,—es wird über beide auf gleiche Weise hinausgegangen; zweitens werden sie auch als unterschiedene, jedes nach dem Andern, als für sich Positive gesetzt. Wir fassen so diese zwei Bestimmungen vergleichend heraus, wie wir in der Vergleichung, einem äußeren Vergleichen, die zwei Betrachtungsweisen, des Endlichen und Unendlichen in ihrer Beziehung, und ihrer jedes für sich genommen, getrennt haben. Aber der unendliche Progreß spricht mehr aus, es ist in ihm auch der Zusammenhang der auch Unterschiedenen gesetzt, jedoch zunächst nur noch als Übergang und Abwechslung; es ist nur in einer einfachen Reflexion von uns zu sehen, was in der That darin vorhanden ist.\n\nZunächst kann die Negation des Endlichen und Unendlichen, die im unendlichen Progresse gesetzt ist, als einfach, somit als auseinander, nur aufeinander folgend genommen werden. Vom Endlichen angefangen, so wird über die Grenze hinausgegangen, das Endliche negirt. Nun ist also das Jenseits desselben, das Unendliche, vorhanden, aber in diesem entsteht wieder die Grenze; so ist das Hinausgehen über das Unendliche vorhanden. Dieß zweifache Aufheben ist jedoch Theils überhaupt nur als ein äußerliches Geschehen und Abwechseln der Momente, Theils noch nicht als Eine Einheit gesetzt; jedes dieser Hinaus ist ein eigener Ansatz, ein neuer Akt, so daß sie so auseinander fallen.—Es ist aber auch ferner im unendlichen Progresse deren Beziehung vorhanden. Es ist erstlich das Endliche; dann wird darüber hinausgegangen, dieß Negative oder Jenseits des Endlichen ist das Unendliche; drittens wird über diese Negation wieder hinausgegangen, es entsteht eine neue Grenze, wieder ein Endliches. —Dieß ist die vollständige, sich selbst schließende Bewegung, die bei dem angekommen, das den Anfang machte; es entsteht dasselbe, von dem ausgegangen worden war, d. i. das Endliche ist wiederhergestellt; dasselbe ist also mit sich selbst zusammengegangen, hat nur sich in seinem Jenseits wiedergefunden.\n\nDasselbe ist der Fall in Ansehung des Unendlichen. Im Unendlichen, dem Jenseits der Grenze entsteht nur eine neue, welche dasselbe Schicksal hat, als Endliches negirt werden zu müssen. Was so wieder vorhanden ist, ist dasselbe Unendliche, das vorhin in der neuen Grenze verschwand; das Unendliche ist daher durch sein Aufheben, durch die neue Grenze hindurch, nicht weiter hinausgeschoben, weder von dem Endlichen entfernt worden, denn dieses ist nur dieß, in das Unendliche überzugehen,—noch von sich selbst, denn es ist bei sich angekommen.\n\nSo ist beides, das Endliche und das Unendliche, diese Bewegung, zu sich durch seine Negation zurückzukehren; sie sind nur als Vermittelung in sich, und das Affirmative beider enthält die Negation beider, und ist die Negation der Negation.—Sie sind so Resultat, hiermit nicht das, was sie in der Bestimmung ihres Anfangs sind; —nicht das Endliche ein Daseyn seinerseits und das Unendliche ein Daseyn, oder Ansichseyn jenseits des Daseyns, d. i. des als endlich bestimmten. Gegen die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen sträubt sich der Verstand nur darum so sehr, weil er die Schranke und das Endliche wie das Ansichseyn als perennirend voraussetzt; damit übersieht er die Negation beider, die im unendlichen Progresse faktisch vorhanden ist, wie ebenso, daß sie darin nur als Momente eines Ganzen vorkommen und daß sie nur vermittelst ihres Gegentheils aber wesentlich ebenso vermittelst des Aufhebens ihres Gegentheils hervortreten.\n\nWenn zunächst die Rückkehr in sich, ebenso wohl als Rückkehr des Endlichen zu sich, wie als die des Unendlichen zu sich betrachtet wurde, so zeigt sich in diesem Resultate selbst eine Unrichtigkeit, die mit der so eben gerügten Schiefheit zusammenhängt; das Endliche ist das eine Mal, das Unendliche das Andere Mal als Ausgangspunkt genommen, und nur dadurch entstehen zwei Resultate. Es ist aber völlig gleichgültig, welches als Anfang genommen werde; damit fällt der Unterschied für sich hinweg, der die Zweiheit der Resultate hervorbrachte. Dieß ist in der nach beiden Seiten unbegrenzten Linie des unendlichen Progresses gleichfalls gesetzt, worin jedes der Momente mit gleichem abwechselnden Vorkommen vorhanden, und es ganz äußerlich ist, in welche Stelle gegriffen und als Anfang genommen werde.—Sie sind in demselben unterschieden, aber auf gleiche Weise das eine nur das Moment des andern. Indem sie beide, das Endliche und das Unendliche selbst Momente des Processes sind, sind sie gemeinschaftlich das Endliche, und indem sie ebenso gemeinschaftlich in ihm und im Resultate negirt sind, so heißt dieses Resultat als Negation jener Endlichkeit beider mit Wahrheit das Unendliche. Ihr Unterschied ist so der Doppelsinn, den beide haben. Das Endliche hat den Doppelsinn, erstens nur das Endliche gegen das Unendliche zu seyn, das ihm gegenübersteht, und zweitens das Endliche und das ihm gegenüberstehende Unendliche zugleich zu seyn. Auch das Unendliche hat den Doppelsinn, eines jener beiden Momente zu seyn, so ist es das Schlechtunendliche, und das Unendliche zu seyn, in welchem jene beide, es selbst und sein anderes, nur Momente sind. Wie also das Unendliche in der That vorhanden ist, ist der Proceß zu seyn, in welchem es sich herabsetzt, nur eine seiner Bestimmungen, dem Endlichen gegenüber und damit selbst nur eines der Endlichen zu seyn, und diesen Unterschied seiner von sich selbst zur Affirmation seiner aufzuheben und durch diese Vermittelung als wahrhaft Unendliches zu seyn.\n\nDiese Bestimmung des wahrhaft Unendlichen kann nicht in die schon gerügte Formel einer Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen gefaßt werden; die Einheit ist abstrakte bewegungslose Sichselbstgleichheit, und die Momente sind ebenso als unbewegte Seyende. Das Unendliche aber ist, wie seine beiden Momente, vielmehr wesentlich nur als Werden, aber das nun in seinen Momenten weiter bestimmte Werden. Dieses hat zunächst das abstrakte Seyn und Nichts zu seinen Bestimmungen; als Veränderung Daseyende, Etwas und Anderes; nun als Unendliches, Endliches und Unendliches, selbst als Werdende.\n\nDieses Unendliche als In-sich-Zurückgekehrtseyn, Beziehung seiner auf sich selbst, ist Seyn aber nicht bestimmungsloses, abstraktes Seyn, denn es ist gesetzt als negirend die Negation; es ist somit auch Daseyn, denn es enthält die Negation überhaupt, somit die Bestimmtheit. Es ist, und ist da, präsent, gegenwärtig. Nur das Schlecht-Unendliche ist das Jenseits, weil es nur die Negation des als real gesetzten Endlichen ist,—so ist es die abstrakte, erste Negation; nur als negativ bestimmt, hat es nicht die Affirmation des Daseyns in ihm; festgehalten als nur Negatives soll es sogar nicht da, soll unerreichbar seyn. Diese Unerreichbarkeit ist aber nicht seine Hoheit, sondern sein Mangel, welcher seinen letzten Grund darin hat, daß das Endliche als solches als seyend festgehalten wird. Das Unwahre ist das Unerreichbare; und es ist einzusehen, daß solches Unendliche das Unwahre ist.—Das Bild des Progresses ins Unendliche ist die gerade Linie, an deren beiden Grenzen nur, das Unendliche und immer nur ist, wo sie,—und sie ist Daseyn—nicht ist, und die zu diesem ihrem Nichtdaseyn, d. i. ins Unbestimmte hinaus geht; als wahrhafte Unendlichkeit, in sich zurückgebogen, wird deren Bild der Kreis, die sich erreicht habende Linie, die geschlossen und ganz gegenwärtig ist, ohne Anfangspunkt und Ende.\n\nDie wahrhafte Unendlichkeit so überhaupt als Daseyn, das als affirmativ gegen die abstrakte Negation gesetzt ist, ist die Realität in höherem Sinn,—als die früher einfach bestimmte; sie hat hier einen konkreten Inhalt erhalten. Das Endliche ist nicht das Reale, sondern das Unendliche. So wird die Realität weiter als das Wesen, der Begriff, die Idee u.s.f. bestimmt. Es ist jedoch überflüssig, solche frühere, abstraktere Kategorien, wie die Realität, bei dem Konkreteren zu wiederholen und sie für konkretere Bestimmungen, als jene an ihnen selbst sind, zu gebrauchen. Solches Wiederholen, wie zu sagen, daß das Wesen oder daß die Idee das Reale sey, hat seine Veranlassung darin, daß dem ungebildeten Denken die abstraktesten Kategorien, wie Seyn, Daseyn, Realität Endlichkeit, die geläufigsten sind.\n\nHier hat die Zurückrufung der Kategorie der Realität ihre bestimmtere Veranlassung, indem die Negation, gegen welche sie das Affirmative ist, hier die Negation der Negation, damit ist sie selbst jener Realität, die das endliche Daseyn ist, gegenüber gesetzt.—Die Negation ist so als Idealität bestimmt; das Ideelle [7] ist das Endliche, wie es im wahrhaften Unendlichen ist,—als eine Bestimmung, Inhalt, der unterschieden, aber nicht selbstständig seyend, sondern als Moment ist. Die Idealität hat diese konkretere Bedeutung, welche durch Negation des endlichen Daseyns nicht vollständig ausgedruckt ist.—In Beziehung auf Realität und Idealität wird aber der Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen so gefaßt, daß das Endliche für das Reale gilt, das Unendliche aber für das Ideelle gilt; wie auch weiterhin der Begriff als ein Ideelles und zwar als ein nur Ideelles, das Daseyn überhaupt dagegen als das Reale betrachtet wird. Auf solche Weise hilft es freilich nichts für die angegebene konkrete Bestimmung der Negation den eigenen Ausdruck des Ideellen zu haben; es wird in jenem Gegensatze wieder zu der Einseitigkeit des abstrakten Negativen, die dem Schlechtunendlichen zukommt, zurückgegangen und bei dem affirmativen Daseyn des Endlichen beharrt.\n\n[7] Das Ideale hat eine weiter bestimmte Bedeutung (des Schönen und was dahin zieht), als das Ideelle; hierher gehört jene noch nicht; es wird hier deswegen der Ausdruck: ideell, gebraucht. Bei der Realität findet dieser Unterschied im Sprachgebrauch wohl nicht Statt; das Reelle und Reale wird ungefähr gleichbedeutend gesagt; die Schattirung beider Ausdrücke etwa gegeneinander hat kein Interesse.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0001","text":"In dem aufgezeigten herüber- und hinübergehenden Wechselbestimmen des Endlichen und Unendlichen ist die Wahrheit derselben an sich schon vorhanden, und es bedarf nur des Aufnehmens dessen, was vorhanden ist. Dieß Herüber- und Hinübergehen macht die äußere Realisation des Begriffes aus; es ist in ihr das, aber äußerlich, außer einander fallend, gesetzt, was der Begriff enthält; es bedarf nur der Vergleichung dieser verschiedenen Momente, in welcher die Einheit sich ergiebt, die den Begriff selbst giebt;—die Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen, ist, wie schon oft bemerkt, hier aber vornehmlich in Erinnerung zu bringen ist, der schiefe Ausdruck für die Einheit, wie sie selbst wahrhaft ist; aber auch das Entfernen dieser schiefen Bestimmung muß in jener vor uns liegenden Äußerung des Begriffes vorhanden seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"34.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0002","text":"Nach ihrer nächsten, nur unmittelbaren Bestimmung genommen, so ist das Unendliche nur als das Hinausgehen über das Endliche; es ist seiner Bestimmung nach die Negation des Endlichen; so ist das Endliche nur als das, worüber hinausgegangen werden muß, die Negation seiner an ihm selbst, welche die Unendlichkeit ist. In jedem liegt hiermit die Bestimmtheit des Andern, die nach der Meinung des unendlichen Progresses von einander ausgeschlossen seyn sollen und nur abwechselnd auf einander folgen; es kann keines gesetzt und gefaßt werden ohne das Andere, das Unendliche nicht ohne das Endliche, dieses nicht ohne das Unendliche. Wenn gesagt wird, was das Unendliche ist, nämlich die Negation des Endlichen, so wird das Endliche selbst mit ausgesprochen; es kann zur Bestimmung des Unendlichen nicht entbehrt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"34.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0003","text":"Man bedarf nur zu wissen, was man sagt, um die Bestimmung des Endlichen im Unendlichen zu finden. Vom Endlichen seinerseits wird sogleich zugegeben, daß es das Nichtige ist, aber eben seine Nichtigkeit ist die Unendlichkeit, von der es ebenso untrennbar ist.—In diesem Auffassen können sie nach ihrer Beziehung auf ihr Anderes genommen zu seyn scheinen. Werden sie hiermit beziehungslos genommen, so daß sie nur durch das: Und verbunden seyen, so stehen sie als selbstständig, jedes nur an ihm selbst seyend, einander gegenüber. Es ist zu sehen, wie sie in solcher Weise beschaffen sind. Das Unendliche so gestellt ist Eines der beiden; aber als nur Eines der beiden ist es selbst endlich, es ist nicht das Ganze, sondern nur die Eine Seite; es hat an dem gegenüberstehenden seine Grenze; es ist so das endliche Unendliche. Es sind nur zwei Endliche vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"34.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0004","text":"Eben darin, daß es so vom Endlichen abgesondert, damit als Einseitiges gestellt wird, liegt seine Endlichkeit, also seine Einheit mit dem Endlichen.—Das Endliche seinerseits als für sich vom Unendlichen entfernt gestellt, ist diese Beziehung auf sich, in der seine Relativität, Abhängigkeit, seine Vergänglichkeit entfernt ist; es ist dieselbe Selbstständigkeit und Affirmation seiner, welche das Unendliche seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"34.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0005","text":"Beide Betrachtungsweisen, die zunächst eine verschiedene Bestimmtheit zu ihrem Ausgangspunkte zu haben scheinen, in sofern die erstere nur als Beziehung des Unendlichen und Endlichen auf einander, eines jeden auf sein Anderes, und die zweite sie in ihrer völligen Absonderung von einander halten soll, geben ein und dasselbe Resultat; das Unendliche und Endliche nach der Beziehung beider auf einander, die ihnen äußerlich wäre, aber die ihnen wesentlich, ohne die keines ist, was es ist, enthält so sein Anderes in seiner eigenen Bestimmung, ebenso sehr als jedes für sich genommen, an ihm selbst betrachtet, sein Anderes in ihm als sein eigenes Moment liegen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"34.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0006","text":"Dieß giebt denn die—verrufene—Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen, —die Einheit, die selbst das Unendliche ist, welches sich selbst und die Endlichkeit in sich begreift,—also das Unendliche in einem anderen Sinne als in dem, wornach das Endliche von ihm abgetrennt und auf die andere Seite gestellt ist. Indem sie nun auch unterschieden werden müssen, ist jedes, wie vorhin gezeigt, selbst an ihm die Einheit beider; so ergeben sich zwei solche Einheiten.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"34.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0007","text":"Das Gemeinschaftliche, die Einheit beider Bestimmtheiten, setzt als Einheit sie zunächst als negirte, da jedes das seyn soll, was es ist in ihrer Unterschiedenheit; in ihrer Einheit verlieren sie also ihre qualitative Natur;—eine wichtige Reflexion gegen die Vorstellung, die sich nicht davon losmachen will, in der Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen sie nach der Qualität, welche sie als außereinander genommen haben sollen, festzuhalten, und daher in jener Einheit nichts als den Widerspruch, nicht auch die Auflösung desselben durch die Negation der qualitativen Bestimmtheit beider sieht; so wird die zunächst einfache, allgemeine Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen verfälscht.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"34.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0008","text":"Ferner aber, indem sie nun auch als unterschieden zu nehmen sind, so ist die Einheit des Unendlichen, die jedes dieser Momente selbst ist, in jedem derselben auf verschiedene Weise bestimmt. Das seiner Bestimmung nach Unendliche hat die von ihm unterschiedene Endlichkeit an ihm, jenes ist das Ansich in dieser Einheit, und dieses ist nur Bestimmtheit, Grenze an ihm, allein es ist eine Grenze, welche das schlechthin Andere desselben, sein Gegentheil ist; seine Bestimmung, welche das An-sich-seyn als solches ist, wird durch den Beischlag einer Qualität solcher Art verdorben; es ist so ein verendlichtes Unendliches. Auf gleiche Weise, indem das Endliche als solches nur das Nicht-ansichseyn ist, aber nach jener Einheit gleichfalls sein Gegentheil an ihm hat, wird es über seinen Werth und zwar so zu sagen unendlich erhoben; es wird als das verunendlichte Endliche gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"34.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0009","text":"Auf gleiche Weise wie vorhin die einfache, so wird vom Verstande auch die gedoppelte Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen verfälscht. Dieß geschieht hier ebenso dadurch, daß in der einen der beiden Einheiten, das Unendliche als nicht negirtes, vielmehr als das An-sich-seyn angenommen wird, an welches also nicht die Bestimmtheit und Schranke gesetzt werden soll; es werde dadurch das An-sich-seyn herabgesetzt und verdorben. Umgekehrt wird das Endliche gleichfalls als das nicht negirte, obgleich an sich Nichtige, festgehalten, so daß es in seiner Verbindung mit dem Unendlichen zu dem, was es nicht sey, erhoben, und dadurch gegen seine nicht verschwundene, vielmehr perennirende Bestimmung verunendlicht werde.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"34.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0010","text":"Die Verfälschung, die der Verstand mit dem Endlichen und Unendlichen vornimmt, ihre Beziehung aufeinander als qualitative Verschiedenheit festzuhalten, sie in ihrer Bestimmung als getrennt und zwar absolut getrennt zu behaupten, gründet sich auf das Vergessen dessen, was für ihn selbst der Begriff dieser Momente ist. Nach diesem ist die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen nicht ein äußerliches Zusammenbringen derselben, noch eine ungehörige, ihrer Bestimmung zuwiderlaufende Verbindung, in welcher an sich getrennte und entgegengesetzte, gegeneinander Selbstständige, Seyende, somit unverträgliche verknüpft würden, sondern jedes ist an ihm selbst diese Einheit, und dieß nur als Aufheben seiner selbst worin keines vor dem andern einen Vorzug des Ansichseyns und affirmativen Daseyns hätte.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"34.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0011","text":"Wie früher gezeigt, ist die Endlichkeit nur als Hinausgehen über sich; es ist also in ihr die Unendlichkeit, das Andere ihrer selbst, enthalten. Eben so ist die Unendlichkeit nur als Hinausgehen über das Endliche; sie enthält also wesentlich ihr Anderes, und ist somit an ihr das Andere ihrer selbst. Das Endliche wird nicht vom Unendlichen als einer außer ihm vorhandenen Macht aufgehoben, sondern es ist seine Unendlichkeit, sich selbst aufzuheben.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"34.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0012","text":"Dieß Aufheben ist somit nicht die Veränderung oder das Andersseyn überhaupt, nicht das Aufheben von Etwas. Das, worin sich das Endliche aufhebt, ist das Unendliche als das Negiren der Endlichkeit; aber diese ist längst selbst nur das Daseyn als ein Nichtseyn bestimmt. Es ist also nur die Negation, die sich in der Negation aufhebt. So ist ihrer Seits die Unendlichkeit als das Negative der Endlichkeit und damit der Bestimmtheit überhaupt, als das leere Jenseits, bestimmt; sein Sich-aufheben im Endlichen ist ein Zurückkehren aus der leeren Flucht, Negation des Jenseits, das ein Negatives an ihm selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"34.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0013","text":"Was also vorhanden ist, ist in beiden dieselbe Negation der Negation. Aber diese ist an sich Beziehung auf sich selbst, die Affirmation aber als Rückkehr zu sich selbst, d. i. durch die Vermittelung, welche die Negation der Negation ist. Diese Bestimmungen sind es, die wesentlich ins Auge zu fassen sind; das zweite aber ist, daß sie im unendlichen Progresse auch gesetzt sind, und wie sie in ihm gesetzt sind,—nämlich noch nicht in ihrer letzten Wahrheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"34.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0014","text":"Es werden darin erstens beide, sowohl das Unendliche als das Endliche negirt,—es wird über beide auf gleiche Weise hinausgegangen; zweitens werden sie auch als unterschiedene, jedes nach dem Andern, als für sich Positive gesetzt. Wir fassen so diese zwei Bestimmungen vergleichend heraus, wie wir in der Vergleichung, einem äußeren Vergleichen, die zwei Betrachtungsweisen, des Endlichen und Unendlichen in ihrer Beziehung, und ihrer jedes für sich genommen, getrennt haben. Aber der unendliche Progreß spricht mehr aus, es ist in ihm auch der Zusammenhang der auch Unterschiedenen gesetzt, jedoch zunächst nur noch als Übergang und Abwechslung; es ist nur in einer einfachen Reflexion von uns zu sehen, was in der That darin vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"34.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0015","text":"Zunächst kann die Negation des Endlichen und Unendlichen, die im unendlichen Progresse gesetzt ist, als einfach, somit als auseinander, nur aufeinander folgend genommen werden. Vom Endlichen angefangen, so wird über die Grenze hinausgegangen, das Endliche negirt. Nun ist also das Jenseits desselben, das Unendliche, vorhanden, aber in diesem entsteht wieder die Grenze; so ist das Hinausgehen über das Unendliche vorhanden. Dieß zweifache Aufheben ist jedoch Theils überhaupt nur als ein äußerliches Geschehen und Abwechseln der Momente, Theils noch nicht als Eine Einheit gesetzt; jedes dieser Hinaus ist ein eigener Ansatz, ein neuer Akt, so daß sie so auseinander fallen.—Es ist aber auch ferner im unendlichen Progresse deren Beziehung vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"34.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0016","text":"Es ist erstlich das Endliche; dann wird darüber hinausgegangen, dieß Negative oder Jenseits des Endlichen ist das Unendliche; drittens wird über diese Negation wieder hinausgegangen, es entsteht eine neue Grenze, wieder ein Endliches. —Dieß ist die vollständige, sich selbst schließende Bewegung, die bei dem angekommen, das den Anfang machte; es entsteht dasselbe, von dem ausgegangen worden war, d. i. das Endliche ist wiederhergestellt; dasselbe ist also mit sich selbst zusammengegangen, hat nur sich in seinem Jenseits wiedergefunden.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"34.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0017","text":"Dasselbe ist der Fall in Ansehung des Unendlichen. Im Unendlichen, dem Jenseits der Grenze entsteht nur eine neue, welche dasselbe Schicksal hat, als Endliches negirt werden zu müssen. Was so wieder vorhanden ist, ist dasselbe Unendliche, das vorhin in der neuen Grenze verschwand; das Unendliche ist daher durch sein Aufheben, durch die neue Grenze hindurch, nicht weiter hinausgeschoben, weder von dem Endlichen entfernt worden, denn dieses ist nur dieß, in das Unendliche überzugehen,—noch von sich selbst, denn es ist bei sich angekommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"34.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0018","text":"So ist beides, das Endliche und das Unendliche, diese Bewegung, zu sich durch seine Negation zurückzukehren; sie sind nur als Vermittelung in sich, und das Affirmative beider enthält die Negation beider, und ist die Negation der Negation.—Sie sind so Resultat, hiermit nicht das, was sie in der Bestimmung ihres Anfangs sind; —nicht das Endliche ein Daseyn seinerseits und das Unendliche ein Daseyn, oder Ansichseyn jenseits des Daseyns, d. i. des als endlich bestimmten.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"34.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0019","text":"Gegen die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen sträubt sich der Verstand nur darum so sehr, weil er die Schranke und das Endliche wie das Ansichseyn als perennirend voraussetzt; damit übersieht er die Negation beider, die im unendlichen Progresse faktisch vorhanden ist, wie ebenso, daß sie darin nur als Momente eines Ganzen vorkommen und daß sie nur vermittelst ihres Gegentheils aber wesentlich ebenso vermittelst des Aufhebens ihres Gegentheils hervortreten.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"34.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0020","text":"Wenn zunächst die Rückkehr in sich, ebenso wohl als Rückkehr des Endlichen zu sich, wie als die des Unendlichen zu sich betrachtet wurde, so zeigt sich in diesem Resultate selbst eine Unrichtigkeit, die mit der so eben gerügten Schiefheit zusammenhängt; das Endliche ist das eine Mal, das Unendliche das Andere Mal als Ausgangspunkt genommen, und nur dadurch entstehen zwei Resultate. Es ist aber völlig gleichgültig, welches als Anfang genommen werde; damit fällt der Unterschied für sich hinweg, der die Zweiheit der Resultate hervorbrachte. Dieß ist in der nach beiden Seiten unbegrenzten Linie des unendlichen Progresses gleichfalls gesetzt, worin jedes der Momente mit gleichem abwechselnden Vorkommen vorhanden, und es ganz äußerlich ist, in welche Stelle gegriffen und als Anfang genommen werde.—Sie sind in demselben unterschieden, aber auf gleiche Weise das eine nur das Moment des andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"34.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0021","text":"Indem sie beide, das Endliche und das Unendliche selbst Momente des Processes sind, sind sie gemeinschaftlich das Endliche, und indem sie ebenso gemeinschaftlich in ihm und im Resultate negirt sind, so heißt dieses Resultat als Negation jener Endlichkeit beider mit Wahrheit das Unendliche. Ihr Unterschied ist so der Doppelsinn, den beide haben. Das Endliche hat den Doppelsinn, erstens nur das Endliche gegen das Unendliche zu seyn, das ihm gegenübersteht, und zweitens das Endliche und das ihm gegenüberstehende Unendliche zugleich zu seyn. Auch das Unendliche hat den Doppelsinn, eines jener beiden Momente zu seyn, so ist es das Schlechtunendliche, und das Unendliche zu seyn, in welchem jene beide, es selbst und sein anderes, nur Momente sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"34.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0022","text":"Wie also das Unendliche in der That vorhanden ist, ist der Proceß zu seyn, in welchem es sich herabsetzt, nur eine seiner Bestimmungen, dem Endlichen gegenüber und damit selbst nur eines der Endlichen zu seyn, und diesen Unterschied seiner von sich selbst zur Affirmation seiner aufzuheben und durch diese Vermittelung als wahrhaft Unendliches zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"34.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0023","text":"Diese Bestimmung des wahrhaft Unendlichen kann nicht in die schon gerügte Formel einer Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen gefaßt werden; die Einheit ist abstrakte bewegungslose Sichselbstgleichheit, und die Momente sind ebenso als unbewegte Seyende. Das Unendliche aber ist, wie seine beiden Momente, vielmehr wesentlich nur als Werden, aber das nun in seinen Momenten weiter bestimmte Werden. Dieses hat zunächst das abstrakte Seyn und Nichts zu seinen Bestimmungen; als Veränderung Daseyende, Etwas und Anderes; nun als Unendliches, Endliches und Unendliches, selbst als Werdende.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"34.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0024","text":"Dieses Unendliche als In-sich-Zurückgekehrtseyn, Beziehung seiner auf sich selbst, ist Seyn aber nicht bestimmungsloses, abstraktes Seyn, denn es ist gesetzt als negirend die Negation; es ist somit auch Daseyn, denn es enthält die Negation überhaupt, somit die Bestimmtheit. Es ist, und ist da, präsent, gegenwärtig. Nur das Schlecht-Unendliche ist das Jenseits, weil es nur die Negation des als real gesetzten Endlichen ist,—so ist es die abstrakte, erste Negation; nur als negativ bestimmt, hat es nicht die Affirmation des Daseyns in ihm; festgehalten als nur Negatives soll es sogar nicht da, soll unerreichbar seyn. Diese Unerreichbarkeit ist aber nicht seine Hoheit, sondern sein Mangel, welcher seinen letzten Grund darin hat, daß das Endliche als solches als seyend festgehalten wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"34.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0025","text":"Das Unwahre ist das Unerreichbare; und es ist einzusehen, daß solches Unendliche das Unwahre ist.—Das Bild des Progresses ins Unendliche ist die gerade Linie, an deren beiden Grenzen nur, das Unendliche und immer nur ist, wo sie,—und sie ist Daseyn—nicht ist, und die zu diesem ihrem Nichtdaseyn, d. i. ins Unbestimmte hinaus geht; als wahrhafte Unendlichkeit, in sich zurückgebogen, wird deren Bild der Kreis, die sich erreicht habende Linie, die geschlossen und ganz gegenwärtig ist, ohne Anfangspunkt und Ende.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"34.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0026","text":"Die wahrhafte Unendlichkeit so überhaupt als Daseyn, das als affirmativ gegen die abstrakte Negation gesetzt ist, ist die Realität in höherem Sinn,—als die früher einfach bestimmte; sie hat hier einen konkreten Inhalt erhalten. Das Endliche ist nicht das Reale, sondern das Unendliche. So wird die Realität weiter als das Wesen, der Begriff, die Idee u.s.f. bestimmt. Es ist jedoch überflüssig, solche frühere, abstraktere Kategorien, wie die Realität, bei dem Konkreteren zu wiederholen und sie für konkretere Bestimmungen, als jene an ihnen selbst sind, zu gebrauchen. Solches Wiederholen, wie zu sagen, daß das Wesen oder daß die Idee das Reale sey, hat seine Veranlassung darin, daß dem ungebildeten Denken die abstraktesten Kategorien, wie Seyn, Daseyn, Realität Endlichkeit, die geläufigsten sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"34.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0027","text":"Hier hat die Zurückrufung der Kategorie der Realität ihre bestimmtere Veranlassung, indem die Negation, gegen welche sie das Affirmative ist, hier die Negation der Negation, damit ist sie selbst jener Realität, die das endliche Daseyn ist, gegenüber gesetzt.—Die Negation ist so als Idealität bestimmt; das Ideelle [7] ist das Endliche, wie es im wahrhaften Unendlichen ist,—als eine Bestimmung, Inhalt, der unterschieden, aber nicht selbstständig seyend, sondern als Moment ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"34.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0028","text":"Die Idealität hat diese konkretere Bedeutung, welche durch Negation des endlichen Daseyns nicht vollständig ausgedruckt ist.—In Beziehung auf Realität und Idealität wird aber der Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen so gefaßt, daß das Endliche für das Reale gilt, das Unendliche aber für das Ideelle gilt; wie auch weiterhin der Begriff als ein Ideelles und zwar als ein nur Ideelles, das Daseyn überhaupt dagegen als das Reale betrachtet wird. Auf solche Weise hilft es freilich nichts für die angegebene konkrete Bestimmung der Negation den eigenen Ausdruck des Ideellen zu haben; es wird in jenem Gegensatze wieder zu der Einseitigkeit des abstrakten Negativen, die dem Schlechtunendlichen zukommt, zurückgegangen und bei dem affirmativen Daseyn des Endlichen beharrt.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"34.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0029","text":"[7] Das Ideale hat eine weiter bestimmte Bedeutung (des Schönen und was dahin zieht), als das Ideelle; hierher gehört jene noch nicht; es wird hier deswegen der Ausdruck: ideell, gebraucht. Bei der Realität findet dieser Unterschied im Sprachgebrauch wohl nicht Statt; das Reelle und Reale wird ungefähr gleichbedeutend gesagt; die Schattirung beider Ausdrücke etwa gegeneinander hat kein Interesse.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"34.29"}],"sha256":"951065eda9528a6edd5877459ff6615e0ab75612ed2b7d6ec8bfd2ba5481750a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102354188412Z_c2b3fdf0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Affirmative Infinity.","source_sha256":"951065eda9528a6edd5877459ff6615e0ab75612ed2b7d6ec8bfd2ba5481750a","sha256":"a6ba4a62c9ac8b2e0e1a345f1426c184e31c959fd9ef1a38bd9e92294cc198ff","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:23:54.188424+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0001","text":"In the exhibited reciprocal determining-over and determining-beyond of the finite and the infinite, their truth is already present in itself, and it is only necessary to take up what is present. This determining-over and determining-beyond constitutes the external realization of the Concept; in it there is posited, though externally, falling apart from one another, that which the Concept contains; only a comparison of these different moments is required, in which there emerges the unity that gives the Concept itself;—the unity of the infinite and finite is, as has already often been remarked, but is here especially to be recalled, the oblique expression for the unity as it is itself in truth; but the removal of this oblique determination must likewise be present in that expression of the Concept lying before us.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"34.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0002","text":"Taken according to its nearest, merely immediate determination, the infinite is only as a going beyond the finite; according to its determination it is the negation of the finite; thus the finite is only as that beyond which one must go, the negation of itself in itself, which is infinity. Each thus contains the determinateness of the other, which according to the opinion of infinite progress ought to be excluded from one another and to follow one another only alternately; neither can be posited and grasped without the other, the infinite not without the finite, the latter not without the infinite. When it is said what the infinite is, namely the negation of the finite, the finite itself is thereby also pronounced; it cannot be dispensed with in determining the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"34.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0003","text":"One need only know what one is saying in order to find the determination of the finite in the infinite. On the part of the finite it is immediately conceded that it is the null; but precisely its nullity is infinity, from which it is equally inseparable.—In this apprehension they may seem to have been taken according to their relation to their other. If they are thereby taken without relation, so that they are connected only by the: And, then they stand over against one another as self-subsistent, each being only in itself. It is to be seen what they are like in this fashion. The infinite thus posited is one of the two; but as merely one of the two, it is itself finite; it is not the whole, but only the one side; it has its limit in that which stands over against it; it is thus the finite infinite. There are only two finites present.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"34.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0004","text":"Precisely in the fact that it is thus separated from the finite, and thereby posited as one-sided, lies its finitude, and hence its unity with the finite.—The finite, for its part, posited as removed from the infinite for itself, is this relation to itself in which its relativity, dependence, and transience are removed; it is the same self-subsistence and affirmation of itself that the infinite is supposed to be.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"34.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0005","text":"Both ways of considering, which at first seem to have a different determinateness as their point of departure, insofar as the first is only supposed to be the relation of the infinite and finite to one another, of each to its other, while the second is supposed to hold them in their complete separation from one another, yield one and the same result; the infinite and finite, according to the relation of the two to one another, which would be external to them but is essential to them, without which neither is what it is, thus contains its other in its own determination, just as much as each, taken for itself and considered in itself, has its other lying within it as its own moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"34.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0006","text":"This then yields the—disreputable—unity of the finite and infinite,—the unity which is itself the infinite, comprehending itself and finitude within itself,—thus the infinite in a sense other than that according to which the finite is separated from it and placed on the other side. Since they must now also be distinguished, each, as was shown above, is itself in itself the unity of both; thus there result two such unities.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"34.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0007","text":"What they have in common, the unity of the two determinatenesses, at first posits them as negated in their unity, since each is supposed to be what it is in their difference; in their unity they therefore lose their qualitative nature;—an important reflection against the representation that will not free itself from holding them fast in the unity of the infinite and finite according to the quality which they are supposed to have when taken as external to one another, and therefore sees in that unity nothing but contradiction, not also its resolution through the negation of the qualitative determinateness of both; thus the initially simple, universal unity of the infinite and finite is falsified.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"34.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0008","text":"But further, since they are now also to be taken as distinct, the unity of the infinite, which each of these moments itself is, is determined differently in each of them. That which is infinite according to its determination has within it finitude, distinct from it; the former is the in-itself in this unity, and the latter is only determinateness, limit in it; yet it is a limit which is its absolute other, its opposite; its determination, which is being-in-itself as such, is corrupted by the admixture of a quality of this kind; it is thus a finitized infinite. In the same way, since the finite as such is only non-being-in-itself, but according to that unity likewise has its opposite within it, it is raised above its worth, and indeed, so to speak, infinitely raised; it is posited as the infinitized finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"34.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0009","text":"Just as previously the simple unity, so too the doubled unity of the infinite and finite is falsified by the Understanding. This occurs here likewise by assuming, in one of the two unities, the infinite as not negated, but rather as being-in-itself, to which therefore determinateness and limit are not supposed to be posited; it is thereby said that being-in-itself would be degraded and corrupted. Conversely, the finite is likewise held fast as not negated, although null in itself, so that in its connection with the infinite it is raised to what it is not, and thereby infinitized contrary to its determination, which has not vanished but rather endures.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"34.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0010","text":"The falsification which the Understanding undertakes with the finite and infinite, namely, to maintain their relation to one another as qualitative difference, to assert them as separated in their determination, indeed as absolutely separated, is grounded on forgetfulness of what the Concept of these moments is for the Understanding itself. According to this Concept, the unity of the finite and infinite is neither an external bringing together of them nor an improper connection, contrary to their determination, in which things separated and opposed in themselves, self-subsistent beings over against one another, hence incompatible things, would be conjoined; rather, each is in itself this unity, and this only as sublation of itself, in which neither would have a precedence over the other in being-in-itself and affirmative existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"34.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0011","text":"As was shown earlier, finitude is only as a going beyond itself; thus infinity, the other of itself, is contained in it. Likewise, infinity is only as a going beyond the finite; it therefore essentially contains its other, and is thus in itself the other of itself. The finite is not sublated by the infinite as a power existing outside it, but it is its infinity to sublate itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"34.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0012","text":"This sublation is thus not alteration or otherness in general, not the sublation of something. That in which the finite sublates itself is the infinite as the negating of finitude; but this has long since itself been determined only as existence as a non-being. Thus it is only negation which sublates itself in negation. For its part, infinity, as the negative of finitude and thereby of determinateness in general, is determined as the empty beyond; its self-sublation in the finite is a return from empty flight, negation of the beyond, which is a negative in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"34.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0013","text":"What is present, therefore, is in both the same negation of negation. But this is in itself relation to itself, affirmation, however, as return to itself, i.e. through the mediation which is the negation of negation. These are the determinations that must essentially be kept in view; but the second point is that they are also posited in infinite progress, and how they are posited in it,—namely, not yet in their final truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"34.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0014","text":"In it, first, both, the infinite as well as the finite, are negated,—one goes beyond both in the same manner; second, they are also posited as distinct, each after the other, as positive for itself. Thus we extract these two determinations comparatively, just as in comparison, an external comparing, we separated the two ways of considering, that of the finite and infinite in their relation and that of each taken for itself. But infinite progress expresses more; in it the connection of those which are also distinct is posited, though at first only as transition and alternation; it is only in a simple reflection on our part that one sees what is in fact present therein.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"34.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0015","text":"At first, the negation of the finite and infinite which is posited in infinite progress may be taken as simple, and hence as apart, merely succeeding one another. Beginning from the finite, one goes beyond the limit, and the finite is negated. Now its beyond, the infinite, is present; but in this the limit arises again; thus going beyond the infinite is present. This twofold sublation, however, is partly in general only an external occurrence and alternation of the moments, partly is not yet posited as one unity; each of these goings-beyond is a separate beginning, a new act, so that they fall apart in this way.—But further, their relation is also present in infinite progress.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"34.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0016","text":"There is first the finite; then one goes beyond it; this negative, or beyond of the finite, is the infinite; thirdly, one goes beyond this negation again, a new limit arises, again a finite. —This is the complete, self-closing movement, which arrives at that which made the beginning; the same arises from which the departure had been made, i.e. the finite is restored; it has thus come together with itself, has only found itself again in its beyond.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"34.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0017","text":"The same is the case with respect to the infinite. In the infinite, the beyond of the limit, there arises only a new limit, which has the same fate, of having to be negated as finite. What is thereby present again is the same infinite that previously vanished in the new limit; the infinite has therefore, through its sublation, through the new limit, not been pushed farther out, neither removed from the finite, for the latter is only this, to pass over into the infinite,—nor from itself, for it has arrived at itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"34.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0018","text":"Thus both, the finite and the infinite, are this movement of returning to themselves through their negation; they are only as mediation within themselves, and the affirmative of both contains the negation of both and is the negation of negation.—They are thus result, and hence not what they are in the determination of their beginning;—not the finite an existence on its own part and the infinite an existence, or being-in-itself, beyond existence, i.e. beyond that determined as finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"34.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0019","text":"The Understanding resists the unity of finite and infinite so strongly only because it presupposes limit and finitude, as well as being-in-itself, as enduring; in doing so, it overlooks the negation of both which is factually present in infinite progress, just as it overlooks that they occur therein only as moments of a whole and that they emerge only by means of their opposite, but essentially equally by means of the sublation of their opposite.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"34.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0020","text":"If, initially, the return into itself was considered both as the return of the finite to itself and as that of the infinite to itself, then in this result itself there appears an incorrectness connected with the obliqueness just reproved; the finite was once, the infinite the other time, taken as the point of departure, and only thereby do two results arise. But it is wholly indifferent which is taken as the beginning; thus the distinction in itself which brought forth the duality of the results falls away. This is likewise posited in the line of infinite progress, unlimited in both directions, in which each of the moments is present with equal alternating occurrence, and it is wholly external which place is seized upon and taken as the beginning.—They are distinct within it, but in the same way the one is only the moment of the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"34.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0021","text":"Since both, the finite and the infinite, are themselves moments of the process, they are jointly the finite, and since they are likewise jointly negated in it and in the result, this result, as negation of the finitude of both, is rightly called the infinite. Their difference is thus the double sense which both have. The finite has the double sense, first, of being only the finite over against the infinite standing opposite it, and second, of being at once the finite and the infinite standing opposite it. The infinite too has the double sense of being one of those two moments, in which case it is the bad infinite, and of being the infinite in which those two, itself and its other, are only moments.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"34.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0022","text":"Thus, as the infinite is present in fact, it is the process of being in which it lowers itself to be only one of its determinations, over against the finite and thereby itself only one of the finites, and of sublating this distinction of itself from itself into its affirmation, and through this mediation of being truly infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"34.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0023","text":"This determination of the truly infinite cannot be comprehended in the formula, already criticized, of a unity of the finite and the infinite; unity is abstract, motionless self-equality, and the moments likewise are motionless beings. But the infinite, like its two moments, is rather essentially only as becoming, but now as becoming further determined in its moments. At first this has abstract being and nothing as its determinations; as existence, it has change, something and other; now, as infinite, finite and infinite, themselves as becoming.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"34.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0024","text":"This infinite, as having-returned-into-itself, relation of itself to itself, is being, but not indeterminate, abstract being; for it is posited as negating negation; it is thus also existence, for it contains negation in general, hence determinacy. It is, and it is there, present, actual. Only the spurious infinite is the beyond, because it is only the negation of the finite posited as real,—thus it is the abstract, first negation; determined only as negative, it does not have in it the affirmation of existence; held fast as merely negative, it is even supposed not to be there, supposed to be unattainable. But this unattainability is not its loftiness, but its defect, whose ultimate ground lies in this, that the finite as such is held fast as being.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"34.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0025","text":"What is untrue is the unattainable; and it is to be seen that such an infinite is the untrue.—The image of the progress into infinity is the straight line, at whose two boundaries alone the infinite is, and always only where it,—and it is existence—is not, and which goes out toward this its non-existence, i.e. into the indeterminate; as true infinity, bent back into itself, its image becomes the circle, the line that has attained itself, which is closed and wholly present, without starting-point and end.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"34.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0026","text":"True infinity thus in general as existence, which is posited as affirmative over against abstract negation, is reality in a higher sense,—than the earlier simply determined reality; it has here received a concrete content. The finite is not the real; rather, the infinite is. Thus reality is further determined as essence, concept, idea, etc. It is, however, superfluous to repeat such earlier, more abstract categories as reality in connection with what is more concrete, and to employ them for more concrete determinations than they are in themselves. Such repetition, as in saying that essence or that the idea is the real, has its occasion in the fact that for uncultivated thinking the most abstract categories, such as being, existence, reality, finitude, are the most familiar.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"34.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0027","text":"Here the recall of the category of reality has its more specific occasion, inasmuch as the negation over against which it is the affirmative is here the negation of negation; thereby it is itself posited over against that reality which is finite existence.—Negation is thus determined as ideality; the ideal [7] is the finite as it is in true infinity,—as a determination, content, which is distinguished, but is not independently being, rather is a moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"34.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0028","text":"Ideality has this more concrete significance, which is not completely expressed by negation of finite existence.—In relation to reality and ideality, however, the opposition of finite and infinite is conceived in such a way that the finite counts as the real, but the infinite as the ideal; just as subsequently the concept is regarded as an ideal, indeed as a merely ideal, whereas existence in general is regarded as the real. In this way, to be sure, it is of no help for the indicated concrete determination of negation to have the distinctive expression of the ideal; in that opposition one returns to the one-sidedness of abstract negativity, which belongs to the spurious infinite, and persists in the affirmative existence of the finite.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"34.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0029","text":"[7] The ideal has a more specifically determined meaning (that of the beautiful and what pertains thereto) than the ideality; that meaning does not yet belong here; for this reason the expression “ideal” is used here. In the case of reality, this distinction does not obtain in linguistic usage; “the real” and “reality” are said with approximately the same meaning; the nuance of the two expressions in relation to one another is of no interest.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"34.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAU:P0029"]}],"source_digest":"cae7be1a1ab7252a4083337aa36012febe554ce96c427add204d8093942dce08","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die affirmative Unendlichkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die affirmative Unendlichkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DERB","title":"The Transition.","order":35,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DERB","text":"Die Idealität kann die Qualität der Unendlichkeit genannt werden; aber sie ist wesentlich der Proceß des Werdens und damit ein Übergang, wie des Werdens in Daseyn, der nun anzugeben ist. Als Aufheben der Endlichkeit, d. i. der Endlichkeit als solcher und ebenso sehr der ihr nur gegenüberstehenden, nur negativen Unendlichkeit ist diese Rückkehr in sich, Beziehung auf sich selbst, Seyn. Da in diesem Seyn Negation ist, ist es Daseyn, aber da sie ferner wesentlich Negation der Negation, die sich auf sich beziehende Negation ist, ist sie das Daseyn, welches Fürsichseyn genannt wird.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DERB:P0001","text":"Die Idealität kann die Qualität der Unendlichkeit genannt werden; aber sie ist wesentlich der Proceß des Werdens und damit ein Übergang, wie des Werdens in Daseyn, der nun anzugeben ist. Als Aufheben der Endlichkeit, d. i. der Endlichkeit als solcher und ebenso sehr der ihr nur gegenüberstehenden, nur negativen Unendlichkeit ist diese Rückkehr in sich, Beziehung auf sich selbst, Seyn. Da in diesem Seyn Negation ist, ist es Daseyn, aber da sie ferner wesentlich Negation der Negation, die sich auf sich beziehende Negation ist, ist sie das Daseyn, welches Fürsichseyn genannt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"35.1"}],"sha256":"f7f1763cbaa4f600ad10a6d0d29fa8fa6a1a1372ae8a5f06164763ef7d9ce7f3","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102356879796Z_cf78fcd7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"The Transition.","source_sha256":"f7f1763cbaa4f600ad10a6d0d29fa8fa6a1a1372ae8a5f06164763ef7d9ce7f3","sha256":"6ac8f8fdbb7c4a8aee09264add3cbda4dc707acdc006583e3851d2f9afe2fab2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:23:56.879816+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DERB:P0001","text":"Ideality can be called the quality of infinity; but it is essentially the process of becoming and thus a transition, like that from becoming into determinate being, which is now to be indicated. As the sublation of finitude, i.e. of finitude as such and equally of the infinity merely opposed to it, merely negative, this return into itself, relation to itself, is being. Since negation is in this being, it is determinate being; but since it is further essentially negation of negation, self-relating negation, it is the determinate being which is called being-for-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"35.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DERB:P0001"]}],"source_digest":"05041e320dce0ffa45459da91e3b9fe59734748a1a161275457e770dd845acd7","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Der Übergang."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Der Übergang.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4","title":"Remark 1.","order":36,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_4","text":"Das Unendliche,—nach dem gewöhnlichen Sinne der schlechten Unendlichkeit,—und der Progreß ins Unendliche, wie das Sollen, sind der Ausdruck eines Widerspruchs, der sich selbst für die Auflösung und für das Letzte giebt. Dieß Unendliche ist eine erste Erhebung des sinnlichen Vorstellens über das Endliche in den Gedanken, der aber nur den Inhalt von Nichts, dem ausdrücklich als Nichtseyend gesetzten, hat,—eine Flucht über das Beschränkte, die sich nicht in sich sammelt, und das Negative nicht zum Positiven zurückzubringen weiß. Diese unvollendete Reflexion hat die beiden Bestimmungen des wahrhaft Unendlichen: den Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen, und die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen, vollständig vor sich, aber bringt diese beiden Gedanken nicht zusammen; der eine führt untrennbar den anderen herbei, aber sie läßt sie nur abwechseln. Die Darstellung dieser Abwechslung, der unendliche Progreß, tritt allenthalben ein, wo in dem Widerspruche der Einheit zweier Bestimmungen und des Gegensatzes derselben verharrt wird. Das Endliche ist das Aufheben seiner selbst, es schließt seine Negation, die Unendlichkeit in sich;—die Einheit beider,—es wird hinaus über das Endliche zum Unendlichen als dem Jenseits desselben gegangen, —Trennung beider; aber über das Unendliche hinaus ist ein anderes Endliches,—das Hinaus, das Unendliche, enthält die Endlichkeit, —Einheit beider; aber dieß Endliche ist auch ein Negatives des Unendlichen;—Trennung beider, u.s.f.—So ist im Kausalitätsverhältniß Ursache und Wirkung untrennbar; eine Ursache, die keine Wirkung haben sollte, ist nicht Ursache, wie die Wirkung, die keine Ursache hätte, nicht mehr Wirkung. Dieß Verhältniß giebt daher den unendlichen Progreß von Ursachen und Wirkungen; Etwas ist als Ursache bestimmt, aber sie hat als ein endliches (—und endlich ist sie eben eigentlich wegen ihrer Trennung von der Wirkung) selbst eine Ursache, d. h. sie ist auch Wirkung; somit ist dasselbe, was als Ursache bestimmt wurde, auch als Wirkung bestimmt;—Einheit der Ursache und der Wirkung;—das nun als Wirkung Bestimmte hat von neuem eine Ursache, d. i. die Ursache ist von ihrer Wirkung zu trennen, und als ein verschiedenes Etwas zu setzen;—diese neue Ursache ist aber selbst nur eine Wirkung—Einheit der Ursache und Wirkung;—sie hat ein Anderes zu ihrer Ursache;—Trennung beider Bestimmungen u.s.f. ins Unendliche.\n\nDem Progreß kann so die eigenthümlichere Form gegeben werden; es wird die Behauptung gemacht, das Endliche und Unendliche sind Eine Einheit; diese falsche Behauptung muß durch die entgegengesetzte berichtigt werden: sie sind schlechthin verschieden und sich entgegengesetzt; diese ist wieder dahin zu berichtigen, daß sie untrennbar sind, in der einen Bestimmung die andere liegt, durch die Behauptung ihrer Einheit und so fort ins Unendliche.—Es ist eine leichte Forderung, welche um die Natur des Unendlichen einzusehen, gemacht wird, das Bewußtseyn zu haben, daß der unendliche Progreß, das entwickelte Unendliche des Verstandes, die Beschaffenheit hat, die Abwechslung der beiden Bestimmungen, der Einheit und der Trennung beider Momente zu seyn, und dann das fernere Bewußtseyn zu haben, daß diese Einheit und diese Trennung selbst untrennbar sind.\n\nDie Auflösung dieses Widerspruchs ist nicht die Anerkennung der gleichen Richtigkeit, und der gleichen Unrichtigkeit beider Behauptungen;—dieß ist nur eine andere Gestalt des bleibenden Widerspruchs,—sondern die Idealität beider, als in welcher sie in ihrem Unterschiede, als gegenseitige Negationen, nur Momente sind; jene eintönige Abwechslung ist faktisch sowohl die Negation der Einheit als der Trennung derselben. In ihr ist ebenso faktisch das oben Aufgezeigte vorhanden, daß das Endliche über sich hinaus in das Unendliche fällt, aber ebenso über dasselbe hinaus sich selbst wieder erzeugt findet, hiermit darin nur mit sich zusammengeht, wie das Unendliche gleichfalls; so daß dieselbe Negation der Negation sich zur Affirmation resultirt, welches Resultat sich damit als ihre Wahrheit und Ursprünglichkeit erweist. In diesem Seyn hiermit als der Idealität der Unterschiedenen ist der Widerspruch nicht abstrakt verschwunden, sondern aufgelöst und versöhnt, und die Gedanken sind nicht nur vollständig, sondern sie sind auch zusammengebracht. Die Natur des spekulativen Denkens zeigt sich hieran als einem ausgeführten Beispiele in ihrer bestimmten Weise, sie besteht allein in dem Auffassen der entgegengesetzten Momente in ihrer Einheit. Indem jedes und zwar faktisch sich an ihm zeigt, sein Gegentheil an ihm selbst zu haben, und in diesem mit sich zusammenzugehen, so ist die affirmative Wahrheit diese sich in sich bewegende Einheit, das Zusammenfassen beider Gedanken, ihre Unendlichkeit,—die Beziehung auf sich selbst, nicht die unmittelbare, sondern die unendliche.\n\nDas Wesen der Philosophie ist häufig von solchen, die mit dem Denken schon vertrauter sind, in die Aufgabe gesetzt worden, zu beantworten, wie das Unendliche aus sich heraus und zur Endlichkeit komme?—Dieß, meint man, sey nicht begreiflich zu machen. Das Unendliche, bei dessen Begriff wir angekommen sind, wird sich im Fortgange dieser Darstellung weiter bestimmen, und an ihm in aller Mannigfaltigkeit der Formen das Geforderte zeigen, wie es, wenn man sich so ausdrücken will, zur Endlichkeit komme. Hier betrachten wir diese Frage nur in ihrer Unmittelbarkeit, und in Rücksicht des vorhin betrachteten Sinnes, den das Unendliche zu haben pflegt.\n\nVon der Beantwortung dieser Frage soll es überhaupt abhängen, ob es eine Philosophie gebe, und indem man es hierauf noch ankommen lassen zu wollen vorgiebt, glaubt man zugleich an der Frage selbst eine Art von Vexirfrage, einen unüberwindlichen Talisman, zu besitzen, durch den man gegen die Beantwortung und damit gegen die Philosophie und das Ankommen bei derselben fest und gesichert sey. Auch bei anderen Gegenständen setzt es eine Bildung voraus, fragen zu verstehen, noch mehr aber bei philosophischen Gegenständen, um eine andere Antwort zu erhalten, als die, daß die Frage nichts tauge.—Es pflegt bei solchen Fragen die Billigkeit in Anspruch genommen zu werden, daß es auf die Worte nicht ankomme, sondern in einer oder anderen Weise des Ausdrucks verständlich sey, worauf es ankomme? Ausdrücke sinnlicher Vorstellung, wie herausgehen und dergleichen, die bei der Frage gebraucht werden, erwecken den Verdacht, daß sie aus dem Boden des gewöhnlichen Vorstellens stamme, und für die Beantwortung auch Vorstellungen, die im gemeinen Leben gangbar sind, und die Gestalt eines sinnlichen Gleichnisses erwartet werden.\n\nWenn statt des Unendlichen das Seyn überhaupt genommen wird, so scheint das Bestimmen des Seyns, eine Negation oder Endlichkeit an ihm, leichter begreiflich. Seyn ist zwar selbst das Unbestimmte, aber es ist nicht unmittelbar an ihm ausgedrückt, daß es das Gegentheil des Bestimmten sey. Das Unendliche hingegen enthält dieß ausgedrückt; es ist das Nicht-Endliche. Die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen scheint somit unmittelbar ausgeschlossen; die unvollendete Reflexion ist darum am hartnäckigsten gegen diese Einheit.\n\nEs ist aber gezeigt worden, und es erhellt, ohne weiter in die Bestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen einzugehen, unmittelbar, daß das Unendliche in dem Sinne, ( in dem es von jenem Reflektiren genommen wird,—nämlich als dem Endlichen gegenüberstehend,—darum weil es ihm gegenübersteht, an ihm sein Anderes hat, daher schon begrenzt, und selbst endlich, das Schlechtunendliche ist. Die Antwort auf die Frage, wie das Unendliche endlich werde, ist somit diese, daß es nicht ein Unendliches gibt, das vorerst unendlich ist, und das nachher erst endlich zu werden, zur Endlichkeit herauszugehen nöthig habe, sondern es ist für sich selbst schon eben so sehr endlich als unendlich. Indem die Frage annimmt, daß das Unendliche einer Seits für sich, und daß das Endliche, das aus ihm heraus in die Trennung gegangen, oder wo es hergekommen seyn möchte, abgesondert von ihm, wahrhaft real sey,—so wäre vielmehr zu sagen, diese Trennung sey unbegreiflich. Weder solches Endliches, noch solches Unendliches hat Wahrheit; das Unwahre aber ist unbegreiflich. Man muß aber ebenso sagen, sie seyen begreiflich; die Betrachtung derselben, auch wie sie in der Vorstellung sind, daß in dem einen die Bestimmung des anderen liegt, die einfache Einsicht in diese ihre Untrennbarkeit haben, heißt sie begreifen; diese Untrennbarkeit ist ihr Begriff.—In der Selbstständigkeit jenes Unendlichen und Endlichen dagegen stellt jene Frage einen unwahren Inhalt auf, und enthält in sich schon eine unwahre Beziehung desselben. Darum ist nicht auf sie zu antworten, sondern vielmehr sind die falschen Voraussetzungen, die sie enthält, d. i. die Frage selbst zu negiren. Durch die Frage nach der Wahrheit jenes Unendlichen und Endlichen wird der Standpunkt verändert, und diese Veränderung wird die Verlegenheit, welche die erste Frage hervorbringen sollte, auf sie zurückbringen; jene unsre Frage ist der Reflexion, aus der die erste Frage stammt, neu, da solches Reflektiren nicht das spekulative Interesse enthält, welches, für sich und ehe es Bestimmungen bezieht, darauf geht, zu erkennen, ob dieselben, wie sie vorausgesetzt werden, etwas Wahres seyen. Insofern aber die Unwahrheit jenes abstrakten Unendlichen, und des eben so auf seiner Seite stehen bleiben sollenden Endlichen erkannt ist, so ist über das Herausgehen des Endlichen aus dem Unendlichen zu sagen, das Unendliche gehe zur Endlichkeit heraus, darum weil es keine Wahrheit, kein Bestehen an ihm, wie es als abstrakte Einheit gefaßt ist, hat; so umgekehrt geht das Endliche aus demselben Grunde seiner Nichtigkeit in das Unendliche hinein. oder vielmehr ist zu sagen, daß das Unendliche ewig zur Endlichkeit herausgegangen, daß es schlechthin nicht ist, so wenig als das reine Seyn, allein für sich, ohne sein Anderes an ihm selbst zu haben.\n\nJene Frage, wie das Unendliche zum Endlichen herausgehe, kann noch die weitere Voraussetzung enthalten, daß das Unendliche an sich das Endliche in sich schliesse, somit an sich die Einheit seiner selbst und seines Anderen sey, so daß die Schwierigkeit sich wesentlich auf das Trennen bezieht, als welches der vorausgesetzten Einheit beider entgegensteht. In dieser Voraussetzung hat der Gegensatz, an welchem festgehalten s wird, nur eine andere Gestalt; die Einheit und das Unterscheiden werden von einander getrennt und isolirt. Wenn aber jene nicht als die abstrakte unbestimmte Einheit, sondern schon wie in jener Voraussetzung als die bestimmte Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen genommen wird, so ist die Unterscheidung beider bereits darin auch vorhanden,—eine Unterscheidung, die so zugleich nicht ein Loslassen derselben zu getrennter Selbstständigkeit ist, sondern sie als ideelle in der Einheit läßt. Diese Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen und deren Unterscheidung sind dasselbe Untrennbare als die Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0001","text":"Das Unendliche,—nach dem gewöhnlichen Sinne der schlechten Unendlichkeit,—und der Progreß ins Unendliche, wie das Sollen, sind der Ausdruck eines Widerspruchs, der sich selbst für die Auflösung und für das Letzte giebt. Dieß Unendliche ist eine erste Erhebung des sinnlichen Vorstellens über das Endliche in den Gedanken, der aber nur den Inhalt von Nichts, dem ausdrücklich als Nichtseyend gesetzten, hat,—eine Flucht über das Beschränkte, die sich nicht in sich sammelt, und das Negative nicht zum Positiven zurückzubringen weiß. Diese unvollendete Reflexion hat die beiden Bestimmungen des wahrhaft Unendlichen: den Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen, und die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen, vollständig vor sich, aber bringt diese beiden Gedanken nicht zusammen; der eine führt untrennbar den anderen herbei, aber sie läßt sie nur abwechseln.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"36.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0002","text":"Die Darstellung dieser Abwechslung, der unendliche Progreß, tritt allenthalben ein, wo in dem Widerspruche der Einheit zweier Bestimmungen und des Gegensatzes derselben verharrt wird. Das Endliche ist das Aufheben seiner selbst, es schließt seine Negation, die Unendlichkeit in sich;—die Einheit beider,—es wird hinaus über das Endliche zum Unendlichen als dem Jenseits desselben gegangen, —Trennung beider; aber über das Unendliche hinaus ist ein anderes Endliches,—das Hinaus, das Unendliche, enthält die Endlichkeit, —Einheit beider; aber dieß Endliche ist auch ein Negatives des Unendlichen;—Trennung beider, u.s.f.—So ist im Kausalitätsverhältniß Ursache und Wirkung untrennbar; eine Ursache, die keine Wirkung haben sollte, ist nicht Ursache, wie die Wirkung, die keine Ursache hätte, nicht mehr Wirkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"36.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0003","text":"Dieß Verhältniß giebt daher den unendlichen Progreß von Ursachen und Wirkungen; Etwas ist als Ursache bestimmt, aber sie hat als ein endliches (—und endlich ist sie eben eigentlich wegen ihrer Trennung von der Wirkung) selbst eine Ursache, d. h. sie ist auch Wirkung; somit ist dasselbe, was als Ursache bestimmt wurde, auch als Wirkung bestimmt;—Einheit der Ursache und der Wirkung;—das nun als Wirkung Bestimmte hat von neuem eine Ursache, d. i. die Ursache ist von ihrer Wirkung zu trennen, und als ein verschiedenes Etwas zu setzen;—diese neue Ursache ist aber selbst nur eine Wirkung—Einheit der Ursache und Wirkung;—sie hat ein Anderes zu ihrer Ursache;—Trennung beider Bestimmungen u.s.f. ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"36.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0004","text":"Dem Progreß kann so die eigenthümlichere Form gegeben werden; es wird die Behauptung gemacht, das Endliche und Unendliche sind Eine Einheit; diese falsche Behauptung muß durch die entgegengesetzte berichtigt werden: sie sind schlechthin verschieden und sich entgegengesetzt; diese ist wieder dahin zu berichtigen, daß sie untrennbar sind, in der einen Bestimmung die andere liegt, durch die Behauptung ihrer Einheit und so fort ins Unendliche.—Es ist eine leichte Forderung, welche um die Natur des Unendlichen einzusehen, gemacht wird, das Bewußtseyn zu haben, daß der unendliche Progreß, das entwickelte Unendliche des Verstandes, die Beschaffenheit hat, die Abwechslung der beiden Bestimmungen, der Einheit und der Trennung beider Momente zu seyn, und dann das fernere Bewußtseyn zu haben, daß diese Einheit und diese Trennung selbst untrennbar sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"36.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0005","text":"Die Auflösung dieses Widerspruchs ist nicht die Anerkennung der gleichen Richtigkeit, und der gleichen Unrichtigkeit beider Behauptungen;—dieß ist nur eine andere Gestalt des bleibenden Widerspruchs,—sondern die Idealität beider, als in welcher sie in ihrem Unterschiede, als gegenseitige Negationen, nur Momente sind; jene eintönige Abwechslung ist faktisch sowohl die Negation der Einheit als der Trennung derselben. In ihr ist ebenso faktisch das oben Aufgezeigte vorhanden, daß das Endliche über sich hinaus in das Unendliche fällt, aber ebenso über dasselbe hinaus sich selbst wieder erzeugt findet, hiermit darin nur mit sich zusammengeht, wie das Unendliche gleichfalls; so daß dieselbe Negation der Negation sich zur Affirmation resultirt, welches Resultat sich damit als ihre Wahrheit und Ursprünglichkeit erweist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"36.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0006","text":"In diesem Seyn hiermit als der Idealität der Unterschiedenen ist der Widerspruch nicht abstrakt verschwunden, sondern aufgelöst und versöhnt, und die Gedanken sind nicht nur vollständig, sondern sie sind auch zusammengebracht. Die Natur des spekulativen Denkens zeigt sich hieran als einem ausgeführten Beispiele in ihrer bestimmten Weise, sie besteht allein in dem Auffassen der entgegengesetzten Momente in ihrer Einheit. Indem jedes und zwar faktisch sich an ihm zeigt, sein Gegentheil an ihm selbst zu haben, und in diesem mit sich zusammenzugehen, so ist die affirmative Wahrheit diese sich in sich bewegende Einheit, das Zusammenfassen beider Gedanken, ihre Unendlichkeit,—die Beziehung auf sich selbst, nicht die unmittelbare, sondern die unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"36.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0007","text":"Das Wesen der Philosophie ist häufig von solchen, die mit dem Denken schon vertrauter sind, in die Aufgabe gesetzt worden, zu beantworten, wie das Unendliche aus sich heraus und zur Endlichkeit komme?—Dieß, meint man, sey nicht begreiflich zu machen. Das Unendliche, bei dessen Begriff wir angekommen sind, wird sich im Fortgange dieser Darstellung weiter bestimmen, und an ihm in aller Mannigfaltigkeit der Formen das Geforderte zeigen, wie es, wenn man sich so ausdrücken will, zur Endlichkeit komme. Hier betrachten wir diese Frage nur in ihrer Unmittelbarkeit, und in Rücksicht des vorhin betrachteten Sinnes, den das Unendliche zu haben pflegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"36.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0008","text":"Von der Beantwortung dieser Frage soll es überhaupt abhängen, ob es eine Philosophie gebe, und indem man es hierauf noch ankommen lassen zu wollen vorgiebt, glaubt man zugleich an der Frage selbst eine Art von Vexirfrage, einen unüberwindlichen Talisman, zu besitzen, durch den man gegen die Beantwortung und damit gegen die Philosophie und das Ankommen bei derselben fest und gesichert sey. Auch bei anderen Gegenständen setzt es eine Bildung voraus, fragen zu verstehen, noch mehr aber bei philosophischen Gegenständen, um eine andere Antwort zu erhalten, als die, daß die Frage nichts tauge.—Es pflegt bei solchen Fragen die Billigkeit in Anspruch genommen zu werden, daß es auf die Worte nicht ankomme, sondern in einer oder anderen Weise des Ausdrucks verständlich sey, worauf es ankomme?","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"36.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0009","text":"Ausdrücke sinnlicher Vorstellung, wie herausgehen und dergleichen, die bei der Frage gebraucht werden, erwecken den Verdacht, daß sie aus dem Boden des gewöhnlichen Vorstellens stamme, und für die Beantwortung auch Vorstellungen, die im gemeinen Leben gangbar sind, und die Gestalt eines sinnlichen Gleichnisses erwartet werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"36.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0010","text":"Wenn statt des Unendlichen das Seyn überhaupt genommen wird, so scheint das Bestimmen des Seyns, eine Negation oder Endlichkeit an ihm, leichter begreiflich. Seyn ist zwar selbst das Unbestimmte, aber es ist nicht unmittelbar an ihm ausgedrückt, daß es das Gegentheil des Bestimmten sey. Das Unendliche hingegen enthält dieß ausgedrückt; es ist das Nicht-Endliche. Die Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen scheint somit unmittelbar ausgeschlossen; die unvollendete Reflexion ist darum am hartnäckigsten gegen diese Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"36.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0011","text":"Es ist aber gezeigt worden, und es erhellt, ohne weiter in die Bestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen einzugehen, unmittelbar, daß das Unendliche in dem Sinne, ( in dem es von jenem Reflektiren genommen wird,—nämlich als dem Endlichen gegenüberstehend,—darum weil es ihm gegenübersteht, an ihm sein Anderes hat, daher schon begrenzt, und selbst endlich, das Schlechtunendliche ist. Die Antwort auf die Frage, wie das Unendliche endlich werde, ist somit diese, daß es nicht ein Unendliches gibt, das vorerst unendlich ist, und das nachher erst endlich zu werden, zur Endlichkeit herauszugehen nöthig habe, sondern es ist für sich selbst schon eben so sehr endlich als unendlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"36.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0012","text":"Indem die Frage annimmt, daß das Unendliche einer Seits für sich, und daß das Endliche, das aus ihm heraus in die Trennung gegangen, oder wo es hergekommen seyn möchte, abgesondert von ihm, wahrhaft real sey,—so wäre vielmehr zu sagen, diese Trennung sey unbegreiflich. Weder solches Endliches, noch solches Unendliches hat Wahrheit; das Unwahre aber ist unbegreiflich. Man muß aber ebenso sagen, sie seyen begreiflich; die Betrachtung derselben, auch wie sie in der Vorstellung sind, daß in dem einen die Bestimmung des anderen liegt, die einfache Einsicht in diese ihre Untrennbarkeit haben, heißt sie begreifen; diese Untrennbarkeit ist ihr Begriff.—In der Selbstständigkeit jenes Unendlichen und Endlichen dagegen stellt jene Frage einen unwahren Inhalt auf, und enthält in sich schon eine unwahre Beziehung desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"36.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0013","text":"Darum ist nicht auf sie zu antworten, sondern vielmehr sind die falschen Voraussetzungen, die sie enthält, d. i. die Frage selbst zu negiren. Durch die Frage nach der Wahrheit jenes Unendlichen und Endlichen wird der Standpunkt verändert, und diese Veränderung wird die Verlegenheit, welche die erste Frage hervorbringen sollte, auf sie zurückbringen; jene unsre Frage ist der Reflexion, aus der die erste Frage stammt, neu, da solches Reflektiren nicht das spekulative Interesse enthält, welches, für sich und ehe es Bestimmungen bezieht, darauf geht, zu erkennen, ob dieselben, wie sie vorausgesetzt werden, etwas Wahres seyen.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"36.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0014","text":"Insofern aber die Unwahrheit jenes abstrakten Unendlichen, und des eben so auf seiner Seite stehen bleiben sollenden Endlichen erkannt ist, so ist über das Herausgehen des Endlichen aus dem Unendlichen zu sagen, das Unendliche gehe zur Endlichkeit heraus, darum weil es keine Wahrheit, kein Bestehen an ihm, wie es als abstrakte Einheit gefaßt ist, hat; so umgekehrt geht das Endliche aus demselben Grunde seiner Nichtigkeit in das Unendliche hinein. oder vielmehr ist zu sagen, daß das Unendliche ewig zur Endlichkeit herausgegangen, daß es schlechthin nicht ist, so wenig als das reine Seyn, allein für sich, ohne sein Anderes an ihm selbst zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"36.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0015","text":"Jene Frage, wie das Unendliche zum Endlichen herausgehe, kann noch die weitere Voraussetzung enthalten, daß das Unendliche an sich das Endliche in sich schliesse, somit an sich die Einheit seiner selbst und seines Anderen sey, so daß die Schwierigkeit sich wesentlich auf das Trennen bezieht, als welches der vorausgesetzten Einheit beider entgegensteht. In dieser Voraussetzung hat der Gegensatz, an welchem festgehalten s wird, nur eine andere Gestalt; die Einheit und das Unterscheiden werden von einander getrennt und isolirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"36.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0016","text":"Wenn aber jene nicht als die abstrakte unbestimmte Einheit, sondern schon wie in jener Voraussetzung als die bestimmte Einheit des Endlichen und Unendlichen genommen wird, so ist die Unterscheidung beider bereits darin auch vorhanden,—eine Unterscheidung, die so zugleich nicht ein Loslassen derselben zu getrennter Selbstständigkeit ist, sondern sie als ideelle in der Einheit läßt. Diese Einheit des Unendlichen und Endlichen und deren Unterscheidung sind dasselbe Untrennbare als die Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"36.16"}],"sha256":"5850730ede7614a495fb9819c516f40e15462803ccbb22e933981420e35554f0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102418736433Z_62592b09","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"5850730ede7614a495fb9819c516f40e15462803ccbb22e933981420e35554f0","sha256":"9687bb9a71f119dccf315ec7de553023616e5a13579222c763eb7de0db2d464b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:24:18.736468+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0001","text":"The infinite,—according to the ordinary sense of the spurious infinite,—and the progress into infinity, like the ought, are the expression of a contradiction which gives itself out as the resolution and as the ultimate. This infinite is a first elevation of sensuous representation above the finite into thought, but it has only the content of nothing, of that which is expressly posited as non-being,—a flight beyond what is limited, which does not gather itself into itself and does not know how to bring the negative back to the positive. This unfinished reflection has completely before it the two determinations of the truly infinite: the opposition of the finite and infinite, and the unity of the finite and infinite, but does not bring these two thoughts together; the one inseparably brings forth the other, but it lets them merely alternate.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"36.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0002","text":"The presentation of this alternation, the infinite progress, occurs everywhere where one persists in the contradiction of the unity of two determinations and their opposition. The finite is the sublation of itself; it includes its negation, infinity, within itself;—the unity of both,—one goes out beyond the finite to the infinite as its beyond, —the separation of both; but beyond the infinite there is another finite,—the going-out-beyond, the infinite, contains finitude, —the unity of both; but this finite is also a negative of the infinite;—the separation of both, etc.—Thus, in the relation of causality, cause and effect are inseparable; a cause that were supposed to have no effect is not a cause, just as an effect that had no cause would no longer be an effect.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"36.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0003","text":"This relation therefore gives the infinite progress of causes and effects; something is determined as cause, but as a finite [cause] (—and it is finite properly precisely because of its separation from the effect) it itself has a cause, i.e. it is also effect; thus the same thing that was determined as cause is also determined as effect;—unity of cause and effect;—that which is now determined as effect has anew a cause, i.e. the cause is to be separated from its effect and posited as a different something;—but this new cause is itself only an effect—unity of cause and effect;—it has an other as its cause;—separation of the two determinations, etc., into infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"36.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0004","text":"The progress can thus be given the more peculiar form that the assertion is made: the finite and infinite are one unity; this false assertion must be corrected by the opposite one: they are absolutely different and opposed to one another; this in turn is to be corrected to the effect that they are inseparable, that in the one determination the other lies, by the assertion of their unity, and so on into infinity.—It is an easy demand that is made, in order to gain insight into the nature of the infinite: to have the consciousness that the infinite progress, the developed infinite of the understanding, has the character of being the alternation of the two determinations, the unity and the separation of both moments, and then to have the further consciousness that this unity and this separation are themselves inseparable.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"36.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0005","text":"The resolution of this contradiction is not the acknowledgment of the equal correctness and equal incorrectness of both assertions;—this is only another shape of the enduring contradiction,—but the ideality of both, in which, in their difference, as reciprocal negations, they are only moments; that monotonous alternation is in fact the negation both of unity and of their separation. In it there is likewise in fact what was shown above, that the finite falls beyond itself into the infinite, but likewise finds itself reproduced beyond the latter, and thereby only comes together with itself therein, as does the infinite equally; so that the same negation of negation results in affirmation, which result thereby proves itself to be their truth and originality.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"36.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0006","text":"In this being, accordingly, as the ideality of the differentiated [terms], the contradiction has not abstractly vanished, but has been resolved and reconciled, and the thoughts are not merely complete, but they have also been brought together. The nature of speculative thinking is shown here, in an elaborated example, in its determinate manner; it consists solely in apprehending the opposed moments in their unity. Since each, and indeed in fact, shows itself to have its opposite in itself, and in this to come together with itself, affirmative truth is this unity moving within itself, the comprehending of both thoughts, their infinity,—the relation to itself, not the immediate but the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"36.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0007","text":"The essence of philosophy has often been posed, by those who are already more familiar with thinking, as the task of answering how the infinite comes out of itself and to finitude?—This, it is thought, cannot be made comprehensible. The infinite, at whose concept we have arrived, will determine itself further in the course of this presentation, and in all the multiplicity of its forms will show what is required: how it, if one wishes to express oneself thus, comes to finitude. Here we consider this question only in its immediacy, and with regard to the sense which the infinite considered above is wont to have.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"36.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0008","text":"Whether there is to be a philosophy at all is supposed to depend upon the answering of this question; and while one professes still to wish to leave it dependent on this, one believes at the same time to possess in the question itself a kind of vexing question, an insuperable talisman, through which one is firm and secure against the answer and thereby against philosophy and against arriving at it. Even with other objects, it presupposes cultivation to understand questions; but still more so with philosophical objects, in order to receive an answer other than that the question is worthless.—In such questions, fairness is customarily invoked: that it is not the words that matter, but that, in one or another mode of expression, it is intelligible what matters?","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"36.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0009","text":"Expressions of sensuous representation, such as going out and the like, which are used in the question, arouse the suspicion that it springs from the ground of ordinary representation and that, for its answer, it also expects representations current in common life and the shape of a sensuous simile.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"36.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0010","text":"If, instead of the infinite, being in general is taken, then the determining of being, a negation or finitude in it, appears more easily comprehensible. Being is indeed itself the indeterminate, but it is not immediately expressed in it that it is the opposite of the determinate. The infinite, on the other hand, contains this expressly; it is the non-finite. The unity of the finite and infinite thus appears immediately excluded; unfinished reflection is therefore most obstinate against this unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"36.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0011","text":"But it has been shown, and it is evident, without entering further into the determination of the finite and infinite, immediately, that the infinite in the sense (in which it is taken by that reflection,—namely as standing opposed to the finite,—precisely because it stands opposed to it, has its other in it, and is therefore already limited and itself finite, the spurious infinite. The answer to the question how the infinite becomes finite is thus this: there is no infinite that is at first infinite and that only afterwards needs to become finite, to go out into finitude, but it is, for itself, already just as much finite as infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"36.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0012","text":"Since the question assumes that the infinite is, on one side, for itself, and that the finite, which has gone out from it into separation, or wherever it may have come from, is truly real apart from it,—one ought rather to say that this separation is incomprehensible. Neither such a finite nor such an infinite has truth; but the untrue is incomprehensible. Yet one must equally say that they are comprehensible; considering them, also as they are in representation, that in the one the determination of the other lies, having the simple insight into this their inseparability, is called comprehending them; this inseparability is their concept.—In contrast, in the self-subsistence of that infinite and finite, that question sets up an untrue content and already contains within itself an untrue relation of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"36.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0013","text":"For this reason it is not to be answered; rather, the false presuppositions that it contains, i.e. the question itself, are to be negated. By the question concerning the truth of that infinite and finite, the standpoint is altered, and this alteration will bring back upon it the embarrassment which the first question was supposed to produce; that question of ours is new to the reflection from which the first question originates, since such reflecting does not contain the speculative interest which, for itself and before it relates determinations, aims at recognizing whether these, as they are presupposed, are something true.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"36.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0014","text":"But insofar as the untruth of that abstract infinite, and of the finite which is likewise supposed to remain on its own side, has been recognized, concerning the going-out of the finite from the infinite it is to be said that the infinite goes out to finitude because it has no truth, no subsistence in it, as it is apprehended as abstract unity; conversely, for the same reason of its nullity, the finite goes into the infinite. Or rather, it is to be said that the infinite has eternally gone out to finitude, that it absolutely is not, any more than pure being is, by itself alone, without having its other in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"36.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0015","text":"That question, how the infinite goes out to the finite, can still contain the further presupposition that the infinite in itself includes the finite within itself, and thus is in itself the unity of itself and its other, so that the difficulty essentially concerns separation, as that which stands opposed to the presupposed unity of both. In this presupposition, the opposition to which one holds fast has only another shape; unity and distinguishing are separated from one another and isolated.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"36.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0016","text":"But if that [unity] is taken not as abstract indeterminate unity, but already, as in that presupposition, as the determinate unity of finite and infinite, then the distinction of the two is already also present within it,—a distinction which is at the same time not a releasing of them into separated self-subsistence, but leaves them as ideal in unity. This unity of infinite and finite and their distinction are the same inseparable [thing] as finitude and infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"36.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_4:P0016"]}],"source_digest":"7faa52831d12070667ea635899fc51ccd41efde7e6d8dd323da4e0c63cf03fa1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5","title":"Remark 2.","order":37,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_5","text":"Der Satz, daß das Endliche ideell ist, macht den Idealismus aus. Der Idealismus der Philosophie besteht in nichts anderem, als darin, das Endliche nicht als ein wahrhaft Seyendes anzuerkennen. Jede Philosophie ist wesentlich Idealismus, oder hat denselben wenigstens zu ihrem Princip, und die Frage ist dann nur, inwiefern dasselbe wirklich durchgeführt ist. Die Philosophie ist es so sehr als die Religion; denn die Religion anerkennt die Endlichkeit ebenso wenig als ein wahrhaftes Seyn, als ein Letztes, Absolutes, oder als ein Nicht-Gesetztes, Unerschaffenes, Ewiges. Der Gegensatz von idealistischer und realistischer Philosophie ist daher ohne Bedeutung. Eine Philosophie, welche dem endlichen Daseyn als solchem wahrhaftes, letztes, absolutes Seyn zuschriebe, verdiente den Namen Philosophie nicht; Principien älterer oder neuerer Philosophien, das Wasser, oder die Materie oder die Atome sind Gedanken, Allgemeine, Ideelle, nicht Dinge, wie sie sich unmittelbar vorfinden, d. h. in sinnlicher Einzelnheit, selbst jenes thaletische Wasser nicht; denn, obgleich auch das empirische Wasser, ist es außerdem zugleich das Ansich oder Wesen aller anderen Dinge; und diese sind nicht selbstständige, in sich gegründete, sondern aus einem Anderen, dem Wasser, gesetzte, d. i. ideelle. Indem vorhin das Princip, das Allgemeine, das Ideelle genannt worden, wie noch mehr der Begriff, die Idee, der Geist, Ideelles zu nennen ist, und dann wiederum die einzelnen sinnlichen Dinge als ideell im Princip, im Begriffe, noch mehr im Geiste, als aufgehoben sind, so ist dabei auf dieselbe Doppelseite vorläufig aufmerksam zu machen, die bei dem Unendlichen sich gezeigt hat, nämlich daß das eine Mal das Ideelle das Konkrete, Wahrhaftseyende ist, das andere Mal aber ebenso sehr seine Momente das Ideelle, in ihm Aufgehobene sind, in der That aber nur das Eine konkrete Ganze ist, von dem die Momente untrennbar sind.\n\nBei dem Ideellen wird vornehmlich die Form der Vorstellung gemeint, und das was in meiner Vorstellung überhaupt, oder im Begriffe, in der Idee, in der Einbildung u.s.f. ist, ideell genannt, so daß Ideelles überhaupt auch für Einbildungen gilt,—Vorstellungen, die nicht nur vom Reellen unterschieden, sondern wesentlich nicht reell seyn sollen. In der That ist der Geist der eigentliche Idealiste überhaupt; in ihm, schon wie er empfindend, vorstellend, noch mehr, insofern er denkend und begreifend ist, ist der Inhalt nicht als sogenanntes reales Daseyn; in der Einfachheit des Ich ist solches äußerliches Seyn nur aufgehoben, es ist für mich, es ist ideell in mir. Dieser subjektive Idealismus, er sey als der bewußtlose Idealismus des Bewußtseyns überhaupt oder bewußt als Princip ausgesprochen und aufgestellt, geht nur auf die Form der Vorstellung, nach der ein Inhalt der Meinige ist; diese Form wird im systematischen Idealismus der Subjektivität als die einzig wahrhafte, die ausschließende gegen die Form der Objektivität oder Realität, des äußerlichen Daseyns jenes Inhalts behauptet. Solcher Idealismus ist formell, indem er den Inhalt des Vorstellens oder Denkens nicht beachtet, welcher im Vorstellen oder Denken dabei ganz in seiner Endlichkeit bleiben kann. Es ist mit solchem Idealismus nichts verloren, ebenso wohl weil die Realität solchen endlichen Inhalts, das mit Endlichkeit erfüllte Daseyn, erhalten ist, als, insofern davon abstrahirt wird, an sich an solchem Inhalt nichts gelegen seyn soll; und es ist nichts mit ihm gewonnen, eben weil nichts verloren ist, weil Ich die Vorstellung, der Geist mit demselben Inhalt der Endlichkeit erfüllt bleibt. Der Gegensatz der Form von Subjektivität und Objektivität ist allerdings eine der Endlichkeiten; aber der Inhalt, wie er in die Empfindung, Anschauung oder auch in das abstraktere Element der Vorstellung, des Denkens, aufgenommen wird, enthält die Endlichkeiten in Fülle, welche mit dem Ausschließen jener nur einen Weise der Endlichkeit, der Form von Subjektivem und objektivem, noch gar nicht weggebracht, noch weniger von selbst weggefallen sind.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0001","text":"Der Satz, daß das Endliche ideell ist, macht den Idealismus aus. Der Idealismus der Philosophie besteht in nichts anderem, als darin, das Endliche nicht als ein wahrhaft Seyendes anzuerkennen. Jede Philosophie ist wesentlich Idealismus, oder hat denselben wenigstens zu ihrem Princip, und die Frage ist dann nur, inwiefern dasselbe wirklich durchgeführt ist. Die Philosophie ist es so sehr als die Religion; denn die Religion anerkennt die Endlichkeit ebenso wenig als ein wahrhaftes Seyn, als ein Letztes, Absolutes, oder als ein Nicht-Gesetztes, Unerschaffenes, Ewiges. Der Gegensatz von idealistischer und realistischer Philosophie ist daher ohne Bedeutung.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"37.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0002","text":"Eine Philosophie, welche dem endlichen Daseyn als solchem wahrhaftes, letztes, absolutes Seyn zuschriebe, verdiente den Namen Philosophie nicht; Principien älterer oder neuerer Philosophien, das Wasser, oder die Materie oder die Atome sind Gedanken, Allgemeine, Ideelle, nicht Dinge, wie sie sich unmittelbar vorfinden, d. h. in sinnlicher Einzelnheit, selbst jenes thaletische Wasser nicht; denn, obgleich auch das empirische Wasser, ist es außerdem zugleich das Ansich oder Wesen aller anderen Dinge; und diese sind nicht selbstständige, in sich gegründete, sondern aus einem Anderen, dem Wasser, gesetzte, d. i. ideelle.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"37.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0003","text":"Indem vorhin das Princip, das Allgemeine, das Ideelle genannt worden, wie noch mehr der Begriff, die Idee, der Geist, Ideelles zu nennen ist, und dann wiederum die einzelnen sinnlichen Dinge als ideell im Princip, im Begriffe, noch mehr im Geiste, als aufgehoben sind, so ist dabei auf dieselbe Doppelseite vorläufig aufmerksam zu machen, die bei dem Unendlichen sich gezeigt hat, nämlich daß das eine Mal das Ideelle das Konkrete, Wahrhaftseyende ist, das andere Mal aber ebenso sehr seine Momente das Ideelle, in ihm Aufgehobene sind, in der That aber nur das Eine konkrete Ganze ist, von dem die Momente untrennbar sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"37.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0004","text":"Bei dem Ideellen wird vornehmlich die Form der Vorstellung gemeint, und das was in meiner Vorstellung überhaupt, oder im Begriffe, in der Idee, in der Einbildung u.s.f. ist, ideell genannt, so daß Ideelles überhaupt auch für Einbildungen gilt,—Vorstellungen, die nicht nur vom Reellen unterschieden, sondern wesentlich nicht reell seyn sollen. In der That ist der Geist der eigentliche Idealiste überhaupt; in ihm, schon wie er empfindend, vorstellend, noch mehr, insofern er denkend und begreifend ist, ist der Inhalt nicht als sogenanntes reales Daseyn; in der Einfachheit des Ich ist solches äußerliches Seyn nur aufgehoben, es ist für mich, es ist ideell in mir.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"37.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0005","text":"Dieser subjektive Idealismus, er sey als der bewußtlose Idealismus des Bewußtseyns überhaupt oder bewußt als Princip ausgesprochen und aufgestellt, geht nur auf die Form der Vorstellung, nach der ein Inhalt der Meinige ist; diese Form wird im systematischen Idealismus der Subjektivität als die einzig wahrhafte, die ausschließende gegen die Form der Objektivität oder Realität, des äußerlichen Daseyns jenes Inhalts behauptet. Solcher Idealismus ist formell, indem er den Inhalt des Vorstellens oder Denkens nicht beachtet, welcher im Vorstellen oder Denken dabei ganz in seiner Endlichkeit bleiben kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"37.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0006","text":"Es ist mit solchem Idealismus nichts verloren, ebenso wohl weil die Realität solchen endlichen Inhalts, das mit Endlichkeit erfüllte Daseyn, erhalten ist, als, insofern davon abstrahirt wird, an sich an solchem Inhalt nichts gelegen seyn soll; und es ist nichts mit ihm gewonnen, eben weil nichts verloren ist, weil Ich die Vorstellung, der Geist mit demselben Inhalt der Endlichkeit erfüllt bleibt. Der Gegensatz der Form von Subjektivität und Objektivität ist allerdings eine der Endlichkeiten; aber der Inhalt, wie er in die Empfindung, Anschauung oder auch in das abstraktere Element der Vorstellung, des Denkens, aufgenommen wird, enthält die Endlichkeiten in Fülle, welche mit dem Ausschließen jener nur einen Weise der Endlichkeit, der Form von Subjektivem und objektivem, noch gar nicht weggebracht, noch weniger von selbst weggefallen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"37.6"}],"sha256":"97e48d40fd29fab7c6c8b0403870fa766a07d75204979d6353bf1b3960cc971d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102427742593Z_41b027a6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"97e48d40fd29fab7c6c8b0403870fa766a07d75204979d6353bf1b3960cc971d","sha256":"5969c7819f2d793f26924750ae438113d081cba469e27a07562418ba4f1d73ba","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:24:27.742609+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0001","text":"The proposition that the finite is ideal constitutes idealism. The idealism of philosophy consists in nothing other than not recognizing the finite as a truly being. Every philosophy is essentially idealism, or at least has the same as its principle, and the question then is only to what extent it has actually been carried through. Philosophy is so no less than religion; for religion recognizes finitude just as little as a true being, as an ultimate, absolute, or as an unposited, uncreated, eternal [being]. The opposition between idealistic and realistic philosophy is therefore without significance.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"37.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0002","text":"A philosophy which ascribed true, ultimate, absolute being to finite existence as such would not deserve the name of philosophy; the principles of older or more recent philosophies—water, or matter, or atoms—are thoughts, universals, idealities, not things as they are immediately found, i.e. in sensuous singularity, not even that Thalesian water; for, although it is also empirical water, it is besides at the same time the in-itself or essence of all other things; and these are not self-subsistent, grounded in themselves, but posited from an other, water, i.e. ideal.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"37.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0003","text":"Since previously the principle, the universal, was called the ideal, as the concept, the idea, spirit are still more to be called ideal, and then again the individual sensuous things, as ideal in the principle, in the concept, still more in spirit, are sublated, attention must provisionally be drawn here to the same twofold aspect that showed itself in the case of the infinite, namely, that on the one occasion the ideal is the concrete, truly being, while on the other its moments are equally the ideal, sublated in it; but in fact only the one concrete whole is that from which the moments are inseparable.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"37.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0004","text":"By the ideal is meant pre-eminently the form of representation, and that which is in my representation in general, or in the concept, in the idea, in imagination, etc., is called ideal, so that ideality in general also applies to imaginings—representations which are not only distinguished from the real, but are essentially supposed not to be real. In fact spirit is the proper idealist in general; in it, already insofar as it is sensing, representing, still more insofar as it is thinking and comprehending, the content is not as so-called real existence; in the simplicity of the I such external being is only sublated; it is for me, it is ideal in me.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"37.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0005","text":"This subjective idealism, whether it be the unconscious idealism of consciousness in general or be consciously pronounced and posited as principle, concerns only the form of representation, according to which a content is mine; in the systematic idealism of subjectivity this form is asserted as the sole true, exclusive one, in opposition to the form of objectivity or reality, of the external existence of that content. Such idealism is formal, since it does not attend to the content of representing or thinking, which in representing or thinking may thereby remain entirely within its finitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"37.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0006","text":"With such idealism nothing is lost, just as surely because the reality of such finite content, existence filled with finitude, is preserved, as because, insofar as abstraction is made from it, nothing is supposed to depend in itself upon such content; and nothing is gained by it, precisely because nothing is lost, because I, representation, spirit, remains filled with the same content of finitude. The opposition of the form of subjectivity and objectivity is indeed one of the finitudes; but the content, as it is taken up into sensation, intuition, or even into the more abstract element of representation, of thinking, contains finitudes in abundance, which have by no means been removed by the exclusion of only that one mode of finitude, the form of subjective and objective, still less have fallen away of themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"37.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_5:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"b5daa38b5fbf8df95c550bc7feeafe6fbf692b2c22fd35b6134e328b91889ec1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA","title":"A. Being-for-Self as Such.","order":38,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DFRA","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das Fürsichseyn.\n\nIm Fürsichseyn ist das qualitative Seyn vollendet; es ist das unendliche Seyn. Das Seyn des Anfangs ist bestimmungslos. Das Daseyn ist das aufgehobene, aber nur unmittelbar aufgehobene Seyn; es enthält so zunächst nur die erste, selbst unmittelbare Negation; das Seyn ist zwar gleichfalls erhalten, und beide im Daseyn in einfacher Einheit vereint, aber eben darum an sich einander noch ungleich, und ihre Einheit noch nicht gesetzt. Das Daseyn ist darum die Sphäre der Differenz, des Dualismus, das Feld der Endlichkeit. Die Bestimmtheit ist Bestimmtheit als solche; ein relatives, nicht absolutes Bestimmtseyn. Im Fürsichseyn ist der Unterschied zwischen dem Seyn und der Bestimmtheit oder Negation gesetzt und ausgeglichen; Qualität, Andersseyn, Grenze, wie Realität, Ansichseyn, Sollen u.s.f.—sind die unvollkommenen Einbildungen der Negation in das Seyn, als in welchen die Differenz beider noch zu Grunde liegt. Indem aber in der Endlichkeit die Negation in die Unendlichkeit, in die gesetzte Negation der Negation, übergegangen, ist sie einfache Beziehung auf sich, also an ihr selbst die Ausgleichung mit dem Seyn;—absolutes Bestimmtseyn.\n\nDas Fürsichseyn ist erstens unmittelbar Fürsichseyendes, Eins.\n\nZweitens geht das Eins in die Vielheit der Eins über,—Repulsion; welches Andersseyn des Eins sich in der Idealität desselben aufhebt, Attraktion.\n\nDrittens die Wechselbestimmung der Repulsion und Attraktion, in welcher sie in das Gleichgewicht zusammensinken, und die Qualität, die sich im Fürsichseyn auf ihre Spitze trieb, in Quantität übergeht.\n\n## A. Das Fürsichseyn als solches.\n\nDer allgemeine Begriff des Fürsichseyns hat sich ergeben. Es käme nur darauf an, nachzuweisen, daß jenem Begriffe die Vorstellung entspricht, die wir mit dem Ausdrucke: Fürsichseyn verbinden, um berechtigt zu seyn, denselben für jenen Begriff zu gebrauchen. Und so scheint es wohl; wir sagen, daß etwas für sich ist, insofern als es das Andersseyn, seine Beziehung und Gemeinschaft mit Anderem aufhebt, sie zurück-gestoßen, davon abstrahirt hat. Das Andere ist in ihm nur als ein Aufgehobenes, als sein Moment; das Fürsichseyn besteht darin, über die Schranke, über sein Andersseyn so hinausgegangen zu seyn, daß es als diese Negation die unendliche Rückkehr in sich ist.—Das Bewußtseyn enthält schon als solches an sich die Bestimmung des Fürsichseyns, indem es einen Gegenstand, den es empfindet, anschaut u.s.f. sich vorstellt, d. i. dessen Inhalt in ihm hat, der auf die Weise als Ideelles ist; es ist in seinem Anschauen selbst, überhaupt in seiner Verwicklung mit dem Negativen seiner, mit dem Anderen, bei sich selbst. Das Fürsichseyn ist das polemische, negative Verhalten, gegen das begrenzende Andere, und durch diese Negation desselben In-sich-reflektirtseyn, ob schon neben dieser Rückkehr des Bewußtseyns in sich, und der Idealität des Gegenstandes, auch noch die Realität desselben erhalten ist, indem er zugleich als ein äußeres Daseyn gewußt wird. Das Bewußtseyn ist so erscheinend, oder der Dualismus, einer Seits von einem ihm andern, äußerlichen Gegenstande zu wissen, und andererseits, für-sich zu seyn, denselben in ihm ideell zu haben, nicht nur bei solchem Andern, sondern darin auch bei sich selbst zu seyn. Das Selbstbewußtseyn dagegen ist das Fürsichseyn als vollbracht und gesetzt; jene Seite der Beziehung auf ein Anderes, einen äußern Gegenstand ist entfernt. Das Selbstbewußtseyn ist so das nächste Beispiel der Präsenz der Unendlichkeit;—einer freilich immer abstrakten Unendlichkeit, die jedoch zugleich von ganz anders konkreter Bestimmung ist, als das Fürsichseyn überhaupt, dessen Unendlichkeit noch ganz nur qualitative Bestimmtheit hat.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0001","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das Fürsichseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"38.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0002","text":"Im Fürsichseyn ist das qualitative Seyn vollendet; es ist das unendliche Seyn. Das Seyn des Anfangs ist bestimmungslos. Das Daseyn ist das aufgehobene, aber nur unmittelbar aufgehobene Seyn; es enthält so zunächst nur die erste, selbst unmittelbare Negation; das Seyn ist zwar gleichfalls erhalten, und beide im Daseyn in einfacher Einheit vereint, aber eben darum an sich einander noch ungleich, und ihre Einheit noch nicht gesetzt. Das Daseyn ist darum die Sphäre der Differenz, des Dualismus, das Feld der Endlichkeit. Die Bestimmtheit ist Bestimmtheit als solche; ein relatives, nicht absolutes Bestimmtseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"38.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0003","text":"Im Fürsichseyn ist der Unterschied zwischen dem Seyn und der Bestimmtheit oder Negation gesetzt und ausgeglichen; Qualität, Andersseyn, Grenze, wie Realität, Ansichseyn, Sollen u.s.f.—sind die unvollkommenen Einbildungen der Negation in das Seyn, als in welchen die Differenz beider noch zu Grunde liegt. Indem aber in der Endlichkeit die Negation in die Unendlichkeit, in die gesetzte Negation der Negation, übergegangen, ist sie einfache Beziehung auf sich, also an ihr selbst die Ausgleichung mit dem Seyn;—absolutes Bestimmtseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"38.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0004","text":"Das Fürsichseyn ist erstens unmittelbar Fürsichseyendes, Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"38.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0005","text":"Zweitens geht das Eins in die Vielheit der Eins über,—Repulsion; welches Andersseyn des Eins sich in der Idealität desselben aufhebt, Attraktion.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"38.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0006","text":"Drittens die Wechselbestimmung der Repulsion und Attraktion, in welcher sie in das Gleichgewicht zusammensinken, und die Qualität, die sich im Fürsichseyn auf ihre Spitze trieb, in Quantität übergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"38.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0007","text":"## A. Das Fürsichseyn als solches.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"38.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0008","text":"Der allgemeine Begriff des Fürsichseyns hat sich ergeben. Es käme nur darauf an, nachzuweisen, daß jenem Begriffe die Vorstellung entspricht, die wir mit dem Ausdrucke: Fürsichseyn verbinden, um berechtigt zu seyn, denselben für jenen Begriff zu gebrauchen. Und so scheint es wohl; wir sagen, daß etwas für sich ist, insofern als es das Andersseyn, seine Beziehung und Gemeinschaft mit Anderem aufhebt, sie zurück-gestoßen, davon abstrahirt hat. Das Andere ist in ihm nur als ein Aufgehobenes, als sein Moment; das Fürsichseyn besteht darin, über die Schranke, über sein Andersseyn so hinausgegangen zu seyn, daß es als diese Negation die unendliche Rückkehr in sich ist.—Das Bewußtseyn enthält schon als solches an sich die Bestimmung des Fürsichseyns, indem es einen Gegenstand, den es empfindet, anschaut u.s.f. sich vorstellt, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"38.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0009","text":"dessen Inhalt in ihm hat, der auf die Weise als Ideelles ist; es ist in seinem Anschauen selbst, überhaupt in seiner Verwicklung mit dem Negativen seiner, mit dem Anderen, bei sich selbst. Das Fürsichseyn ist das polemische, negative Verhalten, gegen das begrenzende Andere, und durch diese Negation desselben In-sich-reflektirtseyn, ob schon neben dieser Rückkehr des Bewußtseyns in sich, und der Idealität des Gegenstandes, auch noch die Realität desselben erhalten ist, indem er zugleich als ein äußeres Daseyn gewußt wird. Das Bewußtseyn ist so erscheinend, oder der Dualismus, einer Seits von einem ihm andern, äußerlichen Gegenstande zu wissen, und andererseits, für-sich zu seyn, denselben in ihm ideell zu haben, nicht nur bei solchem Andern, sondern darin auch bei sich selbst zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"38.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0010","text":"Das Selbstbewußtseyn dagegen ist das Fürsichseyn als vollbracht und gesetzt; jene Seite der Beziehung auf ein Anderes, einen äußern Gegenstand ist entfernt. Das Selbstbewußtseyn ist so das nächste Beispiel der Präsenz der Unendlichkeit;—einer freilich immer abstrakten Unendlichkeit, die jedoch zugleich von ganz anders konkreter Bestimmung ist, als das Fürsichseyn überhaupt, dessen Unendlichkeit noch ganz nur qualitative Bestimmtheit hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"38.10"}],"sha256":"5b69d13cc5fc85aa21c9af9b28544026473eee9af521ab9ad2ac037d55c0d326","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102438279136Z_137e5713","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Being-for-Self as Such.","source_sha256":"5b69d13cc5fc85aa21c9af9b28544026473eee9af521ab9ad2ac037d55c0d326","sha256":"e0ad19b6715c0bea5bde73e401642698f3ad6da1d9f8149e4febf384e297430f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:24:38.279208+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0001","text":"## Third Chapter. Being-for-self.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"38.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0002","text":"In being-for-self qualitative being is completed; it is infinite being. The being of the beginning is indeterminate. Determinate being is sublated being, but only immediately sublated being; it therefore contains at first only the first, itself immediate negation; being is indeed likewise preserved, and both are united in determinate being in simple unity, but for that very reason are still unequal to one another in themselves, and their unity is not yet posited. Determinate being is therefore the sphere of difference, of dualism, the field of finitude. Determinateness is determinateness as such; a relative, not absolute determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"38.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0003","text":"In being-for-self the difference between being and determinateness or negation is posited and equalized; quality, other-being, limit, as also reality, being-in-itself, ought, etc.—are the imperfect embodiments of negation in being, in which the difference of the two still underlies. But since in finitude negation has passed over into infinity, into the posited negation of negation, it is a simple relation to itself, thus in itself the equalization with being;—absolute determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"38.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0004","text":"Being-for-self is, first, immediate being-for-self, the One.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"38.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0005","text":"Secondly, the One passes over into the many Ones,—repulsion; which other-being of the One sublates itself in its ideality, attraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"38.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0006","text":"Thirdly, the reciprocal determination of repulsion and attraction, in which they sink together into equilibrium, and quality, which drove itself to its peak in being-for-self, passes over into quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"38.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0007","text":"## A. Being-for-self as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"38.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0008","text":"The universal concept of being-for-self has emerged. It would only be necessary to demonstrate that the representation which we connect with the expression “being-for-self” corresponds to that concept, in order to be entitled to employ it for that concept. And this indeed seems to be the case; we say that something is for itself insofar as it sublates other-being, its relation and community with something other, has repelled it, has abstracted from it. The other is in it only as a sublated [element], as its moment; being-for-self consists in having gone so far beyond the restriction, beyond its other-being, that, as this negation, it is the infinite return into itself.—Consciousness already contains, as such, in itself the determination of being-for-self, in that it represents to itself an object which it senses, intuits, etc., i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"38.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0009","text":"has its content in it, which is in this manner ideal; in its intuition itself, in general in its involvement with the negative of itself, with the other, it is with itself. Being-for-self is the polemical, negative comportment toward the limiting other, and through this negation of the latter, being-reflected-into-self, although alongside this return of consciousness into itself, and the ideality of the object, its reality is also still preserved, in that it is at the same time known as an external determinate being. Consciousness is thus appearance, or dualism: on the one hand, knowing an object other than it, external to it, and on the other hand, being for itself, having the same ideally within it, not merely being with such an other, but therein also being with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"38.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0010","text":"Self-consciousness, by contrast, is being-for-self as accomplished and posited; that side of the relation to an other, an external object, is removed. Self-consciousness is thus the nearest example of the presence of infinity;—admittedly an infinity still always abstract, which, however, is at the same time of a quite differently concrete determination than being-for-self in general, whose infinity still has altogether only qualitative determinateness.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"38.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFRA:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"e4756483a6eabb9e548d048e3823b184f08ade32083da641453ba8a7633f2a3a","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Fürsichseyn als solches."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Fürsichseyn als solches.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUFR","title":"a. Determinate Being and Being-for-Self.","order":39,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DUFR","text":"Das Fürsichseyn ist, wie schon erinnert ist, die in das einfache Seyn zusammengesunkene Unendlichkeit; es ist Daseyn, insofern die negative Natur der Unendlichkeit, welche Negation der Negation ist, in der nunmehr gesetzten Form der Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, nur als Negation überhaupt, als einfache qualitative Bestimmtheit ist. Das Seyn in solcher Bestimmtheit, in der es Daseyn ist, ist aber sogleich vom Fürsichseyn selbst auch unterschieden, welches nur Fürsichseyn, insofern seine Bestimmtheit jene unendliche ist; jedoch ist das Daseyn zugleich Moment des Fürsichseyns selbst; denn dieses enthält allerdings auch das mit der Negation behaftete Seyn. So ist die Bestimmtheit, welche am Daseyn als solchem ein Anderes und Seyn-für-Anderes ist, in die unendliche Einheit des Fürsichseyns zurückgebogen, und das Moment des Daseyns ist im Fürsichseyn als Seyn-für-Eines vorhanden.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUFR:P0001","text":"Das Fürsichseyn ist, wie schon erinnert ist, die in das einfache Seyn zusammengesunkene Unendlichkeit; es ist Daseyn, insofern die negative Natur der Unendlichkeit, welche Negation der Negation ist, in der nunmehr gesetzten Form der Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, nur als Negation überhaupt, als einfache qualitative Bestimmtheit ist. Das Seyn in solcher Bestimmtheit, in der es Daseyn ist, ist aber sogleich vom Fürsichseyn selbst auch unterschieden, welches nur Fürsichseyn, insofern seine Bestimmtheit jene unendliche ist; jedoch ist das Daseyn zugleich Moment des Fürsichseyns selbst; denn dieses enthält allerdings auch das mit der Negation behaftete Seyn. So ist die Bestimmtheit, welche am Daseyn als solchem ein Anderes und Seyn-für-Anderes ist, in die unendliche Einheit des Fürsichseyns zurückgebogen, und das Moment des Daseyns ist im Fürsichseyn als Seyn-für-Eines vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"39.1"}],"sha256":"4c4888326cf0abcd3967cb87ec4fb5aa2a12489776f3a82978eb9a6822b53d50","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102440852461Z_d293045a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Determinate Being and Being-for-Self.","source_sha256":"4c4888326cf0abcd3967cb87ec4fb5aa2a12489776f3a82978eb9a6822b53d50","sha256":"20319436629d38a3f462e05cd831cb40fde17435fdad84b8844ec471a4eda6bd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:24:40.852487+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DUFR:P0001","text":"Being-for-self is, as has already been recalled, infinity collapsed into simple being; it is determinate being, insofar as the negative nature of infinity, which is negation of negation, is, in the form now posited of the immediacy of being, only as negation in general, as simple qualitative determinacy. But being in such determinacy, in which it is determinate being, is at once also distinct from being-for-self itself, which is being-for-self only insofar as its determinacy is that infinite one; yet determinate being is at the same time a moment of being-for-self itself; for this indeed also contains being affected with negation. Thus the determinacy which, in determinate being as such, is an other and being-for-another, is bent back into the infinite unity of being-for-self, and the moment of determinate being is present in being-for-self as being-for-one.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"39.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DUFR:P0001"]}],"source_digest":"20e65a90532df2d8cdb93276ac9d52a501747ef8d2e5908aada962fc01c261d4","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Daseyn und Fürsichseyn."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Daseyn und Fürsichseyn.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR","title":"b. Being-for-One.","order":40,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BSFR","text":"Dieß Moment drückt aus, wie das Endliche in seiner Einheit mit dem Unendlichen oder als Ideelles ist. Das Fürsichseyn hat die Negation nicht an ihm als eine Bestimmtheit oder Grenze, und damit auch nicht als Beziehung auf ein von ihm anderes Daseyn. Indem nun dieß Moment als Seyn-für-Eines bezeichnet worden, ist noch nichts vorhanden, für welches es wäre,—das Eine nicht, dessen Moment es wäre. Es ist in der That dergleichen noch nicht im Fürsichseyn fixirt; das für welches Etwas (—und ist hier kein Etwas—) wäre, was die andere Seite überhaupt seyn sollte, ist gleicherweise Moment, selbst nur Seyn-für-Eines, noch nicht Eines.—Somit ist noch eine Ununterschiedenheit zweier Seiten, die im Seyn-für-eines vorschweben können, vorhanden; nur Ein Seyn-für-Anderes, und weil es nur Ein Seyn-für-Anderes ist, ist dieses auch nur Seyn-für-Eines; es ist nur die Eine ldealität dessen, für welches oder in welchem eine Bestimmung als Moment und dessen, was Moment in ihm seyn sollte. So machen Für-eines-seyn und das Fürsichseyn keine wahrhaften Bestimmtheiten gegeneinander aus. Insofern der Unterschied auf einen Augenblick angenommen und hier von einem Fürsichseyenden gesprochen wird, so ist es das Fürsichseyende, als Aufgehobenseyn des Andersseyns, selbst, welches sich auf sich als auf das aufgehobene Andere bezieht, also für-Eines ist; es bezieht sich in seinem Andern nur auf sich. Das Ideelle ist nothwendig für-Eines, aber es ist nicht für ein Anderes; das Eine, für welches es ist, ist nur es selbst.—Ich also, der Geist überhaupt, oder Gott, sind Ideelle, weil sie unendlich sind; aber sie sind ideell nicht, als für-sich-seyende, verschieden von dem, das für-Eines ist. Denn so wären sie nur unmittelbare, oder näher Daseyn und ein Seyn-für-Anderes, weil das, welches für sie wäre, nicht sie selbst, sondern ein Anderes wäre, wenn das Moment, für-eines zu seyn, nicht ihnen zukommen sollte. Gott ist daher für sich, insofern er selbst das ist, das für ihn ist.\n\nFür-sich-seyn und Für-Eines-seyn sind also nicht verschiedene Bedeutungen der Idealität, sondern sind wesentliche, untrennbare Momente derselben.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0001","text":"Dieß Moment drückt aus, wie das Endliche in seiner Einheit mit dem Unendlichen oder als Ideelles ist. Das Fürsichseyn hat die Negation nicht an ihm als eine Bestimmtheit oder Grenze, und damit auch nicht als Beziehung auf ein von ihm anderes Daseyn. Indem nun dieß Moment als Seyn-für-Eines bezeichnet worden, ist noch nichts vorhanden, für welches es wäre,—das Eine nicht, dessen Moment es wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"40.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0002","text":"Es ist in der That dergleichen noch nicht im Fürsichseyn fixirt; das für welches Etwas (—und ist hier kein Etwas—) wäre, was die andere Seite überhaupt seyn sollte, ist gleicherweise Moment, selbst nur Seyn-für-Eines, noch nicht Eines.—Somit ist noch eine Ununterschiedenheit zweier Seiten, die im Seyn-für-eines vorschweben können, vorhanden; nur Ein Seyn-für-Anderes, und weil es nur Ein Seyn-für-Anderes ist, ist dieses auch nur Seyn-für-Eines; es ist nur die Eine ldealität dessen, für welches oder in welchem eine Bestimmung als Moment und dessen, was Moment in ihm seyn sollte. So machen Für-eines-seyn und das Fürsichseyn keine wahrhaften Bestimmtheiten gegeneinander aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"40.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0003","text":"Insofern der Unterschied auf einen Augenblick angenommen und hier von einem Fürsichseyenden gesprochen wird, so ist es das Fürsichseyende, als Aufgehobenseyn des Andersseyns, selbst, welches sich auf sich als auf das aufgehobene Andere bezieht, also für-Eines ist; es bezieht sich in seinem Andern nur auf sich. Das Ideelle ist nothwendig für-Eines, aber es ist nicht für ein Anderes; das Eine, für welches es ist, ist nur es selbst.—Ich also, der Geist überhaupt, oder Gott, sind Ideelle, weil sie unendlich sind; aber sie sind ideell nicht, als für-sich-seyende, verschieden von dem, das für-Eines ist. Denn so wären sie nur unmittelbare, oder näher Daseyn und ein Seyn-für-Anderes, weil das, welches für sie wäre, nicht sie selbst, sondern ein Anderes wäre, wenn das Moment, für-eines zu seyn, nicht ihnen zukommen sollte. Gott ist daher für sich, insofern er selbst das ist, das für ihn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"40.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0004","text":"Für-sich-seyn und Für-Eines-seyn sind also nicht verschiedene Bedeutungen der Idealität, sondern sind wesentliche, untrennbare Momente derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"40.4"}],"sha256":"86f21dfb39aaaea049976c37369626aaa3bd6db62821a37da219fe5b7a7862d8","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102446951415Z_4dd4c2c1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Being-for-One.","source_sha256":"86f21dfb39aaaea049976c37369626aaa3bd6db62821a37da219fe5b7a7862d8","sha256":"056af137effc03feda71c25417549d584dc9c53be3693792c33036e16e8d999e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:24:46.951438+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0001","text":"This moment expresses how the finite is in its unity with the infinite, or as ideal. Being-for-self does not have negation within it as a determinacy or limit, and hence not as a relation to a being-there other than it. Now, inasmuch as this moment has been designated as being-for-one, there is as yet nothing present for which it would be,—not the one of which it would be a moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"40.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0002","text":"Indeed, nothing of the sort has as yet been fixed in being-for-self; that for which something (—and here there is no something—) would be, that which should in general constitute the other side, is likewise a moment, itself only being-for-one, not yet one.—Thus there is still present an undifferentiatedness of two sides, which can hover before us in being-for-one: only one being-for-other, and because it is only one being-for-other, this is also only being-for-one; it is only the one ideality of that for which, or in which, a determinacy is as moment, and of that which should be moment in it. Thus being-for-one and being-for-self do not constitute genuine determinacies over against one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"40.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0003","text":"Insofar as the difference is assumed for a moment and there is talk here of something being-for-self, it is the being-for-self, as the sublatedness of being-other, itself, which relates itself to itself as to the sublated other, and thus is for-one; in its other it relates only to itself. The ideal is necessarily for-one, but it is not for another; the one for which it is is only itself.—The I, therefore, spirit in general, or God, are ideal, because they are infinite; but they are not ideal as beings-for-self distinct from that which is for-one. For then they would be only immediate, or more precisely, being-there and a being-for-other, because that which would be for them would not be themselves but another, if the moment of being-for-one were not to accrue to them. God is therefore for himself insofar as he himself is that which is for him.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"40.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0004","text":"Being-for-self and being-for-one are therefore not different meanings of ideality, but are essential, inseparable moments of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"40.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSFR:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"5c6ad22d10e87b6beaebf9b2861d34fe9ba0fd79fdb61b20b9a1f1b3bd5f217c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Seyn-für-eines."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Seyn-für-eines.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6","title":"Remark.","order":41,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_6","text":"Der zunächst als sonderbar erscheinende Ausdruck unserer Sprache für die Frage nach der Qualität, was für ein Ding etwas sey, hebt das hier betrachtete Moment in seiner Reflexion-in-sich heraus. Dieser Ausdruck ist in seinem Ursprung idealistisch, indem er nicht fragt, was dieß Ding A für ein anderes Ding B sey, nicht was dieser Mensch für einen anderen Menschen sey;—sondern was dieß für ein Ding, für ein Mensch ist so daß dieß Seyn-für-Eines zugleich zurückgenommen ist in dieß Ding, in diesen Menschen selbst, daß dasjenige, welches ist, und das für welches es ist, ein und dasselbe ist,—eine Identität, als welche auch die Idealität betrachtet werden muß.\n\nDie Idealität kommt zunächst den aufgehobenen Bestimmungen zu, als unterschieden von dem, worin sie aufgehoben sind, das dagegen als das Reelle genommen werden kann. So aber ist das Ideelle wieder eins der Momente und das Reale das andere; die Idealität aber ist dieß, daß beide Bestimmungen gleicherweise nur für Eines sind, und nur für Eines gelten, welche Eine Idealität somit ununterschieden Realität ist. In diesem Sinn ist das Selbstbewußtseyn, der Geist, Gott, das Ideelle, als unendliche Beziehung rein auf sich,—Ich-ist für Ich, beide sind dasselbe, Ich ist zweimal genannt, aber so von den Zweien ist jedes nur für-Eines, ideell; der Geist ist nur für den Geist, Gott nur für Gott, und nur diese Einheit ist Gott, Gott als Geist. —Das Selbstbewußtseyn aber tritt als Bewußtseyn in den Unterschied seiner und eines Anderen, oder seiner Idealität, in der es vorstellend ist, und seiner Realität, indem seine Vorstellung einen bestimmten Inhalt hat, der noch die Seite hat, als das unaufgehobene Negative, als Daseyn, gewußt zu werden. Jedoch den Gedanken, Geist, Gott nur ein Ideelles zu nennen, setzt den Standpunkt voraus, auf welchem das endliche Daseyn als das Reale gilt, und das Ideelle oder das Seyn-für-Eines nur einen einseitigen Sinn hat.\n\nIn einer vorherg. Anm. ist das Princip des Idealismus angegeben und gesagt worden, daß es bei einer Philosophie alsdann näher darauf ankomme, in wiefern das Princip durchgeführt ist. Über die Art dieser Durchführung kann in Beziehung auf die Kategorie, bei der wir stehen, noch eine weitere Bemerkung gemacht werden. Diese Durchführung hängt zunächst davon ab,—ob neben dem Fürsichseyn nicht noch das endliche Daseyn selbstständig bestehen bleibt, außerdem aber ob in dem Unendlichen schon selbst das Moment: für-Eines, ein Verhalten des Ideellen zu sich als Ideellem, gesetzt sey. So ist das eleatische Seyn oder die Spinozische Substanz nur die abstrakte Negation aller Bestimmtheit, ohne daß in ihr selbst die Idealität gesetzt wäre;—bei Spinoza ist, wie weiter unten erwähnt werden wird, die Unendlichkeit nur die absolute Affirmation eines Dings, somit nur die unbewegte Einheit, die Substanz kommt daher nicht einmal zur Bestimmung des Fürsichseyns, vielweniger des Subjekts und des Geistes. Der Idealismus des edeln Malebranche ist in sich explicirter; er enthält folgende Grundgedanken: da Gott alle ewige Wahrheiten, die Ideen, und Vollkommenheiten aller Dinge in sich schließt, so daß sie nur die seinigen sind, so sehen wir sie nur in ihm; Gott erweckt in uns unsere Empfindungen von den Gegenständen durch eine Aktion, die nichts Sinnliches hat, wobei wir uns einbilden, daß wir vom Gegenstande nicht nur dessen Idee die dessen Wesen vorstellt, sondern auch die Empfindung von dem Daseyn desselben erlangen ( De la recherche de la Verité, Eclairc. sur la nature des idées etc.). Wie also die ewigen Wahrheiten und Ideen (Wesenheiten) der Dinge, so ist ihr Daseyn, in Gott, ideell, nicht ein wirkliches Daseyn; obgleich als unsere Gegenstände, sind sie nur für Eines. Dieß Moment des explicirten und konkreten Idealismus, das im Spinozismus mangelt, ist hier vorhanden, indem die absolute Idealität als Wissen bestimmt ist. So rein und tief dieser Idealismus ist, so enthalten jene Verhältnisse Theils noch viel für den Gedanken Unbestimmtes, Theils aber ist deren Inhalt sogleich ganz konkret (die Sünde und die Erlösung u.s.f. treten sogleich in sie ein); die logische Bestimmung der Unendlichkeit, die dessen Grundlage seyn müßte, ist nicht für sich ausgeführt, und so jener erhabene und erfüllte Idealismus wohl das Produkt eines reinen spekulativen Geistes, aber noch nicht eines reinen spekulativen, allein wahrhaft begründenden, Denkens. Der leibnitzische Idealismus liegt mehr innerhalb der Grenze des abstrakten Begriffes.—Das leibnitzische vorstellende Wesen, die Monade, ist wesentlich Ideelles. Das Vorstellen ist ein Fürsichseyn, in welchem die Bestimmtheiten nicht Grenzen und damit nicht ein Daseyn, sondern nur Momente sind. Vorstellen ist zwar gleichfalls eine konkretere Bestimmung, aber hat hier keine weitere Bedeutung, als die der Idealität; denn auch das Bewußtseynslose überhaupt ist bei Leibnitz Vorstellendes, Percipirendes. Es ist in diesem Systeme also das Andersseyn aufgehoben; Geist und Körper, oder die Monaden überhaupt sind nicht Andere für einander, sie begrenzen sich nicht, haben keine Einwirkung aufeinander; es fallen überhaupt alle Verhältnisse weg, welchen ein Daseyn zum Grunde liegt. Die Mannigfaltigkeit ist nur eine ideelle und innere, die Monade bleibt darin nur auf sich selbst bezogen, die Veränderungen entwickeln sich innerhalb ihrer, und sind keine Beziehungen derselben auf andere. Was nach der realen Bestimmung als da seyende Beziehung der Monaden aufeinander genommen wird, ist ein unabhängiges nur simultanes Werden, in das Fürsichseyn einer jeden eingeschlossen.—Daß es mehrere Monaden giebt, daß sie damit auch als Andere bestimmt werden, geht die Monaden selbst nichts an; es ist dieß die außer ihnen fallende Reflexion eines Dritten; sie sind nicht an ihnen selbst Andere gegeneinander; das Fürsichseyn ist rein ohne das Daneben eines Daseyns gehalten.—Allein hierin liegt zugleich das Unvollendete dieses Systems. Die Monaden sind nur an sich, oder in Gott, als der Monade der Monaden, oder auch im Systeme, so Vorstellende. Das Andersseyn ist gleichfalls vorhanden; es falle wohin es wolle, in die Vorstellung selbst, oder wie das Dritte bestimmt werde, welches sie als Andere, als Viele, betrachtet. Die Vielheit ihres Daseyns ist nur ausgeschlossen und zwar nur momentan, die Monaden nur durch die Abstraktion als solche gesetzt, welche Nicht-Andere seyen. Wenn es ein Drittes ist, welches ihr Andersseyn setzt, so ist es auch ein Drittes, welches ihr Andersseyn aufhebt; aber diese ganze Bewegung, welche sie zu ideellen macht, fällt außer ihnen. Indem aber daran erinnert werden kann, daß diese Bewegung des Gedankens selbst doch nur innerhalb einer vorstellenden Monade falle, so ist zugleich zu erinnern, daß eben der Inhalt solchen Denkens in sich selbst sich äußerlich ist. Es wird von der Einheit der absoluten Idealität (der Monade der Monaden) unmittelbar, unbegriffen (—durch die Vorstellung des Erschaffens) zur Kategorie der abstrakten (beziehungslosen) Vielheit des Daseyns übergegangen, und von dieser ebenso abstrakt zurück zu jener Einheit. Die Idealität, das Vorstellen überhaupt, bleibt etwas formelles, wie gleichfalls das zum Bewußtseyn gesteigerte Vorstellen.\n\nWie in dem oben angeführten Einfalle Leibnitzens von der Magnetnadel, die wenn sie ein Bewußtseyn hätte, ihre Richtung nach Norden für eine Bestimmung ihrer Freiheit ansehen würde, das Bewußtseyn nur als einseitige Form, welche gegen ihre Bestimmung und Inhalt gleichgültig sey, gedacht wird, so ist die Idealität in den Monaden eine der Vielheit äußerlich bleibende Form. Die Idealität soll ihnen immanent, ihre Natur Vorstellen seyn; aber ihr Verhalten ist einer Seits ihre Harmonie, die nicht in ihr Daseyn fällt, sie ist daher prästabilirt; anderer Seits ist dieses ihr Daseyn nicht als Seyn-für-Anderes, noch weiter als Idealität gefaßt, sondern nur als abstrakte Vielheit bestimmt; die Idealität der Vielheit und die weitere Bestimmung derselben zur Harmonie wird nicht dieser Vielheit selbst immanent und angehörig.\n\nAnderer Idealismus, wie zum Beispiel der kantische und fichte'sche, kommt nicht über das Sollen oder den unendlichen Progreß hinaus, und bleibt im Dualismus des Daseyns und des Fürsichseyns. In diesen Systemen tritt das Ding-an-sich oder der unendliche Anstoß zwar unmittelbar in das Ich und wird nur ein für dasselbe; aber er geht von einem freien Andersseyn aus, das als negatives Ansichseyn perennirt. Das Ich wird daher wohl als das Ideelle, als fürsichseyend, als unendliche Beziehung auf sich bestimmt; aber das Für-Eines-seyn ist nicht vollendet zum Verschwinden jenes Jenseitigen oder der Richtung nach dem Jenseits.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0001","text":"Der zunächst als sonderbar erscheinende Ausdruck unserer Sprache für die Frage nach der Qualität, was für ein Ding etwas sey, hebt das hier betrachtete Moment in seiner Reflexion-in-sich heraus. Dieser Ausdruck ist in seinem Ursprung idealistisch, indem er nicht fragt, was dieß Ding A für ein anderes Ding B sey, nicht was dieser Mensch für einen anderen Menschen sey;—sondern was dieß für ein Ding, für ein Mensch ist so daß dieß Seyn-für-Eines zugleich zurückgenommen ist in dieß Ding, in diesen Menschen selbst, daß dasjenige, welches ist, und das für welches es ist, ein und dasselbe ist,—eine Identität, als welche auch die Idealität betrachtet werden muß.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"41.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0002","text":"Die Idealität kommt zunächst den aufgehobenen Bestimmungen zu, als unterschieden von dem, worin sie aufgehoben sind, das dagegen als das Reelle genommen werden kann. So aber ist das Ideelle wieder eins der Momente und das Reale das andere; die Idealität aber ist dieß, daß beide Bestimmungen gleicherweise nur für Eines sind, und nur für Eines gelten, welche Eine Idealität somit ununterschieden Realität ist. In diesem Sinn ist das Selbstbewußtseyn, der Geist, Gott, das Ideelle, als unendliche Beziehung rein auf sich,—Ich-ist für Ich, beide sind dasselbe, Ich ist zweimal genannt, aber so von den Zweien ist jedes nur für-Eines, ideell; der Geist ist nur für den Geist, Gott nur für Gott, und nur diese Einheit ist Gott, Gott als Geist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"41.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0003","text":"—Das Selbstbewußtseyn aber tritt als Bewußtseyn in den Unterschied seiner und eines Anderen, oder seiner Idealität, in der es vorstellend ist, und seiner Realität, indem seine Vorstellung einen bestimmten Inhalt hat, der noch die Seite hat, als das unaufgehobene Negative, als Daseyn, gewußt zu werden. Jedoch den Gedanken, Geist, Gott nur ein Ideelles zu nennen, setzt den Standpunkt voraus, auf welchem das endliche Daseyn als das Reale gilt, und das Ideelle oder das Seyn-für-Eines nur einen einseitigen Sinn hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"41.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0004","text":"In einer vorherg. Anm. ist das Princip des Idealismus angegeben und gesagt worden, daß es bei einer Philosophie alsdann näher darauf ankomme, in wiefern das Princip durchgeführt ist. Über die Art dieser Durchführung kann in Beziehung auf die Kategorie, bei der wir stehen, noch eine weitere Bemerkung gemacht werden. Diese Durchführung hängt zunächst davon ab,—ob neben dem Fürsichseyn nicht noch das endliche Daseyn selbstständig bestehen bleibt, außerdem aber ob in dem Unendlichen schon selbst das Moment: für-Eines, ein Verhalten des Ideellen zu sich als Ideellem, gesetzt sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"41.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0005","text":"So ist das eleatische Seyn oder die Spinozische Substanz nur die abstrakte Negation aller Bestimmtheit, ohne daß in ihr selbst die Idealität gesetzt wäre;—bei Spinoza ist, wie weiter unten erwähnt werden wird, die Unendlichkeit nur die absolute Affirmation eines Dings, somit nur die unbewegte Einheit, die Substanz kommt daher nicht einmal zur Bestimmung des Fürsichseyns, vielweniger des Subjekts und des Geistes.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"41.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0006","text":"Der Idealismus des edeln Malebranche ist in sich explicirter; er enthält folgende Grundgedanken: da Gott alle ewige Wahrheiten, die Ideen, und Vollkommenheiten aller Dinge in sich schließt, so daß sie nur die seinigen sind, so sehen wir sie nur in ihm; Gott erweckt in uns unsere Empfindungen von den Gegenständen durch eine Aktion, die nichts Sinnliches hat, wobei wir uns einbilden, daß wir vom Gegenstande nicht nur dessen Idee die dessen Wesen vorstellt, sondern auch die Empfindung von dem Daseyn desselben erlangen ( De la recherche de la Verité, Eclairc. sur la nature des idées etc.). Wie also die ewigen Wahrheiten und Ideen (Wesenheiten) der Dinge, so ist ihr Daseyn, in Gott, ideell, nicht ein wirkliches Daseyn; obgleich als unsere Gegenstände, sind sie nur für Eines.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"41.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0007","text":"Dieß Moment des explicirten und konkreten Idealismus, das im Spinozismus mangelt, ist hier vorhanden, indem die absolute Idealität als Wissen bestimmt ist. So rein und tief dieser Idealismus ist, so enthalten jene Verhältnisse Theils noch viel für den Gedanken Unbestimmtes, Theils aber ist deren Inhalt sogleich ganz konkret (die Sünde und die Erlösung u.s.f. treten sogleich in sie ein); die logische Bestimmung der Unendlichkeit, die dessen Grundlage seyn müßte, ist nicht für sich ausgeführt, und so jener erhabene und erfüllte Idealismus wohl das Produkt eines reinen spekulativen Geistes, aber noch nicht eines reinen spekulativen, allein wahrhaft begründenden, Denkens. Der leibnitzische Idealismus liegt mehr innerhalb der Grenze des abstrakten Begriffes.—Das leibnitzische vorstellende Wesen, die Monade, ist wesentlich Ideelles.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"41.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0008","text":"Das Vorstellen ist ein Fürsichseyn, in welchem die Bestimmtheiten nicht Grenzen und damit nicht ein Daseyn, sondern nur Momente sind. Vorstellen ist zwar gleichfalls eine konkretere Bestimmung, aber hat hier keine weitere Bedeutung, als die der Idealität; denn auch das Bewußtseynslose überhaupt ist bei Leibnitz Vorstellendes, Percipirendes. Es ist in diesem Systeme also das Andersseyn aufgehoben; Geist und Körper, oder die Monaden überhaupt sind nicht Andere für einander, sie begrenzen sich nicht, haben keine Einwirkung aufeinander; es fallen überhaupt alle Verhältnisse weg, welchen ein Daseyn zum Grunde liegt. Die Mannigfaltigkeit ist nur eine ideelle und innere, die Monade bleibt darin nur auf sich selbst bezogen, die Veränderungen entwickeln sich innerhalb ihrer, und sind keine Beziehungen derselben auf andere.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"41.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0009","text":"Was nach der realen Bestimmung als da seyende Beziehung der Monaden aufeinander genommen wird, ist ein unabhängiges nur simultanes Werden, in das Fürsichseyn einer jeden eingeschlossen.—Daß es mehrere Monaden giebt, daß sie damit auch als Andere bestimmt werden, geht die Monaden selbst nichts an; es ist dieß die außer ihnen fallende Reflexion eines Dritten; sie sind nicht an ihnen selbst Andere gegeneinander; das Fürsichseyn ist rein ohne das Daneben eines Daseyns gehalten.—Allein hierin liegt zugleich das Unvollendete dieses Systems. Die Monaden sind nur an sich, oder in Gott, als der Monade der Monaden, oder auch im Systeme, so Vorstellende. Das Andersseyn ist gleichfalls vorhanden; es falle wohin es wolle, in die Vorstellung selbst, oder wie das Dritte bestimmt werde, welches sie als Andere, als Viele, betrachtet.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"41.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0010","text":"Die Vielheit ihres Daseyns ist nur ausgeschlossen und zwar nur momentan, die Monaden nur durch die Abstraktion als solche gesetzt, welche Nicht-Andere seyen. Wenn es ein Drittes ist, welches ihr Andersseyn setzt, so ist es auch ein Drittes, welches ihr Andersseyn aufhebt; aber diese ganze Bewegung, welche sie zu ideellen macht, fällt außer ihnen. Indem aber daran erinnert werden kann, daß diese Bewegung des Gedankens selbst doch nur innerhalb einer vorstellenden Monade falle, so ist zugleich zu erinnern, daß eben der Inhalt solchen Denkens in sich selbst sich äußerlich ist. Es wird von der Einheit der absoluten Idealität (der Monade der Monaden) unmittelbar, unbegriffen (—durch die Vorstellung des Erschaffens) zur Kategorie der abstrakten (beziehungslosen) Vielheit des Daseyns übergegangen, und von dieser ebenso abstrakt zurück zu jener Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"41.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0011","text":"Die Idealität, das Vorstellen überhaupt, bleibt etwas formelles, wie gleichfalls das zum Bewußtseyn gesteigerte Vorstellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"41.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0012","text":"Wie in dem oben angeführten Einfalle Leibnitzens von der Magnetnadel, die wenn sie ein Bewußtseyn hätte, ihre Richtung nach Norden für eine Bestimmung ihrer Freiheit ansehen würde, das Bewußtseyn nur als einseitige Form, welche gegen ihre Bestimmung und Inhalt gleichgültig sey, gedacht wird, so ist die Idealität in den Monaden eine der Vielheit äußerlich bleibende Form. Die Idealität soll ihnen immanent, ihre Natur Vorstellen seyn; aber ihr Verhalten ist einer Seits ihre Harmonie, die nicht in ihr Daseyn fällt, sie ist daher prästabilirt; anderer Seits ist dieses ihr Daseyn nicht als Seyn-für-Anderes, noch weiter als Idealität gefaßt, sondern nur als abstrakte Vielheit bestimmt; die Idealität der Vielheit und die weitere Bestimmung derselben zur Harmonie wird nicht dieser Vielheit selbst immanent und angehörig.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"41.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0013","text":"Anderer Idealismus, wie zum Beispiel der kantische und fichte'sche, kommt nicht über das Sollen oder den unendlichen Progreß hinaus, und bleibt im Dualismus des Daseyns und des Fürsichseyns. In diesen Systemen tritt das Ding-an-sich oder der unendliche Anstoß zwar unmittelbar in das Ich und wird nur ein für dasselbe; aber er geht von einem freien Andersseyn aus, das als negatives Ansichseyn perennirt. Das Ich wird daher wohl als das Ideelle, als fürsichseyend, als unendliche Beziehung auf sich bestimmt; aber das Für-Eines-seyn ist nicht vollendet zum Verschwinden jenes Jenseitigen oder der Richtung nach dem Jenseits.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"41.13"}],"sha256":"84f1a19213035dfe80d4d576040b72055609c86c1c22d86a375b5e7ab3175be5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102504726877Z_a184829c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"84f1a19213035dfe80d4d576040b72055609c86c1c22d86a375b5e7ab3175be5","sha256":"6dd4c7d038e7a787a6b1e49cd51e6af3277e5a38ca406af4bd1f04b192e10bc8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:04.726903+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0001","text":"The expression in our language, initially seeming strange, for the question concerning quality—what sort of thing something is—brings out the moment here under consideration in its reflection-into-itself. This expression is idealistic in its origin, in that it does not ask what this thing A is for another thing B, nor what this human being is for another human being;—but what sort of a thing, what sort of a human being this is, so that this being-for-one is at the same time taken back into this thing, into this human being himself, so that that which is and that for which it is are one and the same,—an identity which must likewise be regarded as ideality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"41.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0002","text":"Ideality pertains in the first instance to the sublated determinations, as distinguished from that in which they are sublated, which, by contrast, can be taken as the real. But thus the ideal is again one of the moments and the real the other; yet ideality consists in both determinations alike being only for one, and being valid only for one, which one ideality is therefore undistinguished reality. In this sense self-consciousness, spirit, God, is the ideal, as infinite relation purely to itself,—I-is for I, both are the same, I is named twice, but of the two each is only for-one, ideal; spirit is only for spirit, God only for God, and only this unity is God, God as spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"41.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0003","text":"—But self-consciousness, as consciousness, enters into the distinction between itself and an other, or between its ideality, in which it is representing, and its reality, in that its representation has a determinate content which still has the side of being known as the unsublated negative, as determinate being. Yet to call thought, spirit, God merely an ideal presupposes the standpoint at which finite determinate being counts as the real, and the ideal, or being-for-one, has only a one-sided sense.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"41.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0004","text":"In a preceding remark the principle of idealism has been specified, and it has been said that, in the case of a philosophy, it then depends more particularly on the extent to which the principle is carried through. A further remark can be made concerning the manner of this carrying-through in relation to the category at which we stand. This carrying-through depends in the first place on whether finite determinate being itself does not continue to subsist independently alongside being-for-self, and further on whether, in the infinite itself, the moment of for-one, a comportment of the ideal to itself as ideal, is already posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"41.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0005","text":"Thus Eleatic being, or the Spinozistic substance, is only the abstract negation of all determinateness, without ideality itself being posited within it;—in Spinoza, as will be mentioned further below, infinity is only the absolute affirmation of a thing, hence only the unmoved unity; substance therefore does not even attain to the determination of being-for-self, much less to that of subject and spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"41.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0006","text":"The idealism of the noble Malebranche is more explicit in itself; it contains the following fundamental thoughts: since God includes within himself all eternal truths, the ideas, and perfections of all things, so that they are only his, we see them only in him; God awakens in us our sensations of objects through an action which has nothing sensible about it, whereby we imagine that from the object we acquire not only its idea, which represents its essence, but also the sensation of its determinate being (De la recherche de la Verité, Eclairc. sur la nature des idées etc.). Thus, just as the eternal truths and ideas (essences) of things, so their determinate being is, in God, ideal, not an actual determinate being; although, as our objects, they are only for one.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"41.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0007","text":"This moment of explicit and concrete idealism, which is lacking in Spinozism, is present here, in that absolute ideality is determined as knowing. As pure and profound as this idealism is, those relations on the one hand still contain much that is indeterminate for thought, while on the other hand their content is at once quite concrete (sin and redemption, etc., at once enter into them); the logical determination of infinity, which would have to be its foundation, is not developed for itself, and thus that sublime and fulfilled idealism is indeed the product of a pure speculative spirit, but not yet of a pure speculative thinking that alone truly grounds. Leibnizian idealism lies more within the boundary of the abstract concept.—Leibniz's representing being, the monad, is essentially ideal.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"41.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0008","text":"Representing is a being-for-self in which the determinacies are not limits and hence not a determinate being, but only moments. Representing is indeed likewise a more concrete determination, but here it has no further significance than that of ideality; for even the unconscious in general is, in Leibniz, representing, perceiving. In this system, therefore, otherness is sublated; spirit and body, or the monads in general, are not others for one another, they do not limit one another, have no influence upon one another; all relations in general which have a determinate being as their foundation fall away. The multiplicity is only an ideal and internal one; the monad remains therein related only to itself; the changes develop within it and are not relations of it to others.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"41.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0009","text":"What, according to the real determination, is taken as the existent relation of the monads to one another is an independent, merely simultaneous becoming, enclosed within the being-for-self of each.—That there are several monads, that they are thereby also determined as others, does not concern the monads themselves; this is the reflection of a third falling outside them; they are not in themselves others over against one another; being-for-self is kept pure, without the alongside of a determinate being.—Yet herein lies at the same time the incompleteness of this system. The monads are representing only in themselves, or in God, as the monad of monads, or likewise in the system. Otherness is likewise present; wherever it may fall, into representation itself, or however the third may be determined which regards them as others, as many.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"41.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0010","text":"The multiplicity of their determinate being is only excluded, and indeed only momentarily; the monads are posited as such only through the abstraction that they are non-others. If it is a third which posits their otherness, then it is also a third which sublates their otherness; but this entire movement, which makes them ideal, falls outside them. But insofar as it may be recalled that this movement of thought itself nevertheless falls only within a representing monad, it must at the same time be recalled that precisely the content of such thinking is external to itself. From the unity of absolute ideality (the monad of monads), there is an immediate, uncomprehended transition (—through the representation of creation) to the category of abstract (relationless) multiplicity of determinate being, and from this an equally abstract return to that unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"41.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0011","text":"Ideality, representing in general, remains something formal, as likewise does representing raised to consciousness.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"41.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0012","text":"Just as, in Leibniz's above-cited conceit of the magnetic needle—which, if it had a consciousness, would regard its direction toward the north as a determination of its freedom—consciousness is thought only as a one-sided form, indifferent toward its determination and content, so ideality in the monads is a form remaining external to multiplicity. Ideality is supposed to be immanent in them, their nature is supposed to be representing; but their comportment is, on the one hand, their harmony, which does not fall within their determinate being and is therefore pre-established; on the other hand, this their determinate being is not grasped as being-for-other, nor, further, as ideality, but determined only as abstract multiplicity; the ideality of multiplicity and its further determination into harmony are not made immanent in, and belonging to, this multiplicity itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"41.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0013","text":"Other idealism, such as, for example, Kantian and Fichtean idealism, does not get beyond the ought or infinite progress, and remains in the dualism of determinate being and being-for-self. In these systems, the thing-in-itself or the infinite check indeed enters immediately into the I and becomes only a for it; but it proceeds from a free otherness which persists as negative being-in-itself. The I is therefore indeed determined as the ideal, as being-for-self, as infinite relation to itself; but being-for-one is not completed into the disappearance of that beyond, or of the direction toward the beyond.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"41.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_6:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"1a0397afcfeb075a9a3a45fb3ba6c953cf422f9025b52f3b466e1d1d8774c7ac","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN","title":"c. One.","order":42,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CEIN","text":"Das Fürsichseyn ist die einfache Einheit seiner selbst und seines Moments, des Seyns für-Eines. Es ist nur Eine Bestimmung vorhanden, die Beziehung-auf-sich-selbst des Aufhebens. Die Momente des Fürsichseyns sind in Unterschiedslosigkeit zusammengesunken, welche Unmittelbarkeit oder Seyn ist, aber eine Unmittelbarkeit, die sich auf das Negiren gründet, das als ihre Bestimmung gesetzt ist. Das Fürsichseyn ist so, Fürsichseyendes, und indem in dieser Unmittelbarkeit seine innere Bedeutung verschwindet, die ganz abstrakte Grenze seiner selbst,—das Eins.\n\nEs kann zum Voraus auf die Schwierigkeit, welche in der nachfolgenden Darstellung der Entwickelung des Eins liegt, und auf den Grund dieser Schwierigkeit aufmerksam gemacht werden. Die Momente, welche den Begriff des Eins als Fürsichseyns ausmachen, treten darin auseinander; sie sind 1) Negation überhaupt, 2) Zwei Negationen 3) somit Zweier, die dasselbe sind, 4) die schlechthin entgegengesetzt sind; 5) Beziehung auf sich, Identität als solche, 6) negative Beziehung und doch auf sich selbst. Diese Momente treten hier dadurch auseinander, daß die Form der Unmittelbarkeit, des Seyns, am Fürsichseyn als Fürsichseyendem hereinkommt; durch diese Unmittelbarkeit wird jedes Moment als eine eigene, seyende Bestimmung gesetzt; und doch sind sie ebenso untrennbar. Somit muß von jeder Bestimmung ebenso ihr Gegentheil gesagt werden; dieser Widerspruch ist es, der, bei der abstrakten Beschaffenheit der Momente, die Schwierigkeit ausmacht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0001","text":"Das Fürsichseyn ist die einfache Einheit seiner selbst und seines Moments, des Seyns für-Eines. Es ist nur Eine Bestimmung vorhanden, die Beziehung-auf-sich-selbst des Aufhebens. Die Momente des Fürsichseyns sind in Unterschiedslosigkeit zusammengesunken, welche Unmittelbarkeit oder Seyn ist, aber eine Unmittelbarkeit, die sich auf das Negiren gründet, das als ihre Bestimmung gesetzt ist. Das Fürsichseyn ist so, Fürsichseyendes, und indem in dieser Unmittelbarkeit seine innere Bedeutung verschwindet, die ganz abstrakte Grenze seiner selbst,—das Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"42.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0002","text":"Es kann zum Voraus auf die Schwierigkeit, welche in der nachfolgenden Darstellung der Entwickelung des Eins liegt, und auf den Grund dieser Schwierigkeit aufmerksam gemacht werden. Die Momente, welche den Begriff des Eins als Fürsichseyns ausmachen, treten darin auseinander; sie sind 1) Negation überhaupt, 2) Zwei Negationen 3) somit Zweier, die dasselbe sind, 4) die schlechthin entgegengesetzt sind; 5) Beziehung auf sich, Identität als solche, 6) negative Beziehung und doch auf sich selbst. Diese Momente treten hier dadurch auseinander, daß die Form der Unmittelbarkeit, des Seyns, am Fürsichseyn als Fürsichseyendem hereinkommt; durch diese Unmittelbarkeit wird jedes Moment als eine eigene, seyende Bestimmung gesetzt; und doch sind sie ebenso untrennbar.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"42.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0003","text":"Somit muß von jeder Bestimmung ebenso ihr Gegentheil gesagt werden; dieser Widerspruch ist es, der, bei der abstrakten Beschaffenheit der Momente, die Schwierigkeit ausmacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"42.3"}],"sha256":"cdcaf093af6f261fb4a2ac4de80968bf96cb18ec4d14d7c3e263f3efd3b90c38","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102508478735Z_ca61d62e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. One.","source_sha256":"cdcaf093af6f261fb4a2ac4de80968bf96cb18ec4d14d7c3e263f3efd3b90c38","sha256":"9127c74b87750eb5017db15763953f8edb29046e525a0fc754f1d8890251b45e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:08.478753+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0001","text":"Being-for-self is the simple unity of itself and of its moment, of being-for-one. There is present only one determination, the relation-to-itself of sublation. The moments of being-for-self have collapsed into indistinguishability, which is immediacy or being, but an immediacy grounded upon negating, which is posited as its determination. Being-for-self is thus being-for-self-existent, and inasmuch as in this immediacy its inner significance vanishes, it is the wholly abstract limit of itself,—the One.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"42.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0002","text":"Attention may be drawn in advance to the difficulty that lies in the following exposition of the development of the One, and to the ground of this difficulty. The moments that constitute the concept of the One as being-for-self come apart therein; they are 1) negation in general, 2) two negations, 3) hence two which are the same, 4) which are absolutely opposed; 5) relation to self, identity as such, 6) negative relation and yet to itself. These moments come apart here because the form of immediacy, of being, enters into being-for-self as being-for-self-existent; through this immediacy each moment is posited as a distinct, existent determination; and yet they are equally inseparable.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"42.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0003","text":"Thus, of every determination its opposite must equally be said; it is this contradiction which, given the abstract character of the moments, constitutes the difficulty.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"42.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CEIN:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"ace99d3ce5a8169967c2f5cccc47562cba3841cbd746c9a39a51966ec61abdf6","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Eins."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Eins.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV","title":"B. One and Many.","order":43,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BEUV","text":"Das Eins ist die einfache Beziehung des Fürsichseyns auf sich selbst, in der seine Momente in sich zusammengefallen sind, in der es daher die Form der Unmittelbarkeit hat und seine Momente daher nun daseyende werden.\n\nAls Beziehung des Negativen auf sich, ist das Eins Bestimmen,—und als Beziehung auf sich, ist es unendliches Selbstbestimmen. Aber um der nunmehrigen Unmittelbarkeit willen, sind diese Unterschiede nicht mehr nur als Momente Einer und derselben Selbstbestimmung, sondern zugleich als Seyende gesetzt. Die Idealität des Fürsichseyns als Totalität schlägt so fürs erste in die Realität um, und zwar in die festeste, abstrakteste, als Eins. Das Fürsichseyn ist im Eins die gesetzte Einheit des Seyns und Daseyns, als die absolute Vereinigung\n\nder Beziehung auf Anderes und der Beziehung auf sich; aber dann tritt auch die Bestimmtheit des Seyns, gegen die Bestimmung der unendlichen Negation, gegen die Selbstbestimmung ein, so daß was Eins an sich ist, es nun nur an ihm ist, und damit das Negative ein als von ihm unterschiedenes Anderes. Was sich als von ihm unterschieden vorhanden zeigt, ist sein eigenes Selbstbestimmen; dessen Einheit mit sich so als unterschieden von sich ist zur Beziehung herabgesetzt, und als negative Einheit Negation seiner selbst als eines Anderen, Ausschließen des Eins als eines Anderen aus sich, dem Eins.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0001","text":"Das Eins ist die einfache Beziehung des Fürsichseyns auf sich selbst, in der seine Momente in sich zusammengefallen sind, in der es daher die Form der Unmittelbarkeit hat und seine Momente daher nun daseyende werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"43.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0002","text":"Als Beziehung des Negativen auf sich, ist das Eins Bestimmen,—und als Beziehung auf sich, ist es unendliches Selbstbestimmen. Aber um der nunmehrigen Unmittelbarkeit willen, sind diese Unterschiede nicht mehr nur als Momente Einer und derselben Selbstbestimmung, sondern zugleich als Seyende gesetzt. Die Idealität des Fürsichseyns als Totalität schlägt so fürs erste in die Realität um, und zwar in die festeste, abstrakteste, als Eins. Das Fürsichseyn ist im Eins die gesetzte Einheit des Seyns und Daseyns, als die absolute Vereinigung","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"43.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0003","text":"der Beziehung auf Anderes und der Beziehung auf sich; aber dann tritt auch die Bestimmtheit des Seyns, gegen die Bestimmung der unendlichen Negation, gegen die Selbstbestimmung ein, so daß was Eins an sich ist, es nun nur an ihm ist, und damit das Negative ein als von ihm unterschiedenes Anderes. Was sich als von ihm unterschieden vorhanden zeigt, ist sein eigenes Selbstbestimmen; dessen Einheit mit sich so als unterschieden von sich ist zur Beziehung herabgesetzt, und als negative Einheit Negation seiner selbst als eines Anderen, Ausschließen des Eins als eines Anderen aus sich, dem Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"43.3"}],"sha256":"13fa6687825489bc87dc7faa19d181ec72954092ddbf56183b3040c3511ce02d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102512306329Z_c60a1dfd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. One and Many.","source_sha256":"13fa6687825489bc87dc7faa19d181ec72954092ddbf56183b3040c3511ce02d","sha256":"5bf7a6a5d913d469742ebe827c764235b499b4709d2b3d737478282010436546","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:12.306352+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0001","text":"The One is the simple relation of being-for-self to itself, in which its moments have collapsed into themselves, in which it therefore has the form of immediacy and its moments therefore now become existent.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"43.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0002","text":"As the relation of the negative to itself, the One is determining,—and as relation to itself, it is infinite self-determining. But by virtue of the now present immediacy, these distinctions are no longer posited merely as moments of one and the same self-determination, but at the same time as beings. The ideality of being-for-self as totality thus initially passes over into reality, and indeed into the most fixed, most abstract reality, as One. In the One, being-for-self is the posited unity of being and existence, as the absolute unification","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"43.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0003","text":"of relation to another and relation to itself; but then the determinacy of being also enters in, as against the determination of infinite negation, as against self-determination, so that what the One is in itself is now only in it, and thereby the negative [is] an other distinct from it. What shows itself as present, distinct from it, is its own self-determining; its unity with itself, thus as distinct from itself, is reduced to relation, and, as negative unity, [is] negation of itself as an other, exclusion of the One as an other from itself, the One.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"43.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEUV:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"454df726df40c24d771e8e649d66e10001ad2ca541c616f42a5c61caccda8ef7","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Eins und Vieles."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Eins und Vieles.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS","title":"a. The One in Its Own Self.","order":44,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DEIS","text":"An ihm selbst ist das Eins überhaupt; dieß sein Seyn ist kein Daseyn, keine Bestimmung als Beziehung auf Anderes, keine Beschaffenheit, es ist dieß, diesen Kreis von Kategorien negirt zu haben. Das Eins ist somit keines Anderswerdens fähig; es ist unveränderlich.\n\nEs ist unbestimmt, jedoch nicht mehr wie das Seyn; seine Unbestimmtheit ist die Bestimmtheit, welche Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, absolutes Bestimmtseyn; gesetztes Insichseyn. Als nach seinem Begriffe sich auf sich beziehende Negation hat es den Unterschied in ihm,—eine Richtung von sich ab hinaus auf Anderes, die aber unmittelbar umgewendet, weil nach diesem Momente des Selbstbestimmens kein Anderes ist, auf das sie gehe, und die in sich zurückgekehrt ist.\n\nIn dieser einfachen Unmittelbarkeit ist die Vermittelung des Daseyns und der Idealität selbst, und damit alle Verschiedenheit und Mannigfaltigkeit verschwunden. Es ist nichts in ihm; dieß Nichts, die Abstraktion der Beziehung auf sich selbst, ist hier unterschieden von dem Insichseyn selbst, es ist ein Gesetztes, weil dieß Insichseyn nicht mehr das einfache des Etwas ist, sondern-die Bestimmung hat, als Vermittelung konkret zu seyn; als abstrakt aber ist es zwar identisch mit Eins, aber verschieden von dessen Bestimmung. So dieß Nichts gesetzt, als in Einem ist das Nichts als Leeres.—Das Leere ist so die Qualität des Eins in seiner Unmittelbarkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0001","text":"An ihm selbst ist das Eins überhaupt; dieß sein Seyn ist kein Daseyn, keine Bestimmung als Beziehung auf Anderes, keine Beschaffenheit, es ist dieß, diesen Kreis von Kategorien negirt zu haben. Das Eins ist somit keines Anderswerdens fähig; es ist unveränderlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"44.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0002","text":"Es ist unbestimmt, jedoch nicht mehr wie das Seyn; seine Unbestimmtheit ist die Bestimmtheit, welche Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, absolutes Bestimmtseyn; gesetztes Insichseyn. Als nach seinem Begriffe sich auf sich beziehende Negation hat es den Unterschied in ihm,—eine Richtung von sich ab hinaus auf Anderes, die aber unmittelbar umgewendet, weil nach diesem Momente des Selbstbestimmens kein Anderes ist, auf das sie gehe, und die in sich zurückgekehrt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"44.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0003","text":"In dieser einfachen Unmittelbarkeit ist die Vermittelung des Daseyns und der Idealität selbst, und damit alle Verschiedenheit und Mannigfaltigkeit verschwunden. Es ist nichts in ihm; dieß Nichts, die Abstraktion der Beziehung auf sich selbst, ist hier unterschieden von dem Insichseyn selbst, es ist ein Gesetztes, weil dieß Insichseyn nicht mehr das einfache des Etwas ist, sondern-die Bestimmung hat, als Vermittelung konkret zu seyn; als abstrakt aber ist es zwar identisch mit Eins, aber verschieden von dessen Bestimmung. So dieß Nichts gesetzt, als in Einem ist das Nichts als Leeres.—Das Leere ist so die Qualität des Eins in seiner Unmittelbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"44.3"}],"sha256":"8f877ee319e1a421c4aec94b0cad746808465f8319c9409065deb2aec4eabe1f","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102516723470Z_304780ff","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. The One in Its Own Self.","source_sha256":"8f877ee319e1a421c4aec94b0cad746808465f8319c9409065deb2aec4eabe1f","sha256":"64b7d64e3ff7ba55f9d58ac134029153a78b3c2a517e9e3161f53f7453a23fb8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:16.723489+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0001","text":"In it itself, the One is wholly; this its Being is no determinate being, no determinacy as relation to an other, no constitution; it is this, to have negated this circle of categories. The One is thus incapable of becoming other; it is unchangeable.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"44.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0002","text":"It is indeterminate, yet no longer as Being is; its indeterminacy is the determinacy which is relation to itself, absolute determinateness; posited being-within-self. As, according to its Concept, negation relating itself to itself, it has distinction within it,—a direction outward from itself toward an other, which, however, is immediately reversed, because according to this moment of self-determination there is no other to which it could go, and which has returned into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"44.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0003","text":"In this simple immediacy, the mediation of determinate being and of ideality itself, and with it all diversity and multiplicity, has vanished. There is nothing in it; this nothing, the abstraction of relation to itself, is here distinguished from being-within-self itself; it is a posited [moment], because this being-within-self is no longer the simple being-within-self of Something, but has the determinacy of being concrete as mediation; but as abstract it is indeed identical with the One, yet distinct from its determinacy. Thus this nothing, posited as in the One, is nothing as void.—The void is thus the quality of the One in its immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"44.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DEIS:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"ce82dd85312236976ceaff48ec34ab9906fd6d40ec477524cef4e93a7effcc4d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Das Eins an ihm selbst."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Das Eins an ihm selbst.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEU","title":"b. The One and the Void.","order":45,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDEU","text":"Das Eins ist das Leere als die abstrakte Beziehung der Negation auf sich selbst. Aber von der einfachen Unmittelbarkeit, dem auch affirmativen Seyn des Eins, ist das Leeres als das Nichts schlechthin verschieden, und indem sie in Einer Beziehung, des Eins selbst nämlich, stehen, ist ihre Verschiedenheit gesetzt; verschieden aber vom Seyenden ist das Nichts als Leeres außer dem seyenden Eins.\n\nDas Fürsichseyn, indem es sich auf diese Weise als das Eins und das Leere bestimmt, hat wieder ein Daseyn erlangt.—Das Eins und das Leere haben die negative Beziehung auf sich zu ihrem gemeinschaftlichen, einfachen Boden. Die Momente des Fürsichseyns treten aus dieser Einheit, werden sich Äußerliche, indem durch die einfache Einheit der Momente die Bestimmung des Seyns hereinkommt, so setzt sie sich selbst zu einer Seite, damit zum Daseyn herab, und darin stellt sich ihre andere Bestimmung, die Negation überhaupt, gleichfalls als Daseyn des Nichts, als das Leere, gegenüber.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEU:P0001","text":"Das Eins ist das Leere als die abstrakte Beziehung der Negation auf sich selbst. Aber von der einfachen Unmittelbarkeit, dem auch affirmativen Seyn des Eins, ist das Leeres als das Nichts schlechthin verschieden, und indem sie in Einer Beziehung, des Eins selbst nämlich, stehen, ist ihre Verschiedenheit gesetzt; verschieden aber vom Seyenden ist das Nichts als Leeres außer dem seyenden Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"45.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEU:P0002","text":"Das Fürsichseyn, indem es sich auf diese Weise als das Eins und das Leere bestimmt, hat wieder ein Daseyn erlangt.—Das Eins und das Leere haben die negative Beziehung auf sich zu ihrem gemeinschaftlichen, einfachen Boden. Die Momente des Fürsichseyns treten aus dieser Einheit, werden sich Äußerliche, indem durch die einfache Einheit der Momente die Bestimmung des Seyns hereinkommt, so setzt sie sich selbst zu einer Seite, damit zum Daseyn herab, und darin stellt sich ihre andere Bestimmung, die Negation überhaupt, gleichfalls als Daseyn des Nichts, als das Leere, gegenüber.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"45.2"}],"sha256":"05986a37016d0f0e0513605f04397b203429190528602b707dd724241592069c","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102522398884Z_ff1eab92","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The One and the Void.","source_sha256":"05986a37016d0f0e0513605f04397b203429190528602b707dd724241592069c","sha256":"55e0db4f4bffffe7ba9fd0956dd9b1cf6b63ee49120415f937db3f35f2c48fe0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:22.398940+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEU:P0001","text":"The One is the Void as the abstract relation of negation to itself. But the Void, as the Nothing, is absolutely distinct from the simple immediacy, the likewise affirmative Being of the One; and, since they stand in one relation, namely that of the One itself, their difference is posited; but, distinct from what is, the Nothing as Void is outside the being One.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"45.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEU:P0002","text":"Being-for-self, in determining itself in this way as the One and the Void, has once again attained determinate being.—The One and the Void have the negative relation to themselves as their common, simple ground. The moments of being-for-self emerge from this unity, become external to one another, since through the simple unity of the moments the determination of Being enters in; it thereby posits itself as one side, thus descends to determinate being, and therein its other determination, negation in general, likewise presents itself over against it as the determinate being of Nothing, as the Void.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"45.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEU:P0002"]}],"source_digest":"7a725f2bd02a9ea27d58f11edd1759cc44e4c01c391e656290aa44e098c6edbb","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Das Eins und das Leere."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Das Eins und das Leere.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7","title":"Remark.","order":46,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_7","text":"Das Eins in dieser Form von Daseyn ist die Stufe der Kategorie, die bei den Alten, als das atomistische Princip vorgekommen ist, nach welchem das Wesen der Dinge ist, das Atome und das Leere, (…..) Die Abstraktion zu dieser Form gediehen, hat eine größere Bestimmtheit gewonnen, als das Seyn des Parmenides und das Werden des Heraklits. So hoch sie sich stellt, indem sie diese einfache Bestimmtheit des Eins und des Leeren zum Princip aller Dinge macht, die unendliche Mannigfaltigkeit der Welt auf diesen einfachen Gegensatz zurückführt, und sie aus ihm zu erkennen sich erkühnt, ebenso leicht ist es für das vorstellende Reflektiren, sich hier Atome und daneben das Leere vorzustellen. Es ist daher kein Wunder, daß das atomistische Princip sich jederzeit erhalten hat; das gleich triviale und äußerliche Verhältniß der Zusammensetzung, das noch hinzukommen muß, um zum Scheine eines Konkreten und einer Mannigfaltigkeit zu gelangen, ist eben so populär als die Atome selbst und das Leere. Das Eins und das Leere ist das Fürsichseyn, das höchste qualitative Insichseyn zur völligen Äußerlichkeit herabgesunken; die Unmittelbarkeit oder das Seyn des Eins, weil es die Negation alles Andersseyns ist, ist gesetzt nicht mehr bestimmbar und veränderlich zu seyn, für dessen absolute Sprödigkeit bleibt also alle Bestimmung, Mannigfaltigkeit, Verknüpfung schlechthin äußerliche Beziehung.\n\nIn dieser Äußerlichkeit ist jedoch das atomistische Princip nicht bei den ersten Denkern desselben geblieben, sondern es hatte außer seiner Abstraktion auch eine spekulative Bestimmung darin, daß das Leere als der Quell der Bewegung erkannt worden ist; was eine ganz andere Beziehung des Atomen und des Leeren ist, als das bloße Nebeneinander und die Gleichgültigkeit dieser beiden Bestimmungen gegeneinander. Daß das Leere der Quell der Bewegung ist, hat nicht den geringfügigen Sinn, daß sich Etwas nur in ein Leeres hineinbewegen könne, und nicht in einen schon erfüllten Raum, denn in einem solchen fände es keinen Platz mehr offen; in welchem Verstande das Leere nur die Voraussetzung oder Bedingung, nicht der Grund der Bewegung wäre, so wie auch die Bewegung selbst als vorhanden vorausgesetzt, und das Wesentliche, ein Grund derselben, vergessen ist. Die Ansicht, daß das Leere den Grund der Bewegung ausmache, enthält den tiefern Gedanken, daß im Negativen überhaupt, der Grund des Werdens, der Unruhe der Selbstbewegung liegt; in welchem Sinne aber das Negative als die wahrhafte Negativität des Unendlichen zu nehmen ist.—Das Leere ist Grund der Bewegung nur als die negative Beziehung des Eins auf sein Negatives, auf das Eins, d. i. auf sich selbst, das jedoch als Daseyendes gesetzt ist.\n\nSonst aber sind weitere Bestimmungen der Alten über eine Gestalt, Stellung der Atome, die Richtung ihrer Bewegung willkürlich und äußerlich genug; und stehen dabei in direktem Widerspruch mit der Grundbestimmung des Atomen. An den Atomen, dem Princip der höchsten Äußerlichkeit und damit der höchsten Begrifflosigkeit, leidet die Physik in den Molecules, Partikeln ebenso sehr als die Staatswissenschaft, die von dem einzelnen Willen der Individuen ausgeht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0001","text":"Das Eins in dieser Form von Daseyn ist die Stufe der Kategorie, die bei den Alten, als das atomistische Princip vorgekommen ist, nach welchem das Wesen der Dinge ist, das Atome und das Leere, (…..) Die Abstraktion zu dieser Form gediehen, hat eine größere Bestimmtheit gewonnen, als das Seyn des Parmenides und das Werden des Heraklits. So hoch sie sich stellt, indem sie diese einfache Bestimmtheit des Eins und des Leeren zum Princip aller Dinge macht, die unendliche Mannigfaltigkeit der Welt auf diesen einfachen Gegensatz zurückführt, und sie aus ihm zu erkennen sich erkühnt, ebenso leicht ist es für das vorstellende Reflektiren, sich hier Atome und daneben das Leere vorzustellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"46.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0002","text":"Es ist daher kein Wunder, daß das atomistische Princip sich jederzeit erhalten hat; das gleich triviale und äußerliche Verhältniß der Zusammensetzung, das noch hinzukommen muß, um zum Scheine eines Konkreten und einer Mannigfaltigkeit zu gelangen, ist eben so populär als die Atome selbst und das Leere. Das Eins und das Leere ist das Fürsichseyn, das höchste qualitative Insichseyn zur völligen Äußerlichkeit herabgesunken; die Unmittelbarkeit oder das Seyn des Eins, weil es die Negation alles Andersseyns ist, ist gesetzt nicht mehr bestimmbar und veränderlich zu seyn, für dessen absolute Sprödigkeit bleibt also alle Bestimmung, Mannigfaltigkeit, Verknüpfung schlechthin äußerliche Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"46.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0003","text":"In dieser Äußerlichkeit ist jedoch das atomistische Princip nicht bei den ersten Denkern desselben geblieben, sondern es hatte außer seiner Abstraktion auch eine spekulative Bestimmung darin, daß das Leere als der Quell der Bewegung erkannt worden ist; was eine ganz andere Beziehung des Atomen und des Leeren ist, als das bloße Nebeneinander und die Gleichgültigkeit dieser beiden Bestimmungen gegeneinander. Daß das Leere der Quell der Bewegung ist, hat nicht den geringfügigen Sinn, daß sich Etwas nur in ein Leeres hineinbewegen könne, und nicht in einen schon erfüllten Raum, denn in einem solchen fände es keinen Platz mehr offen; in welchem Verstande das Leere nur die Voraussetzung oder Bedingung, nicht der Grund der Bewegung wäre, so wie auch die Bewegung selbst als vorhanden vorausgesetzt, und das Wesentliche, ein Grund derselben, vergessen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"46.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0004","text":"Die Ansicht, daß das Leere den Grund der Bewegung ausmache, enthält den tiefern Gedanken, daß im Negativen überhaupt, der Grund des Werdens, der Unruhe der Selbstbewegung liegt; in welchem Sinne aber das Negative als die wahrhafte Negativität des Unendlichen zu nehmen ist.—Das Leere ist Grund der Bewegung nur als die negative Beziehung des Eins auf sein Negatives, auf das Eins, d. i. auf sich selbst, das jedoch als Daseyendes gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"46.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0005","text":"Sonst aber sind weitere Bestimmungen der Alten über eine Gestalt, Stellung der Atome, die Richtung ihrer Bewegung willkürlich und äußerlich genug; und stehen dabei in direktem Widerspruch mit der Grundbestimmung des Atomen. An den Atomen, dem Princip der höchsten Äußerlichkeit und damit der höchsten Begrifflosigkeit, leidet die Physik in den Molecules, Partikeln ebenso sehr als die Staatswissenschaft, die von dem einzelnen Willen der Individuen ausgeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"46.5"}],"sha256":"9f398fb50ec56be97f11b669599e4baa29fd19b683811b0d74538b688ba0b1e1","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102530300337Z_67f1647e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"9f398fb50ec56be97f11b669599e4baa29fd19b683811b0d74538b688ba0b1e1","sha256":"4a0ab25463b31f4757b9cd9fd5674491d9d80880ae262408f28bbb0c69513a49","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:30.300359+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0001","text":"The One in this form of determinate being is the stage of the category which, among the ancients, appeared as the atomistic principle, according to which the essence of things is atoms and the void, (…..) Abstraction having attained to this form has acquired a greater determinacy than the Being of Parmenides and the Becoming of Heraclitus. However lofty it may set itself, by making this simple determinacy of the One and the void the principle of all things, reducing the infinite manifoldness of the world to this simple opposition, and venturing to cognize it from this, it is just as easy for representational reflection to imagine atoms here and, alongside them, the void.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"46.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0002","text":"It is therefore no wonder that the atomistic principle has maintained itself at all times; the equally trivial and external relation of composition, which must additionally enter in order to arrive at the semblance of a concrete and a manifold, is as popular as the atoms themselves and the void. The One and the void are being-for-self, the highest qualitative being-within-self, sunk down into complete externality; the immediacy or Being of the One, because it is the negation of all other-being, is posited as no longer determinable and mutable; for its absolute rigidity, therefore, every determinacy, manifoldness, connection remains an altogether external relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"46.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0003","text":"Yet the atomistic principle did not remain in this externality among its first thinkers, but besides its abstraction it also had a speculative determination in it, namely, that the void was recognized as the source of motion; which is an altogether different relation of the atom and the void from the mere juxtaposition and indifference of these two determinations toward one another. That the void is the source of motion does not have the insignificant meaning that something could move only into an empty space, and not into a space already filled, for in the latter it would no longer find an open place; in which sense the void would be only the presupposition or condition, not the ground, of motion, just as motion itself is presupposed as present, and what is essential—a ground of it—is forgotten.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"46.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0004","text":"The view that the void constitutes the ground of motion contains the deeper thought that in the negative in general lies the ground of becoming, of the unrest of self-motion; but in this sense the negative is to be taken as the true negativity of the infinite.—The void is the ground of motion only as the negative relation of the One to its negative, to the One, i.e. to itself, which, however, is posited as having determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"46.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0005","text":"Otherwise, further determinations of the ancients concerning a shape, position of the atoms, the direction of their motion, are arbitrary and external enough; and are thereby in direct contradiction with the fundamental determination of the atom. In atoms, the principle of the highest externality and hence of the highest absence of the Concept, physics suffers in molecules and particles just as much as political science, which proceeds from the individual will of individuals.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"46.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_7:P0005"]}],"source_digest":"57542ab3a79dfdf44a434819f33e8b6cc0d80851689e85a82144b3ea899f4646","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER","title":"c. Many Ones. Repulsion.","order":47,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CVER","text":"Das Eins und das Leere macht das Fürsichseyn in seinem nächsten Daseyn aus. Jedes dieser Momente hat zu seiner Bestimmung die Negation, und ist zugleich als ein Daseyn gesetzt. Nach jener ist das Eins und das Leere die Beziehung der Negation auf die Negation als eines Andern auf sein Anderes; das Eins ist die Negation in der Bestimmung des Seyns, das Leere die Negation in der Bestimmung des Nichtseyns. Aber das Eins ist wesentlich nur Beziehung auf sich als beziehende Negation d. h. ist selbst dasjenige, was das Leere außer ihm seyn soll. Beide sind aber auch gesetzt als ein affirmatives Daseyn, das eine als das Fürsichseyn als solches, das andere als unbestimmtes Daseyn überhaupt, und sich aufeinander als auf ein anderes Daseyn beziehend. Das Fürsichseyn des Eins ist jedoch wesentlich die Idealität des Daseyns und des Anderen; es bezieht sich nicht als auf ein Anderes, sondern nur auf sich. Indem aber das Fürsichseyn als Eins, als für sich Seyendes, als unmittelbar vorhandenes fixirt ist, ist seine negative Beziehung auf sich zugleich Beziehung auf ein Seyendes; und da sie eben so sehr negativ ist, bleibt das, worauf es sich bezieht, als ein Daseyn und ein Anderes bestimmt; als wesentlich Beziehung auf sich selbst, ist das Andere nicht die unbestimmte Negation, als Leeres, sondern ist gleichfalls Eins. Das Eins ist somit Werden zu vielen Eins.\n\nEigentlich ist dieß aber nicht sowohl ein Werden; denn Werden ist ein Übergehen von Seyn in Nichts; Eins hingegen wird nur zu Eins. Eins, das Bezogene enthält das Negative als Beziehung, hat dasselbe also an ihm selbst. Statt des Werdens ist also erstens die eigene immanente Beziehung des Eins vorhanden; und zweitens insofern sie negativ und das Eins seyendes zugleich ist, so stößt das Eins sich selbst von sich ab. Die negative Beziehung des Eins auf sich ist Repulsion.\n\nDiese Repulsion, so als das Setzen der vielen Eins aber durch Eins selbst ist das eigne Außersichkommen des Eins, aber zu solchen außer ihm, die selbst nur Eins sind. Es ist dieß die Repulsion dem Begriffe nach, die an sich seyende. Die zweite Repulsion ist davon unterschieden, und ist die der Vorstellung der äußern Reflexion zunächst vorschwebende, als nicht das Erzeugen der Eins, sondern nur als gegenseitiges Abhalten vorausgesetzter, schon vorhandener Eins. Es ist dann zu sehen, wie jene an sich seyende Repulsion zur zweiten, der äußerlichen, sich bestimmt.\n\nZunächst ist festzusetzen, welche Bestimmungen die vielen Eins als solche haben. Das Werden zu Vielen oder Producirtwerden der Vielen, verschwindet unmittelbar als Gesetztwerden; die Producirten sind Eins, nicht für Anderes, sondern beziehen sich unendlich auf sich selbst. Das Eins stößt nur sich von sich selbst ab, wird also nicht, sondern es ist schon; das als das Repellirte vorgestellt wird, ist gleichfalls ein Eins, ein Seyendes; Repelliren und Repellirt-werden kommt beiden auf gleiche Weise zu, und macht keinen Unterschied.\n\nDie Eins sind so vorausgesetzte gegeneinander;—gesetzte durch die Repulsion des Eins von sich selbst; voraus, gesetzt als nicht gesetzt; ihr Gesetztseyn ist aufgehoben, sie sind Seyende gegeneinander, als sich nur auf sich beziehende.\n\nDie Vielheit erscheint somit nicht als ein Andersseyn, sondern als eine dein Eins vollkommen äußere Bestimmung. Eins, indem es sich selbst repellirt, bleibt Beziehung auf sich wie das, das zunächst als repellirt genommen wird. Daß die Eins andere gegeneinander, in die Bestimmtheit der Vielheit zusammengefaßt sind, geht also die Eins nichts an. Wäre die Vielheit eine Beziehung der Eins selbst aufeinander, so begrenzten sie einander und hätten ein Seyn-für-Anderes affirmativ an ihnen. Ihre Beziehung,—und diese haben sie durch ihre an sich seyende Einheit,—wie sie hier gesetzt ist, ist als keine bestimmt; sie ist wieder das vorhingesetzte Leere. Es ist ihre aber ihnen äußerliche Grenze, in der sie nicht für einander seyn sollen. Die Grenze ist das, worin die Begrenzten eben so sehr sind als nicht sind; aber das Leere ist als das reine Nichtseyn bestimmt, und nur dieß macht ihre Grenze aus.\n\nDie Repulsion des Eins von sich selbst ist die Explikation dessen, was das Eins an sich ist; die Unendlichkeit aber als auseinander gelegt ist hier die außer sich gekommene Unendlichkeit; außer sich gekommen ist sie durch die Unmittelbarkeit des Unendlichen, des Eins. Sie ist ein ebenso einfaches Beziehen des Eins auf Eins, als vielmehr die absolute Beziehungslosigkeit der Eins; jenes nach der einfachen affirmativen Beziehung des Eins auf sich, dieses nach eben derselben als negativen. Oder die Vielheit des Eins ist das eigene Setzen des Eins; das Eins ist nichts als die negative Beziehung des Eins auf sich, und diese Beziehung, also das Eins selbst, ist das viele Eins. Aber ebenso ist die Vielheit dem Eins schlechthin äußerlich; denn das Eins ist eben das Aufheben des Andersseyns, die Repulsion ist seine Beziehung auf sich, und einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst. Die Vielheit der Eins ist die Unendlichkeit, als unbefangen sich hervorbringender Widerspruch.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0001","text":"Das Eins und das Leere macht das Fürsichseyn in seinem nächsten Daseyn aus. Jedes dieser Momente hat zu seiner Bestimmung die Negation, und ist zugleich als ein Daseyn gesetzt. Nach jener ist das Eins und das Leere die Beziehung der Negation auf die Negation als eines Andern auf sein Anderes; das Eins ist die Negation in der Bestimmung des Seyns, das Leere die Negation in der Bestimmung des Nichtseyns. Aber das Eins ist wesentlich nur Beziehung auf sich als beziehende Negation d. h. ist selbst dasjenige, was das Leere außer ihm seyn soll. Beide sind aber auch gesetzt als ein affirmatives Daseyn, das eine als das Fürsichseyn als solches, das andere als unbestimmtes Daseyn überhaupt, und sich aufeinander als auf ein anderes Daseyn beziehend.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"47.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0002","text":"Das Fürsichseyn des Eins ist jedoch wesentlich die Idealität des Daseyns und des Anderen; es bezieht sich nicht als auf ein Anderes, sondern nur auf sich. Indem aber das Fürsichseyn als Eins, als für sich Seyendes, als unmittelbar vorhandenes fixirt ist, ist seine negative Beziehung auf sich zugleich Beziehung auf ein Seyendes; und da sie eben so sehr negativ ist, bleibt das, worauf es sich bezieht, als ein Daseyn und ein Anderes bestimmt; als wesentlich Beziehung auf sich selbst, ist das Andere nicht die unbestimmte Negation, als Leeres, sondern ist gleichfalls Eins. Das Eins ist somit Werden zu vielen Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"47.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0003","text":"Eigentlich ist dieß aber nicht sowohl ein Werden; denn Werden ist ein Übergehen von Seyn in Nichts; Eins hingegen wird nur zu Eins. Eins, das Bezogene enthält das Negative als Beziehung, hat dasselbe also an ihm selbst. Statt des Werdens ist also erstens die eigene immanente Beziehung des Eins vorhanden; und zweitens insofern sie negativ und das Eins seyendes zugleich ist, so stößt das Eins sich selbst von sich ab. Die negative Beziehung des Eins auf sich ist Repulsion.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"47.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0004","text":"Diese Repulsion, so als das Setzen der vielen Eins aber durch Eins selbst ist das eigne Außersichkommen des Eins, aber zu solchen außer ihm, die selbst nur Eins sind. Es ist dieß die Repulsion dem Begriffe nach, die an sich seyende. Die zweite Repulsion ist davon unterschieden, und ist die der Vorstellung der äußern Reflexion zunächst vorschwebende, als nicht das Erzeugen der Eins, sondern nur als gegenseitiges Abhalten vorausgesetzter, schon vorhandener Eins. Es ist dann zu sehen, wie jene an sich seyende Repulsion zur zweiten, der äußerlichen, sich bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"47.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0005","text":"Zunächst ist festzusetzen, welche Bestimmungen die vielen Eins als solche haben. Das Werden zu Vielen oder Producirtwerden der Vielen, verschwindet unmittelbar als Gesetztwerden; die Producirten sind Eins, nicht für Anderes, sondern beziehen sich unendlich auf sich selbst. Das Eins stößt nur sich von sich selbst ab, wird also nicht, sondern es ist schon; das als das Repellirte vorgestellt wird, ist gleichfalls ein Eins, ein Seyendes; Repelliren und Repellirt-werden kommt beiden auf gleiche Weise zu, und macht keinen Unterschied.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"47.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0006","text":"Die Eins sind so vorausgesetzte gegeneinander;—gesetzte durch die Repulsion des Eins von sich selbst; voraus, gesetzt als nicht gesetzt; ihr Gesetztseyn ist aufgehoben, sie sind Seyende gegeneinander, als sich nur auf sich beziehende.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"47.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0007","text":"Die Vielheit erscheint somit nicht als ein Andersseyn, sondern als eine dein Eins vollkommen äußere Bestimmung. Eins, indem es sich selbst repellirt, bleibt Beziehung auf sich wie das, das zunächst als repellirt genommen wird. Daß die Eins andere gegeneinander, in die Bestimmtheit der Vielheit zusammengefaßt sind, geht also die Eins nichts an. Wäre die Vielheit eine Beziehung der Eins selbst aufeinander, so begrenzten sie einander und hätten ein Seyn-für-Anderes affirmativ an ihnen. Ihre Beziehung,—und diese haben sie durch ihre an sich seyende Einheit,—wie sie hier gesetzt ist, ist als keine bestimmt; sie ist wieder das vorhingesetzte Leere. Es ist ihre aber ihnen äußerliche Grenze, in der sie nicht für einander seyn sollen. Die Grenze ist das, worin die Begrenzten eben so sehr sind als nicht sind; aber das Leere ist als das reine Nichtseyn bestimmt, und nur dieß macht ihre Grenze aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"47.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0008","text":"Die Repulsion des Eins von sich selbst ist die Explikation dessen, was das Eins an sich ist; die Unendlichkeit aber als auseinander gelegt ist hier die außer sich gekommene Unendlichkeit; außer sich gekommen ist sie durch die Unmittelbarkeit des Unendlichen, des Eins. Sie ist ein ebenso einfaches Beziehen des Eins auf Eins, als vielmehr die absolute Beziehungslosigkeit der Eins; jenes nach der einfachen affirmativen Beziehung des Eins auf sich, dieses nach eben derselben als negativen. Oder die Vielheit des Eins ist das eigene Setzen des Eins; das Eins ist nichts als die negative Beziehung des Eins auf sich, und diese Beziehung, also das Eins selbst, ist das viele Eins. Aber ebenso ist die Vielheit dem Eins schlechthin äußerlich; denn das Eins ist eben das Aufheben des Andersseyns, die Repulsion ist seine Beziehung auf sich, und einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"47.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0009","text":"Die Vielheit der Eins ist die Unendlichkeit, als unbefangen sich hervorbringender Widerspruch.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"47.9"}],"sha256":"e7dc7e97d74f5de97127233cdb6de51265d051375efbf10b3206b78bfa8b79ee","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102540965164Z_a187dbf4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Many Ones. Repulsion.","source_sha256":"e7dc7e97d74f5de97127233cdb6de51265d051375efbf10b3206b78bfa8b79ee","sha256":"e7f08b2e1a8b6115121582837a4a664b5c6d4d94f4d53c47e974c3a6ca19dff2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:40.965201+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0001","text":"The One and the Void constitute being-for-self in its immediate existence. Each of these moments has negation as its determination, and is at the same time posited as an existence. According to the former, the One and the Void are the relation of negation to negation as of one other to its other; the One is negation in the determination of being, the Void negation in the determination of non-being. But the One is essentially only relation to itself as relating negation, i.e. is itself that which the Void outside it is supposed to be. Yet both are also posited as an affirmative existence, the one as being-for-self as such, the other as indeterminate existence in general, and as relating to one another as to another existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"47.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0002","text":"The being-for-self of the One, however, is essentially the ideality of existence and of the Other; it relates not as to an Other, but only to itself. But inasmuch as being-for-self is fixed as One, as being for itself, as immediately present, its negative relation to itself is at the same time relation to a being; and since it is equally negative, that to which it relates remains determined as an existence and an Other; as essentially relation to itself, the Other is not indeterminate negation, as Void, but is likewise One. The One is thus becoming into many Ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"47.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0003","text":"Properly speaking, however, this is not so much a becoming; for becoming is a transition from being into nothing; the One, on the contrary, becomes only One. One, that which relates, contains the negative as relation, thus has it in itself. Therefore, in place of becoming, there is firstly the One's own immanent relation; and secondly, insofar as it is negative and the One at the same time is being, the One repels itself from itself. The negative relation of the One to itself is repulsion.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"47.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0004","text":"This repulsion, however, as the positing of the many Ones by the One itself, is the One's own going-outside-itself, but to such as are outside it and are themselves only Ones. This is repulsion according to the Concept, repulsion existing in itself. The second repulsion is distinct from this, and is that which first presents itself to the representation of external reflection, not as the production of the Ones, but only as the mutual holding-apart of presupposed, already existing Ones. It is then to be seen how that repulsion existing in itself determines itself into the second, the external one.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"47.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0005","text":"First, it must be established what determinations the many Ones have as such. Becoming into many, or the being-produced of the many, immediately vanishes as being-posited; those produced are Ones, not for an Other, but relate infinitely to themselves. The One repels only itself from itself, thus does not become, but already is; that which is represented as repelled is likewise a One, a being; repelling and being-repelled pertain to both in the same way, and make no difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"47.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0006","text":"The Ones are thus presupposed over against one another;—posited through the One's repulsion of itself; presupposed, posited as not posited; their being-posited is sublated, they are beings over against one another, as relating only to themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"47.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0007","text":"Multiplicity thus appears not as an other-being, but as a determination wholly external to the One. The One, in repelling itself, remains relation to itself, as does that which is initially taken as repelled. That the Ones are others over against one another, combined into the determinacy of multiplicity, therefore does not concern the Ones. If multiplicity were a relation of the Ones themselves to one another, they would limit one another and would have being-for-another affirmatively in them. Their relation—and they have this through their unity in itself—as it is posited here, is determined as none; it is again the Void posited above. It is their, yet external to them, limit, in which they are not to be for one another. The limit is that in which the limited equally are and are not; but the Void is determined as pure non-being, and this alone constitutes their limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"47.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0008","text":"The One's repulsion of itself is the explication of what the One is in itself; but infinity, as laid out asunder, is here infinity that has gone outside itself; it has gone outside itself through the immediacy of the infinite, of the One. It is as much a simple relating of One to One as it is the absolute relationlessness of the Ones; the former according to the simple affirmative relation of the One to itself, the latter according to precisely the same relation as negative. Or the multiplicity of the Ones is the One's own positing; the One is nothing but the negative relation of the One to itself, and this relation, hence the One itself, is the many Ones. But likewise multiplicity is absolutely external to the One; for the One is precisely the sublation of other-being, repulsion is its relation to itself, and simple equality with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"47.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVER:P0009","text":"The multiplicity of the Ones is infinity, as contradiction producing itself unimpededly.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"47.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVER:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"2cf711e1916ea4cf16aad410f86b7cd6cf320d67063f8eaf38a997533519a5be","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Viele Eins. Repulsion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Viele Eins. Repulsion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_8","title":"Remark.","order":48,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_8","text":"Es ist vorhin des leibnitzischen Idealismus erwähnt worden. Es kann hier hinzugesetzt werden, daß derselbe von der vorstellenden Monade aus, die als Fürsichseyende bestimmt ist, nur bis zu der so eben betrachteten Repulsion fortging, und zwar nur zu der Vielheit als solcher, in der die Eins jedes nur für sich, gleichgültig gegen das Daseyn und Für-sich-seyn anderer ist, oder überhaupt Andere gar nicht für das Eins sind. Die Monade ist für sich die ganze abgeschlossene Welt; es bedarf keine der andern; aber diese innere Mannigfaltigkeit, die sie in ihrem Vorstellen hat, ändert in ihrer Bestimmung, für sich zu seyn, nichts. Der Leibnitzische Idealismus nimmt die Vielheit unmittelbar als eine gegebene auf, und begreift sie nicht als eine Repulsion der Monade; er hat daher die Vielheit nur nach der Seite ihrer abstrakten Äußerlichkeit. Die Atomistik hat den Begriff der Idealität nicht; sie faßt das Eins nicht als ein solches, das in ihm selbst die beiden Momente des Fürsichseyns und des Für-es-seyns enthält, also als ideelles, sondern nur als einfach, trocken Für-sich-seyendes. Aber sie geht über die bloß gleichgültige Vielheit hinaus; die Atomen kommen in eine weitere Bestimmung gegeneinander, wenn auch eigentlich auf inkonsequente Weise; da hingegen in jener gleichgültigen Unabhängigkeit der Monaden, die Vielheit als starre Grundbestimmung bleibt, so daß ihre Beziehung nur in die Monade der Monaden, oder in den betrachtenden Philosophen fällt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_8:P0001","text":"Es ist vorhin des leibnitzischen Idealismus erwähnt worden. Es kann hier hinzugesetzt werden, daß derselbe von der vorstellenden Monade aus, die als Fürsichseyende bestimmt ist, nur bis zu der so eben betrachteten Repulsion fortging, und zwar nur zu der Vielheit als solcher, in der die Eins jedes nur für sich, gleichgültig gegen das Daseyn und Für-sich-seyn anderer ist, oder überhaupt Andere gar nicht für das Eins sind. Die Monade ist für sich die ganze abgeschlossene Welt; es bedarf keine der andern; aber diese innere Mannigfaltigkeit, die sie in ihrem Vorstellen hat, ändert in ihrer Bestimmung, für sich zu seyn, nichts. Der Leibnitzische Idealismus nimmt die Vielheit unmittelbar als eine gegebene auf, und begreift sie nicht als eine Repulsion der Monade; er hat daher die Vielheit nur nach der Seite ihrer abstrakten Äußerlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"48.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_8:P0002","text":"Die Atomistik hat den Begriff der Idealität nicht; sie faßt das Eins nicht als ein solches, das in ihm selbst die beiden Momente des Fürsichseyns und des Für-es-seyns enthält, also als ideelles, sondern nur als einfach, trocken Für-sich-seyendes. Aber sie geht über die bloß gleichgültige Vielheit hinaus; die Atomen kommen in eine weitere Bestimmung gegeneinander, wenn auch eigentlich auf inkonsequente Weise; da hingegen in jener gleichgültigen Unabhängigkeit der Monaden, die Vielheit als starre Grundbestimmung bleibt, so daß ihre Beziehung nur in die Monade der Monaden, oder in den betrachtenden Philosophen fällt.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"48.2"}],"sha256":"ff3311486db746e0b5e508d2fad8249d7e54961dc11661086daca6e3d7c455fd","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102545863077Z_ed5a224a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"ff3311486db746e0b5e508d2fad8249d7e54961dc11661086daca6e3d7c455fd","sha256":"ab56f6a08b25407b6cea8d79ddf7559fea43c277bcc60e79c942bcb9267009d9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:45.863100+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_8:P0001","text":"Leibnizian idealism was mentioned above. It may be added here that, starting from the representing monad, which is determined as being-for-self, it proceeded only as far as the repulsion just considered, and indeed only to plurality as such, in which the ones are each only for themselves, indifferent to the being-there and being-for-self of others, or in general others are not at all for the one. The monad is, for itself, the whole self-enclosed world; it needs none of the others; but this inner manifoldness which it has in its representation changes nothing in its determination to be for itself. Leibnizian idealism immediately takes plurality as something given, and does not comprehend it as a repulsion of the monad; it therefore has plurality only from the side of its abstract externality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"48.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_8:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_8:P0002","text":"Atomism does not have the concept of ideality; it does not grasp the one as such a one as contains within itself the two moments of being-for-self and being-for-it, hence as ideal, but only as simple, dry being-for-self. Yet it goes beyond merely indifferent plurality; the atoms enter into a further determination with respect to one another, though properly speaking in an inconsistent manner; whereas in that indifferent independence of the monads, plurality remains the rigid fundamental determination, so that their relation falls only into the monad of monads, or into the contemplating philosopher.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"48.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_8:P0002"]}],"source_digest":"e83b3a9944d898e90a58fdfe56ec2ee94c971d9cc91799bd47f43e7246cb0d46","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0","title":"a. Exclusion of the One.","order":49,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ADE0","text":"## C. Repulsion und Attraktion.\n\n## a. Ausschließen des Eins.\n\nDie vielen Eins sind Seyende; ihr Daseyn oder Beziehung aufeinander ist Nicht-Beziehung, sie ist ihnen äußerlich;—das abstrakte Leere. Aber sie selbst sind diese negative Beziehung auf sich nun als auf seyende Andere;—der aufgezeigte Widerspruch, die Unendlichkeit, gesetzt in Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns. Hiermit findet nun die Repulsion das unmittelbar vor, was von ihr repellirt ist. Sie ist in dieser Bestimmung Ausschließen; das Eins repellirt nur die Vielen von ihm unerzeugten, nichtgesetzten Eins von sich. dieß Repelliren ist, gegenseitig oder allseitig,—relativ, durch das Seyn der Eins beschränkt.\n\nDie Vielheit ist zunächst nicht gesetztes Andersseyn; die Grenze nur das Leere, nur das, worin die Eins nicht sind. Aber sie sind auch in der Grenze; sie sind im Leeren, oder ihre Repulsion ist ihre gemeinsame Beziehung. Diese gegenseitige Repulsion ist das gesetzte Daseyn der vielen Eins; sie ist nicht ihr Fürsichseyn, nach dem sie nur in einem Dritten als Vieles unterschieden wären, sondern ihr eigenes sie erhaltendes Unterscheiden.—Sie negiren sich gegenseitig, setzen einander als solche, die nur für-Eines sind. Aber sie negiren eben so sehr zugleich dieß, nur für-Eines zu seyn; sie repelliren diese ihre Idealität und sind.—So sind die Momente getrennt, die in der Idealität schlechthin vereinigt sind. Das Eins ist in seinem Fürsichseyn auch für-Eines, aber dieß Eine, für welches es ist, ist es selbst; sein Unterscheiden von sich ist unmittelbar aufgehoben. Aber in der Vielheit hat das unterschiedne Eins ein Seyn; das Seyn-für-Eines, wie es in dem Ausschließen bestimmt ist, ist daher ein Seyn-für-Anderes. Jedes wird so von einem Andern repellirt, aufgehoben und zu einem gemacht, das nicht für sich, sondern für-eines und zwar ein anderes Eins ist.\n\nDas Fürsichseyn der vielen Eins zeigt sich hiernach als ihre Selbsterhaltung, durch die Vermittelung ihrer Repulsion gegeneinander, in der sie sich gegenseitig aufheben, und die anderen als ein bloßes Seyn-für-Anderes setzen; aber zugleich besteht sie darin, diese Idealität zu repelliren, und die Eins zu setzen, nicht für-ein-Anderes zu seyn. Diese Selbsterhaltung der Eins durch ihre negative Beziehung auf einander ist aber vielmehr ihre Auflösung.\n\nDie Eins sind nicht nur, sondern sie erhalten sich durch ihr gegenseitiges Ausschließen. Erstens ist nun das, wodurch sie den festen Halt ihrer Verschiedenheit gegen ihr Negirtwerden haben sollten, ihr Seyn, und zwar ihr Ansichseyn gegen ihre Beziehung auf-Anderes; dieß Ansichseyn ist, daß sie Eins sind. Aber dieß sind Alle; sie sind in ihrem Ansichseyn dasselbe, statt darin den festen Punkt ihrer Verschiedenheit zu haben. Zweitens ihr Daseyn und ihr Verhalten zu einander, d. i. ihr Sich selbst als Eins setzen, ist das gegenseitige Negiren; dieß ist aber gleichfalls eine und dieselbe Bestimmung Aller, durch welche sie sich also vielmehr als identisch setzen; wie dadurch, daß sie an sich dasselbe sind, ihre als durch Andere zu setzende Idealität ihre eigene ist, welche sie also ebenso wenig repelliren.—Sie sind hiermit ihrem Seyn und Setzen nach nur Eine affirmative Einheit.\n\nDiese Betrachtung der Eins, daß sie nach ihren beiden Bestimmungen sowohl, insofern sie sind, als insofern sie sich aufeinander beziehen, sich nur als ein und dasselbe und ihre Ununterscheidbarkeit zeigen, ist unsere Vergleichung.—Es ist aber auch zu sehen, was in ihrer Beziehung aufeinander selbst gesetzt an ihnen ist.—Sie sind, dieß ist in dieser Beziehung vorausgesetzt,—und sind nur insofern sie sich gegenseitig negiren, und diese ihre Idealität, ihr Negirtseyn zugleich von sich selbst abhalten, d. i. das gegenseitige Negiren negiren. Aber sie sind nur insofern sie negiren, so wird, indem dieß ihr Negiren negirt wird, ihr Seyn negirt. Zwar indem sie sind, würden sie durch dieß Negiren nicht negirt, es ist nur ein Äußerliches für sie; dieß Negiren des Anderen prallt an ihnen ab, und trifft nur berührend ihre Oberfläche. Allein nur durch das Negiren der Anderen kehren sie in sich selbst zurück; sie sind nur als diese Vermittelung, diese ihre Rückkehr ist ihre Selbsterhaltung und ihr Fürsichseyn. Indem ihr Negiren nichts effektuirt, durch den Widerstand, den die Seyenden als solche oder als negirend leisten, so kehren sie nicht in sich zurück, erhalten sich nicht und sind nicht.\n\nVorhin wurde die Betrachtung gemacht, daß die Eins dasselbe, jedes derselben Eins ist, wie das Andere. Dieß ist nicht nur unser Beziehen, ein äußerliches Zusammenbringen; sondern die Repulsion ist selbst Beziehen; das die Eins ausschließende Eins bezieht sich selbst auf sie, die Eins, d. h. auf sich selbst. Das negative Verhalten der Eins zu einander ist somit nur ein Mit-sich-zusammengehen. Diese Identität, in welche ihr Repelliren übergeht, ist das Aufheben ihrer Verschiedenheit und Äußerlichkeit, die sie vielmehr gegeneinander als Ausschließende behaupten sollten.\n\nDieß sich in-Ein-Eines-setzen der vielen Eins ist die Attraktion.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0001","text":"## C. Repulsion und Attraktion.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"49.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0002","text":"## a. Ausschließen des Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"49.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0003","text":"Die vielen Eins sind Seyende; ihr Daseyn oder Beziehung aufeinander ist Nicht-Beziehung, sie ist ihnen äußerlich;—das abstrakte Leere. Aber sie selbst sind diese negative Beziehung auf sich nun als auf seyende Andere;—der aufgezeigte Widerspruch, die Unendlichkeit, gesetzt in Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns. Hiermit findet nun die Repulsion das unmittelbar vor, was von ihr repellirt ist. Sie ist in dieser Bestimmung Ausschließen; das Eins repellirt nur die Vielen von ihm unerzeugten, nichtgesetzten Eins von sich. dieß Repelliren ist, gegenseitig oder allseitig,—relativ, durch das Seyn der Eins beschränkt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"49.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0004","text":"Die Vielheit ist zunächst nicht gesetztes Andersseyn; die Grenze nur das Leere, nur das, worin die Eins nicht sind. Aber sie sind auch in der Grenze; sie sind im Leeren, oder ihre Repulsion ist ihre gemeinsame Beziehung. Diese gegenseitige Repulsion ist das gesetzte Daseyn der vielen Eins; sie ist nicht ihr Fürsichseyn, nach dem sie nur in einem Dritten als Vieles unterschieden wären, sondern ihr eigenes sie erhaltendes Unterscheiden.—Sie negiren sich gegenseitig, setzen einander als solche, die nur für-Eines sind. Aber sie negiren eben so sehr zugleich dieß, nur für-Eines zu seyn; sie repelliren diese ihre Idealität und sind.—So sind die Momente getrennt, die in der Idealität schlechthin vereinigt sind. Das Eins ist in seinem Fürsichseyn auch für-Eines, aber dieß Eine, für welches es ist, ist es selbst; sein Unterscheiden von sich ist unmittelbar aufgehoben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"49.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0005","text":"Aber in der Vielheit hat das unterschiedne Eins ein Seyn; das Seyn-für-Eines, wie es in dem Ausschließen bestimmt ist, ist daher ein Seyn-für-Anderes. Jedes wird so von einem Andern repellirt, aufgehoben und zu einem gemacht, das nicht für sich, sondern für-eines und zwar ein anderes Eins ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"49.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0006","text":"Das Fürsichseyn der vielen Eins zeigt sich hiernach als ihre Selbsterhaltung, durch die Vermittelung ihrer Repulsion gegeneinander, in der sie sich gegenseitig aufheben, und die anderen als ein bloßes Seyn-für-Anderes setzen; aber zugleich besteht sie darin, diese Idealität zu repelliren, und die Eins zu setzen, nicht für-ein-Anderes zu seyn. Diese Selbsterhaltung der Eins durch ihre negative Beziehung auf einander ist aber vielmehr ihre Auflösung.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"49.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0007","text":"Die Eins sind nicht nur, sondern sie erhalten sich durch ihr gegenseitiges Ausschließen. Erstens ist nun das, wodurch sie den festen Halt ihrer Verschiedenheit gegen ihr Negirtwerden haben sollten, ihr Seyn, und zwar ihr Ansichseyn gegen ihre Beziehung auf-Anderes; dieß Ansichseyn ist, daß sie Eins sind. Aber dieß sind Alle; sie sind in ihrem Ansichseyn dasselbe, statt darin den festen Punkt ihrer Verschiedenheit zu haben. Zweitens ihr Daseyn und ihr Verhalten zu einander, d. i. ihr Sich selbst als Eins setzen, ist das gegenseitige Negiren; dieß ist aber gleichfalls eine und dieselbe Bestimmung Aller, durch welche sie sich also vielmehr als identisch setzen; wie dadurch, daß sie an sich dasselbe sind, ihre als durch Andere zu setzende Idealität ihre eigene ist, welche sie also ebenso wenig repelliren.—Sie sind hiermit ihrem Seyn und Setzen nach nur Eine affirmative Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"49.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0008","text":"Diese Betrachtung der Eins, daß sie nach ihren beiden Bestimmungen sowohl, insofern sie sind, als insofern sie sich aufeinander beziehen, sich nur als ein und dasselbe und ihre Ununterscheidbarkeit zeigen, ist unsere Vergleichung.—Es ist aber auch zu sehen, was in ihrer Beziehung aufeinander selbst gesetzt an ihnen ist.—Sie sind, dieß ist in dieser Beziehung vorausgesetzt,—und sind nur insofern sie sich gegenseitig negiren, und diese ihre Idealität, ihr Negirtseyn zugleich von sich selbst abhalten, d. i. das gegenseitige Negiren negiren. Aber sie sind nur insofern sie negiren, so wird, indem dieß ihr Negiren negirt wird, ihr Seyn negirt. Zwar indem sie sind, würden sie durch dieß Negiren nicht negirt, es ist nur ein Äußerliches für sie; dieß Negiren des Anderen prallt an ihnen ab, und trifft nur berührend ihre Oberfläche.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"49.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0009","text":"Allein nur durch das Negiren der Anderen kehren sie in sich selbst zurück; sie sind nur als diese Vermittelung, diese ihre Rückkehr ist ihre Selbsterhaltung und ihr Fürsichseyn. Indem ihr Negiren nichts effektuirt, durch den Widerstand, den die Seyenden als solche oder als negirend leisten, so kehren sie nicht in sich zurück, erhalten sich nicht und sind nicht.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"49.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0010","text":"Vorhin wurde die Betrachtung gemacht, daß die Eins dasselbe, jedes derselben Eins ist, wie das Andere. Dieß ist nicht nur unser Beziehen, ein äußerliches Zusammenbringen; sondern die Repulsion ist selbst Beziehen; das die Eins ausschließende Eins bezieht sich selbst auf sie, die Eins, d. h. auf sich selbst. Das negative Verhalten der Eins zu einander ist somit nur ein Mit-sich-zusammengehen. Diese Identität, in welche ihr Repelliren übergeht, ist das Aufheben ihrer Verschiedenheit und Äußerlichkeit, die sie vielmehr gegeneinander als Ausschließende behaupten sollten.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"49.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0011","text":"Dieß sich in-Ein-Eines-setzen der vielen Eins ist die Attraktion.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"49.11"}],"sha256":"9abcbd92e42cd98ead3a26f815888131d380d71859c86cc82ccb1abb1dfc8d10","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102558143557Z_5b60bcd7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Exclusion of the One.","source_sha256":"9abcbd92e42cd98ead3a26f815888131d380d71859c86cc82ccb1abb1dfc8d10","sha256":"24b1db7a7d51fcfbcf73d37c18c6473e116feff3df812c98a534b5db0e638fcb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:25:58.143596+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0001","text":"## C. Repulsion and Attraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"49.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0002","text":"## a. Excluding the One.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"49.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0003","text":"The many Ones are beings; their existence or relation to one another is non-relation, it is external to them;—abstract emptiness. But they themselves are now this negative relation to themselves as to being Others;—the contradiction indicated, infinity, posited in the immediacy of Being. Thus repulsion now finds immediately before it that which is repelled by it. In this determination it is exclusion; the One repels from itself only the many Ones not generated by it, not posited. This repelling is reciprocal, or in all directions,—relative, limited by the Being of the Ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"49.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0004","text":"Multiplicity is at first not posited otherness; the limit is only the empty, only that in which the Ones are not. But they are also in the limit; they are in the empty, or their repulsion is their common relation. This reciprocal repulsion is the posited existence of the many Ones; it is not their being-for-self, according to which they would be distinguished as Many only in a Third, but their own distinction that preserves them.—They mutually negate themselves, posit one another as such as are only for-One. But they just as much simultaneously negate this, being only for-One; they repel this their ideality and are.—Thus the moments are separated which in ideality are absolutely united. The One is in its being-for-self also for-One, but this One for which it is, is itself; its distinguishing itself from itself is immediately sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"49.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0005","text":"But in multiplicity the distinguished One has a Being; being-for-One, as it is determined in exclusion, is therefore a being-for-Other. Each is thus repelled by another, sublated and made into one which is not for itself, but for-one, and indeed another One.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"49.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0006","text":"The being-for-self of the many Ones accordingly shows itself as their self-preservation, through the mediation of their repulsion against one another, in which they mutually sublate themselves and posit the others as a mere being-for-Other; but at the same time it consists in repelling this ideality and positing the Ones not to be for-an-Other. This self-preservation of the Ones through their negative relation to one another is, however, rather their dissolution.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"49.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0007","text":"The Ones are not merely, but preserve themselves through their reciprocal exclusion. Firstly, then, that through which they ought to have the firm support of their difference against their being negated is their Being, namely their being-in-itself as against their relation-to-Other; this being-in-itself is that they are Ones. But all are this; in their being-in-itself they are the same, instead of having therein the fixed point of their difference. Secondly, their existence and their comportment toward one another, i.e. their positing themselves as Ones, is reciprocal negating; but this likewise is one and the same determination of all, through which they thus rather posit themselves as identical; just as, through the fact that they are the same in themselves, their ideality, which is to be posited through Others, is their own, which they therefore just as little repel.—They are thereby, according to their Being and positing, only one affirmative unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"49.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0008","text":"This consideration of the Ones, that according to both their determinations, both insofar as they are and insofar as they relate to one another, they show themselves only as one and the same and in their indistinguishability, is our comparison.—But it must also be seen what is posited in them in their relation to one another itself.—They are, this is presupposed in this relation,—and are only insofar as they mutually negate one another and at the same time keep this their ideality, their being-negated, away from themselves, i.e. negate reciprocal negating. But they are only insofar as they negate; thus, when this their negating is negated, their Being is negated. To be sure, insofar as they are, they would not be negated by this negating; it is only something external for them; this negating of the Other rebounds from them and touches only their surface.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"49.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0009","text":"Yet only through negating the Others do they return into themselves; they are only as this mediation, this their return is their self-preservation and their being-for-self. Since their negating effects nothing, through the resistance which beings as such or as negating offer, they do not return into themselves, do not preserve themselves, and are not.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"49.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0010","text":"Previously the consideration was made that the Ones are the same, each of them a One, like the Other. This is not merely our relating, an external bringing-together; rather, repulsion is itself relating; the One which excludes the Ones relates itself to them, the Ones, i.e. to itself. The negative comportment of the Ones toward one another is thus only a coming-together-with-itself. This identity, into which their repelling passes over, is the sublation of their difference and externality, which they were rather supposed to maintain against one another as excluding.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"49.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0011","text":"This positing-themselves-into-One-One of the many Ones is attraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"49.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ADE0:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"7426d2aaf36f71368bcee5247f2306d68a5d242b245607c3b41dc96574a9597c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Ausschließen des Eins."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Ausschließen des Eins.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9","title":"Remark.","order":50,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_AN_9","text":"Die Selbstständigkeit auf die Spitze des fürsichseyenden Eins getrieben, ist die abstrakte, formelle Selbstständigkeit, die sich selbst zerstört; der höchste, hartnäckigste Irrthum, der sich für die höchste Wahrheit nimmt;—in konkreteren Formen als abstrakte Freiheit, als reines Ich, und dann weiter als das Böse erscheinend. Es ist die Freiheit, die sich so vergreift, ihr Wesen in diese Abstraktion zu setzen, und in diesem Bei-sich-seyn sich schmeichelt, sich rein zu gewinnen. Diese Selbstständigkeit ist bestimmter der Irrthum, das als negativ anzusehen und sich gegen das als negativ zu verhalten, was ihr eignes Wesen ist. Sie ist so das negative Verhalten gegen sich selbst, welches, indem es sein eigenes Seyn gewinnen will, dasselbe zerstört, und dieß sein Thun ist nur die Manifestation der Nichtigkeit dieses Thuns. Die Versöhnung ist die Anerkennung dessen, gegen welches das negative Verhalten geht, vielmehr als seines Wesens, und ist nur als Ablassen von der Negativität seines Fürsichseyns, statt an ihm festzuhalten.\n\nEs ist ein alter Satz, daß das Eine Vieles und insbesondere: daß das Viele Eines ist. Es ist hierüber die Bemerkung zu wiederholen, daß die Wahrheit des Eins und des Vielen in Sätzen ausgedrückt in einer unangemessenen Form erscheint, daß diese Wahrheit nur als ein Werden, als ein Proceß, Repulsion und Attraktion, nicht als das Seyn, wie es in einem Satze als ruhige Einheit gesetzt ist, zu fassen und auszudrücken ist. Es ist oben der Dialektik Plato's im Parmenides über die Ableitung des Vielen aus dem Eins, nämlich aus dem Satze: Eines ist, erwähnt und erinnert worden. Die innere Dialektik des Begriffes ist angegeben worden; am leichtesten ist die Dialektik des Satzes, daß Vieles Eines ist, als äußerliche Reflexion zu fassen; und äußerlich darf sie hier seyn, insofern auch der Gegenstand, die Vielen, das einander Äußerliche ist. Diese Vergleichung der Vielen miteinander ergiebt sogleich, daß eines schlechthin nur bestimmt ist wie das Andere; jedes ist Eins, jedes ist Eins der Vielen, ist ausschließend die Anderen;—so daß sie schlechthin nur dasselbe sind, schlechthin nur Eine Bestimmung vorhanden ist. Es ist dieß das Faktum, und es ist nur darum zu thun, dieß einfache Faktum aufzufassen. Die Hartnäckigkeit des Verstandes weigert sich nur darum gegen dieses Auffassen, weil ihm auch der Unterschied, und zwar mit Recht, vorschwebt; aber dieser bleibt um jenes Faktums willen so wenig aus, als gewiß jenes Faktum ungeachtet des Unterschiedes existirt. Man könnte den Verstand damit für das schlichte Auffassen des Faktums der Einheit gleichsam trösten, daß der Unterschied auch wieder eintreten werde.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0001","text":"Die Selbstständigkeit auf die Spitze des fürsichseyenden Eins getrieben, ist die abstrakte, formelle Selbstständigkeit, die sich selbst zerstört; der höchste, hartnäckigste Irrthum, der sich für die höchste Wahrheit nimmt;—in konkreteren Formen als abstrakte Freiheit, als reines Ich, und dann weiter als das Böse erscheinend. Es ist die Freiheit, die sich so vergreift, ihr Wesen in diese Abstraktion zu setzen, und in diesem Bei-sich-seyn sich schmeichelt, sich rein zu gewinnen. Diese Selbstständigkeit ist bestimmter der Irrthum, das als negativ anzusehen und sich gegen das als negativ zu verhalten, was ihr eignes Wesen ist. Sie ist so das negative Verhalten gegen sich selbst, welches, indem es sein eigenes Seyn gewinnen will, dasselbe zerstört, und dieß sein Thun ist nur die Manifestation der Nichtigkeit dieses Thuns.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"50.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0002","text":"Die Versöhnung ist die Anerkennung dessen, gegen welches das negative Verhalten geht, vielmehr als seines Wesens, und ist nur als Ablassen von der Negativität seines Fürsichseyns, statt an ihm festzuhalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"50.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0003","text":"Es ist ein alter Satz, daß das Eine Vieles und insbesondere: daß das Viele Eines ist. Es ist hierüber die Bemerkung zu wiederholen, daß die Wahrheit des Eins und des Vielen in Sätzen ausgedrückt in einer unangemessenen Form erscheint, daß diese Wahrheit nur als ein Werden, als ein Proceß, Repulsion und Attraktion, nicht als das Seyn, wie es in einem Satze als ruhige Einheit gesetzt ist, zu fassen und auszudrücken ist. Es ist oben der Dialektik Plato's im Parmenides über die Ableitung des Vielen aus dem Eins, nämlich aus dem Satze: Eines ist, erwähnt und erinnert worden. Die innere Dialektik des Begriffes ist angegeben worden; am leichtesten ist die Dialektik des Satzes, daß Vieles Eines ist, als äußerliche Reflexion zu fassen; und äußerlich darf sie hier seyn, insofern auch der Gegenstand, die Vielen, das einander Äußerliche ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"50.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0004","text":"Diese Vergleichung der Vielen miteinander ergiebt sogleich, daß eines schlechthin nur bestimmt ist wie das Andere; jedes ist Eins, jedes ist Eins der Vielen, ist ausschließend die Anderen;—so daß sie schlechthin nur dasselbe sind, schlechthin nur Eine Bestimmung vorhanden ist. Es ist dieß das Faktum, und es ist nur darum zu thun, dieß einfache Faktum aufzufassen. Die Hartnäckigkeit des Verstandes weigert sich nur darum gegen dieses Auffassen, weil ihm auch der Unterschied, und zwar mit Recht, vorschwebt; aber dieser bleibt um jenes Faktums willen so wenig aus, als gewiß jenes Faktum ungeachtet des Unterschiedes existirt. Man könnte den Verstand damit für das schlichte Auffassen des Faktums der Einheit gleichsam trösten, daß der Unterschied auch wieder eintreten werde.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"50.4"}],"sha256":"fd308a65c1e24c7ed34332d18d100e42978dfe72162be06c6274857870d08ce7","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102607499979Z_d1d54dbb","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"fd308a65c1e24c7ed34332d18d100e42978dfe72162be06c6274857870d08ce7","sha256":"7ecdca9cf960be1de2b15e36f1d9ed1c6f4a87d1536e4a6da2cb06cb208ad26e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:26:07.500016+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0001","text":"Self-subsistence carried to the extreme of the One that is for itself is abstract, formal self-subsistence, which destroys itself; the highest, most obstinate error, which takes itself for the highest truth;—appearing in more concrete forms as abstract freedom, as the pure I, and then further as evil. It is freedom which thus mistakes itself in placing its essence in this abstraction, and flatters itself, in this being-with-self, that it attains itself purely. This self-subsistence is, more determinately, the error of regarding as negative, and comporting itself negatively toward, that which is its own essence. It is thus the negative comportment toward itself which, in seeking to gain its own being, destroys it, and this its doing is merely the manifestation of the nullity of this doing.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"50.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0002","text":"Reconciliation is the recognition of that against which the negative comportment is directed, rather as its essence, and consists only in relinquishing the negativity of its being-for-self, instead of holding fast to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"50.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0003","text":"It is an old proposition that the One is Many and, in particular, that the Many is One. With regard to this, the observation is to be repeated that the truth of the One and the Many, expressed in propositions, appears in an inadequate form; that this truth is to be grasped and expressed only as a becoming, as a process, repulsion and attraction, not as being, as it is posited in a proposition as a tranquil unity. Above, Plato's dialectic in the Parmenides concerning the derivation of the Many from the One, namely from the proposition: One is, has been mentioned and recalled. The inner dialectic of the Concept has been indicated; most easily, the dialectic of the proposition that Many is One may be grasped as external reflection; and it may here be external, insofar as the object too, the Many, is what is external to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"50.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0004","text":"This comparison of the Many with one another immediately yields that one is determined absolutely only like the other; each is One, each is one of the Many, excluding the others;—so that they are absolutely only the same, and absolutely only one determination is present. This is the fact, and the point is only to apprehend this simple fact. The obstinacy of the Understanding refuses this apprehension only because difference too, and indeed rightly, hovers before it; but for the sake of that fact difference no more fails to remain than that fact certainly exists notwithstanding the difference. One might, as it were, console the Understanding for the simple apprehension of the fact of unity by saying that difference too will again enter.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"50.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_AN_9:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"e31b168ac47f3817d8c6f3514f8a9c26452c6aeff21572b64d1a9879ac58b2ed","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE","title":"b. The One One of Attraction.","order":51,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDEE","text":"Die Repulsion ist die Selbstzersplitterung des Eins zunächst in Viele, deren negatives Verhalten unmächtig ist, weil sie einander als Seyende voraussetzen; sie ist nur das Sollen der Idealität; diese aber wird realisirt in der Attraktion. Die Repulsion geht in Attraktion über, die vielen Eins in Ein Eins. Beide, Repulsion und Attraktion, sind\n\nzunächst unterschieden, jene als die Realität der Eins, diese als deren gesetzte Idealität. Die Attraktion bezieht sich auf diese Weise auf die Repulsion, daß sie diese zur Voraussetzung hat. Die Repulsion liefert die Materie für die Attraktion. Wenn keine Eins wären, so wäre nichts zu attrahiren; die Vorstellung fortdauernder Attraktion, der Konsumtion der Eins, setzt ein ebenso fortdauerndes Erzeugen der Eins voraus; die sinnliche Vorstellung der räumlichen Attraktion läßt den Strom der attrahirt-werdenden Eins fortdauern; an die Stelle der Atome, die in dem attrahirenden Punkte verschwinden, tritt eine andere Menge, und wenn man will, ins Unendliche, aus dem Leeren hervor. Wenn die Attraktion vollführt, d. i. die Vielen auf den Punkt Eines Eins gebracht, vorgestellt würden, so wäre nur ein träges Eins, kein Attrahiren mehr vorhanden. Die in der Attraktion daseyende Idealität hat auch noch die Bestimmung der Negation ihrer selbst, die vielen Eins, auf die sie die Beziehung ist, an ihr, und die Attraktion ist untrennbar von der Repulsion.\n\nDas Attrahiren kommt zunächst jedem der vielen als unmittelbar vorhandenen Eins auf gleiche Weise zu; keins hat einen Vorzug vor dem andern; so wäre ein Gleichgewicht im Attrahiren, eigentlich ein Gleichgewicht der Attraktion und der Repulsion selbst vorhanden, und eine träge Ruhe ohne daseyende Idealität. Aber es kann hier nicht von einem Vorzuge eines solchen Eins vor dem andern, was einen bestimmten Unterschied zwischen ihnen voraussetzte, die Rede seyn, vielmehr ist die Attraktion das Setzen der vorhandenen Ununterschiedenheit der Eins. Erst die Attraktion selbst ist das Setzen eines von den anderen unterschiedenen Eins; sie sind nur die unmittelbaren durch die Repulsion sich erhalten sollenden Eins; durch ihre gesetzte Negation aber geht das Eins der Attraktion hervor, das daher als das Vermittelte, das als Eins gesetzte Eins, bestimmt ist. Die ersten als unmittelbare kehren in ihrer Idealität nicht in sich zurück, sondern haben dieselbe an einem andern.\n\nDas Eine Eins aber ist die realisirte, an dem Eins gesetzte Idealität; es ist attrahirend durch die Vermittelung der Repulsion; es enthält diese Vermittelung in sich selbst als seine Bestimmung. Es verschlingt so die attrahirten Eins nicht in sich als in einen Punkt, d. h. es hebt sie nicht abstrakt auf. Indem es die Repulsion in seiner Bestimmung enthält, erhält diese die Eins als Viele zugleich in ihm; es bringt, so zu sagen, durch sein Attrahiren etwas vor sich, gewinnt einen Umfang oder Erfüllung. Es ist so in ihm Einheit der Repulsion und Attraktion überhaupt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0001","text":"Die Repulsion ist die Selbstzersplitterung des Eins zunächst in Viele, deren negatives Verhalten unmächtig ist, weil sie einander als Seyende voraussetzen; sie ist nur das Sollen der Idealität; diese aber wird realisirt in der Attraktion. Die Repulsion geht in Attraktion über, die vielen Eins in Ein Eins. Beide, Repulsion und Attraktion, sind","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"51.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0002","text":"zunächst unterschieden, jene als die Realität der Eins, diese als deren gesetzte Idealität. Die Attraktion bezieht sich auf diese Weise auf die Repulsion, daß sie diese zur Voraussetzung hat. Die Repulsion liefert die Materie für die Attraktion. Wenn keine Eins wären, so wäre nichts zu attrahiren; die Vorstellung fortdauernder Attraktion, der Konsumtion der Eins, setzt ein ebenso fortdauerndes Erzeugen der Eins voraus; die sinnliche Vorstellung der räumlichen Attraktion läßt den Strom der attrahirt-werdenden Eins fortdauern; an die Stelle der Atome, die in dem attrahirenden Punkte verschwinden, tritt eine andere Menge, und wenn man will, ins Unendliche, aus dem Leeren hervor. Wenn die Attraktion vollführt, d. i. die Vielen auf den Punkt Eines Eins gebracht, vorgestellt würden, so wäre nur ein träges Eins, kein Attrahiren mehr vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"51.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0003","text":"Die in der Attraktion daseyende Idealität hat auch noch die Bestimmung der Negation ihrer selbst, die vielen Eins, auf die sie die Beziehung ist, an ihr, und die Attraktion ist untrennbar von der Repulsion.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"51.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0004","text":"Das Attrahiren kommt zunächst jedem der vielen als unmittelbar vorhandenen Eins auf gleiche Weise zu; keins hat einen Vorzug vor dem andern; so wäre ein Gleichgewicht im Attrahiren, eigentlich ein Gleichgewicht der Attraktion und der Repulsion selbst vorhanden, und eine träge Ruhe ohne daseyende Idealität. Aber es kann hier nicht von einem Vorzuge eines solchen Eins vor dem andern, was einen bestimmten Unterschied zwischen ihnen voraussetzte, die Rede seyn, vielmehr ist die Attraktion das Setzen der vorhandenen Ununterschiedenheit der Eins. Erst die Attraktion selbst ist das Setzen eines von den anderen unterschiedenen Eins; sie sind nur die unmittelbaren durch die Repulsion sich erhalten sollenden Eins; durch ihre gesetzte Negation aber geht das Eins der Attraktion hervor, das daher als das Vermittelte, das als Eins gesetzte Eins, bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"51.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0005","text":"Die ersten als unmittelbare kehren in ihrer Idealität nicht in sich zurück, sondern haben dieselbe an einem andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"51.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0006","text":"Das Eine Eins aber ist die realisirte, an dem Eins gesetzte Idealität; es ist attrahirend durch die Vermittelung der Repulsion; es enthält diese Vermittelung in sich selbst als seine Bestimmung. Es verschlingt so die attrahirten Eins nicht in sich als in einen Punkt, d. h. es hebt sie nicht abstrakt auf. Indem es die Repulsion in seiner Bestimmung enthält, erhält diese die Eins als Viele zugleich in ihm; es bringt, so zu sagen, durch sein Attrahiren etwas vor sich, gewinnt einen Umfang oder Erfüllung. Es ist so in ihm Einheit der Repulsion und Attraktion überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"51.6"}],"sha256":"849271d07b40fbb8f9e2f3c53d68e98e5f4f6b6670a606fad972608a893dd299","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102615747465Z_a34aa501","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The One One of Attraction.","source_sha256":"849271d07b40fbb8f9e2f3c53d68e98e5f4f6b6670a606fad972608a893dd299","sha256":"908c551c7ee887f8d2d2e37f65ce7718c10df6e03519105c5e33dfa83d428da5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:26:15.747488+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0001","text":"Repulsion is the self-fragmentation of the One, initially into Many, whose negative comportment is powerless, because they presuppose one another as beings; it is only the ought-to-be of ideality; but this is realized in attraction. Repulsion passes over into attraction, the many Ones into one One. Both, repulsion and attraction, are","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"51.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0002","text":"initially distinct, the former as the reality of the Ones, the latter as their posited ideality. In this way attraction relates to repulsion in that it has the latter as its presupposition. Repulsion supplies the material for attraction. If there were no Ones, there would be nothing to attract; the representation of continuing attraction, of the consumption of the Ones, presupposes an equally continuing production of the Ones; the sensuous representation of spatial attraction allows the stream of Ones-being-attracted to continue; in place of the atoms that disappear in the attracting point, another quantity enters, and, if one will, infinitely, out of the void. If attraction were represented as accomplished, i.e. as having brought the Many to the point of one One, there would be present only an inert One, no attracting any longer.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"51.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0003","text":"The ideality existent in attraction also still has in it the determination of the negation of itself, the many Ones to which it is the relation, and attraction is inseparable from repulsion.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"51.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0004","text":"Attracting initially pertains in the same way to each of the many Ones immediately present; none has any advantage over another; thus there would be a balance in attracting, properly speaking a balance of attraction and repulsion themselves, and an inert repose without existent ideality. But here there can be no question of an advantage of one such One over another, which would presuppose a determinate difference between them; rather, attraction is the positing of the existent undifferentiatedness of the Ones. Only attraction itself is the positing of a One distinct from the others; they are merely the immediate Ones that are to preserve themselves through repulsion; but through their posited negation there emerges the One of attraction, which is therefore determined as the mediated, as the One posited as One.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"51.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0005","text":"The first Ones, as immediate, do not return into themselves in their ideality, but have it in another.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"51.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0006","text":"But the one One is the realized ideality posited in the One; it is attracting through the mediation of repulsion; it contains this mediation within itself as its determination. Thus it does not devour the attracted Ones into itself as into a point, i.e. it does not sublate them abstractly. Since it contains repulsion in its determination, this at the same time preserves the Ones as Many within it; through its attracting it brings, so to speak, something forth before itself, gains an extent or filling. Thus in it there is unity of repulsion and attraction in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"51.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDEE:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"d89b421d11ddd5730f772f59291004e63dbdaa3af1518b9e4c9d6246ab40e951","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Das Eine Eins der Attraktion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Das Eine Eins der Attraktion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD","title":"c. The Relation of Repulsion and Attraction.","order":52,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDBD","text":"Der Unterschied von Einem und Vielen hat sich zum Unterschiede ihrer Beziehung auf einander bestimmt, welche in zwei Beziehungen, die Repulsion und die Attraktion, zerlegt ist, deren jede zunächst selbstständig außer der anderen steht, so daß sie jedoch wesentlich zusammenhängen. Die noch unbestimmte Einheit derselben hat sich näher zu ergeben.\n\nDie Repulsion, als die Grundbestimmung des Eins erscheint zuerst und als unmittelbar, wie ihre zwar von ihr erzeugten jedoch zugleich als unmittelbar gesetzten Eins, und hiermit gleichgültig gegen die Attraktion, welche an sie als so vorausgesetzte äußerlich hinzukommt. Dagegen wird die Attraktion nicht von der Repulsion vorausgesetzt, so daß an deren Setzen und Seyn jene keinen Antheil haben soll d. i. daß die Repulsion nicht an ihr schon die Negation ihrer selbst, die Eins nicht schon an ihnen Negirte wären. Auf solche Weise haben wir die Repulsion abstrakt für sich, wie gleichfalls die Attraktion gegen die Eins als Seyende die Seite eines unmittelbaren Daseyns hat, und von sich aus als ein Anderes an sie kommt.\n\nNehmen wir demnach die bloße Repulsion so für sich, so ist sie die Zerstreuung der vielen Eins ins unbestimmte, außerhalb der Sphäre der Repulsion selbst; denn sie ist dieß, die Beziehung der Vielen aufeinander zu negiren; die Beziehungslosigkeit ist ihre, sie abstrakt genommen, Bestimmung. Die Repulsion ist aber nicht bloß das Leere, die Eins als beziehungslos sind nicht repellirend, nicht ausschließend, was ihre Bestimmung ausmacht. Repulsion ist, obgleich negative, doch wesentlich Beziehung; das gegenseitige Abhalten und Fliehen ist nicht die Befreiung von dem, was abgehalten und geflohen, das ausschließende steht mit dem noch in Verbindung, was von ihm ausgeschlossen wird. dieß Moment der Beziehung aber ist die Attraktion, somit in der Repulsion selbst; sie ist das Negiren jener abstrakten Repulsion, nach welcher die Eins nur sich auf sich beziehende Seyende, nicht ausschließende wären.\n\nIndem aber von der Repulsion der daseyenden Eins ausgegangen worden, hiermit auch die Attraktion als äußerlich an sie tretend gesetzt ist, so sind bei ihrer Untrennbarkeit beide noch als verschiedene Bestimmungen auseinander gehalten; es hat sich jedoch ergeben, daß nicht bloß die Repulsion von der Attraktion vorausgesetzt wird, sondern auch ebenso sehr die Rückbeziehung der Repulsion auf die Attraktion Statt findet, und jene an dieser ebenso sehr ihre Voraussetzung hat.\n\nNach dieser Bestimmung sind sie untrennbar, und zugleich als Sollen und Schranke jede gegen die andere bestimmt. Ihr Sollen ist ihre abstrakte Bestimmtheit als an sich seyender, die aber damit schlechthin über sich hinausgewiesen ist, und auf die andere sich bezieht, und so jede vermittelst der andern als andern ist; ihre Selbstständigkeit besteht darin, daß sie in dieser Vermittelung als ein anderes Bestimmen für einander gesetzt sind.—Die Repulsion als das Setzen der Vielen, die Attraktion als das Setzen des Eins, diese zugleich als Negation der Vielen, und jene als Negation der Idealität derselben im Eins, daß auch die Attraktion nur vermittelst der Repulsion Attraktion, wie die Repulsion vermittelst der Attraktion Repulsion ist. Daß aber darin die Vermittelung durch Anderes mit sich, in der That vielmehr negirt, und jede dieser Bestimmungen Vermittelung ihrer mit sich selbst ist, dieß ergiebt sich aus deren nähern Betrachtung und führt sie zu der Einheit ihres Begriffes zurück.\n\nZuerst daß jede sich selbst voraussetzt, in ihrer Voraussetzung nur sich auf sich bezieht, dieß ist in dem Verhalten der erst noch relativen Repulsion und Attraktion schon vorhanden.\n\nDie relative Repulsion ist das gegenseitige Abhalten der vorhandenen vielen Eins, die sich als unmittelbare vorfinden sollen. Aber daß viele Eins seyen, ist die Repulsion selbst; die Voraussetzung, die sie hätte, ist nur ihr eigenes Setzen. Ferner die Bestimmung des Seyns, die den Eins außerdem, daß sie gesetzte sind, zukäme,—wodurch sie voraus wären, gehört gleichfalls der Repulsion an. Das Repelliren ist das, wodurch die Eins sich als Eins manifestiren und erhalten, wodurch sie als solche sind. Ihr Seyn ist die Repulsion selbst; sie ist so nicht ein relatives gegen ein anderes Daseyn, sondern verhält sich durchaus nur zu sich selbst.\n\nDie Attraktion ist das Setzen des Eins als solchen, des reellen Eins, gegen welches die Vielen in ihrem Daseyn als nur ideell und verschwindend bestimmt werden. So setzt sogleich die Attraktion sich voraus, in der Bestimmung nämlich der anderen Eins, ideell zu seyn, welche sonst für sich seyende und für Andere, also auch für irgend ein Attrahirendes, repellirende seyn sollen. Gegen diese Repulsionsbestimmung erhalten sie die Idealität nicht erst durch Relation auf die Attraktion; sondern sie ist vorausgesetzt, ist die an sich seyende Idealität der Eins, indem sie als Eins,—das als attrahirend vorgestellte mit eingeschlossen, ununterschieden von einander, ein und dasselbe sind.\n\nDieses Sich-selbst-voraussetzen der beiden Bestimmungen jeder für sich ist ferner dieß, daß jede die andere als Moment in sich enthält. Das Sich-Voraussetzen überhaupt ist in Einem sich als das Negative seiner setzen,—Repulsion, und was darin vorausgesetzt wird, ist dasselbe als das Voraussetzende,—Attraktion. Daß jede an sich nur Moment ist, ist das Übergehen jeder aus sich selbst in die andere, sich an ihr selbst zu negiren und sich als das Andere ihrer selbst zu setzen. Indem das Eins als solches das Außersichkommen, es selbst nur dieß ist, sich als sein Anderes, als das Viele zu setzen und das Viele nur ebenso dieß in sich zusammenfallen und sich als sein Anderes, als das Eins zu setzen, und eben darin nur sich auf sich zu beziehen, jedes in seinem Andern sich zu kontinuiren,—so ist hiermit schon an sich das Außersichkommen (die Repulsion) und das sich-als-Eines-Setzen (die Attraktion) ungetrennt vorhanden. Gesetzt aber ist es an der relativen Repulsion und Attraktion d. i. welche unmittelbare, daseyende Eins voraussetzt, daß jede diese Negation ihrer an ihr selbst, und damit auch die Kontinuität ihrer in ihre andere ist. Die Repulsion daseyender Eins ist die Selbsterhaltung des Eins durch die gegenseitige Abhaltung der andern, so daß 1) die anderen Eins an ihm negirt werden, dieß ist die Seite seines Daseyns oder seines Seyns-für-Anderes; diese ist aber somit Attraktion, als die Idealität der Eins;—und daß 2) das Eins an sich sey, ohne die Beziehung auf die andere; aber nicht nur ist das Ansich überhaupt längst in das Fürsichseyn übergegangen, sondern an sich, seiner Bestimmung nach, ist das Eins jenes Werden zu Vielen.—Die Attraktion daseyender Eins ist die Idealität derselben, und das Setzen des Eins, worin sie somit als Negiren und Hervorbringen des Eins sich selbst aufhebt, als Setzen des Eins das Negative ihrer selbst an ihr, Repulsion ist.\n\nDamit ist die Entwickelung des Fürsichseyns vollendet und zu ihrem Resultate gekommenen. Das Eins als sich unendlich d. i. als gesetzte Negation der Negation auf sich selbst beziehend ist die Vermittelung, daß es sich als sein absolutes (d. i. abstraktes) Andersseyn (die Vielen) von sich abstößt und indem es sich auf dieß sein Nichtseyn, negativ, es aufhebend, bezieht, eben darin nur die\n\nBeziehung auf sich selbst ist; und Eins ist nur dieses Werden, in welchem die Bestimmung, daß es anfängt, d. i. als unmittelbares, Seyendes gesetzt, und gleichfalls als Resultat sich zum Eins, d. i. zum ebenso unmittelbaren, ausschließenden Eins wiederhergestellt hätte, verschwunden; der Proceß, der es ist, setzt und enthält es allenthalben nur als ein Aufgehobenes. Das Aufheben zunächst nur zu relativem Aufheben, der Beziehung auf anderes Daseyendes, die damit selbst eine differente Repulsion und Attraktion ist, bestimmt, erweist sich ebenso in die unendliche Beziehung der Vermittelung durch die Negation der äußerlichen Beziehungen von Unmittelbaren und Daseyenden, überzugehen und zum Resultate eben jenes Werden zu haben, das in der Haltungslosigkeit seiner Momente das Zusammensinken, oder vielmehr das Mit-Sich-Zusaummengehen in die einfache Unmittelbarkeit ist. Dieses Seyn nach der Bestimmung, die es nunmehr erhalten, ist die Quantität.\n\nÜbersehen wir kurz die Momente dieses Überganges der Qualität in die Quantität, so hat das Qualitative zu seiner Grundbestimmung das Seyn und die Unmittelbarkeit, in welcher die Grenze und die Bestimmtheit mit dem Seyn des Etwas so identisch ist, daß das Etwas mit ihrer Veränderung selbst verschwindet; so gesetzt ist es als Endliches bestimmt. Um der Unmittelbarkeit dieser Einheit willen, worin der Unterschied verschwunden ist, der aber an sich darin, in der Einheit des Seyns und Nichts, vorhanden ist, fällt er als Andersseyn überhaupt, außer jener Einheit. Diese Beziehung auf Anderes widerspricht der Unmittelbarkeit, in der die qualitative Bestimmtheit Beziehung auf sich ist. Dieß Andersseyn hebt sich in der Unendlichkeit des Fürsichseyns auf, welches den Unterschied, den es in der Negation der Negation an und in ihm selbst hat, zum Eins und Vielen und zu deren Beziehungen realisirt, und das Qualitative zur wahrhaften, d. i. nicht mehr unmittelbaren, sondern als übereinstimmend mit sich gesetzten Einheit erhoben hat.\n\nDiese Einheit ist somit à) Seyn, nur als affirmatives d. i. durch die Negation der Negation mit sich vermittelte Unmittelbarkeit, das Seyn ist gesetzt als die durch seine Bestimmtheiten, Grenze u.s.f. hindurchgehende Einheit, die in ihm als aufgehobene gesetzt sind;—ß) Daseyn; es ist nach solcher Bestimmung die Negation oder Bestimmtheit als Moment des affirmativen Seyns, doch ist sie nicht mehr die unmittelbare, sondern die in sich reflektirte, sich nicht auf anderes, sondern auf sich sich beziehende; das Schlechthin—das An-sich-Bestimmtseyn,—das Eins; das Andersseyn als solches ist selbst Fürsichseyn;—ç) Fürsichseyn, als jenes durch die Bestimmtheit hindurch sich kontinuirende Seyn, in welchem das Eins und An-sich-Bestimmtseyn selbst als Aufgehobenes gesetzt ist. Das Eins ist zugleich als über sich hinausgegangen und als Einheit bestimmt, das Eins damit, die schlechthin bestimmte Grenze, als die Grenze, die keine ist, die am Seyn aber ihm gleichgültig ist, gesetzt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0001","text":"Der Unterschied von Einem und Vielen hat sich zum Unterschiede ihrer Beziehung auf einander bestimmt, welche in zwei Beziehungen, die Repulsion und die Attraktion, zerlegt ist, deren jede zunächst selbstständig außer der anderen steht, so daß sie jedoch wesentlich zusammenhängen. Die noch unbestimmte Einheit derselben hat sich näher zu ergeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"52.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0002","text":"Die Repulsion, als die Grundbestimmung des Eins erscheint zuerst und als unmittelbar, wie ihre zwar von ihr erzeugten jedoch zugleich als unmittelbar gesetzten Eins, und hiermit gleichgültig gegen die Attraktion, welche an sie als so vorausgesetzte äußerlich hinzukommt. Dagegen wird die Attraktion nicht von der Repulsion vorausgesetzt, so daß an deren Setzen und Seyn jene keinen Antheil haben soll d. i. daß die Repulsion nicht an ihr schon die Negation ihrer selbst, die Eins nicht schon an ihnen Negirte wären. Auf solche Weise haben wir die Repulsion abstrakt für sich, wie gleichfalls die Attraktion gegen die Eins als Seyende die Seite eines unmittelbaren Daseyns hat, und von sich aus als ein Anderes an sie kommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"52.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0003","text":"Nehmen wir demnach die bloße Repulsion so für sich, so ist sie die Zerstreuung der vielen Eins ins unbestimmte, außerhalb der Sphäre der Repulsion selbst; denn sie ist dieß, die Beziehung der Vielen aufeinander zu negiren; die Beziehungslosigkeit ist ihre, sie abstrakt genommen, Bestimmung. Die Repulsion ist aber nicht bloß das Leere, die Eins als beziehungslos sind nicht repellirend, nicht ausschließend, was ihre Bestimmung ausmacht. Repulsion ist, obgleich negative, doch wesentlich Beziehung; das gegenseitige Abhalten und Fliehen ist nicht die Befreiung von dem, was abgehalten und geflohen, das ausschließende steht mit dem noch in Verbindung, was von ihm ausgeschlossen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"52.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0004","text":"dieß Moment der Beziehung aber ist die Attraktion, somit in der Repulsion selbst; sie ist das Negiren jener abstrakten Repulsion, nach welcher die Eins nur sich auf sich beziehende Seyende, nicht ausschließende wären.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"52.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0005","text":"Indem aber von der Repulsion der daseyenden Eins ausgegangen worden, hiermit auch die Attraktion als äußerlich an sie tretend gesetzt ist, so sind bei ihrer Untrennbarkeit beide noch als verschiedene Bestimmungen auseinander gehalten; es hat sich jedoch ergeben, daß nicht bloß die Repulsion von der Attraktion vorausgesetzt wird, sondern auch ebenso sehr die Rückbeziehung der Repulsion auf die Attraktion Statt findet, und jene an dieser ebenso sehr ihre Voraussetzung hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"52.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0006","text":"Nach dieser Bestimmung sind sie untrennbar, und zugleich als Sollen und Schranke jede gegen die andere bestimmt. Ihr Sollen ist ihre abstrakte Bestimmtheit als an sich seyender, die aber damit schlechthin über sich hinausgewiesen ist, und auf die andere sich bezieht, und so jede vermittelst der andern als andern ist; ihre Selbstständigkeit besteht darin, daß sie in dieser Vermittelung als ein anderes Bestimmen für einander gesetzt sind.—Die Repulsion als das Setzen der Vielen, die Attraktion als das Setzen des Eins, diese zugleich als Negation der Vielen, und jene als Negation der Idealität derselben im Eins, daß auch die Attraktion nur vermittelst der Repulsion Attraktion, wie die Repulsion vermittelst der Attraktion Repulsion ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"52.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0007","text":"Daß aber darin die Vermittelung durch Anderes mit sich, in der That vielmehr negirt, und jede dieser Bestimmungen Vermittelung ihrer mit sich selbst ist, dieß ergiebt sich aus deren nähern Betrachtung und führt sie zu der Einheit ihres Begriffes zurück.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"52.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0008","text":"Zuerst daß jede sich selbst voraussetzt, in ihrer Voraussetzung nur sich auf sich bezieht, dieß ist in dem Verhalten der erst noch relativen Repulsion und Attraktion schon vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"52.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0009","text":"Die relative Repulsion ist das gegenseitige Abhalten der vorhandenen vielen Eins, die sich als unmittelbare vorfinden sollen. Aber daß viele Eins seyen, ist die Repulsion selbst; die Voraussetzung, die sie hätte, ist nur ihr eigenes Setzen. Ferner die Bestimmung des Seyns, die den Eins außerdem, daß sie gesetzte sind, zukäme,—wodurch sie voraus wären, gehört gleichfalls der Repulsion an. Das Repelliren ist das, wodurch die Eins sich als Eins manifestiren und erhalten, wodurch sie als solche sind. Ihr Seyn ist die Repulsion selbst; sie ist so nicht ein relatives gegen ein anderes Daseyn, sondern verhält sich durchaus nur zu sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"52.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0010","text":"Die Attraktion ist das Setzen des Eins als solchen, des reellen Eins, gegen welches die Vielen in ihrem Daseyn als nur ideell und verschwindend bestimmt werden. So setzt sogleich die Attraktion sich voraus, in der Bestimmung nämlich der anderen Eins, ideell zu seyn, welche sonst für sich seyende und für Andere, also auch für irgend ein Attrahirendes, repellirende seyn sollen. Gegen diese Repulsionsbestimmung erhalten sie die Idealität nicht erst durch Relation auf die Attraktion; sondern sie ist vorausgesetzt, ist die an sich seyende Idealität der Eins, indem sie als Eins,—das als attrahirend vorgestellte mit eingeschlossen, ununterschieden von einander, ein und dasselbe sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"52.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0011","text":"Dieses Sich-selbst-voraussetzen der beiden Bestimmungen jeder für sich ist ferner dieß, daß jede die andere als Moment in sich enthält. Das Sich-Voraussetzen überhaupt ist in Einem sich als das Negative seiner setzen,—Repulsion, und was darin vorausgesetzt wird, ist dasselbe als das Voraussetzende,—Attraktion. Daß jede an sich nur Moment ist, ist das Übergehen jeder aus sich selbst in die andere, sich an ihr selbst zu negiren und sich als das Andere ihrer selbst zu setzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"52.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0012","text":"Indem das Eins als solches das Außersichkommen, es selbst nur dieß ist, sich als sein Anderes, als das Viele zu setzen und das Viele nur ebenso dieß in sich zusammenfallen und sich als sein Anderes, als das Eins zu setzen, und eben darin nur sich auf sich zu beziehen, jedes in seinem Andern sich zu kontinuiren,—so ist hiermit schon an sich das Außersichkommen (die Repulsion) und das sich-als-Eines-Setzen (die Attraktion) ungetrennt vorhanden. Gesetzt aber ist es an der relativen Repulsion und Attraktion d. i. welche unmittelbare, daseyende Eins voraussetzt, daß jede diese Negation ihrer an ihr selbst, und damit auch die Kontinuität ihrer in ihre andere ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"52.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0013","text":"Die Repulsion daseyender Eins ist die Selbsterhaltung des Eins durch die gegenseitige Abhaltung der andern, so daß 1) die anderen Eins an ihm negirt werden, dieß ist die Seite seines Daseyns oder seines Seyns-für-Anderes; diese ist aber somit Attraktion, als die Idealität der Eins;—und daß 2) das Eins an sich sey, ohne die Beziehung auf die andere; aber nicht nur ist das Ansich überhaupt längst in das Fürsichseyn übergegangen, sondern an sich, seiner Bestimmung nach, ist das Eins jenes Werden zu Vielen.—Die Attraktion daseyender Eins ist die Idealität derselben, und das Setzen des Eins, worin sie somit als Negiren und Hervorbringen des Eins sich selbst aufhebt, als Setzen des Eins das Negative ihrer selbst an ihr, Repulsion ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"52.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0014","text":"Damit ist die Entwickelung des Fürsichseyns vollendet und zu ihrem Resultate gekommenen. Das Eins als sich unendlich d. i. als gesetzte Negation der Negation auf sich selbst beziehend ist die Vermittelung, daß es sich als sein absolutes (d. i. abstraktes) Andersseyn (die Vielen) von sich abstößt und indem es sich auf dieß sein Nichtseyn, negativ, es aufhebend, bezieht, eben darin nur die","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"52.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0015","text":"Beziehung auf sich selbst ist; und Eins ist nur dieses Werden, in welchem die Bestimmung, daß es anfängt, d. i. als unmittelbares, Seyendes gesetzt, und gleichfalls als Resultat sich zum Eins, d. i. zum ebenso unmittelbaren, ausschließenden Eins wiederhergestellt hätte, verschwunden; der Proceß, der es ist, setzt und enthält es allenthalben nur als ein Aufgehobenes. Das Aufheben zunächst nur zu relativem Aufheben, der Beziehung auf anderes Daseyendes, die damit selbst eine differente Repulsion und Attraktion ist, bestimmt, erweist sich ebenso in die unendliche Beziehung der Vermittelung durch die Negation der äußerlichen Beziehungen von Unmittelbaren und Daseyenden, überzugehen und zum Resultate eben jenes Werden zu haben, das in der Haltungslosigkeit seiner Momente das Zusammensinken, oder vielmehr das Mit-Sich-Zusaummengehen in die einfache Unmittelbarkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"52.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0016","text":"Dieses Seyn nach der Bestimmung, die es nunmehr erhalten, ist die Quantität.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"52.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0017","text":"Übersehen wir kurz die Momente dieses Überganges der Qualität in die Quantität, so hat das Qualitative zu seiner Grundbestimmung das Seyn und die Unmittelbarkeit, in welcher die Grenze und die Bestimmtheit mit dem Seyn des Etwas so identisch ist, daß das Etwas mit ihrer Veränderung selbst verschwindet; so gesetzt ist es als Endliches bestimmt. Um der Unmittelbarkeit dieser Einheit willen, worin der Unterschied verschwunden ist, der aber an sich darin, in der Einheit des Seyns und Nichts, vorhanden ist, fällt er als Andersseyn überhaupt, außer jener Einheit. Diese Beziehung auf Anderes widerspricht der Unmittelbarkeit, in der die qualitative Bestimmtheit Beziehung auf sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"52.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0018","text":"Dieß Andersseyn hebt sich in der Unendlichkeit des Fürsichseyns auf, welches den Unterschied, den es in der Negation der Negation an und in ihm selbst hat, zum Eins und Vielen und zu deren Beziehungen realisirt, und das Qualitative zur wahrhaften, d. i. nicht mehr unmittelbaren, sondern als übereinstimmend mit sich gesetzten Einheit erhoben hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"52.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0019","text":"Diese Einheit ist somit à) Seyn, nur als affirmatives d. i. durch die Negation der Negation mit sich vermittelte Unmittelbarkeit, das Seyn ist gesetzt als die durch seine Bestimmtheiten, Grenze u.s.f. hindurchgehende Einheit, die in ihm als aufgehobene gesetzt sind;—ß) Daseyn; es ist nach solcher Bestimmung die Negation oder Bestimmtheit als Moment des affirmativen Seyns, doch ist sie nicht mehr die unmittelbare, sondern die in sich reflektirte, sich nicht auf anderes, sondern auf sich sich beziehende; das Schlechthin—das An-sich-Bestimmtseyn,—das Eins; das Andersseyn als solches ist selbst Fürsichseyn;—ç) Fürsichseyn, als jenes durch die Bestimmtheit hindurch sich kontinuirende Seyn, in welchem das Eins und An-sich-Bestimmtseyn selbst als Aufgehobenes gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"52.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0020","text":"Das Eins ist zugleich als über sich hinausgegangen und als Einheit bestimmt, das Eins damit, die schlechthin bestimmte Grenze, als die Grenze, die keine ist, die am Seyn aber ihm gleichgültig ist, gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"52.20"}],"sha256":"fd6019373c5bec576d3a226b5d5e383ee006058021786b9fe327bdcaa78d1e88","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102635714363Z_c7b3a576","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Relation of Repulsion and Attraction.","source_sha256":"fd6019373c5bec576d3a226b5d5e383ee006058021786b9fe327bdcaa78d1e88","sha256":"690da3e69de5931e280d69e5ffcfdbe4dd9380f8e802dc4d5043459b3e60774c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:26:35.714389+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0001","text":"The difference of One and Many has determined itself into the difference of their relation to one another, which is divided into two relations, repulsion and attraction, each of which at first stands independently outside the other, yet such that they are essentially connected. Their still indeterminate unity is to be brought out more precisely.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"52.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0002","text":"Repulsion, as the fundamental determination of the One, appears first and as immediate, as do its Ones, which are indeed generated by it but are at the same time posited as immediate, and thus indifferent to attraction, which joins them externally as thus presupposed. Attraction, on the other hand, is not presupposed by repulsion, such that it should have no part in the positing and being of the latter, i.e. such that repulsion should not already have in attraction the negation of itself, the Ones not already that which is negated in them. In this way we have repulsion abstractly for itself, just as attraction likewise has, in relation to the Ones as beings, the side of an immediate existence, and approaches them from itself as an Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"52.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0003","text":"If accordingly we take mere repulsion by itself, it is the dispersal of the many Ones into the indeterminate, outside the sphere of repulsion itself; for it is this: to negate the relation of the Many to one another; relationlessness is its determination, taken abstractly. But repulsion is not merely the void; Ones, as relationless, are not repelling, not excluding, which constitutes their determination. Repulsion, although negative, is nevertheless essentially relation; reciprocal holding-apart and flight are not liberation from that which is held apart and fled from; that which excludes remains connected with that which is excluded by it.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"52.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0004","text":"but this moment of relation is attraction, and thus is in repulsion itself; it is the negation of that abstract repulsion according to which the Ones would be only beings relating themselves to themselves, not excluding.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"52.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0005","text":"But since we proceeded from the repulsion of existent Ones, and thus attraction too is posited as externally approaching them, then, in their inseparability, both are still held apart as different determinations; yet it has emerged that not only is repulsion presupposed by attraction, but equally the return-relation of repulsion to attraction takes place, and the former equally has its presupposition in the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"52.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0006","text":"According to this determination they are inseparable, and at the same time each is determined over against the other as ought and limit. Their ought is their abstract determinacy as being in itself, which, however, is thereby absolutely referred beyond itself and relates itself to the other, and thus each is, through the other, as another; their independence consists in this, that in this mediation they are posited as an other determining for one another.—Repulsion as the positing of the Many, attraction as the positing of the One, the latter at the same time as the negation of the Many, and the former as the negation of their ideality in the One: thus attraction too is attraction only through repulsion, just as repulsion is repulsion through attraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"52.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0007","text":"But that in this the mediation with itself through an Other is in fact rather negated, and that each of these determinations is mediation of itself with itself, emerges from their closer consideration and leads them back to the unity of their concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"52.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0008","text":"First, that each presupposes itself and in its presupposition relates only to itself, is already present in the conduct of still merely relative repulsion and attraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"52.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0009","text":"Relative repulsion is the reciprocal holding-apart of the present many Ones, which are supposed to find themselves as immediate. But that there are many Ones is repulsion itself; the presupposition which it would have is only its own positing. Further, the determination of being which would accrue to the Ones apart from their being posited,—whereby they would be prior,—likewise belongs to repulsion. Repelling is that whereby the Ones manifest and preserve themselves as Ones, whereby they are as such. Their being is repulsion itself; thus it is not relative to another existence, but relates throughout only to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"52.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0010","text":"Attraction is the positing of the One as such, of the real One, over against which the Many are determined in their existence as merely ideal and vanishing. Thus attraction immediately presupposes itself, namely in the determination of the other Ones to be ideal, which otherwise are supposed to be beings-for-self and beings-for-others, hence also repelling for some attracting entity. They do not first obtain ideality against this determination of repulsion through relation to attraction; rather, it is presupposed, is the ideality of the Ones in themselves, in that, as Ones,—including that represented as attracting—they are indistinguishable from one another, one and the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"52.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0011","text":"This self-presupposing of the two determinations, each for itself, further means that each contains the other as a moment within itself. Presupposing oneself in general is positing oneself as the negative of oneself,—repulsion; and that which is presupposed therein is the same as that which presupposes,—attraction. That each is in itself only a moment is the transition of each from itself into the other, negating itself in itself and positing itself as the Other of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"52.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0012","text":"Since the One as such is coming-outside-itself, itself only this, to posit itself as its Other, as the Many, and the Many likewise are only this, to collapse into themselves and posit themselves as their Other, as the One, and precisely thereby only to relate themselves to themselves, each continuing itself in its Other,—then coming-outside-itself (repulsion) and positing-itself-as-One (attraction) are thereby already present in themselves inseparably. But it is posited in relative repulsion and attraction, i.e. those which presuppose immediate, existent Ones, that each has this negation of itself within itself, and thereby also its continuity into its other.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"52.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0013","text":"The repulsion of existent Ones is the self-preservation of the One through the reciprocal holding-apart of the others, such that 1) the other Ones are negated in it; this is the side of its existence or its being-for-other; but this is thus attraction, as the ideality of the Ones;—and that 2) the One be in itself, without relation to the other; but not only has the in-itself in general long since passed over into being-for-self, but in itself, according to its determination, the One is that becoming of Many.—The attraction of existent Ones is their ideality, and the positing of the One, in which it thus sublates itself as negating and bringing forth the One, is, as positing of the One, the negative of itself in itself, repulsion.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"52.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0014","text":"With this the development of being-for-self is completed and has arrived at its result. The One, as relating itself infinitely to itself, i.e. as posited negation of negation, is the mediation whereby it repels itself from itself as its absolute (i.e. abstract) otherness (the Many), and, in relating itself negatively to this its non-being, sublating it, is precisely thereby only the","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"52.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0015","text":"relation to itself; and One is only this becoming, in which the determination that it begins, i.e. is posited as immediate, being, and likewise would have restored itself as result to the One, i.e. to the likewise immediate, excluding One, has vanished; the process which it is posits and contains it everywhere only as a sublated entity. Sublation, at first determined only as relative sublation, as relation to other existent being, which is thereby itself a different repulsion and attraction, proves likewise to pass over into the infinite relation of mediation through the negation of the external relations of immediate entities and existent entities, and to have as its result precisely that becoming which, in the instability of its moments, is the collapsing together, or rather the coming-together-with-itself, into simple immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"52.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0016","text":"This being, according to the determination which it has now received, is quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"52.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0017","text":"If we briefly survey the moments of this transition of quality into quantity, the qualitative has, as its fundamental determination, being and immediacy, in which limit and determinacy are so identical with the being of the Something that the Something itself vanishes with their alteration; thus posited, it is determined as finite. On account of the immediacy of this unity, in which the difference has vanished, though it is present therein in itself, in the unity of being and nothing, it falls, as otherness in general, outside that unity. This relation to an Other contradicts the immediacy in which qualitative determinacy is relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"52.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0018","text":"This otherness sublates itself in the infinity of being-for-self, which realizes the difference that it has in the negation of negation in and within itself as One and Many and as their relations, and has raised the qualitative into true unity, i.e. unity no longer immediate but posited as in agreement with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"52.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0019","text":"This unity is thus à) being, only as affirmative, i.e. immediacy mediated with itself through the negation of negation; being is posited as the unity passing through its determinacies, limit, etc., which are posited in it as sublated;—ß) existence; according to such determination it is negation or determinacy as a moment of affirmative being, yet it is no longer immediate but reflected into itself, relating itself not to an other but to itself; the Absolute—the being-determined-in-itself,—the One; otherness as such is itself being-for-self;—ç) being-for-self, as that being continuing itself through determinacy, in which the One and being-determined-in-itself are themselves posited as sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"52.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0020","text":"The One is at the same time determined as having gone beyond itself and as unity, the One thereby posited as the absolutely determinate limit, as the limit which is no limit, which is nevertheless indifferent to it in being.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"52.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDBD:P0020"]}],"source_digest":"6861e7b73faab65f645d6f7779a4e02de1e9a140ab24a18194df2831f86eecaa","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die Beziehung der Repulsion und Attraktion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die Beziehung der Repulsion und Attraktion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10","title":"Remark.","order":53,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_10","text":"Attraktion und Repulsion pflegen bekanntlich als Kräfte angesehen zu werden. Diese ihre Bestimmung und die damit zusammenhängende Verhältnisse sind mit den Begriffen, die sich für sie ergeben haben, zu vergleichen.—In jener Vorstellung werden sie als selbstständig betrachtet, so daß sie sich nicht durch ihre Natur auf einander beziehen, d. h. daß nicht jede nur ein in ihre entgegengesetzte übergehendes Moment seyn, sondern fest der andern gegenüber beharren soll. Sie werden ferner vorgestellt, als in einem Dritten, der Materie, zusammenkommend; so jedoch, daß dieß In-Eins-Werden nicht als ihre Wahrheit gilt, sondern jede vielmehr ein Erstes und An-und-fürsich-Seyendes, die Materie aber oder Bestimmungen derselben durch sie gesetzt und hervorgebracht seyen. Wenn gesagt wird, daß die Materie die Kräfte in sich habe, so ist unter dieser ihrer Einheit eine Verknüpfung verstanden, wobei sie zugleich als in sich seyende frei von einander vorausgesetzt werden.\n\nKant hat bekanntlich die Materie aus der Repulsivund AttraktivKraft konstruirt oder wenigstens, wie er sich ausdrückt, die metaphysischen Elemente dieser Konstruction aufgestellt.—Es wird nicht ohne Interesse seyn, diese Konstruction näher zu beleuchten. Diese metaphysische Darstellung eines Gegenstandes, der nicht nur selbst, sondern in seinen Bestimmungen, nur der Erfahrung anzugehören schien, ist eines Theils dadurch merkwürdig, daß sie als ein Versuch des Begriffs wenigstens den Anstoß zur neueren Naturphilosophie gegeben hat,—der Philosophie, welche die Natur nicht als ein der Wahrnehmung sinnlich Gegebenes zum Grunde der Wissenschaft macht, sondern ihre Bestimmungen aus dem absoluten Begriffe erkennt; andern Theils auch, weil bei jener Kantischen Konstruktion noch häufig stehen geblieben und sie für einen philosophischen Anfang und Grundlage der Physik gehalten wird.\n\nEine solche Existenz, wie die sinnliche Materie, ist zwar nicht ein Gegenstand der Logik, eben so wenig als der Raum und Raumbestimmungen. Aber auch der Attraktiv- und Repulsiv-Kraft, sofern sie als Kräfte der sinnlichen Materie angesehen werden, liegen die hier betrachteten reinen Bestimmungen vom Eins und Vielen, und deren Beziehungen aufeinander, die ich Repulsion und Attraktion, weil diese Namen am nächsten liegen, genannt habe, zu Grunde.\n\nKants Verfahren in der Deduktion der Materie aus diesen Kräften, das er eine Konstruktion nennt, verdient, näher betrachtet, diesen Namen nicht, wenn nicht anders jede Art voll Reflexion, selbst die analysirende, eine Konstruktion genannt wird, wie denn freilich spätere Naturphilosophen auch das flachste Raisonnement und das grundloseste Gebräue einer willkürlichen Einbildungskraft und gedankenlosen Reflexion,—das besonders die sogenannten Faktoren der Attraktivkraft und Repulsivkraft gebrauchte und allenthalben vorbrachte,—ein Konstruiren genannt haben.\n\nKants Verfahren ist nämlich Im Grunde analytisch, nicht konstruirend. Er setzt die Vorstellung der Materie voraus, und fragt nun, welche Kräfte dazu gehören, um ihre vorausgesetzten Bestimmungen zu erhalten. So fordert er also eines Theils die Attraktivkraft darum, weil durch die Repulsion allein, ohne Attraktion, eigentlich keine Materie daseyn könnte. (Anfangsgr. der Naturwissensch. S. 53f.) Die Repulsion andern Theils, leitet er gleichfalls aus der Materie ab, und giebt als Grund derselben an, weil wir uns die Materie undurchdringlich vorstellen, indem diese nämlich dem Sinne des Gefühls, durch den sie sich uns offenbare, sich unter dieser Bestimmung präsentirt. Die Repulsion werde daher ferner sogleich im Begriffe der Materie gedacht, weil sie damit unmittelbar gegeben sey; die Attraktion dagegen werde derselben durch Schlüsse beigefügt. Auch diesen Schlüssen aber liegt das so eben Gesagte zu Grunde, daß eine Materie, die bloß Repulsivkraft hätte, das, was wir uns unter Materie vorstellen, nicht erschöpfte.—Dieß ist, wie erhellt, das Verfahren des über die Erfahrung reflektirenden Erkennens, das zuerst in der Erscheinung Bestimmungen wahrnimmt, diese nun zu Grunde legt, und für das sogenannte Erklären derselben entsprechende Grundstoffe oder Kräfte annimmt, welche jene Bestimmungen der Erscheinung hervorbringen sollen.\n\nIn Ansehung des angeführten Unterschieds, wie die Repulsivkraft und wie die Attraktivkraft von dem Erkennen in der Materie gefunden werde, bemerkt Kant weiter, daß die Attraktivkraft zwar eben sowohl zum Begriffe der Materie gehöre, ob sie gleich nicht darin enthalten sey. Kant zeichnet diesen letztern Ausdruck aus. Es ist aber nicht abzusehen, welcher Unterschied darin liegen soll; denn eine Bestimmung, die zum Begriffe einer Sache gehört, muß wahrhaftig darin enthalten seyn.\n\nWas die Schwierigkeit macht und diese leere Ausflucht herbeiführt, besteht darin, daß Kant zum Begriffe der Materie von vorn herein einseitig nur die Bestimmung der Undurchdringlichkeit rechnet, die wir durch das Gefühl wahrnehmen sollen, weswegen die Repulsivkraft, als das Abhalten eines Anderen von sich, unmittelbar gegeben sey. Wenn aber ferner die Materie ohne Attraktivkraft nicht soll daseyn können, so liegt für diese Behauptung eine aus der Wahrnehmung genommene Vorstellung der Materie zu Grunde; die Bestimmung der Attraktion muß also gleichfalls in der Wahrnehmung anzutreffen seyn. Es ist auch wohl wahrzunehmen, daß die Materie außer ihrem Fürsichseyn, welches das Seyn-fur-Anderes aufhebt, (den Widerstand leistet), auch eine Beziehung des Fürsichseyenden aufeinander, räumliche Ausdehnung und Zusammenhalt, und in Starrheit, Festigkeit einen sehr festen Zusammenhalt hat. Die erklärende Physik erfordert zum Zerreißen u.s.f. eines Körpers eine Kraft, welche starker sey, als die Attraktion der Theile desselben gegeneinander. Aus dieser Wahrnehmung kann die Reflexion eben so unmittelbar die Attraktivkraft ableiten, oder sie als gegeben annehmen, als sie es mit der Repulsivkraft that. In der That, wenn die kantischen Schlüsse, aus denen die Attraktivkraft abgeleitet werden soll, betrachtet werden (der Beweis des Lehrsatzes: daß die Möglichkeit der Materie eine Anziehungskraft als zweite Grundkraft erfordere a. a. O.), so enthalten sie nichts, als daß durch die bloße Repulsion die Materie nicht räumlich seyn würde. Indem die Materie, als Raum erfüllend vorausgesetzt ist, ist ihr die Kontinuität zugeschrieben, als deren Grund die Anziehungskraft angenommen wird.\n\nWenn nun solche sogenannte Konstruktion der Materie höchstens ein analytisches Verdienst hätte, das noch durch die unreine Darstellung geschmälert würde, so ist der Grundgedanke immer sehr zu schätzen, die Materie aus diesen zwei entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen als ihren Grundkräften zu erkennen. Es ist Kant vornehmlich um die Verbannung der gemein-mechanischen Vorstellungsweise zu thun, die bei der einen Bestimmung, der Undurchdringlichkeit, der für-sich-seyenden Punktualität, stehen bleibt, und die entgegengesetzte Bestimmung, die Beziehung der Materie in sich oder mehrerer Materien, die wieder als besondere Eins angesehen werden, aufeinander, zu etwas Äußerlichem macht;—die Vorstellungsweise, welche, wie Kant sagt, sonst keine bewegenden Kräfte, als nur durch Druck und Stoß, also nur durch Einwirkung von Aussen, einräumen will. Diese Äußerlichkeit des Erkennens setzt die Bewegung immer schon als der Materie äußerlich vorhanden voraus, und denkt nicht daran, sie als etwas Innerliches zu fassen, und sie selbst in der Materie zu begreifen, welche eben damit für sich als bewegungslos und als träge angenommen wird. Dieser Standpunkt hat nur die gemeine Mechanik, nicht die immanente und freie Bewegung vor sich.—Indem Kant jene Äußerlichkeit zwar insofern aufhebt, als er die Attraktion, die Beziehung der Materien auf einander, insofern diese als von einander getrennt angenommen werden, oder der Materie überhaupt in ihrem Außersichseyn, zu einer Kraft der Materie selbst macht, so bleiben jedoch auf der anderen Seite seine beiden Grundkräfte, innerhalb der Materie, äußerliche und für sich selbstständige gegen einander.\n\nSo nichtig der selbstständige Unterschied dieser beiden Kräfte, der ihnen vom Standpunkte jenes Erkennens beigelegt wird, war, ebenso nichtig muß sich jeder andere Unterschied, der in Ansehung ihrer Inhaltsbestimmung als etwas Festseyn-Sollendes gemacht wird, zeigen, weil sie, wie sie oben in ihrer Wahrheit betrachtet wurden, nur Momente sind, die in einander übergehen.—Ich betrachte diese fernern Unterschiedsbestimmunge, wie sie Kant angiebt.\n\nEr bestimmt nämlich die Attraktivkraft als eine durchdringende Kraft, wodurch eine Materie auf die Theile der anderen auch über die Fläche der Berührung hinaus unmittelbar wirken könne, die Repulsivkraft dagegen als eine Flächenkraft, dadurch Materien nur in der gemeinschaftlichen Fläche der Berührung auf einander wirken können. Der Grund, der angeführt wird, daß die letztere nur eine Flächenkraft seyn soll, ist folgender: \"Die einander berührenden Theile begrenzen einer den Wirkungsraum des andern, und die repulsive Kraft könne keinen entferntern Theil bewegen, ohne vermittelst der dazwischen liegenden; eine quer durch diese gehende unmittelbare Wirkung einer Materie auf eine andere durch Ausdehnungskräfte (das heißt hier Repulsivkräfte) sey unmöglich.\" (s. ebendas. Erklär. u. Zusätze S. 67.)\n\nEs ist sogleich zu erinnern, daß, indem nähere oder entferntere Theile der Materie angenommen werden, in Rücksicht auf die Attraktion gleichfalls der Unterschied entstünde, daß ein Atom zwar auf ein anderes einwirkte, aber ein drittes Entfernteres, zwischen welchem und dem ersten Attrahirenden das Andere sich befände, zunächst in die Anziehungssphäre des dazwischen liegenden ihm Nähern träte, das Erste also nicht eine unmittelbare einfache Wirkung auf das Dritte ausüben würde; woraus sich eben so ein vermitteltes Wirken für die Attractivkraft, als für die Repulsivkraft ergehe; ferner müßte das wahre Durchdringen der Attraktivkraft allein darin bestehen, daß alle Theile der Materie an und für sich attrahirend wären, nicht aber eine gewisse Menge passiv und nur Ein Atom aktiv sich verhielte. —Unmittelbar oder in Rücksicht auf die Repulsivkraft selbst aber ist zu bemerken, daß in der angeführten Stelle sich berührende Theile, also eine Gediegenheit und Kontinuität einer fertigen Materie vorkommt, welche durch sich hindurch ein Repelliren nicht gestatte. Diese Gediegenheit der Materie aber, in welcher Theile sich berühren, nicht mehr durch das Leere getrennt sind, setzt das Aufgehobenseyn der Repulsivkraft bereits voraus; sich berührende Theile sind nach der hier herrschenden sinnlichen Vorstellung der Repulsion als solche zu nehmen, die sich nicht repelliren. Es folgt also ganz tautologisch, daß da, wo das Nichtseyn der Repulsion angenommen ist, keine Repulsion Statt finden kann. Daraus aber folgt nichts weiter für eine Bestimmung der Repulsivkraft.—Wird aber darauf reflektirt, daß berührende Theile sich nur insofern berühren, als sie sich noch außereinander halten, so ist eben damit die Repulsivkraft nicht bloß auf der Oberfläche der Materie, sondern innerhalb der Sphäre, welche nur Sphäre der Attraktion seyn sollte.\n\nWeiter nimmt Kant die Bestimmung an, daß \"durch die Anziehungskraft die Materie einen Raum nur einnehme, ohne ihn zu erfüllen;\" (ebendas.) \"weil die Materie durch die Anziehungskraft den Raum nicht erfülle, so könne diese durch den leeren Raum wirken, indem ihr keine Materie, die dazwischen läge, Grenzen setze.\"—Jener Unterschied ist ungefähr wie der obige beschaffen, wo eine Bestimmung zum Begriffe einer Sache gehören, aber nicht darin enthalten seyn sollte, so soll hier die Materie einen Raum nur einnehmen, ihn aber nicht erfüllen. Alsdenn ist es die Repulsion, wenn wir bei ihrer ersten Bestimmung stehen bleiben, durch welche sich die Eins abstossen und nur negativ, das heißt hier, durch den leeren Raum, sich aufeinander beziehen. Hier aber ist es die Attraktivkraft, welche den Raum leer erhält; sie erfüllt den Raum durch ihre Beziehung der Atome nicht, das heißt, sie erhält die Atome in einer negativen Beziehung auf einander.—Wir sehen, daß hier Kant bewußtlos das begegnet, was in der Natur der Sache liegt, daß er der Attraktivkraft gerade das zuschreibt, was er der ersten Bestimmung nach, der entgegengesetzten Kraft zuschrieb. Unter dem Geschäfte der Festsetzung des Unterschiedes beider Kräfte, war es geschehen, daß eine in die andere übergegangen war.—So soll dagegen durch die Repulsion die Materie einen Raum erfüllen, somit durch sie der leere Raum, den die Attraktivkraft läßt, verschwinden, In der That hebt sie somit, indem sie den leeren Raum aufhebt, die negative Beziehung der Atome oder Eins, d. h. die Repulsion derselben, auf; d. i. die Repulsion ist als das Gegentheil ihrer selbst bestimmt.\n\nZu dieser Verwischung der Unterschiede kommt noch die Verwirrung hinzu, daß, wie anfangs bemerkt worden, die Kantische Darstellung der entgegengesetzten Kräfte analytisch ist, und in dem ganzen Vortrage, die Materie, die erst aus ihren Elementen hergeleitet werden soll, bereits als fertig und konstituirt vorkommt. In der Definition der Flächen- und der durchdringenden Kraft werden beide als bewegende Kräfte angenommen, dadurch Materien auf die eine oder die andere Weise sollen wirken können.—Sie sind also hier als Kräfte dargestellt, nicht durch welche die Materie erst zu Stande käme, sondern wodurch sie, schon fertig, nur bewegt würde. Insofern aber von Kräften die Rede ist, wodurch verschiedene Materien auf einander einwirken und sich bewegen, so ist dieß etwas ganz anderes, als die Bestimmung und Beziehung, die sie als die Momente der Materie haben sollten.\n\nDenselben Gegensatz, als Attraktiv- und Repulsivkraft machen in weiterer Bestimmung Centripetal- und Centrifugalkraft. Diese scheinen einen wesentlichen Unterschied zu gewähren, indem in ihrer Sphäre Ein Eins, ein Centrum, feststeht, gegen das sich die anderen Eins als nicht fürsichseyende verhalten, der Unterschied der Kräfte daher an diesen vorausgesetzten Unterschied Eines centralen Eins und der anderen als gegen dasselbe nicht feststehend angeknüpft werden kann. Insofern sie aber zur Erklärung gebraucht werden—zu welchem Behuf man sie, wie auch sonst die Repulsiv- und Attraktivkraft, in entgegengesetztem quantitativem Verhältniß annimmt, so daß die eine zunehme, wie die andere abnehme, so soll die Erscheinung der Bewegung, für deren Erklärung sie angenommen sind, und deren Ungleichheit erst aus ihnen resultiren. Man braucht aber nur die nächste beste Darstellung einer Erscheinung, z.B. die ungleiche Geschwindigkeit, die ein Planet in seiner Bahn um seinen Centralkörper hat, aus dem Gegensatze jener Kräfte, vor sich nehmen, so erkennt man bald die Verwirrung, die darin herrscht, und die Unmöglichkeit, die Größen derselben auseinander zu bringen, so daß immer eben so diejenige als zunehmend anzunehmen ist, welche in der Erklärung als abnehmend angenommen wird, und umgekehrt; was, um anschaulich gemacht zu werden, einer weitläufigern Exposition bedürfte, als hier gegeben werden könnte; aber das Nöthige kommt späterhin beim umgekehrten Verhältniß vor.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0001","text":"Attraktion und Repulsion pflegen bekanntlich als Kräfte angesehen zu werden. Diese ihre Bestimmung und die damit zusammenhängende Verhältnisse sind mit den Begriffen, die sich für sie ergeben haben, zu vergleichen.—In jener Vorstellung werden sie als selbstständig betrachtet, so daß sie sich nicht durch ihre Natur auf einander beziehen, d. h. daß nicht jede nur ein in ihre entgegengesetzte übergehendes Moment seyn, sondern fest der andern gegenüber beharren soll. Sie werden ferner vorgestellt, als in einem Dritten, der Materie, zusammenkommend; so jedoch, daß dieß In-Eins-Werden nicht als ihre Wahrheit gilt, sondern jede vielmehr ein Erstes und An-und-fürsich-Seyendes, die Materie aber oder Bestimmungen derselben durch sie gesetzt und hervorgebracht seyen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"53.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0002","text":"Wenn gesagt wird, daß die Materie die Kräfte in sich habe, so ist unter dieser ihrer Einheit eine Verknüpfung verstanden, wobei sie zugleich als in sich seyende frei von einander vorausgesetzt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"53.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0003","text":"Kant hat bekanntlich die Materie aus der Repulsivund AttraktivKraft konstruirt oder wenigstens, wie er sich ausdrückt, die metaphysischen Elemente dieser Konstruction aufgestellt.—Es wird nicht ohne Interesse seyn, diese Konstruction näher zu beleuchten. Diese metaphysische Darstellung eines Gegenstandes, der nicht nur selbst, sondern in seinen Bestimmungen, nur der Erfahrung anzugehören schien, ist eines Theils dadurch merkwürdig, daß sie als ein Versuch des Begriffs wenigstens den Anstoß zur neueren Naturphilosophie gegeben hat,—der Philosophie, welche die Natur nicht als ein der Wahrnehmung sinnlich Gegebenes zum Grunde der Wissenschaft macht, sondern ihre Bestimmungen aus dem absoluten Begriffe erkennt; andern Theils auch, weil bei jener Kantischen Konstruktion noch häufig stehen geblieben und sie für einen philosophischen Anfang und Grundlage der Physik gehalten wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"53.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0004","text":"Eine solche Existenz, wie die sinnliche Materie, ist zwar nicht ein Gegenstand der Logik, eben so wenig als der Raum und Raumbestimmungen. Aber auch der Attraktiv- und Repulsiv-Kraft, sofern sie als Kräfte der sinnlichen Materie angesehen werden, liegen die hier betrachteten reinen Bestimmungen vom Eins und Vielen, und deren Beziehungen aufeinander, die ich Repulsion und Attraktion, weil diese Namen am nächsten liegen, genannt habe, zu Grunde.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"53.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0005","text":"Kants Verfahren in der Deduktion der Materie aus diesen Kräften, das er eine Konstruktion nennt, verdient, näher betrachtet, diesen Namen nicht, wenn nicht anders jede Art voll Reflexion, selbst die analysirende, eine Konstruktion genannt wird, wie denn freilich spätere Naturphilosophen auch das flachste Raisonnement und das grundloseste Gebräue einer willkürlichen Einbildungskraft und gedankenlosen Reflexion,—das besonders die sogenannten Faktoren der Attraktivkraft und Repulsivkraft gebrauchte und allenthalben vorbrachte,—ein Konstruiren genannt haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"53.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0006","text":"Kants Verfahren ist nämlich Im Grunde analytisch, nicht konstruirend. Er setzt die Vorstellung der Materie voraus, und fragt nun, welche Kräfte dazu gehören, um ihre vorausgesetzten Bestimmungen zu erhalten. So fordert er also eines Theils die Attraktivkraft darum, weil durch die Repulsion allein, ohne Attraktion, eigentlich keine Materie daseyn könnte. (Anfangsgr. der Naturwissensch. S. 53f.) Die Repulsion andern Theils, leitet er gleichfalls aus der Materie ab, und giebt als Grund derselben an, weil wir uns die Materie undurchdringlich vorstellen, indem diese nämlich dem Sinne des Gefühls, durch den sie sich uns offenbare, sich unter dieser Bestimmung präsentirt. Die Repulsion werde daher ferner sogleich im Begriffe der Materie gedacht, weil sie damit unmittelbar gegeben sey; die Attraktion dagegen werde derselben durch Schlüsse beigefügt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"53.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0007","text":"Auch diesen Schlüssen aber liegt das so eben Gesagte zu Grunde, daß eine Materie, die bloß Repulsivkraft hätte, das, was wir uns unter Materie vorstellen, nicht erschöpfte.—Dieß ist, wie erhellt, das Verfahren des über die Erfahrung reflektirenden Erkennens, das zuerst in der Erscheinung Bestimmungen wahrnimmt, diese nun zu Grunde legt, und für das sogenannte Erklären derselben entsprechende Grundstoffe oder Kräfte annimmt, welche jene Bestimmungen der Erscheinung hervorbringen sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"53.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0008","text":"In Ansehung des angeführten Unterschieds, wie die Repulsivkraft und wie die Attraktivkraft von dem Erkennen in der Materie gefunden werde, bemerkt Kant weiter, daß die Attraktivkraft zwar eben sowohl zum Begriffe der Materie gehöre, ob sie gleich nicht darin enthalten sey. Kant zeichnet diesen letztern Ausdruck aus. Es ist aber nicht abzusehen, welcher Unterschied darin liegen soll; denn eine Bestimmung, die zum Begriffe einer Sache gehört, muß wahrhaftig darin enthalten seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"53.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0009","text":"Was die Schwierigkeit macht und diese leere Ausflucht herbeiführt, besteht darin, daß Kant zum Begriffe der Materie von vorn herein einseitig nur die Bestimmung der Undurchdringlichkeit rechnet, die wir durch das Gefühl wahrnehmen sollen, weswegen die Repulsivkraft, als das Abhalten eines Anderen von sich, unmittelbar gegeben sey. Wenn aber ferner die Materie ohne Attraktivkraft nicht soll daseyn können, so liegt für diese Behauptung eine aus der Wahrnehmung genommene Vorstellung der Materie zu Grunde; die Bestimmung der Attraktion muß also gleichfalls in der Wahrnehmung anzutreffen seyn. Es ist auch wohl wahrzunehmen, daß die Materie außer ihrem Fürsichseyn, welches das Seyn-fur-Anderes aufhebt, (den Widerstand leistet), auch eine Beziehung des Fürsichseyenden aufeinander, räumliche Ausdehnung und Zusammenhalt, und in Starrheit, Festigkeit einen sehr festen Zusammenhalt hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"53.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0010","text":"Die erklärende Physik erfordert zum Zerreißen u.s.f. eines Körpers eine Kraft, welche starker sey, als die Attraktion der Theile desselben gegeneinander. Aus dieser Wahrnehmung kann die Reflexion eben so unmittelbar die Attraktivkraft ableiten, oder sie als gegeben annehmen, als sie es mit der Repulsivkraft that. In der That, wenn die kantischen Schlüsse, aus denen die Attraktivkraft abgeleitet werden soll, betrachtet werden (der Beweis des Lehrsatzes: daß die Möglichkeit der Materie eine Anziehungskraft als zweite Grundkraft erfordere a. a. O.), so enthalten sie nichts, als daß durch die bloße Repulsion die Materie nicht räumlich seyn würde. Indem die Materie, als Raum erfüllend vorausgesetzt ist, ist ihr die Kontinuität zugeschrieben, als deren Grund die Anziehungskraft angenommen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"53.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0011","text":"Wenn nun solche sogenannte Konstruktion der Materie höchstens ein analytisches Verdienst hätte, das noch durch die unreine Darstellung geschmälert würde, so ist der Grundgedanke immer sehr zu schätzen, die Materie aus diesen zwei entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen als ihren Grundkräften zu erkennen. Es ist Kant vornehmlich um die Verbannung der gemein-mechanischen Vorstellungsweise zu thun, die bei der einen Bestimmung, der Undurchdringlichkeit, der für-sich-seyenden Punktualität, stehen bleibt, und die entgegengesetzte Bestimmung, die Beziehung der Materie in sich oder mehrerer Materien, die wieder als besondere Eins angesehen werden, aufeinander, zu etwas Äußerlichem macht;—die Vorstellungsweise, welche, wie Kant sagt, sonst keine bewegenden Kräfte, als nur durch Druck und Stoß, also nur durch Einwirkung von Aussen, einräumen will.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"53.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0012","text":"Diese Äußerlichkeit des Erkennens setzt die Bewegung immer schon als der Materie äußerlich vorhanden voraus, und denkt nicht daran, sie als etwas Innerliches zu fassen, und sie selbst in der Materie zu begreifen, welche eben damit für sich als bewegungslos und als träge angenommen wird. Dieser Standpunkt hat nur die gemeine Mechanik, nicht die immanente und freie Bewegung vor sich.—Indem Kant jene Äußerlichkeit zwar insofern aufhebt, als er die Attraktion, die Beziehung der Materien auf einander, insofern diese als von einander getrennt angenommen werden, oder der Materie überhaupt in ihrem Außersichseyn, zu einer Kraft der Materie selbst macht, so bleiben jedoch auf der anderen Seite seine beiden Grundkräfte, innerhalb der Materie, äußerliche und für sich selbstständige gegen einander.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"53.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0013","text":"So nichtig der selbstständige Unterschied dieser beiden Kräfte, der ihnen vom Standpunkte jenes Erkennens beigelegt wird, war, ebenso nichtig muß sich jeder andere Unterschied, der in Ansehung ihrer Inhaltsbestimmung als etwas Festseyn-Sollendes gemacht wird, zeigen, weil sie, wie sie oben in ihrer Wahrheit betrachtet wurden, nur Momente sind, die in einander übergehen.—Ich betrachte diese fernern Unterschiedsbestimmunge, wie sie Kant angiebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"53.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0014","text":"Er bestimmt nämlich die Attraktivkraft als eine durchdringende Kraft, wodurch eine Materie auf die Theile der anderen auch über die Fläche der Berührung hinaus unmittelbar wirken könne, die Repulsivkraft dagegen als eine Flächenkraft, dadurch Materien nur in der gemeinschaftlichen Fläche der Berührung auf einander wirken können. Der Grund, der angeführt wird, daß die letztere nur eine Flächenkraft seyn soll, ist folgender: \"Die einander berührenden Theile begrenzen einer den Wirkungsraum des andern, und die repulsive Kraft könne keinen entferntern Theil bewegen, ohne vermittelst der dazwischen liegenden; eine quer durch diese gehende unmittelbare Wirkung einer Materie auf eine andere durch Ausdehnungskräfte (das heißt hier Repulsivkräfte) sey unmöglich.\" (s. ebendas. Erklär. u. Zusätze S. 67.)","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"53.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0015","text":"Es ist sogleich zu erinnern, daß, indem nähere oder entferntere Theile der Materie angenommen werden, in Rücksicht auf die Attraktion gleichfalls der Unterschied entstünde, daß ein Atom zwar auf ein anderes einwirkte, aber ein drittes Entfernteres, zwischen welchem und dem ersten Attrahirenden das Andere sich befände, zunächst in die Anziehungssphäre des dazwischen liegenden ihm Nähern träte, das Erste also nicht eine unmittelbare einfache Wirkung auf das Dritte ausüben würde; woraus sich eben so ein vermitteltes Wirken für die Attractivkraft, als für die Repulsivkraft ergehe; ferner müßte das wahre Durchdringen der Attraktivkraft allein darin bestehen, daß alle Theile der Materie an und für sich attrahirend wären, nicht aber eine gewisse Menge passiv und nur Ein Atom aktiv sich verhielte.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"53.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0016","text":"—Unmittelbar oder in Rücksicht auf die Repulsivkraft selbst aber ist zu bemerken, daß in der angeführten Stelle sich berührende Theile, also eine Gediegenheit und Kontinuität einer fertigen Materie vorkommt, welche durch sich hindurch ein Repelliren nicht gestatte. Diese Gediegenheit der Materie aber, in welcher Theile sich berühren, nicht mehr durch das Leere getrennt sind, setzt das Aufgehobenseyn der Repulsivkraft bereits voraus; sich berührende Theile sind nach der hier herrschenden sinnlichen Vorstellung der Repulsion als solche zu nehmen, die sich nicht repelliren. Es folgt also ganz tautologisch, daß da, wo das Nichtseyn der Repulsion angenommen ist, keine Repulsion Statt finden kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"53.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0017","text":"Daraus aber folgt nichts weiter für eine Bestimmung der Repulsivkraft.—Wird aber darauf reflektirt, daß berührende Theile sich nur insofern berühren, als sie sich noch außereinander halten, so ist eben damit die Repulsivkraft nicht bloß auf der Oberfläche der Materie, sondern innerhalb der Sphäre, welche nur Sphäre der Attraktion seyn sollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"53.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0018","text":"Weiter nimmt Kant die Bestimmung an, daß \"durch die Anziehungskraft die Materie einen Raum nur einnehme, ohne ihn zu erfüllen;\" (ebendas.) \"weil die Materie durch die Anziehungskraft den Raum nicht erfülle, so könne diese durch den leeren Raum wirken, indem ihr keine Materie, die dazwischen läge, Grenzen setze.\"—Jener Unterschied ist ungefähr wie der obige beschaffen, wo eine Bestimmung zum Begriffe einer Sache gehören, aber nicht darin enthalten seyn sollte, so soll hier die Materie einen Raum nur einnehmen, ihn aber nicht erfüllen. Alsdenn ist es die Repulsion, wenn wir bei ihrer ersten Bestimmung stehen bleiben, durch welche sich die Eins abstossen und nur negativ, das heißt hier, durch den leeren Raum, sich aufeinander beziehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"53.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0019","text":"Hier aber ist es die Attraktivkraft, welche den Raum leer erhält; sie erfüllt den Raum durch ihre Beziehung der Atome nicht, das heißt, sie erhält die Atome in einer negativen Beziehung auf einander.—Wir sehen, daß hier Kant bewußtlos das begegnet, was in der Natur der Sache liegt, daß er der Attraktivkraft gerade das zuschreibt, was er der ersten Bestimmung nach, der entgegengesetzten Kraft zuschrieb. Unter dem Geschäfte der Festsetzung des Unterschiedes beider Kräfte, war es geschehen, daß eine in die andere übergegangen war.—So soll dagegen durch die Repulsion die Materie einen Raum erfüllen, somit durch sie der leere Raum, den die Attraktivkraft läßt, verschwinden, In der That hebt sie somit, indem sie den leeren Raum aufhebt, die negative Beziehung der Atome oder Eins, d. h. die Repulsion derselben, auf; d. i. die Repulsion ist als das Gegentheil ihrer selbst bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"53.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0020","text":"Zu dieser Verwischung der Unterschiede kommt noch die Verwirrung hinzu, daß, wie anfangs bemerkt worden, die Kantische Darstellung der entgegengesetzten Kräfte analytisch ist, und in dem ganzen Vortrage, die Materie, die erst aus ihren Elementen hergeleitet werden soll, bereits als fertig und konstituirt vorkommt. In der Definition der Flächen- und der durchdringenden Kraft werden beide als bewegende Kräfte angenommen, dadurch Materien auf die eine oder die andere Weise sollen wirken können.—Sie sind also hier als Kräfte dargestellt, nicht durch welche die Materie erst zu Stande käme, sondern wodurch sie, schon fertig, nur bewegt würde. Insofern aber von Kräften die Rede ist, wodurch verschiedene Materien auf einander einwirken und sich bewegen, so ist dieß etwas ganz anderes, als die Bestimmung und Beziehung, die sie als die Momente der Materie haben sollten.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"53.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0021","text":"Denselben Gegensatz, als Attraktiv- und Repulsivkraft machen in weiterer Bestimmung Centripetal- und Centrifugalkraft. Diese scheinen einen wesentlichen Unterschied zu gewähren, indem in ihrer Sphäre Ein Eins, ein Centrum, feststeht, gegen das sich die anderen Eins als nicht fürsichseyende verhalten, der Unterschied der Kräfte daher an diesen vorausgesetzten Unterschied Eines centralen Eins und der anderen als gegen dasselbe nicht feststehend angeknüpft werden kann. Insofern sie aber zur Erklärung gebraucht werden—zu welchem Behuf man sie, wie auch sonst die Repulsiv- und Attraktivkraft, in entgegengesetztem quantitativem Verhältniß annimmt, so daß die eine zunehme, wie die andere abnehme, so soll die Erscheinung der Bewegung, für deren Erklärung sie angenommen sind, und deren Ungleichheit erst aus ihnen resultiren.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"53.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0022","text":"Man braucht aber nur die nächste beste Darstellung einer Erscheinung, z.B. die ungleiche Geschwindigkeit, die ein Planet in seiner Bahn um seinen Centralkörper hat, aus dem Gegensatze jener Kräfte, vor sich nehmen, so erkennt man bald die Verwirrung, die darin herrscht, und die Unmöglichkeit, die Größen derselben auseinander zu bringen, so daß immer eben so diejenige als zunehmend anzunehmen ist, welche in der Erklärung als abnehmend angenommen wird, und umgekehrt; was, um anschaulich gemacht zu werden, einer weitläufigern Exposition bedürfte, als hier gegeben werden könnte; aber das Nöthige kommt späterhin beim umgekehrten Verhältniß vor.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"53.22"}],"sha256":"5bdeea4f52ba20a4ea34fece0d9cf666597a81d1bea29c39bb21c0f1ab137c0b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102707210931Z_4c18be8e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"5bdeea4f52ba20a4ea34fece0d9cf666597a81d1bea29c39bb21c0f1ab137c0b","sha256":"8c5aa5e7f76f87fc883e40fd7aa7cd4aae6e0f838d3c11489581e70483f7a11f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:27:07.210960+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0001","text":"Attraction and repulsion are, as is well known, customarily regarded as forces. This determination of them and the relations connected with it are to be compared with the concepts that have emerged for them.—In that representation they are regarded as self-subsistent, so that by their nature they do not relate to one another, i.e. so that each is not merely a moment passing over into its opposite, but is supposed to persist fixedly over against the other. They are further represented as coming together in a third, matter; yet in such a way that this becoming-one is not valid as their truth, but rather each is a first and a being-in-and-for-itself, while matter, or determinations of it, are posited and produced by them.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"53.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0002","text":"When it is said that matter has the forces within itself, what is understood by this unity of matter is a connection in which they are at the same time presupposed as free from one another, existing within themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"53.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0003","text":"Kant, as is well known, constructed matter out of repulsive and attractive force, or at least, as he expresses it, set forth the metaphysical elements of this construction.—It will not be without interest to elucidate this construction more closely. This metaphysical presentation of an object which seemed to belong only to experience, not merely itself but also in its determinations, is noteworthy, on the one hand, because, as an attempt of the concept, it at least gave the impetus to modern philosophy of nature,—to the philosophy which does not make nature, as something sensuously given to perception, the foundation of science, but cognizes its determinations from the absolute concept; on the other hand, because people still frequently remain at that Kantian construction and take it for a philosophical beginning and foundation of physics.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"53.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0004","text":"An existence such as sensuous matter is indeed not an object of logic, any more than space and spatial determinations are. But the attractive and repulsive force, insofar as they are regarded as forces of sensuous matter, are likewise grounded in the pure determinations of the one and the many considered here, and their relations to one another, which I have called repulsion and attraction because these names lie nearest at hand.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"53.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0005","text":"Kant’s procedure in the deduction of matter from these forces, which he calls a construction, does not deserve this name upon closer consideration, unless every kind of reflection, even analytical reflection, is to be called a construction; as indeed later philosophers of nature have also called a constructing the flattest ratiocination and the most groundless concoction of an arbitrary imagination and thoughtless reflection,—which especially employed and brought forth everywhere the so-called factors of attractive force and repulsive force.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"53.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0006","text":"Kant’s procedure is in fact analytical, not constructive. He presupposes the representation of matter and then asks which forces belong to it in order to preserve its presupposed determinations. Thus, on the one hand, he requires attractive force because through repulsion alone, without attraction, properly speaking no matter could exist. (First Principles of Natural Science, pp. 53f.) On the other hand, he likewise derives repulsion from matter, and gives as its ground that we represent matter as impenetrable, since it presents itself to us under this determination through the sense of feeling, by which it reveals itself to us. Repulsion is therefore, further, thought immediately in the concept of matter, because it is immediately given with it; attraction, on the contrary, is added to it through inferences.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"53.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0007","text":"But these inferences too are grounded in what has just been said: that a matter which had merely repulsive force would not exhaust what we represent under matter.—This is, as is evident, the procedure of cognition reflecting upon experience, which first perceives determinations in appearance, then lays these down as the basis, and for the so-called explanation of them assumes corresponding basic materials or forces which are supposed to bring forth those determinations of appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"53.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0008","text":"With regard to the stated difference as to how repulsive force and how attractive force are found by cognition in matter, Kant further remarks that attractive force indeed equally belongs to the concept of matter, although it is not contained in it. Kant distinguishes this latter expression. Yet it is not apparent what difference this is supposed to involve; for a determination that belongs to the concept of a thing must assuredly be contained in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"53.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0009","text":"What creates the difficulty and brings about this empty evasion consists in Kant’s reckoning, from the outset, only the determination of impenetrability one-sidedly as belonging to the concept of matter, which we are supposed to perceive through feeling, and for that reason repulsive force, as the holding off of another from itself, is immediately given. But if matter is further not supposed to be able to exist without attractive force, then a representation of matter taken from perception lies at the basis of this assertion; thus the determination of attraction must likewise be found in perception. It can indeed be perceived that matter, besides its being-for-self, which sublates being-for-another (offers resistance), also has a relation of beings-for-self to one another, spatial extension and cohesion, and in rigidity, solidity, a very firm cohesion.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"53.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0010","text":"Explanatory physics requires, for the tearing apart, etc. of a body, a force stronger than the attraction of its parts toward one another. From this perception reflection can derive attractive force just as immediately, or assume it as given, as it did with repulsive force. Indeed, if the Kantian inferences by which attractive force is supposed to be derived are considered (the proof of the proposition: that the possibility of matter requires an attractive force as a second fundamental force, loc. cit.), they contain nothing but that through mere repulsion matter would not be spatial. Since matter is presupposed as filling space, continuity is ascribed to it, attraction being assumed as the ground of this.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"53.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0011","text":"If, then, such so-called construction of matter had at most an analytical merit, which would moreover be diminished by its impure presentation, the fundamental thought is nevertheless greatly to be esteemed: to cognize matter from these two opposed determinations as its fundamental forces. Kant is chiefly concerned with banishing the common-mechanical mode of representation, which remains with the one determination, impenetrability, punctuality existing-for-itself, and makes the opposed determination, the relation of matter within itself or of several matters, which are again regarded as particular ones, to one another, into something external;—the mode of representation which, as Kant says, otherwise wishes to admit no moving forces except through pressure and impact, thus only through influence from without.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"53.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0012","text":"This externality of cognition always presupposes movement as already externally present to matter, and does not think of grasping it as something inner and comprehending it in matter itself, which precisely thereby is assumed to be motionless for itself and inert. This standpoint has before it only common mechanics, not immanent and free movement.—While Kant indeed sublates that externality insofar as he makes attraction, the relation of matters to one another, insofar as these are assumed to be separated from one another, or of matter in general in its being-outside-itself, into a force of matter itself, nevertheless, on the other side, his two fundamental forces remain external and self-subsistent toward one another within matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"53.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0013","text":"As nugatory as was the self-subsistent difference between these two forces which is ascribed to them from the standpoint of that cognition, so nugatory must every other difference, made with regard to their determination of content as something that is supposed to be fixed, show itself; for, as they were considered above in their truth, they are only moments that pass over into one another.—I shall consider these further determinations of difference as Kant gives them.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"53.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0014","text":"He determines attractive force, namely, as a penetrating force, through which one matter can act immediately upon the parts of another even beyond the surface of contact; repulsive force, on the contrary, as a surface force, through which matters can act upon one another only at the common surface of contact. The ground adduced for the latter’s being only a surface force is as follows: “The mutually touching parts limit, each, the sphere of action of the other, and the repulsive force could not move a more distant part except by means of those lying between; an immediate action, passing transversely through these, of one matter upon another by expansive forces (that is, here, repulsive forces) is impossible.” (See ibid., Explanations and Additions, p. 67.)","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"53.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0015","text":"It is immediately to be noted that, if nearer or more distant parts of matter are assumed, a difference would likewise arise with respect to attraction: that one atom would indeed act upon another, but that a third, more distant one, between which and the first attracting atom the other were situated, would first enter into the sphere of attraction of the nearer one lying between; the first would thus not exert an immediate simple action upon the third. From this there would result a mediated action for attractive force just as much as for repulsive force; further, the true penetration of attractive force would have to consist solely in all parts of matter being in and for themselves attractive, and not in a certain quantity behaving passively while only one atom behaved actively.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"53.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0016","text":"—Immediately, however, or with regard to repulsive force itself, it is to be noted that the cited passage speaks of touching parts, hence of a solidity and continuity of finished matter which would not permit a repelling through itself. But this solidity of matter, in which parts touch each other and are no longer separated by the void, already presupposes the sublatedness of repulsive force; touching parts are, according to the sensuous representation of repulsion prevailing here, to be taken as such as do not repel each other. Thus it follows quite tautologically that where the non-being of repulsion is assumed, no repulsion can take place.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"53.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0017","text":"But nothing further follows from this for a determination of repulsive force.—If, however, reflection is made upon the fact that touching parts touch only insofar as they still hold themselves apart from one another, then repulsive force is thereby not merely on the surface of matter, but within the sphere which was supposed to be only the sphere of attraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"53.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0018","text":"Kant further assumes the determination that “through attractive force matter merely occupies a space without filling it”; (ibid.) “because matter does not fill space through attractive force, this force can act through empty space, since no matter lying between sets bounds to it.”—That difference is approximately of the same kind as the preceding one, where a determination was supposed to belong to the concept of a thing without being contained in it; so here matter is supposed merely to occupy a space, yet not to fill it. Then it is repulsion, if we remain with its first determination, through which the ones repel themselves and relate to one another only negatively, that is here, through empty space.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"53.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0019","text":"But here it is attractive force that keeps space empty; it does not fill space by means of its relation of the atoms, that is, it maintains the atoms in a negative relation to one another.—We see that here Kant unconsciously encounters what lies in the nature of the matter: he ascribes to attractive force precisely what, according to the first determination, he ascribed to the opposed force. In the business of fixing the difference between the two forces, one had passed over into the other.—Conversely, matter is supposed to fill a space through repulsion, and hence through it the empty space left by attractive force is to disappear. In fact, therefore, in sublating empty space, it sublates the negative relation of the atoms or ones, i.e. their repulsion; that is, repulsion is determined as the opposite of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"53.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0020","text":"To this obliteration of the differences is added the confusion that, as was remarked at the outset, the Kantian presentation of the opposed forces is analytical, and throughout the exposition matter, which is only supposed to be derived from its elements, already appears as finished and constituted. In the definition of surface force and penetrating force, both are assumed as moving forces through which matters are supposed to be able to act in one way or another.—Thus they are here presented as forces not through which matter would first come about, but through which it, already finished, would merely be moved. But insofar as forces are under discussion through which different matters act upon one another and move themselves, this is something altogether different from the determination and relation which they were supposed to have as the moments of matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"53.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0021","text":"The same opposition, as attractive and repulsive force, assumes a further determination as centripetal and centrifugal force. These seem to afford an essential difference, inasmuch as, in their sphere, a one, a centre, stands firm, in relation to which the other ones behave as not being-for-self; the difference of the forces can therefore be linked to this presupposed difference of one central one and of the others as not standing firm in relation to it. But insofar as they are used for explanation—for which purpose they, like attractive and repulsive force otherwise, are assumed in an opposite quantitative relation, such that the one increases as the other decreases—the phenomenon of motion, for the explanation of which they are assumed, and whose inequality is first supposed to result from them.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"53.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_10:P0022","text":"But one need only take up the nearest best presentation of a phenomenon, e.g. the unequal velocity that a planet has in its orbit about its central body, from the opposition of those forces, and one soon recognizes the confusion prevailing therein, and the impossibility of disentangling their magnitudes, so that the very force which is assumed to be decreasing in the explanation must equally be assumed to be increasing, and conversely; which, in order to be made intuitive, would require a more extensive exposition than could be given here; but what is necessary occurs later in the inverse relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"53.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_10:P0022"]}],"source_digest":"ac3c06d27471dc039ce0e987a1d2244e8f775e1e7be109f6a74e4b8dd7896269","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11","title":"Remark.","order":54,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_11","text":"## Zweiter Abschnitt. Die Größe (Quantität).\n\nDer Unterschied der Quantität von der Qualität ist angegeben worden. Die Qualität ist die erste, unmittelbare Bestimmtheit, die Quantität die Bestimmtheit, die dem Seyn gleichgültig geworden, eine Grenze, die eben so sehr keine ist; das Fürsichseyn, das schlechthin identisch mit dem Seyn-für-Anderes,—die Repulsion der vielen Eins, die unmittelbar Nicht-Repulsion, Kontinuität derselben ist.\n\nWeil das Fürsichseyende nun so gesetzt ist, sein Anderes nicht auszuschließen, sondern sich in dasselbe vielmehr affirmativ fortzusetzen, so ist das Andersseyn, insofern das Daseyn an dieser Kontinuität wieder hervortritt, und die Bestimmtheit desselben zugleich nicht mehr als in einfacher Beziehung auf sich, nicht mehr unmittelbare Bestimmtheit des daseyenden Etwas, sondern ist gesetzt, sich als repellirend von sich, die Beziehung auf sich als Bestimmtheit vielmehr in einem anderen Daseyn (einem für-sich-seyenden) zu haben, und indem sie zugleich als gleichgültige in sich reflektirte, beziehungslose Grenzen sind, so ist die Bestimmtheit überhaupt außer sich, ein sich schlechthin Äußerliches und Etwas ebenso Äußerliches; solche Grenze, die Gleichgültigkeit derselben an ihr selbst und des Etwas gegen sie, macht die quantitative Bestimmtheit desselben aus.\n\nZunächst ist die reine Quantität von ihr als bestimmter Quantität, vom Quantum, zu unterscheiden. Als jene ist sie erstens das in sich zurückgekehrte, reale Fürsichseyn, das noch keine Bestimmtheit an ihm hat; als gediegene sich in sich kontinuirende unendliche Einheit.\n\nDiese geht zweitens zu der Bestimmtheit fort, die an ihr gesetzt wird, als solche, die zugleich keine, nur äußerliche ist. Sie wird Quantum. Das Quantum ist die gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, d. h. die über sich hinausgehende, sich selbst negirende; es verfällt als dieß Andersseyn des Andersseyn in den unendlichen Progreß. Das unendliche Quantum aber ist die aufgehobene gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, es ist die Wiederherstellung der Qualität.\n\nDrittens, das Quantum in qualitativer Form ist das quantitative Verhältniß. Das Quantum geht nur überhaupt über sich hinaus; im Verhältnisse aber geht es so über s sich in sein Andersseyn hinaus, daß dieses, in welchem es seine Bestimmung hat, zugleich gesetzt, ein anderes Quantum ist; somit sein In-sich-zurückgekehrtseyn und die Beziehung auf sich als in seinem Andersseyn vorhanden ist.\n\nDiesem Verhältnisse liegt noch die Äußerlichkeit des Quantums zu Grunde, es sind gleichgültige Quanta, die sich zu einander verhalten, d. i. ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst in solchem Außersichseyn haben; —das Verhältniß ist damit nur formelle Einheit der Qualität und Quantität. Die Dialektik desselben ist sein Übergang in ihre absolute Einheit, in das Maaß.\n\n## Anmerkung.\n\nAm Etwas ist seine Grenze als Qualität wesentlich seine Bestimmtheit. Wenn wir aber unter Grenze die quantitative Grenze verstehen, und z. B. ein Acker diese seine Grenze verändert, so bleibt er Acker vor wie nach. Wenn hingegen seine qualitative Grenze verändert wird, so ist dieß seine Bestimmtheit, wodurch er Acker ist, und er wird Wiese, Wald u.s.f.-Ein Roth, das intensiver oder schwächer ist, ist immer Roth; wenn es aber seine Qualität änderte, so hörte es auf Roth zu seyn, es würde Blau u.s.f.—Die Bestimmung der Größe als Quantum, wie sie sich oben ergeben hat, daß ein Seyn als Bleibendes zu Grunde liegt, das gegen die Bestimmtheit, die es hat, gleichgültig ist, ergiebt sich an jedem anderen Beispiel.\n\nUnter dem Ausdruck Größe wird das Quantum, wie an den angegebenen Beispielen, verstanden, nicht die Quantität, weswegen wesentlich dieser Name aus der fremden Sprache gebraucht werden muß.\n\nDie Definition, welche in der Mathematik von der Größe gegeben wird, betrifft gleichfalls das Quantum. Gewöhnlich wird eine Größe definirt, als etwas, das sich vermehren oder vermindern läßt. Vermehren aber heißt, etwas mehr groß, vermindern weniger groß machen. Es liegt darin ein Unterschied der Größe überhaupt von ihr selbst, und die Größe wäre also das, dessen Größe sich verändern läßt. Die Definition zeigt sich insofern als ungeschickt, als in ihr diejenige Bestimmung selbst gebraucht wird, welche definirt werden sollte. Insofern in ihr nicht dieselbe Bestimmung zu gebrauchen ist, ist das Mehr und Weniger in einen Zusatz als Affirmation und zwar nach der Natur des Quantums als eine gleichfalls äußerliche, und in ein Wegnehmen, als eine ebenso äußerliche Negation, aufzulösen. Zu dieser äußerlichen Weise sowohl der Realität als der Negation bestimmt sich überhaupt die Natur der Veränderung am Quantum. Daher ist in jenem unvollkommenen Ausdruck das Hauptmoment nicht zu verkennen, worauf es ankommt; nämlich die Gleichgültigkeit der Veränderung, so daß in ihrem Begriff selbst ihr eigenes Mehr Minder liegt, ihre Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich selbst.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0001","text":"## Zweiter Abschnitt. Die Größe (Quantität).","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"54.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0002","text":"Der Unterschied der Quantität von der Qualität ist angegeben worden. Die Qualität ist die erste, unmittelbare Bestimmtheit, die Quantität die Bestimmtheit, die dem Seyn gleichgültig geworden, eine Grenze, die eben so sehr keine ist; das Fürsichseyn, das schlechthin identisch mit dem Seyn-für-Anderes,—die Repulsion der vielen Eins, die unmittelbar Nicht-Repulsion, Kontinuität derselben ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"54.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0003","text":"Weil das Fürsichseyende nun so gesetzt ist, sein Anderes nicht auszuschließen, sondern sich in dasselbe vielmehr affirmativ fortzusetzen, so ist das Andersseyn, insofern das Daseyn an dieser Kontinuität wieder hervortritt, und die Bestimmtheit desselben zugleich nicht mehr als in einfacher Beziehung auf sich, nicht mehr unmittelbare Bestimmtheit des daseyenden Etwas, sondern ist gesetzt, sich als repellirend von sich, die Beziehung auf sich als Bestimmtheit vielmehr in einem anderen Daseyn (einem für-sich-seyenden) zu haben, und indem sie zugleich als gleichgültige in sich reflektirte, beziehungslose Grenzen sind, so ist die Bestimmtheit überhaupt außer sich, ein sich schlechthin Äußerliches und Etwas ebenso Äußerliches; solche Grenze, die Gleichgültigkeit derselben an ihr selbst und des Etwas gegen sie, macht die quantitative Bestimmtheit desselben aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"54.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0004","text":"Zunächst ist die reine Quantität von ihr als bestimmter Quantität, vom Quantum, zu unterscheiden. Als jene ist sie erstens das in sich zurückgekehrte, reale Fürsichseyn, das noch keine Bestimmtheit an ihm hat; als gediegene sich in sich kontinuirende unendliche Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"54.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0005","text":"Diese geht zweitens zu der Bestimmtheit fort, die an ihr gesetzt wird, als solche, die zugleich keine, nur äußerliche ist. Sie wird Quantum. Das Quantum ist die gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, d. h. die über sich hinausgehende, sich selbst negirende; es verfällt als dieß Andersseyn des Andersseyn in den unendlichen Progreß. Das unendliche Quantum aber ist die aufgehobene gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, es ist die Wiederherstellung der Qualität.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"54.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0006","text":"Drittens, das Quantum in qualitativer Form ist das quantitative Verhältniß. Das Quantum geht nur überhaupt über sich hinaus; im Verhältnisse aber geht es so über s sich in sein Andersseyn hinaus, daß dieses, in welchem es seine Bestimmung hat, zugleich gesetzt, ein anderes Quantum ist; somit sein In-sich-zurückgekehrtseyn und die Beziehung auf sich als in seinem Andersseyn vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"54.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0007","text":"Diesem Verhältnisse liegt noch die Äußerlichkeit des Quantums zu Grunde, es sind gleichgültige Quanta, die sich zu einander verhalten, d. i. ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst in solchem Außersichseyn haben; —das Verhältniß ist damit nur formelle Einheit der Qualität und Quantität. Die Dialektik desselben ist sein Übergang in ihre absolute Einheit, in das Maaß.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"54.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0008","text":"## Anmerkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"54.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0009","text":"Am Etwas ist seine Grenze als Qualität wesentlich seine Bestimmtheit. Wenn wir aber unter Grenze die quantitative Grenze verstehen, und z. B. ein Acker diese seine Grenze verändert, so bleibt er Acker vor wie nach. Wenn hingegen seine qualitative Grenze verändert wird, so ist dieß seine Bestimmtheit, wodurch er Acker ist, und er wird Wiese, Wald u.s.f.-Ein Roth, das intensiver oder schwächer ist, ist immer Roth; wenn es aber seine Qualität änderte, so hörte es auf Roth zu seyn, es würde Blau u.s.f.—Die Bestimmung der Größe als Quantum, wie sie sich oben ergeben hat, daß ein Seyn als Bleibendes zu Grunde liegt, das gegen die Bestimmtheit, die es hat, gleichgültig ist, ergiebt sich an jedem anderen Beispiel.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"54.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0010","text":"Unter dem Ausdruck Größe wird das Quantum, wie an den angegebenen Beispielen, verstanden, nicht die Quantität, weswegen wesentlich dieser Name aus der fremden Sprache gebraucht werden muß.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"54.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0011","text":"Die Definition, welche in der Mathematik von der Größe gegeben wird, betrifft gleichfalls das Quantum. Gewöhnlich wird eine Größe definirt, als etwas, das sich vermehren oder vermindern läßt. Vermehren aber heißt, etwas mehr groß, vermindern weniger groß machen. Es liegt darin ein Unterschied der Größe überhaupt von ihr selbst, und die Größe wäre also das, dessen Größe sich verändern läßt. Die Definition zeigt sich insofern als ungeschickt, als in ihr diejenige Bestimmung selbst gebraucht wird, welche definirt werden sollte. Insofern in ihr nicht dieselbe Bestimmung zu gebrauchen ist, ist das Mehr und Weniger in einen Zusatz als Affirmation und zwar nach der Natur des Quantums als eine gleichfalls äußerliche, und in ein Wegnehmen, als eine ebenso äußerliche Negation, aufzulösen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"54.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0012","text":"Zu dieser äußerlichen Weise sowohl der Realität als der Negation bestimmt sich überhaupt die Natur der Veränderung am Quantum. Daher ist in jenem unvollkommenen Ausdruck das Hauptmoment nicht zu verkennen, worauf es ankommt; nämlich die Gleichgültigkeit der Veränderung, so daß in ihrem Begriff selbst ihr eigenes Mehr Minder liegt, ihre Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"54.12"}],"sha256":"7c6c86037d1e6522065ae2a00bca679082441062bc8d8af25892209ac64d098b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102718248401Z_7d325a0d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"7c6c86037d1e6522065ae2a00bca679082441062bc8d8af25892209ac64d098b","sha256":"f486b9fba07be2c52b47e743b5dc57ad2e70bd91f303d22410b711d09797e993","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:27:18.248435+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0001","text":"## Second Section. Magnitude (Quantity).","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"54.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0002","text":"The difference of quantity from quality has been indicated. Quality is the first, immediate determinacy; quantity, the determinacy that has become indifferent to being, a limit that just as much is not one; being-for-self, which is absolutely identical with being-for-other—the repulsion of the many ones, which is immediately the non-repulsion, the continuity, of the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"54.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0003","text":"Because that which is for itself is now thus posited, not to exclude its other, but rather affirmatively to continue itself into it, otherness is, insofar as determinate being re-emerges in this continuity, and its determinacy is at the same time no longer as in a simple relation to itself, no longer the immediate determinacy of the determinately existing something, but is posited as repelling itself from itself, as having its relation to itself as determinacy rather in another determinate being (one that is for itself), and, since they are at the same time indifferent limits reflected into themselves, without relation, determinacy in general is outside itself, an absolutely external being, and something equally external; such a limit, its indifference in itself and that of something toward it, constitutes its quantitative determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"54.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0004","text":"First, pure quantity is to be distinguished from it as determinate quantity, from quantum. As the former, it is, first, real being-for-self that has not yet any determinacy in it; as a compact, infinitely self-continuing unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"54.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0005","text":"Second, this proceeds to the determinacy that is posited in it, as one which is at the same time none, merely external. It becomes quantum. Quantum is indifferent determinacy, i.e. determinacy going beyond itself, negating itself; as this otherness of otherness, it falls into infinite progress. But infinite quantum is the sublated indifferent determinacy; it is the restoration of quality.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"54.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0006","text":"Third, quantum in qualitative form is the quantitative relation. Quantum in general merely goes beyond itself; but in the relation it goes beyond itself into its otherness in such a way that this, in which it has its determination, is at the same time posited as another quantum; thus its having-returned-into-itself and the relation to itself are present as in its otherness.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"54.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0007","text":"This relation still has as its basis the externality of quantum; they are indifferent quanta that relate to one another, i.e. have their relation to themselves in such being-outside-themselves;—the relation is thereby only the formal unity of quality and quantity. Its dialectic is its transition into their absolute unity, into measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"54.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0008","text":"## Remark.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"54.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0009","text":"In something, its limit, as quality, is essentially its determinacy. But if by limit we understand the quantitative limit, and, for example, a field changes this its limit, it remains a field both before and after. If, however, its qualitative limit is altered, then this is its determinacy by which it is a field, and it becomes meadow, forest, etc.—A red that is more intense or weaker is always red; but if it altered its quality, it would cease to be red; it would become blue, etc.—The determination of magnitude as quantum, as it has emerged above, namely that a being lies at the basis as something enduring, which is indifferent toward the determinacy it has, is evident in every other example.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"54.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0010","text":"By the expression magnitude is understood quantum, as in the examples given, not quantity; which is why this name must essentially be employed from the foreign language.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"54.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0011","text":"The definition given in mathematics of magnitude likewise concerns quantum. Magnitude is commonly defined as something that can be increased or diminished. But to increase means to make something greater, to diminish, less great. Therein lies a distinction of magnitude in general from itself, and magnitude would therefore be that whose magnitude can be altered. The definition proves to be inept insofar as it employs the very determination that was to be defined. Insofar as the same determination is not to be employed in it, more and less are to be resolved into an addition as affirmation, and indeed, according to the nature of quantum, as one likewise external, and into a taking-away as an equally external negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"54.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_11:P0012","text":"It is in general to this external mode of both reality and negation that the nature of alteration in quantum determines itself. Hence, in that imperfect expression, the principal moment on which it depends is not to be overlooked; namely, the indifference of alteration, such that in its very concept its own more lies as less, its indifference toward itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"54.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_11:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"3e40eea319abc7a21530b04f24db5998c0ad4957b0217b183eb170e2aee3c76a","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT","title":"A. Pure Quantity.","order":55,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DRQT","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Die Quantität.\n\n## A. Die reine Quantität.\n\nDie Quantität ist das aufgehobene Fürsichseyn; das repellirende Eins, das sich gegen das ausgeschlossene Eins nur negativ verhielt, in die Beziehung mit demselben übergegangen, verhält sich identisch zu dem Andern, und hat damit seine Bestimmung verloren; das Fürsichseyn ist in Attraktion übergegangen. Die absolute Sprödigkeit des repellirenden Eins ist in diese Einheit zerflossen, welche aber als dieß Eins enthaltend, durch die innwohnende Repulsion zugleich bestimmt, als Einheit des Außersichseyns Einheit mit sich selbst ist. Die Attraktion ist auf diese Weise als das Moment der Kontinuität in der Quantität.\n\nDie Kontinuität ist also einfache, sich selbst gleiche Beziehung auf sich, die durch keine Grenze und Ausschließung unterbrochen ist, aber nicht unmittelbare Einheit, sondern Einheit der fürsichseyenden Eins. Es ist darin das Außereinander der Vielheit noch enthalten, aber zugleich als ein nicht unterschiedenes, Ununterbrochenes. Die Vielheit ist in der Kontinuität so gesetzt, wie sie an sich ist; die Vielen sind Eins was Andere, jedes dem anderen gleich, und die Vielheit daher einfache, unterschiedslose Gleichheit. Die Kontinuität ist dieses Moment der Sichselbstgleichheit des Außereinanderseyns, das Sich-Fortsetzen der unterschiedenen Eins in ihre von ihnen Unterschiedene.\n\nUnmittelbar hat daher die Größe in der Kontinuität das Moment der Diskretion,—die Repulsion, wie sie nur Moment in der Quantität ist. —Die Stätigkeit ist Sichselbstgleichheit aber des Vielen, das jedoch nicht zum Ausschließenden wird; die Repulsion dehnt erst die Sichselbstgleichheit zur Kontinuität aus. Die Diskretion ist daher ihrer Seits zusammenfliessende Diskretion, deren Eins nicht das Leere, das Negative, zu ihrer Beziehung haben, sondern ihre eigne Stätigkeit, und diese Gleichheit mit sich selbst im Vielen nicht unterbrechen.\n\nDie Quantität ist die Einheit dieser Momente, der Kontinuität und Diskretion, aber sie ist dieß zunächst in der Form des einen derselben, der Kontinuität, als Resultat der Dialektik des Fürsichseyns, das in die Form sich-selbst-gleicher Unmittelbarkeit zusammengefallen ist. Die Quantität ist als solche dieß einfache Resultat, insofern es seine Momente noch nicht entwickelt und an ihm gesetzt hat.—Sie enthält sie zunächst, als das Fürsichseyn gesetzt, wie es in Wahrheit ist. Es war seiner Bestimmung nach das sich aufhebende Beziehen auf sich selbst, perennirendes Außersichkommen. Aber das Abgestoßene ist es selbst; die Repulsion ist daher das erzeugende Fortfließen seiner selbst. Um der Dieselbigkeit willen des Abgestoßenen ist dieß Discerniren, ununterbrochene Kontinuität; und um des Außersichkommens willen, ist diese Kontinuität, ohne unterbrochen zu seyn, zugleich Vielheit, die eben so unmittelbar in ihrer Gleichheit mit sich selbst bleibt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0001","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Die Quantität.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"55.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0002","text":"## A. Die reine Quantität.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"55.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0003","text":"Die Quantität ist das aufgehobene Fürsichseyn; das repellirende Eins, das sich gegen das ausgeschlossene Eins nur negativ verhielt, in die Beziehung mit demselben übergegangen, verhält sich identisch zu dem Andern, und hat damit seine Bestimmung verloren; das Fürsichseyn ist in Attraktion übergegangen. Die absolute Sprödigkeit des repellirenden Eins ist in diese Einheit zerflossen, welche aber als dieß Eins enthaltend, durch die innwohnende Repulsion zugleich bestimmt, als Einheit des Außersichseyns Einheit mit sich selbst ist. Die Attraktion ist auf diese Weise als das Moment der Kontinuität in der Quantität.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"55.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0004","text":"Die Kontinuität ist also einfache, sich selbst gleiche Beziehung auf sich, die durch keine Grenze und Ausschließung unterbrochen ist, aber nicht unmittelbare Einheit, sondern Einheit der fürsichseyenden Eins. Es ist darin das Außereinander der Vielheit noch enthalten, aber zugleich als ein nicht unterschiedenes, Ununterbrochenes. Die Vielheit ist in der Kontinuität so gesetzt, wie sie an sich ist; die Vielen sind Eins was Andere, jedes dem anderen gleich, und die Vielheit daher einfache, unterschiedslose Gleichheit. Die Kontinuität ist dieses Moment der Sichselbstgleichheit des Außereinanderseyns, das Sich-Fortsetzen der unterschiedenen Eins in ihre von ihnen Unterschiedene.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"55.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0005","text":"Unmittelbar hat daher die Größe in der Kontinuität das Moment der Diskretion,—die Repulsion, wie sie nur Moment in der Quantität ist. —Die Stätigkeit ist Sichselbstgleichheit aber des Vielen, das jedoch nicht zum Ausschließenden wird; die Repulsion dehnt erst die Sichselbstgleichheit zur Kontinuität aus. Die Diskretion ist daher ihrer Seits zusammenfliessende Diskretion, deren Eins nicht das Leere, das Negative, zu ihrer Beziehung haben, sondern ihre eigne Stätigkeit, und diese Gleichheit mit sich selbst im Vielen nicht unterbrechen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"55.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0006","text":"Die Quantität ist die Einheit dieser Momente, der Kontinuität und Diskretion, aber sie ist dieß zunächst in der Form des einen derselben, der Kontinuität, als Resultat der Dialektik des Fürsichseyns, das in die Form sich-selbst-gleicher Unmittelbarkeit zusammengefallen ist. Die Quantität ist als solche dieß einfache Resultat, insofern es seine Momente noch nicht entwickelt und an ihm gesetzt hat.—Sie enthält sie zunächst, als das Fürsichseyn gesetzt, wie es in Wahrheit ist. Es war seiner Bestimmung nach das sich aufhebende Beziehen auf sich selbst, perennirendes Außersichkommen. Aber das Abgestoßene ist es selbst; die Repulsion ist daher das erzeugende Fortfließen seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"55.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0007","text":"Um der Dieselbigkeit willen des Abgestoßenen ist dieß Discerniren, ununterbrochene Kontinuität; und um des Außersichkommens willen, ist diese Kontinuität, ohne unterbrochen zu seyn, zugleich Vielheit, die eben so unmittelbar in ihrer Gleichheit mit sich selbst bleibt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"55.7"}],"sha256":"7b7ab9322187444131ac10b9e7334ad579e280cee0ce57a34aec7556b5c2dc9b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102724432732Z_58acf468","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Pure Quantity.","source_sha256":"7b7ab9322187444131ac10b9e7334ad579e280cee0ce57a34aec7556b5c2dc9b","sha256":"4089012d40bb83f494de5916ae098ef7178bb2a53c26db36482f7b784c40094c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:27:24.432743+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0001","text":"## First Chapter. Quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"55.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0002","text":"## A. Pure Quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"55.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0003","text":"Quantity is sublated being-for-self; the repelling one, which related itself only negatively to the excluded one, having passed over into relation with the same, relates identically to the other, and has thereby lost its determinacy; being-for-self has passed over into attraction. The absolute brittleness of the repelling one has dissolved into this unity, which, however, as containing this one and at the same time determined by the repulsion dwelling within it, is, as unity of being-outside-itself, unity with itself. Attraction is in this way the moment of continuity in quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"55.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0004","text":"Continuity is thus simple, self-identical relation to itself, which is interrupted by no limit and exclusion, but is not immediate unity, rather unity of the ones that are for themselves. The apartness of plurality is still contained therein, but at the same time as an undistinguished, uninterrupted apartness. Plurality is posited in continuity as it is in itself; the many are one what others are, each equal to the other, and plurality is therefore simple, distinctionless equality. Continuity is this moment of self-equality of being-outside-one-another, the self-continuation of the distinguished ones into their [others] distinguished from them.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"55.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0005","text":"Thus, immediately, magnitude has in continuity the moment of discreteness,—repulsion, as it is only a moment in quantity. —Continuity is self-equality, but of the many, which, however, do not become excluding; repulsion first extends self-equality into continuity. Discreteness is therefore, for its part, coalescing discreteness, whose ones do not have the void, the negative, as their relation, but their own continuity, and do not interrupt this equality with themselves in the many.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"55.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0006","text":"Quantity is the unity of these moments, continuity and discreteness, but initially it is this in the form of one of them, that of continuity, as the result of the dialectic of being-for-self, which has collapsed into the form of self-equal immediacy. Quantity as such is this simple result, insofar as it has not yet developed and posited its moments in it.—It initially contains them as being-for-self posited as it is in truth. According to its determination, it was the self-sublating relating to itself, perpetual coming-outside-itself. But what is repelled is itself; repulsion is therefore the generative flowing-forth of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"55.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0007","text":"By virtue of the sameness of what is repelled, this discerning is uninterrupted continuity; and by virtue of the coming-outside-itself, this continuity, without being interrupted, is at the same time plurality, which likewise immediately remains in its equality with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"55.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRQT:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"c0858e4954a29203815d49b9a7ecde1f9fc6cb28e25eb32ce53973da97abeb9c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Die reine Quantität."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Die reine Quantität.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12","title":"Remark 1.","order":56,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_12","text":"Die reine Quantität hat noch keine Grenze, oder ist noch nicht Quantum; auch insofern sie Quantum wird, wird sie durch die Grenze nicht beschränkt, sie besteht vielmehr eben darin, durch die Grenze nicht beschränkt zu seyn, das Fürsichseyn als ein Aufgehobenes in sich zu haben. Daß die Diskretion Moment in ihr ist, kann so ausgedrückt werden, daß die Quantität schlechthin in ihr allenthalben die reale Möglichkeit des Eins ist, aber umgekehrt, daß das Eins eben so schlechthin nur als kontinuirliches ist.\n\nDer begrifflosen Vorstellung wird die Kontinuität leicht zur Zusammensetzung, nämlich einer äußerlichen Beziehung der Eins aufeinander, worin das Eins in seiner absoluten Sprödigkeit und Ausschließung erhalten bleibt. Es hat sich aber am Eins gezeigt, daß es an und für sich selbst, in die Attraktion, in seine Idealität übergeht, und daß daher die Kontinuität ihm nicht äußerlich ist, sondern ihm selbst angehört, und in seinem Wesen gegründet ist. Diese Äußerlichkeit der Kontinuität für die Eins ist es überhaupt, an der die Atomistik hängen bleibt, und die zu verlassen die Schwierigkeit für das Vorstellen macht.—Die Mathematik dagegen verwirft eine Metaphysik, welche die Zeit aus Zeitpunkten, den Raum überhaupt oder zunächst die Linie aus Raumpunkten, die Fläche aus Linien, den ganzen Raum aus Flächen bestehen lassen wollte; sie läßt solche unkontinuirliche Eins nicht gelten. Wenn sie auch z.B. die Größe einer Fläche so bestimmt, daß sie als die Summe von unendlich vielen Linien vorgestellt wird, gilt diese Diskretion nur als momentane Vorstellung, und in der unendlichen Vielheit der Linien, da der Raum, den sie ausmachen sollen, doch ein beschränkter ist, liegt schon das Aufgehobenseyn ihrer Diskretion.\n\nDen Begriff der reinen Quantität gegen die bloße Vorstellung hat Spinoza, dem es vorzüglich auf denselben ankam, im Sinne, indem er (Eth. P. I. Prop. XV. Schol.) auf folgende Weise von der Quantität spricht:\n\n\"Quantitas duobus modis a nobis concipitur, abstracte scilicet sive superficialiter, prout nempe ipsam imaginamur; vei ut substantia, quod a solo intellectu fit. Si itaque ad quantitatem attendimus, prout in imaginatione est, quod saepe et facilius a nobis fit, reperietur finita, divisibilis et ex partibus conflata, si autem ad ipsam, prout in intellecu est, attendimus, et eam, quatenus substantia est, concipimus, quod difficillime fit,—infinita, unic et indivisibilis reperietur. Quod omnibus, qui inter imaginationem et intellectum distiuguere sciverint, satis manifestum erit.\" Bestimmtere Beispiele der reinen Quantität, wenn man deren verlangt, hat man an Raum und Zeit, auch der Materie überhaupt, Licht u.s.f. selbst Ich, nur ist unter Quantität, wie schon bemerkt, nicht das Quantum zu verstehen. Raum, Zeit u.s.f. sind Ausdehnungen, Vielheiten, die ein Außer-sich-gehen, ein Strömen sind, das aber nicht ins Entgegengesetzte, in die Qualität oder das Eins übergeht, sondern als Außersichkommen ein perennirendes Selbstproduciren ihrer Einheit sind. Der Raum ist dieß absolute Außersichseyn, das eben so sehr schlechthin ununterbrochen, ein Anders- und Wieder-Andersseyn, das identisch mit sich ist; die Zeit ein absolutes Außersichkommen, ein Erzeugen des Eins, Zeitpunktes, des Jetzt, das unmittelbar das Zunichtewerden desselben und stätig wieder das Zunichtewerden dieses Vergebens ist, so daß dieß sich Erzeugen des Nichtseyns eben so sehr einfache Gleichheit und Identität mit sich ist.\n\nWas die Materie als Quantität betrifft, so befindet sich unter den sieben Propositionen, die von der ersten Dissertation Leibnitzens aufbewahrt sind, (l. Seite des I. Th. seiner Werke) eine hierüber, die zweite, die so lautet: Non omnino improbabile est, materiam et quantitatem esse realiter idem.—In der That sind diese Begriffe auch nicht weiter verschieden, als darin, daß die Quantität die reine Denkbestimmung, die Materie aber dieselbe in äußerlicher Existenz ist. —Auch dem Ich kommt die Bestimmung der reinen Quantität zu, als es ein absolutes Anderswerden, eine unendliche Entfernung oder allseitige Repulsion zur negativen Freiheit des Fürsichseyns ist, aber welche schlechthin einfache Kontinuität bleibt,—die Kontinuität der Allgemeinheit, oder des Beisichseyns, die durch die unendlich mannigfaltigen Grenzen, den Inhalt der Empfindungen, Anschauungen u.s. f. nicht unterbrochen wird.-Welche sich dagegen sträuben, die Vielheit als einfache Einheit zu fassen, und außer dem Begriffe, daß von den Vielen jedes dasselbe ist, was das Andere, nämlich eins der Vielen,—indem nämlich hier nicht von weiter bestimmtem Vielem, von Grünem, Rothem u.s.f. sondern von dem Vielen an-und-für-sich betrachtet, die Rede ist,—auch eine Vorstellung von dieser Einheit verlangen, die finden dergleichen hinlänglich an jenen Stätigkeiten, die den deducirten Begriff der Quantität in einfacher Anschauung als vorhanden geben.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0001","text":"Die reine Quantität hat noch keine Grenze, oder ist noch nicht Quantum; auch insofern sie Quantum wird, wird sie durch die Grenze nicht beschränkt, sie besteht vielmehr eben darin, durch die Grenze nicht beschränkt zu seyn, das Fürsichseyn als ein Aufgehobenes in sich zu haben. Daß die Diskretion Moment in ihr ist, kann so ausgedrückt werden, daß die Quantität schlechthin in ihr allenthalben die reale Möglichkeit des Eins ist, aber umgekehrt, daß das Eins eben so schlechthin nur als kontinuirliches ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"56.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0002","text":"Der begrifflosen Vorstellung wird die Kontinuität leicht zur Zusammensetzung, nämlich einer äußerlichen Beziehung der Eins aufeinander, worin das Eins in seiner absoluten Sprödigkeit und Ausschließung erhalten bleibt. Es hat sich aber am Eins gezeigt, daß es an und für sich selbst, in die Attraktion, in seine Idealität übergeht, und daß daher die Kontinuität ihm nicht äußerlich ist, sondern ihm selbst angehört, und in seinem Wesen gegründet ist. Diese Äußerlichkeit der Kontinuität für die Eins ist es überhaupt, an der die Atomistik hängen bleibt, und die zu verlassen die Schwierigkeit für das Vorstellen macht.—Die Mathematik dagegen verwirft eine Metaphysik, welche die Zeit aus Zeitpunkten, den Raum überhaupt oder zunächst die Linie aus Raumpunkten, die Fläche aus Linien, den ganzen Raum aus Flächen bestehen lassen wollte; sie läßt solche unkontinuirliche Eins nicht gelten.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"56.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0003","text":"Wenn sie auch z.B. die Größe einer Fläche so bestimmt, daß sie als die Summe von unendlich vielen Linien vorgestellt wird, gilt diese Diskretion nur als momentane Vorstellung, und in der unendlichen Vielheit der Linien, da der Raum, den sie ausmachen sollen, doch ein beschränkter ist, liegt schon das Aufgehobenseyn ihrer Diskretion.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"56.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0004","text":"Den Begriff der reinen Quantität gegen die bloße Vorstellung hat Spinoza, dem es vorzüglich auf denselben ankam, im Sinne, indem er (Eth. P. I. Prop. XV. Schol.) auf folgende Weise von der Quantität spricht:","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"56.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0005","text":"\"Quantitas duobus modis a nobis concipitur, abstracte scilicet sive superficialiter, prout nempe ipsam imaginamur; vei ut substantia, quod a solo intellectu fit. Si itaque ad quantitatem attendimus, prout in imaginatione est, quod saepe et facilius a nobis fit, reperietur finita, divisibilis et ex partibus conflata, si autem ad ipsam, prout in intellecu est, attendimus, et eam, quatenus substantia est, concipimus, quod difficillime fit,—infinita, unic et indivisibilis reperietur. Quod omnibus, qui inter imaginationem et intellectum distiuguere sciverint, satis manifestum erit.\" Bestimmtere Beispiele der reinen Quantität, wenn man deren verlangt, hat man an Raum und Zeit, auch der Materie überhaupt, Licht u.s.f. selbst Ich, nur ist unter Quantität, wie schon bemerkt, nicht das Quantum zu verstehen. Raum, Zeit u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"56.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0006","text":"sind Ausdehnungen, Vielheiten, die ein Außer-sich-gehen, ein Strömen sind, das aber nicht ins Entgegengesetzte, in die Qualität oder das Eins übergeht, sondern als Außersichkommen ein perennirendes Selbstproduciren ihrer Einheit sind. Der Raum ist dieß absolute Außersichseyn, das eben so sehr schlechthin ununterbrochen, ein Anders- und Wieder-Andersseyn, das identisch mit sich ist; die Zeit ein absolutes Außersichkommen, ein Erzeugen des Eins, Zeitpunktes, des Jetzt, das unmittelbar das Zunichtewerden desselben und stätig wieder das Zunichtewerden dieses Vergebens ist, so daß dieß sich Erzeugen des Nichtseyns eben so sehr einfache Gleichheit und Identität mit sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"56.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0007","text":"Was die Materie als Quantität betrifft, so befindet sich unter den sieben Propositionen, die von der ersten Dissertation Leibnitzens aufbewahrt sind, (l. Seite des I. Th. seiner Werke) eine hierüber, die zweite, die so lautet: Non omnino improbabile est, materiam et quantitatem esse realiter idem.—In der That sind diese Begriffe auch nicht weiter verschieden, als darin, daß die Quantität die reine Denkbestimmung, die Materie aber dieselbe in äußerlicher Existenz ist. —Auch dem Ich kommt die Bestimmung der reinen Quantität zu, als es ein absolutes Anderswerden, eine unendliche Entfernung oder allseitige Repulsion zur negativen Freiheit des Fürsichseyns ist, aber welche schlechthin einfache Kontinuität bleibt,—die Kontinuität der Allgemeinheit, oder des Beisichseyns, die durch die unendlich mannigfaltigen Grenzen, den Inhalt der Empfindungen, Anschauungen u.s. f.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"56.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0008","text":"nicht unterbrochen wird.-Welche sich dagegen sträuben, die Vielheit als einfache Einheit zu fassen, und außer dem Begriffe, daß von den Vielen jedes dasselbe ist, was das Andere, nämlich eins der Vielen,—indem nämlich hier nicht von weiter bestimmtem Vielem, von Grünem, Rothem u.s.f. sondern von dem Vielen an-und-für-sich betrachtet, die Rede ist,—auch eine Vorstellung von dieser Einheit verlangen, die finden dergleichen hinlänglich an jenen Stätigkeiten, die den deducirten Begriff der Quantität in einfacher Anschauung als vorhanden geben.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"56.8"}],"sha256":"b78597d01c2372304ce30e1e2d60b50e41cd46080b4c1883155270e0b95af821","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102736901756Z_b670432b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"b78597d01c2372304ce30e1e2d60b50e41cd46080b4c1883155270e0b95af821","sha256":"1196086491c575b3fa6d668f2f2dbf7b99d1df7d214441d23f8367de0fbdb515","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:27:36.901781+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0001","text":"Pure quantity as yet has no limit, or is not yet quantum; and even insofar as it becomes quantum, it is not restricted by the limit; rather, it consists precisely in not being restricted by the limit, in having being-for-self within itself as a sublated moment. That discreteness is a moment within it may thus be expressed by saying that quantity is, absolutely and everywhere within itself, the real possibility of the One, but conversely that the One is likewise absolutely only as continuous.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"56.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0002","text":"For the notionaless representation, continuity readily becomes composition, namely, an external relation of the Ones to one another, in which the One is preserved in its absolute brittleness and exclusion. But it has been shown of the One that it passes, in and for itself, into attraction, into its ideality, and that continuity is therefore not external to it, but belongs to it itself and is grounded in its essence. This externality of continuity to the Ones is in general that at which atomism remains fixed, and which makes it difficult for representation to abandon it.—Mathematics, on the other hand, rejects a metaphysics which would have time consist of time-points, space in general, or in the first instance the line, of spatial points, the surface of lines, and the whole of space of surfaces; it does not admit such discontinuous Ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"56.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0003","text":"Even when, for example, it determines the magnitude of a surface in such a way that it is represented as the sum of infinitely many lines, this discreteness is valid only as a momentary representation; and in the infinite multitude of the lines, since the space which they are supposed to constitute is nevertheless a limited one, their discreteness already lies sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"56.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0004","text":"Spinoza, for whom this was especially important, had in view the concept of pure quantity as against mere representation, when he speaks of quantity in the following manner (Eth. P. I. Prop. XV. Schol.):","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"56.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0005","text":"\"Quantitas duobus modis a nobis concipitur, abstracte scilicet sive superficialiter, prout nempe ipsam imaginamur; vei ut substantia, quod a solo intellectu fit. Si itaque ad quantitatem attendimus, prout in imaginatione est, quod saepe et facilius a nobis fit, reperietur finita, divisibilis et ex partibus conflata, si autem ad ipsam, prout in intellecu est, attendimus, et eam, quatenus substantia est, concipimus, quod difficillime fit,—infinita, unic et indivisibilis reperietur. Quod omnibus, qui inter imaginationem et intellectum distiuguere sciverint, satis manifestum erit.\" More determinate examples of pure quantity, should one require them, are to be found in space and time, and also in matter in general, light, etc., even in the I; only, as already remarked, quantum is not to be understood by quantity. Space, time, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"56.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0006","text":"are extensions, multiplicities, which are a going-outside-themselves, a flowing, which, however, does not pass over into its opposite, into quality or the One, but, as coming-outside-itself, is a perennial self-production of their unity. Space is this absolute being-outside-itself, which is just as much absolutely uninterrupted, a being-other and again-other that is identical with itself; time is an absolute coming-outside-itself, a producing of the One, of the time-point, of the Now, which immediately is the vanishing of the same and continuously again the vanishing of this passing-away, so that this production of non-being is just as much simple equality and identity with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"56.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0007","text":"As regards matter as quantity, among the seven propositions preserved from Leibniz's first dissertation (see p. [ ] of the first part of his works), there is one concerning this, the second, which reads: Non omnino improbabile est, materiam et quantitatem esse realiter idem.—In fact, these concepts differ no further than in this, that quantity is the pure determination of thought, whereas matter is the same determination in external existence. —The I, too, has the determination of pure quantity, insofar as it is an absolute becoming-other, an infinite distancing or omnidirectional repulsion toward the negative freedom of being-for-self, but one which remains absolutely simple continuity,—the continuity of universality, or of being-within-itself, which through the infinitely manifold limits, the content of sensations, intuitions, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"56.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_12:P0008","text":"is not interrupted.—Those, on the other hand, who resist grasping multiplicity as simple unity, and who, beyond the concept that of the many each is the same as the other, namely one of the many,—since here the matter is not a more specifically determined many, of green, red, etc., but the many considered in-and-for-itself,—also demand a representation of this unity, find such sufficiently in those continuities which present the deduced concept of quantity as existing in simple intuition.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"56.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_12:P0008"]}],"source_digest":"334c236b3df933af457102635fc73de0f10b7712989431b4933bf21c29d32e92","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13","title":"Remark 2.","order":57,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_13","text":"In die Natur der Quantität, diese einfache Einheit der Diskretion und der Kontinuität zu seyn, fällt der Streit oder die Antinomie der unendlichen Theilbarkeit des Raumes, der Zeit, der Materie u.s.f.\n\nDiese Antinomie besteht allein, darin daß die Diskretion eben so sehr als die Kontinuität behauptet werden muß. Die einseitige Behauptung der Diskretion giebt das unendliche oder absolute Getheiltseyn, somit ein Untheilbares zum Princip; die einseitige Behauptung der Kontinuität dagegen die unendliche Theilbarkeit.\n\nDie kantische Kritik der reinen Vernunft stellt bekanntlich vier (kosmologische) Antinomien auf, worunter die zweite den Gegensatz betrifft, den die Momente der Quantität ausmachen.\n\nDiese kantischen Antinomien bleiben immer ein wichtiger Theil der kritischen Philosophie; sie sind es vornehmlich, die den Sturz der vorhergehenden Metaphysik bewirkten, und als ein Hauptübergang in die neuere Philosophie angesehen werden können, indem sie insbesondere die Überzeugung von der Nichtigkeit der Kategorien der Endlichkeit von Seite des Inhalts herbeiführen halfen,—was ein richtigerer Weg ist, als der formelle eines subjektiven Idealismus, nach welchem nur dieß ihr Mangel seyn soll, subjektiv zu seyn, nicht das, was sie an ihnen selbst sind. Bei ihrem grossen Verdienst aber ist diese Darstellung sehr unvollkommen; Theils in sich selbst gehindert und verschroben, Theils schief in Ansehung ihres Resultats, welches voraussetzt, daß das Erkennen keine anderen Formen des Denkens habe, als endliche Kategorien.—In beider Rücksicht verdienen diese Antinomien eine genauere Kritik, die sowohl ihren Standpunkt und Methode näher beleuchten, als auch den Hauptpunkt, worauf es ankommt, von der unnützen Form, in die er hineingezwängt ist, befreien wird.\n\nZunächst bemerke ich, daß Kant seinen vier kosmologischen Antinomien durch das Eintheilungsprincip, das er von seinem Schema der Kategorien hernahm, einen Schein von Vollständigkeit geben wollte. Allein die tiefere Einsicht in die antinomische oder wahrhafter in die dialektische Natur der Vernunft zeigt überhaupt jeden Begriff als Einheit entgegengesetzter Momente auf, denen man also die Form antinomischer Behauptungen geben könnte. Werden, Daseyn u.s.f. und jeder andere Begriff könnte so seine besondere Antinomie liefern, und also so viele Antinomien aufgestellt werden, als sich Begriffe ergeben.—Der alte Skepticismus hat sich die Mühe nicht verdrießen lassen, in allen Begriffen, die er in den Wissenschaften vorfand, diesen Widerspruch oder die Antinomie aufzuzeigen.\n\nFerner hat Kant die Antinomie nicht in den Begriffen selbst, sondern in der schon konkreten Form kosmologischer Bestimmungen aufgefaßt. Um die Antinomie rein zu haben und sie in ihrem einfachen Begriffe zu behandeln, mußten die Denkbestimmungen nicht in ihrer Anwendung und Vermischung mit der Vorstellung der Welt, des Raums, der Zeit, der Materie u.s.f. genommen, sondern ohne diesen konkreten Stoff, der keine Kraft noch Gewalt dabei hat, rein für sich betrachtet werden, indem sie allein das Wesen und den Grund der Antinomien ausmachen.\n\nKant giebt diesen Begriff von den Antinomien, daß sie \"nicht sophistische Künsteleien seyen, sondern Widersprüche, auf welche die Vernunft nothwendig stoßen (nach kantischem Ausdrucke) müsse;\"—was eine wichtige Ansicht ist.—\"Von dem natürlichen Scheine der Antinomien werde die Vernunft, wenn sie seinen Grund einsieht, zwar nicht mehr hintergegangen, aber immer noch getäuscht.\"—Die kritische Auflösung nämlich durch die sogenannte transcendentale Idealität der Welt der Wahrnehmung hat kein anderes Resultat, als daß sie den sogenannten Widerstreit zu etwas Subjektivem macht, worin er freilich noch immer derselbe Schein, d. h. so unaufgelöst bleibt als vorher. Ihre wahrhafte Auflösung kann nur darin bestehen, daß zwei Bestimmungen, indem sie entgegengesetzt und einem und demselben Begriffe nothwendig sind, nicht in ihrer Einseitigkeit, jede für sich, gelten können, sondern daß sie ihre Wahrheit nur in ihrem Aufgehobenseyn, in der Einheit ihres Begriffes haben.\n\nDie Kantischen Antinomien näher betrachtet, enthalten nichts anders, als die ganz einfache kategorische Behauptung eines jeden der zwei entgegengesetzten Momente einer Bestimmung, für sich isolirt von der andern. Aber dabei ist diese einfache kategorische oder eigentlich assertorische Behauptung in ein schiefes, verdrehtes Gerüste von Raisonnement eingehüllt, wodurch ein Schein von Beweisen hervorgebracht, und das bloß Assertorische der Behauptung versteckt und unkenntlich gemacht werden soll; wie sich dieß bei der nähern Betrachtung derselben zeigen wird.\n\nDie Antinomie, die hierher gehört, betrifft die sogenannte unendliche Theilbarkeit der Materie, und beruht auf dem Gegensatze der Momente der Kontinuität und Diskretion, welche der Begriff der Quantität in sich enthält.\n\nDie Thesis derselben nach kantischer Darstellung lautet so:\n\nEine jede zusammengesetzte Substanz in der Welt besteht aus einfachen Theilen, und es existirt überall nichts als das Einfache, oder was aus diesem zusammengesetzt ist.\n\nEs wird hier dem Einfachen, dem Atomen, das Zusammengesetzte gegenübergestellt, was gegen das Stätige oder Kontinuirliche eine sehr zurückstehende Bestimmung ist.—Das Substrat, das diesen Abstraktionen gegeben ist, nämlich Substanzen der Welt, heißt hier weiter nichts, als die Dinge, wie sie sinnlich wahrnehmbar sind, und hat auf das Antinomische selbst keinen Einfluß, es konnte eben so gut auch Raum oder Zeit genommen werden.—Indem nun die Thesis nur von Zusammensetzung statt von Kontinuität lautet, so ist sie eigentlich sogleich ein analytischer oder tautologischer Satz. Daß das Zusammengesetzte nicht an und für sich Eines, sondern nur ein äußerlich Verknüpftes ist, und aus Anderem besteht, ist seine unmittelbare Bestimmung. Das Andere aber des Zusammengesetzten ist das Einfache. Es ist daher tautologisch, zu sagen, daß das Zusammengesetzte aus Einfachem besteht.—Wenn einmal gefragt wird, aus was Etwas bestehe, so wird die Angabe eines Anderen verlangt, dessen Verbindung jenes Etwas ausmache. Läßt man die Dinte wieder aus Dinte bestehen, so ist der Sinn der Frage nach dem Bestehen aus Anderem verfehlt, sie ist nicht beantwortet und wiederholt sich nur. Eine weitere Frage ist dann, ob das, wovon die Rede ist, aus etwas bestehen soll, oder nicht. Aber das Zusammengesetzte ist schlechthin ein solches, das ein Verbundenes seyn, und aus Anderem bestehen soll. —Wird das Einfache, welches das Andere des Zusammengesetzten sey, nur für ein relativ-Einfaches genommen, das für sich wieder zusammengesetzt sey, so bleibt die Frage vor wie nach. Der Vorstellung schwebt etwa nur dieß oder jenes Zusammengesetzte vor, von dem auch dieß oder jenes Etwas als sein Einfaches angegeben würde, was für sich ein Zusammengesetztes wäre. Aber hier ist von dem Zusammengesetzten als solchem die Rede.\n\nWas nun den kantischen Beweis der Thesis betrifft, so macht er, wie alle kantischen Beweise der übrigen antinomischen Sätze, den Umweg, der sich als sehr überflüssig zeigen wird, apogogisch zu seyn.\n\n\"Nehmet an, (beginnt er,) die zusammengesetzten Substanzen beständen nicht aus einfachen Theilen; so würde, wenn alle Zusammensetzung in Gedanken aufgehoben würde, kein zusammengesetzter Theil und da es (nach der so eben gemachten Annahme) keine einfache Theile giebt, auch kein einfacher, mithin gar nichts übrig bleiben, folglich keine Substanz seyn gegeben worden.\"-Diese Folgerung ist ganz richtig: wenn es nichts als Zusammengesetztes giebt, und man denkt sich alles Zusammengesetzte weg, so hat man gar nichts übrig;—man wird dieß zugeben, aber dieser tautologische Überfluß konnte wegbleiben, und der Beweis sogleich mit dem anfangen, was darauf folgt, nämlich: \"Entweder läßt sich unmöglich alle Zusammensetzung in Gedanken aufheben, oder es muß nach deren Aufhebung etwas ohne Zusammensetzung bestehendes, d. i. das Einfache, übrig bleiben.\"\n\n\"Im erstern Fall aber würde das Zusammengesetze wiederum nicht aus Substanzen bestehen (weil bei diesen die Zusammensetzung nur eine zufällige Relation der Substanzen [8] ist, ohne welche diese als für sich beharrliche Wesen, bestehen müssen.)—Da nun dieser Fall der Voraussetzung widerspricht, so bleibt nur der zweite übrig: daß nämlich das substantielle Zusammengesetzte in der Welt aus einfachen Theilen bestehe.\"\n\n[8] Zum Überfluß des Beweisens selbst kommt hier noch der Überfluß der Sprache,—weil bei diesen (den Substanzen nämlich) die Zusammensetzung nur eine zufällige Relation der Substanzen ist.\n\nDerjenige Grund ist nebenher in eine Parenthese gelegt, der die Hauptsache ausmacht, gegen welche alles bisherige völlig überflüssig ist. Das Dilemma ist dieses: Entweder ist das Zusammengesetzte das Bleibende, oder nicht, sondern das Einfache. Wäre das Erstere, nämlich das Zusammengesetze, das Bleibende, so wäre das Bleibende nicht die Substanzen, denn diesen ist die Zusammensetzung nur zufällige Relation; aber Substanzen sind das Bleibende, also ist das, was bleibt, das Einfache.\n\nEs erhellt, daß ohne den apogogischen Umweg an die Thesis: Die zusammengesetze Substanz besteht aus einfachen Theilen, unmittelbar jener Grund als Beweis angeschlossen werden konnte, weil die Zusammensetzung bloß eine zufällige Relation der Substanzen ist, welche ihnen also äußerlich ist, und die Substanzen selbst nichts angeht.—Hat es mit der Zufälligkeit der Zusammensetzung seine Richtigkeit, so ist das Wesen Freilich das Einfache. Diese Zufälligkeit aber, auf welche es allein ankommt, wird nicht bewiesen, sondern geradezu, und zwar im Vorbeigehen in Parenthese angenommen, als etwas das sich von selbst versteht oder eine Nebensache ist. Es versteht sich zwar allerdings von selbst, daß die Zusammensetzung die Bestimmung der Zufälligkeit und Äußerlichkeit ist; aber wenn es sich nur um ein zufälliges Zusammen handeln sollte statt der Kontinuität, so war es nicht der Mühe werth, darüber eine Antinomie aufzustellen, oder vielmehr es ließ sich gar keine aufstellen; die Behauptung der Einfachheit der Theile ist alsdenn, wie erinnert, nur tautologisch.\n\nIn dem apogogischen Umwege sehen wir somit die Behauptung selbst vorkommen, die aus ihm resultiren soll. Kürzer läßt sich daher der Beweis so fassen:\n\nMan nehme an, die Substanzen bestünden nicht aus einfachen Theilen, sondern seyen nur zusammengesetzt. Nun aber kann man alle Zusammensetzung in Gedanken aufheben, (denn sie ist nur eine zufällige Relation;) also blieben nach deren Aufhebung keine Substanzen übrig, wenn sie nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestünden. Substanzen aber müssen wir haben, denn wir haben sie angenommen; es soll uns nicht alles verschwinden, sondern Etwas übrig bleiben, denn wir haben ein solches Beharrliches, das wir Substanz nannten, vorausgesetzt; dieß Etwas muß also einfach seyn.\n\nEs gehört noch zum Ganzen, den Schlußsatz zu betrachten; er lautet folgendermaßen:\n\n\"Hieraus folgt unmittelbar, daß die Dinge der Welt insgesammt einfache Wesen seyn, daß die Zusammensetzung nur ein äußerer Zustand derselben sey, und daß die Vernunft die Elementarsubstanzen als einfache Wesen denken müsse.\"\n\nHier sehen wir die Äußerlichkeit d. i. Zufälligkeit der Zusammensetzung als Folge aufgeführt, nachdem sie vor her im Beweise parenthetisch eingeführt und in ihm gebraucht worden war.\n\nKant protestirt sehr, daß er bei den widerstreitenden Sätzen der Antinomie nicht Blendwerke suche, um etwa (wie man zu sagen pflege) einen Advokatenbeweis zu führen. Der betrachtete Beweis ist nicht so sehr eines Blendwerks zu beschuldigen, als einer unnützen gequälten Geschrobenheit, die nur dazu dient, die äußere Gestalt eines Beweises hervorzubringen, und es nicht in seiner ganzen Durchsichtigkeit zu lassen, daß das was als Folgerung hervortreten sollte, in Parenthese der Angel des Beweises ist, daß überhaupt kein Beweis, sondern nur eine Voraussetzung vorhanden ist.\n\nDie Antithesis lautet:\n\nKein zusammengesetztes Ding in der Welt besteht aus einfachen Theilen, und es existirt überall nichts Einfaches in derselben.\n\nDer Beweis ist gleichfalls apogogisch gewendet, und auf eine andere Weise eben so tadelhaft als der vorige.\n\n\"Setzet, heißt es, ein zusammengesetztes Ding, als Substanz, bestehe aus einfachen Theilen. Weil alles äußere Verhältniß, mithin auch alle Zusammensetzung aus Substanzen nur im Raume möglich ist, so muß, aus so vielen Theilen das Zusammengesetzte bestehet, aus so vielen Theilen auch der Raum bestehen, den es einnimmt. Nun besteht der Raum nicht aus einfachen Theilen, sondern aus Räumen. Also muß jeder Theil des Zusammengesetzten einen Raum einnehmen.\"\n\n\"Die schlechthin ersten Theile aber alles Zusammengesetzten sind einfach.\" \"Also nimmt das Einfache einen Raum ein.\"\n\n\"Da nun alles Reale, was einen Raum einnimmt, ein außerhalb einander befindliches Mannigfaltiges in sich fasset, mithin zusammengesetzt ist, und zwar aus Substanzen, so würde das Einfache ein substantielles Zusammengesetztes seyn. Welches sich widerspricht.\"\n\nDieser Beweis kann ein ganzes Nest (um einen sonst vorkommenden Kantischen Ausdruck zu gebrauchen) von fehlerhaftem Verfahren genannt werden.\n\nZunächst ist die apogogische Wendung ein grundloser Schein. Denn die Annahme, daß alles Substanzielle räumlich sey, der Raum aber nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestehe, ist eine direkte Behauptung, die zum unmittelbaren Grund des zu Beweisenden gemacht und mit der das ganze Beweisen fertig ist.\n\nAlsdann fängt dieser apogogische Beweis mit dem Satze an: \"daß alle Zusammensetzung aus Substanzen, ein äußeres Verhältniß sey,\" vergißt ihn aber sonderbar genug sogleich wieder. Es wird nämlich fortgeschlossen, daß die Zusammensetzung nur im Raume möglich sey, der Raum bestehe aber nicht aus einfachen Theilen, das Reale, das einen Raum einnehme, sey mithin zusammengesetzt. Wenn einmal die Zusammensetzung als ein äußerliches Verhältniß angenommen ist, so ist die Räumlichkeit selbst, als in der allein die Zusammensetzung möglich seyn soll, eben darum ein äußerliches Verhältniß für die Substanzen, das sie nichts angeht und ihre Natur nicht berührt, so wenig als das übrige, was man aus der Bestimmung der Räumlichkeit noch folgern kann. Aus jenem Grunde eben sollten die Substanzen nicht in den Raum gesetzt worden seyn.\n\nFerner ist vorausgesetzt, daß der Raum, in den die Substanzen hier versetzt werden, nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestehe; weil er eine Anschauung, nämlich, nach Kantischer Bestimmung, eine Vorstellung, die nur durch einen einzigen Gegenstand gegeben werden könne, und kein sogenannter diskursiver Begriff sey.—Bekanntlich hat sich aus dieser kantischen Unterscheidung von Anschauung und von Begriff viel Unfug mit dem Anschauen entwickelt, und um das Begreifen zu ersparen, ist der Werth und das Gebiet derselben auf alles Erkennen ausgedehnt worden. Hierher gehört nur, daß der Raum, wie auch die Anschauung selbst, zugleich begriffen werden muß, wenn man nämlich überhaupt begreifen will. Damit entstände die Frage, ob der Raum nicht, wenn er auch als Anschauung einfache Kontinuität wäre, nach seinem Begriffe als aus einfachen Theilen bestehend, gefaßt werden müsse, oder der Raum träte in dieselbe Antinomie ein, in welche nur die Substanz versetzt wurde. In der That wenn die Antinomie abstrakt gefaßt wird, betrifft sie, wie erinnert, die Quantität überhaupt und somit Raum und Zeit eben so sehr.\n\nWeil aber einmal im Beweise angenommen ist, daß der Raum nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestehe, so dieß hätte Grund seyn sollen, das Einfache nicht in dieß Element zu versetzen, welches der Bestimmung des Einfachen nicht angemessen ist.—Hierbei kommt aber auch die Kontinuität des Raumes mit der Zusammensetzung in Kollision; es werden beide mit einander verwechselt, die erstere an die Stelle der letztern untergeschoben, (was im Schlusse eine Quaternio Terminorum giebt). Es ist bei Kant die ausdrückliche Bestimmung des Raums, daß er ein einiger ist, und die Theile desselben nur auf Einschränkungen beruhen, so daß sie nicht vor dem einigen allbefassenden Raume gleichsam als dessen Bestandtheile, daraus seine Zusammensetzung möglich sey, vorhergehen\". (Kr. d. r. Vern. 2te Ausg. S. 39). Hier ist die Kontinuität sehr richtig und bestimmt vom Raume gegen die Zusammensetzung aus Bestandtheilen angegeben. In der Argumentation dagegen soll das Versetzen der Substanzen in den Raum ein \"außerhalb einander befindliches Mannigfaltiges\" und zwar \"mithin ein Zusammengesetztes\" mit sich führen. Wogegen, wie angeführt, die Art, wie im Raume eine Mannigfaltigkeit sich findet, ausdrücklich die Zusammensetzung und der Einigkeit desselben vorhergehende Bestandtheile ausschließen soll.\n\nIn der Anmerkung zu dem Beweis der Antithesis wird noch ausdrücklich die sonstige Grundvorstellung der kritischen Philosophie herbeigebracht, daß wir von Körpern nur als Erscheinungen einen Begriff haben, als solche aber setzen sie den Raum, als die Bedingung der Möglichkeit aller äußern Erscheinung nothwendig voraus. Wenn hiermit unter den Substanzen nur Körper gemeint sind, wie wir sie sehen, fühlen schmecken u. s. f., so ist von dem, was sie in ihrem Begriffe sind, eigentlich nicht die Rede; es handelt sich nur vom sinnlich Wahrgenommenen. Der Beweis der Antithesis war also kurz zu fassen. Die ganze Erfahrung unseres Sehens, Fühlens, u.s.f.. zeigt uns nur Zusammengesetztes; auch die besten Mikroskope und die feinsten Messer haben uns noch auf nichts einfaches stoßen lassen. Also soll auch die Vernunft nicht auf etwas einfaches stoßen wollen.\n\nWenn wir hiermit den Gegensatz dieser Thesis und Antithesis genauer ansehen, und ihre Beweise von allem unnützen Überfluß und Verschrobenheit befreien, so enthält der Beweis der Antithesis, —durch die Versetzung der Substanzen in den Raum,—die assertorische Annahme der Kontinuität, so wie der Beweis der Thesis,—durch die Annahme der Zusammensetzung, als der Art der Beziehung des Substantiellen,—die assertorische Annahme der Zufälligkeit dieser Beziehung, und damit die Annahme der Substanzen als absolute Eins. Die ganze Antinomie reducirt sich also auf die Trennung und direkte Behauptung der beiden Momente der Quantität und zwar derselben als schlechthin getrennter. Nach der bloßen Diskretion genommen sind die Substanz, Materie, Raum, Zeit u.s.f. schlechthin getheilt, das Eins ist ihr Princip. Nach der Kontinuität ist dieses Eins nur ein aufgehobenes; das Theilen bleibt Theilbarkeit, es bleibt die Möglichkeit zu theilen, als Möglichkeit, ohne wirklich auf das Atome zu kommen. Bleiben wir nun auch bei der Bestimmung stehen, die in dem Gesagten von diesen Gegensätzen gegeben ist, so liegt in der Kontinuität selbst das Moment des Atomen, da sie schlechthin als die Möglichkeit des Theilens ist, so wie jenes Getheiltseyn, die Diskretion auch allen Unterschied der Eins aufhebt,—denn die einfachen Eins ist eines was das andere ist,—somit ebenso ihre Gleichheit und damit ihre Kontinuität enthält. Indem jede der beiden entgegengesetzten Seiten an ihr selbst ihre andere enthält, und keine ohne die andere gedacht werden kann, so folgt daraus, daß keine dieser Bestimmungen, allein genommen, Wahrheit hat, sondern nur ihre Einheit. Dieß ist die wahrhafte dialektische Betrachtung derselben, so wie das wahrhafte Resultat.\n\nUnendlich sinnreicher und tiefer, als die betrachtete kantische Antinomie sind die dialektischen Beispiele der alten eleatischen Schule besonders die Bewegung betreffend, die sich gleichfalls auf den Begriff der Quantität gründen, und in ihm ihre Auflösung haben. Es würde zu weitläufig seyn, sie hier noch zu betrachten, sie betreffen die Begriffe von Raum und Zeit, und können bei diesen und in der Geschichte der Philosophie abgehandelt werden. Sie machen der Vernunft ihrer Erfinder die höchste Ehre; sie haben das reine Seyn des Parmenides zum Resultate indem sie die Auflösung alles bestimmten Seyns in sich selbst aufzeigen, und sind somit an ihnen selbst das Fließen des Heraklit Sie sind darum auch einer gründlichern Betrachtung würdig, als der gewöhnlichen Erklärung, daß es eben Sophismen seyen; welche Assertion sich an das empirische Wahrnehmen nach dem, dem gemeinen Menschenverstande einleuchtenden, Vorgange des Diogenes hält, der, als ein Dialektiker den Widerspruch, den die Bewegung enthält, aufzeigte, seine Vernunft weiter nicht angestrengt haben, sondern durch ein stummes Hin- und Hergehen auf den Augenschein verwiesen haben soll,—eine Assertion und Widerlegung, die freilich leichter zu machen ist, als sich in die Gedanken einzulassen, und die Verwicklungen, in welche der Gedanke und zwar der nicht weithergehohlte, sondern im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn selbst sich formirende, hineinführt, festzuhalten und durch den Gedanken selbst aufzulösen.\n\nDie Auflösung, die Aristoteles von diesen dialektischen Gestaltungen macht, ist hoch zu rühmen und in seinen wahrhaft spekulativen Begriffen von Raum, Zeit und Bewegung enthalten. Er setzt der unendlichen Theilbarkeit (was, da sie vorgestellt wird, als ob sie bewerkstelligt werde, mit dem unendlichen Getheiltseyn, den Atomen, dasselbe ist), als worauf die berühmtesten jener Beweise beruhen, die Kontinuität, welche ebenso wohl auf die Zeit, als den Raum geht, entgegen, so daß die unendliche, d. h. abstrakte Vielheit nur an sich, der Möglichkeit nach, in der Kontinuität enthalten sey. Das Wirkliche gegen die abstrakte Vielheit, wie gegen die abstrakte Kontinuität ist das Konkrete derselben, die Zeit und der Raum selbst, wie gegen diese wieder die Bewegung und die Materie. Nur an sich oder nur der Möglichkeit nach ist das Abstrakte; es ist nur als Moment eines Reellen. Bayle, der in seinem Diktionnaire, Art. Zenon, die von Aristoteles gemachte Auflösung der zenonischen Dialektik, \" pitoyable \" findet, versteht nicht was es heißt, daß die Materie nur der Möglichkeit nach ins Unendliche theilbar sey; er erwiedert, wenn die Materie ins Unendliche theilbar sey, so enthalte sie wirklich eine unendliche Menge von Theilen, dieß sey also nicht ein Unendliches en puissance, sondern ein Unendliches, das reell und aktuell existire.—Vielmehr ist schon die Theilbarkeit selbst nur eine Möglichkeit, nicht ein Existiren der Theile, und die Vielheit überhaupt in der Kontinuität nur als Moment, als Aufgehobenes gesetzt. —Scharfsinniger Verstand, an dem Aristoteles wohl auch unübertroffen ist, reicht nicht hin dessen spekulative Begriffe zu fassen und zu beurtheilen, so wenig als die angeführte Plumpheit sinnlicher Vorstellung, Argumentationen des Zeno zu widerlegen; jener Verstand ist in dem Irrthume, solche Gedankendinge, Abstraktionen, wie unendliche Menge von Theilen, für Etwas, für ein Wahres und Wirkliches zu halten; dieses sinnliche Bewußtseyn aber läßt sich nicht über das Empirische hinaus zu Gedanken bringen.\n\nDie kantische Auflösung der Antinomie besteht gleichfalls allein darin, daß die Vernunft die sinnliche Wahrnehmung nicht überfliegen, und die Erscheinung, wie sie ist, nehmen solle. Diese Auflösung läßt den Inhalt der Antinomie selbst auf der Seite liegen, sie erreicht die Natur des Begriffes ihrer Bestimmungen nicht, deren jede, für sich isolirt, nichtig und an ihr selbst nur das Übergehen in ihre Andere ist, und die Quantität als ihre Einheit und darin ihre Wahrheit hat.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0001","text":"In die Natur der Quantität, diese einfache Einheit der Diskretion und der Kontinuität zu seyn, fällt der Streit oder die Antinomie der unendlichen Theilbarkeit des Raumes, der Zeit, der Materie u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"57.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0002","text":"Diese Antinomie besteht allein, darin daß die Diskretion eben so sehr als die Kontinuität behauptet werden muß. Die einseitige Behauptung der Diskretion giebt das unendliche oder absolute Getheiltseyn, somit ein Untheilbares zum Princip; die einseitige Behauptung der Kontinuität dagegen die unendliche Theilbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"57.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0003","text":"Die kantische Kritik der reinen Vernunft stellt bekanntlich vier (kosmologische) Antinomien auf, worunter die zweite den Gegensatz betrifft, den die Momente der Quantität ausmachen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"57.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0004","text":"Diese kantischen Antinomien bleiben immer ein wichtiger Theil der kritischen Philosophie; sie sind es vornehmlich, die den Sturz der vorhergehenden Metaphysik bewirkten, und als ein Hauptübergang in die neuere Philosophie angesehen werden können, indem sie insbesondere die Überzeugung von der Nichtigkeit der Kategorien der Endlichkeit von Seite des Inhalts herbeiführen halfen,—was ein richtigerer Weg ist, als der formelle eines subjektiven Idealismus, nach welchem nur dieß ihr Mangel seyn soll, subjektiv zu seyn, nicht das, was sie an ihnen selbst sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"57.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0005","text":"Bei ihrem grossen Verdienst aber ist diese Darstellung sehr unvollkommen; Theils in sich selbst gehindert und verschroben, Theils schief in Ansehung ihres Resultats, welches voraussetzt, daß das Erkennen keine anderen Formen des Denkens habe, als endliche Kategorien.—In beider Rücksicht verdienen diese Antinomien eine genauere Kritik, die sowohl ihren Standpunkt und Methode näher beleuchten, als auch den Hauptpunkt, worauf es ankommt, von der unnützen Form, in die er hineingezwängt ist, befreien wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"57.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0006","text":"Zunächst bemerke ich, daß Kant seinen vier kosmologischen Antinomien durch das Eintheilungsprincip, das er von seinem Schema der Kategorien hernahm, einen Schein von Vollständigkeit geben wollte. Allein die tiefere Einsicht in die antinomische oder wahrhafter in die dialektische Natur der Vernunft zeigt überhaupt jeden Begriff als Einheit entgegengesetzter Momente auf, denen man also die Form antinomischer Behauptungen geben könnte. Werden, Daseyn u.s.f. und jeder andere Begriff könnte so seine besondere Antinomie liefern, und also so viele Antinomien aufgestellt werden, als sich Begriffe ergeben.—Der alte Skepticismus hat sich die Mühe nicht verdrießen lassen, in allen Begriffen, die er in den Wissenschaften vorfand, diesen Widerspruch oder die Antinomie aufzuzeigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"57.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0007","text":"Ferner hat Kant die Antinomie nicht in den Begriffen selbst, sondern in der schon konkreten Form kosmologischer Bestimmungen aufgefaßt. Um die Antinomie rein zu haben und sie in ihrem einfachen Begriffe zu behandeln, mußten die Denkbestimmungen nicht in ihrer Anwendung und Vermischung mit der Vorstellung der Welt, des Raums, der Zeit, der Materie u.s.f. genommen, sondern ohne diesen konkreten Stoff, der keine Kraft noch Gewalt dabei hat, rein für sich betrachtet werden, indem sie allein das Wesen und den Grund der Antinomien ausmachen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"57.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0008","text":"Kant giebt diesen Begriff von den Antinomien, daß sie \"nicht sophistische Künsteleien seyen, sondern Widersprüche, auf welche die Vernunft nothwendig stoßen (nach kantischem Ausdrucke) müsse;\"—was eine wichtige Ansicht ist.—\"Von dem natürlichen Scheine der Antinomien werde die Vernunft, wenn sie seinen Grund einsieht, zwar nicht mehr hintergegangen, aber immer noch getäuscht.\"—Die kritische Auflösung nämlich durch die sogenannte transcendentale Idealität der Welt der Wahrnehmung hat kein anderes Resultat, als daß sie den sogenannten Widerstreit zu etwas Subjektivem macht, worin er freilich noch immer derselbe Schein, d. h. so unaufgelöst bleibt als vorher.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"57.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0009","text":"Ihre wahrhafte Auflösung kann nur darin bestehen, daß zwei Bestimmungen, indem sie entgegengesetzt und einem und demselben Begriffe nothwendig sind, nicht in ihrer Einseitigkeit, jede für sich, gelten können, sondern daß sie ihre Wahrheit nur in ihrem Aufgehobenseyn, in der Einheit ihres Begriffes haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"57.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0010","text":"Die Kantischen Antinomien näher betrachtet, enthalten nichts anders, als die ganz einfache kategorische Behauptung eines jeden der zwei entgegengesetzten Momente einer Bestimmung, für sich isolirt von der andern. Aber dabei ist diese einfache kategorische oder eigentlich assertorische Behauptung in ein schiefes, verdrehtes Gerüste von Raisonnement eingehüllt, wodurch ein Schein von Beweisen hervorgebracht, und das bloß Assertorische der Behauptung versteckt und unkenntlich gemacht werden soll; wie sich dieß bei der nähern Betrachtung derselben zeigen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"57.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0011","text":"Die Antinomie, die hierher gehört, betrifft die sogenannte unendliche Theilbarkeit der Materie, und beruht auf dem Gegensatze der Momente der Kontinuität und Diskretion, welche der Begriff der Quantität in sich enthält.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"57.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0012","text":"Die Thesis derselben nach kantischer Darstellung lautet so:","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"57.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0013","text":"Eine jede zusammengesetzte Substanz in der Welt besteht aus einfachen Theilen, und es existirt überall nichts als das Einfache, oder was aus diesem zusammengesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"57.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0014","text":"Es wird hier dem Einfachen, dem Atomen, das Zusammengesetzte gegenübergestellt, was gegen das Stätige oder Kontinuirliche eine sehr zurückstehende Bestimmung ist.—Das Substrat, das diesen Abstraktionen gegeben ist, nämlich Substanzen der Welt, heißt hier weiter nichts, als die Dinge, wie sie sinnlich wahrnehmbar sind, und hat auf das Antinomische selbst keinen Einfluß, es konnte eben so gut auch Raum oder Zeit genommen werden.—Indem nun die Thesis nur von Zusammensetzung statt von Kontinuität lautet, so ist sie eigentlich sogleich ein analytischer oder tautologischer Satz. Daß das Zusammengesetzte nicht an und für sich Eines, sondern nur ein äußerlich Verknüpftes ist, und aus Anderem besteht, ist seine unmittelbare Bestimmung. Das Andere aber des Zusammengesetzten ist das Einfache.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"57.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0015","text":"Es ist daher tautologisch, zu sagen, daß das Zusammengesetzte aus Einfachem besteht.—Wenn einmal gefragt wird, aus was Etwas bestehe, so wird die Angabe eines Anderen verlangt, dessen Verbindung jenes Etwas ausmache. Läßt man die Dinte wieder aus Dinte bestehen, so ist der Sinn der Frage nach dem Bestehen aus Anderem verfehlt, sie ist nicht beantwortet und wiederholt sich nur. Eine weitere Frage ist dann, ob das, wovon die Rede ist, aus etwas bestehen soll, oder nicht. Aber das Zusammengesetzte ist schlechthin ein solches, das ein Verbundenes seyn, und aus Anderem bestehen soll. —Wird das Einfache, welches das Andere des Zusammengesetzten sey, nur für ein relativ-Einfaches genommen, das für sich wieder zusammengesetzt sey, so bleibt die Frage vor wie nach.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"57.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0016","text":"Der Vorstellung schwebt etwa nur dieß oder jenes Zusammengesetzte vor, von dem auch dieß oder jenes Etwas als sein Einfaches angegeben würde, was für sich ein Zusammengesetztes wäre. Aber hier ist von dem Zusammengesetzten als solchem die Rede.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"57.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0017","text":"Was nun den kantischen Beweis der Thesis betrifft, so macht er, wie alle kantischen Beweise der übrigen antinomischen Sätze, den Umweg, der sich als sehr überflüssig zeigen wird, apogogisch zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"57.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0018","text":"\"Nehmet an, (beginnt er,) die zusammengesetzten Substanzen beständen nicht aus einfachen Theilen; so würde, wenn alle Zusammensetzung in Gedanken aufgehoben würde, kein zusammengesetzter Theil und da es (nach der so eben gemachten Annahme) keine einfache Theile giebt, auch kein einfacher, mithin gar nichts übrig bleiben, folglich keine Substanz seyn gegeben worden.\"-Diese Folgerung ist ganz richtig: wenn es nichts als Zusammengesetztes giebt, und man denkt sich alles Zusammengesetzte weg, so hat man gar nichts übrig;—man wird dieß zugeben, aber dieser tautologische Überfluß konnte wegbleiben, und der Beweis sogleich mit dem anfangen, was darauf folgt, nämlich: \"Entweder läßt sich unmöglich alle Zusammensetzung in Gedanken aufheben, oder es muß nach deren Aufhebung etwas ohne Zusammensetzung bestehendes, d. i. das Einfache, übrig bleiben.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"57.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0019","text":"\"Im erstern Fall aber würde das Zusammengesetze wiederum nicht aus Substanzen bestehen (weil bei diesen die Zusammensetzung nur eine zufällige Relation der Substanzen [8] ist, ohne welche diese als für sich beharrliche Wesen, bestehen müssen.)—Da nun dieser Fall der Voraussetzung widerspricht, so bleibt nur der zweite übrig: daß nämlich das substantielle Zusammengesetzte in der Welt aus einfachen Theilen bestehe.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"57.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0020","text":"[8] Zum Überfluß des Beweisens selbst kommt hier noch der Überfluß der Sprache,—weil bei diesen (den Substanzen nämlich) die Zusammensetzung nur eine zufällige Relation der Substanzen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"57.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0021","text":"Derjenige Grund ist nebenher in eine Parenthese gelegt, der die Hauptsache ausmacht, gegen welche alles bisherige völlig überflüssig ist. Das Dilemma ist dieses: Entweder ist das Zusammengesetzte das Bleibende, oder nicht, sondern das Einfache. Wäre das Erstere, nämlich das Zusammengesetze, das Bleibende, so wäre das Bleibende nicht die Substanzen, denn diesen ist die Zusammensetzung nur zufällige Relation; aber Substanzen sind das Bleibende, also ist das, was bleibt, das Einfache.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"57.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0022","text":"Es erhellt, daß ohne den apogogischen Umweg an die Thesis: Die zusammengesetze Substanz besteht aus einfachen Theilen, unmittelbar jener Grund als Beweis angeschlossen werden konnte, weil die Zusammensetzung bloß eine zufällige Relation der Substanzen ist, welche ihnen also äußerlich ist, und die Substanzen selbst nichts angeht.—Hat es mit der Zufälligkeit der Zusammensetzung seine Richtigkeit, so ist das Wesen Freilich das Einfache. Diese Zufälligkeit aber, auf welche es allein ankommt, wird nicht bewiesen, sondern geradezu, und zwar im Vorbeigehen in Parenthese angenommen, als etwas das sich von selbst versteht oder eine Nebensache ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"57.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0023","text":"Es versteht sich zwar allerdings von selbst, daß die Zusammensetzung die Bestimmung der Zufälligkeit und Äußerlichkeit ist; aber wenn es sich nur um ein zufälliges Zusammen handeln sollte statt der Kontinuität, so war es nicht der Mühe werth, darüber eine Antinomie aufzustellen, oder vielmehr es ließ sich gar keine aufstellen; die Behauptung der Einfachheit der Theile ist alsdenn, wie erinnert, nur tautologisch.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"57.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0024","text":"In dem apogogischen Umwege sehen wir somit die Behauptung selbst vorkommen, die aus ihm resultiren soll. Kürzer läßt sich daher der Beweis so fassen:","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"57.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0025","text":"Man nehme an, die Substanzen bestünden nicht aus einfachen Theilen, sondern seyen nur zusammengesetzt. Nun aber kann man alle Zusammensetzung in Gedanken aufheben, (denn sie ist nur eine zufällige Relation;) also blieben nach deren Aufhebung keine Substanzen übrig, wenn sie nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestünden. Substanzen aber müssen wir haben, denn wir haben sie angenommen; es soll uns nicht alles verschwinden, sondern Etwas übrig bleiben, denn wir haben ein solches Beharrliches, das wir Substanz nannten, vorausgesetzt; dieß Etwas muß also einfach seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"57.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0026","text":"Es gehört noch zum Ganzen, den Schlußsatz zu betrachten; er lautet folgendermaßen:","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"57.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0027","text":"\"Hieraus folgt unmittelbar, daß die Dinge der Welt insgesammt einfache Wesen seyn, daß die Zusammensetzung nur ein äußerer Zustand derselben sey, und daß die Vernunft die Elementarsubstanzen als einfache Wesen denken müsse.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"57.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0028","text":"Hier sehen wir die Äußerlichkeit d. i. Zufälligkeit der Zusammensetzung als Folge aufgeführt, nachdem sie vor her im Beweise parenthetisch eingeführt und in ihm gebraucht worden war.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"57.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0029","text":"Kant protestirt sehr, daß er bei den widerstreitenden Sätzen der Antinomie nicht Blendwerke suche, um etwa (wie man zu sagen pflege) einen Advokatenbeweis zu führen. Der betrachtete Beweis ist nicht so sehr eines Blendwerks zu beschuldigen, als einer unnützen gequälten Geschrobenheit, die nur dazu dient, die äußere Gestalt eines Beweises hervorzubringen, und es nicht in seiner ganzen Durchsichtigkeit zu lassen, daß das was als Folgerung hervortreten sollte, in Parenthese der Angel des Beweises ist, daß überhaupt kein Beweis, sondern nur eine Voraussetzung vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"57.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0030","text":"Die Antithesis lautet:","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"57.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0031","text":"Kein zusammengesetztes Ding in der Welt besteht aus einfachen Theilen, und es existirt überall nichts Einfaches in derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"57.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0032","text":"Der Beweis ist gleichfalls apogogisch gewendet, und auf eine andere Weise eben so tadelhaft als der vorige.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"57.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0033","text":"\"Setzet, heißt es, ein zusammengesetztes Ding, als Substanz, bestehe aus einfachen Theilen. Weil alles äußere Verhältniß, mithin auch alle Zusammensetzung aus Substanzen nur im Raume möglich ist, so muß, aus so vielen Theilen das Zusammengesetzte bestehet, aus so vielen Theilen auch der Raum bestehen, den es einnimmt. Nun besteht der Raum nicht aus einfachen Theilen, sondern aus Räumen. Also muß jeder Theil des Zusammengesetzten einen Raum einnehmen.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"57.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0034","text":"\"Die schlechthin ersten Theile aber alles Zusammengesetzten sind einfach.\" \"Also nimmt das Einfache einen Raum ein.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"57.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0035","text":"\"Da nun alles Reale, was einen Raum einnimmt, ein außerhalb einander befindliches Mannigfaltiges in sich fasset, mithin zusammengesetzt ist, und zwar aus Substanzen, so würde das Einfache ein substantielles Zusammengesetztes seyn. Welches sich widerspricht.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"57.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0036","text":"Dieser Beweis kann ein ganzes Nest (um einen sonst vorkommenden Kantischen Ausdruck zu gebrauchen) von fehlerhaftem Verfahren genannt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"57.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0037","text":"Zunächst ist die apogogische Wendung ein grundloser Schein. Denn die Annahme, daß alles Substanzielle räumlich sey, der Raum aber nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestehe, ist eine direkte Behauptung, die zum unmittelbaren Grund des zu Beweisenden gemacht und mit der das ganze Beweisen fertig ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"57.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0038","text":"Alsdann fängt dieser apogogische Beweis mit dem Satze an: \"daß alle Zusammensetzung aus Substanzen, ein äußeres Verhältniß sey,\" vergißt ihn aber sonderbar genug sogleich wieder. Es wird nämlich fortgeschlossen, daß die Zusammensetzung nur im Raume möglich sey, der Raum bestehe aber nicht aus einfachen Theilen, das Reale, das einen Raum einnehme, sey mithin zusammengesetzt. Wenn einmal die Zusammensetzung als ein äußerliches Verhältniß angenommen ist, so ist die Räumlichkeit selbst, als in der allein die Zusammensetzung möglich seyn soll, eben darum ein äußerliches Verhältniß für die Substanzen, das sie nichts angeht und ihre Natur nicht berührt, so wenig als das übrige, was man aus der Bestimmung der Räumlichkeit noch folgern kann. Aus jenem Grunde eben sollten die Substanzen nicht in den Raum gesetzt worden seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"57.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0039","text":"Ferner ist vorausgesetzt, daß der Raum, in den die Substanzen hier versetzt werden, nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestehe; weil er eine Anschauung, nämlich, nach Kantischer Bestimmung, eine Vorstellung, die nur durch einen einzigen Gegenstand gegeben werden könne, und kein sogenannter diskursiver Begriff sey.—Bekanntlich hat sich aus dieser kantischen Unterscheidung von Anschauung und von Begriff viel Unfug mit dem Anschauen entwickelt, und um das Begreifen zu ersparen, ist der Werth und das Gebiet derselben auf alles Erkennen ausgedehnt worden. Hierher gehört nur, daß der Raum, wie auch die Anschauung selbst, zugleich begriffen werden muß, wenn man nämlich überhaupt begreifen will.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"57.39"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0040","text":"Damit entstände die Frage, ob der Raum nicht, wenn er auch als Anschauung einfache Kontinuität wäre, nach seinem Begriffe als aus einfachen Theilen bestehend, gefaßt werden müsse, oder der Raum träte in dieselbe Antinomie ein, in welche nur die Substanz versetzt wurde. In der That wenn die Antinomie abstrakt gefaßt wird, betrifft sie, wie erinnert, die Quantität überhaupt und somit Raum und Zeit eben so sehr.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"57.40"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0041","text":"Weil aber einmal im Beweise angenommen ist, daß der Raum nicht aus einfachen Theilen bestehe, so dieß hätte Grund seyn sollen, das Einfache nicht in dieß Element zu versetzen, welches der Bestimmung des Einfachen nicht angemessen ist.—Hierbei kommt aber auch die Kontinuität des Raumes mit der Zusammensetzung in Kollision; es werden beide mit einander verwechselt, die erstere an die Stelle der letztern untergeschoben, (was im Schlusse eine Quaternio Terminorum giebt). Es ist bei Kant die ausdrückliche Bestimmung des Raums, daß er ein einiger ist, und die Theile desselben nur auf Einschränkungen beruhen, so daß sie nicht vor dem einigen allbefassenden Raume gleichsam als dessen Bestandtheile, daraus seine Zusammensetzung möglich sey, vorhergehen\". (Kr. d. r. Vern. 2te Ausg. S. 39).","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"57.41"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0042","text":"Hier ist die Kontinuität sehr richtig und bestimmt vom Raume gegen die Zusammensetzung aus Bestandtheilen angegeben. In der Argumentation dagegen soll das Versetzen der Substanzen in den Raum ein \"außerhalb einander befindliches Mannigfaltiges\" und zwar \"mithin ein Zusammengesetztes\" mit sich führen. Wogegen, wie angeführt, die Art, wie im Raume eine Mannigfaltigkeit sich findet, ausdrücklich die Zusammensetzung und der Einigkeit desselben vorhergehende Bestandtheile ausschließen soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"57.42"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0043","text":"In der Anmerkung zu dem Beweis der Antithesis wird noch ausdrücklich die sonstige Grundvorstellung der kritischen Philosophie herbeigebracht, daß wir von Körpern nur als Erscheinungen einen Begriff haben, als solche aber setzen sie den Raum, als die Bedingung der Möglichkeit aller äußern Erscheinung nothwendig voraus. Wenn hiermit unter den Substanzen nur Körper gemeint sind, wie wir sie sehen, fühlen schmecken u. s. f., so ist von dem, was sie in ihrem Begriffe sind, eigentlich nicht die Rede; es handelt sich nur vom sinnlich Wahrgenommenen. Der Beweis der Antithesis war also kurz zu fassen. Die ganze Erfahrung unseres Sehens, Fühlens, u.s.f.. zeigt uns nur Zusammengesetztes; auch die besten Mikroskope und die feinsten Messer haben uns noch auf nichts einfaches stoßen lassen. Also soll auch die Vernunft nicht auf etwas einfaches stoßen wollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"57.43"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0044","text":"Wenn wir hiermit den Gegensatz dieser Thesis und Antithesis genauer ansehen, und ihre Beweise von allem unnützen Überfluß und Verschrobenheit befreien, so enthält der Beweis der Antithesis, —durch die Versetzung der Substanzen in den Raum,—die assertorische Annahme der Kontinuität, so wie der Beweis der Thesis,—durch die Annahme der Zusammensetzung, als der Art der Beziehung des Substantiellen,—die assertorische Annahme der Zufälligkeit dieser Beziehung, und damit die Annahme der Substanzen als absolute Eins. Die ganze Antinomie reducirt sich also auf die Trennung und direkte Behauptung der beiden Momente der Quantität und zwar derselben als schlechthin getrennter. Nach der bloßen Diskretion genommen sind die Substanz, Materie, Raum, Zeit u.s.f. schlechthin getheilt, das Eins ist ihr Princip.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"57.44"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0045","text":"Nach der Kontinuität ist dieses Eins nur ein aufgehobenes; das Theilen bleibt Theilbarkeit, es bleibt die Möglichkeit zu theilen, als Möglichkeit, ohne wirklich auf das Atome zu kommen. Bleiben wir nun auch bei der Bestimmung stehen, die in dem Gesagten von diesen Gegensätzen gegeben ist, so liegt in der Kontinuität selbst das Moment des Atomen, da sie schlechthin als die Möglichkeit des Theilens ist, so wie jenes Getheiltseyn, die Diskretion auch allen Unterschied der Eins aufhebt,—denn die einfachen Eins ist eines was das andere ist,—somit ebenso ihre Gleichheit und damit ihre Kontinuität enthält. Indem jede der beiden entgegengesetzten Seiten an ihr selbst ihre andere enthält, und keine ohne die andere gedacht werden kann, so folgt daraus, daß keine dieser Bestimmungen, allein genommen, Wahrheit hat, sondern nur ihre Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"57.45"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0046","text":"Dieß ist die wahrhafte dialektische Betrachtung derselben, so wie das wahrhafte Resultat.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"57.46"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0047","text":"Unendlich sinnreicher und tiefer, als die betrachtete kantische Antinomie sind die dialektischen Beispiele der alten eleatischen Schule besonders die Bewegung betreffend, die sich gleichfalls auf den Begriff der Quantität gründen, und in ihm ihre Auflösung haben. Es würde zu weitläufig seyn, sie hier noch zu betrachten, sie betreffen die Begriffe von Raum und Zeit, und können bei diesen und in der Geschichte der Philosophie abgehandelt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"57.47"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0048","text":"Sie machen der Vernunft ihrer Erfinder die höchste Ehre; sie haben das reine Seyn des Parmenides zum Resultate indem sie die Auflösung alles bestimmten Seyns in sich selbst aufzeigen, und sind somit an ihnen selbst das Fließen des Heraklit Sie sind darum auch einer gründlichern Betrachtung würdig, als der gewöhnlichen Erklärung, daß es eben Sophismen seyen; welche Assertion sich an das empirische Wahrnehmen nach dem, dem gemeinen Menschenverstande einleuchtenden, Vorgange des Diogenes hält, der, als ein Dialektiker den Widerspruch, den die Bewegung enthält, aufzeigte, seine Vernunft weiter nicht angestrengt haben, sondern durch ein stummes Hin- und Hergehen auf den Augenschein verwiesen haben soll,—eine Assertion und Widerlegung, die freilich leichter zu machen ist, als sich in die Gedanken einzulassen, und die Verwicklungen, in welche der Gedanke und zwar der nicht weithergehohlte,","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"57.48"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0049","text":"sondern im gewöhnlichen Bewußtseyn selbst sich formirende, hineinführt, festzuhalten und durch den Gedanken selbst aufzulösen.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"57.49"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0050","text":"Die Auflösung, die Aristoteles von diesen dialektischen Gestaltungen macht, ist hoch zu rühmen und in seinen wahrhaft spekulativen Begriffen von Raum, Zeit und Bewegung enthalten. Er setzt der unendlichen Theilbarkeit (was, da sie vorgestellt wird, als ob sie bewerkstelligt werde, mit dem unendlichen Getheiltseyn, den Atomen, dasselbe ist), als worauf die berühmtesten jener Beweise beruhen, die Kontinuität, welche ebenso wohl auf die Zeit, als den Raum geht, entgegen, so daß die unendliche, d. h. abstrakte Vielheit nur an sich, der Möglichkeit nach, in der Kontinuität enthalten sey. Das Wirkliche gegen die abstrakte Vielheit, wie gegen die abstrakte Kontinuität ist das Konkrete derselben, die Zeit und der Raum selbst, wie gegen diese wieder die Bewegung und die Materie. Nur an sich oder nur der Möglichkeit nach ist das Abstrakte; es ist nur als Moment eines Reellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"57.50"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0051","text":"Bayle, der in seinem Diktionnaire, Art. Zenon, die von Aristoteles gemachte Auflösung der zenonischen Dialektik, \" pitoyable \" findet, versteht nicht was es heißt, daß die Materie nur der Möglichkeit nach ins Unendliche theilbar sey; er erwiedert, wenn die Materie ins Unendliche theilbar sey, so enthalte sie wirklich eine unendliche Menge von Theilen, dieß sey also nicht ein Unendliches en puissance, sondern ein Unendliches, das reell und aktuell existire.—Vielmehr ist schon die Theilbarkeit selbst nur eine Möglichkeit, nicht ein Existiren der Theile, und die Vielheit überhaupt in der Kontinuität nur als Moment, als Aufgehobenes gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"57.51"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0052","text":"—Scharfsinniger Verstand, an dem Aristoteles wohl auch unübertroffen ist, reicht nicht hin dessen spekulative Begriffe zu fassen und zu beurtheilen, so wenig als die angeführte Plumpheit sinnlicher Vorstellung, Argumentationen des Zeno zu widerlegen; jener Verstand ist in dem Irrthume, solche Gedankendinge, Abstraktionen, wie unendliche Menge von Theilen, für Etwas, für ein Wahres und Wirkliches zu halten; dieses sinnliche Bewußtseyn aber läßt sich nicht über das Empirische hinaus zu Gedanken bringen.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"57.52"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0053","text":"Die kantische Auflösung der Antinomie besteht gleichfalls allein darin, daß die Vernunft die sinnliche Wahrnehmung nicht überfliegen, und die Erscheinung, wie sie ist, nehmen solle. Diese Auflösung läßt den Inhalt der Antinomie selbst auf der Seite liegen, sie erreicht die Natur des Begriffes ihrer Bestimmungen nicht, deren jede, für sich isolirt, nichtig und an ihr selbst nur das Übergehen in ihre Andere ist, und die Quantität als ihre Einheit und darin ihre Wahrheit hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"57.53"}],"sha256":"36daee910b065c97f937820955470acf930e1df33cf600c8a3863b31d837cac2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102826606868Z_22325bd2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"36daee910b065c97f937820955470acf930e1df33cf600c8a3863b31d837cac2","sha256":"bfa1002798d67cdc25b17025eedc8e94cd1800b610549409afab205d202211d9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:28:26.606893+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0001","text":"The dispute or antinomy of the infinite divisibility of space, time, matter, etc., falls within the nature of quantity, namely, to be this simple unity of discreteness and continuity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"57.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0002","text":"This antinomy consists solely in the fact that discreteness must be asserted just as much as continuity. The one-sided assertion of discreteness yields infinite or absolute dividedness, hence an indivisible as principle; the one-sided assertion of continuity, by contrast, yields infinite divisibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"57.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0003","text":"As is well known, Kant's Critique of Pure Reason sets forth four (cosmological) antinomies, among which the second concerns the opposition constituted by the moments of quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"57.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0004","text":"These Kantian antinomies always remain an important part of critical philosophy; it is chiefly they that brought about the downfall of the preceding metaphysics, and that can be regarded as a principal transition into modern philosophy, since they helped in particular to bring about the conviction of the nullity of the categories of finitude on the side of content,—which is a more correct path than the formal one of a subjective idealism, according to which their deficiency is supposed only to be that they are subjective, and not what they are in themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"57.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0005","text":"But despite its great merit, this exposition is highly imperfect; partly hampered and distorted in itself, partly askew with respect to its result, which presupposes that cognition has no forms of thought other than finite categories.—In both respects these antinomies deserve a more exact critique, which will both illuminate their standpoint and method more closely, and free the main point at issue from the useless form into which it is forced.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"57.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0006","text":"First of all, I note that Kant sought to lend his four cosmological antinomies an appearance of completeness through the principle of division which he took from his schema of the categories. But the deeper insight into the antinomic, or more truly dialectical, nature of reason shows every concept in general to be a unity of opposed moments, to which one could therefore give the form of antinomic assertions. Becoming, determinate being, etc., and every other concept could thus furnish its particular antinomy, and thus as many antinomies could be set forth as there are concepts.—Ancient scepticism did not shrink from the trouble of demonstrating this contradiction or antinomy in all the concepts which it found in the sciences.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"57.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0007","text":"Further, Kant did not conceive the antinomy in the concepts themselves, but in the already concrete form of cosmological determinations. In order to have the antinomy in its purity and to treat it in its simple concept, the determinations of thought ought not to have been taken in their application and intermixture with the representation of the world, space, time, matter, etc., but considered purely for themselves, without this concrete material, which has no force or authority in the matter, since they alone constitute the essence and ground of the antinomies.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"57.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0008","text":"Kant gives this concept of the antinomies: that they \"are not sophistical artifices, but contradictions upon which reason must necessarily stumble (in Kantian expression);\"—which is an important view.—\"Reason, when it sees the ground of the natural illusion of the antinomies, is indeed no longer deceived by it, but is still deluded.\"—The critical resolution, namely, through the so-called transcendental ideality of the world of perception, has no other result than to make the so-called conflict something subjective, in which it admittedly still remains the same illusion, i.e. just as unresolved as before.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"57.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0009","text":"Its true resolution can consist only in this: that two determinations, inasmuch as they are opposed and necessary to one and the same concept, cannot be valid in their one-sidedness, each for itself, but have their truth only in their sublation, in the unity of their concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"57.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0010","text":"More closely considered, the Kantian antinomies contain nothing other than the quite simple categorical assertion of each of the two opposed moments of a determination, each isolated for itself from the other. But this simple categorical, or properly assertoric, assertion is thereby enveloped in an oblique, distorted framework of ratiocination, by which an appearance of proofs is produced, and the merely assertoric character of the assertion is to be concealed and rendered unrecognizable; as will become evident upon closer consideration of them.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"57.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0011","text":"The antinomy belonging here concerns the so-called infinite divisibility of matter, and rests upon the opposition of the moments of continuity and discreteness which the concept of quantity contains within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"57.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0012","text":"The thesis of it, according to Kantian presentation, reads as follows:","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"57.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0013","text":"Every composite substance in the world consists of simple parts, and nothing exists anywhere except the simple, or that which is composed of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"57.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0014","text":"Here the composite is opposed to the simple, to atoms; this is a determination far inferior to the steady or continuous.—The substrate given to these abstractions, namely substances of the world, means here nothing further than things as they are sensibly perceptible, and has no influence upon the antinomic itself; space or time could just as well have been taken.—Now since the thesis speaks only of composition instead of continuity, it is properly at once an analytical or tautological proposition. That the composite is not in and for itself One, but only an externally conjoined entity and consists of an other, is its immediate determination. But the other of the composite is the simple.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"57.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0015","text":"It is therefore tautological to say that the composite consists of simples.—If one asks what something consists of, the specification of an other is required, the combination of which constitutes that something. If ink is again made to consist of ink, the sense of the question concerning consisting of an other is missed; it is not answered and merely repeats itself. A further question is then whether that of which one speaks ought to consist of something, or not. But the composite is absolutely such a thing as ought to be a connected entity and to consist of an other. —If the simple, which is supposed to be the other of the composite, is taken only as a relatively simple entity which is itself again composite, the question remains as before.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"57.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0016","text":"In representation, perhaps only this or that composite hovers before one, of which this or that something would also be specified as its simple, which would be, for itself, a composite. But here the question is of the composite as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"57.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0017","text":"As regards the Kantian proof of the thesis, it, like all Kantian proofs of the other antinomic propositions, takes the detour—which will prove to be very superfluous—of being apagogical.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"57.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0018","text":"\"Assume,\" (he begins,) \"that composite substances did not consist of simple parts; then, if all composition were sublated in thought, no composite part would remain, and since (according to the assumption just made) there are no simple parts, no simple part either; hence nothing at all would remain, and consequently no substance would be given.\"—This inference is quite correct: if there is nothing but composites, and one thinks away all composites, then nothing at all remains;—this will be conceded, but this tautological superfluity could have been omitted, and the proof could immediately have begun with what follows, namely: \"Either it is impossible to sublate all composition in thought, or, after its sublation, something existing without composition, i.e. the simple, must remain.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"57.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0019","text":"\"But in the former case the composite would in turn not consist of substances (for in these composition is only an accidental relation of substances [8], without which they must exist as enduring beings for themselves.)—Since now this case contradicts the presupposition, only the second remains: namely, that the substantial composite in the world consists of simple parts.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"57.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0020","text":"[8] To the superfluity of the proof itself is added here the superfluity of language,—since in these (namely, the substances) composition is only an accidental relation of substances.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"57.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0021","text":"That ground which constitutes the main matter, against which all that has preceded is wholly superfluous, is incidentally placed in a parenthesis. The dilemma is this: either the composite is what endures, or not, but rather the simple. If the former, namely the composite, were what endures, then what endures would not be the substances, for composition is only an accidental relation to these; but substances are what endures, therefore that which remains is the simple.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"57.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0022","text":"It is evident that, without the apagogical detour, that ground could have been directly appended as proof to the thesis: The composite substance consists of simple parts, because composition is merely an accidental relation of substances, which is therefore external to them and does not concern the substances themselves.—If the accidental character of composition is correct, then the essence is indeed the simple. But this accidental character, upon which alone everything depends, is not proved, but simply assumed, and indeed assumed in passing in a parenthesis, as something self-evident or a secondary matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"57.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0023","text":"It is indeed self-evident that composition is the determination of contingency and externality; but if the issue were merely a contingent togetherness instead of continuity, it would not have been worth the trouble to set up an antinomy concerning it, or rather, none could have been set up at all; the assertion of the simplicity of the parts is then, as noted, merely tautological.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"57.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0024","text":"In the apagogical detour we thus see the assertion itself occur which is supposed to result from it. The proof can therefore be stated more briefly as follows:","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"57.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0025","text":"Let it be assumed that substances do not consist of simple parts, but are merely composite. But now all composition can be removed in thought (for it is only an accidental relation); thus, after its removal, no substances would remain, if they did not consist of simple parts. Yet we must have substances, for we have assumed them; not everything is to vanish for us, but Something is to remain, for we have presupposed such an enduring [something], which we called substance; this Something must therefore be simple.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"57.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0026","text":"In order to complete the whole, the concluding proposition must also be considered; it reads as follows:","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"57.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0027","text":"“From this it follows immediately that the things of the world are, one and all, simple beings, that composition is merely an external state of them, and that reason must think the elementary substances as simple beings.”","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"57.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0028","text":"Here we see the externality, i.e. contingency, of composition set forth as a consequence, after it had previously been introduced parenthetically into the proof and used in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"57.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0029","text":"Kant protests strongly that, in the conflicting propositions of the antinomy, he does not seek artifices in order, perhaps (as people are wont to say), to conduct an advocate’s proof. The proof considered is not so much to be accused of an artifice as of a useless, strained artificiality, which serves only to produce the external form of a proof and does not leave it in all its transparency that what was supposed to emerge as a conclusion is, in parentheses, the hinge of the proof; that in general there is no proof, but only a presupposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"57.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0030","text":"The antithesis reads:","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"57.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0031","text":"No composite thing in the world consists of simple parts, and nowhere does anything simple exist in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"57.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0032","text":"The proof is likewise cast in an apagogical form and is, in another way, just as censurable as the preceding one.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"57.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0033","text":"“Assume,” it says, “that a composite thing, as substance, consists of simple parts. Since every external relation, and therefore also every composition of substances, is possible only in space, the space which the composite occupies must consist of as many parts as the composite itself consists of. Now space does not consist of simple parts, but of spaces. Therefore every part of the composite must occupy a space.”","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"57.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0034","text":"“But the absolutely first parts of everything composite are simple.” “Thus the simple occupies a space.”","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"57.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0035","text":"“Now, since everything real that occupies a space contains within itself a manifold situated outside one another, and is therefore composite, indeed composite out of substances, the simple would be a substantial composite. Which is contradictory.”","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"57.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0036","text":"This proof may be called a whole nest (to use a Kantian expression that occurs elsewhere) of faulty procedure.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"57.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0037","text":"First of all, the apagogical turn is an unfounded semblance. For the assumption that everything substantial is spatial, while space does not consist of simple parts, is a direct assertion, made the immediate ground of what is to be proved; with it the entire proving is finished.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"57.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0038","text":"Then this apagogical proof begins with the proposition: “that all composition of substances is an external relation,” but, strangely enough, immediately forgets it again. For the inference proceeds that composition is possible only in space, but that space does not consist of simple parts; therefore the real which occupies a space is composite. Once composition has been assumed to be an external relation, spatiality itself, in which alone composition is supposed to be possible, is for that very reason an external relation for the substances, one which does not concern them and does not touch their nature, any more than does the rest that may be inferred from the determination of spatiality. For that very reason, the substances ought not to have been placed in space.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"57.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0039","text":"Further, it is presupposed that the space into which the substances are here transferred does not consist of simple parts, because it is an intuition, namely, according to the Kantian determination, a representation which can be given only through a single object, and is not a so-called discursive concept.—As is well known, much mischief concerning intuition has developed from this Kantian distinction between intuition and concept, and, in order to spare oneself comprehension, its value and domain have been extended to all cognition. Here it is relevant only that space, like intuition itself, must at the same time be comprehended, if one wishes to comprehend at all.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"57.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0040","text":"This would give rise to the question whether space, even if as intuition it were simple continuity, must not, according to its concept, be conceived as consisting of simple parts; or else space would enter into the same antinomy into which only substance was placed. In fact, if the antinomy is taken abstractly, it concerns, as was recalled, quantity in general, and thus space and time no less.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"57.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0041","text":"But since it has once been assumed in the proof that space does not consist of simple parts, this ought to have been a reason not to place the simple in this element, which is not adequate to the determination of the simple.—Here, however, the continuity of space also comes into collision with composition; the two are confused with one another, and the former is smuggled in in place of the latter (which yields a quaternio terminorum in the conclusion). In Kant, the explicit determination of space is that it is one, and that its parts rest only on limitations, so that they do not, as it were, precede the single, all-encompassing space as its constituents, out of which its composition might be possible.” (Critique of Pure Reason, 2nd ed., p. 39).","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"57.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0042","text":"Here continuity is very correctly and determinately specified of space as against composition out of constituent parts. In the argument, by contrast, the placing of substances in space is supposed to entail a “manifold situated outside one another,” and indeed “therefore a composite.” Yet, as has been stated, the manner in which a manifold is found in space is expressly supposed to exclude composition and constituent parts preceding its unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"57.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0043","text":"In the remark on the proof of the antithesis, the otherwise fundamental representation of critical philosophy is also expressly invoked: that we have a concept of bodies only as appearances, but that, as such, they necessarily presuppose space as the condition of the possibility of all outer appearance. If by substances here only bodies are meant as we see, feel, taste them, etc., then there is properly no question of what they are in their concept; the issue is only what is sensibly perceived. The proof of the antithesis could thus have been stated briefly. The whole experience of our seeing, feeling, etc. shows us only composites; even the best microscopes and the finest knives have not yet caused us to encounter anything simple. Therefore reason too is not supposed to want to encounter something simple.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"57.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0044","text":"If we now consider the opposition of this thesis and antithesis more closely, and free their proofs of all useless excess and artificiality, then the proof of the antithesis contains—through the placing of substances in space—the assertoric assumption of continuity; just as the proof of the thesis contains—through the assumption of composition as the manner of relation of the substantial—the assertoric assumption of the contingency of this relation, and with it the assumption of substances as absolute ones. The entire antinomy thus reduces itself to the separation and direct assertion of the two moments of quantity, namely as absolutely separated. Taken according to mere discreteness, substance, matter, space, time, etc. are absolutely divided; the one is their principle.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"57.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0045","text":"According to continuity, this one is only a sublated one; division remains divisibility; the possibility of dividing remains, as possibility, without actually arriving at the atom. Even if we remain with the determination given in what has been said concerning these opposites, the moment of the atom lies in continuity itself, since it is absolutely the possibility of division; just as that dividedness, discreteness, also sublates every distinction of the ones—for the simple one is one which the other is—and thus likewise contains their equality and with it their continuity. Since each of the two opposed sides contains its other in itself, and neither can be thought without the other, it follows that neither of these determinations, taken alone, has truth, but only their unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"57.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0046","text":"This is the genuine dialectical consideration of them, as well as the genuine result.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"57.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0047","text":"Infinitely more ingenious and profound than the Kantian antinomy considered are the dialectical examples of the ancient Eleatic school, especially those concerning motion, which likewise rest upon the concept of quantity and have their resolution in it. It would be too prolix to consider them here as well; they concern the concepts of space and time, and may be treated under these and in the history of philosophy.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"57.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0048","text":"They do the highest honour to the reason of their inventors; they have the pure being of Parmenides as their result, inasmuch as they exhibit within themselves the dissolution of all determinate being into itself, and are thus in themselves the flux of Heraclitus. For this reason they are also worthy of a more thorough consideration than the usual explanation that they are merely sophisms; an assertion which adheres to empirical perception, following the procedure, evident to common sense, of Diogenes, who, when a dialectician pointed out the contradiction contained in motion, is said not to have strained his reason any further, but to have referred to evident appearance by silently walking to and fro,—an assertion and refutation which, to be sure, is easier to make than to enter into the thoughts and the entanglements into which thought, and indeed thought not fetched from afar,","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"57.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0049","text":"but rather forming itself within ordinary consciousness itself, to grasp firmly and to dissolve through thought itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"57.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0050","text":"The resolution that Aristotle gives of these dialectical configurations is highly to be praised and is contained in his genuinely speculative concepts of space, time, and motion. To infinite divisibility (which, insofar as it is represented as though it were being carried out, is the same as infinite dividedness, the atoms), upon which the most famous of those proofs rest, he opposes continuity, which pertains as much to time as to space, so that infinite, i.e. abstract, plurality is contained in continuity only in itself, according to possibility. The actual, as against abstract plurality as against abstract continuity, is their concrete form, time and space themselves, and as against these again motion and matter. The abstract is only in itself or only according to possibility; it is only as a moment of something real.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"57.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0051","text":"Bayle, who in his Dictionnaire, art. Zeno, finds the resolution of Zeno's dialectic given by Aristotle “ pitoyable,” does not understand what it means that matter is divisible to infinity only according to possibility; he replies that, if matter is divisible to infinity, it really contains an infinite quantity of parts; this, therefore, is not an infinite en puissance, but an infinite that exists really and actually.—Rather, divisibility itself is only a possibility, not an existence of the parts, and plurality in general in continuity is posited only as a moment, as sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"57.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0052","text":"—Acute understanding, in which Aristotle is perhaps likewise unsurpassed, does not suffice to grasp and judge his speculative concepts, any more than the crudeness of sensuous representation referred to suffices to refute Zeno’s arguments; that understanding is under the error of taking such things of thought, abstractions, as an infinite quantity of parts, for something, for something true and actual; but this sensuous consciousness cannot raise itself beyond the empirical to thoughts.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"57.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_13:P0053","text":"The Kantian resolution of the antinomy likewise consists solely in the fact that reason ought not to soar beyond sensuous perception, but ought to take appearance as it is. This resolution leaves aside the content of the antinomy itself; it does not attain the nature of the concept of its determinations, each of which, isolated for itself, is null and is in itself only the passing over into its other, and has quantity as its unity and therein its truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"57.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_13:P0053"]}],"source_digest":"b7b9544451999ea9d6f5319e089d85804f2b87eba923db34883021c3f0b02474","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD","title":"B. Continuous and Discrete Magnitude.","order":58,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BKUD","text":"Die Quantität enthält die beiden Momente der Kontinuität und der Diskretion. Sie ist in beiden als ihren Bestimmungen zu setzen.—Sie ist schon sogleich unmittelbare Einheit derselben, d. h. sie ist zunächst selbst nur in der einen ihrer Bestimmungen, der Kontinuität, gesetzt, und ist so kontinuirliche Größe.\n\nOder die Kontinuität ist zwar eins der Momente der Quantität, die erst mit dem andern, der Diskretion, vollendet ist. Aber die Quantität ist konkrete Einheit nur, insofern sie die Einheit unterschiedener Momente ist. Diese sind daher auch als unterschieden zu nehmen, jedoch nicht in Attraktion und Repulsion wieder aufzulösen, sondern nach ihrer Wahrheit jede in ihrer Einheit mit der anderen d. h. das Ganze bleibend. Die Kontinuität ist nur die zusammenhängende, gediegene Einheit, als Einheit des Diskreten, so gesetzt ist sie nicht mehr nur Moment, sondern ganze Quantität; kontinuirliche Größe.\n\n2. Die unmittelbare Quantität ist kontinuirliche Größe. Aber die Quantität ist überhaupt nicht ein unmittelbares; die Unmittelbarkeit ist eine Bestimmtheit, deren Aufgehobenseyn sie selbst ist. Sie ist also in der ihr immanenten Bestimmtheit zu setzen, diese ist das Eins. Die Quantität ist diskrete Größe.\n\nDie Diskretion ist, wie die Kontinuität, Moment der Quantität, aber ist selbst auch die ganze Quantität, eben weil sie Moment in ihr, dem Ganzen ist, also als unterschieden nicht aus demselben, nicht aus ihrer Einheit mit dem anderen Momente heraustritt.—Die Quantität ist Außereinanderseyn an sich, und die kontinuirliche Größe ist dieß Außereinanderseyn, als sich ohne Negation fortsetzend, als ein in sich selbst gleicher Zusammenhang. Die diskrete Größe aber ist dieß Außereinander als nicht kontinuirlich, als unterbrochen. Mit dieser Menge von Eins ist jedoch nicht die Menge des Atomen und das Leere, die Repulsion überhaupt, wieder vorhanden. Weil die diskrete Größe Quantität ist, ist ihre Diskretion selbst kontinuirlich. Diese Kontinuität am Diskreten besteht darin, daß die Eins das einander Gleiche sind, oder daß sie dieselbe Einheit haben. Die diskrete Größe ist also das Außereinander des vielen Eins, als des Gleichen, nicht das viele Eins überhaupt, sondern als das Viele einer Einheit gesetzt.\n\nAnmerkung.\n\nIn gewöhnlichen Vorstellungen von kontinuirlicher und diskreter Größe wird es übersehen, daß jede dieser Größen beide Momente, sowohl die Kontinuität als die Diskretion, an ihr hat, und ihr Unterschied nur dadurch konstituirt wird, welches von beiden Momenten die gesetzte Bestimmtheit und welche nur die an-sich-seyende ist. Raum, Zeit, Materie u.s.f. sind stätige Größen, indem sie Repulsionen von sich selbst, ein strömendes Außersichkommen sind, das zugleich nicht ein Übergehen oder Verhalten zu einem qualitativ-Andern ist. Sie haben die absolute Möglichkeit, daß das Eins allenthalben an ihnen gesetzt werde; nicht als die leere Möglichkeit eines bloßen Andersseyns (wie man sagt, es wäre möglich, daß an der Stelle dieses Steines ein Baum stünde) sondern sie enthalten das Princip des Eins an ihnen selbst, es ist die eine der Bestimmungen, von denen sie konstituirt sind.\n\nUmgekehrt ist an der diskreten Größe die Kontinuität nicht zu übersehen; dieß Moment ist, wie gezeigt, das Eins als Einheit.\n\nDie kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe können als Arten der Quantität betrachtet werden, aber insofern die Größe nicht unter irgend einer äußerlichen Bestimmtheit gesetzt ist, sondern unter den Bestimmtheiten ihrer eigenen Momente; der gewöhnliche Übergang von Gattung zu Art läßt an jene nach irgend einem ihr äußerlichen Eintheilungsgrunde äußerliche Bestimmungen kommen. Dabei sind die kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe noch keine Quanta; sie sind nur die Quantität selbst in einer jeden ihrer beiden Formen. Sie werden etwa Größen genannt, insofern sie mit dem Quantum dieß überhaupt gemein haben, eine Bestimmtheit an der Quantität zu seyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0001","text":"Die Quantität enthält die beiden Momente der Kontinuität und der Diskretion. Sie ist in beiden als ihren Bestimmungen zu setzen.—Sie ist schon sogleich unmittelbare Einheit derselben, d. h. sie ist zunächst selbst nur in der einen ihrer Bestimmungen, der Kontinuität, gesetzt, und ist so kontinuirliche Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"58.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0002","text":"Oder die Kontinuität ist zwar eins der Momente der Quantität, die erst mit dem andern, der Diskretion, vollendet ist. Aber die Quantität ist konkrete Einheit nur, insofern sie die Einheit unterschiedener Momente ist. Diese sind daher auch als unterschieden zu nehmen, jedoch nicht in Attraktion und Repulsion wieder aufzulösen, sondern nach ihrer Wahrheit jede in ihrer Einheit mit der anderen d. h. das Ganze bleibend. Die Kontinuität ist nur die zusammenhängende, gediegene Einheit, als Einheit des Diskreten, so gesetzt ist sie nicht mehr nur Moment, sondern ganze Quantität; kontinuirliche Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"58.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0003","text":"2. Die unmittelbare Quantität ist kontinuirliche Größe. Aber die Quantität ist überhaupt nicht ein unmittelbares; die Unmittelbarkeit ist eine Bestimmtheit, deren Aufgehobenseyn sie selbst ist. Sie ist also in der ihr immanenten Bestimmtheit zu setzen, diese ist das Eins. Die Quantität ist diskrete Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"58.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0004","text":"Die Diskretion ist, wie die Kontinuität, Moment der Quantität, aber ist selbst auch die ganze Quantität, eben weil sie Moment in ihr, dem Ganzen ist, also als unterschieden nicht aus demselben, nicht aus ihrer Einheit mit dem anderen Momente heraustritt.—Die Quantität ist Außereinanderseyn an sich, und die kontinuirliche Größe ist dieß Außereinanderseyn, als sich ohne Negation fortsetzend, als ein in sich selbst gleicher Zusammenhang. Die diskrete Größe aber ist dieß Außereinander als nicht kontinuirlich, als unterbrochen. Mit dieser Menge von Eins ist jedoch nicht die Menge des Atomen und das Leere, die Repulsion überhaupt, wieder vorhanden. Weil die diskrete Größe Quantität ist, ist ihre Diskretion selbst kontinuirlich. Diese Kontinuität am Diskreten besteht darin, daß die Eins das einander Gleiche sind, oder daß sie dieselbe Einheit haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"58.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0005","text":"Die diskrete Größe ist also das Außereinander des vielen Eins, als des Gleichen, nicht das viele Eins überhaupt, sondern als das Viele einer Einheit gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"58.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0006","text":"Anmerkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"58.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0007","text":"In gewöhnlichen Vorstellungen von kontinuirlicher und diskreter Größe wird es übersehen, daß jede dieser Größen beide Momente, sowohl die Kontinuität als die Diskretion, an ihr hat, und ihr Unterschied nur dadurch konstituirt wird, welches von beiden Momenten die gesetzte Bestimmtheit und welche nur die an-sich-seyende ist. Raum, Zeit, Materie u.s.f. sind stätige Größen, indem sie Repulsionen von sich selbst, ein strömendes Außersichkommen sind, das zugleich nicht ein Übergehen oder Verhalten zu einem qualitativ-Andern ist. Sie haben die absolute Möglichkeit, daß das Eins allenthalben an ihnen gesetzt werde; nicht als die leere Möglichkeit eines bloßen Andersseyns (wie man sagt, es wäre möglich, daß an der Stelle dieses Steines ein Baum stünde) sondern sie enthalten das Princip des Eins an ihnen selbst, es ist die eine der Bestimmungen, von denen sie konstituirt sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"58.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0008","text":"Umgekehrt ist an der diskreten Größe die Kontinuität nicht zu übersehen; dieß Moment ist, wie gezeigt, das Eins als Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"58.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0009","text":"Die kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe können als Arten der Quantität betrachtet werden, aber insofern die Größe nicht unter irgend einer äußerlichen Bestimmtheit gesetzt ist, sondern unter den Bestimmtheiten ihrer eigenen Momente; der gewöhnliche Übergang von Gattung zu Art läßt an jene nach irgend einem ihr äußerlichen Eintheilungsgrunde äußerliche Bestimmungen kommen. Dabei sind die kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe noch keine Quanta; sie sind nur die Quantität selbst in einer jeden ihrer beiden Formen. Sie werden etwa Größen genannt, insofern sie mit dem Quantum dieß überhaupt gemein haben, eine Bestimmtheit an der Quantität zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"58.9"}],"sha256":"8158a118bfbb0eca0059df45aecae352e49f5bb7b6ad0828dee2e55baeed2d76","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102835044263Z_cd3973d8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Continuous and Discrete Magnitude.","source_sha256":"8158a118bfbb0eca0059df45aecae352e49f5bb7b6ad0828dee2e55baeed2d76","sha256":"0c16ffc7a7af22c910bca12d81faca282311a859929e6952ed3764b6c0a5daeb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:28:35.044291+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0001","text":"Quantity contains the two moments of continuity and discreteness. It is to be posited in both as its determinations.—It is already immediately the unity of the same, i.e. it is at first itself posited only in one of its determinations, continuity, and is thus continuous magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"58.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0002","text":"Or continuity is indeed one of the moments of quantity, which is first completed together with the other, discreteness. But quantity is concrete unity only insofar as it is the unity of differentiated moments. These are therefore also to be taken as differentiated, yet not to be dissolved again into attraction and repulsion, but, according to their truth, each in its unity with the other, i.e. with the whole remaining. Continuity is only the coherent, solid unity; as unity of the discrete, thus posited, it is no longer merely a moment, but whole quantity; continuous magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"58.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0003","text":"2. Immediate quantity is continuous magnitude. But quantity is in general not something immediate; immediacy is a determinacy whose sublated-being is quantity itself. It is therefore to be posited in the determinacy immanent to it; this is the one. Quantity is discrete magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"58.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0004","text":"Discreteness, like continuity, is a moment of quantity, but is itself also the whole quantity, precisely because it is a moment in it, in the whole, and thus, as differentiated, does not emerge from the same, does not emerge from its unity with the other moment.—Quantity is being-outside-itself in itself, and continuous magnitude is this being-outside-itself as continuing itself without negation, as a coherence equal to itself. Discrete magnitude, however, is this outside-one-another as not continuous, as interrupted. Yet with this multitude of ones, the multitude of atoms and the void, repulsion in general, is not again present. Because discrete magnitude is quantity, its discreteness is itself continuous. This continuity in the discrete consists in the ones being equal to one another, or in their having the same unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"58.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0005","text":"Discrete magnitude is thus the outside-one-another of the many ones, as equal ones; not the many ones in general, but posited as the many of one unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"58.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0006","text":"Remark.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"58.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0007","text":"In ordinary conceptions of continuous and discrete magnitude, it is overlooked that each of these magnitudes has both moments, both continuity and discreteness, in it, and that their difference is constituted only by which of the two moments is the posited determinacy and which is merely that which is in itself. Space, time, matter, etc. are continuous magnitudes, since they are repulsions of themselves, a flowing coming-outside-themselves, which at the same time is not a transition or relation to a qualitatively other. They have the absolute possibility that the one be posited everywhere in them; not as the empty possibility of a mere being-other (as one says, it would be possible for a tree to stand in the place of this stone), but they contain the principle of the one in themselves; it is one of the determinations of which they are constituted.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"58.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0008","text":"Conversely, continuity is not to be overlooked in discrete magnitude; this moment is, as has been shown, the one as unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"58.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0009","text":"Continuous and discrete magnitude can be regarded as species of quantity, but only insofar as magnitude is not posited under some external determinacy, but under the determinacies of its own moments; the ordinary transition from genus to species causes external determinations to accrue to it according to some ground of division external to it. Moreover, continuous and discrete magnitude are not yet quanta; they are only quantity itself in each of its two forms. They are called magnitudes perhaps insofar as they have this in general in common with quantum: being a determinacy in quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"58.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKUD:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"9d24fa6abebdf4c4bb46259ecd70bdd7de96f4dade492cfad620409dbf2f7bce","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ","title":"C. Limitation of Quantity.","order":59,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CBDQ","text":"Die diskrete Größe hat erstlich das Eins zum Princip und ist zweitens Vielheit der Eins, drittens ist sie wesentlich stätig, sie ist das Eins zugleich als Aufgehobenes, als Einheit, das Sich-kontinuiren als solches in der Diskretion der Eins. Sie ist daher als Eine Größe gesetzt, und die Bestimmtheit derselben ist das Eins, das an diesem Gesetztseyn und Daseyn ausschließendes Eins, Grenze an der Einheit ist. Die diskrete Größe als solche soll unmittelbar nicht begrenzt seyn; aber als unterschieden von der kontinuirlichen ist sie als ein Daseyn und ein Etwas, dessen Bestimmtheit das Eins und als in einem Daseyn auch erste Negation und Grenze ist.\n\nDiese Grenze, außer dem, daß sie auf die Einheit bezogen und die Negation an derselben ist, ist als Eins auch auf sich bezogen; so ist sie umschließende, befassende Grenze. Die Grenze unterscheidet sich hier nicht zuerst von dem Etwas ihres Daseyns, sondern ist als Eins unmittelbar dieser negative Punkt selbst. Aber das Seyn, das hier begrenzt ist, ist wesentlich als Kontinuität, vermöge der es über die Grenze und dieß Eins hinausgeht, und gleichgültig dagegen ist. Die reale diskrete Quantität ist so eine Quantität, oder Quantum,—die Quantität als ein Daseyn und Etwas.\n\nIndem das Eins, welches Grenze ist, die vielen Eins der diskreten Quantität in sich befaßt, setzt sie dieselben ebenso wohl als in ihm aufgehobene; sie ist Grenze an der Kontinuität überhaupt als solcher, und damit ist hier der Unterschied von kontinuirlicher und diskreter Größe gleichgültig; oder richtiger, sie ist Grenze an der Kontinuität der einen sosehr als der andern; beide gehen darein über, Quanta zu seyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0001","text":"Die diskrete Größe hat erstlich das Eins zum Princip und ist zweitens Vielheit der Eins, drittens ist sie wesentlich stätig, sie ist das Eins zugleich als Aufgehobenes, als Einheit, das Sich-kontinuiren als solches in der Diskretion der Eins. Sie ist daher als Eine Größe gesetzt, und die Bestimmtheit derselben ist das Eins, das an diesem Gesetztseyn und Daseyn ausschließendes Eins, Grenze an der Einheit ist. Die diskrete Größe als solche soll unmittelbar nicht begrenzt seyn; aber als unterschieden von der kontinuirlichen ist sie als ein Daseyn und ein Etwas, dessen Bestimmtheit das Eins und als in einem Daseyn auch erste Negation und Grenze ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"59.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0002","text":"Diese Grenze, außer dem, daß sie auf die Einheit bezogen und die Negation an derselben ist, ist als Eins auch auf sich bezogen; so ist sie umschließende, befassende Grenze. Die Grenze unterscheidet sich hier nicht zuerst von dem Etwas ihres Daseyns, sondern ist als Eins unmittelbar dieser negative Punkt selbst. Aber das Seyn, das hier begrenzt ist, ist wesentlich als Kontinuität, vermöge der es über die Grenze und dieß Eins hinausgeht, und gleichgültig dagegen ist. Die reale diskrete Quantität ist so eine Quantität, oder Quantum,—die Quantität als ein Daseyn und Etwas.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"59.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0003","text":"Indem das Eins, welches Grenze ist, die vielen Eins der diskreten Quantität in sich befaßt, setzt sie dieselben ebenso wohl als in ihm aufgehobene; sie ist Grenze an der Kontinuität überhaupt als solcher, und damit ist hier der Unterschied von kontinuirlicher und diskreter Größe gleichgültig; oder richtiger, sie ist Grenze an der Kontinuität der einen sosehr als der andern; beide gehen darein über, Quanta zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"59.3"}],"sha256":"50bffd53580e66ccb2c5fba61798f83fd4c27f052da1c21587a342f25467b074","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102839066437Z_5edf7645","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Limitation of Quantity.","source_sha256":"50bffd53580e66ccb2c5fba61798f83fd4c27f052da1c21587a342f25467b074","sha256":"3c1a3ef1205cbfdfb1ab8dfcc1ebdda20384cd53a960b14dac755bd42103f55c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:28:39.066459+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0001","text":"Discrete magnitude has, first, the one as its principle and is, second, a plurality of ones; third, it is essentially continuous, it is the one at the same time as sublated, as unity, self-continuation as such in the discretion of the ones. It is therefore posited as one magnitude, and its determinacy is the one, which in this positedness and existence is an exclusive one, a limit at unity. Discrete magnitude as such is not supposed to be immediately limited; but as distinguished from continuous magnitude, it is as an existence and a something whose determinacy is the one and, as in an existence, is also first negation and limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"59.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0002","text":"This limit, besides being related to unity and being the negation in it, is, as one, also related to itself; thus it is an enclosing, comprehending limit. Here the limit does not first distinguish itself from the something of its existence, but is, as one, immediately this negative point itself. But the being that is limited here is essentially continuity, by virtue of which it goes beyond the limit and this one, and is indifferent toward them. Real discrete quantity is thus a quantity, or quantum,—quantity as an existence and something.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"59.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0003","text":"Since the one which is limit comprehends within itself the many ones of discrete quantity, it equally posits them as sublated in it; it is a limit on continuity in general as such, and with this the distinction between continuous and discrete magnitude is here indifferent; or, more correctly, it is a limit on the continuity of the one just as much as of the other; both pass over into being quanta.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"59.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDQ:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"dcf017daac75c910f47cf46d7a5d0a45aa9901d5aca55f481c600b3a8bc7529d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Begrenzung der Quantität."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Begrenzung der Quantität.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ","title":"A. Number.","order":60,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DIEZ","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Quantum.\n\nDas Quantum, zunächst Quantität mit einer Bestimmtheit oder Grenze überhaupt,—ist in seiner vollkommenen Bestimmtheit die Zahl. Das Quantum unterscheidet sich\n\nzweitens zunächst in extensives, an dem die Grenze als Beschränkung der daseyenden Vielheit ist, alsdann indem dieses Daseyn ins Fürsichseyn übergeht,—in intensives Quantum, Grad, welches als fürsich und darin als gleichgültige Grenze ebenso unmittelbar außersich, seine Bestimmtheit an einem anderen hat. Als dieser gesetzte Widerspruch, so einfach in sich bestimmt zu seyn und seine Bestimmtheit außer sich zu haben und für sie außer sich zu weisen, geht das Quantum\n\ndrittens, als das an sich selbst äußerliche Gesetzte in die quantitative Unendlichkeit über.\n\n## A. Die Zahl.\n\nDie Quantität ist Quantum, oder hat eine Grenze; sowohl als kontinuirliche wie als diskrete Größe. Der Unterschied dieser Arten hat hier zunächst keine Bedeutung.\n\nDie Quantität ist als das aufgehobene Fürsichseyn schon an und für sich selbst gegen ihre Grenze gleichgültig. Aber damit ist ihr ebenso die Grenze, oder ein Quantum zu seyn, nicht gleichgültig; denn sie enthält das Eins, das absolute Bestimmtseyn, in sich als ihr eigenes Moment, das also als gesetzt an ihrer Kontinuität oder Einheit ihre Grenze ist, die aber als Eins, zu dein sie überhaupt geworden, bleibt.\n\nDieß Eins ist also das Princip des Quantums, aber das Eins als der Quantität. Dadurch ist es erstlich kontinuirlich, es ist Einheit; zweitens ist es diskret, an sich seyende (wie in der kontinuirlichen) oder gesetzte (wie in der diskreten Größe) Vielheit der Eins, welche die Gleichheit miteinander, jene Kontinuität, dieselbe Einheit haben. Drittens ist die ß Eins auch Negation der vielen Eins als einfache Grenze, ein Ausschließen seines Andersseyns aus sich, eine Bestimmung seiner gegen andere Quanta. Das Eins ist insofern sich à) auf sich beziehende, (ß) umschließende, und (ç) Anderes ausschließende Grenze.\n\nDas Quantum in diesen Bestimmungen vollständig gesetzt, ist die Zahl. Das vollständige Gesetztseyn liegt in dem Daseyn der Grenze als Vielheit und damit ihrem Unterschiedenseyn von der Einheit. Die Zahl erscheint, deswegen als diskrete Größe, aber sie hat an der Einheit ebenso die Kontinuität. Sie ist darum auch das Quantum in vollkommener Bestimmtheit; indem in ihr die Grenze als bestimmte Vielheit, die das Eins, das schlechthin bestimmte, zu seinem Principe hat. Die Kontinuität, als in der das Eins nur an sich, als Aufgehobenes ist,—gesetzt als Einheit,—ist die Form der Unbestimmtheit.\n\nDas Quantum nur als solches ist begrenzt überhaupt, seine Grenze ist abstrakte, einfache Bestimmtheit desselben. Indem es aber Zahl ist, ist diese Grenze als in sich selbst mannigfaltig gesetzt. Sie enthält die vielen Eins, die ihr Daseyn ausmachen, enthält sie aber nicht auf unbestimmte Weise, sondern die Bestimmtheit der Grenze fällt in sie; die Grenze schließt anderes Daseyn, d. i. andere Viele aus, und die von ihr umschlossenen Eins sind eine bestimmte Menge, —die Anzahl, zu welcher als der Diskretion, wie sie in der Zahl ist, das andere die Einheit, die Kontinuität derselben, ist. Anzahl und Einheit machen die Momente der Zahl aus.\n\nVon der Anzahl ist noch näher zu sehen, wie die vielen Eins, aus denen sie besteht, in der Grenze sind; von der Anzahl ist der Ausdruck richtig, daß sie aus den Vielen besteht, denn die Eins sind in ihr nicht als aufgehoben, sondern sind in ihr, nur mit der ausschließenden Grenze gesetzt, gegen welche sie gleichgültig sind. Aber diese ist es nicht gegen sie. Beim Daseyn hatte sich zunächst das Verhältniß der Grenze zu demselben so gestellt, daß das Daseyn als das affirmative diesseits seiner Grenze bestehen blieb, und diese, die Negation, außerhalb an seinem Rande sich befand; ebenso erscheint an den vielen Eins das Abbrechen derselben und das Ausschließen anderer Eins als eine Bestimmung, die außerhalb der umschlossenen Eins fällt. Aber es hat sich dort ergeben, daß die Grenze das Daseyn durchdringt, soweit geht als dieses, und daß Etwas dadurch seiner Bestimmung nach begrenzt, d. i. endlich ist.—So stellt man im Quantitativen der Zahl etwa Hundert so vor, daß das hundertste Eins allein die Vielen so begrenze, daß sie Hundert seyen. Einer Seits ist dieß richtig; anderer Seits aber hat unter den hundert Eins keines einen Vorzug, da sie nur gleich sind; jedes ist ebenso das Hundertste; sie gehören also alle der Grenze an, wodurch die Zahl Hundert ist; diese kann für ihre Bestimmtheit keines entbehren; die anderen machen somit gegen das hundertste Eins kein Daseyn aus, das außerhalb der Grenze oder nur innerhalb ihrer, überhaupt verschieden von ihr wäre. Die Anzahl ist daher nicht eine Vielheit gegen das umschließende, begrenzende Eins, sondern macht selbst diese Begrenzung aus, welche ein bestimmtes Quantum ist; die Vielen machen eine Zahl, Ein Zwei, Ein Zehn, Ein Hundert u.s.f. aus.\n\nDas begrenzende Eins ist nun das Bestimmtseyn gegen Anderes, Unterscheidung der Zahl von andern. Aber diese Unterscheidung wird nicht qualitative Bestimmtheit, sondern bleibt quantitativ, fällt nur in die vergleichende äußerliche Reflexion; die Zahl bleibt als Eins in sich zurückgekehrt, und gleichgültig gegen Andere. Diese Gleichgültigkeit der Zahl gegen Andere ist wesentliche Bestimmung derselben; sie macht ihr An-sich-bestimmtseyn, aber zugleich ihre eigene Äußerlichkeit aus.—Sie ist so ein numerisches Eins, als das absolut bestimmte, das zugleich die Form der einfachen Unmittelbarkeit hat, und dem daher die Beziehung auf anderes völlig äußerlich ist. Als Eins, das Zahl ist, hat es ferner die Bestimmtheit, insofern sie Beziehung auf Anderes ist, als seine Momente in ihm selbst, in seinem Unterschiede der Einheit und der Anzahl, und die Anzahl ist selbst Vielheit der Eins d. i. es ist in ihm selbst diese absolute Äußerlichkeit.—Dieser Widerspruch der Zahl oder des Quantums überhaupt in sich ist die Qualität des Quantums, in deren weitern Bestimmungen sich dieser Widerspruch entwickelt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0001","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"60.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0002","text":"Das Quantum, zunächst Quantität mit einer Bestimmtheit oder Grenze überhaupt,—ist in seiner vollkommenen Bestimmtheit die Zahl. Das Quantum unterscheidet sich","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"60.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0003","text":"zweitens zunächst in extensives, an dem die Grenze als Beschränkung der daseyenden Vielheit ist, alsdann indem dieses Daseyn ins Fürsichseyn übergeht,—in intensives Quantum, Grad, welches als fürsich und darin als gleichgültige Grenze ebenso unmittelbar außersich, seine Bestimmtheit an einem anderen hat. Als dieser gesetzte Widerspruch, so einfach in sich bestimmt zu seyn und seine Bestimmtheit außer sich zu haben und für sie außer sich zu weisen, geht das Quantum","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"60.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0004","text":"drittens, als das an sich selbst äußerliche Gesetzte in die quantitative Unendlichkeit über.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"60.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0005","text":"## A. Die Zahl.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"60.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0006","text":"Die Quantität ist Quantum, oder hat eine Grenze; sowohl als kontinuirliche wie als diskrete Größe. Der Unterschied dieser Arten hat hier zunächst keine Bedeutung.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"60.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0007","text":"Die Quantität ist als das aufgehobene Fürsichseyn schon an und für sich selbst gegen ihre Grenze gleichgültig. Aber damit ist ihr ebenso die Grenze, oder ein Quantum zu seyn, nicht gleichgültig; denn sie enthält das Eins, das absolute Bestimmtseyn, in sich als ihr eigenes Moment, das also als gesetzt an ihrer Kontinuität oder Einheit ihre Grenze ist, die aber als Eins, zu dein sie überhaupt geworden, bleibt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"60.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0008","text":"Dieß Eins ist also das Princip des Quantums, aber das Eins als der Quantität. Dadurch ist es erstlich kontinuirlich, es ist Einheit; zweitens ist es diskret, an sich seyende (wie in der kontinuirlichen) oder gesetzte (wie in der diskreten Größe) Vielheit der Eins, welche die Gleichheit miteinander, jene Kontinuität, dieselbe Einheit haben. Drittens ist die ß Eins auch Negation der vielen Eins als einfache Grenze, ein Ausschließen seines Andersseyns aus sich, eine Bestimmung seiner gegen andere Quanta. Das Eins ist insofern sich à) auf sich beziehende, (ß) umschließende, und (ç) Anderes ausschließende Grenze.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"60.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0009","text":"Das Quantum in diesen Bestimmungen vollständig gesetzt, ist die Zahl. Das vollständige Gesetztseyn liegt in dem Daseyn der Grenze als Vielheit und damit ihrem Unterschiedenseyn von der Einheit. Die Zahl erscheint, deswegen als diskrete Größe, aber sie hat an der Einheit ebenso die Kontinuität. Sie ist darum auch das Quantum in vollkommener Bestimmtheit; indem in ihr die Grenze als bestimmte Vielheit, die das Eins, das schlechthin bestimmte, zu seinem Principe hat. Die Kontinuität, als in der das Eins nur an sich, als Aufgehobenes ist,—gesetzt als Einheit,—ist die Form der Unbestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"60.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0010","text":"Das Quantum nur als solches ist begrenzt überhaupt, seine Grenze ist abstrakte, einfache Bestimmtheit desselben. Indem es aber Zahl ist, ist diese Grenze als in sich selbst mannigfaltig gesetzt. Sie enthält die vielen Eins, die ihr Daseyn ausmachen, enthält sie aber nicht auf unbestimmte Weise, sondern die Bestimmtheit der Grenze fällt in sie; die Grenze schließt anderes Daseyn, d. i. andere Viele aus, und die von ihr umschlossenen Eins sind eine bestimmte Menge, —die Anzahl, zu welcher als der Diskretion, wie sie in der Zahl ist, das andere die Einheit, die Kontinuität derselben, ist. Anzahl und Einheit machen die Momente der Zahl aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"60.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0011","text":"Von der Anzahl ist noch näher zu sehen, wie die vielen Eins, aus denen sie besteht, in der Grenze sind; von der Anzahl ist der Ausdruck richtig, daß sie aus den Vielen besteht, denn die Eins sind in ihr nicht als aufgehoben, sondern sind in ihr, nur mit der ausschließenden Grenze gesetzt, gegen welche sie gleichgültig sind. Aber diese ist es nicht gegen sie. Beim Daseyn hatte sich zunächst das Verhältniß der Grenze zu demselben so gestellt, daß das Daseyn als das affirmative diesseits seiner Grenze bestehen blieb, und diese, die Negation, außerhalb an seinem Rande sich befand; ebenso erscheint an den vielen Eins das Abbrechen derselben und das Ausschließen anderer Eins als eine Bestimmung, die außerhalb der umschlossenen Eins fällt. Aber es hat sich dort ergeben, daß die Grenze das Daseyn durchdringt, soweit geht als dieses, und daß Etwas dadurch seiner Bestimmung nach begrenzt, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"60.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0012","text":"endlich ist.—So stellt man im Quantitativen der Zahl etwa Hundert so vor, daß das hundertste Eins allein die Vielen so begrenze, daß sie Hundert seyen. Einer Seits ist dieß richtig; anderer Seits aber hat unter den hundert Eins keines einen Vorzug, da sie nur gleich sind; jedes ist ebenso das Hundertste; sie gehören also alle der Grenze an, wodurch die Zahl Hundert ist; diese kann für ihre Bestimmtheit keines entbehren; die anderen machen somit gegen das hundertste Eins kein Daseyn aus, das außerhalb der Grenze oder nur innerhalb ihrer, überhaupt verschieden von ihr wäre. Die Anzahl ist daher nicht eine Vielheit gegen das umschließende, begrenzende Eins, sondern macht selbst diese Begrenzung aus, welche ein bestimmtes Quantum ist; die Vielen machen eine Zahl, Ein Zwei, Ein Zehn, Ein Hundert u.s.f. aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"60.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0013","text":"Das begrenzende Eins ist nun das Bestimmtseyn gegen Anderes, Unterscheidung der Zahl von andern. Aber diese Unterscheidung wird nicht qualitative Bestimmtheit, sondern bleibt quantitativ, fällt nur in die vergleichende äußerliche Reflexion; die Zahl bleibt als Eins in sich zurückgekehrt, und gleichgültig gegen Andere. Diese Gleichgültigkeit der Zahl gegen Andere ist wesentliche Bestimmung derselben; sie macht ihr An-sich-bestimmtseyn, aber zugleich ihre eigene Äußerlichkeit aus.—Sie ist so ein numerisches Eins, als das absolut bestimmte, das zugleich die Form der einfachen Unmittelbarkeit hat, und dem daher die Beziehung auf anderes völlig äußerlich ist. Als Eins, das Zahl ist, hat es ferner die Bestimmtheit, insofern sie Beziehung auf Anderes ist, als seine Momente in ihm selbst, in seinem Unterschiede der Einheit und der Anzahl, und die Anzahl ist selbst Vielheit der Eins d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"60.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0014","text":"es ist in ihm selbst diese absolute Äußerlichkeit.—Dieser Widerspruch der Zahl oder des Quantums überhaupt in sich ist die Qualität des Quantums, in deren weitern Bestimmungen sich dieser Widerspruch entwickelt.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"60.14"}],"sha256":"fb2a7ed2571dfe223afc23a7011614709a956bdafec7fac8ee63049806c5857b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102852001481Z_72c3ddb8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Number.","source_sha256":"fb2a7ed2571dfe223afc23a7011614709a956bdafec7fac8ee63049806c5857b","sha256":"9e2fe3250ebb84365f6c7efb7b3ecdf9dfd4b4dad4ead88817b4f4be5b6f97fc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:28:52.001502+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0001","text":"## Chapter Two. Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"60.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0002","text":"Quantum, initially quantity with a determinacy or limit in general,—is, in its complete determinacy, number. Quantum distinguishes itself","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"60.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0003","text":"secondly, initially into extensive quantum, in which the limit is the restriction of the existent multiplicity, then, as this existence passes over into being-for-self,—into intensive quantum, degree, which, as for itself and therein as indifferent limit, likewise immediately has its determinacy outside itself, in an other. As this posited contradiction, of being determined so simply within itself and of having its determinacy outside itself and referring outside itself for it, quantum","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"60.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0004","text":"thirdly, as the posited external-to-itself in itself, passes over into quantitative infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"60.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0005","text":"## A. Number.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"60.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0006","text":"Quantity is quantum, or has a limit; both as continuous and as discrete magnitude. The difference between these kinds initially has no significance here.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"60.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0007","text":"As sublated being-for-self, quantity is already in and for itself indifferent towards its limit. But with this, the limit, or being a quantum, is likewise not indifferent to it; for it contains the one, absolute determinacy, within itself as its own moment, which, therefore, as posited in its continuity or unity, is its limit, but remains as the one into which it has generally become.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"60.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0008","text":"This one is therefore the principle of quantum, but the one as belonging to quantity. Thereby it is, firstly, continuous, it is unity; secondly, it is discrete, the multiplicity of ones which are in themselves (as in continuous magnitude) or posited (as in discrete magnitude), and which have equality with one another, that continuity, the same unity. Thirdly, the ß one is also the negation of the many ones as simple limit, an excluding of its otherness from itself, a determination of it over against other quanta. The one is thus a limit (à) relating to itself, (ß) enclosing, and (ç) excluding others.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"60.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0009","text":"Quantum, completely posited in these determinations, is number. Complete positedness consists in the existence of the limit as multiplicity and hence in its difference from unity. Number appears, therefore, as discrete magnitude, but in unity it likewise has continuity. It is consequently also quantum in complete determinacy; since in it the limit is a determinate multiplicity which has the one, the absolutely determinate, as its principle. Continuity, as that in which the one is only in itself, as sublated,—posited as unity,—is the form of indeterminacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"60.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0010","text":"Quantum merely as such is limited in general; its limit is its abstract, simple determinacy. But insofar as it is number, this limit is posited as itself manifold. It contains the many ones that constitute its existence, but does not contain them in an indeterminate manner; rather, the determinacy of the limit falls within them; the limit excludes other existence, i.e. other many ones, and the ones enclosed by it are a determinate aggregate,—the amount, for which, as the discreteness as it is in number, the other is unity, its continuity. Amount and unity constitute the moments of number.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"60.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0011","text":"With regard to the amount, it must be considered more closely how the many ones of which it consists are in the limit; the expression concerning the amount is correct, that it consists of the many, for the ones are not in it as sublated, but are in it, only posited with the excluding limit, towards which they are indifferent. But this is not indifferent towards them. In existence, the relation of the limit to it had initially presented itself in such a way that existence, as the affirmative, remained on this side of its limit, and this, negation, was outside at its edge; likewise, in the many ones their breaking off and the exclusion of other ones appears as a determination falling outside the enclosed ones. But it emerged there that the limit permeates existence, extends as far as it does, and that something is thereby limited according to its determinacy, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"60.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0012","text":"is finite.—Thus, in the quantitative sphere, one conceives, for example, one hundred in such a way that the hundredth one alone limits the many so that they are one hundred. On the one hand, this is correct; but on the other hand, among the hundred ones none has precedence, since they are only equal; each is equally the hundredth; thus they all belong to the limit by which the number is one hundred; for its determinacy, this number can dispense with none of them; the others consequently constitute no existence, over against the hundredth one, which would be outside the limit or merely within it, or generally different from it. The amount is therefore not a multiplicity over against the enclosing, limiting one, but itself constitutes this delimitation, which is a determinate quantum; the many constitute a number, a one two, a one ten, a one hundred, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"60.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0013","text":"The limiting one is now determinacy over against others, the distinction of the number from others. But this distinction does not become qualitative determinacy, but remains quantitative, falling only within comparative external reflection; the number remains returned into itself as one, and indifferent towards others. This indifference of number towards others is its essential determination; it constitutes its being-determined-in-itself, but at the same time its own externality.—It is thus a numerical one, as the absolutely determinate, which at the same time has the form of simple immediacy, and for which, therefore, the relation to another is wholly external. As a one that is number, it further has determinacy, insofar as it is relation to another, as its moments within itself, in its distinction of unity and amount, and the amount is itself a multiplicity of ones, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"60.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0014","text":"it is within itself this absolute externality.—This contradiction of number, or of quantum in general, within itself is the quality of quantum, in whose further determinations this contradiction develops.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"60.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIEZ:P0014"]}],"source_digest":"dc155bf40a2e1c2272ef06c2872b70df553513dd7c5fc586401775470b4eef7b","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Die Zahl."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Die Zahl.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14","title":"Remark 1.","order":61,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_14","text":"Die Raumgröße und Zahlgröße pflegen so als zwei Arten betrachtet zu werden, daß die Raumgröße für sich so sehr bestimmte Größe als die Zahlgröße wäre; ihr Unterschied bestünde nur in den verschiedenen Bestimmungen der Kontinuität und Diskretion; als Quantum aber stünden sie auf derselben Stufe. Die Geometrie hat im Allgemeinen in der Raumgröße die kontinuirliche, und die Arithmetik in der Zahlgröße die diskrete Größe zum Gegenstande. Aber mit dieser Ungleichheit des Gegenstandes haben sie auch nicht eine gleiche Weise und Vollkommenheit der Begrenzung oder des Bestimmtseyns. Die Raumgröße hat nur die Begrenzung überhaupt; insofern sie als ein schlechthin bestimmtes Quantum betrachtet werden soll, hat sie die Zahl nöthig. Die Geometrie als solche mißt die Raumfiguren nicht, ist nicht Meßkunst; sondern vergleicht sie nur. Auch bei ihren Definitionen sind die Bestimmungen zum Theil von der Gleichheit der Seiten, Winkel, der gleichen Entfernung hergenommen. So bedarf der Kreis, weil er allein auf die Gleichheit der Entfernung aller in ihm möglichen Punkte von einem Mittelpunkte beruht, zu seiner Bestimmung keiner Zahl. Diese auf Gleichheit oder Ungleichheit beruhenden Bestimmungen sind ächt geometrisch. Aber sie reichen nicht aus, und zu andern z. B. Dreieck, Viereck, ist die Zahl erforderlich, die in ihrem Princip, dem Eins das Für-sich-bestimmtseyn, nicht das Bestimmtseyn durch Hülfe eines Andern, also nicht durch Vergleichung enthält. Die Raumgröße hat zwar an dem Punkte die dem Eins entsprechende Bestimmtheit; der Punkt aber wird, insofern er außer sich kommt, ein Anderes, er wird zur Linie; weil er wesentlich nur als Eins des Raumes ist, wird er in der Beziehung, zu einer Kontinuität, in der die Punktualität, das Für-sich-Bestimmtseyn, das Eins, aufgehoben ist. Insofern das Für-sich-Bestimmtseyn im Außersichseyn sich erhalten soll, muß die Linie als eine Menge von Eins vorgestellt werden, und die Grenze, die Bestimmung der vielen Eins, in sich bekommen, d. h. die Größe der Linie—eben so der anderen Raum-Bestimmungen—muß als Zahl genommen werden.\n\nDie Arithmetik betrachtet die Zahl und deren Figuren, oder vielmehr betrachtet sie nicht, sondern operirt mit denselben. Denn die Zahl ist die gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, träge; sie muß von außen bethätigt und in Beziehung gebracht werden. Die Beziehungsweisen sind die Rechnungsarten. Sie werden in der Arithmetik nach einander aufgeführt, und es erhellt, daß eine von der andern abhängt. Der Faden, der ihren Fortgang leitet, wird jedoch in der Arithmetik nicht herausgehoben.\n\nAus der Begriffsbestimmung der Zahl selbst aber ergiebt sich leicht die systematische Zusammenstellung, auf welche der Vortrag dieser Elemente in den Lehrbüchern einen gerechten Anspruch hat. Diese leitenden Bestimmungen sollen hier kurz bemerklich gemacht werden.\n\nDie Zahl ist um ihres Principes, des Eins, willen ein äußerlich Zusammengefaßtes überhaupt, eine schlechthin analytische Figur, die keinen inneren Zusammenhang enthält. Weil sie so nur ein äußerlich Erzeugtes ist, ist alles Rechnen das Hervorbringen von Zahlen, ein Zählen oder bestimmter: Zusammenzählen. Eine Verschiedenheit dieses äußerlichen Hervorbringens, das nur iminer dasselbe thut, kann allein in einem Unterschiede der Zahlen gegeneinander, die zusammengezählt werden sollen, liegen; solcher Unterschied muß selbst anderswoher und aus äußerlicher Bestimmung genommen werden.\n\nDer qualitative Unterschied, der die Bestimmtheit der Zahl ausmacht, ist der, den wir gesehen, der Einheit und der Anzahl; auf diesen reducirt sich daher alle Begriffsbestimmtheit, die in den Rechnungsarten vorkommen kann. Der Unterschied aber, der den Zahlen als Quantis zukommt, ist die äußerliche Identität und der äußerliche Unterschied, die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, welches Reflexionsmomente, und unter den Bestimmungen des Wesens beim Unterschiede, abzuhandeln sind.\n\nFerner ist noch vorauszuschicken, daß Zahlen im Allgemeinen auf zwei Weisen hervorgebracht werden können, entweder durch Zusammenfassen oder durch Trennen bereits zusammengefaßter;—indem beides bei einer auf dieselbe Weise bestimmten Art von Zählen Statt findet, so entspricht einem Zusammenfassen von Zahlen, was man positive Rechnungsart, ein Trennen, was man negative Rechnungsart nennen kann; die Bestimmung der Rechnungsart selbst, ist von diesem Gegensatze unabhängig.\n\nNach diesen Bemerkungen folgt hiermit die Angabe der Rechnungsweisen. Das erste Erzeugen der Zahl ist das Zusammenfassen von Vielen als solchen, d. i. deren jedes nur als Eins gesetzt ist,—das Numeriren. Da die Eins äußerliche gegeneinander sind, stellen sie sich unter einem sinnlichen Bilde dar, und die Operation, durch welche die Zahl erzeugt wird, ist ein Abzählen an den Fingern, an Punkten u.s.f. Was Vier, Fünf u.s.f. ist, kann nur gewiesen werden. Das Abbrechen, wie viel zugefaßt werden soll, ist, indem die Grenze äußerlich ist, etwas Zufälliges, Beliebiges.—Der Unterschied von Anzahl und Einheit, der im Fortgange der Rechnungsarten eintritt, begründet ein System, dyadisches, dekadisches u.s.f.—von Zahlen; ein solches beruht im Ganzen auf der Beliebigkeit, welche Anzahl konstant wieder als Einheit genommen werden soll.\n\nDie durch das Numeriren entstandenen Zahlen werden wieder numerirt; und indem sie so unmittelbar gesetzt sind, sind sie noch ohne alle Beziehung auf einander bestimmt, gleichgültig gegen Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, von zufälliger Grösse gegen einander,—daher ungleiche überhaupt;—Addiren.—Daß 7 und 5 Zwölfe ausmacht, erfährt man dadurch, daß zu den 7 noch 5 Eins an den Fingern oder sonst hinzunumerirt werden,—wovon das Resultat nachher im Gedächtnisse, auswendig, behalten wird; denn Innerliches ist nichts dabei. Ebenso daß 7 x 5 = 35 ist, weiß man durch das Abzählen an den Fingern u.s.f., daß zu einem Sieben noch eins hinzu numerirt, dieß fünf Mal bewerkstelligt, und das Resultat gleichfalls auswendig behalten wird. Die Mühe dieses Numerirens, der Erfindung der Summen, Produkte, ist durch die fertigen Eins und Eins oder Eins mal Eins, die man nur auswendig zu lernen hat, abgethan.\n\nKant hat (in der Einleitung zur Kritik der reinen Vernunft V.) den Satz: 7 + 5 = 12, als einen synthetischen Satz betrachtet. \"Man sollte,\" sagt er, \"anfänglich zwar denken, (gewiß!) er sey ein bloß analytischer Satz, der aus dem Begriffe einer Summe von Sieben und Fünf nach dem Satz des Widerspruchs erfolge.\" Der Begriff der Summe heißt weiter nichts, als die abstrakte Bestimmung, daß diese zwei Zahlen zusammengefaßt werden sollen, und zwar als Zahlen auf eine äußerliche, d. i. begrifflose Weise,—daß von Sieben weiter numerirt werden soll, bis die hinzuzufügenden Eins, deren Anzahl auf Fünf bestimmt ist, erschöpft worden; das Resultat führt den sonst bekannten Nahmen Zwölfe. \"Allein,\" fährt Kant fort, \"wenn man es näher betrachtet, so findet man, daß der Begriff der Summe von 7 + 5 nichts weiter enthalte, als die Vereinigung beider Zahlen in eine einzige, wodurch ganz und gar nicht gedacht wird, welches diese einzige Zahl sey, die beide zusammenfaßt;\"—\"ich mag meinen Begriff von einer solchen möglichen Summe noch so sehr zergliedern, so werde ich doch darin die Zwölfe nicht antreffen.\" Mit dem Denken der Summe, Zergliederung des Begriffs, hat der Übergang von jener Aufgabe zu dem Resultat allerdings nichts [zu] thun; \"man muß über diese Begriffe hinausgehen und die Anschauung, fünf Finger u.s.f. zu Hülfe nehmen und so die Einheiten der in der Anschauung gegebenen Fünf zu dem Begriffe von Sieben hinzuthun,\" fügt er hinzu. Fünf ist allerdings in der Anschauung gegeben, d. h. ein ganz äußerliches Zusammengefügtseyn des beliebig wiederholten Gedankens, Eins; aber Sieben ist ebenso wenig ein Begriff; es sind keine Begriffe vorhanden, über die man hinausgeht. Die Summe von 5 und 7 heißt die begrifflose Verbindung beider Zahlen, das so begrifflos fortgesetzte Numeriren von Sieben an, bis die Fünfe erschöpft sind, kann man ein Zusammenfügen, ein Synthesiren, gerade wie das Numeriren von Eins an, nennen—ein Synthesiren, das aber gänzlich analytischer Natur ist, indem der Zusammenhang ein ganz gemachter, nichts darin ist noch hineinkommt, was nicht ganz äußerlich vorliegt. Das Postulat 5 zu 7 zu addiren verhält sich zu dem Postulate, überhaupt zu numeriren, wie das Postulat eine gerade Linie zu verlängern, zu dem, eine gerade Linie zu ziehen.\n\nSo leer als der Ausdruck Synthesiren ist, ist die Bestimmung, daß es a priori geschehe. Zählen ist allerdings keine Empfindungsbestimmung, die für das a posteriori nach der kantischen Bestimmung von Anschauung allein übrig bleibt, und Zählen ist wohl eine Beschäftigung auf dem Boden des abstrakten Anschauens, d. i. welches durch die Kategorie des Eins bestimmt und wobei von allen anderen Empfindungsbestimmungen, ebenso sehr als auch von Begriffen abstrahirt ist. Das a priori ist überhaupt etwas nur Vages; die Gefühlsbestimmung hat als Trieb, Sinn u.s.f. ebenso sehr das Moment der Aprioritaet in ihr, als Raum und Zeit als existirend, Zeitliches und Räumliches, a posteriori bestimmt ist.\n\nIm Zusammenhange hiermit kann hinzugefügt werden, daß Kants Behauptung von der synthetischen Beschaffenheit der Grundsätze der reinen Geometrie ebenso wenig etwas Gründliches enthält. Indem er angiebt, daß mehrere wirklich analytisch seyen, so ist allein der Grundsatz, daß die gerade Linie zwischen zwei Punkten die kürzeste ist, für jene Vorstellung angeführt. \"Mein Begriff vom Geraden enthalte nämlich nichts von Größe, sondern nur eine Qualität; der Begriff des Kürzesten komme also gänzlich hinzu, und könne durch keine Zergliederung aus dem Begriffe der geraden Linie gezogen werden; Anschauung müsse also hier zu Hülfe genommen werden, vermittelst deren allein die Synthesis möglich sey.\"—Es handelt sich aber auch hier nicht von einem Begriffe des Geraden überhaupt, sondern von gerader Linie, und dieselbe ist bereits ein Räumliches, Angeschautes. Die Bestimmung (oder wenn man will, der Begriff) der geraden Linie ist doch wohl keine anderes als daß sie die schlechthin einfache Linie ist, d. i. in dem Außersichkommen (der sogenannten Bewegung des Punktes) schlechthin sich auf sich bezieht, in deren Ausdehnung keine Art von Verschiedenheit der Bestimmung, keine Beziehung auf einen anderen Punkt, oder Linie außerhalb ihrer gesetzt ist, hält;—die schlechthin in sich einfache Richtung. Diese Einfachheit ist allerdings ihre Qualität, und wenn die gerade Linie schwer analytisch zu definiren scheinen sollte, so wäre es nur um der Bestimmung der Einfachheit oder Beziehung auf sich selbst willen, und bloß weil die Reflexion beim Bestimmen zunächst vornehmlich eine Mehrheit, ein Bestimmen durch andere, vor sich hat; es ist aber für sich schlechthin nichts Schweres, diese Bestimmung der Einfachheit der Ausdehnung in sich, ihrer Bestimmungslosigkeit durch Anderes, zu fassen;—Euklids Definition enthält nichts Anderes als diese Einfachheit.—Der Übergang nun aber dieser Qualität zur quantitativen Bestimmung (des Kürzesten), welcher das Synthetische ausmachen sollte, ist ganz nur analytisch. Die Linie ist als räumlich, Quantität überhaupt; das Einfachste, vom Quantum gesagt, ist das Wenigste, und dieß von einer Linie gesagt, ist das Kürzeste. Die Geometrie kann diese Bestimmungen als Corollarium zur Definition aufnehmen; aber Archimedes in seinen Büchern über Kugel und Cylinder (s. Haubers Übers. S. ) hat am zweckmäßigsten gethan, jene Bestimmung der geraden Linie als Grundsatz hinzustellen, in ebenso richtigem Sinne, als Euklides die Bestimmung, die Parallellinien betreffend, unter die Grundsätze gestellt hat, da die Entwickelung dieser Bestimmung, um zu einer Definition zu werden, gleichfalls nicht der Räumlichkeit unmittelbar angehörige, sondern abstraktere qualitative Bestimmungen, wie vorhin Einfachheit, Gleichheit der Richtung und dergleichen erfordert hätte. Diese Alten haben auch ihren Wissenschaften plastischen Charakter gegeben, ihre Darstellung streng in der Eigenthümlichkeit ihres Stoffes gehalten, daher das ausgeschlossen, was für denselben heterogener Art gewesen wäre.\n\nDer Begriff, den Kant in den synthetischen Urtheilen a priori aufgestellt hat,—der Begriff von Unterschiedenem, das ebenso untrennbar ist, einem Identischen, das an ihm selbst ungetrennt Unterschied ist, gehört zu dem Grossen und Unsterblichen seiner Philosophie. Im Anschauen ist dieser Begriffe da er der Begriff selbst und Alles an sich der Begriff ist, freilich gleichfalls vorhanden; aber die Bestimmungen, die in jenen Beispielen herausgenommen sind, stellen ihn nicht dar; vielmehr ist die Zahl und das Zählen eine Identität und Hervorbringen einer Identität, die schlechthin nur äußerlich, nur oberflächliche Synthese ist, eine Einheit von Eins, solchen, die vielmehr als an ihnen nicht identisch mit einander, sondern äußerliche, für sich getrennte, gesetzt sind; in der geraden Linie hat die Bestimmung, die kleinste zwischen zwei Punkten zu seyn, vielmehr nur das Moment des abstrakt Identischen, ohne Unterschied an ihm selbst, zu Grunde zu liegen.\n\nIch kehre von dieser Unterbrechung zum Addiren selbst zurück. Die ihm entsprechende, negative Rechnungsart, das Subtrahiren, ist das ebenso ganz analytische Trennen in Zahlen, die wie im Addiren, nur als Ungleiche überhaupt gegeneinander bestimmt sind.\n\n2. Die nächste Bestimmung ist die Gleichheit der Zahlen, die numerirt werden sollen. Durch diese Gleichheit sind sie eine Einheit, und es tritt hiermit an der Zahl der Unterschied von Einheit und Anzahl ein. Die Multiplikation ist die Aufgabe, eine Anzahl von Einheiten, die selbst eine Anzahl sind, zusammenzuzählen. Es ist dabei gleichgültig, welche von den beiden Zahlen als Einheit und welche als Anzahl angegeben, ob viermal drei, wo Vier die Anzahl, und drei die Einheit ist, oder umgekehrt dreimal vier, gesagt wird.—Es ist oben schon angegeben, daß das ursprüngliche Finden des Produkts durch das einfache Numeriren, d. i. das Abzählen an den Fingern u.s.f. bewerkstelligt wird; das spätere unmittelbare Angebenkönnen des Produkts beruht auf der Sammlung jener Produkte, dem Einmaleins, und dem Auswendig-Wissen desselben.\n\nDie Division ist die negative Rechnungsart nach derselben Bestimmung des Unterschieds. Es ist ebenso gleichgültig, welcher von beiden Faktoren, der Divisor oder der Quotient, als Einheit oder als Anzahl bestimmt wird. Der Divisor wird als Einheit und der Quotient als Anzahl bestimmt, wenn die Aufgabe der Division ausgesprochen wird, daß man sehen wolle, wie oft (Anzahl) eine Zahl (Einheit) in einer gegebenen enthalten sey; umgekehrt wird der Divisor als Anzahl und der Quotient als Einheit genommen, wenn gesagt wird, man soll eine Zahl in eine gegebene Anzahl gleicher Theile theilen und die Grösse solchen Theils (der Einheit) finden.\n\n3. Die beiden Zahlen, welche als Einheit und Anzahl gegeneinander bestimmt sind, sind als Zahl noch unmittelbar gegeneinander, und daher überhaupt ungleich. Die weitere Gleichheit ist die der Einheit und der Anzahl selbst; so ist der Fortgang zur Gleichheit der Bestimmungen, die in der Bestimmung der Zahl liegen, vollendet. Das Zählen, nach dieser vollständigen Gleichheit ist das Potenziren, (die negative Rechnungsart das Wurzelausziehen)—und zwar zunächst das Erheben einer Zahl ins Quadrat,—das vollkommene Bestimmtseyn des Numerirens in sich selbst, wo 1) die vielen Zahlen, die addirt werden, dieselben sind, und 2) deren Vielheit oder Anzahl selbst dieselbe ist mit der Zahl, die vielmal gesetzt wird, die Einheit ist. Es sind sonst keine Bestimmungen in dem Begriffe der Zahl, die einen Unterschied darbieten könnten; noch kann ein weiteres Ausgleichen des Unterschiedes, der in in der Zahl liegt, Statt finden. Erhebung in höhere Potenzen als in das Quadrat, ist eine formelle Fortsetzung Theils—bei den geraden Exponenten,—nur eine Wiederholung des Quadrirens, Theils bei den ungeraden Potenzen—tritt wieder die Ungleichheit ein; bei der nämlich formellen Gleichheit (z.B. zunächst beim Kubus) des neuen Faktors mit der Anzahl sowohl als mit der Einheit, ist er als Einheit, gegen die Anzahl (das Quadrat, 3 gegen 3. 3) ein Ungleiches; noch mehr beim Kubus von Vier, wo die Anzahl, 3, nach der die Zahl, die die Einheit ist, mit sich multiplicirt werden soll, von dieser selbst verschieden ist.—Es sind an sich diese Bestimmungen als der wesentliche Unterschied des Begriffs, die Anzahl und die Einheit, vorhanden, welche für das vollständige In-sich-Zurückgehen des Außer-sich-gehens auszugleichen sind. In dem so eben Dargestellten liegt weiter der Grund, warum Theils die Auflösung der höheren Gleichungen in der Zurückführung auf die quadratische bestehen muß, Theils warum die Gleichungen von ungeraden Exponenten sich nur formell bestimmen, und gerade wenn die Wurzeln rational sind, diese sich nicht anders als durch einen imaginären Ausdruck, d. h. der das Gegentheil dessen ist, was die Wurzeln sind und ausdrücken, finden lassen.—Das Quadrat der Arithmetik enthält nach dem Angegebenen, allein das Schlechthin-Bestimmtseyn in sich; weswegen die Gleichungen mit weitern formellen Potenzen darauf zurückgeführt werden müssen, gerade wie das rechtwinklichte Dreieck in der Geometrie das Schlechthin-in-sich-Bestimmtseyn enthält, das im pythagoräischen Lehrsatz exponirt ist, weswegen auch darauf für die totale Bestimmung alle anderen geometrischen Figurationen reducirt werden müssen.\n\nEin nach einem logisch gebildetem Urtheile fortschreitender Unterricht handelt die Lehre von den Potenzen vor der Lehre über die Proportionen ab; diese schließen sich zwar an den Unterschied von Einheit und Anzahl an, der die Bestimmung der zweiten Rechnungsart ausmacht, aber sie treten aus dem Eins des unmittelbaren Quantums, in welchem Einheit und Anzahl nur Momente sind, heraus; die Fortbestimmung nach demselben bleibt ihm selbst auch noch äußerlich. Die Zahl im Verhältnisse ist nicht mehr als unmittelbares Quantum; es hat seine Bestimmtheit dann als Vermittelung; das quantitative Verhältniß wird im Nachfolgenden betrachtet.\n\nVon der angegebenen Fortbestimmung der Rechnungsarten kann gesagt werden, daß sie keine Philosophie über dieselben, keine Darlegung etwa ihrer innern Bedeutung sey, weil sie in der That nicht eine immanente Entwickelung des Begriffes ist. Aber die Philosophie muß dieß zu unterscheiden wissen, was seiner Natur nach ein sich selbst äußerlicher Stoff ist, daß dann an einem solchen der Fortgang des Begriffs nur auf äußerliche Weise geschehen, und dessen Momente auch nur in der eigenthümlichen Form ihrer Äußerlichkeit, wie hier Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, seyn können. Die Unterscheidung der Sphären, in welche eine bestimmte Form des Begriffs gehört, d. h. als Existenz vorhanden ist, ist ein wesentliches Erforderniß zum Philosophiren über reale Gegenstände, um nicht das Äußerliche und Zufällige durch Ideen in seiner Eigenthümlichkeit zu stören, wie diese Ideen durch die Unangemessenheit des Stoffes zu entstellen und formell zu machen. Jene Äußerlichkeit aber, in welcher die Begriffsmomente an jenem äußerlichen Stoffe, der Zahl, erscheinen, ist hier die angemessene Form; indem sie den Gegenstand in seinem Verstande darstellen, auch da sie keine spekulative Anforderung enthalten und daher leicht erscheinen, verdienen sie in den Lehrbüchern der Elemente angewendet zu werden.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0001","text":"Die Raumgröße und Zahlgröße pflegen so als zwei Arten betrachtet zu werden, daß die Raumgröße für sich so sehr bestimmte Größe als die Zahlgröße wäre; ihr Unterschied bestünde nur in den verschiedenen Bestimmungen der Kontinuität und Diskretion; als Quantum aber stünden sie auf derselben Stufe. Die Geometrie hat im Allgemeinen in der Raumgröße die kontinuirliche, und die Arithmetik in der Zahlgröße die diskrete Größe zum Gegenstande. Aber mit dieser Ungleichheit des Gegenstandes haben sie auch nicht eine gleiche Weise und Vollkommenheit der Begrenzung oder des Bestimmtseyns. Die Raumgröße hat nur die Begrenzung überhaupt; insofern sie als ein schlechthin bestimmtes Quantum betrachtet werden soll, hat sie die Zahl nöthig. Die Geometrie als solche mißt die Raumfiguren nicht, ist nicht Meßkunst; sondern vergleicht sie nur.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"61.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0002","text":"Auch bei ihren Definitionen sind die Bestimmungen zum Theil von der Gleichheit der Seiten, Winkel, der gleichen Entfernung hergenommen. So bedarf der Kreis, weil er allein auf die Gleichheit der Entfernung aller in ihm möglichen Punkte von einem Mittelpunkte beruht, zu seiner Bestimmung keiner Zahl. Diese auf Gleichheit oder Ungleichheit beruhenden Bestimmungen sind ächt geometrisch. Aber sie reichen nicht aus, und zu andern z. B. Dreieck, Viereck, ist die Zahl erforderlich, die in ihrem Princip, dem Eins das Für-sich-bestimmtseyn, nicht das Bestimmtseyn durch Hülfe eines Andern, also nicht durch Vergleichung enthält.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"61.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0003","text":"Die Raumgröße hat zwar an dem Punkte die dem Eins entsprechende Bestimmtheit; der Punkt aber wird, insofern er außer sich kommt, ein Anderes, er wird zur Linie; weil er wesentlich nur als Eins des Raumes ist, wird er in der Beziehung, zu einer Kontinuität, in der die Punktualität, das Für-sich-Bestimmtseyn, das Eins, aufgehoben ist. Insofern das Für-sich-Bestimmtseyn im Außersichseyn sich erhalten soll, muß die Linie als eine Menge von Eins vorgestellt werden, und die Grenze, die Bestimmung der vielen Eins, in sich bekommen, d. h. die Größe der Linie—eben so der anderen Raum-Bestimmungen—muß als Zahl genommen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"61.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0004","text":"Die Arithmetik betrachtet die Zahl und deren Figuren, oder vielmehr betrachtet sie nicht, sondern operirt mit denselben. Denn die Zahl ist die gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, träge; sie muß von außen bethätigt und in Beziehung gebracht werden. Die Beziehungsweisen sind die Rechnungsarten. Sie werden in der Arithmetik nach einander aufgeführt, und es erhellt, daß eine von der andern abhängt. Der Faden, der ihren Fortgang leitet, wird jedoch in der Arithmetik nicht herausgehoben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"61.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0005","text":"Aus der Begriffsbestimmung der Zahl selbst aber ergiebt sich leicht die systematische Zusammenstellung, auf welche der Vortrag dieser Elemente in den Lehrbüchern einen gerechten Anspruch hat. Diese leitenden Bestimmungen sollen hier kurz bemerklich gemacht werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"61.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0006","text":"Die Zahl ist um ihres Principes, des Eins, willen ein äußerlich Zusammengefaßtes überhaupt, eine schlechthin analytische Figur, die keinen inneren Zusammenhang enthält. Weil sie so nur ein äußerlich Erzeugtes ist, ist alles Rechnen das Hervorbringen von Zahlen, ein Zählen oder bestimmter: Zusammenzählen. Eine Verschiedenheit dieses äußerlichen Hervorbringens, das nur iminer dasselbe thut, kann allein in einem Unterschiede der Zahlen gegeneinander, die zusammengezählt werden sollen, liegen; solcher Unterschied muß selbst anderswoher und aus äußerlicher Bestimmung genommen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"61.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0007","text":"Der qualitative Unterschied, der die Bestimmtheit der Zahl ausmacht, ist der, den wir gesehen, der Einheit und der Anzahl; auf diesen reducirt sich daher alle Begriffsbestimmtheit, die in den Rechnungsarten vorkommen kann. Der Unterschied aber, der den Zahlen als Quantis zukommt, ist die äußerliche Identität und der äußerliche Unterschied, die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, welches Reflexionsmomente, und unter den Bestimmungen des Wesens beim Unterschiede, abzuhandeln sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"61.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0008","text":"Ferner ist noch vorauszuschicken, daß Zahlen im Allgemeinen auf zwei Weisen hervorgebracht werden können, entweder durch Zusammenfassen oder durch Trennen bereits zusammengefaßter;—indem beides bei einer auf dieselbe Weise bestimmten Art von Zählen Statt findet, so entspricht einem Zusammenfassen von Zahlen, was man positive Rechnungsart, ein Trennen, was man negative Rechnungsart nennen kann; die Bestimmung der Rechnungsart selbst, ist von diesem Gegensatze unabhängig.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"61.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0009","text":"Nach diesen Bemerkungen folgt hiermit die Angabe der Rechnungsweisen. Das erste Erzeugen der Zahl ist das Zusammenfassen von Vielen als solchen, d. i. deren jedes nur als Eins gesetzt ist,—das Numeriren. Da die Eins äußerliche gegeneinander sind, stellen sie sich unter einem sinnlichen Bilde dar, und die Operation, durch welche die Zahl erzeugt wird, ist ein Abzählen an den Fingern, an Punkten u.s.f. Was Vier, Fünf u.s.f. ist, kann nur gewiesen werden. Das Abbrechen, wie viel zugefaßt werden soll, ist, indem die Grenze äußerlich ist, etwas Zufälliges, Beliebiges.—Der Unterschied von Anzahl und Einheit, der im Fortgange der Rechnungsarten eintritt, begründet ein System, dyadisches, dekadisches u.s.f.—von Zahlen; ein solches beruht im Ganzen auf der Beliebigkeit, welche Anzahl konstant wieder als Einheit genommen werden soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"61.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0010","text":"Die durch das Numeriren entstandenen Zahlen werden wieder numerirt; und indem sie so unmittelbar gesetzt sind, sind sie noch ohne alle Beziehung auf einander bestimmt, gleichgültig gegen Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, von zufälliger Grösse gegen einander,—daher ungleiche überhaupt;—Addiren.—Daß 7 und 5 Zwölfe ausmacht, erfährt man dadurch, daß zu den 7 noch 5 Eins an den Fingern oder sonst hinzunumerirt werden,—wovon das Resultat nachher im Gedächtnisse, auswendig, behalten wird; denn Innerliches ist nichts dabei. Ebenso daß 7 x 5 = 35 ist, weiß man durch das Abzählen an den Fingern u.s.f., daß zu einem Sieben noch eins hinzu numerirt, dieß fünf Mal bewerkstelligt, und das Resultat gleichfalls auswendig behalten wird. Die Mühe dieses Numerirens, der Erfindung der Summen, Produkte, ist durch die fertigen Eins und Eins oder Eins mal Eins, die man nur auswendig zu lernen hat, abgethan.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"61.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0011","text":"Kant hat (in der Einleitung zur Kritik der reinen Vernunft V.) den Satz: 7 + 5 = 12, als einen synthetischen Satz betrachtet. \"Man sollte,\" sagt er, \"anfänglich zwar denken, (gewiß!) er sey ein bloß analytischer Satz, der aus dem Begriffe einer Summe von Sieben und Fünf nach dem Satz des Widerspruchs erfolge.\" Der Begriff der Summe heißt weiter nichts, als die abstrakte Bestimmung, daß diese zwei Zahlen zusammengefaßt werden sollen, und zwar als Zahlen auf eine äußerliche, d. i. begrifflose Weise,—daß von Sieben weiter numerirt werden soll, bis die hinzuzufügenden Eins, deren Anzahl auf Fünf bestimmt ist, erschöpft worden; das Resultat führt den sonst bekannten Nahmen Zwölfe.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"61.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0012","text":"\"Allein,\" fährt Kant fort, \"wenn man es näher betrachtet, so findet man, daß der Begriff der Summe von 7 + 5 nichts weiter enthalte, als die Vereinigung beider Zahlen in eine einzige, wodurch ganz und gar nicht gedacht wird, welches diese einzige Zahl sey, die beide zusammenfaßt;\"—\"ich mag meinen Begriff von einer solchen möglichen Summe noch so sehr zergliedern, so werde ich doch darin die Zwölfe nicht antreffen.\" Mit dem Denken der Summe, Zergliederung des Begriffs, hat der Übergang von jener Aufgabe zu dem Resultat allerdings nichts [zu] thun; \"man muß über diese Begriffe hinausgehen und die Anschauung, fünf Finger u.s.f. zu Hülfe nehmen und so die Einheiten der in der Anschauung gegebenen Fünf zu dem Begriffe von Sieben hinzuthun,\" fügt er hinzu. Fünf ist allerdings in der Anschauung gegeben, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"61.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0013","text":"ein ganz äußerliches Zusammengefügtseyn des beliebig wiederholten Gedankens, Eins; aber Sieben ist ebenso wenig ein Begriff; es sind keine Begriffe vorhanden, über die man hinausgeht. Die Summe von 5 und 7 heißt die begrifflose Verbindung beider Zahlen, das so begrifflos fortgesetzte Numeriren von Sieben an, bis die Fünfe erschöpft sind, kann man ein Zusammenfügen, ein Synthesiren, gerade wie das Numeriren von Eins an, nennen—ein Synthesiren, das aber gänzlich analytischer Natur ist, indem der Zusammenhang ein ganz gemachter, nichts darin ist noch hineinkommt, was nicht ganz äußerlich vorliegt. Das Postulat 5 zu 7 zu addiren verhält sich zu dem Postulate, überhaupt zu numeriren, wie das Postulat eine gerade Linie zu verlängern, zu dem, eine gerade Linie zu ziehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"61.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0014","text":"So leer als der Ausdruck Synthesiren ist, ist die Bestimmung, daß es a priori geschehe. Zählen ist allerdings keine Empfindungsbestimmung, die für das a posteriori nach der kantischen Bestimmung von Anschauung allein übrig bleibt, und Zählen ist wohl eine Beschäftigung auf dem Boden des abstrakten Anschauens, d. i. welches durch die Kategorie des Eins bestimmt und wobei von allen anderen Empfindungsbestimmungen, ebenso sehr als auch von Begriffen abstrahirt ist. Das a priori ist überhaupt etwas nur Vages; die Gefühlsbestimmung hat als Trieb, Sinn u.s.f. ebenso sehr das Moment der Aprioritaet in ihr, als Raum und Zeit als existirend, Zeitliches und Räumliches, a posteriori bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"61.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0015","text":"Im Zusammenhange hiermit kann hinzugefügt werden, daß Kants Behauptung von der synthetischen Beschaffenheit der Grundsätze der reinen Geometrie ebenso wenig etwas Gründliches enthält. Indem er angiebt, daß mehrere wirklich analytisch seyen, so ist allein der Grundsatz, daß die gerade Linie zwischen zwei Punkten die kürzeste ist, für jene Vorstellung angeführt. \"Mein Begriff vom Geraden enthalte nämlich nichts von Größe, sondern nur eine Qualität; der Begriff des Kürzesten komme also gänzlich hinzu, und könne durch keine Zergliederung aus dem Begriffe der geraden Linie gezogen werden; Anschauung müsse also hier zu Hülfe genommen werden, vermittelst deren allein die Synthesis möglich sey.\"—Es handelt sich aber auch hier nicht von einem Begriffe des Geraden überhaupt, sondern von gerader Linie, und dieselbe ist bereits ein Räumliches, Angeschautes.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"61.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0016","text":"Die Bestimmung (oder wenn man will, der Begriff) der geraden Linie ist doch wohl keine anderes als daß sie die schlechthin einfache Linie ist, d. i. in dem Außersichkommen (der sogenannten Bewegung des Punktes) schlechthin sich auf sich bezieht, in deren Ausdehnung keine Art von Verschiedenheit der Bestimmung, keine Beziehung auf einen anderen Punkt, oder Linie außerhalb ihrer gesetzt ist, hält;—die schlechthin in sich einfache Richtung.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"61.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0017","text":"Diese Einfachheit ist allerdings ihre Qualität, und wenn die gerade Linie schwer analytisch zu definiren scheinen sollte, so wäre es nur um der Bestimmung der Einfachheit oder Beziehung auf sich selbst willen, und bloß weil die Reflexion beim Bestimmen zunächst vornehmlich eine Mehrheit, ein Bestimmen durch andere, vor sich hat; es ist aber für sich schlechthin nichts Schweres, diese Bestimmung der Einfachheit der Ausdehnung in sich, ihrer Bestimmungslosigkeit durch Anderes, zu fassen;—Euklids Definition enthält nichts Anderes als diese Einfachheit.—Der Übergang nun aber dieser Qualität zur quantitativen Bestimmung (des Kürzesten), welcher das Synthetische ausmachen sollte, ist ganz nur analytisch. Die Linie ist als räumlich, Quantität überhaupt; das Einfachste, vom Quantum gesagt, ist das Wenigste, und dieß von einer Linie gesagt, ist das Kürzeste.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"61.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0018","text":"Die Geometrie kann diese Bestimmungen als Corollarium zur Definition aufnehmen; aber Archimedes in seinen Büchern über Kugel und Cylinder (s. Haubers Übers. S. ) hat am zweckmäßigsten gethan, jene Bestimmung der geraden Linie als Grundsatz hinzustellen, in ebenso richtigem Sinne, als Euklides die Bestimmung, die Parallellinien betreffend, unter die Grundsätze gestellt hat, da die Entwickelung dieser Bestimmung, um zu einer Definition zu werden, gleichfalls nicht der Räumlichkeit unmittelbar angehörige, sondern abstraktere qualitative Bestimmungen, wie vorhin Einfachheit, Gleichheit der Richtung und dergleichen erfordert hätte. Diese Alten haben auch ihren Wissenschaften plastischen Charakter gegeben, ihre Darstellung streng in der Eigenthümlichkeit ihres Stoffes gehalten, daher das ausgeschlossen, was für denselben heterogener Art gewesen wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"61.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0019","text":"Der Begriff, den Kant in den synthetischen Urtheilen a priori aufgestellt hat,—der Begriff von Unterschiedenem, das ebenso untrennbar ist, einem Identischen, das an ihm selbst ungetrennt Unterschied ist, gehört zu dem Grossen und Unsterblichen seiner Philosophie.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"61.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0020","text":"Im Anschauen ist dieser Begriffe da er der Begriff selbst und Alles an sich der Begriff ist, freilich gleichfalls vorhanden; aber die Bestimmungen, die in jenen Beispielen herausgenommen sind, stellen ihn nicht dar; vielmehr ist die Zahl und das Zählen eine Identität und Hervorbringen einer Identität, die schlechthin nur äußerlich, nur oberflächliche Synthese ist, eine Einheit von Eins, solchen, die vielmehr als an ihnen nicht identisch mit einander, sondern äußerliche, für sich getrennte, gesetzt sind; in der geraden Linie hat die Bestimmung, die kleinste zwischen zwei Punkten zu seyn, vielmehr nur das Moment des abstrakt Identischen, ohne Unterschied an ihm selbst, zu Grunde zu liegen.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"61.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0021","text":"Ich kehre von dieser Unterbrechung zum Addiren selbst zurück. Die ihm entsprechende, negative Rechnungsart, das Subtrahiren, ist das ebenso ganz analytische Trennen in Zahlen, die wie im Addiren, nur als Ungleiche überhaupt gegeneinander bestimmt sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"61.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0022","text":"2. Die nächste Bestimmung ist die Gleichheit der Zahlen, die numerirt werden sollen. Durch diese Gleichheit sind sie eine Einheit, und es tritt hiermit an der Zahl der Unterschied von Einheit und Anzahl ein. Die Multiplikation ist die Aufgabe, eine Anzahl von Einheiten, die selbst eine Anzahl sind, zusammenzuzählen. Es ist dabei gleichgültig, welche von den beiden Zahlen als Einheit und welche als Anzahl angegeben, ob viermal drei, wo Vier die Anzahl, und drei die Einheit ist, oder umgekehrt dreimal vier, gesagt wird.—Es ist oben schon angegeben, daß das ursprüngliche Finden des Produkts durch das einfache Numeriren, d. i. das Abzählen an den Fingern u.s.f. bewerkstelligt wird; das spätere unmittelbare Angebenkönnen des Produkts beruht auf der Sammlung jener Produkte, dem Einmaleins, und dem Auswendig-Wissen desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"61.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0023","text":"Die Division ist die negative Rechnungsart nach derselben Bestimmung des Unterschieds. Es ist ebenso gleichgültig, welcher von beiden Faktoren, der Divisor oder der Quotient, als Einheit oder als Anzahl bestimmt wird. Der Divisor wird als Einheit und der Quotient als Anzahl bestimmt, wenn die Aufgabe der Division ausgesprochen wird, daß man sehen wolle, wie oft (Anzahl) eine Zahl (Einheit) in einer gegebenen enthalten sey; umgekehrt wird der Divisor als Anzahl und der Quotient als Einheit genommen, wenn gesagt wird, man soll eine Zahl in eine gegebene Anzahl gleicher Theile theilen und die Grösse solchen Theils (der Einheit) finden.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"61.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0024","text":"3. Die beiden Zahlen, welche als Einheit und Anzahl gegeneinander bestimmt sind, sind als Zahl noch unmittelbar gegeneinander, und daher überhaupt ungleich. Die weitere Gleichheit ist die der Einheit und der Anzahl selbst; so ist der Fortgang zur Gleichheit der Bestimmungen, die in der Bestimmung der Zahl liegen, vollendet. Das Zählen, nach dieser vollständigen Gleichheit ist das Potenziren, (die negative Rechnungsart das Wurzelausziehen)—und zwar zunächst das Erheben einer Zahl ins Quadrat,—das vollkommene Bestimmtseyn des Numerirens in sich selbst, wo 1) die vielen Zahlen, die addirt werden, dieselben sind, und 2) deren Vielheit oder Anzahl selbst dieselbe ist mit der Zahl, die vielmal gesetzt wird, die Einheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"61.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0025","text":"Es sind sonst keine Bestimmungen in dem Begriffe der Zahl, die einen Unterschied darbieten könnten; noch kann ein weiteres Ausgleichen des Unterschiedes, der in in der Zahl liegt, Statt finden. Erhebung in höhere Potenzen als in das Quadrat, ist eine formelle Fortsetzung Theils—bei den geraden Exponenten,—nur eine Wiederholung des Quadrirens, Theils bei den ungeraden Potenzen—tritt wieder die Ungleichheit ein; bei der nämlich formellen Gleichheit (z.B. zunächst beim Kubus) des neuen Faktors mit der Anzahl sowohl als mit der Einheit, ist er als Einheit, gegen die Anzahl (das Quadrat, 3 gegen 3.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"61.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0026","text":"3) ein Ungleiches; noch mehr beim Kubus von Vier, wo die Anzahl, 3, nach der die Zahl, die die Einheit ist, mit sich multiplicirt werden soll, von dieser selbst verschieden ist.—Es sind an sich diese Bestimmungen als der wesentliche Unterschied des Begriffs, die Anzahl und die Einheit, vorhanden, welche für das vollständige In-sich-Zurückgehen des Außer-sich-gehens auszugleichen sind. In dem so eben Dargestellten liegt weiter der Grund, warum Theils die Auflösung der höheren Gleichungen in der Zurückführung auf die quadratische bestehen muß, Theils warum die Gleichungen von ungeraden Exponenten sich nur formell bestimmen, und gerade wenn die Wurzeln rational sind, diese sich nicht anders als durch einen imaginären Ausdruck, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"61.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0027","text":"der das Gegentheil dessen ist, was die Wurzeln sind und ausdrücken, finden lassen.—Das Quadrat der Arithmetik enthält nach dem Angegebenen, allein das Schlechthin-Bestimmtseyn in sich; weswegen die Gleichungen mit weitern formellen Potenzen darauf zurückgeführt werden müssen, gerade wie das rechtwinklichte Dreieck in der Geometrie das Schlechthin-in-sich-Bestimmtseyn enthält, das im pythagoräischen Lehrsatz exponirt ist, weswegen auch darauf für die totale Bestimmung alle anderen geometrischen Figurationen reducirt werden müssen.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"61.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0028","text":"Ein nach einem logisch gebildetem Urtheile fortschreitender Unterricht handelt die Lehre von den Potenzen vor der Lehre über die Proportionen ab; diese schließen sich zwar an den Unterschied von Einheit und Anzahl an, der die Bestimmung der zweiten Rechnungsart ausmacht, aber sie treten aus dem Eins des unmittelbaren Quantums, in welchem Einheit und Anzahl nur Momente sind, heraus; die Fortbestimmung nach demselben bleibt ihm selbst auch noch äußerlich. Die Zahl im Verhältnisse ist nicht mehr als unmittelbares Quantum; es hat seine Bestimmtheit dann als Vermittelung; das quantitative Verhältniß wird im Nachfolgenden betrachtet.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"61.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0029","text":"Von der angegebenen Fortbestimmung der Rechnungsarten kann gesagt werden, daß sie keine Philosophie über dieselben, keine Darlegung etwa ihrer innern Bedeutung sey, weil sie in der That nicht eine immanente Entwickelung des Begriffes ist. Aber die Philosophie muß dieß zu unterscheiden wissen, was seiner Natur nach ein sich selbst äußerlicher Stoff ist, daß dann an einem solchen der Fortgang des Begriffs nur auf äußerliche Weise geschehen, und dessen Momente auch nur in der eigenthümlichen Form ihrer Äußerlichkeit, wie hier Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, seyn können. Die Unterscheidung der Sphären, in welche eine bestimmte Form des Begriffs gehört, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"61.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0030","text":"als Existenz vorhanden ist, ist ein wesentliches Erforderniß zum Philosophiren über reale Gegenstände, um nicht das Äußerliche und Zufällige durch Ideen in seiner Eigenthümlichkeit zu stören, wie diese Ideen durch die Unangemessenheit des Stoffes zu entstellen und formell zu machen. Jene Äußerlichkeit aber, in welcher die Begriffsmomente an jenem äußerlichen Stoffe, der Zahl, erscheinen, ist hier die angemessene Form; indem sie den Gegenstand in seinem Verstande darstellen, auch da sie keine spekulative Anforderung enthalten und daher leicht erscheinen, verdienen sie in den Lehrbüchern der Elemente angewendet zu werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"61.30"}],"sha256":"093738145a0ad4bf86163471e0e969f0e2501208fef9ae5b72a4420094f6d6dd","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102929472039Z_a4d97d65","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"093738145a0ad4bf86163471e0e969f0e2501208fef9ae5b72a4420094f6d6dd","sha256":"f094e0202a5ecf4f8b39c7074bb0d635885412bb542e70fd0fad011f0235af0f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:29:29.472072+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0001","text":"Spatial magnitude and numerical magnitude are customarily regarded as two kinds, such that spatial magnitude would be magnitude determined in itself just as much as numerical magnitude; their difference would consist only in the different determinations of continuity and discreteness; but as quantum they would stand at the same level. Geometry in general has continuous magnitude in spatial magnitude, and arithmetic discrete magnitude in numerical magnitude, as its object. But with this inequality of object they also do not have an equal mode and completeness of delimitation or of being-determined. Spatial magnitude has only delimitation in general; insofar as it is to be regarded as an absolutely determined quantum, it needs number. Geometry as such does not measure spatial figures, is not the art of measurement; rather, it only compares them.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"61.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0002","text":"Even in its definitions, the determinations are in part drawn from the equality of sides, angles, equal distance. Thus the circle, because it rests solely on the equality of the distance of all points possible in it from a centre, requires no number for its determination. These determinations resting on equality or inequality are genuinely geometrical. But they are not sufficient, and for others, e.g. triangle, quadrilateral, number is required, which in its principle, the one, being-determined-for-self, does not contain being-determined with the aid of another, and thus not by comparison.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"61.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0003","text":"Spatial magnitude does indeed have in the point the determinacy corresponding to the one; but the point, insofar as it comes outside itself, becomes an other, it becomes a line; because it is essentially only as one of space, it becomes, in the relation, a continuity in which pointuality, being-determined-for-self, the one, is sublated. Insofar as being-determined-for-self is to preserve itself in being-outside-itself, the line must be represented as a multitude of ones, and receive within itself the limit, the determination of the many ones, i.e. the magnitude of the line—likewise of the other spatial determinations—must be taken as number.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"61.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0004","text":"Arithmetic considers number and its figures, or rather does not consider them, but operates with them. For number is indifferent determinacy, inert; it must be activated and brought into relation from outside. The modes of relation are the operations of calculation. They are set forth one after another in arithmetic, and it becomes clear that one depends upon another. The thread guiding their progression, however, is not brought out in arithmetic.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"61.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0005","text":"But from the determination of the concept of number itself there readily results the systematic arrangement to which the exposition of these elements in textbooks has a justified claim. These guiding determinations are to be briefly indicated here.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"61.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0006","text":"On account of its principle, the one, number is an externally combined aggregate in general, an absolutely analytical figure, containing no inner connection. Because it is thus only something externally produced, all calculation is the production of numbers, a counting, or more determinately: counting-together. A difference in this external production, which always does only the same thing, can lie solely in a difference of the numbers in relation to one another which are to be counted together; such difference must itself be taken from elsewhere and from external determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"61.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0007","text":"The qualitative difference that constitutes the determinacy of number is that which we have seen, of unity and number; all determinacy of the concept that can occur in the operations of calculation is therefore reduced to this. But the difference belonging to numbers as quanta is external identity and external difference, equality and inequality, which are moments of reflection and are to be treated, among the determinations of essence, under difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"61.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0008","text":"Further, it must be prefaced that numbers in general can be produced in two ways, either by combining or by separating what has already been combined;—since both occur in a kind of counting determined in the same way, to a combining of numbers there corresponds what may be called a positive operation of calculation, to a separating what may be called a negative operation; the determination of the operation of calculation itself is independent of this opposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"61.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0009","text":"Following these remarks, there now ensues the account of the modes of calculation. The first production of number is the combining of many as such, i.e. each of them is posited only as one,—numeration. Since the ones are external to one another, they present themselves under a sensible image, and the operation by which number is produced is a counting-off on the fingers, on points, etc. What four, five, etc. are can only be shown. The breaking off at how much is to be combined is, since the limit is external, something contingent, arbitrary.—The difference of number and unity, which enters in the progression of the operations of calculation, grounds a system—dyadic, decimal, etc.—of numbers; such a system rests as a whole on the arbitrariness of which number is to be taken again constantly as unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"61.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0010","text":"The numbers that have arisen through numeration are numerated again; and since they are thus immediately posited, they are still determined without any relation at all to one another, indifferent to equality and inequality, of contingent magnitude in relation to one another,—therefore unequal in general;—addition.—That 7 and 5 make twelve is learned by numerating a further 5 ones, on the fingers or otherwise, to the 7,—the result of which is afterward retained in memory, by heart; for there is nothing inner involved in it. Likewise, that 7 x 5 = 35 is known by counting off on the fingers, etc., by numerating one further to a seven, accomplishing this five times, and likewise retaining the result by heart. The trouble of this numeration, of discovering the sums, products, is disposed of through the ready-made one and one or one times one, which one need only learn by heart.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"61.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0011","text":"Kant has (in the Introduction to the Critique of Pure Reason V.) regarded the proposition: 7 + 5 = 12, as a synthetic proposition. “One should,” he says, “at first indeed think, (certainly!) that it is a merely analytical proposition, following from the concept of a sum of seven and five according to the principle of contradiction.” The concept of sum means nothing further than the abstract determination that these two numbers are to be combined, and indeed as numbers in an external, i.e. conceptless manner,—that one is to continue numerating from seven until the ones to be added, whose number is determined as five, have been exhausted; the result bears the otherwise familiar name twelve.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"61.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0012","text":"“But,” Kant continues, “if one considers it more closely, one finds that the concept of the sum of 7 + 5 contains nothing further than the union of both numbers into a single one, by which it is not at all thought what this single number is that combines both;”—“however much I may analyse my concept of such a possible sum, I shall nevertheless not encounter twelve in it.” Thinking the sum, analysis of the concept, indeed has nothing to do with the transition from that problem to the result; “one must go beyond these concepts and take intuition, five fingers, etc., to one’s aid, and thus add the units of the five given in intuition to the concept of seven,” he adds. Five is indeed given in intuition, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"61.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0013","text":"a wholly external being-put-together of the arbitrarily repeated thought, one; but seven is just as little a concept; there are no concepts present beyond which one goes. The sum of 5 and 7 means the conceptless connection of both numbers; the numeration, thus continued conceptlessly from seven until the five is exhausted, can be called a putting-together, a synthesizing, just like numeration from one onward—a synthesizing which, however, is of a wholly analytical nature, inasmuch as the connection is wholly made, and there is nothing in it or entering into it that is not wholly externally at hand. The postulate to add 5 to 7 relates to the postulate to numerate in general as the postulate to extend a straight line relates to that of drawing a straight line.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"61.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0014","text":"As empty as the expression synthesizing is the determination that it occurs a priori. Counting is indeed no determination of sensation, which alone remains for the a posteriori according to the Kantian determination of intuition, and counting is indeed an activity on the ground of abstract intuition, i.e. one determined by the category of the one and in which abstraction is made from all other determinations of sensation, just as much as from concepts. The a priori is in general only something vague; the determination of feeling, as drive, sense, etc., has the moment of apriority within it just as much as space and time, as existing, temporal and spatial, are determined a posteriori.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"61.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0015","text":"In connection with this it may be added that Kant’s assertion of the synthetic character of the principles of pure geometry likewise contains nothing fundamental. While he indicates that several are really analytical, only the principle that the straight line between two points is the shortest is adduced for that view. “My concept of the straight, namely, contains nothing of magnitude, but only a quality; the concept of the shortest thus comes wholly in addition, and can be drawn from no analysis out of the concept of the straight line; intuition must therefore be taken to aid here, through which alone synthesis is possible.”—But here too the issue is not a concept of the straight in general, but of a straight line, and this is already something spatial, intuited.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"61.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0016","text":"The determination (or, if one will, the concept) of the straight line is surely no other than that it is the absolutely simple line, i.e. in coming-outside-itself (the so-called movement of the point) it relates absolutely to itself, in whose extension no kind of difference of determination, no relation to another point or line outside it, is posited or maintained;—the direction absolutely simple within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"61.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0017","text":"This simplicity is indeed its quality, and if the straight line should seem difficult to define analytically, this would be only on account of the determination of simplicity or relation to itself, and merely because reflection in determining has initially and pre-eminently a plurality, a determining through others, before it; but it is in itself absolutely not difficult to grasp this determination of the simplicity of extension within itself, of its being undetermined through others;—Euclid’s definition contains nothing other than this simplicity.—But the transition of this quality to the quantitative determination (of the shortest), which was supposed to constitute the synthetic, is wholly only analytical. The line is, as spatial, quantity in general; the simplest, said of quantum, is the least, and this, said of a line, is the shortest.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"61.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0018","text":"Geometry can admit these determinations as a corollary to the definition; but Archimedes, in his books on sphere and cylinder (see Hauber’s trans., p. ), did most suitably in setting down that determination of the straight line as a principle, in as correct a sense as Euclid set the determination concerning parallel lines among the principles, since the development of this determination, in order to become a definition, would likewise have required more abstract qualitative determinations not belonging immediately to spatiality, such as, above, simplicity, equality of direction, and the like. These ancients also gave their sciences a plastic character, kept their presentation strictly within the peculiarity of their material, and therefore excluded what would have been of a heterogeneous kind for it.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"61.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0019","text":"The concept that Kant set forth in synthetic judgments a priori,—the concept of what is different, which is equally inseparable, of an identical which in itself is undivided difference, belongs to what is great and immortal in his philosophy.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"61.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0020","text":"In intuition this concept, since it is the concept itself and everything in itself is concept, is of course likewise present; but the determinations extracted in those examples do not present it; rather, number and counting are an identity and production of an identity which is absolutely only external, only superficial synthesis, a unity of ones, such as are rather posited as not identical with one another in themselves, but external, separately for themselves; in the straight line, the determination of being the smallest between two points has rather only the moment of the abstractly identical, without difference in itself, as its basis.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"61.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0021","text":"I return from this interruption to addition itself. The corresponding negative operation of calculation, subtraction, is the likewise wholly analytical separating into numbers which, as in addition, are determined in relation to one another only as unequal in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"61.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0022","text":"2. The next determination is the equality of the numbers that are to be enumerated. Through this equality they are a unity, and thus the distinction between unit and amount enters into number. Multiplication is the task of adding together an amount of units which are themselves an amount. In this it is immaterial which of the two numbers is specified as unit and which as amount, whether one says four times three, where four is the amount and three the unit, or conversely three times four.—It has already been stated above that the original finding of the product is accomplished through simple enumeration, i.e. counting on the fingers, etc.; the subsequent ability to state the product immediately rests upon the collection of those products, the multiplication table, and knowledge of it by heart.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"61.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0023","text":"Division is the negative mode of calculation according to the same determination of distinction. It is equally immaterial which of the two factors, the divisor or the quotient, is determined as unit or as amount. The divisor is determined as unit and the quotient as amount when the task of division is expressed by saying that one wishes to see how often (amount) a number (unit) is contained in a given one; conversely, the divisor is taken as amount and the quotient as unit when it is said that one is to divide a number into a given amount of equal parts and find the magnitude of such a part (the unit).","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"61.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0024","text":"3. The two numbers which are determined in relation to one another as unit and amount are, as number, still immediate in relation to one another, and hence in general unequal. The further equality is that of the unit and the amount themselves; thus the progression to the equality of the determinations that lie in the determination of number is completed. Counting, according to this complete equality, is exponentiation (the negative mode of calculation being extraction of roots)—and initially the raising of a number to the square,—the complete determinacy of enumeration within itself, where 1) the many numbers that are added are the same, and 2) their multiplicity or amount itself is the same as the number that is posited many times, is the unit.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"61.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0025","text":"There are otherwise no determinations in the concept of number that could present a distinction; nor can any further equalization of the distinction that lies in number take place. Raising to higher powers than the square is a formal continuation, partly—in the case of even exponents—only a repetition of squaring, partly—in the case of odd powers—inequality enters again; namely, with the formal equality (e.g. initially in the cube) of the new factor with both the amount and the unit, it is, as unit, unequal to the amount (the square, 3 against 3.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"61.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0026","text":"3); still more so in the cube of four, where the amount, 3, according to which the number that is the unit is to be multiplied by itself, is different from this number itself.—These determinations, amount and unit, are in themselves present as the essential distinction of the concept, which are to be equalized for the complete return-into-itself of the going-outside-itself. In what has just been set forth there further lies the ground why, partly, the solution of higher equations must consist in reduction to the quadratic equation, and partly why equations of odd exponents can be determined only formally, and, precisely when the roots are rational, these can be found only through an imaginary expression, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"61.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0027","text":"one that is the opposite of what the roots are and express.—According to what has been stated, the square of arithmetic alone contains determinate-being absolutely within itself; for which reason equations with further formal powers must be reduced to it, just as the right-angled triangle in geometry contains the absolute being-determined-within-itself that is expounded in the Pythagorean theorem, and for which reason all other geometrical configurations must likewise be reduced to it for total determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"61.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0028","text":"Instruction proceeding according to a logically formed judgment treats the doctrine of powers before the doctrine of proportions; the latter do indeed connect with the distinction between unit and amount that constitutes the determination of the second mode of calculation, but they emerge from the one of immediate quantum, in which unit and amount are only moments; further determination in accordance with it also remains external to it. Number in ratio is no longer immediate quantum; it then has its determinacy as mediation; quantitative ratio is considered in what follows.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"61.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0029","text":"Of the indicated further determination of the modes of calculation it may be said that it is no philosophy of them, no exposition, perhaps, of their inner significance, because it is in fact not an immanent development of the concept. But philosophy must know how to distinguish this: that which by its nature is a material external to itself, so that in such a material the progression of the concept can occur only in an external manner, and its moments too can exist only in the peculiar form of their externality, as here equality and inequality. The distinction of the spheres in which a determinate form of the concept belongs, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"61.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_14:P0030","text":"is present as existence, is an essential requirement for philosophizing about real objects, so as not to disturb what is external and contingent in its peculiarity by means of Ideas, just as these Ideas are distorted and rendered formal through the inappropriateness of the material. Yet that externality in which the moments of the concept appear in that external material, number, is here the appropriate form; since they present the object in its understanding, even where they contain no speculative requirement and therefore appear easy, they deserve to be employed in textbooks of the elements.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"61.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_14:P0030"]}],"source_digest":"be93fe40ead926336f835fd2b8403f6e5c8c7a1b87490c4850d0e69469ed04f9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15","title":"Remark 2.","order":62,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_15","text":"Bekanntlich hat Pythagoras Vernunftverhältnisse oder Philosopheme in Zahlen dargestellt, auch in neueren Zeiten ist von ihnen und Formen ihrer Beziehungen, wie Potenzen u.s.f. in der Philosophie Gebrauch gemacht worden, um die Gedanken darnach zu reguliren oder damit auszudrücken.—In pädagogischer Rücksicht ist die Zahl für den geeignetsten Gegenstand des innern Anschauens, und die rechnende Beschäftigung mit Verhältnissen derselben für die Thätigkeit des Geistes gehalten worden, worin er seine eigensten Verhältnisse und überhaupt die Grundverhältnisse des Wesens zur Anschauung bringe. —Wiefern der Zahl dieser hohe Werth beikommen könne, geht aus ihrem Begriffe hervor, wie er sich ergeben hat.\n\nDie Zahl sahen wir als die absolute Bestimmtheit der Quantität, und ihr Element als den gleichgültig gewordenen Unterschied;—die Bestimmtheit an sich, die zugleich völlig nur äußerlich gesetzt ist. Die Arithmetik ist analytische Wissenschaft, weil alle Verknüpfungen und Unterschiede, die an ihrem Gegenstande vorkommen, nicht in ihm selbst liegen, sondern ihm völlig äußerlich angethan sind. Sie hat keinen konkreten Gegenstand, welcher innere Verhältnisse an sich hätte, die zunächst für das Wissen verborgen, nicht in der unmittelbaren Vorstellung von ihm gegeben, sondern erst durch die Bemühung des Erkennens herauszubringen wären. Sie enthält nicht nur den Begriff und damit die Aufgabe für das begreifende Denken nicht, sondern ist das Gegentheil desselben. Um der Gleichgültigkeit des Verknüpften gegen die Verknüpfung, der die Nothwendigkeit fehlt, willen, befindet sich das Denken hier in einer Thätigkeit, die zugleich die äußerste Entäußerung seiner selbst ist, in der gewaltsamen Thätigkeit, sich in der Gedankenlosigkeit zu bewegen und das keiner Nothwendigkeit Fähige zu verknüpfen. Der Gegenstand ist der abstrakte Gedanke der Äußerlichkeit selbst.\n\nAls dieser Gedanke der Äußerlichkeit ist die Zahl zugleich die Abstraktion von der sinnlichen Mannigfaltigkeit; sie hat von dem Sinnlichen nichts als die abstrakte Bestimmung der Äußerlichkeit selbst behalten; hierdurch ist dieses in ihr dem Gedanken am nächsten gebracht; sie ist der reine Gedanke der eignen Entäußerung des Gedankens.\n\nDer Geist, der sich über die sinnliche Welt erhebt, und sein Wesen erkennt, indem er ein Element für seine reine Vorstellung, für den Ausdruck seines Wesens sucht, kann daher, ehe er den Gedanken selbst als dieß Element faßt, und für dessen Darstellung den rein geistigen Ausdruck gewinnt, darauf verfallen, die Zahl, diese innerliche, abstrakte Äußerlichkeit zu wählen. Darum sehen wir in der Geschichte der Wissenschaft früh die Zahl zum Ausdruck von Philosophemen gebraucht werden. Sie macht die letzte Stufe der Unvollkommenheit aus, das Allgemeine mit Sinnlichem behaftet zu fassen. Die Alten haben das bestimmte Bewußtseyn darüber gehabt, daß die Zahl zwischen dem Sinnlichen und dem Gedanken in der Mitte stehe. Aristoteles führt es von Plato an (Metaphys. I,5) daß derselbe sage, daß außer dem Sinnlichen und den Ideen die mathematischen Bestimmungen der Dinge dazwischen stehen, von dem Sinnlichen dadurch unterschieden sey, daß sie unsichtbar (ewig) und unbewegt seyen, von den Ideen aber, daß sie ein Vieles und ein Ähnliches seyen, die Idee aber schlechthin nur identisch mit sich und in sich Eines sey.—Eine ausführlichere gründlich gedachte Reflexion hierüber von Moderatus aus Cadix wird in Malchi Vita Pythagorae ed. Ritterhus. p. 30f. angeführt; daß die Pythagoräer auf die Zahlen gefallen seyen, schreibt er dem zu, daß sie noch nicht vermocht haben, die Grundideen und ersten Principien deutlich in der Vernunft zu fassen, weil diese Principien schwer zu denken und schwer auszusprechen seyen; die Zahlen dienen zur Bezeichnung gut beim Unterrichte; sie haben darin unter anderem die Geometer nachgeahmt, welche das Körperliche nicht in Gedanken ausdrücken können, die Figuren gebrauchen, und sagen, dieß sey ein Dreieck, wobei sie aber wollen, daß nicht die in die Augen fallende Zeichnung für das Dreieck genommen, sondern damit nur der Gedanke desselben vorgestellt sey. So haben die Pythagoräer den Gedanken der Einheit, der Dieselbigkeit und Gleichheit und den Grund der Übereinstimmung, des Zusammenhangs und der Erhaltung von Allem, des mit sich selbst Identischen, als Eins ausgesprochen u.s.f.—Es ist überflüssig zu bemerken, daß die Pythagoräer von dem Zahlenauch zum Gedanken-Ausdruck, zu den ausdrücklichen Kategorien des Gleichen und Ungleichen, der Grenze und der Unendlichkeit übergegangen sind, es wird schon in Ansehung jener Zahlausdrücke (ebend. in den Anm. zu p. 31 l.s. aus einem Leben des Pythagoras bei Photius p. 772) angeführt, daß die Pythagoräer zwischen der Monas und dem Eins unterschieden haben; die Monas haben sie als den Gedanken genommen, das Eins aber als die Zahl; ebenso die Zwei für das Arithmetische, die Dyas (denn so soll es daselbst wohl heißen) für den Gedanken des Unbestimmten. —Diese Alten sahen vors Erste das Ungenügende der Zahlformen für Gedankenbestimmungen sehr richtig ein, und ebenso richtig forderten sie ferner stattjenes ersten Nothbehelfs für Gedanken den eigenthümlichen Ausdruck; um wie viel weiter waren sie in ihrem Nachdenken gekommen, als die, welche heutigestages wieder Zahlen selbst und Zahlbestimmungen, wie Potenzen, dann das Unendlichgroße, Unendlichkleine, Eins dividirt durch das Unendliche und sonstige solche Bestimmungen, die selbst auch oft ein verkehrter mathematischer Formalismus sind, an die Stelle von Gedankenbestimmungen zu setzen und zu jener unvermögenden Kindheit zurückzukehren, für etwas Löbliches, ja Gründliches und Tiefes halten.\n\nWenn vorhin der Ausdruck angeführt worden, daß die Zahl zwischen dem Sinnlichen und dem Gedanken stehe, indem sie zugleich von jenem dieß habe, das Viele, das Außereinander, an ihr zu seyn, so ist zu bemerken, daß dieses Viele selbst, das in den Gedanken aufgenommene Sinnliche, die ihm angehörige Kategorie des an ihm selbst Äußerlichen ist. Die weiteren, konkreten, wahren Gedanken, das Lebendigste, Beweglichste, nur im Beziehen Begriffene, in dieses Element des Außersichseyns selbst versetzt, werden zu todten, bewegungslosen Bestimmungen. Je reicher an Bestimmtheit und damit an Beziehung die Gedanken werden, desto verworrener einer Seits und desto willkürlicher und sinnleerer anderer Seits wird ihre Darstellung in solchen Formen, als die Zahlen sind. Das Eins, das Zwei, das Drei, das Vier, Henas oder Monas, Dyas, Trias, Tetraktys, liegen noch den ganz einfachen abstrakten Begriffen nahe; aber wenn Zahlen zu konkreten Verhältnissen übergehen sollen, so ist es vergeblich, sie noch dem Begriffe nahe erhalten zu wollen,\n\nWenn nun aber die Denkbestimmungen durch Eins, Zwei, Drei, Vier für die Bewegung des Begriffs, als durch welche er allein Begriff ist, bezeichnet werden, so ist dieß das Härteste, was dem Denken zugemuthet wird. Es bewegt sich im Elemente seines Gegentheils, der Beziehungslosigkeit; sein Geschäfte ist die Arbeit der Verrücktheit. Daß z.B. Eins Drei, und Drei Eins ist, zu begreifen, ist darum diese harte Zumuthung, weil das Eins das Beziehungslose ist, also nicht an ihm selbst die Bestimmung zeigt, wodurch es in sein Entgegengesetztes übergeht, sondern vielmehr dieß ist, eine solche Beziehung schlechthin auszuschließen und zu verweigern. Umgekehrt benutzt dieß der Verstand gegen die spekulative Wahrheit (wie z.B. gegen die in der Lehre, welche die der Dreieinigkeit genannt wird, niedergelegte) und zählt die Bestimmungen derselben, welche Eine Einheit ausmachen, um sie als klaren Widersinn aufzuzeigen,—d. h. er selbst begeht den Widersinn, das, was schlechthin Beziehung ist, zum Beziehungslosen zu machen. Bei dem Namen Dreieinigkeit ist freilich nicht darauf gerechnet worden, daß vom Verstand das Eins und die Zahl als die wesentliche Bestimmtheit des Inhalts betrachtet werden würde. Jener Name drückt die Verachtung gegen den Verstand aus, der aber seine Eitelkeit, am Eins und der Zahl als solcher zu halten, festgestellt und sie gegen die Vernunft gestellt hat.\n\nZahlen, geometrische Figuren, wie dieß viel vom Kreis, Dreieck u.s.f. geschen ist, als bloße Symbole (des Kreises, z.B. von der Ewigkeit, des Dreiecks von der Dreieinigkeit) zu nehmen ist—einer Seits etwas Unverfängliches; aber thöricht ist es anderer Seits, zu meinen, daß dadurch mehr ausgedrückt sey, als der Gedanke zu fassen und auszudrücken vermöge. Wenn in solchen Symbolen, wie in andern, die von der Phantasie in den Mythologien der Völker und in der Dichtkunst überhaupt erzeugt werden, gegen welche die phantasielosen geometrischen Figuren ohnehin dürftig sind, wie auch in diesen eine tiefe Weisheit, tiefe Bedeutung liegen soll, so ist es eben dem Denken allein darum zu thun, die Weisheit, die nur darin liegt, und nicht nur in Symbolen, sondern in der Natur und im Geiste, heraus zu Tage zu fördern; in Symbolen ist die Wahrheit durch das sinnliche Element noch getrübt und verhüllt; ganz offenbar wird sie allein dem Bewußtseyn in der Form des Gedanken; die Bedeutung ist nur der Gedanke selbst.\n\nAber mathematische Kategorien herbeizunehmen, um daraus für die Methode oder den Inhalt philosophischer Wissenschaft etwas bestimmen zu wollen, zeigt sich wesentlich dadurch als etwas Verkehrtes, daß insofern mathematische Formeln Gedanken und Begriffsunterschiede bedeuten, diese ihre Bedeutung sich vielmehr zuerst in der Philosophie anzugeben, zu bestimmen und zu rechtfertigen hat. In ihren konkreten Wissenschaften hat diese das Logische aus der Logik, nicht aus der Mathematik zu nehmen; es kann nur ein Nothbehelf der philosophischen Unvermögenheit seyn, zu den Gestaltungen, die das Logische in anderen Wissenschaften annimmt, und deren viele nur Ahnungen, andere auch Verkümmerungen desselben sind, für das Logische der Philosophie seine Zuflucht zu nehmen. Die bloße Anwendung solcher entlehnten Formeln ist ohnehin ein äußerliches Verhalten; der Anwendung selbst müßte ein Bewußtseyn über ihren Werth wie über ihre Bedeutung vorangehen; ein solches Bewußtseyn aber giebt nur die denkende Betrachtung, nicht die Autorität derselben aus der Mathematik. Solches Bewußtseyn über sie ist die Logik selbst, und dieß Bewußtseyn streift ihre partikulare Form ab, macht diese überflüssig und unnütz, berichtigt sie und verschafft ihnen allein ihre Berechtigung, Sinn und Werth.\n\nWas es mit dem Gebrauche der Zahl und des Rechnens auf sich hat, insofern er eine pädagogische Hauptgrundlage ausmachen soll, geht aus dem Bisherigen von selbst hervor. Die Zahl ist ein unsinnlicher Gegenstand, und die Beschäftigung mit ihr und ihren Verbindungen, ein unsinnliches Geschäft; der Geist wird somit dadurch zur Reflexion in sich und einer innerlichen abstrakten Arbeit angehalten, was eine große, jedoch einseitige Wichtigkeit hat. Denn auf der anderen Seite, da der Zahl nur der äußerliche, gedankenlose Unterschied zu Grunde liegt, wird jenes Geschäfte ein gedankenloses, mechanisches. Die Kraftanstrengung besteht vornehmlich darin, Begriffloses festzuhalten, und begrifflos es zu verbinden. Der Inhalt ist das leere Eins; der gediegene Gehalt des sittlichen und geistigen Lebens und der individuellen Gestaltungen desselben, mit welchem als der edelsten Nahrung die Erziehung den jugendlichen Geist großziehen soll, sollte von dem inhaltslosen Eins verdrängt werden; die Wirkung, wenn jene Übungen zur Hauptsache und Hauptbeschäftigung gemacht werden, kann keine andere seyn, als den Geist nach Form und Inhalt auszuhöhlen und abzustumpfen. Weil das Rechnen ein so sehr äußerliches, somit mechanisches Geschäft ist, haben sich Maschinen verfertigen lassen, welche die arithmetischen Operationen aufs vollkommenste vollführen. Wenn man über die Natur des Rechnens nur diesen Umstand allein kennte, so läge darin die Entscheidung, was es mit dem Einfalle für eine Bewandniß hatte, das Rechnen zum Hauptbildungsmittel des Geistes zu machen, und ihn auf die Folter, sich zur Maschine zu vervollkommnen, zu legen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0001","text":"Bekanntlich hat Pythagoras Vernunftverhältnisse oder Philosopheme in Zahlen dargestellt, auch in neueren Zeiten ist von ihnen und Formen ihrer Beziehungen, wie Potenzen u.s.f. in der Philosophie Gebrauch gemacht worden, um die Gedanken darnach zu reguliren oder damit auszudrücken.—In pädagogischer Rücksicht ist die Zahl für den geeignetsten Gegenstand des innern Anschauens, und die rechnende Beschäftigung mit Verhältnissen derselben für die Thätigkeit des Geistes gehalten worden, worin er seine eigensten Verhältnisse und überhaupt die Grundverhältnisse des Wesens zur Anschauung bringe. —Wiefern der Zahl dieser hohe Werth beikommen könne, geht aus ihrem Begriffe hervor, wie er sich ergeben hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"62.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0002","text":"Die Zahl sahen wir als die absolute Bestimmtheit der Quantität, und ihr Element als den gleichgültig gewordenen Unterschied;—die Bestimmtheit an sich, die zugleich völlig nur äußerlich gesetzt ist. Die Arithmetik ist analytische Wissenschaft, weil alle Verknüpfungen und Unterschiede, die an ihrem Gegenstande vorkommen, nicht in ihm selbst liegen, sondern ihm völlig äußerlich angethan sind. Sie hat keinen konkreten Gegenstand, welcher innere Verhältnisse an sich hätte, die zunächst für das Wissen verborgen, nicht in der unmittelbaren Vorstellung von ihm gegeben, sondern erst durch die Bemühung des Erkennens herauszubringen wären. Sie enthält nicht nur den Begriff und damit die Aufgabe für das begreifende Denken nicht, sondern ist das Gegentheil desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"62.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0003","text":"Um der Gleichgültigkeit des Verknüpften gegen die Verknüpfung, der die Nothwendigkeit fehlt, willen, befindet sich das Denken hier in einer Thätigkeit, die zugleich die äußerste Entäußerung seiner selbst ist, in der gewaltsamen Thätigkeit, sich in der Gedankenlosigkeit zu bewegen und das keiner Nothwendigkeit Fähige zu verknüpfen. Der Gegenstand ist der abstrakte Gedanke der Äußerlichkeit selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"62.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0004","text":"Als dieser Gedanke der Äußerlichkeit ist die Zahl zugleich die Abstraktion von der sinnlichen Mannigfaltigkeit; sie hat von dem Sinnlichen nichts als die abstrakte Bestimmung der Äußerlichkeit selbst behalten; hierdurch ist dieses in ihr dem Gedanken am nächsten gebracht; sie ist der reine Gedanke der eignen Entäußerung des Gedankens.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"62.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0005","text":"Der Geist, der sich über die sinnliche Welt erhebt, und sein Wesen erkennt, indem er ein Element für seine reine Vorstellung, für den Ausdruck seines Wesens sucht, kann daher, ehe er den Gedanken selbst als dieß Element faßt, und für dessen Darstellung den rein geistigen Ausdruck gewinnt, darauf verfallen, die Zahl, diese innerliche, abstrakte Äußerlichkeit zu wählen. Darum sehen wir in der Geschichte der Wissenschaft früh die Zahl zum Ausdruck von Philosophemen gebraucht werden. Sie macht die letzte Stufe der Unvollkommenheit aus, das Allgemeine mit Sinnlichem behaftet zu fassen. Die Alten haben das bestimmte Bewußtseyn darüber gehabt, daß die Zahl zwischen dem Sinnlichen und dem Gedanken in der Mitte stehe. Aristoteles führt es von Plato an (Metaphys.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"62.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0006","text":"I,5) daß derselbe sage, daß außer dem Sinnlichen und den Ideen die mathematischen Bestimmungen der Dinge dazwischen stehen, von dem Sinnlichen dadurch unterschieden sey, daß sie unsichtbar (ewig) und unbewegt seyen, von den Ideen aber, daß sie ein Vieles und ein Ähnliches seyen, die Idee aber schlechthin nur identisch mit sich und in sich Eines sey.—Eine ausführlichere gründlich gedachte Reflexion hierüber von Moderatus aus Cadix wird in Malchi Vita Pythagorae ed. Ritterhus. p. 30f.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"62.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0007","text":"angeführt; daß die Pythagoräer auf die Zahlen gefallen seyen, schreibt er dem zu, daß sie noch nicht vermocht haben, die Grundideen und ersten Principien deutlich in der Vernunft zu fassen, weil diese Principien schwer zu denken und schwer auszusprechen seyen; die Zahlen dienen zur Bezeichnung gut beim Unterrichte; sie haben darin unter anderem die Geometer nachgeahmt, welche das Körperliche nicht in Gedanken ausdrücken können, die Figuren gebrauchen, und sagen, dieß sey ein Dreieck, wobei sie aber wollen, daß nicht die in die Augen fallende Zeichnung für das Dreieck genommen, sondern damit nur der Gedanke desselben vorgestellt sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"62.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0008","text":"So haben die Pythagoräer den Gedanken der Einheit, der Dieselbigkeit und Gleichheit und den Grund der Übereinstimmung, des Zusammenhangs und der Erhaltung von Allem, des mit sich selbst Identischen, als Eins ausgesprochen u.s.f.—Es ist überflüssig zu bemerken, daß die Pythagoräer von dem Zahlenauch zum Gedanken-Ausdruck, zu den ausdrücklichen Kategorien des Gleichen und Ungleichen, der Grenze und der Unendlichkeit übergegangen sind, es wird schon in Ansehung jener Zahlausdrücke (ebend. in den Anm. zu p. 31 l.s. aus einem Leben des Pythagoras bei Photius p. 772) angeführt, daß die Pythagoräer zwischen der Monas und dem Eins unterschieden haben; die Monas haben sie als den Gedanken genommen, das Eins aber als die Zahl; ebenso die Zwei für das Arithmetische, die Dyas (denn so soll es daselbst wohl heißen) für den Gedanken des Unbestimmten.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"62.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0009","text":"—Diese Alten sahen vors Erste das Ungenügende der Zahlformen für Gedankenbestimmungen sehr richtig ein, und ebenso richtig forderten sie ferner stattjenes ersten Nothbehelfs für Gedanken den eigenthümlichen Ausdruck; um wie viel weiter waren sie in ihrem Nachdenken gekommen, als die, welche heutigestages wieder Zahlen selbst und Zahlbestimmungen, wie Potenzen, dann das Unendlichgroße, Unendlichkleine, Eins dividirt durch das Unendliche und sonstige solche Bestimmungen, die selbst auch oft ein verkehrter mathematischer Formalismus sind, an die Stelle von Gedankenbestimmungen zu setzen und zu jener unvermögenden Kindheit zurückzukehren, für etwas Löbliches, ja Gründliches und Tiefes halten.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"62.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0010","text":"Wenn vorhin der Ausdruck angeführt worden, daß die Zahl zwischen dem Sinnlichen und dem Gedanken stehe, indem sie zugleich von jenem dieß habe, das Viele, das Außereinander, an ihr zu seyn, so ist zu bemerken, daß dieses Viele selbst, das in den Gedanken aufgenommene Sinnliche, die ihm angehörige Kategorie des an ihm selbst Äußerlichen ist. Die weiteren, konkreten, wahren Gedanken, das Lebendigste, Beweglichste, nur im Beziehen Begriffene, in dieses Element des Außersichseyns selbst versetzt, werden zu todten, bewegungslosen Bestimmungen. Je reicher an Bestimmtheit und damit an Beziehung die Gedanken werden, desto verworrener einer Seits und desto willkürlicher und sinnleerer anderer Seits wird ihre Darstellung in solchen Formen, als die Zahlen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"62.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0011","text":"Das Eins, das Zwei, das Drei, das Vier, Henas oder Monas, Dyas, Trias, Tetraktys, liegen noch den ganz einfachen abstrakten Begriffen nahe; aber wenn Zahlen zu konkreten Verhältnissen übergehen sollen, so ist es vergeblich, sie noch dem Begriffe nahe erhalten zu wollen,","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"62.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0012","text":"Wenn nun aber die Denkbestimmungen durch Eins, Zwei, Drei, Vier für die Bewegung des Begriffs, als durch welche er allein Begriff ist, bezeichnet werden, so ist dieß das Härteste, was dem Denken zugemuthet wird. Es bewegt sich im Elemente seines Gegentheils, der Beziehungslosigkeit; sein Geschäfte ist die Arbeit der Verrücktheit. Daß z.B. Eins Drei, und Drei Eins ist, zu begreifen, ist darum diese harte Zumuthung, weil das Eins das Beziehungslose ist, also nicht an ihm selbst die Bestimmung zeigt, wodurch es in sein Entgegengesetztes übergeht, sondern vielmehr dieß ist, eine solche Beziehung schlechthin auszuschließen und zu verweigern. Umgekehrt benutzt dieß der Verstand gegen die spekulative Wahrheit (wie z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"62.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0013","text":"gegen die in der Lehre, welche die der Dreieinigkeit genannt wird, niedergelegte) und zählt die Bestimmungen derselben, welche Eine Einheit ausmachen, um sie als klaren Widersinn aufzuzeigen,—d. h. er selbst begeht den Widersinn, das, was schlechthin Beziehung ist, zum Beziehungslosen zu machen. Bei dem Namen Dreieinigkeit ist freilich nicht darauf gerechnet worden, daß vom Verstand das Eins und die Zahl als die wesentliche Bestimmtheit des Inhalts betrachtet werden würde. Jener Name drückt die Verachtung gegen den Verstand aus, der aber seine Eitelkeit, am Eins und der Zahl als solcher zu halten, festgestellt und sie gegen die Vernunft gestellt hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"62.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0014","text":"Zahlen, geometrische Figuren, wie dieß viel vom Kreis, Dreieck u.s.f. geschen ist, als bloße Symbole (des Kreises, z.B. von der Ewigkeit, des Dreiecks von der Dreieinigkeit) zu nehmen ist—einer Seits etwas Unverfängliches; aber thöricht ist es anderer Seits, zu meinen, daß dadurch mehr ausgedrückt sey, als der Gedanke zu fassen und auszudrücken vermöge.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"62.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0015","text":"Wenn in solchen Symbolen, wie in andern, die von der Phantasie in den Mythologien der Völker und in der Dichtkunst überhaupt erzeugt werden, gegen welche die phantasielosen geometrischen Figuren ohnehin dürftig sind, wie auch in diesen eine tiefe Weisheit, tiefe Bedeutung liegen soll, so ist es eben dem Denken allein darum zu thun, die Weisheit, die nur darin liegt, und nicht nur in Symbolen, sondern in der Natur und im Geiste, heraus zu Tage zu fördern; in Symbolen ist die Wahrheit durch das sinnliche Element noch getrübt und verhüllt; ganz offenbar wird sie allein dem Bewußtseyn in der Form des Gedanken; die Bedeutung ist nur der Gedanke selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"62.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0016","text":"Aber mathematische Kategorien herbeizunehmen, um daraus für die Methode oder den Inhalt philosophischer Wissenschaft etwas bestimmen zu wollen, zeigt sich wesentlich dadurch als etwas Verkehrtes, daß insofern mathematische Formeln Gedanken und Begriffsunterschiede bedeuten, diese ihre Bedeutung sich vielmehr zuerst in der Philosophie anzugeben, zu bestimmen und zu rechtfertigen hat. In ihren konkreten Wissenschaften hat diese das Logische aus der Logik, nicht aus der Mathematik zu nehmen; es kann nur ein Nothbehelf der philosophischen Unvermögenheit seyn, zu den Gestaltungen, die das Logische in anderen Wissenschaften annimmt, und deren viele nur Ahnungen, andere auch Verkümmerungen desselben sind, für das Logische der Philosophie seine Zuflucht zu nehmen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"62.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0017","text":"Die bloße Anwendung solcher entlehnten Formeln ist ohnehin ein äußerliches Verhalten; der Anwendung selbst müßte ein Bewußtseyn über ihren Werth wie über ihre Bedeutung vorangehen; ein solches Bewußtseyn aber giebt nur die denkende Betrachtung, nicht die Autorität derselben aus der Mathematik. Solches Bewußtseyn über sie ist die Logik selbst, und dieß Bewußtseyn streift ihre partikulare Form ab, macht diese überflüssig und unnütz, berichtigt sie und verschafft ihnen allein ihre Berechtigung, Sinn und Werth.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"62.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0018","text":"Was es mit dem Gebrauche der Zahl und des Rechnens auf sich hat, insofern er eine pädagogische Hauptgrundlage ausmachen soll, geht aus dem Bisherigen von selbst hervor. Die Zahl ist ein unsinnlicher Gegenstand, und die Beschäftigung mit ihr und ihren Verbindungen, ein unsinnliches Geschäft; der Geist wird somit dadurch zur Reflexion in sich und einer innerlichen abstrakten Arbeit angehalten, was eine große, jedoch einseitige Wichtigkeit hat. Denn auf der anderen Seite, da der Zahl nur der äußerliche, gedankenlose Unterschied zu Grunde liegt, wird jenes Geschäfte ein gedankenloses, mechanisches. Die Kraftanstrengung besteht vornehmlich darin, Begriffloses festzuhalten, und begrifflos es zu verbinden.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"62.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0019","text":"Der Inhalt ist das leere Eins; der gediegene Gehalt des sittlichen und geistigen Lebens und der individuellen Gestaltungen desselben, mit welchem als der edelsten Nahrung die Erziehung den jugendlichen Geist großziehen soll, sollte von dem inhaltslosen Eins verdrängt werden; die Wirkung, wenn jene Übungen zur Hauptsache und Hauptbeschäftigung gemacht werden, kann keine andere seyn, als den Geist nach Form und Inhalt auszuhöhlen und abzustumpfen. Weil das Rechnen ein so sehr äußerliches, somit mechanisches Geschäft ist, haben sich Maschinen verfertigen lassen, welche die arithmetischen Operationen aufs vollkommenste vollführen.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"62.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0020","text":"Wenn man über die Natur des Rechnens nur diesen Umstand allein kennte, so läge darin die Entscheidung, was es mit dem Einfalle für eine Bewandniß hatte, das Rechnen zum Hauptbildungsmittel des Geistes zu machen, und ihn auf die Folter, sich zur Maschine zu vervollkommnen, zu legen.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"62.20"}],"sha256":"d874b6ee3727a88a022bcc644622c6292073f151bf2593672da74a92cc8d88df","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T102952492090Z_1cbee885","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"d874b6ee3727a88a022bcc644622c6292073f151bf2593672da74a92cc8d88df","sha256":"01e1c0bab0ca32775bc8736f068b4113f3e5fdc6808650572cdbd81aae035ec4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:29:52.492102+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0001","text":"As is well known, Pythagoras represented relations of reason or philosophemes in numbers; and even in more recent times use has been made in philosophy of these and of forms of their relations, such as powers, etc., in order to regulate thoughts accordingly or to express them thereby.—From a pedagogical point of view, number has been held to be the most suitable object of inner intuition, and calculating occupation with its relations to be that activity of spirit in which it brings to intuition its most proper relations and, in general, the fundamental relations of essence. —The extent to which this high value may pertain to number follows from its concept, as it has emerged.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"62.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0002","text":"We saw number as the absolute determinacy of quantity, and its element as the difference that has become indifferent;—determinacy in itself, which at the same time is posited as wholly external. Arithmetic is an analytic science, because all the connections and differences that occur in its object do not lie in the object itself, but are wholly externally attached to it. It has no concrete object that would have inner relations within itself, which would initially be concealed from cognition, not given in the immediate representation of it, but would first have to be brought forth through the effort of cognition. It contains not only no concept, and thus no task for comprehending thought, but is the opposite of the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"62.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0003","text":"On account of the indifference of what is connected toward the connection, which lacks necessity, thinking here finds itself in an activity that is at the same time the utmost externalization of itself: in the violent activity of moving in thoughtlessness and connecting what is incapable of necessity. The object is the abstract thought of externality itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"62.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0004","text":"As this thought of externality, number is at the same time the abstraction from sensuous multiplicity; of the sensuous it has retained nothing but the abstract determination of externality itself; thereby the sensuous has been brought nearest to thought in it; it is the pure thought of thought’s own externalization.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"62.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0005","text":"Spirit, which raises itself above the sensuous world and cognizes its essence, when it seeks an element for its pure representation, for the expression of its essence, may therefore, before it grasps thought itself as this element and obtains the purely spiritual expression for its presentation, fall upon choosing number, this inward, abstract externality. We therefore see number employed early in the history of science for the expression of philosophemes. It constitutes the last stage of imperfection: grasping the universal as encumbered with the sensuous. The ancients had a determinate consciousness that number stands midway between the sensuous and thought. Aristotle reports of Plato (Metaphys.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"62.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0006","text":"I, 5) that he says that, apart from the sensuous and the Ideas, the mathematical determinations of things stand between them, distinguished from the sensuous in that they are invisible (eternal) and unmoved, but from the Ideas in that they are a plurality and a likeness, whereas the Idea is simply identical with itself and one in itself.—A more detailed, thoroughly conceived reflection on this by Moderatus of Cadiz is adduced in Malchi Vita Pythagorae ed. Ritterhus. p. 30f.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"62.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0007","text":"He attributes the fact that the Pythagoreans fell upon numbers to their not yet having been able to grasp the fundamental Ideas and first principles distinctly in reason, because these principles are difficult to think and difficult to express; numbers serve well for designation in instruction. In this they imitated, among others, the geometers, who, unable to express the corporeal in thoughts, use figures and say, this is a triangle, while they intend that not the drawing falling under the eyes should be taken for the triangle, but that only its thought should be represented by it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"62.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0008","text":"Thus the Pythagoreans expressed the thought of unity, selfsame-ness and equality, and the ground of the harmony, connection, and preservation of everything, of what is identical with itself, as One, etc.—It is superfluous to remark that the Pythagoreans also passed from number to thought-expression, to the explicit categories of the equal and unequal, of limit and infinity; it is already reported in regard to those numerical expressions (ibid., in the notes to p. 31 l.s., from a life of Pythagoras in Photius p. 772) that the Pythagoreans distinguished between the Monas and the One; they took the Monas as the thought, but the One as the number; likewise Two as the arithmetical, the Dyas (for that is presumably what it should read there) as the thought of the indeterminate.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"62.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0009","text":"—These ancients, first of all, saw very correctly the inadequacy of numerical forms for determinations of thought, and just as correctly they further demanded, in place of that first makeshift for thoughts, the proper expression; how much further had they come in their reflection than those who nowadays again regard it as something praiseworthy, indeed thorough and profound, to put numbers themselves and numerical determinations, such as powers, then the infinitely great, infinitely small, One divided by infinity, and other such determinations—which are themselves often also a perverse mathematical formalism—in place of determinations of thought, and to return to that impotent childhood.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"62.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0010","text":"If earlier the expression was cited that number stands between the sensuous and thought, inasmuch as it has in itself also that of the former, namely plurality, being-outside-one-another, it is to be noted that this plurality itself, the sensuous taken up into thought, is the category belonging to it of what is external in itself. The further, concrete, true thoughts—the most living, most mobile, grasped only in relation—when transferred into this element of being-outside-itself, themselves become dead, motionless determinations. The richer thoughts become in determinacy and hence in relation, the more confused, on the one hand, and the more arbitrary and meaningless, on the other, does their presentation become in such forms as numbers are.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"62.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0011","text":"One, Two, Three, Four, Henas or Monas, Dyas, Trias, Tetraktys, still lie close to the quite simple abstract concepts; but when numbers are to pass over into concrete relations, it is futile to wish still to keep them close to the concept,","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"62.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0012","text":"But if determinations of thought are designated by One, Two, Three, Four for the movement of the concept, through which alone it is concept, this is the harshest demand that can be made of thinking. It moves in the element of its opposite, relationlessness; its business is the work of derangement. To comprehend, for example, that One is Three and Three is One is therefore this harsh demand, because One is what is relationless, and thus does not show in itself the determination through which it passes over into its opposite, but is rather precisely that which absolutely excludes and refuses such a relation. Conversely, the understanding makes use of this against speculative truth (as, for example,","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"62.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0013","text":"against that laid down in the doctrine called that of the Trinity) and counts its determinations, which constitute one unity, in order to exhibit them as a manifest absurdity,—that is, it itself commits the absurdity of making what is absolutely relation into what is relationless. With the name Trinity it was indeed not reckoned upon that the understanding would regard the One and number as the essential determinacy of the content. That name expresses contempt for the understanding, which, however, has established its vanity in clinging to the One and number as such, and has set them against reason.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"62.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0014","text":"To take numbers, geometrical figures—as has often occurred with the circle, triangle, etc.—as mere symbols (the circle, for example, of eternity, the triangle of the Trinity) is, on the one hand, something unobjectionable; but it is foolish, on the other hand, to suppose that thereby more is expressed than thought is able to grasp and express.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"62.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0015","text":"If in such symbols, as in others produced by imagination in the mythologies of peoples and in poetry in general—beside which the unimaginative geometrical figures are in any case meagre—as also in these there is supposed to lie a profound wisdom, profound significance, then it is precisely thought alone that is concerned with bringing to light the wisdom that lies only therein, and not merely in symbols, but in nature and in spirit; in symbols truth is still clouded and veiled by the sensuous element; it becomes wholly manifest to consciousness only in the form of thought; significance is only thought itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"62.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0016","text":"But to draw upon mathematical categories in order to determine something from them for the method or content of philosophical science proves to be essentially perverse, because insofar as mathematical formulae signify thoughts and conceptual differences, their significance must rather first be specified, determined, and justified in philosophy. In its concrete sciences, philosophy has to take the logical from logic, not from mathematics; it can only be an expedient of philosophical incapacity to resort, for the logical of philosophy, to the configurations which the logical assumes in other sciences, and of which many are merely intimations, while others are also stunted forms of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"62.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0017","text":"The mere application of such borrowed formulae is in any case an external procedure; the application itself would have to be preceded by a consciousness of their value as well as their significance; but such consciousness is supplied only by thinking consideration, not by their authority derived from mathematics. Such consciousness of them is logic itself, and this consciousness strips off their particular form, renders it superfluous and useless, corrects it, and alone procures for them their justification, sense, and value.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"62.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0018","text":"What is involved in the use of number and calculation, insofar as it is supposed to constitute a principal pedagogical foundation, follows of itself from what has preceded. Number is a non-sensuous object, and occupation with it and its combinations a non-sensuous activity; spirit is thus held to reflection within itself and to inward abstract labour by it, which is of great, yet one-sided importance. For on the other hand, since number has as its basis only external, thoughtless difference, that activity becomes a thoughtless, mechanical one. The exertion of strength consists chiefly in holding fast what is conceptless and connecting it conceptlessly.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"62.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0019","text":"The content is the empty One; the solid content of ethical and spiritual life and of its individual formations, with which, as the noblest nourishment, education ought to raise the youthful spirit, should be displaced by the contentless One; the effect, if those exercises are made the principal matter and principal occupation, can be no other than to hollow out and blunt the spirit in form and content. Because calculation is so very external, and consequently mechanical, an activity, machines have been made that perform arithmetical operations most perfectly.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"62.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_15:P0020","text":"If one knew of the nature of calculation only this circumstance alone, the decision would already lie therein as to what was the import of the notion of making calculation the principal means of cultivating spirit, and of putting it to the torture of perfecting itself into a machine.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"62.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_15:P0020"]}],"source_digest":"00081883ba3654888ec03f0cbaa5e2285a21079a478c4d2f36d756423e7ec4fb","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD","title":"a. Their Difference.","order":63,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_UNTD","text":"## B. Extensives und intensives Quantum.\n\n## a. Unterschied derselben.\n\n1. Das Quantum hat, wie sich vorhin ergeben, seine Bestimmtheit als Grenze in der Anzahl. Es ist ein in sich Diskretes, ein Vieles, das nicht ein Seyn hat, welches verschieden wäre von seiner Grenze und sie außer ihm hätte. Das Quantum so mit seiner Grenze, die ein Vielfaches an ihr selbst ist, ist extensive Größe.\n\nDie extensive Größe ist von der kontinuirlichen zu unterscheiden; jener steht direkt nicht die diskrete, sondern die intensive gegenüber. Extensive und intensive Größe sind Bestimmtheiten der quantitativen Grenze selbst, das Quantum aber ist identisch mit seiner Grenze; kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe sind dagegen Bestimmungen der Größe an sich, d. i. der Quantität als solcher, insofern beim Quantum von der Grenze abstrahirt wird.—Die extensive Größe hat das Moment der Kontinuität an ihr selbst und in ihrer Grenze, indem ihr Vieles überhaupt Kontinuirliches ist; die Grenze als Negation erscheint insofern an dieser Gleichheit der Vielen, als Begrenzung der Einheit. Die kontinuirliche Größe ist die sich fortsetzende Quantität ohne Rücksicht auf eine Grenze, und insofern sie mit einer solchen vorgesstellt wird, ist diese eine Begrenzung überhaupt, ohne daß die Diskretion an ihr gesetzt sey. Das Quantum nur als kontinuirliche Größe ist noch nicht wahrhaft für sich bestimmt, weil sie des Eins, worin das Für-sich-bestimmtseyn liegt, und der Zahl entbehrt. Eben so ist die diskrete Größe unmittelbar nur unterschiedenes Vieles überhaupt, das, insofern es als solches eine Grenze haben sollte, nur eine Menge, d. h. ein unbestimmt Begrenztes wäre; daß es als bestimmtes Quantum sey, dazu gehört das Zusammenfassen des Vielen in Eins, wodurch sie mit der Grenze identisch gesetzt werden. Jede, die kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe, als Quantum überhaupt hat nur eine der beiden Seiten an ihr gesetzt, wodurch es vollkommen bestimmt und als Zahl ist. Diese ist unmittelbar extensives Quantum,—die einfache Bestimmtheit, die wesentlich als Anzahl, jedoch als Anzahl einer und derselben Einheit ist; es ist von der Zahl nur dadurch unterschieden, daß ausdrücklich die Bestimmtheit als Vielheit in dieser gesetzt ist.\n\n2. Die Bestimmtheit jedoch, wie groß etwas ist, durch die Zahl, bedarf nicht des Unterschiedes von etwas Anderem Großem, so daß zur Bestimmtheit dieses Großen es selbst und ein Anderes Großes gehörte, indem die Bestimmtheit der Größe überhaupt für-sich-bestimmte, gleichgültige, einfach auf sich bezogene Grenze ist; und in der Zahl ist sie gesetzt als eingeschlossen in das für-sich-seyende Eins, und hat die Äußerlichkeit, die Beziehung-auf-Anderes innerhalb ihrer selbst. Dieses Viele der Grenze selbst ferner, ist wie das Viele überhaupt, nicht ein in sich Ungleiches, sondern ein Kontinuirliches jedes der Vielen ist was das Andere ist; es als vieles Außereinanderseyendes oder Diskretes macht daher die Bestimmtheit als solche nicht aus. dieß Viele fällt also für sich selbst in seine Kontinuität zusammen und wird einfache Einheit.—Die Anzahl ist nur Moment der Zahl; aber macht nicht als eine Menge von numerischen Eins die Bestimmtheit der Zahl aus, sondern diese Eins als gleichgültige, sich Äußerliche, sind im Zurückgekehrtseyn der Zahl in sich aufgehoben; die Äußerlichkeit, welche die Eins der Vielheit ausmachte, verschwindet in dem Eins, als Beziehung der Zahl auf sich selbst.\n\nDie Grenze des Quantums, das als extensives seine daseyende Bestimmtheit als die sich selbst äußerliche Anzahl hatte, geht also in einfache Bestimmtheit über. In dieser einfachen Bestimmung der Grenze ist es intensive Größe; und die Grenze oder Bestimmtheit, die mit dem Quantum identisch ist, ist nun auch so als Einfaches gesetzt, —der Grad.\n\nDer Grad ist also bestimmte Größe, Quantum, aber nicht zugleich Menge, oder Mehreres innerhalb seiner selbst; er ist nur eine Mehrheit; die Mehrheit ist das Mehrere in die einfache Bestimmung zusammengenommen, das Daseyn in das Fürsichseyn zurückgegangen. Seine Bestimmtheit muß zwar durch eine Zahl ausgedrückt werden als dem vollkommenen Bestimmtseyn des Quantums, aber ist nicht als Anzahl, sondern einfach, nur Ein Grad. Wenn von 10, 20 Graden gesprochen wird, ist das Quantum, das so viele Grade hat, der zehente, zwanzigste Grad, nicht die Anzahl und Summe derselben; so wäre es ein extensives; sondern es ist nur Einer, der zehnte, zwanzigste Grad. Er enthält die Bestimmtheit, welche in der Anzahl zehn, zwanzig liegt, aber enthält sie nicht als Mehrere, sondern ist die Zahl als aufgehobene Anzahl, als einfache Bestimmtheit.\n\n3. In der Zahl ist das Quantum in seiner vollständigen Bestimmtheit gesetzt; als intensives Quantum aber als in ihrem Fürsichseyn, ist es gesetzt, wie es seinem Begriffe nach oder an sich ist. Die Form nämlich der Beziehung auf sich, welche es im Grade hat, ist zugleich das Sich-Äußerlichseyn desselben. Die Zahl ist als extensives Quantum numerische Vielheit, und hat so die Äußerlichkeit innerhalb ihrer. Diese, als Vieles überhaupt, fällt in die Ununterschiedenheit zusammen, und hebt sich auf in dem Eins der Zahl, ihrer Beziehung auf sich selbst. Das Quantum hat aber seine Bestimmtheit als Anzahl; es enthält, wie vorhin gezeigt worden, sie, ob sie gleich nicht mehr an ihm gesetzt ist. Der Grad also, der als in sich selbst einfach dieß äußerliche Andersseyn nicht mehr in ihm hat, hat es außer ihm, und bezieht sich darauf als auf seine Bestimmtheit. Eine ihm äußerliche Vielheit macht die Bestimmtheit der einfachen Grenze, welche er für sich ist, aus.\n\nDaß die Anzahl, insofern sie sich innerhalb der Zahl im extensiven Quantum befinden sollte, sich darin aufhob, bestimmt sich somit dahin, daß sie außerhalb derselben gesetzt ist. Indem die Zahl als Eins, in sich reflektirte Beziehung auf sich selbst gesetzt ist, schheßt sie die Gleichgültigkeit und Äußerlichkeit der Anzahl aus sich aus, und ist Beziehung auf sich als Beziehung durch sich selbst auf ein Äußerliches.\n\nHierin hat das Quantum die seinem Begriffe gemäße Realität. Die Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmtheit macht seine Qualität aus; d. i. die Bestimmtheit, die an ihr selbst als die sich äußerliche Bestimmtheit ist.—Sonach ist der Grad einfache Größenbestimmtheit unter einer Mehrheit solcher Intensitäten, die verschieden, jede nur einfache Beziehung auf sich selbst, zugleich aber in wesentlicher Beziehung auf einander sind, so daß jede in dieser Kontinuität mit den anderen ihre Bestimmtheit hat. Diese Beziehung des Grades durch sich selbst auf sein Anderes, macht das Auf- und Absteigen an der Skale der Grade zu einem stätigen Fortgang, einem Fließen, das eine ununterbrochene, untheilbare Veränderung ist; jedes der Mehrern, die darin unterschieden werden, ist nicht getrennt von den Anderen, sondern hat sein Bestimmtseyn nur in diesen. Als sich auf sich beziehende Größebestimmung ist jeder der Grade gleichgültig gegen die andern; aber er ist eben so sehr an sich auf diese Äußerlichkeit bezogen, er ist nur vermittelst derselben, was er ist, seine Beziehung auf sich ist in einem die nicht gleichgültige Beziehung auf das Äußerliche, hat in dieser seine Qualität.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0001","text":"## B. Extensives und intensives Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"63.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0002","text":"## a. Unterschied derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"63.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0003","text":"1. Das Quantum hat, wie sich vorhin ergeben, seine Bestimmtheit als Grenze in der Anzahl. Es ist ein in sich Diskretes, ein Vieles, das nicht ein Seyn hat, welches verschieden wäre von seiner Grenze und sie außer ihm hätte. Das Quantum so mit seiner Grenze, die ein Vielfaches an ihr selbst ist, ist extensive Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"63.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0004","text":"Die extensive Größe ist von der kontinuirlichen zu unterscheiden; jener steht direkt nicht die diskrete, sondern die intensive gegenüber. Extensive und intensive Größe sind Bestimmtheiten der quantitativen Grenze selbst, das Quantum aber ist identisch mit seiner Grenze; kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe sind dagegen Bestimmungen der Größe an sich, d. i. der Quantität als solcher, insofern beim Quantum von der Grenze abstrahirt wird.—Die extensive Größe hat das Moment der Kontinuität an ihr selbst und in ihrer Grenze, indem ihr Vieles überhaupt Kontinuirliches ist; die Grenze als Negation erscheint insofern an dieser Gleichheit der Vielen, als Begrenzung der Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"63.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0005","text":"Die kontinuirliche Größe ist die sich fortsetzende Quantität ohne Rücksicht auf eine Grenze, und insofern sie mit einer solchen vorgesstellt wird, ist diese eine Begrenzung überhaupt, ohne daß die Diskretion an ihr gesetzt sey. Das Quantum nur als kontinuirliche Größe ist noch nicht wahrhaft für sich bestimmt, weil sie des Eins, worin das Für-sich-bestimmtseyn liegt, und der Zahl entbehrt. Eben so ist die diskrete Größe unmittelbar nur unterschiedenes Vieles überhaupt, das, insofern es als solches eine Grenze haben sollte, nur eine Menge, d. h. ein unbestimmt Begrenztes wäre; daß es als bestimmtes Quantum sey, dazu gehört das Zusammenfassen des Vielen in Eins, wodurch sie mit der Grenze identisch gesetzt werden. Jede, die kontinuirliche und diskrete Größe, als Quantum überhaupt hat nur eine der beiden Seiten an ihr gesetzt, wodurch es vollkommen bestimmt und als Zahl ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"63.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0006","text":"Diese ist unmittelbar extensives Quantum,—die einfache Bestimmtheit, die wesentlich als Anzahl, jedoch als Anzahl einer und derselben Einheit ist; es ist von der Zahl nur dadurch unterschieden, daß ausdrücklich die Bestimmtheit als Vielheit in dieser gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"63.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0007","text":"2. Die Bestimmtheit jedoch, wie groß etwas ist, durch die Zahl, bedarf nicht des Unterschiedes von etwas Anderem Großem, so daß zur Bestimmtheit dieses Großen es selbst und ein Anderes Großes gehörte, indem die Bestimmtheit der Größe überhaupt für-sich-bestimmte, gleichgültige, einfach auf sich bezogene Grenze ist; und in der Zahl ist sie gesetzt als eingeschlossen in das für-sich-seyende Eins, und hat die Äußerlichkeit, die Beziehung-auf-Anderes innerhalb ihrer selbst. Dieses Viele der Grenze selbst ferner, ist wie das Viele überhaupt, nicht ein in sich Ungleiches, sondern ein Kontinuirliches jedes der Vielen ist was das Andere ist; es als vieles Außereinanderseyendes oder Diskretes macht daher die Bestimmtheit als solche nicht aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"63.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0008","text":"dieß Viele fällt also für sich selbst in seine Kontinuität zusammen und wird einfache Einheit.—Die Anzahl ist nur Moment der Zahl; aber macht nicht als eine Menge von numerischen Eins die Bestimmtheit der Zahl aus, sondern diese Eins als gleichgültige, sich Äußerliche, sind im Zurückgekehrtseyn der Zahl in sich aufgehoben; die Äußerlichkeit, welche die Eins der Vielheit ausmachte, verschwindet in dem Eins, als Beziehung der Zahl auf sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"63.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0009","text":"Die Grenze des Quantums, das als extensives seine daseyende Bestimmtheit als die sich selbst äußerliche Anzahl hatte, geht also in einfache Bestimmtheit über. In dieser einfachen Bestimmung der Grenze ist es intensive Größe; und die Grenze oder Bestimmtheit, die mit dem Quantum identisch ist, ist nun auch so als Einfaches gesetzt, —der Grad.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"63.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0010","text":"Der Grad ist also bestimmte Größe, Quantum, aber nicht zugleich Menge, oder Mehreres innerhalb seiner selbst; er ist nur eine Mehrheit; die Mehrheit ist das Mehrere in die einfache Bestimmung zusammengenommen, das Daseyn in das Fürsichseyn zurückgegangen. Seine Bestimmtheit muß zwar durch eine Zahl ausgedrückt werden als dem vollkommenen Bestimmtseyn des Quantums, aber ist nicht als Anzahl, sondern einfach, nur Ein Grad. Wenn von 10, 20 Graden gesprochen wird, ist das Quantum, das so viele Grade hat, der zehente, zwanzigste Grad, nicht die Anzahl und Summe derselben; so wäre es ein extensives; sondern es ist nur Einer, der zehnte, zwanzigste Grad. Er enthält die Bestimmtheit, welche in der Anzahl zehn, zwanzig liegt, aber enthält sie nicht als Mehrere, sondern ist die Zahl als aufgehobene Anzahl, als einfache Bestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"63.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0011","text":"3. In der Zahl ist das Quantum in seiner vollständigen Bestimmtheit gesetzt; als intensives Quantum aber als in ihrem Fürsichseyn, ist es gesetzt, wie es seinem Begriffe nach oder an sich ist. Die Form nämlich der Beziehung auf sich, welche es im Grade hat, ist zugleich das Sich-Äußerlichseyn desselben. Die Zahl ist als extensives Quantum numerische Vielheit, und hat so die Äußerlichkeit innerhalb ihrer. Diese, als Vieles überhaupt, fällt in die Ununterschiedenheit zusammen, und hebt sich auf in dem Eins der Zahl, ihrer Beziehung auf sich selbst. Das Quantum hat aber seine Bestimmtheit als Anzahl; es enthält, wie vorhin gezeigt worden, sie, ob sie gleich nicht mehr an ihm gesetzt ist. Der Grad also, der als in sich selbst einfach dieß äußerliche Andersseyn nicht mehr in ihm hat, hat es außer ihm, und bezieht sich darauf als auf seine Bestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"63.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0012","text":"Eine ihm äußerliche Vielheit macht die Bestimmtheit der einfachen Grenze, welche er für sich ist, aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"63.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0013","text":"Daß die Anzahl, insofern sie sich innerhalb der Zahl im extensiven Quantum befinden sollte, sich darin aufhob, bestimmt sich somit dahin, daß sie außerhalb derselben gesetzt ist. Indem die Zahl als Eins, in sich reflektirte Beziehung auf sich selbst gesetzt ist, schheßt sie die Gleichgültigkeit und Äußerlichkeit der Anzahl aus sich aus, und ist Beziehung auf sich als Beziehung durch sich selbst auf ein Äußerliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"63.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0014","text":"Hierin hat das Quantum die seinem Begriffe gemäße Realität. Die Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmtheit macht seine Qualität aus; d. i. die Bestimmtheit, die an ihr selbst als die sich äußerliche Bestimmtheit ist.—Sonach ist der Grad einfache Größenbestimmtheit unter einer Mehrheit solcher Intensitäten, die verschieden, jede nur einfache Beziehung auf sich selbst, zugleich aber in wesentlicher Beziehung auf einander sind, so daß jede in dieser Kontinuität mit den anderen ihre Bestimmtheit hat. Diese Beziehung des Grades durch sich selbst auf sein Anderes, macht das Auf- und Absteigen an der Skale der Grade zu einem stätigen Fortgang, einem Fließen, das eine ununterbrochene, untheilbare Veränderung ist; jedes der Mehrern, die darin unterschieden werden, ist nicht getrennt von den Anderen, sondern hat sein Bestimmtseyn nur in diesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"63.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0015","text":"Als sich auf sich beziehende Größebestimmung ist jeder der Grade gleichgültig gegen die andern; aber er ist eben so sehr an sich auf diese Äußerlichkeit bezogen, er ist nur vermittelst derselben, was er ist, seine Beziehung auf sich ist in einem die nicht gleichgültige Beziehung auf das Äußerliche, hat in dieser seine Qualität.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"63.15"}],"sha256":"e376b3b003bdfbce07b81b820d0d174f4dcb6b0a91fb39da10e71c768cab052c","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103007277166Z_815e06a1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Their Difference.","source_sha256":"e376b3b003bdfbce07b81b820d0d174f4dcb6b0a91fb39da10e71c768cab052c","sha256":"713fca9ec3b0c70493c5f7a694453fb419f42cf8def38524a4a1dd2f5511b2ee","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:30:07.277180+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0001","text":"## B. Extensive and intensive Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"63.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0002","text":"## a. Their difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"63.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0003","text":"1. As has just emerged, the Quantum has its determinacy as limit in number. It is something discrete in itself, a many, which does not have a being that would be different from its limit and would have it outside itself. The Quantum thus with its limit, which is itself a plurality, is extensive magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"63.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0004","text":"Extensive magnitude is to be distinguished from continuous magnitude; what directly stands opposed to the former is not discrete but intensive magnitude. Extensive and intensive magnitude are determinacies of the quantitative limit itself; Quantum, however, is identical with its limit; continuous and discrete magnitude, by contrast, are determinations of magnitude in itself, i.e. of quantity as such, insofar as abstraction is made, in the case of Quantum, from the limit.—Extensive magnitude has the moment of continuity in itself and in its limit, inasmuch as its many is in general continuous; the limit, as negation, thus appears in this equality of the many as the limitation of the unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"63.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0005","text":"Continuous magnitude is quantity continuing itself without regard to a limit, and insofar as it is represented with such a limit, this is a limitation in general, without discreteness being posited in it. Quantum merely as continuous magnitude is not yet truly determined for itself, because it lacks the One, wherein being-determined-for-self lies, and number. Likewise, discrete magnitude is immediately merely differentiated many in general, which, insofar as it should as such have a limit, would be merely an aggregate, i.e. something indeterminately limited; for it to be determinate Quantum, the gathering of the many into One is required, whereby they are posited as identical with the limit. Each, continuous and discrete magnitude, as Quantum in general has only one of the two sides posited in it, through which it is completely determined and is number.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"63.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0006","text":"This is immediately extensive Quantum,—the simple determinacy which is essentially number, yet number of one and the same unit; it is distinguished from number only in that the determinacy is expressly posited in it as multiplicity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"63.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0007","text":"2. Yet the determinacy of how great something is, through number, does not require the difference from another great something, such that for the determinacy of this great something it itself and another great something would belong; for the determinacy of magnitude in general is a self-determined, indifferent, simply self-related limit; and in number it is posited as enclosed in the One that is for itself, and has externality, relation-to-another, within itself. This many of the limit itself, furthermore, like the many in general, is not something unequal in itself, but something continuous; each of the many is what the other is; its being a many external to one another or discrete therefore does not constitute determinacy as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"63.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0008","text":"this many thus collapses, for itself, into its continuity and becomes simple unity.—Number is only a moment of number; but it does not, as an aggregate of numerical ones, constitute the determinacy of number; rather, these ones, as indifferent and external to one another, are sublated in number's having returned into itself; the externality which constituted the ones of multiplicity vanishes in the One, as number's relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"63.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0009","text":"The limit of Quantum, which as extensive had its existent determinacy as the number external to itself, thus passes over into simple determinacy. In this simple determination of the limit it is intensive magnitude; and the limit or determinacy which is identical with Quantum is now also posited thus as simple,—the degree.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"63.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0010","text":"The degree is therefore determinate magnitude, Quantum, but not at the same time an aggregate, or a plurality within itself; it is only a plurality; plurality is the plurality gathered into simple determination, existence having returned into being-for-self. Its determinacy must indeed be expressed through a number, as the complete determinacy of Quantum, but not as number, but simply, merely one degree. When one speaks of 10, 20 degrees, the Quantum that has so many degrees is the tenth, twentieth degree, not their number and sum; thus it would be an extensive Quantum; rather, it is only one, the tenth, twentieth degree. It contains the determinacy which lies in the number ten, twenty, but does not contain it as a plurality, but is number as sublated number, as simple determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"63.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0011","text":"3. In number, Quantum is posited in its complete determinacy; but as intensive Quantum, as in its being-for-self, it is posited as it is according to its Concept or in itself. For the form of relation to itself which it has in the degree is at the same time its being-external-to-itself. Number, as extensive Quantum, is numerical multiplicity, and thus has externality within it. This, as many in general, collapses into undifferentiatedness and sublates itself in the One of number, its relation to itself. But Quantum has its determinacy as number; as was shown above, it contains it, although it is no longer posited in it. The degree, therefore, which as simple within itself no longer has this external otherness in it, has it outside itself, and relates to it as to its determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"63.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0012","text":"A multiplicity external to it constitutes the determinacy of the simple limit which it is for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"63.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0013","text":"That number, insofar as it should be found within number in extensive Quantum, sublated itself therein, thus determines itself to mean that it is posited outside it. In that number is posited as One, as a relation to itself reflected into itself, it excludes from itself the indifference and externality of number, and is relation to itself as relation, through itself, to something external.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"63.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0014","text":"Herein Quantum has the reality commensurate with its Concept. The indifference of determinacy constitutes its quality; i.e. the determinacy which is in itself the determinacy external to itself.—Accordingly, degree is simple determinacy of magnitude among a multiplicity of such intensities, which are different, each merely simple relation to itself, but at the same time in essential relation to one another, such that each has its determinacy in this continuity with the others. This relation of the degree, through itself, to its other makes ascent and descent on the scale of degrees into a continuous progression, a flowing which is an uninterrupted, indivisible alteration; each of the several that are distinguished therein is not separated from the others, but has its determinacy only in these.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"63.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0015","text":"As a self-related determination of magnitude, each of the degrees is indifferent to the others; but it is equally related in itself to this externality, it is only through it what it is; its relation to itself is at one and the same time the non-indifferent relation to the external, and has its quality in this.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"63.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_UNTD:P0015"]}],"source_digest":"c9e95fbcc4a5df5e4bc0b6bcbc136c6af784452608cf9d6335ce7b88c9667f8c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Unterschied derselben."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Unterschied derselben.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD","title":"b. Identity of Extensive and Intensive Magnitude.","order":64,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BITD","text":"Der Grad ist nicht innerhalb seiner ein sich Äußerliches. Allein er ist nicht das unbestimmte Eins, das Princip der Zahl überhaupt, das nicht Anzahl ist, als nur die negative, keine Anzahl zu sein. Die intensive Größe ist zunächst ein einfaches Eins der Mehrern; es sind mehrere Grade; bestimmt sind sie aber nicht, weder als einfaches Eins, noch als Mehrere, sondern nur in der Beziehung dieses Außersichseyns, oder in der Identität des Eins und der Mehrheit. Wenn also die Mehreren als solche zwar außer dem einfachen Grade sind, so besteht in seiner Beziehung auf sie seine Bestimmtheit; er enthält also die Anzahl. Wie zwanzig als extensive Größe die zwanzig Eins als diskrete in sich enthält, so enthält der bestimmte Grad sie als Kontinuität, welche diese bestimmte Mehrheit einfach ist; er ist der zwanzigste Grad; und ist der zwanzigste Grad nur vermittelst dieser Anzahl, die als solche außer ihm ist.\n\nDie Bestimmtheit der intensiven Größe ist daher von doppelter Seite zu betrachten. Sie ist bestimmt durch andere intensive Quanta, und ist in Kontinuität mit ihrem Andersseyn, so daß in dieser Beziehung auf dasselbe ihre Bestimmtheit besteht. Insofern sie nun erstens die einfache Bestimmtheit ist, ist sie bestimmt gegen andere Grade; sie schließt dieselben aus sich aus, und hat ihre Bestimmtheit in diesem Ausschließen. Aber zweitens ist sie an ihr selbst bestimmt; sie ist dieß in der Anzahl, als in ihrer Anzahl, nicht in ihr als ausgeschlossener, oder nicht in der Anzahl anderer Grade. Der zwanzigste Grad enthält die zwanzig an ihm selbst; er ist nicht nur bestimmt als unterschieden vom neunzehnten, ein und zwanzigsten u.s.f. sondern seine Bestimmtheit ist seine Anzahl. Aber insofern die Anzahl die seinige ist, und die Bestimmtheit ist zugleich wesentlich als Anzahl, so ist er extensives Quantum.\n\nExtensive und intensive Größe sind also eine und dieselbe Bestimmtheit des Quantums; sie sind nur dadurch unterschieden, daß die eine die Anzahl als innerhalb ihrer, die andere dasselbe, die Anzahl als außer ihr hat. Die extensive Größe geht in intensive Größe über, weil ihr Vieles an und für sich in die Einheit zusammenfällt, außer welcher das Viele tritt. Aber umgekehrt hat dieses Einfache seine Bestimmtheit nur an der Anzahl und zwar als seiner; als gleichgültig gegen die anders bestimmten Intensitäten hat es die Äußerlichkeit der Anzahl an ihm selbst; so ist die intensive Größe eben so wesentlich extensive Größe.\n\nMit dieser Identität tritt das qualitative Etwas ein; denn sie ist sich durch die Negation ihrer Unterschiede auf sich beziehende Einheit, diese Unterschiede aber machen die daseyende Größe-Bestimmtheit aus; diese negative Identität ist also Etwas, und zwar das gegen seine quantitative Bestimmtheit gleichgültig ist. Etwas ist ein Quantum, aber nun ist das qualitative Daseyn, wie es an sich ist, als gleichgültig dagegen gesetzt. Es konnte vom Quantum, der Zahl als solcher u.s.f. ohne ein Etwas, das deren Substrat wäre, gesprochen werden. Aber nun tritt Etwas diesen seinen Bestimmungen, durch deren Negation init sich vermittelt, als für sich daseyend gegenüber, und, indem es ein Quantum hat, als dasselbe, welches ein extensives und intensives Quantum habe. Seine Eine Bestimmtheit, die es als Quantum hat, ist in den unterschiedenen Momenten der Einheit und der Anzahl gesetzt; sie ist nicht nur an sich Eine und dieselbe, sondern ihr Setzen in diesen Unterschieden, als extensives und intensives Quantum, ist das Zurückgehen in diese Einheit, die als negative das gegen sie gleichgültig gesetzte Etwas ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0001","text":"Der Grad ist nicht innerhalb seiner ein sich Äußerliches. Allein er ist nicht das unbestimmte Eins, das Princip der Zahl überhaupt, das nicht Anzahl ist, als nur die negative, keine Anzahl zu sein. Die intensive Größe ist zunächst ein einfaches Eins der Mehrern; es sind mehrere Grade; bestimmt sind sie aber nicht, weder als einfaches Eins, noch als Mehrere, sondern nur in der Beziehung dieses Außersichseyns, oder in der Identität des Eins und der Mehrheit. Wenn also die Mehreren als solche zwar außer dem einfachen Grade sind, so besteht in seiner Beziehung auf sie seine Bestimmtheit; er enthält also die Anzahl.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"64.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0002","text":"Wie zwanzig als extensive Größe die zwanzig Eins als diskrete in sich enthält, so enthält der bestimmte Grad sie als Kontinuität, welche diese bestimmte Mehrheit einfach ist; er ist der zwanzigste Grad; und ist der zwanzigste Grad nur vermittelst dieser Anzahl, die als solche außer ihm ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"64.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0003","text":"Die Bestimmtheit der intensiven Größe ist daher von doppelter Seite zu betrachten. Sie ist bestimmt durch andere intensive Quanta, und ist in Kontinuität mit ihrem Andersseyn, so daß in dieser Beziehung auf dasselbe ihre Bestimmtheit besteht. Insofern sie nun erstens die einfache Bestimmtheit ist, ist sie bestimmt gegen andere Grade; sie schließt dieselben aus sich aus, und hat ihre Bestimmtheit in diesem Ausschließen. Aber zweitens ist sie an ihr selbst bestimmt; sie ist dieß in der Anzahl, als in ihrer Anzahl, nicht in ihr als ausgeschlossener, oder nicht in der Anzahl anderer Grade. Der zwanzigste Grad enthält die zwanzig an ihm selbst; er ist nicht nur bestimmt als unterschieden vom neunzehnten, ein und zwanzigsten u.s.f. sondern seine Bestimmtheit ist seine Anzahl.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"64.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0004","text":"Aber insofern die Anzahl die seinige ist, und die Bestimmtheit ist zugleich wesentlich als Anzahl, so ist er extensives Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"64.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0005","text":"Extensive und intensive Größe sind also eine und dieselbe Bestimmtheit des Quantums; sie sind nur dadurch unterschieden, daß die eine die Anzahl als innerhalb ihrer, die andere dasselbe, die Anzahl als außer ihr hat. Die extensive Größe geht in intensive Größe über, weil ihr Vieles an und für sich in die Einheit zusammenfällt, außer welcher das Viele tritt. Aber umgekehrt hat dieses Einfache seine Bestimmtheit nur an der Anzahl und zwar als seiner; als gleichgültig gegen die anders bestimmten Intensitäten hat es die Äußerlichkeit der Anzahl an ihm selbst; so ist die intensive Größe eben so wesentlich extensive Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"64.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0006","text":"Mit dieser Identität tritt das qualitative Etwas ein; denn sie ist sich durch die Negation ihrer Unterschiede auf sich beziehende Einheit, diese Unterschiede aber machen die daseyende Größe-Bestimmtheit aus; diese negative Identität ist also Etwas, und zwar das gegen seine quantitative Bestimmtheit gleichgültig ist. Etwas ist ein Quantum, aber nun ist das qualitative Daseyn, wie es an sich ist, als gleichgültig dagegen gesetzt. Es konnte vom Quantum, der Zahl als solcher u.s.f. ohne ein Etwas, das deren Substrat wäre, gesprochen werden. Aber nun tritt Etwas diesen seinen Bestimmungen, durch deren Negation init sich vermittelt, als für sich daseyend gegenüber, und, indem es ein Quantum hat, als dasselbe, welches ein extensives und intensives Quantum habe.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"64.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0007","text":"Seine Eine Bestimmtheit, die es als Quantum hat, ist in den unterschiedenen Momenten der Einheit und der Anzahl gesetzt; sie ist nicht nur an sich Eine und dieselbe, sondern ihr Setzen in diesen Unterschieden, als extensives und intensives Quantum, ist das Zurückgehen in diese Einheit, die als negative das gegen sie gleichgültig gesetzte Etwas ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"64.7"}],"sha256":"a135768ffd20d84a0e011b1e639ca04f664f1af82aff1139a7c387eb24baa565","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103016176630Z_e054f922","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Identity of Extensive and Intensive Magnitude.","source_sha256":"a135768ffd20d84a0e011b1e639ca04f664f1af82aff1139a7c387eb24baa565","sha256":"c21d11af9702aa67d91f9f2f7a337780215a977124bd321154a34c635f4fcbe0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:30:16.176641+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0001","text":"The degree does not have, within itself, an externality to itself. Yet it is not the indeterminate one, the principle of number in general, which is not a number, except negatively, in being no number. Intensive magnitude is at first a simple one of the many; there are several degrees; but they are determined neither as a simple one nor as several, but only in the relation of this being-outside-itself, or in the identity of the one and the plurality. Thus, although the several as such are outside the simple degree, its determinateness consists in its relation to them; it therefore contains the number.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"64.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0002","text":"Just as twenty, as extensive magnitude, contains within itself the twenty ones as discrete, so the determinate degree contains them as continuity, which is this determinate plurality in a simple form; it is the twentieth degree; and the twentieth degree is so only by means of this number, which as such is outside it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"64.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0003","text":"The determinateness of intensive magnitude is therefore to be considered from a twofold side. It is determined by other intensive quanta, and is in continuity with its otherness, so that its determinateness consists in this relation to it. In so far as it is, first, simple determinateness, it is determined in opposition to other degrees; it excludes them from itself, and has its determinateness in this excluding. But, second, it is determined in itself; it is so in the number, as in its number, not in it as excluded, or not in the number of other degrees. The twentieth degree contains the twenty in itself; it is not determined merely as distinct from the nineteenth, twenty-first, and so forth, but its determinateness is its number.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"64.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0004","text":"But in so far as the number is its own, and determinateness is at the same time essentially as number, it is extensive quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"64.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0005","text":"Extensive and intensive magnitude are thus one and the same determinateness of quantum; they are distinguished only in that the one has the number within itself, while the other has the same, the number, outside itself. Extensive magnitude passes over into intensive magnitude because its many, in and for itself, collapses into unity, outside which the many emerges. But conversely, this simple has its determinateness only in the number, and indeed as its own; as indifferent to the otherwise determined intensities, it has the externality of number in itself; thus intensive magnitude is just as essentially extensive magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"64.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0006","text":"With this identity the qualitative something enters; for it is unity relating itself to itself through the negation of its differences, but these differences constitute the existent magnitude-determinateness; this negative identity is therefore something, namely something indifferent to its quantitative determinateness. Something is a quantum, but now qualitative existence, as it is in itself, is posited as indifferent to it. One could speak of quantum, of number as such, and so forth, without a something that would be their substrate. But now something confronts these its determinations, through the negation of which it mediates with itself, as existing for itself, and, inasmuch as it has a quantum, as that which has an extensive and intensive quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"64.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BITD:P0007","text":"Its one determinateness, which it has as quantum, is posited in the distinct moments of unity and number; it is not merely one and the same in itself, but its positing in these distinctions, as extensive and intensive quantum, is the return into this unity, which, as negative, is the something posited as indifferent to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"64.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BITD:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"fe8e5780af5ed6806af175b1b27bb57510f9faa47010b8d93714d756d113aaf0","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Identität der extensiven und intensiven Größe."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Identität der extensiven und intensiven Größe.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16","title":"Remark 1.","order":65,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_16","text":"In der gewöhnlichen Vorstellung pflegen extensives und intensives Quantum so als Arten von Größen unterschieden zu werden, als ob es Gegenstände gäbe, die nur intensive, andere, die nur extensive Größe hätten. Ferner ist die Vorstellung einer philosophischen Naturwissenschaft hinzugekommen, welche das Mehrere, das Extensive, z. B. in der Grundbestimmung der Materie, einen Raum zu erfüllen, so wie in anderen Begriffen, in ein Intensives verwandelte, in dem Sinne, daß das Intensive, als das Dynamische die wahrhafte Bestimmung sey, und z.B. die Dichtigkeit oder specifische Raumerfüllung wesentlich nicht als eine gewisse Menge und Anzahl materieller Theile in einem Quantum Raum, sondern als ein gewisser Grad der raumerfüllenden Kraft der Materie gefaßt werden müsse.\n\nEs sind hierbei zweierlei Bestimmungen zu unterscheiden. Bei dem, was man die Umwandlung der mechanischen Betrachtungsweise in die dynamische genannt hat, kommt der Begriff von außereinander bestehenden selbstständigen Theilen, die nur äußerlich in ein Ganzes verbunden sind, und der davon verschiedene Begriff von Kraft vor. Was in der Raumerfüllung einer Seits nur als eine Menge einander äußerlichen Atome angesehen wird, wird anderer Seits als die Äußerung einer zu Grunde liegenden einfachen Kraft betrachtet.—Diese Verhältnisse voll Ganzen und Theilen, der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung, die hier einander gegenüber treten, gehören aber noch nicht hierher, sondern werden weiterhin betrachtet werden. Soviel läßt sich sogleich erinnern, daß das Verhältniß von Kraft und ihrer Äußerung, das dem Intensiven entspricht, zwar zunächst das wahrhaftere ist gegen das Verhältniß von Ganzen und Theilen; aber daß darum die Kraft nicht weniger einseitig als das Intensive, und die Äußerung, die Äußerlichkeit des Extensiven, ebenso untrennbar von der Kraft ist, so daß ein und derselbe Inhalt ebenso sehr in beiden Formen, des Intensiven und des Extensiven, vorhanden ist.\n\nDie andere Bestimmtheit, die dabei vorkommt, ist die quantitative als solche, die als extensives Quantum aufgehoben und in den Grad, als die wahrhaft seyn sollende Bestimmung, verwandelt wird; es ist aber gezeigt worden, daß dieser ebenso die erstere enthält, so daß die eine Form für die andere wesentlich ist, somit jedes Daseyn seine Größebestimmung eben so sehr als extensives wie als intensives Quantum darstellt.\n\nAls Beispiel hiervon dient daher alles, insofern es in einer Größebestimmung erscheint. Selbst die Zahl hat diese gedoppelte Form nothwendig unmittelbar an ihr. Sie ist eine Anzahl, insofern ist sie extensive Größe; aber sie ist auch Eins, ein Zehen, ein Hundert; insofern steht sie auf dem Übergange zur intensiven Größe, indem in dieser Einheit das Vielfache in Einfaches zusammengeht. Eins ist extensive Größe an sich, es kann als eine beliebige Anzahl von Theilen vorgestellt werden. So das Zehnte, das Hundertste ist dieß Einfache, Intensive, das seine Bestimmtheit an dem außer ihm fallenden Mehrern d. i. am Extensiven hat. Die Zahl ist Zehen, Hundert, und zugleich die Zehnte, Hundertste im Zahlensystem; beides ist dieselbe Bestimmtheit.\n\nDas Eins im Kreise heißt Grad, weil der Theil des Kreises wesentlich seine Bestimmtheit in dem Mehrern außer ihm hat, als eines nur einer geschlossenen Anzahl solcher Eins bestimmt ist. Der Grad des Kreises ist als bloße Raumgröße nur eine gewöhnliche Zahl; als Grad angesehen ist er die intensive Größe, die einen Sinn nur hat, als bestimmt durch die Anzahl von Graden, in die der Kreis getheilt ist, wie die Zahl überhaupt ihren Sinn nur hat in der Zahlenreihe.\n\nDie Größe eines konkretern Gegenstandes stellt ihre gedoppelte Seite, extensiv und intensiv zu seyn, an den gedoppelten Bestimmungen seines Daseyns dar, in deren einer er als ein Äußerliches, in der andern aber als ein Innerliches erscheint. So ist z.B. eine Masse als Gewicht, ein extensiv-Großes, insofern sie eine Anzahl von Pfunden, Centnern u.s.f. ausmacht; ein intensiv-Großes, insofern sie einen gewissen Druck ausübt; die Größe des Drucks ist ein Einfaches, ein Grad, der seine Bestimmtheit an einer Scale von Graden des Druckes hat. Als drückend erscheint die Masse als ein In-sich-seyn, als Subjekt, dem der intensive Größenunterschied zukommt.—Umgekehrt was diesen Grad des Drucks ausübt, ist vermögend, eine gewisse Anzahl von Pfunden u.s.f. von der Stelle zu bewegen, und mißt seine Größe hieran.\n\nOder die Wärme hat einen Grad; der Wärmegrad, er sey der l0te, 20ste u.s.f. ist eine einfache Empfindung, ein Subjektives. Aber dieser Grad ist eben so sehr vorhanden als extensive Größe, als die Ausdehnung einer Flüssigkeit, des Quecksilbers im Thermometer, der Luft oder des Thons u.s.f. Ein höherer Grad der Temperatur drückt sich aus als eine längere Quecksilbersäule, oder als ein schmälerer Thoncylinder; er erwärmt einen größern Raum auf dieselbe Weise als ein geringerer Grad nur den kleinern Raum.\n\nDer höhere Ton ist als der intensivere, zugleich eine größere Menge von Schwingungen, oder ein lauterer Ton, dem ein höherer Grad zugeschrieben wird, macht sich in einem größern Raume hörbar.—Mit der intensivern Farbe läßt sich eine größere Fläche, als mit einer schwächern, auf gleiche Weise färben; oder das Hellere, eine andere Art von Intensität, ist weiter sichtbar als das weniger Helle u.s.f.\n\nEben so im Geistigen ist die hohe Intensität des Charakters, Talents, Genies, von eben so weitgreifendem Daseyn, ausgedehnter Wirkung und vielseitiger Berührung. Der tiefste Begriff hat die allgemeinste Bedeutung und Anwendung.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0001","text":"In der gewöhnlichen Vorstellung pflegen extensives und intensives Quantum so als Arten von Größen unterschieden zu werden, als ob es Gegenstände gäbe, die nur intensive, andere, die nur extensive Größe hätten. Ferner ist die Vorstellung einer philosophischen Naturwissenschaft hinzugekommen, welche das Mehrere, das Extensive, z. B. in der Grundbestimmung der Materie, einen Raum zu erfüllen, so wie in anderen Begriffen, in ein Intensives verwandelte, in dem Sinne, daß das Intensive, als das Dynamische die wahrhafte Bestimmung sey, und z.B. die Dichtigkeit oder specifische Raumerfüllung wesentlich nicht als eine gewisse Menge und Anzahl materieller Theile in einem Quantum Raum, sondern als ein gewisser Grad der raumerfüllenden Kraft der Materie gefaßt werden müsse.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"65.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0002","text":"Es sind hierbei zweierlei Bestimmungen zu unterscheiden. Bei dem, was man die Umwandlung der mechanischen Betrachtungsweise in die dynamische genannt hat, kommt der Begriff von außereinander bestehenden selbstständigen Theilen, die nur äußerlich in ein Ganzes verbunden sind, und der davon verschiedene Begriff von Kraft vor. Was in der Raumerfüllung einer Seits nur als eine Menge einander äußerlichen Atome angesehen wird, wird anderer Seits als die Äußerung einer zu Grunde liegenden einfachen Kraft betrachtet.—Diese Verhältnisse voll Ganzen und Theilen, der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung, die hier einander gegenüber treten, gehören aber noch nicht hierher, sondern werden weiterhin betrachtet werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"65.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0003","text":"Soviel läßt sich sogleich erinnern, daß das Verhältniß von Kraft und ihrer Äußerung, das dem Intensiven entspricht, zwar zunächst das wahrhaftere ist gegen das Verhältniß von Ganzen und Theilen; aber daß darum die Kraft nicht weniger einseitig als das Intensive, und die Äußerung, die Äußerlichkeit des Extensiven, ebenso untrennbar von der Kraft ist, so daß ein und derselbe Inhalt ebenso sehr in beiden Formen, des Intensiven und des Extensiven, vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"65.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0004","text":"Die andere Bestimmtheit, die dabei vorkommt, ist die quantitative als solche, die als extensives Quantum aufgehoben und in den Grad, als die wahrhaft seyn sollende Bestimmung, verwandelt wird; es ist aber gezeigt worden, daß dieser ebenso die erstere enthält, so daß die eine Form für die andere wesentlich ist, somit jedes Daseyn seine Größebestimmung eben so sehr als extensives wie als intensives Quantum darstellt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"65.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0005","text":"Als Beispiel hiervon dient daher alles, insofern es in einer Größebestimmung erscheint. Selbst die Zahl hat diese gedoppelte Form nothwendig unmittelbar an ihr. Sie ist eine Anzahl, insofern ist sie extensive Größe; aber sie ist auch Eins, ein Zehen, ein Hundert; insofern steht sie auf dem Übergange zur intensiven Größe, indem in dieser Einheit das Vielfache in Einfaches zusammengeht. Eins ist extensive Größe an sich, es kann als eine beliebige Anzahl von Theilen vorgestellt werden. So das Zehnte, das Hundertste ist dieß Einfache, Intensive, das seine Bestimmtheit an dem außer ihm fallenden Mehrern d. i. am Extensiven hat. Die Zahl ist Zehen, Hundert, und zugleich die Zehnte, Hundertste im Zahlensystem; beides ist dieselbe Bestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"65.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0006","text":"Das Eins im Kreise heißt Grad, weil der Theil des Kreises wesentlich seine Bestimmtheit in dem Mehrern außer ihm hat, als eines nur einer geschlossenen Anzahl solcher Eins bestimmt ist. Der Grad des Kreises ist als bloße Raumgröße nur eine gewöhnliche Zahl; als Grad angesehen ist er die intensive Größe, die einen Sinn nur hat, als bestimmt durch die Anzahl von Graden, in die der Kreis getheilt ist, wie die Zahl überhaupt ihren Sinn nur hat in der Zahlenreihe.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"65.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0007","text":"Die Größe eines konkretern Gegenstandes stellt ihre gedoppelte Seite, extensiv und intensiv zu seyn, an den gedoppelten Bestimmungen seines Daseyns dar, in deren einer er als ein Äußerliches, in der andern aber als ein Innerliches erscheint. So ist z.B. eine Masse als Gewicht, ein extensiv-Großes, insofern sie eine Anzahl von Pfunden, Centnern u.s.f. ausmacht; ein intensiv-Großes, insofern sie einen gewissen Druck ausübt; die Größe des Drucks ist ein Einfaches, ein Grad, der seine Bestimmtheit an einer Scale von Graden des Druckes hat. Als drückend erscheint die Masse als ein In-sich-seyn, als Subjekt, dem der intensive Größenunterschied zukommt.—Umgekehrt was diesen Grad des Drucks ausübt, ist vermögend, eine gewisse Anzahl von Pfunden u.s.f. von der Stelle zu bewegen, und mißt seine Größe hieran.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"65.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0008","text":"Oder die Wärme hat einen Grad; der Wärmegrad, er sey der l0te, 20ste u.s.f. ist eine einfache Empfindung, ein Subjektives. Aber dieser Grad ist eben so sehr vorhanden als extensive Größe, als die Ausdehnung einer Flüssigkeit, des Quecksilbers im Thermometer, der Luft oder des Thons u.s.f. Ein höherer Grad der Temperatur drückt sich aus als eine längere Quecksilbersäule, oder als ein schmälerer Thoncylinder; er erwärmt einen größern Raum auf dieselbe Weise als ein geringerer Grad nur den kleinern Raum.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"65.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0009","text":"Der höhere Ton ist als der intensivere, zugleich eine größere Menge von Schwingungen, oder ein lauterer Ton, dem ein höherer Grad zugeschrieben wird, macht sich in einem größern Raume hörbar.—Mit der intensivern Farbe läßt sich eine größere Fläche, als mit einer schwächern, auf gleiche Weise färben; oder das Hellere, eine andere Art von Intensität, ist weiter sichtbar als das weniger Helle u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"65.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0010","text":"Eben so im Geistigen ist die hohe Intensität des Charakters, Talents, Genies, von eben so weitgreifendem Daseyn, ausgedehnter Wirkung und vielseitiger Berührung. Der tiefste Begriff hat die allgemeinste Bedeutung und Anwendung.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"65.10"}],"sha256":"16b867a4d98006fe5b89a1b9ac454077d64d8d9d9228347abd5e734f5106ce27","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103027999703Z_7af40783","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"16b867a4d98006fe5b89a1b9ac454077d64d8d9d9228347abd5e734f5106ce27","sha256":"5f83f450e9fbd85b75e8ead747c25702b2896ba6505672a33b927458371cbacd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:30:27.999740+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0001","text":"In ordinary conception, extensive and intensive quantum are customarily distinguished as kinds of magnitude, as though there were objects that had only intensive magnitude, and others that had only extensive magnitude. There has further arisen the conception of a philosophical natural science which transformed the more, the extensive, e.g. in the fundamental determination of matter, to fill a space, as likewise in other concepts, into an intensive, in the sense that the intensive, as the dynamic, is the true determination, and that, e.g., density or specific spatial filling must essentially be conceived not as a certain quantity and number of material parts in a quantum of space, but as a certain degree of the space-filling force of matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"65.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0002","text":"Two kinds of determinations are to be distinguished here. In what has been called the transformation of the mechanical mode of consideration into the dynamic, there occurs the concept of self-subsistent parts existing outside one another, which are only externally combined into a whole, and the concept of force, distinct from this. What, on the one hand, is regarded in the filling of space merely as a multitude of atoms external to one another is, on the other hand, considered as the manifestation of an underlying simple force.—But these relations of whole and parts, of force and its manifestation, which here confront one another, do not yet belong here, but will be considered later.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"65.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0003","text":"Thus much may immediately be observed: that the relation of force and its manifestation, which corresponds to the intensive, is indeed at first the truer one as against the relation of whole and parts; but that for this reason force is no less one-sided than the intensive, and manifestation, the externality of the extensive, is equally inseparable from force, so that one and the same content is present equally in both forms, that of the intensive and that of the extensive.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"65.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0004","text":"The other determinacy that occurs here is the quantitative as such, which, as extensive quantum, is sublated and transformed into degree, as the determination that is supposed to be true; but it has been shown that this equally contains the former, so that the one form is essential to the other, and thus every determinate being presents its determination of magnitude just as much as extensive as intensive quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"65.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0005","text":"Everything therefore serves as an example of this, insofar as it appears in a determination of magnitude. Even number necessarily has this doubled form immediately in it. It is a number [Anzahl], and in this respect it is extensive magnitude; but it is also one, ten, a hundred; in this respect it stands at the transition to intensive magnitude, since in this unity the manifold coalesces into the simple. One is extensive magnitude in itself; it can be represented as any arbitrary number of parts. Thus a tenth, a hundredth, is this simple, intensive magnitude, which has its determinacy in the more that falls outside it, i.e. in the extensive. Number is ten, a hundred, and at the same time the tenth, the hundredth in the number system; both are the same determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"65.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0006","text":"The unit in the circle is called a degree, because the part of the circle essentially has its determinacy in the more outside it, as determined to be only one of a closed number of such units. The degree of the circle, as mere spatial magnitude, is only an ordinary number; regarded as degree, it is the intensive magnitude that has a sense only as determined by the number of degrees into which the circle is divided, just as number in general has its sense only in the numerical series.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"65.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0007","text":"The magnitude of a more concrete object presents its doubled aspect, of being extensive and intensive, in the doubled determinations of its determinate being, in one of which it appears as something external, but in the other as something internal. Thus, e.g., a mass, as weight, is something extensively great insofar as it amounts to a number of pounds, hundredweights, etc.; it is something intensively great insofar as it exerts a certain pressure; the magnitude of the pressure is a simple, a degree, which has its determinacy on a scale of degrees of pressure. As pressing, the mass appears as a being-within-self, as subject, to which the intensive difference of magnitude belongs.—Conversely, that which exerts this degree of pressure is capable of moving a certain number of pounds, etc., from their place, and measures its magnitude by this.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"65.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0008","text":"Or heat has a degree; the degree of heat, be it the 10th, 20th, etc., is a simple sensation, something subjective. But this degree is equally present as extensive magnitude, as the expansion of a liquid, of the mercury in the thermometer, of air or of clay, etc. A higher degree of temperature expresses itself as a longer column of mercury, or as a narrower cylinder of clay; it warms a larger space in the same way as a lower degree warms only the smaller space.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"65.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0009","text":"The higher tone, as the more intensive, is at the same time a greater number of vibrations; or a louder tone, to which a higher degree is ascribed, makes itself audible in a larger space.—With the more intensive colour, a larger surface can be coloured in the same way than with a weaker one; or what is brighter, another kind of intensity, is visible farther than what is less bright, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"65.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_16:P0010","text":"Likewise in the spiritual sphere, the high intensity of character, talent, genius, is of equally far-reaching determinate being, extensive effect, and manifold contact. The deepest concept has the most universal significance and application.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"65.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_16:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"772b75d65b271433131a8b0c3fd85a0c36f42c8fe98c5bffa45fa0c472bea24f","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17","title":"Remark 2.","order":66,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_17","text":"Kant hat einen eigenthümlichen Gebrauch von der Anwendung der Bestimmtheit des intensiven Quantums auf eine metaphysische Bestimmung der Seele gemacht. In der Kritik der metaphysischen Sätze von der Seele, die er Paralogismen der reinen Vernunft nennt, kommt er auf die Betrachtung des Schlusses von der Einfachheit der Seele auf die Beharrlichkeit derselben. Er setzt diesem Schlusse entgegen, (Kr. d. r. Vern. S. 414), \"daß, wenn wir gleich der Seele diese einfache Natur einräumen, da sie nämlich kein Mannigfaltiges außer einander, mithin keine extensive Größe enthält, man ihr doch so wenig wie irgend einem Existirenden, intensive Größe, d. i. einen Grad der Realität in Ansehung aller ihrer Vermögen, ja überhaupt alles dessen, was das Daseyn ausmacht, abläugnen könne, welcher durch alle unendlich viele kleinere Grade abnehmen, und so die vorgebliche Substanz obgleich nicht durch Vertheilung, doch durch allmälige Nachlassung (remissio) ihrer Kräfte, in nichts verwandelt werden könne; denn selbst das Bewußtseyn hatjederzeit einen Grad, der immer noch vermindert werden kann, folglich auch das Vermögen sich seiner bewußt zu seyn, und so alle übrige Vermögen.\"—Die Seele wird in der rationellen Psychologie, wie diese abstrakte Metaphysik war, nicht als Geist, sondern als ein nur unmittelbar Seyendes, als Seelending betrachtet. So hat Kant das Recht, die Kategorie des Quantums, \"wie auf irgend ein Existirendes\" und insofern dieß Seyende als einfach bestimmt ist, die des intensiven Quantums auf dasselbe anzuwenden. Dem Geiste kommt allerdings Seyn zu, aber von ganz anderer Intensität, als die des intensiven Quantums ist, vielmehr einer solchen Intensität, in welcher die Form des nur unmittelbaren Seyns und alle Kategorie desselben als aufgehoben sind. Es war nicht nur die Entfernung der Kategorie des extensiven Quantums zuzugeben, sondern die des Quantums überhaupt zu entfernen. Ein Weiteres aber ist noch, zu erkennen, wie in der ewigen Natur des Geistes Daseyn, Bewußtseyn, Endlichkeit ist und daraus hervorgeht, ohne daß er dadurch ein Ding würde.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17:P0001","text":"Kant hat einen eigenthümlichen Gebrauch von der Anwendung der Bestimmtheit des intensiven Quantums auf eine metaphysische Bestimmung der Seele gemacht. In der Kritik der metaphysischen Sätze von der Seele, die er Paralogismen der reinen Vernunft nennt, kommt er auf die Betrachtung des Schlusses von der Einfachheit der Seele auf die Beharrlichkeit derselben. Er setzt diesem Schlusse entgegen, (Kr. d. r. Vern. S. 414), \"daß, wenn wir gleich der Seele diese einfache Natur einräumen, da sie nämlich kein Mannigfaltiges außer einander, mithin keine extensive Größe enthält, man ihr doch so wenig wie irgend einem Existirenden, intensive Größe, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"66.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17:P0002","text":"einen Grad der Realität in Ansehung aller ihrer Vermögen, ja überhaupt alles dessen, was das Daseyn ausmacht, abläugnen könne, welcher durch alle unendlich viele kleinere Grade abnehmen, und so die vorgebliche Substanz obgleich nicht durch Vertheilung, doch durch allmälige Nachlassung (remissio) ihrer Kräfte, in nichts verwandelt werden könne; denn selbst das Bewußtseyn hatjederzeit einen Grad, der immer noch vermindert werden kann, folglich auch das Vermögen sich seiner bewußt zu seyn, und so alle übrige Vermögen.\"—Die Seele wird in der rationellen Psychologie, wie diese abstrakte Metaphysik war, nicht als Geist, sondern als ein nur unmittelbar Seyendes, als Seelending betrachtet. So hat Kant das Recht, die Kategorie des Quantums, \"wie auf irgend ein Existirendes\" und insofern dieß Seyende als einfach bestimmt ist, die des intensiven Quantums auf dasselbe anzuwenden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"66.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17:P0003","text":"Dem Geiste kommt allerdings Seyn zu, aber von ganz anderer Intensität, als die des intensiven Quantums ist, vielmehr einer solchen Intensität, in welcher die Form des nur unmittelbaren Seyns und alle Kategorie desselben als aufgehoben sind. Es war nicht nur die Entfernung der Kategorie des extensiven Quantums zuzugeben, sondern die des Quantums überhaupt zu entfernen. Ein Weiteres aber ist noch, zu erkennen, wie in der ewigen Natur des Geistes Daseyn, Bewußtseyn, Endlichkeit ist und daraus hervorgeht, ohne daß er dadurch ein Ding würde.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"66.3"}],"sha256":"8958043757cd9ce34e06ad4579e087b53089239de9299f68c46c89ced43c5ec2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103035670951Z_54417628","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"8958043757cd9ce34e06ad4579e087b53089239de9299f68c46c89ced43c5ec2","sha256":"0ef7d58e77517f22c5668d99422d798980cd7fbf6e8557445608a7004bdea96d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:30:35.670982+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17:P0001","text":"Kant made a peculiar use of the application of the determinacy of intensive quantum to a metaphysical determination of the soul. In the critique of the metaphysical propositions concerning the soul, which he calls the Paralogisms of Pure Reason, he comes to consider the inference from the simplicity of the soul to its permanence. He opposes to this inference (Critique of Pure Reason, p. 414) “that, although we may grant the soul this simple nature, namely that it contains no manifold outside one another, and hence no extensive magnitude, one nevertheless can no more deny to it than to any existing entity intensive magnitude, i.e.”","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"66.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_17:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17:P0002","text":"“a degree of reality with respect to all its powers, indeed in general with respect to everything that constitutes existence, which may diminish through all infinitely many lesser degrees, and thus the alleged substance, although not through division, yet through the gradual diminution (remissio) of its powers, may be transformed into nothing; for even consciousness always has a degree which can still be diminished, consequently also the capacity to be conscious of itself, and thus all the other capacities.”—In rational psychology, as this abstract metaphysics was, the soul is considered not as spirit, but as something merely immediately Being, as a soul-thing. Thus Kant has the right to apply to it the category of quantum, “as to any existing entity,” and, insofar as this Being is determined as simple, the category of intensive quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"66.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_17:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_17:P0003","text":"Spirit indeed has Being, but of an entirely different intensity from that of intensive quantum—rather, of an intensity in which the form of merely immediate Being and every category thereof are sublated. It was necessary not merely to concede the removal of the category of extensive quantum, but to remove that of quantum altogether. But it is a further matter to cognize how, in the eternal nature of spirit, existence, consciousness, finitude are, and proceed from it, without its thereby becoming a thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"66.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_17:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"6ece46be91945a15cbff20ac61fbe2d38d3948f06ae0dc056ab1b39879cf7a9d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN","title":"c. The Alteration of Quantum.","order":67,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDVN","text":"Der Unterschied des extensiven und intensiven Quantums ist der Bestimmtheit des Quantums als solcher gleichgültig. Aber überhaupt ist das Quantum die als aufgehoben gesetzte Bestimmtheit, die gleichgültige Grenze, die Bestimmtheit, welche eben so sehr die Negation ihrer selbst ist. In der extensiven Größe ist dieser Unterschied entwickelt, aber die intensive Größe ist das Daseyn dieser Äußerlichkeit, die das Quantum in sich ist. Er ist als sein Widerspruch in sich selbst gesetzt, die einfache sich auf sich beziehende Bestimmtheit zu seyn, welche die Negation ihrer selbst ist, ihre Bestimmtheit nicht an ihr, sondern in einem anderen Quantum zu haben.\n\nEin Quantum ist also seiner Qualität nach in absoluter Kontinuität mit seiner Äußerlichkeit, mit seinem Andersseyn, gesetzt. Es kann daher nicht nur über jede Größebestimmtheit hinausgegangen, sie kann nicht nur verändert werden, sondern es ist dieß gesetzt, daß sie sich verändern muß. Die Größebestimmung kontinuirt sich so in ihr Andersseyn, daß sie ihr Seyn nur in dieser Kontinuität mit einem anderen hat; sie ist nicht eine seyende, sondern eine werdende Grenze.\n\nDas Eins ist unendlich oder die sich auf sich beziehende Negation, daher die Repulsion seiner von sich selbst. Das Quantum ist gleichfalls unendlich, gesetzt als die sich auf sich beziehende Negativität; es repellirt sich von sich selbst. Aber es ist ein bestimmtes Eins, das Eins welches in Daseyn und in die Grenze übergegangen ist, also die Repulsion der Bestimmtheit von sich selbst, nicht das Erzeugen des sich selbst Gleichen, wie die Repulsion des Eins, sondern seines Andersseyns, es ist nun an ihm selbst gesetzt, über sich hinaus zu schicken, und ein Anderes zu werden. Es besteht darin, sich zu vermehren oder zu verhindern; es ist die Äußerlichkeit der Bestimmtheit an ihm selbst.\n\nDas Quantum schickt sich also selbst über sich hinaus; dieß Andere, zu dem es wird, ist zunächst selbst ein Quantum; aber ebenso als eine nicht seyende, sondern sich über sich selbst hinaustreibende Grenze. Die in diesem Hinausgehen wieder entstandene Grenze ist also schlechthin nur eine solche, die sich wieder aufhebt und zu einer fernern schickt, und so fort ins Unendliche.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0001","text":"Der Unterschied des extensiven und intensiven Quantums ist der Bestimmtheit des Quantums als solcher gleichgültig. Aber überhaupt ist das Quantum die als aufgehoben gesetzte Bestimmtheit, die gleichgültige Grenze, die Bestimmtheit, welche eben so sehr die Negation ihrer selbst ist. In der extensiven Größe ist dieser Unterschied entwickelt, aber die intensive Größe ist das Daseyn dieser Äußerlichkeit, die das Quantum in sich ist. Er ist als sein Widerspruch in sich selbst gesetzt, die einfache sich auf sich beziehende Bestimmtheit zu seyn, welche die Negation ihrer selbst ist, ihre Bestimmtheit nicht an ihr, sondern in einem anderen Quantum zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"67.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0002","text":"Ein Quantum ist also seiner Qualität nach in absoluter Kontinuität mit seiner Äußerlichkeit, mit seinem Andersseyn, gesetzt. Es kann daher nicht nur über jede Größebestimmtheit hinausgegangen, sie kann nicht nur verändert werden, sondern es ist dieß gesetzt, daß sie sich verändern muß. Die Größebestimmung kontinuirt sich so in ihr Andersseyn, daß sie ihr Seyn nur in dieser Kontinuität mit einem anderen hat; sie ist nicht eine seyende, sondern eine werdende Grenze.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"67.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0003","text":"Das Eins ist unendlich oder die sich auf sich beziehende Negation, daher die Repulsion seiner von sich selbst. Das Quantum ist gleichfalls unendlich, gesetzt als die sich auf sich beziehende Negativität; es repellirt sich von sich selbst. Aber es ist ein bestimmtes Eins, das Eins welches in Daseyn und in die Grenze übergegangen ist, also die Repulsion der Bestimmtheit von sich selbst, nicht das Erzeugen des sich selbst Gleichen, wie die Repulsion des Eins, sondern seines Andersseyns, es ist nun an ihm selbst gesetzt, über sich hinaus zu schicken, und ein Anderes zu werden. Es besteht darin, sich zu vermehren oder zu verhindern; es ist die Äußerlichkeit der Bestimmtheit an ihm selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"67.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0004","text":"Das Quantum schickt sich also selbst über sich hinaus; dieß Andere, zu dem es wird, ist zunächst selbst ein Quantum; aber ebenso als eine nicht seyende, sondern sich über sich selbst hinaustreibende Grenze. Die in diesem Hinausgehen wieder entstandene Grenze ist also schlechthin nur eine solche, die sich wieder aufhebt und zu einer fernern schickt, und so fort ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"67.4"}],"sha256":"3f9568401bdc159dd0092ad83bc54f0419fbb9b64a146867cf2d8b7dff962967","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103041032952Z_5520459c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Alteration of Quantum.","source_sha256":"3f9568401bdc159dd0092ad83bc54f0419fbb9b64a146867cf2d8b7dff962967","sha256":"b86d05087484ec411a3b805812719f321e0a1f0f964c3693e4884c6e48666d05","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:30:41.032964+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0001","text":"The difference of extensive and intensive quantum is indifferent to the determinateness of quantum as such. But quantum in general is determinateness posited as sublated, the indifferent limit, the determinateness which is just as much the negation of itself. In extensive magnitude this difference is developed, but intensive magnitude is the being-there of this externality which quantum is within itself. It is posited as its contradiction within itself, to be simple self-relating determinateness, which is the negation of itself, to have its determinateness not in itself, but in another quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"67.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0002","text":"Thus, according to its quality, a quantum is posited in absolute continuity with its externality, with its other-being. Hence not only can every determination of magnitude be gone beyond, not only can it be altered, but it is posited that it must alter itself. The determination of magnitude thus continues itself into its other-being, so that it has its being only in this continuity with another; it is not a being, but a becoming limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"67.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0003","text":"The One is infinite, or self-relating negation, hence the repulsion of itself from itself. Quantum is likewise infinite, posited as self-relating negativity; it repels itself from itself. But it is a determinate One, the One which has passed over into being-there and into limit; thus the repulsion of determinateness from itself, not the production of what is equal to itself, as is the repulsion of the One, but [the production] of its other-being; it is now posited in it itself to send itself beyond itself and to become an Other. It consists in increasing or diminishing itself; it is the externality of determinateness in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"67.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0004","text":"Thus quantum sends itself beyond itself; this Other, into which it becomes, is at first itself a quantum; but equally a limit that is not being, but drives itself beyond itself. The limit that has arisen again in this going-beyond is therefore absolutely only such a one as again sublates itself and sends itself on to a further one, and so on to infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"67.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDVN:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"828d15c18d96e0890de5207a923593afb309f3688e637fabd2117f87e44b7806","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die Veränderung des Quantums."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die Veränderung des Quantums.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD","title":"a. Concept of the Same.","order":68,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BEGD","text":"## C. Die quantitative Unendlichkeit.\n\n## a. Begriff derselben.\n\nDas Quantum verändert sich und wird ein anderes Quantum; die weitere Bestimmung dieser Veränderung, daß sie ins Unendliche fortgeht, liegt darin, daß das Quantum als an ihm selbst sich widersprechend gestellt ist.—Das Quantum wird ein Anderes; es kontinuirt sich aber in sein Andersseyn; das Andere ist also auch ein Quantum. Aber dieses ist das Andere nicht nur eines Quantums, sondern des Quantums selbst, das Negative seiner als eines Begrenzten, somit seine Unbegrenztheit, Unendlichkeit. Das Quantum ist ein Sollen; es enthält, Für-sich-bestimmt zu seyn, und dieses Für-sich-bestimmtseyn ist vielmehr das Bestimmtseyn in einem Anderen; und umgekehrt ist es das aufgehobene Bestimmtseyn in einem Andern, ist gleichgültiges Bestehen-für-sich.\n\nDie Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit erhalten dadurch sogleich jede an ihr selbst eine gedoppelte, und zwar entgegengesetzte Bedeutung. Endlich ist das Quantum erstens als Begrenztes überhaupt, zweitens, als das Hinausschicken über sich selbst, als das Bestimmtseyn in einem Anderen. Die Unendlichkeit desselben aber ist erstens sein Nichtbegrenztseyn; zweitens sein Zurückgekehrtseyn-in-sich, das gleichgültige Fürsichseyn. Vergleichen wir sogleich diese Momente mit einander, so ergiebt sich, daß die Bestimmung der Endlichkeit des Quantums, das Hinausschicken über sich zu einem Anderen, in dem seine Bestimmung liege, ebenso Bestimmung des Unendlichen ist; die Negation der Grenze ist dasselbe Hinaus über die Bestimmtheit, so daß das Quantum in dieser Negation, dem Unendlichen, seine letzte Bestimmtheit habe. Das andere Moment der Unendlichkeit ist das gegen die Grenze gleichgültige Fürsichseyn; das Quantum selbst aber ist so das Begrenzte, daß es das für sich Gleichgültige gegen seine Grenze, damit gegen andere Quanta und sein Hinaus, ist. Die Endlichkeit und die (von ihr getrennt seyn sollende, schlechte) Unendlichkeit haben beim Quantum jede das Moment der anderen bereits an ihr.\n\nDas qualitative und quantitative Unendliche unterscheiden sich dadurch, daß im ersten der Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen qualitativ ist, und der Übergang des Endlichen in das Unendliche, oder die Beziehung beider auf einander nur im Ansich, in ihrem Begriffe liegt. Die qualitative Bestimmtheit ist als unmittelbar, und bezieht sich auf das Andersseyn wesentlich als auf ein ihr anderes Seyn, sie ist nicht gesetzt, ihre Negation, ihr Anderes an ihr selbst zu haben. Die Größe hingegen ist, als solche, aufgehobene Bestimmtheit; sie ist gesetzt, ungleich mit sich und gleichgültig gegen sich selbst, daher das Veränderliche zu seyn. Das qualitative Endliche und Unendliche stehen sich daher absolut d. h. abstrakt gegeneinander über; ihre Einheit ist, die zu Grunde liegende innerliche Beziehung; das Endliche kontinuirt sich daher nur an sich, aber nicht an ihm, in sein Anderes. Hingegen das quantitative Endliche bezieht sich an ihm selbst in sein Unendliches, an dem es seine absolute Bestimmtheit habe. Diese ihre Beziehung stellt zunächst der quantitativ-unendliche Progreß dar.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0001","text":"## C. Die quantitative Unendlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"68.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0002","text":"## a. Begriff derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"68.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0003","text":"Das Quantum verändert sich und wird ein anderes Quantum; die weitere Bestimmung dieser Veränderung, daß sie ins Unendliche fortgeht, liegt darin, daß das Quantum als an ihm selbst sich widersprechend gestellt ist.—Das Quantum wird ein Anderes; es kontinuirt sich aber in sein Andersseyn; das Andere ist also auch ein Quantum. Aber dieses ist das Andere nicht nur eines Quantums, sondern des Quantums selbst, das Negative seiner als eines Begrenzten, somit seine Unbegrenztheit, Unendlichkeit. Das Quantum ist ein Sollen; es enthält, Für-sich-bestimmt zu seyn, und dieses Für-sich-bestimmtseyn ist vielmehr das Bestimmtseyn in einem Anderen; und umgekehrt ist es das aufgehobene Bestimmtseyn in einem Andern, ist gleichgültiges Bestehen-für-sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"68.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0004","text":"Die Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit erhalten dadurch sogleich jede an ihr selbst eine gedoppelte, und zwar entgegengesetzte Bedeutung. Endlich ist das Quantum erstens als Begrenztes überhaupt, zweitens, als das Hinausschicken über sich selbst, als das Bestimmtseyn in einem Anderen. Die Unendlichkeit desselben aber ist erstens sein Nichtbegrenztseyn; zweitens sein Zurückgekehrtseyn-in-sich, das gleichgültige Fürsichseyn. Vergleichen wir sogleich diese Momente mit einander, so ergiebt sich, daß die Bestimmung der Endlichkeit des Quantums, das Hinausschicken über sich zu einem Anderen, in dem seine Bestimmung liege, ebenso Bestimmung des Unendlichen ist; die Negation der Grenze ist dasselbe Hinaus über die Bestimmtheit, so daß das Quantum in dieser Negation, dem Unendlichen, seine letzte Bestimmtheit habe.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"68.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0005","text":"Das andere Moment der Unendlichkeit ist das gegen die Grenze gleichgültige Fürsichseyn; das Quantum selbst aber ist so das Begrenzte, daß es das für sich Gleichgültige gegen seine Grenze, damit gegen andere Quanta und sein Hinaus, ist. Die Endlichkeit und die (von ihr getrennt seyn sollende, schlechte) Unendlichkeit haben beim Quantum jede das Moment der anderen bereits an ihr.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"68.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0006","text":"Das qualitative und quantitative Unendliche unterscheiden sich dadurch, daß im ersten der Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen qualitativ ist, und der Übergang des Endlichen in das Unendliche, oder die Beziehung beider auf einander nur im Ansich, in ihrem Begriffe liegt. Die qualitative Bestimmtheit ist als unmittelbar, und bezieht sich auf das Andersseyn wesentlich als auf ein ihr anderes Seyn, sie ist nicht gesetzt, ihre Negation, ihr Anderes an ihr selbst zu haben. Die Größe hingegen ist, als solche, aufgehobene Bestimmtheit; sie ist gesetzt, ungleich mit sich und gleichgültig gegen sich selbst, daher das Veränderliche zu seyn. Das qualitative Endliche und Unendliche stehen sich daher absolut d. h. abstrakt gegeneinander über; ihre Einheit ist, die zu Grunde liegende innerliche Beziehung; das Endliche kontinuirt sich daher nur an sich, aber nicht an ihm, in sein Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"68.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0007","text":"Hingegen das quantitative Endliche bezieht sich an ihm selbst in sein Unendliches, an dem es seine absolute Bestimmtheit habe. Diese ihre Beziehung stellt zunächst der quantitativ-unendliche Progreß dar.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"68.7"}],"sha256":"d62aedd280379ba858c81ffe6014d590cb4d3666c9776ae0e1df0e7a85297869","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103051725335Z_c63b5787","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Concept of the Same.","source_sha256":"d62aedd280379ba858c81ffe6014d590cb4d3666c9776ae0e1df0e7a85297869","sha256":"c4b9ee5266fc06b6cdab29b4982f8e454af4469b329b2f7d4f48002fade6a6df","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:30:51.725391+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0001","text":"## C. Quantitative Infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"68.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0002","text":"## a. Its Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"68.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0003","text":"Quantum alters and becomes another quantum; the further determination of this alteration, namely that it proceeds to infinity, lies in the fact that quantum is posited as self-contradictory.—Quantum becomes an Other; but it continues into its otherness; thus the Other is also a quantum. But this is the Other not merely of a quantum, but of quantum itself, its negative as a limited [quantum], hence its unboundedness, infinity. Quantum is an ought; it contains the determination to be-for-self, and this being-determined-for-self is rather the being-determined in an Other; and conversely, it is the sublated being-determined in an Other, is indifferent subsistence-for-self.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"68.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0004","text":"Finitude and infinity thereby immediately each receive, in themselves, a twofold, and indeed opposed, meaning. Quantum is finite, first, as limited in general; second, as the sending-forth beyond itself, as being-determined in an Other. But its infinity is, first, its not-being-limited; second, its having-returned-into-itself, the indifferent being-for-self. If we at once compare these moments with one another, it emerges that the determination of the finitude of quantum, the sending-forth beyond itself to an Other in which its determination lies, is equally a determination of the infinite; the negation of the limit is the same going-beyond determinateness, so that quantum has its ultimate determinateness in this negation, the infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"68.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0005","text":"The other moment of infinity is being-for-self indifferent toward the limit; but quantum itself is thus the limited, in that it is what is for itself indifferent toward its limit, and thus toward other quanta and its going-beyond. Finitude and the infinity (which is supposed to be separated from it, bad infinity) each already have the moment of the other in them in the case of quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"68.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0006","text":"Qualitative and quantitative infinity differ in that, in the former, the opposition of finite and infinite is qualitative, and the transition of the finite into the infinite, or the relation of both to one another, lies only in itself [an sich], in their concept. Qualitative determinateness is immediate, and relates essentially to otherness as to a being other than itself; it is not posited as having its negation, its Other, in itself. Magnitude, on the other hand, as such, is sublated determinateness; it is posited as unequal to itself and indifferent toward itself, hence as being the alterable. Qualitative finite and infinite therefore stand absolutely, i.e. abstractly, opposed to one another; their unity is the underlying inner relation; the finite therefore continues only in itself, but not in it, into its Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"68.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0007","text":"By contrast, the quantitative finite relates, in itself, to its infinite, in which it has its absolute determinateness. This relation of theirs is initially exhibited by quantitative infinite progress.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"68.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BEGD:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"5dc9a0ce1923696edb8d90aeee4ee588624d227cbc578ec03c46174900f655e6","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Begriff derselben."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Begriff derselben.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU","title":"b. The Quantitative Infinite Progress.","order":69,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDQU","text":"Der Progreß ins Unendliche ist überhaupt der Ausdruck des Widerspruchs, hier desjenigen, den das quantitativ-Endliche oder das Quantum überhaupt enthält. Er ist die Wechselbestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen, die in der qualitativen Sphäre betrachtet worden ist, mit dem Unterschiede, daß wie so eben erinnert, im Quantitativen sich die Grenze an ihr selbst in ihr Jenseits fortschickt und fortsetzt, somit umgekehrt auch das quantitativ-Unendliche gesetzt ist, das Quantum an ihm selbst zu haben, denn das Quantum ist in seinem Außersichseyn zugleich es selbst; seine Äußerlichkeit gehört seiner Bestimmung an.\n\nDer unendliche Progreß ist nun nur der Ausdruck dieses Widerspruchs, nicht die Auflösung desselben, aber um der Kontinuität willen der einen Bestimmtheit in ihre andere führt er eine scheinbare Auflösung in einer Vereinigung beider herbei. Wie er zunächst gesetzt ist, ist er die Aufgabe des Unendlichen, nicht die Erreichung desselben; das perennirende Erzeugen desselben, ohne über das Quantum selbst hinauszukommen, und ohne daß das Unendliche ein Positives und Gegenwärtiges würde. Das Quantum hat es in seinem Begriffe ein Jenseits seiner zu haben. Dieß Jenseits ist erstlich das abstrakte Moment des Nichtseyns des Quantums; dieses löst sich an sich selbst auf; so bezieht es sich auf sein Jenseits als auf seine Unendlichkeit, nach dem qualitativen Momente des Gegensatzes. Aber zweitens steht das Quantum in Kontinuität mit diesem Jenseits; das Quantum besteht eben darin, das Andere seiner selbst, sich selbst äußerlich zu seyn; also ist dieß Äußerliche eben so sehr nicht ein Anderes als das Quantum; das Jenseits oder das Unendliche ist also selbst ein Quantum. Das Jenseits ist auf diese Weise aus seiner Flucht zurückgerufen, und das Unendliche erreicht. Aber weil dieß zum Diesseits gewordene wieder ein Quantum ist, ist nur wieder eine neue Grenze gesetzt worden; diese, als Quantum, ist auch wieder von sich selbst geflohen, ist als solches über sich hinaus, und hat sich in sein Nichtseyn, in sein Jenseits von sich selbst repellirt, das ebenso perennirend zum Quantum wird, als dieses sich von sich selbst zum Jenseits abstößt.\n\nDie Kontinuität des Quantums in sein Anderes bringt die Verbindung beider in dem Ausdruck eines Unendlich-Großen oder Unendlich-Kleinen hervor. Da beide die Bestimmung des Quantums noch an ihnen haben, bleiben sie veränderliche und die absolute Bestimmtheit, die ein Für-sichseyn wäre, ist also nicht erreicht. Dieß Außersichseyn der Bestimmung ist in dem gedoppelten Unendlichen, das sich nach dem Mehr und Weniger entgegengesetzt ist, dem Unendlich-großen und Kleinen, gesetzt. An jedem selbst ist das Quantum im perennirenden Gegensatze gegen sein Jenseits erhalten. Das Große noch so sehr erweitert, schwindet zur Unbeträchtlichkeit zusammen; indem es sich auf das Unendliche als auf sein Nichtseyn bezieht, ist der Gegensatz qualitativ; das erweiterte Quantum hat daher dem Unendlichen nichts abgewonnen; dieses ist vor wie nach das Nichtseyn desselben. Oder, die Vergrößerung des Quantums ist keine Näherung zum Unendlichen, denn der Unterschied des Quantums und seiner Unendlichkeit hat wesentlich auch das Moment ein nicht quantitativer Unterschied zu seyn. Es ist nur der ins Engere gebrachte Ausdruck des Widerspruchs; es soll ein Großes d. i. ein Quantum, und unendlich, d. i. kein Quantum seyn.—Eben so das Unendlichkleine ist als Kleines ein Quantum und bleibt daher absolut d. h. qualitativ zu groß für das Unendliche, und ist diesem entgegengesetzt. Es bleibt in beiden der Widerspruch des unendlichen Progresses erhalten der in ihnen sein Ziel gefunden haben sollte.\n\nDiese Unendlichkeit, welche als das Jenseits des Endlichen beharrlich bestimmt ist, ist als die schlechte quantitative Unendlichkeit zu bezeichnen. Sie ist wie die qualitative schlechte Unendlichkeit, das perennirende Herüber- und Hinübergehen von dem einen Gliede des bleibenden Widerspruchs zum andern, von der Grenze zu ihrem Nichtseyn, von diesem aufs neue zurück zu ebenderselben, zur Grenze. Im Progresse des Quantitativen ist das, zu dem fortgegangen wird, zwar nicht ein abstrakt Anderes überhaupt, sondern ein als verschieden gesetztes Quantum; aber es bleibt auf gleiche Weise im Gegensatze gegen seine Negation. Der Progreß ist daher gleichfalls nicht ein Fortgehen und Weiterkommen, sondern ein Wiederholen von einem und eben demselben, Setzen, Aufheben, und Wiedersetzen und Wiederaufheben; eine Ohnmacht des Negativen, dem das, was es aufhebt, durch sein Aufheben selbst als ein Kontinuirliches wiederkehrt. Es sind zwei so zusammengeknüpft, daß sie sich schlechthin fliehen; und indem sie sich fliehen, können sie sich nicht trennen, sondern sind in ihrer gegenseitigen Flucht verknüpft.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0001","text":"Der Progreß ins Unendliche ist überhaupt der Ausdruck des Widerspruchs, hier desjenigen, den das quantitativ-Endliche oder das Quantum überhaupt enthält. Er ist die Wechselbestimmung des Endlichen und Unendlichen, die in der qualitativen Sphäre betrachtet worden ist, mit dem Unterschiede, daß wie so eben erinnert, im Quantitativen sich die Grenze an ihr selbst in ihr Jenseits fortschickt und fortsetzt, somit umgekehrt auch das quantitativ-Unendliche gesetzt ist, das Quantum an ihm selbst zu haben, denn das Quantum ist in seinem Außersichseyn zugleich es selbst; seine Äußerlichkeit gehört seiner Bestimmung an.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"69.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0002","text":"Der unendliche Progreß ist nun nur der Ausdruck dieses Widerspruchs, nicht die Auflösung desselben, aber um der Kontinuität willen der einen Bestimmtheit in ihre andere führt er eine scheinbare Auflösung in einer Vereinigung beider herbei. Wie er zunächst gesetzt ist, ist er die Aufgabe des Unendlichen, nicht die Erreichung desselben; das perennirende Erzeugen desselben, ohne über das Quantum selbst hinauszukommen, und ohne daß das Unendliche ein Positives und Gegenwärtiges würde. Das Quantum hat es in seinem Begriffe ein Jenseits seiner zu haben. Dieß Jenseits ist erstlich das abstrakte Moment des Nichtseyns des Quantums; dieses löst sich an sich selbst auf; so bezieht es sich auf sein Jenseits als auf seine Unendlichkeit, nach dem qualitativen Momente des Gegensatzes.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"69.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0003","text":"Aber zweitens steht das Quantum in Kontinuität mit diesem Jenseits; das Quantum besteht eben darin, das Andere seiner selbst, sich selbst äußerlich zu seyn; also ist dieß Äußerliche eben so sehr nicht ein Anderes als das Quantum; das Jenseits oder das Unendliche ist also selbst ein Quantum. Das Jenseits ist auf diese Weise aus seiner Flucht zurückgerufen, und das Unendliche erreicht. Aber weil dieß zum Diesseits gewordene wieder ein Quantum ist, ist nur wieder eine neue Grenze gesetzt worden; diese, als Quantum, ist auch wieder von sich selbst geflohen, ist als solches über sich hinaus, und hat sich in sein Nichtseyn, in sein Jenseits von sich selbst repellirt, das ebenso perennirend zum Quantum wird, als dieses sich von sich selbst zum Jenseits abstößt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"69.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0004","text":"Die Kontinuität des Quantums in sein Anderes bringt die Verbindung beider in dem Ausdruck eines Unendlich-Großen oder Unendlich-Kleinen hervor. Da beide die Bestimmung des Quantums noch an ihnen haben, bleiben sie veränderliche und die absolute Bestimmtheit, die ein Für-sichseyn wäre, ist also nicht erreicht. Dieß Außersichseyn der Bestimmung ist in dem gedoppelten Unendlichen, das sich nach dem Mehr und Weniger entgegengesetzt ist, dem Unendlich-großen und Kleinen, gesetzt. An jedem selbst ist das Quantum im perennirenden Gegensatze gegen sein Jenseits erhalten. Das Große noch so sehr erweitert, schwindet zur Unbeträchtlichkeit zusammen; indem es sich auf das Unendliche als auf sein Nichtseyn bezieht, ist der Gegensatz qualitativ; das erweiterte Quantum hat daher dem Unendlichen nichts abgewonnen; dieses ist vor wie nach das Nichtseyn desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"69.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0005","text":"Oder, die Vergrößerung des Quantums ist keine Näherung zum Unendlichen, denn der Unterschied des Quantums und seiner Unendlichkeit hat wesentlich auch das Moment ein nicht quantitativer Unterschied zu seyn. Es ist nur der ins Engere gebrachte Ausdruck des Widerspruchs; es soll ein Großes d. i. ein Quantum, und unendlich, d. i. kein Quantum seyn.—Eben so das Unendlichkleine ist als Kleines ein Quantum und bleibt daher absolut d. h. qualitativ zu groß für das Unendliche, und ist diesem entgegengesetzt. Es bleibt in beiden der Widerspruch des unendlichen Progresses erhalten der in ihnen sein Ziel gefunden haben sollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"69.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0006","text":"Diese Unendlichkeit, welche als das Jenseits des Endlichen beharrlich bestimmt ist, ist als die schlechte quantitative Unendlichkeit zu bezeichnen. Sie ist wie die qualitative schlechte Unendlichkeit, das perennirende Herüber- und Hinübergehen von dem einen Gliede des bleibenden Widerspruchs zum andern, von der Grenze zu ihrem Nichtseyn, von diesem aufs neue zurück zu ebenderselben, zur Grenze. Im Progresse des Quantitativen ist das, zu dem fortgegangen wird, zwar nicht ein abstrakt Anderes überhaupt, sondern ein als verschieden gesetztes Quantum; aber es bleibt auf gleiche Weise im Gegensatze gegen seine Negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"69.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0007","text":"Der Progreß ist daher gleichfalls nicht ein Fortgehen und Weiterkommen, sondern ein Wiederholen von einem und eben demselben, Setzen, Aufheben, und Wiedersetzen und Wiederaufheben; eine Ohnmacht des Negativen, dem das, was es aufhebt, durch sein Aufheben selbst als ein Kontinuirliches wiederkehrt. Es sind zwei so zusammengeknüpft, daß sie sich schlechthin fliehen; und indem sie sich fliehen, können sie sich nicht trennen, sondern sind in ihrer gegenseitigen Flucht verknüpft.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"69.7"}],"sha256":"224321a002414d9d0a9d6b6b200fa3b380a1423fbaf88e8476e78593893e1cc6","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103101851694Z_37ed6360","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The Quantitative Infinite Progress.","source_sha256":"224321a002414d9d0a9d6b6b200fa3b380a1423fbaf88e8476e78593893e1cc6","sha256":"5e341fb5ddd95fef5e94d21dba4a5a23d36681f7d5fdcbdd1b8e9c6db28fa972","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:31:01.851736+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0001","text":"Progress into infinity is in general the expression of contradiction, here of that which the quantitatively finite, or quantum in general, contains. It is the alternating determination of the finite and the infinite that has been considered in the qualitative sphere, with the difference that, as has just been recalled, in the quantitative sphere the limit propels and continues itself, in itself, into its beyond; thus, conversely, the quantitatively infinite is also posited to have quantum within itself, for quantum, in its being-outside-itself, is at the same time itself; its externality belongs to its determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"69.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0002","text":"Infinite progress is now only the expression of this contradiction, not its resolution; but, on account of the continuity of the one determinacy into its other, it brings about an apparent resolution in a union of both. As it is initially posited, it is the task of the infinite, not its attainment; the perennial production of it, without getting beyond quantum itself, and without the infinite becoming something positive and present. Quantum has it in its Concept to have a beyond of itself. This beyond is, first, the abstract moment of the non-being of quantum; the latter dissolves itself in itself; thus it relates to its beyond as to its infinity, according to the qualitative moment of opposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"69.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0003","text":"But secondly, quantum stands in continuity with this beyond; quantum consists precisely in being the other of itself, in being external to itself; thus this external is just as much not an other than quantum; the beyond, or the infinite, is therefore itself a quantum. In this way the beyond is recalled from its flight, and the infinite attained. But since this which has become a here is again a quantum, only a new limit has again been posited; this, as quantum, has likewise again fled from itself, is as such beyond itself, and has repelled itself into its non-being, into its beyond of itself, which perennially becomes quantum just as quantum repels itself from itself into the beyond.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"69.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0004","text":"The continuity of quantum into its other produces the connection of both in the expression of an infinitely large or infinitely small. Since both still have the determination of quantum in them, they remain changeable, and absolute determinacy, which would be a being-for-self, is therefore not attained. This being-outside-itself of determination is posited in the doubled infinite, which is opposed to itself according to more and less, the infinitely large and the infinitely small. In each by itself, quantum is preserved in perpetual opposition to its beyond. However greatly the large is expanded, it contracts into insignificance; in relating itself to the infinite as to its non-being, the opposition is qualitative; the expanded quantum has therefore gained nothing from the infinite; this is, as before, its non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"69.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0005","text":"Or, the enlargement of quantum is no approximation to the infinite, for the difference of quantum and its infinity essentially also has the moment of being a non-quantitative difference. It is only the expression of contradiction brought into narrower compass; there is supposed to be a large, i.e. a quantum, and infinite, i.e. no quantum.—Likewise, the infinitely small, as small, is a quantum and therefore remains absolutely, i.e. qualitatively, too large for the infinite, and is opposed to it. In both, the contradiction of infinite progress remains preserved, which ought to have found its goal in them.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"69.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0006","text":"This infinity, which is persistently determined as the beyond of the finite, is to be designated as bad quantitative infinity. Like bad qualitative infinity, it is the perennial passing-over and passing-back from one member of the enduring contradiction to the other, from the limit to its non-being, and from this anew back to that very same thing, to the limit. In the progress of the quantitative, that to which progress is made is indeed not an abstract other in general, but a quantum posited as distinct; yet it remains in the same way in opposition to its negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"69.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0007","text":"Progress is therefore likewise not a going forward and an advance, but a repetition of one and the same thing: positing, sublating, and re-positing and re-sublating; an impotence of the negative, to which that which it sublates returns through its sublation itself as a continuous. Two are thus conjoined in such a way that they absolutely flee one another; and in fleeing one another they cannot separate themselves, but are bound together in their mutual flight.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"69.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDQU:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"81c352ef4479ef0964d94c26a089768e61ea26b411ffea43a9a05ae4ead263c2","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Der quantitative unendliche Progreß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Der quantitative unendliche Progreß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18","title":"Remark 1.","order":70,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_18","text":"Die schlechte Unendlichkeit pflegt vornehmlich in der Form des Progresses des Quantitativen ins Unendliche,—dieß fortgehende Überfliegen der Grenze, das die Ohnmacht ist, sie aufzuheben, und der perennirende Rückfall in dieselbe,—für etwas Erhabenes und für eine Art von Gottesdienst gehalten zu werden, so wie derselbe in der Philosophie als ein Letztes angesehen worden ist. Dieser Progreß hat vielfach zu Tiraden gedient, die als erhabene Produktionen bewundert worden sind. In der That aber macht diese moderne Erhabenheit nicht den Gegenstand groß, welcher vielmehr entflieht, sondern nur das Subjekt, das so große Quantitäten in sich verschlingt. Die Dürftigkeit dieser subjektiv bleibenden Erhebung, die an der Leiter des Quantitativen hinaufsteigt, thut sich selbst damit kund, daß sie in vergeblicher Arbeit dem unendlichen Ziele nicht näher zu kommen eingesteht, welches zu erreichen freilich ganz anders anzugreifen ist.\n\nBei folgenden Tiraden dieser Art ist zugleich ausgedrückt, in was solche Erhebung übergeht und aufhört. Kant z.B. führt es als erhaben auf, (Kr. d. prakt. V. Schl.)\n\n\"wenn das Subjekt mit dem Gedanken sich über den Platz erhebt, den es in der Sinnenwelt einnimmt, und die Verknüpfung ins unendlich Große erweitert, eine Verknüpfung mit Sternen über Sternen, mit Welten über Welten, Systemen über Systemen, überdem noch in grenzenlose Zeiten ihrer periodischen Bewegung, deren Anfang und Fortdauer.—Das Vorstellen erliegt diesem Fortgehen ins Unermeßlich-Ferne, wo die fernste Welt immer noch eine fernere hat, die so weit zurückgeführte Vergangenheit noch eine weitere hinter sich, die noch so weit hinausgeführte Zukunft immer noch eine andere vor sich; der Gedanke erliegt dieser Vorstellung des Unermeßlichen; wie ein Traum, daß einer einen langen Gang immer weiter und unabsehbar weiter fortgehe, ohne ein Ende abzusehen, mit Fallen oder mit Schwindel endet.\"\n\nDiese Darstellung, außerdem daß sie den Inhalt des quantitativen Erhebens in einen Reichthum der Schilderung zusammendrängt, verdient wegen der Wahrhaftigkeit vornehmlich Lob, mit der sie es angiebt, wie es dieser Erhebung am Ende ergeht: der Gedanke erliegt, das Ende ist Fallen und Schwindel. Was den Gedanken erliegen macht, und das Fallen desselben und den Schwindel hervorbringt, ist nichts anderes, als die Langeweile der Wiederholung, welche eine Grenze verschwinden und wieder auftreten und wieder verschwinden, so immer das eine um das andere, und eins im andern, in dem Jenseits das Diesseits, in dem Diesseits das Jenseits perennierend entstehen und vergehen läßt, und nur das Gefühl der Ohnmacht dieses Unendlichen oder dieses Sollens giebt, das über das Endliche Meister werden will und nicht kann.\n\nAuch die hallersche, von Kant sogenannte schauderhafte Beschreibung der Ewigkeit pflegt besonders bewundert zu werden, aber oft gerade nicht wegen derjenigen Seite, die das wahrhafte Verdienst derselben ausmacht:\n\n\"Ich häuffe ungeheure Zahlen, Gebürge Millionen auf, Ich setze Zeit auf Zeit, und Welt auf Welt zu Hauf Und wenn ich von der grausen Höh Mit Schwindeln wieder nach dir seh, Ist alle Macht der Zahl, vermehrt zu tausendmalen, Noch nicht ein Theil von dir.\" \"Ich zieh sie ab, und du liegst ganz vor mir.\"\n\nWenn auf jenes Aufbürgen und Aufthürmen von Zahlen und Welten als auf eine Beschreibung der Ewigkeit der Werth gelegt wird, so wird übersehen, daß der Dichter selbst dieses sogenannte schauderhafte Hinausgehen für etwas Vergebliches und Hohles erklärt, und daß er damit schließt, daß nur durch das Aufgeben dieses leeren unendlichen Progresses das wahrhafte Unendliche selbst zur Gegenwart vor ihn komme.\n\nEs hat Astronomen gegeben, die sich auf das Erhabene ihrer Wissenschaft gern darum viel zu Gute thaten, weil sie mit einer unermeßlichen Menge von Sternen, mit so unermeßlichen Räumen und Zeiten zu thun habe, in denen Entfernungen und Perioden, die für sich schon groß sind, zu Einheiten dienen, welche noch so vielmal genommen, sich wieder zur Unbedeutenheit verkürzen. Das schaale Erstaunen, dem sie sich dabei überlassen, die abgeschmackten Hoffnungen, erst noch in jenem Leben von einem Sterne zum anderen zu reisen und ins Unermeßliche fort dergleichen neue Kenntnisse zu erwerben, gaben sie für ein Hauptmoment der Vortreflichkeit ihrer Wissenschaft aus, —welche bewundernswürdig ist, nicht um solcher quantitativen Unendlichkeit willen, sondern im Gegentheil um der Maaßverhältnisse und der Gesetze willen, welche die Vernunft in diesen Gegenständen erkennt, und die das vernünftige Unendliche gegen jene unvernünftige Unendlichkeit sind.\n\nDer Unendlichkeit, die sich auf die äußere sinnliche Anschauung bezieht, setzt Kant die andere Unendlichkeit gegenüber, wenn\n\n\"das Individuum auf sein unsichtbares Ich zurückgeht, und die absolute Freiheit seines Willens als ein reines Ich allen Schrecken des Schicksals und der Thyrannei entgegenstellt, von seinen nächsten Umgebungen anfangend, sie für sich verschwinden, eben so das, was als dauernd erscheint, Welten über Welten in Trümmer zusammenstürzen läßt, und einsam sich als sich selbst gleich erkennt.\"\n\nIch in dieser Einsamkeit mit sich ist zwar das erreichte Jenseits, es ist zu sich selbst gekommen, ist bei sich, diesseits; im reinen Selbstbewußtseyn ist die absolute Negativität zur Affirmation und Gegenwart gebracht, welche in jenem Fortgehen über das sinnliche Quantum nur flieht. Aber indem dieß reine Ich in seiner Abstraktion und Inhaltslosigkeit sich fixirt, hat es das Daseyn überhaupt, die Fülle des natürlichen und geistigen Universums, als ein Jenseits sich gegenüber. Es stellt sich derselbe Widerspruch dar, der dem unendlichen Progresse zu Grunde liegt; nämlich ein Zurückgekehrtseyn in sich, das unmittelbar zugleich Außersichseyn, Beziehung auf sein Anderes als auf sein Nichtseyn, ist; welche Beziehung eine Sehnsucht bleibt, weil Ich sich seine gehaltlose und unhaltbare Leere einer Seits, und die in der Negation doch präsent bleibende Fülle als sein Jenseits fixirt hat.\n\nKant fügt diesen beiden Erhabenheiten die Bemerkung bei, \"daß Bewunderung (für die erstere, äußerliche) und Achtung (für die zweite, innerliche) Erhabenheit, zwar zur Nachforschung reizen, aber den Mangel derselben nicht ersetzen können\".—Er erklärt damit jene Erhebungen als unbefriedigend für die Vernunft, welche bei ihnen und den damit verbundenen Empfindungen nicht stehen bleiben, und das Jenseits und Leere nicht für das Letzte gelten lassen kann.\n\nAls ein Letztes aber ist der unendliche Progreß vornehmlich in seiner Anwendung auf die Moralität genommen worden. Der so eben angeführte zweite Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen, als der mannigfaltigen Welt und des in seine Freiheit erhobenen Ichs, ist zunächst qualitativ. Das Selbstbestimmen des Ich geht zugleich darauf, die Natur zu bestimmen und sich von ihr zu befreien; so bezieht es sich durch sich selbst auf sein Anderes, welches als äußerliches Daseyn ein Vielfältiges und auch Quantitatives ist. Die Beziehung auf ein Quantitatives wird selbst quantitativ; die negative Beziehung des Ich darauf, die Macht des Ich über das Nicht-Ich, über die Sinnlichkeit und äußere Natur, wird daher so vorgestellt, daß die Moralität immer größer, die Macht der Sinnlichkeit aber immer kleiner werden könne und solle. Die völlige Angemessenheit aber des Willens zum moralischen Gesetze wird in den ins Unendliche gehenden Progreß verlegt, das heißt, als ein absolutes unerreichbares Jenseits vorgestellt, und eben dieß solle der wahre Anker und der rechte Trost seyn, daß es ein Unerreichbares ist; denn die Moralität soll als Kampf seyn; dieser aber ist nur unter der Unangemessenheit des Willens zum Gesetze, dieses damit schlechthin ein Jenseits für ihn.\n\nIn diesem Gegensatze werden Ich und Nicht-Ich oder der reine Wille und das moralische Gesetz, und die Natur und Sinnlichkeit des Willens als vollkommen selbstständig und gleichgültig gegeneinander vorausgesetzt. Der reine Wille hat sein eigenthümliches Gesetz, das in wesentlicher Beziehung auf die Sinnlichkeit steht; und die Natur und Sinnlichkeit hat ihrer Seits Gesetze, die weder aus dem Willen genommen und ihm entsprechend sind, noch auch nur, wenn gleich verschieden davon, an sich eine wesentliche Beziehung auf ihn hätten, sondern sie sind überhaupt für sich bestimmt, in sich fertig und geschlossen. Zugleich sind beide aber Momente eines und desselben einfachen Wesens, des Ich; der Wille ist als das Negative gegen die Natur bestimmt, so daß er nur ist, insofern ein solches von ihm verschiedenes ist, das von ihm aufgehoben werde, von dem er aber hierin berührt und selbst afficirt ist. Der Natur und ihr als Sinnlichkeit des Menschen ist als einem selbstständigen System von Gesetzen das Beschränken durch ein anderes gleichgültig; sie erhält sich in diesem Begrenztwerden, tritt selbstständig in die Beziehung ein, und begrenzt den Willen des Gesetzes eben so sehr, als er sie begrenzt.—Es ist Ein Act, daß der Wille sich bestimmt und das Andersseyn einer Natur aufhebt, und daß dieß Andersseyn als daseyend gesetzt ist, sich in sein Aufgehobenwerden kontinuirt, und nicht aufgehoben ist. Der Widerspruch, der hierin liegt, wird im unendlichen Progresse nicht aufgelöst, sondern im Gegentheil als unaufgelöst und unauflösbar dargestellt und behauptet; der Kampf der Moralität und der Sinnlichkeit wird vorgestellt, als das an und für sich seyende, absolute Verhältniß.\n\nDie Ohnmacht über den qualitativen Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen Meister zu werden und die Idee des wahrhaften Willens, die substantielle Freiheit, zu fassen, nimmt zur Größe ihre Zuflucht, um sie als die Mittlerin zu gebrauchen, weil sie das aufgehobene Qualitative, der gleichgültig gewordene Unterschied, ist. Allein indem beide Glieder des Gegensatzes als qualitativ verschieden zu Grunde liegen bleiben, so wird vielmehr dadurch, daß sie sich in ihrer gegenseitigen Beziehung als Quanta verhalten, jedes sogleich als gegen diese Veränderung gleichgültig gesetzt. Die Natur wird durch Ich, die Sinnlichkeit durch den Willen des Guten bestimmt, die durch denselben an ihr hervorgebrachte Veränderung ist nur ein quantitativer Unterschied, ein solcher, der sie als das bestehen läßt, was sie ist.\n\nIn der abstraktern Darstellung der kantischen Philosophie oder wenigstens ihrer Principien, nämlich in der fichteschen Wissenschaftslehre, macht der unendliche Progreß auf dieselbe Weise die Grundlage und das Letzte aus. Auf den ersten Grundsatz dieser Darstellung, Ich=Ich, folgt ein zweiter davon unabhängiger, die Entgegensetzung des Nicht-Ich; die Beziehung beider wird sogleich auch als quantitativer Unterschied angenommen, daß Nicht-Ich zum Theil durch Ich bestimmt werde, zum Theil auch nicht. Das Nicht-Ich kontinuirt sich auf diese Weise in sein Nichtseyn so, daß es seinem Nichtseyn entgegengesetzt bleibt, als ein nicht Aufgehobenes. Nachdem daher die Widersprüche, die darin liegen, im System entwickelt worden sind, so ist das schließliche Resultat dasjenige Verhältniß, welches der Anfang war; das Nicht-Ich bleibt ein unendlicher Anstoß, ein absolut-Anderes; die letzte Beziehung seiner und des Ich aufeinander ist der unendliche Progreß, Sehnsucht und Streben,—derselbe Widerspruch, mit welchem angefangen wurde.\n\nWeil das Quantitative die als aufgehoben gesetzte Bestimmtheit ist, so glaubte man für die Einheit des Absoluten, für die Eine Substantialität, Viel oder vielmehr Alles gewonnen zu haben, indem man den Gegensatz überhaupt zu einem nur quantitativen Unterschiede herabsetzte. Aller Gegensatz ist nur quantitativ, war einige Zeit ein Hauptsatz neuerer Philosophie; die entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen haben dasselbe Wesen, denselben Inhalt, sie sind reale Seiten des Gegensatzes, insofern jede derselben seine beiden Bestimmungen, beide Faktoren, in ihr hat, nur daß auf der einen Seite der eine Faktor, auf der anderen der andere überwiegend, in der einen Seite der eine Faktor, eine Materie oder Thätigkeit, in größerer Menge oder in stärkerem Grade vorhanden sey, als in der andern. Insofern verschiedene Stoffe oder Thätigkeiten vorausgesetzt werden, bestätigt und vollendet der quantitative Unterschied vielmehr deren Äußerlichkeit und Gleichgültigkeit gegeneinander und gegen ihre Einheit. Der Unterschied der absoluten Einheit soll nur quantitativ seyn; das Quantitative ist zwar die aufgehobene unmittelbare Bestimmtheit, aber die nur unvollkommene, erst die erste Negation, nicht die unendliche, nicht die Negation der Negation.—Indem Seyn und Denken als quantitative Bestimmungen der absoluten Substanz vorgestellt werden, werden auch sie, als Quanta, wie in untergeordneter Sphäre, der Kohlenstoff, Stickstoff u.s.f. sich vollkommen äußerlich und beziehungslos. Es ist ein Drittes, eine äußerliche Reflexion, welche von ihrem Unterschiede abstrahirt, und ihre innere, nur ansichseyende, nicht ebenso für-sich-seyende, Einheit erkennt. Diese Einheit, wird dann in der That nur als erste unmittelbare vorgestellt, oder nur als Seyn, welches in seinem quantitativen Unterschiede sich gleich bleibt, aber nicht sich durch sich selbst gleich setzt; es ist somit nicht begriffen, als Negation der Negation, als unendliche Einheit. Nur im qualitativen Gegensatze geht die gesetzte Unendlichkeit, das Fürsichseyn, hervor, und die quantitative Bestimmung selbst geht, wie sich sogleich näher ergeben wird, in das Qualitative über.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0001","text":"Die schlechte Unendlichkeit pflegt vornehmlich in der Form des Progresses des Quantitativen ins Unendliche,—dieß fortgehende Überfliegen der Grenze, das die Ohnmacht ist, sie aufzuheben, und der perennirende Rückfall in dieselbe,—für etwas Erhabenes und für eine Art von Gottesdienst gehalten zu werden, so wie derselbe in der Philosophie als ein Letztes angesehen worden ist. Dieser Progreß hat vielfach zu Tiraden gedient, die als erhabene Produktionen bewundert worden sind. In der That aber macht diese moderne Erhabenheit nicht den Gegenstand groß, welcher vielmehr entflieht, sondern nur das Subjekt, das so große Quantitäten in sich verschlingt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"70.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0002","text":"Die Dürftigkeit dieser subjektiv bleibenden Erhebung, die an der Leiter des Quantitativen hinaufsteigt, thut sich selbst damit kund, daß sie in vergeblicher Arbeit dem unendlichen Ziele nicht näher zu kommen eingesteht, welches zu erreichen freilich ganz anders anzugreifen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"70.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0003","text":"Bei folgenden Tiraden dieser Art ist zugleich ausgedrückt, in was solche Erhebung übergeht und aufhört. Kant z.B. führt es als erhaben auf, (Kr. d. prakt. V. Schl.)","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"70.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0004","text":"\"wenn das Subjekt mit dem Gedanken sich über den Platz erhebt, den es in der Sinnenwelt einnimmt, und die Verknüpfung ins unendlich Große erweitert, eine Verknüpfung mit Sternen über Sternen, mit Welten über Welten, Systemen über Systemen, überdem noch in grenzenlose Zeiten ihrer periodischen Bewegung, deren Anfang und Fortdauer.—Das Vorstellen erliegt diesem Fortgehen ins Unermeßlich-Ferne, wo die fernste Welt immer noch eine fernere hat, die so weit zurückgeführte Vergangenheit noch eine weitere hinter sich, die noch so weit hinausgeführte Zukunft immer noch eine andere vor sich; der Gedanke erliegt dieser Vorstellung des Unermeßlichen; wie ein Traum, daß einer einen langen Gang immer weiter und unabsehbar weiter fortgehe, ohne ein Ende abzusehen, mit Fallen oder mit Schwindel endet.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"70.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0005","text":"Diese Darstellung, außerdem daß sie den Inhalt des quantitativen Erhebens in einen Reichthum der Schilderung zusammendrängt, verdient wegen der Wahrhaftigkeit vornehmlich Lob, mit der sie es angiebt, wie es dieser Erhebung am Ende ergeht: der Gedanke erliegt, das Ende ist Fallen und Schwindel. Was den Gedanken erliegen macht, und das Fallen desselben und den Schwindel hervorbringt, ist nichts anderes, als die Langeweile der Wiederholung, welche eine Grenze verschwinden und wieder auftreten und wieder verschwinden, so immer das eine um das andere, und eins im andern, in dem Jenseits das Diesseits, in dem Diesseits das Jenseits perennierend entstehen und vergehen läßt, und nur das Gefühl der Ohnmacht dieses Unendlichen oder dieses Sollens giebt, das über das Endliche Meister werden will und nicht kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"70.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0006","text":"Auch die hallersche, von Kant sogenannte schauderhafte Beschreibung der Ewigkeit pflegt besonders bewundert zu werden, aber oft gerade nicht wegen derjenigen Seite, die das wahrhafte Verdienst derselben ausmacht:","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"70.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0007","text":"\"Ich häuffe ungeheure Zahlen, Gebürge Millionen auf, Ich setze Zeit auf Zeit, und Welt auf Welt zu Hauf Und wenn ich von der grausen Höh Mit Schwindeln wieder nach dir seh, Ist alle Macht der Zahl, vermehrt zu tausendmalen, Noch nicht ein Theil von dir.\" \"Ich zieh sie ab, und du liegst ganz vor mir.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"70.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0008","text":"Wenn auf jenes Aufbürgen und Aufthürmen von Zahlen und Welten als auf eine Beschreibung der Ewigkeit der Werth gelegt wird, so wird übersehen, daß der Dichter selbst dieses sogenannte schauderhafte Hinausgehen für etwas Vergebliches und Hohles erklärt, und daß er damit schließt, daß nur durch das Aufgeben dieses leeren unendlichen Progresses das wahrhafte Unendliche selbst zur Gegenwart vor ihn komme.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"70.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0009","text":"Es hat Astronomen gegeben, die sich auf das Erhabene ihrer Wissenschaft gern darum viel zu Gute thaten, weil sie mit einer unermeßlichen Menge von Sternen, mit so unermeßlichen Räumen und Zeiten zu thun habe, in denen Entfernungen und Perioden, die für sich schon groß sind, zu Einheiten dienen, welche noch so vielmal genommen, sich wieder zur Unbedeutenheit verkürzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"70.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0010","text":"Das schaale Erstaunen, dem sie sich dabei überlassen, die abgeschmackten Hoffnungen, erst noch in jenem Leben von einem Sterne zum anderen zu reisen und ins Unermeßliche fort dergleichen neue Kenntnisse zu erwerben, gaben sie für ein Hauptmoment der Vortreflichkeit ihrer Wissenschaft aus, —welche bewundernswürdig ist, nicht um solcher quantitativen Unendlichkeit willen, sondern im Gegentheil um der Maaßverhältnisse und der Gesetze willen, welche die Vernunft in diesen Gegenständen erkennt, und die das vernünftige Unendliche gegen jene unvernünftige Unendlichkeit sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"70.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0011","text":"Der Unendlichkeit, die sich auf die äußere sinnliche Anschauung bezieht, setzt Kant die andere Unendlichkeit gegenüber, wenn","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"70.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0012","text":"\"das Individuum auf sein unsichtbares Ich zurückgeht, und die absolute Freiheit seines Willens als ein reines Ich allen Schrecken des Schicksals und der Thyrannei entgegenstellt, von seinen nächsten Umgebungen anfangend, sie für sich verschwinden, eben so das, was als dauernd erscheint, Welten über Welten in Trümmer zusammenstürzen läßt, und einsam sich als sich selbst gleich erkennt.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"70.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0013","text":"Ich in dieser Einsamkeit mit sich ist zwar das erreichte Jenseits, es ist zu sich selbst gekommen, ist bei sich, diesseits; im reinen Selbstbewußtseyn ist die absolute Negativität zur Affirmation und Gegenwart gebracht, welche in jenem Fortgehen über das sinnliche Quantum nur flieht. Aber indem dieß reine Ich in seiner Abstraktion und Inhaltslosigkeit sich fixirt, hat es das Daseyn überhaupt, die Fülle des natürlichen und geistigen Universums, als ein Jenseits sich gegenüber. Es stellt sich derselbe Widerspruch dar, der dem unendlichen Progresse zu Grunde liegt; nämlich ein Zurückgekehrtseyn in sich, das unmittelbar zugleich Außersichseyn, Beziehung auf sein Anderes als auf sein Nichtseyn, ist; welche Beziehung eine Sehnsucht bleibt, weil Ich sich seine gehaltlose und unhaltbare Leere einer Seits, und die in der Negation doch präsent bleibende Fülle als sein Jenseits fixirt hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"70.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0014","text":"Kant fügt diesen beiden Erhabenheiten die Bemerkung bei, \"daß Bewunderung (für die erstere, äußerliche) und Achtung (für die zweite, innerliche) Erhabenheit, zwar zur Nachforschung reizen, aber den Mangel derselben nicht ersetzen können\".—Er erklärt damit jene Erhebungen als unbefriedigend für die Vernunft, welche bei ihnen und den damit verbundenen Empfindungen nicht stehen bleiben, und das Jenseits und Leere nicht für das Letzte gelten lassen kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"70.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0015","text":"Als ein Letztes aber ist der unendliche Progreß vornehmlich in seiner Anwendung auf die Moralität genommen worden. Der so eben angeführte zweite Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen, als der mannigfaltigen Welt und des in seine Freiheit erhobenen Ichs, ist zunächst qualitativ. Das Selbstbestimmen des Ich geht zugleich darauf, die Natur zu bestimmen und sich von ihr zu befreien; so bezieht es sich durch sich selbst auf sein Anderes, welches als äußerliches Daseyn ein Vielfältiges und auch Quantitatives ist. Die Beziehung auf ein Quantitatives wird selbst quantitativ; die negative Beziehung des Ich darauf, die Macht des Ich über das Nicht-Ich, über die Sinnlichkeit und äußere Natur, wird daher so vorgestellt, daß die Moralität immer größer, die Macht der Sinnlichkeit aber immer kleiner werden könne und solle.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"70.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0016","text":"Die völlige Angemessenheit aber des Willens zum moralischen Gesetze wird in den ins Unendliche gehenden Progreß verlegt, das heißt, als ein absolutes unerreichbares Jenseits vorgestellt, und eben dieß solle der wahre Anker und der rechte Trost seyn, daß es ein Unerreichbares ist; denn die Moralität soll als Kampf seyn; dieser aber ist nur unter der Unangemessenheit des Willens zum Gesetze, dieses damit schlechthin ein Jenseits für ihn.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"70.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0017","text":"In diesem Gegensatze werden Ich und Nicht-Ich oder der reine Wille und das moralische Gesetz, und die Natur und Sinnlichkeit des Willens als vollkommen selbstständig und gleichgültig gegeneinander vorausgesetzt. Der reine Wille hat sein eigenthümliches Gesetz, das in wesentlicher Beziehung auf die Sinnlichkeit steht; und die Natur und Sinnlichkeit hat ihrer Seits Gesetze, die weder aus dem Willen genommen und ihm entsprechend sind, noch auch nur, wenn gleich verschieden davon, an sich eine wesentliche Beziehung auf ihn hätten, sondern sie sind überhaupt für sich bestimmt, in sich fertig und geschlossen.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"70.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0018","text":"Zugleich sind beide aber Momente eines und desselben einfachen Wesens, des Ich; der Wille ist als das Negative gegen die Natur bestimmt, so daß er nur ist, insofern ein solches von ihm verschiedenes ist, das von ihm aufgehoben werde, von dem er aber hierin berührt und selbst afficirt ist. Der Natur und ihr als Sinnlichkeit des Menschen ist als einem selbstständigen System von Gesetzen das Beschränken durch ein anderes gleichgültig; sie erhält sich in diesem Begrenztwerden, tritt selbstständig in die Beziehung ein, und begrenzt den Willen des Gesetzes eben so sehr, als er sie begrenzt.—Es ist Ein Act, daß der Wille sich bestimmt und das Andersseyn einer Natur aufhebt, und daß dieß Andersseyn als daseyend gesetzt ist, sich in sein Aufgehobenwerden kontinuirt, und nicht aufgehoben ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"70.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0019","text":"Der Widerspruch, der hierin liegt, wird im unendlichen Progresse nicht aufgelöst, sondern im Gegentheil als unaufgelöst und unauflösbar dargestellt und behauptet; der Kampf der Moralität und der Sinnlichkeit wird vorgestellt, als das an und für sich seyende, absolute Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"70.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0020","text":"Die Ohnmacht über den qualitativen Gegensatz des Endlichen und Unendlichen Meister zu werden und die Idee des wahrhaften Willens, die substantielle Freiheit, zu fassen, nimmt zur Größe ihre Zuflucht, um sie als die Mittlerin zu gebrauchen, weil sie das aufgehobene Qualitative, der gleichgültig gewordene Unterschied, ist. Allein indem beide Glieder des Gegensatzes als qualitativ verschieden zu Grunde liegen bleiben, so wird vielmehr dadurch, daß sie sich in ihrer gegenseitigen Beziehung als Quanta verhalten, jedes sogleich als gegen diese Veränderung gleichgültig gesetzt. Die Natur wird durch Ich, die Sinnlichkeit durch den Willen des Guten bestimmt, die durch denselben an ihr hervorgebrachte Veränderung ist nur ein quantitativer Unterschied, ein solcher, der sie als das bestehen läßt, was sie ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"70.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0021","text":"In der abstraktern Darstellung der kantischen Philosophie oder wenigstens ihrer Principien, nämlich in der fichteschen Wissenschaftslehre, macht der unendliche Progreß auf dieselbe Weise die Grundlage und das Letzte aus. Auf den ersten Grundsatz dieser Darstellung, Ich=Ich, folgt ein zweiter davon unabhängiger, die Entgegensetzung des Nicht-Ich; die Beziehung beider wird sogleich auch als quantitativer Unterschied angenommen, daß Nicht-Ich zum Theil durch Ich bestimmt werde, zum Theil auch nicht. Das Nicht-Ich kontinuirt sich auf diese Weise in sein Nichtseyn so, daß es seinem Nichtseyn entgegengesetzt bleibt, als ein nicht Aufgehobenes.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"70.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0022","text":"Nachdem daher die Widersprüche, die darin liegen, im System entwickelt worden sind, so ist das schließliche Resultat dasjenige Verhältniß, welches der Anfang war; das Nicht-Ich bleibt ein unendlicher Anstoß, ein absolut-Anderes; die letzte Beziehung seiner und des Ich aufeinander ist der unendliche Progreß, Sehnsucht und Streben,—derselbe Widerspruch, mit welchem angefangen wurde.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"70.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0023","text":"Weil das Quantitative die als aufgehoben gesetzte Bestimmtheit ist, so glaubte man für die Einheit des Absoluten, für die Eine Substantialität, Viel oder vielmehr Alles gewonnen zu haben, indem man den Gegensatz überhaupt zu einem nur quantitativen Unterschiede herabsetzte. Aller Gegensatz ist nur quantitativ, war einige Zeit ein Hauptsatz neuerer Philosophie; die entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen haben dasselbe Wesen, denselben Inhalt, sie sind reale Seiten des Gegensatzes, insofern jede derselben seine beiden Bestimmungen, beide Faktoren, in ihr hat, nur daß auf der einen Seite der eine Faktor, auf der anderen der andere überwiegend, in der einen Seite der eine Faktor, eine Materie oder Thätigkeit, in größerer Menge oder in stärkerem Grade vorhanden sey, als in der andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"70.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0024","text":"Insofern verschiedene Stoffe oder Thätigkeiten vorausgesetzt werden, bestätigt und vollendet der quantitative Unterschied vielmehr deren Äußerlichkeit und Gleichgültigkeit gegeneinander und gegen ihre Einheit. Der Unterschied der absoluten Einheit soll nur quantitativ seyn; das Quantitative ist zwar die aufgehobene unmittelbare Bestimmtheit, aber die nur unvollkommene, erst die erste Negation, nicht die unendliche, nicht die Negation der Negation.—Indem Seyn und Denken als quantitative Bestimmungen der absoluten Substanz vorgestellt werden, werden auch sie, als Quanta, wie in untergeordneter Sphäre, der Kohlenstoff, Stickstoff u.s.f. sich vollkommen äußerlich und beziehungslos. Es ist ein Drittes, eine äußerliche Reflexion, welche von ihrem Unterschiede abstrahirt, und ihre innere, nur ansichseyende, nicht ebenso für-sich-seyende, Einheit erkennt.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"70.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0025","text":"Diese Einheit, wird dann in der That nur als erste unmittelbare vorgestellt, oder nur als Seyn, welches in seinem quantitativen Unterschiede sich gleich bleibt, aber nicht sich durch sich selbst gleich setzt; es ist somit nicht begriffen, als Negation der Negation, als unendliche Einheit. Nur im qualitativen Gegensatze geht die gesetzte Unendlichkeit, das Fürsichseyn, hervor, und die quantitative Bestimmung selbst geht, wie sich sogleich näher ergeben wird, in das Qualitative über.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"70.25"}],"sha256":"04b9d0a0cd3bd7d600ea25264b1ef9143ae867ab6d9c29081c64faff130ad0c5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103133324302Z_a4f78fc9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"04b9d0a0cd3bd7d600ea25264b1ef9143ae867ab6d9c29081c64faff130ad0c5","sha256":"99ae51b8aaf8bce4a6e9a57aef4b5b25768fb6ed28f375aeb1dff51f6cf7a370","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:31:33.324324+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0001","text":"Bad infinity is customarily regarded chiefly in the form of the progression of the quantitative into infinity,—this continual flight beyond the limit, which is the impotence to sublate it, and the perennial relapse into it,—as something sublime and as a kind of divine service, just as it has been regarded in philosophy as something ultimate. This progression has frequently served for tirades which have been admired as sublime productions. But in fact this modern sublimity does not make the object great, which rather escapes, but only the subject, which devours such great quantities within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"70.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0002","text":"The poverty of this elevation, which remains subjective and ascends the ladder of the quantitative, itself makes known that it admits, in vain labour, that it cannot come nearer to the infinite goal, which, to be sure, must be approached in a quite different manner in order to attain it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"70.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0003","text":"In the following tirades of this kind, what such elevation passes over into and terminates in is at the same time expressed. Kant, for example, adduces it as sublime (Kr. d. prakt. V. Schl.)","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"70.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0004","text":"\"when the subject raises itself in thought above the place which it occupies in the world of sense, and extends the connection into the infinitely great, a connection with stars beyond stars, with worlds beyond worlds, systems beyond systems, and, beyond that, into the boundless times of their periodic motion, whose beginning and duration.—Representation succumbs to this advance into the immeasurably remote, where the most distant world always has a still more distant one, the past, however far it may have been led back, still has a further one behind it, and the future, however far it may have been carried forward, still has another before it; thought succumbs to this representation of the immeasurable; like a dream in which someone proceeds along a long course ever further and unforeseeably further, without discerning an end, ends in falling or in vertigo.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"70.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0005","text":"This presentation, besides compressing the content of quantitative elevation into a richness of depiction, deserves praise above all for the truthfulness with which it indicates what finally happens to this elevation: thought succumbs; the end is falling and vertigo. What makes thought succumb and produces its falling and vertigo is nothing other than the boredom of repetition, which lets a limit disappear and reappear and disappear again, thus allowing one thing after another, and one in the other, on the other side the this-side, on this side the beyond, perennially to arise and perish, and affords only the feeling of the impotence of this infinity, or of this ought, which wishes to master the finite and cannot.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"70.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0006","text":"Haller's description of eternity, likewise called dreadful by Kant, is also customarily especially admired, but often precisely not on account of the aspect that constitutes its true merit:","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"70.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0007","text":"\"I heap up enormous numbers, pile millions of mountains upon one another, I set time upon time, and world upon world in heaps; And when from the dreadful height I look back upon you with vertigo, All the power of number, multiplied a thousandfold, Is still not a part of you.\" \"I subtract them, and you lie wholly before me.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"70.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0008","text":"If value is placed upon that loading and piling up of numbers and worlds as a description of eternity, it is overlooked that the poet himself declares this so-called dreadful going-out to be something vain and hollow, and that he concludes by saying that only through abandoning this empty infinite progression does true infinity itself come into presence before him.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"70.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0009","text":"There have been astronomers who liked to make much of themselves on account of the sublimity of their science because it had to do with an immeasurable multitude of stars, with such immeasurable spaces and times, in which distances and periods that are already great in themselves serve as units which, when taken so many more times, again contract into insignificance.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"70.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0010","text":"The vapid astonishment to which they abandoned themselves in this connection, the absurd hopes of travelling only in that life from one star to another and of acquiring such new knowledge further into the immeasurable, they proclaimed as a principal moment of the excellence of their science,—which is admirable, not for the sake of such quantitative infinity, but, on the contrary, for the sake of the relations of measure and the laws which reason cognizes in these objects, and which are rational infinity as against that irrational infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"70.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0011","text":"To the infinity that relates to external sensible intuition, Kant opposes the other infinity, when","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"70.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0012","text":"\"the individual returns to his invisible I, and sets the absolute freedom of his will, as a pure I, against all the terrors of fate and tyranny, beginning with his nearest surroundings, letting them disappear for himself, and likewise letting that which appears enduring, worlds beyond worlds, collapse into ruins, and recognizes himself, in solitude, as equal to himself.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"70.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0013","text":"The I in this solitude with itself is indeed the beyond attained; it has come to itself, is with itself, on this side; in pure self-consciousness absolute negativity has been brought to affirmation and presence, whereas in that progression beyond sensible quantum it only flees. But insofar as this pure I fixes itself in its abstraction and lack of content, it has existence in general, the fullness of the natural and spiritual universe, over against itself as a beyond. The same contradiction presents itself which underlies infinite progression; namely, a having-returned-into-itself which immediately is at the same time a being-outside-itself, a relation to its other as to its non-being; which relation remains a longing, because the I has fixed for itself, on the one hand, its insubstantial and untenable emptiness, and, on the other, the fullness that nevertheless remains present in negation, as its beyond.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"70.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0014","text":"Kant appends to these two sublimities the remark \"that admiration (for the former, external) and respect (for the latter, internal) sublimity, though they incite to inquiry, cannot replace the lack thereof.\"—Thereby he declares those elevations unsatisfying for reason, which cannot remain with them and the feelings connected with them, and cannot allow the beyond and emptiness to count as the ultimate.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"70.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0015","text":"But infinite progression has been taken as something ultimate chiefly in its application to morality. The second opposition of finite and infinite just cited, as that of the manifold world and the I elevated into its freedom, is initially qualitative. The self-determination of the I is at the same time directed toward determining nature and freeing itself from it; it thus relates through itself to its other, which, as external existence, is a manifold and also quantitative. The relation to a quantitative becomes itself quantitative; the negative relation of the I to it, the power of the I over the non-I, over sensibility and external nature, is therefore represented in such a way that morality can and ought always to become greater, but the power of sensibility always smaller.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"70.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0016","text":"But the complete adequacy of the will to the moral law is placed in the progression that goes on into infinity, that is, represented as an absolute unattainable beyond; and this is supposed to be the true anchor and the proper consolation, that it is something unattainable; for morality is supposed to be a struggle; but this is only possible under the inadequacy of the will to the law, which thereby is absolutely a beyond for it.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"70.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0017","text":"In this opposition, I and non-I, or the pure will and the moral law, and the nature and sensibility of the will, are presupposed as wholly self-subsistent and indifferent toward one another. The pure will has its peculiar law, which stands in an essential relation to sensibility; and nature and sensibility, for their part, have laws which are neither taken from the will and conformable to it, nor even, though different from it, would have an essential relation to it in themselves, but are determined simply for themselves, complete and closed within themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"70.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0018","text":"Yet both are moments of one and the same simple essence, the I; the will is determined as the negative over against nature, so that it is only insofar as there is something different from it, which it sublates, but by which it is, in this, touched and itself affected. To nature, and to it as the sensibility of the human being, as a self-subsistent system of laws, limitation by an other is indifferent; it preserves itself in this being-limited, enters independently into the relation, and limits the will of the law just as much as it limits it.—It is one act that the will determines itself and sublates the other-being of a nature, and that this other-being is posited as existing, continues itself into its sublation, and is not sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"70.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0019","text":"The contradiction that lies herein is not resolved in infinite progression, but, on the contrary, is represented and maintained as unresolved and unresolvable; the struggle of morality and sensibility is represented as the absolute relation that is in and for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"70.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0020","text":"The impotence to master the qualitative opposition of finite and infinite and to grasp the idea of the true will, substantial freedom, takes refuge in magnitude in order to use it as mediator, because it is the sublated qualitative, the distinction that has become indifferent. But since both members of the opposition remain underlying as qualitatively different, then, rather, by their comporting themselves in their reciprocal relation as quanta, each is at once posited as indifferent to this alteration. Nature is determined by the I, sensibility by the will of the good; the alteration produced in it by the latter is only a quantitative difference, one that leaves it as what it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"70.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0021","text":"In the more abstract presentation of Kantian philosophy, or at least of its principles, namely in Fichte's Wissenschaftslehre, infinite progression in the same way constitutes the foundation and the ultimate. Upon the first principle of this presentation, I=I, there follows a second independent of it, the opposition of the non-I; the relation of the two is immediately also assumed as a quantitative difference, namely, that the non-I is determined in part by the I and in part not. In this way the non-I continues itself into its non-being, such that it remains opposed to its non-being, as something not sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"70.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0022","text":"After, therefore, the contradictions that lie therein have been developed in the system, the final result is that relation which was the beginning; the non-I remains an infinite check, an absolute-other; the final relation of it and the I to one another is infinite progression, longing and striving,—the same contradiction with which the beginning was made.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"70.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0023","text":"Because the quantitative is determinacy posited as sublated, it was believed that one had gained much, or rather everything, for the unity of the Absolute, for the one substantiality, by reducing opposition in general to a merely quantitative difference. All opposition is merely quantitative was for some time a principal proposition of modern philosophy; the opposed determinations have the same essence, the same content; they are real sides of the opposition, insofar as each of them has its two determinations, both factors, in itself, only such that on one side the one factor, on the other side the other, predominates, such that in one side the one factor, a matter or activity, is present in a greater quantity or to a stronger degree than in the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"70.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0024","text":"Insofar as different matters or activities are presupposed, quantitative difference rather confirms and completes their externality and indifference toward one another and toward their unity. The difference of absolute unity is supposed to be merely quantitative; the quantitative is indeed immediate determinacy posited as sublated, but only imperfectly so, only the first negation, not the infinite negation, not the negation of negation.—Insofar as being and thinking are represented as quantitative determinations of absolute substance, they too, as quanta, become wholly external and devoid of relation, just as, in a subordinate sphere, carbon, nitrogen, etc. It is a third, an external reflection, which abstracts from their difference and cognizes their inner unity, which is only in itself, not likewise for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"70.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_18:P0025","text":"This unity, then, is in fact only represented as the first immediate unity, or merely as being, which remains equal to itself in its quantitative difference, but does not posit itself as equal through itself; it is thus not comprehended as the negation of negation, as infinite unity. Only in the qualitative opposition does posited infinity, being-for-itself, emerge, and the quantitative determination itself passes over into the qualitative, as will immediately become clearer in greater detail.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"70.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_18:P0025"]}],"source_digest":"795667ac15a346bab7bed52386ad96c2bf4454bb3e287552595dfc8b8d64a32f","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19","title":"Remark 2.","order":71,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_19","text":"Es ist oben erinnert worden, daß die kantischen Antinomien Darstellungen des Gegensatzes des Endlichen und Unendlichen, in einer konkreteren Gestalt, auf speciellere Substrate der Vorstellung angewendet, sind. Die daselbst betrachtete Antinomie enthielt den Gegensatz der qualitativen Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit. In einer andern, der ersten der vier kosmologischen Antinomien, ist es mehr die quantitative Grenze, die in ihrem Widerstreite betrachtet wird. Ich will die Untersuchung dieser Antinomie daher hier anstellen.\n\nSie betrifft die Begrenztheit oder Unbegrenztheit der Welt in Zeit und Raum.—Es konnte eben so gut dieser Gegensatz auch in Rücksicht auf Zeit und Raum selbst betrachtet werden, denn ob Zeit und Raum Verhältnisse der Dinge selbst, oder aber nur Formen der Anschauung sind, ändert nichts für das Antinomische der Begrenztheit oder Unbegrenztheit in ihnen.\n\nDie nähere Auseinanderlegung dieser Antinomie wird gleichfalls zeigen, daß die beiden Sätze und eben so ihre Beweise, die wie bei der oben betrachteten apogogisch geführt sind, auf nichts, als auf die zwei einfachen, entgegengesetzten Behauptungen hinauslaufen: es ist eine Grenze, und: es muß über die Grenze hinausgegangen werden.\n\nDie Thesis ist:\n\n\"Die Welt hat einen Anfang in der Zeit, und ist dem Raume nach auch in Grenzen eingeschlossen.\"\n\nDer eine Theil des Beweises, die Zeit betreffend, nimmt das Gegentheil an, \"die Welt habe der Zeit nach keinen Anfang, so ist bis zu jedem gegebenen Zeitpunkt eine Ewigkeit abgelaufen, und mithin eine unendliche Reihe auf einander folgender Zustände der Dinge in der Welt verflossen. Nun besteht aber eben darin die Unendlichkeit einer Reihe, daß sie durch successive Synthesis niemals vollendet seyn kann. Also ist eine unendliche verflossene Weltreihe unmöglich, mithin ein Anfang der Welt eine nothwendige Bedingung ihres Daseyns; welches zu erweisen war.\"\n\nDer andere Theil des Beweises, der den Raum betrifft, wird auf die Zeit zurückgeführt. Das Zusammenfassen der Theile einer im Raume unendlichen Welt erforderte eine unendliche Zeit, welche als abgelaufen angesehen werden müßte, insofern die Welt im Raume nicht als ein Werdendes, sondern als ein vollendetes Gegebenes anzusehen ist. Von der Zeit aber wurde im ersten Theile des Beweises gezeigt, daß eine unendliche Zeit als abgelaufen anzunehmen unmöglich sey.\n\nMan sieht aber sogleich, daß es unnöthig war, den Beweis apagogisch zu machen, oder überhaupt einen Beweis zu führen, indem in ihm selbst unmittelbar die Behauptung dessen zu Grunde liegt, was bewiesen werden sollte. Es wird nämlich irgend ein oder jeder gegebene Zeitpunkt angenommen, bis zu welchem eine Ewigkeit (—Ewigkeit hat hier nur den geringen Sinii einer schlecht-unendlichen Zeit) abgelaufen sey. Ein gegebener Zeitpunkt heißt nun nichts Anders, als eine bestimmte Grenze in der Zeit. Im Beweise wird also eine Grenze der Zeit als wirklich vorausgesetzt; sie ist aber eben das, was bewiesen werden sollte. Denn die Thesis besteht darin, daß die Welt einen Anfang in der Zeit habe.\n\nNur der Unterschied findet Statt, daß die angenommene Zeitgrenze ein Jetzt, als Ende der vorher verflossenen, die zu beweisende aber Jetzt als Anfang einer Zukunft ist. Allein dieser Unterschied ist unwesentlich. Jetzt wird als der Punkt angenommen, in welchem eine unendliche Reihe auf einander folgender Zustände der Dinge in der Zeit verflossen seyn soll, also als Ende, als qualitative Grenze. Würde dieß Jetzt nur als quantitative Grenze betrachtet, welche fließend und über die nicht nur hinaus zu gehen sondern die vielmehr nur dieß sey, über sich hinauszugehen, so wäre die unendliche Zeitreihe in ihr nicht verflossen, sondern führe fort zu fließen, und das Raisonnement des Beweises fiele weg. Dagegen ist der Zeitpunkt als qualitative Grenze für die Vergangenheit angenommen, aber ist so zugleich Anfang für die Zukunft,—denn an sich ist jeder Zeitpunkt die Beziehung der Vergangenheit und der Zukunft,—auch ist er absoluter d. h. abstrakter Anfang für dieselbe, d. i. das, was bewiesen werden sollte. Es thut nichts zur Sache, daß vor seiner Zukunft und diesem ihrem Anfange schon eine Vergangenheit ist; indem dieser Zeitpunkt qualitative Grenze ist,—und als qualitative ihn anzunehmen, liegt in der Bestimmung des Vollendeten, Abgelaufenen, also sich nicht Kontinuirenden,—so ist die Zeit in ihm abgebrochen, und jene Vergangenheit, ohne Beziehung auf diejenige Zeit, welche nur Zukunft in Rücksicht auf diese Vergangenheit genannt werden konnte, und daher ohne solche Beziehung nur Zeit überhaupt ist, die einen absoluten Anfang hat. Stünde sie aber,—(wie sie es denn tut—) durch das Jetzt, den gegebenen Zeitpunkt, in einer Beziehung auf die Vergangenheit, wäre sie somit als Zukunft bestimmt, so wäre auch dieser Zeitpunkt von der anderen Seite keine Grenze, die unendliche Zeitreihe kontinuirte sich in dem, was Zukunft hieß, und wäre nicht, wie angenommen worden, vollendet.\n\nIn Wahrheit ist die Zeit reine Quantität; der im Beweise gebrauchte Zeitpunkt, in welchem sie unterbrochen seyn sollte, ist vielmehr nur das sich selbst aufhebende Fürsichseyn des Jetzt. Der Beweis leistet nichts, als daß er die in der Thesis behauptete absolute Grenze der Zeit als einen gegebenen Zeitpunkt vorstellig macht und ihn als vollendeten, d. i. abstrakten Punkt, geradezu annimmt,—eine populare Bestimmung, welche das sinnliche Vorstellen leicht als eine Grenze passiren, somit im Beweise dieß als Annahme gelten läßt, was vorher als das zu Beweisende aufgestellt wurde.\n\nDie Antithesis heißt:\n\n\"Die Welt hat keinen Anfang und keine Grenzen im Raume, sondern ist sowohl in Ansehung der Zeit als des Raumes unendlich.\"\n\nDer Beweis setzt gleichfalls das Gegentheil:\n\n\"Die Welt habe einen Anfang. Da der Anfang ein Daseyn ist, wovor eine Zeit vorhergeht, darin das Ding nicht ist, so muß eine Zeit vorhergegangen seyn, darin die Welt nicht war, d. i. eine leere Zeit. Nun ist aber in einer leeren Zeit kein Entstehen irgend eines Dings möglich; weil kein Theil einer solchen Zeit vor einem anderen irgend eine unterscheidende Bedingung des Daseyns vor der des Nichtdaseyns an sich hat. Also kann zwar in der Welt manche Reihe der Dinge anfangen, die Welt selbst aber keinen Anfang nehmen, und ist in Ansehung der vergangenen Zeit unendlich.\"\n\nDieser apogogische Beweis enthält, wie die andern, die direkte und unbewiesene Behauptung dessen, was er beweisen sollte. Er nimmt neihlich zuerst ein Jenseits des weltlichen Daseyns, eine leere Zeit, an; aber kontinuirt alsdann auch das weltliche Daseyn ebenso sehr über sich hinaus in diese leere Zeit hinein, hebt diese dadurch auf, und setzt somit das Daseyn ins Unendliche fort. Die Welt ist ein Daseyn; der Beweis setzt voraus, daß dieß Daseyn entstehe, und das Entstehen eine in der Zeit vorhergehende Bedingung habe. Darin aber eben besteht die Antithesis selbst, daß es kein unbedingtes Daseyn, keine absolute Grenze gebe, sondern das weltliche Daseyn immer eine vorhergehende Bedingung fordere. Das zu Erweisende findet sich somit als Annahme in dem Beweise.—Die Bedingung wird dann ferner in der leeren Zeit gesucht, was so viel heißt, als daß sie als zeitlich und somit als Daseyn, und Beschränktes angenommen wird. Überhaupt also ist die Annahme gemacht, daß die Welt als Daseyn ein anderes bedingtes Daseyn in der Zeit voraussetze und hiermit sofort ins Unendliche.\n\nDer Beweis in Ansehung der Unendlichkeit der Welt im Raume ist dasselbe. Apogogischer Weise wird die räumliche Endlichkeit der Welt gesetzt; \"diese befände sich somit in einem leeren unbegrenzten Raume, und hätte ein Verhältniß zu ihm; ein solches Verhältniß der Welt zu keinem Gegenstande aber ist Nichts.\"\n\nWas bewiesen werden sollte, ist hier ebenso im Beweise direkt vorausgesetzt. Es wird direkt angenommen, daß die begrenzte räumliche Welt sich in einem leeren Raume befinden und ein Verhältniß zu ihm haben sollte, das heißt, daß über sie hinausgegangen werden müsse,—einer Seits in das Leere, in das Jenseits und Nichtseyn derselben, anderer Seits aber daß sie damit im Verhältniß stehe, d. i. sich darein hinein kontinuire, das Jenseits hiermit mit weltlichem Daseyn erfüllt vorzustellen sey. Die Unendlichkeit der Welt im Raume, die in der Antithesis behauptet wird, ist nichts anderes, als einer Seits der leere Raum, anderer Seits das Verhältniß der Welt zu ihm, das heißt Kontinuität derselben in ihm, oder die Erfüllung desselben; welcher Widerspruch, der Raum zugleich als leer und zugleich als erfüllt, der unendliche Progreß des Daseyns im Raume ist. Dieser Widerspruch selbst, das Verhältniß der Welt zum leeren Raume, ist im Beweise direkt zur Grundlage gemacht.\n\nDie Thesis und Antithesis und die Beweise derselben stellen daher nichts dar, als die entgegengesetzten Behauptungen, daß eine Grenze ist, und daß die Grenze eben so sehr nur eine aufgehobene ist; daß die Grenze ein Jenseits hat, mit dem sie aber in Beziehung steht, wohin über sie hinauszugehen ist, worin aber wieder eine solche Grenze entsteht, die keine ist.\n\nDie Auflösung dieser Antinomien ist, wie die der obigen, transcendental, das heißt, sie besteht in der Behauptung der Idealität des Raums und der Zeit, als Formen der Anschauung, in dem Sinne, daß die Welt an ihr selbst nicht im Widerspruch mit sich, nicht ein sich Aufhebendes, sondern nur das Bewußtseyn in seinem Anschauen und in der Beziehung der Anschauung auf Verstand und Vernunft, ein sich selbst widersprechendes Wesen sey. Es ist dieß eine zu große Zärtlichkeit für die Welt, von ihr den Widerspruch zu entfernen, ihn dagegen in den Geist, in die Vernunft, zu verlegen und darin unaufgelöst bestehen zu lassen. In der That ist es der Geist, der so stark ist, den Widerspruch ertragen zu können, aber er ist es auch, der ihn aufzulösen weiß. Die sogenannte Welt aber (sie heiße objektive, reale Welt, oder nach dem transcendentalen Idealismus subjektives Anschauen, und durch die Verstandes-Kategorie bestimmte Sinnlichkeit), entbehrt darum des Widerspruchs nicht und nirgends, vermag ihn aber nicht zu ertragen und ist darum dem Entstehen und Vergehen preisgegeben.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0001","text":"Es ist oben erinnert worden, daß die kantischen Antinomien Darstellungen des Gegensatzes des Endlichen und Unendlichen, in einer konkreteren Gestalt, auf speciellere Substrate der Vorstellung angewendet, sind. Die daselbst betrachtete Antinomie enthielt den Gegensatz der qualitativen Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit. In einer andern, der ersten der vier kosmologischen Antinomien, ist es mehr die quantitative Grenze, die in ihrem Widerstreite betrachtet wird. Ich will die Untersuchung dieser Antinomie daher hier anstellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"71.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0002","text":"Sie betrifft die Begrenztheit oder Unbegrenztheit der Welt in Zeit und Raum.—Es konnte eben so gut dieser Gegensatz auch in Rücksicht auf Zeit und Raum selbst betrachtet werden, denn ob Zeit und Raum Verhältnisse der Dinge selbst, oder aber nur Formen der Anschauung sind, ändert nichts für das Antinomische der Begrenztheit oder Unbegrenztheit in ihnen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"71.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0003","text":"Die nähere Auseinanderlegung dieser Antinomie wird gleichfalls zeigen, daß die beiden Sätze und eben so ihre Beweise, die wie bei der oben betrachteten apogogisch geführt sind, auf nichts, als auf die zwei einfachen, entgegengesetzten Behauptungen hinauslaufen: es ist eine Grenze, und: es muß über die Grenze hinausgegangen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"71.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0004","text":"Die Thesis ist:","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"71.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0005","text":"\"Die Welt hat einen Anfang in der Zeit, und ist dem Raume nach auch in Grenzen eingeschlossen.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"71.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0006","text":"Der eine Theil des Beweises, die Zeit betreffend, nimmt das Gegentheil an, \"die Welt habe der Zeit nach keinen Anfang, so ist bis zu jedem gegebenen Zeitpunkt eine Ewigkeit abgelaufen, und mithin eine unendliche Reihe auf einander folgender Zustände der Dinge in der Welt verflossen. Nun besteht aber eben darin die Unendlichkeit einer Reihe, daß sie durch successive Synthesis niemals vollendet seyn kann. Also ist eine unendliche verflossene Weltreihe unmöglich, mithin ein Anfang der Welt eine nothwendige Bedingung ihres Daseyns; welches zu erweisen war.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"71.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0007","text":"Der andere Theil des Beweises, der den Raum betrifft, wird auf die Zeit zurückgeführt. Das Zusammenfassen der Theile einer im Raume unendlichen Welt erforderte eine unendliche Zeit, welche als abgelaufen angesehen werden müßte, insofern die Welt im Raume nicht als ein Werdendes, sondern als ein vollendetes Gegebenes anzusehen ist. Von der Zeit aber wurde im ersten Theile des Beweises gezeigt, daß eine unendliche Zeit als abgelaufen anzunehmen unmöglich sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"71.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0008","text":"Man sieht aber sogleich, daß es unnöthig war, den Beweis apagogisch zu machen, oder überhaupt einen Beweis zu führen, indem in ihm selbst unmittelbar die Behauptung dessen zu Grunde liegt, was bewiesen werden sollte. Es wird nämlich irgend ein oder jeder gegebene Zeitpunkt angenommen, bis zu welchem eine Ewigkeit (—Ewigkeit hat hier nur den geringen Sinii einer schlecht-unendlichen Zeit) abgelaufen sey. Ein gegebener Zeitpunkt heißt nun nichts Anders, als eine bestimmte Grenze in der Zeit. Im Beweise wird also eine Grenze der Zeit als wirklich vorausgesetzt; sie ist aber eben das, was bewiesen werden sollte. Denn die Thesis besteht darin, daß die Welt einen Anfang in der Zeit habe.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"71.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0009","text":"Nur der Unterschied findet Statt, daß die angenommene Zeitgrenze ein Jetzt, als Ende der vorher verflossenen, die zu beweisende aber Jetzt als Anfang einer Zukunft ist. Allein dieser Unterschied ist unwesentlich. Jetzt wird als der Punkt angenommen, in welchem eine unendliche Reihe auf einander folgender Zustände der Dinge in der Zeit verflossen seyn soll, also als Ende, als qualitative Grenze. Würde dieß Jetzt nur als quantitative Grenze betrachtet, welche fließend und über die nicht nur hinaus zu gehen sondern die vielmehr nur dieß sey, über sich hinauszugehen, so wäre die unendliche Zeitreihe in ihr nicht verflossen, sondern führe fort zu fließen, und das Raisonnement des Beweises fiele weg.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"71.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0010","text":"Dagegen ist der Zeitpunkt als qualitative Grenze für die Vergangenheit angenommen, aber ist so zugleich Anfang für die Zukunft,—denn an sich ist jeder Zeitpunkt die Beziehung der Vergangenheit und der Zukunft,—auch ist er absoluter d. h. abstrakter Anfang für dieselbe, d. i. das, was bewiesen werden sollte. Es thut nichts zur Sache, daß vor seiner Zukunft und diesem ihrem Anfange schon eine Vergangenheit ist; indem dieser Zeitpunkt qualitative Grenze ist,—und als qualitative ihn anzunehmen, liegt in der Bestimmung des Vollendeten, Abgelaufenen, also sich nicht Kontinuirenden,—so ist die Zeit in ihm abgebrochen, und jene Vergangenheit, ohne Beziehung auf diejenige Zeit, welche nur Zukunft in Rücksicht auf diese Vergangenheit genannt werden konnte, und daher ohne solche Beziehung nur Zeit überhaupt ist, die einen absoluten Anfang hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"71.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0011","text":"Stünde sie aber,—(wie sie es denn tut—) durch das Jetzt, den gegebenen Zeitpunkt, in einer Beziehung auf die Vergangenheit, wäre sie somit als Zukunft bestimmt, so wäre auch dieser Zeitpunkt von der anderen Seite keine Grenze, die unendliche Zeitreihe kontinuirte sich in dem, was Zukunft hieß, und wäre nicht, wie angenommen worden, vollendet.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"71.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0012","text":"In Wahrheit ist die Zeit reine Quantität; der im Beweise gebrauchte Zeitpunkt, in welchem sie unterbrochen seyn sollte, ist vielmehr nur das sich selbst aufhebende Fürsichseyn des Jetzt. Der Beweis leistet nichts, als daß er die in der Thesis behauptete absolute Grenze der Zeit als einen gegebenen Zeitpunkt vorstellig macht und ihn als vollendeten, d. i. abstrakten Punkt, geradezu annimmt,—eine populare Bestimmung, welche das sinnliche Vorstellen leicht als eine Grenze passiren, somit im Beweise dieß als Annahme gelten läßt, was vorher als das zu Beweisende aufgestellt wurde.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"71.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0013","text":"Die Antithesis heißt:","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"71.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0014","text":"\"Die Welt hat keinen Anfang und keine Grenzen im Raume, sondern ist sowohl in Ansehung der Zeit als des Raumes unendlich.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"71.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0015","text":"Der Beweis setzt gleichfalls das Gegentheil:","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"71.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0016","text":"\"Die Welt habe einen Anfang. Da der Anfang ein Daseyn ist, wovor eine Zeit vorhergeht, darin das Ding nicht ist, so muß eine Zeit vorhergegangen seyn, darin die Welt nicht war, d. i. eine leere Zeit. Nun ist aber in einer leeren Zeit kein Entstehen irgend eines Dings möglich; weil kein Theil einer solchen Zeit vor einem anderen irgend eine unterscheidende Bedingung des Daseyns vor der des Nichtdaseyns an sich hat. Also kann zwar in der Welt manche Reihe der Dinge anfangen, die Welt selbst aber keinen Anfang nehmen, und ist in Ansehung der vergangenen Zeit unendlich.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"71.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0017","text":"Dieser apogogische Beweis enthält, wie die andern, die direkte und unbewiesene Behauptung dessen, was er beweisen sollte. Er nimmt neihlich zuerst ein Jenseits des weltlichen Daseyns, eine leere Zeit, an; aber kontinuirt alsdann auch das weltliche Daseyn ebenso sehr über sich hinaus in diese leere Zeit hinein, hebt diese dadurch auf, und setzt somit das Daseyn ins Unendliche fort. Die Welt ist ein Daseyn; der Beweis setzt voraus, daß dieß Daseyn entstehe, und das Entstehen eine in der Zeit vorhergehende Bedingung habe. Darin aber eben besteht die Antithesis selbst, daß es kein unbedingtes Daseyn, keine absolute Grenze gebe, sondern das weltliche Daseyn immer eine vorhergehende Bedingung fordere.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"71.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0018","text":"Das zu Erweisende findet sich somit als Annahme in dem Beweise.—Die Bedingung wird dann ferner in der leeren Zeit gesucht, was so viel heißt, als daß sie als zeitlich und somit als Daseyn, und Beschränktes angenommen wird. Überhaupt also ist die Annahme gemacht, daß die Welt als Daseyn ein anderes bedingtes Daseyn in der Zeit voraussetze und hiermit sofort ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"71.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0019","text":"Der Beweis in Ansehung der Unendlichkeit der Welt im Raume ist dasselbe. Apogogischer Weise wird die räumliche Endlichkeit der Welt gesetzt; \"diese befände sich somit in einem leeren unbegrenzten Raume, und hätte ein Verhältniß zu ihm; ein solches Verhältniß der Welt zu keinem Gegenstande aber ist Nichts.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"71.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0020","text":"Was bewiesen werden sollte, ist hier ebenso im Beweise direkt vorausgesetzt. Es wird direkt angenommen, daß die begrenzte räumliche Welt sich in einem leeren Raume befinden und ein Verhältniß zu ihm haben sollte, das heißt, daß über sie hinausgegangen werden müsse,—einer Seits in das Leere, in das Jenseits und Nichtseyn derselben, anderer Seits aber daß sie damit im Verhältniß stehe, d. i. sich darein hinein kontinuire, das Jenseits hiermit mit weltlichem Daseyn erfüllt vorzustellen sey. Die Unendlichkeit der Welt im Raume, die in der Antithesis behauptet wird, ist nichts anderes, als einer Seits der leere Raum, anderer Seits das Verhältniß der Welt zu ihm, das heißt Kontinuität derselben in ihm, oder die Erfüllung desselben; welcher Widerspruch, der Raum zugleich als leer und zugleich als erfüllt, der unendliche Progreß des Daseyns im Raume ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"71.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0021","text":"Dieser Widerspruch selbst, das Verhältniß der Welt zum leeren Raume, ist im Beweise direkt zur Grundlage gemacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"71.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0022","text":"Die Thesis und Antithesis und die Beweise derselben stellen daher nichts dar, als die entgegengesetzten Behauptungen, daß eine Grenze ist, und daß die Grenze eben so sehr nur eine aufgehobene ist; daß die Grenze ein Jenseits hat, mit dem sie aber in Beziehung steht, wohin über sie hinauszugehen ist, worin aber wieder eine solche Grenze entsteht, die keine ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"71.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0023","text":"Die Auflösung dieser Antinomien ist, wie die der obigen, transcendental, das heißt, sie besteht in der Behauptung der Idealität des Raums und der Zeit, als Formen der Anschauung, in dem Sinne, daß die Welt an ihr selbst nicht im Widerspruch mit sich, nicht ein sich Aufhebendes, sondern nur das Bewußtseyn in seinem Anschauen und in der Beziehung der Anschauung auf Verstand und Vernunft, ein sich selbst widersprechendes Wesen sey. Es ist dieß eine zu große Zärtlichkeit für die Welt, von ihr den Widerspruch zu entfernen, ihn dagegen in den Geist, in die Vernunft, zu verlegen und darin unaufgelöst bestehen zu lassen. In der That ist es der Geist, der so stark ist, den Widerspruch ertragen zu können, aber er ist es auch, der ihn aufzulösen weiß.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"71.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0024","text":"Die sogenannte Welt aber (sie heiße objektive, reale Welt, oder nach dem transcendentalen Idealismus subjektives Anschauen, und durch die Verstandes-Kategorie bestimmte Sinnlichkeit), entbehrt darum des Widerspruchs nicht und nirgends, vermag ihn aber nicht zu ertragen und ist darum dem Entstehen und Vergehen preisgegeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"71.24"}],"sha256":"4667338d7cad9c764afd6e765cd2a1aa1683195a6d64631a00d472a14f13ae89","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103155156278Z_17fdd7b9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"4667338d7cad9c764afd6e765cd2a1aa1683195a6d64631a00d472a14f13ae89","sha256":"1539520d3cccf7b3965ab5179b561847fcd783b96f1c4fa9c255c670d9c2a6bf","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:31:55.156290+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0001","text":"It has been recalled above that the Kantian antinomies are presentations of the opposition of the finite and the infinite, applied, in a more concrete form, to more specific substrates of representation. The antinomy considered there contained the opposition of qualitative finitude and infinity. In another, the first of the four cosmological antinomies, it is rather the quantitative limit that is considered in its conflict. I shall therefore undertake the investigation of this antinomy here.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"71.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0002","text":"It concerns the boundedness or unboundedness of the world in time and space.—This opposition could equally well have been considered with respect to time and space themselves; for whether time and space are relations of things themselves, or merely forms of intuition, alters nothing in respect of the antinomial character of boundedness or unboundedness in them.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"71.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0003","text":"The more precise exposition of this antinomy will likewise show that the two propositions, and equally their proofs, which, as in the case considered above, are conducted apagogically, amount to nothing but the two simple, opposed assertions: there is a limit; and: one must go beyond the limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"71.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0004","text":"The thesis is:","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"71.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0005","text":"\"The world has a beginning in time, and is also enclosed within limits in respect of space.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"71.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0006","text":"One part of the proof, concerning time, assumes the contrary: \"if the world has no beginning in respect of time, then an eternity has elapsed up to every given point of time, and consequently an infinite series of successive states of things in the world has passed away. But the infinity of a series consists precisely in this, that it can never be completed by successive synthesis. Therefore an infinite world-series that has elapsed is impossible; consequently, a beginning of the world is a necessary condition of its existence; which was to be proved.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"71.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0007","text":"The other part of the proof, concerning space, is reduced to time. The comprehending of the parts of a world infinite in space would require an infinite time, which would have to be regarded as having elapsed, insofar as the world in space is to be regarded not as something becoming but as a completed given. But in the first part of the proof it was shown of time that it is impossible to assume an infinite time as having elapsed.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"71.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0008","text":"But one sees at once that it was unnecessary to make the proof apagogic, or indeed to give any proof at all, since the assertion of what was to be proved itself immediately underlies it. For some, or every, given point of time is assumed, up to which an eternity (—eternity here has only the meagre sense of a spurious-infinite time) is supposed to have elapsed. Now a given point of time means nothing other than a determinate limit in time. Thus, in the proof a limit of time is presupposed as actual; but this is precisely what was to be proved. For the thesis consists in the assertion that the world has a beginning in time.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"71.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0009","text":"The sole difference is that the assumed limit of time is a Now, as the end of what has previously elapsed, whereas the one to be proved is Now as the beginning of a future. But this difference is inessential. The Now is assumed as the point at which an infinite series of successive states of things in time is supposed to have elapsed, hence as end, as qualitative limit. If this Now were regarded merely as a quantitative limit, which is flowing, and beyond which one is not merely to go, but which rather is only this: to go beyond itself, then the infinite time-series would not have elapsed in it, but would continue to flow, and the reasoning of the proof would fall away.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"71.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0010","text":"Conversely, the point of time is assumed as a qualitative limit for the past, but is thereby at the same time beginning for the future,—for in itself every point of time is the relation of past and future,—and is also absolute, i.e. abstract, beginning for it, i.e. that which was to be proved. It makes no difference that before its future and this beginning of that future there is already a past; since this point of time is qualitative limit,—and to assume it as qualitative lies in the determination of the completed, the elapsed, thus of that which does not continue itself,—time is broken off in it, and that past, without relation to that time which could be called future only in relation to this past, and which therefore without such relation is merely time in general, has an absolute beginning.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"71.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0011","text":"But if it stood,—(as indeed it does—), through the Now, the given point of time, in a relation to the past, and were thus determined as future, then this point of time too would, from the other side, not be a limit; the infinite time-series would continue itself in what was called future, and would not, as had been assumed, be completed.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"71.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0012","text":"In truth, time is pure quantity; the point of time employed in the proof, in which it was supposed to be interrupted, is rather only the self-sublating being-for-self of the Now. The proof accomplishes nothing but to represent the absolute limit of time asserted in the thesis as a given point of time and simply to assume it as a completed, i.e. abstract, point,—a popular determination which sensuous representation readily allows to pass as a limit, and thus allows that to count in the proof as an assumption which was previously set forth as what was to be proved.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"71.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0013","text":"The antithesis reads:","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"71.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0014","text":"\"The world has no beginning and no limits in space, but is infinite both with regard to time and to space.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"71.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0015","text":"The proof likewise posits the contrary:","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"71.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0016","text":"\"Suppose that the world has a beginning. Since the beginning is an existence before which a time precedes in which the thing is not, a time must have preceded in which the world was not, i.e. an empty time. But in an empty time no arising of any thing is possible, because no part of such a time has in itself, before another, any condition distinguishing existence from non-existence. Thus, many a series of things may indeed begin in the world, but the world itself cannot take a beginning, and is infinite with regard to past time.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"71.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0017","text":"This apagogic proof contains, like the others, the direct and unproved assertion of what it was to prove. It first assumes, namely, a beyond of worldly existence, an empty time; but then likewise continues worldly existence beyond itself into this empty time, thereby sublates the latter, and thus carries existence forward into infinity. The world is an existence; the proof presupposes that this existence arises, and that arising has a condition preceding it in time. But therein consists the antithesis itself, namely, that there is no unconditioned existence, no absolute limit, but that worldly existence always demands a preceding condition.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"71.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0018","text":"Thus what was to be proved is found as an assumption in the proof.—The condition is then further sought in empty time, which amounts to assuming it as temporal and hence as existence, and as limited. In general, therefore, the assumption has been made that the world, as existence, presupposes another conditioned existence in time, and thereby proceeds forthwith into infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"71.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0019","text":"The proof concerning the infinity of the world in space is the same. In an apagogic manner the spatial finitude of the world is posited; \"it would thus find itself in an empty unbounded space, and would have a relation to it; but such a relation of the world to no object is nothing.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"71.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0020","text":"What was to be proved is here likewise directly presupposed in the proof. It is directly assumed that the spatially limited world should find itself in an empty space and have a relation to it; that is, that one must go beyond it,—on the one hand into the empty, into its beyond and non-being, but on the other hand that it stands in relation to this, i.e. continues itself into it, so that the beyond is to be represented as thereby filled with worldly existence. The infinity of the world in space, asserted in the antithesis, is nothing other than, on the one hand, empty space, and, on the other, the relation of the world to it, that is, its continuity in it, or its filling; this contradiction, that space is at once empty and at once filled, is the infinite progress of existence in space.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"71.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0021","text":"This contradiction itself, the relation of the world to empty space, is made directly the foundation in the proof.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"71.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0022","text":"The thesis and antithesis and their proofs therefore present nothing but the opposed assertions that there is a limit, and that the limit is equally only a sublated one; that the limit has a beyond, to which, however, it stands in relation, and beyond which one must go, but in which there again arises such a limit, which is not one.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"71.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0023","text":"The resolution of these antinomies is, like that of the preceding ones, transcendental; that is, it consists in the assertion of the ideality of space and time as forms of intuition, in the sense that the world is not in contradiction with itself in itself, is not something self-sublating, but that only consciousness, in its intuition and in the relation of intuition to understanding and reason, is a self-contradictory being. This is too great a tenderness toward the world, to remove contradiction from it, and instead to transfer it into spirit, into reason, and to leave it there unresolved. In fact, it is spirit that is strong enough to endure contradiction, but it is also spirit that knows how to resolve it.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"71.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_19:P0024","text":"But the so-called world (whether it be called objective, real world, or, according to transcendental idealism, subjective intuition and sensibility determined by the category of understanding) is not therefore devoid of contradiction, anywhere; but it is incapable of enduring it and is therefore given over to arising and passing away.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"71.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_19:P0024"]}],"source_digest":"64cdb9d48253cdfd6e83bacfb8ce91d963f3afbc4ff908f46e2370c61b72f8e0","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD","title":"c. The Infinity of Quantum.","order":72,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDUD","text":"Das unendliche Quantum, als Unendlichgroßes oder Unendlichkleines, ist selbst an sich der unendliche Progreß; es ist Quantum als ein Großes oder Kleines, und ist zugleich Nichtseyn des Quantums. Das Unendlichgroße und Unendlichkleine sind daher Bilder der Vorstellung, die bei näherer Betrachtung sich als nichtiger Nebel und Schatten zeigen. Im unendlichen Progreß aber ist dieser Widerspruch explicite vorhanden, und damit das, was die Natur des Quantums ist, das als intensive Größe seine Realität erreicht hat, und in seinem Daseyn nun gesetzt, wie es in seinem Begriffe ist. Diese Identität ist es, die zu betrachten ist.\n\nDas Quantum als Grad ist einfach, auf sich bezogen und als an ihm selbst bestimmt. Indem durch diese Einfachheit das Andersseyn und die Bestimmtheit an ihm aufgehoben ist, ist diese ihm äußerlich; es hat seine Bestimmtheit außer ihm. Dieß sein Außersichseyn ist zunächst das abstrakte Nichtseyn des Quantums überhaupt, die schlechte Unendlichkeit. Aber ferner ist dieß Nichtseyn auch ein Großes, das Quantum kontinuirt sich in sein Nichtseyn, denn es hat eben seine Bestimmtheit in seiner Äußerlichkeit; diese seine Äußerlichkeit ist daher eben so sehr selbst Quantum; jenes sein Nichtseyn, die Unendlichkeit, wird so begrenzt, d. h. dieß Jenseits wird aufgehoben, dieses ist selbst als Quantum bestimmt, das hiermit in seiner Negation bei sich selbst ist.\n\nDieß ist aber das, was das Quantum als solches an sich ist. Denn es ist eben es selbst durch sein Äußerlichseyn; die Äußerlichkeit macht das aus, wodurch es Quantum, bei sich selbst, ist. Es ist also im unendlichen Progresse der Begriff des Quantums gesetzt.\n\nNehmen wir ihn zunächst in seinen abstrakten Bestimmungen wie sie vorliegen, so ist in ihm das Aufheben des Quantums, aber eben so sehr seines Jenseits, also die Negation des Quantums sowohl, als die Negation dieser Negation vorhanden. Seine Wahrheit ist ihre Einheit, worin sie, aber als Momente, sind.—Sie ist die Auflösung des Widerspruchs, dessen Ausdruck er ist, und ihr nächster Sinn somit die Wiederherstellung des Begriffs der Größe, daß sie gleichgültige oder äußerliche Grenze ist. Im unendlichen Progresse als solchem pflegt nur darauf reflektirt zu werden, daß jedes Quantum, es sey noch so groß oder klein, verschwinden, daß über dasselbe muß hinausgegangen werden können; aber nicht darauf, daß dieß sein Aufheben, das Jenseits, das schlecht-Unendliche selbst auch verschwindet.\n\nSchon das erste Aufheben, die Negation der Qualität überhaupt, wodurch das Quantum gesetzt wird, ist an sich das Aufheben der Negation,—das Quantum ist aufgehobene qualitative Grenze, somit aufgehobene Negation,—aber es ist zugleich nur an sich dieß; gesetzt ist es als ein Daseyn, und dann ist seine Negation als das Unendliche fixirt, als das Jenseits des Quantums, welches als ein Diesseits steht, als ein Unmittelbares; so ist das Unendliche nur als erste Negation bestimmt, und so erscheint es im unendlichen Progresse. Es ist gezeigt worden, daß aber in diesem mehr vorhanden ist, die Negation der Negation, oder das, was das Unendliche in Wahrheit ist. Es ist dieß vorhin so angesehen worden, daß der Begriff des Quantums damit wieder hergestellt ist; diese Wiederherstellung heißt zunächst, daß sein Daseyn seine nähere Bestimmung erhalten hat; es ist nämlich das nach seinem Begriff bestimmte Quantum entstanden, was verschieden ist, von dem unmittelbaren Quantum, die Äußerlichkeit ist nun das Gegentheil ihrer selbst, als Moment der Größe selbst gesetzt,—das Quantum so, daß es vermittelst seines Nichtseyns, der Unendlichkeit, in einem anderen Quantum seine Bestimmtheit habe, d. i. qualitativ das ist, was es ist. Jedoch gehört diese Vergleichung des Begriffs des Quantums mit seinem Daseyn mehr unserer Reflexion, einem Verhältniß, das hier noch nicht vorhanden ist, an. Die zunächst liegende Bestimmung ist, daß das Quantum zur Qualität zurückgekehrt, nunmehr qualitativ bestimmt ist. Denn seine Eigenthümlichkeit, Qualität, ist die Äußerlichkeit, Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmtheit; und es ist nun gesetzt, als in seiner Äußerlichkeit vielmehr es selbst zu seyn, darin sich auf sich selbst zu beziehen, in einfacher Einheit mit sich, d. i. qualitativ bestimmt zu seyn.—dieß Qualitative ist noch näher bestimmt, nämlich als Fürsichseyn; denn die Beziehung auf sich selbst, zu der es gekommen, ist aus der Vermittelung, der Negation der Negation, hervorgegangen. Das Quantum hat die Unendlichkeit, das Fürsichbestimmtseyn nicht mehr außer ihm, sondern an ihm selbst.\n\nDas Unendliche, welches im unendlichen Progresse nur die leere Bedeutung eines Nichtsseyns, eines unerreichten, aber gesuchten Jenseits hat, ist in der That nicht anderes als die Qualität. Das Quantum geht als gleichgültige Grenze über sich hinaus ins Unendliche; es sucht damit nichts Anderes, als das Fürsichbestimmtseyn, das qualitative Moment, das aber so nur ein Sollen ist. Seine Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Grenze, damit sein Mangel an fürsichseyender Bestimmtheit und sein Hinausgehen über sich ist, was das Quantum zum Quantum macht; jenes sein Hinausgehen soll negirt werden und im Unendlichen sich seine absolute Bestimmtheit finden.\n\nGanz überhaupt: das Quantum ist die aufgehobene Qualität; aber das Quantum ist unendlich, geht über sich hinaus, es ist die Negation seiner; dieß sein Hinausgehen ist also an sich die Negation der negirten Qualität, die Wiederherstellung derselben; und gesetzt ist dieß, daß die Äußerlichkeit, welche als Jenseits erschien, als das eigene Moment des Quantums bestimmt ist.\n\nDas Quantum ist hiermit gesetzt als von sich repellirt, womit also zwei Quanta sind, diejedoch aufgehoben, nur als Momente einer Einheit sind, und diese Einheit ist die Bestimmtheit des Quantums.—Dieses so in seiner Äußerlichkeit als gleichgültige Grenze auf sich bezogen, hiermit qualitativ gesetzt, ist das quantitative Verhältniß.—Im Verhältnisse ist das Quantum sich äußerlich, von sich selbst verschieden; diese seine Äußerlichkeit ist die Beziehung eines Quantums auf ein anderes Quantum, deren jedes nur gilt in dieser seiner Beziehung auf sein Anderes; und diese Beziehunng macht die Bestimmtheit des Quantums aus, das als solche Einheit ist.\n\nEs hat darin nicht eine gleichgültige, sondern qualitative Bestimmung; ist in dieser seiner Äußerlichkeit in sich zurückgekehrt, ist in derselben, das was es ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0001","text":"Das unendliche Quantum, als Unendlichgroßes oder Unendlichkleines, ist selbst an sich der unendliche Progreß; es ist Quantum als ein Großes oder Kleines, und ist zugleich Nichtseyn des Quantums. Das Unendlichgroße und Unendlichkleine sind daher Bilder der Vorstellung, die bei näherer Betrachtung sich als nichtiger Nebel und Schatten zeigen. Im unendlichen Progreß aber ist dieser Widerspruch explicite vorhanden, und damit das, was die Natur des Quantums ist, das als intensive Größe seine Realität erreicht hat, und in seinem Daseyn nun gesetzt, wie es in seinem Begriffe ist. Diese Identität ist es, die zu betrachten ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"72.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0002","text":"Das Quantum als Grad ist einfach, auf sich bezogen und als an ihm selbst bestimmt. Indem durch diese Einfachheit das Andersseyn und die Bestimmtheit an ihm aufgehoben ist, ist diese ihm äußerlich; es hat seine Bestimmtheit außer ihm. Dieß sein Außersichseyn ist zunächst das abstrakte Nichtseyn des Quantums überhaupt, die schlechte Unendlichkeit. Aber ferner ist dieß Nichtseyn auch ein Großes, das Quantum kontinuirt sich in sein Nichtseyn, denn es hat eben seine Bestimmtheit in seiner Äußerlichkeit; diese seine Äußerlichkeit ist daher eben so sehr selbst Quantum; jenes sein Nichtseyn, die Unendlichkeit, wird so begrenzt, d. h. dieß Jenseits wird aufgehoben, dieses ist selbst als Quantum bestimmt, das hiermit in seiner Negation bei sich selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"72.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0003","text":"Dieß ist aber das, was das Quantum als solches an sich ist. Denn es ist eben es selbst durch sein Äußerlichseyn; die Äußerlichkeit macht das aus, wodurch es Quantum, bei sich selbst, ist. Es ist also im unendlichen Progresse der Begriff des Quantums gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"72.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0004","text":"Nehmen wir ihn zunächst in seinen abstrakten Bestimmungen wie sie vorliegen, so ist in ihm das Aufheben des Quantums, aber eben so sehr seines Jenseits, also die Negation des Quantums sowohl, als die Negation dieser Negation vorhanden. Seine Wahrheit ist ihre Einheit, worin sie, aber als Momente, sind.—Sie ist die Auflösung des Widerspruchs, dessen Ausdruck er ist, und ihr nächster Sinn somit die Wiederherstellung des Begriffs der Größe, daß sie gleichgültige oder äußerliche Grenze ist. Im unendlichen Progresse als solchem pflegt nur darauf reflektirt zu werden, daß jedes Quantum, es sey noch so groß oder klein, verschwinden, daß über dasselbe muß hinausgegangen werden können; aber nicht darauf, daß dieß sein Aufheben, das Jenseits, das schlecht-Unendliche selbst auch verschwindet.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"72.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0005","text":"Schon das erste Aufheben, die Negation der Qualität überhaupt, wodurch das Quantum gesetzt wird, ist an sich das Aufheben der Negation,—das Quantum ist aufgehobene qualitative Grenze, somit aufgehobene Negation,—aber es ist zugleich nur an sich dieß; gesetzt ist es als ein Daseyn, und dann ist seine Negation als das Unendliche fixirt, als das Jenseits des Quantums, welches als ein Diesseits steht, als ein Unmittelbares; so ist das Unendliche nur als erste Negation bestimmt, und so erscheint es im unendlichen Progresse. Es ist gezeigt worden, daß aber in diesem mehr vorhanden ist, die Negation der Negation, oder das, was das Unendliche in Wahrheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"72.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0006","text":"Es ist dieß vorhin so angesehen worden, daß der Begriff des Quantums damit wieder hergestellt ist; diese Wiederherstellung heißt zunächst, daß sein Daseyn seine nähere Bestimmung erhalten hat; es ist nämlich das nach seinem Begriff bestimmte Quantum entstanden, was verschieden ist, von dem unmittelbaren Quantum, die Äußerlichkeit ist nun das Gegentheil ihrer selbst, als Moment der Größe selbst gesetzt,—das Quantum so, daß es vermittelst seines Nichtseyns, der Unendlichkeit, in einem anderen Quantum seine Bestimmtheit habe, d. i. qualitativ das ist, was es ist. Jedoch gehört diese Vergleichung des Begriffs des Quantums mit seinem Daseyn mehr unserer Reflexion, einem Verhältniß, das hier noch nicht vorhanden ist, an. Die zunächst liegende Bestimmung ist, daß das Quantum zur Qualität zurückgekehrt, nunmehr qualitativ bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"72.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0007","text":"Denn seine Eigenthümlichkeit, Qualität, ist die Äußerlichkeit, Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmtheit; und es ist nun gesetzt, als in seiner Äußerlichkeit vielmehr es selbst zu seyn, darin sich auf sich selbst zu beziehen, in einfacher Einheit mit sich, d. i. qualitativ bestimmt zu seyn.—dieß Qualitative ist noch näher bestimmt, nämlich als Fürsichseyn; denn die Beziehung auf sich selbst, zu der es gekommen, ist aus der Vermittelung, der Negation der Negation, hervorgegangen. Das Quantum hat die Unendlichkeit, das Fürsichbestimmtseyn nicht mehr außer ihm, sondern an ihm selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"72.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0008","text":"Das Unendliche, welches im unendlichen Progresse nur die leere Bedeutung eines Nichtsseyns, eines unerreichten, aber gesuchten Jenseits hat, ist in der That nicht anderes als die Qualität. Das Quantum geht als gleichgültige Grenze über sich hinaus ins Unendliche; es sucht damit nichts Anderes, als das Fürsichbestimmtseyn, das qualitative Moment, das aber so nur ein Sollen ist. Seine Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Grenze, damit sein Mangel an fürsichseyender Bestimmtheit und sein Hinausgehen über sich ist, was das Quantum zum Quantum macht; jenes sein Hinausgehen soll negirt werden und im Unendlichen sich seine absolute Bestimmtheit finden.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"72.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0009","text":"Ganz überhaupt: das Quantum ist die aufgehobene Qualität; aber das Quantum ist unendlich, geht über sich hinaus, es ist die Negation seiner; dieß sein Hinausgehen ist also an sich die Negation der negirten Qualität, die Wiederherstellung derselben; und gesetzt ist dieß, daß die Äußerlichkeit, welche als Jenseits erschien, als das eigene Moment des Quantums bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"72.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0010","text":"Das Quantum ist hiermit gesetzt als von sich repellirt, womit also zwei Quanta sind, diejedoch aufgehoben, nur als Momente einer Einheit sind, und diese Einheit ist die Bestimmtheit des Quantums.—Dieses so in seiner Äußerlichkeit als gleichgültige Grenze auf sich bezogen, hiermit qualitativ gesetzt, ist das quantitative Verhältniß.—Im Verhältnisse ist das Quantum sich äußerlich, von sich selbst verschieden; diese seine Äußerlichkeit ist die Beziehung eines Quantums auf ein anderes Quantum, deren jedes nur gilt in dieser seiner Beziehung auf sein Anderes; und diese Beziehunng macht die Bestimmtheit des Quantums aus, das als solche Einheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"72.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0011","text":"Es hat darin nicht eine gleichgültige, sondern qualitative Bestimmung; ist in dieser seiner Äußerlichkeit in sich zurückgekehrt, ist in derselben, das was es ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"72.11"}],"sha256":"891b2c0db96dcc87e636c751f49d1dabf4845ad9001472a666b5fa576febc8e1","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103207770273Z_66aabe1d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Infinity of Quantum.","source_sha256":"891b2c0db96dcc87e636c751f49d1dabf4845ad9001472a666b5fa576febc8e1","sha256":"69d9bcaccbae309e4e5f9922e0758297d67710184e2c9478a582d52ce0b5cef4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:32:07.770301+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0001","text":"The infinite quantum, as infinitely large or infinitely small, is itself in itself the infinite progress; it is quantum as a large or small [magnitude], and is at the same time non-being of quantum. The infinitely large and infinitely small are therefore images of representation which, upon closer consideration, show themselves to be vain mist and shadow. But in infinite progress this contradiction is explicitly present, and therewith that which constitutes the nature of quantum, which, as intensive magnitude, has attained its reality and is now posited in its existence as it is in its concept. It is this identity that is to be considered.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"72.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0002","text":"Quantum as degree is simple, related to itself, and determined as in itself. Since through this simplicity otherness and determinateness are sublated in it, the latter is external to it; it has its determinateness outside itself. This its being-outside-itself is initially the abstract non-being of quantum in general, bad infinity. But further, this non-being is also a large [magnitude]; quantum continues into its non-being, for it has precisely its determinateness in its externality; this its externality is therefore itself just as much quantum; that its non-being, infinity, thus becomes bounded, i.e. this beyond is sublated; it is itself determined as quantum, which thereby is with itself in its negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"72.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0003","text":"But this is what quantum as such is in itself. For it is precisely itself through its being-external; externality constitutes that whereby it is quantum, with itself. Thus in infinite progress the concept of quantum is posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"72.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0004","text":"If we first take it in its abstract determinations as they are at hand, then the sublation of quantum is present in it, but equally that of its beyond, hence the negation of quantum as well as the negation of this negation. Its truth is their unity, in which they are, but as moments.—It is the resolution of the contradiction of which it is the expression, and its immediate meaning is thus the restoration of the concept of magnitude, namely that it is indifferent or external limit. In infinite progress as such, reflection is usually confined to the fact that every quantum, however large or small it may be, vanishes, that one must be able to go beyond it; but not to the fact that this its sublation, the beyond, bad infinity itself, also vanishes.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"72.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0005","text":"Already the first sublation, the negation of quality in general, whereby quantum is posited, is in itself the sublation of negation,—quantum is sublated qualitative limit, hence sublated negation,—but it is at the same time this only in itself; it is posited as an existence, and then its negation is fixed as the infinite, as the beyond of quantum, which stands as a here-side, as an immediate; thus the infinite is determined only as first negation, and thus it appears in infinite progress. It has been shown, however, that more is present in this: the negation of negation, or that which the infinite is in truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"72.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0006","text":"This was previously regarded in such a way that the concept of quantum is thereby restored; this restoration initially means that its existence has received its more specific determination; namely, the quantum determined according to its concept has arisen, which is different from immediate quantum: externality is now posited as the opposite of itself, as a moment of magnitude itself,—quantum in such a way that by means of its non-being, infinity, it has its determinateness in another quantum, i.e. is qualitatively what it is. Yet this comparison of the concept of quantum with its existence belongs more to our reflection, to a relation which is not yet present here. The immediately forthcoming determination is that quantum has returned to quality and is now qualitatively determined.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"72.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0007","text":"For its peculiarity, quality, is the externality, indifference of determinateness; and it is now posited as rather being itself in its externality, as therein relating itself to itself, in simple unity with itself, i.e. as being qualitatively determined.—This qualitative is more closely determined still, namely as being-for-self; for the relation to itself at which it has arrived has arisen from mediation, the negation of negation. Quantum no longer has infinity, determination-for-self, outside itself, but in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"72.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0008","text":"The infinite, which in infinite progress has only the empty meaning of a non-being, of an unattained but sought beyond, is in fact nothing other than quality. Quantum, as indifferent limit, goes beyond itself into infinity; thereby it seeks nothing other than determination-for-self, the qualitative moment, which, however, is thus only an ought. Its indifference toward limit, and therewith its lack of determinateness that is for itself and its going beyond itself, is what makes quantum into quantum; that its going beyond is to be negated, and in the infinite its absolute determinateness is to find itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"72.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0009","text":"Quite generally: quantum is sublated quality; but quantum is infinite, goes beyond itself, it is its own negation; this its going beyond is thus in itself the negation of negated quality, its restoration; and this is posited: that externality, which appeared as beyond, is determined as the proper moment of quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"72.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0010","text":"Quantum is thereby posited as repelled from itself, whereby there are thus two quanta, which, however, are sublated and are only moments of a unity, and this unity is the determinateness of quantum.—This, thus related to itself in its externality as indifferent limit, thereby qualitatively posited, is quantitative relation.—In relation, quantum is external to itself, different from itself; this its externality is the relation of one quantum to another quantum, each of which is valid only in this its relation to its other; and this relating constitutes the determinateness of quantum, which is such unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"72.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0011","text":"In this it has not an indifferent, but a qualitative determination; in this its externality it has returned into itself; in it, it is what it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"72.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDUD:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"a87aa2ddc8e515158ba6835a9c2d686082a1980a7f07cf3be6800d25ac2a3289","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die Unendlichkeit des Quantums."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die Unendlichkeit des Quantums.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB","title":"Remark 1. The Conceptual Determinacy of the Mathematical Infinite.","order":73,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A1DB","text":"Das mathematische Unendliche ist eines Theils interessant durch die Erweiterung der Mathematik und die großen Resultate, welche seine Einführung in dieselbe hervorgebracht hat; andern Theils aber ist es dadurch merkwürdig, daß es dieser Wissenschaft noch nicht gelungen ist, sich über den Gebrauch desselben durch den Begriff (Begriff im eigentlichen Sinne genommen) zu rechtfertigen. Die Rechtfertigungen beruhen am Ende auf der Richtigkeit der mit Hülfe jener Bestimmung sich ergebenden Resultate, welche aus sonstigen Gründen erwiesen ist; nicht aber auf der Klarheit des Gegenstandes und der Operation, durch welche die Resultate herausgebracht werden, sogar daß die Operation vielmehr selbst als unrichtig zugegeben wird.\n\nDieß ist schon ein Mißstand an und für sich; ein solches Verfahren ist unwissenschaftlich. Es führt aber auch den Nachtheil mit sich, daß die Mathematik, indem sie die Natur dieses ihres Instruments nicht kennt, weil sie mit der Metaphysik und Kritik desselben nicht fertig ist, den Umfang seiner Anwendung nicht bestimmen, und von Misbräuchen desselben sich nicht sichern konnte.\n\nIn philosophischer Rücksicht aber ist das mathematische Unendliche darum wichtig, weil ihm in der That der Begriff des wahrhaften Unendlichen zu Grunde liegt und es viel höher steht, als das gewöhnlich sogenannte metaphysische Unendliche, von dem aus die Einwürfe gegen ersteres gemacht werden. Gegen diese Einwürfe weiß sich die Wissenschaft der Mathematik häufig nur dadurch zu retten, daß sie die Kompetenz der Metaphysik verwirft, indem sie behauptet, mit dieser Wissenschaft nichts zu schaffen und sich um deren Begriffe nicht zu bekümmern zu haben, wenn sie nur auf ihrem eigenen Boden konsequent verfahre. Sie habe nicht zu betrachten, was an sich, sondern was auf ihrem Felde das Wahre sey. Die Metaphysik weiß die glänzenden Resultate des Gebrauchs des mathematischen Unendlichen bei ihrem Widerspruche gegen dasselbe nicht zu läugnen oder umzustoßen, und die Mathematik weiß mit der Metaphysik ihres eigenen Begriffs und daher auch mit der Ableitung der Verfahrensweisen, die der Gebrauch des Unendlichen nöthig macht, nicht ins Reine zu kommen.\n\nWenn es die einzige Schwierigkeit des Begriffs überhaupt wäre, von der die Mathematik gedrückt würde, so könnte sie diesen ohne Umstände auf der Seite liegen lassen, insofern nämlich der Begriff mehr ist, als nur die Angabe der wesentlichen Bestimmtheiten, d. i. der Verstandesbestimmungen einer Sache, und an der Schärfe dieser Bestimmtheiten hat sie es nicht fehlen lassen; denn sie ist nicht eine Wissenschaft, die es mit den Begriffen ihrer Gegenstände zu thun, und durch die Entwickelung des Begriffs, wenn auch nur durch Raisonnement, ihren Inhalt zu erzeugen hätte. Allein bei der Methode ihres Unendlichen findet sie den Hauptwiderspruch an der eigenthümlichen Methode selbst, auf welcher sie überhaupt als Wissenschaft beruht. Denn die Rechnung des Unendlichen erlaubt und erfordert Verfahrungsweisen, welche die Mathematik bei Operationen mit endlichen Größen durchaus verwerfen muß, und zugleich behandelt sie ihre unendlichen Größen, wie endliche Quanta, und will auf jene dieselben Verfahrungsweisen anwenden, welche bei diesen gelten; es ist eine Hauptseite der Ausbildung dieser Wissenschaft, für die transcendenten Bestimmungen und deren Behandlung, die Form des gewöhnlichen Kalkuls gewonnen zu haben.\n\nDie Mathematik zeigt bei diesem Widerstreite ihrer Operationen, daß Resultate, die sie dadurch findet, ganz mit denen übereinstimmen, welche durch die eigentlich mathematische, die geometrische und analytische, Methode gefunden werden. Aber Theils betrifft dieß nicht alle Resultate, und der Zweck der Einführung des Unendlichen ist nicht allein, den gewöhnlichen Weg abzukürzen, sondern zu Resultaten zu gelangen, die durch diesen nicht geleistet werden können. Theils rechtfertigt der Erfolg die Manier des Wegs nicht für sich. Diese Manier aber der Rechnung des Unendlichen zeigt sich durch den Schein der Ungenauigkeit gedrückt, den sie sich giebt, indem sie endliche Größen um eine unendlich kleine Größe das eine Mal vermehrt, diese in der fernern Operation zum Theil beibehält, aber einen Theil derselben auch vernachlässigt. Dieß Verfahren enthält die Sonderbarkeit, daß der eingestandenen Ungenauigkeit unerachtet, ein Resultat herauskommt, das nicht nur ziemlich und so nahe, daß der Unterschied außer Acht gelassen werden könnte, sondern vollkommen genau ist. In der Operation selbst aber, die dem Resultate vorher geht, kann die Vorstellung nicht entbehrt werden, daß Einiges nicht gleich Null, aber so unbeträchtlich sey, um außer Acht gelassen werden zu können. Allein bei dem, was unter mathematischer Bestimmtheit zu verstehen ist, fällt aller Unterschied einer größern oder geringern Genauigkeit gänzlich hinweg, wie in der Philosophie nicht von größerer oder geringerer Wahrscheinlichkeit, sondern von der Wahrheit allein die Rede seyn kann. Wenn die Methode und der Gebrauch des Unendlichen durch den Erfolg gerechtfertigt wird, so ist es nicht so überflüssig dessen ungeachtet die Rechtfertigung derselben zu fordern, als es bei der Nase überflüssig scheint, nach dem Erweise des Rechts, sich ihrer zu bedienen, zu fragen. Denn es ist bei der mathematischen als einer wissenschaftlichen Erkenntniß wesentlich um den Beweis zu thun, und auch in Ansehung der Resultate ist es der Fall, daß die streng mathematische Methode nicht zu allen den Beleg des Erfolgs liefert, der aber ohnehin nur ein äußerlicher Beleg ist.\n\nEs ist der Mühe werth, den mathematischen Begriff des Unendlichen und die merkwürdigsten Versuche näher zu betrachten, welche die Absicht haben, den Gebrauch desselben zu rechtfertigen und die Schwierigkeit, von der sich die Methode gedrückt fühlt, zu beseitigen. Die Betrachtung dieser Rechtfertigungen und Bestimmungen des mathematischen Unendlichen, welche ich in dieser Anmerkung weitläufiger anstellen will, wird zugleich das beste Licht auf die Natur des wahren Begriffes selbst werfen, und zeigen, wie er ihnen vorgeschwebt und zu Grunde gelegen hat.\n\nDie gewöhnliche Bestimmung des mathematischen Unendlichen ist, daß es eine Größe sey, über welche es,—wenn sie als das Unendlichgroße—keine größere oder,—wenn sie als das Unendlichkleine bestimmt ist—kleinere mehr gebe, oder die, in jenem Falle, größer, in diesem Falle kleiner sey, als jede beliebige Größe.—In dieser Definition ist freilich der wahre Begriff nicht ausgedrückt, vielmehr nur, wie schon bemerkt, derselbe Widerspruch, der im unendlichen Progresse ist; aber sehen wir, was an sich darin enthalten ist. Eine Größe wird in der Mathematik definirt, daß sie etwas sey, das vermehrt und vermindert werden könne; überhaupt also eine gleichgültige Grenze. Indem nun das Unendlich Große oder Kleine ein solches ist, das nicht mehr vermehrt oder vermindert werden könne, so ist es in der That kein Quantum als solches mehr.\n\nDiese Konsequenz ist nothwendig und unmittelbar. Aber die Reflexion, daß das Quantum,—und ich nenne in dieser Anmerkung Quantum überhaupt, wie es ist, das endliche Quantum,—aufgehoben ist, ist es, welche nicht gemacht zu werden pflegt und die für das gewöhnliche Begreifen die Schwierigkeit ausmacht, indem das Quantum, indem es unendlich ist, als ein Aufgehobenes, als ein solches zu denken gefordert wird, das nicht ein Quantum ist, und dessen quantitative Bestimmtheit doch bleibt.\n\nUm das anzuführen, wie Kant jene Bestimmung beurtheilt, [9] so findet er sie nicht übereinstimmend mit dem, was man unter einem unendlichen Ganzen verstehe. \"Nach dem gewöhnlichen Begriffe sey eine Größe unendlich, über die keine größere (d. i. über die darin enthaltene Menge einer gegebenen Einheit) möglich ist; es sey aber keine Menge die größte, weil noch immer eine oder mehrere Einheiten hinzugefügt werden können.—Durch ein unendliches Ganzes dagegen werde nicht vorgestellt, wie groß es sey, mithin sey sein Begriff nicht der Begriff eines Maximums (oder Minimums), sondern es werde dadurch nur sein Verhältniß zu einer beliebig anzunehmenden Einheit gedacht, in Ansehung deren dasselbe größer ist, als alle Zahl. Je nachdem diese Einheit größer oder kleiner angenommen würde, würde das Unendliche größer oder kleiner seyn; allein die Unendlichkeit, da sie bloß in dem Verhältnisse zu dieser gegebenen Einheit bestehe, würde immer dieselbe bleiben, obgleich Freilich die absolute Größe des Ganzen dadurch gar nicht erkannt würde.\"\n\n[9] In der Anmerkung zur Thesis der ersten kosmologischen Antinomie, in der Kritik der reinen Vernunft.\n\nKant tadelt es, wenn unendliche Ganze als ein Maximum, als eine vollendete Menge einer gegebenen Einheit angesehen werden. Das Maximum oder Minimum als solches erscheint noch immer als ein Quantum, eine Menge. Solche Vorstellung kann die von Kant angeführte Konsequenz nicht ablehnen, die auf ein größeres oder kleineres Unendliches führt. Überhaupt indem das Unendliche als Quantum vorgestellt wird, gilt noch für dasselbe der Unterschied eines Größern oder Kleinern. Allein diese Kritik trifft nicht den Begriff des wahrhaften mathematischen Unendlichen, der unendlichen Differenz, denn diese ist kein endliches Quantum mehr.\n\nKants Begriff der Unendlichkeit dagegen, den er den wahren transcendentalen nennt, ist, \"daß die successive Synthesis der Einheit in Durchmessung eines Quantums niemals vollendet seyn könne.\" Es ist ein Quantum überhaupt als gegeben vorausgesetzt; dieß solle durch das Synthesiren der Einheit zu einer Anzahl, einem bestimmt anzugebenden Quantum gemacht werden, aber dieß Synthesiren niemals vollendet werden können. Hiermit ist wie erhellt, nichts als der Progreß ins Unendliche ausgesprochen, nur transcendental, d. i. eigentlich subjektiv und psychologisch vorgestellt. An sich soll zwar das Quantum vollendet seyn, aber transcendentaler Weise, nämlich im Subjekte, welches ihm ein Verhältniß zu einer Einheit giebt, entstehe nur eine solche Bestimmung des Quantums, die unvollendet und schlechthin mit einem Jenseits behaftet sey. Es wird also hier überhaupt beim Widerspruche, den die Größe enthält, stehen geblieben, aber vertheilt an das Objekt und das Subjekt, so daß jenem die Begrenztheit, diesem aber das Hinausgehen über jede von ihm aufgefaßte Bestimmtheit, in das schlechte Unendliche zukommt.\n\nEs ist dagegen vorhin gesagt worden, daß die Bestimmung des mathematischen Unendlichen und zwar wie es in der höhern Analysis gebraucht wird, dem Begriffe des wahrhaften Unendlichen entspricht; die Zusammenstellung beider Bestimmungen soll nun in ausführlicher Entwickelung vorgenommen werden.—Was zuerst das wahrhafte unendliche Quantum betrifft, so bestimmte es sich als an ihm selbst unendlich; es ist dieß, indem, wie sich ergeben hat, das endliche Quantum oder das Quantum überhaupt, und sein Jenseits, das schlechte Unendliche, auf gleiche Weise aufgehoben sind. Das aufgehobene Quantum ist damit in die Einfachheit und in die Beziehung auf sich selbst zurückgegangen, aber nicht nur wie das extensive, indem es in intensives Quantum überging, das seine Bestimmtheit nur an sich an einer äußern Vielfachheit hat, gegen die es jedoch gleichgültig und wovon es verschieden seyn soll. Das unendliche Quantum enthält vielmehr erstens die Äußerlichkeit und zweitens die Negation derselben an ihm selbst; so ist es nicht mehr irgend ein endliches Quantum, nicht eine Größebestimmtheit, die ein Daseyn als Quantum hätte, sondern es ist einfach, und daher nur als Moment; es ist eine Größebestimmtheit in qualitativer Form; seine Unendlichkeit ist, als eine qualitative Bestimmtheit zu seyn.—So als Moment ist es in wesentlicher Einheit mit seinem Andern, nur als bestimmt durch dieses sein Anderes, d. i. es hat nur Bedeutung in Beziehung auf ein im Verhältniß mit ihm Stehendes. Außer diesem Verhältnisse ist es Null; —da gerade das Quantum als solches gegen das Verhältniß gleichgültig, in ihm doch eine unmittelbare ruhende Bestimmung seyn soll. In dem Verhältnisse als nur Moment ist es nicht ein für sich Gleichgültiges; es ist, in der Unendlichkeit als Fürsichseyn, indem es zugleich eine quantitative Bestimmtheit ist, nur als ein Für-Eines.\n\nDer Begriff des Unendlichen, wie er sich hier abstrakt exponirt hat, wird sich zeigen, dem mathematischen Unendlichen zu Grunde liegen, und er selbst wird deutlicher werden, indem wir die verschiedenen Stufen des Ausdrucks des Quantums als eines Verhältniß-Moments betrachten, von der untersten an, wo es noch zugleich Quantum als solches ist, bis zu der höhern, wo es die Bedeutung und den Ausdruck eigentlicher unendlicher Größe erhält.\n\nNehmen wir also zuerst das Quantum in dem Verhältnisse, wie es eine gebrochene Zahl ist. Solcher Bruch 2/7 z.B. ist nicht ein Quantum wie 1, 2, 3 u.s.f., zwar eine gewöhnliche endliche Zahl, jedoch nicht eine unmittelbare, wie die ganzen Zahlen, sondern als Bruch mittelbar bestimmt durch zwei andere Zahlen, die Anzahl und Einheit gegeneinander sind, wobei auch die Einheit eine bestimmte Anzahl ist. Aber von dieser nähern Bestimmung derselben gegeneinander abstrahirt, und sie bloß nach dem, was ihnen in der qualitativen Beziehung, in der sie hier sind, als Quantis widerfährt, betrachtet, so sind 2 und 7 sonst gleichgültige Quanta; indem sie aber hier nur als Momente, eines des andern, und damit eines Dritten (des Quantums, das der Exponent heißt) auftreten, so gelten sie sogleich nicht als 2 und 7, sondern nur nach ihrer Bestimmtheit gegeneinander. Statt ihrer kann darum eben so gut 4 und 14, oder 6 und 21 u.s.f. ins Unendliche gesetzt werden. Hiermit fangen sie also an, einen qualitativen Charakter zu haben. Gälten sie als bloße Quanta, so ist 2 und 7, schlechthin das eine nur 2, das andere nur 7; 4, 14, 6, 21 u.s.f. sind schlechthin etwas Anderes als jene Zahlen, und können insofern sie nur unmittelbare Quanta wären, die einen nicht an die Stelle der anderen gesetzt werden. Insofern aber und nicht nach der Bestimmtheit, solche Quanta zu seyn, gelten, so ist ihre gleichgültige Grenze aufgehoben; sie haben somit, nach dieser Seite, das Moment der Unendlichkeit an ihnen, indem sie nicht bloß eben nicht mehr sie sind, sondern ihre quantitative Bestimmtheit, aber als eine an sich seyende qualitative,—nämlich nach dem, was sie im Verhältnisse gelten,—bleibt. Es können unendlich viele andere an ihre Stelle gesetzt werden, so daß der Werth des Bruches durch, die Bestimmtheit, welche das Verhältniß hat, sich nicht ändert.\n\nDie Darstellung, welche die Unendlichkeit an einem Zahlenbruche hat, ist aber darum noch unvollkommen, weil die beiden Seiten des Bruchs, 2 und 7, aus dem Verhältnisse genommen werden können, und gewöhnliche gleichgültige Quanta sind; die Beziehung derselben, im Verhältnisse und Momente zu seyn, ist ihnen etwas Äußerliches und Gleichgültiges. Ebenso ist ihre Beziehung selbst ein gewöhnliches Quantum, der Exponent des Verhältnisses.\n\nDie Buchstaben, mit denen in der allgemeinen Arithmetik operirt wird, die nächste Allgemeinheit, in welche die Zahlen erhoben werden, haben die Eigenschaft nicht, daß sie von einem bestimmten Zahlenwerth sind; sie sind nur allgemeine Zeichen und unbestimmte Möglichkeiten jedes bestimmten Werthes. Der Bruch a/b scheint daher ein passenderer Ausdruck des Unendlichen zu seyn, weil a und b aus ihrer Beziehung aufeinander genommen, unbestimmt bleiben, und auch getrennt keinen besonderen eigenthümlichen Werth haben.—Allein diese Buchstaben sind zwar als unbestimmte Größen gesetzt; ihr Sinn aber ist, daß sie irgend ein endliches Quantum seyen. Da sie also zwar die allgemeine Vorstellung, aber nur von der bestimmten Zahl sind, so ist es ihnen ebenfalls gleichgültig, im Verhältnisse zu seyn, und außer demselben behalten sie diesen Werth.\n\nBetrachten wir noch näher, was im Verhältnisse vorhanden ist, so hat es die beiden Bestimmungen an ihm, erstlich ein Quantum zu seyn, dieses aber ist zweitens nicht als ein unmittelbares, sondern das den qualitativen Gegensatz an ihm hat; es bleibt in demselben zugleich jenes bestimmte, gleichgültige Quantum dadurch, daß es aus seinem Andersseyn, dem Gegensatze, in sich zurückgekehrt, somit auch ein Unendliches ist. Diese beiden Bestimmungen stellen sich in der folgenden bekannten Form, in ihrem Unterschiede von einander entwickelt dar.\n\nDer Bruch 2/7 kann ausgedrückt werden als 0,285714…als 1 + a + a[hoch2] + a[hoch3] u.s.f. So ist er als eine unendliche Reihe; der Bruch selbst heißt die Summe oder der endliche Ausdruck derselben. Vergleichen wir die beiden Ausdrücke, so stellt der eine, die unendliche Reihe, ihn nicht mehr als Verhältniß, sondern nach der Seite dar, daß er ein Quantum ist als eine Menge von solchen, die zu einander hinzukommen, als eine Anzahl.—Daß die Größen, die ihn als Anzahl ausmachen sollen, wieder aus Decimalbrüchen, also selbst aus Verhältnissen bestehen, darauf kommt es hier nicht an; denn dieser Umstand betrifft die besondere Art der Einheit dieser Größen, nicht sie, insofern sie die Anzahl constituiren; wie auch eine aus mehreren Ziffern bestehende ganze Zahl des Decimalsystems wesentlich als eine Anzahl gilt, und nicht darauf gesehen wird, daß sie aus Produkten einer Zahl und der Zahl Zehen und deren Potenzen besteht. So wie es hier auch nicht darauf ankommt, daß es andere Brüche giebt als der z. B. genommene 2/7, die zu Dezimalbrüchen gemacht, nicht eine unendliche Reihe geben; jeder aber kann für ein Zahlensystem von anderer Einheit als eine solche ausgedrückt werden.\n\nIndem nun in der unendlichen Reihe, die den Bruch als Anzahl darstellen soll, die Seite, daß er Verhältniß ist, verschwindet, so verschwindet auch die Seite, nach welcher er, wie vorhin gezeigt, die Unendlichkeit an ihm hatte. Diese aber ist auf eine andere Weise hereingekommen; die Reihe ist nämlich selbst unendlich.\n\nVon welcher Art nun die Unendlichkeit der Reihe sey, erhellt von selbst; es ist die schlechte Unendlichkeit des Progresses. Die Reihe enthält und stellt den Widerspruch dar, etwas, das ein Verhältniß ist und qualitative Natur in ihm hat, als ein Verhältnißloses, als ein bloßes Quantum, als Anzahl, darzustellen. Die Folge davon ist, daß an der Anzahl, die in der Reihe ausgedrückt ist, immer etwas fehlt, so daß über das, was gesetzt ist, immer hinausgegangen werden muß, um die geforderte Bestimmtheit zu erreichen. Das Gesetz des Fortgangs ist bekannt, es liegt in der Bestimmung des Quantums, die im Bruche enthalten ist, und in der Natur der Form, in der sie ausgedrückt werden soll. Die Anzahl kann wohl durch Fortsetzung der Reihe so genau gemacht werden, als man nöthig hat; aber immer bleibt die Darstellung durch sie nur ein Sollen; sie ist mit einem Jenseits behaftet, das nicht aufgehoben werden kann, weil ein auf qualitativer Bestimmtheit beruhendes als Anzahl auszudrücken der bleibende Widerspruch ist.\n\nIn dieser unendlichen Reihe ist jene Ungenauigkeit wirklich vorhanden, von der am wahrhaften mathematischen Unendlichen nur der Schein vorkommt. Diese beiden Arten des mathematischen Unendlichen sind so wenig zu verwechseln, als die beiden Arten des philosophischen Unendlichen. Bei der Darstellung des wahrhaften mathematischen Unendlichen ist anfangs die Form der Reihe gebraucht oder auch neuerlich wieder hervorgerufen worden. Aber sie ist für dasselbe nicht nothwendig; im Gegentheil ist das Unendliche der unendlichen Reihe wesentlich von jenem unterschieden, wie die Folge zeigen soll. Diese vielmehr steht sogar dem Ausdrucke des Bruches nach.\n\nDie unendliche Reihe enthält nämlich die schlechte Unendlichkeit, weil das, was die Reihe ausdrücken soll, ein Sollen bleibt; und was sie ausdrückt, mit einem Jenseits, das nicht verschwindet, behaftet und verschieden von dem ist, was ausgedrückt werden soll. Sie ist unendlich nicht um der Glieder willen, die gesetzt sind, sondern darum, weil sie unvollständig sind, weil das Andere, das zu ihnen wesentlich gehört, jenseits ihrer ist; was in ihr da ist, der gesetzten Glieder mögen so viele seyn als wollen, ist nur ein Endliches, im eigentlichen Sinne, gesetzt als Endliches, d. i. als solches, das nicht ist, was es seyn soll. Dagegen ist aber das, was der endliche Ausdruck, oder die Summe solcher Reihe genannt wird, ohne Mangel; er enthält den Werth, den die Reihe nur sucht, vollständig; das Jenseits ist aus der Flucht zurückgerufen; was er ist, und was er seyn soll, ist nicht getrennt, sondern ist dasselbe.\n\nDas beide Unterscheidende liegt näher sogleich darin, daß in der unendlichen Reihe das Negative außerhalb ihrer Glieder ist, welche Gegenwart haben, indem sie nur als Theile der Anzahl gelten. In dem endlichen Ausdrucke dagegen, der ein Verhältniß ist, ist das Negative immanent, als das Bestimmtseyn der Seiten des Verhältnisses durcheinander, welches ein in sich Zurückgekehrtseyn, sich auf sich beziehende Einheit, als Negation der Negation (beide Seiten des Verhältnisses sind nur als Momente), ist, hiermit die Bestimmung der Unendlichkeit in sich hat.—Zu der That ist also die gewöhnlich sogenannte Summe, das 2/7 oder 1/1-a', ein Verhältniß; und dieser sogenannte endliche Ausdruck ist der wahrhaft unendliche Ausdruck. Die unendliche Reihe dagegen ist in Wahrheit Summe; ihr Zweck ist, das was an sich Verhältniß ist, in der Form einer Summe darzustellen, und die vorhandenen Glieder der Reihe sind nicht als Glieder eines Verhältnisses, sondern eines Aggregats. Sie ist ferner vielmehr der endliche Ausdruck; denn sie ist das unvollkommene Aggregat, und bleibt wesentlich ein Mangelhaftes. Sie ist nach dem, was in ihr da ist, ein bestimmtes Quantum, zugleich aber ein geringeres, als sie seyn soll; alsdann auch das, was ihr fehlt, ist ein bestimmtes Quantum; dieser fehlende Theil ist in der That das, was das Unendliche an der Reihe heißt, nach der nur formellen Seite, daß er ein Fehlendes, ein Nichtseyn ist; nach seinem Inhalte ist er ein endliches Quantum. Das was in der Reihe da ist, zusammen mit dem was ihr fehlt, macht erst das aus, was der Bruch ist, das bestimmte Quantum, das sie gleichfalls seyn soll, aber zu seyn nicht vermag. —Das Wort: Unendlich, pflegt, auch in der unendlichen Reihe, in der Meinung etwas Hohes und Hehres zu seyn; es ist dieß eine Art von Aberglauben, der Aberglaube des Verstands; man hat gesehen, wie es sich vielmehr auf die Bestimmung der Mangelhaftigkeit reducirt.\n\nDaß es, kann noch bemerkt werden, unendliche Reihen giebt, die nicht summirbar sind, ist in Bezug auf die Form von Reihe überhaupt ein äußerlicher und zufälliger Umstand. Sie enthalten eine höhere Art der Unendlichkeit, als die summirbaren; nämlich eine Incommensurabilität, oder die Unmöglichkeit, das darin enthaltene quantitative Verhältniß als ein Quantum, sey es auch als Bruch, darzustellen; die Form der Reihe aber als solche, die sie haben, enthält dieselbe Bestimmung der schlechten Unendlichkeit, welche in der summirbaren Reihe ist.\n\nDie so eben am Bruche und an seiner Reihe bemerkte Verkehrung in Ansehung des Ausdrucks findet auch Statt, insofern das mathematische Unendliche nämlich nicht das so eben genannte sondern das wahrhafte, das relative Unendliche,—das gewöhnliche metaphysische dagegen, worunter das abstrakte, schlechte Unendliche verstanden wird, das absolute genannt worden ist. In der That ist vielmehr dieses metaphysische nur das relative, weil die Negation, die es ausdrückt, nur so im Gegensatze einer Grenze ist, daß diese außer ihm bestehen bleibt, und von ihm nicht aufgehoben wird; das mathematische Unendliche hingegen hat die endliche Grenze wahrhaft in sich aufgehoben, weil das Jenseits derselben mit ihr vereinigt ist.\n\nIn dem Sinne, in welchem aufgezeigt worden, daß die sogenannte Summe oder der endliche Ausdruck einer unendlichen Reihe, vielmehr als der unendliche anzusehen ist, ist es vornehmlich, daß Spinoza den Begriff der wahren Unendlichkeit gegen den der schlechten aufstellt und durch Beispiele erläutert. Sein Begriff gewinnt am neisten Licht, indem ich das, was er hierüber sagt, an diese Entwickelung anschließe.\n\nEr definirt zunächst das Unendliche als die absolute Affirmation der Existenz irgend einer Natur, das Endliche im Gegentheil als Bestimmtheit, als Verneinung. Die absolute Affirmation einer Existenz ist nämlich als ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst zu nehmen, nicht dadurch zu seyn, daß ein Anderes ist; das Endliche hingegen ist die Verneinung, ein Aufhören als Beziehung auf ein Anderes, das außer ihm anfängt. Die absolute Affirmation einer Existenz erschöpft nun zwar den Begriff der Unendlichkeit nicht; dieser enthält, daß die Unendlichkeit Affirmation ist, nicht als unmittelbare, sondern nur als wiederhergestellte durch die Reflexion des Anderen in sich selbst, oder als Negation des Negativen. Aber bei Spinoza hat die Substanz und deren absolute Einheit die Form von unbewegter d. i. nicht sich mit sich selbst vermittelnder Einheit, von einer Starrheit, worin der Begriff der negativen Einheit des Selbst, die Subjektivität, sich noch nicht findet.\n\nDas mathematische Beispiel, womit er das wahre Unendliche (Epist. XXIX.) erläutert, ist ein Raum zwischen zwei ungleichen Kreisen, deren einer innerhalb des andern, ohne ihn zu berühren, fällt, und die nicht koncentrisch sind. Er machte, wie es scheint, sich viel aus dieser Figur und dem Begriffe als deren Beispiel er sie gebrauchte, daß er sie zum Motto seiner Ethik machte.—\"Die Mathematiker, sagt er, schließen, daß die Ungleichheiten, die in einem solchen Raume möglich sind, unendlich sind, nicht aus der unendlichen Menge der Theile, denn seine Größe ist bestimmt und begrenzt, und ich kann größere und kleinere solche Räume setzen, sondern weil die Natur der Sache jede Bestimmtheit übertrift.\"—Man sieht, Spinoza verwirftjene Vorstellung vom Unendlichen, nach welcher es als Menge oder als Reihe vorgestellt wird, die nicht vollendet ist, und erinnert, daß hier an dem Raume des Beispiels das Unendliche nichtjenseits, sondern gegenwärtig und vollständig ist; dieser Raum ist ein Begrenztes, aber darum ein Unendliches, \"weil die Natur der Sache jede Bestimmtheit übersteigt,\" weil die darin enthaltene Größenbestimmung zugleich nicht als ein Quantum darstellbar ist, oder nach obigem kantischen Ausdruck das Synthesiren nicht zu einem—diskreten—Quantum vollendet werden kann.—Wie überhaupt der Gegensatz von kontinuirlichem und diskretem Quantum auf das Unendliche führt, soll in einer spätern Anmerkung auseinander gesetzt werden.—Jenes Unendliche einer Reihe nennt Spinoza das Unendliche der Imagination; das Unendliche hingegen als Beziehung auf sich selbst, das Unendliche des Denkens oder infinitum actu. Es ist nämlich actu, es ist wirklich unendlich, weil es in sich vollendet und gegenwärtig ist. So ist die Reihe, 0,285714… oder 1 + a + a[hoch 2] + a[hoch 3]… das Unendliche bloß der Einbildung oder des Meinens; denn es hat keine Wirklichkeit, es fehlt ihm schlechthin etwas; hingegen 2/7 oder 1/1-a ist das wirklich, nicht nur was die Reihe in ihren vorhandenen Gliedern ist, sondern noch das dazu, was ihr mangelt, was sie nur seyn soll. Das 2/7 oder 1/1-a ist gleichfalls eine endliche Größe, wie der zwischen den zwei Kreisen eingeschlossene Raum Spinoza's und dessen Ungleichheiten; und kann wie dieser Raum größer oder kleiner gemacht werden. Aber es kommt damit nicht die Ungereimtheit eines größern oder kleinern Unendlichen heraus; denn dieß Quantum des Ganzen, geht das Verhältniß seiner Momente, die Natur der Sache d. h. die qualitative Größenbestimmung, nichts an; das was in der unendlichen Reihe da ist, ist ebenso ein endliches Quantum, aber außerdem noch ein Mangelhaftes.—Die Einbildung dagegen bleibt beim Quantum als solchem stehen, und reflektirt nicht auf die qualitative Beziehung, welche den Grund der vorhandenen Inkommensurabilität ausmacht.\n\nDie Inkommensurabilität, welche in dem Beispiel Spinoza's liegt, schließt überhaupt die Funktionen krummer Linien in sich, und führt näher auf das Unendliche, das die Mathematik bei solchen Funktionen, überhaupt bei den Funktionen veränderlicher Größen eingeführt hat, und welches das wahrhafte mathematische, quantitative Unendliche ist, das auch Spinoza sich dachte. Diese Bestimmung soll nun hier näher erörtert werden.\n\nWas vors erste die für so wichtig geltende Kategorie der Veränderlichkeit betrifft, unter welche die in jenen Funktionen bezogenen Größen gefaßt werden, so sollen sie zunächst veränderlich nicht in dem Sinne seyn, wie im Bruche 2/7 die beiden Zahlen 2 und 7, indem eben so sehr 4 und 14, 6 und 21 und so fort ins Unendliche andere Zahlen an ihre Stelle gesetzt werden können, ohne den im Bruche gesetzten Werth zu ändern. So kann noch mehr in a/b an die Stelle von a und b jede beliebige Zahl gesetzt werden, ohne das zu ändern was a/b ausdrücken soll. In dem Sinne nur, daß auch an die Stelle von x und y einer Funktion eine unendliche d. h. unerschöpfliche Menge von Zahlen gesetzt werden könne, sind a und b so sehr veränderliche Größe als jene, x und y. Der Ausdruck: veränderliche Größen, ist darum sehr vage, und unglücklich gewählt für Größebestimmungen, die ihr Interesse und Behandlungsart in etwas in etwas ganz Anderem liegen haben, als in ihrer bloßen Veränderlichkeit.\n\nUm es deutlich zu machen, worin die wahrhafte Bestimmung der Momente einer Funktion liegt, mit denen sich das Interesse der höhern Analysis beschäftigt, müssen wir die bemerklich gemachten Stufen noch einmal durchlaufen. In 2/7 oder a/b sind 2 und 7 jedes für sich, bestimmte Quanta und die Beziehung ist ihnen nicht wesentlich; a und b soll gleichfalls solche Quanta vorstellen, die auch außer dem Verhältnisse bleiben, was sie sind. Ferner ist auch 2/7 und a/b ein fixes Quantum, ein Quotient; das Verhältniß macht eine Anzahl aus, deren Einheit der Nenner, und die Anzahl dieser Einheiten der Zähler—oder umgekehrt ausdrückt; wenn auch 4 und 14 u.s.f. an die Stelle von 2 und 7 treten, bleibt das Verhältniß auch als Quantum dasselbe. Dieß verändert sich nun aber wesentlich in der Funktion y[hoch 2]/x = p z.B.; hier haben x und y zwar den Sinn, bestimmte Quanta seyn zu können; aber nicht x und y, sondern nur x und y[hoch 2] haben einen bestimmten Quotienten.\n\nDadurch sind diese Seiten des Verhältnisses, x und y, erstens nicht nur keine bestimmten Quanta, sondern zweitens ihr Verhältniß ist nicht ein fixes Quantum, (noch ist dabei ein solches wie bei a und b gemeint), nicht ein fester Quotient, sondern er ist als Quantum schlechthin veränderlich. Dieß aber ist allein darin enthalten, daß x nicht zu y ein Verhältniß hat, sondern zum Quadrate von y. Das Verhältniß einer Größe zur Potenz ist nicht ein Quantum, sondern wesentlich qualitatives Verhältniß; das Potenzenverhältniß ist der Umstand, der als Grundbestimmung anzusehen ist.—In der Function der geraden Linie y = a x aber, ist x/y = a ein gewöhnlicher Bruch und Quotient; diese Funktion ist daher nur formell eine Funktion von veränderlichen Größen, oder x und y sind hier was a und b in a/b, sie sind nicht in derjenigen Bestimmung, in welcher die Differential- und Integralrechnung sie betrachtet.—Wegen der besondern Natur der veränderlichen Größen in dieser Betrachtungsweise, wäre es zweckmäßig gewesen, für sie sowohl einen besonderen Namen, als andere Bezeichnungen einzuführen, als die gewöhnlichen der unbekannten Größen in jeder endlichen, bestimmten oder unbestimmten Gleichung; um ihrer wesentlichen Verschiedenheit willen von solchen bloß unbekannten Größen, die an sich vollkommen bestimmte Quanta, oder ein bestimmter Umfang von bestimmten Quantis sind.—Es ist auch nur der Mangel des Bewußtseyns, über die Eigenthümlichkeit dessen, was das Interesse der höheren Analysis ausmacht und das Bedürfniß und die Erfindung des Differential-Kalkuls herbeigeführt hat, daß Funktionen des ersten Grades wie die Gleichung der geraden Linie in die Behandlung dieses Kalkuls für sich mit hereingenommen werden; seinen Antheil an solchem Formalismus hat ferner der Mißverstand, der die an sich richtige Forderung der Verallgemeinerung einer Methode dadurch zu erfüllen meint, daß die specifische Bestimmtheit, auf\n\ndie sich das Bedürfniß gründet, weggelassen wird, daß es dafür gilt, als ob es sich in diesem Felde nur um veränderliche Größen überhaupt handle. Es wäre wohl viel Formalismus in den Betrachtungen dieser Gegenstände wie in der Behandlung erspart worden, wenn man eingesehen hätte, daß derselbe nicht veränderliche Größen als solche, sondern Potenzenbestimmungen betreffe.\n\nAber es ist noch eine weitere Stufe, auf der das mathematische Unendliche in seiner Eigenthümlichkeit hervortritt. In einer Gleichung, worin x und y zunächst als durch ein Potenzenverhältniß bestimmt, gesetzt sind, sollen x und y als solche noch Quanta bedeuten; diese Bedeutung nun geht vollends in den sogenannten unendlich kleinen Differenzen gänzlich verloren. d x, d y sind keine Quanta mehr, noch sollen sie solche bedeuten, sondern haben allein in ihrer Beziehung eine Bedeutung, einen Sinn blos als Momente. Sie sind nicht mehr Etwas, das Etwas als Quantum genommen, nicht endliche Differenzen; aber auch nicht Nichts, nicht die bestimmungslose Null. Außer ihrem Verhältnisse sind sie reine Nullen, aber sie sollen nur als Momente des Verhältnisses, als Bestimmungen des Differential-Koefficienten d x/ d y genommen werden.\n\nIn diesem Begriff des Unendlichen ist das Quantum wahrhaft zu einem qualitativen Daseyn vollendet; es ist als wirklich unendlich gesetzt; es ist nicht nur als dieses oder jenes Quantum aufgehoben, sondern als Quantum überhaupt. Es bleibt aber die Quantitätsbestimmtheit als Element von Quantis, Princip, oder sie wie man auch gesagt hat, in ihrem ersten Begriffe.\n\nGegen diesen Begriff ist aller Angriff gerichtet, der auf die Grundbestimmung der Mathematik dieses Unendlichen, der Differentialund Integralrechnung, gemacht worden ist. Unrichtige Vorstellungen der Mathematiker selbst veranlaßten es, wenn er nicht anerkannt worden ist; vornehmlich aber ist die Unvermögenheit, den Gegenstand als Begriff zu rechtfertigen, Schuld an diesen Anfechtungen. Den Begriff kann aber die Mathematik, wie oben erinnert worden, hier nicht umgehen; denn als Mathematik des Unendlichen schränkt sie sich nicht auf die endliche Bestimmtheit ihrer Gegenstände ein,—wie in der reinen Mathematik der Raum und die Zahl und deren Bestimmungen nur nach ihrer Endlichkeit betrachtet und auf einander bezogen werden—; sondern sie versetzt eine von daher aufgenommene und von ihr behandelte Bestimmung in Identität mit ihrer entgegengesetzten, wie sie z.B. eine krumme Linie zu einer geraden, den Kreis zu einem Polygon u.s.f. macht. Die Operationen, die sie sich als Differential- und Integralrechnung erlaubt, sind daher der Natur bloß endlicher Bestimmungen und deren Beziehungen gänzlich widersprechend und hätten darum ihre Rechtfertigung allein in dem Begriff.\n\nWenn die Mathematik des Unendlichen daran festhielt, daß jene Quantitäts-Bestimmungen verschwindende Größen d. h. solche, die nicht mehr irgend ein Quantum, aber auch nicht Nichts, sondern noch eine Bestimmtheit gegen Anderes sind, so schien nichts klarer, als daß es keinen solchen Mittelzustand, wie man es nannte, zwischen Seyn und Nichts gebe.—Was es mit diesem Einwurfe und sogenannten Mittelzustande auf sich habe, ist oben bereits bei der Kategorie des Werdens, Anmerk. 4. gezeigt. Allerdings ist die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts kein Zustand; ein Zustand wäre eine Bestimmung des Seyns und Nichts, worein diese Momente nur etwa zufälligerweise gleichsam als in eine Krankheit oder äußerliche Affektion durch ein irrthümliches Denken gerathen sollten; sondern diese Mitte und Einheit, das Verschwinden oder eben so das Werden, ist vielmehr allein ihre Wahrheit.\n\nWas unendlich sey, ist ferner gesagt worden, sey nicht vergleichbar als ein Größeres oder Kleineres; es könne daher nicht ein Verhältniß von Unendlichen zu Unendlichen, noch Ordnungen oder Dignitäten des Unendlichen geben, als welche Unterschiede der unendlichen Differenzen in der Wissenschaft derselben vorkommen.—Es liegt bei diesem schon erwähnten Einwurfe immer die Vorstellung zu Grunde, daß hier von Quantis die Rede seyn solle, die als Quanta verglichen werden; daß Bestimmungen, die keine Quanta mehr sind, kein Verhältniß mehr zu einander haben. Vielmehr ist aber das, was nur im Verhältniß ist, kein Quantum; das Quantum ist eine solche Bestimmung, die außer ihrem Verhältniß ein vollkommen gleichgültiges Daseyn haben, der ihr Unterschied von einem anderen gleichgültig seyn soll, da hingegen das qualitative nur das ist, was es in seinem Unterschiede von dnem Anderen ist. Jene unendlichen Größen sind daher nicht nur vergleichbar, sondern sind nur als Momente der Vergleichung, des Verhältnisses.\n\nIch führe die wichtigsten Bestimmungen an, welche in der Mathematik über dieß Unendliche gegeben worden sind; es wird daraus erhellen, daß denselben der Gedanke der Sache, übereinstimmend mit dem hier entwickelten Begriffe, zu Grunde liegt, daß ihre Urheber ihn aber als Begriff nicht ergründeten und bei der Anwendung wieder Auskunftsmittel nöthig hatten, welche ihrer besseren Sache widersprechen.\n\nDer Gedanke kann nicht richtiger bestimmt werden, als Newton ihn gegeben hat. Ich trenne dabei die Bestimmungen ab, die der Vorstellung der Bewegung und der Geschwindigkeit angehören, (von welcher er vornehmlich den Namen Fluxionen nahm), weil der Gedanke hierin nicht in der gehörigen Abstraktion, sondern konkret, vermischt mit außerwesentlichen Formen erscheint. Diese Fluxionen erklärt Newton (Princ. mathem. phil. nat. L. 1. Lemma XI. Schol.) dahin, daß er nicht untheilbare—eine Form, deren sich frühere Mathematiker, Cavalleri und andere, bedienten, und welche den Begriff eines an sich bestimmten Quantums enthält,—verstehe, sondern verschwindende Theilbare. Ferner nicht Summen und Verhältnisse bestimmter Theile, sondern die Grenzen (limites) der Summen, und Verhältnisse. Es werde die Einwendung gemacht, daß verschwindende Größen kein letztes Verhältniß haben, weil es, ehe sie verschwunden, nicht das Letzte, und wenn sie verschwunden, keines mehr ist. Aber unter dem Verhältnisse verschwindender Größen sey das Verhältniß zu verstehen, nicht eh sie verschwinden, und nicht nachher, sondern mit dem sie verschwinden ( quacum evanescunt ). Eben so ist das erste Verhältniß werdender Größen, das mit dem sie werden.\n\nNach dem damaligen Stande der wissenschaftlichen Methode wurde nur erklärt, was unter einem Ausdrucke zu verstehen sey; daß aber dieß oder jenes darunter zu verstehen sey, ist eigentlich eine subjektive Zumuthung oder auch eine historische Forderung, wobei nicht gezeigt wird, daß ein solcher Begriff an und für sich nothwendig ist und innere Wahrheit hat. Allein das Angeführte zeigt, daß der von Newton aufgestellte Begriff dem entspricht, wie die unendliche Größe sich in der obigen Darstellung aus der Reflexion des Quantums in sich ergab. Es sind Größen verstanden, in ihrem Verschwinden, d. h. die nicht mehr Quanta sind; ferner nicht Verhältnisse bestimmter Theile, sondern die Grenzen des Verhältnisses. Es sollen also sowohl die Quanta für sich, die Seiten des Verhältnisses, als damit auch das Verhältniß, insofern es ein Quantum wäre, verschwinden; die Grenze des Größen-Verhältnisses ist, worin es ist und nicht ist; dieß heißt genauer, worin das Quantum verschwunden, und damit das Verhältniß nur als qualitatives Quantitäts-Verhältniß, und die Seiten desselben ebenso als qualitative Quantitäts-Momente erhalten sind.—Newton fügt hinzu, daß daraus, daß es letzte Verhältnisse der verschwindenden Größen gebe, nicht zu schließen sey, daß es letzte Größen, Untheilbare, gebe. Dieß wäre nämlich wieder ein Absprung von dem abstrakten Verhältnisse auf solche Seiten desselben, welche für sich außer ihrer Beziehung einen Werth haben sollten, als Untheilbare, als etwas, das ein Eins, ein Verhältnißloses seyn würde.\n\nGegen jenen Mißverstand erinnert er noch, daß die letzten Verhältnisse nicht Verhältnisse letzter Größen seyen, sondern Grenzen, denen die Verhältnisse der ohne Grenze abnehmenden Größen näher sind als jeder gegebene d. h. endliche Unterschied, welche Grenze sie aber nicht überschreiten, so daß sie Nichts würden.—Unter letzten Größen hätten nämlich, wie gesagt, Untheilbare oder Eins verstanden werden können. In der Bestimmung des letzten Verhältnisses aber ist sowohl die Vorstellung des gleichgültigen Eins, des verhältnißlosen, als auch des endlichen Quantums entfernt. Es bedürfte aber weder des Abnehmens ohne Grenze, in das Newton das Quantum versetzt und das nur den Progreß ins Unendliche ausdrückt, noch der Bestimmung der Theilbarkeit, welche hier keine unmittelbare Bedeutung mehr hat, wenn die geforderte Bestimmung sich zum Begriffe einer Größebestimmung, die rein nur Moment des Verhältnisses ist, fortgebildet hätte.\n\nIn Rücksicht der Erhaltung des Verhältnisses im Verschwinden der Quantorum findet sich (anderwärts, wie bei Carnot, Réflexions sur la Métaphysique du Calcul Infinitésimal.) der Ausdruck, daß vermöge des Gesetzes der Stätigkeit die verschwindenden Größen noch das Verhältniß, aus dem sie herkommen, ehe sie verschwinden, behalten. —Diese Vorstellung drückt die wahre Natur der Sache aus, insofern nicht die Stätigkeit des Quantums verstanden wird, die es im unendlichen Progreß hat, sich in sein Verschwinden so zu kontinuiren, daß im Jenseits seiner wieder nur ein endliches Quantum, ein neues Glied der Reihe entsteht; ein stätiger Fortgang wird aber immer so vorgestellt, daß die Werthe durchloffen werden, welche noch endliche Quanta sind.\n\nIn demjenigen Übergange dagegen, welcher in das wahrhafte Unendliche gemacht wird, ist das Verhältniß das stätige; es ist so sehr stätig und sich erhaltend, daß er vielmehr allein darin besteht, das Verhältniß rein herauszuheben, und die verhältnißlose Bestimmung, d. i. daß ein Quantum, welches Seite des Verhältnisses ist, auch außer dieser Beziehung gesetzt, noch Quantum ist, verschwinden zu machen. —Diese Reinigung des quantitativen Verhältnisses ist insofern nichts anders, als wenn ein empirisches Daseyn begriffen wird. Dieß wird hierdurch so über sich selbst erhoben, daß sein Begriff dieselben Bestimmungen enthält, als es selbst, aber in ihrer Wesentlichkeit und in die Einheit des Begriffes gefaßt, worin sie ihr gleichgültiges, begriffloses Bestehen verloren haben.\n\nGleich interessant ist die andere Form der newtonischen Darstellung der in Rede stehenden Größen, nämlich als erzeugender Größen oder Principien. Eine erzeugte Größe (genita) ist ein Produkt oder Quotient, Wurzeln, Rechtecke, Quadrate, auch Seiten von Rechtecken, Quadraten;—überhaupt eine endliche Größe.—\"Sie als veränderlich betrachtet, wie sie in fortdauernder Bewegung und Fließen zu- oder abnehmend ist, so verstehe er ihre momentanen Inkremente oder Dekremente unter dem Namen von Momenten. Diese sollen aber nicht für Theilchen von bestimmter Größe genommen werden ( particulae finitae ). Solche seyen nicht selbst Momente, sondern aus Momenten erzeugte Größen; es seyen vielmehr die werdenden Principien oder Anfänge endlicher Größen zu verstehen.\"—Das Quantum wird hier von sich selbst unterschieden, wie es als ein Produkt oder Daseyendes, und wie es in seinem Werden, in seinem Anfange und Princip, das heißt, wie es in seinem Begriffe, oder was hier dasselbe ist, in seiner qualitativen Bestimmnng ist; in der letztern sind die quantitativen Unterschiede, die unendlichen Inkremente oder Dekremente, nur Momente; erst das Gewordene ist das in die Gleichgültigkeit des Daseyns und in die Äußerlichkeit übergegangene, das Quantum.—Wenn aber diese in Ansehung der Inkremente oder Dekremente angeführten Bestimmungen des Unendlichen, von der Philosophie des wahrhaften Begriffs anerkannt werden müssen, so ist auch sogleich zu bemerken, daß die Formen selbst von Inkrementen u.s.f. innerhalb der Kategorie des unmittelbaren Quantums und des erwähnten stätigen Fortgangs fallen, und vielmehr sind die Vorstellungen von Inkrement, Zuwachs, Zunahme des x um d x oder i u.s.f. als das in den Methoden vorhandene Grundübel anzusehen;—als das bleibende Hinderniß, aus der Vorstellung des gewöhnlichen Quantums die Bestimmung des qualitativen Quantitätsmoments rein herauszuheben.\n\nGegen die angegebenen Bestimmungen steht die Vorstellung von unendlich-kleinen Größen, die auch im Inkrement oder Dekrement selbst steckt, weit zurück. Nach derselben sollen sie von der Beschaffenheit seyn, daß nicht nur sie gegen endliche Größen, sondern auch deren höhere Ordnungen gegen die niedrigere, oder auch die Produkte aus mehrern gegen eine einzelne zu vernachlässigen seyen. —bei Leibnitz hebt sich die Forderung dieser Vernachlässigung, welche die vorhergehenden Erfinder von Methoden, die sich auf diese Größe bezogen, gleichfalls eintreten lassen, auffallender hervor. Sie ist es vornehmlich, die diesem Kalkul beim Gewinne der Bequemlichkeit den Schein von Ungenauigkeit und ausdrücklicher Unrichtigkeit in dem Wege seiner Operation giebt.—Wolf hat sie in seiner Weise, die Sachen populär zu machen, d. h. den Begriff zu verunreinigen und unrichtige sinnliche Vorstellungen an dessen Stelle zu setzen, verständlich zu machen gesucht. Er vergleicht nämlich die Vernachlässigung der unendlichen Differenzen höherer Ordnungen gegen niedrigere, mit dem Verfahren eines Geometers, der bei der Messung der Höhe eines Berges um nicht weniger genau gewesen sey, wenn der Wind indeß ein Sandkörnchen von der Spitze weggeweht habe, oder mit der Vernachlässigung der Höhen der Häuser, Thürme bei der Berechnung der Mondfinsternisse (Element. Mathes. univ. Tom. I. El. Analys. math. P. II. C. I. s. Schol.).\n\nWenn die Billigkeit des gemeinen Menschenverstandes eine solche Ungenauigkeit erlaubt, so haben dagegen alle Geometer diese Vorstellung verworfen. Es dringt sich von selbst auf, daß in der Wissenschaft der Mathematik von einer solchen empirischen Genauigkeit ganz und gar nicht die Rede ist, daß das mathematische Messen durch Operationen des Kalkuls oder durch Konstruktionen und Beweise der Geometrie, gänzlich vom Feldmessen, vom Messen empirischer Linien, Figuren u.s.f. unterschieden ist. Ohnehin zeigen, wie oben angeführt, die Analytiker durch die Vergleichung des Resultats, wie es auf streng geometrischem Wege und wie es nach der Methode der unendlichen Differenzen erhalten wird, daß das eine dasselbe ist als das andere, und daß ein Mehr oder Weniger von Genauigkeit ganz und gar nicht Statt findet. Und es versteht sich von selbst, daß ein absolut genaues Resultat nicht aus einem Verfahren herkommen könne, das ungenau wäre. Jedoch kann wieder auf der anderen Seite das Verfahren selbst, jener Vernachlässigung aus dem Grunde der Unbedeutenheit, des Protestirens gegen die angeführte Rechtfertigungsweise unerachtet, nicht entbehren. Und dieß ist die Schwierigkeit, um welche die Bemühungen der Analytiker gehen, das hierin liegende Widersinnige begreiflich zu machen, und es zu entfernen.\n\nEs ist in dieser Rücksicht vornehmlich Eulers Vorstellung anzuführen. Indem er die allgemeine Newtonische Definition zu Grunde legt, dringt er darauf, daß die Differentialrechnung die Verhältnisse der Inkremente einer Größe betrachte, daß aber die unendliche Differenz als solche ganz als Null zu betrachten sey, (Institut. Calc. different. P. I. C. III.).—Wie dieß zu verstehen ist, liegt im Vorhergehenden; die unendliche Differenz ist Null nur des Quantums, nicht eine qualitative Null, sondern als Null des Quantums vielmehr reines Moment nur des Verhältnisses. Sie ist nicht ein Unterschied um eine Größe; aber darum ist es einer Seits überhaupt schief, jene Momente, welche unendlich-kleine Größen heißen, auch als Inkremente oder Dekremente, und als Differenzen auszusprechen. Dieser Bestimmung liegt zu Grunde, daß zu der zuerst vorhandenen endlichen Größe etwas hinzukomme oder davon abgezogen werde, eine Subtraktion oder Addition, eine arithmetische, äußerliche Operation vorgehe. Der Übergang von der Funktion der veränderlichen Größe in ihr Differential ist aber anzusehen, daß er von ganz anderer Natur ist, nämlich wie erörtert worden, daß er als Zurückführung der endlichen Funktion auf das qualitative Verhältniß ihrer Quantitätsbestimmungen zu betrachten ist.—Anderer Seits fällt die schiefe Seite für sich auf, wenn gesagt wird, daß die Inkremente für sich Nullen seyen, daß nur ihre Verhältnisse betrachtet werden; denn eine Null hat überhaupt keine Bestimmtheit mehr. Diese Vorstellung kommt also zwar bis zum Negativen des Quantums und spricht es bestimmt aus, aber faßt dieß Negative nicht zugleich in seiner positiven Bedeutung, von qualitativen Quantitätsbestimmungen, die, wenn sie aus dem Verhältnisse gerissen und als Quanta genommen werden wollten, nur Nullen wären.—Lagrange ( Théorie des fonct. analyt. Introd. ) urtheilt über die Vorstellung der Grenzen oder letzten Verhältnisse, daß wenn man gleich sehr gut das Verhältniß zweier Größen sich vorstellen könne, so lange sie endlich bleiben, so gebe dieß Verhältniß dem Verstande keinen deutlichen und bestimmten Begriff, sobald seine Glieder zugleich Null werden.—In der That muß der Verstand über diese bloß negative Seite, daß die Verhältnißglieder Nullen als Quanta sind, hinausgehen, und sie positiv, als qualitative Momente auffassen.—Was aber Euler (am angeführten Ort §. 84 ff.) weiter in Betreff der gegebenen Bestimmung hinzufügt, um zu zeigen, daß zwei sogenannte unendlich kleine Größen, welche nichts anders als Nullen seyn sollen, doch ein Verhältniß zu einander haben und deßwegen auch nicht das Zeichen der Null, sondern andere Zeichen für sie im Gebrauch seyen, kann nicht für genügend angesehen werden. Er will dieß durch den Unterschied des arithmetischen und geometrischen Verhältnisses begründen; bei jenem sehen wir auf die Differenz, bei diesem auf den Quotienten, obgleich das erstere zwischen zwei Nullen gleich sey, so sey es deßwegen doch das geometrische nicht; wenn 2:1 = 0:0, so müsse wegen der Natur der Proportion, da das erste Glied doppelt so groß sey als das zweite, auch das dritte Glied doppelt so groß als das vierte seyn; O:O soll also nach der Proportion als das Verhältniß von 2:1 genommen werden.—Auch nach der gemeinen Arithmetik seyn n.O = O; es sey also n:1 = O:O.—Allein eben dadurch, daß 2:1 oder n:1 ein Verhältniß von Quantis ist, entspricht ihm nicht ein Verhältniß noch eine Bezeichnung von O:O.\n\nIch enthalte mich, die Anführungen zu vermehren, indem die betrachteten zur Genüge gezeigt haben, daß in ihnen wohl der wahrhafte Begriff des Unendlichen liegt, daß er aber nicht in seiner Bestimmtheit herausgehoben und gefaßt worden ist. Indem daher zur Operation selbst fortgegangen wird, so kann es nicht geschehen, daß in ihr die wahrhafte Begriffsbestimmung sich geltend mache; die endliche Quantitätsbestimmtheit kehrt vielmehr zurück und die Operation kann der Vorstellung eines bloß relativ-kleinen nicht entbehren. Der Kalkul macht es nothwendig, die sogenannten unendlichen Größen den gewöhnlichen arithmetischen Operationen des Addirens u.s.f., welche sich auf die Natur endlicher Größen gründen, zu unterwerfen, und sie somit als endliche Größen für einen Augenblick gelten zu lassen und als solche zu behandeln. Der Kalkul hätte sich darüber zu rechtfertigen, daß er sie das eine Mal in diese Sphäre herabzieht und sie als Inkremente oder Differenzen behandelt, und daß er auf der anderen Seite sie als Quanta vernachlässigt, nachdem er so eben Formen und Gesetze der endlichen Größen auf sie angewendet hatte.\n\nÜber die Versuche der Geometer, diese Schwierigkeiten zu beseitigen, führe ich noch das Hauptsächlichste an.\n\nDie ältern Analytiker machten sich hierüber weniger Skrupel; aber die Bemühungen der Neueren gingen vornehmlich dahin, den Kalkul des Unendlichen zur Evidenz der eigentlich geometrischen Methode zurückzubringen und in ihr die Strenge der Beweise der Alten (- Ausdrücke von Lagrange—) in der Mathematik zu erreichen. Allein da das Princip der Analysis des Unendlichen höherer Natur, als das Princip der Mathematik endlicher Größen ist, so mußte jene von selbst sogleich auf jene Art von Evidenz Verzicht thun, wie die Philosophie auch auf diejenige Deutlichkeit keinen Anspruch machen kann, die die Wissenschaften des Sinnlichen, z.B. Naturgeschichte hat, und wie Essen und Trinken für ein verständlicheres Geschäfte gilt, als Denken und Begreifen. Es wird sich demnach nur um die Bemühung handeln, die Strenge der Beweise der Alten zu erreichen.\n\nMehrere haben versucht, den Begriff des Unendlichen ganz zu entbehren, und ohne ihn das zu leisten, was an den Gebrauch desselben gebunden schien.—Lagrange spricht z.B. von der Methode, die Landen erfunden hat, und sagt von ihr, daß sie rein analytisch sey und die unendlich kleinen Differenzen nicht gebrauche, sondern zuerst verschiedene Werthe der veränderlichen Größen einführe, und sie in der Folge gleichsetze. Er urtheilt übrigens, daß darin die der Differentialrechnung eignen Vorzüge, Einfachheit der Methode und Leichtigkeit der Operationen verloren gehe.—Es ist dieß wohl ein Verfahren, das mit demjenigen etwas Entsprechendes hat, von welchem Descartes Tangentenmethode ausgeht, die weiterhin noch näher zu erwähnen ist. Soviel, kann hier bemerkt werden, erhellt sogleich im Allgemeinen, daß das Verfahren überhaupt, verschiedene Werthe der veränderlichen Größen anzunehmen, und sie nachher gleichzusetzen, einem anderen Kreise mathematischer Behandlung angehört, als die Methode des Differential-Kalkuls selbst und die späterhin näher zu erörternde Eigenthümiichkeit des einfachen Verhältnisses, auf welches sich die wirkliche konkrete Bestimmung desselben zurückführt, nämlich der abgeleiteten Funktion zu der ursprünglichen, nicht herausgehoben wird.\n\nDie Ältern unter den Neuern, wie z.B. Fermat, Barrow und andere, die sich zuerst des Unendlich-Kleinen in derjenigen Anwendung bedienten, welche später zur Differential- und Integralrechnung ausgebildet wurde, und dann auch Leibnitz und die Folgenden, auch Euler, haben immer unverhohlen, die Produkte von unendlichen Differenzen, so wie ihre höhern Potenzen nur aus dem Grunde weglassen zu dürfen geglaubt, weil sie relativ gegen die niedrige Ordnung verschwinden. Hierauf beruht bei ihnen allein der Fundamentalsatz, nämlich die Bestimmung dessen, was das Differential eines Produkts oder einer Potenz sey, denn hierauf reducirt sich die ganze theoretische Lehre. Das Übrige ist Theils Mechanismus der Entwickelung, Theils aber Anwendung, in welche jedoch, was weiterhin zu betrachten ist, in der That auch das höhere oder vielmehr einzige Interesse fällt.—In Rücksicht auf das Gegenwärtige ist hier nur das Elementarische anzuführen, daß aus dem gleichen Grunde der Unbedeutenheit als der Hauptsatz, die Curven betreffend, angenommen wird, daß die Elemente der Curven, nämlich die Inkremente der Abscisse und der Ordinate, das Verhältniß der Subtangente und der Ordinate zu einander haben; für die Absicht, ähnliche Dreiecke zu erhalten, wird der Bogen, der die dritte Seite eines Dreiecks zu den beiden Inkrementen, des mit Recht vormals sogenannten charakteristischen Dreiecks, ausmacht, als eine gerade Linie, als Theil der Tangente, und damit das eine der Inkremente bis an die Tangente reichend angesehen. Diese Annahmen erheben jene Bestimmungen einer Seits über die Natur endlicher Größen; anderer Seits aber wird ein Verfahren auf die nun unendlich genannten Momente angewendet, das nur von endlichen Größen gilt, und bei dem nichts aus Rücksicht der Unbedeutenheit vernachiässigt werden darf. Die Schwierigkeit, von der die Methode gedrückt wird, bleibt bei solcher Verfahrungsweise in ihrer ganzen Stärke.\n\nEs ist hier eine merkwürdige Procedur Newtons anzuführen; (Princ. Math. phil. nat. Lib. II. Lemma II. Propos. VII.)—die Erfindung eines sinnreichen Kunststücks, uni das arithmetisch unrichtige Weglassen der produkte unendlicher Differenzen oder höherer Ordnungen derselben bei dem Finden der Differentialien, zu beseitigen. Er findet das Differential des Produkts,—woraus sich dann die Differentialien der Quotienten, Potenzen u.s.f. leicht herleiten, —auf folgende Art. Das Produkt, wenn x, y, jedes um die Hälfte seiner unendlichen Differenz kleiner genommen wird, geht über in x y—xdy/2—ydx/2 + dxdy/4; aber wenn man x und y um ebenso viel zunehmen läßt, in x y + xdy/2 + ydx/2 + dxdy/4. Von diesem zweiten Produkt nun das erste abgezogen, bleibt y d x + x d y als Überschuß, und dieß sey der Überschuß des Wachsthums um ein ganzes dx und dy, denn um dieses Wachsthum sind beide Produkte unterschieden; es ist also das Differential von xy.—Man sieht in diesem Verfahren fällt das Glied, welches die Hauptschwierigkeit ausmacht, das Produkt der beiden unendlichen Differenzen, dxdy, durch sich selbst hinweg. Aber des newtonischen Namens unerachtet muß es gesagt werden dürfen, daß solche, obgleich sehr elementarische Operation, unrichtig ist; es ist unrichtig, daß (x + dx/2) (y + dy/2)—(x—dx/2) (y—dy/2) = (x + dx) (y + dy)—xy. Es kann nur das Bedürfniß seyn, den Fluxionen-Kalkul bei seiner Wichtigkeit zu begründen, was einen Newton dahin bringen konnte, die Täuschung solchen Beweisens sich zu machen.\n\nAndere Formen, die Newton bei der Ableitung des Differentials gebraucht, sind an konkrete auf Bewegung sich beziehende Bedeutungen der Elemente und deren Potenzen gebunden.—Beim Gebrauche der Reihenform, der sonst seine Methode auszeichnet, liegt es zu nahe zu sagen, daß man es immer in seiner Macht habe, durch das Hinzufügen weiterer Glieder die Größe so genau zu nehmen, als man nöthig habe, und daß die weggelassenen relativ unbedeutend, überhaupt das Resultat nur eine Näherung sey, als daß er nicht auch hier mit diesem Grunde sich begnügt hätte, wie er bei seiner Methode der Auflösung der Gleichungen höherer Grade durch Näherung die höheren Potenzen, die bei der Substitution jedes gefundenen noch ungenauen Werthes in die gegebene Gleichung entstehen, aus dem rohen Grunde ihrer Kleinigkeit wegläßt; s. Lagrange Equations Numériques p. 125.\n\nDer Fehler, in welchen Newton bei der Auflösung eines Problems durch das Weglassen wesentlicher höherer Potenzen verfiel, der seinen Gegnern die Gelegenheit eines Triumphs ihrer Methode über die seinige gab, und von welchem Lagrange in seiner neuerlichen Untersuchung desselben (Théorie des fonct. analyt. 3me P. Ch. IV.) den wahren Ursprung aufgezeigt hat, beweist das Formelle und die Unsicherheit, die im Gebrauche jenes Instruments noch vorhanden war. Lagrange zeigt, daß Newton dadurch in den Fehler fiel, weil er das Glied der Reihe vernachlässigte, das die Potenz enthielt, auf welche es in der bestimmten Aufgabe ankam. Newton hatte sich an jenes formelle oberflächliche Princip, Glieder wegen ihrer relativen Kleinheit wegzulassen, gehalten.—Es ist nämlich bekannt, daß in der Mechanik den Gliedern der Reihe, in der die Funktion einer Bewegung entwickelt wird, eine bestimmte Bedeutung gegeben wird, so daß sich das erste Glied oder die erste Funktion auf das Moment der Geschwindigkeit, die zweite auf die beschleunigende Kraft, und die dritte auf den Widerstand von Kräften beziehe. Die Glieder der Reihe sind hiermit hier nicht nur als Theile einer Summe anzusehen, sondern als qualitative Momente eines Ganzen des Begriffs. Hiedurch erhält das Weglassen der übrigen Glieder, die der schlechtunendlichen Reihe angehören, eine gänzlich verschiedene Bedeutung, von dem Weglassen aus dem Grunde der relativen Kleinheit derselben. [10] Die newtonsche Auflösung enthielt jenen Fehler, nicht weil in ihr Glieder der Reihe, nur als Theile einer Summe, sondern weil das Glied, das die qualitative Bestimmung, auf die es ankam, enthält, nicht berücksichtigt wurde.\n\n[10] In einfacher Weise finden sich bei Lagrange in der Anwendung der Theorie der Funktionen auf die Mechanik, in dem Kapitel von der geradlinigten Bewegung, beide Rücksichten neben einander gestellt (Théorie des fonct. 3me P. Ch. I. art. 4.). Der durchloffene Raum als Funktion der verflossenen Zeit betrachtet, giebt die Gleichung x = ft; diese als f (t + ë) entwickelt giebt\n\nft + ëft + [ë'[hoch 2]]/2. f\"t + u.s.w.\n\nAlso der während der Zeit durchloffene Raum stellt sich in der Formel dar, ëft + [ë[hoch 2]]/2. f't + [ë[hoch 3]]/2.3. f\"t + u.s.w. Die Bewegung, vermittelst der dieser Raum durchloffen wird, ist also, wird gesagt, d. h. weil die analytische Entwickelung mehrere und zwar unendlich viele Glieder giebt,—zusammengesetzt aus verschiedenen partiellen Bewegungen, deren der Zeit entsprechende Räume seyn werden ëft, [ë[hoch 2]]/2. f\"t, [ë[hoch 3]]/[2.3]. f\"t, u.s.w. die erste partielle Bewegung ist, in bekannter Bewegung die formell=gleichförmige mit einer durch f't bestimmten Geschwindigkeit, die zweite die gleichförmig beschleunigte, die von einer dem f't propertionirten beschleunigenden Kraft herkommt. \"Da nun die übrigen Glieder sich auf keine einfache bekannte Bewegung beziehen, so ist nicht nöthig, sie besonders in Rücksicht zu nehmen, und wir werden zeigen, daß man von ihnen in der Bestimmung der Bewegung zu Anfang des Zeitpunkts abstrahiren kann.\" Dieß wird nun gezeigt, aber freilich nur durch die Vergleichung jener Reihe, deren Glieder alle zur Bestimmung der Größe des in der Zeit durchloffenen Raumes gehörten, mit der art. 3 für die Bewegung des Falls angegebenen Gleichung x = at + bt[hoch 2], als in welcher nur diese zwei Glieder vorkommen. Aber diese Gleichung hat selbst nur diese Gestalt, durch die Voraussetzung der Erklärung, die den durch analytische Entwicklung entstehenden Gliedern gegeben wird, erhalten; diese Voraussetzung ist, daß die gleichförmig beschleunigte Bewegung zusammengesetzt sey, aus einer formell-gleichförmigen mit der im vorhergehenden Zeittheile erlangten Geschwindigkeit fortgesetzten Bewegung, und einem Zuwachse, (dem a in s = at[hoch 2] d.i. dem empirischen Koefficienten), welcher der Kraft der Schwere zugeschrieben wird,—einem Unterschiede, der keineswegs in der Natur der Sache irgend eine Existenz oder Grund hat, sondern nur der fälschlich physikalisch gemachte Ausdruck dessen ist, was bei einer angenommenen analytischen Behandlung herauskommt.\n\nIn diesem Beispiele ist der qualitative Sinn dasjenige, wovon das Verfahren abhängig gemacht ist. Im Zusammenhange hiermit kann sogleich die allgemeine Behauptung aufgestellt werden, daß die ganze Schwierigkeit des Princips beseitigt seyn würde, wenn statt des Formalismus, die Bestimmung des Differentials nur in die ihm den Namen gebende Aufgabe, den Unterschied überhaupt einer Funktion von ihrer Veränderung, nachdem ihre veränderliche Größe einen Zuwachs erhalten, zu stellen, die qualitative Bedeutung des Princips angegeben, und die Operation hiervon abhängig gemacht wäre. In diesem Sinne zeigt sich das Differential von x[hoch n], durch das erste Glied der Reihe, die durch die Entwickelung von (x + dx)[hoch n] sich ergiebt, gänzlich erschöpft. Daß die übrigen Glieder nicht berücksichtigt werden, kommt so nicht von ihrer relativen Kleinheit her;—es wird dabei nicht eine Ungenauigkeit, ein Fehler oder Irrthum vorausgesetzt, der durch einen anderen Irrthum ausgeglichen und verbessert würde; eine Ansicht, von welcher aus Carnot vornehmlich die gewöhnliche Methode der Infinitesimalrechnung rechtfertigt. Indem es sich nicht um eine Summe, sondern um ein Verhältniß handelt, so ist das Differential vollkommen durch das erste Glied gefunden; und wo es fernerer Glieder, der Differentiale höherer Ordnungen bedarf, so liegt in ihrer Bestimmung nicht die Fortsetzung einer Reihe als Summe, sondern die Wiederholung eines und desselben Verhältnisses, das man allein will, und das somit im ersten Glied bereits vollkommen bestimmt ist. Das Bedürfniß der Form einer Reihe des Summirens derselben und was damit zusammenhängt, muß dann ganz von jenem Interesse des Verhältnisses getrennt werden.\n\nDie Erläuterungen, welche Carnot über die Methode der unendlichen Größen giebt, enthalten das Geläutertste und aufs Klarste exponirt, was in den oben angeführten Vorstellungen vorkam. Aber bei dem Übergange zur Operation selbst treten mehr oder weniger die gewöhnlichen Vorstellungen, von der unendlichen Kleinheit der weggelassenen Glieder gegen die andern ein. Er rechtfertigt die Methode vielmehr durch die Thatsache, daß die Resultate richtig werden, und durch den Nutzen, den die Einführung unvollkommner Gleichungen, wie er sie nennt, d. h. solcher, in denen eine solche arithmetisch unrichtige Weglassung geschehen ist, für die Vereinfachung und Abkürzung des Kalkuls habe, als durch die Natur der Sache selbst.\n\nLagrange hat bekanntlich die ursprüngliche Methode Newtons, die Methode der Reihen, wieder aufgenommen, um der Schwierigkeiten, welche die Vorstellung des Unendlich-Kleinen, so wie derjenigen, welche die Methode der ersten und letzten Verhältnisse und Grenzen mit sich führt, überhoben zu seyn. Es ist von seinem Funktionen-Kalkul, dessen sonstige Vorzüge in Rücksicht auf Präcision, Abstraktion und Allgemeinheit anerkannt genug sind, als hierher gehörig nur dieß anzuführen, daß er auf dem Fundamentalsatze beruht, daß die Differenz, ohne daß sie Null werde, so klein angenommen werden könne, daß jedes Glied der Reihe die Summe aller folgenden an Größe übertreffe.—Es wird auch in dieser Methode von den Kategorien vom Zuwachs und von der Differenz der Funktion angefangen, deren veränderliche Größe den Zuwachs erhalte, womit die lästige Reihe hereinkommt, von der ursprünglichen Funktion; so wie im Verfolg die wegzulassenden Glieder der Reihe nur in der Rücksicht, daß sie eine Summe constituiren, in Betracht kommen, und der Grund, sie wegzulassen, in das Relative ihres Quantums gesetzt wird. Die Weglassung ist also hier auch nicht für das Allgemeine auf den Gesichtspunkt zurückgeführt, der Theils in einigen Anwendungen vorkommt, worin, wie vorhin erinnert, die Glieder der Reihe eine bestimmte qualitative Bedeutung haben sollen und Glieder außer Acht gelassen werden, nicht darum weil sie unbedeutend an Größe sind, sondern weil sie unbedeutend der Qualität nach sind; Theils aber fällt dann die Weglassung selbst in dem wesentlichen Gesichtspunkte hinweg, der sich für den sogenannten Differential-Koefficienten erst in der sogenannten Anwendung des Kalkuls bei Lagrange bestimmt heraushebt, was in der folgenden Anmerkung ausführlicher auseinandergesetzt werden wird.\n\nDer qualitative Charakter überhaupt, der hier an der in Rede stehenden Größenform in demjenigen, was dabei das Unendlichkleine genannt wird, nachgewiesen worden ist, findet sich am unmittelbarsten in der Kategorie der Grenze des Verhältnisses, die oben angeführt worden, und deren Durchführung im Kalkul zu einer eigenthümlichen Methode gestempelt worden ist. Was Lagrange von dieser Methode urtheilt, daß sie der Leichtigkeit in der Anwendung entbehre, und der Ausdruck Grenze keine bestimmte Idee darbiete, davon wollen wir das Zweite hier aufnehmen, und näher sehen, was über ihre analytische Bedeutung aufgestellt wird. In der Vorstellung der Grenze liegt nämlich wohl die angegebene wahrhafte Kategorie der qualitativen Verhältnißbestimmung der veränderlichen Größen, denn die Formen, die von ihnen eintreten, dx und dy, sollen schlechthin nur als Momente von dy/dx genommen, und dx/dy selbst als ein einziges untheilbares Zeichen angesehen werden. Daß hiermit für den Mechanismus des Kalkuls besonders in seiner Anwendung der Vortheil verloren geht, den er davon zieht, daß die Seiten des Differential-Koefficienten von einander abgesondert werden, ist hier bei Seite zu setzen. Jene Grenze soll nun Grenze von einer gegebenen Funktion seyn;—sie soll einen gewissen Werth in Beziehung auf dieselbe angeben, der sich durch die Weise der Ableitung bestimmt. Mit der bloßen Kategorie der Grenze aber wären wir nicht weiter, als mit dem, um das es in dieser Anm. zu thun gewesen ist, nämlich aufzuzeigen, daß das Unendlichkleine, das in der Differentialrechnung als dx und dy vorkommt, nicht bloß den negativen, leeren Sinn einer nicht endlichen, nicht gegebenen Größe habe, wie wenn man sagt, eine unendliche Menge, ins unendliche fort und dergleichen, sondern den bestimmten Sinn der qualitativen Bestimmtheit des Quantitativen, eines Verhältnißmoments als eines solchen. Diese Kategorie hat jedoch so noch kein Verhältniß zu dem, was eine gegebene Funktion ist, und greift für sich nicht in die Behandlung einer solchen und in einen Gebrauch, der an ihr von jener Bestimmung zu machen wäre, ein; so würde auch die Vorstellung der Grenze, zurückgehalten in dieser von ihr nachgewiesenen Bestimmtheit, zu nichts führen. Aber der Ausdruck Grenze enthält es schon selbst, daß sie Grenze von Etwas sey, d. h. einen gewissen Werth ausdrücke, der in der Funktion veränderlicher Größe liegt; und es ist zu sehen, wie dieß konkrete Benehmen mit ihr beschaffen ist.—Sie soll die Grenze des Verhältnisses seyn, welches die zwei Inkremente zu einander haben, um welche die zwei veränderlichen Größen, die in einer Gleichung verbunden sind, deren die eine als eine Funktion der andern angesehen wird, als zunehmend angenommen worden;—der Zuwachs wird hier unbestimmt überhaupt genommen und insofern von dem Unendlichkleinen kein Gebrauch gemacht. Aber zunächst führt der Weg, diese Grenze zu finden, dieselben Inkonsequenzen herbei, die in den übrigen Methoden liegen. Dieser Weg ist nämlich folgender. Wenn y = fx, soll fx, wenn y in y + k übergeht, sich in fx + ph + qh[hoch 2] + rh[hoch 3] u.s.f. verändert, hiermit ist k = ph + qh[hoch 2] u.s.f. und k/h = p + qh + rh[hoch 2] u.s.f. Wenn nun k und h verschwinden, so verschwindet das zweite Glied außer p, welches p nun die Grenze des Verhältnisses der beiden Zuwächse sey. Man sieht, daß h als Quantum = 0 gesetzt wird, aber daß darum k/h nicht zugleich = 0 seyn, sondern noch ein Verhältniß bleiben soll. Den Vortheil, die Inkonsequenz, die hierin liegt, abzulehnen, soll nun die Vorstellung der Grenze gewähren; p soll zugleich nicht das wirkliche Verhältniß, das = 0/0 wäre, sondern nur der bestimmte Werth seyn, dem sich das Verhältniß unendlich d.i. so nähern könne, daß der Unterschied kleiner als jeder gegebene werden könne. Der bestimmtere Sinn der Näherung in Rücksicht dessen, was sich eigentlich einander nähern soll, wird unten betrachtet werden. —Daß aber ein quantitativer Unterschied, der die Bestimmung hat, kleiner als jeder gegebene seyn zu können nicht nur, sondern seyn zu sollen, kein quantitativer Unterschied mehr ist, dieß ist für sich klar, so evident als irgend etwas in der Mathematik evident seyn kann; damit aber ist über dy/dx = 0/0 nicht hinausgekommen worden. Wenn dagegen dy/dx = p d.i. als ein bestimmtes quantitatives Verhältniß, angenommen wird, wie dieß in der That der Fall ist, so kommt umgekehrt die Voraussetzung, welche h = 0 gesetzt hat, in Verlegenheit, eine Voraussetzung, durch welche allein k/h = p gefunden wird. Giebt man aber zu, daß k/h = 0 ist, und mit h = 0 wird in der That von selbst auch k = 0; denn der Zuwachs k zu y findet nur unter der Bedingung statt, daß der Zuwachs h ist; so wäre zu sagen, was denn p seyn solle, welches ein ganz bestimmter quantitativer Werth ist. Hierauf giebt sich sogleich die einfache, trockne Antwort von selbst, daß es ein Koefficient ist und aus welcher Ableitung er entsteht,—die auf gewisse bestimmte Weise abgeleitete erste Funktion einer ursprünglichen Funktion. Begnügte man sich damit, wie denn in der That Lagrange sich der Sache nach damit begnügt hat, so wäre der allgemeine Theil der Wissenschaft des Differential-Kalkuls und unmittelbar diese seine Form selbst, welche die Theorie der Grenzen heißt, von den Zuwächsen, dann deren unendlicher oder beliebiger Kleinheit, von der Schwierigkeit, außer dem ersten Gliede oder vielmehr nur dem Coefficienten des ersten Gliedes die weitern Glieder einer Reihe, als welche durch die Einführung jener Zuwächse unabwendbar sich einfinden, wieder wegzubringen, befreit; außerdem aber auch von dem weitern, was damit zusammenhängt, von den formellen Kategorien vor allem des Unendlichen, der unendlichen Annäherung, und der weitern hier ebenso leeren Kategorien von kontinuirlicher Größe, [11] und welche man sonst, wie Bestreben, Werden, Gelegenheit einer Veränderung für nöthig erachtet, gereinigt. Aber dann würde gefordert zu zeigen, was denn p, außer der, für die Theorie ganz genügenden trocknen Bestimmung, daß es weiter nichts als eine aus der Entwickelung eines Binomiums abgeleitete Funktion ist, noch für eine Bedeutung und Werth, d. i. welchen Zusammenhang und Gebrauch für weiteres mathematisches Bedürfniß habe; hiervon soll die zweite Anmerkung handeln.—Es folgt aber zunächst hier noch die Auseinandersetzung der Verwirrung, welche durch den angeführten, in den Darstellungen so geläufigen Gebrauch der Vorstellung von Annäherung in das Auffassen der eigentlichen, qualitativen Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses, um das es zunächst zu thun war, gebracht worden ist.\n\n[11] Die Kategorie von der kontinuirlichen oder fließenden Größe stellt sich mit der Betrachtung der äußerlichen und empirischen Veränderung der Größen, die durch eine Gleichung in die Beziehung, daß die Eine eine Funktion der Andern ist, gebracht sind, ein; da aber der wissenschaftliche Gegenstand der Differentialrechnung ein gewisses (durch den Differential-Koefficienten gewöhnlich ausgedrücktes) Verhältniß, welche Bestimmtheit ebensowohl Gesetz genannt werden kann, ist, so ist für diese specifische Bestimmtheit die bloße Kontinuität Theils schon eine fremdartige Seite, Theils aber auf allen Fall die abstrakte und hier leere Kategorie, da über das Gesetz der Kontinuität gar nichts damit ausgedrückt ist.—Auf welche formelle Definitionen dabei vollends verfallen wird, ist aus meines verehrten Hrn. Collegen, Prof. Dirksen, scharfsinniger allgemeinen Darstellung der Grundbestimmungen, die für die Deduktion des Differential-Kalkuls gebraucht werden, welche sich an die Kritik einiger neueren Werke über diese Wissenschaft anschließt und sich in den Jahrb. f. wissensch. Kritik, 1827 Nr. 153 ff., befindet, zu ersehen, es wird daselbst S. 1251 sogar die Definition angeführt: \"Eine stätige oder kontinuirliche Größe, Kontinuum, ist jede Größe, welche man sich im Zustande des Werdens gedenkt, so daß dieses Werden nicht sprungweise, sondern durch ununterbrochenen Fortgang geschieht.\" Das ist doch wohl tautologisch dasselbe, was das definitum ist.\n\nEs ist gezeigt worden, daß die sogenannten unendlichen Differenzen das Verschwinden der Seiten des Verhältnisses als Quantorum ausdrücken, und daß das, was übrig bleibt, ihr Quantitätsverhältniß ist, rein insofern es auf qualitative Weise bestimmt ist; das qualitative Verhältniß geht hierin so wenig verloren, daß es vielmehr dasjenige ist, was eben durch die Verwandlung endlicher Größen in unendliche resultirt. Hierin besteht, wie wir gesehen, die ganze Natur der Sache.—So verschwinden im letzten Verhältnisse z.B. die Quanta der Abscisse und Ordinate; aber die Seiten dieses Verhältnisses bleiben wesentlich die eine, Element der Ordinate, die andere Element der Abscisse. Indem die Vorstellungsweise gebraucht wird, daß man die eine Ordinate sich der anderen unendlich nähern läßt, so geht die vorher unterschiedene Ordinate in die andere Ordinate, und die vorher unterschiedene Abscisse in die andere Abscisse über; aber wesentlich geht nicht die Ordinate in die Abscisse, oder die Abscisse in die Ordinate über. Das Element der Ordinate,—um bei diesem Beispiele von veränderlichen Größen stehen zu bleiben, ist nicht als der Unterschied einer Ordinate von einer anderen Ordinate zu nehmen, sondern ist vielmehr als der Unterschied oder die qualitative Größenbestimmung gegen das Element der Abscisse; das Princip der einen veränderlichen Größe gegen das der andern steht im Verhältnisse miteinander. Der Unterschied, indem er nicht mehr Unterschied endlicher Größen ist, hat aufgehört, ein Vielfaches innerhalb seiner selbst zu seyn; er ist in die einfache Intensität zusammengesunken, in die Bestimmtheit eines qualitativen Verhältnißmoments gegen das andere.\n\nDiese Beschaffenheit der Sache wird aber dadurch verdunkelt, daß das, was so eben Element z.B. der Ordinate genannt worden, so als Differenz oder Inkrement gefaßt wird, daß es nur der Unterschied des Quantums einer Ordinate zwischen dem Quantum einer andern Ordinate sey. Die Grenze hat hiermit hier nicht den Sinn des Verhältnisses; sie gilt nur als der letzte Werth, dem sich eine andere Größe von gleicher Art beständig so nähere, daß sie von ihm, so wenig als man will, unterschieden seyn könne, und daß das letzte Verhältniß, ein Verhältniß der Gleichheit sey. So ist die unendliche Differenz das Schweben eines Unterschieds eines Quantums von einem Quantum, und die qualitative Natur, nach welcher dx wesentlich nicht eine Verhältnißbestimmung gegen x, sondern gegen dy ist, tritt in der Vorstellung zurück. Man läßt dx[hoch 2] gegen dx verschwinden, aber noch vielmehr verschwindet dx gegen x, dieß heißt aber wahrhaftig: es hat nur ein Verhältniß zu dy.—Es ist den Geometern in solchen Darstellungen immer vorzüglich darum zu thun, die Annäherung einer Größe an ihre Grenze begreiflich zu machen, und sich an diese Seite des Unterschiedes des Quantums vom Quantum, wie er kein Unterschied und doch noch ein Unterschied ist, zu halten. Aber die Annäherung ist ohnehin für sich eine nichts sagende und nichts begreiflich machende Kategorie; dx hat die Annäherung bereits im Rücken, es ist nicht nahe noch ein Näheres; und unendlich nahe heißt selbst die Negation des Naheseyns und des Annäherns.\n\nIndem es nun damit geschehen ist, daß die Inkremente oder unendlichen Differenzen nur nach der Seite des Quantums, das in ihnen verschwindet, und nur als Grenze desselben betrachtet worden sind, so sind sie so als verhältnißlose Momente gefaßt. Es würde die unstatthafte Vorstellung daraus folgen, daß es erlaubt sey, in dem letzten Verhältnisse etwa Abscisse und Ordinate, oder auch Sinus, Cosinus, Tangente, Sinus versus und was alles noch, einander gleich zu setzen.—Diese Vorstellung scheint zunächst darin obzuwalten, wenn ein Bogen als eine Tangente behandelt wird; denn auch der Bogen ist wohl inkommensurabel mft der geraden Linie, und sein Element zunächst von anderer Qualität als das Element der geraden Linie. Es scheint noch widersinniger und unerlaubter, als die Verwechslung der Abscisse, Ordinate, des Sinus versus, Cosinus u.s.f. wenn quadrata rotundis, wenn ein ob zwar unendlich kleiner Theil des Bogens, für ein Stück der Tangente, genommen, und somit als gerade Linie behandelt wird. —Allein diese Behandlung ist von der gerügten Verwechslung wesentlich zu unterscheiden; sie hat ihre Rechtfertigung darin, daß in dem Dreieck, weilches das Element eines Bogens und die Elemente seiner Abscisse und der Ordinate zu seinen Seiten hat, das Verhältniß dasselbe ist, als wenn jenes Element des Bogens das Element einer geraden Linie, der Tangente wäre; die Winkel, welche das wesentliche Verhältniß konstituiren, d. i. dasjenige, das diesen Elementen bleibt, indem von den ihnen zugehörigen endlichen Größen abstrahirt wird, sind die nämlichen.—Man kann sich hierüber auch ausdrücken, gerade Linien, als unendlichklein, seyen in krumme Linien übergegangen, und das Verhältniß ihrer in ihrer Unendlichkeit sey ein Kurvenverhältniß. Da nach ihrer Definition die gerade Linie der kürzeste Weg zwischen zwei Punkten ist, so gründet sich ihr Unterschied von krummer Linie auf die Bestimmung von Menge, auf die geringere Menge des Unterscheidbaren auf diesem Wege, was also eine Bestimmung von Quantum Ist. Aber diese Bestimmung verschwindet in ihr, sie als intensive Größe, als unendliches Moment, als Element genommen; somit auch ihr Unterschied von der krummen Linie, der bloß auf dem Quantumsunterschiede beruhte.—Also als unendlich behält gerade Linie und Bogen kein quantitatives Verhältniß und damit, auf den Grund der angenommenen Definition, auch keine qualitative Verschiedenheit mehr gegeneinander, sondern geht jene vielmehr in diese über.\n\nVerwandt, jedoch zugleich verschieden, von der Gleichsetzung heterogener Bestimmungen ist die für sich unbestimmte und völlig gleichgültige Annahme, daß unendlich kleine Theile desselben Ganzen einander gleich seyen; jedoch angewandt auf einen in sich heterogenen d. i. mit wesentlicher Ungleichförmigkeit der Größebestimmung behafteten Gegenstand, bringt sie die eigenthüniliche Verkehrung hervor, die in dem Satze der höhern Mechanik enthalten ist, daß in gleichen und zwar unendlichkleinen Zeiten unendlichkleine Theile einer Kurve in gleichförmiger Bewegung durchloffen werden, indem dieß von einer Bewegung behauptet wird, in der in gleichen endlichen d. i. existirenden Zeittheilen endliche, d. i. existirende ungleiche Theile der Kurve durchloffen werden, d. i. also von einer Bewegung, die als existirend ungleichförmig ist und so angenommen wird. Dieser Satz ist der Ausdruck desjenigen in Worten, was ein analytisches Glied, das sich in der oben auch angeführten Entwickelung der Formel von ungleichförmiger übrigens einem Gesetze gemäßen Bewegung ergiebt, bedeuten soll. Ältere Mathematiker suchten Ergebnisse der neu erfundenen Infinitesimal-Rechnung, die ohnehin immer mit konkreten Gegenständen zu thun hatte, in Worte und Sätze auszudrücken und sie in geometrischen Verzeichnungen darzustellen, wesentlich um sie für die Lehrsätze nach gewöhnlicher Beweise-Art zu gebrauchen. Die Glieder einer mathematischen Formel, in welche die analytische Behandlung die Größe des Gegenstands z.B. der Bewegung zerlegte, erhielten dort eine gegenständliche Bedeutung, z.B. der Geschwindigkeit, beschleunigende Kraft u.s.f. sie sollten nach solcher Bedeutung richtige Sätze, physikalische Gesetze geben und nach der analytischen Verbindung auch ihre objektiven Verknüpfungen und Verhältnisse bestimmt seyn, wie z.B. eben daß in einer gleichförmig beschleunigten Bewegung eine besondere den Zeiten proportionale Geschwindigkeit existire, außerdem aber ein Zuwachs von der Kraft der Schwere her, immer hinzukomme. Solche Sätze werden in der modernen, analytischen Gestalt der Mechanik durchaus als Ergebnisse des Kalkuls aufgeführt unbekümmert darum, ob sie einen reellen Sinn d. i. dem eine Existenz entspräche, für sich an ihnen selbst hätten, und um einen Beweis eines solchen; die Schwierigkeit, den Zusammenhang solcher Bestimmungen, wenn sie im ausgesprochenen reellen Sinn genommen werden, z.B. den Übergang von jener schlechtgleichförmigen Geschwindigkeit zu einer gleichförmigen beschleunigten, begreifflich zu machen, gilt dafür, durch die analytische Behandlung ganz beseitigt zu seyn, als in welcher solcher Zusammenhang einfache Folge der nunmehrigen festen Autorität der Operationen des Kalkuls ist. Es wird für einen Triumph der Wissenschaft ausgegeben, durch den bloßen Kalkul über die Erfahrung hinaus Gesetze, d. i. Sätze der Existenz, die keine Existenz haben, zu finden. Aber in der erstern noch naiven Zeit des Infinitesimal-Kalkuls sollte von jenen Bestimmungen und Sätzen, in geometrischen Verzeichnungen vorgestellt, ein reeller Sinn für sich angegeben und plausibel gemacht, und sie in solchem Sinne zum Beweise von den Hauptsätzen, um die es zu thun war, angewendet werden, (—man sehe den newtonischen Beweis von seinem Fundamentalsatze der Theorie der Gravitation in den Princ. mathem. philosophiae naturalis lib. I. Sect. II. Prop. I. verglichen mit Schuberts Astronomie (erster Ausg. III. B. §. 20), wo zugestanden wird, daß es sich nicht genau so, d. i. in dem Punkte, welcher der Nerv des Beweises ist, sich nicht so verhalte, wie Newton annimmt—).\n\nEs wird nicht geläugnet werden können, daß man sich in diesem Felde vieles als Beweis, vornehmlich unter der Beihülfe des Nebels des Unendlich-Kleinen hat gefallen lassen, aus keinem andern Grunde als dem, daß das, was herauskam, immer schon vorher bekannt war, und der Beweis, der so eingerichtet wurde, daß es herauskam, wenigstens den Schein eines Gerüstes von Beweis zu Stande brachte;—einen Schein, den man dem bloßen Glauben oder dem Wissen aus Erfahrung immer noch vorzog. Ich aber trage kein Bedenken, diese Manier für nicht mehr als eine bloße Taschenspielerei und Charlatanerie des Beweisens anzusehen, und hierunter selbst newtonische Beweise zu rechnen, ins Besondere die zu dem so eben angeführten gehörigen, wegen welcher man Newton bis an den Himmel und über Keppler erhoben hat, das was dieser bloß durch Erfahrung gefunden, mathematisch dargethan zu haben.\n\nDas leere Gerüste solcher Beweise wurde errichtet, um physische Gesetze zu beweisen. Aber die Mathematik vermag überhaupt nicht Größenbestimmungen der Physik zu beweisen, insofern sie Gesetze sind, welche die qualitative Natur der Momente zum Grunde haben; aus dem einfachen Grunde, weil diese Wissenschaft nicht Philosophie ist, nicht vom Begriffe ausgeht, und das Qualitative daher, insofern es nicht lemmatischerweise aus der Erfahrung aufgenommen wird, außer ihrer Sphäre liegt. Die Behauptung der Ehre der Mathematik, daß alle in ihr vorkommenden Sätze streng bewiesen seyn sollen, ließ sie ihre Grenze oft vergessen; so schien es gegen ihre Ehre, für Erfahrungssätze einfach die Erfahrung als Quelle und als einzigen Beweis anzuerkennen; später ist das Bewußtseyn hierüber gebildeter geworden; eh dieses aber über den Unterschied sich nicht klar wird, was mathematisch beweisbar ist und was nur anderwärts genommen werden kann, wie darüber was nur Glieder analytischer Entwickelung und was physikalische Existenzen sind, kann die Wissenschaftlichkeit sich nicht zu strenger und reiner Haltung herausbilden.—Jenem Gerüste newtonischen Beweisens aber wird ohne Zweifel noch dasselbe Recht widerfahren, das einem anderen grundlosen newtonischen Kunstgebäude aus optischen Experimenten und damit verbundenem Schließen angethan worden ist. Die angewandte Mathematik ist noch voll von einem gleichen Gebräue aus Erfahrung und Reflexion, aber wie vonjener Optik seit geraumer Zeit bereits ein Theil nach dem andern anfing in der Wissenschaft faktisch ignorirt zu werden mit der Inkonsequenz jedoch, das Übrige obgleich damit Widersprechende noch gewähren zu lassen, —so ist es auch Faktum, daß bereits ein Theil jener trügerischen Beweise, von selbst in Vergessenheit gerathen oder durch andere ersetzt worden ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0001","text":"Das mathematische Unendliche ist eines Theils interessant durch die Erweiterung der Mathematik und die großen Resultate, welche seine Einführung in dieselbe hervorgebracht hat; andern Theils aber ist es dadurch merkwürdig, daß es dieser Wissenschaft noch nicht gelungen ist, sich über den Gebrauch desselben durch den Begriff (Begriff im eigentlichen Sinne genommen) zu rechtfertigen. Die Rechtfertigungen beruhen am Ende auf der Richtigkeit der mit Hülfe jener Bestimmung sich ergebenden Resultate, welche aus sonstigen Gründen erwiesen ist; nicht aber auf der Klarheit des Gegenstandes und der Operation, durch welche die Resultate herausgebracht werden, sogar daß die Operation vielmehr selbst als unrichtig zugegeben wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"73.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0002","text":"Dieß ist schon ein Mißstand an und für sich; ein solches Verfahren ist unwissenschaftlich. Es führt aber auch den Nachtheil mit sich, daß die Mathematik, indem sie die Natur dieses ihres Instruments nicht kennt, weil sie mit der Metaphysik und Kritik desselben nicht fertig ist, den Umfang seiner Anwendung nicht bestimmen, und von Misbräuchen desselben sich nicht sichern konnte.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"73.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0003","text":"In philosophischer Rücksicht aber ist das mathematische Unendliche darum wichtig, weil ihm in der That der Begriff des wahrhaften Unendlichen zu Grunde liegt und es viel höher steht, als das gewöhnlich sogenannte metaphysische Unendliche, von dem aus die Einwürfe gegen ersteres gemacht werden. Gegen diese Einwürfe weiß sich die Wissenschaft der Mathematik häufig nur dadurch zu retten, daß sie die Kompetenz der Metaphysik verwirft, indem sie behauptet, mit dieser Wissenschaft nichts zu schaffen und sich um deren Begriffe nicht zu bekümmern zu haben, wenn sie nur auf ihrem eigenen Boden konsequent verfahre. Sie habe nicht zu betrachten, was an sich, sondern was auf ihrem Felde das Wahre sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"73.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0004","text":"Die Metaphysik weiß die glänzenden Resultate des Gebrauchs des mathematischen Unendlichen bei ihrem Widerspruche gegen dasselbe nicht zu läugnen oder umzustoßen, und die Mathematik weiß mit der Metaphysik ihres eigenen Begriffs und daher auch mit der Ableitung der Verfahrensweisen, die der Gebrauch des Unendlichen nöthig macht, nicht ins Reine zu kommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"73.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0005","text":"Wenn es die einzige Schwierigkeit des Begriffs überhaupt wäre, von der die Mathematik gedrückt würde, so könnte sie diesen ohne Umstände auf der Seite liegen lassen, insofern nämlich der Begriff mehr ist, als nur die Angabe der wesentlichen Bestimmtheiten, d. i. der Verstandesbestimmungen einer Sache, und an der Schärfe dieser Bestimmtheiten hat sie es nicht fehlen lassen; denn sie ist nicht eine Wissenschaft, die es mit den Begriffen ihrer Gegenstände zu thun, und durch die Entwickelung des Begriffs, wenn auch nur durch Raisonnement, ihren Inhalt zu erzeugen hätte. Allein bei der Methode ihres Unendlichen findet sie den Hauptwiderspruch an der eigenthümlichen Methode selbst, auf welcher sie überhaupt als Wissenschaft beruht.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"73.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0006","text":"Denn die Rechnung des Unendlichen erlaubt und erfordert Verfahrungsweisen, welche die Mathematik bei Operationen mit endlichen Größen durchaus verwerfen muß, und zugleich behandelt sie ihre unendlichen Größen, wie endliche Quanta, und will auf jene dieselben Verfahrungsweisen anwenden, welche bei diesen gelten; es ist eine Hauptseite der Ausbildung dieser Wissenschaft, für die transcendenten Bestimmungen und deren Behandlung, die Form des gewöhnlichen Kalkuls gewonnen zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"73.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0007","text":"Die Mathematik zeigt bei diesem Widerstreite ihrer Operationen, daß Resultate, die sie dadurch findet, ganz mit denen übereinstimmen, welche durch die eigentlich mathematische, die geometrische und analytische, Methode gefunden werden. Aber Theils betrifft dieß nicht alle Resultate, und der Zweck der Einführung des Unendlichen ist nicht allein, den gewöhnlichen Weg abzukürzen, sondern zu Resultaten zu gelangen, die durch diesen nicht geleistet werden können. Theils rechtfertigt der Erfolg die Manier des Wegs nicht für sich. Diese Manier aber der Rechnung des Unendlichen zeigt sich durch den Schein der Ungenauigkeit gedrückt, den sie sich giebt, indem sie endliche Größen um eine unendlich kleine Größe das eine Mal vermehrt, diese in der fernern Operation zum Theil beibehält, aber einen Theil derselben auch vernachlässigt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"73.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0008","text":"Dieß Verfahren enthält die Sonderbarkeit, daß der eingestandenen Ungenauigkeit unerachtet, ein Resultat herauskommt, das nicht nur ziemlich und so nahe, daß der Unterschied außer Acht gelassen werden könnte, sondern vollkommen genau ist. In der Operation selbst aber, die dem Resultate vorher geht, kann die Vorstellung nicht entbehrt werden, daß Einiges nicht gleich Null, aber so unbeträchtlich sey, um außer Acht gelassen werden zu können. Allein bei dem, was unter mathematischer Bestimmtheit zu verstehen ist, fällt aller Unterschied einer größern oder geringern Genauigkeit gänzlich hinweg, wie in der Philosophie nicht von größerer oder geringerer Wahrscheinlichkeit, sondern von der Wahrheit allein die Rede seyn kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"73.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0009","text":"Wenn die Methode und der Gebrauch des Unendlichen durch den Erfolg gerechtfertigt wird, so ist es nicht so überflüssig dessen ungeachtet die Rechtfertigung derselben zu fordern, als es bei der Nase überflüssig scheint, nach dem Erweise des Rechts, sich ihrer zu bedienen, zu fragen. Denn es ist bei der mathematischen als einer wissenschaftlichen Erkenntniß wesentlich um den Beweis zu thun, und auch in Ansehung der Resultate ist es der Fall, daß die streng mathematische Methode nicht zu allen den Beleg des Erfolgs liefert, der aber ohnehin nur ein äußerlicher Beleg ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"73.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0010","text":"Es ist der Mühe werth, den mathematischen Begriff des Unendlichen und die merkwürdigsten Versuche näher zu betrachten, welche die Absicht haben, den Gebrauch desselben zu rechtfertigen und die Schwierigkeit, von der sich die Methode gedrückt fühlt, zu beseitigen. Die Betrachtung dieser Rechtfertigungen und Bestimmungen des mathematischen Unendlichen, welche ich in dieser Anmerkung weitläufiger anstellen will, wird zugleich das beste Licht auf die Natur des wahren Begriffes selbst werfen, und zeigen, wie er ihnen vorgeschwebt und zu Grunde gelegen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"73.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0011","text":"Die gewöhnliche Bestimmung des mathematischen Unendlichen ist, daß es eine Größe sey, über welche es,—wenn sie als das Unendlichgroße—keine größere oder,—wenn sie als das Unendlichkleine bestimmt ist—kleinere mehr gebe, oder die, in jenem Falle, größer, in diesem Falle kleiner sey, als jede beliebige Größe.—In dieser Definition ist freilich der wahre Begriff nicht ausgedrückt, vielmehr nur, wie schon bemerkt, derselbe Widerspruch, der im unendlichen Progresse ist; aber sehen wir, was an sich darin enthalten ist. Eine Größe wird in der Mathematik definirt, daß sie etwas sey, das vermehrt und vermindert werden könne; überhaupt also eine gleichgültige Grenze. Indem nun das Unendlich Große oder Kleine ein solches ist, das nicht mehr vermehrt oder vermindert werden könne, so ist es in der That kein Quantum als solches mehr.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"73.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0012","text":"Diese Konsequenz ist nothwendig und unmittelbar. Aber die Reflexion, daß das Quantum,—und ich nenne in dieser Anmerkung Quantum überhaupt, wie es ist, das endliche Quantum,—aufgehoben ist, ist es, welche nicht gemacht zu werden pflegt und die für das gewöhnliche Begreifen die Schwierigkeit ausmacht, indem das Quantum, indem es unendlich ist, als ein Aufgehobenes, als ein solches zu denken gefordert wird, das nicht ein Quantum ist, und dessen quantitative Bestimmtheit doch bleibt.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"73.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0013","text":"Um das anzuführen, wie Kant jene Bestimmung beurtheilt, [9] so findet er sie nicht übereinstimmend mit dem, was man unter einem unendlichen Ganzen verstehe. \"Nach dem gewöhnlichen Begriffe sey eine Größe unendlich, über die keine größere (d. i. über die darin enthaltene Menge einer gegebenen Einheit) möglich ist; es sey aber keine Menge die größte, weil noch immer eine oder mehrere Einheiten hinzugefügt werden können.—Durch ein unendliches Ganzes dagegen werde nicht vorgestellt, wie groß es sey, mithin sey sein Begriff nicht der Begriff eines Maximums (oder Minimums), sondern es werde dadurch nur sein Verhältniß zu einer beliebig anzunehmenden Einheit gedacht, in Ansehung deren dasselbe größer ist, als alle Zahl.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"73.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0014","text":"Je nachdem diese Einheit größer oder kleiner angenommen würde, würde das Unendliche größer oder kleiner seyn; allein die Unendlichkeit, da sie bloß in dem Verhältnisse zu dieser gegebenen Einheit bestehe, würde immer dieselbe bleiben, obgleich Freilich die absolute Größe des Ganzen dadurch gar nicht erkannt würde.\"","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"73.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0015","text":"[9] In der Anmerkung zur Thesis der ersten kosmologischen Antinomie, in der Kritik der reinen Vernunft.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"73.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0016","text":"Kant tadelt es, wenn unendliche Ganze als ein Maximum, als eine vollendete Menge einer gegebenen Einheit angesehen werden. Das Maximum oder Minimum als solches erscheint noch immer als ein Quantum, eine Menge. Solche Vorstellung kann die von Kant angeführte Konsequenz nicht ablehnen, die auf ein größeres oder kleineres Unendliches führt. Überhaupt indem das Unendliche als Quantum vorgestellt wird, gilt noch für dasselbe der Unterschied eines Größern oder Kleinern. Allein diese Kritik trifft nicht den Begriff des wahrhaften mathematischen Unendlichen, der unendlichen Differenz, denn diese ist kein endliches Quantum mehr.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"73.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0017","text":"Kants Begriff der Unendlichkeit dagegen, den er den wahren transcendentalen nennt, ist, \"daß die successive Synthesis der Einheit in Durchmessung eines Quantums niemals vollendet seyn könne.\" Es ist ein Quantum überhaupt als gegeben vorausgesetzt; dieß solle durch das Synthesiren der Einheit zu einer Anzahl, einem bestimmt anzugebenden Quantum gemacht werden, aber dieß Synthesiren niemals vollendet werden können. Hiermit ist wie erhellt, nichts als der Progreß ins Unendliche ausgesprochen, nur transcendental, d. i. eigentlich subjektiv und psychologisch vorgestellt. An sich soll zwar das Quantum vollendet seyn, aber transcendentaler Weise, nämlich im Subjekte, welches ihm ein Verhältniß zu einer Einheit giebt, entstehe nur eine solche Bestimmung des Quantums, die unvollendet und schlechthin mit einem Jenseits behaftet sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"73.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0018","text":"Es wird also hier überhaupt beim Widerspruche, den die Größe enthält, stehen geblieben, aber vertheilt an das Objekt und das Subjekt, so daß jenem die Begrenztheit, diesem aber das Hinausgehen über jede von ihm aufgefaßte Bestimmtheit, in das schlechte Unendliche zukommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"73.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0019","text":"Es ist dagegen vorhin gesagt worden, daß die Bestimmung des mathematischen Unendlichen und zwar wie es in der höhern Analysis gebraucht wird, dem Begriffe des wahrhaften Unendlichen entspricht; die Zusammenstellung beider Bestimmungen soll nun in ausführlicher Entwickelung vorgenommen werden.—Was zuerst das wahrhafte unendliche Quantum betrifft, so bestimmte es sich als an ihm selbst unendlich; es ist dieß, indem, wie sich ergeben hat, das endliche Quantum oder das Quantum überhaupt, und sein Jenseits, das schlechte Unendliche, auf gleiche Weise aufgehoben sind. Das aufgehobene Quantum ist damit in die Einfachheit und in die Beziehung auf sich selbst zurückgegangen, aber nicht nur wie das extensive, indem es in intensives Quantum überging, das seine Bestimmtheit nur an sich an einer äußern Vielfachheit hat, gegen die es jedoch gleichgültig und wovon es verschieden seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"73.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0020","text":"Das unendliche Quantum enthält vielmehr erstens die Äußerlichkeit und zweitens die Negation derselben an ihm selbst; so ist es nicht mehr irgend ein endliches Quantum, nicht eine Größebestimmtheit, die ein Daseyn als Quantum hätte, sondern es ist einfach, und daher nur als Moment; es ist eine Größebestimmtheit in qualitativer Form; seine Unendlichkeit ist, als eine qualitative Bestimmtheit zu seyn.—So als Moment ist es in wesentlicher Einheit mit seinem Andern, nur als bestimmt durch dieses sein Anderes, d. i. es hat nur Bedeutung in Beziehung auf ein im Verhältniß mit ihm Stehendes. Außer diesem Verhältnisse ist es Null; —da gerade das Quantum als solches gegen das Verhältniß gleichgültig, in ihm doch eine unmittelbare ruhende Bestimmung seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"73.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0021","text":"In dem Verhältnisse als nur Moment ist es nicht ein für sich Gleichgültiges; es ist, in der Unendlichkeit als Fürsichseyn, indem es zugleich eine quantitative Bestimmtheit ist, nur als ein Für-Eines.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"73.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0022","text":"Der Begriff des Unendlichen, wie er sich hier abstrakt exponirt hat, wird sich zeigen, dem mathematischen Unendlichen zu Grunde liegen, und er selbst wird deutlicher werden, indem wir die verschiedenen Stufen des Ausdrucks des Quantums als eines Verhältniß-Moments betrachten, von der untersten an, wo es noch zugleich Quantum als solches ist, bis zu der höhern, wo es die Bedeutung und den Ausdruck eigentlicher unendlicher Größe erhält.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"73.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0023","text":"Nehmen wir also zuerst das Quantum in dem Verhältnisse, wie es eine gebrochene Zahl ist. Solcher Bruch 2/7 z.B. ist nicht ein Quantum wie 1, 2, 3 u.s.f., zwar eine gewöhnliche endliche Zahl, jedoch nicht eine unmittelbare, wie die ganzen Zahlen, sondern als Bruch mittelbar bestimmt durch zwei andere Zahlen, die Anzahl und Einheit gegeneinander sind, wobei auch die Einheit eine bestimmte Anzahl ist. Aber von dieser nähern Bestimmung derselben gegeneinander abstrahirt, und sie bloß nach dem, was ihnen in der qualitativen Beziehung, in der sie hier sind, als Quantis widerfährt, betrachtet, so sind 2 und 7 sonst gleichgültige Quanta; indem sie aber hier nur als Momente, eines des andern, und damit eines Dritten (des Quantums, das der Exponent heißt) auftreten, so gelten sie sogleich nicht als 2 und 7, sondern nur nach ihrer Bestimmtheit gegeneinander.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"73.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0024","text":"Statt ihrer kann darum eben so gut 4 und 14, oder 6 und 21 u.s.f. ins Unendliche gesetzt werden. Hiermit fangen sie also an, einen qualitativen Charakter zu haben. Gälten sie als bloße Quanta, so ist 2 und 7, schlechthin das eine nur 2, das andere nur 7; 4, 14, 6, 21 u.s.f. sind schlechthin etwas Anderes als jene Zahlen, und können insofern sie nur unmittelbare Quanta wären, die einen nicht an die Stelle der anderen gesetzt werden. Insofern aber und nicht nach der Bestimmtheit, solche Quanta zu seyn, gelten, so ist ihre gleichgültige Grenze aufgehoben; sie haben somit, nach dieser Seite, das Moment der Unendlichkeit an ihnen, indem sie nicht bloß eben nicht mehr sie sind, sondern ihre quantitative Bestimmtheit, aber als eine an sich seyende qualitative,—nämlich nach dem, was sie im Verhältnisse gelten,—bleibt.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"73.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0025","text":"Es können unendlich viele andere an ihre Stelle gesetzt werden, so daß der Werth des Bruches durch, die Bestimmtheit, welche das Verhältniß hat, sich nicht ändert.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"73.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0026","text":"Die Darstellung, welche die Unendlichkeit an einem Zahlenbruche hat, ist aber darum noch unvollkommen, weil die beiden Seiten des Bruchs, 2 und 7, aus dem Verhältnisse genommen werden können, und gewöhnliche gleichgültige Quanta sind; die Beziehung derselben, im Verhältnisse und Momente zu seyn, ist ihnen etwas Äußerliches und Gleichgültiges. Ebenso ist ihre Beziehung selbst ein gewöhnliches Quantum, der Exponent des Verhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"73.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0027","text":"Die Buchstaben, mit denen in der allgemeinen Arithmetik operirt wird, die nächste Allgemeinheit, in welche die Zahlen erhoben werden, haben die Eigenschaft nicht, daß sie von einem bestimmten Zahlenwerth sind; sie sind nur allgemeine Zeichen und unbestimmte Möglichkeiten jedes bestimmten Werthes. Der Bruch a/b scheint daher ein passenderer Ausdruck des Unendlichen zu seyn, weil a und b aus ihrer Beziehung aufeinander genommen, unbestimmt bleiben, und auch getrennt keinen besonderen eigenthümlichen Werth haben.—Allein diese Buchstaben sind zwar als unbestimmte Größen gesetzt; ihr Sinn aber ist, daß sie irgend ein endliches Quantum seyen. Da sie also zwar die allgemeine Vorstellung, aber nur von der bestimmten Zahl sind, so ist es ihnen ebenfalls gleichgültig, im Verhältnisse zu seyn, und außer demselben behalten sie diesen Werth.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"73.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0028","text":"Betrachten wir noch näher, was im Verhältnisse vorhanden ist, so hat es die beiden Bestimmungen an ihm, erstlich ein Quantum zu seyn, dieses aber ist zweitens nicht als ein unmittelbares, sondern das den qualitativen Gegensatz an ihm hat; es bleibt in demselben zugleich jenes bestimmte, gleichgültige Quantum dadurch, daß es aus seinem Andersseyn, dem Gegensatze, in sich zurückgekehrt, somit auch ein Unendliches ist. Diese beiden Bestimmungen stellen sich in der folgenden bekannten Form, in ihrem Unterschiede von einander entwickelt dar.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"73.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0029","text":"Der Bruch 2/7 kann ausgedrückt werden als 0,285714…als 1 + a + a[hoch2] + a[hoch3] u.s.f. So ist er als eine unendliche Reihe; der Bruch selbst heißt die Summe oder der endliche Ausdruck derselben. Vergleichen wir die beiden Ausdrücke, so stellt der eine, die unendliche Reihe, ihn nicht mehr als Verhältniß, sondern nach der Seite dar, daß er ein Quantum ist als eine Menge von solchen, die zu einander hinzukommen, als eine Anzahl.—Daß die Größen, die ihn als Anzahl ausmachen sollen, wieder aus Decimalbrüchen, also selbst aus Verhältnissen bestehen, darauf kommt es hier nicht an; denn dieser Umstand betrifft die besondere Art der Einheit dieser Größen, nicht sie, insofern sie die Anzahl constituiren; wie auch eine aus mehreren Ziffern bestehende ganze Zahl des Decimalsystems wesentlich als eine Anzahl gilt, und nicht darauf gesehen wird, daß sie aus Produkten einer Zahl und der Zahl Zehen","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"73.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0030","text":"und deren Potenzen besteht. So wie es hier auch nicht darauf ankommt, daß es andere Brüche giebt als der z. B. genommene 2/7, die zu Dezimalbrüchen gemacht, nicht eine unendliche Reihe geben; jeder aber kann für ein Zahlensystem von anderer Einheit als eine solche ausgedrückt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"73.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0031","text":"Indem nun in der unendlichen Reihe, die den Bruch als Anzahl darstellen soll, die Seite, daß er Verhältniß ist, verschwindet, so verschwindet auch die Seite, nach welcher er, wie vorhin gezeigt, die Unendlichkeit an ihm hatte. Diese aber ist auf eine andere Weise hereingekommen; die Reihe ist nämlich selbst unendlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"73.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0032","text":"Von welcher Art nun die Unendlichkeit der Reihe sey, erhellt von selbst; es ist die schlechte Unendlichkeit des Progresses. Die Reihe enthält und stellt den Widerspruch dar, etwas, das ein Verhältniß ist und qualitative Natur in ihm hat, als ein Verhältnißloses, als ein bloßes Quantum, als Anzahl, darzustellen. Die Folge davon ist, daß an der Anzahl, die in der Reihe ausgedrückt ist, immer etwas fehlt, so daß über das, was gesetzt ist, immer hinausgegangen werden muß, um die geforderte Bestimmtheit zu erreichen. Das Gesetz des Fortgangs ist bekannt, es liegt in der Bestimmung des Quantums, die im Bruche enthalten ist, und in der Natur der Form, in der sie ausgedrückt werden soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"73.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0033","text":"Die Anzahl kann wohl durch Fortsetzung der Reihe so genau gemacht werden, als man nöthig hat; aber immer bleibt die Darstellung durch sie nur ein Sollen; sie ist mit einem Jenseits behaftet, das nicht aufgehoben werden kann, weil ein auf qualitativer Bestimmtheit beruhendes als Anzahl auszudrücken der bleibende Widerspruch ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"73.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0034","text":"In dieser unendlichen Reihe ist jene Ungenauigkeit wirklich vorhanden, von der am wahrhaften mathematischen Unendlichen nur der Schein vorkommt. Diese beiden Arten des mathematischen Unendlichen sind so wenig zu verwechseln, als die beiden Arten des philosophischen Unendlichen. Bei der Darstellung des wahrhaften mathematischen Unendlichen ist anfangs die Form der Reihe gebraucht oder auch neuerlich wieder hervorgerufen worden. Aber sie ist für dasselbe nicht nothwendig; im Gegentheil ist das Unendliche der unendlichen Reihe wesentlich von jenem unterschieden, wie die Folge zeigen soll. Diese vielmehr steht sogar dem Ausdrucke des Bruches nach.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"73.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0035","text":"Die unendliche Reihe enthält nämlich die schlechte Unendlichkeit, weil das, was die Reihe ausdrücken soll, ein Sollen bleibt; und was sie ausdrückt, mit einem Jenseits, das nicht verschwindet, behaftet und verschieden von dem ist, was ausgedrückt werden soll. Sie ist unendlich nicht um der Glieder willen, die gesetzt sind, sondern darum, weil sie unvollständig sind, weil das Andere, das zu ihnen wesentlich gehört, jenseits ihrer ist; was in ihr da ist, der gesetzten Glieder mögen so viele seyn als wollen, ist nur ein Endliches, im eigentlichen Sinne, gesetzt als Endliches, d. i. als solches, das nicht ist, was es seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"73.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0036","text":"Dagegen ist aber das, was der endliche Ausdruck, oder die Summe solcher Reihe genannt wird, ohne Mangel; er enthält den Werth, den die Reihe nur sucht, vollständig; das Jenseits ist aus der Flucht zurückgerufen; was er ist, und was er seyn soll, ist nicht getrennt, sondern ist dasselbe.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"73.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0037","text":"Das beide Unterscheidende liegt näher sogleich darin, daß in der unendlichen Reihe das Negative außerhalb ihrer Glieder ist, welche Gegenwart haben, indem sie nur als Theile der Anzahl gelten. In dem endlichen Ausdrucke dagegen, der ein Verhältniß ist, ist das Negative immanent, als das Bestimmtseyn der Seiten des Verhältnisses durcheinander, welches ein in sich Zurückgekehrtseyn, sich auf sich beziehende Einheit, als Negation der Negation (beide Seiten des Verhältnisses sind nur als Momente), ist, hiermit die Bestimmung der Unendlichkeit in sich hat.—Zu der That ist also die gewöhnlich sogenannte Summe, das 2/7 oder 1/1-a', ein Verhältniß; und dieser sogenannte endliche Ausdruck ist der wahrhaft unendliche Ausdruck.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"73.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0038","text":"Die unendliche Reihe dagegen ist in Wahrheit Summe; ihr Zweck ist, das was an sich Verhältniß ist, in der Form einer Summe darzustellen, und die vorhandenen Glieder der Reihe sind nicht als Glieder eines Verhältnisses, sondern eines Aggregats. Sie ist ferner vielmehr der endliche Ausdruck; denn sie ist das unvollkommene Aggregat, und bleibt wesentlich ein Mangelhaftes. Sie ist nach dem, was in ihr da ist, ein bestimmtes Quantum, zugleich aber ein geringeres, als sie seyn soll; alsdann auch das, was ihr fehlt, ist ein bestimmtes Quantum; dieser fehlende Theil ist in der That das, was das Unendliche an der Reihe heißt, nach der nur formellen Seite, daß er ein Fehlendes, ein Nichtseyn ist; nach seinem Inhalte ist er ein endliches Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"73.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0039","text":"Das was in der Reihe da ist, zusammen mit dem was ihr fehlt, macht erst das aus, was der Bruch ist, das bestimmte Quantum, das sie gleichfalls seyn soll, aber zu seyn nicht vermag. —Das Wort: Unendlich, pflegt, auch in der unendlichen Reihe, in der Meinung etwas Hohes und Hehres zu seyn; es ist dieß eine Art von Aberglauben, der Aberglaube des Verstands; man hat gesehen, wie es sich vielmehr auf die Bestimmung der Mangelhaftigkeit reducirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"73.39"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0040","text":"Daß es, kann noch bemerkt werden, unendliche Reihen giebt, die nicht summirbar sind, ist in Bezug auf die Form von Reihe überhaupt ein äußerlicher und zufälliger Umstand. Sie enthalten eine höhere Art der Unendlichkeit, als die summirbaren; nämlich eine Incommensurabilität, oder die Unmöglichkeit, das darin enthaltene quantitative Verhältniß als ein Quantum, sey es auch als Bruch, darzustellen; die Form der Reihe aber als solche, die sie haben, enthält dieselbe Bestimmung der schlechten Unendlichkeit, welche in der summirbaren Reihe ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"73.40"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0041","text":"Die so eben am Bruche und an seiner Reihe bemerkte Verkehrung in Ansehung des Ausdrucks findet auch Statt, insofern das mathematische Unendliche nämlich nicht das so eben genannte sondern das wahrhafte, das relative Unendliche,—das gewöhnliche metaphysische dagegen, worunter das abstrakte, schlechte Unendliche verstanden wird, das absolute genannt worden ist. In der That ist vielmehr dieses metaphysische nur das relative, weil die Negation, die es ausdrückt, nur so im Gegensatze einer Grenze ist, daß diese außer ihm bestehen bleibt, und von ihm nicht aufgehoben wird; das mathematische Unendliche hingegen hat die endliche Grenze wahrhaft in sich aufgehoben, weil das Jenseits derselben mit ihr vereinigt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"73.41"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0042","text":"In dem Sinne, in welchem aufgezeigt worden, daß die sogenannte Summe oder der endliche Ausdruck einer unendlichen Reihe, vielmehr als der unendliche anzusehen ist, ist es vornehmlich, daß Spinoza den Begriff der wahren Unendlichkeit gegen den der schlechten aufstellt und durch Beispiele erläutert. Sein Begriff gewinnt am neisten Licht, indem ich das, was er hierüber sagt, an diese Entwickelung anschließe.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"73.42"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0043","text":"Er definirt zunächst das Unendliche als die absolute Affirmation der Existenz irgend einer Natur, das Endliche im Gegentheil als Bestimmtheit, als Verneinung. Die absolute Affirmation einer Existenz ist nämlich als ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst zu nehmen, nicht dadurch zu seyn, daß ein Anderes ist; das Endliche hingegen ist die Verneinung, ein Aufhören als Beziehung auf ein Anderes, das außer ihm anfängt. Die absolute Affirmation einer Existenz erschöpft nun zwar den Begriff der Unendlichkeit nicht; dieser enthält, daß die Unendlichkeit Affirmation ist, nicht als unmittelbare, sondern nur als wiederhergestellte durch die Reflexion des Anderen in sich selbst, oder als Negation des Negativen. Aber bei Spinoza hat die Substanz und deren absolute Einheit die Form von unbewegter d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"73.43"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0044","text":"nicht sich mit sich selbst vermittelnder Einheit, von einer Starrheit, worin der Begriff der negativen Einheit des Selbst, die Subjektivität, sich noch nicht findet.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"73.44"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0045","text":"Das mathematische Beispiel, womit er das wahre Unendliche (Epist. XXIX.) erläutert, ist ein Raum zwischen zwei ungleichen Kreisen, deren einer innerhalb des andern, ohne ihn zu berühren, fällt, und die nicht koncentrisch sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"73.45"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0046","text":"Er machte, wie es scheint, sich viel aus dieser Figur und dem Begriffe als deren Beispiel er sie gebrauchte, daß er sie zum Motto seiner Ethik machte.—\"Die Mathematiker, sagt er, schließen, daß die Ungleichheiten, die in einem solchen Raume möglich sind, unendlich sind, nicht aus der unendlichen Menge der Theile, denn seine Größe ist bestimmt und begrenzt, und ich kann größere und kleinere solche Räume setzen, sondern weil die Natur der Sache jede Bestimmtheit übertrift.\"—Man sieht, Spinoza verwirftjene Vorstellung vom Unendlichen, nach welcher es als Menge oder als Reihe vorgestellt wird, die nicht vollendet ist, und erinnert, daß hier an dem Raume des Beispiels das Unendliche nichtjenseits, sondern gegenwärtig und vollständig ist; dieser Raum ist ein Begrenztes, aber darum ein Unendliches, \"weil die Natur der Sache jede Bestimmtheit übersteigt,\" weil die darin enthaltene","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"73.46"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0047","text":"Größenbestimmung zugleich nicht als ein Quantum darstellbar ist, oder nach obigem kantischen Ausdruck das Synthesiren nicht zu einem—diskreten—Quantum vollendet werden kann.—Wie überhaupt der Gegensatz von kontinuirlichem und diskretem Quantum auf das Unendliche führt, soll in einer spätern Anmerkung auseinander gesetzt werden.—Jenes Unendliche einer Reihe nennt Spinoza das Unendliche der Imagination; das Unendliche hingegen als Beziehung auf sich selbst, das Unendliche des Denkens oder infinitum actu. Es ist nämlich actu, es ist wirklich unendlich, weil es in sich vollendet und gegenwärtig ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"73.47"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0048","text":"So ist die Reihe, 0,285714… oder 1 + a + a[hoch 2] + a[hoch 3]… das Unendliche bloß der Einbildung oder des Meinens; denn es hat keine Wirklichkeit, es fehlt ihm schlechthin etwas; hingegen 2/7 oder 1/1-a ist das wirklich, nicht nur was die Reihe in ihren vorhandenen Gliedern ist, sondern noch das dazu, was ihr mangelt, was sie nur seyn soll. Das 2/7 oder 1/1-a ist gleichfalls eine endliche Größe, wie der zwischen den zwei Kreisen eingeschlossene Raum Spinoza's und dessen Ungleichheiten; und kann wie dieser Raum größer oder kleiner gemacht werden. Aber es kommt damit nicht die Ungereimtheit eines größern oder kleinern Unendlichen heraus; denn dieß Quantum des Ganzen, geht das Verhältniß seiner Momente, die Natur der Sache d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"73.48"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0049","text":"die qualitative Größenbestimmung, nichts an; das was in der unendlichen Reihe da ist, ist ebenso ein endliches Quantum, aber außerdem noch ein Mangelhaftes.—Die Einbildung dagegen bleibt beim Quantum als solchem stehen, und reflektirt nicht auf die qualitative Beziehung, welche den Grund der vorhandenen Inkommensurabilität ausmacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"73.49"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0050","text":"Die Inkommensurabilität, welche in dem Beispiel Spinoza's liegt, schließt überhaupt die Funktionen krummer Linien in sich, und führt näher auf das Unendliche, das die Mathematik bei solchen Funktionen, überhaupt bei den Funktionen veränderlicher Größen eingeführt hat, und welches das wahrhafte mathematische, quantitative Unendliche ist, das auch Spinoza sich dachte. Diese Bestimmung soll nun hier näher erörtert werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"73.50"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0051","text":"Was vors erste die für so wichtig geltende Kategorie der Veränderlichkeit betrifft, unter welche die in jenen Funktionen bezogenen Größen gefaßt werden, so sollen sie zunächst veränderlich nicht in dem Sinne seyn, wie im Bruche 2/7 die beiden Zahlen 2 und 7, indem eben so sehr 4 und 14, 6 und 21 und so fort ins Unendliche andere Zahlen an ihre Stelle gesetzt werden können, ohne den im Bruche gesetzten Werth zu ändern. So kann noch mehr in a/b an die Stelle von a und b jede beliebige Zahl gesetzt werden, ohne das zu ändern was a/b ausdrücken soll. In dem Sinne nur, daß auch an die Stelle von x und y einer Funktion eine unendliche d. h. unerschöpfliche Menge von Zahlen gesetzt werden könne, sind a und b so sehr veränderliche Größe als jene, x und y.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"73.51"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0052","text":"Der Ausdruck: veränderliche Größen, ist darum sehr vage, und unglücklich gewählt für Größebestimmungen, die ihr Interesse und Behandlungsart in etwas in etwas ganz Anderem liegen haben, als in ihrer bloßen Veränderlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"73.52"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0053","text":"Um es deutlich zu machen, worin die wahrhafte Bestimmung der Momente einer Funktion liegt, mit denen sich das Interesse der höhern Analysis beschäftigt, müssen wir die bemerklich gemachten Stufen noch einmal durchlaufen. In 2/7 oder a/b sind 2 und 7 jedes für sich, bestimmte Quanta und die Beziehung ist ihnen nicht wesentlich; a und b soll gleichfalls solche Quanta vorstellen, die auch außer dem Verhältnisse bleiben, was sie sind. Ferner ist auch 2/7 und a/b ein fixes Quantum, ein Quotient; das Verhältniß macht eine Anzahl aus, deren Einheit der Nenner, und die Anzahl dieser Einheiten der Zähler—oder umgekehrt ausdrückt; wenn auch 4 und 14 u.s.f. an die Stelle von 2 und 7 treten, bleibt das Verhältniß auch als Quantum dasselbe.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"73.53"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0054","text":"Dieß verändert sich nun aber wesentlich in der Funktion y[hoch 2]/x = p z.B.; hier haben x und y zwar den Sinn, bestimmte Quanta seyn zu können; aber nicht x und y, sondern nur x und y[hoch 2] haben einen bestimmten Quotienten.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"73.54"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0055","text":"Dadurch sind diese Seiten des Verhältnisses, x und y, erstens nicht nur keine bestimmten Quanta, sondern zweitens ihr Verhältniß ist nicht ein fixes Quantum, (noch ist dabei ein solches wie bei a und b gemeint), nicht ein fester Quotient, sondern er ist als Quantum schlechthin veränderlich. Dieß aber ist allein darin enthalten, daß x nicht zu y ein Verhältniß hat, sondern zum Quadrate von y.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"73.55"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0056","text":"Das Verhältniß einer Größe zur Potenz ist nicht ein Quantum, sondern wesentlich qualitatives Verhältniß; das Potenzenverhältniß ist der Umstand, der als Grundbestimmung anzusehen ist.—In der Function der geraden Linie y = a x aber, ist x/y = a ein gewöhnlicher Bruch und Quotient; diese Funktion ist daher nur formell eine Funktion von veränderlichen Größen, oder x und y sind hier was a und b in a/b, sie sind nicht in derjenigen Bestimmung, in welcher die Differential- und Integralrechnung sie betrachtet.—Wegen der besondern Natur der veränderlichen Größen in dieser Betrachtungsweise, wäre es zweckmäßig gewesen, für sie sowohl einen besonderen Namen, als andere Bezeichnungen einzuführen, als die gewöhnlichen der unbekannten Größen in jeder endlichen, bestimmten oder unbestimmten Gleichung; um ihrer wesentlichen Verschiedenheit willen von solchen bloß unbekannten Größen, die an sich","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"73.56"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0057","text":"vollkommen bestimmte Quanta, oder ein bestimmter Umfang von bestimmten Quantis sind.—Es ist auch nur der Mangel des Bewußtseyns, über die Eigenthümlichkeit dessen, was das Interesse der höheren Analysis ausmacht und das Bedürfniß und die Erfindung des Differential-Kalkuls herbeigeführt hat, daß Funktionen des ersten Grades wie die Gleichung der geraden Linie in die Behandlung dieses Kalkuls für sich mit hereingenommen werden; seinen Antheil an solchem Formalismus hat ferner der Mißverstand, der die an sich richtige Forderung der Verallgemeinerung einer Methode dadurch zu erfüllen meint, daß die specifische Bestimmtheit, auf","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"73.57"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0058","text":"die sich das Bedürfniß gründet, weggelassen wird, daß es dafür gilt, als ob es sich in diesem Felde nur um veränderliche Größen überhaupt handle. Es wäre wohl viel Formalismus in den Betrachtungen dieser Gegenstände wie in der Behandlung erspart worden, wenn man eingesehen hätte, daß derselbe nicht veränderliche Größen als solche, sondern Potenzenbestimmungen betreffe.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"73.58"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0059","text":"Aber es ist noch eine weitere Stufe, auf der das mathematische Unendliche in seiner Eigenthümlichkeit hervortritt. In einer Gleichung, worin x und y zunächst als durch ein Potenzenverhältniß bestimmt, gesetzt sind, sollen x und y als solche noch Quanta bedeuten; diese Bedeutung nun geht vollends in den sogenannten unendlich kleinen Differenzen gänzlich verloren. d x, d y sind keine Quanta mehr, noch sollen sie solche bedeuten, sondern haben allein in ihrer Beziehung eine Bedeutung, einen Sinn blos als Momente. Sie sind nicht mehr Etwas, das Etwas als Quantum genommen, nicht endliche Differenzen; aber auch nicht Nichts, nicht die bestimmungslose Null. Außer ihrem Verhältnisse sind sie reine Nullen, aber sie sollen nur als Momente des Verhältnisses, als Bestimmungen des Differential-Koefficienten d x/ d y genommen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"73.59"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0060","text":"In diesem Begriff des Unendlichen ist das Quantum wahrhaft zu einem qualitativen Daseyn vollendet; es ist als wirklich unendlich gesetzt; es ist nicht nur als dieses oder jenes Quantum aufgehoben, sondern als Quantum überhaupt. Es bleibt aber die Quantitätsbestimmtheit als Element von Quantis, Princip, oder sie wie man auch gesagt hat, in ihrem ersten Begriffe.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"73.60"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0061","text":"Gegen diesen Begriff ist aller Angriff gerichtet, der auf die Grundbestimmung der Mathematik dieses Unendlichen, der Differentialund Integralrechnung, gemacht worden ist. Unrichtige Vorstellungen der Mathematiker selbst veranlaßten es, wenn er nicht anerkannt worden ist; vornehmlich aber ist die Unvermögenheit, den Gegenstand als Begriff zu rechtfertigen, Schuld an diesen Anfechtungen. Den Begriff kann aber die Mathematik, wie oben erinnert worden, hier nicht umgehen; denn als Mathematik des Unendlichen schränkt sie sich nicht auf die endliche Bestimmtheit ihrer Gegenstände ein,—wie in der reinen Mathematik der Raum und die Zahl und deren Bestimmungen nur nach ihrer Endlichkeit betrachtet und auf einander bezogen werden—; sondern sie versetzt eine von daher aufgenommene und von ihr behandelte Bestimmung in Identität mit ihrer entgegengesetzten, wie sie z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"73.61"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0062","text":"eine krumme Linie zu einer geraden, den Kreis zu einem Polygon u.s.f. macht. Die Operationen, die sie sich als Differential- und Integralrechnung erlaubt, sind daher der Natur bloß endlicher Bestimmungen und deren Beziehungen gänzlich widersprechend und hätten darum ihre Rechtfertigung allein in dem Begriff.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"73.62"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0063","text":"Wenn die Mathematik des Unendlichen daran festhielt, daß jene Quantitäts-Bestimmungen verschwindende Größen d. h. solche, die nicht mehr irgend ein Quantum, aber auch nicht Nichts, sondern noch eine Bestimmtheit gegen Anderes sind, so schien nichts klarer, als daß es keinen solchen Mittelzustand, wie man es nannte, zwischen Seyn und Nichts gebe.—Was es mit diesem Einwurfe und sogenannten Mittelzustande auf sich habe, ist oben bereits bei der Kategorie des Werdens, Anmerk. 4. gezeigt. Allerdings ist die Einheit des Seyns und Nichts kein Zustand; ein Zustand wäre eine Bestimmung des Seyns und Nichts, worein diese Momente nur etwa zufälligerweise gleichsam als in eine Krankheit oder äußerliche Affektion durch ein irrthümliches Denken gerathen sollten; sondern diese Mitte und Einheit, das Verschwinden oder eben so das Werden, ist vielmehr allein ihre Wahrheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"73.63"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0064","text":"Was unendlich sey, ist ferner gesagt worden, sey nicht vergleichbar als ein Größeres oder Kleineres; es könne daher nicht ein Verhältniß von Unendlichen zu Unendlichen, noch Ordnungen oder Dignitäten des Unendlichen geben, als welche Unterschiede der unendlichen Differenzen in der Wissenschaft derselben vorkommen.—Es liegt bei diesem schon erwähnten Einwurfe immer die Vorstellung zu Grunde, daß hier von Quantis die Rede seyn solle, die als Quanta verglichen werden; daß Bestimmungen, die keine Quanta mehr sind, kein Verhältniß mehr zu einander haben. Vielmehr ist aber das, was nur im Verhältniß ist, kein Quantum; das Quantum ist eine solche Bestimmung, die außer ihrem Verhältniß ein vollkommen gleichgültiges Daseyn haben, der ihr Unterschied von einem anderen gleichgültig seyn soll, da hingegen das qualitative nur das ist, was es in seinem Unterschiede von dnem Anderen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"73.64"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0065","text":"Jene unendlichen Größen sind daher nicht nur vergleichbar, sondern sind nur als Momente der Vergleichung, des Verhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"73.65"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0066","text":"Ich führe die wichtigsten Bestimmungen an, welche in der Mathematik über dieß Unendliche gegeben worden sind; es wird daraus erhellen, daß denselben der Gedanke der Sache, übereinstimmend mit dem hier entwickelten Begriffe, zu Grunde liegt, daß ihre Urheber ihn aber als Begriff nicht ergründeten und bei der Anwendung wieder Auskunftsmittel nöthig hatten, welche ihrer besseren Sache widersprechen.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"73.66"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0067","text":"Der Gedanke kann nicht richtiger bestimmt werden, als Newton ihn gegeben hat. Ich trenne dabei die Bestimmungen ab, die der Vorstellung der Bewegung und der Geschwindigkeit angehören, (von welcher er vornehmlich den Namen Fluxionen nahm), weil der Gedanke hierin nicht in der gehörigen Abstraktion, sondern konkret, vermischt mit außerwesentlichen Formen erscheint. Diese Fluxionen erklärt Newton (Princ. mathem. phil. nat. L. 1. Lemma XI. Schol.) dahin, daß er nicht untheilbare—eine Form, deren sich frühere Mathematiker, Cavalleri und andere, bedienten, und welche den Begriff eines an sich bestimmten Quantums enthält,—verstehe, sondern verschwindende Theilbare. Ferner nicht Summen und Verhältnisse bestimmter Theile, sondern die Grenzen (limites) der Summen, und Verhältnisse.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"73.67"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0068","text":"Es werde die Einwendung gemacht, daß verschwindende Größen kein letztes Verhältniß haben, weil es, ehe sie verschwunden, nicht das Letzte, und wenn sie verschwunden, keines mehr ist. Aber unter dem Verhältnisse verschwindender Größen sey das Verhältniß zu verstehen, nicht eh sie verschwinden, und nicht nachher, sondern mit dem sie verschwinden ( quacum evanescunt ). Eben so ist das erste Verhältniß werdender Größen, das mit dem sie werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"73.68"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0069","text":"Nach dem damaligen Stande der wissenschaftlichen Methode wurde nur erklärt, was unter einem Ausdrucke zu verstehen sey; daß aber dieß oder jenes darunter zu verstehen sey, ist eigentlich eine subjektive Zumuthung oder auch eine historische Forderung, wobei nicht gezeigt wird, daß ein solcher Begriff an und für sich nothwendig ist und innere Wahrheit hat. Allein das Angeführte zeigt, daß der von Newton aufgestellte Begriff dem entspricht, wie die unendliche Größe sich in der obigen Darstellung aus der Reflexion des Quantums in sich ergab. Es sind Größen verstanden, in ihrem Verschwinden, d. h. die nicht mehr Quanta sind; ferner nicht Verhältnisse bestimmter Theile, sondern die Grenzen des Verhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"73.69"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0070","text":"Es sollen also sowohl die Quanta für sich, die Seiten des Verhältnisses, als damit auch das Verhältniß, insofern es ein Quantum wäre, verschwinden; die Grenze des Größen-Verhältnisses ist, worin es ist und nicht ist; dieß heißt genauer, worin das Quantum verschwunden, und damit das Verhältniß nur als qualitatives Quantitäts-Verhältniß, und die Seiten desselben ebenso als qualitative Quantitäts-Momente erhalten sind.—Newton fügt hinzu, daß daraus, daß es letzte Verhältnisse der verschwindenden Größen gebe, nicht zu schließen sey, daß es letzte Größen, Untheilbare, gebe. Dieß wäre nämlich wieder ein Absprung von dem abstrakten Verhältnisse auf solche Seiten desselben, welche für sich außer ihrer Beziehung einen Werth haben sollten, als Untheilbare, als etwas, das ein Eins, ein Verhältnißloses seyn würde.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"73.70"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0071","text":"Gegen jenen Mißverstand erinnert er noch, daß die letzten Verhältnisse nicht Verhältnisse letzter Größen seyen, sondern Grenzen, denen die Verhältnisse der ohne Grenze abnehmenden Größen näher sind als jeder gegebene d. h. endliche Unterschied, welche Grenze sie aber nicht überschreiten, so daß sie Nichts würden.—Unter letzten Größen hätten nämlich, wie gesagt, Untheilbare oder Eins verstanden werden können. In der Bestimmung des letzten Verhältnisses aber ist sowohl die Vorstellung des gleichgültigen Eins, des verhältnißlosen, als auch des endlichen Quantums entfernt.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"73.71"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0072","text":"Es bedürfte aber weder des Abnehmens ohne Grenze, in das Newton das Quantum versetzt und das nur den Progreß ins Unendliche ausdrückt, noch der Bestimmung der Theilbarkeit, welche hier keine unmittelbare Bedeutung mehr hat, wenn die geforderte Bestimmung sich zum Begriffe einer Größebestimmung, die rein nur Moment des Verhältnisses ist, fortgebildet hätte.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"73.72"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0073","text":"In Rücksicht der Erhaltung des Verhältnisses im Verschwinden der Quantorum findet sich (anderwärts, wie bei Carnot, Réflexions sur la Métaphysique du Calcul Infinitésimal.) der Ausdruck, daß vermöge des Gesetzes der Stätigkeit die verschwindenden Größen noch das Verhältniß, aus dem sie herkommen, ehe sie verschwinden, behalten. —Diese Vorstellung drückt die wahre Natur der Sache aus, insofern nicht die Stätigkeit des Quantums verstanden wird, die es im unendlichen Progreß hat, sich in sein Verschwinden so zu kontinuiren, daß im Jenseits seiner wieder nur ein endliches Quantum, ein neues Glied der Reihe entsteht; ein stätiger Fortgang wird aber immer so vorgestellt, daß die Werthe durchloffen werden, welche noch endliche Quanta sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"73.73"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0074","text":"In demjenigen Übergange dagegen, welcher in das wahrhafte Unendliche gemacht wird, ist das Verhältniß das stätige; es ist so sehr stätig und sich erhaltend, daß er vielmehr allein darin besteht, das Verhältniß rein herauszuheben, und die verhältnißlose Bestimmung, d. i. daß ein Quantum, welches Seite des Verhältnisses ist, auch außer dieser Beziehung gesetzt, noch Quantum ist, verschwinden zu machen. —Diese Reinigung des quantitativen Verhältnisses ist insofern nichts anders, als wenn ein empirisches Daseyn begriffen wird. Dieß wird hierdurch so über sich selbst erhoben, daß sein Begriff dieselben Bestimmungen enthält, als es selbst, aber in ihrer Wesentlichkeit und in die Einheit des Begriffes gefaßt, worin sie ihr gleichgültiges, begriffloses Bestehen verloren haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"73.74"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0075","text":"Gleich interessant ist die andere Form der newtonischen Darstellung der in Rede stehenden Größen, nämlich als erzeugender Größen oder Principien. Eine erzeugte Größe (genita) ist ein Produkt oder Quotient, Wurzeln, Rechtecke, Quadrate, auch Seiten von Rechtecken, Quadraten;—überhaupt eine endliche Größe.—\"Sie als veränderlich betrachtet, wie sie in fortdauernder Bewegung und Fließen zu- oder abnehmend ist, so verstehe er ihre momentanen Inkremente oder Dekremente unter dem Namen von Momenten. Diese sollen aber nicht für Theilchen von bestimmter Größe genommen werden ( particulae finitae ).","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"73.75"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0076","text":"Solche seyen nicht selbst Momente, sondern aus Momenten erzeugte Größen; es seyen vielmehr die werdenden Principien oder Anfänge endlicher Größen zu verstehen.\"—Das Quantum wird hier von sich selbst unterschieden, wie es als ein Produkt oder Daseyendes, und wie es in seinem Werden, in seinem Anfange und Princip, das heißt, wie es in seinem Begriffe, oder was hier dasselbe ist, in seiner qualitativen Bestimmnng ist; in der letztern sind die quantitativen Unterschiede, die unendlichen Inkremente oder Dekremente, nur Momente; erst das Gewordene ist das in die Gleichgültigkeit des Daseyns und in die Äußerlichkeit übergegangene, das Quantum.—Wenn aber diese in Ansehung der Inkremente oder Dekremente angeführten Bestimmungen des Unendlichen, von der Philosophie des wahrhaften Begriffs anerkannt werden müssen, so ist auch sogleich zu bemerken, daß die Formen selbst von Inkrementen u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"73.76"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0077","text":"innerhalb der Kategorie des unmittelbaren Quantums und des erwähnten stätigen Fortgangs fallen, und vielmehr sind die Vorstellungen von Inkrement, Zuwachs, Zunahme des x um d x oder i u.s.f. als das in den Methoden vorhandene Grundübel anzusehen;—als das bleibende Hinderniß, aus der Vorstellung des gewöhnlichen Quantums die Bestimmung des qualitativen Quantitätsmoments rein herauszuheben.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"73.77"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0078","text":"Gegen die angegebenen Bestimmungen steht die Vorstellung von unendlich-kleinen Größen, die auch im Inkrement oder Dekrement selbst steckt, weit zurück. Nach derselben sollen sie von der Beschaffenheit seyn, daß nicht nur sie gegen endliche Größen, sondern auch deren höhere Ordnungen gegen die niedrigere, oder auch die Produkte aus mehrern gegen eine einzelne zu vernachlässigen seyen. —bei Leibnitz hebt sich die Forderung dieser Vernachlässigung, welche die vorhergehenden Erfinder von Methoden, die sich auf diese Größe bezogen, gleichfalls eintreten lassen, auffallender hervor. Sie ist es vornehmlich, die diesem Kalkul beim Gewinne der Bequemlichkeit den Schein von Ungenauigkeit und ausdrücklicher Unrichtigkeit in dem Wege seiner Operation giebt.—Wolf hat sie in seiner Weise, die Sachen populär zu machen, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"73.78"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0079","text":"den Begriff zu verunreinigen und unrichtige sinnliche Vorstellungen an dessen Stelle zu setzen, verständlich zu machen gesucht. Er vergleicht nämlich die Vernachlässigung der unendlichen Differenzen höherer Ordnungen gegen niedrigere, mit dem Verfahren eines Geometers, der bei der Messung der Höhe eines Berges um nicht weniger genau gewesen sey, wenn der Wind indeß ein Sandkörnchen von der Spitze weggeweht habe, oder mit der Vernachlässigung der Höhen der Häuser, Thürme bei der Berechnung der Mondfinsternisse (Element. Mathes. univ. Tom. I. El. Analys. math. P. II. C. I. s. Schol.).","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"73.79"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0080","text":"Wenn die Billigkeit des gemeinen Menschenverstandes eine solche Ungenauigkeit erlaubt, so haben dagegen alle Geometer diese Vorstellung verworfen. Es dringt sich von selbst auf, daß in der Wissenschaft der Mathematik von einer solchen empirischen Genauigkeit ganz und gar nicht die Rede ist, daß das mathematische Messen durch Operationen des Kalkuls oder durch Konstruktionen und Beweise der Geometrie, gänzlich vom Feldmessen, vom Messen empirischer Linien, Figuren u.s.f. unterschieden ist. Ohnehin zeigen, wie oben angeführt, die Analytiker durch die Vergleichung des Resultats, wie es auf streng geometrischem Wege und wie es nach der Methode der unendlichen Differenzen erhalten wird, daß das eine dasselbe ist als das andere, und daß ein Mehr oder Weniger von Genauigkeit ganz und gar nicht Statt findet.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"73.80"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0081","text":"Und es versteht sich von selbst, daß ein absolut genaues Resultat nicht aus einem Verfahren herkommen könne, das ungenau wäre. Jedoch kann wieder auf der anderen Seite das Verfahren selbst, jener Vernachlässigung aus dem Grunde der Unbedeutenheit, des Protestirens gegen die angeführte Rechtfertigungsweise unerachtet, nicht entbehren. Und dieß ist die Schwierigkeit, um welche die Bemühungen der Analytiker gehen, das hierin liegende Widersinnige begreiflich zu machen, und es zu entfernen.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"73.81"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0082","text":"Es ist in dieser Rücksicht vornehmlich Eulers Vorstellung anzuführen. Indem er die allgemeine Newtonische Definition zu Grunde legt, dringt er darauf, daß die Differentialrechnung die Verhältnisse der Inkremente einer Größe betrachte, daß aber die unendliche Differenz als solche ganz als Null zu betrachten sey, (Institut. Calc. different. P. I. C. III.).—Wie dieß zu verstehen ist, liegt im Vorhergehenden; die unendliche Differenz ist Null nur des Quantums, nicht eine qualitative Null, sondern als Null des Quantums vielmehr reines Moment nur des Verhältnisses. Sie ist nicht ein Unterschied um eine Größe; aber darum ist es einer Seits überhaupt schief, jene Momente, welche unendlich-kleine Größen heißen, auch als Inkremente oder Dekremente, und als Differenzen auszusprechen.","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"73.82"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0083","text":"Dieser Bestimmung liegt zu Grunde, daß zu der zuerst vorhandenen endlichen Größe etwas hinzukomme oder davon abgezogen werde, eine Subtraktion oder Addition, eine arithmetische, äußerliche Operation vorgehe. Der Übergang von der Funktion der veränderlichen Größe in ihr Differential ist aber anzusehen, daß er von ganz anderer Natur ist, nämlich wie erörtert worden, daß er als Zurückführung der endlichen Funktion auf das qualitative Verhältniß ihrer Quantitätsbestimmungen zu betrachten ist.—Anderer Seits fällt die schiefe Seite für sich auf, wenn gesagt wird, daß die Inkremente für sich Nullen seyen, daß nur ihre Verhältnisse betrachtet werden; denn eine Null hat überhaupt keine Bestimmtheit mehr.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"73.83"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0084","text":"Diese Vorstellung kommt also zwar bis zum Negativen des Quantums und spricht es bestimmt aus, aber faßt dieß Negative nicht zugleich in seiner positiven Bedeutung, von qualitativen Quantitätsbestimmungen, die, wenn sie aus dem Verhältnisse gerissen und als Quanta genommen werden wollten, nur Nullen wären.—Lagrange ( Théorie des fonct. analyt. Introd. ) urtheilt über die Vorstellung der Grenzen oder letzten Verhältnisse, daß wenn man gleich sehr gut das Verhältniß zweier Größen sich vorstellen könne, so lange sie endlich bleiben, so gebe dieß Verhältniß dem Verstande keinen deutlichen und bestimmten Begriff, sobald seine Glieder zugleich Null werden.—In der That muß der Verstand über diese bloß negative Seite, daß die Verhältnißglieder Nullen als Quanta sind, hinausgehen, und sie positiv, als qualitative Momente auffassen.—Was aber Euler (am angeführten Ort §. 84 ff.)","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"73.84"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0085","text":"weiter in Betreff der gegebenen Bestimmung hinzufügt, um zu zeigen, daß zwei sogenannte unendlich kleine Größen, welche nichts anders als Nullen seyn sollen, doch ein Verhältniß zu einander haben und deßwegen auch nicht das Zeichen der Null, sondern andere Zeichen für sie im Gebrauch seyen, kann nicht für genügend angesehen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"73.85"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0086","text":"Er will dieß durch den Unterschied des arithmetischen und geometrischen Verhältnisses begründen; bei jenem sehen wir auf die Differenz, bei diesem auf den Quotienten, obgleich das erstere zwischen zwei Nullen gleich sey, so sey es deßwegen doch das geometrische nicht; wenn 2:1 = 0:0, so müsse wegen der Natur der Proportion, da das erste Glied doppelt so groß sey als das zweite, auch das dritte Glied doppelt so groß als das vierte seyn; O:O soll also nach der Proportion als das Verhältniß von 2:1 genommen werden.—Auch nach der gemeinen Arithmetik seyn n.O = O; es sey also n:1 = O:O.—Allein eben dadurch, daß 2:1 oder n:1 ein Verhältniß von Quantis ist, entspricht ihm nicht ein Verhältniß noch eine Bezeichnung von O:O.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"73.86"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0087","text":"Ich enthalte mich, die Anführungen zu vermehren, indem die betrachteten zur Genüge gezeigt haben, daß in ihnen wohl der wahrhafte Begriff des Unendlichen liegt, daß er aber nicht in seiner Bestimmtheit herausgehoben und gefaßt worden ist. Indem daher zur Operation selbst fortgegangen wird, so kann es nicht geschehen, daß in ihr die wahrhafte Begriffsbestimmung sich geltend mache; die endliche Quantitätsbestimmtheit kehrt vielmehr zurück und die Operation kann der Vorstellung eines bloß relativ-kleinen nicht entbehren. Der Kalkul macht es nothwendig, die sogenannten unendlichen Größen den gewöhnlichen arithmetischen Operationen des Addirens u.s.f., welche sich auf die Natur endlicher Größen gründen, zu unterwerfen, und sie somit als endliche Größen für einen Augenblick gelten zu lassen und als solche zu behandeln.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"73.87"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0088","text":"Der Kalkul hätte sich darüber zu rechtfertigen, daß er sie das eine Mal in diese Sphäre herabzieht und sie als Inkremente oder Differenzen behandelt, und daß er auf der anderen Seite sie als Quanta vernachlässigt, nachdem er so eben Formen und Gesetze der endlichen Größen auf sie angewendet hatte.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"73.88"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0089","text":"Über die Versuche der Geometer, diese Schwierigkeiten zu beseitigen, führe ich noch das Hauptsächlichste an.","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"73.89"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0090","text":"Die ältern Analytiker machten sich hierüber weniger Skrupel; aber die Bemühungen der Neueren gingen vornehmlich dahin, den Kalkul des Unendlichen zur Evidenz der eigentlich geometrischen Methode zurückzubringen und in ihr die Strenge der Beweise der Alten (- Ausdrücke von Lagrange—) in der Mathematik zu erreichen. Allein da das Princip der Analysis des Unendlichen höherer Natur, als das Princip der Mathematik endlicher Größen ist, so mußte jene von selbst sogleich auf jene Art von Evidenz Verzicht thun, wie die Philosophie auch auf diejenige Deutlichkeit keinen Anspruch machen kann, die die Wissenschaften des Sinnlichen, z.B. Naturgeschichte hat, und wie Essen und Trinken für ein verständlicheres Geschäfte gilt, als Denken und Begreifen. Es wird sich demnach nur um die Bemühung handeln, die Strenge der Beweise der Alten zu erreichen.","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"73.90"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0091","text":"Mehrere haben versucht, den Begriff des Unendlichen ganz zu entbehren, und ohne ihn das zu leisten, was an den Gebrauch desselben gebunden schien.—Lagrange spricht z.B. von der Methode, die Landen erfunden hat, und sagt von ihr, daß sie rein analytisch sey und die unendlich kleinen Differenzen nicht gebrauche, sondern zuerst verschiedene Werthe der veränderlichen Größen einführe, und sie in der Folge gleichsetze. Er urtheilt übrigens, daß darin die der Differentialrechnung eignen Vorzüge, Einfachheit der Methode und Leichtigkeit der Operationen verloren gehe.—Es ist dieß wohl ein Verfahren, das mit demjenigen etwas Entsprechendes hat, von welchem Descartes Tangentenmethode ausgeht, die weiterhin noch näher zu erwähnen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"73.91"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0092","text":"Soviel, kann hier bemerkt werden, erhellt sogleich im Allgemeinen, daß das Verfahren überhaupt, verschiedene Werthe der veränderlichen Größen anzunehmen, und sie nachher gleichzusetzen, einem anderen Kreise mathematischer Behandlung angehört, als die Methode des Differential-Kalkuls selbst und die späterhin näher zu erörternde Eigenthümiichkeit des einfachen Verhältnisses, auf welches sich die wirkliche konkrete Bestimmung desselben zurückführt, nämlich der abgeleiteten Funktion zu der ursprünglichen, nicht herausgehoben wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"73.92"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0093","text":"Die Ältern unter den Neuern, wie z.B. Fermat, Barrow und andere, die sich zuerst des Unendlich-Kleinen in derjenigen Anwendung bedienten, welche später zur Differential- und Integralrechnung ausgebildet wurde, und dann auch Leibnitz und die Folgenden, auch Euler, haben immer unverhohlen, die Produkte von unendlichen Differenzen, so wie ihre höhern Potenzen nur aus dem Grunde weglassen zu dürfen geglaubt, weil sie relativ gegen die niedrige Ordnung verschwinden. Hierauf beruht bei ihnen allein der Fundamentalsatz, nämlich die Bestimmung dessen, was das Differential eines Produkts oder einer Potenz sey, denn hierauf reducirt sich die ganze theoretische Lehre.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"73.93"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0094","text":"Das Übrige ist Theils Mechanismus der Entwickelung, Theils aber Anwendung, in welche jedoch, was weiterhin zu betrachten ist, in der That auch das höhere oder vielmehr einzige Interesse fällt.—In Rücksicht auf das Gegenwärtige ist hier nur das Elementarische anzuführen, daß aus dem gleichen Grunde der Unbedeutenheit als der Hauptsatz, die Curven betreffend, angenommen wird, daß die Elemente der Curven, nämlich die Inkremente der Abscisse und der Ordinate, das Verhältniß der Subtangente und der Ordinate zu einander haben; für die Absicht, ähnliche Dreiecke zu erhalten, wird der Bogen, der die dritte Seite eines Dreiecks zu den beiden Inkrementen, des mit Recht vormals sogenannten charakteristischen Dreiecks, ausmacht, als eine gerade Linie, als Theil der Tangente, und damit das eine der Inkremente bis an die Tangente reichend angesehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"73.94"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0095","text":"Diese Annahmen erheben jene Bestimmungen einer Seits über die Natur endlicher Größen; anderer Seits aber wird ein Verfahren auf die nun unendlich genannten Momente angewendet, das nur von endlichen Größen gilt, und bei dem nichts aus Rücksicht der Unbedeutenheit vernachiässigt werden darf. Die Schwierigkeit, von der die Methode gedrückt wird, bleibt bei solcher Verfahrungsweise in ihrer ganzen Stärke.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"73.95"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0096","text":"Es ist hier eine merkwürdige Procedur Newtons anzuführen; (Princ. Math. phil. nat. Lib. II. Lemma II. Propos. VII.)—die Erfindung eines sinnreichen Kunststücks, uni das arithmetisch unrichtige Weglassen der produkte unendlicher Differenzen oder höherer Ordnungen derselben bei dem Finden der Differentialien, zu beseitigen. Er findet das Differential des Produkts,—woraus sich dann die Differentialien der Quotienten, Potenzen u.s.f. leicht herleiten, —auf folgende Art. Das Produkt, wenn x, y, jedes um die Hälfte seiner unendlichen Differenz kleiner genommen wird, geht über in x y—xdy/2—ydx/2 + dxdy/4; aber wenn man x und y um ebenso viel zunehmen läßt, in x y + xdy/2 + ydx/2 + dxdy/4.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"73.96"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0097","text":"Von diesem zweiten Produkt nun das erste abgezogen, bleibt y d x + x d y als Überschuß, und dieß sey der Überschuß des Wachsthums um ein ganzes dx und dy, denn um dieses Wachsthum sind beide Produkte unterschieden; es ist also das Differential von xy.—Man sieht in diesem Verfahren fällt das Glied, welches die Hauptschwierigkeit ausmacht, das Produkt der beiden unendlichen Differenzen, dxdy, durch sich selbst hinweg. Aber des newtonischen Namens unerachtet muß es gesagt werden dürfen, daß solche, obgleich sehr elementarische Operation, unrichtig ist; es ist unrichtig, daß (x + dx/2) (y + dy/2)—(x—dx/2) (y—dy/2) = (x + dx) (y + dy)—xy. Es kann nur das Bedürfniß seyn, den Fluxionen-Kalkul bei seiner Wichtigkeit zu begründen, was einen Newton dahin bringen konnte, die Täuschung solchen Beweisens sich zu machen.","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"73.97"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0098","text":"Andere Formen, die Newton bei der Ableitung des Differentials gebraucht, sind an konkrete auf Bewegung sich beziehende Bedeutungen der Elemente und deren Potenzen gebunden.—Beim Gebrauche der Reihenform, der sonst seine Methode auszeichnet, liegt es zu nahe zu sagen, daß man es immer in seiner Macht habe, durch das Hinzufügen weiterer Glieder die Größe so genau zu nehmen, als man nöthig habe, und daß die weggelassenen relativ unbedeutend, überhaupt das Resultat nur eine Näherung sey, als daß er nicht auch hier mit diesem Grunde sich begnügt hätte, wie er bei seiner Methode der Auflösung der Gleichungen höherer Grade durch Näherung die höheren Potenzen, die bei der Substitution jedes gefundenen noch ungenauen Werthes in die gegebene Gleichung entstehen, aus dem rohen Grunde ihrer Kleinigkeit wegläßt; s. Lagrange Equations Numériques p. 125.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"73.98"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0099","text":"Der Fehler, in welchen Newton bei der Auflösung eines Problems durch das Weglassen wesentlicher höherer Potenzen verfiel, der seinen Gegnern die Gelegenheit eines Triumphs ihrer Methode über die seinige gab, und von welchem Lagrange in seiner neuerlichen Untersuchung desselben (Théorie des fonct. analyt. 3me P. Ch. IV.) den wahren Ursprung aufgezeigt hat, beweist das Formelle und die Unsicherheit, die im Gebrauche jenes Instruments noch vorhanden war. Lagrange zeigt, daß Newton dadurch in den Fehler fiel, weil er das Glied der Reihe vernachlässigte, das die Potenz enthielt, auf welche es in der bestimmten Aufgabe ankam.","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"73.99"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0100","text":"Newton hatte sich an jenes formelle oberflächliche Princip, Glieder wegen ihrer relativen Kleinheit wegzulassen, gehalten.—Es ist nämlich bekannt, daß in der Mechanik den Gliedern der Reihe, in der die Funktion einer Bewegung entwickelt wird, eine bestimmte Bedeutung gegeben wird, so daß sich das erste Glied oder die erste Funktion auf das Moment der Geschwindigkeit, die zweite auf die beschleunigende Kraft, und die dritte auf den Widerstand von Kräften beziehe. Die Glieder der Reihe sind hiermit hier nicht nur als Theile einer Summe anzusehen, sondern als qualitative Momente eines Ganzen des Begriffs. Hiedurch erhält das Weglassen der übrigen Glieder, die der schlechtunendlichen Reihe angehören, eine gänzlich verschiedene Bedeutung, von dem Weglassen aus dem Grunde der relativen Kleinheit derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"73.100"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0101","text":"[10] Die newtonsche Auflösung enthielt jenen Fehler, nicht weil in ihr Glieder der Reihe, nur als Theile einer Summe, sondern weil das Glied, das die qualitative Bestimmung, auf die es ankam, enthält, nicht berücksichtigt wurde.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"73.101"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0102","text":"[10] In einfacher Weise finden sich bei Lagrange in der Anwendung der Theorie der Funktionen auf die Mechanik, in dem Kapitel von der geradlinigten Bewegung, beide Rücksichten neben einander gestellt (Théorie des fonct. 3me P. Ch. I. art. 4.). Der durchloffene Raum als Funktion der verflossenen Zeit betrachtet, giebt die Gleichung x = ft; diese als f (t + ë) entwickelt giebt","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"73.102"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0103","text":"ft + ëft + [ë'[hoch 2]]/2. f\"t + u.s.w.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"73.103"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0104","text":"Also der während der Zeit durchloffene Raum stellt sich in der Formel dar, ëft + [ë[hoch 2]]/2. f't + [ë[hoch 3]]/2.3. f\"t + u.s.w. Die Bewegung, vermittelst der dieser Raum durchloffen wird, ist also, wird gesagt, d. h. weil die analytische Entwickelung mehrere und zwar unendlich viele Glieder giebt,—zusammengesetzt aus verschiedenen partiellen Bewegungen, deren der Zeit entsprechende Räume seyn werden ëft, [ë[hoch 2]]/2. f\"t, [ë[hoch 3]]/[2.3]. f\"t, u.s.w. die erste partielle Bewegung ist, in bekannter Bewegung die formell=gleichförmige mit einer durch f't bestimmten Geschwindigkeit, die zweite die gleichförmig beschleunigte, die von einer dem f't propertionirten beschleunigenden Kraft herkommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"73.104"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0105","text":"\"Da nun die übrigen Glieder sich auf keine einfache bekannte Bewegung beziehen, so ist nicht nöthig, sie besonders in Rücksicht zu nehmen, und wir werden zeigen, daß man von ihnen in der Bestimmung der Bewegung zu Anfang des Zeitpunkts abstrahiren kann.\" Dieß wird nun gezeigt, aber freilich nur durch die Vergleichung jener Reihe, deren Glieder alle zur Bestimmung der Größe des in der Zeit durchloffenen Raumes gehörten, mit der art. 3 für die Bewegung des Falls angegebenen Gleichung x = at + bt[hoch 2], als in welcher nur diese zwei Glieder vorkommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"73.105"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0106","text":"Aber diese Gleichung hat selbst nur diese Gestalt, durch die Voraussetzung der Erklärung, die den durch analytische Entwicklung entstehenden Gliedern gegeben wird, erhalten; diese Voraussetzung ist, daß die gleichförmig beschleunigte Bewegung zusammengesetzt sey, aus einer formell-gleichförmigen mit der im vorhergehenden Zeittheile erlangten Geschwindigkeit fortgesetzten Bewegung, und einem Zuwachse, (dem a in s = at[hoch 2] d.i. dem empirischen Koefficienten), welcher der Kraft der Schwere zugeschrieben wird,—einem Unterschiede, der keineswegs in der Natur der Sache irgend eine Existenz oder Grund hat, sondern nur der fälschlich physikalisch gemachte Ausdruck dessen ist, was bei einer angenommenen analytischen Behandlung herauskommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"73.106"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0107","text":"In diesem Beispiele ist der qualitative Sinn dasjenige, wovon das Verfahren abhängig gemacht ist. Im Zusammenhange hiermit kann sogleich die allgemeine Behauptung aufgestellt werden, daß die ganze Schwierigkeit des Princips beseitigt seyn würde, wenn statt des Formalismus, die Bestimmung des Differentials nur in die ihm den Namen gebende Aufgabe, den Unterschied überhaupt einer Funktion von ihrer Veränderung, nachdem ihre veränderliche Größe einen Zuwachs erhalten, zu stellen, die qualitative Bedeutung des Princips angegeben, und die Operation hiervon abhängig gemacht wäre. In diesem Sinne zeigt sich das Differential von x[hoch n], durch das erste Glied der Reihe, die durch die Entwickelung von (x + dx)[hoch n] sich ergiebt, gänzlich erschöpft.","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"73.107"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0108","text":"Daß die übrigen Glieder nicht berücksichtigt werden, kommt so nicht von ihrer relativen Kleinheit her;—es wird dabei nicht eine Ungenauigkeit, ein Fehler oder Irrthum vorausgesetzt, der durch einen anderen Irrthum ausgeglichen und verbessert würde; eine Ansicht, von welcher aus Carnot vornehmlich die gewöhnliche Methode der Infinitesimalrechnung rechtfertigt. Indem es sich nicht um eine Summe, sondern um ein Verhältniß handelt, so ist das Differential vollkommen durch das erste Glied gefunden; und wo es fernerer Glieder, der Differentiale höherer Ordnungen bedarf, so liegt in ihrer Bestimmung nicht die Fortsetzung einer Reihe als Summe, sondern die Wiederholung eines und desselben Verhältnisses, das man allein will, und das somit im ersten Glied bereits vollkommen bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"73.108"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0109","text":"Das Bedürfniß der Form einer Reihe des Summirens derselben und was damit zusammenhängt, muß dann ganz von jenem Interesse des Verhältnisses getrennt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"73.109"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0110","text":"Die Erläuterungen, welche Carnot über die Methode der unendlichen Größen giebt, enthalten das Geläutertste und aufs Klarste exponirt, was in den oben angeführten Vorstellungen vorkam. Aber bei dem Übergange zur Operation selbst treten mehr oder weniger die gewöhnlichen Vorstellungen, von der unendlichen Kleinheit der weggelassenen Glieder gegen die andern ein. Er rechtfertigt die Methode vielmehr durch die Thatsache, daß die Resultate richtig werden, und durch den Nutzen, den die Einführung unvollkommner Gleichungen, wie er sie nennt, d. h. solcher, in denen eine solche arithmetisch unrichtige Weglassung geschehen ist, für die Vereinfachung und Abkürzung des Kalkuls habe, als durch die Natur der Sache selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"73.110"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0111","text":"Lagrange hat bekanntlich die ursprüngliche Methode Newtons, die Methode der Reihen, wieder aufgenommen, um der Schwierigkeiten, welche die Vorstellung des Unendlich-Kleinen, so wie derjenigen, welche die Methode der ersten und letzten Verhältnisse und Grenzen mit sich führt, überhoben zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"73.111"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0112","text":"Es ist von seinem Funktionen-Kalkul, dessen sonstige Vorzüge in Rücksicht auf Präcision, Abstraktion und Allgemeinheit anerkannt genug sind, als hierher gehörig nur dieß anzuführen, daß er auf dem Fundamentalsatze beruht, daß die Differenz, ohne daß sie Null werde, so klein angenommen werden könne, daß jedes Glied der Reihe die Summe aller folgenden an Größe übertreffe.—Es wird auch in dieser Methode von den Kategorien vom Zuwachs und von der Differenz der Funktion angefangen, deren veränderliche Größe den Zuwachs erhalte, womit die lästige Reihe hereinkommt, von der ursprünglichen Funktion; so wie im Verfolg die wegzulassenden Glieder der Reihe nur in der Rücksicht, daß sie eine Summe constituiren, in Betracht kommen, und der Grund, sie wegzulassen, in das Relative ihres Quantums gesetzt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"73.112"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0113","text":"Die Weglassung ist also hier auch nicht für das Allgemeine auf den Gesichtspunkt zurückgeführt, der Theils in einigen Anwendungen vorkommt, worin, wie vorhin erinnert, die Glieder der Reihe eine bestimmte qualitative Bedeutung haben sollen und Glieder außer Acht gelassen werden, nicht darum weil sie unbedeutend an Größe sind, sondern weil sie unbedeutend der Qualität nach sind; Theils aber fällt dann die Weglassung selbst in dem wesentlichen Gesichtspunkte hinweg, der sich für den sogenannten Differential-Koefficienten erst in der sogenannten Anwendung des Kalkuls bei Lagrange bestimmt heraushebt, was in der folgenden Anmerkung ausführlicher auseinandergesetzt werden wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"73.113"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0114","text":"Der qualitative Charakter überhaupt, der hier an der in Rede stehenden Größenform in demjenigen, was dabei das Unendlichkleine genannt wird, nachgewiesen worden ist, findet sich am unmittelbarsten in der Kategorie der Grenze des Verhältnisses, die oben angeführt worden, und deren Durchführung im Kalkul zu einer eigenthümlichen Methode gestempelt worden ist. Was Lagrange von dieser Methode urtheilt, daß sie der Leichtigkeit in der Anwendung entbehre, und der Ausdruck Grenze keine bestimmte Idee darbiete, davon wollen wir das Zweite hier aufnehmen, und näher sehen, was über ihre analytische Bedeutung aufgestellt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"73.114"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0115","text":"In der Vorstellung der Grenze liegt nämlich wohl die angegebene wahrhafte Kategorie der qualitativen Verhältnißbestimmung der veränderlichen Größen, denn die Formen, die von ihnen eintreten, dx und dy, sollen schlechthin nur als Momente von dy/dx genommen, und dx/dy selbst als ein einziges untheilbares Zeichen angesehen werden. Daß hiermit für den Mechanismus des Kalkuls besonders in seiner Anwendung der Vortheil verloren geht, den er davon zieht, daß die Seiten des Differential-Koefficienten von einander abgesondert werden, ist hier bei Seite zu setzen. Jene Grenze soll nun Grenze von einer gegebenen Funktion seyn;—sie soll einen gewissen Werth in Beziehung auf dieselbe angeben, der sich durch die Weise der Ableitung bestimmt. Mit der bloßen Kategorie der Grenze aber wären wir nicht weiter, als mit dem, um das es in dieser Anm.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"73.115"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0116","text":"zu thun gewesen ist, nämlich aufzuzeigen, daß das Unendlichkleine, das in der Differentialrechnung als dx und dy vorkommt, nicht bloß den negativen, leeren Sinn einer nicht endlichen, nicht gegebenen Größe habe, wie wenn man sagt, eine unendliche Menge, ins unendliche fort und dergleichen, sondern den bestimmten Sinn der qualitativen Bestimmtheit des Quantitativen, eines Verhältnißmoments als eines solchen. Diese Kategorie hat jedoch so noch kein Verhältniß zu dem, was eine gegebene Funktion ist, und greift für sich nicht in die Behandlung einer solchen und in einen Gebrauch, der an ihr von jener Bestimmung zu machen wäre, ein; so würde auch die Vorstellung der Grenze, zurückgehalten in dieser von ihr nachgewiesenen Bestimmtheit, zu nichts führen. Aber der Ausdruck Grenze enthält es schon selbst, daß sie Grenze von Etwas sey, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":116,"address":"73.116"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0117","text":"einen gewissen Werth ausdrücke, der in der Funktion veränderlicher Größe liegt; und es ist zu sehen, wie dieß konkrete Benehmen mit ihr beschaffen ist.—Sie soll die Grenze des Verhältnisses seyn, welches die zwei Inkremente zu einander haben, um welche die zwei veränderlichen Größen, die in einer Gleichung verbunden sind, deren die eine als eine Funktion der andern angesehen wird, als zunehmend angenommen worden;—der Zuwachs wird hier unbestimmt überhaupt genommen und insofern von dem Unendlichkleinen kein Gebrauch gemacht. Aber zunächst führt der Weg, diese Grenze zu finden, dieselben Inkonsequenzen herbei, die in den übrigen Methoden liegen. Dieser Weg ist nämlich folgender. Wenn y = fx, soll fx, wenn y in y + k übergeht, sich in fx + ph + qh[hoch 2] + rh[hoch 3] u.s.f. verändert, hiermit ist k = ph + qh[hoch 2] u.s.f. und k/h = p + qh + rh[hoch 2] u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":117,"address":"73.117"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0118","text":"Wenn nun k und h verschwinden, so verschwindet das zweite Glied außer p, welches p nun die Grenze des Verhältnisses der beiden Zuwächse sey. Man sieht, daß h als Quantum = 0 gesetzt wird, aber daß darum k/h nicht zugleich = 0 seyn, sondern noch ein Verhältniß bleiben soll. Den Vortheil, die Inkonsequenz, die hierin liegt, abzulehnen, soll nun die Vorstellung der Grenze gewähren; p soll zugleich nicht das wirkliche Verhältniß, das = 0/0 wäre, sondern nur der bestimmte Werth seyn, dem sich das Verhältniß unendlich d.i. so nähern könne, daß der Unterschied kleiner als jeder gegebene werden könne. Der bestimmtere Sinn der Näherung in Rücksicht dessen, was sich eigentlich einander nähern soll, wird unten betrachtet werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":118,"address":"73.118"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0119","text":"—Daß aber ein quantitativer Unterschied, der die Bestimmung hat, kleiner als jeder gegebene seyn zu können nicht nur, sondern seyn zu sollen, kein quantitativer Unterschied mehr ist, dieß ist für sich klar, so evident als irgend etwas in der Mathematik evident seyn kann; damit aber ist über dy/dx = 0/0 nicht hinausgekommen worden. Wenn dagegen dy/dx = p d.i. als ein bestimmtes quantitatives Verhältniß, angenommen wird, wie dieß in der That der Fall ist, so kommt umgekehrt die Voraussetzung, welche h = 0 gesetzt hat, in Verlegenheit, eine Voraussetzung, durch welche allein k/h = p gefunden wird. Giebt man aber zu, daß k/h = 0 ist, und mit h = 0 wird in der That von selbst auch k = 0; denn der Zuwachs k zu y findet nur unter der Bedingung statt, daß der Zuwachs h ist; so wäre zu sagen, was denn p seyn solle, welches ein ganz bestimmter quantitativer Werth ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":119,"address":"73.119"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0120","text":"Hierauf giebt sich sogleich die einfache, trockne Antwort von selbst, daß es ein Koefficient ist und aus welcher Ableitung er entsteht,—die auf gewisse bestimmte Weise abgeleitete erste Funktion einer ursprünglichen Funktion.","kind":"passage","sequence":120,"address":"73.120"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0121","text":"Begnügte man sich damit, wie denn in der That Lagrange sich der Sache nach damit begnügt hat, so wäre der allgemeine Theil der Wissenschaft des Differential-Kalkuls und unmittelbar diese seine Form selbst, welche die Theorie der Grenzen heißt, von den Zuwächsen, dann deren unendlicher oder beliebiger Kleinheit, von der Schwierigkeit, außer dem ersten Gliede oder vielmehr nur dem Coefficienten des ersten Gliedes die weitern Glieder einer Reihe, als welche durch die Einführung jener Zuwächse unabwendbar sich einfinden, wieder wegzubringen, befreit; außerdem aber auch von dem weitern, was damit zusammenhängt, von den formellen Kategorien vor allem des Unendlichen, der unendlichen Annäherung, und der weitern hier ebenso leeren Kategorien von kontinuirlicher Größe, [11] und welche man sonst, wie Bestreben, Werden, Gelegenheit einer Veränderung für nöthig erachtet, gereinigt.","kind":"passage","sequence":121,"address":"73.121"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0122","text":"Aber dann würde gefordert zu zeigen, was denn p, außer der, für die Theorie ganz genügenden trocknen Bestimmung, daß es weiter nichts als eine aus der Entwickelung eines Binomiums abgeleitete Funktion ist, noch für eine Bedeutung und Werth, d. i. welchen Zusammenhang und Gebrauch für weiteres mathematisches Bedürfniß habe; hiervon soll die zweite Anmerkung handeln.—Es folgt aber zunächst hier noch die Auseinandersetzung der Verwirrung, welche durch den angeführten, in den Darstellungen so geläufigen Gebrauch der Vorstellung von Annäherung in das Auffassen der eigentlichen, qualitativen Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses, um das es zunächst zu thun war, gebracht worden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":122,"address":"73.122"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0123","text":"[11] Die Kategorie von der kontinuirlichen oder fließenden Größe stellt sich mit der Betrachtung der äußerlichen und empirischen Veränderung der Größen, die durch eine Gleichung in die Beziehung, daß die Eine eine Funktion der Andern ist, gebracht sind, ein; da aber der wissenschaftliche Gegenstand der Differentialrechnung ein gewisses (durch den Differential-Koefficienten gewöhnlich ausgedrücktes) Verhältniß, welche Bestimmtheit ebensowohl Gesetz genannt werden kann, ist, so ist für diese specifische Bestimmtheit die bloße Kontinuität Theils schon eine fremdartige Seite, Theils aber auf allen Fall die abstrakte und hier leere Kategorie, da über das Gesetz der Kontinuität gar nichts damit ausgedrückt ist.—Auf welche formelle Definitionen dabei vollends verfallen wird, ist aus meines verehrten Hrn. Collegen, Prof.","kind":"passage","sequence":123,"address":"73.123"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0124","text":"Dirksen, scharfsinniger allgemeinen Darstellung der Grundbestimmungen, die für die Deduktion des Differential-Kalkuls gebraucht werden, welche sich an die Kritik einiger neueren Werke über diese Wissenschaft anschließt und sich in den Jahrb. f. wissensch. Kritik, 1827 Nr. 153 ff., befindet, zu ersehen, es wird daselbst S. 1251 sogar die Definition angeführt: \"Eine stätige oder kontinuirliche Größe, Kontinuum, ist jede Größe, welche man sich im Zustande des Werdens gedenkt, so daß dieses Werden nicht sprungweise, sondern durch ununterbrochenen Fortgang geschieht.\" Das ist doch wohl tautologisch dasselbe, was das definitum ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":124,"address":"73.124"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0125","text":"Es ist gezeigt worden, daß die sogenannten unendlichen Differenzen das Verschwinden der Seiten des Verhältnisses als Quantorum ausdrücken, und daß das, was übrig bleibt, ihr Quantitätsverhältniß ist, rein insofern es auf qualitative Weise bestimmt ist; das qualitative Verhältniß geht hierin so wenig verloren, daß es vielmehr dasjenige ist, was eben durch die Verwandlung endlicher Größen in unendliche resultirt. Hierin besteht, wie wir gesehen, die ganze Natur der Sache.—So verschwinden im letzten Verhältnisse z.B. die Quanta der Abscisse und Ordinate; aber die Seiten dieses Verhältnisses bleiben wesentlich die eine, Element der Ordinate, die andere Element der Abscisse.","kind":"passage","sequence":125,"address":"73.125"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0126","text":"Indem die Vorstellungsweise gebraucht wird, daß man die eine Ordinate sich der anderen unendlich nähern läßt, so geht die vorher unterschiedene Ordinate in die andere Ordinate, und die vorher unterschiedene Abscisse in die andere Abscisse über; aber wesentlich geht nicht die Ordinate in die Abscisse, oder die Abscisse in die Ordinate über. Das Element der Ordinate,—um bei diesem Beispiele von veränderlichen Größen stehen zu bleiben, ist nicht als der Unterschied einer Ordinate von einer anderen Ordinate zu nehmen, sondern ist vielmehr als der Unterschied oder die qualitative Größenbestimmung gegen das Element der Abscisse; das Princip der einen veränderlichen Größe gegen das der andern steht im Verhältnisse miteinander.","kind":"passage","sequence":126,"address":"73.126"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0127","text":"Der Unterschied, indem er nicht mehr Unterschied endlicher Größen ist, hat aufgehört, ein Vielfaches innerhalb seiner selbst zu seyn; er ist in die einfache Intensität zusammengesunken, in die Bestimmtheit eines qualitativen Verhältnißmoments gegen das andere.","kind":"passage","sequence":127,"address":"73.127"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0128","text":"Diese Beschaffenheit der Sache wird aber dadurch verdunkelt, daß das, was so eben Element z.B. der Ordinate genannt worden, so als Differenz oder Inkrement gefaßt wird, daß es nur der Unterschied des Quantums einer Ordinate zwischen dem Quantum einer andern Ordinate sey. Die Grenze hat hiermit hier nicht den Sinn des Verhältnisses; sie gilt nur als der letzte Werth, dem sich eine andere Größe von gleicher Art beständig so nähere, daß sie von ihm, so wenig als man will, unterschieden seyn könne, und daß das letzte Verhältniß, ein Verhältniß der Gleichheit sey. So ist die unendliche Differenz das Schweben eines Unterschieds eines Quantums von einem Quantum, und die qualitative Natur, nach welcher dx wesentlich nicht eine Verhältnißbestimmung gegen x, sondern gegen dy ist, tritt in der Vorstellung zurück.","kind":"passage","sequence":128,"address":"73.128"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0129","text":"Man läßt dx[hoch 2] gegen dx verschwinden, aber noch vielmehr verschwindet dx gegen x, dieß heißt aber wahrhaftig: es hat nur ein Verhältniß zu dy.—Es ist den Geometern in solchen Darstellungen immer vorzüglich darum zu thun, die Annäherung einer Größe an ihre Grenze begreiflich zu machen, und sich an diese Seite des Unterschiedes des Quantums vom Quantum, wie er kein Unterschied und doch noch ein Unterschied ist, zu halten. Aber die Annäherung ist ohnehin für sich eine nichts sagende und nichts begreiflich machende Kategorie; dx hat die Annäherung bereits im Rücken, es ist nicht nahe noch ein Näheres; und unendlich nahe heißt selbst die Negation des Naheseyns und des Annäherns.","kind":"passage","sequence":129,"address":"73.129"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0130","text":"Indem es nun damit geschehen ist, daß die Inkremente oder unendlichen Differenzen nur nach der Seite des Quantums, das in ihnen verschwindet, und nur als Grenze desselben betrachtet worden sind, so sind sie so als verhältnißlose Momente gefaßt. Es würde die unstatthafte Vorstellung daraus folgen, daß es erlaubt sey, in dem letzten Verhältnisse etwa Abscisse und Ordinate, oder auch Sinus, Cosinus, Tangente, Sinus versus und was alles noch, einander gleich zu setzen.—Diese Vorstellung scheint zunächst darin obzuwalten, wenn ein Bogen als eine Tangente behandelt wird; denn auch der Bogen ist wohl inkommensurabel mft der geraden Linie, und sein Element zunächst von anderer Qualität als das Element der geraden Linie. Es scheint noch widersinniger und unerlaubter, als die Verwechslung der Abscisse, Ordinate, des Sinus versus, Cosinus u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":130,"address":"73.130"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0131","text":"wenn quadrata rotundis, wenn ein ob zwar unendlich kleiner Theil des Bogens, für ein Stück der Tangente, genommen, und somit als gerade Linie behandelt wird. —Allein diese Behandlung ist von der gerügten Verwechslung wesentlich zu unterscheiden; sie hat ihre Rechtfertigung darin, daß in dem Dreieck, weilches das Element eines Bogens und die Elemente seiner Abscisse und der Ordinate zu seinen Seiten hat, das Verhältniß dasselbe ist, als wenn jenes Element des Bogens das Element einer geraden Linie, der Tangente wäre; die Winkel, welche das wesentliche Verhältniß konstituiren, d. i. dasjenige, das diesen Elementen bleibt, indem von den ihnen zugehörigen endlichen Größen abstrahirt wird, sind die nämlichen.—Man kann sich hierüber auch ausdrücken, gerade Linien, als unendlichklein, seyen in krumme Linien übergegangen, und das Verhältniß ihrer in ihrer Unendlichkeit sey ein Kurvenverhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":131,"address":"73.131"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0132","text":"Da nach ihrer Definition die gerade Linie der kürzeste Weg zwischen zwei Punkten ist, so gründet sich ihr Unterschied von krummer Linie auf die Bestimmung von Menge, auf die geringere Menge des Unterscheidbaren auf diesem Wege, was also eine Bestimmung von Quantum Ist. Aber diese Bestimmung verschwindet in ihr, sie als intensive Größe, als unendliches Moment, als Element genommen; somit auch ihr Unterschied von der krummen Linie, der bloß auf dem Quantumsunterschiede beruhte.—Also als unendlich behält gerade Linie und Bogen kein quantitatives Verhältniß und damit, auf den Grund der angenommenen Definition, auch keine qualitative Verschiedenheit mehr gegeneinander, sondern geht jene vielmehr in diese über.","kind":"passage","sequence":132,"address":"73.132"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0133","text":"Verwandt, jedoch zugleich verschieden, von der Gleichsetzung heterogener Bestimmungen ist die für sich unbestimmte und völlig gleichgültige Annahme, daß unendlich kleine Theile desselben Ganzen einander gleich seyen; jedoch angewandt auf einen in sich heterogenen d. i. mit wesentlicher Ungleichförmigkeit der Größebestimmung behafteten Gegenstand, bringt sie die eigenthüniliche Verkehrung hervor, die in dem Satze der höhern Mechanik enthalten ist, daß in gleichen und zwar unendlichkleinen Zeiten unendlichkleine Theile einer Kurve in gleichförmiger Bewegung durchloffen werden, indem dieß von einer Bewegung behauptet wird, in der in gleichen endlichen d. i. existirenden Zeittheilen endliche, d. i. existirende ungleiche Theile der Kurve durchloffen werden, d. i. also von einer Bewegung, die als existirend ungleichförmig ist und so angenommen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":133,"address":"73.133"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0134","text":"Dieser Satz ist der Ausdruck desjenigen in Worten, was ein analytisches Glied, das sich in der oben auch angeführten Entwickelung der Formel von ungleichförmiger übrigens einem Gesetze gemäßen Bewegung ergiebt, bedeuten soll. Ältere Mathematiker suchten Ergebnisse der neu erfundenen Infinitesimal-Rechnung, die ohnehin immer mit konkreten Gegenständen zu thun hatte, in Worte und Sätze auszudrücken und sie in geometrischen Verzeichnungen darzustellen, wesentlich um sie für die Lehrsätze nach gewöhnlicher Beweise-Art zu gebrauchen. Die Glieder einer mathematischen Formel, in welche die analytische Behandlung die Größe des Gegenstands z.B. der Bewegung zerlegte, erhielten dort eine gegenständliche Bedeutung, z.B. der Geschwindigkeit, beschleunigende Kraft u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":134,"address":"73.134"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0135","text":"sie sollten nach solcher Bedeutung richtige Sätze, physikalische Gesetze geben und nach der analytischen Verbindung auch ihre objektiven Verknüpfungen und Verhältnisse bestimmt seyn, wie z.B. eben daß in einer gleichförmig beschleunigten Bewegung eine besondere den Zeiten proportionale Geschwindigkeit existire, außerdem aber ein Zuwachs von der Kraft der Schwere her, immer hinzukomme. Solche Sätze werden in der modernen, analytischen Gestalt der Mechanik durchaus als Ergebnisse des Kalkuls aufgeführt unbekümmert darum, ob sie einen reellen Sinn d. i. dem eine Existenz entspräche, für sich an ihnen selbst hätten, und um einen Beweis eines solchen; die Schwierigkeit, den Zusammenhang solcher Bestimmungen, wenn sie im ausgesprochenen reellen Sinn genommen werden, z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":135,"address":"73.135"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0136","text":"den Übergang von jener schlechtgleichförmigen Geschwindigkeit zu einer gleichförmigen beschleunigten, begreifflich zu machen, gilt dafür, durch die analytische Behandlung ganz beseitigt zu seyn, als in welcher solcher Zusammenhang einfache Folge der nunmehrigen festen Autorität der Operationen des Kalkuls ist. Es wird für einen Triumph der Wissenschaft ausgegeben, durch den bloßen Kalkul über die Erfahrung hinaus Gesetze, d. i. Sätze der Existenz, die keine Existenz haben, zu finden.","kind":"passage","sequence":136,"address":"73.136"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0137","text":"Aber in der erstern noch naiven Zeit des Infinitesimal-Kalkuls sollte von jenen Bestimmungen und Sätzen, in geometrischen Verzeichnungen vorgestellt, ein reeller Sinn für sich angegeben und plausibel gemacht, und sie in solchem Sinne zum Beweise von den Hauptsätzen, um die es zu thun war, angewendet werden, (—man sehe den newtonischen Beweis von seinem Fundamentalsatze der Theorie der Gravitation in den Princ. mathem. philosophiae naturalis lib. I. Sect. II. Prop. I. verglichen mit Schuberts Astronomie (erster Ausg. III. B. §. 20), wo zugestanden wird, daß es sich nicht genau so, d. i. in dem Punkte, welcher der Nerv des Beweises ist, sich nicht so verhalte, wie Newton annimmt—).","kind":"passage","sequence":137,"address":"73.137"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0138","text":"Es wird nicht geläugnet werden können, daß man sich in diesem Felde vieles als Beweis, vornehmlich unter der Beihülfe des Nebels des Unendlich-Kleinen hat gefallen lassen, aus keinem andern Grunde als dem, daß das, was herauskam, immer schon vorher bekannt war, und der Beweis, der so eingerichtet wurde, daß es herauskam, wenigstens den Schein eines Gerüstes von Beweis zu Stande brachte;—einen Schein, den man dem bloßen Glauben oder dem Wissen aus Erfahrung immer noch vorzog. Ich aber trage kein Bedenken, diese Manier für nicht mehr als eine bloße Taschenspielerei und Charlatanerie des Beweisens anzusehen, und hierunter selbst newtonische Beweise zu rechnen, ins Besondere die zu dem so eben angeführten gehörigen, wegen welcher man Newton bis an den Himmel und über Keppler erhoben hat, das was dieser bloß durch Erfahrung gefunden, mathematisch dargethan zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":138,"address":"73.138"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0139","text":"Das leere Gerüste solcher Beweise wurde errichtet, um physische Gesetze zu beweisen. Aber die Mathematik vermag überhaupt nicht Größenbestimmungen der Physik zu beweisen, insofern sie Gesetze sind, welche die qualitative Natur der Momente zum Grunde haben; aus dem einfachen Grunde, weil diese Wissenschaft nicht Philosophie ist, nicht vom Begriffe ausgeht, und das Qualitative daher, insofern es nicht lemmatischerweise aus der Erfahrung aufgenommen wird, außer ihrer Sphäre liegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":139,"address":"73.139"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0140","text":"Die Behauptung der Ehre der Mathematik, daß alle in ihr vorkommenden Sätze streng bewiesen seyn sollen, ließ sie ihre Grenze oft vergessen; so schien es gegen ihre Ehre, für Erfahrungssätze einfach die Erfahrung als Quelle und als einzigen Beweis anzuerkennen; später ist das Bewußtseyn hierüber gebildeter geworden; eh dieses aber über den Unterschied sich nicht klar wird, was mathematisch beweisbar ist und was nur anderwärts genommen werden kann, wie darüber was nur Glieder analytischer Entwickelung und was physikalische Existenzen sind, kann die Wissenschaftlichkeit sich nicht zu strenger und reiner Haltung herausbilden.—Jenem Gerüste newtonischen Beweisens aber wird ohne Zweifel noch dasselbe Recht widerfahren, das einem anderen grundlosen newtonischen Kunstgebäude aus optischen Experimenten und damit verbundenem Schließen angethan worden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":140,"address":"73.140"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0141","text":"Die angewandte Mathematik ist noch voll von einem gleichen Gebräue aus Erfahrung und Reflexion, aber wie vonjener Optik seit geraumer Zeit bereits ein Theil nach dem andern anfing in der Wissenschaft faktisch ignorirt zu werden mit der Inkonsequenz jedoch, das Übrige obgleich damit Widersprechende noch gewähren zu lassen, —so ist es auch Faktum, daß bereits ein Theil jener trügerischen Beweise, von selbst in Vergessenheit gerathen oder durch andere ersetzt worden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":141,"address":"73.141"}],"sha256":"d0ee2304def2755a367b665c972c74f8be017d33cbab5e43c057da6ce83a1d55","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103542714780Z_57358c3f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1. The Conceptual Determinacy of the Mathematical Infinite.","source_sha256":"d0ee2304def2755a367b665c972c74f8be017d33cbab5e43c057da6ce83a1d55","sha256":"75d15201d1a25a51ee551bdce68f04b33535f3a35c037eb5bc5ef777e76da867","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:35:42.714820+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0001","text":"The mathematical infinite is, on the one hand, interesting because of the extension of mathematics and the great results which its introduction into it has produced; on the other hand, however, it is remarkable because this science has not yet succeeded in justifying itself concerning its use by means of the concept (concept taken in the proper sense). The justifications rest, in the end, on the correctness of the results arising with the aid of that determination, which is proved on other grounds; but not on the clarity of the object and of the operation by which the results are brought forth, indeed such that the operation itself is rather admitted to be incorrect.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"73.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0002","text":"This is already a defect in and for itself; such a procedure is unscientific. But it also brings with it the disadvantage that mathematics, because it does not know the nature of this its instrument, since it has not finished with its metaphysics and critique, has been unable to determine the scope of its application and to secure itself against its misuse.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"73.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0003","text":"From the philosophical point of view, however, the mathematical infinite is important because the concept of the true infinite in fact underlies it, and it stands much higher than the ordinarily so-called metaphysical infinite, from which objections are made against the former. Against these objections, the science of mathematics frequently knows how to save itself only by rejecting the competence of metaphysics, asserting that it has nothing to do with this science and need not concern itself with its concepts, provided only that it proceeds consistently on its own ground. It has not to consider what is true in itself, but what is true in its field.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"73.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0004","text":"Metaphysics does not know how to deny or overthrow the brilliant results of the use of the mathematical infinite in its contradiction of it, and mathematics does not know how to come to terms with metaphysics concerning its own concept and hence also concerning the derivation of the modes of procedure which the use of the infinite makes necessary.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"73.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0005","text":"If the sole difficulty by which mathematics were oppressed were that of the concept in general, it could without further ado leave this aside, namely insofar as the concept is more than merely the statement of the essential determinations, i.e. the determinations of understanding, of a thing; and it has not lacked precision in these determinations, for it is not a science that has to do with the concepts of its objects and has to generate its content through the development of the concept, even if only through ratiocination. But in the method of its infinite it finds the chief contradiction in the peculiar method itself upon which it rests in general as a science.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"73.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0006","text":"For the calculation of the infinite permits and requires modes of procedure which mathematics must absolutely reject in operations with finite magnitudes, and at the same time it treats its infinite magnitudes as finite quanta and wishes to apply to the former the same modes of procedure which hold for the latter; it is a principal aspect of the development of this science to have obtained for transcendental determinations and their treatment the form of ordinary calculus.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"73.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0007","text":"In this conflict of its operations, mathematics shows that results which it finds in this way wholly agree with those found by the properly mathematical, geometrical and analytical, method. But, in part, this does not concern all results, and the purpose of introducing the infinite is not solely to abbreviate the ordinary path, but to arrive at results which cannot be achieved by it. In part, success does not by itself justify the manner of the path. But this manner of calculation of the infinite appears burdened by the semblance of inexactness which it gives itself, in that it at one time increases finite magnitudes by an infinitely small magnitude, retains this in part in the further operation, but also neglects a part of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"73.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0008","text":"This procedure contains the peculiarity that, notwithstanding the admitted inexactness, a result emerges which is not merely approximate and so close that the difference could be disregarded, but perfectly exact. Yet in the operation itself which precedes the result, one cannot dispense with the representation that something is not equal to zero, but is so insignificant as to be capable of being disregarded. But in what is to be understood by mathematical determinacy, every distinction of greater or lesser exactness falls away entirely, just as in philosophy there can be no question of greater or lesser probability, but of truth alone.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"73.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0009","text":"If the method and use of the infinite are justified by success, it is nevertheless not as superfluous to demand their justification as it seems superfluous, in the case of the nose, to ask for proof of the right to use it. For in mathematical cognition as scientific cognition, proof is essential, and even with regard to results it is the case that the strict mathematical method does not furnish for all of them the confirmation of success, which in any case is only an external confirmation.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"73.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0010","text":"It is worth the trouble to consider more closely the mathematical concept of the infinite and the most remarkable attempts which have the intention of justifying its use and removing the difficulty by which the method feels itself oppressed. The consideration of these justifications and determinations of the mathematical infinite, which I shall undertake more extensively in this note, will at the same time cast the best light upon the nature of the true concept itself, and show how it has hovered before them and lain at their foundation.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"73.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0011","text":"The usual determination of the mathematical infinite is that it is a magnitude beyond which—when it is the infinitely great—there is no greater, or—when it is determined as the infinitely small—no smaller, or which, in the former case, is greater, in the latter smaller, than every arbitrary magnitude.—In this definition, to be sure, the true concept is not expressed; rather, as already remarked, only the same contradiction which is in infinite progress. But let us see what it contains in itself. A magnitude is defined in mathematics as something that can be increased and diminished; hence, generally, as an indifferent limit. Now insofar as the infinitely great or small is such that it can no longer be increased or diminished, it is in fact no longer a quantum as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"73.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0012","text":"This consequence is necessary and immediate. But the reflection that the quantum—and in this note I call quantum in general, as it is, the finite quantum—is sublated, is one which is not usually made and which constitutes the difficulty for ordinary understanding, in that the quantum, insofar as it is infinite, is required to be thought as a sublated quantum, as one which is not a quantum and whose quantitative determinacy nevertheless remains.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"73.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0013","text":"To cite how Kant assesses that determination, [9] he finds it not in agreement with what is understood by an infinite whole. “According to the ordinary concept, a magnitude is infinite beyond which no greater (i.e. beyond the multitude of a given unit contained in it) is possible; but no multitude is the greatest, since one or more units can always be added.—By an infinite whole, on the other hand, there is not represented how great it is; thus its concept is not the concept of a maximum (or minimum), but by it only its relation to an arbitrarily assumed unit is thought, in respect of which it is greater than every number.”","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"73.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0014","text":"According as this unit were assumed greater or smaller, the infinite would be greater or smaller; but infinity, since it consists solely in the relation to this given unit, would always remain the same, although, to be sure, the absolute magnitude of the whole would thereby not be cognized at all.”","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"73.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0015","text":"[9] In the note to the thesis of the first cosmological antinomy, in the Critique of Pure Reason.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"73.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0016","text":"Kant censures it when infinite wholes are regarded as a maximum, as a completed multitude of a given unit. The maximum or minimum as such still appears as a quantum, a multitude. Such a representation cannot reject the consequence adduced by Kant, which leads to a greater or lesser infinite. Generally, insofar as the infinite is represented as quantum, the distinction of greater and lesser still holds for it. But this critique does not strike the concept of the true mathematical infinite, the infinite difference, for this is no longer a finite quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"73.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0017","text":"Kant’s concept of infinity, by contrast, which he calls the true transcendental one, is “that the successive synthesis of unity in the measuring-through of a quantum can never be completed.” A quantum in general is presupposed as given; this is supposed to be made into a number, a quantum to be determinately specified, by the synthesis of unity, but this synthesis is never supposed to be able to be completed. Here, as is evident, nothing but progress into infinity is expressed, only represented transcendentally, i.e. properly subjectively and psychologically. In itself, to be sure, the quantum is supposed to be complete; but in a transcendental manner, namely in the subject, which gives it a relation to a unity, there arises only such a determination of the quantum as is uncompleted and absolutely burdened with a beyond.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"73.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0018","text":"Thus here one remains in general with the contradiction which magnitude contains, but distributes it between the object and the subject, so that limitation belongs to the former, but the going beyond every determinacy apprehended by it, into the bad infinite, belongs to the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"73.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0019","text":"It has been stated above, on the contrary, that the determination of the mathematical infinite, namely as it is used in higher analysis, corresponds to the concept of the true infinite; the comparison of the two determinations is now to be undertaken in detailed development.—As concerns first the true infinite quantum, it determined itself as infinite in itself; this is so because, as has emerged, the finite quantum or quantum in general, and its beyond, the bad infinite, are sublated in like manner. The sublated quantum has thereby returned into simplicity and into relation to itself, but not merely as the extensive quantum did when it passed over into intensive quantum, which has its determinacy only in itself in an external multiplicity, toward which it is nevertheless supposed to be indifferent and from which it is supposed to be distinct.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"73.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0020","text":"The infinite quantum rather contains, first, externality and, second, the negation of it within itself; thus it is no longer some finite quantum, not a determination of magnitude which would have an existence as quantum, but it is simple, and therefore only as a moment; it is a determination of magnitude in qualitative form; its infinity is to be as a qualitative determinacy.—As a moment in this way, it is in essential unity with its other, determined only by this its other, i.e. it has significance only in relation to something standing in a relation with it. Outside this relation it is zero;—for quantum as such is precisely supposed to be indifferent to relation, and yet in it to be an immediate, resting determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"73.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0021","text":"In the relation, as merely a moment, it is not something indifferent-for-itself; it is, in infinity as being-for-self, since it is at the same time a quantitative determinacy, only as a being-for-one.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"73.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0022","text":"The concept of the infinite, as it has here been expounded abstractly, will show itself to underlie the mathematical infinite, and will itself become clearer as we consider the different stages of the expression of quantum as a moment of relation, beginning with the lowest, where it is at the same time still quantum as such, up to the higher stage, where it acquires the significance and expression of properly infinite magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"73.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0023","text":"Let us therefore first take quantum in relation, as it is a fractional number. Such a fraction as 2/7, for example, is not a quantum such as 1, 2, 3, etc.; it is indeed an ordinary finite number, yet not an immediate one, like the whole numbers, but as a fraction it is mediately determined by two other numbers, which are number and unit in relation to each other, whereby the unit too is a determinate number. But if one abstracts from this more specific determination of them in relation to each other and considers them merely according to what happens to them as quanta in the qualitative relation in which they are here, then 2 and 7 are otherwise indifferent quanta; but since here they appear only as moments, one of the other, and thus of a third (the quantum which is called the exponent), they immediately count not as 2 and 7, but only according to their determinacy in relation to each other.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"73.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0024","text":"In their place, therefore, 4 and 14, or 6 and 21, etc., ad infinitum, may just as well be posited. By this means they thus begin to have a qualitative character. If they held good as mere quanta, then 2 and 7 are simply the one only 2, the other only 7; 4, 14, 6, 21, etc. are simply something other than those numbers, and, insofar as they were only immediate quanta, the one could not be put in the place of the other. But insofar as they hold good as such, and not according to the determinacy of being such quanta, their indifferent limit is sublated; they thus have, on this side, the moment of infinity in them, in that they not merely are no longer themselves, but their quantitative determinacy, as a qualitative determinacy existing in itself—namely, according to what they hold good for in the relation—remains.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"73.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0025","text":"Infinitely many others can be put in their place, so that the value of the fraction does not alter through the determinacy which the relation has.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"73.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0026","text":"The presentation which infinity has in a numerical fraction is, however, still imperfect for the reason that the two sides of the fraction, 2 and 7, can be taken out of the relation and are ordinary indifferent quanta; their connection, that of being in relation and moments, is something external and indifferent to them. Likewise, their relation itself is an ordinary quantum, the exponent of the relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"73.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0027","text":"The letters with which operations are performed in general arithmetic, the proximate universality into which numbers are raised, do not have the property of being of a determinate numerical value; they are only universal signs and indeterminate possibilities of every determinate value. The fraction a/b therefore seems to be a more suitable expression of infinity, since a and b, taken out of their relation to one another, remain indeterminate and, even separately, have no particular peculiar value.—But these letters are indeed posited as indeterminate magnitudes; yet their sense is that they are some finite quantum. Since, therefore, they are indeed the universal representation, but only of determinate number, it is likewise indifferent to them to be in relation, and outside it they retain this value.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"73.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0028","text":"If we consider more closely what is present in the relation, it has the two determinations in it: first, that of being a quantum; but this is, secondly, not an immediate quantum, but one which has the qualitative opposition in it; it at the same time remains in it that determinate, indifferent quantum by returning into itself out of its otherness, the opposition, and is thus also an infinite. These two determinations present themselves, developed in their distinction from one another, in the following familiar form.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"73.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0029","text":"The fraction 2/7 can be expressed as 0.285714… as 1 + a + a[superscript 2] + a[superscript 3], etc. Thus it is an infinite series; the fraction itself is called its sum or its finite expression. If we compare the two expressions, the one, the infinite series, no longer presents it as a relation, but according to the side that it is a quantum as a multitude of such quanta which are added to one another, as a number.—That the magnitudes which are to constitute it as number in turn consist of decimal fractions, hence themselves of relations, is of no consequence here; for this circumstance concerns the particular kind of unit of these magnitudes, not them insofar as they constitute the number; just as a whole number of the decimal system consisting of several digits essentially holds good as a number, and no attention is paid to the fact that it consists of products of a number and the number ten","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"73.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0030","text":"and its powers. Just as it is likewise of no consequence here that there are fractions other than the 2/7 taken, for example, which, when made into decimal fractions, do not yield an infinite series; yet every one can be expressed for a numerical system of a unit other than such a one.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"73.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0031","text":"Now, since in the infinite series, which is supposed to present the fraction as a number, the side that it is a relation disappears, the side according to which it had infinity in it, as was shown above, also disappears. But this has entered in another way; namely, the series is itself infinite.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"73.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0032","text":"Of what kind the infinity of the series is becomes evident of itself; it is the bad infinity of progress. The series contains and presents the contradiction of presenting something which is a relation and has qualitative nature in it as relationless, as a mere quantum, as a number. The consequence of this is that something is always lacking from the number expressed in the series, so that one must always go beyond what is posited in order to attain the required determinacy. The law of progression is known; it lies in the determination of quantum that is contained in the fraction, and in the nature of the form in which it is to be expressed.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"73.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0033","text":"The number can indeed be made as exact as one needs by continuing the series; but the presentation through it always remains only an ought; it is afflicted with a beyond which cannot be sublated, because expressing as number something that rests on qualitative determinacy is the enduring contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"73.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0034","text":"In this infinite series, that inexactness is actually present of which only the semblance occurs in the true mathematical infinite. These two kinds of mathematical infinite are as little to be confused as the two kinds of philosophical infinite. In the presentation of the true mathematical infinite, the form of the series was at first employed, or has also recently been brought forward again. But it is not necessary for it; on the contrary, the infinite of the infinite series is essentially distinguished from that one, as the sequel is to show. Indeed, this latter even stands opposed to the expression of the fraction.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"73.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0035","text":"The infinite series, namely, contains bad infinity because what the series is to express remains an ought; and what it expresses is afflicted with a beyond that does not vanish and is distinct from what is to be expressed. It is infinite not on account of the terms which are posited, but because they are incomplete, because the other which essentially belongs to them is beyond them; what is there in it, however many of the posited terms there may be, is only a finite, in the proper sense, posited as finite, i.e. as such as is not what it ought to be.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"73.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0036","text":"By contrast, what is called the finite expression, or the sum of such a series, is without defect; it completely contains the value that the series merely seeks; the beyond has been recalled from flight; what it is and what it ought to be are not separate, but are the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"73.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0037","text":"What distinguishes the two lies more immediately in this, that in the infinite series the negative is outside its terms, which have presence insofar as they count only as parts of the number. In the finite expression, on the other hand, which is a relation, the negative is immanent, as the determinateness of the sides of the relation through one another, which is a return-into-itself, self-relating unity, as negation of negation (the two sides of the relation are only moments), and thereby has the determination of infinity in itself.—In fact, then, the usually so-called sum, 2/7 or 1/1-a', is a relation; and this so-called finite expression is the truly infinite expression.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"73.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0038","text":"The infinite series, on the contrary, is in truth sum; its purpose is to present what is in itself relation in the form of a sum, and the existing terms of the series are not terms of a relation, but of an aggregate. Further, it is rather the finite expression; for it is the incomplete aggregate, and remains essentially something defective. According to what is there in it, it is a determinate quantum, but at the same time one less than it ought to be; likewise, what it lacks is a determinate quantum; this missing part is in fact what is called the infinite in the series, according to the merely formal side, that it is something lacking, a non-being; according to its content it is a finite quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"73.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0039","text":"What is there in the series, together with what it lacks, first makes up what the fraction is, the determinate quantum which it likewise ought to be, but is incapable of being. —The word ‘infinite,’ even in the infinite series, is accustomed in opinion to be something lofty and sublime; this is a kind of superstition, the superstition of the understanding; it has been seen how it is rather reduced to the determination of defectiveness.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"73.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0040","text":"That there are, it may further be noted, infinite series which are not summable is, with respect to the form of series in general, an external and contingent circumstance. They contain a higher kind of infinity than the summable ones; namely, an incommensurability, or the impossibility of presenting the quantitative relation contained therein as a quantum, even as a fraction; but the form of series as such, which they have, contains the same determination of bad infinity as is in the summable series.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"73.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0041","text":"The reversal just noted in the case of the fraction and its series with regard to the expression also takes place insofar as the mathematical infinite is not, namely, that just mentioned but the true, the relative infinite,—whereas the ordinary metaphysical infinite, by which the abstract, bad infinite is understood, has been called the absolute. In fact, however, this metaphysical infinite is rather only the relative, because the negation which it expresses is only such in opposition to a limit that this limit remains subsistent outside it and is not sublated by it; the mathematical infinite, on the other hand, has truly sublated the finite limit in itself, because the beyond of the latter is united with it.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"73.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0042","text":"It is chiefly in the sense in which it has been shown that the so-called sum, or finite expression, of an infinite series is rather to be regarded as the infinite expression, that Spinoza sets up the concept of true infinity against that of the bad and elucidates it by examples. His concept gains the nearest illumination if I connect what he says concerning it with this development.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"73.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0043","text":"He first defines the infinite as the absolute affirmation of the existence of some nature, the finite, on the contrary, as determinateness, as negation. The absolute affirmation of an existence is namely to be taken as its relation to itself, as being not through the fact that an other is; the finite, on the other hand, is negation, a ceasing as relation to an other that begins outside it. The absolute affirmation of an existence does not indeed exhaust the concept of infinity; this contains that infinity is affirmation, not as immediate, but only as restored through the reflection of the other into itself, or as negation of the negative. But in Spinoza substance and its absolute unity have the form of unmoved, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"73.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0044","text":"of unity not mediating itself with itself, of a rigidity in which the concept of the negative unity of the self, subjectivity, is not yet to be found.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"73.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0045","text":"The mathematical example by which he elucidates true infinity (Epist. XXIX.) is a space between two unequal circles, one of which falls within the other without touching it, and which are not concentric.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"73.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0046","text":"He seems to have made much of this figure and of the concept for which he used it as an example, so much so that he made it the motto of his Ethics.—“Mathematicians,” he says, “conclude that the inequalities possible in such a space are infinite, not from the infinite multitude of the parts, for its magnitude is determinate and bounded, and I can posit greater and smaller such spaces, but because the nature of the thing surpasses every determinacy.”—One sees that Spinoza rejects that representation of the infinite according to which it is represented as a multitude or as a series which is not completed, and recalls that here, in the space of the example, the infinite is not beyond but present and complete; this space is something bounded, but for that reason an infinite, “because the nature of the thing surpasses every determinacy,” because the determination of magnitude contained therein is at the same time not representable as a quantum, or, according to the Kantian expression given above, synthesis cannot be completed into a—discrete—quantum.—How in general the opposition of continuous and discrete quantum leads to infinity is to be set forth in a later remark.—Spinoza calls that infinite of a series the infinite of imagination; but the infinite as relation to itself, the infinite of thought or infinitum actu. It is namely actu, it is actually infinite, because it is complete and present in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"73.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0047","text":"determination of magnitude contained therein is at the same time not representable as a quantum, or, according to the Kantian expression given above, synthesis cannot be completed into a—discrete—quantum.—How in general the opposition of continuous and discrete quantum leads to infinity is to be set forth in a later remark.—That infinite of a series Spinoza calls the infinite of imagination; but the infinite as relation to itself, the infinite of thought or infinitum actu. It is namely actu, it is actually infinite, because it is complete and present in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"73.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0048","text":"Thus the series, 0.285714… or 1 + a + a[exponent 2] + a[exponent 3]… is infinity merely of imagination or opinion; for it has no reality, it absolutely lacks something; whereas 2/7 or 1/1-a is the actual, not only what the series is in its present terms, but also in addition that which it lacks, that which it is only supposed to be. 2/7 or 1/1-a is likewise a finite magnitude, like Spinoza’s space enclosed between the two circles and its inequalities; and, like this space, it can be made greater or smaller. But this does not result in the absurdity of a greater or lesser infinity; for this quantum of the whole does not affect the relation of its moments, the nature of the matter, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"73.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0049","text":"the qualitative determination of magnitude; that which is present in the infinite series is likewise a finite quantum, but besides this also something defective.—Imagination, on the other hand, remains with quantum as such, and does not reflect upon the qualitative relation which constitutes the ground of the existing incommensurability.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"73.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0050","text":"The incommensurability which lies in Spinoza’s example generally includes the functions of curved lines, and leads more closely to the infinity which mathematics has introduced in such functions, indeed in functions of variable magnitudes generally, and which is the true mathematical, quantitative infinity, which Spinoza too had in mind. This determination is now to be discussed more closely here.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"73.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0051","text":"As regards first of all the category of variability, held to be so important, under which the magnitudes related in those functions are subsumed, they are initially supposed to be variable not in the sense in which, in the fraction 2/7, the two numbers 2 and 7 are variable, inasmuch as 4 and 14, 6 and 21, and so forth to infinity, other numbers can equally well be substituted for them without altering the value posited in the fraction. Still more, in a/b any arbitrary number can be substituted for a and b without altering what a/b is supposed to express. Only in the sense that an infinite, i.e. inexhaustible, multitude of numbers can also be substituted for x and y in a function are a and b just as variable magnitudes as the latter, x and y.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"73.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0052","text":"The expression “variable magnitudes” is therefore very vague, and unhappily chosen for determinations of magnitude whose interest and mode of treatment lie in something, in something quite other than their mere variability.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"73.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0053","text":"In order to make clear wherein the true determination of the moments of a function lies, with which the interest of higher analysis is concerned, we must go through the stages noted once again. In 2/7 or a/b, 2 and 7 are each, for themselves, determinate quanta, and the relation is not essential to them; a and b are likewise supposed to represent such quanta, which remain what they are even outside the relation. Further, 2/7 and a/b too are a fixed quantum, a quotient; the relation constitutes a number, of which the denominator expresses the unit and the numerator the number of these units—or conversely; even if 4 and 14, etc., take the place of 2 and 7, the relation also remains the same as quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"73.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0054","text":"But this now changes essentially in the function y[exponent 2]/x = p, for example; here x and y indeed have the meaning of being able to be determinate quanta; but it is not x and y, but only x and y[exponent 2], that have a determinate quotient.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"73.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0055","text":"Thereby these sides of the relation, x and y, are, first, not merely not determinate quanta, but, second, their relation is not a fixed quantum (nor is such a one intended here as in the case of a and b), not a fixed quotient; rather, as quantum, it is absolutely variable. But this is contained solely in the fact that x does not have a relation to y, but to the square of y.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"73.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0056","text":"The relation of a magnitude to a power is not a quantum, but essentially a qualitative relation; the relation of powers is the circumstance that is to be regarded as the fundamental determination.—But in the function of the straight line y = a x, x/y = a is an ordinary fraction and quotient; this function is therefore only formally a function of variable magnitudes, or x and y are here what a and b are in a/b; they are not in that determination in which differential and integral calculus considers them.—On account of the special nature of variable magnitudes in this mode of consideration, it would have been expedient to introduce for them both a special name and other designations than the ordinary ones for unknown magnitudes in every finite, determinate, or indeterminate equation; on account of their essential difference from such merely unknown magnitudes, which in themselves are","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"73.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0057","text":"completely determinate quanta, or a determinate range of determinate quanta.—It is also only a lack of consciousness concerning the peculiarity of that which constitutes the interest of higher analysis and has brought about the need for and invention of the differential calculus, that functions of the first degree, such as the equation of the straight line, are included by themselves in the treatment of this calculus; furthermore, formalism of this kind owes something to the misunderstanding which imagines that it fulfils the intrinsically correct demand for the generalization of a method by omitting the specific determinacy upon","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"73.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0058","text":"which the need is grounded, by taking it that in this field the concern is only with variable magnitudes in general. Much formalism in the consideration of these objects as well as in their treatment would have been spared, if it had been seen that it concerns not variable magnitudes as such, but determinations of powers.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"73.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0059","text":"But there is yet a further stage at which mathematical infinity emerges in its peculiarity. In an equation in which x and y are initially posited as determined by a relation of powers, x and y as such are still supposed to signify quanta; this meaning now completely disappears in the so-called infinitely small differences. d x, d y are no longer quanta, nor are they supposed to signify such, but have a meaning solely in their relation, a sense merely as moments. They are no longer something, something taken as quantum, not finite differences; but neither are they nothing, not indeterminate zero. Outside their relation they are pure zeros, but they are to be taken only as moments of the relation, as determinations of the differential coefficient d x/ d y.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"73.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0060","text":"In this concept of infinity, quantum is truly consummated into a qualitative being; it is posited as actually infinite; it is sublated not merely as this or that quantum, but as quantum in general. Yet quantitative determinacy remains as the element of quanta, principle, or, as it has also been said, in its first concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"73.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0061","text":"All the attacks that have been made upon the fundamental determination of the mathematics of this infinity, differential and integral calculus, are directed against this concept. Incorrect conceptions of mathematicians themselves occasioned it when it was not recognized; but above all the incapacity to justify the object as concept is to blame for these challenges. But mathematics, as was recalled above, cannot evade the concept here; for, as mathematics of infinity, it does not limit itself to the finite determinacy of its objects,—as in pure mathematics space and number and their determinations are considered and related to one another only according to their finitude—; rather, it transfers a determination taken up from there and treated by it into identity with its opposite, as, for example,","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"73.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0062","text":"it makes a curved line into a straight one, the circle into a polygon, and so forth. The operations which it permits itself as differential and integral calculus are therefore wholly contrary to the nature of merely finite determinations and their relations, and for that reason would have their justification solely in the concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"73.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0063","text":"When the mathematics of infinity maintained that those determinations of quantity were vanishing magnitudes, i.e. such as are no longer any quantum, but are also not nothing, rather still a determinacy in relation to another, nothing seemed clearer than that there was no such intermediate state, as it was called, between being and nothing.—What is involved in this objection and so-called intermediate state has already been shown above under the category of becoming, Remark 4. To be sure, the unity of being and nothing is not a state; a state would be a determination of being and nothing, into which these moments would have chanced to fall only contingently, as it were into an illness or external affection, through an erroneous thinking; rather, this middle and unity, vanishing, or equally becoming, is alone their truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"73.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0064","text":"It has further been said that what is infinite is not comparable as a greater or lesser; there can therefore be no relation of infinities to infinities, nor orders or degrees of infinity, such as are the differences of infinite differences occurring in the science of them.—Underlying this already mentioned objection is always the notion that the discussion is supposed to concern quanta, which are compared as quanta; that determinations which are no longer quanta no longer have any relation to one another. On the contrary, that which is only in relation is not a quantum; quantum is such a determination as is supposed to have a wholly indifferent being outside its relation, whose difference from another is supposed to be indifferent to it; whereas the qualitative is only that which it is in its difference from another.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"73.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0065","text":"Those infinite magnitudes are therefore not merely comparable, but are only as moments of comparison, of relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"73.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0066","text":"I shall adduce the most important determinations which have been given in mathematics concerning this infinity; from them it will become clear that the thought of the matter, in agreement with the concept developed here, lies at their foundation, but that their authors did not fathom it as concept and, in application, again required makeshifts which contradict their better cause.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"73.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0067","text":"The thought cannot be more correctly determined than Newton has given it. In doing so, I separate off the determinations that belong to the representation of motion and velocity (from which he principally took the name fluxions), because the thought here does not appear in the proper abstraction, but concretely, mixed with inessential forms. Newton explains these fluxions (Princ. mathem. phil. nat. L. 1. Lemma XI. Schol.) as meaning not indivisibles—a form employed by earlier mathematicians, Cavalieri and others, and which contains the concept of a quantum determinate in itself—but vanishing divisibles. Further, not sums and relations of determinate parts, but the limits (limites) of the sums and relations.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"73.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0068","text":"The objection may be raised that vanishing magnitudes have no ultimate relation, because before they have vanished it is not the ultimate, and when they have vanished there is no relation any longer. But by the relation of vanishing magnitudes is to be understood the relation not before they vanish and not afterwards, but with which they vanish (quacum evanescunt). Likewise, the first relation of becoming magnitudes is that with which they become.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"73.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0069","text":"According to the state of scientific method at that time, only what was to be understood under an expression was explained; but that this or that was to be understood under it is properly a subjective demand or also a historical requirement, in which it is not shown that such a concept is necessary in and for itself and has inner truth. Yet what has been adduced shows that the concept set forth by Newton corresponds to the way in which infinite magnitude resulted in the above exposition from the reflection of quantum into itself. Magnitudes are understood in their vanishing, i.e. such as are no longer quanta; further, not relations of determinate parts, but the limits of relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"73.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0070","text":"Thus both the quanta for themselves, the sides of the relation, and with them the relation too, insofar as it would be a quantum, are supposed to vanish; the limit of the relation of magnitudes is that in which it is and is not; more precisely, this means that in which quantum has vanished, and with it the relation is preserved only as a qualitative quantitative relation, and its sides likewise as qualitative quantitative moments.—Newton adds that from the fact that there are ultimate relations of vanishing magnitudes, it is not to be inferred that there are ultimate magnitudes, indivisibles. For this would again be a leap from the abstract relation to such sides of it as were supposed to have a value for themselves outside their relation, as indivisibles, as something that would be a one, devoid of relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"73.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0071","text":"Against that misunderstanding he further recalls that the ultimate relations are not relations of ultimate magnitudes, but limits to which the relations of magnitudes decreasing without limit are nearer than any given, i.e. finite, difference, but which limit they do not overstep, so that they would become nothing.—By ultimate magnitudes, namely, as stated, indivisibles or ones could have been understood. But in the determination of the ultimate relation, both the representation of the indifferent one, devoid of relation, and that of finite quantum are removed.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"73.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0072","text":"But there would have been no need either for the diminution without limit, into which Newton places the Quantum and which merely expresses progress to infinity, or for the determination of divisibility, which here no longer has any immediate significance, if the required determination had developed itself into the concept of a determination of magnitude, which purely is only a moment of relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"73.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0073","text":"With respect to the preservation of the relation in the vanishing of the Quanta, one finds (elsewhere, as in Carnot, Réflexions sur la Métaphysique du Calcul Infinitésimal) the expression that, by virtue of the law of continuity, the vanishing magnitudes still retain the relation from which they come before they vanish. —This conception expresses the true nature of the matter, provided that what is meant is not the continuity of the Quantum which it has in infinite progress, namely, to continue itself into its vanishing in such a way that beyond it there again arises only a finite Quantum, a new member of the series; but a continuous progression is always conceived in such a way that the values traversed are still finite Quanta.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"73.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0074","text":"In the transition, on the other hand, which is made into the true infinite, the relation is the continuous element; it is so thoroughly continuous and self-preserving that the transition rather consists solely in bringing out the relation purely, and in making vanish the determination devoid of relation, i.e. that a Quantum which is a side of the relation, when set outside this relation as well, is still Quantum. —This purification of the quantitative relation is, in this respect, nothing other than what occurs when an empirical existence is comprehended. Thereby it is raised above itself, so that its concept contains the same determinations as it itself does, but in their essentiality and grasped into the unity of the concept, in which they have lost their indifferent, conceptless subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"73.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0075","text":"Equally interesting is the other form of Newton's presentation of the magnitudes in question, namely as generating magnitudes or principles. A generated magnitude (genita) is a product or quotient, roots, rectangles, squares, also sides of rectangles, squares;—in general, a finite magnitude.—“Considering it as variable, as it increases or decreases in continuous motion and flux, he understands by the name of moments its momentary increments or decrements. But these are not to be taken for particles of determinate magnitude (particulae finitae).","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"73.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0076","text":"Such are not themselves moments, but magnitudes produced from moments; rather, the becoming principles or beginnings of finite magnitudes are to be understood.”—Here the Quantum is distinguished from itself, as it is a product or an existent, and as it is in its becoming, in its beginning and principle, that is, as it is in its concept, or, what is the same here, in its qualitative determinacy; in the latter, the quantitative differences, the infinite increments or decrements, are only moments; only what has become is that which has passed over into the indifference of existence and into externality, the Quantum.—But if these determinations of the infinite adduced with regard to increments or decrements must be acknowledged by the philosophy of the true concept, it must at once also be observed that the forms themselves of increments, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"73.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0077","text":"fall within the category of the immediate Quantum and of the continuous progression mentioned, and that the conceptions of increment, accession, increase of x by d x or i, etc., are rather to be regarded as the fundamental evil present in the methods;—as the enduring obstacle to purely bringing out, from the conception of the ordinary Quantum, the determination of the qualitative quantitative moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"73.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0078","text":"As against the determinations indicated, the conception of infinitely small magnitudes, which is also contained in increment or decrement itself, falls far short. According to it, they are supposed to be of such a nature that not only they in comparison with finite magnitudes, but also their higher orders in comparison with the lower, or likewise products of several in comparison with a single one, may be neglected. —In Leibniz, the demand for this neglect, which the preceding inventors of methods relating to this magnitude likewise admit, stands out more conspicuously. It is chiefly this which, together with the gain in convenience, gives this calculus the appearance of inexactitude and express incorrectness in the course of its operations.—Wolff has sought, in his manner of making things popular, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"73.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0079","text":"of corrupting the concept and putting incorrect sensuous conceptions in its place, to make it intelligible. Namely, he compares the neglect of infinite differences of higher orders as against lower ones with the procedure of a geometer who, in measuring the height of a mountain, would have been no less exact if in the meantime the wind had blown a grain of sand away from its summit; or with the neglect of the heights of houses and towers in calculating lunar eclipses (Element. Mathes. univ. Tom. I. El. Analys. math. P. II. C. I. s. Schol.).","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"73.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0080","text":"If the fairness of common sense permits such an inexactitude, all geometers, on the other hand, have rejected this conception. It suggests itself of its own accord that, in the science of mathematics, there is no question whatsoever of such empirical exactness, that mathematical measuring by operations of the calculus or by constructions and proofs of geometry is wholly distinct from land-surveying, from measuring empirical lines, figures, etc. Besides, as stated above, analysts show by comparing the result as obtained by the strictly geometrical route and as obtained by the method of infinite differences, that the one is the same as the other, and that there is absolutely no question of a greater or lesser degree of exactness.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"73.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0081","text":"And it is self-evident that an absolutely exact result cannot arise from a procedure that would be inexact. Yet, on the other side, the procedure itself cannot dispense with that neglect on the ground of insignificance, notwithstanding the protest against the mode of justification adduced. And this is the difficulty around which the efforts of analysts revolve: to make intelligible the absurdity lying therein, and to remove it.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"73.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0082","text":"In this respect, Euler's conception is chiefly to be adduced. Taking Newton's general definition as his basis, he insists that differential calculus considers the relations of the increments of a magnitude, but that the infinite difference as such is to be regarded altogether as zero (Institut. Calc. different. P. I. C. III.).—How this is to be understood lies in what precedes; the infinite difference is zero only as Quantum, not a qualitative zero, but, as zero of the Quantum, rather a pure moment only of relation. It is not a difference by a magnitude; but for this reason it is, on the one hand, generally inappropriate to express those moments, which are called infinitely small magnitudes, also as increments or decrements, and as differences.","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"73.82","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0083","text":"This determination is based on the assumption that something is added to or subtracted from the initially existing finite magnitude, that a subtraction or addition, an arithmetical, external operation takes place. But the transition from the function of the variable magnitude to its differential must be regarded as being of a wholly different nature, namely, as has been expounded, as the reduction of the finite function to the qualitative relation of its quantitative determinations.—On the other hand, the incongruity is evident in itself when it is said that the increments are zeros in themselves, that only their relations are considered; for a zero in general no longer has any determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"73.83","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0084","text":"This conception thus indeed reaches the negative of the Quantum and expressly states it, but does not at the same time grasp this negative in its positive significance, as qualitative quantitative determinations which, if they were torn from the relation and taken as Quanta, would be only zeros.—Lagrange (Théorie des fonct. analyt. Introd.) judges concerning the conception of limits or ultimate relations that, although one can indeed very well conceive the relation of two magnitudes so long as they remain finite, this relation gives the understanding no clear and determinate concept as soon as its terms simultaneously become zero.—In fact, the understanding must go beyond this merely negative aspect, that the terms of the relation are zeros as Quanta, and apprehend them positively, as qualitative moments.—But what Euler (in the place cited §. 84 ff.)","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"73.84","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0085","text":"further adds regarding the determination given, in order to show that two so-called infinitely small magnitudes, which are supposed to be nothing other than zeros, nevertheless have a relation to one another and for that reason signs other than the sign of zero are also in use for them, cannot be considered sufficient.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"73.85","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0086","text":"He seeks to ground this on the distinction between arithmetical and geometrical relation; in the former we look to the difference, in the latter to the quotient; although the former is equal between two zeros, the geometrical relation is nevertheless not equal on that account; if 2:1 = 0:0, then, because of the nature of proportion, since the first term is twice as great as the second, the third term too must be twice as great as the fourth; 0:0 is therefore supposed, according to the proportion, to be taken as the relation of 2:1.—Even according to common arithmetic, n.0 = 0; thus n:1 = 0:0.—But precisely because 2:1 or n:1 is a relation of Quanta, neither a relation nor a designation of 0:0 corresponds to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"73.86","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0087","text":"I refrain from multiplying citations, since those considered have sufficiently shown that the true concept of the infinite does indeed lie in them, but has not been brought out and grasped in its determinacy. When, therefore, one proceeds to the operation itself, it cannot happen that the true conceptual determination asserts itself in it; rather, finite quantitative determinacy returns, and the operation cannot dispense with the conception of a merely relatively small [magnitude]. The calculus makes it necessary to subject the so-called infinite magnitudes to the ordinary arithmetical operations of addition, etc., which are founded on the nature of finite magnitudes, and thus to let them count as finite magnitudes for a moment and to treat them as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"73.87","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0088","text":"The calculus would have to justify itself for drawing them down into this sphere on one occasion and treating them as increments or differences, and, on the other hand, for neglecting them as Quanta after it had just applied to them forms and laws of finite magnitudes.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"73.88","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0089","text":"Concerning the attempts of geometers to remove these difficulties, I shall further adduce what is most essential.","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"73.89","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0090","text":"The older analysts had fewer scruples about this; but the efforts of the more recent ones were directed chiefly toward bringing the calculus of the infinite back to the evidence of the properly geometrical method and attaining in it the rigor of the proofs of the ancients (- Lagrange's expressions—) in mathematics. But since the principle of the analysis of the infinite is of a higher nature than the principle of the mathematics of finite magnitudes, it necessarily had at once of itself to renounce that kind of evidence, just as philosophy cannot lay claim to that clarity which the sciences of the sensuous, e.g. natural history, possess, and just as eating and drinking count as more intelligible occupations than thinking and comprehending. The matter, accordingly, can concern only the effort to attain the rigor of the proofs of the ancients.","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"73.90","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0091","text":"Several have attempted to dispense entirely with the concept of the infinite and, without it, to accomplish what seemed bound up with its use.—Lagrange speaks, for example, of the method invented by Landen, and says of it that it is purely analytical and does not employ infinitely small differences, but first introduces different values of the variable magnitudes and subsequently equates them. He judges, moreover, that the advantages peculiar to differential calculus, simplicity of method and ease of operations, are thereby lost.—This is indeed a procedure that has something corresponding to that from which Descartes's method of tangents proceeds, which is still to be mentioned more closely below.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"73.91","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0092","text":"Thus much may here be observed: it is immediately evident in general that the procedure of assuming different values of the variable magnitudes and subsequently equating them belongs to another sphere of mathematical treatment than the method of differential calculus itself, and that the peculiarity, to be discussed more closely later, of the simple relation to which its actual concrete determination is reduced—namely, that of the derived function to the original—is not brought out.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"73.92","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0093","text":"The older among the moderns, such as Fermat, Barrow, and others, who first made use of the infinitely small in the application which was later developed into differential and integral calculus, and then also Leibniz and those following him, including Euler, have always openly believed themselves entitled to omit products of infinite differences, as likewise their higher powers, solely on the ground that they vanish relatively to the lower order. Upon this alone rests for them the fundamental proposition, namely, the determination of what the differential of a product or of a power is; for the whole theoretical doctrine is reduced to this.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"73.93","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0093"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0094","text":"The rest is partly the mechanism of development, partly, however, application, in which nevertheless, as is further to be considered, the higher, or rather the sole, interest in fact also lies.—With regard to the present matter, only the elementary point is to be mentioned here: that, on the same ground of insignificance, it is assumed as the principal proposition concerning curves that the elements of curves, namely the increments of the abscissa and ordinate, have to one another the ratio of the subtangent and the ordinate; for the purpose of obtaining similar triangles, the arc which makes up the third side of a triangle together with the two increments, of the triangle formerly and rightly called the characteristic triangle, is regarded as a straight line, as part of the tangent, and thereby one of the increments as extending as far as the tangent.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"73.94","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0094"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0095","text":"These assumptions elevate those determinations, on the one hand, above the nature of finite magnitudes; but, on the other hand, a procedure is applied to the moments now called infinite which is valid only of finite magnitudes, and in which nothing may be neglected out of regard for insignificance. The difficulty under which the method labours remains, with such a mode of procedure, in its full force.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"73.95","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0095"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0096","text":"A remarkable procedure of Newton's is to be cited here; (Princ. Math. phil. nat. Lib. II. Lemma II. Propos. VII.)—the invention of an ingenious device to eliminate the arithmetically incorrect omission of the products of infinite differences, or of higher orders thereof, in finding differentials. He finds the differential of the product—from which the differentials of quotients, powers, etc. can then easily be derived—in the following way. The product, when x, y are each taken smaller by half of their infinite difference, becomes x y—xdy/2—ydx/2 + dxdy/4; but when x and y are increased by the same amount, it becomes x y + xdy/2 + ydx/2 + dxdy/4.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"73.96","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0096"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0097","text":"Now if the first is subtracted from this second product, y d x + x d y remains as the excess, and this is said to be the excess of growth through a whole dx and dy, for by this growth the two products differ; it is thus the differential of xy.—One sees that in this procedure the term which constitutes the principal difficulty, the product of the two infinite differences, dxdy, cancels itself. But notwithstanding the Newtonian name, it must be permissible to say that such an operation, though very elementary, is incorrect; it is incorrect that (x + dx/2) (y + dy/2)—(x—dx/2) (y—dy/2) = (x + dx) (y + dy)—xy. It can only have been the need to establish the calculus of fluxions, given its importance, that could have led a Newton to practise upon himself the illusion of such proof.","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"73.97","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0097"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0098","text":"Other forms which Newton employs in deriving the differential are bound to concrete meanings relating to motion, of the elements and their powers.—In the use of the series form, which otherwise distinguishes his method, it lies too near at hand to say that it is always in one's power, by adding further terms, to take the magnitude as exactly as one needs, and that the omitted terms are relatively insignificant, the result in general being only an approximation, for him not to have contented himself here too with this ground, just as, in his method of solving equations of higher degrees by approximation, he omits the higher powers which arise upon the substitution of every found yet inexact value into the given equation, on the crude ground of their smallness; see Lagrange Equations Numériques p. 125.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"73.98","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0098"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0099","text":"The error into which Newton fell in solving a problem by omitting essential higher powers, which gave his opponents the opportunity for a triumph of their method over his, and of which Lagrange, in his recent investigation of it (Théorie des fonct. analyt. 3me P. Ch. IV.), has pointed out the true origin, proves the formalism and uncertainty still present in the use of that instrument. Lagrange shows that Newton fell into the error because he neglected the term of the series which contained the power upon which the particular problem turned.","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"73.99","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0099"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0100","text":"Newton had adhered to that formal, superficial principle of omitting terms on account of their relative smallness.—It is known, namely, that in mechanics a determinate meaning is given to the terms of the series in which the function of a motion is developed, so that the first term, or the first function, relates to the moment of velocity, the second to the accelerating force, and the third to the resistance of forces. Thus the terms of the series are here to be regarded not merely as parts of a sum, but as qualitative moments of a whole of the concept. Thereby the omission of the remaining terms, which belong to the badly infinite series, acquires an entirely different meaning from omission on the ground of their relative smallness.","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"73.100","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0100"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0101","text":"[10] The Newtonian solution contained that error, not because in it terms of the series, merely as parts of a sum, but because the term which contains the qualitative determination at issue was not taken into account.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"73.101","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0101"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0102","text":"[10] In a simple manner, Lagrange sets both considerations side by side in the application of the theory of functions to mechanics, in the chapter on rectilinear motion (Théorie des fonct. 3me P. Ch. I. art. 4.). The space traversed, considered as a function of elapsed time, gives the equation x = ft; this, developed as f (t + ë), gives","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"73.102","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0102"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0103","text":"ft + ëft + [ë'[hoch 2]]/2. f\"t + etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"73.103","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0103"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0104","text":"Thus the space traversed during the time is represented in the formula ëft + [ë[hoch 2]]/2. f't + [ë[hoch 3]]/2.3. f\"t + etc. The motion by means of which this space is traversed is therefore, it is said, i.e. because the analytical development yields several, indeed infinitely many, terms—composed of different partial motions, whose spaces corresponding to the time will be ëft, [ë[hoch 2]]/2. f\"t, [ë[hoch 3]]/[2.3]. f\"t, etc. The first partial motion is, in familiar motion, the formally=uniform one with a velocity determined by f't; the second, the uniformly accelerated one, which comes from an accelerating force proportioned to f't.","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"73.104","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0104"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0105","text":"\"Since, now, the remaining terms relate to no simple familiar motion, it is not necessary to take them particularly into consideration, and we shall show that one can abstract from them in determining the motion at the beginning of the instant of time.\" This is now shown, but admittedly only through comparison of that series, whose terms all belonged to the determination of the magnitude of the space traversed in the time, with the equation x = at + bt[hoch 2] given in art. 3 for the motion of falling, in which only these two terms occur.","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"73.105","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0105"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0106","text":"But this equation itself has received this form only through the presupposition of the explanation given to the terms arising from analytical development; this presupposition is that uniformly accelerated motion is composed of a formally-uniform motion continued with the velocity acquired in the preceding portion of time, and an increment (the a in s = at[hoch 2], i.e. the empirical coefficient) which is ascribed to the force of gravity,—a difference which in no way has any existence or ground in the nature of the matter, but is only the falsely physicalized expression of what results from an assumed analytical treatment.","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"73.106","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0106"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0107","text":"In this example, the qualitative sense is that upon which the procedure is made dependent. In connection with this, the general assertion may at once be advanced that the whole difficulty of the principle would be removed if, instead of formalism, the qualitative significance of the principle were indicated by placing the determination of the differential solely in the task which gives it its name, namely the difference in general of a function from its alteration after its variable magnitude has received an increment, and if the operation were made dependent upon this. In this sense the differential of x[hoch n] shows itself to be completely exhausted by the first term of the series that results from the development of (x + dx)[hoch n].","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"73.107","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0107"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0108","text":"That the remaining terms are not taken into consideration does not thus arise from their relative smallness;—no inexactness, error, or mistake is thereby presupposed which would be compensated and corrected by another mistake; a view from which Carnot chiefly justifies the ordinary method of infinitesimal calculus. Since the matter is not a sum but a relation, the differential is completely found through the first term; and where further terms, differentials of higher orders, are required, their determination does not consist in the continuation of a series as a sum, but in the repetition of one and the same relation, which alone is intended, and which is thus already completely determined in the first term.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"73.108","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0108"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0109","text":"The need for the form of a series, for its summation, and for what is connected therewith, must then be entirely separated from that interest of the relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"73.109","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0109"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0110","text":"The elucidations which Carnot gives concerning the method of infinite magnitudes contain, in the most purified form and most clearly expounded, what occurred in the conceptions cited above. But in the transition to the operation itself, the usual conceptions of the infinite smallness of the omitted terms in comparison with the others more or less emerge. He justifies the method rather by the fact that the results turn out correctly, and by the benefit which the introduction of imperfect equations, as he calls them, i.e. such in which such an arithmetically incorrect omission has taken place, has for the simplification and abbreviation of calculation, than by the nature of the matter itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"73.110","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0110"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0111","text":"As is well known, Lagrange took up again Newton's original method, the method of series, in order to be rid of the difficulties which the conception of the infinitely small, as well as those which the method of first and last ratios and limits, entails.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"73.111","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0111"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0112","text":"Of his calculus of functions, whose other merits with respect to precision, abstraction, and generality are sufficiently recognized, only this is to be mentioned here as relevant: that it rests upon the fundamental proposition that the difference, without becoming zero, may be assumed so small that every term of the series exceeds in magnitude the sum of all the following ones.—In this method too, one begins with the categories of increment and of the difference of the function whose variable magnitude receives the increment, whereby the troublesome series of the original function enters; just as in the sequel the terms of the series to be omitted come into consideration only in the respect that they constitute a sum, and the ground for omitting them is placed in the relativity of their quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"73.112","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0112"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0113","text":"Thus the omission here too is not, in general, reduced to the point of view which occurs partly in certain applications, wherein, as was recalled above, the terms of the series are supposed to have a determinate qualitative significance and terms are left out, not because they are insignificant in magnitude, but because they are insignificant qualitatively; partly, however, the omission itself falls away under the essential point of view which first emerges distinctly for the so-called differential coefficient in the so-called application of the calculus in Lagrange, as will be set forth more fully in the following note.","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"73.113","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0113"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0114","text":"The qualitative character in general which has here been demonstrated in the form of magnitude under discussion, in that which in it is called the infinitely small, is found most immediately in the category of the limit of the relation, which was cited above and whose elaboration in the calculus has been stamped as a peculiar method. Of what Lagrange judges concerning this method, namely that it lacks ease in application and that the expression limit presents no determinate idea, we shall take up the latter point here, and look more closely at what is advanced concerning its analytical significance.","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"73.114","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0114"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0115","text":"For in the conception of the limit there indeed lies the indicated true category of the qualitative relational determination of the variable magnitudes, since the forms which arise from them, dx and dy, are to be taken absolutely only as moments of dy/dx, and dx/dy itself is to be regarded as a single indivisible sign. That thereby, for the mechanism of the calculus, especially in its application, the advantage is lost which it draws from the separation of the sides of the differential coefficient from one another, is to be set aside here. That limit is now supposed to be the limit of a given function;—it is supposed to indicate a certain value in relation to it, which determines itself through the mode of derivation. But with the bare category of limit we should be no further than with that which is at issue in this note.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"73.115","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0115"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0116","text":"has been necessary to do, namely, to show that the infinitesimal, which occurs in the differential calculus as dx and dy, does not merely have the negative, empty sense of a non-finite, non-given magnitude, as when one says, an infinite multitude, continuing into infinity, and the like, but the determinate sense of the qualitative determinacy of the quantitative, of a moment of relation as such. Yet this category as yet has no relation to what a given function is, and does not, by itself, enter into the treatment of such a function and into a use that would have to be made in it of that determination; thus the representation of the limit too, retained in this determinacy demonstrated of it, would lead to nothing. But the expression limit already itself contains that it is the limit of Something, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":116,"address":"73.116","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0116"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0117","text":"expresses a certain value which lies in the function of variable magnitude; and it is to be seen what this concrete procedure with it is like.—It is supposed to be the limit of the relation which the two increments have to one another, by which the two variable magnitudes that are connected in an equation, of which the one is regarded as a function of the other, are assumed to have increased;—the increase is here taken indeterminately in general, and to this extent no use is made of the infinitesimal. But initially, the way of finding this limit gives rise to the same inconsistencies that occur in the other methods. This way is namely the following. If y = fx, then, when y passes into y + k, fx is supposed to change into fx + ph + qh[hoch 2] + rh[hoch 3] and so forth; hence k = ph + qh[hoch 2] and so forth, and k/h = p + qh + rh[hoch 2] and so forth.","kind":"passage","sequence":117,"address":"73.117","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0117"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0118","text":"Now if k and h vanish, the second term apart from p vanishes, and p is now supposed to be the limit of the relation of the two increments. One sees that h is set as a quantum = 0, but that for this reason k/h is not simultaneously supposed to be = 0, but is still supposed to remain a relation. The representation of the limit is now supposed to afford the advantage of rejecting the inconsistency which lies herein; p is at the same time supposed not to be the actual relation, which would be = 0/0, but only the determinate value to which the relation can approach infinitely, i.e. in such a way that the difference can become smaller than any given [difference]. The more determinate sense of approximation with respect to what is properly supposed to approach one another will be considered below.","kind":"passage","sequence":118,"address":"73.118","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0118"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0119","text":"—But that a quantitative difference which has the determination not merely of being able, but of having, to be smaller than every given [difference], is no longer a quantitative difference, is clear in itself, as evident as anything in mathematics can be evident; but with this one has not got beyond dy/dx = 0/0. If, on the other hand, dy/dx = p, i.e. as a determinate quantitative relation, is assumed, as is in fact the case, then conversely the presupposition that has set h = 0 is embarrassed, a presupposition through which alone k/h = p is found. But if one concedes that k/h = 0, then with h = 0 k too is indeed of itself = 0; for the increment k of y takes place only under the condition that the increment h is; it would thus have to be said what p, which is a quite determinate quantitative value, is supposed to be.","kind":"passage","sequence":119,"address":"73.119","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0119"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0120","text":"To this there at once presents itself the simple, dry answer, that it is a coefficient and from what derivation it arises,—the first function of an original function derived in a certain determinate way.","kind":"passage","sequence":120,"address":"73.120","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0120"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0121","text":"If one were content with this, as in fact Lagrange was, in substance, content with it, then the general part of the science of the differential calculus, and immediately this form of it itself, which is called the theory of limits, would be freed from increments, then from their infinite or arbitrary smallness, from the difficulty of getting rid again, apart from the first term, or rather only the coefficient of the first term, of the further terms of a series, which inevitably make their appearance through the introduction of those increments; besides this, it would also be purified of what further is connected with this, above all of the formal categories of the infinite, of infinite approximation, and of the further equally empty categories here of continuous magnitude, [11] and those otherwise deemed necessary, such as striving, becoming, occasion of a change.","kind":"passage","sequence":121,"address":"73.121","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0121"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0122","text":"But then it would be required to show what meaning and value p still has, apart from the dry determination, wholly sufficient for the theory, that it is nothing further than a function derived from the expansion of a binomial, i.e. what connection and use it has for further mathematical need; the second remark is to deal with this.—But first there follows here still the exposition of the confusion which has been brought, through the cited use, so customary in expositions, of the representation of approximation, into the apprehension of the proper, qualitative determinacy of the relation which was initially at issue.","kind":"passage","sequence":122,"address":"73.122","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0122"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0123","text":"[11] The category of continuous or flowing magnitude presents itself with the consideration of the external and empirical alteration of magnitudes which are brought, by an equation, into the relation that the one is a function of the other; but since the scientific object of the differential calculus is a certain relation (usually expressed by the differential coefficient), a determinacy which can just as well be called a law, then for this specific determinacy mere continuity is in part already an alien aspect, and in any case the abstract and here empty category, since nothing whatever is thereby expressed concerning the law of continuity.—The formal definitions into which one falls in this connection are, indeed, to be seen from the ingenious general exposition of the fundamental determinations required for the deduction of the differential calculus by my esteemed colleague, Professor","kind":"passage","sequence":123,"address":"73.123","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0123"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0124","text":"Dirksen, which is appended to the critique of some more recent works on this science and is found in the Jahrb. f. wissensch. Kritik, 1827 no. 153 ff.; there, on p. 1251, even the definition is cited: \"A steady or continuous magnitude, continuum, is every magnitude which one thinks of in the state of becoming, so that this becoming does not occur by leaps, but through uninterrupted progression.\" This is surely tautologically the same as what the definitum is.","kind":"passage","sequence":124,"address":"73.124","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0124"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0125","text":"It has been shown that the so-called infinite differences express the vanishing of the sides of the relation as quanta, and that what remains is their quantitative relation, purely insofar as it is determined in a qualitative manner; the qualitative relation is so far from being lost therein that it is rather what results precisely through the transformation of finite magnitudes into infinite ones. In this, as we have seen, consists the entire nature of the matter.—Thus, in the ultimate relation, for example, the quanta of the abscissa and ordinate vanish; but the sides of this relation essentially remain, the one the element of the ordinate, the other the element of the abscissa.","kind":"passage","sequence":125,"address":"73.125","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0125"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0126","text":"When the mode of representation is employed that one lets one ordinate approach the other infinitely, then the previously distinct ordinate passes into the other ordinate, and the previously distinct abscissa into the other abscissa; but essentially the ordinate does not pass into the abscissa, or the abscissa into the ordinate. The element of the ordinate,—to remain with this example of variable magnitudes,—is not to be taken as the difference of one ordinate from another ordinate, but rather as the difference, or the qualitative determination of magnitude, as against the element of the abscissa; the principle of the one variable magnitude stands in relation to that of the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":126,"address":"73.126","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0126"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0127","text":"The difference, inasmuch as it is no longer the difference of finite magnitudes, has ceased to be a multiple within itself; it has collapsed into simple intensity, into the determinacy of a qualitative moment of relation as against the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":127,"address":"73.127","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0127"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0128","text":"But this constitution of the matter is obscured by the fact that what has just been called the element, for example, of the ordinate, is grasped as difference or increment in such a way that it is only the difference of the quantum of one ordinate from the quantum of another ordinate. The limit thereby does not here have the sense of the relation; it counts only as the final value which another magnitude of the same kind continually approaches in such a way that it can be distinguished from it as little as one pleases, and that the ultimate relation is a relation of equality. Thus the infinite difference is the hovering of a difference of one quantum from a quantum, and the qualitative nature according to which dx is essentially not a determination of relation with respect to x, but with respect to dy, recedes in the representation.","kind":"passage","sequence":128,"address":"73.128","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0128"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0129","text":"One lets dx[hoch 2] vanish in comparison with dx, but dx vanishes still more in comparison with x; but this truly means: it has a relation only to dy.—In such expositions geometers are always chiefly concerned with making the approximation of a magnitude to its limit intelligible, and with holding to this aspect of the difference of quantum from quantum, as it is no difference and yet still a difference. But approximation is in any case, by itself, a category that says and makes intelligible nothing; dx already has approximation behind it, it is neither near nor nearer; and infinitely near itself means the negation of being near and of approaching.","kind":"passage","sequence":129,"address":"73.129","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0129"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0130","text":"Now that it has thus come to pass that the increments or infinite differences have been considered only on the side of the quantum that vanishes in them, and only as its limit, they have thereby been grasped as moments without relation. From this would follow the inadmissible representation that it is permissible, in the ultimate relation, for example, to set abscissa and ordinate, or also sine, cosine, tangent, versed sine, and whatever else, equal to one another.—This representation seems initially to prevail when an arc is treated as a tangent; for the arc too is surely incommensurable with the straight line, and its element initially of a different quality from the element of the straight line. It seems still more absurd and impermissible than the interchange of abscissa, ordinate, versed sine, cosine, and so forth.","kind":"passage","sequence":130,"address":"73.130","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0130"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0131","text":"when quadrata rotundis, when a part of the arc, however infinitesimally small, is taken for a piece of the tangent and thus treated as a straight line. —But this treatment is essentially to be distinguished from the censured interchange; it has its justification in the fact that in the triangle which has as its sides the element of an arc and the elements of its abscissa and ordinate, the relation is the same as if that element of the arc were the element of a straight line, of the tangent; the angles that constitute the essential relation, i.e. that which remains to these elements when abstraction is made from the finite magnitudes belonging to them, are the same.—One can also express oneself concerning this by saying that straight lines, as infinitesimal, have passed over into curved lines, and that their relation in their infinity is a curvilinear relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":131,"address":"73.131","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0131"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0132","text":"Since, according to its definition, the straight line is the shortest path between two points, its difference from the curved line is grounded on the determination of amount, on the lesser amount of the distinguishable along this path, which is thus a determination of quantum. But this determination vanishes in it when it is taken as intensive magnitude, as infinite moment, as element; consequently also its difference from the curved line, which rested solely on the difference of quantum.—Thus, as infinite, straight line and arc retain no quantitative relation and, with this, on the basis of the assumed definition, no qualitative difference any longer with respect to one another, but the former rather passes over into the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":132,"address":"73.132","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0132"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0133","text":"Related, yet at the same time distinct, from the equating of heterogeneous determinations is the indeterminate and wholly indifferent assumption in itself that infinitesimal parts of the same whole are equal to one another; yet, applied to an object heterogeneous within itself, i.e. affected by an essential non-uniformity of the determination of magnitude, it produces the peculiar inversion contained in the proposition of higher mechanics that, in equal, indeed infinitesimal times, infinitesimal parts of a curve are traversed in uniform motion, inasmuch as this is asserted of a motion in which, in equal finite, i.e. existing, portions of time, finite, i.e. existing, unequal parts of the curve are traversed, i.e. therefore of a motion which is, as existing, non-uniform and is assumed as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":133,"address":"73.133","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0133"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0134","text":"This proposition is the expression in words of what an analytical term, which results in the development of the formula for non-uniform motion otherwise conformable to a law, cited above as well, is supposed to mean. Older mathematicians sought to express in words and propositions results of the newly invented infinitesimal calculus, which in any case always had to do with concrete objects, and to represent them in geometrical diagrams, essentially in order to employ them for theorems according to the customary kind of proof. The terms of a mathematical formula, into which the analytical treatment decomposed the magnitude of the object, for example of motion, there received an objective meaning, for example that of velocity, accelerating force, and so forth.","kind":"passage","sequence":134,"address":"73.134","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0134"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0135","text":"according to such significance, they should yield correct propositions, physical laws, and, in accordance with the analytical connection, their objective connections and relations should likewise be determined, as, for example, precisely that in a uniformly accelerated motion there exists a particular velocity proportional to the times, while, besides this, an increment from the force of gravity is continually added. Such propositions are set forth in the modern, analytical form of mechanics throughout as results of the calculus, without concern as to whether they have a real sense, i.e. one to which an existence would correspond, in and for themselves, and as to a proof of such a sense; the difficulty of making intelligible the connection of such determinations when they are taken in the expressed real sense, e.g.","kind":"passage","sequence":135,"address":"73.135","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0135"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0136","text":"the transition from that non-uniform velocity to a uniformly accelerated one, is held to have been entirely removed by the analytical treatment, in which such a connection is a simple consequence of the now fixed authority of the operations of the calculus. It is proclaimed as a triumph of science to find, by mere calculus and beyond experience, laws, i.e. propositions of existence, which have no existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":136,"address":"73.136","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0136"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0137","text":"But in the earlier, still naive age of infinitesimal calculus, those determinations and propositions, represented in geometrical diagrams, were to be given a real sense in and for themselves and made plausible, and in such a sense applied to the proof of the principal propositions at issue, (—see Newton’s proof of his fundamental proposition of the theory of gravitation in the Princ. mathem. philosophiae naturalis lib. I. Sect. II. Prop. I., compared with Schubert’s Astronomie (first ed. vol. III, §. 20), where it is admitted that matters are not exactly so, i.e. that at the point which is the nerve of the proof they are not so as Newton assumes—).","kind":"passage","sequence":137,"address":"73.137","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0137"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0138","text":"It cannot be denied that in this field much has been accepted as proof, chiefly with the aid of the haze of the infinitesimal, for no other reason than that what emerged was always already known beforehand, and that the proof so arranged that it emerged produced at least the appearance of a framework of proof;—an appearance which was still preferred to mere belief or knowledge from experience. But I have no hesitation in regarding this manner as no more than mere sleight-of-hand and charlatanry in proving, and in including under this even Newtonian proofs, in particular those belonging to the one just cited, on account of which Newton has been raised to the heavens and above Keppler, as having mathematically demonstrated what the latter had found solely through experience.","kind":"passage","sequence":138,"address":"73.138","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0138"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0139","text":"The empty framework of such proofs was erected in order to prove physical laws. But mathematics is in general incapable of proving determinations of magnitude in physics, insofar as they are laws having the qualitative nature of the moments as their foundation; for the simple reason that this science is not philosophy, does not proceed from the Concept, and the qualitative therefore lies outside its sphere, insofar as it is not taken up from experience by way of lemma.","kind":"passage","sequence":139,"address":"73.139","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0139"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0140","text":"The assertion of the honour of mathematics, that all propositions occurring in it ought to be strictly proved, has often made it forget its boundary; thus it seemed contrary to its honour simply to acknowledge experience as the source and sole proof for propositions of experience; later consciousness in this respect has become more cultivated; but until it becomes clear about the distinction between what is mathematically demonstrable and what can only be taken from elsewhere, as well as about what are merely members of analytical development and what are physical existences, scientificity cannot develop itself into a strict and pure bearing.—But the framework of Newtonian proving will doubtless yet receive the same treatment that has been accorded to another groundless Newtonian artificial structure composed of optical experiments and inferences connected with them.","kind":"passage","sequence":140,"address":"73.140","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0140"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0141","text":"Applied mathematics is still full of a similar concoction of experience and reflection; but just as, for some time now, one part after another of that optics began in fact to be ignored in science, though with the inconsistency of still allowing the remainder, although contradictory to it, to stand,—so it is also a fact that a part of those deceptive proofs has already either fallen into oblivion of itself or been replaced by others.","kind":"passage","sequence":141,"address":"73.141","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A1DB:P0141"]}],"source_digest":"5e102983447d5302419cd7ff2fb92b37c40f5f01b561aaa8cc51d006e79314e6","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1. Die Begriffsbestimmtheit des mathematischen Unendlichen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1. Die Begriffsbestimmtheit des mathematischen Unendlichen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ","title":"Remark 2.The Purpose of Differential Calculus Derived from Its Application.","order":74,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A2DZ","text":"In der vorigen Anmerkung ist Theils die Begriffsbestimmtheit des Unendlich-Kleinen, das in dem Differential-Kalkul gebraucht wird, Theils die Grundlage seiner Einführung in denselben betrachtet worden; Beides sind abstrakte und darum an sich auch leichte Bestimmungen; die sogenannte Anwendung aber bietet größere Schwierigkeiten sowohl als auch die interessantere Seite dar; die Elemente dieser konkreten Seite sollen der Gegenstand dieser Anmerkung seyn.—Die ganze Methode der Differentialrechnung ist in dem Satze, daß dx[hoch n] = nx[hoch n 1]dx, oder f(x+i)-fx/i = P, d.i. gleich dem Koefficienten des ersten Gliedes des nach den Potenzen von dx oder i entwickelten Binomiums x + d, x + i, absolvirt. Man bedarf weiter nichts zu erlernen; die Ableitung der nächsten Formen, des Differentials eines Produkts, einer Exponentialgröße und sofort ergiebt sich daraus mechanisch; in wenig Zeit, vielleicht in einer halben Stunde—mit dem Finden der Differentiale ist das umgekehrte, das Finden der ursprünglichen Funktion aus jenen, die Integration gleichfalls gegeben,—kann man die ganze Theorie inne haben. Was allein länger aufhält, ist die Bemühung es einzusehn, begreifflich zu machen, daß nachdem der eine Umstand der Aufgabe, das Finden jenes Koefficienten, auf analytische d. i. ganz arithmetische Weise, durch die Entwickelung der Funktion der veränderlichen Größe, nachdem diese durch einen Zuwachs die Form eines Binomiums erhalten, so leicht bewerkstelligt worden, es auch mit dem andern Umstand, nämlich mit dem Weglassen der übrigen Glieder der entstehenden Reihe außer den ersten, seine Richtigkeit habe. Wäre es der Fall, daß man jenen Koefficienten allein nöthig hätte, so wäre mit der Bestimmung desselben Alles, was die Theorie betrifft, —wie gesagt in weniger als einer halben Stunde abgethan, und das Weglassen der weitern Glieder der Reihe machte so wenig eine Schwierigkeit, daß vielmehr von ihnen, als Gliedern der Reihe (als zweiten, dritten u.s.f. Funktionen ist ihre Bestimmung schon mit der Bestimmung des ersten gleichfalls absolvirt), gar nicht die Rede wäre, da es um sie ganz und gar nicht zu thun ist.\n\nEs kann die Bemerkung vorangeschickt werden, daß man es der Methode des Differentialkalkuls wohl sogleich ansieht, daß sie nicht für sich selbst erfunden und aufgestellt worden ist; sie ist nicht nur nicht für sich begründet, als eine andere Weise analytischen Verfahrens, sondern die Gewaltsamkeit, Glieder, die sich aus Entwickelung einer Funktion ergeben, indem doch das Ganze dieser Entwickelung vollständig zur Sache zu gehören angenommen ist,—weil die Sache als der Unterschied\n\nder entwickelten Funktion einer veränderlichen Größe, nachdem dieser die Gestalt eines Binomiums gegeben worden, von der ursprünglichen, angesehen wird,—geradezu wegzulassen, widerspricht vielmehr durchaus allen mathematischen Grundsätzen. Das Bedürfniß solcher Verfahrungsweise, wie die ihr an ihr selbst mangelnde Berechtigung, weist sogleich darauf hin, daß anderswo der Ursprung und die Grundlage sich befinden müsse. Es geschieht auch sonst in den Wissenschaften, daß das, was als das Elementarische vornehin gestellt ist und woraus die Sätze der Wissenschaft abgeleitet werden sollen, nicht einleuchtend ist, und daß es sich ausweist, vielmehr in dem Nachfolgenden seine Veranlassung und seine Begründung zu haben. Der Hergang in der Geschichte des Differential-Kalkuls thut dar, daß er in den verschiedenen sogenannten Tangential-Methoden vornehmlich, die Sache gleichsam als in Kunststücken, den Anfang genommen hat; die Art des Verfahrens, nachdem es auch auf weitere Gegenstande ausgedehnt worden, ist spater zum Bewußtseyn und in abstrakte Formeln gebracht worden, welche nun auch zu Principien zu erheben versucht wurde.\n\nAls die Begriffsbestimmtheit des sogenannten Unendlich-Kleinen ist die qualitative Quantitäts-Bestimmtheit solcher, die zunächst als Quanta im Verhältniß zu einander gesetzt sind, aufgezeigt worden, woran sich die empirische Untersuchung knüpfte, jene Begriffs-Bestimmtheit in den Beschreibungen oder Definitionen nachzuweisen, die sich von dem Unendlich-Kleinen, insofern es als unendliche Differenz und dergleichen genommen ist, vorfinden.—Dieß ist nur im Interesse der abstrakten Begriffsbestimmtheit als solcher geschehen; die weitere Frage wäre, wie von ihr der Übergang zur mathematischen Gestaltung und Anwendung beschaffen wäre. Zu dem Ende ist zuerst das Theoretische, die Begriffsbestimmtheit, noch weiter vorzunehmen, welche sich an ihr selbst nicht ganz unfruchtbar zeigen wird; alsdenn ist das Verhältniß derselben zur Anwendung zu betrachten, und bei beidem nachzuweisen, so weit es hier angeht, daß die allgeineinen Folgerungen zugleich demjenigen, um was es in der Differentialrechnung zu thun ist, und der Art, wie sie es bewerkstelligt, angemessen sind.\n\nZunächst ist daran zu erinnern, daß die Form, welche die in Rede stehende Begriffsbestimmtheit im Mathematischen hat, bereits beiläufig angegeben ist. Die qualitative Bestimmtheit des Quantitativen ist zuerst im quantitativen Verhältniß überhaupt aufgewiesen, es ist aber auch schon bei der Nachweisung der unterschiedenen sogenannten Rechnungsarten (s. d. betreff. Anm.) anticipirt worden, daß das nachher an seiner eigenthümlichen Stelle noch zu betrachtende Potenzenverhältniß es ist, worin die Zahl durch Gleichsetzung ihrer Begriffsmomente, der Einheit und der Anzahl als zu sich selbst zurückgekehrte gesetzt ist, und damit das Moment der Unendlichkeit, des Fürsichseyns, d. i. des Bestimmtseyns durch sich selbst, an ihr erhält. Die ausdrückliche qualitative Größenbestimmtheit bezieht sich somit, wie gleichfalls schon erinnert, wesentlich auf Potenzenbestimmungen, und da die Differentialrechnung das Specifische hat, mit qualitativen Größenformen zu operiren, so muß ihr eigenthümlicher mathematischer Gegenstand die Behandlung von Potenzenformen seyn, und die sämmtlichen Aufgaben und deren Auflösungen, zu deren Behuf die Differentialrechnung gebraucht wird, zeigen es, daß das Interesse allein in der Behandlung von Potenzenbestimmungen als solchen liegt.\n\nSo wichtig diese Grundlage ist, und sogleich an die Spitze etwas Bestimmtes stellt, statt der bloß formellen Kategorien von veränderlichen, kontinuirlichen oder unendlichen Größen und dergleichen, oder auch nur von Funktionen uberhaupt, so ist sie noch zu allgemein; andere Operationen haben gleichfalls damit zu thun; schon das Erheben in die Potenz und Wurzelausziehen, dann die Behandlung der Exponentialgrößen und Logarithmen, Reihen, die Gleichungen höherer Ordnungen haben ihr Interesse und ihre Bemühung allein mit Verhältnissen, die auf Potenzen beruhen. Ohne Zweifel müssen sie zusammen ein System der Potenzenbehandlung ausmachen; aber welches unter den verschiedenen Verhältnissen, worein Potenzenbestimmungen gesetzt werden können, dasjenige sey, das der eigentliche Gegenstand und das Interesse für die Differentialrechnung ist, dieß ist aus dieser selbst, d. i. aus den sogenannten Anwendungen derselben zu entnehmen. Diese sind in der That die Sache selbst, das wirkliche Verfahren in der mathematischen Auflösung eines gewissen Kreises von Problemen; dieß Verfahren ist früher gewesen, als die Theorie oder der allgemeine Theil, und Anwendung ist dasselbe später genannt worden nur in Beziehung auf die nachher erschaffene Theorie, welche die allgemeine Methode des Verfahrens Theils aufstellen, Theils ihr aber Principien, d. i. Rechtfertigung geben wollte. Welche vergebliche Bemühung es gewesen ist, für die bisherige Auffassungsweise des Verfahrens Principien aufzufinden, welche den Widerspruch, der dabei zum Vorschein kommt, wirklich lösten, statt ihn nur durch die Unbedeutenheit des nach dem mathematischen Verfahren nothwendigen hier aber wegzulassenden, oder durch die auf dasselbe hinauslaufende Möglichkeit der unendlichen oder beliebigen Annäherung und dergleichen zu entschuldigen oder zu verstecken, ist in voriger Anmerkung gezeigt worden. Wenn aus dem wirklichen Theile der Mathematik, der die Differentialrechnung genannt wird, das Allgemeine des Verfahrens anders abstrahirt würde, als bisher geschehen ist, so würden sich jene Principien und die Bemühung mit denselben auch als entbehrlich zeigen, wie sie an ihnen selbst sich als etwas Schiefes und im Widerspruche Bleibendes ausweisen.\n\nWenn wir diesem Eigenthümlichen durch einfaches Aufnehmen des in diesem Theile der Mathematik Vorhandenen nachforschen, so finden wir als Gegenstand à) Gleichungen, in welchen eine beliebige Anzahl von Größen (wir können hier überhaupt bei zwei stehen bleiben) zu einem Ganzen der Bestimmtheit so verbunden sind, daß diese erstens ihre Bestimmtheit in empirischen Größen, als festen Grenzen und dann in der Art der Verbindung mit denselben, so wie ihrer Verbindung untereinander, haben; wie dieß überhaupt in einer Gleichung der Fall ist; indem aber nur Eine Gleichung für beide Größen (und ebenso relativ wohl mehrere Gleichungen für mehrere Größen, aber immer weniger, als die Anzahl der Größen ist—) vorhanden ist, gehören diese Gleichungen zu den unbestimmten; und daß zweitens eine Seite, wie diese Größen hier ihre Bestimmtheit haben, darin liegt, daß sie (wenigstens eine derselben) in einer höhern, als die erste Potenz, in der Gleichung vorhanden sind.\n\nHierüber sind zunächst einige Bemerkungen zu machen, für's Erste, daß die Größen nach der ersten der angegebenen Bestimmungen ganz nur den Charakter solcher veränderlichen Größen haben, wie sie in den Aufgaben der unbestimmten Analysis vorkommen. Ihr Werth ist unbestimmt, aber so daß wenn anderswoher ein vollkommen bestimmter Werth, d. i. ein Zahlenwerth für die eine kommt, auch die andere bestimmt, so die eine, eine Funktion der andern, ist. Die Kategorien von veränderlichen Größen, Funktionen und dergleichen sind darum für die specifische Größebestimmtheit, die hier in Rede steht, nur formell, wie vorhin gesagt worden ist, weil sie von einer Allgemeinheit sind, in welcher dasjenige Specifische, worauf das ganze Interesse des Differentialkalkuls geht, noch nicht enthalten ist, noch daraus durch Analyse explicirt werden kann; sie sind für sich einfache, unbedeutende, leichte Bestimmungen, die nur erst schwierig gemacht werden, insofern das in sie gelegt werden soll, damit es dann aus ihnen abgeleitet werden könne, was nicht in ihnen liegt, nämlich die specifische Bestimmung der Differentialrechnung. —Was alsdenn die sogenannte Konstante betrifft, so kann über sie bemerkt werden, daß sie zunächst als eine gleichgültige empirische Größe ist, bestimmend für die veränderlichen Größen bloß in Ansehung ihres empirischen Quantums, als Grenze ihres Minimums und Maximums; die Art der Verbindung aber der Konstanten mit den veränderlichen Größen ist selbst eines der Momente für die Natur der besonderen Funktion, welche diese Größen sind. Umgekehrt sind aber auch die Konstanten selbst Funktionen; insofern z.B. eine gerade Linie den Sinn hat, Parameter einer Parabel zu seyn, so ist dieser ihr Sinn dieß, daß sie die Funktion y[hoch 2]/x ist; wie in der Entwickelung des Binomiums überhaupt, die Konstante, welche der Koefficient des ersten Entwickelungsgliedes ist, die Summe der Wurzeln, der des zweiten, die Summe der Produkte derselben zu zwei und zwei u.s.f. also diese Konstanten hier überhaupt Funktionen der Wurzeln sind; wo in der Integralrechnung die Konstante aus der gegebenen Formel bestimmt wird, wird sie insofern als eine Funktion von dieser behandelt. Jene Koefficienten werden wir dann weiter in einer anderen Bestimmung als Funktionen betrachten, deren Bedeutung im Konkreten es ist, worauf das ganze Interesse geht.\n\nDas Eigenthümliche nun aber, wodurch die Betrachtung der veränderlichen Größen sich in der Differentialrechnung von ihrer Beschaffenheit in den unbestimmten Aufgaben unterscheidet, ist in das Angegebene zu setzen, daß wenigstens eine jener Größen oder auch alle sich in einer höhern Potenz als die erste befinde, wobei wieder gleichgültig ist, ob sämmtliche von derselben höhern oder von ungleichen Potenzen sind; ihre specifische Unbestimmtheit, die sie hier haben, liegt allein darin, daß sie in solchem Potenzenverhältnisse Funktionen von einander sind. Dadurch ist die Veränderung der veränderlichen Größen qualitativ determinirt, damit kontinuirlich, und diese Kontinuität, die für sich wieder nur die formelle Kategorie überhaupt einer Identität, einer sich in der Veränderung erhaltenden, gleichbleibenden Bestimmtheit ist, hat hier ihren determinirten Sinn und zwar allein in dem Potenzenverhältnisse, als welches kein Quantum zu seinem Exponenten hat, und die nicht quantitative, bleibende Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses der veränderlichen Größen ausmacht. Daher ist gegen einen andern Formalismus die Bemerkung zu machen, daß die erste Potenz nur Potenz im Verhältniß zu höhern ist; für sich ist x nur irgend ein unbestimmtes Quantum. So hat es keinen Sinn, für sich die Gleichungen y = ax + b, der geraden Linie oder s = ct die der schlechtgleichförmigen Geschwindigkeit zu differentiren; wenn aus y = ax, oder auch aus y = ax + b, a = dy/dx, oder ds/dt = c aus s = ct wird, so ist ebenso sehr a = y/x, die Bestimmung der Tangente oder s/t = c. die der schlechten Geschwindigkeit. Letztere wird als dy/dx exponirt im Zusammenhange dessen, was für die Entwickelung der gleichförmig beschleunigten Bewegung ausgegeben wird; aber daß ein Moment von einfacher, schlechtgleichförmiger, d. i. nicht durch die höhere Potenz eines der Momente der Bewegung bestimmter Geschwindigkeit, im Systeme solcher Bewegung vorkomme, ist, wie früher bemerkt, selbst eine leere, allein in der Routine der Methode gegründete Annahme. Indem die Methode von der Vorstellung des Zuwachses, den die veränderliche Größe erleiden solle, ausgeht, so kann Freilich auch eine solche, die nur eine Funktion von erster Potenz ist, auch einen Zuwachs erleiden; wenn nun hierauf, um das Differential zu finden, der Unterschied der hierdurch entstandenen zweiten Gleichung von der gegebenen genommen werden soll, so zeigt sich das Leere der Operation, daß, wie bemerkt, die Gleichung vor und nach derselben, für die sogenannten Zuwächse dieselbe ist als für die veränderlichen Größen selbst.\n\nß) Durch das Gesagte ist die Natur der zu behandelnden Gleichung bestimmt, und es ist nun anzugeben, auf welches Interesse sich die Behandlung derselben gerichtet findet. Diese Betrachtung kann nur bekannte Resultate, wie sie der Form nach in der Lagrange'schen Auffassung insbesondere vorhanden sind, geben; aber ich habe die Exposition so ganz elementarisch angestellt, um die damit vermischten heterogenen Bestimmungen zu entfernen.—Als die Grundlage der Behandlung der Gleichung von angegebener Art zeigt sich, daß die Potenz innerhalb ihrer selbst als ein Verhältniß, als ein System von Verhältnißbestimmungen, gefaßt wird. Die Potenz ist oben als die Zahl angegeben worden, insofern sie dazu gekommen ist, daß ihre Veränderung durch sie selbst bestimmt, ihre Momente, Einheit und Anzahl identisch ist, wie früher nachgewiesen, vollkommen zunächst im Quadrat, formeller, was hier keinen Unterschied macht, in den höhern Potenzen. Die Potenz nun, da sie als Zahl—wenn man den Ausdruck Größe als den allgemeinern vorzieht, so ist sie an sich immer die Zahl,—eine Menge ist, auch als Summe dargestellt, kann zunächst innerhalb ihrer in eine beliebige Menge von Zahlen zerlegt werden, die ohne alle weitere Bestimmung gegen einander und gegen ihre Summe sind, als nur daß sie zusammen dieser gleich sind. Aber die Potenz kann auch in eine Summe von solchen Unterschieden discernirt werden, die durch die Form der Potenz bestimmt sind. Wird die Potenz als Summe genommen, so ist auch die Grundzahl derselben, die Wurzel als Summe gefaßt, und beliebig nach mannigfaltiger Zerlegung, welche Mannigfaltigkeit aber das gleichgültige empirisch-Quantitative ist. Die Summe als welche die Wurzel seyn soll, auf ihre einfache Bestimmtheit, d. i. ihre wahrhafte Allgemeinheit zurückgeführt, ist das Binomium; alle weitere Vermehrung der Glieder ist eine bloße Wiederholung derselben Bestimmung und daher etwas Leeres. [12] Worauf es ankommt, ist allein die, hiermit qualitative Bestimmtheit der Glieder, welche sich durch die Potenzirung der als Summe angenommenen Wurzel ergiebt, welche Bestimmtheit allein in der Veränderung, die das Potenziren ist, liegt. Diese Glieder sind somit ganz Funktionen der Potenzirung und der Potenz. Jene Darstellung nun der Zahl, als Summe einer Menge von solchen Gliedern, welche Funktionen der Potenzirung sind, alsdenn das Interesse, die Form solcher Funktionen, und ferner diese Summe aus der Menge solcher Glieder, zu finden, insofern dieses Finden allein von jener Form abhängen muß,—dieß macht bekanntlich die besondere Lehre von den Reihen aus. Aber hierbei haben wir wesentlich das fernere Interesse zu unterscheiden, nämlich das Verhältniß der zu Grunde liegenden Größe selbst, deren Bestimmtheit, insofern sie ein Komplex d. i. hier eine Gleichung, ist, eine Potenz in sich schließt, —zu den Funktionen ihrer Potenzirung. Dieß Verhältniß, ganz abstrahirt von dem vorhin genannten Interesse der Summe wird sich als der Gesichtspunkt zeigen, der sich als der einzige, den die Differentialrechnung sich vorsetzt, aus der wirklichen Wissenschaft ergiebt.\n\n[12] Es gehört nur zum Formalismus derjenigen Allgemeinheit, auf welche die Analysis nothwendigen Anspruch macht, wenn statt (a + b)[hoch n] für die Potenzenentwicklung zu nehmen, (a + b + c + d…)[hoch n] gesagt wird, wie dieß auch in vielen andern Fällen gethan wird; es ist solche Form, so zu sagen, nur für eine Koketterie des Scheins der Allgemeinheit zu halten; in dem Binomium ist die Sache erschöpft; es wird durch dessen Entwickelung das Gesetz gefunden, und das Gesetz ist die wahrhafte Allgemeinheit, nicht die äußerliche nur leere Wiederholung des Gesetzes, welche allein es ist, die durch jenes a + b + c + d… hervorgebracht wird.\n\nEs ist jedoch vorher noch eine Bestimmung zu dem Gesagten hinzuzufügen, oder vielmehr eine, die darin liegt, zu entfernen. Es wurde nämlich gesagt, daß die veränderliche Größe, in deren Bestimmung die Potenz eintritt, angesehen werde, innerhalb ihrer selbst als Summe und zwar als ein System von Gliedern, insofern diese Funktionen der Potenzirung sind, womit auch die Wurzel als eine Summe, und in der einfach bestimmten Form als Binomium betrachtet werde; x[hoch n] = (y + z)[hoch n] = (y + ny[hoch n-1] z +….) Diese Darstellung ging für die Entwickelung der Potenz, d. i. für das Erlangen ihrer Potenzirungsfunktionen, von der Summe als solcher aus; es ist jedoch hier nicht um eine Summe als solche noch um die daraus entspringende Reihe zu thun, sondern von der Summe ist nur die Beziehung aufzunehmen. Die Beziehung als solche der Größen ist das was einer Seits übrig bleibt, nachdem von dem plus einer Summa als solcher abstrahirt wird, und was anderer Seits für das Finden der EntwicklungsFunktionen der Potenz erforderlich ist. Solche Beziehung aber ist schon darin bestimmt, daß hier der Gegenstand eine Gleichung, y[hoch m] = ax[hoch n] auch schon ein Komplex von mehrern (veränderlichen) Größen ist, der eine Potenzenbestimmung derselben enthält. In diesem Komplex ist jede dieser Größen schlechthin als in der Beziehung auf die andere mit der Bedeutung, könnte man sagen, eines plus an ihr selbst,—als Funktion der andern Größen gesetzt; ihr Charakter, Funktionen von einander zu seyn, giebt ihnen diese Bestimmung des plus, eben damit aber eines ganz unbestimmten, nicht eines Zuwachses, Inkrements und dergleichen. Doch diesen abstrakten Gesichtspunkt konnten wir auch auf der Seite lassen; es kann ganz einfach dabei stehen geblieben werden, daß nachdem die veränderlichen Größen in der Gleichung als Funktionen von einander, so daß diese Bestimmtheit ein Verhältniß von Potenzen enthält, gegeben sind, nun auch die Funktionen der Potenzirung einer jeden mit einander verglichen werden,—welche zweiten Funktionen durch gar nichts Anderes weiter als durch die Potenzirung selbst bestimmt sind. Es kann zunächst für ein Belieben oder eine Möglichkeit ausgegeben werden, eine Gleichung von den Potenzen ihrer veränderlichen Größen auf ein Verhältniß ihrer Entwickelungsfunktionen zu setzen; ein weiterer Zweck, Nutzen, Gebrauch hat erst das Dienliche solcher Umgestaltung davon anzugeben; durch ihre Nützlichkeit allein ist jene Umstellung veranlaßt worden. Wenn vorhin von der Darstellung dieser Potenzirungsbestimungen an einer Größe, die als Summe in sich different genommen werde, ausgegangen worden, so diente dieß nur Theils zur Angabe von welcher Art solche Funktionen seyen, Theils liegt darin die Weise sie zu finden.\n\nWir befinden uns hiermit bei der gewöhnlichen analytischen Entwickelung, die für den Zweck der Differentialrechnung so gefaßt wird, daß der veränderlichen Größe ein Zuwachs, dx, i gegeben und nun die Potenz des Binomiums durch die Gliederreihe, die ihm angehört, explicirt wird. Der sogenannte Zuwachs aber soll nicht ein Quantum, nur eine Form seyn, deren ganzer Werth ist, zur Entwickelung behülflich zu seyn; was man eingestandenermaßen, am bestimmtesten von Euler und Lagrange, und in der früher erwähnten Vorstellung der Grenze, will, sind nur die sich ergebende Potenzenbestimmungen der veränderlichen Größen, die sogenannten Koefficienten zwar des Zuwachses und der Potenzen desselben, nach denen die Reihe sich ordnet und zu denen die unterschiedenen Koefficienten gehören. Es kann hierzu etwa bemerkt werden, daß indem nur um der Entwickelung willen ein Zuwachs angenommen ist, der ohne Quantum sey, es am geschicktesten gewesen wäre, (das Eins) dafür zu nehmen, indem derselbe in der Entwickelung immer nur als Faktor vorkommt, womit eben der Faktor Eins den Zweck erfüllt, daß keine quantitative Bestimmtheit und Veränderung durch den Zuwachs gesetzt werden solle; dagegen dx mit der falschen Vorstellung von einer quantitativen Differenz, und andere Zeichen, wie i, mit dem hier unnützen Scheine von Allgemeinheit behafftet, immer das Aussehen und die Prätension von einem Quantum und dessen Potenzen haben; welche Prätension dann die Mühe herbeibringt, sie dessenungeachtet wegzubringen und wegzulassen. Um die Form einer nach Potenzen entwickelten Reihe zu behalten, könnten die Exponentenbezeichnungen als indices ebenso gut dem Eins angefügt werden. Aber es muß ohnehin von der Reihe und von der Bestimmung der Koefficienten nach der Stelle, die sie in der Reihe haben, abstrahirt werden, das Verhältniß zwischen allen ist dasselbe; die zweite Funktion wird ganz ebenso aus der ersten, als diese aus der ursprünglichen abgeleitet, und für die als die zweite gezählte ist die erste abgeleitete wieder ursprüngliche Funktion. Wesentlich aber geht das Interesse nicht auf die Reihe, sondern ganz allein auf die sich aus der Entwickelung ergebende Potenzenbestimmung in ihrem Verhältniß zu der für sie unmittelbaren Größe. Anstatt also jene als den Koefficienten des ersten Gliedes der Entwickelung zu bestimmen, da ein Glied als das erste in Beziehung auf die andern in der Reihe folgenden bezeichnet wird, eine solche Potenz als eines Zuwachses aber, wie die Reihe selbst hierher nicht gehören, wäre der bloße Ausdruck abgeleitete Potenzenfunktion oder wie vorhin gesagt wurde, eine Funktion des Potenzirens der Größe vorzuziehen, wobei als bekannt vorausgesetzt wird, auf welche Weise die Ableitung als innerhalb einer Potenz eingeschlossene Entwickelung genommen wird.\n\nWenn nun der eigentliche mathematische Anfang in diesem Theile der Analytik nichts weiter ist, als das Finden der durch die Potenzen-Entwickelung bestimmten Funktion, so ist die weitere Frage, was mit dem damit erhaltenen Verhältnisse anzufangen ist, wo es eine Anwendung und Gebrauch hat, oder in der That, für welchen Zweck solche Funktionen gesucht werden. Durch das Finden von Verhältnissen, an konkreten Gegenständen, welche sich auf jene abstrakte analytische zurückführen lassen, hat die Differentialrechnung ihr großes Interesse erhalten.\n\nÜber die Anwendbarkeit aber ergiebt sich zunächst aus der Natur der Sache, ohne noch aus den Fällen der Anwendung selbst zu schließen, vermöge der aufgezeigten Gestalt der Potenzenmomente, von selbst Folgendes. Die Entwickelung der Potenzengrößen, wodurch sich die Funktionen ihrer Potenzirung ergeben, enthält, von näherer Bestimmung abstrahirt, zunächst überhaupt die Herabsetzung der Größe auf die nächst niedrigere Potenz. Die Anwendbarkeit dieser Operation findet also bei solchen Gegenständen statt, bei welchen gleichfalls ein solcher Unterschied von Potenzenbestimmungen vorhanden ist. Wenn wir nun auf die Raumbestimmtheit reflektiren, so finden wir, daß sie die drei Dimensionen enthält, die wir, um sie von den abstrakten Unterschieden der Höhe, Länge und Breite zu unterscheiden, als die konkreten bezeichnen können, nämlich die Linie, die Fläche und den totalen Raum; und indem sie in ihren einfachsten Formen und in Beziehung auf Selbstbestimmung und damit auf analytische Dimensionen genommen werden, haben wir die gerade Linie, die ebene Fläche und dieselbe als Quadrat, und den Kubus. Die gerade Linie hat ein empirisches Quantum, aber mit der Ebene tritt das Qualitative, die Potenzenbestimmung ein; nähere Modificationen, z.B. daß dieß gleich auch mit den ebenen Kurven geschieht, können wir, insofern es zunächst um den Unterschied bloß im Allgemeinen zu thun ist, unerörtert lassen. Hiermit entsteht auch das Bedürfniß, von einer höheren Potenzenbestimmung zu einer niedrigern und umgekehrt überzugehen, indem z.B. lineare Bestimmungen aus gegebenen Gleichungen der Fläche u.s.f. oder umgekehrt abgeleitet werden sollen. —Die Bewegung ferner, als an der das Größenverhältniß des durchloffenen Raumes und der dazu gehörigen verflossenen Zeit zu betrachten ist, zeigt sich in den verschiedenen Bestimmungen einer schlechtgleichförmigen, einer gleichförmig beschleunigten, einer abwechselnd gleichförmig beschleunigten und gleichförmig retardirten, —in sich zurückkehrenden Bewegung; indem diese unterschiedenen Arten der Bewegung nach dem Größenverhältnisse ihrer Momente, des Raums und der Zeit, ausgedrückt werden, ergeben sich für sie Gleichungen aus unterschiedenen Potenzenbestimmungen, und insofern es Bedürfniß seyn kann, eine Art der Bewegung oder auch der Raumgrößen, an welche eine Art gebunden ist, aus einer anderen Art derselben zu bestimmen, führt die Operation gleichfalls das Übergehen von einer Potenzenfunktion zu einer höhern oder medrigern herbei.—Die Beispiele dieser zwei Gegenstände mögen für den Zweck, zu dem sie angeführt sind, genügen.\n\nDer Anschein von Zufälligkeit, welchen die Differentialrechnung in ihren Anwendungen präsentirt, würde schon vereinfacht werden, durch das Bewußtseyn über die Natur der Gebiete, in welchem die Anwendung statt finden kann, und über das eigenthümliche Bedürfniß und die Bedingung dieser Anwendung. Nun aber kommt es weiter innerhalb dieser Gebiete selbst darauf an, zu wissen, zwischen welchen Theilen der Gegenstände der mathematischen Aufgabe ein solches Verhältniß statt finde, als durch den Differentialkalkul eigenthümlich gesetzt wird. Es muß gleich vorläufig bemerkt werden, daß hierbei zweierlei Verhältnisse zu beachten sind. Die Operation des Depotenzirens einer Gleichung, sie nach den abgeleiteten Funktionen ihrer veränderlichen Größen betrachtet, giebt ein Resultat, welches an ihm selbst wahrhaft nicht mehr eine Gleichung, sondern ein Verhältniß ist; dieses Verhältniß ist der Gegenstand der eigentlichen Differentialrechnung. Eben damit auch ist zweitens das Verhältniß vorhanden von der höhern Potenzenbestimmung (der ursprünglichen Gleichung) selbst zu der niedrigern (dem Abgeleiteten). Dieß zweite Verhältniß haben wir hier zunächst bei Seite zu lassen; es wird sich als der eigenthüniliche Gegenstand der Integralrechnung zeigen.\n\nBetrachten wir zunächst das erste Verhältniß, und nehmen zu der aus der sogenannten Anwendung zu entnehmenden Bestimmung des Moments, worin das Interesse der Operation liegt, das einfachste Beispiel an den Kurven vor, die durch eine Gleichung der zweiten Potenz bestimmt sind. Bekanntlich ist unmittelbar durch die Gleichung das Verhältniß der Koordinaten gegeben in einer Potenzenbestimmung. Folgen von der Grundbestimmung sind die Bestimmungen der mit den Koordinaten zusammenhängenden anderen geraden Linien, der Tangente, Subtangente, Normale u.s.f. Die Gleichungen aber zwischen diesen Linien und den Koordinaten sind lineare Gleichungen; die Ganzen, als deren Theile diese Linien bestimmt sind, sind rechtwinklichte Dreiecke von geraden Linien. Der Übergang von der Grundgleichung, welche die Potenzenbestimmung enthält, zu jenen linearen Gleichungen enthält nun den angegebenen Übergang von der ursprünglichen Funktion, d. i. welche eine Gleichung ist, zu der abgeleiteten, welche ein Verhältniß ist, und zwar zwischen gewissen in der Kurve enthaltenen Linien. Der Zusammenhang zwischen dem Verhältnisse dieser Linien und der Gleichung der Curve ist es, um dessen Finden es sich handelt.\n\nEs ist nicht ohne Interesse, von dem Historischen hierüber so viel zu bemerken, daß die ersten Entdecker ihren Fund nur auf eine ganz empirische Weise anzugeben wissen, ohne eine Rechenschaft von der völlig äußerlich gebliebenen Operation geben zu können. Ich begnüge mich hierüber mit der Anführung Barrow's, des Lehrers Newtons. In seinen lect. Opt. et Geom., worin er Probleme der höhern Geometrie nach der Methode der Untheilbaren behandelt, die sich zunächst von dem Eigenthümlichen der Differentialrechnung unterscheidet, giebt er auch, \"weil seine Freunde in ihn gedrungen,\" (lect. X.) sein Verfahren, die Tangente zu bestimmen, an. Man muß bei ihm selbst nachlesen, wie diese Angabe beschaffen ist, um sich eine gehörige Vorstellung zu machen, wie das Verfahren ganz als äußerliche Regel angegeben ist,—in demselben Style, wie vormals in den arithmetischen Schulbüchern die Regel de tri oder noch besser die sogenannte Neunerprobe der Rechnungsarten vorgetragen worden ist. Er macht die Verzeichnung der Linienchen, die man nachher die Inkremente im charakteristischen Dreieck einer Kurve genannt hat, und giebt nun die Vorschrift als eine bloße Regel, die Glieder als überflüssig wegzuwerfen, die in Folge der Entwickelung der Gleichungen, als Potenzen jener Inkremente oder Produkte zum Vorschein kommen, ( etenim isti termini nihilum valebunt ); ebenso seyen die Glieder, die nur aus der ursprünglichen Gleichung bestimmte Größen enthalten, wegzuwerfen (das nachherige Abziehen der ursprünglichen Gleichung von der mit den Inkrementen gebildeten) und zuletzt für das Inkrement der Ordinate die Ordinate selbst und für das Inkrement der Abscisse die Subtangente zu substituiren. Man kann, wenn es so zu reden erlaubt ist, das Verfahren nicht schulmeistermässiger angeben;—die letztere Substitution ist die für die Tangentenbestimmung in der gewöhnlichen Differentialmethode zur Grundlage gemachte Annahme der Proportionalität der Inkremente der Ordinate und Abscisse mit der Ordinate und Subtangente; in Barrows Regel erscheint diese Annahme in ihrer ganz naiven Nacktheit. Eine einfache Weise, die Subtangente zu bestimmen, war gefunden; die Manieren Robervals und Fermats laufen auf Ähnliches hinaus,—die Methode, die größten und kleinsten Werthe zu finden, von der der Letztere ausging, beruht auf denselben Grundlagen und demselben Verfahren. Es war eine mathematische Sucht jener Zeiten, sogenannte Methoden, d. i. Regeln jener Art zu finden, dabei aus ihnen auch ein Geheimniß zu machen, was nicht nur leicht, sondern selbst in einer Rücksicht nöthig war, aus demselben Grunde, als es leicht war,—nämlich weil die Erfinder nur eine empirische äußerliche Regel, keine Methode, d. i. nichts aus anerkannten Principien Abgeleitetes, gefunden hatten. Solche sogenannte Methoden hat Leibnitz von seiner Zeit, und Newton ebenfalls von derselben und unmittelbarer von seinem Lehrer aufgenommen; sie haben durch die Verallgemeinerung ihrer Form und Anwendbarkeit den Wissenschaften neue Bahnen gebrochen, aber damit zugleich das Bedürfniß gehabt, das Verfahren aus der Gestalt bloß äußerlicher Regeln zu reißen, und demselben die erforderliche Berechtigung zu verschaffen gesucht.\n\nAnalysiren wir die Methode näher, so ist der wahrhafte Vorgang dieser. Es werden erstlich die Potenzenbestimmungen (versteht sich der veränderlichen Größen), welche die Gleichung enthält, auf ihre ersten Funktionen herabgesetzt. Damit aber wird der Werth der Glieder der Gleichung verändert; es bleibt daher keine Gleichung mehr, sondern es ist nur ein Verhältniß entstanden zwischen der ersten Funktion der einen veränderlichen Größe zu der ersten Funktion der andern; statt px = y[hoch 2] hat man p : 2y oder statt 2 ax—x[hoch 2] = y[hoch 2] hat man a—x : y, was nachher als das Verhältniß dy/dx bezeichnet zu werden pflegte. Die Gleichung ist Gleichung der Curve, dieß Verhältniß, das ganz von derselben abhängig, aus derselben (oben nach einer bloßen Regel) abgeleitet ist, ist dagegen ein lineares, mit welchem gewisse Linien in Proportion sind; p : 2y oder a—x : y sind selbst Verhältnisse aus geraden Linien der Kurve, den Koordinaten und den Parameters; aber damit weiß man noch nichts. Das Interesse ist, von andern an der Kurve vorkommenden Linien zu wissen, daß ihnen jenes Verhältniß zukommt, die Gleichheit zweier Verhältnisse zu finden.—Es ist also zweitens die Frage, welches die geraden, durch die Natur der Kurve bestimmten Linien sind, welche in solchem Verhältnisse stehen?—dieß aber ist es, was schon früher bekannt war, daß nämlich solches auf jenem Wege erhaltenes Verhältniß das Verhältniß der Ordinate zur Subtangente ist. dieß hatten die Alten auf sinnreichem geometrischen Wege gefunden; was die neuern Erfinder entdeckt haben, ist das empirische Verfahren, die Gleichung der Kurve so zuzurichten, daß jenes erste Verhältniß geliefert wird, von dem bereits bekannt war, daß es einem Verhältnisse gleich ist, welches die Linie enthält, hier die Subtangente, um deren Bestimmung es zu thun ist. Theils ist nun jene Zurichtung der Gleichung methodisch gefaßt und gemacht worden,—die Differentation,—Theils aber sind die imaginären Inkremente der Koordinaten und das imaginäre hieraus und einem ebensolchen Inkremente der Tangente gebildete, charakteristische Dreieck erfunden worden, damit die Proportionalität des durch die Depotenzirung der Gleichung gefundenen Verhältnisses mit dem Verhältnisse der Ordinate und der Subtangente nicht als etwas empirisch nur aus der alten Bekanntschaft Aufgenommenes, sondern als ein Erwiesenes dargestellt werde. Die alte Bekanntschaft jedoch erweist sich überhaupt und am unverkennbarsten in der angeführten Form von Regeln als die einzige Veranlassung und respektive Berechtigung der Annahme des charakteristischen Dreiecks und jener Proportionalität.\n\nLagrange hat nun diese Simulation verworfen, und den ächtwissenschaftlichen Weg eingeschlagen; seiner Methode ist die Einsicht zu verdanken, worauf es ankommt, indem sie darin besteht, die beiden Übergänge, die für die Auflösung der Aufgabe zu machen sind, zu trennen und jede dieser Seiten für sich zu behandeln und zu erweisen. Der eine Theil dieser Auflösung,—indem wir für die nähere Angabe des Ganges bei dem Beispiele der elementarischen Aufgabe, die Subtangente zu finden, bleiben,—der theoretische oder allgemeine Theil, nämlich das Finden der ersten Funktion aus der gegebenen Kurvengleichung, wird für sich regulirt; derselbe giebt ein lineares Verhältniß, also von geraden Linien, die in dem Systeme der Kurvenbestimmung vorkommen. Der andere Theil der Auflösung ist nun die Findung derjenigen Linien an der Kurve, welche in jenem Verhältnisse stehen. Dieß wird nun auf die direkte Weise (Théorie des Fonct. Anal. II. P. II. Chap.) bewerkstelligt, d. i. ohne das charakteristische Dreieck, nämlich ohne unendlichkleine Bogen, Ordinaten und Abscissen anzunehmen und diesen die Bestimmungen von dy und dx, d. i. von den Seiten jenes Verhältnisses und zugleich unmittelbar die Bedeutung der Gleichheit desselben mit der Ordinate und Subtangente selbst zu geben. Eine Linie (wie auch ein Punkt) hat allein ihre Bestimmung, insofern sie die Seite eines Dreiecks ausmacht, wie auch die Bestimmmung eines Punkts nur in einem solchen liegt. Dieß ist, um es ini Vorbeigehen zu erwähnen, der Fundamentalsatz der analytischen Geometrie, welcher die Coordinaten, wie, was dasselbe ist, in der Mechanik das Parallelogramm der Kräfte herbeiführt, das eben darum der vielen Bemühung um einen Beweis ganz unbedürftig ist.—Die Subtangente wird nun als die Seite eines Dreiecks gesetzt, dessen weitere Seiten die Ordinate und die darauf sich beziehende Tangente ist. Letztere hat als gerade Linie zu einer Gleichung p = aq, (+ b hinzuzufügen ist für die Bestimmung unnütz und wird nur um der beliebten Allgemeinheit hinzugesetzt);—die Determination des Verhältnisses p/q fällt in a, den Koefficienten von q, der die respective erste Funktion der Gleichung ist, überhaupt aber nur als a = p/q betrachtet zu werden braucht als, wie gesagt, die wesentliche Determination der geraden Linie, die als Tangente an die Kurve applicirt ist. Indem nun ferner die erste Funktion der Kurvengleichung genommen wird, ist sie ebenso die Determination einer geraden Linie; indem ferner die eine Koordinate p der ersten geraden Linie und y, die Ordinate der Kurve, als dieselben genommen werden, daß also der Punkt, in welchem jene als Tangente angenommene erste gerade die Kurve berührt, gleichfalls der Anfangspunkt der durch die erste Funktion der Kurve bestimmten geraden Linie ist, so kommt es darauf an, zu zeigen, daß diese zweite gerade Linie mit der ersten zusammenfällt, d. h. Tangente ist; algebraisch ausgedrückt, daß indem y = fx und p = Fq ist, und nun y = p, also fx = Fq angenommen wird, auch f'x = F'q. Daß nun die als Tangente applicirte gerade, und jene aus der Gleichung durch deren erste Funktion determinirte gerade Linie zusammenfallen, daß die letztere also Tangente ist; dieß wird mit Zuhilfnahme des Increments i der Abscisse und des durch die Entwickelung der Funktion bestimmten Increments der Ordinate gezeigt. Hier kommt denn also gleichfalls das berüchtigte Increment herein; aber wie es zu dem so eben angegebenen Behufe eingeführt wird, und die Entwickelung der Funktion nach demselben, muß von dem früher erwähnten Gebrauch des Inkrements für das Finden der Differentialgleichung und für das charakteristische Dreieck, wohl unterschieden werden. Der hier gemachte Gebrauch ist berechtigt und nothwendig; er fällt in den Umkreis der Geometrie, indem es zur geometrischen Bestimmung einer Tangente als solcher gehört, daß zwischen ihr und der Kurve, mit der sie einen Punkt gemeinschaftlich hat, keine andere gerade Linie, die gleichfalls in diesen Punkt fiele, durchgehen könne. Denn mit dieser Bestimmung ist die Qualität der Tangente oder Nicht-Tangente auf den Größenunterschied zurückgeführt, und diejenige Linie ist die Tangente, auf welche die größere Kleinheit—schlechthin in Ansehung der Determination, auf welche es ankommt, falle. Diese scheinbar nur relative Kleinheit enthält durchaus nichts Empirisches, d. i. von einem Quantum als solchem Abhängiges, sie ist qualitativ durch die Natur der Formel gesetzt, wenn der Unterschied des Moments, von dem die zu vergleichende Größe abhängt, ein Potenzenunterschied ist; indem derselbe auf i und i[hoch 2] hinauskommt, und i, das zuletzt doch eine Zahl bedeuten soll, dann als ein Bruch vorzustellen ist, so ist i[hoch 2] an und für sich kleiner als i, so daß selbst die Vorstellung von einer beliebigen Größe, in der man i nehmen könne, hier überflüssig und sogar nicht an ihrem Orte ist. Ebendamit hat der Erweis der größern Kleinheit nichts mit einem Unendlich-Kleinen zu thun, das hiermit hier keineswegs hereinzukommen hat.\n\nWäre es auch nur um der Schönheit und des heutigstags mehr vergessen, aber wohlverdienten Ruhmes willen, daß ich noch Descartes Tangentenmethode anführen will; sie hat übrigens auch eine Beziehung auf die Natur der Gleichungen, über welche dann noch eine fernere Bemerkung zu machen ist. Descartes trägt diese selbstständige Methode, worin die geforderte lineare Bestimmung gleichfalls aus derselben abgeleiteten Funktion gefunden wird, in seiner, sonst auch so fruchtbar gewordenen Geometrie (liv. II. p. 357 ss. Oeuvres compl. ed. Cousin Tom. V.) vor, indem er in derselben die große Grundlage von der Natur der Gleichungen und deren geometrischer Konstruktion und der damit sosehr erweiterten Analysis auf die Geometrie überhaupt, gelehrt hat. Das Problem hat bei ihm die Form der Aufgabe, gerade Linien senkrecht auf beliebige Orte einer Kurve zu ziehen, als wodurch Subtangente u.s.f. bestimmt wird; man begreift die Befriedigung, die er daselbst über seine Entdeckung, die einen Gegenstand von allgemeinem wissenschaftlichen Interesse der damaligen Zeit betraf, und die sosehr geometrisch ist und dadurch so hoch über den oben erwähnten bloßen Regelmethoden seiner Nebenbuhler stand, ausdrückt: j'ose dire que c'est ceci le problème le plus utile et le plus général, non seulement que je sache, mais même que j'aie jamais desire de savoir en géometrie.—Er legt für die Auflösung die analytische Gleichung des rechtwinklichten Dreiecks zu Grund, das durch die Ordinate des Punkts der Kurve, auf welcher die im Probleme verlangte gerade Linie senkrecht seyn soll, dann durch diese selbst, die Normale, und drittens durch den Theil der Achse, der durch die Ordinate und Normale abgeschnitten wird, durch die Subnormale, gebildet wird. Aus der bekannten Gleichung einer Kurve wird nun in jene Gleichung des Dreiecks der Werth es sey der Ordinate oder der Abscisse substituirt, so hat man eine Gleichung des zweiten Grades (und Descartes zeigt, wie auch Kurven, deren Gleichungen höhere Grade enthalten, sich hierauf zurückführen), in welcher nur noch die eine der veränderlichen Größen und zwar im Quadrat und in der ersten Potenz vorkommt;—eine quadratische Gleichung, welche zunächst als eine sogenannte unreine erscheint. Nun macht Descartes die Reflexion, daß wenn der auf der Kurve angenommene Punkt als Durchschnittspunkt derselben und eines Kreises vorgestellt wird, dieser Kreis die Kurve noch in einem anderen Punkte schneiden wird, und alsdenn sich für die zwei damit entstehenden und ungleichen x, zwei Gleichungen mit denselben Konstanten und von derselben Form ergeben;—oder aber nur Eine Gleichung mit ungleichen Werthen von x. Die Gleichung wird aber nur Eine, für das Eine Dreieck, in welchem die Hypotenuse auf die Kurve senkrecht, Normale, ist, was so vorgestellt wird, daß man die beiden Durchschnittspunkte der Kurve durch den Kreis, zusammenfallen, diesen also die Kurve berühren lasse. Damit aber fällt auch der Umstand der ungleichen Wurzeln des x oder y der quadratischen Gleichung hinweg. Bei einer quadratischen Gleichung von zwei gleichen Wurzeln nun aber ist der Koefficient des Gliedes, das die Unbekannte in der ersten Potenz enthält, das Doppelte der nur Einen Wurzel; dieß nun giebt eine Gleichung, durch welche die verlangten Bestimmungen gefunden sind. Dieser Gang ist für den genialen Griff eines ächt analytischen Kopfes anzusehen, wogegen die ganz assertorisch angenommene Proportionalität der Subtangente und der Ordinate mit den unendlich klein seyn sollenden sogenannten Inkrementen der Abscisse und der Ordinate ganz zurücksteht.\n\nDie auf die angegebene Weise erhaltene Endgleichung, welche den Koefficienten des zweiten Gliedes der quadratischen Gleichung gleichsetzt der doppelten Wurzel oder Unbekannten, ist dieselbe, welche durch das Verfahren des Differentialkalkuls gefunden wird. x[hoch 2]—ax—b = 0 differentiirt giebt die neue Gleichung 2x—a = 0; oder x[hoch 3]—px—q = 0 giebt 3x[hoch 2]—p = 0. Es bietet sich hierbei aber die Bemerkung an, daß es sich keineswegs von selbst versteht, daß solche abgeleitete Gleichung auch\n\nrichtig ist. Bei einer Gleichung mit zwei veränderlichen Größen, die darum, daß sie veränderliche sind, den Charakter unbekannte Größen zu seyn nicht verlieren, kommt, wie oben betrachtet wurde, nur ein Verhältniß heraus, aus dem angegebenen einfachen Grunde, weil durch das Substituiren der Funktionen der Potenzirung an die Stelle der Potenzen selbst der Werth der beiden Glieder der Gleichung verändert wird, und es für sich selbst noch unbekannt ist, ob auch zwischen ihnen bei so veränderten Werthen noch eine Gleichung Statt finde. Die Gleichung dy/dx = P drückt gar nichts weiter aus, als daß P ein Verhältniß ist, und es ist dem dy/dx sonst kein reeller Sinn zuzuschreiben. Von diesem Verhältniß = P ist es aber ebenso noch unbekannt, welchem andere Verhältnisse es gleich sey; solche Gleichung, die Proportionalität, giebt demselben erst einen Werth und Bedeutung.—Wie angegeben wurde, daß man diese Bedeutung, was die Anwendung hieß, anderswoher, empirisch aufnahm, so muß bei den hier in Rede stehenden durch Differentation abgeleiteten Gleichungen anderswoher gewußt werden, ob sie gleiche Wurzeln haben, um zu wissen, ob die erhaltene Gleichung noch richtig sey. Dieser Umstand wird aber in den Lehrbüchern nicht ausdrücklich bemerklich gemacht; er wird wohl dadurch beseitigt, daß eine Gleichung mit einer unbekannten, auf Null gebracht, sogleich y gesetzt wird, wodurch dann bei der Differentation allerdings ein dy/dx, nur ein Verhältniß herauskommt. Der Funktionen-Kalkul soll es allerdings mit Funktionen der Potenzirung oder die Differentialrechnung mit Differentialien zu thun haben, aber daraus folgt für sich noch keineswegs, daß die Größen, deren Differentialien oder Funktionen der Potenzirung genommen werden, selbst auch nur Funktionen anderer Größen seyn sollen. In dem theoretischen Theile, der Anweisung, die Differentiale, d. i. die Funktionen der Potenzirung abzuleiten, wird ohnehin noch nicht daran gedacht, daß die Größen, die nach solcher Ableitung zu behandeln gelehrt wird, selbst Funktionen anderer Größen seyn sollen.\n\nNoch kann in Ansehung des Weglassens der Konstante bei dem Differentiiren bemerklich gemacht werden, daß dasselbe hier den Sinn hat, daß die Konstante für die Bestimmung der Wurzeln im Falle ihrer Gleichheit gleichgültig ist, als welche Bestimmung durch den Koefficienten des zweiten Gliedes der Gleichung erschöpft ist. Wie im angeführten Beispiele von Descartes die Konstante das Quadrat der Wurzeln selbst ist, also diese aus der Konstante ebenso wie aus den Koefficienten, bestimmt werden kann; indem sie überhaupt, wie die Koefficienten, Funktion der Wurzeln der Gleichung ist. In der gewöhnlichen Darstellung erfolgt das Wegfallen der sogenannten nur durch + und—mit den übrigen Gliedern verbundenen Konstanten durch den bloßen Mechanismus des Verfahrens, daß um das Differential eines zusammengesetzten Ausdrucks zu finden, nur den veränderlichen Größen ein Zuwachs gegeben, und der hierdurch formirte Ausdruck von dem ursprünglichen abgezogen wird. Der Sinn der Konstanten und ihres Weglassens inwiefern sie selbst Funktionen sind und nach dieser Bestimmung dienen oder nicht, kommt nicht zur Sprache.\n\nMit dem Weglassen der Konstanten, hängt eine ähnliche Bemerkung zusammen, die über die Namen von Differentation und Integration, gemacht werden kann, als früher über den endlichen und unendlichen Ausdruck gemacht wurde, daß nämlich in ihrer Bestimmung vielmehr das Gegentheil von dem liegt, was der Ausdruck besagt. Differentiiren bezeichnet das Setzen von Differenzen; durch das Differentiiren aber wird eine Gleichung vielmehr auf weniger Dimensionen herabgebracht, durch das Weglassen der Konstante wird ein Moment der Bestimmtheit hinweggenommen; wie bemerkt, werden die Wurzeln der veränderlichen Größe auf eine Gleichheit gesetzt, die Differenz also derselben aufgehoben. In der Integration hingegen soll die Konstante wieder hinzugesetzt werden; die Gleichung wird dadurch allerdings, aber in dem Sinne integrirt, daß die vorher aufgehobene Differenz der Wurzeln wieder hergestellt, das Gleichgesetzte wieder differentiirt wird. —Der gewöhnliche Ausdruck trägt dazu bei, die wesentliche Natur der Sache in Schatten zu setzen und Alles auf den untergeordneten, ja der Hauptsache fremdartigen Gesichtspunkt Theils der unendlich kleinen Differenz, des Increments und dergleichen, Theils der bloßen Differenz überhaupt zwischen der gegebenen und der abgeleiteten Funktion, ohne deren specifischen, d. i. den qualitativen Unterschied zu bezeichnen, zu stellen.\n\nEin anderes Hauptgebiet, in welchem von dem Differentialkalkul Gebrauch gemacht wird, ist die Mechanik; von den unterschiedenen Potenzen-Funktionen, die sich bei den elementarischen Gleichungen ihres Gegenstandes, der Bewegung ergeben, sind deren Bedeutungen bereits beiläufig erwähnt; ich will dieselben hier direkt aufnehmen. Die Gleichung, nämlich der mathematische Ausdruck, der schlechtgleichförmigen Bewegung c = s/t oder s = ct, in welcher die durch offenen Räume den verflossenen Zeiten nach einer empirischen Einheit c, der Größe der Geschwindigkeit, proportionirt sind, bietet für die Differentation keinen Sinn dar; der Koefficient c ist bereits vollkommen bestimmt und bekannt, und es kann keine weitere Potenzenentwicklung Statt finden.—Wie s = at[hoch 2], die Gleichung der Bewegung des Falles, analysirt wird, ist früher schon erinnert; —das erste Glied der Analyse ds/dt = 2 at wird in die Sprache und resp. in die Existenz so übersetzt, es solle ein Glied einer Summe (- welche Vorstellung wir längst entfernt haben), der eine Theil der Bewegung seyn und zwar solle dieser der Kraft der Trägheit, d. i. einer schlechtgleichförmigen Geschwindigkeit so zukommen, daß in den unendlich-kleinen Zeittheilen die Bewegung gleichförmig, in den endlichen Zeittheilen d. h. in der That existirenden aber ungleichförmig sey. Freilich ist fs = 2at; und die Bedeutung voll a und von t für sich bekannt, so wie daß hiermit die Bestimmung von gleichförmiger Geschwindigkeit einer Bewegung gesetzt ist; da a = s/[t[hoch 2]] ist 2 at = 2s/t überhaupt; damit aber weiß man im geringsten nichts weiter; nur die fälschliche Annahme, daß 2at ein Theil der Bewegung als einer Summe sey, giebt den fälschlichen Schein eines physikalischen Satzes. Der Faktor selbst, a, die empirische Einheit—ein Quantum als solches—wird der Schwere zugeschrieben; wenn die Kategorie der Kraft der Schwere gebraucht wird, so ist vielmehr zu sagen, daß eben das Ganze s = at[hoch 2] die Wirkung oder besser das Gesetz der Schwere ist.—Gleichmäßig ist der aus ds/dt = 2at abgeleitete Satz, daß wenn die Schwere aufhörte zu wirken, der Körper mit der am Ende seines Falles erlangten Geschwindigkeit den doppelten Raum von dem, welchen er durchloffen hat, in einer der Dauer seines Falles gleichen Zeit zurücklegen würde.—Es liegt hierin auch eine für sich schiefe Metaphysik; das Ende des Falles, oder das Ende eines Zeittheils, in welchem der Körper gefallen, ist immer selbst noch ein Zeittheil; wäre es kein Zeittheil, so wäre Ruhe und damit keine Geschwindigkeit angenommen, die Geschwindigkeit kann nur nach dem Raume angesetzt werden, welcher in einem Zeittheil, nicht an seinem Ende, durchloffen worden ist.—Wenn nun aber vollends in andern physikalischen Gebieten, wo gar keine Bewegung vorhanden ist, wie z.B. im Verhalten des Lichts (außer dem, was seine Fortpflanzung im Raume genannt wird) und Größenbestimmungen an den Farben, eine Anwendung der Differentialrechnung gemacht wird und die erste Funktion von einer quadratischen Funktion hier auch Geschwindigkeit genannt wird, so ist dieß für einen noch unstatthafteren Formalismus der Erdichtung von Existenz anzusehen. -Bewegung, welche durch die Gleichung s = at[hoch 2] vorgestellt wird, finden wir, sagt Lagrange in der Erfahrung vom Falle der Körper; die einfachste Bewegung derselben würde die seyn, deren Gleichung s = ct[hoch 3] wäre, aber die Natur zeige keine Bewegung dieser Art; wir wüßten nicht was der Koefficient c bedeuten könnte. Wenn dem wohl so ist, so giebt es dagegen eine Bewegung, deren Gleichung s[hoch 3] = at[hoch 2] ist,—das kepplerische Gesetz der Bewegung der Körper des Sonnensystems; was hier die erste abgeleitete Funktion 2at/[3s [hoch 2]] u.s.f. bedeuten soll, und die fernere direkte Behandlung dieser Gleichung durch die Differentation, die Entwicklung der Gesetze und Bestimmungen jener absoluten Bewegung von diesem Ausgangspunkte aus, müßte dagegen wohl als eine interessante Aufgabe erscheinen, in welcher die Analysis im würdigsten Glanze sich zeigen würde.\n\nFür sich bietet so die Anwendung des Differential-Kalkuls auf die elementarischen Gleichungen der Bewegung kein reelles Interesse dar; das formelle Interesse kommt von dem allgemeinen Mechanismus des Kalkuls. Eine andre Bedeutung aber erhält die Zerlegung der Bewegung in Beziehung auf die Bestimmung ihrer Trajektorie; wenn dieses eine Kurve ist und ihre Gleichung höhere Potenzen enthält, bedarf es der Übergänge von geradlinigten Funktionen als Funktionen der Potenzirnng, zu den Potenzen selbst, und indem jene aus der ursprünglichen Gleichung der Bewegung, welche den Faktor der Zeit enthält, mit Elimination der Zeit zu gewinnen sind, ist dieser zugleich auf die niedrigern Entwicklungsfunktionen herabzusetzen, aus welchen jene Gleichungen linearer Bestimmungen erhalten werden können. Diese Seite führt auf das Interesse des andern Theils der Differentialrechnung.\n\nDas Bisherige hat den Zweck gehabt, die einfache specifische Bestimmung des Differential-Kalkuls herauszuheben und festzustellen, und dieselbe in einigen der elementarischen Beispiele nachzuweisen. Diese Bestimmung hat sich ergeben darin zu bestehen, daß aus einer Gleichung von Potenzenfunktionen der Koefficient des Entwicklungsgliedes, die sogenannte erste Funktion gefunden, und das Verhältniß, welches diese ist, in Momenten des konkreten Gegenstands aufgewiesen werde, durch welche so erhaltene Gleichung zwischen den beiden Verhältnissen diese Momente selbst bestimmt sind. Es ist ebenso von dem Princip der Integralrechnung kurz zu betrachten, was sich aus dessen Anwendung, für die specifische konkrete Bestimmnng derselben ergiebt. Die Ansicht dieses Kalkuls ist dadurch schon vereinfacht und richtiger bestimmt worden, daß er nicht mehr als Summationsmethode genommen wird, wie er im Gegensatz gegen das Differentiiren, wo der Zuwachs als das wesentliche Ingrediens gilt, genannt wurde, und womit er in wesentlichem Zusammenhang mit der Form der Reihe erschien.—Die Aufgabe dieses Kalkuls ist zunächst ebenso die theoretische oder vielmehr formelle, als die der Differentialrechnung, bekanntlich aber die umgekehrte von dieser;—es wird hier von einer Funktion ausgegangen, die als abgeleitete, als der Koefficient des nächsten aus der Entwicklung einer aber noch unbekannten Gleichung entsprungenen Gliedes betrachtet wird, und aus ihr soll die ursprüngliche Potenzen-Funktion gefunden werden; die in der natürlichen Ordnung der Entwicklung als ursprünglich anzusehende wird hier abgeleitet und die früher als abgeleitet betrachtete ist hier die gegebene oder überhaupt die anfangende. Das Formelle dieser Operation scheint nun aber bereits durch den Differential-Kalkul geleistet zu seyn; indem darin überhaupt der Übergang und das Verhältniß von der ursprünglichen zu der Entwicklungsfunktion festgestellt ist. Wenn hierbei Theils schon um die Funktion, von der auszugehen ist, anzusetzen, Theils aber den Übergang von ihr zu der ursprünglichen zu bewerkstelligen, nothwendig in vielen Fällen zu der Form der Reihe die Zuflucht genommen werden muß, so ist zunächst festzuhalten, daß diese Form als solche mit dem eigenthümlichen Prinzip des Integrirens unmittelbar nichts zu thun hat.\n\nDer andere Theil nun aber der Aufgabe des Kalkuls erscheint in Rücksicht auf die formelle Operation die Anwendung derselben. Diese ist nun selbst die Aufgabe, nämlich die Bedeutung in dem oben angegebenen Sinne zu kennen, welche die ursprüngliche Funktion von der gegebenen als ersten Funktion betrachteten eines besondern Gegenstandes hat. An sich könnte auch diese Lehre bereits in der Differentialrechnung ganz abgethan zu seyn scheinen; allein es tritt ein weiterer Umstand ein, der die Sache nicht so einfach seyn läßt. Indem nämlich in diesem Kalkul sich ergeben, daß durch die erste Funktion der Gleichung einer Kurve das Verhältniß, welches ein lineares ist, erhalten worden, so weiß man damit auch, daß die Integration dieses Verhältnisses die Gleichung der Kurve im Verhältnisse der Abscisse und Ordinate giebt; oder wenn die Gleichung für die Ebene einer Kurve gegeben wäre, so würde die Differentialrechnung über die Bedeutung der ersten Funktion solcher Gleichung bereits gelehrt haben sollen, daß diese Funktion die Ordinate als Funktion der Abscisse, hiermit die Gleichung der Kurve darstellte.\n\nNun kömmt es aber darauf an, welches von den Bestimmungsmomenten des Gegenstandes in der Gleichung selbst gegeben ist; denn nur von dem Gegebenen kann die analytische Behandlung den Ausgang nehmen und von da zu den übrigen Bestimmungen des Gegenstands übergehen. Es ist z. B. nicht die Gleichung eines Flächenraums der Kurve, noch etwa des durch ihre Umdrehung entstehenden Körpers, noch auch eines Bogens derselben, sondern nur das Verhältniß der Abscisse und Ordinate in der Gleichung der Kurve selbst gegeben. Die Übergänge von jenen Bestimmungen zu dieser Gleichung selbst können daher nicht schon in der Differentialrechnung behandelt werden; es wird für die Integralrechnung aufgespart, diese Verhältnisse zu finden.\n\nFerner aber ist gezeigt worden, daß die Differentiirung der Gleichung von mehreren veränderlichen Größen, die Entwicklungspotenz oder Differential-Koefficienten, nicht als eine Gleichung, sondern nur als ein Verhältniß giebt; die Aufgabe ist dann für dieß Verhältniß, welches die abgeleitete Funktion ist, ein zweites in den Momenten des Gegenstandes anzugeben, das jenem gleich sey. Dagegen ist das Object der Integralrechnung das Verhältniß selbst der ursprünglichen zu der abgeleiteten, hier gegeben seyn sollenden Funktion, und die Aufgabe ist, die Bedeutung der zu findenden ursprünglichen Funktion in dem Gegenstande der gegebenen ersten Funktion anzugeben, oder vielmehr indem diese Bedeutung z.B. die Ebene einer Kurve oder die zu rectificirende, als geradlinigt vorgestellte Kurve u.s.f. schon als das Problem ausgesprochen ist, zu zeigen, daß solche Bestimmung durch eine ursprüngliche Funktion gefunden werde und welches das Moment des Gegenstandes sey, welches hierfür zur Ausgangs- (der abgeleiteten) Funktion, angenommen werden müsse.\n\nDie gewöhnliche Methode nun, welche die Vorstellung der Differenz als des Unendlichkleinen gebraucht, macht sich die Sache leicht; für die Quadratur der Kurven also nimmt sie ein unendlich kleines Rektangel, ein Produkt der Ordinate in das Element d. i. das Unendlichkleine der Abscisse, für das Trapez, das zu einer seiner Seiten den unendlichkleinen, jenem unendlichkleinen der Abscisse gegenüberstehenden Bogen habe; das Produkt wird nun in dem Sinne integrirt, daß das Integral die Summe der unendlich vielen Trapeze, die Ebene, deren Bestimmung verlangt wird, nämlich die endliche Größe jenes Elements der Ebene gebe. Ebenso formirt sie aus den Unendlichkleinen des Bogens, und der dazu gehörigen Ordinate und Abscisse ein rechtwincklichtes Dreieck, in welchem das Quadrat jenes Bogens gleich sey der Summe der Quadrate der beiden andern Unendlichkleinen, deren Integration den Bogen als einen endlichen giebt.\n\nDieß Verfahren hat die allgemeine Entdeckung, welche diesem Gebiete der Analysis zu Grunde liegt, zu seiner Voraussetzung, hier in der Weise, daß die quadrirte Kurve, der rectificirte Bogen u.s.f. zu einer gewissen durch die Gleichung der Kurve gegebenen Funktion, in dem Verhältniß der sogenannten ursprünglichen Funktion zu der abgeleiteten steht. Es handelt sich darum zu wissen, wenn ein gewisser Theil eines mathematischen Gegenstandes (z.B. einer Kurve) als die abgeleitete Funktion angenommen werde, welcher andere Theil desselben durch die entsprechende ursprüngliche Funktion ausgedrückt ist. Man weiß, daß wenn die durch die Gleichung der Kurve gegebene Funktion der Ordinate als abgeleitete Funktion genommen wird, die relativ ursprüngliche Funktion der Größenausdruck der von dieser Ordinate abgeschnittenen Area der Kurve ist, daß wenn eine gewisse Tangentenbestimmung als abgeleitete Funktion angesehen wird, die ursprüngliche Funktion derselben die Größe des zu dieser Tangentenbestimmung gehörigen Bogens ausdrückt, u. s. f. daß nun aber diese Verhältnisse, das eine einer ursprünglichen Funktion zu der abgeleiteten, das andere von den Größen zweier Theile oder Umstände des mathematischen Gegenstandes, eine Proportion bilden, dieß zu erkennen und zu beweisen, erspart sich die Methode, die das Unendlichkleine und die mechanische Operation mit demselben gebraucht. Das eigenthümliche Verdienst des Scharfsinns ist, aus den anderwärts her bereits bekannten Resultaten herausgefunden zu haben, daß gewisse und welche Seiten eines mathematischen Gegenstandes, in dem Verhältnisse von ursprünglicher und von abgeleiteter Funktion stehen.\n\nVon diesen beiden Funktionen ist die abgeleitete, oder wie sie bestimmt worden ist, die Funktion der Potenzirung, hier in diesem Kalkul die gegebene, relativ gegen die ursprüngliche, als welche erst aus jener durch die Integration, gefunden werden soll. Allein sie ist nicht unmittelbar gegeben, noch ist es für sich schon gegeben, welcher Theil oder Bestimmung des mathematischen Gegenstands als die abgeleitete Funktion angesehen werden soll, um durch Zurückführung derselben auf die ursprüngliche den andern Theil oder Bestimmung zu finden, deren Größe das Problem verlangt. Die gewöhnliche Methode, die, wie gesagt, sogleich gewisse Theile des Gegenstandes als unendlich klein, in der Form abgeleiteter Funktionen, vorstellt, welche sich aus der ursprünglich gegebenen Gleichung des Gegenstandes überhaupt durch die Differentiirung bestimmen lassen, (—wie für die Rektifikation einer Kurve, die unendlichkleinen Abscissen und Ordinaten), nimmt dafür solche, welche sich mit dem Gegenstande des Problems, (in dem Beispiele, dem Bogen) der ebenso als unendlichklein vorgestellt wird, in eine Verbindung bringen lassen, die in der Elementar-Mathematik festgestellt ist, und wodurch, wenn jene Theile bekannt sind, auch dieser bestimmt ist, dessen Größe zu finden aufgegeben ist; so werden für die Rektifikation die angegebenen drei Unendlichkleinen in die Verbindung der Gleichung des rechtwinklichten Dreiecks gebracht, für die Quadratur die Ordinate mit der unendlichkleinen Abscisse in die Verbindung eines Produkts, indem eine Ebene überhaupt arithmetisch als Produkt von Linien angenommen ist. Der Übergang von solchem sogenannten Elemente der Ebene, des Bogens u.s.f. zur Größe der Ebene, des Bogens u.s.f. selbst, gilt dann nur als das Aufsteigen von dem unendlichen Ausdruck zum endlichen, oder zur Summe der unendlich vielen Elemente, aus denen die verlangte Größe bestehen soll.\n\nEs kann daher nur oberflächlich gesagt werden, daß die Integralrechnung bloß das umgekehrte, überhaupt jedoch schwierigere Problem der Differentialrechnung sey; das reelle Interesse der Integralrechnung geht vielmehr ausschließlich auf das Verhältniß der ursprünglichen und der abgeleiteten Funktion in den konkreten Gegenständen, zu einander.\n\nLagrange ist ebenso wenig in diesem Theile des Kalkuls darauf eingegangen, die Schwierigkeit der Probleme auf die glatte Weise jener direkten Annahmen abzuthun. Es wird zur Erläuterung der Natur der Sache beitragen, gleichfalls das Nähere seines Verfahrens aus einigen wenigen Beispielen anzugeben. Dasselbe macht es sich eben zur Aufgabe, für sich zu beweisen, daß zwischen besondern Bestimmungen eines mathematischen Ganzen z.B. einer Kurve, ein Verhältniß von der ursprünglichen zu der abgeleiteten Funktion Statt finde. Dieß kann nun aber in diesem Felde vermöge der Natur des Verhältnisses selbst, welches am mathematischen Gegenstande, krumme mit geraden Linien, lineare Dimensionen und Funktionen derselben mit Ebenen-Flächen-Dimensionen und deren Funktion u.s.f. also qualitativ verschiedene in Beziehung bringt, nicht auf direkte Weise bewerkstelligt werden, die Bestimmung läßt sich so nur als die Mitte zwischen einem Größern und Kleinern auffassen. Hiermit tritt von selbst wohl wieder die Form eines Zuwachses mit Plus und Minus ein, und das rüstige: Développons, ist an seiner Stelle; aber wie die Zuwächse hier nur arithmetische, endliche Bedeutung haben, davon ist vorhin gesprochen worden. Aus der Entwicklung jener Bedingung, daß die zu bestimmende Größe größer als die eine leicht bestimmbare Grenze und kleiner als die andere sey, wird dann z.B. hergeleitet, daß die Funktion der Ordinate die abgeleitete erste Funktion zu der Funktion der Area ist.\n\nDie Rektifikation der Kurven, wie sie von Lagrange aufgezeigt wird, indem er von dem archimedischen Princip ausgeht, hat das Interesse, die Übersetzung der archimedischen Methode in das Princip der neuern Analysis einzusehen,\n\nwas einen Blick in das Innere und in den wahrhaften Sinn des auf die andere Art mechanisch betriebenen Geschäftes thun läßt. Die Verfahrungsweise ist der so eben angegebenen nothwendig analog; das archimedische Princip, daß der Bogen einer Kurve größer ist, als seine Chorde und kleiner als die Summe zweier an den Endpunkten des Bogens, gezogenen Tangenten, insoweit sie zwischen diesen Punkten und ihrem Durchschnittspunkt enthalten sind, giebt keine direkte Gleichung. Die Übertragung jener archimedischen Grundbestimmung in die moderne analytische Form ist die Erfindung eines Ausdrucks, der für sich eine einfache Grundgleichung sey, während jene Form nur die Forderung aufstellt, zwischen einem zu Großen und zu Kleinen, die sich jedesmal bestimmt haben, ins Unendliche fortzugehen, welches Fortgehen wieder immer nur ein neues zu Großes und ein neues zu Kleines jedoch in immer engern Grenzen giebt. Vermittelst des Formalismus des Unendlichkleinen wird sogleich die Gleichung dz[hoch 2] = dx[hoch 2] + dy[hoch 2] angesetzt. Die lagrangesche Exposition ausgehend von der angegebenen Grundlage zeigt hingegen auf, daß die Größe des Bogens die ursprüngliche Funktion ist zu einer abgeleiteten, von der das eigenthümliche Glied selbst eine Funktion aus dem Verhältnisse einer abgeleiteten zu der ursprünglichen der Ordinate ist.\n\nWeil in dem archimedischen Verfahren, wie dann später in der kepplerschen Behandlung stereometrischer Gegenstände, die Vorstellung vom Unendlichkleinen vorkommt, so ist dieß so oft als eine Autorität für den Gebrauch, der von dieser Vorstellung in dem Differentialkalkul gemacht wird, angeführt worden, ohne daß das Eigenthümliche und Unterscheidende herausgehoben worden wäre. Das Unendlichkleine bedeutet zunächst die Negation des Quantums als eines solchen, d. i. eines sogenannten endlichen Ausdrucks, der vollendeten Bestimmtheit, wie sie das Quantum als solches hat. Ebenso ist in den darauf folgenden berühmten Methoden des Valerius, Cavalleri u. a., die sich auf die Betrachtung der Verhältnisse geometrischer Gegenstände gründen, die Grundbestimmung, daß das Quantum als solches der Bestimmungen, welche nur im Verhältnisse zunächst betrachtet werden, für diesen Behuf auf die Seite gestellt und sie hiernach als ein Nicht-Großes sollen genommen werden. Aber Theils ist hiermit das Affirmative überhaupt, welches hinter der bloß negativen Bestimmung liegt, nicht erkannt und herausgehoben, welches sich oben abstrakt als die qualitative Größebestimmtheit, und diese bestimmter in dem Potenzenverhältnisse liegend, sich ergeben hat;—Theils aber, indem dieß Verhältniß selbst wieder eine Menge näher bestimmter Verhältnisse in sich begreift, wie das einer Potenz und deren Entwicklungsfunktion, so haben sie auch wieder auf die allgemeine und negative Bestimmung desselben Unendlichkleinen gegründet und daraus abgeleitet werden sollen. In der eben ausgehobenen lagrangeschen Exposition ist das bestimmte Affirmative, das in der archimedischen Entwicklungsweise der Aufgabe liegt, gefunden und damit dem mit einem unbegrenzten Herausgehen behafteten Verfahren seine richtige Grenze gegeben worden. Das Große der modernen Erfindung für sich und ihre Fähigkeit vorher intraktable Probleme zu lösen, und die früher lösbaren auf eine einfache Weise zu behandeln, ist allein in die Entdeckung des Verhältnisses der ursprünglichen zu den sogenannten abgeleiteten und der Theile, welche an dem mathematischen Ganzen in solchem Verhältnisse stehen, zu setzen. Die gemachten Anführungen mögen für den Zweck genügen, das Eigenthümliche des Verhältnisses von Größen herauszuheben, welches der Gegenstand der in Rede stehenden besondern Art des Kalkuls ist. Diese Anführungen konnten sich auf einfache Probleme und deren Auflösungsweisen beschränken; und weder wäre es für die Begriffsbestimmung, um die es hier allein zu thun war, zweckmäßig gewesen, noch hätte es in dem Vermögen des Verfassers gestanden, den gesammten Umfang der sogenannten Anwendung der Differential- und Integralrechnung vorzunehmen und die Induktion, daß das aufgezeigte Princip derselben zu Grunde liege, durch die Zurückführung aller ihrer Probleme und deren Lösungen darauf, zu vervollständigen. Das Beigebrachte hat aber hinreichend gezeigt, daß wie jede besondere Rechnungsweise eine besondere Bestimmtheit oder Verhältniß der Größe zu ihrem Gegenstande hat, und ein solches das Addiren, Multipliciren, das Erheben in Potenzen und Ausziehen der Wurzeln, die Rechnung mit Logarithmen, Reihen u.s.f., konstituirt, ebenso der Differential- und Integralkalkul; für das diesem Kalkul Angehörige möchte der Name des Verhältnisses einer Potenzenfunktion und der Funktion ihrer Entwicklung oder Potenzirung der passendste seyn, weil er der Einsicht der Natur der Sache am nächsten liegt. Nur wie die Operationen nach den andern Größenverhältnissen, wie Addiren u.s.f. bei diesem Kalkul überhaupt gleichfalls gebraucht werden, werden auch die Logarithmen—Kreisund Reihen-Verhältnisse angewendet, insbesondere um Ausdrücke zum Behuf der erforderlichen Operationen des Ableitens der ursprünglichen aus den Entwicklungsfunktionen traktabler zu machen. Mit der Reiheform hat die Differential- und Integralrechnung wohl das nähere Interesse geineinschaftlich, die Entwicklungsfunktionen, welche bei den Reihen die Koefficienten der Glieder heissen, zu bestimmen; aber indem das Interesse jenes Kalkuls nur auf das Verhältniß der ursprünglichen Funktion zu dem nächsten Koefficienten ihrer Entwicklung geht, will die Reihe in der nach Potenzen, die mit jenen Koefficienten versehen sind, geordneten Menge von Gliedern eine Summe darstellen. Das Unendliche, das bei der unendlichen Reihe vorkommt, der unbestimmte Ausdruck des Negativen des Quantums überhaupt, hat mit der affirmativen Bestimmung, welche im Unendlichen jenes Kalkuls liegt, nichts gemein. Ebenso ist das Unendlichkleine, als der Zuwachs, vermittelst dessen die Entwicklung in die Form der Reihe fällt, nur ein äußeres Mittel für die Entwickelung, und seine sogenannte Unendlichkeit ohne alle andere Bedeutung, als die, sonst gar keine zu haben, als die jenes Mittels; die Reihe, da sie in der That es nicht ist, die verlangt wird, führt ein Zuviel herbei, welches wieder wegzubringen, die überflüssige Mühe macht. Von dieser Mühe ist die Methode Lagrange's, der die Form der Reihe vorzugsweise wieder aufgenommen hat, gleichfalls gedrückt; obgleich sie es ist, durch welche in dem, was die Anwendung genannt wird, die wahre Eigenthümlichkeit sich heraushebt, indem ohne die Formen von dx, dy u. s.f. in die Gegenstände hinein zu zwängen, direkt derjenige Theil nachgewiesen wird, dem an ihnen die Bestimmtheit der abgeleiteten (- Entwickelungs—) Funktion zukommt, und es sich damit zeigt, daß die Form der Reihe hier nicht das ist, um das es sich handelt. [13]\n\n[13] In der obenangeführten Kritik (Jahrb. für wissensch. Krit. II. B. 1827. Nr. 155. 6. folg.) finden sich interessante Äußerungen eines gründlichen Gelehrten des Faches, Um. Spehr's, aus seinen neuen Principien des Fluentenkalkuls, Braunschw. 1826. angeführt, die nämlich einen Umstand betreffen, der wesentlich zu den Dunkelheiten und dem Unwissenschaftlichen in der Differentialrechnung beitrage, und stimmen mit dem überein, was über das allgemeine Verhältniß der Theorie dieses Kalkuls gesagt worden ist: \"man hat\" heißt es daselbst, \"rein arithmetische Untersuchungen, welche freilich von allen ähnlichen zunächst auf die Differentialrechnung Bezug haben, nicht von der eigentlichen Diff.-Rechnung gesondert, ja diese Untersuchungen wohl gar, wie Lagrange, für die Sache selbst gehalten, während man diese nur als Anwendung jener ansah. Diese arithmetischen Untersuchungen begreifen die Regeln der Differentation, die Ableitung des taylorschen Lehrsatzes u.s.w. ja selbst die verschiedenen Integrationsmethoden in sich. Es ist ganz umgekehrt der Fall, jene Anwendungen sind es gerade, welche den Gegenstand der eigentlichen Differential-Rechnung ausmachen, und alle jene arithmetischen Entwicklungen und Operationen setzt sie aus der Analysis voraus.\"—Es ist aufgezeigt worden, wie bei Lagrange die Trennung der sogenannten Anwendung von dem Verfahren des allgemeinen Theils, das von den Reihen ausgeht, eben dazu dient, die eigenthümliche Sache der Differ.-Rechnung für sich zum Vorschein zu bringen. Aber bei der interessanten Einsicht des Hrn. Vfs., daß eben die sogenannten Anwendungen es sind, welche den Gegenstand der eigentlichen Differ.-Rechnung ausmachen, ist es zu verwundern, wie derselbe sich in die (ebendas. angeführte) formelle Metaphysik von kontinuirlicher Größe, Werden, Fließen u.s.f. hat einlassen und solchen Ballast noch mit neuem gar hat vermehren wollen; formell sind diese Bestimmungen, indem sie nur allgemeine Kategorien sind, welche eben das Specifische der Sache nicht angeben, die aus den konkreten Lehren, den Anwendungen, zu erkennen und zu abstrahiren war.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0001","text":"In der vorigen Anmerkung ist Theils die Begriffsbestimmtheit des Unendlich-Kleinen, das in dem Differential-Kalkul gebraucht wird, Theils die Grundlage seiner Einführung in denselben betrachtet worden; Beides sind abstrakte und darum an sich auch leichte Bestimmungen; die sogenannte Anwendung aber bietet größere Schwierigkeiten sowohl als auch die interessantere Seite dar; die Elemente dieser konkreten Seite sollen der Gegenstand dieser Anmerkung seyn.—Die ganze Methode der Differentialrechnung ist in dem Satze, daß dx[hoch n] = nx[hoch n 1]dx, oder f(x+i)-fx/i = P, d.i. gleich dem Koefficienten des ersten Gliedes des nach den Potenzen von dx oder i entwickelten Binomiums x + d, x + i, absolvirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"74.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0002","text":"Man bedarf weiter nichts zu erlernen; die Ableitung der nächsten Formen, des Differentials eines Produkts, einer Exponentialgröße und sofort ergiebt sich daraus mechanisch; in wenig Zeit, vielleicht in einer halben Stunde—mit dem Finden der Differentiale ist das umgekehrte, das Finden der ursprünglichen Funktion aus jenen, die Integration gleichfalls gegeben,—kann man die ganze Theorie inne haben. Was allein länger aufhält, ist die Bemühung es einzusehn, begreifflich zu machen, daß nachdem der eine Umstand der Aufgabe, das Finden jenes Koefficienten, auf analytische d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"74.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0003","text":"ganz arithmetische Weise, durch die Entwickelung der Funktion der veränderlichen Größe, nachdem diese durch einen Zuwachs die Form eines Binomiums erhalten, so leicht bewerkstelligt worden, es auch mit dem andern Umstand, nämlich mit dem Weglassen der übrigen Glieder der entstehenden Reihe außer den ersten, seine Richtigkeit habe. Wäre es der Fall, daß man jenen Koefficienten allein nöthig hätte, so wäre mit der Bestimmung desselben Alles, was die Theorie betrifft, —wie gesagt in weniger als einer halben Stunde abgethan, und das Weglassen der weitern Glieder der Reihe machte so wenig eine Schwierigkeit, daß vielmehr von ihnen, als Gliedern der Reihe (als zweiten, dritten u.s.f. Funktionen ist ihre Bestimmung schon mit der Bestimmung des ersten gleichfalls absolvirt), gar nicht die Rede wäre, da es um sie ganz und gar nicht zu thun ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"74.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0004","text":"Es kann die Bemerkung vorangeschickt werden, daß man es der Methode des Differentialkalkuls wohl sogleich ansieht, daß sie nicht für sich selbst erfunden und aufgestellt worden ist; sie ist nicht nur nicht für sich begründet, als eine andere Weise analytischen Verfahrens, sondern die Gewaltsamkeit, Glieder, die sich aus Entwickelung einer Funktion ergeben, indem doch das Ganze dieser Entwickelung vollständig zur Sache zu gehören angenommen ist,—weil die Sache als der Unterschied","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"74.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0005","text":"der entwickelten Funktion einer veränderlichen Größe, nachdem dieser die Gestalt eines Binomiums gegeben worden, von der ursprünglichen, angesehen wird,—geradezu wegzulassen, widerspricht vielmehr durchaus allen mathematischen Grundsätzen. Das Bedürfniß solcher Verfahrungsweise, wie die ihr an ihr selbst mangelnde Berechtigung, weist sogleich darauf hin, daß anderswo der Ursprung und die Grundlage sich befinden müsse. Es geschieht auch sonst in den Wissenschaften, daß das, was als das Elementarische vornehin gestellt ist und woraus die Sätze der Wissenschaft abgeleitet werden sollen, nicht einleuchtend ist, und daß es sich ausweist, vielmehr in dem Nachfolgenden seine Veranlassung und seine Begründung zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"74.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0006","text":"Der Hergang in der Geschichte des Differential-Kalkuls thut dar, daß er in den verschiedenen sogenannten Tangential-Methoden vornehmlich, die Sache gleichsam als in Kunststücken, den Anfang genommen hat; die Art des Verfahrens, nachdem es auch auf weitere Gegenstande ausgedehnt worden, ist spater zum Bewußtseyn und in abstrakte Formeln gebracht worden, welche nun auch zu Principien zu erheben versucht wurde.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"74.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0007","text":"Als die Begriffsbestimmtheit des sogenannten Unendlich-Kleinen ist die qualitative Quantitäts-Bestimmtheit solcher, die zunächst als Quanta im Verhältniß zu einander gesetzt sind, aufgezeigt worden, woran sich die empirische Untersuchung knüpfte, jene Begriffs-Bestimmtheit in den Beschreibungen oder Definitionen nachzuweisen, die sich von dem Unendlich-Kleinen, insofern es als unendliche Differenz und dergleichen genommen ist, vorfinden.—Dieß ist nur im Interesse der abstrakten Begriffsbestimmtheit als solcher geschehen; die weitere Frage wäre, wie von ihr der Übergang zur mathematischen Gestaltung und Anwendung beschaffen wäre.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"74.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0008","text":"Zu dem Ende ist zuerst das Theoretische, die Begriffsbestimmtheit, noch weiter vorzunehmen, welche sich an ihr selbst nicht ganz unfruchtbar zeigen wird; alsdenn ist das Verhältniß derselben zur Anwendung zu betrachten, und bei beidem nachzuweisen, so weit es hier angeht, daß die allgeineinen Folgerungen zugleich demjenigen, um was es in der Differentialrechnung zu thun ist, und der Art, wie sie es bewerkstelligt, angemessen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"74.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0009","text":"Zunächst ist daran zu erinnern, daß die Form, welche die in Rede stehende Begriffsbestimmtheit im Mathematischen hat, bereits beiläufig angegeben ist. Die qualitative Bestimmtheit des Quantitativen ist zuerst im quantitativen Verhältniß überhaupt aufgewiesen, es ist aber auch schon bei der Nachweisung der unterschiedenen sogenannten Rechnungsarten (s. d. betreff. Anm.) anticipirt worden, daß das nachher an seiner eigenthümlichen Stelle noch zu betrachtende Potenzenverhältniß es ist, worin die Zahl durch Gleichsetzung ihrer Begriffsmomente, der Einheit und der Anzahl als zu sich selbst zurückgekehrte gesetzt ist, und damit das Moment der Unendlichkeit, des Fürsichseyns, d. i. des Bestimmtseyns durch sich selbst, an ihr erhält.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"74.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0010","text":"Die ausdrückliche qualitative Größenbestimmtheit bezieht sich somit, wie gleichfalls schon erinnert, wesentlich auf Potenzenbestimmungen, und da die Differentialrechnung das Specifische hat, mit qualitativen Größenformen zu operiren, so muß ihr eigenthümlicher mathematischer Gegenstand die Behandlung von Potenzenformen seyn, und die sämmtlichen Aufgaben und deren Auflösungen, zu deren Behuf die Differentialrechnung gebraucht wird, zeigen es, daß das Interesse allein in der Behandlung von Potenzenbestimmungen als solchen liegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"74.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0011","text":"So wichtig diese Grundlage ist, und sogleich an die Spitze etwas Bestimmtes stellt, statt der bloß formellen Kategorien von veränderlichen, kontinuirlichen oder unendlichen Größen und dergleichen, oder auch nur von Funktionen uberhaupt, so ist sie noch zu allgemein; andere Operationen haben gleichfalls damit zu thun; schon das Erheben in die Potenz und Wurzelausziehen, dann die Behandlung der Exponentialgrößen und Logarithmen, Reihen, die Gleichungen höherer Ordnungen haben ihr Interesse und ihre Bemühung allein mit Verhältnissen, die auf Potenzen beruhen. Ohne Zweifel müssen sie zusammen ein System der Potenzenbehandlung ausmachen; aber welches unter den verschiedenen Verhältnissen, worein Potenzenbestimmungen gesetzt werden können, dasjenige sey, das der eigentliche Gegenstand und das Interesse für die Differentialrechnung ist, dieß ist aus dieser selbst, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"74.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0012","text":"aus den sogenannten Anwendungen derselben zu entnehmen. Diese sind in der That die Sache selbst, das wirkliche Verfahren in der mathematischen Auflösung eines gewissen Kreises von Problemen; dieß Verfahren ist früher gewesen, als die Theorie oder der allgemeine Theil, und Anwendung ist dasselbe später genannt worden nur in Beziehung auf die nachher erschaffene Theorie, welche die allgemeine Methode des Verfahrens Theils aufstellen, Theils ihr aber Principien, d. i. Rechtfertigung geben wollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"74.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0013","text":"Welche vergebliche Bemühung es gewesen ist, für die bisherige Auffassungsweise des Verfahrens Principien aufzufinden, welche den Widerspruch, der dabei zum Vorschein kommt, wirklich lösten, statt ihn nur durch die Unbedeutenheit des nach dem mathematischen Verfahren nothwendigen hier aber wegzulassenden, oder durch die auf dasselbe hinauslaufende Möglichkeit der unendlichen oder beliebigen Annäherung und dergleichen zu entschuldigen oder zu verstecken, ist in voriger Anmerkung gezeigt worden. Wenn aus dem wirklichen Theile der Mathematik, der die Differentialrechnung genannt wird, das Allgemeine des Verfahrens anders abstrahirt würde, als bisher geschehen ist, so würden sich jene Principien und die Bemühung mit denselben auch als entbehrlich zeigen, wie sie an ihnen selbst sich als etwas Schiefes und im Widerspruche Bleibendes ausweisen.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"74.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0014","text":"Wenn wir diesem Eigenthümlichen durch einfaches Aufnehmen des in diesem Theile der Mathematik Vorhandenen nachforschen, so finden wir als Gegenstand à) Gleichungen, in welchen eine beliebige Anzahl von Größen (wir können hier überhaupt bei zwei stehen bleiben) zu einem Ganzen der Bestimmtheit so verbunden sind, daß diese erstens ihre Bestimmtheit in empirischen Größen, als festen Grenzen und dann in der Art der Verbindung mit denselben, so wie ihrer Verbindung untereinander, haben; wie dieß überhaupt in einer Gleichung der Fall ist; indem aber nur Eine Gleichung für beide Größen (und ebenso relativ wohl mehrere Gleichungen für mehrere Größen, aber immer weniger, als die Anzahl der Größen ist—) vorhanden ist, gehören diese Gleichungen zu den unbestimmten; und daß zweitens eine Seite, wie diese Größen hier ihre Bestimmtheit haben, darin liegt, daß sie (wenigstens eine derselben) in einer","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"74.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0015","text":"höhern, als die erste Potenz, in der Gleichung vorhanden sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"74.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0016","text":"Hierüber sind zunächst einige Bemerkungen zu machen, für's Erste, daß die Größen nach der ersten der angegebenen Bestimmungen ganz nur den Charakter solcher veränderlichen Größen haben, wie sie in den Aufgaben der unbestimmten Analysis vorkommen. Ihr Werth ist unbestimmt, aber so daß wenn anderswoher ein vollkommen bestimmter Werth, d. i. ein Zahlenwerth für die eine kommt, auch die andere bestimmt, so die eine, eine Funktion der andern, ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"74.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0017","text":"Die Kategorien von veränderlichen Größen, Funktionen und dergleichen sind darum für die specifische Größebestimmtheit, die hier in Rede steht, nur formell, wie vorhin gesagt worden ist, weil sie von einer Allgemeinheit sind, in welcher dasjenige Specifische, worauf das ganze Interesse des Differentialkalkuls geht, noch nicht enthalten ist, noch daraus durch Analyse explicirt werden kann; sie sind für sich einfache, unbedeutende, leichte Bestimmungen, die nur erst schwierig gemacht werden, insofern das in sie gelegt werden soll, damit es dann aus ihnen abgeleitet werden könne, was nicht in ihnen liegt, nämlich die specifische Bestimmung der Differentialrechnung.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"74.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0018","text":"—Was alsdenn die sogenannte Konstante betrifft, so kann über sie bemerkt werden, daß sie zunächst als eine gleichgültige empirische Größe ist, bestimmend für die veränderlichen Größen bloß in Ansehung ihres empirischen Quantums, als Grenze ihres Minimums und Maximums; die Art der Verbindung aber der Konstanten mit den veränderlichen Größen ist selbst eines der Momente für die Natur der besonderen Funktion, welche diese Größen sind. Umgekehrt sind aber auch die Konstanten selbst Funktionen; insofern z.B. eine gerade Linie den Sinn hat, Parameter einer Parabel zu seyn, so ist dieser ihr Sinn dieß, daß sie die Funktion y[hoch 2]/x ist; wie in der Entwickelung des Binomiums überhaupt, die Konstante, welche der Koefficient des ersten Entwickelungsgliedes ist, die Summe der Wurzeln, der des zweiten, die Summe der Produkte derselben zu zwei und zwei u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"74.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0019","text":"also diese Konstanten hier überhaupt Funktionen der Wurzeln sind; wo in der Integralrechnung die Konstante aus der gegebenen Formel bestimmt wird, wird sie insofern als eine Funktion von dieser behandelt. Jene Koefficienten werden wir dann weiter in einer anderen Bestimmung als Funktionen betrachten, deren Bedeutung im Konkreten es ist, worauf das ganze Interesse geht.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"74.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0020","text":"Das Eigenthümliche nun aber, wodurch die Betrachtung der veränderlichen Größen sich in der Differentialrechnung von ihrer Beschaffenheit in den unbestimmten Aufgaben unterscheidet, ist in das Angegebene zu setzen, daß wenigstens eine jener Größen oder auch alle sich in einer höhern Potenz als die erste befinde, wobei wieder gleichgültig ist, ob sämmtliche von derselben höhern oder von ungleichen Potenzen sind; ihre specifische Unbestimmtheit, die sie hier haben, liegt allein darin, daß sie in solchem Potenzenverhältnisse Funktionen von einander sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"74.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0021","text":"Dadurch ist die Veränderung der veränderlichen Größen qualitativ determinirt, damit kontinuirlich, und diese Kontinuität, die für sich wieder nur die formelle Kategorie überhaupt einer Identität, einer sich in der Veränderung erhaltenden, gleichbleibenden Bestimmtheit ist, hat hier ihren determinirten Sinn und zwar allein in dem Potenzenverhältnisse, als welches kein Quantum zu seinem Exponenten hat, und die nicht quantitative, bleibende Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses der veränderlichen Größen ausmacht. Daher ist gegen einen andern Formalismus die Bemerkung zu machen, daß die erste Potenz nur Potenz im Verhältniß zu höhern ist; für sich ist x nur irgend ein unbestimmtes Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"74.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0022","text":"So hat es keinen Sinn, für sich die Gleichungen y = ax + b, der geraden Linie oder s = ct die der schlechtgleichförmigen Geschwindigkeit zu differentiren; wenn aus y = ax, oder auch aus y = ax + b, a = dy/dx, oder ds/dt = c aus s = ct wird, so ist ebenso sehr a = y/x, die Bestimmung der Tangente oder s/t = c. die der schlechten Geschwindigkeit. Letztere wird als dy/dx exponirt im Zusammenhange dessen, was für die Entwickelung der gleichförmig beschleunigten Bewegung ausgegeben wird; aber daß ein Moment von einfacher, schlechtgleichförmiger, d. i. nicht durch die höhere Potenz eines der Momente der Bewegung bestimmter Geschwindigkeit, im Systeme solcher Bewegung vorkomme, ist, wie früher bemerkt, selbst eine leere, allein in der Routine der Methode gegründete Annahme.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"74.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0023","text":"Indem die Methode von der Vorstellung des Zuwachses, den die veränderliche Größe erleiden solle, ausgeht, so kann Freilich auch eine solche, die nur eine Funktion von erster Potenz ist, auch einen Zuwachs erleiden; wenn nun hierauf, um das Differential zu finden, der Unterschied der hierdurch entstandenen zweiten Gleichung von der gegebenen genommen werden soll, so zeigt sich das Leere der Operation, daß, wie bemerkt, die Gleichung vor und nach derselben, für die sogenannten Zuwächse dieselbe ist als für die veränderlichen Größen selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"74.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0024","text":"ß) Durch das Gesagte ist die Natur der zu behandelnden Gleichung bestimmt, und es ist nun anzugeben, auf welches Interesse sich die Behandlung derselben gerichtet findet. Diese Betrachtung kann nur bekannte Resultate, wie sie der Form nach in der Lagrange'schen Auffassung insbesondere vorhanden sind, geben; aber ich habe die Exposition so ganz elementarisch angestellt, um die damit vermischten heterogenen Bestimmungen zu entfernen.—Als die Grundlage der Behandlung der Gleichung von angegebener Art zeigt sich, daß die Potenz innerhalb ihrer selbst als ein Verhältniß, als ein System von Verhältnißbestimmungen, gefaßt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"74.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0025","text":"Die Potenz ist oben als die Zahl angegeben worden, insofern sie dazu gekommen ist, daß ihre Veränderung durch sie selbst bestimmt, ihre Momente, Einheit und Anzahl identisch ist, wie früher nachgewiesen, vollkommen zunächst im Quadrat, formeller, was hier keinen Unterschied macht, in den höhern Potenzen. Die Potenz nun, da sie als Zahl—wenn man den Ausdruck Größe als den allgemeinern vorzieht, so ist sie an sich immer die Zahl,—eine Menge ist, auch als Summe dargestellt, kann zunächst innerhalb ihrer in eine beliebige Menge von Zahlen zerlegt werden, die ohne alle weitere Bestimmung gegen einander und gegen ihre Summe sind, als nur daß sie zusammen dieser gleich sind. Aber die Potenz kann auch in eine Summe von solchen Unterschieden discernirt werden, die durch die Form der Potenz bestimmt sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"74.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0026","text":"Wird die Potenz als Summe genommen, so ist auch die Grundzahl derselben, die Wurzel als Summe gefaßt, und beliebig nach mannigfaltiger Zerlegung, welche Mannigfaltigkeit aber das gleichgültige empirisch-Quantitative ist. Die Summe als welche die Wurzel seyn soll, auf ihre einfache Bestimmtheit, d. i. ihre wahrhafte Allgemeinheit zurückgeführt, ist das Binomium; alle weitere Vermehrung der Glieder ist eine bloße Wiederholung derselben Bestimmung und daher etwas Leeres. [12] Worauf es ankommt, ist allein die, hiermit qualitative Bestimmtheit der Glieder, welche sich durch die Potenzirung der als Summe angenommenen Wurzel ergiebt, welche Bestimmtheit allein in der Veränderung, die das Potenziren ist, liegt. Diese Glieder sind somit ganz Funktionen der Potenzirung und der Potenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"74.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0027","text":"Jene Darstellung nun der Zahl, als Summe einer Menge von solchen Gliedern, welche Funktionen der Potenzirung sind, alsdenn das Interesse, die Form solcher Funktionen, und ferner diese Summe aus der Menge solcher Glieder, zu finden, insofern dieses Finden allein von jener Form abhängen muß,—dieß macht bekanntlich die besondere Lehre von den Reihen aus. Aber hierbei haben wir wesentlich das fernere Interesse zu unterscheiden, nämlich das Verhältniß der zu Grunde liegenden Größe selbst, deren Bestimmtheit, insofern sie ein Komplex d. i. hier eine Gleichung, ist, eine Potenz in sich schließt, —zu den Funktionen ihrer Potenzirung. Dieß Verhältniß, ganz abstrahirt von dem vorhin genannten Interesse der Summe wird sich als der Gesichtspunkt zeigen, der sich als der einzige, den die Differentialrechnung sich vorsetzt, aus der wirklichen Wissenschaft ergiebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"74.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0028","text":"[12] Es gehört nur zum Formalismus derjenigen Allgemeinheit, auf welche die Analysis nothwendigen Anspruch macht, wenn statt (a + b)[hoch n] für die Potenzenentwicklung zu nehmen, (a + b + c + d…)[hoch n] gesagt wird, wie dieß auch in vielen andern Fällen gethan wird; es ist solche Form, so zu sagen, nur für eine Koketterie des Scheins der Allgemeinheit zu halten; in dem Binomium ist die Sache erschöpft; es wird durch dessen Entwickelung das Gesetz gefunden, und das Gesetz ist die wahrhafte Allgemeinheit, nicht die äußerliche nur leere Wiederholung des Gesetzes, welche allein es ist, die durch jenes a + b + c + d… hervorgebracht wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"74.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0029","text":"Es ist jedoch vorher noch eine Bestimmung zu dem Gesagten hinzuzufügen, oder vielmehr eine, die darin liegt, zu entfernen. Es wurde nämlich gesagt, daß die veränderliche Größe, in deren Bestimmung die Potenz eintritt, angesehen werde, innerhalb ihrer selbst als Summe und zwar als ein System von Gliedern, insofern diese Funktionen der Potenzirung sind, womit auch die Wurzel als eine Summe, und in der einfach bestimmten Form als Binomium betrachtet werde; x[hoch n] = (y + z)[hoch n] = (y + ny[hoch n-1] z +….) Diese Darstellung ging für die Entwickelung der Potenz, d. i. für das Erlangen ihrer Potenzirungsfunktionen, von der Summe als solcher aus; es ist jedoch hier nicht um eine Summe als solche noch um die daraus entspringende Reihe zu thun, sondern von der Summe ist nur die Beziehung aufzunehmen.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"74.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0030","text":"Die Beziehung als solche der Größen ist das was einer Seits übrig bleibt, nachdem von dem plus einer Summa als solcher abstrahirt wird, und was anderer Seits für das Finden der EntwicklungsFunktionen der Potenz erforderlich ist. Solche Beziehung aber ist schon darin bestimmt, daß hier der Gegenstand eine Gleichung, y[hoch m] = ax[hoch n] auch schon ein Komplex von mehrern (veränderlichen) Größen ist, der eine Potenzenbestimmung derselben enthält. In diesem Komplex ist jede dieser Größen schlechthin als in der Beziehung auf die andere mit der Bedeutung, könnte man sagen, eines plus an ihr selbst,—als Funktion der andern Größen gesetzt; ihr Charakter, Funktionen von einander zu seyn, giebt ihnen diese Bestimmung des plus, eben damit aber eines ganz unbestimmten, nicht eines Zuwachses, Inkrements und dergleichen.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"74.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0031","text":"Doch diesen abstrakten Gesichtspunkt konnten wir auch auf der Seite lassen; es kann ganz einfach dabei stehen geblieben werden, daß nachdem die veränderlichen Größen in der Gleichung als Funktionen von einander, so daß diese Bestimmtheit ein Verhältniß von Potenzen enthält, gegeben sind, nun auch die Funktionen der Potenzirung einer jeden mit einander verglichen werden,—welche zweiten Funktionen durch gar nichts Anderes weiter als durch die Potenzirung selbst bestimmt sind. Es kann zunächst für ein Belieben oder eine Möglichkeit ausgegeben werden, eine Gleichung von den Potenzen ihrer veränderlichen Größen auf ein Verhältniß ihrer Entwickelungsfunktionen zu setzen; ein weiterer Zweck, Nutzen, Gebrauch hat erst das Dienliche solcher Umgestaltung davon anzugeben; durch ihre Nützlichkeit allein ist jene Umstellung veranlaßt worden.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"74.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0032","text":"Wenn vorhin von der Darstellung dieser Potenzirungsbestimungen an einer Größe, die als Summe in sich different genommen werde, ausgegangen worden, so diente dieß nur Theils zur Angabe von welcher Art solche Funktionen seyen, Theils liegt darin die Weise sie zu finden.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"74.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0033","text":"Wir befinden uns hiermit bei der gewöhnlichen analytischen Entwickelung, die für den Zweck der Differentialrechnung so gefaßt wird, daß der veränderlichen Größe ein Zuwachs, dx, i gegeben und nun die Potenz des Binomiums durch die Gliederreihe, die ihm angehört, explicirt wird. Der sogenannte Zuwachs aber soll nicht ein Quantum, nur eine Form seyn, deren ganzer Werth ist, zur Entwickelung behülflich zu seyn; was man eingestandenermaßen, am bestimmtesten von Euler und Lagrange, und in der früher erwähnten Vorstellung der Grenze, will, sind nur die sich ergebende Potenzenbestimmungen der veränderlichen Größen, die sogenannten Koefficienten zwar des Zuwachses und der Potenzen desselben, nach denen die Reihe sich ordnet und zu denen die unterschiedenen Koefficienten gehören.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"74.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0034","text":"Es kann hierzu etwa bemerkt werden, daß indem nur um der Entwickelung willen ein Zuwachs angenommen ist, der ohne Quantum sey, es am geschicktesten gewesen wäre, (das Eins) dafür zu nehmen, indem derselbe in der Entwickelung immer nur als Faktor vorkommt, womit eben der Faktor Eins den Zweck erfüllt, daß keine quantitative Bestimmtheit und Veränderung durch den Zuwachs gesetzt werden solle; dagegen dx mit der falschen Vorstellung von einer quantitativen Differenz, und andere Zeichen, wie i, mit dem hier unnützen Scheine von Allgemeinheit behafftet, immer das Aussehen und die Prätension von einem Quantum und dessen Potenzen haben; welche Prätension dann die Mühe herbeibringt, sie dessenungeachtet wegzubringen und wegzulassen. Um die Form einer nach Potenzen entwickelten Reihe zu behalten, könnten die Exponentenbezeichnungen als indices ebenso gut dem Eins angefügt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"74.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0035","text":"Aber es muß ohnehin von der Reihe und von der Bestimmung der Koefficienten nach der Stelle, die sie in der Reihe haben, abstrahirt werden, das Verhältniß zwischen allen ist dasselbe; die zweite Funktion wird ganz ebenso aus der ersten, als diese aus der ursprünglichen abgeleitet, und für die als die zweite gezählte ist die erste abgeleitete wieder ursprüngliche Funktion. Wesentlich aber geht das Interesse nicht auf die Reihe, sondern ganz allein auf die sich aus der Entwickelung ergebende Potenzenbestimmung in ihrem Verhältniß zu der für sie unmittelbaren Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"74.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0036","text":"Anstatt also jene als den Koefficienten des ersten Gliedes der Entwickelung zu bestimmen, da ein Glied als das erste in Beziehung auf die andern in der Reihe folgenden bezeichnet wird, eine solche Potenz als eines Zuwachses aber, wie die Reihe selbst hierher nicht gehören, wäre der bloße Ausdruck abgeleitete Potenzenfunktion oder wie vorhin gesagt wurde, eine Funktion des Potenzirens der Größe vorzuziehen, wobei als bekannt vorausgesetzt wird, auf welche Weise die Ableitung als innerhalb einer Potenz eingeschlossene Entwickelung genommen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"74.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0037","text":"Wenn nun der eigentliche mathematische Anfang in diesem Theile der Analytik nichts weiter ist, als das Finden der durch die Potenzen-Entwickelung bestimmten Funktion, so ist die weitere Frage, was mit dem damit erhaltenen Verhältnisse anzufangen ist, wo es eine Anwendung und Gebrauch hat, oder in der That, für welchen Zweck solche Funktionen gesucht werden. Durch das Finden von Verhältnissen, an konkreten Gegenständen, welche sich auf jene abstrakte analytische zurückführen lassen, hat die Differentialrechnung ihr großes Interesse erhalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"74.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0038","text":"Über die Anwendbarkeit aber ergiebt sich zunächst aus der Natur der Sache, ohne noch aus den Fällen der Anwendung selbst zu schließen, vermöge der aufgezeigten Gestalt der Potenzenmomente, von selbst Folgendes. Die Entwickelung der Potenzengrößen, wodurch sich die Funktionen ihrer Potenzirung ergeben, enthält, von näherer Bestimmung abstrahirt, zunächst überhaupt die Herabsetzung der Größe auf die nächst niedrigere Potenz. Die Anwendbarkeit dieser Operation findet also bei solchen Gegenständen statt, bei welchen gleichfalls ein solcher Unterschied von Potenzenbestimmungen vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"74.38"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0039","text":"Wenn wir nun auf die Raumbestimmtheit reflektiren, so finden wir, daß sie die drei Dimensionen enthält, die wir, um sie von den abstrakten Unterschieden der Höhe, Länge und Breite zu unterscheiden, als die konkreten bezeichnen können, nämlich die Linie, die Fläche und den totalen Raum; und indem sie in ihren einfachsten Formen und in Beziehung auf Selbstbestimmung und damit auf analytische Dimensionen genommen werden, haben wir die gerade Linie, die ebene Fläche und dieselbe als Quadrat, und den Kubus. Die gerade Linie hat ein empirisches Quantum, aber mit der Ebene tritt das Qualitative, die Potenzenbestimmung ein; nähere Modificationen, z.B. daß dieß gleich auch mit den ebenen Kurven geschieht, können wir, insofern es zunächst um den Unterschied bloß im Allgemeinen zu thun ist, unerörtert lassen.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"74.39"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0040","text":"Hiermit entsteht auch das Bedürfniß, von einer höheren Potenzenbestimmung zu einer niedrigern und umgekehrt überzugehen, indem z.B. lineare Bestimmungen aus gegebenen Gleichungen der Fläche u.s.f. oder umgekehrt abgeleitet werden sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"74.40"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0041","text":"—Die Bewegung ferner, als an der das Größenverhältniß des durchloffenen Raumes und der dazu gehörigen verflossenen Zeit zu betrachten ist, zeigt sich in den verschiedenen Bestimmungen einer schlechtgleichförmigen, einer gleichförmig beschleunigten, einer abwechselnd gleichförmig beschleunigten und gleichförmig retardirten, —in sich zurückkehrenden Bewegung; indem diese unterschiedenen Arten der Bewegung nach dem Größenverhältnisse ihrer Momente, des Raums und der Zeit, ausgedrückt werden, ergeben sich für sie Gleichungen aus unterschiedenen Potenzenbestimmungen, und insofern es Bedürfniß seyn kann, eine Art der Bewegung oder auch der Raumgrößen, an welche eine Art gebunden ist, aus einer anderen Art derselben zu bestimmen, führt die Operation gleichfalls das Übergehen von einer Potenzenfunktion zu einer höhern oder medrigern herbei.—Die Beispiele dieser zwei Gegenstände mögen für den","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"74.41"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0042","text":"Zweck, zu dem sie angeführt sind, genügen.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"74.42"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0043","text":"Der Anschein von Zufälligkeit, welchen die Differentialrechnung in ihren Anwendungen präsentirt, würde schon vereinfacht werden, durch das Bewußtseyn über die Natur der Gebiete, in welchem die Anwendung statt finden kann, und über das eigenthümliche Bedürfniß und die Bedingung dieser Anwendung. Nun aber kommt es weiter innerhalb dieser Gebiete selbst darauf an, zu wissen, zwischen welchen Theilen der Gegenstände der mathematischen Aufgabe ein solches Verhältniß statt finde, als durch den Differentialkalkul eigenthümlich gesetzt wird. Es muß gleich vorläufig bemerkt werden, daß hierbei zweierlei Verhältnisse zu beachten sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"74.43"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0044","text":"Die Operation des Depotenzirens einer Gleichung, sie nach den abgeleiteten Funktionen ihrer veränderlichen Größen betrachtet, giebt ein Resultat, welches an ihm selbst wahrhaft nicht mehr eine Gleichung, sondern ein Verhältniß ist; dieses Verhältniß ist der Gegenstand der eigentlichen Differentialrechnung. Eben damit auch ist zweitens das Verhältniß vorhanden von der höhern Potenzenbestimmung (der ursprünglichen Gleichung) selbst zu der niedrigern (dem Abgeleiteten). Dieß zweite Verhältniß haben wir hier zunächst bei Seite zu lassen; es wird sich als der eigenthüniliche Gegenstand der Integralrechnung zeigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"74.44"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0045","text":"Betrachten wir zunächst das erste Verhältniß, und nehmen zu der aus der sogenannten Anwendung zu entnehmenden Bestimmung des Moments, worin das Interesse der Operation liegt, das einfachste Beispiel an den Kurven vor, die durch eine Gleichung der zweiten Potenz bestimmt sind. Bekanntlich ist unmittelbar durch die Gleichung das Verhältniß der Koordinaten gegeben in einer Potenzenbestimmung. Folgen von der Grundbestimmung sind die Bestimmungen der mit den Koordinaten zusammenhängenden anderen geraden Linien, der Tangente, Subtangente, Normale u.s.f. Die Gleichungen aber zwischen diesen Linien und den Koordinaten sind lineare Gleichungen; die Ganzen, als deren Theile diese Linien bestimmt sind, sind rechtwinklichte Dreiecke von geraden Linien.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"74.45"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0046","text":"Der Übergang von der Grundgleichung, welche die Potenzenbestimmung enthält, zu jenen linearen Gleichungen enthält nun den angegebenen Übergang von der ursprünglichen Funktion, d. i. welche eine Gleichung ist, zu der abgeleiteten, welche ein Verhältniß ist, und zwar zwischen gewissen in der Kurve enthaltenen Linien. Der Zusammenhang zwischen dem Verhältnisse dieser Linien und der Gleichung der Curve ist es, um dessen Finden es sich handelt.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"74.46"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0047","text":"Es ist nicht ohne Interesse, von dem Historischen hierüber so viel zu bemerken, daß die ersten Entdecker ihren Fund nur auf eine ganz empirische Weise anzugeben wissen, ohne eine Rechenschaft von der völlig äußerlich gebliebenen Operation geben zu können. Ich begnüge mich hierüber mit der Anführung Barrow's, des Lehrers Newtons. In seinen lect. Opt. et Geom., worin er Probleme der höhern Geometrie nach der Methode der Untheilbaren behandelt, die sich zunächst von dem Eigenthümlichen der Differentialrechnung unterscheidet, giebt er auch, \"weil seine Freunde in ihn gedrungen,\" (lect. X.) sein Verfahren, die Tangente zu bestimmen, an.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"74.47"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0048","text":"Man muß bei ihm selbst nachlesen, wie diese Angabe beschaffen ist, um sich eine gehörige Vorstellung zu machen, wie das Verfahren ganz als äußerliche Regel angegeben ist,—in demselben Style, wie vormals in den arithmetischen Schulbüchern die Regel de tri oder noch besser die sogenannte Neunerprobe der Rechnungsarten vorgetragen worden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"74.48"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0049","text":"Er macht die Verzeichnung der Linienchen, die man nachher die Inkremente im charakteristischen Dreieck einer Kurve genannt hat, und giebt nun die Vorschrift als eine bloße Regel, die Glieder als überflüssig wegzuwerfen, die in Folge der Entwickelung der Gleichungen, als Potenzen jener Inkremente oder Produkte zum Vorschein kommen, ( etenim isti termini nihilum valebunt ); ebenso seyen die Glieder, die nur aus der ursprünglichen Gleichung bestimmte Größen enthalten, wegzuwerfen (das nachherige Abziehen der ursprünglichen Gleichung von der mit den Inkrementen gebildeten) und zuletzt für das Inkrement der Ordinate die Ordinate selbst und für das Inkrement der Abscisse die Subtangente zu substituiren.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"74.49"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0050","text":"Man kann, wenn es so zu reden erlaubt ist, das Verfahren nicht schulmeistermässiger angeben;—die letztere Substitution ist die für die Tangentenbestimmung in der gewöhnlichen Differentialmethode zur Grundlage gemachte Annahme der Proportionalität der Inkremente der Ordinate und Abscisse mit der Ordinate und Subtangente; in Barrows Regel erscheint diese Annahme in ihrer ganz naiven Nacktheit. Eine einfache Weise, die Subtangente zu bestimmen, war gefunden; die Manieren Robervals und Fermats laufen auf Ähnliches hinaus,—die Methode, die größten und kleinsten Werthe zu finden, von der der Letztere ausging, beruht auf denselben Grundlagen und demselben Verfahren. Es war eine mathematische Sucht jener Zeiten, sogenannte Methoden, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"74.50"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0051","text":"Regeln jener Art zu finden, dabei aus ihnen auch ein Geheimniß zu machen, was nicht nur leicht, sondern selbst in einer Rücksicht nöthig war, aus demselben Grunde, als es leicht war,—nämlich weil die Erfinder nur eine empirische äußerliche Regel, keine Methode, d. i. nichts aus anerkannten Principien Abgeleitetes, gefunden hatten. Solche sogenannte Methoden hat Leibnitz von seiner Zeit, und Newton ebenfalls von derselben und unmittelbarer von seinem Lehrer aufgenommen; sie haben durch die Verallgemeinerung ihrer Form und Anwendbarkeit den Wissenschaften neue Bahnen gebrochen, aber damit zugleich das Bedürfniß gehabt, das Verfahren aus der Gestalt bloß äußerlicher Regeln zu reißen, und demselben die erforderliche Berechtigung zu verschaffen gesucht.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"74.51"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0052","text":"Analysiren wir die Methode näher, so ist der wahrhafte Vorgang dieser. Es werden erstlich die Potenzenbestimmungen (versteht sich der veränderlichen Größen), welche die Gleichung enthält, auf ihre ersten Funktionen herabgesetzt. Damit aber wird der Werth der Glieder der Gleichung verändert; es bleibt daher keine Gleichung mehr, sondern es ist nur ein Verhältniß entstanden zwischen der ersten Funktion der einen veränderlichen Größe zu der ersten Funktion der andern; statt px = y[hoch 2] hat man p : 2y oder statt 2 ax—x[hoch 2] = y[hoch 2] hat man a—x : y, was nachher als das Verhältniß dy/dx bezeichnet zu werden pflegte.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"74.52"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0053","text":"Die Gleichung ist Gleichung der Curve, dieß Verhältniß, das ganz von derselben abhängig, aus derselben (oben nach einer bloßen Regel) abgeleitet ist, ist dagegen ein lineares, mit welchem gewisse Linien in Proportion sind; p : 2y oder a—x : y sind selbst Verhältnisse aus geraden Linien der Kurve, den Koordinaten und den Parameters; aber damit weiß man noch nichts. Das Interesse ist, von andern an der Kurve vorkommenden Linien zu wissen, daß ihnen jenes Verhältniß zukommt, die Gleichheit zweier Verhältnisse zu finden.—Es ist also zweitens die Frage, welches die geraden, durch die Natur der Kurve bestimmten Linien sind, welche in solchem Verhältnisse stehen?—dieß aber ist es, was schon früher bekannt war, daß nämlich solches auf jenem Wege erhaltenes Verhältniß das Verhältniß der Ordinate zur Subtangente ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"74.53"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0054","text":"dieß hatten die Alten auf sinnreichem geometrischen Wege gefunden; was die neuern Erfinder entdeckt haben, ist das empirische Verfahren, die Gleichung der Kurve so zuzurichten, daß jenes erste Verhältniß geliefert wird, von dem bereits bekannt war, daß es einem Verhältnisse gleich ist, welches die Linie enthält, hier die Subtangente, um deren Bestimmung es zu thun ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"74.54"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0055","text":"Theils ist nun jene Zurichtung der Gleichung methodisch gefaßt und gemacht worden,—die Differentation,—Theils aber sind die imaginären Inkremente der Koordinaten und das imaginäre hieraus und einem ebensolchen Inkremente der Tangente gebildete, charakteristische Dreieck erfunden worden, damit die Proportionalität des durch die Depotenzirung der Gleichung gefundenen Verhältnisses mit dem Verhältnisse der Ordinate und der Subtangente nicht als etwas empirisch nur aus der alten Bekanntschaft Aufgenommenes, sondern als ein Erwiesenes dargestellt werde. Die alte Bekanntschaft jedoch erweist sich überhaupt und am unverkennbarsten in der angeführten Form von Regeln als die einzige Veranlassung und respektive Berechtigung der Annahme des charakteristischen Dreiecks und jener Proportionalität.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"74.55"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0056","text":"Lagrange hat nun diese Simulation verworfen, und den ächtwissenschaftlichen Weg eingeschlagen; seiner Methode ist die Einsicht zu verdanken, worauf es ankommt, indem sie darin besteht, die beiden Übergänge, die für die Auflösung der Aufgabe zu machen sind, zu trennen und jede dieser Seiten für sich zu behandeln und zu erweisen. Der eine Theil dieser Auflösung,—indem wir für die nähere Angabe des Ganges bei dem Beispiele der elementarischen Aufgabe, die Subtangente zu finden, bleiben,—der theoretische oder allgemeine Theil, nämlich das Finden der ersten Funktion aus der gegebenen Kurvengleichung, wird für sich regulirt; derselbe giebt ein lineares Verhältniß, also von geraden Linien, die in dem Systeme der Kurvenbestimmung vorkommen. Der andere Theil der Auflösung ist nun die Findung derjenigen Linien an der Kurve, welche in jenem Verhältnisse stehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"74.56"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0057","text":"Dieß wird nun auf die direkte Weise (Théorie des Fonct. Anal. II. P. II. Chap.) bewerkstelligt, d. i. ohne das charakteristische Dreieck, nämlich ohne unendlichkleine Bogen, Ordinaten und Abscissen anzunehmen und diesen die Bestimmungen von dy und dx, d. i. von den Seiten jenes Verhältnisses und zugleich unmittelbar die Bedeutung der Gleichheit desselben mit der Ordinate und Subtangente selbst zu geben. Eine Linie (wie auch ein Punkt) hat allein ihre Bestimmung, insofern sie die Seite eines Dreiecks ausmacht, wie auch die Bestimmmung eines Punkts nur in einem solchen liegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"74.57"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0058","text":"Dieß ist, um es ini Vorbeigehen zu erwähnen, der Fundamentalsatz der analytischen Geometrie, welcher die Coordinaten, wie, was dasselbe ist, in der Mechanik das Parallelogramm der Kräfte herbeiführt, das eben darum der vielen Bemühung um einen Beweis ganz unbedürftig ist.—Die Subtangente wird nun als die Seite eines Dreiecks gesetzt, dessen weitere Seiten die Ordinate und die darauf sich beziehende Tangente ist. Letztere hat als gerade Linie zu einer Gleichung p = aq, (+ b hinzuzufügen ist für die Bestimmung unnütz und wird nur um der beliebten Allgemeinheit hinzugesetzt);—die Determination des Verhältnisses p/q fällt in a, den Koefficienten von q, der die respective erste Funktion der Gleichung ist, überhaupt aber nur als a = p/q betrachtet zu werden braucht als, wie gesagt, die wesentliche Determination der geraden Linie, die als Tangente an die Kurve applicirt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"74.58"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0059","text":"Indem nun ferner die erste Funktion der Kurvengleichung genommen wird, ist sie ebenso die Determination einer geraden Linie; indem ferner die eine Koordinate p der ersten geraden Linie und y, die Ordinate der Kurve, als dieselben genommen werden, daß also der Punkt, in welchem jene als Tangente angenommene erste gerade die Kurve berührt, gleichfalls der Anfangspunkt der durch die erste Funktion der Kurve bestimmten geraden Linie ist, so kommt es darauf an, zu zeigen, daß diese zweite gerade Linie mit der ersten zusammenfällt, d. h. Tangente ist; algebraisch ausgedrückt, daß indem y = fx und p = Fq ist, und nun y = p, also fx = Fq angenommen wird, auch f'x = F'q.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"74.59"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0060","text":"Daß nun die als Tangente applicirte gerade, und jene aus der Gleichung durch deren erste Funktion determinirte gerade Linie zusammenfallen, daß die letztere also Tangente ist; dieß wird mit Zuhilfnahme des Increments i der Abscisse und des durch die Entwickelung der Funktion bestimmten Increments der Ordinate gezeigt. Hier kommt denn also gleichfalls das berüchtigte Increment herein; aber wie es zu dem so eben angegebenen Behufe eingeführt wird, und die Entwickelung der Funktion nach demselben, muß von dem früher erwähnten Gebrauch des Inkrements für das Finden der Differentialgleichung und für das charakteristische Dreieck, wohl unterschieden werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"74.60"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0061","text":"Der hier gemachte Gebrauch ist berechtigt und nothwendig; er fällt in den Umkreis der Geometrie, indem es zur geometrischen Bestimmung einer Tangente als solcher gehört, daß zwischen ihr und der Kurve, mit der sie einen Punkt gemeinschaftlich hat, keine andere gerade Linie, die gleichfalls in diesen Punkt fiele, durchgehen könne. Denn mit dieser Bestimmung ist die Qualität der Tangente oder Nicht-Tangente auf den Größenunterschied zurückgeführt, und diejenige Linie ist die Tangente, auf welche die größere Kleinheit—schlechthin in Ansehung der Determination, auf welche es ankommt, falle. Diese scheinbar nur relative Kleinheit enthält durchaus nichts Empirisches, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"74.61"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0062","text":"von einem Quantum als solchem Abhängiges, sie ist qualitativ durch die Natur der Formel gesetzt, wenn der Unterschied des Moments, von dem die zu vergleichende Größe abhängt, ein Potenzenunterschied ist; indem derselbe auf i und i[hoch 2] hinauskommt, und i, das zuletzt doch eine Zahl bedeuten soll, dann als ein Bruch vorzustellen ist, so ist i[hoch 2] an und für sich kleiner als i, so daß selbst die Vorstellung von einer beliebigen Größe, in der man i nehmen könne, hier überflüssig und sogar nicht an ihrem Orte ist. Ebendamit hat der Erweis der größern Kleinheit nichts mit einem Unendlich-Kleinen zu thun, das hiermit hier keineswegs hereinzukommen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"74.62"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0063","text":"Wäre es auch nur um der Schönheit und des heutigstags mehr vergessen, aber wohlverdienten Ruhmes willen, daß ich noch Descartes Tangentenmethode anführen will; sie hat übrigens auch eine Beziehung auf die Natur der Gleichungen, über welche dann noch eine fernere Bemerkung zu machen ist. Descartes trägt diese selbstständige Methode, worin die geforderte lineare Bestimmung gleichfalls aus derselben abgeleiteten Funktion gefunden wird, in seiner, sonst auch so fruchtbar gewordenen Geometrie (liv. II. p. 357 ss. Oeuvres compl. ed. Cousin Tom. V.) vor, indem er in derselben die große Grundlage von der Natur der Gleichungen und deren geometrischer Konstruktion und der damit sosehr erweiterten Analysis auf die Geometrie überhaupt, gelehrt hat. Das Problem hat bei ihm die Form der Aufgabe, gerade Linien senkrecht auf beliebige Orte einer Kurve zu ziehen, als wodurch Subtangente u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"74.63"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0064","text":"bestimmt wird; man begreift die Befriedigung, die er daselbst über seine Entdeckung, die einen Gegenstand von allgemeinem wissenschaftlichen Interesse der damaligen Zeit betraf, und die sosehr geometrisch ist und dadurch so hoch über den oben erwähnten bloßen Regelmethoden seiner Nebenbuhler stand, ausdrückt: j'ose dire que c'est ceci le problème le plus utile et le plus général, non seulement que je sache, mais même que j'aie jamais desire de savoir en géometrie.—Er legt für die Auflösung die analytische Gleichung des rechtwinklichten Dreiecks zu Grund, das durch die Ordinate des Punkts der Kurve, auf welcher die im Probleme verlangte gerade Linie senkrecht seyn soll, dann durch diese selbst, die Normale, und drittens durch den Theil der Achse, der durch die Ordinate und Normale abgeschnitten wird, durch die Subnormale, gebildet wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"74.64"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0065","text":"Aus der bekannten Gleichung einer Kurve wird nun in jene Gleichung des Dreiecks der Werth es sey der Ordinate oder der Abscisse substituirt, so hat man eine Gleichung des zweiten Grades (und Descartes zeigt, wie auch Kurven, deren Gleichungen höhere Grade enthalten, sich hierauf zurückführen), in welcher nur noch die eine der veränderlichen Größen und zwar im Quadrat und in der ersten Potenz vorkommt;—eine quadratische Gleichung, welche zunächst als eine sogenannte unreine erscheint.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"74.65"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0066","text":"Nun macht Descartes die Reflexion, daß wenn der auf der Kurve angenommene Punkt als Durchschnittspunkt derselben und eines Kreises vorgestellt wird, dieser Kreis die Kurve noch in einem anderen Punkte schneiden wird, und alsdenn sich für die zwei damit entstehenden und ungleichen x, zwei Gleichungen mit denselben Konstanten und von derselben Form ergeben;—oder aber nur Eine Gleichung mit ungleichen Werthen von x. Die Gleichung wird aber nur Eine, für das Eine Dreieck, in welchem die Hypotenuse auf die Kurve senkrecht, Normale, ist, was so vorgestellt wird, daß man die beiden Durchschnittspunkte der Kurve durch den Kreis, zusammenfallen, diesen also die Kurve berühren lasse. Damit aber fällt auch der Umstand der ungleichen Wurzeln des x oder y der quadratischen Gleichung hinweg.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"74.66"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0067","text":"Bei einer quadratischen Gleichung von zwei gleichen Wurzeln nun aber ist der Koefficient des Gliedes, das die Unbekannte in der ersten Potenz enthält, das Doppelte der nur Einen Wurzel; dieß nun giebt eine Gleichung, durch welche die verlangten Bestimmungen gefunden sind. Dieser Gang ist für den genialen Griff eines ächt analytischen Kopfes anzusehen, wogegen die ganz assertorisch angenommene Proportionalität der Subtangente und der Ordinate mit den unendlich klein seyn sollenden sogenannten Inkrementen der Abscisse und der Ordinate ganz zurücksteht.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"74.67"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0068","text":"Die auf die angegebene Weise erhaltene Endgleichung, welche den Koefficienten des zweiten Gliedes der quadratischen Gleichung gleichsetzt der doppelten Wurzel oder Unbekannten, ist dieselbe, welche durch das Verfahren des Differentialkalkuls gefunden wird. x[hoch 2]—ax—b = 0 differentiirt giebt die neue Gleichung 2x—a = 0; oder x[hoch 3]—px—q = 0 giebt 3x[hoch 2]—p = 0. Es bietet sich hierbei aber die Bemerkung an, daß es sich keineswegs von selbst versteht, daß solche abgeleitete Gleichung auch","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"74.68"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0069","text":"richtig ist. Bei einer Gleichung mit zwei veränderlichen Größen, die darum, daß sie veränderliche sind, den Charakter unbekannte Größen zu seyn nicht verlieren, kommt, wie oben betrachtet wurde, nur ein Verhältniß heraus, aus dem angegebenen einfachen Grunde, weil durch das Substituiren der Funktionen der Potenzirung an die Stelle der Potenzen selbst der Werth der beiden Glieder der Gleichung verändert wird, und es für sich selbst noch unbekannt ist, ob auch zwischen ihnen bei so veränderten Werthen noch eine Gleichung Statt finde. Die Gleichung dy/dx = P drückt gar nichts weiter aus, als daß P ein Verhältniß ist, und es ist dem dy/dx sonst kein reeller Sinn zuzuschreiben.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"74.69"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0070","text":"Von diesem Verhältniß = P ist es aber ebenso noch unbekannt, welchem andere Verhältnisse es gleich sey; solche Gleichung, die Proportionalität, giebt demselben erst einen Werth und Bedeutung.—Wie angegeben wurde, daß man diese Bedeutung, was die Anwendung hieß, anderswoher, empirisch aufnahm, so muß bei den hier in Rede stehenden durch Differentation abgeleiteten Gleichungen anderswoher gewußt werden, ob sie gleiche Wurzeln haben, um zu wissen, ob die erhaltene Gleichung noch richtig sey. Dieser Umstand wird aber in den Lehrbüchern nicht ausdrücklich bemerklich gemacht; er wird wohl dadurch beseitigt, daß eine Gleichung mit einer unbekannten, auf Null gebracht, sogleich y gesetzt wird, wodurch dann bei der Differentation allerdings ein dy/dx, nur ein Verhältniß herauskommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"74.70"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0071","text":"Der Funktionen-Kalkul soll es allerdings mit Funktionen der Potenzirung oder die Differentialrechnung mit Differentialien zu thun haben, aber daraus folgt für sich noch keineswegs, daß die Größen, deren Differentialien oder Funktionen der Potenzirung genommen werden, selbst auch nur Funktionen anderer Größen seyn sollen. In dem theoretischen Theile, der Anweisung, die Differentiale, d. i. die Funktionen der Potenzirung abzuleiten, wird ohnehin noch nicht daran gedacht, daß die Größen, die nach solcher Ableitung zu behandeln gelehrt wird, selbst Funktionen anderer Größen seyn sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"74.71"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0072","text":"Noch kann in Ansehung des Weglassens der Konstante bei dem Differentiiren bemerklich gemacht werden, daß dasselbe hier den Sinn hat, daß die Konstante für die Bestimmung der Wurzeln im Falle ihrer Gleichheit gleichgültig ist, als welche Bestimmung durch den Koefficienten des zweiten Gliedes der Gleichung erschöpft ist. Wie im angeführten Beispiele von Descartes die Konstante das Quadrat der Wurzeln selbst ist, also diese aus der Konstante ebenso wie aus den Koefficienten, bestimmt werden kann; indem sie überhaupt, wie die Koefficienten, Funktion der Wurzeln der Gleichung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"74.72"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0073","text":"In der gewöhnlichen Darstellung erfolgt das Wegfallen der sogenannten nur durch + und—mit den übrigen Gliedern verbundenen Konstanten durch den bloßen Mechanismus des Verfahrens, daß um das Differential eines zusammengesetzten Ausdrucks zu finden, nur den veränderlichen Größen ein Zuwachs gegeben, und der hierdurch formirte Ausdruck von dem ursprünglichen abgezogen wird. Der Sinn der Konstanten und ihres Weglassens inwiefern sie selbst Funktionen sind und nach dieser Bestimmung dienen oder nicht, kommt nicht zur Sprache.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"74.73"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0074","text":"Mit dem Weglassen der Konstanten, hängt eine ähnliche Bemerkung zusammen, die über die Namen von Differentation und Integration, gemacht werden kann, als früher über den endlichen und unendlichen Ausdruck gemacht wurde, daß nämlich in ihrer Bestimmung vielmehr das Gegentheil von dem liegt, was der Ausdruck besagt. Differentiiren bezeichnet das Setzen von Differenzen; durch das Differentiiren aber wird eine Gleichung vielmehr auf weniger Dimensionen herabgebracht, durch das Weglassen der Konstante wird ein Moment der Bestimmtheit hinweggenommen; wie bemerkt, werden die Wurzeln der veränderlichen Größe auf eine Gleichheit gesetzt, die Differenz also derselben aufgehoben.","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"74.74"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0075","text":"In der Integration hingegen soll die Konstante wieder hinzugesetzt werden; die Gleichung wird dadurch allerdings, aber in dem Sinne integrirt, daß die vorher aufgehobene Differenz der Wurzeln wieder hergestellt, das Gleichgesetzte wieder differentiirt wird. —Der gewöhnliche Ausdruck trägt dazu bei, die wesentliche Natur der Sache in Schatten zu setzen und Alles auf den untergeordneten, ja der Hauptsache fremdartigen Gesichtspunkt Theils der unendlich kleinen Differenz, des Increments und dergleichen, Theils der bloßen Differenz überhaupt zwischen der gegebenen und der abgeleiteten Funktion, ohne deren specifischen, d. i. den qualitativen Unterschied zu bezeichnen, zu stellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"74.75"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0076","text":"Ein anderes Hauptgebiet, in welchem von dem Differentialkalkul Gebrauch gemacht wird, ist die Mechanik; von den unterschiedenen Potenzen-Funktionen, die sich bei den elementarischen Gleichungen ihres Gegenstandes, der Bewegung ergeben, sind deren Bedeutungen bereits beiläufig erwähnt; ich will dieselben hier direkt aufnehmen.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"74.76"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0077","text":"Die Gleichung, nämlich der mathematische Ausdruck, der schlechtgleichförmigen Bewegung c = s/t oder s = ct, in welcher die durch offenen Räume den verflossenen Zeiten nach einer empirischen Einheit c, der Größe der Geschwindigkeit, proportionirt sind, bietet für die Differentation keinen Sinn dar; der Koefficient c ist bereits vollkommen bestimmt und bekannt, und es kann keine weitere Potenzenentwicklung Statt finden.—Wie s = at[hoch 2], die Gleichung der Bewegung des Falles, analysirt wird, ist früher schon erinnert; —das erste Glied der Analyse ds/dt = 2 at wird in die Sprache und resp. in die Existenz so übersetzt, es solle ein Glied einer Summe (- welche Vorstellung wir längst entfernt haben), der eine Theil der Bewegung seyn und zwar solle dieser der Kraft der Trägheit, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"74.77"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0078","text":"einer schlechtgleichförmigen Geschwindigkeit so zukommen, daß in den unendlich-kleinen Zeittheilen die Bewegung gleichförmig, in den endlichen Zeittheilen d. h. in der That existirenden aber ungleichförmig sey. Freilich ist fs = 2at; und die Bedeutung voll a und von t für sich bekannt, so wie daß hiermit die Bestimmung von gleichförmiger Geschwindigkeit einer Bewegung gesetzt ist; da a = s/[t[hoch 2]] ist 2 at = 2s/t überhaupt; damit aber weiß man im geringsten nichts weiter; nur die fälschliche Annahme, daß 2at ein Theil der Bewegung als einer Summe sey, giebt den fälschlichen Schein eines physikalischen Satzes.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"74.78"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0079","text":"Der Faktor selbst, a, die empirische Einheit—ein Quantum als solches—wird der Schwere zugeschrieben; wenn die Kategorie der Kraft der Schwere gebraucht wird, so ist vielmehr zu sagen, daß eben das Ganze s = at[hoch 2] die Wirkung oder besser das Gesetz der Schwere ist.—Gleichmäßig ist der aus ds/dt = 2at abgeleitete Satz, daß wenn die Schwere aufhörte zu wirken, der Körper mit der am Ende seines Falles erlangten Geschwindigkeit den doppelten Raum von dem, welchen er durchloffen hat, in einer der Dauer seines Falles gleichen Zeit zurücklegen würde.—Es liegt hierin auch eine für sich schiefe Metaphysik; das Ende des Falles, oder das Ende eines Zeittheils, in welchem der Körper gefallen, ist immer selbst noch ein Zeittheil; wäre es kein Zeittheil, so wäre Ruhe und damit keine Geschwindigkeit angenommen, die Geschwindigkeit kann nur nach dem Raume angesetzt werden, welcher in einem","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"74.79"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0080","text":"Zeittheil, nicht an seinem Ende, durchloffen worden ist.—Wenn nun aber vollends in andern physikalischen Gebieten, wo gar keine Bewegung vorhanden ist, wie z.B. im Verhalten des Lichts (außer dem, was seine Fortpflanzung im Raume genannt wird) und Größenbestimmungen an den Farben, eine Anwendung der Differentialrechnung gemacht wird und die erste Funktion von einer quadratischen Funktion hier auch Geschwindigkeit genannt wird, so ist dieß für einen noch unstatthafteren Formalismus der Erdichtung von Existenz anzusehen. -Bewegung, welche durch die Gleichung s = at[hoch 2] vorgestellt wird, finden wir, sagt Lagrange in der Erfahrung vom Falle der Körper; die einfachste Bewegung derselben würde die seyn, deren Gleichung s = ct[hoch 3] wäre, aber die Natur zeige keine Bewegung dieser Art; wir wüßten nicht was der Koefficient c bedeuten könnte.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"74.80"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0081","text":"Wenn dem wohl so ist, so giebt es dagegen eine Bewegung, deren Gleichung s[hoch 3] = at[hoch 2] ist,—das kepplerische Gesetz der Bewegung der Körper des Sonnensystems; was hier die erste abgeleitete Funktion 2at/[3s [hoch 2]] u.s.f. bedeuten soll, und die fernere direkte Behandlung dieser Gleichung durch die Differentation, die Entwicklung der Gesetze und Bestimmungen jener absoluten Bewegung von diesem Ausgangspunkte aus, müßte dagegen wohl als eine interessante Aufgabe erscheinen, in welcher die Analysis im würdigsten Glanze sich zeigen würde.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"74.81"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0082","text":"Für sich bietet so die Anwendung des Differential-Kalkuls auf die elementarischen Gleichungen der Bewegung kein reelles Interesse dar; das formelle Interesse kommt von dem allgemeinen Mechanismus des Kalkuls. Eine andre Bedeutung aber erhält die Zerlegung der Bewegung in Beziehung auf die Bestimmung ihrer Trajektorie; wenn dieses eine Kurve ist und ihre Gleichung höhere Potenzen enthält, bedarf es der Übergänge von geradlinigten Funktionen als Funktionen der Potenzirnng, zu den Potenzen selbst, und indem jene aus der ursprünglichen Gleichung der Bewegung, welche den Faktor der Zeit enthält, mit Elimination der Zeit zu gewinnen sind, ist dieser zugleich auf die niedrigern Entwicklungsfunktionen herabzusetzen, aus welchen jene Gleichungen linearer Bestimmungen erhalten werden können. Diese Seite führt auf das Interesse des andern Theils der Differentialrechnung.","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"74.82"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0083","text":"Das Bisherige hat den Zweck gehabt, die einfache specifische Bestimmung des Differential-Kalkuls herauszuheben und festzustellen, und dieselbe in einigen der elementarischen Beispiele nachzuweisen. Diese Bestimmung hat sich ergeben darin zu bestehen, daß aus einer Gleichung von Potenzenfunktionen der Koefficient des Entwicklungsgliedes, die sogenannte erste Funktion gefunden, und das Verhältniß, welches diese ist, in Momenten des konkreten Gegenstands aufgewiesen werde, durch welche so erhaltene Gleichung zwischen den beiden Verhältnissen diese Momente selbst bestimmt sind. Es ist ebenso von dem Princip der Integralrechnung kurz zu betrachten, was sich aus dessen Anwendung, für die specifische konkrete Bestimmnng derselben ergiebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"74.83"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0084","text":"Die Ansicht dieses Kalkuls ist dadurch schon vereinfacht und richtiger bestimmt worden, daß er nicht mehr als Summationsmethode genommen wird, wie er im Gegensatz gegen das Differentiiren, wo der Zuwachs als das wesentliche Ingrediens gilt, genannt wurde, und womit er in wesentlichem Zusammenhang mit der Form der Reihe erschien.—Die Aufgabe dieses Kalkuls ist zunächst ebenso die theoretische oder vielmehr formelle, als die der Differentialrechnung, bekanntlich aber die umgekehrte von dieser;—es wird hier von einer Funktion ausgegangen, die als abgeleitete, als der Koefficient des nächsten aus der Entwicklung einer aber noch unbekannten Gleichung entsprungenen Gliedes betrachtet wird, und aus ihr soll die ursprüngliche Potenzen-Funktion gefunden werden; die in der natürlichen Ordnung der Entwicklung als ursprünglich anzusehende wird hier abgeleitet und die früher als abgeleitet","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"74.84"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0085","text":"betrachtete ist hier die gegebene oder überhaupt die anfangende. Das Formelle dieser Operation scheint nun aber bereits durch den Differential-Kalkul geleistet zu seyn; indem darin überhaupt der Übergang und das Verhältniß von der ursprünglichen zu der Entwicklungsfunktion festgestellt ist. Wenn hierbei Theils schon um die Funktion, von der auszugehen ist, anzusetzen, Theils aber den Übergang von ihr zu der ursprünglichen zu bewerkstelligen, nothwendig in vielen Fällen zu der Form der Reihe die Zuflucht genommen werden muß, so ist zunächst festzuhalten, daß diese Form als solche mit dem eigenthümlichen Prinzip des Integrirens unmittelbar nichts zu thun hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"74.85"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0086","text":"Der andere Theil nun aber der Aufgabe des Kalkuls erscheint in Rücksicht auf die formelle Operation die Anwendung derselben. Diese ist nun selbst die Aufgabe, nämlich die Bedeutung in dem oben angegebenen Sinne zu kennen, welche die ursprüngliche Funktion von der gegebenen als ersten Funktion betrachteten eines besondern Gegenstandes hat. An sich könnte auch diese Lehre bereits in der Differentialrechnung ganz abgethan zu seyn scheinen; allein es tritt ein weiterer Umstand ein, der die Sache nicht so einfach seyn läßt.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"74.86"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0087","text":"Indem nämlich in diesem Kalkul sich ergeben, daß durch die erste Funktion der Gleichung einer Kurve das Verhältniß, welches ein lineares ist, erhalten worden, so weiß man damit auch, daß die Integration dieses Verhältnisses die Gleichung der Kurve im Verhältnisse der Abscisse und Ordinate giebt; oder wenn die Gleichung für die Ebene einer Kurve gegeben wäre, so würde die Differentialrechnung über die Bedeutung der ersten Funktion solcher Gleichung bereits gelehrt haben sollen, daß diese Funktion die Ordinate als Funktion der Abscisse, hiermit die Gleichung der Kurve darstellte.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"74.87"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0088","text":"Nun kömmt es aber darauf an, welches von den Bestimmungsmomenten des Gegenstandes in der Gleichung selbst gegeben ist; denn nur von dem Gegebenen kann die analytische Behandlung den Ausgang nehmen und von da zu den übrigen Bestimmungen des Gegenstands übergehen. Es ist z. B. nicht die Gleichung eines Flächenraums der Kurve, noch etwa des durch ihre Umdrehung entstehenden Körpers, noch auch eines Bogens derselben, sondern nur das Verhältniß der Abscisse und Ordinate in der Gleichung der Kurve selbst gegeben. Die Übergänge von jenen Bestimmungen zu dieser Gleichung selbst können daher nicht schon in der Differentialrechnung behandelt werden; es wird für die Integralrechnung aufgespart, diese Verhältnisse zu finden.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"74.88"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0089","text":"Ferner aber ist gezeigt worden, daß die Differentiirung der Gleichung von mehreren veränderlichen Größen, die Entwicklungspotenz oder Differential-Koefficienten, nicht als eine Gleichung, sondern nur als ein Verhältniß giebt; die Aufgabe ist dann für dieß Verhältniß, welches die abgeleitete Funktion ist, ein zweites in den Momenten des Gegenstandes anzugeben, das jenem gleich sey. Dagegen ist das Object der Integralrechnung das Verhältniß selbst der ursprünglichen zu der abgeleiteten, hier gegeben seyn sollenden Funktion, und die Aufgabe ist, die Bedeutung der zu findenden ursprünglichen Funktion in dem Gegenstande der gegebenen ersten Funktion anzugeben, oder vielmehr indem diese Bedeutung z.B. die Ebene einer Kurve oder die zu rectificirende, als geradlinigt vorgestellte Kurve u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"74.89"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0090","text":"schon als das Problem ausgesprochen ist, zu zeigen, daß solche Bestimmung durch eine ursprüngliche Funktion gefunden werde und welches das Moment des Gegenstandes sey, welches hierfür zur Ausgangs- (der abgeleiteten) Funktion, angenommen werden müsse.","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"74.90"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0091","text":"Die gewöhnliche Methode nun, welche die Vorstellung der Differenz als des Unendlichkleinen gebraucht, macht sich die Sache leicht; für die Quadratur der Kurven also nimmt sie ein unendlich kleines Rektangel, ein Produkt der Ordinate in das Element d. i. das Unendlichkleine der Abscisse, für das Trapez, das zu einer seiner Seiten den unendlichkleinen, jenem unendlichkleinen der Abscisse gegenüberstehenden Bogen habe; das Produkt wird nun in dem Sinne integrirt, daß das Integral die Summe der unendlich vielen Trapeze, die Ebene, deren Bestimmung verlangt wird, nämlich die endliche Größe jenes Elements der Ebene gebe.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"74.91"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0092","text":"Ebenso formirt sie aus den Unendlichkleinen des Bogens, und der dazu gehörigen Ordinate und Abscisse ein rechtwincklichtes Dreieck, in welchem das Quadrat jenes Bogens gleich sey der Summe der Quadrate der beiden andern Unendlichkleinen, deren Integration den Bogen als einen endlichen giebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"74.92"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0093","text":"Dieß Verfahren hat die allgemeine Entdeckung, welche diesem Gebiete der Analysis zu Grunde liegt, zu seiner Voraussetzung, hier in der Weise, daß die quadrirte Kurve, der rectificirte Bogen u.s.f. zu einer gewissen durch die Gleichung der Kurve gegebenen Funktion, in dem Verhältniß der sogenannten ursprünglichen Funktion zu der abgeleiteten steht. Es handelt sich darum zu wissen, wenn ein gewisser Theil eines mathematischen Gegenstandes (z.B. einer Kurve) als die abgeleitete Funktion angenommen werde, welcher andere Theil desselben durch die entsprechende ursprüngliche Funktion ausgedrückt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"74.93"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0094","text":"Man weiß, daß wenn die durch die Gleichung der Kurve gegebene Funktion der Ordinate als abgeleitete Funktion genommen wird, die relativ ursprüngliche Funktion der Größenausdruck der von dieser Ordinate abgeschnittenen Area der Kurve ist, daß wenn eine gewisse Tangentenbestimmung als abgeleitete Funktion angesehen wird, die ursprüngliche Funktion derselben die Größe des zu dieser Tangentenbestimmung gehörigen Bogens ausdrückt, u. s. f. daß nun aber diese Verhältnisse, das eine einer ursprünglichen Funktion zu der abgeleiteten, das andere von den Größen zweier Theile oder Umstände des mathematischen Gegenstandes, eine Proportion bilden, dieß zu erkennen und zu beweisen, erspart sich die Methode, die das Unendlichkleine und die mechanische Operation mit demselben gebraucht.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"74.94"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0095","text":"Das eigenthümliche Verdienst des Scharfsinns ist, aus den anderwärts her bereits bekannten Resultaten herausgefunden zu haben, daß gewisse und welche Seiten eines mathematischen Gegenstandes, in dem Verhältnisse von ursprünglicher und von abgeleiteter Funktion stehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"74.95"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0096","text":"Von diesen beiden Funktionen ist die abgeleitete, oder wie sie bestimmt worden ist, die Funktion der Potenzirung, hier in diesem Kalkul die gegebene, relativ gegen die ursprüngliche, als welche erst aus jener durch die Integration, gefunden werden soll. Allein sie ist nicht unmittelbar gegeben, noch ist es für sich schon gegeben, welcher Theil oder Bestimmung des mathematischen Gegenstands als die abgeleitete Funktion angesehen werden soll, um durch Zurückführung derselben auf die ursprüngliche den andern Theil oder Bestimmung zu finden, deren Größe das Problem verlangt.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"74.96"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0097","text":"Die gewöhnliche Methode, die, wie gesagt, sogleich gewisse Theile des Gegenstandes als unendlich klein, in der Form abgeleiteter Funktionen, vorstellt, welche sich aus der ursprünglich gegebenen Gleichung des Gegenstandes überhaupt durch die Differentiirung bestimmen lassen, (—wie für die Rektifikation einer Kurve, die unendlichkleinen Abscissen und Ordinaten), nimmt dafür solche, welche sich mit dem Gegenstande des Problems, (in dem Beispiele, dem Bogen) der ebenso als unendlichklein vorgestellt wird, in eine Verbindung bringen lassen, die in der Elementar-Mathematik festgestellt ist, und wodurch, wenn jene Theile bekannt sind, auch dieser bestimmt ist, dessen Größe zu finden aufgegeben ist; so werden für die Rektifikation die angegebenen drei Unendlichkleinen in die Verbindung der Gleichung des rechtwinklichten Dreiecks gebracht, für die Quadratur die Ordinate mit der unendlichkleinen","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"74.97"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0098","text":"Abscisse in die Verbindung eines Produkts, indem eine Ebene überhaupt arithmetisch als Produkt von Linien angenommen ist. Der Übergang von solchem sogenannten Elemente der Ebene, des Bogens u.s.f. zur Größe der Ebene, des Bogens u.s.f. selbst, gilt dann nur als das Aufsteigen von dem unendlichen Ausdruck zum endlichen, oder zur Summe der unendlich vielen Elemente, aus denen die verlangte Größe bestehen soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"74.98"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0099","text":"Es kann daher nur oberflächlich gesagt werden, daß die Integralrechnung bloß das umgekehrte, überhaupt jedoch schwierigere Problem der Differentialrechnung sey; das reelle Interesse der Integralrechnung geht vielmehr ausschließlich auf das Verhältniß der ursprünglichen und der abgeleiteten Funktion in den konkreten Gegenständen, zu einander.","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"74.99"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0100","text":"Lagrange ist ebenso wenig in diesem Theile des Kalkuls darauf eingegangen, die Schwierigkeit der Probleme auf die glatte Weise jener direkten Annahmen abzuthun. Es wird zur Erläuterung der Natur der Sache beitragen, gleichfalls das Nähere seines Verfahrens aus einigen wenigen Beispielen anzugeben. Dasselbe macht es sich eben zur Aufgabe, für sich zu beweisen, daß zwischen besondern Bestimmungen eines mathematischen Ganzen z.B. einer Kurve, ein Verhältniß von der ursprünglichen zu der abgeleiteten Funktion Statt finde. Dieß kann nun aber in diesem Felde vermöge der Natur des Verhältnisses selbst, welches am mathematischen Gegenstande, krumme mit geraden Linien, lineare Dimensionen und Funktionen derselben mit Ebenen-Flächen-Dimensionen und deren Funktion u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"74.100"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0101","text":"also qualitativ verschiedene in Beziehung bringt, nicht auf direkte Weise bewerkstelligt werden, die Bestimmung läßt sich so nur als die Mitte zwischen einem Größern und Kleinern auffassen. Hiermit tritt von selbst wohl wieder die Form eines Zuwachses mit Plus und Minus ein, und das rüstige: Développons, ist an seiner Stelle; aber wie die Zuwächse hier nur arithmetische, endliche Bedeutung haben, davon ist vorhin gesprochen worden. Aus der Entwicklung jener Bedingung, daß die zu bestimmende Größe größer als die eine leicht bestimmbare Grenze und kleiner als die andere sey, wird dann z.B. hergeleitet, daß die Funktion der Ordinate die abgeleitete erste Funktion zu der Funktion der Area ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"74.101"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0102","text":"Die Rektifikation der Kurven, wie sie von Lagrange aufgezeigt wird, indem er von dem archimedischen Princip ausgeht, hat das Interesse, die Übersetzung der archimedischen Methode in das Princip der neuern Analysis einzusehen,","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"74.102"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0103","text":"was einen Blick in das Innere und in den wahrhaften Sinn des auf die andere Art mechanisch betriebenen Geschäftes thun läßt. Die Verfahrungsweise ist der so eben angegebenen nothwendig analog; das archimedische Princip, daß der Bogen einer Kurve größer ist, als seine Chorde und kleiner als die Summe zweier an den Endpunkten des Bogens, gezogenen Tangenten, insoweit sie zwischen diesen Punkten und ihrem Durchschnittspunkt enthalten sind, giebt keine direkte Gleichung.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"74.103"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0104","text":"Die Übertragung jener archimedischen Grundbestimmung in die moderne analytische Form ist die Erfindung eines Ausdrucks, der für sich eine einfache Grundgleichung sey, während jene Form nur die Forderung aufstellt, zwischen einem zu Großen und zu Kleinen, die sich jedesmal bestimmt haben, ins Unendliche fortzugehen, welches Fortgehen wieder immer nur ein neues zu Großes und ein neues zu Kleines jedoch in immer engern Grenzen giebt. Vermittelst des Formalismus des Unendlichkleinen wird sogleich die Gleichung dz[hoch 2] = dx[hoch 2] + dy[hoch 2] angesetzt. Die lagrangesche Exposition ausgehend von der angegebenen Grundlage zeigt hingegen auf, daß die Größe des Bogens die ursprüngliche Funktion ist zu einer abgeleiteten, von der das eigenthümliche Glied selbst eine Funktion aus dem Verhältnisse einer abgeleiteten zu der ursprünglichen der Ordinate ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"74.104"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0105","text":"Weil in dem archimedischen Verfahren, wie dann später in der kepplerschen Behandlung stereometrischer Gegenstände, die Vorstellung vom Unendlichkleinen vorkommt, so ist dieß so oft als eine Autorität für den Gebrauch, der von dieser Vorstellung in dem Differentialkalkul gemacht wird, angeführt worden, ohne daß das Eigenthümliche und Unterscheidende herausgehoben worden wäre. Das Unendlichkleine bedeutet zunächst die Negation des Quantums als eines solchen, d. i. eines sogenannten endlichen Ausdrucks, der vollendeten Bestimmtheit, wie sie das Quantum als solches hat. Ebenso ist in den darauf folgenden berühmten Methoden des Valerius, Cavalleri u.","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"74.105"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0106","text":"a., die sich auf die Betrachtung der Verhältnisse geometrischer Gegenstände gründen, die Grundbestimmung, daß das Quantum als solches der Bestimmungen, welche nur im Verhältnisse zunächst betrachtet werden, für diesen Behuf auf die Seite gestellt und sie hiernach als ein Nicht-Großes sollen genommen werden. Aber Theils ist hiermit das Affirmative überhaupt, welches hinter der bloß negativen Bestimmung liegt, nicht erkannt und herausgehoben, welches sich oben abstrakt als die qualitative Größebestimmtheit, und diese bestimmter in dem Potenzenverhältnisse liegend, sich ergeben hat;—Theils aber, indem dieß Verhältniß selbst wieder eine Menge näher bestimmter Verhältnisse in sich begreift, wie das einer Potenz und deren Entwicklungsfunktion, so haben sie auch wieder auf die allgemeine und negative Bestimmung desselben Unendlichkleinen gegründet und daraus abgeleitet werden sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"74.106"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0107","text":"In der eben ausgehobenen lagrangeschen Exposition ist das bestimmte Affirmative, das in der archimedischen Entwicklungsweise der Aufgabe liegt, gefunden und damit dem mit einem unbegrenzten Herausgehen behafteten Verfahren seine richtige Grenze gegeben worden. Das Große der modernen Erfindung für sich und ihre Fähigkeit vorher intraktable Probleme zu lösen, und die früher lösbaren auf eine einfache Weise zu behandeln, ist allein in die Entdeckung des Verhältnisses der ursprünglichen zu den sogenannten abgeleiteten und der Theile, welche an dem mathematischen Ganzen in solchem Verhältnisse stehen, zu setzen. Die gemachten Anführungen mögen für den Zweck genügen, das Eigenthümliche des Verhältnisses von Größen herauszuheben, welches der Gegenstand der in Rede stehenden besondern Art des Kalkuls ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"74.107"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0108","text":"Diese Anführungen konnten sich auf einfache Probleme und deren Auflösungsweisen beschränken; und weder wäre es für die Begriffsbestimmung, um die es hier allein zu thun war, zweckmäßig gewesen, noch hätte es in dem Vermögen des Verfassers gestanden, den gesammten Umfang der sogenannten Anwendung der Differential- und Integralrechnung vorzunehmen und die Induktion, daß das aufgezeigte Princip derselben zu Grunde liege, durch die Zurückführung aller ihrer Probleme und deren Lösungen darauf, zu vervollständigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"74.108"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0109","text":"Das Beigebrachte hat aber hinreichend gezeigt, daß wie jede besondere Rechnungsweise eine besondere Bestimmtheit oder Verhältniß der Größe zu ihrem Gegenstande hat, und ein solches das Addiren, Multipliciren, das Erheben in Potenzen und Ausziehen der Wurzeln, die Rechnung mit Logarithmen, Reihen u.s.f., konstituirt, ebenso der Differential- und Integralkalkul; für das diesem Kalkul Angehörige möchte der Name des Verhältnisses einer Potenzenfunktion und der Funktion ihrer Entwicklung oder Potenzirung der passendste seyn, weil er der Einsicht der Natur der Sache am nächsten liegt. Nur wie die Operationen nach den andern Größenverhältnissen, wie Addiren u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"74.109"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0110","text":"bei diesem Kalkul überhaupt gleichfalls gebraucht werden, werden auch die Logarithmen—Kreisund Reihen-Verhältnisse angewendet, insbesondere um Ausdrücke zum Behuf der erforderlichen Operationen des Ableitens der ursprünglichen aus den Entwicklungsfunktionen traktabler zu machen. Mit der Reiheform hat die Differential- und Integralrechnung wohl das nähere Interesse geineinschaftlich, die Entwicklungsfunktionen, welche bei den Reihen die Koefficienten der Glieder heissen, zu bestimmen; aber indem das Interesse jenes Kalkuls nur auf das Verhältniß der ursprünglichen Funktion zu dem nächsten Koefficienten ihrer Entwicklung geht, will die Reihe in der nach Potenzen, die mit jenen Koefficienten versehen sind, geordneten Menge von Gliedern eine Summe darstellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"74.110"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0111","text":"Das Unendliche, das bei der unendlichen Reihe vorkommt, der unbestimmte Ausdruck des Negativen des Quantums überhaupt, hat mit der affirmativen Bestimmung, welche im Unendlichen jenes Kalkuls liegt, nichts gemein. Ebenso ist das Unendlichkleine, als der Zuwachs, vermittelst dessen die Entwicklung in die Form der Reihe fällt, nur ein äußeres Mittel für die Entwickelung, und seine sogenannte Unendlichkeit ohne alle andere Bedeutung, als die, sonst gar keine zu haben, als die jenes Mittels; die Reihe, da sie in der That es nicht ist, die verlangt wird, führt ein Zuviel herbei, welches wieder wegzubringen, die überflüssige Mühe macht.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"74.111"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0112","text":"Von dieser Mühe ist die Methode Lagrange's, der die Form der Reihe vorzugsweise wieder aufgenommen hat, gleichfalls gedrückt; obgleich sie es ist, durch welche in dem, was die Anwendung genannt wird, die wahre Eigenthümlichkeit sich heraushebt, indem ohne die Formen von dx, dy u. s.f. in die Gegenstände hinein zu zwängen, direkt derjenige Theil nachgewiesen wird, dem an ihnen die Bestimmtheit der abgeleiteten (- Entwickelungs—) Funktion zukommt, und es sich damit zeigt, daß die Form der Reihe hier nicht das ist, um das es sich handelt. [13]","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"74.112"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0113","text":"[13] In der obenangeführten Kritik (Jahrb. für wissensch. Krit. II. B. 1827. Nr. 155. 6. folg.) finden sich interessante Äußerungen eines gründlichen Gelehrten des Faches, Um. Spehr's, aus seinen neuen Principien des Fluentenkalkuls, Braunschw. 1826. angeführt, die nämlich einen Umstand betreffen, der wesentlich zu den Dunkelheiten und dem Unwissenschaftlichen in der Differentialrechnung beitrage, und stimmen mit dem überein, was über das allgemeine Verhältniß der Theorie dieses Kalkuls gesagt worden ist: \"man hat\" heißt es daselbst, \"rein arithmetische Untersuchungen, welche freilich von allen ähnlichen zunächst auf die Differentialrechnung Bezug haben, nicht von der eigentlichen Diff.-Rechnung gesondert, ja diese Untersuchungen wohl gar, wie Lagrange, für die Sache selbst gehalten, während man diese nur als Anwendung jener ansah.","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"74.113"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0114","text":"Diese arithmetischen Untersuchungen begreifen die Regeln der Differentation, die Ableitung des taylorschen Lehrsatzes u.s.w. ja selbst die verschiedenen Integrationsmethoden in sich. Es ist ganz umgekehrt der Fall, jene Anwendungen sind es gerade, welche den Gegenstand der eigentlichen Differential-Rechnung ausmachen, und alle jene arithmetischen Entwicklungen und Operationen setzt sie aus der Analysis voraus.\"—Es ist aufgezeigt worden, wie bei Lagrange die Trennung der sogenannten Anwendung von dem Verfahren des allgemeinen Theils, das von den Reihen ausgeht, eben dazu dient, die eigenthümliche Sache der Differ.-Rechnung für sich zum Vorschein zu bringen. Aber bei der interessanten Einsicht des Hrn. Vfs., daß eben die sogenannten Anwendungen es sind, welche den Gegenstand der eigentlichen Differ.-Rechnung ausmachen, ist es zu verwundern, wie derselbe sich in die (ebendas.","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"74.114"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0115","text":"angeführte) formelle Metaphysik von kontinuirlicher Größe, Werden, Fließen u.s.f. hat einlassen und solchen Ballast noch mit neuem gar hat vermehren wollen; formell sind diese Bestimmungen, indem sie nur allgemeine Kategorien sind, welche eben das Specifische der Sache nicht angeben, die aus den konkreten Lehren, den Anwendungen, zu erkennen und zu abstrahiren war.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"74.115"}],"sha256":"f22286572b4343ca4bc3b4f2d3c9e2e1ae63d1c7cbc86a55742376b48472babe","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103817783950Z_cd3075e4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.The Purpose of Differential Calculus Derived from Its Application.","source_sha256":"f22286572b4343ca4bc3b4f2d3c9e2e1ae63d1c7cbc86a55742376b48472babe","sha256":"cd43d8b3263686d32cab722738fe4a54fb2b713dd92e5343d1ed7bb762061a36","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:38:17.783972+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0001","text":"In the preceding Remark, partly the determinacy of the concept of the Infinitely Small, which is employed in the differential calculus, and partly the basis of its introduction into it, have been considered; both are abstract and therefore in themselves also easy determinations; but the so-called application offers greater difficulties as well as the more interesting aspect; the elements of this concrete aspect are to be the subject of this Remark.—The whole method of differential calculus is absolved in the proposition that dx[hoch n] = nx[hoch n 1]dx, or f(x+i)-fx/i = P, i.e. equal to the coefficient of the first term of the binomial x + d, x + i, expanded according to the powers of dx or i.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"74.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0002","text":"Nothing further needs to be learned; the derivation of the next forms, of the differential of a product, of an exponential magnitude, and so on, follows mechanically from this; in a short time, perhaps in half an hour—with the finding of the differentials, the reverse, the finding of the original function from them, integration, is likewise given—one can possess the whole theory. What alone detains one longer is the effort to see it, to make it intelligible, that after the one circumstance of the problem, the finding of that coefficient, has been accomplished in an analytical, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"74.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0003","text":"wholly arithmetical manner, through the expansion of the function of the variable magnitude, after this has received, through an increment, the form of a binomial, it should also be right with the other circumstance, namely, with omitting the remaining terms of the resulting series except the first. If it were the case that one needed that coefficient alone, then with its determination everything pertaining to the theory would be— as stated—disposed of in less than half an hour, and the omission of the further terms of the series would constitute so little a difficulty that there would rather be no mention at all of them, as terms of the series (as second, third, etc. functions, their determination is likewise already absolved with the determination of the first), since they are entirely not at issue.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"74.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0004","text":"The observation may be prefaced that one can readily see from the method of differential calculus that it was not invented and set forth for its own sake; not only is it not grounded for its own sake, as another mode of analytical procedure, but rather the violence of directly omitting terms that result from the expansion of a function, although the whole of this expansion is assumed to belong completely to the matter,—because the matter is regarded as the difference","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"74.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0005","text":"of the expanded function of a variable magnitude, after the latter has been given the shape of a binomial, from the original one,—is thoroughly contrary to all mathematical principles. The need for such a mode of procedure, as well as the justification lacking to it in itself, points at once to the fact that the origin and the basis must be found elsewhere. It also happens otherwise in the sciences that what is put forward first as the elementary and from which the propositions of the science are to be derived is not evident, and that it proves rather to have its occasion and its grounding in what follows.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"74.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0006","text":"The course of events in the history of differential calculus shows that it took its beginning chiefly in the various so-called tangent methods, the matter, as it were, in feats of skill; the manner of procedure, after it had also been extended to further objects, was later brought to consciousness and into abstract formulas, which attempts were then also made to elevate into principles.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"74.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0007","text":"As the determinacy of the concept of the so-called Infinitely Small, the qualitative quantitative determinacy of such [magnitudes] as are at first posited as quanta in relation to one another has been exhibited; to this was attached the empirical investigation of demonstrating that determinacy of the concept in the descriptions or definitions that are found of the Infinitely Small, insofar as it is taken as an infinite difference and the like.—This has occurred only in the interest of abstract determinacy of the concept as such; the further question would be what the transition from it to mathematical configuration and application would be like.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"74.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0008","text":"To this end, the theoretical aspect, the determinacy of the concept, must first be pursued further, which will not show itself wholly unfruitful in itself; then its relation to application is to be considered, and in both it is to be demonstrated, as far as is possible here, that the general consequences are at the same time appropriate to that with which differential calculus is concerned and to the manner in which it accomplishes it.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"74.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0009","text":"First, it is to be recalled that the form which the determinacy of the concept in question has in mathematics has already been indicated incidentally. The qualitative determinacy of the quantitative was first shown in quantitative relation in general, but it was also already anticipated in the demonstration of the distinct so-called modes of calculation (see the relevant Remark) that it is the relation of powers, to be considered afterwards in its peculiar place, in which number is posited as having returned into itself through the equating of its moments of the concept, unity and amount, and thereby receives in it the moment of infinity, of being-for-self, i.e. of being determined through itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"74.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0010","text":"The explicit qualitative determinacy of magnitude thus essentially relates, as has likewise already been recalled, to determinations of powers, and since differential calculus has the specific character of operating with qualitative forms of magnitude, its peculiar mathematical object must be the treatment of forms of powers, and all the problems and their solutions, for the sake of which differential calculus is employed, show that the interest lies solely in the treatment of determinations of powers as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"74.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0011","text":"Important as this foundation is, and as it immediately places something determinate at the head, in place of the merely formal categories of variable, continuous, or infinite magnitudes and the like, or even merely of functions in general, it is still too general; other operations likewise have to do with it; already raising to a power and extracting roots, then the treatment of exponential magnitudes and logarithms, series, equations of higher orders, have their interest and their endeavor solely in relations based upon powers. Undoubtedly, they must together constitute a system of the treatment of powers; but which among the various relations into which determinations of powers can be posited is that which is the proper object and interest for differential calculus, this is to be gathered from it itself, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"74.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0012","text":"from its so-called applications. These are in fact the matter itself, the actual procedure in the mathematical solution of a certain circle of problems; this procedure was earlier than the theory or the general part, and was called application only later in relation to the theory subsequently created, which was intended partly to set forth the general method of procedure, partly, however, to give it principles, i.e. justification.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"74.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0013","text":"What a futile endeavor it has been to find principles for the hitherto prevailing conception of the procedure which genuinely resolved the contradiction that emerges in it, instead of merely excusing or concealing it by means of the insignificance of what is necessary according to the mathematical procedure but is here to be omitted, or by means of the possibility, amounting to the same thing, of infinite or arbitrary approximation and the like, has been shown in the preceding Remark. If the universal of the procedure were abstracted otherwise than has hitherto occurred from the actual part of mathematics called differential calculus, then those principles and the effort concerning them would likewise show themselves to be dispensable, just as they show themselves in themselves to be something askew and remaining in contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"74.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0014","text":"If we investigate this peculiarity by simply taking up what is present in this part of mathematics, we find as object: à) equations in which an arbitrary number of magnitudes (we can here in general remain with two) are so connected into a whole of determinacy that these, first, have their determinacy in empirical magnitudes, as fixed limits, and then in the manner of connection with these, as well as of their connection with one another; as is generally the case in an equation; but since only one equation for both magnitudes (and likewise, relatively, several equations for several magnitudes, but always fewer than the number of magnitudes—) is present, these equations belong to the indeterminate ones; and, second, one aspect of how these magnitudes here have their determinacy lies in the fact that they (at least one of them) occur in a","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"74.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0015","text":"higher than the first power in the equation.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"74.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0016","text":"Some remarks are first to be made about this: first, that according to the first of the indicated determinations the magnitudes have wholly only the character of such variable magnitudes as occur in the problems of indeterminate analysis. Their value is indeterminate, but in such a way that if a completely determinate value, i.e. a numerical value, comes from elsewhere for the one, then the other too is determined; thus the one is a function of the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"74.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0017","text":"The categories of variable magnitudes, functions, and the like are therefore only formal for the specific determinacy of magnitude at issue here, as has been said above, because they are of a universality in which that specific element upon which the whole interest of differential calculus turns is not yet contained, nor can it be explicated from them through analysis; in themselves they are simple, insignificant, easy determinations, which are made difficult only insofar as what is not contained in them, namely the specific determination of differential calculus, is to be put into them so that it may then be derived from them.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"74.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0018","text":"—As for the so-called constant, it may be observed concerning it that it is initially an indifferent empirical magnitude, determining the variable magnitudes merely with respect to their empirical quantum, as the limit of their minimum and maximum; but the manner of connection of the constants with the variable magnitudes is itself one of the moments for the nature of the particular function which these magnitudes are. Conversely, however, the constants themselves are also functions; insofar as, e.g., a straight line has the meaning of being the parameter of a parabola, its meaning is that it is the function y[hoch 2]/x; just as, in the expansion of the binomial generally, the constant which is the coefficient of the first term of expansion is the sum of the roots, that of the second, the sum of their products two by two, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"74.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0019","text":"thus these constants here are in general functions of the roots; where in integral calculus the constant is determined from the given formula, it is insofar treated as a function of this formula. We shall then further consider those coefficients as functions in another determination, whose meaning in the concrete is that upon which the whole interest turns.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"74.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0020","text":"But the peculiarity by which the consideration of variable magnitudes in differential calculus differs from their character in indeterminate problems is to be placed in what has been indicated: that at least one of those magnitudes, or all of them, occurs in a power higher than the first, where again it is indifferent whether all are of the same higher or of unequal powers; their specific indeterminacy, which they have here, lies solely in the fact that they are functions of one another in such a relation of powers.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"74.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0021","text":"Thereby the alteration of the variable magnitudes is qualitatively determined, and thus continuous; and this continuity, which for itself is again only the formal category in general of an identity, of a determinacy preserving itself in alteration and remaining the same, here has its determinate meaning, and indeed solely in the relation of powers, which has no quantum for its exponent and constitutes the non-quantitative, enduring determinacy of the relation of the variable magnitudes. Hence, against another formalism, the observation is to be made that the first power is a power only in relation to higher ones; for itself x is merely some indeterminate quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"74.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0022","text":"Thus it has no sense to differentiate, for itself, the equations y = ax + b, of the straight line, or s = ct, that of simply uniform velocity; if from y = ax, or also from y = ax + b, a = dy/dx, or ds/dt = c from s = ct, then a = y/x is just as much the determination of the tangent, or s/t = c that of simply uniform velocity. The latter is expounded as dy/dx in connection with what is set forth for the development of uniformly accelerated motion; but that a moment of simple, simply uniform, i.e. velocity not determined through the higher power of one of the moments of motion, should occur in the system of such motion is, as previously remarked, itself an empty assumption founded solely in the routine of the method.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"74.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0023","text":"Since the method proceeds from the representation of the increment which the variable magnitude is supposed to undergo, then of course even one which is only a function of the first power can also undergo an increment; if, in order now to find the differential, the difference of the second equation thereby produced is to be taken from the given one, the emptiness of the operation is apparent, namely that, as remarked, the equation before and after it is the same for the so-called increments as for the variable magnitudes themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"74.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0024","text":"ß) By what has been said, the nature of the equation to be treated has been determined, and it remains now to indicate to what interest its treatment is found directed. This consideration can yield only familiar results, such as are present in form especially in Lagrange's conception; but I have made the exposition wholly elementary in order to remove the heterogeneous determinations mingled with it.—The basis of the treatment of the equation of the indicated kind proves to be that the power is apprehended within itself as a relation, as a system of determinations of relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"74.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0025","text":"The power has above been specified as number, insofar as it has come to this, that its alteration is determined by itself, that its moments, unity and number, are identical, as was previously shown, completely and in the first instance in the square, more formally, which here makes no difference, in the higher powers. Now since the power, as number—if one prefers the expression magnitude as the more general, it is nevertheless always number in itself,—is a multiplicity, and is also represented as a sum, it can in the first instance be decomposed within itself into an arbitrary multiplicity of numbers, which are without any further determination in relation to one another and to their sum, except merely that together they are equal to this sum. But the power can also be discerned into a sum of such differences as are determined by the form of the power.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"74.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0026","text":"If the power is taken as a sum, then its base, the root, is likewise apprehended as a sum, and arbitrarily according to a manifold decomposition, which manifoldness, however, is the indifferent empirical-quantitative. The sum which the root is to be, reduced to its simple determinacy, i.e. to its true universality, is the binomial; every further multiplication of the terms is a mere repetition of the same determination and hence something empty. [12] What matters is solely the, thereby qualitative, determinacy of the terms, which results through the raising to a power of the root assumed as a sum, and which determinacy lies solely in the alteration that is the raising to a power. These terms are thus wholly functions of the raising to a power and of the power.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"74.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0027","text":"Now that representation of number as a sum of a multiplicity of such terms, which are functions of the raising to a power; then the interest in finding the form of such functions, and further this sum from the multiplicity of such terms, insofar as this finding must depend solely on that form,—this, as is known, constitutes the special doctrine of series. But here we have essentially to distinguish the further interest, namely the relation of the underlying magnitude itself, whose determinacy, insofar as it is a complex, i.e. here an equation, includes a power within itself,—to the functions of its raising to a power. This relation, wholly abstracted from the interest in the sum mentioned above, will prove to be the point of view which emerges from the actual science as the sole one that differential calculus sets before itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"74.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0028","text":"[12] It belongs only to the formalism of that universality to which analysis necessarily lays claim when, instead of taking (a + b)[to the power n] for the expansion of powers, one says (a + b + c + d…)[to the power n], as is also done in many other cases; such a form is, so to speak, to be regarded merely as a coquetry of the appearance of universality; in the binomial the matter is exhausted; through its development the law is found, and the law is true universality, not the merely external and empty repetition of the law, which alone is what is produced by that a + b + c + d… .","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"74.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0029","text":"Yet one determination must first be added to what has been said, or rather one which lies therein must be removed. It was said, namely, that the variable magnitude, into whose determination the power enters, is considered, within itself, as a sum, and indeed as a system of terms, insofar as these are functions of the raising to a power; whereby the root too is considered as a sum, and in the simply determined form as a binomial; x[to the power n] = (y + z)[to the power n] = (y + ny[to the power n-1] z +….) This representation proceeded, for the development of the power, i.e. for obtaining its functions of raising to a power, from the sum as such; here, however, there is no concern with a sum as such, nor with the series arising therefrom, but only the relation is to be taken up from the sum.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"74.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0030","text":"The relation as such of magnitudes is what, on the one hand, remains after abstraction is made from the plus of a sum as such, and what, on the other hand, is required for finding the developmental functions of the power. But such relation is already determined in that here the object is an equation, y[to the power m] = ax[to the power n], already a complex of several (variable) magnitudes, which contains a determination of powers of them. In this complex each of these magnitudes is posited absolutely as being in relation to the other, with the significance, one might say, of a plus upon itself,—as a function of the other magnitudes; their character of being functions of one another gives them this determination of plus, but thereby one wholly indeterminate, not that of an increase, increment, and the like.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"74.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0031","text":"Yet we could also have left this abstract point of view aside; it may quite simply be maintained that, after the variable magnitudes in the equation are given as functions of one another, so that this determinacy contains a relation of powers, the functions of the raising to a power of each are now likewise compared with one another,—which second functions are determined by nothing further than the raising to a power itself. It can at first be presented as an arbitrary choice or a possibility to set an equation concerning the powers of its variable magnitudes into a relation of their developmental functions; only a further end, utility, use has to indicate the serviceability of such transformation; it is through its usefulness alone that that transposition has been occasioned.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"74.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0032","text":"If previously the representation of these determinations of raising to a power in a magnitude, which is taken as differentiated within itself as a sum, was proceeded from, this served only partly to indicate of what kind such functions are, and partly it contains the way of finding them.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"74.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0033","text":"We thus find ourselves at the ordinary analytical development, which for the purpose of differential calculus is conceived in such a way that an increment, dx, is given to the variable magnitude, and the power of the binomial is then explicated through the series of terms belonging to it. But the so-called increment is not supposed to be a quantum, only a form, whose entire value is to be helpful for the development; what is admittedly intended, most definitely by Euler and Lagrange, and in the previously mentioned representation of the limit, is only the resulting determinations of powers of the variable magnitudes, namely the so-called coefficients of the increment and of its powers, according to which the series arranges itself and to which the differentiated coefficients belong.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"74.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0034","text":"It may be remarked in this connection that, since an increment without a quantum is assumed only for the sake of the development, it would have been most fitting to take (one) for it, since in the development it always occurs only as a factor; whereby precisely the factor one fulfills the purpose that no quantitative determinacy and alteration is to be posited through the increment. By contrast, dx, encumbered with the false representation of a quantitative difference, and other signs, such as i, with the here useless appearance of universality, always have the appearance and pretension of being a quantum and its powers; which pretension then gives rise to the trouble of nevertheless getting rid of them and omitting them. In order to retain the form of a series developed according to powers, the designations of exponents as indices could just as well be affixed to one.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"74.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0035","text":"But in any case abstraction must be made from the series and from the determination of the coefficients according to the place they have in the series; the relation among all of them is the same; the second function is derived from the first in precisely the same way as this is from the original, and for that counted as the second, the first derived function is once again the original function. Essentially, however, the interest is directed not to the series, but solely to the determination of powers resulting from the development in its relation to the magnitude immediate to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"74.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0036","text":"Instead, therefore, of determining the latter as the coefficient of the first term of the development, since a term is designated as the first in relation to the others following it in the series, while such a power of an increment, like the series itself, does not belong here, the mere expression derived function of powers, or, as was said above, a function of the raising to a power of the magnitude, would be preferable; it being presupposed as known in what way derivation is taken as a development enclosed within a power.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"74.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0037","text":"If, now, the proper mathematical beginning in this part of analytics is nothing further than finding the function determined through the development of powers, the further question is what is to be done with the relation thereby obtained, where it has application and use, or indeed, for what end such functions are sought. Differential calculus has acquired its great interest through finding relations in concrete objects which can be reduced to those abstract analytical ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"74.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0038","text":"Concerning applicability, however, the following initially follows of itself from the nature of the matter, without yet inferring it from the cases of application themselves, by virtue of the exhibited shape of the moments of powers. The development of magnitudes of powers, through which the functions of their raising to a power result, contains, abstracting from more specific determination, in the first instance generally the reduction of the magnitude to the next lower power. The applicability of this operation thus occurs with such objects as likewise contain such a difference of determinations of powers.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"74.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0039","text":"If we now reflect upon spatial determinacy, we find that it contains the three dimensions, which, in order to distinguish them from the abstract differences of height, length, and breadth, we may designate as the concrete ones, namely the line, the surface, and total space; and when they are taken in their simplest forms and in relation to self-determination and hence to analytical dimensions, we have the straight line, the plane surface and the latter as square, and the cube. The straight line has an empirical quantum, but with the plane the qualitative, the determination of powers, enters; more specific modifications, e.g. that this also happens at once with plane curves, we can leave undiscussed, insofar as the concern in the first instance is only with the difference in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"74.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0040","text":"Thereby there also arises the need to pass from a higher determination of powers to a lower one and conversely, insofar as, for example, linear determinations are to be derived from given equations of the surface, etc., or conversely.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"74.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0041","text":"—Motion, further, in which the quantitative relation of the traversed space and the corresponding elapsed time is to be considered, presents itself in the different determinations of a non-uniform, a uniformly accelerated, an alternately uniformly accelerated and uniformly retarded,—self-returning motion; insofar as these different kinds of motion are expressed according to the quantitative relation of their moments, space and time, equations result for them from different determinations of powers, and insofar as there may be a need to determine one kind of motion, or also the magnitudes of space to which one kind is bound, from another kind of the same, the operation likewise brings about the transition from one function of powers to a higher or lower one.—The examples of these two objects may suffice for the","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"74.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0042","text":"purpose for which they have been adduced.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"74.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0043","text":"The appearance of contingency which differential calculus presents in its applications would already be simplified by consciousness of the nature of the domains in which application can take place, and of the peculiar need and condition of this application. But further, within these domains themselves, it matters to know between which parts of the objects of the mathematical problem such a relation obtains as is peculiarly posited through differential calculus. It must at once be remarked preliminarily that two kinds of relation are to be considered here.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"74.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0044","text":"The operation of depotentiating an equation, considered according to the derived functions of its variable magnitudes, yields a result which in itself is truly no longer an equation, but a relation; this relation is the subject of differential calculus proper. Thereby, secondly, there is also present the relation of the higher determination of powers (the original equation) itself to the lower one (the derivative). We must for the present set this second relation aside; it will show itself as the peculiar subject of integral calculus.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"74.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0045","text":"Let us first consider the first relation, and, for the determination of the moment to be gathered from the so-called application, in which the interest of the operation lies, take the simplest example in curves determined by an equation of the second power. As is known, the equation immediately gives the relation of the coordinates in a determination of powers. Consequences of the fundamental determination are the determinations of the other straight lines connected with the coordinates: the tangent, subtangent, normal, etc. But the equations between these lines and the coordinates are linear equations; the wholes of which these lines are determined as parts are right-angled triangles of straight lines.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"74.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0046","text":"The transition from the fundamental equation, which contains the determination of powers, to those linear equations now contains the indicated transition from the original function, i.e. one which is an equation, to the derived one, which is a relation, namely between certain lines contained in the curve. It is the connection between the relation of these lines and the equation of the curve that is at issue in finding it.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"74.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0047","text":"It is not without interest to note so much concerning the history of this, namely, that the first discoverers knew how to state their discovery only in a wholly empirical manner, without being able to give an account of the operation, which remained wholly external. I shall content myself in this respect with citing Barrow, Newton's teacher. In his lect. Opt. et Geom., in which he treats problems of higher geometry according to the method of indivisibles, which is at first distinguished from what is peculiar to differential calculus, he also gives, “because his friends pressed him,” (lect. X.) his procedure for determining the tangent.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"74.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0048","text":"One must read in him himself what this account is like, in order to form an adequate idea of how the procedure is given entirely as an external rule—in the same style in which formerly arithmetic schoolbooks set forth the rule of three, or still better the so-called casting out of nines in arithmetic operations.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"74.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0049","text":"He makes the diagram of the little lines which were afterwards called the increments in the characteristic triangle of a curve, and now gives the prescription as a mere rule: to throw away as superfluous the terms which emerge, as powers of those increments or products, in consequence of the development of the equations, (etenim isti termini nihilum valebunt); likewise, the terms containing only magnitudes determined by the original equation are to be thrown away (the subsequent subtraction of the original equation from that formed with the increments), and finally to substitute the ordinate itself for the increment of the ordinate and the subtangent for the increment of the abscissa.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"74.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0050","text":"If one may so speak, the procedure could not be stated more pedantically;—the latter substitution is the assumption, made fundamental to the determination of tangents in the ordinary differential method, of the proportionality of the increments of the ordinate and abscissa with the ordinate and subtangent; in Barrow's rule this assumption appears in all its naive nakedness. A simple way of determining the subtangent had been found; the manners of Roberval and Fermat amount to something similar—the method of finding the greatest and least values, from which the latter proceeded, rests upon the same foundations and the same procedure. It was a mathematical craze of those times to find so-called methods, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"74.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0051","text":"rules of that kind, and at the same time to make a secret of them, which was not only easy but even necessary in one respect, for the same reason that it was easy—namely, because the inventors had found only an empirical external rule, not a method, i.e. nothing derived from acknowledged principles. Leibniz took up such so-called methods from his time, and Newton likewise from the same time and more immediately from his teacher; by generalizing their form and applicability they opened new paths for the sciences, but thereby at the same time had the need to tear the procedure out of the form of merely external rules and sought to procure for it the requisite justification.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"74.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0052","text":"If we analyse the method more closely, the true course of events is this. First, the determinations of powers (of the variable magnitudes, of course) which the equation contains are reduced to their first functions. But thereby the value of the terms of the equation is altered; hence there no longer remains an equation, but only a relation has arisen between the first function of the one variable magnitude and the first function of the other; instead of px = y² one has p : 2y, or instead of 2ax—x² = y² one has a—x : y, which was afterwards customarily designated as the relation dy/dx.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"74.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0053","text":"The equation is the equation of the curve; this relation, which is wholly dependent upon it and derived from it (above according to a mere rule), is, on the other hand, a linear one, with which certain lines are in proportion; p : 2y or a—x : y are themselves relations of straight lines of the curve, of the coordinates and the parameters; but with that one still knows nothing. The interest is to know of other lines occurring in the curve that this relation belongs to them, to find the equality of two relations.—Thus the second question is: which are the straight lines determined by the nature of the curve that stand in such a relation?—but this is what was already known earlier, namely, that a relation obtained in that way is the relation of the ordinate to the subtangent.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"74.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0054","text":"the ancients had found this by an ingenious geometrical route; what the more recent inventors discovered is the empirical procedure for arranging the equation of the curve in such a way that that first relation is yielded, of which it was already known that it is equal to a relation containing the line—here, the subtangent—whose determination is at issue.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"74.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0055","text":"In part, this arranging of the equation has now been methodically conceived and carried out—differentiation; in part, however, the imaginary increments of the coordinates and the characteristic triangle, imaginary and formed from these and from a similar increment of the tangent, have been invented, so that the proportionality of the relation found through the depotentiation of the equation with the relation of the ordinate and the subtangent may be presented not as something empirically taken up merely from the old acquaintance, but as something proved. Yet the old acquaintance proves itself generally, and most unmistakably in the cited form of rules, to be the sole occasion and respective justification for the assumption of the characteristic triangle and that proportionality.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"74.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0056","text":"Lagrange has now rejected this simulation and taken the genuinely scientific path; to his method belongs the insight upon which the matter depends, in that it consists in separating the two transitions that have to be made for the solution of the problem and in treating and proving each of these aspects for itself. One part of this solution—if, for a more detailed specification of the course, we remain with the example of the elementary problem of finding the subtangent—the theoretical or general part, namely the finding of the first function from the given equation of the curve, is regulated for itself; it yields a linear relation, hence one of straight lines which occur in the system of curve-determination. The other part of the solution is then the finding of those lines at the curve which stand in that relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"74.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0057","text":"This is now accomplished in the direct way (Théorie des Fonct. Anal. II. P. II. Chap.), i.e. without the characteristic triangle, namely without assuming infinitely small arcs, ordinates, and abscissas, and assigning to these the determinations of dy and dx, i.e. of the sides of that relation, and at the same time immediately the significance of its equality with the ordinate and subtangent themselves. A line (as also a point) has its determination only insofar as it constitutes the side of a triangle, just as the determination of a point likewise lies only in such a triangle.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"74.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0058","text":"This is, to mention it in passing, the fundamental theorem of analytic geometry, which brings in the coordinates, just as, which is the same thing, in mechanics the parallelogram of forces; for this very reason it is wholly in no need of the many efforts at a proof.—The subtangent is now posited as the side of a triangle, whose further sides are the ordinate and the tangent relating to it. The latter, as a straight line, has an equation p = aq, (+ b is to be added, though it is useless for the determination and is added only for the sake of the favoured generality); the determination of the relation p/q falls into a, the coefficient of q, which is the respective first function of the equation, but which in general need only be considered as a = p/q, as, namely, the essential determination of the straight line applied as a tangent to the curve.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"74.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0059","text":"Now, furthermore, since the first function of the equation of the curve is taken, it is likewise the determination of a straight line; and since the one coordinate p of the first straight line and y, the ordinate of the curve, are taken as the same, so that the point at which that first straight line, assumed as tangent, touches the curve is likewise the initial point of the straight line determined by the first function of the curve, it comes down to showing that this second straight line coincides with the first, i.e. is tangent; expressed algebraically, that if y = fx and p = Fq, and now y = p, thus fx = Fq, are assumed, then also f'x = F'q.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"74.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0060","text":"That the straight line applied as tangent and that straight line determined from the equation through its first function coincide, and that the latter is therefore tangent—this is shown with the aid of the increment i of the abscissa and the increment of the ordinate determined by the development of the function. Here, therefore, the notorious increment likewise enters; but the purpose for which it is introduced just indicated, and the development of the function according to it, must be carefully distinguished from the earlier-mentioned use of the increment for finding the differential equation and for the characteristic triangle.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"74.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0061","text":"The use made here is justified and necessary; it falls within the sphere of geometry, inasmuch as the geometrical determination of a tangent as such requires that no other straight line which likewise passed through this point can pass between it and the curve with which it has a point in common. For by this determination the quality of tangent or non-tangent is reduced to the difference of magnitude, and the line is the tangent to which the greater smallness—simply with respect to the determination that matters—belongs. This apparently merely relative smallness contains absolutely nothing empirical, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"74.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0062","text":"nothing dependent upon a quantum as such; it is qualitatively posited by the nature of the formula when the difference of the moment upon which the magnitude to be compared depends is a difference of powers; since this comes down to i and i², and i, which must ultimately signify a number, is then to be represented as a fraction, i² is in and for itself smaller than i, so that even the representation of an arbitrary magnitude in which i could be taken is here superfluous and indeed out of place. Thus the proof of the greater smallness has nothing to do with an infinitely small, which therefore has by no means to enter here.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"74.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0063","text":"Were it only for the sake of the beauty and the now more forgotten, yet well-deserved fame, I should still like to mention Descartes's method of tangents; moreover, it also has a relation to the nature of equations, concerning which a further remark is then to be made. Descartes presents this independent method, in which the required linear determination is likewise found from the same derived function, in his Geometry, otherwise so fruitful as well (liv. II. p. 357 ss. Oeuvres compl. ed. Cousin Tom. V.), in that in it he taught the great foundation concerning the nature of equations and their geometrical construction, and the analysis thereby so greatly extended to geometry in general. For him the problem has the form of the task of drawing straight lines perpendicular to arbitrary places on a curve, whereby the subtangent etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"74.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0064","text":"is determined; one understands the satisfaction which he expresses there at his discovery, which concerned an object of general scientific interest at that time, and which is so very geometrical and thereby stood so far above the mere rule-methods of his rivals mentioned above: j'ose dire que c'est ceci le problème le plus utile et le plus général, non seulement que je sache, mais même que j'aie jamais desire de savoir en géometrie.—For the solution he takes as his basis the analytical equation of the right-angled triangle which is formed by the ordinate of the point of the curve at which the straight line required in the problem is to be perpendicular, then by this line itself, the normal, and thirdly by the part of the axis cut off by the ordinate and normal, by the subnormal.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"74.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0065","text":"From the known equation of a curve, the value, whether of the ordinate or of the abscissa, is now substituted into that equation of the triangle; thus one has an equation of the second degree (and Descartes shows how curves whose equations contain higher degrees can likewise be reduced to this), in which only one of the variable magnitudes occurs, and indeed in the square and in the first power;—a quadratic equation which at first appears as a so-called incomplete one.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"74.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0066","text":"Now Descartes makes the reflection that, if the point assumed on the curve is represented as the point of intersection of the latter and a circle, this circle will cut the curve at yet another point, and thereupon, for the two x thereby arising and being unequal, two equations with the same constants and of the same form result;—or else only one equation with unequal values of x. But the equation is only one, for the one triangle in which the hypotenuse is perpendicular to the curve, is the normal; this is represented by making the two points at which the circle intersects the curve coincide, thus letting the latter touch the curve. But with this the circumstance of the unequal roots of x or y of the quadratic equation also falls away.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"74.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0067","text":"In a quadratic equation with two equal roots, however, the coefficient of the term that contains the unknown in the first power is twice the one root; this then gives an equation by which the required determinations are found. This procedure is to be regarded as the ingenious stroke of a genuinely analytical mind, beside which the altogether assertorily assumed proportionality of the sub-tangent and the ordinate to the so-called increments of the abscissa and ordinate that are supposed to be infinitely small recedes entirely.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"74.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0068","text":"The final equation obtained in the indicated way, which equates the coefficient of the second term of the quadratic equation to the double root or unknown, is the same as that found by the procedure of differential calculus. x[hoch 2]—ax—b = 0 differentiated gives the new equation 2x—a = 0; or x[hoch 3]—px—q = 0 gives 3x[hoch 2]—p = 0. But here the observation presents itself that it by no means follows of itself that such a derived equation is also","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"74.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0069","text":"correct. In an equation with two variable magnitudes, which, because they are variable, do not lose the character of being unknown magnitudes, as was considered above there results only a relation, for the simple reason indicated: because by substituting the functions of powers for the powers themselves the value of the two terms of the equation is altered, and it is in itself still unknown whether, with values thus altered, an equation still obtains between them. The equation dy/dx = P expresses nothing further than that P is a relation, and no other real sense is to be ascribed to dy/dx.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"74.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0070","text":"But of this relation = P it is equally still unknown to what other relations it is equal; such an equation, the proportionality, first gives it a value and significance.—As it was indicated that this significance, what was called application, was received empirically from elsewhere, so in the case of the equations here in question derived by differentiation it must be known from elsewhere whether they have equal roots, in order to know whether the equation obtained is still correct. This circumstance, however, is not expressly made noticeable in textbooks; it is perhaps removed by the fact that an equation with one unknown, brought to zero, is at once set equal to y, whereby in differentiation there indeed results a dy/dx, but merely a relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"74.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0071","text":"The calculus of functions must indeed have to do with functions of powers, or differential calculation with differentials; but it by no means follows from this alone that the magnitudes whose differentials or functions of powers are taken must themselves also be functions of other magnitudes. In the theoretical part, the instruction in deriving the differentials, i.e. the functions of powers, no thought is yet given to the fact that the magnitudes which one is taught to treat after such derivation are themselves to be functions of other magnitudes.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"74.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0072","text":"Still, with regard to the omission of the constant in differentiating, it may be observed that here this has the sense that the constant is immaterial for the determination of the roots in the case of their equality, which determination is exhausted by the coefficient of the second term of the equation. As in Descartes's example cited, the constant is the square of the roots themselves, so that these can be determined from the constant just as from the coefficients; since it is in general, like the coefficients, a function of the roots of the equation.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"74.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0073","text":"In the usual presentation, the disappearance of the so-called constants connected with the other terms only by + and—takes place through the mere mechanism of the procedure: that, in order to find the differential of a compound expression, an increment is given only to the variable magnitudes, and the expression thereby formed is subtracted from the original one. The sense of the constants and of their omission, insofar as they are themselves functions and serve or do not serve according to this determination, does not come under discussion.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"74.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0074","text":"A similar observation is connected with the omission of the constants, one that may be made concerning the names differentiation and integration, as earlier concerning finite and infinite expression: namely, that their determination contains rather the opposite of what the expression says. Differentiating designates the positing of differences; but by differentiating an equation is instead reduced to fewer dimensions, by omitting the constant a moment of determinateness is removed; as remarked, the roots of the variable magnitude are set into an equality, and thus their difference is aufgehoben.","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"74.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0075","text":"In integration, on the other hand, the constant is to be added again; the equation is indeed thereby integrated, but in the sense that the previously aufgehobene difference of the roots is restored, that what had been equated is differentiated again. —The customary expression contributes to placing the essential nature of the matter in shadow and to putting everything under the subordinate, indeed extraneous to the main matter, point of view partly of the infinitely small difference, the increment and the like, partly of mere difference in general between the given and the derived function, without designating its specific, i.e. qualitative difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"74.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0076","text":"Another principal field in which differential calculus is used is mechanics; the meanings of the different functions of powers which arise in the elementary equations of its object, motion, have already been mentioned incidentally; I shall take them up directly here.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"74.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0077","text":"The equation, namely the mathematical expression, of merely uniform motion c = s/t or s = ct, in which the spaces traversed are proportional to the elapsed times according to an empirical unit c, the magnitude of velocity, offers no sense for differentiation; the coefficient c is already completely determined and known, and no further development of powers can take place.—How s = at[hoch 2], the equation of falling motion, is analysed, has already been recalled earlier;—the first term of the analysis ds/dt = 2 at is translated into language and respectively into existence thus: it is supposed to be a term of a sum (-a representation which we have long since removed), one part of motion, and indeed this is supposed to belong to the force of inertia, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"74.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0078","text":"to a merely uniform velocity, in such a way that in infinitely small portions of time the motion is uniform, but in finite portions of time, i.e. in those actually existing, non-uniform. To be sure, fs = 2at; and the meaning of a and of t by themselves is known, as is the fact that thereby the determination of the uniform velocity of a motion is posited; since a = s/[t[hoch 2]] is 2 at = 2s/t in general; but thereby one knows not the least thing further; only the false assumption that 2at is a part of motion as of a sum gives the false appearance of a physical proposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"74.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0079","text":"The factor itself, a, the empirical unit— a quantum as such—is ascribed to gravity; if the category of the force of gravity is employed, it must rather be said that the whole s = at[hoch 2] is the effect, or better the law, of gravity.—Similarly derived from ds/dt = 2at is the proposition that, if gravity ceased to act, the body, with the velocity attained at the end of its fall, would traverse twice the space which it has traversed in a time equal to the duration of its fall.—There is also in this a metaphysics that is crooked in itself; the end of the fall, or the end of a portion of time in which the body has fallen, is always itself still a portion of time; if it were not a portion of time, rest, and thus no velocity, would be assumed; velocity can only be posited according to the space which has been traversed in a","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"74.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0080","text":"portion of time, not at its end.—But if, moreover, in other physical fields where no motion at all is present, as for example in the behaviour of light (apart from what is called its propagation in space) and in determinations of magnitude in colours, an application of differential calculation is made, and the first function of a quadratic function is here likewise called velocity, then this is to be regarded as an even more inadmissible formalism of the invention of existence. -Motion represented by the equation s = at[hoch 2], says Lagrange, we find in the experience of the fall of bodies; their simplest motion would be that whose equation was s = ct[hoch 3], but nature shows no motion of this kind; we do not know what the coefficient c could signify.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"74.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0081","text":"If this may well be so, there is, on the other hand, a motion whose equation is s[hoch 3] = at[hoch 2],—the Keplerian law of the motion of the bodies of the solar system; what the first derived function 2at/[3s [hoch 2]] etc. is supposed to signify here, and the further direct treatment of this equation by differentiation, the development of the laws and determinations of that absolute motion from this point of departure, would on the other hand have to appear as an interesting task, in which analysis would show itself in its most worthy splendour.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"74.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0082","text":"In itself, then, the application of differential calculus to the elementary equations of motion offers no real interest; the formal interest comes from the general mechanism of the calculus. But the decomposition of motion receives another significance in relation to the determination of its trajectory; if this is a curve and its equation contains higher powers, it requires transitions from rectilinear functions as functions of powers to the powers themselves, and since the former are to be obtained from the original equation of motion, which contains the factor of time, by elimination of time, this factor must at the same time be reduced to the lower functions of development, from which those equations of linear determinations can be obtained. This aspect leads to the interest of the other part of differential calculus.","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"74.82","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0083","text":"What has preceded had the purpose of bringing out and establishing the simple specific determination of differential calculus, and of demonstrating it in some of the elementary examples. This determination has shown itself to consist in this: that from an equation of functions of powers the coefficient of the term of development, the so-called first function, is found, and that the relation which this is be demonstrated in moments of the concrete object, through which, by the equation thus obtained between the two relations, these moments themselves are determined. It is likewise briefly to be considered, concerning the principle of integral calculus, what results from its application for its specific concrete determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"74.83","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0084","text":"The conception of this calculus has thereby already been simplified and more correctly determined, in that it is no longer taken as a method of summation, as it was called in opposition to differentiation, where the increment counts as the essential ingredient, and with which it appeared in an essential connection with the form of the series.—The task of this calculus is initially as theoretical, or rather formal, as that of differential calculus, but, as is well known, the reverse of the latter;—here one proceeds from a function which is considered as derived, as the coefficient of the term next arising from the development of an as yet unknown equation, and from it the original potency-function is to be found; that which in the natural order of development is to be regarded as original is here derived, and that formerly regarded as derived","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"74.84","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0085","text":"is here the given, or in general the initial one. The formal aspect of this operation, however, seems already to have been accomplished by differential calculus; since therein the transition and the relation from the original to the developed function is generally established. If, in this connection, recourse must necessarily be had in many cases to the form of the series, partly in order to posit the function from which one is to proceed, and partly in order to effect the transition from it to the original, it must first be maintained that this form as such has nothing immediately to do with the peculiar principle of integration.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"74.85","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0086","text":"The other part of the task of the calculus, however, appears, with respect to the formal operation, to be its application. This itself is now the task, namely, to know the significance, in the sense indicated above, which the original function has of the given function, considered as the first function, of a particular object. In itself this doctrine too could seem already to have been entirely dealt with in differential calculus; but a further circumstance enters in, which does not leave the matter so simple.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"74.86","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0087","text":"For, since in this calculus it emerges that through the first function of the equation of a curve the relation, which is a linear one, has been obtained, one thereby also knows that the integration of this relation gives the equation of the curve in the relation of abscissa and ordinate; or, if the equation for the plane of a curve were given, differential calculus ought already to have taught concerning the significance of the first function of such an equation that this function represented the ordinate as a function of the abscissa, and thus the equation of the curve.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"74.87","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0088","text":"But what now matters is which of the determining moments of the object is given in the equation itself; for analytical treatment can take its point of departure only from what is given, and from there proceed to the remaining determinations of the object. For example, it is not the equation of an area of the curve, nor perhaps of the solid produced by its rotation, nor yet of an arc of it, but only the relation of abscissa and ordinate in the equation of the curve itself that is given. The transitions from those determinations to this equation itself therefore cannot already be treated in differential calculus; it is reserved for integral calculus to find these relations.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"74.88","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0089","text":"Further, it has been shown that the differentiation of the equation of several variable magnitudes, the developmental potency or differential-coefficients, gives not an equation but only a relation; the task is then to specify for this relation, which is the derived function, a second one in the moments of the object that is equal to the former. By contrast, the object of integral calculus is the relation itself of the original to the derived function, which is here supposed to be given, and the task is to specify the significance of the original function to be found in the object of the given first function, or rather, since this significance is, for example, the plane of a curve or the curve to be rectified, represented as rectilinear, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"74.89","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0090","text":"already stated as the problem, to show that such a determination is found through an original function and which moment of the object it is that must be assumed for this purpose as the initial (the derived) function.","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"74.90","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0091","text":"The usual method, which employs the representation of the difference as the infinitely small, makes the matter easy for itself; thus, for the quadrature of curves, it takes an infinitely small rectangle, a product of the ordinate and the element, i.e. the infinitely small, of the abscissa; for the trapezium, [it takes] one which has as one of its sides the infinitely small arc opposite that infinitely small [part] of the abscissa; the product is now integrated in the sense that the integral gives the sum of the infinitely many trapezia, the plane whose determination is demanded, namely the finite magnitude of that element of the plane.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"74.91","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0092","text":"Likewise it forms, out of the infinitely small [parts] of the arc and of the ordinate and abscissa belonging to it, a right-angled triangle, in which the square of that arc is equal to the sum of the squares of the two other infinitely small [parts], whose integration gives the arc as a finite [magnitude].","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"74.92","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0093","text":"This procedure has as its presupposition the general discovery which underlies this domain of analysis, namely, that the quadrature of the curve, the rectified arc, etc. stand in relation to a certain function, given through the equation of the curve, in the relation of so-called original function to derived function. The point is to know, if a certain part of a mathematical object (e.g. of a curve) is assumed as the derived function, which other part of the same is expressed by the corresponding original function.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"74.93","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0093"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0094","text":"One knows that, if the function of the ordinate given through the equation of the curve is taken as the derived function, the relatively original function is the expression of magnitude of the area of the curve cut off by this ordinate; that, if a certain determination of the tangent is regarded as the derived function, its original function expresses the magnitude of the arc belonging to this determination of the tangent, etc. But the method that employs the infinitely small and the mechanical operation with it spares itself recognizing and proving that these relations, the one of an original function to the derived, the other of the magnitudes of two parts or circumstances of the mathematical object, form a proportion.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"74.94","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0094"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0095","text":"The peculiar merit of acumen is to have discovered, from results already known elsewhere, that certain aspects, and which aspects, of a mathematical object stand in the relation of original and derived function.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"74.95","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0095"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0096","text":"Of these two functions, the derived, or, as it has been determined, the function of potentiation, is here in this calculus the given one, relative to the original, which is first to be found from the former by integration. Yet it is not immediately given, nor is it in itself already given which part or determination of the mathematical object is to be regarded as the derived function, in order, by reduction of it to the original, to find the other part or determination whose magnitude the problem demands.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"74.96","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0096"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0097","text":"The usual method, which, as stated, at once represents certain parts of the object as infinitely small, in the form of derived functions, which can generally be determined from the originally given equation of the object by differentiation,—as, for the rectification of a curve, the infinitely small abscissae and ordinates—takes for this purpose such [parts] as can be brought into a connection with the object of the problem (in the example, the arc), which is likewise represented as infinitely small, a connection established in elementary mathematics and through which, when those parts are known, this too is determined, whose magnitude it is required to find; thus, for rectification, the three infinitely small [parts] indicated are brought into the connection of the equation of the right-angled triangle; for quadrature, the ordinate with the infinitely small","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"74.97","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0097"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0098","text":"abscissa into the connection of a product, since a plane in general is arithmetically assumed as the product of lines. The transition from such a so-called element of the plane, of the arc, etc., to the magnitude of the plane, of the arc, etc. itself, then counts merely as the ascent from the infinite expression to the finite, or to the sum of the infinitely many elements of which the required magnitude is supposed to consist.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"74.98","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0098"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0099","text":"It can therefore be said only superficially that integral calculus is merely the reverse, though in general more difficult, problem of differential calculus; the real interest of integral calculus rather concerns exclusively the relation of the original and the derived function to one another in concrete objects.","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"74.99","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0099"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0100","text":"Lagrange has just as little, in this part of the calculus, undertaken to dispose of the difficulty of the problems in the facile manner of those direct assumptions. To elucidate the nature of the matter, it will likewise contribute to indicate more closely his procedure from a few examples. It makes it precisely its task to prove in itself that, between particular determinations of a mathematical whole, e.g. a curve, there obtains a relation of original to derived function. But in this field, by virtue of the nature of the relation itself, which in the mathematical object brings into relation curves with straight lines, linear dimensions and their functions with plane-surface dimensions and their function, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"74.100","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0100"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0101","text":"and thus qualitatively different [things], this cannot be accomplished in a direct manner; the determination can thus only be grasped as the mean between a greater and a lesser. Herewith the form of an increment with plus and minus naturally enters again, and the brisk: Développons, is in its place; but it has been spoken of above how the increments here have only an arithmetical, finite significance. From the development of that condition, that the magnitude to be determined be greater than the one easily determinable boundary and smaller than the other, it is then derived, for example, that the function of the ordinate is the first derived function of the function of the area.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"74.101","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0101"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0102","text":"The rectification of curves, as Lagrange demonstrates it, by proceeding from the Archimedean principle, has the interest of comprehending the translation of the Archimedean method into the principle of modern analysis,","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"74.102","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0102"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0103","text":"which affords a glimpse into the interior and into the true sense of the operation conducted mechanically in the other manner. The mode of procedure is necessarily analogous to that just indicated; the Archimedean principle, that the arc of a curve is greater than its chord and smaller than the sum of two tangents drawn at the endpoints of the arc, insofar as they are contained between these points and their point of intersection, gives no direct equation.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"74.103","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0103"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0104","text":"The transposition of that Archimedean fundamental determination into the modern analytical form is the invention of an expression which is in itself a simple fundamental equation, whereas that form merely lays down the demand to proceed to infinity between a too-great and a too-small [magnitude], which are determined each time, a proceeding which in turn always gives only a new too-great and a new too-small [magnitude], though within ever narrower limits. By means of the formalism of the infinitely small, the equation dz[hoch 2] = dx[hoch 2] + dy[hoch 2] is immediately posited. The Lagrangian exposition, proceeding from the indicated foundation, shows instead that the magnitude of the arc is the original function of a derived one, whose peculiar term itself is a function from the relation of a derived [function] to the original [function] of the ordinate.","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"74.104","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0104"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0105","text":"Because the representation of the infinitely small occurs in the Archimedean procedure, as later in the Keplerian treatment of stereometric objects, this has so often been adduced as an authority for the use made of this representation in differential calculus, without the peculiar and distinguishing feature having been brought out. The infinitely small signifies initially the negation of quantum as such, i.e. of a so-called finite expression, of completed determinacy, such as quantum as such possesses. Likewise, in the subsequently famous methods of Valerius, Cavalieri, and","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"74.105","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0105"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0106","text":"others, which are grounded on the consideration of the relations of geometrical objects, the fundamental determination is that the quantum as such of the determinations which are initially considered only in relation is, for this purpose, set aside, and that they are accordingly to be taken as a non-magnitude. But, on the one hand, the affirmative in general which lies behind the merely negative determination has not thereby been recognized and brought out, which above emerged abstractly as qualitative determinacy of magnitude, and more determinately as lying in the relation of powers;—on the other hand, since this relation itself again comprehends within it a multitude of more closely determined relations, such as that of a power and its developmental function, these too were supposed again to be grounded on, and derived from, the general and negative determination of the same infinitely small.","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"74.106","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0106"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0107","text":"In the Lagrangian exposition just brought out, the determinate affirmative that lies in the Archimedean mode of developing the problem has been found, and thereby the procedure afflicted with an unbounded going-out has been given its proper limit. The greatness of the modern invention in itself, and its capacity to solve previously intractable problems and to treat those earlier solvable in a simple manner, is to be placed solely in the discovery of the relation of the original to the so-called derived [functions], and of the parts that stand in such a relation within the mathematical whole. The citations made may suffice for the purpose of bringing out the distinctive character of the relation of magnitudes that is the object of the particular kind of calculus under discussion.","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"74.107","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0107"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0108","text":"These citations could confine themselves to simple problems and their modes of solution; and it would neither have been expedient for the determination of the concept, which alone was at issue here, nor would it have lain within the author's powers, to undertake the entire scope of the so-called application of differential and integral calculus and to complete the induction that the principle indicated underlies it, by reducing all its problems and their solutions to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"74.108","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0108"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0109","text":"What has been adduced has, however, sufficiently shown that, just as every particular mode of calculation has a particular determinacy or relation of magnitude as its object, and such a relation constitutes addition, multiplication, raising to powers and extraction of roots, calculation with logarithms, series, etc., so too does differential and integral calculus; for what belongs to this calculus, the name of the relation of a power-function and the function of its development or exponentiation would be the most appropriate, because it comes closest to insight into the nature of the matter. Only, just as the operations according to the other relations of magnitude, such as addition, etc.,","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"74.109","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0109"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0110","text":"are likewise used in this calculus in general, so logarithmic—circular and series-relations are also applied, in particular in order to make expressions more tractable for the required operations of deriving the original [functions] from the development-functions. Differential and integral calculus indeed shares with the form of series the more immediate interest of determining the development-functions, which in series are called the coefficients of the terms; but whereas the interest of that calculus concerns only the relation of the original function to the nearest coefficient of its development, the series seeks to represent a sum in the aggregate of terms ordered according to powers endowed with those coefficients.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"74.110","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0110"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0111","text":"The infinite that occurs in the infinite series, the indeterminate expression of the negative of quantum in general, has nothing in common with the affirmative determinacy that lies in the infinite of that calculus. Likewise, the infinitesimal, as the increment by means of which the development falls into the form of a series, is only an external means for development, and its so-called infinity has no other meaning whatever than that of this means—otherwise none at all; the series, since it is in fact not what is required, brings about a surplus, the removal of which causes superfluous trouble.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"74.111","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0111"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0112","text":"Lagrange's method, which has pre-eminently taken up again the form of series, is likewise burdened by this trouble; although it is the method through which, in what is called application, the true distinctive character emerges, inasmuch as, without forcing the forms of dx, dy, etc. into the objects, that part is directly demonstrated which in them possesses the determinacy of the derived (-development-) function, and it thereby becomes apparent that the form of series is not what is at issue here. [13]","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"74.112","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0112"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0113","text":"[13] In the critique cited above (Jahrb. für wissensch. Krit. II. vol. 1827, no. 155, p. 6 et seq.), interesting remarks by a thorough scholar in the field, Um. Spehr, are quoted from his Neue Principien des Fluentenkalkuls, Brunswick, 1826, namely remarks concerning a circumstance that essentially contributes to the obscurities and the unscientific character in differential calculus, and they agree with what has been said concerning the general relation of the theory of this calculus: “purely arithmetical investigations,” it says there, “which indeed, among all similar investigations, relate most directly to differential calculus, have not been separated from differential calculus proper; indeed, like Lagrange, these investigations have perhaps even been taken for the matter itself, whereas the latter was regarded merely as an application of the former.”","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"74.113","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0113"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0114","text":"These arithmetical investigations comprise within themselves the rules of differentiation, the derivation of Taylor's theorem, etc., indeed even the various methods of integration. The case is quite the reverse: it is precisely those applications that constitute the object of differential calculus proper, and it presupposes from analysis all those arithmetical developments and operations.”—It has been shown how, in Lagrange, the separation of the so-called application from the procedure of the general part, which proceeds from series, serves precisely to bring the distinctive matter of differential calculus to appearance on its own account. But given the interesting insight of the author that it is precisely the so-called applications that constitute the object of differential calculus proper, it is surprising how he could enter into the (just","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"74.114","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0114"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0115","text":"cited) formal metaphysics of continuous magnitude, becoming, flowing, etc., and even wish to augment such ballast with new ballast; these determinations are formal, inasmuch as they are only universal categories, which do not state the specific character of the matter, which was to be recognized and abstracted from the concrete doctrines, the applications.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"74.115","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A2DZ:P0115"]}],"source_digest":"7c60d17c2fcf98ee3d2c5a3ff362a44238e5d06bca3d2633b099b6fc4afb0aa9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.Der Zweck des Differentialkalkuls aus seiner Anwendung abgeleitet."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.Der Zweck des Differentialkalkuls aus seiner Anwendung abgeleitet.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA","title":"Remark 3. Other Forms Connected with Qualitative Determinacy of Magnitude.","order":75,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A3NA","text":"Das Unendlichkleine der Differentialrechnung ist in seinem affirmativen Sinn als die qualitative Größenbestimmtheit, und von dieser näher aufgezeigt worden, daß sie in diesem Kalkul als Potenzenbestimmtheit nicht nur überhaupt, sondern als die besondere des Verhältnisses einer Potenzenfunktion zu der Entwicklungspotenz vorhanden ist. Die qualitative Bestimmtheit ist aber auch noch in weiterer, so zu sagen, schwächerer Form vorhanden, und diese, wie auch der damit zusammenhängende Gebrauch des Unendlichkleinen und dessen Sinn in diesem Gebrauche, soll noch in dieser Anmerkung betrachtet werden.\n\nEs ist, indem wir vom Vorhergehenden ausgehen, in dieser Rücksicht zuerst daran zu erinnern, daß die unterschiedenen Potenzenbestimmungen von der analytischen Seite zunächst so hervortreten, daß sie nur formell, und ganz homogen darin sind, daß sie Zahlengrößen bedeuten, die als solche jene qualitative Verschiedenheit gegeneinander nicht haben. Aber in der Anwendung auf räumliche Gegenstände zeigt sich das analytische Verhältniß ganz in seiner qualitativen Bestimmtheit, als das Übergehen von linearen zu Flächenbestimmungen, von geradlinigten zu krummlinigten u.s.f. Diese Anwendung bringt es ferner mit sich, daß die räumlichen ihrer Natur nach in Form von kontinuirlichen Größen gegebenen Gegenstände in diskreter Weise gefaßt werden, die Fläche also als eine Menge von Linien, die Linie als eine Menge von Punkten u.s.f. Diese Auflösung hat das einzige Interesse, die Punkte, in welche die Linie, die Linien, in welche die Fläche u.s.f. aufgelöst ist, selbst zu bestimmen, um von solcher Bestimmung aus analytisch, d. h. eigentlich arithmetisch fortgehen zu können; diese Ausgangspunkte sind für die zu findenden Größebestimmungen die Elemente, aus welchen die Funktion und Gleichung für das Konkrete, die kontinuirliche Größe, abgeleitet werden soll. Für die Probleme, wo sich nornehmlich das Interesse zeigt, dieß Verfahren zu gebrauchen, wird im Elemente für den Ausgang ein für sich selbst Bestimmtes verlangt, gegen den Gang, der indirekt ist, indem er im Gegentheil nur mit Grenzen beginnen kann, zwischen welchen das Fürsichbestimmte liege, auf das als sein Ziel er losgehe. Das Resultat läuft in beiden Methoden dann auf dasselbe hinaus, wenn sich nur das Gesetz des weitern Fortbestimmens finden läßt, ohne die geforderte vollkommene d. h. sogenannte endliche Bestimmung erlangen zu können. Kepplern wird die Ehre zugeschrieben, zuerst den Gedanken jener Umkehrung des Ganges gehabt und das Diskrete zum Ausgangspunkte gemacht zu haben. Seine Erklärung, wie er den ersten Satz in Archimed's Kreismessung verstehe, drückt dieß auf eine einfache Weise aus. Der erste Satz Archimed's ist bekanntlich, daß der Kreis einem rechtwinklichten Dreieck gleich ist, dessen eine Kathete dem Halbmesser, die andere dem Umfange des Kreises gleich ist. Indem Keppler den Sinn dieses Satzes so nimmt, daß die Peripherie des Kreises ebenso viele Theile als Punkte, d. i. unendlich viele habe, deren jeder als die Grundlinie eines gleichschenklichten Dreiecks betrachtet werden könne, u.s.f., so spricht er die Auflösung des Kontinuirlichen in die Form des Diskreten aus. Der Ausdruck des Unendlichen, der hierbei vorkommt, ist noch weit entfernt von der Bestimmung, die er in dem Differentialkalkul haben soll.—Wenn nun für solche diskrete eine Bestimmtheit, Funktion gefunden ist, so sollen sie ferner zusammengefaßt werden, wesentlich als Elemente des Kontinuirlichen seyn. Da aber eine Summe von Punkten keine Linie, eine Summe von Linien keine Fläche giebt, werden die Punkte schon sogleich als lineare genommen, wie die Linien als flächenhafte. Weil jedoch zugleich jene Lineare noch keine Linien seyn sollen, was sie seyn würden, wenn sie als Quantum genommen würden, so werden sie als unendlich klein vorgestellt. Das Diskrete ist nur eines äußerlichen Zusammenfassens fähig, in welchem die Momente den Sinn von diskretem Eins behalten; der analytische Übergang von denselben geschieht nur zu ihrer Summe, er ist nicht zugleich der geometrische von dem Punkte in die Linie, oder von der Linie in die Fläche u.s.f.; dem Elemente, das als Punkt oder als Linie seine Bestimmung hat, wird daher zugleich auch mit jenem die lineare, dieser die Flächenqualität gegeben, damit die Summe als von kleinen Linien eine Linie, als von kleinen Flächen eine Fläche werde.\n\nDas Bedürfniß, dieß Moment des qualitativen Übergangs zu erhalten und dafür zu dem Unendlich-kleinen die Zuflucht zu nehmen, muß als die Quelle aller der Vorstellungen angesehen werden, welche, indem sie jene Schwierigkeit ausgleichen sollen, an ihnen selbst die größte Schwierigkeit sind. Diese Nothhülfe entbehrlich zu machen, müßte gezeigt werden können, daß in dem analytischen Verfahren selbst, welches als ein bloßes Summiren erscheint, in der That schon ein Multipliciren enthalten ist. Aber in dieser Rücksicht tritt eine neue Annahme, welche die Grundlage in dieser Anwendung arithmetischer Verhältnisse auf geometrische Figurationen ausmacht, ein, nämlich daß das arithmetische Multipliciren auch für die geometrische Bestimmung ein Übergang in eine höhere Dimension,—die arithmetische Multiplikation von Größen, die ihrer räumlichen Bestimmungen nach Linien sind, zugleich eine Produktion des Linearen zur Flächenbestimmung sey; 3mal 4 lineare Fuße giebt 12 lineare Fuße, aber 3 lineare Fuße, mal 4 linearen Fußen giebt 12 Flächenfuße und zwar Quadratfuße, indem die Einheit in beiden als diskreten Größen dieselbe ist. Die Multiplikation von Linien mit Linien bietet sich zunächst als etwas Widersinniges dar, insofern die Multiplikation überhaupt Zahlen betrifft, d. i. eine Veränderung von solchen ist, welche mit dem, in das sie übergehen, mit dem Produkte ganz homogen sind, und nur die Größe verändern. Dagegen ist das, was Multipliciren der Linie als solcher mit Linie hieße,—es ist, ductus lineae in lineam, wie plani in planum genannt worden, es ist auch ductus puncti in lineam—eine Veränderung nicht bloß der Größe, sondern ihrer als qualitativer Bestimmung der Räumlichkeit, als einer Dimension; das Übergehen der Linie in Fläche ist als Außersichkommen derselben zu fassen, wie das Außersichkommen des Punktes die Linie, der Fläche ein ganzer Raum ist. Es ist dieß dasselbe, was so vorgestellt wird, daß die Bewegung des Punktes die Linie u.s.f. sey; aber die Bewegung schließt die Zeitbestimmung ein, und erscheint so in jener Vorstellung mehr nur als eine zufällige, äußerliche Veränderung des Zustands; es ist aber die Begriffsbestimmtheit, die als Außersichkommen ausgedrückt worden, zu nehmen,—die qualitative Veränderung, und welche arithmetisch ein Multipliciren, der Einheit (als des Punktes u.s.f.) in die Anzahl (in die Linie u.s.f.) ist.—Es kann hiezu noch bemerkt werden, daß bei dem Außersichkommen der Fläche, was als ein Multipliciren von Fläche in Fläche erscheinen würde, sich der Schein eines Unterschiedes des arithmetischen und geometrischen Producirens so ergiebt, daß das Außersichkommen der Fläche, als ductus plani in planum arithmetisch eine Multiplikation der zweiten Dimensionsbestimmung mit solcher, hiermit ein Product von vier Dimensionen gäbe, das aber durch die geometrische Bestimmung auf drei herabgesetzt wird. Wenn auf der einen Seite die Zahl darum, weil sie das Eins zu ihrem Princip hat, die feste Bestimmung für das äußerliche Quantitative giebt, so sehr ist ihr Produciren formell; 3. 3 als Zahlbestimmung genommen sich selbst producirend ist 3. 3. 3. 3; aber dieselbe Größe als Flächenbestimmung sich producirend wird bei 3. 3. 3 zurückgehalten, weil der Raum als ein Hinausgehen vom Punkte, der nur abstrakten Grenze, aus vorgestellt, seine wahrhafte Grenze, als konkrete Bestimmtheit von der Linie aus in der dritten Dimension hat. Der angeführte Unterschied könnte sich in Rücksicht der freien Bewegung, worin die eine die räumliche Seite, unter der geometrischen Bestimmung (im kepplerischen Gesetze s[hoch 3] : t[hoch 2]), die andere, die zeitliche Seite unter der arithmetischen steht, von Wirksamkeit zeigen.\n\nWie das Qualitative, das hier betrachtet wird, von dem Gegenstande der vor. Anm. verschieden ist, kann nun ohne weitere Bemerkung von selbst erhellen. In dieser lag das Qualitative in der Potenzenbestimmtheit; hier ist dasselbe, wie das Unendlichkleine, nur als Faktor arithmetisch gegen das Produkt, oder als Punkt gegen die Linie, Linie gegen Fläche u.s.f. Der qualitative Übergang nun, der von dem Diskreten, als in welches die kontinuirliche Größe aufgelöst vorgestellt wird, zu dem Kontinuirlichen zu machen ist, wird als ein Summiren bewerkstelligt.\n\nDaß aber die angebliche bloße Summation in der That eine Multiplikation, also den Übergang von der linearen in die Flächenbestimmung in sich selbst enthält, erscheint am einfachsten in der Art, wie zum Beispiel gezeigt wird, daß der Flächeninhalt eines Trapezes gleich sey dem Produkt der Summe der beiden gegenüberstehenden parallelen Linien in die halbe Höhe. Diese Höhe wird nur als die Anzahl von einer Menge diskreter Größen vorgestellt, welche summirt werden sollen.\n\nDiese Größen sind Linien, die parallel zwischen jenen zwei begrenzenden Parallelen liegen; es sind deren unendlich viele; denn sie sollen die Fläche ausmachen, sind aber Linien, welche also um ein Flächenhaftes zu seyn, zugleich mit der Negation gesetzt werden müssen. Um der Schwierigkeit zu entgehen, daß eine Summe von Linien eine Fläche geben sollte, werden Linien sogleich als Flächen aber gleichfalls als unendlich dünne angenommen, denn ihre Determination haben sie allein in dem Linearen der parallelen Grenzen des Trapezes. Als parallel und durch das andre Paar der geradlinigten Seiten des Trapezes begrenzt, können sie als die Glieder einer arithmetischen Progression vorgestellt werden, deren Differenz dieselbe überhaupt ist, aber nicht bestimmt zu werden braucht, und deren erstes und letztes Glied jene beiden Parallelen sind; die Summe solcher Reihe ist bekanntlich das Produkt jener Parallelen in die halbe Anzahl der Glieder. Dieß letzte Quantum ist nur ganz relativ auf die Vorstellung von den unendlich vielen Linien Anzahl genannt; es ist die Größebestimmtheit überhaupt eines Kontinuirlichen,—der Höhe. Es ist deutlich, daß was Summe heißt, zugleich ein ductus lineae in lineam, Multipliciren von Linearem mit Linearem, nach obiger Bestimmung ein Hervorgehen von Flächenhaftem ist. In dem einfachsten Falle nun eines Rektangels überhaupt a b ist jeder der beiden Faktoren eine einfache Größe, aber schon in dem weitern selbst elementarischen Beispiele vom Trapez ist nur der eine Faktor das Einfache der halben Höhe, der andere dagegen wird durch eine Progression bestimmt; er ist gleichfalls ein Lineares, dessen Größebestimmtheit aber verwickelter ist; insofern sie nur durch eine Reihe ausgedrückt werden kann, so heißt analytisch, d. h. arithmetisch das Interesse, sie zu summiren; das geometrische Moment darin aber ist die Multiplikation, das Qualitative des Übergangs aus der Dimension der Linie in die Fläche; der eine Faktor ist diskret nur für die arithmetische Bestimmung des andern genommen worden, und ist für sich, wie dieser, die Größe eines Linearen.\n\nDas Verfahren, Flächen als Summen von Linien vorzustellen, wird aber auch häufig gebraucht, wo nicht eine Multiplikation als solche zu Behufe des Resultates Statt hat. Dieß geschieht, wo es nicht darum zu thun ist, die Größe in der Gleichung als Quantum anzugeben, sondern in einer Proportion. Es ist z.B. eine bekannte Art zu zeigen, daß eine Kreisfläche sich zur Fläche einer Ellipse, deren große Achse der Diameter jenes Kreises ist, verhalte wie die große zur kleinen Achse, indem jede dieser Flächen als die Summe der ihr zugehörigen Ordinaten genommen wird; jede Ordinate der Ellipse verhält sich zu der entsprechenden des Kreises wie die kleine zur großen Achse, also wird geschlossen, verhalten auch die Summen der Ordinaten d. i. die Flächen ebenso. Diejenigen, welche dabei die Vorstellung der Fläche als eine Summe von Linien vermeiden wollen, machen die Ordinaten mit der gewöhnlichen ganz überflüssigen Aushülfe zu Trapezen von unendlich kleiner Breite; da die Gleichung nur eine Proportion ist, kommt nur das Eine der zwei linearen Elemente der Fläche in Vergleichung. Das andere, die Abscissenachse, ist in Ellipse und Kreis als gleich, als Faktor arithmetischer Größebestimmung also gleich = 1 angenommen, und die Proportion daher ganz nur von dem Verhältniß des einen bestimmenden Moments abhängig. Zur Vorstellung der Fläche sind die zwei Dimensionen nothwendig; aber die Größebestimmung, wie sie in jener Proportion angegeben werden soll, geht nur auf das eine Moment allein; der Vorstellung damit nachgeben oder aufhelfen, daß die Vorstellung von Summe zu diesem einen Momente hinzugefügt wird, ist eigentlich eine Verkennung dessen, worauf es hier für die mathematische Bestimmtheit ankömmt.\n\nWas hier auseinandergesetzt worden, enthält auch das Kriterium für die früher erwähnte Methode der Untheilbaren des Cavalleri, die damit ebenso gerechtfertigt ist, und der Zuflucht zu dem Unendlichkleinen nicht bedarf. Diese Untheilbaren sind Linien, indem er eine Fläche, oder Quadrate, Kreisflächen, indem er eine Pyramide oder Konus u.s.f. betrachtet; die als bestimmt angenommene Grundlinie, Grundfläche nennt er die Regel; es ist die Konstante, in Beziehung auf eine Reihe das erste oder letzte Glied derselben; mit ihr werden jene Untheilbaren parallel, also in gleicher Bestimmung in Rücksicht der Figur betrachtet, Der allgemeine Grundsatz Cavalleri's ist nun, (Exerc. Geometr. VI.—das spätere Werk-Exerc. I. p. 6.), daß alle sowohl ebene, als körperliche Figuren im Verhältnisse aller ihrer Indivisibilien sind, diese kollektive und wenn etwa ein gemeinschaftliches Verhältniß in solchen Statt findet, distributive mit einander verglichen.\"—Er vergleicht zu diesem Behufe in den Figuren von gleicher Grundlinie und Höhe gemacht, die Verhältnisse von den Linien, die parallel mit jener und in gleicher Entfernung mit ihr gezogen werden; alle solche Linien einer Figur haben eine und dieselbe Bestimmung, und machen deren ganzen Inhalt aus. Auf solche Weise beweist Cavalleri z.B. auch den elementarischen Satz, daß Parallelogramme von gleicher Höhe im Verhältnisse ihrer Grundlinie sind; jede zwei Linien, in gleicher Entfernung von der Grundlinie und mit ihr parallel, in beiden Figuren gezogen, sind in demselben Verhältnisse der Grundlinien, also die ganzen Figuren. In der That machen die Linien nicht den Inhalt der Figur als kontinuirlicher aus, aber den Inhalt, insofern er arithmetisch bestimmt werden soll; das Lineare ist sein Element, durch welches allein die Bestimmtheit desselben gefaßt werden muß.\n\nWir werden hierbei darauf geführt, auf den Unterschied zu reflektiren, der in Ansehung dessen Statt findet, worein die Bestimmtheit einer Figur fällt, nämlich entweder ist sie beschaffen, wie hier die Höhe der Figur, oder ist sie äußere Grenze. Insofern sie als äußere Grenze ist, giebt man zu, daß der Gleichheit oder dem Verhältnisse der Grenze die Kontinuität der Figur so zu sagen folgt; z.B. die Gleichheit der Figuren, die sich decken, beruht darauf, daß die begrenzenden Linien sich decken. Bei Parallelogrammen aber von gleicher Höhe und Grundlinie ist nur die letztere Bestimmtheit eine äußere Grenze; die Höhe, nicht die Paralleleität überhaupt, auf welcher die zweite Hauptbestimmung der Figuren, ihr Verhältniß, beruht, führt ein zweites Princip der Bestimmung zu den äußern Grenzen herbei. Der euklidische Beweis von der Gleichheit der Parallelogramme, die gleiche Höhe und Grundlinie haben, führt sie auf Dreiecke zurück, auf äußerlich begrenzte Kontinuirliche; in Cavalleri's Beweis, zunächst über die Proportionalität von Parallelogrammen, ist die Grenze Größebestimmtheit als solche überhaupt, welche als an jedem Paare von Linien, die mit gleichem Abstand in beiden Figuren gezogen werden, genommen, explicirt wird, Diese gleichen oder in gleichem Verhältniß mit der Grundlinie stehenden Linien, kollektiv genommen, geben die in gleichem Verhältnisse stehenden Figuren. Die Vorstellung eines Aggregats von Linien geht gegen die Kontinuität der Figur; allein die Betrachtung der Linien erschöpft die Bestimmtheit, auf welche es ankommt, vollkommen Cavalleri giebt häufige Antwort auf die Schwierigkeit, als ob die Vorstellung von den Untheilbaren es mit sich führe, daß der Anzahl nach unendliche Linien oder Ebenen verglichen werden sollen, (Geom. Lib. II. Prop. 1. Schol.); er macht den richtigen Unterschied, daß er nicht die Anzahl derselben, welche wir nicht kennen,—d. i. vielmehr die, wie bemerkt worden, eine zu Hülfe genommene leere Vorstellung ist,—sondern nur die Größe, d. i. die quantitative Bestimmtheit als solche, welche dem von diesen Linien eingenommenen Raume gleich ist, vergleiche; weil dieser in Grenzen eingeschlossen ist, ist auch jene seine Größe in dieselben Grenzen eingeschlossen; das Kontinuirliche ist nichts anderes, als die Untheilbaren selbst, sagt er; wäre es etwas außer diesen, so wäre es nicht vergleichbar; es würde aber ungereimt seyn, zu sagen, begrenzte Kontinuirliche seyen nicht miteinander vergleichbar.\n\nMan sieht, daß Cavalleri dasjenige, was zur äußerlichen Existenz des Kontinuirlichen gehört, von demjenigen unterscheiden will, worin dessen Bestimmtheit fällt und das für die Vergleichung und zum Behufe von Theoremen über dasselbe allein herauszuheben ist. Die Kategorien, die er dabei gebraucht, daß das Kontinuirliche aus den Untheilbaren zusammengesetzt sey oder bestehe und dergleichen, sind freilich nicht genügend, weil dabei die Anschauung des Kontinuirlichen oder, wie vorhin gesagt, dessen äußerliche Existenz, zugleich in Anspruch genommen wird; statt zu sagen, \"daß das Kontinuirliche nichts anderes ist, als die Untheilbaren selbst,\" würde es richtiger und damit auch sogleich für sich klar heißen, daß die Größebestimmtheit des Kontinuirlichen keine andere ist, als die der Untheilbaren selbst. —Cavalleri macht sich nichts aus der schlechten Folgerung, daß es größere und kleinere Unendliche gebe, welche aus der Vorstellung, daß die Untheilbaren das Kontinuirliche ausmachen, von der Schule gezogen werde, und drückt weiterhin (Geom. Lib. VII. Praef.) das bestimmtere Bewußtseyn aus, daß er durch seine Beweisart keineswegs zur Vorstellung der Zusammensetzung des Kontinuirlichen aus dem Untheilbaren genöthigt sey; die Kontinuirlichen folgen nur der Proportion der Untheilbaren. Er habe die Aggregate der Untheilbaren nicht so genommen, wie sie in die Bestimmung der Unendlichkeit, um einer unendlichen Menge von Linien oder Ebenen willen, zu verfallen scheinen, sondern insofern sie eine bestimmte Beschaffenheit und Natur der Begrenztheit an ihnen haben. Um denn aber doch diesen Stein des Anstoßes zu entfernen, läßt er sich die Mühe nicht verdrießen, noch in dem eigens dafür hinzugefügten siebenten Buche, die Hauptsätze seiner Geometrie auf eine Art zu beweisen, welche von der Einmischung der Unendlichkeit frei bleibe.—Diese Manier reducirt die Beweise auf die vorhin angeführte, gewöhnliche Form des Deckens der Figuren, d. i. wie bemerkt worden, der Vorstellung der Bestimmtheit als äußerer Raumgrenze.\n\nÜber diese Form des Deckens kann zunächst noch diese Bemerkung gemacht werden, daß sie überhaupt eine so zu sagen kindliche Hülfe für die sinnliche Anschauung ist. In den elementarischen Sätzen über die Dreiecke werden zwei solche neben einander vorgestellt, und indem von ihren je sechs Stücken gewisse drei als gleich groß mit den entsprechenden drei des andern Dreiecks angenommen werden, so wird gezeigt, daß solche Dreiecke einander kongruent seyen, d. i. jedes auch die übrigen drei Stücke gleich groß mit denen des andern habe, —weil sie vermöge der Gleichheit nach jenen drei ersten einander decken. Die Sache abstrakter gefaßt, so ist eben um dieser Gleichheit jeden Paars der in beiden einander entsprechenden Stücke, nur Ein Dreieck vorhanden; in diesem sind drei Stücke als bereits bestimmt angenommen, woraus denn die Bestimmtheit auch der drei übrigen Stücke folgt. Die Bestimmtheit wird auf diese Weise als in drei Stücken vollendet aufgezeigt; für die Bestimmtheit als solche sind somit die drei übrigen Stücke ein Überfluß, der Überfluß der sinnlichen Existenz, d. i. der Anschauung der Kontinuität. In solcher Form ausgesprochen, tritt hier die qualitative Bestimmtheit im Unterschiede von dem hervor, was in der Anschauung vorliegt, dem Ganzen als einem in sich kontinuirlichen; das Decken läßt diesen Unterschied nicht zum Bewußtseyn kommen.\n\nMit den Parallellinien und bei den Parallelogrammen tritt, wie bemerkt worden, ein neuer Umstand, Theils die Gleichheit nur der Winkel Theils die Höhe der Figuren ein, von welcher letztern deren äußere Grenzen, die Seiten der Parallelogramme, unterschieden sind. Hierbei kommt die Zweideutigkeit zum Vorschein, inwiefern bei diesen Figuren außer der Bestimmtheit der einen Seite, der Grundlinie, welche als äußere Grenze ist, für die andere Bestimmtheit, die andere äußere Grenze, nämlich die andere Seite des Parallelogramms, oder aber die Höhe zu nehmen ist. Bei zwei solchen Figuren von einerlei Grundlinie und Höhe, wovon das eine rechtwinklich ist, das andere sehr spitze, damit zu den gegenüberstehenden sehr stumpfe Winkel hat, kann der Anschauung letzteres leicht größer scheinen, als das erstere, insofern sie die vorliegende große Seite desselben als bestimmend nimmt, und nach der Vorstellungsweise Cavalleri's die Ebenen nach einer Menge von parallelen Linien, durch welche sie durchschnitten werden können, vergleicht; die größere Seite könnte als eine Möglichkeit von mehrern Linien, als die senkrechte Seite des Rechtecks giebt, angesehen werden. Solche Vorstellung giebtjedoch keinen Einwurf gegen Cavalleri's Methode an die Hand; denn die in beiden Parallelogrammen für die Vergleichung vorgestellte Menge von parallelen Linien setzt die Gleichheit ihrer Entfernung von einander oder von der Grundlinie zugleich voraus, woraus folgt, daß die Höhe, und nicht die andere Seite des Parallelogramms, das andere bestimmende Moment ist. Dieß ändert sich aber ferner, wenn zwei Parallelogramme mit einander verglichen werden, die von gleicher Höhe und Grundlinie sind, aber nicht in Einer Ebene liegen, und zu einer dritten Ebene verschiedene Winkel machen; hier sind die parallelen Durchschnitte, die entstehen, wenn man sich die dritte Ebene durch sie gelegt und sich parallel mit sich fortbewegend vorstellt, nicht mehr gleich weit von einander entfernt, und jene zwei Ebenen sind einander ungleich. Cavalleri macht sehr sorgfältig auf diesen Unterschied, den er als einen Unterschied von transitus rectus und transitus obliquus der Untheilbaren bestimmt, (gleich in Exercit. I. n. XII. ff. wie schon in der Geometr. I. II.) auf merksam, und schneidet damit oberflächlichen Mißverstand ab, der nach dieser Seite entstehen könnte. Ich erinnere mich, daß Barrow in seinem obenangeführten Werke (Lect. Geom. II. p. 21), indem er die Methode der Untheilbaren gleichfalls gebraucht, jedoch sie bereits mit der von ihm aus auf seinen Schüler Newton und die sonstigen mathematischen Zeitgenossen, darunter auch Leibnitz, übergegangenen Annahme der Gleichsetzbarkeit eines krummlinigten Dreiecks, wie das sogenannte charakteristische ist, mit einem geradlinigten, insofern beide unendlich d. h. sehr klein seyen, versetzt und verunreinigt hat, —einen eben dahin gehenden Einwurf Tacquet's, eines damaligen in neuen Methoden gleichfalls thätigen, scharfsinnigen Geometers, anführte. Die von diesem gemachte Schwierigkeit bezieht sich ebenfalls darauf, welche Linie und zwar bei Berechnung konischer und sphärischer Oberflächen als Grundmoment der Bestimmung für die auf Anwendung des Diskreten gestützte Betrachtung genommen werden solle. Tacquet wende gegen die Methode der Untheilbaren ein, daß wenn die Oberfläche eines rechtwinklichten Kegels berechnet werden solle, so werde nach jener atomistischen Methode das Dreieck des Kegels als zusammengesetzt aus den geraden, mit der Grundlinie parallelen auf die Achse senkrechten Linien vorgestellt, welche zugleich die Radien der Kreise sind, aus denen die Oberfläche des Kegels bestehe. Wenn nun diese Oberfläche als Summe der Peripherien, und diese Summe aus der Anzahl ihrer Radien, d. i. der Größe der Achse, der Höhe des Kegels, bestimmt werde, so sey solches Resultat mit der sonst von Archimed gelehrten und bewiesenen Wahrheit im Widerspruch. Barrow zeigt nun dagegen, daß für die Bestimmung der Oberfläche nicht die Achse, sondern die Seite des Dreiecks des Kegels als diejenige Linie genommen werden müsse, deren Umdrehung die Oberfläche erzeuge, und welche daher, und nicht die Achse, als die Größebestimmtheit für die Menge der Peripherien angenommen werden müsse.\n\nDergleichen Einwürfe oder Unsicherheiten haben ihre Quelle allein in der gebrauchten unbestimmten Vorstellung der unendlichen Menge von Punkten, aus denen die Linie, oder von Linien, aus denen die Fläche u. s.f. bestehend angesehen wird; durch diese Vorstellung wird die wesentliche Größebestimmtheit der Linien oder Flächen in Schatten gestellt.—Es ist die Absicht dieser Anmerkungen gewesen, die affirmativen Bestimmungen, die bei dem verschiedenen Gebrauch, der von dem Unendlich-kleinen in der Mathematik gemacht wird, so zu sagen im Hintergrunde bleiben, aufzuweisen und sie aus der Nebulosität hervorzuheben, in welche sie durch jene bloß negativ gehaltene Kategorie gehüllt werden. Bei der unendlichen Reihe, wie in der archimedischen Kreismessung bedeutet das Unendliche nichts weiter, als daß das Gesetz der Fortbestimmung bekannt ist, aber der sogenannte endliche Ausdruck, d. i. der arithmetische, nicht gegeben, die Zurückführung des Bogens auf die gerade Linie nicht bewerkstelligt werden kann; diese Inkommensurabilität ist die qualitative Verschiedenheit derselben. Die qualitative Verschiedenheit des Diskreten mit dem Kontinuirlichen überhaupt, enthält gleichfalls eine negative Bestimmung, welche sie als inkommensurabel erscheinen läßt, und das Unendliche herbeiführt, in dem Sinne, daß das als diskret zu nehmende Kontinuirliche nun kein Quantum nach seiner kontinuirlichen Bestimmtheit mehr haben soll. Das Kontinuirliche, das arithmetisch als Produkt zu nehmen ist, ist damit diskret an ihm selbst gesetzt, nämlich in die Elemente, die seine Faktoren sind, zerlegt; in diesen liegt seine Größebestimmtheit; sie sind als ebendamit, daß sie diese Faktoren oder Elemente sind, von einer niedrigern Dimension, und insofern die Potenzenbestimmtheit eintritt, von einer niedrigern Potenz als die Größe, deren Elemente oder Faktoren sie sind. Arithmetisch erscheint dieser Unterschied als ein bloß quantitativer, der Wurzel und der Potenz oder welcher Potenzenbestimmtheit es sey; jedoch wenn der Ausdruck nur auf das Quantitative als solches geht, z.B. a : a[hoch 2] oder d.a[hoch 2] = 2a : a[hoch 2] = 2 : a, oder für das Gesetz des Falles, t : at[hoch 2] so giebt er die nichtssagenden Verhältnisse von 1 : a, 2 : a, 1: at; die Seiten müßten gegen ihre bloß quantitative Bestimmung durch die unterschiedene qualitative Bedeutung auseinander gehalten werden, wie s : at[hoch]2; wodurch die Größe als eine Qualität ausgesprochen wird, als Funktion der Größe einer andern Qualität. Hierbei steht dann bloß die quantitative Bestimmtheit vor dem Bewußtseyn, mit der nach ihrer Art ohne Schwierigkeit operirt wird, und man kann kein Arges daran haben, die Größe einer Linie mit der Größe einer andern Linie zu multipliciren; aber die Multiplikation dieser selben Größen giebt zugleich die qualitative Veränderung des Überganges von Linie in Fläche; insofern tritt eine negative Bestimmung ein; sie ist es, welche die Schwierigkeit veranlaßt, die durch die Einsicht in ihre Eigenthümlichkeit und in die einfache Natur der Sache gelöst, aber durch die Hilfe des Unendlichen, wodurch sie beseitigt werden soll, vielmehr nur in Verworrenheit gesetzt und ganz unaufgelöst erhalten wird.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Das Unendlichkleine der Differentialrechnung ist in seinem affirmativen Sinn als die qualitative Größenbestimmtheit, und von dieser näher aufgezeigt worden, daß sie in diesem Kalkul als Potenzenbestimmtheit nicht nur überhaupt, sondern als die besondere des Verhältnisses einer Potenzenfunktion zu der Entwicklungspotenz vorhanden ist. Die qualitative Bestimmtheit ist aber auch noch in weiterer, so zu sagen, schwächerer Form vorhanden, und diese, wie auch der damit zusammenhängende Gebrauch des Unendlichkleinen und dessen Sinn in diesem Gebrauche, soll noch in dieser Anmerkung betrachtet werden.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Es ist, indem wir vom Vorhergehenden ausgehen, in dieser Rücksicht zuerst daran zu erinnern, daß die unterschiedenen Potenzenbestimmungen von der analytischen Seite zunächst so hervortreten, daß sie nur formell, und ganz homogen darin sind, daß sie Zahlengrößen bedeuten, die als solche jene qualitative Verschiedenheit gegeneinander nicht haben. Aber in der Anwendung auf räumliche Gegenstände zeigt sich das analytische Verhältniß ganz in seiner qualitativen Bestimmtheit, als das Übergehen von linearen zu Flächenbestimmungen, von geradlinigten zu krummlinigten u.s.f. Diese Anwendung bringt es ferner mit sich, daß die räumlichen ihrer Natur nach in Form von kontinuirlichen Größen gegebenen Gegenstände in diskreter Weise gefaßt werden, die Fläche also als eine Menge von Linien, die Linie als eine Menge von Punkten u.s.f. Diese Auflösung hat das einzige Interesse, die Punkte, in welche die Linie, die Linien, in welche die Fläche u.s.f. aufgelöst ist, selbst zu bestimmen, um von solcher Bestimmung aus analytisch, d. h. eigentlich arithmetisch fortgehen zu können; diese Ausgangspunkte sind für die zu findenden Größebestimmungen die Elemente, aus welchen die Funktion und Gleichung für das Konkrete, die kontinuirliche Größe, abgeleitet werden soll. Für die Probleme, wo sich nornehmlich das Interesse zeigt, dieß Verfahren zu gebrauchen, wird im Elemente für den Ausgang ein für sich selbst Bestimmtes verlangt, gegen den Gang, der indirekt ist, indem er im Gegentheil nur mit Grenzen beginnen kann, zwischen welchen das Fürsichbestimmte liege, auf das als sein Ziel er losgehe. Das Resultat läuft in beiden Methoden dann auf dasselbe hinaus, wenn sich nur das Gesetz des weitern Fortbestimmens finden läßt, ohne die geforderte vollkommene d. h. sogenannte endliche Bestimmung erlangen zu können. Kepplern wird die Ehre zugeschrieben, zuerst den Gedanken jener Umkehrung des Ganges gehabt und das Diskrete zum Ausgangspunkte gemacht zu haben. Seine Erklärung, wie er den ersten Satz in Archimed's Kreismessung verstehe, drückt dieß auf eine einfache Weise aus. Der erste Satz Archimed's ist bekanntlich, daß der Kreis einem rechtwinklichten Dreieck gleich ist, dessen eine Kathete dem Halbmesser, die andere dem Umfange des Kreises gleich ist. Indem Keppler den Sinn dieses Satzes so nimmt, daß die Peripherie des Kreises ebenso viele Theile als Punkte, d. i. unendlich viele habe, deren jeder als die Grundlinie eines gleichschenklichten Dreiecks betrachtet werden könne, u.s.f., so spricht er die Auflösung des Kontinuirlichen in die Form des Diskreten aus. Der Ausdruck des Unendlichen, der hierbei vorkommt, ist noch weit entfernt von der Bestimmung, die er in dem Differentialkalkul haben soll.—Wenn nun für solche diskrete eine Bestimmtheit, Funktion gefunden ist, so sollen sie ferner zusammengefaßt werden, wesentlich als Elemente des Kontinuirlichen seyn. Da aber eine Summe von Punkten keine Linie, eine Summe von Linien keine Fläche giebt, werden die Punkte schon sogleich als lineare genommen, wie die Linien als flächenhafte. Weil jedoch zugleich jene Lineare noch keine Linien seyn sollen, was sie seyn würden, wenn sie als Quantum genommen würden, so werden sie als unendlich klein vorgestellt. Das Diskrete ist nur eines äußerlichen Zusammenfassens fähig, in welchem die Momente den Sinn von diskretem Eins behalten; der analytische Übergang von denselben geschieht nur zu ihrer Summe, er ist nicht zugleich der geometrische von dem Punkte in die Linie, oder von der Linie in die Fläche u.s.f.; dem Elemente, das als Punkt oder als Linie seine Bestimmung hat, wird daher zugleich auch mit jenem die lineare, dieser die Flächenqualität gegeben, damit die Summe als von kleinen Linien eine Linie, als von kleinen Flächen eine Fläche werde.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Das Bedürfniß, dieß Moment des qualitativen Übergangs zu erhalten und dafür zu dem Unendlich-kleinen die Zuflucht zu nehmen, muß als die Quelle aller der Vorstellungen angesehen werden, welche, indem sie jene Schwierigkeit ausgleichen sollen, an ihnen selbst die größte Schwierigkeit sind. Diese Nothhülfe entbehrlich zu machen, müßte gezeigt werden können, daß in dem analytischen Verfahren selbst, welches als ein bloßes Summiren erscheint, in der That schon ein Multipliciren enthalten ist. Aber in dieser Rücksicht tritt eine neue Annahme, welche die Grundlage in dieser Anwendung arithmetischer Verhältnisse auf geometrische Figurationen ausmacht, ein, nämlich daß das arithmetische Multipliciren auch für die geometrische Bestimmung ein Übergang in eine höhere Dimension,—die arithmetische Multiplikation von Größen, die ihrer räumlichen Bestimmungen nach Linien sind, zugleich eine Produktion des Linearen zur Flächenbestimmung sey; 3mal 4 lineare Fuße giebt 12 lineare Fuße, aber 3 lineare Fuße, mal 4 linearen Fußen giebt 12 Flächenfuße und zwar Quadratfuße, indem die Einheit in beiden als diskreten Größen dieselbe ist. Die Multiplikation von Linien mit Linien bietet sich zunächst als etwas Widersinniges dar, insofern die Multiplikation überhaupt Zahlen betrifft, d. i. eine Veränderung von solchen ist, welche mit dem, in das sie übergehen, mit dem Produkte ganz homogen sind, und nur die Größe verändern. Dagegen ist das, was Multipliciren der Linie als solcher mit Linie hieße,—es ist, ductus lineae in lineam, wie plani in planum genannt worden, es ist auch ductus puncti in lineam—eine Veränderung nicht bloß der Größe, sondern ihrer als qualitativer Bestimmung der Räumlichkeit, als einer Dimension; das Übergehen der Linie in Fläche ist als Außersichkommen derselben zu fassen, wie das Außersichkommen des Punktes die Linie, der Fläche ein ganzer Raum ist. Es ist dieß dasselbe, was so vorgestellt wird, daß die Bewegung des Punktes die Linie u.s.f. sey; aber die Bewegung schließt die Zeitbestimmung ein, und erscheint so in jener Vorstellung mehr nur als eine zufällige, äußerliche Veränderung des Zustands; es ist aber die Begriffsbestimmtheit, die als Außersichkommen ausgedrückt worden, zu nehmen,—die qualitative Veränderung, und welche arithmetisch ein Multipliciren, der Einheit (als des Punktes u.s.f.) in die Anzahl (in die Linie u.s.f.) ist.—Es kann hiezu noch bemerkt werden, daß bei dem Außersichkommen der Fläche, was als ein Multipliciren von Fläche in Fläche erscheinen würde, sich der Schein eines Unterschiedes des arithmetischen und geometrischen Producirens so ergiebt, daß das Außersichkommen der Fläche, als ductus plani in planum arithmetisch eine Multiplikation der zweiten Dimensionsbestimmung mit solcher, hiermit ein Product von vier Dimensionen gäbe, das aber durch die geometrische Bestimmung auf drei herabgesetzt wird. Wenn auf der einen Seite die Zahl darum, weil sie das Eins zu ihrem Princip hat, die feste Bestimmung für das äußerliche Quantitative giebt, so sehr ist ihr Produciren formell; 3. 3 als Zahlbestimmung genommen sich selbst producirend ist 3. 3. 3. 3; aber dieselbe Größe als Flächenbestimmung sich producirend wird bei 3. 3. 3 zurückgehalten, weil der Raum als ein Hinausgehen vom Punkte, der nur abstrakten Grenze, aus vorgestellt, seine wahrhafte Grenze, als konkrete Bestimmtheit von der Linie aus in der dritten Dimension hat. Der angeführte Unterschied könnte sich in Rücksicht der freien Bewegung, worin die eine die räumliche Seite, unter der geometrischen Bestimmung (im kepplerischen Gesetze s[hoch 3] : t[hoch 2]), die andere, die zeitliche Seite unter der arithmetischen steht, von Wirksamkeit zeigen.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Wie das Qualitative, das hier betrachtet wird, von dem Gegenstande der vor. Anm. verschieden ist, kann nun ohne weitere Bemerkung von selbst erhellen. In dieser lag das Qualitative in der Potenzenbestimmtheit; hier ist dasselbe, wie das Unendlichkleine, nur als Faktor arithmetisch gegen das Produkt, oder als Punkt gegen die Linie, Linie gegen Fläche u.s.f. Der qualitative Übergang nun, der von dem Diskreten, als in welches die kontinuirliche Größe aufgelöst vorgestellt wird, zu dem Kontinuirlichen zu machen ist, wird als ein Summiren bewerkstelligt.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Daß aber die angebliche bloße Summation in der That eine Multiplikation, also den Übergang von der linearen in die Flächenbestimmung in sich selbst enthält, erscheint am einfachsten in der Art, wie zum Beispiel gezeigt wird, daß der Flächeninhalt eines Trapezes gleich sey dem Produkt der Summe der beiden gegenüberstehenden parallelen Linien in die halbe Höhe. Diese Höhe wird nur als die Anzahl von einer Menge diskreter Größen vorgestellt, welche summirt werden sollen.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Diese Größen sind Linien, die parallel zwischen jenen zwei begrenzenden Parallelen liegen; es sind deren unendlich viele; denn sie sollen die Fläche ausmachen, sind aber Linien, welche also um ein Flächenhaftes zu seyn, zugleich mit der Negation gesetzt werden müssen. Um der Schwierigkeit zu entgehen, daß eine Summe von Linien eine Fläche geben sollte, werden Linien sogleich als Flächen aber gleichfalls als unendlich dünne angenommen, denn ihre Determination haben sie allein in dem Linearen der parallelen Grenzen des Trapezes. Als parallel und durch das andre Paar der geradlinigten Seiten des Trapezes begrenzt, können sie als die Glieder einer arithmetischen Progression vorgestellt werden, deren Differenz dieselbe überhaupt ist, aber nicht bestimmt zu werden braucht, und deren erstes und letztes Glied jene beiden Parallelen sind; die Summe solcher Reihe ist bekanntlich das Produkt jener Parallelen in die halbe Anzahl der Glieder. Dieß letzte Quantum ist nur ganz relativ auf die Vorstellung von den unendlich vielen Linien Anzahl genannt; es ist die Größebestimmtheit überhaupt eines Kontinuirlichen,—der Höhe. Es ist deutlich, daß was Summe heißt, zugleich ein ductus lineae in lineam, Multipliciren von Linearem mit Linearem, nach obiger Bestimmung ein Hervorgehen von Flächenhaftem ist. In dem einfachsten Falle nun eines Rektangels überhaupt a b ist jeder der beiden Faktoren eine einfache Größe, aber schon in dem weitern selbst elementarischen Beispiele vom Trapez ist nur der eine Faktor das Einfache der halben Höhe, der andere dagegen wird durch eine Progression bestimmt; er ist gleichfalls ein Lineares, dessen Größebestimmtheit aber verwickelter ist; insofern sie nur durch eine Reihe ausgedrückt werden kann, so heißt analytisch, d. h. arithmetisch das Interesse, sie zu summiren; das geometrische Moment darin aber ist die Multiplikation, das Qualitative des Übergangs aus der Dimension der Linie in die Fläche; der eine Faktor ist diskret nur für die arithmetische Bestimmung des andern genommen worden, und ist für sich, wie dieser, die Größe eines Linearen.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0007","text":"Das Verfahren, Flächen als Summen von Linien vorzustellen, wird aber auch häufig gebraucht, wo nicht eine Multiplikation als solche zu Behufe des Resultates Statt hat. Dieß geschieht, wo es nicht darum zu thun ist, die Größe in der Gleichung als Quantum anzugeben, sondern in einer Proportion. Es ist z.B. eine bekannte Art zu zeigen, daß eine Kreisfläche sich zur Fläche einer Ellipse, deren große Achse der Diameter jenes Kreises ist, verhalte wie die große zur kleinen Achse, indem jede dieser Flächen als die Summe der ihr zugehörigen Ordinaten genommen wird; jede Ordinate der Ellipse verhält sich zu der entsprechenden des Kreises wie die kleine zur großen Achse, also wird geschlossen, verhalten auch die Summen der Ordinaten d. i. die Flächen ebenso. Diejenigen, welche dabei die Vorstellung der Fläche als eine Summe von Linien vermeiden wollen, machen die Ordinaten mit der gewöhnlichen ganz überflüssigen Aushülfe zu Trapezen von unendlich kleiner Breite; da die Gleichung nur eine Proportion ist, kommt nur das Eine der zwei linearen Elemente der Fläche in Vergleichung. Das andere, die Abscissenachse, ist in Ellipse und Kreis als gleich, als Faktor arithmetischer Größebestimmung also gleich = 1 angenommen, und die Proportion daher ganz nur von dem Verhältniß des einen bestimmenden Moments abhängig. Zur Vorstellung der Fläche sind die zwei Dimensionen nothwendig; aber die Größebestimmung, wie sie in jener Proportion angegeben werden soll, geht nur auf das eine Moment allein; der Vorstellung damit nachgeben oder aufhelfen, daß die Vorstellung von Summe zu diesem einen Momente hinzugefügt wird, ist eigentlich eine Verkennung dessen, worauf es hier für die mathematische Bestimmtheit ankömmt.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0008","text":"Was hier auseinandergesetzt worden, enthält auch das Kriterium für die früher erwähnte Methode der Untheilbaren des Cavalleri, die damit ebenso gerechtfertigt ist, und der Zuflucht zu dem Unendlichkleinen nicht bedarf. Diese Untheilbaren sind Linien, indem er eine Fläche, oder Quadrate, Kreisflächen, indem er eine Pyramide oder Konus u.s.f. betrachtet; die als bestimmt angenommene Grundlinie, Grundfläche nennt er die Regel; es ist die Konstante, in Beziehung auf eine Reihe das erste oder letzte Glied derselben; mit ihr werden jene Untheilbaren parallel, also in gleicher Bestimmung in Rücksicht der Figur betrachtet, Der allgemeine Grundsatz Cavalleri's ist nun, (Exerc. Geometr. VI.—das spätere Werk-Exerc. I. p. 6.), daß alle sowohl ebene, als körperliche Figuren im Verhältnisse aller ihrer Indivisibilien sind, diese kollektive und wenn etwa ein gemeinschaftliches Verhältniß in solchen Statt findet, distributive mit einander verglichen.\"—Er vergleicht zu diesem Behufe in den Figuren von gleicher Grundlinie und Höhe gemacht, die Verhältnisse von den Linien, die parallel mit jener und in gleicher Entfernung mit ihr gezogen werden; alle solche Linien einer Figur haben eine und dieselbe Bestimmung, und machen deren ganzen Inhalt aus. Auf solche Weise beweist Cavalleri z.B. auch den elementarischen Satz, daß Parallelogramme von gleicher Höhe im Verhältnisse ihrer Grundlinie sind; jede zwei Linien, in gleicher Entfernung von der Grundlinie und mit ihr parallel, in beiden Figuren gezogen, sind in demselben Verhältnisse der Grundlinien, also die ganzen Figuren. In der That machen die Linien nicht den Inhalt der Figur als kontinuirlicher aus, aber den Inhalt, insofern er arithmetisch bestimmt werden soll; das Lineare ist sein Element, durch welches allein die Bestimmtheit desselben gefaßt werden muß.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0009","text":"Wir werden hierbei darauf geführt, auf den Unterschied zu reflektiren, der in Ansehung dessen Statt findet, worein die Bestimmtheit einer Figur fällt, nämlich entweder ist sie beschaffen, wie hier die Höhe der Figur, oder ist sie äußere Grenze. Insofern sie als äußere Grenze ist, giebt man zu, daß der Gleichheit oder dem Verhältnisse der Grenze die Kontinuität der Figur so zu sagen folgt; z.B. die Gleichheit der Figuren, die sich decken, beruht darauf, daß die begrenzenden Linien sich decken. Bei Parallelogrammen aber von gleicher Höhe und Grundlinie ist nur die letztere Bestimmtheit eine äußere Grenze; die Höhe, nicht die Paralleleität überhaupt, auf welcher die zweite Hauptbestimmung der Figuren, ihr Verhältniß, beruht, führt ein zweites Princip der Bestimmung zu den äußern Grenzen herbei. Der euklidische Beweis von der Gleichheit der Parallelogramme, die gleiche Höhe und Grundlinie haben, führt sie auf Dreiecke zurück, auf äußerlich begrenzte Kontinuirliche; in Cavalleri's Beweis, zunächst über die Proportionalität von Parallelogrammen, ist die Grenze Größebestimmtheit als solche überhaupt, welche als an jedem Paare von Linien, die mit gleichem Abstand in beiden Figuren gezogen werden, genommen, explicirt wird, Diese gleichen oder in gleichem Verhältniß mit der Grundlinie stehenden Linien, kollektiv genommen, geben die in gleichem Verhältnisse stehenden Figuren. Die Vorstellung eines Aggregats von Linien geht gegen die Kontinuität der Figur; allein die Betrachtung der Linien erschöpft die Bestimmtheit, auf welche es ankommt, vollkommen Cavalleri giebt häufige Antwort auf die Schwierigkeit, als ob die Vorstellung von den Untheilbaren es mit sich führe, daß der Anzahl nach unendliche Linien oder Ebenen verglichen werden sollen, (Geom. Lib. II. Prop. 1. Schol.); er macht den richtigen Unterschied, daß er nicht die Anzahl derselben, welche wir nicht kennen,—d. i. vielmehr die, wie bemerkt worden, eine zu Hülfe genommene leere Vorstellung ist,—sondern nur die Größe, d. i. die quantitative Bestimmtheit als solche, welche dem von diesen Linien eingenommenen Raume gleich ist, vergleiche; weil dieser in Grenzen eingeschlossen ist, ist auch jene seine Größe in dieselben Grenzen eingeschlossen; das Kontinuirliche ist nichts anderes, als die Untheilbaren selbst, sagt er; wäre es etwas außer diesen, so wäre es nicht vergleichbar; es würde aber ungereimt seyn, zu sagen, begrenzte Kontinuirliche seyen nicht miteinander vergleichbar.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Man sieht, daß Cavalleri dasjenige, was zur äußerlichen Existenz des Kontinuirlichen gehört, von demjenigen unterscheiden will, worin dessen Bestimmtheit fällt und das für die Vergleichung und zum Behufe von Theoremen über dasselbe allein herauszuheben ist. Die Kategorien, die er dabei gebraucht, daß das Kontinuirliche aus den Untheilbaren zusammengesetzt sey oder bestehe und dergleichen, sind freilich nicht genügend, weil dabei die Anschauung des Kontinuirlichen oder, wie vorhin gesagt, dessen äußerliche Existenz, zugleich in Anspruch genommen wird; statt zu sagen, \"daß das Kontinuirliche nichts anderes ist, als die Untheilbaren selbst,\" würde es richtiger und damit auch sogleich für sich klar heißen, daß die Größebestimmtheit des Kontinuirlichen keine andere ist, als die der Untheilbaren selbst. —Cavalleri macht sich nichts aus der schlechten Folgerung, daß es größere und kleinere Unendliche gebe, welche aus der Vorstellung, daß die Untheilbaren das Kontinuirliche ausmachen, von der Schule gezogen werde, und drückt weiterhin (Geom. Lib. VII. Praef.) das bestimmtere Bewußtseyn aus, daß er durch seine Beweisart keineswegs zur Vorstellung der Zusammensetzung des Kontinuirlichen aus dem Untheilbaren genöthigt sey; die Kontinuirlichen folgen nur der Proportion der Untheilbaren. Er habe die Aggregate der Untheilbaren nicht so genommen, wie sie in die Bestimmung der Unendlichkeit, um einer unendlichen Menge von Linien oder Ebenen willen, zu verfallen scheinen, sondern insofern sie eine bestimmte Beschaffenheit und Natur der Begrenztheit an ihnen haben. Um denn aber doch diesen Stein des Anstoßes zu entfernen, läßt er sich die Mühe nicht verdrießen, noch in dem eigens dafür hinzugefügten siebenten Buche, die Hauptsätze seiner Geometrie auf eine Art zu beweisen, welche von der Einmischung der Unendlichkeit frei bleibe.—Diese Manier reducirt die Beweise auf die vorhin angeführte, gewöhnliche Form des Deckens der Figuren, d. i. wie bemerkt worden, der Vorstellung der Bestimmtheit als äußerer Raumgrenze.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0011","text":"Über diese Form des Deckens kann zunächst noch diese Bemerkung gemacht werden, daß sie überhaupt eine so zu sagen kindliche Hülfe für die sinnliche Anschauung ist. In den elementarischen Sätzen über die Dreiecke werden zwei solche neben einander vorgestellt, und indem von ihren je sechs Stücken gewisse drei als gleich groß mit den entsprechenden drei des andern Dreiecks angenommen werden, so wird gezeigt, daß solche Dreiecke einander kongruent seyen, d. i. jedes auch die übrigen drei Stücke gleich groß mit denen des andern habe, —weil sie vermöge der Gleichheit nach jenen drei ersten einander decken. Die Sache abstrakter gefaßt, so ist eben um dieser Gleichheit jeden Paars der in beiden einander entsprechenden Stücke, nur Ein Dreieck vorhanden; in diesem sind drei Stücke als bereits bestimmt angenommen, woraus denn die Bestimmtheit auch der drei übrigen Stücke folgt. Die Bestimmtheit wird auf diese Weise als in drei Stücken vollendet aufgezeigt; für die Bestimmtheit als solche sind somit die drei übrigen Stücke ein Überfluß, der Überfluß der sinnlichen Existenz, d. i. der Anschauung der Kontinuität. In solcher Form ausgesprochen, tritt hier die qualitative Bestimmtheit im Unterschiede von dem hervor, was in der Anschauung vorliegt, dem Ganzen als einem in sich kontinuirlichen; das Decken läßt diesen Unterschied nicht zum Bewußtseyn kommen.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012","text":"Mit den Parallellinien und bei den Parallelogrammen tritt, wie bemerkt worden, ein neuer Umstand, Theils die Gleichheit nur der Winkel Theils die Höhe der Figuren ein, von welcher letztern deren äußere Grenzen, die Seiten der Parallelogramme, unterschieden sind. Hierbei kommt die Zweideutigkeit zum Vorschein, inwiefern bei diesen Figuren außer der Bestimmtheit der einen Seite, der Grundlinie, welche als äußere Grenze ist, für die andere Bestimmtheit, die andere äußere Grenze, nämlich die andere Seite des Parallelogramms, oder aber die Höhe zu nehmen ist. Bei zwei solchen Figuren von einerlei Grundlinie und Höhe, wovon das eine rechtwinklich ist, das andere sehr spitze, damit zu den gegenüberstehenden sehr stumpfe Winkel hat, kann der Anschauung letzteres leicht größer scheinen, als das erstere, insofern sie die vorliegende große Seite desselben als bestimmend nimmt, und nach der Vorstellungsweise Cavalleri's die Ebenen nach einer Menge von parallelen Linien, durch welche sie durchschnitten werden können, vergleicht; die größere Seite könnte als eine Möglichkeit von mehrern Linien, als die senkrechte Seite des Rechtecks giebt, angesehen werden. Solche Vorstellung giebtjedoch keinen Einwurf gegen Cavalleri's Methode an die Hand; denn die in beiden Parallelogrammen für die Vergleichung vorgestellte Menge von parallelen Linien setzt die Gleichheit ihrer Entfernung von einander oder von der Grundlinie zugleich voraus, woraus folgt, daß die Höhe, und nicht die andere Seite des Parallelogramms, das andere bestimmende Moment ist. Dieß ändert sich aber ferner, wenn zwei Parallelogramme mit einander verglichen werden, die von gleicher Höhe und Grundlinie sind, aber nicht in Einer Ebene liegen, und zu einer dritten Ebene verschiedene Winkel machen; hier sind die parallelen Durchschnitte, die entstehen, wenn man sich die dritte Ebene durch sie gelegt und sich parallel mit sich fortbewegend vorstellt, nicht mehr gleich weit von einander entfernt, und jene zwei Ebenen sind einander ungleich. Cavalleri macht sehr sorgfältig auf diesen Unterschied, den er als einen Unterschied von transitus rectus und transitus obliquus der Untheilbaren bestimmt, (gleich in Exercit. I. n. XII. ff. wie schon in der Geometr. I. II.) auf merksam, und schneidet damit oberflächlichen Mißverstand ab, der nach dieser Seite entstehen könnte. Ich erinnere mich, daß Barrow in seinem obenangeführten Werke (Lect. Geom. II. p. 21), indem er die Methode der Untheilbaren gleichfalls gebraucht, jedoch sie bereits mit der von ihm aus auf seinen Schüler Newton und die sonstigen mathematischen Zeitgenossen, darunter auch Leibnitz, übergegangenen Annahme der Gleichsetzbarkeit eines krummlinigten Dreiecks, wie das sogenannte charakteristische ist, mit einem geradlinigten, insofern beide unendlich d. h. sehr klein seyen, versetzt und verunreinigt hat, —einen eben dahin gehenden Einwurf Tacquet's, eines damaligen in neuen Methoden gleichfalls thätigen, scharfsinnigen Geometers, anführte. Die von diesem gemachte Schwierigkeit bezieht sich ebenfalls darauf, welche Linie und zwar bei Berechnung konischer und sphärischer Oberflächen als Grundmoment der Bestimmung für die auf Anwendung des Diskreten gestützte Betrachtung genommen werden solle. Tacquet wende gegen die Methode der Untheilbaren ein, daß wenn die Oberfläche eines rechtwinklichten Kegels berechnet werden solle, so werde nach jener atomistischen Methode das Dreieck des Kegels als zusammengesetzt aus den geraden, mit der Grundlinie parallelen auf die Achse senkrechten Linien vorgestellt, welche zugleich die Radien der Kreise sind, aus denen die Oberfläche des Kegels bestehe. Wenn nun diese Oberfläche als Summe der Peripherien, und diese Summe aus der Anzahl ihrer Radien, d. i. der Größe der Achse, der Höhe des Kegels, bestimmt werde, so sey solches Resultat mit der sonst von Archimed gelehrten und bewiesenen Wahrheit im Widerspruch. Barrow zeigt nun dagegen, daß für die Bestimmung der Oberfläche nicht die Achse, sondern die Seite des Dreiecks des Kegels als diejenige Linie genommen werden müsse, deren Umdrehung die Oberfläche erzeuge, und welche daher, und nicht die Achse, als die Größebestimmtheit für die Menge der Peripherien angenommen werden müsse.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0013","text":"Dergleichen Einwürfe oder Unsicherheiten haben ihre Quelle allein in der gebrauchten unbestimmten Vorstellung der unendlichen Menge von Punkten, aus denen die Linie, oder von Linien, aus denen die Fläche u. s.f. bestehend angesehen wird; durch diese Vorstellung wird die wesentliche Größebestimmtheit der Linien oder Flächen in Schatten gestellt.—Es ist die Absicht dieser Anmerkungen gewesen, die affirmativen Bestimmungen, die bei dem verschiedenen Gebrauch, der von dem Unendlich-kleinen in der Mathematik gemacht wird, so zu sagen im Hintergrunde bleiben, aufzuweisen und sie aus der Nebulosität hervorzuheben, in welche sie durch jene bloß negativ gehaltene Kategorie gehüllt werden. Bei der unendlichen Reihe, wie in der archimedischen Kreismessung bedeutet das Unendliche nichts weiter, als daß das Gesetz der Fortbestimmung bekannt ist, aber der sogenannte endliche Ausdruck, d. i. der arithmetische, nicht gegeben, die Zurückführung des Bogens auf die gerade Linie nicht bewerkstelligt werden kann; diese Inkommensurabilität ist die qualitative Verschiedenheit derselben. Die qualitative Verschiedenheit des Diskreten mit dem Kontinuirlichen überhaupt, enthält gleichfalls eine negative Bestimmung, welche sie als inkommensurabel erscheinen läßt, und das Unendliche herbeiführt, in dem Sinne, daß das als diskret zu nehmende Kontinuirliche nun kein Quantum nach seiner kontinuirlichen Bestimmtheit mehr haben soll. Das Kontinuirliche, das arithmetisch als Produkt zu nehmen ist, ist damit diskret an ihm selbst gesetzt, nämlich in die Elemente, die seine Faktoren sind, zerlegt; in diesen liegt seine Größebestimmtheit; sie sind als ebendamit, daß sie diese Faktoren oder Elemente sind, von einer niedrigern Dimension, und insofern die Potenzenbestimmtheit eintritt, von einer niedrigern Potenz als die Größe, deren Elemente oder Faktoren sie sind. Arithmetisch erscheint dieser Unterschied als ein bloß quantitativer, der Wurzel und der Potenz oder welcher Potenzenbestimmtheit es sey; jedoch wenn der Ausdruck nur auf das Quantitative als solches geht, z.B. a : a[hoch 2] oder d.a[hoch 2] = 2a : a[hoch 2] = 2 : a, oder für das Gesetz des Falles, t : at[hoch 2] so giebt er die nichtssagenden Verhältnisse von 1 : a, 2 : a, 1: at; die Seiten müßten gegen ihre bloß quantitative Bestimmung durch die unterschiedene qualitative Bedeutung auseinander gehalten werden, wie s : at[hoch]2; wodurch die Größe als eine Qualität ausgesprochen wird, als Funktion der Größe einer andern Qualität. Hierbei steht dann bloß die quantitative Bestimmtheit vor dem Bewußtseyn, mit der nach ihrer Art ohne Schwierigkeit operirt wird, und man kann kein Arges daran haben, die Größe einer Linie mit der Größe einer andern Linie zu multipliciren; aber die Multiplikation dieser selben Größen giebt zugleich die qualitative Veränderung des Überganges von Linie in Fläche; insofern tritt eine negative Bestimmung ein; sie ist es, welche die Schwierigkeit veranlaßt, die durch die Einsicht in ihre Eigenthümlichkeit und in die einfache Natur der Sache gelöst, aber durch die Hilfe des Unendlichen, wodurch sie beseitigt werden soll, vielmehr nur in Verworrenheit gesetzt und ganz unaufgelöst erhalten wird.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"5d4187081389c45a60029eb33182b1a38e3dce1540f3f3ad15c624aa1a957f0a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 3. Other Forms Connected with Qualitative Determinacy of Magnitude.","source_sha256":"5d4187081389c45a60029eb33182b1a38e3dce1540f3f3ad15c624aa1a957f0a","sha256":"53a029cd857c1ca0cb954c1fb809e51be629b7488935419a8420cc81b7a89748","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:39:13.683778+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0001","text":"The infinitesimal of the differential calculus, in its affirmative sense, is qualitative determinateness of magnitude, and it has been shown more closely of this that, in this calculus, it is present as determinateness of powers not merely in general, but as the particular determinateness of the relation of a power-function to the power of development. But qualitative determinateness is also present in a further, so to speak weaker, form, and this, as also the use of the infinitesimal connected therewith and its meaning in this use, is still to be considered in this note.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Proceeding from what precedes, it is first to be recalled in this respect that the distinct determinations of powers initially emerge, on the analytical side, in such a way that they are merely formal, and quite homogeneous in signifying numerical magnitudes which, as such, do not have that qualitative difference from one another. But in application to spatial objects, the analytical relation displays itself quite in its qualitative determinateness, as the transition from linear to superficial determinations, from rectilinear to curvilinear ones, and so forth. This application further entails that the spatial objects, which by their nature are given in the form of continuous magnitudes, are apprehended in a discrete manner, the surface thus as a multitude of lines, the line as a multitude of points, and so forth.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0003","text":"This resolution has the sole interest of determining the points into which the line, the lines into which the surface, and so forth, are resolved, in order to be able to proceed analytically from such determination, i.e. properly arithmetically; these points of departure are, for the determinations of magnitude to be found, the elements from which the function and equation for the concrete, the continuous magnitude, are to be derived. For the problems in which especially the interest in using this procedure shows itself, something determined for itself is required in the element for the point of departure, as against the course which is indirect, in that it can, on the contrary, begin only with limits between which the self-determined lies, towards which it proceeds as its aim.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0004","text":"The result in both methods then comes to the same thing, provided only that the law of further determination can be found, without being able to attain the required complete, i.e. so-called finite, determination. Kepler is credited with the honour of first having had the thought of that reversal of the course and of having made the discrete the point of departure. His explanation of how he understands the first proposition in Archimedes' Measurement of the Circle expresses this in a simple manner. Archimedes' first proposition is famously that the circle is equal to a right-angled triangle whose one leg is equal to the radius and the other to the circumference of the circle. In taking the meaning of this proposition to be that the periphery of the circle has as many parts as points, i.e.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0005","text":"infinitely many, each of which can be regarded as the base of an isosceles triangle, and so forth, he expresses the resolution of the continuous into the form of the discrete. The expression of the infinite which occurs here is still far removed from the determination it is to have in the differential calculus.—If now a determinateness, a function, has been found for such discrete [elements], they are further to be combined, essentially as elements of the continuous. But since a sum of points gives no line, a sum of lines no surface, the points are immediately taken as linear, just as the lines are taken as superficial. Yet because these linear [elements] are at the same time not yet to be lines, which they would be if they were taken as quantum, they are represented as infinitely small.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0006","text":"The discrete is capable only of an external combination, in which the moments retain the sense of discrete ones; the analytical transition from them proceeds only to their sum; it is not at the same time the geometrical transition from the point into the line, or from the line into the surface, and so forth. Thus to the element which has its determination as point or as line is given, together with the former, the linear quality, and to the latter the superficial quality, so that the sum may become a line as a sum of small lines, and a surface as a sum of small surfaces.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0007","text":"The need to preserve this moment of qualitative transition and for this purpose to have recourse to the infinitesimal must be regarded as the source of all those representations which, while they are meant to compensate for that difficulty, are in themselves the greatest difficulty. In order to make this makeshift unnecessary, it would have to be possible to show that in the analytical procedure itself, which appears as a mere summing, multiplication is in fact already contained.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0008","text":"But in this respect a new assumption enters, which constitutes the basis in this application of arithmetical relations to geometrical configurations, namely that arithmetical multiplication is also, for geometrical determination, a transition into a higher dimension,—that the arithmetical multiplication of magnitudes which, according to their spatial determinations, are lines, is at the same time a production of the linear into the determination of surface; 3 times 4 linear feet gives 12 linear feet, but 3 linear feet multiplied by 4 linear feet gives 12 superficial feet, namely square feet, since the unit is the same in both as discrete magnitudes. The multiplication of lines by lines initially presents itself as something absurd, inasmuch as multiplication in general concerns numbers, i.e.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0009","text":"a change of such [numbers], which are quite homogeneous with that into which they pass, with the product, and only alters the magnitude. On the other hand, what multiplying line as such by line would mean—it has been called ductus lineae in lineam, as [has] plani in planum; it is also ductus puncti in lineam—is a change not merely of magnitude, but of it as qualitative determination of spatiality, as a dimension; the transition of the line into surface is to be apprehended as its coming-outside-itself, just as the coming-outside-itself of the point is the line, [and] of the surface an entire space. This is the same thing as is represented by saying that the movement of the point [produces] the line, and so forth.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0010","text":"is; but movement includes the determination of time, and thus appears in that representation rather only as a contingent, external alteration of state; but the determinateness of the concept, which has been expressed as coming-outside-itself, is to be taken,—the qualitative alteration, and that which arithmetically is a multiplication, of the unit (as point, and so forth) into number (into line, and so forth).—It may further be remarked here that in the coming-outside-itself of the surface, which would appear as a multiplication of surface by surface, the appearance of a difference between arithmetical and geometrical production arises thus: the coming-outside-itself of the surface, as ductus plani in planum, would arithmetically give a multiplication of the determination of the second dimension by the same, hence a product of four dimensions, which, however, is reduced to three by geometrical determination.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0011","text":"If, on the one hand, number, because it has one as its principle, gives the fixed determination for the external quantitative, its production is nevertheless formal; 3. 3, taken as a numerical determination, producing itself, is 3. 3. 3. 3; but the same magnitude, producing itself as a determination of surface, is held back at 3. 3. 3, because space, represented as a going-forth from the point, which is merely the abstract limit, has its true limit, as concrete determinateness, from the line onward in the third dimension. The difference adduced could show itself as effective in respect of free movement, in which the one side, the spatial side, stands under geometrical determination (in the Keplerian law s[super 3] : t[super 2]), the other, the temporal side, under arithmetical [determination].","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0004","text":"How the qualitative which is considered here differs from the object of the preceding note can now become clear of itself without further remark. In that note, the qualitative lay in the determinateness of powers; here it, like the infinitesimal, is only arithmetically a factor as against the product, or a point as against the line, a line as against the surface, and so forth. The qualitative transition which is to be made from the discrete, into which the continuous magnitude is represented as resolved, to the continuous, is effected as a summing.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0005","text":"But that the alleged mere summation in fact contains within itself a multiplication, hence the transition from linear to superficial determination, appears most simply in the manner in which, for example, it is shown that the area of a trapezoid is equal to the product of the sum of the two opposite parallel lines by half the height. This height is represented only as the number of a multitude of discrete magnitudes which are to be summed.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0014","text":"These magnitudes are lines lying parallel between those two bounding parallels; there are infinitely many of them, for they are to constitute the surface, but they are lines which, therefore, in order to be something superficial, must at the same time be posited with negation. To avoid the difficulty that a sum of lines should give a surface, lines are immediately assumed as surfaces, but likewise as infinitely thin, for they have their determination solely in the linearity of the parallel boundaries of the trapezoid.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0015","text":"As parallel and bounded by the other pair of rectilinear sides of the trapezoid, they can be represented as the terms of an arithmetical progression, whose difference is the same in general, but need not be determined, and whose first and last terms are those two parallels; the sum of such a series is famously the product of those parallels by half the number of terms. This latter quantum is called number only quite relatively to the representation of the infinitely many lines; it is the determinateness of magnitude in general of a continuous [magnitude],—the height. It is clear that what is called sum is at the same time a ductus lineae in lineam, a multiplication of linear by linear, according to the above determination an emergence of the superficial.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0016","text":"Now in the simplest case of a rectangle in general a b, each of the two factors is a simple magnitude; but already in the further, itself elementary, example of the trapezoid, only one factor is the simple [one], half the height, whereas the other is determined by a progression; it likewise is something linear, but one whose determinateness of magnitude is more intricate; insofar as it can be expressed only by a series, the analytical, i.e. arithmetical, interest is called that of summing it; but the geometrical moment therein is multiplication, the qualitative [moment] of transition from the dimension of line into surface; the one factor has been taken as discrete only for the arithmetical determination of the other, and is in itself, like the latter, the magnitude of something linear.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0017","text":"But the procedure of representing surfaces as sums of lines is also frequently used where multiplication as such does not take place for the sake of the result. This occurs where the issue is not to state the magnitude in the equation as quantum, but in a proportion. It is, for example, a well-known way of showing that the area of a circle is related to the area of an ellipse, whose major axis is the diameter of that circle, as the major to the minor axis, by taking each of these areas as the sum of its corresponding ordinates; each ordinate of the ellipse is related to the corresponding one of the circle as the minor to the major axis; thus it is concluded that the sums of the ordinates, i.e. the areas, are likewise so related.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0018","text":"Those who wish to avoid in this connection the representation of the surface as a sum of lines turn the ordinates, with the usual quite superfluous expedient, into trapezoids of infinitesimal breadth; since the equation is only a proportion, only one of the two linear elements of the surface enters into comparison. The other, the axis of abscissas, is assumed as equal in ellipse and circle, hence as a factor of arithmetical determination of magnitude equal to = 1, and the proportion is therefore entirely dependent only on the relation of the one determining moment.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0019","text":"For the representation of the surface, the two dimensions are necessary; but the determination of magnitude, as it is to be stated in that proportion, concerns only the one moment alone; to yield to or assist representation by adding to this one moment the representation of sum is properly a misapprehension of what is at issue here for mathematical determinateness.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0007"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0020","text":"What has been expounded here also contains the criterion for the previously mentioned method of Cavalieri's indivisibles, which is thereby equally justified and has no need of recourse to the infinitesimal. These indivisibles are lines when he considers a surface, or squares, circular areas, when he considers a pyramid or cone, and so forth; he calls the assumed determinate base line, base surface, the rule; it is the constant, in relation to a series its first or last term; with it those indivisibles are considered parallel, hence in the same determination with respect to the figure. Cavalieri's general principle is now (Exerc. Geometr. VI.—the later work—Exerc. I. p.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0021","text":"6.), that all figures, both plane and solid, are compared with one another in the ratio of all their indivisibles, collectively, and, where a common ratio obtains in such [indivisibles], distributively.\"—For this purpose he compares, in figures made with the same base-line and height, the ratios of the lines drawn parallel to the latter and at the same distance from it; all such lines of a figure have one and the same determination, and make up its entire content. In this way Cavalleri also proves, for example, the elementary proposition that parallelograms of the same height are in the ratio of their base-lines; any two lines, drawn in both figures at the same distance from the base-line and parallel to it, are in the same ratio as the base-lines, and hence so are the whole figures.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0022","text":"In fact, the lines do not make up the content of the figure as continuous, but [they make up] the content insofar as it is to be determined arithmetically; the linear is its element, by which alone its determinacy must be apprehended.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0008"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0023","text":"We are hereby led to reflect upon the distinction which takes place with regard to that in which the determinacy of a figure falls: namely, it is either constituted as here the height of the figure is, or it is an external boundary. Insofar as it is an external boundary, it is granted that the continuity of the figure, so to speak, follows from the equality or ratio of the boundary; e.g., the equality of figures which cover one another rests on the fact that the bounding lines cover one another. In parallelograms of the same height and base-line, however, only the latter determinacy is an external boundary; the height—not parallelism in general, upon which the second principal determinacy of the figures, their ratio, rests—introduces a second principle of determination alongside the external boundaries.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0024","text":"Euclid’s proof of the equality of parallelograms which have the same height and base-line reduces them to triangles, to continuously extended things externally bounded; in Cavalleri’s proof, initially concerning the proportionality of parallelograms, the boundary is determination of magnitude as such in general, which is explicated as taken in every pair of lines drawn at equal distances in both figures. These lines, equal or standing in the same ratio to the base-line, taken collectively, yield the figures standing in the same ratio.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0025","text":"The representation of an aggregate of lines runs counter to the continuity of the figure; yet the consideration of the lines completely exhausts the determinacy at issue. Cavalleri frequently answers the difficulty as though the representation of indivisibles entailed that lines or planes infinite in number should be compared (Geom. Lib. II. Prop. 1. Schol.); he makes the correct distinction that he compares not their number, which we do not know,—i.e., rather, which, as has been observed, is an empty representation invoked for assistance,—but only the magnitude, i.e.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0026","text":"the quantitative determinacy as such, which is equal to the space occupied by these lines; because this is enclosed within boundaries, its magnitude too is enclosed within the same boundaries; the continuous is nothing other than the indivisibles themselves, he says; if it were something besides these, it would not be comparable; but it would be absurd to say that bounded continuous things are not comparable with one another.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0009"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0027","text":"It can be seen that Cavalleri wishes to distinguish that which belongs to the external existence of the continuous from that in which its determinacy lies and which alone is to be singled out for comparison and for the purpose of theorems concerning it. The categories he employs in this connection, that the continuous is composed of or consists of the indivisibles, and such like, are indeed insufficient, because the intuition of the continuous, or, as was said above, its external existence, is thereby simultaneously invoked; instead of saying \"that the continuous is nothing other than the indivisibles themselves,\" it would be more correct, and therewith immediately clear in itself, to say that the determinacy of magnitude of the continuous is no other than that of the indivisibles themselves.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0028","text":"—Cavalleri makes nothing of the bad inference that there are greater and smaller infinites, which the school draws from the representation that indivisibles make up the continuous; and further on (Geom. Lib. VII. Praef.) he expresses the more determinate consciousness that his mode of proof by no means obliges him to the representation of the composition of the continuous out of the indivisible; the continuous things merely follow the proportion of the indivisibles. He has not taken the aggregates of indivisibles in the manner in which they seem to lapse into the determination of infinity, on account of an infinite multitude of lines or planes, but insofar as they have in them a determinate constitution and nature of boundedness.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0029","text":"But in order nevertheless to remove this stumbling-block, he does not begrudge the trouble, even in the seventh book specially added for this purpose, of proving the principal propositions of his geometry in a manner which remains free from the admixture of infinity.—This manner reduces the proofs to the previously adduced ordinary form of the covering of figures, i.e., as has been noted, to the representation of determinacy as external spatial boundary.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0010"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0030","text":"Concerning this form of covering, the following observation may first be made: that it is in general, so to speak, a childish aid to sensuous intuition. In the elementary propositions concerning triangles, two such [triangles] are presented side by side; and, since of their respective six parts three are assumed to be equal in magnitude to the corresponding three of the other triangle, it is shown that such triangles are congruent to one another, i.e., that each also has the remaining three parts equal in magnitude to those of the other,—because, by virtue of equality in respect of those first three, they cover one another. Taken more abstractly, there is, precisely on account of this equality of each pair of parts corresponding to one another in both, only One triangle present; in this, three parts are assumed as already determined, from which the determinacy of the other three parts then follows.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0031","text":"In this way determinacy is displayed as completed in three parts; for determinacy as such, the three remaining parts are thus a superfluity, the superfluity of sensuous existence, i.e. of the intuition of continuity. Expressed in such a form, qualitative determinacy here emerges in distinction from what lies before intuition, the whole as continuous within itself; covering does not allow this distinction to come to consciousness.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0011"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0032","text":"With parallel lines and in the case of parallelograms, as has been noted, a new circumstance emerges: partly the equality merely of the angles, partly the height of the figures, from which latter their external boundaries, the sides of the parallelograms, are distinguished. Here the ambiguity becomes apparent as to whether, in these figures, besides the determinacy of the one side, the base-line, which is an external boundary, the other side of the parallelogram, the other external boundary, or rather the height, is to be taken for the other determinacy.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0033","text":"In the case of two such figures with the same base-line and height, one of which is rectangular while the other has very acute and thus, opposite these, very obtuse angles, the latter can easily seem greater than the former to intuition, insofar as it takes its large side lying before it as determining, and, in Cavalleri’s manner of representation, compares the planes according to a multitude of parallel lines by which they can be intersected; the greater side could be regarded as the possibility of more lines than the perpendicular side of the rectangle affords.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0034","text":"Such a representation, however, supplies no objection against Cavalleri’s method; for the multitude of parallel lines represented for comparison in both parallelograms simultaneously presupposes the equality of their distance from one another or from the base-line, whence it follows that the height, and not the other side of the parallelogram, is the other determining moment. But this changes further when two parallelograms are compared with one another which have the same height and base-line, but do not lie in One plane and make different angles with a third plane; here the parallel sections which arise when one imagines the third plane laid through them and moving parallel to itself are no longer equally distant from one another, and those two planes are unequal to one another.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0035","text":"Cavalleri very carefully calls attention to this distinction, which he determines as a distinction between transitus rectus and transitus obliquus of the indivisibles (already in Exercit. I. n. XII. ff., as in Geometr. I. II.), and thereby cuts off a superficial misunderstanding which might arise in this respect. I recall that Barrow, in his work cited above (Lect. Geom. II. p. 21), while likewise employing the method of indivisibles, had nevertheless already displaced and contaminated it with the assumption, emanating from him and passing on to his pupil Newton and to the other mathematical contemporaries, among them Leibniz as well, of the equivalence of a curvilinear triangle, such as the so-called characteristic [triangle], with a rectilinear one, insofar as both are infinitely, i.e.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0036","text":"very small,—adduced an objection of Tacquet tending in the same direction, a keen-witted geometer of that time likewise active in new methods. The difficulty raised by him likewise concerns which line, and specifically in the calculation of conical and spherical surfaces, is to be taken as the fundamental moment of determination for the consideration based upon the application of the discrete. Tacquet objects to the method of indivisibles that, if the surface of a right cone is to be calculated, then, according to that atomistic method, the triangle of the cone is represented as composed of the straight lines parallel to the base-line and perpendicular to the axis, which are at the same time the radii of the circles of which the surface of the cone consists.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0037","text":"Now if this surface is determined as the sum of the circumferences, and this sum from the number of their radii, i.e. from the magnitude of the axis, the height of the cone, then such a result is in contradiction with the truth otherwise taught and proved by Archimedes. Barrow, on the other hand, shows that for the determination of the surface not the axis, but the side of the triangle of the cone must be taken as that line whose rotation generates the surface, and which therefore, rather than the axis, must be assumed as the determinacy of magnitude for the multitude of circumferences.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0012"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0038","text":"Objections or uncertainties of this kind have their source solely in the indeterminate representation employed of the infinite multitude of points of which the line, or of lines of which the surface, and so forth, is regarded as consisting; by this representation the essential determinacy of magnitude of lines or surfaces is cast into shadow.—The intention of these remarks has been to point out the affirmative determinations which, in the different use made in mathematics of the infinitely small, remain, so to speak, in the background, and to draw them forth from the nebulousness into which they are enveloped by that merely negatively held category. In the infinite series, as in Archimedean measurement of the circle, the infinite signifies nothing further than that the law of continuation is known, but the so-called finite expression, i.e.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0039","text":"the arithmetical [expression], is not given, [and] the reduction of the arc to the straight line cannot be effected; this incommensurability is their qualitative difference. The qualitative difference of the discrete from the continuous in general likewise contains a negative determination, which makes them appear incommensurable and brings in the infinite, in the sense that the continuous to be taken as discrete is now no longer to have a quantum according to its continuous determinacy.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0040","text":"The continuous which is to be taken arithmetically as a product is thereby posited as discrete in itself, namely, resolved into the elements which are its factors; its determinacy of magnitude lies in these; by virtue precisely of their being these factors or elements, they are of a lower dimension, and insofar as the determination of powers enters, of a lower power than the magnitude of which they are elements or factors. Arithmetically this distinction appears as a merely quantitative one, whether of root and power or of whatever determination of powers it may be; yet if the expression concerns only the quantitative as such, e.g.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0041","text":"a : a[raised to 2] or d.a[raised to 2] = 2a : a[raised to 2] = 2 : a, or, for the law of falling, t : at[raised to 2], then it yields the unmeaning ratios of 1 : a, 2 : a, 1: at; the sides would have to be distinguished from their merely quantitative determination by their distinct qualitative significance, as s : at[raised to]2; whereby magnitude is expressed as a quality, as a function of the magnitude of another quality.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0013"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103913683754Z_f4a1999b:DISPLAY-0042","text":"In this case, then, merely quantitative determinacy is before consciousness, with which, according to its kind, one operates without difficulty, and one can see no harm in multiplying the magnitude of one line by the magnitude of another line; but the multiplication of these same magnitudes at the same time yields the qualitative alteration of the transition from line into surface; insofar a negative determination enters in; it is this which occasions the difficulty, which is resolved through insight into its peculiarity and into the simple nature of the matter, but through the aid of the infinite, by which it is supposed to be removed, is instead only cast into confusion and kept entirely unresolved.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A3NA:DISPLAY-0013"]}],"source_digest":"f702fc0a0f759b2bdefb54fa985353fa5886164c75e161841326e009c5e92733","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 3. Noch andere mit der qualitativen Größenbestimmtheit zusammenhängende Formen."}],"original_title":"Anmerkung 3. Noch andere mit der qualitativen Größenbestimmtheit zusammenhängende Formen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL","title":"A. The Direct Relation.","order":76,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DDVL","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das quantitative Verhältniß.\n\nDie Unendlichkeit des Quantums ist dahin bestimmt worden, daß sie das negative Jenseits desselben ist, das es aber an ihm selbst hat. Dieß Jenseits ist das Qualitative überhaupt. Das unendliche Quantum ist als die Einheit beider Momente, der quantitativen und der qualitativen Bestimmtheit, zunächst Verhältniß.\n\nIm Verhältnisse hat das Quantum nicht mehr eine nur gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, sondern ist qualitativ bestimmt als schlechthin bezogen auf sein Jenseits. Es kontinuirt sich in sein Jenseits; dieses ist zunächst ein anderes Quantum überhaupt. Aber wesentlich sind sie nicht als äußerliche Quanta auf einander bezogen, sondern jedes hat seine Bestimmtheit in dieser Beziehung auf das Andere. Sie sind so in diesem ihrem Andersseyn in sich zurückgekehrt; was jedes ist, ist es in dem Andern; das andere macht die Bestimmtheit eines jeden aus. —Das Hinausgehen des Quantums über sich hat also jetzt diesen Sinn, weder daß es sich nur in ein Anderes noch in sein abstraktes Anderes, in sein negatives Jenseits veränderte, sondern darin zu seiner Bestimmtheit gelangt ist; es findet sich selbst in seinem Jenseits, welches ein anderes Quantum ist. Die Qualität des Quantums, seine Begriffsbestimmtheit, ist seine Äußerlichkeit überhaupt, und im Verhältniß ist es nun so gesetzt, in seiner Äußerlichkeit, an einem andern Quantum, seine Bestimmtheit zu haben, in seinem Jenseits das zu seyn, was es ist.\n\nEs sind Quanta, welche die Beziehung, die sich ergab, auf einander haben. Diese Beziehung ist selbst auch eine Größe; das Quantum ist nicht nur im Verhältniß, sondern es selbst ist als Verhältniß gesetzt; es ist ein Quantum überhaupt, das jene qualitative Bestimmtheit innerhalb seiner hat. So als Verhältniß drückt es sich als in sich geschlossene Totalität und seine Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Grenze aus, dadurch daß es die Äußerlichkeit seines Bestimmtseyns innerhalb seiner selbst hat, und in ihr nur auf sich bezogen, somit an ihm selbst unendlich ist.\n\nDas Verhältniß überhaupt ist\n\n1. das direkte Verhältniß. In demselben tritt das Qualitative noch nicht als solches für sich heraus; es ist noch in keiner weitern Weise, als der des Quantums, daß dieses in seiner Äußerlichkeit selbst seine Bestimmtheit zu haben gesetzt ist.—Das quantitative Verhältniß ist an sich der Widerspruch der Äußerlichkeit und der Beziehung auf sich selbst, des Bestehens der Quantorum und der Negation derselben;—er hebt sich auf, indem zunächst\n\n2. im indirekten Verhältnisse, die Negation des einen Quantums als solche mit in der Veränderung des andern, und die Veränderlichkeit des direkten Verhältnisses selbst, gesetzt wird;\n\n3. im Potenzenverhältniß aber macht sich die in ihrem Unterschiede sich auf sich beziehende Einheit als einfache Selbstproduktion des Quantums geltend; dieß Qualitative selbst endlich in einfacher Bestimmung und identisch mit dem Quantum gesetzt, wird das Maaß.\n\n—Über die Natur der folgenden Verhältnisse ist Vieles in den vorhergehenden Anmerkungen, welche das Unendliche der Quantität, d. i. das qualitative Moment an derselben, betreffen, anticipirt worden; es bleibt daher nur der abstrakte Begriff dieser Verhältnisse auseinander zu setzen.\n\n## A. Das direkte Verhältniß.\n\n1. Im Verhältnisse, welches als unmittelbar das direkte ist, liegt die Bestimmtheit des einen Quantums gegenseitig in der Bestimmtheit des andern. Es ist nur Eine Bestimmtheit oder Grenze beider, die selbst Quantum ist, der Exponent des Verhältnisses.\n\n2. Der Exponent ist irgend ein Quantum, aber in seiner Äußerlichkeit an ihm selbst sich auf sich beziehendes, qualitativ bestimmtes Quantum ist er nur, insofern er den Unterschied seiner, sein Jenseits und Andersseyn an ihm selbst hat. Dieser Unterschied des Quantums an ihm selbst aber ist der Unterschied der Einheit und der Anzahl; die Einheit—das Fürsich-bestimmtseyn; die Anzahl—das gleichgültige Hin- und Hergehen an der Bestimmtheit, die äußere Gleichgültigkeit des Quantums. Einheit und Anzahl waren zuerst die Momente des Quantums; jetzt im Verhältnisse, dem insofern realisirten Quantum, erscheint jedes seiner Momente als ein eignes Quantum, und als Bestimmungen seines Daseyns, als Begrenzungen gegen die sonst nur äußerliche, gleichgültige Größebestimmtheit.\n\nDer Exponent ist dieser Unterschied als einfache Bestimmtheit d. h. er hat unmittelbar die Bedeutung beider Bestimmungen an ihm selbst. Er ist erstens Quantum; so ist er die Anzahl; wenn die eine Seite des Verhältnisses, welche als Einheit genommen wird, als numerisches Eins ausgedrückt ist, und sie gilt nur für solches, so ist die andere, die Anzahl, das Quantum des Exponenten selbst. Zweitens ist er die einfache Bestimmtheit als das Qualitative der Seiten des Verhältnisses; wenn das Quantum der einen bestimmt ist, ist auch das andere durch den Exponenten bestimmt, und es ist völlig gleichgültig, wie das erste bestimmt wird; es hat als für sich bestimmtes Quantum keine Bedeutung mehr, sondern kann ebenso gut jedes Andere seyn, ohne die Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses zu ändern, die allein auf dem Exponenten beruht. Das eine, welches als Einheit genommen ist, bleibt, wie groß es werde, immer Einheit, und das andere, wie groß es ebenso dabei werde, muß dieselbe Anzahl jener Einheit bleiben.\n\n3. Hiernach machen beide eigentlich nur Ein Quantum aus, das eine hat gegen das andere, nur den Werth der Einheit, nicht einer Anzahl; das andre nur den der Anzahl; nach ihrer Begriffsbestimmtheit sind sie selbst somit nicht vollständige Quanta. Diese Unvollständigkeit aber ist eine Negation an ihnen und dieß nicht nach ihrer Veränderlichkeit überhaupt, nach der das Eine (und jedes ist Eines der beiden) alle mögliche Größe annehmen kann, sondern nach der Bestimmung, daß wenn das eine verändert wird, das andere um ebenso viel vermehrt oder vermindert wird; dieß heißt, wie gezeigt, nur das Eine, die Einheit, wird als Quantum verändert, die andere Seite, die Anzahl, bleibt dasselbe Quantum von Einheiten, aber auch jene bleibt ebenso nur als Einheit geltend, sie werde als Quantum verändert wie sie wolle. Jede Seite ist so nur eines der beiden Momente des Quantums, und die Selbstständigkeit, die zu dessen Eigenthümlichkeit gehört, ist an sich negirt; in diesem qualitativen Zusammenhange sind sie als negative gegen einander zu setzen.\n\nDer Exponent soll das vollständige Quantum seyn, indem die Bestimmung der beiden Seiten in ihm zusammenläuft; er hat aber in der That als Quotient selbst nur den Werth der Anzahl, oder der Einheit. Es ist keine Bestimmung vorhanden, welche der Seiten des Verhältnisses als die Einheit oder als die Anzahl genommen werden müße; die eine, das Quantum B an dem Quantum A als der Einheit gemessen, so ist der Quotient C die Anzahl solcher Einheiten; aber A selbst als Anzahl genommen, ist der Quotient C die Einheit, welche zu der Anzahl A für das Quantum B erfordert wird; dieser Quotient ist als Exponent somit nicht als das gesetzt, was er seyn soll,—das Bestimmende des Verhältnisses, oder als seine qualitative Einheit. Als diese ist er nur gesetzt, insofern er den Werth hat, die Einheit der beiden Momente, der Einheit und der Anzahl, zu seyn. Indem diese Seiten zwar als Quanta, wie sie in dem expliciten Quantum, dem Verhältnisse, seyn sollen, vorhanden sind, aber zugleich nur in dem Wertbe, den sie als dessen Seiten haben sollen, unvollständige Quanta zu seyn und nur als eines jener qualitativen Momente zu gelten, so sind sie mit dieser ihrer Negation zu setzen; womit ein seiner Bestimmung entsprechenderes reelleres Verhältniß entsteht, worin der Exponent die Bedeutung des Produkts derselben hat; nach dieser Bestimmtheit ist es das umgekehrte Verhältniß.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0001","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das quantitative Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"76.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0002","text":"Die Unendlichkeit des Quantums ist dahin bestimmt worden, daß sie das negative Jenseits desselben ist, das es aber an ihm selbst hat. Dieß Jenseits ist das Qualitative überhaupt. Das unendliche Quantum ist als die Einheit beider Momente, der quantitativen und der qualitativen Bestimmtheit, zunächst Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"76.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0003","text":"Im Verhältnisse hat das Quantum nicht mehr eine nur gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, sondern ist qualitativ bestimmt als schlechthin bezogen auf sein Jenseits. Es kontinuirt sich in sein Jenseits; dieses ist zunächst ein anderes Quantum überhaupt. Aber wesentlich sind sie nicht als äußerliche Quanta auf einander bezogen, sondern jedes hat seine Bestimmtheit in dieser Beziehung auf das Andere. Sie sind so in diesem ihrem Andersseyn in sich zurückgekehrt; was jedes ist, ist es in dem Andern; das andere macht die Bestimmtheit eines jeden aus. —Das Hinausgehen des Quantums über sich hat also jetzt diesen Sinn, weder daß es sich nur in ein Anderes noch in sein abstraktes Anderes, in sein negatives Jenseits veränderte, sondern darin zu seiner Bestimmtheit gelangt ist; es findet sich selbst in seinem Jenseits, welches ein anderes Quantum ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"76.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0004","text":"Die Qualität des Quantums, seine Begriffsbestimmtheit, ist seine Äußerlichkeit überhaupt, und im Verhältniß ist es nun so gesetzt, in seiner Äußerlichkeit, an einem andern Quantum, seine Bestimmtheit zu haben, in seinem Jenseits das zu seyn, was es ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"76.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0005","text":"Es sind Quanta, welche die Beziehung, die sich ergab, auf einander haben. Diese Beziehung ist selbst auch eine Größe; das Quantum ist nicht nur im Verhältniß, sondern es selbst ist als Verhältniß gesetzt; es ist ein Quantum überhaupt, das jene qualitative Bestimmtheit innerhalb seiner hat. So als Verhältniß drückt es sich als in sich geschlossene Totalität und seine Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Grenze aus, dadurch daß es die Äußerlichkeit seines Bestimmtseyns innerhalb seiner selbst hat, und in ihr nur auf sich bezogen, somit an ihm selbst unendlich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"76.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0006","text":"Das Verhältniß überhaupt ist","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"76.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0007","text":"1. das direkte Verhältniß. In demselben tritt das Qualitative noch nicht als solches für sich heraus; es ist noch in keiner weitern Weise, als der des Quantums, daß dieses in seiner Äußerlichkeit selbst seine Bestimmtheit zu haben gesetzt ist.—Das quantitative Verhältniß ist an sich der Widerspruch der Äußerlichkeit und der Beziehung auf sich selbst, des Bestehens der Quantorum und der Negation derselben;—er hebt sich auf, indem zunächst","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"76.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0008","text":"2. im indirekten Verhältnisse, die Negation des einen Quantums als solche mit in der Veränderung des andern, und die Veränderlichkeit des direkten Verhältnisses selbst, gesetzt wird;","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"76.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0009","text":"3. im Potenzenverhältniß aber macht sich die in ihrem Unterschiede sich auf sich beziehende Einheit als einfache Selbstproduktion des Quantums geltend; dieß Qualitative selbst endlich in einfacher Bestimmung und identisch mit dem Quantum gesetzt, wird das Maaß.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"76.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0010","text":"—Über die Natur der folgenden Verhältnisse ist Vieles in den vorhergehenden Anmerkungen, welche das Unendliche der Quantität, d. i. das qualitative Moment an derselben, betreffen, anticipirt worden; es bleibt daher nur der abstrakte Begriff dieser Verhältnisse auseinander zu setzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"76.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0011","text":"## A. Das direkte Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"76.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0012","text":"1. Im Verhältnisse, welches als unmittelbar das direkte ist, liegt die Bestimmtheit des einen Quantums gegenseitig in der Bestimmtheit des andern. Es ist nur Eine Bestimmtheit oder Grenze beider, die selbst Quantum ist, der Exponent des Verhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"76.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0013","text":"2. Der Exponent ist irgend ein Quantum, aber in seiner Äußerlichkeit an ihm selbst sich auf sich beziehendes, qualitativ bestimmtes Quantum ist er nur, insofern er den Unterschied seiner, sein Jenseits und Andersseyn an ihm selbst hat. Dieser Unterschied des Quantums an ihm selbst aber ist der Unterschied der Einheit und der Anzahl; die Einheit—das Fürsich-bestimmtseyn; die Anzahl—das gleichgültige Hin- und Hergehen an der Bestimmtheit, die äußere Gleichgültigkeit des Quantums. Einheit und Anzahl waren zuerst die Momente des Quantums; jetzt im Verhältnisse, dem insofern realisirten Quantum, erscheint jedes seiner Momente als ein eignes Quantum, und als Bestimmungen seines Daseyns, als Begrenzungen gegen die sonst nur äußerliche, gleichgültige Größebestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"76.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0014","text":"Der Exponent ist dieser Unterschied als einfache Bestimmtheit d. h. er hat unmittelbar die Bedeutung beider Bestimmungen an ihm selbst. Er ist erstens Quantum; so ist er die Anzahl; wenn die eine Seite des Verhältnisses, welche als Einheit genommen wird, als numerisches Eins ausgedrückt ist, und sie gilt nur für solches, so ist die andere, die Anzahl, das Quantum des Exponenten selbst. Zweitens ist er die einfache Bestimmtheit als das Qualitative der Seiten des Verhältnisses; wenn das Quantum der einen bestimmt ist, ist auch das andere durch den Exponenten bestimmt, und es ist völlig gleichgültig, wie das erste bestimmt wird; es hat als für sich bestimmtes Quantum keine Bedeutung mehr, sondern kann ebenso gut jedes Andere seyn, ohne die Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses zu ändern, die allein auf dem Exponenten beruht.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"76.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0015","text":"Das eine, welches als Einheit genommen ist, bleibt, wie groß es werde, immer Einheit, und das andere, wie groß es ebenso dabei werde, muß dieselbe Anzahl jener Einheit bleiben.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"76.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0016","text":"3. Hiernach machen beide eigentlich nur Ein Quantum aus, das eine hat gegen das andere, nur den Werth der Einheit, nicht einer Anzahl; das andre nur den der Anzahl; nach ihrer Begriffsbestimmtheit sind sie selbst somit nicht vollständige Quanta. Diese Unvollständigkeit aber ist eine Negation an ihnen und dieß nicht nach ihrer Veränderlichkeit überhaupt, nach der das Eine (und jedes ist Eines der beiden) alle mögliche Größe annehmen kann, sondern nach der Bestimmung, daß wenn das eine verändert wird, das andere um ebenso viel vermehrt oder vermindert wird; dieß heißt, wie gezeigt, nur das Eine, die Einheit, wird als Quantum verändert, die andere Seite, die Anzahl, bleibt dasselbe Quantum von Einheiten, aber auch jene bleibt ebenso nur als Einheit geltend, sie werde als Quantum verändert wie sie wolle.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"76.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0017","text":"Jede Seite ist so nur eines der beiden Momente des Quantums, und die Selbstständigkeit, die zu dessen Eigenthümlichkeit gehört, ist an sich negirt; in diesem qualitativen Zusammenhange sind sie als negative gegen einander zu setzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"76.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0018","text":"Der Exponent soll das vollständige Quantum seyn, indem die Bestimmung der beiden Seiten in ihm zusammenläuft; er hat aber in der That als Quotient selbst nur den Werth der Anzahl, oder der Einheit. Es ist keine Bestimmung vorhanden, welche der Seiten des Verhältnisses als die Einheit oder als die Anzahl genommen werden müße; die eine, das Quantum B an dem Quantum A als der Einheit gemessen, so ist der Quotient C die Anzahl solcher Einheiten; aber A selbst als Anzahl genommen, ist der Quotient C die Einheit, welche zu der Anzahl A für das Quantum B erfordert wird; dieser Quotient ist als Exponent somit nicht als das gesetzt, was er seyn soll,—das Bestimmende des Verhältnisses, oder als seine qualitative Einheit. Als diese ist er nur gesetzt, insofern er den Werth hat, die Einheit der beiden Momente, der Einheit und der Anzahl, zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"76.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0019","text":"Indem diese Seiten zwar als Quanta, wie sie in dem expliciten Quantum, dem Verhältnisse, seyn sollen, vorhanden sind, aber zugleich nur in dem Wertbe, den sie als dessen Seiten haben sollen, unvollständige Quanta zu seyn und nur als eines jener qualitativen Momente zu gelten, so sind sie mit dieser ihrer Negation zu setzen; womit ein seiner Bestimmung entsprechenderes reelleres Verhältniß entsteht, worin der Exponent die Bedeutung des Produkts derselben hat; nach dieser Bestimmtheit ist es das umgekehrte Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"76.19"}],"sha256":"ebfb6d4ecf6abb1f2e7f466efb4cebd22c7eb9e2309b44f2fa56b0e8236d7f89","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103930107826Z_87f32c10","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Direct Relation.","source_sha256":"ebfb6d4ecf6abb1f2e7f466efb4cebd22c7eb9e2309b44f2fa56b0e8236d7f89","sha256":"68df4d80fb603239c1874bee74f954c4420c1b4815b60d65af943d2df8d76120","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:39:30.107843+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0001","text":"## Third Chapter. The Quantitative Ratio.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"76.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0002","text":"The infinity of quantum has been determined as its negative beyond, which, however, it has within itself. This beyond is quality in general. The infinite quantum, as the unity of both moments, of quantitative and qualitative determinacy, is at first ratio.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"76.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0003","text":"In ratio, quantum no longer has a merely indifferent determinacy, but is qualitatively determined as absolutely related to its beyond. It continues itself into its beyond; this is at first another quantum in general. But essentially they are not related to one another as external quanta; rather, each has its determinacy in this relation to the other. Thus, in this their otherness, they have returned into themselves; what each is, it is in the other; the other constitutes the determinacy of each. —The going-forth of quantum beyond itself therefore now has this meaning: neither that it merely alters itself into an other, nor into its abstract other, into its negative beyond, but that it has attained its determinacy therein; it finds itself in its beyond, which is another quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"76.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0004","text":"The quality of quantum, its conceptual determinacy, is its externality in general; and in ratio it is now posited thus: to have its determinacy in its externality, in another quantum, to be in its beyond what it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"76.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0005","text":"There are quanta which have upon one another the relation that has emerged. This relation is itself also a magnitude; quantum is not merely in ratio, but is itself posited as ratio; it is a quantum in general which has that qualitative determinacy within itself. Thus, as ratio, it expresses itself as a self-enclosed totality and its indifference to the limit, by having the externality of its determinacy within itself and, in it, relating only to itself, and hence being infinite in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"76.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0006","text":"Ratio in general is","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"76.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0007","text":"1. direct ratio. In it the qualitative does not yet emerge as such for itself; it is not yet in any further manner than that of quantum that quantum is posited as having its determinacy in its externality itself.—Quantitative ratio is in itself the contradiction of externality and relation to self, of the subsistence of the quanta and their negation;—it sublates itself, in that at first","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"76.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0008","text":"2. in inverse ratio, the negation of the one quantum as such is posited together with the alteration of the other, and the mutability of direct ratio itself;","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"76.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0009","text":"3. in the ratio of powers, however, the unity which relates itself to itself in its difference makes itself valid as the simple self-production of quantum; this qualitative itself, finally posited in simple determinacy and identical with quantum, becomes measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"76.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0010","text":"—Much concerning the nature of the following ratios has been anticipated in the preceding remarks, which concern the infinite of quantity, i.e. its qualitative moment; it therefore remains only to set forth the abstract concept of these ratios.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"76.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0011","text":"## A. Direct Ratio.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"76.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0012","text":"1. In ratio, which, as immediate, is direct, the determinacy of the one quantum lies reciprocally in the determinacy of the other. There is only one determinacy or limit of both, which is itself quantum, the exponent of the ratio.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"76.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0013","text":"2. The exponent is some quantum, but as a quantum which in its externality relates to itself within itself, as a qualitatively determined quantum, it is only insofar as it has its difference, its beyond and otherness, within itself. But this difference of quantum within itself is the difference of unit and number; unit—the being-determined-for-self; number—the indifferent going to and fro in determinacy, the external indifference of quantum. Unit and number were at first the moments of quantum; now, in ratio, quantum thereby realized, each of its moments appears as a quantum of its own, and as determinations of its existence, as limitations against the otherwise merely external, indifferent determinacy of magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"76.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0014","text":"The exponent is this difference as simple determinacy, i.e. it immediately has the meaning of both determinations within itself. First, it is quantum; thus it is number; when the one side of the ratio, which is taken as unit, is expressed as numerical one, and counts only as such, then the other, number, is the quantum of the exponent itself. Secondly, it is simple determinacy as the qualitative of the sides of the ratio; if the quantum of the one is determined, then the other too is determined through the exponent, and it is wholly indifferent how the first is determined; as a quantum determined for itself, it no longer has any significance, but can equally well be any other without altering the determinacy of the ratio, which rests solely upon the exponent.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"76.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0015","text":"The one which is taken as unit remains, however great it may become, always unit, and the other, however great it may likewise become in the process, must remain the same number of that unit.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"76.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0016","text":"3. Accordingly, the two properly constitute only one quantum; the one has, as against the other, only the value of unit, not of a number; the other only that of number; according to their conceptual determinacy, they themselves are therefore not complete quanta. But this incompleteness is a negation in them, and this not according to their mutability in general, according to which the one (and each is one of the two) can assume every possible magnitude, but according to the determination that, when the one is altered, the other is increased or diminished by just as much; this means, as has been shown, only that the one, the unit, is altered as quantum, while the other side, number, remains the same quantum of units; but that one likewise remains valid only as unit, however it may be altered as quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"76.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0017","text":"Thus each side is only one of the two moments of quantum, and the self-subsistence which belongs to its peculiarity is negated in itself; in this qualitative connection they are to be posited as negative toward one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"76.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0018","text":"The exponent is supposed to be the complete quantum, since the determination of the two sides converges in it; but in fact, as quotient, it itself has only the value of number, or of unit. There is no determination as to which of the sides of the ratio must be taken as the unit or as the number; if the one, quantum B, is measured by quantum A as unit, then the quotient C is the number of such units; but if A itself is taken as number, then the quotient C is the unit required for quantum B relative to the number A; thus, as exponent, this quotient is not posited as what it is supposed to be,—the determining factor of the ratio, or as its qualitative unity. As such, it is posited only insofar as it has the value of being the unity of the two moments, unit and number.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"76.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0019","text":"Since these sides, although they are present as quanta, as they are supposed to be in explicit quantum, in ratio, yet at the same time, in the value which they are supposed to have as its sides, are incomplete quanta and count only as one of those qualitative moments, they are to be posited with this their negation; whereby a more real ratio, more adequate to its determination, arises, in which the exponent has the significance of their product; according to this determinacy, it is inverse ratio.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"76.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDVL:P0019"]}],"source_digest":"0c71628ad7358b00bbabbe0a4ca748f59d6341df0ea77bb129509975ebf315b0","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das direkte Verhältniß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das direkte Verhältniß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV","title":"B. The Inverse Ratio.","order":77,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDUV","text":"1. Das Verhältniß, wie es sich nun ergeben, ist das aufgehobene direkte Verhältniß; es war das unmittelbare, somit noch nicht wahrhaft bestimmte; nunmehr ist die Bestimmtheit so hinzugekommen, daß der Exponent als Produkt, Einheit der Einheit und der Anzahl, gilt. Nach der Unmittelbarkeit konnte er gleichgültig ebensowohl als Einheit wie als Anzahl genommen werden, wie vorhin gezeigt worden; womit er auch nur als Quantum überhaupt und damit vorzugsweise als Anzahl war; die eine Seite war die Einheit, und als Eins zu nehmen, zu welcher die andere eine fixe Anzahl sey, die zugleich der Exponent ist; dessen Qualität war somit nur dieß, daß dieß Quantum als festes genommen oder vielmehr das Feste nur den Sinn des Quantums hat.\n\nIn dem umgekehrten Verhältnisse nun ist der Exponent gleichfalls als Quantum ein unmittelbares, und irgend eines als festes angenommen. Aber dieß Quantum ist nicht fixe Anzahl zu dem Eins des andern Quantums im Verhältnisse; dieses im vorhergehenden feste Verhältniß ist nun vielmehr als veränderlich gesetzt; wenn zum Eins der einen Seite ein anderes Quantum genommen wird, so bleibt nun die andere nicht mehr dieselbe Anzahl von Einheiten der ersten. Im direkten Verhältnisse ist diese Einheit nur das gemeinschaftliche beider Seiten; sie als solche kontinuirt sich in die andere Seite, in die Anzahl; die Anzahl selbst für sich, oder der Exponent, ist gegen die Einheit gleichgültig.\n\nWie nunmehr aber die Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses ist, wird die Anzahl als solche gegen das Eins, zu dem sie die andere Seite des Verhältnisses ausmacht, verändert; je nachdem zum Eins ein anderes Quantum genommen wird, wird sie eine andere. Der Exponent ist daher zwar auch nur ein unmittelbares nur beliebig als fest angenommenes Quantum, aber er erhält sich nicht als solches in der Seite des Verhältnisses, sondern diese und damit das direkte Verhältniß der Seiten ist veränderlich. Hiermit ist, in dem nunmehrigen Verhältnisse, der Exponent, als das bestimmende Quantum, negativ gegen sich als Quantum des Verhältnisses, hiermit als qualitativ als Grenze gesetzt, daß also das Qualitative für sich im Unterschied gegen das Quantitative hervortritt.—In dem direkten Verhältnisse ist die Veränderung der beiden Seiten nur die Eine Veränderung des Quantums, als welches die Einheit, die das Gemeinschaftliche ist, genommen wird, um so viel also die eine Seite vergrößert oder vermindert wird, um so viel auch die andere; das Verhältniß selbst ist gegen diese Veränderung gleichgültig, sie ist ihm äußerlich. Im indirekten Verhältnisse aber ist die Veränderung, obgleich nach dem gleichgültigen quantitativen Momente auch beliebig, innerhalb des Verhältnisses gehalten, und auch dieß beliebige quantitative Hinausgehen durch die negative Bestimmtheit des Exponenten, als durch eine Grenze, beschränkt.\n\n2. Diese qualitative Natur des indirekten Verhältnisses ist noch näher, nämlich in ihrer Realisation zu betrachten, und die Verwicklung des Affirmativen mit dem Negativen, die darin enthalten ist, auseinander zu setzen.—Es ist das Quantum gesetzt, als qualitativ das Quantum d. i. sich selbst bestimmend, als Grenze seiner an ihm sich darstellend. Es ist hiermit erstens eine unmittelbare Größe als einfache Bestimmtheit, das Ganze als seyendes, affirmatives Quantum. Aber zweitens ist diese unmittelbare Bestimmtheit zugleich Grenze; dafür ist es in zwei Quanta unterschieden, die zunächst andere gegeneinander sind; aber als deren qualitative Bestimmtheit, und zwar dieselbe als vollständig ist es die Einheit der Einheit und der Anzahl, Produkt, dessen Faktoren sie sind. So ist der Exponent ihres Verhältnisses eines Theils in ihnen identisch mit sich, und das Affirmative derselben, wonach sie Quanta sind; andern Theils ist er als die an ihnen gesetzte Negation die Einheit an ihnen, nach der zunächst jedes, ein unmittelbares, begrenztes Quantum überhaupt, zugleich so ein begrenztes ist, daß es nur an sich identisch mit seinem Andern ist. Drittens ist er als die einfache Bestimmtheit, die negative Einheit dieser seiner Unterscheidung in die zwei Quanta und die Grenze ihres gegenseitigen Begrenzens.\n\nNach diesen Bestimmungen begrenzen sich die beiden Momente innerhalb des Exponenten und sind das eine das Negative des andern, da er ihre bestimmte Einheit ist; das eine wird um so vielmal kleiner, als das andere größer wird, jedes hat insofern seine Größe, als es die des andern an ihm hat, als dem andern mangelt. Jede kontinuirt sich auf diese Weise negativ in die andere; soviel sie an Anzahl ist, hebt sie an der andern als Anzahl auf, und ist, was sie ist, nur durch die Negation oder Grenze, die an ihr von der andern gesetzt wird. Jede enthält auf diese Weise auch die andere, und ist an ihr gemessen, denn jede soll nur das Quantum seyn, das die andere nicht ist; für den Werth jeder ist die Größe der andern unentbehrlich und damit untrennbar von ihr.\n\nDiese Kontinuität jeder in der Andern macht das Moment der Einheit aus, wodurch sie im Verhältnisse sind;—der Einen Bestimmtheit, der einfachen Grenze, die der Exponent ist. Diese Einheit, das Ganze, macht das Ansichseyn einer jeden aus, von dem ihre vorhandene Größe unterschieden ist, nach welcher jedes nur ist, insofern sie der andern von ihrem gemeinsamen Ansichseyn, dem Ganzen, entzieht. Aber sie kann nur so viel, als sie diesem Ansichseyn gleich macht, der andern entziehen, sie hat an dem Exponent ihr Maximum, der nach der angegebenen zweiten Bestimmung die Grenze ihrer gegenseitigen Begrenzung ist. Und indem jede nur insofern Moment des Verhältnisses ist, als sie die andere begrenzt und damit von der andern begrenzt wird, so verliert sie diese ihre Bestimmung, indem sie sich ihrem Ansichseyn gleich macht; die andere Größe wird nicht nur darin Null, sondern sie selbst verschwindet, da sie nicht bloßes Quantum, sondern was sie als solches ist, nur als solches Verhältnißmoment seyn soll. So ist jede Seite der Widerspruch der Bestimmung, als ihres Ansichseyns, d. i. der Einheit des Ganzen, das der Exponent ist, und der Bestimmung, als Verhältnißmomentes; dieser Widerspruch ist wieder die Unendlichkeit, in einer neuen eigenthümlichen Form.\n\nDer Exponent ist Grenze der Seiten seines Verhältnisses, innerhalb deren sie gegeneinander zu- und abnehmen, dem sie nach der affirmativen Bestimmtheit, die er als Quantum ist, nicht gleich werden können. So als Grenze ihres gegenseitigen Begrenzens ist er à) ihr Jenseits, deni sie sich unendlich nähern, aber das sie nicht erreichen können. Diese Unendlichkeit, als in der sie sich ihm nähern, ist die schlechte des unendlichen Progresses; sie ist selbst endlich, hat in ihrem Gegentheil, in der Endlichkeit jeder Seite und des Exponenten selbst, ihre Schranke, und ist daher nur Näherung. Aber ß) die schlechte Unendlichkeit ist hier zugleich gesetzt, als das was sie in Wahrheit ist, nämlich nur das negative Moment überhaupt, nach welchem der Exponent gegen die unterschiedenen Quanta des Verhältnisses die einfache Grenze als das Ansichseyn ist, auf das ihre Endlichkeit, als das schlechthin Veränderliche, bezogen wird, aber schlechthin von ihnen verschieden, als ihre Negation, bleibt. Dieß Unendliche, dem sich dieselben nur annähern können, ist dann gleichfalls als affirmatives Diesseits vorhanden und gegenwärtig; das simple Quantum des Exponenten. Darin ist das Jenseits, mit dem die Seiten des Verhältnisses behaftet sind, erreicht; es ist an sich die Einheit beider oder damit an sich die andre Seite einer jeden; denn jede hat nur so viel Werth, als die andere nicht hat, ihre ganze Bestimmtheit liegt so in der andern, und dieß ihr Ansichseyn ist als affirmative Unendlichkeit einfach der Exponent.\n\n3. Hiermit aber hat sich der Übergang des umgekehrten Verhältnisses in eine andere Bestimmung ergeben, als es zunächst hatte. Diese bestand darin, daß ein Quantum als unmittelbares zugleich auf ein anderes die Beziehung hat, um so viel größer zu seyn, als dieses kleiner ist, durch negatives Verhalten gegen das andere zu seyn, was es ist; ebenso ist eine dritte Größe die gemeinsame Schranke dieses ihres Größerwerdens. Diese Veränderung ist hier, im Gegensatze gegen das Qualitative als feste Grenze, ihre Eigenthünilichkeit; sie haben die Bestimmung von veränderlichen Größen, für welche jenes Feste ein unendliches Jenseits ist.\n\nDie Bestimmungen aber, die sich gezeigt und die wir zusammen zu fassen haben, sind, nicht nur, daß dieß unendliche Jenseits zugleich als ein gegenwärtiges und irgend ein endliches Quantum ist, sondern daß seine Festigkeit, wodurch es solches unendliches Jenseits gegen das Quantitative ist, und die das Qualitative des Seyns nur als abstrakte Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, sich als Vermittelung seiner in seinem Andern, den Endlichen des Verhältnisses, mit sich selbst, entwickelt hat. Das Allgemeine hiervon liegt darin, daß überhaupt das Ganze als Exponent die Grenze des gegenseitigen Begrenzens der beiden Glieder, also die Negation der Negation, somit die Unendlichkeit, affirmatives Verhalten zu sich selbst, gesetzt ist. Das Bestimmtere ist, daß an sich der Exponent schon als Produkt die Einheit der Einheit und der Anzahl, jedes der beiden Glieder aber nur das eine dieser beiden Momente ist, wodurch er sie also in sich schließt und in ihnen an sich sich auf sich bezieht. Aber der Unterschied ist im umgekehrten Verhältnisse zur Äußerlichkeit des quantitativen Seyns entwickelt, und das Qualitative nicht bloß das Feste, noch nur die Momente unmittelbar in sich einschließend, sondern in dem außersichseyenden Andersseyn sich mit sich zusammenschließend vorhanden. Diese Bestimmung ist es, die sich als Resultat in den Momenten, die sich gezeigt, heraushebt. Der Exponent ergiebt sich nämlich als das Ansichseyn, dessen Momente in Quantis und in deren Veränderlichkeit überhaupt realisirt ist; die Gleichgültigkeit ihrer Größen in ihrer Veränderung stellt sich als unendlicher Progreß dar; was dem zu Grunde liegt, ist, daß in ihrer Gleichgültigkeit dieß ihre Bestimmtheit ist, ihren Werth in dem Werthe des andern zu haben, somit à) nach der affirmativen Seite ihres Quantums an sich das Ganze des Exponenten zu seyn. Ebenso haben sie ß) für ihr negatives Moment, für ihr gegenseitiges Begrenzen die Größe des Exponenten, ihre Grenze ist die seinige. Daß sie keine andere immanente Grenze, eine feste Unmittelbarkeit, mehr haben, ist in dem unendlichen Progresse ihres Daseyns und ihrer Begrenzung, in der Negation jedes besondern Werthes, gesetzt. Diese ist hiernach die Negation des Außersichseyns des Exponenten, das in ihnen dargestellt ist, und dieser, d. i. zugleich selbst ein Quantum überhaupt, und in Quanta auch ausgelegt, ist damit gesetzt, als das in der Negation ihres gleichgültigen Bestehens sich Erhaltende, mit sich Zusammengehende, so das Bestimmende solchen Hinausgehens über sich, zu seyn.\n\nDas Verhältniß ist hiermit zum Potenzenverhältniß bestimmt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0001","text":"1. Das Verhältniß, wie es sich nun ergeben, ist das aufgehobene direkte Verhältniß; es war das unmittelbare, somit noch nicht wahrhaft bestimmte; nunmehr ist die Bestimmtheit so hinzugekommen, daß der Exponent als Produkt, Einheit der Einheit und der Anzahl, gilt. Nach der Unmittelbarkeit konnte er gleichgültig ebensowohl als Einheit wie als Anzahl genommen werden, wie vorhin gezeigt worden; womit er auch nur als Quantum überhaupt und damit vorzugsweise als Anzahl war; die eine Seite war die Einheit, und als Eins zu nehmen, zu welcher die andere eine fixe Anzahl sey, die zugleich der Exponent ist; dessen Qualität war somit nur dieß, daß dieß Quantum als festes genommen oder vielmehr das Feste nur den Sinn des Quantums hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"77.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0002","text":"In dem umgekehrten Verhältnisse nun ist der Exponent gleichfalls als Quantum ein unmittelbares, und irgend eines als festes angenommen. Aber dieß Quantum ist nicht fixe Anzahl zu dem Eins des andern Quantums im Verhältnisse; dieses im vorhergehenden feste Verhältniß ist nun vielmehr als veränderlich gesetzt; wenn zum Eins der einen Seite ein anderes Quantum genommen wird, so bleibt nun die andere nicht mehr dieselbe Anzahl von Einheiten der ersten. Im direkten Verhältnisse ist diese Einheit nur das gemeinschaftliche beider Seiten; sie als solche kontinuirt sich in die andere Seite, in die Anzahl; die Anzahl selbst für sich, oder der Exponent, ist gegen die Einheit gleichgültig.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"77.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0003","text":"Wie nunmehr aber die Bestimmtheit des Verhältnisses ist, wird die Anzahl als solche gegen das Eins, zu dem sie die andere Seite des Verhältnisses ausmacht, verändert; je nachdem zum Eins ein anderes Quantum genommen wird, wird sie eine andere. Der Exponent ist daher zwar auch nur ein unmittelbares nur beliebig als fest angenommenes Quantum, aber er erhält sich nicht als solches in der Seite des Verhältnisses, sondern diese und damit das direkte Verhältniß der Seiten ist veränderlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"77.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0004","text":"Hiermit ist, in dem nunmehrigen Verhältnisse, der Exponent, als das bestimmende Quantum, negativ gegen sich als Quantum des Verhältnisses, hiermit als qualitativ als Grenze gesetzt, daß also das Qualitative für sich im Unterschied gegen das Quantitative hervortritt.—In dem direkten Verhältnisse ist die Veränderung der beiden Seiten nur die Eine Veränderung des Quantums, als welches die Einheit, die das Gemeinschaftliche ist, genommen wird, um so viel also die eine Seite vergrößert oder vermindert wird, um so viel auch die andere; das Verhältniß selbst ist gegen diese Veränderung gleichgültig, sie ist ihm äußerlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"77.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0005","text":"Im indirekten Verhältnisse aber ist die Veränderung, obgleich nach dem gleichgültigen quantitativen Momente auch beliebig, innerhalb des Verhältnisses gehalten, und auch dieß beliebige quantitative Hinausgehen durch die negative Bestimmtheit des Exponenten, als durch eine Grenze, beschränkt.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"77.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0006","text":"2. Diese qualitative Natur des indirekten Verhältnisses ist noch näher, nämlich in ihrer Realisation zu betrachten, und die Verwicklung des Affirmativen mit dem Negativen, die darin enthalten ist, auseinander zu setzen.—Es ist das Quantum gesetzt, als qualitativ das Quantum d. i. sich selbst bestimmend, als Grenze seiner an ihm sich darstellend. Es ist hiermit erstens eine unmittelbare Größe als einfache Bestimmtheit, das Ganze als seyendes, affirmatives Quantum. Aber zweitens ist diese unmittelbare Bestimmtheit zugleich Grenze; dafür ist es in zwei Quanta unterschieden, die zunächst andere gegeneinander sind; aber als deren qualitative Bestimmtheit, und zwar dieselbe als vollständig ist es die Einheit der Einheit und der Anzahl, Produkt, dessen Faktoren sie sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"77.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0007","text":"So ist der Exponent ihres Verhältnisses eines Theils in ihnen identisch mit sich, und das Affirmative derselben, wonach sie Quanta sind; andern Theils ist er als die an ihnen gesetzte Negation die Einheit an ihnen, nach der zunächst jedes, ein unmittelbares, begrenztes Quantum überhaupt, zugleich so ein begrenztes ist, daß es nur an sich identisch mit seinem Andern ist. Drittens ist er als die einfache Bestimmtheit, die negative Einheit dieser seiner Unterscheidung in die zwei Quanta und die Grenze ihres gegenseitigen Begrenzens.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"77.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0008","text":"Nach diesen Bestimmungen begrenzen sich die beiden Momente innerhalb des Exponenten und sind das eine das Negative des andern, da er ihre bestimmte Einheit ist; das eine wird um so vielmal kleiner, als das andere größer wird, jedes hat insofern seine Größe, als es die des andern an ihm hat, als dem andern mangelt. Jede kontinuirt sich auf diese Weise negativ in die andere; soviel sie an Anzahl ist, hebt sie an der andern als Anzahl auf, und ist, was sie ist, nur durch die Negation oder Grenze, die an ihr von der andern gesetzt wird. Jede enthält auf diese Weise auch die andere, und ist an ihr gemessen, denn jede soll nur das Quantum seyn, das die andere nicht ist; für den Werth jeder ist die Größe der andern unentbehrlich und damit untrennbar von ihr.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"77.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0009","text":"Diese Kontinuität jeder in der Andern macht das Moment der Einheit aus, wodurch sie im Verhältnisse sind;—der Einen Bestimmtheit, der einfachen Grenze, die der Exponent ist. Diese Einheit, das Ganze, macht das Ansichseyn einer jeden aus, von dem ihre vorhandene Größe unterschieden ist, nach welcher jedes nur ist, insofern sie der andern von ihrem gemeinsamen Ansichseyn, dem Ganzen, entzieht. Aber sie kann nur so viel, als sie diesem Ansichseyn gleich macht, der andern entziehen, sie hat an dem Exponent ihr Maximum, der nach der angegebenen zweiten Bestimmung die Grenze ihrer gegenseitigen Begrenzung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"77.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0010","text":"Und indem jede nur insofern Moment des Verhältnisses ist, als sie die andere begrenzt und damit von der andern begrenzt wird, so verliert sie diese ihre Bestimmung, indem sie sich ihrem Ansichseyn gleich macht; die andere Größe wird nicht nur darin Null, sondern sie selbst verschwindet, da sie nicht bloßes Quantum, sondern was sie als solches ist, nur als solches Verhältnißmoment seyn soll. So ist jede Seite der Widerspruch der Bestimmung, als ihres Ansichseyns, d. i. der Einheit des Ganzen, das der Exponent ist, und der Bestimmung, als Verhältnißmomentes; dieser Widerspruch ist wieder die Unendlichkeit, in einer neuen eigenthümlichen Form.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"77.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0011","text":"Der Exponent ist Grenze der Seiten seines Verhältnisses, innerhalb deren sie gegeneinander zu- und abnehmen, dem sie nach der affirmativen Bestimmtheit, die er als Quantum ist, nicht gleich werden können. So als Grenze ihres gegenseitigen Begrenzens ist er à) ihr Jenseits, deni sie sich unendlich nähern, aber das sie nicht erreichen können. Diese Unendlichkeit, als in der sie sich ihm nähern, ist die schlechte des unendlichen Progresses; sie ist selbst endlich, hat in ihrem Gegentheil, in der Endlichkeit jeder Seite und des Exponenten selbst, ihre Schranke, und ist daher nur Näherung.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"77.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0012","text":"Aber ß) die schlechte Unendlichkeit ist hier zugleich gesetzt, als das was sie in Wahrheit ist, nämlich nur das negative Moment überhaupt, nach welchem der Exponent gegen die unterschiedenen Quanta des Verhältnisses die einfache Grenze als das Ansichseyn ist, auf das ihre Endlichkeit, als das schlechthin Veränderliche, bezogen wird, aber schlechthin von ihnen verschieden, als ihre Negation, bleibt. Dieß Unendliche, dem sich dieselben nur annähern können, ist dann gleichfalls als affirmatives Diesseits vorhanden und gegenwärtig; das simple Quantum des Exponenten.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"77.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0013","text":"Darin ist das Jenseits, mit dem die Seiten des Verhältnisses behaftet sind, erreicht; es ist an sich die Einheit beider oder damit an sich die andre Seite einer jeden; denn jede hat nur so viel Werth, als die andere nicht hat, ihre ganze Bestimmtheit liegt so in der andern, und dieß ihr Ansichseyn ist als affirmative Unendlichkeit einfach der Exponent.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"77.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0014","text":"3. Hiermit aber hat sich der Übergang des umgekehrten Verhältnisses in eine andere Bestimmung ergeben, als es zunächst hatte. Diese bestand darin, daß ein Quantum als unmittelbares zugleich auf ein anderes die Beziehung hat, um so viel größer zu seyn, als dieses kleiner ist, durch negatives Verhalten gegen das andere zu seyn, was es ist; ebenso ist eine dritte Größe die gemeinsame Schranke dieses ihres Größerwerdens. Diese Veränderung ist hier, im Gegensatze gegen das Qualitative als feste Grenze, ihre Eigenthünilichkeit; sie haben die Bestimmung von veränderlichen Größen, für welche jenes Feste ein unendliches Jenseits ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"77.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0015","text":"Die Bestimmungen aber, die sich gezeigt und die wir zusammen zu fassen haben, sind, nicht nur, daß dieß unendliche Jenseits zugleich als ein gegenwärtiges und irgend ein endliches Quantum ist, sondern daß seine Festigkeit, wodurch es solches unendliches Jenseits gegen das Quantitative ist, und die das Qualitative des Seyns nur als abstrakte Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, sich als Vermittelung seiner in seinem Andern, den Endlichen des Verhältnisses, mit sich selbst, entwickelt hat. Das Allgemeine hiervon liegt darin, daß überhaupt das Ganze als Exponent die Grenze des gegenseitigen Begrenzens der beiden Glieder, also die Negation der Negation, somit die Unendlichkeit, affirmatives Verhalten zu sich selbst, gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"77.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0016","text":"Das Bestimmtere ist, daß an sich der Exponent schon als Produkt die Einheit der Einheit und der Anzahl, jedes der beiden Glieder aber nur das eine dieser beiden Momente ist, wodurch er sie also in sich schließt und in ihnen an sich sich auf sich bezieht. Aber der Unterschied ist im umgekehrten Verhältnisse zur Äußerlichkeit des quantitativen Seyns entwickelt, und das Qualitative nicht bloß das Feste, noch nur die Momente unmittelbar in sich einschließend, sondern in dem außersichseyenden Andersseyn sich mit sich zusammenschließend vorhanden. Diese Bestimmung ist es, die sich als Resultat in den Momenten, die sich gezeigt, heraushebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"77.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0017","text":"Der Exponent ergiebt sich nämlich als das Ansichseyn, dessen Momente in Quantis und in deren Veränderlichkeit überhaupt realisirt ist; die Gleichgültigkeit ihrer Größen in ihrer Veränderung stellt sich als unendlicher Progreß dar; was dem zu Grunde liegt, ist, daß in ihrer Gleichgültigkeit dieß ihre Bestimmtheit ist, ihren Werth in dem Werthe des andern zu haben, somit à) nach der affirmativen Seite ihres Quantums an sich das Ganze des Exponenten zu seyn. Ebenso haben sie ß) für ihr negatives Moment, für ihr gegenseitiges Begrenzen die Größe des Exponenten, ihre Grenze ist die seinige. Daß sie keine andere immanente Grenze, eine feste Unmittelbarkeit, mehr haben, ist in dem unendlichen Progresse ihres Daseyns und ihrer Begrenzung, in der Negation jedes besondern Werthes, gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"77.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0018","text":"Diese ist hiernach die Negation des Außersichseyns des Exponenten, das in ihnen dargestellt ist, und dieser, d. i. zugleich selbst ein Quantum überhaupt, und in Quanta auch ausgelegt, ist damit gesetzt, als das in der Negation ihres gleichgültigen Bestehens sich Erhaltende, mit sich Zusammengehende, so das Bestimmende solchen Hinausgehens über sich, zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"77.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0019","text":"Das Verhältniß ist hiermit zum Potenzenverhältniß bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"77.19"}],"sha256":"f2bb4fdd289270b0a597c95aae235d69f1bdcc61a26bc582bf713dac14d718a3","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T103953123484Z_8ce410ce","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. The Inverse Ratio.","source_sha256":"f2bb4fdd289270b0a597c95aae235d69f1bdcc61a26bc582bf713dac14d718a3","sha256":"2b5de039853d735e2606339ad63a75b98828f1623e5473f277ef7c310e789285","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:39:53.123507+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0001","text":"1. The relation, as it has now emerged, is the sublated direct relation; it was the immediate relation, and thus not yet truly determinate; determinacy has now been added in such a way that the exponent counts as product, unity of the unit and the number. In accordance with immediacy, it could indifferently be taken equally as unit or as number, as was shown above; whereby it was also only quantum in general and hence pre-eminently number; the one side was the unit, and was to be taken as one, in relation to which the other was a fixed number, which is at the same time the exponent; its quality was thus only this, that this quantum was taken as fixed, or rather, that the fixed has only the sense of quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"77.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0002","text":"In the inverse relation, the exponent likewise, as quantum, is an immediate one, and some quantum is assumed as fixed. But this quantum is not a fixed number in relation to the one of the other quantum; this fixed relation in the preceding case is now rather posited as variable; if another quantum is taken as the one of one side, the other no longer remains the same number of units of the first. In the direct relation this unit is only what is common to both sides; as such it continues into the other side, into the number; the number itself, or the exponent, is indifferent toward the unit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"77.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0003","text":"But as the determinacy of the relation now is, the number as such is altered in relation to the one, to which it constitutes the other side of the relation; according as another quantum is taken as the one, it becomes another number. The exponent is therefore indeed likewise only an immediate quantum, arbitrarily assumed as fixed; but it does not preserve itself as such in the side of the relation; rather, this side, and consequently the direct relation of the sides, is variable.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"77.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0004","text":"Thereby, in the present relation, the exponent, as the determining quantum, is posited negatively toward itself as the quantum of the relation, and thus as qualitative, as limit, so that the qualitative emerges on its own account in distinction from the quantitative.—In the direct relation, the alteration of the two sides is only the one alteration of the quantum which is taken as the unit that is common to them; therefore, by as much as one side is increased or diminished, so too is the other; the relation itself is indifferent toward this alteration, which is external to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"77.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0005","text":"In the indirect relation, however, the alteration, although arbitrary also according to the indifferent quantitative moment, is held within the relation, and this arbitrary quantitative going-beyond is also restricted by the negative determinacy of the exponent, as by a limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"77.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0006","text":"2. This qualitative nature of the indirect relation is to be considered more closely, namely in its realization, and the entanglement of the affirmative with the negative which it contains is to be set forth.—Quantum is posited as qualitatively quantum, i.e. as self-determining, as a limit presenting itself in it. Thus it is, first, an immediate magnitude as simple determinacy, the whole as being, affirmative quantum. But, second, this immediate determinacy is at the same time limit; on that account it is distinguished into two quanta, which are at first others in relation to one another; but as their qualitative determinacy—and indeed as the same determinacy in its completeness—it is the unity of the unit and the number, the product, of which they are the factors.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"77.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0007","text":"Thus the exponent of their relation is, on the one hand, identical with itself in them, and is their affirmative aspect, according to which they are quanta; on the other hand, as the negation posited in them, it is the unity in them, according to which each, initially an immediate, limited quantum in general, is at the same time so limited that it is identical with its other only in itself. Third, it is, as simple determinacy, the negative unity of this its distinction into the two quanta and the limit of their reciprocal limiting.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"77.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0008","text":"According to these determinations, the two moments limit one another within the exponent and each is the negative of the other, since it is their determinate unity; the one becomes smaller by as many times as the other becomes larger; each has its magnitude insofar as it has in itself that of the other, insofar as the other lacks it. In this way each continues negatively into the other; insofar as it is number, it sublates the other as number, and is what it is only through the negation or limit which is posited in it by the other. In this way each also contains the other and is measured in it, for each is supposed to be only the quantum which the other is not; for the value of each, the magnitude of the other is indispensable and therefore inseparable from it.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"77.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0009","text":"This continuity of each in the other constitutes the moment of unity through which they are in relation;—the one determinacy, the simple limit, which is the exponent. This unity, the whole, constitutes the being-in-itself of each, from which its existent magnitude is distinguished, according to which each is only insofar as it withdraws it from the other out of their common being-in-itself, the whole. But it can withdraw from the other only as much as it makes itself equal to this being-in-itself; it has its maximum in the exponent, which, according to the second determination indicated, is the limit of their reciprocal limiting.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"77.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0010","text":"And since each is a moment of the relation only insofar as it limits the other and is thereby limited by the other, it loses this its determination when it makes itself equal to its being-in-itself; the other magnitude not only becomes zero therein, but it itself disappears, since it is to be not mere quantum, but only what it is as such, only as such a relational moment. Thus each side is the contradiction of the determination as its being-in-itself, i.e. the unity of the whole, which is the exponent, and the determination as relational moment; this contradiction is again infinity, in a new peculiar form.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"77.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0011","text":"The exponent is the limit of the sides of its relation, within which they increase and decrease in relation to one another, and to which, in accordance with the affirmative determinacy which it is as quantum, they cannot become equal. Thus, as the limit of their reciprocal limiting, it is à) their beyond, which they approach infinitely, but which they cannot attain. This infinity, as that in which they approach it, is the bad infinity of infinite progress; it is itself finite, has its barrier in its opposite, in the finitude of each side and of the exponent itself, and is therefore only approximation.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"77.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0012","text":"But ß) bad infinity is here at the same time posited as what it is in truth, namely only the negative moment in general, according to which the exponent, in relation to the distinguished quanta of the relation, is the simple limit as being-in-itself, to which their finitude, as the absolutely variable, is related, but which remains absolutely distinct from them, as their negation. This infinite, which they can only approach, is then likewise present and at hand as an affirmative this-side; the simple quantum of the exponent.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"77.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0013","text":"Therein the beyond with which the sides of the relation are encumbered is attained; it is in itself the unity of both, or thereby in itself the other side of each; for each has only as much value as the other does not have, so that its entire determinacy lies in the other, and this its being-in-itself, as affirmative infinity, is simply the exponent.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"77.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0014","text":"3. Thereby, however, the transition of the inverse relation into another determination than that which it initially had has emerged. This consisted in the fact that a quantum, as immediate, at the same time has the relation to another of being greater by as much as this is smaller, of being what it is through negative comportment toward the other; likewise, a third magnitude is the common barrier of this their becoming-greater. This alteration, here in contrast to the qualitative as fixed limit, is their peculiarity; they have the determination of variable magnitudes, for which that fixed element is an infinite beyond.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"77.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0015","text":"But the determinations which have shown themselves and which we have to gather together are not merely that this infinite beyond is at the same time a present and some finite quantum, but that its fixity, through which it is such an infinite beyond in relation to the quantitative, and which is the qualitative of being only as abstract relation to itself, has developed as mediation of itself with itself in its other, the finites of the relation. The universal point here is that the whole as exponent is posited as the limit of the reciprocal limiting of the two members, hence as the negation of negation, and thus as infinity, affirmative relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"77.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0016","text":"The more determinate point is that in itself the exponent, already as product, is the unity of the unit and the number, whereas each of the two members is only one of these two moments; whereby it thus encloses them within itself and in them relates itself in itself to itself. But in the inverse relation the distinction has developed into the externality of quantitative being, and the qualitative is not merely the fixed, nor merely immediately enclosing the moments within itself, but is present as joining itself together with itself in the otherness that is external to itself. It is this determination which emerges as result in the moments that have shown themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"77.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0017","text":"For the exponent proves to be the being-in-itself whose moments are realized in quanta and in their variability in general; the indifference of their magnitudes in their alteration presents itself as infinite progress; what underlies this is that, in their indifference, this is their determinacy: to have their value in the value of the other, thus à) on the affirmative side of their quantum, to be in themselves the whole of the exponent. Likewise, ß) for their negative moment, for their reciprocal limiting, they have the magnitude of the exponent; their limit is its limit. That they no longer have any other immanent limit, any fixed immediacy, is posited in the infinite progress of their existence and of their limiting, in the negation of every particular value.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"77.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0018","text":"This is accordingly the negation of the being-external-to-itself of the exponent which is exhibited in them; and it, i.e. at the same time itself a quantum in general and expounded also in quanta, is thereby posited as that which preserves itself in the negation of their indifferent subsistence, which comes together with itself, and thus as the determining element of such going-beyond itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"77.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0019","text":"The relation is thereby determined as the relation of powers.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"77.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDUV:P0019"]}],"source_digest":"f92f28f43157eef123d659efebb115d8b39101969017f1c9b6589bdcb094bec7","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Das umgekehrte Verhältniß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Das umgekehrte Verhältniß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0","title":"C. The Relation of Powers.","order":78,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CPL0","text":"1. Das Quantum in seinem Andersseyn sich identisch mit sich setzend, sein Hinausgehen über sich selbst bestimmend, ist zum Fürsichseyn gekommen. So qualitative Totalität, indem sie sich als entwickelt setzt, hat sie zu ihren Momenten die Begriffsbestimmungen der Zahl, die Einheit und die Anzahl; die letztere ist noch im umgekehrten Verhältnisse eine nicht durch die erstere selbst als solche, sondern anderswoher, durch ein Drittes bestimmte Menge; nun ist sie nur durch jene bestimmt gesetzt. Dieß ist der Fall im Potenzenverhältnisse, wo die Einheit, welche Anzahl an ihr selbst ist, zugleich die Anzahl gegen sich als Einheit ist. Das Andersseyn, die Anzahl der Einheiten, ist die Einheit selbst. Die Potenz ist eine Menge von Einheiten, deren jede diese Menge selbst ist. Das Quantum als gleichgültige Bestimmtheit verändert sich; aber insofern diese Verändernng ein Erheben in die Potenz ist, ist dieß sein Andersseyn rein durch sich selbst begrenzt.—Das Quantum ist so in der Potenz als in sich selbst zurückgekehrt gesetzt; es ist unmittelbar es selbst und auch sein Andersseyn.\n\nDer Exponent dieses Verhältnisses ist nicht mehr ein unmittelbares Quantum, wie im direkten, und auch im umgekehrten Verhältnisse. Er ist im Potenzenverhältniß ganz qualitativer Natur, diese einfache Bestimmtheit, daß die Anzahl die Einheit selbst, das Quantum in seinem Andersseyn mit sich selbst identisch ist. Darin liegt zugleich die Seite seiner quantitativen Natur, daß die Grenze oder Negation nicht als unmittelbar seyendes, sondern das Daseyn als in sein Andersseyn kontinuirt gesetzt ist; denn die Wahrheit der Qualität ist eben dieß, Quantität, die unmittdbare Bestimmtheit als aufgehobene, zu seyn.\n\n2. Das Potenzenverhältniß erscheint zunächst als eine äußere Veränderung, in welche irgend ein Quantum versetzt wird; es hat aber die engere Beziehung auf den Begriff des Quantums, daß dieses in dem Daseyn, zu welchem es in jenem Verhältnisse fortgebildet ist, denselben erreicht, ihn auf vollständige Weise realisirt hat; dieß Verhältniß ist die Darstellung dessen, was das Quantum an sich ist, und drückt dessen Bestimmtheit oder Qualität aus, wodurch es sich von anderem unterscheidet. Das Quantum ist die gleichgültige, als aufgehoben gesetzte Bestimmtheit, das heißt, die Bestimmtheit als Grenze, welche ebenso sehr keine ist, in ihr Andersseyn sich kontinuirt, in ihm sich also identisch mit sich bleibt; so ist es im Potenzenverhältniß gesetzt; sein Andersseyn, Hinausgehen über sich in ein anders Quantum, als durch es selbst bestimmt.\n\nVergleichen wir den Fortgang dieser Realisirung in den bisherigen Verhältnissen, so ist die Qualität des Quantums, als Unterschied seiner von sich selbst gesetzt zu seyn, überhaupt dieß, Verhältniß zu seyn. Als direktes Verhältniß ist es als solcher gesetzte Unterschied nur erst überhaupt oder unmittelbar, so daß seine Beziehung auf sich selbst, die es gegen seine Unterschiede, als der Exponent hat, nur als die Festigkeit einer Anzahl der Einheit gilt. Im umgekehrten Verhältniß ist das Quantum in negativer Bestimmung ein Verhalten seiner zu sich selbst,—zu sich als seiner Negation, in der es aber seinen Werth hat; als affirmative Beziehung auf sich ist es ein Exponent, der als Quantum nur an sich das Bestimmende seiner Momente ist. Im Potenzenverhältniß aber ist es in dem Unterschied als seiner von sich selbst vorhanden. Die Äußerlichkeit der Bestimmtheit ist die Qualität des Quantums, diese Äußerlichkeit ist so nun seinem Begriffe gemäß als sein eigenes Bestimmen, als seine Beziehung auf sich selbst, seine Qualität, gesetzt.\n\n3. Damit aber, daß das Quantum gesetzt ist, wie es seinem Begriffe gemäß ist, ist es in eine andere Bestimmung übergegangen; oder wie es auch ausgedrückt werden kann, daß seine Bestimmung nun auch als die Bestimmtheit, das Ansichseyn auch als Daseyn ist. Es ist als Quantum, insofern die Äußerlichkeit oder Gleichgültigkeit des Bestimmtseyns (—daß es das ist, wie man sagt, was vergrößert oder vermindert werden kann) nur einfach oder unmittelbar gilt und gesetzt ist; es ist zu seinem Andern, der Qualität, geworden, insofern jene Äußerlichkeit nun als vermittelt durch es selbst, so als ein Moment gesetzt ist, daß es eben in ihr sich auf sich selbst bezieht, Seyn als Qualität ist.\n\nZunächst erscheint also die Quantität als solche der Qualität gegenüber; aber die Quantität ist selbst eine Qualität, sich auf sich beziehende Bestimmtheit überhaupt, unterschieden von der ihr andern Bestimmtheit, von der Qualität als solcher. Allein sie ist nicht nur eine Qualität, sondern die Wahrheit der Qualität selbst ist die Quantität; jene hat sich als in diese übergehend gezeigt. Die Quantität ist dagegen in ihrer Wahrheit die in sich selbst zurückgekehrte, nicht gleichgültige Äußerlichkeit. So ist sie die Qualität selbst, so daß außer dieser Bestimmung nicht die Qualität als solche noch etwas wäre.—Daß die Totalität gesetzt sey, dazu gehört der gedoppelte Übergang, nicht nur der der einen Bestimmtheit in ihre andere, sondern ebenso der Übergang dieser andern, ihr Rückgang, in die erste. Durch den ersten ist nur erst an sich die Identität beider vorhanden;—die Qualität ist in der Quantität enthalten, die aber damit noch eine einseitige Bestimmtheit ist. Daß diese umgekehrt ebenso in der ersten enthalten, sie ebenso nur als aufgehobene ist, ergiebt sich im zweiten Übergang,—der Rückkehr in das erste; diese Bemerkung über die Nothwendigkeit des doppelten Übergangs ist von großer Wichtigkeit für das Ganze der wissenschaftlichen Methode.\n\nDas Quantum nunmehr als gleichgültige oder äußerliche Bestimmung, so daß es ebenso als solche aufgehoben, und die Qualität und das ist, wodurch etwas das ist, was es ist, ist die Wahrheit des Quantums, Maaß zu seyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0001","text":"1. Das Quantum in seinem Andersseyn sich identisch mit sich setzend, sein Hinausgehen über sich selbst bestimmend, ist zum Fürsichseyn gekommen. So qualitative Totalität, indem sie sich als entwickelt setzt, hat sie zu ihren Momenten die Begriffsbestimmungen der Zahl, die Einheit und die Anzahl; die letztere ist noch im umgekehrten Verhältnisse eine nicht durch die erstere selbst als solche, sondern anderswoher, durch ein Drittes bestimmte Menge; nun ist sie nur durch jene bestimmt gesetzt. Dieß ist der Fall im Potenzenverhältnisse, wo die Einheit, welche Anzahl an ihr selbst ist, zugleich die Anzahl gegen sich als Einheit ist. Das Andersseyn, die Anzahl der Einheiten, ist die Einheit selbst. Die Potenz ist eine Menge von Einheiten, deren jede diese Menge selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"78.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0002","text":"Das Quantum als gleichgültige Bestimmtheit verändert sich; aber insofern diese Verändernng ein Erheben in die Potenz ist, ist dieß sein Andersseyn rein durch sich selbst begrenzt.—Das Quantum ist so in der Potenz als in sich selbst zurückgekehrt gesetzt; es ist unmittelbar es selbst und auch sein Andersseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"78.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0003","text":"Der Exponent dieses Verhältnisses ist nicht mehr ein unmittelbares Quantum, wie im direkten, und auch im umgekehrten Verhältnisse. Er ist im Potenzenverhältniß ganz qualitativer Natur, diese einfache Bestimmtheit, daß die Anzahl die Einheit selbst, das Quantum in seinem Andersseyn mit sich selbst identisch ist. Darin liegt zugleich die Seite seiner quantitativen Natur, daß die Grenze oder Negation nicht als unmittelbar seyendes, sondern das Daseyn als in sein Andersseyn kontinuirt gesetzt ist; denn die Wahrheit der Qualität ist eben dieß, Quantität, die unmittdbare Bestimmtheit als aufgehobene, zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"78.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0004","text":"2. Das Potenzenverhältniß erscheint zunächst als eine äußere Veränderung, in welche irgend ein Quantum versetzt wird; es hat aber die engere Beziehung auf den Begriff des Quantums, daß dieses in dem Daseyn, zu welchem es in jenem Verhältnisse fortgebildet ist, denselben erreicht, ihn auf vollständige Weise realisirt hat; dieß Verhältniß ist die Darstellung dessen, was das Quantum an sich ist, und drückt dessen Bestimmtheit oder Qualität aus, wodurch es sich von anderem unterscheidet. Das Quantum ist die gleichgültige, als aufgehoben gesetzte Bestimmtheit, das heißt, die Bestimmtheit als Grenze, welche ebenso sehr keine ist, in ihr Andersseyn sich kontinuirt, in ihm sich also identisch mit sich bleibt; so ist es im Potenzenverhältniß gesetzt; sein Andersseyn, Hinausgehen über sich in ein anders Quantum, als durch es selbst bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"78.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0005","text":"Vergleichen wir den Fortgang dieser Realisirung in den bisherigen Verhältnissen, so ist die Qualität des Quantums, als Unterschied seiner von sich selbst gesetzt zu seyn, überhaupt dieß, Verhältniß zu seyn. Als direktes Verhältniß ist es als solcher gesetzte Unterschied nur erst überhaupt oder unmittelbar, so daß seine Beziehung auf sich selbst, die es gegen seine Unterschiede, als der Exponent hat, nur als die Festigkeit einer Anzahl der Einheit gilt. Im umgekehrten Verhältniß ist das Quantum in negativer Bestimmung ein Verhalten seiner zu sich selbst,—zu sich als seiner Negation, in der es aber seinen Werth hat; als affirmative Beziehung auf sich ist es ein Exponent, der als Quantum nur an sich das Bestimmende seiner Momente ist. Im Potenzenverhältniß aber ist es in dem Unterschied als seiner von sich selbst vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"78.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0006","text":"Die Äußerlichkeit der Bestimmtheit ist die Qualität des Quantums, diese Äußerlichkeit ist so nun seinem Begriffe gemäß als sein eigenes Bestimmen, als seine Beziehung auf sich selbst, seine Qualität, gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"78.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0007","text":"3. Damit aber, daß das Quantum gesetzt ist, wie es seinem Begriffe gemäß ist, ist es in eine andere Bestimmung übergegangen; oder wie es auch ausgedrückt werden kann, daß seine Bestimmung nun auch als die Bestimmtheit, das Ansichseyn auch als Daseyn ist. Es ist als Quantum, insofern die Äußerlichkeit oder Gleichgültigkeit des Bestimmtseyns (—daß es das ist, wie man sagt, was vergrößert oder vermindert werden kann) nur einfach oder unmittelbar gilt und gesetzt ist; es ist zu seinem Andern, der Qualität, geworden, insofern jene Äußerlichkeit nun als vermittelt durch es selbst, so als ein Moment gesetzt ist, daß es eben in ihr sich auf sich selbst bezieht, Seyn als Qualität ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"78.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0008","text":"Zunächst erscheint also die Quantität als solche der Qualität gegenüber; aber die Quantität ist selbst eine Qualität, sich auf sich beziehende Bestimmtheit überhaupt, unterschieden von der ihr andern Bestimmtheit, von der Qualität als solcher. Allein sie ist nicht nur eine Qualität, sondern die Wahrheit der Qualität selbst ist die Quantität; jene hat sich als in diese übergehend gezeigt. Die Quantität ist dagegen in ihrer Wahrheit die in sich selbst zurückgekehrte, nicht gleichgültige Äußerlichkeit. So ist sie die Qualität selbst, so daß außer dieser Bestimmung nicht die Qualität als solche noch etwas wäre.—Daß die Totalität gesetzt sey, dazu gehört der gedoppelte Übergang, nicht nur der der einen Bestimmtheit in ihre andere, sondern ebenso der Übergang dieser andern, ihr Rückgang, in die erste.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"78.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0009","text":"Durch den ersten ist nur erst an sich die Identität beider vorhanden;—die Qualität ist in der Quantität enthalten, die aber damit noch eine einseitige Bestimmtheit ist. Daß diese umgekehrt ebenso in der ersten enthalten, sie ebenso nur als aufgehobene ist, ergiebt sich im zweiten Übergang,—der Rückkehr in das erste; diese Bemerkung über die Nothwendigkeit des doppelten Übergangs ist von großer Wichtigkeit für das Ganze der wissenschaftlichen Methode.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"78.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0010","text":"Das Quantum nunmehr als gleichgültige oder äußerliche Bestimmung, so daß es ebenso als solche aufgehoben, und die Qualität und das ist, wodurch etwas das ist, was es ist, ist die Wahrheit des Quantums, Maaß zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"78.10"}],"sha256":"6e19603aedc3da052eecf9a2af8e250de6b2ebad2ebf063b6a7754a291ea8184","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104006613259Z_ed325210","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. The Relation of Powers.","source_sha256":"6e19603aedc3da052eecf9a2af8e250de6b2ebad2ebf063b6a7754a291ea8184","sha256":"16c33e82ebfc2b0a96f632864bc2f2bfb333c4a5b2b70edcde586080815001d8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:40:06.613316+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0001","text":"1. The quantum, in positing itself as identical with itself in its otherness, determining its going-beyond-itself, has attained being-for-self. Thus qualitative totality, inasmuch as it posits itself as developed, has as its moments the determinations of the concept of number, the unit and the number; the latter is still, in inverse ratio, a magnitude determined not by the former itself as such, but from elsewhere, by a third; now it is posited as determined only by that former. This is the case in the relation of powers, where the unit, which is number in itself, is at the same time the number in relation to itself as unit. The otherness, the number of units, is the unit itself. The power is a quantity of units, each of which is this quantity itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"78.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0002","text":"The quantum, as indifferent determinateness, changes; but insofar as this change is an elevation to a power, its otherness is purely bounded by itself.—Thus the quantum is posited in the power as having returned into itself; it is immediately itself and also its otherness.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"78.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0003","text":"The exponent of this relation is no longer an immediate quantum, as in the direct, and also in the inverse relation. In the relation of powers it is of an altogether qualitative nature, this simple determinateness, that number is the unit itself, that the quantum is identical with itself in its otherness. Therein lies at the same time the aspect of its quantitative nature, that the limit or negation is posited not as immediately being, but existence as continued into its otherness; for the truth of quality is precisely this, to be quantity, the immediate determinateness as sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"78.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0004","text":"2. The relation of powers at first appears as an external alteration into which some quantum is transferred; but it has the closer relation to the concept of quantum, that the latter, in the existence into which it is developed in that relation, has attained the same, has realized it in a complete manner; this relation is the presentation of what the quantum is in itself, and expresses its determinateness or quality, whereby it distinguishes itself from another. The quantum is the indifferent determinateness, posited as sublated, that is, determinateness as limit, which is equally much no limit, continues into its otherness, and thus remains identical with itself in it; thus it is posited in the relation of powers; its otherness, its going beyond itself into another quantum, as determined by itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"78.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0005","text":"If we compare the progress of this realization in the relations thus far, the quality of the quantum, as being posited as its difference from itself, is in general this, to be relation. As direct relation, this difference posited as such is at first only in general or immediate, so that its relation to itself, which it has as exponent over against its differences, counts only as the fixedness of a number of the unit. In the inverse relation the quantum, in negative determination, is a comportment of itself toward itself,—toward itself as its negation, in which, however, it has its value; as affirmative relation to itself it is an exponent which, as quantum, is only in itself the determining factor of its moments. But in the relation of powers it is present in the difference as its own difference from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"78.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0006","text":"The externality of determinateness is the quality of the quantum; this externality is now, in accordance with its concept, posited as its own determining, as its relation to itself, its quality.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"78.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0007","text":"3. But in that the quantum is posited as it is in accordance with its concept, it has passed over into another determination; or, as it may also be expressed, its determination is now also as determinateness, being-in-itself also as existence. It is quantum insofar as the externality or indifference of being-determined (—that it is what, as one says, can be increased or diminished) counts and is posited only simply or immediately; it has become its other, quality, insofar as that externality is now posited as mediated through itself, thus as a moment such that it relates itself to itself precisely in it, is being as quality.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"78.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0008","text":"Thus quantity as such initially appears over against quality; but quantity is itself a quality, self-relating determinateness in general, distinguished from the determinateness other than it, from quality as such. Yet it is not merely a quality, but the truth of quality itself is quantity; the former has shown itself as passing over into the latter. Quantity, on the other hand, in its truth is externality returned into itself, not indifferent. Thus it is quality itself, so that outside this determination quality as such would no longer be anything.—For totality to be posited, the twofold transition is required, not only that of the one determinateness into its other, but equally the transition of this other, its return, into the first.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"78.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0009","text":"Through the first, the identity of both is at first present only in itself;—quality is contained in quantity, which thereby is still a one-sided determinateness. That, conversely, this is equally contained in the first, that it too is only as sublated, emerges in the second transition,—the return into the first; this remark concerning the necessity of the twofold transition is of great importance for the whole of scientific method.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"78.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0010","text":"The quantum now, as indifferent or external determination, such that it is equally sublated as such, and quality is that whereby something is what it is, is the truth of the quantum, to be measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"78.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CPL0:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"23e2f0adc0b7e6bb4b4b386e6eeb6defbc93cded192b58b5194b5a00e37d63ce","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Potenzverhältniß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Potenzverhältniß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20","title":"Remark.","order":79,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_20","text":"Es ist oben, in den Anmerkungen über das Quantitativ-Unendliche auseinander gesetzt worden, daß dieses so wie die Schwierigkeiten, die sich darüber ergeben, in dem qualitativen Momente, das sich im Quantitativen hervorthut, ihren Ursprung haben, und wie das Qualitative des Potenzenverhältnisses insbesondere, in die mannigfaltigen Entwickelungen und Verwickelungen ausgeht; als der Grundmangel, der die Auffassung des Begriffes verhindert, wurde auf gezeigt, daß bei dem Unendlichen nur nach der negativen Bestimmung, die Negation des Quantums zu seyn, stehen geblieben und nicht zu der einfachen Bestimmung, dem Affirmativen, daß dieses das Qualitative ist, fortgegangen wird.—Hier bleibt nur übrig, noch eine Bemerkung über die in der Philosophie geschehene Einmischung von Formen des Quantitativen in die reinen qualitativen Formen des Denkens, zu machen. Besonders ist es das Potenzenverhältniß, welches in neuerer Zeit auf Begriffsbestimmungen angewendet worden ist. Der Begriff in seiner Unmittelbarkeit wurde die erste Potenz, in seinem Andersseyn oder der Differenz, dem Daseyn seiner Momente, die zweite, und in seiner Rückkehr in sich oder als Totalität die dritte Potenz genannt. —Hiergegen fällt sogleich auf, daß die Potenz so gebraucht eine Kategorie ist, die dem Quantum wesentlich angehört;—es ist bei diesen Potenzen nicht an die potentia,… des Aristoteles gedacht. So drückt das Potenzenverhältniß die Bestimmtheit aus, wie dieselbe als der Unterschied, wie er im besondern Begriffe des Quantums ist, zu seiner Wahrheit gelangt, aber nicht wie derselbe am Begriffe als solchem ist. Das Quantum enthält die Negativität, welche zur Natur des Begriffs gehört, noch gar nicht in dessen eigenthümlicher Bestimmung gesetzt; Unterschiede, die dem Quantum zukommen, sind oberflächliche Bestimmungen für den Begriff selbst; sie sind noch weit entfernt, bestimmt zu seyn, wie sie es im Begriffe sind. Es ist in der Kindheit des Philosophirens, daß wie von Pythagoras Zahlen—und erste, zweite Potenz u.s.f. haben insofern vor Zahlen nichts voraus,—zur Bezeichnung allgemeiner, wesentlicher Unterschiede gebraucht worden sind. Es war dieß eine Vorstufe des reinen denkenden Erfassens; nach Pythagoras erst sind die Gedankenbestimmungen selbst erfunden, d. i. für sich zum Bewußtseyn gebracht worden. Aber von solchen weg zu Zahlenbestimmungen zurückzugehen, gehört einem sich unvermögend fühlenden Denken an, das nun im Gegensatze gegen vorhandene philosophische Bildung, die an Gedankenbestimmungen gewohnt ist, selbst das Lächerliche hinzufügt, jene Schwäche für etwas Neues, Vornehmes und für einen Fortschritt geltend machen zu wollen.\n\nInsofern der Potenzen-Ausdruck nur als Symbol gebraucht wird, so ist dagegen so wenig zu sagen, als gegen die Zahlen oder Symbole anderer Art für Begriffe; aber zugleich ebenso viel, als gegen alle Symbolik überhaupt, in welcher reine Begriffs- oder philosophische Bestimmungen dargestellt werden sollen. Die Philosophie bedarf solche Hülfe nicht, weder aus der sinnlichen Welt, noch aus der vorstellenden Einbildungskraft, auch nicht aus Sphären ihres eigenthümlichen Bodens, welche untergeordnet sind, deren Bestimmungen daher nicht für höhere Kreise und für das Ganze passen. Das Letztere geschieht, wenn überhaupt Kategorien des Endlichen auf das Unendliche angewendet werden; die geläufigen Bestimmungen von Kraft, oder Substantialität, Ursache und Wirkung u.s.f. sind gleichfalls nur Symbole für den Ausdruck z.B. lebendiger oder geistiger Verhältnisse, d. i. unwahre Bestimmungen für dieselben, so noch mehr die Potenzen des Quantums und gezählte Potenzen, für dergleichen und für spekulative Verhältnisse überhaupt.—Wenn Zahlen, Potenzen, das Mathematisch-Unendliche und dergleichen nicht als Symbole, sondern als Formen für philosophische Bestimmungen, und damit selbst als philosophische Formen sollen gebraucht werden, so müßte vor Allem ihre philosophische Bedeutung, d. i. ihre Begriffsbestimmtheit aufgezeigt werden. Geschieht dieß, so sind sie selbst überflüssige Bezeichnungen; die Begriffsbestimmtheit bezeichnet sich selbst, und ihre Bezeichnung ist allein die richtige und passende. Der Gebrauch jener Formen ist darum weiter nichts, als ein bequemes Mittel, es zu ersparen, die Begriffsbestimmungen zu fassen, anzugeben und zu rechtfertigen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0001","text":"Es ist oben, in den Anmerkungen über das Quantitativ-Unendliche auseinander gesetzt worden, daß dieses so wie die Schwierigkeiten, die sich darüber ergeben, in dem qualitativen Momente, das sich im Quantitativen hervorthut, ihren Ursprung haben, und wie das Qualitative des Potenzenverhältnisses insbesondere, in die mannigfaltigen Entwickelungen und Verwickelungen ausgeht; als der Grundmangel, der die Auffassung des Begriffes verhindert, wurde auf gezeigt, daß bei dem Unendlichen nur nach der negativen Bestimmung, die Negation des Quantums zu seyn, stehen geblieben und nicht zu der einfachen Bestimmung, dem Affirmativen, daß dieses das Qualitative ist, fortgegangen wird.—Hier bleibt nur übrig, noch eine Bemerkung über die in der Philosophie geschehene Einmischung von Formen des Quantitativen in die reinen qualitativen Formen des Denkens, zu machen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"79.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0002","text":"Besonders ist es das Potenzenverhältniß, welches in neuerer Zeit auf Begriffsbestimmungen angewendet worden ist. Der Begriff in seiner Unmittelbarkeit wurde die erste Potenz, in seinem Andersseyn oder der Differenz, dem Daseyn seiner Momente, die zweite, und in seiner Rückkehr in sich oder als Totalität die dritte Potenz genannt. —Hiergegen fällt sogleich auf, daß die Potenz so gebraucht eine Kategorie ist, die dem Quantum wesentlich angehört;—es ist bei diesen Potenzen nicht an die potentia,… des Aristoteles gedacht. So drückt das Potenzenverhältniß die Bestimmtheit aus, wie dieselbe als der Unterschied, wie er im besondern Begriffe des Quantums ist, zu seiner Wahrheit gelangt, aber nicht wie derselbe am Begriffe als solchem ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"79.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0003","text":"Das Quantum enthält die Negativität, welche zur Natur des Begriffs gehört, noch gar nicht in dessen eigenthümlicher Bestimmung gesetzt; Unterschiede, die dem Quantum zukommen, sind oberflächliche Bestimmungen für den Begriff selbst; sie sind noch weit entfernt, bestimmt zu seyn, wie sie es im Begriffe sind. Es ist in der Kindheit des Philosophirens, daß wie von Pythagoras Zahlen—und erste, zweite Potenz u.s.f. haben insofern vor Zahlen nichts voraus,—zur Bezeichnung allgemeiner, wesentlicher Unterschiede gebraucht worden sind. Es war dieß eine Vorstufe des reinen denkenden Erfassens; nach Pythagoras erst sind die Gedankenbestimmungen selbst erfunden, d. i. für sich zum Bewußtseyn gebracht worden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"79.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0004","text":"Aber von solchen weg zu Zahlenbestimmungen zurückzugehen, gehört einem sich unvermögend fühlenden Denken an, das nun im Gegensatze gegen vorhandene philosophische Bildung, die an Gedankenbestimmungen gewohnt ist, selbst das Lächerliche hinzufügt, jene Schwäche für etwas Neues, Vornehmes und für einen Fortschritt geltend machen zu wollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"79.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0005","text":"Insofern der Potenzen-Ausdruck nur als Symbol gebraucht wird, so ist dagegen so wenig zu sagen, als gegen die Zahlen oder Symbole anderer Art für Begriffe; aber zugleich ebenso viel, als gegen alle Symbolik überhaupt, in welcher reine Begriffs- oder philosophische Bestimmungen dargestellt werden sollen. Die Philosophie bedarf solche Hülfe nicht, weder aus der sinnlichen Welt, noch aus der vorstellenden Einbildungskraft, auch nicht aus Sphären ihres eigenthümlichen Bodens, welche untergeordnet sind, deren Bestimmungen daher nicht für höhere Kreise und für das Ganze passen. Das Letztere geschieht, wenn überhaupt Kategorien des Endlichen auf das Unendliche angewendet werden; die geläufigen Bestimmungen von Kraft, oder Substantialität, Ursache und Wirkung u.s.f. sind gleichfalls nur Symbole für den Ausdruck z.B. lebendiger oder geistiger Verhältnisse, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"79.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0006","text":"unwahre Bestimmungen für dieselben, so noch mehr die Potenzen des Quantums und gezählte Potenzen, für dergleichen und für spekulative Verhältnisse überhaupt.—Wenn Zahlen, Potenzen, das Mathematisch-Unendliche und dergleichen nicht als Symbole, sondern als Formen für philosophische Bestimmungen, und damit selbst als philosophische Formen sollen gebraucht werden, so müßte vor Allem ihre philosophische Bedeutung, d. i. ihre Begriffsbestimmtheit aufgezeigt werden. Geschieht dieß, so sind sie selbst überflüssige Bezeichnungen; die Begriffsbestimmtheit bezeichnet sich selbst, und ihre Bezeichnung ist allein die richtige und passende. Der Gebrauch jener Formen ist darum weiter nichts, als ein bequemes Mittel, es zu ersparen, die Begriffsbestimmungen zu fassen, anzugeben und zu rechtfertigen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"79.6"}],"sha256":"c660d75557e00de55660b3f1a16415c7fc6bc007242ac93ddb351a64173650d0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104017388912Z_dc835d9d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"c660d75557e00de55660b3f1a16415c7fc6bc007242ac93ddb351a64173650d0","sha256":"d6df319420c9ce811f22e72c3eabc5379051aa41137e81f1348e76046f61538b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:40:17.388941+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0001","text":"It has been set forth above, in the remarks on the quantitative infinite, that this, as also the difficulties that arise concerning it, have their origin in the qualitative moment which comes to the fore in the quantitative, and how the qualitative of the relation of powers in particular proceeds into manifold developments and complications; it was pointed out as the fundamental defect that prevents the apprehension of the Concept, that with the infinite one remains at the merely negative determination, of being the negation of quantum, and does not advance to the simple determination, the affirmative, namely, that this is the qualitative.—There remains here only to make a further remark concerning the intermingling, which has occurred in philosophy, of forms of the quantitative with the pure qualitative forms of thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"79.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_20:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0002","text":"It is especially the relation of powers that has in recent times been applied to determinations of the Concept. The Concept in its immediacy was called the first power, in its otherness or difference, the existence of its moments, the second, and in its return into itself or as totality, the third power. —Against this it immediately strikes one that power, thus used, is a category belonging essentially to quantum;—in these powers there is no thought of Aristotle's potentia,…. Thus the relation of powers expresses determinacy as it attains its truth as the difference such as it is in the particular Concept of quantum, but not such as it is in the Concept as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"79.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_20:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0003","text":"Quantum does not yet contain the negativity that belongs to the nature of the Concept as posited in its peculiar determinacy at all; differences that pertain to quantum are superficial determinations for the Concept itself; they are still far from being determinate as they are in the Concept. It belongs to the childhood of philosophizing that, as with Pythagoras, numbers—and first, second power, etc., have in this respect no advantage over numbers—have been used to designate universal, essential differences. This was a preliminary stage of pure thinking apprehension; only after Pythagoras were determinations of thought themselves invented, i.e. brought to consciousness for themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"79.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_20:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0004","text":"But to go back from such determinations to numerical determinations belongs to a thinking that feels itself incapable, which, now in opposition to the philosophical cultivation at hand, accustomed to determinations of thought, further adds the ridiculousness of wishing to pass off that weakness as something new, distinguished, and as a progress.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"79.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_20:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0005","text":"Insofar as the expression of powers is used only as a symbol, there is as little to be said against it as against numbers or symbols of another kind for Concepts; but at the same time just as much as against all symbolism in general, in which pure determinations of the Concept or philosophical determinations are supposed to be represented. Philosophy requires no such assistance, neither from the sensible world nor from representational imagination, nor yet from spheres of its own ground that are subordinate, whose determinations therefore do not suit higher circles and the whole. The latter occurs whenever categories of the finite are applied to the infinite; the customary determinations of force, or substantiality, cause and effect, etc., are likewise only symbols for the expression, e.g., of living or spiritual relations, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"79.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_20:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_20:P0006","text":"untrue determinations for them; still more so are the powers of quantum and numbered powers for such relations and for speculative relations in general.—If numbers, powers, the mathematical infinite, and the like are to be used not as symbols but as forms for philosophical determinations, and thereby themselves as philosophical forms, then above all their philosophical significance, i.e. their determinacy of the Concept, would have to be exhibited. If this is done, they are themselves superfluous designations; the determinacy of the Concept designates itself, and its designation alone is the correct and fitting one. The use of those forms is therefore nothing further than a convenient means of sparing oneself the task of grasping, setting forth, and justifying determinations of the Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"79.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_20:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"3ca53e4dc94508155c64e190a04a4a7c7d29fbca9c11e0fcfe43113b14ab5cf2","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM","title":"Third Section. Measure.","order":80,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DADM","text":"Im Maaße sind, abstrakt ausgedrückt, Qualität und Quantität vereinigt. Das Seyn als solches ist unmittelbare Gleichheit der Bestimmtheit mit sich selbst. Diese Unmittelbarkeit der Bestimmtheit hat sich aufgehoben. Die Quantität ist das so in sich zurückgekehrte Seyn, daß es einfache Gleichheit mit sich als Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Bestimmtheit ist. Aber diese Gleichgültigkeit ist nur die Äußerlichkeit, nicht an sich selbst, sondern in Anderem die Bestimmtheit zu haben. Das Dritte ist nun die sich auf sich selbst beziehende Äußerlichkeit; als Beziehung auf sich ist es zugleich aufgehobene Äußerlichkeit, und hat an ihr selbst den Unterschied von sich,—der als Äußerlichkeit das quantitative, als in sich zurückgenommene, das qualitative Moment ist.\n\nIndem die Modalität, unter den Kategorien des transcendentalen Idealismus, nach der Quantität und Qualität, auf Einschiebung der Relation, aufgeführt wird, so kann derselben hier erwähnt werden. Diese Kategorie hat daselbst die Bedeutung, die Beziehung des Gegenstandes auf das Denken zu seyn. Im Sinne jenes Idealismus ist das Denken überhaupt dem Ding-an-sich wesentlich äußerlich. Insofern die andern Kategorien nur die transcendentale Bestimmung haben, dem Bewußtseyn, aber als das Objektive desselben, anzugehören, so enthält die Modalität, als die Kategorie der Beziehung auf das Subjekt, insofern relativ die Bestimmung der Reflexion in sich; d.h. die Objektivität, welche den andern Kategorien zukomme, mangelt denen der Modalität; diese vermehren, nach Kants Ausdruck, den Begriffe als Bestimmung des Objekts nicht im mindesten, sondern drücken nur das Verhältniß zum Erkenntnißvermögen aus, (Kr. d. rein. Vern. 2te Aufl. s. S. 99, 266).—Die Kategorien, die Kant unter der Modalität zusammenfaßt, Möglichkeit, Wirklichkeit und Nothwendigkeit, werden in der Folge an ihrer Stelle vorkommen; Kant hat die unendlich wichtige Form der Triplicität, so sehr sie bei ihm nur erst als ein formeller Lichtfunken erschienen, nicht auf die Gattungen seiner Kategorien (Quantität, Qualität u.s.f.) wie auch diesen Namen, nur auf deren Arten angewendet; daher hat er nicht auf das Dritte der Qualität und Quantität kommen können.\n\nBei Spinoza ist der Modus nach Substanz und Attribut gleichfalls das Dritte; er erklärt ihn für die Affektionen der Substanz, oder für dasjenige, was in einem Andern ist, durch welches es auch begriffen wird. Dieses Dritte ist nach diesem Begriffe nur die Äußerlichkeit als solche; wie sonst erinnert worden, daß bei Spinoza überhaupt der starren Substantialität die Rückkehr in sich selbst fehlt.\n\nDie hier gemachte Bemerkung dehnt sich allgemeiner auf die Systeme des Pantheismus aus, welche der Gedanke etwas ausgebildet hat. Das Seyn, das Eine, die Substanz, das Unendliche, das Wesen ist das Erste; gegen dieses Abstraktum kann das Zweite, alle Bestimmtheit, überhaupt als das nur Endliche, nur Accidentelle, Vergängliche, Außer- und Unwesentliche u.s.f., ebenso abstrakt zusammengefaßt werden wie in dem ganz formalen Denken gewöhnlich und zunächst geschieht. Aber es drängt sich zu sehr der Zusammenhang dieses Zweiten mit dem Ersten auf, um es nicht zugleich in einer Einheit mit demselben zu fassen, wie das Attribut bei Spinoza die ganze Substanz ist, aber von dem Verstand, selbst einer Beschränkung oder Modus, gefaßt; der Modus aber, das Nichtsubstantielle überhaupt, das nur aus einem Andern gefaßt werden kann, macht so das andere Extrem zu der Substanz, das Dritte überhaupt, aus. Der indische Pantheismus hat in seiner ungeheuern Phantasterei gleichfalls, abstrakt genommen, diese Ausbildung erhalten, die sich durch ihr Maßloses hindurch als ein mässigender Faden zu einigem Interesse zieht, daß Brahm, das Eine des abstrakten Denkens durch die Gestaltung in Wischnu besonders in der Form Krischnas, zu dem Dritten, Siwa, fortgeht. Die Bestimmung dieses Dritten ist der Modus, Veränderung, Entstehen und Vergehen, das Feld der Äußerlichkeit überhaupt. Wenn diese indische Dreiheit zu einer Vergleichung nut der christlichen verleitet hat, so ist in ihnen zwar ein gemeinsames Element der Begriffsbestimmung zu erkennen, aber über den Unterschied ist wesentlich ein bestimmteres Bewußtseyn zu fassen; derselbe ist nicht nur unendlich, sondern die wahrhafte Unendlichkeit macht den Unterschied selbst aus. Jenes dritte Princip ist seiner Bestimmung nach das Auseinanderfahren der substantiellen Einheit, in ihr Gegegentheil, nicht die Rückkehr derselben zu sich, —das Geistlose vielmehr, nicht der Geist. In der wahrhaften Dreiheit, ist nicht nur Einheit, sondern Einigkeit, der Schluß zur inhaltsvollen und wirklichen Einheit, die in ihrer ganz konkreten Bestimmung der Geist ist, gebracht. Jenes Princip des Modus und der Veränderung schließt wohl die Einheit nicht überhaupt aus; wie nämlich im Spinozismus eben der Modus als solcher das Unwahre und nur die Substanz das wahrhafte ist, Alles auf diese zurückgeführt werden soll, welches dann ein Versenken alles Inhalts in die Leerheit, in nur formelle, inhaltslose Einheit ist, so ist auch Siwa wieder das große Ganze, von Brahm nicht unterschiedene, Brahm selbst; d. h. der Unterschied und die Bestimmtheit verschwindet nur wieder, aber wird nicht aufbewahrt, nicht aufgehoben, und die Einheit wird nicht zur konkreten Einheit, die Entzweiung nicht zur Versöhnung zurückgeführt. Das höchste Ziel für den in die Sphäre des Entstehens und Vergehens, der Modalität überhaupt versetzten Menschen ist die Versenkung in die Bewußtlosigkeit, die Einheit mit Brahm, die Vernichtung; dasselbe ist das buddhistische Nirvana, Nieban u.s.f.\n\nWenn nun der Modus überhaupt die abstrakte Äußerlichkeit, die Gleichgültigkeit gegen die qualitativen wie gegen die quantitativen Bestimmungen ist, und es im Wesen auf das Äußerliche, Unwesentliche nicht ankommen soll, so wird auch wieder in Vielem zugestanden, daß alles auf die Art und Weise ankomme; der Modus wird damit selbst für wesentlich zum Substantiellen einer Sache gehörig erklärt; in welcher sehr unbestimmten Beziehung wenigstens dieß liegt, daß dieß Äußerliche nicht so abstrakt das Äußerliche sey.\n\nHier hat der Modus die bestimmte Bedeutung das Maaß zu seyn. Der Spinozistische Modus, wie das indische Princip der Veränderung ist das Maaßlose. Das griechische selbst noch unbestimmte Bewußtseyn, daß Alles ein Maaß hat, so daß selbst Parmenides nach dem abstrakten Seyn die Nothwendigkeit, als die alte Grenze, die Allem gesetzt ist, eingeführt, ist der Anfang eines viel höhern Begriffs als die Substanz und der Unterschied des Modus von derselben enthält.-Das entwickeltere, reflektirtere Maaß ist die Nothwendigkeit; das Schicksal, die Nemesis, schränkt sich im Allgemeinen auf die Bestimmtheit des Maaßes ein, daß was sich vermesse, zu groß, zu hoch mache, auf das andere Extrem der Herabsetzung zur Nichtigkeit reducirt, und damit die Mitte des Maaßes, die Mittelmäßigkeit, hergestellt werde.—Das Absolute, Gott ist das Maaß aller Dinge, ist nicht stärker pantheistisch als die Definition: das Absolute, Gott ist das Seyn, aber unendlich wahrhafter.—Das Maaß ist zwar äußerliche Art und Weise, ein Mehr oder Weniger, welches aber zugleich ebenso in sich reflektirt, nicht bloß gleichgültige und äußerliche, sondern an sich seyende Bestimmtheit ist; es ist so die konkrete Wahrheit des Seyns; in dem Maaße haben darum die Völker etwas Unantastbares, Heiliges verehrt.\n\nEs liegt in dem Maaße bereits die Idee des Wesens, nämlich in der Unmittelbarkeit des Bestimmtseyns identisch mit sich zu seyn, so daß jene Unmittelbarkeit durch diese Identität-mit-sich zu einem Vermittelten herabgesetzt ist, wie diese ebenso nur durch diese Äußerlichkeit vermittelt aber die Vermittelung mit sich ist;—die Reflexion, deren Bestimmungen sind, aber in dieseni Seyn schlechthin nur als Momente ihrer negativen Einheit. Im Maaße ist das Qualitative quantitativ; die Bestimmtheit oder der Unterschied ist als gleichgültig, damit ist es ein Unterschied, der keiner ist; er ist aufgehoben; diese Quantitativität macht als Rückkehr in sich, worin sie als das Qualitative ist, das An- und Fürsichseyn aus, welches das Wesen ist. Aber das Maaß ist erst an sich oder im Begriffe das Wesen; dieser Begriff des Maaßes ist noch nicht gesetzt. Das Maaß noch als solches ist selbst die seyende Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen; seine Momente sind als ein Daseyn, eine Qualität und Quanta derselben, die nur erst an sich untrennbar, aber noch nicht die Bedeutung dieser reflektirten Bestimmung haben. Die Entwicklung des Maaßes, enthält die Unterscheidung dieser Momente, aber zugleich die Beziehung derselben, so daß die Identität, welche sie an sich sind, als ihre Beziehung aufeinander wird, d. i. gesetzt wird. Die Bedeutung dieser Entwickelung ist die Realisation des Maaßes, in der es sich zu sich selbst ins Verhältniß, und damit zugleich als Moment setzt; durch diese Vermittelung wird es als Aufgehobenes bestimmt; seine Unmittelbarkeit wie die seiner Momente verschwindet, sie sind als reflektirte; so als das hervorgetreten, was es seinem Begriffe nach ist, ist es in das Wesen übergegangen.\n\nDas Maaß ist zunächst unmittelbare Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen, so daß\n\nerstens ein Quantum ist, das qualitative Bedeutung hat, und als Maaß ist. Dessen Fortbestimmung ist, daß an ihm, dem an sich bestimmten, —der Unterschied seiner Momente, des qualitativen und quantitativen Bestimmtseyns, hervortritt. Diese Momente bestimmen sich weiter selbst zu Ganzen des Maaßes, welche insofern als Selbstständige sind; indem sie sich wesentlich aufeinander beziehen, wird das Maaß\n\nzweitens Verhältniß von specifischen Quantis, als selbstständigen Maaßen. Ihre Selbstständigkeit beruht aber wesentlich zugleich auf dem quantitativen Verhältnisse und dem Größenunterschiede; so wird ihre Selbstständigkeit ein Übergehen in einander. Das Maaß geht damit im Maaßlosen zu Grunde.—Dieß Jenseits des Maaßes ist aber die Negativität desselben nur an sich selbst; es ist dadurch\n\ndrittens die Indifferenz der Maaßbestimmungen, und als reell mit der in ihr enthaltenen Negativität das Maaß gesetzt, als umgekehrtes Verhältniß von Maaßen, welche als selbstständige Qualitäten wesentlich nur auf ihrer Quantität und auf ihrer negativen Beziehung aufeinander beruhen, und damit sich erweisen, nur Momente ihrer wahrhaft selbstständigen Einheit zu seyn, welche ihre Reflexion-in-sich und das Setzen derselben, das Wesen, ist.\n\nDie Entwickelung des Maaßes, die im Folgenden versucht worden, ist eine der schwierigsten Materien; indem sie von dem unmittelbaren, äußerlichen Maaße anfängt, hätte sie einer Seits zu der abstrakten Fortbestimmung des Quantitativen (einer Mathematik der Natur) fortzugehen, anderer Seits den Zusammenhang dieser Maaßbestimmung mit den Qualitäten der natürlichen Dinge anzuzeigen, wenigstens im Allgemeinen; denn die bestimmte Nachweisung des aus dem Begriffe des konkreten Gegenstandes hervorgehenden Zusammenhangs des Qualitativen und Quantitativen gehört in die besondere Wissenschaft des Konkreten; wovon Beispiele in der Encykl. der philos. Wissensch. 3te Aufl. §. 267 u. 270 Anm. das Gesetz des Falles und das der freien himmlischen Bewegung betreffend, nachzusehen sind. Es mag hierbei dieß überhaupt bemerkt werden, daß die verschiedenen Formen, in welchen sich das Maaß realisirt, auch verschiedenen Sphären der natürlichen Realität angehören. Die vollständige, abstrakte Gleichgültigkeit des entwickelten Maaßes d. i. der Gesetze desselben kann nur in der Sphäre des Mechanismus Statt haben, als in welchem das konkrete Körperliche nur die selbst abstrakte Materie ist; die qualitativen Unterschiede derselben haben wesentlich das Quantitative zu ihrer Bestimmtheit; Raum und Zeit sind die reinen Äußerlichkeiten selbst, und die Menge der Materien, Massen, Intensität des Gewichts, sind ebenso äußerliche Bestimmungen, die an dem Quantitativen ihre eigenthümliche Bestimmtheit haben. Dagegen wird solche Größebestimmtheit des abstrakt Materiellen schon durch die Mehrheit und damit einen Konflikt von Qualitäten, im Physikalischen, noch mehr aber im Organischen gestört. Aber es tritt hier nicht bloß der Konflikt von Qualitäten als solchen ein, sondern das Maaß wird hier höhern Verhältnissen untergeordnet, und die immanente Entwicklung des Maaßes vielmehr auf die einfache Form des unmittelbaren Maaßes reducirt. Die Glieder des animalischen Organismus haben ein Maaß, welches als ein einfaches Quantum im Verhältniß zu andern Quantis der andern Glieder steht; die Proportionen des menschlichen Körpers sind die festen Verhältnisse von solchen Quantis; die Naturwissenschaft hat noch weithin, von dem Zusammenhange solcher Größen mit den organischen Funktionen, von denen sie ganz abhängig sind, etwas einzusehen. Aber von der Herabsetzung eines immanenten Maaßes zu einer bloß äußerlich determinirten Größe ist die Bewegung das nächste Beispiel. An den Himmelskörpern ist sie die freie nur durch den Begriff bestimmte Bewegung, deren Größen hiermit ebenso nur von demselben abhängen (s. oben), aber von dem Organischen wird sie zur willkürlichen oder mechanisch-regelmäßigen, d. h. überhaupt abstrakten formellen Bewegung herunter gesetzt.\n\nNoch weniger aber findet im Reich des Geistes eine eigenthümliche, freie Entwicklung des Maaßes Statt. Man sieht z.B. wohl ein, daß eine republikanische Verfassung, wie die atheniensische oder eine durch Demokratie versetzte aristokratische nur bei einer gewissen Größe des Staats Platz haben kann; daß in der entwickelten bürgerlichen Gesellschaft die Mengen von Individuen, welche den verschiedenen Gewerben angehören, in einem Verhältnisse mit einander stehen; aber dieß giebt weder Gesetze von Maaßen noch eigenthümliche Formen desselben. Im Geistigen als solchen kommen Unterschiede von Intensität des Charakters, Stärke der Einbildungskraft, der Empfindungen, der Vorstellungen u.s.f. vor; aber über dieß Unbestimmte der Stärke oder Schwäche geht die Bestimmung nicht hinaus. Wie matt und völlig leer die sogenannten Gesetze ausfallen, die über das Verhältniß von Stärke und Schwäche der Empfindungen, Vorstellungen u.s.f. aufgestellt werden, wird man inne, wenn man die Psychologien nachsieht, welche sich mit dergleichen bemühen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0001","text":"Im Maaße sind, abstrakt ausgedrückt, Qualität und Quantität vereinigt. Das Seyn als solches ist unmittelbare Gleichheit der Bestimmtheit mit sich selbst. Diese Unmittelbarkeit der Bestimmtheit hat sich aufgehoben. Die Quantität ist das so in sich zurückgekehrte Seyn, daß es einfache Gleichheit mit sich als Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Bestimmtheit ist. Aber diese Gleichgültigkeit ist nur die Äußerlichkeit, nicht an sich selbst, sondern in Anderem die Bestimmtheit zu haben. Das Dritte ist nun die sich auf sich selbst beziehende Äußerlichkeit; als Beziehung auf sich ist es zugleich aufgehobene Äußerlichkeit, und hat an ihr selbst den Unterschied von sich,—der als Äußerlichkeit das quantitative, als in sich zurückgenommene, das qualitative Moment ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"80.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0002","text":"Indem die Modalität, unter den Kategorien des transcendentalen Idealismus, nach der Quantität und Qualität, auf Einschiebung der Relation, aufgeführt wird, so kann derselben hier erwähnt werden. Diese Kategorie hat daselbst die Bedeutung, die Beziehung des Gegenstandes auf das Denken zu seyn. Im Sinne jenes Idealismus ist das Denken überhaupt dem Ding-an-sich wesentlich äußerlich. Insofern die andern Kategorien nur die transcendentale Bestimmung haben, dem Bewußtseyn, aber als das Objektive desselben, anzugehören, so enthält die Modalität, als die Kategorie der Beziehung auf das Subjekt, insofern relativ die Bestimmung der Reflexion in sich; d.h.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"80.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0003","text":"die Objektivität, welche den andern Kategorien zukomme, mangelt denen der Modalität; diese vermehren, nach Kants Ausdruck, den Begriffe als Bestimmung des Objekts nicht im mindesten, sondern drücken nur das Verhältniß zum Erkenntnißvermögen aus, (Kr. d. rein. Vern. 2te Aufl. s. S. 99, 266).—Die Kategorien, die Kant unter der Modalität zusammenfaßt, Möglichkeit, Wirklichkeit und Nothwendigkeit, werden in der Folge an ihrer Stelle vorkommen; Kant hat die unendlich wichtige Form der Triplicität, so sehr sie bei ihm nur erst als ein formeller Lichtfunken erschienen, nicht auf die Gattungen seiner Kategorien (Quantität, Qualität u.s.f.) wie auch diesen Namen, nur auf deren Arten angewendet; daher hat er nicht auf das Dritte der Qualität und Quantität kommen können.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"80.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0004","text":"Bei Spinoza ist der Modus nach Substanz und Attribut gleichfalls das Dritte; er erklärt ihn für die Affektionen der Substanz, oder für dasjenige, was in einem Andern ist, durch welches es auch begriffen wird. Dieses Dritte ist nach diesem Begriffe nur die Äußerlichkeit als solche; wie sonst erinnert worden, daß bei Spinoza überhaupt der starren Substantialität die Rückkehr in sich selbst fehlt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"80.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0005","text":"Die hier gemachte Bemerkung dehnt sich allgemeiner auf die Systeme des Pantheismus aus, welche der Gedanke etwas ausgebildet hat. Das Seyn, das Eine, die Substanz, das Unendliche, das Wesen ist das Erste; gegen dieses Abstraktum kann das Zweite, alle Bestimmtheit, überhaupt als das nur Endliche, nur Accidentelle, Vergängliche, Außer- und Unwesentliche u.s.f., ebenso abstrakt zusammengefaßt werden wie in dem ganz formalen Denken gewöhnlich und zunächst geschieht. Aber es drängt sich zu sehr der Zusammenhang dieses Zweiten mit dem Ersten auf, um es nicht zugleich in einer Einheit mit demselben zu fassen, wie das Attribut bei Spinoza die ganze Substanz ist, aber von dem Verstand, selbst einer Beschränkung oder Modus, gefaßt; der Modus aber, das Nichtsubstantielle überhaupt, das nur aus einem Andern gefaßt werden kann, macht so das andere Extrem zu der Substanz, das Dritte überhaupt, aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"80.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0006","text":"Der indische Pantheismus hat in seiner ungeheuern Phantasterei gleichfalls, abstrakt genommen, diese Ausbildung erhalten, die sich durch ihr Maßloses hindurch als ein mässigender Faden zu einigem Interesse zieht, daß Brahm, das Eine des abstrakten Denkens durch die Gestaltung in Wischnu besonders in der Form Krischnas, zu dem Dritten, Siwa, fortgeht. Die Bestimmung dieses Dritten ist der Modus, Veränderung, Entstehen und Vergehen, das Feld der Äußerlichkeit überhaupt. Wenn diese indische Dreiheit zu einer Vergleichung nut der christlichen verleitet hat, so ist in ihnen zwar ein gemeinsames Element der Begriffsbestimmung zu erkennen, aber über den Unterschied ist wesentlich ein bestimmteres Bewußtseyn zu fassen; derselbe ist nicht nur unendlich, sondern die wahrhafte Unendlichkeit macht den Unterschied selbst aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"80.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0007","text":"Jenes dritte Princip ist seiner Bestimmung nach das Auseinanderfahren der substantiellen Einheit, in ihr Gegegentheil, nicht die Rückkehr derselben zu sich, —das Geistlose vielmehr, nicht der Geist. In der wahrhaften Dreiheit, ist nicht nur Einheit, sondern Einigkeit, der Schluß zur inhaltsvollen und wirklichen Einheit, die in ihrer ganz konkreten Bestimmung der Geist ist, gebracht. Jenes Princip des Modus und der Veränderung schließt wohl die Einheit nicht überhaupt aus; wie nämlich im Spinozismus eben der Modus als solcher das Unwahre und nur die Substanz das wahrhafte ist, Alles auf diese zurückgeführt werden soll, welches dann ein Versenken alles Inhalts in die Leerheit, in nur formelle, inhaltslose Einheit ist, so ist auch Siwa wieder das große Ganze, von Brahm nicht unterschiedene, Brahm selbst; d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"80.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0008","text":"der Unterschied und die Bestimmtheit verschwindet nur wieder, aber wird nicht aufbewahrt, nicht aufgehoben, und die Einheit wird nicht zur konkreten Einheit, die Entzweiung nicht zur Versöhnung zurückgeführt. Das höchste Ziel für den in die Sphäre des Entstehens und Vergehens, der Modalität überhaupt versetzten Menschen ist die Versenkung in die Bewußtlosigkeit, die Einheit mit Brahm, die Vernichtung; dasselbe ist das buddhistische Nirvana, Nieban u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"80.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0009","text":"Wenn nun der Modus überhaupt die abstrakte Äußerlichkeit, die Gleichgültigkeit gegen die qualitativen wie gegen die quantitativen Bestimmungen ist, und es im Wesen auf das Äußerliche, Unwesentliche nicht ankommen soll, so wird auch wieder in Vielem zugestanden, daß alles auf die Art und Weise ankomme; der Modus wird damit selbst für wesentlich zum Substantiellen einer Sache gehörig erklärt; in welcher sehr unbestimmten Beziehung wenigstens dieß liegt, daß dieß Äußerliche nicht so abstrakt das Äußerliche sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"80.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0010","text":"Hier hat der Modus die bestimmte Bedeutung das Maaß zu seyn. Der Spinozistische Modus, wie das indische Princip der Veränderung ist das Maaßlose. Das griechische selbst noch unbestimmte Bewußtseyn, daß Alles ein Maaß hat, so daß selbst Parmenides nach dem abstrakten Seyn die Nothwendigkeit, als die alte Grenze, die Allem gesetzt ist, eingeführt, ist der Anfang eines viel höhern Begriffs als die Substanz und der Unterschied des Modus von derselben enthält.-Das entwickeltere, reflektirtere Maaß ist die Nothwendigkeit; das Schicksal, die Nemesis, schränkt sich im Allgemeinen auf die Bestimmtheit des Maaßes ein, daß was sich vermesse, zu groß, zu hoch mache, auf das andere Extrem der Herabsetzung zur Nichtigkeit reducirt, und damit die Mitte des Maaßes, die Mittelmäßigkeit, hergestellt werde.—Das Absolute, Gott ist das Maaß aller Dinge, ist nicht stärker pantheistisch als die Definition:","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"80.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0011","text":"das Absolute, Gott ist das Seyn, aber unendlich wahrhafter.—Das Maaß ist zwar äußerliche Art und Weise, ein Mehr oder Weniger, welches aber zugleich ebenso in sich reflektirt, nicht bloß gleichgültige und äußerliche, sondern an sich seyende Bestimmtheit ist; es ist so die konkrete Wahrheit des Seyns; in dem Maaße haben darum die Völker etwas Unantastbares, Heiliges verehrt.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"80.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0012","text":"Es liegt in dem Maaße bereits die Idee des Wesens, nämlich in der Unmittelbarkeit des Bestimmtseyns identisch mit sich zu seyn, so daß jene Unmittelbarkeit durch diese Identität-mit-sich zu einem Vermittelten herabgesetzt ist, wie diese ebenso nur durch diese Äußerlichkeit vermittelt aber die Vermittelung mit sich ist;—die Reflexion, deren Bestimmungen sind, aber in dieseni Seyn schlechthin nur als Momente ihrer negativen Einheit. Im Maaße ist das Qualitative quantitativ; die Bestimmtheit oder der Unterschied ist als gleichgültig, damit ist es ein Unterschied, der keiner ist; er ist aufgehoben; diese Quantitativität macht als Rückkehr in sich, worin sie als das Qualitative ist, das An- und Fürsichseyn aus, welches das Wesen ist. Aber das Maaß ist erst an sich oder im Begriffe das Wesen; dieser Begriff des Maaßes ist noch nicht gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"80.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0013","text":"Das Maaß noch als solches ist selbst die seyende Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen; seine Momente sind als ein Daseyn, eine Qualität und Quanta derselben, die nur erst an sich untrennbar, aber noch nicht die Bedeutung dieser reflektirten Bestimmung haben. Die Entwicklung des Maaßes, enthält die Unterscheidung dieser Momente, aber zugleich die Beziehung derselben, so daß die Identität, welche sie an sich sind, als ihre Beziehung aufeinander wird, d. i. gesetzt wird. Die Bedeutung dieser Entwickelung ist die Realisation des Maaßes, in der es sich zu sich selbst ins Verhältniß, und damit zugleich als Moment setzt; durch diese Vermittelung wird es als Aufgehobenes bestimmt; seine Unmittelbarkeit wie die seiner Momente verschwindet, sie sind als reflektirte; so als das hervorgetreten, was es seinem Begriffe nach ist, ist es in das Wesen übergegangen.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"80.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0014","text":"Das Maaß ist zunächst unmittelbare Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen, so daß","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"80.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0015","text":"erstens ein Quantum ist, das qualitative Bedeutung hat, und als Maaß ist. Dessen Fortbestimmung ist, daß an ihm, dem an sich bestimmten, —der Unterschied seiner Momente, des qualitativen und quantitativen Bestimmtseyns, hervortritt. Diese Momente bestimmen sich weiter selbst zu Ganzen des Maaßes, welche insofern als Selbstständige sind; indem sie sich wesentlich aufeinander beziehen, wird das Maaß","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"80.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0016","text":"zweitens Verhältniß von specifischen Quantis, als selbstständigen Maaßen. Ihre Selbstständigkeit beruht aber wesentlich zugleich auf dem quantitativen Verhältnisse und dem Größenunterschiede; so wird ihre Selbstständigkeit ein Übergehen in einander. Das Maaß geht damit im Maaßlosen zu Grunde.—Dieß Jenseits des Maaßes ist aber die Negativität desselben nur an sich selbst; es ist dadurch","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"80.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0017","text":"drittens die Indifferenz der Maaßbestimmungen, und als reell mit der in ihr enthaltenen Negativität das Maaß gesetzt, als umgekehrtes Verhältniß von Maaßen, welche als selbstständige Qualitäten wesentlich nur auf ihrer Quantität und auf ihrer negativen Beziehung aufeinander beruhen, und damit sich erweisen, nur Momente ihrer wahrhaft selbstständigen Einheit zu seyn, welche ihre Reflexion-in-sich und das Setzen derselben, das Wesen, ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"80.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0018","text":"Die Entwickelung des Maaßes, die im Folgenden versucht worden, ist eine der schwierigsten Materien; indem sie von dem unmittelbaren, äußerlichen Maaße anfängt, hätte sie einer Seits zu der abstrakten Fortbestimmung des Quantitativen (einer Mathematik der Natur) fortzugehen, anderer Seits den Zusammenhang dieser Maaßbestimmung mit den Qualitäten der natürlichen Dinge anzuzeigen, wenigstens im Allgemeinen; denn die bestimmte Nachweisung des aus dem Begriffe des konkreten Gegenstandes hervorgehenden Zusammenhangs des Qualitativen und Quantitativen gehört in die besondere Wissenschaft des Konkreten; wovon Beispiele in der Encykl. der philos. Wissensch. 3te Aufl. §. 267 u. 270 Anm. das Gesetz des Falles und das der freien himmlischen Bewegung betreffend, nachzusehen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"80.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0019","text":"Es mag hierbei dieß überhaupt bemerkt werden, daß die verschiedenen Formen, in welchen sich das Maaß realisirt, auch verschiedenen Sphären der natürlichen Realität angehören. Die vollständige, abstrakte Gleichgültigkeit des entwickelten Maaßes d. i. der Gesetze desselben kann nur in der Sphäre des Mechanismus Statt haben, als in welchem das konkrete Körperliche nur die selbst abstrakte Materie ist; die qualitativen Unterschiede derselben haben wesentlich das Quantitative zu ihrer Bestimmtheit; Raum und Zeit sind die reinen Äußerlichkeiten selbst, und die Menge der Materien, Massen, Intensität des Gewichts, sind ebenso äußerliche Bestimmungen, die an dem Quantitativen ihre eigenthümliche Bestimmtheit haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"80.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0020","text":"Dagegen wird solche Größebestimmtheit des abstrakt Materiellen schon durch die Mehrheit und damit einen Konflikt von Qualitäten, im Physikalischen, noch mehr aber im Organischen gestört. Aber es tritt hier nicht bloß der Konflikt von Qualitäten als solchen ein, sondern das Maaß wird hier höhern Verhältnissen untergeordnet, und die immanente Entwicklung des Maaßes vielmehr auf die einfache Form des unmittelbaren Maaßes reducirt. Die Glieder des animalischen Organismus haben ein Maaß, welches als ein einfaches Quantum im Verhältniß zu andern Quantis der andern Glieder steht; die Proportionen des menschlichen Körpers sind die festen Verhältnisse von solchen Quantis; die Naturwissenschaft hat noch weithin, von dem Zusammenhange solcher Größen mit den organischen Funktionen, von denen sie ganz abhängig sind, etwas einzusehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"80.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0021","text":"Aber von der Herabsetzung eines immanenten Maaßes zu einer bloß äußerlich determinirten Größe ist die Bewegung das nächste Beispiel. An den Himmelskörpern ist sie die freie nur durch den Begriff bestimmte Bewegung, deren Größen hiermit ebenso nur von demselben abhängen (s. oben), aber von dem Organischen wird sie zur willkürlichen oder mechanisch-regelmäßigen, d. h. überhaupt abstrakten formellen Bewegung herunter gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"80.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0022","text":"Noch weniger aber findet im Reich des Geistes eine eigenthümliche, freie Entwicklung des Maaßes Statt. Man sieht z.B. wohl ein, daß eine republikanische Verfassung, wie die atheniensische oder eine durch Demokratie versetzte aristokratische nur bei einer gewissen Größe des Staats Platz haben kann; daß in der entwickelten bürgerlichen Gesellschaft die Mengen von Individuen, welche den verschiedenen Gewerben angehören, in einem Verhältnisse mit einander stehen; aber dieß giebt weder Gesetze von Maaßen noch eigenthümliche Formen desselben. Im Geistigen als solchen kommen Unterschiede von Intensität des Charakters, Stärke der Einbildungskraft, der Empfindungen, der Vorstellungen u.s.f. vor; aber über dieß Unbestimmte der Stärke oder Schwäche geht die Bestimmung nicht hinaus.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"80.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0023","text":"Wie matt und völlig leer die sogenannten Gesetze ausfallen, die über das Verhältniß von Stärke und Schwäche der Empfindungen, Vorstellungen u.s.f. aufgestellt werden, wird man inne, wenn man die Psychologien nachsieht, welche sich mit dergleichen bemühen.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"80.23"}],"sha256":"c56e7b6feea756b1acb59322550b08bffa5163b3981abe2cf374c54b12564190","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104047206465Z_4eb08df6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Third Section. Measure.","source_sha256":"c56e7b6feea756b1acb59322550b08bffa5163b3981abe2cf374c54b12564190","sha256":"c9486bd191725fc70f9c5c55af37872818764167ef072ec19935728cea03d8c5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:40:47.206496+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0001","text":"In Measure, expressed abstractly, quality and quantity are united. Being as such is immediate equality of determinacy with itself. This immediacy of determinacy has sublated itself. Quantity is Being thus returned into itself, such that it is simple equality with itself as indifference toward determinacy. But this indifference is only the externality of having determinacy, not in itself, but in an other. The third is now externality relating itself to itself; as relation to itself it is at the same time sublated externality, and has in itself the difference from itself,—which, as externality, is the quantitative moment, and, as taken back into itself, the qualitative moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"80.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0002","text":"Since modality, among the categories of transcendental idealism, is listed after quantity and quality, with the interpolation of relation, it may be mentioned here. There this category has the significance of being the relation of the object to thinking. In the sense of that idealism, thinking in general is essentially external to the thing-in-itself. Inasmuch as the other categories have only the transcendental determination of belonging to consciousness, but as its objective element, modality, as the category of relation to the subject, thus relatively contains within itself the determination of reflection; i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"80.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0003","text":"the objectivity which belongs to the other categories is lacking to those of modality; these, in Kant's expression, do not in the least increase the concept as a determination of the object, but express only the relation to the faculty of cognition (Critique of Pure Reason, 2nd ed., pp. 99, 266).—The categories which Kant subsumes under modality, possibility, actuality, and necessity, will occur later in their place; Kant did not apply the infinitely important form of triplicity, however much it appeared in him at first only as a formal flash of light, to the genera of his categories (quantity, quality, etc.), nor indeed this name, but only to their species; consequently he could not arrive at the third of quality and quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"80.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0004","text":"In Spinoza too, mode is the third after substance and attribute; he explains it as the affections of substance, or as that which is in an other, through which it is also conceived. According to this concept, this third is only externality as such; as has otherwise been recalled, that in Spinoza in general rigid substantiality lacks the return into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"80.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0005","text":"The observation made here extends more generally to the systems of pantheism which thought has to some extent elaborated. Being, the One, substance, the infinite, essence, is the first; over against this abstraction the second, all determinacy, can in general be abstractly gathered together as merely finite, merely accidental, transitory, external and inessential, etc., just as is customarily and initially done in wholly formal thinking. But the connection of this second with the first presses itself forward too strongly for it not to be grasped at the same time in a unity with the latter, as the attribute in Spinoza is the whole substance, but is apprehended by the understanding, itself a limitation or mode; mode, however, the non-substantial in general, which can be apprehended only from an other, thus constitutes the other extreme to substance, the third in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"80.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0006","text":"Indian pantheism, in its monstrous fantasy, has likewise received, abstractly considered, this elaboration, which, through its immoderateness, draws itself out as a moderating thread to some interest: Brahma, the One of abstract thinking, proceeds through configuration in Vishnu, especially in the form of Krishna, to the third, Siva. The determination of this third is mode, alteration, coming-to-be and passing-away, the field of externality in general. If this Indian trinity has induced a comparison with the Christian one, a common element of conceptual determination is indeed recognizable in them; but a more determinate consciousness of the difference must essentially be attained; it is not merely infinite, but true infinity itself constitutes the difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"80.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0007","text":"That third principle, according to its determination, is the divergence of substantial unity into its opposite, not its return to itself,—rather the spiritless, not spirit. In true trinity there is not merely unity, but unification; the syllogism into substantial and actual unity, which in its wholly concrete determination is spirit, has been brought about. That principle of mode and alteration does indeed not exclude unity altogether; for, just as in Spinozism mode as such is the untrue and only substance the true, and everything is to be led back to this, which then is a sinking of all content into emptiness, into merely formal, contentless unity, so too Siva is again the great whole, undifferentiated from Brahma, Brahma itself; i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"80.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0008","text":"difference and determinacy merely disappear again, but are not preserved, not sublated, and unity is not brought back to concrete unity, division not to reconciliation. The highest goal for the human being transported into the sphere of coming-to-be and passing-away, of modality in general, is immersion in unconsciousness, unity with Brahma, annihilation; the same is Buddhist Nirvana, Nieban, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"80.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0009","text":"Now if mode in general is abstract externality, indifference toward qualitative as toward quantitative determinations, and if what is external and inessential is not supposed to matter in essence, it is nevertheless again conceded in many matters that everything depends upon the manner and mode; mode is thereby itself declared to belong essentially to the substantial element of a thing; in which very indeterminate relation there lies at least this, that this externality is not so abstractly externality.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"80.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0010","text":"Here mode has the determinate significance of being Measure. The Spinozistic mode, like the Indian principle of alteration, is the measureless. The Greek, still indeterminate consciousness that everything has a measure, so that even Parmenides, after abstract Being, introduced necessity as the ancient limit set to everything, is the beginning of a far higher concept than substance, and contains the difference of mode from it.—The more developed, more reflective Measure is necessity; fate, Nemesis, confines itself in general to the determinacy of Measure, namely that what presumes too much, makes itself too great, too high, is reduced to the other extreme of degradation to nothingness, and thereby the middle of Measure, mediocrity, is restored.—The Absolute, God, is the measure of all things, is no more pantheistic than the definition:","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"80.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0011","text":"the Absolute, God, is Being, but infinitely truer.—Measure is indeed an external manner and mode, a more or less, which, however, is at the same time equally reflected into itself, not merely indifferent and external but determinate being that is in itself; it is thus the concrete truth of Being; in Measure the peoples have therefore venerated something inviolable, sacred.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"80.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0012","text":"The idea of essence already lies in Measure, namely, in being identical with itself in the immediacy of being-determined, so that that immediacy is reduced, through this identity-with-self, to something mediated, just as this identity is likewise mediated only through this externality, but is mediation with itself;—reflection, whose determinations they are, but in this Being are absolutely only moments of their negative unity. In Measure the qualitative is quantitative; determinacy or difference is indifferent, and is thereby a difference that is no difference; it is sublated; this quantitative character, as return into itself, wherein it is the qualitative, constitutes being-in-and-for-itself, which is essence. But Measure is essence only in itself, or in the concept; this concept of Measure is not yet posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"80.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0013","text":"Measure, still as such, is itself the being unity of the qualitative and quantitative; its moments are as an existence, a quality and quanta thereof, which are as yet inseparable only in themselves, but do not yet have the significance of this reflected determination. The development of Measure contains the distinction of these moments, but at the same time their relation, so that the identity which they are in themselves becomes their relation to one another, i.e. is posited. The significance of this development is the realization of Measure, in which it enters into relation to itself, and thereby at the same time posits itself as a moment; through this mediation it is determined as sublated; its immediacy, as also that of its moments, disappears, they are as reflected; thus, having emerged as what it is according to its concept, it has passed over into essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"80.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0014","text":"Measure is initially immediate unity of the qualitative and quantitative, so that","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"80.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0015","text":"firstly, there is a quantum which has qualitative significance and is Measure. Its further determination is that in it, the determinate-in-itself,—the difference of its moments, of qualitative and quantitative being-determined, emerges. These moments further determine themselves as wholes of Measure, which are in so far self-subsistent; since they essentially relate to one another, Measure becomes","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"80.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0016","text":"secondly, a ratio of specific quanta, as self-subsistent Measures. But their self-subsistence rests essentially at the same time upon the quantitative ratio and the difference in magnitude; thus their self-subsistence becomes a passing over into one another. Measure thereby founders in the measureless.—But this beyond of Measure is its negativity only in itself; it is thereby","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"80.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0017","text":"thirdly, the indifference of the determinations of Measure, and Measure is posited as real with the negativity contained in it, as an inverted ratio of Measures, which, as self-subsistent qualities, essentially rest only upon their quantity and upon their negative relation to one another, and thereby prove themselves to be only moments of their truly self-subsistent unity, which is their reflection-into-self and the positing of the same, essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"80.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0018","text":"The development of Measure, which has been attempted in what follows, is one of the most difficult matters; since it begins from immediate, external Measure, it would have, on the one hand, to proceed to the abstract further determination of the quantitative (a mathematics of nature), and, on the other hand, to indicate the connection of this determination of Measure with the qualities of natural things, at least in general; for the determinate demonstration of the connection of the qualitative and quantitative arising from the concept of the concrete object belongs to the special science of the concrete; examples of which, concerning the law of falling and that of free celestial motion, may be consulted in the Encyclopaedia of the Philosophical Sciences, 3rd ed., §§ 267 and 270 remarks.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"80.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0019","text":"In this connection it may generally be observed that the various forms in which Measure realizes itself also belong to different spheres of natural reality. The complete, abstract indifference of developed Measure, i.e. its laws, can have a place only in the sphere of mechanism, in which the concrete corporeal is only abstract matter itself; its qualitative differences essentially have the quantitative as their determinacy; space and time are the pure externalities themselves, and the quantity of matters, masses, intensity of weight, are likewise external determinations which have their peculiar determinacy in the quantitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"80.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0020","text":"By contrast, such determination of magnitude of the abstractly material is already disturbed by plurality, and thereby by a conflict of qualities, in the physical realm, and still more in the organic. But here not merely does the conflict of qualities as such arise; Measure is here subordinated to higher relations, and the immanent development of Measure is rather reduced to the simple form of immediate Measure. The members of the animal organism have a Measure which, as a simple quantum, stands in relation to other quanta of the other members; the proportions of the human body are fixed ratios of such quanta; natural science still has far to discern concerning the connection of such magnitudes with the organic functions, upon which they are wholly dependent.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"80.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0021","text":"But the nearest example of the reduction of an immanent Measure to a magnitude determined merely externally is motion. In the heavenly bodies it is free motion determined only by the concept, and its magnitudes thereby likewise depend only upon this concept (see above); but from the organic it is reduced to arbitrary or mechanically regular, i.e. in general abstract formal motion.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"80.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0022","text":"Still less, however, does a peculiar, free development of Measure have a place in the realm of spirit. One readily sees, for example, that a republican constitution, such as the Athenian, or an aristocratic one modified by democracy, can have a place only with a certain size of state; that, in developed civil society, the numbers of individuals belonging to the various trades stand in a relation to one another; but this yields neither laws of Measures nor peculiar forms of it. In the spiritual as such there occur differences in intensity of character, strength of imagination, of feelings, of representations, etc.; but the determination does not go beyond this indeterminate element of strength or weakness.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"80.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADM:P0023","text":"How insipid and utterly empty the so-called laws turn out to be that are propounded concerning the relation of strength and weakness of sensations, representations, etc., one will perceive when one consults the psychologies that concern themselves with such things.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"80.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADM:P0023"]}],"source_digest":"b4870b189b54f6879be468d7ae8e7481f28408bc53412b19811bd607c1dbb9cb","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Dritter Abschnitt. Das Maaß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Dritter Abschnitt. Das Maaß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0","title":"A. Specific Quantum.","order":81,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DSQ0","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Die specifische Quantität.\n\nDie qualitative Quantität ist zunächst ein unmittelbares specifisches Quantum; das\n\nzweitens, als sich zu Anderem verhaltend, ein quantitatives Specificiren, ein Aheben des gleichgültigen Quantums wird. Dieses Maaß, ist insofern eine Regel und enthält die beiden Momente des Maaßes unterschieden, nämlich die ansichseyende quantitative Bestimmtheit, und das äußerliche Quantum. In diesem Unterschiede werden aber diese beiden Seiten zu Qualitäten, und die Regel zu einem Verhältnisse derselben; das Maaß stellt sich daher dar\n\ndrittens als Verhältniß von Qualitäten, die zunächst Ein Maaß haben; das sich aber ferner so zu einem Unterschiede von Maaßen in sich specificirt.\n\n## A. Das specifische Quantum.\n\n1. Das Maaß ist die einfache Beziehung des Quantums auf sich, seine eigene Bestimmtheit an sich selbst; so ist das Quantum qualitativ. Zunächst ist es als unmittelbares Maaß, ein unmittelbares, daher als irgend ein bestimmtes, Quantum; ebenso unmittelbar ist die ihm zugehörige Qualität, sie ist irgend eine bestimmte Qualität.—Das Quantum als diese nicht mehr gleichgültige Grenze sondern auf sich beziehende Äußerlichkeit, ist so selbst die Qualität, und unterschieden von dieser geht es nich über sie hinaus, so wie diese nicht über dasselbe hinausgeht. Es ist in die einfache Gleichheit mit sich zurückgekehrte Bestimmtheit; eins mit dem bestimmten Daseyn, so wie dieses mit seinem Quantum.\n\nWenn man aus der erhaltenen Bestimmung einen Satz machen will, so kann man sich ausdrücken: Alles, was da ist, hat ein Maaß. Alles Daseyn hat eine Größe, und diese Größe gehört zur Natur von Etwas selbst; sie macht seine bestimmte Natur und sein Insichseyn aus. Etwas ist gegen diese Größe nicht gleichgültig, so daß wenn sie geändert würde, es bliebe was es ist, sondern die Änderung derselben änderte seine Qualität. Das Quantum hat als Maaß aufgehört Grenze zu seyn, die keine ist; es ist nunmehr die Bestimmung der Sache, so daß diese, über dieß Quantum vermehrt oder vermindert, zu Grunde ginge. —Ein Maaß, als Maaßstab im gewöhnlichen Sinne, ist ein Quantum, das als die an sich bestimmte Einheit gegen äußerliche Anzahl willkürlich angenommen wird. Eine solche Einheit kann zwar auch in der That an sich bestimmte Einheit seyn, wie Fuß und dergleichen ursprüngliche Maaße; insofern sie aber als Maaßstab zugleich für andere Dinge gebraucht wird, ist sie für diese nur äußerliches, nicht ihr ursprüngliches Maaß.—So mag der Erddurchmesser, oder die Pendellänge, als specifisches Quantum für sich genommen werden. Aber es ist willkürlich, den wievielsten Theil des Erddurchmessers oder der Pendellänge und unter welchem Breitengrade man diese nehmen wolle, um sie als Maaßstab zu gebrauchen. Noch mehr aber ist für andere Dinge ein solcher Maaßstab etwas Äußerliches. Diese haben das allgemeine specifische Quantum wieder auf besondere Art specificirt, und sind dadurch zu besondern Dingen gemacht. Es ist daher thöricht, von einem natürlichen Maaßstab der Dinge zu sprechen. Ohnehin soll ein allgemeiner Maaßstab nur für die äußerliche Vergleichung dienen; in diesem oberflächlichsten Sinne, in welchem er als allgemeines Maaß genommen wird, ist es völlig gleichgültig, was dafür gebraucht wird. Es soll nicht ein Grundmaaß in dem Sinne seyn, daß die Naturmaaße der besondern Dinge daran dargestellt und daraus nach einer Regel, als Specifikationen Eines allgemeinen Maaßes, des Maaßes ihres allgemeinen Körpers, erkannt würden. Ohne diesen Sinn aber hat ein absoluter Maaßstab nur das Interesse und die Bedeutung eines Gemeinschaftlichen, und ein solches ist nicht an sich, sondern durch Übereinkommen ein Allgemeines.\n\nDas unmittelbare Maaß ist eine einfache Größenbestimmung; wie z.B. die Größe der organischen Wesen, ihrer Gliedmaßen und so fort. Aber jedes Existirende hat eine Größe, um das zu seyn, was es ist, und überhaupt um Daseyn zu haben.—Als Quantum ist es gleichgültige Größe, äußerlicher Bestimmung offen und des Auf- und Abgehens am Mehr und Weniger fähig. Aber als Maaß ist es zugleich von sich selbst als Quantum, als solcher gleichgültiger Bestimmung, verschieden und eine Beschränkung jenes gleichgültigen Hin- und Hergehens an einer Grenze.\n\nIndem die Quantitätsbestimmtheit so an dem Daseyn die gedoppelte ist, das eine Mal die, an welche die Qualität gebunden ist, das andere Mal aber die, an der unbeschadet jener hin- und hergegangen werden kann, so geschieht das Untergehen von Etwas, das ein Maaß hat, darin daß sein Quantum verändert wird. Dieß Untergehen erscheint eines Theils als unerwartet, insofern an dem Quantum, ohne das Maaß und die Qualität zu verändern, geändert werden kann, andern Theils aber wird es zu einem als ganz Begreiflichen gemacht, nämlich durch die Allmähligkeit. Zu dieser Kategorie wird so leicht gegriffen, um das Vergehen von einer Qualität oder von Etwas vorstellig zu machen oder zu erklären, indem man so dem Verschwinden beinahe mit den Augen zusehen zu können scheint, weil das Quantum die als äußerliche, ihrer Natur nach veränderliche Grenze gesetzt ist, hiermit die Veränderung, als nur des Quantums, sich von selbst versteht. In der That aber wird nichts dadurch erklärt; die Veränderung ist zugleich wesentlich der Übergang einer Qualität in eine andere, oder der abstraktere von einem Daseyn in ein Nichtdaseyn; darin liegt eine andere Bestimmung als in der Allmähligkeit, welche nur eine Verminderung oder Vermehrung, und das einseitige Festhalten an der Größe ist.\n\n2. Daß aber eine als bloß quantitativ erscheinende Veränderung auch in eine qualitative umschlägt, auf diesen Zusammenhang sind schon die Alten aufmerksam gewesen, und haben die der Unkenntniß desselben entstehenden Kollisionen in populären Beispielen vorgestellt; unter den Namen des Kahlen, des Haufens sind hierher gehörige Elenchen bekannt, d. i. nach des Aristoteles Erklärung, Weisen, wodurch man genöthigt wird, das Gegentheil von dem zu sagen, was man vorher behauptet hatte. Man fragte: macht das Ausraufen Eines Haares vom Kopfe oder einem Pferdeschweife kam, oder hört ein Haufe auf ein Haufe zu seyn, wenn ein Korn weggenommen wird. Dieß kann man unbedenklich zugeben, indem solche Wegnahme nur einen und zwar selbst ganz unbedeutenden quantitativen Unterschied ausmacht; so wird Ein Haar, Ein Korn weggenommen, und dieß so wiederholt, daß jedesmal nach dem, was zugegeben worden, nur Eines weggenommen wird; zuletzt zeigt sich die qualitative Veränderung, daß der Kopf, der Schweiff kahl, der Haufe verschwunden ist. Man vergaß bei jenem Zugeben nicht nur die Wiederhohlung, sondern daß sich die für sich unbedeutenden Quantitäten (wie die für sich unbedeutenden Ausgaben von einem Vermögen) summiren, und die Summe das qualitativ Ganze ausmacht, so daß am Ende dieses verschwunden, der Kopf kahl, der Beutel leer ist.\n\nDie Verlegenheit, der Widerspruch, welcher als Resultat herauskommt, ist nicht etwas Sophistisches im gebräuchlichen Sinne des Worts, als ob solcher Widerspruch eine falsche Vorspiegelung wäre. Das Falsche ist, was der angenommene Andere, d. h. unser gewöhnliches Bewußtseyn begeht, eine Quantität nur für eine gleichgültige Grenze d. h. sie eben im bestimmten Sinne einer Quantität zu nehmen. Diese Annahme wird durch die Wahrheit, zu der sie geführt wird, Moment des Maaßes zu seyn und mit der Qualität zusammenzuhängen, konfondirt; was widerlegt wird, ist das einseitige Festhalten an der abstrakten Quantumsbestimmtheit.—Jene Wendungen sind darum auch kein leerer oder pedantischer Spaß, sondern in sich richtig und Erzeugnisse eines Bewußtseyns, das ein Interesse an den Erscheinungen hat, die im Denken vorkommen.\n\nDas Quantum, indem es als eine gleichgültige Grenze genommen wird, ist die Seite, an der ein Daseyn unverdächtig angegriffen und zu Grunde gerichtet wird. Es ist die List des Begriffes ein Daseyn an dieser Seite zu fassen, von der seine Qualität nicht ins Spiel zu kommen scheint,—und zwar so sehr', daß die Vergrößerung eines Staats, eines Vermögens u.s.f. welche das Unglück des Staats, des Besitzers herbeiführt, sogar als dessen Glück zunächst erscheint.\n\n3. Das Maaß ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit eine gewöhnliche Qualität von einer bestimmten ihr zugehörigen Größe. Von der Seite nun, nach welcher das Quantum gleichgültige Grenze ist, an der ohne die Qualität zu ändern hin- und hergegangen werden kann, ist seine andere Seite, nach welcher es qualitativ, specifisch ist, auch unterschieden. Beides sind Größebestimmungen Eines und desselben; aber nach der Unmittelbarkeit, in der zuerst das Maaß ist, ist ferner dieser Unterschied als ein unmittelbarer zu nehmen, beide Seiten haben hiernach auch eine verschiedene Existenz. Die Existenz des Maaßes, welche die an sich bestimmte Größe ist, ist dann in ihrem Verhalten zu der Existenz der veränderlichen, äußerlichen Seite, ein Aufheben ihrer Gleichgültigkeit, ein Specificiren desselben.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0001","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Die specifische Quantität.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"81.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0002","text":"Die qualitative Quantität ist zunächst ein unmittelbares specifisches Quantum; das","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"81.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0003","text":"zweitens, als sich zu Anderem verhaltend, ein quantitatives Specificiren, ein Aheben des gleichgültigen Quantums wird. Dieses Maaß, ist insofern eine Regel und enthält die beiden Momente des Maaßes unterschieden, nämlich die ansichseyende quantitative Bestimmtheit, und das äußerliche Quantum. In diesem Unterschiede werden aber diese beiden Seiten zu Qualitäten, und die Regel zu einem Verhältnisse derselben; das Maaß stellt sich daher dar","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"81.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0004","text":"drittens als Verhältniß von Qualitäten, die zunächst Ein Maaß haben; das sich aber ferner so zu einem Unterschiede von Maaßen in sich specificirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"81.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0005","text":"## A. Das specifische Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"81.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0006","text":"1. Das Maaß ist die einfache Beziehung des Quantums auf sich, seine eigene Bestimmtheit an sich selbst; so ist das Quantum qualitativ. Zunächst ist es als unmittelbares Maaß, ein unmittelbares, daher als irgend ein bestimmtes, Quantum; ebenso unmittelbar ist die ihm zugehörige Qualität, sie ist irgend eine bestimmte Qualität.—Das Quantum als diese nicht mehr gleichgültige Grenze sondern auf sich beziehende Äußerlichkeit, ist so selbst die Qualität, und unterschieden von dieser geht es nich über sie hinaus, so wie diese nicht über dasselbe hinausgeht. Es ist in die einfache Gleichheit mit sich zurückgekehrte Bestimmtheit; eins mit dem bestimmten Daseyn, so wie dieses mit seinem Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"81.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0007","text":"Wenn man aus der erhaltenen Bestimmung einen Satz machen will, so kann man sich ausdrücken: Alles, was da ist, hat ein Maaß. Alles Daseyn hat eine Größe, und diese Größe gehört zur Natur von Etwas selbst; sie macht seine bestimmte Natur und sein Insichseyn aus. Etwas ist gegen diese Größe nicht gleichgültig, so daß wenn sie geändert würde, es bliebe was es ist, sondern die Änderung derselben änderte seine Qualität. Das Quantum hat als Maaß aufgehört Grenze zu seyn, die keine ist; es ist nunmehr die Bestimmung der Sache, so daß diese, über dieß Quantum vermehrt oder vermindert, zu Grunde ginge. —Ein Maaß, als Maaßstab im gewöhnlichen Sinne, ist ein Quantum, das als die an sich bestimmte Einheit gegen äußerliche Anzahl willkürlich angenommen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"81.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0008","text":"Eine solche Einheit kann zwar auch in der That an sich bestimmte Einheit seyn, wie Fuß und dergleichen ursprüngliche Maaße; insofern sie aber als Maaßstab zugleich für andere Dinge gebraucht wird, ist sie für diese nur äußerliches, nicht ihr ursprüngliches Maaß.—So mag der Erddurchmesser, oder die Pendellänge, als specifisches Quantum für sich genommen werden. Aber es ist willkürlich, den wievielsten Theil des Erddurchmessers oder der Pendellänge und unter welchem Breitengrade man diese nehmen wolle, um sie als Maaßstab zu gebrauchen. Noch mehr aber ist für andere Dinge ein solcher Maaßstab etwas Äußerliches. Diese haben das allgemeine specifische Quantum wieder auf besondere Art specificirt, und sind dadurch zu besondern Dingen gemacht. Es ist daher thöricht, von einem natürlichen Maaßstab der Dinge zu sprechen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"81.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0009","text":"Ohnehin soll ein allgemeiner Maaßstab nur für die äußerliche Vergleichung dienen; in diesem oberflächlichsten Sinne, in welchem er als allgemeines Maaß genommen wird, ist es völlig gleichgültig, was dafür gebraucht wird. Es soll nicht ein Grundmaaß in dem Sinne seyn, daß die Naturmaaße der besondern Dinge daran dargestellt und daraus nach einer Regel, als Specifikationen Eines allgemeinen Maaßes, des Maaßes ihres allgemeinen Körpers, erkannt würden. Ohne diesen Sinn aber hat ein absoluter Maaßstab nur das Interesse und die Bedeutung eines Gemeinschaftlichen, und ein solches ist nicht an sich, sondern durch Übereinkommen ein Allgemeines.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"81.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0010","text":"Das unmittelbare Maaß ist eine einfache Größenbestimmung; wie z.B. die Größe der organischen Wesen, ihrer Gliedmaßen und so fort. Aber jedes Existirende hat eine Größe, um das zu seyn, was es ist, und überhaupt um Daseyn zu haben.—Als Quantum ist es gleichgültige Größe, äußerlicher Bestimmung offen und des Auf- und Abgehens am Mehr und Weniger fähig. Aber als Maaß ist es zugleich von sich selbst als Quantum, als solcher gleichgültiger Bestimmung, verschieden und eine Beschränkung jenes gleichgültigen Hin- und Hergehens an einer Grenze.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"81.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0011","text":"Indem die Quantitätsbestimmtheit so an dem Daseyn die gedoppelte ist, das eine Mal die, an welche die Qualität gebunden ist, das andere Mal aber die, an der unbeschadet jener hin- und hergegangen werden kann, so geschieht das Untergehen von Etwas, das ein Maaß hat, darin daß sein Quantum verändert wird. Dieß Untergehen erscheint eines Theils als unerwartet, insofern an dem Quantum, ohne das Maaß und die Qualität zu verändern, geändert werden kann, andern Theils aber wird es zu einem als ganz Begreiflichen gemacht, nämlich durch die Allmähligkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"81.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0012","text":"Zu dieser Kategorie wird so leicht gegriffen, um das Vergehen von einer Qualität oder von Etwas vorstellig zu machen oder zu erklären, indem man so dem Verschwinden beinahe mit den Augen zusehen zu können scheint, weil das Quantum die als äußerliche, ihrer Natur nach veränderliche Grenze gesetzt ist, hiermit die Veränderung, als nur des Quantums, sich von selbst versteht. In der That aber wird nichts dadurch erklärt; die Veränderung ist zugleich wesentlich der Übergang einer Qualität in eine andere, oder der abstraktere von einem Daseyn in ein Nichtdaseyn; darin liegt eine andere Bestimmung als in der Allmähligkeit, welche nur eine Verminderung oder Vermehrung, und das einseitige Festhalten an der Größe ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"81.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0013","text":"2. Daß aber eine als bloß quantitativ erscheinende Veränderung auch in eine qualitative umschlägt, auf diesen Zusammenhang sind schon die Alten aufmerksam gewesen, und haben die der Unkenntniß desselben entstehenden Kollisionen in populären Beispielen vorgestellt; unter den Namen des Kahlen, des Haufens sind hierher gehörige Elenchen bekannt, d. i. nach des Aristoteles Erklärung, Weisen, wodurch man genöthigt wird, das Gegentheil von dem zu sagen, was man vorher behauptet hatte. Man fragte: macht das Ausraufen Eines Haares vom Kopfe oder einem Pferdeschweife kam, oder hört ein Haufe auf ein Haufe zu seyn, wenn ein Korn weggenommen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"81.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0014","text":"Dieß kann man unbedenklich zugeben, indem solche Wegnahme nur einen und zwar selbst ganz unbedeutenden quantitativen Unterschied ausmacht; so wird Ein Haar, Ein Korn weggenommen, und dieß so wiederholt, daß jedesmal nach dem, was zugegeben worden, nur Eines weggenommen wird; zuletzt zeigt sich die qualitative Veränderung, daß der Kopf, der Schweiff kahl, der Haufe verschwunden ist. Man vergaß bei jenem Zugeben nicht nur die Wiederhohlung, sondern daß sich die für sich unbedeutenden Quantitäten (wie die für sich unbedeutenden Ausgaben von einem Vermögen) summiren, und die Summe das qualitativ Ganze ausmacht, so daß am Ende dieses verschwunden, der Kopf kahl, der Beutel leer ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"81.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0015","text":"Die Verlegenheit, der Widerspruch, welcher als Resultat herauskommt, ist nicht etwas Sophistisches im gebräuchlichen Sinne des Worts, als ob solcher Widerspruch eine falsche Vorspiegelung wäre. Das Falsche ist, was der angenommene Andere, d. h. unser gewöhnliches Bewußtseyn begeht, eine Quantität nur für eine gleichgültige Grenze d. h. sie eben im bestimmten Sinne einer Quantität zu nehmen. Diese Annahme wird durch die Wahrheit, zu der sie geführt wird, Moment des Maaßes zu seyn und mit der Qualität zusammenzuhängen, konfondirt; was widerlegt wird, ist das einseitige Festhalten an der abstrakten Quantumsbestimmtheit.—Jene Wendungen sind darum auch kein leerer oder pedantischer Spaß, sondern in sich richtig und Erzeugnisse eines Bewußtseyns, das ein Interesse an den Erscheinungen hat, die im Denken vorkommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"81.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0016","text":"Das Quantum, indem es als eine gleichgültige Grenze genommen wird, ist die Seite, an der ein Daseyn unverdächtig angegriffen und zu Grunde gerichtet wird. Es ist die List des Begriffes ein Daseyn an dieser Seite zu fassen, von der seine Qualität nicht ins Spiel zu kommen scheint,—und zwar so sehr', daß die Vergrößerung eines Staats, eines Vermögens u.s.f. welche das Unglück des Staats, des Besitzers herbeiführt, sogar als dessen Glück zunächst erscheint.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"81.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0017","text":"3. Das Maaß ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit eine gewöhnliche Qualität von einer bestimmten ihr zugehörigen Größe. Von der Seite nun, nach welcher das Quantum gleichgültige Grenze ist, an der ohne die Qualität zu ändern hin- und hergegangen werden kann, ist seine andere Seite, nach welcher es qualitativ, specifisch ist, auch unterschieden. Beides sind Größebestimmungen Eines und desselben; aber nach der Unmittelbarkeit, in der zuerst das Maaß ist, ist ferner dieser Unterschied als ein unmittelbarer zu nehmen, beide Seiten haben hiernach auch eine verschiedene Existenz. Die Existenz des Maaßes, welche die an sich bestimmte Größe ist, ist dann in ihrem Verhalten zu der Existenz der veränderlichen, äußerlichen Seite, ein Aufheben ihrer Gleichgültigkeit, ein Specificiren desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"81.17"}],"sha256":"6d15fea5e922d31fed83fa464e758dad07885f8479619ed709f8187c15950a6b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104107092536Z_81aeb71e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Specific Quantum.","source_sha256":"6d15fea5e922d31fed83fa464e758dad07885f8479619ed709f8187c15950a6b","sha256":"ff95d9b93758323588f6c809cc4f06f1fe2300cef1185ff75117a7529baa31fe","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:07.092589+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0001","text":"## First Chapter. The specific Quantity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"81.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0002","text":"Qualitative quantity is, at first, an immediate specific quantum; it","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"81.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0003","text":"secondly, as relating to an other, becomes a quantitative specifying, a sublation of indifferent quantum. This measure is, in so far, a rule and contains the two moments of measure as distinguished, namely the quantitative determinacy which is in itself, and the external quantum. In this distinction, however, these two sides become qualities, and the rule becomes a relation of them; measure therefore presents itself","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"81.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0004","text":"thirdly as a relation of qualities, which at first have One measure; but which further specifies itself into a distinction of measures within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"81.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0005","text":"## A. The specific Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"81.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0006","text":"1. Measure is the simple relation of quantum to itself, its own determinacy within itself; thus quantum is qualitative. At first, as immediate measure, it is an immediate, hence some determinate, quantum; equally immediate is the quality belonging to it, it is some determinate quality.—Quantum, as this no longer indifferent limit but self-relating externality, is thus itself quality, and, distinguished from this, does not go beyond it, just as this does not go beyond the former. It is determinacy returned into simple equality with itself; one with determinate being, just as this is with its quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"81.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0007","text":"If one wishes to make a proposition out of the determination obtained, one may express oneself thus: Everything that is has a measure. All determinate being has a magnitude, and this magnitude belongs to the nature of Something itself; it constitutes its determinate nature and its being-within-itself. Something is not indifferent to this magnitude, so that, if it were altered, it would remain what it is; rather, its alteration would alter its quality. As measure, quantum has ceased to be a limit that is no limit; it is now the determination of the thing, so that this, increased or diminished beyond this quantum, would perish. —A measure, as a standard in the ordinary sense, is a quantum arbitrarily assumed, as the unit determined in itself, in relation to external number.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"81.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0008","text":"Such a unit can indeed in fact also be a unit determined in itself, such as the foot and similar original measures; but insofar as it is at the same time used as a standard for other things, it is for these merely external, not their original measure.—Thus the diameter of the earth, or the length of the pendulum, may be taken as a specific quantum for itself. But it is arbitrary which part of the earth's diameter or of the pendulum's length, and under which degree of latitude, one wishes to take in order to use it as a standard. Still more, however, is such a standard something external for other things. These have again specified the universal specific quantum in a particular manner and have thereby been made into particular things. It is therefore foolish to speak of a natural standard of things.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"81.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0009","text":"In any case, a universal standard is supposed to serve only for external comparison; in this most superficial sense, in which it is taken as a universal measure, it is wholly indifferent what is used for it. It is not supposed to be a fundamental measure in the sense that the natural measures of particular things would be represented in it and recognized from it according to a rule, as specifications of One universal measure, the measure of their universal body. But without this sense, an absolute standard has only the interest and significance of something common, and such a thing is universal not in itself, but by agreement.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"81.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0010","text":"Immediate measure is a simple determination of magnitude; for example, the magnitude of organic beings, of their limbs, and so forth. But everything existing has a magnitude in order to be what it is, and in general in order to have determinate being.—As quantum, it is an indifferent magnitude, open to external determination and capable of increase and decrease in more and less. But as measure, it is at the same time distinct from itself as quantum, as such indifferent determination, and is a restriction of that indifferent movement to and fro at a limit.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"81.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0011","text":"Since the determinacy of quantity in determinate being is thus twofold, being on the one occasion that to which quality is bound, but on the other that within which one can move to and fro without prejudice to the former, the perishing of Something which has a measure takes place in this, that its quantum is altered. This perishing appears, on the one hand, as unexpected, insofar as quantum can be altered without altering measure and quality; on the other hand, however, it is made into something quite comprehensible, namely through gradualness.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"81.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0012","text":"This category is so readily resorted to in order to render imaginable or explain the passing away of a quality or of Something, since one seems thereby almost able to watch the disappearance with one's eyes; for quantum is the limit posited as external and, by its nature, mutable, and thus alteration, as merely that of quantum, is self-explanatory. In fact, however, nothing is thereby explained; alteration is at the same time essentially the transition of one quality into another, or, more abstractly, of a determinate being into a non-being; therein lies a different determination than in gradualness, which is only a diminution or increase, and the one-sided adherence to magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"81.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0013","text":"2. But that an alteration appearing as merely quantitative also turns into a qualitative one, the ancients had already drawn attention to this connection, and they presented in popular examples the collisions arising from ignorance of it; under the names of the Bald Man and the Heap, elenchi belonging here are known, i.e., according to Aristotle's explanation, modes through which one is compelled to say the opposite of what one had previously asserted. One asked: does plucking one hair from a head or a horse's tail make it bald, or does a heap cease to be a heap if one grain is removed?","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"81.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0014","text":"This may be conceded without hesitation, since such removal constitutes only one, and indeed itself quite insignificant, quantitative difference; thus one hair, one grain is removed, and this is repeated in such a way that each time, according to what has been conceded, only one is removed; finally the qualitative alteration shows itself: the head, the tail is bald, the heap has disappeared. In that concession one forgot not only repetition, but that quantities insignificant in themselves (like expenditures insignificant in themselves from a fortune) add up, and that the sum constitutes the qualitative whole, so that in the end this has disappeared, the head is bald, the purse empty.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"81.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0015","text":"The embarrassment, the contradiction which emerges as a result, is not something sophistical in the customary sense of the word, as though such contradiction were a false appearance. The falsehood is what the assumed other, i.e. our ordinary consciousness, commits: taking a quantity merely for an indifferent limit, i.e. taking it precisely in the determinate sense of a quantity. This assumption is confounded by the truth to which it is led, namely, to be a moment of measure and connected with quality; what is refuted is the one-sided adherence to the abstract determination of quantum.—Those turns are therefore also no empty or pedantic jest, but correct in themselves and products of a consciousness that has an interest in the appearances which occur in thinking.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"81.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0016","text":"Quantum, insofar as it is taken as an indifferent limit, is the side on which a determinate being is unassailably attacked and ruined. It is the cunning of the Concept to seize a determinate being on this side, from which its quality does not seem to come into play,—indeed so much so that the enlargement of a state, of a fortune, etc., which brings about the misfortune of the state, of the owner, at first even appears as its happiness.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"81.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0017","text":"3. In its immediacy, measure is an ordinary quality with a determinate magnitude belonging to it. Now from the side according to which quantum is an indifferent limit, within which one can move to and fro without altering the quality, its other side too, according to which it is qualitative, specific, is distinguished. Both are determinations of magnitude of one and the same thing; but according to the immediacy in which measure is at first, this distinction is further to be taken as an immediate one; accordingly, both sides also have a different existence. The existence of measure, which is magnitude determined in itself, is then, in its relation to the existence of the mutable, external side, a sublation of its indifference, a specifying of the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"81.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSQ0:P0017"]}],"source_digest":"6c6a56e10aca5d932c78c51c5c65f65ce24653e85002a6644712e7826ae4900c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das specifische Quantum."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das specifische Quantum.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0","title":"B. Specifying Measure.","order":82,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BSM0","text":"Dasselbe ist\n\nerstlich eine Regel, ein Maaß äußerlich gegen das bloße Quantum;\n\nzweitens specifische Quantität, welche das äußerliche Quantum bestimmt;\n\ndrittens verhalten sich beide Seiten als Qualitäten von specifischer Quantitätsbestimmtheit gegeneinander, als Ein Maaß.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0001","text":"Dasselbe ist","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"82.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0002","text":"erstlich eine Regel, ein Maaß äußerlich gegen das bloße Quantum;","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"82.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0003","text":"zweitens specifische Quantität, welche das äußerliche Quantum bestimmt;","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"82.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0004","text":"drittens verhalten sich beide Seiten als Qualitäten von specifischer Quantitätsbestimmtheit gegeneinander, als Ein Maaß.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"82.4"}],"sha256":"45dd09690b2f08c430db1fc669ba2aa6140d17cbe534f3e6efce8a333debeeba","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104109130770Z_fa7f4edb","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Specifying Measure.","source_sha256":"45dd09690b2f08c430db1fc669ba2aa6140d17cbe534f3e6efce8a333debeeba","sha256":"cc05786eca58a1155f1a4ef4b3c62ba2dd63b183ba6da9cfea750875eea10b35","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:09.130815+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0001","text":"The same is","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"82.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0002","text":"firstly a rule, a measure externally in relation to mere quantum;","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"82.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0003","text":"secondly, specific quantity, which determines the external quantum;","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"82.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0004","text":"thirdly, both sides relate to each other as qualities of specific quantitative determinacy, as One Measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"82.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BSM0:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"727191f67321cac7fed47a86b3611bbe206826458034c0612b250b6f2f684894","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Specificirendes Maaß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Specificirendes Maaß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIER","title":"a. The Rule.","order":83,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DIER","text":"Die Regel oder der Maaßstab, von dem schon gesprochen worden, ist zunächst als eine an sich bestimmte Größe, welche Einheit gegen ein Quantum ist, das eine besondere Existenz ist, an einem andern Etwas, als das Etwas der Regel ist, existirt,—an ihr gemessen, d. i. als Anzahl jener Einheit bestimmt wird. Diese Vergleichung ist ein äußerliches Thun, jene Einheit selbst eine willkürliche Größe, die ebenso wieder als Anzahl (der Fuß als eine Anzahl von Zollen) gesetzt werden kann. Aber das Maaß ist nicht nur äußerliche Regel, sondern als specifisches ist es dieß, sich an sich selbst zu seinem Andern zu verhalten, das ein Quantum ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIER:P0001","text":"Die Regel oder der Maaßstab, von dem schon gesprochen worden, ist zunächst als eine an sich bestimmte Größe, welche Einheit gegen ein Quantum ist, das eine besondere Existenz ist, an einem andern Etwas, als das Etwas der Regel ist, existirt,—an ihr gemessen, d. i. als Anzahl jener Einheit bestimmt wird. Diese Vergleichung ist ein äußerliches Thun, jene Einheit selbst eine willkürliche Größe, die ebenso wieder als Anzahl (der Fuß als eine Anzahl von Zollen) gesetzt werden kann. Aber das Maaß ist nicht nur äußerliche Regel, sondern als specifisches ist es dieß, sich an sich selbst zu seinem Andern zu verhalten, das ein Quantum ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"83.1"}],"sha256":"ab3b74a14a84979097aaa6783c31147e632397b034c4be0ec3f965ae7437b37d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104111833691Z_d5ea6ac7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. The Rule.","source_sha256":"ab3b74a14a84979097aaa6783c31147e632397b034c4be0ec3f965ae7437b37d","sha256":"ce253896f3dcaeebb9542442dde6e764193fa1a8ba4cf0a5c559c2fec586195c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:11.833743+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIER:P0001","text":"The rule or standard, of which mention has already been made, is initially a magnitude determinate in itself, which, as a unit, exists in relation to a quantum that has a particular existence in some other Something than the Something of the rule,—is measured by it, i.e. is determined as a number of that unit. This comparison is an external activity; that unit itself is an arbitrary magnitude, which can likewise again be posited as a number (the foot as a number of inches). But measure is not merely an external rule; rather, as specific, it is this: to relate itself within itself to its other, which is a quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"83.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIER:P0001"]}],"source_digest":"b0a227b2b063e375eed862b3f5e65d8a890dc7487f2190fa4ac18dcec7c27756","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Die Regel."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Die Regel.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM","title":"b. Specifying Measure.","order":84,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDSM","text":"Das Maaß ist specifisches Bestimmen der äußerlichen Größe, d. i. der gleichgültigen, die nun voi einer andern Existenz überhaupt an dem Etwas des Maaßes gesetzt wird, welches zwar selbst Quantum, aber im Unterschiede von solchem das Qualitative, bestimmend das bloß gleichgültige, äußerliche Quantum, ist. Das Etwas hat diese Seite des Seyns-für-Anderes an ihm, der das gleichgültige Vermehrt- und Vermindertwerden, zukommt. Jenes immanente Messende ist eine Qualität des Etwas, dem dieselbe Qualität all einem andern Etwas gegenübersteht; aber an diesem zunächst relativ mit maaßlosem Quantum überhaupt gegen jene, die als messend bestimmt ist.\n\nAn Etwas, insofern es ein Maaß in sich ist, kommt äußerlich eine Veränderung der Größe seiner Qualität; es nimmt davon nicht die arithmetische Menge an. Sein Maaß reagirt dagegen, verhält sich als ein Intensives gegen die Menge, und nimmt sie auf eine eigenthümliche Weise auf; es verändert die äußerlich gesetzte Veränderung, macht aus diesem Quantum ein Anderes, und zeigt sich durch diese Specifikation als Fürsichseyn in dieser Äußerlichkeit.—Diese specifisch-aufgenommene Menge ist selbst ein Quantum, auch abhängig von der andern oder ihr als nur äußerlichen Menge. Die specificirte Menge ist daher auch veränderlich, aber darum nicht ein Quantum als solches, sondern das äußere Quantum als auf eine konstante Weise specificirt. Das Maaß hat so sein Daseyn als ein Verhältniß, und das Specifische desselben ist überhaupt der Exponent dieses Verhältnisses.\n\nIm intensiven und extensiven Quantum ist es, wie sich bei diesen Bestimmungen ergab, dasselbe Quantum, welches das einemal in der Form der Intensität, das anderemal in der Form der Extensität vorhanden ist. Das zu Grunde liegende Quantum erleidet in diesem Unterschiede keine Veränderung, dieser ist nur eine äußere Form. In dem specificirenden Maaße hingegen ist das Quantum das eine Mal in seiner unmittelbaren Größe, das andere Mal aber wird es durch den Verhältnisexponenten in einer andern Anzahl genommen.\n\nDer Exponent, der das Specifische ausmacht, kann zunächst ein fixes Quantum zu seyn scheinen, als Quotient des Verhältnisses zwischen dem äußerlichen und dem qualitativ bestimmten. Aber so wäre er nichts als ein äußerliches Quantum; es ist unter dem Exponenten hier nichts Anderes als das Moment des Qualitativen selbst zu verstehen, welches das Quantum als solches specificirt. Das eigentlich immanente Qualitative des Quantums ist, wie sich früher ergeben hat, nur die Potenz-Bestimmung. Eine solche muß es seyn, welche das Verhältniß konstituirt, und die hier als die an sich seyende Bestimmung dem Quantum als der äußerlichen Beschaffenheit gegenübergetreten ist. Dieses hat zu seinem Princip das numerische Eins, das dessen An-sich-Bestimmtseyn ausmacht; und die Beziehung des numerischen Eins ist die äußerliche und die nur durch die Natur des unmittelbaren Quantums als solchen bestimmte Veränderung besteht für sich in dem Hinzutreten eines solchen numerischen Eins und wieder eines solchen und so fort. Wenn so das äußerliche Quantum in arithmetischer Progression sich verändert, so bringt die specificirende Reaktion der qualitativen Natur des Maaßes eine andere Reihe hervor, welche sich auf die erste bezieht, init ihr zu- und abnimmt, aber nicht in einem durch einen Zahlexponenten bestimmten, sondern einer Zahl inkommensurabeln Verhältnisse, nach einer Potenzenbestimmung.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0001","text":"Das Maaß ist specifisches Bestimmen der äußerlichen Größe, d. i. der gleichgültigen, die nun voi einer andern Existenz überhaupt an dem Etwas des Maaßes gesetzt wird, welches zwar selbst Quantum, aber im Unterschiede von solchem das Qualitative, bestimmend das bloß gleichgültige, äußerliche Quantum, ist. Das Etwas hat diese Seite des Seyns-für-Anderes an ihm, der das gleichgültige Vermehrt- und Vermindertwerden, zukommt. Jenes immanente Messende ist eine Qualität des Etwas, dem dieselbe Qualität all einem andern Etwas gegenübersteht; aber an diesem zunächst relativ mit maaßlosem Quantum überhaupt gegen jene, die als messend bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"84.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0002","text":"An Etwas, insofern es ein Maaß in sich ist, kommt äußerlich eine Veränderung der Größe seiner Qualität; es nimmt davon nicht die arithmetische Menge an. Sein Maaß reagirt dagegen, verhält sich als ein Intensives gegen die Menge, und nimmt sie auf eine eigenthümliche Weise auf; es verändert die äußerlich gesetzte Veränderung, macht aus diesem Quantum ein Anderes, und zeigt sich durch diese Specifikation als Fürsichseyn in dieser Äußerlichkeit.—Diese specifisch-aufgenommene Menge ist selbst ein Quantum, auch abhängig von der andern oder ihr als nur äußerlichen Menge. Die specificirte Menge ist daher auch veränderlich, aber darum nicht ein Quantum als solches, sondern das äußere Quantum als auf eine konstante Weise specificirt. Das Maaß hat so sein Daseyn als ein Verhältniß, und das Specifische desselben ist überhaupt der Exponent dieses Verhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"84.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0003","text":"Im intensiven und extensiven Quantum ist es, wie sich bei diesen Bestimmungen ergab, dasselbe Quantum, welches das einemal in der Form der Intensität, das anderemal in der Form der Extensität vorhanden ist. Das zu Grunde liegende Quantum erleidet in diesem Unterschiede keine Veränderung, dieser ist nur eine äußere Form. In dem specificirenden Maaße hingegen ist das Quantum das eine Mal in seiner unmittelbaren Größe, das andere Mal aber wird es durch den Verhältnisexponenten in einer andern Anzahl genommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"84.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0004","text":"Der Exponent, der das Specifische ausmacht, kann zunächst ein fixes Quantum zu seyn scheinen, als Quotient des Verhältnisses zwischen dem äußerlichen und dem qualitativ bestimmten. Aber so wäre er nichts als ein äußerliches Quantum; es ist unter dem Exponenten hier nichts Anderes als das Moment des Qualitativen selbst zu verstehen, welches das Quantum als solches specificirt. Das eigentlich immanente Qualitative des Quantums ist, wie sich früher ergeben hat, nur die Potenz-Bestimmung. Eine solche muß es seyn, welche das Verhältniß konstituirt, und die hier als die an sich seyende Bestimmung dem Quantum als der äußerlichen Beschaffenheit gegenübergetreten ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"84.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0005","text":"Dieses hat zu seinem Princip das numerische Eins, das dessen An-sich-Bestimmtseyn ausmacht; und die Beziehung des numerischen Eins ist die äußerliche und die nur durch die Natur des unmittelbaren Quantums als solchen bestimmte Veränderung besteht für sich in dem Hinzutreten eines solchen numerischen Eins und wieder eines solchen und so fort. Wenn so das äußerliche Quantum in arithmetischer Progression sich verändert, so bringt die specificirende Reaktion der qualitativen Natur des Maaßes eine andere Reihe hervor, welche sich auf die erste bezieht, init ihr zu- und abnimmt, aber nicht in einem durch einen Zahlexponenten bestimmten, sondern einer Zahl inkommensurabeln Verhältnisse, nach einer Potenzenbestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"84.5"}],"sha256":"f0d8d86ad2ff7c481f04046b5b3770dc8cd2f117be729e91c9a49129b8fc37f0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104120441288Z_e3980a88","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Specifying Measure.","source_sha256":"f0d8d86ad2ff7c481f04046b5b3770dc8cd2f117be729e91c9a49129b8fc37f0","sha256":"ae0948c5363b6c0e623ae21c65fb445d4d64f2cc9751c5a7cfa8b21956652d79","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:20.441310+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0001","text":"Measure is the specific determination of external magnitude, i.e. of the indifferent [magnitude], which is now posited by an other existence in general upon the Something of Measure, which, although itself Quantum, is, in distinction from such, the qualitative, determining the merely indifferent, external Quantum. The Something has in it this side of Being-for-Other, to which indifferent increase and diminution belong. That immanent measuring is a quality of the Something, to which the same quality stands opposed in every other Something; but in this latter, initially relatively, with measureless Quantum in general, against that which is determined as measuring.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"84.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0002","text":"In a Something, insofar as it is a Measure within itself, an alteration of the magnitude of its quality occurs externally; it does not thereby assume the arithmetical amount. Its Measure reacts against this, behaves as an Intensive toward the amount, and takes it up in a peculiar way; it alters the externally posited alteration, makes this Quantum into an Other, and shows itself, through this specification, as Being-for-Self in this externality.—This specifically received amount is itself a Quantum, also dependent upon the other amount, or upon it as a merely external amount. The specified amount is therefore also variable, but for that reason not a Quantum as such, but the external Quantum as specified in a constant way. Measure thus has its determinate being as a relation, and what is specific to it is in general the exponent of this relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"84.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0003","text":"In intensive and extensive Quantum, as emerged in connection with these determinations, it is the same Quantum which is present on one occasion in the form of intensity, on the other in the form of extensity. The underlying Quantum undergoes no alteration in this difference; the latter is only an external form. In specifying Measure, by contrast, the Quantum is at one time in its immediate magnitude, but at another it is taken in a different number through the exponent of the relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"84.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0004","text":"The exponent, which constitutes the specific, may initially seem to be a fixed Quantum, as the quotient of the relation between the external and the qualitatively determined. But then it would be nothing but an external Quantum; by the exponent here nothing other is to be understood than the moment of the qualitative itself, which specifies Quantum as such. As has emerged earlier, what is properly immanent and qualitative in Quantum is only the determination of power. It must be such a determination that constitutes the relation, and that here has confronted Quantum, as the external constitution, as the determination that is in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"84.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0005","text":"This has as its principle the numerical one, which constitutes its determinacy-in-itself; and the relation of the numerical one is the external one, and the alteration determined solely by the nature of immediate Quantum as such subsists for itself in the addition of one such numerical one and again one such one, and so forth. Thus, when external Quantum alters itself in arithmetical progression, the specifying reaction of the qualitative nature of Measure produces another series, which is related to the first, increases and decreases with it, but not in a relation determined by a numerical exponent, but in a relation incommensurable with a number, according to a determination of powers.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"84.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSM:P0005"]}],"source_digest":"812fa4743cfa7b569279fdb54941f93bf0102cc0d6b6a7088f6dc78d059e6b20","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Das specificirende Maaß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Das specificirende Maaß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21","title":"Remark.","order":85,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_21","text":"Um ein Beispiel anzuführen, so ist die Temperatur eine Qualität, an der diese beiden Seiten, äußerliches und specificirtes Quantum zu seyn, sich unterscheiden. Als Quantum ist sie äußerliche Temperatur und zwar auch eines Körpers als allgemeinen Mediums, von der angenommen wird, daß ihre Veränderung an der Skale der arithmetischen Progression fortgehe und daß sie gleichförmig zuoder abnehme, wogegen sie von den verschiedenen in ihr befindlichen besondern Körpern verschieden aufgenommen wird, indem dieselben durch ihr immanentes Maaß die äußerlich empfangene Temperatur bestimmen, die Temperatur-Veränderung derselben nicht der des Mediums oder ihrer untereinander im direkten Verhältnisse entspricht. Verschiedene Körper in einer und derselben Temperatur verglichen, geben Verhältnißzahlen ihrer specifischen Wärmen, ihrer Wärme-Kapacitäten. Aber diese Kapacitäten der Körper ändern sich in verschiedenen Temperaturen, womit das Eintreten einer Veränderung der specifischen Gestalt sich verbindet. In der Vermehrung oder Verminderung der Temperatur zeigt sich somit eine besondere Specifikation. Das Verhältniß der Temperatur, die als äußerliche vorgestellt wird, zur Temperatur eines bestimmten Körpers, die zugleich von jener abhängig ist, hat nicht einen festen Verhältnissexponenten; die Vermehrung oder Verminderung dieser Wärme geht nicht gleichförmig mit der Zu- und Abnahme der äußerlichen fort.—Es wird hierbei eine Temperatur als äußerlich überhaupt angenommen, deren Veränderung bloß äußerlich oder rein quantitativ sey. Sie ist jedoch selbst Temperatur der Luft oder sonst specifische Temperatur. Näher betrachtet würde daher das Verhältniß eigentlich nicht als Verhältniß von einem bloß quantitativen zu einem qualificirenden, sondern von zwei specifischen Quantis zu nehmen seyn. Wie sich das specificirende Verhältniß gleich weiter bestimmen wird, daß die Momente des Maaßes nicht nur in einer quantitativen und einer das Quantum qualificirenden Seite einer und derselben Qualität bestehen, sondern im Verhältnisse zweier Qualitäten, welche an ihnen selbst Maaße sind.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21:P0001","text":"Um ein Beispiel anzuführen, so ist die Temperatur eine Qualität, an der diese beiden Seiten, äußerliches und specificirtes Quantum zu seyn, sich unterscheiden. Als Quantum ist sie äußerliche Temperatur und zwar auch eines Körpers als allgemeinen Mediums, von der angenommen wird, daß ihre Veränderung an der Skale der arithmetischen Progression fortgehe und daß sie gleichförmig zuoder abnehme, wogegen sie von den verschiedenen in ihr befindlichen besondern Körpern verschieden aufgenommen wird, indem dieselben durch ihr immanentes Maaß die äußerlich empfangene Temperatur bestimmen, die Temperatur-Veränderung derselben nicht der des Mediums oder ihrer untereinander im direkten Verhältnisse entspricht. Verschiedene Körper in einer und derselben Temperatur verglichen, geben Verhältnißzahlen ihrer specifischen Wärmen, ihrer Wärme-Kapacitäten.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"85.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21:P0002","text":"Aber diese Kapacitäten der Körper ändern sich in verschiedenen Temperaturen, womit das Eintreten einer Veränderung der specifischen Gestalt sich verbindet. In der Vermehrung oder Verminderung der Temperatur zeigt sich somit eine besondere Specifikation. Das Verhältniß der Temperatur, die als äußerliche vorgestellt wird, zur Temperatur eines bestimmten Körpers, die zugleich von jener abhängig ist, hat nicht einen festen Verhältnissexponenten; die Vermehrung oder Verminderung dieser Wärme geht nicht gleichförmig mit der Zu- und Abnahme der äußerlichen fort.—Es wird hierbei eine Temperatur als äußerlich überhaupt angenommen, deren Veränderung bloß äußerlich oder rein quantitativ sey. Sie ist jedoch selbst Temperatur der Luft oder sonst specifische Temperatur.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"85.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21:P0003","text":"Näher betrachtet würde daher das Verhältniß eigentlich nicht als Verhältniß von einem bloß quantitativen zu einem qualificirenden, sondern von zwei specifischen Quantis zu nehmen seyn. Wie sich das specificirende Verhältniß gleich weiter bestimmen wird, daß die Momente des Maaßes nicht nur in einer quantitativen und einer das Quantum qualificirenden Seite einer und derselben Qualität bestehen, sondern im Verhältnisse zweier Qualitäten, welche an ihnen selbst Maaße sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"85.3"}],"sha256":"c377a27aa79dc414057cddb343ebd1f22ec1f31f5e1d787ceabaa099c322a75e","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104125621137Z_b2ae195b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"c377a27aa79dc414057cddb343ebd1f22ec1f31f5e1d787ceabaa099c322a75e","sha256":"37e0e226361e414827cefd47e4882a416cc293fcfe691a8fc652a631839cc51c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:25.621156+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21:P0001","text":"To cite an example, temperature is a quality in which these two sides, being an external and a specified quantum, are distinct. As quantum, it is external temperature, indeed also that of a body as a universal medium, of which it is assumed that its alteration proceeds on the scale of arithmetic progression and that it increases or decreases uniformly; whereas it is received differently by the various particular bodies found within it, in that these determine, through their immanent measure, the externally received temperature, the alteration of whose temperature does not correspond directly to that of the medium or to that of the others among themselves. Different bodies compared at one and the same temperature yield ratios of their specific heats, their heat capacities.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"85.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_21:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21:P0002","text":"But these capacities of bodies alter at different temperatures, with which the occurrence of an alteration of specific shape is connected. Thus, in the increase or decrease of temperature, a particular specification manifests itself. The relation of temperature, which is represented as external, to the temperature of a determinate body, which is at the same time dependent on the former, does not have a fixed exponent of relation; the increase or decrease of this heat does not proceed uniformly with the increase and decrease of the external [temperature].—Here, a temperature is assumed as external in general, whose alteration is merely external or purely quantitative. Yet it is itself the temperature of the air or some other specific temperature.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"85.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_21:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_21:P0003","text":"Considered more closely, therefore, the relation would properly have to be taken not as the relation of a merely quantitative [term] to a qualifying [term], but of two specific quanta. As the specifying relation will shortly determine itself further, namely, such that the moments of measure consist not merely in a quantitative side and a side qualifying the quantum of one and the same quality, but in the relation of two qualities which are in themselves measures.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"85.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_21:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"3337e170a38012bd12be270c4a97470cda4c775026ffe62381b1360d596ff526","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB","title":"c. The Relation of Both Sides as Qualities.","order":86,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CVLB","text":"l. Die qualitative, an sich bestimmte Seite des Quantums ist nur als Beziehung auf das äußerlich Quantitative; als Specificiren desselben ist sie das Aufheben seiner Äußerlichkeit, durch welche das Quantum als solches ist; sie hat so dasselbe zu ihrer Voraussetzung und fängt von ihm an. Dieses aber ist von der Qualität selbst auch qualitativ unterschieden; dieser Unterschied beider ist in der Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns überhaupt, in welcher das Maaß noch ist, zu setzen, so sind beide Seiten qualitativ gegeneinander, und jede für sich ein solches Daseyn; und das eine zunächst nur als formelle, an ihm unbestimmte Quantum ist das Quantum eines Etwas und seiner Qualität, und wie sich deren Beziehung auf einander nun zum Maaße überhaupt bestimmt hat, gleichfalls die specifische Größe dieser Qualitäten. Diese Qualitäten sind nach der Maaßbestimmung im Verhältniß zu einander; diese ist ihr Exponent, sie sind aber an sich schon im Fürsichseyn des Maaßes aufeinander bezogen, das Quantum ist in seinem Doppelseyn als äußerliches und specifisches, so daß jede der unterschiedenen Quantitäten diese zweifache Bestimmung an ihr hat und zugleich schlechthin mit der andern verschränkt ist; eben darin allein sind die Qualitäten bestimmt. Sie sind so nicht nur für einander seyendes Daseyn überhaupt, sondern untrennbar gesetzt; und die an sie geknüpfte Größebestimmtheit ist eine qualitative Einheit,—Eine Maaßbestimmung, in der sie ihrem Begriffe nach, an sich zusammenhängen. Das Maaß ist so das immanente quantitative Verhalten zweier Qualitäten zu einander.\n\n2. Im Maaß tritt die wesentliche Bestimmung der veränderlichen Größe ein, denn es ist das Quantum als aufgehoben, also nicht mehr als das, was es seyn soll uni Quantum zu seyn, sondern als Quantum und zugleich als etwas Anderes; dieß Andere ist das Qualitative, und wie bestimmt worden, nichts anderes als das Potenzenverhältniß desselben. Im unmittelbaren Maaße ist diese Veränderung noch nicht gesetzt; es ist nur irgend und zwar ein einzelns Quantum überhaupt, an das eine Qualität geknüpft ist. Im Specificiren des Maaßes, der vorhergehenden Bestimmung, als einer Veränderung des bloß äußerlichen Quantums durch das Qualitative ist Unterschiedenheit beider Größebestimmtheiten und damit überhaupt die Mehrheit voll Maaßen an einem gemeinschaftlichen äußerlichen Quantum gesetzt; das Quantum zeigt sich erst als daseyendes Maaß in solcher Unterschiedenheit seiner von sich selbst, indem es, ein und dasselbe (z.B. dieselbe Temperatur des Mediums), zugleich als verschiedenes und zwar quantitatives Daseyn (—in den verschiedenen Temperaturen der in jenem befindlichen Körper) hervortritt. Diese Unterschiedenheit des Quantums in den verschiedenen Qualitäten—den verschiedenen Körpern, —giebt eine weitere, diejenige Form des Maaßes, in welcher beide Seiten als qualitativ bestimmte Quanta sich zu einander verhalten, was das realisirte Maaß genannt werden kann.\n\nDie Größe ist als eine Größe überhaupt veränderlich, denn ihre Bestimmtheit ist als eine Grenze, die zugleich keine ist; die Veränderung betrifft insofern nur ein besonderes Quantum, an dessen Stelle ein anderes gesetzt wird; die wahrhafte Veränderung aber ist die des Quantums als solchen; dieß giebt die, so gefaßt, interessante Bestimmung der veränderlichen Größe in der höhern Mathematik; wobei nicht bei dem Formellen der Veränderlichkeit überhaupt stehen zu bleiben, noch andere als die einfache Bestimmung des Begriffs herbeizunehmen ist, nach welcher das Andere des Quantums nur das Qualitative ist. Die wahrhafte Bestimmung also der reellen veränderlichen Größe ist, daß sie die qualitativ, hiermit, wie zur Genüge gezeigt worden, die durch ein Potenzenverhältniß bestimmte ist; in dieser veränderlichen Größe ist es gesetzt, daß das Quantum nicht als solches gilt, sondern nach seiner ihm andern Bestimmung, der qualitativen.\n\nDie Seiten dieses Verhaltens haben nach ihrer abstrakten Seite als Qualitäten überhaupt irgend eine besondere Bedeutung, z.B. Raum und Zeit. In ihrem Maaßverhältniß als Größebestimmtheiten zunächst überhaupt genommen, ist die eine davon Anzahl, die in äußerlicher, arithmetischer Progression auf- und abgeht, die andere eine Anzahl, die durch jene, welche Einheit für sie ist, specifisch bestimmt wird. Insofern jede ebenso nur eine besondere Qualität überhaupt wäre, läge kein Unterschied in ihnen, welche von den beiden, in Rücksicht auf ihre Größen-Bestimmung als die bloß äußerlich quantitative, und welche als die in quantitativer Specifikation sich verändernde genommen werde. Wenn sie sich z.B. als Wurzel und Quadrat verhalten, ist es gleichviel, an welcher die Vermehrung oder Verminderung als bloß äußerlich, in arithmetischer Progression fortgehend, und welche dagegen an diesem Quantum sich specifisch bestimmend angesehen wird.\n\nAber die Qualitäten sind nicht unbestimmt verschieden gegen einander, denn in ihnen soll als Momenten des Maaßes die Qualifikation desselben liegen. Die nächste Bestimmtheit der Qualitäten selbst ist, der einen, das Extensive, die Äußerlichkeit an ihr selbst zu seyn, der andern, das Intensive, das Insichseyende oder Negative gegen jene. Von den quantitativen Momenten kommt hiernach jener die Anzahl, dieser die Einheit zu, im einfachen direkten Verhältnisse ist jene als der Dividend, diese als Divisor, im specificirenden Verhältniß jene als die Potenz oder das Anderswerden, diese als Wurzel zu nehmen. Insofern hier noch gezählt, d. i. auf das äußerliche Quantum, (das so als die ganz zufällige, empirischgenannte Größebestimmtheit ist) reflektirt, hiermit die Veränderung gleichfalls auch als in äußerlicher, arithmetischer Progression fortgehend genommen wird, so fällt dieß auf die Seite der Einheit, der intensiven Qualität, die äußerliche, extensive Seite hingegen ist als in der specificirten Reihe sich verändernd darzustellen. Aber das direkte Verhältniß (wie die Geschwindigkeit überhaupt, s/t) ist hier zur formellen, nicht existirenden, sondern nur der abstrahirenden Reflexion angehörigen Bestimmung herabgesetzt; und wenn noch im Verhältniß von Wurzel und Quadrat (wie in s = at[hoch 2]) die Wurzel als empirisches Quantum und in arithmetischer Progression fortgehend, die andere Seite aber als specificirt zu nehmen ist, so ist die höhere dem Begriffe entsprechendere Realisation der Qualifikation des Quantitativen diese, daß beide Seiten in höhern Potenzenbestimmungen (wie s[hoch 3] = at[hoch 2] der Fall ist) sich verhalten.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0001","text":"l. Die qualitative, an sich bestimmte Seite des Quantums ist nur als Beziehung auf das äußerlich Quantitative; als Specificiren desselben ist sie das Aufheben seiner Äußerlichkeit, durch welche das Quantum als solches ist; sie hat so dasselbe zu ihrer Voraussetzung und fängt von ihm an. Dieses aber ist von der Qualität selbst auch qualitativ unterschieden; dieser Unterschied beider ist in der Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns überhaupt, in welcher das Maaß noch ist, zu setzen, so sind beide Seiten qualitativ gegeneinander, und jede für sich ein solches Daseyn; und das eine zunächst nur als formelle, an ihm unbestimmte Quantum ist das Quantum eines Etwas und seiner Qualität, und wie sich deren Beziehung auf einander nun zum Maaße überhaupt bestimmt hat, gleichfalls die specifische Größe dieser Qualitäten.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"86.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0002","text":"Diese Qualitäten sind nach der Maaßbestimmung im Verhältniß zu einander; diese ist ihr Exponent, sie sind aber an sich schon im Fürsichseyn des Maaßes aufeinander bezogen, das Quantum ist in seinem Doppelseyn als äußerliches und specifisches, so daß jede der unterschiedenen Quantitäten diese zweifache Bestimmung an ihr hat und zugleich schlechthin mit der andern verschränkt ist; eben darin allein sind die Qualitäten bestimmt. Sie sind so nicht nur für einander seyendes Daseyn überhaupt, sondern untrennbar gesetzt; und die an sie geknüpfte Größebestimmtheit ist eine qualitative Einheit,—Eine Maaßbestimmung, in der sie ihrem Begriffe nach, an sich zusammenhängen. Das Maaß ist so das immanente quantitative Verhalten zweier Qualitäten zu einander.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"86.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0003","text":"2. Im Maaß tritt die wesentliche Bestimmung der veränderlichen Größe ein, denn es ist das Quantum als aufgehoben, also nicht mehr als das, was es seyn soll uni Quantum zu seyn, sondern als Quantum und zugleich als etwas Anderes; dieß Andere ist das Qualitative, und wie bestimmt worden, nichts anderes als das Potenzenverhältniß desselben. Im unmittelbaren Maaße ist diese Veränderung noch nicht gesetzt; es ist nur irgend und zwar ein einzelns Quantum überhaupt, an das eine Qualität geknüpft ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"86.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0004","text":"Im Specificiren des Maaßes, der vorhergehenden Bestimmung, als einer Veränderung des bloß äußerlichen Quantums durch das Qualitative ist Unterschiedenheit beider Größebestimmtheiten und damit überhaupt die Mehrheit voll Maaßen an einem gemeinschaftlichen äußerlichen Quantum gesetzt; das Quantum zeigt sich erst als daseyendes Maaß in solcher Unterschiedenheit seiner von sich selbst, indem es, ein und dasselbe (z.B. dieselbe Temperatur des Mediums), zugleich als verschiedenes und zwar quantitatives Daseyn (—in den verschiedenen Temperaturen der in jenem befindlichen Körper) hervortritt. Diese Unterschiedenheit des Quantums in den verschiedenen Qualitäten—den verschiedenen Körpern, —giebt eine weitere, diejenige Form des Maaßes, in welcher beide Seiten als qualitativ bestimmte Quanta sich zu einander verhalten, was das realisirte Maaß genannt werden kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"86.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0005","text":"Die Größe ist als eine Größe überhaupt veränderlich, denn ihre Bestimmtheit ist als eine Grenze, die zugleich keine ist; die Veränderung betrifft insofern nur ein besonderes Quantum, an dessen Stelle ein anderes gesetzt wird; die wahrhafte Veränderung aber ist die des Quantums als solchen; dieß giebt die, so gefaßt, interessante Bestimmung der veränderlichen Größe in der höhern Mathematik; wobei nicht bei dem Formellen der Veränderlichkeit überhaupt stehen zu bleiben, noch andere als die einfache Bestimmung des Begriffs herbeizunehmen ist, nach welcher das Andere des Quantums nur das Qualitative ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"86.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0006","text":"Die wahrhafte Bestimmung also der reellen veränderlichen Größe ist, daß sie die qualitativ, hiermit, wie zur Genüge gezeigt worden, die durch ein Potenzenverhältniß bestimmte ist; in dieser veränderlichen Größe ist es gesetzt, daß das Quantum nicht als solches gilt, sondern nach seiner ihm andern Bestimmung, der qualitativen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"86.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0007","text":"Die Seiten dieses Verhaltens haben nach ihrer abstrakten Seite als Qualitäten überhaupt irgend eine besondere Bedeutung, z.B. Raum und Zeit. In ihrem Maaßverhältniß als Größebestimmtheiten zunächst überhaupt genommen, ist die eine davon Anzahl, die in äußerlicher, arithmetischer Progression auf- und abgeht, die andere eine Anzahl, die durch jene, welche Einheit für sie ist, specifisch bestimmt wird. Insofern jede ebenso nur eine besondere Qualität überhaupt wäre, läge kein Unterschied in ihnen, welche von den beiden, in Rücksicht auf ihre Größen-Bestimmung als die bloß äußerlich quantitative, und welche als die in quantitativer Specifikation sich verändernde genommen werde. Wenn sie sich z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"86.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0008","text":"als Wurzel und Quadrat verhalten, ist es gleichviel, an welcher die Vermehrung oder Verminderung als bloß äußerlich, in arithmetischer Progression fortgehend, und welche dagegen an diesem Quantum sich specifisch bestimmend angesehen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"86.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0009","text":"Aber die Qualitäten sind nicht unbestimmt verschieden gegen einander, denn in ihnen soll als Momenten des Maaßes die Qualifikation desselben liegen. Die nächste Bestimmtheit der Qualitäten selbst ist, der einen, das Extensive, die Äußerlichkeit an ihr selbst zu seyn, der andern, das Intensive, das Insichseyende oder Negative gegen jene. Von den quantitativen Momenten kommt hiernach jener die Anzahl, dieser die Einheit zu, im einfachen direkten Verhältnisse ist jene als der Dividend, diese als Divisor, im specificirenden Verhältniß jene als die Potenz oder das Anderswerden, diese als Wurzel zu nehmen. Insofern hier noch gezählt, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"86.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0010","text":"auf das äußerliche Quantum, (das so als die ganz zufällige, empirischgenannte Größebestimmtheit ist) reflektirt, hiermit die Veränderung gleichfalls auch als in äußerlicher, arithmetischer Progression fortgehend genommen wird, so fällt dieß auf die Seite der Einheit, der intensiven Qualität, die äußerliche, extensive Seite hingegen ist als in der specificirten Reihe sich verändernd darzustellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"86.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0011","text":"Aber das direkte Verhältniß (wie die Geschwindigkeit überhaupt, s/t) ist hier zur formellen, nicht existirenden, sondern nur der abstrahirenden Reflexion angehörigen Bestimmung herabgesetzt; und wenn noch im Verhältniß von Wurzel und Quadrat (wie in s = at[hoch 2]) die Wurzel als empirisches Quantum und in arithmetischer Progression fortgehend, die andere Seite aber als specificirt zu nehmen ist, so ist die höhere dem Begriffe entsprechendere Realisation der Qualifikation des Quantitativen diese, daß beide Seiten in höhern Potenzenbestimmungen (wie s[hoch 3] = at[hoch 2] der Fall ist) sich verhalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"86.11"}],"sha256":"36b21823ca0463094aa9a9eb9366c3366d883767baec0a50246a5f6255775012","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104140078720Z_981b4158","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Relation of Both Sides as Qualities.","source_sha256":"36b21823ca0463094aa9a9eb9366c3366d883767baec0a50246a5f6255775012","sha256":"9f098a82803f9c458e19053559b3fb15b5c741c1741251a9715f5483674e8211","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:40.078755+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0001","text":"1. The qualitative side of quantum, determined in itself, is only as a relation to the externally quantitative; as the specification of the latter it is the sublation of its externality, through which quantum is as such; it thus has the same as its presupposition and begins from it. But this is itself qualitatively distinct from quality; this distinction of the two is, in the immediacy of Being in general, in which measure still is, to be posited, so that both sides are qualitative over against one another, and each is for itself such a determinate being; and the one, initially only as formal quantum, indeterminate in it, is the quantum of a something and of its quality, and, as their relation to one another has now determined itself into measure in general, likewise the specific magnitude of these qualities.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"86.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0002","text":"According to the determination of measure, these qualities are in relation to one another; this is their exponent; but they are already related to one another in themselves in the being-for-self of measure; quantum is in its dual being as external and specific, so that each of the distinct quantities has this twofold determination in it and at the same time is absolutely intertwined with the other; it is solely thereby that the qualities are determined. Thus they are not merely determinate being existing for one another in general, but are posited as inseparable; and the determinacy of magnitude linked to them is a qualitative unity,—one determination of measure, in which they cohere according to their concept, in themselves. Measure is thus the immanent quantitative relation of two qualities to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"86.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0003","text":"2. In measure there enters the essential determination of variable magnitude, for it is quantum as sublated, hence no longer as that which it is supposed to be in order to be quantum, but as quantum and at the same time as something other; this other is the qualitative, and, as has been determined, nothing other than its relation of powers. In immediate measure this alteration is not yet posited; it is merely some—and indeed a single—quantum in general, to which a quality is linked.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"86.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0004","text":"In the specification of measure, the preceding determination, as an alteration of merely external quantum by the qualitative, the distinctness of the two determinacies of magnitude, and therewith in general a plurality of measures in one common external quantum, is posited; quantum first shows itself as existent measure in such distinctness of itself from itself, in that it, being one and the same (e.g. the same temperature of the medium), at the same time emerges as a different, namely quantitative, determinate being (—in the different temperatures of the bodies contained in it). This distinctness of quantum in the different qualities—the different bodies—yields a further form of measure, that in which both sides relate to one another as qualitatively determined quanta, which may be called realized measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"86.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0005","text":"Magnitude, as magnitude in general, is variable, for its determinacy is as a limit which at the same time is not one; alteration therefore concerns only a particular quantum, in whose place another is posited; but the true alteration is that of quantum as such; this yields the, thus conceived, interesting determination of variable magnitude in higher mathematics; in which one must neither remain with the formal aspect of variability in general, nor introduce determinations other than the simple determination of the concept, according to which the other of quantum is only the qualitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"86.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0006","text":"The true determination, therefore, of real variable magnitude is that it is the qualitatively, and hence, as has been sufficiently shown, the magnitude determined by a relation of powers; in this variable magnitude it is posited that quantum does not count as such, but according to its other determination, the qualitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"86.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0007","text":"The sides of this relation, according to their abstract aspect as qualities in general, have some particular significance, e.g. space and time. In their relation of measure, taken initially in general as determinacies of magnitude, one of them is number, which increases and decreases in external, arithmetical progression; the other is a number which is specifically determined through the former, which is its unit. Insofar as each would likewise be only a particular quality in general, there would lie no distinction in them as to which of the two, with respect to their determination of magnitude, is taken as the merely externally quantitative, and which as changing in quantitative specification. If they, for example,","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"86.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0008","text":"relate as root and square, it is immaterial in which the increase or diminution is viewed as merely external, proceeding in arithmetical progression, and which, on the other hand, as determining itself specifically in this quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"86.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0009","text":"But the qualities are not indeterminately different from one another, for the qualification of measure is supposed to lie in them as moments of measure. The proximate determinacy of the qualities themselves is that one is the extensive, externality in itself, the other the intensive, the being-in-self or negative over against the former. Accordingly, of the quantitative moments, number belongs to the former, unit to the latter; in the simple direct relation, the former is to be taken as the dividend, the latter as divisor; in the specifying relation, the former as power or becoming-other, the latter as root. Insofar as counting still takes place here, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"86.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0010","text":"reflection is made upon external quantum (which is thus the wholly contingent, so-called empirical determinacy of magnitude), and hence alteration is likewise taken as proceeding in external, arithmetical progression, this falls on the side of unit, of intensive quality; the external, extensive side, on the other hand, is to be presented as changing in the specified series.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"86.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0011","text":"But the direct relation (such as velocity in general, s/t) is here reduced to a formal, non-existing determination, belonging only to abstracting reflection; and if, even in the relation of root and square (as in s = at[squared]), the root is to be taken as empirical quantum and as proceeding in arithmetical progression, but the other side as specified, then the higher realization of the qualification of the quantitative, more consonant with the concept, is this: that both sides stand in higher determinations of powers (as is the case in s[cubed] = at[squared]).","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"86.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLB:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"59a78f2cf6316cd6a763101baa075ff633c5370ee96ec78ce45a7dfe266d3632","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Verhältniß beider Seiten als Qualitäten."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Verhältniß beider Seiten als Qualitäten.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22","title":"Remark.","order":87,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_22","text":"Das hier Erörterte in Rücksicht des Zusammenhangs der qualitativen Natur eines Daseyns und seiner Quantitätsbestimmung im Maaße, hat seine Anwendung in dem schon angedeuteten Beispiel der Bewegung, zunächst daß in der Geschwindigkeit, als dem direkten Verhältnisse von durchlaufenem Raume und verflossener Zeit, die Größe der Zeit als Nenner, die Größe des Raums dagegen als Zähler, angenommen wird. Wenn Geschwindigkeit überhaupt nur ein Verhältniß vom Raum und der Zeit einer Bewegung ist, so ist es gleichgültig, welches von beiden Momenten als die Anzahl oder als die Einheit betrachtet werden soll. Aber Raum, wie in der specifischen Schwere das Gewicht, ist äußerliches, reales Ganzes überhaupt, somit Anzahl, die Zeit hingegen, wie das Volumen, ist das Ideelle, das Negative, die Seite der Einheit.—Wesentlich aber gehört hierher das wichtigere Verhältniß, daß in der freien Bewegung,—zuerst der noch bedingten—, des Falls, Zeitund Raum-Quantität, jene als Wurzel, diese als Quadrat,—oder in der absolutfreien Bewegung der Himmelskörper die Umlaufszeit und die Entfernung, jene um eine Potenz tiefer als diese,—jene als Quadrat, diese als Kubus gegen einander bestimmt seyen. Dergleichen Grundverhältnisse beruhen auf der Natur der im Verhältniß stehenden Qualitäten, des Raums und der Zeit, und der Art der Beziehung, in welcher sie stehen, entweder als mechanische Bewegung d. i. als unfreie, durch den Begriff der Momente nicht bestimmte, oder als Fall d. i. bedingtfreie, oder als absolutfreie himmlische Bewegung;— welche Arten der Bewegung ebensowohl als deren Gesetze auf der Entwicklung des Begriffs ihrer Momente, des Raums und der Zeit, beruhen, indem diese Qualitäten als solche, an sich d. i. im Begriffe sich als untrennbar erweisen, und ihr quantitatives Verhältniß das Fürsichseyn des Maaßes, nur Eine Maaßbestimmung ist.\n\nIn Rücksicht auf die absoluten Maaßverhältnisse darf wohl erinnert werden, daß die Mathematik der Natur, wenn sie des Namens von Wissenschaft würdig seyn will, wesentlich die Wissenschaft der Maaße seyn müsse,—eine Wissenschaft für welche empirisch wohl viel, aber eigentlich wissenschaftlich d. i. philosophisch, noch wenig gethan ist. Mathematische Principien der Naturphilosophie,—wie Newton sein Werk genannt hat,—wenn sie diese Bestimmung in einem tiefern Sinn erfüllen sollten, als er und das ganze bakonische Geschlecht von Philosophie und Wissenschaft hatte, müßten ganz andere Dinge enthalten, um ein Licht in diese noch dunkeln aber höchst betrachtungswürdigen Regionen zu bringen.—Es ist ein großes Verdienst, die empirischen Zahlen der Natur kennen zu lernen, z.B. Entfernungen der Planeten von einander; aber ein unendlich größeres, die empirischen Quanta verschwinden zu machen, und sie in eine allgemeine Form von Quantitätsbestimmungen zu erheben, so daß sie Momente eines Gesetzes oder Maaßes werden;—unsterbliche Verdienste, die sich z.B. Galilei in Rücksicht auf den Fall, und Keppler in Rücksicht auf die Bewegung der himmlischen Körper erworben hat. Sie haben die Gesetze, die sie gefunden haben, so erwiesen, daß sie gezeigt haben, daß ihnen der Umfang der Einzelnheiten der Wahrnehmung entspricht. Es muß aber noch ein höheres Beweisen dieser Gesetze gefordert werden; nämlich nichts anders als daß ihre Quantitätsbestimmungen aus den Qualitäten, oder bestimmten Begriffen, die bezogen sind, (wie Zeit und Raum) erkannt werden. Von dieser Art des Beweisens findet sich in jenen mathematischen Principien der Naturphilosophie, so wie in den fernern Arbeiten dieser Art, noch keine Spur. Es ist oben bei Gelegenheit des Scheins mathematischer Beweise von Naturverhältnissen, der sich auf den Mißbrauch des Unendlichkleinen gründet, bemerkt worden, daß der Versuch, solche Beweise eigentlich mathematisch d. h. weder aus der Empirie noch aus dem Begriffe, zu führen, ein widersinniges Unternehmen ist. Diese Beweise setzen ihre Theoreme, eben jene Gesetze, aus der Erfahrung voraus; was sie leisten, besteht darin, sie auf abstrakte Ausdrücke und bequeme Formeln zu bringen. Das ganze reelle Verdienst, das Newton im Vorzug gegen Keppler in Beziehung auf die nämlichen Gegenstände zugeschrieben wird, wird, das Scheingerüste von Beweisen abgezogen,—ohne Zweifel bei gereinigterer Reflexion über das, was die Mathematik zu leisten vermag und was sie geleistet hat, einst mit deutlicher Kenntniß auf jene Umformung des Ausdrucks [14] und der den Anfängen nach eingeführten analytischen Behandlung, eingeschränkt werden.\n\n[14] S Encyklop. der philos. Wissensch. Anm. zu §. 270. über die Umformung des kepplerischen s[hoch 3]/t[hoch 2] in [s[hoch 2]./t[hoch 2] in das newtonische, indem der Theil s/t[hoch 2] die Kraft der Schwere genannt worden ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0001","text":"Das hier Erörterte in Rücksicht des Zusammenhangs der qualitativen Natur eines Daseyns und seiner Quantitätsbestimmung im Maaße, hat seine Anwendung in dem schon angedeuteten Beispiel der Bewegung, zunächst daß in der Geschwindigkeit, als dem direkten Verhältnisse von durchlaufenem Raume und verflossener Zeit, die Größe der Zeit als Nenner, die Größe des Raums dagegen als Zähler, angenommen wird. Wenn Geschwindigkeit überhaupt nur ein Verhältniß vom Raum und der Zeit einer Bewegung ist, so ist es gleichgültig, welches von beiden Momenten als die Anzahl oder als die Einheit betrachtet werden soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"87.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0002","text":"Aber Raum, wie in der specifischen Schwere das Gewicht, ist äußerliches, reales Ganzes überhaupt, somit Anzahl, die Zeit hingegen, wie das Volumen, ist das Ideelle, das Negative, die Seite der Einheit.—Wesentlich aber gehört hierher das wichtigere Verhältniß, daß in der freien Bewegung,—zuerst der noch bedingten—, des Falls, Zeitund Raum-Quantität, jene als Wurzel, diese als Quadrat,—oder in der absolutfreien Bewegung der Himmelskörper die Umlaufszeit und die Entfernung, jene um eine Potenz tiefer als diese,—jene als Quadrat, diese als Kubus gegen einander bestimmt seyen. Dergleichen Grundverhältnisse beruhen auf der Natur der im Verhältniß stehenden Qualitäten, des Raums und der Zeit, und der Art der Beziehung, in welcher sie stehen, entweder als mechanische Bewegung d. i. als unfreie, durch den Begriff der Momente nicht bestimmte, oder als Fall d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"87.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0003","text":"bedingtfreie, oder als absolutfreie himmlische Bewegung;— welche Arten der Bewegung ebensowohl als deren Gesetze auf der Entwicklung des Begriffs ihrer Momente, des Raums und der Zeit, beruhen, indem diese Qualitäten als solche, an sich d. i. im Begriffe sich als untrennbar erweisen, und ihr quantitatives Verhältniß das Fürsichseyn des Maaßes, nur Eine Maaßbestimmung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"87.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0004","text":"In Rücksicht auf die absoluten Maaßverhältnisse darf wohl erinnert werden, daß die Mathematik der Natur, wenn sie des Namens von Wissenschaft würdig seyn will, wesentlich die Wissenschaft der Maaße seyn müsse,—eine Wissenschaft für welche empirisch wohl viel, aber eigentlich wissenschaftlich d. i. philosophisch, noch wenig gethan ist. Mathematische Principien der Naturphilosophie,—wie Newton sein Werk genannt hat,—wenn sie diese Bestimmung in einem tiefern Sinn erfüllen sollten, als er und das ganze bakonische Geschlecht von Philosophie und Wissenschaft hatte, müßten ganz andere Dinge enthalten, um ein Licht in diese noch dunkeln aber höchst betrachtungswürdigen Regionen zu bringen.—Es ist ein großes Verdienst, die empirischen Zahlen der Natur kennen zu lernen, z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"87.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0005","text":"Entfernungen der Planeten von einander; aber ein unendlich größeres, die empirischen Quanta verschwinden zu machen, und sie in eine allgemeine Form von Quantitätsbestimmungen zu erheben, so daß sie Momente eines Gesetzes oder Maaßes werden;—unsterbliche Verdienste, die sich z.B. Galilei in Rücksicht auf den Fall, und Keppler in Rücksicht auf die Bewegung der himmlischen Körper erworben hat. Sie haben die Gesetze, die sie gefunden haben, so erwiesen, daß sie gezeigt haben, daß ihnen der Umfang der Einzelnheiten der Wahrnehmung entspricht. Es muß aber noch ein höheres Beweisen dieser Gesetze gefordert werden; nämlich nichts anders als daß ihre Quantitätsbestimmungen aus den Qualitäten, oder bestimmten Begriffen, die bezogen sind, (wie Zeit und Raum) erkannt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"87.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0006","text":"Von dieser Art des Beweisens findet sich in jenen mathematischen Principien der Naturphilosophie, so wie in den fernern Arbeiten dieser Art, noch keine Spur. Es ist oben bei Gelegenheit des Scheins mathematischer Beweise von Naturverhältnissen, der sich auf den Mißbrauch des Unendlichkleinen gründet, bemerkt worden, daß der Versuch, solche Beweise eigentlich mathematisch d. h. weder aus der Empirie noch aus dem Begriffe, zu führen, ein widersinniges Unternehmen ist. Diese Beweise setzen ihre Theoreme, eben jene Gesetze, aus der Erfahrung voraus; was sie leisten, besteht darin, sie auf abstrakte Ausdrücke und bequeme Formeln zu bringen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"87.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0007","text":"Das ganze reelle Verdienst, das Newton im Vorzug gegen Keppler in Beziehung auf die nämlichen Gegenstände zugeschrieben wird, wird, das Scheingerüste von Beweisen abgezogen,—ohne Zweifel bei gereinigterer Reflexion über das, was die Mathematik zu leisten vermag und was sie geleistet hat, einst mit deutlicher Kenntniß auf jene Umformung des Ausdrucks [14] und der den Anfängen nach eingeführten analytischen Behandlung, eingeschränkt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"87.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0008","text":"[14] S Encyklop. der philos. Wissensch. Anm. zu §. 270. über die Umformung des kepplerischen s[hoch 3]/t[hoch 2] in [s[hoch 2]./t[hoch 2] in das newtonische, indem der Theil s/t[hoch 2] die Kraft der Schwere genannt worden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"87.8"}],"sha256":"ee91880f2ce61fea12da2576232dbf36ce62f56eca9c5b29d8959dab5b38016f","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104152455503Z_6625569f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"ee91880f2ce61fea12da2576232dbf36ce62f56eca9c5b29d8959dab5b38016f","sha256":"3b0ae5f75b909fa1444cf253f8d0248cbce42dcdee166f5f9b473cf5e265e81a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:41:52.455518+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0001","text":"What has here been discussed with respect to the connection of the qualitative nature of an existence and its quantitative determination in measure has its application in the example of motion already indicated, first of all in that, in velocity, as the direct ratio of distance traversed and time elapsed, the magnitude of time is assumed as denominator, but the magnitude of space as numerator. If velocity in general is only a ratio of the space and time of a motion, it is indifferent which of the two moments is to be regarded as the number or as the unit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"87.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0002","text":"But space, like weight in specific gravity, is external, real whole in general, hence number; time, on the other hand, like volume, is the ideal, the negative, the side of unity.—Essentially, however, the more important relation belongs here, that in free motion,—first in the still conditioned—, that of falling, time-quantity and space-quantity, the former as root, the latter as square,—or in the absolutely free motion of the heavenly bodies, the period of revolution and the distance, the former one power lower than the latter,—the former as square, the latter as cube, are determined in relation to one another. Such fundamental relations rest upon the nature of the qualities standing in relation, space and time, and upon the manner of relation in which they stand, either as mechanical motion, i.e. as unfree, not determined by the concept of the moments, or as falling, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"87.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0003","text":"conditioned-free, or as absolutely free celestial motion;—which kinds of motion, as much as their laws, rest upon the development of the concept of their moments, space and time, since these qualities as such, in themselves, i.e. in the concept, prove to be inseparable, and their quantitative relation is the being-for-self of measure, only one determination of measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"87.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0004","text":"With regard to the absolute relations of measure, it may well be recalled that the mathematics of nature, if it is to be worthy of the name of science, must essentially be the science of measures,—a science for which empirically much has indeed been done, but, properly scientifically, i.e. philosophically, still little. Mathematical Principles of Natural Philosophy,—as Newton called his work,—if they were to fulfil this determination in a deeper sense than he and the entire Baconian race of philosophy and science possessed, would have to contain quite different things in order to bring a light into these still dark but highly worthy regions of consideration.—It is a great merit to become acquainted with the empirical numbers of nature, e.g.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"87.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0005","text":"the distances of the planets from one another; but an infinitely greater one to make the empirical quanta disappear and to elevate them into a general form of quantitative determinations, so that they become moments of a law or measure;—immortal merits, which, for example, Galileo with respect to falling, and Kepler with respect to the motion of the heavenly bodies, have acquired. They have demonstrated the laws which they found in such a way that they showed that the compass of the individual details of perception corresponds to them. But a still higher demonstration of these laws must be demanded; namely, none other than that their quantitative determinations be cognized from the qualities, or determinate concepts, which are related (such as time and space).","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"87.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0006","text":"Of this kind of demonstration there is as yet no trace in those Mathematical Principles of Natural Philosophy, any more than in the subsequent works of this kind. Above, on the occasion of the semblance of mathematical proofs of relations of nature, which is founded on the misuse of the infinitesimal, it was remarked that the attempt to conduct such proofs properly mathematically, i.e. neither from empiricism nor from the concept, is an absurd undertaking. These proofs presuppose their theorems, precisely those laws, from experience; what they accomplish consists in bringing them into abstract expressions and convenient formulae.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"87.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0007","text":"The whole real merit attributed to Newton in preference to Kepler in relation to the same objects will, once the illusory scaffolding of proofs has been removed,—without doubt, with a more purified reflection upon what mathematics is capable of accomplishing and what it has accomplished, one day, with clear knowledge, be restricted to that transformation of expression [14] and to the analytical treatment introduced in its beginnings.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"87.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_22:P0008","text":"[14] See Encyclopaedia of the Philosophical Sciences, note to § 270, on the transformation of the Keplerian s[superscript 3]/t[superscript 2] into [s[superscript 2]./t[superscript 2] into the Newtonian, in that the part s/t[superscript 2] has been called the force of gravity.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"87.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_22:P0008"]}],"source_digest":"994a56ce1e8ad5eb713692565648e2b17b7a065d6e187dfedeefa176d90fce77","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR","title":"C. Being-for-Self in Measure.","order":88,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDFR","text":"1. In der so eben betrachteten Form des specificirten Maaßes ist das Quantitative beider Seiten qualitativ bestimmt, (beide im Potenzen-Verhältniß); sie sind so Momente Einer Maaßbestimmtheit von qualitativer Natur. Dabei sind aber die Qualitäten nur erst noch als unmittelbare, nur verschiedene gesetzt, die nicht selbst in jenem Verhältnisse stehen, in welchem ihre Größebestimmtheiten sind, nämlich außer solchem Verhältnisse, keinen Sinn noch Daseyn zu haben, was die Potenzenbestimmtheit der Größe enthält. Das Qualitative verhüllt sich so, als nicht sich selbst, sondern die Größebestimmtheit specificirend; nur als an dieser ist es gesetzt, für sich aber unmittelbare Qualität als solche, die außerhalb dessen, daß die Größe von ihr in Differenz gesetzt wird, und außer ihrer Beziehung auf ihre andere, noch für sich bestehendes Daseyn habe. So Raum und Zeit gelten beide außer jener Specifikation, die ihre Größebestimmtheit in der Bewegung des Falles oder in der absolutfreien Bewegung erhält, als Raum überhaupt, Zeit überhaupt, der Raum bestehend für sich außer und ohne die Zeit als dauernd, und die Zeit als für sich fließend unabhängig vom Raume.\n\nDiese Unmittelbarkeit des Qualitativen gegen seine specifische Maaßbeziehung ist aber ebenso sehr mit einer quantitativen Unmittelbarkeit und der Gleichgültigkeit eines Quantitativen an ihm gegen dieß sein Verhältniß verknüpft; die unmittelbare Qualität hat auch ein nur unmittelbares Quantum. Daher hat denn das specifische Maaß auch eine Seite zunächst äußerlicher Veränderung, deren Fortgang bloß arithmetisch ist, von jenem nicht gestört wird, und in welche die äußerliche, darum nur empirische Größebestimmtheit fällt. Qualität und Quantum auch so außer dem specifischen Maaße auftretend, sind zugleich in der Beziehung auf dieses; die Unmittelbarkeit ist ein Moment von solchen, die selbst zum Maaße gehören. So sind die unmittelbaren Qualitäten dem Maaße auch angehörig, gleichfalls in Beziehung, und stehen nach der Größebestimmtheit in einem Verhältniß, welches als außerhalb des specificirten, der Potenzbestimmung, selbst nur das direkte Verhältniß, und unmittelbares Maaß ist. Diese Folgerung und deren Zusammenhang ist näher anzugeben.\n\n2. Das unmittelbar bestimmte Quantum als solches ist, wenn es auch als Maaßmoment sonst an sich in einem Begriffszusammenhang begründet ist, in der Beziehung zu dem specifischen Maaße als ein äußerlich gegebenes. Die Unmittelbarkeit, die hiermit gesetzt ist, ist aber die Negation der qualitativen Maaßbestimmung; dieselbe wurde vorhin an den Seiten dieser Maaßbestimmung aufgezeigt, welche darum als selbstständige Qualitäten erschienen. Solche Negation und das Zurückkehren zur unmittelbaren Quantitätsbestimmtheit liegt in dem qualitativbestimmten Verhältnisse insofern, als das Verhältniß Unterschiedener überhaupt deren Beziehung als Eine Bestimmtheit enthält, die hiermit hier im Quantitativen, unterschieden von der Verhältnißbestimmung, ein Quantum ist. Als Negation der unterschiedenen qualitativbestimmten Seiten ist dieser Exponent ein Fürsichseyn, das Schlechthin-bestimmtseyn; aber ist solches Fürsichseyn nur an sich; als Daseyn ein einfaches, unmittelbares Quantum, Quotient oder Exponent als eines Verhältnisses der Seiten des Maaßes, dieß Verhältniß als ein direktes genommen; aber überhaupt die als empirisch erscheinende Einheit in dem Quantitativen des Maaßes.—Im Falle der Körper stehen die durchloffenen Räume im Verhältnisse des Quadrats der verflossenen Zeiten; s = at[hoch 2]; —dieß ist das specifisch-bestimmte, ein Potenzenverhälntiß des Raums und der Zeit, das andere, das direkte Verhältniß, käme dem Raum und der Zeit, als gegeneinander gleichgültigen Qualitäten, zu, es soll das des Raumes zu dem ersten Zeitmomente seyn, derselbe Koefficient, a, bleibt in allen folgenden Zeitpunkten;—die Einheit als ein gewöhnlichts Quantum fur die übrigens durch das specificirende Maaß bestimmte Anzahl. Sie gilt zugleich als der Exponent jenes direkten Verhältnisses, welches der vorgestellten schlechten, d. i. formellen, nicht durch den Begriffs specifisch bestimmten Geschwindigkeit zukommt. Solche Geschwindigkeit existirt hier nicht, so wenig als die früher erwähnte, die dem Körper am Ende eines Zeitmoments zukommen sollte. Jene wird dem ersten Zeitmomente des Falles zugeschrieben, aber dieser sogenannte Zeitmoment ist eine selbst nur angenommene Einheit, und hat als solcher atomer Punkt kein Daseyn; der Anfang der Bewegung,—die Kleinheit, die für diesen vorgegeben wird, könnte keinen Unterschied machen,—ist sogleich eine Größe und zwar eine durch das Gesetz des Falles specificirte Größe. Jenes empirische Quantum wird der Kraft der Schwere zugeschrieben, so daß diese Kraft selbst keine Beziehung auf die vorhandene Specifikation, (die Potenzenbestimmtheit), auf das Eigenthümliche der Maaßbestimmung haben soll. Das unmittelbare Moment, daß in der Bewegung des Falles auf eine Zeiteinheit (—eine Sekunde und zwar die sogenannte erste—) die Anzahl von etwa fünfzehn räumlichen Einheiten, die als Fuße angenommen sind, komme, ist ein unmittelbares Maaß, wie die Maaßgröße der menschlichen Gliedmaaßen, die Distanzen, Durchmesser der Planeten u.s.f. Die Bestimmung solchen Maaßes fällt anderswohin, als innerhalb der qualitativen Maaßbestimmung hier des Gesetzes des Falles selbst; wovon aber solche Zahlen, das nur unmittelbar, daher als empirisch erscheinende eines Maaßes, abhängen, darüber haben uns die konkreten Wissenschaften noch keinen Aufschluß gegeben. Hier haben wir es nur mit dieser Begriffsbestimmtheit zu thun; diese ist, daß jener empirische Koefficient das Fürsichseyn in der Maaßbestimmung ausmacht, aber nur das Moment des Fürsichseyns, insofern dasselbe an sich und daher als unmittelbares ist. Das andere ist das Entwickelte dieses Fürsichseyns, die specifische Maaßbestimmtheit der Seiten.—Die Schwere, im Verhältnisse des Fallens, einer zwar noch halb bedingten und nur halbfreien Bewegung, ist nach diesem zweiten Momente als eine Naturkraft anzusehen, so daß durch die Natur der Zeit und des Raums ihr Verhältniß bestimmt ist, und daher in die Schwere jene Specifikation, das Potenzenverhältniß, fällt; jenes das einfache direkte Verhältniß drückt nur ein mechanisches Verhalten der Zeit und des Raumes aus, die formelle, äußerliche hervorgebrachte und determinirte Geschwindigkeit.\n\n3. Das Maaß hat sich dahin bestimmt, ein specificirtes Größenverhältniß zu seyn, das als quantitativ das gewohnliche außerliche Quantum an ihm hat; dieses aber ist nicht ein Quantum überhaupt, sondern wesentlich als Bestimmungsmoment des Verhältnisses als solchen; es ist so Exponent, und als nun unmittelbares Bestimmtseyn ein unveränderlicher Exponent, somit des schon erwähnten direkten Verhaltnisses derselben Qualitäten, durch welches zugleich ihr Größenverhältniß zu einander specifisch bestimmt wird. Dieses direkte Verhältniß ist im gebrauchten Beispiel des Maaßes der Fallbewegung gleichsam anticipirt und als vorhanden angenommen; aber wie bemerkt existirt es in dieser Bewegung noch nicht.—Es macht aber die weitere Bestimmung aus, daß das Maaß nun auf die Weise realisirt ist, daß seine beiden Seiten Maaße, unterschieden als unmittelbares, äußerliches, und als in sich specificirtes, sind, und es die Einheit derselben ist. Als diese Einheit enthält das Maaß das Verhältniß, in welchem die Größen durch die Natur der Qualitäten bestimmt und different gesetzt sind, und dessen Bestimmtheit daher ganz immanent und selbstständig, zugleich in das Fürsichseyn des unmittelbaren Quantums, den Exponenten eines direkten Verhältnisses, zusammen gegangen ist; seine Selbstbestimmung ist darin negirt, indem es in diesem seinem Andern die letzte, fürsichseyende Bestimmtheit hat; und umgekehrt hat das unmittelbare Maaß welches an ihm selbst qualitativ seyn soll, an jenem erst in Wahrheit die qualitative Bestimmtheit. Diese negative Einheit ist reales Fürsichseyn, die Kategorie eines Etwas, als Einheit von Qualitäten, die im Maaßverhältnisse sind; —eine volle Selbstständigkeit. Unmittelbar geben die beiden, welche sich als zwei verschiedene Verhältnisse ergeben haben, auch ein zweifaches Daseyn, oder näher solches selbstständige Ganze ist als Fürsichseyendes überhaupt zugleich ein Abstoßen in sich selbst in unterschiedene Selbstständige, deren qualitative Natur und Bestehen (Materialität) in ihrer Maaßbestimmtheit liegt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0001","text":"1. In der so eben betrachteten Form des specificirten Maaßes ist das Quantitative beider Seiten qualitativ bestimmt, (beide im Potenzen-Verhältniß); sie sind so Momente Einer Maaßbestimmtheit von qualitativer Natur. Dabei sind aber die Qualitäten nur erst noch als unmittelbare, nur verschiedene gesetzt, die nicht selbst in jenem Verhältnisse stehen, in welchem ihre Größebestimmtheiten sind, nämlich außer solchem Verhältnisse, keinen Sinn noch Daseyn zu haben, was die Potenzenbestimmtheit der Größe enthält. Das Qualitative verhüllt sich so, als nicht sich selbst, sondern die Größebestimmtheit specificirend; nur als an dieser ist es gesetzt, für sich aber unmittelbare Qualität als solche, die außerhalb dessen, daß die Größe von ihr in Differenz gesetzt wird, und außer ihrer Beziehung auf ihre andere, noch für sich bestehendes Daseyn habe.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"88.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0002","text":"So Raum und Zeit gelten beide außer jener Specifikation, die ihre Größebestimmtheit in der Bewegung des Falles oder in der absolutfreien Bewegung erhält, als Raum überhaupt, Zeit überhaupt, der Raum bestehend für sich außer und ohne die Zeit als dauernd, und die Zeit als für sich fließend unabhängig vom Raume.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"88.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0003","text":"Diese Unmittelbarkeit des Qualitativen gegen seine specifische Maaßbeziehung ist aber ebenso sehr mit einer quantitativen Unmittelbarkeit und der Gleichgültigkeit eines Quantitativen an ihm gegen dieß sein Verhältniß verknüpft; die unmittelbare Qualität hat auch ein nur unmittelbares Quantum. Daher hat denn das specifische Maaß auch eine Seite zunächst äußerlicher Veränderung, deren Fortgang bloß arithmetisch ist, von jenem nicht gestört wird, und in welche die äußerliche, darum nur empirische Größebestimmtheit fällt. Qualität und Quantum auch so außer dem specifischen Maaße auftretend, sind zugleich in der Beziehung auf dieses; die Unmittelbarkeit ist ein Moment von solchen, die selbst zum Maaße gehören.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"88.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0004","text":"So sind die unmittelbaren Qualitäten dem Maaße auch angehörig, gleichfalls in Beziehung, und stehen nach der Größebestimmtheit in einem Verhältniß, welches als außerhalb des specificirten, der Potenzbestimmung, selbst nur das direkte Verhältniß, und unmittelbares Maaß ist. Diese Folgerung und deren Zusammenhang ist näher anzugeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"88.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0005","text":"2. Das unmittelbar bestimmte Quantum als solches ist, wenn es auch als Maaßmoment sonst an sich in einem Begriffszusammenhang begründet ist, in der Beziehung zu dem specifischen Maaße als ein äußerlich gegebenes. Die Unmittelbarkeit, die hiermit gesetzt ist, ist aber die Negation der qualitativen Maaßbestimmung; dieselbe wurde vorhin an den Seiten dieser Maaßbestimmung aufgezeigt, welche darum als selbstständige Qualitäten erschienen. Solche Negation und das Zurückkehren zur unmittelbaren Quantitätsbestimmtheit liegt in dem qualitativbestimmten Verhältnisse insofern, als das Verhältniß Unterschiedener überhaupt deren Beziehung als Eine Bestimmtheit enthält, die hiermit hier im Quantitativen, unterschieden von der Verhältnißbestimmung, ein Quantum ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"88.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0006","text":"Als Negation der unterschiedenen qualitativbestimmten Seiten ist dieser Exponent ein Fürsichseyn, das Schlechthin-bestimmtseyn; aber ist solches Fürsichseyn nur an sich; als Daseyn ein einfaches, unmittelbares Quantum, Quotient oder Exponent als eines Verhältnisses der Seiten des Maaßes, dieß Verhältniß als ein direktes genommen; aber überhaupt die als empirisch erscheinende Einheit in dem Quantitativen des Maaßes.—Im Falle der Körper stehen die durchloffenen Räume im Verhältnisse des Quadrats der verflossenen Zeiten; s = at[hoch 2]; —dieß ist das specifisch-bestimmte, ein Potenzenverhälntiß des Raums und der Zeit, das andere, das direkte Verhältniß, käme dem Raum und der Zeit, als gegeneinander gleichgültigen Qualitäten, zu, es soll das des Raumes zu dem ersten Zeitmomente seyn, derselbe Koefficient, a, bleibt in allen folgenden Zeitpunkten;—die Einheit als ein gewöhnlichts Quantum fur","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"88.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0007","text":"die übrigens durch das specificirende Maaß bestimmte Anzahl. Sie gilt zugleich als der Exponent jenes direkten Verhältnisses, welches der vorgestellten schlechten, d. i. formellen, nicht durch den Begriffs specifisch bestimmten Geschwindigkeit zukommt. Solche Geschwindigkeit existirt hier nicht, so wenig als die früher erwähnte, die dem Körper am Ende eines Zeitmoments zukommen sollte. Jene wird dem ersten Zeitmomente des Falles zugeschrieben, aber dieser sogenannte Zeitmoment ist eine selbst nur angenommene Einheit, und hat als solcher atomer Punkt kein Daseyn; der Anfang der Bewegung,—die Kleinheit, die für diesen vorgegeben wird, könnte keinen Unterschied machen,—ist sogleich eine Größe und zwar eine durch das Gesetz des Falles specificirte Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"88.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0008","text":"Jenes empirische Quantum wird der Kraft der Schwere zugeschrieben, so daß diese Kraft selbst keine Beziehung auf die vorhandene Specifikation, (die Potenzenbestimmtheit), auf das Eigenthümliche der Maaßbestimmung haben soll. Das unmittelbare Moment, daß in der Bewegung des Falles auf eine Zeiteinheit (—eine Sekunde und zwar die sogenannte erste—) die Anzahl von etwa fünfzehn räumlichen Einheiten, die als Fuße angenommen sind, komme, ist ein unmittelbares Maaß, wie die Maaßgröße der menschlichen Gliedmaaßen, die Distanzen, Durchmesser der Planeten u.s.f. Die Bestimmung solchen Maaßes fällt anderswohin, als innerhalb der qualitativen Maaßbestimmung hier des Gesetzes des Falles selbst; wovon aber solche Zahlen, das nur unmittelbar, daher als empirisch erscheinende eines Maaßes, abhängen, darüber haben uns die konkreten Wissenschaften noch keinen Aufschluß gegeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"88.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0009","text":"Hier haben wir es nur mit dieser Begriffsbestimmtheit zu thun; diese ist, daß jener empirische Koefficient das Fürsichseyn in der Maaßbestimmung ausmacht, aber nur das Moment des Fürsichseyns, insofern dasselbe an sich und daher als unmittelbares ist. Das andere ist das Entwickelte dieses Fürsichseyns, die specifische Maaßbestimmtheit der Seiten.—Die Schwere, im Verhältnisse des Fallens, einer zwar noch halb bedingten und nur halbfreien Bewegung, ist nach diesem zweiten Momente als eine Naturkraft anzusehen, so daß durch die Natur der Zeit und des Raums ihr Verhältniß bestimmt ist, und daher in die Schwere jene Specifikation, das Potenzenverhältniß, fällt; jenes das einfache direkte Verhältniß drückt nur ein mechanisches Verhalten der Zeit und des Raumes aus, die formelle, äußerliche hervorgebrachte und determinirte Geschwindigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"88.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0010","text":"3. Das Maaß hat sich dahin bestimmt, ein specificirtes Größenverhältniß zu seyn, das als quantitativ das gewohnliche außerliche Quantum an ihm hat; dieses aber ist nicht ein Quantum überhaupt, sondern wesentlich als Bestimmungsmoment des Verhältnisses als solchen; es ist so Exponent, und als nun unmittelbares Bestimmtseyn ein unveränderlicher Exponent, somit des schon erwähnten direkten Verhaltnisses derselben Qualitäten, durch welches zugleich ihr Größenverhältniß zu einander specifisch bestimmt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"88.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0011","text":"Dieses direkte Verhältniß ist im gebrauchten Beispiel des Maaßes der Fallbewegung gleichsam anticipirt und als vorhanden angenommen; aber wie bemerkt existirt es in dieser Bewegung noch nicht.—Es macht aber die weitere Bestimmung aus, daß das Maaß nun auf die Weise realisirt ist, daß seine beiden Seiten Maaße, unterschieden als unmittelbares, äußerliches, und als in sich specificirtes, sind, und es die Einheit derselben ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"88.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0012","text":"Als diese Einheit enthält das Maaß das Verhältniß, in welchem die Größen durch die Natur der Qualitäten bestimmt und different gesetzt sind, und dessen Bestimmtheit daher ganz immanent und selbstständig, zugleich in das Fürsichseyn des unmittelbaren Quantums, den Exponenten eines direkten Verhältnisses, zusammen gegangen ist; seine Selbstbestimmung ist darin negirt, indem es in diesem seinem Andern die letzte, fürsichseyende Bestimmtheit hat; und umgekehrt hat das unmittelbare Maaß welches an ihm selbst qualitativ seyn soll, an jenem erst in Wahrheit die qualitative Bestimmtheit. Diese negative Einheit ist reales Fürsichseyn, die Kategorie eines Etwas, als Einheit von Qualitäten, die im Maaßverhältnisse sind; —eine volle Selbstständigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"88.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0013","text":"Unmittelbar geben die beiden, welche sich als zwei verschiedene Verhältnisse ergeben haben, auch ein zweifaches Daseyn, oder näher solches selbstständige Ganze ist als Fürsichseyendes überhaupt zugleich ein Abstoßen in sich selbst in unterschiedene Selbstständige, deren qualitative Natur und Bestehen (Materialität) in ihrer Maaßbestimmtheit liegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"88.13"}],"sha256":"f058d255a65a203a1bf21dd8bb25f4061b24af463f6614cbfab2630f0d8fcbc2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104210819219Z_194d172a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Being-for-Self in Measure.","source_sha256":"f058d255a65a203a1bf21dd8bb25f4061b24af463f6614cbfab2630f0d8fcbc2","sha256":"734bb344124a284e55a09b9c99e661054b79fb93ee257e64337c8f96b6e5d3ad","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:42:10.819242+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0001","text":"1. In the form of specified measure just considered, the quantitative of both sides is qualitatively determined (both are in a relation of powers); they are thus moments of One determination of measure of a qualitative nature. Yet the qualities are at first posited only as immediate, merely different, qualities, which do not themselves stand in that relation in which their determinations of magnitude stand, namely, outside such a relation, to have no sense or existence, which is what the determination of magnitude as powers contains. The qualitative thus conceals itself as specifying, not itself, but the determination of magnitude; it is posited only as being at this latter, but for itself as immediate quality as such, which, apart from the magnitude being posited in difference by it, and apart from its relation to its other, is still to have existence subsisting for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"88.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0002","text":"Thus space and time both count, apart from that specification which their determination of magnitude receives in the motion of falling or in absolutely free motion, as space in general, time in general: space as subsisting for itself outside of and without time, as enduring, and time as flowing for itself independently of space.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"88.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0003","text":"But this immediacy of the qualitative in relation to its specific relation of measure is equally bound up with a quantitative immediacy and the indifference of a quantitative element in it toward this its relation; immediate quality also has a merely immediate quantum. Hence specific measure also has a side of initially external alteration, whose progression is merely arithmetical, is not disturbed by the former, and into which the external, and therefore merely empirical, determination of magnitude falls. Quality and quantum, even as thus appearing outside specific measure, are at the same time in relation to it; immediacy is a moment of such [terms], which themselves belong to measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"88.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0004","text":"Thus the immediate qualities also belong to measure, are likewise in relation, and, according to the determination of magnitude, stand in a relation which, as outside the specified [relation], the determination of powers, is itself only the direct relation and immediate measure. This consequence and its connection are to be indicated more closely.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"88.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0005","text":"2. The immediately determined quantum as such, even if otherwise, as a moment of measure, it is grounded in itself in a conceptual connection, is, in relation to specific measure, an externally given [quantum]. Yet the immediacy thereby posited is the negation of the qualitative determination of measure; this was previously displayed in the sides of this determination of measure, which therefore appeared as self-subsistent qualities. Such negation and the return to immediate determinacy of quantity lie in the qualitatively determined relation insofar as the relation of different [terms] in general contains their reference as One determinacy, which thereby here, in the quantitative, distinguished from the determination of relation, is a quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"88.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0006","text":"As negation of the distinct qualitatively determined sides, this exponent is a being-for-self, being-determined absolutely; but such being-for-self is only in itself; as existence, a simple, immediate quantum, quotient or exponent as of a relation of the sides of measure, this relation taken as a direct one; but in general the unity, appearing as empirical, in the quantitative of measure.—In the fall of bodies, the spaces traversed stand in the relation of the square of the elapsed times; s = at[hoch 2];—this is the specifically determined [relation], a relation of powers of space and time; the other, the direct relation, would pertain to space and time as qualities indifferent toward one another; it is supposed to be that of space to the first moment of time; the same coefficient, a, remains at all subsequent points of time;—the unity as an ordinary quantum for","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"88.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0007","text":"the number otherwise determined by the specifying measure. It counts at the same time as the exponent of that direct relation which belongs to the represented bad, i.e. formal, velocity not specifically determined by the Concept. Such velocity does not exist here, any more than does the one mentioned earlier, which was supposed to accrue to the body at the end of a moment of time. The former is ascribed to the first moment of time of the fall, but this so-called moment of time is itself only an assumed unity and, as such an atomic point, has no existence; the beginning of the motion,—the smallness asserted for it could make no difference,—is at once a magnitude, and indeed a magnitude specified by the law of falling.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"88.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0008","text":"That empirical quantum is ascribed to the force of gravity, so that this force itself is not supposed to have any relation to the existing specification (the determination of powers), to the peculiarity of the determination of measure. The immediate moment that in the motion of falling, for one unit of time (—one second, and indeed the so-called first—), the number of about fifteen spatial units, assumed as feet, occurs, is an immediate measure, like the measure of the size of human limbs, the distances and diameters of planets, etc. The determination of such measure falls elsewhere than within the qualitative determination of measure here, the law of falling itself; but as to what such numbers, the merely immediate and hence empirically appearing element of a measure, depend upon, the concrete sciences have not yet given us any elucidation.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"88.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0009","text":"Here we have to do only with this determinacy of the Concept; this is that the empirical coefficient just mentioned constitutes being-for-self in the determination of measure, but only the moment of being-for-self, insofar as this is in itself and hence immediate. The other is the developed [form] of this being-for-self, the specific determination of measure of the sides.—Gravity, in the relation of falling, a motion still half-conditioned and only half-free, is, according to this second moment, to be regarded as a force of nature, such that its relation is determined through the nature of time and space, and hence that specification, the relation of powers, falls into gravity; the former, the simple direct relation, expresses only a mechanical comportment of time and space, the formal, externally produced and determined velocity.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"88.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0010","text":"3. Measure has determined itself to be a specified relation of magnitudes, which, as quantitative, has the ordinary external quantum at it; but this is not a quantum in general, but essentially, as a determining moment of the relation as such; it is thus exponent, and, as now immediate determinacy, an invariable exponent, consequently of the already mentioned direct relation of the same qualities, through which at the same time their relation of magnitudes to one another is specifically determined.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"88.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0011","text":"This direct relation is, as it were, anticipated and assumed as present in the example used of the measure of falling motion; but, as remarked, it does not yet exist in this motion.—But the further determination consists in this, that measure is now realized in such a way that its two sides are measures, distinct as immediate, external [measure], and as measure specified within itself, and that it is their unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"88.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0012","text":"As this unity, measure contains the relation in which the magnitudes are determined and posited as different by the nature of the qualities, and whose determinacy is therefore wholly immanent and self-subsistent, yet has at the same time gone together into the being-for-self of the immediate quantum, the exponent of a direct relation; its self-determination is therein negated, in that it has the ultimate determinacy, existing-for-itself, in this its other; and conversely, immediate measure, which is supposed to be qualitative in itself, has only in that [other] its qualitative determinacy in truth. This negative unity is real being-for-self, the category of a something, as unity of qualities which are in a relation of measure;—a complete self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"88.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0013","text":"Immediately, the two [relations] which have emerged as two different relations also yield a twofold existence; or, more precisely, such a self-subsistent whole is, as that which exists-for-itself in general, at the same time a repulsion within itself into distinct self-subsistent [entities], whose qualitative nature and subsistence (materiality) lie in their determination of measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"88.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDFR:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"6cc412f4f9a8ebbd9a0689f2a85903cedd9a3506962b72c2ef2c1296715b2c6e","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Das Fürsichseyn im Maaße."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Das Fürsichseyn im Maaße.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS","title":"A. The Relation of Self-Subsistent Measures.","order":89,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DVLS","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Das reale Maaß.\n\nDas Maaß ist bestimmt zu einer Beziehung von Maaßen, welche die Qualität unterschiedener selbstständiger Etwas, geläufiger: Dinge ausmachen. Die so eben betrachteten Maaßverhältnisse gehören abstrakten Qualitäten, wie dem Raume und der Zeit, an; zu den im bevorstehenden zu betrachtenden sind specifische Schwere, weiterhin die chemischen Eigenschaften die Beispiele, welche als Bestimmungen materieller Existenzen sind. Raum und Zeit sind auch Momente solcher Maaße, die aber nun weitern Bestimmungen untergeordnet, nicht mehr nur nach ihrer eigenen Begriffsbestimmung sich zu einander verhalten. Im Klange z.B. ist die Zeit, in welcher eine Anzahl der Schwingungen erfolgt, das Räumliche der Länge, Dicke, des schwingenden Körpers, unter den Bestimmungsmomenten; aber die Größen jener ideellen Momente sind äußerlich bestimmt, sie zeigen sich nicht mehr in einem Potenzen-, sondern in gewöhnlichem direkten Verhältnisse gegeneinander, und das Harmonische reducirt sich auf die ganz äußerliche Einfachheit von Zahlen, deren Verhältnisse sich am leichtesten auffassen lassen, und damit eine Befriedigung gewähren, die ganz der Empfindung anheimfällt, da für den Geist keine Vorstellung, Phantasiebild, Gedanke und dergleichen ihn Erfüllendes vorhanden ist. Indem die Seiten, welche nun das Maaßverhältniß ausmachen, selbst Maaße, aber zugleich reelle Etwas sind, sind ihre Maaße zunächst unmittelbare Maaße und als Verhältnisse an ihnen, direkte Verhältnisse. Es ist das Verhältniß solcher Verhältnisse zu einander, welches nun in seiner Fortbestimmung zu betrachten ist.\n\nDas Maaß, wie es so nunmehr reales ist, ist\n\nerstens ein selbstständiges Maaß einer Körperlichkeit, das sich zu andern verhält und in diesem Verhalten dieselben, so wie damit die selbstständige Materialität, specificirt. Diese Specifikation, als ein äußerliches Beziehen zu vielen Andern überhaupt ist das Hervorbringen anderer Verhältnisse, somit anderer Maaße, und die specifische Selbstständigkeit bleibt nicht in einem direkten Verhältnisse, bestehen, sondern geht in specifische Bestimmtheit, die eine Reihe von Maaßen ist, über.\n\nZweitens sind die dadurch entstehenden direkten Verhältnisse, an sich bestimmte und ausschließende Maaße, (Wahlverwandschaften); indem aber ihr Unterschied von einander zugleich nur quantitativ ist, so ist ein Fortgang von Verhältnissen vorhanden, der zum Theil bloß äußerlich quantitativ ist, aber auch durch qualitative Verhältnisse unterbrochen wird, und eine Knotenlinie von specifischen Selbstständigen bildet.\n\nDrittens aber tritt in diesem Fortgange für das Maaß die Maaßlosigkeit überhaupt, und bestimmter die Unendlichkeit des Maaßes ein, in welcher die sich ausschließenden Selbstständigkeiten Eins mit einander sind, und das Selbstständige in negative Beziehung zu sich selbst tritt.\n\n## A. Das Verhältniß selbstständiger Maaße.\n\nDie Maaße heißen nun nicht mehr bloß unmittelbare, sondern selbstständige, insofern sie an ihnen selbst zu Verhältnissen von Maaßen, welche specificirt sind, so in diesem Fürsichseyn Etwas, physikalische, zunächst materielle Dinge sind. Das Ganze, welches ein Verhältniß solcher Maaße ist, ist aber\n\na. zunächst selbst unmittelbar; so sind die beiden Seiten, welche als solche selbstständige Maaße bestimmt sind, außer einander an besondern Dingen bestehend, und werden äußerlich in Verbindung gesetzt;\n\nb. die selbstständigen Materialitäten sind aber, was sie qualitativ sind, nur durch die quantitative Bestimmung, die sie als Maaße haben, somit durch selbst quantitative Beziehung auf andere, als different dagegen (sogenannte Affinität) und zwar als Glieder einer Reihe solchen quantitativen Verhaltens bestimmt;\n\nc. dieses gleichgültige mannigfaltige Verhalten schließt sich zugleich zum ausschließenden Fürsichseyn ab;—sogenannte Wahlverwandschaft.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0001","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Das reale Maaß.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"89.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0002","text":"Das Maaß ist bestimmt zu einer Beziehung von Maaßen, welche die Qualität unterschiedener selbstständiger Etwas, geläufiger: Dinge ausmachen. Die so eben betrachteten Maaßverhältnisse gehören abstrakten Qualitäten, wie dem Raume und der Zeit, an; zu den im bevorstehenden zu betrachtenden sind specifische Schwere, weiterhin die chemischen Eigenschaften die Beispiele, welche als Bestimmungen materieller Existenzen sind. Raum und Zeit sind auch Momente solcher Maaße, die aber nun weitern Bestimmungen untergeordnet, nicht mehr nur nach ihrer eigenen Begriffsbestimmung sich zu einander verhalten. Im Klange z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"89.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0003","text":"ist die Zeit, in welcher eine Anzahl der Schwingungen erfolgt, das Räumliche der Länge, Dicke, des schwingenden Körpers, unter den Bestimmungsmomenten; aber die Größen jener ideellen Momente sind äußerlich bestimmt, sie zeigen sich nicht mehr in einem Potenzen-, sondern in gewöhnlichem direkten Verhältnisse gegeneinander, und das Harmonische reducirt sich auf die ganz äußerliche Einfachheit von Zahlen, deren Verhältnisse sich am leichtesten auffassen lassen, und damit eine Befriedigung gewähren, die ganz der Empfindung anheimfällt, da für den Geist keine Vorstellung, Phantasiebild, Gedanke und dergleichen ihn Erfüllendes vorhanden ist. Indem die Seiten, welche nun das Maaßverhältniß ausmachen, selbst Maaße, aber zugleich reelle Etwas sind, sind ihre Maaße zunächst unmittelbare Maaße und als Verhältnisse an ihnen, direkte Verhältnisse.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"89.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0004","text":"Es ist das Verhältniß solcher Verhältnisse zu einander, welches nun in seiner Fortbestimmung zu betrachten ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"89.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0005","text":"Das Maaß, wie es so nunmehr reales ist, ist","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"89.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0006","text":"erstens ein selbstständiges Maaß einer Körperlichkeit, das sich zu andern verhält und in diesem Verhalten dieselben, so wie damit die selbstständige Materialität, specificirt. Diese Specifikation, als ein äußerliches Beziehen zu vielen Andern überhaupt ist das Hervorbringen anderer Verhältnisse, somit anderer Maaße, und die specifische Selbstständigkeit bleibt nicht in einem direkten Verhältnisse, bestehen, sondern geht in specifische Bestimmtheit, die eine Reihe von Maaßen ist, über.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"89.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0007","text":"Zweitens sind die dadurch entstehenden direkten Verhältnisse, an sich bestimmte und ausschließende Maaße, (Wahlverwandschaften); indem aber ihr Unterschied von einander zugleich nur quantitativ ist, so ist ein Fortgang von Verhältnissen vorhanden, der zum Theil bloß äußerlich quantitativ ist, aber auch durch qualitative Verhältnisse unterbrochen wird, und eine Knotenlinie von specifischen Selbstständigen bildet.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"89.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0008","text":"Drittens aber tritt in diesem Fortgange für das Maaß die Maaßlosigkeit überhaupt, und bestimmter die Unendlichkeit des Maaßes ein, in welcher die sich ausschließenden Selbstständigkeiten Eins mit einander sind, und das Selbstständige in negative Beziehung zu sich selbst tritt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"89.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0009","text":"## A. Das Verhältniß selbstständiger Maaße.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"89.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0010","text":"Die Maaße heißen nun nicht mehr bloß unmittelbare, sondern selbstständige, insofern sie an ihnen selbst zu Verhältnissen von Maaßen, welche specificirt sind, so in diesem Fürsichseyn Etwas, physikalische, zunächst materielle Dinge sind. Das Ganze, welches ein Verhältniß solcher Maaße ist, ist aber","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"89.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0011","text":"a. zunächst selbst unmittelbar; so sind die beiden Seiten, welche als solche selbstständige Maaße bestimmt sind, außer einander an besondern Dingen bestehend, und werden äußerlich in Verbindung gesetzt;","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"89.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0012","text":"b. die selbstständigen Materialitäten sind aber, was sie qualitativ sind, nur durch die quantitative Bestimmung, die sie als Maaße haben, somit durch selbst quantitative Beziehung auf andere, als different dagegen (sogenannte Affinität) und zwar als Glieder einer Reihe solchen quantitativen Verhaltens bestimmt;","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"89.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0013","text":"c. dieses gleichgültige mannigfaltige Verhalten schließt sich zugleich zum ausschließenden Fürsichseyn ab;—sogenannte Wahlverwandschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"89.13"}],"sha256":"8fc5d643b5146494877480a307aac8e0dbaca46f2a99357d002354cc4ef4fed2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104219584139Z_1c69c5e7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Relation of Self-Subsistent Measures.","source_sha256":"8fc5d643b5146494877480a307aac8e0dbaca46f2a99357d002354cc4ef4fed2","sha256":"3d712b222738ad3f1a9729d83a1081b76730df55b65c0cb21e3431b1bcecf10d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:42:19.584164+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0001","text":"## Chapter Two. Real Measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"89.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0002","text":"Measure is determined as a relation of measures which constitute the quality of different self-subsistent somethings, more commonly: things. The relations of measure just considered belong to abstract qualities, such as space and time; examples of those to be considered next are specific gravity, and subsequently chemical properties, which are determinations of material existences. Space and time are likewise moments of such measures, but now subordinated to further determinations, no longer relating to one another merely in accordance with their own conceptual determination. In sound, e.g.,","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"89.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0003","text":"the time in which a number of vibrations occur, and the spatiality of the length and thickness of the vibrating body, are among the determining moments; but the magnitudes of those ideal moments are externally determined; they no longer show themselves in a relation of powers, but in an ordinary direct relation to one another, and the harmonic is reduced to the wholly external simplicity of numbers, whose relations are most easily apprehended and thereby afford a satisfaction that falls wholly within sensation, since for spirit there is no representation, image of imagination, thought, and the like, that fills it. Since the sides which now constitute the relation of measure are themselves measures, but at the same time real somethings, their measures are at first immediate measures and, as relations in them, direct relations.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"89.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0004","text":"It is the relation of such relations to one another which is now to be considered in its further determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"89.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0005","text":"Measure, as it is now real, is","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"89.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0006","text":"first, a self-subsistent measure of a corporeality, which relates itself to others and in this relation specifies them, as well as therewith the self-subsistent materiality. This specification, as an external relating to many others in general, is the production of other relations, hence of other measures, and the specific self-subsistence does not remain in a direct relation, but passes over into specific determinacy, which is a series of measures.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"89.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0007","text":"Secondly, the direct relations thereby arising are measures determined and exclusive in themselves (elective affinities); but since their difference from one another is at the same time only quantitative, there is a progression of relations which is in part merely externally quantitative, but is also interrupted by qualitative relations, and forms a nodal line of specific self-subsistents.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"89.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0008","text":"Thirdly, however, in this progression there enters for measure measurelessness in general, and more determinately the infinity of measure, in which the self-subsistences that exclude one another are one with one another, and the self-subsistent enters into negative relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"89.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0009","text":"## A. The Relation of Self-Subsistent Measures.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"89.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0010","text":"The measures are now called no longer merely immediate, but self-subsistent, insofar as they are in themselves relations of measures which are specified, and thus in this being-for-self are somethings, physical, at first material things. But the whole which is a relation of such measures is","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"89.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0011","text":"a. at first itself immediate; thus the two sides which are determined as such self-subsistent measures subsist apart from one another in particular things and are externally brought into combination;","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"89.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0012","text":"b. the self-subsistent materialities are, however, what they are qualitatively only through the quantitative determination which they have as measures, hence through quantitative relation itself to others, as different from them (so-called affinity), and indeed determined as members of a series of such quantitative comportment;","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"89.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0013","text":"c. this indifferent manifold comportment at the same time closes itself into exclusive being-for-self;—so-called elective affinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"89.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLS:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"c7c19c58ed293e0dc8effbbee212a5a01f3a4fe586d9716554d7f3c8fd6c76c4","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Verhältniß selbstständiger Maaße."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Verhältniß selbstständiger Maaße.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0","title":"a. Combination of Two Measures.","order":90,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_VZM0","text":"Etwas ist in sich als Maaßverhältniß von Quantis bestimmt, welche ferner Qualitäten zukommen, und das Etwas ist die Beziehung von diesen Qualitäten. Die eine ist dessen Insichseyn, wonach es ein Fürsichseyendes,—Materielles—ist, (wie intensiv genommen, das Gewicht, oder extensiv, die Menge aber von materiellen Theilen); die andere aber ist die Äußerlichkeit dieses Insichseyns, (das Abstrakte, Ideelle, der Raum.) Diese Qualitäten sind quantitativ bestimmt, und das Verhältniß derselben zu einander macht die qualitative Natur des materiellen Etwas aus;—das Verhältniß des Gewichts zum Volumen, die bestimmte specifische Schwere. Das Volumen, das Ideelle, ist als die Einheit anzunehmen, das Intensive aber, das in quantitativer Bestimmtheit und in der Vergleichung mit jenem als extensive Größe, Menge von fürsichseyenden Eins erscheint, als die Anzahl.—Das reine qualitative Verhalten der beiden Größebestimmtheiten, nach einem Potenzenverhältniß ist darin verschwunden, daß in der Selbstständigkeit des Fürsichseyns (—materiellen Seyns—) die Unmittelbarkeit zurückgekehrt ist, an welcher die Größebestimmtheit ein Quantum als solches, und das Verhältniß eines solchen zu der andern Seite ebenfalls in dem gewöhnlichen Exponenten eines direkten Verhältnisses bestimmt ist.\n\nDieser Exponent ist das specifische Quantum des Etwas, aber er ist unmittelbares Quantum und dieses, damit die specifische Natur von solchem Etwas, ist nur in der Vergleichung mit andern Exponenten solcher Verhältnisse bestimmt. Er macht das specifische An-sich-bestimmtseyn, das innere eigenthümliche Maaß von Etwas aus; aber indem dieses sein Maaß auf dem Quantum beruht, ist es auch nur als äußerliche, gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, und solches Etwas ist dadurch der innerlichen Maaßbestimmung ungeachtet veränderlich. Das Andere, zu dem es als veränderlich sich verhalten kann, ist nicht eine Menge von Materie, ein Quantum überhaupt; hiergegen hält sein specifisches Ansichbestimmtseyn aus, sondern ein Quantum, das zugleich ebenso Exponent solchen specifischen Verhältnisses ist. Es sind zwei Dinge, von verschiedenem inneren Maaße, die in Beziehung stehen, und in Verbindung treten; wie zwei Metalle voll verschiedener specifischer Schwere;—welche Gleichartigkeit ihrer Natur, daß es z. B. nicht ein Metall ist, von dessen Verbindung mit Wasser die Rede wäre, sonst zur Möglichkeit solcher Verbindung erforderlich sey, gehört nicht hierher zu betrachten.—Einer Seits erhält sich nun jedes der beiden Maaße in der Veränderung, die an dasselbe durch die Äußerlichkeit des Quantums kommen sollte, weil es Maaß ist, anderer Seits aber ist dieses Sich-erhalten selbst ein negatives Verhalten zu diesem Quantum, eine Specifikation desselben, und da dasselbe Exponent des Maaß Verhältnisses ist, eine Veränderung des Maaßes selbst und zwar eine gegenseitige Specifikation.\n\nNach der bloß quantitativen Bestimmung wäre die Verbindung ein bloßes Summiren der zwei Größen der einen, und der zwei der andern Qualität, z.B. die Summe der beiden Gewichte und der beiden Volumen bei der Verbindung zweier Materien von verschiedener specifischer Schwere, so daß nicht nur das Gewicht des Gemisches gleich jener Summe bliebe, sondern auch der Raum, den dasselbe einnimmt, gleich der Summe jener Räume. Allein nur das Gewicht findet sich als die Summe der Gewichte, —die vor der Verbindung vorhanden waren; es summirt sich die Seite, welche als die für sichseyende zum festen Daseyn und damit von bleibendem unmittelbaren Quantum geworden ist,—das Gewicht der Materie, oder was für dasselbe nach der Rücksicht der quantitativen Bestimmtheit gilt, die Menge der materiellen Theile. Aber in die Exponenten fällt die Veränderung, indem sie der Ausdruck der qualitativen Bestimmtheit, des Fürsichseyns als Maaß-Verhältnisse sind, welches, indem das Quantum als solches die zufällige, äußerliche Veränderung durch Zusatz, der summirt wird, erleidet, zugleich sich als negirend gegen diese Äußerlichkeit erweist.\n\nDieses immanente Bestimmen des Quantitativen, da es, wie gezeigt, nicht am Gewichte erscheinen kann, erweist sich an der andern Qualität, welche die ideelle Seite des Verhältnisses ist. Für die sinnliche Wahrnehmung kann es auffallend seyn, daß sich nach der Vermischung zweier specifisch verschiedener Materien eine Veränderung, —gewöhnlich eine Verminderung,—des summirten Volumens zeigt; der Raum selbst macht das Bestehen der außereinanderseyenden Materie aus. Aber dieß Bestehen, gegen die Negativität, welche das Fürsichseyn in sich enthält, ist das nicht an sich Seyende, das Veränderliche; der Raum wird auf diese Weise als das, was er wahrhaft ist, als das Ideelle gesetzt.\n\nEs ist aber hiermit nicht nur die eine der qualitativen Seiten als veränderlich gesetzt sondern das Maaß selbst, und damit die darauf gegründete qualitative Bestimmtheit des Etwas hat sich so gezeigt, nicht an ihm selbst ein Festes zu seyn, sondern, wie das Quantum überhaupt, seine Bestimmtheit in andern MaaßVerhältnissen zu haben.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0001","text":"Etwas ist in sich als Maaßverhältniß von Quantis bestimmt, welche ferner Qualitäten zukommen, und das Etwas ist die Beziehung von diesen Qualitäten. Die eine ist dessen Insichseyn, wonach es ein Fürsichseyendes,—Materielles—ist, (wie intensiv genommen, das Gewicht, oder extensiv, die Menge aber von materiellen Theilen); die andere aber ist die Äußerlichkeit dieses Insichseyns, (das Abstrakte, Ideelle, der Raum.) Diese Qualitäten sind quantitativ bestimmt, und das Verhältniß derselben zu einander macht die qualitative Natur des materiellen Etwas aus;—das Verhältniß des Gewichts zum Volumen, die bestimmte specifische Schwere.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"90.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0002","text":"Das Volumen, das Ideelle, ist als die Einheit anzunehmen, das Intensive aber, das in quantitativer Bestimmtheit und in der Vergleichung mit jenem als extensive Größe, Menge von fürsichseyenden Eins erscheint, als die Anzahl.—Das reine qualitative Verhalten der beiden Größebestimmtheiten, nach einem Potenzenverhältniß ist darin verschwunden, daß in der Selbstständigkeit des Fürsichseyns (—materiellen Seyns—) die Unmittelbarkeit zurückgekehrt ist, an welcher die Größebestimmtheit ein Quantum als solches, und das Verhältniß eines solchen zu der andern Seite ebenfalls in dem gewöhnlichen Exponenten eines direkten Verhältnisses bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"90.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0003","text":"Dieser Exponent ist das specifische Quantum des Etwas, aber er ist unmittelbares Quantum und dieses, damit die specifische Natur von solchem Etwas, ist nur in der Vergleichung mit andern Exponenten solcher Verhältnisse bestimmt. Er macht das specifische An-sich-bestimmtseyn, das innere eigenthümliche Maaß von Etwas aus; aber indem dieses sein Maaß auf dem Quantum beruht, ist es auch nur als äußerliche, gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, und solches Etwas ist dadurch der innerlichen Maaßbestimmung ungeachtet veränderlich. Das Andere, zu dem es als veränderlich sich verhalten kann, ist nicht eine Menge von Materie, ein Quantum überhaupt; hiergegen hält sein specifisches Ansichbestimmtseyn aus, sondern ein Quantum, das zugleich ebenso Exponent solchen specifischen Verhältnisses ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"90.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0004","text":"Es sind zwei Dinge, von verschiedenem inneren Maaße, die in Beziehung stehen, und in Verbindung treten; wie zwei Metalle voll verschiedener specifischer Schwere;—welche Gleichartigkeit ihrer Natur, daß es z. B. nicht ein Metall ist, von dessen Verbindung mit Wasser die Rede wäre, sonst zur Möglichkeit solcher Verbindung erforderlich sey, gehört nicht hierher zu betrachten.—Einer Seits erhält sich nun jedes der beiden Maaße in der Veränderung, die an dasselbe durch die Äußerlichkeit des Quantums kommen sollte, weil es Maaß ist, anderer Seits aber ist dieses Sich-erhalten selbst ein negatives Verhalten zu diesem Quantum, eine Specifikation desselben, und da dasselbe Exponent des Maaß Verhältnisses ist, eine Veränderung des Maaßes selbst und zwar eine gegenseitige Specifikation.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"90.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0005","text":"Nach der bloß quantitativen Bestimmung wäre die Verbindung ein bloßes Summiren der zwei Größen der einen, und der zwei der andern Qualität, z.B. die Summe der beiden Gewichte und der beiden Volumen bei der Verbindung zweier Materien von verschiedener specifischer Schwere, so daß nicht nur das Gewicht des Gemisches gleich jener Summe bliebe, sondern auch der Raum, den dasselbe einnimmt, gleich der Summe jener Räume. Allein nur das Gewicht findet sich als die Summe der Gewichte, —die vor der Verbindung vorhanden waren; es summirt sich die Seite, welche als die für sichseyende zum festen Daseyn und damit von bleibendem unmittelbaren Quantum geworden ist,—das Gewicht der Materie, oder was für dasselbe nach der Rücksicht der quantitativen Bestimmtheit gilt, die Menge der materiellen Theile.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"90.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0006","text":"Aber in die Exponenten fällt die Veränderung, indem sie der Ausdruck der qualitativen Bestimmtheit, des Fürsichseyns als Maaß-Verhältnisse sind, welches, indem das Quantum als solches die zufällige, äußerliche Veränderung durch Zusatz, der summirt wird, erleidet, zugleich sich als negirend gegen diese Äußerlichkeit erweist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"90.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0007","text":"Dieses immanente Bestimmen des Quantitativen, da es, wie gezeigt, nicht am Gewichte erscheinen kann, erweist sich an der andern Qualität, welche die ideelle Seite des Verhältnisses ist. Für die sinnliche Wahrnehmung kann es auffallend seyn, daß sich nach der Vermischung zweier specifisch verschiedener Materien eine Veränderung, —gewöhnlich eine Verminderung,—des summirten Volumens zeigt; der Raum selbst macht das Bestehen der außereinanderseyenden Materie aus. Aber dieß Bestehen, gegen die Negativität, welche das Fürsichseyn in sich enthält, ist das nicht an sich Seyende, das Veränderliche; der Raum wird auf diese Weise als das, was er wahrhaft ist, als das Ideelle gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"90.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0008","text":"Es ist aber hiermit nicht nur die eine der qualitativen Seiten als veränderlich gesetzt sondern das Maaß selbst, und damit die darauf gegründete qualitative Bestimmtheit des Etwas hat sich so gezeigt, nicht an ihm selbst ein Festes zu seyn, sondern, wie das Quantum überhaupt, seine Bestimmtheit in andern MaaßVerhältnissen zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"90.8"}],"sha256":"d56977e4d8583b5c9d790294371ff48be5a2f654bb023b7fdf028bb726d69b5d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104231990566Z_df16d146","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Combination of Two Measures.","source_sha256":"d56977e4d8583b5c9d790294371ff48be5a2f654bb023b7fdf028bb726d69b5d","sha256":"c9fbdd03c6ec93753b98eddbe2a7c1b257665b781a969651e1a0679a92f0e5b0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:42:31.990647+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0001","text":"Something is determined in itself as a ratio of measure of quanta, to which, further, qualities belong, and the something is the relation of these qualities. The one is its being-in-self, according to which it is a being-for-self,—material—(taken intensively, weight, or extensively, however, the quantity of material parts); but the other is the externality of this being-in-self (the abstract, the ideal, space). These qualities are determined quantitatively, and their relation to one another constitutes the qualitative nature of the material something;—the relation of weight to volume, determinate specific gravity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"90.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0002","text":"Volume, the ideal, is to be taken as the unit; but the intensive, which in quantitative determinacy and in comparison with the former appears as extensive magnitude, as a quantity of ones that are for themselves, as the number.—The purely qualitative comportment of the two magnitude-determinations, according to a relation of powers, has disappeared in this: that, in the self-subsistence of being-for-self (—material being—), immediacy has returned, in which magnitude-determination is a quantum as such, and the relation of such a quantum to the other side is likewise determined in the ordinary exponent of a direct relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"90.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0003","text":"This exponent is the specific quantum of the something; but it is an immediate quantum, and this, and thus the specific nature of such a something, is determined only in comparison with other exponents of such relations. It constitutes the specific being-determined-in-itself, the inner peculiar measure of a something; but since this its measure rests upon quantum, it is also only an external, indifferent determinacy, and such a something is thereby mutable notwithstanding its inner determination of measure. The other to which it can comport itself as mutable is not a quantity of matter, a quantum in general; against this its specific being-determined-in-itself holds firm, but rather a quantum which is at the same time likewise an exponent of such a specific relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"90.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0004","text":"There are two things, of different inner measure, which stand in relation and enter into combination; such as two metals of altogether different specific gravity;—what homogeneity of their nature, namely that it is not, for example, a metal whose combination with water is under discussion, would otherwise be required for the possibility of such combination, does not belong to consideration here.—On the one hand, each of the two measures now maintains itself in the alteration which should come upon it through the externality of quantum, because it is measure; but, on the other hand, this maintaining-itself is itself a negative comportment toward this quantum, a specification of it, and, since it is the exponent of the relation of measure, an alteration of the measure itself, namely a reciprocal specification.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"90.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0005","text":"According to merely quantitative determination, the combination would be a mere summing of the two magnitudes of the one, and of the two of the other quality; e.g. the sum of the two weights and the two volumes in the combination of two materials of different specific gravity, so that not only the weight of the mixture would remain equal to that sum, but also the space which it occupies would be equal to the sum of those spaces. Yet only the weight is found as the sum of the weights—which were present before the combination; the side which, as being-for-self, has become fixed existence and thereby a permanent immediate quantum, is summed,—the weight of matter, or, what counts in its stead from the point of view of quantitative determinacy, the quantity of material parts.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"90.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0006","text":"But the alteration falls into the exponents, since they are the expression of qualitative determinacy, of being-for-self as relations of measure, which, while quantum as such undergoes the contingent, external alteration through addition which is summed, at the same time proves itself to be negating toward this externality.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"90.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0007","text":"This immanent determining of the quantitative, since, as shown, it cannot appear in weight, proves itself in the other quality, which is the ideal side of the relation. For sensuous perception it may be striking that, after the mixing of two specifically different materials, an alteration,—ordinarily a diminution,—of the summed volume shows itself; space itself constitutes the subsistence of material that is outside itself. But this subsistence, as against the negativity which being-for-self contains within itself, is that which is not in itself, the mutable; space is thus posited as what it truly is, as the ideal.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"90.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0008","text":"But thereby not only is one of the qualitative sides posited as mutable; rather, measure itself, and with it the qualitative determinacy of the something founded thereon, has thus shown itself not to be something fixed in itself, but, like quantum in general, to have its determinacy in other relations of measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"90.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_VZM0:P0008"]}],"source_digest":"7c8609c0bcdeaafd1558f701a1e160b4317659394dfe4c8baeb55927e962f061","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Verbindung zweier Maaße."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Verbindung zweier Maaße.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA","title":"b. Measure as a Series of Measure Relations.","order":91,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDMA","text":"1. Wenn Etwas, das mit Anderm vereint wird, und ebenso dieß Andere nur durch die einfache Qualität bestimmt, das wäre, was es ist, so würden sie in dieser Verbindung nur sich aufheben, aber Etwas, das Maaßverhältniß in sich ist, ist selbstständig, aber dadurch zugleich vereinbar mit einem eben solchen; indem es in dieser Einheit aufgehoben wird, erhält es sich durch sein gleichgültiges, quantitatives Bestehen, und verhält sich zugleich als specificirendes Moment eines neuen Maaßverhältnisses. Seine Qualität ist eingehüllt in das Quantitative; damit ist sie ebenso gleichgültig gegen das andere Maaß, kontinuirt sich in dasselbe und in das neue gebildete Maaß hinein; der Exponent des neuen Maaßes ist selbst nur irgend ein Quantum, äußerliche Bestimmtheit; stellt sich als Gleichgültigkeit darin dar, daß das specifisch-bestimmte Etwas mit andern eben solchen Maaßen eben dergleichen Neutralisirungen der beiderseitigen Maaßverhältnisse eingeht; in nur Einem, von ihm und einem andern gebildeten, drückt sich seine specifische Eigenthümlichkeit nicht aus.\n\n2. Diese Verbindung mit Mehrern, die gleichfalls Maaße an ihnen sind, giebt verschiedene Verhältnisse, die also verschiedene Exponenten haben. Das Selbstständige hat den Exponenten seines An-sich-bestimmtseyns nur in der Vergleichung mit andern; die Neutralität mit andern aber macht seine reelle Vergleichung mit denselben aus; es ist seine Vergleichung mit ihnen durch sich selbst. Die Exponenten dieser Verhältnisse aber sind verschieden, und es stellt hiermit seinen qualitativen Exponenten als die—Reihe dieser verschiedenen Anzahlen dar, zu denen es die Einheit ist;—als eine Reihe von specifischem Verhalten zu Andern. Der qualitative Exponent als Ein unmittelbares Quantum drückt eine einzelne Relation aus. Wahrhaft unterscheidet sich das Selbstständige durch die eigenthümliche Reihe der Exponenten, die es, als Einheit angenommen, mit andern solchen Selbstständigen bildet, indem ein anderes derselben ebenso mit ebendenselben in Beziehung gebracht und als Einheit angenommen, eine andere Reihe formirt.—Das Verhältniß solcher Reihe innerhalb ihrer macht nun das Qualitative des Selbstständigen aus.\n\nInsofern nun solches Selbstständiges mit einer Reihe von Selbstständigen eine Reihe von Exponenten bildet, scheint es zunächst von einem Andern außer dieser Reihe selbst, mit welchem es verglichen wird, dadurch unterschieden zu seyn, daß dieses eine andere Reihe von Exponenten mit denselben Gegenüberstehenden macht. Aber auf diese Weise wären diese beiden Selbstständigen nicht vergleichbar, insofern jedes so als Einheit gegen seine Exponenten betrachtet wird, und die beiden aus dieser Beziehung entstehenden Reihen unbestimmt andere sind. Die beiden, die als Selbstständige verglichen werden sollen, sind zunächst gegen einander nur als Quanta unterschieden; ihr Verhältniß zu bestimmen, bedarf es selbst einer gemeinschaftlichen fürsichseyenden Einheit. Diese bestimmte Einheit ist nur in dem zu suchen, worin die zu vergleichenden, wie gezeigt, das specifische Daseyn ihres Maaßes haben, also in dem Verhältnisse, das die Verhältnissexponenten der Reihe zu einander haben. Dieß Verhältniß der Exponenten selbst ist aber nur so für sichseyende, in der That bestimmte Einheit, als die Glieder der Reihe dasselbe, als ein konstantes Verhältniß unter einander, zu beiden haben; so kann es ihre gemeinschaftliche Einheit seyn. In ihr also liegt allein die Vergleichbarkeit der beiden Selbstständigen, die als sich nicht mit einander neutralisirend, sondern als gleichgültig gegen einander angenommen wurden. Jedes abgesondert außerhalb der Vergleichung ist die Einheit der Verhältnisse mit den gegenüberstehenden Gliedern, welche die Anzahlen gegen jene Einheit sind, somit die Reihe von Exponenten vorstellen. Diese Reihe ist dagegen umgekehrt die Einheit für jene beiden, die verglichen miteinander, Quanta gegeneinander sind; als solche sind sie selbst verschiedene Anzahlen ihrer so eben aufgezeigten Einheit.\n\nDiejenigen aber ferner, welche mit den gegenüber stehenden unter sich verglichenen beiden oder vielmehr Vielen überhaupt, die Reihe der Exponenten des Verhaltens derselben abgeben, sind an ihnen selbst gleichfalls Selbstständige, jedes ein specifisches Etwas von einem ihm an sich zuständigen Maaßverhältniß. Sie sind insofern gleichfalls jedes als Einheit zu nehmen, so daß sie an den erst genannten unter sich bloß verglichenen Beiden oder vielmehr unbestimmt Mehrern eine Reihe von Exponenten haben, welche Exponenten die Vergleichungszahlen der so eben genannten unter sich sind; so wie die Vergleichungszahlen der nun einzeln auch als selbstständig genommenen unter sich gleichfalls umgekehrt die Reihe der Exponenten für die Glieder der ersten Reihe sind. Beide Seiten sind auf diese Weise Reihen, in denen jede Zahl erstens Einheit überhaupt ist gegen ihre gegenüber stehende Reihe, an der sie ihr Fürsichbestimmtseyn als eine Reihe von Exponenten hat; zweitens ist sie selbst einer der Exponenten für jedes Glied der gegenüberstehenden Reihe; und drittens Vergleichungszahl zu den übrigen Zahlen ihrer Reihe, und hat als solche Anzahl, die ihr auch als Exponent zukommt, ihre für-sich-bestimmte Einheit an der gegenüber stehenden Reihe.\n\n3. In diesem Verhalten ist die Art und Weise wieder gekehrt, wie das Quantum als fürsichseyend, nämlich als Grad gesetzt ist, einfach zu seyn, aber die Größebestimmtheit an einem außer ihm seyenden Quantum, das ein Kreis von Quantis ist, zu haben. Im Maaße aber ist dieß Äußerliche nicht bloß ein Quantum und ein Kreis voll Quantis, sondern eine Reihe von Verhältnißzahlen, und das Ganze derselben ist es, worin das Fürsich-bestimmtseyn des Maaßes liegt. Wie beim Fürsichseyn des Quantums als Grad der Fall ist, hat in diese Äußerlichkeit seiner selbst sich die Natur des selbstständigen Maaßes verkehrt. Seine Beziehung auf sich ist zunächst als unmittelbares Verhältniß, und damit besteht sogleich seine Gleichgültigkeit gegen Anderes nur in dem Quantum. In diese Äußerlichkeit fällt daher seine qualitative Seite, und sein Verhalten zu Anderem wird zu dem, was die specifische Bestimmung dieses Selbstständigen ausmacht. Sie besteht so schlechthin in der quantitativen Art und Weise dieses Verhaltens, und diese Art und Weise ist so sehr durch das Andere als durch es selbst bestimmt, und dieß Andere ist eine Reihe von Quantis, und es selbst gegenseitig ein solches. Aber diese Beziehung, in welcher sich zwei Specifische zu etwas, zu einem Dritten, dem Exponenten, specificiren, enthält ferner dieß, daß das Eine darin nicht in das Andere übergegangen, also nicht nur eine Negation überhaupt, sondern Beide darin negativ gesetzt sind, und indem jedes sich gleichgültig darin erhält, seine Negation auch wieder negirt ist. Diese ihre qualitative Einheit ist somit für sich seyende ausschließende Einheit. Die Exponenten, welche zunächst Vergleichungszahlen unter sich sind, haben in dem Momente des Ausschließens erst ihre wahrhaft specifische Bestimmtheit gegeneinander an ihnen und ihr Unterschied wird so zugleich qualitativer Natur. Er gründet sich aber auf das Quantitative; das Selbstständige verhält sich erstens nur darum zu einem Mehrern seiner qualitativ andern Seite, weil es in diesem Verhalten zugleich gleichgültig ist; zweitens ist nun die neutrale Beziehung durch die in ihr enthaltene Quantitativität nicht nur Veränderung, sondern als Negation der Negation gesetzt, und ausschließende Einheit. Dadurch ist die Verwandtschaft eines Selbstständigen zu den Mehrern der andern Seite nicht mehr eine indifferente Beziehung, sondern eine Wahlverwandtschaft.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0001","text":"1. Wenn Etwas, das mit Anderm vereint wird, und ebenso dieß Andere nur durch die einfache Qualität bestimmt, das wäre, was es ist, so würden sie in dieser Verbindung nur sich aufheben, aber Etwas, das Maaßverhältniß in sich ist, ist selbstständig, aber dadurch zugleich vereinbar mit einem eben solchen; indem es in dieser Einheit aufgehoben wird, erhält es sich durch sein gleichgültiges, quantitatives Bestehen, und verhält sich zugleich als specificirendes Moment eines neuen Maaßverhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"91.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0002","text":"Seine Qualität ist eingehüllt in das Quantitative; damit ist sie ebenso gleichgültig gegen das andere Maaß, kontinuirt sich in dasselbe und in das neue gebildete Maaß hinein; der Exponent des neuen Maaßes ist selbst nur irgend ein Quantum, äußerliche Bestimmtheit; stellt sich als Gleichgültigkeit darin dar, daß das specifisch-bestimmte Etwas mit andern eben solchen Maaßen eben dergleichen Neutralisirungen der beiderseitigen Maaßverhältnisse eingeht; in nur Einem, von ihm und einem andern gebildeten, drückt sich seine specifische Eigenthümlichkeit nicht aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"91.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0003","text":"2. Diese Verbindung mit Mehrern, die gleichfalls Maaße an ihnen sind, giebt verschiedene Verhältnisse, die also verschiedene Exponenten haben. Das Selbstständige hat den Exponenten seines An-sich-bestimmtseyns nur in der Vergleichung mit andern; die Neutralität mit andern aber macht seine reelle Vergleichung mit denselben aus; es ist seine Vergleichung mit ihnen durch sich selbst. Die Exponenten dieser Verhältnisse aber sind verschieden, und es stellt hiermit seinen qualitativen Exponenten als die—Reihe dieser verschiedenen Anzahlen dar, zu denen es die Einheit ist;—als eine Reihe von specifischem Verhalten zu Andern. Der qualitative Exponent als Ein unmittelbares Quantum drückt eine einzelne Relation aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"91.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0004","text":"Wahrhaft unterscheidet sich das Selbstständige durch die eigenthümliche Reihe der Exponenten, die es, als Einheit angenommen, mit andern solchen Selbstständigen bildet, indem ein anderes derselben ebenso mit ebendenselben in Beziehung gebracht und als Einheit angenommen, eine andere Reihe formirt.—Das Verhältniß solcher Reihe innerhalb ihrer macht nun das Qualitative des Selbstständigen aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"91.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0005","text":"Insofern nun solches Selbstständiges mit einer Reihe von Selbstständigen eine Reihe von Exponenten bildet, scheint es zunächst von einem Andern außer dieser Reihe selbst, mit welchem es verglichen wird, dadurch unterschieden zu seyn, daß dieses eine andere Reihe von Exponenten mit denselben Gegenüberstehenden macht. Aber auf diese Weise wären diese beiden Selbstständigen nicht vergleichbar, insofern jedes so als Einheit gegen seine Exponenten betrachtet wird, und die beiden aus dieser Beziehung entstehenden Reihen unbestimmt andere sind. Die beiden, die als Selbstständige verglichen werden sollen, sind zunächst gegen einander nur als Quanta unterschieden; ihr Verhältniß zu bestimmen, bedarf es selbst einer gemeinschaftlichen fürsichseyenden Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"91.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0006","text":"Diese bestimmte Einheit ist nur in dem zu suchen, worin die zu vergleichenden, wie gezeigt, das specifische Daseyn ihres Maaßes haben, also in dem Verhältnisse, das die Verhältnissexponenten der Reihe zu einander haben. Dieß Verhältniß der Exponenten selbst ist aber nur so für sichseyende, in der That bestimmte Einheit, als die Glieder der Reihe dasselbe, als ein konstantes Verhältniß unter einander, zu beiden haben; so kann es ihre gemeinschaftliche Einheit seyn. In ihr also liegt allein die Vergleichbarkeit der beiden Selbstständigen, die als sich nicht mit einander neutralisirend, sondern als gleichgültig gegen einander angenommen wurden. Jedes abgesondert außerhalb der Vergleichung ist die Einheit der Verhältnisse mit den gegenüberstehenden Gliedern, welche die Anzahlen gegen jene Einheit sind, somit die Reihe von Exponenten vorstellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"91.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0007","text":"Diese Reihe ist dagegen umgekehrt die Einheit für jene beiden, die verglichen miteinander, Quanta gegeneinander sind; als solche sind sie selbst verschiedene Anzahlen ihrer so eben aufgezeigten Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"91.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0008","text":"Diejenigen aber ferner, welche mit den gegenüber stehenden unter sich verglichenen beiden oder vielmehr Vielen überhaupt, die Reihe der Exponenten des Verhaltens derselben abgeben, sind an ihnen selbst gleichfalls Selbstständige, jedes ein specifisches Etwas von einem ihm an sich zuständigen Maaßverhältniß. Sie sind insofern gleichfalls jedes als Einheit zu nehmen, so daß sie an den erst genannten unter sich bloß verglichenen Beiden oder vielmehr unbestimmt Mehrern eine Reihe von Exponenten haben, welche Exponenten die Vergleichungszahlen der so eben genannten unter sich sind; so wie die Vergleichungszahlen der nun einzeln auch als selbstständig genommenen unter sich gleichfalls umgekehrt die Reihe der Exponenten für die Glieder der ersten Reihe sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"91.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0009","text":"Beide Seiten sind auf diese Weise Reihen, in denen jede Zahl erstens Einheit überhaupt ist gegen ihre gegenüber stehende Reihe, an der sie ihr Fürsichbestimmtseyn als eine Reihe von Exponenten hat; zweitens ist sie selbst einer der Exponenten für jedes Glied der gegenüberstehenden Reihe; und drittens Vergleichungszahl zu den übrigen Zahlen ihrer Reihe, und hat als solche Anzahl, die ihr auch als Exponent zukommt, ihre für-sich-bestimmte Einheit an der gegenüber stehenden Reihe.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"91.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0010","text":"3. In diesem Verhalten ist die Art und Weise wieder gekehrt, wie das Quantum als fürsichseyend, nämlich als Grad gesetzt ist, einfach zu seyn, aber die Größebestimmtheit an einem außer ihm seyenden Quantum, das ein Kreis von Quantis ist, zu haben. Im Maaße aber ist dieß Äußerliche nicht bloß ein Quantum und ein Kreis voll Quantis, sondern eine Reihe von Verhältnißzahlen, und das Ganze derselben ist es, worin das Fürsich-bestimmtseyn des Maaßes liegt. Wie beim Fürsichseyn des Quantums als Grad der Fall ist, hat in diese Äußerlichkeit seiner selbst sich die Natur des selbstständigen Maaßes verkehrt. Seine Beziehung auf sich ist zunächst als unmittelbares Verhältniß, und damit besteht sogleich seine Gleichgültigkeit gegen Anderes nur in dem Quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"91.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0011","text":"In diese Äußerlichkeit fällt daher seine qualitative Seite, und sein Verhalten zu Anderem wird zu dem, was die specifische Bestimmung dieses Selbstständigen ausmacht. Sie besteht so schlechthin in der quantitativen Art und Weise dieses Verhaltens, und diese Art und Weise ist so sehr durch das Andere als durch es selbst bestimmt, und dieß Andere ist eine Reihe von Quantis, und es selbst gegenseitig ein solches. Aber diese Beziehung, in welcher sich zwei Specifische zu etwas, zu einem Dritten, dem Exponenten, specificiren, enthält ferner dieß, daß das Eine darin nicht in das Andere übergegangen, also nicht nur eine Negation überhaupt, sondern Beide darin negativ gesetzt sind, und indem jedes sich gleichgültig darin erhält, seine Negation auch wieder negirt ist. Diese ihre qualitative Einheit ist somit für sich seyende ausschließende Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"91.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0012","text":"Die Exponenten, welche zunächst Vergleichungszahlen unter sich sind, haben in dem Momente des Ausschließens erst ihre wahrhaft specifische Bestimmtheit gegeneinander an ihnen und ihr Unterschied wird so zugleich qualitativer Natur. Er gründet sich aber auf das Quantitative; das Selbstständige verhält sich erstens nur darum zu einem Mehrern seiner qualitativ andern Seite, weil es in diesem Verhalten zugleich gleichgültig ist; zweitens ist nun die neutrale Beziehung durch die in ihr enthaltene Quantitativität nicht nur Veränderung, sondern als Negation der Negation gesetzt, und ausschließende Einheit. Dadurch ist die Verwandtschaft eines Selbstständigen zu den Mehrern der andern Seite nicht mehr eine indifferente Beziehung, sondern eine Wahlverwandtschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"91.12"}],"sha256":"66866bc5db83a66ecbf220512a64e6c556ad6fe62cc8c9958af87521a9807d7e","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104248102678Z_4b05c61e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Measure as a Series of Measure Relations.","source_sha256":"66866bc5db83a66ecbf220512a64e6c556ad6fe62cc8c9958af87521a9807d7e","sha256":"23920833f986bcdfef0ebe3ee9e0da377320d49d31777a562ef471f9727f77e6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:42:48.102713+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0001","text":"1. If Something which is combined with an Other, and likewise this Other, were what it is only through simple quality, then in this combination they would merely cancel themselves; but Something which is measure-relation within itself is self-subsistent, yet thereby at the same time combinable with another of the same kind; inasmuch as it is sublated in this unity, it preserves itself through its indifferent, quantitative subsistence, and at the same time relates as a specifying moment of a new measure-relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"91.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0002","text":"Its quality is enveloped in the quantitative; thereby it is likewise indifferent towards the other measure, continues into it and into the newly formed measure; the exponent of the new measure is itself only some quantum, external determinacy; it presents itself as indifference in the fact that the specifically determined Something enters, with other measures of the same kind, into similar neutralizations of the mutual measure-relations; in only one [measure], formed by it and another, its specific peculiarity does not express itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"91.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0003","text":"2. This combination with several others, which are likewise measures in themselves, yields different relations, which thus have different exponents. The self-subsistent has the exponent of its being-determined-in-itself only in comparison with others; but neutrality with others constitutes its real comparison with them; it is its comparison with them through itself. But the exponents of these relations are different, and it thereby presents its qualitative exponent as the—series of these different numbers, for which it is the unit;—as a series of specific comportment towards Others. The qualitative exponent as an immediate quantum expresses a single relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"91.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0004","text":"The self-subsistent is truly distinguished by the peculiar series of exponents which it forms, assumed as unit, with other such self-subsistents, whereas another of them, likewise brought into relation with precisely the same ones and assumed as unit, forms another series.—The relation of such a series within itself now constitutes the qualitative character of the self-subsistent.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"91.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0005","text":"Now insofar as such a self-subsistent forms, with a series of self-subsistents, a series of exponents, it seems at first to be distinguished from another outside this series itself, with which it is compared, by the fact that this one makes another series of exponents with the same counterparts. But in this way these two self-subsistents would not be comparable, insofar as each is thus considered as unit in relation to its exponents, and the two series arising from this relation are indeterminately other. The two which are to be compared as self-subsistents are at first distinguished from one another only as quanta; in order to determine their relation, there is need of a common unit which is itself being-for-self.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"91.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0006","text":"This determinate unit is to be sought only in that wherein the things to be compared, as has been shown, have the specific existence of their measure, thus in the relation which the relation-exponents of the series have to one another. But this relation of the exponents itself is a unit which is being-for-self, indeed determinate, only insofar as the members of the series have the same relation to both, as a constant relation among themselves; thus it can be their common unit. In it alone, therefore, lies the comparability of the two self-subsistents, which were assumed not to neutralize one another, but to be indifferent towards one another. Each, separately outside comparison, is the unit of the relations with the counterpart members, which are the numbers in relation to that unit, and thus represent the series of exponents.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"91.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0007","text":"This series, on the other hand, is conversely the unit for those two, which, compared with one another, are quanta in relation to one another; as such, they are themselves different numbers of their unit just indicated.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"91.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0008","text":"But those, furthermore, which, with the two—or rather, with the indeterminately many—counterparts compared among themselves, generally constitute the series of exponents of their comportment, are in themselves likewise self-subsistents, each a specific Something of a measure-relation pertaining to it in itself. Insofar, they too are each to be taken as unit, so that they have in the first-mentioned two, or rather indeterminately many, merely compared among themselves, a series of exponents; which exponents are the comparative numbers of those just mentioned among themselves; just as the comparative numbers of those now also individually taken as self-subsistent, among themselves, are likewise conversely the series of exponents for the members of the first series.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"91.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0009","text":"In this way both sides are series in which each number is, first, unit in general in relation to its counterpart series, in which it has its being-determined-for-self as a series of exponents; second, it is itself one of the exponents for each member of the counterpart series; and third, it is a comparative number in relation to the remaining numbers of its series, and as such a number, which also pertains to it as exponent, it has its unit determined-for-self in the counterpart series.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"91.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0010","text":"3. In this comportment there has returned the manner in which quantum, as being-for-self, namely as degree, is posited as simple, but has the determination of magnitude in a quantum external to it, which is a circle of quanta. In measure, however, this externality is not merely a quantum and a circle full of quanta, but a series of relation-numbers; and it is the whole of these in which the being-determined-for-self of measure lies. As is the case with the being-for-self of quantum as degree, the nature of self-subsistent measure has reversed itself into this externality of itself. Its relation to itself is at first an immediate relation, and with this its indifference towards Other is immediately present only in quantum.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"91.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0011","text":"Its qualitative side therefore falls into this externality, and its comportment towards Other becomes that which constitutes the specific determinacy of this self-subsistent. It thus consists absolutely in the quantitative manner of this comportment, and this manner is determined as much by the Other as by itself, and this Other is a series of quanta, and it itself reciprocally such a one. But this relation, in which two specific [entities] specify themselves into something, into a third, the exponent, further contains this: that the one has not therein passed over into the other, thus not merely a negation in general, but both are therein posited negatively, and, inasmuch as each preserves itself indifferently therein, its negation too is again negated. This their qualitative unity is thus a being-for-self, exclusive unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"91.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0012","text":"The exponents, which are at first comparative numbers among themselves, acquire only in the moment of exclusion their truly specific determinacy over against one another in themselves, and their difference thus simultaneously becomes qualitative in nature. But it is grounded in the quantitative; the self-subsistent relates, first, only for the reason that it is at the same time indifferent in this comportment, to a plurality of its qualitatively other side; second, the neutral relation is now, through the quantitative character contained in it, posited not merely as alteration but as negation of negation, and as exclusive unity. Thereby the affinity of a self-subsistent to the plurality of the other side is no longer an indifferent relation, but an elective affinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"91.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDMA:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"e3e955c4edcc73017ec7917d1c565ee03c7d2330ae0c2ec154fa2cd3310db692","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Das Maaß als Reihe von Maaßverhältnissen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Das Maaß als Reihe von Maaßverhältnissen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH","title":"c. Elective Affinity.","order":92,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CWAH","text":"Es ist hier der Ausdruck Wahlverwandtschaft, wie auch im vorhergehenden Neutralität, Verwandtschaft, gebraucht worden,— Ausdrücke, die sich auf das chemische Verhältniß beziehen. Denn in der chemischen Sphäre hat wesentlich das Materielle seine specifische Bestimmtheit in der Beziehung auf sein Anderes; es existirt nur als diese Differenz. Diese specifische Beziehung ist ferner an die Quantität gebunden, und ist zugleich nicht nur die Beziehung auf ein einzelnes Anderes, sondern auf eine Reihe solcher ihm gegenüberstehenden Differenten; die Verbindungen mit dieser Reihe beruhen auf einer sogenannten Verwandtschaft mit jedem Gliede derselben, aber bei dieser Gleichgültigkeit ist zugleich jede ausschließend gegen andere; welche Beziehung entgegengesetzter Bestimmungen noch zu betrachten ist.—Es ist aber nicht nur im Chemischen, daß sich das Specifische in einem Kreise von Verbindungen darstellt; auch der einzelne Ton hat erst seinen Sinn in dem Verhalten und der Verbindung mit einem andern und mit der Reihe von andern; die Harmonie oder Disharmonie in solchem Kreise von Verbindungen macht seine qualitative Natur aus, welche zugleich auf quantitativen Verhältnissen beruht, die eine Reihe von Exponenten bilden, und die Verhältnisse von den beiden specifischen Verhältnissen sind, die jeder der verbundenen Töne an ihm selbst ist. Der einzelne Ton ist der Grundton eines Systems, aber ebenso wieder einzelnes Glied im Systeme jedes andern Grundtons. Die Harmonien sind ausschließende Wahlverwandtschaften, deren qualitative Eigenthümlichkeit sich aber ebenso sehr wieder in die Äußerlichkeit bloß quantitativen Fortgehens auflöst.—Worin aber das Princip eines Maaßes für diejenigen Verwandtschaften, welche (chemische oder musikalische oder andere) Wahlverwandtschaften unter und gegen die andern sind, liege, darüber wird im Folgenden in Betreff der chemischen noch eine Bemerkung vorkommen; aber diese höhere Frage hängt mit dem Specifischen des eigentlichen Qualitativen aufs engste zusammen, und gehört in die besondern Theile der konkreten Naturwissenschaft.\n\nInsofern das Glied einer Reihe seine qualitative Einheit in seinem Verhalten zu dem Ganzen einer gegenüberstehenden Reihe hat, deren Glieder aber gegeneinander nur durch das Quantum, nach welchem sie sich mit jenem neutralisiren, verschieden sind, so ist die speciellere Bestimmtheit in dieser vielfachen Verwandtschaft gleichfalls nur eine quantitative. In der Wahlverwandtschaft als ausschließender, qualitativer Beziehung entnimmt das Verhalten sich diesem quantitativen Unterschiede. Die nächste Bestimmung, die sich darbietet, ist: daß nach dem Unterschied der Menge, also der extensiven Größe, der unter den Gliedern der einen Seite für die Neutralisirung eines Gliedes der andern Seite Statt findet, sich auch die Wahlverwandtschaft dieses Gliedes zu den Gliedern der andern Reihe, mit denen allen es in Verwandtschaft steht, richte. Das Ausschließen als ein festeres Zusammenhalten gegen andere Möglichkeiten der Verbindung, welches dadurch begründet wäre, erschiene so umgewandelt in um so viel größere Intensität, nach der früher nachgewiesenen Identität der Formen von extensiver und intensiver Größe, als in welchen beiden Formen die Größenbestimmtheit eine und dieselbe ist. Dieß Umschlagen der einseitigen Form der extensiven Größe auch in ihre andere, die intensive, ändert aber an der Natur der Grundbestimmung, welche das Eine und dasselbe Quantum ist, nichts; so daß hiermit in der That kein Ausschließen gesetzt wäre, sondern gleichgültig entweder nur Eine Verbindung oder ebensowohl eine Kombination unbestimmt von wie vielen Gliedern, wenn nur die Portionen, die von ihnen einträten, in Gemäßheit ihrer Verhältnisse untereinander dem geforderten Quantum entsprechend wären, Statt haben könnte.\n\nAllein die Verbindung, die wir auch Neutralisation genannt haben, ist nicht nur die Form der Intensität; der Exponent ist wesentlich Maaßbestimmung, und damit ausschließend; die Zahlen haben in dieser Seite ausschließenden Verhaltens ihre Kontinuität und Zusammenfließbarkeit mit einander verloren; es ist das Mehr oder Weniger, was einen negativen Charakter erhält, und der Vorzug, den ein Exponent gegen andere hat, bleibt nicht in der Größenbestimmtheit stehen. Ebenso sehr ist aber auch diese andere Seite vorhanden, nach welcher es einem Momente wieder gleichgültig ist von mehrern ihm gegenüber stehenden Momenten das neutralisirende Quantum zu erhalten, von jedem nach seiner specifischen Bestimmtheit gegen das Andere; das ausschließende, negative Verhalten leidet zugleich diesen Eintrag von der quantitativen Seite her.—Es ist hiermit ein Umschlagen von gleichgültigem, bloß quantitativem Verhalten in ein qualitatives und umgekehrt ein Übergehen des specifischen Bestimmtseyns in das bloß äußerliche Verhältniß gesetzt;—eine Reihe von Verhältnissen, die bald bloß quantitativer Natur, bald specifische und Maaße sind.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0001","text":"Es ist hier der Ausdruck Wahlverwandtschaft, wie auch im vorhergehenden Neutralität, Verwandtschaft, gebraucht worden,— Ausdrücke, die sich auf das chemische Verhältniß beziehen. Denn in der chemischen Sphäre hat wesentlich das Materielle seine specifische Bestimmtheit in der Beziehung auf sein Anderes; es existirt nur als diese Differenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"92.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0002","text":"Diese specifische Beziehung ist ferner an die Quantität gebunden, und ist zugleich nicht nur die Beziehung auf ein einzelnes Anderes, sondern auf eine Reihe solcher ihm gegenüberstehenden Differenten; die Verbindungen mit dieser Reihe beruhen auf einer sogenannten Verwandtschaft mit jedem Gliede derselben, aber bei dieser Gleichgültigkeit ist zugleich jede ausschließend gegen andere; welche Beziehung entgegengesetzter Bestimmungen noch zu betrachten ist.—Es ist aber nicht nur im Chemischen, daß sich das Specifische in einem Kreise von Verbindungen darstellt; auch der einzelne Ton hat erst seinen Sinn in dem Verhalten und der Verbindung mit einem andern und mit der Reihe von andern; die Harmonie oder Disharmonie in solchem Kreise von Verbindungen macht seine qualitative Natur aus, welche zugleich auf quantitativen Verhältnissen beruht, die eine Reihe von Exponenten bilden, und die","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"92.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0003","text":"Verhältnisse von den beiden specifischen Verhältnissen sind, die jeder der verbundenen Töne an ihm selbst ist. Der einzelne Ton ist der Grundton eines Systems, aber ebenso wieder einzelnes Glied im Systeme jedes andern Grundtons. Die Harmonien sind ausschließende Wahlverwandtschaften, deren qualitative Eigenthümlichkeit sich aber ebenso sehr wieder in die Äußerlichkeit bloß quantitativen Fortgehens auflöst.—Worin aber das Princip eines Maaßes für diejenigen Verwandtschaften, welche (chemische oder musikalische oder andere) Wahlverwandtschaften unter und gegen die andern sind, liege, darüber wird im Folgenden in Betreff der chemischen noch eine Bemerkung vorkommen; aber diese höhere Frage hängt mit dem Specifischen des eigentlichen Qualitativen aufs engste zusammen, und gehört in die besondern Theile der konkreten Naturwissenschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"92.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0004","text":"Insofern das Glied einer Reihe seine qualitative Einheit in seinem Verhalten zu dem Ganzen einer gegenüberstehenden Reihe hat, deren Glieder aber gegeneinander nur durch das Quantum, nach welchem sie sich mit jenem neutralisiren, verschieden sind, so ist die speciellere Bestimmtheit in dieser vielfachen Verwandtschaft gleichfalls nur eine quantitative. In der Wahlverwandtschaft als ausschließender, qualitativer Beziehung entnimmt das Verhalten sich diesem quantitativen Unterschiede. Die nächste Bestimmung, die sich darbietet, ist: daß nach dem Unterschied der Menge, also der extensiven Größe, der unter den Gliedern der einen Seite für die Neutralisirung eines Gliedes der andern Seite Statt findet, sich auch die Wahlverwandtschaft dieses Gliedes zu den Gliedern der andern Reihe, mit denen allen es in Verwandtschaft steht, richte.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"92.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0005","text":"Das Ausschließen als ein festeres Zusammenhalten gegen andere Möglichkeiten der Verbindung, welches dadurch begründet wäre, erschiene so umgewandelt in um so viel größere Intensität, nach der früher nachgewiesenen Identität der Formen von extensiver und intensiver Größe, als in welchen beiden Formen die Größenbestimmtheit eine und dieselbe ist. Dieß Umschlagen der einseitigen Form der extensiven Größe auch in ihre andere, die intensive, ändert aber an der Natur der Grundbestimmung, welche das Eine und dasselbe Quantum ist, nichts; so daß hiermit in der That kein Ausschließen gesetzt wäre, sondern gleichgültig entweder nur Eine Verbindung oder ebensowohl eine Kombination unbestimmt von wie vielen Gliedern, wenn nur die Portionen, die von ihnen einträten, in Gemäßheit ihrer Verhältnisse untereinander dem geforderten Quantum entsprechend wären, Statt haben könnte.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"92.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0006","text":"Allein die Verbindung, die wir auch Neutralisation genannt haben, ist nicht nur die Form der Intensität; der Exponent ist wesentlich Maaßbestimmung, und damit ausschließend; die Zahlen haben in dieser Seite ausschließenden Verhaltens ihre Kontinuität und Zusammenfließbarkeit mit einander verloren; es ist das Mehr oder Weniger, was einen negativen Charakter erhält, und der Vorzug, den ein Exponent gegen andere hat, bleibt nicht in der Größenbestimmtheit stehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"92.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0007","text":"Ebenso sehr ist aber auch diese andere Seite vorhanden, nach welcher es einem Momente wieder gleichgültig ist von mehrern ihm gegenüber stehenden Momenten das neutralisirende Quantum zu erhalten, von jedem nach seiner specifischen Bestimmtheit gegen das Andere; das ausschließende, negative Verhalten leidet zugleich diesen Eintrag von der quantitativen Seite her.—Es ist hiermit ein Umschlagen von gleichgültigem, bloß quantitativem Verhalten in ein qualitatives und umgekehrt ein Übergehen des specifischen Bestimmtseyns in das bloß äußerliche Verhältniß gesetzt;—eine Reihe von Verhältnissen, die bald bloß quantitativer Natur, bald specifische und Maaße sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"92.7"}],"sha256":"ed6ae03b79a3f012f1d6b8da8e807adb15ec5d0281523914f40be100ab94b3f0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104259140125Z_b984d07b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Elective Affinity.","source_sha256":"ed6ae03b79a3f012f1d6b8da8e807adb15ec5d0281523914f40be100ab94b3f0","sha256":"0eb3e3d7a37699961ece1954bebc75bc7d4450007f100f78abf470572b557618","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:42:59.140144+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0001","text":"Here the expression elective affinity, as also previously neutrality, affinity, has been used,—expressions which refer to the chemical relation. For in the chemical sphere it is essentially the material that has its specific determinacy in relation to its other; it exists only as this difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"92.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0002","text":"This specific relation is further bound to quantity, and is at the same time not merely the relation to a single other, but to a series of such different things confronting it; the combinations with this series rest upon a so-called affinity with each member of it, but within this indifference each is at the same time exclusive against the others; which relation of opposed determinations is yet to be considered.—But it is not only in the chemical sphere that the specific presents itself in a circle of combinations; the individual tone, too, first has its sense in its comportment and combination with another and with the series of others; harmony or disharmony in such a circle of combinations constitutes its qualitative nature, which at the same time rests upon quantitative relations, which form a series of exponents, and which","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"92.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0003","text":"are relations of the two specific relations that each of the combined tones is in itself. The individual tone is the fundamental tone of a system, but equally again an individual member in the system of every other fundamental tone. Harmonies are exclusive elective affinities, whose qualitative peculiarity, however, likewise dissolves again into the externality of merely quantitative progression.—But wherein the principle of a measure for those affinities which are (chemical or musical or other) elective affinities among and against the others lies, a remark will occur below with respect to the chemical ones; yet this higher question is most closely connected with the specificity of the properly qualitative, and belongs to the particular parts of concrete natural science.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"92.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0004","text":"In so far as the member of a series has its qualitative unity in its comportment toward the whole of an opposing series, whose members, however, differ from one another only through the quantum according to which they neutralize themselves with that member, the more specific determinacy in this manifold affinity is likewise only a quantitative one. In elective affinity as an exclusive, qualitative relation, comportment derives from this quantitative difference. The next determination that presents itself is this: that, according to the difference of amount, thus of extensive magnitude, which obtains among the members of the one side for the neutralization of one member of the other side, the elective affinity of this member toward the members of the other series, with all of which it stands in affinity, should also be directed.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"92.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0005","text":"Exclusion, as a firmer holding-together against other possibilities of combination, which would thereby be grounded, would thus appear transformed into so much greater intensity, according to the previously demonstrated identity of the forms of extensive and intensive magnitude, in both of which forms the determinacy of magnitude is one and the same. But this transition of the one-sided form of extensive magnitude into its other form, the intensive, changes nothing in the nature of the fundamental determination, which is one and the same quantum; so that thereby in fact no exclusion would be posited, but indifferently either only one combination or just as well a combination of indeterminately many members, provided only that the portions contributed by them corresponded, in conformity with their relations to one another, to the required quantum, could take place.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"92.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0006","text":"Yet the combination, which we have also called neutralization, is not merely the form of intensity; the exponent is essentially a determination of measure, and thereby exclusive; on this side of exclusive comportment, the numbers have lost their continuity and their capacity to flow together with one another; it is the more or less that receives a negative character, and the preference that one exponent has over others does not remain within determinacy of magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"92.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0007","text":"But equally there is also this other side, according to which it is again indifferent to one moment to receive the neutralizing quantum from several moments confronting it, from each according to its specific determinacy toward the other; the exclusive, negative comportment at the same time suffers this impairment from the quantitative side.—There is thereby posited a transition of indifferent, merely quantitative comportment into a qualitative one and, conversely, a passing-over of specific determinacy into the merely external relation;—a series of relations that are now of a merely quantitative nature, now specific and measures.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"92.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWAH:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"69f7a9148efb8c00818d3a98eba6da2a7ead8f5106b6265b2abc0f711c49fd07","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Wahlverwandtschaft."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Wahlverwandtschaft.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23","title":"Remark.","order":93,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_23","text":"Die chemischen Stoffe sind die eigenthümlichsten Beispiele solcher Maaße, welche Maaßmomente sind, die dasjenigr, was ihre Bestimmung ausmacht, allein im Verhalten zu andern haben. Säuren und Kalien oder Basen überhaupt erscheinen als unmittelbar an sich bestimmte Dinge, aber vielmehr als unvollkommene Körperelemente, als Bestandtheile, die eigentlich nicht für sich existiren, sondern nur diese Existenz haben, ihr isolirtes Bestehen aufzuheben und sich mit einem andern zu verbinden. Der Unterschied ferner, wodurch sie als selbstständige sind, besteht nicht in dieser unmittelbaren Qualität, sondern in der quantitativen Art und Weise des Verhaltens. Er ist nämlich nicht auf den chemischen Gegensatz von Säure und Kali oder Basis überhaupt, eingeschränkt, sondern ist zu einem Maaße der Sättigung specificirt, und besteht in der specifischen Bestimmtheit der Quantität der sich neutralisirenden Stoffe. Diese Quantitäts-Bestimmung in Rücksicht auf die Sättigung macht die qualitative Natur eines Stoffes aus, sie macht ihn zu dem, was er für sich ist, und die Zahl, die dieß ausdrückt, ist wesentlich einer von mehrern Exponenten für eine gegenüber stehende Einheit.—Solcher Stoff steht mit einem andern in sogenannter Verwandtschafft; insofern diese Beziehung rein qualitativer Natur bliebe, so wäre,—wie die Beziehung der magnetischen Pole oder der Elektricitäten,—die eine Bestimmtheit nur die negative der andern, und beide Seiten zeigten sich nicht auch zugleich gleichgültig gegeneinander. Aber weil die Beziehung auch quantitativer Natur ist, ist jeder dieser Stoffe fähig mit Mehrern sich zu neutralisiren, und nicht auf einen gegenüber stehenden eingeschränkt. Es verhält sich nicht nur die Säure und das Kali oder Basis, sondern Säuren und Kalien oder Basen zu einander. Sie charakterisiren sich zunächst dadurch gegen einander, je nachdem eine Säure z.B. von einem Kali mehr bedarf um sich mit ihm zu sättigen, als eine andere. Aber die fürsichseyende Selbstständigkeit zeigt sich darin, daß die Verwandtschaften sich ausschließend verhalten und eine vor der andern den Vorzug hat, indem für sich eine Säure mit allen Kalien, und umgekehrt, eine Verbindung eingehen kann. Es macht so den Hauptunterschied einer Säure gegen eine andere aus, ob sie zu einer Basis eine nähere Verwandtschaft habe, als eine andere, d. i. eine sogenannte Wahlverwandschaft.\n\nÜber die chemischen Verwandtschaften der Säuren und Kalien ist das Gesetz gefunden worden, daß wenn zwei neutrale Solutionen gemischt werden, wodurch eine Scheidung und daraus zwei neue Verbindungen entstehen, diese Produkte gleichfalls neutral sind. Es folgt hieraus, daß die Mengen von zwei kalischen Basen, die zur Sättigung einer Säure erfordert werden, in demselben Verhältnisse zur Sättigung einer andern nöthig sind; überhaupt wenn für ein Kali als Einheit genommen die Reihe der Verhältnißzahlen bestimmt worden ist, in denen die verschiedenen Säuren dasselbe sättigen, so ist für jedes andere Kali diese Reihe dieselbe, nur daß die verschiedenen Kalien gegen einander in verschiedenen Anzahlen zu nehmen sind;—Anzahlen, die wieder ihrer Seits eine eben solche beständige Reihe von Exponenten für jede der gegenüber stehenden Säuren bilden, indem sie ebenso zujeder einzelnen Säure sich in demselben Verhältnisse beziehen, als zujeder andern. —Fischer hat zuerst diese Reihen aus den richterischen Arbeiten in ihrer Einfachheit herausgehoben; s. in s. Anmerkungen zur Übersetzung von Berthollets Abhandlung über die Gesetze der Verwandtschaft in der Chemie, S. 232. und Berthollet Statique chimique I. Part. p. 134. ff.—Die, seit dieß zuerst geschrieben worden, nach allen Seiten hin so sehr ausgebildete Kenntniß von den Verhältnißzahlen der Mischungen der chemischen Elemente, hier berücksichtigen zu wollen, würde auch darum eine Abschweifung seyn, da diese empirische zu einem Theil aber auch nur hypothetische Erweiterung innerhalb derselben Begriffsbestimmungen eingeschlossen bleibt. Aber über die dabei gebrauchten Kategorien, ferner über die Ansichten der chemischen Wahlverwandtschaft selbst und ihrer Beziehung auf das Quantitative, so wie über den Versuch, dieselbe auf bestimmte physikalische Qualitäten zu gründen, mögen noch einige Bemerkungen hinzugefügt werden.\n\nBekanntlich hat Berthollet die allgemeine Vorstellung von der Wahlverwandtschaft durch den Begriff von der Wirksamkeit einer chemischen Masse modificirt. Diese Modification hat, was wohl zu unterscheiden ist, auf die Quantitäts-Verhältnisse der chemischen Sättigungs-Gesetze selbst keinen Einfluß, aber das qualitative Moment der ausschließenden Wahlverwandtschaft als solcher wird nicht nur geschwächt, sondern vielmehr aufgehoben. Wenn zwei Säuren auf ein Kali wirken, und diejenige, von welcher gesagt wird, daß sie eine größere Verwandtschaft zu derselben habe, auch in dem Quantum vorhanden ist, welches fähig ist, das Quantum der Basis zu sättigen, so erfolgt nach der Vorstellung der Wahlverwandtschaft nur diese Sättigung; die andere Säure bleibt ganz unwirksam und von der neutralen Verbindung ausgeschlossen. Nach jenem Begriffe der Wirksamkeit einer chemischen Masse hingegen, ist jede von beiden wirksam in einem Verhältniß, das aus ihrer vorhandenen Menge und ihrer Sättigungsfähigkeit oder sogenannten Affinität zusammengesetzt ist. Berthollets Untersuchungen haben die nähern Umstände angegeben, unter welchen die Wirksamkeit der chemischen Masse aufgehoben wird, und eine (stärker verwandte) Säure die andere (schwächere) auszutreiben und deren Wirkung auszuschließen, somit nach dem Sinne der Wahlverwandtschaft thätig zu seyn scheint. Er hat gezeigt, daß es Umstände, wie die Stärke der Kohäsion, Unauflösbarkeit der gebildeten Salze im Wasser, sind, unter welchen jenes Ausschließen Statt findet, nicht die qualitative Natur der Agentien als solche, —Umstände, welche wieder durch andere Umstände z.B. die Temperatur in ihrer Wirkung aufgehoben werden können. Mit der Beseitigung dieser Hindernisse tritt die chemische Masse unverkümmert in Wirksamkeit, und das, was als rein qualitatives Ausschließen, als Wahlverwandtschaft erschien, zeigt sich nur in äußerlichen Modifikationen zu liegen.\n\nBerzelius wäre es vornehmlich, der weiter über diesen Gegenstand zu hören ist. Derselbe stellt aber in seinem Lehrbuche der Chemie über die Sache nichts Eigenthümliches und Bestimmteres auf. Es sind die berthollet'schen Ansichten aufgenommen und wörtlich wiederhohlt, nur mit der eigenthümlichen Metaphysik einer unkritischen Reflexion ausstaffirt worden, deren Kategorien also allein sich für die nähere Betrachtung darbieten. Die Theorie geht über die Erfahrung hinaus, und erfindet Theils sinnliche Vorstellungen, wie sie nicht selbst in der Erfahrung gegeben sind, Theils wendet sie Denkbestimmungen an, und macht sich auf beide Weise zum Gegenstande logischer Kritik. Wir wollen daher das in jenem Lehrbuche selbst III. Band I. Abth. (übers. von Wöhler S. 82. ff) über die Theorie Vorgetragene vornehmen. Daselbst nun liest man, \"daß man sich vorstellen müsse, in einer gleichförmig gemischten Flüssigkeit sey ein jedes Atom vom aufgelösten Körper von einer gleichen Anzahl von Atomen des Auflösungsmittels umgeben; und wenn mehrere Substanzen zusammen aufgelöst sind, so müssen sie die Zwischenräume zwischen den Atomen des Auflösungsmittels unter sich theilen, so daß, bei einer gleichförmigen Mischung der Flüssigkeit, eine solche Symmetrie in der Lage der Atome entstehe, daß alle Atome der einzelnen Körper sich in Beziehung zu den Atomen der andern Körper in einer gleichförmigen Lage befinden; man könne daher sagen, daß die Auflösung durch die Symmetrie in der Stellung der Atome, so wie die Verbindung durch die bestimmten Proportionen charakterisirt sey.\"—Dieß wird hierauf durch ein Beispiel der Verbindungen erläutert, die aus einer Auflösung von Kupferchlorid, zu welcher Schwefelsäure hinzugesetzt wird, entstehen; aber an diesem Beispiele wird freilich weder aufgezeigt, daß Atome existiren, noch daß eine Anzahl von Atomen der aufgelösten Körper Atome der Flüssigkeit umgeben, freie Atome der beiden Säuren sich um die (mit dem Kupferoxid) verbunden bleibenden lagern, noch daß die Symmetrie in der Stellung und Lage, noch daß Zwischenräume zwischen den Atomen existiren,—am allerwenigsten daß die aufgelösten Substanzen die Zwischenräume der Atome des Auflösungsmittels unter sich theilen. Dieß hiesse, daß die aufgelösten da ihre Stellung nehmen, wo das Auflösungsmittel nicht ist,—denn die Zwischenräume desselben sind die von ihm leeren Räume,—somit daß die aufgelösten Substanzen sich nicht im Auflösungsmittel befinden, sondern wenn auch dasselbe umgebend und umlagernd, oder von demselben umgeben und umlagert,—außerhalb desselben, also gewiß auch von ihm nicht aufgelöst sind. Man sieht somit nicht ein, daß man sich solche Vorstellungen machen müsse, welche in der Erfahrung nicht aufgezeigt sind, im Wesentlichen sich sogleich widersprechen, und sonst auf andere Weise nicht erhärtet sind. Dieß könnte nur durch die Betrachtung dieser Vorstellungen selbst, d. i. durch Metaphysik, welche Logik ist, geschehen, durch diese aber werden sie so wenig als durch die Erfahrung bestätigt,—im Gegentheil!—Übrigens giebt Berzelius zu, was auch oben gesagt worden, daß die Sätze Berthollets der Theorie von den bestimmten Proportionen nicht entgegen seyen,—er fügt freilich hinzu, daß sie auch den Ansichten von der Korpuskularphilosophie, d. i. der vorhin angeführten Vorstellungen von den Atomen, der Erfüllung der Zwischenräume der auflösenden Flüssigkeit durch die Atome der festen Körper u.s.f. nicht entgegen seyen,—diese letztere grundlose Metaphysik hat aber wesentlich nichts mit den Proportionen der Sättigung selbst zu thun. Das Specifische, was in den Sättigungsgesetzen ausgedrückt ist, betrifft somit nur die Menge von selbst quantitativen Einheiten (nicht Atomen) eines Körpers, mit welcher sich die quantitative Einheit (ebenso wenig ein Atom) eines andern gegen erstern chemisch differenten Körpers neutralisirt; die Verschiedenheit besteht allein in diesen verschiedenen Proportionen. Wenn dann Berzelius, ungeachtet seine Proportionenlehre ganz nur eine Bestimmung von Mengen ist, doch auch von Affinitätsgraden spricht, z.B. S. 86. indem er die chemische Masse Berthollets als die Summe des Affinitätsgrades aus der vorhandenen Quantität des wirksamen Körpers erklärt, statt dessen Berthollet consequenter den Ausdruck capacité de saturation gebraucht, so verfällt er damit selbst in die Form intensiver Größe. Dieß ist aber die Form, welche das Eigenthümliche der sogenannten dynamischen Philosophie ausmacht, die er früher S. 29. a. a. O. \"die speculative Philosophie gewisser deutschen Schulen\" nennt, und zum Besten der vortrefflichen \"Korpuskularphilosophie\" nachdrücklich verwirft. Von dieser dynamischen Philosophie giebt er dort an, daß sie annehme, die Elemente in ihrer chemischen Vereinigung durchdringen sich, und die Neutralisation bestehe in dieser gegenseitigen Durchdringung; dieß heißt nichts Anders, als daß die chemisch differenten Partikeln, die als Menge gegeneinander sind, in die Einfachheit einer intensiven Größe zusammengehen, was sich auch als Verminderung des Volums kund giebt. Dagegen sollen in der Korpuskulartheorie auch die chemisch verbundenen Atome sich in den Zwischenräumen, d. h. außereinander erhalten, (Juxtaposition); Grad der Affinität hat in solchem Verhalten als einer nur extensiven Größe, eines Perennirens von Menge, keinen Sinn. Wenn ebendas angegeben wird, daß die Erscheinungen der bestimmten Proportionen für die dynamische Ansicht ganz unvorgesehen gekommen seyen, so wäre dieß nur ein äußerlicher historischer Umstand, abgesehen davon, daß die richterschen stöchiometrischen Reihen, in der fischerschen Zusammenstellung bereits Berthollet bekannt und in der ersten Ausg. dieser Logik, welche die Nichtigkeit der Kategorien erweist, auf denen die alte wie die neuseynwolleude Korpuskulartheorie beruht, angeführt sind. Irrthümlich aber urtheilt Berzelius als ob unter der Herrschaft \"der dynamischen Ansicht\" die Erscheinungen der bestimmten Proportionen \"für immer\" unbekannt geblieben wären,—in dem Sinne, daß jene Ansicht sich nicht mit der Bestimmtheit der Proportionen vertrüge. Diese ist auf allen Fall nur Größebestimmtheit, gleichgültig ob in extensiver und intensiver Form, —so daß auch Berzelius, so sehr er an der erstern Form, der Menge, hängt, selbst die Vorstellung von Affinitätsgraden gebraucht.\n\nIndem hiermit die Verwandschaft auf den quantitativen Unterschied zurückgeführt ist, ist sie als Wahlverwandschaft aufgehoben; das Ausschließende aber, das bei derselben Statt findet, ist auf Umstände zurückgeführt, d. i. auf Bestimmungen, welche als etwas der Verwandschaft Äußerliches erscheinen, auf Kohäsion, Unauflöslichkeit der zu Stande gekommenen Verbindungen u.s.f. Es kann mit dieser Vorstellung zum Theil das Verfahren bei der Betrachtung der Wirkung der Schwere verglichen werden, wo das, was an sich der Schwere selbst zukommt, daß der bewegte Pendel durch sie nothwendig zur Ruhe übergeht, nur als der zugleich vorhandene Umstand des äußern Widerstands der Luft des Fadens u.s.f. genommen und der Reibung allein statt der Schwere zugeschrieben wird.—Hier für die Natur des Qualitativen, welches in der Wahlverwandschaft liegt, macht es keinen Unterschied, ob dasselbe in der Form jener Umstände als seiner Bedingungen erscheint und aufgefaßt wird. Es beginnt mit dem Qualitativen als solchen eine neue Ordnung, deren Specifikation nicht mehr nur quantitativer Unterschied ist.\n\nWenn nun sonach der Unterschied der chemischen Affinität in einer Reihe quantitativer Verhältnisse sich genau feststellt gegen die Wahlverwandsehaft als eintretender qualitativer Bestimmtheit, deren Verhalten mit jener Ordnung keineswegs zusammenfällt, so wird dieser Unterschied wieder in völlige Verwirrung durch die Art geworfen, in welcher mit dem chemischen Verhalten das elektrische in neuern Zeiten in Verbindung gebracht wird, und die Hoffnung von diesem tiefer seyn sollenden Princip aus über das wichtigste, das Maaßverhältniß, einen Aufschluß zu erhalten, wird gänzlich getäuscht. Diese Theorie, in welcher die Erscheinungen der Elektricität und des Chemismus vollkommen identificirt werden, insofern sie das Physikalische und nicht bloß die Maaßverhältnisse betrifft, ist hier nicht in nähere Betrachtung zu nehmen, und nur insofern zu erwähnen, als die Unterschiedenheit der Maaßbestimmungen dadurch verworren wird. Für sich selbst ist sie seicht zu nennen, weil die Seichtigkeit darin besteht, das Verschiedene mit Weglassung der Verschiedenheit identisch zu nehmen. War hierbei die Affinität betrifft, so ist sie, indem so chemische Processe mit elektrischen, ingleichen mit Feuer und Licht-Erscheinungen, identificirt werden, \"auf Neutralisation entgegengesetzter Electricitäten\" reducirt worden. Die Identifikation der Elektricität und des Chemismus selbst ist es beinahe komisch (S. 63. a. a. O.) in folgender Weise dargestellt zu finden, daß \"die eletrischen Phänomene wohl die Wirkung der Körper auf größern oder geringern Abstand, ihre Anziehung vor der Vereinigung (d. i. das noch nicht chemische Verhalten)—und das durch diese Vereinigung entstehende Feuer (?) wohl erklären, aber uns über die Ursache der mit einer so großen Kraft, nach Vernichtung des entgegengesetzten elektrischen Zustandes, fortdauernden Vereinigung der Körper keinen Aufschluß geben;\" d. h. die Theorie giebt den Aufschluß, daß die Electricität die Ursache des chemischen Verhaltens sey, daß aber die Electricität über das, was im chemischen Processe chemisch ist, keinen Aufschluß gebe.—Damit, daß die chemische Differenz überhaupt auf den Gegensatz positiver und negativer Elektricität zurückgeführt wird, wird die Affinitätsverschiedenheit der auf die eine und auf die andere Seite fallenden Agentien unter sich als die Ordnung von zwei Reihen elektropositiver und elektronegativer Körper bestimmt. Bei dem Identificiren der Elektricität und des Chemismus ihrer allgemeinen Bestimmung nach, wird schon dieß übersehen, daß die erstere überhaupt und deren Neutralisirung flüchtig ist und der Qualität der Körper äußerlich bleibt, der Chemismus in seiner Aktion und besonders in der Neutralisation die ganze qualitative Natur der Körper in Anspruch nimmt und alterirt. Ebenso flüchtig ist innerhalb der Elektricität ihr Gegensatz von positiver und negativer; er ist ein so Unstätes, daß er von den geringsten äußerlichen Umständen abhängig ist, und in keinen Vergleich gestellt werden kann mit der Bestimmtheit und Festigkeit des Gegensatzes von Säuren z.B. gegen die Metalle u.s.w. Die Veränderlichkeit, die in diesem chemischen Verhalten, durch höchst gewaltsame Einwirkungen z.B. einer erhöhten Temperatur u.s.f. statt finden kann, steht in keinem Vergleich mit der Oberflächlichkeit des elektrischen Gegensatzes. Der fernere Unterschied nun innerhalb der Reihe jeder der beiden Seiten zwischen mehr oder weniger positiv-elektrischer, oder mehr oder weniger negativ-elektrischer Beschaffenheit, ist vollends sowohl ein völlig Unsicheres als Unkonstatirtes. Aus diesen Reihen der Körper aber (Berzelius am ang. Ort S. 64. f.) \"nach ihren elektrischen Dispositionen soll das elektrochemische System entstehen, welches sich von allen am besten eigne, eine Idee voll der Chemie zu geben;\" diese Reihen werden nun angegeben; wie sie aber in der That beschaffen sind, darüber wird S. 67. hinzugefügt:\n\n\"daß dieß ungefähr die Ordnung dieser Körper sey, aber diese Materie sey so wenig untersucht, daß sich noch nichts ganz Gewisses hinsichtlich dieser relativen Ordnung bestimmen lasse.\"—Sowohl die Verhältnißzahlen jener (von Richter zuerst gemachten) Affinitätsreihen, als die höchst interessante von Berzelius aufgestellte Reduktion der Verbindungen von zwei Körpern auf die Einfachheit weniger quantitativen Verhältnisse sind ganz und gar unabhängig von jenem elektrochemisch seyn sollenden Gebräue. Wenn in jenen Proportionen und in deren seit Richter nach allen Seiten hin gewonnenen Ausdehnung der experimentale Weg der richtige Leitstern gewesen, so kontrastirt für sich damit umsomehr die Vermischung dieser großen Entdeckungen mit der außer dem Weg der Erfahrung liegenden Öde der sogenannten Korpuskulartheorie; nur dieser Anfang, das Princip der Erfahrung zu verlassen, konnte es motiviren, noch weiter jenen früher von Ritter vornehmlich angefangenen Einfall wieder aufzunehmen, feste Ordnungen von elektropositiven und elektronegativen Körpern, die zugleich chemische Bedeutung haben sollten, aufzustellen.\n\nSchon die Nichtigkeit der Grundlage, die für die chemische Affinität in dem Gegensatze von elektropositiven und elektronegativen Körpern, wenn dieser für sieh auch faktisch richtiger wäre, als er ist, angenommen wird, zeigt sich bald selbst auf dem experimentalen Wege, was denn aber wieder zu weiterer Inkonsequenz führt. Es wird S. 73. (a. a. O.) zugestanden, daß zwei sogenannte elektronegative Körper, wie Schwefel und Sauerstoff auf eine viel innigere Art sich mit einander verbinden, als z.B. der Sauerstoff und das Kupfer, obgleich letzteres elektropositiv sey. Die auf den allgemeinen Gegensatz von positiver und negativer-Elektricität basirte Grundlage für die Affinität muß hier hiermit gegen ein bloßes Mehr oder Weniger innerhalb Einer und derselben Reihe von elektrischer Bestimmtheit zurückgestellt werden. Der Verwandschaftsgrad der Körper, wird nun hieraus geschlossen, hänge demnach nicht allein von ihrer specifischen Unipolarität (mit welcher Hypothese diese Bestimmung zusammenhängt, thut hierher nichts, sie gilt hier nur für das Entweder des Positiven und das Oder des Negativen) ab; der Verwandschaftsgrad müsse hauptsächlich von der Intensität ihrer Polarität im Allgemeinen hergeleitet werden. Hier geht somit näher die Betrachtung der Affinität zu dem Verhältniß der Wahlverwandschaft über, um die uns vornehmlich zu thun ist; sehen wir, was sich denn für diese nun ergiebt. Indem sogleich (ebendas. S. 73.) zugestanden wird, daß der Grad dieser Polarität, wenn sie nicht bloß in unserer Vorstellung existire, keine konstante Quantität zu seyn scheine, sondern sehr von der Temperatur abhänge, so findet sich nach allem diesem als Resultat angegeben, nicht nur, daß jede chemische Wirkung so ihrem Grunde nach ein elektrisches Phänomensey, sondern auch was Wirkung der sogenannten Wahlverwandschaft zu seyn scheine, nur durch eine in gewissen Körpern stärker, als in andren vorhandene elektrische Polarität bewirkt werde. Zum Beschlusse des bisherigen Herumwindens in hypothetischen Vorstellungen bleibt es somit bei der Kategorie stärkerer Intensität, welche dasselbe Formelle als die Wahlverwandschaft überhaupt ist, und diese damit, daß sie auf eine stärkere Intensität elektrischer Polarität gestellt wird, im geringsten nicht weiter auf einen physikalschen Grund bringt als vorher. Aber auch das was hier als größere specifische Intensität bestimmt seyn soll, wird späterhin nur auf die bereits angeführten, von Berthollet aufgezeigten Modifikationen zurückgeführt.\n\nDas Verdienst und der Ruhm von Berzelius wegen der auf alle chemischen Verhältnisse ausgedehnten Proportionenlehre durfte für sich kein Abhaltungsgrund seyn, die Blöße der angeführten Theorie auseinander zu setzen; ein näherer Grund aber, dieß zu thun, muß der Umstand seyn, daß solches Verdienst in einer Seite der Wissenschaft, wie bei Newton, Autorität für ein damit in Zusammenhang gesetztes grundloses Gebäude von schlechten Kategorien zu werden pflegt, und daß gerade solche Metaphysik dasjenige ist, was mit der größten Prätension ausgegeben und ebenso nachgesprochen wird.\n\nAußer den Formen des Maaßverhältnisses, die sich auf die chemische Affinität und Wahlverwandschaft beziehen, können auch noch andere in Rücksicht auf Quantitäten, die sich zu einem System qualificiren, betrachtet werden. Die chemischen Körper bilden in Beziehung auf Sättigung ein System von Verhältnissen; die Sättigung selbst beruht auf der bestimmten Proportion, in welcher die beiderseitigen Mengen, die eine besondere materielle Existenz gegeneinander haben, sich verbinden. Aber es giebt auch Maaßverhältnisse, deren Momente untrennbar sind und nicht in einer eignen von einander verschiedenen Existenz dargestellt werden können. Diese sind das, was vorhin die unmittelbaren selbstständigen Maaße genannt, und die in den specifischen Schweren der Körper repräsentirt sind.—Sie sind innerhalb der Körper ein Verhältniß von Gewicht zum Volumen; der Verhältnissexponent, welcher die Bestimmtheit einer speeifischen Schwere zum Unterschiede von andern ausdrückt, ist bestimmtes Quantum nur der Vergleichung, ein ihnen äußeres Verhältniß in einer äußern Reflexion, das sich nicht auf das eigne qualitative Verhalten zu einer gegenüber stehenden Existenz gründet. Es wäre die Aufgabe vorhanden, die Verhältnißexponenten der Reihe der specifischen Schweren, als ein System aus einer Regel zu erkennen, welche eine bloß arithmetische Vielheit zu einer Reihe harmonischer Knoten specificirte.—Dieselbe Forderung fände für die Erkenntniß der angeführten chemischen Verwandtschaftsreihen statt. Aber die Wissenschaft hat noch weit, um dahin zu gelangen, soweit als dahin, die Zahlen der Entfernungen der Planeten des Sonnensystems in einem Maaßsysteme zu fassen.\n\nDie specifischen Schweren, ob sie gleich zunächst kein qualitatives Verhältniß zu einander zu haben scheinen, treten jedoch gleichfalls in qualitative Beziehung. Indem die Körper chemisch verbunden, auch nur amalgamirt oder synsomatisirt werden, zeigt sich gleichfalls eine Neutralisation der specifischen Schweren. Es ist vorhin die Erscheinung angeführt worden, daß das Volumen, auch des Gemisches von chemisch gegen einander eigentlich gleichgültig bleibenden Materien, nicht von gleicher Größe mit der Summe des Volumens derselben vor der Vermischung ist. Sie modificiren in dieser gegenseitig das Quantum der Bestimmtheit, mit dem sie in die Beziehung eintreten, und geben sich auf diese Weise als sich qualitativ verhaltend gegen einander kund. Hier äußert sich das Quantum der specifischen Schwere nicht bloß als eine fixe Vergleichungszahl, sondern als eine Verhältnißzahl, die verrückbar ist; und die Exponenten der Gemische geben Reihen von Maaßen, deren Fortgang von einem andern Princip bestimmt wird, als den Verhältnißzahlen der specifischen Schweren, die miteinander verbunden werden. Die Exponenten dieser Verhältnisse sind nicht ausschließende Maaßbestimmungen; ihr Fortgang ist ein kontinuirlicher, aber enthält ein specificirendes Gesetz in sich, das von den formell fortgehenden Verhältnissen, in denen die Mengen verbunden werden, verschieden und jenen Fortgang mit diesem inkommensurabel macht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0001","text":"Die chemischen Stoffe sind die eigenthümlichsten Beispiele solcher Maaße, welche Maaßmomente sind, die dasjenigr, was ihre Bestimmung ausmacht, allein im Verhalten zu andern haben. Säuren und Kalien oder Basen überhaupt erscheinen als unmittelbar an sich bestimmte Dinge, aber vielmehr als unvollkommene Körperelemente, als Bestandtheile, die eigentlich nicht für sich existiren, sondern nur diese Existenz haben, ihr isolirtes Bestehen aufzuheben und sich mit einem andern zu verbinden. Der Unterschied ferner, wodurch sie als selbstständige sind, besteht nicht in dieser unmittelbaren Qualität, sondern in der quantitativen Art und Weise des Verhaltens.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"93.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0002","text":"Er ist nämlich nicht auf den chemischen Gegensatz von Säure und Kali oder Basis überhaupt, eingeschränkt, sondern ist zu einem Maaße der Sättigung specificirt, und besteht in der specifischen Bestimmtheit der Quantität der sich neutralisirenden Stoffe. Diese Quantitäts-Bestimmung in Rücksicht auf die Sättigung macht die qualitative Natur eines Stoffes aus, sie macht ihn zu dem, was er für sich ist, und die Zahl, die dieß ausdrückt, ist wesentlich einer von mehrern Exponenten für eine gegenüber stehende Einheit.—Solcher Stoff steht mit einem andern in sogenannter Verwandtschafft; insofern diese Beziehung rein qualitativer Natur bliebe, so wäre,—wie die Beziehung der magnetischen Pole oder der Elektricitäten,—die eine Bestimmtheit nur die negative der andern, und beide Seiten zeigten sich nicht auch zugleich gleichgültig gegeneinander.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"93.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0003","text":"Aber weil die Beziehung auch quantitativer Natur ist, ist jeder dieser Stoffe fähig mit Mehrern sich zu neutralisiren, und nicht auf einen gegenüber stehenden eingeschränkt. Es verhält sich nicht nur die Säure und das Kali oder Basis, sondern Säuren und Kalien oder Basen zu einander. Sie charakterisiren sich zunächst dadurch gegen einander, je nachdem eine Säure z.B. von einem Kali mehr bedarf um sich mit ihm zu sättigen, als eine andere. Aber die fürsichseyende Selbstständigkeit zeigt sich darin, daß die Verwandtschaften sich ausschließend verhalten und eine vor der andern den Vorzug hat, indem für sich eine Säure mit allen Kalien, und umgekehrt, eine Verbindung eingehen kann. Es macht so den Hauptunterschied einer Säure gegen eine andere aus, ob sie zu einer Basis eine nähere Verwandtschaft habe, als eine andere, d. i. eine sogenannte Wahlverwandschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"93.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0004","text":"Über die chemischen Verwandtschaften der Säuren und Kalien ist das Gesetz gefunden worden, daß wenn zwei neutrale Solutionen gemischt werden, wodurch eine Scheidung und daraus zwei neue Verbindungen entstehen, diese Produkte gleichfalls neutral sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"93.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0005","text":"Es folgt hieraus, daß die Mengen von zwei kalischen Basen, die zur Sättigung einer Säure erfordert werden, in demselben Verhältnisse zur Sättigung einer andern nöthig sind; überhaupt wenn für ein Kali als Einheit genommen die Reihe der Verhältnißzahlen bestimmt worden ist, in denen die verschiedenen Säuren dasselbe sättigen, so ist für jedes andere Kali diese Reihe dieselbe, nur daß die verschiedenen Kalien gegen einander in verschiedenen Anzahlen zu nehmen sind;—Anzahlen, die wieder ihrer Seits eine eben solche beständige Reihe von Exponenten für jede der gegenüber stehenden Säuren bilden, indem sie ebenso zujeder einzelnen Säure sich in demselben Verhältnisse beziehen, als zujeder andern. —Fischer hat zuerst diese Reihen aus den richterischen Arbeiten in ihrer Einfachheit herausgehoben; s. in s.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"93.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0006","text":"Anmerkungen zur Übersetzung von Berthollets Abhandlung über die Gesetze der Verwandtschaft in der Chemie, S. 232. und Berthollet Statique chimique I. Part. p. 134. ff.—Die, seit dieß zuerst geschrieben worden, nach allen Seiten hin so sehr ausgebildete Kenntniß von den Verhältnißzahlen der Mischungen der chemischen Elemente, hier berücksichtigen zu wollen, würde auch darum eine Abschweifung seyn, da diese empirische zu einem Theil aber auch nur hypothetische Erweiterung innerhalb derselben Begriffsbestimmungen eingeschlossen bleibt. Aber über die dabei gebrauchten Kategorien, ferner über die Ansichten der chemischen Wahlverwandtschaft selbst und ihrer Beziehung auf das Quantitative, so wie über den Versuch, dieselbe auf bestimmte physikalische Qualitäten zu gründen, mögen noch einige Bemerkungen hinzugefügt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"93.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0007","text":"Bekanntlich hat Berthollet die allgemeine Vorstellung von der Wahlverwandtschaft durch den Begriff von der Wirksamkeit einer chemischen Masse modificirt. Diese Modification hat, was wohl zu unterscheiden ist, auf die Quantitäts-Verhältnisse der chemischen Sättigungs-Gesetze selbst keinen Einfluß, aber das qualitative Moment der ausschließenden Wahlverwandtschaft als solcher wird nicht nur geschwächt, sondern vielmehr aufgehoben. Wenn zwei Säuren auf ein Kali wirken, und diejenige, von welcher gesagt wird, daß sie eine größere Verwandtschaft zu derselben habe, auch in dem Quantum vorhanden ist, welches fähig ist, das Quantum der Basis zu sättigen, so erfolgt nach der Vorstellung der Wahlverwandtschaft nur diese Sättigung; die andere Säure bleibt ganz unwirksam und von der neutralen Verbindung ausgeschlossen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"93.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0008","text":"Nach jenem Begriffe der Wirksamkeit einer chemischen Masse hingegen, ist jede von beiden wirksam in einem Verhältniß, das aus ihrer vorhandenen Menge und ihrer Sättigungsfähigkeit oder sogenannten Affinität zusammengesetzt ist. Berthollets Untersuchungen haben die nähern Umstände angegeben, unter welchen die Wirksamkeit der chemischen Masse aufgehoben wird, und eine (stärker verwandte) Säure die andere (schwächere) auszutreiben und deren Wirkung auszuschließen, somit nach dem Sinne der Wahlverwandtschaft thätig zu seyn scheint. Er hat gezeigt, daß es Umstände, wie die Stärke der Kohäsion, Unauflösbarkeit der gebildeten Salze im Wasser, sind, unter welchen jenes Ausschließen Statt findet, nicht die qualitative Natur der Agentien als solche, —Umstände, welche wieder durch andere Umstände z.B. die Temperatur in ihrer Wirkung aufgehoben werden können.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"93.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0009","text":"Mit der Beseitigung dieser Hindernisse tritt die chemische Masse unverkümmert in Wirksamkeit, und das, was als rein qualitatives Ausschließen, als Wahlverwandtschaft erschien, zeigt sich nur in äußerlichen Modifikationen zu liegen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"93.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0010","text":"Berzelius wäre es vornehmlich, der weiter über diesen Gegenstand zu hören ist. Derselbe stellt aber in seinem Lehrbuche der Chemie über die Sache nichts Eigenthümliches und Bestimmteres auf. Es sind die berthollet'schen Ansichten aufgenommen und wörtlich wiederhohlt, nur mit der eigenthümlichen Metaphysik einer unkritischen Reflexion ausstaffirt worden, deren Kategorien also allein sich für die nähere Betrachtung darbieten. Die Theorie geht über die Erfahrung hinaus, und erfindet Theils sinnliche Vorstellungen, wie sie nicht selbst in der Erfahrung gegeben sind, Theils wendet sie Denkbestimmungen an, und macht sich auf beide Weise zum Gegenstande logischer Kritik. Wir wollen daher das in jenem Lehrbuche selbst III. Band I. Abth. (übers. von Wöhler S. 82. ff) über die Theorie Vorgetragene vornehmen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"93.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0011","text":"Daselbst nun liest man, \"daß man sich vorstellen müsse, in einer gleichförmig gemischten Flüssigkeit sey ein jedes Atom vom aufgelösten Körper von einer gleichen Anzahl von Atomen des Auflösungsmittels umgeben; und wenn mehrere Substanzen zusammen aufgelöst sind, so müssen sie die Zwischenräume zwischen den Atomen des Auflösungsmittels unter sich theilen, so daß, bei einer gleichförmigen Mischung der Flüssigkeit, eine solche Symmetrie in der Lage der Atome entstehe, daß alle Atome der einzelnen Körper sich in Beziehung zu den Atomen der andern Körper in einer gleichförmigen Lage befinden; man könne daher sagen, daß die Auflösung durch die Symmetrie in der Stellung der Atome, so wie die Verbindung durch die bestimmten Proportionen charakterisirt sey.\"—Dieß wird hierauf durch ein Beispiel der Verbindungen erläutert, die aus einer Auflösung von Kupferchlorid, zu welcher Schwefelsäure","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"93.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0012","text":"hinzugesetzt wird, entstehen; aber an diesem Beispiele wird freilich weder aufgezeigt, daß Atome existiren, noch daß eine Anzahl von Atomen der aufgelösten Körper Atome der Flüssigkeit umgeben, freie Atome der beiden Säuren sich um die (mit dem Kupferoxid) verbunden bleibenden lagern, noch daß die Symmetrie in der Stellung und Lage, noch daß Zwischenräume zwischen den Atomen existiren,—am allerwenigsten daß die aufgelösten Substanzen die Zwischenräume der Atome des Auflösungsmittels unter sich theilen.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"93.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0013","text":"Dieß hiesse, daß die aufgelösten da ihre Stellung nehmen, wo das Auflösungsmittel nicht ist,—denn die Zwischenräume desselben sind die von ihm leeren Räume,—somit daß die aufgelösten Substanzen sich nicht im Auflösungsmittel befinden, sondern wenn auch dasselbe umgebend und umlagernd, oder von demselben umgeben und umlagert,—außerhalb desselben, also gewiß auch von ihm nicht aufgelöst sind. Man sieht somit nicht ein, daß man sich solche Vorstellungen machen müsse, welche in der Erfahrung nicht aufgezeigt sind, im Wesentlichen sich sogleich widersprechen, und sonst auf andere Weise nicht erhärtet sind. Dieß könnte nur durch die Betrachtung dieser Vorstellungen selbst, d. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"93.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0014","text":"durch Metaphysik, welche Logik ist, geschehen, durch diese aber werden sie so wenig als durch die Erfahrung bestätigt,—im Gegentheil!—Übrigens giebt Berzelius zu, was auch oben gesagt worden, daß die Sätze Berthollets der Theorie von den bestimmten Proportionen nicht entgegen seyen,—er fügt freilich hinzu, daß sie auch den Ansichten von der Korpuskularphilosophie, d. i. der vorhin angeführten Vorstellungen von den Atomen, der Erfüllung der Zwischenräume der auflösenden Flüssigkeit durch die Atome der festen Körper u.s.f. nicht entgegen seyen,—diese letztere grundlose Metaphysik hat aber wesentlich nichts mit den Proportionen der Sättigung selbst zu thun.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"93.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0015","text":"Das Specifische, was in den Sättigungsgesetzen ausgedrückt ist, betrifft somit nur die Menge von selbst quantitativen Einheiten (nicht Atomen) eines Körpers, mit welcher sich die quantitative Einheit (ebenso wenig ein Atom) eines andern gegen erstern chemisch differenten Körpers neutralisirt; die Verschiedenheit besteht allein in diesen verschiedenen Proportionen. Wenn dann Berzelius, ungeachtet seine Proportionenlehre ganz nur eine Bestimmung von Mengen ist, doch auch von Affinitätsgraden spricht, z.B. S. 86. indem er die chemische Masse Berthollets als die Summe des Affinitätsgrades aus der vorhandenen Quantität des wirksamen Körpers erklärt, statt dessen Berthollet consequenter den Ausdruck capacité de saturation gebraucht, so verfällt er damit selbst in die Form intensiver Größe.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"93.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0016","text":"Dieß ist aber die Form, welche das Eigenthümliche der sogenannten dynamischen Philosophie ausmacht, die er früher S. 29. a. a. O. \"die speculative Philosophie gewisser deutschen Schulen\" nennt, und zum Besten der vortrefflichen \"Korpuskularphilosophie\" nachdrücklich verwirft. Von dieser dynamischen Philosophie giebt er dort an, daß sie annehme, die Elemente in ihrer chemischen Vereinigung durchdringen sich, und die Neutralisation bestehe in dieser gegenseitigen Durchdringung; dieß heißt nichts Anders, als daß die chemisch differenten Partikeln, die als Menge gegeneinander sind, in die Einfachheit einer intensiven Größe zusammengehen, was sich auch als Verminderung des Volums kund giebt. Dagegen sollen in der Korpuskulartheorie auch die chemisch verbundenen Atome sich in den Zwischenräumen, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"93.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0017","text":"außereinander erhalten, (Juxtaposition); Grad der Affinität hat in solchem Verhalten als einer nur extensiven Größe, eines Perennirens von Menge, keinen Sinn. Wenn ebendas angegeben wird, daß die Erscheinungen der bestimmten Proportionen für die dynamische Ansicht ganz unvorgesehen gekommen seyen, so wäre dieß nur ein äußerlicher historischer Umstand, abgesehen davon, daß die richterschen stöchiometrischen Reihen, in der fischerschen Zusammenstellung bereits Berthollet bekannt und in der ersten Ausg. dieser Logik, welche die Nichtigkeit der Kategorien erweist, auf denen die alte wie die neuseynwolleude Korpuskulartheorie beruht, angeführt sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"93.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0018","text":"Irrthümlich aber urtheilt Berzelius als ob unter der Herrschaft \"der dynamischen Ansicht\" die Erscheinungen der bestimmten Proportionen \"für immer\" unbekannt geblieben wären,—in dem Sinne, daß jene Ansicht sich nicht mit der Bestimmtheit der Proportionen vertrüge. Diese ist auf allen Fall nur Größebestimmtheit, gleichgültig ob in extensiver und intensiver Form, —so daß auch Berzelius, so sehr er an der erstern Form, der Menge, hängt, selbst die Vorstellung von Affinitätsgraden gebraucht.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"93.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0019","text":"Indem hiermit die Verwandschaft auf den quantitativen Unterschied zurückgeführt ist, ist sie als Wahlverwandschaft aufgehoben; das Ausschließende aber, das bei derselben Statt findet, ist auf Umstände zurückgeführt, d. i. auf Bestimmungen, welche als etwas der Verwandschaft Äußerliches erscheinen, auf Kohäsion, Unauflöslichkeit der zu Stande gekommenen Verbindungen u.s.f. Es kann mit dieser Vorstellung zum Theil das Verfahren bei der Betrachtung der Wirkung der Schwere verglichen werden, wo das, was an sich der Schwere selbst zukommt, daß der bewegte Pendel durch sie nothwendig zur Ruhe übergeht, nur als der zugleich vorhandene Umstand des äußern Widerstands der Luft des Fadens u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"93.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0020","text":"genommen und der Reibung allein statt der Schwere zugeschrieben wird.—Hier für die Natur des Qualitativen, welches in der Wahlverwandschaft liegt, macht es keinen Unterschied, ob dasselbe in der Form jener Umstände als seiner Bedingungen erscheint und aufgefaßt wird. Es beginnt mit dem Qualitativen als solchen eine neue Ordnung, deren Specifikation nicht mehr nur quantitativer Unterschied ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"93.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0021","text":"Wenn nun sonach der Unterschied der chemischen Affinität in einer Reihe quantitativer Verhältnisse sich genau feststellt gegen die Wahlverwandsehaft als eintretender qualitativer Bestimmtheit, deren Verhalten mit jener Ordnung keineswegs zusammenfällt, so wird dieser Unterschied wieder in völlige Verwirrung durch die Art geworfen, in welcher mit dem chemischen Verhalten das elektrische in neuern Zeiten in Verbindung gebracht wird, und die Hoffnung von diesem tiefer seyn sollenden Princip aus über das wichtigste, das Maaßverhältniß, einen Aufschluß zu erhalten, wird gänzlich getäuscht.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"93.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0022","text":"Diese Theorie, in welcher die Erscheinungen der Elektricität und des Chemismus vollkommen identificirt werden, insofern sie das Physikalische und nicht bloß die Maaßverhältnisse betrifft, ist hier nicht in nähere Betrachtung zu nehmen, und nur insofern zu erwähnen, als die Unterschiedenheit der Maaßbestimmungen dadurch verworren wird. Für sich selbst ist sie seicht zu nennen, weil die Seichtigkeit darin besteht, das Verschiedene mit Weglassung der Verschiedenheit identisch zu nehmen. War hierbei die Affinität betrifft, so ist sie, indem so chemische Processe mit elektrischen, ingleichen mit Feuer und Licht-Erscheinungen, identificirt werden, \"auf Neutralisation entgegengesetzter Electricitäten\" reducirt worden. Die Identifikation der Elektricität und des Chemismus selbst ist es beinahe komisch (S. 63. a. a. O.)","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"93.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0023","text":"in folgender Weise dargestellt zu finden, daß \"die eletrischen Phänomene wohl die Wirkung der Körper auf größern oder geringern Abstand, ihre Anziehung vor der Vereinigung (d. i. das noch nicht chemische Verhalten)—und das durch diese Vereinigung entstehende Feuer (?) wohl erklären, aber uns über die Ursache der mit einer so großen Kraft, nach Vernichtung des entgegengesetzten elektrischen Zustandes, fortdauernden Vereinigung der Körper keinen Aufschluß geben;\" d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"93.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0024","text":"die Theorie giebt den Aufschluß, daß die Electricität die Ursache des chemischen Verhaltens sey, daß aber die Electricität über das, was im chemischen Processe chemisch ist, keinen Aufschluß gebe.—Damit, daß die chemische Differenz überhaupt auf den Gegensatz positiver und negativer Elektricität zurückgeführt wird, wird die Affinitätsverschiedenheit der auf die eine und auf die andere Seite fallenden Agentien unter sich als die Ordnung von zwei Reihen elektropositiver und elektronegativer Körper bestimmt. Bei dem Identificiren der Elektricität und des Chemismus ihrer allgemeinen Bestimmung nach, wird schon dieß übersehen, daß die erstere überhaupt und deren Neutralisirung flüchtig ist und der Qualität der Körper äußerlich bleibt, der Chemismus in seiner Aktion und besonders in der Neutralisation die ganze qualitative Natur der Körper in Anspruch nimmt und alterirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"93.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0025","text":"Ebenso flüchtig ist innerhalb der Elektricität ihr Gegensatz von positiver und negativer; er ist ein so Unstätes, daß er von den geringsten äußerlichen Umständen abhängig ist, und in keinen Vergleich gestellt werden kann mit der Bestimmtheit und Festigkeit des Gegensatzes von Säuren z.B. gegen die Metalle u.s.w. Die Veränderlichkeit, die in diesem chemischen Verhalten, durch höchst gewaltsame Einwirkungen z.B. einer erhöhten Temperatur u.s.f. statt finden kann, steht in keinem Vergleich mit der Oberflächlichkeit des elektrischen Gegensatzes. Der fernere Unterschied nun innerhalb der Reihe jeder der beiden Seiten zwischen mehr oder weniger positiv-elektrischer, oder mehr oder weniger negativ-elektrischer Beschaffenheit, ist vollends sowohl ein völlig Unsicheres als Unkonstatirtes. Aus diesen Reihen der Körper aber (Berzelius am ang. Ort S. 64. f.)","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"93.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0026","text":"\"nach ihren elektrischen Dispositionen soll das elektrochemische System entstehen, welches sich von allen am besten eigne, eine Idee voll der Chemie zu geben;\" diese Reihen werden nun angegeben; wie sie aber in der That beschaffen sind, darüber wird S. 67. hinzugefügt:","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"93.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0027","text":"\"daß dieß ungefähr die Ordnung dieser Körper sey, aber diese Materie sey so wenig untersucht, daß sich noch nichts ganz Gewisses hinsichtlich dieser relativen Ordnung bestimmen lasse.\"—Sowohl die Verhältnißzahlen jener (von Richter zuerst gemachten) Affinitätsreihen, als die höchst interessante von Berzelius aufgestellte Reduktion der Verbindungen von zwei Körpern auf die Einfachheit weniger quantitativen Verhältnisse sind ganz und gar unabhängig von jenem elektrochemisch seyn sollenden Gebräue.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"93.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0028","text":"Wenn in jenen Proportionen und in deren seit Richter nach allen Seiten hin gewonnenen Ausdehnung der experimentale Weg der richtige Leitstern gewesen, so kontrastirt für sich damit umsomehr die Vermischung dieser großen Entdeckungen mit der außer dem Weg der Erfahrung liegenden Öde der sogenannten Korpuskulartheorie; nur dieser Anfang, das Princip der Erfahrung zu verlassen, konnte es motiviren, noch weiter jenen früher von Ritter vornehmlich angefangenen Einfall wieder aufzunehmen, feste Ordnungen von elektropositiven und elektronegativen Körpern, die zugleich chemische Bedeutung haben sollten, aufzustellen.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"93.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0029","text":"Schon die Nichtigkeit der Grundlage, die für die chemische Affinität in dem Gegensatze von elektropositiven und elektronegativen Körpern, wenn dieser für sieh auch faktisch richtiger wäre, als er ist, angenommen wird, zeigt sich bald selbst auf dem experimentalen Wege, was denn aber wieder zu weiterer Inkonsequenz führt. Es wird S. 73. (a. a. O.) zugestanden, daß zwei sogenannte elektronegative Körper, wie Schwefel und Sauerstoff auf eine viel innigere Art sich mit einander verbinden, als z.B. der Sauerstoff und das Kupfer, obgleich letzteres elektropositiv sey. Die auf den allgemeinen Gegensatz von positiver und negativer-Elektricität basirte Grundlage für die Affinität muß hier hiermit gegen ein bloßes Mehr oder Weniger innerhalb Einer und derselben Reihe von elektrischer Bestimmtheit zurückgestellt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"93.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0030","text":"Der Verwandschaftsgrad der Körper, wird nun hieraus geschlossen, hänge demnach nicht allein von ihrer specifischen Unipolarität (mit welcher Hypothese diese Bestimmung zusammenhängt, thut hierher nichts, sie gilt hier nur für das Entweder des Positiven und das Oder des Negativen) ab; der Verwandschaftsgrad müsse hauptsächlich von der Intensität ihrer Polarität im Allgemeinen hergeleitet werden. Hier geht somit näher die Betrachtung der Affinität zu dem Verhältniß der Wahlverwandschaft über, um die uns vornehmlich zu thun ist; sehen wir, was sich denn für diese nun ergiebt. Indem sogleich (ebendas. S. 73.)","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"93.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0031","text":"zugestanden wird, daß der Grad dieser Polarität, wenn sie nicht bloß in unserer Vorstellung existire, keine konstante Quantität zu seyn scheine, sondern sehr von der Temperatur abhänge, so findet sich nach allem diesem als Resultat angegeben, nicht nur, daß jede chemische Wirkung so ihrem Grunde nach ein elektrisches Phänomensey, sondern auch was Wirkung der sogenannten Wahlverwandschaft zu seyn scheine, nur durch eine in gewissen Körpern stärker, als in andren vorhandene elektrische Polarität bewirkt werde. Zum Beschlusse des bisherigen Herumwindens in hypothetischen Vorstellungen bleibt es somit bei der Kategorie stärkerer Intensität, welche dasselbe Formelle als die Wahlverwandschaft überhaupt ist, und diese damit, daß sie auf eine stärkere Intensität elektrischer Polarität gestellt wird, im geringsten nicht weiter auf einen physikalschen Grund bringt als vorher.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"93.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0032","text":"Aber auch das was hier als größere specifische Intensität bestimmt seyn soll, wird späterhin nur auf die bereits angeführten, von Berthollet aufgezeigten Modifikationen zurückgeführt.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"93.32"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0033","text":"Das Verdienst und der Ruhm von Berzelius wegen der auf alle chemischen Verhältnisse ausgedehnten Proportionenlehre durfte für sich kein Abhaltungsgrund seyn, die Blöße der angeführten Theorie auseinander zu setzen; ein näherer Grund aber, dieß zu thun, muß der Umstand seyn, daß solches Verdienst in einer Seite der Wissenschaft, wie bei Newton, Autorität für ein damit in Zusammenhang gesetztes grundloses Gebäude von schlechten Kategorien zu werden pflegt, und daß gerade solche Metaphysik dasjenige ist, was mit der größten Prätension ausgegeben und ebenso nachgesprochen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"93.33"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0034","text":"Außer den Formen des Maaßverhältnisses, die sich auf die chemische Affinität und Wahlverwandschaft beziehen, können auch noch andere in Rücksicht auf Quantitäten, die sich zu einem System qualificiren, betrachtet werden. Die chemischen Körper bilden in Beziehung auf Sättigung ein System von Verhältnissen; die Sättigung selbst beruht auf der bestimmten Proportion, in welcher die beiderseitigen Mengen, die eine besondere materielle Existenz gegeneinander haben, sich verbinden. Aber es giebt auch Maaßverhältnisse, deren Momente untrennbar sind und nicht in einer eignen von einander verschiedenen Existenz dargestellt werden können.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"93.34"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0035","text":"Diese sind das, was vorhin die unmittelbaren selbstständigen Maaße genannt, und die in den specifischen Schweren der Körper repräsentirt sind.—Sie sind innerhalb der Körper ein Verhältniß von Gewicht zum Volumen; der Verhältnissexponent, welcher die Bestimmtheit einer speeifischen Schwere zum Unterschiede von andern ausdrückt, ist bestimmtes Quantum nur der Vergleichung, ein ihnen äußeres Verhältniß in einer äußern Reflexion, das sich nicht auf das eigne qualitative Verhalten zu einer gegenüber stehenden Existenz gründet. Es wäre die Aufgabe vorhanden, die Verhältnißexponenten der Reihe der specifischen Schweren, als ein System aus einer Regel zu erkennen, welche eine bloß arithmetische Vielheit zu einer Reihe harmonischer Knoten specificirte.—Dieselbe Forderung fände für die Erkenntniß der angeführten chemischen Verwandtschaftsreihen statt.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"93.35"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0036","text":"Aber die Wissenschaft hat noch weit, um dahin zu gelangen, soweit als dahin, die Zahlen der Entfernungen der Planeten des Sonnensystems in einem Maaßsysteme zu fassen.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"93.36"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0037","text":"Die specifischen Schweren, ob sie gleich zunächst kein qualitatives Verhältniß zu einander zu haben scheinen, treten jedoch gleichfalls in qualitative Beziehung. Indem die Körper chemisch verbunden, auch nur amalgamirt oder synsomatisirt werden, zeigt sich gleichfalls eine Neutralisation der specifischen Schweren. Es ist vorhin die Erscheinung angeführt worden, daß das Volumen, auch des Gemisches von chemisch gegen einander eigentlich gleichgültig bleibenden Materien, nicht von gleicher Größe mit der Summe des Volumens derselben vor der Vermischung ist. Sie modificiren in dieser gegenseitig das Quantum der Bestimmtheit, mit dem sie in die Beziehung eintreten, und geben sich auf diese Weise als sich qualitativ verhaltend gegen einander kund.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"93.37"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0038","text":"Hier äußert sich das Quantum der specifischen Schwere nicht bloß als eine fixe Vergleichungszahl, sondern als eine Verhältnißzahl, die verrückbar ist; und die Exponenten der Gemische geben Reihen von Maaßen, deren Fortgang von einem andern Princip bestimmt wird, als den Verhältnißzahlen der specifischen Schweren, die miteinander verbunden werden. Die Exponenten dieser Verhältnisse sind nicht ausschließende Maaßbestimmungen; ihr Fortgang ist ein kontinuirlicher, aber enthält ein specificirendes Gesetz in sich, das von den formell fortgehenden Verhältnissen, in denen die Mengen verbunden werden, verschieden und jenen Fortgang mit diesem inkommensurabel macht.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"93.38"}],"sha256":"ccb75e2513280c807d372e82a0d56f6373365e19aeadb9849d2c777ed0bd5fe2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104350116291Z_52ab8c3b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"ccb75e2513280c807d372e82a0d56f6373365e19aeadb9849d2c777ed0bd5fe2","sha256":"b4a81fde646e00f2bffda3dc9203109caef3f375c532de8811486caf92eb9fd1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:43:50.116327+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0001","text":"Chemical substances are the most peculiar examples of such measures, which are moments of measure, that have that which constitutes their determination solely in their relation to others. Acids and alkalis or bases in general appear as immediately determined things in themselves, but rather as incomplete bodily elements, as constituents that do not properly exist for themselves, but have this existence only in order to sublate their isolated subsistence and to combine with another. The difference, furthermore, whereby they are independent, does not consist in this immediate quality, but in the quantitative manner of relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"93.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0002","text":"It is, namely, not restricted to the chemical opposition of acid and alkali or base in general, but is specified into a measure of saturation, and consists in the specific determinateness of the quantity of the substances neutralizing one another. This determination of quantity with respect to saturation constitutes the qualitative nature of a substance; it makes it what it is for itself, and the number which expresses this is essentially one of several exponents for an opposing unit.—Such a substance stands in so-called affinity with another; insofar as this relation remained of a purely qualitative nature, then,—like the relation of magnetic poles or of electricities,—the one determinateness would only be the negative of the other, and the two sides would not at the same time show themselves as indifferent to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"93.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0003","text":"But because the relation is also of a quantitative nature, each of these substances is capable of neutralizing itself with several others, and is not restricted to one opposing substance. It is not merely acid and alkali or base, but acids and alkalis or bases that relate to one another. They initially characterize themselves in relation to one another according as an acid, e.g., requires more of an alkali in order to saturate itself with it than does another. But being-for-itself, independence, shows itself in the fact that the affinities behave exclusively and one has precedence over another, since in itself an acid can enter into a combination with all alkalis, and conversely. Thus the principal distinction of one acid from another consists in whether it has a closer affinity to a base than another does, i.e. a so-called elective affinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"93.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0004","text":"Concerning the chemical affinities of acids and alkalis, the law has been found that, when two neutral solutions are mixed, whereby a separation and thence two new combinations arise, these products are likewise neutral.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"93.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0005","text":"It follows from this that the quantities of two alkaline bases required for the saturation of one acid are necessary in the same ratio for the saturation of another; in general, if, taking one alkali as unit, the series of ratio-numbers in which the different acids saturate it has been determined, then this series is the same for every other alkali, except that the different alkalis are to be taken in different numbers in relation to one another;—numbers which in turn form an equally constant series of exponents for each of the opposed acids, inasmuch as they likewise relate to each individual acid in the same ratio as to every other. —Fischer was the first to draw out these series from Richter's works in their simplicity; see below.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"93.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0006","text":"Notes to the translation of Berthollet's Treatise on the Laws of Affinity in Chemistry, p. 232, and Berthollet, Statique chimique, Part I, p. 134 ff.—To wish here to take account of the knowledge, so highly developed in every direction since this was first written, of the ratio-numbers of the mixtures of chemical elements, would for that reason too be a digression, since this empirical, but in part also merely hypothetical, extension remains enclosed within the same determinations of the concept. But some remarks may yet be added concerning the categories employed therein, further concerning the views of chemical elective affinity itself and its relation to the quantitative, as well as concerning the attempt to ground it in determinate physical qualities.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"93.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0007","text":"As is known, Berthollet modified the general conception of elective affinity by the concept of the efficacy of a chemical mass. This modification, which must be carefully distinguished, has no influence upon the quantitative ratios of the chemical laws of saturation themselves; but the qualitative moment of exclusive elective affinity as such is not merely weakened, but rather sublated. If two acids act upon an alkali, and the one of which it is said that it has a greater affinity to it is also present in the quantum capable of saturating the quantum of the base, then, according to the conception of elective affinity, this saturation alone takes place; the other acid remains wholly ineffective and excluded from the neutral combination.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"93.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0008","text":"According to that concept of the efficacy of a chemical mass, on the other hand, each of the two is efficacious in a ratio composed of its amount present and its capacity for saturation or so-called affinity. Berthollet's investigations have indicated the more specific circumstances under which the efficacy of the chemical mass is sublated, and one (more strongly affiliated) acid seems to expel the other (weaker) one and exclude its action, thus to be active in the sense of elective affinity. He has shown that these are circumstances such as the strength of cohesion, the insolubility of the salts formed in water, under which that exclusion takes place, and not the qualitative nature of the agents as such,—circumstances which, in turn, can be sublated in their effect by other circumstances, e.g. temperature.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"93.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0009","text":"With the removal of these obstacles, the chemical mass enters upon efficacy unimpaired, and what appeared as purely qualitative exclusion, as elective affinity, shows itself to lie merely in external modifications.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"93.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0010","text":"It would chiefly be Berzelius from whom more is to be heard concerning this subject. But in his textbook he advances nothing peculiar or more determinate about the matter. Berthollet's views have been adopted and repeated verbatim, only furnished with the peculiar metaphysics of an uncritical reflection, whose categories therefore alone present themselves for closer consideration. Theory goes beyond experience, and partly invents sensible representations such as are not themselves given in experience, partly applies determinations of thought, and in both ways makes itself an object of logical criticism. We shall therefore take up what is presented concerning theory in that textbook itself, vol. III, pt. I (trans. by Wöhler, p. 82 ff.).","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"93.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0011","text":"There one now reads, “that one must conceive that, in a uniformly mixed fluid, every atom of the dissolved body is surrounded by an equal number of atoms of the solvent; and if several substances are dissolved together, they must divide among themselves the interstices between the atoms of the solvent, so that, in a uniform mixture of the fluid, such a symmetry in the position of the atoms arises that all the atoms of the individual bodies are situated in a uniform position in relation to the atoms of the other bodies; one may therefore say that solution is characterized by the symmetry in the arrangement of the atoms, just as combination is characterized by definite proportions.”—This is then illustrated by an example of the combinations arising from a solution of copper chloride to which sulphuric acid","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"93.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0012","text":"is added; but in this example it is admittedly shown neither that atoms exist, nor that a number of atoms of the dissolved bodies surround atoms of the fluid, that free atoms of the two acids arrange themselves around those remaining combined (with the copper oxide), nor that symmetry in position and arrangement exists, nor that interstices between atoms exist,—least of all that the dissolved substances divide among themselves the interstices of the atoms of the solvent.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"93.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0013","text":"This would mean that the dissolved substances take up their position where the solvent is not,—for its interstices are the spaces empty of it,—thus that the dissolved substances are not in the solvent, but, even if surrounding and encircling it, or surrounded and encircled by it,—outside it, and thus certainly not dissolved by it either. It is therefore not apparent why one must form such representations, which are not displayed in experience, essentially contradict themselves at once, and are not otherwise established. This could only occur through the consideration of these representations themselves, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"93.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0014","text":"through metaphysics, which is logic; but by this they are confirmed no more than by experience,—on the contrary!—Moreover, Berzelius admits what was also said above, that Berthollet's propositions are not contrary to the theory of definite proportions,—he adds, admittedly, that they are likewise not contrary to the views of corpuscular philosophy, i.e. to the aforementioned representations of atoms, of the filling of the interstices of the dissolving fluid by the atoms of solid bodies, etc.,—but this latter groundless metaphysics essentially has nothing to do with the proportions of saturation themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"93.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0015","text":"The specific element expressed in the laws of saturation thus concerns only the quantity of units of a body that are themselves quantitative (not atoms), with which the quantitative unit (just as little an atom) of another body chemically different from the former neutralizes itself; the difference consists solely in these different proportions. If then Berzelius, although his doctrine of proportions is entirely only a determination of quantities, nevertheless also speaks of degrees of affinity, e.g. p. 86, in that he explains Berthollet's chemical mass as the sum of the degree of affinity and the quantity present of the efficacious body, whereas Berthollet more consistently uses the expression capacité de saturation, he thereby himself falls into the form of intensive magnitude.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"93.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0016","text":"But this is the form that constitutes the distinctive feature of so-called dynamic philosophy, which he earlier, p. 29 loc. cit., calls “the speculative philosophy of certain German schools,” and emphatically rejects in favour of the excellent “corpuscular philosophy.” He there states of this dynamic philosophy that it assumes that the elements interpenetrate in their chemical combination, and that neutralization consists in this reciprocal interpenetration; this means nothing other than that the chemically different particles, which are as quantity in relation to one another, pass over into the simplicity of an intensive magnitude, which also manifests itself as a diminution of volume. By contrast, in corpuscular theory the chemically combined atoms too are supposed to maintain themselves in the interstices, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"93.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0017","text":"external to one another, (juxtaposition); degree of affinity has no sense in such a relation as one of merely extensive magnitude, of a persistence of quantity. When it is likewise asserted that the phenomena of definite proportions came wholly unexpectedly for the dynamic view, this would be only an external historical circumstance, apart from the fact that Richter's stoichiometric series, in Fischer's compilation, were already known to Berthollet and are cited in the first edition of this Logic, which demonstrates the nullity of the categories upon which the old, as well as the corpuscular theory that wishes to be new, rests.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"93.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0018","text":"But Berzelius judges erroneously as though, under the dominion of “the dynamic view,” the phenomena of definite proportions would have remained unknown “for ever,”—in the sense that that view is incompatible with the determinateness of proportions. This is in any case only determinateness of magnitude, whether in extensive or intensive form,—so that Berzelius too, however greatly he adheres to the former form, quantity, himself employs the representation of degrees of affinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"93.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0019","text":"Since affinity is thereby reduced to quantitative difference, it is sublated as elective affinity; but the exclusive element which occurs in it is reduced to circumstances, i.e. to determinations which appear as something external to affinity, to cohesion, insolubility of the combinations that have come about, etc. This conception can in part be compared with the procedure in considering the effect of gravity, where that which belongs in itself to gravity itself, namely that the moving pendulum necessarily comes to rest through it, is taken merely as the simultaneously present circumstance of the external resistance of the air, the thread, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"93.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0020","text":"and attributed to friction alone instead of to gravity.—Here, for the nature of the qualitative which lies in elective affinity, it makes no difference whether it appears and is apprehended in the form of those circumstances as its conditions. With the qualitative as such, a new order begins, whose specification is no longer merely quantitative difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"93.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0021","text":"If, then, in this way the difference of chemical affinity is established exactly in a series of quantitative relations, as against elective affinity as an intervening qualitative determinacy, whose behaviour by no means coincides with that order, this difference is once again thrown into complete confusion by the manner in which, in recent times, the electrical has been brought into connection with chemical behaviour; and the hope of obtaining from this supposedly deeper principle an elucidation concerning what is most important, the measure-relation, is entirely disappointed.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"93.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0022","text":"This theory, in which the phenomena of electricity and of chemism are completely identified, insofar as it concerns the physical and not merely the measure-relations, need not be considered more closely here, and need only be mentioned insofar as the distinctness of the measure-determinations is confused thereby. In itself it is to be called shallow, for the shallowness consists in taking what is different as identical, with omission of the difference. As regards affinity in this connection, it has, inasmuch as chemical processes are thus identified with electrical ones, likewise with phenomena of fire and light, been reduced to “neutralization of opposed electricities.” The identification of electricity and chemism itself is almost comic (p. 63, loc. cit.)","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"93.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0023","text":"to find represented in the following manner, that “electrical phenomena may indeed explain the action of bodies at greater or lesser distance, their attraction prior to combination (i.e. behaviour not yet chemical)—and the fire (?) arising through this combination, but give us no elucidation concerning the cause of the union of bodies, continuing with so great a force after the annihilation of the opposed electrical state;” i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"93.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0024","text":"the theory gives the elucidation that electricity is the cause of chemical behaviour, but that electricity gives no elucidation concerning what is chemical in the chemical process.—By reducing chemical difference in general to the opposition of positive and negative electricity, the difference of affinity among the agents falling on the one and on the other side is determined as the order of two series of electropositive and electronegative bodies. In identifying electricity and chemism according to their general determination, it is already overlooked that the former in general, and its neutralization, is transient and remains external to the quality of the bodies, whereas chemism, in its action and especially in neutralization, lays claim to and alters the whole qualitative nature of the bodies.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"93.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0025","text":"Equally transient, within electricity, is its opposition of positive and negative; it is so unstable that it depends on the slightest external circumstances, and cannot be placed in any comparison with the determinacy and firmness of the opposition, for example, of acids to metals, etc. The mutability that can take place in this chemical behaviour through highly violent influences, for example an elevated temperature, etc., bears no comparison with the superficiality of the electrical opposition. The further difference, within the series of each of the two sides, between a more or less positive-electric, or more or less negative-electric, constitution is, moreover, both entirely uncertain and unascertained. Yet from these series of bodies (Berzelius at the cited place, pp. 64 f.)","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"93.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0026","text":"“according to their electrical dispositions the electrochemical system is supposed to arise, which is best suited of all to give an idea of chemistry;” these series are now indicated; but as to what they are actually like, it is added on p. 67:","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"93.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0027","text":"“that this is approximately the order of these bodies, but that this matter has been so little investigated that nothing wholly certain can yet be determined concerning this relative order.”—Both the ratio-numbers of those affinity-series (first made by Richter), and the highly interesting reduction, established by Berzelius, of compounds of two bodies to the simplicity of a few quantitative relations, are wholly and entirely independent of that brew which is supposed to be electrochemical.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"93.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0028","text":"If, in those proportions and in their extension, acquired since Richter in every direction, the experimental path has been the correct guiding star, the admixture of these great discoveries with the barrenness of the so-called corpuscular theory, lying outside the path of experience, contrasts with this all the more on its own account; only this beginning, of abandoning the principle of experience, could motivate the further resumption of that idea, earlier initiated chiefly by Ritter, of establishing fixed orders of electropositive and electronegative bodies which were at the same time supposed to have chemical significance.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"93.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0029","text":"The nullity of the foundation assumed for chemical affinity in the opposition of electropositive and electronegative bodies, even if this were in itself factually more correct than it is, soon shows itself on the experimental path itself, which, however, again leads to further inconsistency. It is admitted on p. 73 (loc. cit.) that two so-called electronegative bodies, such as sulphur and oxygen, combine with one another in a far more intimate manner than, for example, oxygen and copper, although the latter is electropositive. The foundation for affinity, based upon the general opposition of positive and negative electricity, must thereby here be relegated in favour of a mere more or less within one and the same series of electrical determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"93.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0030","text":"From this it is now concluded that the degree of affinity of bodies depends not solely on their specific unipolarity (with what hypothesis this determination is connected is of no concern here; it holds here only for the Either of the Positive and the Or of the Negative); the degree of affinity must be derived principally from the intensity of their polarity in general. Thus the consideration of affinity here passes more closely over to the relation of elective affinity, with which we are chiefly concerned; let us see, then, what now results for this. Since it is immediately admitted (ibid., p. 73)","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"93.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0031","text":"that the degree of this polarity, if it does not exist merely in our representation, appears to be no constant quantity, but depends greatly upon temperature, the result given after all this is found to be not only that every chemical action is, according to its ground, an electrical phenomenon, but also that what appears to be the action of so-called elective affinity is brought about only by an electrical polarity present more strongly in certain bodies than in others. To conclude the preceding twisting about in hypothetical representations, there thus remains the category of greater intensity, which is the same formal element as elective affinity in general; and by being posited as a stronger intensity of electrical polarity, the latter is not in the least brought any further to a physical ground than before.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"93.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0032","text":"But even what is here supposed to be determined as greater specific intensity is later reduced only to the modifications already adduced, indicated by Berthollet.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"93.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0033","text":"The merit and renown of Berzelius on account of the doctrine of proportions extended to all chemical relations ought not in itself to have been a reason for refraining from setting forth the defect of the theory adduced; but a closer reason for doing so must be the circumstance that such merit in one aspect of science, as in the case of Newton, is apt to become authority for a baseless edifice of bad categories connected with it, and that precisely such metaphysics is what is put forward with the greatest pretension and repeated just as readily.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"93.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0034","text":"Besides the forms of measure-relation that refer to chemical affinity and elective affinity, others may also be considered with respect to quantities that qualify themselves into a system. Chemical bodies form, in relation to saturation, a system of relations; saturation itself rests upon the determinate proportion in which the reciprocal amounts, which have a particular material existence over against one another, combine. But there are also measure-relations whose moments are inseparable and cannot be represented in an existence of their own, distinct from one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"93.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0035","text":"These are what were previously called immediate self-subsistent measures, and which are represented in the specific gravities of bodies.—Within bodies, they are a relation of weight to volume; the exponent of the relation, which expresses the determinacy of a specific gravity as distinct from others, is a determinate quantum only of comparison, a relation external to them in an external reflection, which is not grounded in their own qualitative behaviour toward an existence standing over against them. The task would be to cognize the exponents of the relations in the series of specific gravities as a system from a rule which would specify a merely arithmetical multiplicity into a series of harmonic nodes.—The same demand would hold for cognition of the chemical affinity-series mentioned.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"93.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0036","text":"But science still has far to go in order to arrive there, as far as to grasp the numbers of the distances of the planets of the solar system in a system of measures.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"93.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0037","text":"Specific gravities, although at first they appear to have no qualitative relation to one another, likewise enter into qualitative relation. When bodies are chemically combined, or merely amalgamated or synsomatized, a neutralization of specific gravities likewise shows itself. The phenomenon was previously adduced that the volume even of a mixture of materials that properly remain chemically indifferent toward one another is not of equal magnitude with the sum of their volume before mixing. In this, they reciprocally modify the quantum of determinacy with which they enter into the relation, and in this way make themselves known as behaving qualitatively toward one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"93.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_23:P0038","text":"Here the quantum of specific gravity manifests itself not merely as a fixed number of comparison, but as a ratio-number that is displaceable; and the exponents of mixtures yield series of measures whose progression is determined by another principle than the ratio-numbers of the specific gravities that are combined with one another. The exponents of these relations are not exclusive measure-determinations; their progression is a continuous one, but contains within itself a specifying law that is distinct from the formally progressing relations in which the amounts are combined, and renders that progression incommensurable with this one.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"93.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_23:P0038"]}],"source_digest":"b3e1d0a5338bebf14723db5d40f9e82ab3bc10087095609fb25f17f494e8481c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM","title":"B. Nodal Line of Measure Relations.","order":94,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BKVM","text":"Die letzte Bestimmung des Maaßverhältnisses war, daß es als specifisch ausschließend ist; das Ausschließen kommt der Neutralität als negativer Einheit der unterschiedenen Momente zu. Für diese fürsichseyende Einheit, die Wahlverwandtschaft, hat sich in Ansehung ihrer Beziehung auf die andern Neutralitäten kein weiteres Princip der Specifikation ergeben; diese bleibt nur in der quantitativen Bestimmung der Affinität überhaupt, nach der es bestimmte Mengen sind, welche sich neutralisiren, und damit anderen relativen Wahlverwandtschaften ihrer Momente gegenüberstehen. Aber ferner um der quantitativen Grundbestimmung willen kontinuirt sich die ausschließende Wahlverwandtschaft auch in die ihr andern Neutralitäten, und diese Kontinuität ist nicht nur äußerliche Beziehung der verschiedenen Neutralitäts-Verhältnisse, als eine Vergleichung, sondern die Neutralität hat als solche eine Trennbarkeit in ihr, indem die, aus deren Einheit sie geworden ist, als selbstständige Etwas, jedes als gleichgültig, mit diesem oder mit andern der gegenüberstehenden Reihe, ob zwar in verschiedenen specifisch bestimmten Mengen sich zu verbinden, in Beziehung treten. Dadurch ist dieß Maaß, das auf einem solchen Verhältnisse in ihm selbst beruht, mit eigner Gleichgültigkeit behaftet; es ist ein an ihm selbst Äußerliches und in seiner Beziehung auf sich ein Veränderliches.\n\nDiese Beziehung des Verhältnißmaaßes auf sich ist verschieden von seiner Äußerlichkeit und Veränderlichkeit, als seiner quantitativen Seite, es ist als Beziehung auf sich gegen diese, eine seyende, qualitative Grundlage;—bleibendes, materielles Substrat, welches, zugleich als die Kontinuität des Maaßes in seiner Äußerlichkeit mit sich selbst, in seiner Qualität jenes Princip der Specification dieser Äußerlichkeit enthalten müßte. Das ausschließende Maaß nach dieser nähern Bestimmung nun, in seinem Fürsichseyn sich äußerlich, stößt sich von sich selbst ab, setzt sich sowohl als ein anderes nur quantitatives, als auch als ein solches anderes Verhältniß, das zugleich ein anderes Maaß ist; ist als an sich selbst specificirende Einheit bestimmt, welche an ihr Maaßverhältnisse producirt. Diese Verhältnisse sind von der obigen Art der Affinitäten, in welchen ein Selbstständiges sich zu Selbstständigen anderer Qualität und zu einer Reihe solcher verhält, verschieden; sie finden an einem und demselben Substrate, innerhalb derselben Momente der Neutralität statt; das Maaß bestimmt sich von sich abstoßend zu andern nur quantitativ verschiedenen Verhältnissen, welche gleichfalls Affinitäten und Maaße bilden abwechselnd mit solchen, welche nur quantitative Verschiedenheiten bleiben. Sie bilden auf solche Weise eine Knotenlinie von Maaßen auf einer Skale des Mehr und Weniger.\n\nEs ist ein Maaßverhältniß vorhanden; eine selbstständige Realität, die qualitativ von andern unterschieden ist. Ein solches Fürsichseyn ist, weil es zugleich wesentlich ein Verhältniß von Quantis ist, der Äußerlichkeit und der Quantumsveränderung offen; es hat eine Weite, innerhalb deren es gegen diese Veränderung gleichgültig bleibt und seine Qualität nicht ändert. Aber es tritt ein Punkt dieser Änderung des Quantitativen ein, auf welchem die Qualität geändert wird, das Quantum sich als specificirend erweist, so daß das veränderte quantitative Verhältniß in ein Maaß und damit in eine neue Qualität, ein neues Etwas, umgeschlagen ist. Das Verhältniß, das an die Stelle des ersten getreten, ist durch dieses bestimmt Theils nach der qualitativen Dieselbigkeit der Momente, die in Affinität stehen, Theils nach der quantitativen Kontinuität. Aber indem der Unterschied in dieses Quantitative fällt, verhält sich das neue Etwas gleichgültig gegen das Vorhergehende, ihr Unterschied ist der äußerliche des Quantums. Es ist also nicht aus dem vorhergehenden, sondern unmittelbar aus sich hervorgetreten; d. i. aus der innerlichen, noch nicht ins Daseyn getretenen specificirenden Einheit. —Die neue Qualität oder das neue Etwas ist demselben Fortgange seiner Veränderung unterworfen und sofort ins Unendliche.\n\nInsofern der Fortgang von einer Qualität in stätiger Kontinuität der Quantität ist, sind die einem qualificirenden Punkte sich nähernden Verhältnisse quantitativ betrachtet, nur durch das Mehr und Weniger unterschieden. Die Veränderung ist nach dieser Seite ['Seice' bei Henning/A.R.] eine allmählige. Aber die Allmähligkeit betrifft bloß das Äußerliche der Veränderung, nicht das Qualitative derselben; das vorhergehende quantitative Verhältniß, das dem folgenden unendlich nahe ist, ist noch ein anderes qualitatives Daseyn. Nach der qualitativen Seite wird daher das bloß quantitative Fortgehen der Allmähligkeit, das keine Grenze an sich selbst ist, absolut abgebrochen; indem die neu eintretende Qualität nach ihrer bloß quantitativen Beziehung eine gegen die verschwindende unbestimmt andere, eine gleichgültige ist, ist der Übergang ein Sprung; beide sind s als völlig äußerliche gegeneinander gesetzt.—Man sucht sich gern durch die Allmähligkeit des Übergangs eine Veränderung begreiflich zu machen; aber vielmehr ist die Allmähligkeit gerade die bloß gleichgültige Änderung, das Gegentheil der qualitativen. In der Allmähligkeit ist vielmehr der Zusammenhang der beiden Realitäten, —sie werden als Zustände, oder als selbstständige Dinge genommen, —aufgehoben; es ist gesetzt, daß keine die Grenze der andern, sondern eine der andern schlechthin äußerlich ist; hiermit wird gerade das, was zum Begreiffen nöthig ist, wenn auch noch so wenig dazu erfordert wird, entfernt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0001","text":"Die letzte Bestimmung des Maaßverhältnisses war, daß es als specifisch ausschließend ist; das Ausschließen kommt der Neutralität als negativer Einheit der unterschiedenen Momente zu. Für diese fürsichseyende Einheit, die Wahlverwandtschaft, hat sich in Ansehung ihrer Beziehung auf die andern Neutralitäten kein weiteres Princip der Specifikation ergeben; diese bleibt nur in der quantitativen Bestimmung der Affinität überhaupt, nach der es bestimmte Mengen sind, welche sich neutralisiren, und damit anderen relativen Wahlverwandtschaften ihrer Momente gegenüberstehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"94.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0002","text":"Aber ferner um der quantitativen Grundbestimmung willen kontinuirt sich die ausschließende Wahlverwandtschaft auch in die ihr andern Neutralitäten, und diese Kontinuität ist nicht nur äußerliche Beziehung der verschiedenen Neutralitäts-Verhältnisse, als eine Vergleichung, sondern die Neutralität hat als solche eine Trennbarkeit in ihr, indem die, aus deren Einheit sie geworden ist, als selbstständige Etwas, jedes als gleichgültig, mit diesem oder mit andern der gegenüberstehenden Reihe, ob zwar in verschiedenen specifisch bestimmten Mengen sich zu verbinden, in Beziehung treten. Dadurch ist dieß Maaß, das auf einem solchen Verhältnisse in ihm selbst beruht, mit eigner Gleichgültigkeit behaftet; es ist ein an ihm selbst Äußerliches und in seiner Beziehung auf sich ein Veränderliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"94.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0003","text":"Diese Beziehung des Verhältnißmaaßes auf sich ist verschieden von seiner Äußerlichkeit und Veränderlichkeit, als seiner quantitativen Seite, es ist als Beziehung auf sich gegen diese, eine seyende, qualitative Grundlage;—bleibendes, materielles Substrat, welches, zugleich als die Kontinuität des Maaßes in seiner Äußerlichkeit mit sich selbst, in seiner Qualität jenes Princip der Specification dieser Äußerlichkeit enthalten müßte. Das ausschließende Maaß nach dieser nähern Bestimmung nun, in seinem Fürsichseyn sich äußerlich, stößt sich von sich selbst ab, setzt sich sowohl als ein anderes nur quantitatives, als auch als ein solches anderes Verhältniß, das zugleich ein anderes Maaß ist; ist als an sich selbst specificirende Einheit bestimmt, welche an ihr Maaßverhältnisse producirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"94.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0004","text":"Diese Verhältnisse sind von der obigen Art der Affinitäten, in welchen ein Selbstständiges sich zu Selbstständigen anderer Qualität und zu einer Reihe solcher verhält, verschieden; sie finden an einem und demselben Substrate, innerhalb derselben Momente der Neutralität statt; das Maaß bestimmt sich von sich abstoßend zu andern nur quantitativ verschiedenen Verhältnissen, welche gleichfalls Affinitäten und Maaße bilden abwechselnd mit solchen, welche nur quantitative Verschiedenheiten bleiben. Sie bilden auf solche Weise eine Knotenlinie von Maaßen auf einer Skale des Mehr und Weniger.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"94.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0005","text":"Es ist ein Maaßverhältniß vorhanden; eine selbstständige Realität, die qualitativ von andern unterschieden ist. Ein solches Fürsichseyn ist, weil es zugleich wesentlich ein Verhältniß von Quantis ist, der Äußerlichkeit und der Quantumsveränderung offen; es hat eine Weite, innerhalb deren es gegen diese Veränderung gleichgültig bleibt und seine Qualität nicht ändert. Aber es tritt ein Punkt dieser Änderung des Quantitativen ein, auf welchem die Qualität geändert wird, das Quantum sich als specificirend erweist, so daß das veränderte quantitative Verhältniß in ein Maaß und damit in eine neue Qualität, ein neues Etwas, umgeschlagen ist. Das Verhältniß, das an die Stelle des ersten getreten, ist durch dieses bestimmt Theils nach der qualitativen Dieselbigkeit der Momente, die in Affinität stehen, Theils nach der quantitativen Kontinuität.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"94.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0006","text":"Aber indem der Unterschied in dieses Quantitative fällt, verhält sich das neue Etwas gleichgültig gegen das Vorhergehende, ihr Unterschied ist der äußerliche des Quantums. Es ist also nicht aus dem vorhergehenden, sondern unmittelbar aus sich hervorgetreten; d. i. aus der innerlichen, noch nicht ins Daseyn getretenen specificirenden Einheit. —Die neue Qualität oder das neue Etwas ist demselben Fortgange seiner Veränderung unterworfen und sofort ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"94.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0007","text":"Insofern der Fortgang von einer Qualität in stätiger Kontinuität der Quantität ist, sind die einem qualificirenden Punkte sich nähernden Verhältnisse quantitativ betrachtet, nur durch das Mehr und Weniger unterschieden. Die Veränderung ist nach dieser Seite ['Seice' bei Henning/A.R.] eine allmählige. Aber die Allmähligkeit betrifft bloß das Äußerliche der Veränderung, nicht das Qualitative derselben; das vorhergehende quantitative Verhältniß, das dem folgenden unendlich nahe ist, ist noch ein anderes qualitatives Daseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"94.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0008","text":"Nach der qualitativen Seite wird daher das bloß quantitative Fortgehen der Allmähligkeit, das keine Grenze an sich selbst ist, absolut abgebrochen; indem die neu eintretende Qualität nach ihrer bloß quantitativen Beziehung eine gegen die verschwindende unbestimmt andere, eine gleichgültige ist, ist der Übergang ein Sprung; beide sind s als völlig äußerliche gegeneinander gesetzt.—Man sucht sich gern durch die Allmähligkeit des Übergangs eine Veränderung begreiflich zu machen; aber vielmehr ist die Allmähligkeit gerade die bloß gleichgültige Änderung, das Gegentheil der qualitativen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"94.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0009","text":"In der Allmähligkeit ist vielmehr der Zusammenhang der beiden Realitäten, —sie werden als Zustände, oder als selbstständige Dinge genommen, —aufgehoben; es ist gesetzt, daß keine die Grenze der andern, sondern eine der andern schlechthin äußerlich ist; hiermit wird gerade das, was zum Begreiffen nöthig ist, wenn auch noch so wenig dazu erfordert wird, entfernt.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"94.9"}],"sha256":"bc685b2f2334c2bb8a0eea190ec35e2fcc7750ba8eedd2d687c2ad8106483079","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104401184213Z_19b60b3c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Nodal Line of Measure Relations.","source_sha256":"bc685b2f2334c2bb8a0eea190ec35e2fcc7750ba8eedd2d687c2ad8106483079","sha256":"279a524ad2b162c97627f364fe1c4e8975363f11edab8315cd95f882df1a8cb1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:44:01.184275+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0001","text":"The final determination of the relation of measure was that it is specifically exclusive; exclusion belongs to neutrality as the negative unity of the distinguished moments. For this unity that is for itself, elective affinity, no further principle of specification has emerged with regard to its relation to the other neutralities; it remains merely in the quantitative determination of affinity in general, according to which it is determinate quantities that neutralize themselves and thereby stand opposed to other relative elective affinities of their moments.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"94.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0002","text":"But further, by virtue of the quantitative fundamental determination, exclusive elective affinity also continues itself into the neutralities other than it, and this continuity is not merely an external relation of the different relations of neutrality, as a comparison, but neutrality as such has a separability within it, in that those from whose unity it has become enter into relation, as self-subsistent somethings, each as indifferent to combining with this or with others of the opposed series, although in differently specifically determined quantities. Thereby this measure, which rests upon such a relation within itself, is affected with an indifference of its own; it is something external in itself and something mutable in its relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"94.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0003","text":"This relation of relational measure to itself is distinct from its externality and mutability, as its quantitative side; as relation to itself over against this, it is a being, qualitative foundation;—an enduring, material substrate, which, at the same time as the continuity of measure with itself in its externality, would have to contain in its quality that principle of the specification of this externality. Exclusive measure in accordance with this more precise determination, now external to itself in its being-for-itself, repels itself from itself, posits itself both as another merely quantitative relation and as such another relation that is at the same time another measure; it is determined as a unity specifying itself in itself, which produces relations of measure in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"94.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0004","text":"These relations are different from the above kind of affinities, in which a self-subsistent entity relates to self-subsistent entities of another quality and to a series of such entities; they take place in one and the same substrate, within the same moments of neutrality; repelling itself from itself, measure determines itself into other relations differing merely quantitatively, which likewise constitute affinities and measures, alternating with such as remain merely quantitative differences. In this way they form a nodal line of measures upon a scale of more and less.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"94.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0005","text":"A relation of measure is present; a self-subsistent reality qualitatively distinct from others. Since such a being-for-itself is at the same time essentially a relation of quanta, it is open to externality and to alteration of quantum; it has a range within which it remains indifferent to this alteration and does not alter its quality. But there occurs a point in this alteration of the quantitative at which the quality is altered, the quantum proves itself to be specifying, so that the altered quantitative relation has passed over into a measure and thereby into a new quality, a new something. The relation that has taken the place of the first is determined by this, partly according to the qualitative sameness of the moments that stand in affinity, partly according to quantitative continuity.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"94.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0006","text":"But since the difference falls into this quantitative element, the new something behaves indifferently toward the preceding one; their difference is the external difference of quantum. Thus it has not emerged from the preceding one, but immediately from itself; i.e. from the internal, not yet emerged into existence, specifying unity. —The new quality or the new something is subject to the same course of its alteration, and so on to infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"94.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0007","text":"Insofar as the progression from one quality is in continuous continuity of quantity, the relations approaching a qualifying point are, viewed quantitatively, distinguished only by more and less. The alteration is, on this side ['Seice' in Henning/A.R.], gradual. But gradualness concerns only the externality of the alteration, not its qualitative aspect; the preceding quantitative relation, which is infinitely close to the following one, is still another qualitative existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"94.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0008","text":"On the qualitative side, therefore, the merely quantitative progression of gradualness, which has no limit in itself, is absolutely interrupted; since the newly entering quality, according to its merely quantitative relation, is an indeterminately other, an indifferent one, as against the vanishing quality, the transition is a leap; the two are posited as wholly external to one another.—One likes to make a change comprehensible to oneself by means of the gradualness of the transition; but rather, gradualness is precisely the merely indifferent alteration, the opposite of the qualitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"94.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0009","text":"In gradualness, rather, the connection of the two realities—whether they are taken as states or as self-subsistent things—is sublated; it is posited that neither is the limit of the other, but that one is simply external to the other; thereby precisely that which is necessary for comprehending, however little may be required for it, is removed.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"94.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BKVM:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"fd8565cab8e6bc91f838f469060dcfafa2a041a9fe562d74b270e12f389b66ff","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Knotenlinie von Maaßverhältnissen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Knotenlinie von Maaßverhältnissen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24","title":"Remark.","order":95,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_24","text":"Das natürliche Zahlensystem zeigt schon eine solche Knotenlinie von qualitativen Momenten, die sich in dem bloß äußerlichen Fortgang hervorthun. Es ist eines Theils ein bloß quantitatives Vor- und Zurückgehen, ein fortwährendes Hinzuthun oder Wegnehmen, so daß jede Zahl dasselbe arithmetische Verhältniß zu ihrer vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden hat, als diese zu ihrer vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden u.s.f. Aber die hierdurch entstehenden Zahlen haben auch zu andern vorhergehenden oder folgenden ein specifisches Verhältniß, entweder ein solches vielfaches von einer derselben als eine ganze Zahl ausdrückt, oder Potenz und Wurzel zu seyn.—In den musikalischen Verhältnissen, tritt ein harmonisches Verhältniß in der Skale des quantitativen Fortgehens durch ein Quantum ein, ohne daß dieses Quantum für sich auf der Skale zu seinem vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden ein anderes Verhältniß hätte, als diese wieder zu ihren vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden. Indem folgende Töne vom Grundtone sich immer mehr zu entfernen oder Zahlen durch das arithmetische Fortgehen nur noch mehr andere zu werden scheinen, thut sich vielmehr auf einmal eine Rückkehr, eine überraschende Übereinstimmung hervor, die nicht durch das unmittelbar vorhergehende qualitativ vorbereitet war, sondern als eine actio in distans, als eine Beziehung zu einem Entfernten, erscheint; der Fortgang an bloß gleichgültigen Verhältnissen, welche die vorhergehende specifische Realität nicht ändern oder auch überhaupt keine solche bilden, unterbricht sich auf einmal, und indem er in quantitativer Rücksicht auf dieselbe Weise fortgesetzt ist, bricht somit durch einen Sprung ein specifisches Verhältniß ein.\n\nIn chemischen Verbindungen kommen bei der progressiven Änderung der Mischungsverhältnisse solche qualitative Knoten und Sprünge vor, daß zwei Stoffe auf besondern Punkten der Mischungsskale, Produkte bilden, welche besondere Qualitäten zeigen. Diese Produkte unterscheiden sich nicht bloß durch ein Mehr und Weniger von einander, noch sind sie mit den Verhältnissen, die jenen Knotenverhältnissen nahe liegen, schon vorhanden, etwa nur in einem schwächern Grade, sondern sind an solche Punkte selbst gebunden. Z. B. die Verbindungen voll Sauerstoff und Stikstoff geben die verschiedenen Stikstoffoxyde und Salpetersäuren, die nur an bestimmten Quantitäts-Verhältnissen der Mischung hervortreten und wesentlich verschiedene Qualitäten haben, so daß in dazwischen liegenden Mischungsverhältnissen keine Verbindungen Von specifischen Existenzen erfolgen.—Die Metalloxyde, z.B. die Bleioxyde bilden sich auf gewissen quantitativen Punkten der Oxydation, und unterscheiden sich durch Farben und andere Qualitäten. Sie gehen nicht allmählig in einander über, die zwischen jenen Knoten liegende Verhältnisse geben kein Neutrales, kein specifisches Daseyn. Ohne durch Zwischenstufen durchgegangen zu seyn, tritt eine specifische Verbindung auf, die auf einem Maaßverhältnisse beruht, und eigene Qualitäten hat.—Oder das Wasser, indem es seine Temperatur ändert, wird damit nicht bloß mehr oder weniger warm, sondern geht durch die Zustände der Härte, der tropfbaren Flüssigkeit und der elastischen Flüssigkeit hindurch; diese verschiedenen Zustände treten nicht allmählig ein, sondern eben das bloß allmählige Fortgehen der Temperatur-Änderung wird durch diese Punkte mit einemmale unterbrochen und gehemmt, und der Eintritt eines andern Zustandes ist ein Sprung.—Alle Geburt und Tod, sind, statt eine fortgesetzte Allmähligkeit zu seyn, vielmehr ein Abbrechen derselben, und der Sprung aus quantitativer Veränderung in qualitative.\n\nEs giebt keinen Sprung in der Natur, wird gesagt; und die gewöhnliche Vorstellung, wenn sie ein Entstehen oder Vergehen begreifen soll, meint, wie erinnert, es damit begriffen zu haben, daß sie es als ein allmähliges Hervorgehen oder Verschwinden vorstellt. Es hat sich aber gezeigt, daß die Veränderungen des Seyns überhaupt nicht nur das Übergehen einer Größe in eine andere Größe, sondern Übergang vom Qualitativen in das Quantitative und umgekehrt sind, ein Anders-werden, das ein Abbrechen des Allmähligen und ein Qualitativ-Anderes gegen das vorhergehende Daseyn ist. Das Wasser wird durch die Erkältung nicht nach und nach hart, so daß es breiartig würde und allmählig bis zur Konsistenz des Eises sich verhärtete, sondern ist auf einmal hart; schon mit der ganzen Temperatur des Eispunktes, wenn es ruhig steht, kann es noch seine ganze Flüssigkeit haben, und eine geringe Erschütterung bringt es in den Zustand der Härte.\n\nBei der Allmähligkeit des Entstehens liegt die Vorstellung zu Grunde, daß das Entstehende schon sinnlich oder überhaupt wirklich vorhanden, nur wegen seiner Kleinheit noch nicht wahrnehmbar, so wie bei der Allmähligkeit des Verschwindens, daß das Nichtseyn oder das Andere an seine Stelle Tretende gleichfalls vorhanden, nur noch nicht bemerkbar sey;—und zwar vorhanden nicht in dem Sinne, daß das Andere in dem vorhandenen Andern an sich enthalten, sondern daß es als Daseyn, nur unbemerkbar, vorhanden sey. Es wird damit das Entstehen und Vergehen überhaupt aufgehoben, oder das An-sich, das Innere, in welchem etwas vor seinem Daseyn ist, in eine Kleinheit des äußerlichen Daseyns verwandelt, und der wesentliche, oder der Begriffsunterschied in einen äußerlichen, bloßen Größeunterschied.—Das Begreiflichmachen eines Entstehens oder Vergehens aus der Allmähligkeit der Veränderung hat die der Tautologie eigene Langweiligkeit; es hat das Entstehende oder Vergehende schon vorher ganz fertig und macht die Veränderung zu einer bloßen Änderung eines äußerlichen Unterschiedes, wodurch sie in der That nur eine Tautologie ist. Die Schwierigkeit für solchen begreifen wollenden Verstand liegt in dem qualitativen Übergang von Etwas in sein Anderes überhaupt und in sein Entgegengesetztes; dagegen spiegelt er sich die Identität und die Veränderung als die gleichgültige, äußerliche des Quantitativen vor.\n\nIm Moralischen, insofern es in der Sphäre des Seyns betrachtet wird, findet derselbe Übergang des Quantitativen ins Qualitative statt; und verschiedene Qualitäten erscheinen, sich auf eine Verschiedenheit der Größe zu gründen. Es ist ein Mehr und Weniger, wodurch das Maaß des Leichtsinns überschritten wird, und etwas ganz Anderes, Verbrechen, hervortritt, wodurch Recht in Unrecht, Tugend in Laster übergeht.—So erhalten auch Staaten durch ihren Größenunterschied, wenn das Übrige als gleich angenommen wird, einen verschiedenen qualitativen Charakter. Gesetze und Verfassung werden zu etwas Anderem, wenn der Umfang des Staats und die Anzahl der Bürger sich erweitert. Der Staat hat ein Maaß seiner Größe, über welche hinausgetrieben er haltungslos in sich zerfällt, unter derselben Verfassung, welche bei nur anderem Umfange sein Glück und seine Stärke ausmachte.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0001","text":"Das natürliche Zahlensystem zeigt schon eine solche Knotenlinie von qualitativen Momenten, die sich in dem bloß äußerlichen Fortgang hervorthun. Es ist eines Theils ein bloß quantitatives Vor- und Zurückgehen, ein fortwährendes Hinzuthun oder Wegnehmen, so daß jede Zahl dasselbe arithmetische Verhältniß zu ihrer vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden hat, als diese zu ihrer vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"95.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0002","text":"Aber die hierdurch entstehenden Zahlen haben auch zu andern vorhergehenden oder folgenden ein specifisches Verhältniß, entweder ein solches vielfaches von einer derselben als eine ganze Zahl ausdrückt, oder Potenz und Wurzel zu seyn.—In den musikalischen Verhältnissen, tritt ein harmonisches Verhältniß in der Skale des quantitativen Fortgehens durch ein Quantum ein, ohne daß dieses Quantum für sich auf der Skale zu seinem vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden ein anderes Verhältniß hätte, als diese wieder zu ihren vorhergehenden und nachfolgenden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"95.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0003","text":"Indem folgende Töne vom Grundtone sich immer mehr zu entfernen oder Zahlen durch das arithmetische Fortgehen nur noch mehr andere zu werden scheinen, thut sich vielmehr auf einmal eine Rückkehr, eine überraschende Übereinstimmung hervor, die nicht durch das unmittelbar vorhergehende qualitativ vorbereitet war, sondern als eine actio in distans, als eine Beziehung zu einem Entfernten, erscheint; der Fortgang an bloß gleichgültigen Verhältnissen, welche die vorhergehende specifische Realität nicht ändern oder auch überhaupt keine solche bilden, unterbricht sich auf einmal, und indem er in quantitativer Rücksicht auf dieselbe Weise fortgesetzt ist, bricht somit durch einen Sprung ein specifisches Verhältniß ein.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"95.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0004","text":"In chemischen Verbindungen kommen bei der progressiven Änderung der Mischungsverhältnisse solche qualitative Knoten und Sprünge vor, daß zwei Stoffe auf besondern Punkten der Mischungsskale, Produkte bilden, welche besondere Qualitäten zeigen. Diese Produkte unterscheiden sich nicht bloß durch ein Mehr und Weniger von einander, noch sind sie mit den Verhältnissen, die jenen Knotenverhältnissen nahe liegen, schon vorhanden, etwa nur in einem schwächern Grade, sondern sind an solche Punkte selbst gebunden. Z. B. die Verbindungen voll Sauerstoff und Stikstoff geben die verschiedenen Stikstoffoxyde und Salpetersäuren, die nur an bestimmten Quantitäts-Verhältnissen der Mischung hervortreten und wesentlich verschiedene Qualitäten haben, so daß in dazwischen liegenden Mischungsverhältnissen keine Verbindungen Von specifischen Existenzen erfolgen.—Die Metalloxyde, z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"95.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0005","text":"die Bleioxyde bilden sich auf gewissen quantitativen Punkten der Oxydation, und unterscheiden sich durch Farben und andere Qualitäten. Sie gehen nicht allmählig in einander über, die zwischen jenen Knoten liegende Verhältnisse geben kein Neutrales, kein specifisches Daseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"95.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0006","text":"Ohne durch Zwischenstufen durchgegangen zu seyn, tritt eine specifische Verbindung auf, die auf einem Maaßverhältnisse beruht, und eigene Qualitäten hat.—Oder das Wasser, indem es seine Temperatur ändert, wird damit nicht bloß mehr oder weniger warm, sondern geht durch die Zustände der Härte, der tropfbaren Flüssigkeit und der elastischen Flüssigkeit hindurch; diese verschiedenen Zustände treten nicht allmählig ein, sondern eben das bloß allmählige Fortgehen der Temperatur-Änderung wird durch diese Punkte mit einemmale unterbrochen und gehemmt, und der Eintritt eines andern Zustandes ist ein Sprung.—Alle Geburt und Tod, sind, statt eine fortgesetzte Allmähligkeit zu seyn, vielmehr ein Abbrechen derselben, und der Sprung aus quantitativer Veränderung in qualitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"95.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0007","text":"Es giebt keinen Sprung in der Natur, wird gesagt; und die gewöhnliche Vorstellung, wenn sie ein Entstehen oder Vergehen begreifen soll, meint, wie erinnert, es damit begriffen zu haben, daß sie es als ein allmähliges Hervorgehen oder Verschwinden vorstellt. Es hat sich aber gezeigt, daß die Veränderungen des Seyns überhaupt nicht nur das Übergehen einer Größe in eine andere Größe, sondern Übergang vom Qualitativen in das Quantitative und umgekehrt sind, ein Anders-werden, das ein Abbrechen des Allmähligen und ein Qualitativ-Anderes gegen das vorhergehende Daseyn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"95.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0008","text":"Das Wasser wird durch die Erkältung nicht nach und nach hart, so daß es breiartig würde und allmählig bis zur Konsistenz des Eises sich verhärtete, sondern ist auf einmal hart; schon mit der ganzen Temperatur des Eispunktes, wenn es ruhig steht, kann es noch seine ganze Flüssigkeit haben, und eine geringe Erschütterung bringt es in den Zustand der Härte.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"95.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0009","text":"Bei der Allmähligkeit des Entstehens liegt die Vorstellung zu Grunde, daß das Entstehende schon sinnlich oder überhaupt wirklich vorhanden, nur wegen seiner Kleinheit noch nicht wahrnehmbar, so wie bei der Allmähligkeit des Verschwindens, daß das Nichtseyn oder das Andere an seine Stelle Tretende gleichfalls vorhanden, nur noch nicht bemerkbar sey;—und zwar vorhanden nicht in dem Sinne, daß das Andere in dem vorhandenen Andern an sich enthalten, sondern daß es als Daseyn, nur unbemerkbar, vorhanden sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"95.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0010","text":"Es wird damit das Entstehen und Vergehen überhaupt aufgehoben, oder das An-sich, das Innere, in welchem etwas vor seinem Daseyn ist, in eine Kleinheit des äußerlichen Daseyns verwandelt, und der wesentliche, oder der Begriffsunterschied in einen äußerlichen, bloßen Größeunterschied.—Das Begreiflichmachen eines Entstehens oder Vergehens aus der Allmähligkeit der Veränderung hat die der Tautologie eigene Langweiligkeit; es hat das Entstehende oder Vergehende schon vorher ganz fertig und macht die Veränderung zu einer bloßen Änderung eines äußerlichen Unterschiedes, wodurch sie in der That nur eine Tautologie ist. Die Schwierigkeit für solchen begreifen wollenden Verstand liegt in dem qualitativen Übergang von Etwas in sein Anderes überhaupt und in sein Entgegengesetztes; dagegen spiegelt er sich die Identität und die Veränderung als die gleichgültige, äußerliche des Quantitativen vor.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"95.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0011","text":"Im Moralischen, insofern es in der Sphäre des Seyns betrachtet wird, findet derselbe Übergang des Quantitativen ins Qualitative statt; und verschiedene Qualitäten erscheinen, sich auf eine Verschiedenheit der Größe zu gründen. Es ist ein Mehr und Weniger, wodurch das Maaß des Leichtsinns überschritten wird, und etwas ganz Anderes, Verbrechen, hervortritt, wodurch Recht in Unrecht, Tugend in Laster übergeht.—So erhalten auch Staaten durch ihren Größenunterschied, wenn das Übrige als gleich angenommen wird, einen verschiedenen qualitativen Charakter. Gesetze und Verfassung werden zu etwas Anderem, wenn der Umfang des Staats und die Anzahl der Bürger sich erweitert. Der Staat hat ein Maaß seiner Größe, über welche hinausgetrieben er haltungslos in sich zerfällt, unter derselben Verfassung, welche bei nur anderem Umfange sein Glück und seine Stärke ausmachte.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"95.11"}],"sha256":"1c6d43b0e12d2284b70acc19d1b0a94dbe5fc7ae7e709165766ed8e45350146a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104415333693Z_da5b6bc7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"1c6d43b0e12d2284b70acc19d1b0a94dbe5fc7ae7e709165766ed8e45350146a","sha256":"ef2c49381f53d40b97549d26d9c87a0fe1df5fa61cf81ccb97811e9448e4a398","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:44:15.333735+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0001","text":"The natural system of numbers already displays such a nodal line of qualitative moments, which make themselves manifest in merely external progression. On the one hand, it is a merely quantitative going forward and backward, a continual adding or subtracting, so that each number has the same arithmetical relation to its preceding and succeeding number as these have to their preceding and succeeding numbers, and so forth.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"95.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0002","text":"But the numbers thereby arising also have a specific relation to other preceding or succeeding ones, either such a multiple of one of them as is expressed by a whole number, or being power and root.—In musical relations, a harmonic relation enters into the scale of quantitative progression through a quantum, without this quantum, taken by itself, having on the scale any relation to its preceding and succeeding one other than these in turn have to their preceding and succeeding ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"95.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0003","text":"While subsequent tones seem to move ever farther away from the fundamental tone, or numbers, through arithmetical progression, seem merely to become ever more other, there instead suddenly manifests itself a return, a surprising correspondence, which was not qualitatively prepared by what immediately preceded, but appears as an actio in distans, as a relation to something distant; the progression in merely indifferent relations, which do not alter the preceding specific reality or indeed do not constitute any such reality at all, is suddenly interrupted, and while it is continued in the same way in quantitative respect, a specific relation thus breaks in through a leap.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"95.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0004","text":"In chemical compounds, in the progressive alteration of the proportions of mixture, such qualitative nodes and leaps occur, such that two substances, at particular points on the scale of mixture, form products which display particular qualities. These products are distinguished from one another not merely by a more or less, nor are they already present in proportions close to those nodal relations, perhaps merely in a weaker degree, but are bound to such points themselves. For example, the compounds of oxygen and nitrogen yield the various nitrogen oxides and nitric acids, which emerge only at determinate quantitative proportions of mixture and have essentially different qualities, so that in intervening proportions of mixture no compounds of specific existences take place.—The metallic oxides, e.g.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"95.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0005","text":"the oxides of lead, are formed at certain quantitative points of oxidation and differ in colour and other qualities. They do not pass gradually into one another; the proportions lying between those nodes yield nothing neutral, no specific being.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"95.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0006","text":"Without having passed through intermediate stages, a specific compound emerges, which rests upon a relation of measure and has qualities of its own.—Or water, in changing its temperature, does not thereby merely become more or less warm, but passes through the states of solidity, droplet-form fluidity, and elastic fluidity; these different states do not arise gradually, but rather the merely gradual progression of the change in temperature is at once interrupted and arrested by these points, and the onset of another state is a leap.—All birth and death, instead of being a continuous gradualness, are rather an interruption of it, and the leap from quantitative alteration into qualitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"95.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0007","text":"There is said to be no leap in nature; and ordinary representation, when it is to comprehend an arising or passing away, thinks, as was recalled, that it has thereby comprehended it by representing it as a gradual emergence or disappearance. But it has been shown that the alterations of being in general are not merely the transition of one magnitude into another magnitude, but transition from the qualitative into the quantitative and conversely, a becoming-other that is an interruption of gradualness and a qualitatively-other as against the preceding determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"95.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0008","text":"Water does not gradually become hard through cooling, so that it would become mushy and gradually harden to the consistency of ice; rather, it is hard all at once. Even at the entire temperature of the freezing point, if it stands still, it can still retain its entire fluidity, and a slight agitation brings it into the state of solidity.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"95.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0009","text":"At the basis of the idea of the gradualness of arising lies the notion that what arises is already sensuously or generally actually present, only not yet perceptible because of its smallness; just as, in the gradualness of disappearance, non-being or the other taking its place is likewise present, only not yet noticeable;—namely, present not in the sense that the other is contained in itself in the other that is present, but that it is present as determinate being, only unnoticeable.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"95.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0010","text":"Thereby arising and passing away in general are sublated, or the in-itself, the inner, in which something is before its determinate being, is transformed into a smallness of external determinate being, and the essential, or conceptual, difference into an external, merely difference of magnitude.—The making comprehensible of an arising or passing away from the gradualness of alteration has the tediousness proper to tautology; it already has what is arising or passing away entirely ready-made beforehand and makes alteration into a mere modification of an external difference, whereby it is in fact only a tautology. The difficulty for an understanding that wishes to comprehend in such a manner lies in the qualitative transition of something into its other in general and into its opposite; in contrast, it deludes itself with identity and with alteration as the indifferent, external alteration of the quantitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"95.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_24:P0011","text":"In the moral sphere, insofar as it is considered within the sphere of being, the same transition of the quantitative into the qualitative takes place; and different qualities appear to be based upon a difference of magnitude. It is a more and less through which the measure of frivolity is exceeded and something entirely other, crime, emerges, through which right passes over into wrong, virtue into vice.—States likewise acquire a different qualitative character through their difference in size, when everything else is assumed to be the same. Laws and constitution become something other when the extent of the state and the number of citizens expands. The state has a measure of its size, beyond which, when driven, it disintegrates within itself without stability, under the same constitution which, with only a different extent, constituted its happiness and strength.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"95.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_24:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"58571710d6aba387714a6769cd6ccbc30f094c90b3a851951f0368b5eb723182","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0","title":"C. The Measureless.","order":96,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDM0","text":"Das ausschließende Maaß bleibt in seinem realisirten Fürsichseyn selbst, mit dem Momente quantitativen Daseyns behaftet, darum des Auf- und Absteigens an der Skale des Quantums fähig, auf welcher die Verhältnisse sich ändern. Etwas oder eine Qualität als auf solchem Verhältnisse beruhend, wird über sich hinaus in das Maaßlose getrieben, und geht durch die bloße Änderung seiner Größe zu Grunde. Die Größe ist die Beschaffenheit, an der ein Daseyn mit dem Scheine von Unverfänglichkeit ergriffen und wodurch es zerstört werden kann.\n\nDas abstrakte Maaßlose ist das Quantum überhaupt als in sich bestimmungslos, und als nur gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, durch welche das Maaß nicht verändert wird. In der Knotenlinie der Maaße ist sie zugleich als specificirend gesetzt; jenes abstrakte Maaßlose hebt sich zur qualitativen Bestimmtheit auf; das neue Maaßverhältniß, in welches das zuerst vorhandene übergeht, ist ein Maaßloses in Rücksicht auf dieses, an ihm selbst aber ebenso eine für sich-seyende Qualität; so ist die Abwechslung von specifischen Existenzen miteinander und derselben ebenso mit bloß quantitativbleibenden Verhältnissen gesetzt,—sofort ins Unendliche. Was also in diesem Übergehen vorhanden ist, ist sowohl die Negation der specifischen Verhältnisse, als die Negation des quantitativen Fortgangs selbst; das fürsichseyende Unendliche.—Die qualitative Unendlichkeit, wie sie am Daseyn ist, war das Hervorbrechen des Unendlichen am Endlichen, als unmittelbarer Übergang und Verschwinden des Diesseits in seinem Jenseits. Die quantitative Unendlichkeit hingegen ist ihrer Bestimmtheit nach schon die Kontinuität des Quantums, eine Kontinuität desselben über sich hinaus. Das Qualitativ-Endliche wird zum Unendlichen; das Quantitativ-Endliche ist sein Jenseits an ihm selbst, und weist über sich hinaus. Aber diese Unendlichkeit der Specifikation des Maaßes setzt ebensowohl das Qualitative wie das Quantitative als sich in einander aufhebend, und damit die erste, unmittelbare Einheit derselben, welche das Maaß überhaupt ist, als in sich zurückgekehrt und damit selbst als gesetzt. Das Qualitative, eine specifische Existenz, geht in eine andere so über, daß nur eine Veränderung der Größebestimmtheit eines Verhältnisses vorgeht; die Veränderung des Qualitativen selbst in Qualitatives ist damit als eine äußerliche und gleichgültige, und als ein Zusammengehen mit sich selbst gesetzt; das Quantitative hebt sich ohnehin als umschlagend in Qualitatives, das An- und Für-Sichbestimmtseyn, auf. Diese so sich in ihrem Wechsel der Maaße in sich selbst kontinuirende Einheit ist die wahrhaft bestehenbleibende, selbstständige Materie, Sache.\n\nWas hiermit vorhanden ist, ist à) eine und dieselbe Sache, welche als Grundlage in ihren Unterscheidungen und als perennirend gesetzt ist. Schon im Quantum überhaupt beginnt dieß Abtrennen des Seyns von seiner Bestimmtheit; groß ist etwas, als gleichgültig gegen seine seyende Bestimmtheit. Im Maaße ist die Sache selbst bereits an sich Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen,—der beiden Momente, die innerhalb der allgemeinen Sphäre des Seyns, den Unterschied ausmachen, und wovon das Eine das Jenseits des Andern ist; das perennirende Substrat hat auf diese Weise zunachst an ihm selbst die Bestimmung seyender Unendlichkeit. ß) Diese Dieselbigkeit des Substrats ist darin gesetzt, daß die qualitativen Selbstständigkeiten, in welche die maaßbestimmende Einheit abgestoßen ist, nur in quantitativen Unterschieden bestehen, so daß das Substrat sich in dieß sein Unterscheiden kontinuirt; ç) in dem unendlichen Progresse der Knotenreihe ist die Kontinuirung des Qualitativen in das quantitative Fortgehen, als in eine gleichgültige Veränderung, aber ebenso die darin enthaltene Negation des Qualitativen, und zugleich damit der bloß quantitativen Äußerlichkeit, gesetzt. Das quantitative Hinausweisen über sich zu einem Andern, als anderem Quantitativen geht unter in dem Hervortreten eines Verhältnißmaaßes, einer Qualität, und das qualitative Übergehen hebt sich eben darin auf, daß die neue Qualität selbst nur ein quantitatives Verhältniß ist. Dieß Übergehen des Qualitativen und des Quantitativen in einander geht auf dem Boden ihrer Einheit vor, und der Sinn dieses Processes ist nur das Daseyn, das Zeigen oder Setzen, daß demselben ein solches Substrat zu Grunde liegt, welches ihre Einheit sey.\n\nIn den Reihen selbstständiger Maaßverhältnisse sind die einseitigen Glieder der Reihen unmittelbare qualitative Etwas, (die specifischen Schweren, oder die chemische Stoffe, die basischen oder kalischen, die sauren z.B.), und dann die Neutralisationen derselben, (- worunter hier auch die Verbindungen von Stoffen verschiedener specifischer Schwere zu begreiffen sind—) sind selbstständige und selbst ausschließende Maaßverhältnisse, gegeneinander gleichgültige Totalitäten fürsichseyenden Daseyns. Nun sind solche Verhältnisse nur als Knoten eines und desselben Substrats bestimmt. Damit sind die Maaße und die damit gesetzten Selbstständigkeiten zu Zuständen herabgesetzt. Die Veränderung ist nur Änderung eines Zustandes und das Übergehende ist als darin dasselbe bleibend gesetzt.\n\nUm die Fortbestimmung, welche das Maaß durchloffen hat, zu übersehen, so fassen sich die Momente derselben so zusammen, daß das Maaß zunächst die selbst unmittelbare Einheit der Qualität und der Quantität ist als ein gewöhnliches Quantum, das aber specifisch ist. Hiermit als nicht auf Anderes, sondern auf sich beziehende Quantitätsbestimmtheit ist es wesentlich Verhaltniß. Daher ferner enthält es seine Momente als aufgehobene und ungetrennte in sich; wie immer in einem Begriffe, ist der Unterschied in demselben so, daß jedes von dessen Momenten selbst Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen ist. Dieser hiermit reale Unterschied ergiebt eine Menge von Maaßverhältnissen die als formelle Totalitäten in sich selbstständig sind. Die Reihen, welche die Seiten dieser Verhaltnisse bilden, sind für jedes einzelne Glied, das als einer Seite zugehörig sich zu der ganzen gegenüberstehenden Reihe verhält, dieselbe konstante Ordnung. Diese, als bloße Ordnung, noch ganz äußerliche Einheit, zeigt sich zwar als immanente specificirende Einheit eines fürsichseyenden Maaßes unterschieden von seinen Specifikationen; aber das specificirende Princip ist noch nicht der freie Begriff welcher allein seinen Unterschieden immanente Bestimmung giebt, sondern das Princip ist zunächst nur Substrat, eine Materie, für deren Unterschiede, um als Totalitäten, zu seyn, d. i. die Natur des sich selbst gleich bleibenden Substrats in sich zu haben, nur die äußerliche quantitative Bestimmung vorhanden ist, die sich als Verschiedenheit der Qualität zugleich zeigt. Die Maaßbestimmnng ist in dieser Einheit des Substrats mit sich selbst eine aufgehobene, ihre Qualität ein durch das Quantum (bestimmter, äußerlicher Zustand.—Dieser Verlauf ist ebensowohl die realisirende Fortbestimmung des Maaßes, als sie das Herabsetzen desselben zu einem Momente ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0001","text":"Das ausschließende Maaß bleibt in seinem realisirten Fürsichseyn selbst, mit dem Momente quantitativen Daseyns behaftet, darum des Auf- und Absteigens an der Skale des Quantums fähig, auf welcher die Verhältnisse sich ändern. Etwas oder eine Qualität als auf solchem Verhältnisse beruhend, wird über sich hinaus in das Maaßlose getrieben, und geht durch die bloße Änderung seiner Größe zu Grunde. Die Größe ist die Beschaffenheit, an der ein Daseyn mit dem Scheine von Unverfänglichkeit ergriffen und wodurch es zerstört werden kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"96.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0002","text":"Das abstrakte Maaßlose ist das Quantum überhaupt als in sich bestimmungslos, und als nur gleichgültige Bestimmtheit, durch welche das Maaß nicht verändert wird. In der Knotenlinie der Maaße ist sie zugleich als specificirend gesetzt; jenes abstrakte Maaßlose hebt sich zur qualitativen Bestimmtheit auf; das neue Maaßverhältniß, in welches das zuerst vorhandene übergeht, ist ein Maaßloses in Rücksicht auf dieses, an ihm selbst aber ebenso eine für sich-seyende Qualität; so ist die Abwechslung von specifischen Existenzen miteinander und derselben ebenso mit bloß quantitativbleibenden Verhältnissen gesetzt,—sofort ins Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"96.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0003","text":"Was also in diesem Übergehen vorhanden ist, ist sowohl die Negation der specifischen Verhältnisse, als die Negation des quantitativen Fortgangs selbst; das fürsichseyende Unendliche.—Die qualitative Unendlichkeit, wie sie am Daseyn ist, war das Hervorbrechen des Unendlichen am Endlichen, als unmittelbarer Übergang und Verschwinden des Diesseits in seinem Jenseits. Die quantitative Unendlichkeit hingegen ist ihrer Bestimmtheit nach schon die Kontinuität des Quantums, eine Kontinuität desselben über sich hinaus. Das Qualitativ-Endliche wird zum Unendlichen; das Quantitativ-Endliche ist sein Jenseits an ihm selbst, und weist über sich hinaus.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"96.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0004","text":"Aber diese Unendlichkeit der Specifikation des Maaßes setzt ebensowohl das Qualitative wie das Quantitative als sich in einander aufhebend, und damit die erste, unmittelbare Einheit derselben, welche das Maaß überhaupt ist, als in sich zurückgekehrt und damit selbst als gesetzt. Das Qualitative, eine specifische Existenz, geht in eine andere so über, daß nur eine Veränderung der Größebestimmtheit eines Verhältnisses vorgeht; die Veränderung des Qualitativen selbst in Qualitatives ist damit als eine äußerliche und gleichgültige, und als ein Zusammengehen mit sich selbst gesetzt; das Quantitative hebt sich ohnehin als umschlagend in Qualitatives, das An- und Für-Sichbestimmtseyn, auf. Diese so sich in ihrem Wechsel der Maaße in sich selbst kontinuirende Einheit ist die wahrhaft bestehenbleibende, selbstständige Materie, Sache.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"96.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0005","text":"Was hiermit vorhanden ist, ist à) eine und dieselbe Sache, welche als Grundlage in ihren Unterscheidungen und als perennirend gesetzt ist. Schon im Quantum überhaupt beginnt dieß Abtrennen des Seyns von seiner Bestimmtheit; groß ist etwas, als gleichgültig gegen seine seyende Bestimmtheit. Im Maaße ist die Sache selbst bereits an sich Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen,—der beiden Momente, die innerhalb der allgemeinen Sphäre des Seyns, den Unterschied ausmachen, und wovon das Eine das Jenseits des Andern ist; das perennirende Substrat hat auf diese Weise zunachst an ihm selbst die Bestimmung seyender Unendlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"96.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0006","text":"ß) Diese Dieselbigkeit des Substrats ist darin gesetzt, daß die qualitativen Selbstständigkeiten, in welche die maaßbestimmende Einheit abgestoßen ist, nur in quantitativen Unterschieden bestehen, so daß das Substrat sich in dieß sein Unterscheiden kontinuirt; ç) in dem unendlichen Progresse der Knotenreihe ist die Kontinuirung des Qualitativen in das quantitative Fortgehen, als in eine gleichgültige Veränderung, aber ebenso die darin enthaltene Negation des Qualitativen, und zugleich damit der bloß quantitativen Äußerlichkeit, gesetzt. Das quantitative Hinausweisen über sich zu einem Andern, als anderem Quantitativen geht unter in dem Hervortreten eines Verhältnißmaaßes, einer Qualität, und das qualitative Übergehen hebt sich eben darin auf, daß die neue Qualität selbst nur ein quantitatives Verhältniß ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"96.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0007","text":"Dieß Übergehen des Qualitativen und des Quantitativen in einander geht auf dem Boden ihrer Einheit vor, und der Sinn dieses Processes ist nur das Daseyn, das Zeigen oder Setzen, daß demselben ein solches Substrat zu Grunde liegt, welches ihre Einheit sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"96.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0008","text":"In den Reihen selbstständiger Maaßverhältnisse sind die einseitigen Glieder der Reihen unmittelbare qualitative Etwas, (die specifischen Schweren, oder die chemische Stoffe, die basischen oder kalischen, die sauren z.B.), und dann die Neutralisationen derselben, (- worunter hier auch die Verbindungen von Stoffen verschiedener specifischer Schwere zu begreiffen sind—) sind selbstständige und selbst ausschließende Maaßverhältnisse, gegeneinander gleichgültige Totalitäten fürsichseyenden Daseyns. Nun sind solche Verhältnisse nur als Knoten eines und desselben Substrats bestimmt. Damit sind die Maaße und die damit gesetzten Selbstständigkeiten zu Zuständen herabgesetzt. Die Veränderung ist nur Änderung eines Zustandes und das Übergehende ist als darin dasselbe bleibend gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"96.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0009","text":"Um die Fortbestimmung, welche das Maaß durchloffen hat, zu übersehen, so fassen sich die Momente derselben so zusammen, daß das Maaß zunächst die selbst unmittelbare Einheit der Qualität und der Quantität ist als ein gewöhnliches Quantum, das aber specifisch ist. Hiermit als nicht auf Anderes, sondern auf sich beziehende Quantitätsbestimmtheit ist es wesentlich Verhaltniß. Daher ferner enthält es seine Momente als aufgehobene und ungetrennte in sich; wie immer in einem Begriffe, ist der Unterschied in demselben so, daß jedes von dessen Momenten selbst Einheit des Qualitativen und Quantitativen ist. Dieser hiermit reale Unterschied ergiebt eine Menge von Maaßverhältnissen die als formelle Totalitäten in sich selbstständig sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"96.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0010","text":"Die Reihen, welche die Seiten dieser Verhaltnisse bilden, sind für jedes einzelne Glied, das als einer Seite zugehörig sich zu der ganzen gegenüberstehenden Reihe verhält, dieselbe konstante Ordnung. Diese, als bloße Ordnung, noch ganz äußerliche Einheit, zeigt sich zwar als immanente specificirende Einheit eines fürsichseyenden Maaßes unterschieden von seinen Specifikationen; aber das specificirende Princip ist noch nicht der freie Begriff welcher allein seinen Unterschieden immanente Bestimmung giebt, sondern das Princip ist zunächst nur Substrat, eine Materie, für deren Unterschiede, um als Totalitäten, zu seyn, d. i. die Natur des sich selbst gleich bleibenden Substrats in sich zu haben, nur die äußerliche quantitative Bestimmung vorhanden ist, die sich als Verschiedenheit der Qualität zugleich zeigt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"96.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0011","text":"Die Maaßbestimmnng ist in dieser Einheit des Substrats mit sich selbst eine aufgehobene, ihre Qualität ein durch das Quantum (bestimmter, äußerlicher Zustand.—Dieser Verlauf ist ebensowohl die realisirende Fortbestimmung des Maaßes, als sie das Herabsetzen desselben zu einem Momente ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"96.11"}],"sha256":"6467d255256db99eb737df4a36120645ff6e90ee7e445a8a6f704345e65e89bb","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104429427796Z_6a8fa03f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. The Measureless.","source_sha256":"6467d255256db99eb737df4a36120645ff6e90ee7e445a8a6f704345e65e89bb","sha256":"602fa676cbbdf2673a6a12a3c8de70fe1eede267abaf32d65d0f85d723540ba7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:44:29.427807+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0001","text":"The excluding measure remains, in its realized being-for-self itself, burdened with the moment of quantitative existence, and is therefore capable of ascending and descending on the scale of quantum, on which the relations change. Something or a quality, as resting upon such a relation, is driven beyond itself into the measureless, and perishes through the mere alteration of its magnitude. Magnitude is the constitution by which an existence, with the appearance of harmlessness, can be seized and through which it can be destroyed.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"96.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0002","text":"The abstract measureless is quantum in general as indeterminate in itself, and as merely indifferent determinacy, through which measure is not altered. In the nodal line of measures it is at the same time posited as specifying; that abstract measureless sublates itself into qualitative determinacy; the new measure-relation into which the one initially present passes is measureless in respect to the latter, but is in itself likewise a quality that is for itself; thus the alternation of specific existences with one another, and likewise of the same with merely quantitatively persisting relations, is posited,—and so on to infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"96.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0003","text":"What is thus present in this transition is both the negation of the specific relations and the negation of quantitative progression itself; the infinite that is for itself.—Qualitative infinity, as it is in existence, was the breaking forth of the infinite in the finite, as the immediate transition and disappearance of this side in its beyond. Quantitative infinity, on the other hand, according to its determinacy, is already the continuity of quantum, a continuity of the latter beyond itself. The qualitatively finite becomes infinite; the quantitatively finite has its beyond in itself, and points beyond itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"96.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0004","text":"But this infinity of the specification of measure equally posits both the qualitative and the quantitative as sublating themselves into one another, and thereby posits the first, immediate unity of these, which is measure in general, as returned into itself and thus itself as posited. The qualitative, a specific existence, passes over into another in such a way that only a change in the magnitude-determinacy of a relation takes place; the change of the qualitative itself into qualitative is thereby posited as external and indifferent, and as a coinciding with itself; the quantitative in any case sublates itself, as turning into qualitative, into being determined in and for itself. This unity, thus continuing itself within itself in its alternation of measures, is the truly enduring, self-subsistent matter, thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"96.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0005","text":"What is thereby present is, α) one and the same thing, which is posited as foundation in its distinctions and as enduring. Already in quantum in general this separation of being from its determinacy begins; something is great as indifferent to its determinacy of being. In measure the thing itself is already in itself the unity of the qualitative and quantitative,—of the two moments which, within the general sphere of being, constitute the distinction, and of which one is the beyond of the other; the enduring substrate thus has, initially, in itself the determinacy of being infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"96.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0006","text":"β) This identity of the substrate is posited in the fact that the qualitative self-subsistences into which the measure-determining unity is repelled consist only in quantitative distinctions, so that the substrate continues itself into this its distinguishing; γ) in the infinite progression of the series of nodes, the continuation of the qualitative into quantitative progression, as into an indifferent alteration, is posited, but likewise the negation of the qualitative contained therein, and at the same time the negation of merely quantitative externality. The quantitative pointing-beyond-itself to an other, as another quantitative, perishes in the emergence of a relational measure, a quality, and qualitative transition sublates itself precisely therein, in that the new quality itself is only a quantitative relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"96.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0007","text":"This transition of the qualitative and the quantitative into one another occurs on the ground of their unity, and the sense of this process is only the existence, the showing or positing, that such a substrate underlies it, which is their unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"96.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0008","text":"In the series of self-subsistent measure-relations, the one-sided members of the series are immediate qualitative somethings (the specific gravities, or the chemical substances, the basic or alkaline, the acidic, for example), and then their neutralizations, (- under which the combinations of substances of different specific gravity are here also to be understood—) are self-subsistent and themselves excluding measure-relations, indifferent totalities of existence that is for itself in relation to one another. Now such relations are determined only as nodes of one and the same substrate. Thereby the measures and the self-subsistences posited with them are reduced to states. The alteration is only alteration of a state, and what passes over is posited as remaining the same therein.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"96.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0009","text":"In order to survey the further determination that measure has undergone, its moments may be summed up as follows: measure is initially the self-immediate unity of quality and quantity, as an ordinary quantum, but one that is specific. Thereby, as a determinacy of quantity relating not to an other but to itself, it is essentially relation. It therefore further contains its moments within itself as sublated and undivided; as always in a concept, the distinction in it is such that each of its moments is itself unity of the qualitative and quantitative. This thus real distinction yields a multiplicity of measure-relations which, as formal totalities, are self-subsistent in themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"96.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0010","text":"The series which form the sides of these relations are, for each individual member which, as belonging to one side, relates itself to the entire opposed series, the same constant order. This, as mere order, still wholly external unity, does indeed show itself as immanent specifying unity of a measure that is for itself, distinguished from its specifications; but the specifying principle is not yet the free concept, which alone gives its distinctions immanent determinacy; rather, the principle is initially only substrate, a matter, for whose distinctions, in order to be totalities, i.e. to have within themselves the nature of the substrate remaining equal to itself, there is present only external quantitative determinacy, which at the same time shows itself as difference of quality.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"96.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0011","text":"In this unity of the substrate with itself, measure-determinacy is a sublated one, its quality a state determined through quantum, external.—This course is just as much the realizing further determination of measure as it is its reduction to a moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"96.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDM0:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"0d16201d1c96293d2cfb693e8e66a345d22925e587ad2583836f987764368177","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Das Maaßlose."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Das Maaßlose.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0","title":"A. Absolute Indifference.","order":97,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DAI0","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das Werden des Wesens.\n\n## A. Die absolute Indifferenz.\n\nDas Seyn ist die abstrakte Gleichgültigkeit, wofür, da sie für sich als Seyn gedacht werden soll, der Ausdruck Indifferenz gebraucht worden ist,—an der noch keine Art von Bestimmtheit seyn soll; die reine Quantität ist die Indifferenz als aller Bestimmungen fähig, so aber daß diese ihr äußerlich, und sie aus sich keinen Zusammenhang mit denselben hat; die Indifferenz aber, welche die absolute genannt werden kann, ist, die durch die Negation aller Bestimmtheiten des Seyns, der Qualität und Quantität und deren zunächst unmittelbaren Einheit, des Maaßes, sich mit sich zur einfachen Einheit vermittelt. Die Bestimmtheit ist an ihr nur noch als Zustand d. i. als ein qualitatives Äußerliches, das die Indifferenz zum Substrate hat.\n\nDas aber, was so als qualitatives Äußerliches bestimmt worden, ist nur ein Verschwindendes; als so äußerlich gegen das Seyn ist das Qualitative als das Gegentheil seiner selbst nur das sich Aufhebende. Die Bestimmtheit ist auf diese Weise an dem Substrate nur noch gesetzt als ein leeres Unterscheiden. Aber eben dieß leere Unterscheiden ist die Indifferenz selbst als Resultat. Und zwar ist sie so das Konkrete, das in ihm selbst durch die Negation aller Bestimmungen des Seyns mit sich vermittelte. Als diese Vermittelung enthält sie die Negation und Verhältniß, und was Zustand hieß, ist ihr immanentes, sich auf sich beziehendes Unterscheiden; eben die Äußerlichkeit und deren Verschwinden macht die Einheit des Seyns zur Indifferenz, und ist also innerhalb dieser, welche damit aufhört, nur Substrat und an ihr selbst nur abstrakt zu seyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0001","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das Werden des Wesens.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"97.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0002","text":"## A. Die absolute Indifferenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"97.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0003","text":"Das Seyn ist die abstrakte Gleichgültigkeit, wofür, da sie für sich als Seyn gedacht werden soll, der Ausdruck Indifferenz gebraucht worden ist,—an der noch keine Art von Bestimmtheit seyn soll; die reine Quantität ist die Indifferenz als aller Bestimmungen fähig, so aber daß diese ihr äußerlich, und sie aus sich keinen Zusammenhang mit denselben hat; die Indifferenz aber, welche die absolute genannt werden kann, ist, die durch die Negation aller Bestimmtheiten des Seyns, der Qualität und Quantität und deren zunächst unmittelbaren Einheit, des Maaßes, sich mit sich zur einfachen Einheit vermittelt. Die Bestimmtheit ist an ihr nur noch als Zustand d. i. als ein qualitatives Äußerliches, das die Indifferenz zum Substrate hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"97.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0004","text":"Das aber, was so als qualitatives Äußerliches bestimmt worden, ist nur ein Verschwindendes; als so äußerlich gegen das Seyn ist das Qualitative als das Gegentheil seiner selbst nur das sich Aufhebende. Die Bestimmtheit ist auf diese Weise an dem Substrate nur noch gesetzt als ein leeres Unterscheiden. Aber eben dieß leere Unterscheiden ist die Indifferenz selbst als Resultat. Und zwar ist sie so das Konkrete, das in ihm selbst durch die Negation aller Bestimmungen des Seyns mit sich vermittelte. Als diese Vermittelung enthält sie die Negation und Verhältniß, und was Zustand hieß, ist ihr immanentes, sich auf sich beziehendes Unterscheiden; eben die Äußerlichkeit und deren Verschwinden macht die Einheit des Seyns zur Indifferenz, und ist also innerhalb dieser, welche damit aufhört, nur Substrat und an ihr selbst nur abstrakt zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"97.4"}],"sha256":"c1d3c8aa08ba9e3880e156e9bf9f60707e67524725bb5f5a895b5b61cacab635","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104433863377Z_5ea0e35c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Absolute Indifference.","source_sha256":"c1d3c8aa08ba9e3880e156e9bf9f60707e67524725bb5f5a895b5b61cacab635","sha256":"e4efe187fdc9b89278fe589986a7901a56a87e3544d822981de9fd71b09d2647","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:44:33.863445+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0001","text":"## Chapter Three. The Becoming of Essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"97.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0002","text":"## A. Absolute Indifference.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"97.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0003","text":"Being is abstract indifference, for which, since it is to be thought as Being for itself, the expression indifference has been employed,—in which there is as yet to be no kind of determinacy; pure quantity is indifference as capable of all determinations, but such that these are external to it, and it has from itself no connection with them; but the indifference which can be called absolute is that which, through the negation of all determinacies of Being, of quality and quantity and of their initially immediate unity, measure, mediates itself with itself into simple unity. Determinacy is in it now only as state, i.e. as a qualitative externality which has indifference as its substrate.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"97.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0004","text":"But that which has thus been determined as qualitative externality is only something vanishing; as external in this way in relation to Being, the qualitative, as the opposite of itself, is only that which sublates itself. In this way determinacy is in the substrate only posited as an empty distinguishing. But precisely this empty distinguishing is indifference itself as result. And indeed it is thus the concrete, which in itself has mediated itself with itself through the negation of all determinations of Being. As this mediation it contains negation and relation, and what was called state is its immanent, self-related distinguishing; precisely externality and its vanishing make the unity of Being into indifference, and are thus within this, which thereby ceases to be merely substrate and abstract in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"97.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DAI0:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"524cff3fbcb110043dec253916587861a3771fb788fce1ed2d33e74311dfc864","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Die absolute Indifferenz."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Die absolute Indifferenz.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA","title":"B. Indifference as the Inverse Ratio of Its Factors.","order":98,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDIA","text":"Es ist nun zu sehen, wie diese Bestimmung der Indifferenz an ihr selbst und sie damit als fürsichseyend gesetzt ist.\n\n1. Die Reduktion der zunächst als selbstständig geltenden Maaßverhältnisse begründet Ein Substrat derselben; dieses ist deren Kontinuirung in einander, somit das untrennbare Selbstständige, das in seinen Unterschieden ganz vorhanden ist. Für diesen Unterschied sind die in ihm enthaltenen Bestimmungen, die Qualität und die Quantität vorhanden, und es kommt ganz nur darauf an, wie diese an ihm gesetzt sind. Dieß aber ist dadurch bestimmt, daß das Substrat zunächst als Resultat, und an sich die Vermittelung, aber diese so an ihm noch nicht als solche gesetzt ist; wodurch dasselbe zunächst Substrat und in Ansehung der Bestimmtheit als die Indifferenz ist.\n\nDer Unterschied ist daher an ihr wesentlich zunächst der nur quantitative äußerliche; und es sind zwei unterschiedene Quanta eines und desselben Substrats, welches auf diese Weise die Summe derselben, somit selbst als Quantum bestimmt wäre. Die Indifferenz ist aber dieses feste Maaß, die ansichseyende absolute Grenze nur in Beziehung auf jene Unterschiede so, daß sie nicht an ihr selbst Quantum wäre, und in irgend einer Weise als Summe oder auch Exponent Andern, es sey Summen, Indifferenzen, gegenüber träte. Es ist nur die abstrakte Bestimmtheit, welche in die Indifferenz fällt; die beiden Quanta um als Momente an ihr gesetzt zu seyn, sind veränderlich, gleichgültig, größer oder kleiner gegeneinander. Durch die feste Grenze ihrer Summe beschränkt aber verhalten sie sich zugleich nicht äußerlich, sondern negativ gegeneinander; was nun die qualitative Bestimmung ist, in der sie zu einander stehen. Sie sind darnach im umgekehrten Verhältnisse zu einander. Von dem frühern formellen umgekehrten Verhältnisse ist dieses dadurch unterschieden, daß hier das Ganze ein reales Substrat, und jede der beiden Seiten gesetzt ist, selbst an sich dieß Ganze seyn zu sollen.\n\nNach der angegebenen qualitativen Bestimmtheit ist der Unterschied ferner als von zwei Qualitäten vorhanden, deren eine durch die andere aufgehoben wird, aber als in Einer Einheit gehalten und sie ausmachend, von der andern untrennbar ist. Das Substrat selbst ist als die Indifferenz gleichfalls an sich die Einheit der beiden Qualitäten; jede der Seiten des Verhältnisses enthält daher ebenso sie beide in sich, und ist nur durch ein Mehr der einen Qualität und das Weniger der andern und umgekehrt unterschieden; die eine Qualität ist durch ihr Quantum, in der einen Seite nur die überwiegende, die andere in der andern.\n\nJede Seite ist somit an ihr selbst ein umgekehrtes Verhältniß; dieses Verhältniß kehrt als formelles an den unterschiedenen Seiten zurück. Diese Seiten selbst kontinuiren sich so auch nach ihren qualitativen Bestimmungen in einander, jede der Qualitäten verhält in der andern sich zu sich selbst, und ist in jeder der beiden Seiten nur in einem verschiedenen Quantum. Ihr quantitativer Unterschied ist jene Indifferenz, nach der sie sich in einander kontinuiren, und diese Kontinuation ist als Dieselbigkeit der Qualitäten in jeder der beiden Einheiten.—Die Seiten aber, jede als das Ganze der Bestimmungen, hiermit die Indifferenz selbst enthaltend, sind so gegeneinander zugleich als selbstständig gesetzt.\n\n2. Das Seyn ist nun als diese Indifferenz, das Bestimmtseyn des Maaßes nicht mehr in seiner Unmittelbarkeit; sondern dasselbe auf die so eben aufgezeigte entwickelte Weise;—Indifferenz als es an sich das Ganze der Bestimmungen des Seyns, welche zu dieser Einheit aufgelöst sind;—ebenso Daseyn, als Totalität der gesetzten Realisation, in welcher die Momente selbst die ansichseyende Totalität der Indifferenz, von ihr als ihrer Einheit getragen, sind. Weil aber die Einheit nur als Indifferenz und damit nur als an sich festgehalten, und die Momente noch nicht als fürsichseyend, d. i. noch nicht an ihnen selbst und durcheinander sich zur Einheit aufhebend, bestimmt sind, so ist damit überhaupt die Gleichgültigkeit ihrer selbst gegen sich als entwickelte Bestimmtheit vorhanden.\n\nDieß so untrennbare Selbstständige ist nun näher zu betrachten. Es ist immanent in allen seinen Bestimmungen und bleibt in ihnen in der Einheit mit sich ungetrübt von ihnen, aber hat à) als an sich die Totalität bleibend die Bestimmtheiten, welche in ihr aufgehoben sind, nur grundlos an ihr hervortretend. Das Ansich der Indifferenz und dieß ihr Daseyn ist unverbunden; die Bestimmtheiten zeigen sich auf unmittelbare Weise an ihr; sie ist ganz in jeder derselben; deren Unterschied hiermit zunächst als ein aufgehobener, also als quantitativer gesetzt; aber eben damit nicht als das Abstoßen ihrer von sich selbst, sie nicht als selbstbestimmend, nur als äußerlich bestimmtseyend und bestimmtwerdend.\n\nß) Die beiden Momente sind in umgekehrtem quantitativem Verhältnisse; —ein Hin- und Hergehen an der Größe, das aber nicht durch die Indifferenz, welche eben die Gleichgültigkeit dieses Hinund Hergehens ist, sondern hiermit nur äußerlich bestimmt ist. Es wird auf ein Anderes hingewiesen, das außerhalb ihr ist und in welchem das Bestimmen liegt. Das Absolute als Indifferenz hat nach dieser Seite den zweiten Mangel der quantitativen Form, daß die Bestimmtheit des Unterschieds nicht durch dasselbe determinirt ist, wie es daran den ersten hat, daß die Unterschiede an ihm nur überhaupt hervortreten, d. i. das Setzen desselben etwas Unmittelbares nicht seine Vermittelung mit sich selbst ist.\n\nç) Die quantitative Bestimmtheit der Momente, welche nun Seiten des Verhältnisses sind, macht die Weise ihres Bestehens aus; ihr Daseyn ist durch diese Gleichgültigkeit dem Übergehen des Qualitativen entnommen. Aber sie haben ein von diesem ihrem Daseyn verschiedenes, ihr an sichseyendes Bestehen darin, daß sie an sich die Indifferenz selbst, jede selbst die Einheit der beiden Qualitäten ist, in welche das qualitative Moment sich spaltet. Der Unterschied der beiden Seiten beschränkt sich darauf, daß die eine Qualität in der einen Seite mit einem Mehr, in der andern mit einem Weniger, und die andere darnach umgekehrt gesetzt ist. So ist jede Seite an ihr die Totalität der Indifferenz.—Jede der beiden Qualitäten einzeln für sich genommen, bleibt gleichfalls dieselbe Summe, welche die Indifferenz ist; sie kontinuirt sich aus der einen Seite in die andere, und wird durch die quantitative Grenze, die dabei in ihr gesetzt wird, nicht beschränkt. Hieran kommen die Bestimmungen in unmittelbaren Gegensatz, welcher sich zum Widerspruch entwickelt, was nun zu sehen ist.\n\n3. Nämlich jede Qualität tritt innerhalb jeder Seite in die Beziehung zu der andern, und zwar so daß auch, wie bestimmt worden ist, diese Beziehung nur ein quantitativer Unterschied seyn soll. Sind beide Qualitäten selbstständig,—etwa genommen wie von einander unabhängige, sinnliche Materien, so fällt die ganze Bestimmtheit der Indifferenz auseinander; ihre Einheit und Totalität wären leere Namen. Sie sind aber vielmehr zugleich so bestimmt, daß sie in Einer Einheit befaßt, daß sie untrennbar sind, jede nur Sinn und Realität in dieser einen qualitativen Beziehung auf die andere hat. Darum nun aber, weil ihre Quantitativität schlechthin von dieser qualitativen Natur ist, reicht jede nur so weit, als die andere. Insofern sie als Quanta verschieden seyn sollten, ginge die eine über die andere hinaus und hätte in ihrem Mehr ein gleichgültiges Daseyn, welches die andere nicht hätte. Aber in ihrer qualitativen Beziehung ist jede nur insofern die andere ist.—Hieraus folgt dieß, daß sie im Gleichgewicht sind, daß um soviel die eine sich vermehrte oder verminderte, die andere gleichfalls zu- oder abnähme, und in demselben Verhältnisse zu- oder abnähme.\n\nAus dem Grunde ihrer qualitativen Beziehung kann es daher zu keinem quantitativen Unterschiede und keinem Mehr der einen Qualität kommen. Das Mehr, um welches das eine der in Beziehung stehenden Momente über das andere hinaus wäre, wäre nur eine haltungslose Bestimmung, oder dieß Mehr wäre nur wieder das andere selbst; in dieser Gleichheit beider aber ist keines vorhanden, denn ihr Daseyn sollte nur auf der Ungleichheit ihres Quantums beruhen.—Jeder dieser seyn sollenden Faktoren verschwindet ebenso, indem er über den andern hinaus als indem er ihm gleich seyn soll. Jenes Verschwinden erscheint so, daß von der quantitativen Vorstellung aus das Gleichgewicht gestört und der eine Faktor größer genommen wird, als der andere; so ist das Aufheben der Qualität des andern und seine Haltungslosigkeit gesetzt; der erstere wird das überwiegende, daß der andere mit beschleunigter Geschwindigkeit abnimmt und von dem ersten überwältigt wird, dieser also sich zum einzigen Selbstständigen macht; aber damit sind nicht mehr zwei Specifische und Faktoren, sondern nur das eine Ganze.\n\nDiese Einheit so gesetzt als die Totalität des Bestimmens, wie sie selbst darin als Indifferenz bestimmt ist, ist der allseitige Widerspruch; sie ist somit so zu setzen, als dieser sich selbst aufhebende Widerspruch, zur fürsichseyenden Selbstständigkeit bestimmt zu seyn, welche die nicht mehr nur indifferente, sondern die in ihr selbst immanent negative absolute Einheit zum Resultate und Wahrheit hat, welche das Wesen ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0001","text":"Es ist nun zu sehen, wie diese Bestimmung der Indifferenz an ihr selbst und sie damit als fürsichseyend gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"98.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0002","text":"1. Die Reduktion der zunächst als selbstständig geltenden Maaßverhältnisse begründet Ein Substrat derselben; dieses ist deren Kontinuirung in einander, somit das untrennbare Selbstständige, das in seinen Unterschieden ganz vorhanden ist. Für diesen Unterschied sind die in ihm enthaltenen Bestimmungen, die Qualität und die Quantität vorhanden, und es kommt ganz nur darauf an, wie diese an ihm gesetzt sind. Dieß aber ist dadurch bestimmt, daß das Substrat zunächst als Resultat, und an sich die Vermittelung, aber diese so an ihm noch nicht als solche gesetzt ist; wodurch dasselbe zunächst Substrat und in Ansehung der Bestimmtheit als die Indifferenz ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"98.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0003","text":"Der Unterschied ist daher an ihr wesentlich zunächst der nur quantitative äußerliche; und es sind zwei unterschiedene Quanta eines und desselben Substrats, welches auf diese Weise die Summe derselben, somit selbst als Quantum bestimmt wäre. Die Indifferenz ist aber dieses feste Maaß, die ansichseyende absolute Grenze nur in Beziehung auf jene Unterschiede so, daß sie nicht an ihr selbst Quantum wäre, und in irgend einer Weise als Summe oder auch Exponent Andern, es sey Summen, Indifferenzen, gegenüber träte. Es ist nur die abstrakte Bestimmtheit, welche in die Indifferenz fällt; die beiden Quanta um als Momente an ihr gesetzt zu seyn, sind veränderlich, gleichgültig, größer oder kleiner gegeneinander.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"98.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0004","text":"Durch die feste Grenze ihrer Summe beschränkt aber verhalten sie sich zugleich nicht äußerlich, sondern negativ gegeneinander; was nun die qualitative Bestimmung ist, in der sie zu einander stehen. Sie sind darnach im umgekehrten Verhältnisse zu einander. Von dem frühern formellen umgekehrten Verhältnisse ist dieses dadurch unterschieden, daß hier das Ganze ein reales Substrat, und jede der beiden Seiten gesetzt ist, selbst an sich dieß Ganze seyn zu sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"98.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0005","text":"Nach der angegebenen qualitativen Bestimmtheit ist der Unterschied ferner als von zwei Qualitäten vorhanden, deren eine durch die andere aufgehoben wird, aber als in Einer Einheit gehalten und sie ausmachend, von der andern untrennbar ist. Das Substrat selbst ist als die Indifferenz gleichfalls an sich die Einheit der beiden Qualitäten; jede der Seiten des Verhältnisses enthält daher ebenso sie beide in sich, und ist nur durch ein Mehr der einen Qualität und das Weniger der andern und umgekehrt unterschieden; die eine Qualität ist durch ihr Quantum, in der einen Seite nur die überwiegende, die andere in der andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"98.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0006","text":"Jede Seite ist somit an ihr selbst ein umgekehrtes Verhältniß; dieses Verhältniß kehrt als formelles an den unterschiedenen Seiten zurück. Diese Seiten selbst kontinuiren sich so auch nach ihren qualitativen Bestimmungen in einander, jede der Qualitäten verhält in der andern sich zu sich selbst, und ist in jeder der beiden Seiten nur in einem verschiedenen Quantum. Ihr quantitativer Unterschied ist jene Indifferenz, nach der sie sich in einander kontinuiren, und diese Kontinuation ist als Dieselbigkeit der Qualitäten in jeder der beiden Einheiten.—Die Seiten aber, jede als das Ganze der Bestimmungen, hiermit die Indifferenz selbst enthaltend, sind so gegeneinander zugleich als selbstständig gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"98.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0007","text":"2. Das Seyn ist nun als diese Indifferenz, das Bestimmtseyn des Maaßes nicht mehr in seiner Unmittelbarkeit; sondern dasselbe auf die so eben aufgezeigte entwickelte Weise;—Indifferenz als es an sich das Ganze der Bestimmungen des Seyns, welche zu dieser Einheit aufgelöst sind;—ebenso Daseyn, als Totalität der gesetzten Realisation, in welcher die Momente selbst die ansichseyende Totalität der Indifferenz, von ihr als ihrer Einheit getragen, sind. Weil aber die Einheit nur als Indifferenz und damit nur als an sich festgehalten, und die Momente noch nicht als fürsichseyend, d. i. noch nicht an ihnen selbst und durcheinander sich zur Einheit aufhebend, bestimmt sind, so ist damit überhaupt die Gleichgültigkeit ihrer selbst gegen sich als entwickelte Bestimmtheit vorhanden.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"98.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0008","text":"Dieß so untrennbare Selbstständige ist nun näher zu betrachten. Es ist immanent in allen seinen Bestimmungen und bleibt in ihnen in der Einheit mit sich ungetrübt von ihnen, aber hat à) als an sich die Totalität bleibend die Bestimmtheiten, welche in ihr aufgehoben sind, nur grundlos an ihr hervortretend. Das Ansich der Indifferenz und dieß ihr Daseyn ist unverbunden; die Bestimmtheiten zeigen sich auf unmittelbare Weise an ihr; sie ist ganz in jeder derselben; deren Unterschied hiermit zunächst als ein aufgehobener, also als quantitativer gesetzt; aber eben damit nicht als das Abstoßen ihrer von sich selbst, sie nicht als selbstbestimmend, nur als äußerlich bestimmtseyend und bestimmtwerdend.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"98.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0009","text":"ß) Die beiden Momente sind in umgekehrtem quantitativem Verhältnisse; —ein Hin- und Hergehen an der Größe, das aber nicht durch die Indifferenz, welche eben die Gleichgültigkeit dieses Hinund Hergehens ist, sondern hiermit nur äußerlich bestimmt ist. Es wird auf ein Anderes hingewiesen, das außerhalb ihr ist und in welchem das Bestimmen liegt. Das Absolute als Indifferenz hat nach dieser Seite den zweiten Mangel der quantitativen Form, daß die Bestimmtheit des Unterschieds nicht durch dasselbe determinirt ist, wie es daran den ersten hat, daß die Unterschiede an ihm nur überhaupt hervortreten, d. i. das Setzen desselben etwas Unmittelbares nicht seine Vermittelung mit sich selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"98.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0010","text":"ç) Die quantitative Bestimmtheit der Momente, welche nun Seiten des Verhältnisses sind, macht die Weise ihres Bestehens aus; ihr Daseyn ist durch diese Gleichgültigkeit dem Übergehen des Qualitativen entnommen. Aber sie haben ein von diesem ihrem Daseyn verschiedenes, ihr an sichseyendes Bestehen darin, daß sie an sich die Indifferenz selbst, jede selbst die Einheit der beiden Qualitäten ist, in welche das qualitative Moment sich spaltet. Der Unterschied der beiden Seiten beschränkt sich darauf, daß die eine Qualität in der einen Seite mit einem Mehr, in der andern mit einem Weniger, und die andere darnach umgekehrt gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"98.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0011","text":"So ist jede Seite an ihr die Totalität der Indifferenz.—Jede der beiden Qualitäten einzeln für sich genommen, bleibt gleichfalls dieselbe Summe, welche die Indifferenz ist; sie kontinuirt sich aus der einen Seite in die andere, und wird durch die quantitative Grenze, die dabei in ihr gesetzt wird, nicht beschränkt. Hieran kommen die Bestimmungen in unmittelbaren Gegensatz, welcher sich zum Widerspruch entwickelt, was nun zu sehen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"98.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0012","text":"3. Nämlich jede Qualität tritt innerhalb jeder Seite in die Beziehung zu der andern, und zwar so daß auch, wie bestimmt worden ist, diese Beziehung nur ein quantitativer Unterschied seyn soll. Sind beide Qualitäten selbstständig,—etwa genommen wie von einander unabhängige, sinnliche Materien, so fällt die ganze Bestimmtheit der Indifferenz auseinander; ihre Einheit und Totalität wären leere Namen. Sie sind aber vielmehr zugleich so bestimmt, daß sie in Einer Einheit befaßt, daß sie untrennbar sind, jede nur Sinn und Realität in dieser einen qualitativen Beziehung auf die andere hat. Darum nun aber, weil ihre Quantitativität schlechthin von dieser qualitativen Natur ist, reicht jede nur so weit, als die andere. Insofern sie als Quanta verschieden seyn sollten, ginge die eine über die andere hinaus und hätte in ihrem Mehr ein gleichgültiges Daseyn, welches die andere nicht hätte.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"98.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0013","text":"Aber in ihrer qualitativen Beziehung ist jede nur insofern die andere ist.—Hieraus folgt dieß, daß sie im Gleichgewicht sind, daß um soviel die eine sich vermehrte oder verminderte, die andere gleichfalls zu- oder abnähme, und in demselben Verhältnisse zu- oder abnähme.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"98.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0014","text":"Aus dem Grunde ihrer qualitativen Beziehung kann es daher zu keinem quantitativen Unterschiede und keinem Mehr der einen Qualität kommen. Das Mehr, um welches das eine der in Beziehung stehenden Momente über das andere hinaus wäre, wäre nur eine haltungslose Bestimmung, oder dieß Mehr wäre nur wieder das andere selbst; in dieser Gleichheit beider aber ist keines vorhanden, denn ihr Daseyn sollte nur auf der Ungleichheit ihres Quantums beruhen.—Jeder dieser seyn sollenden Faktoren verschwindet ebenso, indem er über den andern hinaus als indem er ihm gleich seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"98.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0015","text":"Jenes Verschwinden erscheint so, daß von der quantitativen Vorstellung aus das Gleichgewicht gestört und der eine Faktor größer genommen wird, als der andere; so ist das Aufheben der Qualität des andern und seine Haltungslosigkeit gesetzt; der erstere wird das überwiegende, daß der andere mit beschleunigter Geschwindigkeit abnimmt und von dem ersten überwältigt wird, dieser also sich zum einzigen Selbstständigen macht; aber damit sind nicht mehr zwei Specifische und Faktoren, sondern nur das eine Ganze.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"98.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0016","text":"Diese Einheit so gesetzt als die Totalität des Bestimmens, wie sie selbst darin als Indifferenz bestimmt ist, ist der allseitige Widerspruch; sie ist somit so zu setzen, als dieser sich selbst aufhebende Widerspruch, zur fürsichseyenden Selbstständigkeit bestimmt zu seyn, welche die nicht mehr nur indifferente, sondern die in ihr selbst immanent negative absolute Einheit zum Resultate und Wahrheit hat, welche das Wesen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"98.16"}],"sha256":"774121ac151c76cbc07e7e58ce3e5f8d9abd45250cdd89bc3391e60d8c4602d5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104453198296Z_d748bb36","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Indifference as the Inverse Ratio of Its Factors.","source_sha256":"774121ac151c76cbc07e7e58ce3e5f8d9abd45250cdd89bc3391e60d8c4602d5","sha256":"fb41fbd9b24af88ce28d206087dd733bfc296b3ed637b4f3b7a6b5adc34e1d3f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:44:53.198326+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0001","text":"It is now to be seen how this determination of indifference is in itself and is thereby posited as being-for-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"98.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0002","text":"1. The reduction of the relations of measure initially valid as self-subsistent grounds a substrate of them; this is their continuation into one another, hence the inseparable self-subsistent [entity] that is wholly present in its distinctions. For this distinction, the determinations contained in it, quality and quantity, are present, and everything depends solely on how these are posited in it. But this is determined by the fact that the substrate is initially a result, and in itself the mediation, but this as such is not yet posited in it; whereby it is initially substrate and, in respect of determinacy, indifference.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"98.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0003","text":"The distinction is therefore essentially at first in it merely the quantitative, external one; and there are two distinct quanta of one and the same substrate, which in this way would be the sum of them, hence itself determined as quantum. But indifference is this fixed measure, the absolute limit existing in itself, only in relation to those distinctions, in such a way that it would not itself be quantum and would not confront another, whether sums or indifferences, as a sum or exponent in any way. It is only abstract determinacy that falls into indifference; the two quanta, in order to be posited as moments in it, are mutable, indifferent, greater or smaller in relation to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"98.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0004","text":"Restricted by the fixed limit of their sum, however, they at the same time do not relate externally, but negatively, to one another; which is now the qualitative determinacy in which they stand to one another. Accordingly, they are in inverse ratio to one another. This differs from the earlier formal inverse ratio in that here the whole is a real substrate, and each of the two sides is posited as itself being in itself supposed to be this whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"98.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0005","text":"According to the indicated qualitative determinacy, the distinction further exists as one of two qualities, of which one is sublated by the other, but, as held in one unity and constituting it, is inseparable from the other. The substrate itself, as indifference, is likewise in itself the unity of the two qualities; each of the sides of the relation therefore equally contains both within itself, and is distinguished only by a more of the one quality and the less of the other, and conversely; one quality, through its quantum, is merely the preponderant one in the one side, the other in the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"98.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0006","text":"Each side is thus in itself an inverse ratio; this ratio returns as formal in the distinct sides. These sides themselves thus also continue into one another according to their qualitative determinations; each of the qualities relates in the other to itself, and is in each of the two sides only in a different quantum. Their quantitative distinction is that indifference according to which they continue into one another, and this continuation is as the sameness of the qualities in each of the two unities.—But the sides, each as the whole of the determinations, thereby containing indifference itself, are thus at the same time posited as self-subsistent in relation to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"98.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0007","text":"2. Being is now this indifference, the being-determined of measure no longer in its immediacy; but the latter in the just indicated developed manner;—indifference as in itself the whole of the determinations of being, which are dissolved into this unity;—likewise existence, as the totality of posited realization, in which the moments themselves are the totality of indifference existing in itself, borne by it as their unity. But because the unity is only as indifference and thereby only held fast in itself, and the moments are not yet determined as being-for-themselves, i.e. as not yet sublating themselves into unity in themselves and through one another, there is thereby present in general their indifference toward themselves as developed determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"98.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0008","text":"This thus inseparable self-subsistent [entity] is now to be considered more closely. It is immanent in all its determinations and remains in them, unclouded by them, in unity with itself; but, à) as in itself remaining the totality, it has the determinacies that are sublated in it emerging in it only without ground. The in-itself of indifference and this its existence are unconnected; the determinacies show themselves in it in an immediate manner; it is wholly in each of them; their distinction is thereby initially posited as a sublated one, thus as quantitative; but precisely thereby not as their repulsion from themselves, not as self-determining, only as externally determined and becoming determined.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"98.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0009","text":"ß) The two moments are in an inverse quantitative ratio;—a to-and-fro movement of magnitude, but one determined not by indifference, which is precisely the indifference of this to-and-fro movement, but thereby only externally. Reference is made to an other that lies outside it and in which the determining resides. The absolute as indifference has, on this side, the second defect of quantitative form, that the determinacy of distinction is not determined by it itself, just as it has in it the first defect, that the distinctions merely emerge in it in general, i.e. that the positing of it is something immediate, not its mediation with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"98.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0010","text":"ç) The quantitative determinacy of the moments, which are now sides of the relation, constitutes the mode of their subsistence; their existence is withdrawn by this indifference from the transition of the qualitative. But they have a subsistence distinct from this their existence, their subsistence in itself, in that they are in themselves indifference itself, each itself the unity of the two qualities into which the qualitative moment splits. The distinction of the two sides is limited to this, that the one quality is posited in the one side with a more, in the other with a less, and the other quality accordingly conversely.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"98.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0011","text":"Thus each side is in itself the totality of indifference.—Each of the two qualities, taken singly for itself, likewise remains the same sum that indifference is; it continues from the one side into the other, and is not restricted by the quantitative limit thereby posited in it. In this respect the determinations enter into immediate opposition, which develops into contradiction, as is now to be seen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"98.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0012","text":"3. Namely, each quality enters, within each side, into relation with the other, and indeed in such a way that, as has been determined, this relation too is supposed to be only a quantitative distinction. If both qualities are self-subsistent,—taken, for example, as sensible matters independent of one another,—the entire determinacy of indifference falls apart; its unity and totality would be empty names. But they are rather at the same time so determined that they are comprehended in one unity, that they are inseparable, that each has sense and reality only in this one qualitative relation to the other. Yet because their quantitiveness is absolutely of this qualitative nature, each extends only as far as the other. Insofar as they were to be distinct as quanta, the one would go beyond the other and would have, in its more, an indifferent existence that the other would not have.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"98.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0013","text":"But in their qualitative relation each is only insofar as the other is.—From this follows that they are in equilibrium, that by as much as the one increased or diminished, the other would likewise increase or diminish, and would increase or diminish in the same ratio.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"98.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0014","text":"On the ground of their qualitative relation, therefore, no quantitative distinction and no more of the one quality can arise. The more by which one of the moments standing in relation would exceed the other would be only a determination lacking all support, or this more would only again be the other itself; but in this equality of both neither is present, for their existence was supposed to rest only on the inequality of their quantum.—Each of these factors that are supposed to be disappears equally by being supposed to go beyond the other and by being supposed to be equal to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"98.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0015","text":"That disappearance thus appears in such a way that, proceeding from the quantitative representation, equilibrium is disturbed and the one factor is taken as greater than the other; thus the sublation of the quality of the other and its lack of support is posited; the former becomes preponderant, so that the other diminishes with accelerated velocity and is overpowered by the first, which thus makes itself into the sole self-subsistent [entity]; but with this there are no longer two specific [entities] and factors, but only the one whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"98.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0016","text":"This unity, thus posited as the totality of determining, as it itself is determined therein as indifference, is the all-sided contradiction; it is therefore to be posited as this contradiction sublating itself, as determined to self-subsistence that is for itself, which has as its result and truth the absolute unity no longer merely indifferent, but immanently negative within itself, which is essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"98.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDIA:P0016"]}],"source_digest":"9f719cde5eb8bd1f30eb3a33a64dc1a13d1935ed402280c234b5212d3714a299","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Die Indifferenz als umgekehrtes Verhältniß ihrer Faktoren."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Die Indifferenz als umgekehrtes Verhältniß ihrer Faktoren.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25","title":"Remark.","order":99,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_25","text":"Das Verhältniß eines Ganzen, das seine Bestimmtheit in dem Größenunterschiede qualitativ gegen einander bestimmter Faktoren haben soll, wird bei der elliptischen Bewegung der Himmelskörper gebraucht. Dieß Beispiel zeigt zunächst nur zwei Qualitäten im umgekehrten Verhältnisse zu einander, nicht zwei Seiten, deren jede selbst die Einheit beider und ihr umgekehrtes Verhältniß wäre. Bei der Festigkeit der empirischen Grundlage wird die Konsequenz übersehen, auf welche die in dieselbe gebrachte Theorie führt, nämlich das zu Grunde liegende Faktum zu zerstören, oder indem dieses, wie gehörig, festgehalten wird, die Leerheit der Theorie gegen dasselbe darzuthun. Das Ignoriren der Konsequenz läßt Faktum und die ihm widersprechende Theorie ruhig nebeneinander bestehen.—Das einfache Faktum ist, daß in der elliptischen Bewegung der Himmelskörper sich ihre Geschwindigkeit beschleunigt, indem sie sich dem Perihelium, und sich vermindert, indem sie sich dem Aphelium nähert. Das Quantitative dieses Faktums ist durch den unermüdlichen Fleiß des Beobachtens genau bestimmt und dasselbe weiter auf sein einfaches Gesetz und Formel zurückgeführt, somit alles geleistet, was wahrhaft an die Theorie zu fordern ist. Aber dieß hat dem reflektirenden Verstande nicht genügend geschienen. Zur sogenannten Erklärung des Phänomens und seines Gesetzes werden eine Centripetal- und Centrifugalkraft, als qualitative Momente der Bewegung in der krummen Linie, angenommen. Ihr qualitativer Unterschied besteht in der Entgegensetzung der Richtung, und in quantitativer Rücksicht darin, indem sie als ungleich bestimmt sind, daß wie die eine zu-, die andere abnehmen soll, und umgekehrt; dann auch ferner, daß das Verhältniß derselben wieder umschlage, daß nachdem die Centripetalkraft eine Zeitlang zugenommen, die Centrifugalkraft aber abgenommen, ein Punkt eintrete, wo die Centripetalkraft ab-, die Centrifugalkraft dagegen zunehme. Dieser Vorstellung widerspricht aber das Verhältniß ihrer wesentlich qualitativen Bestimmtheit gegeneinander. Durch diese sind sie schlechthin nicht auseinander zu bringen; jede hat nur Bedeutung in Rücksicht auf die andere; insofern also eine einen Überschuß über die andere hätte, insofern hätte sie keine Beziehung auf diese und wäre nicht vorhanden.—Bei der Annahme, daß die eine das einemal größer sey als die andere, wenn sie als größere in Beziehung auf die kleinere stünde, tritt das oben Gesagte ein, daß sie absolut das Übergewicht erhielte, und die andere verschwände; die letztere ist als das Verschwindende, Haltungslose gesetzt, und an dieser Bestimmung ändert es nichts, daß das Verschwinden nur allmählig geschehen, und ebenso wenig, daß so viel sie abnähme an Größe, der erstern zuwachsen soll; dieses geht mit der andern zu Grunde, da was sie ist allein insofern ist, insofern die andere ist. Es ist eine sehr einfache Betrachtung, daß wenn z.B. wie vorgegeben wird, die Centripetalkraft des Körpers, indem er sich dem Perihelium nähert, zunehmen, die Centrifugalkraft hingegen um ebenso viel abnehmen soll, die letztere nicht mehr vermöchte, ihn der erstern zu entreißen, und von seinem Centralkörper wieder zu entfernen; im Gegentheil da die erstere einmal das Übergewicht haben soll, so ist die andere überwältigt, und der Körper wird mit beschleunigter Geschwindigkeit seinem Centralkörper zugeführt. Wie umgekehrt, wenn die Centrifugalkraft an der unendlichen Nähe des Apheliums die Oberhand hat, es ebenso widersprechend ist, daß sie nun im Aphelium selbst von der schwächern überwältigt werden sollte.—Es erhellt ferner, daß es eine fremde Kraft wäre, welche diese Umkehrung bewirkte, dieß heißt, daß die bald beschleunigte, bald retardirte Geschwindigkeit der Bewegung nicht aus der angenommenen Bestimmung jener Faktoren erkannt oder, wie es genannt wird, erklärt werden könne, welche gerade deswegen angenommen worden sind, um diesen Unterschied zu erklären. Die Konsequenz des Verschwindens der einen oder der andern Richtung und damit der elliptischen Bewegung überhaupt, wird um des feststehenden Faktums willen, daß diese Bewegung fortdauert und aus der beschleunigten in die retardirte Geschwindigkeit übergeht, ignorirt und verborgen. Die Annahme des Umschlagens der Schwäche der Centripetalkraft im Aphelium in eine überwiegende Stärke gegen die Centrifugalkraft, und umgekehrt beim Perihelium, enthält Theils dasjenige, was oben entwickelt worden, daß jede der Seiten des umgekehrten Verhältnisses an ihr selbst dieß ganze umgekehrte Verhältniß ist; denn die Seite der Bewegung vom Aphelium zum Perihelium,—der überwiegend seyn sollenden Centripetalkraft,—soll noch die Centrifugalkraft enthalten, aber im Abnehmen, wie jene zunimmt; in eben dem umgekehrten Verhältniß soll sich in der Seite der retardirten Bewegung die überwiegende und immer überwiegender werdende Centrifugalkraft zur Centripetalkraft befinden, so daß auf keiner Seite eine derselben verschwunden sey, sondern nur immer kleiner werde bis zur Zeit ihres Umschlagens zum Überwiegen über die andere. Es rekurrirt damit nur an jeder Seite das, was der Mangel an diesem umgekehrten Verhältniß ist, daß entweder jede Kraft selbstständig für sich genommen wird, und mit dem bloß äußerlichen Zusammentreffen derselben zu einer Bewegung, wie im Parallelogramm der Kräfte, die Einheit des Begriffs, die Natur der Sache, aufgehoben ist, oder daß, indem beide sich qualitativ durch den Begriff zu einander verhalten, keine ein gleichgültiges, selbstständiges Bestehen gegen die andere erhalten kann, was ihr durch ein Mehr zugetheilt werden sollte; die Form der Intensität, das sogenannte Dynamische, ändert nichts, da es selbst in dem Quantum seine Bestimmtheit hat, und damit ebenso nur so viel Kraft äußern kann, d. h. nur insoweit existirt, als es an der entgegengesetzten Kraft sich gegenüber stehen hat. Theils aber enthält jenes Umschlagen aus dem Überwiegen in das Gegentheil die Abwechslung der qualitativen Bestimmung von Positiven und Negativen; das Zunehmen der einen ist ebenso viel Verlust der andern. Der untrennbare qualitative Zusammenhang dieses qualitativen Gegensatzes ist in der Theorie in ein Nacheinander auseinander gerückt; aber damit bleibt sie die Erklärung dieser Abwechslung sowohl als vornehmlich dieses Auseinanderrückens selbst schuldig. Der Schein von Einheit, der noch in dem Zunehmen der einen mit ebenso vielem Abnehmen der andern liegt, verschwindet hier vollends; es ist ein bloß äußerliches Erfolgen angegeben, das nur der Konsequenz jenes Zusammenhangs, nach der insofern die eine überwiegend geworden, die andere verschwinden muß, widerspricht.\n\nDasselbe Verhältniß ist auf die Attraktiv- und Repulsivkraft angewendet worden, um die verschiedene Dichtigkeit der Körper zu begreifen; auch das umgekehrte Verhältniß der Sensibilität und Irritabilität, hat dazu dienen sollen, um aus dem Ungleichwerden dieser Faktoren des Lebens die verschiedenen Bestimmungen des Ganzen, der Gesundheit, wie auch die Verschiedenheit der Gattungen der Lebendigen zu begreifen. Jedoch die Verwirrung, und der Galimathias, in welchen sich dieß Erklären, das eine naturphilosophische Grundlage der Physiologie, Nosologie, und dann der Zoologie werden sollte, in dem unkritischen Gebrauche dieser Begriffsbestimmungen verwickelte, hat hier zur Folge gehabt, daß dieser Formalismus bald wieder aufgegeben worden ist, der in der Wissenschaft besonders der physikalischen Astronomie in seiner ganzen Ausdehnung fortgeführt wird.\n\nInsofern die absolute Indifferenz die Grundbestimmung der spinozistischen Substanz zu seyn scheinen kann, so kann hierüber noch bemerkt werden, daß sie dieß allerdings in der Rücksicht ist, daß in beiden alle Bestimmungen des Seyns, wie überhaupt jede weitere konkrete Unterscheidung von Denken und Ausdehnung u.s.f. als verschwunden gesetzt werden. Es ist überhaupt gleichgültig, wenn bei der Abstraktion stehen geblieben werden soll, wie dasjenige, was in diesem Abgrund untergegangen ist, in seinem Daseyn ausgesehen habe. Aber die Substanz als Indifferenz ist Theils mit dem Bedürfniß des Bestimmens und mit der Rücksicht auf dasselbe verbunden; sie soll nicht die Substanz des Spinoza bleiben, deren einzige Bestimmung das Negative ist, daß in ihr alles absorbirt sey. Bei Spinoza kommt der Unterschied, die Attribute, Denken und Ausdehnung, alsdann auch die Modi, die Affekten und alle übrigen Determinationen, ganz empirisch herbei; es ist der Verstand, selbst ein Modus, in welchen dieß Unterscheiden fällt; die Attribute stehen zur Substanz und zu einander in keiner weitern Bestimmtheit, als daß sie die Substanz ganz ausdrücken, und ihr Inhalt, die Ordnung der Dinge als ausgedehnter und als Gedanken dieselbe ist. Durch die Bestimmung der Substanz als Indifferenz kommt aber die Reflexion auf den Unterschied hinzu, er wird nun gesetzt, als das was er bei Spinoza an sich ist, nämlich als äußerlicher, und damit näher als quantitativer. Die Indifferenz bleibt so in ihm wohl sich immanent, wie die Substanz, —aber abstrakt, nur an sich; der Unterschied ist nicht ihr immanent, als quantitativer ist er vielmehr das Gegentheil der Immanenz, und die quantitative Indifferenz ist vielmehr das Außersichseyn der Einheit. Der Unterschied ist damit auch nicht qualitativ aufgefaßt, die Substanz nicht als das sich selbst Unterscheidende, nicht als Subjekt bestimmt. Die nächste Folge in Rücksicht auf die Kategorie der Indifferenz selbst ist, daß an ihr der Unterschied von quantitativer und qualitativer Bestimmung auseinander fällt, wie in der Entwicklung der Indifferenz sich ergab; sie ist die Auflösung des Maaßes, in welchem beide Momente unmittelbar als eins gesetzt waren.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0001","text":"Das Verhältniß eines Ganzen, das seine Bestimmtheit in dem Größenunterschiede qualitativ gegen einander bestimmter Faktoren haben soll, wird bei der elliptischen Bewegung der Himmelskörper gebraucht. Dieß Beispiel zeigt zunächst nur zwei Qualitäten im umgekehrten Verhältnisse zu einander, nicht zwei Seiten, deren jede selbst die Einheit beider und ihr umgekehrtes Verhältniß wäre. Bei der Festigkeit der empirischen Grundlage wird die Konsequenz übersehen, auf welche die in dieselbe gebrachte Theorie führt, nämlich das zu Grunde liegende Faktum zu zerstören, oder indem dieses, wie gehörig, festgehalten wird, die Leerheit der Theorie gegen dasselbe darzuthun.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"99.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0002","text":"Das Ignoriren der Konsequenz läßt Faktum und die ihm widersprechende Theorie ruhig nebeneinander bestehen.—Das einfache Faktum ist, daß in der elliptischen Bewegung der Himmelskörper sich ihre Geschwindigkeit beschleunigt, indem sie sich dem Perihelium, und sich vermindert, indem sie sich dem Aphelium nähert. Das Quantitative dieses Faktums ist durch den unermüdlichen Fleiß des Beobachtens genau bestimmt und dasselbe weiter auf sein einfaches Gesetz und Formel zurückgeführt, somit alles geleistet, was wahrhaft an die Theorie zu fordern ist. Aber dieß hat dem reflektirenden Verstande nicht genügend geschienen. Zur sogenannten Erklärung des Phänomens und seines Gesetzes werden eine Centripetal- und Centrifugalkraft, als qualitative Momente der Bewegung in der krummen Linie, angenommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"99.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0003","text":"Ihr qualitativer Unterschied besteht in der Entgegensetzung der Richtung, und in quantitativer Rücksicht darin, indem sie als ungleich bestimmt sind, daß wie die eine zu-, die andere abnehmen soll, und umgekehrt; dann auch ferner, daß das Verhältniß derselben wieder umschlage, daß nachdem die Centripetalkraft eine Zeitlang zugenommen, die Centrifugalkraft aber abgenommen, ein Punkt eintrete, wo die Centripetalkraft ab-, die Centrifugalkraft dagegen zunehme. Dieser Vorstellung widerspricht aber das Verhältniß ihrer wesentlich qualitativen Bestimmtheit gegeneinander.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"99.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0004","text":"Durch diese sind sie schlechthin nicht auseinander zu bringen; jede hat nur Bedeutung in Rücksicht auf die andere; insofern also eine einen Überschuß über die andere hätte, insofern hätte sie keine Beziehung auf diese und wäre nicht vorhanden.—Bei der Annahme, daß die eine das einemal größer sey als die andere, wenn sie als größere in Beziehung auf die kleinere stünde, tritt das oben Gesagte ein, daß sie absolut das Übergewicht erhielte, und die andere verschwände; die letztere ist als das Verschwindende, Haltungslose gesetzt, und an dieser Bestimmung ändert es nichts, daß das Verschwinden nur allmählig geschehen, und ebenso wenig, daß so viel sie abnähme an Größe, der erstern zuwachsen soll; dieses geht mit der andern zu Grunde, da was sie ist allein insofern ist, insofern die andere ist. Es ist eine sehr einfache Betrachtung, daß wenn z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"99.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0005","text":"wie vorgegeben wird, die Centripetalkraft des Körpers, indem er sich dem Perihelium nähert, zunehmen, die Centrifugalkraft hingegen um ebenso viel abnehmen soll, die letztere nicht mehr vermöchte, ihn der erstern zu entreißen, und von seinem Centralkörper wieder zu entfernen; im Gegentheil da die erstere einmal das Übergewicht haben soll, so ist die andere überwältigt, und der Körper wird mit beschleunigter Geschwindigkeit seinem Centralkörper zugeführt.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"99.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0006","text":"Wie umgekehrt, wenn die Centrifugalkraft an der unendlichen Nähe des Apheliums die Oberhand hat, es ebenso widersprechend ist, daß sie nun im Aphelium selbst von der schwächern überwältigt werden sollte.—Es erhellt ferner, daß es eine fremde Kraft wäre, welche diese Umkehrung bewirkte, dieß heißt, daß die bald beschleunigte, bald retardirte Geschwindigkeit der Bewegung nicht aus der angenommenen Bestimmung jener Faktoren erkannt oder, wie es genannt wird, erklärt werden könne, welche gerade deswegen angenommen worden sind, um diesen Unterschied zu erklären. Die Konsequenz des Verschwindens der einen oder der andern Richtung und damit der elliptischen Bewegung überhaupt, wird um des feststehenden Faktums willen, daß diese Bewegung fortdauert und aus der beschleunigten in die retardirte Geschwindigkeit übergeht, ignorirt und verborgen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"99.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0007","text":"Die Annahme des Umschlagens der Schwäche der Centripetalkraft im Aphelium in eine überwiegende Stärke gegen die Centrifugalkraft, und umgekehrt beim Perihelium, enthält Theils dasjenige, was oben entwickelt worden, daß jede der Seiten des umgekehrten Verhältnisses an ihr selbst dieß ganze umgekehrte Verhältniß ist; denn die Seite der Bewegung vom Aphelium zum Perihelium,—der überwiegend seyn sollenden Centripetalkraft,—soll noch die Centrifugalkraft enthalten, aber im Abnehmen, wie jene zunimmt; in eben dem umgekehrten Verhältniß soll sich in der Seite der retardirten Bewegung die überwiegende und immer überwiegender werdende Centrifugalkraft zur Centripetalkraft befinden, so daß auf keiner Seite eine derselben verschwunden sey, sondern nur immer kleiner werde bis zur Zeit ihres Umschlagens zum Überwiegen über die andere.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"99.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0008","text":"Es rekurrirt damit nur an jeder Seite das, was der Mangel an diesem umgekehrten Verhältniß ist, daß entweder jede Kraft selbstständig für sich genommen wird, und mit dem bloß äußerlichen Zusammentreffen derselben zu einer Bewegung, wie im Parallelogramm der Kräfte, die Einheit des Begriffs, die Natur der Sache, aufgehoben ist, oder daß, indem beide sich qualitativ durch den Begriff zu einander verhalten, keine ein gleichgültiges, selbstständiges Bestehen gegen die andere erhalten kann, was ihr durch ein Mehr zugetheilt werden sollte; die Form der Intensität, das sogenannte Dynamische, ändert nichts, da es selbst in dem Quantum seine Bestimmtheit hat, und damit ebenso nur so viel Kraft äußern kann, d. h. nur insoweit existirt, als es an der entgegengesetzten Kraft sich gegenüber stehen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"99.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0009","text":"Theils aber enthält jenes Umschlagen aus dem Überwiegen in das Gegentheil die Abwechslung der qualitativen Bestimmung von Positiven und Negativen; das Zunehmen der einen ist ebenso viel Verlust der andern. Der untrennbare qualitative Zusammenhang dieses qualitativen Gegensatzes ist in der Theorie in ein Nacheinander auseinander gerückt; aber damit bleibt sie die Erklärung dieser Abwechslung sowohl als vornehmlich dieses Auseinanderrückens selbst schuldig. Der Schein von Einheit, der noch in dem Zunehmen der einen mit ebenso vielem Abnehmen der andern liegt, verschwindet hier vollends; es ist ein bloß äußerliches Erfolgen angegeben, das nur der Konsequenz jenes Zusammenhangs, nach der insofern die eine überwiegend geworden, die andere verschwinden muß, widerspricht.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"99.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0010","text":"Dasselbe Verhältniß ist auf die Attraktiv- und Repulsivkraft angewendet worden, um die verschiedene Dichtigkeit der Körper zu begreifen; auch das umgekehrte Verhältniß der Sensibilität und Irritabilität, hat dazu dienen sollen, um aus dem Ungleichwerden dieser Faktoren des Lebens die verschiedenen Bestimmungen des Ganzen, der Gesundheit, wie auch die Verschiedenheit der Gattungen der Lebendigen zu begreifen. Jedoch die Verwirrung, und der Galimathias, in welchen sich dieß Erklären, das eine naturphilosophische Grundlage der Physiologie, Nosologie, und dann der Zoologie werden sollte, in dem unkritischen Gebrauche dieser Begriffsbestimmungen verwickelte, hat hier zur Folge gehabt, daß dieser Formalismus bald wieder aufgegeben worden ist, der in der Wissenschaft besonders der physikalischen Astronomie in seiner ganzen Ausdehnung fortgeführt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"99.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0011","text":"Insofern die absolute Indifferenz die Grundbestimmung der spinozistischen Substanz zu seyn scheinen kann, so kann hierüber noch bemerkt werden, daß sie dieß allerdings in der Rücksicht ist, daß in beiden alle Bestimmungen des Seyns, wie überhaupt jede weitere konkrete Unterscheidung von Denken und Ausdehnung u.s.f. als verschwunden gesetzt werden. Es ist überhaupt gleichgültig, wenn bei der Abstraktion stehen geblieben werden soll, wie dasjenige, was in diesem Abgrund untergegangen ist, in seinem Daseyn ausgesehen habe. Aber die Substanz als Indifferenz ist Theils mit dem Bedürfniß des Bestimmens und mit der Rücksicht auf dasselbe verbunden; sie soll nicht die Substanz des Spinoza bleiben, deren einzige Bestimmung das Negative ist, daß in ihr alles absorbirt sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"99.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0012","text":"Bei Spinoza kommt der Unterschied, die Attribute, Denken und Ausdehnung, alsdann auch die Modi, die Affekten und alle übrigen Determinationen, ganz empirisch herbei; es ist der Verstand, selbst ein Modus, in welchen dieß Unterscheiden fällt; die Attribute stehen zur Substanz und zu einander in keiner weitern Bestimmtheit, als daß sie die Substanz ganz ausdrücken, und ihr Inhalt, die Ordnung der Dinge als ausgedehnter und als Gedanken dieselbe ist. Durch die Bestimmung der Substanz als Indifferenz kommt aber die Reflexion auf den Unterschied hinzu, er wird nun gesetzt, als das was er bei Spinoza an sich ist, nämlich als äußerlicher, und damit näher als quantitativer.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"99.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0013","text":"Die Indifferenz bleibt so in ihm wohl sich immanent, wie die Substanz, —aber abstrakt, nur an sich; der Unterschied ist nicht ihr immanent, als quantitativer ist er vielmehr das Gegentheil der Immanenz, und die quantitative Indifferenz ist vielmehr das Außersichseyn der Einheit. Der Unterschied ist damit auch nicht qualitativ aufgefaßt, die Substanz nicht als das sich selbst Unterscheidende, nicht als Subjekt bestimmt. Die nächste Folge in Rücksicht auf die Kategorie der Indifferenz selbst ist, daß an ihr der Unterschied von quantitativer und qualitativer Bestimmung auseinander fällt, wie in der Entwicklung der Indifferenz sich ergab; sie ist die Auflösung des Maaßes, in welchem beide Momente unmittelbar als eins gesetzt waren.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"99.13"}],"sha256":"619bc7a8481bfa0ce8739bdeaa0ba2232bf34e6cfb3f528b7efddb77e7f9ec9d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104512776918Z_57b151bd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"619bc7a8481bfa0ce8739bdeaa0ba2232bf34e6cfb3f528b7efddb77e7f9ec9d","sha256":"87b5202f497412f88ecabba1f1db22711130ce163c4a3a9014fd2a5042fbba69","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:45:12.776954+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0001","text":"The relation of a whole which is supposed to have its determinacy in the difference in magnitude of factors qualitatively determined in relation to one another is employed in the elliptical motion of the heavenly bodies. This example initially shows only two qualities in inverse relation to one another, not two sides each of which would itself be the unity of both and their inverse relation. Given the solidity of the empirical foundation, the consequence to which the theory introduced into it leads is overlooked, namely, to destroy the underlying fact, or, if this is properly held fast, to demonstrate the emptiness of the theory in relation to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"99.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0002","text":"Ignoring the consequence allows the fact and the theory contradicting it to subsist peacefully alongside one another.—The simple fact is that, in the elliptical motion of the heavenly bodies, their velocity accelerates as they approach perihelion, and diminishes as they approach aphelion. The quantitative aspect of this fact has been precisely determined by the tireless diligence of observation and further reduced to its simple law and formula; thus everything has been accomplished that can genuinely be demanded of theory. But this has not appeared sufficient to the reflecting understanding. For the so-called explanation of the phenomenon and its law, a centripetal and a centrifugal force are assumed as qualitative moments of motion in the curved line.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"99.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0003","text":"Their qualitative difference consists in the opposition of direction, and, in quantitative respect, in their being determined as unequal, such that as the one is supposed to increase, the other is supposed to decrease, and conversely; and further, in the fact that their relation is again supposed to reverse itself, so that, after the centripetal force has increased for a time while the centrifugal force has decreased, a point occurs at which the centripetal force decreases, whereas the centrifugal force increases. But this conception contradicts the relation of their essentially qualitative determinacy to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"99.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0004","text":"By virtue of this they are absolutely inseparable; each has meaning only in relation to the other; insofar, therefore, as one had an excess over the other, it would have no relation to it and would not be present.—On the assumption that one is at one time greater than the other, if it stood as the greater in relation to the lesser, what was stated above ensues: it would absolutely acquire the preponderance, and the other would disappear; the latter is posited as vanishing, without stability, and this determinacy is not altered by the fact that the vanishing should occur only gradually, nor likewise by the fact that, by as much as it diminished in magnitude, the former should increase; this perishes along with the other, since what it is, it is only insofar as the other is. It is a very simple consideration that, if, e.g.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"99.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0005","text":"as is asserted, the centripetal force of the body is supposed to increase as it approaches perihelion, while the centrifugal force is supposed to decrease by an equal amount, the latter would no longer be able to tear it away from the former and remove it again from its central body; on the contrary, since the former is once supposed to have the preponderance, the other is overpowered, and the body is conveyed with accelerated velocity to its central body.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"99.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0006","text":"Conversely, if the centrifugal force has the upper hand in the infinite proximity of aphelion, it is equally contradictory that it should then, at aphelion itself, be overpowered by the weaker force.—It is further evident that it would be an alien force that brought about this reversal; that is, that the now accelerated, now retarded velocity of motion cannot be cognized or, as it is called, explained from the assumed determinacy of those factors, which have been assumed precisely in order to explain this difference. The consequence of the disappearance of one or the other direction, and thus of elliptical motion altogether, is ignored and concealed for the sake of the established fact that this motion continues and passes from accelerated to retarded velocity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"99.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0007","text":"The assumption that the weakness of the centripetal force at aphelion reverses itself into a preponderating strength against the centrifugal force, and conversely at perihelion, contains in part what was developed above: that each of the sides of the inverse relation is in itself this whole inverse relation; for the side of motion from aphelion to perihelion,—that of the centripetal force which is supposed to predominate,—is still supposed to contain the centrifugal force, but as decreasing, as the former increases; in precisely the same inverse relation, the predominant and ever more predominant centrifugal force is supposed to be found in the side of retarded motion in relation to the centripetal force, so that on neither side has either of them disappeared, but each merely becomes ever smaller until the time of its reversal into predominance over the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"99.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0008","text":"Thus there recurs on each side only what is the defect in this inverse relation: either each force is taken independently by itself, and, with their merely external coming together into one motion, as in the parallelogram of forces, the unity of the concept, the nature of the matter, is abolished; or, since both are qualitatively related to one another through the concept, neither can acquire an indifferent, independent subsistence over against the other, which should be assigned to it through a greater amount; the form of intensity, the so-called dynamical, changes nothing, since it itself has its determinacy in the quantum, and thus can likewise exert only so much force, i.e. exists only insofar as it has the opposite force standing over against it.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"99.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0009","text":"But in part that reversal from predominance into the opposite contains the alternation of the qualitative determinacy of positive and negative; the increase of the one is equally the loss of the other. The inseparable qualitative connection of this qualitative opposition is stretched out in the theory into a succession; but in so doing it remains indebted for an explanation both of this alternation and, above all, of this stretching apart itself. The semblance of unity still present in the increase of the one together with an equal decrease of the other here disappears altogether; a merely external succession is indicated, which only contradicts the consequence of that connection, according to which, insofar as the one has become predominant, the other must disappear.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"99.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0010","text":"The same relation has been applied to attractive and repulsive force in order to comprehend the differing density of bodies; likewise, the inverse relation of sensibility and irritability was supposed to serve to comprehend, from the becoming unequal of these factors of life, the various determinations of the whole, health, as well as the diversity of the species of living things. Yet the confusion and gibberish into which this explaining, which was supposed to become a philosophy-of-nature foundation for physiology, nosology, and then zoology, became entangled through the uncritical use of these conceptual determinations, has here had the consequence that this formalism was soon again abandoned, whereas in science, especially in physical astronomy, it is carried through in its whole extent.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"99.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0011","text":"Insofar as absolute indifference can seem to be the fundamental determination of Spinozistic substance, it may further be observed concerning this that it certainly is so in the respect that in it all determinations of being, as well as every further concrete distinction of thought and extension, etc., are posited as vanished. It is generally indifferent, if one is to remain at abstraction, what that which has gone under in this abyss may have looked like in its existence. But substance as indifference is in part connected with the need for determining and with reference to it; it is not supposed to remain the substance of Spinoza, whose sole determination is the negative one that everything is absorbed in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"99.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0012","text":"In Spinoza, difference, the attributes, thought and extension, then also the modes, the affections and all the remaining determinations, arrive quite empirically; it is the understanding, itself a mode, into which this distinguishing falls; the attributes stand in no further determinacy, either toward substance or toward one another, than that they express substance wholly and that their content, the order of things as extended and as thoughts, is the same. But through the determination of substance as indifference, reflection upon difference is added; it is now posited as what it is in itself in Spinoza, namely as external, and thus, more closely, as quantitative.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"99.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_25:P0013","text":"Indifference thus indeed remains immanent in it, as substance,—but abstractly, only in itself; difference is not immanent in it; as quantitative, it is rather the opposite of immanence, and quantitative indifference is rather the being-outside-itself of unity. Difference is thereby not apprehended qualitatively either; substance is not determined as that which distinguishes itself, not as subject. The immediate consequence with respect to the category of indifference itself is that in it the difference between quantitative and qualitative determinacy falls apart, as emerged in the development of indifference; it is the dissolution of measure, in which both moments were immediately posited as one.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"99.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_25:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"bcd4a453fec7d8c9371539ee35b791b521595086423182f7a587fd8865d51c06","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW","title":"C. Transition into Essence.","order":100,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CBDW","text":"Die absolute Indifferenz ist die letzte Bestimmung des Seyns, ehe dieses zum Wesen wird; sie erreicht aber dieses nicht. Sie zeigt sich noch der Sphäre des Seyns anzugehören, indem sie noch als gleichgültig bestimmt, den Unterschied als äußerlichen, quantitativen an ihr hat. Dieß ist ihr Daseyn, womit sie sich zugleich in dem Gegensatze befindet, gegen dasselbe als nur das an sichseyende bestimmt, nicht als das fürsichseyende Absolute gedacht zu seyn. Oder es ist die äußere Reflexion, welche dabei stehen bleibt, daß die Specifischen an sich oder im Absoluten dasselbe und eins sind, daß ihr Unterschied nur ein gleichgültiger, kein Unterschied an sich ist. Was hier noch fehlt, besteht darin, daß diese Reflexion, nicht die äußere Reflexion des denkenden, subjektiven Bewußtseyns, sondern die eigene Bestimmung der Unterschiede jener Einheit sey, sich aufzuheben, welche Einheit denn so sich erweist, die absolute Negativität, ihre Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich selbst, gegen ihre eigene Gleichgültigkeit, ebenso sehr als gegen das Andersseyn zu seyn.\n\nDieß Sich-Aufheben der Bestimmung der Indifferenz aber hat sich bereits ergeben; sie hat sich in der Entwicklung ihres Gesetztseyns nach allen Seiten als der Widerspruch gezeigt. Sie ist an sich die Totalität, in der alle Bestimmungen des Seyns aufgehoben und enthalten sind; so ist sie die Grundlage, aber ist nur erst in der einseitigen Bestimmung des Ansichseyns und damit sind die Unterschiede, die quantitative Differenz und das umgekehrte Verhältniß von Faktoren, als äußerlich an ihr. So der Widerspruch ihrer selbst und ihres Bestimmtseyns, ihrer an sich seyenden Bestimmung und ihrer gesetzten Bestimmtheit ist sie die negative Totalität, deren Bestimmtheiten sich an ihnen selbst und damit diese ihre Grundeinseitigkeit, ihr Ansichseyn, aufgehoben haben. Gesetzt hiermit als das, was die Indifferenz in der That ist, ist sie einfache und unendliche negative Beziehung auf sich, die Unverträglichkeit ihrer mit ihr selbst, Abstoßen ihrer von sich selbst. Das Bestimmen und Bestimmtwerden ist nicht ein Übergehen, noch äußerliche Veränderung, noch ein Hervortreten der Bestimmungen an ihr, sondern ihr eignes Beziehen auf sich, das die Negativität ihrer selbst, ihres Ansichseyns, ist.\n\nDie Bestimmungen, als solche abgestoßene, gehören aber nun nicht sich selbst an, treten nicht in Selbstständigkeit oder Äußerlichkeit hervor, sondern sind als Momente;—erstens der ansichseyenden Einheit angehörig, nicht von ihr entlassen, sondern von ihr als dem Substrate getragen und nur von ihr erfüllt; und zweitens als die Bestimmungen, die der fürsichseyenden Einheit immanent, nur durch deren Abstoßen von sich, sind. Sie sind statt Seyender, wie in der ganzen Sphäre des Seyns nunmehr schlechthin nur als Gesetzte, schlechthin mit der Bestimmung und Bedeutung, auf ihre Einheit, somit jede auf ihre andere und Negation, bezogen zu seyn,—bezeichnet mit dieser ihrer Relativität.\n\nDamit ist das Seyn überhaupt und das Seyn oder die Unmittelbarkeit der unterschiedenen Bestimmtheiten ebenso sehr als das Ansichseyn verschwunden, und die Einheit ist Seyn, unmittelbare vorausgesetzte Totalität, so daß sie diese einfache Beziehung auf sich nur ist, vermittelt durch das Aufheben dieser Voraussetzung, und dieß Vorausgesetztseyn und unmittelbare Seyn selbst nur ein Moment ihres Abstoßens ist, die ursprüngliche Selbstständigkeit und Identität mit sich nur ist, als das resultirende, unendliche Zusammengehen mit sich; so ist das Seyn zum Wesen bestimmt, das Seyn, als durch Aufheben des Seyns einfaches Seyn nnt sich.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Die absolute Indifferenz ist die letzte Bestimmung des Seyns, ehe dieses zum Wesen wird; sie erreicht aber dieses nicht. Sie zeigt sich noch der Sphäre des Seyns anzugehören, indem sie noch als gleichgültig bestimmt, den Unterschied als äußerlichen, quantitativen an ihr hat. Dieß ist ihr Daseyn, womit sie sich zugleich in dem Gegensatze befindet, gegen dasselbe als nur das an sichseyende bestimmt, nicht als das fürsichseyende Absolute gedacht zu seyn. Oder es ist die äußere Reflexion, welche dabei stehen bleibt, daß die Specifischen an sich oder im Absoluten dasselbe und eins sind, daß ihr Unterschied nur ein gleichgültiger, kein Unterschied an sich ist. Was hier noch fehlt, besteht darin, daß diese Reflexion, nicht die äußere Reflexion des denkenden, subjektiven Bewußtseyns, sondern die eigene Bestimmung der Unterschiede jener Einheit sey, sich aufzuheben, welche Einheit denn so sich erweist, die absolute Negativität, ihre Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich selbst, gegen ihre eigene Gleichgültigkeit, ebenso sehr als gegen das Andersseyn zu seyn.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Dieß Sich-Aufheben der Bestimmung der Indifferenz aber hat sich bereits ergeben; sie hat sich in der Entwicklung ihres Gesetztseyns nach allen Seiten als der Widerspruch gezeigt. Sie ist an sich die Totalität, in der alle Bestimmungen des Seyns aufgehoben und enthalten sind; so ist sie die Grundlage, aber ist nur erst in der einseitigen Bestimmung des Ansichseyns und damit sind die Unterschiede, die quantitative Differenz und das umgekehrte Verhältniß von Faktoren, als äußerlich an ihr. So der Widerspruch ihrer selbst und ihres Bestimmtseyns, ihrer an sich seyenden Bestimmung und ihrer gesetzten Bestimmtheit ist sie die negative Totalität, deren Bestimmtheiten sich an ihnen selbst und damit diese ihre Grundeinseitigkeit, ihr Ansichseyn, aufgehoben haben. Gesetzt hiermit als das, was die Indifferenz in der That ist, ist sie einfache und unendliche negative Beziehung auf sich, die Unverträglichkeit ihrer mit ihr selbst, Abstoßen ihrer von sich selbst. Das Bestimmen und Bestimmtwerden ist nicht ein Übergehen, noch äußerliche Veränderung, noch ein Hervortreten der Bestimmungen an ihr, sondern ihr eignes Beziehen auf sich, das die Negativität ihrer selbst, ihres Ansichseyns, ist.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Die Bestimmungen, als solche abgestoßene, gehören aber nun nicht sich selbst an, treten nicht in Selbstständigkeit oder Äußerlichkeit hervor, sondern sind als Momente;—erstens der ansichseyenden Einheit angehörig, nicht von ihr entlassen, sondern von ihr als dem Substrate getragen und nur von ihr erfüllt; und zweitens als die Bestimmungen, die der fürsichseyenden Einheit immanent, nur durch deren Abstoßen von sich, sind. Sie sind statt Seyender, wie in der ganzen Sphäre des Seyns nunmehr schlechthin nur als Gesetzte, schlechthin mit der Bestimmung und Bedeutung, auf ihre Einheit, somit jede auf ihre andere und Negation, bezogen zu seyn,—bezeichnet mit dieser ihrer Relativität.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Damit ist das Seyn überhaupt und das Seyn oder die Unmittelbarkeit der unterschiedenen Bestimmtheiten ebenso sehr als das Ansichseyn verschwunden, und die Einheit ist Seyn, unmittelbare vorausgesetzte Totalität, so daß sie diese einfache Beziehung auf sich nur ist, vermittelt durch das Aufheben dieser Voraussetzung, und dieß Vorausgesetztseyn und unmittelbare Seyn selbst nur ein Moment ihres Abstoßens ist, die ursprüngliche Selbstständigkeit und Identität mit sich nur ist, als das resultirende, unendliche Zusammengehen mit sich; so ist das Seyn zum Wesen bestimmt, das Seyn, als durch Aufheben des Seyns einfaches Seyn nnt sich.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"40832abb71d9d075d3bc88326b3eb4030d137eeefe92d91382309c993fa9f31a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104523517707Z_022f6d28","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Transition into Essence.","source_sha256":"40832abb71d9d075d3bc88326b3eb4030d137eeefe92d91382309c993fa9f31a","sha256":"0212723a1eaf468b59d21ae8163496bb641c0c88aa9dec9ee8b05d2a495a11bb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:45:23.517734+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104523517707Z_022f6d28:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Absolute indifference is the final determination of Being before it becomes Essence; yet it does not attain to this. It shows itself still to belong to the sphere of Being in that it is still determined as indifferent, having difference in it as external, quantitative difference. This is its determinate being, whereby it is at the same time in opposition to it, being determined over against the same only as that which is being-in-itself, not thought as the absolute being-for-itself. Or it is external reflection, which remains at the point that the Specifics are the same and one in themselves or in the Absolute, that their difference is only an indifferent difference, not a difference in itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104523517707Z_022f6d28:DISPLAY-0002","text":"What is still lacking here consists in this: that this reflection should be, not the external reflection of thinking, subjective consciousness, but the proper determination of the differences of that unity, to sublate itself; which unity then thereby proves itself to be absolute negativity, to be its indifference toward itself, toward its own indifference, just as much as toward otherness.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104523517707Z_022f6d28:DISPLAY-0003","text":"But this self-sublation of the determination of indifference has already emerged; in the development of its positedness in all directions, it has shown itself to be contradiction. It is in itself the totality in which all determinations of Being are sublated and contained; thus it is the ground, but is as yet only in the one-sided determination of being-in-itself, and thereby the differences, the quantitative difference and the inverse relation of factors, are external to it. Thus, as the contradiction of itself and its determinacy, of its determination which is being-in-itself and its posited determinateness, it is the negative totality, whose determinatenesses have sublated themselves in themselves and thereby have sublated this their one-sidedness of ground, their being-in-itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104523517707Z_022f6d28:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Posited thereby as what indifference is in fact, it is simple and infinite negative relation to itself, the incompatibility of itself with itself, its repulsion of itself from itself. Determining and being-determined is not a transition, nor external alteration, nor an emergence of the determinations in it, but its own relating itself to itself, which is the negativity of itself, of its being-in-itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0003","text":"But the determinations, as such repelled ones, now do not belong to themselves, do not emerge into self-subsistence or externality, but are as moments;—first, belonging to the unity that is being-in-itself, not released from it, but borne by it as by the substrate and fulfilled only by it; and second, as the determinations that are immanent in the unity that is being-for-itself, existing only through its repulsion of itself from itself. Instead of beings, as throughout the entire sphere of Being, they are henceforth absolutely only as posited, absolutely with the determination and significance of being related to their unity, and thus each to its other and to negation,—designated by this their relativity.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0004","text":"With this, Being in general, and Being or the immediacy of the differentiated determinatenesses, just as much as being-in-itself, has vanished, and unity is Being, immediate presupposed totality, such that it is this simple relation to itself only as mediated through the sublation of this presupposition, and this presupposedness and immediate Being itself are only a moment of its repulsion, primordial self-subsistence and identity with itself being only as the resultant, infinite coming-together with itself; thus Being is determined as Essence, Being, as simple Being through the sublation of Being nnt itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CBDW:DISPLAY-0004"]}],"source_digest":"cd3ea8ecd1d1881f3f8f65475e481410b92564b9cb538c239d3ff0309a855703","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Übergang in das Wesen."}],"original_title":"C. Übergang in das Wesen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW","title":"Second Book. The Doctrine of Essence.","order":101,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ZBDW","text":"Die Wahrheit des Seyns ist das Wesen.\n\nDas Seyn ist das Unmittelbare. Indem das Wissen das Wahre erkennen will, was das Seyn an und für sich ist, so bleibt es nicht beim Unmittelbaren und dessen Bestimmungen stehen, sondern dringt durch dasselbe hindurch, mit der Voraussetzung, daß hinter diesem Seyn noch etwas Anderes ist, als das Seyn selbst, daß dieser Hintergrund die Wahrheit des Seyns ausmacht. Diese Erkenntniß ist ein vermitteltes Wissen, denn sie befindet sich nicht unmittelbar beim und im Wesen, sondern beginnt von einem Andern, dem Seyn, und hat einen vorläufigen Weg, den Weg des Hinausgehens über das Seyn oder vielmehr des Hineingehens in dasselbe zu machen. Erst indem das Wissen sich aus dem unmittelbaren Seyn erinnert, durch diese Vermittlung findet es das Wesen.—Die Sprache hat im Zeitwort: Seyn, das Wesen in der vergangenen Zeit: gewesen, behalten; denn das Wesen ist das vergangene, aber zeitlos vergangene Seyn.\n\nDiese Bewegung, als Weg des Wissens vorgestellt, so erscheint dieser Anfang vom Seyn und der Fortgang, der es aufhebt und beim Wesen als einem Vermittelten anlangt, eine Thätigkeit des Erkennens zu seyn, die dem Seyn äußerlich sey und dessen eigene Natur nichts angehe.\n\nAber dieser Gang ist die Bewegung des Seyns selbst. Es zeigte sich an diesem, daß es durch seine Natur sich erinnert, und durch dieß Insichgehen zum Wesen wird.\n\nWenn also das Absolute zuerst als Seyn bestimmt war, so ist es jetzt als Wesen bestimmt. Das Erkennen kann überhaupt nicht bei dem mannigfaltigen Daseyn, aber auch nicht bei dem Seyn, dem reinen Seyn, stehen bleiben; es dringt sich unmittelbar die Reflexion auf, daß dieses reine Seyn, die Negation alles Endlichen, eine Erinnerung und Bewegung voraussetzt, welche das unmittelbare Daseyn zum reinen Seyn gereinigt hat. Das Seyn wird hiernach als Wesen bestimmt, als ein solches Seyn, an dem alles Bestimmte und Endliche negirt ist. So ist es die bestimmungslose einfache Einheit, von der das Bestimmte auf eine äußerliche Weise hinweggenommen worden; dieser Einheit war das Bestimmte selbst ein Äußerliches, und es bleibt ihr nach diesem Wegnehmen noch gegenüber stehen; denn es ist nicht an sich, sondern relativ, nur in Beziehung auf diese Einheit, aufgehoben worden.—Es wurde oben schon erinnert, daß wenn das reine Wesen als Inbegriff aller Realitäten bestimmt wird, diese Realitäten gleichfalls der Natur der Bestimmtheit, und der abstrahirenden Reflexion unterliegen, und dieser Innbegriff sich zur leeren Einfachheit reducirt. Das Wesen ist auf diese Weise nur Produkt, ein Gemachtes. Die äußerliche Negation, welche Abstraktion ist, hebt die Bestimmtheiten des Seyns nur hinweg von dem, was als Wesen übrig bleibt; es stellt sie gleichsam nur an einen andern Ort, und läßt sie als seyende vor wie nach. Das Wesen ist aber auf diese Weise weder an sich, noch für sich selbst; es ist durch ein Anderes, die äußerliche, abstrahirende Reflexion; und ist für ein Anderes, nämlich für die Abstraktion und überhaupt für das ihm gegenüber stehen bleibende Seyende. In seiner Bestimmung ist es daher die in sich todte, leere Bestimmungslosigkeit.\n\nDas Wesen aber, wie es hier geworden ist, ist das, was es ist, nicht durch eine ihm fremde Negativität, sondern durch seine eigne, die unendliche Bewegung des Seyns. Es ist An-und-Fürsichseyn; absolutes Ansichseyn, indem es gleichgültig gegen alle Bestimmtheit des Seyns ist, das Andersseyn und die Beziehung auf anderes schlechthin aufgehoben worden ist. Es ist aber nicht nur dieß Ansichseyn; als bloßes Ansichseyn wäre es nur die Abstraktion des reinen Wesens; sondern es ist ebenso wesentlich Fürsichseyn; es selbst ist diese Negativität, das sich Aufheben des Andersseyns und der Bestimmtheit.\n\nDas Wesen als die vollkommene Rückkehr des Seyns in sich ist so zunächst das unbestimmte Wesen; die Bestimmtheiten des Seyns sind in ihm aufgehoben; es enthält sie an sich; aber nicht wie sie an ihm gesetzt sind. Das absolute Wesen in dieser Einfachheit mit sich hat kein Daseyn. Aber es muß zum Daseyn übergehen; denn es ist An-und-Fürsichseyn, das heißt, es unterscheidet die Bestimmungen, welche es an sich enthält; weil es Abstoßen seiner von sich oder Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich, negative Beziehung auf sich ist, setzt es sich somit sich selbst gegenüber, und ist nur insofern unendliches Fürsichseyn als es die Einheit mit sich in diesem seinem Unterschiede von sich ist.—Dieses Bestimmen ist denn anderer Natur, als das Bestimmen in der Sphäre des Seyns, und die Bestimmungen des Wesens haben einen andern Charakter als die Bestimmtheiten des Seyns. Das Wesen ist absolute Einheit des An-und-Fürsichseyns; sein Bestimmen bleibt daher innerhalb dieser Einheit, und ist kein Werden noch Übergehen, so wie die Bestimmungen selbst nicht ein Anderes als anderes, noch Beziehungen auf Anderes sind; sie sind Selbstständige aber damit nur als solche, die in ihrer Einheit mit einander sind. —Indem das Wesen zuerst einfache Negativität ist, so hat es nun die Bestimmtheit, welche es nur an sich enthält, in seiner Sphäre zu setzen, um sich Daseyn und dann sein Fürsichseyn zu geben.\n\nDas Wesen ist im Ganzen das, was die Quantität in der Sphäre des Seyns war; die absolute Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Grenze. Die Quantität aber ist diese Gleichgültigkeit in unmittelbarer Bestimmung, und die Grenze an ihr unmittelbar äußerliche Bestimmtheit, sie geht ins Quantum über; die äußerliche Grenze ist ihr nothwendig, und ist an ihr seyend. Am Wesen hingegen ist die Bestimmtheit nicht; sie ist nur durch das Wesen selbst gesetzt; nicht frey, sondern nur in der Beziehung auf seine Einheit.—Die Negativität des Wesens ist die Reflexion, und die Bestimmungen reflektirte, durch das Wesen selbst gesetzte und in ihm als aufgehoben bleibende.\n\nDas Wesen steht zwischen Seyn und Begriff und macht die Mitte derselben und seine Bewegung den Übergang von Seyn in den Begriff aus. Das Wesen ist das An-und-Fürsichseyn, aber dasselbe in der Bestimmung des Ansichseyns; denn seine allgemeine Bestimmung ist, aus dem Seyn herzukommen, oder die erste Negation des Seyns zu seyn. Seine Bewegung besteht darin, die Negation oder Bestimmung an ihm zu setzen, dadurch sich Daseyn zu geben, und das als unendliches Fürsichseyn zu werden, was es an sich ist. So giebt es sich sein Daseyn, das seinem Ansichseyn gleich ist, und wird der Begriff. Denn der Begriff ist das Absolute, wie es in seinem Daseyn absolut oder an und für sich ist. Das Daseyn aber, das sich das Wesen giebt, ist noch nicht das Daseyn, wie es an und für sich ist, sondern wie das Wesen es sich giebt, oder wie es gesetzt wird, daher noch von dem Daseyn des Begriffs unterschieden.\n\nDas Wesen scheint zuerst in sich selbst, oder ist Reflexion; zweitens erscheint es; drittens offenbart es sich. Es setzt sich in seiner Bewegung in folgende Bestimmungen,\n\nI. als einfaches, ansichseyendes Wesen in seinen Bestimmungen innerhalb seiner;\n\nII. als heraustretend in das Daseyn, oder nach seiner Existenz und Erscheinung;\n\nIII. als Wesen, das mit seiner Erscheinung eins ist, als Wirklichkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0001","text":"Die Wahrheit des Seyns ist das Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"101.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0002","text":"Das Seyn ist das Unmittelbare. Indem das Wissen das Wahre erkennen will, was das Seyn an und für sich ist, so bleibt es nicht beim Unmittelbaren und dessen Bestimmungen stehen, sondern dringt durch dasselbe hindurch, mit der Voraussetzung, daß hinter diesem Seyn noch etwas Anderes ist, als das Seyn selbst, daß dieser Hintergrund die Wahrheit des Seyns ausmacht. Diese Erkenntniß ist ein vermitteltes Wissen, denn sie befindet sich nicht unmittelbar beim und im Wesen, sondern beginnt von einem Andern, dem Seyn, und hat einen vorläufigen Weg, den Weg des Hinausgehens über das Seyn oder vielmehr des Hineingehens in dasselbe zu machen. Erst indem das Wissen sich aus dem unmittelbaren Seyn erinnert, durch diese Vermittlung findet es das Wesen.—Die Sprache hat im Zeitwort: Seyn, das Wesen in der vergangenen Zeit: gewesen, behalten; denn das Wesen ist das vergangene, aber zeitlos vergangene Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"101.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0003","text":"Diese Bewegung, als Weg des Wissens vorgestellt, so erscheint dieser Anfang vom Seyn und der Fortgang, der es aufhebt und beim Wesen als einem Vermittelten anlangt, eine Thätigkeit des Erkennens zu seyn, die dem Seyn äußerlich sey und dessen eigene Natur nichts angehe.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"101.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0004","text":"Aber dieser Gang ist die Bewegung des Seyns selbst. Es zeigte sich an diesem, daß es durch seine Natur sich erinnert, und durch dieß Insichgehen zum Wesen wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"101.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0005","text":"Wenn also das Absolute zuerst als Seyn bestimmt war, so ist es jetzt als Wesen bestimmt. Das Erkennen kann überhaupt nicht bei dem mannigfaltigen Daseyn, aber auch nicht bei dem Seyn, dem reinen Seyn, stehen bleiben; es dringt sich unmittelbar die Reflexion auf, daß dieses reine Seyn, die Negation alles Endlichen, eine Erinnerung und Bewegung voraussetzt, welche das unmittelbare Daseyn zum reinen Seyn gereinigt hat. Das Seyn wird hiernach als Wesen bestimmt, als ein solches Seyn, an dem alles Bestimmte und Endliche negirt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"101.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0006","text":"So ist es die bestimmungslose einfache Einheit, von der das Bestimmte auf eine äußerliche Weise hinweggenommen worden; dieser Einheit war das Bestimmte selbst ein Äußerliches, und es bleibt ihr nach diesem Wegnehmen noch gegenüber stehen; denn es ist nicht an sich, sondern relativ, nur in Beziehung auf diese Einheit, aufgehoben worden.—Es wurde oben schon erinnert, daß wenn das reine Wesen als Inbegriff aller Realitäten bestimmt wird, diese Realitäten gleichfalls der Natur der Bestimmtheit, und der abstrahirenden Reflexion unterliegen, und dieser Innbegriff sich zur leeren Einfachheit reducirt. Das Wesen ist auf diese Weise nur Produkt, ein Gemachtes. Die äußerliche Negation, welche Abstraktion ist, hebt die Bestimmtheiten des Seyns nur hinweg von dem, was als Wesen übrig bleibt; es stellt sie gleichsam nur an einen andern Ort, und läßt sie als seyende vor wie nach.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"101.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0007","text":"Das Wesen ist aber auf diese Weise weder an sich, noch für sich selbst; es ist durch ein Anderes, die äußerliche, abstrahirende Reflexion; und ist für ein Anderes, nämlich für die Abstraktion und überhaupt für das ihm gegenüber stehen bleibende Seyende. In seiner Bestimmung ist es daher die in sich todte, leere Bestimmungslosigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"101.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0008","text":"Das Wesen aber, wie es hier geworden ist, ist das, was es ist, nicht durch eine ihm fremde Negativität, sondern durch seine eigne, die unendliche Bewegung des Seyns. Es ist An-und-Fürsichseyn; absolutes Ansichseyn, indem es gleichgültig gegen alle Bestimmtheit des Seyns ist, das Andersseyn und die Beziehung auf anderes schlechthin aufgehoben worden ist. Es ist aber nicht nur dieß Ansichseyn; als bloßes Ansichseyn wäre es nur die Abstraktion des reinen Wesens; sondern es ist ebenso wesentlich Fürsichseyn; es selbst ist diese Negativität, das sich Aufheben des Andersseyns und der Bestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"101.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0009","text":"Das Wesen als die vollkommene Rückkehr des Seyns in sich ist so zunächst das unbestimmte Wesen; die Bestimmtheiten des Seyns sind in ihm aufgehoben; es enthält sie an sich; aber nicht wie sie an ihm gesetzt sind. Das absolute Wesen in dieser Einfachheit mit sich hat kein Daseyn. Aber es muß zum Daseyn übergehen; denn es ist An-und-Fürsichseyn, das heißt, es unterscheidet die Bestimmungen, welche es an sich enthält; weil es Abstoßen seiner von sich oder Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich, negative Beziehung auf sich ist, setzt es sich somit sich selbst gegenüber, und ist nur insofern unendliches Fürsichseyn als es die Einheit mit sich in diesem seinem Unterschiede von sich ist.—Dieses Bestimmen ist denn anderer Natur, als das Bestimmen in der Sphäre des Seyns, und die Bestimmungen des Wesens haben einen andern Charakter als die Bestimmtheiten des Seyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"101.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0010","text":"Das Wesen ist absolute Einheit des An-und-Fürsichseyns; sein Bestimmen bleibt daher innerhalb dieser Einheit, und ist kein Werden noch Übergehen, so wie die Bestimmungen selbst nicht ein Anderes als anderes, noch Beziehungen auf Anderes sind; sie sind Selbstständige aber damit nur als solche, die in ihrer Einheit mit einander sind. —Indem das Wesen zuerst einfache Negativität ist, so hat es nun die Bestimmtheit, welche es nur an sich enthält, in seiner Sphäre zu setzen, um sich Daseyn und dann sein Fürsichseyn zu geben.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"101.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0011","text":"Das Wesen ist im Ganzen das, was die Quantität in der Sphäre des Seyns war; die absolute Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Grenze. Die Quantität aber ist diese Gleichgültigkeit in unmittelbarer Bestimmung, und die Grenze an ihr unmittelbar äußerliche Bestimmtheit, sie geht ins Quantum über; die äußerliche Grenze ist ihr nothwendig, und ist an ihr seyend. Am Wesen hingegen ist die Bestimmtheit nicht; sie ist nur durch das Wesen selbst gesetzt; nicht frey, sondern nur in der Beziehung auf seine Einheit.—Die Negativität des Wesens ist die Reflexion, und die Bestimmungen reflektirte, durch das Wesen selbst gesetzte und in ihm als aufgehoben bleibende.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"101.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0012","text":"Das Wesen steht zwischen Seyn und Begriff und macht die Mitte derselben und seine Bewegung den Übergang von Seyn in den Begriff aus. Das Wesen ist das An-und-Fürsichseyn, aber dasselbe in der Bestimmung des Ansichseyns; denn seine allgemeine Bestimmung ist, aus dem Seyn herzukommen, oder die erste Negation des Seyns zu seyn. Seine Bewegung besteht darin, die Negation oder Bestimmung an ihm zu setzen, dadurch sich Daseyn zu geben, und das als unendliches Fürsichseyn zu werden, was es an sich ist. So giebt es sich sein Daseyn, das seinem Ansichseyn gleich ist, und wird der Begriff. Denn der Begriff ist das Absolute, wie es in seinem Daseyn absolut oder an und für sich ist. Das Daseyn aber, das sich das Wesen giebt, ist noch nicht das Daseyn, wie es an und für sich ist, sondern wie das Wesen es sich giebt, oder wie es gesetzt wird, daher noch von dem Daseyn des Begriffs unterschieden.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"101.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0013","text":"Das Wesen scheint zuerst in sich selbst, oder ist Reflexion; zweitens erscheint es; drittens offenbart es sich. Es setzt sich in seiner Bewegung in folgende Bestimmungen,","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"101.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0014","text":"I. als einfaches, ansichseyendes Wesen in seinen Bestimmungen innerhalb seiner;","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"101.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0015","text":"II. als heraustretend in das Daseyn, oder nach seiner Existenz und Erscheinung;","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"101.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0016","text":"III. als Wesen, das mit seiner Erscheinung eins ist, als Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"101.16"}],"sha256":"84991ea8ec8a1aa13d835906fb396cf201400ef9364b6723e13847591373dce7","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104537959554Z_5ca054ee","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Second Book. The Doctrine of Essence.","source_sha256":"84991ea8ec8a1aa13d835906fb396cf201400ef9364b6723e13847591373dce7","sha256":"7bfa5372e54d9d63ae41ad7db3804a8ba842fa633289b44770aada0fca9f0121","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:45:37.959612+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0001","text":"The truth of Being is essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"101.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0002","text":"Being is the immediate. Since cognition seeks to cognize the True, what Being is in and for itself, it does not remain at the immediate and its determinations, but penetrates through it, on the presupposition that behind this Being there is something other than Being itself, that this background constitutes the truth of Being. This cognition is a mediated knowing, for it is not immediately with and in essence, but begins from an other, from Being, and has a preliminary path to traverse, the path of going out beyond Being, or rather of going into it. Only in so far as knowing recollects itself out of immediate Being does it find essence through this mediation.—Language has retained, in the verb “to be” [Seyn], essence [Wesen] in the past tense: “been” [gewesen]; for essence is the past, but timelessly past, Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"101.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0003","text":"If this movement is represented as the path of knowing, then this beginning from Being and the progression which sublates it and arrives at essence as something mediated appears to be an activity of cognition that is external to Being and does not concern its own nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"101.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0004","text":"But this course is the movement of Being itself. It was shown of Being that by its nature it recollects itself, and through this going-into-itself becomes essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"101.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0005","text":"Thus, if the Absolute was at first determined as Being, it is now determined as essence. Cognition cannot in general remain with manifold determinate being, nor with Being, with pure Being; reflection immediately obtrudes itself, that this pure Being, the negation of everything finite, presupposes a recollection and movement which has purified immediate determinate being into pure Being. Being is accordingly determined as essence, as such Being in which everything determinate and finite is negated.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"101.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0006","text":"Thus it is the indeterminate simple unity from which the determinate has been removed in an external manner; the determinate itself was an externality to this unity, and after this removal it still remains opposed to it; for it has been sublated not in itself, but relatively, only in relation to this unity.—It was already recalled above that, when pure essence is determined as the sum total of all realities, these realities likewise fall under the nature of determinateness and abstracting reflection, and this sum total reduces itself to empty simplicity. In this way essence is only a product, something made. The external negation which is abstraction merely removes the determinations of Being from what remains as essence; it merely places them, as it were, in another place, and leaves them as being, before as after.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"101.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0007","text":"But essence in this way is neither in itself nor for itself; it is through an other, external, abstracting reflection; and it is for an other, namely for abstraction and, in general, for the being that remains standing opposed to it. In its determination it is therefore the dead-in-itself, empty indeterminateness.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"101.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0008","text":"But essence, as it has become here, is what it is not through a negativity foreign to it, but through its own, the infinite movement of Being. It is being-in-and-for-itself; absolute being-in-itself, inasmuch as it is indifferent to all determinateness of Being, other-being and relation to another having been absolutely sublated. But it is not merely this being-in-itself; as mere being-in-itself, it would only be the abstraction of pure essence; rather, it is just as essentially being-for-itself; it itself is this negativity, the self-sublation of other-being and determinateness.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"101.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0009","text":"Essence, as the complete return of Being into itself, is thus at first indeterminate essence; the determinations of Being are sublated in it; it contains them in itself, but not as they are posited in it. Absolute essence, in this simplicity with itself, has no determinate being. But it must pass over into determinate being; for it is being-in-and-for-itself, that is, it distinguishes the determinations which it contains in itself; because it is repulsion of itself from itself, or indifference to itself, negative relation to itself, it thereby posits itself over against itself, and is infinite being-for-itself only in so far as it is unity with itself in this its difference from itself.—This determining is therefore of another nature than determining in the sphere of Being, and the determinations of essence have another character than the determinatenesses of Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"101.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0010","text":"Essence is the absolute unity of being-in-and-for-itself; its determining therefore remains within this unity and is neither becoming nor transition, just as the determinations themselves are not an other as other, nor relations to another; they are self-subsistent, but thereby only as such as are in their unity with one another. —Since essence is at first simple negativity, it now has to posit in its sphere the determinateness which it contains only in itself, in order to give itself determinate being and then its being-for-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"101.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0011","text":"Essence is, on the whole, what quantity was in the sphere of Being: absolute indifference to limit. Quantity, however, is this indifference in immediate determinateness, and limit in it is immediately external determinateness; it passes over into quantum; the external limit is necessary to it, and is being in it. In essence, on the other hand, determinateness is not; it is posited only through essence itself; not free, but only in relation to its unity.—The negativity of essence is reflection, and its determinations are reflected determinations, posited through essence itself and remaining in it as sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"101.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0012","text":"Essence stands between Being and Concept, and constitutes their middle and its movement the transition from Being into Concept. Essence is being-in-and-for-itself, but the same in the determination of being-in-itself; for its universal determination is to come forth from Being, or to be the first negation of Being. Its movement consists in positing in it the negation or determination, thereby giving itself determinate being, and becoming, as infinite being-for-itself, what it is in itself. Thus it gives itself its determinate being, which is equal to its being-in-itself, and becomes Concept. For Concept is the Absolute as it is absolute in its determinate being, or in and for itself. But the determinate being which essence gives itself is not yet determinate being as it is in and for itself, but as essence gives it to itself, or as it is posited, and is therefore still distinct from the determinate being of Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"101.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0013","text":"Essence first shines into itself, or is reflection; secondly, it appears; thirdly, it manifests itself. In its movement it posits itself in the following determinations,","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"101.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0014","text":"I. as simple essence, being-in-itself in its determinations within itself;","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"101.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0015","text":"II. as emerging into determinate being, or according to its existence and appearance;","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"101.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0016","text":"III. as essence which is one with its appearance, as actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"101.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZBDW:P0016"]}],"source_digest":"1184e83b082b87924e944991acdf4b8eb46df1bd3c80423d8c36b13d12705e10","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Zweites Buch Das Wesen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Zweites Buch Das Wesen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW","title":"First Section. Essence as Reflection into Itself.","order":102,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_EADW","text":"Das Wesen kommt aus dem Seyn her; es ist insofern nicht unmittelbar an und für sich, sondern ein Resultat jener Bewegung. Oder das Wesen zunächst als ein unmittelbares genommen, so ist es ein bestimmtes Daseyn, dem ein anderes gegenüber steht; es ist nur wesentliches Daseyn gegen unwesentliches. Das Wesen ist aber das an und für sich aufgehobene Seyn; es ist nur Schein, was ihm gegenüber steht. Allein der Schein ist das eigene Setzen des Wesens.\n\nDas Wesen ist erstens Reflexion. Die Reflexion bestimmt sich; ihre Bestimmungen sind ein Gesetztseyn, das zugleich Reflexion in sich ist; es sind\n\nzweitens diese Reflexions-Bestimmungen oder die Wesenheiten zu betrachten.\n\nDrittens macht sich das Wesen als die Reflexion des Bestimmens in sich selbst, zum Grunde, und geht in die Existenz und Erscheinung über.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0001","text":"Das Wesen kommt aus dem Seyn her; es ist insofern nicht unmittelbar an und für sich, sondern ein Resultat jener Bewegung. Oder das Wesen zunächst als ein unmittelbares genommen, so ist es ein bestimmtes Daseyn, dem ein anderes gegenüber steht; es ist nur wesentliches Daseyn gegen unwesentliches. Das Wesen ist aber das an und für sich aufgehobene Seyn; es ist nur Schein, was ihm gegenüber steht. Allein der Schein ist das eigene Setzen des Wesens.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"102.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0002","text":"Das Wesen ist erstens Reflexion. Die Reflexion bestimmt sich; ihre Bestimmungen sind ein Gesetztseyn, das zugleich Reflexion in sich ist; es sind","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"102.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0003","text":"zweitens diese Reflexions-Bestimmungen oder die Wesenheiten zu betrachten.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"102.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0004","text":"Drittens macht sich das Wesen als die Reflexion des Bestimmens in sich selbst, zum Grunde, und geht in die Existenz und Erscheinung über.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"102.4"}],"sha256":"55c954d758441f28bcd7b2ec3be908a9660a4cd0367f7bb53f77239b895a5a9d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104541469322Z_a23d7599","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Section. Essence as Reflection into Itself.","source_sha256":"55c954d758441f28bcd7b2ec3be908a9660a4cd0367f7bb53f77239b895a5a9d","sha256":"56c663640a957ed210b75916fca98319cac112d576f96e8310a7f327e987bae8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:45:41.469350+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0001","text":"Essence proceeds from being; to that extent it is not immediate in and for itself, but a result of that movement. Or, if essence is initially taken as an immediate, then it is a determinate being to which another stands opposed; it is only essential determinate being as against unessential [determinate being]. But essence is being sublated in and for itself; that which stands opposed to it is only semblance. Yet semblance is essence’s own positing.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"102.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EADW:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0002","text":"Essence is, first, reflection. Reflection determines itself; its determinations are a positedness which is at the same time reflection into itself; they are","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"102.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EADW:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0003","text":"second, these determinations of reflection, or the essentialities, to be considered.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"102.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EADW:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EADW:P0004","text":"Third, essence, as the reflection of determining into itself, makes itself into ground, and passes over into existence and appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"102.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_EADW:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"cfa9774da5c4dd02064f2c8dc0442c059064a8a383d6939e5cff44adf62d5ce3","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Erster Abschnitt. Das Wesen als Reflexion in ihm selbst."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Erster Abschnitt. Das Wesen als Reflexion in ihm selbst.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD","title":"A. The Essential and the Unessential.","order":103,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DWUD","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Der Schein.\n\nDas Wesen aus dem Seyn herkommend scheint demselben gegenüber zu stehen; dieß unmittelbare Seyn ist zunächst das Unwesentliche.\n\nAllein es ist zweitens mehr als nur unwesentliches, es ist wesenloses Seyn, es ist Schein.\n\nDrittens dieser Schein ist nicht ein Äußerliches, dem Wesen Anderes, sondern er ist sein eigner Schein. Das Scheinen des Wesens in ihm selbst ist die Reflexion.\n\n## A. Das Wesentliche und das Unwesentliche.\n\nDas Wesen ist das aufgehobene Seyn. Es ist einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst, aber insofern es die Negation der Sphäre des Seyns überhaupt ist. So hat das Wesen die Unmittelbarkeit sich gegenüber, als eine solche, aus der es geworden ist, und die sich in diesem Aufheben aufbewahrt und erhalten hat. Das Wesen selbst ist in dieser Bestimmung seyendes, unmittelbares Wesen, und das Seyn nur ein Negatives in Beziehung auf das Wesen, nicht an und für sich selbst, das Wesen ist also eine bestimmte Negation. Seyn und Wesen verhalten sich auf diese Weise wieder als Andere überhaupt zu einander, denn jedes hat ein Seyn, eine Unmittelbarkeit, die gegen einander gleichgültig sind, und stehen diesem Seyn nach in gleichem Werthe.\n\nZugleich aber ist das Seyn im Gegensatze gegen das Wesen, das Unwesentliche, es hat gegen dasselbe die Bestimmung des Aufgehobenen. Insofern es sich jedoch zum Wesen nur überhaupt als ein Anderes verhält, so ist das Wesen nicht eigentlich Wesen, sondern nur ein anders bestimmtes Daseyn, das Wesentliche.\n\nDer Unterschied von Wesentlichem und Unwesentlichem hat das Wesen in die Sphäre des Daseyns zurückfallen lassen; indem das Wesen, wie es zunächst ist, als unmittelbares seyendes, und damit nur als Anderes bestimmt ist gegen das Seyn. Die Sphäre des Daseyns ist damit zu Grunde gelegt, und daß das, was das Seyn in diesem Daseyn ist, An-und-Fürsichseyn ist, ist eine weitere dem Daseyn selbst äußerliche Bestimmung; so wie umgekehrt das Wesen wohl das An-und-Fürsichseyn ist, aber nur gegen Anderes, in bestimmter Rücksicht.—Insofern daher an einem Daseyn ein Wesentliches und ein Unwesentliches von einander unterschieden werden, so ist dieser Unterschied ein äußerliches Setzen, eine das Daseyn selbst nicht berührende Absonderung eines Theils desselben, von einem andern Theile; eine Trennung, die in ein Drittes fällt. Es ist dabei unbestimmt, was zum Wesentlichen oder Unwesentlichen gehört. Es ist irgend eine äußerliche Rücksicht und Betrachtung, die ihn macht, und derselbe Inhalt deswegen bald als wesentlich, bald als unwesentlich anzusehen.\n\nGenauer betrachtet, wird das Wesen zu einem nur Wesentlichen gegen ein Unwesentliches dadurch, daß das Wesen nur genommen ist, als aufgehobenes Seyn oder Daseyn. Das Wesen ist auf diese Weise nur die erste oder die Negation, welche Bestimmtheit ist, durch welche das Seyn nur Daseyn, oder das Daseyn nur ein Anderes wird. Das Wesen aber ist die absolute Negativität des Seyns; es ist das Seyn selbst, aber nicht nur als ein Anderes bestimmt, sondern das Seyn, das sich sowohl als unmittelbares Seyn, wie auch als unmittelbare Negation, als Negation, die mit einem Andersseyn behaftet ist, aufgehoben hat. Das Seyn oder Daseyn hat sich somit nicht als Anderes, denn das Wesen ist, erhalten, und das noch vom Wesen unterschiedene Unmittelbare ist nicht bloß ein unwesentliches Daseyn, sondern das an und für sich nichtige Unmittelbare; es ist nur ein Unwesen, der Schein.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0001","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Der Schein.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"103.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0002","text":"Das Wesen aus dem Seyn herkommend scheint demselben gegenüber zu stehen; dieß unmittelbare Seyn ist zunächst das Unwesentliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"103.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0003","text":"Allein es ist zweitens mehr als nur unwesentliches, es ist wesenloses Seyn, es ist Schein.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"103.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0004","text":"Drittens dieser Schein ist nicht ein Äußerliches, dem Wesen Anderes, sondern er ist sein eigner Schein. Das Scheinen des Wesens in ihm selbst ist die Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"103.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0005","text":"## A. Das Wesentliche und das Unwesentliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"103.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0006","text":"Das Wesen ist das aufgehobene Seyn. Es ist einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst, aber insofern es die Negation der Sphäre des Seyns überhaupt ist. So hat das Wesen die Unmittelbarkeit sich gegenüber, als eine solche, aus der es geworden ist, und die sich in diesem Aufheben aufbewahrt und erhalten hat. Das Wesen selbst ist in dieser Bestimmung seyendes, unmittelbares Wesen, und das Seyn nur ein Negatives in Beziehung auf das Wesen, nicht an und für sich selbst, das Wesen ist also eine bestimmte Negation. Seyn und Wesen verhalten sich auf diese Weise wieder als Andere überhaupt zu einander, denn jedes hat ein Seyn, eine Unmittelbarkeit, die gegen einander gleichgültig sind, und stehen diesem Seyn nach in gleichem Werthe.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"103.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0007","text":"Zugleich aber ist das Seyn im Gegensatze gegen das Wesen, das Unwesentliche, es hat gegen dasselbe die Bestimmung des Aufgehobenen. Insofern es sich jedoch zum Wesen nur überhaupt als ein Anderes verhält, so ist das Wesen nicht eigentlich Wesen, sondern nur ein anders bestimmtes Daseyn, das Wesentliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"103.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0008","text":"Der Unterschied von Wesentlichem und Unwesentlichem hat das Wesen in die Sphäre des Daseyns zurückfallen lassen; indem das Wesen, wie es zunächst ist, als unmittelbares seyendes, und damit nur als Anderes bestimmt ist gegen das Seyn. Die Sphäre des Daseyns ist damit zu Grunde gelegt, und daß das, was das Seyn in diesem Daseyn ist, An-und-Fürsichseyn ist, ist eine weitere dem Daseyn selbst äußerliche Bestimmung; so wie umgekehrt das Wesen wohl das An-und-Fürsichseyn ist, aber nur gegen Anderes, in bestimmter Rücksicht.—Insofern daher an einem Daseyn ein Wesentliches und ein Unwesentliches von einander unterschieden werden, so ist dieser Unterschied ein äußerliches Setzen, eine das Daseyn selbst nicht berührende Absonderung eines Theils desselben, von einem andern Theile; eine Trennung, die in ein Drittes fällt. Es ist dabei unbestimmt, was zum Wesentlichen oder Unwesentlichen gehört.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"103.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0009","text":"Es ist irgend eine äußerliche Rücksicht und Betrachtung, die ihn macht, und derselbe Inhalt deswegen bald als wesentlich, bald als unwesentlich anzusehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"103.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0010","text":"Genauer betrachtet, wird das Wesen zu einem nur Wesentlichen gegen ein Unwesentliches dadurch, daß das Wesen nur genommen ist, als aufgehobenes Seyn oder Daseyn. Das Wesen ist auf diese Weise nur die erste oder die Negation, welche Bestimmtheit ist, durch welche das Seyn nur Daseyn, oder das Daseyn nur ein Anderes wird. Das Wesen aber ist die absolute Negativität des Seyns; es ist das Seyn selbst, aber nicht nur als ein Anderes bestimmt, sondern das Seyn, das sich sowohl als unmittelbares Seyn, wie auch als unmittelbare Negation, als Negation, die mit einem Andersseyn behaftet ist, aufgehoben hat. Das Seyn oder Daseyn hat sich somit nicht als Anderes, denn das Wesen ist, erhalten, und das noch vom Wesen unterschiedene Unmittelbare ist nicht bloß ein unwesentliches Daseyn, sondern das an und für sich nichtige Unmittelbare; es ist nur ein Unwesen, der Schein.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"103.10"}],"sha256":"2d04de17403a74742cb74892ad050bf1ea8c487b269290e6a6209ff392b57b0c","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104549372795Z_95ade73f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Essential and the Unessential.","source_sha256":"2d04de17403a74742cb74892ad050bf1ea8c487b269290e6a6209ff392b57b0c","sha256":"518d4da9b4eb928ae3ac19f6cd5df295fe6712b4498daf353fa8b7dee01173b1","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:45:49.372834+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0001","text":"## First Chapter. Appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"103.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0002","text":"Essence, having emerged from Being, seems to stand opposed to it; this immediate Being is initially the unessential.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"103.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0003","text":"But secondly it is more than merely unessential; it is essence-less Being, it is appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"103.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0004","text":"Thirdly, this appearance is not an externality, something other than essence, but is its own appearance. The shining of essence within itself is reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"103.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0005","text":"## A. The Essential and the Unessential.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"103.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0006","text":"Essence is sublated Being. It is simple equality with itself, but insofar as it is the negation of the sphere of Being in general. Thus essence has immediacy confronting it, as an immediacy from which it has become, and which has preserved and maintained itself in this sublation. Essence itself, in this determination, is being, immediate essence, and Being only a negative in relation to essence, not in and for itself; essence is therefore a determinate negation. Being and essence thus once more relate to each other as others in general, for each has a Being, an immediacy, which are indifferent to one another, and according to this Being stand at equal value.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"103.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0007","text":"At the same time, however, Being, in contrast to essence, is the unessential; over against essence it has the determination of what has been sublated. Yet insofar as it relates to essence merely as an other in general, essence is not properly essence, but only an otherwise determined Dasein, the essential.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"103.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0008","text":"The distinction between essential and unessential has caused essence to fall back into the sphere of Dasein; for essence, as it is initially, is determined as immediate being, and hence only as an other over against Being. The sphere of Dasein is thereby laid at the foundation, and that which Being is in this Dasein, Being-in-and-for-itself, is a further determination external to Dasein itself; just as, conversely, essence is indeed Being-in-and-for-itself, but only in opposition to an other, in a determinate respect.—Insofar, therefore, as an essential and an unessential are distinguished from each other in a Dasein, this distinction is an external positing, a separation of one part of it from another part, which does not affect Dasein itself; a separation which falls into a third. It remains indeterminate what belongs to the essential or the unessential.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"103.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0009","text":"It is some external respect and consideration that makes it, and the same content is consequently to be regarded now as essential, now as unessential.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"103.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0010","text":"More closely considered, essence becomes something merely essential over against an unessential by virtue of essence being taken only as sublated Being or Dasein. Essence is in this way only the first, or the negation, which is determinateness, through which Being becomes only Dasein, or Dasein only an other. But essence is the absolute negativity of Being; it is Being itself, but determined not merely as an other, rather Being that has sublated itself both as immediate Being and also as immediate negation, as negation that is encumbered with an otherness. Being or Dasein has thus not preserved itself as an other than essence is, and the immediate still distinguished from essence is not merely an unessential Dasein, but the immediate null in and for itself; it is only a non-essence, appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"103.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DWUD:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"180689b68d1dca1abe86e0570a4307c1b49dc79c42045ceb519883f03a47e601","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Wesentliche und das Unwesentliche."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Wesentliche und das Unwesentliche.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0","title":"B. The Show.","order":104,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDS0","text":"1. Das Seyn ist Schein. Das Seyn des Scheins besteht allein in dem Aufgehobenseyn des Seyns, in seiner Nichtigkeit; diese Nichtigkeit hat es im Wesen, und außer seiner Nichtigkeit, außer dem Wesen ist er nicht. Er ist das Negative gesetzt, als Negatives.\n\nDer Schein ist der ganze Rest, der noch von der Sphäre des Seyns übrig geblieben ist. Er scheint aber selbst noch eine vom Wesen unabhängige unmittelbare Seite zu haben und ein Anderes desselben überhaupt zu seyn. Das Andere enthält überhaupt die zwei Momente des Daseyns und des Nichtdaseyns. Das Unwesentliche, indem es nicht mehr ein Seyn hat, so bleibt ihm vom Andersseyn nur das reine Moment des Nichtdaseyns, der Schein ist dieß unmittelbare Nichtdaseyn, so in der Bestimmtheit des Seyns, daß es nur in der Beziehung auf Anderes, in seinem Nichtdaseyn Daseyn hat; das Unselbstständige, das nur in seiner Negation ist. Es bleibt ihm also nur die reine Bestimmtheit der Unmittelbarkeit, es ist als die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, das ist, welche nur vermittelst ihrer Negation ist, und die ihrer Vermittelung gegenüber nichts ist, als die leere Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit des Nichtdaseyns.\n\nSo ist der Schein, das Phänomen des Skepticismus oder auch die Erscheinung des Idealismus eine solche Unmittelbarkeit, die kein Etwas oder kein Ding ist, überhaupt nicht ein gleichgültiges Seyn, das außer seiner Bestimmtheit und Beziehung auf das Subjekt wäre. Es ist, erlaubte sich der Skepticismus nicht zu sagen; der neuere Idealismus erlaubte sich nicht, die Erkenntnisse, als ein Wissen vom Ding-an-sich anzusehen; jener Schein sollte überhaupt keine Grundlage eines Seyns haben, in diese Erkenntnisse sollte nicht das Ding-an-sich eintreten. Zugleich aber ließ der Skepticismus mannigfaltige Bestimmmungen seines Scheins zu, oder vielmehr sein Schein hatte den ganzen mannigfaltigen Reichthum der Welt zum Inhalte. Ebenso begreift die Erscheinung des Idealismus den ganzen Umfang dieser mannigfaltigen Bestimmtheiten in sich. Jener Schein und diese Erscheinung sind unmittelbar so mannigfaltig bestimmt. Diesem Inhalte mag also wohl kein Seyn, kein Ding, oder Ding-an-sich zu Grunde liegen; er für sich bleibt wie er ist; er ist nur aus dem Seyn in den Schein übersetzt worden; so daß der Schein innerhalb seiner selbst jene mannigfaltigen Bestimmtheiten hat, welche unmittelbare, seyende, andere gegen einander sind. Der Schein ist also selbst ein unmittelbar Bestimmtes. Er kann diesen oder jenen Inhalt haben; aber welchen er hat, ist nicht durch ihn selbst gesetzt, sondern er hat ihn unmittelbar. Der leibnitzische, oder kantische, fichtesche Idealismus, wie andere Formen desselben, sind so wenig als der Skepticismus über das Seyn als Bestimmtheit, über diese Unmittelbarkeit, hinausgekommen. Der Skepticismus läßt sich den Inhalt seines Scheins geben; es ist unmittelbar für ihn, welchen Inhalt er haben soll. Die leibnitzische Monade entwickelt aus ihr selbst ihre Vorstellungen; aber sie ist nicht die erzeugende und verbindende Kraft, sondern sie steigen in ihr als Blasen auf; sie sind gleichgültig, unmittelbar gegen einander, und so gegen die Monade selbst. Ebenso ist die kantische Erscheinung ein gegebener Inhalt der Wahrnehmung, er setzt Affektionen voraus, Bestimmungen des Subjekts, welche gegen sich selbst und gegen dasselbe unmittelbar sind. Der unendliche Anstoß des fichteschen Idealismus mag wohl kein Ding-an-sich zu Grunde liegen haben, so daß er rein eine Bestimmtheit im Ich wird. Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist eine dem Ich, das sie zu der seinigen macht und ihre Äußerlichkeit aufhebt, zugleich unmittelbare, eine Schranke desselben, über die es hinausgehen kann, welche aber eine Seite der Gleichgültigkeit an ihr hat, nach der sie ob zwar im Ich, ein unmittelbares Nichtseyn desselben enthält.-2. Der Schein also enthält eine unmittelbare Voraussetzung, eine unabhängige Seite gegen das Wesen. Es ist aber von ihm, insofern er vom Wesen unterschieden ist, nicht zu zeigen, daß er sich aufhebt und in dasselbe zurückgeht; denn das Seyn ist in seiner Totalität in das Wesen zurückgegangen; der Schein ist das an sich nichtige; es ist nur zu zeigen, daß die Bestimmungen, die ihn vom Wesen unterscheiden, Bestimmungen des Wesens selbst sind, und ferner, daß diese Bestimmtheit des Wesens, welche der Schein ist, im Wesen selbst aufgehoben ist.\n\nEs ist die Unmittelbarkeit des Nichtseyns, welche den Schein ausmacht; dieß Nichtseyn aber ist nichts Anderes als die Negativität des Wesens an ihm selbst. Das Seyn ist Nichtseyn in dem Wesen. Seine Nichtigkeit an sich ist die negative Natur des Wesens selbst. Die Unmittelbarkeit oder Gleichgültigkeit aber, welche dieß Nichtseyn enthält, ist das eigene absolute Ansichseyn des Wesens. Die Negativität des Wesens ist seine Gleichheit mit sich selbst, oder seine einfache Unmittelbarkeit und Gleichgültigkeit. Das Seyn hat sich im Wesen erhalten, insofern dieses an seiner unendlichen Negativität diese Gleichheit mit sich selbst hat; hierdurch ist das Wesen selbst das Seyn. Die Unmittelbarkeit, welche die Bestimmtheit am Scheine gegen das Wesen hat, ist daher nichts anderes, als die eigene Unmittelbarkeit des Wesens; aber nicht die seyende Unmittelbarkeit, sondern die schlechthin vermittelte oder reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, welche der Schein ist;—das Seyn nicht als Seyn, sondern nur als die Bestimmtheit des Seyns, gegen die Vermittlung; das Seyn als Moment.\n\nDiese beiden Momente, die Nichtigkeit aber als Bestehen, und das Seyn aber als Moment, oder die an sich seyende Negativität und die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, welche die Momente des Scheins ausmachen, sind somit die Momente des Wesens selbst; es ist nicht ein Schein des Seyns am Wesen, oder ein Schein des Wesens am Seyn vorhanden, der Schein im Wesen ist nicht der Schein eines Andern; sondern er ist der Schein an sich, der Schein des Wesens selbst.\n\nDer Schein ist das Wesen selbst in der Bestimmtheit des Seyns. Das, wodurch das Wesen einen Schein hat, ist, daß es bestimmt in sich, und dadurch von seiner absoluten Einheit unterschieden ist. Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist ebenso schlechthin an ihr selbst aufgehoben. Denn das Wesen ist das Selbstständige, das ist als durch seine Negation, welche es selbst ist, sich mit sich vermittelnd; es ist also die identische Einheit der absoluten Negativität und der Unmittelbarkeit. —Die Negativität ist die Negativität an sich; sie ist ihre Beziehung auf sich, so ist sie an sich Unmittelbarkeit; aber sie ist negative Beziehung auf sich, abstoßendes Negiren ihrer selbst, so ist die an sich seyende Unmittelbarkeit das Negative oder Bestimmte gegen sie. Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist selbst die absolute Negativität und dieß Bestimmen, das unmittelbar als Bestimmen das Aufheben seiner selbst, Rückkehr in sich ist.\n\nDer Schein ist das Negative, das ein Seyn hat aber in einem Andern, in seiner Negation; er ist die Unselbstständigkeit, die an ihr selbst aufgehoben und nichtig ist. So ist er das in sich zurückgehende Negative, das Unselbstständige, als das an ihm selbst Unselbstständige. Diese Beziehung des Negativen oder der Unselbstständigkeit auf sich, ist seine Unmittelbarkeit; sie ist ein Anderes als es selbst; sie ist seine Bestimmtheit gegen sich, oder sie ist die Negation gegen das Negative. Aber die Negation gegen das Negative ist die sich nur auf sich beziehende Negativität, das absolute Aufheben der Bestimmtheit selbst.\n\nDie Bestimmtheit also, welche der Schein im Wesen ist, ist unendliche Bestimmtheit; sie ist nur das mit sich zusammengehende Negative; sie ist so die Bestimmtheit, die als solche die Selbstständigkeit, und nicht bestimmt ist.—Umgekehrt die Selbstständigkeit als sich auf sich beziehende Unmittelbarkeit ist ebenso schlechthin Bestimmtheit und Moment und nur als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität.—Diese Negativität, die identisch mit der Unmittelbarkeit, und so die Unmittelbarkeit, die identisch mit der Negativität ist, ist das Wesen. Der Schein ist also das Wesen selbst, aber das Wesen in einer Bestimmtheit, aber so daß sie nur sein Moment ist, und das Wesen ist das Scheinen seiner in sich selbst.\n\nIn der Sphäre des Seyns entsteht dem Seyn als unmittelbarem, das Nichtseyn gleichfalls als unmittelbares gegenüber, und ihre Wahrheit ist das Werden. In der Sphäre des Wesens findet sich zuerst das Wesen und das Unwesentliche, dann das Wesen und der Schein gegenüber; das Unwesentliche und der Schein als Reste des Seyns. Aber sie beide, so wie der Unterschied des Wesens von ihnen, bestehen in weiter nichts, als darin, daß das Wesen zuerst, als ein unmittelbares genommen wird, nicht wie es an sich ist, nämlich nicht als die Unmittelbarkeit, die als die reine Vermittelung oder als absolute Negativität Unmittelbarkeit ist. Jene erste Unmittelbarkeit, ist somit nur die Bestimmtheit der Unmittelbarkeit. Das Aufheben dieser Bestimmtheit des Wesens besteht daher in nichts weiter, als in dem Aufzeigen, daß das Unwesentliche nur Schein, und daß das Wesen vielmehr den Schein in sich selbst enthält, als die unendliche Bewegung in sich, welche seine Unmittelbarkeit, als die Negativität und seine Negativität als die Unmittelbarkeit bestimmt und so das Scheinen seiner in sich selbst ist. Das Wesen in dieser seiner Selbstbewegung ist die Reflexion.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0001","text":"1. Das Seyn ist Schein. Das Seyn des Scheins besteht allein in dem Aufgehobenseyn des Seyns, in seiner Nichtigkeit; diese Nichtigkeit hat es im Wesen, und außer seiner Nichtigkeit, außer dem Wesen ist er nicht. Er ist das Negative gesetzt, als Negatives.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"104.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0002","text":"Der Schein ist der ganze Rest, der noch von der Sphäre des Seyns übrig geblieben ist. Er scheint aber selbst noch eine vom Wesen unabhängige unmittelbare Seite zu haben und ein Anderes desselben überhaupt zu seyn. Das Andere enthält überhaupt die zwei Momente des Daseyns und des Nichtdaseyns. Das Unwesentliche, indem es nicht mehr ein Seyn hat, so bleibt ihm vom Andersseyn nur das reine Moment des Nichtdaseyns, der Schein ist dieß unmittelbare Nichtdaseyn, so in der Bestimmtheit des Seyns, daß es nur in der Beziehung auf Anderes, in seinem Nichtdaseyn Daseyn hat; das Unselbstständige, das nur in seiner Negation ist. Es bleibt ihm also nur die reine Bestimmtheit der Unmittelbarkeit, es ist als die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, das ist, welche nur vermittelst ihrer Negation ist, und die ihrer Vermittelung gegenüber nichts ist, als die leere Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit des Nichtdaseyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"104.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0003","text":"So ist der Schein, das Phänomen des Skepticismus oder auch die Erscheinung des Idealismus eine solche Unmittelbarkeit, die kein Etwas oder kein Ding ist, überhaupt nicht ein gleichgültiges Seyn, das außer seiner Bestimmtheit und Beziehung auf das Subjekt wäre. Es ist, erlaubte sich der Skepticismus nicht zu sagen; der neuere Idealismus erlaubte sich nicht, die Erkenntnisse, als ein Wissen vom Ding-an-sich anzusehen; jener Schein sollte überhaupt keine Grundlage eines Seyns haben, in diese Erkenntnisse sollte nicht das Ding-an-sich eintreten. Zugleich aber ließ der Skepticismus mannigfaltige Bestimmmungen seines Scheins zu, oder vielmehr sein Schein hatte den ganzen mannigfaltigen Reichthum der Welt zum Inhalte. Ebenso begreift die Erscheinung des Idealismus den ganzen Umfang dieser mannigfaltigen Bestimmtheiten in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"104.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0004","text":"Jener Schein und diese Erscheinung sind unmittelbar so mannigfaltig bestimmt. Diesem Inhalte mag also wohl kein Seyn, kein Ding, oder Ding-an-sich zu Grunde liegen; er für sich bleibt wie er ist; er ist nur aus dem Seyn in den Schein übersetzt worden; so daß der Schein innerhalb seiner selbst jene mannigfaltigen Bestimmtheiten hat, welche unmittelbare, seyende, andere gegen einander sind. Der Schein ist also selbst ein unmittelbar Bestimmtes. Er kann diesen oder jenen Inhalt haben; aber welchen er hat, ist nicht durch ihn selbst gesetzt, sondern er hat ihn unmittelbar. Der leibnitzische, oder kantische, fichtesche Idealismus, wie andere Formen desselben, sind so wenig als der Skepticismus über das Seyn als Bestimmtheit, über diese Unmittelbarkeit, hinausgekommen. Der Skepticismus läßt sich den Inhalt seines Scheins geben; es ist unmittelbar für ihn, welchen Inhalt er haben soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"104.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0005","text":"Die leibnitzische Monade entwickelt aus ihr selbst ihre Vorstellungen; aber sie ist nicht die erzeugende und verbindende Kraft, sondern sie steigen in ihr als Blasen auf; sie sind gleichgültig, unmittelbar gegen einander, und so gegen die Monade selbst. Ebenso ist die kantische Erscheinung ein gegebener Inhalt der Wahrnehmung, er setzt Affektionen voraus, Bestimmungen des Subjekts, welche gegen sich selbst und gegen dasselbe unmittelbar sind. Der unendliche Anstoß des fichteschen Idealismus mag wohl kein Ding-an-sich zu Grunde liegen haben, so daß er rein eine Bestimmtheit im Ich wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"104.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0006","text":"Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist eine dem Ich, das sie zu der seinigen macht und ihre Äußerlichkeit aufhebt, zugleich unmittelbare, eine Schranke desselben, über die es hinausgehen kann, welche aber eine Seite der Gleichgültigkeit an ihr hat, nach der sie ob zwar im Ich, ein unmittelbares Nichtseyn desselben enthält.-2. Der Schein also enthält eine unmittelbare Voraussetzung, eine unabhängige Seite gegen das Wesen. Es ist aber von ihm, insofern er vom Wesen unterschieden ist, nicht zu zeigen, daß er sich aufhebt und in dasselbe zurückgeht; denn das Seyn ist in seiner Totalität in das Wesen zurückgegangen; der Schein ist das an sich nichtige; es ist nur zu zeigen, daß die Bestimmungen, die ihn vom Wesen unterscheiden, Bestimmungen des Wesens selbst sind, und ferner, daß diese Bestimmtheit des Wesens, welche der Schein ist, im Wesen selbst aufgehoben ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"104.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0007","text":"Es ist die Unmittelbarkeit des Nichtseyns, welche den Schein ausmacht; dieß Nichtseyn aber ist nichts Anderes als die Negativität des Wesens an ihm selbst. Das Seyn ist Nichtseyn in dem Wesen. Seine Nichtigkeit an sich ist die negative Natur des Wesens selbst. Die Unmittelbarkeit oder Gleichgültigkeit aber, welche dieß Nichtseyn enthält, ist das eigene absolute Ansichseyn des Wesens. Die Negativität des Wesens ist seine Gleichheit mit sich selbst, oder seine einfache Unmittelbarkeit und Gleichgültigkeit. Das Seyn hat sich im Wesen erhalten, insofern dieses an seiner unendlichen Negativität diese Gleichheit mit sich selbst hat; hierdurch ist das Wesen selbst das Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"104.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0008","text":"Die Unmittelbarkeit, welche die Bestimmtheit am Scheine gegen das Wesen hat, ist daher nichts anderes, als die eigene Unmittelbarkeit des Wesens; aber nicht die seyende Unmittelbarkeit, sondern die schlechthin vermittelte oder reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, welche der Schein ist;—das Seyn nicht als Seyn, sondern nur als die Bestimmtheit des Seyns, gegen die Vermittlung; das Seyn als Moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"104.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0009","text":"Diese beiden Momente, die Nichtigkeit aber als Bestehen, und das Seyn aber als Moment, oder die an sich seyende Negativität und die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, welche die Momente des Scheins ausmachen, sind somit die Momente des Wesens selbst; es ist nicht ein Schein des Seyns am Wesen, oder ein Schein des Wesens am Seyn vorhanden, der Schein im Wesen ist nicht der Schein eines Andern; sondern er ist der Schein an sich, der Schein des Wesens selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"104.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0010","text":"Der Schein ist das Wesen selbst in der Bestimmtheit des Seyns. Das, wodurch das Wesen einen Schein hat, ist, daß es bestimmt in sich, und dadurch von seiner absoluten Einheit unterschieden ist. Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist ebenso schlechthin an ihr selbst aufgehoben. Denn das Wesen ist das Selbstständige, das ist als durch seine Negation, welche es selbst ist, sich mit sich vermittelnd; es ist also die identische Einheit der absoluten Negativität und der Unmittelbarkeit. —Die Negativität ist die Negativität an sich; sie ist ihre Beziehung auf sich, so ist sie an sich Unmittelbarkeit; aber sie ist negative Beziehung auf sich, abstoßendes Negiren ihrer selbst, so ist die an sich seyende Unmittelbarkeit das Negative oder Bestimmte gegen sie.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"104.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0011","text":"Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist selbst die absolute Negativität und dieß Bestimmen, das unmittelbar als Bestimmen das Aufheben seiner selbst, Rückkehr in sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"104.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0012","text":"Der Schein ist das Negative, das ein Seyn hat aber in einem Andern, in seiner Negation; er ist die Unselbstständigkeit, die an ihr selbst aufgehoben und nichtig ist. So ist er das in sich zurückgehende Negative, das Unselbstständige, als das an ihm selbst Unselbstständige. Diese Beziehung des Negativen oder der Unselbstständigkeit auf sich, ist seine Unmittelbarkeit; sie ist ein Anderes als es selbst; sie ist seine Bestimmtheit gegen sich, oder sie ist die Negation gegen das Negative. Aber die Negation gegen das Negative ist die sich nur auf sich beziehende Negativität, das absolute Aufheben der Bestimmtheit selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"104.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0013","text":"Die Bestimmtheit also, welche der Schein im Wesen ist, ist unendliche Bestimmtheit; sie ist nur das mit sich zusammengehende Negative; sie ist so die Bestimmtheit, die als solche die Selbstständigkeit, und nicht bestimmt ist.—Umgekehrt die Selbstständigkeit als sich auf sich beziehende Unmittelbarkeit ist ebenso schlechthin Bestimmtheit und Moment und nur als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität.—Diese Negativität, die identisch mit der Unmittelbarkeit, und so die Unmittelbarkeit, die identisch mit der Negativität ist, ist das Wesen. Der Schein ist also das Wesen selbst, aber das Wesen in einer Bestimmtheit, aber so daß sie nur sein Moment ist, und das Wesen ist das Scheinen seiner in sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"104.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0014","text":"In der Sphäre des Seyns entsteht dem Seyn als unmittelbarem, das Nichtseyn gleichfalls als unmittelbares gegenüber, und ihre Wahrheit ist das Werden. In der Sphäre des Wesens findet sich zuerst das Wesen und das Unwesentliche, dann das Wesen und der Schein gegenüber; das Unwesentliche und der Schein als Reste des Seyns. Aber sie beide, so wie der Unterschied des Wesens von ihnen, bestehen in weiter nichts, als darin, daß das Wesen zuerst, als ein unmittelbares genommen wird, nicht wie es an sich ist, nämlich nicht als die Unmittelbarkeit, die als die reine Vermittelung oder als absolute Negativität Unmittelbarkeit ist. Jene erste Unmittelbarkeit, ist somit nur die Bestimmtheit der Unmittelbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"104.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDS0:P0015","text":"Das Aufheben dieser Bestimmtheit des Wesens besteht daher in nichts weiter, als in dem Aufzeigen, daß das Unwesentliche nur Schein, und daß das Wesen vielmehr den Schein in sich selbst enthält, als die unendliche Bewegung in sich, welche seine Unmittelbarkeit, als die Negativität und seine Negativität als die Unmittelbarkeit bestimmt und so das Scheinen seiner in sich selbst ist. Das Wesen in dieser seiner Selbstbewegung ist die Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"104.15"}],"sha256":"e1b9a2d9ba7c5d4248fd416ef75346be9811dfac840c178e9196349e646d4694","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Der Schein.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0","title":"C. Reflection.","order":105,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDR0","text":"Der Schein ist dasselbe, was die Reflexion ist; aber er ist die Reflexion als unmittelbare; für den in sich gegangenen, hiermit seiner Unmittelbarkeit entfremdeten Schein, haben wir das Wort der fremden Sprache, die Reflexion.\n\nDas Wesen ist Reflexion; die Bewegung des Werdens und Übergehens, das in sich selbst bleibt; worin das unterschiedene schlechthin nur als das an sich negative, als Schein bestimmt ist.—In dem Werden des Seyns liegt der Bestimmtheit das Seyn zu Grunde, und sie ist Beziehung auf Anderes. Die reflectirende Bewegung hingegen ist das Andere als die Negation an sich, die nur als sich auf sich beziehende Negation ein Seyn hat. Oder indem diese Beziehung auf sich eben dieß Negiren der Negation ist, so ist die Negation als Negation vorhanden, als ein solches, das sein Seyn in seinem Negirtseyn hat, als Schein. Das Andere ist hier also nicht das Seyn mit der Negation oder Grenze, sondern die Negation mit der Negation. Das Erste aber gegen dieß Andere, das Unmittelbare oder Seyn, ist nur diese Gleichheit selbst der Negation mit sich, die negirte Negation, die absolute Negativität. Diese Gleichheit mit sich oder Unmittelbarkeit ist daher nicht ein Erstes, von dem angefangen wird, und das in seine Negation überginge; noch ist es ein seyendes Substrat, das sich durch die Reflexion hindurch bewegte; sondern die Unmittelbarkeit ist nur diese Bewegung selbst.\n\nDas Werden im Wesen, seine reflektirende Bewegung, ist daher die Bewegung von Nichts zu Nichts, und dadurch zu sich selbst zurück. Das Übergehen oder Werden hebt in seinem Übergehen sich auf; das Andere, das in diesem Übergehen wird, ist nicht das Nichtseyn eines Seyns, sondern das Nichts eines Nichts, und dieß, die Negation eines Nichts zu seyn, macht das Seyn aus.—Das Seyn ist nur als die Bewegung des Nichts zu Nichts, so ist es das Wesen; und dieses hat nicht diese Bewegung in sich, sondern ist sie als der absolute Schein selbst, die reine Negativität, die nichts außer ihr hat, das sie negirte, sondern die nur ihr Negatives selbst negirt, das nur in diesem Negiren ist.\n\nDiese reine absolute Reflexion, welche die Bewegung von Nichts zu Nichts ist, bestimmt sich selbst weiter.\n\nSie ist erstlich setzende Reflexion; sie macht zweitens den Anfang von dem vorausgesetzten Unmittelbaren, und ist so äußerliche Reflexion.\n\nDrittens aber hebt sie diese Voraussetzung auf, und indem sie in dem Aufheben der Voraussetzung zugleich voraussetzend ist, ist sie bestimmende Reflexion.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0001","text":"Der Schein ist dasselbe, was die Reflexion ist; aber er ist die Reflexion als unmittelbare; für den in sich gegangenen, hiermit seiner Unmittelbarkeit entfremdeten Schein, haben wir das Wort der fremden Sprache, die Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"105.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0002","text":"Das Wesen ist Reflexion; die Bewegung des Werdens und Übergehens, das in sich selbst bleibt; worin das unterschiedene schlechthin nur als das an sich negative, als Schein bestimmt ist.—In dem Werden des Seyns liegt der Bestimmtheit das Seyn zu Grunde, und sie ist Beziehung auf Anderes. Die reflectirende Bewegung hingegen ist das Andere als die Negation an sich, die nur als sich auf sich beziehende Negation ein Seyn hat. Oder indem diese Beziehung auf sich eben dieß Negiren der Negation ist, so ist die Negation als Negation vorhanden, als ein solches, das sein Seyn in seinem Negirtseyn hat, als Schein. Das Andere ist hier also nicht das Seyn mit der Negation oder Grenze, sondern die Negation mit der Negation. Das Erste aber gegen dieß Andere, das Unmittelbare oder Seyn, ist nur diese Gleichheit selbst der Negation mit sich, die negirte Negation, die absolute Negativität.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"105.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0003","text":"Diese Gleichheit mit sich oder Unmittelbarkeit ist daher nicht ein Erstes, von dem angefangen wird, und das in seine Negation überginge; noch ist es ein seyendes Substrat, das sich durch die Reflexion hindurch bewegte; sondern die Unmittelbarkeit ist nur diese Bewegung selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"105.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0004","text":"Das Werden im Wesen, seine reflektirende Bewegung, ist daher die Bewegung von Nichts zu Nichts, und dadurch zu sich selbst zurück. Das Übergehen oder Werden hebt in seinem Übergehen sich auf; das Andere, das in diesem Übergehen wird, ist nicht das Nichtseyn eines Seyns, sondern das Nichts eines Nichts, und dieß, die Negation eines Nichts zu seyn, macht das Seyn aus.—Das Seyn ist nur als die Bewegung des Nichts zu Nichts, so ist es das Wesen; und dieses hat nicht diese Bewegung in sich, sondern ist sie als der absolute Schein selbst, die reine Negativität, die nichts außer ihr hat, das sie negirte, sondern die nur ihr Negatives selbst negirt, das nur in diesem Negiren ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"105.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0005","text":"Diese reine absolute Reflexion, welche die Bewegung von Nichts zu Nichts ist, bestimmt sich selbst weiter.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"105.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0006","text":"Sie ist erstlich setzende Reflexion; sie macht zweitens den Anfang von dem vorausgesetzten Unmittelbaren, und ist so äußerliche Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"105.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0007","text":"Drittens aber hebt sie diese Voraussetzung auf, und indem sie in dem Aufheben der Voraussetzung zugleich voraussetzend ist, ist sie bestimmende Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"105.7"}],"sha256":"6fe8479ba63c7fd76aab6d2223e14fadd7645e96e361bbd9c6615590624dc663","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104607470459Z_5b22f3d4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Reflection.","source_sha256":"6fe8479ba63c7fd76aab6d2223e14fadd7645e96e361bbd9c6615590624dc663","sha256":"18dbf6da8657b50876404d4f282fe21c8d2f62db82d2c53022533a0aac6f44e5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:46:07.470487+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0001","text":"Appearance is the same as reflection; but it is reflection as immediate; for appearance that has withdrawn into itself, and thereby become alienated from its immediacy, we have the word of the foreign language, reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"105.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0002","text":"Essence is reflection; the movement of becoming and passing-over that remains within itself; in which what is differentiated is determined absolutely only as what is negative in itself, as appearance.—In the becoming of being, being underlies determinacy, and determinacy is relation to an other. The reflecting movement, on the other hand, is the other as negation in itself, which has a being only as self-relating negation. Or, since this relation to self is precisely this negating of negation, negation is present as negation, as something that has its being in its being-negated, as appearance. Thus, the other here is not being with negation or limit, but negation with negation. But the first as against this other, the immediate or being, is only this equality of negation with itself, negated negation, absolute negativity.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"105.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0003","text":"This equality with itself, or immediacy, is therefore not a first from which a beginning is made and which would pass over into its negation; nor is it a being substrate which moved through reflection; rather, immediacy is only this movement itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"105.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0004","text":"Becoming in essence, its reflecting movement, is therefore the movement from nothing to nothing, and thereby back to itself. Passing-over or becoming sublates itself in its passing-over; the other which becomes in this passing-over is not the non-being of a being, but the nothing of a nothing, and this, being the negation of a nothing, constitutes being.—Being is only as the movement from nothing to nothing; thus it is essence; and this does not have this movement within it, but is it as absolute appearance itself, pure negativity, which has nothing outside itself that would negate it, but only negates its negative itself, which is only in this negating.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"105.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0005","text":"This pure absolute reflection, which is the movement from nothing to nothing, further determines itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"105.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0006","text":"It is, first, positing reflection; second, it makes a beginning from the presupposed immediate, and is thus external reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"105.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0007","text":"Third, however, it sublates this presupposition, and in that it is at the same time presupposing in the sublation of the presupposition, it is determining reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"105.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDR0:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"22d31d4a74f8d2fd2f9c55a1bdd73fc5b74a6979820ae65469e577ae953657e9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Die Reflexion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Die Reflexion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR","title":"1. Positing Reflection.","order":106,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_1DSR","text":"Der Schein ist das Nichtige oder Wesenlose; aber das Nichtige oder Wesenlose hat sein Seyn nicht in einem Andern, in dem es scheint, sondern sein Seyn ist seine eigne Gleichheit mit sich; dieser Wechsel des Negativen mit sich selbst hat sich als die absolute Reflexion des Wesens bestimmt.\n\nDiese sich auf sich beziehende Negativität ist also das Negiren ihrer selbst. Sie ist somit überhaupt so sehr aufgehobene Negativität als sie Negativität ist. Oder sie ist selbst das Negative und die einfache Gleichheit mit sich oder Unmittelbarkeit. Sie besteht also darin sie selbst und nicht sie selbst und zwar in Einer Einheit zu seyn.-Zunächst ist die Reflexion die Bewegung des Nichts zu Nichts, somit die mit sich selbst zusammengehende Negation. Dieses Zusammengehen mit sich ist überhaupt einfache Gleichheit mit sich; die Unmittelbarkeit. Aber dieß Zusammenfallen ist nicht Übergehen der Negation in die Gleichheit mit sich als in ihr Andersseyn, sondern die Reflexion ist Übergehen als Aufheben des Übergehens; denn sie ist unmittelbares Zusammenfallen des Negativen mit sich selbst; so ist dieß Zusammengehen erstlich Gleichheit mit sich, oder Unmittelbarkeit; aber zweitens ist diese Unmittelbarkeit die Gleichheit des Negativen mit sich, somit die sich selbst negirende Gleichheit; die Unmittelbarkeit, die an sich das Negative, das Negative ihrer selbst ist, dieß zu seyn was sie nicht ist.\n\nDie Beziehung des Negativen auf sich selbst ist also seine Rückkehr in sich; sie ist Unmittelbarkeit, als das Aufheben des Negativen; aber Unmittelbarkeit schlechthin nur als diese Beziehung oder als Rückkehr aus einem, somit sich selbst aufhebende Unmittelbarkeit. —Dieß ist das Gesetztseyn; die Unmittelbarkeit rein nur als Bestimmtheit oder als sich reflectirend. Diese Unmittelbarkeit, die nur als Rückkehr des Negativen in sich ist,—ist jene Unmittelbarkeit, welche die Bestimmtheit des Scheins ausmacht, und von der vorhin die reflectirende Bewegung anzufangen schien. Statt von dieser Unmittelbarkeit anfangen zu können, ist diese vielmehr erst als die Rückkehr, oder als die Reflexion selbst. Die Reflexion ist also die Bewegung, die, indem sie die Rückkehr ist, erst darin das ist, das anfängt oder das zurückkehrt.\n\nSie ist Setzen, insofern sie die Unmittelbarkeit als ein Rückkehren ist; es ist nämlich nicht ein Anderes vorhanden, weder ein solches, aus dem sie, noch in das sie zurückkehrte; sie ist also nur als Rückkehren oder als das Negative ihrer selbst. Aber ferner ist diese Unmittelbarkeit die aufgehobene Negation und die aufgehobene Rückkehr in sich. Die Reflexion ist als Aufheben des Negativen, Aufheben ihres Anderen, der Unmittelbarkeit. Indem sie also die Unmittelbarkeit als ein Rückkehren, Zusammengehen des Negativen mit sich selbst ist, so ist sie ebenso Negation des Negativen als des Negativen. So ist sie Voraussetzen.—Oder die Unmittelbarkeit ist als Rückkehren nur das Negative ihrer selbst, nur dieß, nicht Unmittelbarkeit zu seyn; aber die Reflexion ist das Aufheben des Negativen seiner selbst, sie ist Zusammengehen mit sich; sie hebt also ihr Setzen auf, und indem sie das Aufheben des Setzens in ihrem Setzen ist, ist sie Voraussetzen.—In dem Voraussetzen bestimmt die Reflexion die Rückkehr in sich, als das Negative ihrer selbst, als dasjenige, dessen Aufheben das Wesen ist. Es ist sein Verhalten zu sich selbst; aber zu sich als dem Negativen seiner; nur so ist es die insichbleibende, sich auf sich beziehende Negativität. Die Unmittelbarkeit kommt überhaupt nur als Rückkehr hervor und ist dasjenige Negative, welches der Schein des Anfangs ist, der durch die Rückkehr negirt wird. Die Rückkehr des Wesens ist somit sein sich Abstoßen von sich selbst. Oder die Reflexion in sich ist wesentlich das Voraussetzen dessen, aus dem sie die Rückkehr ist.\n\nEs ist das Aufheben seiner Gleichheit mit sich, wodurch das Wesen erst die Gleichheit mit sich ist. Es setzt sich selbst voraus, und das Aufheben dieser Voraussetzung ist es selbst; umgekehrt ist dieß Aufheben seiner Voraussetzung die Voraussetzung selbst.—Die Reflexion also findet ein Unmittelbares vor, über das sie hinausgeht, und aus dem sie die Rückkehr ist. Aber diese Rückkehr ist erst das Voraussetzen des Vorgefundenen. Dieß Vorgefundene wird nur darin, daß es verlassen wird; seine Unmittelbarkeit ist die aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit.—Die aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit umgekehrt ist die Rückkehr in sich, das Ankommen des Wesens bei sich, das einfache sich selbst gleiche Seyn. Damit ist dieses Ankommen bei sich das Aufheben seiner und die von sich selbst abstoßende, voraussetzende Reflexion, und ihr Abstoßen von sich ist das Ankommen bei sich selbst.\n\nDie reflektirende Bewegung ist somit, nach dem Betrachteten, als absoluter Gegenstoß in sich selbst zu nehmen. Denn die Voraussetzung der Rückkehr in sich,—das woraus das Wesen herkommt und erst als dieses Zurückkommen ist—, ist nur in der Rückkehr selbst. Das Hinausgehen über das Unmittelbare, von dem die Reflexion anfängt, ist vielmehr erst durch dieß Hinausgehen; und das Hinausgehen über das Unmittelbare ist das Ankommen bei demselben. Die Bewegung wendet sich als Fortgehen unmittelbar in ihr selbst um, und ist nur so Selbstbewegung,—Bewegung, die aus sich kommt, insofern die setzende Reflexion voraussetzende, aber als voraussetzende Reflexion schlechthin setzende ist.\n\nSo ist die Reflexion sie selbst, und ihr Nichtseyn; und ist nur sie selbst, indem sie das Negative ihrer ist, denn nur so ist das Aufheben des Negativen zugleich als ein Zusammengehen mit sich.\n\nDie Unmittelbarkeit, die sie als Aufheben sich voraussetzt, ist schlechthin nur als Gesetztseyn, als an sich aufgehobenes, das nicht verschieden ist, von der Rückkehr in sich, und selbst nur dieses Rückkehren ist. Aber es ist zugleich bestimmt als Negatives, als unmittelbar gegen eines, also gegen ein Anderes. So ist die Reflexion bestimmt; sie ist, indem sie nach dieser Bestimmtheit, eine Voraussetzung hat, und von dem Unmittelbaren, als ihrem Andern anfängt, äußere Reflexion.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0001","text":"Der Schein ist das Nichtige oder Wesenlose; aber das Nichtige oder Wesenlose hat sein Seyn nicht in einem Andern, in dem es scheint, sondern sein Seyn ist seine eigne Gleichheit mit sich; dieser Wechsel des Negativen mit sich selbst hat sich als die absolute Reflexion des Wesens bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"106.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0002","text":"Diese sich auf sich beziehende Negativität ist also das Negiren ihrer selbst. Sie ist somit überhaupt so sehr aufgehobene Negativität als sie Negativität ist. Oder sie ist selbst das Negative und die einfache Gleichheit mit sich oder Unmittelbarkeit. Sie besteht also darin sie selbst und nicht sie selbst und zwar in Einer Einheit zu seyn.-Zunächst ist die Reflexion die Bewegung des Nichts zu Nichts, somit die mit sich selbst zusammengehende Negation. Dieses Zusammengehen mit sich ist überhaupt einfache Gleichheit mit sich; die Unmittelbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"106.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0003","text":"Aber dieß Zusammenfallen ist nicht Übergehen der Negation in die Gleichheit mit sich als in ihr Andersseyn, sondern die Reflexion ist Übergehen als Aufheben des Übergehens; denn sie ist unmittelbares Zusammenfallen des Negativen mit sich selbst; so ist dieß Zusammengehen erstlich Gleichheit mit sich, oder Unmittelbarkeit; aber zweitens ist diese Unmittelbarkeit die Gleichheit des Negativen mit sich, somit die sich selbst negirende Gleichheit; die Unmittelbarkeit, die an sich das Negative, das Negative ihrer selbst ist, dieß zu seyn was sie nicht ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"106.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0004","text":"Die Beziehung des Negativen auf sich selbst ist also seine Rückkehr in sich; sie ist Unmittelbarkeit, als das Aufheben des Negativen; aber Unmittelbarkeit schlechthin nur als diese Beziehung oder als Rückkehr aus einem, somit sich selbst aufhebende Unmittelbarkeit. —Dieß ist das Gesetztseyn; die Unmittelbarkeit rein nur als Bestimmtheit oder als sich reflectirend. Diese Unmittelbarkeit, die nur als Rückkehr des Negativen in sich ist,—ist jene Unmittelbarkeit, welche die Bestimmtheit des Scheins ausmacht, und von der vorhin die reflectirende Bewegung anzufangen schien. Statt von dieser Unmittelbarkeit anfangen zu können, ist diese vielmehr erst als die Rückkehr, oder als die Reflexion selbst. Die Reflexion ist also die Bewegung, die, indem sie die Rückkehr ist, erst darin das ist, das anfängt oder das zurückkehrt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"106.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0005","text":"Sie ist Setzen, insofern sie die Unmittelbarkeit als ein Rückkehren ist; es ist nämlich nicht ein Anderes vorhanden, weder ein solches, aus dem sie, noch in das sie zurückkehrte; sie ist also nur als Rückkehren oder als das Negative ihrer selbst. Aber ferner ist diese Unmittelbarkeit die aufgehobene Negation und die aufgehobene Rückkehr in sich. Die Reflexion ist als Aufheben des Negativen, Aufheben ihres Anderen, der Unmittelbarkeit. Indem sie also die Unmittelbarkeit als ein Rückkehren, Zusammengehen des Negativen mit sich selbst ist, so ist sie ebenso Negation des Negativen als des Negativen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"106.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0006","text":"So ist sie Voraussetzen.—Oder die Unmittelbarkeit ist als Rückkehren nur das Negative ihrer selbst, nur dieß, nicht Unmittelbarkeit zu seyn; aber die Reflexion ist das Aufheben des Negativen seiner selbst, sie ist Zusammengehen mit sich; sie hebt also ihr Setzen auf, und indem sie das Aufheben des Setzens in ihrem Setzen ist, ist sie Voraussetzen.—In dem Voraussetzen bestimmt die Reflexion die Rückkehr in sich, als das Negative ihrer selbst, als dasjenige, dessen Aufheben das Wesen ist. Es ist sein Verhalten zu sich selbst; aber zu sich als dem Negativen seiner; nur so ist es die insichbleibende, sich auf sich beziehende Negativität. Die Unmittelbarkeit kommt überhaupt nur als Rückkehr hervor und ist dasjenige Negative, welches der Schein des Anfangs ist, der durch die Rückkehr negirt wird. Die Rückkehr des Wesens ist somit sein sich Abstoßen von sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"106.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0007","text":"Oder die Reflexion in sich ist wesentlich das Voraussetzen dessen, aus dem sie die Rückkehr ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"106.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0008","text":"Es ist das Aufheben seiner Gleichheit mit sich, wodurch das Wesen erst die Gleichheit mit sich ist. Es setzt sich selbst voraus, und das Aufheben dieser Voraussetzung ist es selbst; umgekehrt ist dieß Aufheben seiner Voraussetzung die Voraussetzung selbst.—Die Reflexion also findet ein Unmittelbares vor, über das sie hinausgeht, und aus dem sie die Rückkehr ist. Aber diese Rückkehr ist erst das Voraussetzen des Vorgefundenen. Dieß Vorgefundene wird nur darin, daß es verlassen wird; seine Unmittelbarkeit ist die aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit.—Die aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit umgekehrt ist die Rückkehr in sich, das Ankommen des Wesens bei sich, das einfache sich selbst gleiche Seyn. Damit ist dieses Ankommen bei sich das Aufheben seiner und die von sich selbst abstoßende, voraussetzende Reflexion, und ihr Abstoßen von sich ist das Ankommen bei sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"106.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0009","text":"Die reflektirende Bewegung ist somit, nach dem Betrachteten, als absoluter Gegenstoß in sich selbst zu nehmen. Denn die Voraussetzung der Rückkehr in sich,—das woraus das Wesen herkommt und erst als dieses Zurückkommen ist—, ist nur in der Rückkehr selbst. Das Hinausgehen über das Unmittelbare, von dem die Reflexion anfängt, ist vielmehr erst durch dieß Hinausgehen; und das Hinausgehen über das Unmittelbare ist das Ankommen bei demselben. Die Bewegung wendet sich als Fortgehen unmittelbar in ihr selbst um, und ist nur so Selbstbewegung,—Bewegung, die aus sich kommt, insofern die setzende Reflexion voraussetzende, aber als voraussetzende Reflexion schlechthin setzende ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"106.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0010","text":"So ist die Reflexion sie selbst, und ihr Nichtseyn; und ist nur sie selbst, indem sie das Negative ihrer ist, denn nur so ist das Aufheben des Negativen zugleich als ein Zusammengehen mit sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"106.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0011","text":"Die Unmittelbarkeit, die sie als Aufheben sich voraussetzt, ist schlechthin nur als Gesetztseyn, als an sich aufgehobenes, das nicht verschieden ist, von der Rückkehr in sich, und selbst nur dieses Rückkehren ist. Aber es ist zugleich bestimmt als Negatives, als unmittelbar gegen eines, also gegen ein Anderes. So ist die Reflexion bestimmt; sie ist, indem sie nach dieser Bestimmtheit, eine Voraussetzung hat, und von dem Unmittelbaren, als ihrem Andern anfängt, äußere Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"106.11"}],"sha256":"5f5eb2b445a4cdec7db7924358ff0e63d8ef748233ecdfeb64280dc900bb8933","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104621130187Z_58ae0176","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"1. Positing Reflection.","source_sha256":"5f5eb2b445a4cdec7db7924358ff0e63d8ef748233ecdfeb64280dc900bb8933","sha256":"8695f5ae47c21c891158a2bcb606c9b9b24bac7b45e522cba2f2254d5490f461","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:46:21.130211+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0001","text":"Semblance is the null or the essenceless; but the null or essenceless does not have its Being in an Other in which it seems, but its Being is its own equality with itself; this alternation of the negative with itself has determined itself as the absolute reflection of essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"106.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0002","text":"This self-relating negativity is therefore the negating of itself. It is thus, in general, as much sublated negativity as it is negativity. Or it is itself the negative and the simple equality with itself, or immediacy. It thus consists in being itself and not itself, and indeed in one unity.—At first, reflection is the movement from nothing to nothing, thus the negation coinciding with itself. This coincidence with itself is, in general, simple equality with itself; immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"106.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0003","text":"But this coincidence is not a transition of negation into equality with itself as into its other-being, but reflection is transition as the sublation of transition; for it is the immediate coincidence of the negative with itself; thus this coincidence is, firstly, equality with itself, or immediacy; but, secondly, this immediacy is the equality of the negative with itself, thus equality negating itself; the immediacy which is in itself the negative, the negative of itself, is this: to be what it is not.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"106.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0004","text":"The relation of the negative to itself is therefore its return into itself; it is immediacy, as the sublation of the negative; but immediacy simply only as this relation, or as return from an [other], thus self-sublating immediacy. —This is positedness; immediacy purely only as determinacy, or as reflecting itself. This immediacy, which is only as the return of the negative into itself,—is that immediacy which constitutes the determinacy of semblance, and from which the reflecting movement previously seemed to begin. Instead of being able to begin from this immediacy, this is rather only as the return, or as reflection itself. Reflection is therefore the movement which, inasmuch as it is the return, is only therein that which begins or that which returns.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"106.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0005","text":"It is positing, insofar as it is the immediacy as a returning; namely, there is no Other present, neither one from which it, nor one into which it would return; it is therefore only as returning, or as the negative of itself. But further, this immediacy is the sublated negation and the sublated return into itself. Reflection is, as the sublation of the negative, the sublation of its Other, of immediacy. Since, therefore, it is the immediacy as a returning, coincidence of the negative with itself, it is equally negation of the negative as of the negative.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"106.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0006","text":"Thus it is presupposing.—Or, immediacy as returning is only the negative of itself, only this: not to be immediacy; but reflection is the sublation of the negative of itself, it is coincidence with itself; it therefore sublates its positing, and inasmuch as it is the sublation of positing in its positing, it is presupposing.—In presupposing, reflection determines the return into itself as the negative of itself, as that whose sublation is essence. It is its comportment toward itself; but toward itself as its negative; only thus is it the negativity remaining within itself, relating itself to itself. Immediacy in general emerges only as return and is that negative which is the semblance of the beginning, which is negated through the return. The return of essence is thus its repulsion of itself from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"106.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0007","text":"Or reflection into itself is essentially the presupposing of that from which it is the return.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"106.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0008","text":"It is the sublation of its equality with itself through which essence first is equality with itself. It presupposes itself, and the sublation of this presupposition is itself; conversely, this sublation of its presupposition is the presupposition itself.—Reflection thus finds an immediate before it, beyond which it goes, and from which it is the return. But this return is first the presupposing of what is found before it. What is found before it comes to be only in that it is abandoned; its immediacy is sublated immediacy.—Sublated immediacy, conversely, is the return into itself, the arrival of essence at itself, simple Being equal to itself. Thereby this arrival at itself is the sublation of itself and the reflection repelling itself from itself, presupposing itself, and its repulsion of itself from itself is its arrival at itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"106.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0009","text":"The reflecting movement is thus, according to what has been considered, to be taken as absolute counter-thrust into itself. For the presupposition of the return into itself,—that from which essence comes and is only as this returning—, is only in the return itself. The going beyond the immediate, from which reflection begins, is rather first through this going beyond; and the going beyond the immediate is the arrival at the same. The movement, as going forward, immediately turns round within itself, and is only thus self-movement,—movement which comes from itself, insofar as positing reflection is presupposing, but, as presupposing reflection, is simply positing.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"106.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0010","text":"Thus reflection is itself, and its non-being; and it is itself only in that it is the negative of itself, for only thus is the sublation of the negative at the same time a coincidence with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"106.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0011","text":"The immediacy which it presupposes as sublating is simply only as positedness, as something sublated in itself, which is not distinct from the return into itself and is itself only this returning. But it is at the same time determined as negative, as immediately opposed to a one, thus to an Other. Thus reflection is determined; inasmuch as, according to this determinacy, it has a presupposition and begins from the immediate as its Other, it is external reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"106.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DSR:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"7ce6b99c4ec6715bbdf169dcd033e1470cf3da211b3cba0f8d704be25aaabb19","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"1. Die setzende Reflexion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"1. Die setzende Reflexion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR","title":"2. External Reflection.","order":107,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_2DUR","text":"Die Reflexion als absolute Reflexion ist das in ihm selbst scheinende Wesen, und setzt sich nur den Schein, das Gesetztseyn, voraus; sie ist als voraussetzende unmittelbar nur setzende Reflexion. Aber die äußerliche oder reale Reflexion setzt sich als aufgehoben, als das Negative ihrer voraus. Sie ist in dieser Bestimmung verdoppelt; das einemal als das Vorausgesetzte, oder die Reflexion in sich, die das Unmittelbare ist. Das andere Mal ist sie die als negativ sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion; sie bezieht sich auf sich als auf jenes ihr Nichtseyn.\n\nDie äußerliche Reflexion setzt also ein Seyn voraus, erstens nicht in dem Sinne, daß seine Unmittelbarkeit nur Gesetztseyn oder Moment ist, sondern vielmehr, daß diese Unmittelbarkeit die Beziehung auf sich, und die Bestimmtheit nur als Moment ist. Sie bezieht sich auf ihre Voraussetzung so, daß diese das Negative der Reflexion ist, aber so daß dieses Negative als Negatives aufgehoben ist.—Die Reflexion in ihrem Setzen, hebt unmittelbar ihr Setzen auf, so hat sie eine unmittelbare Voraussetzung. Sie findet also dasselbe vor, als ein solches von dem sie anfängt, und von dem aus sie erst das Zurückgehen in sich, das Negiren dieses ihres Negativen ist. Aber daß dieß Vorausgesetzte ein Negatives oder Gesetztes ist, geht dasselbe nichts an; diese Bestimmtheit gehört nur der setzenden Reflexion an, aber in dem Voraussetzen ist das Gesetztseyn nur als aufgehobenes. Was die äußerliche Reflexion an dem Unmittelbaren bestimmt und setzt, sind insofern demselben äußerliche Bestimmungen.—Sie war das Unendliche in der Sphäre des Seyns; das Endliche gilt als das Erste, als das Reale, von ihm wird als dem zu Grunde liegenden und zu Grund liegen bleibenden angefangen, und das Unendliche ist die gegenüber stehende Reflexion in sich.\n\nDiese äußere Reflexion ist der Schluß, in welchem die beiden Extreme, das Unmittelbare und die Reflexion in sich, sind; die Mitte desselben ist die Beziehung beider, das bestimmte Unmittelbare, so daß der eine Theil derselben, die Unmittelbarkeit nur dem einen Extreme, die andere, die Bestimmtheit oder Negation, nur dem andern Extreme zukommt.\n\nAber das Thun der äußeren Reflexion näher betrachtet, so ist sie zweitens Setzen des Unmittelbaren, das insofern das Negative oder Bestimmte wird; aber sie ist unmittelbar auch das Aufheben dieses ihres Setzens; denn sie setzt das Unmittelbare voraus; sie ist im Negiren das Negiren dieses ihres Negirens. Sie ist aber unmittelbar damit ebenso Setzen, Aufheben des ihr negativen Unmittelbaren, und dieses, von dem sie als von einem Fremden anzufangen schien, ist erst in diesem ihrem Anfangen. Das Unmittelbare ist auf diese Weise nicht nur an sich, das hieße für uns oder in der äußeren Reflexion, dasselbe was die Reflexion ist, sondern es ist gesetzt, daß es dasselbe ist. Es ist nämlich durch die Reflexion als ihr Negatives oder als ihr Anderes bestimmt, aber sie ist es selbst, welche dieses Bestimmen negirt.—Es ist damit die Äußerlichkeit der Reflexion gegen das Unmittelbare aufgehoben; ihr sich selbst negirendes Setzen ist das Zusammengehen ihrer mit ihrem Negativen, mit dem Unmittelbaren und dieses Zusammengehen ist die wesentliche Unmittelbarkeit selbst. —Es ist also vorhanden, daß die äußere Reflexion nicht äußere, sondern ebenso sehr immanente Reflexion der Unmittelbarkeit selbst ist; oder daß das was durch die setzende Reflexion ist, das an und für sich seyende Wesen ist. So ist sie bestimmende Reflexion.\n\nAnmerkung.\n\nDie Reflexion wird gewöhhlicher Weise in subjektivem Sinne genommen, als die Bewegung der Urtheilskraft, die über eine gegebene unmittelbare Vorstellung hinausgeht, und allgemeine Bestimmungen für dieselbe sucht oder damit vergleicht. Kant setzt die reflektirende Urtheilskraft, der bestimmenden Urtheilskraft entgegen. (Kritik der Urtheilskraft. Einleit. S. XXIII. f.) Er definirt die Urtheilskraft überhaupt als das Vermögen, das Besondere als enthalten unter dem Allgemeinen zu denken. Ist das Allgemeine (die Regel, das Princip, das Gesetz) gegeben, so ist die Urtheilskraft, welche das Besondere darunter subsumirt, bestimmend. Ist aber nur das Besondere wozu sie das Allgemeine finden soll, so ist die Urtheilskraft bloß reflektirend. Die Reflexion ist somit hier gleichfalls das Hinausgehen über ein Unmittelbares zum Allgemeinen. Das Unmittelbare wird theils erst durch diese Beziehung desselben auf sein Allgemeines bestimmt als Besonders; für sich ist es nur ein Einzelnes, oder ein unmittelbares Seyendes. Theils aber ist das, worauf es bezogen wird, sein Allgemeines, seine Regel, Princip, Gesetz; überhaupt das in sich reflektirte, sich auf sich selbst beziehende, das Wesen oder das Wesentliche.\n\nEs ist aber hier nicht, weder von der Reflexion des Bewußtseyns, noch von der bestimmteren Reflexion des Verstandes, die das Besondere und Allgemeine zu ihren Bestimmungen hat, sondern von der Reflexion überhaupt die Rede. Jene Reflexion, der Kant das Aufsuchen des Allgemeinen zum gegebenen Besondern zuschreibt, ist, wie erhellt, gleichfalls nur die äußere Reflexion, die sich auf das Unmittelbare als auf ein gegebenes bezieht.\n\n—Aber es liegt darin auch der Begriff der absoluten Reflexion; denn das Allgemeine, das Princip oder Regel und Gesetz, zu dem sie in ihrem Bestimmen fortgeht, gilt als das Wesen jenes Unmittelbaren, von dem angefangen wird, somit dieses als ein Nichtiges, und die Rückkehr aus demselben, das Bestimmen der Reflexion, erst als das Setzen des Unmittelbaren nach seinem wahrhaften Seyn; also das was die Reflexion an ihm thut und die Bestimmungen, die von ihr herkommen, nicht als ein jenem Unmittelbaren Äußerliches, sondern als dessen eigentliches Seyn.\n\nDie äußerliche Reflexion war auch gemeint, wenn der Reflexion überhaupt, wie es eine Zeitlang Ton in der neuern Philosophie war, alles Üble nachgesagt und sie mit ihrem Bestimmen als der Antipode und Erbfeind der absoluten Betrachtungsweise angesehen wurde. In der That geht auch die denkende Reflexion, insofern sie sich als äußerliche verhält, schlechthin von einem gegebenen, ihr fremden Unmittelbaren aus, und betrachtet sich als ein bloß formelles Thun, das Inhalt und Stoff von außen empfange, und für sich nur die durch ihn bedingte Bewegung sey.—Ferner, wie sich sogleich bei der bestimmenden Reflexion näher ergeben wird, sind die reflektirten Bestimmungen anderer Art, als die bloß unmittelbaren Bestimmungen des Seyns. Letztere werden leichter als vorübergehende, bloß relative, in der Beziehung auf Anderes stehende zugegeben; aber die reflektirten Bestimmungen haben die Form des An-und-Fürsichseyns; sie machen sich daher als die Wesentlichen geltend, und statt übergehend in ihre entgegengesetzten zu seyn, erscheinen sie vielmehr als absolut, frei und gleichgültig gegen einander. Sie widersetzen sich daher hartnäckig ihrer Bewegung, das Seyn derselben ist ihre Identität mit sich in ihrer Bestimmtheit, nach welcher sie, ob sie sich zwar gegenseitig voraussetzen, in dieser Beziehung sich schlechthin getrennt erhalten.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0001","text":"Die Reflexion als absolute Reflexion ist das in ihm selbst scheinende Wesen, und setzt sich nur den Schein, das Gesetztseyn, voraus; sie ist als voraussetzende unmittelbar nur setzende Reflexion. Aber die äußerliche oder reale Reflexion setzt sich als aufgehoben, als das Negative ihrer voraus. Sie ist in dieser Bestimmung verdoppelt; das einemal als das Vorausgesetzte, oder die Reflexion in sich, die das Unmittelbare ist. Das andere Mal ist sie die als negativ sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion; sie bezieht sich auf sich als auf jenes ihr Nichtseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"107.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0002","text":"Die äußerliche Reflexion setzt also ein Seyn voraus, erstens nicht in dem Sinne, daß seine Unmittelbarkeit nur Gesetztseyn oder Moment ist, sondern vielmehr, daß diese Unmittelbarkeit die Beziehung auf sich, und die Bestimmtheit nur als Moment ist. Sie bezieht sich auf ihre Voraussetzung so, daß diese das Negative der Reflexion ist, aber so daß dieses Negative als Negatives aufgehoben ist.—Die Reflexion in ihrem Setzen, hebt unmittelbar ihr Setzen auf, so hat sie eine unmittelbare Voraussetzung. Sie findet also dasselbe vor, als ein solches von dem sie anfängt, und von dem aus sie erst das Zurückgehen in sich, das Negiren dieses ihres Negativen ist. Aber daß dieß Vorausgesetzte ein Negatives oder Gesetztes ist, geht dasselbe nichts an; diese Bestimmtheit gehört nur der setzenden Reflexion an, aber in dem Voraussetzen ist das Gesetztseyn nur als aufgehobenes.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"107.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0003","text":"Was die äußerliche Reflexion an dem Unmittelbaren bestimmt und setzt, sind insofern demselben äußerliche Bestimmungen.—Sie war das Unendliche in der Sphäre des Seyns; das Endliche gilt als das Erste, als das Reale, von ihm wird als dem zu Grunde liegenden und zu Grund liegen bleibenden angefangen, und das Unendliche ist die gegenüber stehende Reflexion in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"107.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0004","text":"Diese äußere Reflexion ist der Schluß, in welchem die beiden Extreme, das Unmittelbare und die Reflexion in sich, sind; die Mitte desselben ist die Beziehung beider, das bestimmte Unmittelbare, so daß der eine Theil derselben, die Unmittelbarkeit nur dem einen Extreme, die andere, die Bestimmtheit oder Negation, nur dem andern Extreme zukommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"107.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0005","text":"Aber das Thun der äußeren Reflexion näher betrachtet, so ist sie zweitens Setzen des Unmittelbaren, das insofern das Negative oder Bestimmte wird; aber sie ist unmittelbar auch das Aufheben dieses ihres Setzens; denn sie setzt das Unmittelbare voraus; sie ist im Negiren das Negiren dieses ihres Negirens. Sie ist aber unmittelbar damit ebenso Setzen, Aufheben des ihr negativen Unmittelbaren, und dieses, von dem sie als von einem Fremden anzufangen schien, ist erst in diesem ihrem Anfangen. Das Unmittelbare ist auf diese Weise nicht nur an sich, das hieße für uns oder in der äußeren Reflexion, dasselbe was die Reflexion ist, sondern es ist gesetzt, daß es dasselbe ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"107.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0006","text":"Es ist nämlich durch die Reflexion als ihr Negatives oder als ihr Anderes bestimmt, aber sie ist es selbst, welche dieses Bestimmen negirt.—Es ist damit die Äußerlichkeit der Reflexion gegen das Unmittelbare aufgehoben; ihr sich selbst negirendes Setzen ist das Zusammengehen ihrer mit ihrem Negativen, mit dem Unmittelbaren und dieses Zusammengehen ist die wesentliche Unmittelbarkeit selbst. —Es ist also vorhanden, daß die äußere Reflexion nicht äußere, sondern ebenso sehr immanente Reflexion der Unmittelbarkeit selbst ist; oder daß das was durch die setzende Reflexion ist, das an und für sich seyende Wesen ist. So ist sie bestimmende Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"107.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0007","text":"Anmerkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"107.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0008","text":"Die Reflexion wird gewöhhlicher Weise in subjektivem Sinne genommen, als die Bewegung der Urtheilskraft, die über eine gegebene unmittelbare Vorstellung hinausgeht, und allgemeine Bestimmungen für dieselbe sucht oder damit vergleicht. Kant setzt die reflektirende Urtheilskraft, der bestimmenden Urtheilskraft entgegen. (Kritik der Urtheilskraft. Einleit. S. XXIII. f.) Er definirt die Urtheilskraft überhaupt als das Vermögen, das Besondere als enthalten unter dem Allgemeinen zu denken. Ist das Allgemeine (die Regel, das Princip, das Gesetz) gegeben, so ist die Urtheilskraft, welche das Besondere darunter subsumirt, bestimmend. Ist aber nur das Besondere wozu sie das Allgemeine finden soll, so ist die Urtheilskraft bloß reflektirend. Die Reflexion ist somit hier gleichfalls das Hinausgehen über ein Unmittelbares zum Allgemeinen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"107.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0009","text":"Das Unmittelbare wird theils erst durch diese Beziehung desselben auf sein Allgemeines bestimmt als Besonders; für sich ist es nur ein Einzelnes, oder ein unmittelbares Seyendes. Theils aber ist das, worauf es bezogen wird, sein Allgemeines, seine Regel, Princip, Gesetz; überhaupt das in sich reflektirte, sich auf sich selbst beziehende, das Wesen oder das Wesentliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"107.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0010","text":"Es ist aber hier nicht, weder von der Reflexion des Bewußtseyns, noch von der bestimmteren Reflexion des Verstandes, die das Besondere und Allgemeine zu ihren Bestimmungen hat, sondern von der Reflexion überhaupt die Rede. Jene Reflexion, der Kant das Aufsuchen des Allgemeinen zum gegebenen Besondern zuschreibt, ist, wie erhellt, gleichfalls nur die äußere Reflexion, die sich auf das Unmittelbare als auf ein gegebenes bezieht.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"107.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0011","text":"—Aber es liegt darin auch der Begriff der absoluten Reflexion; denn das Allgemeine, das Princip oder Regel und Gesetz, zu dem sie in ihrem Bestimmen fortgeht, gilt als das Wesen jenes Unmittelbaren, von dem angefangen wird, somit dieses als ein Nichtiges, und die Rückkehr aus demselben, das Bestimmen der Reflexion, erst als das Setzen des Unmittelbaren nach seinem wahrhaften Seyn; also das was die Reflexion an ihm thut und die Bestimmungen, die von ihr herkommen, nicht als ein jenem Unmittelbaren Äußerliches, sondern als dessen eigentliches Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"107.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0012","text":"Die äußerliche Reflexion war auch gemeint, wenn der Reflexion überhaupt, wie es eine Zeitlang Ton in der neuern Philosophie war, alles Üble nachgesagt und sie mit ihrem Bestimmen als der Antipode und Erbfeind der absoluten Betrachtungsweise angesehen wurde. In der That geht auch die denkende Reflexion, insofern sie sich als äußerliche verhält, schlechthin von einem gegebenen, ihr fremden Unmittelbaren aus, und betrachtet sich als ein bloß formelles Thun, das Inhalt und Stoff von außen empfange, und für sich nur die durch ihn bedingte Bewegung sey.—Ferner, wie sich sogleich bei der bestimmenden Reflexion näher ergeben wird, sind die reflektirten Bestimmungen anderer Art, als die bloß unmittelbaren Bestimmungen des Seyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"107.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0013","text":"Letztere werden leichter als vorübergehende, bloß relative, in der Beziehung auf Anderes stehende zugegeben; aber die reflektirten Bestimmungen haben die Form des An-und-Fürsichseyns; sie machen sich daher als die Wesentlichen geltend, und statt übergehend in ihre entgegengesetzten zu seyn, erscheinen sie vielmehr als absolut, frei und gleichgültig gegen einander. Sie widersetzen sich daher hartnäckig ihrer Bewegung, das Seyn derselben ist ihre Identität mit sich in ihrer Bestimmtheit, nach welcher sie, ob sie sich zwar gegenseitig voraussetzen, in dieser Beziehung sich schlechthin getrennt erhalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"107.13"}],"sha256":"260e82777c90bbb6206805c184520b1180bbda2b1a46d329451b2255f22d608d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104635276247Z_90ea199f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"2. External Reflection.","source_sha256":"260e82777c90bbb6206805c184520b1180bbda2b1a46d329451b2255f22d608d","sha256":"d800476dd27007d99a392385028841ecf48cf5764c35621735a321ea591b065a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:46:35.276270+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0001","text":"Reflection as absolute reflection is essence shining within itself, and presupposes only semblance, positedness; as presupposing, it is immediately only positing reflection. But external or real reflection posits itself as sublated, as the negative of its presupposition. In this determination it is duplicated; on the one hand as the presupposed, or reflection into itself, which is the immediate. On the other hand, it is reflection relating itself negatively to itself; it relates itself to itself as to that its non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"107.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0002","text":"External reflection thus presupposes a being, firstly not in the sense that its immediacy is only positedness or a moment, but rather that this immediacy is relation to itself, and determinateness only as a moment. It relates itself to its presupposition in such a way that this is the negative of reflection, but such that this negative is sublated as negative.—Reflection, in its positing, immediately sublates its positing; thus it has an immediate presupposition. It therefore finds the same before it, as something from which it begins, and from which only its return into itself, the negating of this its negative, proceeds. But that this presupposed is a negative or a posited, does not concern it; this determinateness belongs only to positing reflection, but in presupposing positedness is only as sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"107.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0003","text":"What external reflection determines and posits in the immediate are, to that extent, determinations external to it.—It was the infinite in the sphere of Being; the finite counts as the first, as the real; one begins from it as from what lies at the ground and remains lying at the ground, and the infinite is the reflection into itself standing opposite.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"107.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0004","text":"This external reflection is the syllogism in which the two extremes, the immediate and reflection into itself, are; its middle is the relation of the two, the determinate immediate, so that one part of it, immediacy, belongs only to the one extreme, the other, determinateness or negation, only to the other extreme.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"107.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0005","text":"But if the activity of external reflection is considered more closely, it is secondly the positing of the immediate, which thereby becomes the negative or the determinate; but it is immediately also the sublating of this its positing; for it presupposes the immediate; in negating, it is the negating of this its negating. But thereby it is immediately likewise positing, sublating the immediate negative to it, and this, from which it seemed to begin as from something alien, is only in this its beginning. In this way the immediate is not merely in itself—that is, for us or in external reflection—the same as reflection is, but it is posited that it is the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"107.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0006","text":"Namely, it is determined by reflection as its negative or as its other, but reflection itself is that which negates this determining.—Thereby the externality of reflection towards the immediate is sublated; its positing, which negates itself, is the coalescing of it with its negative, with the immediate, and this coalescing is essential immediacy itself. —Thus it is present that external reflection is not external, but just as much immanent reflection of immediacy itself; or that what is through positing reflection is essence that is in and for itself. Thus it is determining reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"107.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0007","text":"Remark.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"107.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0008","text":"Reflection is customarily taken in a subjective sense, as the movement of the power of judgment which goes beyond a given immediate representation and seeks universal determinations for it or compares it with them. Kant opposes the reflecting power of judgment to the determining power of judgment. (Critique of Judgment. Introduction, p. XXIII f.) He defines the power of judgment in general as the faculty of thinking the particular as contained under the universal. If the universal (the rule, the principle, the law) is given, then the power of judgment which subsumes the particular under it is determining. But if only the particular is given, for which it is to find the universal, then the power of judgment is merely reflecting. Reflection here too is thus the going beyond an immediate to the universal.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"107.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0009","text":"The immediate is in part first determined as particular through this relation of it to its universal; for itself it is only a singular, or an immediate being. In part, however, that to which it is related is its universal, its rule, principle, law; in general, that which is reflected into itself, relates itself to itself, essence or the essential.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"107.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0010","text":"But here the discussion is neither of the reflection of consciousness nor of the more determinate reflection of understanding, which has the particular and the universal for its determinations, but of reflection in general. That reflection to which Kant ascribes the seeking of the universal for the given particular is, as is evident, likewise only external reflection, which relates itself to the immediate as to something given.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"107.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0011","text":"—But the concept of absolute reflection also lies therein; for the universal, the principle or rule and law, to which it proceeds in its determining, counts as the essence of that immediate from which one begins; hence this immediate as something null, and the return from it, the determining of reflection, first as the positing of the immediate according to its true Being; thus what reflection does to it and the determinations which come from reflection, not as something external to that immediate, but as its proper Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"107.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0012","text":"External reflection was also intended when all evil was ascribed to reflection in general, as for a time it was the fashion in modern philosophy, and it, with its determining, was regarded as the antipode and hereditary enemy of the absolute mode of consideration. In fact, thinking reflection too, insofar as it behaves as external, proceeds absolutely from a given immediate alien to it, and regards itself as a merely formal activity which receives content and material from without, and is for itself only the movement conditioned by them.—Further, as will immediately emerge more closely in the case of determining reflection, reflected determinations are of another kind than the merely immediate determinations of Being.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"107.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0013","text":"The latter are more readily admitted to be transient, merely relative, standing in relation to an other; but reflected determinations have the form of being-in-and-for-itself; they therefore assert themselves as the essential, and instead of passing over into their opposites, they appear rather as absolute, free, and indifferent to one another. They therefore stubbornly resist their movement; their being is their identity with themselves in their determinateness, according to which, although they mutually presuppose one another, they nevertheless maintain themselves absolutely separate in this relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"107.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DUR:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"b2ec35b5e2619e2209072cb435e2cd55f0c02b4d25c261521c8097a40a6ea058","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"2. Die äußere Reflexion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"2. Die äußere Reflexion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0","title":"3. Determining Reflection.","order":108,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_3BR0","text":"Die bestimmende Reflexion ist überhaupt die Einheit der setzenden und der äußeren Reflexion. Dieß ist näher zu betrachten.-1. Die äußere Reflexion fängt vom unmittelbaren Seyn all, die setzende vom Nichts. Die äußere Reflexion, die bestimmend wird, setzt ein Anderes, aber das Wesen, an die Stelle des aufgehobenen Seyns; das Setzen setzt seine Bestimmung nicht an die Stelle eines Anderen; es hat keine Voraussetzung. Aber deswegen ist es nicht die vollendete, bestimmende Reflexion; die Bestimmung, die es setzt, ist daher nur ein Gesetztes; es ist Unmittelbares, aber nicht als sich selbst gleich, sondern als sich negirend, es hat absolute Beziehung auf die Rückkehr in sich, es ist nur in der Reflexion in sich, aber es ist nicht diese Reflexion selbst.\n\nDas Gesetzte ist daher ein Anderes, aber so, daß die Gleichheit der Reflexion mit sich schlechthin erhalten ist; denn das Gesetzte ist nur als Aufgehobenes, als Beziehung auf die Rückkehr in sich selbst. —In der Sphäre des Seyns, war das Daseyn das Seyn, das die Negation an ihm hatte, und das Seyn der unmittelbare Boden und Element dieser Negation, die daher selbst die unmittelbare war. Dem Daseyn entspricht in der Sphäre des Wesens das Gesetztseyn. Es ist gleichfalls ein Daseyn, aber sein Boden ist das Seyn, als Wesen oder als reine Negativität; es ist eine Bestimmtheit oder Negation nicht als seyend, sondern unmittelbar als aufgehoben. Das Daseyn ist nur Gesetztseyn; dieß ist der Satz des Wesens vom Daseyn. Das Gesetztseyn steht einer Seits dem Daseyn, anderer Seits dem Wesen gegenüber, und ist als die Mitte zu betrachten, welche das Daseyn mit dem Wesen und umgekehrt das Wesen mit dem Daseyn zusammenschließt. —Wenn man sagt, eine Bestimmung ist nur ein Gesetztseyn, so kann dieß daher den doppelten Sinn haben; sie ist dieß im Gegensatze gegen das Daseyn, oder gegen das Wesen. In jenem Sinne wird das Daseyn für etwas Höheres genommen, als das Gesetztseyn, und dieses der äußern Reflexion, dem Subjektiven zugeschrieben. In der That aber ist das Gesetztseyn das Höhere; denn als Gesetztseyn ist das Daseyn, als das was es an sich ist, als Negatives, ein schlechthin nur auf die Rückkehr in sich bezogenes. Deswegen ist das Gesetztseyn nur ein Gesetztseyn in Rücksicht auf das Wesen, als die Negation des Zurückgekehrtseyns in sich selbst.\n\n2. Das Gesetztseyn ist noch nicht Reflexions-Bestimmung; es ist nur Bestimmtheit, als Negation überhaupt. Aber das Setzen ist nun in Einheit mit der äußern Reflexion; diese ist in dieser Einheit absolutes Voraussetzen; das heißt, das Abstoßen der Reflexion von sich selbst, oder Setzen der Bestimmtheit als ihrer selbst. Das Gesetztseyn ist daher, als solches Negation; aber als vorausgesetztes ist sie als in sich reflektirte. So ist das Gesetztseyn Reflexions-Bestimmung.\n\nDie Reflexions-Bestimmung ist von der Bestimmtheit des Seyns, der Qualität, unterschieden; diese ist unmittelbare Beziehung auf Anderes überhaupt; auch das Gesetztseyn ist Beziehung auf Anderes, aber auf das Reflektirtseyn in sich. Die Negation als Qualität ist Negation als seyend; das Seyn macht ihren Grund und Element aus. Die Reflexionsbestimmung hingegen hat zu diesem Grunde das Reflektirtseyn in sich selbst. Das Gesetztseyn fixirt sich zur Bestimmung, eben darum, weil die Reflexion die Gleichheit mit sich selbst in ihrem Negirtseyn ist; ihr Negirtseyn ist daher selbst Reflexion in sich. Die Bestimmung besteht hier nicht durch das Seyn, sondern durch ihre Gleichheit mit sich. Weil das Seyn, das die Qualität trägt, das der Negation ungleiche ist, so ist die Qualität in sich selbst ungleich, daher übergehendes, im Andern verschwindendes Moment. Hingegen die Reflexionsbestimmung ist das Gesetztseyn als Negation, Negation die zu ihrem Grunde das Negirtseyn hat, also sich in sich selbst nicht ungleich ist, somit wesentliche, nicht übergehende Bestimmtheit. Die Sich-selbst-Gleichheit der Reflexion, welche das Negative nur als Negatives, als Aufgehobenes oder Gesetztes hat, ist es, welche demselben Bestehen giebt.\n\nUm dieser Reflexion in sich willen erscheinen die Reflexionsbestimmungen als freie, im Leeren ohne Anziehung oder Abstoßung gegen einander schwebende Wesenheiten. In ihnen hat sich die Bestimmtheit durch die Beziehung auf sich befestigt und unendlich fixirt. Es ist das Bestimmte, das sein Übergehen und sein bloßes Gesetztseyn sich unterworfen, oder seine Reflexion in Anderes in Reflexion in sich umgebogen hat. Diese Bestimmungen machen hierdurch den bestimmten Schein aus, wie er im Wesen ist, den wesentlichen Schein. Aus diesem Grunde ist die bestimmende Reflexion die außer sich gekommene Reflexion; die Gleichheit des Wesens mit sich selbst ist in die Negation verloren, die das Herrschende ist.\n\nEs sind also an der Reflexionsbestimmung zwei Seiten, die zunächst sich unterscheiden. Erstlich ist sie das Gesetztseyn, die Negation als solche; zweitens ist sie die Reflexion in sich. Nach dem Gesetztseyn ist sie die Negation als Negation; dieß ist somit bereits ihre Einheit mit sich selbst. Aber sie ist dieß nur erst an sich; oder sie ist das Unmittelbare als sich an ihm aufhebend, als das Andere seiner selbst.—Insofern ist die Reflexion in sich bleibendes Bestimmen. Das Wesen geht darin nicht außer sich; die Unterschiede sind schlechthin gesetzt, in das Wesen zurückgenommen. Aber nach der andern Seite sind sie nicht gesetzte, sondern in sich selbst reflektirt; die Negation als Negation, ist in Gleichheit mit ihr selbst, nicht in ihr Anderes, nicht in ihr Nichtseyn reflektirt.\n\n3. Indem nun die Reflexionsbestimmung sowohl reflektirte Beziehung in sich selbst, als auch Gesetztseyn ist, so erhellt unmittelbar daraus ihre Natur näher. Als Gesetztseyn nämlich ist sie die Negation als solche, ein Nichtseyn gegen ein Anderes, nämlich gegen die absolute Reflexion in sich oder gegen das Wesen. Aber als Beziehung auf sich ist sie in sich reflektirt.—Diese ihre Reflexion und jenes Gesetztseyn sind verschieden; ihr Gesetztseyn ist vielmehr ihr Aufgehobenseyn; ihr Reflektirtseyn in sich aber ist ihr Bestehen. Insofern es nun also das Gesetztseyn ist, das zugleich Reflexion in sich selbst ist, so ist die Reflexionsbestimmtheit die Beziehung auf ihr Andersseyn an ihr selbst.—Sie ist nicht als eine seyende, ruhende Bestimmtheit, welche bezogen würde auf ein Anderes, so daß das Bezogene und dessen Beziehung verschieden von einander sind, jenes ein Insichseyendes, ein Etwas, welches sein Anderes und seine Beziehung auf dieß Andere von sich ausschließt. Sondern die Reflexions-Bestimmung ist an ihr selbst die bestimmte Seite, und die Beziehung dieser bestimmten Seite als bestimmter, das heißt, auf ihre Negation.—Die Qualität geht durch ihre Beziehung in Anderes über; in ihrer Beziehung beginnt ihre Veränderung. Die Reflexionsbestimmung hingegen hat ihr Andersseyn in sich zurückgenommen. Sie ist Gesetztseyn, Negation, welche aber die Beziehung auf Anderes in sich zurückbeugt, und Negation, die sich selbst gleich, die Einheit ihrer selbst und ihres Andern und nur dadurch Wesensheit ist. Sie ist also Gesetztseyn, Negation, aber als Reflexion in sich ist sie zugleich das Aufgehobenseyn dieses Gesetztseyns, unendliche Beziehung auf sich.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0001","text":"Die bestimmende Reflexion ist überhaupt die Einheit der setzenden und der äußeren Reflexion. Dieß ist näher zu betrachten.-1. Die äußere Reflexion fängt vom unmittelbaren Seyn all, die setzende vom Nichts. Die äußere Reflexion, die bestimmend wird, setzt ein Anderes, aber das Wesen, an die Stelle des aufgehobenen Seyns; das Setzen setzt seine Bestimmung nicht an die Stelle eines Anderen; es hat keine Voraussetzung. Aber deswegen ist es nicht die vollendete, bestimmende Reflexion; die Bestimmung, die es setzt, ist daher nur ein Gesetztes; es ist Unmittelbares, aber nicht als sich selbst gleich, sondern als sich negirend, es hat absolute Beziehung auf die Rückkehr in sich, es ist nur in der Reflexion in sich, aber es ist nicht diese Reflexion selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"108.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0002","text":"Das Gesetzte ist daher ein Anderes, aber so, daß die Gleichheit der Reflexion mit sich schlechthin erhalten ist; denn das Gesetzte ist nur als Aufgehobenes, als Beziehung auf die Rückkehr in sich selbst. —In der Sphäre des Seyns, war das Daseyn das Seyn, das die Negation an ihm hatte, und das Seyn der unmittelbare Boden und Element dieser Negation, die daher selbst die unmittelbare war. Dem Daseyn entspricht in der Sphäre des Wesens das Gesetztseyn. Es ist gleichfalls ein Daseyn, aber sein Boden ist das Seyn, als Wesen oder als reine Negativität; es ist eine Bestimmtheit oder Negation nicht als seyend, sondern unmittelbar als aufgehoben. Das Daseyn ist nur Gesetztseyn; dieß ist der Satz des Wesens vom Daseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"108.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0003","text":"Das Gesetztseyn steht einer Seits dem Daseyn, anderer Seits dem Wesen gegenüber, und ist als die Mitte zu betrachten, welche das Daseyn mit dem Wesen und umgekehrt das Wesen mit dem Daseyn zusammenschließt. —Wenn man sagt, eine Bestimmung ist nur ein Gesetztseyn, so kann dieß daher den doppelten Sinn haben; sie ist dieß im Gegensatze gegen das Daseyn, oder gegen das Wesen. In jenem Sinne wird das Daseyn für etwas Höheres genommen, als das Gesetztseyn, und dieses der äußern Reflexion, dem Subjektiven zugeschrieben. In der That aber ist das Gesetztseyn das Höhere; denn als Gesetztseyn ist das Daseyn, als das was es an sich ist, als Negatives, ein schlechthin nur auf die Rückkehr in sich bezogenes. Deswegen ist das Gesetztseyn nur ein Gesetztseyn in Rücksicht auf das Wesen, als die Negation des Zurückgekehrtseyns in sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"108.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0004","text":"2. Das Gesetztseyn ist noch nicht Reflexions-Bestimmung; es ist nur Bestimmtheit, als Negation überhaupt. Aber das Setzen ist nun in Einheit mit der äußern Reflexion; diese ist in dieser Einheit absolutes Voraussetzen; das heißt, das Abstoßen der Reflexion von sich selbst, oder Setzen der Bestimmtheit als ihrer selbst. Das Gesetztseyn ist daher, als solches Negation; aber als vorausgesetztes ist sie als in sich reflektirte. So ist das Gesetztseyn Reflexions-Bestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"108.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0005","text":"Die Reflexions-Bestimmung ist von der Bestimmtheit des Seyns, der Qualität, unterschieden; diese ist unmittelbare Beziehung auf Anderes überhaupt; auch das Gesetztseyn ist Beziehung auf Anderes, aber auf das Reflektirtseyn in sich. Die Negation als Qualität ist Negation als seyend; das Seyn macht ihren Grund und Element aus. Die Reflexionsbestimmung hingegen hat zu diesem Grunde das Reflektirtseyn in sich selbst. Das Gesetztseyn fixirt sich zur Bestimmung, eben darum, weil die Reflexion die Gleichheit mit sich selbst in ihrem Negirtseyn ist; ihr Negirtseyn ist daher selbst Reflexion in sich. Die Bestimmung besteht hier nicht durch das Seyn, sondern durch ihre Gleichheit mit sich. Weil das Seyn, das die Qualität trägt, das der Negation ungleiche ist, so ist die Qualität in sich selbst ungleich, daher übergehendes, im Andern verschwindendes Moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"108.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0006","text":"Hingegen die Reflexionsbestimmung ist das Gesetztseyn als Negation, Negation die zu ihrem Grunde das Negirtseyn hat, also sich in sich selbst nicht ungleich ist, somit wesentliche, nicht übergehende Bestimmtheit. Die Sich-selbst-Gleichheit der Reflexion, welche das Negative nur als Negatives, als Aufgehobenes oder Gesetztes hat, ist es, welche demselben Bestehen giebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"108.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0007","text":"Um dieser Reflexion in sich willen erscheinen die Reflexionsbestimmungen als freie, im Leeren ohne Anziehung oder Abstoßung gegen einander schwebende Wesenheiten. In ihnen hat sich die Bestimmtheit durch die Beziehung auf sich befestigt und unendlich fixirt. Es ist das Bestimmte, das sein Übergehen und sein bloßes Gesetztseyn sich unterworfen, oder seine Reflexion in Anderes in Reflexion in sich umgebogen hat. Diese Bestimmungen machen hierdurch den bestimmten Schein aus, wie er im Wesen ist, den wesentlichen Schein. Aus diesem Grunde ist die bestimmende Reflexion die außer sich gekommene Reflexion; die Gleichheit des Wesens mit sich selbst ist in die Negation verloren, die das Herrschende ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"108.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0008","text":"Es sind also an der Reflexionsbestimmung zwei Seiten, die zunächst sich unterscheiden. Erstlich ist sie das Gesetztseyn, die Negation als solche; zweitens ist sie die Reflexion in sich. Nach dem Gesetztseyn ist sie die Negation als Negation; dieß ist somit bereits ihre Einheit mit sich selbst. Aber sie ist dieß nur erst an sich; oder sie ist das Unmittelbare als sich an ihm aufhebend, als das Andere seiner selbst.—Insofern ist die Reflexion in sich bleibendes Bestimmen. Das Wesen geht darin nicht außer sich; die Unterschiede sind schlechthin gesetzt, in das Wesen zurückgenommen. Aber nach der andern Seite sind sie nicht gesetzte, sondern in sich selbst reflektirt; die Negation als Negation, ist in Gleichheit mit ihr selbst, nicht in ihr Anderes, nicht in ihr Nichtseyn reflektirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"108.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0009","text":"3. Indem nun die Reflexionsbestimmung sowohl reflektirte Beziehung in sich selbst, als auch Gesetztseyn ist, so erhellt unmittelbar daraus ihre Natur näher. Als Gesetztseyn nämlich ist sie die Negation als solche, ein Nichtseyn gegen ein Anderes, nämlich gegen die absolute Reflexion in sich oder gegen das Wesen. Aber als Beziehung auf sich ist sie in sich reflektirt.—Diese ihre Reflexion und jenes Gesetztseyn sind verschieden; ihr Gesetztseyn ist vielmehr ihr Aufgehobenseyn; ihr Reflektirtseyn in sich aber ist ihr Bestehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"108.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0010","text":"Insofern es nun also das Gesetztseyn ist, das zugleich Reflexion in sich selbst ist, so ist die Reflexionsbestimmtheit die Beziehung auf ihr Andersseyn an ihr selbst.—Sie ist nicht als eine seyende, ruhende Bestimmtheit, welche bezogen würde auf ein Anderes, so daß das Bezogene und dessen Beziehung verschieden von einander sind, jenes ein Insichseyendes, ein Etwas, welches sein Anderes und seine Beziehung auf dieß Andere von sich ausschließt. Sondern die Reflexions-Bestimmung ist an ihr selbst die bestimmte Seite, und die Beziehung dieser bestimmten Seite als bestimmter, das heißt, auf ihre Negation.—Die Qualität geht durch ihre Beziehung in Anderes über; in ihrer Beziehung beginnt ihre Veränderung. Die Reflexionsbestimmung hingegen hat ihr Andersseyn in sich zurückgenommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"108.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0011","text":"Sie ist Gesetztseyn, Negation, welche aber die Beziehung auf Anderes in sich zurückbeugt, und Negation, die sich selbst gleich, die Einheit ihrer selbst und ihres Andern und nur dadurch Wesensheit ist. Sie ist also Gesetztseyn, Negation, aber als Reflexion in sich ist sie zugleich das Aufgehobenseyn dieses Gesetztseyns, unendliche Beziehung auf sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"108.11"}],"sha256":"15f727b6d3e3ea778f75335952f895597e66ece9ce7162dd6631b741b564f129","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104649640548Z_ec536d0a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"3. Determining Reflection.","source_sha256":"15f727b6d3e3ea778f75335952f895597e66ece9ce7162dd6631b741b564f129","sha256":"ef5165bee98bf08579f6141197ae3802e42f522462c61f8e21ffe0b05fbc5c61","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:46:49.640616+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0001","text":"Determining reflection is in general the unity of positing and external reflection. This is to be considered more closely.—1. External reflection begins from immediate Being, positing from nothing. External reflection, which becomes determining, posits an other, but essence, in the place of the sublated Being; positing does not posit its determination in the place of an other; it has no presupposition. But for this reason it is not the completed, determining reflection; the determination which it posits is therefore only a posited; it is immediate, but not as equal to itself, rather as negating itself; it has absolute relation to the return into itself, it is only in reflection into itself, but it is not this reflection itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"108.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0002","text":"The posited is therefore an other, but in such a way that the equality of reflection with itself is absolutely preserved; for the posited is only as sublated, as relation to the return into itself.—In the sphere of Being, determinate being was the Being which had negation in it, and Being was the immediate ground and element of this negation, which was therefore itself immediate. Positedness corresponds to determinate being in the sphere of essence. It is likewise a determinate being, but its ground is Being as essence or as pure negativity; it is a determinateness or negation not as being, but immediately as sublated. Determinate being is only positedness; this is the proposition of essence concerning determinate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"108.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0003","text":"Positedness stands opposed, on the one hand, to determinate being, and, on the other hand, to essence, and is to be considered as the middle which joins determinate being to essence and, conversely, essence to determinate being.—When one says that a determination is only a positedness, this can thus have the double meaning: it is this in opposition to determinate being, or to essence. In the former sense, determinate being is taken as something higher than positedness, and the latter is ascribed to external reflection, to the subjective. In fact, however, positedness is the higher; for as positedness, determinate being is what it is in itself, as negative, as related absolutely only to the return into itself. For this reason positedness is only a positedness with respect to essence, as the negation of having returned into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"108.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0004","text":"2. Positedness is not yet reflection-determination; it is only determinateness, as negation in general. But positing is now in unity with external reflection; in this unity, the latter is absolute presupposing; that is, the repulsion of reflection from itself, or the positing of determinateness as its own self. Positedness is therefore, as such, negation; but as presupposed it is as reflected into itself. Thus positedness is reflection-determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"108.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0005","text":"Reflection-determination is distinct from the determinateness of Being, quality; the latter is immediate relation to other in general; positedness too is relation to other, but to reflectedness into itself. Negation as quality is negation as being; Being constitutes its ground and element. Reflection-determination, on the other hand, has reflectedness into itself as this ground. Positedness fixes itself as determination precisely because reflection is equality with itself in its being-negated; its being-negated is therefore itself reflection into itself. Determination here subsists not through Being, but through its equality with itself. Because the Being which bears quality is that which is unequal to negation, quality is unequal within itself and therefore a passing-over, a moment vanishing in the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"108.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0006","text":"Reflection-determination, on the contrary, is positedness as negation, negation which has being-negated as its ground, and thus is not unequal to itself within itself, hence essential, non-passing determinateness. The self-equality of reflection, which has the negative only as negative, as sublated or posited, is what gives it subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"108.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0007","text":"By virtue of this reflection into itself, reflection-determinations appear as free essences hovering in the void without attraction or repulsion towards one another. In them determinateness has established and infinitely fixed itself through relation to itself. It is the determinate which has subjected to itself its passing-over and its mere positedness, or which has bent its reflection into other back into reflection into itself. These determinations thereby constitute determinate shine, as it is in essence, essential shine. For this reason determining reflection is reflection that has come outside itself; the equality of essence with itself is lost in negation, which is the ruling factor.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"108.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0008","text":"Thus there are two sides to reflection-determination, which at first distinguish themselves. First, it is positedness, negation as such; second, it is reflection into itself. According to positedness, it is negation as negation; thus this is already its unity with itself. But it is this only in itself; or it is the immediate as sublating itself in it, as the other of itself.—In this respect it is reflection remaining within itself, determining. Essence does not go outside itself in this; the differences are absolutely posited, taken back into essence. But according to the other side, they are not posited, but reflected into themselves; negation as negation is in equality with itself, not reflected into its other, not into its non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"108.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0009","text":"3. Since reflection-determination is now both reflected relation into itself and positedness, its nature follows immediately from this more closely. As positedness, namely, it is negation as such, a non-being in opposition to an other, namely to absolute reflection into itself or to essence. But as relation to itself, it is reflected into itself.—This its reflection and that positedness are distinct; its positedness is rather its sublatedness; but its reflectedness into itself is its subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"108.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0010","text":"Insofar, then, as it is positedness which is at the same time reflection into itself, reflection-determinateness is relation to its otherness in itself.—It is not as a being, resting determinateness which would be related to an other, such that what is related and its relation are distinct from one another, the former being an in-itself-being, a something which excludes from itself its other and its relation to this other. Rather, reflection-determination is in itself the determinate side, and the relation of this determinate side as determinate, that is, to its negation.—Quality passes over into other through its relation; its alteration begins in its relation. Reflection-determination, on the contrary, has taken its otherness back into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"108.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0011","text":"It is positedness, negation, which, however, bends the relation to other back into itself, and negation equal to itself, the unity of itself and its other, and only thereby essentiality. It is thus positedness, negation, but as reflection into itself it is at the same time the sublatedness of this positedness, infinite relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"108.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3BR0:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"645ae3f52ab2880072c9a95ce004a06e22dd4faf32b755a01efa1f2410bcbcb2","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"3. Bestimmende Reflexion."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"3. Bestimmende Reflexion.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26","title":"Remark.","order":109,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_26","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Die Wesenheiten oder die Reflexions-Bestimmungen.\n\nDie Reflexion ist bestimmte Reflexion; somit ist das Wesen bestimmtes Wesen, oder es ist Wesenheit.\n\nDie Reflexion ist das Scheinen des Wesens in sich selbst. Das Wesen als unendliche Rückkehr in sich ist nicht unmittelbare, sondern negative Einfachheit; es ist eine Bewegung durch unterschiedene Momente, absolute Vermittelung mit sich. Aber es scheint in diese seine Momente; sie sind daher selbst in sich reflektirte Bestimmungen.\n\nDas Wesen ist zuerst einfache Beziehung auf sich selbst; reine Identität. Dieß ist seine Bestimmung, nach der es vielmehr Bestimmungslosigkeit ist.\n\nZweitens die eigentliche Bestimmung ist der Unterschied; und zwar theils als äußerlicher oder gleichgültiger Unterschied, die Verschiedenheit überhaupt; theils aber als entgegengesetzte Verschiedenheit oder als Gegensatz.\n\nDrittens als Widerspruch reflektirt sich der Gegensatz in sich selbst und geht in seinen Grund zurück.\n\n## Anmerkung.\n\nDie Reflexions-Bestimmungen pflegten sonst in die Form von Sätzen aufgenommen zu werden, worin von ihnen ausgesagt wurde, daß sie von Allem gelten. Diese Sätze galten als die allgemeinen Denkgesetze, die allem Denken zum Grunde liegen, an ihnen selbst absolut und unbeweisbar seyen, aber von jedem Denken, wie es ihren Sinn fasse, unmittelbar und unwidersprochen als wahr anerkannt und angenommen werden.\n\nSo wird die wesentliche Bestimmung der Identität in dem Satze ausgesprochen: Alles ist sich selbst gleich; A=A. Oder negativ: A kann nicht zugleich A und nicht A seyn. Es ist zunächst nicht abzusehen, warum nur diese einfachen Bestimmungen der Reflexion in diese besondere Form gefaßt werden sollen, und nicht auch die andern Kategorien, wie alle Bestimmtheiten der Sphäre des Seyns. Es ergäben sich die Sätze z.B. Alles ist, Alles hat ein Daseyn u.s.f. oder Alles hat eine Qualität, Quantität u.s.w. Denn Seyn, Daseyn u.s.f. sind als logische Bestimmungen überhaupt Prädikate von Allem. Die Kategorie ist ihrer Etymologie und der Definition des Aristoteles nach, dasjenige, was von dem Seyenden gesagt, behauptet wird.—Allein eine Bestimmtheit des Seyns ist wesentlich ein Übergehen ins Entgegengesetzte; die negative einer jeden Bestimmtheit ist so nothwendig als sie selbst; als unmittelbaren Bestimmtheiten steht jeder die andere unmittelbar gegenüber. Wenn diese Kategorien daher in solche Sätze gefaßt werden, so kommen ebenso sehr die entgegengesetzten Sätze zum Vorschein; beide bieten sich mit gleicher Nothwendigkeit dar, und haben als unmittelbare Behauptungen wenigstens gleiches Recht. Der eine erforderte dadurch einen Beweis gegen den andern, und diesen Behauptungen könnte daher nicht mehr der Charakter von unmittelbar wahren und unwidersprechlichen Sätzen des Denkens zukommen.\n\nDie Reflexions-Bestimmungen dagegen sind nicht von qualitativer Art. Sie sind sich auf sich beziehende und damit der Bestimmtheit gegen Anderes zugleich entnommene Bestimmungen. Ferner indem es Bestimmtheiten sind, welche Beziehungen an sich selbst sind, so enthalten sie insofern die Form des Satzes schon in sich. Denn der Satz unterscheidet sich vom Urtheil vornehmlich dadurch, daß in jenem der Inhalt die Beziehung selbst ausmacht, oder daß er eine bestimmte Beziehung ist. Das Urtheil dagegen verlegt den Inhalt in das Prädikat, als eine allgemeine Bestimmtheit, die für sich und von ihrer Beziehung, der einfachen Copula, unterschieden ist. Wenn ein Satz in ein Urtheil verwandelt werden soll, so wird der bestimmte Inhalt, wenn er z.B. in einem Zeitworte liegt, in ein Particip verwandelt, um auf diese Art die Bestimmung selbst und ihre Beziehung auf ein Subjekt zu trennen. Den Reflexions-Bestimmungen dagegen als in sich reflektirtem Gesetztseyn liegt die Form des Satzes selbst nahe.—Allein indem sie als allgemeine Denkgesetze ausgesprochen werden, so bedürfen sie noch eines Subjekts ihrer Beziehung, und dieß Subjekt ist: Alles; oder ein A, was ebenso viel als Alles und Jedes Seyn bedeutet.\n\nEines Theils ist diese Form von Sätzen etwas Überflüssiges; die Reflexions-Bestimmungen sind an und für sich zu betrachten. Ferner haben diese Sätze die schiefe Seite, das Seyn, Alles Etwas, zum Subjekte zu haben. Sie erwecken damit das Seyn wieder, und sprechen die Reflexions-Bestimmungen, die Identität u.s.f. von dem Etwas als eine Qualität aus, die es an ihm habe; nicht in spekulativem Sinne, sondern daß Etwas als Subjekt in einer solchen Qualität bleibe als seyendes, nicht daß es in die Identität u.s.f. als in seine Wahrheit und sein Wesen übergegangen sey.\n\nEndlich aber haben die Reflexions-Bestimmungen zwar die Form sich selbst gleich und daher unbezogen auf Anderes und ohne Entgegensetzung zu seyn; aber wie sich aus ihrer nähern Betrachtung ergeben wird,—oder wie unmittelbar an ihnen, als der Identität, der Verschiedenheit, der Entgegensetzung erhellt—sind sie bestimmte gegen einander, sie sind also durch ihre Form der Reflexion, dem Übergehen und dem Widerspruche nicht entnommen. Die mehrern Sätze, die als absolute Denkgesetze aufgestellt werden, sind daher, näher betrachtet, einander entgegengesetzt, sie widersprechen einander und heben sich gegenseitig auf.—Wenn Alles identisch mit sich ist, so ist es nicht verschieden, nicht entgegengesetzt, hat keinen Grund. Oder wenn angenommen wird, es giebt nicht zwei gleiche Dinge d. h. Alles ist von einander verschieden, so ist A nicht gleich A, so ist A auch nicht entgegengesetzt u.s.f. Die Annahme eines jeden von diesen Sätzen läßt die Annahme der andern nicht zu.—Die gedankenlose Betrachtung derselben zählt sie nach einander auf, so daß sie in keiner Beziehung auf einander erscheinen; sie hat bloß ihr Reflektirtseyn in sich im Sinne, ohne ihr anderes Moment, das Gesetztseyn oder ihre Bestimmtheit als solche zu beachten, welche sie in den Übergang und in ihre Negation fortreiBt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0001","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Die Wesenheiten oder die Reflexions-Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"109.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0002","text":"Die Reflexion ist bestimmte Reflexion; somit ist das Wesen bestimmtes Wesen, oder es ist Wesenheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"109.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0003","text":"Die Reflexion ist das Scheinen des Wesens in sich selbst. Das Wesen als unendliche Rückkehr in sich ist nicht unmittelbare, sondern negative Einfachheit; es ist eine Bewegung durch unterschiedene Momente, absolute Vermittelung mit sich. Aber es scheint in diese seine Momente; sie sind daher selbst in sich reflektirte Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"109.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0004","text":"Das Wesen ist zuerst einfache Beziehung auf sich selbst; reine Identität. Dieß ist seine Bestimmung, nach der es vielmehr Bestimmungslosigkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"109.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0005","text":"Zweitens die eigentliche Bestimmung ist der Unterschied; und zwar theils als äußerlicher oder gleichgültiger Unterschied, die Verschiedenheit überhaupt; theils aber als entgegengesetzte Verschiedenheit oder als Gegensatz.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"109.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0006","text":"Drittens als Widerspruch reflektirt sich der Gegensatz in sich selbst und geht in seinen Grund zurück.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"109.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0007","text":"## Anmerkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"109.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0008","text":"Die Reflexions-Bestimmungen pflegten sonst in die Form von Sätzen aufgenommen zu werden, worin von ihnen ausgesagt wurde, daß sie von Allem gelten. Diese Sätze galten als die allgemeinen Denkgesetze, die allem Denken zum Grunde liegen, an ihnen selbst absolut und unbeweisbar seyen, aber von jedem Denken, wie es ihren Sinn fasse, unmittelbar und unwidersprochen als wahr anerkannt und angenommen werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"109.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0009","text":"So wird die wesentliche Bestimmung der Identität in dem Satze ausgesprochen: Alles ist sich selbst gleich; A=A. Oder negativ: A kann nicht zugleich A und nicht A seyn. Es ist zunächst nicht abzusehen, warum nur diese einfachen Bestimmungen der Reflexion in diese besondere Form gefaßt werden sollen, und nicht auch die andern Kategorien, wie alle Bestimmtheiten der Sphäre des Seyns. Es ergäben sich die Sätze z.B. Alles ist, Alles hat ein Daseyn u.s.f. oder Alles hat eine Qualität, Quantität u.s.w. Denn Seyn, Daseyn u.s.f. sind als logische Bestimmungen überhaupt Prädikate von Allem.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"109.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0010","text":"Die Kategorie ist ihrer Etymologie und der Definition des Aristoteles nach, dasjenige, was von dem Seyenden gesagt, behauptet wird.—Allein eine Bestimmtheit des Seyns ist wesentlich ein Übergehen ins Entgegengesetzte; die negative einer jeden Bestimmtheit ist so nothwendig als sie selbst; als unmittelbaren Bestimmtheiten steht jeder die andere unmittelbar gegenüber. Wenn diese Kategorien daher in solche Sätze gefaßt werden, so kommen ebenso sehr die entgegengesetzten Sätze zum Vorschein; beide bieten sich mit gleicher Nothwendigkeit dar, und haben als unmittelbare Behauptungen wenigstens gleiches Recht. Der eine erforderte dadurch einen Beweis gegen den andern, und diesen Behauptungen könnte daher nicht mehr der Charakter von unmittelbar wahren und unwidersprechlichen Sätzen des Denkens zukommen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"109.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0011","text":"Die Reflexions-Bestimmungen dagegen sind nicht von qualitativer Art. Sie sind sich auf sich beziehende und damit der Bestimmtheit gegen Anderes zugleich entnommene Bestimmungen. Ferner indem es Bestimmtheiten sind, welche Beziehungen an sich selbst sind, so enthalten sie insofern die Form des Satzes schon in sich. Denn der Satz unterscheidet sich vom Urtheil vornehmlich dadurch, daß in jenem der Inhalt die Beziehung selbst ausmacht, oder daß er eine bestimmte Beziehung ist. Das Urtheil dagegen verlegt den Inhalt in das Prädikat, als eine allgemeine Bestimmtheit, die für sich und von ihrer Beziehung, der einfachen Copula, unterschieden ist. Wenn ein Satz in ein Urtheil verwandelt werden soll, so wird der bestimmte Inhalt, wenn er z.B. in einem Zeitworte liegt, in ein Particip verwandelt, um auf diese Art die Bestimmung selbst und ihre Beziehung auf ein Subjekt zu trennen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"109.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0012","text":"Den Reflexions-Bestimmungen dagegen als in sich reflektirtem Gesetztseyn liegt die Form des Satzes selbst nahe.—Allein indem sie als allgemeine Denkgesetze ausgesprochen werden, so bedürfen sie noch eines Subjekts ihrer Beziehung, und dieß Subjekt ist: Alles; oder ein A, was ebenso viel als Alles und Jedes Seyn bedeutet.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"109.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0013","text":"Eines Theils ist diese Form von Sätzen etwas Überflüssiges; die Reflexions-Bestimmungen sind an und für sich zu betrachten. Ferner haben diese Sätze die schiefe Seite, das Seyn, Alles Etwas, zum Subjekte zu haben. Sie erwecken damit das Seyn wieder, und sprechen die Reflexions-Bestimmungen, die Identität u.s.f. von dem Etwas als eine Qualität aus, die es an ihm habe; nicht in spekulativem Sinne, sondern daß Etwas als Subjekt in einer solchen Qualität bleibe als seyendes, nicht daß es in die Identität u.s.f. als in seine Wahrheit und sein Wesen übergegangen sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"109.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0014","text":"Endlich aber haben die Reflexions-Bestimmungen zwar die Form sich selbst gleich und daher unbezogen auf Anderes und ohne Entgegensetzung zu seyn; aber wie sich aus ihrer nähern Betrachtung ergeben wird,—oder wie unmittelbar an ihnen, als der Identität, der Verschiedenheit, der Entgegensetzung erhellt—sind sie bestimmte gegen einander, sie sind also durch ihre Form der Reflexion, dem Übergehen und dem Widerspruche nicht entnommen. Die mehrern Sätze, die als absolute Denkgesetze aufgestellt werden, sind daher, näher betrachtet, einander entgegengesetzt, sie widersprechen einander und heben sich gegenseitig auf.—Wenn Alles identisch mit sich ist, so ist es nicht verschieden, nicht entgegengesetzt, hat keinen Grund. Oder wenn angenommen wird, es giebt nicht zwei gleiche Dinge d. h. Alles ist von einander verschieden, so ist A nicht gleich A, so ist A auch nicht entgegengesetzt u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"109.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0015","text":"Die Annahme eines jeden von diesen Sätzen läßt die Annahme der andern nicht zu.—Die gedankenlose Betrachtung derselben zählt sie nach einander auf, so daß sie in keiner Beziehung auf einander erscheinen; sie hat bloß ihr Reflektirtseyn in sich im Sinne, ohne ihr anderes Moment, das Gesetztseyn oder ihre Bestimmtheit als solche zu beachten, welche sie in den Übergang und in ihre Negation fortreiBt.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"109.15"}],"sha256":"78852cc8162be8b3d349abee0ae8b7e81a41c97f321216525941522396988716","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104703207910Z_80477e9e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"78852cc8162be8b3d349abee0ae8b7e81a41c97f321216525941522396988716","sha256":"445e71ce3cc4ab575780d283a480e1fde9699506ddc1b705e1eb1a8869fba52b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:47:03.207980+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0001","text":"## Second Chapter. The Essentialities, or the Determinations of Reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"109.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0002","text":"Reflection is determinate reflection; thus essence is determinate essence, or it is essentiality.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"109.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0003","text":"Reflection is the shining of essence within itself. Essence, as infinite return into itself, is not immediate but negative simplicity; it is a movement through distinct moments, absolute mediation with itself. But it shines into these its moments; they are therefore themselves determinations reflected into themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"109.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0004","text":"Essence is at first simple relation to itself; pure identity. This is its determination, according to which it is rather determinatenesslessness.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"109.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0005","text":"Secondly, determination proper is difference; namely, partly as external or indifferent difference, diversity in general; partly, however, as opposed diversity or as opposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"109.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0006","text":"Thirdly, as contradiction, opposition reflects itself into itself and goes back into its ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"109.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0007","text":"## Note.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"109.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0008","text":"The determinations of reflection used formerly to be taken up in the form of propositions, in which it was asserted of them that they hold of everything. These propositions were regarded as the universal laws of thought, which underlie all thinking, are in themselves absolute and incapable of proof, but are immediately and uncontradictedly recognized and accepted as true by every thinking, insofar as it apprehends their sense.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"109.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0009","text":"Thus the essential determination of identity is expressed in the proposition: Everything is equal to itself; A=A. Or negatively: A cannot at the same time be A and not-A. It is not initially apparent why only these simple determinations of reflection should be cast into this particular form, and not also the other categories, such as all determinatenesses of the sphere of Being. There would result, for example, the propositions: Everything is, Everything has an existence, etc.; or Everything has a quality, quantity, etc. For Being, existence, etc., as logical determinations in general, are predicates of everything.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"109.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0010","text":"According to its etymology and Aristotle's definition, the category is that which is said, asserted, of what is.―But a determinateness of Being is essentially a transition into the opposite; the negative of every determinateness is as necessary as it itself; as immediate determinatenesses, each has the other immediately confronting it. If these categories are therefore cast into such propositions, the opposite propositions likewise come to light; both present themselves with equal necessity, and, as immediate assertions, have at least equal right. The one would thereby require a proof against the other, and these assertions could therefore no longer possess the character of immediately true and uncontradicted propositions of thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"109.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0011","text":"The determinations of reflection, on the other hand, are not of a qualitative kind. They are determinations relating themselves to themselves and thereby at the same time withdrawn from determinateness over against another. Further, since they are determinatenesses which are relations in themselves, they thus already contain the form of the proposition within themselves. For the proposition differs from the judgment chiefly in that, in the former, the content itself constitutes the relation, or that it is a determinate relation. The judgment, on the other hand, places the content in the predicate, as a universal determinateness which is distinct for itself and from its relation, the simple copula. If a proposition is to be transformed into a judgment, the determinate content, when it lies, for example, in a verb, is transformed into a participle, in order in this way to separate the determination itself and its relation to a subject.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"109.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0012","text":"To the determinations of reflection, on the other hand, as positedness reflected into itself, the form of the proposition itself lies close at hand.―But inasmuch as they are expressed as universal laws of thought, they still require a subject of their relation, and this subject is: Everything; or an A, which means as much as Everything and Each.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"109.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0013","text":"On the one hand, this form of propositions is something superfluous; the determinations of reflection are to be considered in and for themselves. Further, these propositions have the oblique aspect of having Being, Everything, Something, as their subject. Thereby they reawaken Being, and express the determinations of reflection, identity, etc., of Something as a quality which it has in it; not in the speculative sense, but such that Something remains as subject in such a quality, as being, not such that it has passed over into identity, etc., as into its truth and its essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"109.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0014","text":"Finally, however, the determinations of reflection do indeed have the form of being equal to themselves and hence unrelated to another and without opposition; but, as will emerge from their closer consideration—or as is immediately evident in them, as identity, diversity, opposition—they are determinate against one another; they are thus not withdrawn, through their form of reflection, from transition and contradiction. The several propositions which are set up as absolute laws of thought are therefore, more closely considered, opposed to one another; they contradict one another and mutually sublate one another.—If everything is identical with itself, then it is not diverse, not opposed, has no ground. Or if it is assumed that there are no two equal things, i.e. everything is diverse from everything else, then A is not equal to A, so A is also not opposed, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"109.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_26:P0015","text":"The assumption of each one of these propositions does not admit the assumption of the others.—Thoughtless consideration of them enumerates them one after another, so that they appear to stand in no relation to one another; it has in mind merely their being reflected into themselves, without attending to their other moment, positedness or their determinateness as such, which carries them forward into transition and into their negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"109.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_26:P0015"]}],"source_digest":"0c79a29ca7370cd3fda4c8cbb391ab852c39ec38af760307c0431b4b390047c3","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0","title":"A. Identity.","order":110,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DIT0","text":"1. Das Wesen ist die einfache Unmittelbarkeit als aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit. Seine Negativität ist sein Seyn; es ist sich selbst gleich in seiner absoluten Negativität, durch die das Andersseyn und die Beziehung auf Anderes schlechthin an sich selbst in die reine Sichselbstgleichheit verschwunden ist. Das Wesen ist also einfache Identität mit sich.\n\nDiese Identität mit sich ist die Unmittelbarkeit der Reflexion. Sie ist nicht diejenige Gleichheit mit sich, welche das Seyn oder auch das Nichts ist, sondern die Gleichheit mit sich, welche als sich zur Einheit herstellende ist, nicht ein Wiederherstellen aus einem Andern, sondern dieß reine Herstellen aus und in sich selbst; die wesentliche Identität. Sie ist insofern nicht abstrakte Identität, oder nicht durch ein relatives Negiren entstanden, das außerhalb ihrer vorgegangen wäre, und das Unterschiedene nur von ihr abgetrennt, übrigens aber dasselbe außer ihr als seyend gelassen hätte, vor wie nach. Sondern das Seyn und alle Bestimmtheit des Seyns hat sich nicht relativ, sondern an sich selbst aufgehoben; und diese einfache Negativität, des Seyns an sich, ist die Identität selbst.\n\nSie ist insofern noch überhaupt dasselbe, als das Wesen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0001","text":"1. Das Wesen ist die einfache Unmittelbarkeit als aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit. Seine Negativität ist sein Seyn; es ist sich selbst gleich in seiner absoluten Negativität, durch die das Andersseyn und die Beziehung auf Anderes schlechthin an sich selbst in die reine Sichselbstgleichheit verschwunden ist. Das Wesen ist also einfache Identität mit sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"110.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0002","text":"Diese Identität mit sich ist die Unmittelbarkeit der Reflexion. Sie ist nicht diejenige Gleichheit mit sich, welche das Seyn oder auch das Nichts ist, sondern die Gleichheit mit sich, welche als sich zur Einheit herstellende ist, nicht ein Wiederherstellen aus einem Andern, sondern dieß reine Herstellen aus und in sich selbst; die wesentliche Identität. Sie ist insofern nicht abstrakte Identität, oder nicht durch ein relatives Negiren entstanden, das außerhalb ihrer vorgegangen wäre, und das Unterschiedene nur von ihr abgetrennt, übrigens aber dasselbe außer ihr als seyend gelassen hätte, vor wie nach. Sondern das Seyn und alle Bestimmtheit des Seyns hat sich nicht relativ, sondern an sich selbst aufgehoben; und diese einfache Negativität, des Seyns an sich, ist die Identität selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"110.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0003","text":"Sie ist insofern noch überhaupt dasselbe, als das Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"110.3"}],"sha256":"ede1c39f19e011277df8202040630f3fbafab85a20e0093b84ee080d0f12f02d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104706908343Z_a4970641","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Identity.","source_sha256":"ede1c39f19e011277df8202040630f3fbafab85a20e0093b84ee080d0f12f02d","sha256":"12ae85299b492b314193474cc06e8408975b64587e8a991c0254dd92a4fc0e47","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:47:06.908354+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0001","text":"1. Essence is simple immediacy as sublated immediacy. Its negativity is its being; it is equal to itself in its absolute negativity, through which other-being and relation to an other have, absolutely in themselves, vanished into pure self-equality. Essence is thus simple identity with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"110.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0002","text":"This identity with itself is the immediacy of reflection. It is not that equality with itself which being, or also nothing, is, but the equality with itself which, as bringing itself forth into unity, is not a restoration from an other, but this pure bringing-forth out of and into itself; essential identity. It is therefore not abstract identity, or one that has arisen through a relative negating which would have proceeded outside it, and which would merely have separated the differentiated from it, while otherwise leaving it, as being, outside it, as before and after. Rather, being and all determinacy of being have sublated themselves not relatively but in themselves; and this simple negativity, of being in itself, is identity itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"110.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0003","text":"In this respect it is still altogether the same as essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"110.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DIT0:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"2c299a1878e026ec3603942824c5c5b665492f62f437c951ed7972e1240b090b","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Die Identität."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Die Identität.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27","title":"Remark 1.","order":111,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_27","text":"Das Denken, das sich in der äußern Reflexion hält, und von keinem andern Denken weiß, als der äußern Reflexion, kommt nicht dazu, die Identität wie sie so eben gefaßt worden ist, oder das Wesen, was dasselbe ist, zu erkennen. Solches Denken hat immer nur die abstrakte Identität vor sich, und außer und neben derselben den Unterschied. Es meint, die Vernunft sey weiter nichts als ein Webstuhl, auf dem sie den Zettel, etwa die Identität, und dann den Eintrag, den Unterschied, äußerlich mit einander verbinde und verschlinge; oder auch wieder analysirend jetzt die Identität besonders herausziehe, und dann auch wieder den Unterschied daneben erhalte, jetzt ein Gleichsetzen, und dann auch wieder ein Ungleichsetzen sey;—ein Gleichsetzen, indem man vom Unterschiede, —ein Ungleichsetzen, indem man vom Gleichsetzen abstrahire.—Man muß diese Versicherungen und Meinungen von dem, was die Vernunft thue, ganz bei Seite gestellt lassen, indem sie gewissermassen bloß historische sind, und vielmehr die Betrachtung von Allem, was ist, an ihm selbst zeigt, daß es in seiner Gleichheit mit sich sich ungleich und widersprechend, und in seiner Verschiedenheit, in seinem Widerspruche, mit sich identisch, und an ihm selbst, diese Bewegung des Übergehens einer dieser Bestimmungen in die andere ist, und dieß darum, weil jede an ihr selbst das Gegentheil ihrer selbst ist. Der Begriff der Identität, einfache sich auf sich beziehende Negativität zu seyn, ist nicht ein Produkt der äußern Reflexion, sondern hat sich an dem Seyn selbst ergeben. Da hingegen jene Identität, die außer dem Unterschied, und der Unterschied, der außer der Identität sey, Produkte der äußern Reflexion und der Abstraktion sind, die sich willkürlicher Weise auf diesem Punkte der gleichgültigen Verschiedenheit festhält.\n\n2. Diese Identität ist zunächst das Wesen selbst, noch keine Bestimmung desselben; die ganze Reflexion, nicht ein unterschiedenes Moment derselben. Als absolute Negation ist sie die Negation, die unmittelbar sich selbst negirt; ein Nichtseyn und Unterschied, der in seinem Entstehen verschwindet, oder ein Unterscheiden, wodurch nichts unterschieden wird, sondern das unmittelbar in sich selbst zusammenfällt. Das Unterscheiden ist das Setzen des Nichtseyns, als des Nichtseyns des Andern. Aber das Nichtseyn des Andern ist Aufheben des Andern, und somit des Unterscheidens selbst. So ist aber das Unterscheiden hier vorhanden, als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, als ein Nichtseyn, das das Nichtseyn seiner selbst ist; ein Nichtseyn, das sein Nichtseyn nicht an einem andern, sondern an sich selbst hat. Es ist also der sich auf sich beziehende, der reflektirte Unterschied vorhanden, oder reine, absolute Unterschied.\n\nOder die Identität ist die Reflexion in sich selbst, welche dieß nur ist, als innerliches Abstoßen, und dieß Abstoßen ist es als Reflexion in sich, unmittelbar sich in sich zurücknehmendes Abstoßen. Sie ist somit die Identität als der mit sich identische Unterschied. Der Unterschied ist aber nur identisch mit sich, insofern er nicht die Identität, sondern absolute Nichtidentität ist. Absolut aber ist die Nichtidentität, insofern sie nichts von ihr Anderes enthält, sondern nur sich selbst, das heißt, insofern sie absolute Identität mit sich ist.\n\nDie Identität ist also an ihr selbst absolute Nichtidentität. Aber sie ist auch die Bestimmung der Identität dagegen. Denn als Reflexion in sich setzt sie sich als ihr eigenes Nichtseyn; sie ist das Ganze, aber als Reflexion setzt sie sich als ihr eigenes Moment, als Gesetztseyn, aus welchem sie die Rückkehr in sich ist. So als ihr Moment ist sie erst die Identität als solche als Bestimmung der einfachen Gleichheit mit sich selbst, gegen den absoluten Unterschied.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0001","text":"Das Denken, das sich in der äußern Reflexion hält, und von keinem andern Denken weiß, als der äußern Reflexion, kommt nicht dazu, die Identität wie sie so eben gefaßt worden ist, oder das Wesen, was dasselbe ist, zu erkennen. Solches Denken hat immer nur die abstrakte Identität vor sich, und außer und neben derselben den Unterschied.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"111.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0002","text":"Es meint, die Vernunft sey weiter nichts als ein Webstuhl, auf dem sie den Zettel, etwa die Identität, und dann den Eintrag, den Unterschied, äußerlich mit einander verbinde und verschlinge; oder auch wieder analysirend jetzt die Identität besonders herausziehe, und dann auch wieder den Unterschied daneben erhalte, jetzt ein Gleichsetzen, und dann auch wieder ein Ungleichsetzen sey;—ein Gleichsetzen, indem man vom Unterschiede, —ein Ungleichsetzen, indem man vom Gleichsetzen abstrahire.—Man muß diese Versicherungen und Meinungen von dem, was die Vernunft thue, ganz bei Seite gestellt lassen, indem sie gewissermassen bloß historische sind, und vielmehr die Betrachtung von Allem, was ist, an ihm selbst zeigt, daß es in seiner Gleichheit mit sich sich ungleich und widersprechend, und in seiner Verschiedenheit, in seinem Widerspruche, mit sich identisch, und an ihm selbst, diese Bewegung","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"111.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0003","text":"des Übergehens einer dieser Bestimmungen in die andere ist, und dieß darum, weil jede an ihr selbst das Gegentheil ihrer selbst ist. Der Begriff der Identität, einfache sich auf sich beziehende Negativität zu seyn, ist nicht ein Produkt der äußern Reflexion, sondern hat sich an dem Seyn selbst ergeben. Da hingegen jene Identität, die außer dem Unterschied, und der Unterschied, der außer der Identität sey, Produkte der äußern Reflexion und der Abstraktion sind, die sich willkürlicher Weise auf diesem Punkte der gleichgültigen Verschiedenheit festhält.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"111.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0004","text":"2. Diese Identität ist zunächst das Wesen selbst, noch keine Bestimmung desselben; die ganze Reflexion, nicht ein unterschiedenes Moment derselben. Als absolute Negation ist sie die Negation, die unmittelbar sich selbst negirt; ein Nichtseyn und Unterschied, der in seinem Entstehen verschwindet, oder ein Unterscheiden, wodurch nichts unterschieden wird, sondern das unmittelbar in sich selbst zusammenfällt. Das Unterscheiden ist das Setzen des Nichtseyns, als des Nichtseyns des Andern. Aber das Nichtseyn des Andern ist Aufheben des Andern, und somit des Unterscheidens selbst. So ist aber das Unterscheiden hier vorhanden, als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, als ein Nichtseyn, das das Nichtseyn seiner selbst ist; ein Nichtseyn, das sein Nichtseyn nicht an einem andern, sondern an sich selbst hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"111.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0005","text":"Es ist also der sich auf sich beziehende, der reflektirte Unterschied vorhanden, oder reine, absolute Unterschied.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"111.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0006","text":"Oder die Identität ist die Reflexion in sich selbst, welche dieß nur ist, als innerliches Abstoßen, und dieß Abstoßen ist es als Reflexion in sich, unmittelbar sich in sich zurücknehmendes Abstoßen. Sie ist somit die Identität als der mit sich identische Unterschied. Der Unterschied ist aber nur identisch mit sich, insofern er nicht die Identität, sondern absolute Nichtidentität ist. Absolut aber ist die Nichtidentität, insofern sie nichts von ihr Anderes enthält, sondern nur sich selbst, das heißt, insofern sie absolute Identität mit sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"111.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0007","text":"Die Identität ist also an ihr selbst absolute Nichtidentität. Aber sie ist auch die Bestimmung der Identität dagegen. Denn als Reflexion in sich setzt sie sich als ihr eigenes Nichtseyn; sie ist das Ganze, aber als Reflexion setzt sie sich als ihr eigenes Moment, als Gesetztseyn, aus welchem sie die Rückkehr in sich ist. So als ihr Moment ist sie erst die Identität als solche als Bestimmung der einfachen Gleichheit mit sich selbst, gegen den absoluten Unterschied.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"111.7"}],"sha256":"ba4f085c00528e93cb35b49a02314c9ed52f8194a805c373c5c5c256a48e26a1","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104714694309Z_489a1553","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"ba4f085c00528e93cb35b49a02314c9ed52f8194a805c373c5c5c256a48e26a1","sha256":"b7a82a610b912b33a66c393a0cf49c24b87ac4f0fae446f6659a6dbfca9298bc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:47:14.694336+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0001","text":"Thought that remains within external reflection, and knows no thought other than external reflection, does not arrive at cognizing identity as it has just been apprehended, or essence, which is the same thing. Such thought always has before it only abstract identity, and, outside and alongside it, difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"111.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0002","text":"It imagines that reason is nothing further than a loom, upon which it externally connects and interweaves the warp, say identity, and then the weft, difference; or again, analytically, now draws out identity separately, and then again retains difference alongside it; that it is now an equating, and then again a making-unequal;—an equating, insofar as one abstracts from difference,—a making-unequal, insofar as one abstracts from equating.—These assurances and opinions concerning what reason does must be set wholly aside, since they are in a certain respect merely historical; rather, the consideration of everything that is shows in itself that, in its equality with itself, it is unequal and contradictory, and, in its diversity, in its contradiction, identical with itself, and is, in itself, this movement","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"111.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0003","text":"of the transition of one of these determinations into the other, and this because each is in itself the opposite of itself. The concept of identity, of being simple negativity relating itself to itself, is not a product of external reflection, but has emerged in being itself. Whereas that identity which is outside difference, and that difference which is outside identity, are products of external reflection and abstraction, which arbitrarily holds fast at this point of indifferent diversity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"111.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0004","text":"2. This identity is at first essence itself, as yet no determination of it; the whole of reflection, not a distinct moment of it. As absolute negation, it is the negation that immediately negates itself; a non-being and difference that vanishes in its arising, or a distinguishing through which nothing is distinguished, but which immediately collapses into itself. Distinguishing is the positing of non-being, as the non-being of the other. But the non-being of the other is the sublation of the other, and hence of distinguishing itself. Thus, however, distinguishing is present here as negativity relating itself to itself, as a non-being that is the non-being of itself; a non-being that has its non-being not in another, but in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"111.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0005","text":"Thus there is present difference relating itself to itself, reflected difference, or pure, absolute difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"111.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0006","text":"Or identity is reflection into itself, which is this only as inner repulsion, and this repulsion is it as reflection into itself, repulsion immediately taking itself back into itself. It is thus identity as difference identical with itself. But difference is identical with itself only insofar as it is not identity, but absolute non-identity. Yet non-identity is absolute insofar as it contains nothing other than itself, but only itself; that is, insofar as it is absolute identity with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"111.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_27:P0007","text":"Identity is therefore in itself absolute non-identity. But it is also, as against this, the determination of identity. For as reflection into itself, it posits itself as its own non-being; it is the whole, but as reflection it posits itself as its own moment, as positedness, from which it is the return into itself. Thus, as its moment, it is only then identity as such, as the determination of simple equality with itself, over against absolute difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"111.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_27:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"d9b05d496ecb004b7ba728f97d05eeded3c55491cb57599643277101fffc0abc","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28","title":"Remark 2.","order":112,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_28","text":"Ich werde in dieser Anmerkung die Identität als den Satz der Identität näher betrachten, der als das erste Denkgesetz aufgeführt zu werden pflegt.\n\nDieser Satz in seinem positiven Ausdrucke A=A, ist zunächst nichts weiter, als der Ausdruck der leeren Tautologie. Es ist daher richtig bemerkt worden, daß dieses Denkgesetz ohne Inhalt sey und nicht weiter führe. So ist die leere Identität, an welcher diejenigen festhangen bleiben, welche sie als solche für etwas Wahres nehmen und immer vorzubringen pflegen, die Identität sey nicht die Verschiedenheit, sondern die Identität und die Verschiedenheit seyen verschieden. Sie sehen nicht, daß sie schon hierin selbst sagen, daß die Identität ein Verschiedenes ist; denn sie sagen, die Identität sey verschieden von der Verschiedenheit; indem dieß zugleich als die Natur der Identität zugegeben werden muß, so liegt darin, daß die Identität nicht äußerlich, sondern an ihr selbst, in ihrer Natur dieß sey, verschieden zu seyn.—Ferner aber indem sie an dieser unbewegten Identität festhalten, welche ihren Gegensatz an der Verschiedenheit hat, so sehen sie nicht, daß sie hiermit dieselbe zu einer einseitigen Bestimmtheit machen, die als solche keine Wahrheit hat. Es wird zugegeben, daß der Satz der Identität nur eine einseitige Bestimmtheit ausdrücke, daß er nur die formelle eine abstrakte, unvollständige Wahrheit enthalte.—In diesem richtigen Urtheil liegt aber unmittelbar, daß die Wahrheit nur in der Einheit der Identität mit der Verschiedenheit vollständig ist, und somit nur in dieser Einheit bestehe. Indem behauptet wird, daß jene Identität unvollkommen ist, so schwebt diese Totalität, an der gemessen die Identität unvollkommen ist, als das Vollkommene dem Gedanken vor; indem aber auf der andern Seite die Identität als absolut getrennt von der Verschiedenheit festgehalten und in dieser Trennung als ein Wesentliches, Geltendes, Wahres genommen wird, so ist in diesen widerstreitenden Behauptungen nichts zu sehen, als der Mangel, diese Gedanken, daß die Identität als abstrakte wesentlich, und daß sie als solche ebenso unvollkommen ist, zusammenzubringen; der Mangel des Bewußtseyns über die negative Bewegung, als welche in diesen Behauptungen die Identität selbst dargestellt wird.—Oder indem sich so ausgedrückt wird, die Identität sey wesentliche Identität als Trennung von der Verschiedenheit, oder in der Trennung von der Verschiedenheit, so ist dieß unmittelbar die ausgesprochene Wahrheit derselben, daß sie darin besteht, Trennung als solche zu seyn, oder in der Trennung wesentlich, das ist, nichts für sich, sondern Moment der Trennung zu seyn.\n\nWas nun die sonstige Beglaubigung der absoluten Wahrheit des Satzes der Identität betrifft, so wird sie insofern auf die Erfahrung gegründet, als sich auf die Erfahrung jedes Bewußtseyns berufen wird, daß es, wie man ihm diesen Satz, A ist A, ein Baum ist ein Baum, ausspreche, es denselben unmittelbar zugebe und darin befriedigt sey, daß der Satz als unmittelbar klar durch sich selbst, keiner andern Begründung und Beweises bedürfe.\n\nEines Theils ist diese Berufung auf die Erfahrung, daß allgemein jedes Bewußtseyn ihn anerkenne, bloße Redensart. Denn man will nicht sagen, daß man das Experiment mit dem abstrakten Satze A=A an jedem Bewußtseyn gemacht habe. Es ist insofern weiter nicht Ernst mit jener Berufung auf wirklich gemachte Erfahrung, sondern sie ist nur die Versicherung, daß wenn man die Erfahrung machte, sich das Resultat des allgemeinen Anerkennens ergeben würde.—Wäre aber nicht der abstrakte Satz als solcher, sondern der Satz in konkreter Anwendung gemeint, aus der jener erst entwickelt werden sollte, so bestünde die Behauptung von seiner Allgemeinheit und Unmittelbarkeit darin, daß jedes Bewußtseyn, und selbst in jeder seiner Äußerungen ihn zu Grunde lege, oder daß er implicite in jeder liege. Allein das Konkrete und die Anwendung ist ja eben die Beziehung des einfachen Identischen auf ein von ihm verschiedenes Mannigfaltiges. Als Satz ausgedrückt, wäre das Konkrete zunächst ein synthetischer Satz. Aus dem Konkreten selbst oder seinem synthetischen Satze würde die Abstraktion den Satz der Identität wohl durch Analyse herausbringen können; aber in der That hätte sie die Erfahrung nicht gelassen wie sie ist, sondern verändert; denn die Erfahrung enthielt vielmehr die Identität in Einheit mit der Verschiedenheit, und ist die unmittelbare Widerlegung von der Behauptung, daß die abstrakte Identität als solche etwas Wahres sey, denn das gerade Gegentheil, nämlich die Identität nur vereinigt mit der Verschiedenheit, kommt in jeder Erfahrung vor.\n\nAuf der andern Seite wird aber auch die Erfahrung mit dem reinen Satze der Identität, nur zu oft, gemacht, und es zeigt sich in dieser Erfahrung klar genug, wie die Wahrheit, die er enthält, angesehen wird. Wenn nämlich z.B. auf die Frage: was ist eine Pflanze? die Antwort gegeben wird: eine Pflanze ist—eine Pflanze, so wird die Wahrheit eines solchen Satzes, von der ganzen Gesellschaft, an der sie erprobt wird, zugleich zugegeben, und zugleich ebenso einstimmig gesagt werden, daß damit Nichts gesagt ist. Wenn einer den Mund aufthut, und anzugeben verspricht, was Gott sey, nämlich Gott sey—Gott, so findet sich die Erwartung getäuscht, denn sie sah einer verschiedenen Bestimmung entgegen; und wenn dieser Satz absolute Wahrheit ist, wird solche absolute Rednerei sehr gering geachtet; es wird nichts für langweiliger und lästiger gehalten werden, als eine nur dasselbe wiederkäuende Unterhaltung, als solches Reden, das doch Wahrheit seyn soll.\n\nNäher diese Wirkung der Langeweile bei solcher Wahrheit betrachtet, so macht der Anfang: die Pflanze ist—, Anstalten etwas zu sagen, eine weitere Bestimmung vorzubringen. Indem aber nur dasselbe wiederkehrt, so ist vielmehr das Gegentheil geschehen, es ist Nichts herausgekommen. Solches identische Reden widerspricht sich also selbst. Die Identität, statt an ihr die Wahrheit und absolute Wahrheit zu seyn, ist daher vielmehr das Gegentheil; statt das unbewegte Einfache zu seyn, ist sie das Hinausgehen über sich in die Auflösung ihrer selbst.\n\nEs liegt also in der Form des Satzes, in der die Identität ausgedrückt ist, mehr als die einfache, abstrakte Identität; es liegt diese reine Bewegung der Reflexion darin, in der das Andere nur als Schein, als unmittelbares Verschwinden auftritt; A ist, ist ein Beginnen, dem ein Verschiedenes vorschwebt, zu dem hinausgegangen werde; aber es kommt nicht zu dem Verschiedenen; A ist—A: die Verschiedenheit ist nur ein Verschwinden; die Bewegung geht in sich selbst zurück.—Die Form des Satzes kann als die verborgene Nothwendigkeit angesehen werden, noch das Mehr jener Bewegung zu der abstrakten Identität hinzuzufügen.—So kommt auch ein A, oder eine Pflanze oder sonst ein Substrat hinzu, das als ein unnützer Inhalt keine Bedeutung hat; aber er macht die Verschiedenheit aus, die sich zufälligerweise beizugesellen scheint. Wenn statt des A und jedes andern Substrats, die Identität selbst genommen wird,—die Identität ist die Identität,—so ist ebenso zugegeben, daß statt dieser gleichfalls jedes andere Substrat genommen werden könne. Wenn sich daher einmal darauf berufen werden soll, was die Erscheinung zeigt, so zeigt sie dieß, daß in dem Ausdrucke der Identität auch unmmittelbar die Verschiedenheit vorkommt;—oder bestimmter nach dem Obigen, daß diese Identität das Nichts, daß sie die Negativität, der absolute Unterschied von sich selbst ist.\n\nDer andre Ausdruck des Satzes der Identität: A kann nicht zugleich A und Nicht-A seyn, hat negative Form; er heißt der Satz des Widerspruchs. Es pflegt darüber, wie die Form der Negation, wodurch sich dieser Satz vom vorigen unterscheidet, an die Identität komme, keine Rechtfertigung gegeben zu werden.—Diese Form liegt aber darin, daß die Identität als die reine Bewegung der Reflexion, die einfache Negativität ist, welche der angeführte zweite Ausdruck des Satzes entwickelter enthält. Es ist A ausgesprochen und ein Nicht-A, das Rein-Andre des A, aber es zeigt sich nur um zu verschwinden. Die Identität ist also in diesem Satze ausgedrückt,—als Negation der Negation. A und Nicht-A, sind unterschieden, diese unterschiedenen sind auf ein und dasselbe A bezogen. Die Identität ist also als diese Unterschiedenheit in Einer Beziehung oder als der einfache Unterschied an ihnen selbst hier dargestellt.\n\nEs erhellt hieraus, daß der Satz der Identität selbst und noch mehr der Satz des Widerspruchs nicht bloß analytischer, sondern synthetischer Natur ist. Denn der letztere enthält in seinem Ausdrucke nicht nur die leere, einfache Gleichheit mit sich, sondern nicht allein das Andere derselben überhaupt, sondern sogar die absolute Ungleichheit, den Widerspruch an sich. Der Satz der Identität selbst aber enthält, wie an ihm gezeigt wurde, die Reflexions-Bewegung, die Identität als Verschwinden des Andersseyns.\n\nWas sich also aus dieser Betrachtung ergiebt, ist, daß erstens der Satz der Identität oder des Widerspruchs, wie er nur die abstrakte Identität im Gegensatz gegen den Unterschied, als Wahres ausdrücken soll, kein Denkgesetz, sondern vielmehr das Gegentheil davon ist; zweitens, daß diese Sätze mehr, als mit ihnen gemeint wird, nämlich dieses Gegentheil, den absoluten Unterschied selbst, enthalten.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0001","text":"Ich werde in dieser Anmerkung die Identität als den Satz der Identität näher betrachten, der als das erste Denkgesetz aufgeführt zu werden pflegt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"112.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0002","text":"Dieser Satz in seinem positiven Ausdrucke A=A, ist zunächst nichts weiter, als der Ausdruck der leeren Tautologie. Es ist daher richtig bemerkt worden, daß dieses Denkgesetz ohne Inhalt sey und nicht weiter führe. So ist die leere Identität, an welcher diejenigen festhangen bleiben, welche sie als solche für etwas Wahres nehmen und immer vorzubringen pflegen, die Identität sey nicht die Verschiedenheit, sondern die Identität und die Verschiedenheit seyen verschieden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"112.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0003","text":"Sie sehen nicht, daß sie schon hierin selbst sagen, daß die Identität ein Verschiedenes ist; denn sie sagen, die Identität sey verschieden von der Verschiedenheit; indem dieß zugleich als die Natur der Identität zugegeben werden muß, so liegt darin, daß die Identität nicht äußerlich, sondern an ihr selbst, in ihrer Natur dieß sey, verschieden zu seyn.—Ferner aber indem sie an dieser unbewegten Identität festhalten, welche ihren Gegensatz an der Verschiedenheit hat, so sehen sie nicht, daß sie hiermit dieselbe zu einer einseitigen Bestimmtheit machen, die als solche keine Wahrheit hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"112.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0004","text":"Es wird zugegeben, daß der Satz der Identität nur eine einseitige Bestimmtheit ausdrücke, daß er nur die formelle eine abstrakte, unvollständige Wahrheit enthalte.—In diesem richtigen Urtheil liegt aber unmittelbar, daß die Wahrheit nur in der Einheit der Identität mit der Verschiedenheit vollständig ist, und somit nur in dieser Einheit bestehe.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"112.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0005","text":"Indem behauptet wird, daß jene Identität unvollkommen ist, so schwebt diese Totalität, an der gemessen die Identität unvollkommen ist, als das Vollkommene dem Gedanken vor; indem aber auf der andern Seite die Identität als absolut getrennt von der Verschiedenheit festgehalten und in dieser Trennung als ein Wesentliches, Geltendes, Wahres genommen wird, so ist in diesen widerstreitenden Behauptungen nichts zu sehen, als der Mangel, diese Gedanken, daß die Identität als abstrakte wesentlich, und daß sie als solche ebenso unvollkommen ist, zusammenzubringen; der Mangel des Bewußtseyns über die negative Bewegung, als welche in diesen Behauptungen die Identität selbst dargestellt wird.—Oder indem sich so ausgedrückt wird, die Identität sey wesentliche Identität als Trennung von der Verschiedenheit, oder in der Trennung von der Verschiedenheit, so ist dieß unmittelbar die ausgesprochene","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"112.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0006","text":"Wahrheit derselben, daß sie darin besteht, Trennung als solche zu seyn, oder in der Trennung wesentlich, das ist, nichts für sich, sondern Moment der Trennung zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"112.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0007","text":"Was nun die sonstige Beglaubigung der absoluten Wahrheit des Satzes der Identität betrifft, so wird sie insofern auf die Erfahrung gegründet, als sich auf die Erfahrung jedes Bewußtseyns berufen wird, daß es, wie man ihm diesen Satz, A ist A, ein Baum ist ein Baum, ausspreche, es denselben unmittelbar zugebe und darin befriedigt sey, daß der Satz als unmittelbar klar durch sich selbst, keiner andern Begründung und Beweises bedürfe.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"112.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0008","text":"Eines Theils ist diese Berufung auf die Erfahrung, daß allgemein jedes Bewußtseyn ihn anerkenne, bloße Redensart. Denn man will nicht sagen, daß man das Experiment mit dem abstrakten Satze A=A an jedem Bewußtseyn gemacht habe. Es ist insofern weiter nicht Ernst mit jener Berufung auf wirklich gemachte Erfahrung, sondern sie ist nur die Versicherung, daß wenn man die Erfahrung machte, sich das Resultat des allgemeinen Anerkennens ergeben würde.—Wäre aber nicht der abstrakte Satz als solcher, sondern der Satz in konkreter Anwendung gemeint, aus der jener erst entwickelt werden sollte, so bestünde die Behauptung von seiner Allgemeinheit und Unmittelbarkeit darin, daß jedes Bewußtseyn, und selbst in jeder seiner Äußerungen ihn zu Grunde lege, oder daß er implicite in jeder liege.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"112.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0009","text":"Allein das Konkrete und die Anwendung ist ja eben die Beziehung des einfachen Identischen auf ein von ihm verschiedenes Mannigfaltiges. Als Satz ausgedrückt, wäre das Konkrete zunächst ein synthetischer Satz. Aus dem Konkreten selbst oder seinem synthetischen Satze würde die Abstraktion den Satz der Identität wohl durch Analyse herausbringen können; aber in der That hätte sie die Erfahrung nicht gelassen wie sie ist, sondern verändert; denn die Erfahrung enthielt vielmehr die Identität in Einheit mit der Verschiedenheit, und ist die unmittelbare Widerlegung von der Behauptung, daß die abstrakte Identität als solche etwas Wahres sey, denn das gerade Gegentheil, nämlich die Identität nur vereinigt mit der Verschiedenheit, kommt in jeder Erfahrung vor.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"112.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0010","text":"Auf der andern Seite wird aber auch die Erfahrung mit dem reinen Satze der Identität, nur zu oft, gemacht, und es zeigt sich in dieser Erfahrung klar genug, wie die Wahrheit, die er enthält, angesehen wird. Wenn nämlich z.B. auf die Frage: was ist eine Pflanze? die Antwort gegeben wird: eine Pflanze ist—eine Pflanze, so wird die Wahrheit eines solchen Satzes, von der ganzen Gesellschaft, an der sie erprobt wird, zugleich zugegeben, und zugleich ebenso einstimmig gesagt werden, daß damit Nichts gesagt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"112.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0011","text":"Wenn einer den Mund aufthut, und anzugeben verspricht, was Gott sey, nämlich Gott sey—Gott, so findet sich die Erwartung getäuscht, denn sie sah einer verschiedenen Bestimmung entgegen; und wenn dieser Satz absolute Wahrheit ist, wird solche absolute Rednerei sehr gering geachtet; es wird nichts für langweiliger und lästiger gehalten werden, als eine nur dasselbe wiederkäuende Unterhaltung, als solches Reden, das doch Wahrheit seyn soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"112.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0012","text":"Näher diese Wirkung der Langeweile bei solcher Wahrheit betrachtet, so macht der Anfang: die Pflanze ist—, Anstalten etwas zu sagen, eine weitere Bestimmung vorzubringen. Indem aber nur dasselbe wiederkehrt, so ist vielmehr das Gegentheil geschehen, es ist Nichts herausgekommen. Solches identische Reden widerspricht sich also selbst. Die Identität, statt an ihr die Wahrheit und absolute Wahrheit zu seyn, ist daher vielmehr das Gegentheil; statt das unbewegte Einfache zu seyn, ist sie das Hinausgehen über sich in die Auflösung ihrer selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"112.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0013","text":"Es liegt also in der Form des Satzes, in der die Identität ausgedrückt ist, mehr als die einfache, abstrakte Identität; es liegt diese reine Bewegung der Reflexion darin, in der das Andere nur als Schein, als unmittelbares Verschwinden auftritt; A ist, ist ein Beginnen, dem ein Verschiedenes vorschwebt, zu dem hinausgegangen werde; aber es kommt nicht zu dem Verschiedenen; A ist—A: die Verschiedenheit ist nur ein Verschwinden; die Bewegung geht in sich selbst zurück.—Die Form des Satzes kann als die verborgene Nothwendigkeit angesehen werden, noch das Mehr jener Bewegung zu der abstrakten Identität hinzuzufügen.—So kommt auch ein A, oder eine Pflanze oder sonst ein Substrat hinzu, das als ein unnützer Inhalt keine Bedeutung hat; aber er macht die Verschiedenheit aus, die sich zufälligerweise beizugesellen scheint.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"112.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0014","text":"Wenn statt des A und jedes andern Substrats, die Identität selbst genommen wird,—die Identität ist die Identität,—so ist ebenso zugegeben, daß statt dieser gleichfalls jedes andere Substrat genommen werden könne. Wenn sich daher einmal darauf berufen werden soll, was die Erscheinung zeigt, so zeigt sie dieß, daß in dem Ausdrucke der Identität auch unmmittelbar die Verschiedenheit vorkommt;—oder bestimmter nach dem Obigen, daß diese Identität das Nichts, daß sie die Negativität, der absolute Unterschied von sich selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"112.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0015","text":"Der andre Ausdruck des Satzes der Identität: A kann nicht zugleich A und Nicht-A seyn, hat negative Form; er heißt der Satz des Widerspruchs. Es pflegt darüber, wie die Form der Negation, wodurch sich dieser Satz vom vorigen unterscheidet, an die Identität komme, keine Rechtfertigung gegeben zu werden.—Diese Form liegt aber darin, daß die Identität als die reine Bewegung der Reflexion, die einfache Negativität ist, welche der angeführte zweite Ausdruck des Satzes entwickelter enthält. Es ist A ausgesprochen und ein Nicht-A, das Rein-Andre des A, aber es zeigt sich nur um zu verschwinden. Die Identität ist also in diesem Satze ausgedrückt,—als Negation der Negation. A und Nicht-A, sind unterschieden, diese unterschiedenen sind auf ein und dasselbe A bezogen.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"112.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0016","text":"Die Identität ist also als diese Unterschiedenheit in Einer Beziehung oder als der einfache Unterschied an ihnen selbst hier dargestellt.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"112.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0017","text":"Es erhellt hieraus, daß der Satz der Identität selbst und noch mehr der Satz des Widerspruchs nicht bloß analytischer, sondern synthetischer Natur ist. Denn der letztere enthält in seinem Ausdrucke nicht nur die leere, einfache Gleichheit mit sich, sondern nicht allein das Andere derselben überhaupt, sondern sogar die absolute Ungleichheit, den Widerspruch an sich. Der Satz der Identität selbst aber enthält, wie an ihm gezeigt wurde, die Reflexions-Bewegung, die Identität als Verschwinden des Andersseyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"112.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0018","text":"Was sich also aus dieser Betrachtung ergiebt, ist, daß erstens der Satz der Identität oder des Widerspruchs, wie er nur die abstrakte Identität im Gegensatz gegen den Unterschied, als Wahres ausdrücken soll, kein Denkgesetz, sondern vielmehr das Gegentheil davon ist; zweitens, daß diese Sätze mehr, als mit ihnen gemeint wird, nämlich dieses Gegentheil, den absoluten Unterschied selbst, enthalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"112.18"}],"sha256":"2905b79cf25d5ac65edeb9e1f1ec68891b601a35c8603465ee12a7c9aeb6d80b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104731248523Z_d0818589","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"2905b79cf25d5ac65edeb9e1f1ec68891b601a35c8603465ee12a7c9aeb6d80b","sha256":"101470aa7beeba03573d5537277ea509fab0e775ef303110360bd67885e7aa0d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:47:31.248570+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0001","text":"In this note I shall consider identity more closely as the proposition of identity, which is customarily listed as the first law of thought.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"112.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0002","text":"This proposition in its positive expression A=A is initially nothing further than the expression of empty tautology. It has therefore rightly been observed that this law of thought is without content and leads no further. Such is the empty identity to which those remain attached who take it as such to be something true, and who are always wont to advance that identity is not difference, but that identity and difference are different.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"112.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0003","text":"They do not see that in this itself they already say that identity is something different; for they say that identity is different from difference; since this must at the same time be granted as the nature of identity, it follows that identity is not externally, but in itself, in its nature, different.—But further, in holding fast to this unmoved identity, which has its opposite in difference, they do not see that they thereby make it into a one-sided determinacy which, as such, has no truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"112.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0004","text":"It is conceded that the proposition of identity expresses only a one-sided determinacy, that it contains only the formal, abstract, incomplete truth.—But this correct judgment immediately entails that truth is complete only in the unity of identity with difference, and thus consists only in this unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"112.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0005","text":"In asserting that that identity is imperfect, this totality, by which identity is measured as imperfect, hovers before thought as the perfect; but since, on the other hand, identity is held fast as absolutely separated from difference and is taken in this separation as something essential, valid, true, nothing is to be seen in these conflicting assertions but the lack of bringing together these thoughts: that identity as abstract is essential, and that as such it is equally imperfect; the lack of consciousness concerning the negative movement in which identity itself is represented in these assertions.—Or, if it is expressed thus, that identity is essential identity as separation from difference, or in separation from difference, then this is immediately the expressed","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"112.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0006","text":"truth of the same, that it consists in being separation as such, or in being essential in separation, that is, in being nothing for itself, but a moment of separation.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"112.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0007","text":"Now, as regards the further authentication of the absolute truth of the proposition of identity, it is founded to this extent upon experience, that appeal is made to the experience of every consciousness: that when one pronounces this proposition to it, A is A, a tree is a tree, it immediately grants it and is satisfied that the proposition, as immediately clear through itself, requires no other grounding or proof.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"112.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0008","text":"On the one hand, this appeal to experience—that every consciousness universally acknowledges it—is mere rhetoric. For one does not mean to say that one has carried out the experiment with the abstract proposition A=A upon every consciousness. To that extent, there is no further seriousness in that appeal to actually performed experience; rather, it is only the assurance that, if one made the experiment, the result of universal acknowledgment would emerge.—But if not the abstract proposition as such, but the proposition in concrete application were meant, from which the former should first be developed, then the assertion of its universality and immediacy would consist in this: that every consciousness, and indeed in each of its expressions, lays it at the foundation, or that it lies implicitly in each.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"112.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0009","text":"Yet the concrete and the application are precisely the relation of the simple identical to a manifold different from it. Expressed as a proposition, the concrete would initially be a synthetic proposition. From the concrete itself, or from its synthetic proposition, abstraction could indeed bring forth the proposition of identity through analysis; but in fact it would not have left experience as it is, but altered it; for experience contained identity rather in unity with difference, and is the immediate refutation of the assertion that abstract identity as such is something true, since precisely the opposite, namely identity only united with difference, occurs in every experience.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"112.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0010","text":"On the other hand, however, experience with the pure proposition of identity is also made, only too often, and in this experience it shows clearly enough how the truth it contains is regarded. For if, for example, to the question: what is a plant? the answer is given: a plant is—a plant, then the truth of such a proposition is at once granted by the whole company upon which it is tried, and it will at the same time just as unanimously be said that nothing has thereby been said.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"112.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0011","text":"If someone opens his mouth and promises to state what God is, namely, God is—God, expectation finds itself disappointed, for it anticipated a different determination; and if this proposition is absolute truth, such absolute talk is held in very low esteem; nothing will be considered more boring and tiresome than a conversation merely chewing over the same thing, than such speech, which is nevertheless supposed to be truth.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"112.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0012","text":"If one considers more closely this effect of boredom in the case of such truth, the beginning, the plant is—, makes preparations to say something, to advance a further determination. But since only the same thing recurs, the opposite has rather happened: nothing has come out. Such identical speech thus contradicts itself. Identity, instead of being in it truth and absolute truth, is therefore rather the opposite; instead of being the unmoved simple, it is the going beyond itself into its own dissolution.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"112.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0013","text":"Thus there lies in the form of the proposition in which identity is expressed more than simple, abstract identity; there lies within it this pure movement of reflection, in which the other appears only as semblance, as immediate vanishing; A is, is a beginning before which something different hovers, toward which it is to go forth; but it does not reach the different; A is—A: difference is only a vanishing; the movement returns into itself.—The form of the proposition can be regarded as the hidden necessity to add still the surplus of that movement to abstract identity.—Thus an A, or a plant, or some other substrate is also added, which as a useless content has no significance; but it constitutes the difference, which seems contingently to associate itself with it.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"112.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0014","text":"If, instead of A and every other substrate, identity itself is taken,—identity is identity,—then it is equally conceded that any other substrate could likewise be taken in place of this. If, therefore, one is ever to appeal to what appearance shows, it shows this: that in the expression of identity difference also occurs immediately;—or, more determinately in accordance with the foregoing, that this identity is nothing, that it is negativity, the absolute difference from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"112.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0015","text":"The other expression of the proposition of identity, A cannot at the same time be A and not-A, has negative form; it is called the proposition of contradiction. As to how the form of negation, whereby this proposition differs from the preceding one, comes to identity, no justification is customarily given.—But this form lies in the fact that identity is the pure movement of reflection, the simple negativity, which the cited second expression of the proposition contains in a more developed manner. A is expressed, and a not-A, the pure other of A, but it shows itself only in order to vanish. Identity is therefore expressed in this proposition—as negation of negation. A and not-A are distinguished; these distinguished terms are related to one and the same A.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"112.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0016","text":"Identity is thus here represented as this distinguishedness in one relation, or as the simple difference in themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"112.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0017","text":"It is evident from this that the proposition of identity itself, and still more the proposition of contradiction, are not merely of an analytical but of a synthetic nature. For the latter contains in its expression not only empty, simple equality with itself, but not merely its other in general, but even absolute inequality, contradiction in itself. But the proposition of identity itself contains, as has been shown in it, the movement of reflection, identity as the vanishing of otherness.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"112.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_28:P0018","text":"What thus results from this consideration is, first, that the proposition of identity or of contradiction, insofar as it is meant to express as true merely abstract identity in opposition to difference, is not a law of thought, but rather its opposite; second, that these propositions contain more than is meant by them, namely this opposite, absolute difference itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"112.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_28:P0018"]}],"source_digest":"ed423de7ed2ad98168644ffd968f14441b5b269adaacc93ee92df66e71c32183","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU","title":"1. The Absolute Difference.","order":113,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_1DAU","text":"## B. Der Unterschied.\n\n## 1. Der absolute Unterschied.\n\nDer Unterschied ist die Negativität, welche die Reflexion in sich hat; das Nichts, das durch das identische Sprechen gesagt wird; das wesentliche Moment der Identität selbst, die zugleich als Negativität ihrer selbst, sich bestimmt und unterschieden vom Unterschied ist.\n\n1. Dieser Unterschied ist der Unterschied an und für sich, der absolute Unterschied, der Unterschied des Wesens.—Er ist der Unterschied an und für sich, nicht Unterschied durch ein Äußerliches, sondern sich auf sich beziehender, also einfacher Unterschied.—Es ist wesentlich den absoluten Unterschied als einfachen zu fassen. Im absoluten Unterschiede des A und Nicht-A von einander ist es das einfache Nicht, was als solches denselben ausmacht. Der Unterschied selbst ist einfacher Begriff. Darin, drückt man sich aus, sind zwei Dinge unterschieden, daß sie u.s.f.—Darin, das heißt, in einer und derselben Rücksicht, in demselben Bestimmungsgrunde. Er ist der Unterschied der Reflexion, nicht das Andersseyn des Daseyns. Ein Daseyn und ein anderes Daseyn sind gesetzt als außereinanderfallend, jedes der gegen einander bestimmten Daseyn hat ein unmittelbares Seyn für sich. Das Andre des Wesens dagegen ist das Andre an und für sich, nicht das Andre als eines andern außer ihm Befindlichen; die einfache Bestimmtheit an sich. Auch in der Sphäre des Daseyns erwies sich das Andersseyn und die Bestimmtheit von dieser Natur, einfache Bestimmtheit, identischer Gegensatz zu seyn; aber diese Identität zeigte sich nur als das Übergehen einer Bestimmtheit in die andere. Hier in der Sphäre der Reflexion tritt der Unterschied als reflektirter auf, der so gesetzt ist, wie er an sich ist.\n\n2. Der Unterschied an sich ist der sich auf sich beziehende Unterschied; so ist er die Negativität seiner selbst, der Unterschied nicht von einem Andern, sondern seiner von sich selbst; er ist nicht er selbst, sondern sein Anderes. Das Unterschiedene aber vom Unterschiede ist die Identität. Er ist also er selbst und die Identität. Beide zusammen machen den Unterschied aus; er ist das Ganze und sein Moment.—Es kann ebenso gesagt werden, der Unterschied als einfacher ist kein Unterschied; er ist dieß erst in Beziehung auf die Identität; aber vielmehr enthält er als Unterschied ebenso sie und diese Beziehung selbst.—Der Unterschied ist das Ganze und sein eignes Moment; wie die Identität ebenso sehr ihr Ganzes und ihr Moment ist.—Dieß ist als die wesentliche Natur der Reflexion und als bestimmter Urgrund aller Thätigkeit und Selbstbewegung zu betrachten. —Unterschied wie die Identität machen sich zum Momente oder zum Gesetztseyn, weil sie als Reflexion die negative Beziehung auf sich selbst sind.\n\nDer Unterschied, so als Einheit seiner und der Identität, ist an sich selbst bestimmter Unterschied. Er ist nicht Übergehen in ein Anderes, nicht Beziehung auf Anderes außer ihm; er hat sein Anderes, die Identität an ihm selbst; so wie diese, indem sie in die Bestimmung des Unterschieds getreten, nicht in ihn als ihr Anderes sich verloren hat, sondern in ihm sich erhält, seine Reflexion in sich und sein Moment ist.\n\n3. Der Unterschied hat die beiden Momente, Identität und Unterschied; beide sind so ein Gesetztseyn, Bestimmtheit. Aber in diesem Gesetztseyn ist jedes Beziehung auf sich selbst. Das eine, die Identität ist unmittelbar selbst das Moment der Reflexion in sich; ebenso ist aber das andere, der Unterschied, Unterschied an sich, der reflektirte Unterschied. Der Unterschied, indem er zwei solche Momente hat, die selbst die Reflexionen in sich sind, ist Verschiedenheit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0001","text":"## B. Der Unterschied.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"113.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0002","text":"## 1. Der absolute Unterschied.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"113.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0003","text":"Der Unterschied ist die Negativität, welche die Reflexion in sich hat; das Nichts, das durch das identische Sprechen gesagt wird; das wesentliche Moment der Identität selbst, die zugleich als Negativität ihrer selbst, sich bestimmt und unterschieden vom Unterschied ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"113.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0004","text":"1. Dieser Unterschied ist der Unterschied an und für sich, der absolute Unterschied, der Unterschied des Wesens.—Er ist der Unterschied an und für sich, nicht Unterschied durch ein Äußerliches, sondern sich auf sich beziehender, also einfacher Unterschied.—Es ist wesentlich den absoluten Unterschied als einfachen zu fassen. Im absoluten Unterschiede des A und Nicht-A von einander ist es das einfache Nicht, was als solches denselben ausmacht. Der Unterschied selbst ist einfacher Begriff. Darin, drückt man sich aus, sind zwei Dinge unterschieden, daß sie u.s.f.—Darin, das heißt, in einer und derselben Rücksicht, in demselben Bestimmungsgrunde. Er ist der Unterschied der Reflexion, nicht das Andersseyn des Daseyns. Ein Daseyn und ein anderes Daseyn sind gesetzt als außereinanderfallend, jedes der gegen einander bestimmten Daseyn hat ein unmittelbares Seyn für sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"113.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0005","text":"Das Andre des Wesens dagegen ist das Andre an und für sich, nicht das Andre als eines andern außer ihm Befindlichen; die einfache Bestimmtheit an sich. Auch in der Sphäre des Daseyns erwies sich das Andersseyn und die Bestimmtheit von dieser Natur, einfache Bestimmtheit, identischer Gegensatz zu seyn; aber diese Identität zeigte sich nur als das Übergehen einer Bestimmtheit in die andere. Hier in der Sphäre der Reflexion tritt der Unterschied als reflektirter auf, der so gesetzt ist, wie er an sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"113.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0006","text":"2. Der Unterschied an sich ist der sich auf sich beziehende Unterschied; so ist er die Negativität seiner selbst, der Unterschied nicht von einem Andern, sondern seiner von sich selbst; er ist nicht er selbst, sondern sein Anderes. Das Unterschiedene aber vom Unterschiede ist die Identität. Er ist also er selbst und die Identität. Beide zusammen machen den Unterschied aus; er ist das Ganze und sein Moment.—Es kann ebenso gesagt werden, der Unterschied als einfacher ist kein Unterschied; er ist dieß erst in Beziehung auf die Identität; aber vielmehr enthält er als Unterschied ebenso sie und diese Beziehung selbst.—Der Unterschied ist das Ganze und sein eignes Moment; wie die Identität ebenso sehr ihr Ganzes und ihr Moment ist.—Dieß ist als die wesentliche Natur der Reflexion und als bestimmter Urgrund aller Thätigkeit und Selbstbewegung zu betrachten.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"113.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0007","text":"—Unterschied wie die Identität machen sich zum Momente oder zum Gesetztseyn, weil sie als Reflexion die negative Beziehung auf sich selbst sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"113.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0008","text":"Der Unterschied, so als Einheit seiner und der Identität, ist an sich selbst bestimmter Unterschied. Er ist nicht Übergehen in ein Anderes, nicht Beziehung auf Anderes außer ihm; er hat sein Anderes, die Identität an ihm selbst; so wie diese, indem sie in die Bestimmung des Unterschieds getreten, nicht in ihn als ihr Anderes sich verloren hat, sondern in ihm sich erhält, seine Reflexion in sich und sein Moment ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"113.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0009","text":"3. Der Unterschied hat die beiden Momente, Identität und Unterschied; beide sind so ein Gesetztseyn, Bestimmtheit. Aber in diesem Gesetztseyn ist jedes Beziehung auf sich selbst. Das eine, die Identität ist unmittelbar selbst das Moment der Reflexion in sich; ebenso ist aber das andere, der Unterschied, Unterschied an sich, der reflektirte Unterschied. Der Unterschied, indem er zwei solche Momente hat, die selbst die Reflexionen in sich sind, ist Verschiedenheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"113.9"}],"sha256":"eeb7d05b60e785ebbdcb35e395de0bcdd809844a6c016690686fa7f7a95871cd","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104738504278Z_8f138fd1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"1. The Absolute Difference.","source_sha256":"eeb7d05b60e785ebbdcb35e395de0bcdd809844a6c016690686fa7f7a95871cd","sha256":"09d07e26dc09f7dbf410f835b79360f0a873e83ca625c6c0b5e2d52eae69259a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:47:38.504304+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0001","text":"## B. Difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"113.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0002","text":"## 1. Absolute Difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"113.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0003","text":"Difference is the negativity which reflection has within itself; the nothing that is expressed by identical speaking; the essential moment of identity itself, which at the same time, as negativity of itself, determines itself and is distinct from difference.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"113.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0004","text":"1. This difference is difference in and for itself, absolute difference, the difference of essence.—It is difference in and for itself, not difference through an externality, but self-relating, hence simple difference.—It is essential to grasp absolute difference as simple. In the absolute difference of A and non-A from one another, it is the simple not which as such constitutes the same. Difference itself is a simple concept. In this, it is said, two things are different, in that they etc.—In this, that is, in one and the same respect, in the same ground of determination. It is the difference of reflection, not the other-being of existence. One existence and another existence are posited as falling apart from one another; each of the existences determined over against one another has an immediate being for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"113.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0005","text":"The other of essence, on the contrary, is the other in and for itself, not the other as that of another existing outside it; simple determinacy in itself. Even in the sphere of existence, other-being and determinacy proved to be of this nature, simple determinacy, identical opposition; but this identity showed itself only as the transition of one determinacy into the other. Here, in the sphere of reflection, difference emerges as reflected, posited as it is in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"113.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0006","text":"2. Difference in itself is self-relating difference; thus it is the negativity of itself, difference not from an other, but of itself from itself; it is not itself, but its other. But that which is differentiated from difference is identity. Thus it is itself and identity. Together, both constitute difference; it is the whole and its moment.—It can equally be said that difference as simple is no difference; it is this only in relation to identity; but rather, as difference, it equally contains identity and this relation itself.—Difference is the whole and its own moment; just as identity is equally much its whole and its moment.—This is to be regarded as the essential nature of reflection and as the determinate primordial ground of all activity and self-motion.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"113.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0007","text":"—Difference, like identity, makes itself into a moment or into positedness, because as reflection it is the negative relation to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"113.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0008","text":"Difference, thus as the unity of itself and identity, is in itself determinate difference. It is not transition into an other, not relation to another outside it; it has its other, identity, in itself; just as identity, having entered into the determination of difference, has not lost itself in difference as its other, but preserves itself in it, is its reflection into itself and its moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"113.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0009","text":"3. Difference has the two moments, identity and difference; both are thus a positedness, determinacy. But in this positedness each is relation to itself. The one, identity, is immediately itself the moment of reflection into itself; but likewise the other, difference, is difference in itself, reflected difference. Difference, in that it has two such moments, which are themselves reflections into themselves, is diversity.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"113.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_1DAU:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"ca1678367d04ff24f1c57d972c3aef5be53a5d12a7ee65e9662ca60a7ad586fe","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"1. Der absolute Unterschied."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"1. Der absolute Unterschied.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0","title":"2. Diversity.","order":114,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_2DV0","text":"1. Die Identität zerfällt an ihr selbst in Verschiedenheit, weil sie als absoluter Unterschied in sich selbst, sich als das Negative ihrer setzt, und diese ihre Momente, sie selbst und das Negative ihrer, Reflexionen in sich, identisch mit sich sind; oder eben weil sie ihr Negiren unmittelbar selbst aufhebt, und in ihrer Bestimmung in sich reflektirt ist. Das Unterschiedne besteht als gegen einander gleichgültig verschiedenes, weil es identisch mit sich ist, weil die Identität seinen Boden und Element ausmacht; oder das Verschiedene ist das, was es ist, eben nur in seinem Gegentheile, der Identität.\n\nDie Verschiedenheit macht das Andersseyn als solches der Reflexion aus. Das Andere des Daseyns hat das unmittelbare Seyn zu seinem Grunde, in welchem das Negative besteht. In der Reflexion aber macht die Identität mit sich, die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, das Bestehen des Negativen und die Gleichgültigkeit desselben aus.\n\nDie Momente des Unterschiedes sind die Identität und der Unterschied selbst. Verschiedene sind sie als in sich selbst reflektirte, sich auf sich beziehende; so sind sie in der Bestimmung der Identität, Beziehungen nur auf sich; die Identität ist nicht bezogen auf den Unterschied, noch ist der Unterschied bezogen auf die Identität; indem so jedes dieser Momente nur auf sich bezogen ist, sind sie nicht bestimmt gegen einander.—Weil sie nun auf diese Weise nicht an ihnen selbst unterschiedene sind, so ist der Unterschied ihnen äußerlich. Die Verschiedenen verhalten sich also nicht als Identität und Unterschied zu einander, sondern nur als Verschiedene überhaupt, die gleichgültig gegeneinander und gegen ihre Bestimmtheit sind.\n\n2. In der Verschiedenheit als der Gleichgültigkeit des Unterschieds, ist sich überhaupt die Reflexion äußerlich geworden; der Unterschied ist nur ein Gesetztseyn oder als aufgehobener, aber er ist selbst die ganze Reflexion.—Dieß näher betrachtet, so sind beide, die Identität und der Unterschied, wie sich so eben bestimmt hat, Reflexionen; jedes Einheit seiner selbst und seines Andern; jedes ist das Ganze. Damit aber ist die Bestimmtheit, nur Identität oder nur Unterschied zu seyn, ein Aufgehobenes. Sie sind darum keine Qualitäten, weil ihre Bestimmtheit durch die Reflexion in sich zugleich nur als Negation ist. Es ist also dieß Gedoppelte vorhanden, die Reflexion in sich als solche, und die Bestimmtheit als Negation, oder das Gesetztseyn. Das Gesetztseyn ist die sich äußerliche Reflexion; es ist die Negation als Negation; hiermit an sich zwar die sich auf sich beziehende Negation und Reflexion in sich; aber nur an sich; es ist die Beziehung darauf als auf ein Äußerliches.\n\nDie Reflexion an sich und die äußere Reflexion, sind somit die zwei Bestimmungen, in die sich die Momente des Unterschiedes, Identität und Unterschied, setzten. Sie sind diese Momente selbst, insofern sie sich nunmehr bestimmt haben.—Die Reflexion an sich ist die Identität, aber bestimmt, gleichgültig gegen den Unterschied zu seyn; nicht den Unterschied gar nicht zu haben, sondern sich als mit sich identisch gegen ihn zu verhalten; sie ist die Verschiedenheit. Es ist die Identität, die sich so in sich reflektirt hat, daß sie eigentlich die Eine Reflexion der beiden Momente in sich ist, beide sind Reflexionen in sich. Die Identität ist diese eine Reflexion beider, die den Unterschied nur als einen gleichgültigen an ihr hat, und Verschiedenheit überhaupt ist.—Die äußere Reflexion dagegen ist der bestimmte Unterschied derselben nicht als absolute Reflexion in sich, sondern als Bestimmung, wogegen die an sich seyende Reflexion gleichgültig ist; seine beiden Momente, die Identität und der Unterschied selbst, sind so äußerlich gesetzte, nicht an und für sich seyende Bestimmungen.\n\nDiese äußerliche Identität nun ist die Gleichheit, und der äußerliche Unterschied die Ungleichheit.—Die Gleichheit ist zwar Identität, aber nur als ein Gesetztseyn, eine Identität, die nicht an und für sich ist.—Ebenso die Ungleichheit ist Unterschied, aber als ein äußerlicher, der nicht an und für sich der Unterschied des Ungleichen selbst ist. Ob Etwas einem andern Etwas gleich ist oder nicht, geht weder das eine noch das andere an; jedes derselben ist nur auf sich bezogen; ist an und für sich selbst was es ist; die Identität oder Nichtidentität als Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist die Rücksicht eines Dritten, die außer ihnen fällt.\n\n3. Die äußere Reflexion bezieht das Verschiedene auf die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit. Diese Beziehung, das Vergleichen, geht von der Gleichheit zur Ungleichheit, und von dieser zu jener herüber und hinüber. Aber dieses herüber- und hinübergehende Beziehen der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist diesen Bestimmungen selbst äußerlich; auch werden sie nicht auf einander, sondern jede für sich nur auf ein Drittes bezogen. Jede tritt in dieser Abwechslung unmittelbar für sich hervor.—Die äußerliche Reflexion ist als solche sich selbst äußerlich; der bestimmte Unterschied ist der negirte absolute Unterschied; er ist somit nicht einfach, nicht die Reflexion in sich, sondern diese hat er außer ihm; seine Momente fallen daher aus einander, und beziehen sieh auch als gegen einander äußerliche, auf die ihnen gegenüber stehende Reflexion in sich.\n\nAn der sich entfremdeten Reflexion kommen also die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit als gegen einander selbst unbezogene hervor, und sie trennt sie, indem sie sie auf ein und dasselbe bezieht, durch die Insoferns, Seiten und Rücksichten. Die Verschiedenen, die das eine und dasselbe sind, worauf beide, die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, bezogen werden, sind also nach der einen Seite einander gleich, nach der andern Seite aber ungleich, und insofern sie gleich sind, insofern sind sie nicht ungleich. Die Gleichheit bezieht sich nur auf sich, und die Ungleichheit ist ebenso nur Ungleichheit.\n\nDurch diese ihre Trennung von einander aber heben sie sich nur auf. Gerade, was den Widerspruch und die Auflösung von ihnen abhalten soll, daß nämlich Etwas einem Andern in einer Rücksicht gleich, in einer andern aber ungleich sey;—dieß Auseinanderhalten der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist ihre Zerstörung. Denn beide sind Bestimmungen des Unterschiedes; sie sind Beziehungen aufeinander, das eine, zu seyn, was das andere nicht ist; gleich ist nicht ungleich, und ungleich ist nicht gleich; und beide haben wesentlich diese Beziehung, und außer ihr keine Bedeutung; als Bestimmungen des Unterschiedes ist jedes das was es ist, als unterschieden von seinem andern. Durch ihre Gleichgültigkeit aber gegen einander, ist die Gleichheit nur bezogen auf sich, die Ungleichheit ist ebenso eine eigene Rücksicht und Reflexion für sich; jede ist somit sich selbst gleich; der Unterschied ist verschwunden, da sie keine Bestimmtheit gegen einander haben; oder jede ist hiermit nur Gleichheit.\n\nDiese gleichgültige Rücksicht, oder der äußerliche Unterschied hebt somit sich selbst auf, und ist die Negativität seiner an sich selbst. Er ist diejenige Negativität, welche in dem Vergleichen dem Vergleichenden zukommt. Das Vergleichende geht von der Gleichheit zur Ungleichheit, und von dieser zu jener zurück; läßt also das eine im andern verschwinden, und ist in der That die negative Einheit beider. Sie ist zunächst jenseits des Verglichenen so wie jenseits der Momente der Vergleichung, als ein Subjektives, außerhalb ihnen fallendes Thun. Aber diese negative Einheit ist in der That die Natur der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit selbst, wie sich ergeben hat. Eben die selbstständige Rücksicht, die eine jede ist, ist vielmehr die ihre Unterschiedenheit und damit sie selbst aufhebende Beziehung auf sich.\n\nNach dieser Seite, als Momente der äußern Reflexion und als sich selbst äußerlich, verschwinden die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit in ihre Gleichheit zusammen. Aber diese ihre negative Einheit ist ferner auch an ihnen gesetzt; sie haben nämlich die an sich seyende Reflexion außer ihnen, oder sind die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit eines Dritten, eines Andern als sie selbst sind. So ist das Gleiche nicht das Gleiche seiner selbst, und das Ungleiche als das Ungleiche nicht seiner selbst, sondern eines ihm ungleichen, ist selbst das Gleiche. Das Gleiche und das Ungleiche ist also das Ungleiche seiner selbst. Jedes ist somit diese Reflexion, die Gleichheit, daß sie sie selbst und die Ungleichheit, die Ungleichheit, daß sie sie selbst und die Gleichheit ist.\n\nGleichheit und Ungleichheit machten die Seite des Gesetztseyns, gegen das Verglichene oder das Verschiedene aus, das sich als die an sich seyende Reflexion gegen sie bestimmt hatte. Aber dieses hat damit seine Bestimmtheit gegen sie ebenfalls verloren. Eben die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, die Bestimmungen der äußerlichen Reflexion, sind die nur an sich seyende Reflexion, welche das Verschiedene als solches seyn sollte, sein nur unbestimmter Unterschied. Die an sich seyende Reflexion ist die Beziehung auf sich ohne Negation, die abstrakte Identität mit sich; damit eben das Gesetztseyn selbst.—Das bloß Verschiedene geht also durch das Gesetztseyn über in die negative Reflexion. Das Verschiedene ist der bloß gesetzte Unterschied, also der Unterschied, der keiner ist, also die Negation seiner an ihm selbst. So die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit selbst, das Gesetztseyn, geht durch die Gleichgültigkeit oder die an sich seyende Reflexion zurück in die negative Einheit mit sich; in die Reflexion, welche der Unterschied der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit an sich selbst ist. Die Verschiedenheit, deren gleichgültige Seiten ebenso sehr schlechthin nur Momente als Einer negativen Einheit sind, ist der Gegensatz.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0001","text":"1. Die Identität zerfällt an ihr selbst in Verschiedenheit, weil sie als absoluter Unterschied in sich selbst, sich als das Negative ihrer setzt, und diese ihre Momente, sie selbst und das Negative ihrer, Reflexionen in sich, identisch mit sich sind; oder eben weil sie ihr Negiren unmittelbar selbst aufhebt, und in ihrer Bestimmung in sich reflektirt ist. Das Unterschiedne besteht als gegen einander gleichgültig verschiedenes, weil es identisch mit sich ist, weil die Identität seinen Boden und Element ausmacht; oder das Verschiedene ist das, was es ist, eben nur in seinem Gegentheile, der Identität.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"114.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0002","text":"Die Verschiedenheit macht das Andersseyn als solches der Reflexion aus. Das Andere des Daseyns hat das unmittelbare Seyn zu seinem Grunde, in welchem das Negative besteht. In der Reflexion aber macht die Identität mit sich, die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, das Bestehen des Negativen und die Gleichgültigkeit desselben aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"114.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0003","text":"Die Momente des Unterschiedes sind die Identität und der Unterschied selbst. Verschiedene sind sie als in sich selbst reflektirte, sich auf sich beziehende; so sind sie in der Bestimmung der Identität, Beziehungen nur auf sich; die Identität ist nicht bezogen auf den Unterschied, noch ist der Unterschied bezogen auf die Identität; indem so jedes dieser Momente nur auf sich bezogen ist, sind sie nicht bestimmt gegen einander.—Weil sie nun auf diese Weise nicht an ihnen selbst unterschiedene sind, so ist der Unterschied ihnen äußerlich. Die Verschiedenen verhalten sich also nicht als Identität und Unterschied zu einander, sondern nur als Verschiedene überhaupt, die gleichgültig gegeneinander und gegen ihre Bestimmtheit sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"114.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0004","text":"2. In der Verschiedenheit als der Gleichgültigkeit des Unterschieds, ist sich überhaupt die Reflexion äußerlich geworden; der Unterschied ist nur ein Gesetztseyn oder als aufgehobener, aber er ist selbst die ganze Reflexion.—Dieß näher betrachtet, so sind beide, die Identität und der Unterschied, wie sich so eben bestimmt hat, Reflexionen; jedes Einheit seiner selbst und seines Andern; jedes ist das Ganze. Damit aber ist die Bestimmtheit, nur Identität oder nur Unterschied zu seyn, ein Aufgehobenes. Sie sind darum keine Qualitäten, weil ihre Bestimmtheit durch die Reflexion in sich zugleich nur als Negation ist. Es ist also dieß Gedoppelte vorhanden, die Reflexion in sich als solche, und die Bestimmtheit als Negation, oder das Gesetztseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"114.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0005","text":"Das Gesetztseyn ist die sich äußerliche Reflexion; es ist die Negation als Negation; hiermit an sich zwar die sich auf sich beziehende Negation und Reflexion in sich; aber nur an sich; es ist die Beziehung darauf als auf ein Äußerliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"114.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0006","text":"Die Reflexion an sich und die äußere Reflexion, sind somit die zwei Bestimmungen, in die sich die Momente des Unterschiedes, Identität und Unterschied, setzten. Sie sind diese Momente selbst, insofern sie sich nunmehr bestimmt haben.—Die Reflexion an sich ist die Identität, aber bestimmt, gleichgültig gegen den Unterschied zu seyn; nicht den Unterschied gar nicht zu haben, sondern sich als mit sich identisch gegen ihn zu verhalten; sie ist die Verschiedenheit. Es ist die Identität, die sich so in sich reflektirt hat, daß sie eigentlich die Eine Reflexion der beiden Momente in sich ist, beide sind Reflexionen in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"114.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0007","text":"Die Identität ist diese eine Reflexion beider, die den Unterschied nur als einen gleichgültigen an ihr hat, und Verschiedenheit überhaupt ist.—Die äußere Reflexion dagegen ist der bestimmte Unterschied derselben nicht als absolute Reflexion in sich, sondern als Bestimmung, wogegen die an sich seyende Reflexion gleichgültig ist; seine beiden Momente, die Identität und der Unterschied selbst, sind so äußerlich gesetzte, nicht an und für sich seyende Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"114.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0008","text":"Diese äußerliche Identität nun ist die Gleichheit, und der äußerliche Unterschied die Ungleichheit.—Die Gleichheit ist zwar Identität, aber nur als ein Gesetztseyn, eine Identität, die nicht an und für sich ist.—Ebenso die Ungleichheit ist Unterschied, aber als ein äußerlicher, der nicht an und für sich der Unterschied des Ungleichen selbst ist. Ob Etwas einem andern Etwas gleich ist oder nicht, geht weder das eine noch das andere an; jedes derselben ist nur auf sich bezogen; ist an und für sich selbst was es ist; die Identität oder Nichtidentität als Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist die Rücksicht eines Dritten, die außer ihnen fällt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"114.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0009","text":"3. Die äußere Reflexion bezieht das Verschiedene auf die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit. Diese Beziehung, das Vergleichen, geht von der Gleichheit zur Ungleichheit, und von dieser zu jener herüber und hinüber. Aber dieses herüber- und hinübergehende Beziehen der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist diesen Bestimmungen selbst äußerlich; auch werden sie nicht auf einander, sondern jede für sich nur auf ein Drittes bezogen. Jede tritt in dieser Abwechslung unmittelbar für sich hervor.—Die äußerliche Reflexion ist als solche sich selbst äußerlich; der bestimmte Unterschied ist der negirte absolute Unterschied; er ist somit nicht einfach, nicht die Reflexion in sich, sondern diese hat er außer ihm; seine Momente fallen daher aus einander, und beziehen sieh auch als gegen einander äußerliche, auf die ihnen gegenüber stehende Reflexion in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"114.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0010","text":"An der sich entfremdeten Reflexion kommen also die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit als gegen einander selbst unbezogene hervor, und sie trennt sie, indem sie sie auf ein und dasselbe bezieht, durch die Insoferns, Seiten und Rücksichten. Die Verschiedenen, die das eine und dasselbe sind, worauf beide, die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, bezogen werden, sind also nach der einen Seite einander gleich, nach der andern Seite aber ungleich, und insofern sie gleich sind, insofern sind sie nicht ungleich. Die Gleichheit bezieht sich nur auf sich, und die Ungleichheit ist ebenso nur Ungleichheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"114.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0011","text":"Durch diese ihre Trennung von einander aber heben sie sich nur auf. Gerade, was den Widerspruch und die Auflösung von ihnen abhalten soll, daß nämlich Etwas einem Andern in einer Rücksicht gleich, in einer andern aber ungleich sey;—dieß Auseinanderhalten der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist ihre Zerstörung. Denn beide sind Bestimmungen des Unterschiedes; sie sind Beziehungen aufeinander, das eine, zu seyn, was das andere nicht ist; gleich ist nicht ungleich, und ungleich ist nicht gleich; und beide haben wesentlich diese Beziehung, und außer ihr keine Bedeutung; als Bestimmungen des Unterschiedes ist jedes das was es ist, als unterschieden von seinem andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"114.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0012","text":"Durch ihre Gleichgültigkeit aber gegen einander, ist die Gleichheit nur bezogen auf sich, die Ungleichheit ist ebenso eine eigene Rücksicht und Reflexion für sich; jede ist somit sich selbst gleich; der Unterschied ist verschwunden, da sie keine Bestimmtheit gegen einander haben; oder jede ist hiermit nur Gleichheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"114.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0013","text":"Diese gleichgültige Rücksicht, oder der äußerliche Unterschied hebt somit sich selbst auf, und ist die Negativität seiner an sich selbst. Er ist diejenige Negativität, welche in dem Vergleichen dem Vergleichenden zukommt. Das Vergleichende geht von der Gleichheit zur Ungleichheit, und von dieser zu jener zurück; läßt also das eine im andern verschwinden, und ist in der That die negative Einheit beider. Sie ist zunächst jenseits des Verglichenen so wie jenseits der Momente der Vergleichung, als ein Subjektives, außerhalb ihnen fallendes Thun. Aber diese negative Einheit ist in der That die Natur der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit selbst, wie sich ergeben hat. Eben die selbstständige Rücksicht, die eine jede ist, ist vielmehr die ihre Unterschiedenheit und damit sie selbst aufhebende Beziehung auf sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"114.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0014","text":"Nach dieser Seite, als Momente der äußern Reflexion und als sich selbst äußerlich, verschwinden die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit in ihre Gleichheit zusammen. Aber diese ihre negative Einheit ist ferner auch an ihnen gesetzt; sie haben nämlich die an sich seyende Reflexion außer ihnen, oder sind die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit eines Dritten, eines Andern als sie selbst sind. So ist das Gleiche nicht das Gleiche seiner selbst, und das Ungleiche als das Ungleiche nicht seiner selbst, sondern eines ihm ungleichen, ist selbst das Gleiche. Das Gleiche und das Ungleiche ist also das Ungleiche seiner selbst. Jedes ist somit diese Reflexion, die Gleichheit, daß sie sie selbst und die Ungleichheit, die Ungleichheit, daß sie sie selbst und die Gleichheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"114.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0015","text":"Gleichheit und Ungleichheit machten die Seite des Gesetztseyns, gegen das Verglichene oder das Verschiedene aus, das sich als die an sich seyende Reflexion gegen sie bestimmt hatte. Aber dieses hat damit seine Bestimmtheit gegen sie ebenfalls verloren. Eben die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit, die Bestimmungen der äußerlichen Reflexion, sind die nur an sich seyende Reflexion, welche das Verschiedene als solches seyn sollte, sein nur unbestimmter Unterschied. Die an sich seyende Reflexion ist die Beziehung auf sich ohne Negation, die abstrakte Identität mit sich; damit eben das Gesetztseyn selbst.—Das bloß Verschiedene geht also durch das Gesetztseyn über in die negative Reflexion. Das Verschiedene ist der bloß gesetzte Unterschied, also der Unterschied, der keiner ist, also die Negation seiner an ihm selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"114.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0016","text":"So die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit selbst, das Gesetztseyn, geht durch die Gleichgültigkeit oder die an sich seyende Reflexion zurück in die negative Einheit mit sich; in die Reflexion, welche der Unterschied der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit an sich selbst ist. Die Verschiedenheit, deren gleichgültige Seiten ebenso sehr schlechthin nur Momente als Einer negativen Einheit sind, ist der Gegensatz.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"114.16"}],"sha256":"f107e36e9dacc43af96779b6d60f24f989b6284240eff7d06745c35318c372fb","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104757099526Z_f5868a2c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"2. Diversity.","source_sha256":"f107e36e9dacc43af96779b6d60f24f989b6284240eff7d06745c35318c372fb","sha256":"814c37a91e7c7c67e5a527fed179522c9192c406cb329381ada46a306e23078f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:47:57.099542+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0001","text":"1. Identity disintegrates within itself into diversity, because, as absolute difference within itself, it posits itself as the negative of itself, and these its moments—itself and its negative—are reflections into themselves, identical with themselves; or, precisely because it immediately sublates its own negating, and is reflected into itself in its determinacy. The diverse subsists as indifferently diverse over against one another because it is identical with itself, because identity constitutes its ground and element; or the diverse is what it is only in its opposite, identity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"114.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0002","text":"Diversity constitutes other-being as such of reflection. The other of determinate being has immediate Being as its ground, in which the negative subsists. In reflection, however, identity with itself, reflected immediacy, constitutes the subsistence of the negative and its indifference.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"114.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0003","text":"The moments of difference are identity and difference itself. They are diverse as reflected into themselves, relating themselves to themselves; thus they are in the determination of identity, relations only to themselves; identity is not related to difference, nor is difference related to identity; since each of these moments is thus related only to itself, they are not determined over against one another.—Since they are not in this way differentiated in themselves, difference is external to them. The diverse, therefore, do not comport themselves toward one another as identity and difference, but only as diverse in general, which are indifferent toward one another and toward their determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"114.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0004","text":"2. In diversity, as the indifference of difference, reflection has in general become external to itself; difference is only a positedness, or as sublated, but it is itself the whole of reflection.—Considered more closely, both, identity and difference, as has just been determined, are reflections; each is unity of itself and its other; each is the whole. But with this, the determinacy of being only identity or only difference is something sublated. They are therefore not qualities, because their determinacy is, through reflection into itself, at the same time only as negation. Thus there is this twofold: reflection into itself as such, and determinacy as negation, or positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"114.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0005","text":"Positedness is reflection external to itself; it is negation as negation; thereby indeed in itself self-related negation and reflection into itself, but only in itself; it is relation to this as to something external.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"114.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0006","text":"Reflection in itself and external reflection are therefore the two determinations into which the moments of difference, identity and difference, have posited themselves. They are these moments themselves, insofar as they have now determined themselves.—Reflection in itself is identity, but determined to be indifferent toward difference; not not to have difference at all, but to comport itself toward it as identical with itself; it is diversity. It is identity that has thus reflected itself into itself, such that it is properly the one reflection of the two moments into itself; both are reflections into themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"114.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0007","text":"Identity is this one reflection of both, which has difference in it only as an indifferent one, and is diversity in general.—External reflection, on the other hand, is their determinate difference, not as absolute reflection into itself, but as a determination toward which reflection that is in itself is indifferent; its two moments, identity and difference itself, are thus externally posited determinations, not determinations that are in and for themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"114.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0008","text":"This external identity, then, is equality, and external difference is inequality.—Equality is indeed identity, but only as a positedness, an identity which is not in and for itself.—Likewise, inequality is difference, but as an external difference, which is not in and for itself the difference of the unequal itself. Whether something is equal to another something or not concerns neither the one nor the other; each of them is related only to itself; is in and for itself what it is; identity or non-identity as equality and inequality is the consideration of a third, which falls outside them.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"114.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0009","text":"3. External reflection relates the diverse to equality and inequality. This relation, comparison, passes from equality to inequality and from the latter back and forth to the former. But this relating back and forth of equality and inequality is external to these determinations themselves; nor are they related to one another, but each for itself only to a third. In this alternation each immediately emerges for itself.—External reflection as such is external to itself; determinate difference is negated absolute difference; it is thus not simple, not reflection into itself, but has this outside itself; its moments therefore fall apart, and, as external to one another, also relate themselves to the reflection into itself standing over against them.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"114.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0010","text":"Thus, in alienated reflection, equality and inequality emerge as themselves unrelated to one another, and it separates them by relating them to one and the same thing, through the insofar, sides, and respects. The diverse, which are the one and the same thing to which both equality and inequality are related, are therefore equal to one another in one respect, but unequal in another; and insofar as they are equal, insofar are they not unequal. Equality relates only to itself, and inequality is likewise only inequality.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"114.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0011","text":"But through this their separation from one another, they only sublate themselves. Precisely that which is supposed to ward off contradiction and their dissolution—namely, that something is equal to another in one respect, but unequal in another;—this keeping apart of equality and inequality is their destruction. For both are determinations of difference; they are relations to one another, the one being what the other is not; equal is not unequal, and unequal is not equal; and both essentially have this relation, and outside it no significance; as determinations of difference, each is what it is as differentiated from its other.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"114.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0012","text":"But through their indifference toward one another, equality is related only to itself; inequality is likewise a distinct respect and reflection for itself; each is thus equal to itself; difference has vanished, since they have no determinacy over against one another; or each is thereby only equality.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"114.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0013","text":"This indifferent respect, or external difference, thus sublates itself and is the negativity of itself within itself. It is that negativity which belongs to the comparer in comparison. The comparer passes from equality to inequality, and from the latter back to the former; thus allows the one to vanish in the other, and is in fact the negative unity of both. It is at first beyond what is compared as well as beyond the moments of comparison, as a subjective activity falling outside them. But this negative unity is in fact the nature of equality and inequality themselves, as has emerged. Precisely the independent respect that each is, is rather their self-sublating relation to itself—its differentiatedness, and with it itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"114.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0014","text":"From this side, as moments of external reflection and as external to themselves, equality and inequality vanish together into their equality. But this their negative unity is further posited in them; namely, they have reflection that is in itself outside them, or they are the equality and inequality of a third, of an other than they themselves are. Thus the equal is not equal to itself, and the unequal, as unequal, is not unequal to itself, but to one unequal to it, is itself the equal. The equal and the unequal are therefore unequal to themselves. Each is consequently this reflection: equality, in that it is itself and inequality; inequality, in that it is itself and equality.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"114.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0015","text":"Equality and inequality constituted the side of positedness over against that which is compared, or the diverse, which had determined itself over against them as reflection that is in itself. But with this it has likewise lost its determinacy over against them. Precisely equality and inequality, the determinations of external reflection, are the reflection that is only in itself, which the diverse as such was supposed to be, its merely indeterminate difference. Reflection that is in itself is relation to itself without negation, abstract identity with itself; thereby positedness itself.—The merely diverse thus passes through positedness into negative reflection. The diverse is merely posited difference, thus difference that is no difference, thus its negation within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"114.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0016","text":"Thus equality and inequality themselves, positedness, return through indifference or reflection that is in itself into negative unity with themselves; into reflection which is the difference of equality and inequality within themselves. Diversity, whose indifferent sides are just as absolutely only moments of a single negative unity, is opposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"114.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_2DV0:P0016"]}],"source_digest":"9af0013c73092c0b5b89a0970e5b82befd696cd54e31df3f21fa53bf25a0976c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"2. Die Verschiedenheit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"2. Die Verschiedenheit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29","title":"Remark.","order":115,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_29","text":"Die Verschiedenheit wird, wie die Identität, in einem eigenen Satze ausgedrückt. Übrigens bleiben diese beide Sätze in der gleichgültigen Verschiedenheit gegeneinander gehalten, so daß jeder für sich gilt ohne Rücksicht auf den andern.\n\nAlle Dinge sind verschieden, oder: Es giebt nicht zwei Dinge, die einander gleich sind.—Dieser Satz ist in der That dem Satze der Identität entgegengesetzt, denn er sagt aus: A ist ein Verschiedenes, also A ist auch nicht A; oder A ist einem andern ungleich, so ist es nicht A überhaupt, sondern vielmehr ein bestimmtes A. An die Stelle des A im identischen Satze kann jedes andere Substrat gesetzt, aber A als Ungleiches nicht mehr mit jedem andern vertauscht werden. Es soll zwar nicht ein Verschiedenes von sich, sondern nur von Anderem seyn; aber diese Verschiedenheit ist seine eigene Bestimmung. Als mit sich identisches A ist es das Unbestimmte; aber als Bestimmtes ist es das Gegentheil hiervon, es hat nicht mehr nur die Identität mit sich, sondern auch eine Negation, somit eine Verschiedenheit seiner selbst von sich an ihm.\n\nDaß alle Dinge verschieden sind von einander, ist ein sehr überflüssiger Satz, denn im Plural der Dinge liegt unmittelbar die Mehrheit und die ganz unbestimmte Verschiedenheit.—Der Satz aber: es giebt nicht zwei Dinge, die einander vollkommen gleich sind, drückt mehr, nämlich die bestimmte Verschiedenheit aus. Zwei Dinge sind nicht bloß zwei; die numerische Vielheit ist nur die Einerleiheit, sondern sie sind durch eine Bestimmung verschieden. Der Satz, daß es nicht zwei Dinge giebt, die einander gleich sind, fällt dem Vorstellen,—auch nach der Anekdote, an einem Hofe auf, wo ihn Leibniz vorgebracht und die Damen veranlaßt haben soll, unter Baumblättern zu suchen, ob sie nicht zwei gleiche finden.—Glückliche Zeiten für die Metaphysik, wo man sich am Hofe mit ihr beschäftigte, und wo es keiner andern Anstrengung bedurfte, ihre Sätze zu prüfen, als Baumblätter zu vergleichen!—Der Grund, daß jener Satz auffallend ist, liegt in dem Gesagten, daß zwei oder die numerische Mehrheit noch keine bestimmte Verschiedenheit enthält, und daß die Verschiedenheit als solche in ihrer Abstraktion zunächst gleichgültig gegen die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist. Das Vorstellen, indem es auch zur Bestimmung übergeht, nimmt diese Momente selbst als gegen einander gleichgültige auf, so daß das eine ohne das andere, die bloße Gleichheit der Dinge ohne die Ungleichheit zur Bestimmung hinreiche, oder daß die Dinge verschieden seyen, wenn sie auch nur numerisch Viele, verschiedene überhaupt, nicht ungleiche sind. Der Satz der Verschiedenheit hingegen drückt aus, daß die Dinge durch die Ungleichheit von einander verschieden sind, daß ihnen die Bestimmung der Ungleichheit so sehr zukomme als die der Gleichheit, denn erst beide zusammen machen den bestimmten Unterschied aus.\n\nDieser Satz nun, daß allen Dingen die Bestimmung der Ungleichheit zukommt, bedürfte eines Beweises; er kann nicht als unmittelbarer Satz aufgestellt werden, denn die gewöhnliche Weise des Erkennens selbst fotdert für die Verknüpfung verschiedener Bestimmungen in einem synthetischen Satze einen Beweis oder das Aufzeigen eines Dritten, worin sie vermittelt sind. Dieser Beweis müßte den Übergang der Identität in die Verschiedenheit, und dann den Übergang dieser in die bestimmte Verschiedenheit, in die Ungleichheit darthun. Dieß pflegt aber nicht geleistet zu werden; es ergab sich darin, daß die Verschiedenheit oder der äußerliche Unterschied, in Wahrheit in sich reflektirter, Unterschied an ihm selbst ist, daß das gleichgültige Bestehen des Verschiedenen das bloße Gesetztseyn, und damit nicht äußerlicher, gleichgültiger Unterschied, sondern Eine Beziehung der beiden Momente ist.\n\nEs liegt darin auch die Auflösung und Nichtigkeit des Satzes der Verschiedenheit. Zwei Dinge sind nicht vollkommen gleich; so sind sie gleich und ungleich zugleich; gleich schon darin, daß sie Dinge oder zwei überhaupt sind, denn jedes ist ein Ding und ein Eins so gut als das andere,jedes also dasselbe, was das andere; ungleich aber sind sie durch die Annahme. Es ist somit die Bestimmung vorhanden, daß beide Momente, die Gleichheit und die Ungleichheit, in Einem und demselben verschieden, oder daß der außereinanderfallende Unterschied, zugleich eine und dieselbe Beziehung ist. Somit ist sie in Entgegensetzung übergegangen.\n\nDas Zugleich der beiden Prädikate wird zwar durch das Insofern aus einander gehalten; daß zwei Dinge insofern sie gleich, insofern nicht ungleich, oder nach einer Seite und Rücksicht gleich, nach der andern Seite und Rücksicht aber ungleich sind. Damit wird die Einheit der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit aus dem Dinge entfernt, und was seine eigene, und die Reflexion der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit an sich wäre, als eine dem Dinge äußerliche Reflexion festgehalten. Diese ist es aber somit, die in einer und derselben Thätigkeit die zwei Seiten der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit unterscheidet, somit in Einer Thätigkeit beide enthält, die eine in die andere scheinen läßt und reflektirt.—Die gewöhnliche Zärtlichkeit für die Dinge aber, die nur dafür sorgt, daß diese sich nicht widersprechen, vergißt hier wie sonst, daß damit der Widerspruch nicht aufgelöst, sondern nur anderswohin, in die Subjektive oder äußere Reflexion überhaupt geschoben wird, und daß diese in der That die beiden Momente, welche durch diese Entfernung und Versetzung als bloßes Gesetztseyn ausgesprochen werden, als aufgehobene und auf einander bezogene in Einer Einheit enthält.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Die Verschiedenheit wird, wie die Identität, in einem eigenen Satze ausgedrückt. Übrigens bleiben diese beide Sätze in der gleichgültigen Verschiedenheit gegeneinander gehalten, so daß jeder für sich gilt ohne Rücksicht auf den andern.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Alle Dinge sind verschieden, oder: Es giebt nicht zwei Dinge, die einander gleich sind.—Dieser Satz ist in der That dem Satze der Identität entgegengesetzt, denn er sagt aus: A ist ein Verschiedenes, also A ist auch nicht A; oder A ist einem andern ungleich, so ist es nicht A überhaupt, sondern vielmehr ein bestimmtes A. An die Stelle des A im identischen Satze kann jedes andere Substrat gesetzt, aber A als Ungleiches nicht mehr mit jedem andern vertauscht werden. Es soll zwar nicht ein Verschiedenes von sich, sondern nur von Anderem seyn; aber diese Verschiedenheit ist seine eigene Bestimmung. Als mit sich identisches A ist es das Unbestimmte; aber als Bestimmtes ist es das Gegentheil hiervon, es hat nicht mehr nur die Identität mit sich, sondern auch eine Negation, somit eine Verschiedenheit seiner selbst von sich an ihm.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Daß alle Dinge verschieden sind von einander, ist ein sehr überflüssiger Satz, denn im Plural der Dinge liegt unmittelbar die Mehrheit und die ganz unbestimmte Verschiedenheit.—Der Satz aber: es giebt nicht zwei Dinge, die einander vollkommen gleich sind, drückt mehr, nämlich die bestimmte Verschiedenheit aus. Zwei Dinge sind nicht bloß zwei; die numerische Vielheit ist nur die Einerleiheit, sondern sie sind durch eine Bestimmung verschieden. Der Satz, daß es nicht zwei Dinge giebt, die einander gleich sind, fällt dem Vorstellen,—auch nach der Anekdote, an einem Hofe auf, wo ihn Leibniz vorgebracht und die Damen veranlaßt haben soll, unter Baumblättern zu suchen, ob sie nicht zwei gleiche finden.—Glückliche Zeiten für die Metaphysik, wo man sich am Hofe mit ihr beschäftigte, und wo es keiner andern Anstrengung bedurfte, ihre Sätze zu prüfen, als Baumblätter zu vergleichen!—Der Grund, daß jener Satz auffallend ist, liegt in dem Gesagten, daß zwei oder die numerische Mehrheit noch keine bestimmte Verschiedenheit enthält, und daß die Verschiedenheit als solche in ihrer Abstraktion zunächst gleichgültig gegen die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist. Das Vorstellen, indem es auch zur Bestimmung übergeht, nimmt diese Momente selbst als gegen einander gleichgültige auf, so daß das eine ohne das andere, die bloße Gleichheit der Dinge ohne die Ungleichheit zur Bestimmung hinreiche, oder daß die Dinge verschieden seyen, wenn sie auch nur numerisch Viele, verschiedene überhaupt, nicht ungleiche sind. Der Satz der Verschiedenheit hingegen drückt aus, daß die Dinge durch die Ungleichheit von einander verschieden sind, daß ihnen die Bestimmung der Ungleichheit so sehr zukomme als die der Gleichheit, denn erst beide zusammen machen den bestimmten Unterschied aus.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Dieser Satz nun, daß allen Dingen die Bestimmung der Ungleichheit zukommt, bedürfte eines Beweises; er kann nicht als unmittelbarer Satz aufgestellt werden, denn die gewöhnliche Weise des Erkennens selbst fotdert für die Verknüpfung verschiedener Bestimmungen in einem synthetischen Satze einen Beweis oder das Aufzeigen eines Dritten, worin sie vermittelt sind. Dieser Beweis müßte den Übergang der Identität in die Verschiedenheit, und dann den Übergang dieser in die bestimmte Verschiedenheit, in die Ungleichheit darthun. Dieß pflegt aber nicht geleistet zu werden; es ergab sich darin, daß die Verschiedenheit oder der äußerliche Unterschied, in Wahrheit in sich reflektirter, Unterschied an ihm selbst ist, daß das gleichgültige Bestehen des Verschiedenen das bloße Gesetztseyn, und damit nicht äußerlicher, gleichgültiger Unterschied, sondern Eine Beziehung der beiden Momente ist.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Es liegt darin auch die Auflösung und Nichtigkeit des Satzes der Verschiedenheit. Zwei Dinge sind nicht vollkommen gleich; so sind sie gleich und ungleich zugleich; gleich schon darin, daß sie Dinge oder zwei überhaupt sind, denn jedes ist ein Ding und ein Eins so gut als das andere,jedes also dasselbe, was das andere; ungleich aber sind sie durch die Annahme. Es ist somit die Bestimmung vorhanden, daß beide Momente, die Gleichheit und die Ungleichheit, in Einem und demselben verschieden, oder daß der außereinanderfallende Unterschied, zugleich eine und dieselbe Beziehung ist. Somit ist sie in Entgegensetzung übergegangen.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Das Zugleich der beiden Prädikate wird zwar durch das Insofern aus einander gehalten; daß zwei Dinge insofern sie gleich, insofern nicht ungleich, oder nach einer Seite und Rücksicht gleich, nach der andern Seite und Rücksicht aber ungleich sind. Damit wird die Einheit der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit aus dem Dinge entfernt, und was seine eigene, und die Reflexion der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit an sich wäre, als eine dem Dinge äußerliche Reflexion festgehalten. Diese ist es aber somit, die in einer und derselben Thätigkeit die zwei Seiten der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit unterscheidet, somit in Einer Thätigkeit beide enthält, die eine in die andere scheinen läßt und reflektirt.—Die gewöhnliche Zärtlichkeit für die Dinge aber, die nur dafür sorgt, daß diese sich nicht widersprechen, vergißt hier wie sonst, daß damit der Widerspruch nicht aufgelöst, sondern nur anderswohin, in die Subjektive oder äußere Reflexion überhaupt geschoben wird, und daß diese in der That die beiden Momente, welche durch diese Entfernung und Versetzung als bloßes Gesetztseyn ausgesprochen werden, als aufgehobene und auf einander bezogene in Einer Einheit enthält.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"cddddef47d065bd2ceef7f04f62e416e9101ca83cb8462d1991a91c0cfaf0058","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104807943341Z_dd508efb","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"cddddef47d065bd2ceef7f04f62e416e9101ca83cb8462d1991a91c0cfaf0058","sha256":"e49cf7b4bf1b4a3d4855fe801451afbbd126761fad06a2f0bd7042dfd8f90ef3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:48:07.943367+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Difference, like identity, is expressed in a proposition of its own. Besides, these two propositions remain held in indifferent difference from one another, so that each is valid on its own without regard to the other.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0002","text":"All things are different, or: There are not two things that are equal to one another.—This proposition is in fact opposed to the proposition of identity, for it states: A is a different [thing], thus A is also not A; or A is unequal to another, thus it is not A in general, but rather a determinate A. In place of the A in the identical proposition, every other substrate may be put, but A as unequal can no longer be interchanged with every other. It is indeed not supposed to be different from itself, but only from another; yet this difference is its own determination. As A identical with itself, it is the indeterminate; but as determinate, it is the opposite of this: it no longer has merely identity with itself, but also a negation, hence a difference of itself from itself in it.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104807943341Z_dd508efb:DISPLAY-0003","text":"That all things are different from one another is a very superfluous proposition, for in the plural of things there lies immediately multiplicity and wholly indeterminate difference.—But the proposition: there are not two things that are perfectly equal to one another, expresses more, namely determinate difference. Two things are not merely two; numerical multiplicity is only sameness, but they are different through a determination.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104807943341Z_dd508efb:DISPLAY-0004","text":"The proposition that there are not two things that are equal to one another strikes representation as remarkable,—also, according to the anecdote, at a court where Leibniz advanced it and is said to have induced the ladies to search among tree leaves to see whether they might not find two alike.—Happy times for metaphysics, when people occupied themselves with it at court, and when no other effort was required to test its propositions than to compare tree leaves!—The reason why that proposition is striking lies in what has been said, namely that two, or numerical multiplicity, does not yet contain determinate difference, and that difference as such, in its abstraction, is initially indifferent to equality and inequality.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104807943341Z_dd508efb:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Representation, in proceeding also to determination, takes these moments themselves as indifferent to one another, so that the one suffices for determination without the other: the mere equality of things without inequality; or that things are different even if they are merely numerically many, different in general, not unequal. The proposition of difference, on the other hand, expresses that things are different from one another through inequality, that the determination of inequality belongs to them just as much as that of equality, for only both together constitute determinate difference.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Now this proposition, that the determination of inequality belongs to all things, would require a proof; it cannot be set up as an immediate proposition, for the ordinary mode of cognition itself demands, for the connection of different determinations in a synthetic proposition, a proof or the showing of a third in which they are mediated. This proof would have to demonstrate the transition of identity into difference, and then the transition of the latter into determinate difference, into inequality. But this is not usually supplied; it emerged therein that difference, or external difference, is in truth difference reflected into itself, difference in itself; that the indifferent subsistence of the different is mere positedness, and therewith not external, indifferent difference, but one relation of the two moments.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Therein also lies the dissolution and nullity of the proposition of difference. Two things are not completely equal; thus they are equal and unequal at once: equal already in that they are things, or two in general, for each is a thing and a one just as much as the other; each, therefore, is the same as the other; but they are unequal through the assumption. Thus there is present the determination that both moments, equality and inequality, are different in one and the same [thing], or that the difference falling apart is at the same time one and the same relation. Thus it has passed over into opposition.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104807943341Z_dd508efb:DISPLAY-0008","text":"The at-once of the two predicates is indeed kept apart by the in-so-far-as: that two things, in so far as they are equal, are in so far not unequal, or are equal in one respect and regard, but unequal in the other respect and regard. Thereby the unity of equality and inequality is removed from the thing, and what would be its own reflection, and the reflection of equality and inequality in themselves, is maintained as a reflection external to the thing.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104807943341Z_dd508efb:DISPLAY-0009","text":"But it is this reflection that, in one and the same activity, distinguishes the two sides of equality and inequality, thus contains both in one activity, lets the one shine into the other and reflects it.—Yet the usual tenderness for things, which merely takes care that they should not contradict themselves, forgets here as elsewhere that contradiction is thereby not dissolved, but only shifted elsewhere, into subjective or external reflection in general, and that this reflection in fact contains in one unity the two moments which, through this removal and displacement, are expressed as mere positedness, as sublated and related to one another.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_29:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"4c890af202bf70dd07f5b1107d7042c116c2af13a2f5c1cfa35d3fb0c21a5cd1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0","title":"3. Opposition.","order":116,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_3DG0","text":"Im Gegensatze ist die bestimmte Reflexion, der Unterschied vollendet. Er ist die Einheit der Identität und der Verschiedenheit; seine Momente sind in Einer Identität verschiedene; so sind sie entgegengesetzte.\n\nDie Identität und der Unterschied sind die Momente des Unterschiedes innerhalb seiner selbst gehalten; sie sind reflektirte Momente seiner Einheit. Gleichheit und Ungleichheit aber sind die entäußerte Reflexion; ihre Identität mit sich ist nicht nur die Gleichgültigkeit eines jeden gegen das von ihm Unterschiedene, sondern gegen das An-und-Fürsichseyn, als solches; eine Identität mit sich gegen die in sich reflektirte; sie ist also die nicht in sich reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit. Das Gesetztseyn der Seiten der äußerlichen Reflexion ist daher ein Seyn; so wie ihr Nichtgesetztseyn ein Nichtseyn.\n\nDie Momente des Gegensatzes näher betrachtet, so sind sie das in sich reflektirte Gesetztseyn oder Bestimmung überhaupt. Das Gesetztseyn ist die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit; sie beide in sich reflektirt machen die Bestimmungen des Gegensatzes aus. Ihre Reflexion in sich besteht darin, daß jedes an ihm selbst die Einheit der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist. Die Gleichheit ist nur in der Reflexion, welche nach der Ungleichheit vergleicht, somit durch ihr anderes gleichgültiges Moment vermittelt; ebenso die Ungleichheit ist nur in derselben reflektirenden Beziehung, in welcher die Gleichheit ist. —Jedes dieser Momente ist also in seiner Bestimmtheit das Ganze. Es ist das Ganze, insofern es auch sein anderes Moment enthält; aber dieß sein anderes ist ein gleichgültig seyendes, so enthält jedes die Beziehung auf sein Nichtseyn, und ist nur die Reflexion in sich oder das Ganze als sich wesentlich auf sein Nichtseyn beziehend.\n\nDiese in sich reflektirte Gleichheit mit sich, die in ihr selbst die Beziehung auf die Ungleichheit enthält, ist das Positive; so die Ungleichheit die in ihr selbst die Beziehung auf ihr Nichtseyn, die Gleichheit enthält, ist das Negative.—Oder beide sind das Gesetztseyn; insofern nun die unterschiedene Bestimmtheit als unterschiedene bestimmte Beziehung des Gesetztseyns auf sich genommen wird, so ist der Gegensatz eines Theils das Gesetztseyn in seine Gleichheit mit sich reflektirt; andern Theils dasselbe in seine Ungleichheit mit sich reflektirt; das Positive und Negative.—Das Positive ist das Gesetztseyn als in die Gleichheit mit sich reflektirt; aber das reflektirte ist das Gesetztseyn, das ist, die Negation als Negation, so hat diese Reflexion in sich die Beziehung auf das Andere zu ihrer Bestimmung. Das Negative ist das Gesetztseyn als in die Ungleichheit reflektirt; aber das Gesetztseyn ist die Ungleichheit selbst, so ist diese Reflexion somit die Identität der Ungleichheit mit sich selbst und absolute Beziehung auf sich.—Beide also, das in die Gleichheit mit sich reflektirte Gesetztseyn hat die Ungleichheit, und das in die Ungleichheit mit sich reflektirte Gesetztseyn hat auch die Gleichheit an ihm.\n\nDas Positive und das Negative sind so die selbstständig gewordenen Seiten des Gegensatzes. Sie sind selbstständig, indem sie die Reflexion des Ganzen in sich sind, und sie gehören dem Gegensatze an, insofern es die Bestimmtheit ist, die als Ganzes in sich reflektirt ist. Um ihrer Selbstständigkeit willen machen sie den an sich bestimmten Gegensatz aus. Jedes ist es selbst und sein Anderes, dadurch hat jedes seine Bestimmtheit nicht an einem andern, sondern an ihm selbst.—Jedes bezieht sich auf sich selbst, nur als sich beziehend auf sein Anderes. Dieß hat die doppelte Seite; jedes ist Beziehung auf sein Nichtseyn als Aufheben dieses Andersseyns in sich; so ist sein Nichtseyn nur ein Moment in ihm. Aber andern Theils ist hier das Gesetztseyn ein Seyn, ein gleichgültiges Bestehen geworden; das andre seiner, das jedes enthält, ist daher auch das Nichtseyn dessen, in welchem es nur als Moment enthalten seyn soll. Jedes ist daher nur, insofern sein Nichtseyn ist, und zwar in einer identischen Beziehung.\n\nDie Bestimmungen, welche das Positive und Negative konstituiren, bestehen also darin, daß das Positive und das Negative erstens absolute Momente des Gegensatzes sind; ihr Bestehen ist untrennbar Eine Reflexion; es ist Eine Vermittelung, in welcher jedes durch das Nichtseyn seines Andern, damit durch sein Anderes oder sein eigenes Nichtseyn ist.—So sind sie Entgegengesetzte überhaupt; oder jedes ist nur das Entgegengesetzte des Andern; das eine ist noch nicht positiv, und das andre noch nicht negativ, sondern beide sind negativ gegen einander. Jedes ist so überhaupt erstens insofern das Andre ist; es ist durch das Andre, durch sein eignes Nichtseyn, das was es ist; es ist nur Gesetztseyn; zweitens es ist insofern das Andre nicht ist; es ist durch das Nichtseyn des Andern das was es ist; es ist Reflexion in sich.—Dieses beides ist aber die eine Vermittelung des Gegensatzes überhaupt, in der sie überhaupt nur Gesetzte sind.\n\nAber ferner dieß bloße Gesetztseyn ist in sich reflektirt überhaupt; das Positive und Negative ist nach diesem Momente der äußern Reflexion gleichgültig gegen jene erste Identität, worin sie nur Momente sind; oder indem jene erste Reflexion die eigne Reflexion des Positiven und Negativen in sich selbst, jedes sein Gesetztseyn an ihm selbst ist, so ist jedes gleichgültig gegen diese seine Reflexion in sein Nichtseyn, gegen sein eigenes Gesetztseyn. Die beiden Seiten sind so bloß verschiedene, und insofern ihre Bestimmtheit, positiv und negativ zu seyn, ihr Gesetztseyn gegen einander ausmacht, so ist jede nicht an ihr selbst so bestimmt, sondern ist nur Bestimmtheit überhaupt; jeder Seite kommt daher zwar eine der Bestimmtheiten von Positivem und Negativem zu; aber sie können verwechselt werden, und jede Seite ist von der Art, daß sie ebenso gut als positiv wie als negativ genommen werden kann.\n\nAber das Positive und Negative ist drittens nicht nur ein Gesetztes, noch bloß ein Gleichgültiges, sondern ihr Gesetztseyn oder die Beziehung auf das andere in einer Einheit, die nicht sie selbst sind, ist in jedes zurückgenommen. Jedes ist an ihm selbst positiv und negativ; das Positive und Negative ist die Reflexionsbestimmung an und für sich; erst in dieser Reflexion des Entgegengesetzten in sich ist es positiv und negativ. Das Positive hat die Beziehung auf das Andere, in der die Bestimmtheit des Positiven ist, an ihm selbst; ebenso das Negative ist nicht Negatives als gegen ein anderes, sondern hat die Bestimmtheit, wodurch es negativ ist, gleichfalls in ihm selbst.\n\nSo ist jedes Selbstständige, für sich seyende Einheit mit sich. Das Positive ist wohl ein Gesetztseyn, aber so daß für es das Gesetztseyn nur Gesetztseyn, als aufgehobenes ist. Es ist das Nichtentgegengesetzte; der aufgehobene Gegensatz, aber als Seite des Gegensatzes selbst.—Als positiv ist zwar Etwas bestimmt in Beziehung auf ein Andersseyn, aber so daß seine Natur dieß ist, nicht ein Gesetztes zu seyn; es ist die das Andersseyn negirende Reflexion in sich. Aber das Andere seiner, das Negative, ist selbst nicht mehr Gesetztseyn oder Moment, sondern ein selbstständiges Seyn; so ist die negirende Reflexion des Positiven in sich bestimmt, dieß sein Nichtseyn von sich auszuschließen.\n\nSo das Negative als absolute Reflexion ist nicht das unmittelbare Negative, sondern dasselbe als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn; das Negative an und für sich, das positiv auf sich selbst beruht. Als Reflexion in sich negirt es seine Beziehung auf Anderes; sein Anderes ist das Positive, ein selbstständiges Seyn;—seine negative Beziehung darauf ist daher, es aus sich auszuschließen. Das Negative ist das für sich bestehende Entgegengesetzte, gegen das Positive, das die Bestimmung des aufgehobenen Gegensatzes ist; der auf sich beruhende ganze Gegensatz, entgegengesetzt dem mit sich identischen Gesetztseyn.\n\nDas Positive und Negative ist hiermit nicht nur an sich positiv und negativ, sondern an und für sich. An sich sind sie es, insofern von ihrer ausschließenden Beziehung auf Anderes abstrahirt, und sie nur nach ihrer Bestimmung genommen werden. An sich ist etwas positiv oder negativ, indem es nicht bloß gegen Anderes so bestimmt seyn soll. Aber das Positive oder Negative nicht als Gesetztseyn und damit nicht als Entgegengesetztes, ist es jedes das Unmittelbare, Seyn und Nichtseyn. Das Positive und Negative sind aber die Momente des Gegensatzes, das Ansichseyn derselben macht nur die Form ihres Reflektirtseyns in sich aus. Es ist etwas an sich positiv, außer der Beziehung auf das Negative; und es ist etwas an sich negativ, außer der Beziehung auf das Negative; in dieser Bestimmung wird bloß an dem abstrakten Momente dieses Reflektirtseyns festgehalten. Allein das ansichseyende Positive oder Negative heißt wesentlich, daß entgegengesetzt zu seyn, nicht bloß Moment sey, noch der Vergleichung angehöre, sondern die eigene Bestimmung der Seiten des Gegensatzes ist. An sich positiv oder negativ sind sie also nicht außer der Beziehung auf Anderes, sondern daß diese Beziehung und zwar als ausschließende, die Bestimmung oder das Ansichseyn derselben ausmacht; hierin sind sie es also zugleich an und für sich.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0001","text":"Im Gegensatze ist die bestimmte Reflexion, der Unterschied vollendet. Er ist die Einheit der Identität und der Verschiedenheit; seine Momente sind in Einer Identität verschiedene; so sind sie entgegengesetzte.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"116.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0002","text":"Die Identität und der Unterschied sind die Momente des Unterschiedes innerhalb seiner selbst gehalten; sie sind reflektirte Momente seiner Einheit. Gleichheit und Ungleichheit aber sind die entäußerte Reflexion; ihre Identität mit sich ist nicht nur die Gleichgültigkeit eines jeden gegen das von ihm Unterschiedene, sondern gegen das An-und-Fürsichseyn, als solches; eine Identität mit sich gegen die in sich reflektirte; sie ist also die nicht in sich reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit. Das Gesetztseyn der Seiten der äußerlichen Reflexion ist daher ein Seyn; so wie ihr Nichtgesetztseyn ein Nichtseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"116.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0003","text":"Die Momente des Gegensatzes näher betrachtet, so sind sie das in sich reflektirte Gesetztseyn oder Bestimmung überhaupt. Das Gesetztseyn ist die Gleichheit und Ungleichheit; sie beide in sich reflektirt machen die Bestimmungen des Gegensatzes aus. Ihre Reflexion in sich besteht darin, daß jedes an ihm selbst die Einheit der Gleichheit und Ungleichheit ist. Die Gleichheit ist nur in der Reflexion, welche nach der Ungleichheit vergleicht, somit durch ihr anderes gleichgültiges Moment vermittelt; ebenso die Ungleichheit ist nur in derselben reflektirenden Beziehung, in welcher die Gleichheit ist. —Jedes dieser Momente ist also in seiner Bestimmtheit das Ganze.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"116.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0004","text":"Es ist das Ganze, insofern es auch sein anderes Moment enthält; aber dieß sein anderes ist ein gleichgültig seyendes, so enthält jedes die Beziehung auf sein Nichtseyn, und ist nur die Reflexion in sich oder das Ganze als sich wesentlich auf sein Nichtseyn beziehend.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"116.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0005","text":"Diese in sich reflektirte Gleichheit mit sich, die in ihr selbst die Beziehung auf die Ungleichheit enthält, ist das Positive; so die Ungleichheit die in ihr selbst die Beziehung auf ihr Nichtseyn, die Gleichheit enthält, ist das Negative.—Oder beide sind das Gesetztseyn; insofern nun die unterschiedene Bestimmtheit als unterschiedene bestimmte Beziehung des Gesetztseyns auf sich genommen wird, so ist der Gegensatz eines Theils das Gesetztseyn in seine Gleichheit mit sich reflektirt; andern Theils dasselbe in seine Ungleichheit mit sich reflektirt; das Positive und Negative.—Das Positive ist das Gesetztseyn als in die Gleichheit mit sich reflektirt; aber das reflektirte ist das Gesetztseyn, das ist, die Negation als Negation, so hat diese Reflexion in sich die Beziehung auf das Andere zu ihrer Bestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"116.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0006","text":"Das Negative ist das Gesetztseyn als in die Ungleichheit reflektirt; aber das Gesetztseyn ist die Ungleichheit selbst, so ist diese Reflexion somit die Identität der Ungleichheit mit sich selbst und absolute Beziehung auf sich.—Beide also, das in die Gleichheit mit sich reflektirte Gesetztseyn hat die Ungleichheit, und das in die Ungleichheit mit sich reflektirte Gesetztseyn hat auch die Gleichheit an ihm.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"116.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0007","text":"Das Positive und das Negative sind so die selbstständig gewordenen Seiten des Gegensatzes. Sie sind selbstständig, indem sie die Reflexion des Ganzen in sich sind, und sie gehören dem Gegensatze an, insofern es die Bestimmtheit ist, die als Ganzes in sich reflektirt ist. Um ihrer Selbstständigkeit willen machen sie den an sich bestimmten Gegensatz aus. Jedes ist es selbst und sein Anderes, dadurch hat jedes seine Bestimmtheit nicht an einem andern, sondern an ihm selbst.—Jedes bezieht sich auf sich selbst, nur als sich beziehend auf sein Anderes. Dieß hat die doppelte Seite; jedes ist Beziehung auf sein Nichtseyn als Aufheben dieses Andersseyns in sich; so ist sein Nichtseyn nur ein Moment in ihm.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"116.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0008","text":"Aber andern Theils ist hier das Gesetztseyn ein Seyn, ein gleichgültiges Bestehen geworden; das andre seiner, das jedes enthält, ist daher auch das Nichtseyn dessen, in welchem es nur als Moment enthalten seyn soll. Jedes ist daher nur, insofern sein Nichtseyn ist, und zwar in einer identischen Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"116.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0009","text":"Die Bestimmungen, welche das Positive und Negative konstituiren, bestehen also darin, daß das Positive und das Negative erstens absolute Momente des Gegensatzes sind; ihr Bestehen ist untrennbar Eine Reflexion; es ist Eine Vermittelung, in welcher jedes durch das Nichtseyn seines Andern, damit durch sein Anderes oder sein eigenes Nichtseyn ist.—So sind sie Entgegengesetzte überhaupt; oder jedes ist nur das Entgegengesetzte des Andern; das eine ist noch nicht positiv, und das andre noch nicht negativ, sondern beide sind negativ gegen einander.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"116.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0010","text":"Jedes ist so überhaupt erstens insofern das Andre ist; es ist durch das Andre, durch sein eignes Nichtseyn, das was es ist; es ist nur Gesetztseyn; zweitens es ist insofern das Andre nicht ist; es ist durch das Nichtseyn des Andern das was es ist; es ist Reflexion in sich.—Dieses beides ist aber die eine Vermittelung des Gegensatzes überhaupt, in der sie überhaupt nur Gesetzte sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"116.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0011","text":"Aber ferner dieß bloße Gesetztseyn ist in sich reflektirt überhaupt; das Positive und Negative ist nach diesem Momente der äußern Reflexion gleichgültig gegen jene erste Identität, worin sie nur Momente sind; oder indem jene erste Reflexion die eigne Reflexion des Positiven und Negativen in sich selbst, jedes sein Gesetztseyn an ihm selbst ist, so ist jedes gleichgültig gegen diese seine Reflexion in sein Nichtseyn, gegen sein eigenes Gesetztseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"116.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0012","text":"Die beiden Seiten sind so bloß verschiedene, und insofern ihre Bestimmtheit, positiv und negativ zu seyn, ihr Gesetztseyn gegen einander ausmacht, so ist jede nicht an ihr selbst so bestimmt, sondern ist nur Bestimmtheit überhaupt; jeder Seite kommt daher zwar eine der Bestimmtheiten von Positivem und Negativem zu; aber sie können verwechselt werden, und jede Seite ist von der Art, daß sie ebenso gut als positiv wie als negativ genommen werden kann.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"116.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0013","text":"Aber das Positive und Negative ist drittens nicht nur ein Gesetztes, noch bloß ein Gleichgültiges, sondern ihr Gesetztseyn oder die Beziehung auf das andere in einer Einheit, die nicht sie selbst sind, ist in jedes zurückgenommen. Jedes ist an ihm selbst positiv und negativ; das Positive und Negative ist die Reflexionsbestimmung an und für sich; erst in dieser Reflexion des Entgegengesetzten in sich ist es positiv und negativ. Das Positive hat die Beziehung auf das Andere, in der die Bestimmtheit des Positiven ist, an ihm selbst; ebenso das Negative ist nicht Negatives als gegen ein anderes, sondern hat die Bestimmtheit, wodurch es negativ ist, gleichfalls in ihm selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"116.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0014","text":"So ist jedes Selbstständige, für sich seyende Einheit mit sich. Das Positive ist wohl ein Gesetztseyn, aber so daß für es das Gesetztseyn nur Gesetztseyn, als aufgehobenes ist. Es ist das Nichtentgegengesetzte; der aufgehobene Gegensatz, aber als Seite des Gegensatzes selbst.—Als positiv ist zwar Etwas bestimmt in Beziehung auf ein Andersseyn, aber so daß seine Natur dieß ist, nicht ein Gesetztes zu seyn; es ist die das Andersseyn negirende Reflexion in sich. Aber das Andere seiner, das Negative, ist selbst nicht mehr Gesetztseyn oder Moment, sondern ein selbstständiges Seyn; so ist die negirende Reflexion des Positiven in sich bestimmt, dieß sein Nichtseyn von sich auszuschließen.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"116.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0015","text":"So das Negative als absolute Reflexion ist nicht das unmittelbare Negative, sondern dasselbe als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn; das Negative an und für sich, das positiv auf sich selbst beruht. Als Reflexion in sich negirt es seine Beziehung auf Anderes; sein Anderes ist das Positive, ein selbstständiges Seyn;—seine negative Beziehung darauf ist daher, es aus sich auszuschließen. Das Negative ist das für sich bestehende Entgegengesetzte, gegen das Positive, das die Bestimmung des aufgehobenen Gegensatzes ist; der auf sich beruhende ganze Gegensatz, entgegengesetzt dem mit sich identischen Gesetztseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"116.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0016","text":"Das Positive und Negative ist hiermit nicht nur an sich positiv und negativ, sondern an und für sich. An sich sind sie es, insofern von ihrer ausschließenden Beziehung auf Anderes abstrahirt, und sie nur nach ihrer Bestimmung genommen werden. An sich ist etwas positiv oder negativ, indem es nicht bloß gegen Anderes so bestimmt seyn soll. Aber das Positive oder Negative nicht als Gesetztseyn und damit nicht als Entgegengesetztes, ist es jedes das Unmittelbare, Seyn und Nichtseyn. Das Positive und Negative sind aber die Momente des Gegensatzes, das Ansichseyn derselben macht nur die Form ihres Reflektirtseyns in sich aus. Es ist etwas an sich positiv, außer der Beziehung auf das Negative; und es ist etwas an sich negativ, außer der Beziehung auf das Negative; in dieser Bestimmung wird bloß an dem abstrakten Momente dieses Reflektirtseyns festgehalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"116.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0017","text":"Allein das ansichseyende Positive oder Negative heißt wesentlich, daß entgegengesetzt zu seyn, nicht bloß Moment sey, noch der Vergleichung angehöre, sondern die eigene Bestimmung der Seiten des Gegensatzes ist. An sich positiv oder negativ sind sie also nicht außer der Beziehung auf Anderes, sondern daß diese Beziehung und zwar als ausschließende, die Bestimmung oder das Ansichseyn derselben ausmacht; hierin sind sie es also zugleich an und für sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"116.17"}],"sha256":"0b4971757c7d69b3894a8b0959a841463f40840cf697c31c47a676efbf2547a2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104825365355Z_f11057e0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"3. Opposition.","source_sha256":"0b4971757c7d69b3894a8b0959a841463f40840cf697c31c47a676efbf2547a2","sha256":"d19c4dad86c2d123c341df77aef64d09f812a954892c907c36c5aeabb2fbd6d4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:48:25.365383+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0001","text":"In opposition, by contrast, determinate reflection, difference, is complete. It is the unity of identity and diversity; its moments are different in one identity; thus they are opposed.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"116.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0002","text":"Identity and difference are the moments of difference held within itself; they are reflected moments of its unity. Equality and inequality, however, are externalized reflection; their identity with themselves is not merely the indifference of each toward that which is different from it, but toward being-in-and-for-itself as such; an identity with itself as against that which is reflected into itself; it is thus immediacy not reflected into itself. The positedness of the sides of external reflection is therefore a being; just as their non-positedness is a non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"116.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0003","text":"The moments of opposition, considered more closely, are positedness reflected into itself, or determinateness in general. Positedness is equality and inequality; both, reflected into themselves, constitute the determinations of opposition. Their reflection into themselves consists in each being, in itself, the unity of equality and inequality. Equality is only in the reflection which compares according to inequality, thus mediated through its other indifferent moment; likewise, inequality is only in the same reflecting relation in which equality is. —Each of these moments is therefore, in its determinateness, the whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"116.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0004","text":"It is the whole insofar as it also contains its other moment; but this its other is an indifferent being, and thus each contains the relation to its non-being, and is only reflection into itself, or the whole as essentially relating itself to its non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"116.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0005","text":"This equality with itself reflected into itself, which contains within itself the relation to inequality, is the positive; likewise inequality, which contains within itself the relation to its non-being, equality, is the negative.—Or both are positedness; insofar, now, as the distinct determinateness is taken as the distinct determinate relation of positedness to itself, opposition is, on the one hand, positedness reflected into its equality with itself; on the other hand, the same reflected into its inequality with itself; the positive and negative.—The positive is positedness as reflected into equality with itself; but what is reflected is positedness, that is, negation as negation; hence this reflection contains within itself the relation to the other as its determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"116.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0006","text":"The negative is positedness as reflected into inequality; but positedness is inequality itself, and thus this reflection is consequently the identity of inequality with itself and absolute relation to itself.—Both, therefore, positedness reflected into equality with itself, has inequality, and positedness reflected into inequality with itself also has equality in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"116.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0007","text":"The positive and the negative are thus the sides of opposition that have become self-subsistent. They are self-subsistent in that they are the reflection of the whole into themselves, and they belong to opposition insofar as it is determinateness reflected into itself as a whole. By virtue of their self-subsistence, they constitute opposition determined in itself. Each is itself and its other; thereby each has its determinateness not in another, but in itself.—Each relates to itself only as relating to its other. This has the double aspect: each is relation to its non-being as sublation of this otherness within itself; thus its non-being is only a moment in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"116.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0008","text":"But, on the other hand, here positedness has become a being, an indifferent subsistence; its other, which each contains, is therefore also the non-being of that in which it is supposed to be contained only as a moment. Each therefore is only insofar as its non-being is, and indeed in an identical relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"116.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0009","text":"The determinations which constitute the positive and negative thus consist in this: first, the positive and negative are absolute moments of opposition; their subsistence is inseparably one reflection; it is one mediation, in which each is through the non-being of its other, and hence through its other or its own non-being.—Thus they are opposites in general; or each is only the opposite of the other; the one is not yet positive, and the other not yet negative, but both are negative toward one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"116.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0010","text":"Thus each is in general, first, insofar as the other is; it is through the other, through its own non-being, what it is; it is only positedness; second, it is insofar as the other is not; it is through the non-being of the other what it is; it is reflection into itself.—But these two are the one mediation of opposition in general, in which they are in general only posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"116.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0011","text":"But further, this mere positedness is reflected into itself in general; according to this moment of external reflection, the positive and negative are indifferent toward that first identity in which they are only moments; or, since that first reflection is the positive’s and negative’s own reflection into themselves, each’s positedness in itself, each is indifferent toward this its reflection into its non-being, toward its own positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"116.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0012","text":"The two sides are thus merely different, and insofar as their determinateness of being positive and negative constitutes their positedness toward one another, neither is so determined in itself, but is only determinateness in general; each side therefore does indeed accrue one of the determinatenesses of positive and negative; but they can be interchanged, and each side is of such a kind that it can equally well be taken as positive or as negative.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"116.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0013","text":"But thirdly, the positive and negative are not merely something posited, nor merely something indifferent, but their positedness, or the relation to the other in a unity which is not themselves, is taken back into each. Each is in itself positive and negative; the positive and negative are determinations of reflection in and for themselves; only in this reflection of the opposite into itself is it positive and negative. The positive has in itself the relation to the other in which the determinateness of the positive consists; likewise, the negative is not negative merely as against another, but likewise has in itself the determinateness through which it is negative.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"116.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0014","text":"Thus each is a self-subsistent unity with itself, being-for-itself. The positive is indeed a positedness, but in such a way that, for it, positedness is only positedness as sublated. It is the non-opposed; the sublated opposition, but as a side of opposition itself.—As positive, something is indeed determined in relation to an otherness, but in such a way that its nature is not to be something posited; it is reflection into itself negating otherness. But its other, the negative, is itself no longer positedness or moment, but a self-subsistent being; thus the positive’s negating reflection into itself is determined to exclude this its non-being from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"116.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0015","text":"Thus the negative as absolute reflection is not the immediate negative, but the same as sublated positedness; the negative in and for itself, which rests positively upon itself. As reflection into itself, it negates its relation to another; its other is the positive, a self-subsistent being;—its negative relation to this is therefore to exclude it from itself. The negative is the opposite subsisting for itself, as against the positive, which is the determination of sublated opposition; the whole opposition resting upon itself, opposed to positedness identical with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"116.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0016","text":"The positive and negative are hereby not only positive and negative in themselves, but in and for themselves. They are so in themselves insofar as abstraction is made from their exclusive relation to another and they are taken only according to their determination. Something is positive or negative in itself insofar as it is not supposed to be so determined merely as against another. But the positive or negative not as positedness and hence not as an opposite, each is the immediate, being and non-being. The positive and negative are, however, the moments of opposition; their being-in-itself constitutes only the form of their being reflected into themselves. Something is positive in itself, apart from the relation to the negative; and something is negative in itself, apart from the relation to the negative; in this determination one holds fast merely to the abstract moment of this being reflected into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"116.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0017","text":"Yet the positive or negative that is in itself essentially means that being opposed is not merely a moment, nor belongs to comparison, but is the proper determination of the sides of opposition. Thus they are positive or negative in themselves not apart from the relation to another, but rather in that this relation, and indeed as exclusive, constitutes their determination or their being-in-itself; in this they are therefore at the same time in and for themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"116.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_3DG0:P0017"]}],"source_digest":"04d1028cf438cb26f666251fcd80aa0f129b3586adbc908838764fddb0ca23b6","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"3. Der Gegensatz."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"3. Der Gegensatz.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30","title":"Remark.","order":117,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_30","text":"Es ist hier der Begriff des Positiven und Negativen anzuführen, wie er in der Arithmetik vorkommt. Er wird darin als bekannt vorausgesetzt; weil er aber nicht in seinem bestimmten Unterschiede aufgefaßt wird, entgeht er nicht unauflösbaren Schwierigkeiten und Verwicklungen. Es haben sich so eben die beiden realen Bestimmungen des Positiven und Negativen ergeben,—außer dem einfachen Begriffe ihrer Entgegensetzung,—daß nämlich das erstemal, ein nur verschiedenes, unmittelbares Daseyn zu Grunde liegt, dessen einfache Reflexion in sich unterschieden wird von seinem Gesetztseyn, der Entgegensetzung selbst. Diese gilt daher nur als nicht an und für sich seyend, und dem Verschiedenen zwar zukommend, so daß jedes ein Entgegengesetztes überhaupt ist, aber auch gleichgültig dagegen für sich besteht, und es einerley ist, welches der beiden entgegengesetzten Verschiedenen als positiv oder als negativ betrachte werde.—Das andremal aber ist das Positive das an sich selbst Positive, das Negative das an sich selbst Negative, so daß das Verschiedene nicht gleichgültig dagegen, sondern dieß seine Bestimmung an und für sich ist.—Diese beiden Formen des Positiven und Negativen kommen gleich in den ersten Bestimmungen vor, in denen sie in der Arithmetik gebraucht werden.\n\nDas + a und—a sind zuerst entgegengesetzte Größen überhaupt; a ist die beiden zum Grunde liegende, ansichseyende Einheit, das gegen die Entgegensetzung selbst gleichgültige, das hier ohne weitern Begriff als todte Grundlage dient. Das—a ist zwar als das Negative, das + a als das Positive bezeichnet, aber das eine ist so gut ein Entgegengesetztes als das andere.\n\nFerner ist a nicht nur die einfache zum Grunde liegende Einheit, sondern als + a und—a, ist sie die Reflexion dieser Entgegengesetzten in sich; es sind zwei verschiedene a vorhanden und es ist gleichgültig, welches von beiden inan als das positive oder negative bezeichnen will; beide haben ein besonderes Bestehen und sind positiv.\n\nNach jener ersten Seite ist + y—y = 0; oder in—8 + 3, sind die 3 positiven, negative im 8. Die Entgegengesetzten heben sich in ihrer Verbindung auf. Eine Stunde Wegs nach Osten gemacht, und ebenso viel zurück nach Westen hebt den erst gemachten Weg auf; so viel Schulden, um so viel weniger Vermögen, und so viel Vermögen vorhanden ist, so viel hebt sich von den Schulden auf. Die Stunde Wegs nach Osten ist zugleich nicht der positive Weg an sich, noch der nach Westen der negative Weg; sondern diese Richtungen sind gleichgültig gegen diese Bestimmtheit des Gegensatzes; nur eine dritte außer ihnen fallende Rücksicht macht die eine zur positiven, die andere zur negativen. So auch die Schulden sind nicht an und für sich das Negative; sie sind es nur in Beziehung auf den Schuldner; für den Gläubiger sind sie sein positives Vermögen; sie sind eine Summe Geld, oder was es sey von einem gewissen Werth, das nach außerhalb seiner fallenden Rücksichten Schulden oder Vermögen ist.\n\nDie Entgegengesetzten heben sich zwar in ihrer Beziehung auf, so daß das Resultat gleich Null ist; aber es ist in ihnen auch ihre identische Beziehung vorhanden, die gegen den Gegensatz selbst gleichgültig ist; so machen sie Eines aus. Wie so eben von der Summe Geld erinnert worden, die nur Eine Summe ist, oder das a, das nur Ein a ist im + a und—a; auch der Weg, der nur ein Stück Wegs ist, nicht zwei Wege, deren einer nach Osten, der andere nach Westen ginge. So auch eine Ordinate y, die dasselbe ist, auf dieser oder jener Seite der Axe genommen; insofern ist + y—y = y; sie ist nur die Ordinate, es ist nur Eine Bestimmung und Gesetz derselben.\n\nFerner aber sind die Entgegengesetzten nicht nur Ein Gleichgültiges, sondern auch zwei Gleichgültige. Sie sind nämlich als Entgegengesetzte auch in sich Reflektirte, und bestehen so als Verschiedene.\n\nSo sind in—8 + 3 überhaupt elf Einheiten vorhanden; + y,—y, sind Ordinaten auf der entgegengesetzten Seite der Axe, wo jede ein gegen diese Grenze und gegen ihren Gegensatz gleichgültiges Daseyn ist; so ist + y—y = 2 y.—Auch der nach Osten und nach Westen zurückgelegte Weg, ist die Summe einer zweifachen Bemühung, oder die Summe von zwei Zeitperioden. Ebenso ist in der Staatsökonomie ein Quantum von Geld, oder von Werth, nicht nur dieß Eine Quantum als Mittel der Subsistenz, sondern es ist ein verdoppeltes; es ist Mittel der Subsistenz sowohl für den Gläubiger als den Schuldner. Das Staatsvermögen berechnet sich nicht bloß als Summe des baaren Gelds und des sonstigen Werths von den Immobilien und Mobilien, der im Staate vorhanden ist, noch weniger aber als Summe, die übrig bliebe nach Abzug des passiven Vermögens vom activen, sondern das Kapital, wenn seine active und passive Bestimmung sich auch zur Null reducirten, bleibt erstens positives Kapital; als + a—a = a; aber zweitens indem es auf vielfältige Weise passives, verliehenes und wieder verliehenes ist, ist es dadurch ein sehr vervielfältigtes Mittel.\n\nNicht nur aber sind die entgegengesetzten Größen, einer Seits bloß entgegengesetzte überhaupt, anderer Seits reale oder gleichgültige. Sondern ob zwar das Quantum selbst das gleichgültig begrenzte Seyn ist, so kommt doch an ihm auch das an sich Positive und das an sich Negative vor. Das a z.B. insofern es kein Zeichen hat, gilt dafür, daß es als positives zu nehmmen sey, wenn es zu bezeichnen ist. Wenn es nur überhaupt ein entgegengesetztes werden sollte, so könnte es ebenso gut als—a genommen werden. Aber das positive Zeichen wird ihm unmittelbar gegeben, weil das Positive für sich die eigenthümliche Bedeutung des Unmittelbaren, als mit sich identischen, gegen die Entgegensetzung hat.\n\nFerner indem positive und negative Größen addirt oder subtrahirt werden, gelten sie als solche, die für sich positiv und negativ seyen, und es nicht bloß durch die Beziehung des Addirens oder Subtrahirens, auf diese äußerliche Weise werden. In 8—(- 3) heißt das erste Minus entgegengesetzt gegen 8, das zweite Minus aber (- 3) gilt als entgegengesetztes an sich, außer dieser Beziehung.\n\nNäher tritt dieß bei der Multiplikation und Division hervor; hier ist das Positive wesentlich als das Nichtentgegengesetzte, das Negative hingegen als das Entgegengesetzte zu nehmen, nicht beide Bestimmungen auf gleiche Weise nur als Entgegengesetzte überhaupt. Indem die Lehrbücher in den Beweisen, wie sich die Zeichen in diesen beiden Rechnungsarten verhalten, bei dem Begriffe der entgegengesetzten Größen überhaupt stehen bleiben, so sind diese Beweise unvollständig und verwickeln sich in Widersprüche.—Plus und Minus erhalten aber bei der Multiplikation und Division die bestimmtere Bedeutung von Positivem und Negativem an sich, weil das Verhältniß der Faktoren, Einheit und Anzahl gegen einander zu seyn, nicht ein bloßes Verhältniß des Mehrens und Minderns ist, wie bei dem Addiren und Subtrahiren, sondern ein qualitatives; womit auch Plus und Minus die qualitative Bedeutung des Positiven und Negativen erhält.—Ohne diese Bestimmung und bloß aus dem Begriffe entgegengesetzter Größen, kann leicht die schiefe Folgerung gezogen werden, daß wenn—a.-a =—a[hoch 2] ist, umgekehrt +a.—a = +a[hoch 2] gebe. Indem der eine Faktor die Anzahl und der andere die Einheit, und zwar der voranstehende wie gewöhnlich die erstere bedeutet, so unterscheiden sich die beiden Ausdrücke—a.+a und +a.-a dadurch, daß im erstern +a die Einheit und—a die Anzahl, und im andern es umgekehrt ist. Es pflegt nun beim erstern gesagt zu werden, wenn ich +a nehmen soll—a mal, so nehme ich +a nicht bloß a mal, sondern zugleich auf die ihm entgegengesetzte Weise, +a mahl—a; also da es Plus ist, so habe ich es negativ zu nehmen, und das Produkt ist—a[hoch 2].—Wenn aber im zweiten Falle—a zu nehmen ist +a mal, so soll—a gleichfalls nicht—a mal genommen werden, sondern in der ihm entgegengesetzten Bestimmung nämlich +a mal. Nach dem Räsonnement des ersten Falles folgt also, daß das Produkt +a[hoch 2] seyn müsse.—Ebenso bei der Division.\n\nDiese Konsequenz ist nothwendig, insofern Plus und Minus nur als entgegengesetzte Größen überhaupt genommen werden; dem Minus wird im ersten Falle die Kraft zugeschrieben, das Plus zu verändern; aber im andern sollte Plus nicht dieselbe Kraft über Minus haben, ungeachtet es so gut eine entgegengesetzte Größebestimmung ist, als dieses. In der That hat Plus diese Kraft nicht, denn es ist hier nach seiner qualitativen Bestimmung gegen Minus zu nehmen, indem die Faktoren ein qualitatives Verhältniß zu einander haben. Insofern ist also das Negative hier das an sich Entgegengesetzte als solches, das Positive aber ist das Unbestimmte, Gleichgültige überhaupt; es ist wohl auch das Negative, aber des Andern, nicht an ihm selbst.—Eine Bestimmung als Negation kommt also allein durch das Negative herein, nicht durch das Positive.\n\nSo ist denn auch—a.—a = +a[hoch 2], darum weil das negative a nicht bloß auf die entgegengesetzte Weise, (so würde es zu nehmen seyn, mit—a multiplicirt) sondern weil es negativ genommen werden soll. Die Negation der Negation aber ist das Positive.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0001","text":"Es ist hier der Begriff des Positiven und Negativen anzuführen, wie er in der Arithmetik vorkommt. Er wird darin als bekannt vorausgesetzt; weil er aber nicht in seinem bestimmten Unterschiede aufgefaßt wird, entgeht er nicht unauflösbaren Schwierigkeiten und Verwicklungen. Es haben sich so eben die beiden realen Bestimmungen des Positiven und Negativen ergeben,—außer dem einfachen Begriffe ihrer Entgegensetzung,—daß nämlich das erstemal, ein nur verschiedenes, unmittelbares Daseyn zu Grunde liegt, dessen einfache Reflexion in sich unterschieden wird von seinem Gesetztseyn, der Entgegensetzung selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"117.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0002","text":"Diese gilt daher nur als nicht an und für sich seyend, und dem Verschiedenen zwar zukommend, so daß jedes ein Entgegengesetztes überhaupt ist, aber auch gleichgültig dagegen für sich besteht, und es einerley ist, welches der beiden entgegengesetzten Verschiedenen als positiv oder als negativ betrachte werde.—Das andremal aber ist das Positive das an sich selbst Positive, das Negative das an sich selbst Negative, so daß das Verschiedene nicht gleichgültig dagegen, sondern dieß seine Bestimmung an und für sich ist.—Diese beiden Formen des Positiven und Negativen kommen gleich in den ersten Bestimmungen vor, in denen sie in der Arithmetik gebraucht werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"117.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0003","text":"Das + a und—a sind zuerst entgegengesetzte Größen überhaupt; a ist die beiden zum Grunde liegende, ansichseyende Einheit, das gegen die Entgegensetzung selbst gleichgültige, das hier ohne weitern Begriff als todte Grundlage dient. Das—a ist zwar als das Negative, das + a als das Positive bezeichnet, aber das eine ist so gut ein Entgegengesetztes als das andere.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"117.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0004","text":"Ferner ist a nicht nur die einfache zum Grunde liegende Einheit, sondern als + a und—a, ist sie die Reflexion dieser Entgegengesetzten in sich; es sind zwei verschiedene a vorhanden und es ist gleichgültig, welches von beiden inan als das positive oder negative bezeichnen will; beide haben ein besonderes Bestehen und sind positiv.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"117.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0005","text":"Nach jener ersten Seite ist + y—y = 0; oder in—8 + 3, sind die 3 positiven, negative im 8. Die Entgegengesetzten heben sich in ihrer Verbindung auf. Eine Stunde Wegs nach Osten gemacht, und ebenso viel zurück nach Westen hebt den erst gemachten Weg auf; so viel Schulden, um so viel weniger Vermögen, und so viel Vermögen vorhanden ist, so viel hebt sich von den Schulden auf. Die Stunde Wegs nach Osten ist zugleich nicht der positive Weg an sich, noch der nach Westen der negative Weg; sondern diese Richtungen sind gleichgültig gegen diese Bestimmtheit des Gegensatzes; nur eine dritte außer ihnen fallende Rücksicht macht die eine zur positiven, die andere zur negativen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"117.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0006","text":"So auch die Schulden sind nicht an und für sich das Negative; sie sind es nur in Beziehung auf den Schuldner; für den Gläubiger sind sie sein positives Vermögen; sie sind eine Summe Geld, oder was es sey von einem gewissen Werth, das nach außerhalb seiner fallenden Rücksichten Schulden oder Vermögen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"117.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0007","text":"Die Entgegengesetzten heben sich zwar in ihrer Beziehung auf, so daß das Resultat gleich Null ist; aber es ist in ihnen auch ihre identische Beziehung vorhanden, die gegen den Gegensatz selbst gleichgültig ist; so machen sie Eines aus. Wie so eben von der Summe Geld erinnert worden, die nur Eine Summe ist, oder das a, das nur Ein a ist im + a und—a; auch der Weg, der nur ein Stück Wegs ist, nicht zwei Wege, deren einer nach Osten, der andere nach Westen ginge. So auch eine Ordinate y, die dasselbe ist, auf dieser oder jener Seite der Axe genommen; insofern ist + y—y = y; sie ist nur die Ordinate, es ist nur Eine Bestimmung und Gesetz derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"117.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0008","text":"Ferner aber sind die Entgegengesetzten nicht nur Ein Gleichgültiges, sondern auch zwei Gleichgültige. Sie sind nämlich als Entgegengesetzte auch in sich Reflektirte, und bestehen so als Verschiedene.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"117.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0009","text":"So sind in—8 + 3 überhaupt elf Einheiten vorhanden; + y,—y, sind Ordinaten auf der entgegengesetzten Seite der Axe, wo jede ein gegen diese Grenze und gegen ihren Gegensatz gleichgültiges Daseyn ist; so ist + y—y = 2 y.—Auch der nach Osten und nach Westen zurückgelegte Weg, ist die Summe einer zweifachen Bemühung, oder die Summe von zwei Zeitperioden. Ebenso ist in der Staatsökonomie ein Quantum von Geld, oder von Werth, nicht nur dieß Eine Quantum als Mittel der Subsistenz, sondern es ist ein verdoppeltes; es ist Mittel der Subsistenz sowohl für den Gläubiger als den Schuldner.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"117.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0010","text":"Das Staatsvermögen berechnet sich nicht bloß als Summe des baaren Gelds und des sonstigen Werths von den Immobilien und Mobilien, der im Staate vorhanden ist, noch weniger aber als Summe, die übrig bliebe nach Abzug des passiven Vermögens vom activen, sondern das Kapital, wenn seine active und passive Bestimmung sich auch zur Null reducirten, bleibt erstens positives Kapital; als + a—a = a; aber zweitens indem es auf vielfältige Weise passives, verliehenes und wieder verliehenes ist, ist es dadurch ein sehr vervielfältigtes Mittel.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"117.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0011","text":"Nicht nur aber sind die entgegengesetzten Größen, einer Seits bloß entgegengesetzte überhaupt, anderer Seits reale oder gleichgültige. Sondern ob zwar das Quantum selbst das gleichgültig begrenzte Seyn ist, so kommt doch an ihm auch das an sich Positive und das an sich Negative vor. Das a z.B. insofern es kein Zeichen hat, gilt dafür, daß es als positives zu nehmmen sey, wenn es zu bezeichnen ist. Wenn es nur überhaupt ein entgegengesetztes werden sollte, so könnte es ebenso gut als—a genommen werden. Aber das positive Zeichen wird ihm unmittelbar gegeben, weil das Positive für sich die eigenthümliche Bedeutung des Unmittelbaren, als mit sich identischen, gegen die Entgegensetzung hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"117.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0012","text":"Ferner indem positive und negative Größen addirt oder subtrahirt werden, gelten sie als solche, die für sich positiv und negativ seyen, und es nicht bloß durch die Beziehung des Addirens oder Subtrahirens, auf diese äußerliche Weise werden. In 8—(- 3) heißt das erste Minus entgegengesetzt gegen 8, das zweite Minus aber (- 3) gilt als entgegengesetztes an sich, außer dieser Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"117.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0013","text":"Näher tritt dieß bei der Multiplikation und Division hervor; hier ist das Positive wesentlich als das Nichtentgegengesetzte, das Negative hingegen als das Entgegengesetzte zu nehmen, nicht beide Bestimmungen auf gleiche Weise nur als Entgegengesetzte überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"117.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0014","text":"Indem die Lehrbücher in den Beweisen, wie sich die Zeichen in diesen beiden Rechnungsarten verhalten, bei dem Begriffe der entgegengesetzten Größen überhaupt stehen bleiben, so sind diese Beweise unvollständig und verwickeln sich in Widersprüche.—Plus und Minus erhalten aber bei der Multiplikation und Division die bestimmtere Bedeutung von Positivem und Negativem an sich, weil das Verhältniß der Faktoren, Einheit und Anzahl gegen einander zu seyn, nicht ein bloßes Verhältniß des Mehrens und Minderns ist, wie bei dem Addiren und Subtrahiren, sondern ein qualitatives; womit auch Plus und Minus die qualitative Bedeutung des Positiven und Negativen erhält.—Ohne diese Bestimmung und bloß aus dem Begriffe entgegengesetzter Größen, kann leicht die schiefe Folgerung gezogen werden, daß wenn—a.-a =—a[hoch 2] ist, umgekehrt +a.—a = +a[hoch 2] gebe.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"117.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0015","text":"Indem der eine Faktor die Anzahl und der andere die Einheit, und zwar der voranstehende wie gewöhnlich die erstere bedeutet, so unterscheiden sich die beiden Ausdrücke—a.+a und +a.-a dadurch, daß im erstern +a die Einheit und—a die Anzahl, und im andern es umgekehrt ist. Es pflegt nun beim erstern gesagt zu werden, wenn ich +a nehmen soll—a mal, so nehme ich +a nicht bloß a mal, sondern zugleich auf die ihm entgegengesetzte Weise, +a mahl—a; also da es Plus ist, so habe ich es negativ zu nehmen, und das Produkt ist—a[hoch 2].—Wenn aber im zweiten Falle—a zu nehmen ist +a mal, so soll—a gleichfalls nicht—a mal genommen werden, sondern in der ihm entgegengesetzten Bestimmung nämlich +a mal. Nach dem Räsonnement des ersten Falles folgt also, daß das Produkt +a[hoch 2] seyn müsse.—Ebenso bei der Division.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"117.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0016","text":"Diese Konsequenz ist nothwendig, insofern Plus und Minus nur als entgegengesetzte Größen überhaupt genommen werden; dem Minus wird im ersten Falle die Kraft zugeschrieben, das Plus zu verändern; aber im andern sollte Plus nicht dieselbe Kraft über Minus haben, ungeachtet es so gut eine entgegengesetzte Größebestimmung ist, als dieses. In der That hat Plus diese Kraft nicht, denn es ist hier nach seiner qualitativen Bestimmung gegen Minus zu nehmen, indem die Faktoren ein qualitatives Verhältniß zu einander haben. Insofern ist also das Negative hier das an sich Entgegengesetzte als solches, das Positive aber ist das Unbestimmte, Gleichgültige überhaupt; es ist wohl auch das Negative, aber des Andern, nicht an ihm selbst.—Eine Bestimmung als Negation kommt also allein durch das Negative herein, nicht durch das Positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"117.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0017","text":"So ist denn auch—a.—a = +a[hoch 2], darum weil das negative a nicht bloß auf die entgegengesetzte Weise, (so würde es zu nehmen seyn, mit—a multiplicirt) sondern weil es negativ genommen werden soll. Die Negation der Negation aber ist das Positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"117.17"}],"sha256":"cbcbb9caee37dc4bb3a4e630d917312bc600c046b37bf3244badcf37ac7892c7","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104847991219Z_67b77a86","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"cbcbb9caee37dc4bb3a4e630d917312bc600c046b37bf3244badcf37ac7892c7","sha256":"d379fbc5980611971162dad6bd4feaddce91d3218bb655fcff7ee3901e20fe8c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:48:47.991229+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0001","text":"The concept of the positive and negative, as it occurs in arithmetic, is to be mentioned here. It is therein presupposed as known; but because it is not grasped in its determinate difference, it does not escape insoluble difficulties and entanglements. The two real determinations of the positive and negative have just emerged,—apart from the simple concept of their opposition,—namely, first, that a merely different, immediate being-there lies at the foundation, whose simple reflection into itself is distinguished from its positedness, from opposition itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"117.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0002","text":"This therefore counts only as not being in and for itself, and indeed as accruing to the different, so that each is an opposite in general, but also subsists indifferently against it for itself, and it is all the same which of the two opposed different things is regarded as positive or as negative.—But secondly, the positive is the positive in itself, the negative the negative in itself, so that the different is not indifferent towards this, but this is its determination in and for itself.—These two forms of the positive and negative occur at once in the first determinations in which they are employed in arithmetic.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"117.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0003","text":"The +a and −a are at first opposed magnitudes in general; a is the unity lying at the foundation of both, being-in-itself, indifferent towards opposition itself, which here serves without further concept as a dead basis. −a is indeed designated as the negative, +a as the positive, but the one is just as much an opposite as the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"117.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0004","text":"Further, a is not merely the simple unity lying at the foundation, but, as +a and −a, it is the reflection of these opposites into themselves; there are two different a's present, and it is indifferent which of the two one wishes to designate as positive or negative; both have a particular subsistence and are positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"117.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0005","text":"According to that first aspect, +y − y = 0; or, in −8 + 3, the 3 positive units are negative in the 8. The opposites cancel one another in their combination. A journey of one hour eastward, and an equally long one back westward, cancels the journey first made; so much debt, so much less wealth, and where so much wealth is present, so much of the debts is cancelled. The journey of one hour eastward is at the same time not the positive journey in itself, nor is that westward the negative journey; rather, these directions are indifferent towards this determinacy of opposition; only a third respect falling outside them makes the one positive, the other negative.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"117.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0006","text":"Likewise debts are not negative in and for themselves; they are so only in relation to the debtor; for the creditor they are his positive wealth; they are a sum of money, or whatever it may be, of a certain value, which, according to respects falling outside it, is debt or wealth.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"117.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0007","text":"The opposites do indeed cancel one another in their relation, so that the result is equal to zero; but their identical relation is also present in them, which is indifferent towards opposition itself; thus they constitute one. As was just remarked of the sum of money, which is only one sum, or of the a, which is only one a in +a and −a; likewise of the path, which is only one stretch of path, not two paths, one of which went eastward, the other westward. Likewise an ordinate y, which is the same whether taken on this or that side of the axis; in this respect +y − y = y; it is only the ordinate, there is only one determination and law of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"117.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0008","text":"Further, however, the opposites are not merely one indifferent thing, but also two indifferent things. For, as opposites, they are also reflected into themselves, and thus subsist as different.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"117.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0009","text":"Thus in −8 + 3 there are, in general, eleven units present; +y, −y, are ordinates on the opposite side of the axis, where each is a being-there indifferent towards this boundary and towards its opposite; thus +y − y = 2y.—Likewise the path traversed eastward and westward is the sum of a twofold effort, or the sum of two periods of time. Similarly, in political economy, a quantum of money, or of value, is not merely this one quantum as a means of subsistence, but is a doubled one; it is a means of subsistence both for the creditor and for the debtor.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"117.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0010","text":"The wealth of the state is calculated not merely as the sum of the cash money and the other value of the immovable and movable property present in the state, still less as the sum that would remain after deducting passive wealth from active wealth; rather, capital, even if its active and passive determination reduced themselves to zero, remains, first, positive capital; as +a − a = a; but secondly, inasmuch as it is in manifold ways passive, lent, and re-lent, it is thereby a greatly multiplied means.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"117.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0011","text":"But the opposed magnitudes are not only, on the one hand, merely opposites in general, and, on the other hand, real or indifferent. Rather, although quantum itself is indifferently bounded being, the positive in itself and the negative in itself nevertheless also occur in it. Thus a, insofar as it has no sign, counts as being to be taken as positive if it is to be designated. If it were only to become an opposite in general, it could equally well be taken as −a. But the positive sign is immediately given to it because the positive has, for itself, the peculiar significance of the immediate, as identical with itself, over against opposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"117.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0012","text":"Further, when positive and negative magnitudes are added or subtracted, they count as such as are positive and negative for themselves, and do not become so merely through the relation of adding or subtracting, in this external manner. In 8 − (−3), the first minus is called opposed to 8, but the second minus, (−3), counts as an opposite in itself, apart from this relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"117.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0013","text":"This emerges more closely in multiplication and division; here the positive is essentially to be taken as the non-opposed, whereas the negative is to be taken as the opposed, not both determinations alike merely as opposites in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"117.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0014","text":"Since the textbooks, in their proofs of how the signs behave in these two operations, remain with the concept of opposed magnitudes in general, these proofs are incomplete and become entangled in contradictions.—But in multiplication and division plus and minus acquire the more determinate significance of the positive and negative in themselves, because the relation of the factors, of being unity and number in relation to one another, is not a merely quantitative relation of increase and diminution, as in addition and subtraction, but a qualitative one; with which plus and minus also acquire the qualitative significance of the positive and negative.—Without this determination, and merely from the concept of opposed magnitudes, the false inference may easily be drawn that if −a·−a = −a², conversely +a·−a yields +a².","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"117.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0015","text":"Since one factor signifies the number and the other the unity, and indeed the preceding one, as usual, signifies the former, the two expressions −a·+a and +a·−a differ in that, in the former, +a is the unity and −a the number, while in the latter it is the reverse. Now, in the former case it is customarily said: if I am to take +a, −a times, then I take +a not merely a times, but at the same time in the manner opposite to it, +a times −a; thus, since it is plus, I have to take it negatively, and the product is −a².—But if, in the second case, −a is to be taken +a times, then −a is likewise not to be taken −a times, but in the determination opposite to it, namely +a times. According to the reasoning of the first case, it therefore follows that the product must be +a².—Likewise in division.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"117.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0016","text":"This consequence is necessary insofar as plus and minus are taken only as opposed magnitudes in general; in the first case minus is ascribed the power to alter plus; but in the other, plus ought not to have the same power over minus, notwithstanding that it is just as much an opposed determination of magnitude as the latter. In fact, plus does not have this power, for here it is to be taken, according to its qualitative determination, in contrast with minus, since the factors have a qualitative relation to one another. In this respect, therefore, the negative here is the opposed in itself as such, while the positive is the indeterminate, indifferent in general; it is indeed also the negative, but of the other, not in itself.—Thus a determination as negation enters solely through the negative, not through the positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"117.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_30:P0017","text":"Thus also −a·−a = +a², because the negative a is not merely to be taken in the opposite manner (thus it would have to be taken, multiplied by −a), but because it is to be taken negatively. But the negation of negation is the positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"117.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_30:P0017"]}],"source_digest":"f697b60ef496ae4d83e6efb259a05b029e38691a25c79d5d38e587c6f0559025","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0","title":"C. Contradiction.","order":118,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDW0","text":"1. Der Unterschied überhaupt enthält seine beiden Seiten als Momente; in der Verschiedenheit fallen sie gleichgültig auseinander; im Gegensatze als solchem sind sie Seiten des Unterschiedes, eines nur durchs andere bestimmt, somit nur Momente; aber sie sind ebenso sehr bestimmt an ihnen selbst, gleichgültig gegen einander und sich gegenseitig ausschließend; die selbstständigen Reflexions-Bestimmungen.\n\nDie eine ist das Positive, die andere das Negative, aber jene als das an ihm selbst Positive, diese als das an ihm selbst Negative. Die gleichgültige Selbstständigkeit für sich hat jedes dadurch, daß es die Beziehung auf sein anderes Moment an ihm selbst hat; so ist es der ganze in sich geschlossene Gegensatz.—Als dieses Ganze ist jedes vermittelt durch sein Anderes mit sich, und enthält dasselbe. Aber es ist ferner durch das Nichtseyn seines Andern mit sich vermittelt; so ist es für sich seyende Einheit und schließt das Andere aus sich aus.\n\nIndem die selbstständige Reflexions-Bestimmung in derselben Rüksicht, als sie die andere enthält, und dadurch selbstständig ist, die andere ausschließt, so schließt sie in ihrer Selbstständigkeit ihre eigene Selbstständigkeit aus sich aus; denn diese besteht darin, die ihr andre Bestimmung in sich zu enthalten und dadurch allein nicht Beziehung auf ein äußerliches zu seyn, aber ebenso sehr unmittelbar darin, sie selbst zu seyn und die ihr negative Bestimmung von sich auszuschließen. Sie ist so der Widerspruch.\n\nDer Unterschied überhaupt ist schon der Widerspruch an sich; denn er ist die Einheit von solchen, die nur sind, insofern sie nicht eins sind,—und die Trennung solcher, die nur sind als in derselben Beziehung getrennte. Das Positive und Negative aber sind der gesetzte Widerspruch, weil sie als negative Einheiten, selbst das Setzen ihrer, und darin jedes das Aufheben seiner und das Setzen seines Gegentheils ist.—Sie machen die bestimmende Reflexion als ausschließende aus; weil das Ausschließen Ein Unterscheiden, und jedes der Unterschiedenen als Ausschließendes selbst das ganze Ausschließen ist, so schließt jedes in ihm selbst sich aus.\n\nDie beiden selbstständigen Reflexions-Bestimmungen für sich betrachtet, so ist das Positive das Gesetztseyn als in die Gleichheit mit sich reflektirt; das Gesetztseyn, das nicht Beziehung auf ein Anderes ist, das Bestehen also, insofern das Gesetztseyn aufgehoben und ausgeschlossen ist. Damit aber macht sich das Positive zur Beziehung eines Nichtseyns,—zu einem Gesetztseyn.—So ist es der Widerspruch, daß es als das Setzen der Identität mit sich durch Ausschließen des Negativen sich selbst zum Negativen von einem macht, also zu dem Andern, das es von sich ausschließt. Dieses ist als Ausgeschlossenes frei von dem Ausschließenden gesetzt; hiermit als in sich reflektirt und selbst ausschließend. So ist die ausschließende Reflexion Setzen des Positiven, als ausschließend das Andre, so daß dieß Setzen unmittelbar das Setzen seines Andern, es ausschließenden, ist.\n\nDieß ist der absolute Widerspruch des Positiven, aber er ist unmittelbar der absolute Widerspruch des Negativen; das Setzen beider ist Eine Reflexion.—Das Negative für sich betrachtet gegen das Positive ist das Gesetztseyn als in die Ungleichheit mit sich reflektirt, das Negative als Negatives. Aber das Negative ist selbst das Ungleiche, das Nichtseyn eines andern; somit ist die Reflexion in seine Ungleichheit vielmehr seine Beziehung auf sich selbst.—Die Negation überhaupt ist das Negative als Qualität, oder unmittelbare Bestimmtheit; das Negative aber als Negatives, ist es bezogen auf das Negative seiner, auf sein Anderes. Wird dieß Negative nur als identisch mit dem ersten genommen, so ist es, wie auch das erstere, nur unmittelbar; sie werden so nicht genommen als Andere gegeneinander, somit nicht als Negative; das Negative ist überhaupt nicht ein Unmittelbares.—Indem nun ferner aber ebenso sehr jedes dasselbe ist, was das Andere, so ist diese Beziehung der Ungleichen ebenso sehr ihre identische Beziehung.\n\nDieß ist also derselbe Widerspruch, der das Positive ist, nämlich Gesetztseyn oder Negation, als Beziehung auf sich. Aber das Positive ist nur an sich dieser Widerspruch; das Negative dagegen der gesetzte Widerspruch; denn in seiner Reflexion in sich, an und für sich Negatives oder als Negatives identisch mit sich zu seyn, hat es die Bestimmung, daß es Nichtidentisches, Ausschließen der Identität sey. Es ist dieß, gegen die Identität identisch mit sich zu seyn, hiermit durch seine ausschließende Reflexion sich selbst von sich auszuschließen.\n\nDas Negative ist also die ganze, als Entgegensetzung auf sich beruhende Entgegensetzung, der absolute sich nicht auf Anderes beziehende Unterschied; er schließt als Entgegensetzung die Identität von sich aus; aber somit sich selbst, denn als Beziehung auf sich bestimmt er sich als die Identität selbst, die er ausschließt.\n\n2. Der Widerspruch löst sich auf.\n\nIn der sich selbst ausschließenden Reflexion, die betrachtet wurde, hebt das Positive und das Negative jedes in seiner Selbstständigkeit sich selbst auf; jedes ist schlechthin das Übergehen oder vielmehr das sich Übersetzen seiner in sein Gegentheil. Dieß rastlose Verschwinden der Entgegengesetzten in ihnen selbst ist die nächste Einheit, welche durch den Widerspruch zu Stande kommt; sie ist die Null.\n\nDer Widerspruch enthält aber nicht bloß das Negative sondern auch das Positive; oder die sich selbst ausschließende Reflexion ist zugleich setzende Reflexion; das Resultat des Widerspruchs ist nicht nur Null. —Das Positive und Negative machen das Gesetztseyn der Selbstständigkeit aus; die Negation ihrer durch sie selbst hebt das Gesetztseyn der Selbstständigkeit auf. Dieß ist es, was in Wahrheit im Widerspruche zu Grund geht.\n\nDie Reflexion in sich, wodurch die Seiten des Gegensatzes sich zu selbstständigen Beziehungen auf sich machen, ist zunächst ihre Selbstständigkeit als unterschiedener Momente; sie sind so nur an sich diese Selbstständigkeit, denn sie sind noch entgegengesetzte, und daß sie es an sich sind, macht ihr Gesetztseyn aus. Aber ihre ausschließende Reflexion hebt dieß Gesetztseyn auf, macht sie zu fürsichseyenden Selbstständigen, zu solchen, die nicht nur an sich, sondern durch ihre negative Beziehung auf ihr Anderes selbstständig sind; ihre Selbstständigkeit ist auf diese Weise auch gesetzt. Aber ferner machen sie sich durch dieß ihr Setzen zu einem Gesetztseyn. Sie richten sich zu Grunde, indem sie sich bestimmen als das mit sich Identische, aber darin vielmehr als das Negative, als ein mit sich Identisches, das Beziehung auf Anderes ist.\n\nAllein diese ausschließende Reflexion ist näher betrachtet, nicht nur diese formelle Bestimmung. Sie ist ansichseyende Selbstständigkeit, und ist das Aufheben dieses Gesetztseyns und durch dieß Aufheben erst fürsichseyende und in der That selbstständige Einheit. Durch das Aufheben des Andersseyns oder Gesetztseyns ist zwar wieder das Gesetztseyn, das Negative eines Andern, vorhanden. Aber in der That ist diese Negation nicht wieder nur erste unmittelbare Beziehung auf Anderes, nicht Gesetztseyn als aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit, sondern als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn. Die ausschließende Reflexion der Selbstständigkeit, indem sie ausschließend ist, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn, aber ist ebenso sehr Aufheben ihres Gesetztseyns. Sie ist aufhebende Beziehung auf sich; sie hebt darin erstens das Negative auf und zweitens setzt sie sich als Negatives, und dieß ist erst dasjenige Negative, das sie aufhebt; im Aufheben des Negativen setzt und hebt sie zugleich es auf. Die ausschließende Bestimmung selbst ist auf diese Weise sich das Andre, dessen Negation sie ist; das Aufheben dieses Gesetztseyns ist daher nicht wieder Gesetztseyn als das Negative eines Andern, sondern ist das Zusammengehen mit sich selbst, das positive Einheit mit sich ist. Die Selbstständigkeit ist so durch ihre eigene Negation in sich zurückkehrende Einheit, indem sie durch die Negation ihres Gesetztseyns in sich zurückkehrt. Sie ist die Einheit des Wesens, durch die Negation nicht eines Andern, sondern ihrer selbst identisch mit sich zu seyn.\n\n3. Nach dieser positiven Seite, daß die Selbstständigkeit im Gegensatze, als ausschließende Reflexion sich zum Gesetztseyn macht, und es ebenso sehr aufhebt, Gesetztseyn zu seyn, ist der Gegensatz nicht nur zu Grunde, sondern in seinen Grund zurückgegangen.—Die ausschließende Reflexion des selbstständigen Gegensatzes macht ihn zu einem Negativen, nur Gesetzten; sie setzt dadurch ihre zunächst selbstständigen Bestimmungen, das Positive und Negative, zu solchen herab, welche nur Bestimmungen sind; und indem so das Gesetztseyn zum Gesetztseyn gemacht wird, ist es überhaupt in seine Einheit mit sich zurückgekehrt; es ist das einfache Wesen, aber das Wesen als Grund. Durch das Aufheben der sich an sich selbst widersprechenden Bestimmungen des Wesens, ist dieses wiederhergestellt, jedoch mit der Bestimmung, ausschließende Reflexionseinheit zu seyn,—einfache Einheit, welche sich selbst als Negatives bestimmt, aber in diesem Gesetztseyn unmittelbar sich selbst gleich und mit sich zusammen-gegangen ist.\n\nZunächst geht also der selbstständige Gegensatz durch seinen Widerspruch in den Grund zurück; jener ist das Erste, Unmittelbare, von dem angefangen wird, und der aufgehobene Gegensatz oder das aufgehobene Gesetztseyn ist selbst ein Gesetztseyn. Somit ist das Wesen als Grund ein Gesetztseyn, ein Gewordenes. Aber umgekehrt hat sich nur dieß gesetzt, daß der Gegensatz oder das Gesetztseyn ein Aufgehobenes, nur als Gesetztseyn ist. Das Wesen ist also als Grund so ausschließende Reflexion, daß es sich selbst zum Gesetztseyn macht, daß der Gegensatz, von dem vorhin der Anfang gemacht wurde und der das Unmittelbare war, die nur gesetzte, bestimmte Selbstständigkeit des Wesens ist, und daß er nur das sich an ihm selbst Aufhebende, das Wesen aber das in seiner Bestimmtheit in sich Reflektirte ist. Das Wesen schließt als Grund sich von sich selbst aus, es setzt sich; sein Gesetztseyn,—welches das Ausgeschlossene ist,—ist nur als Gesetztseyn, als Identität des Negativen mit sich selbst. Dieß Selbstständige ist das Negative, gesetzt als Negatives; ein sich selbst Widersprechendes, das daher unmittelbar im Wesen als seinem Grunde bleibt.\n\nDer aufgelöste Widerspruch ist also der Grund, das Wesen als Einheit des Positiven und Negativen. Im Gegensatze ist die Bestimmung zur Selbstständigkeit gediehen; der Grund aber ist diese vollendete Selbstständigkeit; das Negative ist in ihm selbstständiges Wesen, aber als Negatives; so ist er ebenso sehr das Positive als das in dieser Negativität mit sich Identische. Der Gegensatz und sein Widerspruch ist daher im Grunde so sehr aufgehoben, als erhalten. Der Grund ist das Wesen als die positive Identität mit sich; aber die sich zugleich als die Negativität auf sich bezieht, sich also bestimmt und zum ausgeschlossenen Gesetztseyn macht; dieß Gesetztseyn aber ist das ganze selbstständige Wesen, und das Wesen ist Grund, als in dieser seiner Negation identisch mit sich selbst und positiv. Der sich widersprechende selbstständige Gegensatz war also bereits selbst der Grund; es kam nur die Bestimmung der Einheit mit sich selbst hinzu, welche dadurch hervortritt, daß die selbstständigen Entgegengesetzten jedes sich selbst aufhebt, und sich zu dem andern seiner macht, somit zu Grunde geht, aber darin zugleich nur mit sich selbst zusammengeht, also in seinem Untergange, das ist, in seinem Gesetztseyn oder in der Negation vielmehr erst das in sich reflektirte, mit sich identische Wesen ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0001","text":"1. Der Unterschied überhaupt enthält seine beiden Seiten als Momente; in der Verschiedenheit fallen sie gleichgültig auseinander; im Gegensatze als solchem sind sie Seiten des Unterschiedes, eines nur durchs andere bestimmt, somit nur Momente; aber sie sind ebenso sehr bestimmt an ihnen selbst, gleichgültig gegen einander und sich gegenseitig ausschließend; die selbstständigen Reflexions-Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"118.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0002","text":"Die eine ist das Positive, die andere das Negative, aber jene als das an ihm selbst Positive, diese als das an ihm selbst Negative. Die gleichgültige Selbstständigkeit für sich hat jedes dadurch, daß es die Beziehung auf sein anderes Moment an ihm selbst hat; so ist es der ganze in sich geschlossene Gegensatz.—Als dieses Ganze ist jedes vermittelt durch sein Anderes mit sich, und enthält dasselbe. Aber es ist ferner durch das Nichtseyn seines Andern mit sich vermittelt; so ist es für sich seyende Einheit und schließt das Andere aus sich aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"118.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0003","text":"Indem die selbstständige Reflexions-Bestimmung in derselben Rüksicht, als sie die andere enthält, und dadurch selbstständig ist, die andere ausschließt, so schließt sie in ihrer Selbstständigkeit ihre eigene Selbstständigkeit aus sich aus; denn diese besteht darin, die ihr andre Bestimmung in sich zu enthalten und dadurch allein nicht Beziehung auf ein äußerliches zu seyn, aber ebenso sehr unmittelbar darin, sie selbst zu seyn und die ihr negative Bestimmung von sich auszuschließen. Sie ist so der Widerspruch.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"118.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0004","text":"Der Unterschied überhaupt ist schon der Widerspruch an sich; denn er ist die Einheit von solchen, die nur sind, insofern sie nicht eins sind,—und die Trennung solcher, die nur sind als in derselben Beziehung getrennte. Das Positive und Negative aber sind der gesetzte Widerspruch, weil sie als negative Einheiten, selbst das Setzen ihrer, und darin jedes das Aufheben seiner und das Setzen seines Gegentheils ist.—Sie machen die bestimmende Reflexion als ausschließende aus; weil das Ausschließen Ein Unterscheiden, und jedes der Unterschiedenen als Ausschließendes selbst das ganze Ausschließen ist, so schließt jedes in ihm selbst sich aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"118.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0005","text":"Die beiden selbstständigen Reflexions-Bestimmungen für sich betrachtet, so ist das Positive das Gesetztseyn als in die Gleichheit mit sich reflektirt; das Gesetztseyn, das nicht Beziehung auf ein Anderes ist, das Bestehen also, insofern das Gesetztseyn aufgehoben und ausgeschlossen ist. Damit aber macht sich das Positive zur Beziehung eines Nichtseyns,—zu einem Gesetztseyn.—So ist es der Widerspruch, daß es als das Setzen der Identität mit sich durch Ausschließen des Negativen sich selbst zum Negativen von einem macht, also zu dem Andern, das es von sich ausschließt. Dieses ist als Ausgeschlossenes frei von dem Ausschließenden gesetzt; hiermit als in sich reflektirt und selbst ausschließend. So ist die ausschließende Reflexion Setzen des Positiven, als ausschließend das Andre, so daß dieß Setzen unmittelbar das Setzen seines Andern, es ausschließenden, ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"118.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0006","text":"Dieß ist der absolute Widerspruch des Positiven, aber er ist unmittelbar der absolute Widerspruch des Negativen; das Setzen beider ist Eine Reflexion.—Das Negative für sich betrachtet gegen das Positive ist das Gesetztseyn als in die Ungleichheit mit sich reflektirt, das Negative als Negatives. Aber das Negative ist selbst das Ungleiche, das Nichtseyn eines andern; somit ist die Reflexion in seine Ungleichheit vielmehr seine Beziehung auf sich selbst.—Die Negation überhaupt ist das Negative als Qualität, oder unmittelbare Bestimmtheit; das Negative aber als Negatives, ist es bezogen auf das Negative seiner, auf sein Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"118.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0007","text":"Wird dieß Negative nur als identisch mit dem ersten genommen, so ist es, wie auch das erstere, nur unmittelbar; sie werden so nicht genommen als Andere gegeneinander, somit nicht als Negative; das Negative ist überhaupt nicht ein Unmittelbares.—Indem nun ferner aber ebenso sehr jedes dasselbe ist, was das Andere, so ist diese Beziehung der Ungleichen ebenso sehr ihre identische Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"118.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0008","text":"Dieß ist also derselbe Widerspruch, der das Positive ist, nämlich Gesetztseyn oder Negation, als Beziehung auf sich. Aber das Positive ist nur an sich dieser Widerspruch; das Negative dagegen der gesetzte Widerspruch; denn in seiner Reflexion in sich, an und für sich Negatives oder als Negatives identisch mit sich zu seyn, hat es die Bestimmung, daß es Nichtidentisches, Ausschließen der Identität sey. Es ist dieß, gegen die Identität identisch mit sich zu seyn, hiermit durch seine ausschließende Reflexion sich selbst von sich auszuschließen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"118.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0009","text":"Das Negative ist also die ganze, als Entgegensetzung auf sich beruhende Entgegensetzung, der absolute sich nicht auf Anderes beziehende Unterschied; er schließt als Entgegensetzung die Identität von sich aus; aber somit sich selbst, denn als Beziehung auf sich bestimmt er sich als die Identität selbst, die er ausschließt.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"118.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0010","text":"2. Der Widerspruch löst sich auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"118.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0011","text":"In der sich selbst ausschließenden Reflexion, die betrachtet wurde, hebt das Positive und das Negative jedes in seiner Selbstständigkeit sich selbst auf; jedes ist schlechthin das Übergehen oder vielmehr das sich Übersetzen seiner in sein Gegentheil. Dieß rastlose Verschwinden der Entgegengesetzten in ihnen selbst ist die nächste Einheit, welche durch den Widerspruch zu Stande kommt; sie ist die Null.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"118.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0012","text":"Der Widerspruch enthält aber nicht bloß das Negative sondern auch das Positive; oder die sich selbst ausschließende Reflexion ist zugleich setzende Reflexion; das Resultat des Widerspruchs ist nicht nur Null. —Das Positive und Negative machen das Gesetztseyn der Selbstständigkeit aus; die Negation ihrer durch sie selbst hebt das Gesetztseyn der Selbstständigkeit auf. Dieß ist es, was in Wahrheit im Widerspruche zu Grund geht.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"118.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0013","text":"Die Reflexion in sich, wodurch die Seiten des Gegensatzes sich zu selbstständigen Beziehungen auf sich machen, ist zunächst ihre Selbstständigkeit als unterschiedener Momente; sie sind so nur an sich diese Selbstständigkeit, denn sie sind noch entgegengesetzte, und daß sie es an sich sind, macht ihr Gesetztseyn aus. Aber ihre ausschließende Reflexion hebt dieß Gesetztseyn auf, macht sie zu fürsichseyenden Selbstständigen, zu solchen, die nicht nur an sich, sondern durch ihre negative Beziehung auf ihr Anderes selbstständig sind; ihre Selbstständigkeit ist auf diese Weise auch gesetzt. Aber ferner machen sie sich durch dieß ihr Setzen zu einem Gesetztseyn. Sie richten sich zu Grunde, indem sie sich bestimmen als das mit sich Identische, aber darin vielmehr als das Negative, als ein mit sich Identisches, das Beziehung auf Anderes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"118.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0014","text":"Allein diese ausschließende Reflexion ist näher betrachtet, nicht nur diese formelle Bestimmung. Sie ist ansichseyende Selbstständigkeit, und ist das Aufheben dieses Gesetztseyns und durch dieß Aufheben erst fürsichseyende und in der That selbstständige Einheit. Durch das Aufheben des Andersseyns oder Gesetztseyns ist zwar wieder das Gesetztseyn, das Negative eines Andern, vorhanden. Aber in der That ist diese Negation nicht wieder nur erste unmittelbare Beziehung auf Anderes, nicht Gesetztseyn als aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit, sondern als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn. Die ausschließende Reflexion der Selbstständigkeit, indem sie ausschließend ist, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn, aber ist ebenso sehr Aufheben ihres Gesetztseyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"118.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0015","text":"Sie ist aufhebende Beziehung auf sich; sie hebt darin erstens das Negative auf und zweitens setzt sie sich als Negatives, und dieß ist erst dasjenige Negative, das sie aufhebt; im Aufheben des Negativen setzt und hebt sie zugleich es auf. Die ausschließende Bestimmung selbst ist auf diese Weise sich das Andre, dessen Negation sie ist; das Aufheben dieses Gesetztseyns ist daher nicht wieder Gesetztseyn als das Negative eines Andern, sondern ist das Zusammengehen mit sich selbst, das positive Einheit mit sich ist. Die Selbstständigkeit ist so durch ihre eigene Negation in sich zurückkehrende Einheit, indem sie durch die Negation ihres Gesetztseyns in sich zurückkehrt. Sie ist die Einheit des Wesens, durch die Negation nicht eines Andern, sondern ihrer selbst identisch mit sich zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"118.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0016","text":"3. Nach dieser positiven Seite, daß die Selbstständigkeit im Gegensatze, als ausschließende Reflexion sich zum Gesetztseyn macht, und es ebenso sehr aufhebt, Gesetztseyn zu seyn, ist der Gegensatz nicht nur zu Grunde, sondern in seinen Grund zurückgegangen.—Die ausschließende Reflexion des selbstständigen Gegensatzes macht ihn zu einem Negativen, nur Gesetzten; sie setzt dadurch ihre zunächst selbstständigen Bestimmungen, das Positive und Negative, zu solchen herab, welche nur Bestimmungen sind; und indem so das Gesetztseyn zum Gesetztseyn gemacht wird, ist es überhaupt in seine Einheit mit sich zurückgekehrt; es ist das einfache Wesen, aber das Wesen als Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"118.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0017","text":"Durch das Aufheben der sich an sich selbst widersprechenden Bestimmungen des Wesens, ist dieses wiederhergestellt, jedoch mit der Bestimmung, ausschließende Reflexionseinheit zu seyn,—einfache Einheit, welche sich selbst als Negatives bestimmt, aber in diesem Gesetztseyn unmittelbar sich selbst gleich und mit sich zusammen-gegangen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"118.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0018","text":"Zunächst geht also der selbstständige Gegensatz durch seinen Widerspruch in den Grund zurück; jener ist das Erste, Unmittelbare, von dem angefangen wird, und der aufgehobene Gegensatz oder das aufgehobene Gesetztseyn ist selbst ein Gesetztseyn. Somit ist das Wesen als Grund ein Gesetztseyn, ein Gewordenes. Aber umgekehrt hat sich nur dieß gesetzt, daß der Gegensatz oder das Gesetztseyn ein Aufgehobenes, nur als Gesetztseyn ist. Das Wesen ist also als Grund so ausschließende Reflexion, daß es sich selbst zum Gesetztseyn macht, daß der Gegensatz, von dem vorhin der Anfang gemacht wurde und der das Unmittelbare war, die nur gesetzte, bestimmte Selbstständigkeit des Wesens ist, und daß er nur das sich an ihm selbst Aufhebende, das Wesen aber das in seiner Bestimmtheit in sich Reflektirte ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"118.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0019","text":"Das Wesen schließt als Grund sich von sich selbst aus, es setzt sich; sein Gesetztseyn,—welches das Ausgeschlossene ist,—ist nur als Gesetztseyn, als Identität des Negativen mit sich selbst. Dieß Selbstständige ist das Negative, gesetzt als Negatives; ein sich selbst Widersprechendes, das daher unmittelbar im Wesen als seinem Grunde bleibt.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"118.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0020","text":"Der aufgelöste Widerspruch ist also der Grund, das Wesen als Einheit des Positiven und Negativen. Im Gegensatze ist die Bestimmung zur Selbstständigkeit gediehen; der Grund aber ist diese vollendete Selbstständigkeit; das Negative ist in ihm selbstständiges Wesen, aber als Negatives; so ist er ebenso sehr das Positive als das in dieser Negativität mit sich Identische. Der Gegensatz und sein Widerspruch ist daher im Grunde so sehr aufgehoben, als erhalten. Der Grund ist das Wesen als die positive Identität mit sich; aber die sich zugleich als die Negativität auf sich bezieht, sich also bestimmt und zum ausgeschlossenen Gesetztseyn macht; dieß Gesetztseyn aber ist das ganze selbstständige Wesen, und das Wesen ist Grund, als in dieser seiner Negation identisch mit sich selbst und positiv.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"118.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0021","text":"Der sich widersprechende selbstständige Gegensatz war also bereits selbst der Grund; es kam nur die Bestimmung der Einheit mit sich selbst hinzu, welche dadurch hervortritt, daß die selbstständigen Entgegengesetzten jedes sich selbst aufhebt, und sich zu dem andern seiner macht, somit zu Grunde geht, aber darin zugleich nur mit sich selbst zusammengeht, also in seinem Untergange, das ist, in seinem Gesetztseyn oder in der Negation vielmehr erst das in sich reflektirte, mit sich identische Wesen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"118.21"}],"sha256":"243f46ad2f4d612bd3158cddd23c19f29ce147bf8b7930d979694ce93e9c0cf6","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104907862289Z_bec4af85","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Contradiction.","source_sha256":"243f46ad2f4d612bd3158cddd23c19f29ce147bf8b7930d979694ce93e9c0cf6","sha256":"2bd440ed79dec3e2755921565afaf7bd32e7605ab9db6e20866670cc604171f4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:49:07.862313+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0001","text":"1. Difference in general contains its two sides as moments; in diversity they fall apart indifferently; in opposition as such they are sides of difference, each determined only through the other, thus only moments; but they are equally determinate in themselves, indifferent towards one another and mutually exclusive; the self-subsistent determinations of reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"118.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0002","text":"The one is the positive, the other the negative, but the former as that which is positive in itself, the latter as that which is negative in itself. Each has indifferent self-subsistence for itself by having within itself the relation to its other moment; thus each is the whole opposition closed within itself.—As this whole, each is mediated with itself through its other, and contains the same. But it is further mediated with itself through the non-being of its other; thus it is a unity existing for itself and excludes the other from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"118.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0003","text":"Inasmuch as the self-subsistent determination of reflection, in the same respect in which it contains the other and thereby is self-subsistent, excludes the other, it excludes from itself, in its self-subsistence, its own self-subsistence; for this consists in containing within itself the determination other than it and thereby alone not being relation to an external [thing], but equally immediately in being itself and excluding from itself the determination negative to it. It is thus contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"118.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0004","text":"Difference in general is already contradiction in itself; for it is the unity of such as are only insofar as they are not one,—and the separation of such as are only as separated in the same relation. But the positive and negative are posited contradiction, because, as negative unities, they are themselves the positing of themselves, and therein each is the sublation of itself and the positing of its opposite.—They constitute determining reflection as excluding; because excluding is a distinguishing, and each of the distinguished, as excluding, is itself the whole excluding, each excludes itself within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"118.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0005","text":"If the two self-subsistent determinations of reflection are considered for themselves, then the positive is positedness as reflected into equality with itself; positedness which is not relation to an other, subsistence therefore, insofar as positedness is sublated and excluded. But thereby the positive makes itself into the relation of a non-being,—into a positedness.—Thus it is the contradiction that, as the positing of identity with itself through exclusion of the negative, it makes itself into the negative of an [other], thus into the other which it excludes from itself. This, as excluded, is posited as free from the excluding [term]; hence as reflected into itself and itself excluding. Thus excluding reflection is the positing of the positive, as excluding the other, so that this positing is immediately the positing of its other, which excludes it.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"118.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0006","text":"This is the absolute contradiction of the positive, but it is immediately the absolute contradiction of the negative; the positing of both is one reflection.—The negative, considered for itself over against the positive, is positedness as reflected into inequality with itself, the negative as negative. But the negative is itself the unequal, the non-being of an other; thus reflection into its inequality is rather its relation to itself.—Negation in general is the negative as quality, or immediate determinateness; but the negative as negative is related to the negative of itself, to its other.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"118.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0007","text":"If this negative is taken merely as identical with the first, then it is, like the former also, merely immediate; they are thus not taken as others over against each other, hence not as negatives; the negative is in general not an immediate.—But inasmuch as, further, each is equally that which the other is, this relation of the unequals is equally their identical relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"118.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0008","text":"This is therefore the same contradiction which the positive is, namely, positedness or negation, as relation to itself. But the positive is this contradiction only in itself; the negative, on the other hand, is the posited contradiction; for in its reflection into itself, in being negative in and for itself, or as negative identical with itself, it has the determination that it is non-identical, exclusion of identity. It is this, to be identical with itself against identity, hence through its excluding reflection to exclude itself from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"118.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0009","text":"The negative is therefore the whole opposition, opposition resting upon itself as opposition, the absolute difference not relating to an other; as opposition it excludes identity from itself, but thereby itself, for as relation to itself it determines itself as the identity itself which it excludes.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"118.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0010","text":"2. Contradiction resolves itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"118.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0011","text":"In the self-excluding reflection which has been considered, the positive and the negative each sublate themselves in their self-subsistence; each is absolutely the transition, or rather the translation of itself into its opposite. This restless vanishing of the opposites in themselves is the immediate unity which comes about through contradiction; it is zero.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"118.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0012","text":"But contradiction contains not merely the negative but also the positive; or self-excluding reflection is at the same time positing reflection; the result of contradiction is not merely zero. —The positive and negative constitute the positedness of self-subsistence; their negation through themselves sublates the positedness of self-subsistence. This is what truly goes to ground in contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"118.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0013","text":"Reflection into themselves, whereby the sides of opposition make themselves into self-subsistent relations to themselves, is initially their self-subsistence as distinct moments; they are thus this self-subsistence only in themselves, for they are still opposites, and that they are so in themselves constitutes their positedness. But their excluding reflection sublates this positedness, makes them self-subsistent beings-for-self, such as are self-subsistent not merely in themselves but through their negative relation to their other; their self-subsistence is thus also posited. But further, through this their positing, they make themselves into a positedness. They go to ground in determining themselves as that which is identical with itself, but therein rather as the negative, as an identical-with-itself which is relation to an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"118.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0014","text":"Yet this excluding reflection, considered more closely, is not merely this formal determination. It is self-subsistence in itself, and is the sublation of this positedness, and only through this sublation is it unity existing for itself and in fact self-subsistent. Through the sublation of otherness or positedness, positedness indeed again exists, the negative of an other. But in fact this negation is no longer merely the first immediate relation to an other, not positedness as sublated immediacy, but as sublated positedness. The excluding reflection of self-subsistence, in being excluding, makes itself into positedness, but equally sublates its positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"118.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0015","text":"It is sublating relation to itself; therein it first sublates the negative and secondly posits itself as negative, and this is only then that negative which it sublates; in sublating the negative, it posits and at the same time sublates it. The excluding determination itself is in this way the other of itself, whose negation it is; the sublation of this positedness is therefore not again positedness as the negative of an other, but is the coming-together with itself, which is positive unity with itself. Self-subsistence is thus unity returning into itself through its own negation, in that it returns into itself through the negation of its positedness. It is the unity of essence, being identical with itself through the negation not of an other but of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"118.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0016","text":"3. According to this positive side, namely that self-subsistence in opposition, as excluding reflection, makes itself into positedness and equally sublates being positedness, opposition has not merely gone to ground, but has returned into its ground.—The excluding reflection of self-subsistent opposition makes it into a negative, merely posited; it thereby reduces its initially self-subsistent determinations, the positive and negative, to such as are only determinations; and in that positedness is made into positedness, it has in general returned into its unity with itself; it is simple essence, but essence as ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"118.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0017","text":"Through the sublation of the determinations of essence that contradict themselves in themselves, essence is restored, yet with the determination of being excluding unity of reflection,—simple unity, which determines itself as negative, but in this positedness is immediately equal to itself and has come together with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"118.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0018","text":"Thus, initially, self-subsistent opposition returns through its contradiction into ground; that opposition is the first, immediate [thing] from which the beginning is made, and the sublated opposition or sublated positedness is itself a positedness. Hence essence as ground is a positedness, a becoming. But conversely, only this has been posited, that opposition or positedness is a sublated [thing], is only as positedness. Essence as ground is therefore excluding reflection in such a way that it makes itself into positedness, that opposition, from which the beginning was previously made and which was the immediate, is the merely posited, determinate self-subsistence of essence, and that it is only that which sublates itself in itself, while essence is that which is reflected into itself in its determinateness.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"118.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0019","text":"Essence, as ground, excludes itself from itself, it posits itself; its positedness,—which is the excluded [thing],—is only as positedness, as the identity of the negative with itself. This self-subsistent [thing] is the negative, posited as negative; something self-contradictory, which therefore immediately remains in essence as its ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"118.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0020","text":"The resolved contradiction is therefore ground, essence as the unity of positive and negative. In opposition, determination has advanced to self-subsistence; but ground is this completed self-subsistence; in it the negative is self-subsistent essence, but as negative; thus it is equally the positive, as that which is identical with itself in this negativity. Opposition and its contradiction are therefore as much sublated in ground as preserved. Ground is essence as positive identity with itself; but at the same time relating itself to itself as negativity, thus determining itself and making itself into excluded positedness; but this positedness is the whole self-subsistent essence, and essence is ground, as identical with itself and positive in this its negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"118.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0021","text":"The self-contradictory self-subsistent opposition was therefore already itself ground; only the determination of unity with itself was added, which emerges in that each of the self-subsistent opposites sublates itself and makes itself into its other, thus goes to ground, but therein at the same time only comes together with itself, and thus in its perishing, that is, in its positedness or in negation, is rather only then essence reflected into itself and identical with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"118.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDW0:P0021"]}],"source_digest":"6d4f0be059d6cecdd932b12387fb3c4a56191aba9178bb85e8a9d65bb48700f9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Der Widerspruch."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Der Widerspruch.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31","title":"Remark 1.","order":119,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_31","text":"Das Positive und Negative ist dasselbe. Dieser Ausdruck gehört der äußern Reflexion an, insofern sie mit diesen beiden Bestimmungen eine Vergleichung anstellt. Es ist aber nicht eine äußere Vergleichung, welche zwischen denselben, ebenso wenig als zwischen andern Kategorien anzustellen ist, sondern sie sind an ihnen selbst zu betrachten, d. h. es ist zu betrachten, was ihre eigene Reflexion ist. An dieser aber hat es sich gezeigt, daß jedes wesentlich das Scheinen seiner im Andern und selbst das Setzen seiner als des Andern ist.\n\nDas Vorstellen, insofern es das Positive und Negative nicht betrachtet, wie sie an und für sich sind, kann aber allerdings an das Vergleichen verwiesen werden, um das Haltlose dieser Unterschiedenen, die von ihm als fest einander gegenüber angenommen sind, aufmerksam zu werden. Eine geringe Erfahrung in dem reflektirenden Denken wird es schon wahrnehmen, daß wenn etwas als positiv bestimmt worden, indem man nun von dieser Grundlage weiter geht, sich dasselbe unmittelbar unter der Hand in Negatives verkehrt hat, und umgekehrt das negative Bestimmte in Positives, daß das reflektirende Denken sich in diesen Bestimmungen verwirrt und sich widersprechend wird. Die Unbekanntschaft mit der Natur derselben ist der Meinung, diese Verwirrung sey etwas Unrechtes, das nicht geschehen soll und schreibt sie einem subjektiven Fehler zu. Dieses Übergehen bleibt in der That auch bloße Verwirrung, insofern das Bewußtseyn über die Nothwendigkeit der Verwandelung nicht vorhan den ist.—Es ist aber, auch für die äußere Reflexion, eine einfache Betrachtung, daß fürs erste das Positive nicht ein unmittelbar Identisches ist, sondern Theils ein Entgegengesetztes gegen das Negative, und daß es nur in dieser Beziehung Bedeutung hat, also das Negative selbst in seinem Begriffe liegt, Theils aber, daß es an ihm selbst die sich auf sich beziehende Negation des bloßen Gesetztseyns oder des Negativen also selbst die absolute Negation in sich ist.—Ebenso das Negative, das dem Positiven gegenüber steht, hat nur Sinn in dieser Beziehung auf dieß sein Anderes; es enthält also dasselbe in seinem Begriffe. Das Negative hat aber auch ohne Beziehung auf das Positive ein eigenes Bestehen; es ist mit sich identisch; so ist es aber selbst das, was das Positive seyn sollte.\n\nVornemlich wird der Gegensatz vom Positiven und Negativen in dem Sinne genommen, daß jenes (ob es gleich seinem Namen nach das Ponirtseyn, Gesetztseyn ausdrückt) ein Objectives seyn soll, dieses aber ein Subjektives, welches nur einer äußern Reflexion angehöre, das an und für sich seyende Objective nichts angehe, und ganz und gar nicht für dasselbe vorhanden sey. In der That, wenn das Negative nichts anders als die Abstraktion einer subjektiven Willkür oder eine Bestimmung einer äußerlichen Vergleichung ausdrückt, so ist es freilich für das objektive Positive nicht vorhanden, d. h. dieses ist nicht an ihm selbst auf eine solche leere Abstraktion bezogen; aber dann ist ihm die Bestimmung, daß es ein Positives sey, gleichfalls nur äußerlich.—So gilt, um ein Beispiel von dem fixen Gegensatze dieser Reflexions-Bestimmungen anzuführen, das Licht überhaupt für das nur Positive, die Finsterniß aber für das nur Negative. Aber das Licht hat in seiner unendlichen Expansion und der Kraft seiner aufschließenden und belebenden Wirksamkeit wesentlich die Natur absoluter Negativität. Die Finsterniß dagegen, als Unmannigfaltiges oder der sich nicht selbst in sich unterscheidende Schooß der Erzeugung, ist das einfache mit sich Identische, das Positive. Sie wird als das nur Negative in dem Sinne genommen, daß sie als bloße Abwesenheit des Lichts für dasselbe ganz und gar nicht vorhanden seye, —so daß dieses, indem es sich auf sie bezieht, sich nicht auf ein Anderes, sondern rein auf sich selbst beziehen, also diese nur vor ihm verschwinden soll. Aber bekanntlich wird das Licht durch die Finsterniß zum Grau getrübt; und außer dieser bloß quantitativen Veränderung erleidet es auch die qualitative, durch die Beziehung darauf zur Farbe bestimmt zu werden.—So ist z.B. auch die Tugend nicht ohne Kampf; sie ist vielmehr der höchste, vollendete Kampf; so ist sie nicht nur das Positive, sondern absolute Negativität; sie ist auch nicht nur in Vergleichung mit dem Laster Tugend, sondern ist an ihr selbst Entgegensetzung und Bekämpfung. Oder das Laster ist nicht nur der Mangel der Tugend,—auch die Unschuld ist dieser Mangel,—und nicht nur für eine äußere Reflexion von der Tugend unterschieden, sondern an sich selbst ihr entgegengesetzt, es ist böse. Das Böse besteht in dem Beruhen auf sich, gegen das Gute; es ist die positive Negativität. Die Unschuld aber, als Mangel sowohl des Guten als des Bösen, ist gleichgültig gegen beide Bestimmungen, weder positiv noch negativ. Aber zugleich ist dieser Mangel auch als Bestimmtheit zu nehmen, und einer Seits ist sie als die positive Natur von Etwas zu betrachten, als sie sich anderer Seits auf ein Entgegengesetztes bezieht, und alle Naturen aus ihrer Unschuld, aus ihrer gleichgültigen Identität mit sich, heraustreten, sich durch sich selbst auf ihr Anderes beziehen und dadurch zu Grunde richten, oder, im positiven Sinne, in ihren Grund zurückgehen.—Auch die Wahrheit ist das Positive als das mit dem Objecte übereinstimmende Wissen, aber sie ist nur diese Gleichheit mit sich, insofern das Wissen sich negativ gegen das Andere verhalten, das Object durchdrungen und die Negation, die es ist, aufgehoben hat. Der Irrthum ist ein Positives, als eine Meinung des nicht an und für sich seyenden, die sich weiß und behauptet. Die Unwissenheit aber ist entweder das gegen Wahrheit und Irrthum Gleichgültige, somit weder als positiv noch als negativ bestimmt und die Bestimmung derselben als ein Mangel gehört der äußeren Reflexion an, oder aber als objektiv, als eigene Bestimmung einer Natur, ist sie der Trieb, der gegen sich gerichtet ist; ein Negatives, das eine positive Richtung in sich enthält.—Es ist eine der wichtigsten Erkenntnisse, diese Natur der betrachteten Reflexions-Bestimmungen, daß ihre Wahrheit nur in ihrer Beziehung auf einander, und damit darin besteht, daß jede in ihrem Begriffe selbst die andere enthält, einzusehen und festzuhalten; ohne diese Erkenntniß läßt sich eigentlich kein Schritt in der Philosophie thun.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0001","text":"Das Positive und Negative ist dasselbe. Dieser Ausdruck gehört der äußern Reflexion an, insofern sie mit diesen beiden Bestimmungen eine Vergleichung anstellt. Es ist aber nicht eine äußere Vergleichung, welche zwischen denselben, ebenso wenig als zwischen andern Kategorien anzustellen ist, sondern sie sind an ihnen selbst zu betrachten, d. h. es ist zu betrachten, was ihre eigene Reflexion ist. An dieser aber hat es sich gezeigt, daß jedes wesentlich das Scheinen seiner im Andern und selbst das Setzen seiner als des Andern ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"119.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0002","text":"Das Vorstellen, insofern es das Positive und Negative nicht betrachtet, wie sie an und für sich sind, kann aber allerdings an das Vergleichen verwiesen werden, um das Haltlose dieser Unterschiedenen, die von ihm als fest einander gegenüber angenommen sind, aufmerksam zu werden. Eine geringe Erfahrung in dem reflektirenden Denken wird es schon wahrnehmen, daß wenn etwas als positiv bestimmt worden, indem man nun von dieser Grundlage weiter geht, sich dasselbe unmittelbar unter der Hand in Negatives verkehrt hat, und umgekehrt das negative Bestimmte in Positives, daß das reflektirende Denken sich in diesen Bestimmungen verwirrt und sich widersprechend wird. Die Unbekanntschaft mit der Natur derselben ist der Meinung, diese Verwirrung sey etwas Unrechtes, das nicht geschehen soll und schreibt sie einem subjektiven Fehler zu.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"119.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0003","text":"Dieses Übergehen bleibt in der That auch bloße Verwirrung, insofern das Bewußtseyn über die Nothwendigkeit der Verwandelung nicht vorhan den ist.—Es ist aber, auch für die äußere Reflexion, eine einfache Betrachtung, daß fürs erste das Positive nicht ein unmittelbar Identisches ist, sondern Theils ein Entgegengesetztes gegen das Negative, und daß es nur in dieser Beziehung Bedeutung hat, also das Negative selbst in seinem Begriffe liegt, Theils aber, daß es an ihm selbst die sich auf sich beziehende Negation des bloßen Gesetztseyns oder des Negativen also selbst die absolute Negation in sich ist.—Ebenso das Negative, das dem Positiven gegenüber steht, hat nur Sinn in dieser Beziehung auf dieß sein Anderes; es enthält also dasselbe in seinem Begriffe.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"119.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0004","text":"Das Negative hat aber auch ohne Beziehung auf das Positive ein eigenes Bestehen; es ist mit sich identisch; so ist es aber selbst das, was das Positive seyn sollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"119.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0005","text":"Vornemlich wird der Gegensatz vom Positiven und Negativen in dem Sinne genommen, daß jenes (ob es gleich seinem Namen nach das Ponirtseyn, Gesetztseyn ausdrückt) ein Objectives seyn soll, dieses aber ein Subjektives, welches nur einer äußern Reflexion angehöre, das an und für sich seyende Objective nichts angehe, und ganz und gar nicht für dasselbe vorhanden sey. In der That, wenn das Negative nichts anders als die Abstraktion einer subjektiven Willkür oder eine Bestimmung einer äußerlichen Vergleichung ausdrückt, so ist es freilich für das objektive Positive nicht vorhanden, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"119.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0006","text":"dieses ist nicht an ihm selbst auf eine solche leere Abstraktion bezogen; aber dann ist ihm die Bestimmung, daß es ein Positives sey, gleichfalls nur äußerlich.—So gilt, um ein Beispiel von dem fixen Gegensatze dieser Reflexions-Bestimmungen anzuführen, das Licht überhaupt für das nur Positive, die Finsterniß aber für das nur Negative. Aber das Licht hat in seiner unendlichen Expansion und der Kraft seiner aufschließenden und belebenden Wirksamkeit wesentlich die Natur absoluter Negativität. Die Finsterniß dagegen, als Unmannigfaltiges oder der sich nicht selbst in sich unterscheidende Schooß der Erzeugung, ist das einfache mit sich Identische, das Positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"119.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0007","text":"Sie wird als das nur Negative in dem Sinne genommen, daß sie als bloße Abwesenheit des Lichts für dasselbe ganz und gar nicht vorhanden seye, —so daß dieses, indem es sich auf sie bezieht, sich nicht auf ein Anderes, sondern rein auf sich selbst beziehen, also diese nur vor ihm verschwinden soll. Aber bekanntlich wird das Licht durch die Finsterniß zum Grau getrübt; und außer dieser bloß quantitativen Veränderung erleidet es auch die qualitative, durch die Beziehung darauf zur Farbe bestimmt zu werden.—So ist z.B. auch die Tugend nicht ohne Kampf; sie ist vielmehr der höchste, vollendete Kampf; so ist sie nicht nur das Positive, sondern absolute Negativität; sie ist auch nicht nur in Vergleichung mit dem Laster Tugend, sondern ist an ihr selbst Entgegensetzung und Bekämpfung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"119.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0008","text":"Oder das Laster ist nicht nur der Mangel der Tugend,—auch die Unschuld ist dieser Mangel,—und nicht nur für eine äußere Reflexion von der Tugend unterschieden, sondern an sich selbst ihr entgegengesetzt, es ist böse. Das Böse besteht in dem Beruhen auf sich, gegen das Gute; es ist die positive Negativität. Die Unschuld aber, als Mangel sowohl des Guten als des Bösen, ist gleichgültig gegen beide Bestimmungen, weder positiv noch negativ.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"119.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0009","text":"Aber zugleich ist dieser Mangel auch als Bestimmtheit zu nehmen, und einer Seits ist sie als die positive Natur von Etwas zu betrachten, als sie sich anderer Seits auf ein Entgegengesetztes bezieht, und alle Naturen aus ihrer Unschuld, aus ihrer gleichgültigen Identität mit sich, heraustreten, sich durch sich selbst auf ihr Anderes beziehen und dadurch zu Grunde richten, oder, im positiven Sinne, in ihren Grund zurückgehen.—Auch die Wahrheit ist das Positive als das mit dem Objecte übereinstimmende Wissen, aber sie ist nur diese Gleichheit mit sich, insofern das Wissen sich negativ gegen das Andere verhalten, das Object durchdrungen und die Negation, die es ist, aufgehoben hat. Der Irrthum ist ein Positives, als eine Meinung des nicht an und für sich seyenden, die sich weiß und behauptet.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"119.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0010","text":"Die Unwissenheit aber ist entweder das gegen Wahrheit und Irrthum Gleichgültige, somit weder als positiv noch als negativ bestimmt und die Bestimmung derselben als ein Mangel gehört der äußeren Reflexion an, oder aber als objektiv, als eigene Bestimmung einer Natur, ist sie der Trieb, der gegen sich gerichtet ist; ein Negatives, das eine positive Richtung in sich enthält.—Es ist eine der wichtigsten Erkenntnisse, diese Natur der betrachteten Reflexions-Bestimmungen, daß ihre Wahrheit nur in ihrer Beziehung auf einander, und damit darin besteht, daß jede in ihrem Begriffe selbst die andere enthält, einzusehen und festzuhalten; ohne diese Erkenntniß läßt sich eigentlich kein Schritt in der Philosophie thun.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"119.10"}],"sha256":"fb6e72a7716f7fc89710ff7119fd81c94dde450663eb2b1e40dd05fe5c09572c","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104921085088Z_bc54c100","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 1.","source_sha256":"fb6e72a7716f7fc89710ff7119fd81c94dde450663eb2b1e40dd05fe5c09572c","sha256":"179b39ea2cbfb5b3f0fa1c699dfb62d2153e682faf41da7015b02b9cf5493cff","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:49:21.085138+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0001","text":"The positive and the negative are the same. This expression belongs to external reflection, insofar as it institutes a comparison with these two determinations. But it is not an external comparison which is to be instituted between them, any more than between other categories; rather, they are to be considered in themselves, i.e. it is to be considered what their own reflection is. In this, however, it has shown itself that each is essentially the shining of itself in the other, and even the positing of itself as the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"119.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0002","text":"Representational thinking, insofar as it does not consider the positive and the negative as they are in and for themselves, may indeed be referred to comparison, in order to become aware of the instability of these distinct things, which it assumes as fixed over against one another. A slight experience in reflective thinking will already perceive that, when something has been determined as positive, if one now proceeds further from this foundation, it has immediately, as it were under one's hand, turned into something negative, and conversely the negatively determined into something positive; that reflective thinking becomes confused in these determinations and contradictory. Unfamiliarity with their nature is of the opinion that this confusion is something incorrect, which ought not to occur, and ascribes it to a subjective error.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"119.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0003","text":"This transition does in fact also remain mere confusion, insofar as consciousness of the necessity of the transformation is not present.—But, even for external reflection, it is a simple consideration that, in the first place, the positive is not something immediately identical, but is partly an opposite to the negative, and has significance only in this relation, thus has the negative itself in its concept; and partly, that in itself it is the negation relating itself to itself of mere positedness, or of the negative, thus itself contains absolute negation within itself.—Likewise, the negative which stands over against the positive has sense only in this relation to this its other; it thus contains the same in its concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"119.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0004","text":"But the negative also has an existence of its own without relation to the positive; it is identical with itself; but thus it is itself that which the positive was supposed to be.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"119.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0005","text":"Pre-eminently, the opposition of positive and negative is taken in the sense that the former (although according to its name it expresses being-posited, positedness) is supposed to be something objective, but the latter something subjective, belonging only to an external reflection, not concerning the objective that is in and for itself, and not at all being present for it. In fact, if the negative expresses nothing but the abstraction of a subjective arbitrariness or a determination of an external comparison, then it is indeed not present for the objective positive, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"119.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0006","text":"the latter is not related in itself to such an empty abstraction; but then the determination that it is something positive is likewise merely external to it.—Thus, to adduce an example of the fixed opposition of these determinations of reflection, light in general counts as the merely positive, darkness, however, as the merely negative. Yet light, in its infinite expansion and in the force of its opening and enlivening efficacy, essentially has the nature of absolute negativity. Darkness, on the other hand, as the undifferentiated, or the womb of generation that does not distinguish itself within itself, is the simple identical-with-itself, the positive.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"119.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0007","text":"It is taken as the merely negative in the sense that, as mere absence of light, it is not at all present for light,—so that light, in relating itself to it, is not to relate itself to an other, but purely to itself, and thus darkness is only to vanish before it. But, as is well known, light is clouded into grey by darkness; and apart from this merely quantitative alteration, it also undergoes the qualitative one of being determined as colour through its relation to it.—Thus, for example, virtue too is not without struggle; it is rather the highest, completed struggle; thus it is not merely the positive, but absolute negativity; nor is it virtue merely in comparison with vice, but is in itself opposition and combat.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"119.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0008","text":"Or vice is not merely the lack of virtue,—innocence too is this lack,—and is distinguished from virtue not merely for an external reflection, but is in itself opposed to it; it is evil. Evil consists in resting upon itself, against the good; it is positive negativity. Innocence, however, as lack alike of good and of evil, is indifferent toward both determinations, neither positive nor negative.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"119.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0009","text":"But at the same time this lack is also to be taken as determinacy, and on the one hand it is to be considered as the positive nature of something, while on the other hand it relates itself to an opposite; and all natures emerge from their innocence, from their indifferent identity with themselves, relate themselves through themselves to their other, and thereby go to ruin, or, in the positive sense, return into their ground.—Truth too is the positive as knowledge agreeing with the object; but it is this equality with itself only insofar as knowledge has behaved negatively toward the other, has penetrated the object, and has sublated the negation that it is. Error is a positive, as an opinion of what is not in and for itself, which knows and asserts itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"119.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_31:P0010","text":"Ignorance, however, is either that which is indifferent toward truth and error, thus determined neither as positive nor as negative, and its determination as a lack belongs to external reflection; or else, objectively, as the proper determination of a nature, it is the drive that is directed against itself; a negative which contains a positive direction within itself.—It is one of the most important cognitions to understand and hold fast this nature of the determinations of reflection under consideration, namely, that their truth consists only in their relation to one another, and hence in the fact that each contains the other in its concept itself; without this cognition, properly speaking, no step can be taken in philosophy.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"119.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_31:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"77fb528ff5f9964f740ddacdd697af86a130278613fd391d87ca4124015af17b","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32","title":"Remark 2.","order":120,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_32","text":"Die Bestimmung der Entgegensetzung ist gleichfalls zu einem Satze gemacht worden, dem sogenannten Satze des ausgeschlossenen Dritten.\n\nEtwas ist entweder A oder Nicht-A; es giebt kein Drittes.\n\nDieser Satz enthält zuerst, daß Alles ein Entgegengesetztes ist, ein entweder als positiv oder als negativ Bestimmtes.—Ein wichtiger Satz, der darin seine Nothwendigkeit hat, daß die Identität in Verschiedenheit und diese in Entgegensetzung übergeht. Allein er pflegt nicht in diesem Sinne verstanden zu werden, sondern soll gewöhnlich so viel heißen, daß einem Dinge von allen Prädikaten entweder dieses Prädikat selbst oder sein Nichtseyn zukomme. Das Entgegengesetzte bedeutet hier bloß den Mangel oder vielmehr die Unbestimmtheit; und der Satz ist so unbedeutend, daß es nicht der Mühe werth ist, ihn zu sagen. Wenn die Bestimmungen süß, grün, viereckig genommen,—und es sollen alle Prädikate genommen werden—und nun vom Geiste gesagt wird, er sey entweder süß oder nicht süß, grün oder nicht grün, u.s.f. so ist dieß eine Trivialität, die zu nichts führt. Die Bestimmtheit, das Prädikat, wird auf Etwas bezogen; das Etwas ist bestimmt, sagt der Satz aus; nun soll er wesentlich dieß enthalten, daß die Bestimmtheit sich näher bestimme, zur Bestimmtheit an sich, zur Entgegensetzung werde. Statt dessen geht er aber in jenem trivialen Sinne von der Bestimmtheit nur über zu ihrem Nichtseyn überhaupt, zurück zur Unbestimmtheit.\n\nDer Satz des ausgeschlossenen Dritten unterscheidet sich ferner vom oben betrachteten Satze der Identität oder des Widerspruchs, der so hieß: es giebt nicht etwas, das zugleich A und Nicht-A ist. Er enthält, daß es nicht Etwas gebe, welches weder A noch Nicht-A, daß es nicht ein Drittes gebe, das gegen den Gegensatz gleichgültig sey. In der That aber giebt es in diesem Satze selbst das Dritte, das gleichgültig gegen den Gegensatz ist, nämlich A selbst ist darin vorhanden. Dieß A ist weder +A noch—A, und ebenso wohl auch +A als—A.—Das Etwas, das entweder +A oder Nicht-A seyn sollte, ist hiermit auf +A sowohl als Nicht-A bezogen; und wieder, indem es auf A bezogen ist, solle es nicht auf Nicht-A bezogen seyn, so wie nicht auf A, indem es auf Nicht-A bezogen ist. Das Etwas selbst ist also das Dritte, welches ausgeschlossen seyn sollte. Indem die entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen, im Etwas ebenso sehr gesetzt als in diesem Setzen aufgehobene sind, so ist das Dritte, das hier die Gestalt eines todten Etwas hat, tiefer genommen, die Einheit der Reflexion, in welche, als in den Grund die Entgegensetzung zurückgeht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0001","text":"Die Bestimmung der Entgegensetzung ist gleichfalls zu einem Satze gemacht worden, dem sogenannten Satze des ausgeschlossenen Dritten.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"120.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0002","text":"Etwas ist entweder A oder Nicht-A; es giebt kein Drittes.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"120.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0003","text":"Dieser Satz enthält zuerst, daß Alles ein Entgegengesetztes ist, ein entweder als positiv oder als negativ Bestimmtes.—Ein wichtiger Satz, der darin seine Nothwendigkeit hat, daß die Identität in Verschiedenheit und diese in Entgegensetzung übergeht. Allein er pflegt nicht in diesem Sinne verstanden zu werden, sondern soll gewöhnlich so viel heißen, daß einem Dinge von allen Prädikaten entweder dieses Prädikat selbst oder sein Nichtseyn zukomme. Das Entgegengesetzte bedeutet hier bloß den Mangel oder vielmehr die Unbestimmtheit; und der Satz ist so unbedeutend, daß es nicht der Mühe werth ist, ihn zu sagen. Wenn die Bestimmungen süß, grün, viereckig genommen,—und es sollen alle Prädikate genommen werden—und nun vom Geiste gesagt wird, er sey entweder süß oder nicht süß, grün oder nicht grün, u.s.f. so ist dieß eine Trivialität, die zu nichts führt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"120.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0004","text":"Die Bestimmtheit, das Prädikat, wird auf Etwas bezogen; das Etwas ist bestimmt, sagt der Satz aus; nun soll er wesentlich dieß enthalten, daß die Bestimmtheit sich näher bestimme, zur Bestimmtheit an sich, zur Entgegensetzung werde. Statt dessen geht er aber in jenem trivialen Sinne von der Bestimmtheit nur über zu ihrem Nichtseyn überhaupt, zurück zur Unbestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"120.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0005","text":"Der Satz des ausgeschlossenen Dritten unterscheidet sich ferner vom oben betrachteten Satze der Identität oder des Widerspruchs, der so hieß: es giebt nicht etwas, das zugleich A und Nicht-A ist. Er enthält, daß es nicht Etwas gebe, welches weder A noch Nicht-A, daß es nicht ein Drittes gebe, das gegen den Gegensatz gleichgültig sey. In der That aber giebt es in diesem Satze selbst das Dritte, das gleichgültig gegen den Gegensatz ist, nämlich A selbst ist darin vorhanden. Dieß A ist weder +A noch—A, und ebenso wohl auch +A als—A.—Das Etwas, das entweder +A oder Nicht-A seyn sollte, ist hiermit auf +A sowohl als Nicht-A bezogen; und wieder, indem es auf A bezogen ist, solle es nicht auf Nicht-A bezogen seyn, so wie nicht auf A, indem es auf Nicht-A bezogen ist. Das Etwas selbst ist also das Dritte, welches ausgeschlossen seyn sollte.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"120.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0006","text":"Indem die entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen, im Etwas ebenso sehr gesetzt als in diesem Setzen aufgehobene sind, so ist das Dritte, das hier die Gestalt eines todten Etwas hat, tiefer genommen, die Einheit der Reflexion, in welche, als in den Grund die Entgegensetzung zurückgeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"120.6"}],"sha256":"4575b447ed1472d9e0b36b3f41b52fcad22e3bc3e1d2a1575f5dd5addc86e599","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104926717277Z_e9f1719e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 2.","source_sha256":"4575b447ed1472d9e0b36b3f41b52fcad22e3bc3e1d2a1575f5dd5addc86e599","sha256":"3924845b216cfc919873fe2135b2142aa87e9b9d080c23ddb0e7909e1f4ee053","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:49:26.717322+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0001","text":"The determination of opposition has likewise been made into a proposition, the so-called law of the excluded middle.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"120.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_32:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0002","text":"Something is either A or not-A; there is no third.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"120.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_32:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0003","text":"This proposition contains, first, that everything is an opposite, something determined either as positive or as negative.—An important proposition, which has its necessity in the fact that identity passes over into difference, and this into opposition. Yet it is not usually understood in this sense, but is ordinarily supposed to mean no more than that, of all predicates, either this predicate itself or its non-being pertains to a thing. Here the opposite signifies merely the lack, or rather the indeterminacy; and the proposition is so insignificant that it is not worth the trouble of stating it. If the determinations sweet, green, square are taken—and all predicates are supposed to be taken—and it is then said of spirit that it is either sweet or not sweet, green or not green, etc., this is a triviality that leads nowhere.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"120.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_32:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0004","text":"Determinacy, the predicate, is related to something; the proposition states that the something is determined; now it ought essentially to contain that determinacy determines itself more specifically, becomes determinacy in itself, becomes opposition. Instead, however, in that trivial sense it passes from determinacy only to its non-being in general, back to indeterminacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"120.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_32:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0005","text":"The law of the excluded middle further differs from the proposition of identity or contradiction considered above, which ran: there is not something which is at once A and not-A. It contains that there is no something which is neither A nor not-A, that there is no third which is indifferent to the opposition. But in fact the third, which is indifferent to the opposition, is present in this proposition itself, namely A itself is present in it. This A is neither +A nor—A, and equally well both +A and—A.—The something which was supposed to be either +A or not-A is thereby related both to +A and to not-A; and again, inasmuch as it is related to A, it ought not to be related to not-A, just as it ought not to be related to A inasmuch as it is related to not-A. The something itself is thus the third which was supposed to be excluded.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"120.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_32:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_32:P0006","text":"Since the opposed determinations are as much posited in the something as they are sublated in this positing, the third, which here has the shape of a dead something, taken more deeply, is the unity of reflection, into which opposition recedes as into its ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"120.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_32:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"aeb1a9362befd4e1a986cee2d29a9225252f91012661bef397d2e8a436fb5d93","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33","title":"Remark 3.","order":121,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_33","text":"Wenn nun die ersten Reflexions-Bestimmungen, die Identität, die Verschiedenheit und die Entgegensetzung, in einem Satze aufgestellt worden, so sollte noch vielmehr diejenige, in welche sie als in ihre Wahrheit übergehen, nämlich der Widerspruch, in einen Satz gefaßt und gesagt werden: Alle Dinge sind an sich selbst widersprechend, und zwar in dem Sinne, daß dieser Satz gegen die übrigen vielmehr die Wahrheit und das Wesen der Dinge ausdrücke.—Der Widerspruch, der an der Entgegensetzung hervortritt, ist nur das entwickelte Nichts, das in der Identität enthalten ist, und in dem Ausdrucke vorkam, daß der Satz der Identität Nichts sage. Diese Negation bestimmt sich weiter zur Verschiedenheit und zur Entgegensetzung, welche nun der gesetzte Widerspruch ist.\n\nEs ist aber eines der Grundvorurtheile der bisherigen Logik und des gewöhnlichen Vorstellens, als ob der Widerspruch nicht eine so wesenhafte und immanente Bestimmung sey, als die Identität; ja wenn von Rangordnung die Rede, und beide Bestimmungen als getrennte festzuhalten wären, so wäre der Widerspruch für das Tiefere und Wesenhaftere zu nehmen. Denn die Identität ihm gegenüber ist nur die Bestimmung des einfachen Unmittelbaren, des todten Seyns; er aber ist die Wurzel aller Bewegung und Lebendigkeit; nur insofern etwas in sich selbst einen Widerspruch hat, bewegt es sich, hat Trieb und Thätigkeit.\n\nDer Widerspruch wird gewöhnlich fürs erste von den Dingen, von dem Seyenden und Wahren überhaupt, entfernt; es wird behauptet, daß es nichts Widersprechendes gebe. Er wird fürs andre dagegen in die subjektive Reflexion geschoben, die durch ihre Beziehung und Vergleichung ihn erst setze. Aber auch in dieser Reflexion sey er nicht eigentlich vorhanden, denn das Widersprechende könne nicht vorgestellt noch gedacht werden. Er gilt überhaupt, sey es am Wirklichen oder in der denkenden Reflexion, für eine Zufälligkeit, gleichsam für eine Abnormität und vorübergehenden Krankheitsparoxysmus.\n\nWas nun die Behauptung betrifft, daß es den Widerspruch nicht gebe, daß er nicht ein Vorhandenes sey, so brauchen wir uns um eine solche Versicherung nicht zu bekümmern; eine absolute Bestimmung des Wesens muß sich in aller Erfahrung finden, in allem Wirklichen wie in jedem Begriffe. Oben beim Unendlichen, das der Widerspruch ist, wie er in der Sphäre des Seyns sich zeigt, ist das Gleiche bereits erinnert worden. Die gemeine Erfahrung aber spricht es selbst aus, daß es wenigstens eine Menge widersprechender Dinge, widersprechender Einrichtungen u.s.f. gebe, deren Widerspruch nicht bloß in einer äußerlichen Reflexion, sondern in ihnen selbst vorhanden ist. Er ist aber ferner nicht bloß als eine Abnormität zu nehmen, die nur hier und da vorkäme, sondern ist das Negative in seiner wesenhaften Bestimmung, das Princip aller Selbstbewegung, die in nichts weiter besteht, als in einer Darstellung desselben. Die äußerliche sinnliche Bewegung selbst ist sein unmittelbares Daseyn. Es bewegt sich etwas nur, nicht indem es in diesem Jetzt hier ist, und in einem andern Jetzt dort, sondern indem es in einem und demselben Jetzt hier und nicht hier, indem es in diesem Hier zugleich ist und nicht ist. Man muß den alten Dialektikern die Widersprüche zugeben, die sie in der Bewegung aufzeigen, aber daraus folgt nicht, daß darum die Bewegung nicht ist, sondern vielmehr daß die Bewegung der daseyende Widerspruch selbst ist.\n\nEbenso ist die innere, die eigentliche Selbstbewegung, der Trieb überhaupt, (Appetit oder Nisus der Monade, die Entelechie des absolut einfachen Wesens) nichts anderes, als daß Etwas in sich selbst, und der Mangel, das Negative seiner selbst, in einer und derselben Rücksicht ist. Die abstrakte Identität mit sich ist noch keine Lebendigkeit, sondern daß das Positive an sich selbst die Negativität ist, dadurch geht es außer sich und setzt sich in Veränderung. Etwas ist also lebendig, nur insofern es den Widerspruch in sich enthält, und zwar diese Kraft ist, den Widerspruch in sich zu fassen und auszuhalten. Wenn aber ein Existirendes nicht in seiner positiven Bestimmung zugleich über seine negative überzugreiffen und eine in der andern festzuhalten, den Widerspruch nicht in ihm selbst zu haben vermag, so ist es nicht die lebendige Einheit selbst, nicht Grund, sondern geht in dem Widerspruche zu Grunde.—Das spekulative Denken besteht nur darin, daß das Denken den Widerspruch und in ihm sich selbst festhält, nicht aber daß es sich, wie es dem Vorstellen geht, von ihm beherrschen und durch ihn sich seine Bestimmungen nur in andere oder in Nichts auflösen läßt.\n\nWenn in der Bewegung, dem Triebe und dergleichen der Widerspruch in die Einfachheit dieser Bestimmungen für das Vorstellen verhüllt ist, so stellt sich hingegen in den Verhältnißbestimmungen der Widerspruch unmittelbar dar. Die trivialsten Beispiele, von Oben und Unten, Rechts und Links, Vater und Sohn und so fort ins Unendliche, enthalten alle den Gegensatz in Einem. Oben ist, was nicht Unten ist; Oben ist bestimmt nur dieß, nicht Unten zu seyn, und ist nur, insofern ein Unten ist; und umgekehrt; in der einen Bestimmung liegt ihr Gegentheil. Vater ist das Andre des Sohnes, und Sohn das Andre des Vaters und jedes ist nur als dieß Andre des andern; und zugleich ist die eine Bestimmung nur in Beziehung auf die andere; ihr Seyn ist Ein Bestehen. Der Vater ist außer der Beziehung auf Sohn auch etwas für sich; aber so ist er nicht Vater, sondern ein Mann überhaupt; wie Oben und Unten, Rechts und Links auch in sich reflektirte, außer der Beziehung etwas sind; aber nur Orte überhaupt.—Die Entgegengesetzten enthalten insofern den Widerspruch, als sie in derselben Rücksicht sich negativ auf einander beziehende oder sich gegenseitig aufhebende und gegen einander gleichgültige sind. Die Vorstellung, indem sie zum Momente der Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmungen übergeht, vergißt darin ihre negative Einheit und behält sie somit nur als Verschiedene überhaupt, in welcher Bestimmung Rechts nicht mehr Rechts, Links nicht mehr Links u.s.f. ist. Indem sie aber Rechts und Links in der That vor sich hat, so hat sie diese Bestimmungen vor sich als sich negirend, die eine in der andern, und in dieser Einheit zugleich sich nicht negirend, sondern jede gleichgültig für sich seyend.\n\nDas Vorstellen hat daher wohl allenthalben den Widerspruch zu seinem Inhalte, kommt aber nicht zum Bewußtseyn desselben; es bleibt äußerliche Reflexion, die von der Gleichheit zur Ungleichheit, oder von der negativen Beziehung zum Reflektirtseyn der Unterschiedenen in sich, übergeht. Sie hält diese beiden Bestimmungen einander äußerlich gegenüber und hat nur sie, nicht aber das Übergehen, welches das Wesentliche ist, und den Widerspruch enthält, im Sinne. —Die geistreiche Reflexion, um diese hier zu erwähnen, besteht dagegen im Auffassen und Aussprechen des Widerspruchs. Ob sie zwar den Begriff der Dinge und ihrer Verhältnisse nicht ausdrückt und nur Vorstellungsbestimmungen zu ihrem Material und Inhalt hat, so bringt sie dieselben in eine Beziehung, die ihren Widerspruch enthält und durch diesen hindurch ihren Begriff scheinen läßt.—Die denkende Vernunft aber spitzt, so zu sagen, den abgestumpften Unterschied des Verschiedenen, die bloße Mannigfaltigkeit der Vorstellung, zum wesentlichen Unterschiede, zum Gegensatze, zu. Die Mannigfaltigen werden erst, auf die Spitze des Widerspruchs getrieben, regsam und lebendig gegen einander, und erhalten in ihm die Negativität, welche die inwohnende Pulsation der Selbstbewegung und Lebendigkeit ist.\n\nEs ist schon über den ontologischen Beweis vom Daseyn Gottes erinnert worden, daß die darin zu Grunde gelegte Bestimmung, der Inbegriff aller Realitäten ist. Von dieser Bestimmung pflegt zuerst gezeigt zu werden, daß sie möglich sey, weil sie keinen Widerspruch enthalte, indem die Realität nur als Realität ohne Schranken genommen werde. Es wurde erinnert, daß damit jener Inbegriff zum einfachen unbestimmten Seyn, oder wenn die Realitäten in der That als mehrere Bestimmte genommen werden, zum Inbegriff aller Negationen wird. Näher den Unterschied der Realität genommen, so wird er aus der Verschiedenheit zum Gegensatze und damit zum Widerspruch, und der Inbegriff aller Realitäten überhaupt zum absoluten Widerspruch in sich selbst. Der gewöhnliche Horror, den das vorstellende, nicht speculative Denken, wie die Natur vor dem Vacuum, vor dem Widerspruche hat, verwirft diese Konsequenz; denn es bleibt bei der einseitigen Betrachtung der Auflösung des Widerspruchs in Nichts stehen, und erkennt die positive Seite desselben nicht, nach welcher er absolute Thätigkeit, und absoluter Grund wird.\n\nEs ist überhaupt aus der Betrachtung der Natur des Widerspruchs hervorgegangen, daß es für sich noch, so zu sagen, kein Schaden, Mangel oder Fehler einer Sache ist, wenn an ihr ein Widerspruch aufgezeigt werden kann. Vielmehr jede Bestimmung, jedes Konkrete, jeder Begriff ist wesentlich eine Einheit unterschiedener und unterscheidbarer Momente, die durch den bestimmten, wesentlichen Unterschied in widersprechende übergehen. Dieses Widersprechende löst sich allerdings in Nichts auf, es geht in seine negative Einheit zurück. Das Ding, das Subjekt, der Begriff ist nun eben diese negative Einheit selbst; es ist ein an sich selbst Widersprechendes, aber ebenso sehr der aufgelöste Widerspruch; es ist der Grund, der seine Bestimmungen enthält und trägt. Das Ding, das Subjekt, oder der Begriff ist als in seiner Sphäre in sich reflektirt, sein aufgelöster Widerspruch, aber seine ganze Sphäre ist auch wieder eine bestimmte, verschiedene; so ist sie eine endliche, und dieß heißt eine widersprechende. Von diesem höhern Widerspruche ist nicht sie selbst die Auflösung; sondern hat eine höhere Sphäre zu ihrer negativen Einheit, zu ihrem Grunde. Die endlichen Dinge in ihrer gleichgültigen Mannigfaltigkeit, sind daher überhaupt dieß, widersprechend an sich selbst, in sich gebrochen zu seyn und in ihren Grund zurückzugehen.—Wie weiterhin betrachtet werden wird, so besteht der wahre Schluß von einem Endlichen und Zufälligen auf ein absolut-nothwendiges Wesen nicht darin, daß von dem Endlichen und Zufälligen als dem zum Grunde liegenden und liegen bleibenden Seyn, sondern daß, was auch unmittelbar in der Zufälligkeit liegt, von einem nur fallenden, sich an sich selbst widersprechendem Seyn aus, auf ein absolut nothwendiges geschlossen, oder daß vielmehr aufgezeigt wird, das zufällige Seyn gehe an sich selbst in seinen Grund zurück, worin es sich aufhebt,—ferner daß es durch dieß Zurückgehen den Grund nur so setze, daß es sich selbst vielmehr zum Gesetzten macht. Im gewöhnlichen Schließen erscheint das Seyn des Endlichen als Grund des Absoluten; darum weil Endliches ist, ist das Absolute. Die Wahrheit aber ist, daß darum weil das Endliche der an sich selbst widersprechende Gegensatz, weil es nicht ist, das Absolute ist. In jenem Sinne lautet der Satz des Schlusses so: Das Seyn des Endlichen ist das Seyn des Absoluten; in diesem Sinne aber so: Das Nichtseyn des Endlichen ist das Seyn des Absoluten.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0001","text":"Wenn nun die ersten Reflexions-Bestimmungen, die Identität, die Verschiedenheit und die Entgegensetzung, in einem Satze aufgestellt worden, so sollte noch vielmehr diejenige, in welche sie als in ihre Wahrheit übergehen, nämlich der Widerspruch, in einen Satz gefaßt und gesagt werden: Alle Dinge sind an sich selbst widersprechend, und zwar in dem Sinne, daß dieser Satz gegen die übrigen vielmehr die Wahrheit und das Wesen der Dinge ausdrücke.—Der Widerspruch, der an der Entgegensetzung hervortritt, ist nur das entwickelte Nichts, das in der Identität enthalten ist, und in dem Ausdrucke vorkam, daß der Satz der Identität Nichts sage. Diese Negation bestimmt sich weiter zur Verschiedenheit und zur Entgegensetzung, welche nun der gesetzte Widerspruch ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"121.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0002","text":"Es ist aber eines der Grundvorurtheile der bisherigen Logik und des gewöhnlichen Vorstellens, als ob der Widerspruch nicht eine so wesenhafte und immanente Bestimmung sey, als die Identität; ja wenn von Rangordnung die Rede, und beide Bestimmungen als getrennte festzuhalten wären, so wäre der Widerspruch für das Tiefere und Wesenhaftere zu nehmen. Denn die Identität ihm gegenüber ist nur die Bestimmung des einfachen Unmittelbaren, des todten Seyns; er aber ist die Wurzel aller Bewegung und Lebendigkeit; nur insofern etwas in sich selbst einen Widerspruch hat, bewegt es sich, hat Trieb und Thätigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"121.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0003","text":"Der Widerspruch wird gewöhnlich fürs erste von den Dingen, von dem Seyenden und Wahren überhaupt, entfernt; es wird behauptet, daß es nichts Widersprechendes gebe. Er wird fürs andre dagegen in die subjektive Reflexion geschoben, die durch ihre Beziehung und Vergleichung ihn erst setze. Aber auch in dieser Reflexion sey er nicht eigentlich vorhanden, denn das Widersprechende könne nicht vorgestellt noch gedacht werden. Er gilt überhaupt, sey es am Wirklichen oder in der denkenden Reflexion, für eine Zufälligkeit, gleichsam für eine Abnormität und vorübergehenden Krankheitsparoxysmus.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"121.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0004","text":"Was nun die Behauptung betrifft, daß es den Widerspruch nicht gebe, daß er nicht ein Vorhandenes sey, so brauchen wir uns um eine solche Versicherung nicht zu bekümmern; eine absolute Bestimmung des Wesens muß sich in aller Erfahrung finden, in allem Wirklichen wie in jedem Begriffe. Oben beim Unendlichen, das der Widerspruch ist, wie er in der Sphäre des Seyns sich zeigt, ist das Gleiche bereits erinnert worden. Die gemeine Erfahrung aber spricht es selbst aus, daß es wenigstens eine Menge widersprechender Dinge, widersprechender Einrichtungen u.s.f. gebe, deren Widerspruch nicht bloß in einer äußerlichen Reflexion, sondern in ihnen selbst vorhanden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"121.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0005","text":"Er ist aber ferner nicht bloß als eine Abnormität zu nehmen, die nur hier und da vorkäme, sondern ist das Negative in seiner wesenhaften Bestimmung, das Princip aller Selbstbewegung, die in nichts weiter besteht, als in einer Darstellung desselben. Die äußerliche sinnliche Bewegung selbst ist sein unmittelbares Daseyn. Es bewegt sich etwas nur, nicht indem es in diesem Jetzt hier ist, und in einem andern Jetzt dort, sondern indem es in einem und demselben Jetzt hier und nicht hier, indem es in diesem Hier zugleich ist und nicht ist. Man muß den alten Dialektikern die Widersprüche zugeben, die sie in der Bewegung aufzeigen, aber daraus folgt nicht, daß darum die Bewegung nicht ist, sondern vielmehr daß die Bewegung der daseyende Widerspruch selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"121.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0006","text":"Ebenso ist die innere, die eigentliche Selbstbewegung, der Trieb überhaupt, (Appetit oder Nisus der Monade, die Entelechie des absolut einfachen Wesens) nichts anderes, als daß Etwas in sich selbst, und der Mangel, das Negative seiner selbst, in einer und derselben Rücksicht ist. Die abstrakte Identität mit sich ist noch keine Lebendigkeit, sondern daß das Positive an sich selbst die Negativität ist, dadurch geht es außer sich und setzt sich in Veränderung. Etwas ist also lebendig, nur insofern es den Widerspruch in sich enthält, und zwar diese Kraft ist, den Widerspruch in sich zu fassen und auszuhalten.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"121.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0007","text":"Wenn aber ein Existirendes nicht in seiner positiven Bestimmung zugleich über seine negative überzugreiffen und eine in der andern festzuhalten, den Widerspruch nicht in ihm selbst zu haben vermag, so ist es nicht die lebendige Einheit selbst, nicht Grund, sondern geht in dem Widerspruche zu Grunde.—Das spekulative Denken besteht nur darin, daß das Denken den Widerspruch und in ihm sich selbst festhält, nicht aber daß es sich, wie es dem Vorstellen geht, von ihm beherrschen und durch ihn sich seine Bestimmungen nur in andere oder in Nichts auflösen läßt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"121.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0008","text":"Wenn in der Bewegung, dem Triebe und dergleichen der Widerspruch in die Einfachheit dieser Bestimmungen für das Vorstellen verhüllt ist, so stellt sich hingegen in den Verhältnißbestimmungen der Widerspruch unmittelbar dar. Die trivialsten Beispiele, von Oben und Unten, Rechts und Links, Vater und Sohn und so fort ins Unendliche, enthalten alle den Gegensatz in Einem. Oben ist, was nicht Unten ist; Oben ist bestimmt nur dieß, nicht Unten zu seyn, und ist nur, insofern ein Unten ist; und umgekehrt; in der einen Bestimmung liegt ihr Gegentheil. Vater ist das Andre des Sohnes, und Sohn das Andre des Vaters und jedes ist nur als dieß Andre des andern; und zugleich ist die eine Bestimmung nur in Beziehung auf die andere; ihr Seyn ist Ein Bestehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"121.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0009","text":"Der Vater ist außer der Beziehung auf Sohn auch etwas für sich; aber so ist er nicht Vater, sondern ein Mann überhaupt; wie Oben und Unten, Rechts und Links auch in sich reflektirte, außer der Beziehung etwas sind; aber nur Orte überhaupt.—Die Entgegengesetzten enthalten insofern den Widerspruch, als sie in derselben Rücksicht sich negativ auf einander beziehende oder sich gegenseitig aufhebende und gegen einander gleichgültige sind. Die Vorstellung, indem sie zum Momente der Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmungen übergeht, vergißt darin ihre negative Einheit und behält sie somit nur als Verschiedene überhaupt, in welcher Bestimmung Rechts nicht mehr Rechts, Links nicht mehr Links u.s.f. ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"121.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0010","text":"Indem sie aber Rechts und Links in der That vor sich hat, so hat sie diese Bestimmungen vor sich als sich negirend, die eine in der andern, und in dieser Einheit zugleich sich nicht negirend, sondern jede gleichgültig für sich seyend.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"121.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0011","text":"Das Vorstellen hat daher wohl allenthalben den Widerspruch zu seinem Inhalte, kommt aber nicht zum Bewußtseyn desselben; es bleibt äußerliche Reflexion, die von der Gleichheit zur Ungleichheit, oder von der negativen Beziehung zum Reflektirtseyn der Unterschiedenen in sich, übergeht. Sie hält diese beiden Bestimmungen einander äußerlich gegenüber und hat nur sie, nicht aber das Übergehen, welches das Wesentliche ist, und den Widerspruch enthält, im Sinne. —Die geistreiche Reflexion, um diese hier zu erwähnen, besteht dagegen im Auffassen und Aussprechen des Widerspruchs.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"121.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0012","text":"Ob sie zwar den Begriff der Dinge und ihrer Verhältnisse nicht ausdrückt und nur Vorstellungsbestimmungen zu ihrem Material und Inhalt hat, so bringt sie dieselben in eine Beziehung, die ihren Widerspruch enthält und durch diesen hindurch ihren Begriff scheinen läßt.—Die denkende Vernunft aber spitzt, so zu sagen, den abgestumpften Unterschied des Verschiedenen, die bloße Mannigfaltigkeit der Vorstellung, zum wesentlichen Unterschiede, zum Gegensatze, zu. Die Mannigfaltigen werden erst, auf die Spitze des Widerspruchs getrieben, regsam und lebendig gegen einander, und erhalten in ihm die Negativität, welche die inwohnende Pulsation der Selbstbewegung und Lebendigkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"121.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0013","text":"Es ist schon über den ontologischen Beweis vom Daseyn Gottes erinnert worden, daß die darin zu Grunde gelegte Bestimmung, der Inbegriff aller Realitäten ist. Von dieser Bestimmung pflegt zuerst gezeigt zu werden, daß sie möglich sey, weil sie keinen Widerspruch enthalte, indem die Realität nur als Realität ohne Schranken genommen werde. Es wurde erinnert, daß damit jener Inbegriff zum einfachen unbestimmten Seyn, oder wenn die Realitäten in der That als mehrere Bestimmte genommen werden, zum Inbegriff aller Negationen wird. Näher den Unterschied der Realität genommen, so wird er aus der Verschiedenheit zum Gegensatze und damit zum Widerspruch, und der Inbegriff aller Realitäten überhaupt zum absoluten Widerspruch in sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"121.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0014","text":"Der gewöhnliche Horror, den das vorstellende, nicht speculative Denken, wie die Natur vor dem Vacuum, vor dem Widerspruche hat, verwirft diese Konsequenz; denn es bleibt bei der einseitigen Betrachtung der Auflösung des Widerspruchs in Nichts stehen, und erkennt die positive Seite desselben nicht, nach welcher er absolute Thätigkeit, und absoluter Grund wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"121.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0015","text":"Es ist überhaupt aus der Betrachtung der Natur des Widerspruchs hervorgegangen, daß es für sich noch, so zu sagen, kein Schaden, Mangel oder Fehler einer Sache ist, wenn an ihr ein Widerspruch aufgezeigt werden kann. Vielmehr jede Bestimmung, jedes Konkrete, jeder Begriff ist wesentlich eine Einheit unterschiedener und unterscheidbarer Momente, die durch den bestimmten, wesentlichen Unterschied in widersprechende übergehen. Dieses Widersprechende löst sich allerdings in Nichts auf, es geht in seine negative Einheit zurück. Das Ding, das Subjekt, der Begriff ist nun eben diese negative Einheit selbst; es ist ein an sich selbst Widersprechendes, aber ebenso sehr der aufgelöste Widerspruch; es ist der Grund, der seine Bestimmungen enthält und trägt.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"121.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0016","text":"Das Ding, das Subjekt, oder der Begriff ist als in seiner Sphäre in sich reflektirt, sein aufgelöster Widerspruch, aber seine ganze Sphäre ist auch wieder eine bestimmte, verschiedene; so ist sie eine endliche, und dieß heißt eine widersprechende. Von diesem höhern Widerspruche ist nicht sie selbst die Auflösung; sondern hat eine höhere Sphäre zu ihrer negativen Einheit, zu ihrem Grunde.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"121.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0017","text":"Die endlichen Dinge in ihrer gleichgültigen Mannigfaltigkeit, sind daher überhaupt dieß, widersprechend an sich selbst, in sich gebrochen zu seyn und in ihren Grund zurückzugehen.—Wie weiterhin betrachtet werden wird, so besteht der wahre Schluß von einem Endlichen und Zufälligen auf ein absolut-nothwendiges Wesen nicht darin, daß von dem Endlichen und Zufälligen als dem zum Grunde liegenden und liegen bleibenden Seyn, sondern daß, was auch unmittelbar in der Zufälligkeit liegt, von einem nur fallenden, sich an sich selbst widersprechendem Seyn aus, auf ein absolut nothwendiges geschlossen, oder daß vielmehr aufgezeigt wird, das zufällige Seyn gehe an sich selbst in seinen Grund zurück, worin es sich aufhebt,—ferner daß es durch dieß Zurückgehen den Grund nur so setze, daß es sich selbst vielmehr zum Gesetzten macht.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"121.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0018","text":"Im gewöhnlichen Schließen erscheint das Seyn des Endlichen als Grund des Absoluten; darum weil Endliches ist, ist das Absolute. Die Wahrheit aber ist, daß darum weil das Endliche der an sich selbst widersprechende Gegensatz, weil es nicht ist, das Absolute ist. In jenem Sinne lautet der Satz des Schlusses so: Das Seyn des Endlichen ist das Seyn des Absoluten; in diesem Sinne aber so: Das Nichtseyn des Endlichen ist das Seyn des Absoluten.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"121.18"}],"sha256":"c796148dceba768c943ca8ddda4f25dd3f21bba62ad6dd0b514aa8ec8fb9df30","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T104947998808Z_b0915ccb","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark 3.","source_sha256":"c796148dceba768c943ca8ddda4f25dd3f21bba62ad6dd0b514aa8ec8fb9df30","sha256":"a4629baea56dab237383f8cfa7edc63912c915bc59967cbfd6fe1891648b9751","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:49:47.998827+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0001","text":"If, then, the first determinations of reflection, identity, difference, and opposition, have been set forth in a proposition, then all the more should that into which they pass as into their truth, namely contradiction, be comprehended in a proposition and it should be said: All things are in themselves contradictory, and indeed in the sense that this proposition, as against the others, rather expresses the truth and the essence of things.—The contradiction that emerges in opposition is only the developed nothing that is contained in identity, and that occurred in the expression that the proposition of identity says nothing. This negation determines itself further into difference and into opposition, which is now the posited contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"121.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0002","text":"But it is one of the fundamental prejudices of hitherto existing logic and of ordinary representation, as though contradiction were not as essential and immanent a determination as identity; indeed, if there were talk of rank and if both determinations had to be maintained as separate, then contradiction would have to be taken as the deeper and more essential. For identity, in contrast to it, is only the determination of simple immediacy, of dead Being; but contradiction is the root of all movement and vitality; only insofar as something has a contradiction within itself does it move, have impulse and activity.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"121.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0003","text":"Contradiction is ordinarily, first of all, removed from things, from what is and from truth in general; it is maintained that there is nothing contradictory. Secondly, it is instead shifted into subjective reflection, which first posits it through its relating and comparing. But even in this reflection it is said not actually to be present, for what is contradictory can be neither represented nor thought. In general, whether in actuality or in thinking reflection, it counts as an accidental matter, as it were as an abnormality and a passing paroxysm of illness.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"121.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0004","text":"As regards, then, the assertion that contradiction does not exist, that it is not something present, we need not concern ourselves with such an assurance; an absolute determination of essence must be found in all experience, in everything actual as in every concept. The same has already been recalled above concerning the infinite, which is contradiction as it shows itself in the sphere of Being. But common experience itself declares that there are at least a multitude of contradictory things, contradictory institutions, etc., whose contradiction is present not merely in an external reflection, but in themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"121.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0005","text":"Further, it is not to be taken merely as an abnormality occurring only here and there, but is the negative in its essential determination, the principle of all self-movement, which consists in nothing other than a presentation of it. External sensible movement itself is its immediate existence. Something moves only, not by being here in this Now and there in another Now, but by being here and not here in one and the same Now, by at once being and not being in this Here. One must grant the ancient dialecticians the contradictions that they point out in movement; but it does not follow from this that movement is therefore not, but rather that movement is existent contradiction itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"121.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0006","text":"Likewise, inner, proper self-movement, impulse in general, (appetite or the nisus of the monad, the entelechy of the absolutely simple essence) is nothing other than that something is within itself, and that the lack, the negative of itself, is in one and the same respect. Abstract identity with itself is not yet vitality; rather, because the positive is negativity in itself, it thereby goes outside itself and posits itself in alteration. Something is therefore alive only insofar as it contains contradiction within itself, and indeed is this force of grasping and enduring contradiction within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"121.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0007","text":"But if an existing thing is unable, in its positive determination, at the same time to reach over into its negative and to hold the one fast in the other, unable to have contradiction within itself, then it is not the living unity itself, not ground, but perishes in contradiction.—Speculative thinking consists only in this, that thinking holds fast contradiction and itself within it, but does not, as happens to representation, allow itself to be dominated by it and allow its determinations through it to be resolved merely into others or into nothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"121.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0008","text":"If, in movement, impulse, and the like, contradiction is concealed for representation in the simplicity of these determinations, it presents itself immediately, on the other hand, in determinations of relation. The most trivial examples, of Above and Below, Right and Left, Father and Son, and so on to infinity, all contain opposition in one. Above is what is not Below; Above is determined only as this, not to be Below, and is only insofar as there is a Below; and conversely; in the one determination lies its opposite. Father is the other of Son, and Son the other of Father, and each is only as this other of the other; and at the same time the one determination is only in relation to the other; its Being is one subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"121.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0009","text":"Apart from the relation to Son, the Father is also something for himself; but then he is not Father, but a man in general; just as Above and Below, Right and Left, too, as reflected into themselves, are something apart from the relation; but only places in general.—The opposites contain contradiction insofar as, in the same respect, they are negatively related to one another, or mutually sublating, and indifferent to one another. Representation, in passing over to the moment of the indifference of the determinations, forgets therein their negative unity and thus retains them only as different in general, in which determination Right is no longer Right, Left no longer Left, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"121.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0010","text":"But insofar as it in fact has Right and Left before it, it has these determinations before it as negating themselves, the one in the other, and at the same time, in this unity, as not negating themselves, but each being indifferent for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"121.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0011","text":"Representation therefore indeed has contradiction everywhere as its content, but does not arrive at consciousness of it; it remains external reflection, which passes from equality to inequality, or from negative relation to the reflectedness-into-itself of the differentiated. It holds these two determinations externally opposed to one another and has only them in view, but not the transition, which is the essential thing and contains contradiction. —Ingenious reflection, to mention it here, on the other hand consists in apprehending and expressing contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"121.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0012","text":"Although it does not express the concept of things and their relations and has only determinations of representation as its material and content, it brings them into a relation that contains their contradiction and lets their concept shine through it.—Thinking reason, however, so to speak sharpens the blunted difference of the different, the mere manifoldness of representation, into the essential difference, into opposition. Only when driven to the point of contradiction do the manifold become active and alive against one another, and receive in it the negativity that is the indwelling pulsation of self-movement and vitality.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"121.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0013","text":"It has already been recalled concerning the ontological proof of the existence of God that the determination underlying it is the sum-total of all realities. Of this determination it is customarily first shown that it is possible because it contains no contradiction, inasmuch as reality is taken only as reality without limitation. It was recalled that thereby that sum-total becomes simple indeterminate Being, or, if the realities are in fact taken as several determinate ones, the sum-total of all negations. Taking the difference of reality more closely, it passes from difference into opposition and thereby into contradiction, and the sum-total of all realities in general becomes absolute contradiction within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"121.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0014","text":"The ordinary horror that representational, non-speculative thinking has before contradiction, like nature before the vacuum, rejects this consequence; for it remains fixed at the one-sided consideration of the dissolution of contradiction into nothing, and does not recognize its positive side, according to which it becomes absolute activity and absolute ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"121.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0015","text":"It has in general emerged from the consideration of the nature of contradiction that it is, so to speak, not yet in itself a detriment, defect, or fault of a thing if a contradiction can be demonstrated in it. Rather, every determination, every concrete, every concept is essentially a unity of differentiated and differentiable moments, which, through determinate, essential difference, pass into contradictory ones. This contradictory element certainly resolves itself into nothing; it returns into its negative unity. The thing, the subject, the concept is now precisely this negative unity itself; it is something contradictory in itself, but equally the resolved contradiction; it is the ground that contains and bears its determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"121.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0016","text":"The thing, the subject, or the concept is, as reflected into itself in its sphere, its resolved contradiction; but its entire sphere is again also a determinate, differentiated one; thus it is finite, and this means contradictory. This higher contradiction does not have that sphere itself as its resolution; rather, it has a higher sphere as its negative unity, as its ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"121.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0017","text":"Finite things in their indifferent manifoldness are therefore in general this: to be contradictory within themselves, broken within themselves, and to return into their ground.—As will be considered further on, the true inference from a finite and contingent being to an absolutely necessary being does not consist in inferring from the finite and contingent as the Being that lies at the ground and remains lying there, but in inferring, as indeed lies immediately in contingency, from a Being that merely falls, that contradicts itself in itself, to an absolutely necessary being; or rather, in showing that contingent Being returns in itself into its ground, in which it sublates itself,—and further, that through this return it posits the ground only in such a way that it rather makes itself into something posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"121.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_33:P0018","text":"In ordinary inference, the Being of the finite appears as the ground of the Absolute; because the finite is, the Absolute is. But the truth is that because the finite is the opposition contradictory in itself, because it is not, the Absolute is. In the former sense, the proposition of the inference reads thus: The Being of the finite is the Being of the Absolute; but in the latter sense thus: The non-being of the finite is the Being of the Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"121.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_33:P0018"]}],"source_digest":"dffa146369af8850ee55004045c83008c6bf4fee699566eaa470fbf01617fb9d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung 3."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung 3.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34","title":"Remark.","order":122,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_34","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Der Grund.\n\nDas Wesen bestimmt sich selbst als Grund.\n\nWie das Nichts zuerst mit dem Seyn in einfacher unmittelbarer Einheit, so ist auch hier zuerst die einfache Identität des Wesens mit seiner absoluten Negativität in unmittelbarer Einheit. Das Wesen ist nur diese seine Negativität, welche die reine Reflexion ist. Es ist diese reine Negativität als die Rückkehr des Seyns in sich; so ist es an sich oder für uns bestimmt, als der Grund, in dem sich das Seyn auflöst. Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist nicht durch es selbst gesetzt; oder es ist nicht Grund, eben insofern es diese seine Bestimmtheit nicht selbst gesetzt hat. Seine Reflexion aber besteht darin, sich als das, was es an sich ist, als Negatives zu setzen und sich zu bestimmen. Das Positive und Negative machen die wesenhafte Bestimmung aus, in die es als in seine Negation verloren ist. Diese selbstständigen Reflexions-Bestimmungen heben sich auf, und die zu Grunde gegangene Bestimmung ist die wahrhafte Bestimmung des Wesens.\n\nDer Grund ist daher selbst eine der Reflexions-Bestimmungen des Wesens, aber die letzte, vielmehr nur die Bestimmung, daß sie aufgehobene Bestimmung ist. Die Reflexionsbestimmung, indem sie zu Grunde geht, erhält ihre wahrhafte Bedeutung, der absolute Gegenstoß ihrer in sich selbst zu seyn, nämlich daß das Gesetztseyn, das dem Wesen zukommt, nur als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn ist, und umgekehrt, daß nur das sich aufhebende Gesetztseyn das Gesetztseyn des Wesens ist. Das Wesen, indem es sich als Grund bestimmt, bestimmt sich als das Nichtbestimmte, und nur das Aufheben seines Bestimmtseyns ist sein Bestimmen.—In diesem Bestimmtseyn als dem sich selbst aufhebenden, ist es nicht aus anderem herkommendes, sondern in seiner Negativität mit sich identisches Wesen.\n\nInsofern von der Bestimmung aus, als dem Ersten, Unmittelbaren zum Grunde fortgegangen wird, (durch die Natur der Bestimmung selbst, die durch sich zu Grunde geht,) so ist der Grund zunächst ein durch jenes Erste Bestimmtes. Allein dieß Bestimmen ist eines Theils als Aufheben des Bestimmens die nur wiederhergestellte, gereinigte oder geoffenbarte Identität des Wesens, welche die Reflexions-Bestimmung an sich ist;—andern Theils ist diese negirende Bewegung als Bestimmen erst das Setzen jener Reflexionsbestimmtheit, welche als die unmittelbare erschien, die aber nur von der sich selbst ausschließenden Reflexion des Grundes gesetzt und hierin als nur Gesetztes oder Aufgehobenes gesetzt ist.—So kommt das Wesen, indem es sich als Grund bestimmt, nur aus sich her. Als Grund also setzt es sich als Wesen, und daß es sich als Wesen setzt, darin besteht sein Bestimmen. Dieß Setzen ist die Reflexion des Wesens, die in ihrem Bestimmen sich selbst aufhebt, nach jener Seite Setzen, nach dieser das Setzen des Wesens, somit beides in einem Thun ist.\n\nDie Reflexion ist die reine Vermittelung überhaupt, der Grund ist die reale Vermittelung des Wesens mit sich. Jene, die Bewegung des Nichts durch Nichts zu sich selbst zurück, ist das Scheinen seiner in einem Andern; aber weil der Gegensatz in dieser Reflexion noch keine Selbstständigkeit hat, so ist weder jenes erste, das Scheinende ein Positives, noch das andere, in dem es scheint, ein Negatives. Beide sind Substrate, eigentlich nur der Einbildungskraft; sie sind noch nicht sich auf sich selbst beziehende. Die reine Vermittelung ist nur reine Beziehung, ohne Bezogene. Die bestimmende Reflexion setzt zwar solche, die identisch mit sich, aber zugleich nur bestimmte Beziehungen sind. Der Grund dagegen ist die reale Vermittelung, weil er die Reflexion als aufgehobene Reflexion enthält; er ist das durch sein Nichtseyn in sich zurückkehrende und sich setzende Wesen. Nach diesem Momente der aufgehobenen Reflexion erhält das Gesetzte die Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit, eines solchen, das außer der Beziehung oder seinem Scheine identisch mit sich ist. Dieß Unmittelbare ist das durch das Wesen wiederhergestellte Seyn; das Nichtseyn der Reflexion, durch das das Wesen sich vermittelt. In sich kehrt das Wesen zurück als negirendes; es giebt sich also in seiner Rückkehr in sich, die Bestimmtheit, die eben darum das mit sich identische Negative, das aufgehobene Gesetztseyn, und somit ebenso sehr seyendes, als die Identität des Wesens mit sich als Grund ist.\n\nDer Grund ist zuerst absoluter Grund, in dem das Wesen zunächst als Grundlage überhaupt für die Grundbeziehung ist; näher bestimmt er sich aber als Form und Materie, und giebt sich einen Inhalt.\n\nZweitens ist er bestimmter Grund, als Grund von einem bestimmten Inhalt; indem die Grundbeziehung sich in ihrer Realisirung überhaupt äußerlich wird, geht sie in die bedingende Vermittelung über.\n\nDrittens, der Grund setzt eine Bedingung voraus; aber die Bedingung setzt ebenso sehr den Grund voraus; das Unbedingte ist ihre Einheit, die Sache an sich, die durch die Vermittelung der bedingenden Beziehung in die Existenz übergeht.\n\n## Anmerkung.\n\nDer Grund ist, wie die andern Reflexions-Bestimmungen, in einem Satze ausgedrückt worden: Alles hat seinen zureichenden Grund.—Dieß heißt im Allgemeinen nichts anderes, als was ist, ist nicht als seyendes Unmittelbares, sondern als Gesetztes zu betrachten; es ist nicht bei dem unmittelbaren Daseyn oder bei der Bestimmtheit überhaupt stehen zu bleiben, sondern davon zurückzugehen in seinen Grund, in welcher Reflexion es als Aufgehobenes und in seinem An- und Fürsichseyn ist. In dem Satze des Grundes wird also die Wesentlichkeit der Reflexion in sich gegen das bloße Seyn ausgesprochen.—Daß der Grund zureichend sey, ist eigentlich sehr überflüssig hinzuzusetzen, denn es versteht sich von selbst; das, für was der Grund nicht zureicht, hätte keinen Grund, aber alles soll einen Grund haben. Allein Leibnitz, dem das Princip des zureichenden Grundes vornemlich am Herzen lag, und der es sogar zum Grundsatz seiner ganzen Philosophie machte, verband damit einen tiefern Sinn und wichtigern Begriffe als gewöhnlich damit verbunden wird, indem man nur bei dem unmittelbaren Ausdruck stehen bleibt; obgleich der Satz auch nur in diesem Sinne schon für wichtig anzusehen ist, daß nämlich das Seyn als solches in seiner Unmittelbarkeit für das Unwahre und wesentlich für ein Gesetztes, der Grund aber für das wahrhafte Unmittelbare erklärt wird. Leibnitz aber stellte das Zureichende des Grundes vornemlich der Kausalität in ihrem strengen Sinne, als der mechanischen Wirkungsweise, entgegen. Indem diese eine äußerliche ihrem Inhalte nach auf Eine Bestimmtheit beschränkte Thätigkeit überhaupt ist, so treten die durch sie gesetzten Bestimmungen äußerlich und zufällig in eine Verbindung; die Theilbestimmungen werden durch ihre Ursachen begriffen; aber die Beziehung derselben, welche das Wesentliche einer Existenz ausmacht, ist nicht in den Ursachen des Mechanismus enthalten. Diese Beziehung, das Ganze als wesentliche Einheit, liegt nur im Begriffe, im Zwecke. Für diese Einheit sind die mechanischen Ursachen nicht zureichend, weil ihnen nicht der Zweck, als die Einheit der Bestimmungen, zu Grunde liegt. Unter dem zureichenden Grunde hat Leibnitz daher einen solchen verstanden, der auch für diese Einheit zureichte, daher nicht die bloßen Ursachen, sondern die Endursachen in sich begriffe. Diese Bestimmung des Grundes gehört aber noch nicht hierher; der teleologische Grund ist ein Eigenthum des Begriffs und der Vermittelung durch denselben, welche die Vernunft ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0001","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Der Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"122.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0002","text":"Das Wesen bestimmt sich selbst als Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"122.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0003","text":"Wie das Nichts zuerst mit dem Seyn in einfacher unmittelbarer Einheit, so ist auch hier zuerst die einfache Identität des Wesens mit seiner absoluten Negativität in unmittelbarer Einheit. Das Wesen ist nur diese seine Negativität, welche die reine Reflexion ist. Es ist diese reine Negativität als die Rückkehr des Seyns in sich; so ist es an sich oder für uns bestimmt, als der Grund, in dem sich das Seyn auflöst. Aber diese Bestimmtheit ist nicht durch es selbst gesetzt; oder es ist nicht Grund, eben insofern es diese seine Bestimmtheit nicht selbst gesetzt hat. Seine Reflexion aber besteht darin, sich als das, was es an sich ist, als Negatives zu setzen und sich zu bestimmen. Das Positive und Negative machen die wesenhafte Bestimmung aus, in die es als in seine Negation verloren ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"122.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0004","text":"Diese selbstständigen Reflexions-Bestimmungen heben sich auf, und die zu Grunde gegangene Bestimmung ist die wahrhafte Bestimmung des Wesens.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"122.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0005","text":"Der Grund ist daher selbst eine der Reflexions-Bestimmungen des Wesens, aber die letzte, vielmehr nur die Bestimmung, daß sie aufgehobene Bestimmung ist. Die Reflexionsbestimmung, indem sie zu Grunde geht, erhält ihre wahrhafte Bedeutung, der absolute Gegenstoß ihrer in sich selbst zu seyn, nämlich daß das Gesetztseyn, das dem Wesen zukommt, nur als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn ist, und umgekehrt, daß nur das sich aufhebende Gesetztseyn das Gesetztseyn des Wesens ist. Das Wesen, indem es sich als Grund bestimmt, bestimmt sich als das Nichtbestimmte, und nur das Aufheben seines Bestimmtseyns ist sein Bestimmen.—In diesem Bestimmtseyn als dem sich selbst aufhebenden, ist es nicht aus anderem herkommendes, sondern in seiner Negativität mit sich identisches Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"122.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0006","text":"Insofern von der Bestimmung aus, als dem Ersten, Unmittelbaren zum Grunde fortgegangen wird, (durch die Natur der Bestimmung selbst, die durch sich zu Grunde geht,) so ist der Grund zunächst ein durch jenes Erste Bestimmtes. Allein dieß Bestimmen ist eines Theils als Aufheben des Bestimmens die nur wiederhergestellte, gereinigte oder geoffenbarte Identität des Wesens, welche die Reflexions-Bestimmung an sich ist;—andern Theils ist diese negirende Bewegung als Bestimmen erst das Setzen jener Reflexionsbestimmtheit, welche als die unmittelbare erschien, die aber nur von der sich selbst ausschließenden Reflexion des Grundes gesetzt und hierin als nur Gesetztes oder Aufgehobenes gesetzt ist.—So kommt das Wesen, indem es sich als Grund bestimmt, nur aus sich her. Als Grund also setzt es sich als Wesen, und daß es sich als Wesen setzt, darin besteht sein Bestimmen.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"122.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0007","text":"Dieß Setzen ist die Reflexion des Wesens, die in ihrem Bestimmen sich selbst aufhebt, nach jener Seite Setzen, nach dieser das Setzen des Wesens, somit beides in einem Thun ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"122.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0008","text":"Die Reflexion ist die reine Vermittelung überhaupt, der Grund ist die reale Vermittelung des Wesens mit sich. Jene, die Bewegung des Nichts durch Nichts zu sich selbst zurück, ist das Scheinen seiner in einem Andern; aber weil der Gegensatz in dieser Reflexion noch keine Selbstständigkeit hat, so ist weder jenes erste, das Scheinende ein Positives, noch das andere, in dem es scheint, ein Negatives. Beide sind Substrate, eigentlich nur der Einbildungskraft; sie sind noch nicht sich auf sich selbst beziehende. Die reine Vermittelung ist nur reine Beziehung, ohne Bezogene. Die bestimmende Reflexion setzt zwar solche, die identisch mit sich, aber zugleich nur bestimmte Beziehungen sind. Der Grund dagegen ist die reale Vermittelung, weil er die Reflexion als aufgehobene Reflexion enthält; er ist das durch sein Nichtseyn in sich zurückkehrende und sich setzende Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"122.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0009","text":"Nach diesem Momente der aufgehobenen Reflexion erhält das Gesetzte die Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit, eines solchen, das außer der Beziehung oder seinem Scheine identisch mit sich ist. Dieß Unmittelbare ist das durch das Wesen wiederhergestellte Seyn; das Nichtseyn der Reflexion, durch das das Wesen sich vermittelt. In sich kehrt das Wesen zurück als negirendes; es giebt sich also in seiner Rückkehr in sich, die Bestimmtheit, die eben darum das mit sich identische Negative, das aufgehobene Gesetztseyn, und somit ebenso sehr seyendes, als die Identität des Wesens mit sich als Grund ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"122.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0010","text":"Der Grund ist zuerst absoluter Grund, in dem das Wesen zunächst als Grundlage überhaupt für die Grundbeziehung ist; näher bestimmt er sich aber als Form und Materie, und giebt sich einen Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"122.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0011","text":"Zweitens ist er bestimmter Grund, als Grund von einem bestimmten Inhalt; indem die Grundbeziehung sich in ihrer Realisirung überhaupt äußerlich wird, geht sie in die bedingende Vermittelung über.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"122.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0012","text":"Drittens, der Grund setzt eine Bedingung voraus; aber die Bedingung setzt ebenso sehr den Grund voraus; das Unbedingte ist ihre Einheit, die Sache an sich, die durch die Vermittelung der bedingenden Beziehung in die Existenz übergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"122.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0013","text":"## Anmerkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"122.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0014","text":"Der Grund ist, wie die andern Reflexions-Bestimmungen, in einem Satze ausgedrückt worden: Alles hat seinen zureichenden Grund.—Dieß heißt im Allgemeinen nichts anderes, als was ist, ist nicht als seyendes Unmittelbares, sondern als Gesetztes zu betrachten; es ist nicht bei dem unmittelbaren Daseyn oder bei der Bestimmtheit überhaupt stehen zu bleiben, sondern davon zurückzugehen in seinen Grund, in welcher Reflexion es als Aufgehobenes und in seinem An- und Fürsichseyn ist. In dem Satze des Grundes wird also die Wesentlichkeit der Reflexion in sich gegen das bloße Seyn ausgesprochen.—Daß der Grund zureichend sey, ist eigentlich sehr überflüssig hinzuzusetzen, denn es versteht sich von selbst; das, für was der Grund nicht zureicht, hätte keinen Grund, aber alles soll einen Grund haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"122.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0015","text":"Allein Leibnitz, dem das Princip des zureichenden Grundes vornemlich am Herzen lag, und der es sogar zum Grundsatz seiner ganzen Philosophie machte, verband damit einen tiefern Sinn und wichtigern Begriffe als gewöhnlich damit verbunden wird, indem man nur bei dem unmittelbaren Ausdruck stehen bleibt; obgleich der Satz auch nur in diesem Sinne schon für wichtig anzusehen ist, daß nämlich das Seyn als solches in seiner Unmittelbarkeit für das Unwahre und wesentlich für ein Gesetztes, der Grund aber für das wahrhafte Unmittelbare erklärt wird. Leibnitz aber stellte das Zureichende des Grundes vornemlich der Kausalität in ihrem strengen Sinne, als der mechanischen Wirkungsweise, entgegen.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"122.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0016","text":"Indem diese eine äußerliche ihrem Inhalte nach auf Eine Bestimmtheit beschränkte Thätigkeit überhaupt ist, so treten die durch sie gesetzten Bestimmungen äußerlich und zufällig in eine Verbindung; die Theilbestimmungen werden durch ihre Ursachen begriffen; aber die Beziehung derselben, welche das Wesentliche einer Existenz ausmacht, ist nicht in den Ursachen des Mechanismus enthalten. Diese Beziehung, das Ganze als wesentliche Einheit, liegt nur im Begriffe, im Zwecke. Für diese Einheit sind die mechanischen Ursachen nicht zureichend, weil ihnen nicht der Zweck, als die Einheit der Bestimmungen, zu Grunde liegt. Unter dem zureichenden Grunde hat Leibnitz daher einen solchen verstanden, der auch für diese Einheit zureichte, daher nicht die bloßen Ursachen, sondern die Endursachen in sich begriffe.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"122.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0017","text":"Diese Bestimmung des Grundes gehört aber noch nicht hierher; der teleologische Grund ist ein Eigenthum des Begriffs und der Vermittelung durch denselben, welche die Vernunft ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"122.17"}],"sha256":"d28195ccffd608f3ce69357357451fc096b915ac657a80d7fa01edb067abbefc","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105004152378Z_10f2e7f7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"d28195ccffd608f3ce69357357451fc096b915ac657a80d7fa01edb067abbefc","sha256":"3cbb3c338244016c0284e793cea88817716820d49bf35ba0b06808494be45575","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:50:04.152394+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0001","text":"## Third Chapter. The Ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"122.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0002","text":"Essence determines itself as ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"122.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0003","text":"Just as Nothing is at first in simple immediate unity with Being, so here too the simple identity of essence with its absolute negativity is at first in immediate unity. Essence is only this its negativity, which is pure reflection. It is this pure negativity as the return of Being into itself; thus it is determined in itself or for us, as ground, in which Being resolves itself. But this determinacy is not posited by essence itself; or it is not ground, precisely in so far as it has not itself posited this its determinacy. Its reflection, however, consists in positing itself as what it is in itself, as negative, and in determining itself. The positive and the negative constitute the essential determinacy, into which it is lost as into its negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"122.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0004","text":"These self-subsistent determinations of reflection sublate themselves, and the determination that has gone to ground is the true determination of essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"122.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0005","text":"Ground is therefore itself one of the determinations of reflection of essence, but the last one; or rather, merely the determination that it is sublated determination. The determination of reflection, in going to ground, receives its true significance: to be the absolute recoil of itself into itself, namely, that positedness, which belongs to essence, is only as sublated positedness, and conversely, that only self-sublating positedness is the positedness of essence. Essence, in determining itself as ground, determines itself as the undetermined, and only the sublation of its being-determined is its determining.—In this determinacy, as self-sublating, it is not essence coming from another, but essence identical with itself in its negativity.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"122.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0006","text":"In so far as the advance is made from determination, as the first, immediate [term], to ground (through the nature of determination itself, which goes to ground through itself), ground is at first something determined by that first [term]. Yet this determining is, on the one hand, as sublation of determining, merely the restored, purified, or manifested identity of essence, which is the determination of reflection in itself;—on the other hand, this negating movement, as determining, is only the positing of that determinacy of reflection which appeared as immediate, but which is posited only by the self-excluding reflection of ground, and is therein posited as merely posited, or sublated.—Thus essence, in determining itself as ground, comes only from itself. As ground, therefore, it posits itself as essence, and its determining consists in its positing itself as essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"122.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0007","text":"This positing is the reflection of essence, which in its determining sublates itself: according to that side, positing; according to this, the positing of essence; thus both are in one act.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"122.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0008","text":"Reflection is pure mediation in general; ground is the real mediation of essence with itself. The former, the movement of Nothing through Nothing back to itself, is its shining in an other; but because opposition in this reflection does not yet have self-subsistence, neither is that first, the shining, a positive, nor the other, in which it shines, a negative. Both are substrates, properly speaking only of imagination; they are not yet self-related. Pure mediation is only pure relation, without related terms. Determining reflection does indeed posit such [terms], which are identical with themselves, but at the same time are only determinate relations. Ground, on the other hand, is real mediation, because it contains reflection as sublated reflection; it is essence returning into itself and positing itself through its non-being.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"122.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0009","text":"According to this moment of sublated reflection, the posited acquires the determination of immediacy, of something that, outside relation or its shining, is identical with itself. This immediate is Being restored by essence; the non-being of reflection, through which essence mediates itself. Essence returns into itself as negating; thus, in its return into itself, it gives itself the determinacy which, precisely for that reason, is the negative identical with itself, sublated positedness, and hence equally being, as the identity of essence with itself as ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"122.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0010","text":"Ground is at first absolute ground, in which essence is initially the basis in general for the relation of ground; more closely, however, it determines itself as form and matter, and gives itself a content.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"122.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0011","text":"Secondly, it is determinate ground, as the ground of a determinate content; in that the relation of ground, in its realization in general, becomes external to itself, it passes over into conditioning mediation.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"122.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0012","text":"Thirdly, ground presupposes a condition; but the condition equally presupposes ground; the unconditioned is their unity, the thing in itself, which passes over into existence through the mediation of the conditioning relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"122.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0013","text":"## Remark.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"122.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0014","text":"Ground, like the other determinations of reflection, has been expressed in a proposition: Everything has its sufficient ground.—This means in general nothing other than that what is, is not to be considered as an immediate being, but as posited; one must not remain with immediate determinate being or with determinacy in general, but must go back from it into its ground, in which reflection it is as sublated and in its being-in-and-for-itself. Thus, in the proposition of ground, the essentiality of reflection into itself is expressed over against mere Being.—That ground be sufficient is really quite superfluous to add, for it is self-evident; that for which ground did not suffice would have no ground, but everything is supposed to have a ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"122.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0015","text":"Yet Leibniz, to whom the principle of sufficient ground lay especially at heart, and who even made it the fundamental principle of his whole philosophy, connected with it a deeper sense and more important concept than is usually connected with it when one merely remains with the immediate expression; although the proposition, even in this sense alone, is already to be regarded as important, namely, that Being as such in its immediacy is declared to be the untrue and essentially a posited [being], but ground the true immediate. Leibniz, however, set the sufficiency of ground chiefly against causality in its strict sense, as the mechanical mode of operation.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"122.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0016","text":"Since this is in general an external activity restricted, according to its content, to one determinacy, the determinations posited by it enter externally and contingently into a combination; the partial determinations are comprehended through their causes; but their relation, which constitutes the essentiality of an existence, is not contained in the causes of mechanism. This relation, the whole as essential unity, lies only in the concept, in purpose. Mechanical causes are not sufficient for this unity, because purpose, as the unity of determinations, does not underlie them. By sufficient ground Leibniz therefore understood one which also sufficed for this unity, and thus comprehended within itself not mere causes, but final causes.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"122.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_34:P0017","text":"But this determination of ground does not yet belong here; teleological ground is a property of the concept and of mediation through it, which is reason.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"122.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_34:P0017"]}],"source_digest":"eb27a9a06d2ec563e5bb7059c910b61e92f77ac64ef924c2803c1fa2ff2110d9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0","title":"a. Form and Essence.","order":123,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_FUW0","text":"## A. Der absolute Grund.\n\n## a. Form und Wesen.\n\nDie Reflexions-Bestimmung, insofern sie in den Grund zurückgeht, ist ein erstes, ein unmittelbares Daseyn überhaupt, von dem angefangen wird. Aber das Daseyn hat nur noch die Bedeutung des Gesetztseyns und setzt wesentlich einen Grund voraus; in dem Sinne, daß es ihn vielmehr nicht setzt; daß dieß Setzen ein Aufheben seiner selbst, das Unmittelbare vielmehr das Gesetzte und der Grund das Nichtgesetzte ist. Wie es sich ergeben hat, ist dieß Voraussetzen, das auf das Setzende rückschlagende Setzen; der Grund ist als das aufgehobene Bestimmtseyn nicht das Unbestimmte, sondern das durch sich selbst bestimmte Wesen, aber als unbestimmt oder als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn Bestimmtes. Er ist das Wesen, das in seiner Negativität mit sich identisch ist.\n\nDie Bestimmtheit des Wesens als Grund wird hiermit die gedoppelte, des Grundes und des Begründeten. Sie ist erstens das Wesen als Grund, bestimmt das Wesen zu seyn gegen das Gesetztseyn, als Nichtgesetztseyn. Zweitens ist sie das Begründete, das Unmittelbare, das aber nicht an und für sich ist, das Gesetztseyn als Gesetztseyn. Dieses ist somit gleichfalls mit sich identisch, aber die Identität des Negativen mit sich. Das mit sich identische Negative und das mit sich identische Positive ist nun eine und dieselbe Identität. Denn der Grund ist Identität des Positiven oder selbst auch des Gesetztseyns mit sich; das Begründete ist das Gesetztseyn als Gesetztseyn, diese seine Reflexion in sich aber ist die Identität des Grundes.—Diese einfache Identität ist also nicht selbst der Grund, denn der Grund ist das Wesen gesetzt, als das Nichtgesetzte gegen das Gesetztseyn. Sie ist, als die Einheit dieser bestimmten Identität, (des Grundes) und der negativen Identität (des Begründeten) das Wesen überhaupt, unterschieden von seiner Vermittelung.\n\nDiese Vermittelung, mit den vorhergehenden Reflexionen verglichen, aus denen sie herkommt, ist erstlich nicht die reine Reflexion, als welche nicht vom Wesen unterschieden ist, und das Negative, damit auch die Selbstständigkeit der Bestimmungen, noch nicht an ihr hat. Im Grunde als der aufgehobenen Reflexion aber haben diese Bestimmungen ein Bestehen.—Auch ist sie nicht die bestimmende Reflexion, deren Bestimmungen wesentliche Selbstständigkeit haben; denn diese ist im Grunde zu Grunde gegangen, in dessen Einheit sind sie nur gesetzte.—Diese Vermittelung des Grundes ist daher die Einheit der reinen und der bestimmenden Reflexion; ihre Bestimmungen oder das Gesetzte hat Bestehen, und umgekehrt das Bestehen derselben ist ein Gesetztes. Weil dieß ihr Bestehen selbst ein Gesetztes ist oder Bestimmtheit hat, so sind sie somit von ihrer einfachen Identität unterschieden, und machen die Form aus gegen das Wesen.\n\nDas Wesen hat eine Form, und Bestimmungen derselben. Erst als Grund hat es eine feste Unmittelbarkeit oder ist Substrat. Das Wesen als solches ist eins mit seiner Reflexion, und ununterschieden ihre Bewegung selbst. Es ist daher nicht das Wesen, welches sie durchläuft; auch ist es nicht dasjenige, von dem sie als von einem Ersten anfängt. Dieser Umstand erschwert die Darstellung der Reflexion überhaupt; denn man kann eigentlich nicht sagen, das Wesen geht in sich selbst zurück, das Wesen scheint in sich, weil es nicht vor oder in seiner Bewegung ist, und diese keine Grundlage hat, an der sie sich verläuft. Ein Bezogenes tritt erst im Grund nach dem Momente der aufgehobenen Reflexion hervor. Das Wesen als das bezogene Substrat aber ist das bestimmte Wesen; um dieses Gesetztseyns willen hat es wesentlich die Form an ihm.—Die Formbestimmungen dagegen sind nun die Bestimmungen als an dem Wesen; es liegt ihnen zu Grunde, als das Unbestimmte, das in seiner Bestimmung gleichgültig gegen sie ist; sie haben an ihm ihre Reflexion in sich. Die Reflexions-Bestimmungen sollten ihr Bestehen an ihnen selbst haben und selbstständig seyn; aber ihre Selbstständigkeit ist ihre Auflösung; so haben sie dieselbe an einem Andern; aber diese Auflösung ist selbst diese Identität mit sich oder der Grund des Bestehens, den sie sich geben.\n\nDer Form gehört überhaupt alles Bestimmte an; es ist Formbestimmung, insofern es ein Gesetztes, hiermit von einem solchen, dessen Form es ist, Unterschiedenes ist; die Bestimmtheit als Qualität ist eins mit ihrem Substrat, dem Seyn; das Seyn ist das unmittelbar Bestimmte, das von seiner Bestimmtheit noch nicht unterschieden,—oder das in ihr noch nicht in sich reflektirt, so wie diese daher eine seyende, noch nicht eine Gesetzte ist.—Die Formbestimmungen des Wesens sind ferner als die Reflexions-Bestimmtheiten, ihrer nähern Bestimmtheit nach, die oben betrachteten Momente der Reflexion. Die Identität, und der Unterschied, dieser Theils als Verschiedenheit, Theils als Gegensatz. Ferner aber gehört auch die Grundbeziehung dazu, insofern sie zwar die aufgehobene Reflexions-Bestimmung aber dadurch das Wesen zugleich als Gesetztes ist. Dagegen gehört zur Form nicht die Identität, welche der Grund in sich hat, nämlich daß das Gesetztseyn als aufgehobenes und das Gesetztseyn als solches,—der Grund und das Begründete,—Eine Reflexion ist, welche das Wesen als einfache Grundlage ausmacht, die das Bestehen der Form ist. Allein dieß Bestehen ist im Grunde gesetzt; oder dieß Wesen ist selbst wesentlich als bestimmtes; somit ist es auch wieder das Moment der Grundbeziehung und Form.—Dieß ist die absolute Wechselbeziehung der Form und des Wesens, daß dieses einfache Einheit des Grundes und des Begründeten, darin aber eben selbst bestimmt oder Negatives ist, und sich als Grundlage von der Form unterscheidet, aber so zugleich selbst Grund und Moment der Form wird.\n\nDie Form ist daher das vollendete Ganze der Reflexion; sie enthält auch diese Bestimmung derselben, aufgehobene zu seyn; daher ist sie ebenso sehr als sie eine Einheit ihres Bestimmens ist, auch bezogen auf ihr Aufgehobenseyn, auf ein Anderes, das nicht selbst Form, sondern an dem sie sey. Als die wesentliche sich auf sich selbst beziehende Negativität, gegen dieß einfache Negative ist sie das Setzende und Bestimmende; das einfache Wesen hingegen ist die unbestimmte und unthätige Grundlage, an welcher die Formbestimmungen das Bestehen oder die Reflexion in sich haben.—Bei dieser Unterscheidung des Wesens und der Form pflegt die äußere Reflexion stehen zu bleiben; sie ist nothwendig, aber dieses Unterscheiden selbst ist ihre Einheit, so wie diese Grundeinheit das sich von sich abstoßende und zum Gesetztseyn machende Wesen ist. Die Form ist die absolute Negativität selbst, oder die negative absolute Identität mit sich, wodurch eben das Wesen nicht Seyn, sondern Wesen ist. Diese Identität abstrakt genommen, ist das Wesen gegen die Form; so wie die Negativität abstrakt genommen als das Gesetztseyn, die einzelne Formbestimmung ist. Die Bestimmung aber, wie sie sich gezeigt hat, ist in ihrer Wahrheit, die totale sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, die somit als diese Identität das einfache Wesen an ihr selbst ist. Die Form hat daher an ihrer eigenen Identität das Wesen; wie das Wesen an seiner negativen Natur die absolute Form. Es kann also nicht gefragt werden, wie die Form zum Wesen hinzukomme, denn sie ist nur das Scheinen desselben in sich selbst, die eigene ihm inwohnende Reflexion. Die Form ebenso an ihr selbst ist die in sich zurückkehrende Reflexion, oder das identische Wesen; in ihrem Bestimmen macht sie die Bestimmung zum Gesetztseyn als Gesetztseyn. —Sie bestimmt also nicht das Wesen, als ob sie wahrhaft vorausgesetzt, getrennt vom Wesen sey, denn so ist sie die unwesentliche, rastlos zu Grunde gehende Reflexionsbestimmung, hiermit ist sie so selbst vielmehr der Grund ihres Aufhebens oder die identische Beziehung ihrer Bestimmungen. Die Form bestimmt das Wesen, heißt also, die Form in ihrem Unterscheiden hebt dieß Unterscheiden selbst auf, und ist die Identität mit sich, welche das Wesen als das Bestehen der Bestimmung ist; sie ist der Widerspruch in ihrem Gesetztseyn aufgehoben zu seyn und an diesem Aufgehobenseyn das Bestehen zu haben; somit der Grund, als das im Bestimmt- oder Negirtseyn mit sich identische Wesen.\n\nDiese Unterschiede, der Form und des Wesens, sind daher nur Momente der einfachen Formbeziehung selbst. Aber sie sind näher zu betrachten und festzuhalten. Die bestimmende Form bezieht sich auf sich als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn, sie bezieht sich damit auf ihre Identität als auf ein Andres. Sie setzt sich als aufgehoben; sie setzt damit ihre Identität voraus; das Wesen ist nach diesem Momente das Unbestimmte, dem die Form ein anderes ist. So ist es nicht das Wesen, das die absolute Reflexion an ihm selbst ist, sondern bestimmt als die formlose Identität; es ist die Materie.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0001","text":"## A. Der absolute Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"123.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0002","text":"## a. Form und Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"123.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0003","text":"Die Reflexions-Bestimmung, insofern sie in den Grund zurückgeht, ist ein erstes, ein unmittelbares Daseyn überhaupt, von dem angefangen wird. Aber das Daseyn hat nur noch die Bedeutung des Gesetztseyns und setzt wesentlich einen Grund voraus; in dem Sinne, daß es ihn vielmehr nicht setzt; daß dieß Setzen ein Aufheben seiner selbst, das Unmittelbare vielmehr das Gesetzte und der Grund das Nichtgesetzte ist. Wie es sich ergeben hat, ist dieß Voraussetzen, das auf das Setzende rückschlagende Setzen; der Grund ist als das aufgehobene Bestimmtseyn nicht das Unbestimmte, sondern das durch sich selbst bestimmte Wesen, aber als unbestimmt oder als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn Bestimmtes. Er ist das Wesen, das in seiner Negativität mit sich identisch ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"123.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0004","text":"Die Bestimmtheit des Wesens als Grund wird hiermit die gedoppelte, des Grundes und des Begründeten. Sie ist erstens das Wesen als Grund, bestimmt das Wesen zu seyn gegen das Gesetztseyn, als Nichtgesetztseyn. Zweitens ist sie das Begründete, das Unmittelbare, das aber nicht an und für sich ist, das Gesetztseyn als Gesetztseyn. Dieses ist somit gleichfalls mit sich identisch, aber die Identität des Negativen mit sich. Das mit sich identische Negative und das mit sich identische Positive ist nun eine und dieselbe Identität. Denn der Grund ist Identität des Positiven oder selbst auch des Gesetztseyns mit sich; das Begründete ist das Gesetztseyn als Gesetztseyn, diese seine Reflexion in sich aber ist die Identität des Grundes.—Diese einfache Identität ist also nicht selbst der Grund, denn der Grund ist das Wesen gesetzt, als das Nichtgesetzte gegen das Gesetztseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"123.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0005","text":"Sie ist, als die Einheit dieser bestimmten Identität, (des Grundes) und der negativen Identität (des Begründeten) das Wesen überhaupt, unterschieden von seiner Vermittelung.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"123.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0006","text":"Diese Vermittelung, mit den vorhergehenden Reflexionen verglichen, aus denen sie herkommt, ist erstlich nicht die reine Reflexion, als welche nicht vom Wesen unterschieden ist, und das Negative, damit auch die Selbstständigkeit der Bestimmungen, noch nicht an ihr hat. Im Grunde als der aufgehobenen Reflexion aber haben diese Bestimmungen ein Bestehen.—Auch ist sie nicht die bestimmende Reflexion, deren Bestimmungen wesentliche Selbstständigkeit haben; denn diese ist im Grunde zu Grunde gegangen, in dessen Einheit sind sie nur gesetzte.—Diese Vermittelung des Grundes ist daher die Einheit der reinen und der bestimmenden Reflexion; ihre Bestimmungen oder das Gesetzte hat Bestehen, und umgekehrt das Bestehen derselben ist ein Gesetztes.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"123.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0007","text":"Weil dieß ihr Bestehen selbst ein Gesetztes ist oder Bestimmtheit hat, so sind sie somit von ihrer einfachen Identität unterschieden, und machen die Form aus gegen das Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"123.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0008","text":"Das Wesen hat eine Form, und Bestimmungen derselben. Erst als Grund hat es eine feste Unmittelbarkeit oder ist Substrat. Das Wesen als solches ist eins mit seiner Reflexion, und ununterschieden ihre Bewegung selbst. Es ist daher nicht das Wesen, welches sie durchläuft; auch ist es nicht dasjenige, von dem sie als von einem Ersten anfängt. Dieser Umstand erschwert die Darstellung der Reflexion überhaupt; denn man kann eigentlich nicht sagen, das Wesen geht in sich selbst zurück, das Wesen scheint in sich, weil es nicht vor oder in seiner Bewegung ist, und diese keine Grundlage hat, an der sie sich verläuft. Ein Bezogenes tritt erst im Grund nach dem Momente der aufgehobenen Reflexion hervor.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"123.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0009","text":"Das Wesen als das bezogene Substrat aber ist das bestimmte Wesen; um dieses Gesetztseyns willen hat es wesentlich die Form an ihm.—Die Formbestimmungen dagegen sind nun die Bestimmungen als an dem Wesen; es liegt ihnen zu Grunde, als das Unbestimmte, das in seiner Bestimmung gleichgültig gegen sie ist; sie haben an ihm ihre Reflexion in sich. Die Reflexions-Bestimmungen sollten ihr Bestehen an ihnen selbst haben und selbstständig seyn; aber ihre Selbstständigkeit ist ihre Auflösung; so haben sie dieselbe an einem Andern; aber diese Auflösung ist selbst diese Identität mit sich oder der Grund des Bestehens, den sie sich geben.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"123.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0010","text":"Der Form gehört überhaupt alles Bestimmte an; es ist Formbestimmung, insofern es ein Gesetztes, hiermit von einem solchen, dessen Form es ist, Unterschiedenes ist; die Bestimmtheit als Qualität ist eins mit ihrem Substrat, dem Seyn; das Seyn ist das unmittelbar Bestimmte, das von seiner Bestimmtheit noch nicht unterschieden,—oder das in ihr noch nicht in sich reflektirt, so wie diese daher eine seyende, noch nicht eine Gesetzte ist.—Die Formbestimmungen des Wesens sind ferner als die Reflexions-Bestimmtheiten, ihrer nähern Bestimmtheit nach, die oben betrachteten Momente der Reflexion. Die Identität, und der Unterschied, dieser Theils als Verschiedenheit, Theils als Gegensatz. Ferner aber gehört auch die Grundbeziehung dazu, insofern sie zwar die aufgehobene Reflexions-Bestimmung aber dadurch das Wesen zugleich als Gesetztes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"123.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0011","text":"Dagegen gehört zur Form nicht die Identität, welche der Grund in sich hat, nämlich daß das Gesetztseyn als aufgehobenes und das Gesetztseyn als solches,—der Grund und das Begründete,—Eine Reflexion ist, welche das Wesen als einfache Grundlage ausmacht, die das Bestehen der Form ist. Allein dieß Bestehen ist im Grunde gesetzt; oder dieß Wesen ist selbst wesentlich als bestimmtes; somit ist es auch wieder das Moment der Grundbeziehung und Form.—Dieß ist die absolute Wechselbeziehung der Form und des Wesens, daß dieses einfache Einheit des Grundes und des Begründeten, darin aber eben selbst bestimmt oder Negatives ist, und sich als Grundlage von der Form unterscheidet, aber so zugleich selbst Grund und Moment der Form wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"123.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0012","text":"Die Form ist daher das vollendete Ganze der Reflexion; sie enthält auch diese Bestimmung derselben, aufgehobene zu seyn; daher ist sie ebenso sehr als sie eine Einheit ihres Bestimmens ist, auch bezogen auf ihr Aufgehobenseyn, auf ein Anderes, das nicht selbst Form, sondern an dem sie sey. Als die wesentliche sich auf sich selbst beziehende Negativität, gegen dieß einfache Negative ist sie das Setzende und Bestimmende; das einfache Wesen hingegen ist die unbestimmte und unthätige Grundlage, an welcher die Formbestimmungen das Bestehen oder die Reflexion in sich haben.—Bei dieser Unterscheidung des Wesens und der Form pflegt die äußere Reflexion stehen zu bleiben; sie ist nothwendig, aber dieses Unterscheiden selbst ist ihre Einheit, so wie diese Grundeinheit das sich von sich abstoßende und zum Gesetztseyn machende Wesen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"123.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0013","text":"Die Form ist die absolute Negativität selbst, oder die negative absolute Identität mit sich, wodurch eben das Wesen nicht Seyn, sondern Wesen ist. Diese Identität abstrakt genommen, ist das Wesen gegen die Form; so wie die Negativität abstrakt genommen als das Gesetztseyn, die einzelne Formbestimmung ist. Die Bestimmung aber, wie sie sich gezeigt hat, ist in ihrer Wahrheit, die totale sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, die somit als diese Identität das einfache Wesen an ihr selbst ist. Die Form hat daher an ihrer eigenen Identität das Wesen; wie das Wesen an seiner negativen Natur die absolute Form. Es kann also nicht gefragt werden, wie die Form zum Wesen hinzukomme, denn sie ist nur das Scheinen desselben in sich selbst, die eigene ihm inwohnende Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"123.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0014","text":"Die Form ebenso an ihr selbst ist die in sich zurückkehrende Reflexion, oder das identische Wesen; in ihrem Bestimmen macht sie die Bestimmung zum Gesetztseyn als Gesetztseyn. —Sie bestimmt also nicht das Wesen, als ob sie wahrhaft vorausgesetzt, getrennt vom Wesen sey, denn so ist sie die unwesentliche, rastlos zu Grunde gehende Reflexionsbestimmung, hiermit ist sie so selbst vielmehr der Grund ihres Aufhebens oder die identische Beziehung ihrer Bestimmungen. Die Form bestimmt das Wesen, heißt also, die Form in ihrem Unterscheiden hebt dieß Unterscheiden selbst auf, und ist die Identität mit sich, welche das Wesen als das Bestehen der Bestimmung ist; sie ist der Widerspruch in ihrem Gesetztseyn aufgehoben zu seyn und an diesem Aufgehobenseyn das Bestehen zu haben; somit der Grund, als das im Bestimmt- oder Negirtseyn mit sich identische Wesen.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"123.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0015","text":"Diese Unterschiede, der Form und des Wesens, sind daher nur Momente der einfachen Formbeziehung selbst. Aber sie sind näher zu betrachten und festzuhalten. Die bestimmende Form bezieht sich auf sich als aufgehobenes Gesetztseyn, sie bezieht sich damit auf ihre Identität als auf ein Andres. Sie setzt sich als aufgehoben; sie setzt damit ihre Identität voraus; das Wesen ist nach diesem Momente das Unbestimmte, dem die Form ein anderes ist. So ist es nicht das Wesen, das die absolute Reflexion an ihm selbst ist, sondern bestimmt als die formlose Identität; es ist die Materie.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"123.15"}],"sha256":"75552f1343fc97db465aaf95c91715e51d98aefe09d97fb1686f6ec2d8d9d366","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105023168103Z_06d9ac82","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Form and Essence.","source_sha256":"75552f1343fc97db465aaf95c91715e51d98aefe09d97fb1686f6ec2d8d9d366","sha256":"d40059b4973f95a832cfc01d624a2d547b04fd504472327a35ec9268050fec74","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:50:23.168122+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0001","text":"## A. The absolute ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"123.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0002","text":"## a. Form and essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"123.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0003","text":"The determination of reflection, insofar as it goes back into the ground, is a first, an immediate existence in general, from which a beginning is made. But existence now has only the meaning of positedness, and essentially presupposes a ground; in the sense that it rather does not posit it; that this positing is a sublating of itself, that the immediate is rather the posited, and the ground the unposited. As has emerged, this presupposing is positing rebounding upon that which posits; the ground, as sublated determinateness, is not the indeterminate, but the essence determined through itself, yet determined as indeterminate or as sublated positedness. It is the essence which is identical with itself in its negativity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"123.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0004","text":"The determinateness of essence as ground thereby becomes the twofold determinateness, of the ground and of that which is grounded. It is, first, essence as ground, determined to be essence as against positedness, as unpositedness. Secondly, it is that which is grounded, the immediate, which, however, is not in and for itself, positedness as positedness. This, therefore, is likewise identical with itself, but the identity of the negative with itself. The negative identical with itself and the positive identical with itself are now one and the same identity. For the ground is the identity of the positive, or likewise of positedness itself, with itself; that which is grounded is positedness as positedness, but this its reflection into itself is the identity of the ground.—This simple identity, therefore, is not itself the ground, for the ground is essence posited as the unposited against positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"123.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0005","text":"As the unity of this determinate identity (of the ground) and the negative identity (of that which is grounded), it is essence in general, distinguished from its mediation.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"123.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0006","text":"This mediation, compared with the preceding reflections from which it proceeds, is, first, not pure reflection, which is not distinguished from essence and does not yet have within it the negative, and hence also not the self-subsistence of the determinations. But in the ground, as sublated reflection, these determinations have subsistence.—Nor is it determining reflection, whose determinations have essential self-subsistence; for this has foundered in the ground, in whose unity they are only posited.—This mediation of the ground is therefore the unity of pure and determining reflection; its determinations, or the posited, have subsistence, and conversely their subsistence is a positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"123.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0007","text":"Because this their subsistence is itself a positedness, or has determinateness, they are consequently distinguished from their simple identity and constitute form as against essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"123.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0008","text":"Essence has a form, and determinations of this form. Only as ground does it have a fixed immediacy, or is substrate. Essence as such is one with its reflection, and is itself undifferentiated from its movement. Hence it is not the essence which traverses this movement; nor is it that from which the movement begins as from a first. This circumstance makes the exposition of reflection in general difficult; for one cannot properly say that essence returns into itself, that essence shines within itself, since it is not prior to or within its movement, and this movement has no basis on which it takes place. Something related first emerges in the ground, after the moment of sublated reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"123.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0009","text":"But essence as the related substrate is determinate essence; on account of this positedness, it essentially has form in it.—The determinations of form, on the other hand, are now the determinations as existing in essence; essence underlies them as the indeterminate which, in its determinateness, is indifferent towards them; in it they have their reflection into themselves. The determinations of reflection were supposed to have their subsistence in themselves and to be self-subsistent; but their self-subsistence is their dissolution; thus they have it in an other; but this dissolution is itself this identity with themselves, or the ground of subsistence which they give themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"123.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0010","text":"To form in general belongs everything determinate; it is a determination of form insofar as it is a positedness, and is thereby distinct from that of which it is the form; determinateness as quality is one with its substrate, being; being is what is immediately determinate, which is not yet distinguished from its determinateness,—or which has not yet reflected into itself within it, just as this determinateness is therefore a being determinateness, not yet a posited one.—The determinations of form of essence are further, as determinations of reflection, according to their more precise determinateness, the moments of reflection considered above: identity and difference, the latter partly as diversity, partly as opposition. Further, the relation of ground also belongs thereto, insofar as it is indeed the sublated determination of reflection, but thereby is at the same time essence as posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"123.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0011","text":"By contrast, what does not belong to form is the identity which the ground has within itself, namely, that positedness as sublated and positedness as such,—the ground and that which is grounded,—are one reflection, which constitutes essence as simple foundation, the subsistence of form. Yet this subsistence is posited in the ground; or this essence is itself essentially as determinate; thus it is again also the moment of the relation of ground and of form.—This is the absolute reciprocal relation of form and essence: that the latter is the simple unity of ground and that which is grounded, but therein is itself precisely determined, or negative, and distinguishes itself as foundation from form, yet thereby at the same time itself becomes ground and moment of form.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"123.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0012","text":"Form is therefore the completed whole of reflection; it also contains this determination of reflection, that it is sublated; hence, just as it is a unity of its determining, it is also related to its sublatedness, to an other which is not itself form, but in which it is. As essential negativity relating itself to itself, it is, as against this simple negative, the positing and determining factor; simple essence, on the other hand, is the indeterminate and inactive foundation in which the determinations of form have their subsistence, or reflection into themselves.—At this distinction of essence and form external reflection is accustomed to stop; it is necessary, but this distinguishing itself is their unity, just as this fundamental unity is the essence which repels itself from itself and makes itself into positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"123.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0013","text":"Form is absolute negativity itself, or negative absolute identity with itself, whereby essence is precisely not being but essence. This identity, taken abstractly, is essence as against form; just as negativity, taken abstractly as positedness, is the individual determination of form. But determinateness, as it has shown itself, is in its truth total negativity relating itself to itself, which is therefore, as this identity, simple essence in itself. Form thus has essence in its own identity; just as essence has absolute form in its negative nature. Therefore it cannot be asked how form comes to essence, for it is only the shining of essence within itself, the reflection proper to it and dwelling in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"123.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0014","text":"Form, likewise in itself, is reflection returning into itself, or identical essence; in its determining it makes determinateness into positedness as positedness. —It therefore does not determine essence as though it were truly presupposed, separate from essence; for thus it is the inessential determination of reflection, restlessly foundering, and hence is itself rather the ground of its sublation, or the identical relation of its determinations. That form determines essence thus means: form, in its distinguishing, sublates this distinguishing itself, and is identity with itself, which is essence as the subsistence of determinateness; it is the contradiction of being sublated in its positedness and of having subsistence in this sublatedness; thus it is ground, as essence identical with itself in being determined or negated.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"123.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0015","text":"These differences, of form and essence, are therefore only moments of the simple relation of form itself. But they are to be considered more closely and held fast. Determining form relates itself to itself as sublated positedness; thereby it relates itself to its identity as to an other. It posits itself as sublated; thereby it presupposes its identity; essence is, according to this moment, the indeterminate to which form is an other. Thus it is not essence that is absolute reflection in itself, but is determined as the formless identity; it is matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"123.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_FUW0:P0015"]}],"source_digest":"213279cd7b238113d32242f7db61e1977874f7a57abb2d1900cfa287fd54ae23","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Form und Wesen."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Form und Wesen.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM","title":"b. Form and Matter.","order":124,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BFUM","text":"Das Wesen wird zur Materie, indem seine Reflexion sich bestimmt, zu demselben als zu dem formlosen Unbestimmten sich zu verhalten. Die Materie ist also die einfache unterschiedslose Identität, welche das Wesen ist, mit der Bestimmung das Andere der Form zu seyn. Sie ist daher die eigentliche Grundlage oder Substrat der Form, weil sie die Reflexion in sich der Formbestimmungen oder das Selbstständige ausmacht, auf das sie sich als auf ihr positives Bestehen beziehen.\n\nWenn von allen Bestimmungen, aller Form eines Etwas abstrahirt wird, so bleibt die unbestimmte Materie übrig. Die Materie ist ein schlechthin Abstraktes. (—Man kann die Materie nicht sehen, fühlen u. s.f.—was man sieht, fühlt, ist eine bestimmte Materie, d. h. eine Einheit der Materie und der Form). Diese Abstraktion, aus der die Materie hervorgeht, ist aber nicht nur ein äußerliches Wegnehmen und Aufheben der Form, sondern die Form reducirt sich durch sich selbst, wie sich ergeben hat, zu dieser einfachen Identität.\n\nFerner setzt die Form eine Materie voraus, auf welche sie sich bezieht. Aber darum finden sich beide nicht äußerlich und zufällig einander gegenüber; weder die Materie noch die Form ist aus sich selbst, oder in anderer Sprache ewig. Die Materie ist das gegen die Form gleichgültige, aber diese Gleichgültigkeit ist die Bestimmtheit der Identität mit sich, in welche als in ihre Grundlage die Form zurückgeht. Die Form setzt die Materie voraus; eben darin, daß sie sich als Aufgehobenes setzt, somit sich auf diese ihre Identität als auf ein Anderes bezieht. Umgekehrt ist die Form von der Materie vorausgesetzt; denn diese ist nicht das einfache Wesen, das unmittelbar selbst die absolute Reflexion ist, sondern dasselbe bestimmt als das Positive, nämlich das nur ist, als aufgehobene Negation.—Aber von der andern Seite weil die Form sich nur als Materie setzt, insofern sie sich selbst aufhebt, somit dieselbe voraussetzt, ist die Materie auch bestimmt als grundloses Bestehen. Ebenso ist die Materie nicht bestimmt als der Grund der Form; sondern, indem die Materie sich setzt als die abstrakte Identität der aufgehobenen Formbestimmung, ist sie nicht die Identität als Grund, und die Form insofern gegen sie grundlos. Form und Materie sind somit bestimmt, die eine wie die andere, nicht gesetzt durch einander, nicht Grund von einander zu seyn. Die Materie ist vielmehr die Identität des Grundes und des Begründeten, als Grundlage, welche dieser Formbeziehung gegenüber steht. Diese ihre gemeinschaftliche Bestimmung der Gleichgültigkeit ist die Bestimmung der Materie als solcher, und macht auch die Beziehung beider aufeinander aus. Ebenso die Bestimmung der Form, die Beziehung als unterschiedener zu seyn, ist auch das andere Moment des Verhaltens beider zu einander.—Die Materie, das als gleichgültig Bestimmte, ist das Passive gegen die Form als Thätiges. Diese ist als das sich auf sich beziehende Negative der Widerspruch in sich selbst, das sich Auflösende sich von sich Abstoßende und Bestimmende. Sie bezieht sich auf die Materie, und sie ist gesetzt, sich auf dieß ihr Bestehen, als auf ein Anderes zu beziehen. Die Materie hingegen ist gesetzt, sich nur auf sich selbst zu beziehen, und gleichgültig gegen Anderes zu seyn; aber sie bezieht sich an sich auf die Form; denn sie enthält die aufgehobene Negativität, und ist nur Materie durch diese Bestimmung. Sie bezieht sich auf sie nur darum als auf ein Anderes, weil die Form nicht an ihr gesetzt, weil sie dieselbe nur an sich ist. Sie enthält die Form in sich verschlossen, und ist die absolute Empfänglichkeit für sie, nur darum weil sie dieselbe absolut in ihr hat, weil dieß ihre an sich seyende Bestimmung ist. Die Materie muß daher formirt werden, und die Form muß sich materialisiren, sich an der Materie die Identität mit sich oder das Bestehen geben.\n\n2. Die Form bestimmt daher die Materie, und die Materie wird von der Form bestimmt.—Weil die Form selbst die absolute Identität mit sich ist, also die Materie in sich enthält; ebenso weil die Materie in ihrer reinen Abstraktion oder absoluten Negativität die Form in ihr selbst hat, so ist die Thätigkeit der Form auf die Materie, und das Bestimmtwerden dieser durch jene vielmehr nur das Aufheben des Scheines ihrer Gleichgültigkeit und Unterschiedenheit. Diese Beziehung des Bestimmens ist so die Vermittelung jeder der beiden mit sich durch ihr eigenes Nichtseyn,—aber diese beiden Vermittelungen sind Eine Bewegung und die Wiederherstellung ihrer ursprünglichen Identität;—die Erinnerung ihrer Entäußerung.\n\nZuerst setzen Form und Materie sich gegenseitig voraus. Wie sich ergeben hat, heißt dieß so viel, die eine wesentliche Einheit ist negative Beziehung auf sich selbst, so entzweit sie sich in die wesentliche Identität bestimmt als die gleichgültige Grundlage, und in den wesentlichen Unterschied oder Negativität, als die bestimmende Form. Jene Einheit des Wesens und der Form, die sich als Form und Materie gegenübersetzen, ist der absolute Grund, der sich bestimmt. Indem sie sich zu einem Verschiedenen macht, wird die Beziehung um der zu Grunde liegenden Identität der Verschiedenen willen zur gegenseitigen Voraussetzung.\n\nZweitens, die Form als selbstständig ist ohnehin der sich selbst aufhebende Widerspruch; aber sie ist auch als solcher gesetzt, denn sie ist zugleich selbstständig und zugleich wesentlich auf ein Anderes bezogen;—sie hebt sich somit auf. Da sie selbst zweiseitig ist, so hat auch dieß Aufheben die gedoppeite Seite, erstlich, sie hebt ihre Selbstständigkeit auf, sie macht sich zu einem Gesetzten, zu einem, das an einem Andern ist, und dieß ihr Anderes ist die Materie. Zweitens sie hebt ihre Bestimmtheit gegen die Materie, ihre Beziehung auf dieselbe somit ihr Gesetztseyn auf, und giebt sich dadurch Bestehen. Indem sie ihr Gesetztseyn aufhebt, so ist diese ihre Reflexion die eigene Identität, in welche sie übergeht; indem sie aber diese Identität zugleich entäußert und als Materie sich gegenübersetzt, so ist jene Reflexion des Gesetztseyns in sich als Vereinigung mit einer Materie, an der sie Bestehen erhält; sie geht also in dieser Vereinigung ebenso sehr mit der Materie als einem Andern,—nach der ersten Seite, daß sie sich zu einem Gesetzten macht, —als auch darin mit ihrer eigenen Identität zusammen.\n\nDie Thätigkeit der Form also, wodurch die Materie bestimmt wird, besteht in einem negativen Verhalten der Form gegen sich selbst. Aber umgekehrt verhält sie sich damit auch negativ gegen die Materie; allein dieß Bestimmtwerden der Materie ist ebenso sehr die eigene Bewegung der Form selbst. Diese ist frei von der Materie, aber sie hebt diese ihre Selbstständigkeit auf; aber ihre Selbstständigkeit ist die Materie selbst, denn an dieser hat sie ihre wesentliche Identität. Indem sie sich also zum Gesetzten macht, so ist dieß ein und dasselbe, daß sie die Materie zu einem Bestimmten macht.—Aber von der andern Seite betrachtet, ist die eigene Identität der Form zugleich sich entäußert, und die Materie ihr Anderes; insofern wird die Materie auch nicht bestimmt, dadurch, daß die Form ihre eigne Selbstständigkeit aufhebt. Allein die Materie ist nur selbstständig der Form gegenüber; indem das Negative sich aufhebt, hebt sich auch das Positive auf. Indem die Form also sich aufhebt, so fällt auch die Bestimmtheit der Materie weg, welche sie gegen die Form hat, nämlich das unbestimmte Bestehen zu seyn.\n\nDieß, was als Thätigkeit der Form erscheint, ist ferner ebenso sehr die eigene Bewegung der Materie selbst. Die ansichseyende Bestimmung oder das Sollen der Materie ist ihre absolute Negativität. Durch diese bezieht sich die Materie schlechthin nicht nur auf die Form als auf ein Anderes, sondern dieses Äußere ist die Form, welche sie selbst als verschlossen in sich enthält. Die Materie ist derselbe Widerspruch an sich, welchen die Form enthält, und dieser Widerspruch ist wie seine Auflösung, nur Einer. Die Materie ist aber in sich selbst widersprechend, weil sie als die unbestimmte Identität mit sich zugleich die absolute Negativität ist; sie hebt sich daher an ihr selbst auf, und ihre Identität zerfällt in ihrer Negativität, und diese erhält an jener ihr Bestehen. Indem also die Materie von der Form als von einem Äußern bestimmt wird, so erreicht damit sie ihre Bestimmung, und die Äußerlichkeit des Verhaltens sowohl für die Form als für die Materie besteht darin, daß jede oder vielmehr ihre ursprüngliche Einheit in ihrem Setzen zugleich voraussetzend ist; wodurch die Beziehung auf sich, zugleich Beziehung auf sich als aufgehobenes oder Beziehung auf sein anderes ist.\n\nDrittens, durch diese Bewegung der Form und Matene ist ihre ursprüngliche Einheit einer Seits hergestellt, anderer Seits nunmehr eine gesetzte. Die Materie bestimmt ebensowohl sich selbst, als dieß Bestimmen ein für sie äußerliches Thun der Form ist; umgekehrt die Form bestimmt ebenso sehr nur sich oder hat die Materie, die von ihr bestimmt wird, an ihr selbst, als sie in ihrem Bestimmen sich gegen ein Anderes verhält; und beides, das Thun der Form und die Bewegung der Materie ist dasselbe, nur daß jenes ein Thun ist, d. h. die Negativität als gesetzte, dieß aber Bewegung oder Werden, die Negativität als ansichseyende Bestimmung. Das Resultat ist daher die Einheit des Ansichseyns und des Gesetztseyns. Die Materie ist als solche bestimmt, oder hat nothwendig eine Form, und die Form ist schlechthin materielle, bestehende Form.\n\nDie Form, insofern sie eine Materie als das ihr Andere voraussetzt, ist endlich. Sie ist nicht Grund, sondern nur das Thätige. Ebenso ist die Materie, insofern sie die Form als ihr Nichtseyn voraussetzt, die endliche Materie, sie ist ebenso wenig Grund ihrer Einheit mit der Form, sondern nur die Grundlage für die Form. Aber sowohl diese endliche Materie als die endliche Form hat keine Wahrheit; jede bezieht sich auf die andere, oder nur ihre Einheit ist ihre Wahrheit. In diese Einheit gehen diese beiden Bestimmungen zurück, und heben darin ihre Selbstständigkeit auf; sie erweist sich damit als ihr Grund. Die Materie ist daher nur insofern Grund ihrer Formbestimmung, als sie nicht Materie als Materie, sondern die absolute Einheit des Wesens und der Form ist; ebenso die Form ist nur Grund des Bestehens ihrer Bestimmungen, insofern sie dieselbe eine Einheit ist. Aber diese eine Einheit als die absolute Negativität und bestimmter als ausschließende Einheit ist in ihrer Reflexion voraussetzend; oder es ist Ein Thun, im Setzen sich als Gesetztes in der Einheit zu erhalten und sich von sich selbst abzustoßen, sich auf sich als sich, und sich auf sich als auf ein Anderes zu beziehen. Oder das Bestimmtwerden der Materie durch die Form ist die Vermittelung des Wesens als Grund mit sich in einer Einheit, durch sich selbst und durch die Negation seiner selbst.\n\nDie formirte Materie oder die Bestehen habende Form, ist nun nicht nur jene absolute Einheit des Grundes mit sich, sondern auch die gesetzte Einheit. Die betrachtete Bewegung ist es, in welcher der absolute Grund seine Momente zugleich als sich aufhebende und somit als gesetzte dargestellt hat. Oder die wiederhergestellte Einheit hat in ihrem Zusammengehen mit sich, sich ebenso sehr von sich selbst abgestoßen und sich bestimmt; denn ihre Einheit ist als durch Negation zu Stande gekommen, auch negative Einheit. Sie ist daher die Einheit der Form und der Materie, als ihre Grundlage, aber als ihre bestimmte Grundlage, welche formirte Materie, aber gegen Form und Materie zugleich als gegen aufgehobene und unwesendiche gleichgültig ist. Sie ist der Inhalt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0001","text":"Das Wesen wird zur Materie, indem seine Reflexion sich bestimmt, zu demselben als zu dem formlosen Unbestimmten sich zu verhalten. Die Materie ist also die einfache unterschiedslose Identität, welche das Wesen ist, mit der Bestimmung das Andere der Form zu seyn. Sie ist daher die eigentliche Grundlage oder Substrat der Form, weil sie die Reflexion in sich der Formbestimmungen oder das Selbstständige ausmacht, auf das sie sich als auf ihr positives Bestehen beziehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"124.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0002","text":"Wenn von allen Bestimmungen, aller Form eines Etwas abstrahirt wird, so bleibt die unbestimmte Materie übrig. Die Materie ist ein schlechthin Abstraktes. (—Man kann die Materie nicht sehen, fühlen u. s.f.—was man sieht, fühlt, ist eine bestimmte Materie, d. h. eine Einheit der Materie und der Form). Diese Abstraktion, aus der die Materie hervorgeht, ist aber nicht nur ein äußerliches Wegnehmen und Aufheben der Form, sondern die Form reducirt sich durch sich selbst, wie sich ergeben hat, zu dieser einfachen Identität.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"124.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0003","text":"Ferner setzt die Form eine Materie voraus, auf welche sie sich bezieht. Aber darum finden sich beide nicht äußerlich und zufällig einander gegenüber; weder die Materie noch die Form ist aus sich selbst, oder in anderer Sprache ewig. Die Materie ist das gegen die Form gleichgültige, aber diese Gleichgültigkeit ist die Bestimmtheit der Identität mit sich, in welche als in ihre Grundlage die Form zurückgeht. Die Form setzt die Materie voraus; eben darin, daß sie sich als Aufgehobenes setzt, somit sich auf diese ihre Identität als auf ein Anderes bezieht.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"124.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0004","text":"Umgekehrt ist die Form von der Materie vorausgesetzt; denn diese ist nicht das einfache Wesen, das unmittelbar selbst die absolute Reflexion ist, sondern dasselbe bestimmt als das Positive, nämlich das nur ist, als aufgehobene Negation.—Aber von der andern Seite weil die Form sich nur als Materie setzt, insofern sie sich selbst aufhebt, somit dieselbe voraussetzt, ist die Materie auch bestimmt als grundloses Bestehen. Ebenso ist die Materie nicht bestimmt als der Grund der Form; sondern, indem die Materie sich setzt als die abstrakte Identität der aufgehobenen Formbestimmung, ist sie nicht die Identität als Grund, und die Form insofern gegen sie grundlos. Form und Materie sind somit bestimmt, die eine wie die andere, nicht gesetzt durch einander, nicht Grund von einander zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"124.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0005","text":"Die Materie ist vielmehr die Identität des Grundes und des Begründeten, als Grundlage, welche dieser Formbeziehung gegenüber steht. Diese ihre gemeinschaftliche Bestimmung der Gleichgültigkeit ist die Bestimmung der Materie als solcher, und macht auch die Beziehung beider aufeinander aus. Ebenso die Bestimmung der Form, die Beziehung als unterschiedener zu seyn, ist auch das andere Moment des Verhaltens beider zu einander.—Die Materie, das als gleichgültig Bestimmte, ist das Passive gegen die Form als Thätiges. Diese ist als das sich auf sich beziehende Negative der Widerspruch in sich selbst, das sich Auflösende sich von sich Abstoßende und Bestimmende. Sie bezieht sich auf die Materie, und sie ist gesetzt, sich auf dieß ihr Bestehen, als auf ein Anderes zu beziehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"124.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0006","text":"Die Materie hingegen ist gesetzt, sich nur auf sich selbst zu beziehen, und gleichgültig gegen Anderes zu seyn; aber sie bezieht sich an sich auf die Form; denn sie enthält die aufgehobene Negativität, und ist nur Materie durch diese Bestimmung. Sie bezieht sich auf sie nur darum als auf ein Anderes, weil die Form nicht an ihr gesetzt, weil sie dieselbe nur an sich ist. Sie enthält die Form in sich verschlossen, und ist die absolute Empfänglichkeit für sie, nur darum weil sie dieselbe absolut in ihr hat, weil dieß ihre an sich seyende Bestimmung ist. Die Materie muß daher formirt werden, und die Form muß sich materialisiren, sich an der Materie die Identität mit sich oder das Bestehen geben.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"124.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0007","text":"2. Die Form bestimmt daher die Materie, und die Materie wird von der Form bestimmt.—Weil die Form selbst die absolute Identität mit sich ist, also die Materie in sich enthält; ebenso weil die Materie in ihrer reinen Abstraktion oder absoluten Negativität die Form in ihr selbst hat, so ist die Thätigkeit der Form auf die Materie, und das Bestimmtwerden dieser durch jene vielmehr nur das Aufheben des Scheines ihrer Gleichgültigkeit und Unterschiedenheit. Diese Beziehung des Bestimmens ist so die Vermittelung jeder der beiden mit sich durch ihr eigenes Nichtseyn,—aber diese beiden Vermittelungen sind Eine Bewegung und die Wiederherstellung ihrer ursprünglichen Identität;—die Erinnerung ihrer Entäußerung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"124.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0008","text":"Zuerst setzen Form und Materie sich gegenseitig voraus. Wie sich ergeben hat, heißt dieß so viel, die eine wesentliche Einheit ist negative Beziehung auf sich selbst, so entzweit sie sich in die wesentliche Identität bestimmt als die gleichgültige Grundlage, und in den wesentlichen Unterschied oder Negativität, als die bestimmende Form. Jene Einheit des Wesens und der Form, die sich als Form und Materie gegenübersetzen, ist der absolute Grund, der sich bestimmt. Indem sie sich zu einem Verschiedenen macht, wird die Beziehung um der zu Grunde liegenden Identität der Verschiedenen willen zur gegenseitigen Voraussetzung.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"124.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0009","text":"Zweitens, die Form als selbstständig ist ohnehin der sich selbst aufhebende Widerspruch; aber sie ist auch als solcher gesetzt, denn sie ist zugleich selbstständig und zugleich wesentlich auf ein Anderes bezogen;—sie hebt sich somit auf. Da sie selbst zweiseitig ist, so hat auch dieß Aufheben die gedoppeite Seite, erstlich, sie hebt ihre Selbstständigkeit auf, sie macht sich zu einem Gesetzten, zu einem, das an einem Andern ist, und dieß ihr Anderes ist die Materie. Zweitens sie hebt ihre Bestimmtheit gegen die Materie, ihre Beziehung auf dieselbe somit ihr Gesetztseyn auf, und giebt sich dadurch Bestehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"124.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0010","text":"Indem sie ihr Gesetztseyn aufhebt, so ist diese ihre Reflexion die eigene Identität, in welche sie übergeht; indem sie aber diese Identität zugleich entäußert und als Materie sich gegenübersetzt, so ist jene Reflexion des Gesetztseyns in sich als Vereinigung mit einer Materie, an der sie Bestehen erhält; sie geht also in dieser Vereinigung ebenso sehr mit der Materie als einem Andern,—nach der ersten Seite, daß sie sich zu einem Gesetzten macht, —als auch darin mit ihrer eigenen Identität zusammen.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"124.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0011","text":"Die Thätigkeit der Form also, wodurch die Materie bestimmt wird, besteht in einem negativen Verhalten der Form gegen sich selbst. Aber umgekehrt verhält sie sich damit auch negativ gegen die Materie; allein dieß Bestimmtwerden der Materie ist ebenso sehr die eigene Bewegung der Form selbst. Diese ist frei von der Materie, aber sie hebt diese ihre Selbstständigkeit auf; aber ihre Selbstständigkeit ist die Materie selbst, denn an dieser hat sie ihre wesentliche Identität. Indem sie sich also zum Gesetzten macht, so ist dieß ein und dasselbe, daß sie die Materie zu einem Bestimmten macht.—Aber von der andern Seite betrachtet, ist die eigene Identität der Form zugleich sich entäußert, und die Materie ihr Anderes; insofern wird die Materie auch nicht bestimmt, dadurch, daß die Form ihre eigne Selbstständigkeit aufhebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"124.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0012","text":"Allein die Materie ist nur selbstständig der Form gegenüber; indem das Negative sich aufhebt, hebt sich auch das Positive auf. Indem die Form also sich aufhebt, so fällt auch die Bestimmtheit der Materie weg, welche sie gegen die Form hat, nämlich das unbestimmte Bestehen zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"124.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0013","text":"Dieß, was als Thätigkeit der Form erscheint, ist ferner ebenso sehr die eigene Bewegung der Materie selbst. Die ansichseyende Bestimmung oder das Sollen der Materie ist ihre absolute Negativität. Durch diese bezieht sich die Materie schlechthin nicht nur auf die Form als auf ein Anderes, sondern dieses Äußere ist die Form, welche sie selbst als verschlossen in sich enthält. Die Materie ist derselbe Widerspruch an sich, welchen die Form enthält, und dieser Widerspruch ist wie seine Auflösung, nur Einer. Die Materie ist aber in sich selbst widersprechend, weil sie als die unbestimmte Identität mit sich zugleich die absolute Negativität ist; sie hebt sich daher an ihr selbst auf, und ihre Identität zerfällt in ihrer Negativität, und diese erhält an jener ihr Bestehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"124.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0014","text":"Indem also die Materie von der Form als von einem Äußern bestimmt wird, so erreicht damit sie ihre Bestimmung, und die Äußerlichkeit des Verhaltens sowohl für die Form als für die Materie besteht darin, daß jede oder vielmehr ihre ursprüngliche Einheit in ihrem Setzen zugleich voraussetzend ist; wodurch die Beziehung auf sich, zugleich Beziehung auf sich als aufgehobenes oder Beziehung auf sein anderes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"124.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0015","text":"Drittens, durch diese Bewegung der Form und Matene ist ihre ursprüngliche Einheit einer Seits hergestellt, anderer Seits nunmehr eine gesetzte. Die Materie bestimmt ebensowohl sich selbst, als dieß Bestimmen ein für sie äußerliches Thun der Form ist; umgekehrt die Form bestimmt ebenso sehr nur sich oder hat die Materie, die von ihr bestimmt wird, an ihr selbst, als sie in ihrem Bestimmen sich gegen ein Anderes verhält; und beides, das Thun der Form und die Bewegung der Materie ist dasselbe, nur daß jenes ein Thun ist, d. h. die Negativität als gesetzte, dieß aber Bewegung oder Werden, die Negativität als ansichseyende Bestimmung. Das Resultat ist daher die Einheit des Ansichseyns und des Gesetztseyns. Die Materie ist als solche bestimmt, oder hat nothwendig eine Form, und die Form ist schlechthin materielle, bestehende Form.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"124.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0016","text":"Die Form, insofern sie eine Materie als das ihr Andere voraussetzt, ist endlich. Sie ist nicht Grund, sondern nur das Thätige. Ebenso ist die Materie, insofern sie die Form als ihr Nichtseyn voraussetzt, die endliche Materie, sie ist ebenso wenig Grund ihrer Einheit mit der Form, sondern nur die Grundlage für die Form. Aber sowohl diese endliche Materie als die endliche Form hat keine Wahrheit; jede bezieht sich auf die andere, oder nur ihre Einheit ist ihre Wahrheit. In diese Einheit gehen diese beiden Bestimmungen zurück, und heben darin ihre Selbstständigkeit auf; sie erweist sich damit als ihr Grund. Die Materie ist daher nur insofern Grund ihrer Formbestimmung, als sie nicht Materie als Materie, sondern die absolute Einheit des Wesens und der Form ist; ebenso die Form ist nur Grund des Bestehens ihrer Bestimmungen, insofern sie dieselbe eine Einheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"124.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0017","text":"Aber diese eine Einheit als die absolute Negativität und bestimmter als ausschließende Einheit ist in ihrer Reflexion voraussetzend; oder es ist Ein Thun, im Setzen sich als Gesetztes in der Einheit zu erhalten und sich von sich selbst abzustoßen, sich auf sich als sich, und sich auf sich als auf ein Anderes zu beziehen. Oder das Bestimmtwerden der Materie durch die Form ist die Vermittelung des Wesens als Grund mit sich in einer Einheit, durch sich selbst und durch die Negation seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"124.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0018","text":"Die formirte Materie oder die Bestehen habende Form, ist nun nicht nur jene absolute Einheit des Grundes mit sich, sondern auch die gesetzte Einheit. Die betrachtete Bewegung ist es, in welcher der absolute Grund seine Momente zugleich als sich aufhebende und somit als gesetzte dargestellt hat. Oder die wiederhergestellte Einheit hat in ihrem Zusammengehen mit sich, sich ebenso sehr von sich selbst abgestoßen und sich bestimmt; denn ihre Einheit ist als durch Negation zu Stande gekommen, auch negative Einheit. Sie ist daher die Einheit der Form und der Materie, als ihre Grundlage, aber als ihre bestimmte Grundlage, welche formirte Materie, aber gegen Form und Materie zugleich als gegen aufgehobene und unwesendiche gleichgültig ist. Sie ist der Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"124.18"}],"sha256":"1ab52eb0e17a07b7ef63b7d8715cd78f1b8ca78d0c0c925b293db039ba9bfbea","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105046999619Z_30a2db0b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Form and Matter.","source_sha256":"1ab52eb0e17a07b7ef63b7d8715cd78f1b8ca78d0c0c925b293db039ba9bfbea","sha256":"779ac839efeac6ec1c90bb123b01322b63cabbffe6541931c5a8a009c24637eb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:50:46.999665+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0001","text":"Essence becomes matter by its reflection determining itself to relate to the same as to the formless indeterminate. Matter is therefore the simple undifferentiated identity which essence is, with the determination of being the other of form. It is therefore the proper foundation or substrate of form, because it constitutes the reflection-into-self of the determinations of form, or the self-subsistent, to which they relate as to their positive subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"124.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0002","text":"When abstraction is made from all determinations, from all form of a something, indeterminate matter remains. Matter is an absolutely abstract [thing]. (—One cannot see, feel, etc., matter—what one sees and feels is determinate matter, i.e. a unity of matter and form.) Yet this abstraction, from which matter emerges, is not merely an external removal and sublation of form, but form reduces itself through itself, as has emerged, to this simple identity.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"124.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0003","text":"Further, form presupposes a matter to which it relates. But for that reason the two do not confront one another externally and contingently; neither matter nor form is from itself, or, in other words, eternal. Matter is what is indifferent to form, but this indifference is the determinacy of identity with itself, into which, as into its foundation, form returns. Form presupposes matter; precisely in that it posits itself as sublated, and thus relates to this its identity as to an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"124.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0004","text":"Conversely, form is presupposed by matter; for the latter is not the simple essence that is immediately itself absolute reflection, but is the same determined as the positive, namely as that which is only as sublated negation.—But on the other side, because form posits itself as matter only insofar as it sublates itself, and thus presupposes the same, matter too is determined as groundless subsistence. Likewise, matter is not determined as the ground of form; rather, in that matter posits itself as the abstract identity of the sublated determination of form, it is not identity as ground, and form is in this respect groundless over against it. Form and matter are thus determined, each alike, to be not posited by one another, not the ground of one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"124.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0005","text":"Matter is rather the identity of ground and grounded, as foundation, which stands opposed to this relation of form. This their common determination of indifference is the determination of matter as such, and also constitutes the relation of the two to one another. Likewise, the determination of form, to be relation as differentiated, is also the other moment of the comportment of the two towards one another.—Matter, as that determined to be indifferent, is the passive as against form as the active. Form, as the negative relating itself to itself, is the contradiction within itself, that which dissolves itself, repels itself from itself, and determines itself. It relates to matter, and is posited to relate to this its subsistence as to an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"124.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0006","text":"Matter, on the other hand, is posited to relate only to itself, and to be indifferent towards an other; but in itself it relates to form, for it contains sublated negativity, and is matter only through this determination. It relates to form merely as to an other because form is not posited in it, because it is form only in itself. It contains form enclosed within itself, and is absolute receptivity for it, only because it has form absolutely within it, because this is its determination that is in itself. Matter must therefore be formed, and form must materialize itself, must give itself identity with itself, or subsistence, in matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"124.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0007","text":"2. Form therefore determines matter, and matter is determined by form.—Because form is itself absolute identity with itself, and thus contains matter within itself; likewise because matter, in its pure abstraction or absolute negativity, has form within itself, the activity of form upon matter, and the being-determined of the latter by the former, are rather only the sublation of the semblance of their indifference and difference. This relation of determining is thus the mediation of each of the two with itself through its own non-being,—but these two mediations are one movement and the restoration of their original identity;—the recollection of their externalization.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"124.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0008","text":"At first form and matter mutually presuppose one another. As has emerged, this means that the one essential unity is negative relation to itself, and thus divides itself into essential identity, determined as the indifferent foundation, and into essential difference or negativity, as determining form. That unity of essence and form which confronts itself as form and matter is the absolute ground which determines itself. In making itself into a differentiated [thing], the relation becomes, on account of the underlying identity of the differentiated [things], reciprocal presupposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"124.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0009","text":"Secondly, form, as self-subsistent, is in any case the contradiction that sublates itself; but it is also posited as such, for it is at once self-subsistent and at once essentially related to an other;—it thus sublates itself. Since it is itself two-sided, this sublation also has the twofold side: first, it sublates its self-subsistence; it makes itself into a posited [thing], into something that is in an other, and this its other is matter. Secondly, it sublates its determinacy over against matter, and thus its relation to matter, its positedness, and thereby gives itself subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"124.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0010","text":"In that it sublates its positedness, this its reflection is the proper identity into which it passes; but in that it at the same time externalizes this identity and confronts itself as matter, that reflection of positedness into itself is union with a matter, in which it receives subsistence; in this union, therefore, it unites as much with matter as with an other,—according to the first side, that it makes itself into a posited [thing],—as it also unites therein with its own identity.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"124.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0011","text":"Thus the activity of form, whereby matter is determined, consists in a negative comportment of form towards itself. But conversely, it thereby also behaves negatively towards matter; yet this being-determined of matter is equally the proper movement of form itself. Form is free from matter, but it sublates this its self-subsistence; but its self-subsistence is matter itself, for in matter it has its essential identity. In making itself into a posited [thing], therefore, it is one and the same thing that it makes matter into a determinate [thing].—But considered from the other side, the proper identity of form is at the same time externalized, and matter is its other; insofar, matter is also not determined by form's sublating its own self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"124.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0012","text":"Yet matter is self-subsistent only over against form; in that the negative sublates itself, the positive too sublates itself. In that form therefore sublates itself, the determinacy of matter which it has over against form also falls away, namely, that of being indeterminate subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"124.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0013","text":"That which appears as activity of form is further equally the proper movement of matter itself. The determination that is in itself, or the ought, of matter is its absolute negativity. Through this, matter relates absolutely not merely to form as to an other, but this external [thing] is form, which it itself contains enclosed within itself. Matter is the same contradiction in itself that form contains, and this contradiction, as also its resolution, is only one. But matter is self-contradictory because, as indeterminate identity with itself, it is at the same time absolute negativity; it therefore sublates itself in itself, and its identity disintegrates in its negativity, and this receives its subsistence in the former.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"124.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0014","text":"In that matter is thus determined by form as by something external, it thereby attains its determination, and the externality of the relation, both for form and for matter, consists in this: that each, or rather their original unity, in its positing is at the same time presupposing; whereby relation to itself is at the same time relation to itself as sublated, or relation to its other.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"124.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0015","text":"Thirdly, through this movement of form and matter their original unity is, on the one hand, restored, and, on the other hand, is now a posited unity. Matter determines itself just as much as this determining is an activity of form external to it; conversely, form determines only itself just as much, or has the matter that is determined by it within itself, as it behaves in its determining towards an other; and both, the activity of form and the movement of matter, are the same, except that the former is an activity, i.e. negativity as posited, whereas the latter is movement or becoming, negativity as determination that is in itself. The result is therefore the unity of being-in-itself and positedness. Matter as such is determined, or necessarily has a form, and form is absolutely material, subsisting form.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"124.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0016","text":"Form, insofar as it presupposes a matter as its other, is finite. It is not ground, but only the active [element]. Likewise matter, insofar as it presupposes form as its non-being, is finite matter; it is just as little the ground of its unity with form, but only the foundation for form. But neither this finite matter nor this finite form has truth; each relates to the other, or only their unity is their truth. Into this unity these two determinations return and therein sublate their self-subsistence; it thereby proves itself to be their ground. Matter is therefore ground of its determination of form only insofar as it is not matter as matter, but the absolute unity of essence and form; likewise, form is ground of the subsistence of its determinations only insofar as it is this one unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"124.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0017","text":"But this one unity, as absolute negativity and, more determinately, as exclusive unity, is presupposing in its reflection; or it is one activity to preserve oneself in the unity, in positing, as posited, and to repel oneself from oneself, to relate to oneself as oneself, and to oneself as to an other. Or the being-determined of matter by form is the mediation of essence as ground with itself in a unity, through itself and through the negation of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"124.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0018","text":"Formed matter, or form having subsistence, is now not only that absolute unity of ground with itself, but also posited unity. The movement considered is that in which the absolute ground has at the same time exhibited its moments as self-sublating and thus as posited. Or the restored unity, in its uniting with itself, has equally repelled itself from itself and determined itself; for its unity, as having come to pass through negation, is also negative unity. It is therefore the unity of form and matter, as their foundation, but as their determinate foundation, which is formed matter, yet is indifferent, over against form and matter at once, as against sublated and inessential [things]. It is content.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"124.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BFUM:P0018"]}],"source_digest":"7e864fe04fae00ad14d541609cd8b1b39f5f41d1a908f8384184fe991433cf71","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Form und Materie."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Form und Materie.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI","title":"c. Form and Content.","order":125,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CFUI","text":"Die Form steht zuerst dem Wesen gegenüber; so ist sie Grundbeziehung überhaupt, und ihre Bestimmungen, der Grund und das Begründete. Alsdenn steht sie der Materie gegenüber; so ist sie bestimmende Reflexion und ihre Bestimmungen sind die Reflexionsbestimmung selbst und das Bestehen derselben. Endlich steht sie dem Inhalte gegenüber, so sind ihre Bestimmungen wieder sie selbst und die Materie. Was vorher das mit sich Identische war, zuerst der Grund, dann das Bestehen überhaupt, und zulezt die Materie tritt unter die Herrschaft der Form und ist wieder eine ihrer Bestimmungen.\n\nDer Inhalt hat erstlich eine Form und eine Materie, die ihm angehören und wesentlich sind; er ist ihre Einheit. Aber indem diese Einheit zugleich bestimmte oder gesetzte Einheit ist, so steht er der Form gegenüber; diese macht das Gesetztseyn aus, und ist gegen ihn das Unwesentliche. Er ist daher gleichgültig gegen sie; sie begreift sowohl die Form als solche, als auch die Materie; und er hat also eine Form und eine Materie, deren Grundlage er ausmacht, und die ihm als bloßes Gesetztseyn sind.\n\nDer Inhalt ist zweitens das in Form und Materie identische, so daß diese nur gleichgültige äußerliche Bestimmungen wären. Sie sind das Gesetztseyn überhaupt, das aber in dem Inhalte in seine Einheit oder seinen Grund zurückgegangen ist. Die Identität des Inhalts mit sich selbst ist daher das eine Mal jene gegen die Form gleichgültige Identität; das andere Mal aber ist sie die Identität des Grundes. Der Grund ist in dem Inhalte zunächst verschwunden; der Inhalt aber ist zugleich die negative Reflexion der Formbestimmungen in sich; seine Einheit, welche zunächst nur die gegen die Form gleichgültige ist, ist daher auch die formelle Einheit oder die Grundbeziehung als solche. Der Inhalt hat daher diese zu seiner wesentlichen Form und der Grund umgekehrt hat einen Inhalt.\n\nDer Inhalt des Grundes ist also der in seine Einheit mit sich zurückgekehrte Grund; der Grund ist zunächst das Wesen, das in seinem Gesetztseyn mit sich identisch ist; als verschieden und gleichgültig gegen sein Gesetztseyn, ist es die unbestimmte, die Materie; aber als Inhalt ist es zugleich die formirte Identität, und diese Form wird darum Grundbeziehung, weil die Bestimmungen ihres Gegensatzes im Inhalte auch als negirte gesetzt sind.—Der Inhalt ist ferner bestimmt an ihm selbst; nicht nur wie die Materie als das Gleichgültige überhaupt, sondern als die formirte Materie, so daß die Bestimmungen der Form ein materielles, gleichgültiges Bestehen haben. Einer Seits ist der Inhalt die wesentliche Identität des Grundes mit sich in seinem Gesetztseyn, anderer Seits die gesetzte Identität gegen die Grundbeziehung; dieß Gesetztseyn, das als Formbestimmung an dieser Identität ist, ist dem freien Gesetztseyn, das heißt, der Form als ganzer Beziehung von Grund und Begründetem, gegenüber; diese Form ist das totale in sich zurückkehrende Gesetztseyn; jene daher nur das Gesetztseyn als unmittelbares, die Bestimmtheit als solche.\n\nDer Grund hat sich damit überhaupt zum bestimmten Grunde gemacht, und die Bestimmtheit selbst ist die gedoppelte; erstens der Form und zweitens des Inhalts. Jene ist seine Bestimmtheit dem Inhalte überhaupt äußerlich zu seyn, der gegen diese Beziehung gleichgültig ist. Diese ist die Bestimmtheit des Inhalts, den der Grund hat.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0001","text":"Die Form steht zuerst dem Wesen gegenüber; so ist sie Grundbeziehung überhaupt, und ihre Bestimmungen, der Grund und das Begründete. Alsdenn steht sie der Materie gegenüber; so ist sie bestimmende Reflexion und ihre Bestimmungen sind die Reflexionsbestimmung selbst und das Bestehen derselben. Endlich steht sie dem Inhalte gegenüber, so sind ihre Bestimmungen wieder sie selbst und die Materie. Was vorher das mit sich Identische war, zuerst der Grund, dann das Bestehen überhaupt, und zulezt die Materie tritt unter die Herrschaft der Form und ist wieder eine ihrer Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"125.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0002","text":"Der Inhalt hat erstlich eine Form und eine Materie, die ihm angehören und wesentlich sind; er ist ihre Einheit. Aber indem diese Einheit zugleich bestimmte oder gesetzte Einheit ist, so steht er der Form gegenüber; diese macht das Gesetztseyn aus, und ist gegen ihn das Unwesentliche. Er ist daher gleichgültig gegen sie; sie begreift sowohl die Form als solche, als auch die Materie; und er hat also eine Form und eine Materie, deren Grundlage er ausmacht, und die ihm als bloßes Gesetztseyn sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"125.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0003","text":"Der Inhalt ist zweitens das in Form und Materie identische, so daß diese nur gleichgültige äußerliche Bestimmungen wären. Sie sind das Gesetztseyn überhaupt, das aber in dem Inhalte in seine Einheit oder seinen Grund zurückgegangen ist. Die Identität des Inhalts mit sich selbst ist daher das eine Mal jene gegen die Form gleichgültige Identität; das andere Mal aber ist sie die Identität des Grundes. Der Grund ist in dem Inhalte zunächst verschwunden; der Inhalt aber ist zugleich die negative Reflexion der Formbestimmungen in sich; seine Einheit, welche zunächst nur die gegen die Form gleichgültige ist, ist daher auch die formelle Einheit oder die Grundbeziehung als solche. Der Inhalt hat daher diese zu seiner wesentlichen Form und der Grund umgekehrt hat einen Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"125.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0004","text":"Der Inhalt des Grundes ist also der in seine Einheit mit sich zurückgekehrte Grund; der Grund ist zunächst das Wesen, das in seinem Gesetztseyn mit sich identisch ist; als verschieden und gleichgültig gegen sein Gesetztseyn, ist es die unbestimmte, die Materie; aber als Inhalt ist es zugleich die formirte Identität, und diese Form wird darum Grundbeziehung, weil die Bestimmungen ihres Gegensatzes im Inhalte auch als negirte gesetzt sind.—Der Inhalt ist ferner bestimmt an ihm selbst; nicht nur wie die Materie als das Gleichgültige überhaupt, sondern als die formirte Materie, so daß die Bestimmungen der Form ein materielles, gleichgültiges Bestehen haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"125.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0005","text":"Einer Seits ist der Inhalt die wesentliche Identität des Grundes mit sich in seinem Gesetztseyn, anderer Seits die gesetzte Identität gegen die Grundbeziehung; dieß Gesetztseyn, das als Formbestimmung an dieser Identität ist, ist dem freien Gesetztseyn, das heißt, der Form als ganzer Beziehung von Grund und Begründetem, gegenüber; diese Form ist das totale in sich zurückkehrende Gesetztseyn; jene daher nur das Gesetztseyn als unmittelbares, die Bestimmtheit als solche.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"125.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0006","text":"Der Grund hat sich damit überhaupt zum bestimmten Grunde gemacht, und die Bestimmtheit selbst ist die gedoppelte; erstens der Form und zweitens des Inhalts. Jene ist seine Bestimmtheit dem Inhalte überhaupt äußerlich zu seyn, der gegen diese Beziehung gleichgültig ist. Diese ist die Bestimmtheit des Inhalts, den der Grund hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"125.6"}],"sha256":"6143050fd48e8779ca509973a19551f8374725439e3b6d4fb37887ea70305e69","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105054800488Z_7430cea2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Form and Content.","source_sha256":"6143050fd48e8779ca509973a19551f8374725439e3b6d4fb37887ea70305e69","sha256":"ac00ec7cf43fac6699813e2940830a5ce74b0c36dff01aaba2f48bfc9ed43a5e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:50:54.800553+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0001","text":"Form first stands opposed to essence; thus it is the relation of ground in general, and its determinations are the ground and the grounded. Then it stands opposed to matter; thus it is determining reflection, and its determinations are the determination of reflection itself and the subsistence of the latter. Finally it stands opposed to content; thus its determinations are again itself and matter. What previously was that which is identical with itself—first the ground, then subsistence in general, and finally matter—comes under the dominion of form and is again one of its determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"125.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0002","text":"Content has, first, a form and a matter that belong to it and are essential to it; it is their unity. But inasmuch as this unity is at the same time determinate or posited unity, it stands opposed to form; this constitutes positedness and is the unessential in relation to it. Content is therefore indifferent to it; it comprehends both form as such and matter; and it thus has a form and a matter whose foundation it constitutes, and which are for it mere positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"125.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0003","text":"Secondly, content is that which is identical in form and matter, so that these would be merely indifferent external determinations. They are positedness in general, which, however, has returned in content into its unity or its ground. The identity of content with itself is therefore, on the one hand, that identity indifferent to form; on the other hand, however, it is the identity of ground. The ground has at first disappeared in content; but content is at the same time the negative reflection of the determinations of form into itself; its unity, which at first is only that indifferent to form, is therefore also formal unity, or the relation of ground as such. Content therefore has this as its essential form, and conversely the ground has a content.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"125.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0004","text":"The content of the ground is thus the ground returned into its unity with itself; the ground is at first essence that is identical with itself in its positedness; as distinct from, and indifferent to, its positedness, it is the indeterminate, matter; but as content it is at the same time formed identity, and this form therefore becomes the relation of ground, because the determinations of its opposition are also posited in content as negated.—Content is further determined in itself; not merely like matter as the indifferent in general, but as formed matter, so that the determinations of form have a material, indifferent subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"125.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0005","text":"On the one side, content is the essential identity of the ground with itself in its positedness; on the other side, the posited identity as against the relation of ground; this positedness, which is a determination of form in this identity, stands opposed to free positedness, that is, to form as the whole relation of ground and grounded; this form is total positedness returning into itself; that former positedness is therefore only positedness as immediate, determinateness as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"125.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0006","text":"The ground has thereby in general made itself into determinate ground, and determinateness itself is twofold: first, that of form, and second, that of content. The former is its determinateness of being external to content in general, which is indifferent to this relation. The latter is the determinateness of the content that the ground has.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"125.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CFUI:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"b6ab30b518994fa58323bcbf47f77e2e38fc8ed74b61bd675a93eff298fc34e8","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Form und Inhalt."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Form und Inhalt.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0","title":"a. Formal Ground.","order":126,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DFG0","text":"## B. Der bestimmte Grund.\n\n## a. Der formelle Grund.\n\nDer Grund hat einen bestimmten Inhalt. Die Bestimmtheit des Inhalts ist, wie sich ergeben, die Grundlage für die Form; das einfache Unmittelbare gegen die Vermittelung der Form. Der Grund ist negativ sich auf sich beziehende Identität, welche sich dadurch zum Gesetztseyn macht; sie bezieht sich negativ auf sich, indem sie identisch in dieser ihrer Negativität mit sich ist; diese Identität ist die Grundlage oder der Inhalt der auf diese Weise die gleichgültige oder positive Einheit der Grundbeziehung ausmacht, und das Vermittelnde derselben ist.\n\nIn diesem Inhalte ist zunächst die Bestimmtheit des Grundes und des Begründeten gegen einander verschwunden. Die Vermittelung ist aber ferner negative Einheit. Das Negative als an jener gleichgültigen Grundlage ist die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit derselben, wodurch der Grund einen bestimmten Inhalt hat. Alsdann aber ist das Negative die negative Beziehung der Form auf sich selbst. Das Gesetzte einer Seits liebt sich selbst auf und geht in seinen Grund zurück; der Grund aber, die wesentliche Selbstständigkeit, bezieht sich negativ auf sich selbst und macht sich zum Gesetzten. Diese negative Vermittelung des Grundes und des Begründeten ist die eigenthümliche Vermittelung der Form als solcher, die formelle Vermittelung. Die beiden Seiten der Form nun, weil die eine in die andere übergeht, setzen sich damit gemeinschaftlich in Einer Identität als aufgehobene; sie setzen dieselbe hierdurch zugleich voraus. Sie ist der bestimmte Inhalt, auf den sich also die formelle Vermittelung als auf das positive Vermittelnde durch sich selbst bezieht. Er ist das Identische beider, und indem sie unterschieden, jedes aber in seinem Unterschiede die Beziehung auf das andere ist, ist er das Bestehen derselben, eines jeden als das Ganze selbst.\n\nHiernach ergiebt sich, daß im bestimmten Grunde dieß vorhanden ist; erstens, ein bestimmter Inhalt wird nach zwei Seiten betrachtet, das eine Mal insofern er als Grund, das andere Mal insofern er als Begründetes gesetzt ist. Er selbst ist gleichgültig gegen diese Form; er ist in beiden überhaupt nur Eine Bestimmung. Zweitens ist der Grund selbst so sehr Moment der Form als das durch ihn gesetzte; dieß ist ihre Identität der Form nach. Es ist gleichgültig, welche von beiden Bestimmungen zum Ersten gemacht wird, von dem als dem Gesetzten zum Andern als zum Grunde, oder von dem als dem Grunde zum Andern als zum Gesetzten übergegangen wird. Das Begründete für sich betrachtet, ist das Aufheben seiner selbst; damit macht es sich einer Seits zum Gesetzten, und ist zugleich Setzen des Grundes. Dieselbe Bewegung ist der Grund als solcher, er macht sich zum Gesetzten, dadurch wird er Grund von etwas, das heißt, darin ist er sowohl als Gesetztes, wie auch erst als Grund vorhanden. Daß ein Grund ist, davon ist das Gesetzte der Grund, und umgekehrt ist hiermit der Grund Gesetztes. Die Vermittelung fängt ebenso sehr von dem einen als von dem andern an, jede Seite ist so sehr Grund als Gesetztes, und jede die ganze Vermittelung oder die ganze Form.—Diese ganze Form ist ferner selbst als das mit sich identische, die Grundlage der Bestimmungen, welche die beiden Seiten des Grundes und des Begründeten sind, Form und Inhalt sind so selbst eine und dieselbe Identität.\n\nUm dieser Identität des Grundes und Begründeten willen, sowohl dem Inhalte als der Form nach, ist der Grund zureichend (das Zureichende auf dieß Verhältniß eingeschränkt); es ist nichts im Grunde, was nicht im Begründeten ist, so wie nichts im Begründeten, was nicht im Grunde ist. Wenn nach einem Grunde gefragt wird, will man dieselbe Bestimmung, die der Inhalt ist, doppelt sehen, das eine Mal in der Form des Gesetzten, das andere Mal in der des in sich reflektirten Daseyns, der Wesentlichkeit.\n\nInsofern nun im bestimmten Grunde Grund und Begründetes beide die ganze Form, und ihr Inhalt zwar ein bestimmter, aber einer und derselbe ist, so ist der Grund in seinen beiden Seiten noch nicht real bestimmt, sie haben keinen verschiedenen Inhalt; die Bestimmtheit ist erst einfache, noch nicht an die Seiten übergegangene Bestimmtheit; es ist der bestimmte Grund erst in seiner reinen Form, der formelle Grund, vorhanden.—Weil der Inhalt nur diese einfache Bestimmtheit ist, die nicht die Form der Grundbeziehung an ihr selbst hat, so ist sie der mit sich identische Inhalt, gegen die Form gleichgültig und diese ihm äußerlich; er ist ein Anderes als sie.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0001","text":"## B. Der bestimmte Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"126.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0002","text":"## a. Der formelle Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"126.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0003","text":"Der Grund hat einen bestimmten Inhalt. Die Bestimmtheit des Inhalts ist, wie sich ergeben, die Grundlage für die Form; das einfache Unmittelbare gegen die Vermittelung der Form. Der Grund ist negativ sich auf sich beziehende Identität, welche sich dadurch zum Gesetztseyn macht; sie bezieht sich negativ auf sich, indem sie identisch in dieser ihrer Negativität mit sich ist; diese Identität ist die Grundlage oder der Inhalt der auf diese Weise die gleichgültige oder positive Einheit der Grundbeziehung ausmacht, und das Vermittelnde derselben ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"126.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0004","text":"In diesem Inhalte ist zunächst die Bestimmtheit des Grundes und des Begründeten gegen einander verschwunden. Die Vermittelung ist aber ferner negative Einheit. Das Negative als an jener gleichgültigen Grundlage ist die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit derselben, wodurch der Grund einen bestimmten Inhalt hat. Alsdann aber ist das Negative die negative Beziehung der Form auf sich selbst. Das Gesetzte einer Seits liebt sich selbst auf und geht in seinen Grund zurück; der Grund aber, die wesentliche Selbstständigkeit, bezieht sich negativ auf sich selbst und macht sich zum Gesetzten. Diese negative Vermittelung des Grundes und des Begründeten ist die eigenthümliche Vermittelung der Form als solcher, die formelle Vermittelung.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"126.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0005","text":"Die beiden Seiten der Form nun, weil die eine in die andere übergeht, setzen sich damit gemeinschaftlich in Einer Identität als aufgehobene; sie setzen dieselbe hierdurch zugleich voraus. Sie ist der bestimmte Inhalt, auf den sich also die formelle Vermittelung als auf das positive Vermittelnde durch sich selbst bezieht. Er ist das Identische beider, und indem sie unterschieden, jedes aber in seinem Unterschiede die Beziehung auf das andere ist, ist er das Bestehen derselben, eines jeden als das Ganze selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"126.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0006","text":"Hiernach ergiebt sich, daß im bestimmten Grunde dieß vorhanden ist; erstens, ein bestimmter Inhalt wird nach zwei Seiten betrachtet, das eine Mal insofern er als Grund, das andere Mal insofern er als Begründetes gesetzt ist. Er selbst ist gleichgültig gegen diese Form; er ist in beiden überhaupt nur Eine Bestimmung. Zweitens ist der Grund selbst so sehr Moment der Form als das durch ihn gesetzte; dieß ist ihre Identität der Form nach. Es ist gleichgültig, welche von beiden Bestimmungen zum Ersten gemacht wird, von dem als dem Gesetzten zum Andern als zum Grunde, oder von dem als dem Grunde zum Andern als zum Gesetzten übergegangen wird. Das Begründete für sich betrachtet, ist das Aufheben seiner selbst; damit macht es sich einer Seits zum Gesetzten, und ist zugleich Setzen des Grundes.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"126.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0007","text":"Dieselbe Bewegung ist der Grund als solcher, er macht sich zum Gesetzten, dadurch wird er Grund von etwas, das heißt, darin ist er sowohl als Gesetztes, wie auch erst als Grund vorhanden. Daß ein Grund ist, davon ist das Gesetzte der Grund, und umgekehrt ist hiermit der Grund Gesetztes. Die Vermittelung fängt ebenso sehr von dem einen als von dem andern an, jede Seite ist so sehr Grund als Gesetztes, und jede die ganze Vermittelung oder die ganze Form.—Diese ganze Form ist ferner selbst als das mit sich identische, die Grundlage der Bestimmungen, welche die beiden Seiten des Grundes und des Begründeten sind, Form und Inhalt sind so selbst eine und dieselbe Identität.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"126.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0008","text":"Um dieser Identität des Grundes und Begründeten willen, sowohl dem Inhalte als der Form nach, ist der Grund zureichend (das Zureichende auf dieß Verhältniß eingeschränkt); es ist nichts im Grunde, was nicht im Begründeten ist, so wie nichts im Begründeten, was nicht im Grunde ist. Wenn nach einem Grunde gefragt wird, will man dieselbe Bestimmung, die der Inhalt ist, doppelt sehen, das eine Mal in der Form des Gesetzten, das andere Mal in der des in sich reflektirten Daseyns, der Wesentlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"126.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0009","text":"Insofern nun im bestimmten Grunde Grund und Begründetes beide die ganze Form, und ihr Inhalt zwar ein bestimmter, aber einer und derselbe ist, so ist der Grund in seinen beiden Seiten noch nicht real bestimmt, sie haben keinen verschiedenen Inhalt; die Bestimmtheit ist erst einfache, noch nicht an die Seiten übergegangene Bestimmtheit; es ist der bestimmte Grund erst in seiner reinen Form, der formelle Grund, vorhanden.—Weil der Inhalt nur diese einfache Bestimmtheit ist, die nicht die Form der Grundbeziehung an ihr selbst hat, so ist sie der mit sich identische Inhalt, gegen die Form gleichgültig und diese ihm äußerlich; er ist ein Anderes als sie.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"126.9"}],"sha256":"c6f5ca1847448e3cd5150e81214ef60d185f827344f6c78435cafea802241f9a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105104744584Z_b8c4929e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Formal Ground.","source_sha256":"c6f5ca1847448e3cd5150e81214ef60d185f827344f6c78435cafea802241f9a","sha256":"5a73d0ca35456bf785f0856590709280ee44198cafe613ad000084ca1253a2f0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:51:04.744605+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0001","text":"## B. The determinate ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"126.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0002","text":"## a. The formal ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"126.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0003","text":"The ground has a determinate content. The determinacy of the content is, as will emerge, the foundation for the form; the simple immediate as against the mediation of the form. The ground is negatively self-relating identity, which thereby makes itself into positedness; it relates negatively to itself in that it is identical with itself in this its negativity; this identity is the foundation or the content which in this way constitutes the indifferent or positive unity of the ground-relation, and is its mediating term.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"126.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0004","text":"In this content, the determinacy of the ground and of the grounded has at first vanished as against one another. But the mediation is further negative unity. The negative, as belonging to that indifferent foundation, is its immediate determinacy, whereby the ground has a determinate content. But then the negative is the negative relation of form to itself. The posited, on the one hand, sublates itself and returns into its ground; but the ground, essential self-subsistence, relates negatively to itself and makes itself into the posited. This negative mediation of the ground and the grounded is the peculiar mediation of form as such, formal mediation.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"126.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0005","text":"Now, since the two sides of form, because the one passes over into the other, thereby jointly posit themselves in One identity as sublated, they simultaneously presuppose it thereby. It is the determinate content to which formal mediation thus relates, as to the positive mediating term through itself. It is the identical element of both; and since they are distinct, yet each in its distinction is the relation to the other, it is their subsistence, of each as the whole itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"126.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0006","text":"Accordingly, it emerges that in the determinate ground this is present: first, a determinate content is considered from two sides, on the one occasion insofar as it is posited as ground, on the other insofar as it is posited as grounded. It itself is indifferent to this form; in both it is in general only One determination. Secondly, the ground itself is as much a moment of form as that which is posited by it; this is their identity according to form. It is indifferent which of the two determinations is made the first, from which, as the posited, one proceeds to the other as ground, or from which, as ground, one proceeds to the other as posited. The grounded, considered for itself, is the sublation of itself; thereby it makes itself, on the one hand, into the posited, and is at the same time the positing of the ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"126.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0007","text":"The same movement is the ground as such: it makes itself into the posited; thereby it becomes the ground of something, that is, in this it is present both as posited and, equally, only then as ground. That there is a ground—the posited is the ground of this; and conversely, the ground is thereby posited. Mediation begins as much from the one as from the other; each side is as much ground as posited, and each is the entire mediation or the entire form.—This entire form is further itself, as that which is identical with itself, the foundation of the determinations which are the two sides of the ground and the grounded; form and content are thus themselves one and the same identity.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"126.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0008","text":"By virtue of this identity of ground and grounded, both according to content and according to form, the ground is sufficient (the sufficient restricted to this relation); there is nothing in the ground which is not in the grounded, just as there is nothing in the grounded which is not in the ground. When one asks after a ground, one wishes to see the same determination, which is the content, twice: on the one occasion in the form of the posited, on the other in that of existence reflected into itself, of essentiality.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"126.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0009","text":"Now insofar as, in the determinate ground, ground and grounded both are the whole form, and their content is indeed a determinate one, but one and the same, the ground is not yet really determinate in its two sides; they have no different content; determinacy is as yet simple determinacy, not yet determinacy that has passed over into the sides; the determinate ground is present only in its pure form, as formal ground.—Because the content is only this simple determinacy, which does not have in itself the form of the ground-relation, it is content identical with itself, indifferent to form, and form is external to it; it is an Other than form.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"126.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFG0:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"0dfe053132d93ef828781ab6a6f45c95c536f36d4d52dcd4bd230bd45587dc80","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Der formelle Grund."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Der formelle Grund.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35","title":"Remark.","order":127,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_35","text":"Wenn die Reflexion über bestimmte Gründe sich an diejenige Form des Grundes hält, welche sich hier ergeben hat, so bleibt die Angabe eines Grundes ein bloßer Formalismus und leere Tautologie, welche denselben Inhalt in der Form der Reflexion in sich, der Wesentlichkeit, ausdrückt, der schon in der Form des unmittelbaren, als gesetzt betrachteten Daseyns vorhanden ist. Ein solches Angeben von Gründen ist deswegen von derselben Leerheit begleitet, als das Reden nach dem Satze der Identität. Die Wissenschaften, vornemlich die physikalischen, sind mit den Tautologien dieser Art angefüllt, welche gleichsam ein Vorrecht der Wissenschaft ausmachen.—Es wird z. B. als der Grund, daß die Planeten sich um die Sonne bewegen, die anziehende Kraft der Erde und Sonne gegen einander angegeben. Es ist damit dem Inhalt nach nichts Anders ausgesprochen, als was das Phänomen, nämlich die Beziehung dieser Körper auf einander in ihrer Bewegung, enthält, nur in der Form von in sich reflektirter Bestimmung, von Kraft. Wenn danach gefragt wird, was die anziehende Kraft für eine Kraft sey, so ist die Antwort, daß sie die Kraft ist, welche macht, daß sich die Erde um die Sonne bewegt; das heißt, sie hat durchaus denselben Inhalt, als das Daseyn, dessen Grund sie seyn soll; die Beziehung der Erde und der Sonne in Rüksicht der Bewegung ist die identische Grundlage des Grundes und des Begründeten.—Wenn eine Krystallisationsform dadurch erklärt wird, daß sie ihren Grund in dem besondern Arrangement habe, in das die Molecules zu einander treten, so ist die daseyende Krystallisation dieß Arrangement selbst, welches als Grund ausgedrückt wird. Im gewöhnlichen Leben gelten diese Ätiologieen, auf welche die Wissenschaften das Privilegium haben, für das, was sie sind, für ein tautologisches, leeres Gerede. Wenn auf die Frage, warum dieser Mensch in die Stadt reise, der Grund angegeben wird, weil in der Stadt sich eine anziehende Kraft befinde, die ihn dahin treibe, so gilt diese Art des Antwortens für abgeschmackt, die in den Wissenschaften sanctionirt ist.—Leibnitz warf der newtonischen anziehenden Kraft vor, daß sie eine solche verborgene Qualität sey, als die Scholastiker zum Behuf des Erklärens gebrauchten. Man müßte ihr eher das Gegentheil zum Vorwurf machen, daß sie eine zu bekannte Qualität sey; denn sie hat keinen andern Inhalt, als die Erscheinung selbst.—Wodurch sich diese Erklärungsweise eben empfiehlt, ist ihre große Deutlichkeit und Begreiflichkeit; denn es ist nichts deutlicher und begreiflicher, als daß z. E. eine Pflanze ihren Grund in einer vegetativen, d. h. Pflanzen hervorbringenden Kraft habe.—Eine occulte Qualität könnte sie nur in dem Sinne genannt werden, als der Grund einen andern Inhalt haben soll, als das zu Erklärende; ein solcher ist nicht angegeben; insofern ist jene zum Erklären gebrauchte Kraft allerdings ein verborgener Grund, als ein Grund, wie er gefordert wird, nicht angegeben ist. Es wird durch diesen Formalismus so wenig etwas erklärt, als die Natur einer Pflanze erkannt wird, wenn ich sage, daß sie eine Pflanze ist; bei aller Deutlichkeit dieses Satzes, oder daß sie ihren Grund in einer Pflanzen hervorbringenden Kraft habe, kann man dieß deswegen eine sehr occulte Erklärungsweise nennen.\n\nZweitens, der Form nach, kommen in dieser Erklärungsweise die beiden entgegengesetzten Richtungen der Grundbeziehung vor, ohne in ihrem bestimmten Verhältnisse erkannt zu seyn. Der Grund ist eines Theils Grund, als die in sich reflektirte Inhaltsbestimmung des Daseyns, das er begründet, andern Theils ist er das Gesetzte. Er ist das, woraus das Daseyn begriffen werden soll; umgekehrt aber wird von diesem auf ihn geschlossen und er aus dem Daseyn begriffen. Das Hauptgeschäfte dieser Reflexion besteht nämlich darin, aus dem Daseyn die Gründe zu finden, das heißt, das unmittelbare Daseyn in die Form des Reflektirtseyns umzusetzen; der Grund statt an und für sich und selbstständig zu seyn, ist somit vielmehr das Gesetzte und Abgeleitete. Weil er nun durch dieß Verfahren nach dem Phänomen eingerichtet ist, und seine Bestimmungen auf diesem beruhen, so fließt dieses freilich ganz glatt und mit günstigem Winde aus seinem Grunde aus. Aber die Erkenntniß ist hierdurch nicht vom Flecke gekommen; sie treibt sich in einem Unterschiede der Form herum, den dieß Verfahren selbst umkehrt und aufhebt. Eine der Hauptschwierigkeiten, sich in die Wissenschaften einzustudiren, worin dieß Verfahren herrschend ist, beruht deswegen auf dieser Verkehrtheit der Stellung, das als Grund vorauszuschicken, was in der That abgeleitet ist und indem zu den Folgen fortgegangen wird, in ihnen in der That erst den Grund jener seyn sollenden Gründe anzugeben. Es wird in der Darstellung mit den Gründen angefangen, sie werden als Principien und erste Begriffe in die Luft hingestellt; sie sind einfache Bestimmungen, ohne alle Nothwendigkeit an und für sich selbst; das Folgende soll auf sie gegründet werden. Wer daher in dergleichen Wissenschaften eindringen will, muß damit anfangen, sich jene Gründe zu inkulkiren; ein Geschäft, das der Vernunft sauer ankommt, weil sie Grundloses als Grundlage gelten lassen soll. Am besten kommt derjenige fort, der sich ohne vieles Nachdenken die Principien als gegebene gefallen läßt, und sie von nun an als Grundregeln seines Verstandes gebraucht. Ohne diese Methode kann man den Anfang nicht gewinnen; ebenso wenig läßt sich ohne sie ein Fortgang machen. Dieser aber hindert sich nun dadurch, daß in ihnen der Gegenstoß der Methode zum Vorschein kommt, die im Folgenden das Abgeleitete aufzeigen will, das aber in der That erst die Gründe zu jenen Voraussetzungen enthält. Ferner weil das Folgende sich als das Daseyn zeigt, aus welchem der Grund abgeleitet wurde, so giebt dieß Verhältniß, in dem das Phänomen aufgeführt wird, ein Mißtrauen gegen die Darstellung desselben; denn es zeigt sich nicht in seiner Unmittelbarkeit ausgedrückt, sondern als Beleg des Grundes. Weil aber dieser hinwieder aus jenem hergeleitet ist, verlangt man es vielmehr in seiner Unmittelbarkeit zu sehen, um den Grund aus ihm beurtheilen zu können. Man weiß daher in solcher Darstellung, worin das eigentlich Begründende als Abgeleitetes vorkommt, nicht, weder wie man mit dem Grunde, noch wie man mit dem Phänomen daran ist. Die Ungewißheit wird dadurch vermehrt, besonders wenn der Vortrag nicht streng konsequent, sondern mehr ehrlich ist, daß sich allenthalben Spuren und Umstände des Phänomens verrathen, die auf Mehreres und oft ganz Anderes hindeuten, als bloß in den Principien enthalten ist. Die Verwirrung wird endlich noch größer, indem reflektirte, und bloß hypothetische Bestimmungen mit unmittelbaren Bestimmungen des Phänomens selbst vermischt werden, wenn jene auf eine Art ausgesprochen sind, als ob sie der unmittelbaren Erfahrung angehörten. So kann wohl mancher, der mit ehrlichem Glauben zu diesen Wissenschaften hinzutritt, der Meinung seyn, die Molecules, die leeren Zwischenräume, die Fliehkraft, der Äther, der vereinzelnte Lichtstrahl, die elektrische, magnetische Materie und noch eine Menge dergleichen seyen Dinge oder Verhältnisse, die, nach der Art, wie von ihnen als unmittelbaren Daseynsbestimmungen gesprochen wird, in der That in der Wahrnehmung vorhanden seyen. Sie dienen als erste Gründe für Anderes, wer den als Wirklichkeiten ausgesprochen, und zuversichtlich angewendet; man läßt sie auf guten Glauben hin dafür gelten, ehe man inne wird, daß sie vielmehr aus dem, was sie begründen sollen, geschlossene Bestimmungen, von einer unkritischen Reflexion abgeleitete Hypothesen und Erdichtungen sind. In der That befindet man sich in einer Art von Hexenkreise, worin Bestimmungen des Daseyns und Bestimmungen der Reflexion, Grund und Begründetes, Phänomene und Phantome in unausgeschiedener Gesellschaft durch einander laufen und gleichen Rang mit einander geniessen.\n\nBei dem formellen Geschäfte dieser Erklärungsweise aus Gründen, hört man zugleich auch wieder, alles Erklärens aus den wohlbekannten Kräften und Materien ungeachtet, sagen, daß wir das innre Wesen dieser Kräfte und Materien selbst nicht kennen. Es ist hierin nur das Geständniß zu sehen, daß dieses Begründen sich selbst völlig ungenügend ist; daß es selbst etwas ganz Anderes fordere, als solche Gründe. Es ist dann nur nicht abzusehen, wozu sich denn diese Bemühung mit diesem Erklären gemacht, warum nicht das Andere gesucht, oder jenes Erklären wenigstens bei Seite gethan, und bei den einfachen Thatsachen stehen geblieben wird.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0001","text":"Wenn die Reflexion über bestimmte Gründe sich an diejenige Form des Grundes hält, welche sich hier ergeben hat, so bleibt die Angabe eines Grundes ein bloßer Formalismus und leere Tautologie, welche denselben Inhalt in der Form der Reflexion in sich, der Wesentlichkeit, ausdrückt, der schon in der Form des unmittelbaren, als gesetzt betrachteten Daseyns vorhanden ist. Ein solches Angeben von Gründen ist deswegen von derselben Leerheit begleitet, als das Reden nach dem Satze der Identität. Die Wissenschaften, vornemlich die physikalischen, sind mit den Tautologien dieser Art angefüllt, welche gleichsam ein Vorrecht der Wissenschaft ausmachen.—Es wird z. B. als der Grund, daß die Planeten sich um die Sonne bewegen, die anziehende Kraft der Erde und Sonne gegen einander angegeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"127.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0002","text":"Es ist damit dem Inhalt nach nichts Anders ausgesprochen, als was das Phänomen, nämlich die Beziehung dieser Körper auf einander in ihrer Bewegung, enthält, nur in der Form von in sich reflektirter Bestimmung, von Kraft. Wenn danach gefragt wird, was die anziehende Kraft für eine Kraft sey, so ist die Antwort, daß sie die Kraft ist, welche macht, daß sich die Erde um die Sonne bewegt; das heißt, sie hat durchaus denselben Inhalt, als das Daseyn, dessen Grund sie seyn soll; die Beziehung der Erde und der Sonne in Rüksicht der Bewegung ist die identische Grundlage des Grundes und des Begründeten.—Wenn eine Krystallisationsform dadurch erklärt wird, daß sie ihren Grund in dem besondern Arrangement habe, in das die Molecules zu einander treten, so ist die daseyende Krystallisation dieß Arrangement selbst, welches als Grund ausgedrückt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"127.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0003","text":"Im gewöhnlichen Leben gelten diese Ätiologieen, auf welche die Wissenschaften das Privilegium haben, für das, was sie sind, für ein tautologisches, leeres Gerede. Wenn auf die Frage, warum dieser Mensch in die Stadt reise, der Grund angegeben wird, weil in der Stadt sich eine anziehende Kraft befinde, die ihn dahin treibe, so gilt diese Art des Antwortens für abgeschmackt, die in den Wissenschaften sanctionirt ist.—Leibnitz warf der newtonischen anziehenden Kraft vor, daß sie eine solche verborgene Qualität sey, als die Scholastiker zum Behuf des Erklärens gebrauchten. Man müßte ihr eher das Gegentheil zum Vorwurf machen, daß sie eine zu bekannte Qualität sey; denn sie hat keinen andern Inhalt, als die Erscheinung selbst.—Wodurch sich diese Erklärungsweise eben empfiehlt, ist ihre große Deutlichkeit und Begreiflichkeit; denn es ist nichts deutlicher und begreiflicher, als daß z. E.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"127.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0004","text":"eine Pflanze ihren Grund in einer vegetativen, d. h. Pflanzen hervorbringenden Kraft habe.—Eine occulte Qualität könnte sie nur in dem Sinne genannt werden, als der Grund einen andern Inhalt haben soll, als das zu Erklärende; ein solcher ist nicht angegeben; insofern ist jene zum Erklären gebrauchte Kraft allerdings ein verborgener Grund, als ein Grund, wie er gefordert wird, nicht angegeben ist. Es wird durch diesen Formalismus so wenig etwas erklärt, als die Natur einer Pflanze erkannt wird, wenn ich sage, daß sie eine Pflanze ist; bei aller Deutlichkeit dieses Satzes, oder daß sie ihren Grund in einer Pflanzen hervorbringenden Kraft habe, kann man dieß deswegen eine sehr occulte Erklärungsweise nennen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"127.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0005","text":"Zweitens, der Form nach, kommen in dieser Erklärungsweise die beiden entgegengesetzten Richtungen der Grundbeziehung vor, ohne in ihrem bestimmten Verhältnisse erkannt zu seyn. Der Grund ist eines Theils Grund, als die in sich reflektirte Inhaltsbestimmung des Daseyns, das er begründet, andern Theils ist er das Gesetzte. Er ist das, woraus das Daseyn begriffen werden soll; umgekehrt aber wird von diesem auf ihn geschlossen und er aus dem Daseyn begriffen. Das Hauptgeschäfte dieser Reflexion besteht nämlich darin, aus dem Daseyn die Gründe zu finden, das heißt, das unmittelbare Daseyn in die Form des Reflektirtseyns umzusetzen; der Grund statt an und für sich und selbstständig zu seyn, ist somit vielmehr das Gesetzte und Abgeleitete.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"127.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0006","text":"Weil er nun durch dieß Verfahren nach dem Phänomen eingerichtet ist, und seine Bestimmungen auf diesem beruhen, so fließt dieses freilich ganz glatt und mit günstigem Winde aus seinem Grunde aus. Aber die Erkenntniß ist hierdurch nicht vom Flecke gekommen; sie treibt sich in einem Unterschiede der Form herum, den dieß Verfahren selbst umkehrt und aufhebt. Eine der Hauptschwierigkeiten, sich in die Wissenschaften einzustudiren, worin dieß Verfahren herrschend ist, beruht deswegen auf dieser Verkehrtheit der Stellung, das als Grund vorauszuschicken, was in der That abgeleitet ist und indem zu den Folgen fortgegangen wird, in ihnen in der That erst den Grund jener seyn sollenden Gründe anzugeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"127.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0007","text":"Es wird in der Darstellung mit den Gründen angefangen, sie werden als Principien und erste Begriffe in die Luft hingestellt; sie sind einfache Bestimmungen, ohne alle Nothwendigkeit an und für sich selbst; das Folgende soll auf sie gegründet werden. Wer daher in dergleichen Wissenschaften eindringen will, muß damit anfangen, sich jene Gründe zu inkulkiren; ein Geschäft, das der Vernunft sauer ankommt, weil sie Grundloses als Grundlage gelten lassen soll. Am besten kommt derjenige fort, der sich ohne vieles Nachdenken die Principien als gegebene gefallen läßt, und sie von nun an als Grundregeln seines Verstandes gebraucht. Ohne diese Methode kann man den Anfang nicht gewinnen; ebenso wenig läßt sich ohne sie ein Fortgang machen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"127.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0008","text":"Dieser aber hindert sich nun dadurch, daß in ihnen der Gegenstoß der Methode zum Vorschein kommt, die im Folgenden das Abgeleitete aufzeigen will, das aber in der That erst die Gründe zu jenen Voraussetzungen enthält. Ferner weil das Folgende sich als das Daseyn zeigt, aus welchem der Grund abgeleitet wurde, so giebt dieß Verhältniß, in dem das Phänomen aufgeführt wird, ein Mißtrauen gegen die Darstellung desselben; denn es zeigt sich nicht in seiner Unmittelbarkeit ausgedrückt, sondern als Beleg des Grundes. Weil aber dieser hinwieder aus jenem hergeleitet ist, verlangt man es vielmehr in seiner Unmittelbarkeit zu sehen, um den Grund aus ihm beurtheilen zu können. Man weiß daher in solcher Darstellung, worin das eigentlich Begründende als Abgeleitetes vorkommt, nicht, weder wie man mit dem Grunde, noch wie man mit dem Phänomen daran ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"127.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0009","text":"Die Ungewißheit wird dadurch vermehrt, besonders wenn der Vortrag nicht streng konsequent, sondern mehr ehrlich ist, daß sich allenthalben Spuren und Umstände des Phänomens verrathen, die auf Mehreres und oft ganz Anderes hindeuten, als bloß in den Principien enthalten ist. Die Verwirrung wird endlich noch größer, indem reflektirte, und bloß hypothetische Bestimmungen mit unmittelbaren Bestimmungen des Phänomens selbst vermischt werden, wenn jene auf eine Art ausgesprochen sind, als ob sie der unmittelbaren Erfahrung angehörten.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"127.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0010","text":"So kann wohl mancher, der mit ehrlichem Glauben zu diesen Wissenschaften hinzutritt, der Meinung seyn, die Molecules, die leeren Zwischenräume, die Fliehkraft, der Äther, der vereinzelnte Lichtstrahl, die elektrische, magnetische Materie und noch eine Menge dergleichen seyen Dinge oder Verhältnisse, die, nach der Art, wie von ihnen als unmittelbaren Daseynsbestimmungen gesprochen wird, in der That in der Wahrnehmung vorhanden seyen. Sie dienen als erste Gründe für Anderes, wer den als Wirklichkeiten ausgesprochen, und zuversichtlich angewendet; man läßt sie auf guten Glauben hin dafür gelten, ehe man inne wird, daß sie vielmehr aus dem, was sie begründen sollen, geschlossene Bestimmungen, von einer unkritischen Reflexion abgeleitete Hypothesen und Erdichtungen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"127.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0011","text":"In der That befindet man sich in einer Art von Hexenkreise, worin Bestimmungen des Daseyns und Bestimmungen der Reflexion, Grund und Begründetes, Phänomene und Phantome in unausgeschiedener Gesellschaft durch einander laufen und gleichen Rang mit einander geniessen.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"127.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0012","text":"Bei dem formellen Geschäfte dieser Erklärungsweise aus Gründen, hört man zugleich auch wieder, alles Erklärens aus den wohlbekannten Kräften und Materien ungeachtet, sagen, daß wir das innre Wesen dieser Kräfte und Materien selbst nicht kennen. Es ist hierin nur das Geständniß zu sehen, daß dieses Begründen sich selbst völlig ungenügend ist; daß es selbst etwas ganz Anderes fordere, als solche Gründe. Es ist dann nur nicht abzusehen, wozu sich denn diese Bemühung mit diesem Erklären gemacht, warum nicht das Andere gesucht, oder jenes Erklären wenigstens bei Seite gethan, und bei den einfachen Thatsachen stehen geblieben wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"127.12"}],"sha256":"645986a584d8e0757ff5e865cdc2095de5b820588947142ede121d39767383c8","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105123634983Z_cf43ee37","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"645986a584d8e0757ff5e865cdc2095de5b820588947142ede121d39767383c8","sha256":"d78de2f47c02a8a4179b4678f4d8749d5397a55324cbb07a9fddf587649619e5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:51:23.635028+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0001","text":"If reflection upon determinate grounds adheres to that form of ground which has emerged here, then the adducing of a ground remains a mere formalism and empty tautology, expressing in the form of reflection into itself, of essentiality, the same content that is already present in the form of immediate existence, regarded as posited. Such adducing of grounds is therefore accompanied by the same emptiness as discourse according to the principle of identity. The sciences, especially the physical sciences, are filled with tautologies of this kind, which constitute, as it were, a prerogative of science.—Thus, for example, the attractive force of the earth and the sun towards one another is given as the ground why the planets move around the sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"127.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0002","text":"As regards content, this expresses nothing other than what the phenomenon contains, namely, the relation of these bodies to one another in their motion, only in the form of a determination reflected into itself, of force. If one then asks what sort of force the attractive force is, the answer is that it is the force which causes the earth to move around the sun; that is, it has precisely the same content as the existence whose ground it is supposed to be; the relation of the earth and the sun with respect to motion is the identical foundation of the ground and of the grounded.—If a form of crystallization is explained by saying that it has its ground in the particular arrangement into which the molecules enter with one another, then the existent crystallization is itself this arrangement, expressed as ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"127.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0003","text":"In ordinary life, these etiologies, for which the sciences have the privilege, count for what they are: tautological, empty talk. If, in answer to the question why this man is travelling to the city, the ground is given that there is an attractive force in the city driving him thither, this kind of answer counts as absurd, though it is sanctioned in the sciences.—Leibniz reproached Newtonian attractive force with being such a hidden quality as the Scholastics employed for the purpose of explaining. Rather, the opposite ought to be reproached to it, namely, that it is too well-known a quality; for it has no content other than the appearance itself.—What recommends this manner of explanation is precisely its great clarity and intelligibility; for nothing is clearer and more intelligible than, for example,","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"127.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0004","text":"that a plant has its ground in a vegetative, i.e. plant-producing, force.—It could be called an occult quality only in the sense that the ground is supposed to have a content other than that which is to be explained; no such content is adduced; to that extent, the force employed for explanation is indeed a hidden ground, since a ground such as is required has not been adduced. This formalism explains as little as the nature of a plant is known when I say that it is a plant; notwithstanding all the clarity of this proposition, or of the statement that it has its ground in a plant-producing force, one may for that reason call this a very occult manner of explanation.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"127.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0005","text":"Secondly, as to form, this manner of explanation contains the two opposed directions of the relation of ground, without their determinate relation being recognized. On the one hand, the ground is ground as the determination of content reflected into itself of the existence which it grounds; on the other hand, it is the posited. It is that from which existence is supposed to be comprehended; conversely, however, it is inferred from existence and comprehended from existence. The principal business of this reflection consists, namely, in finding the grounds from existence, that is, in transposing immediate existence into the form of reflectedness; instead of being in and for itself and self-subsistent, the ground is thus rather the posited and the derivative.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"127.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0006","text":"Since, then, by this procedure it is fashioned in accordance with the phenomenon, and its determinations rest upon the latter, it indeed flows quite smoothly and with a favorable wind out of its ground. But cognition has not thereby advanced a step; it moves about within a difference of form which this procedure itself reverses and cancels. One of the principal difficulties in studying oneself into the sciences in which this procedure predominates rests, therefore, on this perversity of position: to send ahead as ground what is in fact derivative, and, in proceeding to the consequences, in fact only there to indicate the ground of those purported grounds.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"127.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0007","text":"The exposition begins with the grounds; they are set up in the air as principles and first concepts; they are simple determinations, without any necessity in and for themselves; what follows is supposed to be grounded upon them. Whoever therefore wishes to penetrate into sciences of this kind must begin by inculcating those grounds into himself; a task which comes hard to reason, since it is supposed to let what is groundless count as a foundation. He makes the best progress who, without much reflection, accepts the principles as given, and henceforth employs them as fundamental rules of his understanding. Without this method one cannot gain the beginning; just as little can one make progress without it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"127.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0008","text":"But this progress now impedes itself by the fact that in it the counterstroke of the method comes to light, which in what follows wishes to exhibit the derivative, whereas what follows in fact first contains the grounds for those presuppositions. Further, because what follows shows itself as the existence from which the ground was derived, this relation in which the phenomenon is presented gives rise to a distrust of its exposition; for it does not show itself expressed in its immediacy, but as evidence for the ground. Yet since the latter is in turn derived from the former, one rather demands to see it in its immediacy in order to be able to judge the ground from it. Thus, in such an exposition, in which what properly grounds appears as derivative, one does not know where one stands, either with the ground or with the phenomenon.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"127.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0009","text":"The uncertainty is increased by the fact, especially where the exposition is not strictly consistent but more candid, that everywhere traces and circumstances of the phenomenon betray themselves which point to more, and often to something quite different, than is merely contained in the principles. Finally, the confusion becomes still greater when reflected and merely hypothetical determinations are mixed with immediate determinations of the phenomenon itself, when the former are expressed in such a way as though they belonged to immediate experience.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"127.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0010","text":"Thus many a person who approaches these sciences with honest faith may well be of the opinion that the molecules, the empty interstices, centrifugal force, the ether, the isolated ray of light, electrical and magnetic matter, and a multitude of similar things, are things or relations which, according to the manner in which they are spoken of as immediate determinations of existence, are in fact present in perception. They serve as first grounds for other things; those who have pronounced them actualities and applied them confidently allow them to count as such on good faith, before becoming aware that they are rather determinations inferred from what they are supposed to ground, hypotheses and fictions derived from an uncritical reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"127.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0011","text":"In fact, one finds oneself in a kind of magic circle, in which determinations of existence and determinations of reflection, ground and grounded, phenomena and phantoms, run about intermixed in an undifferentiated society and enjoy equal rank with one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"127.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_35:P0012","text":"In the formal business of this manner of explanation from grounds, one also hears it said again, notwithstanding all explanation from the well-known forces and matters, that we do not know the inner essence of these forces and matters themselves. In this one is only to see the admission that this grounding is wholly inadequate to itself; that it itself demands something quite different from such grounds. It is then simply not apparent why this effort with this explaining should be made at all, why the other is not sought, or why that explaining is not at least set aside and one remains with the simple facts.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"127.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_35:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"655d3b9b3ecb2f23ba5f450b6601e31e0012b82d551513f123cb90559461b56a","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG","title":"b. The Real Ground.","order":128,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDRG","text":"Die Bestimmtheit des Grundes, ist, wie sich gezeigt hat, eines Theils Bestimmtheit der Grundlage oder Inhaltsbestimmung; andern Theils das Andersseyn in der Grundbeziehung selbst, nämlich die Unterschiedenheit ihres Inhalts und der Form; die Beziehung von Grund und Begründetem verläuft sich als eine äußerliche Form an dem Inhalt, der gegen diese Bestimmungen gleichgültig ist.—In der That aber sind beide einander nicht äußerlich; denn der Inhalt ist dieß, die Identität des Grundes mit sich selbst im Begründeten, und des Begründeten im Grunde zu seyn. Die Seite des Grundes hat sich gezeigt, selbst ein Gesetztes, und die Seite des Begründeten, selbst Grund zu seyn; jede ist an ihr selbst diese Identität des Ganzen. Weil sie aber zugleich der Form angehören und ihre bestimmte Unterschiedenheit ausmachen, so ist jede in ihrer Bestimmtheit die Identität des Ganzen mit sich. Jede hat somit einen gegen die andere verschiedenen Inhalt.—Oder von Seite des Inhalts betrachtet, weil er die Identität als der Grundbeziehung mit sich ist, hat er wesentlich diesen Formunterschied an ihm selbst, und ist als Grund ein anderer, denn als Begründetes.\n\nDarin nun, daß Grund und Begründetes einen verschiedenen Inhalt haben, hat die Grundbeziehung aufgehört, eine formale zu seyn; der Rückgang in den Grund, und das Hervorgehen aus ihm zum Gesetzten ist nicht mehr die Tautologie; der Grund ist realisirt. Man verlangt daher, wenn man nach einem Grund fragt, eigentlich für den Grund eine andere Inhaltsbestimmung als diejenige ist, nach deren Grund man fragt.\n\nDiese Beziehung bestimmt sich nun weiter. Insofern nämlich ihre beide Seiten verschiedener Inhalt sind, sind sie gleichgültig gegen einander; jede ist eine unmittelbare mit sich identische Bestimmung. Ferner als Grund und Begründetes auf einander bezogen, ist der Grund das in dem Andern als in seinem Gesetztseyn in sich reflektirte; der Inhalt also, welchen die Seite des Grundes hat, ist ebenso im Begründeten; dieses als das Gesetzte hat nur in jenem seine Identität mit sich und sein Bestehen. Außer diesem Inhalte des Grundes hat aber das Begründete nunmehr auch seinen eigenthümlichen, und ist somit die Einheit von einem zweifachen Inhalt. Diese nun ist zwar als Einheit unterschiedener deren negative Einheit, aber weil es gegen einander gleichgültige Inhaltsbestimmungen sind, ist sie nur ihre leere, an ihr selbst inhaltslose Beziehung, nicht ihre Vermittelung; ein Eins oder Etwas als äußerliche Verknüpfung derselben.\n\nEs ist also in der realen Grundbeziehung das doppelte vorhanden, einmal die Inhaltsbestimmung, welche Grund ist, in dem Gesetztseyn mit sich selbst kontinuirt, so daß sie das einfach Identische des Grundes und Begründeten ausmacht; das Begründete enthält so den Grund vollkommen in sich, ihre Beziehung ist unterschiedslose wesentliche Gediegenheit. Was im Begründeten zu diesem einfachen Wesen noch hinzukommt, ist daher nur eine unwesentliche Form, äußerliche Inhaltsbestimmungen, die als solche vom Grunde frei, und eine unmittelbare Mannigfaltigkeit sind. Von diesem Unwesentlichen ist also jenes Wesentliche nicht der Grund, noch ist es Grund von der Beziehung beider aufeinander in dem Begründeten. Es ist ein positiv Identisches, das dem Begründeten inwohnt, aber sich darin in keinen Formunterschied setzt, sondern als sich auf sich selbst beziehender Inhalt gleichgültige positive Grundlage ist.—Fürs andere ist das mit dieser Grundlage im Etwas Verknüpfte ein gleichgültiger Inhalt, aber als die unwesentliche Seite. Die Hauptsache ist die Beziehung der Grundlage und der unwesentlichen Mannigfaltigkeit. Diese Beziehung aber, weil die bezogenen Bestimmungen gleichgültiger Inhalt sind, ist auch nicht Grund; eine ist zwar als wesentlicher, das Andere nur als unwesentlicher oder gesetzter Inhalt bestimmt, aber als sich auf sich beziehender Inhalt ist beiden diese Form äußerlich. Das Eins des Etwas, das ihre Beziehung ausmacht, ist deswegen nicht Formbeziehung, sondern nur ein äußerliches Band, das den unwesentlichen mannigfaltigen Inhalt nicht als gesetzten enthält; es ist also gleichfalls nur Grundlage.\n\nDer Grund, wie er als realer sich bestimmt, zerfällt hiermit um der Inhaltsverschiedenheit willen, die seine Realität ausmacht, in äußerliche Bestimmungen. Die beiden Beziehungen, der wesentliche Inhalt, als die einfache unmittelbare Identität des Grundes und des Begründeten; und dann das Etwas, als die Beziehung des unterschiedenen Inhalts, sind zwei verschiedene Grundlagen; die mit sich identische Form des Grundes, daß Dasselbe das eine Mal als Wesentliches, das andere Mal als Gesetztes sey, ist verschwunden; die Grundbeziehung ist so sich selbst äußerlich geworden.\n\nEs ist daher nun ein äußerlicher Grund, welcher verschiedenen Inhalt in Verknüpfung bringt und es bestimmt, welcher der Grund und welcher das durch ihn Gesetzte sey; in dem beiderseitigen Inhalte selbst liegt diese Bestimmung nicht. Der reale Grund ist daher Beziehung auf Anderes, einer Seits des Inhalts auf andern Inhalt, anderer Seits der Grundbeziehung selbst (der Form) auf Anderes, nämlich auf ein Unmittelbares, nicht durch sie Gesetztes.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Die Bestimmtheit des Grundes, ist, wie sich gezeigt hat, eines Theils Bestimmtheit der Grundlage oder Inhaltsbestimmung; andern Theils das Andersseyn in der Grundbeziehung selbst, nämlich die Unterschiedenheit ihres Inhalts und der Form; die Beziehung von Grund und Begründetem verläuft sich als eine äußerliche Form an dem Inhalt, der gegen diese Bestimmungen gleichgültig ist.—In der That aber sind beide einander nicht äußerlich; denn der Inhalt ist dieß, die Identität des Grundes mit sich selbst im Begründeten, und des Begründeten im Grunde zu seyn. Die Seite des Grundes hat sich gezeigt, selbst ein Gesetztes, und die Seite des Begründeten, selbst Grund zu seyn; jede ist an ihr selbst diese Identität des Ganzen. Weil sie aber zugleich der Form angehören und ihre bestimmte Unterschiedenheit ausmachen, so ist jede in ihrer Bestimmtheit die Identität des Ganzen mit sich. Jede hat somit einen gegen die andere verschiedenen Inhalt.—Oder von Seite des Inhalts betrachtet, weil er die Identität als der Grundbeziehung mit sich ist, hat er wesentlich diesen Formunterschied an ihm selbst, und ist als Grund ein anderer, denn als Begründetes.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Darin nun, daß Grund und Begründetes einen verschiedenen Inhalt haben, hat die Grundbeziehung aufgehört, eine formale zu seyn; der Rückgang in den Grund, und das Hervorgehen aus ihm zum Gesetzten ist nicht mehr die Tautologie; der Grund ist realisirt. Man verlangt daher, wenn man nach einem Grund fragt, eigentlich für den Grund eine andere Inhaltsbestimmung als diejenige ist, nach deren Grund man fragt.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0003","text":"Diese Beziehung bestimmt sich nun weiter. Insofern nämlich ihre beide Seiten verschiedener Inhalt sind, sind sie gleichgültig gegen einander; jede ist eine unmittelbare mit sich identische Bestimmung. Ferner als Grund und Begründetes auf einander bezogen, ist der Grund das in dem Andern als in seinem Gesetztseyn in sich reflektirte; der Inhalt also, welchen die Seite des Grundes hat, ist ebenso im Begründeten; dieses als das Gesetzte hat nur in jenem seine Identität mit sich und sein Bestehen. Außer diesem Inhalte des Grundes hat aber das Begründete nunmehr auch seinen eigenthümlichen, und ist somit die Einheit von einem zweifachen Inhalt. Diese nun ist zwar als Einheit unterschiedener deren negative Einheit, aber weil es gegen einander gleichgültige Inhaltsbestimmungen sind, ist sie nur ihre leere, an ihr selbst inhaltslose Beziehung, nicht ihre Vermittelung; ein Eins oder Etwas als äußerliche Verknüpfung derselben.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Es ist also in der realen Grundbeziehung das doppelte vorhanden, einmal die Inhaltsbestimmung, welche Grund ist, in dem Gesetztseyn mit sich selbst kontinuirt, so daß sie das einfach Identische des Grundes und Begründeten ausmacht; das Begründete enthält so den Grund vollkommen in sich, ihre Beziehung ist unterschiedslose wesentliche Gediegenheit. Was im Begründeten zu diesem einfachen Wesen noch hinzukommt, ist daher nur eine unwesentliche Form, äußerliche Inhaltsbestimmungen, die als solche vom Grunde frei, und eine unmittelbare Mannigfaltigkeit sind. Von diesem Unwesentlichen ist also jenes Wesentliche nicht der Grund, noch ist es Grund von der Beziehung beider aufeinander in dem Begründeten. Es ist ein positiv Identisches, das dem Begründeten inwohnt, aber sich darin in keinen Formunterschied setzt, sondern als sich auf sich selbst beziehender Inhalt gleichgültige positive Grundlage ist.—Fürs andere ist das mit dieser Grundlage im Etwas Verknüpfte ein gleichgültiger Inhalt, aber als die unwesentliche Seite. Die Hauptsache ist die Beziehung der Grundlage und der unwesentlichen Mannigfaltigkeit. Diese Beziehung aber, weil die bezogenen Bestimmungen gleichgültiger Inhalt sind, ist auch nicht Grund; eine ist zwar als wesentlicher, das Andere nur als unwesentlicher oder gesetzter Inhalt bestimmt, aber als sich auf sich beziehender Inhalt ist beiden diese Form äußerlich. Das Eins des Etwas, das ihre Beziehung ausmacht, ist deswegen nicht Formbeziehung, sondern nur ein äußerliches Band, das den unwesentlichen mannigfaltigen Inhalt nicht als gesetzten enthält; es ist also gleichfalls nur Grundlage.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Der Grund, wie er als realer sich bestimmt, zerfällt hiermit um der Inhaltsverschiedenheit willen, die seine Realität ausmacht, in äußerliche Bestimmungen. Die beiden Beziehungen, der wesentliche Inhalt, als die einfache unmittelbare Identität des Grundes und des Begründeten; und dann das Etwas, als die Beziehung des unterschiedenen Inhalts, sind zwei verschiedene Grundlagen; die mit sich identische Form des Grundes, daß Dasselbe das eine Mal als Wesentliches, das andere Mal als Gesetztes sey, ist verschwunden; die Grundbeziehung ist so sich selbst äußerlich geworden.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Es ist daher nun ein äußerlicher Grund, welcher verschiedenen Inhalt in Verknüpfung bringt und es bestimmt, welcher der Grund und welcher das durch ihn Gesetzte sey; in dem beiderseitigen Inhalte selbst liegt diese Bestimmung nicht. Der reale Grund ist daher Beziehung auf Anderes, einer Seits des Inhalts auf andern Inhalt, anderer Seits der Grundbeziehung selbst (der Form) auf Anderes, nämlich auf ein Unmittelbares, nicht durch sie Gesetztes.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"c0d3c59361f161c92a85e5b8b3a94e3100dc63f2e4b45add1e85fd8b201a8d3d","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The Real Ground.","source_sha256":"c0d3c59361f161c92a85e5b8b3a94e3100dc63f2e4b45add1e85fd8b201a8d3d","sha256":"7c6c134b48ef0830b923a258e811f6d54c45f0c5056dd6f2c63ac7e770ae744b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:51:34.250292+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0001","text":"The determinacy of the ground is, as has been shown, on the one hand determinacy of the substrate or determination of content; on the other hand, being-other in the relation of ground itself, namely the difference of its content and form; the relation of ground and grounded dissipates itself as an external form upon the content, which is indifferent to these determinations.—In fact, however, the two are not external to one another; for the content is this: to be the identity of the ground with itself in the grounded, and of the grounded in the ground. The side of the ground has shown itself to be itself a posited, and the side of the grounded to be itself ground; each is in itself this identity of the whole. But since they at the same time belong to form and constitute its determinate difference, each in its determinacy is the identity of the whole with itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Each thus has a content different from that of the other.—Or, considered from the side of content, since it is the identity of the relation of ground with itself, it essentially has this difference of form in itself, and is, as ground, other than as grounded.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Now in the fact that ground and grounded have a different content, the relation of ground has ceased to be formal; the return into the ground and the emergence from it to the posited is no longer tautology; the ground is realized. Thus, when one asks after a ground, one properly demands for the ground a determination of content other than that whose ground is being asked after.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0004","text":"This relation now determines itself further. Namely, insofar as its two sides are different contents, they are indifferent to one another; each is an immediate determination identical with itself. Further, as ground and grounded are related to one another, the ground is what is reflected into itself in the other as in its positedness; thus the content which the side of the ground has is likewise in the grounded; the latter, as the posited, has its identity with itself and its subsistence only in the former. But apart from this content of the ground, the grounded now also has its own peculiar content, and is thus the unity of a twofold content.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0005","text":"This, indeed, as the unity of distinct [contents], is their negative unity; but because they are determinations of content indifferent to one another, it is only their empty relation, itself devoid of content, not their mediation; a one or something as their external connection.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0006","text":"Thus in the real relation of ground there is the double: first, the determination of content which is ground, continued with itself in positedness, so that it constitutes the simply identical of ground and grounded; the grounded thus contains the ground completely within itself, their relation is undifferentiated essential solidity. What is added in the grounded to this simple essence is therefore only an unessential form, external determinations of content, which as such are free from the ground and are an immediate manifold. Thus, of this unessential [element], that essential [element] is not the ground, nor is it ground of the relation of the two to one another in the grounded.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0007","text":"It is a positively identical [element] that inheres in the grounded, but does not posit itself therein in any difference of form, but as content relating itself to itself is an indifferent positive substrate.—Secondly, what is connected with this substrate in the something is an indifferent content, but as the unessential side. The main point is the relation of the substrate and the unessential manifold. But this relation, because the determinations related are indifferent content, is likewise not ground; one is indeed determined as more essential, the other merely as unessential or posited content, but as content relating itself to itself this form is external to both.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105134250265Z_931b1c12:DISPLAY-0008","text":"The unity of the something which constitutes their relation is therefore not a relation of form, but only an external bond, which does not contain the unessential manifold content as posited; it is thus likewise only substrate.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0005","text":"The ground, as it determines itself as real, thereby falls apart, on account of the difference of content that constitutes its reality, into external determinations. The two relations—the essential content, as the simple immediate identity of ground and grounded; and then the something, as the relation of the differentiated content—are two different substrates; the form of the ground identical with itself, namely that the same is once essential and another time posited, has disappeared; the relation of ground has thus become external to itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0006","text":"There is therefore now an external ground, which brings different content into connection and determines which is to be the ground and which that posited through it; this determination does not lie in the reciprocal content itself. The real ground is therefore relation to an other: on the one side, of content to other content; on the other side, of the relation of ground itself (of form) to an other, namely to an immediate [element] not posited through it.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDRG:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"66333b1cfb11978b633b3c902d740a8f694256fa6bfed472dd838a597e016e4b","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Der reale Grund."}],"original_title":"b. Der reale Grund.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36","title":"Remark.","order":129,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_36","text":"Die formelle Grundbeziehung enthält nur Einen Inhalt für Grund und Begründetes, in dieser Identität liegt ihre Nothwendigkeit, aber zugleich ihre Tautologie. Der reale Grund enthält einen verschiedenen Inhalt, damit tritt aber die Zufälligkeit und Äußerlichkeit der Grundbeziehung ein. Einer Seits ist dasjenige, was als das Wesentliche und deswegen als die Grundbestimmung betrachtet wird, nicht Grund der anderen Bestimmungen, die mit ihr verknüpft sind. Anderer Seits ist es auch unbestimmt, welche von mehrern Inhaltsbestimmungen eines konkreten Dinges als die wesentliche und als Grund angenommen werden soll; die Wahl ist daher zwischen ihnen frei. So ist in ersterer Rücksicht z.B. der Grund eines Hauses die Unterlage desselben; wodurch diese Grund ist, ist die der sinnlichen Materie inwohnende Schwere, das sowohl in dem Grunde als dem begründeten Hause schlechthin Identische. Daß an der schweren Materie nun ein solcher Unterschied ist, wie der einer Unterlage und einer davon unterschiedenen Modifikation, wodurch sie eine Wohnung ausmacht, ist dem Schweren selbst vollkommen gleichgültig, seine Beziehung auf die anderen Inhaltsbestimmungen des Zwecks, der Einrichtung des Hauses u.s.f. ist ihm äußerlich; es ist daher wohl Grundlage, aber nicht Grund derselben. Die Schwere ist so sehr als Grund, daß ein Haus steht, auch Grund, daß ein Stein fällt; der Stein hat diesen Grund, die Schwere, in sich; aber daß er eine weitere Inhaltsbestimmung hat, wodurch er nicht bloß ein Schweres, sondern Stein ist, ist der Schwere äußerlich; es ist ferner durch ein Anderes gesetzt, daß er von dem Körper vorher entfernt worden sey, auf welchen er fällt, wie auch die Zeit und der Raum und deren Beziehung, die Bewegung, ein anderer Inhalt als die Schwere sind, und ohne sie (wie man zu sprechen pflegt) vorgestellt werden können, folglich nicht wesentlich durch sie gesetzt sind.—Sie ist auch so sehr Grund, daß ein Projektil die dem Fallen entgegengesetzte Wurfbewegung nacht. —Aus der Verschiedenheit der Bestimmungen, deren Grund sie ist, erhellt, daß ein Anderes zugleich erfordert wird, welches sie zum Grunde dieser oder einer andern Bestimmung macht.-Wenn von der Natur gesagt wird, daß sie der Grund der Welt ist, so ist das, was Natur genannt wird, einer Seits eins mit der Welt, und die Welt nichts als die Natur selbst. Aber sie sind auch unterschieden, so daß die Natur mehr das Unbestimmte, oder wenigstens nur das in den allgemeinen Unterschieden, welche Gesetze sind, bestimmte, mit sich identische Wesen der Welt ist, und zur Natur, um Welt zu seyn, noch eine Mannigfaltigkeit von Bestimmungen äußerlich hinzukommt. Diese aber haben ihren Grund nicht in der Natur als solcher, sie ist vielmehr das gegen sie als Zufälligkeiten Gleichgültige.—Es ist dasselbe Verhältniß, wenn Gott als Grund der Natur bestimmt wird. Als Grund ist er ihr Wesen, sie enthält es in ihr und ist ein identisches mit ihm; aber sie hat noch eine weitere Mannigfaltigkeit, die von dem Grunde selbst unterschieden ist; sie ist das Dritte, worin dieses beide Verschiedene verknüpft ist; jener Grund ist weder Grund der von ihm verschiedenen Mannigfaltigkeit noch seiner Verknüpfung mit ihr. Die Natur wird daher nicht aus Gott als dem Grunde erkannt, denn so wäre er nur ihr allgemeines Wesen, der sie nicht, wie sie bestimmtes Wesen und Natur ist, enthält.\n\nDas Angeben von realen Gründen wird also um dieser Inhaltsverschiedenheit des Grundes oder eigentlich der Grundlage und dessen, was mit ihm im Begründeten verbunden ist, ebenso sehr ein Formalismus, als der formale Grund selbst. In diesem ist der mit sich identische Inhalt gleichgültig gegen die Form; im realen Grunde findet dieß gleichfalls Statt. Dadurch ist nun ferner der Fall, daß er es nicht an ihm selbst enthält, welche der mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen als die wesentliche genommen werden soll. Etwas ist ein Konkretes von solchen mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen, die sich gleich beständig und bleibend an ihm zeigen. Die eine kann daher so sehr wie die andere als Grund bestimmt werden; nämlich als die wesentliche, in Vergleichung mit welcher alsdann die andere nur ein Gesetztes sey. Es verbindet sich damit das vorhin Erwähnte, daß, wenn eine Bestimmung vorhanden ist, die in einem Falle als Grund einer andern angesehen wird, daraus nicht folgt, daß diese andere in einem andern Falle oder überhaupt, mit ihr gesetzt sey.—Die Strafe z.B. hat die mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen, daß sie Wiedervergeltung, ferner abschreckendes Beispiel, daß sie ein vom Gesetz zur Abschreckung Angedrohtes, auch ein den Verbrecher zur Besinnung und Besserung Bringendes ist. Jede dieser verschiedenen Bestimmungen ist als Grund der Strafe betrachtet worden, weil jede eine wesentliche Bestimmung ist, und dadurch die anderen als von ihr unterschieden, gegen sie nur als Zufälliges bestimmt werden. Diejenige aber, die als Grund angenommen wird, ist noch nicht die ganze Strafe selbst; dieses Konkrete enthält auch jene anderen, die mit ihr darin nur verknüpft sind, ohne daß sie in ihr ihren Grund hätten.—Oder ein Beamter hat Amts-Geschicklichkeit, steht als Individuum in Verwandschaft, hat diese und jene Bekanntschaft, einen besondern Charakter, war in diesen und jenen Umständen und Gelegenheiten, sich zu zeigen, u.s.f. Es kann jede dieser Eigenschaften Grund seyn, oder als solcher angesehen werden, daß er dieß Amt hat; sie sind ein verschiedener Inhalt, der in einem Dritten verbunden ist; die Form, als das Wesentliche und als das Gesetzte gegeneinander bestimmt zu seyn, ist demselben äußerlich. Jede dieser Eigenschaften ist dem Beamten wesentlich, weil er durch sie das bestimmte Individuum ist, welches er ist; insofern das Amt als eine äußerliche gesetzte Bestimmung betrachtet werden kann, kann jede gegen dieses als Grund bestimmt, aber auch selbst umgekehrt können jene als gesetzte, und das Amt als Grund derselben angesehen werden. Wie sie sich wirklich, d. h. im einzelnen Fall, verhalten, dieß ist eine der Grundbeziehung und dem Inhalte selbst, äußerliche Bestimmung; es ist ein Drittes, was ihnen die Form von Grund und Begründetem ertheilt.\n\nSo kann überhaupt jedes Daseyn mancherlei Gründe haben, jede seiner Inhaltsbestimmungen durchdringt als mit sich identisch das konkrete Ganze, und läßt sich daher als wesentlich betrachten; den mancherlei Rüksichten d. h. Bestimmungen, die außer der Sache selbst liegen, ist um der Zufälligkeit der Verknüpfungsweise Thür und Thor unendlich aufgethan.—Ob ein Grund diese oder jene Folge habe, ist deswegen ebenso zufällig. Die moralischen Beweggründe z.B. sind wesentliche Bestimmungen der sittlichen Natur, aber das, was aus ihnen folgt, ist zugleich eine von ihnen verschiedene Äußerlichkeit, die aus ihnen folgt, und auch nicht folgt; erst durch ein Drittes kommt sie zu ihnen hinzu. Genauer ist dieß so zu nehmen, daß es der moralischen Bestimmung, wenn sie Grund ist, nicht zufällig sey, eine Folge oder ein Begründetes zu haben, aber ob sie überhaupt zum Grund gemacht werde oder nicht. Allein da auch wieder der Inhalt, der ihre Folge ist, wenn sie zum Grund gemacht worden, die Natur der Äußerlichkeit hat, kann er unmittelbar durch eine andere Äußerlichkeit aufgehoben werden. Aus einem moralischen Beweggrunde kann also eine Handlung hervorgehen oder auch nicht. Umgekehrt kann eine Handlung mancherlei Gründe haben; sie enthält als ein Konkretes mannigfaltige wesentliche Bestimmungen, deren jede deswegen als Grund angegeben werden kann. Das Aufsuchen und Angeben von Gründen, worin vornemlich das Raisonnement besteht, ist darum ein endloses Herumtreiben, das keine letzte Bestimmung enthält; es kann von allem und jeden einer und mehrere gute Gründe angegeben werden, so wie von seinem Entgegengesetzten, und es können eine Menge Gründe vorhanden seyn, ohne daß aus ihnen etwas erfolgt. Was Sokrates und Plato Sophisterei nennen, ist nichts anderes als das Raisonnement aus Gründen; Plato setzt demselben die Betrachtung der Idee, d. h. der Sache an und für sich selbst, oder in ihrem Begriffe entgegen. Die Gründe sind nur von wesentlichen Inhaltsbestimmungen, Verhältnissen und Rüksichten genommen, deren jede Sache, gerade wie auch ihr Gegentheil, mehrere hat; in ihrer Form der Wesentlichkeit gilt die eine so gut als die andere; weil sie nicht den ganzen Umfang der Sache enthält, ist sie einseitiger Grund, deren die anderen besondern Seiten wieder besondere haben, und wovon keiner die Sache, welche ihre Verknüpfung ausmacht und sie alle enthält, erschöpft; keiner ist zureichender Grund, d. h. der Begriff","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0001","text":"Die formelle Grundbeziehung enthält nur Einen Inhalt für Grund und Begründetes, in dieser Identität liegt ihre Nothwendigkeit, aber zugleich ihre Tautologie. Der reale Grund enthält einen verschiedenen Inhalt, damit tritt aber die Zufälligkeit und Äußerlichkeit der Grundbeziehung ein. Einer Seits ist dasjenige, was als das Wesentliche und deswegen als die Grundbestimmung betrachtet wird, nicht Grund der anderen Bestimmungen, die mit ihr verknüpft sind. Anderer Seits ist es auch unbestimmt, welche von mehrern Inhaltsbestimmungen eines konkreten Dinges als die wesentliche und als Grund angenommen werden soll; die Wahl ist daher zwischen ihnen frei. So ist in ersterer Rücksicht z.B. der Grund eines Hauses die Unterlage desselben; wodurch diese Grund ist, ist die der sinnlichen Materie inwohnende Schwere, das sowohl in dem Grunde als dem begründeten Hause schlechthin Identische.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"129.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0002","text":"Daß an der schweren Materie nun ein solcher Unterschied ist, wie der einer Unterlage und einer davon unterschiedenen Modifikation, wodurch sie eine Wohnung ausmacht, ist dem Schweren selbst vollkommen gleichgültig, seine Beziehung auf die anderen Inhaltsbestimmungen des Zwecks, der Einrichtung des Hauses u.s.f. ist ihm äußerlich; es ist daher wohl Grundlage, aber nicht Grund derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"129.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0003","text":"Die Schwere ist so sehr als Grund, daß ein Haus steht, auch Grund, daß ein Stein fällt; der Stein hat diesen Grund, die Schwere, in sich; aber daß er eine weitere Inhaltsbestimmung hat, wodurch er nicht bloß ein Schweres, sondern Stein ist, ist der Schwere äußerlich; es ist ferner durch ein Anderes gesetzt, daß er von dem Körper vorher entfernt worden sey, auf welchen er fällt, wie auch die Zeit und der Raum und deren Beziehung, die Bewegung, ein anderer Inhalt als die Schwere sind, und ohne sie (wie man zu sprechen pflegt) vorgestellt werden können, folglich nicht wesentlich durch sie gesetzt sind.—Sie ist auch so sehr Grund, daß ein Projektil die dem Fallen entgegengesetzte Wurfbewegung nacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"129.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0004","text":"—Aus der Verschiedenheit der Bestimmungen, deren Grund sie ist, erhellt, daß ein Anderes zugleich erfordert wird, welches sie zum Grunde dieser oder einer andern Bestimmung macht.-Wenn von der Natur gesagt wird, daß sie der Grund der Welt ist, so ist das, was Natur genannt wird, einer Seits eins mit der Welt, und die Welt nichts als die Natur selbst. Aber sie sind auch unterschieden, so daß die Natur mehr das Unbestimmte, oder wenigstens nur das in den allgemeinen Unterschieden, welche Gesetze sind, bestimmte, mit sich identische Wesen der Welt ist, und zur Natur, um Welt zu seyn, noch eine Mannigfaltigkeit von Bestimmungen äußerlich hinzukommt. Diese aber haben ihren Grund nicht in der Natur als solcher, sie ist vielmehr das gegen sie als Zufälligkeiten Gleichgültige.—Es ist dasselbe Verhältniß, wenn Gott als Grund der Natur bestimmt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"129.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0005","text":"Als Grund ist er ihr Wesen, sie enthält es in ihr und ist ein identisches mit ihm; aber sie hat noch eine weitere Mannigfaltigkeit, die von dem Grunde selbst unterschieden ist; sie ist das Dritte, worin dieses beide Verschiedene verknüpft ist; jener Grund ist weder Grund der von ihm verschiedenen Mannigfaltigkeit noch seiner Verknüpfung mit ihr. Die Natur wird daher nicht aus Gott als dem Grunde erkannt, denn so wäre er nur ihr allgemeines Wesen, der sie nicht, wie sie bestimmtes Wesen und Natur ist, enthält.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"129.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0006","text":"Das Angeben von realen Gründen wird also um dieser Inhaltsverschiedenheit des Grundes oder eigentlich der Grundlage und dessen, was mit ihm im Begründeten verbunden ist, ebenso sehr ein Formalismus, als der formale Grund selbst. In diesem ist der mit sich identische Inhalt gleichgültig gegen die Form; im realen Grunde findet dieß gleichfalls Statt. Dadurch ist nun ferner der Fall, daß er es nicht an ihm selbst enthält, welche der mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen als die wesentliche genommen werden soll. Etwas ist ein Konkretes von solchen mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen, die sich gleich beständig und bleibend an ihm zeigen. Die eine kann daher so sehr wie die andere als Grund bestimmt werden; nämlich als die wesentliche, in Vergleichung mit welcher alsdann die andere nur ein Gesetztes sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"129.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0007","text":"Es verbindet sich damit das vorhin Erwähnte, daß, wenn eine Bestimmung vorhanden ist, die in einem Falle als Grund einer andern angesehen wird, daraus nicht folgt, daß diese andere in einem andern Falle oder überhaupt, mit ihr gesetzt sey.—Die Strafe z.B. hat die mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen, daß sie Wiedervergeltung, ferner abschreckendes Beispiel, daß sie ein vom Gesetz zur Abschreckung Angedrohtes, auch ein den Verbrecher zur Besinnung und Besserung Bringendes ist. Jede dieser verschiedenen Bestimmungen ist als Grund der Strafe betrachtet worden, weil jede eine wesentliche Bestimmung ist, und dadurch die anderen als von ihr unterschieden, gegen sie nur als Zufälliges bestimmt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"129.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0008","text":"Diejenige aber, die als Grund angenommen wird, ist noch nicht die ganze Strafe selbst; dieses Konkrete enthält auch jene anderen, die mit ihr darin nur verknüpft sind, ohne daß sie in ihr ihren Grund hätten.—Oder ein Beamter hat Amts-Geschicklichkeit, steht als Individuum in Verwandschaft, hat diese und jene Bekanntschaft, einen besondern Charakter, war in diesen und jenen Umständen und Gelegenheiten, sich zu zeigen, u.s.f. Es kann jede dieser Eigenschaften Grund seyn, oder als solcher angesehen werden, daß er dieß Amt hat; sie sind ein verschiedener Inhalt, der in einem Dritten verbunden ist; die Form, als das Wesentliche und als das Gesetzte gegeneinander bestimmt zu seyn, ist demselben äußerlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"129.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0009","text":"Jede dieser Eigenschaften ist dem Beamten wesentlich, weil er durch sie das bestimmte Individuum ist, welches er ist; insofern das Amt als eine äußerliche gesetzte Bestimmung betrachtet werden kann, kann jede gegen dieses als Grund bestimmt, aber auch selbst umgekehrt können jene als gesetzte, und das Amt als Grund derselben angesehen werden. Wie sie sich wirklich, d. h. im einzelnen Fall, verhalten, dieß ist eine der Grundbeziehung und dem Inhalte selbst, äußerliche Bestimmung; es ist ein Drittes, was ihnen die Form von Grund und Begründetem ertheilt.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"129.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0010","text":"So kann überhaupt jedes Daseyn mancherlei Gründe haben, jede seiner Inhaltsbestimmungen durchdringt als mit sich identisch das konkrete Ganze, und läßt sich daher als wesentlich betrachten; den mancherlei Rüksichten d. h. Bestimmungen, die außer der Sache selbst liegen, ist um der Zufälligkeit der Verknüpfungsweise Thür und Thor unendlich aufgethan.—Ob ein Grund diese oder jene Folge habe, ist deswegen ebenso zufällig. Die moralischen Beweggründe z.B. sind wesentliche Bestimmungen der sittlichen Natur, aber das, was aus ihnen folgt, ist zugleich eine von ihnen verschiedene Äußerlichkeit, die aus ihnen folgt, und auch nicht folgt; erst durch ein Drittes kommt sie zu ihnen hinzu. Genauer ist dieß so zu nehmen, daß es der moralischen Bestimmung, wenn sie Grund ist, nicht zufällig sey, eine Folge oder ein Begründetes zu haben, aber ob sie überhaupt zum Grund gemacht werde oder nicht.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"129.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0011","text":"Allein da auch wieder der Inhalt, der ihre Folge ist, wenn sie zum Grund gemacht worden, die Natur der Äußerlichkeit hat, kann er unmittelbar durch eine andere Äußerlichkeit aufgehoben werden. Aus einem moralischen Beweggrunde kann also eine Handlung hervorgehen oder auch nicht. Umgekehrt kann eine Handlung mancherlei Gründe haben; sie enthält als ein Konkretes mannigfaltige wesentliche Bestimmungen, deren jede deswegen als Grund angegeben werden kann. Das Aufsuchen und Angeben von Gründen, worin vornemlich das Raisonnement besteht, ist darum ein endloses Herumtreiben, das keine letzte Bestimmung enthält; es kann von allem und jeden einer und mehrere gute Gründe angegeben werden, so wie von seinem Entgegengesetzten, und es können eine Menge Gründe vorhanden seyn, ohne daß aus ihnen etwas erfolgt.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"129.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0012","text":"Was Sokrates und Plato Sophisterei nennen, ist nichts anderes als das Raisonnement aus Gründen; Plato setzt demselben die Betrachtung der Idee, d. h. der Sache an und für sich selbst, oder in ihrem Begriffe entgegen. Die Gründe sind nur von wesentlichen Inhaltsbestimmungen, Verhältnissen und Rüksichten genommen, deren jede Sache, gerade wie auch ihr Gegentheil, mehrere hat; in ihrer Form der Wesentlichkeit gilt die eine so gut als die andere; weil sie nicht den ganzen Umfang der Sache enthält, ist sie einseitiger Grund, deren die anderen besondern Seiten wieder besondere haben, und wovon keiner die Sache, welche ihre Verknüpfung ausmacht und sie alle enthält, erschöpft; keiner ist zureichender Grund, d. h. der Begriff","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"129.12"}],"sha256":"142b85a9c54e23036ec4783d141082ed91c92326fd400ed65b1df4505cf2fe68","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105151717695Z_aeeecb94","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"142b85a9c54e23036ec4783d141082ed91c92326fd400ed65b1df4505cf2fe68","sha256":"d545d0cf0d7ff7e86eea3ee1026ec4d2068d7d26bf9542b0c6511caf25d49459","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:51:51.717734+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0001","text":"The formal relation of ground contains only one content for ground and grounded; in this identity lies its necessity, but at the same time its tautology. The real ground contains a different content, but with this the contingency and externality of the relation of ground enter in. On the one hand, that which is regarded as the essential and therefore as the determination of ground is not the ground of the other determinations connected with it. On the other hand, it is also indeterminate which of several determinations of content of a concrete thing is to be assumed as the essential and as ground; the choice among them is therefore free. Thus, in the former respect, for example, the ground of a house is its foundation; that whereby this is ground is the gravity inherent in sensible matter, what is absolutely identical both in the ground and in the grounded house.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"129.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0002","text":"That there is now such a difference in heavy matter as that of a foundation and a modification distinct from it, whereby it constitutes a dwelling, is entirely indifferent to heaviness itself; its relation to the other determinations of content of the purpose, the arrangement of the house, etc., is external to it; it is therefore indeed a foundation, but not their ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"129.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0003","text":"Gravity is as much the ground that a house stands as it is the ground that a stone falls; the stone has this ground, gravity, within itself; but that it has a further determination of content whereby it is not merely something heavy but a stone, is external to gravity; it is further posited through an Other that it has previously been removed from the body upon which it falls, just as time and space and their relation, motion, are a content other than gravity and can be represented without it (as one is accustomed to say), consequently are not essentially posited through it.—It is equally the ground that a projectile makes the motion of throwing opposed to falling.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"129.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0004","text":"—From the diversity of the determinations of which it is the ground, it is evident that at the same time an Other is required which makes it the ground of this or another determination.—When it is said of nature that it is the ground of the world, what is called nature is, on the one hand, one with the world, and the world is nothing but nature itself. But they are also distinct, in such a way that nature is more the indeterminate, or at least the essence of the world determined only in the universal differences, which are laws, identical with itself; and, in order to be world, a multiplicity of determinations further accrues externally to nature. But these do not have their ground in nature as such; rather, nature is indifferent to them as contingencies.—It is the same relation when God is determined as the ground of nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"129.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0005","text":"As ground, He is its essence; it contains this essence within it and is identical with Him; but it has yet a further multiplicity, distinct from the ground itself; it is the third in which these two distinct things are connected; that ground is neither the ground of the multiplicity distinct from it nor of its connection with it. Nature is therefore not cognized from God as ground, for then He would be only its universal essence, which does not contain it as it is determinate essence and nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"129.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0006","text":"The adducing of real grounds thus becomes, on account of this diversity of content between the ground, or rather the basis, and that which is connected with it in the grounded, just as much a formalism as formal ground itself. In the latter, the content identical with itself is indifferent to the form; in real ground this likewise takes place. Thereby there is further the circumstance that it does not contain within itself which of the manifold determinations is to be taken as the essential one. Something is a concrete of such manifold determinations, which show themselves in it equally constant and enduring. One can therefore be determined as ground just as much as another; namely, as the essential one, in comparison with which the other is then to be merely something posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"129.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0007","text":"Connected with this is what was mentioned above: that when a determination is present which in one case is regarded as the ground of another, it does not follow from this that this other is posited with it in another case, or in general.—Punishment, for example, has the manifold determinations that it is retribution, further an intimidating example, that it is something threatened by the law for deterrence, and also something bringing the criminal to reflection and improvement. Each of these different determinations has been regarded as the ground of punishment, because each is an essential determination and thereby the others, as distinct from it, are determined as merely contingent in relation to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"129.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0008","text":"But that which is assumed as ground is not yet the entire punishment itself; this concrete also contains those other determinations, which are only connected with it therein, without having their ground in it.—Or an official has aptitude for office, as an individual is in kinship relations, has this or that acquaintance, a particular character, has been in these or those circumstances and opportunities to show himself, etc. Each of these qualities can be ground, or be regarded as such, for his holding this office; they are a different content, connected in a third; the form of being determined over against one another as the essential and as the posited is external to this content.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"129.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0009","text":"Each of these qualities is essential to the official, because through them he is the determinate individual that he is; insofar as the office can be regarded as an external posited determination, each can be determined as ground in relation to it; but conversely those qualities themselves can also be regarded as posited, and the office as their ground. How they actually relate, i.e. in the particular case, is a determination external to the relation of ground and to the content itself; it is a third which confers upon them the form of ground and grounded.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"129.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0010","text":"Thus, in general, every existent can have manifold grounds; each of its determinations of content pervades the concrete whole as identical with itself and can therefore be regarded as essential; to the manifold respects, i.e. determinations, which lie outside the thing itself, the contingency of the mode of connection has opened door and gate without limit.—Whether a ground has this or that consequence is therefore equally contingent. Moral motives, for example, are essential determinations of moral nature, but what follows from them is at the same time an externality distinct from them, which follows from them and also does not follow; only through a third does it accede to them. More precisely, this is to be understood thus: that it is not contingent to the moral determination, when it is ground, to have a consequence or a grounded; but whether it is made ground at all or not is contingent.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"129.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0011","text":"But since the content which is its consequence, when it has been made ground, also again has the nature of externality, it can immediately be annulled through another externality. Thus an action can proceed from a moral motive, or it may not. Conversely, an action can have manifold grounds; as a concrete, it contains manifold essential determinations, each of which can therefore be adduced as ground. The seeking and adducing of grounds, in which reasoning principally consists, is therefore an endless roving about that contains no final determination; for one or several good grounds can be adduced for everything and anything, as well as for its opposite, and a multitude of grounds can be present without anything resulting from them.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"129.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_36:P0012","text":"What Socrates and Plato call sophistry is nothing other than reasoning from grounds; Plato opposes to it the consideration of the Idea, i.e. of the thing in and for itself, or in its Concept. Grounds are taken only from essential determinations of content, relations, and respects, of which every thing, just like its opposite, has several; in their form of essentiality, one is as valid as another; because it does not contain the whole scope of the thing, it is a one-sided ground, of which the other particular sides in turn have particular grounds, and none of which exhausts the thing that constitutes their connection and contains them all; none is a sufficient ground, i.e. the Concept","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"129.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_36:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"2d20c0efdfa71f7d5a45891a3860dc77f363fba91a738cfed9b0589674eaf65d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2","title":"c. The Complete Ground.","order":130,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CD_2","text":"1. Im realen Grunde sind der Grund als Inhalt, und als Beziehung, nur Grundlagen. Jener ist nur gesetzt als wesentlich und als Grund; die Beziehung ist das Etwas des Begründeten, als das unbestimmte Substrat eines verschiedenen Inhalts, eine Verknüpfung desselben, die nicht seine eigne Reflexion, sondern eine äußerliche und somit nur eine gesetzte ist. Die reale Grundbeziehung ist daher vielmehr der Grund als aufgehobener; sie macht somit vielmehr die Seite des Begründeten oder des Gesetztseyns aus. Als Gesetztseyn aber ist nun der Grund selbst in seinen Grund zurückgegangen; er ist nun ein Begründetes, das einen andern Grund hat. Dieser bestimmt sich hierdurch so, daß er erstlich das mit dem realen Grunde als seinem Begründeten Identische ist; beide Seiten haben nach dieser Bestimmung einen und denselben Inhalt; die zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen und deren Verknüpfung im Etwas befinden sich gleichfalls im neuen Grunde. Aber zweitens der neue Grund, in welchen sich jene nur gesetzte äußerliche Verknüpfung aufgehoben hat, ist als ihre Reflexion in sich die absolute Beziehung der zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen.\n\nDadurch daß der reale Grund selbst in seinen Grund zurückgegangen ist, stellt sich an ihm die Identität des Grundes und Begründeten, oder der formelle Grund wieder her. Die entstandene Grundbeziehung ist darum die vollständige, die den formellen und realen Grund zugleich in sich enthält und die im letztern gegen einander unmittelbaren Inhaltsbestimmungen vermittelt.\n\n2. Die Grundbeziehung hat sich hiermit folgendermassen näher bestimmt. Erstens Etwas hat einen Grund; es enthält die Inhaltsbestimmung, welche der Grund ist, und noch eine zweite als durch ihn gesetzte. Aber als gleichgültiger Inhalt, ist die eine nicht an ihr selbst Grund, die andere nicht an ihr selbst das Begründete von jener, sondern diese Beziehung ist in der Unmittelbarkeit des Inhalts als eine aufgehobene oder gesetzte, und hat als solche in einer andern ihren Grund. Diese zweite Beziehung als nur der Form nach unterschieden, hat denselben Inhalt als die erstere, nämlich die beiden Inhaltsbestimmungen, ist aber die unmittelbare Verknüpfung derselben. Indem jedoch das Verknüpfte überhaupt verschiedener Inhalt, somit gegen einander gleichgültige Bestimmung ist, ist sie nicht ihre wahrhaft absolute Beziehung, daß die eine der Bestimmungen das im Gesetztseyn mit sich Identische, die andere nur dieß Gesetztseyn desselben Identischen wäre; sondern ein Etwas trägt sie und macht ihre nicht reflektirte, sondern nur unmittelbare Beziehung aus, welche daher nur relativer Grund gegen die Verknüpfung im andern Etwas ist. Die beiden Etwas sind also die zwei unterschiedenen Beziehungen von Inhalt, die sich ergeben haben. Sie stehen in der identischen Grundbeziehung der Form; sie sind ein und derselbe ganze Inhalt, nämlich die zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen und deren Beziehung; unterschieden sind sie nur durch die Art dieser Beziehung, die in dem einen unmittelbare, in dem andern gesetzte Beziehung ist; wodurch sich das eine von dem Andern nur der Form nach als Grund und Begründetes unterscheidet.—Zweitens ist diese Grundbeziehung nicht nur formell, sondern auch real. Der formelle Grund geht in den realen über, wie sich gezeigt hat; die Momente der Form reflektiren sich in sich selbst; sie sind ein selbstständiger Inhalt, und die Grundbeziehung enthält auch einen eigenthümlichen Inhalt als Grund und einen als Begründetes. Der Inhalt macht zuerst die unmittelbare Identität der beiden Seiten des formellen Grundes aus, so haben sie einen und denselben Inhalt. Aber er hat auch die Form an ihm selbst und ist so gedoppelter Inhalt, der sich als Grund und Begründetes verhält. Die eine der zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen der beiden Etwas ist daher bestimmt, als ihnen nicht bloß gemeinschaftlich nach äußerer Vergleichung, sondern ihr identisches Substrat und die Grundlage ihrer Beziehung zu seyn. Gegen die andere Inhaltsbestimmung ist sie die wesentliche und Grund derselben als der gesetzten, nämlich in dem Etwas, dessen Beziehung die begründete ist. Im ersten Etwas, das die Grundbeziehung ist, ist auch diese zweite InhaltsBestimmung unmittelbar und an sich mit der ersten verknüpft. Das andere Etwas aber enthält nur die eine an sich als das, worin es mit dem ersten Etwas unmittelbar identisch ist, die andere aber als die in ihm gesetzte. Die erstere Inhaltsbestimmung ist Grund derselben dadurch, daß sie in dem ersten Etwas ursprünglich mit der andern Inhaltsbestimmung verknüpft ist.\n\nDie Grundbeziehung der Inhaltsbestimmungen im zweiten Etwas ist so durch die erste an sich seyende Beziehung des ersten Etwas vermittelt. Der Schluß ist, weil in einem Etwas die Bestimmung B mit der Bestimmung A an sich verknüpft ist, so ist im zweiten Etwas, dem nur die eine Bestimmung A unmittelbar zukommt, auch B damit verknüpft. Im zweiten Etwas ist nicht nur diese zweite Bestimmung mittelbar, sondern auch daß seine unmittelbare Grund ist, ist vermittelt, nämlich durch ihre ursprüngliche Beziehung auf B im ersten Etwas. Diese Beziehung ist somit Grund des Grundes A, und die ganze Grundbeziehung ist zweiten Etwas als Gesetztes oder Begründetes.\n\n3. Der reale Grund zeigt sich als die sich äußerliche Reflexion des Grundes; die vollständige Vermittelung desselben ist die Wiederherstellung seiner Identität mit sich. Aber indem diese dadurch zugleich die Äußerlichkeit des realen Grundes erhalten hat, so ist die Formelle Grundbeziehung in dieser Einheit ihrer selbst und des realen Grundes, ebenso sehr sich setzender als sich aufhebender Grund; die Grundbeziehung vermittelt sich durch ihre Negation mit sich. Erstlich ist der Grund als die ursprüngliche Beziehung, Beziehung von unmittelbaren Inhaltsbestimmungen. Die Grundbeziehung hat als wesentliche Form zu ihren Seiten solche, welche aufgehobene oder Momente sind. Daher als Form unmittelbarer Bestimmungen ist sie die mit sich identische Beziehung zugleich als Beziehung ihrer Negation; somit ist sie Grund nicht an und für sich selbst, sondern als Beziehung auf die aufgehobene Grundbeziehung.—Zweitens die aufgehobene Beziehung oder das Unmittelbare, das in der ursprünglichen und der gesetzten Beziehung die identische Grundlage ist, ist realer Grund gleichfalls nicht an und für sich selbst, sondern es ist durch jene ursprüngliche Verknüpfung gesetzt, daß es Grund sey.-Die Grundbeziehung in ihrer Totalität ist somit wesentlich voraussetzende Reflexion; der formelle Grund setzt die unmittelbare Inhaltsbestimmung voraus, und diese als realer Grund setzt die Form voraus. Der Grund ist also die Form als unmittelbare Verknüpfung; aber so daß sie sich von sich selbst abstößt, und die Unmittelbarkeit vielmehr voraussetzt, sich darin auf sich als auf ein Anderes bezieht. Dieses Unmittelbare ist die Inhaltsbestimmung, der einfache Grund; aber er ist als dieß, nämlich als Grund, ebenso von sich abgestoßen und bezieht sich auf sich gleichfalls als auf ein Anderes.—So hat sich die totale Grundbeziehung zur bedingenden Vermittlung bestimmt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0001","text":"1. Im realen Grunde sind der Grund als Inhalt, und als Beziehung, nur Grundlagen. Jener ist nur gesetzt als wesentlich und als Grund; die Beziehung ist das Etwas des Begründeten, als das unbestimmte Substrat eines verschiedenen Inhalts, eine Verknüpfung desselben, die nicht seine eigne Reflexion, sondern eine äußerliche und somit nur eine gesetzte ist. Die reale Grundbeziehung ist daher vielmehr der Grund als aufgehobener; sie macht somit vielmehr die Seite des Begründeten oder des Gesetztseyns aus. Als Gesetztseyn aber ist nun der Grund selbst in seinen Grund zurückgegangen; er ist nun ein Begründetes, das einen andern Grund hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"130.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0002","text":"Dieser bestimmt sich hierdurch so, daß er erstlich das mit dem realen Grunde als seinem Begründeten Identische ist; beide Seiten haben nach dieser Bestimmung einen und denselben Inhalt; die zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen und deren Verknüpfung im Etwas befinden sich gleichfalls im neuen Grunde. Aber zweitens der neue Grund, in welchen sich jene nur gesetzte äußerliche Verknüpfung aufgehoben hat, ist als ihre Reflexion in sich die absolute Beziehung der zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"130.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0003","text":"Dadurch daß der reale Grund selbst in seinen Grund zurückgegangen ist, stellt sich an ihm die Identität des Grundes und Begründeten, oder der formelle Grund wieder her. Die entstandene Grundbeziehung ist darum die vollständige, die den formellen und realen Grund zugleich in sich enthält und die im letztern gegen einander unmittelbaren Inhaltsbestimmungen vermittelt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"130.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0004","text":"2. Die Grundbeziehung hat sich hiermit folgendermassen näher bestimmt. Erstens Etwas hat einen Grund; es enthält die Inhaltsbestimmung, welche der Grund ist, und noch eine zweite als durch ihn gesetzte. Aber als gleichgültiger Inhalt, ist die eine nicht an ihr selbst Grund, die andere nicht an ihr selbst das Begründete von jener, sondern diese Beziehung ist in der Unmittelbarkeit des Inhalts als eine aufgehobene oder gesetzte, und hat als solche in einer andern ihren Grund. Diese zweite Beziehung als nur der Form nach unterschieden, hat denselben Inhalt als die erstere, nämlich die beiden Inhaltsbestimmungen, ist aber die unmittelbare Verknüpfung derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"130.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0005","text":"Indem jedoch das Verknüpfte überhaupt verschiedener Inhalt, somit gegen einander gleichgültige Bestimmung ist, ist sie nicht ihre wahrhaft absolute Beziehung, daß die eine der Bestimmungen das im Gesetztseyn mit sich Identische, die andere nur dieß Gesetztseyn desselben Identischen wäre; sondern ein Etwas trägt sie und macht ihre nicht reflektirte, sondern nur unmittelbare Beziehung aus, welche daher nur relativer Grund gegen die Verknüpfung im andern Etwas ist. Die beiden Etwas sind also die zwei unterschiedenen Beziehungen von Inhalt, die sich ergeben haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"130.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0006","text":"Sie stehen in der identischen Grundbeziehung der Form; sie sind ein und derselbe ganze Inhalt, nämlich die zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen und deren Beziehung; unterschieden sind sie nur durch die Art dieser Beziehung, die in dem einen unmittelbare, in dem andern gesetzte Beziehung ist; wodurch sich das eine von dem Andern nur der Form nach als Grund und Begründetes unterscheidet.—Zweitens ist diese Grundbeziehung nicht nur formell, sondern auch real. Der formelle Grund geht in den realen über, wie sich gezeigt hat; die Momente der Form reflektiren sich in sich selbst; sie sind ein selbstständiger Inhalt, und die Grundbeziehung enthält auch einen eigenthümlichen Inhalt als Grund und einen als Begründetes. Der Inhalt macht zuerst die unmittelbare Identität der beiden Seiten des formellen Grundes aus, so haben sie einen und denselben Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"130.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0007","text":"Aber er hat auch die Form an ihm selbst und ist so gedoppelter Inhalt, der sich als Grund und Begründetes verhält. Die eine der zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen der beiden Etwas ist daher bestimmt, als ihnen nicht bloß gemeinschaftlich nach äußerer Vergleichung, sondern ihr identisches Substrat und die Grundlage ihrer Beziehung zu seyn. Gegen die andere Inhaltsbestimmung ist sie die wesentliche und Grund derselben als der gesetzten, nämlich in dem Etwas, dessen Beziehung die begründete ist. Im ersten Etwas, das die Grundbeziehung ist, ist auch diese zweite InhaltsBestimmung unmittelbar und an sich mit der ersten verknüpft. Das andere Etwas aber enthält nur die eine an sich als das, worin es mit dem ersten Etwas unmittelbar identisch ist, die andere aber als die in ihm gesetzte.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"130.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0008","text":"Die erstere Inhaltsbestimmung ist Grund derselben dadurch, daß sie in dem ersten Etwas ursprünglich mit der andern Inhaltsbestimmung verknüpft ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"130.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0009","text":"Die Grundbeziehung der Inhaltsbestimmungen im zweiten Etwas ist so durch die erste an sich seyende Beziehung des ersten Etwas vermittelt. Der Schluß ist, weil in einem Etwas die Bestimmung B mit der Bestimmung A an sich verknüpft ist, so ist im zweiten Etwas, dem nur die eine Bestimmung A unmittelbar zukommt, auch B damit verknüpft. Im zweiten Etwas ist nicht nur diese zweite Bestimmung mittelbar, sondern auch daß seine unmittelbare Grund ist, ist vermittelt, nämlich durch ihre ursprüngliche Beziehung auf B im ersten Etwas. Diese Beziehung ist somit Grund des Grundes A, und die ganze Grundbeziehung ist zweiten Etwas als Gesetztes oder Begründetes.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"130.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0010","text":"3. Der reale Grund zeigt sich als die sich äußerliche Reflexion des Grundes; die vollständige Vermittelung desselben ist die Wiederherstellung seiner Identität mit sich. Aber indem diese dadurch zugleich die Äußerlichkeit des realen Grundes erhalten hat, so ist die Formelle Grundbeziehung in dieser Einheit ihrer selbst und des realen Grundes, ebenso sehr sich setzender als sich aufhebender Grund; die Grundbeziehung vermittelt sich durch ihre Negation mit sich. Erstlich ist der Grund als die ursprüngliche Beziehung, Beziehung von unmittelbaren Inhaltsbestimmungen. Die Grundbeziehung hat als wesentliche Form zu ihren Seiten solche, welche aufgehobene oder Momente sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"130.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0011","text":"Daher als Form unmittelbarer Bestimmungen ist sie die mit sich identische Beziehung zugleich als Beziehung ihrer Negation; somit ist sie Grund nicht an und für sich selbst, sondern als Beziehung auf die aufgehobene Grundbeziehung.—Zweitens die aufgehobene Beziehung oder das Unmittelbare, das in der ursprünglichen und der gesetzten Beziehung die identische Grundlage ist, ist realer Grund gleichfalls nicht an und für sich selbst, sondern es ist durch jene ursprüngliche Verknüpfung gesetzt, daß es Grund sey.-Die Grundbeziehung in ihrer Totalität ist somit wesentlich voraussetzende Reflexion; der formelle Grund setzt die unmittelbare Inhaltsbestimmung voraus, und diese als realer Grund setzt die Form voraus.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"130.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0012","text":"Der Grund ist also die Form als unmittelbare Verknüpfung; aber so daß sie sich von sich selbst abstößt, und die Unmittelbarkeit vielmehr voraussetzt, sich darin auf sich als auf ein Anderes bezieht. Dieses Unmittelbare ist die Inhaltsbestimmung, der einfache Grund; aber er ist als dieß, nämlich als Grund, ebenso von sich abgestoßen und bezieht sich auf sich gleichfalls als auf ein Anderes.—So hat sich die totale Grundbeziehung zur bedingenden Vermittlung bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"130.12"}],"sha256":"568d53cce6e04e3de28a2d327d6c54744ce4784a0d6a856cf7678f7ee497b46e","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105205640664Z_88dcc0dd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Complete Ground.","source_sha256":"568d53cce6e04e3de28a2d327d6c54744ce4784a0d6a856cf7678f7ee497b46e","sha256":"6e65e72c8180d036aaa83d9462f30e2d9cc5ec47a4d3e76658610d3d10e41b86","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:52:05.640676+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0001","text":"1. In the real ground, the ground as content, and as relation, are only grounds. The former is only posited as essential and as ground; the relation is the Something of the grounded, as the indeterminate substrate of a different content, a connection of the same which is not its own reflection, but an external and thus only a posited one. The real ground-relation is therefore rather the ground as sublated; it thus rather constitutes the side of the grounded or of positedness. But as positedness, the ground itself has now returned into its ground; it is now a grounded, which has another ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"130.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0002","text":"Through this the latter determines itself in such a way that, first, it is identical with the real ground as its grounded; both sides, according to this determination, have one and the same content; the two determinations of content and their connection in the Something are likewise found in the new ground. But secondly, the new ground, into which that merely posited external connection has sublated itself, is, as its reflection into itself, the absolute relation of the two determinations of content.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"130.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0003","text":"By the real ground itself having returned into its ground, the identity of ground and grounded, or the formal ground, is restored in it. The ground-relation which has arisen is therefore the complete one, which contains within itself formal and real ground at once and mediates the determinations of content that are immediate with respect to one another in the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"130.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0004","text":"2. The ground-relation has hereby determined itself more precisely as follows. First, Something has a ground; it contains the determination of content which is the ground, and yet a second one as posited by it. But, as indifferent content, the one is not in itself ground, nor the other in itself the grounded of the former; rather, this relation is, in the immediacy of content, a sublated or posited one, and as such has its ground in another. This second relation, as distinguished only in respect of form, has the same content as the first, namely the two determinations of content, but is their immediate connection.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"130.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0005","text":"Yet inasmuch as what is connected is in general different content, hence a determination indifferent toward the other, it is not their truly absolute relation, such that one of the determinations would be that which is identical with itself in positedness, the other only this positedness of the identical; rather, a Something bears them and constitutes their not reflected, but only immediate relation, which is therefore only a relative ground as against the connection in the other Something. The two Somethings are thus the two distinct relations of content which have resulted.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"130.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0006","text":"They stand in the identical ground-relation of form; they are one and the same whole content, namely the two determinations of content and their relation; they are distinguished only by the mode of this relation, which in the one is immediate relation, in the other posited relation; whereby the one is distinguished from the other only in respect of form as ground and grounded.—Secondly, this ground-relation is not only formal, but also real. The formal ground passes over into the real, as has been shown; the moments of form reflect into themselves; they are a self-subsistent content, and the ground-relation also contains a peculiar content as ground and one as grounded. Content first constitutes the immediate identity of the two sides of the formal ground; thus they have one and the same content.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"130.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0007","text":"But it also has form in itself and is thus a doubled content, which behaves as ground and grounded. One of the two determinations of content of the two Somethings is therefore determined as not merely common to them according to external comparison, but as their identical substrate and the foundation of their relation. With respect to the other determination of content, it is the essential one and the ground of it as posited, namely in the Something whose relation is the grounded one. In the first Something, which is the ground-relation, this second determination of content is also immediately and in itself connected with the first. But the other Something contains only the one in itself, as that in which it is immediately identical with the first Something, but the other as posited in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"130.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0008","text":"The former determination of content is the ground of the latter by virtue of its being originally connected in the first Something with the other determination of content.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"130.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0009","text":"The ground-relation of the determinations of content in the second Something is thus mediated through the first relation of the first Something, which is in itself. The inference is: because in one Something determination B is connected in itself with determination A, in the second Something, to which only the one determination A belongs immediately, B is also connected with it. In the second Something not only is this second determination mediated, but also that its immediate determination is ground is mediated, namely through its original relation to B in the first Something. This relation is thus the ground of the ground A, and the whole ground-relation is positedness or groundedness in the second Something.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"130.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0010","text":"3. The real ground shows itself as the reflection of the ground external to itself; its complete mediation is the restoration of its identity with itself. But inasmuch as this has thereby at the same time retained the externality of the real ground, the formal ground-relation, in this unity of itself and the real ground, is just as much ground that posits itself as ground that sublates itself; the ground-relation mediates itself with itself through its negation. First, the ground, as the original relation, is relation of immediate determinations of content. The ground-relation has, as essential form, for its sides such as are sublated or moments.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"130.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0011","text":"Hence, as form of immediate determinations, it is the relation identical with itself, at the same time as relation to its negation; thus it is ground not in and for itself, but as relation to the sublated ground-relation.—Secondly, the sublated relation, or the immediate, which in the original and in the posited relation is the identical foundation, is likewise real ground not in and for itself, but it is posited through that original connection that it is ground.—The ground-relation in its totality is thus essentially presupposing reflection; the formal ground presupposes the immediate determination of content, and this, as real ground, presupposes form.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"130.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0012","text":"The ground is therefore form as immediate connection; but such that it repels itself from itself, and rather presupposes immediacy, relates itself therein to itself as to an Other. This immediate is the determination of content, the simple ground; but as this, namely as ground, it is likewise repelled from itself and relates itself to itself equally as to an Other.—Thus the total ground-relation has determined itself as conditioning mediation.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"130.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_2:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"716c5b31d699103f82fbead0ca12e21dd68646a82b67a09bad2720c65b53f6a6","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Der vollständige Grund."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Der vollständige Grund.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0","title":"a. The Relatively Unconditioned.","order":131,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DRU0","text":"## C. Die Bedingung.\n\n## a. Das relativ Unbedingte.\n\n1. Der Grund ist das Unmittelbare und das Begründete das Vermittelte. Aber er ist setzende Reflexion, als solche macht er sich zum Gesetztseyn, und ist voraussetzende Reflexion, so bezieht er sich auf sich als auf ein Aufgehobenes, auf ein Unmittelbares, wodurch er selbst vermittelt ist. Diese Vermittelung, als Fortgehen vom Unmittelbaren zum Grunde, ist nicht eine äußere Reflexion, sondern, wie sich ergeben, das eigne Thun des Grundes, oder was dasselbe ist, die Grundbeziehung ist als Reflexion in die Identität mit sich ebenso wesentlich sich entäußernde Reflexion. Das Unmittelbare, auf das der Grund sich als auf seine wesentliche Voraussetzung bezieht, ist die Bedingung; der reale Grund ist daher wesentlich bedingt. Die Bestimmtheit, die er enthält, ist das Andersseyn seiner selbst.\n\nDie Bedingung ist also erstens ein unmittelbares, mannigfaltiges Daseyn. Zweitens ist dieses Daseyn bezogen auf ein Anderes, auf etwas, das Grund ist, nicht dieses Daseyns, sondern in anderer Rüksicht; denn das Daseyn selbst ist unmittelbar und ohne Grund. Nach jener Beziehung ist es ein Gesetztes; das unmittelbare Daseyn soll als Bedingung nicht für sich, sondern für Anderes seyn. Aber zugleich ist dieß, daß es so für Anderes ist, selbst nur ein Gesetztseyn; daß es ein Gesetztes ist, ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben, und ein Daseyn ist dagegen, Bedingung zu seyn, gleichgültig. Drittens ist die Bedingung so ein Unmittelbares, daß sie die Voraussetzung des Grundes ausmacht. Sie ist in dieser Bestimmung die in die Identität mit sich zurückgegangene Formbeziehung des Grundes, hiermit der Inhalt desselben. Aber der Inhalt als solcher ist nur die gleichgültige Einheit des Grundes, als in der Form; ohne Form kein Inhalt. Er befreit sich noch von derselben, indem die Grundbeziehung im vollständigen Grunde zu einer gegen ihre Identität äußerlichen Beziehung wird; wodurch der Inhalt die Unmittelbarkeit erhält. Insofern daher die Bedingung das ist, worin die Grundbeziehung ihre Identität mit sich hat, macht sie seinen Inhalt aus; aber weil er das gegen diese Form Gleichgültige ist, ist er nur an sich ihr Inhalt, ein solches, das erst Inhalt werden soll, hiermit das Material für den Grund ausmacht. Als Bedingung gesetzt, hat das Daseyn nach dem zweiten Momente die Bestimmung, seine gleichgültige Unmittelbarkeit zu verlieren und Moment eines Andern zu werden. Durch seine Unmittelbarkeit ist es gleichgültig gegen diese Beziehung; insofern es aber in dieselbe tritt, macht es das Ansichseyn des Grundes aus, und ist das Unbedingte für denselben. Um Bedingung zu seyn, hat es am Grunde seine Voraussetzung, und ist selbst bedingt; aber diese Bestimmung ist ihm äußerlich.\n\n2. Etwas ist nicht durch seine Bedingung; seine Bedingung ist nicht sein Grund. Sie ist das Moment der unbedingten Unmittelbarkeit für den Grund, aber ist nicht selbst die Bewegung und das Setzen, das sich negativ auf sich bezieht, und sich zum Gesetztseyn macht. Der Bedingung steht daher die Grundbeziehung gegenüber. Etwas hat außer seiner Bedingung auch einen Grund.—Dieser ist die leere Bewegung der Reflexion, weil sie die Unmittelbarkeit als ihre Voraussetzung außer ihr hat. Sie ist aber die ganze Form und das selbstständige Vermitteln; denn die Bedingung ist nicht ihr Grund. Indem dieses Vermitteln sich als Setzen auf sich bezieht, ist es nach dieser Seite gleichfalls ein Unmittelbares und Unbedingtes; es setzt sich zwar voraus, aber als entäußertes oder aufgehobenes Setzen; das was es hingegen seiner Bestimmung nach ist, ist es an und für sich selbst. —Insofern so die Grundbeziehung selbstständige Beziehung auf sich ist und die Identität der Reflexion an ihr selbst hat, hat sie einen eigenthümlichen Inhalt, gegen den Inhalt der Bedingung. Jener ist Inhalt des Grundes und darum wesentlich formirt; dieser hingegen ist nur unmittelbares Material, dem die Beziehung auf den Grund zugleich ebenso äußerlich ist, als es auch das Ansichseyn desselben ausmacht; es ist somit eine Vermischung von selbstständigem Inhalt, der keine Beziehung auf den Inhalt der Grundbestimmung hat, und von solchem, der in sie eingeht, und als ihr Material, Moment derselben werden soll.\n\n3. Die beiden Seiten des Ganzen, Bedingung und Grund, sind also einer Seits gleichgültige und unbedingte gegen einander; das eine als das Unbezogene, dem die Beziehung, in welcher es Bedingung ist, äußerlich ist; das andere als die Beziehung oder Form, für welche das bestimmte Daseyn der Bedingung nur als Material ist, als ein Passives, dessen Form, die es für sich an ihm hat, eine unwesentliche ist. Ferner sind auch beide vermittelte. Die Bedingung ist das Ansichseyn des Grundes; sie ist so sehr wesentliches Moment der Grundbeziehung, daß sie die einfache Identität desselben mit sich ist. Aber dieß ist auch aufgehoben; dieß Ansichseyn ist nur ein gesetztes; das unmittelbare Daseyn ist gleichgültig dagegen Bedingung zu seyn. Daß die Bedingung des Ansichseyns für den Grund ist, macht also ihre Seite aus, nach welcher sie eine vermittelte ist. Ebenso die Grundbeziehung hat in ihrer Selbstständigkeit, auch eine Voraussetzung, und ihr Ansichseyn außer sich.—Somit ist jede der beiden Seiten der Widerspruch der gleichgültigen Unmittelbarkeit und der wesentlichen Vermittelung, Beides in Einer Beziehung;—oder der Widerspruch des selbstständigen Bestehens und der Bestimmung, nur Moment zu seyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0001","text":"## C. Die Bedingung.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"131.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0002","text":"## a. Das relativ Unbedingte.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"131.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0003","text":"1. Der Grund ist das Unmittelbare und das Begründete das Vermittelte. Aber er ist setzende Reflexion, als solche macht er sich zum Gesetztseyn, und ist voraussetzende Reflexion, so bezieht er sich auf sich als auf ein Aufgehobenes, auf ein Unmittelbares, wodurch er selbst vermittelt ist. Diese Vermittelung, als Fortgehen vom Unmittelbaren zum Grunde, ist nicht eine äußere Reflexion, sondern, wie sich ergeben, das eigne Thun des Grundes, oder was dasselbe ist, die Grundbeziehung ist als Reflexion in die Identität mit sich ebenso wesentlich sich entäußernde Reflexion. Das Unmittelbare, auf das der Grund sich als auf seine wesentliche Voraussetzung bezieht, ist die Bedingung; der reale Grund ist daher wesentlich bedingt. Die Bestimmtheit, die er enthält, ist das Andersseyn seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"131.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0004","text":"Die Bedingung ist also erstens ein unmittelbares, mannigfaltiges Daseyn. Zweitens ist dieses Daseyn bezogen auf ein Anderes, auf etwas, das Grund ist, nicht dieses Daseyns, sondern in anderer Rüksicht; denn das Daseyn selbst ist unmittelbar und ohne Grund. Nach jener Beziehung ist es ein Gesetztes; das unmittelbare Daseyn soll als Bedingung nicht für sich, sondern für Anderes seyn. Aber zugleich ist dieß, daß es so für Anderes ist, selbst nur ein Gesetztseyn; daß es ein Gesetztes ist, ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben, und ein Daseyn ist dagegen, Bedingung zu seyn, gleichgültig. Drittens ist die Bedingung so ein Unmittelbares, daß sie die Voraussetzung des Grundes ausmacht. Sie ist in dieser Bestimmung die in die Identität mit sich zurückgegangene Formbeziehung des Grundes, hiermit der Inhalt desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"131.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0005","text":"Aber der Inhalt als solcher ist nur die gleichgültige Einheit des Grundes, als in der Form; ohne Form kein Inhalt. Er befreit sich noch von derselben, indem die Grundbeziehung im vollständigen Grunde zu einer gegen ihre Identität äußerlichen Beziehung wird; wodurch der Inhalt die Unmittelbarkeit erhält. Insofern daher die Bedingung das ist, worin die Grundbeziehung ihre Identität mit sich hat, macht sie seinen Inhalt aus; aber weil er das gegen diese Form Gleichgültige ist, ist er nur an sich ihr Inhalt, ein solches, das erst Inhalt werden soll, hiermit das Material für den Grund ausmacht. Als Bedingung gesetzt, hat das Daseyn nach dem zweiten Momente die Bestimmung, seine gleichgültige Unmittelbarkeit zu verlieren und Moment eines Andern zu werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"131.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0006","text":"Durch seine Unmittelbarkeit ist es gleichgültig gegen diese Beziehung; insofern es aber in dieselbe tritt, macht es das Ansichseyn des Grundes aus, und ist das Unbedingte für denselben. Um Bedingung zu seyn, hat es am Grunde seine Voraussetzung, und ist selbst bedingt; aber diese Bestimmung ist ihm äußerlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"131.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0007","text":"2. Etwas ist nicht durch seine Bedingung; seine Bedingung ist nicht sein Grund. Sie ist das Moment der unbedingten Unmittelbarkeit für den Grund, aber ist nicht selbst die Bewegung und das Setzen, das sich negativ auf sich bezieht, und sich zum Gesetztseyn macht. Der Bedingung steht daher die Grundbeziehung gegenüber. Etwas hat außer seiner Bedingung auch einen Grund.—Dieser ist die leere Bewegung der Reflexion, weil sie die Unmittelbarkeit als ihre Voraussetzung außer ihr hat. Sie ist aber die ganze Form und das selbstständige Vermitteln; denn die Bedingung ist nicht ihr Grund. Indem dieses Vermitteln sich als Setzen auf sich bezieht, ist es nach dieser Seite gleichfalls ein Unmittelbares und Unbedingtes; es setzt sich zwar voraus, aber als entäußertes oder aufgehobenes Setzen; das was es hingegen seiner Bestimmung nach ist, ist es an und für sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"131.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0008","text":"—Insofern so die Grundbeziehung selbstständige Beziehung auf sich ist und die Identität der Reflexion an ihr selbst hat, hat sie einen eigenthümlichen Inhalt, gegen den Inhalt der Bedingung. Jener ist Inhalt des Grundes und darum wesentlich formirt; dieser hingegen ist nur unmittelbares Material, dem die Beziehung auf den Grund zugleich ebenso äußerlich ist, als es auch das Ansichseyn desselben ausmacht; es ist somit eine Vermischung von selbstständigem Inhalt, der keine Beziehung auf den Inhalt der Grundbestimmung hat, und von solchem, der in sie eingeht, und als ihr Material, Moment derselben werden soll.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"131.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0009","text":"3. Die beiden Seiten des Ganzen, Bedingung und Grund, sind also einer Seits gleichgültige und unbedingte gegen einander; das eine als das Unbezogene, dem die Beziehung, in welcher es Bedingung ist, äußerlich ist; das andere als die Beziehung oder Form, für welche das bestimmte Daseyn der Bedingung nur als Material ist, als ein Passives, dessen Form, die es für sich an ihm hat, eine unwesentliche ist. Ferner sind auch beide vermittelte. Die Bedingung ist das Ansichseyn des Grundes; sie ist so sehr wesentliches Moment der Grundbeziehung, daß sie die einfache Identität desselben mit sich ist. Aber dieß ist auch aufgehoben; dieß Ansichseyn ist nur ein gesetztes; das unmittelbare Daseyn ist gleichgültig dagegen Bedingung zu seyn. Daß die Bedingung des Ansichseyns für den Grund ist, macht also ihre Seite aus, nach welcher sie eine vermittelte ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"131.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0010","text":"Ebenso die Grundbeziehung hat in ihrer Selbstständigkeit, auch eine Voraussetzung, und ihr Ansichseyn außer sich.—Somit ist jede der beiden Seiten der Widerspruch der gleichgültigen Unmittelbarkeit und der wesentlichen Vermittelung, Beides in Einer Beziehung;—oder der Widerspruch des selbstständigen Bestehens und der Bestimmung, nur Moment zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"131.10"}],"sha256":"5c035efb246993e53507bccf4a6fcbcb5ba0973ce3e9459722bc4bd23b7f54da","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105219099152Z_e579c500","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. The Relatively Unconditioned.","source_sha256":"5c035efb246993e53507bccf4a6fcbcb5ba0973ce3e9459722bc4bd23b7f54da","sha256":"c1744fda3b0d891f64ff21d74850ef1e8ec20277b3cf703d5c5c6e20b5475b6d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:52:19.099174+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0001","text":"## C. The Condition.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"131.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0002","text":"## a. The Relatively Unconditioned.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"131.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0003","text":"1. The ground is the immediate, and what is grounded is the mediated. But it is positing reflection; as such it makes itself into positedness, and it is presupposing reflection, thus it relates itself to itself as to something sublated, as to an immediate, whereby it is itself mediated. This mediation, as a proceeding from the immediate to the ground, is not an external reflection but, as has emerged, the ground's own doing, or, what is the same, the ground-relation, as reflection into identity with itself, is equally essentially self-externalizing reflection. The immediate to which the ground relates itself as to its essential presupposition is the condition; the real ground is therefore essentially conditioned. The determinacy which it contains is its own otherness.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"131.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0004","text":"The condition is thus, first, an immediate, manifold existence. Second, this existence is related to an other, to something which is ground, not of this existence, but in another respect; for existence itself is immediate and without ground. According to that relation it is a posited; immediate existence, as condition, is not to be for itself but for an other. But at the same time, this being for an other is itself only a positedness; its being a posited is sublated in its immediacy, and existence is indifferent to being a condition. Third, the condition is thus an immediate such that it constitutes the presupposition of the ground. In this determination it is the ground's form-relation returned into identity with itself, and thereby its content.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"131.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0005","text":"But content as such is only the indifferent unity of the ground, as in the form; without form, no content. It further frees itself from the latter, in that the ground-relation in the complete ground becomes a relation external to its identity; whereby the content receives immediacy. In so far, therefore, as the condition is that wherein the ground-relation has its identity with itself, it constitutes its content; but because this content is what is indifferent toward this form, it is only in itself its content, something which is only to become content, and thereby constitutes the material for the ground. Posited as condition, existence has, according to the second moment, the determination of losing its indifferent immediacy and becoming a moment of an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"131.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0006","text":"By virtue of its immediacy it is indifferent to this relation; but in so far as it enters into it, it constitutes the in-itself-being of the ground, and is the unconditioned for it. In order to be condition, it has its presupposition in the ground, and is itself conditioned; but this determination is external to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"131.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0007","text":"2. Something is not through its condition; its condition is not its ground. It is the moment of unconditioned immediacy for the ground, but is not itself the movement and the positing which relates itself negatively to itself and makes itself into positedness. The ground-relation therefore stands opposed to the condition. Something has, besides its condition, also a ground.—This is the empty movement of reflection, because it has immediacy as its presupposition outside itself. But it is the whole form and self-subsistent mediating; for the condition is not its ground. In that this mediating relates itself to itself as positing, it is, from this side likewise, an immediate and unconditioned; it does indeed presuppose itself, but as externalized or sublated positing; what, on the other hand, it is according to its determination, it is in and for itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"131.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0008","text":"—In so far as the ground-relation is thus a self-subsistent relation to itself and has the identity of reflection in itself, it has a peculiar content as against the content of the condition. That content is the content of the ground and is therefore essentially formed; this content, on the other hand, is only immediate material, to which the relation to the ground is at the same time as external as it also constitutes its in-itself-being; it is thus a mixture of self-subsistent content which has no relation to the content of the ground-determination, and of such content as enters into it and, as its material, is to become its moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"131.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0009","text":"3. The two sides of the whole, condition and ground, are thus, on the one hand, indifferent and unconditioned with respect to one another; the one as the unrelated, to which the relation in which it is condition is external; the other as the relation or form, for which the determinate existence of the condition is only material, as something passive, whose form, which it has in itself for itself, is an inessential one. Further, both are also mediated. The condition is the in-itself-being of the ground; it is so much an essential moment of the ground-relation that it is its simple identity with itself. But this too is sublated; this in-itself-being is only a posited; immediate existence is indifferent to being a condition. That the condition is the in-itself-being for the ground thus constitutes its side according to which it is a mediated.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"131.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0010","text":"Likewise, the ground-relation, in its self-subsistence, also has a presupposition, and its in-itself-being outside itself.—Thus each of the two sides is the contradiction of indifferent immediacy and essential mediation, both in one relation;—or the contradiction of self-subsistent subsistence and the determination of being only a moment.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"131.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DRU0:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"cf240068288c76dce49cc37af5043b3ae8a08c060f17bc07b0fc98f8986ba2a5","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Das relativ Unbedingte."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Das relativ Unbedingte.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU","title":"b. The Absolute Unconditioned.","order":132,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDAU","text":"Die beiden relativ-Unbedingten scheinen zunächst, jedes in das andere; die Bedingung als Unmittelbares in die Formbeziehung des Grundes, und diese in das unmittelbare Daseyn als sein Gesetztseyn; aber jedes ist außer diesem Scheine seines Andern an ihm selbstständig und hat seinen eigenthümlichen Inhalt.\n\nZuerst ist die Bedingung unmittelbares Daseyn; seine Form hat die zwei Momente, das Gesetztseyn, nach welchem es als Bedingung Material und Moment des Grundes ist;—und das Ansichseyn, nach welchem es die Wesentlichkeit des Grundes oder seine einfache Reflexion in sich ausmacht. Beide Seiten der Form sind dem unmittelbaren Daseyn äußerlich; denn es ist die aufgehobene Grundbeziehung.—Aber erstens ist das Daseyn an ihm selbst nur dieß, in seiner Unmittelbarkeit sich aufzuheben und zu Grunde zu gehen. Das Seyn ist überhaupt nur das Werden zum Wesen; es ist seine wesentliche Natur sich zum Gesetzten und zur Identität zu machen, die durch die Negation ihrer das Unmittelbare ist. Die Formbestimmungen also, des Gesetztseyns und des mit sich identischen Ansichseyns, die Form, wodurch das unmittelbare Daseyn Bedingung ist, sind ihm daher nicht äußerlich, sondern es ist diese Reflexion selbst. Zweitens, als Bedingung ist das Seyn nun auch als das gesetzt, was es wesentlich ist; nämlich als Moment, somit eines Andern, und zugleich als das Ansichseyn gleichfalls eines Andern; es ist an sich aber nur durch die Negation seiner, nämlich durch den Grund und durch dessen sich aufhebende und damit voraussetzende Reflexion; das Ansichseyn des Seyns ist somit nur ein Gesetztes. Dieß Ansichseyn der Bedingung hat die zwei Seiten, einer Seits ihre Wesentlichkeit als des Grundes, anderer Seits aber die Unmittelbarkeit ihres Daseyns zu seyn. Oder vielmehr Beides ist dasselbe. Das Daseyn ist ein Unmittelbares, aber die Unmittelbarkeit ist wesentlich das Vermittelte, nämlich durch den sich selbst aufhebenden Grund. Als diese durch das sich aufhebende Vermitteln vermittelte Unmittelbarkeit ist es zugleich das Ansichseyn des Grundes, und das Unbedingte desselben; aber dieß Ansichseyn ist zugleich selbst wieder ebenso sehr nur Moment oder Gesetztseyn, denn es ist vermittelt.—Die Bedingung ist daher die ganze Form der Grundbeziehung; sie ist das vorausgesetzte Ansichseyn derselben, aber damit selbst ein Gesetztseyn, und ihre Unmittelbarkeit dieß, sich zum Gesetztseyn zu machen; sich somit von sich selbst so abzustoßen, daß sie sowohl zu Grunde geht, als sie Grund ist, der sich zum Gesetztseyn macht und hiermit auch zum Begründeten; und beides ist ein und dasselbe.\n\nEbenso ist an dem bedingten Grunde das Ansichseyn nicht nur als Scheinen eines Andern an ihm. Er ist die selbstständige, das heißt, die sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion des Setzens; und hiermit das mit sich Identische, oder ist in ihm selbst sein Ansichseyn, und sein Inhalt. Aber zugleich ist er voraussetzende Reflexion; er bezieht sich negativ auf sich selbst, und setzt sich sein Ansichseyn als ihm Anderes entgegen, und die Bedingung sowohl nach ihrem Momente des Ansichseyns als des unmittelbaren Daseyns ist das eigene Moment der Grundbeziehung; das unmittelbare Daseyn ist wesentlich nur durch seinen Grund, und ist das Moment seiner als Voraussetzens. Dieser ist daher ebenso das Ganze selbst.\n\nEs ist somit überhaupt nur Ein Ganzes der Form vorhanden; aber ebenso sehr nur Ein Ganzes des Inhalts. Denn der eigenthümliche Inhalt der Bedingung ist nur wesentlicher Inhalt, insofern er die Identität der Reflexion mit sich in der Form, oder als dieß unmittelbare Daseyn an ihm selbst die Grundbeziehung ist. Dieses ist ferner nur Bedingung durch die voraussetzende Reflexion des Grundes; es ist dessen Identität mit sich selbst, oder sein Inhalt, dem er sich gegenüber setzt. Das Daseyn ist daher nicht bloß formloses Material für die Grundbeziehung, sondern weil es an ihm selbst diese Form hat, ist es formirte Materie, und als zugleich das in der Identität mit ihr gegen sie Gleichgültige ist es Inhalt. Es ist endlich derselbe Inhalt, den der Grund hat, denn es ist eben Inhalt als das in der Formbeziehung mit sich Identische.\n\nDie beiden Seiten des Ganzen, Bedingung und Grund, sind also Eine wesentliche Einheit; sowohl als Inhalt, wie als Form. Sie gehen durch sich selbst in einander über, oder indem sie Reflexionen sind, so setzen sie sich selbst als aufgehobene, beziehen sich auf diese ihre Negation und setzen sich gegenseitig voraus. Aber dieß ist zugleich nur Eine Reflexion beider, ihr Voraussetzen daher auch nur eines; die Gegenseitigkeit desselben geht vielmehr darein über, daß sie ihre Eine Identität als ihr Bestehen und ihre Grundlage voraussetzen. Diese, der eine Inhalt und Formeinheit beider, ist das wahrhaft Unbedingte; die Sache an sich selbst.—Die Bedingung ist, wie sich oben ergeben hat, nur das relativ-Unbedingte. Man pflegt sie daher selbst als ein Bedingtes zu betrachten, und nach einer neuen Bedingung zu fragen, womit der gewöhnliche Progreß ins Unendliche von Bedingung zu Bedingung eingeleitet ist. Warum wird nun bei einer Bedingung nach einer neuen Bedingung gefragt, das heißt, warum wird sie als Bedingtes angenommen? Weil sie irgend ein endliches Daseyn ist. Aber dieß ist eine weitere Bestimmung der Bedingung, die nicht in ihrem Begriffe liegt. Allein die Bedingung als solche ist darum ein Bedingtes, weil sie das gesetzte Ansichseyn ist; sie ist daher im absolut Unbedingten aufgehoben.\n\nDieses nun enthält die beiden Seiten, die Bedingung und den Grund, als seine Momente in sich; es ist die Einheit, in welche sie zurückgegangen sind. Sie beide zusammen machen die Form oder das Gesetztseyn desselben aus. Die unbedingte Sache ist Bedingung beider, aber die absolute, das heißt, die Bedingung, welche selbst Grund ist. —Als Grund ist sie nun die negative Identität, die sich in jene beiden Momente abgestoßen hat;—erstens in die Gestalt der aufgehobenen Grundbeziehung, einer unmittelbaren, einheitslosen, sich selbst äußerlichen Mannigfaltigkeit, welche sich auf den Grund als ein ihr Anderes bezieht, und zugleich das Ansichseyn desselben ausmacht; zweitens, in die Gestalt einer innerlichen, einfachen Form, welche Grund ist, aber sich auf das mit sich identische Unmittelbare als auf ein Anderes bezieht, und dasselbe als Bedingung, d. h. dieß ihr Ansich als ihr eigenes Moment bestimmt.—Diese beiden Seiten setzen die Totalität so voraus, daß sie das Setzende derselben ist. Umgekehrt, weil sie die Totalität voraussetzen, so scheint diese auch wieder durch jene bedingt zu seyn, und die Sache aus ihrer Bedingung und aus ihrem Grunde zu entspringen. Aber indem diese beiden Seiten sich als das Identische gezeigt haben, so ist das Verhältniß von Bedingung und Grund verschwunden, sie sind zu einem Scheine herabgesetzt; das absolut Unbedingte ist in seiner Bewegung des Setzens und Voraussetzens, nur die Bewegung, in welcher dieser Schein sich aufhebt. Es ist das Thun der Sache, sich zu bedingen, und ihren Bedingungen sich als Grund gegenüber zu stellen; ihre Beziehung als der Bedingungen und des Grundes ist aber ein Scheinen in sich und ihr Verhalten zu ihnen ihr Zusammengehen mit sich selbst.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0001","text":"Die beiden relativ-Unbedingten scheinen zunächst, jedes in das andere; die Bedingung als Unmittelbares in die Formbeziehung des Grundes, und diese in das unmittelbare Daseyn als sein Gesetztseyn; aber jedes ist außer diesem Scheine seines Andern an ihm selbstständig und hat seinen eigenthümlichen Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"132.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0002","text":"Zuerst ist die Bedingung unmittelbares Daseyn; seine Form hat die zwei Momente, das Gesetztseyn, nach welchem es als Bedingung Material und Moment des Grundes ist;—und das Ansichseyn, nach welchem es die Wesentlichkeit des Grundes oder seine einfache Reflexion in sich ausmacht. Beide Seiten der Form sind dem unmittelbaren Daseyn äußerlich; denn es ist die aufgehobene Grundbeziehung.—Aber erstens ist das Daseyn an ihm selbst nur dieß, in seiner Unmittelbarkeit sich aufzuheben und zu Grunde zu gehen. Das Seyn ist überhaupt nur das Werden zum Wesen; es ist seine wesentliche Natur sich zum Gesetzten und zur Identität zu machen, die durch die Negation ihrer das Unmittelbare ist. Die Formbestimmungen also, des Gesetztseyns und des mit sich identischen Ansichseyns, die Form, wodurch das unmittelbare Daseyn Bedingung ist, sind ihm daher nicht äußerlich, sondern es ist diese Reflexion selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"132.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0003","text":"Zweitens, als Bedingung ist das Seyn nun auch als das gesetzt, was es wesentlich ist; nämlich als Moment, somit eines Andern, und zugleich als das Ansichseyn gleichfalls eines Andern; es ist an sich aber nur durch die Negation seiner, nämlich durch den Grund und durch dessen sich aufhebende und damit voraussetzende Reflexion; das Ansichseyn des Seyns ist somit nur ein Gesetztes. Dieß Ansichseyn der Bedingung hat die zwei Seiten, einer Seits ihre Wesentlichkeit als des Grundes, anderer Seits aber die Unmittelbarkeit ihres Daseyns zu seyn. Oder vielmehr Beides ist dasselbe. Das Daseyn ist ein Unmittelbares, aber die Unmittelbarkeit ist wesentlich das Vermittelte, nämlich durch den sich selbst aufhebenden Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"132.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0004","text":"Als diese durch das sich aufhebende Vermitteln vermittelte Unmittelbarkeit ist es zugleich das Ansichseyn des Grundes, und das Unbedingte desselben; aber dieß Ansichseyn ist zugleich selbst wieder ebenso sehr nur Moment oder Gesetztseyn, denn es ist vermittelt.—Die Bedingung ist daher die ganze Form der Grundbeziehung; sie ist das vorausgesetzte Ansichseyn derselben, aber damit selbst ein Gesetztseyn, und ihre Unmittelbarkeit dieß, sich zum Gesetztseyn zu machen; sich somit von sich selbst so abzustoßen, daß sie sowohl zu Grunde geht, als sie Grund ist, der sich zum Gesetztseyn macht und hiermit auch zum Begründeten; und beides ist ein und dasselbe.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"132.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0005","text":"Ebenso ist an dem bedingten Grunde das Ansichseyn nicht nur als Scheinen eines Andern an ihm. Er ist die selbstständige, das heißt, die sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion des Setzens; und hiermit das mit sich Identische, oder ist in ihm selbst sein Ansichseyn, und sein Inhalt. Aber zugleich ist er voraussetzende Reflexion; er bezieht sich negativ auf sich selbst, und setzt sich sein Ansichseyn als ihm Anderes entgegen, und die Bedingung sowohl nach ihrem Momente des Ansichseyns als des unmittelbaren Daseyns ist das eigene Moment der Grundbeziehung; das unmittelbare Daseyn ist wesentlich nur durch seinen Grund, und ist das Moment seiner als Voraussetzens. Dieser ist daher ebenso das Ganze selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"132.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0006","text":"Es ist somit überhaupt nur Ein Ganzes der Form vorhanden; aber ebenso sehr nur Ein Ganzes des Inhalts. Denn der eigenthümliche Inhalt der Bedingung ist nur wesentlicher Inhalt, insofern er die Identität der Reflexion mit sich in der Form, oder als dieß unmittelbare Daseyn an ihm selbst die Grundbeziehung ist. Dieses ist ferner nur Bedingung durch die voraussetzende Reflexion des Grundes; es ist dessen Identität mit sich selbst, oder sein Inhalt, dem er sich gegenüber setzt. Das Daseyn ist daher nicht bloß formloses Material für die Grundbeziehung, sondern weil es an ihm selbst diese Form hat, ist es formirte Materie, und als zugleich das in der Identität mit ihr gegen sie Gleichgültige ist es Inhalt. Es ist endlich derselbe Inhalt, den der Grund hat, denn es ist eben Inhalt als das in der Formbeziehung mit sich Identische.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"132.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0007","text":"Die beiden Seiten des Ganzen, Bedingung und Grund, sind also Eine wesentliche Einheit; sowohl als Inhalt, wie als Form. Sie gehen durch sich selbst in einander über, oder indem sie Reflexionen sind, so setzen sie sich selbst als aufgehobene, beziehen sich auf diese ihre Negation und setzen sich gegenseitig voraus. Aber dieß ist zugleich nur Eine Reflexion beider, ihr Voraussetzen daher auch nur eines; die Gegenseitigkeit desselben geht vielmehr darein über, daß sie ihre Eine Identität als ihr Bestehen und ihre Grundlage voraussetzen. Diese, der eine Inhalt und Formeinheit beider, ist das wahrhaft Unbedingte; die Sache an sich selbst.—Die Bedingung ist, wie sich oben ergeben hat, nur das relativ-Unbedingte.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"132.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0008","text":"Man pflegt sie daher selbst als ein Bedingtes zu betrachten, und nach einer neuen Bedingung zu fragen, womit der gewöhnliche Progreß ins Unendliche von Bedingung zu Bedingung eingeleitet ist. Warum wird nun bei einer Bedingung nach einer neuen Bedingung gefragt, das heißt, warum wird sie als Bedingtes angenommen? Weil sie irgend ein endliches Daseyn ist. Aber dieß ist eine weitere Bestimmung der Bedingung, die nicht in ihrem Begriffe liegt. Allein die Bedingung als solche ist darum ein Bedingtes, weil sie das gesetzte Ansichseyn ist; sie ist daher im absolut Unbedingten aufgehoben.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"132.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0009","text":"Dieses nun enthält die beiden Seiten, die Bedingung und den Grund, als seine Momente in sich; es ist die Einheit, in welche sie zurückgegangen sind. Sie beide zusammen machen die Form oder das Gesetztseyn desselben aus. Die unbedingte Sache ist Bedingung beider, aber die absolute, das heißt, die Bedingung, welche selbst Grund ist. —Als Grund ist sie nun die negative Identität, die sich in jene beiden Momente abgestoßen hat;—erstens in die Gestalt der aufgehobenen Grundbeziehung, einer unmittelbaren, einheitslosen, sich selbst äußerlichen Mannigfaltigkeit, welche sich auf den Grund als ein ihr Anderes bezieht, und zugleich das Ansichseyn desselben ausmacht; zweitens, in die Gestalt einer innerlichen, einfachen Form, welche Grund ist, aber sich auf das mit sich identische Unmittelbare als auf ein Anderes bezieht, und dasselbe als Bedingung, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"132.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0010","text":"dieß ihr Ansich als ihr eigenes Moment bestimmt.—Diese beiden Seiten setzen die Totalität so voraus, daß sie das Setzende derselben ist. Umgekehrt, weil sie die Totalität voraussetzen, so scheint diese auch wieder durch jene bedingt zu seyn, und die Sache aus ihrer Bedingung und aus ihrem Grunde zu entspringen. Aber indem diese beiden Seiten sich als das Identische gezeigt haben, so ist das Verhältniß von Bedingung und Grund verschwunden, sie sind zu einem Scheine herabgesetzt; das absolut Unbedingte ist in seiner Bewegung des Setzens und Voraussetzens, nur die Bewegung, in welcher dieser Schein sich aufhebt. Es ist das Thun der Sache, sich zu bedingen, und ihren Bedingungen sich als Grund gegenüber zu stellen; ihre Beziehung als der Bedingungen und des Grundes ist aber ein Scheinen in sich und ihr Verhalten zu ihnen ihr Zusammengehen mit sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"132.10"}],"sha256":"6664f12a763fb814603953394aaaee53b303975c80907d1660fed98b04b41177","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105318641436Z_c7328a71","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The Absolute Unconditioned.","source_sha256":"6664f12a763fb814603953394aaaee53b303975c80907d1660fed98b04b41177","sha256":"9fae1d1d5967fede7b66d9595c4e9029e28b51a4c8c0341238ca99ad91984abe","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:53:18.641466+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0001","text":"The two relatively unconditioned [terms] at first seem, each, to pass into the other: the condition, as immediate, into the formal relation of the ground, and this into immediate existence as its positedness; but each is, apart from this seeming of its other, self-subsistent in itself and has its own peculiar content.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"132.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0002","text":"First, the condition is immediate existence; its form has the two moments, positedness, according to which it is, as condition, material and moment of the ground;—and being-in-itself, according to which it constitutes the essentiality of the ground or its simple reflection into itself. Both sides of the form are external to immediate existence; for it is the sublated relation of ground.—But first, existence is in itself only this: to sublate itself in its immediacy and to go to ground. Being is in general only the becoming of essence; it is its essential nature to make itself into the posited and into the identity which, through the negation of itself, is the immediate. The determinations of form, therefore, of positedness and of being-in-itself identical with itself, the form through which immediate existence is condition, are not external to it, but it is itself this reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"132.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0003","text":"Second, as condition, being is now also posited as what it essentially is; namely, as a moment, hence of an other, and at the same time as the being-in-itself likewise of an other; but it is in itself only through its negation, namely through the ground and through the latter's self-sublating and thereby presupposing reflection; the being-in-itself of being is thus only a posited [being]. This being-in-itself of the condition has the two sides: on the one hand, to be its essentiality as that of the ground, but on the other hand, the immediacy of its existence. Or rather, both are the same. Existence is an immediate; but immediacy is essentially the mediated, namely through the ground that sublates itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"132.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0004","text":"As this immediacy mediated through self-sublating mediation, it is at the same time the being-in-itself of the ground, and its unconditioned; but this being-in-itself is at the same time itself again just as much only moment or positedness, for it is mediated.—The condition is therefore the whole form of the relation of ground; it is the presupposed being-in-itself of this relation, but thereby itself a positedness, and its immediacy is this: to make itself into positedness; thus to repel itself from itself in such a way that it both goes to ground and is ground, which makes itself into positedness and therewith also into the grounded; and both are one and the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"132.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0005","text":"Likewise, in the conditioned ground, being-in-itself is not merely the seeming of an other in it. It is the self-subsistent, that is, the reflection of positing that relates itself to itself; and therewith the identical with itself, or its being-in-itself is in it itself, as is its content. But at the same time it is presupposing reflection; it relates negatively to itself, and sets its being-in-itself over against itself as an other; and the condition, both according to its moment of being-in-itself and according to that of immediate existence, is the ground-relation's own moment; immediate existence is essentially only through its ground, and is its moment as presupposing. Thus this too is itself the whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"132.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0006","text":"Thus, in general, there is only one whole of form present; but likewise only one whole of content. For the peculiar content of the condition is essential content only insofar as it is the identity of reflection with itself in form, or as this immediate existence is in itself the relation of ground. Furthermore, this is condition only through the presupposing reflection of the ground; it is the ground's identity with itself, or its content, which it sets over against itself. Existence is therefore not merely formless material for the relation of ground, but, because it has this form in itself, it is formed matter, and, as at the same time indifferent to it in identity with it over against it, it is content. Finally, it is the same content that the ground has, for it is content precisely as that which is identical with itself in the formal relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"132.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0007","text":"The two sides of the whole, condition and ground, are therefore one essential unity, both as content and as form. They pass into one another of themselves, or, being reflections, they posit themselves as sublated, relate themselves to this their negation, and mutually presuppose one another. But this is at the same time only one reflection of both, and their presupposing therefore also only one; the reciprocity of the same rather passes over into their presupposing their one identity as their subsistence and their foundation. This, the one unity of content and form of both, is the truly unconditioned; the thing in itself.—The condition is, as has emerged above, only the relatively unconditioned.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"132.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0008","text":"It is therefore customary to regard it itself as a conditioned [thing], and to ask after a new condition, whereby the ordinary progress to infinity from condition to condition is introduced. Why, then, is a new condition asked for in the case of a condition, that is, why is it assumed as conditioned? Because it is some finite existence. But this is a further determination of the condition which does not lie in its concept. Yet the condition as such is a conditioned [thing] because it is posited being-in-itself; it is therefore sublated in the absolutely unconditioned.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"132.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0009","text":"This now contains the two sides, condition and ground, within itself as its moments; it is the unity into which they have retreated. Together they constitute its form or its positedness. The unconditioned thing is the condition of both, but the absolute [condition], that is, the condition which is itself ground. —As ground, it is now the negative identity which has repelled itself into those two moments;—first, into the shape of the sublated relation of ground, of an immediate, unityless, self-external multiplicity, which relates itself to the ground as to an other than itself, and at the same time constitutes its being-in-itself; second, into the shape of an inward, simple form, which is ground, but relates itself to the immediate identical with itself as to an other, and determines the same as condition, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"132.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0010","text":"this its in-itself as its own moment.—These two sides presuppose totality in such a way that it is what posits them. Conversely, because they presuppose totality, this too seems in turn to be conditioned by them, and the thing to arise from its condition and from its ground. But since these two sides have shown themselves to be the identical, the relation of condition and ground has vanished; they are reduced to a seeming; the absolutely unconditioned, in its movement of positing and presupposing, is only the movement in which this seeming sublates itself. It is the doing of the thing to condition itself, and to set itself over against its conditions as ground; but its relation as that of the conditions and the ground is a seeming within itself, and its comportment toward them its coming-together with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"132.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAU:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"fb68547e57f492c0f84b798e2fbf5d6f528b9dbe4c691853f4895fcdcdfcc2a9","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Das absolute Unbedingte."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Das absolute Unbedingte.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS","title":"c. The Emergence of the Thing into Existence.","order":133,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CHDS","text":"Das absolut Unbedingte ist der absolute mit seiner Bedingung identische Grund; die unmittelbare Sache, als die wahrhaft Wesenhafte. Als Grund bezieht sie sich negativ auf sich selbst, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn, aber zum Gesetztseyn, das die in ihren Seiten vollständige Reflexion, und die in ihnen mit sich identische Formbeziehung ist, wie sich ihr Begriff ergeben hat. Dieß Gesetztseyn ist daher erstlich der aufgehobene Grund, die Sache als das Reflexionslose Unmittelbare; die Seite der Bedingungen. Diese ist die Totalität der Bestimmungen der Sache,—die Sache selbst, aber in die Äußerlichkeit des Seyns hinausgeworfen; der wiederhergestellte Kreis des Seyns. In der Bedingung entläßt das Wesen die Einheit seiner Reflexion-in-sich als eine Unmittelbarkeit, die aber nunmehr die Bestimmung hat, bedingende Voraussetzung zu seyn, und wesentlich nur eine seiner Seiten auszumachen.—Die Bedingungen sind darum der ganze Inhalt der Sache, weil sie das Unbedingte in der Form des formlosen Seyns sind. Sie haben aber um dieser Form willen auch noch eine andere Gestalt, als die Bestimmungen des Inhalts, wie er in der Sache als solcher ist. Sie erscheinen als eine einheitslose Mannigfaltigkeit, vermischt mit Außerwesentlichem und andern Umständen, die zu dem Kreise des Daseyns, insofern es die Bedingungen dieser bestimmten Sache ausmacht, nicht gehören.—Für die absolute uneingeschränkte Sache ist die Sphäre des Seyns selbst die Bedingung. Der Grund, der in sich zurückgeht, setzt sie als die erste Unmittelbarkeit, worauf er sich als auf sein Unbedingtes bezieht. Diese Unmittelbarkeit als die aufgehobene Reflexion, ist die Reflexion in dem Elemente des Seyns, das also sich als solches zu einem Ganzen ausbildet; die Form wuchert als Bestimmtheit des Seyns fort, und erscheint so als ein mannigfaltiger von der Reflexions-Bestimmung verschiedener, und gegen sie gleichgültiger Inhalt.\n\nDas Unwesentliche, welches die Sphäre des Seyns an ihr hat, und was sie, insofern sie Bedingung ist, abstreift, ist die Bestimmtheit der Unmittelbarkeit, in welche die Formeinheit versenkt ist. Diese Formeinheit, als die Beziehung des Seyns, ist an ihm zunächst als das Werden,—das Übergehen einer Bestimmtheit des Seyns in eine andere. Aber das Werden des Seyns ist ferner Werden zum Wesen und das Zurückgehen in den Grund. Das Daseyn also, welches die Bedingungen ausmacht, wird in Wahrheit nicht von einem Andern als Bedingung bestimmt und als Material gebraucht; sondern es macht sich durch sich selbst zum Moment eines Andern.—Sein Werden ist ferner nicht ein Anfangen von sich als dem wahrhaft Ersten und Unmittelbaren; sondern seine Unmittelbarkeit ist nur das Vorausgesetzte; und die Bewegung seines Werdens ist das Thun der Reflexion selbst. Die Wahrheit des Daseyns ist daher Bedingung zu seyn; seine Unmittelbarkeit ist allein durch die Reflexion der Grundbeziehung, welche sich selbst als aufgehobene setzt. Das Werden ist somit, wie die Unmittelbarkeit nur der Schein des Unbedingten, indem dieses sich selbst voraussetzt, und darin seine Form hat; und die Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns ist daher wesentlich nur Moment der Form.\n\nDie andere Seite dieses Scheinens des Unbedingten ist die Grundbeziehung als solche, als Form bestimmt gegen die Unmittelbarkeit der Bedingungen und des Inhalts. Aber sie ist die Form der absoluten Sache, welche die Einheit ihrer Form mit sich selbst oder ihren Inhalt an ihr selbst hat, und indem sie ihn zur Bedingung bestimmt, in diesem Setzen selbst seine Verschiedenheit aufhebt und ihn zum Momente macht; so wie sie umgekehrt sich als wesenloser Form in dieser Identität mit sich die Unmittelbarkeit des Bestehens gibt. Die Reflexion des Grundes hebt die Unmittelbarkeit der Bedingungen auf, und bezieht sie zu Momenten in der Einheit der Sache; aber die Bedingungen sind das von der unbedingten Sache selbst Vorausgesetzte, sie hebt damit also ihr eigenes Setzen auf; oder ihr Setzen macht sich somit unmittelbar selbst ebenso sehr zum Werden. —Beides ist daher Eine Einheit; die Bewegung der Bedingungen an ihnen selbst ist Werden, Zurückgehen in den Grund und Setzen des Grundes; aber der Grund als gesetzter, das heißt als aufgehobener, ist das Unmittelbare. Der Grund bezieht sich negativ auf sich selbst, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn und begründet die Bedingungen; aber darin, daß so das unmittelbare Daseyn als ein Gesetztes bestimmt ist, liebt der Grund es auf und macht sich erst zum Grunde.—Diese Reflexion also ist die Vermittelung der unbedingten Sache durch ihre Negation mit sich. Oder vielmehr die Reflexion des Unbedingten ist zuerst Voraussetzen, aber dieß Aufheben ihrer selbst ist unmittelbar bestimmendes Setzen; zweitens ist sie darin unmittelbar Aufheben des Vorausgesetzten und Bestimmen aus sich; somit ist dieß Bestimmen wieder Aufheben des Setzens und ist das Werden an sich selbst. Darin ist die Vermittelung als Rückehr zu sich durch die Negation, verschwunden; sie ist einfache in sich scheinende Reflexion, und grundloses absolutes Werden. Die Bewegung der Sache, durch ihre Bedingungen einer Seits und anderer Seits durch ihren Grund gesetzt zu werden, ist nur das Verschwinden des Scheins der Vermittelung. Das Gesetztwerden der Sache ist hiermit ein Hervortreten, das einfache sich Herausstellen in die Existenz; reine Bewegung der Sache zu sich selbst.\n\nWenn alle Bedingungen einer Sache vorhanden sind, so tritt sie in die Existenz. Die Sache ist, eh sie existirt; und zwar ist sie erstens als Wesen, oder als Unbedingtes; zweitens hat sie Daseyn, oder ist bestimmt, und dieß auf die betrachtete gedoppelte Weise, einer Seits in ihren Bedingungen, anderer Seits in ihrem Grunde. In jenen hat sie sich die Form des äußerlichen, grundlosen Seyns gegeben, weil sie als absolute Reflexion die negative Beziehung auf sich ist und sich zu ihrer Voraussetzung macht. Dieß voraus gesetzte Unbedingte ist daher das grundlose Unmittelbare, dessen Seyn nichts ist, denn als Grundloses da zu seyn. Wenn also alle Bedingungen der Sache vorhanden sind, das heißt, wenn die Totalität der Sache als grundloses Unmittelbares gesetzt ist, so erinnert sich diese zerstreute Mannigfaltigkeit an ihr selbst.—Die ganze Sache muß in ihren Bedingungen da seyn, oder es gehören alle Bedingungen zu ihrer Existenz; denn Alle machen die Reflexion aus; oder das Daseyn, weil es Bedingung ist, ist durch die Form bestimmt, seine Bestimmungen sind daher Reflexions-Bestimmungen und mit einer wesentlich die andern gesetzt.—Die Erinnerung der Bedingungen ist zunächst das zu Grunde gehen des unmittelbaren Daseyns, und das Werden des Grundes. Aber damit ist der Grund ein gesetzter, d. h. er ist, so sehr er als Grund ist, so sehr als Grund aufgehoben, und unmittelbares Seyn. Wenn also alle Bedingungen der Sache vorhanden sind, so heben sie sich als unmittelbares Daseyn und Voraussetzung und ebenso sehr hebt sich der Grund auf. Der Grund zeigt sich nur, als ein Schein, der unmittelbar verschwindet; dieß Hervortreten ist somit die tautologische Bewegung der Sache zu sich, und ihre Vermittelung durch die Bedingungen und durch den Grund ist das Verschwinden beider. Das Hervortreten in die Existenz ist daher so unmittelbar, daß es nur durch das Verschwinden der Vermittelung vermittelt ist.\n\nDie Sache geht aus dem Grunde hervor. Sie wird nicht durch ihn so begründet oder gesetzt, daß er noch unten bliebe, sondern das Setzen ist die Herausbewegung des Grundes zu sich selbst, und das einfache Verschwinden desselben. Er erhält durch die Vereinigung mit den Bedingungen die äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit und das Moment des Seyns. Aber er erhält sie nicht als ein Äußerliches noch durch eine äußerliche Beziehung; sondern als Grund macht er sich zum Gesetztseyn, seine einfache Wesentlichkeit geht im Gesetztseyn mit sich zusammen, und ist in diesem Aufheben seiner selbst das Verschwinden seines Unterschiedes von seinem Gesetztseyn, somit einfache wesentliche Unmittelbarkeit. Er bleibt also nicht als ein Verschiedenes vom Begründeten zurück, sondern die Wahrheit des Begründens ist, daß der Grund darin mit sich selbst sich vereint und somit seine Reflexion in Anderes, seine Reflexion in sich selbst ist. Die Sache ist hiermit ebenso, wie sie das Unbedingte ist, auch das Grundlose, und tritt aus dem Grunde nur insofern er zu Grunde gegangen und keiner ist, aus dem Grundlosen, d. h. aus der eigenen wesentlichen Negativität oder reinen Form hervor.\n\nDiese durch Grund und Bedingung vermittelte, und durch das Aufheben der Vermittelung mit sich identische Unmittelbarkeit ist die Existenz.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0001","text":"Das absolut Unbedingte ist der absolute mit seiner Bedingung identische Grund; die unmittelbare Sache, als die wahrhaft Wesenhafte. Als Grund bezieht sie sich negativ auf sich selbst, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn, aber zum Gesetztseyn, das die in ihren Seiten vollständige Reflexion, und die in ihnen mit sich identische Formbeziehung ist, wie sich ihr Begriff ergeben hat. Dieß Gesetztseyn ist daher erstlich der aufgehobene Grund, die Sache als das Reflexionslose Unmittelbare; die Seite der Bedingungen. Diese ist die Totalität der Bestimmungen der Sache,—die Sache selbst, aber in die Äußerlichkeit des Seyns hinausgeworfen; der wiederhergestellte Kreis des Seyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"133.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0002","text":"In der Bedingung entläßt das Wesen die Einheit seiner Reflexion-in-sich als eine Unmittelbarkeit, die aber nunmehr die Bestimmung hat, bedingende Voraussetzung zu seyn, und wesentlich nur eine seiner Seiten auszumachen.—Die Bedingungen sind darum der ganze Inhalt der Sache, weil sie das Unbedingte in der Form des formlosen Seyns sind. Sie haben aber um dieser Form willen auch noch eine andere Gestalt, als die Bestimmungen des Inhalts, wie er in der Sache als solcher ist. Sie erscheinen als eine einheitslose Mannigfaltigkeit, vermischt mit Außerwesentlichem und andern Umständen, die zu dem Kreise des Daseyns, insofern es die Bedingungen dieser bestimmten Sache ausmacht, nicht gehören.—Für die absolute uneingeschränkte Sache ist die Sphäre des Seyns selbst die Bedingung.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"133.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0003","text":"Der Grund, der in sich zurückgeht, setzt sie als die erste Unmittelbarkeit, worauf er sich als auf sein Unbedingtes bezieht. Diese Unmittelbarkeit als die aufgehobene Reflexion, ist die Reflexion in dem Elemente des Seyns, das also sich als solches zu einem Ganzen ausbildet; die Form wuchert als Bestimmtheit des Seyns fort, und erscheint so als ein mannigfaltiger von der Reflexions-Bestimmung verschiedener, und gegen sie gleichgültiger Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"133.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0004","text":"Das Unwesentliche, welches die Sphäre des Seyns an ihr hat, und was sie, insofern sie Bedingung ist, abstreift, ist die Bestimmtheit der Unmittelbarkeit, in welche die Formeinheit versenkt ist. Diese Formeinheit, als die Beziehung des Seyns, ist an ihm zunächst als das Werden,—das Übergehen einer Bestimmtheit des Seyns in eine andere. Aber das Werden des Seyns ist ferner Werden zum Wesen und das Zurückgehen in den Grund. Das Daseyn also, welches die Bedingungen ausmacht, wird in Wahrheit nicht von einem Andern als Bedingung bestimmt und als Material gebraucht; sondern es macht sich durch sich selbst zum Moment eines Andern.—Sein Werden ist ferner nicht ein Anfangen von sich als dem wahrhaft Ersten und Unmittelbaren; sondern seine Unmittelbarkeit ist nur das Vorausgesetzte; und die Bewegung seines Werdens ist das Thun der Reflexion selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"133.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0005","text":"Die Wahrheit des Daseyns ist daher Bedingung zu seyn; seine Unmittelbarkeit ist allein durch die Reflexion der Grundbeziehung, welche sich selbst als aufgehobene setzt. Das Werden ist somit, wie die Unmittelbarkeit nur der Schein des Unbedingten, indem dieses sich selbst voraussetzt, und darin seine Form hat; und die Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns ist daher wesentlich nur Moment der Form.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"133.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0006","text":"Die andere Seite dieses Scheinens des Unbedingten ist die Grundbeziehung als solche, als Form bestimmt gegen die Unmittelbarkeit der Bedingungen und des Inhalts. Aber sie ist die Form der absoluten Sache, welche die Einheit ihrer Form mit sich selbst oder ihren Inhalt an ihr selbst hat, und indem sie ihn zur Bedingung bestimmt, in diesem Setzen selbst seine Verschiedenheit aufhebt und ihn zum Momente macht; so wie sie umgekehrt sich als wesenloser Form in dieser Identität mit sich die Unmittelbarkeit des Bestehens gibt. Die Reflexion des Grundes hebt die Unmittelbarkeit der Bedingungen auf, und bezieht sie zu Momenten in der Einheit der Sache; aber die Bedingungen sind das von der unbedingten Sache selbst Vorausgesetzte, sie hebt damit also ihr eigenes Setzen auf; oder ihr Setzen macht sich somit unmittelbar selbst ebenso sehr zum Werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"133.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0007","text":"—Beides ist daher Eine Einheit; die Bewegung der Bedingungen an ihnen selbst ist Werden, Zurückgehen in den Grund und Setzen des Grundes; aber der Grund als gesetzter, das heißt als aufgehobener, ist das Unmittelbare. Der Grund bezieht sich negativ auf sich selbst, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn und begründet die Bedingungen; aber darin, daß so das unmittelbare Daseyn als ein Gesetztes bestimmt ist, liebt der Grund es auf und macht sich erst zum Grunde.—Diese Reflexion also ist die Vermittelung der unbedingten Sache durch ihre Negation mit sich. Oder vielmehr die Reflexion des Unbedingten ist zuerst Voraussetzen, aber dieß Aufheben ihrer selbst ist unmittelbar bestimmendes Setzen; zweitens ist sie darin unmittelbar Aufheben des Vorausgesetzten und Bestimmen aus sich; somit ist dieß Bestimmen wieder Aufheben des Setzens und ist das Werden an sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"133.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0008","text":"Darin ist die Vermittelung als Rückehr zu sich durch die Negation, verschwunden; sie ist einfache in sich scheinende Reflexion, und grundloses absolutes Werden. Die Bewegung der Sache, durch ihre Bedingungen einer Seits und anderer Seits durch ihren Grund gesetzt zu werden, ist nur das Verschwinden des Scheins der Vermittelung. Das Gesetztwerden der Sache ist hiermit ein Hervortreten, das einfache sich Herausstellen in die Existenz; reine Bewegung der Sache zu sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"133.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0009","text":"Wenn alle Bedingungen einer Sache vorhanden sind, so tritt sie in die Existenz. Die Sache ist, eh sie existirt; und zwar ist sie erstens als Wesen, oder als Unbedingtes; zweitens hat sie Daseyn, oder ist bestimmt, und dieß auf die betrachtete gedoppelte Weise, einer Seits in ihren Bedingungen, anderer Seits in ihrem Grunde. In jenen hat sie sich die Form des äußerlichen, grundlosen Seyns gegeben, weil sie als absolute Reflexion die negative Beziehung auf sich ist und sich zu ihrer Voraussetzung macht. Dieß voraus gesetzte Unbedingte ist daher das grundlose Unmittelbare, dessen Seyn nichts ist, denn als Grundloses da zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"133.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0010","text":"Wenn also alle Bedingungen der Sache vorhanden sind, das heißt, wenn die Totalität der Sache als grundloses Unmittelbares gesetzt ist, so erinnert sich diese zerstreute Mannigfaltigkeit an ihr selbst.—Die ganze Sache muß in ihren Bedingungen da seyn, oder es gehören alle Bedingungen zu ihrer Existenz; denn Alle machen die Reflexion aus; oder das Daseyn, weil es Bedingung ist, ist durch die Form bestimmt, seine Bestimmungen sind daher Reflexions-Bestimmungen und mit einer wesentlich die andern gesetzt.—Die Erinnerung der Bedingungen ist zunächst das zu Grunde gehen des unmittelbaren Daseyns, und das Werden des Grundes. Aber damit ist der Grund ein gesetzter, d. h. er ist, so sehr er als Grund ist, so sehr als Grund aufgehoben, und unmittelbares Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"133.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0011","text":"Wenn also alle Bedingungen der Sache vorhanden sind, so heben sie sich als unmittelbares Daseyn und Voraussetzung und ebenso sehr hebt sich der Grund auf. Der Grund zeigt sich nur, als ein Schein, der unmittelbar verschwindet; dieß Hervortreten ist somit die tautologische Bewegung der Sache zu sich, und ihre Vermittelung durch die Bedingungen und durch den Grund ist das Verschwinden beider. Das Hervortreten in die Existenz ist daher so unmittelbar, daß es nur durch das Verschwinden der Vermittelung vermittelt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"133.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0012","text":"Die Sache geht aus dem Grunde hervor. Sie wird nicht durch ihn so begründet oder gesetzt, daß er noch unten bliebe, sondern das Setzen ist die Herausbewegung des Grundes zu sich selbst, und das einfache Verschwinden desselben. Er erhält durch die Vereinigung mit den Bedingungen die äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit und das Moment des Seyns. Aber er erhält sie nicht als ein Äußerliches noch durch eine äußerliche Beziehung; sondern als Grund macht er sich zum Gesetztseyn, seine einfache Wesentlichkeit geht im Gesetztseyn mit sich zusammen, und ist in diesem Aufheben seiner selbst das Verschwinden seines Unterschiedes von seinem Gesetztseyn, somit einfache wesentliche Unmittelbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"133.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0013","text":"Er bleibt also nicht als ein Verschiedenes vom Begründeten zurück, sondern die Wahrheit des Begründens ist, daß der Grund darin mit sich selbst sich vereint und somit seine Reflexion in Anderes, seine Reflexion in sich selbst ist. Die Sache ist hiermit ebenso, wie sie das Unbedingte ist, auch das Grundlose, und tritt aus dem Grunde nur insofern er zu Grunde gegangen und keiner ist, aus dem Grundlosen, d. h. aus der eigenen wesentlichen Negativität oder reinen Form hervor.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"133.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0014","text":"Diese durch Grund und Bedingung vermittelte, und durch das Aufheben der Vermittelung mit sich identische Unmittelbarkeit ist die Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"133.14"}],"sha256":"756962c69831b53dfea6af1b66ce38e4b0ba753aaa46c5c6e81da3d0a99b7b1c","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105334175366Z_129646e2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Emergence of the Thing into Existence.","source_sha256":"756962c69831b53dfea6af1b66ce38e4b0ba753aaa46c5c6e81da3d0a99b7b1c","sha256":"e51c8991efdb04ef82c980baf77bd4a56fc2b6607ec9d22df3d5edbcddae9217","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:53:34.175402+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0001","text":"The absolutely unconditioned is the absolute ground identical with its condition; the immediate thing, as that which is truly essential. As ground, it relates negatively to itself, makes itself into positedness, but into positedness that is the reflection complete in its sides, and the relation of form identical with itself in them, as its concept has turned out to be. This positedness is therefore, first, the sublated ground, the thing as the reflectionless immediate; the side of the conditions. This is the totality of the determinations of the thing—the thing itself, but thrown out into the externality of being; the restored circle of being.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"133.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0002","text":"In the condition, essence releases the unity of its reflection-into-itself as an immediacy, which, however, now has the determination of being a conditioning presupposition, and essentially constitutes only one of its sides.—The conditions are therefore the whole content of the thing, because they are the unconditioned in the form of formless being. But by virtue of this form they also have another shape than the determinations of the content as it is in the thing as such. They appear as a diversity devoid of unity, mingled with what is inessential and with other circumstances that do not belong to the circle of existence, insofar as it constitutes the conditions of this determinate thing.—For the absolute unrestricted thing, the sphere of being itself is the condition.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"133.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0003","text":"The ground that returns into itself posits them as the first immediacy, to which it relates as to its unconditioned. This immediacy, as sublated reflection, is reflection in the element of being, which thus develops itself as such into a whole; form proliferates as determinacy of being, and thus appears as a manifold content distinct from the determination of reflection, and indifferent toward it.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"133.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0004","text":"The inessential which the sphere of being has in itself, and which it casts off insofar as it is condition, is the determinacy of the immediacy into which the unity of form is sunk. This unity of form, as the relation of being, is at first in it as becoming—the transition of one determinacy of being into another. But the becoming of being is further becoming into essence and return into ground. Existence, therefore, which constitutes the conditions, is not in truth determined by another as condition and used as material; rather, it makes itself through itself into a moment of another.—Its becoming is further not a beginning from itself as the truly first and immediate; rather, its immediacy is only what is presupposed, and the movement of its becoming is the doing of reflection itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"133.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0005","text":"The truth of existence is therefore to be condition; its immediacy is solely through the reflection of the relation of ground, which posits itself as sublated. Becoming is consequently, like immediacy, only the semblance of the unconditioned, in that this presupposes itself and has its form therein; and the immediacy of being is therefore essentially only a moment of form.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"133.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0006","text":"The other side of this shining-forth of the unconditioned is the relation of ground as such, determined as form over against the immediacy of the conditions and of the content. But it is the form of the absolute thing, which has the unity of its form with itself, or its content, in itself, and, in determining it as condition, sublates its difference in this positing itself and makes it into a moment; just as, conversely, as inessential form, in this identity with itself, it gives itself the immediacy of subsistence. The reflection of ground sublates the immediacy of the conditions and relates them as moments in the unity of the thing; but the conditions are what is presupposed by the unconditioned thing itself, and it thereby sublates its own positing; or its positing thus immediately makes itself into becoming just as much.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"133.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0007","text":"—Both are therefore one unity; the movement of the conditions in themselves is becoming, return into ground, and positing of ground; but ground as posited, that is, as sublated, is the immediate. Ground relates negatively to itself, makes itself into positedness, and grounds the conditions; but in that immediate existence is thus determined as a posited, ground sublates it and thereby first makes itself into ground.—This reflection, therefore, is the mediation of the unconditioned thing with itself through its negation. Or rather, the reflection of the unconditioned is at first presupposing, but this self-sublation of itself is immediately determining positing; secondly, therein it is immediately sublation of the presupposed and determining out of itself; thus this determining is again sublation of positing and is becoming in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"133.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0008","text":"Therein mediation, as return to itself through negation, has disappeared; it is simple reflection shining within itself, and groundless absolute becoming. The movement of the thing, to be posited through its conditions on the one hand and through its ground on the other, is only the vanishing of the semblance of mediation. The being-posited of the thing is thereby a coming-forth, the simple setting-forth of itself into existence; the pure movement of the thing toward itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"133.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0009","text":"When all the conditions of a thing are present, it enters into existence. The thing is before it exists; namely, it is, first, as essence, or as the unconditioned; second, it has existence, or is determinate, and this in the double manner considered: on the one hand in its conditions, on the other in its ground. In the former it has given itself the form of external, groundless being, because as absolute reflection it is the negative relation to itself and makes itself into its presupposition. This presupposed unconditioned is therefore the groundless immediate, whose being is nothing other than being there as groundless.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"133.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0010","text":"Thus, when all the conditions of the thing are present, that is, when the totality of the thing is posited as groundless immediate, this scattered diversity recollects itself.—The whole thing must be there in its conditions, or all the conditions belong to its existence; for all constitute reflection; or existence, because it is condition, is determined through form, and its determinations are therefore determinations of reflection and are posited with one another essentially as the others.—The recollection of the conditions is at first the perishing of immediate existence, and the becoming of ground. But thereby ground is a posited ground, i.e. it is, as much as it is ground, just as much sublated as ground, and immediate being.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"133.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0011","text":"Thus, when all the conditions of the thing are present, they sublate themselves as immediate existence and presupposition, and ground likewise sublates itself. Ground shows itself only as a semblance that immediately vanishes; this coming-forth is therefore the tautological movement of the thing toward itself, and its mediation through the conditions and through ground is the vanishing of both. The coming-forth into existence is therefore so immediate that it is mediated only through the vanishing of mediation.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"133.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0012","text":"The thing proceeds from ground. It is not grounded or posited by it in such a way that it remains below; rather, positing is the movement-out of ground toward itself, and its simple vanishing. Through union with the conditions, it receives external immediacy and the moment of being. But it does not receive these as something external, nor through an external relation; rather, as ground it makes itself into positedness, its simple essentiality coincides with itself in positedness, and in this self-sublation it is the vanishing of its difference from its positedness, hence simple essential immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"133.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0013","text":"Thus it does not remain behind as something different from what is grounded; rather, the truth of grounding is that ground therein unites with itself, and thus its reflection into another is its reflection into itself. The thing is hereby, just as it is the unconditioned, also the groundless, and proceeds from ground only insofar as ground has perished and is no ground, from the groundless, i.e. from its own essential negativity or pure form.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"133.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0014","text":"This immediacy, mediated through ground and condition and identical with itself through the sublation of mediation, is existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"133.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CHDS:P0014"]}],"source_digest":"75c6b480e6bc3a304e288c20b3f92290ebe9b566318b32e7ca8d3155a6d182c7","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Hervorgang der Sache in die Existenz."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Hervorgang der Sache in die Existenz.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZADE","title":"Second Section. Appearance.","order":134,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ZADE","text":"Das Wesen muß erscheinen.\n\nDas Seyn ist die absolute Abstraktion; diese Negativität ist ihm nicht ein Äußerliches, sondern es ist Seyn und sonst nichts als Seyn, nur als diese absolute Negativität. Um derselben willen ist Seyn nur als sich aufhebendes Seyn, und ist Wesen. Das Wesen aber ist als die einfache Gleichheit mit sich umgekehrt ebenfalls Seyn. Die Lehre vom Seyn enthält den ersten Satz: Das Seyn ist Wesen. Der zweite Satz: Das Wesen ist Seyn, macht den Inhalt des ersten Abschnittes der Lehre vom Wesen aus. Dieses Seyn aber, zu dem das Wesen sich macht, ist das wesentliche Seyn, die Existenz; ein Herausgegangenseyn aus der Negativität und Innerlichkeit.\n\nSo erscheint das Wesen. Die Reflexion ist das Scheinen des Wesens in ihm selbst. Die Bestimmungen derselben sind in die Einheit eingeschlossen schlechthin nur als gesetzte, aufgehobene; oder sie ist das in seinem Gesetztseyn unmittelbar mit sich identische Wesen. Indem dieses aber Grund ist, bestimmt es sich real, durch seine sich selbst aufhebende oder in sich zurückkehrende Reflexion; indem weiter diese Bestimmung oder das Andersseyn der Grundbeziehung sich in der Reflexion des Grundes aufhebt und Existenz wird, so haben die Formbestimmungen hieran ein Element des selbstständigen Bestehens. Ihr Schein vervollständigt sich zur Erscheinung.\n\nDie zur Unmittelbarkeit fortgegangene Wesenheit ist zunächst Existenz, und Existirendes oder Ding; als ununterschiedne Einheit des Wesens mit seiner Unmittelbarkeit. Das Ding enthält zwar die Reflexion, aber ihre Negativität ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit zunächst erloschen; allein weil sein Grund wesentlich die Reflexion ist, hebt sich seine Unmittelbarkeit auf; es macht sich zu einem Gesetztseyn.\n\nSo ist es zweitens Erscheinung. Die Erscheinung ist das, was das Ding an sich ist, oder seine Wahrheit. Diese nur gesetzte, in das Andersseyn reflektirte Existenz ist aber ebenso das Hinausgehen über sich in ihre Unendlichkeit; der Welt der Erscheinung stellt sich die in sich reflektirte, an sich seyende Welt gegenüber. Aber das erscheinende und das wesentliche Seyn stehen schlechthin in Beziehung auf einander. So ist die Existenz drittens wesendiches Verhältniß; das Erscheinende zeigt das Wesentliche, und dieses ist in seiner Erscheinung.—Das Verhältniß ist die noch unvollkommene Vereinigung der Reflexion in das Andersseyn und der Reflexion in sich; die vollkommene Durchdringung beider ist die Wirklichkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZADE:P0001","text":"Das Wesen muß erscheinen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"134.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZADE:P0002","text":"Das Seyn ist die absolute Abstraktion; diese Negativität ist ihm nicht ein Äußerliches, sondern es ist Seyn und sonst nichts als Seyn, nur als diese absolute Negativität. Um derselben willen ist Seyn nur als sich aufhebendes Seyn, und ist Wesen. Das Wesen aber ist als die einfache Gleichheit mit sich umgekehrt ebenfalls Seyn. Die Lehre vom Seyn enthält den ersten Satz: Das Seyn ist Wesen. Der zweite Satz: Das Wesen ist Seyn, macht den Inhalt des ersten Abschnittes der Lehre vom Wesen aus. Dieses Seyn aber, zu dem das Wesen sich macht, ist das wesentliche Seyn, die Existenz; ein Herausgegangenseyn aus der Negativität und Innerlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"134.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZADE:P0003","text":"So erscheint das Wesen. Die Reflexion ist das Scheinen des Wesens in ihm selbst. Die Bestimmungen derselben sind in die Einheit eingeschlossen schlechthin nur als gesetzte, aufgehobene; oder sie ist das in seinem Gesetztseyn unmittelbar mit sich identische Wesen. Indem dieses aber Grund ist, bestimmt es sich real, durch seine sich selbst aufhebende oder in sich zurückkehrende Reflexion; indem weiter diese Bestimmung oder das Andersseyn der Grundbeziehung sich in der Reflexion des Grundes aufhebt und Existenz wird, so haben die Formbestimmungen hieran ein Element des selbstständigen Bestehens. Ihr Schein vervollständigt sich zur Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"134.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZADE:P0004","text":"Die zur Unmittelbarkeit fortgegangene Wesenheit ist zunächst Existenz, und Existirendes oder Ding; als ununterschiedne Einheit des Wesens mit seiner Unmittelbarkeit. Das Ding enthält zwar die Reflexion, aber ihre Negativität ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit zunächst erloschen; allein weil sein Grund wesentlich die Reflexion ist, hebt sich seine Unmittelbarkeit auf; es macht sich zu einem Gesetztseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"134.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZADE:P0005","text":"So ist es zweitens Erscheinung. Die Erscheinung ist das, was das Ding an sich ist, oder seine Wahrheit. Diese nur gesetzte, in das Andersseyn reflektirte Existenz ist aber ebenso das Hinausgehen über sich in ihre Unendlichkeit; der Welt der Erscheinung stellt sich die in sich reflektirte, an sich seyende Welt gegenüber. Aber das erscheinende und das wesentliche Seyn stehen schlechthin in Beziehung auf einander. So ist die Existenz drittens wesendiches Verhältniß; das Erscheinende zeigt das Wesentliche, und dieses ist in seiner Erscheinung.—Das Verhältniß ist die noch unvollkommene Vereinigung der Reflexion in das Andersseyn und der Reflexion in sich; die vollkommene Durchdringung beider ist die Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"134.5"}],"sha256":"532e9f5133d4f7c38b2c78352aff551e201bebcb6b0e84d5524518d6965955ad","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Zweiter Abschnitt. Die Erscheinung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS","title":"A. The Thing and Its Properties.","order":135,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DDUS","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Die Existenz.\n\nWie der Satz des Grundes ausdrückt: Alles was ist, hat einen Grund, oder ist ein Gesetztes, ein Vermitteltes; so müßte auch ein Satz der Existenz aufgestellt und so ausgedrückt werden: Alles, was ist, existirt. Die Wahrheit des Seyns ist, nicht ein erstes Unmittelbares, sondern das in die Unmittelbarkeit hervorgegangene Wesen zu seyn.\n\nWenn aber ferner auch gesagt wurde, was existirt, hat einen Grund und ist bedingt, so müßte auch ebenso gesagt werden: es hat keinen Grund und ist unbedingt. Denn die Existenz ist die aus dem Aufheben der durch Grund und Bedingung beziehenden Vermittelung hervorgegangene Unmittelbarkeit, die im Hervorgehen eben dieß Hervorgehen selbst aufhebt.\n\nInsofern die Beweise von der Existenz Gottes hier erwähnt werden können, ist zum voraus zu erinnern, daß es außer dem unmittelbaren Seyn erstens, und zweitens der Existenz, dem Seyn, das aus dem Wesen hervorgeht, noch ein ferneres Seyn gibt, welches aus dem Begriffe hervorgeht, die Objektivität.—Das Beweisen ist überhaupt die vermittelte Erkenntniß. Die verschiedenen Arten des Seyns fordern oder enthalten ihre eigene Art der Vermittelung; so wird auch die Natur des Beweisens in Ansehung einer jeden verschieden. Der ontologische Beweis will vom Begriffe ausgehen; er legt den Inbegriff aller Realitäten zu Grunde, und subsumirt alsdann auch die Existenz unter die Realität. Er ist also die Vermittelung, welche Schluß ist, und die hier noch nicht zu betrachten ist. Es ist bereits oben (I. Th. I. Abth. S. 27.ff.) auf das, was Kant hiergegen erinnert, Rüksicht genommen und bemerkt worden, daß Kant unter Existenz das bestimmte Daseyn versteht, wodurch etwas in den Kontext der gesammten Erfahrung, d. h. in die Bestimmung eines Andersseyns und in die Beziehung auf Anderes tritt. So ist als Existirendes Etwas vermittelt durch Anderes, und die Existenz überhaupt die Seite seiner Vermittelung. Nun liegt in dem, was Kant den Begriff nennt, nämlich in Etwas, insofern es als nur einfach auf sich bezogen genommen wird, oder in der Vorstellung als solcher, nicht seine Vermittelung; in der abstrakten Identität mit sich ist die Entgegensetzung weggelassen. Der ontologische Beweis hätte nun darzustellen, daß der absolute Begriff, nämlich der Begriff Gottes, zum bestimmten Daseyn, zur Vermittelung komme, oder wie das einfache Wesen sich mit der Vermittelung vermittle. Dieß geschieht durch die angegebene Subsumtion der Existenz unter ihr Allgemeines, nämlich die Realität, welche als das Mittlere zwischen Gott in seinem Begriffe einer Seits, und zwischen der Existenz anderer Seits angenommen wird.—Von dieser Vermittelung, insofern sie die Form des Schlusses hat, ist, wie gesagt, hier nicht die Rede. Wie aber jene Vermittelung des Wesens mit der Existenz in Wahrheit beschaffen ist, dieß hat die bisherige Darstellung enthalten. Die Natur des Beweisens selbst ist in der Lehre von der Erkenntniß zu betrachten. Hier ist nur anzugeben, was sich auf die Natur der Vermittelung überhaupt bezieht.\n\nDie Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes geben einen Grund für dieses Daseyn an.\n\nEr soll nicht ein objektiver Grund des Daseyns Gottes seyn; denn dieses ist an und für sich selbst. So ist er bloß ein Grund für die Erkenntniß. Damit giebt er sich zugleich für ein solches aus, das in dem Gegenstande, der zunächst als begründet dadurch erscheint, verschwindet. Der Grund nun, der von der Zufälligkeit der Welt hergenommen ist, enthält den Rükgang derselben in das absolute Wesen; denn das Zufällige ist das an sich selbst Grundlose, und sich Aufhebende. Das absolute Wesen geht somit in dieser Weise in der That aus dem Grundlosen hervor; der Grund hebt sich selbst auf, somit verschwindet auch der Schein des Verhältnisses, das Gott gegeben wurde, ein in einem Andern Begründetes zu seyn. Diese Vermittelung ist hiermit die wahrhafte. Allein jene beweisende Reflexion kennt diese Natur ihrer Vermittelung nicht; sie nimmt sich einer Seits für ein bloß Subjektives, und entfernt hiermit ihre Vermittlung von Gott selbst, andern Theils aber erkennt sie deswegen nicht die vermittelnde Bewegung, daß und wie sie im Wesen selbst ist. Ihr wahrhaftes Verhältniß besteht darin, daß sie Beides in Einem ist, die Vermittelung als solche, aber zugleich allerdings eine Subjektive, äußerliche nämlich die sich äußerliche Vermittelung, welche sich an ihr selbst wieder aufhebt. In jener Darstellung aber erhält die Existenz das schiefe Verhältniß, nur als Vermitteltes oder Gesetztes zu erscheinen.\n\nSo kann auf der andern Seite die Existenz auch nicht bloß als Unmittelbares betrachtet werden. In der Bestimmung einer Unmittelbarkeit genommen, ist das Auffassen der Existenz Gottes, für etwas Unbeweisbares, und das Wissen von ihr als ein nur unmittelbares Bewußtseyn, als ein Glauben ausgedrückt worden. Das Wissen soll zu diesem Resultate kommen, daß es Nichts weiß, das heißt, daß es seine vermittelnde Bewegung und die in ihr vorkommenden Bestimmungen selbst wieder aufgiebt. Dieß hat sich auch im Vorhergehenden ergeben; allein es ist hinzuzusetzen, daß die Reflexion, indem sie mit dem Aufheben ihrer selbst endigt, darum nicht das Nichts zum Resultat hat, so daß nun das positive Wissen vom Wesen als unmittelbare Beziehung auf dasselbe, von jenem Resultate getrennt und ein eigenes Hervorgehen, ein nur von sich anfangender Akt wäre; sondern dieß Ende selbst, dieß zu Grunde gehen der Vermittlung, ist zugleich der Grund, aus dem das Unmittelbare hervorgeht. Die Sprache vereinigt, wie oben bemerkt, die Bedeutung dieses Untergangs und des Grundes; man sagt, das Wesen Gottes sey der Abgrund für die endliche Vernunft. Er ist es in der That, insofern sie darin ihre Endlichkeit aufgibt und ihre vermittelnde Bewegung versenkt; aber dieser Abgrund, der negative Grund, ist zugleich der positive des Hervorgehens des Seyenden, des an sich selbst unmittelbaren Wesens; die Vermittelung ist wesentliches Moment. Die Vermittelung durch den Grund hebt sich auf, läßt aber nicht den Grund unten, so daß das aus ihm Hervorgehende, ein Gesetztes wäre, das sein Wesen anderswo nämlich im Grunde hätte, sondern dieser Grund ist als Abgrund, die verschwundene Vermittelung; und umgekehrt ist nur die verschwundene Vermittelung zugleich der Grund, und nur durch diese Negation das sich selbst Gleiche und Unmittelbare.\n\nSo ist die Existenz hier nicht als ein Prädikat oder als Bestimmung des Wesens zu nehmen, daß ein Satz davon hieße: Das Wesen existirt, oder hat Existenz;—sondern das Wesen ist in die Existenz übergegangen; die Existenz ist seine absolute Entäußerung, jenseits deren es nicht zurückgeblieben ist. Der Satz also hieße: Das Wesen ist die Existenz; es ist nicht von seiner Existenz unterschieden. —Das Wesen ist in die Existenz übergegangen, insofern das Wesen als Grund sich von sich als dem Begründeten nicht mehr nnterscheidet, oder jener Grund sich aufgehoben hat. Aber diese Negation ist ebenso wesentlich seine Position, oder schlechthin positive Kontinuität mit sich selbst; die Existenz ist die Reflexion des Grundes in sich; seine in seiner Negation zu Stande gekommene Identität mit sich selbst, also die Vermittelung, die sich mit sich identisch gesetzt hat, und dadurch Unmittelbarkeit ist.\n\nWeil nun die Existenz wesentlich die mit sich identische Vermittelung ist, so hat sie die Bestimmungen der Vermittelung an ihr, aber so daß sie zugleich in sich reflektirte sind, und das wesentliche und unmittelbare Bestehen haben. Als die durch Aufheben sich setzende Unmittelbarkeit ist die Existenz negative Einheit und Insichseyn; sie bestimmt sich daher unmittelbar als ein Existirendes und als Ding.\n\n## A. Das Ding und seine Eigenschaften.\n\nDie Existenz als Existirendes ist gesetzt in der Form der negativen Einheit, welche sie wesentlich ist. Aber diese negative Einheit ist zunächst nur unmittelbare Bestimmung, somit das Eins des Etwas überhaupt. Das existirende Etwas ist aber unterschieden von dem seyenden Etwas. Jenes ist wesentlich eine solche Unmittelbarkeit, die durch die Reflexion der Vermittelung in sich selbst entstanden ist. So ist das existirende Etwas ein Ding.\n\nDas Ding wird von seiner Existenz unterschieden, wie das Etwas von seinem Seyn unterschieden werden kann. Das Ding und das Existirende ist unmittelbar eins und dasselbe. Aber weil die Existenz nicht die erste Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns ist, sondern das Moment der Vermittelung an ihr selbst hat, so ist ihre Bestimmung zum Dinge und die Unterscheidung beider nicht ein Übergang, sondern eigentlich eine Analyse; und die Existenz als solche enthält diese Unterscheidung selbst in dem Momente ihrer Vermittelung; den Unterschied von Ding-an-sich, und von äußerlicher Existenz.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0001","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Die Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"135.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0002","text":"Wie der Satz des Grundes ausdrückt: Alles was ist, hat einen Grund, oder ist ein Gesetztes, ein Vermitteltes; so müßte auch ein Satz der Existenz aufgestellt und so ausgedrückt werden: Alles, was ist, existirt. Die Wahrheit des Seyns ist, nicht ein erstes Unmittelbares, sondern das in die Unmittelbarkeit hervorgegangene Wesen zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"135.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0003","text":"Wenn aber ferner auch gesagt wurde, was existirt, hat einen Grund und ist bedingt, so müßte auch ebenso gesagt werden: es hat keinen Grund und ist unbedingt. Denn die Existenz ist die aus dem Aufheben der durch Grund und Bedingung beziehenden Vermittelung hervorgegangene Unmittelbarkeit, die im Hervorgehen eben dieß Hervorgehen selbst aufhebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"135.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0004","text":"Insofern die Beweise von der Existenz Gottes hier erwähnt werden können, ist zum voraus zu erinnern, daß es außer dem unmittelbaren Seyn erstens, und zweitens der Existenz, dem Seyn, das aus dem Wesen hervorgeht, noch ein ferneres Seyn gibt, welches aus dem Begriffe hervorgeht, die Objektivität.—Das Beweisen ist überhaupt die vermittelte Erkenntniß. Die verschiedenen Arten des Seyns fordern oder enthalten ihre eigene Art der Vermittelung; so wird auch die Natur des Beweisens in Ansehung einer jeden verschieden. Der ontologische Beweis will vom Begriffe ausgehen; er legt den Inbegriff aller Realitäten zu Grunde, und subsumirt alsdann auch die Existenz unter die Realität. Er ist also die Vermittelung, welche Schluß ist, und die hier noch nicht zu betrachten ist. Es ist bereits oben (I. Th. I. Abth. S. 27.ff.)","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"135.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0005","text":"auf das, was Kant hiergegen erinnert, Rüksicht genommen und bemerkt worden, daß Kant unter Existenz das bestimmte Daseyn versteht, wodurch etwas in den Kontext der gesammten Erfahrung, d. h. in die Bestimmung eines Andersseyns und in die Beziehung auf Anderes tritt. So ist als Existirendes Etwas vermittelt durch Anderes, und die Existenz überhaupt die Seite seiner Vermittelung. Nun liegt in dem, was Kant den Begriff nennt, nämlich in Etwas, insofern es als nur einfach auf sich bezogen genommen wird, oder in der Vorstellung als solcher, nicht seine Vermittelung; in der abstrakten Identität mit sich ist die Entgegensetzung weggelassen. Der ontologische Beweis hätte nun darzustellen, daß der absolute Begriff, nämlich der Begriff Gottes, zum bestimmten Daseyn, zur Vermittelung komme, oder wie das einfache Wesen sich mit der Vermittelung vermittle.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"135.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0006","text":"Dieß geschieht durch die angegebene Subsumtion der Existenz unter ihr Allgemeines, nämlich die Realität, welche als das Mittlere zwischen Gott in seinem Begriffe einer Seits, und zwischen der Existenz anderer Seits angenommen wird.—Von dieser Vermittelung, insofern sie die Form des Schlusses hat, ist, wie gesagt, hier nicht die Rede. Wie aber jene Vermittelung des Wesens mit der Existenz in Wahrheit beschaffen ist, dieß hat die bisherige Darstellung enthalten. Die Natur des Beweisens selbst ist in der Lehre von der Erkenntniß zu betrachten. Hier ist nur anzugeben, was sich auf die Natur der Vermittelung überhaupt bezieht.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"135.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0007","text":"Die Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes geben einen Grund für dieses Daseyn an.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"135.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0008","text":"Er soll nicht ein objektiver Grund des Daseyns Gottes seyn; denn dieses ist an und für sich selbst. So ist er bloß ein Grund für die Erkenntniß. Damit giebt er sich zugleich für ein solches aus, das in dem Gegenstande, der zunächst als begründet dadurch erscheint, verschwindet. Der Grund nun, der von der Zufälligkeit der Welt hergenommen ist, enthält den Rükgang derselben in das absolute Wesen; denn das Zufällige ist das an sich selbst Grundlose, und sich Aufhebende. Das absolute Wesen geht somit in dieser Weise in der That aus dem Grundlosen hervor; der Grund hebt sich selbst auf, somit verschwindet auch der Schein des Verhältnisses, das Gott gegeben wurde, ein in einem Andern Begründetes zu seyn. Diese Vermittelung ist hiermit die wahrhafte.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"135.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0009","text":"Allein jene beweisende Reflexion kennt diese Natur ihrer Vermittelung nicht; sie nimmt sich einer Seits für ein bloß Subjektives, und entfernt hiermit ihre Vermittlung von Gott selbst, andern Theils aber erkennt sie deswegen nicht die vermittelnde Bewegung, daß und wie sie im Wesen selbst ist. Ihr wahrhaftes Verhältniß besteht darin, daß sie Beides in Einem ist, die Vermittelung als solche, aber zugleich allerdings eine Subjektive, äußerliche nämlich die sich äußerliche Vermittelung, welche sich an ihr selbst wieder aufhebt. In jener Darstellung aber erhält die Existenz das schiefe Verhältniß, nur als Vermitteltes oder Gesetztes zu erscheinen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"135.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0010","text":"So kann auf der andern Seite die Existenz auch nicht bloß als Unmittelbares betrachtet werden. In der Bestimmung einer Unmittelbarkeit genommen, ist das Auffassen der Existenz Gottes, für etwas Unbeweisbares, und das Wissen von ihr als ein nur unmittelbares Bewußtseyn, als ein Glauben ausgedrückt worden. Das Wissen soll zu diesem Resultate kommen, daß es Nichts weiß, das heißt, daß es seine vermittelnde Bewegung und die in ihr vorkommenden Bestimmungen selbst wieder aufgiebt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"135.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0011","text":"Dieß hat sich auch im Vorhergehenden ergeben; allein es ist hinzuzusetzen, daß die Reflexion, indem sie mit dem Aufheben ihrer selbst endigt, darum nicht das Nichts zum Resultat hat, so daß nun das positive Wissen vom Wesen als unmittelbare Beziehung auf dasselbe, von jenem Resultate getrennt und ein eigenes Hervorgehen, ein nur von sich anfangender Akt wäre; sondern dieß Ende selbst, dieß zu Grunde gehen der Vermittlung, ist zugleich der Grund, aus dem das Unmittelbare hervorgeht. Die Sprache vereinigt, wie oben bemerkt, die Bedeutung dieses Untergangs und des Grundes; man sagt, das Wesen Gottes sey der Abgrund für die endliche Vernunft.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"135.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0012","text":"Er ist es in der That, insofern sie darin ihre Endlichkeit aufgibt und ihre vermittelnde Bewegung versenkt; aber dieser Abgrund, der negative Grund, ist zugleich der positive des Hervorgehens des Seyenden, des an sich selbst unmittelbaren Wesens; die Vermittelung ist wesentliches Moment. Die Vermittelung durch den Grund hebt sich auf, läßt aber nicht den Grund unten, so daß das aus ihm Hervorgehende, ein Gesetztes wäre, das sein Wesen anderswo nämlich im Grunde hätte, sondern dieser Grund ist als Abgrund, die verschwundene Vermittelung; und umgekehrt ist nur die verschwundene Vermittelung zugleich der Grund, und nur durch diese Negation das sich selbst Gleiche und Unmittelbare.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"135.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0013","text":"So ist die Existenz hier nicht als ein Prädikat oder als Bestimmung des Wesens zu nehmen, daß ein Satz davon hieße: Das Wesen existirt, oder hat Existenz;—sondern das Wesen ist in die Existenz übergegangen; die Existenz ist seine absolute Entäußerung, jenseits deren es nicht zurückgeblieben ist. Der Satz also hieße: Das Wesen ist die Existenz; es ist nicht von seiner Existenz unterschieden. —Das Wesen ist in die Existenz übergegangen, insofern das Wesen als Grund sich von sich als dem Begründeten nicht mehr nnterscheidet, oder jener Grund sich aufgehoben hat. Aber diese Negation ist ebenso wesentlich seine Position, oder schlechthin positive Kontinuität mit sich selbst; die Existenz ist die Reflexion des Grundes in sich; seine in seiner Negation zu Stande gekommene Identität mit sich selbst, also die Vermittelung, die sich mit sich identisch gesetzt hat, und dadurch Unmittelbarkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"135.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0014","text":"Weil nun die Existenz wesentlich die mit sich identische Vermittelung ist, so hat sie die Bestimmungen der Vermittelung an ihr, aber so daß sie zugleich in sich reflektirte sind, und das wesentliche und unmittelbare Bestehen haben. Als die durch Aufheben sich setzende Unmittelbarkeit ist die Existenz negative Einheit und Insichseyn; sie bestimmt sich daher unmittelbar als ein Existirendes und als Ding.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"135.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0015","text":"## A. Das Ding und seine Eigenschaften.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"135.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0016","text":"Die Existenz als Existirendes ist gesetzt in der Form der negativen Einheit, welche sie wesentlich ist. Aber diese negative Einheit ist zunächst nur unmittelbare Bestimmung, somit das Eins des Etwas überhaupt. Das existirende Etwas ist aber unterschieden von dem seyenden Etwas. Jenes ist wesentlich eine solche Unmittelbarkeit, die durch die Reflexion der Vermittelung in sich selbst entstanden ist. So ist das existirende Etwas ein Ding.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"135.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0017","text":"Das Ding wird von seiner Existenz unterschieden, wie das Etwas von seinem Seyn unterschieden werden kann. Das Ding und das Existirende ist unmittelbar eins und dasselbe. Aber weil die Existenz nicht die erste Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns ist, sondern das Moment der Vermittelung an ihr selbst hat, so ist ihre Bestimmung zum Dinge und die Unterscheidung beider nicht ein Übergang, sondern eigentlich eine Analyse; und die Existenz als solche enthält diese Unterscheidung selbst in dem Momente ihrer Vermittelung; den Unterschied von Ding-an-sich, und von äußerlicher Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"135.17"}],"sha256":"cf2e3f9a0fe1f006b7fe6dd63a89641a8bfadf8fffb5a2f00530f54670bf85fa","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105353954651Z_b1ec977a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Thing and Its Properties.","source_sha256":"cf2e3f9a0fe1f006b7fe6dd63a89641a8bfadf8fffb5a2f00530f54670bf85fa","sha256":"5f8506d643136a773685e3f53a292838f678ebfe7f6d78ee992544feffc2d655","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:53:53.954711+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0001","text":"## Chapter One. Existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"135.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0002","text":"As the proposition of ground expresses: Everything that is has a ground, or is a posited, a mediated [entity]; so too a proposition of existence would have to be set forth and expressed thus: Everything that is exists. The truth of being is to be, not a first immediate, but essence that has emerged into immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"135.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0003","text":"But if it was further said that what exists has a ground and is conditioned, then it would likewise have to be said: it has no ground and is unconditioned. For existence is the immediacy that has emerged from the sublation of mediation relating by ground and condition, which, in emerging, sublates precisely this emerging itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"135.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0004","text":"Insofar as the proofs of the existence of God may be mentioned here, it is to be recalled in advance that, besides immediate being, firstly, and secondly existence, being that proceeds from essence, there is yet a further being, which proceeds from the Concept: objectivity.—Proof in general is mediated cognition. The different kinds of being require or contain their own kind of mediation; thus the nature of proof too is different in respect of each. The ontological proof intends to proceed from the Concept; it takes as its ground the sum-total of all realities, and then subsumes existence too under reality. Thus it is the mediation which is syllogism, and which is not yet to be considered here. It has already been noted above (Part I, Division I, pp. 27 ff.)","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"135.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0005","text":"with respect to what Kant observes against this, that Kant understands by existence determinate Dasein, through which something enters into the context of the totality of experience, i.e. into the determination of being-other and into relation to others. Thus, as existing, something is mediated through another, and existence in general is the side of its mediation. Now, in what Kant calls the Concept, namely in something insofar as it is taken as merely simply related to itself, or in representation as such, its mediation does not lie; in abstract identity with itself, opposition has been omitted. The ontological proof would then have to demonstrate that the absolute Concept, namely the Concept of God, comes to determinate Dasein, to mediation, or how simple essence mediates itself with mediation.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"135.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0006","text":"This occurs through the indicated subsumption of existence under its universal, namely reality, which is assumed as the middle term between God in his Concept on the one side, and existence on the other.—Of this mediation, insofar as it has the form of syllogism, there is, as said, no question here. But what that mediation of essence with existence truly is has been contained in the exposition thus far. The nature of proof itself is to be considered in the doctrine of cognition. Here it is only to be indicated what pertains to the nature of mediation in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"135.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0007","text":"The proofs of the Dasein of God state a ground for this Dasein.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"135.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0008","text":"It is not supposed to be an objective ground of God's Dasein; for this is in and for itself. Thus it is merely a ground for cognition. Thereby it at the same time presents itself as something which vanishes in the object that at first appears as grounded by it. Now the ground taken from the contingency of the world contains its regress into absolute essence; for the contingent is that which is in itself without ground and self-sublating. Thus absolute essence in this manner in fact proceeds out of the groundless; the ground sublates itself, and thus the semblance of the relation attributed to God, of being something grounded in another, also vanishes. This mediation is thereby the true one.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"135.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0009","text":"Yet that proving reflection does not know this nature of its mediation; on the one hand, it takes itself to be merely subjective, and thereby removes its mediation from God himself; on the other hand, for this reason it does not cognize the mediating movement, that and how it is in essence itself. Its true relation consists in its being both in one: mediation as such, but at the same time indeed a subjective, external mediation, namely mediation external to itself, which once again sublates itself within itself. But in that exposition existence receives the distorted relation of appearing only as mediated or posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"135.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0010","text":"Thus, on the other side, existence cannot be considered merely as immediate either. Taken in the determination of an immediacy, the apprehension of God's existence as something indemonstrable, and knowledge of it as a merely immediate consciousness, as a faith, have been expressed. Knowledge is supposed to arrive at this result, that it knows nothing, that is, that it relinquishes once again its mediating movement and the determinations occurring within it themselves.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"135.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0011","text":"This has also emerged in what precedes; but it must be added that reflection, in ending with the sublation of itself, does not therefore have nothing as its result, such that positive knowledge of essence as immediate relation to it would now be separated from that result and would be an independent emergence, an act beginning merely from itself; rather, this end itself, this going-to-ground of mediation, is at the same time the ground from which the immediate proceeds. Language unites, as remarked above, the meaning of this downfall and of ground; one says that the essence of God is the abyss for finite reason.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"135.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0012","text":"It is so in fact, insofar as it relinquishes its finitude therein and immerses its mediating movement; but this abyss, the negative ground, is at the same time the positive ground of the emergence of the being, of essence immediate in itself; mediation is an essential moment. Mediation through ground sublates itself, but does not leave the ground below, so that what proceeds from it would be a posited [entity] whose essence it would have elsewhere, namely in the ground; rather, this ground is, as abyss, vanished mediation; and conversely, only vanished mediation is at the same time ground, and only through this negation is it self-equal and immediate.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"135.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0013","text":"Thus existence here is not to be taken as a predicate or as a determination of essence, such that a proposition concerning it would be: Essence exists, or has existence;—rather, essence has passed over into existence; existence is its absolute externalization, beyond which it has not remained behind. The proposition would therefore be: Essence is existence; it is not distinct from its existence. —Essence has passed over into existence insofar as essence, as ground, no longer distinguishes itself from itself as the grounded, or that ground has sublated itself. But this negation is just as essentially its positing, or absolutely positive continuity with itself; existence is the reflection of ground into itself; its identity with itself, brought about in its negation, thus the mediation that has posited itself as identical with itself and thereby is immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"135.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0014","text":"Now because existence is essentially mediation identical with itself, it has the determinations of mediation within itself, but in such a way that they are at the same time reflected into themselves and have essential and immediate subsistence. As immediacy positing itself through sublation, existence is negative unity and being-within-self; it therefore determines itself immediately as an existing [entity] and as thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"135.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0015","text":"## A. The Thing and Its Properties.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"135.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0016","text":"Existence as existing [entity] is posited in the form of negative unity which it essentially is. But this negative unity is at first only immediate determination, hence the one of something in general. But the existing something is distinct from the being something. The former is essentially such an immediacy as has arisen through the reflection of mediation into itself. Thus the existing something is a thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"135.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0017","text":"The thing is distinguished from its existence, just as something can be distinguished from its being. The thing and the existing [entity] are immediately one and the same. But because existence is not the first immediacy of being, but has the moment of mediation in itself, its determination as thing and the distinction of the two are not a transition, but properly an analysis; and existence as such itself contains this distinction in the moment of its mediation: the distinction between thing-in-itself and external existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"135.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DDUS:P0017"]}],"source_digest":"c6980fac3871b85d7371685ac2602c7fb95ce5434c3ef6926a276169d90d8587","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Ding und seine Eigenschaften."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Ding und seine Eigenschaften.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE","title":"a. Thing-in-Itself and Existence.","order":136,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DSUE","text":"1. Das Ding an sich ist das Existirende als das durch die aufgehobene Vermittelung vorhandene, wesentliche Unmittelbare. Darin ist dem Ding an sich die Vermittelung ebenso wesentlich; aber dieser Unterschied in dieser ersten oder unmittelbaren Existenz, fällt in gleichgültige Bestimmungen auseinander. Die eine Seite, nämlich die Vermittelung des Dinges ist seine nicht reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit; also sein Seyn überhaupt, das, weil es zugleich als Vermittelung bestimmt ist, ein sich selbst anderes, in sich mannigfaltiges und äußerliches Daseyn ist. Es ist aber nicht nur Daseyn, sondern in Beziehung auf die aufgehobene Vermittelung und wesentliche Unmittelbarkeit; es ist daher das Daseyn als Unwesentliches, als Gesetztseyn.—(Wenn das Ding von seiner Existenz unterschieden wird, so ist es das Mögliche, das Ding der Vorstellung, oder das Gedankending, welches als solches nicht zugleich existiren soll. Die Bestimmung der Möglichkeit und der Gegensatz des Dings gegen seine Existenz ist jedoch später.)—Aber das Ding-an-sich und sein vermitteltes Seyn sind beide in der Existenz enthalten, und beide selbst Existenzen; das Ding-an-sich existirt, und ist die wesentliche, das vermittelte Seyn aber die unwesentliche Existenz des Dinges.\n\nDas Ding an sich, als das einfache Reflektirt-seyn der Existenz in sich, ist nicht der Grund des unwesentlichen Daseyns; es ist die unbewegte, unbestimmte Einheit, weil es eben die Bestimmung hat, die aufgehobene Vermittelung zu seyn, und daher nur die Grundlage desselben. Darum fällt auch die Reflexion als das sich durch anderes vermittelnde Daseyn außer dem Dinge-an-sich. Dieses soll keine bestimmte Mannigfaltigkeit an ihm selbst haben; und erhält sie deswegen erst an die äußerliche Reflexion gebracht; aber bleibt gleichgültig dagegen. (—Das Ding-an-sich hat Farbe erst an das Auge gebracht, Geschmack an die Nase u.s.f.) Seine Verschiedenheit sind Rüksichten, welche ein Andres nimmt, bestimmte Beziehungen, die sich dieses auf das Ding-an-sich gibt, und die nicht eigene Bestimmungen desselben sind.\n\n2. Dieß Andere ist nun die Reflexion, welche bestimmt als äußerlich erstens sich selbst äußerlich, und die bestimmte Mannigfaltigkeit ist. Alsdann ist sie dem wesentlich Existirenden äußerlich, und bezieht sich darauf als auf seine absolute Voraussetzung. Diese beiden Momente der äußerlichen Reflexion aber, ihre eigene Mannigfaltigkeit und ihre Beziehung auf das ihr andere Ding-an-sich, sind ein und dasselbe. Denn diese Existenz ist nur äußerlich, insofern sie sich auf die wesentliche Identität als auf ein Anderes bezieht. Die Mannigfaltigkeit hat daher nicht jenseits des Dinges-an-sich ein eigenes selbstständiges Bestehen, sondern ist erst als Schein gegen dieses, in ihrer nothwendigen Beziehung darauf, als der sich an ihm brechende Reflex. Die Verschiedenheit ist also vorhanden, als die Beziehung eines Andern auf das Ding-an-sich; aber dieses Andere ist nichts für sich Bestehendes, sondern ist erst als Beziehung auf das Ding-an-sich; zugleich aber ist es nur als das Abstoßen von diesem; es ist so der haltlose Gegenstoß seiner in sich selbst.\n\nDem Ding-an-sich nun, da es die wesentliche Identität der Existenz ist, kommt daher diese wesenlose Reflexion nicht zu, sondern sie fällt ihm äußerlich in sich selbst zusammen. Sie geht zu Grunde, und wird damit selbst zur wesentlichen Identität oder zum Ding-an-sich. —Dieß kann auch so betrachtet werden: Die wesenlose Existenz hat am Ding-an-sich ihre Reflexion in sich; sie bezieht sich dar-auf zunächst als auf ihr Anderes; aber als das Andre gegen das, was an sich ist, ist sie nur das Aufheben ihrer selbst, und das Werden zum An- sich-seyn. Das Ding-an-sich ist somit identisch mit der äußerlichen Existenz.\n\nDieß stellt sich am Ding-an-sich so dar. Das Ding-an-sich ist die sich auf sich beziehende, wesentliche Existenz; es ist nur insofern die Identität mit sich, als es die Negativität der Reflexion in sich selbst enthält; das was als ihm äußerliche Existenz erschien, ist daher Moment in ihm selbst. Es ist deswegen auch sich von sich abstoßendes Ding-an-sich, das sich also zu sich als zu einem Andern verhält. Somit sind nun mehrere Dinge-an-sich vorhanden, die in der Beziehung der äußerlichen Reflexion auf einander stehen. Diese unwesentliche Existenz ist ihr Verhältniß zu einander als zu anderen; aber sie ist ihnen ferner selbst wesentlich—oder diese unwesentliche Existenz, indem sie in sich zusammenfällt, ist Ding-an-sich; aber ein anderes, als jenes erste; denn jenes erste ist unmittelbare Wesentlichkeit, dieses aber das aus der unwesentlichen Existenz hervorgehende. Allein dieses andere Ding-an-sich ist nur ein Anderes überhaupt; denn als mit sich identisches Ding hat es weiter keine Bestimmtheit gegen das erste; es ist die Reflexion der unwesentlichen Existenz in sich wie das erste. Die Bestimmtheit der verschiedenen Dinge-an-sich gegen einander fällt daher in die äußerliche Reflexion.\n\n3. Diese äußerliche Reflexion ist nunmehr ein Verhalten der Dinge-an-sich zu einander, ihre gegenseitige Vermittelung als anderer. Die Dinge-an-sich sind so die Extreme eines Schlusses, dessen Mitte ihre äußerliche Existenz ausmacht, die Existenz, durch welche sie andere für einander und unterschiedene sind. Dieser ihr Unterschied fällt nur in ihre Beziehung; sie schicken gleichsam nur von ihrer Oberfläche Bestimmungen in die Beziehung, gegen welche sie als absolut in sich reflektirte gleichgültig bleiben.—Dieses Verhältniß macht nun die Totalität der Existenz aus. Das Ding-an-sich steht in Beziehung auf eine ihm äußerliche Reflexion, worin es mannigfaltige Bestimmungen hat; es ist dieß das Abstoßen seiner von sich selbst in ein anderes Ding-an-sich; dieß Abstoßen ist der Gegenstoß seiner in sich selbst, indem jedes nur ein Anderes ist als sich aus dem Andern wiederscheinend; es hat sein Gesetztseyn nicht an ihm selbst, sondern an dem Andern, ist bestimmt nur durch die Bestimmtheit des Andern; dieß Andere ist ebenso bestimmt nur durch die Bestimmtheit des ersten. Aber die beiden Dinge-an-sich, da sie hiermit nicht die Verschiedenheit an ihnen selbst haben, sondern jedes nur an dem andern, sind keine unterschiedene; das Ding-an-sich verhält sich, indem es sich auf das andere Extrem als ein anderes Ding-an-sich verhalten soll, zu einem von ihm Ununterschiedenen, und die äußerliche Reflexion, welche die vermittelnde Beziehung zwischen Extremen ausmachen sollte, ist ein Verhalten des Dings-an-sich nur zu sich selbst, oder wesentlich seine Reflexion in sich; sie ist somit an sich seyende Bestimmtheit, oder die Bestimmtheit des Dings-an-sich. Dieses hat dieselbe also nicht in einer ihm äußerlichen Beziehung auf ein anderes Ding-an-sich, und des Anderen auf es; die Bestimmtheit ist nicht nur eine Oberfläche desselben, sondern ist die wesentliche Vermittelung seiner mit sich als mit einem Andern.—Die beiden Dinge-an-sich, welche die Extreme der Beziehung ausmachen sollen, indem sie an sich keine Bestimmtheit gegen einander haben sollen, fallen in der That in eins zusammen; es ist nur Ein Ding-an-sich, das in der äußerlichen Reflexion sich zu sich selbst verhält, und es ist dessen eigene Beziehung auf sich als auf ein Anderes, was dessen Bestimmtheit ausmacht.\n\nDiese Bestimmtheit des Dings-an-sich ist die Eigenschaft des Dings.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0001","text":"1. Das Ding an sich ist das Existirende als das durch die aufgehobene Vermittelung vorhandene, wesentliche Unmittelbare. Darin ist dem Ding an sich die Vermittelung ebenso wesentlich; aber dieser Unterschied in dieser ersten oder unmittelbaren Existenz, fällt in gleichgültige Bestimmungen auseinander. Die eine Seite, nämlich die Vermittelung des Dinges ist seine nicht reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit; also sein Seyn überhaupt, das, weil es zugleich als Vermittelung bestimmt ist, ein sich selbst anderes, in sich mannigfaltiges und äußerliches Daseyn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"136.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0002","text":"Es ist aber nicht nur Daseyn, sondern in Beziehung auf die aufgehobene Vermittelung und wesentliche Unmittelbarkeit; es ist daher das Daseyn als Unwesentliches, als Gesetztseyn.—(Wenn das Ding von seiner Existenz unterschieden wird, so ist es das Mögliche, das Ding der Vorstellung, oder das Gedankending, welches als solches nicht zugleich existiren soll. Die Bestimmung der Möglichkeit und der Gegensatz des Dings gegen seine Existenz ist jedoch später.)—Aber das Ding-an-sich und sein vermitteltes Seyn sind beide in der Existenz enthalten, und beide selbst Existenzen; das Ding-an-sich existirt, und ist die wesentliche, das vermittelte Seyn aber die unwesentliche Existenz des Dinges.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"136.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0003","text":"Das Ding an sich, als das einfache Reflektirt-seyn der Existenz in sich, ist nicht der Grund des unwesentlichen Daseyns; es ist die unbewegte, unbestimmte Einheit, weil es eben die Bestimmung hat, die aufgehobene Vermittelung zu seyn, und daher nur die Grundlage desselben. Darum fällt auch die Reflexion als das sich durch anderes vermittelnde Daseyn außer dem Dinge-an-sich. Dieses soll keine bestimmte Mannigfaltigkeit an ihm selbst haben; und erhält sie deswegen erst an die äußerliche Reflexion gebracht; aber bleibt gleichgültig dagegen. (—Das Ding-an-sich hat Farbe erst an das Auge gebracht, Geschmack an die Nase u.s.f.) Seine Verschiedenheit sind Rüksichten, welche ein Andres nimmt, bestimmte Beziehungen, die sich dieses auf das Ding-an-sich gibt, und die nicht eigene Bestimmungen desselben sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"136.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0004","text":"2. Dieß Andere ist nun die Reflexion, welche bestimmt als äußerlich erstens sich selbst äußerlich, und die bestimmte Mannigfaltigkeit ist. Alsdann ist sie dem wesentlich Existirenden äußerlich, und bezieht sich darauf als auf seine absolute Voraussetzung. Diese beiden Momente der äußerlichen Reflexion aber, ihre eigene Mannigfaltigkeit und ihre Beziehung auf das ihr andere Ding-an-sich, sind ein und dasselbe. Denn diese Existenz ist nur äußerlich, insofern sie sich auf die wesentliche Identität als auf ein Anderes bezieht. Die Mannigfaltigkeit hat daher nicht jenseits des Dinges-an-sich ein eigenes selbstständiges Bestehen, sondern ist erst als Schein gegen dieses, in ihrer nothwendigen Beziehung darauf, als der sich an ihm brechende Reflex.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"136.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0005","text":"Die Verschiedenheit ist also vorhanden, als die Beziehung eines Andern auf das Ding-an-sich; aber dieses Andere ist nichts für sich Bestehendes, sondern ist erst als Beziehung auf das Ding-an-sich; zugleich aber ist es nur als das Abstoßen von diesem; es ist so der haltlose Gegenstoß seiner in sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"136.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0006","text":"Dem Ding-an-sich nun, da es die wesentliche Identität der Existenz ist, kommt daher diese wesenlose Reflexion nicht zu, sondern sie fällt ihm äußerlich in sich selbst zusammen. Sie geht zu Grunde, und wird damit selbst zur wesentlichen Identität oder zum Ding-an-sich. —Dieß kann auch so betrachtet werden: Die wesenlose Existenz hat am Ding-an-sich ihre Reflexion in sich; sie bezieht sich dar-auf zunächst als auf ihr Anderes; aber als das Andre gegen das, was an sich ist, ist sie nur das Aufheben ihrer selbst, und das Werden zum An- sich-seyn. Das Ding-an-sich ist somit identisch mit der äußerlichen Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"136.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0007","text":"Dieß stellt sich am Ding-an-sich so dar. Das Ding-an-sich ist die sich auf sich beziehende, wesentliche Existenz; es ist nur insofern die Identität mit sich, als es die Negativität der Reflexion in sich selbst enthält; das was als ihm äußerliche Existenz erschien, ist daher Moment in ihm selbst. Es ist deswegen auch sich von sich abstoßendes Ding-an-sich, das sich also zu sich als zu einem Andern verhält. Somit sind nun mehrere Dinge-an-sich vorhanden, die in der Beziehung der äußerlichen Reflexion auf einander stehen. Diese unwesentliche Existenz ist ihr Verhältniß zu einander als zu anderen; aber sie ist ihnen ferner selbst wesentlich—oder diese unwesentliche Existenz, indem sie in sich zusammenfällt, ist Ding-an-sich; aber ein anderes, als jenes erste; denn jenes erste ist unmittelbare Wesentlichkeit, dieses aber das aus der unwesentlichen Existenz hervorgehende.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"136.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0008","text":"Allein dieses andere Ding-an-sich ist nur ein Anderes überhaupt; denn als mit sich identisches Ding hat es weiter keine Bestimmtheit gegen das erste; es ist die Reflexion der unwesentlichen Existenz in sich wie das erste. Die Bestimmtheit der verschiedenen Dinge-an-sich gegen einander fällt daher in die äußerliche Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"136.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0009","text":"3. Diese äußerliche Reflexion ist nunmehr ein Verhalten der Dinge-an-sich zu einander, ihre gegenseitige Vermittelung als anderer. Die Dinge-an-sich sind so die Extreme eines Schlusses, dessen Mitte ihre äußerliche Existenz ausmacht, die Existenz, durch welche sie andere für einander und unterschiedene sind. Dieser ihr Unterschied fällt nur in ihre Beziehung; sie schicken gleichsam nur von ihrer Oberfläche Bestimmungen in die Beziehung, gegen welche sie als absolut in sich reflektirte gleichgültig bleiben.—Dieses Verhältniß macht nun die Totalität der Existenz aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"136.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0010","text":"Das Ding-an-sich steht in Beziehung auf eine ihm äußerliche Reflexion, worin es mannigfaltige Bestimmungen hat; es ist dieß das Abstoßen seiner von sich selbst in ein anderes Ding-an-sich; dieß Abstoßen ist der Gegenstoß seiner in sich selbst, indem jedes nur ein Anderes ist als sich aus dem Andern wiederscheinend; es hat sein Gesetztseyn nicht an ihm selbst, sondern an dem Andern, ist bestimmt nur durch die Bestimmtheit des Andern; dieß Andere ist ebenso bestimmt nur durch die Bestimmtheit des ersten.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"136.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0011","text":"Aber die beiden Dinge-an-sich, da sie hiermit nicht die Verschiedenheit an ihnen selbst haben, sondern jedes nur an dem andern, sind keine unterschiedene; das Ding-an-sich verhält sich, indem es sich auf das andere Extrem als ein anderes Ding-an-sich verhalten soll, zu einem von ihm Ununterschiedenen, und die äußerliche Reflexion, welche die vermittelnde Beziehung zwischen Extremen ausmachen sollte, ist ein Verhalten des Dings-an-sich nur zu sich selbst, oder wesentlich seine Reflexion in sich; sie ist somit an sich seyende Bestimmtheit, oder die Bestimmtheit des Dings-an-sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"136.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0012","text":"Dieses hat dieselbe also nicht in einer ihm äußerlichen Beziehung auf ein anderes Ding-an-sich, und des Anderen auf es; die Bestimmtheit ist nicht nur eine Oberfläche desselben, sondern ist die wesentliche Vermittelung seiner mit sich als mit einem Andern.—Die beiden Dinge-an-sich, welche die Extreme der Beziehung ausmachen sollen, indem sie an sich keine Bestimmtheit gegen einander haben sollen, fallen in der That in eins zusammen; es ist nur Ein Ding-an-sich, das in der äußerlichen Reflexion sich zu sich selbst verhält, und es ist dessen eigene Beziehung auf sich als auf ein Anderes, was dessen Bestimmtheit ausmacht.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"136.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0013","text":"Diese Bestimmtheit des Dings-an-sich ist die Eigenschaft des Dings.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"136.13"}],"sha256":"7f3e6019a82a41c8f670a82f70e7d28114482b07af9fb851432c4f545f4a76af","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105410776077Z_54001f19","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Thing-in-Itself and Existence.","source_sha256":"7f3e6019a82a41c8f670a82f70e7d28114482b07af9fb851432c4f545f4a76af","sha256":"121f8bf4b24e7b40fd59f7a39bb869724e8bd242ec1e068ba7b390c1ce2455f4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:54:10.776102+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0001","text":"1. The thing-in-itself is that which exists as that which is present through sublated mediation, essential immediacy. Therein mediation is equally essential to the thing-in-itself; but this difference, in this first or immediate existence, falls asunder into indifferent determinations. The one side, namely the mediation of the thing, is its unreflected immediacy; thus its being in general, which, because it is at the same time determined as mediation, is a being-there that is other than itself, manifold and external within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"136.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0002","text":"But it is not merely being-there, but being-there in relation to sublated mediation and essential immediacy; it is therefore being-there as non-essential, as positedness.—(When the thing is distinguished from its existence, it is the possible, the thing of representation, or the thing of thought, which as such is not also supposed to exist. The determination of possibility and the opposition of the thing to its existence, however, come later.)—But the thing-in-itself and its mediated being are both contained in existence, and are themselves both existences; the thing-in-itself exists, and is the essential existence, whereas mediated being is the non-essential existence of the thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"136.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0003","text":"The thing-in-itself, as the simple being-reflected-into-itself of existence, is not the ground of non-essential being-there; it is the unmoved, indeterminate unity, because it has precisely the determination of being sublated mediation, and hence is only the substratum of the latter. For this reason reflection too, as being-there mediated through an other, falls outside the thing-in-itself. The latter is to have no determinate manifoldness in itself; and therefore receives it only when it is brought to it by external reflection, but remains indifferent to it. (—The thing-in-itself has colour only when brought to the eye, taste when brought to the nose, etc.) Its differences are respects which an other takes, determinate relations which this other gives itself to the thing-in-itself, and which are not determinations proper to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"136.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0004","text":"2. This other is now reflection, which, determined as external, is first externally related to itself, and is determinate manifoldness. Then it is external to that which essentially exists, and relates to it as to its absolute presupposition. But these two moments of external reflection, its own manifoldness and its relation to the thing-in-itself which is other than it, are one and the same. For this existence is external only insofar as it relates to essential identity as to an other. Manifoldness therefore has no independent subsistence of its own beyond the thing-in-itself, but is only as semblance in contrast to it, in its necessary relation to it, as the reflection refracted upon it.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"136.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0005","text":"Difference is thus present as the relation of an other to the thing-in-itself; but this other is nothing subsisting for itself, but is only as relation to the thing-in-itself; yet at the same time it is only as repulsion from the latter; it is thus the unstable counter-thrust of the latter within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"136.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0006","text":"Now, since the thing-in-itself is the essential identity of existence, this non-essential reflection does not belong to it, but falls together externally to it within itself. It perishes, and thereby itself becomes essential identity or the thing-in-itself. —This can also be considered thus: non-essential existence has in the thing-in-itself its reflection into itself; it relates to it initially as to its other; but as the other in opposition to that which is in itself, it is only the sublation of itself and the becoming of being-in-itself. The thing-in-itself is thus identical with external existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"136.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0007","text":"This presents itself in the thing-in-itself as follows. The thing-in-itself is essential existence relating itself to itself; it is identity with itself only insofar as it contains within itself the negativity of reflection; that which appeared as existence external to it is therefore a moment within it itself. It is therefore also a thing-in-itself repelling itself from itself, which thus relates to itself as to an other. Thus there are now several things-in-themselves, which stand in the relation of external reflection to one another. This non-essential existence is their relation to one another as to others; but it is furthermore itself essential to them—or this non-essential existence, in falling together within itself, is thing-in-itself; but another than that first one; for that first one is immediate essentiality, whereas this one is that which emerges from non-essential existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"136.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0008","text":"Yet this other thing-in-itself is only an other in general; for as a thing identical with itself it has no further determinacy in opposition to the first; it is the reflection of non-essential existence into itself, just as the first is. The determinacy of the different things-in-themselves in opposition to one another therefore falls into external reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"136.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0009","text":"3. This external reflection is now a comportment of things-in-themselves toward one another, their reciprocal mediation as others. The things-in-themselves are thus the extremes of a syllogism, the middle term of which is constituted by their external existence, the existence through which they are others for one another and distinct. This their difference falls only into their relation; they send, as it were, determinations into the relation only from their surface, toward which they remain indifferent as absolutely reflected into themselves.—This relation now constitutes the totality of existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"136.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0010","text":"The thing-in-itself stands in relation to a reflection external to it, in which it has manifold determinations; this is its repulsion from itself into another thing-in-itself; this repulsion is its counter-thrust within itself, since each is only an other as reflected back from the other; it does not have its positedness in itself, but in the other, is determined only through the determinacy of the other; this other is likewise determined only through the determinacy of the first.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"136.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0011","text":"But the two things-in-themselves, since they thereby do not have difference in themselves, but each only in the other, are not distinct; in relating itself to the other extreme as to another thing-in-itself, the thing-in-itself relates to something not distinct from it, and external reflection, which was supposed to constitute the mediating relation between extremes, is a comportment of the thing-in-itself only toward itself, or essentially its reflection into itself; it is thus determinacy which is in itself, or the determinacy of the thing-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"136.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0012","text":"Thus it does not have this in a relation external to it to another thing-in-itself, and of the other to it; determinacy is not merely a surface of it, but is its essential mediation with itself as with an other.—The two things-in-themselves which are supposed to constitute the extremes of the relation, since they are supposed to have no determinacy in themselves in opposition to one another, in fact fall together into one; there is only one thing-in-itself which in external reflection relates to itself, and it is its own relation to itself as to an other which constitutes its determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"136.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0013","text":"This determinacy of the thing-in-itself is the property of the thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"136.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DSUE:P0013"]}],"source_digest":"7c90082fc455ba9fda20bee5716bb4aea096e772d05824f8c75e9f69aedffaa3","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Ding an sich und Existenz."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Ding an sich und Existenz.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2","title":"b. Property.","order":137,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BD_2","text":"Die Qualität ist die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit des Etwas; das Negative selbst, wodurch das Seyn Etwas ist. So ist die Eigenschaft des Dings die Negativität der Reflexion, wodurch die Existenz überhaupt ein Existirendes, und als einfache Identität mit sich, Ding-an-sich ist. Die Negativität der Reflexion, die aufgehobene Vermittelung, ist aber wesentlich selbst Vermittelung, und Beziehung, nicht auf ein Anderes überhaupt, wie die Qualität als die nicht reflektirte Bestimmtheit; sondern Beziehung auf sich als auf ein Anderes; oder Vermittelung, die unmittelbar ebenso sehr Identität mit sich ist. Das abstrakte Ding an-sich ist selbst dieß aus anderem in sich zurückkehrende Verhalten; es ist dadurch an sich selbst bestimmt; aber seine Bestimmtheit ist Beschaffenheit, die als solche selbst Bestimmung ist, und als Verhalten zu Anderem nicht in das Andersseyn übergeht und der Veränderung entnommen ist.\n\nEin Ding hat Eigenschaften; sie sind erstlich seine bestimmten Beziehungen auf Anderes; die Eigenschaft ist nur vorhanden als eine Weise des Verhaltens zu einander; sie ist daher die äußerliche Reflexion, und die Seite des Gesetztseyns des Dings. Aber zweitens ist das Ding in diesem Gesetztseyn an sich; es erhält sich, in der Beziehung auf Anderes; es ist also allerdings nur eine Oberfläche, mit der die Existenz sich dem Werden des Seyns und der Veränderung preisgibt; die Eigenschaft verliert sich darin nicht. Ein Ding hat die Eigenschaft, dieß oder jenes im Andern zu bewirken und auf eine eigenthümliche Weise sich in seiner Beziehung zu äußern. Es beweist diese Eigenschaft nur unter der Bedingung einer entsprechenden Beschaffenheit des andern Dinges, aber sie ist ihm zugleich eigenthümlich und seine mit sich identische Grundlage;—diese reflektirte Qualität heißt darum Eigenschaft. Es geht darin in eine Äußerlichkeit über, aber die Eigenschaft erhält sich darin. Das Ding wird durch seine Eigenschaften Ursache, und die Ursache ist dieß, als Wirkung sich zu erhalten. Jedoch ist hier das Ding nur erst das ruhige Ding von vielen Eigenschaften; noch nicht als wirkliche Ursache bestimmt; es ist nur erst die ansichseyende, noch nicht selbst die setzende Reflexion seiner Bestimmungen.\n\nDas Ding-an-sich ist also, wie sich ergeben hat, wesentlich nicht nur so Ding-an-sich, daß seine Eigenschaften Gesetztseyn einer äußerlichen Reflexion sind, sondern sie sind seine eigenen Bestimmungen, durch die es sich auf bestimmte Weise verhält; es ist nicht eine jenseits seiner äußerlichen Existenz befindliche bestimmungslose Grundlage; sondern ist in seinen Eigenschaften, als Grund vorhanden, das heißt, die Identität mit sich in seinem Gesetztseyn; aber zugleich als bedingter Grund; das heißt, sein Gesetztseyn ist ebenso sehr sich äußerliche Reflexion; es ist nur insofern in sich reflektirt und an sich, insofern es äußerlich ist. —Durch die Existenz tritt das Ding-an-sich in äußerliche Beziehungen; und die Existenz besteht in dieser Äußerlichkeit; sie ist die Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, und das Ding dadurch der Veränderung unterworfen; aber sie ist auch die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit des Grundes, das Ding somit an sich in seiner Veränderung.—Diese Erwähnung der Grundbeziehung ist jedoch hier nicht so zu nehmen, daß das Ding überhaupt als Grund seiner Eigenschaften bestimmt sey; die Dingheit selbst ist als solche die Grundbestimmung, die Eigenschaft ist nicht von ihrem Grunde unterschieden, noch macht sie bloß das Gesetztseyn aus, sondern ist der in seine Äußerlichkeit übergegangene, und damit wahrhaft in sich reflektirte Grund; die Eigenschaft selbst als solche ist der Grund, an sich seyendes Gesetztseyn, oder er macht die Form ihrer Identität mit sich aus; ihre Bestimmtheit ist die sich äußerliche Reflexion des Grundes; und das Ganze der in seinem Abstoßen und Bestimmen, in seiner äußerlichen Unmittelbarkeit sich auf sich beziehende Grund.—Das Ding-an-sich existirt also wesentlich, und daß es existirt, heißt umgekehrt, die Existenz ist als äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit zugleich Ansichseyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0001","text":"Die Qualität ist die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit des Etwas; das Negative selbst, wodurch das Seyn Etwas ist. So ist die Eigenschaft des Dings die Negativität der Reflexion, wodurch die Existenz überhaupt ein Existirendes, und als einfache Identität mit sich, Ding-an-sich ist. Die Negativität der Reflexion, die aufgehobene Vermittelung, ist aber wesentlich selbst Vermittelung, und Beziehung, nicht auf ein Anderes überhaupt, wie die Qualität als die nicht reflektirte Bestimmtheit; sondern Beziehung auf sich als auf ein Anderes; oder Vermittelung, die unmittelbar ebenso sehr Identität mit sich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"137.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0002","text":"Das abstrakte Ding an-sich ist selbst dieß aus anderem in sich zurückkehrende Verhalten; es ist dadurch an sich selbst bestimmt; aber seine Bestimmtheit ist Beschaffenheit, die als solche selbst Bestimmung ist, und als Verhalten zu Anderem nicht in das Andersseyn übergeht und der Veränderung entnommen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"137.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0003","text":"Ein Ding hat Eigenschaften; sie sind erstlich seine bestimmten Beziehungen auf Anderes; die Eigenschaft ist nur vorhanden als eine Weise des Verhaltens zu einander; sie ist daher die äußerliche Reflexion, und die Seite des Gesetztseyns des Dings. Aber zweitens ist das Ding in diesem Gesetztseyn an sich; es erhält sich, in der Beziehung auf Anderes; es ist also allerdings nur eine Oberfläche, mit der die Existenz sich dem Werden des Seyns und der Veränderung preisgibt; die Eigenschaft verliert sich darin nicht. Ein Ding hat die Eigenschaft, dieß oder jenes im Andern zu bewirken und auf eine eigenthümliche Weise sich in seiner Beziehung zu äußern. Es beweist diese Eigenschaft nur unter der Bedingung einer entsprechenden Beschaffenheit des andern Dinges, aber sie ist ihm zugleich eigenthümlich und seine mit sich identische Grundlage;—diese reflektirte Qualität heißt darum Eigenschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"137.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0004","text":"Es geht darin in eine Äußerlichkeit über, aber die Eigenschaft erhält sich darin. Das Ding wird durch seine Eigenschaften Ursache, und die Ursache ist dieß, als Wirkung sich zu erhalten. Jedoch ist hier das Ding nur erst das ruhige Ding von vielen Eigenschaften; noch nicht als wirkliche Ursache bestimmt; es ist nur erst die ansichseyende, noch nicht selbst die setzende Reflexion seiner Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"137.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0005","text":"Das Ding-an-sich ist also, wie sich ergeben hat, wesentlich nicht nur so Ding-an-sich, daß seine Eigenschaften Gesetztseyn einer äußerlichen Reflexion sind, sondern sie sind seine eigenen Bestimmungen, durch die es sich auf bestimmte Weise verhält; es ist nicht eine jenseits seiner äußerlichen Existenz befindliche bestimmungslose Grundlage; sondern ist in seinen Eigenschaften, als Grund vorhanden, das heißt, die Identität mit sich in seinem Gesetztseyn; aber zugleich als bedingter Grund; das heißt, sein Gesetztseyn ist ebenso sehr sich äußerliche Reflexion; es ist nur insofern in sich reflektirt und an sich, insofern es äußerlich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"137.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0006","text":"—Durch die Existenz tritt das Ding-an-sich in äußerliche Beziehungen; und die Existenz besteht in dieser Äußerlichkeit; sie ist die Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, und das Ding dadurch der Veränderung unterworfen; aber sie ist auch die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit des Grundes, das Ding somit an sich in seiner Veränderung.—Diese Erwähnung der Grundbeziehung ist jedoch hier nicht so zu nehmen, daß das Ding überhaupt als Grund seiner Eigenschaften bestimmt sey; die Dingheit selbst ist als solche die Grundbestimmung, die Eigenschaft ist nicht von ihrem Grunde unterschieden, noch macht sie bloß das Gesetztseyn aus, sondern ist der in seine Äußerlichkeit übergegangene, und damit wahrhaft in sich reflektirte Grund; die Eigenschaft selbst als solche ist der Grund, an sich seyendes Gesetztseyn, oder er macht die Form ihrer Identität mit sich aus; ihre Bestimmtheit ist die sich äußerliche Reflexion des","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"137.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0007","text":"Grundes; und das Ganze der in seinem Abstoßen und Bestimmen, in seiner äußerlichen Unmittelbarkeit sich auf sich beziehende Grund.—Das Ding-an-sich existirt also wesentlich, und daß es existirt, heißt umgekehrt, die Existenz ist als äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit zugleich Ansichseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"137.7"}],"sha256":"814bf2688e72532eb3515073c1cbaa8862658acdf29f748d8035c125e2a867d6","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105420306385Z_0da55bfb","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. Property.","source_sha256":"814bf2688e72532eb3515073c1cbaa8862658acdf29f748d8035c125e2a867d6","sha256":"7bd345b495d9957655a2565953c8849ff3c17bc3321eafee1adc3bb8fae9e183","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:54:20.306402+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0001","text":"Quality is the immediate determinacy of the Something; the negative itself, whereby Being is Something. Thus the property of the Thing is the negativity of reflection, whereby existence in general is an existent, and, as simple identity with itself, Thing-in-itself. But the negativity of reflection, the sublated mediation, is essentially itself mediation and relation—not relation to an Other in general, as quality is as unreflected determinacy; but relation to itself as to an Other; or mediation that is immediately just as much identity with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"137.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0002","text":"The abstract Thing-in-itself is itself this conduct returning into itself out of an other; thereby it is determined in itself; but its determinacy is constitution, which as such is itself determination, and, as conduct toward an Other, does not pass over into otherness and is withdrawn from alteration.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"137.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0003","text":"A Thing has properties; first, they are its determinate relations to Others; property is present only as a mode of conduct toward one another; it is therefore external reflection, and the side of the Thing’s positedness. But secondly, the Thing is in itself in this positedness; it maintains itself in relation to Others; it is thus indeed only a surface through which existence gives itself over to the becoming of Being and to alteration; the property does not lose itself therein. A Thing has the property of effecting this or that in the Other and of manifesting itself in a peculiar manner in its relation. It proves this property only under the condition of a corresponding constitution of the other Thing, but it is at the same time peculiar to it and its basis identical with itself;—this reflected quality is therefore called property.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"137.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0004","text":"In this it passes over into an externality, but the property maintains itself therein. Through its properties the Thing becomes cause, and the cause is this: to maintain itself as effect. Yet here the Thing is as yet only the tranquil Thing of many properties; not yet determined as actual cause; it is as yet only the reflection of its determinations which is in itself, not yet itself the positing reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"137.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0005","text":"Thus, as has emerged, the Thing-in-itself is essentially not merely Thing-in-itself in such a way that its properties are the positedness of an external reflection, but they are its own determinations, through which it conducts itself in a determinate manner; it is not a indeterminate basis situated beyond its external existence; rather, it is present in its properties as ground, that is, as identity with itself in its positedness; but at the same time as conditioned ground; that is, its positedness is just as much reflection external to itself; it is reflected into itself and in itself only insofar as it is external.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"137.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0006","text":"—Through existence the Thing-in-itself enters into external relations; and existence consists in this externality; it is the immediacy of Being, and the Thing thereby subject to alteration; but it is also the reflected immediacy of ground, the Thing thus in itself in its alteration.—This mention of the ground-relation, however, is not to be understood here as meaning that the Thing is in general determined as the ground of its properties; thinghood itself as such is the determination of ground; property is not distinguished from its ground, nor does it merely constitute positedness, but is the ground that has passed over into its externality and thereby is truly reflected into itself; property itself as such is the ground, positedness that is in itself, or it constitutes the form of its identity with itself; its determinacy is the reflection external to itself of the","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"137.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0007","text":"ground; and the whole of the ground relating itself to itself in its repulsion and determination, in its external immediacy.—Thus the Thing-in-itself essentially exists, and that it exists means, conversely, that existence as external immediacy is at the same time being-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"137.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_2:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"0fde582e8722e8a5816d90294208d7d974f40ec548a447929803352fec05ac38","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Die Eigenschaft."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Die Eigenschaft.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37","title":"Remark.","order":138,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_37","text":"Es ist schon oben (1r Thl. 1e Abth. S. 127) bei dem Momente des Daseyns, dem Ansichseyn, des Dings-an-sich erwähnt, und dabei bemerkt worden, daß das Ding-an-sich als solches, nichts anderes, als die leere Abstraktion von aller Bestimmtheit ist, von dem man allerdings nichts wissen kann, eben darum weil es die Abstraktion von aller Bestimmung seyn soll.—Nachdem so das Ding-an-sich als das Unbestimmte vorausgesetzt wird, so fällt alle Bestimmung außerhalb desselben, in eine ihm fremde Reflexion, gegen welche es gleichgültig ist. Dem transcendentalen Idealismus ist diese äußerliche Reflexion das Bewußtseyn. Indem dieses philosophische System alle Bestimmtheit der Dinge sowohl der Form als dem Inhalte nach in das Bewußtseyn verlegt, so fällt es nach diesem Standpunkt in mich, in das Subjekt, daß ich die Baumblätter nicht als schwarz, sondern als grün, die Sonne rund und nicht viereckig sehe, den Zucker süß und nicht bitter schmecke; daß ich den ersten und zweiten Schlag einer Uhr als succedirend, und nicht neben einander, noch den ersten als Ursache, auch nicht als Wirkung des zweiten bestimme u.s.f.—Dieser grellen Darstellung des subjektiven Idealismus widerspricht unmittelbar das Bewußtseyn der Freyheit, nach welchem Ich mich vielmehr als das Allgemeine und Unbestimmte weiß, jene mannigfaltigen und nothwendigen Bestimmungen von mir abtrenne und sie als ein für mich Äußerliches nur den Dingen Zukommendes erkenne.—Ich ist in diesem Bewußtseyn seiner Freyheit sich diejenige wahrhafte in sich reflektirte Identität, welche das Ding-an-sich seyn sollte.—Anderwärts habe ich gezeigt, daß jener transcendentale Idealismus über die Beschränktheit des Ich durch das Object, überhaupt über die endliche Welt nicht hinauskommt, sondern allein die Form der Schranke, die ihm ein Absolutes bleibt, ändert, indem er sie nämlich nur aus der objektiven Gestalt in die Subjektive übersezt, und dasjenige zu Bestimmtheiten des Ich und einem in diesem als einem Dinge vorgehenden wilden Wechsel derselben macht, was das gewöhnliche Bewußtseyn als eine ihm nur äußerlichen Dingen angehörige Mannigfaltigkeit und Veränderung weiß.—In der gegenwärtigen Betrachtung steht nur das Ding-an-sich und die ihm zunächst äußerliche Reflexion gegenüber; diese hat sich noch nicht als Bewußtseyn bestimmt, wie auch das Ding-an-sich nicht als Ich. Aus der Natur des Dinges-an-sich und der äußerlichen Reflexion hat sich ergeben, daß dieses Äußerliche selbst sich zum Dinge-an-sich bestimmt, oder umgekehrt zur eigenen Bestimmung jenes ersten Dinges-an-sich wird. Das Wesentliche der Unzulänglichkeit des Standpunkts, auf dem jene Philosophie stehen bleibt, besteht nun darin, daß sie an dem abstrakten Dinge-an-sich als einer letzten Bestimmung fest hält und die Reflexion, oder die Bestimmtheit und Mannigfaltigkeit der Eigenschaften dem Dinge-an-sich gegenüber stellt, indem in der That das Ding-an-sich wesentlich jene äußerliche Reflexion an ihm selbst hat, und sich zu einem mit eigenen Bestimmungen, mit Eigenschaften begabten bestimmt, wodurch sich die Abstraktion des Dinges, reines Ding-an-sich zu seyn, als eine unwahre Bestimmung erweist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0001","text":"Es ist schon oben (1r Thl. 1e Abth. S. 127) bei dem Momente des Daseyns, dem Ansichseyn, des Dings-an-sich erwähnt, und dabei bemerkt worden, daß das Ding-an-sich als solches, nichts anderes, als die leere Abstraktion von aller Bestimmtheit ist, von dem man allerdings nichts wissen kann, eben darum weil es die Abstraktion von aller Bestimmung seyn soll.—Nachdem so das Ding-an-sich als das Unbestimmte vorausgesetzt wird, so fällt alle Bestimmung außerhalb desselben, in eine ihm fremde Reflexion, gegen welche es gleichgültig ist. Dem transcendentalen Idealismus ist diese äußerliche Reflexion das Bewußtseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"138.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0002","text":"Indem dieses philosophische System alle Bestimmtheit der Dinge sowohl der Form als dem Inhalte nach in das Bewußtseyn verlegt, so fällt es nach diesem Standpunkt in mich, in das Subjekt, daß ich die Baumblätter nicht als schwarz, sondern als grün, die Sonne rund und nicht viereckig sehe, den Zucker süß und nicht bitter schmecke; daß ich den ersten und zweiten Schlag einer Uhr als succedirend, und nicht neben einander, noch den ersten als Ursache, auch nicht als Wirkung des zweiten bestimme u.s.f.—Dieser grellen Darstellung des subjektiven Idealismus widerspricht unmittelbar das Bewußtseyn der Freyheit, nach welchem Ich mich vielmehr als das Allgemeine und Unbestimmte weiß, jene mannigfaltigen und nothwendigen Bestimmungen von mir abtrenne und sie als ein für mich Äußerliches nur den Dingen Zukommendes erkenne.—Ich ist in diesem Bewußtseyn seiner Freyheit sich diejenige wahrhafte in sich","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"138.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0003","text":"reflektirte Identität, welche das Ding-an-sich seyn sollte.—Anderwärts habe ich gezeigt, daß jener transcendentale Idealismus über die Beschränktheit des Ich durch das Object, überhaupt über die endliche Welt nicht hinauskommt, sondern allein die Form der Schranke, die ihm ein Absolutes bleibt, ändert, indem er sie nämlich nur aus der objektiven Gestalt in die Subjektive übersezt, und dasjenige zu Bestimmtheiten des Ich und einem in diesem als einem Dinge vorgehenden wilden Wechsel derselben macht, was das gewöhnliche Bewußtseyn als eine ihm nur äußerlichen Dingen angehörige Mannigfaltigkeit und Veränderung weiß.—In der gegenwärtigen Betrachtung steht nur das Ding-an-sich und die ihm zunächst äußerliche Reflexion gegenüber; diese hat sich noch nicht als Bewußtseyn bestimmt, wie auch das Ding-an-sich nicht als Ich.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"138.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0004","text":"Aus der Natur des Dinges-an-sich und der äußerlichen Reflexion hat sich ergeben, daß dieses Äußerliche selbst sich zum Dinge-an-sich bestimmt, oder umgekehrt zur eigenen Bestimmung jenes ersten Dinges-an-sich wird. Das Wesentliche der Unzulänglichkeit des Standpunkts, auf dem jene Philosophie stehen bleibt, besteht nun darin, daß sie an dem abstrakten Dinge-an-sich als einer letzten Bestimmung fest hält und die Reflexion, oder die Bestimmtheit und Mannigfaltigkeit der Eigenschaften dem Dinge-an-sich gegenüber stellt, indem in der That das Ding-an-sich wesentlich jene äußerliche Reflexion an ihm selbst hat, und sich zu einem mit eigenen Bestimmungen, mit Eigenschaften begabten bestimmt, wodurch sich die Abstraktion des Dinges, reines Ding-an-sich zu seyn, als eine unwahre Bestimmung erweist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"138.4"}],"sha256":"abfd58ac8cad5e49825debab82fd176d5747975e165b9a6b2d187eecb72748dd","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105428569836Z_8ef3aaf1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"abfd58ac8cad5e49825debab82fd176d5747975e165b9a6b2d187eecb72748dd","sha256":"535467d2d614423a869a68414423b1c7cad16e2443be773545512153d4c29d82","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:54:28.569854+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0001","text":"It has already been mentioned above (Part 1, Division 1, p. 127) in connection with the moment of existence, being-in-itself, of the thing-in-itself, and it was observed that the thing-in-itself as such is nothing other than the empty abstraction from all determinacy, of which indeed nothing can be known, precisely because it is supposed to be the abstraction from all determination.—Since the thing-in-itself is thus presupposed as the indeterminate, all determination falls outside it, into a reflection alien to it, toward which it is indifferent. For transcendental idealism, this external reflection is consciousness.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"138.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_37:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0002","text":"Since this philosophical system places all determinacy of things, both as to form and as to content, in consciousness, it follows, from this standpoint, that it lies in me, in the subject, that I see the leaves of trees not as black but as green, the sun as round and not square, taste sugar as sweet and not bitter; that I determine the first and second strokes of a clock as successive, and not as alongside one another, nor the first as the cause, nor as the effect, of the second, etc.—This glaring presentation of subjective idealism is directly contradicted by consciousness of freedom, according to which I rather know myself as the universal and indeterminate, separate those manifold and necessary determinations from myself, and recognize them as something external to me, belonging only to things.—In this consciousness of its freedom, the I is that true identity reflected within itself which the thing-in-itself was supposed to be.—Elsewhere I have shown that that transcendental idealism does not get beyond the limitation of the I by the object, or indeed beyond the finite world, but merely alters the form of the limitation, which remains an Absolute for it, by transferring it only from objective shape into subjective shape, and making into determinations of the I and into a wild alternation of these occurring in it as in a thing, what ordinary consciousness knows as a manifoldness and alteration belonging only to things external to it.—In the present consideration, only the thing-in-itself and reflection initially external to it stand opposed to one another; the latter has not yet determined itself as consciousness, just as the thing-in-itself has not determined itself as I.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"138.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_37:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0003","text":"reflected identity, which the thing-in-itself was supposed to be.—Elsewhere I have shown that that transcendental idealism does not get beyond the limitation of the I by the object, or indeed beyond the finite world, but merely alters the form of the limitation, which remains an Absolute for it, by transferring it only from objective shape into subjective shape, and making into determinations of the I and into a wild alternation of these occurring in it as in a thing, what ordinary consciousness knows as a manifoldness and alteration belonging only to things external to it.—In the present consideration, only the thing-in-itself and reflection initially external to it stand opposed to one another; the latter has not yet determined itself as consciousness, just as the thing-in-itself has not determined itself as I.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"138.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_37:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_37:P0004","text":"From the nature of the thing-in-itself and of external reflection, it has emerged that this externality itself determines itself as the thing-in-itself, or conversely becomes the proper determination of that first thing-in-itself. Now, the essential inadequacy of the standpoint at which that philosophy remains consists in its holding fast to the abstract thing-in-itself as a final determination and setting reflection, or the determinacy and manifoldness of properties, over against the thing-in-itself; whereas in fact the thing-in-itself essentially has that external reflection within itself and determines itself as endowed with its own determinations, with properties, whereby the abstraction of the thing, of being a pure thing-in-itself, proves itself to be an untrue determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"138.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_37:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"5c903796f419bb9d467986af4404cdaf2a516b4ee981add18830bde3a5e8f2e5","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD","title":"c. The Reciprocal Action of Things.","order":139,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDWD","text":"Das Ding-an-sich existirt wesentlich; die äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit und die Bestimmtheit gehört zu seinem Ansichseyn, oder zu seiner Reflexion-in-sich. Das Ding an-sich ist dadurch ein Ding, das Eigenschaften hat, und es sind dadurch mehrere Dinge, die nicht durch eine ihnen fremde Rücksicht, sondern sich durch sich selbst von einander unterscheiden. Diese mehrern verschiedenen Dinge stehen in wesentlicher Wechselwirkung durch ihre Eigenschaften; die Eigenschaft ist diese Wechselbeziehung selbst, und das Ding ist nichts außer derselben; die gegenseitige Bestimmung, die Mitte der Dinge-an-sich, die als Extreme gleichgültig gegen diese ihre Beziehung bleiben sollten, ist selbst die mit sich identische Reflexion und das Ding-an-sich, das jene Extreme seyn sollten. Die Dingheit ist damit zur Form der unbestimmten Identität mit sich herabgesetzt, die ihre Wesentlichkeit nur in ihrer Eigenschaft hat. Wenn daher von einem Dinge oder von Dingen überhaupt ohne die bestimmte Eigenschaft die Rede ist, so ist ihr Unterschied ein bloß gleichgültiger, quantitativer. Dasselbe, was als ein Ding betrachtet wird, kann ebenso sehr zu mehrern Dingen gemacht, oder als mehrere Dinge betrachtet werden; es ist eine äußerliche Trennung oder Vereinigung. —Ein Buch ist ein Ding, und jedes seiner Blätter ist auch ein Ding, und ebenso jedes Stükchen seiner Blätter und so fort ins Unendliche. Die Bestimmtheit, wodurch ein Ding, nur dieses Ding ist, liegt allein in seinen Eigenschaften. Es unterscheidet sich durch sie von andern Dingen, weil die Eigenschaft die negative Reflexion und das Unterscheiden ist; das Ding hat daher nur in seiner Eigenschaft den Unterschied seiner von andern, an ihm selbst. Sie ist der in sich reflektirte Unterschied, wodurch das Ding in seinem Gesetztseyn, d. h. in seiner Beziehung auf Anderes zugleich gleichgültig gegen das Andere und gegen seine Beziehung ist. Dem Dinge ohne seine Eigenschaften, bleibt deswegen nichts als das abstrakte An-sich-seyn, ein unwesentlicher Umfang und äußerliches Zusammenfassen. Das wahrhafte Ansichseyn ist das Ansichseyn in seinem Gesetztseyn; dieses ist die Eigenschaft.\n\nDamit ist die Dingheit in die Eigenschaft übergegangen.\n\nDas Ding sollte sich als an-sich-seyendes Extrem gegen die Eigenschaft verhalten und diese die Mitte zwischen den in Beziehung stehenden Dingen ausmachen. Allein diese Beziehung ist das, worin die Dinge sich als die sich von sich selbst abstoßende Reflexion begegnen, worin sie unterschieden und bezogen sind. Dieser ihr Unterschied und ihre Beziehung, ist Eine Reflexion und Eine Kontinuität derselben. Die Dinge selbst fallen hiermit nur in diese Kontinuität, welche die Eigenschaft ist, und verschwinden als bestehende Extreme, die außer dieser Eigenschaft eine Existenz hätten.\n\nDie Eigenschaft, welche die Beziehung der selbstständigen Extreme ausmachen sollte, ist daher das Selbstständige selbst. Die Dinge dagegen sind das Unwesentliche. Sie sind ein Wesentliches nur als die, als sich unterscheidend sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion; aber dieß ist die Eigenschaft. Diese ist also nicht das im Dinge aufgehobene, oder sein bloßes Moment; sondern das Ding ist in Wahrheit nur jener unwesentliche Umfang, der zwar negative Einheit ist, aber nur wie das Eins des Etwas, nämlich ein unmittelbares Eins. Wenn vorhin das Ding als unwesentlicher Umfang insofern bestimmt wurde, als es durch eine äußerliche Abstraktion, welche die Eigenschaft von demselben wegläßt, dazu gemacht werde, so ist nunmehr diese Abstraktion durch das Übergehen des Dings-an-sich in die Eigenschaft selbst geschehen, aber mit umgekehrtem Werthe, so daß wenn jenem Abstrahiren das abstrakte Ding ohne seine Eigenschaft noch als das Wesentliche, die Eigenschaft aber als eine äußerliche Bestimmung vorschwebt, hier das Ding als solches sich durch sich selbst zu einer gleichgültigen äußerlichen Form der Eigenschaft bestimmt.—Diese ist somit nunmehr befreit von der unbestimmten und kraftlosen Verbindung, die das Eins des Dinges ist; sie ist das, was das Bestehen desselben ausmacht; eine selbstständige Materie.—Indem sie einfache Kontinuität mit sich ist, hat sie die Form zunächst nur als Verschiedenheit an ihr; es giebt daher mannigfaltige dergleichen selbstständige Materien und das Ding besteht aus ihnen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0001","text":"Das Ding-an-sich existirt wesentlich; die äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit und die Bestimmtheit gehört zu seinem Ansichseyn, oder zu seiner Reflexion-in-sich. Das Ding an-sich ist dadurch ein Ding, das Eigenschaften hat, und es sind dadurch mehrere Dinge, die nicht durch eine ihnen fremde Rücksicht, sondern sich durch sich selbst von einander unterscheiden. Diese mehrern verschiedenen Dinge stehen in wesentlicher Wechselwirkung durch ihre Eigenschaften; die Eigenschaft ist diese Wechselbeziehung selbst, und das Ding ist nichts außer derselben; die gegenseitige Bestimmung, die Mitte der Dinge-an-sich, die als Extreme gleichgültig gegen diese ihre Beziehung bleiben sollten, ist selbst die mit sich identische Reflexion und das Ding-an-sich, das jene Extreme seyn sollten.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"139.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0002","text":"Die Dingheit ist damit zur Form der unbestimmten Identität mit sich herabgesetzt, die ihre Wesentlichkeit nur in ihrer Eigenschaft hat. Wenn daher von einem Dinge oder von Dingen überhaupt ohne die bestimmte Eigenschaft die Rede ist, so ist ihr Unterschied ein bloß gleichgültiger, quantitativer. Dasselbe, was als ein Ding betrachtet wird, kann ebenso sehr zu mehrern Dingen gemacht, oder als mehrere Dinge betrachtet werden; es ist eine äußerliche Trennung oder Vereinigung. —Ein Buch ist ein Ding, und jedes seiner Blätter ist auch ein Ding, und ebenso jedes Stükchen seiner Blätter und so fort ins Unendliche. Die Bestimmtheit, wodurch ein Ding, nur dieses Ding ist, liegt allein in seinen Eigenschaften.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"139.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0003","text":"Es unterscheidet sich durch sie von andern Dingen, weil die Eigenschaft die negative Reflexion und das Unterscheiden ist; das Ding hat daher nur in seiner Eigenschaft den Unterschied seiner von andern, an ihm selbst. Sie ist der in sich reflektirte Unterschied, wodurch das Ding in seinem Gesetztseyn, d. h. in seiner Beziehung auf Anderes zugleich gleichgültig gegen das Andere und gegen seine Beziehung ist. Dem Dinge ohne seine Eigenschaften, bleibt deswegen nichts als das abstrakte An-sich-seyn, ein unwesentlicher Umfang und äußerliches Zusammenfassen. Das wahrhafte Ansichseyn ist das Ansichseyn in seinem Gesetztseyn; dieses ist die Eigenschaft.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"139.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0004","text":"Damit ist die Dingheit in die Eigenschaft übergegangen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"139.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0005","text":"Das Ding sollte sich als an-sich-seyendes Extrem gegen die Eigenschaft verhalten und diese die Mitte zwischen den in Beziehung stehenden Dingen ausmachen. Allein diese Beziehung ist das, worin die Dinge sich als die sich von sich selbst abstoßende Reflexion begegnen, worin sie unterschieden und bezogen sind. Dieser ihr Unterschied und ihre Beziehung, ist Eine Reflexion und Eine Kontinuität derselben. Die Dinge selbst fallen hiermit nur in diese Kontinuität, welche die Eigenschaft ist, und verschwinden als bestehende Extreme, die außer dieser Eigenschaft eine Existenz hätten.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"139.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0006","text":"Die Eigenschaft, welche die Beziehung der selbstständigen Extreme ausmachen sollte, ist daher das Selbstständige selbst. Die Dinge dagegen sind das Unwesentliche. Sie sind ein Wesentliches nur als die, als sich unterscheidend sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion; aber dieß ist die Eigenschaft. Diese ist also nicht das im Dinge aufgehobene, oder sein bloßes Moment; sondern das Ding ist in Wahrheit nur jener unwesentliche Umfang, der zwar negative Einheit ist, aber nur wie das Eins des Etwas, nämlich ein unmittelbares Eins.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"139.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0007","text":"Wenn vorhin das Ding als unwesentlicher Umfang insofern bestimmt wurde, als es durch eine äußerliche Abstraktion, welche die Eigenschaft von demselben wegläßt, dazu gemacht werde, so ist nunmehr diese Abstraktion durch das Übergehen des Dings-an-sich in die Eigenschaft selbst geschehen, aber mit umgekehrtem Werthe, so daß wenn jenem Abstrahiren das abstrakte Ding ohne seine Eigenschaft noch als das Wesentliche, die Eigenschaft aber als eine äußerliche Bestimmung vorschwebt, hier das Ding als solches sich durch sich selbst zu einer gleichgültigen äußerlichen Form der Eigenschaft bestimmt.—Diese ist somit nunmehr befreit von der unbestimmten und kraftlosen Verbindung, die das Eins des Dinges ist; sie ist das, was das Bestehen desselben ausmacht; eine selbstständige Materie.—Indem sie einfache Kontinuität mit sich ist, hat sie die Form zunächst nur als Verschiedenheit an ihr; es giebt","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"139.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0008","text":"daher mannigfaltige dergleichen selbstständige Materien und das Ding besteht aus ihnen.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"139.8"}],"sha256":"a10e3a3ce66020ad620a2599496279d2f6db55885b0d707642f2f6177ae2cfb6","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105437783225Z_8b08e208","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Reciprocal Action of Things.","source_sha256":"a10e3a3ce66020ad620a2599496279d2f6db55885b0d707642f2f6177ae2cfb6","sha256":"628811bc4078d3d4955959a096cf4d91e7435756609238eb8b6e657ee8aeafcf","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:54:37.783247+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0001","text":"The thing-in-itself exists essentially; external immediacy and determinateness belong to its being-in-itself, or to its reflection-into-itself. The thing-in-itself is thereby a thing that has properties, and there are thereby several things which are distinguished from one another not by a respect foreign to them, but through themselves. These several different things stand in essential reciprocal interaction through their properties; the property is this reciprocal relation itself, and the thing is nothing apart from it; the reciprocal determination, the middle of the things-in-themselves, which as extremes were supposed to remain indifferent to this their relation, is itself the reflection identical with itself and the thing-in-itself which those extremes were supposed to be.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"139.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0002","text":"Thinghood is thereby reduced to the form of indeterminate identity with itself, which has its essentiality only in its property. Thus, when there is talk of a thing or of things in general without the determinate property, their difference is merely an indifferent, quantitative one. The same thing which is regarded as one thing can just as well be made into several things, or regarded as several things; it is an external separation or combination. —A book is a thing, and each of its leaves is likewise a thing, and so too every little piece of its leaves, and so on to infinity. The determinateness whereby a thing is only this thing lies solely in its properties.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"139.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0003","text":"Through them it is distinguished from other things, because property is negative reflection and distinguishing; the thing therefore has only in its property its distinction from others, in itself. It is the difference reflected into itself, whereby the thing, in its positedness, i.e. in its relation to an Other, is at the same time indifferent toward the Other and toward its relation. To the thing without its properties, therefore, there remains nothing but abstract being-in-itself, an inessential circumference and external comprehending. True being-in-itself is being-in-itself in its positedness; this is property.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"139.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0004","text":"Thereby thinghood has passed over into property.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"139.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0005","text":"The thing was supposed to comport itself as an extreme existing-in-itself over against property, and the latter was supposed to constitute the middle between the things standing in relation. But this relation is that in which the things encounter one another as reflection repelling itself from itself, in which they are distinguished and related. This their distinction and their relation is one reflection and one continuity of the same. The things themselves thereby fall only into this continuity, which is property, and vanish as subsisting extremes that would have an existence outside this property.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"139.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0006","text":"The property which was supposed to constitute the relation of the self-subsistent extremes is therefore self-subsistence itself. The things, on the other hand, are the inessential. They are an essential only as reflection relating itself to itself as distinguishing itself; but this is property. Thus it is not what is sublated in the thing, or its mere moment; rather, the thing is in truth only that inessential circumference, which is indeed negative unity, but only like the One of the Something, namely, an immediate One.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"139.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0007","text":"If previously the thing was determined as an inessential circumference insofar as it was made into this by an external abstraction which leaves aside the property from it, now this abstraction has occurred through the transition of the thing-in-itself into property itself, but with inverted value, so that whereas in that abstracting the abstract thing without its property still presented itself as the essential, but property as an external determination, here the thing as such determines itself through itself into an indifferent external form of property.—The latter is thus now freed from the indeterminate and powerless connection which is the One of the thing; it is that which constitutes its subsistence; a self-subsistent matter.—Inasmuch as it is simple continuity with itself, it has form at first only as difference within itself; there are","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"139.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0008","text":"therefore manifold such self-subsistent matters, and the thing consists of them.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"139.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDWD:P0008"]}],"source_digest":"8c4af38ca4fe34fd76bebca958efa958e720e74bf85fd06abb72664724b5b45d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die Wechselwirkung der Dinge."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die Wechselwirkung der Dinge.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD","title":"B. The Subsistence of the Thing in Matters.","order":140,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDBD","text":"Der Übergang der Eigenschaft in eine Materie oder in einen selbstständigen Stoff ist der bekannte Übergang, den an der sinnlichen Materie die Chemie macht, indem sie die Eigenschaften der Farbe, des Geruchs, des Geschmacks u.s.f. als Lichtstoff, Färbestoff, Riechstoff, sauren, bittern u.s.f. Stoff darzustellen sucht oder andere wie den Wärmestoff, die elektrische, magnetische Materie geradezu nur annimmt, und damit die Eigenschaften in ihrer Wahrhaftigkeit zu handhaben überzeugt ist.—Ebenso geläufig ist der Ausdruck, daß die Dinge aus verschiedenen Materien oder Stoffen bestehen. Man hütet sich, diese Materien oder Stoffe Dinge zu nennen; ob man wohl auch einräumen wird, daß z.B. ein Pigment, ein Ding ist; ich weiß aber nicht, ob z.B. auch der Lichtstoff, der Wärmestoff, oder die elektrische Materie u.s.f. Dinge genannt werden. Man unterscheidet die Dinge und ihre Bestandtheile, ohne genau anzugeben, ob diese und in wie weit sie auch Dinge, oder etwa nur Halbdinge seyen; aber Existirende überhaupt sind sie wenigstens.\n\nDie Nothwendigkeit, von den Eigenschaften zu Materien überzugehen, oder daß die Eigenschaften in Wahrheit Materien sind, hat sich daraus ergeben, daß sie das Wesentliche und damit das wahrhaft Selbstständige der Dinge sind.—Zugleich aber macht die Reflexion der Eigenschaft in sich nur die eine Seite der ganzen Reflexion aus; nämlich das Aufheben des Unterschieds und die Kontinuität der Eigenschaft, die eine Existenz für Anderes seyn sollte, mit sich selbst. Die Dingheit, als die negative Reflexion in sich, und das sich von Anderem abstoßende Unterscheiden ist dadurch zu einem unwesentlichen Momente herabgesetzt; zugleich aber hat es sich damit weiter bestimmt. Dieß negative Moment hat sich erstens erhalten; denn die Eigenschaft ist nur insofern mit sich kontinuirlich und selbstständige Materie geworden, als sich der Unterschied der Dinge aufgehoben hat; die Kontinuität der Eigenschaft in das Andersseyn enthält also selbst das Moment des Negativen, und ihre Selbstständigkeit ist zugleich als diese negative Einheit das wiederhergestellte Etwas der Dingheit; die negative Selbstständigkeit gegen die positive des Stoffes. Zweitens ist hierdurch das Ding aus seiner Unbestimmtheit zur vollkommenen Bestimmtheit gediehen. Als Ding an sich ist es die abstrakte Identität, die einfach negative Existenz, oder sie bestimmt als das Unbestimmte; alsdann ist es bestimmt durch seine Eigenschaften, durch welche es sich von andern unterscheiden soll; aber indem es durch die Eigenschaft vielmehr kontinuirlich mit andern ist, so hebt sich dieser unvollkommene Unterschied auf; das Ding ist dadurch in sich zurückgegangen und nun bestimmt als bestimmt; es ist an sich bestimmt oder dieses Ding.-Aber drittens ist diese Rückkehr in sich zwar die sich auf sich beziehende Bestimmung; aber sie ist zugleich unwesentlich; das mit sich kontinuirliche Bestehen macht die selbstständige Materie aus, in welcher der Unterschied der Dinge, ihre an und für sich seyende Bestimmtheit aufgehoben und ein Äußerliches ist. Das Ding als dieses ist also zwar vollkommene Bestimmtheit, aber es ist dieß die Bestimmtheit im Elemente der Unwesentlichkeit.\n\nDieß von Seite der Bewegung der Eigenschaft aus betrachtet, ergiebt sich so. Die Eigenschaft ist nicht nur äußerliche Bestimmung, sondern an sich seyende Existenz. Diese Einheit der Äußerlichkeit und Wesentlichkeit stößt sich, weil sie die Reflexion-in-sich und die Reflexion in Anderes enthält, von sich selbst ab, und ist einer Seits die Bestimmung als einfaches sich identisch auf sich beziehendes Selbstständiges, in welchem die negative Einheit, das Eins des Dinges ein Aufgehobenes ist;—anderer Seits diese Bestimmung gegen Anderes, aber ebenfalls als in sich reflektirtes an sich bestimmtes Eins; die Materien also, und dieses Ding. Dieß sind die zwei Momente der mit sich identischen Äußerlichkeit, oder der in sich reflektirten Eigenschaft.—Die Eigenschaft war das, wodurch sich die Dinge unterscheiden sollten; indem sie sich von dieser ihrer negativen Seite, einem andern zu inhäriren, befreit hat, so ist damit auch das Ding von seinem Bestimmtseyn durch andere Dinge befreit worden, und aus der Beziehung auf Anderes, in sich zurückgegangen; aber es ist zugleich nur das sich anderes gewordene Ding-an-sich; weil die mannigfaltigen Eigenschaften ihrer Seits selbstständig, hierin also ihre negative Beziehung in dem Eins des Dinges nur eine aufgehobene geworden ist; es ist darum die mit sich identische Negation nur gegen die positive Kontinuität des Stoffes.\n\nDas Diese macht also so die vollkommene Bestimmtheit des Dinges aus, daß sie zugleich eine äußerliche ist. Das Ding besteht aus selbstständigen Materien, die gegen ihre Beziehung im Dinge gleichgültig sind. Diese Beziehung ist daher nur eine unwesentliche Verknüpfung derselben, und der Unterschied eines Dinges von anderen beruht darauf, ob mehrere der besondern Materien und in welcher Menge sie sich in ihm befinden. Sie gehen über dieses Ding hinaus, kontinuiren sich in andere, und diesem Dinge anzugehören, ist keine Schranke derselben. Ebenso wenig sind sie ferner eine Beschränkung für einander, weil ihre negative Beziehung nur das kraftlose Diese ist. Sie heben sich daher, indem sie in ihm verbunden werden, nicht auf; sie sind als Selbstständige undurchdringlich für einander; beziehen sich in ihrer Bestimmtheit nur auf sich, und sind eine gegen einander gleichgültige Mannigfaltigkeit des Bestehens; sie sind nur einer quantitativen Grenze fähig.—Das Ding als dieses ist diese ihre bloß quantitative Beziehung, eine bloße Sammlung, das Auch derselben. Es besteht aus irgend einem Quantum von einem Stoffe, auch aus dem eines andern, auch andern; diesen Zusammenhang, keinen Zusammenhang zu haben, macht allein das Ding aus.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0001","text":"Der Übergang der Eigenschaft in eine Materie oder in einen selbstständigen Stoff ist der bekannte Übergang, den an der sinnlichen Materie die Chemie macht, indem sie die Eigenschaften der Farbe, des Geruchs, des Geschmacks u.s.f. als Lichtstoff, Färbestoff, Riechstoff, sauren, bittern u.s.f. Stoff darzustellen sucht oder andere wie den Wärmestoff, die elektrische, magnetische Materie geradezu nur annimmt, und damit die Eigenschaften in ihrer Wahrhaftigkeit zu handhaben überzeugt ist.—Ebenso geläufig ist der Ausdruck, daß die Dinge aus verschiedenen Materien oder Stoffen bestehen. Man hütet sich, diese Materien oder Stoffe Dinge zu nennen; ob man wohl auch einräumen wird, daß z.B. ein Pigment, ein Ding ist; ich weiß aber nicht, ob z.B. auch der Lichtstoff, der Wärmestoff, oder die elektrische Materie u.s.f. Dinge genannt werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"140.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0002","text":"Man unterscheidet die Dinge und ihre Bestandtheile, ohne genau anzugeben, ob diese und in wie weit sie auch Dinge, oder etwa nur Halbdinge seyen; aber Existirende überhaupt sind sie wenigstens.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"140.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0003","text":"Die Nothwendigkeit, von den Eigenschaften zu Materien überzugehen, oder daß die Eigenschaften in Wahrheit Materien sind, hat sich daraus ergeben, daß sie das Wesentliche und damit das wahrhaft Selbstständige der Dinge sind.—Zugleich aber macht die Reflexion der Eigenschaft in sich nur die eine Seite der ganzen Reflexion aus; nämlich das Aufheben des Unterschieds und die Kontinuität der Eigenschaft, die eine Existenz für Anderes seyn sollte, mit sich selbst. Die Dingheit, als die negative Reflexion in sich, und das sich von Anderem abstoßende Unterscheiden ist dadurch zu einem unwesentlichen Momente herabgesetzt; zugleich aber hat es sich damit weiter bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"140.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0004","text":"Dieß negative Moment hat sich erstens erhalten; denn die Eigenschaft ist nur insofern mit sich kontinuirlich und selbstständige Materie geworden, als sich der Unterschied der Dinge aufgehoben hat; die Kontinuität der Eigenschaft in das Andersseyn enthält also selbst das Moment des Negativen, und ihre Selbstständigkeit ist zugleich als diese negative Einheit das wiederhergestellte Etwas der Dingheit; die negative Selbstständigkeit gegen die positive des Stoffes. Zweitens ist hierdurch das Ding aus seiner Unbestimmtheit zur vollkommenen Bestimmtheit gediehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"140.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0005","text":"Als Ding an sich ist es die abstrakte Identität, die einfach negative Existenz, oder sie bestimmt als das Unbestimmte; alsdann ist es bestimmt durch seine Eigenschaften, durch welche es sich von andern unterscheiden soll; aber indem es durch die Eigenschaft vielmehr kontinuirlich mit andern ist, so hebt sich dieser unvollkommene Unterschied auf; das Ding ist dadurch in sich zurückgegangen und nun bestimmt als bestimmt; es ist an sich bestimmt oder dieses Ding.-Aber drittens ist diese Rückkehr in sich zwar die sich auf sich beziehende Bestimmung; aber sie ist zugleich unwesentlich; das mit sich kontinuirliche Bestehen macht die selbstständige Materie aus, in welcher der Unterschied der Dinge, ihre an und für sich seyende Bestimmtheit aufgehoben und ein Äußerliches ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"140.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0006","text":"Das Ding als dieses ist also zwar vollkommene Bestimmtheit, aber es ist dieß die Bestimmtheit im Elemente der Unwesentlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"140.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0007","text":"Dieß von Seite der Bewegung der Eigenschaft aus betrachtet, ergiebt sich so. Die Eigenschaft ist nicht nur äußerliche Bestimmung, sondern an sich seyende Existenz. Diese Einheit der Äußerlichkeit und Wesentlichkeit stößt sich, weil sie die Reflexion-in-sich und die Reflexion in Anderes enthält, von sich selbst ab, und ist einer Seits die Bestimmung als einfaches sich identisch auf sich beziehendes Selbstständiges, in welchem die negative Einheit, das Eins des Dinges ein Aufgehobenes ist;—anderer Seits diese Bestimmung gegen Anderes, aber ebenfalls als in sich reflektirtes an sich bestimmtes Eins; die Materien also, und dieses Ding.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"140.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0008","text":"Dieß sind die zwei Momente der mit sich identischen Äußerlichkeit, oder der in sich reflektirten Eigenschaft.—Die Eigenschaft war das, wodurch sich die Dinge unterscheiden sollten; indem sie sich von dieser ihrer negativen Seite, einem andern zu inhäriren, befreit hat, so ist damit auch das Ding von seinem Bestimmtseyn durch andere Dinge befreit worden, und aus der Beziehung auf Anderes, in sich zurückgegangen; aber es ist zugleich nur das sich anderes gewordene Ding-an-sich; weil die mannigfaltigen Eigenschaften ihrer Seits selbstständig, hierin also ihre negative Beziehung in dem Eins des Dinges nur eine aufgehobene geworden ist; es ist darum die mit sich identische Negation nur gegen die positive Kontinuität des Stoffes.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"140.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0009","text":"Das Diese macht also so die vollkommene Bestimmtheit des Dinges aus, daß sie zugleich eine äußerliche ist. Das Ding besteht aus selbstständigen Materien, die gegen ihre Beziehung im Dinge gleichgültig sind. Diese Beziehung ist daher nur eine unwesentliche Verknüpfung derselben, und der Unterschied eines Dinges von anderen beruht darauf, ob mehrere der besondern Materien und in welcher Menge sie sich in ihm befinden. Sie gehen über dieses Ding hinaus, kontinuiren sich in andere, und diesem Dinge anzugehören, ist keine Schranke derselben. Ebenso wenig sind sie ferner eine Beschränkung für einander, weil ihre negative Beziehung nur das kraftlose Diese ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"140.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0010","text":"Sie heben sich daher, indem sie in ihm verbunden werden, nicht auf; sie sind als Selbstständige undurchdringlich für einander; beziehen sich in ihrer Bestimmtheit nur auf sich, und sind eine gegen einander gleichgültige Mannigfaltigkeit des Bestehens; sie sind nur einer quantitativen Grenze fähig.—Das Ding als dieses ist diese ihre bloß quantitative Beziehung, eine bloße Sammlung, das Auch derselben. Es besteht aus irgend einem Quantum von einem Stoffe, auch aus dem eines andern, auch andern; diesen Zusammenhang, keinen Zusammenhang zu haben, macht allein das Ding aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"140.10"}],"sha256":"1270f841a3997382116515f853e0e70e6c47686b2a4ed262d617816e78a8b941","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105453666157Z_a9a5438b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. The Subsistence of the Thing in Matters.","source_sha256":"1270f841a3997382116515f853e0e70e6c47686b2a4ed262d617816e78a8b941","sha256":"0ffda54f61a92ebc7a96f745652da461311454701aa5235712cd7990abf70330","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:54:53.666188+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0001","text":"The transition of property into a matter or into a self-subsistent material is the familiar transition which chemistry makes in the case of sensuous matter, in that it seeks to represent the properties of colour, smell, taste, etc. as luminous matter, colouring matter, odoriferous matter, acid, bitter, etc. material, or simply assumes others, such as caloric matter, electrical and magnetic matter, and thereby is convinced that it handles the properties in their truth.—Equally familiar is the expression that things consist of various matters or materials. One is cautious not to call these matters or materials things; although one will also concede that, for example, a pigment is a thing; but I do not know whether, for example, luminous matter, caloric matter, or electrical matter, etc. are also called things.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"140.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0002","text":"One distinguishes things and their constituent parts, without stating precisely whether these too, and to what extent, are things, or perhaps only half-things; but at least they are existents in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"140.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0003","text":"The necessity of passing from properties to matters, or that properties are in truth matters, has resulted from the fact that they are the essential and thereby the truly self-subsistent element of things.—At the same time, however, the reflection of property into itself constitutes only the one side of the whole reflection; namely, the sublation of distinction and the continuity of property, which was supposed to be a being-for-other, with itself. Thinghood, as negative reflection into itself, and the distinguishing which repels itself from other, is thereby reduced to an unessential moment; but at the same time it has thereby been further determined.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"140.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0004","text":"This negative moment has, firstly, preserved itself; for property has become continuous with itself and self-subsistent matter only insofar as the distinction of things has sublated itself; the continuity of property into otherness thus itself contains the moment of the negative, and its self-subsistence is at the same time, as this negative unity, the restored something of thinghood; negative self-subsistence as against the positive self-subsistence of material. Secondly, the thing has thereby advanced from its indeterminacy to complete determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"140.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0005","text":"As a thing in itself, it is abstract identity, simple negative existence, or, determined as such, the indeterminate; it is then determined by its properties, through which it is supposed to distinguish itself from others; but since through property it is instead continuous with others, this imperfect distinction sublates itself; the thing has thereby gone back into itself and is now determined as determinate; it is determinate in itself, or this thing.—But, thirdly, this return into itself is indeed the determination relating itself to itself; but it is at the same time unessential; the continuous subsistence with itself constitutes self-subsistent matter, in which the distinction of things, their determinacy which is in and for itself, is sublated and is an externality.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"140.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0006","text":"The thing as this is therefore indeed complete determinacy, but it is determinacy in the element of unessentiality.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"140.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0007","text":"Considered from the side of the movement of property, this results as follows. Property is not merely external determinacy, but existence that is in itself. This unity of externality and essentiality repels itself from itself, because it contains reflection-into-itself and reflection into other, and is, on the one hand, determinacy as a simple self-subsistent entity relating identically to itself, in which the negative unity, the One of the thing, is a sublated element;—on the other hand, this determinacy against other, but likewise as a One reflected into itself and determinate in itself; the matters, therefore, and this thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"140.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0008","text":"These are the two moments of externality identical with itself, or of property reflected into itself.—Property was that by which things were supposed to distinguish themselves; in freeing itself from this its negative side, of inhering in another, the thing too has thereby been freed from its being-determined by other things, and has gone back out of its relation to other into itself; but it is at the same time only the thing-in-itself become other; because the manifold properties are, on their side, self-subsistent, and their negative relation in the One of the thing has therefore become only a sublated one; it is consequently negation identical with itself only as against the positive continuity of material.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"140.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0009","text":"This thus constitutes the complete determinacy of the thing in such a way that it is at the same time an external one. The thing consists of self-subsistent matters, which are indifferent to their relation in the thing. This relation is therefore only an unessential connection of them, and the distinction of one thing from others rests on whether several of the particular matters, and in what quantity, are found in it. They extend beyond this thing, continue into others, and belonging to this thing is no limit for them. Nor, furthermore, are they a limitation for one another, since their negative relation is only the powerless this.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"140.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0010","text":"Therefore, in being combined in it, they do not sublate themselves; as self-subsistent, they are impenetrable to one another; in their determinacy they relate only to themselves, and are a multiplicity of subsistence indifferent to one another; they are capable only of a quantitative limit.—The thing as this is this merely quantitative relation of theirs, a mere collection, their also. It consists of some quantum of one material, also of that of another, also of others; this coherence, of having no coherence, alone constitutes the thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"140.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBD:P0010"]}],"source_digest":"4e8690fb05644d9721ebb865712480629b173e9fb303584cee826d0b95abd350","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Das Bestehen des Dings aus Materien."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Das Bestehen des Dings aus Materien.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS","title":"C. Dissolution of the Thing.","order":141,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDAS","text":"Dieses Ding, wie es sich bestimmt hat, als der bloß quantitative Zusammenhang der freien Stoffe, ist das schlechthin veränderliche. Seine Veränderung besteht darin, daß eine oder mehrere Materien aus der Sammlung ausgeschieden oder zu diesem Auch hinzugefügt werden, oder daß ihr Mengenverhältniß zu einander verändert wird. Das Entstehen und Vergehen dieses Dings ist die äußerliche Auflösung solcher äußerlichen Verbindung, oder die Verbindung solcher, denen es gleichgültig ist verbunden zu seyn oder nicht. Die Stoffe circuliren aus diesem Dinge unaufgehalten hinaus oder herein; es selbst ist die absolute Porosität ohne eigenes Maaß oder Form.\n\nSo ist das Ding in seiner absoluten Bestimmtheit, wodurch es dieses ist, das schlechthin auflösbare. Diese Auflösung ist ein äußerliches Bestimmtwerden, so wie auch das Seyn desselben; aber seine Auflösung und die Äußerlichkeit seines Seyns ist das Wesentliche dieses Seyns; es ist nur das Auch; es besteht nur in dieser Äußerlichkeit. Aber es besteht auch aus seinen Materien, und nicht nur das abstrakte Dieses als solches, sondern das ganze diese Ding ist die Auflösung seiner selbst. Das Ding ist nämlich bestimmt als eine äußerliche Sammlung selbst-ständiger Materien; diese Materien sind nicht Dinge, sie haben nicht die negative Selbstständigkeit; sondern sind die Eigenschaften als das Selbstständige, nämlich das Bestimmtseyn, das als solches in sich reflektirt ist. Die Materien sind daher zwar einfach und beziehen sich nur auf sich selbst; aber ihr Inhalt ist eine Bestimmtheit; die Reflexion-in-sich ist nur die Form dieses Inhalts, der nicht als solcher in sich reflektirt ist, sondern nach seiner Bestimmtheit sich auf Anderes bezieht. Das Ding ist daher nicht nur das Auch derselben,—die Beziehung derselben als gegen einander gleichgültiger, sondern ebenso sehr ihre negative Beziehung;—um ihrer Bestimmtheit sind die Materien selbst, diese ihre negative Reflexion; welche die Punktualität des Dinges ist. Die eine Materie ist nicht, was die andere ist, nach der Bestimmtheit ihres Inhalts gegen einander; und die eine ist nicht, insofern die andere ist, nach ihrer Selbstständigkeit.\n\nDas Ding ist daher so die Beziehung der Materien, aus denen es besteht, auf einander, daß in ihm die eine und die andere auch bestehen, aber daß darin zugleich die eine nicht besteht, insofern die andere besteht. Insofern also die eine Materie in dem Dinge ist, so ist die andere dadurch aufgehoben; aber das Ding ist zugleich das Auch, oder das Bestehen der andern. In dem Bestehen der einen Materie besteht daher die andere nicht, und ebenso sehr besteht sie auch in der erstern; und so gegenseitig alle diese verschiedenen Materien. Indem also in derselben Rüksicht, als die eine besteht, auch die andern bestehen, welches Eine Bestehen derselben die Punktualität oder negative Einheit des Dings ist, so durchdringen sie sich schlechthin; und indem das Ding zugleich nur das Auch der-selben, und die Materien in ihre Bestimmtheit reflektirt sind, so sind sie gleichgültig gegen einander, und berühren sich in ihrer Durchdringung nicht. Die Materien sind daher wesentlich porös, so daß die eine besteht in den Poren oder in dem Nichtbestehen der andern; aber diese andern sind selbst porös; in ihren Poren oder ihrem Nichtbestehen besteht auch die erste, und alle die übrigen; ihr Bestehen ist zugleich ihr Aufgehobenseyn, und das Bestehen von anderen; und dieß Bestehen der andern ist ebenso sehr dieser ihr Aufgehobenseyn und das Bestehen der ersteren und auf gleiche Weise aller andern. Das Ding ist daher die sich widersprechende Vermittelung des selbstständigen Bestehens mit sich durch sein Gegentheil, nämlich durch seine Negation, oder einer selbstständigen Materie durch das Bestehen und Nichtbestehen einer andern.—Die Existenz hat in diesem Dinge ihre Vollständigkeit erreicht, nämlich in Einem an sich seyendes Seyn oder selbstständiges Bestehen, und unwesentliche Existenz zu seyn; die Wahrheit der Existenz ist daher, ihr Ansichseyn in der Unwesentlichkeit, oder ihr Bestehen in einem Andern und zwar dem absolut Andern, oder zu ihrer Grundlage ihre Nichtigkeit zu haben. Sie ist daher Erscheinung.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0001","text":"Dieses Ding, wie es sich bestimmt hat, als der bloß quantitative Zusammenhang der freien Stoffe, ist das schlechthin veränderliche. Seine Veränderung besteht darin, daß eine oder mehrere Materien aus der Sammlung ausgeschieden oder zu diesem Auch hinzugefügt werden, oder daß ihr Mengenverhältniß zu einander verändert wird. Das Entstehen und Vergehen dieses Dings ist die äußerliche Auflösung solcher äußerlichen Verbindung, oder die Verbindung solcher, denen es gleichgültig ist verbunden zu seyn oder nicht. Die Stoffe circuliren aus diesem Dinge unaufgehalten hinaus oder herein; es selbst ist die absolute Porosität ohne eigenes Maaß oder Form.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"141.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0002","text":"So ist das Ding in seiner absoluten Bestimmtheit, wodurch es dieses ist, das schlechthin auflösbare. Diese Auflösung ist ein äußerliches Bestimmtwerden, so wie auch das Seyn desselben; aber seine Auflösung und die Äußerlichkeit seines Seyns ist das Wesentliche dieses Seyns; es ist nur das Auch; es besteht nur in dieser Äußerlichkeit. Aber es besteht auch aus seinen Materien, und nicht nur das abstrakte Dieses als solches, sondern das ganze diese Ding ist die Auflösung seiner selbst. Das Ding ist nämlich bestimmt als eine äußerliche Sammlung selbst-ständiger Materien; diese Materien sind nicht Dinge, sie haben nicht die negative Selbstständigkeit; sondern sind die Eigenschaften als das Selbstständige, nämlich das Bestimmtseyn, das als solches in sich reflektirt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"141.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0003","text":"Die Materien sind daher zwar einfach und beziehen sich nur auf sich selbst; aber ihr Inhalt ist eine Bestimmtheit; die Reflexion-in-sich ist nur die Form dieses Inhalts, der nicht als solcher in sich reflektirt ist, sondern nach seiner Bestimmtheit sich auf Anderes bezieht. Das Ding ist daher nicht nur das Auch derselben,—die Beziehung derselben als gegen einander gleichgültiger, sondern ebenso sehr ihre negative Beziehung;—um ihrer Bestimmtheit sind die Materien selbst, diese ihre negative Reflexion; welche die Punktualität des Dinges ist. Die eine Materie ist nicht, was die andere ist, nach der Bestimmtheit ihres Inhalts gegen einander; und die eine ist nicht, insofern die andere ist, nach ihrer Selbstständigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"141.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0004","text":"Das Ding ist daher so die Beziehung der Materien, aus denen es besteht, auf einander, daß in ihm die eine und die andere auch bestehen, aber daß darin zugleich die eine nicht besteht, insofern die andere besteht. Insofern also die eine Materie in dem Dinge ist, so ist die andere dadurch aufgehoben; aber das Ding ist zugleich das Auch, oder das Bestehen der andern. In dem Bestehen der einen Materie besteht daher die andere nicht, und ebenso sehr besteht sie auch in der erstern; und so gegenseitig alle diese verschiedenen Materien.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"141.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0005","text":"Indem also in derselben Rüksicht, als die eine besteht, auch die andern bestehen, welches Eine Bestehen derselben die Punktualität oder negative Einheit des Dings ist, so durchdringen sie sich schlechthin; und indem das Ding zugleich nur das Auch der-selben, und die Materien in ihre Bestimmtheit reflektirt sind, so sind sie gleichgültig gegen einander, und berühren sich in ihrer Durchdringung nicht. Die Materien sind daher wesentlich porös, so daß die eine besteht in den Poren oder in dem Nichtbestehen der andern; aber diese andern sind selbst porös; in ihren Poren oder ihrem Nichtbestehen besteht auch die erste, und alle die übrigen; ihr Bestehen ist zugleich ihr Aufgehobenseyn, und das Bestehen von anderen; und dieß Bestehen der andern ist ebenso sehr dieser ihr Aufgehobenseyn und das Bestehen der ersteren und auf gleiche Weise aller andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"141.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0006","text":"Das Ding ist daher die sich widersprechende Vermittelung des selbstständigen Bestehens mit sich durch sein Gegentheil, nämlich durch seine Negation, oder einer selbstständigen Materie durch das Bestehen und Nichtbestehen einer andern.—Die Existenz hat in diesem Dinge ihre Vollständigkeit erreicht, nämlich in Einem an sich seyendes Seyn oder selbstständiges Bestehen, und unwesentliche Existenz zu seyn; die Wahrheit der Existenz ist daher, ihr Ansichseyn in der Unwesentlichkeit, oder ihr Bestehen in einem Andern und zwar dem absolut Andern, oder zu ihrer Grundlage ihre Nichtigkeit zu haben. Sie ist daher Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"141.6"}],"sha256":"110ec52db420546170d93e38cee9f016ae68d67b6f3f08d5932b62e3c1fb208b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105504346970Z_b20adc4d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Dissolution of the Thing.","source_sha256":"110ec52db420546170d93e38cee9f016ae68d67b6f3f08d5932b62e3c1fb208b","sha256":"98d0b2a7dac953e6426bbc40ab5b6475b4bc65b6955aab816fbce97d4d1b786c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:55:04.346988+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0001","text":"This thing, as it has determined itself, as the merely quantitative connection of the free matters, is the absolutely mutable. Its alteration consists in one or several matters being separated from the collection or added to this also, or in their ratio of quantity to one another being altered. The coming-to-be and passing-away of this thing is the external dissolution of such an external combination, or the combination of such [matters] to which it is indifferent whether they are combined or not. The matters circulate unimpededly out of this thing or into it; it itself is absolute porosity without a measure or form of its own.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"141.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0002","text":"Thus the thing, in its absolute determinateness whereby it is this, is the absolutely dissoluble. This dissolution is an external being-determined, just as its being is also; but its dissolution and the externality of its being are the essential [aspect] of this being; it is only the also; it subsists only in this externality. But it also consists of its matters, and not only the abstract this as such, but the whole this thing is the dissolution of itself. The thing is namely determined as an external collection of self-subsistent matters; these matters are not things, they do not have negative self-subsistence; rather, they are the properties as the self-subsistent, namely being-determined, which as such is reflected into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"141.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0003","text":"The matters are therefore indeed simple and relate only to themselves; but their content is a determinateness; reflection-into-self is only the form of this content, which is not as such reflected into itself, but, in accordance with its determinateness, relates to an other. The thing is therefore not only their also—their relation as indifferent toward one another—but equally their negative relation; by virtue of their determinateness, the matters are themselves this their negative reflection, which is the punctuality of the thing. One matter is not what the other is, in accordance with the determinateness of their content with respect to one another; and the one is not, insofar as the other is, in accordance with its self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"141.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0004","text":"The thing is therefore the relation of the matters of which it consists to one another, such that in it the one and the other also subsist, but that therein at the same time the one does not subsist insofar as the other subsists. Insofar, therefore, as the one matter is in the thing, the other is thereby sublated; but the thing is at the same time the also, or the subsistence of the other. In the subsistence of the one matter, therefore, the other does not subsist, and equally it also subsists in the former; and thus reciprocally all these different matters.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"141.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0005","text":"Since, therefore, in the same respect in which the one subsists, the others also subsist—which one subsistence of them is the punctuality or negative unity of the thing—they absolutely interpenetrate; and since the thing is at the same time only the also of them, and the matters are reflected into their determinateness, they are indifferent toward one another and do not touch one another in their interpenetration. The matters are therefore essentially porous, so that the one subsists in the pores, or in the non-subsistence, of the others; but these others are themselves porous; in their pores or their non-subsistence, the first too, and all the rest, subsist; their subsistence is at the same time their being-sublated, and the subsistence of others; and this subsistence of the others is equally their being-sublated and the subsistence of the first, and in the same way of all the others.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"141.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0006","text":"The thing is therefore the self-contradictory mediation of self-subsistent subsistence with itself through its opposite, namely through its negation, or [the mediation] of one self-subsistent matter through the subsistence and non-subsistence of another.—Existence has attained its completeness in this thing, namely, [in being] in one respect being-in-itself or self-subsistent subsistence, and [in another] inessential existence; the truth of existence is therefore to have its being-in-itself in inessentiality, or its subsistence in an other, indeed in the absolute other, or to have its nullity as its foundation. It is therefore appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"141.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDAS:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"82bec740258c8c7d8e891c22952290edea8d7a14b76ae5bff20f3057aac49fd0","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Die Auflösung des Dings."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Die Auflösung des Dings.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38","title":"Remark.","order":142,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_38","text":"Es ist eine der geläufigsten Bestimmungen des Vorstellens, daß ein Ding aus vielen selbstständigen Materien bestehe. Einer Seits wird das Ding betrachtet, daß es Eigenschaften habe, deren Bestehen das Ding ist. Anderer Seits aber werden diese verschiedenen Bestimmungen als Materien genommen, deren Bestehen nicht das Ding ist, sondern umgekehrt besteht das Ding aus ihnen; es selbst ist nur ihre äußerliche Verbindung und quantitative Grenze. Beides, die Eigenschaften und die Materien sind dieselben Inhaltsbestimmungen, nur daß sie dort Momente, in ihre negative Einheit als in eine von ihnen selbst unterschiedene Grundlage, die Dingheit, reflektirte sind, hier selbstständige verschiedene, deren jedes in seine eigene Einheit mit sich reflektirt ist. Diese Materien nun bestimmen sich ferner als selbstständiges Bestehen; aber sie sind auch zusammen in einem Dinge. Dieses Ding hat die zwei Bestimmungen, erstlich dieses zu seyn, und zweitens das Auch zu seyn. Das Auch ist dasjenige, was in der äußeren Anschauung als Raumausdehnung vorkommt; Dieses aber, die negative Einheit, ist die Punktualität des Dinges. Die Materien sind zusammen in der Punktualität, und ihr Auch oder die Ausdehnung ist allenthalben diese Punktualität; denn das Auch als Dingheit ist wesentlich auch als negative Einheit bestimmt. Wo daher die eine dieser Materien ist, in einem und demselben Punkte ist die andere; das Ding hat nicht an einem andern Orte seine Farbe, an einem andern seinen Riechstoff, an einem dritten seinen Wärmestoff u.s.f. sondern in dem Punkte, in dem es warm ist, ist es auch farbig, sauer, elektrisch u.s.w. Weil nun diese Stoffe nicht außer einander, sondern in Einem Diesen sind, werden sie als porös angenommen, so daß die eine in den Zwischenräumen der andern existirt. Diejenige, die sich in den Zwischenräumen der andern befindet, ist aber auch selbst porös; in ihren Poren existirt daher umgekehrt die andere; aber nicht nur diese, sondern auch die dritte, zehnte, u.s.f. Alle sind porös und in den Zwischenräumen einer jeden befinden sich alle andern, wie sie sich mit den übrigen in diesen Poren einer jeden befindet. Sie sind daher eine Menge, die sich so gegenseitig durchdringt, daß die durchdringenden von den anderen ebenso durchdrungen werden, daß somit jede ihr eigenes Durchdrungenseyn wieder durchdringt. Jede ist als ihre Negation gesetzt, und diese Negation ist das Bestehen einer anderen; aber dieß Bestehen ist ebenso sehr die Negation dieser andern und das Bestehen der ersten.\n\nDie Ausrede, durch welche das Vorstellen den Widerspruch des selbstständigen Bestehens der mehreren Materien in Einem, oder die Gleichgültigkeit derselben gegen einander in ihrer Durchdringung abhält, pflegt bekanntlich die Kleinheit der Theile und der Poren zu seyn. Wo der Unterschied-an-sich, der Widerspruch und die Negation der Negation eintritt, überhaupt wo begriffen werden soll, läßt das Vorstellen sich in den äußerlichen, den quantitativen Unterschied herunterfallen; in Ansehung des Entstehens und Vergehens nimmt es seine Zuflucht zur Allmähligkeit und in Ansehung des Seyns zur Kleinheit, worin das Verschwindende zum Unbemerkbaren, der Widerspruch zu einer Verwirrung herabgesetzt, und das wahre Verhältniß in ein unbestimmtes Vorstellen hinübergespielt wird, dessen Trübheit das sich Aufhebende rettet.\n\nNäher aber diese Trübheit beleuchtet, so zeigt sie sich als der Widerspruch, Theils als der subjektive des Vorstellens, Theils als der objektive des Gegenstands; das Vorstellen selbst enthält vollständig die Elemente desselben. Was es nämlich erstlich selbst thut, ist der Widerspruch, sich an die Wahrnehmung halten und Dinge des Daseyns vor sich haben zu wollen, und anderer Seits dem Nichtwahrnehmbaren, durch die Reflexion bestimmten, sinnliches Daseyn zuzuschreiben;—die kleinen Theile und Poren sollen zugleich ein sinnliches Daseyn seyn und es wird von ihrem Gesetztseyn als von derselben Weise der Realität gesprochen,—welche der Farbe, Wärme u. s.f. zukommt. Wenn ferner das Vorstellen diesen gegenständlichen Nebel, die Poren und die kleinen Theilchen, näher betrachtete, so erkennte es darin nicht nur eine Materie und auch deren Negation, so daß hier die Materie, und daneben ihre Negation, der Porus, und neben diesem wieder Materie und so fort sich befände, sondern daß es in diesem Dinge, 1) die selbstständige Materie, 2) ihre Negation oder Porosität und die andere selbstständige Materie in einem in und demselben Punkte hat, daß diese Porosität und das selbstständige Bestehen der Materien ineinander als in Einem eine gegenseitige Negation und Durchdringen des Durchdringens ist.—Die neueren Darstellungen der Physik über die Verbreitung des Wasserdampfes in der atmosphärischen Luft und der Gasarten durch einander, heben eine Seite des Begriffs, der sich hier über die Natur des Dinges ergeben hat, bestimmter heraus.\n\nSie zeigen nämlich, daß z.B. ein gewisses Volumen eben so viel Wasserdampf aufnimmt, es sey leer von athmosphärischer Luft oder damit erfüllt; auch daß die Gasarten so sich in einander verbreiten, daß jede für die andere so gut als ein Vacuum ist, wenigstens daß sie in keiner chemischen Verbindung miteinander sind, jedes ununterbrochen durch das andere mit sich kontinuirlich bleibt und sich in seiner Durchdringung mit den andern, gleichgültig gegen sie erhält.—Aber das weitere Moment im Begriffe des Dinges ist, daß im Diesen die eine Materie sich befindet wo die andere, und das Durchdringende in demselben Punkte auch durchdrungen ist, oder das Selbstständige unmittelbar die Selbstständigkeit eines Andern ist. Dieß ist widersprechend; aber das Ding ist nichts Anderes als dieser Widerspruch selbst; darum ist es Erscheinung.\n\nEine ähnliche Bewandtniß, als es mit diesen Materien hat, hat es im Geistigen mit der Vorstellung der Seelenkräfte oder Seelenvermögen. Der Geist ist in viel tieferem Sinne dieses, die negative Einheit, in welcher sich seine Bestimmungen durchdringen. Aber als Seele vorgestellt, pflegt er häufig als ein Ding genommen zu werden. Wie man den Menschen überhaupt aus Seele und Leib bestehen läßt, deren jedes als ein Selbstständiges für sich gilt, so läßt man die Seele aus sogenannten Seelenkräften bestehen, deren jede eine für sich bestehende Selbstständigkeit hat, oder eine unmittelbare für sich nach ihrer Bestimmtheit wirkende Thätigkeit ist. Man stellt sich so vor, daß hier der Verstand, hier die Einbildungskraft für sich wirke, daß man den Verstand, das Gedächtniß, u.s.f. jede für sich kultivire, und einstweilen die andern Kräfte in Unthätigkeit linker Hand liegen lasse, bis die Reihe vielleicht, vielleicht auch nicht an sie komme. Indem sie in das materiell-einfache Seelending verlegt werden, welches als einfach immateriell sey, so werden die Vermögen zwar nicht als besondere Materien vorgestellt; aber als Kräfte werden sie gleich indifferent gegen einander angenommen, als jene Materien. Aber der Geist ist nicht jener Widerspruch, welcher das Ding ist, das sich auflöst und in Erscheinung übergeht; sondern er ist schon an ihm selbst der in seine absolute Einheit, nämlich den Begriffe zurückgegangene Widerspruch, worin die Unterschiede nicht mehr als selbstständige, sondern nur als besondere Momente im Subjekte, der einfachen Individualität, zu denken sind.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0001","text":"Es ist eine der geläufigsten Bestimmungen des Vorstellens, daß ein Ding aus vielen selbstständigen Materien bestehe. Einer Seits wird das Ding betrachtet, daß es Eigenschaften habe, deren Bestehen das Ding ist. Anderer Seits aber werden diese verschiedenen Bestimmungen als Materien genommen, deren Bestehen nicht das Ding ist, sondern umgekehrt besteht das Ding aus ihnen; es selbst ist nur ihre äußerliche Verbindung und quantitative Grenze. Beides, die Eigenschaften und die Materien sind dieselben Inhaltsbestimmungen, nur daß sie dort Momente, in ihre negative Einheit als in eine von ihnen selbst unterschiedene Grundlage, die Dingheit, reflektirte sind, hier selbstständige verschiedene, deren jedes in seine eigene Einheit mit sich reflektirt ist. Diese Materien nun bestimmen sich ferner als selbstständiges Bestehen; aber sie sind auch zusammen in einem Dinge.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"142.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0002","text":"Dieses Ding hat die zwei Bestimmungen, erstlich dieses zu seyn, und zweitens das Auch zu seyn. Das Auch ist dasjenige, was in der äußeren Anschauung als Raumausdehnung vorkommt; Dieses aber, die negative Einheit, ist die Punktualität des Dinges. Die Materien sind zusammen in der Punktualität, und ihr Auch oder die Ausdehnung ist allenthalben diese Punktualität; denn das Auch als Dingheit ist wesentlich auch als negative Einheit bestimmt. Wo daher die eine dieser Materien ist, in einem und demselben Punkte ist die andere; das Ding hat nicht an einem andern Orte seine Farbe, an einem andern seinen Riechstoff, an einem dritten seinen Wärmestoff u.s.f. sondern in dem Punkte, in dem es warm ist, ist es auch farbig, sauer, elektrisch u.s.w.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"142.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0003","text":"Weil nun diese Stoffe nicht außer einander, sondern in Einem Diesen sind, werden sie als porös angenommen, so daß die eine in den Zwischenräumen der andern existirt. Diejenige, die sich in den Zwischenräumen der andern befindet, ist aber auch selbst porös; in ihren Poren existirt daher umgekehrt die andere; aber nicht nur diese, sondern auch die dritte, zehnte, u.s.f. Alle sind porös und in den Zwischenräumen einer jeden befinden sich alle andern, wie sie sich mit den übrigen in diesen Poren einer jeden befindet. Sie sind daher eine Menge, die sich so gegenseitig durchdringt, daß die durchdringenden von den anderen ebenso durchdrungen werden, daß somit jede ihr eigenes Durchdrungenseyn wieder durchdringt. Jede ist als ihre Negation gesetzt, und diese Negation ist das Bestehen einer anderen; aber dieß Bestehen ist ebenso sehr die Negation dieser andern und das Bestehen der ersten.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"142.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0004","text":"Die Ausrede, durch welche das Vorstellen den Widerspruch des selbstständigen Bestehens der mehreren Materien in Einem, oder die Gleichgültigkeit derselben gegen einander in ihrer Durchdringung abhält, pflegt bekanntlich die Kleinheit der Theile und der Poren zu seyn. Wo der Unterschied-an-sich, der Widerspruch und die Negation der Negation eintritt, überhaupt wo begriffen werden soll, läßt das Vorstellen sich in den äußerlichen, den quantitativen Unterschied herunterfallen; in Ansehung des Entstehens und Vergehens nimmt es seine Zuflucht zur Allmähligkeit und in Ansehung des Seyns zur Kleinheit, worin das Verschwindende zum Unbemerkbaren, der Widerspruch zu einer Verwirrung herabgesetzt, und das wahre Verhältniß in ein unbestimmtes Vorstellen hinübergespielt wird, dessen Trübheit das sich Aufhebende rettet.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"142.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0005","text":"Näher aber diese Trübheit beleuchtet, so zeigt sie sich als der Widerspruch, Theils als der subjektive des Vorstellens, Theils als der objektive des Gegenstands; das Vorstellen selbst enthält vollständig die Elemente desselben. Was es nämlich erstlich selbst thut, ist der Widerspruch, sich an die Wahrnehmung halten und Dinge des Daseyns vor sich haben zu wollen, und anderer Seits dem Nichtwahrnehmbaren, durch die Reflexion bestimmten, sinnliches Daseyn zuzuschreiben;—die kleinen Theile und Poren sollen zugleich ein sinnliches Daseyn seyn und es wird von ihrem Gesetztseyn als von derselben Weise der Realität gesprochen,—welche der Farbe, Wärme u. s.f. zukommt.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"142.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0006","text":"Wenn ferner das Vorstellen diesen gegenständlichen Nebel, die Poren und die kleinen Theilchen, näher betrachtete, so erkennte es darin nicht nur eine Materie und auch deren Negation, so daß hier die Materie, und daneben ihre Negation, der Porus, und neben diesem wieder Materie und so fort sich befände, sondern daß es in diesem Dinge, 1) die selbstständige Materie, 2) ihre Negation oder Porosität und die andere selbstständige Materie in einem in und demselben Punkte hat, daß diese Porosität und das selbstständige Bestehen der Materien ineinander als in Einem eine gegenseitige Negation und Durchdringen des Durchdringens ist.—Die neueren Darstellungen der Physik über die Verbreitung des Wasserdampfes in der atmosphärischen Luft und der Gasarten durch einander, heben eine Seite des Begriffs, der sich hier über die Natur des Dinges ergeben hat, bestimmter heraus.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"142.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0007","text":"Sie zeigen nämlich, daß z.B. ein gewisses Volumen eben so viel Wasserdampf aufnimmt, es sey leer von athmosphärischer Luft oder damit erfüllt; auch daß die Gasarten so sich in einander verbreiten, daß jede für die andere so gut als ein Vacuum ist, wenigstens daß sie in keiner chemischen Verbindung miteinander sind, jedes ununterbrochen durch das andere mit sich kontinuirlich bleibt und sich in seiner Durchdringung mit den andern, gleichgültig gegen sie erhält.—Aber das weitere Moment im Begriffe des Dinges ist, daß im Diesen die eine Materie sich befindet wo die andere, und das Durchdringende in demselben Punkte auch durchdrungen ist, oder das Selbstständige unmittelbar die Selbstständigkeit eines Andern ist. Dieß ist widersprechend; aber das Ding ist nichts Anderes als dieser Widerspruch selbst; darum ist es Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"142.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0008","text":"Eine ähnliche Bewandtniß, als es mit diesen Materien hat, hat es im Geistigen mit der Vorstellung der Seelenkräfte oder Seelenvermögen. Der Geist ist in viel tieferem Sinne dieses, die negative Einheit, in welcher sich seine Bestimmungen durchdringen. Aber als Seele vorgestellt, pflegt er häufig als ein Ding genommen zu werden. Wie man den Menschen überhaupt aus Seele und Leib bestehen läßt, deren jedes als ein Selbstständiges für sich gilt, so läßt man die Seele aus sogenannten Seelenkräften bestehen, deren jede eine für sich bestehende Selbstständigkeit hat, oder eine unmittelbare für sich nach ihrer Bestimmtheit wirkende Thätigkeit ist. Man stellt sich so vor, daß hier der Verstand, hier die Einbildungskraft für sich wirke, daß man den Verstand, das Gedächtniß, u.s.f.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"142.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0009","text":"jede für sich kultivire, und einstweilen die andern Kräfte in Unthätigkeit linker Hand liegen lasse, bis die Reihe vielleicht, vielleicht auch nicht an sie komme. Indem sie in das materiell-einfache Seelending verlegt werden, welches als einfach immateriell sey, so werden die Vermögen zwar nicht als besondere Materien vorgestellt; aber als Kräfte werden sie gleich indifferent gegen einander angenommen, als jene Materien. Aber der Geist ist nicht jener Widerspruch, welcher das Ding ist, das sich auflöst und in Erscheinung übergeht; sondern er ist schon an ihm selbst der in seine absolute Einheit, nämlich den Begriffe zurückgegangene Widerspruch, worin die Unterschiede nicht mehr als selbstständige, sondern nur als besondere Momente im Subjekte, der einfachen Individualität, zu denken sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"142.9"}],"sha256":"f528f0f9e704cef6b5d243baac12eb5bea6e86d3146daa1d83903a96d06966b9","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105519368357Z_ccafcb7a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"f528f0f9e704cef6b5d243baac12eb5bea6e86d3146daa1d83903a96d06966b9","sha256":"4407e07ff6df16ce9f7db203fb7c310b72ac37468519ea5b01c8b4afcb689de0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:55:19.368373+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0001","text":"It is one of the most customary determinations of representation that a thing consists of many self-subsistent matters. On the one hand, the thing is considered as having properties, whose subsistence is the thing. On the other hand, however, these different determinations are taken as matters, whose subsistence is not the thing, but conversely the thing consists of them; it itself is only their external connection and quantitative limit. Both, the properties and the matters, are the same determinations of content, only that there they are moments reflected into their negative unity, as into a substrate distinct from themselves, thinghood; here they are self-subsistent different things, each of which is reflected into its own unity with itself. These matters, then, further determine themselves as self-subsistent subsistence; but they are also together in one thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"142.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0002","text":"This thing has the two determinations: first, to be this, and second, to be also. The also is that which occurs in external intuition as spatial extension; this, however, the negative unity, is the punctuality of the thing. The matters are together in the punctuality, and their also, or extension, is everywhere this punctuality; for the also, as thinghood, is essentially also determined as negative unity. Thus, where one of these matters is, the other is in one and the same point; the thing does not have its colour in one place, its odorous matter in another, its heat-matter in a third, etc., but in the point in which it is warm, it is also coloured, sour, electric, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"142.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0003","text":"Since these stuffs are not outside one another, but in One This, they are assumed to be porous, so that one exists in the interstices of the other. But that which is situated in the interstices of the other is itself also porous; in its pores, therefore, conversely the other exists; but not only this one, but also the third, tenth, etc. All are porous, and in the interstices of each are found all the others, just as each is found with the rest in these pores of each. They are therefore a multitude which thus mutually interpenetrates, such that those interpenetrating are equally interpenetrated by the others, so that each in turn interpenetrates its own being-interpenetrated. Each is posited as its negation, and this negation is the subsistence of another; but this subsistence is equally the negation of this other and the subsistence of the first.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"142.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0004","text":"The evasion by which representation wards off the contradiction of the self-subsistent subsistence of the several matters in One, or their indifference toward one another in their interpenetration, is, as is well known, usually the smallness of the parts and pores. Where the difference-in-itself, contradiction, and the negation of negation enter in—where, in general, something is to be comprehended—representation lets itself sink down into external, quantitative difference; with respect to arising and passing away it takes refuge in gradualness, and with respect to being in smallness, wherein that which vanishes is degraded to the unnoticeable, contradiction to a confusion, and the true relation is played over into an indeterminate representation, whose murkiness saves that which sublates itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"142.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0005","text":"But when this murkiness is examined more closely, it shows itself to be the contradiction, partly as the subjective contradiction of representation, partly as the objective contradiction of the object; representation itself fully contains its elements. For what it itself does first of all is the contradiction of wishing to adhere to perception and to have before itself things of existence, and, on the other hand, of ascribing sensible existence to the imperceptible, determined through reflection;—the small parts and pores are supposed at once to be a sensible existence, and their positedness is spoken of as the same mode of reality—which belongs to colour, heat, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"142.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0006","text":"Further, if representation were to consider this objective mist, the pores and the small particles, more closely, it would recognize therein not merely one matter and also its negation, so that here matter, and beside it its negation, the pore, and beside this again matter, and so on, would be found; but rather that in this thing it has, 1) the self-subsistent matter, 2) its negation or porosity, and the other self-subsistent matter in one and the same point; that this porosity and the self-subsistent subsistence of the matters, within one another as in One, are a reciprocal negation and interpenetration of interpenetration.—The more recent presentations of physics concerning the diffusion of water vapour in atmospheric air and of gases through one another bring out more determinately one aspect of the concept that has here emerged concerning the nature of the thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"142.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0007","text":"They show, namely, that, e.g., a certain volume takes up just as much water vapour whether it is empty of atmospheric air or filled with it; also, that gases diffuse into one another in such a way that each is, for the other, as good as a vacuum, at least that they are in no chemical combination with one another, each remaining uninterruptedly continuous with itself through the other and maintaining itself, in its interpenetration with the others, indifferent toward them.—But the further moment in the concept of the thing is that, in This, one matter is found where the other is, and that what interpenetrates is, in the same point, also interpenetrated, or that the self-subsistent is immediately the self-subsistence of an Other. This is contradictory; but the thing is nothing other than this contradiction itself; therefore it is appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"142.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0008","text":"A situation similar to that of these matters obtains in the spiritual sphere with the representation of the powers or faculties of the soul. The spirit is, in a much deeper sense, this, the negative unity in which its determinations interpenetrate. But represented as soul, it is often taken to be a thing. Just as one generally allows the human being to consist of soul and body, each of which counts as a self-subsistent entity for itself, so one allows the soul to consist of so-called powers of the soul, each of which has a self-subsistence existing for itself, or is an immediate activity operating for itself according to its determinacy. Thus one imagines that here the understanding, there the imagination, operates for itself, that one cultivates the understanding, memory, etc.,","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"142.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_38:P0009","text":"each for itself, and meanwhile leaves the other powers lying idle to the left, until their turn perhaps, perhaps also not, comes. In being placed into the materially simple soul-thing, which is supposed to be simple and immaterial, the faculties are indeed not represented as particular matters; but as powers they are assumed equally indifferent toward one another, like those matters. But spirit is not that contradiction which the thing is, which dissolves itself and passes over into appearance; rather, it is already in itself the contradiction returned into its absolute unity, namely, the concept, in which the differences are no longer to be thought as self-subsistent, but only as particular moments in the subject, simple individuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"142.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_38:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"c935d02569078614dda6ae9b27877a6b8238f4ee601b2897cfdbd2139014f010","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE","title":"A. The Law of Appearance.","order":143,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DGDE","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Die Erscheinung.\n\nDie Existenz ist die Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, zu der sich das Wesen wieder hergestellt hat. Diese Unmittelbarkeit ist an sich die Reflexion des Wesens in sich. Das Wesen ist als Existenz aus seinem Grunde heraufgetreten, der selbst in sie übergegangen ist. Die Existenz ist diese reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, insofern sie an ihr selbst die absolute Negativität ist. Sie ist nunmehr auch als dieß gesetzt, indem sie sich als Erscheinung bestimmt hat.\n\nDie Erscheinung ist daher zunächst das Wesen in seiner Existenz; das Wesen ist unmittelbar an ihr vorhanden. Daß sie nicht als unmittelbare, sondern die reflektirte Existenz ist, dieß macht das Moment des Wesens an ihr aus; oder die Existenz als wesentliche Existenz ist Erscheinung.\n\nEs ist etwas nur Erscheinung,—in dem Sinne, daß die Existenz als solche nur ein Gesetztes, nicht an- und für-sich-Seyendes ist. Dieß macht ihre Wesentlichkeit aus, an ihr selbst die Negativität der Reflexion, die Natur des Wesens, zu haben. Es ist dieß nicht eine fremde, äußerliche Reflexion, welcher das Wesen zugehörte, und die durch Vergleichung desselben mit der Existenz diese für Erscheinung erklärte. Sondern, wie sich ergeben hat, ist diese Wesentlichkeit der Existenz, Erscheinung zu seyn, die eigne Wahrheit der Existenz. Die Reflexion, wodurch sie dieß ist, gehört ihr selbst an.\n\nWenn aber gesagt wird, Etwas sey nur Erscheinung in dem Sinne, als ob dagegen die unmittelbare Existenz die Wahrheit wäre; so ist vielmehr die Erscheinung die höhere Wahrheit; denn sie ist die Existenz wie sie als wesentliche, da hingegen die Existenz die noch wesenlose Erscheinung ist; weil sie nur das eine Moment der Erscheinung, nämlich die Existenz als unmittelbare, noch nicht ihre negative Reflexion, an ihr hat. Wenn die Erscheinung wesenlos genannt wird, so wird an das Moment ihrer Negativität so gedacht, als ob das Unmittelbare dagegen das Positive und Wahrhafte wäre; aber vielmehr enthält dieß Unmittelbare die wesentliche Wahrheit noch nicht an ihm. Die Existenz hört vielmehr auf, wesenlos zu seyn, darin, daß sie in Erscheinung übergeht.\n\nDas Wesen scheint zunächst in ihm selbst, in seiner einfachen Identität; so ist es die abstrakte Reflexion, die reine Bewegung von Nichts durch Nichts zu sich selbst zurück. Das Wesen erscheint, so ist es nunmehr realer Schein, indem die Momente des Scheins Existenz haben. Die Erscheinung ist, wie sich ergeben hat, das Ding als die negative Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst; die Unterschiede, welche es enthält, sind selbstständige Materien, die der Widerspruch sind, ein unmittelbares Bestehen zu seyn, und zugleich nur in fremder Selbstständigkeit also in der Negation der eigenen ihr Bestehen zu haben, und wieder eben darum auch nur in der Negation jener fremden oder in der Negation ihrer eigenen Negation. Der Schein ist dieselbe Vermittelung, aber seine haltlosen Momente haben in der Erscheinung die Gestalt unmittelbarer Selbstständigkeit. Dagegen ist die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit, die der Existenz zukommt, ihrer Seits zum Momente herabgesetzt. Die Erscheinung ist daher Einheit des Scheins und der Existenz.\n\nDie Erscheinung bestimmt sich nun näher. Sie ist die wesentliche Existenz; die Wesentlichkeit derselben unterscheidet sich von ihr als unwesentlicher und diese beiden Seiten treten in Beziehung mit einander.—Sie ist daher zuerst einfache Identität mit sich, die zugleich verschiedene Inhaltsbestimmungen enthält, welche sowohl selbst als deren Beziehung das im Wechsel der Erscheinung sich gleich bleibende ist; das Gesetz der Erscheinung.\n\nZweitens aber geht das in seiner Verschiedenheit einfache Gesetz in den Gegensatz über; das Wesentliche der Erscheinung wird ihr selbst entgegengesetzt und der erscheinenden Welt tritt die an sich seyende Welt gegenüber.\n\nDrittens geht dieser Gegensatz in seinen Grund zurück; das Ansichseyende ist in der Erscheinung und umgekehrt ist das Erscheinende bestimmt als in sein Ansichseyn aufgenommen; die Erscheinung wird Verhältniß.\n\n## A. Das Gesetz der Erscheinung.\n\n1. Die Erscheinung ist das Existirende vermittelt durch seine Negation, welche sein Bestehen ausmacht. Diese seine Negation ist zwar ein anderes Selbstständiges; aber dieß ist ebenso wesentlich ein aufgehobenes. Das Existirende ist daher die Rückkehr seiner in sich selbst durch seine Negation und durch die Negation dieser seiner Negation; es hat also wesentliche Selbstständigkeit; so wie es gleich unmittelbar schlechthin Gesetztseyn ist, das einen Grund und ein Anderes zu seinem Bestehen hat.—Fürs Erste ist also die Erscheinung die Existenz zugleich mit ihrer Wesentlichkeit, das Gesetztseyn mit seinem Grunde; aber dieser Grund ist die Negation; und das andere Selbstständige, der Grund des ersten, ist gleichfalls nur ein Gesetztseyn. Oder das Existirende ist als Erscheinendes in ein Anderes reflektirt und hat es zu seinem Grunde, welches selbst nur dieß ist, in ein Anderes reflektirt zu seyn. Die wesentliche Selbstständigkeit, die ihm zukommt, weil es Rückkehr in sich selbst ist, ist um der Negativität der Momente willen, die Rückkehr des Nichts durch Nichts zu sich selbst zurück; die Selbstständigkeit des Existirenden ist daher nur der wesentliche Schein. Der Zusammenhang des sich gegenseitig begründenden Existirenden besteht darum in dieser gegenseitigen Negation, daß das Bestehen des einen nicht das Bestehen des andern, sondern dessen Gesetztseyn ist, welche Beziehung des Gesetztseyns allein ihr Bestehen ausmacht. Der Grund ist vorhanden, wie er in seiner Wahrheit ist, nämlich ein Erstes zu seyn, das nur ein Vorausgesetztes ist.\n\nDieß macht nun die negative Seite der Erscheinung aus. Aber in dieser negativen Vermittelung ist unmittelbar die positive Identität des Existirenden mit sich enthalten. Denn es ist nicht Gesetztseyn gegen einen wesentlichen Grund, oder ist nicht der Schein an einem Selbstständigen; sondern ist Gesetztseyn, das sich auf ein Gesetztseyn bezieht, oder ist ein Schein nur in einem Scheine. Es bezieht sich in dieser seiner Negation oder in seinem Andern, das selbst ein Aufgehobenes ist, auf sich selbst; ist also mit sich identische oder positive Wesentlichkeit.—Dieses Identische ist nicht die Unmittelbarkeit, die der Existenz als solcher zukommt, und nur das Unwesentliche ist, sein Bestehen in einem Andern zu haben. Sondern es ist der wesentliche Inhalt der Erscheinung, welcher zwei Seiten hat, erstens in der Form des Gesetztseyns oder der äußerlichen Unmittelbarkeit, zweitens das Gesetztseyn als mit sich Identisches zu seyn. Nach der ersten Seite ist er als ein Daseyn, aber als ein zufälliges, unwesentliches, das nach seiner Unmittelbarkeit dem Übergehen, Entstehen und Vergehen unterworfen ist. Nach der andern Seite ist er die einfache jenem Wechsel entnommene Inhaltsbestimmung, das Bleibende desselben.\n\nAußerdem daß dieser Inhalt überhaupt das Einfache des Vergänglichen ist, ist er auch bestimmter, in sich verschiedener Inhalt. Er ist die Reflexion der Erscheinung, des negativen Daseyns, in sich, enthält also die Bestimmtheit wesentlich. Die Erscheinung aber ist die seyende vielfache Verschiedenheit, die sich in unwesentlicher Mannigfaltigkeit herumwirft; ihr reflektirter Inhalt dagegen ist ihre Mannigfaltigkeit auf den einfachen Unterschied reducirt. Der bestimmte wesentliche Inhalt ist nämlich näher, nicht nur bestimmt überhaupt, sondern als das Wesentliche der Erscheinung die vollständige Bestimmtheit; eines und sein Anderes. In der Erscheinung hat jedes dieser beiden sein Bestehen so in dem Andern, daß es zugleich nur in dessen Nichtbestehen ist. Dieser Widerspruch hebt sich auf; und die Reflexion desselben in sich, ist die Identität ihres beiderseitigen Bestehens, daß das Gesetztseyn des einen auch das Gesetztseyn des Andern ist. Sie machen Ein Bestehen aus, zugleich als verschiedener, gegen einander gleichgültiger Inhalt. In der wesentlichen Seite der Erscheinung ist somit das Negative des unwesentlichen Inhalts, sich aufzuheben, in die Identität zurückgegangen; er ist ein gleichgültiges Bestehen, welches nicht das Aufgehobenseyn, sondern vielmehr das Bestehen des Andern ist.\n\nDiese Einheit ist das Gesetz der Erscheinung.\n\n2. Das Gesetz ist also das Positive der Vermittelung des Erscheinenden. Die Erscheinung ist zunächst die Existenz als die negative Vermittelung mit sich, so daß das Existirende durch sein eigenes Nichtbestehen, durch ein Anderes, und wieder durch das Nichtbestehen dieses Andern mit sich vermittelt ist. Darin ist enthalten erstens das bloße Scheinen und das Verschwinden beider, die unwesentliche Erscheinung; zweitens auch das Bleiben oder das Gesetz; denn jedes der beiden existirt in jenem Aufheben des Andern; und ihr Gesetztseyn als ihre Negativität ist zugleich das identische, positive Gesetztseyn beider.\n\nDieß bleibende Bestehen, welches die Erscheinung im Gesetze hat, ist somit, wie es sich bestimmt hat, erstlich entgegengesetzt der Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, welche die Existenz hat. Diese Unmittelbarkeit ist zwar an sich die reflektirte, nämlich der in sich zurückgegangene Grund; aber in der Erscheinung ist nun diese einfache Unmittelbarkeit von der reflektirten unterschieden, welche im Dinge erst sich zu trennen anfingen. Das existirende Ding ist in seiner Auflösung dieser Gegensatz geworden; das Positive seiner Auflösung ist jene Identität des Erscheinenden als Gesetztseyns mit sich in seinem andern Gesetztseyn.—Zweitens ist diese reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit selbst bestimmt als das Gesetztseyn, gegen die seyende Unmittelbarkeit der Existenz. Dieß Gesetztseyn ist nunmehr das Wesentliche, und wahrhaft Positive. Der deutsche Ausdruck Gesetz enthält diese Bestimmung gleichfalls. In diesem Gesetztseyn liegt die wesentliche Beziehung der beiden Seiten des Unterschiedes, die das Gesetz enthält; sie sind verschiedener gegen einander unmittelbarer Inhalt und sind dieß als die Reflexion des der Erscheinung angehörigen, verschwindenden Inhalts. Als wesentliche Verschiedenheit, sind die Verschiedenen einfache sich auf sich beziehende Inhaltsbestimmungen. Aber ebenso sehr ist keine für sich unmittelbar, sondern jede ist wesentlich Gesetztseyn, oder ist nur, insofern die andere ist.\n\nDrittens Erscheinung und Gesetz haben einen und denselben Inhalt. Das Gesetz ist die Reflexion der Erscheinung in die Identität mit sich; so steht die Erscheinung als das nichtige Unmittelbare dem Insichreflektirten gegenüber, und sie sind nach dieser Form unterschieden. Aber die Reflexion der Erscheinung, wodurch dieser Unterschied ist, ist auch die wesentliche Identität der Erscheinung selbst und ihrer Reflexion, was überhaupt die Natur der Reflexion ist; sie ist das im Gesetztseyn identische mit sich, und gleichgültig gegen jenen Unterschied, welcher die Form oder das Gesetztseyn ist; also ein Inhalt, der sich aus der Erscheinung in das Gesetz kontinuirt, der Inhalt des Gesetzes, und der Erscheinung.\n\nDieser Inhalt macht hiermit die Grundlage der Erscheinung aus; das Gesetz ist diese Grundlage selbst, die Erscheinung ist derselbe Inhalt, aber enthält noch mehr, nämlich den unwesentlichen Inhalt ihres unmittelbaren Seyns. Auch die Formbestimmung, wodurch die Erscheinung als solche von dem Gesetze unterschieden ist, ist nämlich ein Inhalt und gleichfalls ein vom Inhalte des Gesetzes unterschiedener. Denn die Existenz ist als Unmittelbarkeit überhaupt gleichfalls ein mit sich Identisches der Materie und Form, das gegen seine Formbestimmungen gleichgültig und daher Inhalt ist; sie ist die Dingheit mit ihren Eigenschaften und Materien. Aber sie ist der Inhalt, dessen selbstständige Unmittelbarkeit zugleich nur als ein Nichtbestehen ist. Die Identität desselben mit sich in diesem seinem Nichtbestehen aber ist der andere, wesentliche Inhalt. Diese Identität, die Grundlage der Erscheinung, welche das Gesetz ausmacht, ist ihr eigenes Moment; es ist die positive Seite der Wesentlichkeit, wodurch die Existenz Erscheinung ist.\n\nDas Gesetz ist daher nicht jenseits der Erscheinung, sondern in ihr unmittelbar gegenwärtig; das Reich der Gesetze ist das ruhige Abbild der existirenden oder erscheinenden Welt. Aber vielmehr ist beides Eine Totalität, und die existirende Welt ist selbst das Reich der Gesetze, das als das einfache Identische, zugleich als in dem Gesetztseyn oder in der sich selbstauflösenden Selbstständigkeit der Existenz identisch mit sich ist. Die Existenz geht in das Gesetz als in ihren Grund zurück; die Erscheinung enthält dieß Beides, den einfachen Grund, und die auflösende Bewegung des erscheinenden Universums, deren Wesentlichkeit er ist.\n\n3. Das Gesetz ist also die wesentliche Erscheinung; es ist die Reflexion derselben in sich in ihrem Gesetztseyn, der identische Inhalt seiner und der unwesentlichen Existenz. Erstlich ist nun diese Identität des Gesetzes mit seiner Existenz nur erst die unmittelbare, einfache Identität, und das Gesetz ist gleichgültig gegen seine Existenz; die Erscheinung hat noch einen andern Inhalt gegen den Inhalt des Gesetzes. Jener ist zwar der unwesentliche, und das Zurückgehen in diesen; aber für das Gesetz ist er ein Erstes, das nicht durch dieses gesetzt ist; er ist daher als Inhalt äußerlich mit dem Gesetze verbunden. Die Erscheinung ist eine Menge näherer Bestimmungen, die dem Diesen oder dem Konkreten angehören und nicht im Gesetze enthalten, sondern durch ein Anderes bestimmt sind. —Zweitens das, was die Erscheinung von dem Gesetze Verschiedenes enthält, bestimmte sich als ein Positives oder als ein anderer Inhalt; aber es ist wesentlich ein Negatives; es ist die Form und ihre Bewegung als solche, die der Erscheinung zukommt. Das Reich der Gesetze ist der ruhige Inhalt der Erscheinung; diese ist derselbe aber sich im unruhigen Wechsel und als die Reflexion in anderes darstellend. Sie ist das Gesetz als die negative sich schlechthin verändernde Existenz, die Bewegung des Übergehens in Entgegengesetzte, des sich Aufhebens und des Zurückgehens in die Einheit. Diese Seite der unruhigen Form oder der Negativität enthält das Gesetz nicht; die Erscheinung ist daher gegen das Gesetz die Totalität, denn sie enthält das Gesetz, aber auch noch mehr, nämlich das Moment der sich selbst bewegenden Form.—Dieser Mangel ist drittens am Gesetze so vorhanden, daß dessen Inhalt nur erst ein verschiedener, damit ein gegen sich gleichgültiger ist; daher die Identität seiner Seiten miteinander nur erst eine unmittelbare und damit innere, oder noch nicht nothwendige ist. Im Gesetze sind zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen als wesentlich verbunden (z.B. im Gesetze der Bewegung des Falls die Raumgröße und die Zeitgröße; die durchloffenen Räume verhalten sich wie die Quadrate der verflossenen Zeiten); sie sind verbunden; diese Beziehung ist nur erst eine unmittelbare. Sie ist daher gleichfalls nur erst eine gesetzte, wie in der Erscheinung das Unmittelbare überhaupt die Bedeutung des Gesetztseyns erhalten bat. Die wesentliche Einheit der beiden Seiten des Gesetzes wäre ihre Negativität, daß nämlich die eine an ihr selbst ihre andere enthielte; aber diese wesentliche Einheit ist noch nicht am Gesetze hervorgetreten. (—So ist es nicht im Begriffe des im Falle durchloffenen Raumes enthalten, daß ihm die Zeit als Quadrat entspricht. Weil der Fall eine sinnliche Bewegung ist, ist er die Beziehung von Zeit und Raum; aber erstens liegt es in der Bestimmung der Zeit selbst nicht,—d. h. wie die Zeit nach ihrer Vorstellung genommen wird, daß sie sich auf den Raum bezieht, und umgekehrt; man sagt, man könne sich die Zeit sehr wohl ohne den Raum und den Raum ohne die Zeit vorstellen; das eine tritt also äußerlich zu dem andern hinzu, welche äußerliche Beziehung die Bewegung ist. Zweitens ist die nähere Bestimmung gleichgültig, nach welchen Größen sich in der Bewegung Raum und Zeit zu einander verhalten. Das Gesetz hierüber wird aus der Erfahrung erkannt; insofern ist es nur unmittelbar; es erfordert noch einen Beweis, d. h. eine Vermittelung, für das Erkennen, daß das Gesetz nicht nur Statt hat, sondern nothwendig ist; diesen Beweis und seine objektive Nothwendigkeit enthält das Gesetz als solches nicht.—) Das Gesetz ist daher nur die positive Wesentlichkeit der Erscheinung, nicht ihre negative, nach welcher die Inhaltsbestimmungen Momente der Form sind, als solche in ihr Anderes übergehen, und an ihnen selbst ebenso sehr nicht sie, sondern ihr anderes sind. Im Gesetze ist also zwar das Gesetztseyn der einen Seite desselben das Gesetztseyn der andern; aber ihr Inhalt ist gleichgültig gegen diese Beziehung, er enthält nicht an ihm selbst dieß Gesetztseyn. Das Gesetz ist daher wohl die wesentliche Form, aber noch nicht die in ihre Seiten als Inhalt reflektirte, reale Form.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0001","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Die Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"143.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0002","text":"Die Existenz ist die Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, zu der sich das Wesen wieder hergestellt hat. Diese Unmittelbarkeit ist an sich die Reflexion des Wesens in sich. Das Wesen ist als Existenz aus seinem Grunde heraufgetreten, der selbst in sie übergegangen ist. Die Existenz ist diese reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, insofern sie an ihr selbst die absolute Negativität ist. Sie ist nunmehr auch als dieß gesetzt, indem sie sich als Erscheinung bestimmt hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"143.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0003","text":"Die Erscheinung ist daher zunächst das Wesen in seiner Existenz; das Wesen ist unmittelbar an ihr vorhanden. Daß sie nicht als unmittelbare, sondern die reflektirte Existenz ist, dieß macht das Moment des Wesens an ihr aus; oder die Existenz als wesentliche Existenz ist Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"143.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0004","text":"Es ist etwas nur Erscheinung,—in dem Sinne, daß die Existenz als solche nur ein Gesetztes, nicht an- und für-sich-Seyendes ist. Dieß macht ihre Wesentlichkeit aus, an ihr selbst die Negativität der Reflexion, die Natur des Wesens, zu haben. Es ist dieß nicht eine fremde, äußerliche Reflexion, welcher das Wesen zugehörte, und die durch Vergleichung desselben mit der Existenz diese für Erscheinung erklärte. Sondern, wie sich ergeben hat, ist diese Wesentlichkeit der Existenz, Erscheinung zu seyn, die eigne Wahrheit der Existenz. Die Reflexion, wodurch sie dieß ist, gehört ihr selbst an.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"143.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0005","text":"Wenn aber gesagt wird, Etwas sey nur Erscheinung in dem Sinne, als ob dagegen die unmittelbare Existenz die Wahrheit wäre; so ist vielmehr die Erscheinung die höhere Wahrheit; denn sie ist die Existenz wie sie als wesentliche, da hingegen die Existenz die noch wesenlose Erscheinung ist; weil sie nur das eine Moment der Erscheinung, nämlich die Existenz als unmittelbare, noch nicht ihre negative Reflexion, an ihr hat. Wenn die Erscheinung wesenlos genannt wird, so wird an das Moment ihrer Negativität so gedacht, als ob das Unmittelbare dagegen das Positive und Wahrhafte wäre; aber vielmehr enthält dieß Unmittelbare die wesentliche Wahrheit noch nicht an ihm. Die Existenz hört vielmehr auf, wesenlos zu seyn, darin, daß sie in Erscheinung übergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"143.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0006","text":"Das Wesen scheint zunächst in ihm selbst, in seiner einfachen Identität; so ist es die abstrakte Reflexion, die reine Bewegung von Nichts durch Nichts zu sich selbst zurück. Das Wesen erscheint, so ist es nunmehr realer Schein, indem die Momente des Scheins Existenz haben. Die Erscheinung ist, wie sich ergeben hat, das Ding als die negative Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst; die Unterschiede, welche es enthält, sind selbstständige Materien, die der Widerspruch sind, ein unmittelbares Bestehen zu seyn, und zugleich nur in fremder Selbstständigkeit also in der Negation der eigenen ihr Bestehen zu haben, und wieder eben darum auch nur in der Negation jener fremden oder in der Negation ihrer eigenen Negation. Der Schein ist dieselbe Vermittelung, aber seine haltlosen Momente haben in der Erscheinung die Gestalt unmittelbarer Selbstständigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"143.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0007","text":"Dagegen ist die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit, die der Existenz zukommt, ihrer Seits zum Momente herabgesetzt. Die Erscheinung ist daher Einheit des Scheins und der Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"143.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0008","text":"Die Erscheinung bestimmt sich nun näher. Sie ist die wesentliche Existenz; die Wesentlichkeit derselben unterscheidet sich von ihr als unwesentlicher und diese beiden Seiten treten in Beziehung mit einander.—Sie ist daher zuerst einfache Identität mit sich, die zugleich verschiedene Inhaltsbestimmungen enthält, welche sowohl selbst als deren Beziehung das im Wechsel der Erscheinung sich gleich bleibende ist; das Gesetz der Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"143.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0009","text":"Zweitens aber geht das in seiner Verschiedenheit einfache Gesetz in den Gegensatz über; das Wesentliche der Erscheinung wird ihr selbst entgegengesetzt und der erscheinenden Welt tritt die an sich seyende Welt gegenüber.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"143.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0010","text":"Drittens geht dieser Gegensatz in seinen Grund zurück; das Ansichseyende ist in der Erscheinung und umgekehrt ist das Erscheinende bestimmt als in sein Ansichseyn aufgenommen; die Erscheinung wird Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"143.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0011","text":"## A. Das Gesetz der Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"143.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0012","text":"1. Die Erscheinung ist das Existirende vermittelt durch seine Negation, welche sein Bestehen ausmacht. Diese seine Negation ist zwar ein anderes Selbstständiges; aber dieß ist ebenso wesentlich ein aufgehobenes. Das Existirende ist daher die Rückkehr seiner in sich selbst durch seine Negation und durch die Negation dieser seiner Negation; es hat also wesentliche Selbstständigkeit; so wie es gleich unmittelbar schlechthin Gesetztseyn ist, das einen Grund und ein Anderes zu seinem Bestehen hat.—Fürs Erste ist also die Erscheinung die Existenz zugleich mit ihrer Wesentlichkeit, das Gesetztseyn mit seinem Grunde; aber dieser Grund ist die Negation; und das andere Selbstständige, der Grund des ersten, ist gleichfalls nur ein Gesetztseyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"143.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0013","text":"Oder das Existirende ist als Erscheinendes in ein Anderes reflektirt und hat es zu seinem Grunde, welches selbst nur dieß ist, in ein Anderes reflektirt zu seyn. Die wesentliche Selbstständigkeit, die ihm zukommt, weil es Rückkehr in sich selbst ist, ist um der Negativität der Momente willen, die Rückkehr des Nichts durch Nichts zu sich selbst zurück; die Selbstständigkeit des Existirenden ist daher nur der wesentliche Schein. Der Zusammenhang des sich gegenseitig begründenden Existirenden besteht darum in dieser gegenseitigen Negation, daß das Bestehen des einen nicht das Bestehen des andern, sondern dessen Gesetztseyn ist, welche Beziehung des Gesetztseyns allein ihr Bestehen ausmacht. Der Grund ist vorhanden, wie er in seiner Wahrheit ist, nämlich ein Erstes zu seyn, das nur ein Vorausgesetztes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"143.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0014","text":"Dieß macht nun die negative Seite der Erscheinung aus. Aber in dieser negativen Vermittelung ist unmittelbar die positive Identität des Existirenden mit sich enthalten. Denn es ist nicht Gesetztseyn gegen einen wesentlichen Grund, oder ist nicht der Schein an einem Selbstständigen; sondern ist Gesetztseyn, das sich auf ein Gesetztseyn bezieht, oder ist ein Schein nur in einem Scheine. Es bezieht sich in dieser seiner Negation oder in seinem Andern, das selbst ein Aufgehobenes ist, auf sich selbst; ist also mit sich identische oder positive Wesentlichkeit.—Dieses Identische ist nicht die Unmittelbarkeit, die der Existenz als solcher zukommt, und nur das Unwesentliche ist, sein Bestehen in einem Andern zu haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"143.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0015","text":"Sondern es ist der wesentliche Inhalt der Erscheinung, welcher zwei Seiten hat, erstens in der Form des Gesetztseyns oder der äußerlichen Unmittelbarkeit, zweitens das Gesetztseyn als mit sich Identisches zu seyn. Nach der ersten Seite ist er als ein Daseyn, aber als ein zufälliges, unwesentliches, das nach seiner Unmittelbarkeit dem Übergehen, Entstehen und Vergehen unterworfen ist. Nach der andern Seite ist er die einfache jenem Wechsel entnommene Inhaltsbestimmung, das Bleibende desselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"143.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0016","text":"Außerdem daß dieser Inhalt überhaupt das Einfache des Vergänglichen ist, ist er auch bestimmter, in sich verschiedener Inhalt. Er ist die Reflexion der Erscheinung, des negativen Daseyns, in sich, enthält also die Bestimmtheit wesentlich. Die Erscheinung aber ist die seyende vielfache Verschiedenheit, die sich in unwesentlicher Mannigfaltigkeit herumwirft; ihr reflektirter Inhalt dagegen ist ihre Mannigfaltigkeit auf den einfachen Unterschied reducirt. Der bestimmte wesentliche Inhalt ist nämlich näher, nicht nur bestimmt überhaupt, sondern als das Wesentliche der Erscheinung die vollständige Bestimmtheit; eines und sein Anderes. In der Erscheinung hat jedes dieser beiden sein Bestehen so in dem Andern, daß es zugleich nur in dessen Nichtbestehen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"143.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0017","text":"Dieser Widerspruch hebt sich auf; und die Reflexion desselben in sich, ist die Identität ihres beiderseitigen Bestehens, daß das Gesetztseyn des einen auch das Gesetztseyn des Andern ist. Sie machen Ein Bestehen aus, zugleich als verschiedener, gegen einander gleichgültiger Inhalt. In der wesentlichen Seite der Erscheinung ist somit das Negative des unwesentlichen Inhalts, sich aufzuheben, in die Identität zurückgegangen; er ist ein gleichgültiges Bestehen, welches nicht das Aufgehobenseyn, sondern vielmehr das Bestehen des Andern ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"143.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0018","text":"Diese Einheit ist das Gesetz der Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"143.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0019","text":"2. Das Gesetz ist also das Positive der Vermittelung des Erscheinenden. Die Erscheinung ist zunächst die Existenz als die negative Vermittelung mit sich, so daß das Existirende durch sein eigenes Nichtbestehen, durch ein Anderes, und wieder durch das Nichtbestehen dieses Andern mit sich vermittelt ist. Darin ist enthalten erstens das bloße Scheinen und das Verschwinden beider, die unwesentliche Erscheinung; zweitens auch das Bleiben oder das Gesetz; denn jedes der beiden existirt in jenem Aufheben des Andern; und ihr Gesetztseyn als ihre Negativität ist zugleich das identische, positive Gesetztseyn beider.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"143.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0020","text":"Dieß bleibende Bestehen, welches die Erscheinung im Gesetze hat, ist somit, wie es sich bestimmt hat, erstlich entgegengesetzt der Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns, welche die Existenz hat. Diese Unmittelbarkeit ist zwar an sich die reflektirte, nämlich der in sich zurückgegangene Grund; aber in der Erscheinung ist nun diese einfache Unmittelbarkeit von der reflektirten unterschieden, welche im Dinge erst sich zu trennen anfingen. Das existirende Ding ist in seiner Auflösung dieser Gegensatz geworden; das Positive seiner Auflösung ist jene Identität des Erscheinenden als Gesetztseyns mit sich in seinem andern Gesetztseyn.—Zweitens ist diese reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit selbst bestimmt als das Gesetztseyn, gegen die seyende Unmittelbarkeit der Existenz. Dieß Gesetztseyn ist nunmehr das Wesentliche, und wahrhaft Positive. Der deutsche Ausdruck Gesetz enthält diese Bestimmung gleichfalls.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"143.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0021","text":"In diesem Gesetztseyn liegt die wesentliche Beziehung der beiden Seiten des Unterschiedes, die das Gesetz enthält; sie sind verschiedener gegen einander unmittelbarer Inhalt und sind dieß als die Reflexion des der Erscheinung angehörigen, verschwindenden Inhalts. Als wesentliche Verschiedenheit, sind die Verschiedenen einfache sich auf sich beziehende Inhaltsbestimmungen. Aber ebenso sehr ist keine für sich unmittelbar, sondern jede ist wesentlich Gesetztseyn, oder ist nur, insofern die andere ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"143.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0022","text":"Drittens Erscheinung und Gesetz haben einen und denselben Inhalt. Das Gesetz ist die Reflexion der Erscheinung in die Identität mit sich; so steht die Erscheinung als das nichtige Unmittelbare dem Insichreflektirten gegenüber, und sie sind nach dieser Form unterschieden. Aber die Reflexion der Erscheinung, wodurch dieser Unterschied ist, ist auch die wesentliche Identität der Erscheinung selbst und ihrer Reflexion, was überhaupt die Natur der Reflexion ist; sie ist das im Gesetztseyn identische mit sich, und gleichgültig gegen jenen Unterschied, welcher die Form oder das Gesetztseyn ist; also ein Inhalt, der sich aus der Erscheinung in das Gesetz kontinuirt, der Inhalt des Gesetzes, und der Erscheinung.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"143.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0023","text":"Dieser Inhalt macht hiermit die Grundlage der Erscheinung aus; das Gesetz ist diese Grundlage selbst, die Erscheinung ist derselbe Inhalt, aber enthält noch mehr, nämlich den unwesentlichen Inhalt ihres unmittelbaren Seyns. Auch die Formbestimmung, wodurch die Erscheinung als solche von dem Gesetze unterschieden ist, ist nämlich ein Inhalt und gleichfalls ein vom Inhalte des Gesetzes unterschiedener. Denn die Existenz ist als Unmittelbarkeit überhaupt gleichfalls ein mit sich Identisches der Materie und Form, das gegen seine Formbestimmungen gleichgültig und daher Inhalt ist; sie ist die Dingheit mit ihren Eigenschaften und Materien. Aber sie ist der Inhalt, dessen selbstständige Unmittelbarkeit zugleich nur als ein Nichtbestehen ist. Die Identität desselben mit sich in diesem seinem Nichtbestehen aber ist der andere, wesentliche Inhalt.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"143.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0024","text":"Diese Identität, die Grundlage der Erscheinung, welche das Gesetz ausmacht, ist ihr eigenes Moment; es ist die positive Seite der Wesentlichkeit, wodurch die Existenz Erscheinung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"143.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0025","text":"Das Gesetz ist daher nicht jenseits der Erscheinung, sondern in ihr unmittelbar gegenwärtig; das Reich der Gesetze ist das ruhige Abbild der existirenden oder erscheinenden Welt. Aber vielmehr ist beides Eine Totalität, und die existirende Welt ist selbst das Reich der Gesetze, das als das einfache Identische, zugleich als in dem Gesetztseyn oder in der sich selbstauflösenden Selbstständigkeit der Existenz identisch mit sich ist. Die Existenz geht in das Gesetz als in ihren Grund zurück; die Erscheinung enthält dieß Beides, den einfachen Grund, und die auflösende Bewegung des erscheinenden Universums, deren Wesentlichkeit er ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"143.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0026","text":"3. Das Gesetz ist also die wesentliche Erscheinung; es ist die Reflexion derselben in sich in ihrem Gesetztseyn, der identische Inhalt seiner und der unwesentlichen Existenz. Erstlich ist nun diese Identität des Gesetzes mit seiner Existenz nur erst die unmittelbare, einfache Identität, und das Gesetz ist gleichgültig gegen seine Existenz; die Erscheinung hat noch einen andern Inhalt gegen den Inhalt des Gesetzes. Jener ist zwar der unwesentliche, und das Zurückgehen in diesen; aber für das Gesetz ist er ein Erstes, das nicht durch dieses gesetzt ist; er ist daher als Inhalt äußerlich mit dem Gesetze verbunden. Die Erscheinung ist eine Menge näherer Bestimmungen, die dem Diesen oder dem Konkreten angehören und nicht im Gesetze enthalten, sondern durch ein Anderes bestimmt sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"143.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0027","text":"—Zweitens das, was die Erscheinung von dem Gesetze Verschiedenes enthält, bestimmte sich als ein Positives oder als ein anderer Inhalt; aber es ist wesentlich ein Negatives; es ist die Form und ihre Bewegung als solche, die der Erscheinung zukommt. Das Reich der Gesetze ist der ruhige Inhalt der Erscheinung; diese ist derselbe aber sich im unruhigen Wechsel und als die Reflexion in anderes darstellend. Sie ist das Gesetz als die negative sich schlechthin verändernde Existenz, die Bewegung des Übergehens in Entgegengesetzte, des sich Aufhebens und des Zurückgehens in die Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"143.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0028","text":"Diese Seite der unruhigen Form oder der Negativität enthält das Gesetz nicht; die Erscheinung ist daher gegen das Gesetz die Totalität, denn sie enthält das Gesetz, aber auch noch mehr, nämlich das Moment der sich selbst bewegenden Form.—Dieser Mangel ist drittens am Gesetze so vorhanden, daß dessen Inhalt nur erst ein verschiedener, damit ein gegen sich gleichgültiger ist; daher die Identität seiner Seiten miteinander nur erst eine unmittelbare und damit innere, oder noch nicht nothwendige ist. Im Gesetze sind zwei Inhaltsbestimmungen als wesentlich verbunden (z.B. im Gesetze der Bewegung des Falls die Raumgröße und die Zeitgröße; die durchloffenen Räume verhalten sich wie die Quadrate der verflossenen Zeiten); sie sind verbunden; diese Beziehung ist nur erst eine unmittelbare.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"143.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0029","text":"Sie ist daher gleichfalls nur erst eine gesetzte, wie in der Erscheinung das Unmittelbare überhaupt die Bedeutung des Gesetztseyns erhalten bat. Die wesentliche Einheit der beiden Seiten des Gesetzes wäre ihre Negativität, daß nämlich die eine an ihr selbst ihre andere enthielte; aber diese wesentliche Einheit ist noch nicht am Gesetze hervorgetreten. (—So ist es nicht im Begriffe des im Falle durchloffenen Raumes enthalten, daß ihm die Zeit als Quadrat entspricht. Weil der Fall eine sinnliche Bewegung ist, ist er die Beziehung von Zeit und Raum; aber erstens liegt es in der Bestimmung der Zeit selbst nicht,—d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"143.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0030","text":"wie die Zeit nach ihrer Vorstellung genommen wird, daß sie sich auf den Raum bezieht, und umgekehrt; man sagt, man könne sich die Zeit sehr wohl ohne den Raum und den Raum ohne die Zeit vorstellen; das eine tritt also äußerlich zu dem andern hinzu, welche äußerliche Beziehung die Bewegung ist. Zweitens ist die nähere Bestimmung gleichgültig, nach welchen Größen sich in der Bewegung Raum und Zeit zu einander verhalten. Das Gesetz hierüber wird aus der Erfahrung erkannt; insofern ist es nur unmittelbar; es erfordert noch einen Beweis, d. h.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"143.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0031","text":"eine Vermittelung, für das Erkennen, daß das Gesetz nicht nur Statt hat, sondern nothwendig ist; diesen Beweis und seine objektive Nothwendigkeit enthält das Gesetz als solches nicht.—) Das Gesetz ist daher nur die positive Wesentlichkeit der Erscheinung, nicht ihre negative, nach welcher die Inhaltsbestimmungen Momente der Form sind, als solche in ihr Anderes übergehen, und an ihnen selbst ebenso sehr nicht sie, sondern ihr anderes sind. Im Gesetze ist also zwar das Gesetztseyn der einen Seite desselben das Gesetztseyn der andern; aber ihr Inhalt ist gleichgültig gegen diese Beziehung, er enthält nicht an ihm selbst dieß Gesetztseyn. Das Gesetz ist daher wohl die wesentliche Form, aber noch nicht die in ihre Seiten als Inhalt reflektirte, reale Form.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"143.31"}],"sha256":"cb5cac26fd1e82a4d86f2d9d429dd244bac7aaf0882764b2fe9e709594030325","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105551224819Z_a26a0b58","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Law of Appearance.","source_sha256":"cb5cac26fd1e82a4d86f2d9d429dd244bac7aaf0882764b2fe9e709594030325","sha256":"0fb18cf9d22d71350cf761e42947cb2ab78d52f4198e0d620cd7d17bbdc33b36","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:55:51.224871+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0001","text":"## Second Chapter. Appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"143.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0002","text":"Existence is the immediacy of Being, to which essence has restored itself. This immediacy is in itself the reflection of essence into itself. Essence has emerged as existence from its ground, which has itself passed over into it. Existence is this reflected immediacy, insofar as it is in itself absolute negativity. It is now also posited as such, in that it has determined itself as appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"143.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0003","text":"Appearance is therefore, in the first instance, essence in its existence; essence is immediately present in it. That it is not immediate, but reflected existence, constitutes the moment of essence in it; or existence as essential existence is appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"143.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0004","text":"Something is only appearance—in the sense that existence as such is only a posited, not an in-and-for-itself being. This constitutes its essentiality: to have in itself the negativity of reflection, the nature of essence. This is not an alien, external reflection to which essence belonged, and which, by comparing it with existence, declared the latter to be appearance. Rather, as has emerged, this essentiality of existence, to be appearance, is the proper truth of existence. The reflection through which it is this belongs to it itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"143.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0005","text":"But when it is said that something is only appearance in the sense as though immediate existence, by contrast, were the truth, then appearance is rather the higher truth; for it is existence as it is essential, whereas existence is the still essenceless appearance, because it has in it only the one moment of appearance, namely existence as immediate, not yet its negative reflection. When appearance is called essenceless, the moment of its negativity is thought of as though the immediate, by contrast, were the positive and true; but this immediate does not yet contain the essential truth in itself. Existence rather ceases to be essenceless in that it passes over into appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"143.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0006","text":"Essence at first shines within itself, in its simple identity; thus it is abstract reflection, the pure movement from nothing through nothing back to itself. Essence appears; thus it is now real semblance, in that the moments of semblance have existence. Appearance is, as has emerged, the thing as the negative mediation of itself with itself; the differences which it contains are themselves self-subsistent matters, which are the contradiction of being an immediate subsistence and yet of having their subsistence only in alien self-subsistence, hence in the negation of their own, and again, precisely for this reason, only in the negation of that alien self-subsistence, or in the negation of their own negation. Semblance is the same mediation, but its unsubstantial moments have in appearance the form of immediate self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"143.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0007","text":"Conversely, the immediate self-subsistence which belongs to existence is, on its side, reduced to a moment. Appearance is therefore the unity of semblance and existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"143.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0008","text":"Appearance now determines itself more closely. It is essential existence; its essentiality distinguishes itself from it as unessential, and these two sides enter into relation with one another.—It is therefore, first, simple identity with itself, which at the same time contains distinct determinations of content, both these themselves and their relation being what remains identical in the alteration of appearance: the law of appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"143.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0009","text":"But secondly, the law that is simple in its diversity passes over into opposition; the essential of appearance is opposed to appearance itself, and the world that is in itself confronts the appearing world.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"143.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0010","text":"Thirdly, this opposition returns into its ground; that which is in itself is in appearance, and conversely the appearing is determined as taken up into its being-in-itself; appearance becomes relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"143.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0011","text":"## A. The Law of Appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"143.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0012","text":"1. Appearance is the existent mediated through its negation, which constitutes its subsistence. This its negation is indeed another self-subsistent; but this is just as essentially a sublated one. The existent is therefore the return of itself into itself through its negation and through the negation of this its negation; it thus has essential self-subsistence; just as it is equally immediately and absolutely positedness, which has a ground and an other for its subsistence.—Thus, in the first place, appearance is existence together with its essentiality, positedness together with its ground; but this ground is negation; and the other self-subsistent, the ground of the first, is likewise only a positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"143.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0013","text":"Or the existent, as appearing, is reflected into an other and has this as its ground, which itself is only this, to be reflected into an other. The essential self-subsistence which belongs to it because it is return into itself is, on account of the negativity of the moments, the return of nothing through nothing back to itself; the self-subsistence of the existent is therefore only essential semblance. The connection of the existents which mutually ground one another consists therefore in this reciprocal negation: that the subsistence of the one is not the subsistence of the other, but its positedness; this relation of positedness alone constitutes their subsistence. The ground is present as it is in its truth, namely as a first which is only a presupposed.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"143.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0014","text":"This now constitutes the negative side of appearance. But in this negative mediation the positive identity of the existent with itself is immediately contained. For it is not positedness over against an essential ground, or semblance in a self-subsistent; rather, it is positedness that relates itself to a positedness, or is semblance only in a semblance. In this its negation, or in its other, which is itself a sublated, it relates itself to itself; it is thus essentiality identical with itself, or positive essentiality.—This identical is not the immediacy which belongs to existence as such and is only the unessential, namely to have its subsistence in an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"143.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0015","text":"Rather, it is the essential content of appearance, which has two sides: first, in the form of positedness or external immediacy; second, to be positedness as identical with itself. According to the first side, it is a determinate being, but a contingent, unessential one, which according to its immediacy is subject to transition, coming-to-be, and passing-away. According to the other side, it is the simple determination of content withdrawn from that alteration, its enduring element.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"143.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0016","text":"Besides being in general the simple element of the transitory, this content is also more determinate, a content differentiated within itself. It is the reflection of appearance, of negative determinate being, into itself; it thus essentially contains determinacy. Appearance, however, is the being manifold diversity that casts itself about in unessential multiplicity; its reflected content, by contrast, is its multiplicity reduced to simple difference. More precisely, the determinate essential content is not only determinate in general, but, as the essential of appearance, is complete determinacy: one and its other. In appearance each of these two has its subsistence in the other in such a way that it is at the same time only in the non-subsistence of the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"143.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0017","text":"This contradiction sublates itself; and its reflection into itself is the identity of their reciprocal subsistence: that the positedness of the one is also the positedness of the other. They constitute one subsistence, while at the same time they are distinct contents indifferent to one another. Thus, on the essential side of appearance, the negative of the unessential content, namely to sublate itself, has returned into identity; it is an indifferent subsistence which is not sublatedness, but rather the subsistence of the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"143.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0018","text":"This unity is the law of appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"143.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0019","text":"2. The law is thus the positive of the mediation of the appearing. Appearance is at first existence as negative mediation with itself, so that the existent is mediated with itself through its own non-subsistence, through an other, and again through the non-subsistence of this other. This contains, first, the mere shining and vanishing of both, unessential appearance; secondly, also their enduring, or the law; for each of the two exists in that sublating of the other, and their positedness as their negativity is at the same time the identical, positive positedness of both.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"143.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0020","text":"This enduring subsistence which appearance has in the law is thus, as it has determined itself, first opposed to the immediacy of Being which existence has. This immediacy is indeed in itself the reflected, namely the ground which has returned into itself; but in appearance this simple immediacy is now distinguished from the reflected immediacy, which only began to separate in the thing. In its dissolution, the existing thing has become this opposition; the positive of its dissolution is that identity of the appearing as positedness with itself in its other positedness.—Secondly, this reflected immediacy is itself determined as positedness, in contrast to the immediate being of existence. This positedness is now the essential and truly positive. The German expression Gesetz likewise contains this determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"143.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0021","text":"In this positedness lies the essential relation of the two sides of difference which the law contains; they are mutually distinct immediate content, and are this as the reflection of the vanishing content belonging to appearance. As essential difference, the different are simple determinations of content relating themselves to themselves. But equally, neither is immediate for itself; rather, each is essentially positedness, or is only insofar as the other is.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"143.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0022","text":"Thirdly, appearance and law have one and the same content. The law is the reflection of appearance into identity with itself; appearance thus stands as the null immediate over against that which is reflected into itself, and they are distinguished according to this form. But the reflection of appearance, through which this difference is, is also the essential identity of appearance itself and of its reflection, which is in general the nature of reflection; it is what is identical with itself in positedness, and indifferent to that difference which is form or positedness; thus a content which continues itself from appearance into law, the content of the law and of appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"143.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0023","text":"This content thereby constitutes the foundation of appearance; the law is this foundation itself, appearance is the same content, but contains still more, namely the unessential content of its immediate being. For the determination of form through which appearance as such is distinguished from the law is likewise a content, and likewise one distinguished from the content of the law. For existence, as immediacy in general, is likewise a self-identical of matter and form, which is indifferent to its determinations of form and hence is content; it is thinghood with its properties and matters. But it is the content whose self-subsistent immediacy is at the same time only a non-subsistence. Its identity with itself in this its non-subsistence, however, is the other, essential content.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"143.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0024","text":"This identity, the foundation of appearance which constitutes the law, is its own moment; it is the positive side of essentiality, through which existence is appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"143.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0025","text":"The law is therefore not beyond appearance, but immediately present within it; the realm of laws is the tranquil image of the existing or appearing world. But rather, both are One Totality, and the existing world is itself the realm of laws, which, as the simple identical, is at the same time identical with itself in posited-being or in the self-dissolving self-subsistence of existence. Existence returns into the law as into its ground; appearance contains both of these, the simple ground and the dissolving movement of the appearing universe, whose essentiality it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"143.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0026","text":"3. The law is thus essential appearance; it is the reflection of the latter into itself in its posited-being, the identical content of itself and of unessential existence. To begin with, this identity of the law with its existence is only immediate, simple identity, and the law is indifferent to its existence; appearance still has another content as against the content of the law. That content is indeed the unessential one, and [appearance is] the returning into it; but for the law it is a first, which is not posited by the latter; it is therefore connected with the law externally as content. Appearance is a multitude of more determinate determinations, which belong to this or to the concrete and are not contained in the law, but are determined by something other.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"143.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0027","text":"—Secondly, that which appearance contains as distinct from the law determined itself as a positive, or as another content; but it is essentially a negative; it is form and its movement as such, which belong to appearance. The realm of laws is the tranquil content of appearance; appearance is the same content, but presenting itself in restless alternation and as reflection into another. It is the law as negative existence, absolutely changing itself, the movement of passing over into opposites, of sublating itself and returning into unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"143.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0028","text":"This side of restless form, or of negativity, is not contained in the law; appearance is therefore, as against the law, the totality, for it contains the law, but also something more, namely the moment of self-moving form.—Thirdly, this deficiency is present in the law in such a way that its content is at first only a diverse, and thus an indifferent content with respect to itself; hence the identity of its sides with one another is at first only immediate and thus inward, or not yet necessary. In the law two determinations of content are essentially connected (e.g. in the law of the motion of falling, the magnitude of space and the magnitude of time; the distances traversed are related as the squares of the times elapsed); they are connected; this relation is at first only immediate.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"143.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0029","text":"It is therefore likewise only a posited one, just as in appearance the immediate in general has received the significance of posited-being. The essential unity of the two sides of the law would be their negativity, namely, that the one contained the other within itself; but this essential unity has not yet emerged in the law. (—Thus it is not contained in the concept of the space traversed in falling that time corresponds to it as a square. Because falling is a sensible movement, it is the relation of time and space; but, first, it does not lie in the determination of time itself—not, that is to say,","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"143.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0030","text":"as time is taken according to its representation—that it relates itself to space, and conversely; one says that one can quite well represent time without space and space without time; thus the one is added externally to the other, which external relation is movement. Secondly, the more determinate specification according to what magnitudes space and time are related to one another in movement is indifferent. The law concerning this is cognized from experience; insofar, it is only immediate; it still requires a proof, i.e.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"143.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0031","text":"a mediation, for cognition, that the law not only obtains, but is necessary; this proof and its objective necessity the law as such does not contain.—) The law is therefore only the positive essentiality of appearance, not its negative essentiality, according to which the determinations of content are moments of form, as such pass over into their other, and in themselves are just as much not themselves but their other. In the law, therefore, the posited-being of one side of it is indeed the posited-being of the other; but its content is indifferent to this relation; it does not contain this posited-being within itself. The law is thus indeed the essential form, but not yet the real form reflected into its sides as content.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"143.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DGDE:P0031"]}],"source_digest":"5c184e3a3da588a465b5a2a9491b4a8fe28410821d97fa8a701d52522516e937","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Gesetz der Erscheinung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Gesetz der Erscheinung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3","title":"B. The World of Appearance and the World-in-Itself.","order":144,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BD_3","text":"I. Die existirende Welt erhebt sich ruhig zu einem Reiche von Gesetzen; der nichtige Inhalt ihres mannigfaltigen Daseyns hat in einem Andern sein Bestehen; sein Bestehen ist daher seine Auflösung. Aber in diesem Andern geht das Erscheinende auch mit sich selbst zusammen; so ist die Erscheinung in ihrem Wandel auch ein Bleiben, und ihr Gesetztseyn ist Gesetz. Das Gesetz ist diese einfache Identität der Erscheinung mit sich; daher die Grundlage, nicht der Grund derselben; denn es ist nicht die negative Einheit der Erscheinung; sondern als ihre einfache Identität, die unmittelbare als abstrakte Einheit, neben welcher daher auch der andre Inhalt derselben Statt hat. Der Inhalt ist dieser, hängt in sich zusammen, oder hat seine negative Reflexion innerhalb seiner selbst. Er ist in ein anderes reflektirt; dieß Andere ist selbst eine Existenz der Erscheinung; die erscheinenden Dinge haben ihre Gründe und Bedingungen an andern erscheinenden Dingen.\n\nIn der That aber ist das Gesetz auch das Andere der Erscheinung als solcher, und ihre negative Reflexion als in ihr Anderes. Der Inhalt der Erscheinung, der vom Inhalt des Gesetzes verschieden ist, ist das Existirende, das seine Negativität zu seinem Grunde hat oder in sein Nichtseyn reflektirt ist. Aber dieß Andere, das auch ein Existirendes ist, ist gleichfalls ein solches in sein Nichtseyn Reflektirtes; es ist also dasselbe, und das Erscheinende ist darin in der That nicht in ein anderes, sondern in sich reflektirt; eben diese Reflexion des Gesetztseyns in sich ist das Gesetz. Aber als Erscheinendes ist es wesentlich in sein Nichtseyn reflektirt, oder seine Identität ist selbst wesentlich ebenso sehr seine Negativität und sein Anderes. Die Reflexion-in-sich der Erscheinung, das Gesetz, ist also auch nicht nur ihre identische Grundlage, sondern sie hat an ihm ihren Gegensatz, und es ist ihre negative Einheit.\n\nDadurch hat sich nun die Bestimmung des Gesetzes an ihm selbst verändert.\n\nZunächst ist es nur ein verschiedener Inhalt, und die formale Reflexion des Gesetztseyns in sich, so daß das Gesetztseyn der einen seiner Seiten das Gesetztseyn der andern ist. Weil es aber auch die negative Reflexion in sich ist, so verhalten sich seine Seiten nicht nur als verschiedene, sondern als negativ sich auf einander beziehende.—Oder das Gesetz bloß für sich betrachtet, so sind die Seiten seines Inhalts gleichgültige gegen einander; aber ebenso sehr sind sie durch ihre Identität aufgehobene; das Gesetztseyn der einen ist das Gesetztseyn der andern; also ist das Bestehen einer jeden auch das Nichtbestehen ihrer selbst. Dieß Gesetztseyn der einen in der andern ist ihre negative Einheit und jedes ist nicht nur das Gesetztseyn ihrer, sondern auch der andern, oder jede ist selbst diese negative Einheit. Die positive Identität, welche sie im Gesetze als solchem haben, ist nur erst ihre innere Einheit, welche des Beweises und der Vermittelung bedarf, weil diese negative Einheit noch nicht an ihnen gesetzt ist. Aber indem die verschiedenen Seiten des Gesetzes nunmehr bestimmt sind, als in ihrer negativen Einheit verschiedene zu seyn, oder als solche, deren jedes sein Anderes an ihm selbst enthält und zugleich als Selbstständiges dieß sein Andersseyn von sich abstößt, so ist die Identität des Gesetzes nunmehr auch eine gesetzte und reale.\n\nDamit hat also das Gesetz das mangelnde Moment der negativen Form seiner Seiten gleichfalls erhalten; das Moment, das vorhin noch der Erscheinung angehörte; die Existenz ist somit vollständig in sich zurückgegangen, und hat sich in ihr absolutes an- und für-sichseyendes Andersseyn reflektirt. Das, was vorher Gesetz war, ist daher nicht mehr nur Eine Seite des Ganzen, dessen andere die Erscheinung als solche war, sondern ist selbst das Ganze. Sie ist die wesentliche Totalität der Erscheinung, so daß sie nun auch das Moment der Unwesentlichkeit, das noch dieser zukam, enthält; aber als die reflektirte, an sich seyende Unwesentlichkeit, d. h. als die wesentliche Negativität.—Das Gesetz ist als unmittelbarer Inhalt, bestimmt überhaupt, unterschieden von andern Gesetzen, und es giebt deren eine unbestimmbare Menge. Aber indem es die wesentliche Negativität nun an ihm selbst hat, enthält es nicht mehr eine solche nur gleichgültige, zufällige Inhaltsbestimmung; sondern sein Inhalt ist alle Bestimmtheit überhaupt, in wesentlicher sich zur Totalität machenden Beziehung. So ist die in sich reflektirte Erscheinung nun eine Welt, die sich als an und für sich seyende über der erscheinenden Welt aufthut.\n\nDas Reich der Gesetze enthält nur den einfachen, wandellosen aber verschiedenen Inhalt der existirenden Welt. Indem es nun aber die totale Reflexion von dieser ist, enthält es auch das Moment ihrer wesenlosen Mannigfaltigkeit. Dieses Moment der Veränderlichkeit und Veränderung als in sich reflektirtes, wesentliches, ist die absolute Negativität oder die Form überhaupt als solche, deren Momente aber in der an- und für-sichseyenden Welt die Realität selbstständiger, aber reflektirter Existenz haben; so wie umgekehrt diese reflektirte Selbstständigkeit nunmehr die Form an ihr selbst hat, und dadurch ihr Inhalt nicht ein bloß mannigfaltiger, sondern ein wesentlich mit sich zusammenhängender ist.\n\n—Diese an und für sich seyende Welt heißt auch die übersinnliche Welt; insofern die existirende Welt als sinnliche, nämlich als solche bestimmt wird, die für die Anschauung, das unmittelbare Verhalten des Bewußtseyns, ist.—Die übersinnliche Welt hat gleichfalls Unmittelbarkeit, Existenz, aber reflektirte, wesentliche Existenz. Das Wesen hat noch kein Daseyn; aber es ist, und in tieferem Sinne, als das Seyn; das Ding ist der Beginn der reflektirten Existenz; es ist eine Unmittelbarkeit, die noch nicht gesetzt ist, als wesentliche oder reflektirte; es ist aber in Wahrheit nicht ein seyendes Unmittelbares. Die Dinge erst, als Dinge einer andern, übersinnlichen Welt sind gesetzt, erstens als wahrhafte Existenzen, und zweitens als das Wahre gegen das Seyende;—in ihnen ist es anerkannt, daß es ein von dem unmittelbaren Seyn unterschiedenes Seyn gibt, das wahrhafte Existenz ist. Eines Theils ist in dieser Bestimmung die sinnliche Vorstellung überwunden, welche nur dem unmittelbaren Seyn des Gefühls und der Anschauung Existenz zuschreibt; andern Theils aber auch die bewußtlose Reflexion, welche zwar die Vorstellung von Dingen, Kräften, Innerlichem und so fort hat, ohne zu wissen, daß solche Bestimmungen nicht sinnliche oder seyende Unmittelbarkeiten, sondern reflektirte Existenzen sind.\n\n2. Die an und für sich seyende Welt ist die Totalität der Existenz; es ist nichts Anderes außer ihr. Indem sie aber an ihr selbst die absolute Negativität oder Form ist, so ist ihre Reflexion-in-sich, negative Beziehung auf sich. Sie enthält den Gegensatz, und stößt sich ab in sich als die wesentliche Welt, und in sich als die Welt des Andersseyns oder die Welt der Erscheinung. So ist sie darum, weil sie die Totalität ist, auch nur als eine Seite derselben, und macht in dieser Bestimmung eine gegen die Welt der Erscheinung verschiedene Selbstständigkeit aus. Die erscheinende Welt hat an der wesentlichen Welt ihre negative Einheit, in der sie zu Grunde und in die sie als in ihren Grund zurückgeht. Ferner ist die wesentliche Welt auch der setzende Grund der erscheinenden Welt; denn, die absolute Form in ihrer Wesentlichkeit enthaltend, hebt sich ihre Identität mit sich auf, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn und ist als diese gesetzte Unmittelbarkeit die erscheinende Welt.\n\nSie ist ferner nicht nur überhaupt Grund der erscheinenden Welt, sondern ihr bestimmter Grund. Schon als das Reich der Gesetze ist sie mannigfaltiger Inhalt, und zwar der wesentliche der erscheinenden Welt, und als inhaltsvoller Grund, der bestimmte Grund der andern, aber nur diesem Inhalt nach; denn die erscheinende Welt hatte noch mannigfaltigen andern Inhalt als jenes Reich, weil ihr noch das negative Moment eigenthümlich zukam. Aber indem das Reich der Gesetze dieß Moment nun gleichfalls an ihm hat, so ist es die Totalität des Inhalts der erscheinenden Welt und der Grund aller ihrer Mannigfaltigkeit. Aber sie ist zugleich das negative derselben, so ist die derselben entgegengesetzte Welt.—Nämlich in der Identität beider Welten, und indem die eine der Form nach bestimmt ist, als die wesentliche und die andere als dieselbe aber als gesetzte und unwesentliche, hat sich zwar die Grundbeziehung wieder hergestellt; aber zugleich als die Grundbeziehung der Erscheinung, nämlich als Beziehung nicht eines identischen Inhalts, noch auch eines bloß verschiedenen, wie das Gesetz ist, sondern als totale Beziehung, oder als negative Identität und wesentliche Beziehung des Inhalts als entgegengesetzten.—Das Reich der Gesetze ist nicht nur dieß, daß das Gesetztseyn eines Inhalts das Gesetztseyn eines Andern ist, sondern diese Identität ist wesentlich, wie sich ergeben hat, auch negative Einheit; jede der beiden Seiten des Gesetzes ist in der negativen Einheit an ihr selbst ihr anderer Inhalt; das Andere ist daher nicht unbestimmt ein Anderes überhaupt, sondern es ist ihr Anderes, oder es enthält gleichfalls die Inhaltsbestimmung von jener; so sind die beiden Seiten entgegengesetzte. Indem das Reich der Gesetze nun dieß negative Moment und den Gegensatz an ihm hat, und sich somit als die Totalität, von sich selbst in eine an und für sich seyende und eine erscheinende Welt abstößt, so ist die Identität beider die wesentliche Beziehung der Entgegensetzung.—Die Grundbeziehung als solche ist der in seinem Widerspruch zu Grunde gegangene Gegensatz; und die Existenz der mit sich selbst zusammengehende Grund. Aber die Existenz wird zur Erscheinung; der Grund ist in der Existenz aufgehoben; er stellt sich als Rückkehr der Erscheinung in sich, wieder her; aber zugleich als aufgehobener, nämlich als Grundbeziehung entgegengesetzter Bestimmungen; die Identität solcher aber ist wesentlich Werden und Übergehen, nicht mehr die Grundbeziehung als solche.\n\nDie an und für sich seyende Welt ist also selbst eine in sich in die Totalität des mannigfaltigen Inhalts unterschiedene Welt; sie ist identisch mit der erscheinenden oder gesetzten, insofern Grund derselben, aber ihr identischer Zusammenhang ist zugleich als Entgegensetzung bestimmt, weil die Form der erscheinenden Welt die Reflexion in ihr Andersseyn ist, sie also in der an und für sich seyenden Welt wahrhaft so in sich selbst zurückgegangen ist, als diese ihre entgegengesetzte ist. Die Beziehung ist also bestimmt diese, daß die an und für sich seyende Welt die verkehrte der erscheinenden ist.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0001","text":"I. Die existirende Welt erhebt sich ruhig zu einem Reiche von Gesetzen; der nichtige Inhalt ihres mannigfaltigen Daseyns hat in einem Andern sein Bestehen; sein Bestehen ist daher seine Auflösung. Aber in diesem Andern geht das Erscheinende auch mit sich selbst zusammen; so ist die Erscheinung in ihrem Wandel auch ein Bleiben, und ihr Gesetztseyn ist Gesetz. Das Gesetz ist diese einfache Identität der Erscheinung mit sich; daher die Grundlage, nicht der Grund derselben; denn es ist nicht die negative Einheit der Erscheinung; sondern als ihre einfache Identität, die unmittelbare als abstrakte Einheit, neben welcher daher auch der andre Inhalt derselben Statt hat. Der Inhalt ist dieser, hängt in sich zusammen, oder hat seine negative Reflexion innerhalb seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"144.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0002","text":"Er ist in ein anderes reflektirt; dieß Andere ist selbst eine Existenz der Erscheinung; die erscheinenden Dinge haben ihre Gründe und Bedingungen an andern erscheinenden Dingen.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"144.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0003","text":"In der That aber ist das Gesetz auch das Andere der Erscheinung als solcher, und ihre negative Reflexion als in ihr Anderes. Der Inhalt der Erscheinung, der vom Inhalt des Gesetzes verschieden ist, ist das Existirende, das seine Negativität zu seinem Grunde hat oder in sein Nichtseyn reflektirt ist. Aber dieß Andere, das auch ein Existirendes ist, ist gleichfalls ein solches in sein Nichtseyn Reflektirtes; es ist also dasselbe, und das Erscheinende ist darin in der That nicht in ein anderes, sondern in sich reflektirt; eben diese Reflexion des Gesetztseyns in sich ist das Gesetz. Aber als Erscheinendes ist es wesentlich in sein Nichtseyn reflektirt, oder seine Identität ist selbst wesentlich ebenso sehr seine Negativität und sein Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"144.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0004","text":"Die Reflexion-in-sich der Erscheinung, das Gesetz, ist also auch nicht nur ihre identische Grundlage, sondern sie hat an ihm ihren Gegensatz, und es ist ihre negative Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"144.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0005","text":"Dadurch hat sich nun die Bestimmung des Gesetzes an ihm selbst verändert.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"144.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0006","text":"Zunächst ist es nur ein verschiedener Inhalt, und die formale Reflexion des Gesetztseyns in sich, so daß das Gesetztseyn der einen seiner Seiten das Gesetztseyn der andern ist. Weil es aber auch die negative Reflexion in sich ist, so verhalten sich seine Seiten nicht nur als verschiedene, sondern als negativ sich auf einander beziehende.—Oder das Gesetz bloß für sich betrachtet, so sind die Seiten seines Inhalts gleichgültige gegen einander; aber ebenso sehr sind sie durch ihre Identität aufgehobene; das Gesetztseyn der einen ist das Gesetztseyn der andern; also ist das Bestehen einer jeden auch das Nichtbestehen ihrer selbst. Dieß Gesetztseyn der einen in der andern ist ihre negative Einheit und jedes ist nicht nur das Gesetztseyn ihrer, sondern auch der andern, oder jede ist selbst diese negative Einheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"144.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0007","text":"Die positive Identität, welche sie im Gesetze als solchem haben, ist nur erst ihre innere Einheit, welche des Beweises und der Vermittelung bedarf, weil diese negative Einheit noch nicht an ihnen gesetzt ist. Aber indem die verschiedenen Seiten des Gesetzes nunmehr bestimmt sind, als in ihrer negativen Einheit verschiedene zu seyn, oder als solche, deren jedes sein Anderes an ihm selbst enthält und zugleich als Selbstständiges dieß sein Andersseyn von sich abstößt, so ist die Identität des Gesetzes nunmehr auch eine gesetzte und reale.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"144.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0008","text":"Damit hat also das Gesetz das mangelnde Moment der negativen Form seiner Seiten gleichfalls erhalten; das Moment, das vorhin noch der Erscheinung angehörte; die Existenz ist somit vollständig in sich zurückgegangen, und hat sich in ihr absolutes an- und für-sichseyendes Andersseyn reflektirt. Das, was vorher Gesetz war, ist daher nicht mehr nur Eine Seite des Ganzen, dessen andere die Erscheinung als solche war, sondern ist selbst das Ganze. Sie ist die wesentliche Totalität der Erscheinung, so daß sie nun auch das Moment der Unwesentlichkeit, das noch dieser zukam, enthält; aber als die reflektirte, an sich seyende Unwesentlichkeit, d. h. als die wesentliche Negativität.—Das Gesetz ist als unmittelbarer Inhalt, bestimmt überhaupt, unterschieden von andern Gesetzen, und es giebt deren eine unbestimmbare Menge.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"144.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0009","text":"Aber indem es die wesentliche Negativität nun an ihm selbst hat, enthält es nicht mehr eine solche nur gleichgültige, zufällige Inhaltsbestimmung; sondern sein Inhalt ist alle Bestimmtheit überhaupt, in wesentlicher sich zur Totalität machenden Beziehung. So ist die in sich reflektirte Erscheinung nun eine Welt, die sich als an und für sich seyende über der erscheinenden Welt aufthut.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"144.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0010","text":"Das Reich der Gesetze enthält nur den einfachen, wandellosen aber verschiedenen Inhalt der existirenden Welt. Indem es nun aber die totale Reflexion von dieser ist, enthält es auch das Moment ihrer wesenlosen Mannigfaltigkeit. Dieses Moment der Veränderlichkeit und Veränderung als in sich reflektirtes, wesentliches, ist die absolute Negativität oder die Form überhaupt als solche, deren Momente aber in der an- und für-sichseyenden Welt die Realität selbstständiger, aber reflektirter Existenz haben; so wie umgekehrt diese reflektirte Selbstständigkeit nunmehr die Form an ihr selbst hat, und dadurch ihr Inhalt nicht ein bloß mannigfaltiger, sondern ein wesentlich mit sich zusammenhängender ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"144.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0011","text":"—Diese an und für sich seyende Welt heißt auch die übersinnliche Welt; insofern die existirende Welt als sinnliche, nämlich als solche bestimmt wird, die für die Anschauung, das unmittelbare Verhalten des Bewußtseyns, ist.—Die übersinnliche Welt hat gleichfalls Unmittelbarkeit, Existenz, aber reflektirte, wesentliche Existenz. Das Wesen hat noch kein Daseyn; aber es ist, und in tieferem Sinne, als das Seyn; das Ding ist der Beginn der reflektirten Existenz; es ist eine Unmittelbarkeit, die noch nicht gesetzt ist, als wesentliche oder reflektirte; es ist aber in Wahrheit nicht ein seyendes Unmittelbares. Die Dinge erst, als Dinge einer andern, übersinnlichen Welt sind gesetzt, erstens als wahrhafte Existenzen, und zweitens als das Wahre gegen das Seyende;—in ihnen ist es anerkannt, daß es ein von dem unmittelbaren Seyn unterschiedenes Seyn gibt, das wahrhafte Existenz ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"144.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0012","text":"Eines Theils ist in dieser Bestimmung die sinnliche Vorstellung überwunden, welche nur dem unmittelbaren Seyn des Gefühls und der Anschauung Existenz zuschreibt; andern Theils aber auch die bewußtlose Reflexion, welche zwar die Vorstellung von Dingen, Kräften, Innerlichem und so fort hat, ohne zu wissen, daß solche Bestimmungen nicht sinnliche oder seyende Unmittelbarkeiten, sondern reflektirte Existenzen sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"144.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0013","text":"2. Die an und für sich seyende Welt ist die Totalität der Existenz; es ist nichts Anderes außer ihr. Indem sie aber an ihr selbst die absolute Negativität oder Form ist, so ist ihre Reflexion-in-sich, negative Beziehung auf sich. Sie enthält den Gegensatz, und stößt sich ab in sich als die wesentliche Welt, und in sich als die Welt des Andersseyns oder die Welt der Erscheinung. So ist sie darum, weil sie die Totalität ist, auch nur als eine Seite derselben, und macht in dieser Bestimmung eine gegen die Welt der Erscheinung verschiedene Selbstständigkeit aus. Die erscheinende Welt hat an der wesentlichen Welt ihre negative Einheit, in der sie zu Grunde und in die sie als in ihren Grund zurückgeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"144.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0014","text":"Ferner ist die wesentliche Welt auch der setzende Grund der erscheinenden Welt; denn, die absolute Form in ihrer Wesentlichkeit enthaltend, hebt sich ihre Identität mit sich auf, macht sich zum Gesetztseyn und ist als diese gesetzte Unmittelbarkeit die erscheinende Welt.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"144.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0015","text":"Sie ist ferner nicht nur überhaupt Grund der erscheinenden Welt, sondern ihr bestimmter Grund. Schon als das Reich der Gesetze ist sie mannigfaltiger Inhalt, und zwar der wesentliche der erscheinenden Welt, und als inhaltsvoller Grund, der bestimmte Grund der andern, aber nur diesem Inhalt nach; denn die erscheinende Welt hatte noch mannigfaltigen andern Inhalt als jenes Reich, weil ihr noch das negative Moment eigenthümlich zukam. Aber indem das Reich der Gesetze dieß Moment nun gleichfalls an ihm hat, so ist es die Totalität des Inhalts der erscheinenden Welt und der Grund aller ihrer Mannigfaltigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"144.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0016","text":"Aber sie ist zugleich das negative derselben, so ist die derselben entgegengesetzte Welt.—Nämlich in der Identität beider Welten, und indem die eine der Form nach bestimmt ist, als die wesentliche und die andere als dieselbe aber als gesetzte und unwesentliche, hat sich zwar die Grundbeziehung wieder hergestellt; aber zugleich als die Grundbeziehung der Erscheinung, nämlich als Beziehung nicht eines identischen Inhalts, noch auch eines bloß verschiedenen, wie das Gesetz ist, sondern als totale Beziehung, oder als negative Identität und wesentliche Beziehung des Inhalts als entgegengesetzten.—Das Reich der Gesetze ist nicht nur dieß, daß das Gesetztseyn eines Inhalts das Gesetztseyn eines Andern ist, sondern diese Identität ist wesentlich, wie sich ergeben hat, auch negative Einheit; jede der beiden Seiten des Gesetzes ist in der negativen Einheit an ihr selbst ihr anderer Inhalt; das","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"144.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0017","text":"Andere ist daher nicht unbestimmt ein Anderes überhaupt, sondern es ist ihr Anderes, oder es enthält gleichfalls die Inhaltsbestimmung von jener; so sind die beiden Seiten entgegengesetzte. Indem das Reich der Gesetze nun dieß negative Moment und den Gegensatz an ihm hat, und sich somit als die Totalität, von sich selbst in eine an und für sich seyende und eine erscheinende Welt abstößt, so ist die Identität beider die wesentliche Beziehung der Entgegensetzung.—Die Grundbeziehung als solche ist der in seinem Widerspruch zu Grunde gegangene Gegensatz; und die Existenz der mit sich selbst zusammengehende Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"144.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0018","text":"Aber die Existenz wird zur Erscheinung; der Grund ist in der Existenz aufgehoben; er stellt sich als Rückkehr der Erscheinung in sich, wieder her; aber zugleich als aufgehobener, nämlich als Grundbeziehung entgegengesetzter Bestimmungen; die Identität solcher aber ist wesentlich Werden und Übergehen, nicht mehr die Grundbeziehung als solche.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"144.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0019","text":"Die an und für sich seyende Welt ist also selbst eine in sich in die Totalität des mannigfaltigen Inhalts unterschiedene Welt; sie ist identisch mit der erscheinenden oder gesetzten, insofern Grund derselben, aber ihr identischer Zusammenhang ist zugleich als Entgegensetzung bestimmt, weil die Form der erscheinenden Welt die Reflexion in ihr Andersseyn ist, sie also in der an und für sich seyenden Welt wahrhaft so in sich selbst zurückgegangen ist, als diese ihre entgegengesetzte ist. Die Beziehung ist also bestimmt diese, daß die an und für sich seyende Welt die verkehrte der erscheinenden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"144.19"}],"sha256":"80ca3d200ea24ff4bac6556fddb5138029bc7d920ebf19c5638034114bd3bcbc","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105610697386Z_c01d4c36","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. The World of Appearance and the World-in-Itself.","source_sha256":"80ca3d200ea24ff4bac6556fddb5138029bc7d920ebf19c5638034114bd3bcbc","sha256":"bd57c2c862205a872d2848d45d5c9cf2a10b791417d948ba89d1114f9b2f27ee","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:56:10.697413+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0001","text":"I. The existing world rises tranquilly into a realm of laws; the null content of its manifold being has its subsistence in an Other; its subsistence is therefore its dissolution. But in this Other, that which appears also coincides with itself; thus appearance, in its alteration, is also an abiding, and its positedness is law. Law is this simple identity of appearance with itself; hence the foundation, not the ground, of the latter; for it is not the negative unity of appearance, but, as its simple identity, the immediate, as abstract unity, alongside which, therefore, its other content also has place. The content is this, is coherent within itself, or has its negative reflection within itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"144.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0002","text":"It is reflected into another; this Other is itself an existence of appearance; appearing things have their grounds and conditions in other appearing things.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"144.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0003","text":"But in fact law is also the Other of appearance as such, and its negative reflection as into its Other. The content of appearance, which is distinct from the content of law, is the existing, which has its negativity as its ground, or is reflected into its non-being. But this Other, which is likewise an existing, is equally such a one reflected into its non-being; it is therefore the same, and that which appears is therein in fact reflected not into an other, but into itself; precisely this reflection of positedness into itself is law. But as appearing, it is essentially reflected into its non-being, or its identity is itself essentially just as much its negativity and its Other.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"144.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0004","text":"The reflection-into-itself of appearance, law, is therefore also not merely its identical foundation, but it has in law its opposite, and law is its negative unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"144.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0005","text":"Thereby the determination of law has now altered in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"144.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0006","text":"At first it is merely a different content, and the formal reflection of positedness into itself, such that the positedness of one of its sides is the positedness of the other. But since it is also the negative reflection into itself, its sides do not relate merely as different, but as negatively relating to one another.—Or, if law is considered merely for itself, the sides of its content are indifferent to one another; but they are equally much sublated through their identity; the positedness of the one is the positedness of the other; thus the subsistence of each is also its own non-subsistence. This positedness of the one in the other is their negative unity, and each is not merely the positedness of itself, but also of the other, or each is itself this negative unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"144.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0007","text":"The positive identity which they have in law as such is at first only their inner unity, which requires proof and mediation, because this negative unity is not yet posited in them. But since the different sides of law are now determined as different in their negative unity, or as such that each contains its Other within itself and at the same time, as self-subsistent, repels this its otherness from itself, the identity of law is now likewise a posited and real one.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"144.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0008","text":"Thus law has also received in itself the missing moment of the negative form of its sides; the moment which previously still belonged to appearance; existence has thereby completely returned into itself and has reflected itself into its absolute otherness which is in-and-for-itself. That which was previously law is therefore no longer merely one side of the whole, whose other side was appearance as such, but is itself the whole. It is the essential totality of appearance, so that it now also contains the moment of unessentiality which still pertained to the latter; but as reflected unessentiality, being in itself, i.e. as essential negativity.—As immediate content, law is determined in general as distinct from other laws, and there is an indeterminable multitude of them.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"144.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0009","text":"But since it now has essential negativity in itself, it no longer contains such a merely indifferent, contingent determination of content; rather, its content is all determinateness in general, in an essential relation making itself into totality. Thus appearance reflected into itself is now a world which opens itself up, as a world being in-and-for-itself, above the appearing world.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"144.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0010","text":"The realm of laws contains only the simple, unchanging, yet different content of the existing world. But since it is now the total reflection of the latter, it also contains the moment of its inessential manifoldness. This moment of mutability and alteration, as reflected into itself and essential, is absolute negativity, or form in general as such, whose moments, however, in the world being in-and-for-itself have the reality of self-subsistent, yet reflected existence; just as, conversely, this reflected self-subsistence now has form in itself, and thereby its content is not merely manifold, but essentially coherent with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"144.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0011","text":"—This world being in-and-for-itself is also called the supersensible world, insofar as the existing world is determined as sensible, namely as that which is for intuition, the immediate relation of consciousness.—The supersensible world likewise has immediacy, existence, but reflected, essential existence. Essence does not yet have existence; but it is, and in a deeper sense than being; the thing is the beginning of reflected existence; it is an immediacy which is not yet posited as essential or reflected; but it is in truth not an immediate which is. Only things, as things of another, supersensible world, are posited, first, as true existences, and second, as the true in opposition to being;—in them it is acknowledged that there is a being distinct from immediate being, which is true existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"144.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0012","text":"On the one hand, in this determination the sensible representation is overcome, which attributes existence only to the immediate being of feeling and intuition; on the other hand, however, also unconscious reflection, which indeed has the representation of things, forces, inwardness, and so forth, without knowing that such determinations are not sensible or being immediacies, but reflected existences.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"144.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0013","text":"2. The world being in-and-for-itself is the totality of existence; there is nothing other outside it. But since it is in itself absolute negativity or form, its reflection-into-itself is negative relation to itself. It contains opposition, and repels itself within itself as the essential world, and within itself as the world of otherness or the world of appearance. Thus, because it is totality, it is also only as one side of the same, and in this determination constitutes a self-subsistence distinct from the world of appearance. The appearing world has in the essential world its negative unity, in which it goes to ground and into which it returns as into its ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"144.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0014","text":"Further, the essential world is also the positing ground of the appearing world; for, containing absolute form in its essentiality, its identity with itself sublates itself, makes itself into positedness, and as this posited immediacy it is the appearing world.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"144.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0015","text":"Further, it is not merely the ground of the appearing world in general, but its determinate ground. Already as the realm of laws it is manifold content, namely the essential content of the appearing world, and as a contentful ground, the determinate ground of the other, but only according to this content; for the appearing world still had manifold other content than that realm, because the negative moment still pertained to it peculiarly. But since the realm of laws now likewise has this moment in itself, it is the totality of the content of the appearing world and the ground of all its manifoldness.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"144.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0016","text":"But it is at once the negative of the same; thus it is the world opposed to the latter.—Namely, in the identity of both worlds, and since the one is determined according to form as the essential and the other as the same, but as posited and unessential, the ground-relation has indeed been restored; but at the same time as the ground-relation of appearance, namely as the relation not of an identical content, nor indeed of a merely different one, as law is, but as total relation, or as negative identity and essential relation of content as opposed.—The realm of laws is not merely this, that the positedness of one content is the positedness of another, but this identity is essentially, as has emerged, also negative unity; each of the two sides of law is, in negative unity, in itself its other content; the","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"144.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0017","text":"Other is therefore not indeterminately an Other in general, but it is its Other, or it likewise contains the determination of content of that side; thus the two sides are opposed. Since the realm of laws now has this negative moment and opposition in itself, and thus repels itself, as totality, from itself into a world being in-and-for-itself and an appearing world, the identity of both is the essential relation of opposition.—The ground-relation as such is the opposition which has gone to ground in its contradiction; and existence is the ground coinciding with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"144.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0018","text":"But existence becomes appearance; the ground is sublated in existence; it re-establishes itself as the return of appearance into itself; but at the same time as sublated, namely as the ground-relation of opposed determinations; but the identity of such determinations is essentially becoming and transition, no longer the ground-relation as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"144.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0019","text":"The world being in-and-for-itself is therefore itself a world differentiated within itself into the totality of manifold content; it is identical with the appearing or posited world insofar as it is its ground, but its identical coherence is at the same time determined as opposition, because the form of the appearing world is reflection into its otherness, and thus in the world being in-and-for-itself it has truly returned into itself just as much as this latter is its opposite. The relation is therefore determined thus: that the world being in-and-for-itself is the inverted one of the appearing world.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"144.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BD_3:P0019"]}],"source_digest":"6a290122e1d232b2e3105ac84b2c739761db7ac4491da0cee67a07c916faffe3","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Die erscheinende und die an-sich-seynede Welt."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Die erscheinende und die an-sich-seynede Welt.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD","title":"C. Dissolution of Appearance.","order":145,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CASD","text":"Die an und für sich seyende Welt ist der bestimmte Grund der erscheinenden Welt, und ist dieß nur, insofern sie an ihr selbst das negative Moment und damit die Totalität der Inhaltsbestimmungen und ihrer Veränderungen ist, welche der erscheinenden Welt entspricht, aber zugleich ihre durchaus entgegengesetzte Seite ausmacht. Beide Welten verhalten sich also so zu einander, daß was in der erscheinenden Welt positiv, in der an und für sich seyenden Welt negativ, umgekehrt was in jener negativ, in dieser positiv ist. Der Nordpol in der erscheinenden Welt, ist an und für sich der Südpol, und umgekehrt; die positive Elektricität ist an sich negative u.s.f. Was im erscheinenden Daseyn böse, Unglück u.s.f. ist, ist an und für sich gut und ein Glück. [15]\n\n[15] Vergl. Phänomenologie des Geistes. S. 121 ff.\n\nIn der That ist gerade in diesem Gegensatz beider Welten ihr Unterschied verschwunden, und was an und für sich seyende Welt seyn sollte, ist selbst erscheinende Welt, und diese umgekehrt an ihr selbst wesentliche Welt.—Die erscheinende Welt ist zunächst bestimmt als die Reflexion in das Andersseyn, so daß ihre Bestimmungen und Existenzen in einem Andern ihren Grund und Bestehen haben; aber indem dieß Andre gleichfalls ein solches in ein anderes Reflektirtes ist, so beziehen sie sich darin nur auf ein sich aufhebendes Anderes, somit auf sich selbst; die erscheinende Welt ist hiermit an ihr selbst sich selbst gleiches Gesetz.—Umgekehrt die an und für sich seyende Welt ist zunächst der mit sich identische, dem Andersseyn und Wechsel entnommene Inhalt; aber dieser, als vollständige Reflexion der erscheinenden Welt in sich selbst, oder weil seine Verschiedenheit in sich reflektirter und absoluter Unterschied ist, so enthält er das negative Moment und die Beziehung auf sich als auf das Andersseyn; er wird dadurch sich selbst entgegengesetzter, sich verkehrender, wesenloser Inhalt. Ferner hat dieser Inhalt der an und für sich seyenden Welt damit auch die Form unmittelbarer Existenz erhalten. Denn sie ist zunächst Grund der erscheinenden; aber indem sie die Entgegensetznng an ihr selbst hat, ist sie ebenso sehr aufgehobener Grund und unmittelbare Existenz.\n\nDie erscheinende und die wesentliche Welt sind hiermit jede an ihr selbst die Totalität der mit sich identischen Reflexion und der Reflexion-in-Anderes, oder des An-und-für-sich-seyns und des Erscheinens. Sie sind beide die selbstständigen Ganzen der Existenz; die eine sollte nur die reflektirte Existenz, die andere die unmittelbare Existenz seyn; aber jede kontinuirt sich in ihrer andern und ist daher an ihr selbst die Identität dieser beiden Momente. Was also vorhanden ist, ist diese Totalität, welche sich von sich selbst in zwei Totalitäten abstößt, die eine die reflektirte Totalität, und die andere die unmittelbare. Beide sind erstlich Selbstständige, aber sie sind dieß nur als Totalitäten, und dieß sind sie insofern, daß jede wesentlich das Moment der andern an ihr hat. Die unterschiedene Selbstständigkeit einer jeden, der als unmittelbar und der als reflektirt bestimmten, ist daher nunmehr so gesetzt, nur als wesentliche Beziehung auf die andre zu seyn, und ihre Selbstständigkeit in dieser Einheit beider zu haben.\n\nEs wurde vom Gesetz der Erscheinung ausgegangen; dieses ist die Identität eines verschiedenen Inhalts mit einem andern Inhalte, so daß das Gesetztseyn des einen das Gesetztseyn des andern ist. Im Gesetze ist noch dieser Unterschied vorhanden, daß die Identität seiner Seiten nur erst eine innere ist, und diese Seiten sie noch nicht an ihnen selbst haben; damit ist eines Theils jene Identität nicht realisirt; der Inhalt des Gesetzes ist nicht als identischer, sondern ein gleichgültiger, verschiedener Inhalt; andern Theils ist er damit nur an sich so bestimmt, daß das Gesetztseyn des einen, das Gesetztseyn des andern ist; dieß ist noch nicht an ihm vorhanden. Nunmehr aber ist das Gesetz realisirt; seine innere Identität ist zugleich daseyende, und umgekehrt ist der Inhalt des Gesetzes in die Idealität erhoben; denn er ist an ihm selbst aufgehobener, in sich reflektirter, indem jede Seite an ihr ihre andere hat, und damit wahrhaft mit ihr und mit sich identisch ist.\n\nSo ist das Gesetz wesentliches Verhältniß. Die Wahrheit der unwesentlichen Welt ist zunächst eine ihr andere an und für sich seyende Welt; aber diese ist die Totalität, indem sie, sie selbst und jene erste ist; so sind beide unmittelbare Existenzen und damit Reflexionen in ihr Andersseyn, als auch eben damit wahrhaft in sich reflektirte. Welt drückt überhaupt die formlose Totalität der Mannigfaltigkeit aus; diese Welt, sowohl als wesentliche wie als erscheinende ist zu Grunde gegangen, indem die Mannigfaltigkeit aufgehört hat, eine bloß verschiedene zu seyn; so ist sie noch Totalität oder Universum aber als wesentliches Verhältniß. Es sind zwei Totalitäten des Inhalts in der Erscheinung entstanden; zunächst sind sie als gleichgültige Selbstständige gegen einander bestimmt und haben zwar die Form jede an ihr selbst, aber nicht gegen einander; diese aber hat sich auch als ihre Beziehung gezeigt, und das wesentliche Verhältniß ist die Vollendung ihrer Formeinheit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Die an und für sich seyende Welt ist der bestimmte Grund der erscheinenden Welt, und ist dieß nur, insofern sie an ihr selbst das negative Moment und damit die Totalität der Inhaltsbestimmungen und ihrer Veränderungen ist, welche der erscheinenden Welt entspricht, aber zugleich ihre durchaus entgegengesetzte Seite ausmacht. Beide Welten verhalten sich also so zu einander, daß was in der erscheinenden Welt positiv, in der an und für sich seyenden Welt negativ, umgekehrt was in jener negativ, in dieser positiv ist. Der Nordpol in der erscheinenden Welt, ist an und für sich der Südpol, und umgekehrt; die positive Elektricität ist an sich negative u.s.f. Was im erscheinenden Daseyn böse, Unglück u.s.f. ist, ist an und für sich gut und ein Glück. [15]","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0002","text":"[15] Vergl. Phänomenologie des Geistes. S. 121 ff.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0003","text":"In der That ist gerade in diesem Gegensatz beider Welten ihr Unterschied verschwunden, und was an und für sich seyende Welt seyn sollte, ist selbst erscheinende Welt, und diese umgekehrt an ihr selbst wesentliche Welt.—Die erscheinende Welt ist zunächst bestimmt als die Reflexion in das Andersseyn, so daß ihre Bestimmungen und Existenzen in einem Andern ihren Grund und Bestehen haben; aber indem dieß Andre gleichfalls ein solches in ein anderes Reflektirtes ist, so beziehen sie sich darin nur auf ein sich aufhebendes Anderes, somit auf sich selbst; die erscheinende Welt ist hiermit an ihr selbst sich selbst gleiches Gesetz.—Umgekehrt die an und für sich seyende Welt ist zunächst der mit sich identische, dem Andersseyn und Wechsel entnommene Inhalt; aber dieser, als vollständige Reflexion der erscheinenden Welt in sich selbst, oder weil seine Verschiedenheit in sich reflektirter und absoluter Unterschied ist, so enthält er das negative Moment und die Beziehung auf sich als auf das Andersseyn; er wird dadurch sich selbst entgegengesetzter, sich verkehrender, wesenloser Inhalt. Ferner hat dieser Inhalt der an und für sich seyenden Welt damit auch die Form unmittelbarer Existenz erhalten. Denn sie ist zunächst Grund der erscheinenden; aber indem sie die Entgegensetznng an ihr selbst hat, ist sie ebenso sehr aufgehobener Grund und unmittelbare Existenz.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0004","text":"Die erscheinende und die wesentliche Welt sind hiermit jede an ihr selbst die Totalität der mit sich identischen Reflexion und der Reflexion-in-Anderes, oder des An-und-für-sich-seyns und des Erscheinens. Sie sind beide die selbstständigen Ganzen der Existenz; die eine sollte nur die reflektirte Existenz, die andere die unmittelbare Existenz seyn; aber jede kontinuirt sich in ihrer andern und ist daher an ihr selbst die Identität dieser beiden Momente. Was also vorhanden ist, ist diese Totalität, welche sich von sich selbst in zwei Totalitäten abstößt, die eine die reflektirte Totalität, und die andere die unmittelbare. Beide sind erstlich Selbstständige, aber sie sind dieß nur als Totalitäten, und dieß sind sie insofern, daß jede wesentlich das Moment der andern an ihr hat. Die unterschiedene Selbstständigkeit einer jeden, der als unmittelbar und der als reflektirt bestimmten, ist daher nunmehr so gesetzt, nur als wesentliche Beziehung auf die andre zu seyn, und ihre Selbstständigkeit in dieser Einheit beider zu haben.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0005","text":"Es wurde vom Gesetz der Erscheinung ausgegangen; dieses ist die Identität eines verschiedenen Inhalts mit einem andern Inhalte, so daß das Gesetztseyn des einen das Gesetztseyn des andern ist. Im Gesetze ist noch dieser Unterschied vorhanden, daß die Identität seiner Seiten nur erst eine innere ist, und diese Seiten sie noch nicht an ihnen selbst haben; damit ist eines Theils jene Identität nicht realisirt; der Inhalt des Gesetzes ist nicht als identischer, sondern ein gleichgültiger, verschiedener Inhalt; andern Theils ist er damit nur an sich so bestimmt, daß das Gesetztseyn des einen, das Gesetztseyn des andern ist; dieß ist noch nicht an ihm vorhanden. Nunmehr aber ist das Gesetz realisirt; seine innere Identität ist zugleich daseyende, und umgekehrt ist der Inhalt des Gesetzes in die Idealität erhoben; denn er ist an ihm selbst aufgehobener, in sich reflektirter, indem jede Seite an ihr ihre andere hat, und damit wahrhaft mit ihr und mit sich identisch ist.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0006","text":"So ist das Gesetz wesentliches Verhältniß. Die Wahrheit der unwesentlichen Welt ist zunächst eine ihr andere an und für sich seyende Welt; aber diese ist die Totalität, indem sie, sie selbst und jene erste ist; so sind beide unmittelbare Existenzen und damit Reflexionen in ihr Andersseyn, als auch eben damit wahrhaft in sich reflektirte. Welt drückt überhaupt die formlose Totalität der Mannigfaltigkeit aus; diese Welt, sowohl als wesentliche wie als erscheinende ist zu Grunde gegangen, indem die Mannigfaltigkeit aufgehört hat, eine bloß verschiedene zu seyn; so ist sie noch Totalität oder Universum aber als wesentliches Verhältniß. Es sind zwei Totalitäten des Inhalts in der Erscheinung entstanden; zunächst sind sie als gleichgültige Selbstständige gegen einander bestimmt und haben zwar die Form jede an ihr selbst, aber nicht gegen einander; diese aber hat sich auch als ihre Beziehung gezeigt, und das wesentliche Verhältniß ist die Vollendung ihrer Formeinheit.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"38e088fa9eae96098fb434af16d55573df0022d37945ba77249ccf8ff4bebf24","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Dissolution of Appearance.","source_sha256":"38e088fa9eae96098fb434af16d55573df0022d37945ba77249ccf8ff4bebf24","sha256":"d63948eb2598b744bba522145b07b20285680b5a962ed7f3d8b9d48fe38c41ef","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:56:20.121342+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0001","text":"The world that is in and for itself is the determinate ground of the world of appearance, and it is this only insofar as it is in itself the negative moment, and thereby the totality of the determinations of content and of their alterations, which corresponds to the world of appearance, but at the same time constitutes its thoroughly opposed side. The two worlds thus relate to one another in such a way that what is positive in the world of appearance is negative in the world that is in and for itself, and conversely, what is negative in the former is positive in the latter. The North Pole in the world of appearance is in and for itself the South Pole, and conversely; positive electricity is in itself negative, etc. What in appearing existence is evil, misfortune, etc., is in and for itself good and a good fortune. [15]","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0002","text":"[15] Cf. Phenomenology of Spirit. p. 121 ff.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0002"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0003","text":"In fact, it is precisely in this opposition of the two worlds that their difference has vanished, and what was supposed to be the world that is in and for itself is itself a world of appearance, and this, conversely, is in itself an essential world.—The world of appearance is at first determined as reflection into otherness, so that its determinations and existences have their ground and subsistence in an other; but since this other is likewise such a one reflected into another, they relate therein only to an other that sublates itself, hence to themselves; the world of appearance is thereby in itself a law equal to itself.—Conversely, the world that is in and for itself is at first the content identical with itself, withdrawn from otherness and alteration; but this, as the complete reflection of the world of appearance into itself, or because its difference is reflected into itself and","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0004","text":"absolute difference, contains the negative moment and the relation to itself as to otherness; it thereby becomes content opposed to itself, self-reversing, devoid of essence. Further, this content of the world that is in and for itself has thereby also received the form of immediate existence. For it is at first the ground of what appears; but since it has opposition in itself, it is equally sublated ground and immediate existence.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0003"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0005","text":"The world of appearance and the essential world are thereby each in itself the totality of reflection identical with itself and reflection-into-another, or of being-in-and-for-itself and appearance. Both are the self-subsistent wholes of existence; the one was supposed to be only reflected existence, the other immediate existence; but each continues itself in its other and is therefore in itself the identity of these two moments. What is present, therefore, is this totality, which repels itself from itself into two totalities, the one the reflected totality and the other the immediate. Both are at first self-subsistent, but they are this only as totalities, and they are this insofar as each essentially has the moment of the other in it.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0006","text":"The distinct self-subsistence of each, of that determined as immediate and of that determined as reflected, is therefore now posited as being only an essential relation to the other, and as having its self-subsistence in this unity of both.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0004"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0007","text":"The point of departure was the law of appearance; this is the identity of a different content with another content, such that the positedness of the one is the positedness of the other. In the law, this difference is still present, namely, that the identity of its sides is as yet only an inner one, and these sides do not yet have it in themselves; thereby, on the one hand, that identity is not realized; the content of the law is not as identical, but as an indifferent, different content; on the other hand, it is thereby determined only in itself such that the positedness of the one is the positedness of the other; this is not yet present in it.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0008","text":"But now the law is realized; its inner identity is at the same time existent, and conversely the content of the law is raised into ideality; for it is in itself sublated, reflected into itself, in that each side has its other in it, and thereby is truly identical with it and with itself.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0005"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0009","text":"Thus the law is essential relation. The truth of the unessential world is at first an other world that is in and for itself; but this is the totality, since it is both itself and that first world; thus both are immediate existences and thereby reflections into their otherness, as also precisely thereby truly reflections into themselves. World in general expresses the formless totality of multiplicity; this world, both as essential and as appearing, has perished, since multiplicity has ceased to be merely different; thus it is still totality or universe, but as essential relation.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0006"]},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105620121325Z_a50557f8:DISPLAY-0010","text":"Two totalities of content have arisen in appearance; at first they are determined as indifferent self-subsistent entities over against one another and indeed each has the form in itself, but not over against the other; yet this has also shown itself to be their relation, and the essential relation is the completion of their unity of form.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CASD:DISPLAY-0006"]}],"source_digest":"e97a681ec1e978af43ccb25183f4add1d6e8f87767d24201fa922f09bcbb8de5","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Auflösung der Erscheinung."}],"original_title":"C. Auflösung der Erscheinung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD","title":"A. The Relation of Whole and Parts.","order":146,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DVLD","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das wesentliche Verhältniß.\n\nDie Wahrheit der Erscheinung ist das wesentliche Verhältniß. Sein Inhalt hat unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit, und zwar die seyende Unmittelbarkeit, und die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit oder die mit sich identische Reflexion. Zugleich ist er in dieser Selbstständigkeit ein relativer, schlechthin nur als Reflexion in sein Anderes, oder als Einheit der Beziehung mit seinem Andern. In dieser Einheit ist der selbstständige Inhalt ein Gesetztes, Aufgehobenes; aber eben diese Einheit macht seine Wesentlichkeit und Selbstständigkeit aus; diese Reflexion in Anderes ist Reflexion in sich selbst. Das Verhältniß hat Seiten, weil es Reflexion in Anderes ist; so hat es den Unterschied seiner selbst an ihm; und die Seiten desselben sind selbstständiges Bestehen, indem sie in ihrer gleichgültigen Verschiedenheit gegen einander, in sich selbst gebrochen sind, so daß das Bestehen einer jeden, ebenso sehr nur seine Bedeutung in der Beziehung auf die andere oder in ihrer negativen Einheit hat.\n\nDas wesentliche Verhältniß ist daher zwar noch nicht das wahrhafte Dritte zum Wesen und zur Existenz; aber enthält bereits die bestimmte Vereinigung beider. Das Wesen ist in ihm so realisirt, daß es selbstständig-existirende zu seinem Bestehen hat; und diese sind aus ihrer Gleichgültigkeit in ihre wesentliche Einheit zurückgegangen, so daß sie nur diese zu ihrem Bestehen haben. Die Reflexions-Bestimmungen des Positiven und Negativen sind gleichfalls in sich reflektirte nur als reflektirt in ihr Entgegengesetztes; aber sie haben keine andere Bestimmung als diese ihre negative Einheit; das wesentliche Verhältniß hingegen hat solche zu seinen Seiten, welche als selbstständige Totalitäten gesetzt sind. Es ist dieselbe Entgegensetzung als die des Positiven und Negativen; aber zugleich als eine verkehrte Welt. Die Seite des wesentlichen Verhältnisses ist eine Totalität, die aber als wesentlich ein Entgegengesetztes, ein Jenseits seiner hat; es ist nur Erscheinung; seine Existenz ist vielmehr nicht die seinige, sondern die seines Andern. Es ist daher ein in sich selbst Gebrochenes; aber dieß sein Aufgehobenseyn besteht darin, daß es die Einheit seiner selbst und seines Andern also Ganzes ist, und eben darum hat es selbstständige Existenz und ist wesentliche Reflexion in sich.\n\nDieß ist der Begriff des Verhältnisses. Zunächst aber ist die Identität, die es enthält, noch nicht vollkommen; die Totalität, welche jedes relative an ihm selbst ist, ist erst ein Inneres; die Seite des Verhältnisses ist zunächst gesetzt in einer der Bestimmungen der negativen Einheit; die eigene Selbstständigkeit jeder der beiden Seiten ist dasjenige, was die Form des Verhältnisses ausmacht. Seine Identität ist daher nur eine Beziehung, außerhalb welcher ihre Selbstständigkeit fällt; nämlich in die Seiten; es ist noch nicht die reflektirte Einheit jener Identität und der selbstständigen Existenzen vorhanden, noch nicht die Substanz.—Der Begriff des Verhältnisses hat sich daher zwar ergeben, Einheit der reflektirten und der unmittelbaren Selbstständigkeit zu seyn. Aber zuerst ist dieser Begriff selbst noch unmittelbar, seine Momente daher unmittelbare gegen einander, und die Einheit deren wesentliche Beziehung, die erst dann die wahrhafte, dem Begriffe entsprechende Einheit ist, insofern sie sich realisirt, nämlich durch ihre Bewegung als jene Einheit gesetzt hat.\n\nDas wesentliche Verhältniß ist daher unmittelbar das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile;—die Beziehung der reflektirten und der unmittelbaren Selbstständigkeit, so daß beide zugleich nur sind als sich gegenseitig bedingend und voraussetzend.\n\nIn diesem Verhältnisse ist noch keine der Seiten als Moment der andern gesetzt, ihre Identität ist daher selbst eine Seite; oder sie ist nicht ihre negative Einheit. Es geht darum zweitens darein über, daß die eine Moment der andern und in ihr als in ihrem Grunde, dem wahrhaft Selbstständigen von beiden, ist;—Verhältniß der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung.\n\nDrittens hebt sich die noch vorhandene Ungleichheit dieser Beziehung auf, und das letzte Verhältniß ist das des Innern und Äußern.—In diesem ganz formell gewordenen Unterschiede geht das Verhältniß selbst zu Grunde, und die Substanz oder das Wirkliche tritt hervor, als die absolute Einheit der unmittelbaren und der reflektirten Existenz.\n\n## A. Das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile.\n\nDas wesentliche Verhältniß enthält erstens die in sich reflektirte Selbstständigkeit der Existenz; so ist es die einfache Form, deren Bestimmungen zwar auch Existenzen, aber zugleich gesetzte, Momente in der Einheit gehalten, sind. Diese in sich reflektirte Selbstständigkeit ist zugleich Reflexion in ihr Entgegengesetztes, nämlich die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit; und ihr Bestehen ist wesentlich ebenso sehr als es eigene Selbstständigkeit ist, diese Identität mit seinem Entgegengesetzten.—Eben damit ist auch unmittelbar zweitens die andre Seite gesetzt; die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit, welche als das Andre bestimmt, eine vielfache Mannigfaltigkeit in sich ist, aber so daß diese Mannigfaltigkeit wesentlich auch die Beziehung der andern Seite, die Einheit der reflektirten Selbstständigkeit an ihr hat. Jene Seite, das Ganze, ist die Selbstständigkeit, welche die an und für sich seyende Welt ausmachte; die andere Seite, die Theile, ist die unmittelbare Existenz, welche die erscheinende Welt war. Im Verhältnisse des Ganzen und der Theile sind die beiden Seiten diese Selbstständigkeiten, aber so daß jede die andere in ihr scheinen hat, und nur ist zugleich als diese Identität beider. Weil nun das wesentliche Verhältniß nur erst das erste, unmittelbare ist, so ist die negative Einheit und die positive Selbstständigkeit durch das Auch verbunden; beide Seiten sind zwar als Momente gesetzt, aber ebenso sehr als existirende Selbstständigkeiten.—Daß beide als Momente gesetzt sind, dieß ist daher so vertheilt, daß erstens das Ganze, die reflektirte Selbstständigkeit, als Existirendes und in ihr die andere, die unmittelbare als Moment ist;—hier macht das Ganze die Einheit beider Seiten, die Grundlage aus, und die unmittelbare Existenz ist als Gesetztseyn.—Umgekehrt ist auf der andern Seite, nämlich der Seite der Theile, die unmittelbare, in sich mannigfaltige Existenz, die selbstständige Grundlage; die reflektirte Einheit dagegen, das Ganze ist nur äußerliche Beziehung.\n\n2. Dieß Verhältniß enthält somit die Selbstständigkeit der Seiten, und ebenso sehr ihr Aufgehobenseyn, und beides schlechthin in Einer Beziehung. Das Ganze ist das Selbstständige, die Theile sind nur Momente dieser Einheit; aber ebenso sehr sind sie auch das Selbstständige, und ihre reflektirte Einheit nur ein Moment; und jedes ist in seiner Selbstständigkeit schlechthin das Relative eines Andern. Dieß Verhältniß ist daher der unmittelbare Widerspruch an ihm selbst, und hebt sich auf.\n\nDieß näher betrachtet, so ist das Ganze die reflektirte Einheit, welche selbstständiges Bestehen für sich hat; aber dieß ihr Bestehen ist ebenso sehr von ihr abgestoßen; das Ganze ist als die negative Einheit, negative Beziehung auf sich selbst; so ist sie sich entäußert; sie hat ihr Bestehen an ihrem Entgegengesetzten, der mannigfaltigen Unmittelbarkeit, den Theilen. Das Ganze besteht daher aus den Theilen; so daß es nicht etwas ist ohne sie. Es ist also das ganze Verhältniß und die selbstständige Totalität; aber gerade aus demselben Grunde ist es nur ein Relatives, denn was es zur Totalität macht, ist vielmehr sein Anderes, die Theile; und es hat nicht an sich selbst, sondern an seinem Andern sein Bestehen.\n\nSo sind die Theile gleichfalls das ganze Verhältniß. Sie sind die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit gegen die reflektirte, und bestehen nicht im Ganzen, sondern sind für sich. Sie haben ferner dieß Ganze als ihr Moment an ihnen; es macht ihre Beziehung aus; ohne Ganzes giebt es keine Theile. Aber weil sie das Selbstständige sind, so ist diese Beziehung nur ein äußerliches Moment, gegen welches sie an und für sich gleichgültig sind. Zugleich aber fallen die Theile als mannigfaltige Existenz in sich selbst zusammen, denn diese ist das reflexionslose Seyn; sie haben ihre Selbstständigkeit nur in der reflektirten Einheit, welche sowohl diese Einheit als auch die existirende Mannigfaltigkeit ist; das heißt, sie haben Selbstständigkeit nur im Ganzen, das aber zugleich die den Theilen andere Selbstständigkeit ist.\n\nDas Ganze und die Theile bedingen sich daher gegenseitig; aber das hier betrachtete Verhältniß, steht zugleich höher, als die Beziehung des Bedingten und der Bedingung auf einander, wie sie sich oben bestimmt hatte. Diese Beziehung ist hier realisirt; nämlich es ist gesetzt, daß die Bedingung so die wesentliche Selbstständigkeit des Bedingten ist, daß sie durch dieses vorausgesetzt wird. Die Bedingung als solche ist nur das Unmittelbare, und nur an sich vorausgesetzt. Das Ganze aber ist die Bedingung zwar der Theile, aber es enthält zugleich unmittelbar selbst, daß auch es nur ist, insofern es die Theile zur Voraussetzung hat. Indem so beide Seiten des Verhältnisses gesetzt sind als sich gegenseitig bedingend, ist jede eine unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit an ihr selbst, aber ihre Selbstständigkeit ist ebenso sehr vermittelt oder gesetzt durch die andere. Das ganze Verhältniß ist durch diese Gegenseitigkeit die Rückkehr des Bedingens in sich selbst, das nicht Relative, das Unbedingte.\n\nIndem nun die Seiten des Verhältnisses jede nicht in ihr selbst ihre Selbstständigkeit, sondern in ihrer andern hat, so ist nur Eine Identität beider vorhanden, in welcher beide nur Momente sind; aber indem jede an ihr selbst selbstständig ist, so sind sie zwei selbstständige Existenzen, die gegen einander gleichgültig sind.\n\nNach der ersten Rüksicht, der wesentlichen Identität dieser Seiten, ist das Ganze den Theilen und die Theile dem Ganzen gleich. Es ist nichts im Ganzen, was nicht in den Theilen, und nichts in den Theilen, was nicht im Ganzen ist. Das Ganze ist nicht abstrakte Einheit, sondern die Einheit als einer verschiedenen Mannigfaltigkeit; diese Einheit aber als das, worin das Mannigfaltige sich auf einander bezieht, ist die Bestimmtheit desselben, wodurch es Theil ist. Das Verhältniß hat also eine untrennbare Identität, und mir Eine Selbstständigkeit.\n\nAber ferner ist das Ganze den Theilen gleich; allein nicht denselben als Theilen; das Ganze ist die reflektirte Einheit, die Theile aber machen das bestimmte Moment oder das Andersseyn der Einheit aus, und sind das verschiedene Mannigfaltige. Das Ganze ist ihnen nicht gleich als diesem selbstständigen Verschiedenen, sondern als ihnen zusammen. Dieß ihr Zusammen aber ist nichts Anderes, als ihre Einheit, das Ganze als solches. Das Ganze ist also in den Theilen nur sich selbst gleich, und die Gleichheit desselben und der Theile drückt nur die Tautologie aus, daß das Ganze als Ganzes nicht den Theilen, sondern dem Ganzen gleich ist.\n\nUmgekehrt sind die Theile dem Ganzen gleich; aber weil sie das Moment des Andersseyns an ihnen selbst sind, so sind sie ihm nicht gleich als der Einheit, sondern so daß eine seiner mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen auf den Theil kommt, oder daß sie ihm als Mannigfaltigem gleich sind; das heißt, sie sind ihm als getheiltem Ganzen d. i. als den Theilen gleich. Es ist hiermit dieselbe Tautologie vorhanden, daß die Theile als Theile, nicht dem Ganzen als solchem, sondern in ihm sich selbst, den Theilen, gleich sind.\n\nDas Ganze und die Theile fallen auf diese Weise gleichgültig aus einander; jede dieser Seiten bezieht sich nur auf sich. Aber so aus einander gehalten zerstören sie sich selbst. Das Ganze, das gleichgültig ist gegen die Theile, ist die abstrakte, in sich nicht unterschiedene Identität; diese ist Ganzes nur als in sich selbst unterschieden, und zwar so in sich unterschieden, daß diese mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen in sich reflektirt sind und unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit haben. Und die Reflexionsidentität hat sich durch ihre Bewegung gezeigt, diese Reflexion in ihr Anderes zu ihrer Wahrheit zu haben.—Ebenso sind die Theile als gleichgültig gegen die Einheit des Ganzen, nur das unbezogene Mannigfaltige, das in sich Andere, welches als solches das Andere seiner selbst und sich nur Aufhebende ist.—Diese Beziehung-auf-sich jeder der beiden Seiten, ist ihre Selbstständigkeit; aber diese ihre Selbstständigkeit, die jede für sich hat, ist vielmehr die Negation ihrer selbst. Jede hat daher ihre Selbstständigkeit nicht an ihr selbst, sondern an der andern; diese andere, die das Bestehen ausmacht, ist ihr vorausgesetztes Unmittelbare, das Erstes und ihr Anfang seyn soll; aber dieses Erste einer jeder ist selbst nur ein solches, das nicht Erstes ist, sondern an dem andern seinen Anfang hat.\n\nDie Wahrheit des Verhältnisses besteht also in der Vermittelung; sein Wesen ist die negative Einheit, in welcher ebenso wohl die reflektirte als die seyende Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben sind. Das Verhältniß ist der Widerspruch, der in seinen Grund zurückgeht, in die Einheit, welche als rückkehrend die reflektirte Einheit ist, aber indem diese ebenso sehr sich als aufgehobene gesetzt hat, bezieht sie sich negativ auf sich selbst, hebt sich auf, und macht sich zur seyenden Unmittelbarkeit. Aber diese ihre negative Beziehung, insofern sie ein Erstes und Unmittelbares ist, ist nur vermittelt durch ihr Anderes, und ebenso sehr ein Gesetztes. Dieß Andere, die seyende Unmittelbarkeit, ist ebenso sehr nur als aufgehobene; ihre Selbstständigkeit ist ein Erstes, aber nur um zu verschwinden, und hat ein Daseyn, das gesetzt und vermittelt ist.\n\nIn dieser Bestimmung ist das Verhältniß nicht mehr das des Ganzen und der Theile; die Unmittelbarkeit, welche seine Seiten hatten, ist in Gesetztseyn und Vermittelung übergegangen; es ist jede gesetzt, insofern sie unmittelbar ist, als sich aufhebend, und in die andere übergehend; und insofern sie selbst negative Beziehung ist, zugleich durch die andere als durch ihr Positives bedingt zu seyn; wie auch ihr unmittelbares Übergehen ebenso sehr ein Vermitteltes ist, ein Aufheben nämlich, das durch die andere gesetzt wird.—So ist das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile in das Verhältniß der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung übergegangen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0001","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das wesentliche Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"146.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0002","text":"Die Wahrheit der Erscheinung ist das wesentliche Verhältniß. Sein Inhalt hat unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit, und zwar die seyende Unmittelbarkeit, und die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit oder die mit sich identische Reflexion. Zugleich ist er in dieser Selbstständigkeit ein relativer, schlechthin nur als Reflexion in sein Anderes, oder als Einheit der Beziehung mit seinem Andern. In dieser Einheit ist der selbstständige Inhalt ein Gesetztes, Aufgehobenes; aber eben diese Einheit macht seine Wesentlichkeit und Selbstständigkeit aus; diese Reflexion in Anderes ist Reflexion in sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"146.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0003","text":"Das Verhältniß hat Seiten, weil es Reflexion in Anderes ist; so hat es den Unterschied seiner selbst an ihm; und die Seiten desselben sind selbstständiges Bestehen, indem sie in ihrer gleichgültigen Verschiedenheit gegen einander, in sich selbst gebrochen sind, so daß das Bestehen einer jeden, ebenso sehr nur seine Bedeutung in der Beziehung auf die andere oder in ihrer negativen Einheit hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"146.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0004","text":"Das wesentliche Verhältniß ist daher zwar noch nicht das wahrhafte Dritte zum Wesen und zur Existenz; aber enthält bereits die bestimmte Vereinigung beider. Das Wesen ist in ihm so realisirt, daß es selbstständig-existirende zu seinem Bestehen hat; und diese sind aus ihrer Gleichgültigkeit in ihre wesentliche Einheit zurückgegangen, so daß sie nur diese zu ihrem Bestehen haben. Die Reflexions-Bestimmungen des Positiven und Negativen sind gleichfalls in sich reflektirte nur als reflektirt in ihr Entgegengesetztes; aber sie haben keine andere Bestimmung als diese ihre negative Einheit; das wesentliche Verhältniß hingegen hat solche zu seinen Seiten, welche als selbstständige Totalitäten gesetzt sind. Es ist dieselbe Entgegensetzung als die des Positiven und Negativen; aber zugleich als eine verkehrte Welt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"146.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0005","text":"Die Seite des wesentlichen Verhältnisses ist eine Totalität, die aber als wesentlich ein Entgegengesetztes, ein Jenseits seiner hat; es ist nur Erscheinung; seine Existenz ist vielmehr nicht die seinige, sondern die seines Andern. Es ist daher ein in sich selbst Gebrochenes; aber dieß sein Aufgehobenseyn besteht darin, daß es die Einheit seiner selbst und seines Andern also Ganzes ist, und eben darum hat es selbstständige Existenz und ist wesentliche Reflexion in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"146.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0006","text":"Dieß ist der Begriff des Verhältnisses. Zunächst aber ist die Identität, die es enthält, noch nicht vollkommen; die Totalität, welche jedes relative an ihm selbst ist, ist erst ein Inneres; die Seite des Verhältnisses ist zunächst gesetzt in einer der Bestimmungen der negativen Einheit; die eigene Selbstständigkeit jeder der beiden Seiten ist dasjenige, was die Form des Verhältnisses ausmacht. Seine Identität ist daher nur eine Beziehung, außerhalb welcher ihre Selbstständigkeit fällt; nämlich in die Seiten; es ist noch nicht die reflektirte Einheit jener Identität und der selbstständigen Existenzen vorhanden, noch nicht die Substanz.—Der Begriff des Verhältnisses hat sich daher zwar ergeben, Einheit der reflektirten und der unmittelbaren Selbstständigkeit zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"146.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0007","text":"Aber zuerst ist dieser Begriff selbst noch unmittelbar, seine Momente daher unmittelbare gegen einander, und die Einheit deren wesentliche Beziehung, die erst dann die wahrhafte, dem Begriffe entsprechende Einheit ist, insofern sie sich realisirt, nämlich durch ihre Bewegung als jene Einheit gesetzt hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"146.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0008","text":"Das wesentliche Verhältniß ist daher unmittelbar das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile;—die Beziehung der reflektirten und der unmittelbaren Selbstständigkeit, so daß beide zugleich nur sind als sich gegenseitig bedingend und voraussetzend.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"146.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0009","text":"In diesem Verhältnisse ist noch keine der Seiten als Moment der andern gesetzt, ihre Identität ist daher selbst eine Seite; oder sie ist nicht ihre negative Einheit. Es geht darum zweitens darein über, daß die eine Moment der andern und in ihr als in ihrem Grunde, dem wahrhaft Selbstständigen von beiden, ist;—Verhältniß der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"146.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0010","text":"Drittens hebt sich die noch vorhandene Ungleichheit dieser Beziehung auf, und das letzte Verhältniß ist das des Innern und Äußern.—In diesem ganz formell gewordenen Unterschiede geht das Verhältniß selbst zu Grunde, und die Substanz oder das Wirkliche tritt hervor, als die absolute Einheit der unmittelbaren und der reflektirten Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"146.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0011","text":"## A. Das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"146.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0012","text":"Das wesentliche Verhältniß enthält erstens die in sich reflektirte Selbstständigkeit der Existenz; so ist es die einfache Form, deren Bestimmungen zwar auch Existenzen, aber zugleich gesetzte, Momente in der Einheit gehalten, sind. Diese in sich reflektirte Selbstständigkeit ist zugleich Reflexion in ihr Entgegengesetztes, nämlich die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit; und ihr Bestehen ist wesentlich ebenso sehr als es eigene Selbstständigkeit ist, diese Identität mit seinem Entgegengesetzten.—Eben damit ist auch unmittelbar zweitens die andre Seite gesetzt; die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit, welche als das Andre bestimmt, eine vielfache Mannigfaltigkeit in sich ist, aber so daß diese Mannigfaltigkeit wesentlich auch die Beziehung der andern Seite, die Einheit der reflektirten Selbstständigkeit an ihr hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"146.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0013","text":"Jene Seite, das Ganze, ist die Selbstständigkeit, welche die an und für sich seyende Welt ausmachte; die andere Seite, die Theile, ist die unmittelbare Existenz, welche die erscheinende Welt war. Im Verhältnisse des Ganzen und der Theile sind die beiden Seiten diese Selbstständigkeiten, aber so daß jede die andere in ihr scheinen hat, und nur ist zugleich als diese Identität beider.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"146.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0014","text":"Weil nun das wesentliche Verhältniß nur erst das erste, unmittelbare ist, so ist die negative Einheit und die positive Selbstständigkeit durch das Auch verbunden; beide Seiten sind zwar als Momente gesetzt, aber ebenso sehr als existirende Selbstständigkeiten.—Daß beide als Momente gesetzt sind, dieß ist daher so vertheilt, daß erstens das Ganze, die reflektirte Selbstständigkeit, als Existirendes und in ihr die andere, die unmittelbare als Moment ist;—hier macht das Ganze die Einheit beider Seiten, die Grundlage aus, und die unmittelbare Existenz ist als Gesetztseyn.—Umgekehrt ist auf der andern Seite, nämlich der Seite der Theile, die unmittelbare, in sich mannigfaltige Existenz, die selbstständige Grundlage; die reflektirte Einheit dagegen, das Ganze ist nur äußerliche Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"146.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0015","text":"2. Dieß Verhältniß enthält somit die Selbstständigkeit der Seiten, und ebenso sehr ihr Aufgehobenseyn, und beides schlechthin in Einer Beziehung. Das Ganze ist das Selbstständige, die Theile sind nur Momente dieser Einheit; aber ebenso sehr sind sie auch das Selbstständige, und ihre reflektirte Einheit nur ein Moment; und jedes ist in seiner Selbstständigkeit schlechthin das Relative eines Andern. Dieß Verhältniß ist daher der unmittelbare Widerspruch an ihm selbst, und hebt sich auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"146.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0016","text":"Dieß näher betrachtet, so ist das Ganze die reflektirte Einheit, welche selbstständiges Bestehen für sich hat; aber dieß ihr Bestehen ist ebenso sehr von ihr abgestoßen; das Ganze ist als die negative Einheit, negative Beziehung auf sich selbst; so ist sie sich entäußert; sie hat ihr Bestehen an ihrem Entgegengesetzten, der mannigfaltigen Unmittelbarkeit, den Theilen. Das Ganze besteht daher aus den Theilen; so daß es nicht etwas ist ohne sie. Es ist also das ganze Verhältniß und die selbstständige Totalität; aber gerade aus demselben Grunde ist es nur ein Relatives, denn was es zur Totalität macht, ist vielmehr sein Anderes, die Theile; und es hat nicht an sich selbst, sondern an seinem Andern sein Bestehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"146.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0017","text":"So sind die Theile gleichfalls das ganze Verhältniß. Sie sind die unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit gegen die reflektirte, und bestehen nicht im Ganzen, sondern sind für sich. Sie haben ferner dieß Ganze als ihr Moment an ihnen; es macht ihre Beziehung aus; ohne Ganzes giebt es keine Theile. Aber weil sie das Selbstständige sind, so ist diese Beziehung nur ein äußerliches Moment, gegen welches sie an und für sich gleichgültig sind. Zugleich aber fallen die Theile als mannigfaltige Existenz in sich selbst zusammen, denn diese ist das reflexionslose Seyn; sie haben ihre Selbstständigkeit nur in der reflektirten Einheit, welche sowohl diese Einheit als auch die existirende Mannigfaltigkeit ist; das heißt, sie haben Selbstständigkeit nur im Ganzen, das aber zugleich die den Theilen andere Selbstständigkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"146.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0018","text":"Das Ganze und die Theile bedingen sich daher gegenseitig; aber das hier betrachtete Verhältniß, steht zugleich höher, als die Beziehung des Bedingten und der Bedingung auf einander, wie sie sich oben bestimmt hatte. Diese Beziehung ist hier realisirt; nämlich es ist gesetzt, daß die Bedingung so die wesentliche Selbstständigkeit des Bedingten ist, daß sie durch dieses vorausgesetzt wird. Die Bedingung als solche ist nur das Unmittelbare, und nur an sich vorausgesetzt. Das Ganze aber ist die Bedingung zwar der Theile, aber es enthält zugleich unmittelbar selbst, daß auch es nur ist, insofern es die Theile zur Voraussetzung hat. Indem so beide Seiten des Verhältnisses gesetzt sind als sich gegenseitig bedingend, ist jede eine unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit an ihr selbst, aber ihre Selbstständigkeit ist ebenso sehr vermittelt oder gesetzt durch die andere.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"146.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0019","text":"Das ganze Verhältniß ist durch diese Gegenseitigkeit die Rückkehr des Bedingens in sich selbst, das nicht Relative, das Unbedingte.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"146.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0020","text":"Indem nun die Seiten des Verhältnisses jede nicht in ihr selbst ihre Selbstständigkeit, sondern in ihrer andern hat, so ist nur Eine Identität beider vorhanden, in welcher beide nur Momente sind; aber indem jede an ihr selbst selbstständig ist, so sind sie zwei selbstständige Existenzen, die gegen einander gleichgültig sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"146.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0021","text":"Nach der ersten Rüksicht, der wesentlichen Identität dieser Seiten, ist das Ganze den Theilen und die Theile dem Ganzen gleich. Es ist nichts im Ganzen, was nicht in den Theilen, und nichts in den Theilen, was nicht im Ganzen ist. Das Ganze ist nicht abstrakte Einheit, sondern die Einheit als einer verschiedenen Mannigfaltigkeit; diese Einheit aber als das, worin das Mannigfaltige sich auf einander bezieht, ist die Bestimmtheit desselben, wodurch es Theil ist. Das Verhältniß hat also eine untrennbare Identität, und mir Eine Selbstständigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"146.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0022","text":"Aber ferner ist das Ganze den Theilen gleich; allein nicht denselben als Theilen; das Ganze ist die reflektirte Einheit, die Theile aber machen das bestimmte Moment oder das Andersseyn der Einheit aus, und sind das verschiedene Mannigfaltige. Das Ganze ist ihnen nicht gleich als diesem selbstständigen Verschiedenen, sondern als ihnen zusammen. Dieß ihr Zusammen aber ist nichts Anderes, als ihre Einheit, das Ganze als solches. Das Ganze ist also in den Theilen nur sich selbst gleich, und die Gleichheit desselben und der Theile drückt nur die Tautologie aus, daß das Ganze als Ganzes nicht den Theilen, sondern dem Ganzen gleich ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"146.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0023","text":"Umgekehrt sind die Theile dem Ganzen gleich; aber weil sie das Moment des Andersseyns an ihnen selbst sind, so sind sie ihm nicht gleich als der Einheit, sondern so daß eine seiner mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen auf den Theil kommt, oder daß sie ihm als Mannigfaltigem gleich sind; das heißt, sie sind ihm als getheiltem Ganzen d. i. als den Theilen gleich. Es ist hiermit dieselbe Tautologie vorhanden, daß die Theile als Theile, nicht dem Ganzen als solchem, sondern in ihm sich selbst, den Theilen, gleich sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"146.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0024","text":"Das Ganze und die Theile fallen auf diese Weise gleichgültig aus einander; jede dieser Seiten bezieht sich nur auf sich. Aber so aus einander gehalten zerstören sie sich selbst. Das Ganze, das gleichgültig ist gegen die Theile, ist die abstrakte, in sich nicht unterschiedene Identität; diese ist Ganzes nur als in sich selbst unterschieden, und zwar so in sich unterschieden, daß diese mannigfaltigen Bestimmungen in sich reflektirt sind und unmittelbare Selbstständigkeit haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"146.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0025","text":"Und die Reflexionsidentität hat sich durch ihre Bewegung gezeigt, diese Reflexion in ihr Anderes zu ihrer Wahrheit zu haben.—Ebenso sind die Theile als gleichgültig gegen die Einheit des Ganzen, nur das unbezogene Mannigfaltige, das in sich Andere, welches als solches das Andere seiner selbst und sich nur Aufhebende ist.—Diese Beziehung-auf-sich jeder der beiden Seiten, ist ihre Selbstständigkeit; aber diese ihre Selbstständigkeit, die jede für sich hat, ist vielmehr die Negation ihrer selbst. Jede hat daher ihre Selbstständigkeit nicht an ihr selbst, sondern an der andern; diese andere, die das Bestehen ausmacht, ist ihr vorausgesetztes Unmittelbare, das Erstes und ihr Anfang seyn soll; aber dieses Erste einer jeder ist selbst nur ein solches, das nicht Erstes ist, sondern an dem andern seinen Anfang hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"146.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0026","text":"Die Wahrheit des Verhältnisses besteht also in der Vermittelung; sein Wesen ist die negative Einheit, in welcher ebenso wohl die reflektirte als die seyende Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben sind. Das Verhältniß ist der Widerspruch, der in seinen Grund zurückgeht, in die Einheit, welche als rückkehrend die reflektirte Einheit ist, aber indem diese ebenso sehr sich als aufgehobene gesetzt hat, bezieht sie sich negativ auf sich selbst, hebt sich auf, und macht sich zur seyenden Unmittelbarkeit. Aber diese ihre negative Beziehung, insofern sie ein Erstes und Unmittelbares ist, ist nur vermittelt durch ihr Anderes, und ebenso sehr ein Gesetztes. Dieß Andere, die seyende Unmittelbarkeit, ist ebenso sehr nur als aufgehobene; ihre Selbstständigkeit ist ein Erstes, aber nur um zu verschwinden, und hat ein Daseyn, das gesetzt und vermittelt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"146.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0027","text":"In dieser Bestimmung ist das Verhältniß nicht mehr das des Ganzen und der Theile; die Unmittelbarkeit, welche seine Seiten hatten, ist in Gesetztseyn und Vermittelung übergegangen; es ist jede gesetzt, insofern sie unmittelbar ist, als sich aufhebend, und in die andere übergehend; und insofern sie selbst negative Beziehung ist, zugleich durch die andere als durch ihr Positives bedingt zu seyn; wie auch ihr unmittelbares Übergehen ebenso sehr ein Vermitteltes ist, ein Aufheben nämlich, das durch die andere gesetzt wird.—So ist das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile in das Verhältniß der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung übergegangen.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"146.27"}],"sha256":"1bbd2502d702e57872291f7b22e6ed29f602d78abf5c2fc7337b6a42c8c88c1b","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105647482541Z_20dc68df","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Relation of Whole and Parts.","source_sha256":"1bbd2502d702e57872291f7b22e6ed29f602d78abf5c2fc7337b6a42c8c88c1b","sha256":"e88ac5b4b77af380c161270a43a9da3775a89e616cd08fb7d4cb98ade4219f5f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:56:47.482595+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0001","text":"## Third Chapter. The Essential Relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"146.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0002","text":"The truth of appearance is the essential relation. Its content has immediate self-subsistence, namely, the being immediacy, and reflected immediacy, or reflection identical with itself. At the same time, in this self-subsistence it is a relative, solely as reflection into its other, or as unity of relation with its other. In this unity the self-subsistent content is a posited, a sublated; but precisely this unity constitutes its essentiality and self-subsistence; this reflection into other is reflection into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"146.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0003","text":"Relation has sides, because it is reflection into other; thus it has the difference of itself within it; and its sides are self-subsistent existence, inasmuch as, in their indifferent difference from one another, they are broken within themselves, so that the subsistence of each has its significance equally only in relation to the other or in their negative unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"146.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0004","text":"The essential relation is therefore indeed not yet the true third to essence and existence; but it already contains the determinate union of both. Essence is realized in it in such a way that it has self-subsistently existing things for its subsistence; and these have returned from their indifference into their essential unity, so that they have only this as their subsistence. The determinations of reflection, positive and negative, are likewise reflected into themselves only as reflected into their opposite; but they have no other determination than this their negative unity; the essential relation, on the other hand, has such things for its sides as are posited as self-subsistent totalities. It is the same opposition as that of positive and negative; but at the same time as an inverted world.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"146.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0005","text":"The side of the essential relation is a totality which, however, essentially has an opposite, a beyond, of itself; it is only appearance; its existence is rather not its own, but that of its other. It is therefore broken within itself; but this its sublatedness consists in its being the unity of itself and its other, thus a whole, and precisely for that reason it has self-subsistent existence and is essential reflection into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"146.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0006","text":"This is the concept of relation. At first, however, the identity which it contains is not yet complete; the totality which each relative is in itself is at first only an inner; the side of relation is initially posited in one of the determinations of negative unity; the self-subsistence proper to each of the two sides is what constitutes the form of relation. Its identity is therefore only a relation, outside of which their self-subsistence falls; namely, into the sides; the reflected unity of that identity and of the self-subsistent existences is not yet present, not yet substance.—The concept of relation has therefore indeed emerged as being the unity of reflected and immediate self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"146.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0007","text":"But at first this concept itself is still immediate; its moments are therefore immediate with respect to one another, and their unity is essential relation, which is only then the true unity corresponding to the concept, in so far as it realizes itself, namely, has posited itself through its movement as that unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"146.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0008","text":"The essential relation is therefore immediately the relation of whole and parts;—the relation of reflected and immediate self-subsistence, such that both at once are only as mutually conditioning and presupposing one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"146.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0009","text":"In this relation neither side is yet posited as a moment of the other; their identity is therefore itself a side; or it is not their negative unity. It therefore passes over, secondly, into the fact that one is a moment of the other and is in it as in its ground, the truly self-subsistent of the two;—the relation of force and its expression.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"146.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0010","text":"Thirdly, the inequality of this relation still present is sublated, and the final relation is that of inner and outer.—In this distinction, which has become wholly formal, relation itself perishes, and substance, or the actual, emerges as the absolute unity of immediate and reflected existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"146.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0011","text":"## A. The Relation of Whole and Parts.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"146.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0012","text":"The essential relation contains, first, the self-subsistence of existence reflected into itself; thus it is the simple form, whose determinations are indeed likewise existences, but at the same time posited, moments held in unity. This self-subsistence reflected into itself is at the same time reflection into its opposite, namely immediate self-subsistence; and its subsistence, essentially as much as it is its own self-subsistence, is this identity with its opposite.—Thereby the other side too is immediately posited, secondly; immediate self-subsistence, which, as determined as the other, is a manifold multiplicity within itself, but such that this multiplicity essentially also has within it the relation of the other side, the unity of reflected self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"146.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0013","text":"That side, the whole, is the self-subsistence which constituted the world that is in and for itself; the other side, the parts, is immediate existence, which was the world of appearance. In the relation of whole and parts, the two sides are these self-subsistences, but in such a way that each has the other appearing within it, and is at once only as this identity of both.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"146.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0014","text":"Now because the essential relation is as yet only the first, immediate one, negative unity and positive self-subsistence are connected by the also; the two sides are indeed posited as moments, but equally as existing self-subsistences.—That both are posited as moments is therefore distributed in such a way that, first, the whole, reflected self-subsistence, is as existing, and the other, the immediate, is a moment within it;—here the whole constitutes the unity of both sides, the foundation, and immediate existence is as positedness.—Conversely, on the other side, namely that of the parts, immediate existence, manifold within itself, is the self-subsistent foundation; reflected unity, on the other hand, the whole, is only external relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"146.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0015","text":"2. This relation thus contains the self-subsistence of the sides, and equally their sublatedness, and both absolutely in one relation. The whole is the self-subsistent, the parts are only moments of this unity; but equally they too are the self-subsistent, and their reflected unity only a moment; and each, in its self-subsistence, is absolutely the relative of an other. This relation is therefore the immediate contradiction within itself, and sublates itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"146.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0016","text":"Considered more closely, the whole is the reflected unity which has self-subsistent subsistence for itself; but this its subsistence is equally repelled from it; the whole, as negative unity, is negative relation to itself; thus it externalizes itself; it has its subsistence in its opposite, in manifold immediacy, the parts. The whole therefore consists of the parts; so that it is not something without them. It is thus the entire relation and the self-subsistent totality; but precisely for the same reason it is only a relative, for what makes it a totality is rather its other, the parts; and it has its subsistence not in itself, but in its other.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"146.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0017","text":"Thus the parts likewise are the entire relation. They are immediate self-subsistence as against reflected self-subsistence, and do not subsist in the whole, but are for themselves. They further have this whole as their moment within them; it constitutes their relation; without a whole there are no parts. But because they are the self-subsistent, this relation is only an external moment, toward which they are indifferent in and for themselves. Yet at the same time the parts, as manifold existence, collapse into themselves, for this is reflectionless Being; they have their self-subsistence only in reflected unity, which is both this unity and the existing multiplicity; that is, they have self-subsistence only in the whole, which, however, is at the same time the self-subsistence other than that of the parts.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"146.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0018","text":"Whole and parts thus condition one another reciprocally; but the relation considered here at the same time stands higher than the relation of conditioned and condition to one another, as it had determined itself above. This relation is here realized; namely, it is posited that the condition is so much the essential self-subsistence of the conditioned that it is presupposed by the latter. The condition as such is only the immediate, and presupposed only in itself. But the whole is indeed the condition of the parts, yet it immediately contains in itself as well that it too is only in so far as it has the parts as presupposition. Since thus both sides of the relation are posited as mutually conditioning one another, each is an immediate self-subsistence in itself, but its self-subsistence is equally mediated or posited through the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"146.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0019","text":"Through this reciprocity, the entire relation is the return of conditioning into itself, the non-relative, the unconditioned.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"146.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0020","text":"Now since the sides of relation each have their self-subsistence not in themselves but in their other, there is only one identity of both, in which both are only moments; but since each is self-subsistent in itself, they are two self-subsistent existences that are indifferent to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"146.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0021","text":"According to the first respect, the essential identity of these sides, the whole is equal to the parts and the parts to the whole. There is nothing in the whole that is not in the parts, and nothing in the parts that is not in the whole. The whole is not abstract unity, but unity as of a differentiated multiplicity; but this unity, as that in which the manifold relates itself to one another, is its determinateness through which it is a part. Relation thus has an inseparable identity, and only one self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"146.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0022","text":"But further, the whole is equal to the parts; yet not to them as parts; the whole is reflected unity, while the parts constitute the determinate moment, or the otherness, of unity, and are the differentiated manifold. The whole is not equal to them as this self-subsistent differentiated, but as their togetherness. But this their togetherness is nothing other than their unity, the whole as such. The whole is thus equal only to itself in the parts, and the equality of it and the parts expresses only the tautology that the whole, as whole, is equal not to the parts but to the whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"146.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0023","text":"Conversely, the parts are equal to the whole; but because they have the moment of otherness in themselves, they are not equal to it as unity, but in such a way that one of its manifold determinations falls to the part, or that they are equal to it as manifold; that is, they are equal to it as divided whole, i.e. as the parts. Thus there is the same tautology that the parts, as parts, are equal not to the whole as such, but within it to themselves, the parts.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"146.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0024","text":"Whole and parts thus fall indifferently apart; each of these sides relates only to itself. But held apart in this way, they destroy themselves. The whole, which is indifferent to the parts, is abstract identity, undifferentiated within itself; this is a whole only as differentiated within itself, and indeed differentiated within itself in such a way that these manifold determinations are reflected into themselves and have immediate self-subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"146.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0025","text":"And reflective identity has shown itself, through its movement, to have this reflection into its other as its truth.—Likewise, the parts are indifferent to the unity of the whole, merely the unrelated manifold, the other within itself, which as such is the other of itself and only sublates itself.—This relation-to-self of each of the two sides is their self-subsistence; but this their self-subsistence, which each has for itself, is rather the negation of itself. Each therefore has its self-subsistence not in itself, but in the other; this other, which constitutes subsistence, is its presupposed immediacy, which is supposed to be first and its beginning; but this first of each is itself only such a first as is not first, but has its beginning in the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"146.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0026","text":"The truth of the relation thus consists in mediation; its essence is the negative unity in which reflective as well as being immediacy are sublated. The relation is the contradiction that returns into its ground, into the unity which, as returning, is reflective unity; but since this unity has equally posited itself as sublated, it relates negatively to itself, sublates itself, and makes itself into being immediacy. But this its negative relation, insofar as it is a first and immediate, is only mediated through its other, and equally is a posited. This other, being immediacy, likewise is only as sublated; its self-subsistence is a first, but only in order to vanish, and has an existence that is posited and mediated.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"146.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0027","text":"In this determination, the relation is no longer that of the whole and the parts; the immediacy which its sides had has passed over into positedness and mediation; each is posited, insofar as it is immediate, as sublating itself and passing over into the other; and insofar as it is itself negative relation, as at the same time being conditioned through the other as through its positive; just as its immediate transition is equally a mediated one, namely a sublation that is posited through the other.—Thus the relation of the whole and the parts has passed over into the relation of force and its manifestation.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"146.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DVLD:P0027"]}],"source_digest":"7afc68d96dd31dc30787a40ef6fa0bc157621800439c59a249389a62b83f5f23","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39","title":"Remark.","order":147,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_39","text":"Es ist oben (1ster Th. 1ste Abth. S. 216) die Antinomie der unendlichen Theilbarkeit der Materie, beim Begriffe der Quantität betrachtet worden. Die Quantität ist die Einheit der Kontinuität und der Diskretion; sie enthält im selbstständigen Eins sein Zusammengeflossenseyn mit andern, und in dieser sich ohne Unterbrechung fortsetzenden Identität mit sich ebenso die Negation derselben. Indem die unmittelbare Beziehung dieser Momente der Quantität, als das wesentliche Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile, das Eins der Quantität als Theil, die Kontinuität desselben aber als Ganzes, das zusammengesetzt ist aus Theilen, ausgedrückt wird, so besteht die Antinomie in dem Widerspruche, der am Verhältnisse des Ganzen und der Theile, vorgekommen und aufgelöst worden ist.—Ganzes und Theile sind nämlich ebenso wesentlich auf einander bezogen und machen nur Eine Identität aus, als sie gleichgültig gegen einander sind und selbstständiges Bestehen haben. Das Verhältniß ist daher diese Antinomie, daß das Eine Moment, darin, daß es sich vom andern befreit, unmittelbar das andere herbeiführt.\n\nDas Existirende also als Ganzes bestimmt, so hat es Theile, und die Theile machen sein Bestehen aus; die Einheit des Ganzen ist nur eine gesetzte Beziehung, eine äußere Zusammensetzung, welche das selbstständig Existirende nichts angeht. Insofern dieses nun Theil ist, so ist es nicht Ganzes, nicht Zusammengesetztes, somit Einfaches. Aber indem ihm die Beziehung auf ein Ganzes äußerlich ist, so geht sie dasselbe nichts an; das Selbstständige ist somit auch nicht an sich Theil; denn Theil ist es nur durch jene Beziehung. Aber indem es nun nicht Theil ist, so ist es Ganzes, denn es ist nur dieß Verhältniß von Ganzem und von Theilen vorhanden; und das Selbstständige ist eins von beiden. Indem es aber Ganzes ist, so ist es wieder zusammengesetzt; es besteht wieder aus Theilen und so fort ins Unendliche.—Diese Unendlichkeit besteht in nichts anderem als in der perennirenden Abwechslung der beiden Bestimmungen des Verhältnisses, in deren jeder die andere unmittelbar entsteht, so daß das Gesetztseyn jeder das Verschwinden ihrer selbst ist. Die Materie als Ganzes bestimmt, so besteht sie aus Theilen und an diesen wird das Ganze zur unwesentlichen Beziehung und verschwindet. Der Theil aber so für sich, ist er auch nicht Theil, sondern das Ganze.—Die Antinomie dieses Schlusses ganz nahe zusammengerückt, ist eigentlich diese: Weil das Ganze nicht das Selbstständige ist, ist der Theil das Selbstständige; aber weil er nur ohne das Ganze selbstständig ist, so ist er selbstständig, nicht als Theil, sondern vielmehr als Ganzes. Die Unendlichkeit des Progresses, der entsteht, ist die Unfähigkeit, die beiden Gedanken zusammen zu bringen, welche diese Vermittelung enthält, daß nämlich jede der beiden Bestimmungen durch ihre Selbstständigkeit und Trennung von der andern, in Unselbstständigkeit und in die andre übergeht.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0001","text":"Es ist oben (1ster Th. 1ste Abth. S. 216) die Antinomie der unendlichen Theilbarkeit der Materie, beim Begriffe der Quantität betrachtet worden. Die Quantität ist die Einheit der Kontinuität und der Diskretion; sie enthält im selbstständigen Eins sein Zusammengeflossenseyn mit andern, und in dieser sich ohne Unterbrechung fortsetzenden Identität mit sich ebenso die Negation derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"147.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0002","text":"Indem die unmittelbare Beziehung dieser Momente der Quantität, als das wesentliche Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile, das Eins der Quantität als Theil, die Kontinuität desselben aber als Ganzes, das zusammengesetzt ist aus Theilen, ausgedrückt wird, so besteht die Antinomie in dem Widerspruche, der am Verhältnisse des Ganzen und der Theile, vorgekommen und aufgelöst worden ist.—Ganzes und Theile sind nämlich ebenso wesentlich auf einander bezogen und machen nur Eine Identität aus, als sie gleichgültig gegen einander sind und selbstständiges Bestehen haben. Das Verhältniß ist daher diese Antinomie, daß das Eine Moment, darin, daß es sich vom andern befreit, unmittelbar das andere herbeiführt.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"147.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0003","text":"Das Existirende also als Ganzes bestimmt, so hat es Theile, und die Theile machen sein Bestehen aus; die Einheit des Ganzen ist nur eine gesetzte Beziehung, eine äußere Zusammensetzung, welche das selbstständig Existirende nichts angeht. Insofern dieses nun Theil ist, so ist es nicht Ganzes, nicht Zusammengesetztes, somit Einfaches. Aber indem ihm die Beziehung auf ein Ganzes äußerlich ist, so geht sie dasselbe nichts an; das Selbstständige ist somit auch nicht an sich Theil; denn Theil ist es nur durch jene Beziehung. Aber indem es nun nicht Theil ist, so ist es Ganzes, denn es ist nur dieß Verhältniß von Ganzem und von Theilen vorhanden; und das Selbstständige ist eins von beiden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"147.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0004","text":"Indem es aber Ganzes ist, so ist es wieder zusammengesetzt; es besteht wieder aus Theilen und so fort ins Unendliche.—Diese Unendlichkeit besteht in nichts anderem als in der perennirenden Abwechslung der beiden Bestimmungen des Verhältnisses, in deren jeder die andere unmittelbar entsteht, so daß das Gesetztseyn jeder das Verschwinden ihrer selbst ist. Die Materie als Ganzes bestimmt, so besteht sie aus Theilen und an diesen wird das Ganze zur unwesentlichen Beziehung und verschwindet. Der Theil aber so für sich, ist er auch nicht Theil, sondern das Ganze.—Die Antinomie dieses Schlusses ganz nahe zusammengerückt, ist eigentlich diese: Weil das Ganze nicht das Selbstständige ist, ist der Theil das Selbstständige; aber weil er nur ohne das Ganze selbstständig ist, so ist er selbstständig, nicht als Theil, sondern vielmehr als Ganzes.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"147.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0005","text":"Die Unendlichkeit des Progresses, der entsteht, ist die Unfähigkeit, die beiden Gedanken zusammen zu bringen, welche diese Vermittelung enthält, daß nämlich jede der beiden Bestimmungen durch ihre Selbstständigkeit und Trennung von der andern, in Unselbstständigkeit und in die andre übergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"147.5"}],"sha256":"9dbc63ef62a2013cdb9cd2aa8fba5dea63acc6e2c442b84f76512b9bd6b00004","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105653922577Z_237a50ee","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"9dbc63ef62a2013cdb9cd2aa8fba5dea63acc6e2c442b84f76512b9bd6b00004","sha256":"607ff5c2566994152a3245eb673aa2e4a850d2c5e599247a9e579874cde1dfa3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:56:53.922599+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0001","text":"Above (Part 1, Division 1, p. 216), the antinomy of the infinite divisibility of matter was considered under the concept of quantity. Quantity is the unity of continuity and discreteness; in its self-subsistent being-one it contains its having flowed together with others, and, in this identity with itself that continues without interruption, equally their negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"147.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_39:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0002","text":"Inasmuch as the immediate relation of these moments of quantity is expressed as the essential relation of the whole and the parts—the one of quantity as part, but its continuity as whole, which is composed of parts—the antinomy consists in the contradiction that has occurred and been resolved in the relation of the whole and the parts.—For whole and parts are as essentially related to one another and constitute only one identity as they are indifferent to one another and possess self-subsistent existence. The relation is therefore this antinomy: that the one moment, in that it frees itself from the other, immediately brings forth the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"147.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_39:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0003","text":"Thus, if what exists is determined as whole, it has parts, and the parts constitute its subsistence; the unity of the whole is only a posited relation, an external composition, which does not concern what exists self-subsistently. Insofar as this is now part, it is not whole, not composite, hence simple. But since the relation to a whole is external to it, it does not concern it; what is self-subsistent is thus also not in itself part; for it is part only through that relation. But since it is now not part, it is whole, for only this relation of whole and parts is present; and what is self-subsistent is one of the two.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"147.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_39:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0004","text":"But inasmuch as it is whole, it is again composite; it again consists of parts, and so on to infinity.—This infinity consists in nothing other than the perennial alternation of the two determinations of the relation, in each of which the other immediately arises, so that the positedness of each is the vanishing of itself. Matter determined as whole thus consists of parts, and in these the whole becomes an inessential relation and vanishes. But the part, thus for itself, is likewise not part, but the whole.—The antinomy of this inference, brought quite close together, is properly this: Because the whole is not what is self-subsistent, the part is what is self-subsistent; but because it is self-subsistent only without the whole, it is self-subsistent not as part, but rather as whole.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"147.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_39:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_39:P0005","text":"The infinity of the progression that arises is the incapacity to bring together the two thoughts contained in this mediation: namely, that each of the two determinations, through its self-subsistence and separation from the other, passes over into non-self-subsistence and into the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"147.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_39:P0005"]}],"source_digest":"d01907dbd45e003204428886fd5c95cbafc426489b9d708c1696a7097cfbd58b","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL","title":"B. The Relation of Force and Its Expression.","order":148,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDVL","text":"Die Kraft ist die negative Einheit, in welche sich der Widerspruch des Ganzen und der Theile aufgelöst hat, die Wahrheit jenes ersten Verhältnisses. Das Ganze und die Theile ist das gedankenlose Verhältniß, auf welches die Vorstellung zunächst verfällt; oder objektiv ist es das todte, mechanische Aggregat, das zwar Formbestimmungen hat, wodurch die Mannigfaltigkeit seiner selbstständigen Materie in einer Einheit bezogen wird, welche aber derselben äußerlich ist.—Das Verhältniß der Kraft aber ist die höhere Rückkehr in sich, worin die Einheit des Ganzen, welche die Beziehung des selbstständigen Andersseyns ausmachte, aufhört, dieser Mannigfaltigkeit ein Äußerliches und Gleichgültiges zu seyn.\n\nWie sich das wesentliche Verhältniß nunmehr bestimmt hat, sind die unmittelbare und die reflektirte Selbstständigkeit in derselben als aufgehobene oder als Momente gesetzt, die im vorhergehenden Verhältnisse für sich bestehende Seiten oder Extreme waren. Es ist darin enthalten erstens, daß die reflektirte Einheit, und ihr unmittelbares Daseyn, insofern beide erste und unmittelbare sind, sich an sich selbst aufheben und in ihr Anderes übergehen; jene, die Kraft, geht in ihre Äußerung, über, und das Äußerliche ist ein Verschwindendes, das in die Kraft, als in ihren Grund zurückgeht, und nur ist, als von derselben getragen und gesetzt. Zweitens ist dieß Übergehen nicht nur ein Werden und Verschwinden, sondern es ist negative Beziehung auf sich, oder das seine Bestimmung Ändernde ist darin zugleich in sich reflektirt und erhält sich; die Bewegung der Kraft ist nicht so sehr ein Übergehen, als daß sie sich selbst über setzt, und in dieser durch sie selbst gesetzten Veränderung bleibt, was sie ist.—Drittens ist diese reflektirte, sich auf sich beziehende Einheit selbst auch aufgehoben und Moment; sie ist vermittelt durch ihr Anderes, und hat dasselbe zur Bedingung; ihre negative Beziehung auf sich, die Erstes ist und die Bewegung ihres Übergehens aus sich anfängt, hat ebenso sehr eine Voraussetzung, von der sie sollicitirt wird, und ein Anderes, von dem sie anfängt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0001","text":"Die Kraft ist die negative Einheit, in welche sich der Widerspruch des Ganzen und der Theile aufgelöst hat, die Wahrheit jenes ersten Verhältnisses. Das Ganze und die Theile ist das gedankenlose Verhältniß, auf welches die Vorstellung zunächst verfällt; oder objektiv ist es das todte, mechanische Aggregat, das zwar Formbestimmungen hat, wodurch die Mannigfaltigkeit seiner selbstständigen Materie in einer Einheit bezogen wird, welche aber derselben äußerlich ist.—Das Verhältniß der Kraft aber ist die höhere Rückkehr in sich, worin die Einheit des Ganzen, welche die Beziehung des selbstständigen Andersseyns ausmachte, aufhört, dieser Mannigfaltigkeit ein Äußerliches und Gleichgültiges zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"148.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0002","text":"Wie sich das wesentliche Verhältniß nunmehr bestimmt hat, sind die unmittelbare und die reflektirte Selbstständigkeit in derselben als aufgehobene oder als Momente gesetzt, die im vorhergehenden Verhältnisse für sich bestehende Seiten oder Extreme waren. Es ist darin enthalten erstens, daß die reflektirte Einheit, und ihr unmittelbares Daseyn, insofern beide erste und unmittelbare sind, sich an sich selbst aufheben und in ihr Anderes übergehen; jene, die Kraft, geht in ihre Äußerung, über, und das Äußerliche ist ein Verschwindendes, das in die Kraft, als in ihren Grund zurückgeht, und nur ist, als von derselben getragen und gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"148.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0003","text":"Zweitens ist dieß Übergehen nicht nur ein Werden und Verschwinden, sondern es ist negative Beziehung auf sich, oder das seine Bestimmung Ändernde ist darin zugleich in sich reflektirt und erhält sich; die Bewegung der Kraft ist nicht so sehr ein Übergehen, als daß sie sich selbst über setzt, und in dieser durch sie selbst gesetzten Veränderung bleibt, was sie ist.—Drittens ist diese reflektirte, sich auf sich beziehende Einheit selbst auch aufgehoben und Moment; sie ist vermittelt durch ihr Anderes, und hat dasselbe zur Bedingung; ihre negative Beziehung auf sich, die Erstes ist und die Bewegung ihres Übergehens aus sich anfängt, hat ebenso sehr eine Voraussetzung, von der sie sollicitirt wird, und ein Anderes, von dem sie anfängt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"148.3"}],"sha256":"e5e11a691674388a469056a17ba59e34c4b68735477190c5e3fb51949b998b11","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105703195147Z_0436e5e2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. The Relation of Force and Its Expression.","source_sha256":"e5e11a691674388a469056a17ba59e34c4b68735477190c5e3fb51949b998b11","sha256":"317899c026c94cb7e430a1a910b4befe19a39add210b3b5655a388f560d85bbd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:57:03.195166+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0001","text":"Force is the negative unity into which the contradiction of the whole and the parts has resolved itself, the truth of that first relation. The whole and the parts is the thoughtless relation upon which representation initially falls; or, objectively, it is the dead, mechanical aggregate, which indeed has determinations of form through which the multiplicity of its self-subsistent matter is related in a unity, but which is external to it.—The relation of force, however, is the higher return into itself, in which the unity of the whole, which constituted the relation of self-subsistent otherness, ceases to be something external and indifferent to this multiplicity.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"148.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0002","text":"As the essential relation has now determined itself, immediate and reflected self-subsistence are posited in it as sublated, or as moments, which in the preceding relation were sides or extremes existing for themselves. It contains, first, that the reflected unity and its immediate existence, insofar as both are first and immediate, sublate themselves in themselves and pass over into their other; the former, force, passes over into its manifestation, and the external is something vanishing, which returns into force as into its ground, and only is as borne and posited by it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"148.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0003","text":"Secondly, this transition is not merely a becoming and vanishing, but it is a negative relation to itself, or that which alters its determination is therein at the same time reflected into itself and maintains itself; the movement of force is not so much a transition as that it translates itself, and in this alteration posited by itself remains what it is.—Thirdly, this reflected unity relating itself to itself is itself likewise sublated and a moment; it is mediated through its other and has the same as its condition; its negative relation to itself, which is first and begins the movement of its transition out of itself, equally has a presupposition from which it is solicited, and an other from which it begins.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"148.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDVL:P0003"]}],"source_digest":"29f25eb320ce550e1a5bfa0d09859e80bdd456758e4bd71635cd846013d8f278","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Das Verhältniß der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Das Verhältniß der Kraft und ihrer Äußerung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK","title":"a. The Conditionedness of Force.","order":149,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DBDK","text":"In ihren näheren Bestimmungen betrachtet, hat erstens die Kraft das Moment der seyenden Unmittelbarkeit an ihr; sie selbst ist dagegen bestimmt als die negative Einheit. Aber diese in der Bestimmung des unmittelbaren Seyns ist ein existirendes Etwas. Dieß Etwas erscheint, weil es die negative Einheit als Unmittelbares ist, als das Erste, die Kraft dagegen, weil sie das reflektirte ist, als das Gesetztseyn, und insofern als angehörig dem existirenden Dinge oder einer Materie. Nicht daß sie die Form dieses Dings und das Ding durch sie bestimmt wäre; sondern das Ding ist als Unmittelbares gleichgültig gegen sie. —Es liegt in ihm nach dieser Bestimmung kein Grund, eine Kraft zu haben; die Kraft hingegen als die Seite des Gesetztseyns hat wesentlich das Ding zu seiner Voraussetzung. Wenn daher gefragt wird, wie das Ding oder die Materie dazu komme, eine Kraft zu haben, so erscheint diese als äußerlich damit verbunden und dem Dinge durch eine fremde Gewalt eingedrückt.\n\nAls dieß unmittelbare Bestehen ist die Kraft eine ruhige Bestimmtheit des Dings überhaupt; nicht ein sich Äußerndes, sondern unmittelbar ein äußerliches. So wird die Kraft auch als Materie bezeichnet, und statt magnetischer, elektrischer u.s.f. Kraft, eine magnetische, elektrische u.s.f. Materie angenommen; oder statt der berühmten anziehenden Kraft ein feiner Äther, der alles zusammenhalte.—Es sind die Materien, in welche sich die unthätige, kraftlose negative Einheit des Dings auflöst, und die oben betrachtet wurden.\n\nAber die Kraft enthält die unmittelbare Existenz, als Moment, als ein solches das zwar Bedingung ist, aber übergeht und sich aufhebt; also nicht als ein existirendes Ding. Sie ist ferner nicht die Negation als Bestimmtheit, sondern negative, sich in sich reflektirende Einheit. Das Ding, an dem die Kraft seyn sollte, hat somit hier keine Bedeutung mehr; sie selbst ist vielmehr Setzen der Äußerlichkeit, welche als Existenz erscheint. Sie ist also auch nicht bloß eine bestimmte Materie; solche Selbstständigkeit ist längst in das Gesetztseyn und in die Erscheinung übergegangen.\n\nZweitens, die Kraft ist die Einheit des reflektirten und des unmittelbaren Bestehens, oder der Formeinheit und der äußerlichen Selbstständigkeit. Sie ist beides in Einem; sie ist die Berührung solcher, deren das Eine ist, insofern das Andere nicht ist; die mit sich identische positive, und die negirte Reflexion. Die Kraft ist so der sich von sich selbst abstoßende Widerspruch; sie ist thätig; oder sie ist die sich auf sich beziehende negative Einheit, in welcher die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit oder das wesentliche Insichseyn gesetzt ist, nur als Aufgehobenes oder Moment zu seyn, somit insofern sie sich von der unmittelbaren Existenz unterscheidet, in diese überzugehen. Die Kraft also als die Bestimmung der reflektirten Einheit des Ganzen ist gesetzt, als zur existirenden äußerlichen Mannigfaltigkeit aus sich selbst zu werden.\n\nAber drittens ist die Kraft nur erst ansichseyende und unmittelbare Thätigkeit; sie ist die reflektirte Einheit, und ebenso wesentlich die Negation derselben; indem sie von dieser verschieden, aber nur als die Identität ihrer selbst und ihrer Negation ist, so ist sie auf diese, als eine ihr äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit wesentlich bezogen und hat dieselbe zur Voraussetzung und Bedingung.\n\nDiese Voraussetzung nun ist nicht ein ihr gegenüber sich befindliches Ding; diese gleichgültige Selbstständigkeit ist in der Kraft aufgehoben; als ihre Bedingung ist es ein ihr anderes Selbstständiges. Weil es aber nicht Ding ist, sondern die selbstständige Unmittelbarkeit hier sich zugleich als sich auf sich selbst beziehende negative Einheit bestimmt hat, so ist es selbst Kraft. —Die Thätigkeit der Kraft ist durch sich selbst als durch das sich Andere, durch eine Kraft bedingt.\n\nDie Kraft ist auf diese Weise Verhältniß, in welchem jede Seite dasselbe ist als die andere. Es sind Kräfte, die im Verhältnisse stehen, und zwar wesentlich sich auf einander beziehen.—Sie sind ferner zunächst nur verschiedene überhaupt; die Einheit ihres Verhältnisses ist nur erst die innre an sich seyende Einheit. Das Bedingtseyn durch eine andere Kraft ist so an sich das Thun der Kraft selbst; oder sie ist insofern erst voraus setzendes, sich nur negativ auf sich beziehendes Thun; diese andere Kraft liegt noch jenseits ihrer setzenden Thätigkeit, nämlich der in ihrem Bestimmen unmittelbar in sich zurückkehrenden Reflexion.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0001","text":"In ihren näheren Bestimmungen betrachtet, hat erstens die Kraft das Moment der seyenden Unmittelbarkeit an ihr; sie selbst ist dagegen bestimmt als die negative Einheit. Aber diese in der Bestimmung des unmittelbaren Seyns ist ein existirendes Etwas. Dieß Etwas erscheint, weil es die negative Einheit als Unmittelbares ist, als das Erste, die Kraft dagegen, weil sie das reflektirte ist, als das Gesetztseyn, und insofern als angehörig dem existirenden Dinge oder einer Materie. Nicht daß sie die Form dieses Dings und das Ding durch sie bestimmt wäre; sondern das Ding ist als Unmittelbares gleichgültig gegen sie. —Es liegt in ihm nach dieser Bestimmung kein Grund, eine Kraft zu haben; die Kraft hingegen als die Seite des Gesetztseyns hat wesentlich das Ding zu seiner Voraussetzung.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"149.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0002","text":"Wenn daher gefragt wird, wie das Ding oder die Materie dazu komme, eine Kraft zu haben, so erscheint diese als äußerlich damit verbunden und dem Dinge durch eine fremde Gewalt eingedrückt.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"149.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0003","text":"Als dieß unmittelbare Bestehen ist die Kraft eine ruhige Bestimmtheit des Dings überhaupt; nicht ein sich Äußerndes, sondern unmittelbar ein äußerliches. So wird die Kraft auch als Materie bezeichnet, und statt magnetischer, elektrischer u.s.f. Kraft, eine magnetische, elektrische u.s.f. Materie angenommen; oder statt der berühmten anziehenden Kraft ein feiner Äther, der alles zusammenhalte.—Es sind die Materien, in welche sich die unthätige, kraftlose negative Einheit des Dings auflöst, und die oben betrachtet wurden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"149.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0004","text":"Aber die Kraft enthält die unmittelbare Existenz, als Moment, als ein solches das zwar Bedingung ist, aber übergeht und sich aufhebt; also nicht als ein existirendes Ding. Sie ist ferner nicht die Negation als Bestimmtheit, sondern negative, sich in sich reflektirende Einheit. Das Ding, an dem die Kraft seyn sollte, hat somit hier keine Bedeutung mehr; sie selbst ist vielmehr Setzen der Äußerlichkeit, welche als Existenz erscheint. Sie ist also auch nicht bloß eine bestimmte Materie; solche Selbstständigkeit ist längst in das Gesetztseyn und in die Erscheinung übergegangen.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"149.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0005","text":"Zweitens, die Kraft ist die Einheit des reflektirten und des unmittelbaren Bestehens, oder der Formeinheit und der äußerlichen Selbstständigkeit. Sie ist beides in Einem; sie ist die Berührung solcher, deren das Eine ist, insofern das Andere nicht ist; die mit sich identische positive, und die negirte Reflexion. Die Kraft ist so der sich von sich selbst abstoßende Widerspruch; sie ist thätig; oder sie ist die sich auf sich beziehende negative Einheit, in welcher die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit oder das wesentliche Insichseyn gesetzt ist, nur als Aufgehobenes oder Moment zu seyn, somit insofern sie sich von der unmittelbaren Existenz unterscheidet, in diese überzugehen. Die Kraft also als die Bestimmung der reflektirten Einheit des Ganzen ist gesetzt, als zur existirenden äußerlichen Mannigfaltigkeit aus sich selbst zu werden.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"149.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0006","text":"Aber drittens ist die Kraft nur erst ansichseyende und unmittelbare Thätigkeit; sie ist die reflektirte Einheit, und ebenso wesentlich die Negation derselben; indem sie von dieser verschieden, aber nur als die Identität ihrer selbst und ihrer Negation ist, so ist sie auf diese, als eine ihr äußerliche Unmittelbarkeit wesentlich bezogen und hat dieselbe zur Voraussetzung und Bedingung.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"149.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0007","text":"Diese Voraussetzung nun ist nicht ein ihr gegenüber sich befindliches Ding; diese gleichgültige Selbstständigkeit ist in der Kraft aufgehoben; als ihre Bedingung ist es ein ihr anderes Selbstständiges. Weil es aber nicht Ding ist, sondern die selbstständige Unmittelbarkeit hier sich zugleich als sich auf sich selbst beziehende negative Einheit bestimmt hat, so ist es selbst Kraft. —Die Thätigkeit der Kraft ist durch sich selbst als durch das sich Andere, durch eine Kraft bedingt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"149.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0008","text":"Die Kraft ist auf diese Weise Verhältniß, in welchem jede Seite dasselbe ist als die andere. Es sind Kräfte, die im Verhältnisse stehen, und zwar wesentlich sich auf einander beziehen.—Sie sind ferner zunächst nur verschiedene überhaupt; die Einheit ihres Verhältnisses ist nur erst die innre an sich seyende Einheit. Das Bedingtseyn durch eine andere Kraft ist so an sich das Thun der Kraft selbst; oder sie ist insofern erst voraus setzendes, sich nur negativ auf sich beziehendes Thun; diese andere Kraft liegt noch jenseits ihrer setzenden Thätigkeit, nämlich der in ihrem Bestimmen unmittelbar in sich zurückkehrenden Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"149.8"}],"sha256":"6050557e4f2efbf46f0d6b43cf5ef4aefc538750e2678c13b0cd47972c6c19e7","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105714927409Z_92ecda51","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. The Conditionedness of Force.","source_sha256":"6050557e4f2efbf46f0d6b43cf5ef4aefc538750e2678c13b0cd47972c6c19e7","sha256":"aeb99f73410f6d61ee0ae2e8e916785ad72ab3d18707b09f1b5ad06d7b9f9381","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:57:14.927420+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0001","text":"Considered in its more determinate specifications, force has, firstly, the moment of being immediacy within it; it itself, on the other hand, is determined as the negative unity. But this, in the determination of immediate being, is an existent something. This something appears, because it is the negative unity as an immediate, as the first; force, on the other hand, because it is the reflected, as positedness, and insofar as belonging to the existent thing or to a matter. Not that it is the form of this thing and that the thing would be determined through it; rather, the thing, as immediate, is indifferent to it. —According to this determination, there lies in it no ground for having a force; force, by contrast, as the side of positedness, essentially has the thing as its presupposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"149.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0002","text":"If, therefore, it is asked how the thing or matter comes to have a force, then this appears as externally connected with it and impressed upon the thing by an alien power.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"149.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0003","text":"As this immediate subsistence, force is a tranquil determinacy of the thing in general; not something expressing itself, but immediately something external. Thus force too is designated as matter, and instead of magnetic, electrical, etc. force, a magnetic, electrical, etc. matter is assumed; or, instead of the celebrated attractive force, a subtle ether that holds everything together.—These are the matters into which the inactive, powerless negative unity of the thing dissolves, and which were considered above.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"149.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0004","text":"But force contains immediate existence as a moment, as something which is indeed condition, but passes over and sublates itself; thus, not as an existent thing. Further, it is not negation as determinacy, but negative unity reflecting itself into itself. The thing on which force was supposed to be thus no longer has any significance here; rather, force itself is the positing of externality, which appears as existence. Thus it is not merely a determinate matter either; such self-subsistence has long since passed over into positedness and into appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"149.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0005","text":"Secondly, force is the unity of reflected and immediate subsistence, or of the unity of form and external self-subsistence. It is both in one; it is the contact of such terms, of which the one is insofar as the other is not; the positive reflection identical with itself, and the negated reflection. Force is thus the contradiction repelling itself from itself; it is active; or it is the negative unity relating itself to itself, in which reflected immediacy, or essential being-within-itself, is posited as being only something sublated or a moment, hence, insofar as it distinguishes itself from immediate existence, as passing over into it. Force, therefore, as the determinacy of the reflected unity of the whole, is posited as becoming, out of itself, existent external multiplicity.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"149.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0006","text":"But thirdly, force is at first only activity that is in itself and immediate; it is reflected unity, and equally essentially its negation; since it is different from this, yet only as the identity of itself and its negation, it is essentially related to this as to an immediacy external to it, and has it as presupposition and condition.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"149.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0007","text":"This presupposition, now, is not a thing situated over against it; this indifferent self-subsistence is sublated in force; as its condition, it is a self-subsistent other to it. But since it is not a thing, but self-subsistent immediacy has here at the same time determined itself as negative unity relating itself to itself, it is itself force. —The activity of force is conditioned through itself as through the othering itself, through a force.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"149.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0008","text":"In this way force is a relation in which each side is the same as the other. There are forces that stand in relation, and indeed essentially relate themselves to one another.—Further, they are at first only different in general; the unity of their relation is as yet only the inner unity that is in itself. Thus, being conditioned by another force is in itself the doing of force itself; or, to that extent, it is at first presupposing activity, activity relating itself to itself only negatively; this other force still lies beyond its positing activity, namely, beyond the reflection that immediately returns into itself in its determining.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"149.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DBDK:P0008"]}],"source_digest":"1979f59df56ea87120bdbe8ce3af09505c524af28f6d920df66d5b779c93ff6f","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Das Bedingtseyn der Kraft."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Das Bedingtseyn der Kraft.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD","title":"b. The Solicitation of Force.","order":150,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDSD","text":"Die Kraft ist bedingt, weil das Moment der unmittdbaren Existenz, das sie enthält, nur als ein Gesetztes,—aber weil es zugleich Unmittelbares ist, ein Vorausgesetztes ist, in welchem die Kraft sich selbst negirt. Die für die Kraft vorhandene Äußerlichkeit ist daher ihre eigene voraussetzende Thätigkeit selbst, welche zunächst als eine andere Kraft gesetzt ist.\n\nDieses Voraussetzen ist ferner gegenseitig. Jede der beiden Kräfte enthält die in sich reflektirte Einheit als aufgehoben, und ist daher voraussetzend; sie setzt sich selbst als äußerlich; dieß Moment der Äußerlichkeit ist ihr eigenes; aber weil sie ebenso sehr in sich reflektirte Einheit ist, setzt sie zugleich diese ihre Äußerlichkeit nicht in ihr selbst, sondern als eine andre Kraft.\n\nAber das Äußerliche als solches ist das sich selbst aufhebende; ferner die sich in sich reflektirende Thätigkeit ist wesentlich bezogen auf jenes Äußerliche als auf das ihr Andre, aber ebenso sehr als auf ein an sich Nichtiges und mit ihr Identisches. Da die voraussetzende Thätigkeit ebenso sehr Reflexion in sich ist, ist sie das Aufheben jener ihrer Negation, und setzt dieselbe als sich selbst oder als ihr Äußerliches. So ist die Kraft als bedingend, gegenseitig ein Anstoß für die andre Kraft, gegen den sie thätig ist. Ihr Verhalten ist nicht die Passivität des Bestimmtwerdens, so daß dadurch etwas Anderes in sie käme; sondern der Anstoß sollicitirt sie nur. Sie ist an ihr selbst die Negativität ihrer, das Abstoßen ihrer von sich ist ihr eigenes Setzen. Ihr Thun besteht also darin, dieß aufzuheben, daß jener Anstoß ein Äußerliches sey; sie macht es zu einem bloßen Anstoß und setzt es als das eigne Abstoßen ihrer selbst von sich, als ihre eigene Äußerung.\n\nDie sich äußernde Kraft ist also dasselbe, was zuerst nur die voraussetzende Thätigkeit war; nämlich sich äußerlich machend; aber die Kraft als sich äußernd ist zugleich die Äußerlichkeit negirende und sie als das ihrige setzende Thätigkeit. Insofern nun in dieser Betrachtung von der Kraft angefangen wird, als sie die negative Einheit ihrer selbst und damit voraussetzende Reflexion ist, so ist es dasselbe, als wenn in der Äußerung der Kraft vom sollicitirenden Anstosse angefangen wird. Die Kraft ist so in ihrem Begriffe zuerst bestimmt als sich aufhebende Identität, und in ihrer Realität, die eine der beiden Kräfte als sollicitirend und die andere als sollicitirt werdend. Aber der Begriff der Kraft ist überhaupt die Identität der setzenden und voraussetzenden Reflexion oder der reflektirten und der unmittelbaren Einheit, und jede dieser Bestimmungen schlechthin nur Moment, in Einheit, und somit als vermittelt durch die andere. Aber ebenso ist keine Bestimmung an den beiden in Wechselbeziehung stehenden Kräften vorhanden, welche die sollicitirende oder die sollicitirt werdende sey, oder vielmehr jeder kommen auf gleiche Weise beide Formbestimmungen zu. Aber diese Identität ist nicht nur eine äußerliche der Vergleichung, sondern eine wesentliche Einheit derselben.\n\nDie eine Kraft nämlich ist zunächst bestimmt als sollicitirende, und die andere als sollicitirt-werdende; diese Formbestimmungen erscheinen auf diese Weise als unmittelbare, an sich vorhandene Unterschiede der beiden Kräfte. Aber sie sind wesentlich vermittelt. Die eine Kraft wird sollicitirt; dieser Anstoß ist eine in sie von außen gesetzte Bestimmung. Aber die Kraft ist selbst das Voraussetzende; sie ist wesentlich sich in sich reflektirend und es aufhebend, daß der Anstoß ein Äußerliches sey. Daß sie sollicitirt wird, ist daher ihr eigenes Thun, oder es ist durch sie selbst bestimmt, daß die andere Kraft eine andere überhaupt und die sollicitirende ist. Die sollicitirende bezieht sich auf ihre andere negativ, so daß sie die Äußerlichkeit derselben aufhebt, sie ist insofern setzend; aber sie ist dieß nur durch die Voraussetzung, sich eine andere gegenüber zu haben; das ist, sie ist sollicitirend selbst nur, insofern sie eine Äußerlichkeit an ihr hat, somit insofern sie sollicitirt wird. Oder sie ist sollicitirend nur insofern als sie dazu sollicitirt wird, sollicitirend zu seyn. Somit wird umgekehrt die erste sollicitirt, nur insofern als sie selbst die andere dazu sollicitirt, sie, nämlich die erstere zu sollicitiren. Jede von beiden erhält also den Anstoß von der anderen; aber der Aiistoß, den sie als thätige gibt, besteht darin, daß sie von der anderen einen Anstoß erhalte; der Anstoß, den sie erhält, ist von ihr selbst sollicitirt. Beides, der gegebene und der empfangene Anstoß, oder die thätige Äußerung und die passive Äußerlichkeit ist daher nicht ein Unmittelbares, sondern vermittelt, und zwar ist jede der beiden Kräfte hiermit selbst die Bestimmtheit, welche die andere gegen sie hat, ist vermittelt durch die andere, und dieß vermittelnde Andere ist wieder ihr eigenes bestimmendes Setzen.\n\nSo ist also dieß, daß auf die Kraft ein Anstoß durch eine andere Kraft geschieht, daß sie sich insofern passiv verhält, aber hinwieder von dieser Passivität in die Aktivität übergeht,—der Rükgang der Kraft in sie selbst. Sie äussert sich. Die Äußerung ist Reaktion in dem Sinne, daß sie die Äußerlichkeit als ihr eigenes Moment setzt, und somit es aufhebt, daß sie durch eine andere Kraft sollicitirt worden sey. Beides ist daher eines, die Äußerung der Kraft, wodurch sie sich durch ihre negative Thätigkeit auf sich selbst ein Daseyn-für-Anderes giebt, und die unendliche Rückkehr in dieser Äußerlichkeit auf sich selbst, so daß sie darin sich nur auf sich bezieht. Die voraussetzende Reflexion, welcher das Bedingtseyn und der Anstoß angehört, ist daher unmittelbar auch die in sich zurückkehrende Reflexion, und die Thätigkeit ist wesentlich reagirende, gegen sich. Das Setzen des Anstoßes oder Äußerlichen ist selbst das Aufheben desselben, und umgekehrt ist das Aufheben des Anstoßes das Setzen der Äußerlichkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0001","text":"Die Kraft ist bedingt, weil das Moment der unmittdbaren Existenz, das sie enthält, nur als ein Gesetztes,—aber weil es zugleich Unmittelbares ist, ein Vorausgesetztes ist, in welchem die Kraft sich selbst negirt. Die für die Kraft vorhandene Äußerlichkeit ist daher ihre eigene voraussetzende Thätigkeit selbst, welche zunächst als eine andere Kraft gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"150.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0002","text":"Dieses Voraussetzen ist ferner gegenseitig. Jede der beiden Kräfte enthält die in sich reflektirte Einheit als aufgehoben, und ist daher voraussetzend; sie setzt sich selbst als äußerlich; dieß Moment der Äußerlichkeit ist ihr eigenes; aber weil sie ebenso sehr in sich reflektirte Einheit ist, setzt sie zugleich diese ihre Äußerlichkeit nicht in ihr selbst, sondern als eine andre Kraft.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"150.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0003","text":"Aber das Äußerliche als solches ist das sich selbst aufhebende; ferner die sich in sich reflektirende Thätigkeit ist wesentlich bezogen auf jenes Äußerliche als auf das ihr Andre, aber ebenso sehr als auf ein an sich Nichtiges und mit ihr Identisches. Da die voraussetzende Thätigkeit ebenso sehr Reflexion in sich ist, ist sie das Aufheben jener ihrer Negation, und setzt dieselbe als sich selbst oder als ihr Äußerliches. So ist die Kraft als bedingend, gegenseitig ein Anstoß für die andre Kraft, gegen den sie thätig ist. Ihr Verhalten ist nicht die Passivität des Bestimmtwerdens, so daß dadurch etwas Anderes in sie käme; sondern der Anstoß sollicitirt sie nur. Sie ist an ihr selbst die Negativität ihrer, das Abstoßen ihrer von sich ist ihr eigenes Setzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"150.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0004","text":"Ihr Thun besteht also darin, dieß aufzuheben, daß jener Anstoß ein Äußerliches sey; sie macht es zu einem bloßen Anstoß und setzt es als das eigne Abstoßen ihrer selbst von sich, als ihre eigene Äußerung.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"150.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0005","text":"Die sich äußernde Kraft ist also dasselbe, was zuerst nur die voraussetzende Thätigkeit war; nämlich sich äußerlich machend; aber die Kraft als sich äußernd ist zugleich die Äußerlichkeit negirende und sie als das ihrige setzende Thätigkeit. Insofern nun in dieser Betrachtung von der Kraft angefangen wird, als sie die negative Einheit ihrer selbst und damit voraussetzende Reflexion ist, so ist es dasselbe, als wenn in der Äußerung der Kraft vom sollicitirenden Anstosse angefangen wird. Die Kraft ist so in ihrem Begriffe zuerst bestimmt als sich aufhebende Identität, und in ihrer Realität, die eine der beiden Kräfte als sollicitirend und die andere als sollicitirt werdend.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"150.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0006","text":"Aber der Begriff der Kraft ist überhaupt die Identität der setzenden und voraussetzenden Reflexion oder der reflektirten und der unmittelbaren Einheit, und jede dieser Bestimmungen schlechthin nur Moment, in Einheit, und somit als vermittelt durch die andere. Aber ebenso ist keine Bestimmung an den beiden in Wechselbeziehung stehenden Kräften vorhanden, welche die sollicitirende oder die sollicitirt werdende sey, oder vielmehr jeder kommen auf gleiche Weise beide Formbestimmungen zu. Aber diese Identität ist nicht nur eine äußerliche der Vergleichung, sondern eine wesentliche Einheit derselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"150.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0007","text":"Die eine Kraft nämlich ist zunächst bestimmt als sollicitirende, und die andere als sollicitirt-werdende; diese Formbestimmungen erscheinen auf diese Weise als unmittelbare, an sich vorhandene Unterschiede der beiden Kräfte. Aber sie sind wesentlich vermittelt. Die eine Kraft wird sollicitirt; dieser Anstoß ist eine in sie von außen gesetzte Bestimmung. Aber die Kraft ist selbst das Voraussetzende; sie ist wesentlich sich in sich reflektirend und es aufhebend, daß der Anstoß ein Äußerliches sey. Daß sie sollicitirt wird, ist daher ihr eigenes Thun, oder es ist durch sie selbst bestimmt, daß die andere Kraft eine andere überhaupt und die sollicitirende ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"150.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0008","text":"Die sollicitirende bezieht sich auf ihre andere negativ, so daß sie die Äußerlichkeit derselben aufhebt, sie ist insofern setzend; aber sie ist dieß nur durch die Voraussetzung, sich eine andere gegenüber zu haben; das ist, sie ist sollicitirend selbst nur, insofern sie eine Äußerlichkeit an ihr hat, somit insofern sie sollicitirt wird. Oder sie ist sollicitirend nur insofern als sie dazu sollicitirt wird, sollicitirend zu seyn. Somit wird umgekehrt die erste sollicitirt, nur insofern als sie selbst die andere dazu sollicitirt, sie, nämlich die erstere zu sollicitiren. Jede von beiden erhält also den Anstoß von der anderen; aber der Aiistoß, den sie als thätige gibt, besteht darin, daß sie von der anderen einen Anstoß erhalte; der Anstoß, den sie erhält, ist von ihr selbst sollicitirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"150.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0009","text":"Beides, der gegebene und der empfangene Anstoß, oder die thätige Äußerung und die passive Äußerlichkeit ist daher nicht ein Unmittelbares, sondern vermittelt, und zwar ist jede der beiden Kräfte hiermit selbst die Bestimmtheit, welche die andere gegen sie hat, ist vermittelt durch die andere, und dieß vermittelnde Andere ist wieder ihr eigenes bestimmendes Setzen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"150.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0010","text":"So ist also dieß, daß auf die Kraft ein Anstoß durch eine andere Kraft geschieht, daß sie sich insofern passiv verhält, aber hinwieder von dieser Passivität in die Aktivität übergeht,—der Rükgang der Kraft in sie selbst. Sie äussert sich. Die Äußerung ist Reaktion in dem Sinne, daß sie die Äußerlichkeit als ihr eigenes Moment setzt, und somit es aufhebt, daß sie durch eine andere Kraft sollicitirt worden sey. Beides ist daher eines, die Äußerung der Kraft, wodurch sie sich durch ihre negative Thätigkeit auf sich selbst ein Daseyn-für-Anderes giebt, und die unendliche Rückkehr in dieser Äußerlichkeit auf sich selbst, so daß sie darin sich nur auf sich bezieht. Die voraussetzende Reflexion, welcher das Bedingtseyn und der Anstoß angehört, ist daher unmittelbar auch die in sich zurückkehrende Reflexion, und die Thätigkeit ist wesentlich reagirende, gegen sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"150.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0011","text":"Das Setzen des Anstoßes oder Äußerlichen ist selbst das Aufheben desselben, und umgekehrt ist das Aufheben des Anstoßes das Setzen der Äußerlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"150.11"}],"sha256":"48fd2aa26eed0695ad2b37c30c46235aec96f14f5066bef735e5145bb438f32e","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105727096416Z_8b354a53","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The Solicitation of Force.","source_sha256":"48fd2aa26eed0695ad2b37c30c46235aec96f14f5066bef735e5145bb438f32e","sha256":"14cff9dd536108e6d3835e99963b4c2099cb5663fb2ea81245b28dc9701a776d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:57:27.096426+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0001","text":"Force is conditioned, because the moment of immediate existence which it contains is only as a posited [moment],—but because it is at the same time immediate, it is a presupposed [moment], in which force negates itself. The externality present for force is therefore its own presupposing activity itself, which is at first posited as another force.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"150.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0002","text":"This presupposing is further reciprocal. Each of the two forces contains the unity reflected into itself as sublated, and is therefore presupposing; it posits itself as external; this moment of externality is its own; but because it is equally much unity reflected into itself, it at the same time posits this its externality not in itself, but as another force.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"150.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0003","text":"But the external as such is that which sublates itself; further, the activity reflecting itself into itself is essentially related to that external as to its other, but equally much as to something null in itself and identical with it. Since the presupposing activity is equally much reflection into itself, it is the sublation of that its negation, and posits the latter as itself or as its externality. Thus force, as conditioning, is reciprocally an impulse for the other force, against which it is active. Its relation is not the passivity of being determined, such that something other would thereby enter into it; rather, the impulse merely solicits it. It is in itself its own negativity; its repulsion of itself from itself is its own positing.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"150.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0004","text":"Its doing therefore consists in sublating the fact that that impulse is an externality; it makes it into a mere impulse and posits it as its own repulsion of itself from itself, as its own expression.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"150.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0005","text":"The expressing force is therefore the same as what at first was only the presupposing activity; namely, making itself external; but force as expressing is at the same time the activity negating externality and positing it as its own. Now insofar as, in this consideration, one starts from force, as it is the negative unity of itself and thereby presupposing reflection, this is the same as if, in the expression of force, one started from the soliciting impulse. Force is thus at first determined in its concept as self-sublating identity, and in its reality as one of the two forces soliciting and the other being solicited.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"150.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0006","text":"But the concept of force in general is the identity of positing and presupposing reflection, or of reflected and immediate unity, and each of these determinations is absolutely only a moment, in unity, and thus as mediated through the other. Yet likewise there is no determination present in the two forces standing in reciprocal relation, such that one would be the soliciting or the solicited one; or rather, both form-determinations belong to each in the same way. But this identity is not merely an external one of comparison, but an essential unity of them.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"150.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0007","text":"One force, namely, is at first determined as soliciting, and the other as being solicited; these form-determinations thus appear as immediate differences of the two forces existing in themselves. But they are essentially mediated. The one force is solicited; this impulse is a determination posited in it from without. But force is itself the presupposing; it is essentially reflecting itself into itself and sublating the fact that the impulse is an externality. That it is solicited is therefore its own doing, or it is determined through itself that the other force is another at all and is the soliciting one.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"150.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0008","text":"The soliciting force relates negatively to its other, such that it sublates the latter's externality; to that extent it is positing; but it is this only through the presupposition of having an other confronting it; that is, it is itself soliciting only insofar as it has an externality in it, thus insofar as it is solicited. Or it is soliciting only insofar as it is solicited to be soliciting. Thus, conversely, the first is solicited only insofar as it itself solicits the other to solicit it, namely, the former. Each of the two therefore receives the impulse from the other; but the impulse which it gives as active consists in its receiving an impulse from the other; the impulse which it receives is solicited by itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"150.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0009","text":"Both, the impulse given and the impulse received, or active expression and passive externality, are therefore not an immediate, but mediated, and indeed each of the two forces is thereby itself the determinacy which the other has over against it, is mediated through the other, and this mediating other is again its own determining positing.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"150.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0010","text":"Thus, then, the fact that an impulse occurs upon force through another force, that it behaves passively to that extent, but in turn passes over from this passivity into activity,—is the return of force into itself. It expresses itself. Expression is reaction in the sense that it posits externality as its own moment, and thereby sublates the fact that it was solicited by another force. Both are therefore one: the expression of force, through which it gives itself, by its negative activity, a being-for-another, and the infinite return in this externality into itself, so that in it it relates only to itself. Presupposing reflection, to which conditionedness and impulse belong, is therefore immediately also reflection returning into itself, and activity is essentially reacting, against itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"150.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0011","text":"The positing of the impulse or of the external is itself the sublation of the same, and conversely, the sublation of the impulse is the positing of externality.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"150.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDSD:P0011"]}],"source_digest":"8afb019dfeba4cc3de8f1c08de8da27e05a768c29adf7aaef3023bece72a37ea","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Die Sollicitation der Kraft."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Die Sollicitation der Kraft.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_3","title":"c. The Infinity of Force.","order":151,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CD_3","text":"Die Kraft ist endlich, insofern ihre Momente noch die Form der Unmittelbarkeit haben; ihre voraussetzende und ihre sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion sind in dieser Bestimmung unterschieden; jene erscheint als eine für sich bestehende äußerliche Kraft, und die andere in der Beziehung auf sie als passiv. Die Kraft ist so der Form nach bedingt, und dem Inhalte nach gleichfalls beschränkt; denn eine Bestimmtheit der Form nach enthält auch eine Beschränkung des Inhalts. Aber die Thätigkeit der Kraft besteht darin sich zu äußern; das heißt, wie sich ergeben hat, die Äußerlichkeit aufzuheben und sie als das zu bestimmen, worin sie identisch mit sich ist. Was also die Kraft in Wahrheit äußert, ist dieß, daß ihre Beziehung auf Anderes ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, daß ihre Passivität in ihrer Aktivität selbst besteht. Der Anstoß, wodurch sie zur Thätigkeit sollicitirt wird, ist ihr eigenes Sollicitiren; die Äußerlichkeit, welche an sie kommt, ist kein Unmittelbares, sondern ein durch sie Vermitteltes; so wie ihre eigene wesentliche Identität mit sich, nicht unmittelbar, sondern durch ihre Negation vermittelt ist; oder die Kraft äußert dieß, daß ihre Äußerlichkeit identisch ist mit ihrer Innerlichkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_3:P0001","text":"Die Kraft ist endlich, insofern ihre Momente noch die Form der Unmittelbarkeit haben; ihre voraussetzende und ihre sich auf sich beziehende Reflexion sind in dieser Bestimmung unterschieden; jene erscheint als eine für sich bestehende äußerliche Kraft, und die andere in der Beziehung auf sie als passiv. Die Kraft ist so der Form nach bedingt, und dem Inhalte nach gleichfalls beschränkt; denn eine Bestimmtheit der Form nach enthält auch eine Beschränkung des Inhalts. Aber die Thätigkeit der Kraft besteht darin sich zu äußern; das heißt, wie sich ergeben hat, die Äußerlichkeit aufzuheben und sie als das zu bestimmen, worin sie identisch mit sich ist. Was also die Kraft in Wahrheit äußert, ist dieß, daß ihre Beziehung auf Anderes ihre Beziehung auf sich selbst ist, daß ihre Passivität in ihrer Aktivität selbst besteht.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"151.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_3:P0002","text":"Der Anstoß, wodurch sie zur Thätigkeit sollicitirt wird, ist ihr eigenes Sollicitiren; die Äußerlichkeit, welche an sie kommt, ist kein Unmittelbares, sondern ein durch sie Vermitteltes; so wie ihre eigene wesentliche Identität mit sich, nicht unmittelbar, sondern durch ihre Negation vermittelt ist; oder die Kraft äußert dieß, daß ihre Äußerlichkeit identisch ist mit ihrer Innerlichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"151.2"}],"sha256":"f9c1cc305559d26a9d2fd18bb4da6479fc712dee4f33385b40cc1c0b82e6f6a5","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105730301349Z_aff14dda","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. The Infinity of Force.","source_sha256":"f9c1cc305559d26a9d2fd18bb4da6479fc712dee4f33385b40cc1c0b82e6f6a5","sha256":"bc9241151bee4c9f820e81e3c2c7c9488b214d4570ee23f928ef4bf11d2215b4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:57:30.301381+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_3:P0001","text":"Force is finite insofar as its moments still have the form of immediacy; its presupposing reflection and its self-relating reflection are distinguished in this determination; the former appears as an externally existing force subsisting for itself, and the latter, in relation to it, as passive. Force is thus conditioned in respect of form, and likewise limited in respect of content; for a determinacy in respect of form also contains a limitation of content. But the activity of force consists in externalizing itself; that is, as has emerged, in sublating externality and determining it as that in which it is identical with itself. What force therefore truly externalizes is this: that its relation to another is its relation to itself, that its passivity consists in its activity itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"151.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_3:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_3:P0002","text":"The impulse by which it is solicited to activity is its own soliciting; the externality which comes to it is not an immediate, but one mediated through it; just as its own essential identity with itself is mediated not immediately, but through its negation; or force externalizes this: that its externality is identical with its inwardness.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"151.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_3:P0002"]}],"source_digest":"6fcbe951007b39d88d0241c1303a12426c8e1be2977c4a4befa1471fc8f2f274","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Die Unendlichkeit der Kraft."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Die Unendlichkeit der Kraft.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD","title":"C. The Relation of Outer and Inner.","order":152,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CVLD","text":"1. Das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile ist das unmittelbare; die reflektirte und die seyende Unmittelbarkeit haben daher in ihm jede eine eigene Selbstständigkeit; aber indem sie im wesentlichen Verhältnisse stehen, so ist ihre Selbstständigkeit nur ihre negative Einheit. Dieß ist nun in der Äußerung der Kraft gesetzt; die reflektirte Einheit ist wesentlich das Anderswerden, als Übersetzen ihrer selbst in die Äußerlichkeit; aber diese ist ebenso unmittelbar in jene zurückgenommen; der Unterschied der selbstständigen Kräfte hebt sich auf; die Äußerung der Kraft ist nur eine Vermittelung der reflektirten Einheit mit sich selbst. Es ist nur ein leerer durchsichtiger Unterschied, der Schein, vorhanden, aber dieser Schein ist die Vermittelung, welche das selbstständige Bestehen selbst ist. Es sind nicht nur entgegengesetzte Bestimmungen, die sich an ihnen selbst aufheben, und ihre Bewegung nicht nur ein Übergehen, sondern Theils ist die Unmittelbarkeit, von der angefangen und ins Andersseyn übergegangen wurde, selbst nur als gesetzte, Theils ist dadurch jede der Bestimmungen in ihrer Unmittelbarkeit schon die Einheit mit ihrer andern und das Übergehen dadurch schlechthin ebenso sehr die sich setzende Rückkehr in sich.\n\nDas Innere ist als die Form der reflektirten Unmittelbarkeit oder des Wesens, gegen das Äußere als die Form des Seyns bestimmt, aber beide sind nur Eine Identität.—Diese Identität ist erstens die gediegene Einheit beider als inhaltsvolle Grundlage, oder die absolute Sache, an der die beiden Bestimmungen gleichgültige, äußerliche Momente sind. Insofern ist sie Inhalt und die Totalität, welche das Innere ist, das ebenso sehr äußerlich wird, aber darin nicht ein Gewordenes oder Übergegangenes, sondern sich selbst gleich ist. Das Äußere ist nach dieser Bestimmung dem Innern, dem Inhalte nach nicht nur gleich, sondern beide sind nur Eine Sache.—Aber diese Sache als einfache Identität mit sich ist verschieden von ihren Formbestimmungen, oder diese sind ihr äußerlich; sie ist insofern selbst ein Inneres, das von ihrer Äußerlichkeit verschieden ist. Diese Äußerlichkeit aber besteht darin, daß die beiden Bestimmungen selbst, nämlich das Innere und Äußere, sie ausmachen. Aber die Sache ist selbst nichts Anderes, als die Einheit beider. Somit sind beide Seiten dem Inhalte nach wieder dasselbe. Aber in der Sache sind sie als sich durchdringende Identität, als inhaltsvolle Grundlage. Aber in der Äußerlichkeit, als Formen der Sache, sind sie gegen jene Identität und somit beide gegen einander gleichgültig.\n\n2. Sie sind auf diese Weise die verschiedenen Formbestimmungen, welche nicht an ihnen selbst, sondern an einem Andern eine identische Grundlage haben; Reflexions-Bestimmungen, die für sich sind; das Innere als die Form der Reflexion-in-sich, der Wesentlichkeit; das Äußere aber als die Form der in Anderes reflektirten Unmittelbarkeit, oder der Unwesentlichkeit. Allein die Natur des Verhältnisses hat gezeigt, daß diese Bestimmungen schlechthin nur eine Identität ausmachen. Die Kraft ist in ihrer Äußerung dieß, daß das voraussetzende und das in sich zurückkehrende Bestimmen eines und dasselbe ist. Insofern daher Inneres und Äußeres als Formbestimmungen betrachtet worden, so sind sie erstlich nur die einfache Form selbst, und zweitens weil sie darin zugleich als entgegengesetzte bestimmt sind, so ist ihre Einheit die reine abstrakte Vermittelung, in welcher die eine unmittelbar die andere, und darum die andere ist, weil sie die eine ist. So ist das Innere unmittelbar nur das Äußere, und es ist darum die Bestimmtheit der Äußerlichkeit, weil es das Innere ist; umgekehrt das Äußere ist nur ein Inneres, weil es nur ein Äußeres ist.—Indem nämlich diese Formeinheit ihre beiden Bestimmungen als entgegengesetzte enthält, ist ihre Identität nur dieß Übergehen; und darin nur die andere von beiden, nicht ihre inhaltsvolle Identität. Oder dieß Festhalten der Form ist überhaupt die Seite der Bestimmtheit. Was nach derselben gesetzt ist, ist nicht die reale Totalität des Ganzen, sondern die Totalität oder die Sache selbst nur in der Bestimmtheit der Form; weil diese die schlechthin zusammengebundene Einheit beider entgegengesetzter Bestimmungen ist, so ist, indem die eine zuerst genommen wird, und es ist gleichgültig, welche es sey, von der Grundlage oder Sache zu sagen, daß sie darum ebenso wesentlich in der andern Bestimmtheit, aber gleichfalls nur in der andern ist; so wie zuerst gesagt wurde, daß sie nur in der erstern ist.-So ist Etwas, das nur erst ein Inneres ist, eben darum nur ein Äußeres. Oder umgekehrt, etwas das nur ein Äußeres ist, ist eben darum nur ein Inneres. Oder indem das Innere als Wesen, das Äußere aber als Seyn bestimmt ist, so ist eine Sache, insofern sie nur in ihrem Wesen ist, eben darum nur ein unmittelbares Seyn; oder eine Sache, welche nur ist, ist eben darum nur erst noch in ihrem Wesen.—Das Äußere und Innere sind die Bestimmtheit so gesetzt, daß jede dieser beiden Bestimmungen, nicht nur die andere voraussetzt und in sie als in ihre Wahrheit übergeht, sondern daß sie, insofern sie diese Wahrheit der andern ist, als Bestimmtheit gesetzt bleibt, und auf die Totalität beider hinweist.—Das Innere ist somit die Vollendung des Wesens der Form nach. Das Wesen, indem es nämlich als Inneres bestimmt ist, enthält es, daß es mangelhaft und nur ist, als Beziehung auf sein Anderes, das Äußere; aber dieses ist ebenso nicht nur Seyn oder auch Existenz, sondern als auf das Wesen oder das Innere sich beziehend. Aber es ist nicht nur die Beziehung beider auf einander, sondern die bestimmte der absoluten Form, daß jedes unmittelbar sein Gegentheil ist, und ihre gemeinschaftliche Beziehung auf ihr Drittes oder vielmehr auf ihre Einheit vorhanden. Ihre Vermittelung entbehrt aber noch dieser sie beide enthaltenden identischen Grundlage; ihre Beziehung ist deswegen die unmittelbare Umkehrung des Einen in das Andere; und diese negative Einheit, die sie zusammenknüpft, ist der einfache, inhaltslose Punkt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0001","text":"1. Das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile ist das unmittelbare; die reflektirte und die seyende Unmittelbarkeit haben daher in ihm jede eine eigene Selbstständigkeit; aber indem sie im wesentlichen Verhältnisse stehen, so ist ihre Selbstständigkeit nur ihre negative Einheit. Dieß ist nun in der Äußerung der Kraft gesetzt; die reflektirte Einheit ist wesentlich das Anderswerden, als Übersetzen ihrer selbst in die Äußerlichkeit; aber diese ist ebenso unmittelbar in jene zurückgenommen; der Unterschied der selbstständigen Kräfte hebt sich auf; die Äußerung der Kraft ist nur eine Vermittelung der reflektirten Einheit mit sich selbst. Es ist nur ein leerer durchsichtiger Unterschied, der Schein, vorhanden, aber dieser Schein ist die Vermittelung, welche das selbstständige Bestehen selbst ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"152.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0002","text":"Es sind nicht nur entgegengesetzte Bestimmungen, die sich an ihnen selbst aufheben, und ihre Bewegung nicht nur ein Übergehen, sondern Theils ist die Unmittelbarkeit, von der angefangen und ins Andersseyn übergegangen wurde, selbst nur als gesetzte, Theils ist dadurch jede der Bestimmungen in ihrer Unmittelbarkeit schon die Einheit mit ihrer andern und das Übergehen dadurch schlechthin ebenso sehr die sich setzende Rückkehr in sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"152.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0003","text":"Das Innere ist als die Form der reflektirten Unmittelbarkeit oder des Wesens, gegen das Äußere als die Form des Seyns bestimmt, aber beide sind nur Eine Identität.—Diese Identität ist erstens die gediegene Einheit beider als inhaltsvolle Grundlage, oder die absolute Sache, an der die beiden Bestimmungen gleichgültige, äußerliche Momente sind. Insofern ist sie Inhalt und die Totalität, welche das Innere ist, das ebenso sehr äußerlich wird, aber darin nicht ein Gewordenes oder Übergegangenes, sondern sich selbst gleich ist. Das Äußere ist nach dieser Bestimmung dem Innern, dem Inhalte nach nicht nur gleich, sondern beide sind nur Eine Sache.—Aber diese Sache als einfache Identität mit sich ist verschieden von ihren Formbestimmungen, oder diese sind ihr äußerlich; sie ist insofern selbst ein Inneres, das von ihrer Äußerlichkeit verschieden ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"152.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0004","text":"Diese Äußerlichkeit aber besteht darin, daß die beiden Bestimmungen selbst, nämlich das Innere und Äußere, sie ausmachen. Aber die Sache ist selbst nichts Anderes, als die Einheit beider. Somit sind beide Seiten dem Inhalte nach wieder dasselbe. Aber in der Sache sind sie als sich durchdringende Identität, als inhaltsvolle Grundlage. Aber in der Äußerlichkeit, als Formen der Sache, sind sie gegen jene Identität und somit beide gegen einander gleichgültig.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"152.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0005","text":"2. Sie sind auf diese Weise die verschiedenen Formbestimmungen, welche nicht an ihnen selbst, sondern an einem Andern eine identische Grundlage haben; Reflexions-Bestimmungen, die für sich sind; das Innere als die Form der Reflexion-in-sich, der Wesentlichkeit; das Äußere aber als die Form der in Anderes reflektirten Unmittelbarkeit, oder der Unwesentlichkeit. Allein die Natur des Verhältnisses hat gezeigt, daß diese Bestimmungen schlechthin nur eine Identität ausmachen. Die Kraft ist in ihrer Äußerung dieß, daß das voraussetzende und das in sich zurückkehrende Bestimmen eines und dasselbe ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"152.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0006","text":"Insofern daher Inneres und Äußeres als Formbestimmungen betrachtet worden, so sind sie erstlich nur die einfache Form selbst, und zweitens weil sie darin zugleich als entgegengesetzte bestimmt sind, so ist ihre Einheit die reine abstrakte Vermittelung, in welcher die eine unmittelbar die andere, und darum die andere ist, weil sie die eine ist. So ist das Innere unmittelbar nur das Äußere, und es ist darum die Bestimmtheit der Äußerlichkeit, weil es das Innere ist; umgekehrt das Äußere ist nur ein Inneres, weil es nur ein Äußeres ist.—Indem nämlich diese Formeinheit ihre beiden Bestimmungen als entgegengesetzte enthält, ist ihre Identität nur dieß Übergehen; und darin nur die andere von beiden, nicht ihre inhaltsvolle Identität. Oder dieß Festhalten der Form ist überhaupt die Seite der Bestimmtheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"152.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0007","text":"Was nach derselben gesetzt ist, ist nicht die reale Totalität des Ganzen, sondern die Totalität oder die Sache selbst nur in der Bestimmtheit der Form; weil diese die schlechthin zusammengebundene Einheit beider entgegengesetzter Bestimmungen ist, so ist, indem die eine zuerst genommen wird, und es ist gleichgültig, welche es sey, von der Grundlage oder Sache zu sagen, daß sie darum ebenso wesentlich in der andern Bestimmtheit, aber gleichfalls nur in der andern ist; so wie zuerst gesagt wurde, daß sie nur in der erstern ist.-So ist Etwas, das nur erst ein Inneres ist, eben darum nur ein Äußeres. Oder umgekehrt, etwas das nur ein Äußeres ist, ist eben darum nur ein Inneres.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"152.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0008","text":"Oder indem das Innere als Wesen, das Äußere aber als Seyn bestimmt ist, so ist eine Sache, insofern sie nur in ihrem Wesen ist, eben darum nur ein unmittelbares Seyn; oder eine Sache, welche nur ist, ist eben darum nur erst noch in ihrem Wesen.—Das Äußere und Innere sind die Bestimmtheit so gesetzt, daß jede dieser beiden Bestimmungen, nicht nur die andere voraussetzt und in sie als in ihre Wahrheit übergeht, sondern daß sie, insofern sie diese Wahrheit der andern ist, als Bestimmtheit gesetzt bleibt, und auf die Totalität beider hinweist.—Das Innere ist somit die Vollendung des Wesens der Form nach. Das Wesen, indem es nämlich als Inneres bestimmt ist, enthält es, daß es mangelhaft und nur ist, als Beziehung auf sein Anderes, das Äußere; aber dieses ist ebenso nicht nur Seyn oder auch Existenz, sondern als auf das Wesen oder das Innere sich beziehend.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"152.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0009","text":"Aber es ist nicht nur die Beziehung beider auf einander, sondern die bestimmte der absoluten Form, daß jedes unmittelbar sein Gegentheil ist, und ihre gemeinschaftliche Beziehung auf ihr Drittes oder vielmehr auf ihre Einheit vorhanden. Ihre Vermittelung entbehrt aber noch dieser sie beide enthaltenden identischen Grundlage; ihre Beziehung ist deswegen die unmittelbare Umkehrung des Einen in das Andere; und diese negative Einheit, die sie zusammenknüpft, ist der einfache, inhaltslose Punkt.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"152.9"}],"sha256":"4a3788063be5043b4840a7bc4ca109d3ba466fe3c219efc7dfed5114a2cb3553","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105743975581Z_1aa246c1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. The Relation of Outer and Inner.","source_sha256":"4a3788063be5043b4840a7bc4ca109d3ba466fe3c219efc7dfed5114a2cb3553","sha256":"16feb35018d0cff527ea5233301c898093c6ec3291adf5755e89d855825a38b0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:57:43.975621+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0001","text":"1. The relation of the whole and the parts is the immediate one; reflected and being immediacy therefore each have in it a self-subsistence of their own; but, since they stand in essential relation, their self-subsistence is only their negative unity. This is now posited in the manifestation of force; reflected unity is essentially becoming-other, as translating itself into externality; but this is equally immediately taken back into the former; the difference of the self-subsistent forces sublates itself; the manifestation of force is only a mediation of reflected unity with itself. There is present only an empty, transparent difference, semblance; but this semblance is the mediation which is self-subsistent subsistence itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"152.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0002","text":"They are not merely opposed determinations which sublate themselves in themselves, and whose movement is not merely a transition; rather, on the one hand, the immediacy from which the beginning was made and into other-being was transitioned is itself only as posited; on the other hand, thereby each of the determinations, in its immediacy, is already the unity with its other, and the transition is thereby absolutely just as much the self-positing return into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"152.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0003","text":"The inner is determined as the form of reflected immediacy, or of essence, over against the outer as the form of Being; but both are only one identity.—This identity is, first, the solid unity of both as a contentful ground, or the absolute thing, in which the two determinations are indifferent, external moments. To that extent, it is content and the totality which is the inner, which equally becomes outer, but in this does not become something that has come to be or has passed over, but is equal to itself. According to this determination, the outer is not merely equal to the inner in content, but both are only one thing.—But this thing, as simple identity with itself, is distinct from its determinations of form, or these are external to it; it is, to that extent, itself an inner which is distinct from their externality.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"152.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0004","text":"But this externality consists in the fact that the two determinations themselves, namely the inner and the outer, constitute it. Yet the thing is itself nothing other than the unity of both. Thus both sides are again the same as regards content. But in the thing they are as an identity interpenetrating itself, as a contentful ground. But in externality, as forms of the thing, they are indifferent toward that identity and hence both toward one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"152.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0005","text":"2. In this way, they are the distinct determinations of form which have an identical ground, not in themselves, but in an other; determinations of reflection which are for themselves; the inner as the form of reflection-into-self, of essentiality; the outer, however, as the form of immediacy reflected into an other, or of unessentiality. Yet the nature of the relation has shown that these determinations absolutely constitute only one identity. Force is, in its manifestation, this: that the presupposing and the determining that returns into itself are one and the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"152.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0006","text":"Insofar, therefore, as inner and outer have been considered as determinations of form, they are, first, only simple form itself; and second, since in it they are at the same time determined as opposites, their unity is pure abstract mediation, in which the one is immediately the other, and is therefore the other because it is the one. Thus the inner is immediately only the outer, and it is therefore the determinacy of externality because it is the inner; conversely, the outer is only an inner because it is only an outer.—For, since this unity of form contains its two determinations as opposites, its identity is only this transition; and in it only the other of the two, not their contentful identity. Or this holding fast to form is in general the side of determinacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"152.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0007","text":"What is posited according to it is not the real totality of the whole, but totality, or the thing itself, only in the determinacy of form; because this is the absolutely conjoined unity of both opposed determinations, then, if one is taken first—and it is indifferent which it may be—it is [necessary] to say of the ground or thing that it is therefore just as essentially in the other determinacy, but equally only in the other; just as it was first said that it is only in the former.—Thus something which is at first only an inner is, for that very reason, only an outer. Or conversely, something which is only an outer is, for that very reason, only an inner.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"152.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0008","text":"Or, since the inner is determined as essence, but the outer as Being, a thing, insofar as it is only in its essence, is, for that very reason, only an immediate Being; or a thing which merely is is, for that very reason, only as yet in its essence.—The outer and inner are posited as determinacy in such a way that each of these two determinations not only presupposes the other and passes over into it as into its truth, but also, insofar as it is this truth of the other, remains posited as determinacy and points to the totality of both.—The inner is thus the completion of essence according to form. For essence, insofar as it is determined as inner, contains that it is deficient and is only as relation to its other, the outer; but this likewise is not merely Being or even existence, but as relating itself to essence or the inner.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"152.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0009","text":"But it is not merely the relation of the two to one another, but the determinate relation of absolute form: that each is immediately its opposite, and that their common relation to their third, or rather to their unity, is present. Yet their mediation still lacks this identical ground containing them both; their relation is therefore the immediate reversal of the one into the other; and this negative unity which binds them together is the simple, contentless point.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"152.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CVLD:P0009"]}],"source_digest":"32828cb743046d361f0cf67c8c33810fc8181ac14f8d7ea510f80a911ddff92c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Verhältniß des Äußern und Innern."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Verhältniß des Äußern und Innern.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40","title":"Remark.","order":153,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_40","text":"Die Bewegung des Wesens ist überhaupt das Werden zum Begriffe. In dem Verhältnisse des Innern und Äußern tritt das wesentliche Moment desselben hervor, daß nämlich seine Bestimmungen gesetzt sind, so in der negativen Einheit zu seyn, daß jede unmittelbar nicht nur als ihre andere, sondern auch als die Totalität des Ganzen ist. Aber diese Totalität ist im Begriffe als solchem das Allgemeine;—eine Grundlage, die im Verhältniß des Innern und Äußern noch nicht vorhanden ist.—In der negativen Identität des Innern und Äußern, welche die unmittelbare Umkehrung der einen dieser Bestimmungen in die andere ist, fehlt auch diejenige Grundlage, welche vorhin die Sache genannt wurde.-Die unvermittelte Identität der Form, wie sie hier noch ohne die inhaltsvolle Bewegung der Sache selbst gesetzt ist, ist sehr wichtig bemerkt zu werden. Sie kommt in der Sache vor, wie diese in ihrem Anfange ist. So ist das reine Seyn unmittelbar das Nichts. Überhaupt ist alles Reale in seinem Anfange eine solche nur unmittelbare Identität; denn in seinem Anfange hat es die Momente noch nicht entgegengesetzt und entwickelt, einer Seits aus der Äußerlichkeit sich noch nicht erinnert, anderer Seits sich aus der Innerlichkeit durch seine Thätigkeit noch nicht entäußert und hervorgebracht; es ist daher nur das Innere als Bestimmtheit gegen das Äußere, und nur das Äußere als Bestimmtheit gegen das Innere. Somit ist es Theils nur ein unmittelbares Seyn; Theils insofern es ebenso sehr die Negativität ist, welche die Thätigkeit der Entwicklung werden soll, ist es als solches wesentlich erst nur ein Inneres.—In aller natürlichen, wissenschaftlichen und geistigen Entwicklung überhaupt, bietet sich dieß dar, und es ist wesentlich dieß zu erkennen, daß das Erste, indem Etwas nur erst innerlich oder auch in seinem Begriffe ist, eben darum nur sein unmittelbares, passives Daseyn ist. So—um gleich das nächste Beispiel zu nehmen, —ist das hier betrachtete wesentliche Verhältniß, eh es sich durch die Vermittelung, das Verhältniß der Kraft, hindurch bewegt und realisirt hat, nur das Verhältniß an sich, sein Begriff, oder erst innerlich. Deswegen aber ist es nur das äußerliche, unmittelbare Verhältniß; das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile, in welchem die Seiten ein gleichgültiges Bestehen gegen einander haben. Ihre Identität ist an ihnen selbst noch nicht; sie ist erst innerlich, und deswegen fallen sie auseinander, haben ein unmittelbares, äußerliches Bestehen.—So ist die Sphäre des Seyns überhaupt nur erst das schlechthin noch Innere, und deswegen ist sie die Sphäre der seyenden Unmittelbarkeit oder der Äußerlichkeit.—Das Wesen ist nur erst das Innere; darum wird es auch für eine ganz äußerliche, systemlose Gemeinschaftlichkeit genommen; man sagt, das Schulwesen, Zeitungswesen, und versteht darunter ein Gemeinschaftliches, das durch äußeres Zusammennehmen von existirenden Gegenständen, insofern sie ohne alle wesentliche Verbindung, ohne Organisation, gemacht ist. —Oder an konkreten Gegenständen, so ist der Keim der Pflanze, das Kind, nur erst innere Pflanze, innerlicher Mensch. Aber darum ist die Pflanze oder der Mensch als Keim ein Unmittelbares, ein Äußeres, das sich noch nicht die negative Beziehung auf sich selbst gegeben hat, ein Passives, dem Andersseyn Preisgegebenes.—So ist auch Gott in seinem unmittelbaren Begriffe nicht Geist; der Geist ist nicht das Unmittelbare, der Vermittelung entgegengesetzte, sondern vielmehr das seine Unmittelbarkeit ewig setzende und ewig aus ihr in sich zurückkehrende Wesen. Unmittelbar ist daher Gott nur die Natur. Oder die Natur ist nur der innere, nicht als Geist wirkliche und damit nicht der wahrhafte Gott.—Oder Gott ist im Denken, als erstem Denken, nur das reine Seyn, oder auch das Wesen, das abstrakte Absolute; nicht aber Gott als absoluter Geist, als welcher allein die wahrhafte Natur Gottes ist.\n\n3. Die erste der betrachteten Identitäten des Innern und Äußern ist die gegen den Unterschied dieser Bestimmungen als gegen eine ihr äußere Form gleichgültige Grundlage, oder sie als Inhalt. Die zweite ist die unvermittelte Identität ihres Unterschiedes, die unmittelbare Umkehrung jeder in ihre entgegengesetzte;—oder sie als reine Form. Aber diese beiden Identitäten sind nur die Seiten Einer Totalität; oder sie selbst ist nur die Umkehrung der einen in die andre. Die Totalität als Grundlage und Inhalt ist diese in sich reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit nur durch die voraussetzende Reflexion der Form, die ihren Unterschied aufhebt, und sich als gleichgültige Identität, als reflektirte Einheit gegen ihn setzt. Oder der Inhalt ist die Form selbst, insofern sie sich als Verschiedenheit bestimmt, und sich selbst zu einer ihrer Seiten, als Äußerlichkeit, zu der andern aber als in sich reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit oder zum Innern macht.\n\nDadurch sind also umgekehrt die Unterschiede der Form, das Innere und das Äußere, jedes an ihm selbst gesetzt als die Totalität seiner und seines Andern; das Innere ist als einfache in sich reflektirte Identität, das Unmittelbare und daher so sehr Seyn und Äußerlichkeit, als Wesen; und das Äußere ist als das mannigfaltige, bestimmte Seyn, nur Äußeres d. h. gesetzt als unwesentlich und in seinen Grund zurückgegangen, somit als Inneres. Dieses Übergehen beider in einander ist ihre unmittelbare Identität, als Grundlage; aber es ist auch ihre vermittelte Identität; nämlich jedes ist eben durch sein Anderes, was es an sich ist, die Totalität des Verhältnisses. Oder umgekehrt die Bestimmtheit einer jeden Seite ist dadurch, daß sie an ihr die Totalität ist, mit der andern Bestimmtheit vermittelt; die Totalität vermittelt sich so durch die Form oder die Bestimmtheit mit sich selbst, und die Bestimmtheit vermittelt sich durch ihre einfache Identität mit sich.\n\nWas Etwas ist, das ist es daher ganz in seiner Äußerlichkeit; seine Äußerlichkeit ist seine Totalität, sie ist ebenso sehr seine in sich reflektirte Einheit. Seine Erscheinung ist nicht nur die Reflexion in Anderes, sondern in sich, und seine Äußerlichkeit daher die Äußerung dessen, was es an sich ist; und indem so sein Inhalt und seine Form schlechthin identisch sind, so ist es nichts an und für sich als dieß, sich zu äußern. Es ist das Offenbaren seines Wesens, so daß dieß Wesen eben nur darin besteht, das sich Offenbarende zu seyn.\n\nDas wesentliche Verhältniß hat sich in dieser Identität der Erscheinung mit dem Innern oder dem Wesen zur Wirklichkeit bestimmt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0001","text":"Die Bewegung des Wesens ist überhaupt das Werden zum Begriffe. In dem Verhältnisse des Innern und Äußern tritt das wesentliche Moment desselben hervor, daß nämlich seine Bestimmungen gesetzt sind, so in der negativen Einheit zu seyn, daß jede unmittelbar nicht nur als ihre andere, sondern auch als die Totalität des Ganzen ist. Aber diese Totalität ist im Begriffe als solchem das Allgemeine;—eine Grundlage, die im Verhältniß des Innern und Äußern noch nicht vorhanden ist.—In der negativen Identität des Innern und Äußern, welche die unmittelbare Umkehrung der einen dieser Bestimmungen in die andere ist, fehlt auch diejenige Grundlage, welche vorhin die Sache genannt wurde.-Die unvermittelte Identität der Form, wie sie hier noch ohne die inhaltsvolle Bewegung der Sache selbst gesetzt ist, ist sehr wichtig bemerkt zu werden. Sie kommt in der Sache vor, wie diese in ihrem Anfange ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"153.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0002","text":"So ist das reine Seyn unmittelbar das Nichts. Überhaupt ist alles Reale in seinem Anfange eine solche nur unmittelbare Identität; denn in seinem Anfange hat es die Momente noch nicht entgegengesetzt und entwickelt, einer Seits aus der Äußerlichkeit sich noch nicht erinnert, anderer Seits sich aus der Innerlichkeit durch seine Thätigkeit noch nicht entäußert und hervorgebracht; es ist daher nur das Innere als Bestimmtheit gegen das Äußere, und nur das Äußere als Bestimmtheit gegen das Innere.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"153.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0003","text":"Somit ist es Theils nur ein unmittelbares Seyn; Theils insofern es ebenso sehr die Negativität ist, welche die Thätigkeit der Entwicklung werden soll, ist es als solches wesentlich erst nur ein Inneres.—In aller natürlichen, wissenschaftlichen und geistigen Entwicklung überhaupt, bietet sich dieß dar, und es ist wesentlich dieß zu erkennen, daß das Erste, indem Etwas nur erst innerlich oder auch in seinem Begriffe ist, eben darum nur sein unmittelbares, passives Daseyn ist. So—um gleich das nächste Beispiel zu nehmen, —ist das hier betrachtete wesentliche Verhältniß, eh es sich durch die Vermittelung, das Verhältniß der Kraft, hindurch bewegt und realisirt hat, nur das Verhältniß an sich, sein Begriff, oder erst innerlich.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"153.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0004","text":"Deswegen aber ist es nur das äußerliche, unmittelbare Verhältniß; das Verhältniß des Ganzen und der Theile, in welchem die Seiten ein gleichgültiges Bestehen gegen einander haben. Ihre Identität ist an ihnen selbst noch nicht; sie ist erst innerlich, und deswegen fallen sie auseinander, haben ein unmittelbares, äußerliches Bestehen.—So ist die Sphäre des Seyns überhaupt nur erst das schlechthin noch Innere, und deswegen ist sie die Sphäre der seyenden Unmittelbarkeit oder der Äußerlichkeit.—Das Wesen ist nur erst das Innere; darum wird es auch für eine ganz äußerliche, systemlose Gemeinschaftlichkeit genommen; man sagt, das Schulwesen, Zeitungswesen, und versteht darunter ein Gemeinschaftliches, das durch äußeres Zusammennehmen von existirenden Gegenständen, insofern sie ohne alle wesentliche Verbindung, ohne Organisation, gemacht ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"153.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0005","text":"—Oder an konkreten Gegenständen, so ist der Keim der Pflanze, das Kind, nur erst innere Pflanze, innerlicher Mensch. Aber darum ist die Pflanze oder der Mensch als Keim ein Unmittelbares, ein Äußeres, das sich noch nicht die negative Beziehung auf sich selbst gegeben hat, ein Passives, dem Andersseyn Preisgegebenes.—So ist auch Gott in seinem unmittelbaren Begriffe nicht Geist; der Geist ist nicht das Unmittelbare, der Vermittelung entgegengesetzte, sondern vielmehr das seine Unmittelbarkeit ewig setzende und ewig aus ihr in sich zurückkehrende Wesen. Unmittelbar ist daher Gott nur die Natur. Oder die Natur ist nur der innere, nicht als Geist wirkliche und damit nicht der wahrhafte Gott.—Oder Gott ist im Denken, als erstem Denken, nur das reine Seyn, oder auch das Wesen, das abstrakte Absolute; nicht aber Gott als absoluter Geist, als welcher allein die wahrhafte Natur Gottes ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"153.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0006","text":"3. Die erste der betrachteten Identitäten des Innern und Äußern ist die gegen den Unterschied dieser Bestimmungen als gegen eine ihr äußere Form gleichgültige Grundlage, oder sie als Inhalt. Die zweite ist die unvermittelte Identität ihres Unterschiedes, die unmittelbare Umkehrung jeder in ihre entgegengesetzte;—oder sie als reine Form. Aber diese beiden Identitäten sind nur die Seiten Einer Totalität; oder sie selbst ist nur die Umkehrung der einen in die andre. Die Totalität als Grundlage und Inhalt ist diese in sich reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit nur durch die voraussetzende Reflexion der Form, die ihren Unterschied aufhebt, und sich als gleichgültige Identität, als reflektirte Einheit gegen ihn setzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"153.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0007","text":"Oder der Inhalt ist die Form selbst, insofern sie sich als Verschiedenheit bestimmt, und sich selbst zu einer ihrer Seiten, als Äußerlichkeit, zu der andern aber als in sich reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit oder zum Innern macht.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"153.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0008","text":"Dadurch sind also umgekehrt die Unterschiede der Form, das Innere und das Äußere, jedes an ihm selbst gesetzt als die Totalität seiner und seines Andern; das Innere ist als einfache in sich reflektirte Identität, das Unmittelbare und daher so sehr Seyn und Äußerlichkeit, als Wesen; und das Äußere ist als das mannigfaltige, bestimmte Seyn, nur Äußeres d. h. gesetzt als unwesentlich und in seinen Grund zurückgegangen, somit als Inneres. Dieses Übergehen beider in einander ist ihre unmittelbare Identität, als Grundlage; aber es ist auch ihre vermittelte Identität; nämlich jedes ist eben durch sein Anderes, was es an sich ist, die Totalität des Verhältnisses.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"153.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0009","text":"Oder umgekehrt die Bestimmtheit einer jeden Seite ist dadurch, daß sie an ihr die Totalität ist, mit der andern Bestimmtheit vermittelt; die Totalität vermittelt sich so durch die Form oder die Bestimmtheit mit sich selbst, und die Bestimmtheit vermittelt sich durch ihre einfache Identität mit sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"153.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0010","text":"Was Etwas ist, das ist es daher ganz in seiner Äußerlichkeit; seine Äußerlichkeit ist seine Totalität, sie ist ebenso sehr seine in sich reflektirte Einheit. Seine Erscheinung ist nicht nur die Reflexion in Anderes, sondern in sich, und seine Äußerlichkeit daher die Äußerung dessen, was es an sich ist; und indem so sein Inhalt und seine Form schlechthin identisch sind, so ist es nichts an und für sich als dieß, sich zu äußern. Es ist das Offenbaren seines Wesens, so daß dieß Wesen eben nur darin besteht, das sich Offenbarende zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"153.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_40:P0011","text":"Das wesentliche Verhältniß hat sich in dieser Identität der Erscheinung mit dem Innern oder dem Wesen zur Wirklichkeit bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"153.11"}],"sha256":"ffe6e12f132139b81ef4367a6adcfea34989a05719b4968243608ed6e3061764","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW","title":"Third Section. Actuality.","order":154,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DADW","text":"Die Wirklichkeit ist die Einheit des Wesens und der Existenz; in ihr hat das gestaltlose Wesen und die haltlose Erscheinung;—oder das bestimmungslose Bestehen und die bestandlose Mannigfaltigkeit ihre Wahrheit. Die Existenz ist zwar die aus dem Grunde hervorgegangene Unmittelbarkeit, aber sie hat die Form noch nicht an ihr gesetzt; indem sie sich bestimmt und formirt, ist sie die Erscheinung; und indem sich dieß nur als Reflexion-in-Anderes bestimmte Bestehen zur Reflexion-in-sich fortbildet, wird es zu zwei Welten, zwei Totalitäten des Inhalts, deren die eine als in sich, die andere als in Anderes reflektirte bestimmt ist. Das wesentliche Verhältniß aber stellt ihre Formbeziehung dar, deren Vollendung das Verhältniß des Innern und Äußern ist, daß der Inhalt beider nur Eine identische Grundlage und ebenso sehr nur Eine Identität der Form ist.—Dadurch daß sich auch diese Identität in Ansehung der Form ergeben hat, ist die Formbestimmung ihrer Verschiedenheit aufgehoben und es ist gesetzt, daß sie Eine absolute Totalität sind.\n\nDiese Einheit des Innern und Äußern ist die absolute Wirklichkeit. Diese Wirklichkeit aber ist zunächst das Absolute als solches; —insofern sie als Einheit gesetzt ist, in der sich die Form aufgehoben, und zu dem leeren oder äußern Unterschiede eines Äußern und Innern gemacht hat. Die Reflexion verhält sich gegen dieß Absolute als äußerliche, welche es vielmehr nur betrachtet, als daß sie seine eigene Bewegung wäre. Indem sie aber wesentlich dieß ist, ist sie als seine negative Rückkehr in sich. Zweitens die eigentliche Wirklichkeit. Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit machen die formellen Momente des Absoluten, oder die Reflexion desselben aus.\n\nDrittens die Einheit des Absoluten und seiner Reflexion ist das absolute Verhältniß, oder vielmehr das Absolute als Verhältniß zu sich selbst; Substanz.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0001","text":"Die Wirklichkeit ist die Einheit des Wesens und der Existenz; in ihr hat das gestaltlose Wesen und die haltlose Erscheinung;—oder das bestimmungslose Bestehen und die bestandlose Mannigfaltigkeit ihre Wahrheit. Die Existenz ist zwar die aus dem Grunde hervorgegangene Unmittelbarkeit, aber sie hat die Form noch nicht an ihr gesetzt; indem sie sich bestimmt und formirt, ist sie die Erscheinung; und indem sich dieß nur als Reflexion-in-Anderes bestimmte Bestehen zur Reflexion-in-sich fortbildet, wird es zu zwei Welten, zwei Totalitäten des Inhalts, deren die eine als in sich, die andere als in Anderes reflektirte bestimmt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"154.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0002","text":"Das wesentliche Verhältniß aber stellt ihre Formbeziehung dar, deren Vollendung das Verhältniß des Innern und Äußern ist, daß der Inhalt beider nur Eine identische Grundlage und ebenso sehr nur Eine Identität der Form ist.—Dadurch daß sich auch diese Identität in Ansehung der Form ergeben hat, ist die Formbestimmung ihrer Verschiedenheit aufgehoben und es ist gesetzt, daß sie Eine absolute Totalität sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"154.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0003","text":"Diese Einheit des Innern und Äußern ist die absolute Wirklichkeit. Diese Wirklichkeit aber ist zunächst das Absolute als solches; —insofern sie als Einheit gesetzt ist, in der sich die Form aufgehoben, und zu dem leeren oder äußern Unterschiede eines Äußern und Innern gemacht hat. Die Reflexion verhält sich gegen dieß Absolute als äußerliche, welche es vielmehr nur betrachtet, als daß sie seine eigene Bewegung wäre. Indem sie aber wesentlich dieß ist, ist sie als seine negative Rückkehr in sich. Zweitens die eigentliche Wirklichkeit. Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit machen die formellen Momente des Absoluten, oder die Reflexion desselben aus.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"154.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0004","text":"Drittens die Einheit des Absoluten und seiner Reflexion ist das absolute Verhältniß, oder vielmehr das Absolute als Verhältniß zu sich selbst; Substanz.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"154.4"}],"sha256":"16c326923cd01a62809a5c9e5e1a96d9a91cf15bf26dd97e45ae37ae8ea5e8d3","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105750708751Z_ae1d19a8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Third Section. Actuality.","source_sha256":"16c326923cd01a62809a5c9e5e1a96d9a91cf15bf26dd97e45ae37ae8ea5e8d3","sha256":"defd695079f96f587efe2a13224b48f01297c30e67c617d0fbf98122c7386a3d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:57:50.708799+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0001","text":"Reality is the unity of essence and existence; in it the formless essence and the unsubstantial appearance—or indeterminate subsistence and insubstantial multiplicity—have their truth. Existence is indeed the immediacy that has issued from the ground, but it has not yet posited form in itself; in determining and forming itself, it is appearance; and as this subsistence, determined only as reflection-into-another, develops into reflection-into-itself, it becomes two worlds, two totalities of content, of which the one is determined as reflected into itself, the other as reflected into another.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"154.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADW:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0002","text":"But the essential relation represents their relation of form, whose completion is the relation of the inner and outer, namely, that the content of both is only one identical foundation and, equally, only one identity of form.—Because this identity has also emerged with respect to form, the form-determination of their difference is sublated, and it is posited that they are one absolute totality.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"154.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADW:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0003","text":"This unity of inner and outer is absolute reality. But this reality is initially the Absolute as such;—insofar as it is posited as unity, in which form has sublated itself and made itself into the empty or external difference of an outer and an inner. Reflection relates to this Absolute as something external, which merely contemplates it rather than being its own movement. But since it essentially is this, it is its negative return into itself. Secondly, actuality proper. Actuality, possibility, and necessity constitute the formal moments of the Absolute, or its reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"154.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADW:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADW:P0004","text":"Thirdly, the unity of the Absolute and its reflection is the absolute relation, or rather the Absolute as relation to itself; substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"154.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADW:P0004"]}],"source_digest":"20121b5651f6c56d7ec21db74e3b8598d07719f01b0a4e06f8fbad6c267a7331","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Dritter Abschnitt. Die Wirklichkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Dritter Abschnitt. Die Wirklichkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA","title":"A. The Exposition of the Absolute.","order":155,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DADA","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Das Absolute.\n\nDie einfache gediegene Identität des Absoluten ist unbestimmt, oder in ihr hat sich vielmehr alle Bestimmtheit des Wesens und der Existenz, oder des Seyns überhaupt sowohl als der Reflexion aufgelöst. Insofern fällt das Bestimmen dessen, was das Absolute sey, negativ aus, und das Absolute selbst erscheint nur als die Negation aller Prädikate und als das Leere. Aber indem es ebenso sehr als die Position aller Prädikate ausgesprochen werden muß, erscheint es als der formellste Widerspruch. Insofern jenes Negiren und dieses Setzen, der äußern Reflexion angehört, so ist es eine formelle unsystematische Dialektik, die mit leichter Mühe die mancherlei Bestimmungen hierher und dorther aufgreift, und mit ebenso leichter Mühe einer Seits ihre Endlichkeit und bloße Relativität aufzeigt, als anderer Seits, indem es ihr als die Totalität vorschwebt, auch das Innwohnen aller Bestimmungen von ihm ausspricht,—ohne diese Positionen und jene Negationen zu einer wahrhaften Einheit erheben zu können.—Es soll aber dargestellt werden, was das Absolute ist; aber dieß Darstellen kann nicht ein Bestimmen noch äußere Reflexion seyn, wodurch Bestimmungen desselben würden, sondern es ist die Auslegung und zwar die eigene Auslegung des Absoluten, und nur ein Zeigen dessen was es ist.\n\n## A. Die Auslegung des Absoluten.\n\nDas Absolute ist nicht nur das Seyn, noch auch das Wesen. Jene ist die erste unreflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, diese die reflektirte; jedes ist ferner Totalität an ihm selbst; aber eine bestimmte. Am Wesen tritt das Seyn als Existenz hervor; und die Beziehung von Seyn und Wesen hat sich bis zum Verhältnisse des Innern und Äußern fortgebildet. Das Innere ist das Wesen aber als die Totalität, welche wesentlich die Bestimmung hat, auf das Seyn bezogen und unmittelbar Seyn zu seyn. Das Äußere ist das Seyn, aber mit der wesentlichen Bestimmung, auf die Reflexion bezogen unmittelbar ebenso verhältnißlose Identität mit dem Wesen zu seyn. Das Absolute selbst ist die absolute Einheit beider; es ist dasjenige, was überhaupt den Grund des wesentlichen Verhältnisses ausmacht, das als Verhältniß nur noch nicht in diese seine Identität zurückgegangen, und dessen Grund noch nicht gesetzt ist.\n\nHieraus ergiebt sich, daß die Bestimmung des Absoluten ist, die absolute Form zu seyn, aber zugleich nicht als die Identität, deren Momente nur eInfache Bestimmtheiten sind;—sondern die Identität, deren Momente jedes an ihm selbst die Totalität, und somit als gleichgültig gegen die Form, der vollständige Inhalt des Ganzen ist. Aber umgekehrt ist das Absolute so der absolute Inhalt, daß der Inhalt, der als solcher gleichgültige Mannigfaltigkeit ist, die negative Formbeziehung an ihm hat, wodurch seine Mannigfaltigkeit nur Eine gediegene Identität ist.\n\nDie Identität des Absoluten ist somit dadurch die absolute, daß jeder seiner Theile selbst das Ganze oder jede Bestimmtheit die Totalität ist, d. h. daß die Bestimmtheit überhaupt ein schlechthin durchsichtiger Schein, ein in seinem Gesetztseyn verschwundener Unterschied geworden ist. Wesen, Existenz, an sich seyende Welt, Ganzes, Theile, Kraft,—diese reflektirten Bestimmungen erscheinen dem Vorstellen als an und für sich geltendes, wahres Seyn; das Absolute aber ist gegen sie der Grund, in dem sie untergegangen sind. —Weil nun im Absoluten die Form nur die einfache Identität mit sich ist, so bestimmt sich das Absolute nicht; denn die Bestimmung ist ein Formunterschied, der zunächst als solcher gilt. Weil es aber zugleich allen Unterschied und Formbestimmung überhaupt enthält, oder weil es selbst die absolute Form und Reflexion ist, so muß auch die Verschiedenheit des Inhalts an ihm hervortreten. Aber das Absolute selbst ist die absolute Identität; dieß ist seine Bestimmung, indem alle Mannigfaltigkeit der an sich seyenden und der erscheinenden Welt, oder der innerlichen und äußerlichen Totalität in ihm aufgehoben ist. —In ihm selbst ist kein Werden, denn es ist nicht das Seyn, noch ist es das sich reflektirende Bestimmen; denn es ist nicht das sich nur in sich bestimmende Wesen; es ist auch nicht ein sich Äußern; denn es ist als die Identität des Innern und Äußern.—Aber so steht die Bewegung der Reflexion seiner absoluten Identität gegenüber. Sie ist in dieser aufgehoben, so ist sie nur deren Inneres, hiermit aber ist sie ihr äußerlich.—Sie besteht daher zunächst nur darin, ihr Thun im Absoluten aufzuheben. Sie ist das Jenseits der mannigfaltigen Unterschiede und Bestimmungen und deren Bewegung, welches dem Absoluten im Rücken liegt; sie ist daher zwar das Aufnehmen derselben, aber zugleich ihr Untergehen; so ist sie die negative Auslegung des Absoluten, die vorhin erwähnt wurde.—In ihrer wahrhaften Darstellung ist diese Auslegung das bisherige Ganze der logischen Bewegung der Sphäre des Seyns und des Wesens, deren Inhalt nicht von außen als ein gegebener und zufälliger aufgerafft, noch durch eine ihm äußere Reflexion in den Abgrund des Absoluten versenkt worden, sondern sich an ihm durch seine innere Nothwendigkeit bestimmt und als eignes Werden des Seyns, und als Reflexion des Wesens in das Absolute als in seinen Grund zurückgegangen ist.\n\nDiese Auslegung hat aber selbst zugleich eine positive Seite; insofern nämlich das Endliche darin, daß es zu Grunde geht, diese Natur beweist, auf das Absolute bezogen zu seyn, oder das Absolute an ihm selbst zu enthalten. Aber diese Seite ist nicht so sehr die positive Auslegung des Absoluten selbst, als vielmehr die Auslegung der Bestimmungen, daß sie nämlich das Absolute zu ihrem Abgrunde, aber auch zu ihrem Grunde haben, oder daß das, was ihnen, dem Schein, ein Bestehen gibt, das Absolute selbst ist.—Der Schein ist nicht das Nichts, sondern er ist Reflexion, Beziehung auf das Absolute; oder er ist Schein, insofern das Absolute in ihm scheint. Diese positive Auslegung hält so noch das Endliche vor seinem Verschwinden auf, und betrachtet es als einen Ausdruck und Abbild des Absoluten. Aber die Durchsichtigkeit des Endlichen, das nur das Absolute durch sich hindurchblicken läßt, endigt in gänzliches Verschwinden; denn es ist nichts am Endlichen, was ihm einen Unterschied gegen das Absolute erhalten könnte; es ist ein Medium, das von dem, was durch es scheint, absorbirt wird.\n\nDiese positive Auslegung des Absoluten ist daher selbst nur ein Scheinen; denn das wahrhaft Positive, was sie und der ausgelegte Inhalt enthält, ist das Absolute selbst. Was für weitere Bestimmungen vorkommen, die Form, worin das Absolute scheint, ist ein Nichtiges, das die Auslegung von außen her aufnimmt, und woran sie einen Anfang zu ihrem Thun gewinnt. Eine solche Bestimmung hat nicht im Absoluten ihren Anfang, sondern nur ihr Ende. Dieses Auslegen ist daher zwar absolutes Thun durch seine Beziehung auf das Absolute, in das es zurückgeht, aber nicht nach seinem Ausgangspunkte, der eine dem Absoluten äußerliche Bestimmung ist.\n\nIn der That aber ist das Auslegen des Absoluten sein eigenes Thun, und das bei sich anfängt, wie es bei sich ankommt. Das Absolute, nur als absolute Identität, ist es bestimmt; nämlich als Identisches; es ist durch die Reflexion so gesetzt, gegen die Entgegensetzung und Mannigfaltigkeit; oder es ist nur das Negative der Reflexion und des Bestimmens überhaupt.—Nicht nur jenes Auslegen des Absoluten ist daher ein Unvollkommenes, sondern auch dieß Absolute selbst, bei welchem nur angekommen wird. Oder jenes Absolute, das nur als absolute Identität ist, ist nur das Absolute einer äußern Reflexion. Es ist daher nicht das Absolut-Absolute, sondern das Absolute in einer Bestimmtheit, oder es ist Attribut.\n\nAber das Absolute ist nicht nur Attribut, weil es Gegenstand einer äußern Reflexion und somit ein durch sie Bestimmtes ist.—Oder die Reflexion ist nicht nur ihm äußerlich; sondern unmittelbar, darum weil sie ihm äußerlich ist, ist sie ihm innerlich. Das Absolute ist nur das Absolute, weil es nicht die abstrakte Identität, sondern die Identität des Seyns und Wesens, oder die Identität des Innern und Äußern ist. Es ist also selbst die absolute Form, welche es in sich scheinen macht, und es zum Attribut bestimmt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0001","text":"## Erstes Kapitel. Das Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"155.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0002","text":"Die einfache gediegene Identität des Absoluten ist unbestimmt, oder in ihr hat sich vielmehr alle Bestimmtheit des Wesens und der Existenz, oder des Seyns überhaupt sowohl als der Reflexion aufgelöst. Insofern fällt das Bestimmen dessen, was das Absolute sey, negativ aus, und das Absolute selbst erscheint nur als die Negation aller Prädikate und als das Leere. Aber indem es ebenso sehr als die Position aller Prädikate ausgesprochen werden muß, erscheint es als der formellste Widerspruch.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"155.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0003","text":"Insofern jenes Negiren und dieses Setzen, der äußern Reflexion angehört, so ist es eine formelle unsystematische Dialektik, die mit leichter Mühe die mancherlei Bestimmungen hierher und dorther aufgreift, und mit ebenso leichter Mühe einer Seits ihre Endlichkeit und bloße Relativität aufzeigt, als anderer Seits, indem es ihr als die Totalität vorschwebt, auch das Innwohnen aller Bestimmungen von ihm ausspricht,—ohne diese Positionen und jene Negationen zu einer wahrhaften Einheit erheben zu können.—Es soll aber dargestellt werden, was das Absolute ist; aber dieß Darstellen kann nicht ein Bestimmen noch äußere Reflexion seyn, wodurch Bestimmungen desselben würden, sondern es ist die Auslegung und zwar die eigene Auslegung des Absoluten, und nur ein Zeigen dessen was es ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"155.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0004","text":"## A. Die Auslegung des Absoluten.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"155.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0005","text":"Das Absolute ist nicht nur das Seyn, noch auch das Wesen. Jene ist die erste unreflektirte Unmittelbarkeit, diese die reflektirte; jedes ist ferner Totalität an ihm selbst; aber eine bestimmte. Am Wesen tritt das Seyn als Existenz hervor; und die Beziehung von Seyn und Wesen hat sich bis zum Verhältnisse des Innern und Äußern fortgebildet. Das Innere ist das Wesen aber als die Totalität, welche wesentlich die Bestimmung hat, auf das Seyn bezogen und unmittelbar Seyn zu seyn. Das Äußere ist das Seyn, aber mit der wesentlichen Bestimmung, auf die Reflexion bezogen unmittelbar ebenso verhältnißlose Identität mit dem Wesen zu seyn. Das Absolute selbst ist die absolute Einheit beider; es ist dasjenige, was überhaupt den Grund des wesentlichen Verhältnisses ausmacht, das als Verhältniß nur noch nicht in diese seine Identität zurückgegangen, und dessen Grund noch nicht gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"155.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0006","text":"Hieraus ergiebt sich, daß die Bestimmung des Absoluten ist, die absolute Form zu seyn, aber zugleich nicht als die Identität, deren Momente nur eInfache Bestimmtheiten sind;—sondern die Identität, deren Momente jedes an ihm selbst die Totalität, und somit als gleichgültig gegen die Form, der vollständige Inhalt des Ganzen ist. Aber umgekehrt ist das Absolute so der absolute Inhalt, daß der Inhalt, der als solcher gleichgültige Mannigfaltigkeit ist, die negative Formbeziehung an ihm hat, wodurch seine Mannigfaltigkeit nur Eine gediegene Identität ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"155.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0007","text":"Die Identität des Absoluten ist somit dadurch die absolute, daß jeder seiner Theile selbst das Ganze oder jede Bestimmtheit die Totalität ist, d. h. daß die Bestimmtheit überhaupt ein schlechthin durchsichtiger Schein, ein in seinem Gesetztseyn verschwundener Unterschied geworden ist. Wesen, Existenz, an sich seyende Welt, Ganzes, Theile, Kraft,—diese reflektirten Bestimmungen erscheinen dem Vorstellen als an und für sich geltendes, wahres Seyn; das Absolute aber ist gegen sie der Grund, in dem sie untergegangen sind. —Weil nun im Absoluten die Form nur die einfache Identität mit sich ist, so bestimmt sich das Absolute nicht; denn die Bestimmung ist ein Formunterschied, der zunächst als solcher gilt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"155.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0008","text":"Weil es aber zugleich allen Unterschied und Formbestimmung überhaupt enthält, oder weil es selbst die absolute Form und Reflexion ist, so muß auch die Verschiedenheit des Inhalts an ihm hervortreten. Aber das Absolute selbst ist die absolute Identität; dieß ist seine Bestimmung, indem alle Mannigfaltigkeit der an sich seyenden und der erscheinenden Welt, oder der innerlichen und äußerlichen Totalität in ihm aufgehoben ist. —In ihm selbst ist kein Werden, denn es ist nicht das Seyn, noch ist es das sich reflektirende Bestimmen; denn es ist nicht das sich nur in sich bestimmende Wesen; es ist auch nicht ein sich Äußern; denn es ist als die Identität des Innern und Äußern.—Aber so steht die Bewegung der Reflexion seiner absoluten Identität gegenüber.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"155.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0009","text":"Sie ist in dieser aufgehoben, so ist sie nur deren Inneres, hiermit aber ist sie ihr äußerlich.—Sie besteht daher zunächst nur darin, ihr Thun im Absoluten aufzuheben. Sie ist das Jenseits der mannigfaltigen Unterschiede und Bestimmungen und deren Bewegung, welches dem Absoluten im Rücken liegt; sie ist daher zwar das Aufnehmen derselben, aber zugleich ihr Untergehen; so ist sie die negative Auslegung des Absoluten, die vorhin erwähnt wurde.—In ihrer wahrhaften Darstellung ist diese Auslegung das bisherige Ganze der logischen Bewegung der Sphäre des Seyns und des Wesens, deren Inhalt nicht von außen als ein gegebener und zufälliger aufgerafft, noch durch eine ihm äußere Reflexion in den Abgrund des Absoluten versenkt worden, sondern sich an ihm durch seine innere Nothwendigkeit bestimmt und als eignes Werden des Seyns, und als Reflexion des Wesens in das Absolute als in seinen Grund","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"155.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0010","text":"zurückgegangen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"155.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0011","text":"Diese Auslegung hat aber selbst zugleich eine positive Seite; insofern nämlich das Endliche darin, daß es zu Grunde geht, diese Natur beweist, auf das Absolute bezogen zu seyn, oder das Absolute an ihm selbst zu enthalten. Aber diese Seite ist nicht so sehr die positive Auslegung des Absoluten selbst, als vielmehr die Auslegung der Bestimmungen, daß sie nämlich das Absolute zu ihrem Abgrunde, aber auch zu ihrem Grunde haben, oder daß das, was ihnen, dem Schein, ein Bestehen gibt, das Absolute selbst ist.—Der Schein ist nicht das Nichts, sondern er ist Reflexion, Beziehung auf das Absolute; oder er ist Schein, insofern das Absolute in ihm scheint. Diese positive Auslegung hält so noch das Endliche vor seinem Verschwinden auf, und betrachtet es als einen Ausdruck und Abbild des Absoluten.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"155.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0012","text":"Aber die Durchsichtigkeit des Endlichen, das nur das Absolute durch sich hindurchblicken läßt, endigt in gänzliches Verschwinden; denn es ist nichts am Endlichen, was ihm einen Unterschied gegen das Absolute erhalten könnte; es ist ein Medium, das von dem, was durch es scheint, absorbirt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"155.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0013","text":"Diese positive Auslegung des Absoluten ist daher selbst nur ein Scheinen; denn das wahrhaft Positive, was sie und der ausgelegte Inhalt enthält, ist das Absolute selbst. Was für weitere Bestimmungen vorkommen, die Form, worin das Absolute scheint, ist ein Nichtiges, das die Auslegung von außen her aufnimmt, und woran sie einen Anfang zu ihrem Thun gewinnt. Eine solche Bestimmung hat nicht im Absoluten ihren Anfang, sondern nur ihr Ende. Dieses Auslegen ist daher zwar absolutes Thun durch seine Beziehung auf das Absolute, in das es zurückgeht, aber nicht nach seinem Ausgangspunkte, der eine dem Absoluten äußerliche Bestimmung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"155.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0014","text":"In der That aber ist das Auslegen des Absoluten sein eigenes Thun, und das bei sich anfängt, wie es bei sich ankommt. Das Absolute, nur als absolute Identität, ist es bestimmt; nämlich als Identisches; es ist durch die Reflexion so gesetzt, gegen die Entgegensetzung und Mannigfaltigkeit; oder es ist nur das Negative der Reflexion und des Bestimmens überhaupt.—Nicht nur jenes Auslegen des Absoluten ist daher ein Unvollkommenes, sondern auch dieß Absolute selbst, bei welchem nur angekommen wird. Oder jenes Absolute, das nur als absolute Identität ist, ist nur das Absolute einer äußern Reflexion. Es ist daher nicht das Absolut-Absolute, sondern das Absolute in einer Bestimmtheit, oder es ist Attribut.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"155.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0015","text":"Aber das Absolute ist nicht nur Attribut, weil es Gegenstand einer äußern Reflexion und somit ein durch sie Bestimmtes ist.—Oder die Reflexion ist nicht nur ihm äußerlich; sondern unmittelbar, darum weil sie ihm äußerlich ist, ist sie ihm innerlich. Das Absolute ist nur das Absolute, weil es nicht die abstrakte Identität, sondern die Identität des Seyns und Wesens, oder die Identität des Innern und Äußern ist. Es ist also selbst die absolute Form, welche es in sich scheinen macht, und es zum Attribut bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"155.15"}],"sha256":"408f83bf9b18b757010f6dfe0ac4020cd113d22040a9bd329a04b602af2f90d0","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105806681220Z_2a13c2e8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Exposition of the Absolute.","source_sha256":"408f83bf9b18b757010f6dfe0ac4020cd113d22040a9bd329a04b602af2f90d0","sha256":"4bd6ae38b9216efb27d08c31ba467963dbee45a7e6b050d701be59d8d1f2c171","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:58:06.681272+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0001","text":"## First Chapter. The Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"155.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0002","text":"The simple substantial identity of the Absolute is indeterminate, or rather all determinacy of essence and existence, or of Being in general as well as of reflection, has dissolved within it. Insofar as this is so, the determining of what the Absolute is turns out negatively, and the Absolute itself appears only as the negation of all predicates and as the empty. But since it must equally be pronounced as the positing of all predicates, it appears as the most formal contradiction.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"155.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0003","text":"Insofar as that negating and this positing belong to external reflection, it is a formal unsystematic dialectic, which with little effort picks up the various determinations from here and there, and with equally little effort on the one hand shows their finitude and mere relativity, while on the other hand, since totality hovers before it, it also pronounces that all determinations inhere in it,—without being able to raise these positions and those negations to a true unity.—But what the Absolute is is to be exhibited; yet this exhibiting cannot be a determining or external reflection, whereby they would become determinations of it, but it is the explication, indeed the Absolute's own explication, and merely a showing of what it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"155.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0004","text":"## A. The Explication of the Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"155.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0005","text":"The Absolute is not merely Being, nor yet essence. The former is the first unreflected immediacy, the latter the reflected; each is, further, totality in itself; but a determinate totality. In essence, Being emerges as existence; and the relation of Being and essence has developed into the relation of inner and outer. The inner is essence, but as the totality which essentially has the determination of being related to Being and immediately Being. The outer is Being, but with the essential determination of being related to reflection, and immediately likewise being unconditioned identity with essence. The Absolute itself is the absolute unity of both; it is that which in general constitutes the ground of the essential relation, which, as relation, has not yet returned into this its identity, and whose ground has not yet been posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"155.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0006","text":"From this it follows that the determination of the Absolute is to be absolute form, but at the same time not as the identity whose moments are only simple determinacies;—but the identity whose moments are each, in themselves, totality, and thus, as indifferent to form, the complete content of the whole. Conversely, however, the Absolute is thus absolute content, such that content, which as such is indifferent multiplicity, has in it the negative relation to form, whereby its multiplicity is only one substantial identity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"155.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0007","text":"The identity of the Absolute is thus absolute by virtue of each of its parts itself being the whole, or every determinacy being totality; i.e. by virtue of determinacy in general having become an absolutely transparent semblance, a difference vanished in its positedness. Essence, existence, world being in itself, whole, parts, force,—these reflected determinations appear to representation as valid in and for themselves, as true Being; but the Absolute is, in relation to them, the ground in which they have perished. —Now because in the Absolute form is only simple identity with itself, the Absolute does not determine itself; for determination is a difference of form that initially counts as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"155.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0008","text":"But because it at the same time contains all difference and determination of form in general, or because it is itself absolute form and reflection, the difference of content must also emerge in it. Yet the Absolute itself is absolute identity; this is its determination, in that all multiplicity of the world being in itself and of the world of appearance, or of inner and outer totality, is sublated in it. —In itself there is no becoming in it, for it is not Being, nor is it self-reflecting determining; for it is not essence determining itself merely within itself; neither is it an externalizing itself, for it is the identity of inner and outer.—But thus the movement of reflection stands opposed to its absolute identity.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"155.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0009","text":"It is sublated in this identity, and so it is only its inner; but thereby it is external to it.—It therefore initially consists only in sublating its activity in the Absolute. It is the beyond of the manifold differences and determinations and their movement, which lies behind the Absolute; it is therefore indeed their receiving, but at the same time their perishing; thus it is the negative explication of the Absolute mentioned above.—In its true presentation this explication is the whole hitherto of the logical movement of the sphere of Being and essence, the content of which has not been gathered up from outside as something given and contingent, nor sunk into the abyss of the Absolute by a reflection external to it, but has determined itself in it through its inner necessity and, as the proper becoming of Being and as the reflection of essence, has returned into the Absolute as into its ground","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"155.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0010","text":".","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"155.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0011","text":"But this explication itself at the same time has a positive side; namely, insofar as the finite, in that it perishes, demonstrates this nature of being related to the Absolute, or of containing the Absolute within itself. Yet this side is not so much the positive explication of the Absolute itself as rather the explication of the determinations, namely that they have the Absolute as their abyss, but also as their ground, or that what gives them, to the semblance, a subsistence is the Absolute itself.—Semblance is not nothing; rather, it is reflection, relation to the Absolute; or it is semblance insofar as the Absolute shines in it. This positive explication thus still holds the finite back from its vanishing and considers it as an expression and image of the Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"155.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0012","text":"But the transparency of the finite, which permits only the Absolute to look through it, ends in complete vanishing; for there is nothing in the finite that could preserve for it a difference from the Absolute; it is a medium that is absorbed by that which shines through it.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"155.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0013","text":"This positive explication of the Absolute is therefore itself only a shining; for the truly positive that it and the explicated content contain is the Absolute itself. Whatever further determinations occur, the form in which the Absolute shines, is a nullity, which the explication takes up from without and by which it gains a beginning for its activity. Such a determination does not have its beginning in the Absolute, but only its end. This explication is therefore indeed absolute activity through its relation to the Absolute, into which it returns, but not according to its point of departure, which is a determination external to the Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"155.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0014","text":"In fact, however, the explication of the Absolute is its own activity, one which begins with itself as it arrives at itself. The Absolute, merely as absolute identity, is determinate; namely, as the identical; it is thus posited through reflection, over against opposition and multiplicity; or it is merely the negative of reflection and of determining in general.—Thus not only is that explication of the Absolute something imperfect, but this Absolute itself, at which one merely arrives, is imperfect as well. Or that Absolute which is merely as absolute identity is only the Absolute of an external reflection. It is therefore not the absolute Absolute, but the Absolute in a determinacy, or it is attribute.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"155.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DADA:P0015","text":"But the Absolute is not merely attribute because it is the object of an external reflection and thus something determined by it.—Or reflection is not merely external to it; rather, immediately, precisely because it is external to it, it is internal to it. The Absolute is Absolute only because it is not abstract identity, but the identity of Being and essence, or the identity of inner and outer. It is therefore itself the absolute form which makes it shine within itself and determines it as attribute.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"155.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DADA:P0015"]}],"source_digest":"6fe472787f38860fb3c18736ad598d66ec6f734b2f1dd765ca73c9740c8621a3","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Die Auslegung des Absoluten."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Die Auslegung des Absoluten.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA","title":"B. The Absolute Attribute.","order":156,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDAA","text":"Der Ausdruck, der gebraucht worden ist: das Absolut-Absolute, bezeichnet das in seiner Form in sich zurückgekehrte Absolute, oder dessen Form seinem Inhalte gleich ist. Das Attribut ist das nur relative Absolute, eine Verknüpfung, welche nichts anderes bedeutet, als das Absolute in einer Formbestimmung. Die Form ist nämlich zuerst vor ihrer vollendeten Auslegung nur erst innerlich,\" oder was dasselbe ist, nur äußerlich, überhaupt zuerst bestimmte Form oder Negation überhaupt. Aber weil sie zugleich als Form des Absoluten ist, so ist das Attribut der ganze Inhalt des Absoluten; es ist die Totalität, welche früher als eine Welt erschien, oder als eine der Seiten des wesentlichen Verhältnisses, deren jede selbst das Ganze ist. Aber die beiden Welten, die erscheinende und die an und für sich seyende, sollten jede in ihrem Wesen einander entgegengesetzt seyn. Die eine Seite des wesentlichen Verhältnisses war zwar der andern gleich; das Ganze so viel als die Theile; die Äußerung der Kraft derselbe Inhalt, als diese selbst, und das Äußere überhaupt dasselbe was das Innere. Aber zugleich sollten diese Seiten, jede noch ein eigenes unmittelbares Bestehen haben, die eine als die seyende, die andere als die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit. Im Absoluten dagegen sind diese unterschiedenen Unmittelbarkeiten zum Scheine herabgesetzt, und die Totalität, welche das Attribut ist, ist gesetzt als sein wahres und einziges Bestehen; die Bestimmung aber, in der es ist, als das unwesentliche.\n\nDas Absolute ist darum Attribut, weil es als einfache absolute Identität in der Bestimmung der Identität ist; an die Bestimmung überhaupt können nun andere Bestimmungen angeknüpft werden, z.B. auch daß mehrere Attribute seyen. Aber weil die absolute Identität nur diese Bedeutung hat, nicht nur daß alle Bestimmungen aufgehoben sind, sondern daß sie auch die Reflexion ist, die sich selbst aufgehoben hat, so sind an ihr alle Bestimmungen gesetzt, als aufgehobene. Oder die Totalität ist gesetzt als die absolute, oder das Attribut hat das Absolute zu seinem Inhalt und Bestehen; seine Formbestimmung, wodurch es Attribut ist, ist daher auch gesetzt, unmittelbar als bloßer Schein; das Negative als Negatives. Der positive Schein, den die Auslegung sich durch das Attribut gibt, indem sie das Endliche in seiner Schranke nicht als ein an und für sich Seyendes nimmt, sondern sein Bestehen in das Absolute auflöst, und es zum Attribut erweitert, hebt dieß selbst auf, daß es Attribut sey; sie versenkt dasselbe und ihr unterscheidendes Thun in das einfache Absolute.\n\nAber indem die Reflexion von ihrem Unterscheiden so nur zur Identität des Absoluten zurückkehrt, ist sie zugleich nicht aus ihrer Äußerlichkeit heraus und zum wahrhaften Absoluten gekommen. Sie hat nur die unbestimmte, abstrakte Identität erreicht; das heißt, diejenige, welche in der Bestimmtheit der Identität ist.—Oder die Reflexion, indem sie als innere Form das Absolute zum Attribut bestimmt, so ist dieses Bestimmen ein noch von der Äußerlichkeit Verschiedenes; die innere Bestimmung durchdringt das Absolute nicht; seine Äußerung ist, als ein bloß gesetztes am Absoluten zu verschwinden.\n\nDie Form also, sie werde als äußere oder innere genommen, wodurch das Absolute Attribut wäre, ist zugleich gesetzt, ein an sich selbst Nichtiges, ein äußerlicher Schein, oder bloße Art und Weise zu seyn.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0001","text":"Der Ausdruck, der gebraucht worden ist: das Absolut-Absolute, bezeichnet das in seiner Form in sich zurückgekehrte Absolute, oder dessen Form seinem Inhalte gleich ist. Das Attribut ist das nur relative Absolute, eine Verknüpfung, welche nichts anderes bedeutet, als das Absolute in einer Formbestimmung. Die Form ist nämlich zuerst vor ihrer vollendeten Auslegung nur erst innerlich,\" oder was dasselbe ist, nur äußerlich, überhaupt zuerst bestimmte Form oder Negation überhaupt. Aber weil sie zugleich als Form des Absoluten ist, so ist das Attribut der ganze Inhalt des Absoluten; es ist die Totalität, welche früher als eine Welt erschien, oder als eine der Seiten des wesentlichen Verhältnisses, deren jede selbst das Ganze ist. Aber die beiden Welten, die erscheinende und die an und für sich seyende, sollten jede in ihrem Wesen einander entgegengesetzt seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"156.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0002","text":"Die eine Seite des wesentlichen Verhältnisses war zwar der andern gleich; das Ganze so viel als die Theile; die Äußerung der Kraft derselbe Inhalt, als diese selbst, und das Äußere überhaupt dasselbe was das Innere. Aber zugleich sollten diese Seiten, jede noch ein eigenes unmittelbares Bestehen haben, die eine als die seyende, die andere als die reflektirte Unmittelbarkeit. Im Absoluten dagegen sind diese unterschiedenen Unmittelbarkeiten zum Scheine herabgesetzt, und die Totalität, welche das Attribut ist, ist gesetzt als sein wahres und einziges Bestehen; die Bestimmung aber, in der es ist, als das unwesentliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"156.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0003","text":"Das Absolute ist darum Attribut, weil es als einfache absolute Identität in der Bestimmung der Identität ist; an die Bestimmung überhaupt können nun andere Bestimmungen angeknüpft werden, z.B. auch daß mehrere Attribute seyen. Aber weil die absolute Identität nur diese Bedeutung hat, nicht nur daß alle Bestimmungen aufgehoben sind, sondern daß sie auch die Reflexion ist, die sich selbst aufgehoben hat, so sind an ihr alle Bestimmungen gesetzt, als aufgehobene. Oder die Totalität ist gesetzt als die absolute, oder das Attribut hat das Absolute zu seinem Inhalt und Bestehen; seine Formbestimmung, wodurch es Attribut ist, ist daher auch gesetzt, unmittelbar als bloßer Schein; das Negative als Negatives.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"156.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0004","text":"Der positive Schein, den die Auslegung sich durch das Attribut gibt, indem sie das Endliche in seiner Schranke nicht als ein an und für sich Seyendes nimmt, sondern sein Bestehen in das Absolute auflöst, und es zum Attribut erweitert, hebt dieß selbst auf, daß es Attribut sey; sie versenkt dasselbe und ihr unterscheidendes Thun in das einfache Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"156.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0005","text":"Aber indem die Reflexion von ihrem Unterscheiden so nur zur Identität des Absoluten zurückkehrt, ist sie zugleich nicht aus ihrer Äußerlichkeit heraus und zum wahrhaften Absoluten gekommen. Sie hat nur die unbestimmte, abstrakte Identität erreicht; das heißt, diejenige, welche in der Bestimmtheit der Identität ist.—Oder die Reflexion, indem sie als innere Form das Absolute zum Attribut bestimmt, so ist dieses Bestimmen ein noch von der Äußerlichkeit Verschiedenes; die innere Bestimmung durchdringt das Absolute nicht; seine Äußerung ist, als ein bloß gesetztes am Absoluten zu verschwinden.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"156.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0006","text":"Die Form also, sie werde als äußere oder innere genommen, wodurch das Absolute Attribut wäre, ist zugleich gesetzt, ein an sich selbst Nichtiges, ein äußerlicher Schein, oder bloße Art und Weise zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"156.6"}],"sha256":"22cde828249e7bca0929d6d41288b077ba87973fea34cad5791d0926669dca2a","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105814949311Z_21dd87fe","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. The Absolute Attribute.","source_sha256":"22cde828249e7bca0929d6d41288b077ba87973fea34cad5791d0926669dca2a","sha256":"b0f29e607ea74d0c0741fb24e9955328e859818900ad88b65d1dd0b0a307ceb8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:58:14.949347+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0001","text":"The expression that has been used: the absolute-absolute, denotes the Absolute that has returned into itself in its form, or whose form is equal to its content. The attribute is the merely relative Absolute, a connection which means nothing other than the Absolute in a determination of form. For the form is at first, before its completed exposition, only internal,” or, what is the same thing, only external; in general, at first determinate form, or negation in general. But because it is at the same time form of the Absolute, the attribute is the entire content of the Absolute; it is the totality which previously appeared as a world, or as one of the sides of the essential relation, each of which is itself the whole. But the two worlds, the appearing one and the one that is in and for itself, were supposed each to be opposed to the other in its essence.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"156.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0002","text":"One side of the essential relation was indeed equal to the other; the whole as much as the parts; the expression of force the same content as force itself; and the external in general the same as the internal. But at the same time these sides were supposed each still to have a proper immediate subsistence, the one as the being immediacy, the other as the reflected immediacy. In the Absolute, on the contrary, these distinguished immediacies are reduced to semblance, and the totality which is the attribute is posited as its true and sole subsistence; but the determination in which it is, as the unessential.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"156.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0003","text":"The Absolute is therefore attribute because, as simple absolute identity, it is in the determination of identity; other determinations may now be attached to the determination in general, e.g. also that there are several attributes. But because absolute identity has only this meaning, not merely that all determinations are sublated, but that it is also the reflection which has sublated itself, all determinations are posited in it as sublated. Or, the totality is posited as the absolute, or the attribute has the Absolute as its content and subsistence; its determination of form, through which it is attribute, is therefore also posited immediately as mere semblance; the negative as negative.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"156.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0004","text":"The positive semblance that exposition gives itself through the attribute, in that it does not take the finite in its limitation as something that is in and for itself, but dissolves its subsistence into the Absolute and expands it into an attribute, itself sublates the fact that it is attribute; it sinks the same and its distinguishing activity into the simple Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"156.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0005","text":"But in thus returning from its distinguishing only to the identity of the Absolute, reflection has at the same time not emerged from its externality and arrived at the true Absolute. It has attained only indeterminate, abstract identity; that is, that which is in the determinacy of identity.—Or, in that reflection, as inner form, determines the Absolute as attribute, this determining is still distinct from externality; the inner determination does not penetrate the Absolute; its expression is to disappear, as something merely posited, in the Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"156.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0006","text":"Thus the form, whether taken as external or internal, through which the Absolute would be attribute, is at the same time posited as something null in itself, as an external semblance, or as mere mode and manner.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"156.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDAA:P0006"]}],"source_digest":"ea306e7496413c2735d2bf5845911855da46d950f1925b1237575f2fdea187c2","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Das absolute Attribut."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Das absolute Attribut.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD","title":"C. The Mode of the Absolute.","order":157,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CDMD","text":"Das Attribut ist erstlich das Absolute als in der einfachen Identität mit sich. Zweitens ist es Negation, und diese als Negation ist die formelle Reflexion-in-sich. Diese beiden Seiten machen zunächst die zwei Extreme des Attributs aus, deren Mitte es selbst ist, indem es sowohl das Absolute als die Bestimmtheit ist.—Das zweite dieser Extreme ist das Negative als Negatives, die dem Absoluten äußerliche Reflexion.—Oder insofern es als das Innere des Absoluten genommen wird, und seine eigene Bestimmung es ist, sich als Modus zu setzen, so ist er das Außersichseyn des Absoluten, der Verlust seiner in die Veränderlichkeit und Zufälligkeit des Seyns, sein Übergegangenseyn ins Entgegengesetzte ohne Rückkehr in sich; die totalitätslose Mannigfaltigkeit der Form und Inhaltsbestimmungen.\n\nDer Modus, die Äußerlichkeit des Absoluten, ist aber nicht nur dieß, sondern die als Äußerlichkeit gesetzte Äußerlichkeit, eine bloße Art und Weise; somit der Schein als Schein, oder die Reflexion der Form in sich; somit die Identität mit sich, welche das Absolute ist. In der That ist also erst im Modus das Absolute als absolute Identität gesetzt; es ist nur, was es ist, nämlich Identität mit sich, als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, als Scheinen, das als Scheinen gesetzt ist.\n\nInsofern daher die Auslegung des Absoluten von seiner absoluten Identität anfängt, und zu dem Attribute und von da zum Modus übergeht, so hat sie darin vollständig ihre Momente durchloffen. Aber erstlich ist sie darin nicht ein bloß negatives Verhalten gegen diese Bestimmungen, sondern dieß ihr Thun ist die reflektirende Bewegung selbst, als welche das Absolute nur wahrhaft die absolute Identität ist.—Zweitens hat sie es dabei nicht bloß mit Äußerlichem zu thun, und der Modus ist nicht nur die äußerste Äußerlichkeit, sondern weil er der Schein als Schein ist, so ist er die Rückkehr in sich, die sich selbst auflösende Reflexion, als welche das Absolute absolutes Seyn ist.—Drittens scheint die auslegende Reflexion von ihren eigenen Bestimmungen und von Äußerlichem anzufangen, die Modos oder auch die Bestimmungen des Attributs, als sonst außer dem Absoluten vorgefundene aufzunehmen, und ihr Thun darin zu bestehen, daß sie dieselben in die indifferente Identität nur zurückführt. In der That aber hat sie an dem Absoluten selbst die Bestimmtheit, von der sie anfängt. Denn das Absolute als erste indifferente Identität ist selbst nur das bestimmte Absolute, oder Attribut, weil es das unbewegte, noch unreflektirte Absolute ist. Diese Bestimmtheit, weil sie Bestimmtheit ist, gehört der reflektirenden Bewegung an; nur durch sie ist es bestimmt als das erste Identische, ebenso nur durch sie hat es die absolute Form, und ist nicht das sich Gleichseyende, sondern das sich selbst Gleichsetzende.\n\nDie wahrhafte Bedeutung des Modus ist daher, daß er die reflektirende eigene Bewegung des Absoluten ist; ein Bestimmen, aber nicht wodurch es ein Anderes würde, sondern nur dessen, was es schon ist; die durchsichtige Äußerlichkeit, welche das Zeigen seiner selbst ist; eine Bewegung aus sich heraus; aber so daß dieß Seyn-nach-Aussen, ebenso sehr die Innerlichkeit selbst ist; und damit ebenso sehr ein Setzen, das nicht bloß Gesetztseyn, sondern absolutes Seyn ist.\n\nWenn daher nach einem Inhalt der Auslegung gefragt wird, was denn das Absolute zeige? so ist der Unterschied von Form und Inhalt im Absoluten ohnehin aufgelöst. Oder eben dieß ist der Inhalt des Absoluten, sich zu manifestiren. Das Absolute ist die absolute Form, welche als die Entzweiung ihrer schlechthin identisch mit sich ist, das Negative als Negatives; oder das mit sich zusammengeht, und nur so die absolute Identität mit sich ist, die ebenso sehr gleichgültig gegen ihre Unterschiede, oder absoluter Inhalt ist; der Inhalt ist daher nur diese Auslegung selbst.\n\nDas Absolute als diese sich selbst tragende Bewegung der Auslegung, als Art und Weise, welche seine absolute Identität mit sich selbst ist, ist Äußerung, nicht eines Innern, nicht gegen ein Anderes, sondern ist nur als absolutes sich für sich selbst Manifestiren; es ist so Wirklichkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0001","text":"Das Attribut ist erstlich das Absolute als in der einfachen Identität mit sich. Zweitens ist es Negation, und diese als Negation ist die formelle Reflexion-in-sich. Diese beiden Seiten machen zunächst die zwei Extreme des Attributs aus, deren Mitte es selbst ist, indem es sowohl das Absolute als die Bestimmtheit ist.—Das zweite dieser Extreme ist das Negative als Negatives, die dem Absoluten äußerliche Reflexion.—Oder insofern es als das Innere des Absoluten genommen wird, und seine eigene Bestimmung es ist, sich als Modus zu setzen, so ist er das Außersichseyn des Absoluten, der Verlust seiner in die Veränderlichkeit und Zufälligkeit des Seyns, sein Übergegangenseyn ins Entgegengesetzte ohne Rückkehr in sich; die totalitätslose Mannigfaltigkeit der Form und Inhaltsbestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"157.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0002","text":"Der Modus, die Äußerlichkeit des Absoluten, ist aber nicht nur dieß, sondern die als Äußerlichkeit gesetzte Äußerlichkeit, eine bloße Art und Weise; somit der Schein als Schein, oder die Reflexion der Form in sich; somit die Identität mit sich, welche das Absolute ist. In der That ist also erst im Modus das Absolute als absolute Identität gesetzt; es ist nur, was es ist, nämlich Identität mit sich, als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, als Scheinen, das als Scheinen gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"157.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0003","text":"Insofern daher die Auslegung des Absoluten von seiner absoluten Identität anfängt, und zu dem Attribute und von da zum Modus übergeht, so hat sie darin vollständig ihre Momente durchloffen. Aber erstlich ist sie darin nicht ein bloß negatives Verhalten gegen diese Bestimmungen, sondern dieß ihr Thun ist die reflektirende Bewegung selbst, als welche das Absolute nur wahrhaft die absolute Identität ist.—Zweitens hat sie es dabei nicht bloß mit Äußerlichem zu thun, und der Modus ist nicht nur die äußerste Äußerlichkeit, sondern weil er der Schein als Schein ist, so ist er die Rückkehr in sich, die sich selbst auflösende Reflexion, als welche das Absolute absolutes Seyn ist.—Drittens scheint die auslegende Reflexion von ihren eigenen Bestimmungen und von Äußerlichem anzufangen, die Modos oder auch die Bestimmungen des Attributs, als sonst außer dem Absoluten vorgefundene aufzunehmen, und","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"157.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0004","text":"ihr Thun darin zu bestehen, daß sie dieselben in die indifferente Identität nur zurückführt. In der That aber hat sie an dem Absoluten selbst die Bestimmtheit, von der sie anfängt. Denn das Absolute als erste indifferente Identität ist selbst nur das bestimmte Absolute, oder Attribut, weil es das unbewegte, noch unreflektirte Absolute ist. Diese Bestimmtheit, weil sie Bestimmtheit ist, gehört der reflektirenden Bewegung an; nur durch sie ist es bestimmt als das erste Identische, ebenso nur durch sie hat es die absolute Form, und ist nicht das sich Gleichseyende, sondern das sich selbst Gleichsetzende.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"157.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0005","text":"Die wahrhafte Bedeutung des Modus ist daher, daß er die reflektirende eigene Bewegung des Absoluten ist; ein Bestimmen, aber nicht wodurch es ein Anderes würde, sondern nur dessen, was es schon ist; die durchsichtige Äußerlichkeit, welche das Zeigen seiner selbst ist; eine Bewegung aus sich heraus; aber so daß dieß Seyn-nach-Aussen, ebenso sehr die Innerlichkeit selbst ist; und damit ebenso sehr ein Setzen, das nicht bloß Gesetztseyn, sondern absolutes Seyn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"157.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0006","text":"Wenn daher nach einem Inhalt der Auslegung gefragt wird, was denn das Absolute zeige? so ist der Unterschied von Form und Inhalt im Absoluten ohnehin aufgelöst. Oder eben dieß ist der Inhalt des Absoluten, sich zu manifestiren. Das Absolute ist die absolute Form, welche als die Entzweiung ihrer schlechthin identisch mit sich ist, das Negative als Negatives; oder das mit sich zusammengeht, und nur so die absolute Identität mit sich ist, die ebenso sehr gleichgültig gegen ihre Unterschiede, oder absoluter Inhalt ist; der Inhalt ist daher nur diese Auslegung selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"157.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0007","text":"Das Absolute als diese sich selbst tragende Bewegung der Auslegung, als Art und Weise, welche seine absolute Identität mit sich selbst ist, ist Äußerung, nicht eines Innern, nicht gegen ein Anderes, sondern ist nur als absolutes sich für sich selbst Manifestiren; es ist so Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"157.7"}],"sha256":"19190dfc8863e6957c5dd0795f1fbf6c7c746e7c6b9bd05d85fa4ee9f4dbfc00","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105824198183Z_0347e073","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. The Mode of the Absolute.","source_sha256":"19190dfc8863e6957c5dd0795f1fbf6c7c746e7c6b9bd05d85fa4ee9f4dbfc00","sha256":"563e32728dcfebb8fa41281e19d1dc067a4ddcfa668046258166157b7b28be8c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:58:24.198216+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0001","text":"The attribute is, first, the Absolute as in simple identity with itself. Second, it is negation, and this, as negation, is formal reflection-into-itself. These two sides initially constitute the two extremes of the attribute, whose middle it itself is, in that it is both the Absolute and determinateness.—The second of these extremes is the negative as negative, reflection external to the Absolute.—Or, insofar as it is taken as the inner of the Absolute, and its own determination is to posit itself as mode, it is the being-outside-itself of the Absolute, its loss of itself in the mutability and contingency of being, its having-passed-over into the opposite without return into itself; the multiplicity of determinations of form and content devoid of totality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"157.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0002","text":"But the mode, the externality of the Absolute, is not merely this, but externality posited as externality, a mere manner; thus semblance as semblance, or the reflection of form into itself; thus the identity with itself which is the Absolute. In fact, therefore, it is only in the mode that the Absolute is posited as absolute identity; it is only what it is, namely identity with itself, as self-relating negativity, as semblance which is posited as semblance.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"157.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0003","text":"Insofar, therefore, as the exposition of the Absolute begins from its absolute identity, and proceeds to the attribute and thence to the mode, it has therein completely run through its moments. But first, it is therein not a merely negative relation to these determinations; rather, this its activity is the reflecting movement itself, as which alone the Absolute is truly absolute identity.—Second, it does not thereby deal merely with something external, and the mode is not merely the utmost externality; rather, because it is semblance as semblance, it is the return into itself, self-dissolving reflection, as which the Absolute is absolute being.—Third, the expounding reflection seems to begin from its own determinations and from something external, to take up the modes, or also the determinations of the attribute, as otherwise found outside the Absolute, and","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"157.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0004","text":"to consist in its activity of merely leading them back into indifferent identity. But in fact it has in the Absolute itself the determinateness from which it begins. For the Absolute as first indifferent identity is itself only the determinate Absolute, or attribute, because it is the unmoved, as yet unreflected Absolute. This determinateness, because it is determinateness, belongs to the reflecting movement; only through it is it determined as the first identical, just as only through it does it have absolute form, and is not that which is equal to itself, but that which posits itself as equal to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"157.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0005","text":"The true significance of the mode is therefore that it is the reflective movement proper to the Absolute itself; a determining, yet not one through which it would become an other, but only a determining of what it already is; transparent externality, which is the showing of itself; a movement out of itself; but such that this being-outward is equally inwardness itself; and thus equally a positing which is not merely positedness, but absolute being.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"157.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0006","text":"If, therefore, one asks after a content of the exposition, what then the Absolute shows, the distinction between form and content is in any case dissolved in the Absolute. Or rather, this is the content of the Absolute: to manifest itself. The Absolute is the absolute form which, as the diremption of itself, is absolutely identical with itself, the negative as negative; or that which goes together with itself, and only thus is absolute identity with itself, which is equally indifferent to its distinctions, or absolute content; the content is therefore only this exposition itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"157.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0007","text":"The Absolute, as this self-sustaining movement of exposition, as manner which is its absolute identity with itself, is expression, not of an inner, not toward an other, but is only as absolute manifesting-itself-for-itself; it is thus actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"157.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CDMD:P0007"]}],"source_digest":"3d3d90323819d5270542c0150b278aa15948085a57ce219937261cd165483e17","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Der Modus des Absoluten."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Der Modus des Absoluten.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41","title":"Remark.","order":158,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_A_41","text":"Dem Begriffe des Absoluten und dem Verhältnisse der Reflexion zu demselben, wie es sich hier dargestellt hat, entspricht der Begriff der spinozistischen Substanz. Der Spinozismus ist darin eine mangelhafte Philosophie, daß die Reflexion und deren mannigfaltiges Bestimmen ein äußerliches Denken ist.—Die Substanz dieses Systems ist Eine Substanz, Eine untrennbare Totalität; es giebt keine Bestimmtheit, die nicht in diesem Absoluten enthalten und aufgelöst wäre; und es ist wichtig genug, daß Alles, was dem natürlichen Vorstellen oder dem bestimmenden Verstande als selbstständiges erscheint und vorschwebt, in jenem nothwendigen Begriffe gänzlich zu einem bloßen Gesetztseyn herabgesetzt ist.—Die Bestimmtheit ist Negation, ist das absolute Princip der Spinozistischen Philosophie; diese wahrhafte und einfache Einsicht begründet die absolute Einheit der Substanz. Aber Spinoza bleibt bei der Negation als Bestimmtheit oder Qualität stehen; er geht nicht zur Erkenntniß derselben als absoluter, das heißt, sich negirender Negation fort; somit enthält seine Substanz nicht selbst die absolute Form, und das Erkennen derselben ist kein immanentes Erkennen. Zwar ist die Substanz absolute Einheit des Denkens und Seyns oder der Ausdehnung; sie enthält also das Denken selbst, aber nur in seiner Einheit mit der Ausdehnung; das heißt nicht als sich von der Ausdehnung trennend, somit überhaupt nicht als Bestimmen und Formiren, noch auch als die zurückkehrende und aus sich selbst anfangende Bewegung. Theils fehlt dadurch der Substanz, das Princip der Persönlichkeit,—ein Mangel, welcher vornehmlich gegen das spinozistische System empört hat; —Theils ist das Erkennen die äußerliche Reflexion, welche das, was als Endliches erscheint, die Bestimmtheit des Attributs und den Modus, wie auch überhaupt sich selbst, nicht aus der Substanz begreift und ableitet, sondern als ein äußerlicher Verstand thätig ist, die Bestimmungen als gegebene aufnimmt, und sie auf das Absolute zurückführt, nicht aber von diesem ihre Anfänge hernimmt.\n\nDie Begriffe, die Spinoza von der Substanz giebt, sind die Begriffe der Ursache seiner selbst,—daß sie das ist, dessen Wesen die Existenz in sich schließe;—daß der Begriff des Absoluten nicht des Begriffs eines Andern bedürfe, von dem er gebildet werden müsse; —diese Begriffe, so tief und richtig sie sind, sind Definitionen, welche vorne in der Wissenschaft unmittelbar angenommen werden. Mathematik und andere untergeordnete Wissenschaften müssen mit einem Vorausgesetzten anfangen, das ihr Element und positive Grundlage ausmacht. Aber das Absolute kann nicht ein Erstes, Unmittelbares seyn, sondern das Absolute ist wesentlich sein Resultat.\n\nNach der Definition des Absoluten tritt bei Spinoza ferner die Definition des Attributs auf; und wird als dasjenige bestimmt, wie der Verstand dessen Wesen begreift. Außerdem daß der Verstand seiner Natur nach als später angenommen wird, als das Attribut,—denn Spinoza bestimmt ihn als Modus,—so wird das Attribut, die Bestimmung als Bestimmung des Absoluten, von einem Andern, dem Verstande, abhängig gemacht, welches der Substanz gegenüber äußerlich und unmittelbar auftritt.\n\nDie Attribute bestimmt Spinoza ferner als unendlich; und zwar unendlich auch im Sinne einer unendlichen Vielheit. Es kommen zwar weiterhin nur die zwei vor,—Denken und Ausdehnung, und es ist nicht gezeigt, wie die unendliche Vielheit sich nothwendig nur auf den Gegensatz und zwar diesen bestimmten, des Denkens und der Ausdehnung, reducirt.-Diese beiden Attribute sind deswegen empirisch aufgenommen. Denken und Seyn stellen das Absolute in einer Determination vor, das Absolute selbst ist ihre absolute Einheit, so daß sie nur unwesentliche Formen sind, die Ordnung der Dinge dieselbe ist, als die der Vorstellungen oder Gedanken, und das Eine Absolute nur von der äußerlichen Reflexion, einem Modus, unter jenen beiden Bestimmungen, das eine Mal als eine Totalität von Vorstellungen, das andere Mal als eine Totalität von Dingen und deren Veränderungen betrachtet wird. Wie es diese äußere Reflexion ist, welche jenen Unterschied macht, so ist sie es auch, die ihn in die absolute Identität zurückführt und versenkt. Diese ganze Bewegung aber geht außer dem Absoluten vor. Zwar ist dieses selbst auch das Denken, und sofern diese Bewegung nur im Absoluten; aber, wie bemerkt, ist sie im Absoluten nur als Einheit mit der Ausdehnung, somit nicht als diese Bewegung, welche wesentlich auch das Moment der Entgegensetzung ist. —Spinoza macht die erhabene Forderung an das Denken, alles unter der Gestalt der Ewigkeit, sub Specie aeterni, zu betrachten, das heißt, wie es im Absoluten ist. Aber in jenem Absoluten, das nur die unbewegte Identität ist, ist das Attribut, wie der Modus, nur als verschwindend, nicht als werdend, so daß hiermit auch jenes Verschwinden seinen positiven Anfang nur von Außen nimmt.\n\nDas dritte, der Modus, ist bei Spinoza, Affektion der Substanz, die bestimmte Bestimmtheit, was in einem Andern ist, und durch dieß Andere gefaßt wird. Die Attribute haben eigentlich nur die unbestimmte Verschiedenheit zu ihrer Bestimmung; jedes soll die Totalität der Substanz ausdrücken und aus sich selbst begriffen werden; insofern es aber das Absolute als bestimmt ist, so enthält es das Andersseyn, und ist nicht nur aus sich selbst zu begreifen. In dem Modus ist daher erst eigentlich die Bestimmung des Attributs gesetzt.\n\nDieß Dritte bleibt ferner bloßer Modus, einer Seits ist er unmittelbar Gegebenes, anderer Seits wird seine Nichtigkeit nicht als Reflexion in sich erkannt.—Die spinozistische Auslegung des Absoluten ist daher insofern wohl vollständig, als sie von dem Absoluten anfängt, hierauf das Attribut folgen läßt und mit dem Modus endigt; aber diese drei werden nur nach einander ohne innere Folge der Entwicklung aufgezählt, und das Dritte ist nicht die Negation als Negation, nicht sich negativ auf sich beziehende Negation, wodurch sie an ihr selbst, die Rückkehr in die erste Identität und diese, wahrhafte Identität wäre. Es fehlt daher die Nothwendigkeit des Fortgangs des Absoluten zur Unwesentlichkeit, so wie ihre Auflösung an und für sich selbst in die Identität; oder es mangelt sowohl das Werden der Identität als ihrer Bestimmungen.\n\nAuf gleiche Weise ist in der orientalischen Vorstellung der Emanation das Absolute das sich selbst erleuchtende Licht. Allein es erleuchtet sich nicht nur, sondern strömt auch aus. Seine Ausströmungen sind Entfernungen von seiner ungetrübten Klarheit; die folgenden Ausgeburten sind unvollkommener als die vorhergehenden, aus denen sie entstehen. Das Ausströmen ist nur als ein Geschehen genommen, das Werden nur als ein fortgehender Verlust. So verdunkelt sich das Seyn immer mehr, und die Nacht, das Negative, ist das Letzte der Linie, das nicht in das erste Licht zurück kehrt.\n\nDer Mangel der Reflexion in sich, den die Spinozistische Auslegung des Absoluten wie die Emanationslehre an ihr hat, ist in dem Begriffe der leibnizischen Monade ergänzt.—Der Einseitigkeit eines philosophischen Princips pflegt sich die entgegengesetzte gegenüber zu stellen, und, wie in Allem, die Totalität wenigstens als eine zerstreute Vollständigkeit vorhanden zu seyn.—Die Monade ist ein Eins, ein in sich reflektirtes Negatives; sie ist die Totalität des Inhalts der Welt; das verschiedene Mannigfaltige ist in ihr nicht nur verschwunden, sondern auf negative Weise aufbewahrt; die spinozistische Substanz ist die Einheit alles Inhalts; aber dieser mannigfaltige Inhalt der Welt ist nicht als solcher in ihr, sondern in der ihr äußerlichen Reflexion. Die Monade ist daher wesentlich vorstellend; sie hat aber, ob sie wohl eine endliche ist, keine Passivität; sondern die Veränderungen und Bestimmungen in ihr sind Manifestationen ihrer in ihr selbst. Sie ist Entelechie; das Offenbahren ist ihr eigenes Thun.—Dabei ist die Monade auch bestimmt, von anderen unterschieden; die Bestimmtheit fällt in den besondern Inhalt und die Art und Weise der Manifestation. Die Monade ist daher an sich, ihrer Substanz nach, die Totalität, nicht in ihrer Manifestation. Diese Beschränkung der Monade fällt nothwendig nicht in die sich selbst setzende oder vorstellende Monade, sondern in ihr Ansichseyn, oder ist absolute Grenze, eine Prädestination, welche durch ein anderes Wesen, als sie ist, gesetzt wird. Ferner da Begrenzte nur sind, als sich auf andere Begrenzte beziehend, die Monade aber zugleich ein in sich geschlossenes Absolutes ist, so fällt die Harmonie dieser Begrenzungen, nämlich die Beziehung der Monaden auf einander, außer ihnen und ist gleichfalls von einem andern Wesen oder an sich prästabilirt.\n\nEs erhellt, daß durch das Princip der Reflexion-in-sich, welches die Grundbestimmung der Monade ausmacht, zwar das Andersseyn und die Einwirkung von außen überhaupt entfernt ist, und die Veränderungen der Monade ihr eigenes Setzen sind,—daß aber auf der andern Seite die Passivität durch Anderes, nur in eine absolute Schranke, in eine Schranke des Ansichseyns verwandelt ist. Leibnitz schreibt den Monaden eine gewisse Vollendung in sich zu, eine Art von Selbstständigkeit; sie sind geschaffene Wesen.—Näher ihre Schranke betrachtet, so ergiebt sich aus dieser Darstellung, daß die Manifestation ihrer selbst, die ihnen zukommt, die Totalität der Form ist. Es ist ein höchst wichtiger Begriffe daß die Veränderungen der Monade als passivitätslose Aktionen, als Manifestationen ihrer selbst vorgestellt, und das Princip der Reflexion in sich, oder der Individuation als wesentlich hervorsteht. Ferner ist es nothwendig, die Endlichkeit darin bestehen zu lassen, daß der Inhalt oder die Substanz von der Form unterschieden, und dann weiter jene beschränkt, diese aber unendlich ist. Aber nun wäre im Begriffe der absoluten Monade nicht nur jene absolute Einheit der Form und des Inhalts, sondern auch die Natur der Reflexion, als die sich auf sich selbst beziehende Negativität sich von sich abzustoßen, wodurch sie setzend und schaffend ist, zu finden. Es ist zwar im leibnitzischen Systeme das Weitere gleichfalls vorhanden, daß Gott die Quelle der Existenz und des Wesens der Monaden ist, d. h. daß jene absoluten Schranken im Ansichseyn der Monaden nicht an und für sich seyende sind, sondern im Absoluten verschwinden. Aber es zeigen sich in diesen Bestimmungen nur die gewöhnlichen Vorstellungen, die ohne philosophische Entwicklung gelassen und nicht zu spekulativen Begriffen erhoben sind. So erhält das Princip der Individuation seine tiefere Ausführung nicht; die Begriffe über die Unterscheidungen der verschiedenen endlichen Monaden, und über ihr Verhältniß zu ihrem Absoluten, entspringen nicht aus diesem Wesen selbst oder nicht auf absolute Weise, sondern gehören der räsonnirenden, dogmatischen Reflexion an, und sind daher zu keiner innern Kohärenz gediehen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0001","text":"Dem Begriffe des Absoluten und dem Verhältnisse der Reflexion zu demselben, wie es sich hier dargestellt hat, entspricht der Begriff der spinozistischen Substanz. Der Spinozismus ist darin eine mangelhafte Philosophie, daß die Reflexion und deren mannigfaltiges Bestimmen ein äußerliches Denken ist.—Die Substanz dieses Systems ist Eine Substanz, Eine untrennbare Totalität; es giebt keine Bestimmtheit, die nicht in diesem Absoluten enthalten und aufgelöst wäre; und es ist wichtig genug, daß Alles, was dem natürlichen Vorstellen oder dem bestimmenden Verstande als selbstständiges erscheint und vorschwebt, in jenem nothwendigen Begriffe gänzlich zu einem bloßen Gesetztseyn herabgesetzt ist.—Die Bestimmtheit ist Negation, ist das absolute Princip der Spinozistischen Philosophie; diese wahrhafte und einfache Einsicht begründet die absolute Einheit der Substanz.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"158.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0002","text":"Aber Spinoza bleibt bei der Negation als Bestimmtheit oder Qualität stehen; er geht nicht zur Erkenntniß derselben als absoluter, das heißt, sich negirender Negation fort; somit enthält seine Substanz nicht selbst die absolute Form, und das Erkennen derselben ist kein immanentes Erkennen. Zwar ist die Substanz absolute Einheit des Denkens und Seyns oder der Ausdehnung; sie enthält also das Denken selbst, aber nur in seiner Einheit mit der Ausdehnung; das heißt nicht als sich von der Ausdehnung trennend, somit überhaupt nicht als Bestimmen und Formiren, noch auch als die zurückkehrende und aus sich selbst anfangende Bewegung.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"158.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0003","text":"Theils fehlt dadurch der Substanz, das Princip der Persönlichkeit,—ein Mangel, welcher vornehmlich gegen das spinozistische System empört hat; —Theils ist das Erkennen die äußerliche Reflexion, welche das, was als Endliches erscheint, die Bestimmtheit des Attributs und den Modus, wie auch überhaupt sich selbst, nicht aus der Substanz begreift und ableitet, sondern als ein äußerlicher Verstand thätig ist, die Bestimmungen als gegebene aufnimmt, und sie auf das Absolute zurückführt, nicht aber von diesem ihre Anfänge hernimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"158.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0004","text":"Die Begriffe, die Spinoza von der Substanz giebt, sind die Begriffe der Ursache seiner selbst,—daß sie das ist, dessen Wesen die Existenz in sich schließe;—daß der Begriff des Absoluten nicht des Begriffs eines Andern bedürfe, von dem er gebildet werden müsse; —diese Begriffe, so tief und richtig sie sind, sind Definitionen, welche vorne in der Wissenschaft unmittelbar angenommen werden. Mathematik und andere untergeordnete Wissenschaften müssen mit einem Vorausgesetzten anfangen, das ihr Element und positive Grundlage ausmacht. Aber das Absolute kann nicht ein Erstes, Unmittelbares seyn, sondern das Absolute ist wesentlich sein Resultat.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"158.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0005","text":"Nach der Definition des Absoluten tritt bei Spinoza ferner die Definition des Attributs auf; und wird als dasjenige bestimmt, wie der Verstand dessen Wesen begreift. Außerdem daß der Verstand seiner Natur nach als später angenommen wird, als das Attribut,—denn Spinoza bestimmt ihn als Modus,—so wird das Attribut, die Bestimmung als Bestimmung des Absoluten, von einem Andern, dem Verstande, abhängig gemacht, welches der Substanz gegenüber äußerlich und unmittelbar auftritt.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"158.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0006","text":"Die Attribute bestimmt Spinoza ferner als unendlich; und zwar unendlich auch im Sinne einer unendlichen Vielheit. Es kommen zwar weiterhin nur die zwei vor,—Denken und Ausdehnung, und es ist nicht gezeigt, wie die unendliche Vielheit sich nothwendig nur auf den Gegensatz und zwar diesen bestimmten, des Denkens und der Ausdehnung, reducirt.-Diese beiden Attribute sind deswegen empirisch aufgenommen. Denken und Seyn stellen das Absolute in einer Determination vor, das Absolute selbst ist ihre absolute Einheit, so daß sie nur unwesentliche Formen sind, die Ordnung der Dinge dieselbe ist, als die der Vorstellungen oder Gedanken, und das Eine Absolute nur von der äußerlichen Reflexion, einem Modus, unter jenen beiden Bestimmungen, das eine Mal als eine Totalität von Vorstellungen, das andere Mal als eine Totalität von Dingen und deren Veränderungen betrachtet wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"158.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0007","text":"Wie es diese äußere Reflexion ist, welche jenen Unterschied macht, so ist sie es auch, die ihn in die absolute Identität zurückführt und versenkt. Diese ganze Bewegung aber geht außer dem Absoluten vor. Zwar ist dieses selbst auch das Denken, und sofern diese Bewegung nur im Absoluten; aber, wie bemerkt, ist sie im Absoluten nur als Einheit mit der Ausdehnung, somit nicht als diese Bewegung, welche wesentlich auch das Moment der Entgegensetzung ist. —Spinoza macht die erhabene Forderung an das Denken, alles unter der Gestalt der Ewigkeit, sub Specie aeterni, zu betrachten, das heißt, wie es im Absoluten ist. Aber in jenem Absoluten, das nur die unbewegte Identität ist, ist das Attribut, wie der Modus, nur als verschwindend, nicht als werdend, so daß hiermit auch jenes Verschwinden seinen positiven Anfang nur von Außen nimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"158.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0008","text":"Das dritte, der Modus, ist bei Spinoza, Affektion der Substanz, die bestimmte Bestimmtheit, was in einem Andern ist, und durch dieß Andere gefaßt wird. Die Attribute haben eigentlich nur die unbestimmte Verschiedenheit zu ihrer Bestimmung; jedes soll die Totalität der Substanz ausdrücken und aus sich selbst begriffen werden; insofern es aber das Absolute als bestimmt ist, so enthält es das Andersseyn, und ist nicht nur aus sich selbst zu begreifen. In dem Modus ist daher erst eigentlich die Bestimmung des Attributs gesetzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"158.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0009","text":"Dieß Dritte bleibt ferner bloßer Modus, einer Seits ist er unmittelbar Gegebenes, anderer Seits wird seine Nichtigkeit nicht als Reflexion in sich erkannt.—Die spinozistische Auslegung des Absoluten ist daher insofern wohl vollständig, als sie von dem Absoluten anfängt, hierauf das Attribut folgen läßt und mit dem Modus endigt; aber diese drei werden nur nach einander ohne innere Folge der Entwicklung aufgezählt, und das Dritte ist nicht die Negation als Negation, nicht sich negativ auf sich beziehende Negation, wodurch sie an ihr selbst, die Rückkehr in die erste Identität und diese, wahrhafte Identität wäre. Es fehlt daher die Nothwendigkeit des Fortgangs des Absoluten zur Unwesentlichkeit, so wie ihre Auflösung an und für sich selbst in die Identität; oder es mangelt sowohl das Werden der Identität als ihrer Bestimmungen.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"158.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0010","text":"Auf gleiche Weise ist in der orientalischen Vorstellung der Emanation das Absolute das sich selbst erleuchtende Licht. Allein es erleuchtet sich nicht nur, sondern strömt auch aus. Seine Ausströmungen sind Entfernungen von seiner ungetrübten Klarheit; die folgenden Ausgeburten sind unvollkommener als die vorhergehenden, aus denen sie entstehen. Das Ausströmen ist nur als ein Geschehen genommen, das Werden nur als ein fortgehender Verlust. So verdunkelt sich das Seyn immer mehr, und die Nacht, das Negative, ist das Letzte der Linie, das nicht in das erste Licht zurück kehrt.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"158.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0011","text":"Der Mangel der Reflexion in sich, den die Spinozistische Auslegung des Absoluten wie die Emanationslehre an ihr hat, ist in dem Begriffe der leibnizischen Monade ergänzt.—Der Einseitigkeit eines philosophischen Princips pflegt sich die entgegengesetzte gegenüber zu stellen, und, wie in Allem, die Totalität wenigstens als eine zerstreute Vollständigkeit vorhanden zu seyn.—Die Monade ist ein Eins, ein in sich reflektirtes Negatives; sie ist die Totalität des Inhalts der Welt; das verschiedene Mannigfaltige ist in ihr nicht nur verschwunden, sondern auf negative Weise aufbewahrt; die spinozistische Substanz ist die Einheit alles Inhalts; aber dieser mannigfaltige Inhalt der Welt ist nicht als solcher in ihr, sondern in der ihr äußerlichen Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"158.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0012","text":"Die Monade ist daher wesentlich vorstellend; sie hat aber, ob sie wohl eine endliche ist, keine Passivität; sondern die Veränderungen und Bestimmungen in ihr sind Manifestationen ihrer in ihr selbst. Sie ist Entelechie; das Offenbahren ist ihr eigenes Thun.—Dabei ist die Monade auch bestimmt, von anderen unterschieden; die Bestimmtheit fällt in den besondern Inhalt und die Art und Weise der Manifestation. Die Monade ist daher an sich, ihrer Substanz nach, die Totalität, nicht in ihrer Manifestation. Diese Beschränkung der Monade fällt nothwendig nicht in die sich selbst setzende oder vorstellende Monade, sondern in ihr Ansichseyn, oder ist absolute Grenze, eine Prädestination, welche durch ein anderes Wesen, als sie ist, gesetzt wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"158.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0013","text":"Ferner da Begrenzte nur sind, als sich auf andere Begrenzte beziehend, die Monade aber zugleich ein in sich geschlossenes Absolutes ist, so fällt die Harmonie dieser Begrenzungen, nämlich die Beziehung der Monaden auf einander, außer ihnen und ist gleichfalls von einem andern Wesen oder an sich prästabilirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"158.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0014","text":"Es erhellt, daß durch das Princip der Reflexion-in-sich, welches die Grundbestimmung der Monade ausmacht, zwar das Andersseyn und die Einwirkung von außen überhaupt entfernt ist, und die Veränderungen der Monade ihr eigenes Setzen sind,—daß aber auf der andern Seite die Passivität durch Anderes, nur in eine absolute Schranke, in eine Schranke des Ansichseyns verwandelt ist. Leibnitz schreibt den Monaden eine gewisse Vollendung in sich zu, eine Art von Selbstständigkeit; sie sind geschaffene Wesen.—Näher ihre Schranke betrachtet, so ergiebt sich aus dieser Darstellung, daß die Manifestation ihrer selbst, die ihnen zukommt, die Totalität der Form ist. Es ist ein höchst wichtiger Begriffe daß die Veränderungen der Monade als passivitätslose Aktionen, als Manifestationen ihrer selbst vorgestellt, und das Princip der Reflexion in sich, oder der Individuation als wesentlich hervorsteht.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"158.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0015","text":"Ferner ist es nothwendig, die Endlichkeit darin bestehen zu lassen, daß der Inhalt oder die Substanz von der Form unterschieden, und dann weiter jene beschränkt, diese aber unendlich ist. Aber nun wäre im Begriffe der absoluten Monade nicht nur jene absolute Einheit der Form und des Inhalts, sondern auch die Natur der Reflexion, als die sich auf sich selbst beziehende Negativität sich von sich abzustoßen, wodurch sie setzend und schaffend ist, zu finden. Es ist zwar im leibnitzischen Systeme das Weitere gleichfalls vorhanden, daß Gott die Quelle der Existenz und des Wesens der Monaden ist, d. h. daß jene absoluten Schranken im Ansichseyn der Monaden nicht an und für sich seyende sind, sondern im Absoluten verschwinden.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"158.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0016","text":"Aber es zeigen sich in diesen Bestimmungen nur die gewöhnlichen Vorstellungen, die ohne philosophische Entwicklung gelassen und nicht zu spekulativen Begriffen erhoben sind. So erhält das Princip der Individuation seine tiefere Ausführung nicht; die Begriffe über die Unterscheidungen der verschiedenen endlichen Monaden, und über ihr Verhältniß zu ihrem Absoluten, entspringen nicht aus diesem Wesen selbst oder nicht auf absolute Weise, sondern gehören der räsonnirenden, dogmatischen Reflexion an, und sind daher zu keiner innern Kohärenz gediehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"158.16"}],"sha256":"a95f967f970df63084859a409fdc0cdbabc3cca4d53d396c955e7d18bb9b7699","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105845773108Z_bfe5231b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Remark.","source_sha256":"a95f967f970df63084859a409fdc0cdbabc3cca4d53d396c955e7d18bb9b7699","sha256":"d525c2137243bda3e33248090b70d3c1e49207f89d145551a51187c615b2184b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:58:45.773121+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0001","text":"The concept of the Absolute and the relation of reflection to it, as it has presented itself here, corresponds to the concept of Spinozistic substance. Spinozism is an inadequate philosophy in that reflection and its manifold determining are an external thinking.—The substance of this system is One substance, One indivisible totality; there is no determinacy that would not be contained and dissolved in this Absolute; and it is important enough that everything which appears and presents itself to natural representation or to the determining understanding as self-subsistent is in that necessary concept wholly reduced to a mere positedness.—Determinacy is negation, is the absolute principle of Spinozistic philosophy; this true and simple insight grounds the absolute unity of substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"158.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0002","text":"But Spinoza stops at negation as determinacy or quality; he does not proceed to the cognition of it as absolute, that is, self-negating negation; consequently his substance does not itself contain absolute form, and the cognition of it is not immanent cognition. Substance is indeed the absolute unity of thinking and Being or extension; it thus contains thinking itself, but only in its unity with extension; that is, not as separating itself from extension, thus not at all as determining and forming, nor as the movement that returns and begins from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"158.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0003","text":"In part, substance thereby lacks the principle of personality,—a defect which has chiefly provoked opposition to the Spinozistic system;—in part, cognition is external reflection, which does not comprehend and derive from substance that which appears as finite, the determinacy of the attribute and the mode, as also itself in general, but is active as an external understanding, receiving determinations as given and leading them back to the Absolute, but not taking their beginnings from it.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"158.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0004","text":"The concepts which Spinoza gives of substance are the concepts of cause of itself,—that it is that whose essence includes existence within itself;—that the concept of the Absolute does not require the concept of another from which it would have to be formed;—these concepts, however deep and correct they are, are definitions which are immediately assumed at the beginning of the science. Mathematics and other subordinate sciences must begin with something presupposed, which constitutes their element and positive foundation. But the Absolute cannot be a First, an immediate; rather, the Absolute is essentially its result.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"158.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0005","text":"After the definition of the Absolute, Spinoza further introduces the definition of the attribute; and this is determined as that whereby the understanding comprehends its essence. Apart from the fact that the understanding is, by its nature, assumed as later than the attribute,—for Spinoza determines it as a mode,—the attribute, the determinacy as determinacy of the Absolute, is made dependent on an Other, the understanding, which confronts substance externally and immediately.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"158.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0006","text":"Spinoza further determines the attributes as infinite; indeed, infinite also in the sense of an infinite multiplicity. To be sure, only the two occur subsequently,—thinking and extension,—and it is not shown how the infinite multiplicity necessarily reduces itself merely to the opposition, and indeed this determinate one, of thinking and extension.—These two attributes are therefore received empirically. Thinking and Being represent the Absolute in a determination; the Absolute itself is their absolute unity, so that they are only inessential forms, the order of things being the same as that of representations or thoughts, and the One Absolute being considered only by external reflection, a mode, under those two determinations, now as a totality of representations, now as a totality of things and their alterations.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"158.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0007","text":"Just as it is this external reflection which makes that distinction, so too is it that which leads it back and immerses it in absolute identity. But this entire movement takes place outside the Absolute. To be sure, this itself is also thinking, and insofar as this movement is only in the Absolute; but, as remarked, it is in the Absolute only as unity with extension, thus not as this movement, which essentially also is the moment of opposition.—Spinoza makes the sublime demand upon thinking to consider everything under the form of eternity, sub Specie aeterni, that is, as it is in the Absolute. But in that Absolute, which is only immobile identity, the attribute, like the mode, is only as vanishing, not as becoming, so that this vanishing too takes its positive beginning only from outside.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"158.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0008","text":"The third, the mode, is for Spinoza an affection of substance, determinate determinacy, that which is in an Other and is comprehended through this Other. The attributes properly have only indeterminate difference for their determinacy; each is supposed to express the totality of substance and to be comprehended from itself; but insofar as it is the Absolute as determinate, it contains otherness and is not to be comprehended merely from itself. Thus it is only in the mode that the determinacy of the attribute is properly posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"158.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0009","text":"This third further remains a mere mode; on the one hand it is immediately given, on the other hand its nullity is not cognized as reflection into itself.—The Spinozistic exposition of the Absolute is therefore complete to the extent that it begins with the Absolute, then lets the attribute follow, and ends with the mode; but these three are merely enumerated one after another without an inner sequence of development, and the third is not negation as negation, not negation relating negatively to itself, whereby it would be in itself the return into the first identity and this would be true identity. Thus there is lacking the necessity of the progression of the Absolute to inessentiality, as well as its dissolution in and for itself into identity; or there is lacking both the becoming of identity and that of its determinations.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"158.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0010","text":"In the same way, in the Oriental representation of emanation, the Absolute is the light that illuminates itself. Yet it does not merely illuminate itself, but also streams forth. Its emanations are distances from its unclouded brightness; the subsequent offspring are more imperfect than the preceding ones from which they arise. The streaming forth is taken merely as an occurrence, becoming merely as a continuing loss. Thus Being grows ever darker, and night, the negative, is the last point of the line, which does not return into the first light.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"158.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0011","text":"The deficiency of reflection into itself which the Spinozistic exposition of the Absolute, as well as the doctrine of emanation, has in itself, is supplemented in the concept of the Leibnizian monad.—To the one-sidedness of a philosophical principle, the opposite is wont to set itself alongside it, and, as in everything, totality is present at least as a dispersed completeness.—The monad is a One, a negative reflected into itself; it is the totality of the content of the world; the diverse manifold has not merely vanished in it, but is preserved in a negative manner; Spinozistic substance is the unity of all content, but this manifold content of the world is not in it as such, but in reflection external to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"158.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0012","text":"The monad is therefore essentially representational; but although it is finite, it has no passivity; rather, the alterations and determinations in it are manifestations of itself within itself. It is entelechy; manifesting is its own doing.—At the same time, the monad is determined, distinguished from others; determinacy falls into the particular content and the manner of manifestation. The monad is therefore in itself, according to its substance, totality, not in its manifestation. This limitation of the monad necessarily falls not into the self-positing or representational monad, but into its being-in-itself, or is an absolute limit, a predestination which is posited by a being other than it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"158.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0013","text":"Further, since limited things are only as relating to other limited things, while the monad is at the same time an Absolute closed within itself, the harmony of these limitations, namely the relation of the monads to one another, falls outside them and is likewise pre-established by another being, or in itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"158.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0014","text":"It is evident that through the principle of reflection-into-itself, which constitutes the fundamental determination of the monad, otherness and external influence in general are indeed removed, and the alterations of the monad are its own positing,—but that, on the other hand, passivity through another is only transformed into an absolute barrier, into a barrier of being-in-itself. Leibniz ascribes to the monads a certain perfection within themselves, a kind of self-subsistence; they are created beings.—On considering their limit more closely, it follows from this exposition that the manifestation of themselves which belongs to them is the totality of form. It is a most important concept that the alterations of the monad are represented as actions devoid of passivity, as manifestations of themselves, and that the principle of reflection into itself, or of individuation, emerges as essential.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"158.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0015","text":"Further, it is necessary to allow finitude to consist in the content or substance being distinguished from form, and then further in the former being limited, while the latter is infinite. But then in the concept of the absolute monad there would be found not only that absolute unity of form and content, but also the nature of reflection, as self-relating negativity, to repel itself from itself, whereby it is positing and creating. In the Leibnizian system there is indeed likewise the further point that God is the source of the existence and essence of the monads, i.e. that those absolute limits in the being-in-itself of the monads are not beings in and for themselves, but vanish in the Absolute.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"158.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_A_41:P0016","text":"But in these determinations there appear only the ordinary representations, which are left without philosophical development and not raised to speculative concepts. Thus the principle of individuation does not receive its deeper elaboration; the concepts concerning the distinctions among the various finite monads, and concerning their relation to their Absolute, do not arise from this essence itself or in an absolute manner, but belong to reasoning, dogmatic reflection, and have therefore not attained any inner coherence.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"158.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_A_41:P0016"]}],"source_digest":"aec6ae8b3b71acc1e6864cbe7a54fe43336618602f176de3738cf562417eb05d","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"Anmerkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"Anmerkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF","title":"A. Contingency, or Formal Actuality, Possibility, and Necessity.","order":159,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_ZLOF","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Die Wirklichkeit.\n\nDas Absolute ist die Einheit des Innern und Äußern als erste, ansichseyende Einheit. Die Auslegung erschien als äußere Reflexion, die auf ihrer Seite das Unmittelbare als ein Vorgefundenes hat, aber zugleich die Bewegung und Beziehung desselben auf das Absolute ist, und als solche es in dieses zurückführt, und als eine bloße Art und Weise bestimmt. Aber diese Art und Weise ist die Bestimmung des Absoluten selbst, nämlich seine erste Identität oder seine bloß an sich seyende Einheit. Und zwar wird durch diese Reflexion nicht nur jenes erste Ansichseyn gesetzt als wesenlose Bestimmung, sondern weil sie negative Beziehung auf sich ist, wird erst durch sie jener Modus. Diese Reflexion als sich selbst in ihren Bestimmungen aufhebend, und überhaupt als die in sich zurückkehrende Bewegung ist erst wahrhaft absolute Identität, und zugleich ist sie das Bestimmen des Absoluten oder die Modalität desselben. Der Modus ist daher die Äußerlichkeit des Absoluten, aber ebenso sehr nur als dessen Reflexion in sich, —oder er ist die eigne Manifestation desselben, so daß diese Äußerung seine Reflexion-in-sich und damit sein An-und-für-sich-seyn ist.\n\nSo als die Manifestation, daß es sonst nichts ist und keinen Inhalt hat, als die Manifestation seiner zu seyn, ist das Absolute die absolute Form. Die Wirklichkeit ist als diese reflektirte Absolutheit zu nehmen. Das Seyn ist noch nicht wirklich; es ist die er ste Unmittelbarkeit; seine Reflexion ist daher Werden und Übergehen in Anderes; oder seine Unmittelbarkeit ist nicht An-und-für-sich-seyn. Die Wirklichkeit steht auch höher als die Existenz. Diese ist zwar die aus dem Grunde und den Bedingungen, oder aus dem Wesen und dessen Reflexion hervorgegangene Unmittelbarkeit. Sie ist daher an sich das, was die Wirklichkeit ist, reale Reflexion, aber ist noch nicht die gesetzte Einheit der Reflexion und der Unmittelbarkeit. Die Existenz geht daher in Erscheinung über, indem sie die Reflexion, welche sie enthält, entwickelt. Sie ist der zu Grunde gegangene Grund; ihre Bestimmung ist die Wiederherstellung desselben, so wird sie wesentliches Verhältniß, und ihre letzte Reflexion ist, daß ihre Unmittelbarkeit gesetzt ist als die Reflexion-in-sich, und umgekehrt; diese Einheit, in welcher Existenz oder Unmittelbarkeit, und das Ansichseyn, der Grund oder das Reflektirte schlechthin Momente sind, ist nun die Wirklichkeit. Das Wirkliche ist darum Manifestation, es wird durch seine Äußerlichkeit nicht in die Sphäre der Veränderung gezogen, noch ist es Scheinen seiner in einem Andern, sondern es manifestirt sich; das heißt, es ist in seiner Äußerlichkeit es selbst, und ist nur in ihr, nämlich nur als sich von sich unterscheidende und bestimmende Bewegung, es selbst.\n\nIn der Wirklichkeit nun als dieser absoluten Form, sind die Momente nur als aufgehobene oder formelle noch nicht realisirt; ihre Verschiedenheit gehört so zunächst der äußern Reflexion an und ist nicht als Inhalt bestimmt.\n\nDie Wirklichkeit als selbst unmittelbare Formeinheit des Innern und Äußern ist damit in der Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit gegen die Bestimmung der Reflexion in sich; oder sie ist eine Wirklichkeit gegen eine Möglichkeit. Die Beziehung beider auf einander ist das Dritte, das Wirkliche bestimmt ebenso sehr als in sich reflektirtes Seyn, und dieses zugleich als unmittelbar existirendes. Dieses Dritte ist die Nothwendigkeit.\n\nAber zunächst, indem Wirkliches und Mögliches formelle Unterschiede sind, ist ihre Beziehung gleichfalls nur formell, und besteht nur darinn, daß das Eine wie das Andere ein Gesetztseyn ist, oder in der Zufälligkeit.\n\nDamit nun, daß in der Zufälligkeit das Wirkliche wie das Mögliche, das Gesetztseyn ist, haben sie die Bestimmung an ihnen erhalten; es wird dadurch zweitens die reale Wirklichkeit; womit ebenso reale Möglichkeit, und die relative Nothwendigkeit hervorgeht.\n\nDie Reflexion der relativen Nothwendigkeit in sich giebt drittens die absolute Nothwendigkeit, welche absolute Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit ist.\n\n## A. Zufälligkeit oder formelle Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit.\n\n1. Die Wirklichikeit ist formell, insofern sie als erste Wirklichkeit nur unmittelbare, unreflektirte Wirklichkeit, somit nur in dieser Formbestimmung, aber nicht als Totalität der Form ist. Sie ist so weiter nichts als ein Seyn oder Existenz überhaupt. Aber weil sie wesentlich nicht bloße unmittelbare Existenz, sondern, als Formeinheit des Ansichseyns oder der Innerlichkeit, und der Äußerlichkeit ist, so enthält sie unmittelbar das Ansichseyn oder die Möglichkeit. Was wirklich ist, ist möglich.\n\n2. Diese Möglichkeit ist die in sich reflektirte Wirklichkeit. Aber dieß selbst erste Reflektirtseyn ist ebenfalls das Formelle, und hiermit überhaupt nur die Bestimmung der Identität mit sich oder des Ansichseyns überhaupt.\n\nWeil aber die Bestimmung hier Totalität der Form ist, ist dieses Ansichseyn, bestimmt als Aufgehobenes, oder als wesentlich nur in Beziehung auf die Wirklichkeit; als das Negative von dieser, gesetzt als Negatives. Die Möglichkeit enthält daher die zwei Momente; erstlich das positive, daß es ein Reflektirtseyn in sich selbst ist; aber indem es in der absoluten Form herabgesetzt ist zu einem Momente, so gilt das Reflektirtseyn-in-sich nicht mehr als Wesen, sondern hat zweitens die negative Bedeutung, daß die Möglichkeit ein Mangelhaftes ist, auf ein Anderes, die Wirklichkeit, hinweist, und an dieser sich ergänzt.\n\nNach der ersten, der bloß positiven Seite ist die Möglichkeit also die bloße Formbestimmung der Identität mit sich, oder die Form der Wesentlichkeit. So ist sie der verhältnißlose, unbestimmte Behälter für Alles überhaupt.—Im Sinne dieser formellen Möglichkeit ist Alles möglich, was sich nicht widerspricht; das Reich der Möglichkeit ist daher die grenzenlose Mannigfaltigkeit. Aber jedes Mannigfaltige ist in sich und gegen Anderes bestimmt und hat die Negation an ihm; überhaupt geht die gleichgültige Verschiedenheit in die Entgegensetzung über; die Entgegensetzung aber ist der Widerspruch. Daher ist Alles ebenso sehr ein Widersprechendes und daher Unmögliches.\n\n—Dieß bloß formelle von Etwas aussagen,—es ist möglich,—ist daher ebenso flach und leer, als der Satz des Widerspruchs und jeder in ihn aufgenommene Inhalt, A ist möglich, heißt so viel als A ist A. Insofern man sich nicht auf die Entwicklung des Inhalts einläßt, so hat dieser die Form der Einfachheit; erst durch die Auflösung desselben in seine Bestimmungen kommt der Unterschied an ihm hervor. Indem man sich an jene einfache Form hält, so bleibt der Inhalt ein mit sich Identisches und daher ein Mögliches. Es ist aber damit ebenso Nichts gesagt, als mit dem formellen identischen Satze.\n\nDas Mögliche enthält jedoch mehr, als der bloß identische Satz. Das Mögliche ist das reflektirte In-sich-reflektirtseyn; oder das Identische schlechthin als Moment der Totalität, somit auch bestimmt, nicht an sich zu seyn; es hat daher die zweite Bestimmung, nur ein Mögliches zu seyn, und das Sollen der Totalität der Form. Die Möglichkeit ohne dieses Sollen ist die Wesentlichkeit als solche; aber die absolute Form enthält dieß, daß das Wesen selbst nur Moment, und ohne Seyn seine Wahrheit nicht hat. Die Möglichkeit ist diese bloße Wesentlichkeit, so gesetzt, daß sie nur Moment und der absoluten Form nicht gemäß ist. Sie ist das Ansichseyn, bestimmt, als nur ein Gesetztes; oder ebenso sehr als nicht an sich zu seyn. —Die Möglichkeit ist daher an ihr selbst auch der Widerspruch, oder sie ist die Unmöglichkeit.\n\nZunächst drückt sieh dieß so aus, daß die Möglichkeit als aufgehoben gesetzte Formbestimmung, einen Inhalt überhaupt an ihr hat. Dieser ist als möglich ein Ansichseyn, das zugleich ein aufgehobenes oder ein Andersseyn ist. Weil er also nur ein möglicher ist, ist ebenso sehr ein anderer und sein Gegentheil möglich. A ist A; ebenso—A ist—A. Diese beiden Sätze drücken, jeder die Möglichkeit seiner Inhaltsbestimmung aus. Aber als diese identischen Sätze sind sie gleichgültig gegen einander; es ist mit dem einen nicht gesetzt, daß auch der andere hinzukomme. Die Möglichkeit ist die vergleichende Beziehung beider; sie enthält es in ihrer Bestimmung, als eine Reflexion der Totalität, daß auch das Gegentheil möglich sey. Sie ist daher der beziehende Grund, daß darum, weil A=A, auch—A=-A ist; in dem möglichen A ist auch das Mögliche Nicht-A enthalten, und diese Beziehung selbst ist es, welche beide als mögliche bestimmt.\n\nAls diese Beziehung aber, daß in dem einen Möglichen, auch sein Anderes enthalten ist, ist sie der Widerspruch, der sich aufhebt. Da sie nun ihrer Bestimmung nach das Reflektirte, und wie sich gezeigt hat, das sich aufhebende Reflektirte ist, so ist sie somit auch das Unmittelbare, und damit wird sie Wirklichkeit.\n\n3. Diese Wirklichkeit ist nicht die erste, sondern die reflektirte, gesetzt als Einheit ihrer selbst und der Möglichkeit. Das Wirkliche als solches ist möglich; es ist in unmittelbarer positiver Identität mit der Möglichkeit; aber diese hat sich bestimmt als nur Möglichkeit; somit ist auch das Wirkliche bestimmt als nur ein Mögliches. Und unmittelbar, darum weil die Möglichkeit in der Wirklichkeit unmittelbar enthalten ist, ist sie darin als aufgehobene, als nur Möglichkeit.\n\nUmgekehrt die Wirklichkeit, die in Einheit ist mit der Möglichkeit, ist nur die aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit;—oder darum weil die formelle Wirklichkeit nur unmittelbare erste ist, ist sie nur Moment, nur aufgehobene Wirklichkeit, oder nur Möglichkeit.\n\nHiermit ist zugleich näher die Bestimmung ausgedrückt, inwiefern die Möglichkeit Wirklichkeit ist. Die Möglichkeit ist nämlich noch nicht alle Wirklichkeit, von der realen und absoluten Wirklichkeit ist noch nicht die Rede gewesen;—sie ist nur erst diejenige, welche zuerst vorkam, nämlich die formelle, die sich bestimmt hat, nur Möglichkeit zu seyn, also die formelle Wirklichkeit, welche nur Seyn oder Existenz überhaupt ist. Alles Mögliche hat daher überhaupt ein Seyn oder eine Existenz.\n\nDiese Einheit der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit ist die Zufälligkeit. —Das Zufällige ist ein Wirkliches, das zugleich nur als möglich bestimmt, dessen Anderes oder Gegentheil ebenso sehr ist. Diese Wirklichkeit ist daher bloßes Seyn oder Existenz, aber in seiner Wahrheit gesetzt, den Werth eines Gesetztseyns oder der Möglichkeit zu haben. Umgekehrt ist die Möglichkeit als die Reflexion-in-sich oder das Ansichseyn gesetzt als Gesetztseyn; was möglich ist, ist ein Wirkliches in diesem Sinne der Wirklichkeit, es hat nur so viel Werth als die zufällige Wirklichkeit; es ist selbst ein Zufälliges.\n\nDas Zufällige bietet daher die zwei Seiten dar; erstens insofern es die Möglichkeit unmittelbar an ihm hat, oder, was dasselbe ist, insofern sie in ihm aufgehoben ist, ist es nicht Gesetztseyn noch vermittelt, sondern unmittelbare Wirklichkeit; es hat keinen Grund. —Weil auch dem Möglichen diese unmittelbare Wirklichkeit zukommt, so ist es so sehr als das Wirkliche, bestimmt als zufällig, und ebenfalls ein Grundloses.\n\nDas Zufällige ist aber zweitens das Wirkliche als ein nur Mögliches oder als ein Gesetztseyn; so auch das Mögliche ist als formelles An-sich-seyn nur Gesetztseyn. Somit ist Beides nicht an und für sich selbst, sondern hat seine wahrhafte Reflexion-in-sich in einem Andern, oder es hat einen Grund.\n\nDas Zufällige hat also darum keinen Grund, weil es zufällig ist; und ebenso wohl hat es einen Grund, darum weil es zufällig ist.\n\nEs ist das gesetzte, unvermittelte Umschlagen des Innern und Äußern, oder des In-sich-reflektirt-seyns und des Seyns in einander; gesetzt dadurch daß Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit, jede an ihr selbst diese Bestimmung hat, dadurch daß sie Momente der absoluten Form sind.—So ist die Wirklichkeit in ihrer unmittelbaren Einheit mit der Möglichkeit nur die Existenz und bestimmt als Grundloses, das nur ein Gesetztes oder nur Mögliches ist;—oder als reflektirt und bestimmt gegen die Möglichkeit, so ist sie von der Möglichkeit, von dem In-sich-reflektirt-seyn getrennt, und somit ebenso unmittelbar auch nur ein Mögliches.—Ebenso die Möglichkeit, als einfaches Ansichseyn, ist es ein Unmittelbares, nur ein Seyendes überhaupt; oder entgegengesetzt gegen die Wirklichkeit, ebenso ein Wirklichkeitsloses Ansichseyn, nur ein Mögliches, aber eben darum wieder nur eine nicht in sich reflektirte Existenz überhaupt.\n\nDiese absolute Unruhe des Werdens dieser beiden Bestimmungen ist die Zufälligkeit. Aber darum weil jede unmittelbar in die entgegengesetzte umschlägt, so geht sie in dieser ebenso schlechthin mit sich selbst zusammen, und diese Identität derselben einer in der andern ist die Nothwendigkeit.\n\nDas Nothwendige ist ein Wirkliches; so ist es als unmittelbares, Grundloses; es hat aber ebenso sehr seine Wirklichkeit durch ein Anderes oder in seinem Grunde, aber ist zugleich das Gesetztseyn dieses Grundes und die Reflexion desselben in sich; die Möglichkeit des Nothwendigen ist eine aufgehobene. Das Zufällige ist also nothwendig, darum weil das Wirkliche als Mögliches bestimmt, damit seine Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben und in Grund oder Ansichseyn, und in Begründetes abgestoßen ist, als auch weil diese seine Möglichkeit, die Grundbeziehung, schlechthin aufgehoben und als Seyn gesetzt ist. Das Nothwendige ist, und dieß Seyende ist selbst das Nothwendige. Zugleich ist es an sich; diese Reflexion-in-sich ist ein Anderes als jene Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns; und die Nothwendigkeit des Seyenden ist ein Anderes. Das Seyende selbst ist so nicht das Nothwendige; aber dieses Ansichseyn ist selbst nur Gesetztseyn, es ist aufgehoben und selbst unmittelbar. So ist die Wirklichkeit in ihrem unterschiedenen, der Möglichkeit, identisch mit sich selbst. Als diese Identität ist sie Nothwendigkeit.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0001","text":"## Zweites Kapitel. Die Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"159.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0002","text":"Das Absolute ist die Einheit des Innern und Äußern als erste, ansichseyende Einheit. Die Auslegung erschien als äußere Reflexion, die auf ihrer Seite das Unmittelbare als ein Vorgefundenes hat, aber zugleich die Bewegung und Beziehung desselben auf das Absolute ist, und als solche es in dieses zurückführt, und als eine bloße Art und Weise bestimmt. Aber diese Art und Weise ist die Bestimmung des Absoluten selbst, nämlich seine erste Identität oder seine bloß an sich seyende Einheit. Und zwar wird durch diese Reflexion nicht nur jenes erste Ansichseyn gesetzt als wesenlose Bestimmung, sondern weil sie negative Beziehung auf sich ist, wird erst durch sie jener Modus.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"159.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0003","text":"Diese Reflexion als sich selbst in ihren Bestimmungen aufhebend, und überhaupt als die in sich zurückkehrende Bewegung ist erst wahrhaft absolute Identität, und zugleich ist sie das Bestimmen des Absoluten oder die Modalität desselben. Der Modus ist daher die Äußerlichkeit des Absoluten, aber ebenso sehr nur als dessen Reflexion in sich, —oder er ist die eigne Manifestation desselben, so daß diese Äußerung seine Reflexion-in-sich und damit sein An-und-für-sich-seyn ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"159.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0004","text":"So als die Manifestation, daß es sonst nichts ist und keinen Inhalt hat, als die Manifestation seiner zu seyn, ist das Absolute die absolute Form. Die Wirklichkeit ist als diese reflektirte Absolutheit zu nehmen. Das Seyn ist noch nicht wirklich; es ist die er ste Unmittelbarkeit; seine Reflexion ist daher Werden und Übergehen in Anderes; oder seine Unmittelbarkeit ist nicht An-und-für-sich-seyn. Die Wirklichkeit steht auch höher als die Existenz. Diese ist zwar die aus dem Grunde und den Bedingungen, oder aus dem Wesen und dessen Reflexion hervorgegangene Unmittelbarkeit. Sie ist daher an sich das, was die Wirklichkeit ist, reale Reflexion, aber ist noch nicht die gesetzte Einheit der Reflexion und der Unmittelbarkeit. Die Existenz geht daher in Erscheinung über, indem sie die Reflexion, welche sie enthält, entwickelt.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"159.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0005","text":"Sie ist der zu Grunde gegangene Grund; ihre Bestimmung ist die Wiederherstellung desselben, so wird sie wesentliches Verhältniß, und ihre letzte Reflexion ist, daß ihre Unmittelbarkeit gesetzt ist als die Reflexion-in-sich, und umgekehrt; diese Einheit, in welcher Existenz oder Unmittelbarkeit, und das Ansichseyn, der Grund oder das Reflektirte schlechthin Momente sind, ist nun die Wirklichkeit. Das Wirkliche ist darum Manifestation, es wird durch seine Äußerlichkeit nicht in die Sphäre der Veränderung gezogen, noch ist es Scheinen seiner in einem Andern, sondern es manifestirt sich; das heißt, es ist in seiner Äußerlichkeit es selbst, und ist nur in ihr, nämlich nur als sich von sich unterscheidende und bestimmende Bewegung, es selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"159.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0006","text":"In der Wirklichkeit nun als dieser absoluten Form, sind die Momente nur als aufgehobene oder formelle noch nicht realisirt; ihre Verschiedenheit gehört so zunächst der äußern Reflexion an und ist nicht als Inhalt bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"159.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0007","text":"Die Wirklichkeit als selbst unmittelbare Formeinheit des Innern und Äußern ist damit in der Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit gegen die Bestimmung der Reflexion in sich; oder sie ist eine Wirklichkeit gegen eine Möglichkeit. Die Beziehung beider auf einander ist das Dritte, das Wirkliche bestimmt ebenso sehr als in sich reflektirtes Seyn, und dieses zugleich als unmittelbar existirendes. Dieses Dritte ist die Nothwendigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"159.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0008","text":"Aber zunächst, indem Wirkliches und Mögliches formelle Unterschiede sind, ist ihre Beziehung gleichfalls nur formell, und besteht nur darinn, daß das Eine wie das Andere ein Gesetztseyn ist, oder in der Zufälligkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"159.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0009","text":"Damit nun, daß in der Zufälligkeit das Wirkliche wie das Mögliche, das Gesetztseyn ist, haben sie die Bestimmung an ihnen erhalten; es wird dadurch zweitens die reale Wirklichkeit; womit ebenso reale Möglichkeit, und die relative Nothwendigkeit hervorgeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"159.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0010","text":"Die Reflexion der relativen Nothwendigkeit in sich giebt drittens die absolute Nothwendigkeit, welche absolute Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"159.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0011","text":"## A. Zufälligkeit oder formelle Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"159.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0012","text":"1. Die Wirklichikeit ist formell, insofern sie als erste Wirklichkeit nur unmittelbare, unreflektirte Wirklichkeit, somit nur in dieser Formbestimmung, aber nicht als Totalität der Form ist. Sie ist so weiter nichts als ein Seyn oder Existenz überhaupt. Aber weil sie wesentlich nicht bloße unmittelbare Existenz, sondern, als Formeinheit des Ansichseyns oder der Innerlichkeit, und der Äußerlichkeit ist, so enthält sie unmittelbar das Ansichseyn oder die Möglichkeit. Was wirklich ist, ist möglich.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"159.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0013","text":"2. Diese Möglichkeit ist die in sich reflektirte Wirklichkeit. Aber dieß selbst erste Reflektirtseyn ist ebenfalls das Formelle, und hiermit überhaupt nur die Bestimmung der Identität mit sich oder des Ansichseyns überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"159.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0014","text":"Weil aber die Bestimmung hier Totalität der Form ist, ist dieses Ansichseyn, bestimmt als Aufgehobenes, oder als wesentlich nur in Beziehung auf die Wirklichkeit; als das Negative von dieser, gesetzt als Negatives. Die Möglichkeit enthält daher die zwei Momente; erstlich das positive, daß es ein Reflektirtseyn in sich selbst ist; aber indem es in der absoluten Form herabgesetzt ist zu einem Momente, so gilt das Reflektirtseyn-in-sich nicht mehr als Wesen, sondern hat zweitens die negative Bedeutung, daß die Möglichkeit ein Mangelhaftes ist, auf ein Anderes, die Wirklichkeit, hinweist, und an dieser sich ergänzt.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"159.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0015","text":"Nach der ersten, der bloß positiven Seite ist die Möglichkeit also die bloße Formbestimmung der Identität mit sich, oder die Form der Wesentlichkeit. So ist sie der verhältnißlose, unbestimmte Behälter für Alles überhaupt.—Im Sinne dieser formellen Möglichkeit ist Alles möglich, was sich nicht widerspricht; das Reich der Möglichkeit ist daher die grenzenlose Mannigfaltigkeit. Aber jedes Mannigfaltige ist in sich und gegen Anderes bestimmt und hat die Negation an ihm; überhaupt geht die gleichgültige Verschiedenheit in die Entgegensetzung über; die Entgegensetzung aber ist der Widerspruch. Daher ist Alles ebenso sehr ein Widersprechendes und daher Unmögliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"159.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0016","text":"—Dieß bloß formelle von Etwas aussagen,—es ist möglich,—ist daher ebenso flach und leer, als der Satz des Widerspruchs und jeder in ihn aufgenommene Inhalt, A ist möglich, heißt so viel als A ist A. Insofern man sich nicht auf die Entwicklung des Inhalts einläßt, so hat dieser die Form der Einfachheit; erst durch die Auflösung desselben in seine Bestimmungen kommt der Unterschied an ihm hervor. Indem man sich an jene einfache Form hält, so bleibt der Inhalt ein mit sich Identisches und daher ein Mögliches. Es ist aber damit ebenso Nichts gesagt, als mit dem formellen identischen Satze.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"159.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0017","text":"Das Mögliche enthält jedoch mehr, als der bloß identische Satz. Das Mögliche ist das reflektirte In-sich-reflektirtseyn; oder das Identische schlechthin als Moment der Totalität, somit auch bestimmt, nicht an sich zu seyn; es hat daher die zweite Bestimmung, nur ein Mögliches zu seyn, und das Sollen der Totalität der Form. Die Möglichkeit ohne dieses Sollen ist die Wesentlichkeit als solche; aber die absolute Form enthält dieß, daß das Wesen selbst nur Moment, und ohne Seyn seine Wahrheit nicht hat. Die Möglichkeit ist diese bloße Wesentlichkeit, so gesetzt, daß sie nur Moment und der absoluten Form nicht gemäß ist. Sie ist das Ansichseyn, bestimmt, als nur ein Gesetztes; oder ebenso sehr als nicht an sich zu seyn. —Die Möglichkeit ist daher an ihr selbst auch der Widerspruch, oder sie ist die Unmöglichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"159.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0018","text":"Zunächst drückt sieh dieß so aus, daß die Möglichkeit als aufgehoben gesetzte Formbestimmung, einen Inhalt überhaupt an ihr hat. Dieser ist als möglich ein Ansichseyn, das zugleich ein aufgehobenes oder ein Andersseyn ist. Weil er also nur ein möglicher ist, ist ebenso sehr ein anderer und sein Gegentheil möglich. A ist A; ebenso—A ist—A. Diese beiden Sätze drücken, jeder die Möglichkeit seiner Inhaltsbestimmung aus. Aber als diese identischen Sätze sind sie gleichgültig gegen einander; es ist mit dem einen nicht gesetzt, daß auch der andere hinzukomme. Die Möglichkeit ist die vergleichende Beziehung beider; sie enthält es in ihrer Bestimmung, als eine Reflexion der Totalität, daß auch das Gegentheil möglich sey.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"159.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0019","text":"Sie ist daher der beziehende Grund, daß darum, weil A=A, auch—A=-A ist; in dem möglichen A ist auch das Mögliche Nicht-A enthalten, und diese Beziehung selbst ist es, welche beide als mögliche bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"159.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0020","text":"Als diese Beziehung aber, daß in dem einen Möglichen, auch sein Anderes enthalten ist, ist sie der Widerspruch, der sich aufhebt. Da sie nun ihrer Bestimmung nach das Reflektirte, und wie sich gezeigt hat, das sich aufhebende Reflektirte ist, so ist sie somit auch das Unmittelbare, und damit wird sie Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"159.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0021","text":"3. Diese Wirklichkeit ist nicht die erste, sondern die reflektirte, gesetzt als Einheit ihrer selbst und der Möglichkeit. Das Wirkliche als solches ist möglich; es ist in unmittelbarer positiver Identität mit der Möglichkeit; aber diese hat sich bestimmt als nur Möglichkeit; somit ist auch das Wirkliche bestimmt als nur ein Mögliches. Und unmittelbar, darum weil die Möglichkeit in der Wirklichkeit unmittelbar enthalten ist, ist sie darin als aufgehobene, als nur Möglichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"159.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0022","text":"Umgekehrt die Wirklichkeit, die in Einheit ist mit der Möglichkeit, ist nur die aufgehobene Unmittelbarkeit;—oder darum weil die formelle Wirklichkeit nur unmittelbare erste ist, ist sie nur Moment, nur aufgehobene Wirklichkeit, oder nur Möglichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"159.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0023","text":"Hiermit ist zugleich näher die Bestimmung ausgedrückt, inwiefern die Möglichkeit Wirklichkeit ist. Die Möglichkeit ist nämlich noch nicht alle Wirklichkeit, von der realen und absoluten Wirklichkeit ist noch nicht die Rede gewesen;—sie ist nur erst diejenige, welche zuerst vorkam, nämlich die formelle, die sich bestimmt hat, nur Möglichkeit zu seyn, also die formelle Wirklichkeit, welche nur Seyn oder Existenz überhaupt ist. Alles Mögliche hat daher überhaupt ein Seyn oder eine Existenz.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"159.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0024","text":"Diese Einheit der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit ist die Zufälligkeit. —Das Zufällige ist ein Wirkliches, das zugleich nur als möglich bestimmt, dessen Anderes oder Gegentheil ebenso sehr ist. Diese Wirklichkeit ist daher bloßes Seyn oder Existenz, aber in seiner Wahrheit gesetzt, den Werth eines Gesetztseyns oder der Möglichkeit zu haben. Umgekehrt ist die Möglichkeit als die Reflexion-in-sich oder das Ansichseyn gesetzt als Gesetztseyn; was möglich ist, ist ein Wirkliches in diesem Sinne der Wirklichkeit, es hat nur so viel Werth als die zufällige Wirklichkeit; es ist selbst ein Zufälliges.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"159.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0025","text":"Das Zufällige bietet daher die zwei Seiten dar; erstens insofern es die Möglichkeit unmittelbar an ihm hat, oder, was dasselbe ist, insofern sie in ihm aufgehoben ist, ist es nicht Gesetztseyn noch vermittelt, sondern unmittelbare Wirklichkeit; es hat keinen Grund. —Weil auch dem Möglichen diese unmittelbare Wirklichkeit zukommt, so ist es so sehr als das Wirkliche, bestimmt als zufällig, und ebenfalls ein Grundloses.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"159.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0026","text":"Das Zufällige ist aber zweitens das Wirkliche als ein nur Mögliches oder als ein Gesetztseyn; so auch das Mögliche ist als formelles An-sich-seyn nur Gesetztseyn. Somit ist Beides nicht an und für sich selbst, sondern hat seine wahrhafte Reflexion-in-sich in einem Andern, oder es hat einen Grund.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"159.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0027","text":"Das Zufällige hat also darum keinen Grund, weil es zufällig ist; und ebenso wohl hat es einen Grund, darum weil es zufällig ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"159.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0028","text":"Es ist das gesetzte, unvermittelte Umschlagen des Innern und Äußern, oder des In-sich-reflektirt-seyns und des Seyns in einander; gesetzt dadurch daß Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit, jede an ihr selbst diese Bestimmung hat, dadurch daß sie Momente der absoluten Form sind.—So ist die Wirklichkeit in ihrer unmittelbaren Einheit mit der Möglichkeit nur die Existenz und bestimmt als Grundloses, das nur ein Gesetztes oder nur Mögliches ist;—oder als reflektirt und bestimmt gegen die Möglichkeit, so ist sie von der Möglichkeit, von dem In-sich-reflektirt-seyn getrennt, und somit ebenso unmittelbar auch nur ein Mögliches.—Ebenso die Möglichkeit, als einfaches Ansichseyn, ist es ein Unmittelbares, nur ein Seyendes überhaupt; oder entgegengesetzt gegen die Wirklichkeit, ebenso ein Wirklichkeitsloses Ansichseyn, nur ein Mögliches, aber eben darum wieder nur eine nicht in sich reflektirte Existenz","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"159.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0029","text":"überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"159.29"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0030","text":"Diese absolute Unruhe des Werdens dieser beiden Bestimmungen ist die Zufälligkeit. Aber darum weil jede unmittelbar in die entgegengesetzte umschlägt, so geht sie in dieser ebenso schlechthin mit sich selbst zusammen, und diese Identität derselben einer in der andern ist die Nothwendigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"159.30"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0031","text":"Das Nothwendige ist ein Wirkliches; so ist es als unmittelbares, Grundloses; es hat aber ebenso sehr seine Wirklichkeit durch ein Anderes oder in seinem Grunde, aber ist zugleich das Gesetztseyn dieses Grundes und die Reflexion desselben in sich; die Möglichkeit des Nothwendigen ist eine aufgehobene. Das Zufällige ist also nothwendig, darum weil das Wirkliche als Mögliches bestimmt, damit seine Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben und in Grund oder Ansichseyn, und in Begründetes abgestoßen ist, als auch weil diese seine Möglichkeit, die Grundbeziehung, schlechthin aufgehoben und als Seyn gesetzt ist. Das Nothwendige ist, und dieß Seyende ist selbst das Nothwendige. Zugleich ist es an sich; diese Reflexion-in-sich ist ein Anderes als jene Unmittelbarkeit des Seyns; und die Nothwendigkeit des Seyenden ist ein Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"159.31"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0032","text":"Das Seyende selbst ist so nicht das Nothwendige; aber dieses Ansichseyn ist selbst nur Gesetztseyn, es ist aufgehoben und selbst unmittelbar. So ist die Wirklichkeit in ihrem unterschiedenen, der Möglichkeit, identisch mit sich selbst. Als diese Identität ist sie Nothwendigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"159.32"}],"sha256":"2f11950652e77eb1c132b2c11e8347c752e65c0eecce4a7ac3ebbb756258cdc4","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105928907253Z_572cc7d4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Contingency, or Formal Actuality, Possibility, and Necessity.","source_sha256":"2f11950652e77eb1c132b2c11e8347c752e65c0eecce4a7ac3ebbb756258cdc4","sha256":"d9fd7b298885a1921d928f0686ba5c69324965620f77e8c7a1d323aa19805d08","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:59:28.907266+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0001","text":"## Second Chapter. Actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"159.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0002","text":"The Absolute is the unity of inner and outer as the first, being-in-itself unity. Explication appeared as external reflection, which has, on its side, the immediate as something found, but is at the same time the movement and relation of the same to the Absolute, and as such leads it back into the latter, and determines it as a mere mode. But this mode is the determination of the Absolute itself, namely, its first identity or its merely being-in-itself unity. Indeed, by this reflection not only is that first being-in-itself posited as an inessential determination, but, because it is negative relation to itself, that mode first comes to be through it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"159.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0003","text":"This reflection, as sublating itself in its determinations, and in general as the movement returning into itself, is only truly absolute identity; and at the same time it is the determining of the Absolute, or its modality. The mode is therefore the externality of the Absolute, but equally only as its reflection into itself—or it is its own manifestation, so that this expression is its reflection-into-itself and thus its being-in-and-for-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"159.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0004","text":"Thus, as the manifestation that it is otherwise nothing and has no content except that of being the manifestation of itself, the Absolute is absolute form. Actuality is to be taken as this reflected absoluteness. Being is not yet actual; it is the first immediacy; its reflection is therefore becoming and transition into something other; or its immediacy is not being-in-and-for-itself. Actuality also stands higher than existence. Existence is indeed the immediacy that has issued from ground and conditions, or from essence and its reflection. Hence it is in itself what actuality is, real reflection, but it is not yet the posited unity of reflection and immediacy. Existence therefore passes over into appearance, in that it develops the reflection which it contains.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"159.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0005","text":"It is the ground that has gone to ground; its determination is the restoration of the latter; thus it becomes essential relation, and its final reflection is that its immediacy is posited as reflection-into-itself, and conversely; this unity, in which existence or immediacy, and being-in-itself, ground or the reflected, are absolutely moments, is now actuality. The actual is therefore manifestation; through its externality it is not drawn into the sphere of alteration, nor is it a shining of itself in an other, but it manifests itself; that is, in its externality it is itself, and is only in it, namely, only as movement distinguishing and determining itself from itself, itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"159.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0006","text":"Now in actuality as this absolute form, the moments are only as sublated or formal, not yet realized; their difference thus initially belongs to external reflection and is not determined as content.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"159.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0007","text":"Actuality, as itself the immediate unity of form of inner and outer, is thereby in the determination of immediacy as against the determination of reflection into itself; or it is an actuality over against a possibility. The relation of the two to one another is the third, which determines the actual equally as being reflected into itself, and this at the same time as immediately existing. This third is necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"159.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0008","text":"But initially, since actual and possible are formal differences, their relation likewise is only formal, and consists only in this, that the one as well as the other is a positedness, or in contingency.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"159.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0009","text":"Now in that, in contingency, the actual as well as the possible is positedness, they have received determination within themselves; thereby, secondly, real actuality comes to be, along with which real possibility and relative necessity likewise issue forth.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"159.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0010","text":"The reflection of relative necessity into itself gives, thirdly, absolute necessity, which is absolute possibility and actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"159.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0011","text":"## A. Contingency, or formal actuality, possibility, and necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"159.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0012","text":"1. Actuality is formal insofar as, as first actuality, it is only immediate, unreflected actuality, hence only in this determination of form, but not as totality of form. Thus it is nothing further than a being or existence in general. But because it is essentially not mere immediate existence, but, as unity of form of being-in-itself or inwardness and externality, it immediately contains being-in-itself or possibility. What is actual is possible.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"159.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0013","text":"2. This possibility is actuality reflected into itself. But this first reflectedness itself is likewise the formal, and hence in general only the determination of identity with itself or of being-in-itself in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"159.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0014","text":"But because determination here is totality of form, this being-in-itself is determined as sublated, or as essentially only in relation to actuality; as the negative of the latter, posited as negative. Possibility therefore contains the two moments: first, the positive, that it is a reflectedness into itself; but since in absolute form it is reduced to a moment, reflectedness-into-itself no longer counts as essence, but has, secondly, the negative meaning that possibility is something defective, points to an other, actuality, and completes itself in the latter.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"159.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0015","text":"According to the first, merely positive side, possibility is thus the mere determination of form of identity with itself, or the form of essentiality. Thus it is the relationless, indeterminate receptacle for everything in general.—In the sense of this formal possibility, everything is possible that does not contradict itself; the realm of possibility is therefore the boundless multiplicity. But every manifold is determined in itself and over against others and has negation in it; in general, indifferent difference passes over into opposition; but opposition is contradiction. Hence everything is equally a self-contradictory and therefore impossible.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"159.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0016","text":"—To predicate this merely formal thing of something—\"it is possible\"—is therefore as shallow and empty as the proposition of contradiction and every content taken up into it; A is possible means as much as A is A. Insofar as one does not enter into the development of the content, it has the form of simplicity; only through its dissolution into its determinations does difference emerge in it. In holding to that simple form, the content remains something identical with itself and hence something possible. But thereby nothing more is said than by the formal identical proposition.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"159.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0017","text":"The possible, however, contains more than the merely identical proposition. The possible is reflected being-reflected-into-itself; or the identical absolutely as a moment of totality, thus also determined not to be in itself; it therefore has the second determination of being only a possible, and the ought of the totality of form. Possibility without this ought is essentiality as such; but absolute form contains this, that essence itself is only a moment and without being does not have its truth. Possibility is this mere essentiality, so posited that it is only a moment and not adequate to absolute form. It is being-in-itself, determined as only a posited; or equally as not being in itself. —Possibility is therefore in itself also contradiction, or it is impossibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"159.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0018","text":"Initially this expresses itself thus: that possibility, as a determination of form posited as sublated, has a content in general in it. As possible, this content is a being-in-itself which is at the same time a sublated being or an other-being. Since it is therefore only a possible, an other and its opposite are equally possible. A is A; equally—A is—A. These two propositions each express the possibility of its determination of content. But as these identical propositions, they are indifferent to one another; by the one it is not posited that the other also be added. Possibility is the comparative relation of both; it contains in its determination, as a reflection of totality, that the opposite too is possible.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"159.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0019","text":"It is therefore the relating ground that, because A=A, also—A=-A is; in the possible A, possible non-A is also contained, and this relation itself is what determines both as possible.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"159.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0020","text":"But as this relation, that in the one possible its other is also contained, it is the contradiction that sublates itself. Since now, according to its determination, it is the reflected, and, as has been shown, the self-sublating reflected, it is thus also the immediate, and thereby it becomes actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"159.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0021","text":"3. This actuality is not the first, but the reflected, posited as unity of itself and possibility. The actual as such is possible; it is in immediate positive identity with possibility; but this has determined itself as only possibility; thus the actual too is determined as only a possible. And immediately, because possibility is immediately contained in actuality, it is therein as sublated, as only possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"159.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0022","text":"Conversely, actuality, which is in unity with possibility, is only sublated immediacy;—or because formal actuality is only immediate first actuality, it is only a moment, only sublated actuality, or only possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"159.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0023","text":"Therewith the determination is at the same time expressed more precisely as to the extent in which possibility is actuality. For possibility is not yet all actuality; real and absolute actuality have not yet been spoken of;—it is only that which first occurred, namely formal actuality, which has determined itself to be only possibility, thus formal actuality, which is only being or existence in general. Everything possible therefore has in general a being or an existence.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"159.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0024","text":"This unity of possibility and actuality is contingency. —The contingent is an actual which is at the same time determined only as possible, whose other or opposite equally is. This actuality is therefore mere being or existence, but posited in its truth, as having the value of a positedness or of possibility. Conversely, possibility as reflection-into-itself or being-in-itself is posited as positedness; what is possible is an actual in this sense of actuality; it has only as much value as contingent actuality; it is itself a contingent.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"159.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0025","text":"The contingent therefore presents the two sides; first, insofar as it has possibility immediately within it, or, what is the same, insofar as possibility is sublated in it, it is not positedness nor mediated, but immediate actuality; it has no ground. —Since this immediate actuality also pertains to the possible, it is, just as much as the actual, determined as contingent, and likewise groundless.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"159.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0026","text":"But secondly, the contingent is the actual as a merely possible [thing], or as a positedness; and likewise the possible, as formal being-in-itself, is only positedness. Thus neither is in and for itself, but has its true reflection-into-itself in an other, or it has a ground.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"159.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0027","text":"The contingent therefore has no ground because it is contingent; and equally well it has a ground because it is contingent.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"159.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0028","text":"It is the posited, unmediated transition of the inner and the outer, or of reflectedness-into-itself and Being, into one another; posited by the fact that possibility and actuality, each in itself, has this determination, by the fact that they are moments of the absolute form.—Thus actuality, in its immediate unity with possibility, is only existence and determined as groundless, which is only a posited [thing] or only possible;—or, as reflected and determined over against possibility, it is separated from possibility, from reflectedness-into-itself, and thus likewise immediately only a possible [thing].—Likewise possibility, as simple being-in-itself, is an immediate [thing], only a being in general; or, opposed to actuality, likewise a being-in-itself devoid of actuality, only a possible [thing], but precisely thereby again only an existence not reflected into itself","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"159.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0029","text":"in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"159.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0030","text":"This absolute unrest of the becoming of these two determinations is contingency. But because each immediately passes over into the opposite, it thereby equally absolutely coincides with itself in the latter, and this identity of the two, of one in the other, is necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"159.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0031","text":"The necessary is an actual; thus it is, as immediate, groundless; but it equally has its actuality through an other or in its ground, yet is at the same time the positedness of this ground and its reflection into itself; the possibility of the necessary is a sublated one. The contingent is therefore necessary because the actual is determined as possible, whereby its immediacy is sublated and repelled into ground or being-in-itself, and into what is grounded, as also because this its possibility, the relation of ground, is absolutely sublated and posited as Being. The necessary is, and this being is itself the necessary. At the same time, it is in itself; this reflection-into-itself is an other than that immediacy of Being; and the necessity of the being is an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"159.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0032","text":"Thus the being itself is not the necessary; but this being-in-itself is itself only positedness, it is sublated and itself immediate. Thus actuality, in its distinct [moment], possibility, is identical with itself. As this identity, it is necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"159.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_ZLOF:P0032"]}],"source_digest":"7dc8f0889d91331ecd5cafb9bbc3ad50a5a7dfc956e3a2a3f008a5ac7a0f04ce","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Zufälligkeit oder formelle Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Zufälligkeit oder formelle Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO","title":"B. Relative Necessity or Actuality, Possibility, and Necessity.","order":160,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BRNO","text":"1. Die Nothwendigkeit, die sich ergeben hat, ist formell, weil ihre Momente formell sind, nämlich einfache Bestimmungen, die nur als unmittelbare Einheit, oder als unmittelbares Umschlagen des Einen in das Andere Totalität sind, und somit nicht die Gestalt der Selbstständigkeit haben.—In dieser formellen Nothwendigkeit ist daher die Einheit zunächst einfach und gegen ihre Unterschiede gleichgültig. Als unmittelbare Einheit der Formbestimmungen, ist diese Nothwendigkeit Wirklichkeit; aber eine solche, die, weil ihre Einheit nunmehr bestimmt ist als gleichgültig gegen den Unterschied der Formbestimmungen, nämlich ihrer selbst und der Möglichkeit, einen Inhalt hat. Dieser als gleichgültige Identität enthält auch die Form als gleichgültige, d. h. als bloß verschiedene Bestimmungen, und ist mannigfaltiger Inhalt überhaupt. Diese Wirklichkeit ist reale Wirklichkeit.\n\nDie reale Wirklichkeit als solche ist zunächst das Ding von vielen Eigenschaften, die existirende Welt; aber sie ist nicht die Existenz, welche sich in Erscheinung auflöst, sondern als Wirklichkeit ist sie zugleich Ansichseyn und Reflexion-in-sich; sie erhält sich in der Mannigfaltigkeit der bloßen Existenz; ihre Äußerlichkeit ist innerliches Verhalten nur zu sich selbst. Was wirklich ist, kann wirken; seine Wirklichkeit giebt Etwas kund durch das, was es hervorbringt. Sein Verhalten zu Anderem ist die Manifestation seiner, weder ein Übergehen, so bezieht das seyende Etwas sich auf Anderes; —noch ein Erscheinen, so ist das Ding nur im Verhältniß zu andern, ist ein Selbstständiges, das aber seine Reflexion-in-sich, seine bestimmte Wesentlichkeit, in einem andern Selbstständigen hat.\n\nDie reale Wirklichkeit hat nun gleichfalls die Möglichkeit unmittelbar an ihr selbst. Sie enthält das Moment des Ansichseyns; aber als nur erst die unmittelbare Einheit ist sie in einer der Bestimmungen der Fonn, hiermit als das Seyende von dem Ansichseyn oder der Möglichkeit unterschieden.\n\n2. Diese Möglichkeit als das Ansichseyn der realen Wirklichkeit ist selbst reale Möglichkeit, zunächst das inhaltsvolle Ansichseyn.—Die formelle Möglichkeit ist die Reflexion-in-sich nur als die abstrakte Identität, daß Etwas sich in sich nicht widerspreche. Insofern man sich aber auf die Bestimmungen, Umstände, Bedingungen einer Sache einläßt, um daraus ihre Möglichkeit zu erkennen, bleibt man nicht mehr bei der formellen stehen, sondern betrachtet ihre reale Möglichkeit.\n\nDiese reale Möglichkeit ist selbst unmittelbare Existenz, nicht mehr aber darum, weil die Möglichkeit als solche, als formelles Moment, unmittelbar ihr Gegentheil, eine nicht reflektirte Wirklichkeit ist; sondern weil sie reale Möglichkeit ist, hat sie sogleich diese Bestimmung an ihr selbst. Die reale Möglichkeit einer Sache ist daher die daseyende Mannigfaltigkeit von Umständen, die sich auf sie beziehen.\n\nDiese Mannigfaltigkeit des Daseyns ist also zwar sowohl Möglichkeit als Wirklichkeit, aber ihre Identität ist nur erst der Inhalt, der gegen diese Formbestimmungen gleichgültig ist; sie machen daher die Form aus bestimmt gegen ihre Identität.—Oder die unmittelbare reale Wirklichkeit, darum weil sie unmittelbare ist, ist gegen ihre Möglichkeit bestimmt; als diese bestimmte, somit reflektirte ist sie die reale Möglichkeit. Diese ist nun zwar das gesetzte Ganze der Form, aber der Form in ihrer Bestimmtheit, nämlich der Wirklichkeit als formeller oder unmittelbarer, und ebenso der Möglichkeit, als des abstrakten Ansichseyns. Diese Wirklichkeit, welche die Möglichkeit einer Sache ausmacht, ist daher nicht ihre eigene Möglichkeit, sondern das Ansichseyn eines andern Wirklichen; sie selbst ist die Wirklichkeit, die aufgehoben werden soll, die Möglichkeit als nur Möglichkeit.—So macht die reale Möglichkeit das Ganze von Bedingungen aus, eine nicht in sich reflektirte, zerstreute Wirklichkeit, welche aber bestimmt ist, das Ansichseyn aber eines Andern zu seyn und in sich zurückgehen zu sollen.\n\nWas real möglich ist, ist also nach seinem Ansichseyn, ein formelles Identisches, das nach seiner einfachen Inhaltsbestimmung sich nicht widerspricht; aber auch nach seinen entwickelten und unterschiedenen Umständen und allem, womit es im Zusammenhange steht, muß es als das mit sich Identische sich nicht widersprechen. Aber zweitens weil es in sich mannigfaltig und mit Anderem in mannigfaltigem Zusammenhange ist, die Verschiedenheit aber an sich selbst in Entgegensetzung übergeht, ist es ein Widersprechendes. Wenn von einer Möglichkeit die Rede ist und deren Widerspruch aufgezeigt werden soll, so hat man sich nur an die Mannigfaltigkeit, die sie als Inhalt oder als ihre bedingende Existenz enthält, zu halten; woraus sich leicht ihr Widerspruch auffinden läßt.—Dieß ist aber nicht ein Widerspruch der Vergleichung, sondern die mannigfaltige Existenz ist an sich selbst dieß, sich aufzuheben und zu Grunde zu gehen; und hat darin wesentlich die Bestimmung, nur ein Mögliches zu seyn, an ihr selbst. —Wenn alle Bedingungen einer Sache vollständig vorhanden sind, so tritt sie in Wirklichkeit;—die Vollständigkeit der Bedingungen ist die Totalität als am Inhalte, und die Sache selbst ist dieser Inhalt bestimmt ebenso ein Wirkliches als Mögliches zu seyn. In der Sphäre des bedingten Grundes haben die Bedingungen die Form, nämlich den Grund oder die für sich seyende Reflexion, außer ihnen, welche sie zu Momenten der Sache bezieht und die Existenz an ihnen hervorbringt. Hier hingegen ist die unmittelbare Wirklichkeit nicht durch eine voraussetzende Reflexion bestimmt, Bedingung zu seyn, sondern es ist gesetzt, daß sie selbst die Möglichkeit ist.\n\nIn der sich aufhebenden realen Möglichkeit ist es nun ein Gedoppeltes, das aufgehoben wird; denn sie ist selbst das Gedoppelte, Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit zu seyn. 1) Die Wirklichkeit ist die formelle, oder eine Existenz, die als selbstständige unmittelbare erschien, und durch ihr Aufheben zum reflektirten Seyn, zum Moment eines Andern wird, und somit das Ansichseyn an ihr erhält. 2) Jene Existenz war auch bestimmt als Möglichkeit oder als das Ansichseyn aber eines Andern. Indem es sich also aufhebt, so wird auch dieß Ansichseyn aufgehoben, und geht in Wirklichkeit über.—Diese Bewegung der sich selbst aufhebenden realen Möglichkeit bringt also dieselben schon vorhandenen Momente hervor, nur jedes aus dem andern werdend; sie ist daher in dieser Negation auch nicht ein Übergehen, sondern ein Zusammengehen mit sich selbst.—Nach der formellen Möglichkeit war darum, weil etwas möglich war, auch nicht es selbst, sondern sein Anderes möglich. Die reale Möglichkeit hat nicht mehr ein solches Anderes sich gegenüber, denn sie ist real, insofern sie selbst auch die Wirklichkeit ist. Indem sich also die unmittelbare Existenz derselben, der Kreis der Bedingungen, aufhebt, so macht sie sich zum Ansichseyn, welches sie selbst schon ist, nämlich als das Ansichseyn eines Andern. Und indem umgekehrt dadurch zugleich ihr Moment des Ansichseyns sich aufhebt, wird sie zur Wirklichkeit, also zu dem Momente, das sie gleichfalls selbst schon ist.—Was verschwindet, ist damit dieß, daß die Wirklichkeit bestimmt war als die Möglichkeit oder das Ansichseyn eines Andern, und umgekehrt die Möglichkeit als eine Wirklichkeit, die nicht diejenige ist, deren Möglichkeit sie ist\n\n3. Die Negation der realen Möglichkeit ist somit ihre Identität mit sich: indem sie so in ihrem Aufheben der Gegenstoß dieses Aufhebens in sich selbsi ist, ist sie die reale Nothwendigkeit.\n\nWas nothwendig ist, kann nicht anders seyn; aber wohl was überhaupt möglich ist; denn die Möglichkeit ist das Ansichseyn, das nur Gesetztseyn, und daher wesentlich Andersseyn ist. Die formelle Möglichkeit ist diese Identität als Übergehen in schlechthin Anderes; die reale aber, weil sie das andere Moment, die Wirklichkeit, an ihr hat, ist schon selbst die Nothwendigkeit. Was daher real möglich ist, das kann nicht mehr anders seyn; unter diesen Bedingungen und Umständen kann nicht etwas Anderes erfolgen. Reale Möglichkeit und die Nothwendigkeit sind daher nur scheinbar unterschieden; diese ist eine Identität, die nicht erst wird, sondern schon vorausgesetzt ist, und zu Grunde liegt. Die reale Nothwendigkeit ist daher inhaltsvolle Beziehung; denn der Inhalt ist jene ansichseyende Identität, die gegen die Formunterschiede gleichgültig ist.\n\nDiese Nothwendigkeit aber ist zugleich relativ.—Sie hat nämlich eine Voraussetzung, von der sie anfängt, sie hat an dem Zufälligen ihren Ausgangspunkt. Das reale Wirkliche als solches, ist nämlich das bestimmte Wirkliche, und hat zunächst seine Bestimmtheit als unmittelbares Seyn darin, daß es eine Mannigfaltigkeit existirender Umstände ist; aber dieß unmittelbare Seyn als Bestimmtheit, ist es auch das Negative seiner, ist Ansichseyn oder Möglichkeit; so ist es reale Möglichkeit. Als diese Einheit der beiden Momente ist sie die Totalität der Form, aber die sich noch äußerliche Totalität; sie ist so Einheit der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit, daß 1) die mannigfaltige Existenz unmittelbar oder positiv die Möglichkeit ist;—ein Mögliches, mit sich Identisches überhaupt, darum weil sie ein Wirkliches ist; 2) insofern diese Möglichkeit der Existenz gesetzt ist, ist sie bestimmt als nur Möglichkeit, als unmittelbares Umschlagen der Wirklichkeit in ihr Gegentheil,—oder als Zufälligkeit. Daher ist diese Möglichkeit, welche die unmittelbare Wirklichkeit, indem sie Bedingung ist, an ihr hat, nur das Ansichseyn als die Möglichkeit eines Andern. Dadurch daß, wie gezeigt, dieß Andersseyn sich aufhebt, und dieß Gesetztseyn selbst gesetzt wird, wird die reale Möglichkeit zwar Nothwendigkeit; aber diese fängt somit von jener noch nicht in sich reflektirten Einheit des Möglichen und Wirklichen an;—dieses Voraussetzen und die in sich zurückkehrende Bewegung ist noch getrennt;—oder die Nothwendigkeit hat sich noch nicht aus sich selbst zur Zufälligkeit bestimmt.\n\nDie Relativität der realen Nothwendigkeit stellt sich an dem Inhalte so dar, daß er nur erst die gegen die Form gleichgültige Identität, daher von ihr unterschieden und ein bestimmter Inhalt überhaupt ist. Das real Nothwendige ist deswegen irgend eine beschränkte Wirklichkeit, die um dieser Beschränktheit willen in anderer Rüksicht auch nur ein Zufälliges ist.\n\nIn der That ist somit die reale Nothwendigkeit an sich auch Zufälligkeit.—Dieß erscheint zunächst so, daß das real Nothwendige, der Form nach, zwar ein Nothwendiges, aber dem Inhalte nach ein Beschränktes sey, und durch ihn seine Zufälligkeit habe. Allein auch in der Form der realen Nothwendigkeit ist die Zufälligkeit enthalten; denn wie sich gezeigt, ist die reale Möglichkeit nur an sich das Nothwendige, gesetzt aber ist sie als das Andersseyn der Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit gegen einander. Die reale Nothwendigkeit enthält daher die Zufälligkeit; sie ist die Rückkehr in-sich aus jenem unruhigen Andersseyn der Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit gegen einander, aber nicht aus sich selbst zu sich.\n\nAn sich ist also hier die Einheit der Nothwendigkeit und Zufälligkeit vorhanden; diese Einheit ist die absolute Wirklichkeit zu nennen.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0001","text":"1. Die Nothwendigkeit, die sich ergeben hat, ist formell, weil ihre Momente formell sind, nämlich einfache Bestimmungen, die nur als unmittelbare Einheit, oder als unmittelbares Umschlagen des Einen in das Andere Totalität sind, und somit nicht die Gestalt der Selbstständigkeit haben.—In dieser formellen Nothwendigkeit ist daher die Einheit zunächst einfach und gegen ihre Unterschiede gleichgültig. Als unmittelbare Einheit der Formbestimmungen, ist diese Nothwendigkeit Wirklichkeit; aber eine solche, die, weil ihre Einheit nunmehr bestimmt ist als gleichgültig gegen den Unterschied der Formbestimmungen, nämlich ihrer selbst und der Möglichkeit, einen Inhalt hat. Dieser als gleichgültige Identität enthält auch die Form als gleichgültige, d. h. als bloß verschiedene Bestimmungen, und ist mannigfaltiger Inhalt überhaupt. Diese Wirklichkeit ist reale Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"160.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0002","text":"Die reale Wirklichkeit als solche ist zunächst das Ding von vielen Eigenschaften, die existirende Welt; aber sie ist nicht die Existenz, welche sich in Erscheinung auflöst, sondern als Wirklichkeit ist sie zugleich Ansichseyn und Reflexion-in-sich; sie erhält sich in der Mannigfaltigkeit der bloßen Existenz; ihre Äußerlichkeit ist innerliches Verhalten nur zu sich selbst. Was wirklich ist, kann wirken; seine Wirklichkeit giebt Etwas kund durch das, was es hervorbringt. Sein Verhalten zu Anderem ist die Manifestation seiner, weder ein Übergehen, so bezieht das seyende Etwas sich auf Anderes; —noch ein Erscheinen, so ist das Ding nur im Verhältniß zu andern, ist ein Selbstständiges, das aber seine Reflexion-in-sich, seine bestimmte Wesentlichkeit, in einem andern Selbstständigen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"160.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0003","text":"Die reale Wirklichkeit hat nun gleichfalls die Möglichkeit unmittelbar an ihr selbst. Sie enthält das Moment des Ansichseyns; aber als nur erst die unmittelbare Einheit ist sie in einer der Bestimmungen der Fonn, hiermit als das Seyende von dem Ansichseyn oder der Möglichkeit unterschieden.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"160.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0004","text":"2. Diese Möglichkeit als das Ansichseyn der realen Wirklichkeit ist selbst reale Möglichkeit, zunächst das inhaltsvolle Ansichseyn.—Die formelle Möglichkeit ist die Reflexion-in-sich nur als die abstrakte Identität, daß Etwas sich in sich nicht widerspreche. Insofern man sich aber auf die Bestimmungen, Umstände, Bedingungen einer Sache einläßt, um daraus ihre Möglichkeit zu erkennen, bleibt man nicht mehr bei der formellen stehen, sondern betrachtet ihre reale Möglichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"160.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0005","text":"Diese reale Möglichkeit ist selbst unmittelbare Existenz, nicht mehr aber darum, weil die Möglichkeit als solche, als formelles Moment, unmittelbar ihr Gegentheil, eine nicht reflektirte Wirklichkeit ist; sondern weil sie reale Möglichkeit ist, hat sie sogleich diese Bestimmung an ihr selbst. Die reale Möglichkeit einer Sache ist daher die daseyende Mannigfaltigkeit von Umständen, die sich auf sie beziehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"160.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0006","text":"Diese Mannigfaltigkeit des Daseyns ist also zwar sowohl Möglichkeit als Wirklichkeit, aber ihre Identität ist nur erst der Inhalt, der gegen diese Formbestimmungen gleichgültig ist; sie machen daher die Form aus bestimmt gegen ihre Identität.—Oder die unmittelbare reale Wirklichkeit, darum weil sie unmittelbare ist, ist gegen ihre Möglichkeit bestimmt; als diese bestimmte, somit reflektirte ist sie die reale Möglichkeit. Diese ist nun zwar das gesetzte Ganze der Form, aber der Form in ihrer Bestimmtheit, nämlich der Wirklichkeit als formeller oder unmittelbarer, und ebenso der Möglichkeit, als des abstrakten Ansichseyns.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"160.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0007","text":"Diese Wirklichkeit, welche die Möglichkeit einer Sache ausmacht, ist daher nicht ihre eigene Möglichkeit, sondern das Ansichseyn eines andern Wirklichen; sie selbst ist die Wirklichkeit, die aufgehoben werden soll, die Möglichkeit als nur Möglichkeit.—So macht die reale Möglichkeit das Ganze von Bedingungen aus, eine nicht in sich reflektirte, zerstreute Wirklichkeit, welche aber bestimmt ist, das Ansichseyn aber eines Andern zu seyn und in sich zurückgehen zu sollen.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"160.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0008","text":"Was real möglich ist, ist also nach seinem Ansichseyn, ein formelles Identisches, das nach seiner einfachen Inhaltsbestimmung sich nicht widerspricht; aber auch nach seinen entwickelten und unterschiedenen Umständen und allem, womit es im Zusammenhange steht, muß es als das mit sich Identische sich nicht widersprechen. Aber zweitens weil es in sich mannigfaltig und mit Anderem in mannigfaltigem Zusammenhange ist, die Verschiedenheit aber an sich selbst in Entgegensetzung übergeht, ist es ein Widersprechendes.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"160.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0009","text":"Wenn von einer Möglichkeit die Rede ist und deren Widerspruch aufgezeigt werden soll, so hat man sich nur an die Mannigfaltigkeit, die sie als Inhalt oder als ihre bedingende Existenz enthält, zu halten; woraus sich leicht ihr Widerspruch auffinden läßt.—Dieß ist aber nicht ein Widerspruch der Vergleichung, sondern die mannigfaltige Existenz ist an sich selbst dieß, sich aufzuheben und zu Grunde zu gehen; und hat darin wesentlich die Bestimmung, nur ein Mögliches zu seyn, an ihr selbst. —Wenn alle Bedingungen einer Sache vollständig vorhanden sind, so tritt sie in Wirklichkeit;—die Vollständigkeit der Bedingungen ist die Totalität als am Inhalte, und die Sache selbst ist dieser Inhalt bestimmt ebenso ein Wirkliches als Mögliches zu seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"160.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0010","text":"In der Sphäre des bedingten Grundes haben die Bedingungen die Form, nämlich den Grund oder die für sich seyende Reflexion, außer ihnen, welche sie zu Momenten der Sache bezieht und die Existenz an ihnen hervorbringt. Hier hingegen ist die unmittelbare Wirklichkeit nicht durch eine voraussetzende Reflexion bestimmt, Bedingung zu seyn, sondern es ist gesetzt, daß sie selbst die Möglichkeit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"160.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0011","text":"In der sich aufhebenden realen Möglichkeit ist es nun ein Gedoppeltes, das aufgehoben wird; denn sie ist selbst das Gedoppelte, Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit zu seyn. 1) Die Wirklichkeit ist die formelle, oder eine Existenz, die als selbstständige unmittelbare erschien, und durch ihr Aufheben zum reflektirten Seyn, zum Moment eines Andern wird, und somit das Ansichseyn an ihr erhält. 2) Jene Existenz war auch bestimmt als Möglichkeit oder als das Ansichseyn aber eines Andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"160.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0012","text":"Indem es sich also aufhebt, so wird auch dieß Ansichseyn aufgehoben, und geht in Wirklichkeit über.—Diese Bewegung der sich selbst aufhebenden realen Möglichkeit bringt also dieselben schon vorhandenen Momente hervor, nur jedes aus dem andern werdend; sie ist daher in dieser Negation auch nicht ein Übergehen, sondern ein Zusammengehen mit sich selbst.—Nach der formellen Möglichkeit war darum, weil etwas möglich war, auch nicht es selbst, sondern sein Anderes möglich. Die reale Möglichkeit hat nicht mehr ein solches Anderes sich gegenüber, denn sie ist real, insofern sie selbst auch die Wirklichkeit ist. Indem sich also die unmittelbare Existenz derselben, der Kreis der Bedingungen, aufhebt, so macht sie sich zum Ansichseyn, welches sie selbst schon ist, nämlich als das Ansichseyn eines Andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"160.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0013","text":"Und indem umgekehrt dadurch zugleich ihr Moment des Ansichseyns sich aufhebt, wird sie zur Wirklichkeit, also zu dem Momente, das sie gleichfalls selbst schon ist.—Was verschwindet, ist damit dieß, daß die Wirklichkeit bestimmt war als die Möglichkeit oder das Ansichseyn eines Andern, und umgekehrt die Möglichkeit als eine Wirklichkeit, die nicht diejenige ist, deren Möglichkeit sie ist","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"160.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0014","text":"3. Die Negation der realen Möglichkeit ist somit ihre Identität mit sich: indem sie so in ihrem Aufheben der Gegenstoß dieses Aufhebens in sich selbsi ist, ist sie die reale Nothwendigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"160.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0015","text":"Was nothwendig ist, kann nicht anders seyn; aber wohl was überhaupt möglich ist; denn die Möglichkeit ist das Ansichseyn, das nur Gesetztseyn, und daher wesentlich Andersseyn ist. Die formelle Möglichkeit ist diese Identität als Übergehen in schlechthin Anderes; die reale aber, weil sie das andere Moment, die Wirklichkeit, an ihr hat, ist schon selbst die Nothwendigkeit. Was daher real möglich ist, das kann nicht mehr anders seyn; unter diesen Bedingungen und Umständen kann nicht etwas Anderes erfolgen. Reale Möglichkeit und die Nothwendigkeit sind daher nur scheinbar unterschieden; diese ist eine Identität, die nicht erst wird, sondern schon vorausgesetzt ist, und zu Grunde liegt. Die reale Nothwendigkeit ist daher inhaltsvolle Beziehung; denn der Inhalt ist jene ansichseyende Identität, die gegen die Formunterschiede gleichgültig ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"160.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0016","text":"Diese Nothwendigkeit aber ist zugleich relativ.—Sie hat nämlich eine Voraussetzung, von der sie anfängt, sie hat an dem Zufälligen ihren Ausgangspunkt. Das reale Wirkliche als solches, ist nämlich das bestimmte Wirkliche, und hat zunächst seine Bestimmtheit als unmittelbares Seyn darin, daß es eine Mannigfaltigkeit existirender Umstände ist; aber dieß unmittelbare Seyn als Bestimmtheit, ist es auch das Negative seiner, ist Ansichseyn oder Möglichkeit; so ist es reale Möglichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"160.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0017","text":"Als diese Einheit der beiden Momente ist sie die Totalität der Form, aber die sich noch äußerliche Totalität; sie ist so Einheit der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit, daß 1) die mannigfaltige Existenz unmittelbar oder positiv die Möglichkeit ist;—ein Mögliches, mit sich Identisches überhaupt, darum weil sie ein Wirkliches ist; 2) insofern diese Möglichkeit der Existenz gesetzt ist, ist sie bestimmt als nur Möglichkeit, als unmittelbares Umschlagen der Wirklichkeit in ihr Gegentheil,—oder als Zufälligkeit. Daher ist diese Möglichkeit, welche die unmittelbare Wirklichkeit, indem sie Bedingung ist, an ihr hat, nur das Ansichseyn als die Möglichkeit eines Andern.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"160.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0018","text":"Dadurch daß, wie gezeigt, dieß Andersseyn sich aufhebt, und dieß Gesetztseyn selbst gesetzt wird, wird die reale Möglichkeit zwar Nothwendigkeit; aber diese fängt somit von jener noch nicht in sich reflektirten Einheit des Möglichen und Wirklichen an;—dieses Voraussetzen und die in sich zurückkehrende Bewegung ist noch getrennt;—oder die Nothwendigkeit hat sich noch nicht aus sich selbst zur Zufälligkeit bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"160.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0019","text":"Die Relativität der realen Nothwendigkeit stellt sich an dem Inhalte so dar, daß er nur erst die gegen die Form gleichgültige Identität, daher von ihr unterschieden und ein bestimmter Inhalt überhaupt ist. Das real Nothwendige ist deswegen irgend eine beschränkte Wirklichkeit, die um dieser Beschränktheit willen in anderer Rüksicht auch nur ein Zufälliges ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"160.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0020","text":"In der That ist somit die reale Nothwendigkeit an sich auch Zufälligkeit.—Dieß erscheint zunächst so, daß das real Nothwendige, der Form nach, zwar ein Nothwendiges, aber dem Inhalte nach ein Beschränktes sey, und durch ihn seine Zufälligkeit habe. Allein auch in der Form der realen Nothwendigkeit ist die Zufälligkeit enthalten; denn wie sich gezeigt, ist die reale Möglichkeit nur an sich das Nothwendige, gesetzt aber ist sie als das Andersseyn der Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit gegen einander. Die reale Nothwendigkeit enthält daher die Zufälligkeit; sie ist die Rückkehr in-sich aus jenem unruhigen Andersseyn der Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit gegen einander, aber nicht aus sich selbst zu sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"160.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0021","text":"An sich ist also hier die Einheit der Nothwendigkeit und Zufälligkeit vorhanden; diese Einheit ist die absolute Wirklichkeit zu nennen.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"160.21"}],"sha256":"331b55ade24283e6b6bf70b2dd257e7a00582d69e9c308452f3e22c4c40b9705","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T105953285835Z_7b731d7c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Relative Necessity or Actuality, Possibility, and Necessity.","source_sha256":"331b55ade24283e6b6bf70b2dd257e7a00582d69e9c308452f3e22c4c40b9705","sha256":"d676e2dd8ddfbf24fa42556ac3d26c3546019eb5058dafa27281f95401c58530","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T10:59:53.285862+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0001","text":"1. The necessity that has arisen is formal, because its moments are formal, namely simple determinations which are totality only as immediate unity, or as the immediate conversion of the one into the other, and thus do not have the shape of self-subsistence.—In this formal necessity, therefore, unity is at first simple and indifferent towards its differences. As immediate unity of the determinations of form, this necessity is actuality; but such an actuality as, because its unity is henceforth determined as indifferent towards the difference of the determinations of form, namely of itself and possibility, has a content. This content, as indifferent identity, also contains form as indifferent, i.e. as merely different determinations, and is manifold content in general. This actuality is real actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"160.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0002","text":"Real actuality as such is at first the thing with many properties, the existing world; but it is not existence which dissolves into appearance; rather, as actuality, it is at the same time being-in-itself and reflection-into-itself; it maintains itself in the manifoldness of mere existence; its externality is an internal relation only to itself. What is actual can act; its actuality makes something manifest through what it produces. Its relation to another is the manifestation of itself, neither a transition—in which the being something relates itself to another;—nor an appearing—in which the thing is only in relation to others, is a self-subsistent entity which, however, has its reflection-into-itself, its determinate essentiality, in another self-subsistent entity.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"160.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0003","text":"Real actuality now likewise has possibility immediately in itself. It contains the moment of being-in-itself; but, as at first only immediate unity, it is in one of the determinations of form, and is consequently, as the being, distinguished from being-in-itself or possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"160.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0004","text":"2. This possibility, as the being-in-itself of real actuality, is itself real possibility, at first being-in-itself filled with content.—Formal possibility is reflection-into-itself only as abstract identity, namely that something does not contradict itself within itself. But insofar as one enters upon the determinations, circumstances, conditions of a thing in order to cognize its possibility from them, one no longer remains with formal possibility, but considers its real possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"160.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0005","text":"This real possibility is itself immediate existence, but no longer for the reason that possibility as such, as a formal moment, is immediately its opposite, an actuality not reflected into itself; rather, because it is real possibility, it immediately has this determination in itself. The real possibility of a thing is therefore the existing manifoldness of circumstances which relate to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"160.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0006","text":"This manifoldness of determinate being is thus indeed both possibility and actuality, but their identity is at first only the content, which is indifferent towards these determinations of form; they therefore constitute form as determined against their identity.—Or, immediate real actuality, precisely because it is immediate, is determined against its possibility; as this determinate, and thus reflected, actuality, it is real possibility. This is indeed now the posited whole of form, but of form in its determinacy, namely actuality as formal or immediate, and likewise possibility as abstract being-in-itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"160.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0007","text":"This actuality, which constitutes the possibility of a thing, is therefore not its own possibility, but the being-in-itself of another actual; it itself is the actuality which is to be sublated, possibility as mere possibility.—Thus real possibility constitutes the whole of conditions, an actuality not reflected into itself, dispersed, but which is determined to be the being-in-itself of another and to have to return into itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"160.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0008","text":"What is really possible is thus, according to its being-in-itself, a formal identical, which, according to its simple determination of content, does not contradict itself; but also according to its developed and differentiated circumstances and everything with which it stands in connection, it must not contradict itself as that which is identical with itself. But secondly, because it is manifold within itself and stands in manifold connection with another, while difference in itself passes over into opposition, it is something contradictory.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"160.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0009","text":"When there is talk of a possibility and its contradiction is to be exhibited, one need only adhere to the manifoldness which it contains as content or as its conditioning existence; from which its contradiction may readily be found.—But this is not a contradiction of comparison; rather, manifold existence is in itself this: to sublate itself and perish; and therein it essentially has the determination of being only a possible.—When all the conditions of a thing are completely present, it enters into actuality;—the completeness of the conditions is totality as in the content, and the thing itself is this content, determined to be equally an actual as a possible.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"160.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0010","text":"In the sphere of conditioned ground, the conditions have form, namely ground or reflection being-for-itself, outside them, which relates them to the moments of the thing and brings forth existence in them. Here, on the contrary, immediate actuality is not determined by a presupposing reflection to be condition; rather, it is posited that it itself is possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"160.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0011","text":"In self-sublating real possibility there is now a twofold which is sublated; for it is itself the twofold of being actuality and possibility. 1) Actuality is the formal, or an existence which appeared as self-subsistent and immediate, and through its sublation becomes reflected being, the moment of another, and thus receives being-in-itself in it. 2) That existence was also determined as possibility, or as the being-in-itself, however, of another.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"160.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0012","text":"Since it thus sublates itself, this being-in-itself too is sublated and passes over into actuality.—This movement of self-sublating real possibility thus brings forth the same moments already present, only each becoming out of the other; it is therefore, in this negation, not a transition either, but a coming-together with itself.—According to formal possibility, because something was possible, not it itself but its other was also possible. Real possibility no longer has such an other confronting it, for it is real insofar as it itself is also actuality. Since, therefore, its immediate existence, the circle of conditions, sublates itself, it makes itself into being-in-itself, which it already is itself, namely as the being-in-itself of another.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"160.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0013","text":"And since conversely, thereby, its moment of being-in-itself is at the same time sublated, it becomes actuality, thus the moment which it likewise already is itself.—What thereby disappears is this: that actuality was determined as the possibility or being-in-itself of another, and conversely possibility as an actuality which is not that whose possibility it is.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"160.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0014","text":"3. The negation of real possibility is thus its identity with itself: in that, in its sublation, the counterstroke of this sublation is in itself, it is real necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"160.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0015","text":"What is necessary cannot be otherwise; but what is possible in general can indeed be otherwise; for possibility is being-in-itself, which is only positedness, and is therefore essentially being-other. Formal possibility is this identity as transition into an absolutely other; but real possibility, because it has the other moment, actuality, in it, is already itself necessity. What is really possible, therefore, can no longer be otherwise; under these conditions and circumstances, something else cannot occur. Real possibility and necessity are therefore only apparently distinct; the latter is an identity which does not first become, but is already presupposed and lies at the ground. Real necessity is therefore a relation filled with content; for content is that identity which is in itself, and which is indifferent towards the differences of form.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"160.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0016","text":"But this necessity is at the same time relative.—It has, namely, a presupposition from which it begins; it has its point of departure in the contingent. Real actuality as such is, namely, determinate actuality, and initially has its determinacy as immediate being in the fact that it is a manifoldness of existing circumstances; but this immediate being, as determinacy, is also its negative, is being-in-itself or possibility; thus it is real possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"160.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0017","text":"As this unity of the two moments, it is the totality of form, but a totality still external to itself; it is thus unity of possibility and actuality, such that 1) manifold existence is immediately or positively possibility;—a possible, identical with itself in general, precisely because it is an actual; 2) insofar as this possibility of existence is posited, it is determined as mere possibility, as the immediate conversion of actuality into its opposite,—or as contingency. Hence this possibility, which has in it immediate actuality, insofar as it is condition, is only being-in-itself as the possibility of another.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"160.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0018","text":"Since, as shown, this being-other sublates itself, and this positedness itself is posited, real possibility indeed becomes necessity; but it thus begins from that unity of possible and actual which is not yet reflected into itself;—this presupposing and the movement returning into itself are still separated;—or necessity has not yet determined itself out of itself into contingency.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"160.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0019","text":"The relativity of real necessity displays itself in the content in such a way that it is at first only identity indifferent towards form, hence distinguished from it and a determinate content in general. What is really necessary is for that reason some restricted actuality, which, on account of this restriction, is in another respect also only a contingent.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"160.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0020","text":"Thus real necessity is in fact in itself also contingency.—This at first appears thus, that what is really necessary is, according to form, indeed a necessary, but according to content a restricted, and has its contingency through the latter. Yet contingency is also contained in the form of real necessity; for, as has been shown, real possibility is necessary only in itself, but is posited as the being-other of actuality and possibility over against each other. Real necessity therefore contains contingency; it is the return into itself out of that restless being-other of actuality and possibility over against each other, but not from itself to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"160.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0021","text":"Thus, in itself, the unity of necessity and contingency is present here; this unity is to be called absolute actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"160.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BRNO:P0021"]}],"source_digest":"093ae67a092b9c3eed2013b4922fbfcc9d63745748905e89f0e2d76f445f6f85","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Relative Nothwendigkeit oder reale Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"B. Relative Nothwendigkeit oder reale Wirklichkeit, Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0","title":"C. Absolute Necessity.","order":161,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CAN0","text":"Die reale Nothwendigkeit ist bestimmte Nothwendigkeit; die formelle hat noch keinen Inhalt und Bestimmtheit an ihr. Die Bestimmtheit der Nothwendigkeit besteht darin, daß sie ihre Negation, die Zufälligkeit, an ihr hat. So hat sie sich ergeben.\n\nDiese Bestimmtheit aber in ihrer ersten Einfachheit ist Wirklichkeit; die bestimmte Nothwendigkeit ist daher unmittelbar wirkliche Nothwendigkeit. Diese Wirklichkeit, die selbst als solche nothwendig ist, indem sie nämlich die Nothwendigkeit als ihr Ansichseyn enthält, ist absolute Wirklichkeit;—Wirklichkeit, die nicht mehr anders seyn kann, denn ihr Ansichseyn ist nicht die Möglichkeit, sondern die Nothwendigkeit selbst.\n\nAber damit ist diese Wirklichkeit, weil sie gesetzt ist, absolut, das heißt, selbst die Einheit ihrer und der Möglichkeit zu seyn, nur eine leere Bestimmung; oder sie ist Zufälligkeit.—Dieß Leere ihrer Bestimmung macht sie zu einer bloßen Möglichkeit, zu einem, das ebenso sehr auch anders seyn und als Mögliches bestimmt werden kann. Diese Möglichkeit aber ist selbst die absolute; denn sie ist eben die Möglichkeit, ebenso sehr als Möglichkeit wie als Wirklichkeit bestimmt zu werden. Damit, daß sie diese Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich selbst ist, ist sie gesetzt als leere, zufällige Bestimmung.\n\nSo enthält die reale Nothwendigkeit nicht nur an sich die Zufälligkeit, sondern diese wird auch an ihr; aber dieß Werden als die Äußerlichkeit ist selbst nur das Ansichseyn derselben, weil es nur ein unmittelbares Bestimmtseyn ist. Aber es ist nicht nur dieß, sondern ihr eigenes Werden,—oder die Voraussetzung, welche sie hatte, ist ihr eigenes Setzen. Denn als reale Nothwendigkeit ist sie das Aufgehobenseyn der Wirklichkeit in der Möglichkeit und umgekehrt; —indem sie dieß einfache Umschlagen des einen dieser Momente in das andere ist, ist sie auch ihre einfache positive Einheit, indem jedes, wie sich zeigte, in dem andern nur mit sich selbst zusammengeht. So ist sie aber die Wirklichkeit; jedoch eine solche, die nur ist, als dieses einfache Zusammen-gehen der Form mit sich selbst. Ihr negatives Setzen jener Momente ist dadurch selbst das Voraussetzen, oder Setzen ihrer selbst als aufgehobener oder der Unmittelbarkeit.\n\nEben darin aber ist diese Wirklichkeit bestimmt als Negatives; sie ist ein Zusammengehen aus der Wirklichkeit, welche reale Möglichkeit war, mit sich; also wird diese neue Wirklichkeit nur aus ihrem Ansichseyn, aus der Negation ihrer selbst.—Damit ist sie zugleich unmittelbar als Möglichkeit bestimmt, als Vermitteltes durch ihre Negation. Diese Möglichkeit aber ist somit unmittelbar nichts als dieß Vermitteln, in welchem das Ansichseyn, nämlich sie selbst, und die Unmittelbarkeit, beide auf gleiche Weise Gesetztseyn sind.—So ist es die Nothwendigkeit, welche ebenso sehr Aufheben dieses Gesetztseyns oder Setzen der Unmittelbarkeit, und des Ansichseyns, so wie eben darin Bestimmen dieses Aufhebens als Gesetztseyns ist. Sie ist daher es selbst, welche sich als Zufälligkeit bestimmt;—in ihrem Seyn sich von sich abstößt, in diesem Abstoßen selbst nur in sich zurückgekehrt ist, und in dieser Rückkehr als ihrem Seyn sich von sich selbst abgestoßen hat.\n\nSo hat die Form in ihrer Realisirung alle ihre Unterschiede durchdrungen und sich durchsichtig gemacht, und ist als absolute Nothwendigkeit nur diese einfache Identität des Seyns in seiner Negation oder in dem Wesen mit sich selbst.—Der Unterschied von dem Inhalte und der Form selbst ist ebenso verschwunden; denn jene Einheit der Möglichkeit in der Wirklichkeit und umgekehrt ist die in ihrer Bestimmtheit oder im Gesetztseyn gegen sich selbst gleichgültige Form, die inhaltsvolle Sache, an der sich die Form der Nothwendigkeit äußerlich verlief. Aber so ist sie diese reflektirte Identität beider Bestimmungen, als gegen sie gleichgültig, somit die Formbestimmung des Ansichseyns gegen das Gesetztseyn, und diese Möglichkeit macht die Beschränktheit des Inhalts aus, den die reale Nothwendigkeit hatte. Die Auflösung dieses Unterschieds aber ist die absolute Nothwendigkeit, deren Inhalt dieser in ihr sich durchdringende Unterschied ist.\n\nDie absolute Nothwendigkeit ist also die Wahrheit, in welche Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit überhaupt, so wie die formelle und reale Nothwendigkeit zurückgeht.—Sie ist, wie sich ergeben hat, das Seyn, das in seiner Negation, im Wesen, sich auf sich bezieht und Seyn ist. Sie ist ebenso sehr einfache Unmittelbarkeit oder reines Seyn, als einfache Reflexion-in-sich, oder reines Wesen; sie ist dieß, daß dieß Beides ein und dasselbe ist.—Das schlechthin Nothwendige ist nur, weil es ist; es hat sonst keine Bedingung, noch Grund.—Es ist aber ebenso reines Wesen, sein Seyn ist die einfache Reflexion-in-sich; es ist, weil es ist. Als Reflexion hat es Grund und Bedingung, aber es hat nur sich zum Grunde und Bedingung. Es ist Ansichseyn, aber sein Ansichseyn ist seine Unmittelbarkeit, seine Möglichkeit ist seine Wirklichkeit.—Es ist also, weil es ist; als das Zusammengehen des Seyns mit sich, ist es Wesen; aber weil dieß Einfache ebenso die unmittelbare Einfachheit ist, ist es Seyn.\n\nDie absolute Nothwendigkeitt ist so die Reflexion oder Form des Absoluten; Einheit des Seyns und Wesens, einfache Unmittelbarkeit, welche absolute Negativität ist. Einer Seits sind ihre Unterschiede daher nicht als Reflexions-Bestimmungen, sondern als seyende Mannigfaltigkeit, als unterschiedene Wirklichkeit, welche die Gestalt von selbstständigen Anderen gegen einander hat. Anderer Seits da ihre Beziehung die absolute Identität ist, ist sie das absolute Umkehren ihrer Wirklichkeit in ihre Möglichkeit und ihrer Möglichkeit in Wirklichkeit.—Die absolute Nothwendigkeit ist daher blind. Einer Seits haben die unterschiedenen, welche als Wirklichkeit und als die Möglichkeit bestimmt sind, die Gestalt der Reflexion-in-sich als des Seyns; sie sind daher beide als freie Wirklichkeiten, deren keins im Andern scheint, keins eine Spur seiner Beziehung auf das Andere an ihm zeigen will; in sich gegründet ist jedes das Nothwendige an ihm selbst. Die Nothwendigkeit als Wesen ist in diesem Seyn verschlossen; die Berührung dieser Wirklichkeiten durch einander erscheint daher als eine leere Äußerlichkeit; die Wirklichkeit des einen in dem Andern ist die nur Möglichkeit, die Zufälligkeit. Denn das Seyn ist gesetzt als absolut nothwendig, als die Vermittelung-mit-sich, welche absolute Negation der Vermittelung-durch-Anderes ist, oder als Seyn das nur mit dem Seyn identisch ist; ein Anderes, das im Seyn Wirklichkeit hat, ist daher als schlechthin nur Mögliches, leeres Gesetztseyn bestimmt.\n\nAber diese Zufälligkeit ist vielmehr die absolute Nothwendigkeit; sie ist das Wesen jener freien, an sich nothwendigen Wirklichkeiten. Dieses Wesen ist das Lichtscheue, weil an diesen Wirklichkeiten kein Scheinen, kein Reflex ist, weil sie nur rein in sich gegründet, für sich gestaltet sind, sich nur sich selbst manifestiren,—weil sie nur Seyn sind.—Aber ihr Wesen wird an ihnen hervorbrechen und offenbaren, was es ist und was sie sind. Die Einfachheit ihres Seyns, ihres Beruhens auf sich, ist die absolute Negativität; sie ist die Freiheit ihrer scheinlosen Unmittelbarkeit. Dieses Negative bricht an ihnen hervor, weil das Seyn durch dieß sein Wesen der Widerspruch mit sich selbst ist;—und zwar gegen dieß Seyn in der Form des Seyns, also als die Negation jener Wirklichkeiten, welche absolut verschieden ist von ihrem Seyn, als ihr Nichts, als ein ebenso freies Andersseyn gegen sie, als ihr Seyn es ist.—Jedoch war es an ihnen nicht zu verkennen. Sie sind in ihrer auf sich beruhenden Gestaltung gleichgültig gegen die Form, ein Inhalt, damit unterschiedene Wirklichkeiten und ein bestimmter Inhalt; dieser ist das Maal, das die Nothwendigkeit, indem sie, welche absolute Rückkehr in sich selbst in ihrer Bestimmung ist, dieselben frei als absolut wirkliche entließ,—ihnen aufdrückte, worauf sie als den Zeugen ihres Rechts sich beruft, und an dem sie ergriffen nun untergehen. Diese Manifestation dessen, was die Bestimmtheit in Wahrheit ist, negative Beziehung auf sich selbst, ist blinder Untergang im Andersseyn; das hervorbrechende Scheinen oder die Reflexion ist an den Seyenden als Werden oder Übergehen des Seyns in Nichts. Aber das Seyn ist umgekehrt ebenso sehr Wesen, und das Werden ist Reflexion oder Scheinen. So ist die Äußerlichkeit ihre Innerlichkeit, ihre Beziehung ist absolute Identität; und das Übergehen des Wirklichen in Mögliches, des Seyns in Nichts ein Zusammengehen mit sich selbst; die Zufälligkeit ist absolute Nothwendigkeit; sie selbst ist das Voraussetzen jener ersten absoluten Wirklichkeiten.\n\nDiese Identität des Seyns in seiner Negation mit sich selbst, ist sie nun Substanz. Sie ist diese Einheit als in ihrer Negation oder als in der Zufälligkeit; so ist sie die Substanz als Verhältniß zu sich selbst. Das blinde Übergehen der Nothwendigkeit ist vielmehr die eigene Auslegung des Absoluten, die Bewegung desselben in sich, welches in seiner Entäußerung vielmehr sich selbst zeigt.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0001","text":"Die reale Nothwendigkeit ist bestimmte Nothwendigkeit; die formelle hat noch keinen Inhalt und Bestimmtheit an ihr. Die Bestimmtheit der Nothwendigkeit besteht darin, daß sie ihre Negation, die Zufälligkeit, an ihr hat. So hat sie sich ergeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"161.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0002","text":"Diese Bestimmtheit aber in ihrer ersten Einfachheit ist Wirklichkeit; die bestimmte Nothwendigkeit ist daher unmittelbar wirkliche Nothwendigkeit. Diese Wirklichkeit, die selbst als solche nothwendig ist, indem sie nämlich die Nothwendigkeit als ihr Ansichseyn enthält, ist absolute Wirklichkeit;—Wirklichkeit, die nicht mehr anders seyn kann, denn ihr Ansichseyn ist nicht die Möglichkeit, sondern die Nothwendigkeit selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"161.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0003","text":"Aber damit ist diese Wirklichkeit, weil sie gesetzt ist, absolut, das heißt, selbst die Einheit ihrer und der Möglichkeit zu seyn, nur eine leere Bestimmung; oder sie ist Zufälligkeit.—Dieß Leere ihrer Bestimmung macht sie zu einer bloßen Möglichkeit, zu einem, das ebenso sehr auch anders seyn und als Mögliches bestimmt werden kann. Diese Möglichkeit aber ist selbst die absolute; denn sie ist eben die Möglichkeit, ebenso sehr als Möglichkeit wie als Wirklichkeit bestimmt zu werden. Damit, daß sie diese Gleichgültigkeit gegen sich selbst ist, ist sie gesetzt als leere, zufällige Bestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"161.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0004","text":"So enthält die reale Nothwendigkeit nicht nur an sich die Zufälligkeit, sondern diese wird auch an ihr; aber dieß Werden als die Äußerlichkeit ist selbst nur das Ansichseyn derselben, weil es nur ein unmittelbares Bestimmtseyn ist. Aber es ist nicht nur dieß, sondern ihr eigenes Werden,—oder die Voraussetzung, welche sie hatte, ist ihr eigenes Setzen. Denn als reale Nothwendigkeit ist sie das Aufgehobenseyn der Wirklichkeit in der Möglichkeit und umgekehrt; —indem sie dieß einfache Umschlagen des einen dieser Momente in das andere ist, ist sie auch ihre einfache positive Einheit, indem jedes, wie sich zeigte, in dem andern nur mit sich selbst zusammengeht. So ist sie aber die Wirklichkeit; jedoch eine solche, die nur ist, als dieses einfache Zusammen-gehen der Form mit sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"161.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0005","text":"Ihr negatives Setzen jener Momente ist dadurch selbst das Voraussetzen, oder Setzen ihrer selbst als aufgehobener oder der Unmittelbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"161.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0006","text":"Eben darin aber ist diese Wirklichkeit bestimmt als Negatives; sie ist ein Zusammengehen aus der Wirklichkeit, welche reale Möglichkeit war, mit sich; also wird diese neue Wirklichkeit nur aus ihrem Ansichseyn, aus der Negation ihrer selbst.—Damit ist sie zugleich unmittelbar als Möglichkeit bestimmt, als Vermitteltes durch ihre Negation. Diese Möglichkeit aber ist somit unmittelbar nichts als dieß Vermitteln, in welchem das Ansichseyn, nämlich sie selbst, und die Unmittelbarkeit, beide auf gleiche Weise Gesetztseyn sind.—So ist es die Nothwendigkeit, welche ebenso sehr Aufheben dieses Gesetztseyns oder Setzen der Unmittelbarkeit, und des Ansichseyns, so wie eben darin Bestimmen dieses Aufhebens als Gesetztseyns ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"161.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0007","text":"Sie ist daher es selbst, welche sich als Zufälligkeit bestimmt;—in ihrem Seyn sich von sich abstößt, in diesem Abstoßen selbst nur in sich zurückgekehrt ist, und in dieser Rückkehr als ihrem Seyn sich von sich selbst abgestoßen hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"161.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0008","text":"So hat die Form in ihrer Realisirung alle ihre Unterschiede durchdrungen und sich durchsichtig gemacht, und ist als absolute Nothwendigkeit nur diese einfache Identität des Seyns in seiner Negation oder in dem Wesen mit sich selbst.—Der Unterschied von dem Inhalte und der Form selbst ist ebenso verschwunden; denn jene Einheit der Möglichkeit in der Wirklichkeit und umgekehrt ist die in ihrer Bestimmtheit oder im Gesetztseyn gegen sich selbst gleichgültige Form, die inhaltsvolle Sache, an der sich die Form der Nothwendigkeit äußerlich verlief. Aber so ist sie diese reflektirte Identität beider Bestimmungen, als gegen sie gleichgültig, somit die Formbestimmung des Ansichseyns gegen das Gesetztseyn, und diese Möglichkeit macht die Beschränktheit des Inhalts aus, den die reale Nothwendigkeit hatte.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"161.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0009","text":"Die Auflösung dieses Unterschieds aber ist die absolute Nothwendigkeit, deren Inhalt dieser in ihr sich durchdringende Unterschied ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"161.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0010","text":"Die absolute Nothwendigkeit ist also die Wahrheit, in welche Wirklichkeit und Möglichkeit überhaupt, so wie die formelle und reale Nothwendigkeit zurückgeht.—Sie ist, wie sich ergeben hat, das Seyn, das in seiner Negation, im Wesen, sich auf sich bezieht und Seyn ist. Sie ist ebenso sehr einfache Unmittelbarkeit oder reines Seyn, als einfache Reflexion-in-sich, oder reines Wesen; sie ist dieß, daß dieß Beides ein und dasselbe ist.—Das schlechthin Nothwendige ist nur, weil es ist; es hat sonst keine Bedingung, noch Grund.—Es ist aber ebenso reines Wesen, sein Seyn ist die einfache Reflexion-in-sich; es ist, weil es ist. Als Reflexion hat es Grund und Bedingung, aber es hat nur sich zum Grunde und Bedingung.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"161.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0011","text":"Es ist Ansichseyn, aber sein Ansichseyn ist seine Unmittelbarkeit, seine Möglichkeit ist seine Wirklichkeit.—Es ist also, weil es ist; als das Zusammengehen des Seyns mit sich, ist es Wesen; aber weil dieß Einfache ebenso die unmittelbare Einfachheit ist, ist es Seyn.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"161.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0012","text":"Die absolute Nothwendigkeitt ist so die Reflexion oder Form des Absoluten; Einheit des Seyns und Wesens, einfache Unmittelbarkeit, welche absolute Negativität ist. Einer Seits sind ihre Unterschiede daher nicht als Reflexions-Bestimmungen, sondern als seyende Mannigfaltigkeit, als unterschiedene Wirklichkeit, welche die Gestalt von selbstständigen Anderen gegen einander hat. Anderer Seits da ihre Beziehung die absolute Identität ist, ist sie das absolute Umkehren ihrer Wirklichkeit in ihre Möglichkeit und ihrer Möglichkeit in Wirklichkeit.—Die absolute Nothwendigkeit ist daher blind.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"161.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0013","text":"Einer Seits haben die unterschiedenen, welche als Wirklichkeit und als die Möglichkeit bestimmt sind, die Gestalt der Reflexion-in-sich als des Seyns; sie sind daher beide als freie Wirklichkeiten, deren keins im Andern scheint, keins eine Spur seiner Beziehung auf das Andere an ihm zeigen will; in sich gegründet ist jedes das Nothwendige an ihm selbst. Die Nothwendigkeit als Wesen ist in diesem Seyn verschlossen; die Berührung dieser Wirklichkeiten durch einander erscheint daher als eine leere Äußerlichkeit; die Wirklichkeit des einen in dem Andern ist die nur Möglichkeit, die Zufälligkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"161.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0014","text":"Denn das Seyn ist gesetzt als absolut nothwendig, als die Vermittelung-mit-sich, welche absolute Negation der Vermittelung-durch-Anderes ist, oder als Seyn das nur mit dem Seyn identisch ist; ein Anderes, das im Seyn Wirklichkeit hat, ist daher als schlechthin nur Mögliches, leeres Gesetztseyn bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"161.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0015","text":"Aber diese Zufälligkeit ist vielmehr die absolute Nothwendigkeit; sie ist das Wesen jener freien, an sich nothwendigen Wirklichkeiten. Dieses Wesen ist das Lichtscheue, weil an diesen Wirklichkeiten kein Scheinen, kein Reflex ist, weil sie nur rein in sich gegründet, für sich gestaltet sind, sich nur sich selbst manifestiren,—weil sie nur Seyn sind.—Aber ihr Wesen wird an ihnen hervorbrechen und offenbaren, was es ist und was sie sind. Die Einfachheit ihres Seyns, ihres Beruhens auf sich, ist die absolute Negativität; sie ist die Freiheit ihrer scheinlosen Unmittelbarkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"161.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0016","text":"Dieses Negative bricht an ihnen hervor, weil das Seyn durch dieß sein Wesen der Widerspruch mit sich selbst ist;—und zwar gegen dieß Seyn in der Form des Seyns, also als die Negation jener Wirklichkeiten, welche absolut verschieden ist von ihrem Seyn, als ihr Nichts, als ein ebenso freies Andersseyn gegen sie, als ihr Seyn es ist.—Jedoch war es an ihnen nicht zu verkennen. Sie sind in ihrer auf sich beruhenden Gestaltung gleichgültig gegen die Form, ein Inhalt, damit unterschiedene Wirklichkeiten und ein bestimmter Inhalt; dieser ist das Maal, das die Nothwendigkeit, indem sie, welche absolute Rückkehr in sich selbst in ihrer Bestimmung ist, dieselben frei als absolut wirkliche entließ,—ihnen aufdrückte, worauf sie als den Zeugen ihres Rechts sich beruft, und an dem sie ergriffen nun untergehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"161.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0017","text":"Diese Manifestation dessen, was die Bestimmtheit in Wahrheit ist, negative Beziehung auf sich selbst, ist blinder Untergang im Andersseyn; das hervorbrechende Scheinen oder die Reflexion ist an den Seyenden als Werden oder Übergehen des Seyns in Nichts. Aber das Seyn ist umgekehrt ebenso sehr Wesen, und das Werden ist Reflexion oder Scheinen. So ist die Äußerlichkeit ihre Innerlichkeit, ihre Beziehung ist absolute Identität; und das Übergehen des Wirklichen in Mögliches, des Seyns in Nichts ein Zusammengehen mit sich selbst; die Zufälligkeit ist absolute Nothwendigkeit; sie selbst ist das Voraussetzen jener ersten absoluten Wirklichkeiten.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"161.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0018","text":"Diese Identität des Seyns in seiner Negation mit sich selbst, ist sie nun Substanz. Sie ist diese Einheit als in ihrer Negation oder als in der Zufälligkeit; so ist sie die Substanz als Verhältniß zu sich selbst. Das blinde Übergehen der Nothwendigkeit ist vielmehr die eigene Auslegung des Absoluten, die Bewegung desselben in sich, welches in seiner Entäußerung vielmehr sich selbst zeigt.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"161.18"}],"sha256":"a251f5dedd63ef53bf4c51fb3e7a16cb6792e294f3db4079380dad61addaa568","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110012714510Z_452d3729","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Absolute Necessity.","source_sha256":"a251f5dedd63ef53bf4c51fb3e7a16cb6792e294f3db4079380dad61addaa568","sha256":"bd561d5a2000bc18ec8702e66e9ab2e65e274212104d36b6d5ec4b0747710a34","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:00:12.714532+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0001","text":"Real necessity is determinate necessity; formal necessity does not yet have content and determinacy in it. The determinacy of necessity consists in its having its negation, contingency, in it. Thus it has resulted.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"161.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0002","text":"But this determinacy in its first simplicity is actuality; determinate necessity is therefore immediately actual necessity. This actuality, which is itself necessary as such, since namely it contains necessity as its being-in-itself, is absolute actuality;—actuality which can no longer be otherwise, for its being-in-itself is not possibility, but necessity itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"161.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0003","text":"But thereby this actuality, because it is posited, is absolute, that is, is itself the unity of itself and possibility, only an empty determination; or it is contingency.—This emptiness of its determination makes it into a mere possibility, into something that can just as much be otherwise and be determined as possible. But this possibility is itself the absolute; for it is precisely the possibility of being determined as possibility just as much as as actuality. In being this indifference toward itself, it is posited as an empty, contingent determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"161.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0004","text":"Thus real necessity contains contingency not only in itself, but contingency also becomes in it; but this becoming, as externality, is itself only its being-in-itself, because it is only an immediate determinacy. But it is not only this, but its own becoming,—or the presupposition which it had is its own positing. For as real necessity it is the sublatedness of actuality in possibility and conversely;—in that it is this simple transition of one of these moments into the other, it is also their simple positive unity, since each, as was shown, comes together with itself only in the other. But thus it is actuality; yet an actuality which is only as this simple coming-together of form with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"161.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0005","text":"Its negative positing of those moments is thereby itself presupposing, or positing of itself as sublated, or of immediacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"161.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0006","text":"But precisely therein this actuality is determined as negative; it is a coming-together, from actuality, which was real possibility, with itself; thus this new actuality becomes only from its being-in-itself, from the negation of itself.—Thereby it is at once immediately determined as possibility, as mediated through its negation. But this possibility is thus immediately nothing but this mediating, in which being-in-itself, namely itself, and immediacy are both, in the same manner, positedness.—Thus it is necessity which is just as much the sublating of this positedness or the positing of immediacy and of being-in-itself, as it is precisely therein the determining of this sublating as positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"161.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0007","text":"It is therefore itself which determines itself as contingency;—in its being repels itself from itself, in this repulsion itself has only returned into itself, and in this return as its being has repelled itself from itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"161.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0008","text":"Thus form, in its realization, has penetrated all its distinctions and made itself transparent, and as absolute necessity is only this simple identity of being, in its negation or in essence, with itself.—The distinction between content and form itself has likewise vanished; for that unity of possibility in actuality and conversely is form indifferent toward itself in its determinacy or in positedness, the contentful matter, upon which the form of necessity externally ran its course. But thus it is this reflected identity of both determinations, as indifferent toward them, hence the form-determination of being-in-itself as against positedness, and this possibility constitutes the limitation of the content which real necessity had.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"161.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0009","text":"But the dissolution of this distinction is absolute necessity, whose content is this distinction penetrating itself within it.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"161.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0010","text":"Absolute necessity is therefore the truth into which actuality and possibility in general, as well as formal and real necessity, return.—It is, as has resulted, being which, in its negation, in essence, relates itself to itself and is being. It is just as much simple immediacy or pure being as simple reflection-into-itself, or pure essence; it is this, that these two are one and the same.—That which is absolutely necessary is only because it is; it has no other condition or ground.—But it is equally pure essence; its being is simple reflection-into-itself; it is because it is. As reflection it has ground and condition, but it has only itself as ground and condition.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"161.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0011","text":"It is being-in-itself, but its being-in-itself is its immediacy, its possibility is its actuality.—It is therefore because it is; as the coming-together of being with itself, it is essence; but because this simple is equally immediate simplicity, it is being.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"161.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0012","text":"Absolute necessity is thus the reflection or form of the Absolute; unity of being and essence, simple immediacy, which is absolute negativity. On the one hand, its distinctions are therefore not as determinations of reflection, but as being multiplicity, as distinct actuality, which has the shape of self-subsisting others over against one another. On the other hand, since their relation is absolute identity, it is the absolute reversal of their actuality into their possibility and of their possibility into actuality.—Absolute necessity is therefore blind.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"161.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0013","text":"On the one hand, the distinct [terms], which are determined as actuality and as possibility, have the shape of reflection-into-itself as being; they are therefore both as free actualities, neither of which shines in the other, neither of which will show in it a trace of its relation to the other; each, grounded in itself, is the necessary in itself. Necessity as essence is enclosed in this being; the contact of these actualities with one another therefore appears as an empty externality; the actuality of the one in the other is only possibility, contingency.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"161.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0014","text":"For being is posited as absolutely necessary, as mediation-with-itself, which is the absolute negation of mediation-through-other, or as being that is identical only with being; an other which has actuality in being is therefore determined as what is absolutely only possible, empty positedness.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"161.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0015","text":"But this contingency is rather absolute necessity; it is the essence of those free actualities necessary in themselves. This essence is light-shunning, because in these actualities there is no shining, no reflection, because they are only purely grounded in themselves, formed for themselves, manifesting only themselves,—because they are only being.—But their essence will break forth in them and reveal what it is and what they are. The simplicity of their being, of their repose upon themselves, is absolute negativity; it is the freedom of their immediacy devoid of semblance.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"161.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0016","text":"This negative breaks forth in them because, through this its essence, being is contradiction with itself;—and indeed over against this being in the form of being, thus as the negation of those actualities, which is absolutely distinct from their being, as their nothing, as an otherness just as free over against them as their being is.—Yet it was not unrecognizable in them. In their formation reposing upon itself, they are indifferent toward form, a content, thereby distinct actualities and a determinate content; this is the measure which necessity, in that it, which is absolute return into itself in its determination, released them freely as absolutely actual,—impressed upon them, to which it appeals as the witness of its right, and by which, once seized, they perish.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"161.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0017","text":"This manifestation of what determinacy is in truth, negative relation to itself, is blind perishing in otherness; the breaking-forth shining, or reflection, is in beings as becoming or transition of being into nothing. But being is conversely just as much essence, and becoming is reflection or shining. Thus externality is their inwardness, their relation is absolute identity; and the transition of the actual into the possible, of being into nothing, is a coming-together with itself; contingency is absolute necessity; it itself is the presupposing of those first absolute actualities.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"161.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0018","text":"This identity of being in its negation with itself is now substance. It is this unity as in its negation or as in contingency; thus it is substance as relation to itself. The blind transition of necessity is rather the Absolute's own explication, its movement within itself, which in its self-externalization rather shows itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"161.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CAN0:P0018"]}],"source_digest":"46343994e45b4848e9b65c59da1ff7d0368ab7235fc4037d472b1112bad51d66","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Absolute Nothwendigkeit."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Absolute Nothwendigkeit.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2","title":"A. The Relation of Substantiality.","order":162,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DV_2","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das absolute Verhältniß.\n\nDie absolute Nothwendigkeit ist nicht sowohl das Nothwendige, noch weniger ein Nothwendiges, sondern Nothwendigkeit;—Seyn schlechthin als Reflexion. Sie ist Verhältniß, weil sie Unterscheiden ist, dessen Momente selbst ihre ganze Totalität sind, die also absolut bestehen, so daß dieß aber nur Ein Bestehen und der Unterschied nur der Schein des Auslegens, und dieser das Absolute selbst ist.—Das Wesen als solches ist die Reflexion oder das Scheinen; das Wesen als absolutes Verhältniß aber ist der als Schein gesetzte Schein, oder als dieß Beziehen auf sich die absolute Wirklichkeit ist.—Das Absolute, zuerst von der äußern Reflexion ausgelegt, legt nun als absolute Form oder als Nothwendigkeit, sich selbst aus; dieß Auslegen seiner selbst ist sein Sich-selbst-setzen, und es ist nur dieß Sich-setzen.—Wie das Licht der Natur nicht Etwas, noch Ding, sondern sein Seyn nur sein Scheinen ist, so ist die Manifestation die sich selbst gleiche absolute Wirklichkeit.\n\nDie Seiten des absoluten Verhältnisses sind daher keine Attribute. Im Attribute scheint das Absolute nur in einem seiner Momente, als einem vorausgesetzten und von der äußern Reflexion aufgenommenen. Die Auslegerin des Absoluten aber ist die absolute Nothwendigkeit, die identisch mit sich ist, als sich selbst bestimmend. Da sie das Scheinen ist, das als Schein gesetzt ist, so sind die Seiten dieses Verhältnisses Totalitäten, weil sie als Schein sind; denn als Schein sind die Unterschiede sie selbst und ihr Entgegengesetztes, oder das Ganze;—umgekehrt sind sie so Schein, weil sie Totalitäten sind. Dieß Unterscheiden oder Scheinen des Absoluten ist so nur das identische Setzen seiner selbst.\n\nDieß Verhältniß in seinem unmittelbaren Begriff ist das Verhältniß der Substanz und der Accidenzen, das unmittelbare Verschwinden und Werden des absoluten Scheines in sich selbst. Indem die Substanz sich zum Fürsichseyn gegen ein Anderes bestimmt, oder das absolute Verhältniß als reales, ist das Verhältniß der Kausalität. Endlich indem dieses als sich auf sich Beziehendes in Wechselwirkung übergeht, so ist damit das absolute Verhältniß nach den Bestimmungen, welche es enthält, auch gesetzt; diese gesetzte Einheit seiner in seinen Bestimmungen, die als das Ganze selbst und damit ebenso sehr als Bestimmungen gesetzt sind, ist alsdann der Begriff.\n\n## A. Das Verhältniß der Substantialität.\n\nDie absolute Nothwendigkeit ist absolutes Verhältniß, weil sie nicht das Seyn als solches ist, sondern das Seyn, das ist, weil es ist, das Seyn als die absolute Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst. Dieses Seyn ist die Substanz; als die letzte Einheit des Wesens und Seyns, ist sie das Seyn in allem Seyn; weder das unreflektirte Unmittelbare, noch auch ein abstraktes, hinter der Existenz und Erscheinung stehendes, sondern die unmittelbare Wirklichkeit selbst, und diese als absolutes Reflektirtseyn in sich, als an und fürsichseyendes Bestehen.—Die Substanz als diese Einheit des Seyns und der Reflexion ist wesentlich das Scheinen und Gesetztseyn ihrer. Das Scheinen ist das sich auf sich beziehende Scheinen, so ist es; dieß Seyn ist die Substanz als solche. Umgekehrt ist dieses Seyn nur das mit sich identische Gesetztseyn, so ist es scheinende Totalität, die Accidentalität.\n\nDieß Scheinen ist die Identität als der Form;—die Einheit der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit. Sie ist erstlich Werden, die Zufälligkeit als die Sphäre des Entstehens und Vergehens; denn nach der Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit ist die Beziehung der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit unmittelbares Umschlagen derselben als Seyender in einander, eines jeden als in sein ihm nur Anderes.—Aber weil das Seyn Schein ist, so ist die Beziehung derselben auch als identischer oder scheinender an einander, Reflexion. Die Bewegung der Accidentalität stellt daher an jedem ihrer Momente das Scheinen der Kategorien des Seyns und der Reflexions-Bestimmungen des Wesens in einander dar.—Das unmittelbare Etwas hat einen Inhalt; seine Unmittelbarkeit ist zugleich reflektirte Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Form. Dieser Inhalt ist bestimmt, und indem dieß Bestimmtheit des Seyns ist, geht das Etwas über in ein Anderes. Aber die Qualität ist auch Bestimmtheit der Reflexion; so ist sie gleichgültige Verschiedenheit. Aber diese begeistet sich zur Entgegensetzung, und geht in den Grund zurück, der das Nichts, aber auch Reflexion-in-sich ist. Diese hebt sich auf; aber sie ist selbst reflektirtes Ansichseyn, so ist sie Möglichkeit und dieß Ansichseyn ist in seinem Übergehen, das ebenso sehr Reflexion-in-sich ist, das nothwendige Wirkliche.\n\nDiese Bewegung der Accidentalität ist die Aktuosität der Substanz, als ruhiges Hervorgehen ihrer selbst. Sie ist nicht thätig gegen Etwas, sondern nur gegen sich als einfaches widerstandloses Element. Das Aufheben eines Vorausgesetzten ist der verschwindende Schein; erst in dem das unmittelbare aufhebenden Thun wird dieß Unmittelbare selbst, oder ist jenes Scheinen; das Anfangen von sich selbst ist erst das Setzen dieses Selbsts, von dem das Anfangen ist.\n\nDie Substanz als diese Identität des Scheinens ist die Totalität des Ganzen, und begreift die Accidentalität in sich, und die Accidentalität ist die ganze Substanz selbst. Der Unterschied ihrer in die einfache Identität des Seyns, und in den Wechsel der Accidenzen an derselben ist eine Form ihres Scheins. Jenes ist die formlose Substanz des Vorstellens, dem der Schein sich nicht als Schein bestimmt hat, sondern das als an einem Absoluten an solcher unbestimmten Identität festhält, die keine Wahrheit hat, nur die Bestimmtheit der unmittelbaren Wirklichkeit oder ebenso des Ansichseyns oder der Möglichkeit ist;—Formbestimmungen, welche in die Accidentalität fallen.-Die andere Bestimmung, der Wechsel der Accidenzen, ist die absolute Formeinheit der Accidentalität, die Substanz als die absolute Macht.—Das Vergehen der Accidenz ist Zurückgehen ihrer als Wirklichkeit in sich als in ihr Ansichseyn oder in ihre Möglichkeit, aber dieß ihr Ansichseyn ist selbst nur ein Gesetztseyn; daher ist es auch Wirklichkeit, und weil diese Formbestimmungen ebenso sehr Inhaltsbestimmungen sind, ist dieß Mögliche auch dem Inhalte nach ein anders bestimmtes Wirkliches. Die Substanz manifestirt sich durch die Wirklichkeit mit ihrem Inhalte, in die sie das Mögliche übersetzt, als schaffende, durch die Möglichkeit, in die sie das Wirkliche zurückführt, als zerstörende Macht. Aber beides ist identisch; das Schaffen zerstörend, die Zerstörung schaffend; denn das Negative und Positive, die Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit sind in der substantiellen Nothwendigkeit absolut vereint.\n\nDie Accidenzen als solche,—und es sind mehrere, indem die Mehrheit eine der Bestimmungen des Seyns ist,—haben keine Macht über einander. Sie sind das seyende oder für sich seyende Etwas, existirende Dinge von mannigfaltigen Eigenschaften, oder Ganze, die aus Theilen bestehen, selbstständige Theile, Kräfte, die der Sollicitation durch einander bedürfen und einander zur Bedingung haben. Insofern ein solches Accidentelles über ein Anderes eine Macht auszuüben scheint, ist es die Macht der Substanz, welche beide in sich begreift, als Negativität einen ungleichen Werth setzt, das eine als Vo[e]rgehendes, das Andere mit anderem Inhalte und als Entstehendes, oder jenes in seine Möglichkeit, dieses daran in Wirklichkeit übergehend bestimmt; —ewig sich in diese Unterschiede der Form und des Inhalts entzweit und ewig sich von dieser Einseitigkeit reinigt, aber in dieser Reinigung selbst in die Bestimmung und Entzweiung zurückgefallen ist. —Eine Accidenz vertreibt also eine andere nur darum, weil ihr eigenes Subsistiren diese Totalität dar Form und des Inhalts selbst ist, in der sie wie ihre andere ebenso sehr untergeht.\n\nUm dieser unmittelbaren Identität und Gegenwart der Substanz in den Accidenzen willen ist noch kein realer Unterschied vorhanden. In dieser ersten Bestimmung ist die Substanz noch nicht nach ihrem ganzen Begriffe manifestirt. Wenn die Substanz als das mit sich identische An- und Fürsichseyn, von ihr selbst als Totalität der Accidenzen unterschieden wird, so ist sie als Macht das Vermittelnde. Diese ist die Nothwendigkeit, das in der Negativität der Accidenzen positive Beharren derselben, und ihr bloßes Gesetztseyn in ihrem Bestehen; diese Mitte ist somit Einheit der Substantialität und Accidentalität selbst, und ihre Extreme haben kein eigenthümliches Bestehen. Die Substantialität ist daher nur das Verhältniß als unmittelbar verschwindend, sie bezieht sich auf sich nicht als Negatives, ist als die unmittelbare Einheit der Macht mit sich selbst in der Form nur ihrer Identität, nicht ihres negativen Wesens; nur das eine Moment, nämlich das Negative oder der Unterschied, ist das schlechthin verschwindende, nicht aber das andere, das Identische. —Dieß ist auch so zu betrachten. Der Schein oder die Accidentalität ist an sich wohl Substanz durch die Macht, aber er ist nicht so gesetzt als dieser mit sich identische Schein; so hat die Substanz nur die Accidentalität zu ihrer Gestalt oder Gesetztseyn, nicht sich selbst; ist nicht Substanz als Substanz. Das Substantialitäts-Verhältniß ist also zunächst sie nur, daß sie sich als formelle Macht offenbart, deren Unterschiede nicht substantiell sind; sie ist in der That nur als Inneres der Accidenzen, und diese sind nur an der Substanz. Oder dieß Verhältniß ist nur die scheinende Totalität als Werden; aber sie ist ebenso sehr Reflexion; die Accidentalität, die an sich Substanz ist, ist eben darum auch gesetzt als solche; so ist sie bestimmt als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, gegen sich, bestimmt als sich auf sich beziehende einfache Identität mit sich; und ist für-sich-seyende, mächtige Substanz. So geht das Substantialitäts-Verhältniß in das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß über.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0001","text":"## Drittes Kapitel. Das absolute Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"162.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0002","text":"Die absolute Nothwendigkeit ist nicht sowohl das Nothwendige, noch weniger ein Nothwendiges, sondern Nothwendigkeit;—Seyn schlechthin als Reflexion. Sie ist Verhältniß, weil sie Unterscheiden ist, dessen Momente selbst ihre ganze Totalität sind, die also absolut bestehen, so daß dieß aber nur Ein Bestehen und der Unterschied nur der Schein des Auslegens, und dieser das Absolute selbst ist.—Das Wesen als solches ist die Reflexion oder das Scheinen; das Wesen als absolutes Verhältniß aber ist der als Schein gesetzte Schein, oder als dieß Beziehen auf sich die absolute Wirklichkeit ist.—Das Absolute, zuerst von der äußern Reflexion ausgelegt, legt nun als absolute Form oder als Nothwendigkeit, sich selbst aus; dieß Auslegen seiner selbst ist sein Sich-selbst-setzen, und es ist nur dieß Sich-setzen.—Wie das Licht der Natur nicht Etwas, noch Ding, sondern sein Seyn nur sein Scheinen ist, so","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"162.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0003","text":"ist die Manifestation die sich selbst gleiche absolute Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"162.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0004","text":"Die Seiten des absoluten Verhältnisses sind daher keine Attribute. Im Attribute scheint das Absolute nur in einem seiner Momente, als einem vorausgesetzten und von der äußern Reflexion aufgenommenen. Die Auslegerin des Absoluten aber ist die absolute Nothwendigkeit, die identisch mit sich ist, als sich selbst bestimmend. Da sie das Scheinen ist, das als Schein gesetzt ist, so sind die Seiten dieses Verhältnisses Totalitäten, weil sie als Schein sind; denn als Schein sind die Unterschiede sie selbst und ihr Entgegengesetztes, oder das Ganze;—umgekehrt sind sie so Schein, weil sie Totalitäten sind. Dieß Unterscheiden oder Scheinen des Absoluten ist so nur das identische Setzen seiner selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"162.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0005","text":"Dieß Verhältniß in seinem unmittelbaren Begriff ist das Verhältniß der Substanz und der Accidenzen, das unmittelbare Verschwinden und Werden des absoluten Scheines in sich selbst. Indem die Substanz sich zum Fürsichseyn gegen ein Anderes bestimmt, oder das absolute Verhältniß als reales, ist das Verhältniß der Kausalität. Endlich indem dieses als sich auf sich Beziehendes in Wechselwirkung übergeht, so ist damit das absolute Verhältniß nach den Bestimmungen, welche es enthält, auch gesetzt; diese gesetzte Einheit seiner in seinen Bestimmungen, die als das Ganze selbst und damit ebenso sehr als Bestimmungen gesetzt sind, ist alsdann der Begriff.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"162.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0006","text":"## A. Das Verhältniß der Substantialität.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"162.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0007","text":"Die absolute Nothwendigkeit ist absolutes Verhältniß, weil sie nicht das Seyn als solches ist, sondern das Seyn, das ist, weil es ist, das Seyn als die absolute Vermittelung seiner mit sich selbst. Dieses Seyn ist die Substanz; als die letzte Einheit des Wesens und Seyns, ist sie das Seyn in allem Seyn; weder das unreflektirte Unmittelbare, noch auch ein abstraktes, hinter der Existenz und Erscheinung stehendes, sondern die unmittelbare Wirklichkeit selbst, und diese als absolutes Reflektirtseyn in sich, als an und fürsichseyendes Bestehen.—Die Substanz als diese Einheit des Seyns und der Reflexion ist wesentlich das Scheinen und Gesetztseyn ihrer. Das Scheinen ist das sich auf sich beziehende Scheinen, so ist es; dieß Seyn ist die Substanz als solche. Umgekehrt ist dieses Seyn nur das mit sich identische Gesetztseyn, so ist es scheinende Totalität, die Accidentalität.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"162.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0008","text":"Dieß Scheinen ist die Identität als der Form;—die Einheit der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit. Sie ist erstlich Werden, die Zufälligkeit als die Sphäre des Entstehens und Vergehens; denn nach der Bestimmung der Unmittelbarkeit ist die Beziehung der Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit unmittelbares Umschlagen derselben als Seyender in einander, eines jeden als in sein ihm nur Anderes.—Aber weil das Seyn Schein ist, so ist die Beziehung derselben auch als identischer oder scheinender an einander, Reflexion. Die Bewegung der Accidentalität stellt daher an jedem ihrer Momente das Scheinen der Kategorien des Seyns und der Reflexions-Bestimmungen des Wesens in einander dar.—Das unmittelbare Etwas hat einen Inhalt; seine Unmittelbarkeit ist zugleich reflektirte Gleichgültigkeit gegen die Form. Dieser Inhalt ist bestimmt, und indem dieß Bestimmtheit des Seyns ist, geht das Etwas über in ein Anderes.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"162.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0009","text":"Aber die Qualität ist auch Bestimmtheit der Reflexion; so ist sie gleichgültige Verschiedenheit. Aber diese begeistet sich zur Entgegensetzung, und geht in den Grund zurück, der das Nichts, aber auch Reflexion-in-sich ist. Diese hebt sich auf; aber sie ist selbst reflektirtes Ansichseyn, so ist sie Möglichkeit und dieß Ansichseyn ist in seinem Übergehen, das ebenso sehr Reflexion-in-sich ist, das nothwendige Wirkliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"162.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0010","text":"Diese Bewegung der Accidentalität ist die Aktuosität der Substanz, als ruhiges Hervorgehen ihrer selbst. Sie ist nicht thätig gegen Etwas, sondern nur gegen sich als einfaches widerstandloses Element. Das Aufheben eines Vorausgesetzten ist der verschwindende Schein; erst in dem das unmittelbare aufhebenden Thun wird dieß Unmittelbare selbst, oder ist jenes Scheinen; das Anfangen von sich selbst ist erst das Setzen dieses Selbsts, von dem das Anfangen ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"162.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0011","text":"Die Substanz als diese Identität des Scheinens ist die Totalität des Ganzen, und begreift die Accidentalität in sich, und die Accidentalität ist die ganze Substanz selbst. Der Unterschied ihrer in die einfache Identität des Seyns, und in den Wechsel der Accidenzen an derselben ist eine Form ihres Scheins.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"162.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0012","text":"Jenes ist die formlose Substanz des Vorstellens, dem der Schein sich nicht als Schein bestimmt hat, sondern das als an einem Absoluten an solcher unbestimmten Identität festhält, die keine Wahrheit hat, nur die Bestimmtheit der unmittelbaren Wirklichkeit oder ebenso des Ansichseyns oder der Möglichkeit ist;—Formbestimmungen, welche in die Accidentalität fallen.-Die andere Bestimmung, der Wechsel der Accidenzen, ist die absolute Formeinheit der Accidentalität, die Substanz als die absolute Macht.—Das Vergehen der Accidenz ist Zurückgehen ihrer als Wirklichkeit in sich als in ihr Ansichseyn oder in ihre Möglichkeit, aber dieß ihr Ansichseyn ist selbst nur ein Gesetztseyn; daher ist es auch Wirklichkeit, und weil diese Formbestimmungen ebenso sehr Inhaltsbestimmungen sind, ist dieß Mögliche auch dem Inhalte nach ein anders bestimmtes Wirkliches.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"162.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0013","text":"Die Substanz manifestirt sich durch die Wirklichkeit mit ihrem Inhalte, in die sie das Mögliche übersetzt, als schaffende, durch die Möglichkeit, in die sie das Wirkliche zurückführt, als zerstörende Macht. Aber beides ist identisch; das Schaffen zerstörend, die Zerstörung schaffend; denn das Negative und Positive, die Möglichkeit und Wirklichkeit sind in der substantiellen Nothwendigkeit absolut vereint.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"162.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0014","text":"Die Accidenzen als solche,—und es sind mehrere, indem die Mehrheit eine der Bestimmungen des Seyns ist,—haben keine Macht über einander. Sie sind das seyende oder für sich seyende Etwas, existirende Dinge von mannigfaltigen Eigenschaften, oder Ganze, die aus Theilen bestehen, selbstständige Theile, Kräfte, die der Sollicitation durch einander bedürfen und einander zur Bedingung haben.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"162.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0015","text":"Insofern ein solches Accidentelles über ein Anderes eine Macht auszuüben scheint, ist es die Macht der Substanz, welche beide in sich begreift, als Negativität einen ungleichen Werth setzt, das eine als Vo[e]rgehendes, das Andere mit anderem Inhalte und als Entstehendes, oder jenes in seine Möglichkeit, dieses daran in Wirklichkeit übergehend bestimmt; —ewig sich in diese Unterschiede der Form und des Inhalts entzweit und ewig sich von dieser Einseitigkeit reinigt, aber in dieser Reinigung selbst in die Bestimmung und Entzweiung zurückgefallen ist. —Eine Accidenz vertreibt also eine andere nur darum, weil ihr eigenes Subsistiren diese Totalität dar Form und des Inhalts selbst ist, in der sie wie ihre andere ebenso sehr untergeht.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"162.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0016","text":"Um dieser unmittelbaren Identität und Gegenwart der Substanz in den Accidenzen willen ist noch kein realer Unterschied vorhanden. In dieser ersten Bestimmung ist die Substanz noch nicht nach ihrem ganzen Begriffe manifestirt. Wenn die Substanz als das mit sich identische An- und Fürsichseyn, von ihr selbst als Totalität der Accidenzen unterschieden wird, so ist sie als Macht das Vermittelnde. Diese ist die Nothwendigkeit, das in der Negativität der Accidenzen positive Beharren derselben, und ihr bloßes Gesetztseyn in ihrem Bestehen; diese Mitte ist somit Einheit der Substantialität und Accidentalität selbst, und ihre Extreme haben kein eigenthümliches Bestehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"162.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0017","text":"Die Substantialität ist daher nur das Verhältniß als unmittelbar verschwindend, sie bezieht sich auf sich nicht als Negatives, ist als die unmittelbare Einheit der Macht mit sich selbst in der Form nur ihrer Identität, nicht ihres negativen Wesens; nur das eine Moment, nämlich das Negative oder der Unterschied, ist das schlechthin verschwindende, nicht aber das andere, das Identische. —Dieß ist auch so zu betrachten. Der Schein oder die Accidentalität ist an sich wohl Substanz durch die Macht, aber er ist nicht so gesetzt als dieser mit sich identische Schein; so hat die Substanz nur die Accidentalität zu ihrer Gestalt oder Gesetztseyn, nicht sich selbst; ist nicht Substanz als Substanz.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"162.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0018","text":"Das Substantialitäts-Verhältniß ist also zunächst sie nur, daß sie sich als formelle Macht offenbart, deren Unterschiede nicht substantiell sind; sie ist in der That nur als Inneres der Accidenzen, und diese sind nur an der Substanz. Oder dieß Verhältniß ist nur die scheinende Totalität als Werden; aber sie ist ebenso sehr Reflexion; die Accidentalität, die an sich Substanz ist, ist eben darum auch gesetzt als solche; so ist sie bestimmt als sich auf sich beziehende Negativität, gegen sich, bestimmt als sich auf sich beziehende einfache Identität mit sich; und ist für-sich-seyende, mächtige Substanz. So geht das Substantialitäts-Verhältniß in das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß über.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"162.18"}],"sha256":"b91fa53451d49b060c1a47a1ff3d9640f2df9ecce3767fe359bfbcdeefb79836","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110033608519Z_867dc1fa","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. The Relation of Substantiality.","source_sha256":"b91fa53451d49b060c1a47a1ff3d9640f2df9ecce3767fe359bfbcdeefb79836","sha256":"641f5c90a98660adbb81ffd43c19b029c5f5c31479d68ca10b21e4ae9487757c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:00:33.608544+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0001","text":"## Third Chapter. The Absolute Relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"162.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0002","text":"Absolute necessity is not so much the necessary, still less a necessary [thing], but necessity;—Being simply as reflection. It is relation, because it is distinguishing, whose moments are themselves their entire totality, which therefore subsist absolutely, so that this, however, is only one subsistence and the difference only the semblance of explication, and this is the Absolute itself.—Essence as such is reflection or shining; but essence as absolute relation is the shining posited as semblance, or, as this relating itself to itself, is absolute actuality.—The Absolute, at first explicated by external reflection, now explicates itself as absolute form or as necessity; this explication of itself is its self-positing, and it is only this self-positing.—Just as the light of nature is not something, nor a thing, but its Being is only its shining, so","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"162.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0003","text":"is manifestation the absolute actuality equal to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"162.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0004","text":"The sides of the absolute relation are therefore not attributes. In the attribute the Absolute shines only in one of its moments, as one presupposed and taken up by external reflection. But the explicator of the Absolute is absolute necessity, which is identical with itself as self-determining. Since it is shining that is posited as semblance, the sides of this relation are totalities, because they are as semblance; for as semblance the differences are themselves and their opposite, or the whole;—conversely, they are semblance in this way, because they are totalities. This distinguishing or shining of the Absolute is thus only the identical positing of itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"162.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0005","text":"This relation in its immediate Concept is the relation of substance and accidents, the immediate vanishing and becoming of absolute semblance within itself. In that substance determines itself to being-for-self over against an other, or the absolute relation as real, it is the relation of causality. Finally, in that this, as relating itself to itself, passes over into reciprocal action, the absolute relation is thereby also posited according to the determinations which it contains; this posited unity of itself in its determinations, which are posited as the whole itself and thereby equally as determinations, is then the Concept.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"162.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0006","text":"## A. The Relation of Substantiality.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"162.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0007","text":"Absolute necessity is absolute relation, because it is not Being as such, but Being that is because it is, Being as the absolute mediation of itself with itself. This Being is substance; as the ultimate unity of essence and Being, it is Being in all Being; neither the unreflected immediate, nor an abstraction standing behind existence and appearance, but immediate actuality itself, and this as absolute reflectedness into itself, as subsistence being in-and-for-itself.—Substance as this unity of Being and reflection is essentially its shining and its positedness. Shining is shining that relates itself to itself; thus it is; this Being is substance as such. Conversely, this Being is only positedness identical with itself; thus it is shining totality, accidentality.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"162.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0008","text":"This shining is identity as form;—the unity of possibility and actuality. It is at first becoming, contingency as the sphere of arising and passing away; for according to the determination of immediacy, the relation of possibility and actuality is the immediate passing-over of these, as Beings, into one another, of each into its merely other.—But because Being is semblance, their relation is also, as identical or shining in one another, reflection. The movement of accidentality therefore exhibits in each of its moments the shining of the categories of Being and of the reflection-determinations of essence into one another.—The immediate something has a content; its immediacy is at the same time reflected indifference toward form. This content is determinate, and in that this is determinateness of Being, the something passes over into an other.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"162.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0009","text":"But quality is also determinateness of reflection; thus it is indifferent diversity. But this animates itself into opposition, and goes back into the ground, which is nothing, but also reflection-into-itself. This sublates itself; but it is itself reflected being-in-itself, and thus it is possibility, and this being-in-itself is, in its passing-over—which is equally reflection-into-itself—the necessary actual.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"162.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0010","text":"This movement of accidentality is the activity of substance, as the tranquil emergence of itself. It is not active against something, but only against itself as a simple element without resistance. The sublation of something presupposed is vanishing semblance; only in the act that sublates the immediate does this immediate itself become, or is, that shining; beginning from itself is only the positing of this self, from which the beginning is.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"162.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0011","text":"Substance, as this identity of shining, is the totality of the whole, and comprehends accidentality within itself, and accidentality is the whole substance itself. Their difference into the simple identity of Being and into the alternation of accidents in it is a form of its semblance.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"162.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0012","text":"The former is the formless substance of representation, for which semblance has not determined itself as semblance, but which holds fast, as to an Absolute, to such indeterminate identity, which has no truth, but is only the determinateness of immediate actuality or equally of being-in-itself or of possibility;—form-determinations which fall within accidentality.—The other determination, the alternation of accidents, is the absolute unity of form of accidentality, substance as absolute power.—The passing away of accident is its return, as actuality, into itself as into its being-in-itself or into its possibility; but this its being-in-itself is itself only a positedness; hence it is also actuality, and because these form-determinations are equally determinations of content, this possible is also, as regards content, an actually determinate other.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"162.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0013","text":"Substance manifests itself through actuality with its content, into which it translates the possible, as creative power; through possibility, into which it leads actuality back, as destructive power. But both are identical; creation destructive, destruction creative; for the negative and positive, possibility and actuality, are absolutely united in substantial necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"162.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0014","text":"Accidents as such,—and there are several, since plurality is one of the determinations of Being,—have no power over one another. They are the being or being-for-self something, existing things with manifold properties, or wholes consisting of parts, self-subsistent parts, forces which require solicitation by one another and have one another as their condition.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"162.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0015","text":"Insofar as such an accidental seems to exercise a power over another, it is the power of substance, which comprehends both within itself, which, as negativity, posits an unequal value, determining the one as pre[e]xisting, the other as arising with another content, or the former as passing over into its possibility, the latter thereby into actuality;—eternally dividing itself into these differences of form and content and eternally purifying itself from this one-sidedness, but in this purification itself having fallen back into determination and division.—Thus one accident drives out another only because its own subsistence is itself this totality of form and content, in which it equally perishes like its other.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"162.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0016","text":"By virtue of this immediate identity and presence of substance in the accidents, no real difference is yet present. In this first determination substance is not yet manifested according to its entire Concept. When substance, as being-in-and-for-itself identical with itself, is distinguished from itself as the totality of accidents, it is, as power, the mediating term. This is necessity, the positive persistence of the accidents in their negativity, and their mere positedness in their subsistence; this middle is thus the unity of substantiality and accidentality itself, and its extremes have no peculiar subsistence.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"162.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0017","text":"Substantiality is therefore only the relation as immediately vanishing; it does not relate itself to itself as negative, is the immediate unity of power with itself in the form only of its identity, not of its negative essence; only the one moment, namely the negative or difference, is what absolutely vanishes, but not the other, the identical.—This is also to be considered thus. Semblance or accidentality is indeed substance in itself through power, but it is not thus posited as this semblance identical with itself; thus substance has only accidentality as its shape or positedness, not itself; it is not substance as substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"162.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0018","text":"The relation of substantiality, therefore, is at first only this: that it manifests itself as formal power, whose differences are not substantial; it is in fact only as the inwardness of accidents, and these are only in substance. Or this relation is only shining totality as becoming; but it is equally reflection; accidentality, which is substance in itself, is precisely for that reason also posited as such; thus it is determined as negativity relating itself to itself, against itself determined as simple identity relating itself to itself; and is substance being-for-itself, powerful. Thus the relation of substantiality passes over into the relation of causality.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"162.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DV_2:P0018"]}],"source_digest":"73b9085f5333b037bb539259976bdee72ad2a1503aba07d15fccb5e24b9abe35","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Das Verhältniß der Substantialität."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"A. Das Verhältniß der Substantialität.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDKT","title":"B. The Causal Relation.","order":163,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDKT","text":"Die Substanz ist Macht, und in sich reflektirte nicht bloß übergehende, sondern die Bestimmungen setzende und von sich unterscheidende Macht. Als in ihrem Bestimmen sich auf sich selbst beziehend ist sie selbst das, was sie als negatives setzt oder zum Gesetztseyn macht. Dieses ist somit überhaupt die aufgehobene Substantialität, das nur Gesetzte, die Wirkung; die für sich seyende Substanz aber ist die Ursache.\n\nDieß Kausalitätsverhältniß ist zunächst nur dieß Verhältniß von Ursache und Wirkung; so ist es das formelle Kausalitäts-Verhältniß.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDKT:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Die Substanz ist Macht, und in sich reflektirte nicht bloß übergehende, sondern die Bestimmungen setzende und von sich unterscheidende Macht. Als in ihrem Bestimmen sich auf sich selbst beziehend ist sie selbst das, was sie als negatives setzt oder zum Gesetztseyn macht. Dieses ist somit überhaupt die aufgehobene Substantialität, das nur Gesetzte, die Wirkung; die für sich seyende Substanz aber ist die Ursache.","kind":"display"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDKT:DISPLAY-0002","text":"Dieß Kausalitätsverhältniß ist zunächst nur dieß Verhältniß von Ursache und Wirkung; so ist es das formelle Kausalitäts-Verhältniß.","kind":"display"}],"sha256":"77edb038bf839c458fac70058f4349ba5c8b2e66f48810b705035f130bd789d2","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110036430339Z_51cf617f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. The Causal Relation.","source_sha256":"77edb038bf839c458fac70058f4349ba5c8b2e66f48810b705035f130bd789d2","sha256":"1837b198ff57015a4f17081e9831d71bda49163b5a805fbc6441bd5ab2089ee4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:00:36.430408+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDKT:DISPLAY-0001","text":"Substance is power, and power reflected into itself, not merely transitory, but positing determinations and distinguishing itself from itself. As relating itself to itself in its determining, it is itself that which it posits as negative or makes into positedness. This is thus, in general, sublated substantiality, the merely posited, the effect; but substance that is for itself is the cause.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDKT:DISPLAY-0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDKT:DISPLAY-0002","text":"This relation of causality is at first only this relation of cause and effect; thus it is the formal relation of causality.","kind":"display","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDKT:DISPLAY-0002"]}],"source_digest":"922168ab3742028dc68317f32bc914c1b137e1e8a40f7f726d97b7c6eacc1f5a","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"B. Das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß."}],"original_title":"B. Das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT","title":"a. Formal Causality.","order":164,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_DFKT","text":"1. Die Ursache ist das Ursprüngliche gegen die Wirkung.—Die Substanz ist als Macht das Scheinen, oder hat Accidentalität. Aber sie ist als Macht ebenso sehr Reflexion-in-sich in ihrem Scheine; so legt sie ihr Übergehen aus, und dieß Scheinen ist bestimmt als Schein, oder die Accidenz ist gesetzt, als das, daß sie nur ein Gesetztes sey. —Die Substanz geht aber in ihrem Bestimmen nicht von der Accidentalität aus, als ob diese voraus ein Anderes wäre, und nun erst als Bestimmtheit gesetzt würde, son dern beides ist Eine Aktuosität. Die Substanz, als Macht bestimmt sich; aber dieß Bestimmen ist unmittelbar selbst das Aufheben des Bestimmens und die Rückkehr. Sie bestimmt sich,—sie, das Bestimmende ist so das Unmittelbare, und das selbst schon Bestimmte;—indem sie sich bestimmt, setzt sie also dieß schon Bestimmte als bestimmt; hat so das Gesetztseyn aufgehoben, und ist in sich zurückgekehrt.—Umgekehrt ist diese Rückkehr, weil sie die negative Beziehung der Substanz auf sich ist, selbst ein Bestimmen oder Abstoßen ihrer von sich; durch diese Rückkehr wird das Bestimmte, von dem sie anzufangen und es als vorgefundenes Bestimmtes nun als solches zu setzen scheint.—So ist die absolute Actuosität Ursache;—die Macht der Substanz in ihrer Wahrheit als Manifestation, die das, was an sich ist, die Accidenz, die das Gesetztseyn ist, unmittelbar im Werden derselben auch auslegt, sie setzt als Gesetztseyn; die Wirkung.—Diese ist also erstlich dasselbe, was die Accidentalität des Substantialitäts-Verhältnisses ist, nämlich die Substanz als Gesetztseyn; aber zweitens ist die Accidenz als solche substantiell nur durch ihr Verschwinden, als Übergehendes; als Wirkung aber ist sie das Gesetztseyn als mit sich identisch; die Ursache ist in der Wirkung als ganze Substanz manifestirt, nämlich als an dem Gesetztseyn selbst als solchem in sich reflektirt.\n\n2. Diesem in sich reflektirten Gesetztseyn, dem Bestimmten als Bestimmten, steht die Substanz als nicht gesetztes Ursprüngliches gegenüber. Weil sie als absolute Macht Rückkehr in sich, aber diese Rückkehr selbst Bestimmen ist, so ist sie nicht mehr bloß das An-sich ihrer Accidenz, sondern ist auch gesetzt als dieß Ansichseyn. Die Substanz hat daher erst als Ursache Wirklichkeit. Aber diese Wirklichkeit, daß ihr Ansichseyn, ihre Bestimmtheit im Substantialitäts-Verhältnisse, nunmehr als Bestimmtheit gesetzt ist, ist die Wirkung; die Substanz hat daher die Wirklichkeit, die sie als Ursache hat, nur in ihrer Wirkung.—Dieß ist die Nothwendigkeit, welche die Ursache ist.—Sie ist die wirkliche Substanz, weil die Substanz als Macht sich selbst bestimmt; aber ist zugleich Ursache, weil sie diese Bestimmtheit auslegt oder als Gesetztseyn setzt; so setzt sie ihre Wirklichkeit als das Gesetztseyn oder als die Wirkung. Diese ist das Andere der Ursache, das Gesetztseyn gegen das Ursprüngliche und durch dieses vermittelt. Aber die Ursache hebt als Nothwendigkeit ebenso dieß ihr Vermitteln auf, und ist in dem Bestimmen ihrer selbst als das ursprünglich sich auf sich beziehende gegen das Vermittelte, die Rückkehr in sich; denn das Gesetztseyn ist als Gesetztseyn bestimmt, somit identisch mit sich; die Ursache ist daher erst in ihrer Wirkung das wahrhaft Wirkliche und mit sich Identische.—Die Wirkung ist daher nothwendig, weil sie eben Manifestation der Ursache, oder diese Nothwendigkeit ist, welche die Ursache ist.—Nur als diese Nothwendigkeit ist die Ursache selbst bewegend, aus sich anfangend, ohne von einem Andern sollicitirt zu werden, und selbstständige Quelle des Hervorbringens aus sich;—sie muß wirken, ihre Ursprünglichkeit ist dieß, daß ihre Reflexion-in-sich bestimmendes Setzen und umgekehrt, beides eine Einheit ist.\n\nDie Wirkung enthält daher überhaupt nichts, was nicht die Ursache enthält. Umgekehrt enthält die Ursache nichts, was nicht in ihrer Wirkung ist. Die Ursache ist nur Ursache, insofern sie eine Wirkung hervorbringt; und die Ursache ist nichts als diese Bestimmung, eine Wirkung zu haben, und die Wirkung nichts, als dieß, eine Ursache zu haben. In der Ursache als solcher selbst liegt ihre Wirkung, und in der Wirkung die Ursache; insofern die Ursache noch nicht wirkte, oder insofern sie aufgehört hätte zu wirken, so wäre sie nicht Ursache; —und die Wirkung, insofern ihre Ursache verschwunden ist, ist nicht mehr Wirkung, sondern eine gleichgültige Wirklichkeit.-3. In dieser Identität der Ursache und Wirkung ist nun die Form, wodurch sie als das an sich seyende und als das Gesetztseyn sich unterscheiden, aufgehoben. Die Ursache erlischt in ihrer Wirkung; damit ist ebenso die Wirkung erloschen, denn sie ist nur die Bestimmtheit der Ursache. Diese in der Wirkung erloschene Kausalität ist somit eine Unmittelbarkeit, welche gegen das Verhältniß von Ursache und Wirkung gleichgültig ist, und es äußerlich an ihr hat.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0001","text":"1. Die Ursache ist das Ursprüngliche gegen die Wirkung.—Die Substanz ist als Macht das Scheinen, oder hat Accidentalität. Aber sie ist als Macht ebenso sehr Reflexion-in-sich in ihrem Scheine; so legt sie ihr Übergehen aus, und dieß Scheinen ist bestimmt als Schein, oder die Accidenz ist gesetzt, als das, daß sie nur ein Gesetztes sey. —Die Substanz geht aber in ihrem Bestimmen nicht von der Accidentalität aus, als ob diese voraus ein Anderes wäre, und nun erst als Bestimmtheit gesetzt würde, son dern beides ist Eine Aktuosität. Die Substanz, als Macht bestimmt sich; aber dieß Bestimmen ist unmittelbar selbst das Aufheben des Bestimmens und die Rückkehr.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"164.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0002","text":"Sie bestimmt sich,—sie, das Bestimmende ist so das Unmittelbare, und das selbst schon Bestimmte;—indem sie sich bestimmt, setzt sie also dieß schon Bestimmte als bestimmt; hat so das Gesetztseyn aufgehoben, und ist in sich zurückgekehrt.—Umgekehrt ist diese Rückkehr, weil sie die negative Beziehung der Substanz auf sich ist, selbst ein Bestimmen oder Abstoßen ihrer von sich; durch diese Rückkehr wird das Bestimmte, von dem sie anzufangen und es als vorgefundenes Bestimmtes nun als solches zu setzen scheint.—So ist die absolute Actuosität Ursache;—die Macht der Substanz in ihrer Wahrheit als Manifestation, die das, was an sich ist, die Accidenz, die das Gesetztseyn ist, unmittelbar im Werden derselben auch auslegt, sie setzt als Gesetztseyn; die Wirkung.—Diese ist also erstlich dasselbe, was die Accidentalität des Substantialitäts-Verhältnisses ist, nämlich die Substanz als Gesetztseyn;","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"164.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0003","text":"aber zweitens ist die Accidenz als solche substantiell nur durch ihr Verschwinden, als Übergehendes; als Wirkung aber ist sie das Gesetztseyn als mit sich identisch; die Ursache ist in der Wirkung als ganze Substanz manifestirt, nämlich als an dem Gesetztseyn selbst als solchem in sich reflektirt.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"164.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0004","text":"2. Diesem in sich reflektirten Gesetztseyn, dem Bestimmten als Bestimmten, steht die Substanz als nicht gesetztes Ursprüngliches gegenüber. Weil sie als absolute Macht Rückkehr in sich, aber diese Rückkehr selbst Bestimmen ist, so ist sie nicht mehr bloß das An-sich ihrer Accidenz, sondern ist auch gesetzt als dieß Ansichseyn. Die Substanz hat daher erst als Ursache Wirklichkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"164.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0005","text":"Aber diese Wirklichkeit, daß ihr Ansichseyn, ihre Bestimmtheit im Substantialitäts-Verhältnisse, nunmehr als Bestimmtheit gesetzt ist, ist die Wirkung; die Substanz hat daher die Wirklichkeit, die sie als Ursache hat, nur in ihrer Wirkung.—Dieß ist die Nothwendigkeit, welche die Ursache ist.—Sie ist die wirkliche Substanz, weil die Substanz als Macht sich selbst bestimmt; aber ist zugleich Ursache, weil sie diese Bestimmtheit auslegt oder als Gesetztseyn setzt; so setzt sie ihre Wirklichkeit als das Gesetztseyn oder als die Wirkung. Diese ist das Andere der Ursache, das Gesetztseyn gegen das Ursprüngliche und durch dieses vermittelt.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"164.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0006","text":"Aber die Ursache hebt als Nothwendigkeit ebenso dieß ihr Vermitteln auf, und ist in dem Bestimmen ihrer selbst als das ursprünglich sich auf sich beziehende gegen das Vermittelte, die Rückkehr in sich; denn das Gesetztseyn ist als Gesetztseyn bestimmt, somit identisch mit sich; die Ursache ist daher erst in ihrer Wirkung das wahrhaft Wirkliche und mit sich Identische.—Die Wirkung ist daher nothwendig, weil sie eben Manifestation der Ursache, oder diese Nothwendigkeit ist, welche die Ursache ist.—Nur als diese Nothwendigkeit ist die Ursache selbst bewegend, aus sich anfangend, ohne von einem Andern sollicitirt zu werden, und selbstständige Quelle des Hervorbringens aus sich;—sie muß wirken, ihre Ursprünglichkeit ist dieß, daß ihre Reflexion-in-sich bestimmendes Setzen und umgekehrt, beides eine Einheit ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"164.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0007","text":"Die Wirkung enthält daher überhaupt nichts, was nicht die Ursache enthält. Umgekehrt enthält die Ursache nichts, was nicht in ihrer Wirkung ist. Die Ursache ist nur Ursache, insofern sie eine Wirkung hervorbringt; und die Ursache ist nichts als diese Bestimmung, eine Wirkung zu haben, und die Wirkung nichts, als dieß, eine Ursache zu haben. In der Ursache als solcher selbst liegt ihre Wirkung, und in der Wirkung die Ursache; insofern die Ursache noch nicht wirkte, oder insofern sie aufgehört hätte zu wirken, so wäre sie nicht Ursache; —und die Wirkung, insofern ihre Ursache verschwunden ist, ist nicht mehr Wirkung, sondern eine gleichgültige Wirklichkeit.-3. In dieser Identität der Ursache und Wirkung ist nun die Form, wodurch sie als das an sich seyende und als das Gesetztseyn sich unterscheiden, aufgehoben.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"164.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0008","text":"Die Ursache erlischt in ihrer Wirkung; damit ist ebenso die Wirkung erloschen, denn sie ist nur die Bestimmtheit der Ursache. Diese in der Wirkung erloschene Kausalität ist somit eine Unmittelbarkeit, welche gegen das Verhältniß von Ursache und Wirkung gleichgültig ist, und es äußerlich an ihr hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"164.8"}],"sha256":"e888ce2dfb29fbb9b1d99d2e9f890294c58677bd30766571437029af7263febc","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110048140367Z_ffd1f4c8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"a. Formal Causality.","source_sha256":"e888ce2dfb29fbb9b1d99d2e9f890294c58677bd30766571437029af7263febc","sha256":"0f8912269476c8c35396c8f8bc51a6effab71af846409cceb28bbc4cd03b0668","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:00:48.140397+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0001","text":"1. The cause is the original as against the effect.—Substance, as power, is semblance, or has accidentality. But as power it is equally reflection-into-self in its semblance; thus it explicates its transition, and this semblance is determined as semblance, or the accident is posited as that which is only a positedness. —But in its determining substance does not proceed from accidentality as though this were beforehand an other and were only then posited as determinacy, but both are one actuosity. Substance, as power, determines itself; but this determining is immediately itself the sublation of determining and the return.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"164.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0002","text":"It determines itself,—it, the determining, is thus the immediate, and itself already determined;—in determining itself, it thus posits this already determined as determined; it has thus sublated positedness, and has returned into itself.—Conversely, this return, because it is the negative relation of substance to itself, is itself a determining or a repelling of itself from itself; through this return the determined becomes that from which it seems to begin and which it now posits as such, as a determinate found present.—Thus absolute actuosity is cause;—the power of substance in its truth as manifestation, which also immediately explicates, in the becoming of the same, that which is in itself, the accident, which is positedness; it posits it as positedness; the effect.—This is therefore, first, the same as what the accidentality of the relation of substantiality is, namely, substance as positedness;","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"164.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0003","text":"but secondly, the accident as such is substantial only through its vanishing, as something transitioning; as effect, however, it is positedness as identical with itself; the cause is manifest in the effect as whole substance, namely, as reflected into itself in positedness itself as such.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"164.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0004","text":"2. Substance, as unposited original, stands opposed to this positedness reflected into itself, to the determined as determined. Since, as absolute power, it is return into itself, but this return is itself determining, it is no longer merely the in-itself of its accident, but is also posited as this being-in-itself. Thus it is only as cause that substance has actuality.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"164.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0005","text":"But this actuality, that its being-in-itself, its determinacy in the relation of substantiality, is now posited as determinacy, is the effect; substance therefore has the actuality which it has as cause only in its effect.—This is necessity, which is the cause.—It is actual substance, because substance as power determines itself; but it is at the same time cause, because it explicates this determinacy or posits it as positedness; thus it posits its actuality as positedness or as the effect. This is the other of the cause, positedness as against the original and mediated through it.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"164.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0006","text":"But as necessity the cause equally sublates this its mediating, and in the determining of itself is, as that which originally relates itself to itself, as against the mediated, the return into itself; for positedness is determined as positedness, thus identical with itself; the cause is therefore only in its effect the truly actual and identical with itself.—The effect is therefore necessary, because it is precisely manifestation of the cause, or this necessity which is the cause.—Only as this necessity is the cause itself moving, beginning from itself, without being solicited by an other, and the independent source of production from itself;—it must act; its originality is this, that its reflection-into-self is determining positing and conversely, both are one unity.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"164.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0007","text":"The effect therefore contains in general nothing that the cause does not contain. Conversely, the cause contains nothing that is not in its effect. The cause is cause only insofar as it brings forth an effect; and the cause is nothing but this determinacy, to have an effect, and the effect nothing but this, to have a cause. In the cause as such itself lies its effect, and in the effect the cause; insofar as the cause had not yet acted, or insofar as it had ceased to act, it would not be cause; —and the effect, insofar as its cause has vanished, is no longer effect, but an indifferent actuality.—3. In this identity of cause and effect, the form through which they distinguish themselves as that which is in itself and as positedness is now sublated.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"164.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0008","text":"The cause is extinguished in its effect; with this the effect is likewise extinguished, for it is only the determinacy of the cause. This causality extinguished in the effect is thus an immediacy which is indifferent to the relation of cause and effect, and has it external to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"164.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_DFKT:P0008"]}],"source_digest":"61244df1da845ca56f2ade540d4334a07902265a573029bda163a6103a2f004c","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"a. Die formelle Kausalität."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"a. Die formelle Kausalität.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK","title":"b. The Determinate Causal Relation.","order":165,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_BDBK","text":"1. Die Identität der Ursache in ihrer Wirkung mit sich ist das Aufheben ihrer Macht und Negativität, daher die gegen die Formunterschiede gleichgültige Einheit, der Inhalt.—Er ist daher nur an sich auf die Form, hier die Kausalität, bezogen. Sie sind somit als verschieden gesetzt, und die Form gegen den Inhalt eine selbst nur unmittelbar wirkliche, eine zufällige Kausalität.\n\nFerner der Inhalt so als bestimmtes, ist ein verschiedener Inhalt an ihm selbst; und die Ursache ist ihrem Inhalte nach bestimmt, damit ebenso die Wirkung.—Der Inhalt, da das Reflektirtseyn hier auch unmittelbare Wirklichkeit ist, ist insofern wirkliche, aber die endliche Substanz.\n\nDieß ist nunmehr das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß in seiner Realität und Endlichkeit. Als formell ist es das unendliche Verhältniß der absoluten Macht, deren Inhalt die reine Manifestation oder Nothwendigkeit ist. Als endliche Kausalität hingegen hat es einen gegebenen Inhalt, und verläuft sich als ein äußerlicher Unterschied an diesem Identischen, das in seinen Bestimmungen eine und dieselbe Substanz ist.\n\nDurch diese Identität des Inhalts ist diese Kausalität ein analytischer Satz. Es ist dieselbe Sache, welche sich das eine Mal als Ursache, das andere Mal als Wirkung darstellt, dort als eigenthümliches Bestehen, hier als Gesetztseyn oder Bestimmung an einem Andern. Da diese Bestimmungen der Form äußerliche Reflexion sind, so ist es die der Sache nach tautologische Betrachtung eines subjektiven Verstandes, eine Erscheinung als Wirkung zu bestimmen und davon zu ihrer Ursache aufzusteigen, um sie zu begreifen und zu erklären; es wird nur ein und derselbe Inhalt wiederhohlt; man hat in der Ursache nichts Anderes als in der Wirkung.—Der Regen z.B. ist Ursache der Feuchtigkeit, welche seine Wirkung ist;—der Regen macht naß, dieß ist ein analytischer Satz; dasselbe Wasser, was der Regen ist, ist die Feuchtigkeit; als Regen ist dieß Wasser nur in der Form einer Sache für sich, als Wässerigkeit oder Feuchtigkeit dagegen ist es ein adjectives, ein gesetztes, das nicht mehr sein Bestehen an ihm selbst haben soll; und die eine Bestimmung, wie die andere, ist ihm äußerlich.—So ist die Ursache dieser Farbe ein Färbendes, ein Pigment, welches eine und dieselbe Wirklichkeit ist, das eine Mal in der ihm äußern Form eines thätigen, das heißt, mit einem von ihm verschiedenen Thätigen äußerlich verbunden, das andere Mal aber in der ihm ebenso äußerlichen Bestimmung einer Wirkung.—Die Ursache einer That ist die innere Gesinnung in einem thätigen Subjekt, die als äußeres Daseyn, das sie durch die Handlung erhält, derselbe Inhalt und Werth ist. Wenn die Bewegung eines Körpers als Wirkung betrachtet wird, so ist die Ursache derselben eine stoßende Kraft; aber es ist dasselbe Quantum der Bewegung, das vor und nach dem Stoß vorhanden ist, dieselbe Existenz, welche der stoßende Körper enthielt, und dem gestoßenen mittheilte; und so viel er mittheilt, so viel verliert er selbst.\n\nDie Ursache, z.B. der Mahler, oder der stoßende Körper hat wohl noch einen andern Inhalt, jener, als die Farben und deren sie zum Gemälde verbindende Form; dieser, als eine Bewegung von bestimmter Stärke und Richtung. Allein dieser weitere Inhalt ist ein zufälliges Beiwesen, das die Ursache nichts angeht; was der Maler sonst für Qualitäten enthält, abstrahirt davon, daß er Maler dieses Gemäldes ist, dieß tritt nicht in dieses Gemälde ein; nur was von seinen Eigenschaften sich in der Wirkung darstellt, ist in ihm als Ursache vorhanden, nach seinen übrigen Eigenschaften ist er nicht Ursache. So ob der stoßende Körper Stein oder Holz, grün, gelb ist u.s.f. dieß tritt nicht in seinen Stoß ein; insofern ist er nicht Ursache.\n\nEs ist in Rücksicht dieser Tautologie des Kausalitäts-Verhältnisses zu bemerken, daß es dieselbe dann nicht zu enthalten scheint, wenn nicht die nächste, sondern die entfernte Ursache einer Wirkung angegeben wird. Die Formveränderung, welche die zu Grunde liegende Sache in diesem Durchgange durch mehrere Mittelglieder erleidet, versteckt die Identität, die sie darin behält. Sie verknüpft sich zugleich in dieser Vervielfältigung der Ursachen, welche zwischen sie und die letzte Wirkung eingetreten sind, mit andern Dingen und Umständen, so daß nicht jenes Erste, was als Ursache ausgesprochen wird, sondern nur diese mehrere Ursachen zusammen die vollständige Wirkung enthalten.—So wenn z. ein Mensch dadurch unter Umstände kam, in denen sich sein Talent entwickelte, daß er seinen Vater verlor, den in einer Schlacht eine Kugel traf, so könnte dieser Schuß, (oder noch weiter zurück der Krieg oder eine Ursache des Kriegs und so fort ins Unendliche) als Ursache der Geschicklichkeit jenes Menschen angegeben werden. Allein es erhellt, daß z.B. jener Schuß nicht für sich diese Ursache ist, sondern nur die Verknüpfung desselben mit andern wirkenden Bestimmungen. Oder vielmehr ist er überhaupt nicht Ursache, sondern nur ein einzelnes Moment, das zu den Umständen der Möglichkeit gehörte.\n\nDenn hauptsächlich ist noch die unstatthafte Anwendung des Kausalitätsverhältnisses auf Verhältnisse des physisch-organischen und des geistigen Lebens zu bemerken. Hier zeigt sich das, was als Ursache genannt wird, freilich von anderem Inhalte als die Wirkung, darum aber, weil das, was auf das Lebendige wirkt, von diesem selbstständig bestimmt, verändert und verwandelt wird, weil das Lebendige die Ursache nicht zu ihrer Wirkung kommen läßt, das heißt, sie als Ursache aufhebt. So ist es unstatthaft gesprochen, daß die Nahrung die Ursache des Bluts, oder diese Speisen oder Kälte, Nässe, Ursachen des Fiebers u.s.fort seyen; so unstatthaft es ist, das jonische Klima als die Ursache der homerischen Werke, oder Cäsar's Ehrgeiz als die Ursache des Untergangs der republikanischen Verfassung Roms anzugeben. In der Geschichte überhaupt sind geistige Massen und Individuen im Spiele und in der Wechselbestimmung mit einander; die Natur des Geistes ist es aber noch in viel höherem Sinne, als der Charakter des Lebendigen überhaupt, vielmehr nicht ein anderes Ursprüngliches in sich aufzunehmen, oder nicht eine Ursache sich in ihn kontinuiren zu lassen, sondern sie abzubrechen und zu verwandeln.—Welche Verhältnisse aber der Idee angehören und bei ihr erst zu betrachten sind.—Dieß kann hier noch bemerkt werden, daß insofern das Verhältniß von Ursache und Wirkung, obwohl in uneigentlichem Sinne, zugelassen wird, die Wirkung nicht größer seyn könne, als die Ursache; denn die Wirkung ist nichts weiter als die Manifestation der Ursache. Es ist ein gewöhnlich gewordener Witz in der Geschichte, aus kleinen Ursachen große Wirkungen entstehen zu lassen, und für die umfassende und tiefe Begebenheit eine Anekdote als erste Ursache aufzuführen. Eine solche sogenannte Ursache ist für nichts weiteres als eine Veranlassung, als äußere Erregung anzusehen, deren der innere Geist der Begebenheit nicht bedurft hätte, oder deren er eine unzählige Menge anderer hätte gebrauchen können, um von ihnen in der Erscheinung anzufangen, sich Luft zu machen und seine Manifestation zu geben. Vielmehr ist umgekehrt so etwas für sich Kleinliches und Zufälliges erst von ihm zu seiner Veranlassung bestimmt worden. Jene Arabesken-Malerei der Geschichte, die aus einem schwanken Stengel eine große Gestalt hervorgehen läßt, ist daher wohl eine geistreiche, aber höchst oberflächliche Behandlung. Es ist in diesem Entspringen des Großen aus dem Kleinen zwar überhaupt die Umkehrung vorhanden, die der Geist mit dem Äußerlichen vornimmt; aber eben darum ist dieses nicht Ursache in ihm, oder diese Umkehrung hebt selbst das Verhältniß der Kausalität auf.\n\n2. Diese Bestimmtheit des Kausalitäts-Verhältnisses aber, daß Inhalt und Form verschieden und gleichgültig sind, erstreckt sich weiter. Die Formbestimmung ist auch Inhaltsbestimmung; Ursache und Wirkung, die beiden Seiten des Verhältnisses, sind daher auch ein anderer Inhalt. Oder der Inhalt, weil er nur als Inhalt einer Form ist, hat ihren Unterschied an ihm selbst und ist wesentlich verschieden. Aber indem diese seine Form das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß ist, das ein in Ursache und Wirkung identischer Inhalt ist, so ist der verschiedene Inhalt äußerlich mit der Ursache einer Seits, und anderer Seits mit der Wirkung verbunden; er tritt somit nicht selbst in das Wirken und in das Verhältniß ein.\n\nDieser äußerliche Inhalt ist also verhältnißlos;—eine unmittelbare Existenz;—oder weil er als Inhalt die ansichseyende Identität der Ursache und Wirkung ist, ist auch er unmittelbare, seyende Identität. Dieß ist daher irgend ein Ding, das mannigfaltige Bestimmungen seines Daseyns hat, unter Anderem auch diese, daß es in irgend einer Rücksicht Ursache oder auch Wirkung ist. Die Formbestimmungen, Ursache und Wirkung, haben an ihm ihr Substrat, das heißt ihr wesentliches Bestehen,—und jede ein besonderes—, denn ihre Identität ist ihr Bestehen;—zugleich aber ist es ihr unmittelbares Bestehen, nicht ihr Bestehen als Formeinheit, oder als Verhältniß.\n\nAber dieses Ding ist nicht nur Substrat, sondern auch Substanz, denn es ist das identische Bestehen nur als des Verhältnisses. Ferner ist sie endliche Substanz, denn sie ist bestimmt als unmittelbare gegen ihre Ursachlichkeit. Aber sie hat zugleich Kausalität, weil sie ebenso sehr nur das Identische als dieses Verhältnisses ist.—Als Ursache nun ist dieses Substrat die negative Beziehung auf sich. Aber es selbst, worauf es sich bezieht, ist erstens ein Gesetztseyn, weil es als unmittelbar Wirkliches bestimmt ist; dieß Gesetztseyn als Inhalt ist irgend eine Bestimmung überhaupt.—Zweitens ist ihin die Kausalität äußerlich; diese macht somit selbst sein Gesetztseyn aus. Indem es nun ursachliche Substanz ist, besteht seine Kausalität darin, sich negativ auf sich, also auf sein Gesetztseyn und äußere Kausalität, zu beziehen. Das Wirken dieser Substanz fängt daher von einem Äußern an, befreit sich von dieser äußern Bestimmung, und seine Rückkehr in sich ist die Erhaltung seiner unmittelbaren Existenz und das Aufheben seiner gesetzten, und damit seiner Kausalität überhaupt.\n\nSo ist ein Stein, der sich bewegt, Ursache; seine Bewegung ist eine Bestimmung, die er hat, außer welcher er aber noch viele andere Bestimmungen der Farbe, Gestalt u.s.f. enthält, welche nicht in seine Ursachlichkeit eingehen. Weil seine unmittelbare Existenz getrennt ist von seiner Formbeziehung, nämlich der Kausalität, so ist diese ein Äußerliches; seine Bewegung, und die Kausalität, die ihm in ihr zukommt, ist an ihm nur Gesetztseyn.—Aber die Kausalität ist auch seine eigene; dieß ist darin vorhanden, daß sein substantielles Bestehen seine identische Beziehung auf sich ist, diese aber ist nunmehr als Gesetztseyn bestimmt, sie ist also zugleich negative Beziehung auf sich.—Seine Kausalität, welche sich auf sich als auf das Gesetztseyn oder als ein Äußeres richtet, besteht daher darin, es aufzuheben, und durch die Entfernung desselben in sich zurückzukehren, —somit insofern nicht in seinem Gesetztseyn identisch mit sich zu seyn, sondern nur seine abstrakte Ursprünglichkeit wiederherzustellen. —Oder der Regen ist Ursache der Nässe, welche dasselbe Wasser ist als jener. Dieses Wasser hat die Bestimmung, Regen und Ursache zu seyn, dadurch daß sie von einem Andern in ihm gesetzt ist;—eine andere Kraft oder was es sey, hat es in die Luft erhoben und in eine Masse zusammengebracht, deren Schwere es fallen macht. Seine Entfernung von der Erde, ist eine seiner ursprünglichen Identität mit sich, der Schwere, fremde Bestimmung; seine Ursachlichkeit besteht darin dieselbe zu entfernen, und jene Identität wieder herzustellen, damit aber auch seine Kausalität aufzuheben.\n\nDie jetzt betrachtete zweite Bestimmtheit der Kausalität geht die Form an; dieß Verhältniß ist die Kausalität als sich selbst äußerlich, als die Ursprünglichkeit, welche ebenso sehr an ihr selbst Gesetztseyn oder Wirkung ist.\n\nDiese Vereinigung der entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen als im seyenden Substrat macht den unendlichen Regreß von Ursachen zu Ursachen aus. —Es wird von der Wirkung angefangen; sie hat als solche eine Ursache, diese hat wieder eine Ursache und so fort. Warum hat die Ursache wieder eine Ursachen das heißt, warum wird dieselbe Seite, die vorher als Ursache bestimmt war, nunmehr als Wirkung bestimmt und damit nach einer neuen Ursache gefragt?—Aus dem Grunde, weil die Ursache ein Endliches, Bestimmtes überhaupt ist; bestimmt als Ein Moment der Form gegen die Wirkung; so hat sie ihre Bestimmtheit oder Negation außer ihr; eben damit aber ist sie selbst endlich, hat ihre Bestimmtheit an ihr, und ist somit Gesetztseyn oder Wirkung. Diese ihre Identität ist auch gesetzt, aber sie ist ein Drittes, odas unmittelbare Substrat; die Kausalität ist darum sich selbst äußerlich, weil hier ihre Ursprünglichkeit eine Unmittelbarkeit ist. Der Formunterschied ist daher erste Bestimmtheit, noch nicht die Bestimmtheit als Bestimmtheit gesetzt, er ist seyendes Andersseyn. Die endliche Reflexion bleibt einer Seits bei diesem Unmittelbaren stehen, entfernt die Formeinheit davon und läßt es in anderer Rüksicht Ursache und in anderer Wirkung seyn; anderer Seits verlegt sie die Formeinheit in das Unendliche, und drükt durch das perennirende Fortgehen ihre Ohnmacht aus, sie erreichen und festhalten zu können.\n\nMit der Wirkung ist es unmittelbar der nämliche Fall, oder vielmehr der unendliche Progreß von Wirkung zu Wirkung ist ganz und dasselbe was der Regreß von Ursache zu Ursache ist. In diesem wurde die Ursache zur Wirkung, welche wieder eine andere Ursache hat; ebenso wird umgekehrt die Wirkung zur Ursache, die wieder eine andere Wirkung hat.—Die betrachtete bestimmte Ursache fängt von einer Äußerlichkeit an, und kehrt in ihrer Wirkung nicht als Ursache in sich zurück, sondern verliert vielmehr die Kausalität darin. Aber umgekehrt kommt die Wirkung an ein Substrat, welches Substanz, ursprünglich sich auf sich beziehendes Bestehen ist; an ihm wird daher dieß Gesetztseyn zum Gesetztseyn; das heißt, diese Substanz, indem eine Wirkung in ihr gesetzt wird, verhält sich als Ursache. Aber jene erste Wirkung, das Gesetztseyn, das an sie äußerlich kommt, ist ein Anderes als die zweite, die von ihr hervorgebracht wird; denn diese zweite ist bestimmt, als ihre Reflexion-in-sich, jene aber als eine Äußerlichkeit an ihr.—Aber weil die Kausalität hier die sich selbst äußerliche Ursachlichkeit ist, so kehrt sie auch ebenso sehr in ihrer Wirkung nicht in sich zurück; wird sich darin äußerlich, ihre Wirkung wird wieder Gesetztseyn an einem Substrate,—als einer andern Substanz, die aber ebenso es zum Gesetztseyn macht, oder sich als Ursache manifestirt, ihre Wirkung wieder von sich abstößt und so fort in das Schlecht-Unendliche.\n\n3. Es ist nun zu sehen, was durch die Bewegung des bestimmten Kausalitäts-Verhältnisses geworden ist.—Die formelle Kausalität erlischt in der Wirkung; dadurch ist das Identische dieser beiden Momente geworden; aber damit nur als an sich die Einheit von Ursache und Wirkung, woran die Formbeziehung äußerlich ist.—Dieß Identische ist dadurch auch unmittelbar nach den beiden Bestimmungen der Unmittelbarkeit, erstens als Ansichseyn, ein Inhalt, an dem die Kausalität sich äußerlich verläuft; zweitens als ein existirendes Substrat, dem die Ursache und die Wirkung inhäriren, als unterschiedene Formbestimmungen. Diese sind darin an sich eins, aber jede ist um dieses Ansichseyns oder der Äußerlichkeit der Form willen sich selbst äußerlich, somit in ihrer Einheit mit der andern auch als andre gegen sie bestimmt. Daher hat zwar die Ursache eine Wirkung, und ist zugleich selbst Wirkung; und die Wirkung hat nicht nur eine Ursache, sondern ist auch selbst Ursache. Aber die Wirkung, welche die Ursache hat, und die Wirkung, die sie ist;—ebenso die Ursache, welche die Wirkung hat, und die Ursache, die sie ist, sind verschieden.\n\nDurch die Bewegung des bestimmten Kausalitätsverhältnisses ist aber nun dieß geworden, daß die Ursache nicht nur in der Wirkung erlischt, und damit auch die Wirkung, wie in der formellen Kausalität, sondern daß die Ursache in ihrem Erlöschen, in der Wirkung wieder wird, daß die Wirkung in Ursache verschwindet, aber in ihr ebenso wieder wird. Jede dieser Bestimmungen hebt sich in ihrem Setzen auf, und setzt sich in ihrem Aufheben; es ist nicht ein äußerliches Übergehen der Kausalität von einem Substrat an ein anderes vorhanden, sondern dieß Anderswerden derselben ist zugleich ihr eigenes Setzen. Die Kausalität setzt also sich selbst voraus oder bedingt sich. Die vorher nur an sich seyende Identität, das Substrat, ist daher nunmehr bestimmt als Voraussetzung oder gesetzt gegen die wirkende Kausalität, und die vorhin dem Identischen nur äußerliche Reflexion steht nun im Verhältnisse zu demselben.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0001","text":"1. Die Identität der Ursache in ihrer Wirkung mit sich ist das Aufheben ihrer Macht und Negativität, daher die gegen die Formunterschiede gleichgültige Einheit, der Inhalt.—Er ist daher nur an sich auf die Form, hier die Kausalität, bezogen. Sie sind somit als verschieden gesetzt, und die Form gegen den Inhalt eine selbst nur unmittelbar wirkliche, eine zufällige Kausalität.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"165.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0002","text":"Ferner der Inhalt so als bestimmtes, ist ein verschiedener Inhalt an ihm selbst; und die Ursache ist ihrem Inhalte nach bestimmt, damit ebenso die Wirkung.—Der Inhalt, da das Reflektirtseyn hier auch unmittelbare Wirklichkeit ist, ist insofern wirkliche, aber die endliche Substanz.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"165.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0003","text":"Dieß ist nunmehr das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß in seiner Realität und Endlichkeit. Als formell ist es das unendliche Verhältniß der absoluten Macht, deren Inhalt die reine Manifestation oder Nothwendigkeit ist. Als endliche Kausalität hingegen hat es einen gegebenen Inhalt, und verläuft sich als ein äußerlicher Unterschied an diesem Identischen, das in seinen Bestimmungen eine und dieselbe Substanz ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"165.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0004","text":"Durch diese Identität des Inhalts ist diese Kausalität ein analytischer Satz. Es ist dieselbe Sache, welche sich das eine Mal als Ursache, das andere Mal als Wirkung darstellt, dort als eigenthümliches Bestehen, hier als Gesetztseyn oder Bestimmung an einem Andern. Da diese Bestimmungen der Form äußerliche Reflexion sind, so ist es die der Sache nach tautologische Betrachtung eines subjektiven Verstandes, eine Erscheinung als Wirkung zu bestimmen und davon zu ihrer Ursache aufzusteigen, um sie zu begreifen und zu erklären; es wird nur ein und derselbe Inhalt wiederhohlt; man hat in der Ursache nichts Anderes als in der Wirkung.—Der Regen z.B.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"165.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0005","text":"ist Ursache der Feuchtigkeit, welche seine Wirkung ist;—der Regen macht naß, dieß ist ein analytischer Satz; dasselbe Wasser, was der Regen ist, ist die Feuchtigkeit; als Regen ist dieß Wasser nur in der Form einer Sache für sich, als Wässerigkeit oder Feuchtigkeit dagegen ist es ein adjectives, ein gesetztes, das nicht mehr sein Bestehen an ihm selbst haben soll; und die eine Bestimmung, wie die andere, ist ihm äußerlich.—So ist die Ursache dieser Farbe ein Färbendes, ein Pigment, welches eine und dieselbe Wirklichkeit ist, das eine Mal in der ihm äußern Form eines thätigen, das heißt, mit einem von ihm verschiedenen Thätigen äußerlich verbunden, das andere Mal aber in der ihm ebenso äußerlichen Bestimmung einer Wirkung.—Die Ursache einer That ist die innere Gesinnung in einem thätigen Subjekt, die als äußeres Daseyn, das sie durch die Handlung erhält, derselbe Inhalt und Werth ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"165.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0006","text":"Wenn die Bewegung eines Körpers als Wirkung betrachtet wird, so ist die Ursache derselben eine stoßende Kraft; aber es ist dasselbe Quantum der Bewegung, das vor und nach dem Stoß vorhanden ist, dieselbe Existenz, welche der stoßende Körper enthielt, und dem gestoßenen mittheilte; und so viel er mittheilt, so viel verliert er selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"165.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0007","text":"Die Ursache, z.B. der Mahler, oder der stoßende Körper hat wohl noch einen andern Inhalt, jener, als die Farben und deren sie zum Gemälde verbindende Form; dieser, als eine Bewegung von bestimmter Stärke und Richtung. Allein dieser weitere Inhalt ist ein zufälliges Beiwesen, das die Ursache nichts angeht; was der Maler sonst für Qualitäten enthält, abstrahirt davon, daß er Maler dieses Gemäldes ist, dieß tritt nicht in dieses Gemälde ein; nur was von seinen Eigenschaften sich in der Wirkung darstellt, ist in ihm als Ursache vorhanden, nach seinen übrigen Eigenschaften ist er nicht Ursache. So ob der stoßende Körper Stein oder Holz, grün, gelb ist u.s.f. dieß tritt nicht in seinen Stoß ein; insofern ist er nicht Ursache.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"165.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0008","text":"Es ist in Rücksicht dieser Tautologie des Kausalitäts-Verhältnisses zu bemerken, daß es dieselbe dann nicht zu enthalten scheint, wenn nicht die nächste, sondern die entfernte Ursache einer Wirkung angegeben wird. Die Formveränderung, welche die zu Grunde liegende Sache in diesem Durchgange durch mehrere Mittelglieder erleidet, versteckt die Identität, die sie darin behält. Sie verknüpft sich zugleich in dieser Vervielfältigung der Ursachen, welche zwischen sie und die letzte Wirkung eingetreten sind, mit andern Dingen und Umständen, so daß nicht jenes Erste, was als Ursache ausgesprochen wird, sondern nur diese mehrere Ursachen zusammen die vollständige Wirkung enthalten.—So wenn z.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"165.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0009","text":"ein Mensch dadurch unter Umstände kam, in denen sich sein Talent entwickelte, daß er seinen Vater verlor, den in einer Schlacht eine Kugel traf, so könnte dieser Schuß, (oder noch weiter zurück der Krieg oder eine Ursache des Kriegs und so fort ins Unendliche) als Ursache der Geschicklichkeit jenes Menschen angegeben werden. Allein es erhellt, daß z.B. jener Schuß nicht für sich diese Ursache ist, sondern nur die Verknüpfung desselben mit andern wirkenden Bestimmungen. Oder vielmehr ist er überhaupt nicht Ursache, sondern nur ein einzelnes Moment, das zu den Umständen der Möglichkeit gehörte.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"165.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0010","text":"Denn hauptsächlich ist noch die unstatthafte Anwendung des Kausalitätsverhältnisses auf Verhältnisse des physisch-organischen und des geistigen Lebens zu bemerken. Hier zeigt sich das, was als Ursache genannt wird, freilich von anderem Inhalte als die Wirkung, darum aber, weil das, was auf das Lebendige wirkt, von diesem selbstständig bestimmt, verändert und verwandelt wird, weil das Lebendige die Ursache nicht zu ihrer Wirkung kommen läßt, das heißt, sie als Ursache aufhebt. So ist es unstatthaft gesprochen, daß die Nahrung die Ursache des Bluts, oder diese Speisen oder Kälte, Nässe, Ursachen des Fiebers u.s.fort seyen; so unstatthaft es ist, das jonische Klima als die Ursache der homerischen Werke, oder Cäsar's Ehrgeiz als die Ursache des Untergangs der republikanischen Verfassung Roms anzugeben.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"165.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0011","text":"In der Geschichte überhaupt sind geistige Massen und Individuen im Spiele und in der Wechselbestimmung mit einander; die Natur des Geistes ist es aber noch in viel höherem Sinne, als der Charakter des Lebendigen überhaupt, vielmehr nicht ein anderes Ursprüngliches in sich aufzunehmen, oder nicht eine Ursache sich in ihn kontinuiren zu lassen, sondern sie abzubrechen und zu verwandeln.—Welche Verhältnisse aber der Idee angehören und bei ihr erst zu betrachten sind.—Dieß kann hier noch bemerkt werden, daß insofern das Verhältniß von Ursache und Wirkung, obwohl in uneigentlichem Sinne, zugelassen wird, die Wirkung nicht größer seyn könne, als die Ursache; denn die Wirkung ist nichts weiter als die Manifestation der Ursache.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"165.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0012","text":"Es ist ein gewöhnlich gewordener Witz in der Geschichte, aus kleinen Ursachen große Wirkungen entstehen zu lassen, und für die umfassende und tiefe Begebenheit eine Anekdote als erste Ursache aufzuführen. Eine solche sogenannte Ursache ist für nichts weiteres als eine Veranlassung, als äußere Erregung anzusehen, deren der innere Geist der Begebenheit nicht bedurft hätte, oder deren er eine unzählige Menge anderer hätte gebrauchen können, um von ihnen in der Erscheinung anzufangen, sich Luft zu machen und seine Manifestation zu geben. Vielmehr ist umgekehrt so etwas für sich Kleinliches und Zufälliges erst von ihm zu seiner Veranlassung bestimmt worden. Jene Arabesken-Malerei der Geschichte, die aus einem schwanken Stengel eine große Gestalt hervorgehen läßt, ist daher wohl eine geistreiche, aber höchst oberflächliche Behandlung.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"165.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0013","text":"Es ist in diesem Entspringen des Großen aus dem Kleinen zwar überhaupt die Umkehrung vorhanden, die der Geist mit dem Äußerlichen vornimmt; aber eben darum ist dieses nicht Ursache in ihm, oder diese Umkehrung hebt selbst das Verhältniß der Kausalität auf.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"165.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0014","text":"2. Diese Bestimmtheit des Kausalitäts-Verhältnisses aber, daß Inhalt und Form verschieden und gleichgültig sind, erstreckt sich weiter. Die Formbestimmung ist auch Inhaltsbestimmung; Ursache und Wirkung, die beiden Seiten des Verhältnisses, sind daher auch ein anderer Inhalt. Oder der Inhalt, weil er nur als Inhalt einer Form ist, hat ihren Unterschied an ihm selbst und ist wesentlich verschieden. Aber indem diese seine Form das Kausalitäts-Verhältniß ist, das ein in Ursache und Wirkung identischer Inhalt ist, so ist der verschiedene Inhalt äußerlich mit der Ursache einer Seits, und anderer Seits mit der Wirkung verbunden; er tritt somit nicht selbst in das Wirken und in das Verhältniß ein.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"165.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0015","text":"Dieser äußerliche Inhalt ist also verhältnißlos;—eine unmittelbare Existenz;—oder weil er als Inhalt die ansichseyende Identität der Ursache und Wirkung ist, ist auch er unmittelbare, seyende Identität. Dieß ist daher irgend ein Ding, das mannigfaltige Bestimmungen seines Daseyns hat, unter Anderem auch diese, daß es in irgend einer Rücksicht Ursache oder auch Wirkung ist. Die Formbestimmungen, Ursache und Wirkung, haben an ihm ihr Substrat, das heißt ihr wesentliches Bestehen,—und jede ein besonderes—, denn ihre Identität ist ihr Bestehen;—zugleich aber ist es ihr unmittelbares Bestehen, nicht ihr Bestehen als Formeinheit, oder als Verhältniß.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"165.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0016","text":"Aber dieses Ding ist nicht nur Substrat, sondern auch Substanz, denn es ist das identische Bestehen nur als des Verhältnisses. Ferner ist sie endliche Substanz, denn sie ist bestimmt als unmittelbare gegen ihre Ursachlichkeit. Aber sie hat zugleich Kausalität, weil sie ebenso sehr nur das Identische als dieses Verhältnisses ist.—Als Ursache nun ist dieses Substrat die negative Beziehung auf sich. Aber es selbst, worauf es sich bezieht, ist erstens ein Gesetztseyn, weil es als unmittelbar Wirkliches bestimmt ist; dieß Gesetztseyn als Inhalt ist irgend eine Bestimmung überhaupt.—Zweitens ist ihin die Kausalität äußerlich; diese macht somit selbst sein Gesetztseyn aus. Indem es nun ursachliche Substanz ist, besteht seine Kausalität darin, sich negativ auf sich, also auf sein Gesetztseyn und äußere Kausalität, zu beziehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"165.16"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0017","text":"Das Wirken dieser Substanz fängt daher von einem Äußern an, befreit sich von dieser äußern Bestimmung, und seine Rückkehr in sich ist die Erhaltung seiner unmittelbaren Existenz und das Aufheben seiner gesetzten, und damit seiner Kausalität überhaupt.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"165.17"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0018","text":"So ist ein Stein, der sich bewegt, Ursache; seine Bewegung ist eine Bestimmung, die er hat, außer welcher er aber noch viele andere Bestimmungen der Farbe, Gestalt u.s.f. enthält, welche nicht in seine Ursachlichkeit eingehen.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"165.18"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0019","text":"Weil seine unmittelbare Existenz getrennt ist von seiner Formbeziehung, nämlich der Kausalität, so ist diese ein Äußerliches; seine Bewegung, und die Kausalität, die ihm in ihr zukommt, ist an ihm nur Gesetztseyn.—Aber die Kausalität ist auch seine eigene; dieß ist darin vorhanden, daß sein substantielles Bestehen seine identische Beziehung auf sich ist, diese aber ist nunmehr als Gesetztseyn bestimmt, sie ist also zugleich negative Beziehung auf sich.—Seine Kausalität, welche sich auf sich als auf das Gesetztseyn oder als ein Äußeres richtet, besteht daher darin, es aufzuheben, und durch die Entfernung desselben in sich zurückzukehren, —somit insofern nicht in seinem Gesetztseyn identisch mit sich zu seyn, sondern nur seine abstrakte Ursprünglichkeit wiederherzustellen. —Oder der Regen ist Ursache der Nässe, welche dasselbe Wasser ist als jener.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"165.19"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0020","text":"Dieses Wasser hat die Bestimmung, Regen und Ursache zu seyn, dadurch daß sie von einem Andern in ihm gesetzt ist;—eine andere Kraft oder was es sey, hat es in die Luft erhoben und in eine Masse zusammengebracht, deren Schwere es fallen macht. Seine Entfernung von der Erde, ist eine seiner ursprünglichen Identität mit sich, der Schwere, fremde Bestimmung; seine Ursachlichkeit besteht darin dieselbe zu entfernen, und jene Identität wieder herzustellen, damit aber auch seine Kausalität aufzuheben.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"165.20"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0021","text":"Die jetzt betrachtete zweite Bestimmtheit der Kausalität geht die Form an; dieß Verhältniß ist die Kausalität als sich selbst äußerlich, als die Ursprünglichkeit, welche ebenso sehr an ihr selbst Gesetztseyn oder Wirkung ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"165.21"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0022","text":"Diese Vereinigung der entgegengesetzten Bestimmungen als im seyenden Substrat macht den unendlichen Regreß von Ursachen zu Ursachen aus. —Es wird von der Wirkung angefangen; sie hat als solche eine Ursache, diese hat wieder eine Ursache und so fort. Warum hat die Ursache wieder eine Ursachen das heißt, warum wird dieselbe Seite, die vorher als Ursache bestimmt war, nunmehr als Wirkung bestimmt und damit nach einer neuen Ursache gefragt?—Aus dem Grunde, weil die Ursache ein Endliches, Bestimmtes überhaupt ist; bestimmt als Ein Moment der Form gegen die Wirkung; so hat sie ihre Bestimmtheit oder Negation außer ihr; eben damit aber ist sie selbst endlich, hat ihre Bestimmtheit an ihr, und ist somit Gesetztseyn oder Wirkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"165.22"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0023","text":"Diese ihre Identität ist auch gesetzt, aber sie ist ein Drittes, odas unmittelbare Substrat; die Kausalität ist darum sich selbst äußerlich, weil hier ihre Ursprünglichkeit eine Unmittelbarkeit ist. Der Formunterschied ist daher erste Bestimmtheit, noch nicht die Bestimmtheit als Bestimmtheit gesetzt, er ist seyendes Andersseyn. Die endliche Reflexion bleibt einer Seits bei diesem Unmittelbaren stehen, entfernt die Formeinheit davon und läßt es in anderer Rüksicht Ursache und in anderer Wirkung seyn; anderer Seits verlegt sie die Formeinheit in das Unendliche, und drükt durch das perennirende Fortgehen ihre Ohnmacht aus, sie erreichen und festhalten zu können.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"165.23"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0024","text":"Mit der Wirkung ist es unmittelbar der nämliche Fall, oder vielmehr der unendliche Progreß von Wirkung zu Wirkung ist ganz und dasselbe was der Regreß von Ursache zu Ursache ist. In diesem wurde die Ursache zur Wirkung, welche wieder eine andere Ursache hat; ebenso wird umgekehrt die Wirkung zur Ursache, die wieder eine andere Wirkung hat.—Die betrachtete bestimmte Ursache fängt von einer Äußerlichkeit an, und kehrt in ihrer Wirkung nicht als Ursache in sich zurück, sondern verliert vielmehr die Kausalität darin. Aber umgekehrt kommt die Wirkung an ein Substrat, welches Substanz, ursprünglich sich auf sich beziehendes Bestehen ist; an ihm wird daher dieß Gesetztseyn zum Gesetztseyn; das heißt, diese Substanz, indem eine Wirkung in ihr gesetzt wird, verhält sich als Ursache.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"165.24"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0025","text":"Aber jene erste Wirkung, das Gesetztseyn, das an sie äußerlich kommt, ist ein Anderes als die zweite, die von ihr hervorgebracht wird; denn diese zweite ist bestimmt, als ihre Reflexion-in-sich, jene aber als eine Äußerlichkeit an ihr.—Aber weil die Kausalität hier die sich selbst äußerliche Ursachlichkeit ist, so kehrt sie auch ebenso sehr in ihrer Wirkung nicht in sich zurück; wird sich darin äußerlich, ihre Wirkung wird wieder Gesetztseyn an einem Substrate,—als einer andern Substanz, die aber ebenso es zum Gesetztseyn macht, oder sich als Ursache manifestirt, ihre Wirkung wieder von sich abstößt und so fort in das Schlecht-Unendliche.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"165.25"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0026","text":"3. Es ist nun zu sehen, was durch die Bewegung des bestimmten Kausalitäts-Verhältnisses geworden ist.—Die formelle Kausalität erlischt in der Wirkung; dadurch ist das Identische dieser beiden Momente geworden; aber damit nur als an sich die Einheit von Ursache und Wirkung, woran die Formbeziehung äußerlich ist.—Dieß Identische ist dadurch auch unmittelbar nach den beiden Bestimmungen der Unmittelbarkeit, erstens als Ansichseyn, ein Inhalt, an dem die Kausalität sich äußerlich verläuft; zweitens als ein existirendes Substrat, dem die Ursache und die Wirkung inhäriren, als unterschiedene Formbestimmungen. Diese sind darin an sich eins, aber jede ist um dieses Ansichseyns oder der Äußerlichkeit der Form willen sich selbst äußerlich, somit in ihrer Einheit mit der andern auch als andre gegen sie bestimmt.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"165.26"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0027","text":"Daher hat zwar die Ursache eine Wirkung, und ist zugleich selbst Wirkung; und die Wirkung hat nicht nur eine Ursache, sondern ist auch selbst Ursache. Aber die Wirkung, welche die Ursache hat, und die Wirkung, die sie ist;—ebenso die Ursache, welche die Wirkung hat, und die Ursache, die sie ist, sind verschieden.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"165.27"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0028","text":"Durch die Bewegung des bestimmten Kausalitätsverhältnisses ist aber nun dieß geworden, daß die Ursache nicht nur in der Wirkung erlischt, und damit auch die Wirkung, wie in der formellen Kausalität, sondern daß die Ursache in ihrem Erlöschen, in der Wirkung wieder wird, daß die Wirkung in Ursache verschwindet, aber in ihr ebenso wieder wird. Jede dieser Bestimmungen hebt sich in ihrem Setzen auf, und setzt sich in ihrem Aufheben; es ist nicht ein äußerliches Übergehen der Kausalität von einem Substrat an ein anderes vorhanden, sondern dieß Anderswerden derselben ist zugleich ihr eigenes Setzen. Die Kausalität setzt also sich selbst voraus oder bedingt sich.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"165.28"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0029","text":"Die vorher nur an sich seyende Identität, das Substrat, ist daher nunmehr bestimmt als Voraussetzung oder gesetzt gegen die wirkende Kausalität, und die vorhin dem Identischen nur äußerliche Reflexion steht nun im Verhältnisse zu demselben.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"165.29"}],"sha256":"b8e95a138c5f5539a6675cc2c58ffcb5ce492cdb3a34d77cd4dc2029b64ab316","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110128147039Z_8bfc48a6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"b. The Determinate Causal Relation.","source_sha256":"b8e95a138c5f5539a6675cc2c58ffcb5ce492cdb3a34d77cd4dc2029b64ab316","sha256":"ad4ed8d4598b1f1ddb67393081ccaaa2301f94e4ab67603cbab9cf7e617fed83","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:01:28.147074+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0001","text":"1. The identity of the cause with itself in its effect is the sublation of its power and negativity, hence the unity indifferent to the differences of form, the content.—It is therefore related to form, here causality, only implicitly. They are thus posited as different, and form is, in contrast to content, a causality that is itself only immediately actual, a contingent causality.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"165.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0002","text":"Further, content, as thus determinate, is a different content in itself; and the cause is determinate according to its content, and likewise the effect.—Since reflectedness here is also immediate actuality, content is to that extent actual, but finite substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"165.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0003","text":"This is now the relation of causality in its reality and finitude. As formal, it is the infinite relation of absolute power, whose content is pure manifestation or necessity. As finite causality, on the other hand, it has a given content, and dissipates itself as an external difference in this identical [element], which in its determinations is one and the same substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"165.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0004","text":"Through this identity of content, this causality is an analytical proposition. It is the same thing that presents itself at one time as cause, at another as effect, there as independent subsistence, here as positedness or determination in an other. Since these determinations of form are external reflection, it is the tautological consideration, as regards the thing, of a subjective understanding, to determine an appearance as effect and to ascend from it to its cause, in order to comprehend and explain it; only one and the same content is repeated; one has nothing in the cause other than in the effect.—Rain, for example,","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"165.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0005","text":"is the cause of moisture, which is its effect;—rain makes wet; this is an analytical proposition; the same water which rain is, is moisture; as rain, this water is only in the form of a thing for itself, whereas as wateriness or moisture it is an adjective, a posited [element], which is no longer supposed to have its subsistence in itself; and the one determination, as well as the other, is external to it.—Thus the cause of this colour is a colouring matter, a pigment, which is one and the same actuality, on the one occasion in the form external to it of an active [element], that is, externally connected with an active [element] distinct from it, but on the other occasion in the determination, equally external to it, of an effect.—The cause of a deed is the inner disposition in an active subject, which, as the external existence that it receives through the action, is the same content and value.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"165.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0006","text":"If the motion of a body is considered as an effect, its cause is an impelling force; but it is the same quantum of motion that is present before and after the impact, the same existence that the impelling body contained and communicated to the body impelled; and as much as it communicates, so much it itself loses.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"165.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0007","text":"The cause, for example the painter or the impelling body, certainly has yet another content: the former, as colours and the form connecting them into a painting; the latter, as a motion of determinate strength and direction. But this further content is a contingent adjunct, which does not concern the cause; whatever other qualities the painter contains, abstracted from the fact that he is the painter of this painting, does not enter into this painting; only what of his properties presents itself in the effect is present in him as cause; according to his remaining properties he is not cause. Thus, whether the impelling body is stone or wood, green or yellow, etc., this does not enter into its impact; to that extent it is not cause.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"165.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0008","text":"With respect to this tautology of the relation of causality, it is to be noted that it then seems not to contain it when not the proximate but the remote cause of an effect is specified. The alteration of form which the underlying thing undergoes in this passage through several intermediate terms conceals the identity that it retains therein. At the same time, in this multiplication of causes that have intervened between it and the final effect, it connects itself with other things and circumstances, so that not that first [element] which is pronounced the cause, but only these several causes taken together contain the complete effect.—Thus, if, for example,","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"165.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0009","text":"a human being came into circumstances in which his talent developed because he lost his father, who was struck by a bullet in a battle, then this shot (or, going still further back, the war, or a cause of the war, and so on to infinity) could be given as the cause of that human being's skill. But it is evident that, for example, that shot is not by itself this cause, but only its connection with other efficacious determinations. Or rather, it is not a cause at all, but only a single moment belonging to the circumstances of possibility.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"165.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0010","text":"For above all, the inadmissible application of the relation of causality to the relations of physically organic and of spiritual life is still to be noted. Here, what is called the cause admittedly appears to be of a different content from the effect, but this is because what acts upon the living is independently determined, altered, and transformed by the latter, because the living does not allow the cause to arrive at its effect, that is, sublates it as cause. Thus it is inadmissible to say that nourishment is the cause of blood, or that these foods, or cold, dampness, are causes of fever, etc.; just as it is inadmissible to state the Ionian climate as the cause of the Homeric works, or Caesar's ambition as the cause of the downfall of Rome's republican constitution.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"165.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0011","text":"In history in general, spiritual masses and individuals are at play and in reciprocal determination with one another; but the nature of spirit is, in a far higher sense still than the character of the living in general, rather not to take up another original [element] into itself, or not to permit a cause to continue itself into it, but to break it off and transform it.—But what relations belong to the Idea and are to be considered only with it.—This may further be noted here: insofar as the relation of cause and effect is admitted, although in an improper sense, the effect cannot be greater than the cause; for the effect is nothing further than the manifestation of the cause.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"165.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0012","text":"It has become a common witticism in history to have great effects arise from small causes, and to adduce an anecdote as the first cause of a comprehensive and profound event. Such a so-called cause is to be regarded as nothing further than an occasion, as an external stimulus, which the inner spirit of the event would not have needed, or of which it could have made use of an innumerable multitude of others in order to begin from them in appearance, to give itself air and give its manifestation. On the contrary, something petty and contingent in itself is only first determined by it as its occasion. That arabesque painting of history which lets a great figure arise out of a wavering stem is therefore indeed a witty, but an exceedingly superficial treatment.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"165.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0013","text":"In this arising of the great from the small there is indeed in general the reversal which spirit undertakes with the external; but for that very reason this is not cause in it, or this reversal itself sublates the relation of causality.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"165.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0014","text":"2. But this determinacy of the relation of causality, namely that content and form are different and indifferent, extends further. The determination of form is also determination of content; cause and effect, the two sides of the relation, are therefore also a different content. Or, because content is only as the content of a form, it has the latter's difference in itself and is essentially different. But since this its form is the relation of causality, which is a content identical in cause and effect, the different content is externally connected, on the one side with the cause and, on the other side, with the effect; it thus does not itself enter into the acting and into the relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"165.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0015","text":"This external content is thus without relation;—an immediate existence;—or, because as content it is the identity of cause and effect that is in itself, it too is immediate, being identity. This is therefore some thing which has manifold determinations of its existence, among others this one: that in some respect it is cause or also effect. The determinations of form, cause and effect, have in it their substrate, that is, their essential subsistence,—and each a particular one—for their identity is their subsistence;—but at the same time it is their immediate subsistence, not their subsistence as unity of form, or as relation.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"165.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0016","text":"But this thing is not merely substrate, but also substance, for it is the identical subsistence only as that of the relation. Further, it is finite substance, because it is determined as immediate in contrast to its causality. But it at the same time has causality, because it is equally only the identical [element] as that of this relation.—Now as cause, this substrate is negative relation to itself. But that to which it relates itself is, first, a positedness, because it is determined as immediately actual; this positedness, as content, is some determination in general.—Second, causality is external to it; this thus itself constitutes its positedness. Since it is now causal substance, its causality consists in relating itself negatively to itself, hence to its positedness and external causality.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"165.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0017","text":"The acting of this substance therefore begins from an external [element], frees itself from this external determination, and its return into itself is the preservation of its immediate existence and the sublation of its posited [existence], and thereby of its causality in general.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"165.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0018","text":"Thus a stone which moves is cause; its motion is a determination which it has, apart from which, however, it contains yet many other determinations of colour, shape, etc., which do not enter into its causality.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"165.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0019","text":"Because its immediate existence is separated from its relation of form, namely causality, the latter is something external; its motion, and the causality which belongs to it in that motion, is in it only positedness.—But causality is also its own; this is present in the fact that its substantial subsistence is its identical relation to itself, but this is now determined as positedness; it is therefore at the same time negative relation to itself.—Its causality, which directs itself to itself as positedness or as something external, thus consists in sublating this [externality] and, by its removal, returning into itself,—thus, insofar as it is not identical with itself in its positedness, but only restoring its abstract originality.—Or rain is the cause of dampness, which is the same water as the former.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"165.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0020","text":"This water has the determination of being rain and cause because it is posited in it by an other;—another force, or whatever it may be, has raised it into the air and brought it together into a mass whose weight makes it fall. Its removal from the earth is a determination foreign to its original identity with itself, gravity; its causality consists in removing the same and restoring that identity, but thereby also in sublating its causality.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"165.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0021","text":"The second determinacy of causality now considered concerns form; this relation is causality as external to itself, as originality which is equally, in itself, positedness or effect.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"165.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0022","text":"This union of opposed determinations in the being substrate constitutes the infinite regress from causes to causes.—One begins from the effect; as such it has a cause; this in turn has a cause, and so on. Why does the cause in turn have a cause, that is, why is the same side which was previously determined as cause now determined as effect and thereby queried after a new cause?—On the ground that the cause is a finite, determinate [element] in general; determined as one moment of form in contrast to the effect, it has its determinacy or negation outside itself; but precisely thereby it is itself finite, has its determinacy in it, and is thus positedness or effect.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"165.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0023","text":"This its identity is also posited, but it is a third [element], the immediate substrate; causality is therefore external to itself, because here its originality is an immediacy. The difference of form is therefore the first determinacy, not yet determinacy posited as determinacy; it is being otherness. Finite reflection, on the one hand, remains fixed at this immediate [element], removes the unity of form from it, and lets it be cause in one respect and effect in another; on the other hand, it transfers the unity of form into infinity, and through the perpetual progression expresses its impotence to attain and hold it fast.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"165.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0024","text":"With the effect, the case is immediately the same; or rather, the infinite progress from effect to effect is altogether the same as the regress from cause to cause. In the latter, the cause became an effect, which again has another cause; likewise, conversely, the effect becomes a cause, which again has another effect.—The determinate cause considered begins from an externality, and in its effect does not return into itself as cause, but rather loses causality therein. But conversely, the effect comes upon a substrate which is substance, originally self-related subsistence; in it, therefore, this positedness becomes positedness; that is, this substance, in that an effect is posited in it, behaves as cause.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"165.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0025","text":"But that first effect, the positedness which comes to it externally, is something other than the second which is produced by it; for this second is determined as its reflection-into-itself, but the former as an externality upon it.—But because causality here is causality external to itself, it equally does not return into itself in its effect; it makes itself external therein, its effect again becomes positedness upon a substrate,—upon another substance, which, however, likewise makes it into positedness, or manifests itself as cause, again repels its effect from itself, and so on into bad infinity.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"165.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0026","text":"3. It is now to be seen what has become through the movement of the determinate causal relation.—Formal causality is extinguished in the effect; thereby the identicalness of these two moments has come to be; but thereby only as the unity of cause and effect in itself, to which the relation of form is external.—This identicalness is thereby also immediately, according to the two determinations of immediacy: first, as being-in-itself, a content in which causality runs its course externally; second, as an existing substrate, in which cause and effect inhere as distinct determinations of form. They are in themselves one therein, but each, on account of this being-in-itself, or of the externality of form, is external to itself, and thus, in its unity with the other, is also determined as other over against it.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"165.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0027","text":"Thus the cause indeed has an effect, and is at the same time itself effect; and the effect not only has a cause, but is itself also cause. But the effect which the cause has, and the effect which it is;—likewise the cause which the effect has, and the cause which it is, are different.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"165.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0028","text":"But through the movement of the determinate causal relation, this has now come to be: that the cause not only is extinguished in the effect, and with it also the effect, as in formal causality, but that the cause, in its extinction, becomes again in the effect; that the effect disappears into cause, but in it likewise becomes again. Each of these determinations sublates itself in its positing, and posits itself in its sublation; there is not an external transition of causality from one substrate to another, but this becoming-other of it is at the same time its own positing. Causality therefore presupposes itself, or conditions itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"165.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0029","text":"The identity which previously was only in itself, the substrate, is therefore henceforth determined as presupposition, or as posited over against acting causality, and the reflection formerly merely external to the identical now stands in relation to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"165.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_BDBK:P0029"]}],"source_digest":"9e535fe3cfeffbffdde0ed595afa18b1de07ce3e2d172495a8ff69dc1c2080f4","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"b. Das bestimmte Kausalitätsverhältniß."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"b. Das bestimmte Kausalitätsverhältniß.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG","title":"c. Action and Reaction.","order":166,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CWUG","text":"Die Kausalität ist voraussetzendes Thun. Die Ursache ist bedingt; sie ist die negative Beziehung auf sich als vorausgesetztes, als äußerliches Anderes, welches an sich aber nur an sich die Kausalität selbst ist. Es ist, wie sich ergeben hat, die substantielle Identität, in welche die formelle Kausalität übergeht, die sich nunmehr gegen dieselbe als ihr Negatives bestimmt hat. Oder es ist dasselbe, was die Substanz des Kausalitätsverhältnisses, aber welcher die Macht der Accidentalität als selbstsubstantielle Thätigkeit gegenüber steht.—Es ist die passive Substanz.—Passiv ist das Unmittelbare, oder Ansichseyende, das nicht auch für sich ist;—das reine Seyn oder das Wesen, das nur in dieser Bestimmtheit der abstrakten Identität mit sich ist.—Der passiven steht die als negativ sich auf sich beziebende, die wirkende Substanz gegenüber. Sie ist die Ursache, insofern sie sich in der bestimmten Kausalität durch die Negation ihrer selbst, aus der Wirkung wiederhergestellt hat, das in seinem Andersseyn oder als Unmittelbares sich wesentlich als setzend verhält, und durch seine Negation sich mit sich vermittelt. Die Kausalität hat deswegen hier kein Substrat mehr, dem sie inhärirte und ist nicht Formbestimmung gegen diese Identität sondern selbst die Substanz, oder das Ursprüngliche ist nur die Kausalität.—Das Substrat ist die passive Substanz, die sie sich vorausgesetzt hat.\n\nDiese Ursache wirkt nun; denn sie ist die negative Macht auf sich selbst; zugleich ist sie ihr Vorausgesetztes; so wirkt sie auf sich als auf ein Anderes, auf die passive Substanz.—Somit hebt sie erstlich das Andersseyn derselben auf; und kehrt in ihr in sich zurück; zweitens bestimmt sie dieselbe, sie setzt dieß Aufheben ihres Andersseyns oder die Rückkehr in sich als eine Bestimmtheit. Dieß Gesetztseyn, weil es zugleich ihre Rückkehr in sich ist, ist zunächst ihre Wirkung. Aber umgekehrt weil sie als voraussetzend sich selbst als ihr Anderes bestimmt, so setzt sie die Wirkung in der andern, der passiven Substanz.—Oder weil die passive Substanz selbst das Gedoppelte ist, nämlich ein selbstständiges Anderes, und zugleich ein Vorausgesetztes und an sich schon mit der wirkenden Ursache Identisches, so ist das Wirken von dieser selbst ein Gedoppeltes; es ist beides in Einem, das Aufheben ihres Bestimmtseyns, nämlich ihrer Bedingung, oder das Aufheben der Selbstständigkeit der passiven Substanz;—und daß sie ihre Identität mit derselben aufhebt, somit sich voraus oder als Anderes setzt.—Durch das letztere Moment wird die passive Substanz erhalten; jenes erste Aufheben derselben erscheint in Beziehung hierauf zugleich auch so, daß nur einige Bestimmungen an ihr aufgehoben werden und die Identität ihrer mit der ersten in der Wirkung äußerlich an ihr geschieht.\n\nInsofern leidet sie Gewalt.—Die Gewalt ist die Erscheinung der Macht, oder die Macht als Äußerliches. Äußerliches ist aber die Macht, nur insofern die ursachliche Substanz in ihrem Wirken, d. h. im Setzen ihrer selbst zugleich voraussetzend ist, d. h. sich selbst als aufgehobenes setzt. Umgekehrt ist daher ebenso sehr das Thun der Gewalt, ein Thun der Macht. Es ist nur ein von ihr selbst vorausgesetztes Anderes, auf welches die gewaltige Ursache wirkt, ihre Wirkung auf dasselbe ist negative Beziehung auf sich, oder die Manifestation ihrer selbst. Das Passive ist das Selbstständige, das nur ein Gesetztes ist; ein in sich selbst Gebrochenes,—eine Wirklichkeit, welche Bedingung ist und zwar die Bedingung nunmehr in ihrer Wahrheit nämlich eine Wirklichkeit, welche nur eine Möglichkeit ist, oder umgekehrt ein Ansichseyn, das nur die Bestimmtheit des Ansichseyns, nur passiv ist. Demjenigen daher, dem Gewalt geschieht, ist es nicht nur möglich, Gewalt anzuthun, sondern sie muß ihm auch angethan werden; was Gewalt über das Andere hat, hat sie nur, weil es die Macht desselben ist, die sich darin und das Andere manifestirt. Die passive Substanz wird durch die Gewalt nur gesetzt, als das was sie in Wahrheit ist, nämlich weil sie das einfache Positive oder unmittelbare Substanz ist, eben darum nur ein Gesetztes zu seyn; das Voraus, das sie als Bedingung ist, ist der Schein der Unmittelbarkeit, den die wirkende Kausalität ihr abstreift.\n\nDer passiven Substanz wird daher durch die Einwirkung einer andern Gewalt nur ihr Recht angethan. Was sie verliert, ist jene Unmittelbarkeit, die ihr fremde Substantialität. Was sie als ein Fremdes erhält, nämlich als ein Gesetztseyn bestimmt zu werden, ist ihre eigene Bestimmung.\n\nIndem sie nun aber in ihrem Gesetztseyn oder in ihrer eigenen Bestimmung gesetzt wird, wird sie dadurch vielmehr nicht aufgehoben, sondern geht so nur mit sich selbst zusammen, und ist also in ihrem Bestimmtwerden Ursprünglichkeit.—Die passive Substanz wird also einer Seits durch die aktive erhalten oder gesetzt, nämlich insofern diese sich selbst zur aufgehobenen macht;—anderer Seits aber ist es das Thun des Passiven selbst, mit sich zusammenzugehen, und somit sich zum Ursprünglichen und zur Ursache zu machen. Das Gesetztwerden durch ein Anderes und das eigene Werden ist ein und dasselbe.\n\nHierdurch, daß die passive Substanz nun selbst in Ursache verkehrt ist, wird erstlich die Wirkung in ihr aufgehoben; darin besteht ihre Gegenwirkung überhaupt. Sie ist an sich das Gesetztseyn, als passive Substanz; auch ist das Gesetztseyn durch die andere Substanz in ihr gesetzt worden, insofern sie nämlich die Wirkung derselben an ihr bekam. Ihre Gegenwirkung enthält daher ebenso das Gedoppelte; daß nämlich erstlich was sie an sich ist, gesetzt wird, zweitens als was sie gesetzt wird, sich als ihr Ansichseyn darstellt; sie ist an sich Gesetztseyn, daher erhält sie eine Wirkung an ihr durch die andere; aber dieß Gesetztseyn ist umgekehrt ihr eigenes Ansichseyn, so ist dieß ihre Wirkung, sie selbst stellt sich als Ursache dar.\n\nZweitens geht die Gegenwirkung gegen die erste wirkende Ursache. Die Wirkung, welche die vorher passive Substanz in sich aufhebt, ist nämlich eben jene Wirkung der ersten. Die Ursache hat aber ihre substantielle Wirklichkeit nur in ihrer Wirkung; indem diese aufgehoben wird, so wird ihre ursachliche Substantialität aufgehoben. Dieß geschieht erstlich an sich durch sich selbst, indem sie sich zur Wirkung macht; in dieser Identität verschwindet ihre negative Bestimmung und sie wird Passives; zweitens geschieht es durch die vorhin passive, nun rückwirkende Substanz, welche deren Wirkung aufhebt.-In der bestimmten Kausalität wird die Substanz, auf welche gewirkt wird, zwar auch wieder Ursache, sie wirkt hiermit dagegen, daß eine Wirkung in ihr gesetzt wurde. Aber sie wirkte nicht zurück gegen jene Ursache, sondern setzte ihre Wirkung wieder in eine andere Substanz, wodurch der Progreß von Wirkungen ins Unendliche zum Vorschein kam; weil hier die Ursache in ihrer Wirkung nur erst an sich mit sich identisch ist, daher einer Seits in einer unmittelbaren Identität in ihrer Ruhe verschwindet, anderer Seits in einer andern Substanz sich wieder erweckt.—In der bedingten Kausalität hingegen bezieht die Ursache in der Wirkung sich auf sich selbst, wäl sie ihr Anderes als Bedingung als vorausgesetztes ist, und ihr Wirken dadurch ebenso sehr Werden, als Setzen und Aufheben des Andern ist.\n\nFerner verhält sie sich hiermit als passive Substanz; aber, wie sich ergab, entsteht diese durch die auf sie geschehene Wirkung als ursachliche Substanz. Jene erste Ursache, welche zuerst wirkt, und ihre Wirkung als Gegenwirkung in sich zurück erhält, tritt damit wieder als Ursache auf; wodurch das in der endlichen Kausalität in den schlecht-unendlichen Progreß auslaufende Wirken umgebogen, und zu einem in sich zurückkehrenden, einem unendlichen Wechselwirken wird.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0001","text":"Die Kausalität ist voraussetzendes Thun. Die Ursache ist bedingt; sie ist die negative Beziehung auf sich als vorausgesetztes, als äußerliches Anderes, welches an sich aber nur an sich die Kausalität selbst ist. Es ist, wie sich ergeben hat, die substantielle Identität, in welche die formelle Kausalität übergeht, die sich nunmehr gegen dieselbe als ihr Negatives bestimmt hat. Oder es ist dasselbe, was die Substanz des Kausalitätsverhältnisses, aber welcher die Macht der Accidentalität als selbstsubstantielle Thätigkeit gegenüber steht.—Es ist die passive Substanz.—Passiv ist das Unmittelbare, oder Ansichseyende, das nicht auch für sich ist;—das reine Seyn oder das Wesen, das nur in dieser Bestimmtheit der abstrakten Identität mit sich ist.—Der passiven steht die als negativ sich auf sich beziebende, die wirkende Substanz gegenüber.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"166.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0002","text":"Sie ist die Ursache, insofern sie sich in der bestimmten Kausalität durch die Negation ihrer selbst, aus der Wirkung wiederhergestellt hat, das in seinem Andersseyn oder als Unmittelbares sich wesentlich als setzend verhält, und durch seine Negation sich mit sich vermittelt. Die Kausalität hat deswegen hier kein Substrat mehr, dem sie inhärirte und ist nicht Formbestimmung gegen diese Identität sondern selbst die Substanz, oder das Ursprüngliche ist nur die Kausalität.—Das Substrat ist die passive Substanz, die sie sich vorausgesetzt hat.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"166.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0003","text":"Diese Ursache wirkt nun; denn sie ist die negative Macht auf sich selbst; zugleich ist sie ihr Vorausgesetztes; so wirkt sie auf sich als auf ein Anderes, auf die passive Substanz.—Somit hebt sie erstlich das Andersseyn derselben auf; und kehrt in ihr in sich zurück; zweitens bestimmt sie dieselbe, sie setzt dieß Aufheben ihres Andersseyns oder die Rückkehr in sich als eine Bestimmtheit. Dieß Gesetztseyn, weil es zugleich ihre Rückkehr in sich ist, ist zunächst ihre Wirkung.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"166.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0004","text":"Aber umgekehrt weil sie als voraussetzend sich selbst als ihr Anderes bestimmt, so setzt sie die Wirkung in der andern, der passiven Substanz.—Oder weil die passive Substanz selbst das Gedoppelte ist, nämlich ein selbstständiges Anderes, und zugleich ein Vorausgesetztes und an sich schon mit der wirkenden Ursache Identisches, so ist das Wirken von dieser selbst ein Gedoppeltes; es ist beides in Einem, das Aufheben ihres Bestimmtseyns, nämlich ihrer Bedingung, oder das Aufheben der Selbstständigkeit der passiven Substanz;—und daß sie ihre Identität mit derselben aufhebt, somit sich voraus oder als Anderes setzt.—Durch das letztere Moment wird die passive Substanz erhalten; jenes erste Aufheben derselben erscheint in Beziehung hierauf zugleich auch so, daß nur einige Bestimmungen an ihr aufgehoben werden und die Identität ihrer mit der ersten in der Wirkung äußerlich an ihr geschieht.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"166.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0005","text":"Insofern leidet sie Gewalt.—Die Gewalt ist die Erscheinung der Macht, oder die Macht als Äußerliches. Äußerliches ist aber die Macht, nur insofern die ursachliche Substanz in ihrem Wirken, d. h. im Setzen ihrer selbst zugleich voraussetzend ist, d. h. sich selbst als aufgehobenes setzt. Umgekehrt ist daher ebenso sehr das Thun der Gewalt, ein Thun der Macht. Es ist nur ein von ihr selbst vorausgesetztes Anderes, auf welches die gewaltige Ursache wirkt, ihre Wirkung auf dasselbe ist negative Beziehung auf sich, oder die Manifestation ihrer selbst. Das Passive ist das Selbstständige, das nur ein Gesetztes ist; ein in sich selbst Gebrochenes,—eine Wirklichkeit, welche Bedingung ist und zwar die Bedingung nunmehr in ihrer Wahrheit nämlich eine Wirklichkeit, welche nur eine Möglichkeit ist, oder umgekehrt ein Ansichseyn, das nur die Bestimmtheit des Ansichseyns, nur passiv ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"166.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0006","text":"Demjenigen daher, dem Gewalt geschieht, ist es nicht nur möglich, Gewalt anzuthun, sondern sie muß ihm auch angethan werden; was Gewalt über das Andere hat, hat sie nur, weil es die Macht desselben ist, die sich darin und das Andere manifestirt. Die passive Substanz wird durch die Gewalt nur gesetzt, als das was sie in Wahrheit ist, nämlich weil sie das einfache Positive oder unmittelbare Substanz ist, eben darum nur ein Gesetztes zu seyn; das Voraus, das sie als Bedingung ist, ist der Schein der Unmittelbarkeit, den die wirkende Kausalität ihr abstreift.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"166.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0007","text":"Der passiven Substanz wird daher durch die Einwirkung einer andern Gewalt nur ihr Recht angethan. Was sie verliert, ist jene Unmittelbarkeit, die ihr fremde Substantialität. Was sie als ein Fremdes erhält, nämlich als ein Gesetztseyn bestimmt zu werden, ist ihre eigene Bestimmung.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"166.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0008","text":"Indem sie nun aber in ihrem Gesetztseyn oder in ihrer eigenen Bestimmung gesetzt wird, wird sie dadurch vielmehr nicht aufgehoben, sondern geht so nur mit sich selbst zusammen, und ist also in ihrem Bestimmtwerden Ursprünglichkeit.—Die passive Substanz wird also einer Seits durch die aktive erhalten oder gesetzt, nämlich insofern diese sich selbst zur aufgehobenen macht;—anderer Seits aber ist es das Thun des Passiven selbst, mit sich zusammenzugehen, und somit sich zum Ursprünglichen und zur Ursache zu machen. Das Gesetztwerden durch ein Anderes und das eigene Werden ist ein und dasselbe.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"166.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0009","text":"Hierdurch, daß die passive Substanz nun selbst in Ursache verkehrt ist, wird erstlich die Wirkung in ihr aufgehoben; darin besteht ihre Gegenwirkung überhaupt. Sie ist an sich das Gesetztseyn, als passive Substanz; auch ist das Gesetztseyn durch die andere Substanz in ihr gesetzt worden, insofern sie nämlich die Wirkung derselben an ihr bekam. Ihre Gegenwirkung enthält daher ebenso das Gedoppelte; daß nämlich erstlich was sie an sich ist, gesetzt wird, zweitens als was sie gesetzt wird, sich als ihr Ansichseyn darstellt; sie ist an sich Gesetztseyn, daher erhält sie eine Wirkung an ihr durch die andere; aber dieß Gesetztseyn ist umgekehrt ihr eigenes Ansichseyn, so ist dieß ihre Wirkung, sie selbst stellt sich als Ursache dar.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"166.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0010","text":"Zweitens geht die Gegenwirkung gegen die erste wirkende Ursache. Die Wirkung, welche die vorher passive Substanz in sich aufhebt, ist nämlich eben jene Wirkung der ersten. Die Ursache hat aber ihre substantielle Wirklichkeit nur in ihrer Wirkung; indem diese aufgehoben wird, so wird ihre ursachliche Substantialität aufgehoben. Dieß geschieht erstlich an sich durch sich selbst, indem sie sich zur Wirkung macht; in dieser Identität verschwindet ihre negative Bestimmung und sie wird Passives; zweitens geschieht es durch die vorhin passive, nun rückwirkende Substanz, welche deren Wirkung aufhebt.-In der bestimmten Kausalität wird die Substanz, auf welche gewirkt wird, zwar auch wieder Ursache, sie wirkt hiermit dagegen, daß eine Wirkung in ihr gesetzt wurde.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"166.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0011","text":"Aber sie wirkte nicht zurück gegen jene Ursache, sondern setzte ihre Wirkung wieder in eine andere Substanz, wodurch der Progreß von Wirkungen ins Unendliche zum Vorschein kam; weil hier die Ursache in ihrer Wirkung nur erst an sich mit sich identisch ist, daher einer Seits in einer unmittelbaren Identität in ihrer Ruhe verschwindet, anderer Seits in einer andern Substanz sich wieder erweckt.—In der bedingten Kausalität hingegen bezieht die Ursache in der Wirkung sich auf sich selbst, wäl sie ihr Anderes als Bedingung als vorausgesetztes ist, und ihr Wirken dadurch ebenso sehr Werden, als Setzen und Aufheben des Andern ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"166.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0012","text":"Ferner verhält sie sich hiermit als passive Substanz; aber, wie sich ergab, entsteht diese durch die auf sie geschehene Wirkung als ursachliche Substanz. Jene erste Ursache, welche zuerst wirkt, und ihre Wirkung als Gegenwirkung in sich zurück erhält, tritt damit wieder als Ursache auf; wodurch das in der endlichen Kausalität in den schlecht-unendlichen Progreß auslaufende Wirken umgebogen, und zu einem in sich zurückkehrenden, einem unendlichen Wechselwirken wird.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"166.12"}],"sha256":"2ba9a32c623db8ac8d4aed552725728afad764eacd25d1736449e5e5cc347948","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110144553615Z_39bb5229","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"c. Action and Reaction.","source_sha256":"2ba9a32c623db8ac8d4aed552725728afad764eacd25d1736449e5e5cc347948","sha256":"ec63ae6cb712cf25602a40b8a0ee47067070eecc94d159f77f9b3b0fbe663d3a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:01:44.553752+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0001","text":"Causality is presupposing activity. The cause is conditioned; it is the negative relation to itself as presupposed, as external other, which in itself, however, is only in itself causality itself. It is, as has emerged, the substantial identity into which formal causality passes over, which has now determined itself over against it as its negative. Or it is the same as the substance of the relation of causality, but one over against which the power of accidentality stands as self-substantial activity.—It is the passive substance.—Passive is the immediate, or that which is in itself, which is not also for itself;—pure being or essence, which is only in this determinacy of abstract identity with itself.—Over against the passive stands the substance negatively relating itself to itself, the active substance.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"166.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0002","text":"It is the cause insofar as, in determinate causality, it has restored itself out of the effect through the negation of itself, [and] in its otherness or as immediate essentially behaves as positing, and mediates itself with itself through its negation. Causality therefore no longer has here a substrate in which it inhered, and is not determination of form over against this identity, but is itself the substance; or the original is only causality.—The substrate is the passive substance which it has presupposed to itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"166.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0003","text":"This cause now acts; for it is the negative power upon itself; at the same time it is its presupposed [term]; thus it acts upon itself as upon an other, upon the passive substance.—Thus, first, it sublates the otherness of the latter; and returns in it into itself; second, it determines the latter, it posits this sublation of its otherness, or the return into itself, as a determinacy. This positedness, because it is at the same time its return into itself, is at first its effect.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"166.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0004","text":"But conversely, because as presupposing it determines itself as its other, it posits the effect in the other, the passive substance.—Or because the passive substance itself is the doubled [term], namely an independent other, and at the same time a presupposed [term] and in itself already identical with the active cause, the acting of the latter itself is a doubled [one]; it is both in one, the sublation of its determinacy, namely of its condition, or the sublation of the independence of the passive substance;—and that it sublates its identity with the latter, thus posits itself in advance or as other.—Through the latter moment the passive substance is preserved; that first sublation of it appears, in relation to this, at the same time also such that only some determinations in it are sublated and its identity with the first takes place externally upon it in the effect.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"166.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0005","text":"Insofar, it suffers violence.—Violence is the appearance of power, or power as external. But power is external only insofar as the causal substance, in its acting, i.e. in positing itself, is at the same time presupposing, i.e. posits itself as sublated. Conversely, therefore, the exercise of violence is equally an exercise of power. It is only an other presupposed by itself upon which the violent cause acts; its effect upon the same is negative relation to itself, or the manifestation of itself. The passive is the independent [term], which is only a posited [term]; something fractured within itself,—a reality which is condition, indeed the condition now in its truth, namely a reality which is only a possibility, or conversely, a being-in-itself which is only the determinacy of being-in-itself, only passive.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"166.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0006","text":"To that, therefore, to which violence is done, it is not only possible to do violence, but it must also be done to it; what has violence over the other has it only because it is the power of the latter that manifests itself therein and [manifests] the other. Through violence, the passive substance is only posited as what it is in truth, namely, because it is the simple positive or immediate substance, precisely thereby to be only a posited [term]; the in-advance that it is as condition is the semblance of immediacy which active causality strips from it.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"166.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0007","text":"Thus, through the influence of another violence, the passive substance is only accorded its right. What it loses is that immediacy, that alien substantiality to it. What it receives as something alien, namely to be determined as a posited [term], is its own determination.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"166.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0008","text":"But in that it is posited in its positedness or in its own determination, it is thereby rather not sublated, but only thereby comes together with itself, and is thus, in its being-determined, originality.—The passive substance is therefore, on the one hand, preserved or posited by the active, namely insofar as the latter makes itself into the sublated [term];—but, on the other hand, it is the doing of the passive itself to come together with itself, and thus to make itself into the original and into the cause. Being posited through an other and its own becoming are one and the same.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"166.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0009","text":"Thereby, that the passive substance is now itself transformed into cause, the effect in it is first sublated; its counter-action in general consists in this. In itself it is positedness, as passive substance; positedness through the other substance has also been posited in it, insofar as it received the latter's effect upon it. Its counter-action therefore likewise contains the doubled [element]: namely, first, that what it is in itself is posited; second, that what it is posited as presents itself as its being-in-itself; in itself it is positedness, and therefore receives an effect upon it through the other; but conversely this positedness is its own being-in-itself, thus this is its effect: it itself presents itself as cause.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"166.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0010","text":"Second, the counter-action proceeds against the first active cause. For the effect which the previously passive substance sublates within itself is precisely that effect of the first. But the cause has its substantial actuality only in its effect; when this is sublated, its causal substantiality is sublated. This happens first in itself through itself, in that it makes itself into effect; in this identity its negative determination vanishes and it becomes passive; second, it happens through the previously passive, now reacting substance, which sublates its effect.—In determinate causality, the substance upon which action is exerted does indeed again become cause, and thereby acts against the fact that an effect was posited in it.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"166.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0011","text":"But it did not act back against that cause, but posited its effect again in another substance, whereby the progression of effects into infinity came to appearance; because here the cause is only in itself identical with itself in its effect, and therefore, on the one hand, vanishes in an immediate identity in its repose, while, on the other hand, it awakens again in another substance.—In conditioned causality, on the other hand, the cause relates itself to itself in the effect, because its other is its condition, as presupposed [term], and its acting is thereby just as much becoming as positing and sublating the other.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"166.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0012","text":"Further, it thereby behaves as passive substance; but, as has emerged, the latter arises through the effect exerted upon it as causal substance. That first cause, which initially acts and receives its effect back into itself as counter-action, thereby again comes forward as cause; whereby the acting that in finite causality runs out into the spurious-infinite progression is bent back, and becomes an interaction returning into itself, an infinite interaction.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"166.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CWUG:P0012"]}],"source_digest":"fc03cee31af88cf9e34fb1aaaaab67dc24f4fb6f5daab6834d39ee5310255ea7","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"c. Wirkung und Gegenwirkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"c. Wirkung und Gegenwirkung.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4","title":"C. Reciprocal Action.","order":167,"chapter_id":"CH_GB18_CD_4","text":"In der endlichen Kausalität sind es Substanzen, die sich wirkend zu einander verhalten. Der Mechanismus besteht in dieser Äußerlichkeit der Kausalität, daß die Reflexion der Ursache in ihrer Wirkung in sich zugleich ein abstoßendes Seyn ist, oder daß in der Identität, welche die ursachliche Substanz in ihrer Wirkung mit sich hat, sie sich ebenso unmittelbar Äußerliches bleibt, und die Wirkung in eine andere Substanz übergegangen ist. In der Wechselwirkung ist nun dieser Mechanismus aufgehoben; denn sie enthält erstens das Verschwinden jenes ursprünglichen Beharrens der unmittelbaren Substantiaiität; zweitens das Entstehen der Ursache; und damit die Ursprünglichkeit als durch ihre Negation sich mit sich vermittelnd.\n\nZunächst stellt die Wechselwirkung sich dar als eine gegenseitige Kausalität von vorausgesetzten, sich bedingenden Substanzen; jede ist gegen die andere zugleich aktive und zugleich passive Substanz. Indem beide hiermit sowohl passiv als aktiv sind, so hat sich bereits jeder Unterschied derselben aufgehoben; er ist ein völlig durchsichtiger Schein; sie sind Substanzen nur darin, daß sie die Identität des Aktiven und Passiven sind. Die Wechselwirkung selbst ist daher nur noch leere Art und Weise; und es bedarf bloß noch eines äußern Zusammenfassens dessen, was bereits sowohl an sich als gesetzt ist. Fürs erste sind es keine Substrate mehr, welche miteinander in Beziehung stehen, sondern Substanzen; in der Bewegung der bedingten Kausalität hat sich die noch übrige vorausgesetzte Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben, und das Bedingende der ursachlichen Activität ist nur noch die Einwirkung, oder die eigene Passivität. Diese Einwirkung kommt aber ferner nicht von einer andern ursprünglichen Substanz her; sondern eben von einer Ursachlichkeit, welche durch Einwirkung bedingt, oder ein Vermitteltes ist. Dieß zunächst Äußerliche, das an die Ursache kommt und die Seite ihrer Passivität ausmacht, ist daher durch sie selbst vermittelt, es ist durch ihre eigene Aktivität hervorgebracht, somit die durch ihre Aktivität selbst gesetzte Passivität.—Die Kausalität ist bedingt und bedingend; das Bedingende ist das Passive, aber ebenso sehr ist das Bedingte passiv. Dieß Bedingen oder die Passivität ist die Negation der Ursache durch sich selbst, indem sie sich wesentlich zur Wirkung macht, und eben dadurch Ursache ist. Die Wechselwirkung ist daher nur die Kausalität selbst; die Ursache hat nicht nur eine Wirkung, sondern in der Wirkung steht sie als Ursache mit sich selbst in Beziehung.\n\nHierdurch ist die Kausalität zu ihrem absoluten Begriffe zurückgekehrt, und zugleich zum Begriffe selbst gekommen. Sie ist zunächst die reale Nothwendigkeit; absolute Identität mit sich, so daß der Unterschied der Nothwendigkeit und die in ihr sich auf einander beziehenden Bestimmungen, Substanzen, freie Wirklichkeiten, gegen einander, sind. Die Nothwendigkeit ist auf diese Weise die innere Identität; die Kausalität ist die Manifestation derselben, worin ihr Schein des substantiellen Andersseyn sich aufgehoben hat, und die Nothwendigkeit zur Freiheit erhoben ist.—In der Wechselwirkung stellt die ursprüngliche Kausalität sich als ein Entstehen aus ihrer Negation, der Passivität, und als Vergehen in dieselbe, als ein Werden dar; aber so daß dieß Werden zugleich ebenso sehr nur Scheinen ist; das Übergehen in Anderes ist Reflexion-in-sich selbst; die Negation, welche Grund der Ursache ist, ist ihr positives Zusammengehen mit sich selbst.\n\nNothwendigkeit und Kausalität sind also darin verschwunden; sie enthalten beides die unmittelbare Identität als Zusammenhang und Beziehung, und die absolute Substantialität der Unterschiedenen somit die absolute Zufälligkeit derselben; die ursprüngliche Einheit substantieller Verschiedenheit; also den absoluten Widerspruch. Die Nothwendigkeit ist das Seyn, weil es ist; die Einheit des Seyns mit sich selbst, das sich zum Grunde hat; aber umgekehrt weil es einen Grund hat, ist es nicht Seyn, ist es schlechthin nur Schein, Beziehung oder Vermittelung. Die Kausalität ist dieß gesetzte Übergehen des ursprünglichen Seyns, der Ursache, in Schein oder bloßes Gesetztseyn, umgekehrt des Gesetztseyns in Ursprünglichkeit; aber die Identität selbst des Seyns und Scheins ist noch die innere Nothwendigkeit. Diese Innerlichkeit oder dieß Ansichseyn hebt die Bewegung der Kausalität auf; damit verliert sich die Substantialität der im Verhältnisse stehenden Seiten, und die Nothwendigkeit enthüllt sich. Die Nothwendigkeit wird nicht dadurch zur Freiheit, daß sie verschwindet, sondern daß nur ihre noch innere Identität manifestirt wird; eine Manifestation, welche die identische Bewegung des Unterschiedenen in sich selbst, die Reflexion des Scheins als Scheins in sich ist.—Umgekehrt wird zugleich dadurch die Zufälligkeit zur Freiheit, indem die Seiten der Nothwendigkeit, welche die Gestalt für sich freier, nicht in einander scheinender Wirklichkeiten haben, nunmehr gesetzt sind als Identität, so daß diese Totalitäten der Reflexion-in-sich, in ihrem Unterschiede nun auch als identische scheinen, oder gesetzt sind nur als eine und dieselbe Reflexion.\n\nDie absolute Substanz, als absolute Form sich von sich unterscheidend, stößt sich daher nicht mehr als Nothwendigkeit von sich ab, noch fällt sie als Zufälligkeit in gleichgültige, sich äußerliche Substanzen aus einander, sondern unterscheidet sich einer Seits in die Totalität, welche,—die vorhin passive Substanz Ursprüngliches ist als die Reflexion aus der Bestimmtheit in sich, als einfaches Ganzes, das sein Gesetztseyn in sich selbst enthält und als identisch darin mit sich gesetzt ist, das Allgemeine;—anderer Seits in die Totalität,—die vorhin ursachliche Substanz,—als in die Reflexion ebenso aus der Bestimmtheit in sich zur negativen Bestimmtheit, welche so als die mit sich identische Bestimmtheit ebenfalls das Ganze, aber als die mit sich identische Negativität gesetzt ist;—das Einzelne. Unmittelbar aber, weil das Allgemeine nur identisch mit sich ist, indem es die Bestimmtheit als aufgehoben in sich enthält, also das Negative als Negatives ist,—ist es dieselbe Negativität, welche die Einzelnheit ist;—und die Einzelnheit, weil sie ebenso das bestimmte Bestimmte, das Negative als Negatives ist, ist sie unmittelbar dieselbe Identität, welche die Allgemeinheit ist. Diese ihre einfache Identität ist die Besonderheit, welche vom Einzelnen das Moment der Bestimmtheit, vom Allgemeinen das Moment der Reflexion-in-sich in unmittelbarer Einheit enthält. Diese drei Totalitäten sind daher Eine und dieselbe Reflexion, welche als negative Beziehung auf sich in jene beiden sich unterscheidet, aber als in einen vollkommen durchsichtigen Unterschied, nämlich in die bestimmte Einfachheit, oder in die einfache Bestimmtheit, welche ihre Eine und dieselbe Identität ist.—Dieß ist der Begriff, das Reich der Subjektivität oder der Freiheit.\n\n*** END OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG EBOOK WISSENSCHAFT DER LOGIK — BAND 1 ***\n\nUpdated editions will replace the previous one—the old editions will be renamed.\n\nCreating the works from print editions not protected by U.S. copyright law means that no one owns a United States copyright in these works, so the Foundation (and you!) can copy and distribute it in the United States without permission and without paying copyright royalties. Special rules, set forth in the General Terms of Use part of this license, apply to copying and distributing Project Gutenberg™ electronic works to protect the PROJECT GUTENBERG™ concept and trademark. Project Gutenberg is a registered trademark, and may not be used if you charge for an eBook, except by following the terms of the trademark license, including paying royalties for use of the Project Gutenberg trademark. If you do not charge anything for copies of this eBook, complying with the trademark license is very easy. You may use this eBook for nearly any purpose such as creation of derivative works, reports, performances and research. Project Gutenberg eBooks may be modified and printed and given away—you may do practically ANYTHING in the United States with eBooks not protected by U.S. copyright law. Redistribution is subject to the trademark license, especially commercial redistribution.\n\nSTART: FULL LICENSE","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0001","text":"In der endlichen Kausalität sind es Substanzen, die sich wirkend zu einander verhalten. Der Mechanismus besteht in dieser Äußerlichkeit der Kausalität, daß die Reflexion der Ursache in ihrer Wirkung in sich zugleich ein abstoßendes Seyn ist, oder daß in der Identität, welche die ursachliche Substanz in ihrer Wirkung mit sich hat, sie sich ebenso unmittelbar Äußerliches bleibt, und die Wirkung in eine andere Substanz übergegangen ist. In der Wechselwirkung ist nun dieser Mechanismus aufgehoben; denn sie enthält erstens das Verschwinden jenes ursprünglichen Beharrens der unmittelbaren Substantiaiität; zweitens das Entstehen der Ursache; und damit die Ursprünglichkeit als durch ihre Negation sich mit sich vermittelnd.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"167.1"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0002","text":"Zunächst stellt die Wechselwirkung sich dar als eine gegenseitige Kausalität von vorausgesetzten, sich bedingenden Substanzen; jede ist gegen die andere zugleich aktive und zugleich passive Substanz. Indem beide hiermit sowohl passiv als aktiv sind, so hat sich bereits jeder Unterschied derselben aufgehoben; er ist ein völlig durchsichtiger Schein; sie sind Substanzen nur darin, daß sie die Identität des Aktiven und Passiven sind. Die Wechselwirkung selbst ist daher nur noch leere Art und Weise; und es bedarf bloß noch eines äußern Zusammenfassens dessen, was bereits sowohl an sich als gesetzt ist.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"167.2"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0003","text":"Fürs erste sind es keine Substrate mehr, welche miteinander in Beziehung stehen, sondern Substanzen; in der Bewegung der bedingten Kausalität hat sich die noch übrige vorausgesetzte Unmittelbarkeit aufgehoben, und das Bedingende der ursachlichen Activität ist nur noch die Einwirkung, oder die eigene Passivität. Diese Einwirkung kommt aber ferner nicht von einer andern ursprünglichen Substanz her; sondern eben von einer Ursachlichkeit, welche durch Einwirkung bedingt, oder ein Vermitteltes ist. Dieß zunächst Äußerliche, das an die Ursache kommt und die Seite ihrer Passivität ausmacht, ist daher durch sie selbst vermittelt, es ist durch ihre eigene Aktivität hervorgebracht, somit die durch ihre Aktivität selbst gesetzte Passivität.—Die Kausalität ist bedingt und bedingend; das Bedingende ist das Passive, aber ebenso sehr ist das Bedingte passiv.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"167.3"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0004","text":"Dieß Bedingen oder die Passivität ist die Negation der Ursache durch sich selbst, indem sie sich wesentlich zur Wirkung macht, und eben dadurch Ursache ist. Die Wechselwirkung ist daher nur die Kausalität selbst; die Ursache hat nicht nur eine Wirkung, sondern in der Wirkung steht sie als Ursache mit sich selbst in Beziehung.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"167.4"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0005","text":"Hierdurch ist die Kausalität zu ihrem absoluten Begriffe zurückgekehrt, und zugleich zum Begriffe selbst gekommen. Sie ist zunächst die reale Nothwendigkeit; absolute Identität mit sich, so daß der Unterschied der Nothwendigkeit und die in ihr sich auf einander beziehenden Bestimmungen, Substanzen, freie Wirklichkeiten, gegen einander, sind.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"167.5"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0006","text":"Die Nothwendigkeit ist auf diese Weise die innere Identität; die Kausalität ist die Manifestation derselben, worin ihr Schein des substantiellen Andersseyn sich aufgehoben hat, und die Nothwendigkeit zur Freiheit erhoben ist.—In der Wechselwirkung stellt die ursprüngliche Kausalität sich als ein Entstehen aus ihrer Negation, der Passivität, und als Vergehen in dieselbe, als ein Werden dar; aber so daß dieß Werden zugleich ebenso sehr nur Scheinen ist; das Übergehen in Anderes ist Reflexion-in-sich selbst; die Negation, welche Grund der Ursache ist, ist ihr positives Zusammengehen mit sich selbst.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"167.6"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0007","text":"Nothwendigkeit und Kausalität sind also darin verschwunden; sie enthalten beides die unmittelbare Identität als Zusammenhang und Beziehung, und die absolute Substantialität der Unterschiedenen somit die absolute Zufälligkeit derselben; die ursprüngliche Einheit substantieller Verschiedenheit; also den absoluten Widerspruch. Die Nothwendigkeit ist das Seyn, weil es ist; die Einheit des Seyns mit sich selbst, das sich zum Grunde hat; aber umgekehrt weil es einen Grund hat, ist es nicht Seyn, ist es schlechthin nur Schein, Beziehung oder Vermittelung. Die Kausalität ist dieß gesetzte Übergehen des ursprünglichen Seyns, der Ursache, in Schein oder bloßes Gesetztseyn, umgekehrt des Gesetztseyns in Ursprünglichkeit; aber die Identität selbst des Seyns und Scheins ist noch die innere Nothwendigkeit.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"167.7"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0008","text":"Diese Innerlichkeit oder dieß Ansichseyn hebt die Bewegung der Kausalität auf; damit verliert sich die Substantialität der im Verhältnisse stehenden Seiten, und die Nothwendigkeit enthüllt sich. Die Nothwendigkeit wird nicht dadurch zur Freiheit, daß sie verschwindet, sondern daß nur ihre noch innere Identität manifestirt wird; eine Manifestation, welche die identische Bewegung des Unterschiedenen in sich selbst, die Reflexion des Scheins als Scheins in sich ist.—Umgekehrt wird zugleich dadurch die Zufälligkeit zur Freiheit, indem die Seiten der Nothwendigkeit, welche die Gestalt für sich freier, nicht in einander scheinender Wirklichkeiten haben, nunmehr gesetzt sind als Identität, so daß diese Totalitäten der Reflexion-in-sich, in ihrem Unterschiede nun auch als identische scheinen, oder gesetzt sind nur als eine und dieselbe Reflexion.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"167.8"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0009","text":"Die absolute Substanz, als absolute Form sich von sich unterscheidend, stößt sich daher nicht mehr als Nothwendigkeit von sich ab, noch fällt sie als Zufälligkeit in gleichgültige, sich äußerliche Substanzen aus einander, sondern unterscheidet sich einer Seits in die Totalität, welche,—die vorhin passive Substanz Ursprüngliches ist als die Reflexion aus der Bestimmtheit in sich, als einfaches Ganzes, das sein Gesetztseyn in sich selbst enthält und als identisch darin mit sich gesetzt ist, das Allgemeine;—anderer Seits in die Totalität,—die vorhin ursachliche Substanz,—als in die Reflexion ebenso aus der Bestimmtheit in sich zur negativen Bestimmtheit, welche so als die mit sich identische Bestimmtheit ebenfalls das Ganze, aber als die mit sich identische Negativität gesetzt ist;—das Einzelne.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"167.9"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0010","text":"Unmittelbar aber, weil das Allgemeine nur identisch mit sich ist, indem es die Bestimmtheit als aufgehoben in sich enthält, also das Negative als Negatives ist,—ist es dieselbe Negativität, welche die Einzelnheit ist;—und die Einzelnheit, weil sie ebenso das bestimmte Bestimmte, das Negative als Negatives ist, ist sie unmittelbar dieselbe Identität, welche die Allgemeinheit ist. Diese ihre einfache Identität ist die Besonderheit, welche vom Einzelnen das Moment der Bestimmtheit, vom Allgemeinen das Moment der Reflexion-in-sich in unmittelbarer Einheit enthält.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"167.10"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0011","text":"Diese drei Totalitäten sind daher Eine und dieselbe Reflexion, welche als negative Beziehung auf sich in jene beiden sich unterscheidet, aber als in einen vollkommen durchsichtigen Unterschied, nämlich in die bestimmte Einfachheit, oder in die einfache Bestimmtheit, welche ihre Eine und dieselbe Identität ist.—Dieß ist der Begriff, das Reich der Subjektivität oder der Freiheit.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"167.11"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0012","text":"*** END OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG EBOOK WISSENSCHAFT DER LOGIK — BAND 1 ***","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"167.12"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0013","text":"Updated editions will replace the previous one—the old editions will be renamed.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"167.13"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0014","text":"Creating the works from print editions not protected by U.S. copyright law means that no one owns a United States copyright in these works, so the Foundation (and you!) can copy and distribute it in the United States without permission and without paying copyright royalties. Special rules, set forth in the General Terms of Use part of this license, apply to copying and distributing Project Gutenberg™ electronic works to protect the PROJECT GUTENBERG™ concept and trademark. Project Gutenberg is a registered trademark, and may not be used if you charge for an eBook, except by following the terms of the trademark license, including paying royalties for use of the Project Gutenberg trademark. If you do not charge anything for copies of this eBook, complying with the trademark license is very easy.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"167.14"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0015","text":"You may use this eBook for nearly any purpose such as creation of derivative works, reports, performances and research. Project Gutenberg eBooks may be modified and printed and given away—you may do practically ANYTHING in the United States with eBooks not protected by U.S. copyright law. Redistribution is subject to the trademark license, especially commercial redistribution.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"167.15"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0016","text":"START: FULL LICENSE","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"167.16"}],"sha256":"c5829611cd7bfbd566957c5221146f164f385cfde85ee378110c2193df74f030","language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261019T110205368790Z_05d9eed8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"C. Reciprocal Action.","source_sha256":"c5829611cd7bfbd566957c5221146f164f385cfde85ee378110c2193df74f030","sha256":"9f5023e81235b516f8265565d10ee3ba0b4f8eda2d3356cb3de63bb8434eb0b0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:02:05.368819+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0001","text":"In finite causality, substances are those which relate to one another as acting. Mechanism consists in this externality of causality: that the reflection of the cause into itself in its effect is at the same time a repelling being, or that, in the identity which the causal substance has with itself in its effect, it likewise remains immediately external to itself, and the effect has passed over into another substance. In reciprocal action, however, this mechanism is sublated; for it contains, first, the vanishing of that original persistence of immediate substantiality; second, the arising of the cause; and with this, originality as mediating itself with itself through its negation.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"167.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0002","text":"At first, reciprocal action presents itself as a mutual causality of presupposed, mutually conditioning substances; each is, with respect to the other, at once active and at once passive substance. Since both are thereby both passive and active, every difference between them has already sublated itself; it is a wholly transparent appearance; they are substances only insofar as they are the identity of the active and the passive. Reciprocal action itself is therefore now only an empty manner; and there is needed merely an external bringing-together of what is already both in itself and posited.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"167.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0003","text":"In the first place, it is no longer substrates that stand in relation to one another, but substances; in the movement of conditioned causality, the still remaining presupposed immediacy has sublated itself, and what conditions causal activity is now only the influence, or its own passivity. But this influence, furthermore, does not come from another original substance; rather, it comes precisely from a causality which is conditioned through influence, or is a mediated one. This at first external element which comes to the cause and constitutes the side of its passivity is therefore mediated through the cause itself; it is produced through its own activity, hence the passivity posited through its activity itself.—Causality is conditioned and conditioning; what conditions is the passive, but likewise what is conditioned is passive.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"167.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0004","text":"This conditioning, or passivity, is the negation of the cause by itself, in that it essentially makes itself into an effect, and precisely thereby is cause. Reciprocal action is therefore only causality itself; the cause does not merely have an effect, but in the effect it relates to itself as cause.","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"167.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0005","text":"Thereby causality has returned to its absolute concept, and at the same time has arrived at concept itself. At first it is real necessity; absolute identity with itself, such that the difference of necessity and the determinations relating to one another within it, the substances, are free actualities in relation to one another.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"167.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0006","text":"In this way necessity is the inner identity; causality is its manifestation, in which its appearance of substantial other-being has sublated itself, and necessity is elevated to freedom.—In reciprocal action, original causality presents itself as an arising out of its negation, passivity, and as a passing away into the same, as a becoming; but in such a way that this becoming is at the same time just as much only appearance; the transition into an other is reflection-into-itself; the negation which is the ground of the cause is its positive coming-together with itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"167.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0007","text":"Necessity and causality have thus vanished therein; both contain immediate identity as connection and relation, and the absolute substantiality of what is distinct, hence their absolute contingency; the original unity of substantial difference; thus the absolute contradiction. Necessity is being because it is; the unity of being with itself, which has itself for ground; but conversely, because it has a ground, it is not being, it is absolutely only appearance, relation, or mediation. Causality is this posited transition of original being, of the cause, into appearance or mere positedness, conversely of positedness into originality; but the identity itself of being and appearance is still inner necessity.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"167.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0008","text":"This inwardness, or this being-in-itself, sublates the movement of causality; with this the substantiality of the sides standing in relation is lost, and necessity unveils itself. Necessity becomes freedom not by vanishing, but because only its still inner identity is manifested; a manifestation which is the identical movement of what is distinct within itself, the reflection of appearance as appearance into itself.—Conversely, contingency thereby at the same time becomes freedom, in that the sides of necessity, which have the shape of actualities free for themselves, not appearing into one another, are now posited as identity, so that these totalities of reflection-into-self, in their difference, now also appear as identical, or are posited only as one and the same reflection.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"167.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0009","text":"The absolute substance, as absolute form distinguishing itself from itself, therefore no longer repels itself from itself as necessity, nor does it fall apart as contingency into indifferent substances external to one another, but on the one hand distinguishes itself into the totality which,—the previously passive substance—is original as reflection out of determinacy into itself, as a simple whole which contains its positedness within itself and is posited as identical with itself therein, the universal;—on the other hand into the totality,—the previously causal substance,—as reflection likewise out of determinacy into itself, into negative determinacy, which, as determinacy identical with itself, is likewise the whole, but is posited as negativity identical with itself;—the individual.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"167.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0010","text":"But immediately, because the universal is identical with itself only in that it contains determinacy as sublated within itself, hence is the negative as negative,—it is the same negativity which is individuality;—and individuality, because it is likewise the determinate determinate, the negative as negative, is immediately the same identity which universality is. This its simple identity is particularity, which contains in immediate unity the moment of determinacy from the individual, and the moment of reflection-into-itself from the universal.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"167.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0011","text":"These three totalities are therefore one and the same reflection, which as negative relation to itself distinguishes itself into those two, but as into a wholly transparent difference, namely, into determinate simplicity, or into simple determinacy, which is their one and the same identity.—This is the concept, the realm of subjectivity or of freedom.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"167.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0012","text":"*** END OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG EBOOK WISSENSCHAFT DER LOGIK — BAND 1 ***","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"167.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0013","text":"Updated editions will replace the previous one—the old editions will be renamed.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"167.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0014","text":"Creating the works from print editions not protected by U.S. copyright law means that no one owns a United States copyright in these works, so the Foundation (and you!) can copy and distribute it in the United States without permission and without paying copyright royalties. Special rules, set forth in the General Terms of Use part of this license, apply to copying and distributing Project Gutenberg™ electronic works to protect the PROJECT GUTENBERG™ concept and trademark. Project Gutenberg is a registered trademark, and may not be used if you charge for an eBook, except by following the terms of the trademark license, including paying royalties for use of the Project Gutenberg trademark. If you do not charge anything for copies of this eBook, complying with the trademark license is very easy.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"167.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0015","text":"You may use this eBook for nearly any purpose such as creation of derivative works, reports, performances and research. Project Gutenberg eBooks may be modified and printed and given away—you may do practically ANYTHING in the United States with eBooks not protected by U.S. copyright law. Redistribution is subject to the trademark license, especially commercial redistribution.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"167.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0016","text":"START: FULL LICENSE","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"167.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_GB18_CD_4:P0016"]}],"source_digest":"7336ef6d68f5e89962ae0e2ef43c4961c07149f9a8451e97254a062295a98660","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"C. Die Wechselwirkung."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"C. Die Wechselwirkung.","title_language_code":"en"}],"units":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA","layer":"CH","title":"Preface to the First Edition.","order":1,"parents":["RAW_GB18_VZEA"],"revision":"CH_GB18_VZEA@R001","sha256":"6c9cd566619e6de16fc27b601f50d819f78668419acda97b732621d443358d81","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS1","text":"Die Vorrede diagnostiziert eine Diskrepanz zwischen der Umgestaltung des geistigen Selbstbewusstseins und der fortbestehenden Gestalt der Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS2","text":"Der Verlust der vormaligen Metaphysik wird als kulturelle und wissenschaftliche Entleerung des reinen Denkens bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS3","text":"Die überlieferte Logik überlebt institutionell, bleibt aber in Inhalt und Form eine verdünnte Vergangenheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS4","text":"Die geschichtliche Reife eines neuen Prinzips erzeugt die Forderung, dessen anfängliche Intensität in Wissenschaft zu überführen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS5","text":"Wissenschaftliche Philosophie kann ihre Methode weder von äußeren Wissenschaften noch von äußerer Reflexion beziehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS6","text":"Die Selbstbewegung des Begriffs erzeugt zugleich Methode, Inhalt, Wahrheit und Objektivität der logischen Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS7","text":"Die Phänomenologie führt das Bewusstsein zum reinen Wissen; die Logik exponiert danach die reinen Gedanken als ihr eigenes geistiges Leben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","text":"Eine Umgestaltung der substantiellen Geistesform macht überlieferte Bildungsformen inadäquat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A2","text":"Der Verlust der Metaphysik betrifft zugleich ihren Inhalt, ihre Form und die Wirklichkeit des sich mit seinem reinen Wesen beschäftigenden Geistes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","text":"Die erhaltene institutionelle Stellung der Logik garantiert weder ihre wissenschaftliche Erneuerung noch ihre inhaltliche Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","text":"Die logische Wissenschaft ist die eigentliche Metaphysik oder reine spekulative Philosophie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","text":"Wissenschaftliche Methode kann nur aus der Natur ihres Inhalts hervorgehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","text":"Die Reflexion des Inhalts setzt und erzeugt dessen Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A7","text":"Der Verstand fixiert Bestimmungen als getrennte Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A8","text":"Die negative Vernunft löst feste Verstandesbestimmungen auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A9","text":"Die positive Vernunft erzeugt das Allgemeine, in welchem das Besondere immanent bestimmt ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A10","text":"Der Geist vereinigt verständiges Festhalten, dialektische Negation und positive Allgemeinheit in einer Bewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A11","text":"Die immanente Selbstbewegung des Begriffs ist absolute Methode und immanente Seele des Inhalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A12","text":"Das Bewusstsein muss seine Unmittelbarkeit und äußerliche Konkretion ablegen, um reines Wissen zu werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A13","text":"Reines Wissen hat die reinen Gedanken oder Wesenheiten als Gegenstand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A14","text":"Nur der sich selbst konstruierende Weg des Inhalts kann Philosophie als objektive und demonstrierte Wissenschaft begründen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX1","text":"Metaphysik ist nicht durch die Wiederholung der vormaligen Ontologie, Psychologie, Kosmologie oder natürlichen Theologie wiederzugewinnen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX2","text":"Spekulatives Denken ist nicht als Überschreitung der Erfahrung zu verwerfen, die notwendig Hirngespinste hervorbringt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX3","text":"Logik ist nicht ein bloßes Instrument, durch dessen Studium Denken erst erlernt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX4","text":"Die wissenschaftliche Methode ist nicht aus Mathematik, innerer Anschauung oder äußerem Raisonnement zu entlehnen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX5","text":"Dialektik ist nicht ein isoliertes negatives Verfahren, das im Nichts seines Resultats stehenbleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX6","text":"Das Allgemeine ist nicht ein abstrakter Rahmen, unter den ein äußerlich gegebenes Besonderes subsumiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX7","text":"Die Entwicklung eines neuen Prinzips ist nicht durch fanatische Ablehnung, Flucht in Formalismus oder Vermeidung des Besonderen zu vollenden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX8","text":"Wissenschaftliche Objektivität ist nicht durch die Beibehaltung historisch überlieferter Formen erreichbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D1","text":"Der institutionelle Fortbestand der Logik erscheint als äußerliches Überleben einer Wissenschaft, deren innere Form durch die geistige Umgestaltung überholt ist.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D2","text":"Die Erneuerung der Logik verlangt keine Wiederherstellung der alten Metaphysik, sondern ihre Umformung zur Wissenschaft der reinen Gedanken.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A2","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D3","text":"Die wissenschaftliche Ausbildung eines neuen Prinzips verlangt die Durcharbeitung des Besonderen statt dessen Abwehr durch bloße Intensität oder Formalismus.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D4","text":"Die Auflösung einer Bestimmung ist produktiv, weil sie das Allgemeine als konkrete Einheit von Bestimmtheit und Selbstgleichheit hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A7","CH_GB18_VZEA:A8","CH_GB18_VZEA:A9","CH_GB18_VZEA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D5","text":"Die logische Wissenschaft kann nicht zwischen einem fertigen Inhalt und einer nachträglich angewandten Methode unterscheiden.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D6","text":"Die Phänomenologie fungiert als Übergang, in welchem erscheinendes Wissen die Bedingung seiner logischen Selbstexposition hervorbringt.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A12","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13","CH_GB18_VZEA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D7","text":"Die Logik wird von einer formalen Unterrichtsdisziplin zur Darstellung des geistigen Lebens der reinen Wesenheiten umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD1","text":"Objektivität wird als immanente Erzeugung der Bestimmungen bestimmt, nicht als Übereinstimmung eines fertigen Denkens mit einem äußerlich vorausgesetzten Gegenstand.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11","CH_GB18_VZEA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD2","text":"Die historische Niederlage der Metaphysik wird in eine Bedingung ihrer spekulativen Reorganisation überführt: Gerade ihr Verlust macht die Neubegründung der Logik erforderlich.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","CH_GB18_VZEA:A2","CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD3","text":"Negativität und Positivität sind keine entgegengesetzten Erkenntnisweisen, sondern notwendige Momente derselben geistigen Selbstproduktion.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A8","CH_GB18_VZEA:A9","CH_GB18_VZEA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD4","text":"Die Systemarchitektur wird als gestufte Reinigung der Exteriorität konstruiert: Bewusstsein wird reines Wissen, reines Wissen wird Logik, Logik begründet die realen Wissenschaften.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","CH_GB18_VZEA:A12","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13","CH_GB18_VZEA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD5","text":"Die Methode besitzt keinen äußeren Anfangspunkt, weil jeder methodische Anfang bereits durch die Selbstbestimmung des Inhalts legitimiert sein muss.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Verhältnis von Methode und Inhalt, in dem eine fertige Form auf einen vorausgesetzten Gegenstand angewandt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Erkenntnisordnung, in der Verstand, negative Vernunft und positive Vernunft dauerhaft voneinander getrennt bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Begriff des Besonderen, das dem Allgemeinen äußerlich bleibt und nur nachträglich unter es fällt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Annahme, dass der geschichtliche Verlust traditioneller Metaphysik deren spekulativen Gegenstand widerlegt habe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX5","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Wissenschaft, die ihre Legitimation aus praktischer Nützlichkeit, pädagogischer Verwertbarkeit oder bloßem Unterrichtsnutzen bezieht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SNX1","text":"Unverfügbar ist ein endgültiger, unmittelbarer Standpunkt des Denkens, der ohne bestimmte Negation zu Wahrheit gelangt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SNX2","text":"Unzulässig ist ein objektives Wissen, dessen Objektivität durch eine vom Inhalt unabhängige Instanz verbürgt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SNX3","text":"Versperrt ist die Möglichkeit, dass Geist, Methode, Inhalt und Wissenschaft als voneinander äußerliche Ordnungen bestehen könnten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS1","text":"Geistige Umgestaltung → Unangemessenheit überlieferter Formen → Diagnose der überlebenden, aber entleerten Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS2","text":"Verlust traditioneller Metaphysik → Bestimmung der Logik als erneuerte spekulative Wissenschaft → Notwendigkeit eines neuen Wissenschaftsbegriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS3","text":"Ausschluss äußerer Methode → Rückführung der Methode auf die Reflexion des Inhalts → Selbstsetzung der Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS4","text":"Fixierte Bestimmung → bestimmte Negation → Auflösung der Trennung → konkrete Allgemeinheit mit immanentem Besonderen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS5","text":"Konkrete Allgemeinheit → Selbstbewegung des Begriffs → Einheit von Methode und Inhalt → objektive Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS6","text":"Äußerliches Bewusstsein → Befreiung von Unmittelbarkeit → reines Wissen → Logik der reinen Wesenheiten → Grundarchitektur des Systems.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF1","text":"Verlust der Metaphysik → Fortbestand einer alten Logikform → Diagnose wissenschaftlicher Unzulänglichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF2","text":"Reife eines neuen geistigen Prinzips → Forderung nach wissenschaftlicher Ausarbeitung → Zurückweisung externer Methoden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF3","text":"Verstandesbestimmung → dialektische Negation → konkrete Allgemeinheit → absolute Methode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF4","text":"Erscheinendes Bewusstsein → reines Wissen → logische Wissenschaft → zukünftige Systemwissenschaften.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME1","text":"Metaphysik wird von einem historisch erloschenen Disziplinensystem zu der immanenten Wissenschaft der Logik verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME2","text":"Logik wird von einem formalen Werkzeug des richtigen Denkens zu einer Darstellung der Selbstbewegung ihres Inhalts verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME3","text":"Die Opposition von negativ-dialektischer und positiv-konstruierender Vernunft wird als interne Artikulation des Geistes aufgehoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME4","text":"Das Verhältnis von Allgemeinem und Besonderem wird von Subsumtion zu ko-konstitutiver Selbstbestimmung umgeordnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME5","text":"Geschichtlicher Wandel erscheint nicht als äußerer Kontext der Wissenschaft, sondern als Symptom einer notwendigen Transformation ihrer Formen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT1","text":"Surface — Die Vorrede begründet die Notwendigkeit einer erneuerten Logik und ordnet die geplanten Teile des Systems der Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die institutionell erhaltene Logik wird als Form ohne angemessenen Inhalt diagnostiziert, während Methode und Inhalt als untrennbar bestimmt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Der Übergang von einem neuen Prinzip zu Wissenschaft erfordert die Aufgabe äußerer Begründungsformen und die Bearbeitung des Besonderen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Geist ist die zeitlich wirksame Selbstbewegung, in der Bestimmtheit, Negation, Allgemeinheit und Wissenschaft ineinander übergehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Umdeutung der Logik in erneuerte Metaphysik und ihre Bindung an die Selbstbewegung des Begriffs zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt die konkrete kategoriale Durchführung, durch welche die Logik ihre behauptete Selbstbewegung im Einzelnen ausweist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist kohärent, sofern die Identität von Inhalt, Reflexion und Methode zugelassen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT4","text":"Ihre stärkste Verbindung liegt in der produktiven Funktion der Negation, durch welche feste Bestimmungen nicht vernichtet, sondern in konkrete Allgemeinheit überführt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT5","text":"Eine strukturelle Spannung entsteht, weil die Methode als erst in der Logik auszuführende Erkenntnis angekündigt wird, ihre absolute Geltung aber bereits in der Vorrede beansprucht wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT6","text":"Eine weitere Spannung entsteht zwischen der geschichtlichen Diagnose eines Neubeginns und dem Anspruch, dass die logische Bewegung aus dem zeitunabhängigen Inhalt selbst hervorgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT7","text":"Die Vermittlung von Phänomenologie und Logik bleibt zirkulär belastet, weil die Logik sowohl Ergebnis der Reinigung des Bewusstseins als auch Grundlage aller geistigen Entwicklung ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT8","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die Bewegung des Textes, sofern sie historische Diagnose, methodische Ausschlüsse, dialektische Erzeugung und systematische Schließung als eine Maschine behandelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T120048446998Z_c32b8961","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Preface to the First Edition.","source_sha256":"6c9cd566619e6de16fc27b601f50d819f78668419acda97b732621d443358d81","sha256":"82886225351b10e295e8c76f650a76acbbda4f737c3fe9147092fd9147e8a5d2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T12:00:48.448375+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS1","text":"The preface diagnoses a discrepancy between the transformation of spiritual self-consciousness and the persisting form of logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS2","text":"The loss of former metaphysics is determined as a cultural and scientific depletion of pure thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS3","text":"Traditional logic survives institutionally, but remains, in content and form, a diluted past.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS4","text":"The historical maturity of a new principle produces the demand to bring its initial intensity into science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS5","text":"Scientific philosophy can derive its method neither from external sciences nor from external reflection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS6","text":"The self-movement of the Concept simultaneously produces the method, content, truth, and objectivity of logical science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AS7","text":"Phenomenology leads consciousness to pure knowing; logic subsequently expounds the pure thoughts as its own spiritual life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","text":"A transformation of the substantial form of spirit renders traditional forms of education inadequate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A2","text":"The loss of metaphysics concerns at once its content, its form, and the actuality of spirit occupied with its pure essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","text":"The preserved institutional standing of logic guarantees neither its scientific renewal nor its truth in content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","text":"Logical science is metaphysics proper, or pure speculative philosophy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","text":"Scientific method can arise only from the nature of its content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","text":"The reflection of content posits and produces its determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A7","text":"Understanding fixes determinations as separate determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A8","text":"Negative reason dissolves fixed determinations of the understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A9","text":"Positive reason produces the universal in which the particular is immanently determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A10","text":"Spirit unites intellectual fixation, dialectical negation, and positive universality in one movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A11","text":"The immanent self-movement of the Concept is absolute method and the immanent soul of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A12","text":"Consciousness must relinquish its immediacy and external concreteness in order to become pure knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A13","text":"Pure knowing has the pure thoughts or essences as its object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:A14","text":"Only the path of content constructing itself can ground philosophy as objective and demonstrated science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX1","text":"Metaphysics is not to be recovered through the repetition of former ontology, psychology, cosmology, or natural theology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX2","text":"Speculative thinking is not to be rejected as a transgression of experience that necessarily produces figments of the brain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX3","text":"Logic is not a mere instrument through whose study thinking is first learned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX4","text":"Scientific method is not to be borrowed from mathematics, inner intuition, or external reasoning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX5","text":"Dialectic is not an isolated negative procedure that remains at the nothingness of its result.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX6","text":"The universal is not an abstract framework under which an externally given particular is subsumed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX7","text":"The development of a new principle is not to be completed through fanatical rejection, flight into formalism, or avoidance of the particular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:NX8","text":"Scientific objectivity is not attainable through the retention of historically transmitted forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D1","text":"The institutional persistence of logic appears as the external survival of a science whose inner form has been superseded by spiritual transformation.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D2","text":"The renewal of logic demands not the restoration of old metaphysics, but its transformation into the science of pure thoughts.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A2","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D3","text":"The scientific elaboration of a new principle demands the working-through of the particular rather than its warding off by mere intensity or formalism.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D4","text":"The dissolution of a determination is productive because it brings forth the universal as the concrete unity of determinateness and self-sameness.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A7","CH_GB18_VZEA:A8","CH_GB18_VZEA:A9","CH_GB18_VZEA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D5","text":"Logical science cannot distinguish between a finished content and a method applied subsequently.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D6","text":"Phenomenology functions as a transition in which appearing knowing produces the condition of its logical self-exposition.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A12","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13","CH_GB18_VZEA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:D7","text":"Logic is reclassified from a formal discipline of instruction into the exposition of the spiritual life of pure essences.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD1","text":"Objectivity is determined as the immanent production of determinations, not as the correspondence of a finished thinking with an externally presupposed object.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11","CH_GB18_VZEA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD2","text":"The historical defeat of metaphysics is transformed into a condition of its speculative reorganization: precisely its loss makes the re-grounding of logic necessary.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A1","CH_GB18_VZEA:A2","CH_GB18_VZEA:A3","CH_GB18_VZEA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD3","text":"Negativity and positivity are not opposing modes of cognition, but necessary moments of one and the same spiritual self-production.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A8","CH_GB18_VZEA:A9","CH_GB18_VZEA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD4","text":"The system architecture is constructed as a graduated purification of exteriority: consciousness becomes pure knowing, pure knowing becomes logic, logic grounds the real sciences.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A4","CH_GB18_VZEA:A12","CH_GB18_VZEA:A13","CH_GB18_VZEA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SD5","text":"Method has no external point of departure, because every methodological beginning must already be legitimized through the self-determination of content.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZEA:A5","CH_GB18_VZEA:A6","CH_GB18_VZEA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX1","text":"Excluded is a relation of method and content in which a finished form is applied to a presupposed object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX2","text":"Excluded is an order of cognition in which understanding, negative reason, and positive reason remain permanently separate from one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX3","text":"Excluded is a concept of the particular that remains external to the universal and only subsequently falls under it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX4","text":"Excluded is the assumption that the historical loss of traditional metaphysics has refuted its speculative object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:DNX5","text":"Excluded is a science that derives its legitimation from practical utility, pedagogical applicability, or mere instructional benefit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SNX1","text":"Unavailable is a final, immediate standpoint of thinking that arrives at truth without determinate negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SNX2","text":"Impermissible is an objective knowing whose objectivity is guaranteed by an instance independent of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:SNX3","text":"Barred is the possibility that spirit, method, content, and science could subsist as orders external to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS1","text":"Spiritual transformation → inadequacy of traditional forms → diagnosis of surviving yet depleted logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS2","text":"Loss of traditional metaphysics → determination of logic as renewed speculative science → necessity of a new concept of science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS3","text":"Exclusion of external method → reduction of method to the reflection of content → self-positing of determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS4","text":"Fixed determination → determinate negation → dissolution of separation → concrete universality with immanent particularity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS5","text":"Concrete universality → self-movement of the Concept → unity of method and content → objective science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:FGS6","text":"External consciousness → liberation from immediacy → pure knowing → logic of pure essences → fundamental architecture of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF1","text":"Loss of metaphysics → persistence of an old form of logic → diagnosis of scientific inadequacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF2","text":"Maturity of a new spiritual principle → demand for scientific elaboration → rejection of external methods.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF3","text":"Determination of the understanding → dialectical negation → concrete universality → absolute method.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:AF4","text":"Appearing consciousness → pure knowing → logical science → future systematic sciences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME1","text":"Metaphysics is shifted from a historically extinct system of disciplines to the immanent science of logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME2","text":"Logic is shifted from a formal tool of correct thinking to an exposition of the self-movement of its content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME3","text":"The opposition of negative-dialectical and positive-constructive reason is sublated as an internal articulation of spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME4","text":"The relation of universal and particular is reordered from subsumption to co-constitutive self-determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ME5","text":"Historical change appears not as an external context of science, but as a symptom of a necessary transformation of its forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT1","text":"Surface — The preface grounds the necessity of a renewed logic and orders the planned parts of the system of science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT2","text":"Structural — Institutionally preserved logic is diagnosed as form without adequate content, while method and content are determined as inseparable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The transition from a new principle to science requires the abandonment of external forms of grounding and the treatment of the particular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Spirit is the temporally effective self-movement in which determinateness, negation, universality, and science pass over into one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the reinterpretation of logic as renewed metaphysics and its binding to the self-movement of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT2","text":"What remains underdetermined is the concrete categorial execution through which logic exhibits its claimed self-movement in detail.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT3","text":"The structure is coherent insofar as the identity of content, reflection, and method is admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT4","text":"Its strongest connection lies in the productive function of negation, through which fixed determinations are not destroyed but transferred into concrete universality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT5","text":"A structural tension arises because the method is announced as cognition to be carried out only in logic, while its absolute validity is already claimed in the preface.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT6","text":"A further tension arises between the historical diagnosis of a new beginning and the claim that logical movement arises from the time-independent content itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT7","text":"The mediation of phenomenology and logic remains burdened by circularity, because logic is both the result of the purification of consciousness and the foundation of all spiritual development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZEA:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text insofar as it treats historical diagnosis, methodological exclusions, dialectical production, and systematic closure as one machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZEA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_VZEA@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_VZEA:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 01","title":"Preface to the First Edition.","context":"Chapter 01","original_title":"Vorrede zur ersten Ausgabe."},"original_title":"Vorrede zur ersten Ausgabe.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA","layer":"CH","title":"Preface to the Second Edition.","order":2,"parents":["RAW_GB18_VZZA"],"revision":"CH_GB18_VZZA@R001","sha256":"9d1712648ee045f1ba4e386934d5bb7fbdc808ad6d5766c4fb30fb9e5e12ac8c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS1","text":"Die überlieferte Logik stellt Denkformen bereit, erfasst sie aber nur äußerlich und nicht in ihrer spekulativen Notwendigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS2","text":"Logik wird erst Wissenschaft, wenn sie das Denken als immanente und notwendige Selbstentwicklung darstellt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS3","text":"Das Argument verfährt rekonstruktiv, spekulativ und polemisch gegen instrumentelle, formalistische und erkenntniskritische Modelle des Denkens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS4","text":"Die Bewegung führt vom bewusstlosen Gebrauch vertrauter Kategorien über deren abstrakte Isolierung zur Kritik ihrer fixierten Endlichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS5","text":"Das Verhältnis kehrt sich um: Nicht das Subjekt verfügt über Kategorien, sondern Kategorien strukturieren Subjektivität und Gegenständlichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS6","text":"Die Trennung von Form und Inhalt wird in den einen Begriff zurückgeführt, dessen Bestimmungen sich immanent auseinander entwickeln.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS7","text":"Die bewusste Rekonstruktion dieser Entwicklung erzeugt Freiheit und Wahrheit, bleibt aber als Darstellung durch kontingente Reflexionen und moderne Rezeptionsbedingungen gebrochen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A1","text":"Die überlieferte Logik liefert die Denkformen nur als äußerlich fixiertes Material.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","text":"Gegenstand der logischen Wissenschaft ist die notwendige immanente Selbstentwicklung des Denkens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A3","text":"Denkbestimmungen durchziehen Sprache, Vorstellung, Begehren, Wollen und Handeln überwiegend bewusstlos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A4","text":"Die Vertrautheit mit einer Denkbestimmung ist nicht deren Erkenntnis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","text":"Die Absonderung der Denkformen von ihrem sinnlichen und praktischen Stoff ist die notwendige Anfangsstufe ihrer Erkenntnis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A6","text":"Die Beschäftigung mit reinen Gedanken setzt Distanz zu unmittelbaren Bedürfnissen und konkreten Interessen voraus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A7","text":"Denkbestimmungen sind keine vom Subjekt beherrschten Mittel, sondern Bestimmungen seiner geistigen Tätigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","text":"Der reine Begriff bildet zugleich das Innerste des subjektiven Denkens und das objektive Wesen der Sache.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A9","text":"Für das Erkennen ist die Sache nicht anders gegeben als in ihrem Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","text":"Inhalt besitzt Bestimmtheit und Gehalt nur durch seine immanente Form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","text":"Jeder bestimmte Begriff ist eine Formbestimmung des einen substantiellen Begriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","text":"Isolierte und als selbständig fixierte Denkbestimmungen sind endlich und unwahr.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A13","text":"Zweck der Logik ist Wahrheit und nicht bloß formale Richtigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A14","text":"Das Bewusstmachen und Reinigen instinktiv wirkender Kategorien ist Bedingung geistiger Freiheit und Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","text":"Jede Stufe der logischen Darstellung darf nur Bestimmungen verwenden, die aus ihr und den vorangegangenen Stufen hervorgehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A16","text":"Die Prüfung des logischen Anfangs verlangt den Durchgang durch die gesamte Entwicklung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A17","text":"Die wirkliche Darstellung muss wegen der Unruhe des modernen Bewusstseins kontingente Abwehrreflexionen aufnehmen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX1","text":"Eine Sammlung, Wiederholung oder mechanische Bearbeitung überlieferter Denkformen ist keine spekulative Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX2","text":"Der alltägliche Gebrauch von Kategorien ist nicht ihre wissenschaftliche Erkenntnis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX3","text":"Logik ist kein bloßes Hilfsmittel für außerhalb ihrer liegende Zwecke.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX4","text":"Denkbestimmungen sind keine inhaltslosen äußeren Formen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX5","text":"Kategorien sind kein frei verfügbares Eigentum des denkenden Subjekts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX6","text":"Gedanken bilden keine trennende Mitte zwischen Subjekt und Sache.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX7","text":"Das Ding-an-sich ist kein positiv bestimmter Gegenstand jenseits des Denkens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX8","text":"Formale Identität und Schlussregeln konstituieren nicht selbst Wahrheit; ihre Geltung bleibt auf Richtigkeit beschränkt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX9","text":"Gegenstand der Logik ist keine äußerliche Vielheit von Dingen oder unverbundenen Begriffen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX10","text":"Gegensätze wie Form und Inhalt, Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit oder Inneres und Äußeres dürfen nicht ungeprüft vorausgesetzt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX11","text":"Die Fixierung auf den Anfang ersetzt nicht die Untersuchung der vollständigen Entwicklung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX12","text":"Philosophie ist nicht auf eine künstlich abgesonderte Terminologie angewiesen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D1","text":"Natürliches Denken ist bereits logisch strukturiert, bevor es seine logische Struktur erkennt.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A3","CH_GB18_VZZA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D2","text":"Logische Wissenschaft rekonstruiert die in Sprache und Überlieferung vorhandenen Denkformen als notwendige Entwicklung.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A1","CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D3","text":"Die notwendige Abstraktion der Denkformen wird unwahr, sobald sie als endgültige Trennung von Form und Inhalt fixiert wird.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","CH_GB18_VZZA:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D4","text":"Geistige Freiheit besteht nicht in der Willkür über Kategorien, sondern im bewussten Verhältnis zu ihrer Notwendigkeit.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A7","CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D5","text":"Das als gedankenjenseitig gesetzte Ding-an-sich fällt als leere Abstraktion selbst in das Denken zurück.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D6","text":"Ein formloser Inhalt ist leer, während Form selbst die Bestimmtheit hervorbringt, die als Inhalt erscheint.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D7","text":"Die Vielheit bestimmter Begriffe ist die interne Differenzierung eines einzigen substantiellen Begriffs.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D8","text":"Die immanente Prüfung einer fixierten Kategorie legt ihre Endlichkeit offen und erzwingt ihren Übergang in eine umfassendere Bestimmung.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D9","text":"Formale Verfahren können richtige Schlüsse sichern und zugleich Irrtum oder Sophisterei dienen, weil sie Wahrheit nicht aus sich bestimmen.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","CH_GB18_VZZA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D10","text":"Die Freiheit reiner Wissenschaft beruht darauf, dass ihr Gegenstand nicht durch unmittelbaren Nutzen oder äußere Interessen bestimmt wird.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A6","CH_GB18_VZZA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D11","text":"Ein Einwand gegen eine Kategorie ist unzulänglich, solange er ungeprüfte Kategorien aus späteren oder anderen Stufen voraussetzt.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D12","text":"Die tatsächliche Darstellung verbindet notwendige Entwicklung mit methodisch fremden, aber rezeptionsbedingt unvermeidlichen Reflexionen.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD1","text":"Logische Wissenschaft ist zugleich Ontologie und Selbstwissen des Geistes, weil derselbe Begriff Denken und Sache strukturiert.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A9","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","CH_GB18_VZZA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD2","text":"Ein außerlogisches Außen ist systematisch ausgeschlossen, weil Gegenstände, Inhalte und Einwände nur durch Denkbestimmungen bestimmbar werden.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A3","CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A9","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD3","text":"Freiheit wird als bewusst gewordene begriffliche Notwendigkeit und nicht als Abwesenheit von Bestimmung erzeugt.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A7","CH_GB18_VZZA:A14","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD4","text":"Die formale Abstraktion ist eine notwendige, aber selbstaufhebende Stufe: Sie ermöglicht Erkenntnis und verhindert Wahrheit, sofern sie fixiert bleibt.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","CH_GB18_VZZA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD5","text":"Methode und Gegenstand fallen zusammen, weil allein die Selbstbewegung des Begriffs den Begriff angemessen darstellen kann.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD6","text":"Das System begründet seinen Anfang rückwirkend durch die Totalität seiner Entwicklung.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD7","text":"Die logische Darstellung ist strukturell gespalten zwischen dem Ideal reiner Immanenz und der Notwendigkeit polemischer Selbstverteidigung.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD8","text":"Das System trennt die historische Ermöglichung reinen Denkens von der nicht-historischen Notwendigkeit seines Gegenstands.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A6","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX1","text":"Ein bestimmter nichtbegrifflicher Gegenstand kann dem Denken keinen äußeren Maßstab liefern.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX2","text":"Das Subjekt verfügt über keinen Standort außerhalb der Kategorien, durch die es denkt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX3","text":"Eine endliche Denkbestimmung besitzt isoliert keine Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX4","text":"Ein formloser Inhalt kann keine positive Bestimmtheit besitzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX5","text":"Die Vielheit bestimmter Begriffe ist nicht ontologisch ursprünglich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX6","text":"Fixierte Gegensätze sind keine voraussetzungslosen Evidenzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX7","text":"Ein erster Grund kann nicht vor seiner Entwicklung durch ein äußeres Kriterium gesichert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX8","text":"Darstellung ist kein der dargestellten Sache gleichgültiger Behälter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX9","text":"Freiheit kann nicht als Willkür gegenüber begrifflicher Notwendigkeit gelten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX1","text":"Ein extra-logischer Standpunkt, von dem aus Denken und Sache unabhängig voneinander verglichen werden könnten, ist nicht verfügbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX2","text":"Eine unmittelbare und vorprozessuale Letztbegründung des Anfangs ist versperrt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX3","text":"Keine stabile Trennung von Subjekt und Objekt, Form und Inhalt oder Endlichkeit und Unendlichkeit darf als Endzustand bestehen bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX4","text":"Eine vollkommen reine Selbstdarstellung des Begriffs bleibt unter den Bedingungen moderner Rezeption und äußerer Textproduktion unerreichbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS1","text":"Überlieferte Denkformen plus sprachliche Sedimentierung → vertraute, aber bewusstlose natürliche Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS2","text":"Absonderung vom sinnlichen und praktischen Stoff → Gegenständlichkeit der Denkformen → formale Anfangswissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS3","text":"Kritik des Mittelmodells → Umkehrung des Besitzverhältnisses → Kategorien als strukturierende Mächte → Begriff als subjektiv-objektive Grundlage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS4","text":"Kritik der äußeren Form → Leere des formlosen Inhalts → Form als Inhaltsbestimmung → Einheit von Form und Gehalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS5","text":"Fixierte Kategorie → Prüfung ihres Für-sich-Seins → Offenlegung ihrer Endlichkeit → notwendiger Übergang → begriffliche Totalität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS6","text":"Immanente Gesamtsequenz → Bewusstmachen der Kategorien → Reinigung ihrer vereinzelten Wirksamkeit → Freiheit und Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS7","text":"Einwurf → Freilegung seiner vorausgesetzten Kategorien → Zurückweisung des äußeren Maßstabs → Zuweisung einer systematischen Stelle → Fortgang durch die Gesamtentwicklung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS8","text":"Immanenzideal → Ausschluss äußerer Reflexionen; moderne Rezeptionsbedingung → Wiedereinführung negativer Reflexionen → unvermeidliche Darstellungsunreinheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF1","text":"Äußerlich überlieferte Denkformen → sprachliche und praktische Allgegenwart → Differenz von Bekanntheit und Erkenntnis → Absonderung der Formen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF2","text":"Kategorien als Mittel → Kategorien als beherrschende Strukturen → Begriff als Innerstes von Denken und Sache → Kollaps des Ding-an-sich als Außen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF3","text":"Fixierte Form-Inhalt-Trennung → Endlichkeit formaler Kategorien → Form als Gehalt → bestimmte Begriffe als Momente des einen Begriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF4","text":"Unbewusste natürliche Logik → immanente Rekonstruktion → kategoriales Selbstwissen → geistige Freiheit und Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF5","text":"Reine Entwicklungsforderung → Kritik voraussetzungsreicher Einwürfe → Vorrang des vollständigen Durchgangs → rezeptionsbedingte Einschränkung der Darstellungsreinheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME1","text":"Vertraute Kategorien werden von selbstverständlichen Mitteln zu unerkannten Gegenständen wissenschaftlicher Erkenntnis umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME2","text":"Kategorien wechseln ihren Status von subjektiven Werkzeugen zu Strukturen, die Subjektivität und Gegenständlichkeit zugleich bestimmen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME3","text":"Logik wird von einer Lehre formaler Richtigkeit zu einer Wissenschaft der Wahrheit und des Seienden verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME4","text":"Die Opposition von Denken und Sache wird als interne Differenz des Begriffs neu kartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME5","text":"Form und Inhalt erscheinen nicht länger als unabhängige Bestandteile, sondern als Momente derselben begrifflichen Selbstbestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME6","text":"Die Vielheit der Begriffe wird von einer äußerlichen Sammlung in die Gliederung einer einzigen Totalität überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME7","text":"Einwände werden nicht mehr als externe Prüfungen, sondern als selbst kategorial bestimmte Operationen innerhalb des Systems behandelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME8","text":"Freiheit wird von kategorialer Verfügungsmacht zu bewusstem Vollzug begrifflicher Notwendigkeit umgezeichnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME9","text":"Sprache wird vom neutralen Ausdrucksmittel zum Sedimentierungsraum und Vorfeld logischer Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT1","text":"Surface — Die Neubearbeitung wird durch die Unzulänglichkeit der überlieferten und früheren Darstellung sowie durch die Schwierigkeit einer immanenten Exposition begründet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT2","text":"Structural — Kategorien bilden die unbewusste Struktur von Sprache, geistiger Tätigkeit und Gegenständlichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Kritik wird an die immanente Entwicklung gebunden; externe Einwände werden als ungeprüfte kategoriale Voraussetzungen reklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT4","text":"Ontological — Der Begriff fungiert als Logos, substantielle Einheit und gemeinsame Grundlage von Denken und Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT5","text":"Temporal — Die Bewegung verläuft von bedürfnisgebundener Unmittelbarkeit über Abstraktion und formale Fixierung zur systematischen Selbstvermittlung und bewussten Freiheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT1","text":"Das Axiomensystem reicht aus, um die diagnostische, ontologische und methodische Bewegung der Vorrede zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleiben die konkreten Übergangsregeln zwischen einzelnen Kategorien, weil die Vorrede deren Notwendigkeit fordert, aber nicht ausführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist dort am stärksten, wo das Mittel- und Formmodell des Denkens in eine Analyse kategorialer Wirksamkeit überführt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT4","text":"Die interne Kohärenz hängt von der vorausgesetzten Einheit des subjektiven Denkens und des objektiven Begriffs ab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT5","text":"Die Forderung strenger Immanenz steht in Spannung zur Aufnahme polemischer, psychologischer und rezeptionsbezogener Reflexionen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT6","text":"Die Identität von Begriff und Sache trägt die Aufhebung des Ding-an-sich, wird in der Vorrede jedoch eher gesetzt als entwickelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT7","text":"Die rückwirkende Rechtfertigung des Anfangs durch das Ganze kontrolliert die Zirkularität des Systems, beseitigt sie aber nicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT8","text":"Die Bestimmung der Logik als zweckfreie Wissenschaft steht in Spannung zu ihrer zugewiesenen Funktion, den Geist zu Freiheit und Wahrheit zu erheben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT9","text":"Die Zurückweisungen formaler Logik und kritischer Philosophie gewinnen ihre Kraft durch Kompression konkurrierender Positionen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT10","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur, wenn notwendige Entwicklung, rückwirkende Begründung und eingestandene Darstellungsunreinheit zugleich erhalten bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T120139522888Z_3da8359b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Preface to the Second Edition.","source_sha256":"9d1712648ee045f1ba4e386934d5bb7fbdc808ad6d5766c4fb30fb9e5e12ac8c","sha256":"f312fbd3acb63724a318de01a427e29c3b1f6af09dbae2048308d60e4f1a4357","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T12:01:39.525224+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS1","text":"Traditional logic provides forms of thought, but grasps them only externally and not in their speculative necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS2","text":"Logic becomes science only when it presents thinking as immanent and necessary self-development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds reconstructively, speculatively, and polemically against instrumental, formalist, and epistemologically critical models of thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS4","text":"The movement leads from the unconscious use of familiar categories, through their abstract isolation, to the critique of their fixed finitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS5","text":"The relation is reversed: it is not the subject that disposes of categories, but categories that structure subjectivity and objectivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS6","text":"The separation of form and content is brought back into the one Concept, whose determinations develop themselves immanently apart.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AS7","text":"The conscious reconstruction of this development produces freedom and truth, but as presentation remains fractured by contingent reflections and modern conditions of reception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A1","text":"Traditional logic supplies forms of thought only as externally fixed material.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","text":"The object of logical science is the necessary immanent self-development of thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A3","text":"Determinations of thought pervade language, representation, desire, willing, and acting predominantly unconsciously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A4","text":"Familiarity with a determination of thought is not knowledge of it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","text":"The separation of forms of thought from their sensuous and practical material is the necessary initial stage of their cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A6","text":"Preoccupation with pure thoughts presupposes distance from immediate needs and concrete interests.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A7","text":"Determinations of thought are not means controlled by the subject, but determinations of its spiritual activity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","text":"The pure Concept constitutes at once the innermost of subjective thinking and the objective essence of the thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A9","text":"For cognition, the thing is given no otherwise than in its Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","text":"Content possesses determinacy and import only through its immanent form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","text":"Every determinate Concept is a determination of form of the one substantial Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","text":"Isolated determinations of thought, fixed as self-subsistent, are finite and untrue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A13","text":"The purpose of logic is truth and not merely formal correctness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A14","text":"Making instinctively operative categories conscious and purifying them is a condition of spiritual freedom and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","text":"Each stage of logical presentation may use only determinations that proceed from it and from the preceding stages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A16","text":"The examination of the logical beginning requires passage through the entire development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:A17","text":"The actual presentation must, because of the unrest of modern consciousness, incorporate contingent defensive reflections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX1","text":"A collection, repetition, or mechanical treatment of traditional forms of thought is not speculative logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX2","text":"The everyday use of categories is not their scientific cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX3","text":"Logic is not a mere auxiliary for purposes lying outside it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX4","text":"Determinations of thought are not contentless external forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX5","text":"Categories are not freely disposable property of the thinking subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX6","text":"Thoughts do not form a separating middle between subject and thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX7","text":"The thing-in-itself is not a positively determinate object beyond thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX8","text":"Formal identity and rules of inference do not themselves constitute truth; their validity remains restricted to correctness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX9","text":"The object of logic is not an external multiplicity of things or unconnected Concepts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX10","text":"Oppositions such as form and content, finitude and infinity, or inner and outer must not be presupposed without examination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX11","text":"Fixation upon the beginning does not replace the investigation of the complete development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:NX12","text":"Philosophy does not depend on an artificially segregated terminology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D1","text":"Natural thinking is already logically structured before it recognizes its logical structure.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A3","CH_GB18_VZZA:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D2","text":"Logical science reconstructs the forms of thought present in language and tradition as necessary development.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A1","CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D3","text":"The necessary abstraction of forms of thought becomes untrue as soon as it is fixed as a final separation of form and content.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","CH_GB18_VZZA:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D4","text":"Spiritual freedom does not consist in arbitrariness over categories, but in the conscious relation to their necessity.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A7","CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D5","text":"The thing-in-itself posited as beyond thought falls back into thinking itself as an empty abstraction.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D6","text":"Formless content is empty, whereas form itself brings forth the determinacy that appears as content.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D7","text":"The multiplicity of determinate Concepts is the internal differentiation of a single substantial Concept.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D8","text":"The immanent examination of a fixed category discloses its finitude and compels its transition into a more comprehensive determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D9","text":"Formal procedures can secure correct inferences and at the same time serve error or sophistry, because they do not determine truth from themselves.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","CH_GB18_VZZA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D10","text":"The freedom of pure science rests on the fact that its object is not determined by immediate utility or external interests.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A6","CH_GB18_VZZA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D11","text":"An objection to a category is inadequate so long as it presupposes unexamined categories from later or other stages.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:D12","text":"The actual presentation combines necessary development with reflections methodologically alien to it, yet unavoidable owing to conditions of reception.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD1","text":"Logical science is at once ontology and the self-knowledge of spirit, because the same Concept structures thinking and thing.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A9","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","CH_GB18_VZZA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD2","text":"An extra-logical outside is systematically excluded, because objects, contents, and objections become determinable only through determinations of thought.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A3","CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A9","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD3","text":"Freedom is produced as conceptual necessity that has become conscious, and not as the absence of determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A7","CH_GB18_VZZA:A14","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD4","text":"Formal abstraction is a necessary but self-sublating stage: it makes cognition possible and prevents truth insofar as it remains fixed.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A5","CH_GB18_VZZA:A10","CH_GB18_VZZA:A12","CH_GB18_VZZA:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD5","text":"Method and object coincide, because only the self-movement of the Concept can adequately present the Concept.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A8","CH_GB18_VZZA:A11","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD6","text":"The system retrospectively grounds its beginning through the totality of its development.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD7","text":"Logical presentation is structurally split between the ideal of pure immanence and the necessity of polemical self-defense.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A15","CH_GB18_VZZA:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SD8","text":"The system separates the historical enabling of pure thinking from the non-historical necessity of its object.","refs":["CH_GB18_VZZA:A2","CH_GB18_VZZA:A6","CH_GB18_VZZA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX1","text":"A determinate non-conceptual object cannot provide thinking with an external standard.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX2","text":"The subject has no standpoint outside the categories through which it thinks.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX3","text":"A finite determination of thought possesses no truth in isolation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX4","text":"Formless content cannot possess positive determinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX5","text":"The multiplicity of determinate Concepts is not ontologically original.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX6","text":"Fixed oppositions are not presuppositionless evidences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX7","text":"A first ground cannot be secured by an external criterion prior to its development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX8","text":"Presentation is not a container indifferent to the thing presented.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:DNX9","text":"Freedom cannot count as arbitrariness in relation to conceptual necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX1","text":"An extra-logical standpoint from which thinking and thing could be compared independently of one another is unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX2","text":"An immediate and pre-processual ultimate grounding of the beginning is blocked.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX3","text":"No stable separation of subject and object, form and content, or finitude and infinity may remain as a final state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:SNX4","text":"A completely pure self-presentation of the Concept remains unattainable under the conditions of modern reception and external textual production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS1","text":"Traditional forms of thought plus linguistic sedimentation → familiar yet unconscious natural logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS2","text":"Separation from sensuous and practical material → objectivity of forms of thought → formal initial science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS3","text":"Critique of the means-model → reversal of the relation of possession → categories as structuring powers → Concept as subjective-objective foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS4","text":"Critique of external form → emptiness of formless content → form as determination of content → unity of form and import.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS5","text":"Fixed category → examination of its being-for-itself → disclosure of its finitude → necessary transition → conceptual totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS6","text":"Immanent total sequence → making categories conscious → purification of their isolated efficacy → freedom and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS7","text":"Objection → disclosure of its presupposed categories → rejection of the external standard → assignment of a systematic place → progression through the total development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:FGS8","text":"Ideal of immanence → exclusion of external reflections; modern condition of reception → reintroduction of negative reflections → unavoidable impurity of presentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF1","text":"Externally transmitted forms of thought → linguistic and practical ubiquity → difference between familiarity and cognition → separation of the forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF2","text":"Categories as means → categories as governing structures → Concept as innermost of thinking and thing → collapse of the thing-in-itself as an outside.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF3","text":"Fixed form-content separation → finitude of formal categories → form as import → determinate Concepts as moments of the one Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF4","text":"Unconscious natural logic → immanent reconstruction → categorial self-knowledge → spiritual freedom and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:AF5","text":"Demand for pure development → critique of presupposition-laden objections → priority of the complete passage → reception-conditioned restriction of the purity of presentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME1","text":"Familiar categories are reclassified from self-evident means into unrecognized objects of scientific cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME2","text":"Categories change their status from subjective tools to structures that determine subjectivity and objectivity at once.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME3","text":"Logic is shifted from a doctrine of formal correctness to a science of truth and of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME4","text":"The opposition of thinking and thing is remapped as an internal difference of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME5","text":"Form and content no longer appear as independent components, but as moments of the same conceptual self-determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME6","text":"The multiplicity of Concepts is transferred from an external collection into the articulation of a single totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME7","text":"Objections are no longer treated as external examinations, but as operations themselves categorically determined within the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME8","text":"Freedom is redrawn from categorial power of disposal into conscious enactment of conceptual necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ME9","text":"Language is transformed from a neutral means of expression into a space of sedimentation and preliminary field of logical determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT1","text":"Surface — The revision is grounded in the inadequacy of the traditional and earlier presentation, as well as in the difficulty of an immanent exposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT2","text":"Structural — Categories constitute the unconscious structure of language, spiritual activity, and objectivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Critique is bound to immanent development; external objections are reclassified as unexamined categorial presuppositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT4","text":"Ontological — The Concept functions as Logos, substantial unity, and the common foundation of thinking and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:ALT5","text":"Temporal — The movement proceeds from need-bound immediacy through abstraction and formal fixation to systematic self-mediation and conscious freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT1","text":"The axiom system suffices to reconstruct the diagnostic, ontological, and methodological movement of the Preface.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT2","text":"The concrete rules of transition between individual categories remain underdetermined, because the Preface demands their necessity but does not carry it out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT3","text":"The structure is strongest where the means- and form-model of thinking is transformed into an analysis of categorial efficacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence depends on the presupposed unity of subjective thinking and the objective Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT5","text":"The demand for strict immanence stands in tension with the incorporation of polemical, psychological, and reception-related reflections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT6","text":"The identity of Concept and thing bears the sublation of the thing-in-itself, but in the Preface it is posited rather than developed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT7","text":"The retrospective justification of the beginning through the whole controls the circularity of the system, but does not eliminate it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT8","text":"The determination of logic as purposeless science stands in tension with its assigned function of raising spirit to freedom and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT9","text":"The rejections of formal logic and critical philosophy gain their force through compression of competing positions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_VZZA:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if necessary development, retrospective grounding, and acknowledged impurity of presentation are maintained together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_VZZA:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_VZZA@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_VZZA:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 02","title":"Preface to the Second Edition.","context":"Chapter 02","original_title":"Vorrede zur zweiten Auflage."},"original_title":"Vorrede zur zweiten Auflage.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL","layer":"CH","title":"General Concept of Logic","order":3,"parents":["RAW_GB18_ABDL"],"revision":"CH_GB18_ABDL@R001","sha256":"67a738218dd884797817cf53bda36b7ae5cf3a30bf7ee48276016a73354d1d65","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS1","text":"Die Logik kann ihren Gegenstand, ihre Formen, ihre Methode und ihren Wissenschaftsbegriff nicht voraussetzen, weil sie selbst deren Begründung leisten muss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS2","text":"Der überlieferte Logikbegriff erzeugt seine Gehaltlosigkeit durch die Trennung von Form und Inhalt sowie von Denken und Gegenstand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS3","text":"Die reine Wissenschaft wird erst möglich, nachdem der Gegensatz von Selbstgewissheit und Gegenstand im absoluten Wissen aufgehoben ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS4","text":"Die Logik ist nicht ein formales Instrument des Erkennens, sondern das sich entwickelnde System objektiver Denkbestimmungen und damit der reinen Vernunft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS5","text":"Das Argument verfährt diagnostisch gegen die formelle Logik, rekonstruktiv gegenüber Metaphysik und Idealismus und dialektisch in der Bestimmung seiner Methode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS6","text":"Die generative Bewegung verläuft von der fixierten Bestimmung über ihren inneren Widerspruch und ihre bestimmte Negation zum reicheren Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS7","text":"Die zunächst abstrakt gelernte Logik wird in der Rückkehr aus den konkreten Wissenschaften als deren erfülltes Allgemeines und Wesen erkannt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","text":"Die Logik darf keine Denkform, Regel, Methode, Gegenstandsbestimmung oder Wissenschaftsdefinition ungeprüft voraussetzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A2","text":"Der Begriff der Logik erhält wissenschaftliche Geltung erst als Resultat ihrer eigenen Durchführung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A3","text":"Der überlieferte Logikbegriff beruht auf der Trennung von Erkenntnisform und Erkenntnisinhalt sowie von Denken und Gegenstand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A4","text":"Diese Trennung gehört dem erscheinenden Bewusstsein an und besitzt keine Wahrheit für die Vernunft an sich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","text":"Das absolute Wissen hebt den Gegensatz zwischen dem Gegenstand und der Gewissheit seiner selbst auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","text":"Im reinen Wissen ist der Gedanke ebenso die Sache an sich selbst, wie die Sache an sich selbst reiner Gedanke ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","text":"Der Gehalt logischer Bestimmungen liegt in ihrer organischen Einheit innerhalb der logischen Vernunft, nicht in einer äußerlich zugeführten Materie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","text":"Festgehaltene Verstandesbestimmungen geraten durch ihre notwendige Beziehung aufeinander in Widerspruch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","text":"Die Negation einer widersprüchlichen Bestimmung ist bestimmte Negation und bewahrt den Inhalt des Negierten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A10","text":"Die bestimmte Negation erzeugt einen reicheren Begriff als Einheit der vorherigen Bestimmung und ihres Entgegengesetzten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A11","text":"Die wissenschaftliche Methode ist mit der inneren dialektischen Selbstbewegung ihres Inhalts identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A12","text":"Wissenschaftliche Systematik besteht nur dort, wo Unterschiede und Übergänge durch die Selbstfortbestimmung des Begriffs entstehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A13","text":"Das Logische erscheint dem subjektiven Geist zunächst als isolierte Abstraktion und erst nach der Erfahrung konkreter Wissenschaften als deren erfülltes Allgemeines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX1","text":"Die Logik ist keine von allem Inhalt abstrahierende Sammlung formaler Denkregeln.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX2","text":"Das Denken ist keine leere Form, die sich einer unabhängig fertigen Gegenstandsmaterie äußerlich anpasst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX3","text":"Wahrheit ist keine erst herzustellende äußerliche Übereinstimmung des Denkens mit einem ihm fremden Gegenstand.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX4","text":"Wahre Erkenntnis kann nicht auf Erscheinungen beschränkt bleiben und zugleich ein unerkennbares Ding an sich als Jenseits festhalten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX5","text":"Sinnliche Handgreiflichkeit ist kein Kriterium von Wirklichkeit oder Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX6","text":"Der Widerspruch der Verstandesbestimmungen beweist nicht die Erkenntnisunfähigkeit der Vernunft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX7","text":"Dialektik ist weder subjektive Willkür noch eine äußerliche Auflösung fester Bestimmungen in abstraktes Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX8","text":"Mathematische, klassifikatorische oder empirische Verfahren sind nicht die Methode philosophischer Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX9","text":"Psychologische, pädagogische und physiologische Zusätze können die Gehaltlosigkeit der formellen Logik nicht beheben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX10","text":"Definitionen, Einteilungen und Überschriften erzeugen keinen notwendigen wissenschaftlichen Zusammenhang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX11","text":"Eine anfängliche Definition kann die Notwendigkeit des Gegenstandes und der Wissenschaft nicht beweisen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D1","text":"Die Einleitung kann den Begriff der Logik nur vorläufig erläutern, nicht wissenschaftlich begründen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D2","text":"Die Trennung von Denken und Gegenstand macht den Gegenstand unerreichbar und lässt Wissen zur bloßen Meinung zurückfallen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A3","CH_GB18_ABDL:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D3","text":"Die Beschränkung der Verstandesformen auf Erscheinungen verändert ihre innere Unwahrheit nicht, sondern verlegt sie unverändert in das Subjekt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A3","CH_GB18_ABDL:A4","CH_GB18_ABDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D4","text":"Die Aufhebung des Bewusstseinsgegensatzes eröffnet die reine Wissenschaft als Einheit von Wahrheit und Gewissheit.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","CH_GB18_ABDL:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D5","text":"Die Logik enthält reale Wahrheit, weil ihre Denkbestimmungen zugleich Bestimmungen der Sache selbst sind.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D6","text":"Logische Formen werden nur durch ihre Fixierung und äußerliche Verknüpfung zu leeren, toten und kalkulatorischen Formen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","CH_GB18_ABDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D7","text":"Der Widerspruch markiert nicht das Scheitern der Vernunft, sondern ihre Erhebung über die Beschränkungen des Verstandes.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A4","CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","CH_GB18_ABDL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D8","text":"Der wissenschaftliche Fortgang besitzt die Form Bestimmung → Widerspruch → bestimmte Negation → reichere Einheit.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","CH_GB18_ABDL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D9","text":"Nur die immanente Dialektik des Inhalts kann als wahrhafte philosophische Methode gelten.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A11","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D10","text":"Einteilungen und Überschriften besitzen lediglich vorläufigen oder retrospektiv-historischen Wert.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D11","text":"Das Spekulative besteht im Erfassen des Positiven im Negativen und des Entgegengesetzten in seiner Einheit.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","CH_GB18_ABDL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D12","text":"Die abstrakte Beschäftigung mit reinen Begriffen bildet die Selbstständigkeit des Denkens und ermöglicht die Erfassung des logischen Wesens konkreter Wissenschaften.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","CH_GB18_ABDL:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD1","text":"Die Logik ist innerhalb ihrer Durchführung selbstbegründend, während der Eintritt in sie durch das phänomenologisch erzeugte absolute Wissen vermittelt bleibt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A2","CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","CH_GB18_ABDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD2","text":"Die Aufhebung des Subjekt-Objekt-Gegensatzes überführt Erkenntnistheorie in Ontologie, weil Denkbestimmung und Gegenstandsbestimmung denselben Inhalt erhalten.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD3","text":"Die innere Unwahrheit endlicher Bestimmungen wird zum produktiven Prinzip ihrer Überschreitung und Erhaltung in höheren Begriffen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","CH_GB18_ABDL:A10","CH_GB18_ABDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD4","text":"Die Wissenschaft besitzt eine retrospektive Grundstruktur: Erst ihr Resultat erzeugt den Begriff, der ihren Anfang als notwendigen Anfang verständlich macht.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A2","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD5","text":"Die besonderen Wissenschaften liefern der Logik keinen fremden Wahrheitsstoff; ihre Inhalte erscheinen in der Rückkehr zur Logik als Konkretionen logischer Wesenheiten.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","CH_GB18_ABDL:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD6","text":"Wissenschaftlichkeit wird ausschließlich durch die immanente Notwendigkeit der Übergänge bestimmt; äußere Ordnung, Vollständigkeit und Klassifikation bleiben außerwissenschaftlich.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A11","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX1","text":"Eine irreduzible ontologische Differenz zwischen Denken und Sein darf nicht bestehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX2","text":"Kein außerhalb des logischen Prozesses liegendes Kriterium kann dessen Wahrheit oder Methode begründen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX3","text":"Keine endliche Bestimmung darf als widerspruchsfreie und endgültige Identität bestehen bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX4","text":"Negation darf weder reiner Verlust noch inhaltslose Vernichtung sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX5","text":"Der Widerspruch darf nicht von der besonderen Beschaffenheit eines äußeren Stoffes abhängen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX6","text":"Der begriffliche Fortgang darf weder kontingent noch durch eine Pluralität gleichberechtigter Methoden bestimmt sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX1","text":"Eine dem Begriff dauerhaft entzogene Außenheit besitzt innerhalb des Systems keinen zulässigen Ort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX2","text":"Ein Anfang, der bereits vor seiner Durchführung vollständig begründet wäre, ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX3","text":"Ein Widerspruch ohne aufhebbaren bestimmten Nachfolger ist systemisch unzulässig, obwohl die Eindeutigkeit dieses Nachfolgers nicht eigens formalisiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX4","text":"Eine Wahrheit, die nicht zugleich zur Selbstgewissheit und zum Selbstwissen der Wahrheit wird, bleibt außerhalb des Begriffs reiner Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS1","text":"Eigeninhalt von Gegenstand, Form, Methode und Wissenschaftsbegriff → Verbot äußerer Voraussetzungen → nur vorläufige Einleitung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS2","text":"Trennung von Form und Inhalt → leeres Denken und äußerlicher Gegenstand → unerreichbares Ding an sich → Verlust objektiver Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS3","text":"Phänomenologische Auflösung des Bewusstseinsgegensatzes → Gleichheit von Wahrheit und Gewissheit → objektives Denken → reine Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS4","text":"Fixierte Bestimmung → notwendige Beziehung auf ihr Anderes → innerer Widerspruch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS5","text":"Widerspruch → bestimmte Negation → Bewahrung des negierten Inhalts → Einheit mit dem Entgegengesetzten → höherer Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS6","text":"Höherer Begriff → neue Bestimmtheit → erneuter Widerspruch → rekursive Selbstfortbestimmung → System der Begriffe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS7","text":"Identität von Methode und Selbstbewegung des Inhalts → notwendiger Übergang als Geltungskriterium → äußere Einteilung nur als retrospektive Karte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS8","text":"Anfängliche Abstraktion → Erfahrung konkreter Wissenschaften → Rückkehr zur Logik → erfüllte Universalität → selbstständige begriffliche Denkkraft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AF1","text":"Unmöglichkeit voraussetzungsvoller Grundlegung → Kritik des formellen Logikbegriffs → Demontage der Subjekt-Objekt-Trennung → absolutes Wissen → objektive Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AF2","text":"Gehaltlosigkeit fixer Formen → innerer Widerspruch → bestimmte Negation → spekulative Einheit → immanente Methode → selbstbewegtes Begriffssystem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AF3","text":"Logik als anfänglich isolierte Abstraktion → Durchgang durch konkrete Wissenschaften → Rückkehr zum Logischen → Erkenntnis seiner Universalität → Bildung selbstständigen Denkens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME1","text":"Form und Materie werden von äußerlichen Bestandteilen zu Momenten der absoluten Form umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME2","text":"Subjekt und Objekt werden von selbstständigen Sphären zu aufgehobenen Momenten objektiven Denkens umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME3","text":"Wahrheit wird von äußerlicher Korrespondenz zur Selbstentwicklung der Einheit von Begriff und Gegenstand verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME4","text":"Der Widerspruch wird von einem Erkenntnisdefekt zum Motor begrifflicher Fortbestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME5","text":"Negation wird von inhaltsloser Vernichtung zur bewahrenden Erzeugung bestimmteren Inhalts transformiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME6","text":"Methode wird von einem äußerlich angewandten Verfahren zur Selbstbewegung der Sache selbst umbestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME7","text":"Logik wird von einem formalen Hilfsinstrument zum System der reinen Vernunft und zum ontologischen Wahrheitsraum umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME8","text":"Definitionen, Klassifikationen und Einteilungen werden von Begründungsformen zu nachträglichen Orientierungsformen herabgestuft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME9","text":"Das Allgemeine wird von leerer Abstraktion zur den Reichtum des Besonderen in sich enthaltenden begrifflichen Totalität umbestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT1","text":"Surface — Die Logik wird gegen ihre überlieferte formelle Gestalt als inhaltliche Wissenschaft des reinen Denkens neu bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT2","text":"Structural — Der notwendige Zusammenhang entsteht durch Widerspruch, bestimmte Negation, Bewahrung und begriffliche Anreicherung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Wissenschaftliche Geltung wird an immanente Übergänge gebunden; äußere Definition, Klassifikation, mathematische Methode und subjektives Raisonnement werden disqualifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Denken und Sache besitzen denselben Inhalt; der Wissenschaftsbegriff entsteht erst am Ende und begründet rückwirkend den Anfang; das Reich des reinen Gedankens wird als Wahrheit an und für sich und als Darstellung Gottes vor Natur und endlichem Geist bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Kritik der formellen Logik, den Standpunkt reiner Wissenschaft, die dialektische Methode und die pädagogische Rückkehrbewegung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, mit welcher ersten logischen Bestimmung die voraussetzungslose Selbstbewegung konkret beginnen muss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern die phänomenologische Aufhebung des Bewusstseinsgegensatzes als gültiger Übergang zur reinen Wissenschaft anerkannt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste generative Verbindung liegt in der Sequenz innerer Widerspruch → bestimmte Negation → Bewahrung → reicherer Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT5","text":"Die beanspruchte Voraussetzungslosigkeit steht unter Spannung zur externen Deduktion des Wissenschaftsbegriffs durch die Phänomenologie und zur einleitenden Vorwegnahme der Methode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT6","text":"Die bestimmte Negation erklärt Erhaltung und Anreicherung, beweist jedoch noch nicht die Eindeutigkeit jedes höheren Begriffs oder die notwendige Vollendung des Gesamtsystems.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT7","text":"Die Totalisierung zur Darstellung Gottes und zum Wesen aller sonstigen Inhalte wird hier nicht kategorial vermittelt; sie hängt an der komprimierten Identitätsthese von Denken und Sache.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT8","text":"Die subjektive Erschließung des Logischen durch konkrete Wissenschaftserfahrung steht zur objektiven Selbstgenügsamkeit der Logik in Spannung, ohne von ihr ausdrücklich unterschieden zu werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT9","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung nur dann, wenn phänomenologische Eintrittsbedingung, immanente logische Durchführung und nachträgliche subjektive Aneignung getrennt gehalten werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T110818264219Z_46f4d1df","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"General Concept of Logic","source_sha256":"67a738218dd884797817cf53bda36b7ae5cf3a30bf7ee48276016a73354d1d65","sha256":"b0ff075bd481b399d914706f23c9196452b75dcfafed4e9873a3db7ed7fa6fc4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:08:18.266084+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS1","text":"Logic cannot presuppose its object, its forms, its method, or its concept of science, because it must itself provide their grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS2","text":"The inherited concept of logic produces its lack of content through the separation of form and content, as well as of thought and object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS3","text":"Pure science first becomes possible after the opposition between self-certainty and object has been sublated in absolute knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS4","text":"Logic is not a formal instrument of cognition, but the developing system of objective determinations of thought and thus of pure reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS5","text":"The argument proceeds diagnostically against formal logic, reconstructively with respect to metaphysics and idealism, and dialectically in determining its method.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS6","text":"The generative movement proceeds from fixed determination through its inner contradiction and its determinate negation to the richer concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AS7","text":"Logic, initially learned abstractly, is recognized in the return from the concrete sciences as their fulfilled universal and essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","text":"Logic may not presuppose without examination any form of thought, rule, method, determination of object, or definition of science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A2","text":"The concept of logic acquires scientific validity only as the result of its own execution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A3","text":"The inherited concept of logic rests on the separation of the form and content of cognition, as well as of thought and object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A4","text":"This separation belongs to appearing consciousness and possesses no truth for reason in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","text":"Absolute knowing sublates the opposition between the object and certainty of itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","text":"In pure knowing, thought is the thing in itself just as the thing in itself is pure thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","text":"The content of logical determinations lies in their organic unity within logical reason, not in matter externally introduced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","text":"Fixed determinations of the understanding fall into contradiction through their necessary relation to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","text":"The negation of a contradictory determination is determinate negation and preserves the content of what is negated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A10","text":"Determinate negation generates a richer concept as the unity of the preceding determination and its opposite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A11","text":"The scientific method is identical with the inner dialectical self-movement of its content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A12","text":"Scientific systematicity exists only where differences and transitions arise through the self-determination of the concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:A13","text":"The logical initially appears to subjective spirit as an isolated abstraction, and only after the experience of concrete sciences as their fulfilled universal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX1","text":"Logic is not a collection of formal rules of thought abstracting from all content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX2","text":"Thought is not an empty form that externally adapts itself to independently completed matter of objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX3","text":"Truth is not an external correspondence of thought with an object alien to it, to be produced only subsequently.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX4","text":"True cognition cannot remain restricted to appearances while at the same time retaining an unknowable thing in itself as a beyond.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX5","text":"Sensuous tangibility is not a criterion of actuality or truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX6","text":"The contradiction of the determinations of the understanding does not prove reason's incapacity for cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX7","text":"Dialectic is neither subjective arbitrariness nor an external dissolution of fixed determinations into abstract nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX8","text":"Mathematical, classificatory, or empirical procedures are not the method of philosophical science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX9","text":"Psychological, pedagogical, and physiological additions cannot remedy the lack of content of formal logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX10","text":"Definitions, divisions, and headings do not produce a necessary scientific connection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:NX11","text":"An initial definition cannot prove the necessity of the object and of science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D1","text":"The introduction can only provisionally elucidate the concept of logic, not scientifically ground it.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D2","text":"The separation of thought and object renders the object unattainable and lets knowledge relapse into mere opinion.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A3","CH_GB18_ABDL:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D3","text":"Restricting the forms of understanding to appearances does not alter their inner untruth, but transfers it unchanged into the subject.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A3","CH_GB18_ABDL:A4","CH_GB18_ABDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D4","text":"The sublation of the opposition of consciousness opens pure science as the unity of truth and certainty.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","CH_GB18_ABDL:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D5","text":"Logic contains real truth because its determinations of thought are at the same time determinations of the thing itself.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D6","text":"Logical forms become empty, dead, and calculative forms only through their fixation and external combination.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","CH_GB18_ABDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D7","text":"Contradiction marks not the failure of reason, but its elevation above the limitations of the understanding.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A4","CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","CH_GB18_ABDL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D8","text":"Scientific progression has the form determination → contradiction → determinate negation → richer unity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","CH_GB18_ABDL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D9","text":"Only the immanent dialectic of content can count as the true philosophical method.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A11","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D10","text":"Divisions and headings possess merely provisional or retrospectively historical value.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D11","text":"The speculative consists in grasping the positive in the negative and the opposite in its unity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","CH_GB18_ABDL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:D12","text":"Abstract engagement with pure concepts cultivates the independence of thought and enables the grasp of the logical essence of concrete sciences.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","CH_GB18_ABDL:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD1","text":"Logic is self-grounding within its execution, while entry into it remains mediated by phenomenologically generated absolute knowing.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A2","CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","CH_GB18_ABDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD2","text":"The sublation of the subject-object opposition transforms epistemology into ontology, because determination of thought and determination of object receive the same content.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A5","CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD3","text":"The inner untruth of finite determinations becomes the productive principle of their transcendence and preservation in higher concepts.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A8","CH_GB18_ABDL:A9","CH_GB18_ABDL:A10","CH_GB18_ABDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD4","text":"Science possesses a retrospective basic structure: only its result generates the concept that makes its beginning intelligible as a necessary beginning.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A1","CH_GB18_ABDL:A2","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD5","text":"The particular sciences supply logic with no alien material of truth; in the return to logic, their contents appear as concretizations of logical essences.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A6","CH_GB18_ABDL:A7","CH_GB18_ABDL:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SD6","text":"Scientificity is determined exclusively by the immanent necessity of transitions; external order, completeness, and classification remain extra-scientific.","refs":["CH_GB18_ABDL:A11","CH_GB18_ABDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX1","text":"There must be no irreducible ontological difference between thought and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX2","text":"No criterion lying outside the logical process can ground its truth or method.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX3","text":"No finite determination may remain as a contradiction-free and final identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX4","text":"Negation may be neither pure loss nor contentless annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX5","text":"Contradiction may not depend on the particular constitution of an external material.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:DNX6","text":"Conceptual progression may be determined neither contingently nor by a plurality of equally entitled methods.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX1","text":"An externality permanently withdrawn from the concept possesses no permissible place within the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX2","text":"A beginning that would already be fully grounded prior to its execution is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX3","text":"A contradiction without a sublatable determinate successor is systemically inadmissible, although the uniqueness of this successor is not separately formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:SNX4","text":"A truth that does not at the same time become self-certainty and the self-knowing of truth remains outside the concept of pure science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS1","text":"Intrinsic content of object, form, method, and concept of science → prohibition of external presuppositions → only provisional introduction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS2","text":"Separation of form and content → empty thought and external object → unattainable thing in itself → loss of objective truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS3","text":"Phenomenological dissolution of the opposition of consciousness → equality of truth and certainty → objective thought → pure science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS4","text":"Fixed determination → necessary relation to its other → inner contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS5","text":"Contradiction → determinate negation → preservation of negated content → unity with the opposite → higher concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS6","text":"Higher concept → new determinacy → renewed contradiction → recursive self-determination → system of concepts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS7","text":"Identity of method and self-movement of content → necessary transition as criterion of validity → external division only as retrospective map.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:FGS8","text":"Initial abstraction → experience of concrete sciences → return to logic → fulfilled universality → independent conceptual power of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AF1","text":"Impossibility of presupposition-laden grounding → critique of the concept of formal logic → dismantling of the subject-object separation → absolute knowing → objective logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AF2","text":"Lack of content of fixed forms → inner contradiction → determinate negation → speculative unity → immanent method → self-moving system of concepts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:AF3","text":"Logic as initially isolated abstraction → passage through concrete sciences → return to the logical → cognition of its universality → formation of independent thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME1","text":"Form and matter are remapped from external components into moments of absolute form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME2","text":"Subject and object are reclassified from independent spheres into sublated moments of objective thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME3","text":"Truth is shifted from external correspondence to the self-development of the unity of concept and object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME4","text":"Contradiction is transformed from a defect of cognition into the motor of conceptual self-determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME5","text":"Negation is transformed from contentless annihilation into the preserving production of more determinate content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME6","text":"Method is redefined from an externally applied procedure into the self-movement of the thing itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME7","text":"Logic is remapped from a formal auxiliary instrument into the system of pure reason and into the ontological space of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME8","text":"Definitions, classifications, and divisions are downgraded from forms of grounding to subsequent forms of orientation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ME9","text":"The universal is redefined from empty abstraction into conceptual totality containing within itself the richness of the particular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT1","text":"Surface — Logic is newly determined, against its inherited formal shape, as the contentful science of pure thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT2","text":"Structural — The necessary connection arises through contradiction, determinate negation, preservation, and conceptual enrichment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Scientific validity is bound to immanent transitions; external definition, classification, mathematical method, and subjective ratiocination are disqualified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Thought and thing possess the same content; the concept of science arises only at the end and retrospectively grounds the beginning; the realm of pure thought is determined as truth in and for itself and as the presentation of God before nature and finite spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the critique of formal logic, the standpoint of pure science, the dialectical method, and the pedagogical movement of return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT2","text":"What remains underdetermined is with which first logical determination presuppositionless self-movement must concretely begin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent, provided that the phenomenological sublation of the opposition of consciousness is recognized as a valid transition to pure science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT4","text":"The strongest generative connection lies in the sequence inner contradiction → determinate negation → preservation → richer concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT5","text":"The claimed presuppositionlessness stands in tension with the external deduction of the concept of science through phenomenology and with the introductory anticipation of the method.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT6","text":"Determinate negation explains preservation and enrichment, but does not yet prove the uniqueness of every higher concept or the necessary completion of the overall system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT7","text":"The totalization into the presentation of God and into the essence of all other contents is not here categorically mediated; it depends upon the compressed identity-thesis of thought and thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT8","text":"The subjective disclosure of the logical through the experience of concrete sciences stands in tension with the objective self-sufficiency of logic, without being expressly distinguished from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0071","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ABDL:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement only if phenomenological condition of entry, immanent logical execution, and subsequent subjective appropriation are kept distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ABDL:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_ABDL@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_ABDL:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 03","title":"General Concept of Logic","context":"Chapter 03","original_title":"Allgemeiner Begriff der Logik"},"original_title":"Allgemeiner Begriff der Logik","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL","layer":"CH","title":"General Division of Logic","order":4,"parents":["RAW_GB18_AEDL"],"revision":"CH_GB18_AEDL@R001","sha256":"864f6e36ca2cc221c05f9ede2a21e83cc2e4a2e89fc78044486a804425d1e958","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS1","text":"Die Eintheilung der Logik kann nur vorläufig angegeben werden, weil ihre Rechtfertigung erst aus der voll entwickelten Wissenschaft hervorgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS2","text":"Eine philosophische Eintheilung ist nur gültig, wenn sie die Selbstbestimmung des Begriffs expliziert und keine von außen aufgenommene Klassifikation anwendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS3","text":"Das logische Prinzip besteht in der konkreten Einheit von Seyn und Begriff, Subjektivem und Objektivem, deren Unterschied ohne selbstständige Trennung erhalten bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS4","text":"Die Entwicklung der Logik setzt die immanenten Unterschiede dieser Einheit, ohne in den Bewußtseinsgegensatz von Denken und Gegenstand zurückzufallen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS5","text":"Der Begriff entfaltet sich als Seyn, als vermittelndes Wesen und als freier Begriff; daraus entsteht die Dreiteilung der Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS6","text":"Die objektive Logik ersetzt und kritisiert die vormalige Metaphysik, indem sie reine Denkformen ohne vorgestellte Substrate untersucht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS7","text":"Die Kantische transscendentale Logik eröffnet zwar die Untersuchung der Denkform, bleibt aber durch den Bewußtseinsgegensatz und das Ding-an-sich begrenzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","text":"Die Eintheilung ist das Urteil des Begriffs über sich selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A2","text":"Der Begriff ist an ihm selbst bestimmt und enthält den Ursprung seiner eigenen Unterschiede.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","text":"Das reine Wissen ist die konkrete Einheit von Seyn und Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A4","text":"Die Momente des Logischen sind unterschieden, aber nicht als selbstständige Seiende.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","text":"Die Entwicklung des Begriffs geschieht innerhalb der konkreten Einheit des Logischen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A6","text":"In der Entwicklung werden die früher selbstständig erscheinenden Gegensätze zu Formen des ganzen Begriffs herabgesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","text":"Das Wesen ist die vermittelnde Sphäre, in der das Seyn zum Insichseyn des Begriffs übergeht, ohne bereits freier Begriff zu sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","text":"Der Begriff erscheint zunächst als Begriff an sich im Seyn und sodann als für sich seyender Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A9","text":"Die objektive Logik untersucht reine Denkformen frei von den vorgestellten Substraten der Seele, der Welt und Gottes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A10","text":"Die Kantische Bestimmung der Kategorien durch das subjektive Ich läßt einen dem Denken äußerlichen Rest als Ding-an-sich zurück.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A11","text":"Die subjektive Logik ist die Logik des Begriffs als freien, selbstständigen und sich selbst bestimmenden Subjekts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A12","text":"Die Logik gliedert sich in die Logik des Seyns, des Wesens und des Begriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX1","text":"Die logische Eintheilung ist keine empirische Taxonomie nach äußerlich aufgenommenen Merkmalen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX2","text":"Die Bestimmungen des Logischen sind keine voneinander getrennten Substanzen oder Gegenstände.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX3","text":"Die Entwicklung des Begriffs ist keine Wiederherstellung des Bewußtseinsgegensatzes zwischen Subjekt und Objekt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX4","text":"Das Seyn ist nicht ein dem Begriff schlechthin fremdes Äußeres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX5","text":"Der Begriff ist nicht bloß abstrakte Form ohne notwendigen Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX6","text":"Das Ding-an-sich ist nicht ein vom Denken unabhängiger positiver Rest, sondern selbst ein Produkt abstrahirenden Denkens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX7","text":"Die wahre Kritik der Metaphysik ist nicht die bloße Prüfung ihrer apriorischen Form gegen ein Aposteriorisches.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX8","text":"Das Subjektive der subjektiven Logik ist weder Willkür noch die Endlichkeit des Bewußtseyns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D1","text":"Jede gültige logische Gliederung muß als Selbstgliederung des Begriffs erscheinen und kann nicht durch äußere Vergleichung erzeugt werden.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","CH_GB18_AEDL:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D2","text":"Objektive und subjektive Logik sind keine getrennten Wissenschaften über verschiedene Gegenstandsbereiche, sondern Entwicklungsweisen desselben ganzen Begriffs.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A4","CH_GB18_AEDL:A6","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D3","text":"Das Wesen vermittelt zwischen dem unmittelbaren Seyn und dem freien Begriff, weil es das Seyn reflektiert, ohne die Selbstständigkeit des Begriffs erreicht zu haben.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D4","text":"Die objektive Logik umfaßt Seyn und Wesen, während die subjektive Logik den Begriff als solchen behandelt.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","CH_GB18_AEDL:A11","CH_GB18_AEDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D5","text":"Reines Denken kann sich notwendigen Inhalt geben, wenn die Form des Bewußtseyns abgestreift und die Form als selbstbestimmender Begriff gefaßt wird.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A2","CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D6","text":"Die Kantische Untersuchung der Denkform ist ein notwendiger Übergang zur Begriffslogik, bleibt aber unvollständig, solange sie Kategorien auf die abstrakte Beziehung zum Ich reduziert.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A10","CH_GB18_AEDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D7","text":"Die objektive Logik fungiert als immanente Kritik der Metaphysik, weil sie die Geltung und Natur ihrer Denkbestimmungen in deren besonderem Inhalt prüft.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A9","CH_GB18_AEDL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD1","text":"Die Dreiteilung der Logik ist keine äußerliche Ordnung ihrer Kapitel, sondern die notwendige Gestalt, in der der eine Begriff seine eigenen Entwicklungsstufen setzt.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","CH_GB18_AEDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD2","text":"Die Differenz von Denken und Seyn wird systematisch entontologisiert: Sie bleibt als Formdifferenz wirksam, verliert aber den Rang einer letzten Wirklichkeitstrennung.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A4","CH_GB18_AEDL:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD3","text":"Die Logik beansprucht den Platz der Grundwissenschaft, weil sie nicht nur Regeln des Denkens, sondern die Selbstbestimmung des Seyns als Begriff behandelt.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","CH_GB18_AEDL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD4","text":"Die frühere Metaphysik wird nicht verworfen, sondern in eine substratfreie Untersuchung ihrer eigenen Denkformen überführt.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A6","CH_GB18_AEDL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD5","text":"Die vorläufige Eintheilung erhält ihre Wahrheit nur rückwirkend durch den Vollzug der Wissenschaft, die sie zunächst voraussetzen muß.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","CH_GB18_AEDL:A2","CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","CH_GB18_AEDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein externer Standpunkt, von dem aus der Begriff nach fremden Kriterien eingetheilt oder beurteilt werden könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Annahme eines letzten nichtbegrifflichen Substrats, das dem Denken als unverfügbare Realität gegenüberstände.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Endgültigkeit des Bewußtseyns als Form philosophischer Erkenntniß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Kritik, die sich außerhalb ihres Gegenstands stellt und dessen Kategorien nicht aus ihrer eigenen Bewegung bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX5","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine metaphysische Vielheit selbstständiger Gegenstände, die den Denkformen ihren Inhalt äußerlich liefern würde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SNX1","text":"Unverfügbar ist eine irreduzible Grenze zwischen Begriff und Realität, weil Realität als Moment des Begriffs bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SNX2","text":"Unzulässig ist eine endgültige Rechtfertigung der logischen Eintheilung vor dem Vollzug der Wissenschaft, die allein ihre Notwendigkeit ausweisen soll.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SNX3","text":"Verworfen wird die Möglichkeit, daß die Wahrheit des Denkens in einem Jenseits des Denkens liegen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS1","text":"Selbstbestimmter Begriff → immanentes Urteil → begriffseigene Eintheilung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS2","text":"Reines Wissen → Einheit von Seyn und Begriff → Aufhebung der Selbstständigkeit von Subjekt und Objekt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS3","text":"Konkrete Einheit → immanente Differenz → Entwicklung ohne Rückkehr zum Bewußtseinsgegensatz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS4","text":"Begriff als Seyn → Reflexion des Seyns in sich → Wesen als Vermittlung → Begriff als freies Subjekt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS5","text":"Seyn + Wesen → objektive Logik; freier Begriff → subjektive Logik; beide → vollständige Dreiteilung der Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS6","text":"Denkformen ohne vorgestellte Substrate → immanente Prüfung ihrer Natur und ihres Werths → Ersetzung der vormaligen Metaphysik durch objektive Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS7","text":"Kantische Bindung der Kategorien an das Ich → Rest eines Ding-an-sich → Unzulänglichkeit der transscendentalen Begrenzung → Erforderniß einer absoluten Begriffslogik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF1","text":"Vorläufigkeit der Eintheilung → Notwendigkeit einer Rechtfertigung aus der Wissenschaft selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF2","text":"Zurückweisung äußerer Klassifikation → Bestimmung der Eintheilung als Urteil des Begriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF3","text":"Reines Wissen als Einheit von Seyn und Begriff → Aufhebung des Bewußtseinsgegensatzes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF4","text":"Einheit mit immanenter Differenz → Entwicklung der logischen Formen innerhalb eines einzigen Elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF5","text":"Seyn → Wesen als Vermittlung → Begriff als freie Selbstbestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF6","text":"Dreifache Entwicklung des Begriffs → objektive Logik und subjektive Logik → Seyn, Wesen und Begriff.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF7","text":"Kritik der Kantischen Begrenzung → substratfreie Kritik der Metaphysik → Anspruch der Logik auf ihre Ersetzung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME1","text":"Eintheilung wird von einer äußeren Ordnung von Gegenständen zu einer Selbstartikulation des Begriffs umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME2","text":"Subjektiv und objektiv werden von getrennten Realitätsbereichen zu nichtselbstständigen Formen innerhalb einer konkreten Einheit umgeordnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME3","text":"Das Wesen wird als notwendige Vermittlungszone sichtbar, welche den unmittelbaren Gegensatz von Seyn und Begriff aufbricht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME4","text":"Metaphysik wird nicht mehr als Lehre besonderer Gegenstände, sondern als unkritische Verwendung reiner Denkformen lesbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME5","text":"Die Kantische Transscendentalphilosophie erscheint zugleich als historischer Durchbruch zur Formfrage und als Grenze, die durch den absoluten Begriff überschritten werden muß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME6","text":"Das Ding-an-sich wird von einem Erkenntnislimit zu einer abstrakt erzeugten Denkbestimmung reklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT1","text":"Surface — Die Logik wird in die Lehre vom Seyn, vom Wesen und vom Begriff gegliedert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die Dreiteilung folgt aus der Selbstentwicklung eines Begriffs, dessen Unterschiede nur als Formen seiner Einheit bestehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Philosophie wird von äußerer Klassifikation und transscendentaler Grenzprüfung auf immanente Selbstkritik der Denkformen umgestellt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Seyn ist nicht dem Begriff vorausgesetzt, sondern dessen erste Entwicklungsform; die Begründung der Eintheilung erfolgt rückwirkend durch den Prozeß ihrer Entfaltung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Eintheilung als immanente Selbstgliederung des Begriffs und nicht als äußere Taxonomie zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT2","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Sequenz Seyn, Wesen und Begriff als notwendige Entwicklungsordnung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT3","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wie die behauptete Einheit von Seyn und Begriff unabhängig vom bereits vollzogenen Systemausgang begründet wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Struktur liegt in der Vermittlungsfunktion des Wesens, weil sie die bipolare Gegenüberstellung von objektiver und subjektiver Logik verhindert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT5","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bleibt zirkulär, weil die vorläufige Eintheilung die vollendete Wissenschaft voraussetzt, deren Vollzug erst ihre Rechtfertigung leisten soll.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT6","text":"Eine Spannung bleibt bestehen, weil die Unterscheidung von objektiver und subjektiver Logik zugleich systematisch notwendig gesetzt und gegen eine zu starke Gewichtung abgesichert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT7","text":"Die Kritik Kants hängt von der eigenen Voraussetzung ab, daß ein dem Denken äußerliches Ding-an-sich nur als abstrakte Denkproduktion gelten kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT8","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung des Textes, sofern die Dreiteilung als Resultat der Selbstbestimmung des Begriffs und nicht als vorausgesetztes Ordnungsschema behandelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T110905129531Z_58dc88e4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"General Division of Logic","source_sha256":"864f6e36ca2cc221c05f9ede2a21e83cc2e4a2e89fc78044486a804425d1e958","sha256":"c7c5d48508d289bd7a79d515d3aa4612ba79b1887561765e7458ecaa6afdfcfa","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:09:05.130513+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS1","text":"The division of logic can only be stated provisionally, because its justification first emerges from the fully developed science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS2","text":"A philosophical division is valid only if it explicates the self-determination of the Concept and does not apply a classification adopted from without.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS3","text":"The logical principle consists in the concrete unity of Being and Concept, subjective and objective, whose difference is preserved without independent separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS4","text":"The development of logic posits the immanent differences of this unity without lapsing back into the opposition of consciousness between thinking and object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS5","text":"The Concept unfolds as Being, as mediating Essence, and as free Concept; from this arises the tripartition of logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS6","text":"Objective logic replaces and criticizes former metaphysics by investigating pure forms of thought without represented substrates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AS7","text":"Kantian transcendental logic does indeed open the investigation of the form of thought, but remains limited by the opposition of consciousness and the thing-in-itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","text":"Division is the judgment of the Concept upon itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A2","text":"The Concept is determined in itself and contains the origin of its own differences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","text":"Pure knowing is the concrete unity of Being and Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A4","text":"The moments of the Logical are distinct, but not as independently existing beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","text":"The development of the Concept takes place within the concrete unity of the Logical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A6","text":"In development, the oppositions that previously appeared independent are reduced to forms of the whole Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","text":"Essence is the mediating sphere in which Being passes over into the being-within-itself of the Concept, without yet being free Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","text":"The Concept appears first as Concept in itself in Being and then as Concept existing for itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A9","text":"Objective logic investigates pure forms of thought free from the represented substrates of the soul, the world, and God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A10","text":"The Kantian determination of the categories by the subjective I leaves behind, as a remainder external to thought, the thing-in-itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A11","text":"Subjective logic is the logic of the Concept as free, independent, and self-determining subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:A12","text":"Logic is divided into the logic of Being, Essence, and Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX1","text":"Logical division is not an empirical taxonomy according to externally adopted characteristics.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX2","text":"The determinations of the Logical are not substances or objects separated from one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX3","text":"The development of the Concept is not a restoration of the opposition of consciousness between subject and object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX4","text":"Being is not an externality absolutely alien to the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX5","text":"The Concept is not merely abstract form without necessary content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX6","text":"The thing-in-itself is not a positive remainder independent of thought, but itself a product of abstracting thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX7","text":"The true critique of metaphysics is not the mere examination of its a priori form against an a posteriori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:NX8","text":"The subjective of subjective logic is neither arbitrariness nor the finitude of consciousness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D1","text":"Every valid logical articulation must appear as self-articulation of the Concept and cannot be produced by external comparison.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","CH_GB18_AEDL:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D2","text":"Objective and subjective logic are not separate sciences concerning different domains of objects, but modes of development of the same whole Concept.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A4","CH_GB18_AEDL:A6","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D3","text":"Essence mediates between immediate Being and free Concept, because it reflects Being into itself without having attained the independence of the Concept.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D4","text":"Objective logic comprises Being and Essence, whereas subjective logic treats the Concept as such.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","CH_GB18_AEDL:A11","CH_GB18_AEDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D5","text":"Pure thinking can give itself necessary content when the form of consciousness is cast off and form is apprehended as self-determining Concept.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A2","CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D6","text":"The Kantian investigation of the form of thought is a necessary transition to the logic of the Concept, but remains incomplete so long as it reduces categories to the abstract relation to the I.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A10","CH_GB18_AEDL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:D7","text":"Objective logic functions as an immanent critique of metaphysics because it examines the validity and nature of its determinations of thought in their particular content.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A9","CH_GB18_AEDL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD1","text":"The tripartition of logic is not an external ordering of its chapters, but the necessary shape in which the one Concept posits its own stages of development.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","CH_GB18_AEDL:A7","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","CH_GB18_AEDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD2","text":"The difference between thinking and Being is systematically de-ontologized: it remains operative as a formal difference, but loses the status of an ultimate division of reality.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A4","CH_GB18_AEDL:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD3","text":"Logic claims the place of the foundational science because it treats not only rules of thinking, but the self-determination of Being as Concept.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A3","CH_GB18_AEDL:A8","CH_GB18_AEDL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD4","text":"Former metaphysics is not rejected, but transformed into a substrate-free investigation of its own forms of thought.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A6","CH_GB18_AEDL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SD5","text":"The provisional division receives its truth only retrospectively through the execution of the science that it must initially presuppose.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDL:A1","CH_GB18_AEDL:A2","CH_GB18_AEDL:A5","CH_GB18_AEDL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX1","text":"Excluded is an external standpoint from which the Concept could be divided or judged according to alien criteria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX2","text":"Excluded is the assumption of an ultimate non-conceptual substrate that would stand opposed to thought as an unavailable reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX3","text":"Excluded is the finality of consciousness as a form of philosophical cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX4","text":"Excluded is a critique that places itself outside its object and does not determine its categories from their own movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:DNX5","text":"Excluded is a metaphysical multiplicity of independent objects that would furnish their content externally to the forms of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SNX1","text":"Unavailable is an irreducible boundary between Concept and reality, because reality is determined as a moment of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SNX2","text":"Impermissible is a final justification of logical division before the execution of the science that alone is to demonstrate its necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:SNX3","text":"Rejected is the possibility that the truth of thinking could lie in a beyond of thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS1","text":"Self-determined Concept → immanent judgment → division proper to the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS2","text":"Pure knowing → unity of Being and Concept → sublation of the independence of subject and object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS3","text":"Concrete unity → immanent difference → development without return to the opposition of consciousness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS4","text":"Concept as Being → reflection of Being into itself → Essence as mediation → Concept as free subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS5","text":"Being + Essence → objective logic; free Concept → subjective logic; both → complete tripartition of logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS6","text":"Forms of thought without represented substrates → immanent examination of their nature and worth → replacement of former metaphysics by objective logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:FGS7","text":"Kantian binding of the categories to the I → remainder of a thing-in-itself → inadequacy of the transcendental limitation → requirement of an absolute logic of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF1","text":"Provisionality of the division → necessity of a justification from science itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF2","text":"Rejection of external classification → determination of division as judgment of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF3","text":"Pure knowing as unity of Being and Concept → sublation of the opposition of consciousness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF4","text":"Unity with immanent difference → development of logical forms within a single element.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF5","text":"Being → Essence as mediation → Concept as free self-determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF6","text":"Threefold development of the Concept → objective logic and subjective logic → Being, Essence, and Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:AF7","text":"Critique of the Kantian limitation → substrate-free critique of metaphysics → logic's claim to replace it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME1","text":"Division is reclassified from an external ordering of objects into a self-articulation of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME2","text":"Subjective and objective are rearranged from separate domains of reality into non-independent forms within a concrete unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME3","text":"Essence becomes visible as a necessary zone of mediation that breaks up the immediate opposition of Being and Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME4","text":"Metaphysics becomes legible no longer as a doctrine of particular objects, but as an uncritical use of pure forms of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME5","text":"Kantian transcendental philosophy appears at once as a historical breakthrough toward the question of form and as a limit that must be surpassed by the absolute Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ME6","text":"The thing-in-itself is reclassified from a limit of cognition into an abstractly produced determination of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT1","text":"Surface — Logic is divided into the doctrine of Being, Essence, and Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT2","text":"Structural — The tripartition follows from the self-development of a Concept whose differences exist only as forms of its unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Philosophy is shifted from external classification and transcendental examination of limits to immanent self-critique of the forms of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Being is not presupposed to the Concept, but is its first form of development; the grounding of the division occurs retrospectively through the process of its unfolding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct division as the immanent self-articulation of the Concept and not as external taxonomy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT2","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the sequence Being, Essence, and Concept as a necessary order of development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT3","text":"It remains underdetermined how the asserted unity of Being and Concept is grounded independently of the system's already accomplished starting point.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT4","text":"The strongest structure lies in the mediating function of Essence, because it prevents the bipolar opposition of objective and subjective logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction remains circular because the provisional division presupposes the completed science, whose execution is only to provide its justification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT6","text":"A tension remains because the distinction between objective and subjective logic is at once posited as systematically necessary and secured against being weighted too heavily.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT7","text":"The critique of Kant depends on its own presupposition that a thing-in-itself external to thought can count only as an abstract production of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDL:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text insofar as the tripartition is treated as a result of the self-determination of the Concept and not as a presupposed schema of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_AEDL@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_AEDL:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 04","title":"General Division of Logic","context":"Chapter 04","original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung der Logik"},"original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung der Logik","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA","layer":"CH","title":"With What Must the Science Begin?","order":5,"parents":["RAW_GB18_WMDA"],"revision":"CH_GB18_WMDA@R001","sha256":"fdc93f53d1008b04bf7ce141d48b5766289f65f8d26528f48088210e6089629e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS1","text":"Ein wissenschaftlicher Anfang darf weder bloß subjektive Einleitung noch vom Erkenntnisgang abgetrenntes objektives Prinzip sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS2","text":"Die Einheit von Methode und Inhalt verlangt, dass das sachliche Prinzip zugleich das Erste des Denkens sei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS3","text":"Das Argument verfährt rekonstruktiv und apophatisch, indem es zwei Anfangswege auf denselben Minimalgehalt zurückführt und reichere Kandidaten ausschließt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS4","text":"Der ausschließende Gegensatz von Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittlung wird durch ihre notwendige Einheit ersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS5","text":"Die vermittelte Route führt vom phänomenologisch erzeugten reinen Wissen über die Aufhebung des Subjekt-Objekt-Gegensatzes zur einfachen Unmittelbarkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS6","text":"Die voraussetzungslose Route entfernt Grund, Bestimmung, Unterschied und Inhalt, bis nur einfache Unmittelbarkeit verbleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS7","text":"Beide Routen bestimmen reines Sein als einzigen zulässigen logischen Anfang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS8","text":"Der Fortgang bestimmt diesen Anfang immanent, kehrt in seinen Grund zurück und schließt Wissenschaft als Kreis von Erstem und Letztem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A1","text":"Wissenschaftliche Wahrheit verlangt die Einheit von Methode und Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A2","text":"Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittlung sind ungetrennte Bestimmungen derselben Sache.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A3","text":"Eine wissenschaftliche Erörterung des Erkennens ist außerhalb der Wissenschaft unmöglich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A4","text":"Die Logik bewegt sich im Element des reinen Wissens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","text":"Reines Wissen ist das Resultat der phänomenologisch vermittelten Bewegung des Bewusstseins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","text":"Im reinen Wissen ist der Gegensatz von Wissen und Gegenstand aufgehoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","text":"Das unterschiedslose reine Wissen hört als Wissen auf und ist einfache Unmittelbarkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","text":"Der wahre Gedankenausdruck einfacher Unmittelbarkeit ist reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","text":"Der voraussetzungslose Zugang enthält zunächst nur den Entschluss, Denken als solches zu betrachten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","text":"Ein absoluter Anfang ist der voraussetzungs-, grund-, vermittlungs- und bestimmungslose Grund der Wissenschaft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","text":"Jede Bestimmung und jedes Konkrete enthält Unterschied, Beziehung und Vermittlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","text":"Der wissenschaftliche Fortgang ist die immanente Selbstdetermination des Anfangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","text":"Das Vorwärtsgehen der Wissenschaft ist zugleich Rückgang in den Grund, aus dem das Anfängliche hervorgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","text":"Die Wissenschaft ist ein Kreislauf, in dem das Erste zum Letzten und das Letzte zum Ersten wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","text":"Der Anfang wird erst durch die Gesamtentwicklung inhaltlich erkannt und vollständig begründet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A16","text":"Wissenschaftliche Notwendigkeit entsteht ausschließlich aus der eigenen Bewegung der Sache und ihres Inhalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX1","text":"Der Anfang ist weder ausschließlich unmittelbar noch ausschließlich vermittelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX2","text":"Ein vom Erkenntnisgang getrenntes objektives Prinzip genügt nicht als wissenschaftlicher Anfang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX3","text":"Dogmatischer Prinzipienbeweis und skeptisches Erkenntniskriterium lassen Methode und Inhalt getrennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX4","text":"Glaube, innere Offenbarung und unmittelbare Gewissheit ersetzen keine wissenschaftliche Vermittlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX5","text":"Eine der Wissenschaft vorausgehende wissenschaftliche Prüfung des Erkennens ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX6","text":"Der Anfang ist keine hypothetische, problematische oder provisorische Annahme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX7","text":"Die als bekannt vorausgesetzte Vorstellung des Anfangs kann nicht durch äußerliche Analyse den absoluten Anfang erzeugen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX8","text":"Ein konkreter oder in sich unterschiedener Inhalt kann nicht das Erste sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX9","text":"Die Sache selbst kann vor ihrer wissenschaftlichen Entwicklung nicht als bereits bekannt vorausgesetzt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX10","text":"Das empirische Ich ist zu konkret, das reine Ich zu vermittelt und zu wenig unmittelbar bekannt, um Anfang zu sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX11","text":"Intellektuelle Anschauung begründet keinen Anfang, sofern sie Vermittlung nur zurückweist, ohne ihren Inhalt denkend zu entwickeln.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX12","text":"Die Namen Gott, das Absolute oder das Ewige enthalten am Anfang keinen ausgewiesenen Gedankenreichtum über reines Sein hinaus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX13","text":"Äußerliche Analyse, Vergleichung oder Konstruktion erzeugt keine objektiv notwendige Verbindung der Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D1","text":"Ein sachliches Prinzip, das nicht zugleich erstes Moment des Denkens ist, bleibt der wissenschaftlichen Form äußerlich.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A1","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D2","text":"Das phänomenologisch vermittelte reine Wissen reduziert sich nach Aufhebung seiner Unterschiede auf reines Sein.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A4","CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","CH_GB18_WMDA:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D3","text":"Der voraussetzungslose Vollzug des Denkens muss mit reinem Sein beginnen, weil jeder bestimmtere Inhalt bereits Vermittlung enthielte.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D4","text":"Reines Sein ist als Resultat absolut vermittelt und als logischer Anfang rein unmittelbar.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A2","CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D5","text":"Jeder konkrete Anfang setzt denjenigen Fortgang bereits voraus, den die Wissenschaft erst erzeugen soll.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D6","text":"Ein der Wissenschaft vorgelagertes Erkenntniskriterium kann den Anfang nicht wissenschaftlich legitimieren.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A3","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D7","text":"Die Analyse eines vorausgesetzten Konkreten liefert subjektiv ausgewählte Bestimmungen statt einer notwendigen Einheit.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D8","text":"Der Fortgang hebt die anfängliche abstrakte Unmittelbarkeit auf, ohne den Anfang aus den späteren Bestimmungen zu entfernen.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D9","text":"Das Resultat ist zugleich aus dem Anfang abgeleitet und der Grund, aus dem der Anfang hervorgeht.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D10","text":"Die rückwirkende Begründung des Anfangs macht ihn nicht hypothetisch, sofern der gesamte Fortgang immanent notwendig ist.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D11","text":"Der Anfang mit dem Ich verliert entweder die Unmittelbarkeit im abstraktiven Selbsterhebungsakt oder die Reinheit im empirisch-konkreten Selbstbewusstsein.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D12","text":"Jeder reichere Name des Absoluten ist am Anfang entweder bloßes Wort oder ein unbewiesen vorausgesetztes Gefüge von Bestimmungen.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD1","text":"Reines Sein fungiert als Konvergenzpunkt einer systematisch vermittelten und einer voraussetzungslos abstrahierenden Anfangsarchitektur.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A2","CH_GB18_WMDA:A4","CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD2","text":"Lineare Grundlegung wird durch wechselseitige Begründung ersetzt: Der Anfang trägt die Entwicklung, während das Resultat den Anfang als notwendig ausweist.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD3","text":"Die Geltung des Anfangs ist logisch rückwirkend, ohne deshalb zeitlich oder methodisch provisorisch zu sein.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD4","text":"Inhaltsreiche Anfangskandidaten werden nicht schlechthin vernichtet, sondern aus der Anfangsposition in die spätere immanente Entwicklung verlagert.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD5","text":"Das erkennende Subjekt verliert die Funktion eines äußeren Produzenten der Bestimmungen; die generative Funktion geht auf die Selbstbewegung des Inhalts über.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A1","CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD6","text":"Legitim ist nur, was innerhalb der Kreisbewegung als notwendiges Moment erzeugt werden kann; ein dauerhaft äußeres Kriterium, Subjekt oder Inhalt ist systematisch ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A3","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX1","text":"Wissenschaft kann nicht von einem ihr äußerlichen epistemischen Standpunkt autorisiert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX2","text":"Methode kann nicht als selbständiges Werkzeug auf einen bereits gegebenen Inhalt angewandt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX3","text":"Bestimmtheit kann nicht zugleich ursprünglich, voraussetzungslos und unvermittelt sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX4","text":"Der Gegensatz von Subjekt und Objekt kann nicht die letzte Form des Wissens bilden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX5","text":"Analytische Zerlegung eines Vorgegebenen kann keine objektive Notwendigkeit der Verbindung hervorbringen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX6","text":"Der Grund muss nicht linear vor dem von ihm Begründeten liegen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX7","text":"Wissenschaftlicher Fortgang kann den Anfang weder verlassen noch in ein schlechthin Anderes übergehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX8","text":"Vorstellungsreichtum oder Namensfülle ist nicht mit gedanklich ausgewiesenem Inhalt identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX1","text":"Ein zugleich unmittelbar gegebener, vollständig bestimmter und vorweg gerechtfertigter Anfang ist strukturell unmöglich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX2","text":"Ein archimedisches Außen der Wissenschaft, von dem aus ihr Anfang neutral begründet werden könnte, ist nicht verfügbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX3","text":"Eine von der vollendeten Totalität unabhängige Letztgarantie des Anfangs ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX4","text":"Irreduzible Äußerlichkeit, kontingente Fremdheit und ein nicht aufhebbares Anderes besitzen innerhalb der generativen Bewegung keinen endgültigen Ort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS1","text":"Wissenschaftlichkeit → Einheit von Methode und Inhalt → sachliches Prinzip als Anfang des Denkens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS2","text":"Exklusive Alternative von Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittlung → Widerlegung → beide Bestimmungen als untrennbare Momente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS3","text":"Endliches Bewusstsein → phänomenologische Vermittlung → reines Wissen → Aufhebung des Subjekt-Objekt-Gegensatzes → einfache Unmittelbarkeit → reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS4","text":"Entschluss zum Denken als solchem → Entfernung jeder Voraussetzung → Ausschluss von Grund, Unterschied und Inhalt → reine Unmittelbarkeit → reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS5","text":"Vermittelte Resultatroute und unmittelbare Abstraktionsroute → identischer Anfangsgehalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS6","text":"Bestimmung oder Konkretion → innere Differenz → Beziehung → Vermittlung → Unzulässigkeit als absoluter Anfang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS7","text":"Reines Sein → immanente Selbstdetermination → Erhaltung des Anfangs in seinen Bestimmungen → Aufhebung abstrakter Unmittelbarkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS8","text":"Vorwärtsbewegung → Rückgang in den Grund → Resultat als Grund des Anfangs → Kreis von Erstem und Letztem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS9","text":"Selbstbewegung des Inhalts → notwendiger Fortgang → rückwirkende Begründung → Ausschluss von Hypothese und äußerer Konstruktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF1","text":"Schwierigkeit des Anfangs → Einheit von Prinzip und Methode → Widerlegung der exklusiven Alternative von Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF2","text":"Phänomenologie des Bewusstseins → reines Wissen → unterschiedslose Einheit → einfache Unmittelbarkeit → reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF3","text":"Denken als solches → voraussetzungsloser Anfang → Ausschluss jeder Bestimmtheit → reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF4","text":"Prüfung alternativer Anfänge → Nachweis verborgener Konkretion, Subjektivität oder äußerer Vermittlung → erneute Fixierung des reinen Seins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF5","text":"Reines Sein → immanente Entwicklung → Rückkehr in den Grund → vollständige Erkenntnis des Anfangs → kreisförmige Totalität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME1","text":"Die Ordnung der Darstellung wird von einer äußerlichen Vortragsfrage zu einem konstitutiven Moment objektiver Wahrheit umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME2","text":"Unmittelbarkeit und Vermittlung erscheinen nicht mehr als konkurrierende Anfangstypen, sondern als verschiedene Funktionsweisen desselben Anfangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME3","text":"Reines Sein wird von einem möglichen Prinzip unter anderen zum durch Ausschluss erzeugten Minimalgehalt jedes zulässigen Anfangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME4","text":"Ich, Gott, Absolutes und intellektuelle Anschauung werden nicht als mögliche Inhalte schlechthin, sondern als logisch verfrühte Anfangsformen klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME5","text":"Fortschritt wird von linearer Ableitung eines Anderen zur immanenten Bestimmung und Erhaltung des Anfangs umgezeichnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME6","text":"Die Unterscheidung zwischen dem Ersten der Darstellung und dem absoluten Grund wird zunächst geöffnet und anschließend durch den Kreis geschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME7","text":"Der Ort der Notwendigkeit verschiebt sich vom analysierenden Subjekt und seinem Verfahren in die Eigenbewegung des Inhalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der explizite Gegenstand ist die Bestimmung des reinen Seins als Anfang der Logik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT2","text":"Structural — Zwei konvergierende Ableitungswege und ein Ausschlussfilter für Bestimmtheit erzeugen den Anfang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Die Wahl zwischen konkurrierenden Prinzipien wird durch die Prüfung ersetzt, ob ein Kandidat seine eigenen Voraussetzungen immanent erzeugen kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Wissenschaftliche Realität wird als Selbstvermittlung gedacht, deren Ende den Anfang rückwirkend gründet und deren Zeitform kreisförmig ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die beiden Ableitungswege, den Ausschluss bestimmter Anfangskandidaten und die kreisförmige Begründungsstruktur zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT2","text":"Die stärkste interne Verbindung liegt in der Konvergenz von vermitteltem reinen Wissen und voraussetzungsloser Abstraktion auf reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT3","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wie das völlig Unbestimmte ohne vorgreifende Bestimmung als Sein benannt wird und aus sich in Nichts und Werden übergeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT4","text":"Die Voraussetzungslosigkeit der Logik bleibt mit ihrer systematischen Voraussetzung in der Phänomenologie gespannt; Kohärenz verlangt die nicht vollständig formalisierte Unterscheidung von systematischer Genese und logischer Funktion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT5","text":"Der Entschluss, Denken als solches zu betrachten, verbleibt zwischen zugestandener Willkür und behaupteter sachlicher Notwendigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT6","text":"Die vorläufigen Reflexionen sollen nur Vorurteile entfernen, erzeugen aber faktisch einen erheblichen Teil der argumentativen Rechtfertigung des Anfangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT7","text":"Der universale Ausschluss jeder alternativen Anfangsform wird durch exemplarische Kandidatenprüfungen gestützt, aber nicht erschöpfend demonstriert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT8","text":"Die volle Begründung des Anfangs wird an die noch ausstehende Totalität delegiert; die lokale Geltung hängt daher von erfolgreicher Systemvollendung ab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT9","text":"Die tatsächliche Bewegung bleibt nur erhalten, wenn reines Sein zugleich als unmittelbarer Ausgang, vermitteltes Resultat, persistierende Grundlage und rückwirkend begründetes Moment rekonstruiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T120206524034Z_ae43cb21","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"With What Must the Beginning of Science Be Made?","source_sha256":"fdc93f53d1008b04bf7ce141d48b5766289f65f8d26528f48088210e6089629e","sha256":"a1e8ae7dfe2e4352c0769d189c250e14990359db30e989a9bba8366d595cf431","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T12:02:06.525858+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS1","text":"A scientific beginning must be neither a merely subjective introduction nor an objective principle separated from the course of cognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS2","text":"The unity of method and content requires that the objective principle also be the first of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds reconstructively and apophatically by leading two paths of beginning back to the same minimal content and excluding richer candidates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS4","text":"The exclusive opposition of immediacy and mediation is replaced by their necessary unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS5","text":"The mediated route leads from phenomenologically generated pure knowing, through the sublation of the subject-object opposition, to simple immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS6","text":"The presuppositionless route removes ground, determinacy, difference, and content until only simple immediacy remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS7","text":"Both routes determine pure being as the sole permissible logical beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AS8","text":"The progression determines this beginning immanently, returns into its ground, and completes science as a circle of first and last.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A1","text":"Scientific truth requires the unity of method and content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A2","text":"Immediacy and mediation are inseparable determinations of the same thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A3","text":"A scientific discussion of cognition outside science is impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A4","text":"Logic moves in the element of pure knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","text":"Pure knowing is the result of the phenomenologically mediated movement of consciousness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","text":"In pure knowing, the opposition of knowing and object is sublated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","text":"Undifferentiated pure knowing ceases to be knowing and is simple immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","text":"The true thought-expression of simple immediacy is pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","text":"The presuppositionless approach initially contains only the resolve to consider thinking as such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","text":"An absolute beginning is the presuppositionless, groundless, unmediated, and indeterminate ground of science.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","text":"Every determination and every concrete entity contains difference, relation, and mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","text":"Scientific progression is the immanent self-determination of the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","text":"The advance of science is at the same time regression into the ground from which the initial proceeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","text":"Science is a cycle in which the first becomes the last and the last becomes the first.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","text":"The beginning is recognized in content and fully grounded only through the total development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:A16","text":"Scientific necessity arises exclusively from the movement of the thing itself and its content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX1","text":"The beginning is neither exclusively immediate nor exclusively mediated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX2","text":"An objective principle separated from the course of cognition does not suffice as a scientific beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX3","text":"Dogmatic proof of principles and skeptical criterion of cognition leave method and content separate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX4","text":"Faith, inner revelation, and immediate certainty do not replace scientific mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX5","text":"A scientific examination of cognition preceding science is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX6","text":"The beginning is not a hypothetical, problematic, or provisional assumption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX7","text":"The representation of the beginning presupposed as known cannot produce the absolute beginning through external analysis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX8","text":"A concrete or internally differentiated content cannot be the first.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX9","text":"The thing itself cannot, prior to its scientific development, be presupposed as already known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX10","text":"The empirical I is too concrete, the pure I too mediated and too little immediately known, to be a beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX11","text":"Intellectual intuition does not ground a beginning insofar as it merely rejects mediation without developing its content in thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX12","text":"The names God, the Absolute, or the Eternal contain at the beginning no demonstrated wealth of thought beyond pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:NX13","text":"External analysis, comparison, or construction produces no objectively necessary connection of determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D1","text":"An objective principle that is not at the same time the first moment of thought remains external to scientific form.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A1","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D2","text":"Phenomenologically mediated pure knowing reduces itself, after the sublation of its differences, to pure being.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A4","CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","CH_GB18_WMDA:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D3","text":"The presuppositionless enactment of thinking must begin with pure being, because every more determinate content would already contain mediation.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D4","text":"Pure being is, as result, absolutely mediated and, as logical beginning, purely immediate.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A2","CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D5","text":"Every concrete beginning already presupposes the progression that science is only supposed to produce.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D6","text":"A criterion of cognition antecedent to science cannot scientifically legitimate the beginning.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A3","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D7","text":"The analysis of a presupposed concrete entity yields subjectively selected determinations instead of a necessary unity.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D8","text":"The progression sublates the initial abstract immediacy without removing the beginning from the later determinations.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D9","text":"The result is at once derived from the beginning and the ground from which the beginning proceeds.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D10","text":"The retroactive grounding of the beginning does not make it hypothetical, provided that the entire progression is immanently necessary.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D11","text":"The beginning with the I loses either immediacy in the abstractive act of self-elevation or purity in empirical-concrete self-consciousness.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:D12","text":"Every richer name of the Absolute is at the beginning either a mere word or an unproven presupposed configuration of determinations.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD1","text":"Pure being functions as the point of convergence of a systematically mediated and a presuppositionlessly abstracting architecture of beginning.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A2","CH_GB18_WMDA:A4","CH_GB18_WMDA:A5","CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","CH_GB18_WMDA:A7","CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A9","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD2","text":"Linear grounding is replaced by reciprocal grounding: the beginning bears the development, while the result demonstrates the beginning as necessary.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD3","text":"The validity of the beginning is logically retroactive without thereby being temporally or methodologically provisional.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD4","text":"Content-rich candidates for a beginning are not simply annihilated, but displaced from the position of beginning into later immanent development.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A8","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A11","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD5","text":"The cognizing subject loses the function of an external producer of determinations; the generative function passes over to the self-movement of content.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A1","CH_GB18_WMDA:A6","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SD6","text":"Only that is legitimate which can be generated as a necessary moment within the circular movement; a permanently external criterion, subject, or content is systematically excluded.","refs":["CH_GB18_WMDA:A3","CH_GB18_WMDA:A10","CH_GB18_WMDA:A12","CH_GB18_WMDA:A13","CH_GB18_WMDA:A14","CH_GB18_WMDA:A15","CH_GB18_WMDA:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX1","text":"Science cannot be authorized from an epistemic standpoint external to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX2","text":"Method cannot be applied as an independent tool to an already given content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX3","text":"Determinacy cannot at once be original, presuppositionless, and unmediated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX4","text":"The opposition of subject and object cannot constitute the final form of knowing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX5","text":"Analytical decomposition of something given cannot bring forth an objective necessity of connection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX6","text":"The ground need not lie linearly prior to that which it grounds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX7","text":"Scientific progression can neither leave the beginning nor pass over into an absolutely other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:DNX8","text":"Wealth of representations or abundance of names is not identical with content demonstrated in thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX1","text":"A beginning that is at once immediately given, completely determined, and justified in advance is structurally impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX2","text":"An Archimedean outside of science, from which its beginning could be neutrally grounded, is unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX3","text":"An ultimate guarantee of the beginning independent of the completed totality is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:SNX4","text":"Irreducible externality, contingent foreignness, and a non-sublatable other have no final place within the generative movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS1","text":"Scientificity → unity of method and content → objective principle as beginning of thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS2","text":"Exclusive alternative of immediacy and mediation → refutation → both determinations as inseparable moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS3","text":"Finite consciousness → phenomenological mediation → pure knowing → sublation of the subject-object opposition → simple immediacy → pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS4","text":"Resolve to think as such → removal of every presupposition → exclusion of ground, difference, and content → pure immediacy → pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS5","text":"Mediated route of result and immediate route of abstraction → identical content of beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS6","text":"Determination or concretion → internal difference → relation → mediation → inadmissibility as absolute beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS7","text":"Pure being → immanent self-determination → preservation of the beginning in its determinations → sublation of abstract immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS8","text":"Forward movement → regression into the ground → result as ground of the beginning → circle of first and last.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:FGS9","text":"Self-movement of content → necessary progression → retroactive grounding → exclusion of hypothesis and external construction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF1","text":"Difficulty of the beginning → unity of principle and method → refutation of the exclusive alternative of immediacy and mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF2","text":"Phenomenology of consciousness → pure knowing → undifferentiated unity → simple immediacy → pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF3","text":"Thinking as such → presuppositionless beginning → exclusion of every determinacy → pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF4","text":"Examination of alternative beginnings → demonstration of concealed concretion, subjectivity, or external mediation → renewed fixation of pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:AF5","text":"Pure being → immanent development → return into the ground → complete cognition of the beginning → circular totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME1","text":"The order of presentation is reclassified from an external question of exposition into a constitutive moment of objective truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME2","text":"Immediacy and mediation no longer appear as competing types of beginning, but as different modes of functioning of the same beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME3","text":"Pure being is transformed from one possible principle among others into the minimal content of every permissible beginning, produced through exclusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME4","text":"I, God, Absolute, and intellectual intuition are classified not as possible contents as such, but as logically premature forms of beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME5","text":"Progress is redrawn from a linear derivation of an other into the immanent determination and preservation of the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME6","text":"The distinction between the first of presentation and the absolute ground is initially opened and subsequently closed by the circle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ME7","text":"The locus of necessity shifts from the analyzing subject and its procedure into the self-movement of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT1","text":"Surface — The explicit subject is the determination of pure being as the beginning of logic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT2","text":"Structural — Two converging paths of derivation and an exclusion filter for determinacy generate the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The choice among competing principles is replaced by examining whether a candidate can immanently generate its own presuppositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Scientific reality is conceived as self-mediation, whose end retroactively grounds the beginning and whose temporal form is circular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the two paths of derivation, the exclusion of determinate candidates for a beginning, and the circular structure of grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT2","text":"The strongest internal connection lies in the convergence of mediated pure knowing and presuppositionless abstraction upon pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT3","text":"It remains underdetermined how the wholly indeterminate is named as being without anticipatory determination and passes from itself into nothing and becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT4","text":"The presuppositionlessness of logic remains in tension with its systematic presupposition in phenomenology; coherence requires the not fully formalized distinction between systematic genesis and logical function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0011","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT5","text":"The resolve to consider thinking as such remains between conceded arbitrariness and asserted objective necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT6","text":"The preliminary reflections are supposed only to remove prejudices, but in fact produce a considerable part of the argumentative justification of the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT7","text":"The universal exclusion of every alternative form of beginning is supported by exemplary examinations of candidates, but not exhaustively demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT8","text":"The full grounding of the beginning is delegated to the totality still outstanding; its local validity therefore depends on successful completion of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0027","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_WMDA:MRT9","text":"The actual movement is preserved only if pure being is reconstructed at once as immediate point of departure, mediated result, persisting ground, and retroactively grounded moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_WMDA:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_WMDA@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_WMDA:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 05","title":"With What Must the Science Begin?","context":"Chapter 05","original_title":"Womit muß der Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht werden?"},"original_title":"Womit muß der Anfang der Wissenschaft gemacht werden?","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS","layer":"CH","title":"General Division of Being","order":6,"parents":["RAW_GB18_AEDS"],"revision":"CH_GB18_AEDS@R001","sha256":"37d22b18371d81da15e1f0ab5015cc721f894c879f573f3d494c754479676cb2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS1","text":"Das Seyn wird zunächst durch seine Abgrenzung gegen Anderes überhaupt bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS2","text":"Danach wird das Seyn als sich innerhalb seiner eigenen Sphäre bestimmend gefasst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS3","text":"Die zunächst vorläufige Eintheilung wird durch die Bewegung des Seyns selbst begründet und gerechtfertigt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS4","text":"Die innere Entwicklung des Seyns erzeugt die Stufen Qualität, Quantität und Maaß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS5","text":"Die dritte Bestimmung führt zur abstrakten Unmittelbarkeit einer einzelnen Bestimmtheit innerhalb der Sphäre der Qualität zurück.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A1","text":"Das Seyn ist zunächst gegen Anderes überhaupt bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A2","text":"Das Seyn bestimmt sich innerhalb seiner selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A3","text":"Die abstrakte Unbestimmtheit und Unmittelbarkeit ist die Form, in der das Seyn den Anfang bildet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A4","text":"Das Seyn und das Wesen bilden getrennte Sphären des Begriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A5","text":"Die Totalität des Seyns erscheint in seiner Entwicklung als eine Sphäre des Begriffs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A6","text":"Die Bestimmungen des Seyns entstehen aus seiner eigenen Bewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A7","text":"Die unmittelbare Bestimmtheit ist Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A8","text":"Die aufgehobene Bestimmtheit ist Quantität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A9","text":"Die qualitativ bestimmte Quantität ist Maaß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A10","text":"Qualität ist mit dem Seyn unmittelbar eins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A11","text":"Quantität ist von dem Seyn unterschieden und als aufgehobene Qualität gleichgültig gegen es.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A12","text":"Quantität schließt Veränderlichkeit der Bestimmung ein, ohne das Seyn selbst zu verändern.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A13","text":"Maaß ist die bestimmte Relation von Qualität und Quantität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A14","text":"Die Kategorien der Relation und Modalität bei Kant gehören nicht in die Bestimmung des Maaßes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A15","text":"Die qualitative Bestimmung ist der Natur nach früher als die quantitative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A16","text":"Die dritte Bestimmung des Seyns setzt abstrakte Unmittelbarkeit als einzelne Bestimmtheit gegen andere Bestimmungen innerhalb seiner Sphäre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX1","text":"Die Eintheilung des Seyns ist nicht von Anfang an endgültig gerechtfertigt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX2","text":"Die Ordnung der Kategorien folgt nicht der gewöhnlichen Reihenfolge Quantität, Qualität, Relation und Modalität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX3","text":"Quantität ist nicht die ursprüngliche Bestimmung des Seyns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX4","text":"Qualität ist nicht eine vom Seyn ablösbare Bestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX5","text":"Maaß ist nicht Relation überhaupt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX6","text":"Maaß ist nicht bloß die Beziehung eines Inhalts auf das subjektive Denken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX7","text":"Die Kantischen Bestimmungen von Relation und Modalität werden nicht im Maaß aufgehoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX8","text":"Die vorläufige Eintheilung kann nicht als äußerlich übernommene Klassifikation bestehen bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D1","text":"Der Anfang muss mit dem Seyn als solchem und daher mit dem qualitativen Seyn gemacht werden.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A3","CH_GB18_AEDS:A7","CH_GB18_AEDS:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D2","text":"Quantität setzt Qualität voraus, weil sie als negativ gewordene Qualität bestimmt ist.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A8","CH_GB18_AEDS:A11","CH_GB18_AEDS:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D3","text":"Die quantitative Bestimmung ist gegenüber dem Seyn gleichgültig, weil sie dessen unmittelbare Einheit bereits aufgehoben hat.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A10","CH_GB18_AEDS:A11","CH_GB18_AEDS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D4","text":"Die qualitative Bestimmung ist unmittelbare Beschränktheit des Seyns.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A7","CH_GB18_AEDS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D5","text":"Maaß vermittelt Qualität und Quantität durch eine bestimmte, nicht allgemeine Relation.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A9","CH_GB18_AEDS:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D6","text":"Die Kategorien, die Kant unter Relation fasst, müssen außerhalb des Maaßes entwickelt werden.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A13","CH_GB18_AEDS:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D7","text":"Die Kategorie Modalität ist für das Maaß ungeeignet, sofern sie nur das Verhältnis des Inhalts zum subjektiven Denken bezeichnet.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A13","CH_GB18_AEDS:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D8","text":"Die Eintheilung Qualität–Quantität–Maaß erhält ihre Geltung erst durch die Entwicklung des Seyns.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A2","CH_GB18_AEDS:A6","CH_GB18_AEDS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD1","text":"Die Kategorienordnung wird von einer äußerlich klassifikatorischen Liste in eine immanente Entwicklungsfolge umgebildet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD2","text":"Die Priorität der Qualität beruht auf der Einheit von Bestimmung und Seyn, während Quantität bereits deren Differenz voraussetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD3","text":"Die Totalität des Seyns entsteht nicht durch Addition einzelner Kategorien, sondern durch die Bewegung von unmittelbarer Bestimmtheit über aufgehobene Bestimmtheit zur bestimmten Vermittlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD4","text":"Maaß fungiert als Grenzform, in der qualitative Identität und quantitative Gleichgültigkeit zugleich erhalten und vermittelt sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD5","text":"Die Kritik der gewöhnlichen Kategorienordnung ist eine Kritik ihrer fehlenden Begründung aus dem Gegenstand selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX1","text":"Das System schließt eine von der Bewegung des Seyns unabhängige Ordnung der Kategorien aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX2","text":"Es schließt aus, dass quantitative Bestimmung ohne vorausgesetzte qualitative Bestimmtheit verständlich ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX3","text":"Es schließt eine Bestimmung aus, die zugleich unmittelbar mit dem Seyn identisch und vollständig von ihm getrennt wäre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX4","text":"Es schließt eine bloß subjektive oder erkenntnistheoretische Auffassung der Kategorien aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX5","text":"Es schließt die Reduktion des Maaßes auf allgemeine Relation oder bloße Modalität aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX6","text":"Es schließt eine endgültige begriffliche Bestimmung vor dem Durchgang durch die Bewegung des Seyns aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX1","text":"Unzulässig ist ein System, in dem Kategorien äußerlich nebeneinanderstehen, ohne durch eine immanente Notwendigkeit erzeugt zu werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX2","text":"Unverfügbar ist ein Anfang, der bereits eine inhaltlich bestimmte Kategorie voraussetzt, bevor das Seyn seine Bestimmungen hervorgebracht hat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt eine Trennung von ontologischer Bestimmung und begrifflicher Bewegung, durch die Kategorien nur als Formen des subjektiven Denkens erscheinen würden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX4","text":"Die verborgene Gegenmöglichkeit des Systems ist eine unmittelbare Identität von Seyn und Bestimmung ohne qualitative Beschränkung, quantitative Aufhebung oder maßhafte Vermittlung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS1","text":"Abstrakte Unbestimmtheit → Anfang des Seyns → erste Bestimmung gegen Anderes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS2","text":"Erste Bestimmung → Abgrenzung des Seyns vom Wesen → Konstitution einer eigenen Begriffssphäre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS3","text":"Eigene Begriffssphäre → innere Selbstbestimmung → Hervortreten von Bestimmungen und Reflexionsbewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS4","text":"Unmittelbare Bestimmtheit → Einheit von Bestimmung und Seyn → Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS5","text":"Aufhebung dieser Einheit → Unterscheidung und Gleichgültigkeit der Bestimmung → Quantität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS6","text":"Bestimmte Beziehung von Qualität und Quantität → Vermittlung ihrer Differenz → Maaß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS7","text":"Vorläufige Eintheilung → immanente Entwicklung → nachträgliche Definition und Rechtfertigung der Kategorien.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS8","text":"Maaß als dritte Bestimmung → Herabsetzung abstrakter Unmittelbarkeit zu einer einzelnen Bestimmtheit innerhalb der Sphäre der Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF1","text":"Vorläufige Kategorienordnung → Forderung immanenter Begründung → Entwicklung des Seyns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF2","text":"Abstraktes Seyn → unmittelbare Bestimmtheit → Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF3","text":"Qualität → negative Aufhebung ihrer Einheit mit dem Seyn → Quantität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF4","text":"Qualität und Quantität → bestimmte Vermittlungsrelation → Maaß.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF5","text":"Maaß → Abgrenzung von allgemeiner Relation und subjektiver Modalität → eigenständige Bestimmung des Seyns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF6","text":"Eigene Entwicklung des Seyns → Rechtfertigung der Eintheilung → Abweichung von der gewöhnlichen Kategorienordnung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME1","text":"Kategorien werden von einer taxonomischen Reihenfolge in eine genetische Ordnung überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME2","text":"Qualität und Quantität werden nicht mehr als gleichrangige Klassen, sondern als aufeinander bezogene Entwicklungsstufen kartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME3","text":"Der Gegensatz von Qualität und Quantität wird als Übergang von unmittelbarer Einheit zu aufgehobener Bestimmtheit neu klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME4","text":"Maaß wird als spezifische Vermittlungsform zwischen qualitativer Identität und quantitativer Differenz sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME5","text":"Relation und Modalität werden aus ihrer gewöhnlichen systematischen Nachbarschaft herausgelöst und auf andere begriffliche Orte verwiesen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME6","text":"Die Grenze zwischen ontologischer Bestimmung und subjektiver Kategorienordnung wird als systematische Trennlinie sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT1","text":"Surface — Das Seyn wird in Qualität, Quantität und Maaß eingetheilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die Eintheilung wird durch die immanente Bewegung von unmittelbarer Bestimmtheit, aufgehobener Bestimmtheit und Vermittlung erzeugt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Die gewöhnliche Kategorienordnung wird durch den Vorrang der immanenten Begründung neu gerahmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Das Seyn ist eine sich entwickelnde Begriffssphäre, deren Bestimmungen in einer gerichteten Folge aus abstrakter Unmittelbarkeit hervorgehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Folge Qualität → Quantität → Maaß und ihre grundlegende Begründungsrichtung zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt der konkrete Übergang von der ersten zur zweiten und von der zweiten zur dritten Bestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern die Aufhebung der qualitativen Einheit als Erzeugung der Quantität akzeptiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT4","text":"Ihre stärkste Stelle ist die Ableitung der Priorität der Qualität aus der Einheit von Bestimmung und Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT5","text":"Eine Spannung besteht zwischen der vorläufigen Anführung der Kategorien und ihrer nachträglichen immanenten Rechtfertigung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT6","text":"Eine weitere Spannung besteht darin, dass Maaß als dritte Bestimmung erscheint, zugleich aber innerhalb der Qualität lokalisiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT7","text":"Die Abgrenzung von Maaß gegen Relation und Modalität wird behauptet, ohne die spätere positive Bestimmung dieser Kategorien auszuführen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT8","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung des Textes, sofern sie die Kategorien nicht als fertige Klassen, sondern als erzeugte Übergänge behandelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T110926422015Z_baceeffc","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"General Division of Being","source_sha256":"37d22b18371d81da15e1f0ab5015cc721f894c879f573f3d494c754479676cb2","sha256":"2a828e857cded643ed9016b7b70dc676edeba60077c07fecfa1d1d0149729b44","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:09:26.424034+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS1","text":"Being is initially determined through its delimitation from otherness in general.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS2","text":"Thereafter, Being is conceived as determining itself within its own sphere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS3","text":"The initially provisional division is grounded and justified by the movement of Being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS4","text":"The inner development of Being produces the stages of Quality, Quantity, and Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AS5","text":"The third determination leads back to the abstract immediacy of a single determinacy within the sphere of Quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A1","text":"Being is initially determined over against otherness in general.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A2","text":"Being determines itself within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A3","text":"Abstract indeterminacy and immediacy is the form in which Being constitutes the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A4","text":"Being and Essence constitute separate spheres of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A5","text":"The totality of Being appears in its development as a sphere of the Concept.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A6","text":"The determinations of Being arise from its own movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A7","text":"Immediate determinacy is Quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A8","text":"Sublated determinacy is Quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A9","text":"Qualitatively determined Quantity is Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A10","text":"Quality is immediately one with Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A11","text":"Quantity is distinguished from Being and, as sublated Quality, is indifferent to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A12","text":"Quantity includes the alterability of determination without altering Being itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A13","text":"Measure is the determinate relation of Quality and Quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A14","text":"Kant's categories of Relation and Modality do not belong to the determination of Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A15","text":"Qualitative determination is by nature prior to quantitative determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:A16","text":"The third determination of Being posits abstract immediacy as a single determinacy over against other determinations within its sphere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX1","text":"The division of Being is not definitively justified from the outset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX2","text":"The order of categories does not follow the customary sequence of Quantity, Quality, Relation, and Modality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX3","text":"Quantity is not the original determination of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX4","text":"Quality is not a determination detachable from Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX5","text":"Measure is not Relation in general.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX6","text":"Measure is not merely the relation of a content to subjective thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX7","text":"The Kantian determinations of Relation and Modality are not sublated in Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:NX8","text":"The provisional division cannot remain as an externally adopted classification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D1","text":"The beginning must be made with Being as such and therefore with qualitative Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A3","CH_GB18_AEDS:A7","CH_GB18_AEDS:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D2","text":"Quantity presupposes Quality because it is determined as Quality become negative.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A8","CH_GB18_AEDS:A11","CH_GB18_AEDS:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D3","text":"Quantitative determination is indifferent to Being because it has already sublated its immediate unity.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A10","CH_GB18_AEDS:A11","CH_GB18_AEDS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D4","text":"Qualitative determination is the immediate limitation of Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A7","CH_GB18_AEDS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D5","text":"Measure mediates Quality and Quantity through a determinate, not general, relation.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A9","CH_GB18_AEDS:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D6","text":"The categories that Kant subsumes under Relation must be developed outside Measure.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A13","CH_GB18_AEDS:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D7","text":"The category of Modality is unsuitable for Measure insofar as it designates only the relation of content to subjective thinking.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A13","CH_GB18_AEDS:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:D8","text":"The division Quality–Quantity–Measure acquires its validity only through the development of Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_AEDS:A2","CH_GB18_AEDS:A6","CH_GB18_AEDS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD1","text":"The order of categories is transformed from an externally classificatory list into an immanent sequence of development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD2","text":"The priority of Quality rests on the unity of determination and Being, whereas Quantity already presupposes their difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD3","text":"The totality of Being does not arise through the addition of individual categories, but through the movement from immediate determinacy, through sublated determinacy, to determinate mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD4","text":"Measure functions as a boundary form in which qualitative identity and quantitative indifference are at once preserved and mediated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SD5","text":"The critique of the customary order of categories is a critique of its lacking foundation in the object itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an order of categories independent of the movement of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX2","text":"It excludes the intelligibility of quantitative determination without presupposed qualitative determinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX3","text":"It excludes a determination that would be at once immediately identical with Being and completely separate from it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX4","text":"It excludes a merely subjective or epistemological conception of the categories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX5","text":"It excludes the reduction of Measure to general Relation or mere Modality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:DNX6","text":"It excludes a definitive conceptual determination prior to passage through the movement of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX1","text":"Inadmissible is a system in which categories stand externally alongside one another without being generated through an immanent necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX2","text":"Unavailable is a beginning that already presupposes a materially determinate category before Being has produced its determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX3","text":"Excluded remains a separation of ontological determination and conceptual movement through which categories would appear only as forms of subjective thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:SNX4","text":"The hidden counter-possibility of the system is an immediate identity of Being and determination without qualitative limitation, quantitative sublation, or mediation of Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS1","text":"Abstract indeterminacy → beginning of Being → first determination over against otherness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS2","text":"First determination → delimitation of Being from Essence → constitution of a sphere of the Concept of its own.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS3","text":"Sphere of the Concept of its own → inner self-determination → emergence of determinations and movement of reflection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS4","text":"Immediate determinacy → unity of determination and Being → Quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS5","text":"Sublation of this unity → distinction and indifference of determination → Quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS6","text":"Determinate relation of Quality and Quantity → mediation of their difference → Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS7","text":"Provisional division → immanent development → subsequent definition and justification of the categories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:FGS8","text":"Measure as third determination → reduction of abstract immediacy to a single determinacy within the sphere of Quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF1","text":"Provisional order of categories → demand for immanent grounding → development of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF2","text":"Abstract Being → immediate determinacy → Quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF3","text":"Quality → negative sublation of its unity with Being → Quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF4","text":"Quality and Quantity → determinate relation of mediation → Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF5","text":"Measure → delimitation from general Relation and subjective Modality → autonomous determination of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:AF6","text":"Being's own development → justification of the division → deviation from the customary order of categories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME1","text":"Categories are transferred from a taxonomic sequence into a genetic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME2","text":"Quality and Quantity are no longer mapped as coequal classes, but as mutually related stages of development.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME3","text":"The opposition of Quality and Quantity is reclassified as the transition from immediate unity to sublated determinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME4","text":"Measure becomes visible as a specific form of mediation between qualitative identity and quantitative difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME5","text":"Relation and Modality are detached from their customary systematic adjacency and referred to other conceptual loci.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ME6","text":"The boundary between ontological determination and subjective ordering of categories becomes visible as a systematic dividing line.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT1","text":"Surface — Being is divided into Quality, Quantity, and Measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT2","text":"Structural — The division is generated through the immanent movement of immediate determinacy, sublated determinacy, and mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The customary order of categories is reframed through the primacy of immanent grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Being is a developing sphere of the Concept whose determinations emerge in a directed sequence from abstract immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the sequence Quality → Quantity → Measure and its basic direction of grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT2","text":"The concrete transition from the first to the second and from the second to the third determination remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent insofar as the sublation of qualitative unity is accepted as the generation of Quantity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT4","text":"Its strongest point is the derivation of the priority of Quality from the unity of determination and Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT5","text":"A tension exists between the provisional introduction of the categories and their subsequent immanent justification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT6","text":"A further tension consists in the fact that Measure appears as the third determination while at the same time being located within Quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT7","text":"The delimitation of Measure from Relation and Modality is asserted without carrying out the later positive determination of these categories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_AEDS:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text insofar as it treats the categories not as ready-made classes but as generated transitions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_AEDS:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_AEDS@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_AEDS:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 06","title":"General Division of Being","context":"Chapter 06","original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung des Seyns"},"original_title":"Allgemeine Eintheilung des Seyns","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ","layer":"CH","title":"First Section. Determinateness (Quality).","order":7,"parents":["RAW_GB18_EABQ"],"revision":"CH_GB18_EABQ@R001","sha256":"fe09a3b1ada980fe17ce09eff4bb3c80e05ccb5793f1038a244baa976e2c0cc2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS1","text":"Das Seyn wird als unbestimmte, reflexionslose Unmittelbarkeit bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS2","text":"Seine Qualitätslosigkeit gilt nur im Gegensatz zur Bestimmtheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS3","text":"Gegenüber dem bestimmten Seyn wird die Unbestimmtheit selbst zur Qualität des Seyns überhaupt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS4","text":"Die Bestimmungslogik führt vom unmittelbaren Seyn in das Daseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS5","text":"Das endliche Daseyn hebt sich auf und geht in die unendliche Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst über.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS6","text":"Diese Bewegung bestimmt das Fürsichseyn als dritte Form der Seinsbestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","text":"Das Seyn ist das unbestimmte Unmittelbare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A2","text":"Das Seyn ist frei von der Bestimmtheit gegen das Wesen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A3","text":"Das Seyn ist zunächst frei von jeder inneren Bestimmtheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A4","text":"Das reflexionslose Seyn ist nur unmittelbar an ihm selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A5","text":"Unbestimmtheit macht das Seyn zunächst qualitätslos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","text":"Die Unbestimmtheit ist nur im Gegensatz zum Bestimmten oder Qualitativen als solche charakterisiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A7","text":"Dem Seyn überhaupt tritt das bestimmte Seyn als eigenständige Gegenbestimmung gegenüber.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A8","text":"Durch diesen Gegensatz wird die Unbestimmtheit selbst zur Qualität des Seyns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","text":"Das bestimmte Seyn ist als Daseyn gefasst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","text":"Das Daseyn ist endliches Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A11","text":"Das endliche Seyn hebt sich auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A12","text":"Die Aufhebung des endlichen Seyns führt in die unendliche Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A13","text":"Die unendliche Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst ist Fürsichseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX1","text":"Das erste Seyn ist nicht durch eine Bestimmtheit gegen das Wesen vermittelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX2","text":"Das erste Seyn ist nicht reflexiv bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX3","text":"Das erste Seyn enthält zunächst keine innere qualitative Bestimmtheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX4","text":"Das Seyn ist nicht unmittelbar ein bestimmtes oder qualitatives Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX5","text":"Das Daseyn ist nicht als bleibende Endlichkeit haltbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX6","text":"Das endliche Seyn ist nicht die letzte Form des Seyns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX7","text":"Unbestimmtheit ist nicht unabhängig von ihrem Gegensatz zum Bestimmten verständlich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D1","text":"Die Bestimmung des Seyns als qualitätslos setzt einen Gegensatz zwischen Unbestimmtheit und Bestimmtheit voraus.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A5","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D2","text":"Die Gegenüberstellung von Seyn überhaupt und bestimmtem Seyn verwandelt die bloße Unbestimmtheit in eine positive Qualitätsbestimmung.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A7","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D3","text":"Das unmittelbar unbestimmte Seyn wird durch seine eigene begriffliche Bestimmung als bestimmungsfähig ausgewiesen.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D4","text":"Die bestimmte Qualität des Seyns konkretisiert sich als Daseyn.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A8","CH_GB18_EABQ:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D5","text":"Das Daseyn besitzt Endlichkeit, weil seine Bestimmtheit als begrenzte Form des Seyns auftritt.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","CH_GB18_EABQ:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D6","text":"Die Endlichkeit des Daseyns erzeugt seine Aufhebung.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","CH_GB18_EABQ:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D7","text":"Die Aufhebung des Daseyns führt nicht in das Nichts, sondern in eine höhere Seinsrelation.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A11","CH_GB18_EABQ:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD1","text":"Bestimmtheit entsteht nicht außerhalb des Seyns, sondern aus der reflexionslosen Unmittelbarkeit durch deren Gegensatzbildung.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","CH_GB18_EABQ:A4","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD2","text":"Die Unbestimmtheit ist keine vorausgehende Leere, sondern eine relationale Qualität.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A5","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD3","text":"Die Entwicklung des Seyns ist eine Selbstüberschreitung von unmittelbarer Unbestimmtheit über endliche Bestimmtheit zu selbstbezogener Unendlichkeit.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","CH_GB18_EABQ:A12","CH_GB18_EABQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD4","text":"Endlichkeit fungiert als notwendige Durchgangsform der Bewegung zur Selbstbeziehung des Seyns.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","CH_GB18_EABQ:A11","CH_GB18_EABQ:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX1","text":"Das Seyn kann nicht als vollkommen bestimmungslose, von jeder Relation isolierte Abstraktion bestehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX2","text":"Qualität kann nicht als äußerlich hinzugefügte Eigenschaft eines bereits abgeschlossenen Seyns gelten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX3","text":"Endlichkeit kann nicht als selbständige Endstation der Bestimmung bestehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX4","text":"Aufhebung kann nicht als bloße Vernichtung des Seyns verstanden werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX5","text":"Unendlichkeit kann nicht als bloße Abwesenheit von Endlichkeit auftreten, sondern muss als Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst bestimmt sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Seyn, dessen Unbestimmtheit ohne Gegensatz, Vermittlung oder Übergang bestehen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine statische Ontologie, in der Unmittelbarkeit, Bestimmtheit und Selbstbeziehung getrennte Zustände bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Endlichkeit, die keine innere Tendenz zu ihrer Aufhebung enthält.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Unendlichkeit, die lediglich grenzenlose Ausdehnung statt Selbstbeziehung bedeutet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS1","text":"Unbestimmte Unmittelbarkeit → Ausschluss innerer und wesensbezogener Bestimmtheit → reflexionsloses Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS2","text":"Reflexionsloses Seyn → Gegensatz zum bestimmten Seyn → Unbestimmtheit als eigene Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS3","text":"Qualität des Seyns → bestimmte Seinsform → Daseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS4","text":"Daseyn → Endlichkeit → Selbstaufhebung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS5","text":"Selbstaufhebung des endlichen Seyns → unendliche Beziehung des Seyns auf sich selbst → Fürsichseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS6","text":"Die Negation einer isolierten Bestimmungsstufe erzeugt jeweils die nächsthöhere Seinsform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AF1","text":"Unbestimmte Unmittelbarkeit → relationale Bestimmung der Unbestimmtheit → bestimmte Qualität → Daseyn → Endlichkeit → Aufhebung → unendliche Selbstbeziehung → Fürsichseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME1","text":"Unbestimmtheit wird von einer bloßen Abwesenheit von Bestimmung in eine relationale Qualität umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME2","text":"Gegensatz wird als produktive Bedingung der Bestimmung und nicht als äußerliche Gegenüberstellung klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME3","text":"Daseyn wird als vermittelnde Übergangsform zwischen unmittelbarem Seyn und Selbstbeziehung neu eingeordnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME4","text":"Endlichkeit wird als strukturell aufhebungsbedürftige Bestimmtheit sichtbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME5","text":"Unendlichkeit wird als Selbstbeziehung statt als bloße Negation von Grenzen bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT1","text":"Surface — Das Seyn erscheint zunächst als unbestimmtes und qualitätsloses Unmittelbares.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die Bestimmung entsteht durch den Gegensatz zwischen Seyn überhaupt und bestimmtem Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Jede isolierte Bestimmungsform wird durch ihre eigene Negation in die nächste Form überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Seyn ist eine gestufte Bewegungsordnung von Unmittelbarkeit über Endlichkeit zu unendlicher Selbstbeziehung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Bewegung vom unbestimmten Seyn zum Daseyn und weiter zum Fürsichseyn zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt die im Quelltext nur angekündigte nähere Begründung dafür, wie das erste Seyn „an sich bestimmtes“ ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern Gegensatz und Aufhebung als immanente Bewegungen des Seyns gelten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Stelle des Systems ist die Umwandlung der Unbestimmtheit in eine relationale Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT5","text":"Die Rekonstruktion hängt an der nicht vollständig explizierten Vermittlung zwischen Unbestimmtheit, Bestimmtheit und Daseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT6","text":"Die Argumentbewegung bleibt trotz der textlichen Ellipse rekonstruierbar, weil die Übergangsfolge Daseyn → Endlichkeit → Fürsichseyn ausdrücklich gesetzt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T115843222988Z_7df40dc7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"First Section. Determinacy (Quality).","source_sha256":"fe09a3b1ada980fe17ce09eff4bb3c80e05ccb5793f1038a244baa976e2c0cc2","sha256":"68b46e118258acf5d0c9162faa4e91e022443616ca2349bcd279057007d3b265","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:58:43.224767+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS1","text":"Being is determined as indeterminate, reflectionless immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS2","text":"Its lack of quality holds only in contrast to determinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS3","text":"In contrast to determinate Being, indeterminacy itself becomes the quality of Being as such.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS4","text":"The logic of determination leads from immediate Being into determinate being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS5","text":"Finite determinate being sublates itself and passes over into the infinite relation of Being to itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AS6","text":"This movement determines being-for-self as the third form of the determination of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","text":"Being is indeterminate immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A2","text":"Being is free of determinacy in contrast to Essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A3","text":"Being is initially free of every inner determinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A4","text":"Reflectionless Being is only immediately in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A5","text":"Indeterminacy initially renders Being devoid of quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","text":"Indeterminacy is characterized as such only in contrast to the determinate or qualitative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A7","text":"Determinate Being confronts Being as such as an autonomous counter-determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A8","text":"Through this contrast, indeterminacy itself becomes the quality of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","text":"Determinate Being is conceived as determinate being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","text":"Determinate being is finite Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A11","text":"Finite Being sublates itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A12","text":"The sublation of finite Being leads into the infinite relation of Being to itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:A13","text":"The infinite relation of Being to itself is being-for-self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX1","text":"The first Being is not mediated through a determinacy in contrast to Essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX2","text":"The first Being is not determined reflectively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX3","text":"The first Being initially contains no inner qualitative determinacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX4","text":"Being is not immediately a determinate or qualitative Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX5","text":"Determinate being cannot be sustained as abiding finitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX6","text":"Finite Being is not the final form of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:NX7","text":"Indeterminacy cannot be understood independently of its contrast to the determinate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D1","text":"The determination of Being as devoid of quality presupposes a contrast between indeterminacy and determinacy.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A5","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D2","text":"The juxtaposition of Being as such and determinate Being transforms mere indeterminacy into a positive qualitative determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A7","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D3","text":"Immediately indeterminate Being is shown, through its own conceptual determination, to be capable of determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D4","text":"The determinate quality of Being concretizes itself as determinate being.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A8","CH_GB18_EABQ:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D5","text":"Determinate being possesses finitude because its determinacy appears as a limited form of Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","CH_GB18_EABQ:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D6","text":"The finitude of determinate being generates its sublation.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","CH_GB18_EABQ:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:D7","text":"The sublation of determinate being leads not into Nothing, but into a higher relation of Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A11","CH_GB18_EABQ:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD1","text":"Determinacy arises not outside Being, but from reflectionless immediacy through its formation of contrast.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","CH_GB18_EABQ:A4","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD2","text":"Indeterminacy is not a preceding emptiness, but a relational quality.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A5","CH_GB18_EABQ:A6","CH_GB18_EABQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD3","text":"The development of Being is a self-transcendence from immediate indeterminacy through finite determinacy to self-related infinity.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A1","CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","CH_GB18_EABQ:A12","CH_GB18_EABQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SD4","text":"Finitude functions as a necessary transitional form of the movement toward the self-relation of Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_EABQ:A9","CH_GB18_EABQ:A10","CH_GB18_EABQ:A11","CH_GB18_EABQ:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX1","text":"Being cannot subsist as a completely determinationless abstraction isolated from every relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX2","text":"Quality cannot count as an externally added property of an already completed Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX3","text":"Finitude cannot subsist as an autonomous final station of determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX4","text":"Sublation cannot be understood as mere annihilation of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:DNX5","text":"Infinity cannot appear as the mere absence of finitude, but must be determined as the relation of Being to itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX1","text":"Excluded is a Being whose indeterminacy could subsist without contrast, mediation, or transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX2","text":"Excluded is a static ontology in which immediacy, determinacy, and self-relation remain separate states.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX3","text":"Excluded is a finitude that contains no inner tendency toward its sublation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:SNX4","text":"Excluded is an infinity that signifies merely boundless extension rather than self-relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS1","text":"Indeterminate immediacy → exclusion of inner and essence-related determinacy → reflectionless Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS2","text":"Reflectionless Being → contrast to determinate Being → indeterminacy as its own quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS3","text":"Quality of Being → determinate form of Being → determinate being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS4","text":"Determinate being → finitude → self-sublation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS5","text":"Self-sublation of finite Being → infinite relation of Being to itself → being-for-self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:FGS6","text":"The negation of an isolated stage of determination generates in each case the next higher form of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:AF1","text":"Indeterminate immediacy → relational determination of indeterminacy → determinate quality → determinate being → finitude → sublation → infinite self-relation → being-for-self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME1","text":"Indeterminacy is remapped from a mere absence of determination into a relational quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME2","text":"Contrast is classified as a productive condition of determination and not as an external juxtaposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME3","text":"Determinate being is newly situated as a mediating transitional form between immediate Being and self-relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME4","text":"Finitude becomes visible as a determinacy structurally requiring sublation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ME5","text":"Infinity is determined as self-relation rather than as the mere negation of limits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT1","text":"Surface — Being initially appears as indeterminate and qualityless immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT2","text":"Structural — Determination arises through the contrast between Being as such and determinate Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Every isolated form of determination is transferred into the next form through its own negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Being is a graduated order of movement from immediacy through finitude to infinite self-relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the movement from indeterminate Being to determinate being and onward to being-for-self.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT2","text":"What remains underdetermined is the more detailed justification, only announced in the source text, of how the first Being is „an sich bestimmtes“.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent, provided that contrast and sublation count as immanent movements of Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT4","text":"The strongest point of the system is the transformation of indeterminacy into a relational quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction depends on the mediation between indeterminacy, determinacy, and determinate being, which is not fully explicated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_EABQ:MRT6","text":"Despite the textual ellipsis, the movement of the argument remains reconstructible because the transitional sequence determinate being → finitude → being-for-self is explicitly posited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_EABQ:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_EABQ@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_EABQ:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 07","title":"First Section. Determinateness (Quality).","context":"Chapter 07","original_title":"Erster Abschnitt. Bestimmtheit (Qualität)."},"original_title":"Erster Abschnitt. Bestimmtheit (Qualität).","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN","layer":"CH","title":"A. Being.","order":8,"parents":["RAW_GB18_SEYN"],"revision":"CH_GB18_SEYN@R001","sha256":"960f93b07e2c869ee0d892a44c57a54a8afccb7b302bdaa6f1ab141456addda2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS1","text":"Das zentrale Problem ist die Bestimmung dessen, was von Seyn übrig bleibt, wenn jede weitere Bestimmung ausgeschlossen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS2","text":"Seyn wird als reine, unbestimmte Unmittelbarkeit angesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS3","text":"Jede Bestimmung würde eine Differenz innerhalb des Seyns oder gegenüber einem Anderen einführen und damit seine Reinheit aufheben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS4","text":"Die Ausschließung jeder Differenz reduziert Seyn auf reine Unbestimmtheit und Leere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS5","text":"Diese Leere gilt gleichermaßen für Anschauung und Denken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS6","text":"Die Rekonstruktion führt daher von reinem Seyn zur Bestimmung desselben als Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS7","text":"Das Argument ist eine ontologisch-diagnostische Reduktion von unmittelbarer Setzung zu negativer Identität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A1","text":"Reines Seyn besitzt keine weitere Bestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A2","text":"Reines Seyn ist in seiner Unmittelbarkeit nur sich selbst gleich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A3","text":"Reines Seyn ist weder gegen ein Anderes ungleich noch in sich verschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A4","text":"Eine unterschiedene Bestimmung oder ein Inhalt würde Seyn von Anderem unterscheiden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A5","text":"Eine solche Unterscheidung würde die Reinheit des Seyns aufheben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","text":"Reines Seyn ist reine Unbestimmtheit und Leere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A7","text":"In reinem Seyn ist nichts anzuschauen, sofern überhaupt von Anschauung gesprochen werden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A8","text":"In reinem Seyn ist nichts zu denken, sofern überhaupt von Denken gesprochen werden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX1","text":"Reines Seyn ist nicht durch irgendeine weitere Bestimmung charakterisiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX2","text":"Reines Seyn enthält keine innere Verschiedenheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX3","text":"Reines Seyn steht in keiner äußeren Verschiedenheit zu einem Anderen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX4","text":"Reines Seyn ist kein bestimmter Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX5","text":"Reines Seyn ist keine positive Anschauung eines Gegenstandes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX6","text":"Reines Seyn ist kein gedanklich bestimmbarer Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX7","text":"Jede Differenzierung ist mit der behaupteten Reinheit des Seyns unvereinbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D1","text":"Die vollständige Abwesenheit von Bestimmung lässt reines Seyn als reine Leere erscheinen.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A1","CH_GB18_SEYN:A4","CH_GB18_SEYN:A5","CH_GB18_SEYN:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D2","text":"Reines Seyn besitzt keinen unterscheidbaren Gegenstand der Anschauung.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D3","text":"Reines Seyn besitzt keinen unterscheidbaren Inhalt des Denkens.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D4","text":"Die Bestimmung des reinen Seyns als Seyn liefert keinen größeren positiven Gehalt als die Bestimmung als Nichts.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A7","CH_GB18_SEYN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D5","text":"Reines Seyn wird aufgrund seiner vollkommenen Unbestimmtheit als Nichts bestimmt.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A1","CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A7","CH_GB18_SEYN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD1","text":"Eine vollständig von Bestimmungen gereinigte positive Setzung kippt in die negative Bestimmung des Nichts um.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD2","text":"Die Identität von Seyn und Nichts entsteht nicht durch äußere Vermittlung, sondern aus der inneren Konsequenz reiner Unmittelbarkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD3","text":"Die Grenze zwischen positiver ontologischer Setzung und ihrer Negation wird durch den Ausschluss jeder Differenz unentscheidbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD4","text":"Die behauptete Unmittelbarkeit erzeugt eine Bestimmung, die ihren eigenen positiven Anspruch entleert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX1","text":"Das System schließt stillschweigend aus, dass eine Bestimmung ohne Differenz möglich ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX2","text":"Das System schließt aus, dass reine Unmittelbarkeit einen eigenständigen positiven Gehalt bewahren kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX3","text":"Das System disqualifiziert die Annahme, Seyn könne ohne Relation, Inhalt oder Unterschied denkbar bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX4","text":"Das System behandelt jede positive Bestimmbarkeit des reinen Seyns als Verletzung seiner ursprünglichen Setzung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Ontologie, in der das absolut Unbestimmte dennoch als positiver Gegenstand verfügbar bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX2","text":"Die versperrte Möglichkeit ist ein reines Seyn, das zugleich vollständig leer und dennoch von Nichts unterschieden wäre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX3","text":"Die Abwesenheit jeder Differenz strukturiert den Übergang von Seyn zu Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX4","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine begriffliche Bestimmung des Seyns, die weder Inhalt noch Unterschied einführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS1","text":"Setzung reines Seyn → Ausschluss jeder Bestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS2","text":"Ausschluss jeder Bestimmung → Ausschluss innerer und äußerer Differenz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS3","text":"Ausschluss jeder Differenz → reine Unbestimmtheit und Leere in Anschauung und Denken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS4","text":"Reine Unbestimmtheit und Leere → Bestimmung des reinen Seyns als Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS5","text":"Bestimmung als Nichts → Gleichrangigkeit von Seyn und Nichts hinsichtlich positiven Gehalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AF1","text":"Reines Seyn → Ausschluss jeder Bestimmung → Ausschluss jeder Differenz → Leere von Anschauung und Denken → reine Unbestimmtheit → Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME1","text":"Der Gegenstandsbereich wird von einem scheinbar positiven ontologischen Ausgangspunkt auf die Abwesenheit jedes bestimmbaren Inhalts umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME2","text":"Die Unterscheidung zwischen Seyn und Nichts wird als abhängig von Bestimmung sichtbar und dadurch aufgehoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME3","text":"Anschauung und Denken werden nicht als unabhängige Zugänge, sondern als gleichartig leere Formen der Unbestimmtheit klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME4","text":"Differenz erscheint nicht mehr als nachträgliche Eigenschaft, sondern als notwendige Bedingung jedes positiven Gehalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT1","text":"Surface: Seyn wird als unbestimmte Unmittelbarkeit ohne weiteren Inhalt gesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT2","text":"Structural: Der Ausschluss von Bestimmungen beseitigt zugleich innere, äußere, anschauliche und begriffliche Differenz.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Die Argumentation verwandelt die anfängliche positive Setzung durch konsequente Reinigung in ihre negative Grenzbestimmung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Sein und Nichts werden als gleich unmittelbare, nicht vermittelte Bestimmungen desselben leeren Anfangs konfiguriert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Reduktion von reinem Seyn auf reine Unbestimmtheit und Nichts zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT2","text":"Für die Rekonstruktion genügt die Verbindung von Bestimmungslosigkeit, Differenzlosigkeit, leerer Anschauung und leerem Denken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT3","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wie die Identität von Seyn und Nichts über den bloßen Anfang hinaus weiter vermittelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT4","text":"Intern kohärent ist die Struktur insofern, als jede positive Ergänzung als Widerspruch zur Reinheit ausgeschlossen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT5","text":"Die stärkste Stelle liegt in der systematischen Kopplung von Unbestimmtheit und Inhaltslosigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT6","text":"Die zentrale Spannung besteht darin, dass Seyn zunächst als selbstgleiche Setzung behauptet und anschließend aufgrund seiner Inhaltslosigkeit als Nichts bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung vom positiven Anfang über apophatische Reinigung zur negativen Identität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T120003622211Z_2961749b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"A. Being.","source_sha256":"960f93b07e2c869ee0d892a44c57a54a8afccb7b302bdaa6f1ab141456addda2","sha256":"b936bb2519eba1ef66ed1e70d21816fbc20c10591cd118a7f38d2d567b2d3ef2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T12:00:03.623323+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS1","text":"The central problem is the determination of what remains of Seyn when every further determination is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS2","text":"Seyn is posited as pure, indeterminate immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS3","text":"Every determination would introduce a difference within Seyn or in relation to an Other, and would thereby annul its purity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS4","text":"The exclusion of every difference reduces Seyn to pure indeterminacy and emptiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS5","text":"This emptiness applies equally to intuition and thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS6","text":"The reconstruction therefore leads from pure Seyn to its determination as Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AS7","text":"The argument is an ontological-diagnostic reduction from immediate positing to negative identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A1","text":"Pure Seyn possesses no further determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A2","text":"Pure Seyn, in its immediacy, is only equal to itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A3","text":"Pure Seyn is neither unequal to an Other nor different within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A4","text":"A differentiated determination or a content would distinguish Seyn from an Other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A5","text":"Such a distinction would annul the purity of Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","text":"Pure Seyn is pure indeterminacy and emptiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A7","text":"In pure Seyn, there is nothing to intuit, insofar as intuition can be spoken of at all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:A8","text":"In pure Seyn, there is nothing to think, insofar as thought can be spoken of at all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX1","text":"Pure Seyn is not characterized by any further determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX2","text":"Pure Seyn contains no inner difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX3","text":"Pure Seyn stands in no external difference from an Other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX4","text":"Pure Seyn is not a determinate content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX5","text":"Pure Seyn is not a positive intuition of an object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX6","text":"Pure Seyn is not a content determinable in thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:NX7","text":"Every differentiation is incompatible with the asserted purity of Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D1","text":"The complete absence of determination makes pure Seyn appear as pure emptiness.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A1","CH_GB18_SEYN:A4","CH_GB18_SEYN:A5","CH_GB18_SEYN:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D2","text":"Pure Seyn possesses no distinguishable object of intuition.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D3","text":"Pure Seyn possesses no distinguishable content of thought.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D4","text":"The determination of pure Seyn as Seyn yields no greater positive content than its determination as Nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A7","CH_GB18_SEYN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:D5","text":"Pure Seyn is determined as Nothing on account of its complete indeterminacy.","refs":["CH_GB18_SEYN:A1","CH_GB18_SEYN:A6","CH_GB18_SEYN:A7","CH_GB18_SEYN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD1","text":"A positive positing completely purified of determinations tips over into the negative determination of Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD2","text":"The identity of Seyn and Nothing arises not through external mediation, but from the inner consequence of pure immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD3","text":"The boundary between positive ontological positing and its negation becomes undecidable through the exclusion of every difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SD4","text":"The asserted immediacy produces a determination that empties its own positive claim.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX1","text":"The system tacitly excludes the possibility that a determination without difference is possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that pure immediacy can preserve an independent positive content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX3","text":"The system disqualifies the assumption that Seyn could remain thinkable without relation, content, or difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:DNX4","text":"The system treats every positive determinability of pure Seyn as a violation of its original positing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX1","text":"Excluded is an ontology in which the absolutely indeterminate nevertheless remains available as a positive object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX2","text":"The blocked possibility is a pure Seyn that is at once completely empty and yet distinguished from Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX3","text":"The absence of every difference structures the transition from Seyn to Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:SNX4","text":"Unavailable is a conceptual determination of Seyn that introduces neither content nor difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS1","text":"Positing pure Seyn → exclusion of every determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS2","text":"Exclusion of every determination → exclusion of inner and external difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS3","text":"Exclusion of every difference → pure indeterminacy and emptiness in intuition and thought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS4","text":"Pure indeterminacy and emptiness → determination of pure Seyn as Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:FGS5","text":"Determination as Nothing → equivalence of Seyn and Nothing with respect to positive content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:AF1","text":"Pure Seyn → exclusion of every determination → exclusion of every difference → emptiness of intuition and thought → pure indeterminacy → Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME1","text":"The object-domain is remapped from a seemingly positive ontological point of departure to the absence of every determinable content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME2","text":"The distinction between Seyn and Nothing becomes visible as dependent on determination and is thereby annulled.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME3","text":"Intuition and thought are classified not as independent modes of access, but as equally empty forms of indeterminacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ME4","text":"Difference no longer appears as a subsequent property, but as a necessary condition of every positive content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT1","text":"Surface: Seyn is posited as indeterminate immediacy without further content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT2","text":"Structural: The exclusion of determinations simultaneously eliminates inner, external, intuitive, and conceptual difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: Through consistent purification, the argumentation transforms the initial positive positing into its negative limiting determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Being and Nothing are configured as equally immediate, unmediated determinations of the same empty beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the reduction of pure Seyn to pure indeterminacy and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT2","text":"For the reconstruction, the conjunction of lack of determination, lack of difference, empty intuition, and empty thought suffices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT3","text":"It remains underdetermined how the identity of Seyn and Nothing is further mediated beyond the mere beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT4","text":"The structure is internally coherent insofar as every positive addition is excluded as a contradiction of purity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT5","text":"The strongest point lies in the systematic coupling of indeterminacy and lack of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT6","text":"The central tension consists in Seyn first being asserted as a self-identical positing and subsequently being determined as Nothing on account of its lack of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_SEYN:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement from the positive beginning, through apophatic purification, to negative identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_SEYN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_SEYN@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_SEYN:v1","source_language_code":"de","original_title":"A. Seyn."}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 08","title":"A. Being.","context":"Chapter 08","original_title":"A. Seyn."},"original_title":"A. Seyn.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC","layer":"CH","title":"B. Nothing.","order":9,"parents":["RAW_GB18_BNIC"],"revision":"CH_GB18_BNIC@R001","sha256":"dce6f8c515b2ccb33ca44c77d62f9e543eac6abe2bb513da93b08759bc7b5ee5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS1","text":"Das zentrale Problem ist die Bestimmung des reinen Nichts ohne Rückgriff auf einen bestimmten Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS2","text":"Das reine Nichts wird als vollkommene Bestimmungslosigkeit und als einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst angesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS3","text":"Anschauen und Denken führen zunächst eine Differenz zwischen etwas und nichts ein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS4","text":"Das Denken oder Anschauen des Nichts besitzt dennoch Bedeutung und macht das Nichts als leere Tätigkeit präsent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS5","text":"Die leere Tätigkeit des Anschauens und Denkens fällt mit der Bestimmungslosigkeit des reinen Seins zusammen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS6","text":"Die Argumentbewegung führt von der isolierten Bestimmungslosigkeit über die leere Bewusstseinsform zur Identität von reinem Nichts und reinem Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A1","text":"Das reine Nichts ist einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A2","text":"Das reine Nichts ist vollkommen leer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","text":"Das reine Nichts besitzt keine Bestimmung und keinen Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A4","text":"Das reine Nichts ist in sich ununterschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A5","text":"Anschauen und Denken können sich auf etwas oder auf nichts richten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A6","text":"Das Anschauen oder Denken des Nichts bildet eine unterscheidbare Bedeutung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A7","text":"Das Nichts ist im Anschauen oder Denken als leere Tätigkeit gegenwärtig.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A8","text":"Das leere Anschauen oder Denken hat dieselbe Bestimmungslosigkeit wie das reine Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A9","text":"Das reine Sein und das reine Nichts sind hinsichtlich ihrer Bestimmungslosigkeit identisch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX1","text":"Das reine Nichts ist kein bestimmter Inhalt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX2","text":"Das reine Nichts ist keine bestimmte Eigenschaft oder Qualität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX3","text":"Das reine Nichts ist nicht durch innere Unterschiede gegliedert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX4","text":"Das reine Nichts ist nicht als empirisches Fehlen eines bestimmten Etwas bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX5","text":"Das reine Nichts ist nicht außerhalb von Anschauen oder Denken als eigenständiger Gegenstand gegeben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX6","text":"Das reine Nichts ist nicht vom reinen Sein durch einen positiven Inhalt unterschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D1","text":"Die vollständige Inhaltslosigkeit des Nichts erzeugt seine Gleichheit mit sich selbst.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A1","CH_GB18_BNIC:A2","CH_GB18_BNIC:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D2","text":"Die Rede vom Anschauen oder Denken des Nichts führt eine relationale Differenz ein, ohne dem Nichts einen Inhalt zu geben.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","CH_GB18_BNIC:A5","CH_GB18_BNIC:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D3","text":"Das Nichts ist als leeres Anschauen oder Denken nicht bloß abwesend, sondern als Bestimmungslosigkeit präsent.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A6","CH_GB18_BNIC:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D4","text":"Die unterscheidende Tätigkeit des Anschauens oder Denkens hebt die inhaltliche Ununterschiedenheit des Nichts nicht auf.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","CH_GB18_BNIC:A4","CH_GB18_BNIC:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D5","text":"Das reine Nichts erhält durch seine Gegenüberstellung mit dem Etwas keine positive Bestimmung.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","CH_GB18_BNIC:A5","CH_GB18_BNIC:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D6","text":"Die Bestimmungslosigkeit des leeren Denkens beziehungsweise Anschauens entspricht der Bestimmungslosigkeit des reinen Seins.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A7","CH_GB18_BNIC:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD1","text":"Die Differenz zwischen etwas und nichts entsteht auf der Ebene der intentionalen Tätigkeit, nicht durch einen inhaltlichen Unterschied zwischen reinem Sein und reinem Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD2","text":"Das System verschiebt die Bestimmung des Nichts von einem vermeintlichen Gegenstand auf die Form eines leeren Vollzugs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD3","text":"Reines Sein und reines Nichts bilden eine Einheit, weil beide jede positive Bestimmung ausschließen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD4","text":"Die Möglichkeit, Nichts zu denken, fungiert als Beweis seiner begrifflichen Präsenz und zugleich als Nachweis seiner Inhaltslosigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD5","text":"Die anfängliche ontologische Gegenüberstellung von Sein und Nichts wird in eine Identität ihrer abstraktesten Bestimmungen überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX1","text":"Das Argument setzt die Unwahrheit eines Nichts voraus, das als eigenständige positive Realität neben dem Sein steht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX2","text":"Es wird ausgeschlossen, dass das Nichts durch die Negation eines bestimmten Etwas vollständig bestimmt ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX3","text":"Es wird ausgeschlossen, dass Bewusstsein dem Nichts durch seine Bezugnahme einen Inhalt verleiht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX4","text":"Es wird ausgeschlossen, dass die Differenz zwischen Sein und Nichts aus einer qualitativen Verschiedenheit ihrer reinen Anfangsbestimmungen hervorgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX5","text":"Es wird ausgeschlossen, dass die Existenzweise des Nichts unabhängig von Anschauen oder Denken bestimmt werden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX1","text":"Der Text schließt die Möglichkeit eines inhaltlich bestimmbaren reinen Anfangs aus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX2","text":"Der Text lässt keinen externen Standpunkt zu, von dem aus das Nichts als vom Denken unabhängiges Gegenstück des Seins fixiert werden könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX3","text":"Die versperrte Möglichkeit ist eine stabile Trennung von Sein und Nichts auf der Ebene reiner Bestimmungslosigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen bleibt eine Negation, die bereits über einen positiven Gegenstand und dessen bestimmte Aufhebung verfügt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX5","text":"Die gesamte Bestimmung des Nichts organisiert sich um die Abwesenheit jedes Unterschieds, der seine Identität mit dem reinen Sein verhindern könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS1","text":"Vollkommene Inhaltslosigkeit → Ausschluss jeder positiven Bestimmung → einfache Gleichheit mit sich selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS2","text":"Bezug auf etwas oder nichts → Einführung einer intentionalen Differenz → Bedeutung des Nichts im Anschauen oder Denken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS3","text":"Bedeutung des Nichts → Präsenz als leeres Anschauen oder Denken → keine Aufhebung der Inhaltslosigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS4","text":"Leeres Anschauen oder Denken → Identität der Bestimmungslosigkeit mit reinem Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS5","text":"Identität der Bestimmungslosigkeit → Gleichsetzung von reinem Nichts und reinem Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AF1","text":"Reines Nichts als Inhaltslosigkeit → leere Gleichheit mit sich selbst → intentionale Differenz zwischen etwas und nichts → Präsenz des Nichts als leerer Vollzug → Identität mit dem reinen Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME1","text":"Das Nichts wird von einem vermeintlichen Gegenstand zu einer Form leerer Anschauungs- und Denktätigkeit umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME2","text":"Die Differenz zwischen etwas und nichts wird von einer ontologischen Differenz in eine Differenz der Bezugnahme verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME3","text":"Reines Sein und reines Nichts werden als gleichrangige Ausdrücke derselben Bestimmungslosigkeit klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME4","text":"Die Opposition von Sein und Nichts verliert ihren Gegensatzcharakter, sobald sie auf reine, inhaltslose Anfangsbestimmungen reduziert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME5","text":"Denken und Anschauen erscheinen nicht als externe Instanzen, sondern als der Ort, an dem die Bestimmungslosigkeit des Nichts überhaupt artikuliert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT1","text":"Surface — Das reine Nichts wird als leer, bestimmungslos, inhaltslos und in sich ununterschieden bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die Differenz von etwas und nichts wird durch die relationale Struktur des Anschauens und Denkens erzeugt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Die vermeintliche Opposition von Sein und Nichts wird durch Rückführung auf gemeinsame Bestimmungslosigkeit neutralisiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Der ontologische Anfang besitzt keine positive Bestimmung; reines Sein und reines Nichts sind daher dieselbe abstrakte Anfangsform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Bewegung von der Inhaltslosigkeit des Nichts zu seiner Identität mit dem reinen Sein zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT2","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bleibt unterbestimmt hinsichtlich eines weiteren Übergangs, insbesondere hinsichtlich einer möglichen Vermittlung von Sein und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern Bestimmungslosigkeit als entscheidendes Identitätskriterium gilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT4","text":"Ihre stärkste Stelle ist die Ableitung der Identität aus dem gemeinsamen Ausschluss jedes Inhalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT5","text":"Eine ungelöste Spannung entsteht daraus, dass Anschauen und Denken zunächst unterscheiden, während das reine Nichts zugleich als ununterschieden bestimmt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT6","text":"Eine weitere Spannung liegt in der Formulierung, das Nichts „existiere“ im Anschauen oder Denken, obwohl seine Bestimmung gerade in der Inhaltslosigkeit besteht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Argumentbewegung, solange die intentionale Differenz nicht mit einer positiven ontologischen Differenz verwechselt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T113602633735Z_e5f3af5d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"B. Nothing.","source_sha256":"dce6f8c515b2ccb33ca44c77d62f9e543eac6abe2bb513da93b08759bc7b5ee5","sha256":"877a6861cda584f49b103564804d926c213a5037674ffe8669dffdb2d4a54d5e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:36:02.635620+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS1","text":"The central problem is the determination of pure nothing without recourse to a determinate content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS2","text":"Pure nothing is posited as complete indeterminacy and as simple equality with itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS3","text":"Intuition and thinking initially introduce a difference between something and nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS4","text":"The thinking or intuition of nothing nevertheless possesses significance and makes nothing present as empty activity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS5","text":"The empty activity of intuition and thinking coincides with the indeterminacy of pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AS6","text":"The movement of the argument proceeds from isolated indeterminacy, through the empty form of consciousness, to the identity of pure nothing and pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A1","text":"Pure nothing is simple equality with itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A2","text":"Pure nothing is completely empty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","text":"Pure nothing possesses no determination and no content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A4","text":"Pure nothing is undifferentiated within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A5","text":"Intuition and thinking can be directed toward something or toward nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A6","text":"The intuition or thinking of nothing constitutes a distinguishable meaning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A7","text":"Nothing is present in intuition or thinking as empty activity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A8","text":"Empty intuition or thinking has the same indeterminacy as pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:A9","text":"Pure being and pure nothing are identical with respect to their indeterminacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX1","text":"Pure nothing is not a determinate content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX2","text":"Pure nothing is not a determinate property or quality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX3","text":"Pure nothing is not articulated by internal differences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX4","text":"Pure nothing is not determined as the empirical absence of a determinate something.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX5","text":"Pure nothing is not given outside intuition or thinking as an independent object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:NX6","text":"Pure nothing is not distinguished from pure being by a positive content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D1","text":"The complete lack of content of nothing produces its equality with itself.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A1","CH_GB18_BNIC:A2","CH_GB18_BNIC:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D2","text":"Talk of the intuition or thinking of nothing introduces a relational difference without giving nothing a content.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","CH_GB18_BNIC:A5","CH_GB18_BNIC:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D3","text":"As empty intuition or thinking, nothing is not merely absent, but present as indeterminacy.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A6","CH_GB18_BNIC:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D4","text":"The distinguishing activity of intuition or thinking does not abolish the contentual undifferentiatedness of nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","CH_GB18_BNIC:A4","CH_GB18_BNIC:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D5","text":"Pure nothing acquires no positive determination through its opposition to something.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A3","CH_GB18_BNIC:A5","CH_GB18_BNIC:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:D6","text":"The indeterminacy of empty thinking or intuition corresponds to the indeterminacy of pure being.","refs":["CH_GB18_BNIC:A7","CH_GB18_BNIC:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD1","text":"The difference between something and nothing arises at the level of intentional activity, not through a contentual difference between pure being and pure nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD2","text":"The system shifts the determination of nothing from a supposed object to the form of an empty enactment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD3","text":"Pure being and pure nothing form a unity because both exclude every positive determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD4","text":"The possibility of thinking nothing functions as proof of its conceptual presence and, at the same time, as evidence of its lack of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SD5","text":"The initial ontological opposition of being and nothing is transformed into an identity of their most abstract determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX1","text":"The argument presupposes the untruth of a nothing that stands alongside being as an independent positive reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX2","text":"It is excluded that nothing is completely determined through the negation of a determinate something.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX3","text":"It is excluded that consciousness confers content upon nothing through its relation to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX4","text":"It is excluded that the difference between being and nothing proceeds from a qualitative difference between their pure initial determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:DNX5","text":"It is excluded that the mode of existence of nothing can be determined independently of intuition or thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX1","text":"The text excludes the possibility of a pure beginning determinable in terms of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX2","text":"The text permits no external standpoint from which nothing could be fixed as a counterpart of being independent of thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX3","text":"The barred possibility is a stable separation of being and nothing at the level of pure indeterminacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX4","text":"Excluded remains a negation that already possesses a positive object and its determinate sublation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:SNX5","text":"The entire determination of nothing is organized around the absence of every difference that could prevent its identity with pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS1","text":"Complete lack of content → exclusion of every positive determination → simple equality with itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS2","text":"Relation to something or nothing → introduction of an intentional difference → significance of nothing in intuition or thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS3","text":"Significance of nothing → presence as empty intuition or thinking → no abolition of the lack of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS4","text":"Empty intuition or thinking → identity of indeterminacy with pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:FGS5","text":"Identity of indeterminacy → equation of pure nothing and pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:AF1","text":"Pure nothing as lack of content → empty equality with itself → intentional difference between something and nothing → presence of nothing as empty enactment → identity with pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME1","text":"Nothing is remapped from a supposed object into a form of empty intuitive and thinking activity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME2","text":"The difference between something and nothing is shifted from an ontological difference into a difference of relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME3","text":"Pure being and pure nothing are classified as equivalent expressions of the same indeterminacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME4","text":"The opposition of being and nothing loses its oppositional character as soon as it is reduced to pure, contentless initial determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ME5","text":"Thinking and intuition appear not as external instances, but as the locus in which the indeterminacy of nothing is articulated at all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT1","text":"Surface — Pure nothing is determined as empty, indeterminate, contentless, and undifferentiated within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT2","text":"Structural — The difference between something and nothing is generated by the relational structure of intuition and thinking.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The supposed opposition of being and nothing is neutralized by reduction to shared indeterminacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The ontological beginning possesses no positive determination; pure being and pure nothing are therefore the same abstract initial form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the movement from the lack of content of nothing to its identity with pure being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined with regard to a further transition, in particular with regard to a possible mediation of being and nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent insofar as indeterminacy counts as the decisive criterion of identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT4","text":"Its strongest point is the derivation of identity from the shared exclusion of every content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT5","text":"An unresolved tension arises from the fact that intuition and thinking initially distinguish, while pure nothing is at the same time determined as undifferentiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT6","text":"A further tension lies in the formulation that nothing “exists” in intuition or thinking, although its determination consists precisely in lack of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_BNIC:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the argument so long as the intentional difference is not confused with a positive ontological difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_BNIC:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_BNIC@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_BNIC:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 09","title":"B. Nothing.","context":"Chapter 09","original_title":"B. Nichts."},"original_title":"B. Nichts.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS","layer":"CH","title":"1. Unity of Being and Nothing.","order":10,"parents":["RAW_GB18_1EDS"],"revision":"CH_GB18_1EDS@R001","sha256":"b0aec1e9a7f203f60111c890dc801dd3a86b3bd029ca745140d98d926ecfdbf9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS1","text":"Das reine Seyn und das reine Nichts werden zunächst als dasselbe bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS2","text":"Ihre Wahrheit wird von beiden isolierten Bestimmungen auf die Bewegung ihres gegenseitigen Übergehens verlagert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS3","text":"Dieses Übergehen ist nicht ein noch ausstehender Vorgang, sondern als bereits vollzogen bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS4","text":"Die Wahrheit besteht weder in bloßer Identität noch in bloßer Unterschiedenheit, sondern in absoluter Differenz bei ungetrennter Untrennbarkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS5","text":"Weil jedes Moment unmittelbar in seinem Gegenteil verschwindet und der Unterschied sich ebenso unmittelbar auflöst, wird diese Bewegung als Werden bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A1","text":"Das reine Seyn und das reine Nichts sind dasselbe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A2","text":"Die Wahrheit ist nicht das reine Seyn allein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A3","text":"Die Wahrheit ist nicht das reine Nichts allein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A4","text":"Die Wahrheit besteht im Übergegangensein des Seyns in das Nichts und des Nichts in das Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A5","text":"Die Wahrheit ist nicht die Ununterschiedenheit von Seyn und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A6","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind absolut unterschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A7","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind dennoch ungetrennt und untrennbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A8","text":"Jedes der beiden Momente verschwindet unmittelbar in seinem Gegenteil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A9","text":"Der Unterschied zwischen beiden löst sich unmittelbar auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A10","text":"Die Bewegung des unmittelbaren Verschwindens ist Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX1","text":"Das Wahre ist nicht das isolierte Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX2","text":"Das Wahre ist nicht das isolierte Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX3","text":"Das Wahre ist nicht die bloße Gleichheit oder Ununterschiedenheit beider Momente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX4","text":"Das Verhältnis von Seyn und Nichts ist kein Getrenntsein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX5","text":"Das Übergehen ist kein bloß noch bevorstehender Übergang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX6","text":"Die Unterscheidung ist kein stabil fixierter Unterschied.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX7","text":"Die Wahrheit ist keine der beiden Bestimmungen für sich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D1","text":"Die anfängliche Identität von Seyn und Nichts reicht als Wahrheitsbestimmung nicht aus.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A1","CH_GB18_1EDS:A2","CH_GB18_1EDS:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D2","text":"Seyn und Nichts erhalten ihre Wahrheit nur in einer gegenseitigen Bewegungsrelation.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A4","CH_GB18_1EDS:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D3","text":"Die gegenseitige Bewegungsrelation bewahrt zugleich Differenz und Untrennbarkeit.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A6","CH_GB18_1EDS:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D4","text":"Der Unterschied zwischen Seyn und Nichts ist nur als sich selbst auflösender Unterschied wirksam.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A8","CH_GB18_1EDS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D5","text":"Werden bezeichnet die Einheit einer bereits vollzogenen Übergegangenheit mit der fortbestehenden Bestimmtheit ihrer Momente.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A4","CH_GB18_1EDS:A6","CH_GB18_1EDS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD1","text":"Die Wahrheit wird von einer statischen Bestimmung auf eine relationale Selbstauflösung der Bestimmungen umgestellt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD2","text":"Identität und Differenz bilden keine ausschließenden Alternativen mehr, sondern koexistieren als Momente einer untrennbaren Umschlagsbewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD3","text":"Werden ist nicht die Addition zweier fertiger Bestimmungen, sondern die operative Einheit ihres unmittelbaren Verschwindens ineinander.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD4","text":"Die Bewegung ist zugleich Resultat und Struktur: Das Übergehen ist vollzogen, während seine Momente nur in diesem Übergehen bestimmt bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX1","text":"Die Wahrheit darf nicht als ruhende Identität unabhängig von Bewegung gefasst werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX2","text":"Die Wahrheit darf nicht als äußerliche Beziehung zweier bereits selbständiger Gegensätze gefasst werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX3","text":"Der Unterschied darf nicht als dauerhafte Trennlinie zwischen Seyn und Nichts bestehen bleiben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX4","text":"Die Bewegung darf nicht als einseitiger Übergang nur eines Moments in das andere verstanden werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX5","text":"Das Werden darf nicht auf eine zeitlich nachträgliche Verbindung von Seyn und Nichts reduziert werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX6","text":"Die Einheit darf nicht durch Tilgung der absoluten Differenz gewonnen werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Seinsbegriff, der seine Wahrheit ohne das Nichts besitzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Nichtsbegriff, der als selbständiger Gegenpol außerhalb des Seyns verbleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Ordnung, in der Identität und Differenz nur nacheinander oder äußerlich vermittelt auftreten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX4","text":"Unverfügbar ist eine endgültige Fixierung eines der beiden Momente; jedes Moment besteht nur unter der Bedingung seines Verschwindens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX5","text":"Die terminale Abwesenheit ist eine statische Wahrheit jenseits der Umschlagsbewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS1","text":"Reines Seyn = reines Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS2","text":"Identität wird als unzureichend bestimmt → Wahrheit wird auf das Übergegangensein beider Momente verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS3","text":"Übergegangensein ≠ bloßes Übergehen → die Bewegung ist als vollzogen gesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS4","text":"Vollzogene Bewegung + absolute Differenz → Seyn und Nichts bleiben unterschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS5","text":"Absolute Differenz + Ungetrenntheit → die Momente sind untrennbar aufeinander bezogen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS6","text":"Untrennbare Bezogenheit + unmittelbares Verschwinden → der Unterschied löst sich in jedem Umschlag auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS7","text":"Gegenseitiges unmittelbares Verschwinden → Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AF1","text":"Reines Seyn und reines Nichts als dasselbe → Unzulänglichkeit isolierter Identität → Wahrheit als gegenseitiges Übergegangensein → Differenz ohne Trennung → unmittelbares Verschwinden ineinander → Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME1","text":"Wahrheit wird von einem isolierten Begriff auf die Relation und Bewegung seiner Gegenbestimmungen umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME2","text":"Der Gegensatz von Identität und Differenz wird in eine Einheit aus absoluter Unterschiedenheit und Untrennbarkeit überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME3","text":"Werden wird nicht mehr als nachträglicher Prozess, sondern als Grundform der Einheit von Seyn und Nichts klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME4","text":"Der Unterschied wird als vorübergehende, sich unmittelbar auflösende Struktur sichtbar gemacht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Seyn und Nichts werden als dasselbe und zugleich als absolut unterschieden bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Ihre Wahrheit liegt in der untrennbaren Wechselbewegung, in der jedes Moment in sein Gegenteil verschwindet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Der Text ersetzt die Entscheidung zwischen Identität und Differenz durch eine Bestimmung, die beide als Momente des Werdens integriert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Das Sein des jeweiligen Moments besteht nur in einer bereits vollzogenen, zugleich als Bewegung wirksamen Übergegangenheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um den Übergang von der Identität von Seyn und Nichts zur Bestimmung des Werdens zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wie die vollzogene Übergegangenheit zeitlich oder logisch genau zu verstehen ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern nur kohärent, wenn Bewegung nicht als empirischer Zeitvorgang, sondern als begriffliche Selbstumschlagsstruktur gelesen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Stelle liegt in der gleichzeitigen Fixierung von absoluter Differenz und untrennbarer Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT5","text":"Die zentrale Spannung liegt darin, dass jedes Moment verschwindet, aber dennoch als unterschieden erhalten bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT6","text":"Eine weitere Spannung entsteht zwischen dem vollzogenen Übergegangensein und der fortbestehenden Beschreibung als Bewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die argumentative Bewegung, sofern Werden als Einheit von Resultat, Umschlag und Selbstauflösung angesetzt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T110333168004Z_2302ec17","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"1. Unity of Being and Nothing.","source_sha256":"b0aec1e9a7f203f60111c890dc801dd3a86b3bd029ca745140d98d926ecfdbf9","sha256":"21d2c0f210e7979048d789467e1b57d52b5e7192588d5a44794d87133fa86354","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:03:33.171610+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS1","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing are initially determined as the same.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS2","text":"Their truth is shifted from both isolated determinations to the movement of their reciprocal passing-over.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS3","text":"This passing-over is not a process still pending, but is determined as already accomplished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS4","text":"Truth consists neither in mere identity nor in mere difference, but in absolute difference with inseparable non-separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AS5","text":"Because each moment immediately vanishes into its opposite and the difference likewise immediately dissolves, this movement is determined as Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A1","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing are the same.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A2","text":"Truth is not pure Being alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A3","text":"Truth is not pure Nothing alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A4","text":"Truth consists in the having-passed-over of Being into Nothing and of Nothing into Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A5","text":"Truth is not the indistinguishability of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A6","text":"Being and Nothing are absolutely distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A7","text":"Being and Nothing are nevertheless unseparated and inseparable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A8","text":"Each of the two moments immediately vanishes into its opposite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A9","text":"The difference between the two immediately dissolves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:A10","text":"The movement of immediate vanishing is Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX1","text":"The true is not isolated Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX2","text":"The true is not isolated Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX3","text":"The true is not the mere equality or indistinguishability of both moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX4","text":"The relation of Being and Nothing is not a state of separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX5","text":"The passing-over is not a transition still merely impending.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX6","text":"The distinction is not a stably fixed difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:NX7","text":"Truth is not either of the two determinations taken separately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D1","text":"The initial identity of Being and Nothing does not suffice as a determination of truth.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A1","CH_GB18_1EDS:A2","CH_GB18_1EDS:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D2","text":"Being and Nothing obtain their truth only in a reciprocal relation of movement.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A4","CH_GB18_1EDS:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D3","text":"The reciprocal relation of movement preserves both difference and inseparability.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A6","CH_GB18_1EDS:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D4","text":"The difference between Being and Nothing is effective only as a difference dissolving itself.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A8","CH_GB18_1EDS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:D5","text":"Becoming designates the unity of an already accomplished having-passed-over with the persisting determinacy of its moments.","refs":["CH_GB18_1EDS:A4","CH_GB18_1EDS:A6","CH_GB18_1EDS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD1","text":"Truth is reoriented from a static determination to a relational self-dissolution of determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD2","text":"Identity and difference no longer constitute exclusive alternatives, but coexist as moments of an inseparable movement of reversal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD3","text":"Becoming is not the addition of two finished determinations, but the operative unity of their immediate vanishing into one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SD4","text":"The movement is at once result and structure: the passing-over is accomplished, while its moments remain determined only in this passing-over.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX1","text":"Truth must not be conceived as resting identity independent of movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX2","text":"Truth must not be conceived as an external relation of two opposites already independent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX3","text":"The difference must not remain as a permanent line of separation between Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX4","text":"The movement must not be understood as the one-sided transition of only one moment into the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX5","text":"Becoming must not be reduced to a temporally subsequent connection of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:DNX6","text":"Unity must not be gained through the effacement of absolute difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX1","text":"Excluded is a concept of Being that possesses its truth without Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX2","text":"Excluded is a concept of Nothing that remains as an independent counter-pole outside Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX3","text":"Excluded is an order in which identity and difference occur only successively or are externally mediated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX4","text":"Unavailable is a final fixation of either of the two moments; each moment subsists only under the condition of its vanishing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:SNX5","text":"Terminal absence is a static truth beyond the movement of reversal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS1","text":"Pure Being = pure Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS2","text":"Identity is determined as insufficient → truth is shifted to the having-passed-over of both moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS3","text":"Having-passed-over ≠ mere passing-over → the movement is posited as accomplished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS4","text":"Accomplished movement + absolute difference → Being and Nothing remain distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS5","text":"Absolute difference + non-separation → the moments are inseparably related to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS6","text":"Inseparable relatedness + immediate vanishing → the difference dissolves in every reversal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:FGS7","text":"Reciprocal immediate vanishing → Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:AF1","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing as the same → inadequacy of isolated identity → truth as reciprocal having-passed-over → difference without separation → immediate vanishing into one another → Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME1","text":"Truth is remapped from an isolated concept to the relation and movement of its counter-determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME2","text":"The opposition of identity and difference is transformed into a unity of absolute distinctness and inseparability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME3","text":"Becoming is no longer classified as a subsequent process, but as the basic form of the unity of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ME4","text":"Difference is made visible as a transitory structure that immediately dissolves itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Being and Nothing are determined as the same and at the same time as absolutely distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Their truth lies in the inseparable reciprocal movement in which each moment vanishes into its opposite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text replaces the decision between identity and difference with a determination that integrates both as moments of Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The being of the respective moment consists only in an already accomplished having-passed-over that is at the same time effective as movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the transition from the identity of Being and Nothing to the determination of Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT2","text":"It remains underdetermined how the accomplished having-passed-over is to be understood precisely in temporal or logical terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent only if movement is read not as an empirical temporal process, but as a conceptual structure of self-reversal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT4","text":"The strongest point lies in the simultaneous fixation of absolute difference and inseparable unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT5","text":"The central tension lies in the fact that each moment vanishes, yet nevertheless remains preserved as distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT6","text":"A further tension arises between the accomplished having-passed-over and the persisting description as movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_1EDS:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the argumentative movement, provided that Becoming is posited as the unity of result, reversal, and self-dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_1EDS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_1EDS@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_1EDS:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 10","title":"1. Unity of Being and Nothing.","context":"Chapter 10","original_title":"1. Einheit des Seyns und Nichts."},"original_title":"1. Einheit des Seyns und Nichts.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1","layer":"CH","title":"Remark 1.","order":11,"parents":["RAW_GB18_ANM1"],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM1@R001","sha256":"263c5fddf850b0194874e9703294ef2b76e3687af881be569889a2e7d8953e76","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS1","text":"Die Verwechslung des reinen Seyns und Nichts mit bestimmten Formen von Seyn, Nichtseyn und Inhalt erzeugt den zentralen Einwand gegen ihre Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS2","text":"Reines Seyn und reines Nichts sind als beziehungslose, inhaltslose Abstraktionen zu bestimmen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS3","text":"Die reine Unbestimmtheit des Seyns und die reine Unbestimmtheit des Nichts lassen keinen festhaltbaren Unterschied zwischen beiden zu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS4","text":"Die Wahrheit ihrer abstrakten Unterschiedenheit ist ihre Einheit im Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS5","text":"Bestimmtes Daseyn erzeugt reale Unterschiede nicht durch das abstrakte Seyn oder Nichts, sondern durch seinen Inhalts- und Beziehungszusammenhang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS6","text":"Kants Trennung von Begriff und Existenz gilt für endliche Inhalte, verfehlt aber Gott, dessen Begriff und Seyn untrennbar bestimmt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A1","text":"Ein dem Etwas entgegengesetztes Nichts ist bestimmtes Nichts und nicht reines Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A2","text":"Reines Nichts ist unmittelbare, beziehungslose und inhaltslose Negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A3","text":"Reines Seyn ist unmittelbare, beziehungslose und inhaltslose Allgemeinheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","text":"Reines Seyn und reines Nichts sind in ihrer abstrakten Reinheit ununterscheidbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","text":"Die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts ist Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A6","text":"Werden enthält den Übergang des Nichts in Seyn und des Seyns in Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","text":"Bestimmtes Seyn ist nur als Beziehung eines Inhalts auf andere Inhalte bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A8","text":"Der reale Unterschied von Seyn und Nichts entsteht erst im Daseyn als Unterschied von Etwas und Anderem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A9","text":"Existenz fügt einem isolierten Inhalt keine Inhaltsbestimmung hinzu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","text":"Endliche Dinge sind dadurch bestimmt, daß Begriff und Seyn in ihnen trennbar sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A11","text":"Gott ist dadurch abstrakt bestimmt, daß Begriff und Seyn in ihm untrennbar sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A12","text":"Die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts ist das Element aller weiteren logischen Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX1","text":"Reines Nichts ist nicht das Nichts eines bestimmten Etwas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX2","text":"Reines Nichts ist nicht Nichtseyn, sofern dieses bereits die Beziehung auf Seyn enthält.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX3","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind nicht als zeitlich abwechselnde Zustände eines vorausgesetzten Substrats zu denken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX4","text":"Die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts ist nicht die Gleichgültigkeit gegenüber dem Bestehen oder Nichtbestehen bestimmter Dinge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX5","text":"Das abstrakte Seyn ist nicht die Realität eines bestimmten Inhalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX6","text":"Das abstrakte Nichts ist nicht die Negation eines bestimmten Inhalts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX7","text":"Die Existenz ist nicht ein reales Prädikat, das den Begriff eines endlichen Gegenstands inhaltlich vermehrt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX8","text":"Der ontologische Beweis darf nicht durch Kategorien endlicher Dinge beurteilt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D1","text":"Die Behauptung, Seyn sei nur Seyn und Nichts nur Nichts, fixiert beide Abstraktionen außerhalb ihres Übergangs und hebt damit das Werden auf.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D2","text":"Der Satz „Aus Nichts wird Nichts“ ist entweder tautologisch oder schließt jedes wirkliche Werden aus.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A2","CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D3","text":"Jede Berufung auf konkrete Gegenstände gegen die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts setzt bereits Daseyn voraus und verfehlt daher die Ebene reiner Abstraktion.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A1","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D4","text":"Positives und Negatives sind nicht ursprüngliche Gegensätze, sondern reflektierte Formen des Seyns und Nichts.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A3","CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","CH_GB18_ANM1:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D5","text":"Die Nichtgleichgültigkeit des Daseyns bestimmter Dinge beruht auf ihren Beziehungen zu anderem Inhalt und nicht auf dem bloßen Unterschied von Seyn und Nichts.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8","CH_GB18_ANM1:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D6","text":"Kants These, daß hundert wirkliche Thaler keinen anderen Inhalt als hundert mögliche Thaler besitzen, trifft den isolierten Inhalt, nicht aber dessen Stellung im Vermögenszustand und Erfahrungszusammenhang.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8","CH_GB18_ANM1:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D7","text":"Der isolierte Begriff eines endlichen Gegenstands verfälscht dessen Natur, weil endlicher Inhalt nicht selbstbezüglich, sondern veränderlich und vergänglich ist.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D8","text":"Die Kantische Kritik des ontologischen Beweises bleibt für endliche Gegenstände gültig, kann aber nicht ohne Kategorienfehler auf Gott übertragen werden.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","CH_GB18_ANM1:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD1","text":"Das System verlegt den Ursprung realer Differenz aus der isolierten Opposition von Seyn und Nichts in die vermittelnde Struktur des Daseyns.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD2","text":"Alle endlichen Bestimmungen erscheinen als instabile Einheiten von Positivität und Negativität und damit als Formen des Werdens.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A6","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","CH_GB18_ANM1:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD3","text":"Der Übergang von reiner Logik zu Metaphysik wird durch die Trennung zwischen endlicher Trennbarkeit und göttlicher Untrennbarkeit von Begriff und Seyn organisiert.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A9","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","CH_GB18_ANM1:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD4","text":"Die Kritik des gemeinen Verstandes beruht darauf, daß dieser die Bedingungen konkreter Erfahrung in die Analyse reiner Kategorien einschleust.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A1","CH_GB18_ANM1:A2","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD5","text":"Die Erhebung über endliche Verluste wird als praktische Entsprechung der theoretischen Abstraktion vom bestimmten Daseyn bestimmt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A3","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX1","text":"Das System schließt aus, daß konkrete Erfahrung den Maßstab für die Wahrheit reiner logischer Bestimmungen bilden kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX2","text":"Das System schließt aus, daß Negation ursprünglich bloß privativ, mangelhaft oder an einen vorgegebenen Inhalt gebunden ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX3","text":"Das System schließt aus, daß Identität die Fixierung eines unveränderlichen Selbstverhältnisses bedeutet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX4","text":"Das System schließt aus, daß Endlichkeit und Göttlichkeit unter denselben Modalitäten von Begriff, Realität und Existenz stehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SNX1","text":"Unzulässig ist eine letzte Realität, in der Seyn ohne Negation oder Negation ohne Seyn bestehen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SNX2","text":"Unzulässig ist ein absoluter Ursprung, der als bloßes Seyn, bloßes Nichts oder bloßes fertiges Etwas gedacht wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SNX3","text":"Unzulässig ist eine Gottesbestimmung, die göttliches Seyn als äußerlich hinzutretende Existenz behandelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS1","text":"Bestimmtes Etwas und bestimmtes Nichts werden von reinem Seyn und reinem Nichts abgetrennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS2","text":"Reines Seyn und reines Nichts werden von Inhalt, Beziehung und zeitlichem Substrat entleert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS3","text":"Die Entleerung hebt den behaupteten festen Unterschied zwischen Seyn und Nichts auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS4","text":"Die aufgehobene Trennung erscheint als Einheit des Übergangs und wird Werden genannt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS5","text":"Konkrete Unterschiede werden dem Daseyn, seinem Inhalt und seinen Relationen zugeordnet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS6","text":"Die Unterscheidung zwischen endlichem und göttlichem Seyn entscheidet über die Geltungsgrenze der Kantischen Existenzkritik.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF1","text":"Bestimmtes Nichts **→** Abstraktion von jedem Etwas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF2","text":"Abstraktion von Inhalt und Beziehung **→** reines Nichts und reines Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF3","text":"Reine Unbestimmtheit **→** Ununterscheidbarkeit von Seyn und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF4","text":"Ununterscheidbarkeit **→** Werden als ihre Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF5","text":"Werden **→** Daseyn als bestimmter Unterschied von Etwas und Anderem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF6","text":"Daseyn und Inhaltsbeziehung **→** Zurückweisung konkreter Einwände gegen die abstrakte Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF7","text":"Endlichkeit als Trennbarkeit von Begriff und Seyn **→** Begrenzung der Kantischen Kritik und Ausnahme Gottes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME1","text":"Der Gegensatz von Seyn und Nichts wird von einer statischen Opposition in eine Übergangsstruktur umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME2","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen abstrakter Logik und konkreter Wirklichkeit wird durch die Ebene des Daseyns vermittelt, statt unmittelbar behandelt zu werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME3","text":"Existenz wird vom Inhaltsmerkmal eines Gegenstands zur relationalen Stellung eines bestimmten Daseyns im Erfahrungszusammenhang verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME4","text":"Der Unterschied zwischen möglichen und wirklichen Gegenständen wird als Unterschied ihrer Einbindung in weitere Bestimmungszusammenhänge lesbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME5","text":"Gott und endliche Dinge werden nicht nach demselben Existenzschema klassifiziert, sondern durch gegensätzliche Verhältnisse von Begriff und Seyn getrennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der Text behandelt die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts sowie den Einwand, konkrete Dinge seien nicht gleichgültig gegenüber ihrem Bestehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT2","text":"Structural — Der Text unterscheidet reine Abstraktion, bestimmtes Daseyn, Inhalt und Vermittlungszusammenhang als verschiedene logische Ebenen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Der Text neutralisiert Einwände durch den Nachweis eines Ebenenwechsels, in dem reine Kategorien unbemerkt zu Bestimmungen konkreter Gegenstände gemacht werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Wirklichkeit wird als Werden bestimmt; Endlichkeit ist trennbare Vermittlung von Begriff und Seyn, Gott dagegen ihre untrennbare Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um den Übergang von reinem Seyn und Nichts zum Werden sowie die Zurückweisung konkreter Gegeneinwände zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, weshalb reine Unbestimmtheit nicht nur Gleichheit, sondern notwendig Übergang und Werden erzeugt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT3","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bleibt intern kohärent, sofern reine Abstraktion, Daseyn und endlicher Inhalt strikt auseinandergehalten werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Operation des Systems ist die Diagnose, daß die meisten Einwände gegen die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts einen unzulässigen Wechsel von Abstraktion zu bestimmtem Daseyn vollziehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT5","text":"Die Struktur hängt an der nicht weiter begründeten Behauptung, daß Seyn und Nichts in ihrer Reinheit nicht unterscheidbar sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT6","text":"Eine Spannung entsteht daraus, daß Seyn und Nichts zugleich als getrennte reine Abstraktionen exponiert und als in ihrer Wahrheit ungetrennt bestimmt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT7","text":"Eine weitere Spannung entsteht zwischen der allgemeinen Behauptung, alles Wirkliche enthalte Seyn und Nichts, und der Ausnahme Gottes als untrennbarer Einheit von Begriff und Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT8","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die Bewegung des Textes, wenn die Sequenz Abstraktion, Identitätskritik, Werden, Daseyn, Endlichkeit und Gottesbestimmung erhalten bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T110949360725Z_0ae52f49","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Note 1.","source_sha256":"263c5fddf850b0194874e9703294ef2b76e3687af881be569889a2e7d8953e76","sha256":"9d5f59f1f5b8c209ea6667ed287ed311c68076ffeecdccdb9d6e84dceb353077","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:09:49.363068+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS1","text":"The confusion of pure Being and Nothing with determinate forms of Being, non-being, and content produces the central objection to their unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS2","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing are to be determined as relationless, contentless abstractions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS3","text":"The pure indeterminacy of Being and the pure indeterminacy of Nothing permit no difference between the two that can be maintained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS4","text":"The truth of their abstract distinctness is their unity in Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS5","text":"Determinate being generates real differences not through abstract Being or Nothing, but through its context of content and relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AS6","text":"Kant's separation of Concept and existence applies to finite contents, but misses God, whose Concept and Being are determined as inseparable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A1","text":"A Nothing opposed to Something is determinate Nothing and not pure Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A2","text":"Pure Nothing is immediate, relationless, and contentless negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A3","text":"Pure Being is immediate, relationless, and contentless universality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing are indistinguishable in their abstract purity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","text":"The unity of Being and Nothing is Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A6","text":"Becoming contains the transition of Nothing into Being and of Being into Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","text":"Determinate Being is determined only as the relation of one content to other contents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A8","text":"The real difference of Being and Nothing arises only in determinate being as the difference between Something and Other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A9","text":"Existence adds no determination of content to an isolated content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","text":"Finite things are determined by the fact that Concept and Being are separable in them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A11","text":"God is abstractly determined by the fact that Concept and Being are inseparable in him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:A12","text":"The unity of Being and Nothing is the element of all further logical determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX1","text":"Pure Nothing is not the Nothing of a determinate Something.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX2","text":"Pure Nothing is not non-being, insofar as this already contains the relation to Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX3","text":"Being and Nothing are not to be thought as temporally alternating states of a presupposed substrate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX4","text":"The unity of Being and Nothing is not indifference toward the existence or non-existence of determinate things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX5","text":"Abstract Being is not the reality of a determinate content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX6","text":"Abstract Nothing is not the negation of a determinate content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX7","text":"Existence is not a real predicate that increases the Concept of a finite object in respect of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:NX8","text":"The ontological proof must not be judged through the categories of finite things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D1","text":"The assertion that Being is only Being and Nothing only Nothing fixes both abstractions outside their transition and thereby abolishes Becoming.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D2","text":"The proposition “Out of Nothing comes Nothing” is either tautological or excludes every actual Becoming.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A2","CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D3","text":"Every appeal to concrete objects against the unity of Being and Nothing already presupposes determinate being and therefore misses the level of pure abstraction.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A1","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D4","text":"Positive and negative are not original opposites, but reflected forms of Being and Nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A3","CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","CH_GB18_ANM1:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D5","text":"The non-indifference of the determinate being of determinate things rests on their relations to other content and not on the mere difference of Being and Nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8","CH_GB18_ANM1:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D6","text":"Kant's thesis that one hundred actual thalers possess no content other than one hundred possible thalers applies to isolated content, but not to its position in the state of assets and context of experience.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8","CH_GB18_ANM1:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D7","text":"The isolated Concept of a finite object falsifies its nature, because finite content is not self-relating, but mutable and perishable.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:D8","text":"The Kantian critique of the ontological proof remains valid for finite objects, but cannot be transferred to God without a category mistake.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","CH_GB18_ANM1:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD1","text":"The system relocates the origin of real difference from the isolated opposition of Being and Nothing into the mediating structure of determinate being.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A4","CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD2","text":"All finite determinations appear as unstable unities of positivity and negativity and thus as forms of Becoming.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A5","CH_GB18_ANM1:A6","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","CH_GB18_ANM1:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD3","text":"The transition from pure logic to metaphysics is organized through the distinction between finite separability and divine inseparability of Concept and Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A9","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10","CH_GB18_ANM1:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD4","text":"The critique of common understanding rests on its smuggling the conditions of concrete experience into the analysis of pure categories.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A1","CH_GB18_ANM1:A2","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SD5","text":"Elevation above finite losses is determined as the practical counterpart of theoretical abstraction from determinate being.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM1:A3","CH_GB18_ANM1:A7","CH_GB18_ANM1:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that concrete experience can constitute the standard for the truth of pure logical determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that negation is originally merely privative, defective, or bound to a given content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the possibility that identity means the fixation of an unchangeable self-relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that finitude and divinity stand under the same modalities of Concept, reality, and existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SNX1","text":"Impermissible is an ultimate reality in which Being without negation or negation without Being could subsist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SNX2","text":"Impermissible is an absolute origin thought as mere Being, mere Nothing, or mere finished Something.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:SNX3","text":"Impermissible is a determination of God that treats divine Being as externally added existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS1","text":"Determinate Something and determinate Nothing are separated from pure Being and pure Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS2","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing are emptied of content, relation, and temporal substrate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS3","text":"The emptying abolishes the asserted fixed difference between Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS4","text":"The abolished separation appears as the unity of transition and is called Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS5","text":"Concrete differences are assigned to determinate being, its content, and its relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:FGS6","text":"The distinction between finite and divine Being decides the limit of validity of the Kantian critique of existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF1","text":"Determinate Nothing **→** abstraction from every Something.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF2","text":"Abstraction from content and relation **→** pure Nothing and pure Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF3","text":"Pure indeterminacy **→** indistinguishability of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF4","text":"Indistinguishability **→** Becoming as their truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF5","text":"Becoming **→** determinate being as the determinate difference between Something and Other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF6","text":"Determinate being and relation of content **→** rejection of concrete objections to abstract unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:AF7","text":"Finitude as separability of Concept and Being **→** limitation of the Kantian critique and exception of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME1","text":"The opposition of Being and Nothing is reclassified from a static opposition into a structure of transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME2","text":"The opposition between abstract logic and concrete actuality is mediated through the level of determinate being, rather than treated immediately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME3","text":"Existence is shifted from being a feature of an object's content to being the relational position of a determinate being in the context of experience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME4","text":"The difference between possible and actual objects becomes legible as a difference in their integration into further contexts of determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ME5","text":"God and finite things are not classified according to the same schema of existence, but separated by opposed relations of Concept and Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text treats the unity of Being and Nothing, as well as the objection that concrete things are not indifferent to their existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT2","text":"Structural — The text distinguishes pure abstraction, determinate being, content, and the context of mediation as different logical levels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text neutralizes objections by demonstrating a change of level in which pure categories are imperceptibly made into determinations of concrete objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Actuality is determined as Becoming; finitude is the separable mediation of Concept and Being, whereas God is their inseparable unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the transition from pure Being and Nothing to Becoming, as well as the rejection of concrete counter-objections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT2","text":"It remains underdetermined why pure indeterminacy produces not merely equality, but necessarily transition and Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT3","text":"The reconstruction remains internally coherent provided that pure abstraction, determinate being, and finite content are strictly kept apart.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT4","text":"The system's strongest operation is the diagnosis that most objections to the unity of Being and Nothing carry out an impermissible shift from abstraction to determinate being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT5","text":"The structure depends on the further ungrounded assertion that Being and Nothing are not distinguishable in their purity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT6","text":"A tension arises from the fact that Being and Nothing are at once expounded as separate pure abstractions and determined as undivided in their truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0011","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT7","text":"A further tension arises between the general assertion that all actuality contains Being and Nothing and the exception of God as the inseparable unity of Concept and Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0009","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM1:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if the sequence of abstraction, critique of identity, Becoming, determinate being, finitude, and determination of God is retained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM1:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM1@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_ANM1:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 11","title":"Remark 1.","context":"Chapter 11","original_title":"Anmerkung 1."},"original_title":"Anmerkung 1.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2","layer":"CH","title":"Remark 2.","order":12,"parents":["RAW_GB18_ANM2"],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM2@R001","sha256":"e13c381b3691e9fe68a16c0358e7d09082005823e6e20c37c4a89ac17ba2f99f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS1","text":"Der Satz „Seyn und Nichts ist eins und dasselbe“ verfehlt seinen spekulativen Inhalt, weil seine Urteilsform die im Satz zugleich gesetzte Differenz verdeckt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS2","text":"Die Identitätsbehauptung enthält Sein und Nichts als unterschiedene Bestimmungen und widerspricht daher ihrer eigenen Prädikationsform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS3","text":"Der Selbstwiderspruch des Satzes ist nicht sein Scheitern, sondern seine immanente Auflösung zur Bewegung des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS4","text":"Die Ergänzung durch den entgegengesetzten Satz erzeugt nur eine Antinomie, sofern die Einheit beider Sätze nicht als Bewegung begriffen wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS5","text":"Der Unterschied von reinem Sein und reinem Nichts kann nicht in ihnen selbst angegeben werden, weil jede angebbare Bestimmung sie zu bestimmtem Sein und bestimmtem Nichts machte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS6","text":"Werden ist die allein angemessene Gestalt, in der Sein und Nichts zugleich unterschieden, untrennbar und nicht selbständig bestehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","text":"Reines Sein ist unmittelbar und unbestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","text":"Reines Nichts ist ebenso unbestimmt wie reines Sein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","text":"Reines Sein und reines Nichts besitzen keine immanente Bestimmtheit, durch welche ihr Unterschied aussprechbar wäre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A4","text":"Ein Unterschied, der beiden reinen Bestimmungen immanent zukäme, würde sie zu bestimmten Bestimmungen machen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","text":"Das Urteil drückt eine Identitätsbeziehung von Subjekt und Prädikat aus und unterschlägt deren wesentliche Nichtidentität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","text":"Spekulativer Inhalt enthält die Nichtidentität seiner Bestimmungen als wesentliches Moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","text":"Die Gleichsetzung von Sein und Nichts enthält beide Bestimmungen zugleich als unterschiedene und widerspricht daher ihrer eigenen Aussageform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","text":"Die immanente Auflösung des Widerspruchs von Sein und Nichts ist Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A9","text":"Sein und Nichts bestehen nicht für sich, sondern nur in ihrem Übergang und Bestehen im Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A10","text":"Bestimmtheit entsteht nur dort, wo Licht und Finsternis, analog Sein und Nichts, wechselseitig bestimmt sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX1","text":"Sein und Nichts sind nicht als unterschiedslose Einheit zu verstehen, in der ihre Differenz ausgelöscht wäre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX2","text":"Die spekulative Einheit ist nicht durch Abstraktion von Sein und Nichts zu gewinnen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX3","text":"Ein einzelner Identitätssatz ist nicht geeignet, spekulative Wahrheit vollständig auszudrücken.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX4","text":"Die bloße Gegenüberstellung der Sätze „dasselbe“ und „nicht dasselbe“ ist keine Darstellung ihrer Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX5","text":"Einheit ist nicht als äußerliches Resultat einer vergleichenden subjektiven Reflexion zu verstehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX6","text":"Der Unterschied von reinem Sein und reinem Nichts besteht nicht als positive Bestimmtheit an ihnen selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX7","text":"Sinnliche Bilder von reinem Licht und reiner Finsternis begründen keinen Unterschied, solange beide als reine Leeren gefasst werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D1","text":"Die Urteilsform produziert beim spekulativen Inhalt notwendig den Anschein eines Widerspruchs, weil sie Identität aussagt und Nichtidentität nicht darstellen kann.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D2","text":"Die Herauslösung nur eines Satzes aus einer spekulativen Bestimmung verfälscht deren Inhalt durch einseitige Fixierung.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D3","text":"Der Unterschied von Sein und Nichts ist nur als Moment ihres Übergangs, nicht als selbständige Eigenschaft eines der beiden Pole, artikulierbar.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","CH_GB18_ANM2:A4","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D4","text":"Werden ist keine statische Einheit, sondern die Einheit, die ihren Unterschied setzt, aufhebt und dadurch trägt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D5","text":"Bestimmtes Sein oder Daseyn setzt wechselseitige Bestimmung voraus und kann nicht aus isolierter Reinheit entstehen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","CH_GB18_ANM2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD1","text":"Spekulative Wahrheit ist strukturell unabschließbar in einer einzelnen prädikativen Aussage, weil ihr Inhalt die Form ihrer Aussage überschreitet.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD2","text":"Die Grundbestimmungen Sein und Nichts werden von selbständigen Entitäten zu unselbständigen Momenten einer vermittelnden Bewegung umklassifiziert.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD3","text":"Wissenschaftliche Geltung von Aussagen über Sein und Nichts hängt von ihrer Definitionsfähigkeit ab; bloße Versicherung ersetzt keine Bestimmung.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","CH_GB18_ANM2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD4","text":"Die Möglichkeit von Unterscheidung entsteht erst innerhalb bestimmter Vermittlung und nicht vor oder außerhalb derselben.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A4","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9","CH_GB18_ANM2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein selbständiges, unmittelbar bestimmbares Sein, das vor jeder Vermittlung feststünde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Unterschied, der vor dem Werden besteht und dessen Bewegung lediglich nachträglich erklären würde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Erkenntnisform, in der äußere Vergleichung die Wahrheit ihrer Gegenstände erzeugen oder erschöpfen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Annahme, dass sinnliche Anschaulichkeit den reinen logischen Bestimmungen einen positiven Inhalt verschafft.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SNX1","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein ruhender ontologischer Anfang, der sich ohne Übergang, Negation und Vermittlung als Grund ausweisen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SNX2","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist eine endgültige sprachliche Formel, die spekulative Bewegung ausdrückt, ohne ihren Überschuss über die Urteilsform zu verlieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SNX3","text":"Nicht zulässig ist eine Differenz, die als festes Eigentum isolierter Pole bestehen bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS1","text":"Reine Unbestimmtheit von Sein und Nichts → keine immanente positive Differenz → Unmöglichkeit ihrer isolierten Definition.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","CH_GB18_ANM2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS2","text":"Urteilsförmige Identität von Sein und Nichts → zugleich gesetzte Differenz → Selbstwiderspruch der Aussageform.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS3","text":"Selbstwiderspruch → immanentes Verschwinden des Satzes → Werden als wirklicher Inhalt des Satzes.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS4","text":"Werden als Einheit des Unterschieds → Nichtselbständigkeit von Sein und Nichts → bestimmte Vermittlung als Bedingung von Daseyn.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9","CH_GB18_ANM2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AF1","text":"Unzulänglichkeit des Identitätssatzes → Sichtbarwerden seiner verdrängten Differenz → Selbstwiderspruch → Werden als immanentes Resultat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AF2","text":"Kritik der Urteilsform → Zurückweisung einseitiger Antinomie → Verwerfung äußerlicher Einheit → Bestimmung des Werdens als untrennbare Bewegungsrelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AF3","text":"Unmöglichkeit der Definition reiner Differenz → Ausschluss sinnlicher Ersatzbilder → wechselseitige Bestimmung → Daseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME1","text":"Identität und Differenz werden nicht als ausschließende Alternativen kartiert, sondern als zugleich notwendige Momente einer Bewegung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME2","text":"Sein und Nichts erscheinen nicht mehr als Grundgegenstände, sondern als unselbständige Grenzmomente des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME3","text":"Der Gegensatz von Einheit und Vielheit wird umgeordnet: Äußerliche Einheit wird disqualifiziert, Untrennbarkeit wird als negative Bedingung der Bewegung bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME4","text":"Sinnliche Oppositionen werden von Beweisen reiner Differenz zu Analogien bestimmter, wechselseitig vermittelter Verhältnisse umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der Text bestimmt das Verhältnis von Sein, Nichts und Werden sowie die Unzulänglichkeit ihrer urteilsmäßigen Formulierung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT2","text":"Structural — Die Urteilsform erzeugt systematisch Einseitigkeit, weil sie spekulative Nichtidentität nicht explizit artikulieren kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Spekulatives Denken wird als Verfahren bestimmt, das isolierte Sätze in ihre notwendige Gegenbewegung und deren immanente Vermittlung zurückführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Unmittelbarkeit besitzt keinen stabilen Vorrang; Sein und Nichts sind nur als verschwindende Momente eines Übergangs wirklich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Transformation von Sein und Nichts in Werden sowie die Kritik der Urteilsform zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wie die externe Reflexion, welche das Werden im Satz erkennt, zu dessen behaupteter Immanenz steht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist kohärent, sofern Widerspruch als Selbstbewegung und nicht als bloßer logischer Defekt behandelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT4","text":"Die stärkste Operation liegt in der Ableitung der Nichtselbständigkeit beider reinen Bestimmungen aus der Unmöglichkeit ihres ausdrückbaren Unterschieds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT5","text":"Die Hauptbruchlinie liegt darin, dass der Unterschied als subjektives Meinen ausgeschlossen wird, während das Werden dennoch unterscheidbare Momente voraussetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT6","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die Argumentbewegung nur, wenn Werden weder als dritte ruhende Bestimmung noch als bloße Synthese zweier vorgegebener Entitäten gelesen wird.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T111008492450Z_0247bb1a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Note 2.","source_sha256":"e13c381b3691e9fe68a16c0358e7d09082005823e6e20c37c4a89ac17ba2f99f","sha256":"ed77bbaa1bb45701a7e4f2d0358b2f0b8866eb2619bae53662b3ac4823665279","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:10:08.499266+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS1","text":"The proposition “Being and Nothing are one and the same” misses its speculative content because its judgment-form conceals the difference posited in the proposition at the same time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS2","text":"The assertion of identity contains Being and Nothing as distinct determinations and therefore contradicts its own predicative form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS3","text":"The self-contradiction of the proposition is not its failure, but its immanent dissolution into the movement of Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS4","text":"The supplementation by the opposite proposition produces only an antinomy, insofar as the unity of both propositions is not comprehended as movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS5","text":"The difference between pure Being and pure Nothing cannot be specified in themselves, because every specifiable determination would make them determinate Being and determinate Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AS6","text":"Becoming is the sole adequate form in which Being and Nothing simultaneously subsist as distinct, inseparable, and not self-subsistent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","text":"Pure Being is immediate and indeterminate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","text":"Pure Nothing is as indeterminate as pure Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing possess no immanent determinacy through which their difference could be expressed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A4","text":"A difference that belonged immanently to both pure determinations would make them determinate determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","text":"The judgment expresses a relation of identity between subject and predicate and suppresses their essential non-identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","text":"Speculative content contains the non-identity of its determinations as an essential moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","text":"The equation of Being and Nothing contains both determinations simultaneously as distinct and therefore contradicts its own form of assertion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","text":"The immanent dissolution of the contradiction between Being and Nothing is Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A9","text":"Being and Nothing do not subsist for themselves, but only in their transition and subsistence in Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:A10","text":"Determinacy arises only where light and darkness, analogously to Being and Nothing, are reciprocally determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX1","text":"Being and Nothing are not to be understood as an undifferentiated unity in which their difference would be effaced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX2","text":"Speculative unity is not to be attained through abstraction from Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX3","text":"A single proposition of identity is not suited to express speculative truth completely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX4","text":"The mere juxtaposition of the propositions “the same” and “not the same” is not a presentation of their unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX5","text":"Unity is not to be understood as the external result of a comparative subjective reflection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX6","text":"The difference between pure Being and pure Nothing does not exist as a positive determinacy in themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:NX7","text":"Sensuous images of pure light and pure darkness do not ground a difference so long as both are grasped as pure emptinesses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D1","text":"In speculative content, the judgment-form necessarily produces the appearance of a contradiction, because it asserts identity and cannot present non-identity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D2","text":"The extraction of only one proposition from a speculative determination falsifies its content through one-sided fixation.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D3","text":"The difference between Being and Nothing can be articulated only as a moment of their transition, not as an independent property of either pole.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","CH_GB18_ANM2:A4","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D4","text":"Becoming is not a static unity, but the unity that posits, sublates, and thereby sustains its difference.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:D5","text":"Determinate Being, or Daseyn, presupposes reciprocal determination and cannot arise from isolated purity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","CH_GB18_ANM2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD1","text":"Speculative truth is structurally incapable of closure in a single predicative statement, because its content exceeds the form of its statement.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD2","text":"The fundamental determinations Being and Nothing are reclassified from self-subsistent entities into non-self-subsistent moments of a mediating movement.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD3","text":"The scientific validity of statements about Being and Nothing depends on their capacity for definition; mere assurance does not replace determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","CH_GB18_ANM2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SD4","text":"The possibility of distinction first arises within determinate mediation, and not before or outside it.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A4","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9","CH_GB18_ANM2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX1","text":"Excluded is a self-subsistent, immediately determinable Being that would stand fixed prior to all mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX2","text":"Excluded is a difference that exists prior to Becoming and would merely explain its movement retrospectively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX3","text":"Excluded is a form of cognition in which external comparison could produce or exhaust the truth of its objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:DNX4","text":"Excluded is the assumption that sensuous intuitiveness provides the pure logical determinations with a positive content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SNX1","text":"Unavailable is a resting ontological beginning that could establish itself as ground without transition, negation, and mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SNX2","text":"Unavailable is a final linguistic formula that expresses speculative movement without losing its excess over the judgment-form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:SNX3","text":"Not admissible is a difference that remains as a fixed property of isolated poles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS1","text":"Pure indeterminacy of Being and Nothing → no immanent positive difference → impossibility of their isolated definition.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A1","CH_GB18_ANM2:A2","CH_GB18_ANM2:A3","CH_GB18_ANM2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS2","text":"Judgment-form identity of Being and Nothing → difference simultaneously posited → self-contradiction of the form of statement.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A5","CH_GB18_ANM2:A6","CH_GB18_ANM2:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS3","text":"Self-contradiction → immanent vanishing of the proposition → Becoming as the actual content of the proposition.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:FGS4","text":"Becoming as unity of difference → non-self-subsistence of Being and Nothing → determinate mediation as condition of Daseyn.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9","CH_GB18_ANM2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AF1","text":"Inadequacy of the proposition of identity → becoming visible of its repressed difference → self-contradiction → Becoming as immanent result.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AF2","text":"Critique of the judgment-form → rejection of one-sided antinomy → rejection of external unity → determination of Becoming as inseparable relation of movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:AF3","text":"Impossibility of defining pure difference → exclusion of sensuous substitute-images → reciprocal determination → Daseyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME1","text":"Identity and difference are not mapped as mutually exclusive alternatives, but as simultaneously necessary moments of a movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME2","text":"Being and Nothing no longer appear as fundamental objects, but as non-self-subsistent boundary moments of Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME3","text":"The opposition between unity and multiplicity is reordered: external unity is disqualified, and inseparability is determined as the negative condition of movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ME4","text":"Sensuous oppositions are reclassified from proofs of pure difference into analogies of determinate, reciprocally mediated relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text determines the relation of Being, Nothing, and Becoming, as well as the inadequacy of their judgmental formulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT2","text":"Structural — The judgment-form systematically produces one-sidedness because it cannot explicitly articulate speculative non-identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Speculative thinking is determined as a procedure that returns isolated propositions to their necessary counter-movement and its immanent mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Immediacy possesses no stable priority; Being and Nothing are actual only as vanishing moments of a transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the transformation of Being and Nothing into Becoming, as well as the critique of the judgment-form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT2","text":"It remains underdetermined how the external reflection that recognizes Becoming in the proposition relates to its asserted immanence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT3","text":"The structure is coherent insofar as contradiction is treated as self-movement and not as a mere logical defect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT4","text":"The strongest operation lies in deriving the non-self-subsistence of both pure determinations from the impossibility of their expressible difference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT5","text":"The principal fault line lies in the fact that difference is excluded as subjective opinion, while Becoming nevertheless presupposes distinguishable moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0009","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM2:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the argument only if Becoming is read neither as a third resting determination nor as the mere synthesis of two pre-given entities.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM2:A7","CH_GB18_ANM2:A8","CH_GB18_ANM2:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM2:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM2@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_ANM2:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 12","title":"Remark 2.","context":"Chapter 12","original_title":"Anmerkung 2."},"original_title":"Anmerkung 2.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3","layer":"CH","title":"Remark 3.","order":13,"parents":["RAW_GB18_ANM3"],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM3@R001","sha256":"9739124cb81fd58d73e14c09fb5f2d5c9ccf00ee1312e78081348ad21110bc4d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS1","text":"Die zu lösende Schwierigkeit ist die Behauptung, Seyn und Nichts könnten als isolierte Erste bestehen, während ihr Übergehen negiert wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS2","text":"Der Text setzt dem die These entgegen, daß Werden die Wahrheit beider Momente als ihre untrennbare, von ihnen unterschiedene Einheit ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS3","text":"Die Beweisform ist eine immanente Dialektik gegen die äußere Reflexion, welche deren Festsetzungen durch das in ihnen selbst hervortretende Andere aufhebt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS4","text":"Die Bewegung führt von der empirischen Widerlegung leerer Abstraktionen zur begrifflichen Bestimmung der Unbestimmtheit als abstrakter Negativität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS5","text":"Das Resultat bestimmt den Übergang von Seyn und Nichts als unmittelbares Umschlagen, das weder durch Grund, Ursache, Bedingung noch ein äußeres Verhältnis vermittelt werden darf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","text":"Reines Seyn und reines Nichts bestehen nicht für sich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","text":"Werden ist die Wahrheit von Seyn und Nichts als eine von beiden Momenten unterschiedene Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","text":"Die Trennung von Seyn und Nichts ist ein Produkt der Abstraktion und reflexiven Fixierung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","text":"Ein schlechthin unbestimmter Anfang enthält keinen immanenten Fortgang zu einem Anderen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A5","text":"Wahre Synthesis ist die immanente Einheit des Unterschiedenen und nicht die Verknüpfung äußerlich vorgegebener Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","text":"Unbestimmtheit ist als Gegensatz zur Bestimmtheit selbst bestimmte abstrakte Negativität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A7","text":"Ein bestimmtes negatives Nichts ist affirmativ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A8","text":"Die empirische Nichtigkeit leerer Abstraktionen ersetzt nicht den immanenten Nachweis, daß der abstrakte Gedanke sein Gegenteil in sich enthält.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","text":"Die Forderung nach einem kategorial bestimmten Wie des Übergangs setzt die festen Kategorien voraus, die sie zur Erklärung verwenden will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A10","text":"Der Übergang von Seyn und Nichts ist unmittelbar und noch kein Verhältnis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A11","text":"Das gedachte, vorgestellte oder ausgesprochene Nichts steht bereits in Beziehung auf Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX1","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind keine selbständigen Gegenstände, die außerhalb ihres Werdens bestehen könnten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX2","text":"Werden ist keine äußere Bewegung zwischen zwei ruhenden und zuvor fertigen Polen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX3","text":"Ein absoluter Anfang darf weder durch äußeren Zusatz fortgesetzt noch als zweiter Anfang verdoppelt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX4","text":"Synthesis ist nicht die nachträgliche Verbindung bereits vorhandener Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX5","text":"Reiner Raum, reine Zeit und reines Bewußtseyn besitzen keine empirische Selbstständigkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX6","text":"Das reflektierende Wie liefert keine zulässige Erklärung des anfänglichen Übergangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX7","text":"Grund, Ursache und Bedingung können nicht als Vermittlungen von reinem Seyn und reinem Nichts angesetzt werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX8","text":"Bestimmte Negativität ist keine ontologisch mindere, bloß subjektive oder unwirksame Abwesenheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX9","text":"Die Widerlegung des abstrakten Standpunkts besteht nicht in der vollständigen Verfolgung jedes Einwands der Reflexion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D1","text":"Reines Seyn schlägt in Nichts um, weil seine Unbestimmtheit als abstrakte Negativität bestimmt ist.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D2","text":"Reines Nichts kann nicht als beziehungslose Abwesenheit festgehalten werden, weil sein Gedachtwerden bereits Seyn und Einheit mit Seyn enthält.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D3","text":"Werden ist nicht eine spätere Verknüpfung von Seyn und Nichts, sondern die immanente Wahrheit ihrer Nichtselbständigkeit.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D4","text":"Das Festhalten eines reinen Ersten erzeugt entweder Stillstand oder den Widerspruch eines äußerlich hinzugefügten zweiten Anfangs.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D5","text":"Die behandelten Modelle Parmenides’, Spinozas, Fichtes und Jacobis erscheinen als Varianten derselben reflexiven Fixierung, die Unterschied ausschließt und dennoch Fortgang beansprucht.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D6","text":"Die Berufung auf unmittelbar vorhandenes Seyn widerlegt sich, weil sie nur bestimmtes Daseyn mit Schranke und Negation aufzeigen kann.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D7","text":"Bestimmte Negationen wie Finsterniß und Kälte sind positive Wirklichkeiten ihrer jeweiligen Bestimmtheit und keine bloßen Leerstellen des Positiven.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D8","text":"Das äußerliche Spiel des Abstrahirens, das beliebig von Seyn zu Nichts und zurück wechselt, besitzt keinen Vorrang der Wahrheit.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D9","text":"Der anfängliche Übergang bleibt im reinen Beginn verborgen und wird erst in späteren konkreteren Bestimmungen als Vermittlung ausdrücklich gesetzt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD1","text":"Ein absoluter Anfang kann nur entweder abstrakt fortgangslos oder als Selbstbewegung verstanden werden; ein zugleich isolierter und produktiver Ursprung ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD2","text":"Die Geltung der Dialektik beruht nicht auf einer äußeren Widerlegung gegnerischer Aussagen, sondern auf dem Nachweis, daß ihre Abstraktionen ihr Ausgeschlossenes selbst erzeugen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8","CH_GB18_ANM3:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD3","text":"Kausale, begründende und bedingende Erklärungsformen sind sekundär gegenüber der logischen Entstehung bestimmter Seiten und können deren anfängliche Einheit nicht fundieren.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A5","CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD4","text":"Die ontologische Vorrangstellung eines positiven Seyns gegenüber dem Negativen zerfällt, weil bestimmte Negativität affirmativ und reines Seyn selbst negativ bestimmt ist.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A7","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD5","text":"Empirische Erfahrung besitzt im Argument eine asymmetrische Funktion: Sie destabilisiert die Abstraktion, begründet aber nicht die begriffliche Notwendigkeit ihres Umschlags.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX1","text":"Es gibt keine unterschiedslose Selbstidentität, die von aller Negation frei und dennoch bestimmbar wäre.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX2","text":"Es gibt keinen Ursprung, der zugleich völlig unmittelbar bleibt und durch ein äußerlich hinzutretendes Anderes produktiv wird.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX3","text":"Es gibt kein reines Nichts, das vollständig ohne Seyn, Beziehung, Gedachtwerden oder Bestimmung verfügbar wäre.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX4","text":"Es gibt keinen äußeren Erklärungspunkt, von dem aus der Übergang durch schon feststehende Kategorien begriffen werden könnte.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SNX1","text":"Ein absoluter, von Vermittlung und Negativität unberührter Anfang ist im System nicht verfügbar.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SNX2","text":"Eine statische Wahrheit der Momente ist nicht verfügbar; ihre Wahrheit existiert allein als ihr Umschlagen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SNX3","text":"Eine absolute Exteriorität zwischen Affirmation und Negation ist nicht verfügbar, weil jede Bestimmung die Beziehung auf ihr Anderes mitführt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A7","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS1","text":"Abstraktion des Anderen → Isolierung von Seyn oder Nichts → Negation des Übergehens.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS2","text":"Fixierung eines schlechthin unbestimmten Ersten → Ausschluß immanenten Fortgangs → äußerlicher zweiter Anfang oder Stillstand.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS3","text":"Analyse der Unbestimmtheit → Gegensatz zur Bestimmtheit → abstrakte Negativität.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS4","text":"Abstrakte Negativität des Seyns → Seyn als Nichts; Gedachtwerden des Nichts → Nichts in Beziehung auf Seyn.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS5","text":"Gegenseitiges Umschlagen der nichtselbständigen Momente → immanente Synthesis → Werden als Wahrheit beider.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS6","text":"Unmittelbarkeit des Übergangs → Ausschluß von Grund, Ursache, Bedingung und kategorialem Wie.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF1","text":"Behauptete Einheit von Seyn und Nichts → abstrakte Trennung der Momente → Negation des Übergehens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF2","text":"Festhalten eines unbestimmten Anfangs → Unmöglichkeit immanenten Fortgangs → äußerlicher zweiter Anfang als Widerspruch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF3","text":"Kritik der äußeren Synthesis → Neubestimmung der Synthesis als immanente Erzeugung des Unterschiedenen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF4","text":"Empirische Entleerung der Abstraktionen → begrifflicher Nachweis ihrer immanenten Negativität → Seyn und Nichts als nichtselbständige Momente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF5","text":"Umschlagen von Seyn und Nichts → Werden → Ausschluß jeder relationalen oder kausalen Vermittlung des anfänglichen Übergangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME1","text":"Seyn und Nichts werden von gegensätzlichen Gegenständen zu abstrakten, nichtselbständigen Momenten eines Prozesses umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME2","text":"Synthesis wird von äußerlicher Zusammensetzung zu immanenter Selbstdifferenzierung umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME3","text":"Parmenideische, spinozistische, fichtesche, jacobische und platonische Fixierungen werden als Varianten äußerer Reflexion lesbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME4","text":"Unmittelbare Erfahrung wird nicht mehr als Beleg reinen Seyns lesbar, sondern als bestimmtes Daseyn mit Schranke und Negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME5","text":"Abwesenheit, Mangel und Negativität werden von ontologisch defizitären Zuständen zu möglichen affirmativen Bestimmtheiten verschoben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME6","text":"Grund, Ursache und Bedingung erscheinen nicht als universale Erklärungsmittel, sondern als Kategorien, die bereits bestimmte Seiten voraussetzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT1","text":"Surface — Der unmittelbare Gegenstand ist die Einheit, Verschiedenheit und das Übergehen von Seyn und Nichts im Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT2","text":"Structural — Der operative Mechanismus ist die Abstraktion, welche Untrennbares trennt, fixiert und dadurch die eigene Negativität erzeugt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Der Text ersetzt die Widerlegung einzelner Einwände durch eine Kritik der Reflexionsformen, aus denen diese Einwände hervorgehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Der logische Anfang ist unmittelbar, erweist sich jedoch rückblickend als abstraktive Negativität und als in späterer Vermittlung explizierbar.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome reichen aus, um die Notwendigkeit des Werdens aus der Nichtselbständigkeit und Negativität von Seyn und Nichts zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt das genaue Verhältnis zwischen der logischen Immanenz des Übergangs, seiner empirischen Illustration und seiner späteren Vermittlung im Wesen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT3","text":"Das System bleibt kohärent, sofern Werden als Wahrheit der Momente und nicht als dritter äußerlicher Gegenstand verstanden wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT4","text":"Seine stärkste Operation ist die Umkehrung der Unbestimmtheit: Was als reine Positivität auftreten soll, wird als abstrakte Negativität bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT5","text":"Seine stärkste Kompression liegt im Übergang von der Gegenstellung von Bestimmtheit und Unbestimmtheit zur Identität von Seyn und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT6","text":"Eine strukturelle Spannung entsteht, weil der Übergang als unmittelbar und vermittlungsfrei gilt, sein Nachweis jedoch über die Reflexionsbestimmung der Unbestimmtheit geführt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT7","text":"Eine weitere Spannung liegt darin, daß empirische Widerlegung als unzureichend zurückgestuft wird, obwohl sie die abstrakten Gegenmodelle operativ destabilisiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT8","text":"Die Verweigerung vollständiger Einzelwiderlegung verlagert die Geltung auf die kritische Erkenntniß der Verstandesformen, deren eigene Begründung innerhalb dieser Einheit nicht ausgeführt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT9","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung, wenn sie Abstraktion, Selbstwiderspruch, immanente Negativität, Umschlagen und die Sperre äußerer Vermittlung als eine Sequenz behandelt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T111032746711Z_e11a51d2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Note 3.","source_sha256":"9739124cb81fd58d73e14c09fb5f2d5c9ccf00ee1312e78081348ad21110bc4d","sha256":"79e44ab1f66851e560cd7aa927caec7ef9fc9ade74039b17a24443023c02c01a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:10:32.748797+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS1","text":"The difficulty to be resolved is the assertion that Being and Nothing could subsist as isolated firsts, while their passing over is negated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS2","text":"Against this, the text posits the thesis that Becoming is the truth of both moments as their inseparable unity, distinct from them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS3","text":"The form of proof is an immanent dialectic against external reflection, which sublates its posited determinations through the Other that emerges within them themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS4","text":"The movement leads from the empirical refutation of empty abstractions to the conceptual determination of indeterminacy as abstract negativity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AS5","text":"The result determines the transition from Being and Nothing as immediate passing over, which may be mediated neither by ground, cause, condition, nor an external relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","text":"Pure Being and pure Nothing do not subsist for themselves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","text":"Becoming is the truth of Being and Nothing as a unity distinct from both moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","text":"The separation of Being and Nothing is a product of abstraction and reflective fixation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","text":"An absolutely indeterminate beginning contains no immanent progression to an Other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A5","text":"True synthesis is the immanent unity of what is differentiated, and not the connection of externally pre-given determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","text":"As the opposite of determinacy, indeterminacy is itself determinate abstract negativity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A7","text":"A determinate negative Nothing is affirmative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A8","text":"The empirical nullity of empty abstractions does not replace the immanent demonstration that abstract thought contains its opposite within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","text":"The demand for a categorically determined how of the transition presupposes the fixed categories it would use for explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A10","text":"The transition from Being and Nothing is immediate and not yet a relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:A11","text":"Nothing that is thought, represented, or expressed already stands in relation to Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX1","text":"Being and Nothing are not self-subsistent objects that could subsist outside their Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX2","text":"Becoming is not an external movement between two resting and previously complete poles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX3","text":"An absolute beginning may neither be continued through external addition nor doubled as a second beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX4","text":"Synthesis is not the subsequent connection of already existing determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX5","text":"Pure space, pure time, and pure consciousness possess no empirical self-subsistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX6","text":"The reflecting how provides no permissible explanation of the initial transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX7","text":"Ground, cause, and condition cannot be posited as mediations of pure Being and pure Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX8","text":"Determinate negativity is not an ontologically inferior, merely subjective, or ineffective absence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:NX9","text":"The refutation of the abstract standpoint does not consist in fully pursuing every objection of reflection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D1","text":"Pure Being passes over into Nothing because its indeterminacy is determined as abstract negativity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D2","text":"Pure Nothing cannot be maintained as relationless absence, because its being thought already contains Being and unity with Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D3","text":"Becoming is not a later connection of Being and Nothing, but the immanent truth of their non-self-subsistence.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D4","text":"Maintaining a pure first produces either stasis or the contradiction of an externally added second beginning.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D5","text":"The models discussed of Parmenides, Spinoza, Fichte, and Jacobi appear as variants of the same reflective fixation, which excludes difference and yet claims progression.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D6","text":"The appeal to immediately present Being refutes itself because it can show only determinate existence with limit and negation.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D7","text":"Determinate negations such as darkness and cold are positive realities of their respective determinacy and not mere empty spaces of the positive.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D8","text":"The external play of abstracting, which arbitrarily alternates from Being to Nothing and back, possesses no priority of truth.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:D9","text":"The initial transition remains concealed in the pure beginning and is explicitly posited as mediation only in later, more concrete determinations.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD1","text":"An absolute beginning can be understood only as either abstractly without progression or as self-movement; an origin that is at once isolated and productive is excluded.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD2","text":"The validity of dialectic rests not on an external refutation of opposing assertions, but on the demonstration that their abstractions themselves produce what they exclude.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8","CH_GB18_ANM3:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD3","text":"Causal, grounding, and conditioning forms of explanation are secondary to the logical emergence of determinate sides and cannot ground their initial unity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A5","CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD4","text":"The ontological priority of a positive Being over the negative collapses because determinate negativity is affirmative and pure Being is itself negatively determined.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A7","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SD5","text":"Empirical experience has an asymmetrical function in the argument: it destabilizes abstraction but does not ground the conceptual necessity of its passing over.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX1","text":"There is no undifferentiated self-identity that would be free from all negation and yet determinable.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX2","text":"There is no origin that at once remains wholly immediate and becomes productive through an externally supervening Other.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX3","text":"There is no pure Nothing that would be available wholly without Being, relation, being thought, or determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:DNX4","text":"There is no external explanatory standpoint from which the transition could be comprehended through already fixed categories.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SNX1","text":"An absolute beginning untouched by mediation and negativity is not available in the system.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A4","CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SNX2","text":"A static truth of the moments is not available; their truth exists solely as their passing over.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:SNX3","text":"An absolute exteriority between affirmation and negation is not available, because every determination carries with it the relation to its Other.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A7","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS1","text":"Abstraction from the Other → isolation of Being or Nothing → negation of passing over.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS2","text":"Fixation of an absolutely indeterminate first → exclusion of immanent progression → external second beginning or stasis.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS3","text":"Analysis of indeterminacy → opposition to determinacy → abstract negativity.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS4","text":"Abstract negativity of Being → Being as Nothing; being thought of Nothing → Nothing in relation to Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A6","CH_GB18_ANM3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS5","text":"Reciprocal passing over of the non-self-subsistent moments → immanent synthesis → Becoming as the truth of both.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A1","CH_GB18_ANM3:A2","CH_GB18_ANM3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:FGS6","text":"Immediacy of the transition → exclusion of ground, cause, condition, and categorical how.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM3:A9","CH_GB18_ANM3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF1","text":"Asserted unity of Being and Nothing → abstract separation of the moments → negation of passing over.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF2","text":"Maintaining an indeterminate beginning → impossibility of immanent progression → external second beginning as contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF3","text":"Critique of external synthesis → redetermination of synthesis as immanent production of what is differentiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF4","text":"Empirical emptying of abstractions → conceptual demonstration of their immanent negativity → Being and Nothing as non-self-subsistent moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:AF5","text":"Passing over of Being and Nothing → Becoming → exclusion of every relational or causal mediation of the initial transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME1","text":"Being and Nothing are reclassified from opposed objects into abstract, non-self-subsistent moments of a process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME2","text":"Synthesis is remapped from external composition to immanent self-differentiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME3","text":"Parmenidean, Spinozist, Fichtean, Jacobian, and Platonic fixations become legible as variants of external reflection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME4","text":"Immediate experience is no longer legible as evidence of pure Being, but as determinate existence with limit and negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME5","text":"Absence, lack, and negativity are shifted from ontologically deficient states to possible affirmative determinacies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ME6","text":"Ground, cause, and condition appear not as universal means of explanation, but as categories that already presuppose determinate sides.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT1","text":"Surface — The immediate subject is the unity, difference, and passing over of Being and Nothing in Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT2","text":"Structural — The operative mechanism is abstraction, which separates and fixes what is inseparable and thereby generates its own negativity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text replaces the refutation of individual objections with a critique of the forms of reflection from which these objections arise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The logical beginning is immediate, yet proves retrospectively to be abstractive negativity and capable of explication in later mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the necessity of Becoming from the non-self-subsistence and negativity of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT2","text":"The precise relation between the logical immanence of the transition, its empirical illustration, and its later mediation in Essence remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT3","text":"The system remains coherent provided that Becoming is understood as the truth of the moments and not as a third external object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT4","text":"Its strongest operation is the reversal of indeterminacy: what is supposed to appear as pure positivity is determined as abstract negativity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT5","text":"Its strongest compression lies in the transition from the opposition of determinacy and indeterminacy to the identity of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT6","text":"A structural tension arises because the transition counts as immediate and free of mediation, yet its demonstration is conducted through the reflective determination of indeterminacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT7","text":"A further tension lies in the fact that empirical refutation is downgraded as insufficient, although it operationally destabilizes the abstract countermodels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT8","text":"The refusal of complete individual refutation shifts validity onto the critical cognition of the forms of understanding, whose own grounding within this unity is not carried out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM3:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement if it treats abstraction, self-contradiction, immanent negativity, passing over, and the barring of external mediation as one sequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM3:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM3@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_ANM3:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 13","title":"Remark 3.","context":"Chapter 13","original_title":"Anmerkung 3."},"original_title":"Anmerkung 3.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4","layer":"CH","title":"Remark 4.","order":14,"parents":["RAW_GB18_ANM4"],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM4@R001","sha256":"e0e09b08692500bb90b25028d310a92e6e026211710b0cd3d3ac6dcef65816e0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS1","text":"Der Text prüft die Dialektik gegen Anfang, Werden, Aufhören und Vergehen auf Grundlage des Gegensatzes von Sein und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS2","text":"Die gewöhnliche Dialektik macht aus der Trennung von Sein und Nichts einen Beweis gegen jeden Anfang und jedes Ende.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS3","text":"Die reflektierende Vorstellung setzt dieselbe Trennung absolut, lässt Anfang und Aufhören jedoch zugleich gelten und erzeugt dadurch das Unbegreifliche selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS4","text":"Die Einrede gegen die unendlich-kleinen Größen wiederholt strukturell die Zurückweisung jeder Einheit von Sein und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS5","text":"Der Text unterscheidet Sophisterei als Schluss aus einer ungeprüften Voraussetzung von Dialektik als immanenter Bewegung der Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS6","text":"Sein und Nichts zeigen in ihrem eigenen Übergang das Werden als ihre Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","text":"Die gewöhnliche Dialektik setzt Sein und Nichts als schlechthin getrennte Gegensätze.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A2","text":"Ein Anfang schließt Sein in sich.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A3","text":"Was bereits ist, beginnt nicht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A4","text":"Das Nichts enthält kein Sein und kann daher keinen Anfang bilden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A5","text":"Das Sein ist als isolierte Bestimmung nur Sein und enthält nicht sein Gegenteil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","text":"Die absolute Trennung schreibt Sein und Nichts jeweils für sich Wahrheit zu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A7","text":"Anfang und Aufhören setzen faktisch eine Ungetrenntheit von Sein und Nichts voraus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","text":"Das Werden ist die Einheit von Sein und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A9","text":"Unendlich-kleine Größen sind als Größen im Verschwinden bestimmt, weder vor noch nach ihrem Verschwinden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A10","text":"Die mathematischen Erfolge beruhen auf der Bestimmung, die Sein und Nichts nicht absolut trennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A11","text":"Sophisterei ist ein Schluss aus einer grundlosen, ungeprüft geltend gemachten Voraussetzung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A12","text":"Dialektik ist die immanente Bewegung, durch die schlechthin getrennt scheinende Bestimmungen ineinander übergehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX1","text":"Ein Anfang aus dem Nichts ist ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX2","text":"Ein Ende, in dem das Sein in das Nichts übergeht, ist unter der Voraussetzung isolierten Seins ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX3","text":"Die absolute Trennung von Sein und Nichts ist keine gültige Erklärung des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX4","text":"Das Unbegreifliche löst den Widerspruch nicht, sondern bezeichnet einen durch die Voraussetzung erzeugten Widerspruch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX5","text":"Die Einordnung eines Gegenstands als entweder Etwas oder Nichts ist für die unendlich-kleinen Größen ausgeschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX6","text":"Die Einheit von Sein und Nichts darf nicht als statischer „Mittelzustand“ missverstanden werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX7","text":"Ein Raisonnement aus der absoluten Getrenntheit von Sein und Nichts ist nicht Dialektik, sondern Sophisterei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D1","text":"Unter der Voraussetzung absoluter Trennung wird jeder Anfang unmöglich, weil weder das bereits Seiende noch das Nichtseiende anfangen kann.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A2","CH_GB18_ANM4:A3","CH_GB18_ANM4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D2","text":"Unter derselben Voraussetzung wird jedes Aufhören unmöglich, weil das Sein sein Gegenteil nicht enthalten darf.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D3","text":"Die gewöhnliche Dialektik widerlegt die Einheit von Sein und Nichts nicht, sondern verneint sie lediglich assertorisch.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D4","text":"Die reflektierende Vorstellung nimmt die Einheit von Sein und Nichts faktisch an, sobald sie Anfang und Aufhören zulässt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D5","text":"Das Unbegreifliche entsteht aus einer Voraussetzung, die das Werden aufhebt und es zugleich als Bestimmung gelten lässt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D6","text":"Die Einrede gegen die unendlich-kleinen Größen wiederholt die falsche Alternative von Etwas oder Nichts.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D7","text":"In der Sprache der kritisierten Alternative gibt es kein Etwas, das vollständig außerhalb einer Bestimmung zwischen Sein und Nichts steht.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D8","text":"Die mathematische Verwendbarkeit unendlich-kleiner Größen bestätigt die operative Tragfähigkeit einer nicht-atomistischen Bestimmung.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A9","CH_GB18_ANM4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D9","text":"Der Unterschied zwischen Sophisterei und Dialektik liegt im Verhältnis der Schlussbewegung zu ihrer Voraussetzung: äußerlich festgehaltene Trennung erzeugt Sophisterei, immanenter Übergang erzeugt Dialektik.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A11","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD1","text":"Die absolute Trennung von Sein und Nichts erzeugt selbst die Unmöglichkeit des Werdens, die sie anschließend als Unbegreiflichkeit ausgibt.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A7","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD2","text":"Werden ist keine nachträgliche Verbindung isolierter Bestimmungen, sondern die immanente Wahrheit ihrer scheinbaren Trennung.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD3","text":"Die Dialektik von Weltanfang und Weltuntergang sowie die Dialektik der unendlich-kleinen Größen beruhen auf derselben logischen Fehlannahme.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD4","text":"Der Text verschiebt das Kriterium dialektischer Geltung von der formalen Widerspruchsfreiheit zur immanenten Bewegung der Bestimmungen.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A11","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD5","text":"Sein und Nichts besitzen ihre begriffliche Wahrheit nicht isoliert, sondern nur in dem Übergang, durch den sie Werden sind.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Ontologie selbstständiger, vollständig voneinander isolierter Bestimmungen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine statische Seinsordnung, die Anfang, Aufhören und Übergang erklären könnte, ohne Einheit von Sein und Nichts vorauszusetzen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist die Annahme, jede Bestimmung müsse in ein vollständig Seiendes oder vollständig Nichtiges zerfallen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Erklärung, die einen selbst erzeugten Widerspruch durch das bloße Prädikat des Unbegreiflichen beseitigt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX5","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine äußere Vermittlung, die Sein und Nichts erst nachträglich verbindet; der Übergang muss aus ihren eigenen Bestimmungen hervorgehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX1","text":"Unmöglich ist eine Weltordnung, in der Werden real gelten soll, während Sein und Nichts als absolut unverbundene Pole festgehalten werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX2","text":"Unzulässig ist jede begriffliche Architektur, die Bewegung, Entstehung oder Verschwinden aus ausschließlich statischen Kategorien rekonstruieren will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX3","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein neutraler dritter Bereich zwischen Sein und Nichts, sofern „Bereich“ oder „Zustand“ als selbstständige statische Bestimmung verstanden wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX4","text":"Versperrt ist die Möglichkeit, die Geltung von Sein und Nichts unabhängig von ihrem Übergang zu bestimmen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS1","text":"Absolute Trennung von Sein und Nichts → Ausschluss jeder Einheit → Ausschluss des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS2","text":"Anfang → erforderliches Sein; bereits Seiendes → kein Anfang; Nichtseiendes → kein Anfang; daher → Unmöglichkeit des Anfangs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS3","text":"Aufhören → Sein enthält Nichts; isoliertes Sein → enthält nicht sein Gegenteil; daher → Unmöglichkeit des Aufhörens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS4","text":"Zulassung von Anfang und Aufhören + Festhalten an absoluter Trennung → faktische Annahme der Einheit → selbst erzeugte Unbegreiflichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS5","text":"Unendlich-kleine Größe → Bestimmung im Verschwinden → weder endliche Größe vor dem Verschwinden noch Nichts nach dem Verschwinden → Zusammenbruch der binären Einrede.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS6","text":"Grundlose Festsetzung der Trennung → Sophisterei; immanenter Übergang der Bestimmungen → Dialektik; Sein und Nichts → Werden als Wahrheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AF1","text":"Festgehaltener Gegensatz von Sein und Nichts → Beweis gegen Anfang und Aufhören → faktische Wiedereinführung ihrer Einheit → Erzeugung des Unbegreiflichen → Nachweis der Voraussetzung als Fehler.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AF2","text":"Übertragung derselben Trennungslogik auf unendlich-kleine Größen → Zurückweisung des Entweder-Etwas-oder-Nichts → mathematische Bestätigung der Übergangsbestimmung → Unterscheidung von Sophisterei und Dialektik → Werden als Wahrheit von Sein und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME1","text":"Der Anfang wird von einer kosmologischen Streitfrage in einen Test der vorausgesetzten Beziehung zwischen Sein und Nichts umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME2","text":"Das Aufhören erscheint nicht mehr als isolierte Negation des Seins, sondern als Fall derselben Übergangsstruktur wie das Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME3","text":"Unendlich-kleine Größen werden nicht als dritter statischer Zustand, sondern als Bestimmungen im Übergang klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME4","text":"Die kosmologische und die mathematische Dialektik werden als Varianten eines gemeinsamen logischen Mechanismus kartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME5","text":"„Unbegreiflichkeit“ wird von einer Eigenschaft des Gegenstands zu einer Wirkung der widersprüchlichen Voraussetzung umklassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME6","text":"Der Gegensatz zwischen Sophisterei und Dialektik wird nach der Herkunft der Bewegung und nicht nach ihrer bloßen Form bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** Der Text behandelt die Möglichkeit von Anfang, Aufhören, Werden und unendlich-kleinen Größen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** Die behandelten Streitfragen werden auf die gemeinsame Struktur einer absoluten Trennung von Sein und Nichts zurückgeführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** Der Text ersetzt die Zurückweisung des Werdens durch die Prüfung der Voraussetzung, aus der diese Zurückweisung hervorgeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Realität wird als Übergang bestimmt; Sein und Nichts gelten nicht als zeitlose isolierte Substanzen, sondern als Momente des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Bewegung von der absoluten Trennung über die Unbegreiflichkeit zum Werden als Wahrheit zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt die genaue begriffliche Differenz zwischen „Einheit“, „Dasselbe“ und „ineinander Übergehen“.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern die Einheit von Sein und Nichts als immanente Übergangsbewegung und nicht als statischer Mittelzustand verstanden wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT4","text":"Ihre stärkste Stelle liegt im Nachweis, dass die absolute Trennung den Widerspruch von Werden und Nichtwerden selbst hervorbringt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT5","text":"Die mathematische Bestätigung bleibt als behauptete Wirkung der nichtgetrennten Bestimmung strukturell komprimiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT6","text":"Eine Spannung bleibt zwischen der Rede von Sein und Nichts als „demselben“ und ihrer Bestimmung als ineinander übergehenden Momenten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT7","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Bewegung vom Ausschluss des Werdens über die Selbstwiderlegung der Trennung zur immanenten Wahrheit des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T111056011664Z_8ba27a0f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Note 4.","source_sha256":"e0e09b08692500bb90b25028d310a92e6e026211710b0cd3d3ac6dcef65816e0","sha256":"4b8e48b46519a0de89a1c48d619443ef69319bac1f8e86fec5614f415dd59efd","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:10:56.014974+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS1","text":"The text examines dialectic with respect to beginning, becoming, cessation, and passing away on the basis of the opposition between Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS2","text":"Ordinary dialectic turns the separation of Being and Nothing into a proof against every beginning and every end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS3","text":"Reflective representation posits the same separation absolutely, yet at the same time allows beginning and cessation to hold, thereby itself producing the incomprehensible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS4","text":"The objection to infinitesimal magnitudes structurally repeats the rejection of every unity of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS5","text":"The text distinguishes sophistry as inference from an unexamined presupposition from dialectic as the immanent movement of determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AS6","text":"Being and Nothing show becoming, in their own transition, as their truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","text":"Ordinary dialectic posits Being and Nothing as absolutely separated opposites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A2","text":"A beginning contains Being within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A3","text":"What already is does not begin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A4","text":"Nothing contains no Being and can therefore constitute no beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A5","text":"Being, as an isolated determination, is only Being and does not contain its opposite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","text":"Absolute separation ascribes truth to Being and Nothing, each for itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A7","text":"Beginning and cessation in fact presuppose an inseparateness of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","text":"Becoming is the unity of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A9","text":"Infinitesimal magnitudes are determined as magnitudes in vanishing, neither before nor after their vanishing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A10","text":"The mathematical successes rest upon the determination that does not absolutely separate Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A11","text":"Sophistry is inference from a groundless presupposition advanced as unexamined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:A12","text":"Dialectic is the immanent movement through which determinations appearing absolutely separated pass over into one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX1","text":"A beginning out of Nothing is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX2","text":"An end in which Being passes over into Nothing is excluded under the presupposition of isolated Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX3","text":"The absolute separation of Being and Nothing is no valid explanation of becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX4","text":"The incomprehensible does not resolve the contradiction, but designates a contradiction produced by the presupposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX5","text":"The classification of an object as either Something or Nothing is excluded for infinitesimal magnitudes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX6","text":"The unity of Being and Nothing must not be misunderstood as a static “Mittelzustand”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:NX7","text":"A Raisonnement proceeding from the absolute separateness of Being and Nothing is not dialectic, but sophistry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D1","text":"Under the presupposition of absolute separation, every beginning becomes impossible, because neither what already is nor what is not can begin.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A2","CH_GB18_ANM4:A3","CH_GB18_ANM4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D2","text":"Under the same presupposition, every cessation becomes impossible, because Being may not contain its opposite.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D3","text":"Ordinary dialectic does not refute the unity of Being and Nothing, but merely denies it assertorically.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D4","text":"Reflective representation in fact assumes the unity of Being and Nothing as soon as it admits beginning and cessation.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D5","text":"The incomprehensible arises from a presupposition that sublates becoming while at the same time allowing it to hold as a determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D6","text":"The objection to infinitesimal magnitudes repeats the false alternative of Something or Nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D7","text":"In the language of the criticized alternative, there is no Something that stands wholly outside a determination between Being and Nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D8","text":"The mathematical usability of infinitesimal magnitudes confirms the operative viability of a non-atomistic determination.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A9","CH_GB18_ANM4:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:D9","text":"The difference between sophistry and dialectic lies in the relation of inferential movement to its presupposition: externally maintained separation produces sophistry; immanent transition produces dialectic.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A11","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD1","text":"The absolute separation of Being and Nothing itself produces the impossibility of becoming, which it subsequently presents as incomprehensibility.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A7","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD2","text":"Becoming is not a subsequent connection of isolated determinations, but the immanent truth of their apparent separation.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD3","text":"The dialectic of the beginning and end of the world, as well as the dialectic of infinitesimal magnitudes, rest on the same logical false presupposition.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A1","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD4","text":"The text shifts the criterion of dialectical validity from formal freedom from contradiction to the immanent movement of determinations.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A11","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SD5","text":"Being and Nothing possess their conceptual truth not in isolation, but only in the transition through which they are becoming.","refs":["CH_GB18_ANM4:A6","CH_GB18_ANM4:A8","CH_GB18_ANM4:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX1","text":"Excluded is an ontology of self-subsistent determinations completely isolated from one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX2","text":"Excluded is a static order of Being that could explain beginning, cessation, and transition without presupposing the unity of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX3","text":"Excluded is the assumption that every determination must disintegrate into a wholly existing or wholly null entity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX4","text":"Excluded is an explanation that eliminates a self-produced contradiction by the mere predicate of the incomprehensible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:DNX5","text":"Excluded is an external mediation that connects Being and Nothing only subsequently; the transition must arise from their own determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX1","text":"Impossible is an order of the world in which becoming is to hold as real while Being and Nothing are maintained as absolutely unconnected poles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX2","text":"Inadmissible is every conceptual architecture that seeks to reconstruct movement, emergence, or vanishing from exclusively static categories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX3","text":"Unavailable is a neutral third domain between Being and Nothing, insofar as “Bereich” or “Zustand” is understood as a self-subsistent static determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:SNX4","text":"Foreclosed is the possibility of determining the validity of Being and Nothing independently of their transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS1","text":"Absolute separation of Being and Nothing → exclusion of every unity → exclusion of becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS2","text":"Beginning → required Being; what already is → no beginning; what is not → no beginning; therefore → impossibility of beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS3","text":"Cessation → Being contains Nothing; isolated Being → does not contain its opposite; therefore → impossibility of cessation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS4","text":"Admission of beginning and cessation + adherence to absolute separation → factual assumption of unity → self-produced incomprehensibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS5","text":"Infinitesimal magnitude → determination in vanishing → neither finite magnitude before vanishing nor Nothing after vanishing → collapse of the binary objection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:FGS6","text":"Groundless positing of separation → sophistry; immanent transition of determinations → dialectic; Being and Nothing → becoming as truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AF1","text":"Maintained opposition of Being and Nothing → proof against beginning and cessation → factual reintroduction of their unity → production of the incomprehensible → demonstration of the presupposition as error.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:AF2","text":"Transfer of the same logic of separation to infinitesimal magnitudes → rejection of the either-Something-or-Nothing → mathematical confirmation of the transitional determination → distinction between sophistry and dialectic → becoming as the truth of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME1","text":"Beginning is remapped from a cosmological disputed question into a test of the presupposed relation between Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME2","text":"Cessation no longer appears as an isolated negation of Being, but as a case of the same transitional structure as becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME3","text":"Infinitesimal magnitudes are classified not as a third static state, but as determinations in transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME4","text":"The cosmological and mathematical dialectics are mapped as variants of a common logical mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME5","text":"“Unbegreiflichkeit” is reclassified from a property of the object into an effect of the contradictory presupposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ME6","text":"The opposition between sophistry and dialectic is determined according to the origin of movement and not according to its mere form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** The text treats the possibility of beginning, cessation, becoming, and infinitesimal magnitudes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** The disputed questions treated are traced back to the common structure of an absolute separation of Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** The text replaces the rejection of becoming with the examination of the presupposition from which this rejection arises.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Reality is determined as transition; Being and Nothing hold not as timeless isolated substances, but as moments of becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the movement from absolute separation through incomprehensibility to becoming as truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT2","text":"What remains underdetermined is the precise conceptual difference between “Einheit”, “Dasselbe”, and “ineinander Übergehen”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent, provided that the unity of Being and Nothing is understood as immanent transitional movement and not as a static intermediate state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT4","text":"Its strongest point lies in demonstrating that absolute separation itself brings forth the contradiction of becoming and non-becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT5","text":"The mathematical confirmation remains structurally compressed as an asserted effect of the non-separated determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT6","text":"A tension remains between speaking of Being and Nothing as “demselben” and determining them as moments passing over into one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_ANM4:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement from the exclusion of becoming through the self-refutation of separation to the immanent truth of becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_ANM4:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_GB18_ANM4@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_GB18_ANM4:v1","source_language_code":"de"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 14","title":"Remark 4.","context":"Chapter 14","original_title":"Anmerkung 4."},"original_title":"Anmerkung 4.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW","layer":"CH","title":"2. Moments of Becoming.","order":15,"parents":["RAW_GB18_2MDW"],"revision":"CH_GB18_2MDW@R001","sha256":"0048efa37f0651f2b888668b5b0a5a64539f0e18484d5bfb0dd87e8c0cd045b0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS1","text":"Das zentrale Problem ist die Bestimmung der Einheit von Seyn und Nichts, ohne ihre Differenz oder ihre Selbstaufhebung zu verlieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS2","text":"Werden wird als eine bestimmte Einheit bestimmt, in der Seyn und Nichts zugleich enthalten und aufgehoben sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS3","text":"Die zunächst selbstständigen Bestimmungen sinken zu unterschiedenen Momenten einer gemeinsamen Bewegung herab.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS4","text":"Diese Bewegung gliedert sich in die gegenläufigen Richtungen Entstehen und Vergehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS5","text":"Die gegenläufigen Richtungen sind identisch, durchdringen und paralysieren einander, weil jede Richtung an sich selbst in ihr Gegenteil übergeht.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A1","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind im Werden ungetrennt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A2","text":"Die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts ist eine bestimmte Einheit und keine abstrakte Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A3","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind in ihrer Einheit nicht als selbstständige Bestimmungen vorhanden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A4","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind als verschwindende und aufgehobene Momente vorhanden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A5","text":"Jedes der beiden Momente ist in seiner Unterschiedenheit Einheit mit dem jeweils anderen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A6","text":"Das Werden enthält zwei Einheiten, in denen Seyn und Nichts jeweils mit ungleichem unmittelbarem Gewicht bestimmt sind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A7","text":"Die Einheit mit Nichts als Unmittelbarem ist der Übergang von Nichts in Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A8","text":"Die Einheit mit Seyn als Unmittelbarem ist der Übergang von Seyn in Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A9","text":"Entstehen und Vergehen sind zwei unterschiedene Richtungen desselben Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A10","text":"Jede Richtung hebt sich an sich selbst auf und ist dadurch das Gegenteil ihrer selbst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX1","text":"Werden ist nicht die von Seyn und Nichts abstrahierte Einheit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX2","text":"Seyn und Nichts sind im Werden nicht selbstständig.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX3","text":"Entstehen und Vergehen heben einander nicht äußerlich auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX4","text":"Keine der beiden Richtungen bleibt auf ihren unmittelbaren Ausgangspunkt beschränkt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX5","text":"Nichts ist nicht ausschließlich Nichts, und Seyn ist nicht ausschließlich Seyn.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX6","text":"Die Einheit von Seyn und Nichts ist keine unterschiedslose Identität.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D1","text":"Seyn und Nichts werden durch ihre Aufhebung zu Momenten des Werdens.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A1","CH_GB18_2MDW:A3","CH_GB18_2MDW:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D2","text":"Die Unterscheidung von Seyn und Nichts bleibt innerhalb ihrer Einheit erhalten, ohne ihre frühere Selbstständigkeit zu bewahren.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A4","CH_GB18_2MDW:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D3","text":"Das Werden ist doppelt bestimmt, weil seine Einheit zwei asymmetrische Ausgangsbestimmungen enthält.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D4","text":"Entstehen bezeichnet den Übergang des unmittelbar gesetzten Nichts in Seyn.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D5","text":"Vergehen bezeichnet den Übergang des unmittelbar gesetzten Seyns in Nichts.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D6","text":"Entstehen und Vergehen sind trotz ihrer entgegengesetzten Richtungen dasselbe Werden.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D7","text":"Jede Richtung enthält die entgegengesetzte Richtung als ihre eigene innere Bewegung.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD1","text":"Werden ist keine statische Verbindung zweier fertiger Bestimmungen, sondern die Selbstbewegung ihrer aufgehobenen Gegensätzlichkeit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD2","text":"Die Identität des Werdens entsteht nicht trotz, sondern durch die wechselseitige Selbstaufhebung von Entstehen und Vergehen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD3","text":"Die Differenz von Seyn und Nichts wird in eine zeitlich gerichtete, aber intern umkehrende Struktur überführt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD4","text":"Das Werden totalisiert die Gegensätze, indem jeder Gegensatzpol nur als Übergang zu seinem Gegenteil bestehen kann.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX1","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Seyn, das unabhängig von Nichts als isolierte Unmittelbarkeit bestehen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX2","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist ein Nichts, das ohne Beziehung auf Seyn als isolierte Unmittelbarkeit bestehen könnte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX3","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Einheit, die die Differenz ihrer Momente durch Abstraktion beseitigt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX4","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine äußerliche Dialektik, in der ein Moment nur von einem äußerlich entgegengesetzten Moment aufgehoben wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX5","text":"Ausgeschlossen ist eine Bewegung, deren Anfangsbestimmung unverändert erhalten bleibt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SNX1","text":"Unmöglich ist eine stabile ontologische Position außerhalb des Übergangs zwischen Seyn und Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SNX2","text":"Nicht verfügbar ist ein reiner Anfang, der nicht bereits den Übergang in sein Gegenteil enthielte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SNX3","text":"Unzulässig ist die Trennung von Identität und Differenz: Ihre Abstraktion voneinander zerstört die bestimmte Einheit des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SNX4","text":"Die versperrte Möglichkeit ist ein abgeschlossenes Seyn oder Nichts; gerade deren Unmöglichkeit erzeugt die Bewegungsform des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS1","text":"Unmittelbare Gegensätze werden als ungetrennte Einheit gesetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS2","text":"Die ungetrennte Einheit hebt die selbstständige Geltung ihrer Bestimmungen auf.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS3","text":"Die aufgehobenen Bestimmungen bleiben als unterschiedene Momente erhalten.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS4","text":"Jedes Moment wird als Einheit mit seinem Gegenteil bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS5","text":"Die unterschiedliche Unmittelbarkeit der Momente erzeugt zwei Richtungen: Nichts → Seyn und Seyn → Nichts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS6","text":"Die Richtungen werden als Entstehen und Vergehen unterschieden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS7","text":"Jede Richtung kehrt durch ihre eigene Selbstaufhebung in die Gegenrichtung um.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:FGS8","text":"Die gegenläufigen Richtungen werden dadurch als identische Gesamtbewegung des Werdens geschlossen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AF1","text":"Abstrakte Einheitsvorstellung → bestimmte Einheit von Seyn und Nichts → Aufhebung ihrer Selbstständigkeit → Erhaltung als Momente → asymmetrische Doppelbestimmung → Entstehen und Vergehen → innere Umkehrung jeder Richtung → identisches Werden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ME1","text":"Seyn und Nichts werden von isolierten Seinsbestimmungen zu relationalen Momenten einer Bewegung umkartiert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ME2","text":"Der Gegensatz von Entstehen und Vergehen wird als Richtungsdifferenz innerhalb einer identischen Bewegung klassifiziert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ME3","text":"Äußerliche Aufhebung wird durch innere Selbstaufhebung ersetzt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ME4","text":"Identität und Differenz erscheinen nicht mehr als Gegensätze, sondern als ko-konstitutive Bestimmungen des Werdens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ME5","text":"Anfang und Ende verlieren ihre absolute Trennbarkeit, weil jeder Anfang bereits den Übergang in sein Gegenteil enthält.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ALT1","text":"**Surface:** Werden wird als Einheit von Seyn und Nichts sowie als Entstehen und Vergehen bestimmt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ALT2","text":"**Structural:** Die Bestimmungen werden durch Aufhebung ihrer Selbstständigkeit zu Momenten einer relationalen Bewegungsstruktur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic:** Der Gegensatz wird nicht durch Entscheidung für eine Seite, sondern durch die Rekonstruktion seiner inneren Umkehrbarkeit aufgelöst.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal:** Realität erscheint als Übergangsgeschehen, in dem Seyn und Nichts nur in ihrer gegenseitigen Aufhebung Bestand haben.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:MRT1","text":"Die Axiome sind hinreichend, um die Bewegung von der bestimmten Einheit über die aufgehobenen Momente bis zu Entstehen und Vergehen zu rekonstruieren.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:MRT2","text":"Unterbestimmt bleibt, wodurch die asymmetrische Gewichtung von Seyn und Nichts in den beiden Einheiten formal festgelegt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:MRT3","text":"Die Struktur ist intern kohärent, sofern Aufhebung zugleich Negation und Erhaltung bedeutet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:MRT4","text":"Ihre stärkste Stelle ist die Ableitung der Gegenrichtung aus der inneren Bestimmung jeder Richtung.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:MRT5","text":"Ihre schwächste Stelle liegt in der nicht weiter begründeten Setzung, dass jede Bestimmung an sich selbst ihr Gegenteil ist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:MRT6","text":"Die Rekonstruktion bewahrt die tatsächliche Argumentbewegung, sofern Werden als selbstaufhebende Einheit und nicht als bloße Verbindung zweier Zustände behandelt wird.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"de","language_name":"Deutsch","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261019T110502454342Z_ff937c4f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"2. Moments of Becoming.","source_sha256":"0048efa37f0651f2b888668b5b0a5a64539f0e18484d5bfb0dd87e8c0cd045b0","sha256":"8dddc94c8962af33ce4717220ee6897647ee89328bbc5fefb9e25495ee042f3a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-19T11:05:02.456522+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS1","text":"The central problem is the determination of the unity of Being and Nothing without losing their difference or their self-sublation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS2","text":"Becoming is determined as a determinate unity in which Being and Nothing are at once contained and sublated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS3","text":"The determinations that are initially self-subsistent descend into distinct moments of a common movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS4","text":"This movement is articulated into the opposed directions of coming-to-be and ceasing-to-be.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:AS5","text":"The opposed directions are identical, interpenetrate and paralyze one another, because each direction passes over into its opposite in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A1","text":"Being and Nothing are inseparable in Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A2","text":"The unity of Being and Nothing is a determinate unity and not an abstract unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A3","text":"Being and Nothing are not present in their unity as self-subsistent determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A4","text":"Being and Nothing are present as vanishing and sublated moments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A5","text":"Each of the two moments is, in its distinctness, unity with the respectively other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A6","text":"Becoming contains two unities in which Being and Nothing are each determined with unequal immediate weight.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A7","text":"The unity with Nothing as the immediate is the transition from Nothing into Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A8","text":"The unity with Being as the immediate is the transition from Being into Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A9","text":"Coming-to-be and ceasing-to-be are two distinct directions of the same Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:A10","text":"Each direction sublates itself in itself and is thereby its own opposite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX1","text":"Becoming is not the unity abstracted from Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX2","text":"Being and Nothing are not self-subsistent in Becoming.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX3","text":"Coming-to-be and ceasing-to-be do not sublate one another externally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX4","text":"Neither of the two directions remains confined to its immediate point of departure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX5","text":"Nothing is not exclusively Nothing, and Being is not exclusively Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:NX6","text":"The unity of Being and Nothing is not an undifferentiated identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D1","text":"Through their sublation, Being and Nothing become moments of Becoming.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A1","CH_GB18_2MDW:A3","CH_GB18_2MDW:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D2","text":"The distinction between Being and Nothing remains preserved within their unity without preserving their former self-subsistence.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A4","CH_GB18_2MDW:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D3","text":"Becoming is doubly determined because its unity contains two asymmetric initial determinations.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D4","text":"Coming-to-be designates the transition of immediately posited Nothing into Being.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D5","text":"Ceasing-to-be designates the transition of immediately posited Being into Nothing.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D6","text":"Despite their opposed directions, coming-to-be and ceasing-to-be are the same Becoming.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:D7","text":"Each direction contains the opposed direction as its own inner movement.","refs":["CH_GB18_2MDW:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD1","text":"Becoming is not a static connection of two finished determinations, but the self-movement of their sublated opposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD2","text":"The identity of Becoming arises not despite, but through, the reciprocal self-sublation of coming-to-be and ceasing-to-be.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD3","text":"The difference of Being and Nothing is transferred into a temporally directed but internally reversible structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SD4","text":"Becoming totalizes the opposites by virtue of each pole of opposition being able to subsist only as a transition to its opposite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX1","text":"Excluded is a Being that could subsist independently of Nothing as isolated immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX2","text":"Excluded is a Nothing that could subsist without relation to Being as isolated immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX3","text":"Excluded is a unity that eliminates the difference of its moments through abstraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX4","text":"Excluded is an external dialectic in which a moment is sublated only by an externally opposed moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:DNX5","text":"Excluded is a movement whose initial determination remains preserved unchanged.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SNX1","text":"Impossible is a stable ontological position outside the transition between Being and Nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_GB18_2MDW:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_GB18_2MDW:SNX2","text